
#bookname=wilson (sa-en)
#stripmethod=keep
#sametypesequence=h
#description=Data from https://www.sanskrit-lexicon.uni-koeln.de/ as on 2026-09-26

अ|अं|अः
अ<BR>The first letter of the alphabet, and inherent short vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ<BR>ind.<BR>1 No, not.<BR>2 A privative, prohibitive, and diminutive particle.<BR>3 An interjection of pity. It also implies degrees of difference, and similarity.<BR>As a negative prefix to words beginning with a vowel, अ is changed to अन्, as अ and अन्त form अनन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अ|अं|अः
अ<BR>m. (अः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अऋणिन्
अऋणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिणी-णि)<BR>Free from debt or obligation; also अनृणिन्.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ऋणिन् a debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश|अंशः
अंश<BR>r. 10th cl. (अंशयति)<BR>To separate or divide. See अंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश|अंशः
अंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A share or portion.<BR>2 A part.<BR>3 A shoulder, the shoulder blade.<BR>4 (In arithmetic) a fraction.<BR>5 The numerator of a fraction.<BR>6 A degree of latitude or longitude, &c. See अंस.<BR>E.<BR>अंश to divide, अच् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशक|अंशकं|अंशकः
अंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kinsman, a relation, a coheir.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>a day.<BR>E.<BR>अंश to separate or divide, and वुन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशभाज्
अंशभाज्<BR>mfn. (भाक्)<BR>An heir, a coheir, one who has a share or portion.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशन|अंशनं
अंशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dividing, sharing.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशनीय
अंशनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be divided, divisible.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशमान
अंशमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dividing, sharing.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयत्
अंशयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यती-यत्)<BR>Dividing, sharing.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and यति affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितव्य
अंशयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Divisible, to be divided.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशयितृ
अंशयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-ची-तृ)<BR>Dividing, sharing.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशल|अंशलः
अंशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, stout, lusty. See अंसस्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहर
अंशहर<BR>mfn. (-रः रा-री-रं)<BR>A sharer, a divider, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशहारिन्
अंशहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>A sharer, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांश|अंशांशः
अंशांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Part of a portion or share.<BR>E.<BR>अंश repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशांशि
अंशांशि<BR>ind.<BR>Share by share.<BR>E.<BR>अंश repeated and इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशित
अंशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Divided, portioned, shared.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशिन्
अंशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>A sharer, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंश्य
अंश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Divisible, to be shared or divided.<BR>E.<BR>अश and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशु|अंशुः
अंशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 A ray of light, a sun-beam.<BR>2 Light, splendor, effulgence.<BR>3 Dress, decoration.<BR>4 A small filament or end of thread.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>6 A minute particle or atom.<BR>E.<BR>अंश to divide, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुक|अंशुकं
अंशुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Fine cloth, muslin.<BR>2 A mantle, a wrapper, a robe, a linen garment worn round the upper part of the body.<BR>3 Cloth in general.<BR>4 White cloth.<BR>5 A leaf.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुजाल
अंशुजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A collection or blaze of light.<BR>2 A parcel or pencil of rays.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुधर|अंशुधरः
अंशुधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुभर्तृ|अंशुभर्त्तृ
अंशुभर्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अंश and भर्तृ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्|अंशुमन्त्
अंशुमत्<BR>mfn.(-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Radiant, luminous.<BR>2 Acuminated, pointed.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A prince of the solar race, son of ASAMAÑJAS, grandson of SĀGARA.<BR>(-ती)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum Gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमत्फला
अंशुमत्फला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The plantain, (Musa paradisiaca.)<BR>E.<BR>अंशुमत् and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमाला
अंशुमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A garland of light, a halo.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुमालिन्
अंशुमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अंशुमाला and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुल|अंशुलः
अंशुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Radiant, splendid.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुवाण
अंशुवाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and वाण an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंशुहस्त|अंशुहस्तः
अंशुहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अंशु and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस|अंसः
अंस<BR>r. 10th cl. (अंसयति)<BR>To separate of divide; also written अंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंस|अंसः
अंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A shoulder, a scapula.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>E.<BR>अंस to divide, अच् aff. it is also written अंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसकूट|अंसकूटः
अंसकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A bull's hump, the protuberance between the shoulders of the Indian ox.<BR>E.<BR>अंस the shoulder, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंसल|अंसलः
अंसल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, stout, lusty.<BR>E.<BR>अंस the shoulder, and लच् aff. also written अंशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहति|अंहतिः
अंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A gift, a donation.<BR>2 Sickness, disease.<BR>3 Leaving, abandoning.<BR>4 A gift.<BR>E.<BR>अहि to go, क्तिन् affix or अंह for हन to kill, and अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहती
अंहती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A gift or donation.<BR>E.<BR>See अंहति, इ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=001" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहस्
अंहस्<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>Sin. See अङ्घस्.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and the Uṇādi affix, असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंहिति|अंहितिः
अंहिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A gift or donation.<BR>E.<BR>See अंहति, इट् being inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रि|अंह्रिः
अंह्रि<BR>m. (-ह्रिः)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 The root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अहि to go, and क्रिण् Uṇādi affix: also अङ्घ्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिप|अंह्रिपः
अंह्रिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>अंह्रि the root, and प from पा to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंह्रिस्कन्ध|अंह्रिस्कंध|अंह्रिस्कन्धः
अंह्रिस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The heel.<BR>E.<BR>अंह्रि the foot, and स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक<BR>r. 1st cl. (अकति)<BR>To wind or move tortuously.<BR>With an indicatory इ। अकि<BR>(अंकति)<BR>1 To mark or bespot.<BR>2 To go. See अङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक|अकं
अक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Moving tortuously.<BR>2 One who goes crookedly.<BR>3 Pain, affliction.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and क happiness, or अक to move crookedly, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकच|अकचः
अकच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>Name of KETU, the dragon's tail, or descending node.<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Bald, destitute of hair.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कच hair: this applies to KETU, as the symbol of the asterism is a headless trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकण्टक
अकण्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Free from thorns, literally or metaphorically.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकथ्य|अकथ्यः
अकथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>Not to be mentioned or spoken of; also similar forms as अकयनीय &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कथ to speak, with the participial affixes यत् अनीयर् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठ|अकनिष्ठः
अकनिष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A deified saint according to the Bauddhas.<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Elder, superior.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कनिष्ठ youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकनिष्ठग|अकनिष्ठगः
अकनिष्ठग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A deified saint according to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>अकनिष्ठ superior and गम to go; affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकम्पित|अकंपित|अकम्पितः
अकम्पित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The name of a Jaina saint, one of the pupils of the last Tīrthakara.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Firm, unshaken, not agitated or trembling.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कपि to tremble; the participial affix क्त, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर
अकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Maimed, handless.<BR>2 Privileged, exempt from tax or duty.<BR>3 One who does not act.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कर the hand, tax, duty.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कृञ to injure, अन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणि|अकरणिः
अकरणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Failure, disappointment, (it is used only as an imprecation,) as तस्याकरणिरेवास्तु may he fail.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कृञ to do, and अनि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरणीय
अकरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be done, improper or impracticable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. करणीय to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकरुण|अकरुणः
अकरुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unfeeling, void of compassion or tenderness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. करुणा tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्क्कश|अकर्कश|अकर्कशः
अकर्क्कश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Soft, not hard.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कर्क्कश hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्ण|अकर्णः|अकर्ण्ण
अकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Deaf.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्त्तन|अकर्तन|अकर्त्तनः
अकर्त्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>A dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्त्तव्य|अकर्तव्य|अकर्त्तव्यं
अकर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Not to be done, improper, impracticable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मण्य|अकर्मण्य|अकर्म्मण्यं
अकर्म्मण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Not to be done, improper.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कर्म्मन् act, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मन्|अकर्मन्
अकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Idle, unoccupied, without work.<BR>2 Degraded, no longer performing essential rites.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Absence of occupation.<BR>2 Loss or neglect of essential observances.<BR>3 Improper act, crime, offence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकर्म्मकृत्|अकर्मकृत्
अकर्म्मकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Free from action, necessary as vital, or essential as religious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कर्म्म act, कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्क
अकल्क<BR>mfn. (-क्लः-ल्का-ल्कं)<BR>1 Clear, clean.<BR>2 Pure, sinless.<BR>3 Free from sediment.<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कल्क dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्कन|अकल्कनः
अकल्कन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Humble, not proud, (this word is sometimes written अकल्कल.)<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कल्क pride, and न or ल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्पित|अकल्पितः
अकल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Natural, not artificial, not made.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कल्पित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्मष
अकल्मष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Faultless, sinless.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्य|अकल्यः
अकल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. कल्य well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकल्याण|अकल्याणं
अकल्याण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कल्याण prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकस्मात्
अकस्मात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Immediately, instantly, presently.<BR>2 Without a cause, without a wherefore.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कस्मात् from what.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्ड|अकांड
अकाण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Sudden, unexpected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डजात
अकाण्डजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suddenly born or produced.<BR>E.<BR>अकाण्ड and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाण्डपातजात
अकाण्डपातजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perishing suddenly after birth, dying as soon as born.<BR>E.<BR>अकाण्ड, and पात perishing, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारण|अकारणं
अकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Absence or non-existence of a cause. (Used adverbially,) Causelessly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकारणोत्पन्न
अकारणोत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Born or produced without a cause.<BR>E.<BR>अकारण and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकार्य्य|अकार्य|अकार्य्यं
अकार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Improper not to be done.<BR>n. (र्य्यं)<BR>An improper act.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कार्य्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकाल|अकालः
अकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Irregular or unusual, as time or season.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालकुसुम
अकालकुसुम<BR>m. (-मंः)<BR>A flower budding out of season.<BR>E.<BR>अकाल and कुमुम a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालज|अकालजः
अकालज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Unseasonable, produced out of time or season; also अकालजात, अकालोत्पन्न and similar compounds.<BR>E.<BR>अकाल with ज or जात &c. born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालजलदोदय|अकालजलदोदयः
अकालजलदोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A fog, or mist.<BR>2 Unseasonable gathering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and काल time, जलट् a cloud, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालमेघोदय|अकालमेघोदयः
अकालमेघोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Unseasonable cloudiness.<BR>2 A fog or mist.<BR>E.<BR>अकाल with मेघ a cloud, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकालसह
अकालसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Impatient, premature, not waiting for the proper season.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कालसह time-enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चन|अकिंचन|अकिञ्चनः
अकिञ्चन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and किञ्चन any thing, something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिञ्चनता|अकिंचनता
अकिञ्चनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Voluntary poverty, one of the duties of a Jaina ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>अकिञ्चन and ता affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकिल्विष|अकिल्विषः
अकिल्विष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Faultless, free from sin.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. किल्विष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकीर्त्ति|अकीर्ति|अकीर्तिः|अकीर्त्तिः
अकीर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Infamy, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अ reverse, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुत्सित
अकुत्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unreproached, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कुत्सित bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुप्य|अकुप्यं
अकुप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Gold or silver.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and कुण base metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुल|अकुलः
अकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Low, mean, of low family.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कुल family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=002" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुलीन
अकुलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Low, mean, of low origin or race.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कुलीन of family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकुशल
अकुशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>2 Clumsy, not clever.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कुशल lucky, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूपार|अकूपारः
अकूपार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sea or ocean.<BR>2 A tortoise.<BR>3 The king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold the world.<BR>4 A stone or rock.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कू the earth, and पृ to cherish, or अ neg. कू for कुत्सित contemptible, vile, and पार bank, boundary: there are other etymologies, and वृ being substituted for पृ, the word is sometimes written अकूवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकूर्च्च|अकूर्च|अकूर्चः|अकूर्च्चः
अकूर्च्च<BR>m. (-र्च्चः)<BR>A deified saint, according to the Bauddhas.<BR>mfn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्चा-र्च्चं)<BR>Void of guile.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and कूर्च्च fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत|अकृतं
अकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undone, neglected, incomplete.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Any act unperformed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञ|अकृतज्ञः
अकृतज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Ungrateful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृतज्ञ grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञता
अकृतज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ingratitude.<BR>E.<BR>ता added to अकृतज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतज्ञत्व
अकृतज्ञत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Ingratitude.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अकृतज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतात्मन्
अकृतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Not identified or made one with oneself, especially in a spiritual sense, not one with spirit, or God.<BR>E.<BR>अकृत unmade, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतित्व|अकृतित्वं
अकृतित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Awkwardness, clumsiness, unfitness.<BR>E.<BR>अकृतिन् and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृतिन्
अकृतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Awkward, stupid, incapable of or unfit for doing any thing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृ to do, इन् aff. and त augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृत्रिम|अकृत्रिमं
अकृत्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Natural, inartificial, not made.<BR>E.<BR>अ. neg. कृतिम artificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृप|अकृपः
अकृप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Unmerciful, unkind.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृपा mercy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृपण|अकृपणः
अकृपण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Liberal, not miserly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृपण miserly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृश
अकृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Full, entire.<BR>2 Strong, fierce.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कृश little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकृष्णकर्म्मन्|अकृष्णकर्मन्
अकृष्णकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Innocent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and कृष्णकर्म्मन् guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकेश|अकेशः
अकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Bald, hairless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोट|अकोटः
अकोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The betel-nut tree. (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and कुट to be crooked, because it grows with a straight stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अकोविद|अकोविदः
अकोविद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Stupid, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. कोविद् clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्का
अक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>अक pain, कै to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तां)<BR>1 Joined, combined.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>3 Spread abroad.<BR>4 Anointed.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to go, and क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्तु|अक्तुः
अक्तु<BR>f. (-क्तुः)<BR>Night, (on the authority of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to go, and क्तु affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रम|अक्रमः
अक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Want of order or arrangement, confusion, irregularity.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रान्त|अक्रांत
अक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Unpassed, unsurpassed.<BR>2 Unconquered.<BR>f. (-त्तः)<BR>The egg-plant. (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्रान्त passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रोध|अक्रोधः
अक्रोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Dispassionateness, restraint of anger, one of the ten duties of an ascetic.<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Dispassionate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्रोध anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रिय|अक्रियः
अक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Inactive, dull, torpid.<BR>2 Abstaining from religious rites.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Inactivity, neglect of what ought to be done.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रियत्व
अक्रियत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Inactivity, torpor. त्व added to the preceding. also अक्रियता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्रूर|अक्रूरः
अक्रूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Gentle, not cruel.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The paternal uncle and friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्रूर cruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेद्य
अक्लेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Incapable of distress or pain.<BR>2 Unfit to be pained or distressed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्लेद्य to be pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लम
अक्लम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Absence of weariness or fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and क्लम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लान्त|अक्लान्तः
अक्लान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Unwearied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्लान्त wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिष्ट
अक्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unvexed, not distressed or annoyed.<BR>2 Unwearied, indefatigable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्लिष्ट wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लेश|अक्लेशं|अक्लेशः
अक्लेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Absence of weariness or vexation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्लेश distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्लिका
अक्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The indigo plant. (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष<BR>r. 1st and 3d cl. (अक्षति अक्ष्णोति)<BR>1 To reach or obtain.<BR>2 To pervade.<BR>3 To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष|अक्षं|अक्षः
अक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A die, cubic or oblong, for playing with.<BR>2 Part of a car.<BR>3 A wheel.<BR>4 A car.<BR>5 A snake.<BR>6 Law suit, legal proceedings.<BR>7 Sacred knowledge.<BR>8 The soul.<BR>9 A seed of which Rosaries are made, in which sense it occurs mostly in composition, as, Rudrākṣa, Indrākṣa.<BR>10 A Karṣa or weight of sixteen māṣas.<BR>11 A tree bearing a medicinal fruit. (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>12 A proper name. the son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>13 A name of GARUḌA.<BR>14 A person born blind.<BR>15 Terrestrial latitude.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 An organ of sense.<BR>2 Sea salt.<BR>3 Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>अशु to pervade, Uṇādi affix स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षक|अक्षकः
अक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree. (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष Beleric myrobalan, and क affix: from its resembling that plant; or the termination being a pleonastic affix, the word may have all the senses of the preceding: also read अक्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षकर्ण|अक्षकर्णः
अक्षकर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The hypothenuse, especially of the triangle formed with the gnomon of a dial and its shadow.<BR>2 (In astronomy.) Argument of the latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षत|अक्षतं|अक्षतः
अक्षत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Fried grain, (in this sense it is also used in the mas. plu. -ताः).<BR>2 A eunuch.<BR>3 Whole grain.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, named also Kāṅkarasriṅgī.<BR>mfn. (-त-ता-तं.)<BR>1 Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>2 Whole, unbroken.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्षत torn, broken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षतयोनि|अक्षतयोनिः
अक्षतयोनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A virgin.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षत and योनि pudendum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदर्शक|अक्षदर्शकः
अक्षदर्शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a law suit, दर्शक who sees; from दृश to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यू
अक्षद्यू<BR>m. (-द्यूः)<BR>A gambler, a dicer.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष dice and द्यू who plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यूत
अक्षद्यूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A gambler, a dicer.<BR>n. (-तंः)<BR>Gambling.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and द्यूत play or who plays: also अक्षद्यूत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षद्यूतिक
अक्षद्यूतिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Dispute at play.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and द्यूत with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदृश्
अक्षदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a law suit, and दृश् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षदेविन्
अक्षदेविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A gamester.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a dice, and देविन् a player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधर|अक्षधरः
अक्षधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Trophis aspera.) See साखोट.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>One who holds dice &c.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधूर्त्त|अक्षधूर्त|अक्षधूर्तः|अक्षधूर्त्तः
अक्षधूर्त्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A gamester, a gambler.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष dice, and धूचै a rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=003" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षधूर्त्तिल|अक्षधूर्तिल|अक्षधूर्तिलः
अक्षधूर्त्तिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bull, an ox.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a cart, धूर् its forepart, or धुर् a load, and तिल affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाट|अक्षपाटः
अक्षपाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An arena, a boxing or wrestling ground; also read अक्षवाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाटक|अक्षपाटकः
अक्षपाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष law suit, and पाट to arrange, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाटिक
अक्षपाटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>as before with टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षपाद|अक्षपादः
अक्षपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष contest, and पाद who goes; the Nyāya is the logical school; also आक्षपाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षभाग|अक्षभागः
अक्षभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A degree of latitude.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षम|अक्षमः
अक्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Impatient, intolerant.<BR>2 Unable, incompetent, impotent.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Impatience, intolerance.<BR>2 Envy, impatience of another's success.<BR>3 Inability, incapacity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षमा patience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमता
अक्षमता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Impatience, &c. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमत्व
अक्षमत्व<BR>m. (-त्वं)<BR>Impatience, &c. See अक्षम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षमाला
अक्षमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A rosary, a string of beads, especially of the seeds of the Eleocarpus.<BR>2 The name of ARUNDHATĪ, wife of VAŚIṢṬHA, (from her wearing a rosary.)<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a kind of seed or bead, and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षय|अक्षयः
अक्षय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Durable, permanent, imperishable.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The seventh day of a lunar month, which happens on a Sunday or Monday, and the fourth, which falls on a Wednesday.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्षै to waste or decay, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयता
अक्षयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Durability, imperishableness.<BR>E.<BR>ता added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयतृतीया
अक्षयतृतीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The third day of the lunar half of the month Vaiśākha. (April-May.)<BR>E.<BR>अक्षय durable, and तृतीया the third day: the consequences of meritorious actions performed on this day being permanent, as it is the first day of the Satya Yuga or the anniversary of creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयत्व
अक्षयत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Imperishableness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अक्षय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षयलोक|अक्षयलोकः
अक्षयलोक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>Heaven, the imperishable world or region.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षय and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षर|अक्षरं|अक्षरः
अक्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>BRAHM, the supreme being, (in this sense it is sometimes mas.)<BR>2 Eternal beatitude, or exemption from further transmigration.<BR>3 Religious austerity.<BR>4 Moral merit.<BR>5 The sky or atmosphere.<BR>6 A letter of the alphabet.<BR>7 A plant. (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>8 Water (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Unalterable.<BR>2 Unperishable, undecayable^1.<BR>E.<BR>अशू to pervade, and सर Uṇādi affix.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचञ्च|अक्षरचञ्चः
अक्षरचञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर letter, and चञ्च affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचण|अक्षरचणः
अक्षरचण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A scribe.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and चण affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचन|अक्षरचनः
अक्षरचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A scribe.<BR>E.<BR>See the last word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरचुञ्चु|अक्षरचुंचु|अक्षरचुञ्चुः
अक्षरचुञ्चु<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A scribe, a writer. See अक्षरचञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजननी
अक्षरजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and जननी a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरजीवक|अक्षरजीवकः
अक्षरजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A scribe.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and जीवक who lives, i. e. who gets a livelihood by letters; also अक्षरजीविक and अक्षरजीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरतूलिका
अक्षरतूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and तूलिका a brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरविन्यास|अक्षरविन्यासः
अक्षरविन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Scripture, a writing.<BR>2 The alphabet.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and विन्यास assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरमुख|अक्षरमुखः
अक्षरमुख<BR>(-खः)<BR>A scholar, a student.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and मुख commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षरसंस्थान|अक्षरसंस्थानं
अक्षरसंस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Scripture, a writing.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षर a letter, and अंस्थान placing, collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षवत्|अक्षवन्त्
अक्षवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a die, &c.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Gaming, playing with dice.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a die, and मतुप् possessive affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षवाट|अक्षवाटः
अक्षवाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An amphitheatre for wrestling, the arena of a gymnasium.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष contest, and वाट an enclosure, an area.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षविद्
अक्षविद्<BR>mfn. (-वित्)<BR>Versed in law, or in play.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष law or dice, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षसूत्र|अक्षसूत्रं
अक्षसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A rosary, a string of elaeocarpus^1 seeds so used.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and सूत्र a thread.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षांश|अक्षांशः
अक्षांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A degree of latitude.<BR>E.<BR>अंक्ष and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्र
अक्षाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>1 The fore part of a car.<BR>2 The axle or bar to which the wheels are attached.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष and अग्र fore part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षाग्रकीलक|अक्षाग्रकीलकः
अक्षाग्रकीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The pin of the axle of a carriage, the linchpin, also one at the extremity of the pole.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a cart, अग्र fore part, and कीलक a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षान्ति|अक्षांति|अक्षांतिः|अक्षान्तिः
अक्षान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Impatience, intolerance.<BR>2 Envy, impatience of another's superiority or success.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and क्षान्ति sufferance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षारलवण|अक्षारलवणं
अक्षारलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Such food as may be eaten during a season of mourning, religious observance, &c. as cow's milk, ghee, rice, kidney-beans, barley, sesamum, and sea or river salt.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षार alkali, लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षि
अक्षि<BR>n. (-क्षि)<BR>The eye.<BR>E.<BR>अश to pervade, and सि affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिक|अक्षिकः
अक्षिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis.) See also अक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिकूटक|अक्षिकूटकः
अक्षिकूटक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>The eye-ball.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि the eye, and कूटक a globe, or ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगोल|अक्षिगोलः
अक्षिगोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The ball or globe of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि and गोल ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिगत|अक्षिगतः
अक्षिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hateful, hated, disliked.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि the eye, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षितारा
अक्षितारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The pupil of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपक्ष्मन्
अक्षिपक्ष्मन्<BR>n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>The eye lash.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि and पलक्ष्मन् lash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिपटल
अक्षिपटल<BR>n. (-ल)<BR>A coat of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि and पटल a coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिभेषज|अक्षिभेषजः
अक्षिभेषज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A tree, (Pale Lodh.) See गालव.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Any medicament or collyrium for the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि the eye, and भेषज a remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिव|अक्षिवः
अक्षिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant. (Morunga).<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sea-salt. See अक्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षिविकूशित
अक्षिविकूशित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A glance or side look; one with the eye lids partly closed.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षि the eye, and कूशित from कूश to contract, with वि prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षीव|अक्षीवं|अक्षीवः
अक्षीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant. (Guilandina or Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sea-salt.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष to pervade, ईव aff.: it is also written अक्षिव and अक्षीव.<BR>mfn. (-व-वा-वं)<BR>Sober, not intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>neg. and क्षीव intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुण्ण|अक्षुण्णः
अक्षुण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Unpared, uncut, not comminuted.<BR>2 Inexpert.<BR>3 Unconquered.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षुण्ण cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुण्णता
अक्षुण्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Entireness, fulness.<BR>2 Want of practice or conversancy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षुण्णता spareness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षुब्ध|अक्षुब्धः
अक्षुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Unshaken, undisturbed, unagitated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षब्ध shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=004" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोट|अक्षोटः
अक्षोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A tree, (described as a Pilu, growing in the hills.) See पीलु.<BR>2 A walnut.<BR>3 A tree bearing an oily nut, (Aleurites triloba.) Also written आखोट.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष to pervade, and ओट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोड|अक्षोडः
अक्षोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>See the preceding word, also आखोड.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष to pervade, and ओड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोडक|अक्षोडकः
अक्षोडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See अक्षोड.<BR>E.<BR>अक्षोड and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभ|अक्षोभः
अक्षोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Firmness, absence of agitation.<BR>2 The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Unshaken, unagitated.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. क्षोभ shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षोभित
अक्षोभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unshaken, unagitated, firm.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षोभित shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्षौहिणी
अक्षौहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A complete army, consisting of 1,09,350 foot, 65,610 horse, 21,870 chariots, and 21,870 elephants.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a carriage, ऊहिणी assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्ष्ण|अक्ष्णं
अक्ष्ण^1<BR>n. (-क्ष्णं)<BR>Time.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, and क्स्न Uṇādi aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160315. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/252. note: 'zn' usually not possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखट्टि|अखट्टिः
अखट्टि<BR>m. (-ट्टिः)<BR>Childish fancy, whim, caprice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and खट to desire, undesirable by the wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्ड|अखंड|अखण्डः
अखण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>All, entire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डन|अखंडन|अखण्डनः
अखण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 Leaving entire.<BR>3 Admitting, non-refutation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खडि to break, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डित|अखंडित
अखण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unbroken, undivided.<BR>2 Undisturbed, uninterrupted, continuous.<BR>3 Unrefuted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खण्डित divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखण्डितर्त्तु|अखण्डितर्तु|अखण्डितर्तुः|अखण्डितर्त्तुः
अखण्डितर्त्तु<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तुः-र्त्तुः-र्त्तु)<BR>Fruitful, bearing fruit in due season.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खण्डित broken, and ऋतु season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखात|अखातं|अखातः
अखात<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 A natural pond or lake.<BR>2 A pool before a temple. Sometimes written आखात.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and खात dug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखाद्य|अखाद्यं
अखाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Improper to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खाद्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखादित
अखादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uneaten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खादित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिन्न
अखिन्न<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unwearied, indefatigable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. खिन्न wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अखिल|अखिलं
अखिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>All, entire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and खिल separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्यात|अख्यातः
अख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unknown, obscure, not famous or notorious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ख्यात famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अख्याति|अख्यातिः
अख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Disrepute, want of fame.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग|अगः
अग<BR>r. 1st cl. (अगति)<BR>To wind or move tortuously. See अक.<BR>With an indicatory इ। अगि<BR>(अंगति)<BR>To go, move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग|अगः
अग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A snake.<BR>5 Moving crookedly, twining, twisting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ग who goes, from गम to go, or अग to go tortuously, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगच्छ|अगच्छः|अगछ
अगच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and गच्छ, from गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगज|अगजं
अगज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Mountainous, produced on a mountain.<BR>2 Vegetable, produced from a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अग and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगणनीय
अगणनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be numbered or reckoned, also अगण्य, अगणितव्य, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गणनीय to be numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगणित
अगणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not reckoned, uncounted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गणित counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगद|अगदः
अगद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A medicament, a medicine, a drug.<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Well, healthy, free from disease.<BR>2 Wholesome, salubrious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and गद disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगदङ्कार|अगदंकार|अगदंकारः|अगदङ्कारः
अगदङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A physician.<BR>E.<BR>अगद well, healthy, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगन्तव्य
अगन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Not to be visited or approached, also अगमनीय, अगम्य, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गन्तव्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम|अगमः
अगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्य|अगम्यं
अगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Not to be visited or approached.<BR>2 Difficult of acquirement, unattainable.<BR>3 Unequalled, unsurpassable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गम्य to be gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगम्यरूप
अगम्यरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Of superior and unequalled form or nature.<BR>E.<BR>अगम्य and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरी
अगरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of grass, vulg. Deotar. See देवताड.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and गर poison: an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगरु
अगरु<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>Agallochum, (Aquilaria agallocha, Rox.) See अगुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगर्व्व|अगर्व
अगर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Modest, humble, void of pride.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्ति|अगस्तिः
अगस्ति<BR>m. (-स्तिः)<BR>1 The name of a saint, celebrated in Hindu mythology, more usually entitled AGASTYA, the son of both MITRA and VARUṆA, by URVAŚĪ; he is represented of short stature, and is said by some to have been born in a water jar: he is famed for having swallowed the ocean, when it had given him offence; at his command also, the VINDHYA range of mountains prostrated itself, and so remains; hence his present appellation: he is also considered as the regent of the star Canopus.<BR>2 The name of a tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>अग a mountain, and स्ति, with an adventitious meaning, to fix, or in the second instance, to be fixed; also अग as before, and स्ति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्तिद्रु|अगस्तिद्रुः
अगस्तिद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.) See अगस्ति.<BR>E.<BR>अगस्ति, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगस्त्य|अगस्त्यः
अगस्त्य<BR>m. (-स्त्यः)<BR>1 The name of a saint.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 The star Canopus. See अगलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगात्मजा
अगात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ, the daughter of the mountain or Himālaya.<BR>E.<BR>अग a mountain, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाध|अगाधं|अगाधः
अगाध<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>A hole, a chasm.<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Very deep, bottomless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गाध fixed place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधजल|अगाधजलः
अगाधजल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lake.<BR>E.<BR>अगाध deep, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधता
अगाधता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Depth.<BR>E.<BR>अगाध and ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगाधत्व
अगाधत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Depth.<BR>E.<BR>अगाध and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगार|अगारं
अगार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A house. See आगार.<BR>E.<BR>अग a mountain, and ऋ to go; rising like a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिन|अगिनः
अगिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अग to go, इन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगिर|अगिरः
अगिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A demon.<BR>E.<BR>अग to go, and इर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुण|अगुणः
अगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A defect, a fault.<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Void of good qualities, bad.<BR>2 Void of attributes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गुण qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणता
अगुणता<BR>(-ता)<BR>Absence of all good qualities; also अगुणत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गुण with ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुणवादिन्
अगुणवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Censorious, pointing out defects.<BR>E.<BR>अगुण and वादिन् declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=005" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरु|अगुरुः
अगुरु<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>1 A fragrant wood, aloe wood, or agallochum, (Aquilaria agallocha, Rox.)<BR>2 Another tree which produces Bdellium, (Amyris agallocha.)<BR>3 A timber tree, commonly Sisū, (Dalbergia sisu, Rox.)<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रू or-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>Light, not heavy.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and गुरु heavy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुप्त
अगुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Unhidden, unconcealed.<BR>2 One who cannot keep a secret.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगुरुशिंशपा
अगुरुशिंशपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A timber tree, (Dalbergia sisu.) The best authorities consider this as formed of two distinct words. See अगुरु and शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढ
अगूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Unhidden, unconcealed, manifest, evident.<BR>2 One who is not secret.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गूढ hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढगन्ध|अगूढगन्धं|अगूढगन्धः
अगूढगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>अगूढ and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगूढभाव
अगूढभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Open, honest, candid; one whose purpose or inclinations are evident.<BR>E.<BR>अगूढ and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगोचर|अगोचरः
अगोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Covert, unseen, unwitnessed.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Absence, unconsciousness; not being witnessed or known.<BR>2 Any act or event not the object of the senses.<BR>3 The imperceptible, BRAHMA, or the invisible Supreme.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. गोचर object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अगौकस्
अगौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 The Śarabha, a fabulous animal with eight legs.<BR>E.<BR>अग a tree or mountain, ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नायी
अग्नायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 A goddess, the wife of AGNI, the deity of fire, and presiding over prayers accompanied with burnt offerings.<BR>2 The Tretā or second age of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and fem. aff. ङीप्^1, with आय substituted for ऐ inserted.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नि|अग्निः
अग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 Fire, always associated with the idea of the deity presiding over it, and who is worshipped by the Hindus. AGNI is also regent of the south-east quarter.<BR>2 A consecrated fire.<BR>3 The fire of the stomach, the digestive faculty, appetite.<BR>4 Bile.<BR>5 Gold.<BR>6 A plant of which the fruit has escharotic properties, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR>7 Another plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग to mark, and नि Uṇādi aff, ङ being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निक|अग्निकः
अग्निक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An insect of a scarlet color, the lady-bird.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and क aff. resembling fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकण|अग्निकणः
अग्निकण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A spark.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and कण a small particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकारिका
अग्निकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Maintaining a sacrificial fire, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and कारिका making, from कृ to do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकारित
अग्निकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused by fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and कारित caused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकार्य्य|अग्निकार्य|अग्निकार्य्यं
अग्निकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकाष्ठ|अग्निकाष्ठं
अग्निकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Agallochum. See अगुरु.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकुक्कुट|अग्निकुक्कुटः
अग्निकुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A firebrand, a lighted wisp of straw.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and कुक्कुट a wisp of lighted straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकृत|अग्निकृतः
अग्निकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done with or made by fire, offered with fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निकोण|अग्निकोणं|अग्निकोणः
अग्निकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The east.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and कोण corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निक्रीडा
अग्निक्रीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Illuminations, fireworks, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and क्रीडा play<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निगर्भ|अग्निगर्भः
अग्निगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 The sun-stone, crystal, or a fabulous gem; supposed to contain and impart solar heat.<BR>2 A plant.<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>The name of another plant.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and गर्भ the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निचित्
अग्निचित्<BR>m. (-चित्)<BR>A householder who has placed and consecrated a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and चित् who collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निचित्या
अग्निचित्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and चित्या collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निज|अग्निजः
अग्निज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant used in medicine, of stimulant properties.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Produced by or producing fire, also अग्निजात.<BR>2 Digestive.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रि fire, and ज who or what is born, from जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजार|अग्निजारः
अग्निजार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A medicinal plant. See अग्निज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजाल|अग्निजालः
अग्निजाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A medicinal plant. See अग्निज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निजिह्वा
अग्निजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>1 A medicinal plant. See लाङ्गलिकी.<BR>2 A flame of fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, and जिह्वा the tongue, growing like a flame of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निज्वाला
अग्निज्वाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A flame of fire.<BR>2 A plant bearing red blossoms used by dyers, (Grislea tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>3 Another plant, commonly Jalapippalī.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and ज्वाला flame, from the fiery colour of its blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नित्रेता
अग्नित्रेता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The aggregate of the three fires maintained by the Brahman householder, the Gārhapatya or domestic, Ahavanīya or consecrated, and Dakṣiṇa or southern.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and त्रेता triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निद
अग्निद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Setting on fire, incendiary.<BR>2 Supplying with fire.<BR>3 Stomachic, tonic, digestive.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदमनी
अग्निदमनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A medicinal plant, of narcotic properties, (Solanum jacquini.) See कण्ठकारिका.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रि bile, and दमनी what tames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदग्ध
अग्निदग्ध<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>A Pitṛ or progenitor to whom oblations are made.<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Burnt.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदीप्त
अग्निदीप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Blazing, on fire.<BR>2 Digestive.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>The name of a plant.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and दीप्त inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदेव|अग्निदेवः
अग्निदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 AGNI, the god of fire.<BR>2 A worshipper of fire.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A name of the third lunar mansion, identified with the Pleiades: AGNI being the ruling deity of the constellation, Also अग्निदेवता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निदैवत्य
अग्निदैवत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>The supremacy or divinity of fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and दैवत्य divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निनिर्य्यास|अग्निनिर्यास|अग्निनिर्यासः|अग्निनिर्य्यासः
अग्निनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The name of a plant, also अग्निजार.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and निर्य्यास decoction or extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपक्व
अग्निपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Cooked or dressed with fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and पक्क mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपरिच्छद|अग्निपरिच्छदः
अग्निपरिच्छद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The implements and apparatus used in oblations to fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and परिच्छद accompaniments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निपरीक्षा
अग्निपरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>The fiery ordeal, by a heated iron or boiling oil, or passing through fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निप्रस्तर|अग्निप्रस्तरः
अग्निप्रस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire-stone, flint, or any stone producing fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and प्रस्तर a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभ|अग्निभं
अग्निभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and भ for भा lustre, brilliant as fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभू
अग्निभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A name of SKANDA, the Hindu deity of war. See कार्त्तिकेय and स्कन्द.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and भू being; being, or born, from fire. ŚIVA having cast his seed into flame, for the purpose of generating a warrior, able to subdue TĀRAKA, a demon, SKANDA was produced.<BR>n. (-भु)<BR>Water, which is generated, in the Hindu cosmogony, from fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=006" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निभूति|अग्निभूतिः
अग्निभूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A proper name. One of the pupils of the last Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and भूति superhuman power: equal to AGNI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमणि|अग्निमणिः
अग्निमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun-stone.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and मणि a jewel or gem, brilliant as fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमत्|अग्निमन्त्
अग्निमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत)<BR>1 Having a consecrated fire.<BR>2 Having fire in general.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमन्थ|अग्निमन्थः
अग्निमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A small tree, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and मन्य churning, because fire is produced by friction of two pieces of its wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमारुति|अग्निमारुतिः
अग्निमारुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of the saint, AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, i. e. the fire of the stomach, the digestive faculty, and मारुति a name of HANUMĀN; because the saint could digest as well as the monkey: the epithet alludes to a story of his devouring and digesting VĀTĀPI, a demon, who had assumed the form of a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निमुख|अग्निमुखः
अग्निमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and मुख the mouth; oblations to the gods passing through fire as their mouths.<BR>3 A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>4 Marking nut, (Semecarpus anacardium.) (In this sense it is also fem. -खी.)<BR>E.<BR>as before, from its marking like fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरक्षण|अग्निरक्षणं
अग्निरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Maintenance of a sacred fire; preserving a fire in a family for perpetuity, which supplies that lighted on occasions of worship.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरक्षित
अग्निरक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Maintaining a sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and रक्षित preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरहित
अग्निरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Being without fire, especially a sacred fire.<BR>2 Devoid of appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and रहित lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरजस्
अग्निरजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>An insect of a scarlet color.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and रजस् dust or farina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निरुहा
अग्निरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The name of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्ण|अग्निवर्ण्ण
अग्निवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Hot, scalding, scorching.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वर्ण quality; of the property of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्द्धक
अग्निवर्द्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Tonic, stomachic.<BR>2 Feeding or exciting fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वर्द्धक what augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवर्द्धन
अग्निवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Exciting fire.<BR>2 Improving the appetite.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A stomachic or any thing improving the appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and बर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवल्लभ|अग्निवल्लभः
अग्निवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Resin, pitch.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वल्लभ a friend, from its exciting or befriending fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवाण
अग्निवाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fiery arrow, a rocket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवाह|अग्निवाहः
अग्निवाह<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वाह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवाहु
अग्निवाहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निविसर्प|अग्निविसर्पः
अग्निविसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>Pain from a boil.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and विसर्प a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवीज|अग्निवीजं
अग्निवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवीर्य्य|अग्निवीर्य|अग्निवीर्य्यं
अग्निवीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निवृद्धि
अग्निवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Improved digestion, appetite.<BR>2 Increase of fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशिख|अग्निशिखं|अग्निशिखः
अग्निशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A lamp.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A fiery arrow, a rocket.<BR>4 The Safflower plant, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>mn. (-खः-खं)<BR>Saffron, the plant and die.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 Flame.<BR>2 A plant. (Gloriosa superba.)<BR>3 A medicinal plant, (Menispermum cordifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and शिखा a crest or flame or splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निशेखर|अग्निशेखरं|अग्निशेखरः
अग्निशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टुत्
अग्निष्टुत्<BR>f. (-ष्टुत)<BR>An expiatory sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and ष्टु to sacrifice, aff. क्विप् with तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्टोम|अग्निष्टोमः
अग्निष्टोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sacrifice, or rather a series of offerings to fire for five days, to be celebrated in the spring.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and स्तोम oblation, burnt-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्ठ|अग्निष्ठः
अग्निष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>An iron frying-pan.<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Placed in or on fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and ष्ठ what stays or remains, from स्था to stand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निष्वात्त|अग्निष्वात्तः
अग्निष्वात्त<BR>m. pl. (-त्ताः)<BR>Demigods or manes to whom funeral oblations are presented. They are said to be the sons of MARĪCI, and progenitors especially of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, स्व own, and आत्त taken, who receive what is offered them by fire as their own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसंस्कार|अग्निसंस्कारः
अग्निसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Any ceremony performed with the consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, संस्कार purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसख|अग्निसखः
अग्निसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The wind.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and सखि friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसम्भव|अग्निसंभव|अग्निसम्भवः
अग्निसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Wild safflower.<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Originating from fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसहाय|अग्निसहायः
अग्निसहाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A pigeon.<BR>2 The wind.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and सहाय a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निसार|अग्निसारं|अग्निसारः
अग्निसार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A medicinal application to the eyes, a collyrium from the calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and सार strength, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निहोत्र|अग्निहोत्रं|अग्निहोत्रः
अग्निहोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Maintenance of a perpetual or sacred fire.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and होत्र oblation with fire, burnt offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्निहोत्रिन्
अग्निहोत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>One who maintains a perpetual and sacred fire; this is sometimes read अग्निहोतृ. nom. (-ता)<BR>E.<BR>अग्निहोत्र, and णिनि, or हु to sacrifice, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीध्
अग्नीध्<BR>m. (-ग्नीत्)<BR>A priest who attends the fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, ईन्ध to excite, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीध्र|अग्नीध्रः
अग्नीध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>An officiating priest, whose duty is to attend the fire.<BR>f. (ध्रा)<BR>Exciting the sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and ईन्ध, to light or kindle; and the aff. रन्; the न of इन्ध being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्नीन्धन|अग्नीन्धनं|अग्नीन्धनः
अग्नीन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Exciting a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and इन्धन kindling, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यभाव
अग्न्यभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Loss or extinction of the sacred fire.<BR>2 Loss of appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यस्त्र|अग्न्यस्त्रं
अग्न्यस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Fire-arms; in poetry, it is usually applied to a superhuman power over the element of fire, but occasionally indicates, apparently, a rocket.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यागार|अग्न्यागारः
अग्न्यागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fire-temple; a chamber or building where the sacred fire is kept.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याधान|अग्न्याधानं
अग्न्याधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Maintenance of a perpetual and sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and आधान preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याधेय|अग्न्याधेयः
अग्न्याधेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Consecration of a perpetual fire.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, आधेय placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्यालय|अग्न्यालयः
अग्न्यालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A place in which consecrated fire is kept.<BR>2 A hole, with compartments of prescribed dimensions and shape, for the several sacred fires.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्याहित
अग्न्याहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A householder who maintains a perpetual fire; also आहिताग्नि.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि, आहित preserved; by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्न्युत्पात|अग्न्युत्पातः
अग्न्युत्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A fiery meteor, a falling star, a comet.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि and उत्पात् portent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=007" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र|अग्रं|अग्रः
अग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Chief, principal.<BR>2 Prior, first.<BR>3 Excessive, more, much.<BR>4 Excellent, best.<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>1 Front, fore part.<BR>2 Top, summit, upper part.<BR>3 End, point.<BR>4 Goal, resting place.<BR>5 Assemblage, multitude.<BR>6 A weight equal to one Pala.<BR>7 Limited alms, (four mouthfuls.)<BR>8 (In astronomy) the sun's amplitude.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and the Uṇādi aff. रन् the nasal of the derivative is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रकर|अग्रकरः
अग्रकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The tip of the extended hand.<BR>2 The right or better hand.<BR>3 The extremity of a ray of light; the focal point.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, कर hand or ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रगण्य|अग्रगण्यः
अग्रगण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>To be reckoned or considered as first or best.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and गण्य to be counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रगामिन्
अग्रगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Preceding; going before.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रज|अग्रजः
अग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 An elder brother; the first-born.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>First-born or produced.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र first, ज who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजङ्घा
अग्रजङ्घा<BR>f. (-ङ्घा)<BR>The fore part of the thigh.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र the first part, and जङ्घा thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजन्मन्
अग्रजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>1 A priest or Brahman; a man of the sacerdotal tribe.<BR>2 An elder brother or first-born.<BR>3 BRAHMĀ, the first-born of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र first or best, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजातक|अग्रजातकः
अग्रजातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman; a man of the first class.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, and जातक who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रजाति|अग्रजातिः
अग्रजाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A Brahman; a man of the first class.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and जाति race, class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रज्या
अग्रज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>(In astronomy) Sine of the amplitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रणी
अग्रणी<BR>mfn. (-णीः-णीः-णि)<BR>First, principal.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and नी, from णीञ्^1 to lead, aff. क्विप्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: Cf WIL and WIL1819 णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतःसर|अग्रतःसरः
अग्रतःसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Going before, preceding.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A leader.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रतस्, and सर, who goes, from सृ with अच् or ट aff. to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रतस्
अग्रतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Before, in front.<BR>2 Before in rank, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रदानिन्
अग्रदानिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>A degraded Brahman; one who receives the presents of Śūdras, or things first offered to the deceased.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, दान gift, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रनिरूपण
अग्रनिरूपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Determining beforehand, prophecy, predestination.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, निरूपण declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपर्णी
अग्रपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, cowage^1, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, पर्ण leaf.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रपाणि|अग्रपाणिः
अग्रपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 The tip of the hand.<BR>2 The right hand.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभाग|अग्रभागः
अग्रभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Part of the top or end.<BR>2 Fore or top part.<BR>3 (In astronomy) Degree of amplitude, also अग्रांशः.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रभूमि|अग्रभूमिः
अग्रभूमि<BR>mf. (मिः)<BR>A goal, an object, the place or thing to be attained.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र before, भूमि earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रमांस
अग्रमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The heart.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र principal, and मांस, flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रयान|अग्रयानं
अग्रयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Advancing before an army, for the purpose of defiance; military ardor or daring.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रवीज|अग्रवीजः
अग्रवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A viviparous plant, as the Gomphroena globosa, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र in front, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसन्धानी|अग्रसंधानी
अग्रसन्धानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The register of human actions, kept by YAMA, the judge of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र first, and सं, preposition, with धा to take; recording all actions from the original birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रसर|अग्रसरः
अग्रसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Preceding, going before, a leader.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रह|अग्रहः
अग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An anchorite, a man who has retired from the world.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ग्रह a house, being no longer a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहणीय
अग्रहणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be taken, accepted or acquired.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ग्रहणीय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहस्त|अग्रहस्तः
अग्रहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>1 The tip of the extended hand.<BR>2 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>2 The right or better hand.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, हल hand, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहायण|अग्रहायणः
अग्रहायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The name of a month; the eighth of the lunar year of the Hindus, when the moon is full near the head of Orion, or about November-December.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and हायन, year; according to the ancient system, the first month of the Hindu year: also आग्रहायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रहार|अग्रहारः
अग्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An endowment of lands or villages conferred upon Brahmans.<BR>2 A field of corn.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र chief (tribe), हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रांश
अग्रांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>See अग्रभाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रांशु|अग्रांशुः
अग्रांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The extreme ray or point of a ray of light, the focal point.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्राह्य|अग्राह्यं
अग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 Not fit or proper to be accepted.<BR>2 Not to be attained.<BR>3 Not to be trusted or consented to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिम|अग्रिमः
अग्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Chief, principal, best.<BR>2 Elder, elder born.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The name of a fruit, (Annona reticulata.) See लवनी.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रिय|अग्रियं|अग्रियः
अग्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An elder brother.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र and इय or ईय aff. whence also अग्रीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रु|अग्रुः
अग्रु<BR>f. (-ग्रुः)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>अग to go, and रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगा
अग्रेगा<BR>m. (-गाः)<BR>A leader, a preceder.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे in front, गा who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेगू
अग्रेगू<BR>m. (-गूः)<BR>A leader.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे, ग from गम to go, and ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेदिधिषु|अग्रेदिधिषुः
अग्रेदिधिषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>A man of either of the three first classes, whose wife has been before married, and has borne him children.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे principal, and दिघिषु the husband of a twice married woman.<BR>f. (-षुः)<BR>A younger sister married before her elder; also अग्रेदिघिषू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेवन
अग्रेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The skirts of a wood.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे the fore-part, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसर|अग्रेसरः
अग्रेसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A leader.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Preceding, going before.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे in front, and सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्रेसरिक|अग्रेसरिकः
अग्रेसरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A leader.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रे in front, and सरिक who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अग्र्य|अग्र्यः
अग्र्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं)<BR>Chief, principal.<BR>m. (-ग्र्यः)<BR>An elder brother.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ|अघं|अघः
अघ<BR>r. 1st cl. With an indicatory इ। यघि (अंघति.)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To go swiftly.<BR>3 To begin moving.<BR>4 To begin.<BR>5 To blame or censure.<BR>r. 10th cl. (अघयति)<BR>To sin, to commit sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ|अघं|अघः
अघ<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Pain.<BR>3 Passion.<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>Name of a demon; the general of KAṂSA.<BR>E.<BR>अघ to go, and अच् affix, removed by charity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=008" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशक
अघनाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Purifying, freeing from sin.<BR>E.<BR>अघ, and नाशक what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघनाशन|अघनाशनः
अघनाशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Purifying, freeing from sin.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 An expiator.<BR>E.<BR>अघ and नाशन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमय
अघमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sinful, identical with or fruitful in sin.<BR>E.<BR>अघ and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघमर्षण|अघमर्षणं
अघमर्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>An expiatory prayer: reciting mentally a particular passage from the Vedas, while a little water, in the palm of the right hand, is held to the nose; this forms a part of the daily ceremonies of the Brahmans.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The author of the passage recited upon the above occasion.<BR>E.<BR>अघ sin, and मृष to bear with, or to sprinkle, युच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्म्म|अघर्म
अघर्म्म<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मा-र्म्मं)<BR>Cool, not warm.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. घर्म्म hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघर्म्मधामन्|अघर्मधामन्
अघर्म्मधामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The moon, as the source of coolness.<BR>E.<BR>अघर्म्म cool, धामन् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघवत्|अघवन्त्
अघवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wicked, vicious, sinful.<BR>E.<BR>अघ sin, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघाह|अघाहः
अघाह<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>Time or day of impurity, consequent on the death of a relative, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अघ and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघृण
अघृण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unkind, cruel.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. घृणा compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोर|अघोरः
अघोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Formidable, terrible.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A worshipper of ŚIVA and DEVĪ in their terrific forms.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The fourteenth day of the dark half of the month Bhadra, upon which ŚIVA is worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>अ implying resemblance, and धोर formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोरपथिन्
अघोरपथिन्<BR>m. (-पन्थ)<BR>A worshipper of the terrific forms of SIVA and DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अघोर and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोष|अघोषः
अघोष<BR>mfn. (-ष-षा-षं)<BR>1 Without noise.<BR>2 Without cowherd, (a country.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. घोष noise, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघोस्
अघोस्<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle: the final स is usually dropped in composition, as अघोयज, ho, pay worship.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हन to kill, and ओस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अघ्न
अघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-घ्ना)<BR>A cow. घ्न<BR>f. (घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>1 Inviolable, not to be slain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हन to kill, and अक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क|अंक|अंकः|अङ्कः
अङ्क<BR>(क, त) r. 10th cl. (अङ्कयति)<BR>1 To number or count.<BR>2 To mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क|अंक|अंकः|अङ्कः
अङ्क<BR>n. (-ङ्कं)<BR>1 A mark or spot.<BR>2 The flank or part above the hips.<BR>3 A species of dramatic entertainment.<BR>4 The act of a play, &c.<BR>5 Fault, offence.<BR>6 A line, a stroke.<BR>7 Mimic war or conflict.<BR>8 Ornament, decoration.<BR>9 Place, abode.<BR>10 Proximity, proximate.<BR>11 A chapter or section.<BR>12 The body.<BR>13 A cypher, an arithmetical sign.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्च to go, and the Uṇādi affix क; or अङ्क to stain or spot, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कति|अंकति|अंकतिः|अङ्कतिः
अङ्कति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A Brahman who maintains a sacred fire.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्च to go, and the Uṇādi aff. अति; च being changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कन|अंकन|अंकनं|अङ्कनं
अङ्कन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cyphering, writing or making cyphers.<BR>2 Stamping, impressing, making marks.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कनीय
अङ्कनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be marked.<BR>2 To be numbered.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपरिवर्त्तन|अङ्कपरिवर्तन
अङ्कपरिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Turning on the side.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क and परिवर्त्तन turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपालिका|अंकपालिका
अङ्कपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An embrace, embracing.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क the flank, and पालिका or पाली, nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कपाली|अंकपाली
अङ्कपाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 An embrace, embracing.<BR>2 A nurse.<BR>3 A plant, (Piring or Medicago esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>See अङ्कपालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कभाज्|अंकभाज्
अङ्कभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Resting or placed upon the side or hip.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क and भाज् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कयितव्य
अङ्कयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be marked.<BR>2 To be numbered.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कविद्या|अंकविद्या
अङ्कविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Arithmetic.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कित|अङ्कितः
अङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Marked, spotted.<BR>2 Counted, numbered.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark, and participial aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्की|अंकी
अङ्की<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A small oblong drum.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क the hip or flank, being carried upon that part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुट|अंकुट|अंकुटः|अङ्कुटः
अङ्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A key.<BR>E.<BR>अकि to go, उटि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुर|अंकुर|अंकुरं|अंकुरः|अङ्कुरः
अङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A shoot or sprout.<BR>2 The hair of the body.<BR>3 Blood.<BR>4 Water.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to stain, and Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरक|अंकुरकः|अङ्कुरकः
अङ्कुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A nest.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कुर a shoot, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुरित|अंकुरित
अङ्कुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Budded, sprouted, germinated.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कुर and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुश|अंकुश|अंकुशः|अङ्कुशः
अङ्कुश<BR>mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>The hook used to drive an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अक to go, and उशच् Uṇādi aff. with नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशग्रह|अंकुशग्रह|अङ्कुशग्रहः
अङ्कुशग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An elephant-driver.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कुश् —, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशदुर्द्धर
अङ्कुशदुर्द्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A restive elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कुश, and टुर् bad, difficult, धर who holds: who is ill restrained by the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कुशी
अङ्कुशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>One of the twenty-four female deities peculiar to the Jainas, supposed to preside more immediately over human beings.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कुश, and ङीप् fem. aff. having or holding a hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूष|अंकूष|अंकूषः|अङ्कूषः
अङ्कूष<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sprout, a germin.<BR>E.<BR>See अङ्कुर, उ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कूष|अंकूष|अंकूषः|अङ्कूषः
अङ्कूष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>The hook or goad for driving an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>See अङ्कुश, उ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोट|अंकोट|अंकोटः|अङ्कोटः
अङ्कोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant: also अङ्कोठ.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark or stain, ओट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोठ|अंकोठ|अङ्कोठः
अङ्कोठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A plant, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>E.<BR>See अङ्कोट, ठ being used for ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल|अंकोल|अङ्कोलः
अङ्कोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant. See अङ्कोट; also अङ्कालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल्लसार|अङ्कोल्लसारः
अङ्कोल्लसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of poison, probably prepared from the plant अङ्कोल, or अंकोट.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्कोल, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्कोल्लिका
अङ्कोल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क the side, उत् pre. and ल, from ला, to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्क्य|अंक्य|अङ्क्यः
अङ्क्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं)<BR>1 To be counted.<BR>2 To be marked.<BR>m. (-ङ्क्यः)<BR>A small oblong drum. See अङ्की.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्क to mark, aff. यत्; or अङ्क the hip, and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग<BR>(क, त) r. 10th cl. (अंगयति)<BR>1 To mark.<BR>2 To count. See अङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्ग|अंग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A limb or member.<BR>2 A division of Hindu learning, comprehending such science as is considered dependant upon the Vedas, hence also called Vedāṅga; works on six subjects come under this description, viz. pronunciation, grammar, prosody, explanation of obscure terms, description of religious rites, and astronomy.<BR>3 The body.<BR>4 An expedient, a means of success.<BR>5 Mind, understanding.<BR>6 A term in grammar, the inflective root, with the affix subjoined-<BR>7 (Sing. only,) Chief, principal.<BR>8 Inferior, secondary.<BR>9 All [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=10" target="_blank">Page10</a>] the dramatis personoe of a play, except the hero and heroine, the body of the characters.<BR>10 (In rhetoric.) An incidental passion or figure, illustrative of, but subordinate to the main object of the description.<BR>11 A scriptural work in the Jain religion; there are twelve works so named.<BR>m. (ङ्गः)<BR>A country, Bengal proper, including Bhāgalpur.<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Corporeal, embodied.<BR>2 Near, proximate.<BR>ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle.<BR>2 Again, further, the rather.<BR>3 A particle of assent used in composition, with ई substituted for the vowel termination, as in अङ्गीकरण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=009" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गक|अंगक|अंगकं
अङ्गक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The body, &c. See the preceding.<BR>f. (अङ्गिका)<BR>A bodice or jacket.<BR>mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं)<BR>Relating to the body, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गग्रह|अङ्गग्रहः
अङ्गग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Bodily pain.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and ग्रह what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गज|अंगज|अङ्गजं|अङ्गजः
अङ्गज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं).<BR>1 Produced or born of the body.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 Love, desire.<BR>3 The hair of the head.<BR>4 Sickness, disease.<BR>5 A son.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the body, and ज what is born; also similar compounds, as अङ्गजात, अङ्गजन्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गण|अंगण|अंगणं|अङ्गणं
अङ्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A court, or yard. See अङ्गन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गति|अंगति|अंगतिः|अङ्गतिः
अङ्गति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 A Brahman, who has preserved a sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गद|अंगद|अंगदं|अङ्गदं|अङ्गदः
अङ्गद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The name of a celebrated monkey, one of the heroes of the Rāmāyaṇa, the son of BĀLI.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A bracelet worn upon the upper arm.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The female elephant of the south.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the body, and दे to nourish, or दै to cleanse, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन|अंगन|अंगनं|अङ्गनं
अङ्गन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A court or yard.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A woman, a female.<BR>2 The sign Virgo.<BR>3 The female elephant of the north.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनागण|अंगनागण
अङ्गनागण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A number of women.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गना and गण troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाजन|अङ्गनाजनः
अङ्गनाजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A female, a female person.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गना and जन a being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गनाप्रिय|अंगनाप्रिय|अङ्गनाप्रियः
अङ्गनाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Jonesia asoka.) See अशोक.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गना a woman, and प्रिय, beloved; worship being performed by women to this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गन्यास|अंगन्यास|अङ्गन्यासः
अङ्गन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Touching various parts of the body, as a religious ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and न्यास arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गपालि|अंगपालि|अङ्गपालिः
अङ्गपालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and पाल to nourish, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गप्रायश्चित्त
अङ्गप्रायश्चित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Expiation for bodily impurity, especially the oblation offered by the heir at the first funeral obsequies, to remove the impurity contracted during the period of mourning.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग body and प्रायश्चित्त expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गमर्द्द|अङ्गमर्द|अंगमर्द|अङ्गमर्दः|अङ्गमर्द्दः
अङ्गमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A servant, whose business it is to rub and knead the body.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, मृद् to rub, and अच् aff. Also अङ्गमर्द्दकः and अङ्गमर्द्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्त|अङ्गरक्तः
अङ्गरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A plant, vulg. Śuṇḍārocanī. See रक्ताङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and रक्त red, giving a red dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरक्षिणी|अंगरक्षिणी
अङ्गरक्षिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Armour, coat of mail, thick quilting, or an iron netting worn upon the body.<BR>2 A garment.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and रक्षिणी what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराग|अंगराग|अङ्गरागः
अङ्गराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Perfuming the body after cleansing; smearing it with unguents of sandal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and राग colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गराज्|अंगराज्
अङ्गराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A name of KARṆA, king of Aṅga, the son of KUNTĪ by SŪRYA. See कर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the country so named, and राज् a king; also अङ्गराजा and अङ्गराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गरुह|अंगरुह
अङ्गरुह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Hair of the body, wool, fleece, down.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and रुह what rises on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गलोड्य|अङ्गलोड्यः
अङ्गलोड्य<BR>m. (-ड्यः)<BR>Ginger, (Amomum zinziber.) See चिञ्चाटक.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and लोड, to be mad, aff. यत्; exciting or stimulating the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गस्कन्ध|अङ्गस्कन्धः
अङ्गस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A subdivision of a branch of science or philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग a part of science, and स्कन्ध division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गव|अंगवं|अङ्गवः
अङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A dried or withered fruit.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग and य, from वै to dry or wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविकृति|अंगविकृति|अङ्गविकृतिः
अङ्गविकृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Syncope, apoplexy.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and विकृति change of condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गविक्षेप|अंगविक्षेप|अङ्गविक्षेपः
अङ्गविक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Gesture, gesticulation.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and विक्षेप throwing, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गवैकृत|अंगवैकृत|अङ्गवैकृतं
अङ्गवैकृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sign, token, hint.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and वैकृत change of form, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंस्कार|अंगसंस्कार|अङ्गसंस्कारः
अङ्गसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Embellishment of person, dressing, cleansing or perfuming it.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and संस्कार making perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसंहति|अंगसंहति|अङ्गसंहतिः
अङ्गसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Bodily strength, or symmetry.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and संहति compactness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गसङ्ग|अङ्गसंग|अंगसंग|अङ्गसङ्गः
अङ्गसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Bodily union or contact, coition.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and सङ्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहार|अंगहार|अङ्गहारः
अङ्गहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Gesture, gesticulation.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग, and हार taking, moving; also अङ्गहारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहारि|अङ्गहारिः
अङ्गहारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>See अङ्गहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गहीन|अंगहीन|अङ्गहीनः
अङ्गहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Mutilated, maimed, defective.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग a limb, हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाङ्गि|अंगांगि
अङ्गाङ्गि<BR>ind.<BR>Body and body, implying contact or co-operation.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग repeated with इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाङ्गिभाव|अंगांगिभाव|अङ्गाङ्गिभावः
अङ्गाङ्गिभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Personal relation or co-operation.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गाङ्गि, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गाधिप|अंगाधिप|अङ्गाधिपः
अङ्गाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of KARṆA, king of Aṅga. See कर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the country, अधिप a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गार|अंगार|अंगारं|अंगारः|अङ्गारः
अङ्गार<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Charcoal, whether burning or not, but more usually the latter.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of the planet Mars; from his fiery colour.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and आरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारक|अंगारक|अंगारकं|अंगारकः|अङ्गारकः
अङ्गारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The planet Mars.<BR>2 Charcoal, burning or extinguished.<BR>3 Yellow or white amaranth. See कुरुण्ठक.<BR>4 Another plant, (Eclipta or Verbesina prostrata.) See भृङ्गराज.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A medicated oil, prepared by boiling turmeric and various vegetable substances in common oil.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार and कन् affix; resembling a burning brand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारकमणि|अंगारकमणि|अङ्गारकमणिः
अङ्गारकमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गारक, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारधानिका|अंगारधानिका
अङ्गारधानिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small portable fire-place or fire-pan.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and घानिका what holds, from धा root, with the affs. ल्युट्^1, कन् and टाप्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: cf wil1819.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपरिपाचित|अङ्गारपरिपाचितं
अङ्गारपरिपाचित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Roasted food.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and परिपाचित cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपर्ण|अङ्गारपर्णः|अङ्गारपर्ण्ण
अङ्गारपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A name of CITRARATHA, chief of the Gandharbas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=010" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारपुष्प|अङ्गारपुष्पः
अङ्गारपुष्प<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A plant, vulg. Ingua. See इङ्गुदी. The seeds are used for rosaries, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and पुष्प a flower; the flowers supposed to resemble coals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारमञ्जी
अङ्गारमञ्जी<BR>f. (-ञ्जी)<BR>A tree, or shrub, (Cesalpinia bonducella.)<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and मञ्जी a pedicle, compared to a coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारवल्लरी
अङ्गारवल्लरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A species of Karanja, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Ovieda verticillata^1, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार and वल्लरी a compound pedicle.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारवल्ली|अंगारवल्ली
अङ्गारवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>See अङ्गारवल्लरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारशकटी|अंगारशकटी
अङ्गारशकटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A small portable fire-pan.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार and शकटी a little cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारि|अंगारिः|अङ्गारिः
अङ्गारि<BR>f. (रिः)<BR>A small portable fire-pan.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारिका|अंगारिका
अङ्गारिका<BR>f. (-क)<BR>1 The stalk of the Sugarcane.<BR>2 The bud of the Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारिणी|अंगारिणी
अङ्गारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A small portable fire-place.<BR>2 The quarter from which the sun has departed.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and णिनि poss. aff. and fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गारित|अंगारित|अङ्गारितं|अङ्गारितः
अङ्गारित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The early blossom of the Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa).<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Burnt.<BR>2 Charred.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिका|अंगिका
अङ्गिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of bodice or jacket.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the body, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिन्|अंगिन्
अङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Corporeal, bodily.<BR>2 Limbed, having limbs or members.<BR>3 Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गिरस्|अंगिरस्
अङ्गिरस्<BR>m. (-राः)<BR>The name of a Ṛṣi or saint, born of BRAHMĀ, one of the seven principal sages; in one legend identified with fire, and apparently an astronomical personification, having for, his sons UTATHYA and VṚHASPATI, and for daughters Sinīvālī, Kuhū, Rākā, and Anumati.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and असि Uṇādi aff. with इरक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकरण|अंगीकरण|अंगीकरणं
अङ्गीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Promising, agreeing, assenting.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग a particle of assent, करण doing, च्ची inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकार|अंगीकार|अंगीकारः|अङ्गीकारः
अङ्गीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An agreement, a promise.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग a particle of asseveration, and कार making, from कृ to do. घञ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गीकृत|अङ्गीकृतं
अङ्गीकृत<BR>n. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Agreed, promised.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गी as before, and कृत participle of कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरि|अंगुरिः|अङ्गुरिः
अङ्गुरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 A finger.<BR>2 A toe, also written अङ्गुरी. See अङ्गुलि.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग to count, and उरी Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरीय|अंगुरीय|अंगुरीयं|अङ्गुरीयः
अङ्गुरीय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>A finger-ring. See अङ्गुलीयक.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुरी a finger, and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुरीयक|अंगुरीयक|अंगुरीयकं|अङ्गुरीयकं
अङ्गुरीयक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A finger-ring. See अङ्गुरीयक.<BR>E.<BR>कन् affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुल|अंगुल|अंगुलः|अङ्गुलः
अङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The thumb.<BR>2 A finger.<BR>3 A measure of eight barley corns.<BR>4 The name of a saint. See वत्स्यायन.<BR>5 A digit, or one-twelfth part of any dimension.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग to count, and उल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलि|अंगुलि|अंगुलिः|अङ्गुलिः
अङ्गुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 A finger.<BR>2 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>3 A toe; also अङ्गली.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग to count, and उलि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलितोरण|अंगुलितोरण|अङ्गुलितोरणं
अङ्गुलितोरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Three semicircular lines drawn across the forehead, with sandal, &c. a sectarial mark, especially of the followers of Śakti.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि a finger, and तोरण the ornamented arch of a gateway, to which the mark made by the fingers upon the forehead may be compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्र|अंगुलित्र
अङ्गुलित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A guard for the finger, applied to the bowstring used by archers.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and त्र what protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलित्राण|अंगुलित्राण
अङ्गुलित्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>See the last.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and त्राण what protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुख|अंगुलिमुख
अङ्गुलिमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The tip of the finger.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and मुख end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमुद्रा|अंगुलिमुद्रा
अङ्गुलिमुद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A seal ring.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and मुद्रा a seal; also अङ्गुलिमुद्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिमोटन|अंगुलिमोटन|अङ्गुलिमोटनं
अङ्गुलिमोटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cracking, or snapping the finger joints.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and मोटन rubbing, from मुट aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिसन्देश|अङ्गुलिसंदेश|अंगुलिसंदेश|अङ्गुलिसन्देशः
अङ्गुलिसन्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Snapping the finger joints.<BR>2 Making signs, talking with the fingers.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and सन्देश information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलिस्फोटन|अंगुलिस्फोटन
अङ्गुलिस्फोटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Snapping the fingers.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुलि, and स्फोटन bursting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुली|अंगुली
अङ्गुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A finger.<BR>2 The tip of an elephant's trunk. See अङ्गुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीक|अंगुलीक|अंगुलीकं|अङ्गुलीकः
अङ्गुलीक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A finger ring.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुली, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीपञ्चक|अङ्गुलीपञ्चकं
अङ्गुलीपञ्चक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The five fingers collectively.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुली, and पञ्चक a five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीयक|अंगुलीयक|अंगुलीयकं|अङ्गुलीयकं
अङ्गुलीयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A finger ring.<BR>E.<BR>see अङ्गुरीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुलीसम्भूत|अङ्गुलीसंभूत|अङ्गुलीसम्भूतः
अङ्गुलीसम्भूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुली, and सम्भूत born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठ|अंगुष्ठः|अङ्गुष्ठः
अङ्गुष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The thumb.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गु here said to be the hand, and ष्ठ, from स्था to stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्गूष|अंगूष|अंगूषः|अङ्गूषः
अङ्गूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 An ichneumon.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>अगि to go, and ऊषः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घस्|अंघस्
अङ्घस्<BR>n. (-घः)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>अघि to go, and असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रि|अंघ्रि|अङ्घ्रिः
अङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 The root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, and क्रिन् Uṇādi aff. the formative is irregular. See अंह्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिनामक|अङ्घ्रिनामकः
अङ्घ्रिनामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The root of a tree, being named from a foot; every synonym of a foot, being also that of the root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्घ्रि, and नामक name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिनामन्
अङ्घ्रिनामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्घ्रि a foot or root, and नामन् a name. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिप|अंघ्रिप|अङ्घ्रिपः
अङ्घ्रिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A tree. See अंह्रिप.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्घ्रि a root, and प, from पा to drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिपर्णी
अङ्घ्रिपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant. See अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्घ्रि, and पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीप्, the leaves rising from the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका
अङ्घ्रिवल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अङ्घ्रि, and वल्लिका a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच
अच<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) or (ञ-इ) (अचति) (अंचति अंचते)<BR>1 To go, to go to or towards.<BR>2 To worship.<BR>3 To speak indistinctly. See अञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचक्षुस्
अचक्षुस्<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>A bad or contracted eye.<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्ष)<BR>Eyeless, sightless.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. or dim, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचण्ड|अचंड
अचण्ड<BR>mfn. f. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>Gentle, not passionate.<BR>(-ण्डी)<BR>1 A tractable cow.<BR>2 A mild and gentle woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and चण्डं passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचपल
अचपल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Steady, not fickle.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चपल unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचल|अचलः
अचल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fixed, immoveable.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A pin or bolt.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, and चल who goes, from चल and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलकीला
अचलकीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>अचल a mountain, कील a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलत्विष्
अचलत्विष्<BR>m. (त्विट्)<BR>The Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>अचल mountain, and त्विष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=011" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलाधिप|अचलाधिपः
अचलाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The king of mountains, the personified Himālaya; also analogous compounds, as अचलेन्द्रः, अचलेश्वरः, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अचल and अधिप king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचलभ्रातृ
अचलभ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>The name of a Jaina saint, one of the eleven pupils of the last pontiff.<BR>E.<BR>अचल and भ्रातृ brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचापल्य
अचापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Firmness, steadiness, consistency: also अचपलता, &c.<BR>E.<BR>च neg. चापल्य in constancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्त
अचिन्त<BR>mfn. (न्तः-न्ता-न्तं-)<BR>Insensible, inanimate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिन्ता reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्तता
अचिन्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Insensibility, want of sense or intellect.<BR>E.<BR>ता added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्ता
अचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Disregard, absence of thought or consideration.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिन्ता thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्तित|अचिंतित
अचिन्तित<BR>mfn. (-त-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unthought of, unexpected.<BR>2 Disregarded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिन्तित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिन्त्य|अचिंत्य|अचिन्त्यः
अचिन्त्य<BR>mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>Inconceivable, unimaginable, incomprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिन्त्य conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिर
अचिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Brief, momentary, not long.<BR>(-रा)<BR>A proper name, the mother of ŚĀNTI, the sixteenth Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिर long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरद्युति|अचिरद्युतिः
अचिरद्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चिर long, and द्युति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरप्रभा
अचिरप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अचिर as before, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिररोचिस्
अचिररोचिस्<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अचिर as before, and रोचिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरांशु|अचिरांशुः
अचिरांशु<BR>f. (-शुः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अचिर and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिरात्
अचिरात्<BR>ind.<BR>Directly, without delay.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and चिरात् from length of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचिराभा
अचिराभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अचिर as above, and भा light, with आङ prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचेतन|अचेतनः
अचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Insensible, unconscious, devoid of reason or feeling.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चेतना consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अचैतन्य|अचैतन्यं
अचैतन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Unconsciousness, insensibility.<BR>2 The material universe, as opposed to spiritual being or God.<BR>3 Ignorance, especially spiritual.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चैतन्य intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युत|अच्युतः
अच्युत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU; also of KṚṢṆA, as a form of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A shrub (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fixed, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and च्युत participle of च्युङ to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युतवास|अच्युतवासः
अच्युतवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The religious fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अच्युत VIṢṆU, वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्युताग्रज|अच्युताग्रजः
अच्युताग्रज<BR>m. (जः)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अच्युत KṚṢṆA as VIṢṆU, and अग्रज elder born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छ|अच्छं|अच्छः|अछ
अच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Clear, transparent.<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 A bear.<BR>2 Crystal.<BR>ind.<BR>Fronting, before, in presence of.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. or comparative, and च्छो to cut, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छभल्ल|अच्छभल्लः
अच्छभल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A bear. This is sometimes considered as two words. See अच्छ and भल्ल.<BR>E.<BR>अच्छ in front of, and भल्ल to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अच्छेद्य|अछेद्य
अच्छेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Not to be cut, incapable of injury or comminution.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. छेद्य to be cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज<BR>r. 1st cl. (अजति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To blame, or censure: the root is irregular, वी being substituted for it before many of the inflections, as विवाय, वीयात्, &c. with an indicatory<BR>इ। अजि r. 10th cl. (अञ्जयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज|अजः
अज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 Also of KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>5 A proper name, the son of RAGHU, and father of DĀŚARATHA.<BR>6 A he-goat.<BR>7 A sheep.<BR>8 A mineral substance. See माक्षिक.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A she-goat.<BR>2 Illusion, the unreality of the universe, personified as Śakti.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Unborn.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ज born, unborn; or अज to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्ण|अजकर्णः
अजकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The ear of a goat.<BR>2 A tree, (Terminalia alata tomentosa, Rox.) See असन.<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, कर्ण an ear; the leaf being compared to the ear of a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकर्णक|अजकर्णकः|अजकर्ण्णक
अजकर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, vulg. Śāl, (Shorea robusta, Rox.) See शाल.<BR>E.<BR>क affixed to the preceding, denoting resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकव|अजकवं|अजकवः
अजकव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The bow of ŚIVA. See अजकाव अजगव, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अज VIṢṆU, and क BRAHMĀ, with ब aff. BRAHMĀ being placed in the centre, and VIṢṆU on the upper part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजकाव|अजकावं|अजकावः
अजकाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>See अजकव.<BR>E.<BR>as before, अ being made आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धा
अजगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, (Ocymum gratissimum.)<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, and गन्ध small; smelling like a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिका
अजगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Ocymum gratissimum.) See अजगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगन्धिनी
अजगन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant. See अजशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>See अजगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगर|अजगरः
अजगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Bor, or Boa, a large serpent. (Boa constrictor.)<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, and गर who swallows, from गृ with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगव|अजगवं
अजगव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The bow of ŚIVA. See अजकव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजगाव|अजगावं|अजगावः
अजगाव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>See अजगव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजजीविक|अजजीविकः
अजजीविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goatherd.<BR>E.<BR>अज, and जीविक who lives or gets a livelihood by goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजटा
अजटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>The name of a plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.) Also written अञ्झडा and अञ्झटा.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जट a fibrous root; or अ and जड foolish, brightening the intellects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजथ्या
अजथ्या<BR>f. (-थ्या)<BR>A plant, (Yellow jasmin.)<BR>E.<BR>अज, and थ्यन् aff. of propriety or fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजनक|अजनकः
अजनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One not a parent or producer, unproductive, ungenerative.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जनक generator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननि|अजननिः
अजननि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Privation of birth, used as an imprecation. See अकरणि, &c. Ex. अजननिरस्तु तस्य may he cease to exist.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and जननि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्त
अजन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>(In grammar) A noun ending in a vowel.<BR>E.<BR>अच् the syllable including all the vowels, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्मन्
अजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Unborn.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्य|अजन्यं
अजन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>A portent, an omen; any natural phenomenon, as an earthquake, &c. so considered.<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Not to be born or produced.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जन्य birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजप|अजपः
अजप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A reader of works considered heterodox.<BR>2 A goatherd.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 A particular mantra or mystical formula employed by the Tāntrikas, the essence of which is in the letters H and S, whence it is termed the Haṃsa mantra.<BR>2 ŚIVA and ŚAKTI combined, to which form, the mantra is particularly addressed.<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Who or what does not perform the Japa.<BR>2 Cherishing or feeding goats.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, and जप silent prayer; or अज a goat, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमीढ|अजमीढः
अजमीढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA; the friend of AJA, i. e.<BR>E.<BR>अज VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, and ईह to seek, to love, with the participial क्त, the termination of the accusative is retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=012" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजमोदा
अजमोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Common carroway, (Carum carui.)<BR>2 A kind of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>3 A sort of parsley, (Apium involucratum); this latter application is the one used in the dialects.<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, and मोद what pleases, from मुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजम्भ|अजंभ|अजम्भः
अजम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Defeat.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unsurpassed, unsubdued, over whom or which no triumph is obtained.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Hemp.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय्य|अजय्यं
अजय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Invincible, not to be subdued or surpassed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जय्य conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य्य|अजर्य|अजर्य्यं
अजर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Friendship.<BR>2 Imperishableness, exemption from infirmity or decay.<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Imperishable, undecaying.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जर्य्य from जॄ to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अजर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Imperishable, undecaying.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Aloes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जरा decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजलम्वन
अजलम्वन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजलोमन्
अजलोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>अज, and लोमन् the hair of the body, hair, wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजशृङ्गी
अजशृङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant; described as a milky and thorny plant, with a fruit of a crooked figure, like a ram's horn, and used as a medicine for the eyes; vulg, Mera Śṛṅgī, and Kaṅkara Śṛṅgī. See कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>अज a ram, and शृङ्गी a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र<BR>n. Adverbial. (-स्रं)<BR>Eternally, continually.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जस to let loose, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्स्वार्था
अजहत्स्वार्था<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>A figure of speech, metonymy, one name being put for another, as ‘the spears enter’ for the spearmen.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जहत् leaving, स्वार्थं sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहल्लिङ्ग|अजहल्लिंग|अजहल्लिंगं|अजहल्लिङ्गः
अजहल्लिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>In grammar, a noun that does not vary its gender; even when it is used attributively.<BR>E.<BR>अजहत् not leaving, लिङ्ग gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहा
अजहा<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Not relinquishing, not leaving.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>अज and ह, from हा to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागर|अजागरः
अजागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Not wakeful, not awake.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Eclipta or verbesina prostrata.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जागर wakeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजी
अजाजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>Cumin seed.<BR>E.<BR>अज, a goat, and अज to go, affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजीव|अजाजीवः
अजाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A goatherd; also अजाजीविन् अजापालकः, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अजा a she goat, and जीव who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unborn, unproduced.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातशत्रु|अजातशत्रुः
अजातशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>अजात unborn, and शत्रु an enemy, who never made an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजातारि|अजातारिः
अजातारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>See अजातशत्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजादनी
अजादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A small species of prickly nightshade.<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानेय|अजानेयः
अजानेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A horse of a good breed. See अजानेय.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>See अजानेय the initial being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजान्त्री
अजान्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.) See female, छगलान्त्री.<BR>E.<BR>अज, and अन्त्र an entrail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजापालक|अजापालकः
अजापालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goatherd.<BR>E.<BR>अजा a she goat, पाल to nourish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजित|अजितं|अजितः
अजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unconquered.<BR>2 Unexcelled, unsurpassed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The second of the twenty-four principal Jaina Tīrthakaras or deified sages.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A name of BUDDHA.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जित, participle of जि to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिन|अजिनं
अजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A hide used as a seat, bed, &c. by the religious student; generally the hide of an antelope.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, and the Uṇādi aff. इनच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनपत्रा
अजिनपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा-त्री)<BR>A bat.<BR>E.<BR>अजिन a hide, and पत्र a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनयोनि|अजिनयोनिः
अजिनयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A deer, or antelope.<BR>E.<BR>अजिन a hide, and योनि place or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A court or yard.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 The body.<BR>4 An object of sense.<BR>5 A frog.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, and किरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अजिह्म<BR>mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं)<BR>Straight, not crooked, literally or metaphorically; upright, sincere, honest, direct.<BR>m. (-ह्मः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जिह्म crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्मग|अजिह्मगः
अजिह्मग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going or moving in a straight line.<BR>E.<BR>अजिह्म straight, direct, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्व|अजिह्वः
अजिह्व<BR>mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>Tongueless, having no tongue.<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जिह्व from जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्त्त|अजीगर्त|अजीगर्तः
अजीगर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A Ṛṣi, the father of Śunaḥśepha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णः)<BR>1 Flatulency, indigestion.<BR>2 Vigour, absence of old age or decay.<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Undigested.<BR>2 Undecayed, unimpaired.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जीर्ण old, digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीव|अजीवः
अजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 Non-existence.<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Lifeless, dead.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनि|अजीवनिः
अजीवनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Non-existence; used as an imprecation. See अकरणि, अजीवनिस्तस्य भूयात्.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जीव and अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेतव्य
अजेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Invincible, not to be conquered or overcome.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जेतव्य conquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेय|अजेयः
अजेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Invincible, insuperable, not to be overcome or surpassed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. जेय to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजैकपाद|अजैकपादः
अजैकपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>One of the eleven Rudras or deities so named, forms of ŚIVA. Sometimes read अज एकपाद.<BR>E.<BR>अज ŚIVA, एक one, and पाद a quarter, a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A courtezan, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, or here, to gain, and उकन् affix; sometimes read अर्ज्जुका, from अर्ज to earn, to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झटा
अज्झटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>अत् particle of surprise, and भट to be entangled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झल|अज्झलं
अज्झल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A shield.<BR>E.<BR>अभ् to join, and अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञ|अज्ञः
अज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Ignorant, unwise, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञता
अज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ignorance; also अज्ञत्व.<BR>E.<BR>ता added to अज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञत्व
अज्ञत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>अज्ञ and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात
अज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unknown.<BR>2 Unknowing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञान|अज्ञानं
अज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Ignorance.<BR>2 Spiritual ignorance, wordly illusion or belief in external appearances.<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ignorant, unwise.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानता
अज्ञानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ignorance, also अज्ञानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=013" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानिन्
अज्ञानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Ignorant, unwise.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ज्ञानिन् knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञेय
अज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Incomprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ज्ञेय to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्च
अञ्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ.) (अञ्चति)<BR>1 To adore, to worship, to treat with respect.<BR>(ञ, उ.) (अंचति-ते)<BR>2 To go, to approach.<BR>3 To ask or beg.<BR>4 To speak indistinctly.<BR>With प्र,<BR>to move in an eastern direction;<BR>with प्रति,<BR>to go westerly;<BR>with उत्,<BR>to go northerly;<BR>with अव,<BR>to move southerly;<BR>with परा,<BR>to turn aside or away.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cl. (अंचति अंचयति)<BR>To discriminate, to individualize, to possess especially. See अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चति|अंचतिः|अञ्चतिः
अञ्चति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्च to go, and अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चल|अंचलं|अंचलः|अञ्चलः
अञ्चल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The end or border of a cloth, veil, shawl, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्च to go, and अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चित|अंचित|अञ्चितः
अञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Worshipped, revered.<BR>2 Admired.<BR>3 Gone.<BR>E.<BR>the participial derivative of अञ्च to worship, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्चितभ्रू
अञ्चितभ्रू<BR>f. (-भ्रूः)<BR>A woman having beautiful eye brows.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्चित, and भ्रू the brow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्ज|अञ्जः
अञ्ज<BR>r. 7th cl. (ध, ऊ, ञि.) (अनक्ति)<BR>1 To make clear.<BR>2 To anoint.<BR>3 To be beautiful.<BR>4 To go: with अभि, to anoint: with वि, to make manifest, to call into being, to create, to mark or designate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अंजनः|अञ्जनः
अञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Anointing.<BR>2 Going.<BR>3 Making clear, distinct.<BR>4 A collyrium or application to the eye lashes, to darken and improve them; a universal article of the eastern toilet.<BR>5 Particular applications, as lamp black, antimony, and another kind. See रसाञ्जन.<BR>6 Night.<BR>7 Ink.<BR>8 A term in rhetoric; the use of a word of several meanings in one specific sense, which is determined by the context.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The elephant of the west.<BR>2 A species of lizard.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The mother of HANUMĀN.<BR>2 A green lizard.<BR>(-नी)<BR>3 A woman perfumed with sandal, &c.<BR>4 A medicinal plant. See कटुका.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to beautify or anoint, and ल्यु or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनकेशी
अञ्जनकेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A vegetable perfume. See हट्ठविलासिनी.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन collyrium, केश hair, and ङीप् fem, affix; the fibres being like the crystals, perhaps, of antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाधिका
अञ्जनाधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of lizard.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन, and अधिक much, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनाम्भस्
अञ्जनाम्भस्<BR>n. (-म्भः)<BR>Eye-water, liquid collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन collyrium, and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनावती|अंजनावती
अञ्जनावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The female elephant of the north-east.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन, and वतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जनिका|अंजनिका
अञ्जनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A species of lizard, (Lacerta anjaneya.)<BR>2 A small mouse.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन, and इकन् affix, with the fem. termination: also read अञ्जलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलि|अंजलिः|अञ्जलिः
अञ्जलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 The cavity formed by putting the hands together, and hollowing the palms: being in this form carried to the forehead, it forms the appropriate salutation from inferiors of respectability to their superiors.<BR>2 A measure, a Kuḍava. See कुडव.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to go, and लिच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिका|अंजलिका
अञ्जलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See अञ्जनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकारिका
अञ्जलिकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of sensitive plant, (Mimosa natans,) or according to some, a different plant, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जलि, and कारिका making; from the shape or closing of the petals, like the hollowed palms of the hand.<BR>2 A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिकर्म्मन्|अञ्जलिकर्मन्
अञ्जलिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Making salutations, civility, respect.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जलि, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जलिबन्धन
अञ्जलिबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Making a salutation with the hands joined and applied to the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जलि, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जस|अंजस|अञ्जसः
अञ्जस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Straight, even, upright, (in morals.)<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to make clear, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जसा|अंजसा
अञ्जसा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Soon, instantly.<BR>2 Truly, justly.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज as before, षे to destroy, and क्विष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जि|अंजि|अञ्जिः
अञ्जि<BR>m. (-ञ्जिः)<BR>A superior, a commander, a sender.<BR>E.<BR>अजि to go, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जिष्ठ|अंजिष्ठः|अञ्जिष्ठः
अञ्जिष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to make manifest, and इष्ठन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अञ्जीर|अंजीर|अंजीरं|अञ्जीरं|अंजीरः|अञ्जीरः
अञ्जीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The fig tree, also its fruit. In Bengal, the word derived from this implies the Guava; the term has, possibly, been borrowed from the Persian انجير<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to make clear, and ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट<BR>r. 1st cl. (अटति)<BR>To move, to go or approach:<BR>with परि prefixed,<BR>to go round about, to roam, to rove, to ramble, to wander about, especially as a religious mendicant.<BR>10th cl. (अटयति)<BR>To slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Roaming, wandering.<BR>E.<BR>अट, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटन|अटनं
अटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Roaming about, leading a vagrant life.<BR>E.<BR>अट, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनि|अटनिः
अटनि<BR>f. (-निः or नी)<BR>The notched extremity of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>अट to go, अनि affix, also with ङीष fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरुष|अटरुषः
अटरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A tree, (Justicia adhatoda.)<BR>E.<BR>अट here, disease, from अट to go, and रुष to destroy; destroying disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरूष|अटरूषः
अटरूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>See the last word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवि|अटविः
अटवि<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>A forest, or wood.<BR>E.<BR>अट to go, and अवि affix^1, or ङीष् being added अटवी ut infra; birds, &c. resting there.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20230726. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/1279.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटविक|अटविकः
अटविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wood-man, a forester.<BR>E.<BR>अटवि a wood, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटल
अटल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Immoveable, unchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवी
अटवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A forest, or grove. See अटवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटाट्या
अटाट्या<BR>f. (-ट्या)<BR>Roaming about as a devotee or religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>अट to go, frequentative form, affs. अच् and यप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ.) (अटृते)<BR>1 To surpass or excel, to transgress or exceed.<BR>2 To kill or hurt.<BR>10th cl. (अट्टयति)<BR>1 To slight.<BR>2 To be small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 A room on the top of the house; but it is also applicable to other structures; as the back of an edifice, a fortified place in front of a building, a room on the top of a temporary hall, or a particular kind of building.<BR>2 Much, excessive.<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Food, boiled rice especially.<BR>mfn. (-ट्टः-ट्टा-ट्टं)<BR>Dry, dried.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट to go, surpass, or transcend, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टट्ट
अट्टट्ट<BR>ind.<BR>Very lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टन|अट्टनं
अट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A circular weapon, a kind of discus.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट to kill or hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहास|अट्टहासः
अट्टहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Violent laughter, a horse-laugh.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट excessive, and हास a laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहासक|अट्टहासकः
अट्टहासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Jasminum multiflorum.)<BR>E.<BR>अट्टहास, and कन्; resembling a laugh or smile on beauty's countenance; the comparison is common to the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=014" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टहासिन्
अट्टहासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Laughing, loudly and violently.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अट्टहास, and णिनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाल|अट्टालः
अट्टाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An upper room or pavilion, on the flat roof of an Indian house.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट much, and अल to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालक|अट्टालकः
अट्टालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A room on the top of the house.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट much, अल to adorn, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालिका
अट्टालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A palace, an upper-roomed house.<BR>E.<BR>as before, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालिकाकार|अट्टालिकाकारः
अट्टालिकाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bricklayer, a mason, a builder; born of a Śūdra mother and painter father.<BR>E.<BR>अट्टालिका, and कार who enables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्या
अट्या<BR>f. (-ट्या)<BR>Wandering as a beggar or devotee.<BR>E.<BR>अट्ट to go. See अटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठ
अठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (अठति) With a redundant इ। अठि (अंठते)<BR>To go, to go to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड
अड<BR>r. 1st cl. (अडति)<BR>To strive or endeavour.<BR>5th cl. (अड्नोति)<BR>To occupy or possess, (peculiar to the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्ड
अड्ड<BR>r. 1st cl. (अड्डति)<BR>1 To connect.<BR>2 To solve, or demonstrate.<BR>3 To strive, to endeavour. The radical penultimate is द, and the root is also written by VOPADEVA, अद्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण
अण<BR>r. 1st cl. (अणति)<BR>To sound.<BR>(ङ,) 4th cl. (अण्यते)<BR>To breathe, to live;<BR>with प्र,<BR>to exist, to live. See अन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणक|अणकः
अणक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Inferior, low.<BR>E.<BR>अण to sound, अच् affix; and कन् affix of depreciation; also written अणक, and आणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणव्य|अणव्यं
अणव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A field bearing panic.<BR>E.<BR>अणु panic, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणि|अणिः
अणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A pin or bolt, at the extremity of the pole of a carriage, the pin of the axle.<BR>2 The edge or point of a sharp weapon.<BR>3 A limit, a boundary; also अणी.<BR>E.<BR>अण to sound, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिमन्
अणिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Subtility, infinite minuteness, moleculism.<BR>2 The same considered as a superhuman faculty, to be acquired by austere devotion and the performance of magical rites, or as possessed by a deity.<BR>E.<BR>अण an atom, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणीयस्
अणीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very small.<BR>E.<BR>अणु small, and इयसुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणु|अणुः
अणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 An atom, a minute and elementary particle of matter.<BR>2 A sort of grain, (Panicum miliaceum, Rox.)<BR>m. or mfn. (-णुः-ण्वी-णु)<BR>1 Atomic, small, minute.<BR>E.<BR>अण to sound, and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुक|अणुकः
अणुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Skilful, clever.<BR>2 Small, minute.<BR>E.<BR>अणु small, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुत्व
अणुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The state or being of an atom, also अणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुभा
अणुभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अणु minute, and भा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेणु|अणुरेणुः
अणुरेणु<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>Small particles of dust, a dust of atoms.<BR>E.<BR>अण, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेणुजाल
अणुरेणुजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The moats in a sunbeam.<BR>E.<BR>अणुरेणु, and जाल assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुरेवती
अणुरेवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A tree, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुव्रीहि|अणुव्रीहिः
अणुव्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>Small grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्ड|अंडं|अण्डं|अंडः|अण्डः
अण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 An egg.<BR>2 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>3 Semen genitale.<BR>4 The musk bag, regarded as the scrotum of the deer.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and ड Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डक|अंडकः|अण्डकः
अण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड scrotum, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोटरपुष्पा
अण्डकोटरपुष्पा<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A plant, (perhaps Convolvulus argenteus.) See अजन्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोश|अण्डकोशः
अण्डकोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोष|अण्डकोषः
अण्डकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The scrotum.<BR>2 The testicle.<BR>3 A boundary.<BR>4 The rind of a fruit.<BR>5 Fruit.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड a testicle, and कोश or कोष a sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डकोषक|अण्डकोषकः
अण्डकोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डज|अण्डजः
अण्डज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Oviparous.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A serpent.<BR>2 A fish.<BR>3 A bird.<BR>4 A lizard.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड an egg, &c. and ज what is born, from जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डाकार|अण्डाकारः
अण्डाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Egg-shaped, oval, elliptical.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An oval, an ellipsis; also अण्डाकृति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डालु|अंडालुः|अण्डालुः
अण्डालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड, and आलु, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्डीर|अंडीरः|अण्डीरः
अण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A man.<BR>2 Strong, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड, and ईर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्वी
अण्वी<BR>f. (-ण्वी)<BR>A finger, (from the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत|अतः
अत<BR>r. 1st cl. (अतति)<BR>To go, to move or approach progressively and continually.<BR>With an indicatory इ। अति<BR>(अंतति)<BR>To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतएव
अतएव<BR>ind.<BR>Even, thus, or hence, so, from this cause, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतट|अतटः
अतट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A precipice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथ्य
अतथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>Untrue, false, unreal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तथ्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनु
अतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः न्वी-नु)<BR>Large, great, not small or slight.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तनु minute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्र|अतंद्र
अतन्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रः)<BR>Awake, active, alert.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तन्द्रा sloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतन्द्रित|अतंद्रित
अतन्द्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smart, active, energetical.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तन्द्रित slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप
अतप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Cool.<BR>2 Unanxious.<BR>3 Unemployed.<BR>4 Unostentatious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तप ardor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्त
अतप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Cool, not heated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क|अतर्कः
अतर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>Absence of reasoning, want of consideration.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तर्क consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कित
अतर्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unconsidered.<BR>2 Unexpected, unweighed.<BR>adv. n. (-तं)<BR>Unexpectedly, suddenly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. अर्कित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अतर्क्य<BR>mfn. (-र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं)<BR>Unsearchable, incomprehensible, inscrutable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तर्क्य to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्पणीय
अतर्पणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Insatiable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तर्पणीय to be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्पित
अतर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unsatisfied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तर्पित satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A particular hell or division of the infernal regions, the portion immediately below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and तल bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पर्श|अतलस्पर्शः
अतलस्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Very deep, bottomless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तल bottom, and स्पर्श the touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतलस्पृश्
अतलस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Hence, therefore, from this cause.<BR>2 An interjection of command.<BR>E.<BR>एतद this, and तस् affix; irregular formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस|अतसः
अतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Wind, air.<BR>2 The self, the soul.<BR>3 Cloth made from bark.<BR>4 A weapon.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 Common flax, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>2 Śaṇa, Bengal sun, a kind of flax, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, and the Uṇādi affix असच, when fem. with ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति<BR>ind.<BR>Over, beyond, exceeding, much, very much, &c. it implies general excess, or preeminence.<BR>E.<BR>अप्त to go, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=015" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथ|अतिकथः
अतिकथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Incredible, unworthy of belief or trust.<BR>2 Erring, deviating from the duties of a profession or cast.<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Idle or unmeaning speech.<BR>E.<BR>अति excess or exceeding, and कथा speech: some works substitute for this word, इतिकथ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकन्दक|अतिकंदकः|अतिकन्दकः
अतिकन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree. See हलिकन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकाय|अतिकायः
अतिकाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Gigantic.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्र|अतिकृच्छ्रः
अतिकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रः)<BR>1 A kind of penance, eating a handful of food a day for six days, and fasting three.<BR>2 Extreme pain or suffering.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृति|अतिकृतिः
अतिकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with twenty-five syllables to each line.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and कृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृश
अतिकृश<BR>mfn. (-शःशा-शी-शं)<BR>Very thin, emaciated.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and कृश thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम|अतिक्रमः
अतिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going over or beyond, lit. or fig.<BR>2 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>2 Transgressing.<BR>4 Contrariety, opposition.<BR>5 Neglect, aversion, disregard.<BR>6 Privation.<BR>7 A groundless demand.<BR>8 A gallant attack, advance of an army in front of an enemy. See अभिक्रम.<BR>E.<BR>अति over, beyond, and क्रम to go; going beyond duty or daring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमिन्
अतिक्रमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>1 Transgressing.<BR>2 Exceeding, surpassing.<BR>E.<BR>अतिक्रम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम्य
अतिक्रम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having gone over or beyond. i. e. Exceeded, transgressed, surpassed, overcome, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अति before, क्रम to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रश
अतिक्रश<BR>mfn. (शः-शा-शी-शं)<BR>Thin emaciated.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and क्रश spare; ऋ changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रान्त|अतिक्रांत|अतिक्रान्तः
अतिक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Transgressed, exceeded, passed the proper bounds.<BR>2 Excelled, surpassed.<BR>3 Passed in time.<BR>4 Attacked, assaulted.<BR>5 Excessive, unlimited.<BR>6 Prolix, diffuse.<BR>7 Disregarded, disliked.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and क्रम to go, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रामक|अतिक्रामकः
अतिक्रामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Exceeding, one who oversteps due bounds.<BR>E.<BR>अति and क्रम to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगण्ड|अतिगंडः|अतिगण्डः
अतिगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The sixth of the twenty-seven astrological yogas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्ध|अतिगंध|अतिगन्धः
अतिगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, lemon-grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>2 Champac, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>3 A kind of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>4 Sulphur.<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Of strong or exceeding odour.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगन्धालु|अतिगंधालु|अतिगन्धालुः
अतिगन्धालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A creeper.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and गन्धालु a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगर्व्वित|अतिगर्वित|अतिगर्व्वितः
अतिगर्व्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Arrogant, proud.<BR>E.<BR>अति very, गर्व्व pride, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगर्हित
अतिगर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Despicable, vile.<BR>E.<BR>अति before, गर्हित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुप्त
अतिगुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्त)<BR>Very secret, closely hidden or concealed.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुहा
अतिगुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.) See पृष्णिपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>अति surpassing, and गुहा a hole; rising above the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर
अतिचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Going over or beyond, lit. or fig.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.) See पद्मचारिणी.<BR>E.<BR>अतिचर to go beyond, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचार|अतिचारः
अतिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Going quickly.<BR>2 Going over or beyond.<BR>3 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>4 The passage of a planet from one zodiacal sign to another, in a shorter than common period.<BR>E.<BR>अति before चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्र|अतिच्छत्रः|अतिछत्र
अतिच्छत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Anise, (Anethum pimpinella.)<BR>2 Barleria longifolia.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and च्छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रक|अतिच्छत्रकः|अतिछत्रक
अतिच्छत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजगती
अतिजगती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A form of metre, a stanza of four lines, with thirteen syllables in each line.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and जगती another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजव|अतिजवः
अतिजव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Marching fast or fleet.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and जव quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजागर|अतिजागरः
अतिजागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very wakeful, restless.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The black curlew.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and जागर wakeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीर्ण
अतिजीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Very old.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and जीर्ण old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिडीन|अतिडीनं
अतिडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Very lofty, or very rapid flight of birds.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितराम्
अतितराम्<BR>ind.<BR>Much, excessively, exceedingly.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and तरान् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीव्र
अतितीव्र<BR>mfn. (-व्रः-व्रा-व्रं)<BR>Very sharp or pungent.<BR>f. (-ब्रा)<BR>Doob grass.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and तीव्र sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीक्ष्ण|अतितीक्ष्णः
अतितीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>Very pungent, sharp, hot or acrid.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and तीक्ष्म sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथि|अतिथिः
अतिथि<BR>mfn. (-थिः-था)<BR>A guest, a person entitled to the rites of hospitality.<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>1 A proper name, the son of KUŚA, and grandson of RĀMA.<BR>2 Wrath.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, and इथिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिक्रिया
अतिथिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Hospitality considered as a religious duty.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिद्वेष
अतिथिद्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Inhospitality.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि, and द्वेष dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिपूजन|अतिथिपूजनं
अतिथिपूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hospitality considered as one of the principal sacraments of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि a guest, and पूजन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिसत्कार|अतिथिसत्कारः
अतिथिसत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The rite of hospitality, hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि, and सत्कार pious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिसेवा
अतिथिसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Service of a guest, hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदातृ
अतिदातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A liberal man.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and दातृ who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदान|अतिदानं
अतिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Munificence, giving largely.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदाह|अतिदाहः
अतिदाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Greatheat.<BR>2 Violent inflammation.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिष्ट|अतिदिष्टः
अतिदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Substituted, supplementary.<BR>E.<BR>अति over, and दिष्ट enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुःसह
अतिदुःसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Intolerable, unbearable, not to be borne or endured.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and दुःसह painful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुर्गत
अतिदुर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>In great difficulty or distress.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and टुर्गत badly off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदुष्कर
अतिदुष्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Very arduous, very difficult.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and टुष्कर difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूर
अतिदूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A great distance, afar off.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and दूर afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेश|अतिदेशः
अतिदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Substitution, supplement.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and देश direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदोष
अतिदोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A great fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधृति|अतिधृतिः
अतिधृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with nineteen syllables in each line.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and धृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनौ
अतिनौ<BR>mfn. (-नौः-नौः-नु)<BR>Landed from a boat.<BR>E.<BR>अति over beyond, and नो a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=016" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपतन|अतिपतनं
अतिपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Exceeding, going beyond bounds.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, and पत to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपथिन्
अतिपथिन्<BR>m. (-पन्था)<BR>A good road.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and पथिन् a road, a very road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपर|अतिपरः
अतिपर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A great enemy.<BR>2 One who has conquered his enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and पर a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात|अतिपातः
अतिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Neglect of duty.<BR>2 Transgression, deviation from laws or customs.<BR>3 Contrariety, opposition.<BR>4 Going beyond bounds.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, and पात, from पत to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातक|अतिपातकं
अतिपातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Heinous sin, the worst of the great sins.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and पातक crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातकिन्
अतिपातकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>A great sinner, flagrantly criminal.<BR>E.<BR>अतिपातक and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपारक
अतिपारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Very capable, of great abilities.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and पारक who traverses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपेशल
अतिपेशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very dexterous or clever.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and पेशल clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसङ्ग|अतिप्रसंग|अतिप्रसंगः|अतिप्रसङ्गः
अतिप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Frequent repetition, uninterrupted continuance.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and प्रसङ्ग connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबल|अतिबलः
अतिबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An active soldier.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia, and rhombifolia.) See वाट्यपुष्पी.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभार|अतिभारः
अतिभार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A great or excessive burden.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and भार a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभारग|अतिभारगः
अतिभारग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A mule.<BR>E.<BR>अतिभार, and ग who goes with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभी
अतिभी<BR>m. (-भीः)<BR>Lightning, the flash accompanying thunder.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and भी dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभूमि|अतिभूमिः
अतिभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 Something more than was expected or aimed at.<BR>2 Extensive land or limits.<BR>3 Improper conduct, exceeding proper bounds.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभृत
अतिभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Carefully cherished or protected.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and भृत cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमङ्गल्य|अतिमंगल्य|अतिमङ्गल्यः
अतिमङ्गल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Very auspicious.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A fruit, (Ægle, or Cratoeva marmelos.) See विल्व.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्य्याद|अतिमर्याद|अतिमर्य्यादः
अतिमर्य्याद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>or adverb<BR>m. (-द्रं)<BR>Much, excessive, unlimited, unbounded.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मर्य्यादा a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्त्त्य
अतिमर्त्त्य<BR>mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>Superhuman, divine.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मर्त्त्य mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमात्र|अतिमात्रं
अतिमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>or adverb<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मात्रा a minute quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानुष
अतिमानुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>1 Superhuman, more than mortal.<BR>2 Immortal, divine.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मानुष human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमाय
अतिमाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Free from illusion.<BR>2 Entirely liberated or freed.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and माया delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित
अतिमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dry, not wet.<BR>2 Over measured, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तिमित moist, or अति and मित meted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्त|अतिमुक्तः
अतिमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Seedless, barren.<BR>2 Entirely liberated or freed.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>1 A creeping plant, (Goertnera racemosa.) See माधवीलता.<BR>2 A tree, (Dalbergia oujeiniensis.)<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मुक्त liberated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्तक|अतिमुक्तकः
अतिमुक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (Dalbergia oujeiniensis.)<BR>2 Mountain ebony. See तिन्दुक.<BR>3 A creeper. (Goertnera racemosa, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>See अतिमुक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमोदा
अतिमोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A tree, (Jasmimum arboreum.)<BR>E.<BR>अति, and मोद delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथ|अतिरथः
अतिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A warrior of a particular order fighting in a car.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and रथ a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथिन्
अतिरथिन्<BR>m. (-थी)<BR>A warrior of a particular class, fighting in a car.<BR>E.<BR>अति before रथ a car, and इनि aff. also अतिरथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरसा
अतिरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A creeper.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्त|अतिरिक्तः
अतिरिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Excessive, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and रिच to flow, with the participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्तता
अतिरिक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Increase of bulk or quantity, expansion, enlargement, elevation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ता added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेक|अतिरेकः
अतिरेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and रिच to flow, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेकिन्
अतिरेकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किणी-कि)<BR>More, superior.<BR>E.<BR>अतिरक and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोग|अतिरोगः
अतिरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Consumption, (Phthisis pulmonalis.)<BR>E.<BR>अति, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोमश|अतिरोमशः
अतिरोमश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A wild goat, or according to some, a large monkey.<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Very hairy.<BR>E.<BR>अति and रामश hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलुब्ध
अतिलुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Very covetous.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलोमश
अतिलोमश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Very hairy.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and लोमश hairy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्त्तन|अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्तनं
अतिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An accident, a circumstance not capable of being prevented or guarded against.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वर्त्तन being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्त्तुल|अतिवर्तुल|अतिवर्तुलः|अतिवर्त्तुलः
अतिवर्त्तुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of grain.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वर्त्तुल round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवात|अतिवातः
अतिवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A storm, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाद|अतिवादः
अतिवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Opprobrious or unfriendly speech, See अभिवाद.<BR>E.<BR>अति overcoming, वद to speak, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवालक
अतिवालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An infant.<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Childish.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वालक a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविकट|अतिविकटः
अतिविकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A vicious elephant.<BR>mfn. (टः-टा-टं)<BR>Very fierce, very formidable.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and विकट large or formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविष
अतिविष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Antidote, exceeding or subduing poison.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A tree used in medicine, the bark is also employed in dyeing; it is of three kinds; white, red, and black. (Atis or Betula.)<BR>E.<BR>अति overcoming, and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृष्टि|अतिवृष्टिः
अतिवृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Heavy rain.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेल|अतिवेलं
अतिवेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>or adverb<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Much, excessive, unlimited.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and वेला a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यय
अतिव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Extravagance, great expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and व्यय expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्ययिन्
अतिव्ययिन्<BR>mfn. (यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Extravagant, spendthrift.<BR>E.<BR>अतिव्यय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यथा
अतिव्यथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Excessive pain, agony.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्याप्ति|अतिव्याप्तिः
अतिव्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Extreme pervasion or extension.<BR>2 Going beyond the mark, drawing an inference unwarranted by the premises.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and व्याप्ति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्करी
अतिशक्करी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of metre; of four lines, with fifteen syllables to the line.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, शक्करी another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्त
अतिशक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Very powerful.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and शक्त powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्ति|अतिशक्तिः
अतिशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Great power.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्तिता
अतिशक्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Heroick valor, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>अति, शक्ति power, and ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=017" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्तिभाज्
अतिशक्तिभाज्<BR>m. (-क)<BR>A man of gigantic power.<BR>E.<BR>अतिशक्ति, and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशय|अतिशयः
अतिशय<BR>If an adj. mas. only. (-यः) If an adverb n. (-यं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>शीङ्^1 to sleep; अति being prefixed, to excel; aff. अच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयनं|अतिशयन
अतिशयनं<BR>adv. n. (-नं)<BR>See अतिशय.<BR>E.<BR>ल्युट् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयिन्
अतिशयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Superior, exceeding.<BR>2 Increased, improved, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अतिशय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयोक्ति|अतिशयोक्तिः
अतिशयोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Hyperbole.<BR>2 Verbosity, prolixity.<BR>E.<BR>अतिशय excess, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयन|अतिशयनं
अतिशयन<BR>adv. n. (-नं) adj. mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>अतिशय, and ल्युट् the ante-pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायित
अतिशायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Exceeded, surpassed, excelled.<BR>2 Increased.<BR>E.<BR>अति before शीङ्^1, and क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशोभन|अतिशोभनः
अतिशोभन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Excellent.<BR>2 Chief, principal.<BR>3 Beautiful, splendid.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and शुभ to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसञ्चय|अतिसंचय
अतिसञ्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A hoard, a great accumulation.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and सञ्चय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंहित
अतिसंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cheated, deceived, imposed upon.<BR>2 Explained, declared.<BR>E.<BR>अति, before संहित combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसन्धान|अतिसंधान|अतिसंधानं
अतिसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Falsehood, deceit, fraud, cheating, overreaching.<BR>E.<BR>अति, before सन्धान combining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्जन|अतिसर्जनं|अतिसर्ज्जनं
अतिसर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Liberality, giving.<BR>2 Appointing, engaging.<BR>3 A gift, a donation.<BR>4 Slaughter, killing.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and हृज to create, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसान्तपन|अतिसांतपनं
अतिसान्तपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Severe penance or expiation, especially for the guilt of eating unclean animals; taking as food nothing but cow's urine, cowdung, curds, milk, and ghee, each two days in succession.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and सान्तपन penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाम्या
अतिसाम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>Liquorice plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसार|अतिसारः
अतिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Diarrhoea or dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and सार what goes; from सृ to go, with घञ् affix; also अतीसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारकिन्
अतिसारकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किणी-कि)<BR>Dysenteric, afflicted with dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>अतिसार, and the affixes इनि and कुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारिन्
अतिसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Afflicted with dysentery.<BR>2 Cathartic.<BR>E.<BR>अतिसार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्फिर|अतिस्फिरः
अतिस्फिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very tremulous.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and स्फिर trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहसित|अतिहसितं
अतिहसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Violent laughter.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and हसित laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहास|अतिहासः
अतिहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A horse-laugh, violent laughter.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीन्द्रिय|अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतीन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Imperceptible, unattainable by the senses.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीक्ष्ण
अतीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>Blunt, not sharp, dull, obtuse.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तीक्ष्ण sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीक्ष्णता
अतीक्ष्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Bluntness. So अतीक्ष्णत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीच्छ
अतीच्छ<BR>mfn. (-छः-छा-छं)<BR>Very desirous, eager, ardent.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत|अतीतं|अतीतः
अतीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Passed, gone.<BR>2 Passed away, deceased, dead.<BR>3 Liberated from worldly restraint.<BR>4 Surpassed, gone over or beyond.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीतकाल
अतीतकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>In gram. the preterite tense.<BR>E.<BR>अतीत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव<BR>ind.<BR>Much, very much, much indeed.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and इव as, so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव्र
अतीव्र<BR>mfn. (-व्रः-व्रा-व्रं)<BR>Blunt, dull, insipid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तीव्र sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीसार|अतीसारः
अतीसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Diarrhoea or dysentery. See अतिसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुङ्ग
अतुङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Short of stature, a dwarf.<BR>2 Low.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुङ्ग tall or high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुन्द|अतुंद
अतुन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Lank, thin.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुन्द fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अतुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unequalled.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant that has an oily seed, (Sesamum orientale.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुल to be like, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुलनीय
अतुलनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Incomparable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुलनीय comparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल्य|अतुल्यं
अतुल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Unequalled, unparalleled.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुल्य to be equalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुहिनरश्मि
अतुहिनरश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>The sun, whose rays are not cold, i. e. hot: also analogous compounds, as अतुहिनधाम, अतुहिनरुचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्त
अतृप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Unsatisfied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तृप्त satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृप्ति|अतृप्तिः
अतृप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Insatiableness, voraciousness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तृप्ति satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Dark, dim, dull.<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 Shade, shadow.<BR>2 Insignificance, feebleness, imbecility.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तेजस् light or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्विन्
अतेजस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Void of splendour or energy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तेजस्विन् splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतोषणीय
अतोषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Implacable, not to be appeased.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तोषणीय to be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्क|अत्कः
अत्क<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>A limb, a member of the body.<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, and कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 An elder sister.<BR>3 A mother's elder sister.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, अच, and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ति|अत्तिः
अत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>In theatrical language, an elder sister.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तिका
अत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>In theatrical language, an elder sister.<BR>E.<BR>अत्ता a mother, and कन् affix, who is, as it were, a mother; it is also written अन्तिका and अर्विका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्वी-त्तॄ)<BR>A feeder, one who eats.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नु|अत्नुः
अत्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, क्नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्य|अत्यः
अत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A horse, from the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go constantly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यजनीय
अत्यजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-था-यं)<BR>Not to be abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. त्यजनीय to be abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्त|अत्यंत|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यन्त<BR>mfn. or adv. n. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, and अन्त end, or boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तकोपन|अत्यन्तकोपनः
अत्यन्तकोपन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Very passionate.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त, and कोपन passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तगामिन्
अत्यन्तगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>What goes much or quickly.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तसुकुमार|अत्यन्तसुकुमारः
अत्यन्तसुकुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A species of grain, (Panicum Italicum.)<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त, and सुकुमार very soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्ताभाव|अत्यन्ताभावः
अत्यन्ताभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>(In logic) absolute negation or non-existence.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त much, अभाव not being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तिक|अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यन्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who rambles much, a great rover.<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Much, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त, with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यन्तीन|अत्यंतीन|अत्यन्तीनः
अत्यन्तीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One who goes quickly or actively.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त much, and ईन for गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=018" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं|अत्यम्लः
अत्यम्ल<BR>mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं)<BR>Very sour.<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>f. (-म्ला)<BR>Another plant and fruit; a species of citron. See मातुलुङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्लपर्णी|अत्यम्लपर्ण्णी
अत्यम्लपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A creeper and medicinal plant.<BR>E.<BR>अति excessive, अम्ल sour; and पर्ण a leaf, with the fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 Distress.<BR>3 Transgression.<BR>4 Vice, fault, guilt.<BR>5 Punishment.<BR>6 Going over or beyond.<BR>7 Absence.<BR>8 Loss, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, away, इण to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययित
अत्ययित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Exceeded, surpassed.<BR>2 Outraged.<BR>E.<BR>अति before इण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ<BR>n. adv. mfn. adj. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and अर्थ substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यल्प|अत्यल्पं
अत्यल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Very small, very little.<BR>E.<BR>अति very, and अल्प small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टी
अत्यष्टी<BR>f. (-ष्टी)<BR>A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with seventeen syllables to the line.<BR>E.<BR>अति beyond, अष्टी another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यसम
अत्यसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Very rough, uneven, craggy.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and असम unequal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकार|अत्याकारः
अत्याकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Censure, blame, contempt.<BR>E.<BR>अति and आङ prefixed to कृ to do, वज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Deviating from prescribed observances, contemning religious and moral laws.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचारिन्
अत्याचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Transgressing.<BR>E.<BR>अत्याचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याज्य|अत्याज्यं
अत्याज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Not to be abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. त्याज्य to be abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याशा
अत्याशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Unreasonable hope or desire.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहार
अत्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Excessive food.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहारिन्
अत्याहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Eating excessively, a glutton, a gormandizer.<BR>E.<BR>अत्याहार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहित|अत्याहितं
अत्याहित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Great dread.<BR>2 Desperate or daring action.<BR>E.<BR>अति, with धा to have; आङ prefixed, and the participial क्त; हि is substituted for धा; what engrosses the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ति|अत्युक्तिः
अत्युक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Idle or excessive talk.<BR>2 Expatiating, enlarging.<BR>3 A figure of rhetoric, description of any thing surprising or extraordinary, hyperbole.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्था
अत्युक्था<BR>f. (-क्था)<BR>A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines, with two syllables to the line.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and उक्था another kind: it is also read अत्युक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कट
अत्युत्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Extreme, exceeding great.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and उत्कट much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युत्कृष्ट
अत्युत्कृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टां-ष्टं)<BR>1 Most excellent, best.<BR>2 Most valuable, precious.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and उत्कृष्ट excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूह|अत्यूहः
अत्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, (Jasminum villosum, Rox. or in Bengal, Nyctanthes tristis.) See शेफालिका.<BR>E.<BR>अति, and ऊह to reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र<BR>ind.<BR>In this place, here, herein.<BR>E.<BR>त्र being substituted for the termination of the seventh case of इदम् this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Shameless, immodest.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रभवत्|अत्रभवन्त्
अत्रभवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Respectable, venerable, (especially in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>अत्र here, भू to be, and the participial affix शतृ; being present or principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रास
अत्रास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि<BR>m. (-त्रिः)<BR>The name of one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints, born from the eye of BRAHMĀ, married to ANASŪYĀ, daughter of KARDAMA MUNI, and the father of DATTA or DATTĀTREYA, DURVĀSAS and CANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat and त्रिप् Uṇādi aff. The correct reading is अत्त्रि, but the word is always written with one त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिजात|अत्रिजातः
अत्रिजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A man of the three first classes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. त्रि three, and जात born, not thrice born; born twice. The moon, from the eye of ATRI, and from the ocean. The Brahman &c. from the womb and investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिदृग्ज|अत्रिदृग्जः
अत्रिदृग्ज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>अत्रि a saint, दृश् the eye, and ज born, produced. Born from the eye of ATRI, “a flash of light from the eye of ATRI, was received by space, a goddess, the via lactea personified, who bore SOMA.” The following and other similar names refer to this legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A muni. See अत्र.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, Uṇādi aff. त्रिन्; also अत्त्रिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रज|अत्रिनेत्रजः
अत्रिनेत्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>See अत्तिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत|अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूतः
अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>See अत्रिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिनेत्रभू
अत्रिनेत्रभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>See अत्रिदृग्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिभारद्वाजिका
अत्रिभारद्वाजिका<BR>m. (-का)<BR>The marriage union of ATRI and BHĀRADVĀJĪ.<BR>E.<BR>अत्रि, and भारद्वाजी; affix वुञ्, implying in this and similar compounds, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-र)<BR>Deliberate, not in haste.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. तुर for त्वरा haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रि
अत्त्रि<BR>m. (-त्त्रिः)<BR>A sage. See अत्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्त्रिन्
अत्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्त्री)<BR>A sage. See अत्त्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ<BR>ind.<BR>An auspicious and inceptive particle; it serves to introduce a remark, a question, an affirmation, &c. and corresponds to,<BR>1 After.<BR>2 And.<BR>3 Now, (inceptive or premising.)<BR>4 What, (interrogatively.)<BR>5 All, (comprehensively.)<BR>6 Therefore, thus, further, moreover. &c. It also implies doubt or command, and is frequently redundant.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ to ask, ड affix, and र is dropped, also अथो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथकिम्
अथकिम्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of assent, how else, what else, assuredly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथच
अथच<BR>ind.<BR>Also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वण|अथर्वण|अथर्वणः|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्व्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अथर्व्व the name of a Veda, and ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वन्|अथर्वन्
अथर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A name of VASIṢṬHA.<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>The name of the fourth Veda.<BR>E.<BR>अथ an auspicious particle, ऋ to go, and वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्व्वणि|अथर्वणि|अथर्वणिः|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्व्वणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A Brahman versed in the Atharva Veda.<BR>2 A family priest.<BR>E.<BR>अथर्व्व the Veda, and णि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथवा<BR>ind.<BR>Or.<BR>E.<BR>अथ, and वा sometimes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो<BR>ind.<BR>The same as अथ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद|अदः
अद<BR>(औ) r. 2d cl. (अत्ति)<BR>To eat. The root is imperfect; घस being substituted for it in several inflections; as जघास, &c. Implying injury, it is not conjugated in the middle voice, although the action be reciprocal: as व्यत्यदन्ति they bite, or devour each other.<BR>With an indicatory इ, अदि<BR>(अन्दति)<BR>To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=019" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्ष
अदक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Awkward, unskilful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दक्ष clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अदक्षिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Not clever, unskilful.<BR>2 Not comprehending the fee given to the Brahmans, a sacrifice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दक्षिण clever, or दक्षिणा a fee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदग्ध
अदग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Unscorched, not burnt.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड|अदंड
अदण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Unpunished.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Impunity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्ड्य|अदंड्य
अदण्ड्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं)<BR>Unpunishable, unworthy of or exempt from punishment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दण्ड्य to be punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदण्डनीय
अदण्डनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unpunishable, unfit to be punished, exempt from punishment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दण्डनीय to be punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त|अदत्तं
अदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Not given.<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>An unmarried girl.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन|अदनं
अदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदनीय
अदनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be eaten, what may be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदन्त|अदंत|अदन्तः
अदन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Toothless. So अदन्तक (-कः-का-कं)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदम्य
अदम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Uncontroulable, untameable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दम्य to be tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदभ्र|अदभ्रः
अदभ्र<BR>mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दभ्र little, few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदय
अदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unfeeling, unmerciful, destitute of pity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दया clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शन|अदर्शनं
अदर्शन<BR>n. (-न)<BR>Disappearance, not being visible or present.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दर्शन sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदल|अदलः
अदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Eugenia acutangula.) See हिज्जल.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Socotrine aloe, (Aloes perfoliata.) See घृतकुमारी.<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Leafless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्
अदस्<BR>mfn. (असौ असौ अदः)<BR>1 This.<BR>2 That.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदहनीय
अदहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Incombustible; so अदाहनीय.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दाहनीय or दहनीय to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदातृ
अदातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A niggard, a miser.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दातृ who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान
अदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not giving, withholding.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान्त|अदांत|अदान्तः
अदान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Untamed, unsubdued, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दान्त daunted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिक
अदायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Unclaimed, as inheritance, lapsed.<BR>2 Not relating to inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दाय heritage, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाह्य
अदाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Inconsumable by fire, incombustible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दाह्य to be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
अदिति<BR>f. (-ति.)<BR>1 The daughter of DAKṢA, wife of KAŚYAPA, and mother of the gods.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 Being entire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दा to give, and दिति affix, not giving pain; or अ, and दो to cut or break, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदितिनन्दन|अदितिनंदन|अदितिनन्दनः
अदितिनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deity, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>अदिति, and नन्दन, a son of ADITI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुष्ट
अदुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unspoiled, unvitiated.<BR>2 Good, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. टुष्ट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषित
अदूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undefiled, unvitiated.<BR>2 Virtuous, good.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दूषित corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्
अदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>Blind.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and दृश the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्य|अदृश्यं
अदृश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>1 Invisible, not to be seen.<BR>2 Improper to be beheld.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. दृश्य to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं|अदृष्टः
अदृष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Casual and unseen danger, (as from conflagration, inundation, &c.)<BR>2 Fortune, destiny, fate.<BR>3 (In logic) Virtue or vice, as the eventual cause of pleasure or pain.<BR>mfn. (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unseen, unforeseen.<BR>2 Unknown, unfelt, not experienced.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपुरुष|अदृष्टपुरुषः
अदृष्टपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A form of treaty, in which the parties treat direct, without any mediator or surety, also अदृष्टनर and similar compounds.<BR>E.<BR>अदृष्ट unseen, and पुरुष, &c. man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टपूर्व्व|अदृष्टपूर्व
अदृष्टपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Unseen previously, unseen till now.<BR>E.<BR>अदृष्ट, and पूर्व्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टवत्
अदृष्टवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत)<BR>1 Enjoying or undergoing good or bad fortune, more usually the former, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>अदृष्ट, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टि|अदृष्टिः
अदृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A look of displeasure, evil eye.<BR>E.<BR>अ bad, and दृष्टि look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टिका
अदृष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An angry or displeased look, evil-eye.<BR>E.<BR>अदृष्टि, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेय
अदेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-पं)<BR>Improper or unfit to be given.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेयदान
अदेयदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving what ought not to be given, what is not one's own, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अदेय, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्ग|अद्गः
अद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>Oiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, and गम् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धा
अद्धा<BR>ind.<BR>Truly, verily.<BR>E.<BR>अत going constantly, धा to have, and विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Surprise, astonishment.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wonderful, surprising.<BR>E.<BR>अत a particle of surprise, भू to be, and उतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुतश्वन
अद्भुतश्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अद्भुत astonishing, and श्वन who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मनि|अद्मनिः
अद्मनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, Uṇādi affix अनि, and म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मर|अद्मरः
अद्मर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Gluttonous.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, and क्मरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य<BR>ind.<BR>To-day.<BR>E.<BR>इदम् this; an irregular formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The period of a current day, from midnight to midnight in the usual acceptation, but sometimes considered to begin and end with sun-set.<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Of or belonging to the current day, of to-day.<BR>E.<BR>अद्य, and द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनभूत
अद्यतनभूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>In grammar, the aorist past.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Past or gone to-day, i. e. any time previous to to-day.<BR>E.<BR>अद्यतन of to-day, भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यापि
अद्यापि<BR>ind.<BR>Even now, still.<BR>E.<BR>अद्य, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यावधि
अद्यावधि<BR>n. (-धि)<BR>Beginning or ending with the current day, from or till to-day.<BR>E.<BR>अद्य, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यश्वीन|अद्यश्वीनं
अद्यश्वीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Near to any event, at the point of death &c.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman or any female animal near the time of delivery.<BR>E.<BR>अद्य, and श्व to-morrow, affix स्व, what will happen to-day or to-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्य|अद्रव्यं
अद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A worthless or good for nothing object.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रि|अद्रिः
अद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A measure.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, and क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिकीला
अद्रिकीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि a mountain, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिज|अद्रिजं
अद्रिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced or found in the hills.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ or DURGĀ, the daughter [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=21" target="_blank">Page21</a>] of HIMĀLA, ruler of the HIMĀLAYA mountain, and hence this her appellation, mountain-born.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and ज, from जन to be born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=020" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रितनया
अद्रितनया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ, the daughter of the mountain HIMĀLAYA.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिनन्दिनी
अद्रिनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>PĀRVATĪ. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिपति|अद्रिपतिः
अद्रिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Hima, lord of mountains: also similar compounds, as अद्रीन्द्र, अद्रिराज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभिद्
अद्रिभिद्<BR>m. (-भित्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and भिद who breaks; the splitter of mountains, (with his thunderbolt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिभू
अद्रिभू<BR>mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु)<BR>Mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A plant, (Salvinea cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिराज्
अद्रिराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>The king of mountains, the HIMĀLAYA mountains; the snowy range on the north of Hindustan, confounded with the mythological ruler of them, and the father of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and राज् a king, the king of mountains, deservedly so called, being the loftiest in the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिवह्नि|अद्रिवह्निः
अद्रिवह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>Fire on a mountain, a volcano.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिशृङ्ग|अद्रिशृंग
अद्रिशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A peak, the horn or summit of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिसार|अद्रिसारः
अद्रिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रीश|अद्रीशः
अद्रीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Also of HIMĀLAYA, as king of mountains.<BR>E.<BR>अद्रि, and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोह|अद्रोहः
अद्रोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Mildness, moderation, the absence of tyranny or oppression.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्रोह tyranny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोहिन्
अद्रोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Innocuous, mild.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्रोहिन् violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अद्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयवादिन्
अद्वयवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A Bauddha.<BR>2 A unitarian.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वय two, and वादिन् who speaks, one who acknowledges but one principle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीय|अद्वितीयः
अद्वितीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Only, sole, without a second.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वितीय second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष|अद्वेषः
अद्वेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Harmless, not malicious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वेष malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषिन्
अद्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Harmless, inoffensive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वेषिन् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Unity, not duality.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. द्वैत duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैतवादिन्
अद्वैतवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A unitarian, one who maintains the existence of but one principle in the universe.<BR>E.<BR>अद्वैत unity, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकाय
अधःकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The lower part of the body, the lower extremities.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःकृत
अधःकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrown or put down.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःक्षिप्त|अधःक्षिप्तः
अधःक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Precipitated, thrown down.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् down, and क्षिप्त participle past of क्षिप् to throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपतित
अधःपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fallen down.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःप्रस्तर|अधःप्रस्तरः
अधःप्रस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A seat or bed, made of grass.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and प्रस्तर a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःपुष्पी
अधःपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, (Hieracium.)<BR>E.<BR>अधस् downwards, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधःस्थ
अधःस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Below.<BR>2 Inferior.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Inferior, low.<BR>2 Vile, despicable.<BR>E.<BR>अब to preserve, अम Uṇādi affix, and व changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमभृतक|अधमभृतकः
अधमभृतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A porter, a bearer of burdens.<BR>2 Low, servile.<BR>E.<BR>अधम low, and भृतक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्ण|अधमर्णः
अधमर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>अधम low, and ऋण debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिक|अधमर्णिकः
अधमर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>अधम, and ऋण debt, with ठक added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमर्णिन्
अधमर्णिन्<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>अधम, and ऋण debt, with इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधमाङ्ग|अधमांग|अधमाङ्गं
अधमाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A foot.<BR>E.<BR>अधम low, and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Low, inferior, below.<BR>2 Low, vile.<BR>3 Silenced, refuted, overcome in abuse or controversy.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The lower region.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The lower lip. (dual. -रौ) The lips.<BR>mn. (-रः or रं)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धृ to have or hold, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतस्
अधरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Underneath.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरमधु
अधरमधु<BR>n. (-घु)<BR>The moisture of the lips.<BR>E.<BR>अधर the lower lip, and मधु honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्तात्
अधरस्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>Below, behind.<BR>E.<BR>स्तात् added to अधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्मात्
अधरस्मात्<BR>ind.<BR>Below, underneath.<BR>E.<BR>the form of the ablative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरात्
अधरात्<BR>ind.<BR>Underneath.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, with the termination आत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरामृत|अधरामृतं
अधरामृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The moisture, honey or nectar of the lips.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and अमृत nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरावलोप
अधरावलोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Biting the lip.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and अव before लुप to cut, affix धञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीकृत
अधरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contradicted, invalidated.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and कृत made with च्ची inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीण|अधरीणः
अधरीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Reproached, censured.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीभूत
अधरीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contradicted, invalidated.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and भूत become, with च्ची inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेण
अधरेण<BR>ind.<BR>Underneath.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and the affix एन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेद्युस्
अधरेद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>A future day, the day after the morrow.<BR>E.<BR>अधर, and एद्युस् irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्म|अधर्म|अधर्मः|अधर्म्मः
अधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Unrighteousness, injustice, all behaviour contrary to the Śruti and Smṛti, or religious and legal institutes.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and धर्म्म virtue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मचारिन्|अधर्मचारिन्
अधर्म्मचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-रीः-रिणी-रि^1)<BR>Unrighteous, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>अधम्म, and चारिन् who follows.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321. note: print is missing a '-'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मता|अधर्मता
अधर्म्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unrighteousness; also अधर्म्मत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अधर्म्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मात्मन्|अधर्मात्मन्
अधर्म्मात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Wicked, unrighteous.<BR>E.<BR>अधर्म्म, and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मिन्|अधर्मिन्
अधर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>Wicked, sinful, unrighteous.<BR>E.<BR>अधर्म्म, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्मिष्ठ|अधर्मिष्ठ
अधर्म्मिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very wicked.<BR>E.<BR>अधर्म्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधश्चर|अधश्चरः
अधश्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Going.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् low, vile, and चर who goes down or below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधश्चौर|अधश्चौरः
अधश्चौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् below, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Down, downwards, below.<BR>2 The lower or infernal regions.<BR>2 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>अधर with असि affix, and र dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तन
अधस्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Below, underneath.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and ट्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=021" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्तात्
अधस्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Down, downwards, underneath.<BR>2 Behind.<BR>3 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>अधर or अधम्, and तात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधामार्गव|अधामार्गवः
अधामार्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>अधम vile, मार्ग a road, and व from वा to gain or possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधार्म्मिक|अधार्मिक|अधार्म्मिकः
अधार्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unjust, unrighteous, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and धार्म्मिक virtuous, &c. from धर्म्म, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Anxiety, mental pain; more usually आधिः.<BR>E.<BR>आङ before, धा to have, कि affix; आ is made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधि|अधिः
अधि<BR>ind.<BR>Over, above, upon, &c. a preposition and prefix to verbs implying superiority in place, quality, or quantity; as अधिष्ठातुं to stand in or on, अधिकर्त्तुं to rule over, अधिशयितुं to exceed: also used in the figurative sense of the same, as अधिगन्तुं to go to or attain; अधिकर्त्तुं to do over again, to repeat or recall; अधीतुं to go over or through, as a book; अधिवस्तुं to reside in or on, to continue in or on, to persevere: forming also indeclinables with nouns, as अधिरात्रि in the night; अधि ग्रहं in or over the house: and compounds with nouns, as अधिदेवप्ता, &c. q. v.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक|अधिकं|अधिकः
अधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Exceeding, more, over, more than, in addition to.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A figure in rhetoric, (Hyperbole.)<BR>E.<BR>अधि and क, from कै to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकतर
अधिकतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>More, comparatively more.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकतम
अधिकतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-भं)<BR>Most, superlatively more.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकता
अधिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Excess, addition; also अधिकत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अधिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकन्तु
अधिकन्तु<BR>ind.<BR>Moreover.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक, and तु but.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकरण|अधिकरणं
अधिकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Superiority, supremacy.<BR>2 Title, right.<BR>3 In the Mīmāṃsā philosophy, a case or topic, comprehending five members, the subject, the doubt, the first side or prima facie argument, the answer or conclusion, the application.<BR>4 (In the Vedānta.) A case or question.<BR>5 (In grammar) Location, the sense of the seventh or locative case, defined to imply four kinds: .²1 Proximity, as, ‘a village on the Ganges.’ .²2 Inclusion, as, ‘the gods in heaven.’ .²3 End or object, as, ‘versed in the Śāstras; and .²4 Integral existence, as, ‘the spirit is in all.’<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, कृ to do; and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्द्धि
अधिकर्द्धि<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धिः-र्द्धिः-र्द्धि)<BR>Prosperous, every way happy.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक excessive, and ऋद्धि prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्म्मन्|अधिकर्मन्
अधिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Superintendence, supervision.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and कर्म्म business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकर्म्मिक|अधिकर्मिक|अधिकर्मिकः|अधिकर्म्मिकः
अधिकर्म्मिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Clerk or prefect of the market or fair.<BR>2 An overseer, a superintendent.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, कर्म्म business, and इक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकाङ्ग|अधिकाङ्गं
अधिकाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Having more members than natural or common.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The girdle over the coat of mail, worn as a kind of scarf.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक exceeding, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकार|अधिकारः
अधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Authority.<BR>2 Supremacy.<BR>3 Rule, government.<BR>4 Right, title.<BR>5 Property, ownership.<BR>6 Privilege.<BR>7 Duty, office.<BR>3 A chapter, a section.<BR>9 The use of royal insignia.<BR>10 (In grammar) Government, the dependance of a form on a previous one.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, and कार what makes, from कृ with घञ् affix; what gives or exercises preeminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिता
अधिकारिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Ownership, lordship.<BR>2 Right, title.<BR>E.<BR>अधिकारिन् with ता affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारित्व|अधिकारित्वं
अधिकारित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Ownership.<BR>2 Right, title.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, affix त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकारिन्
अधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A superintendent, a ruler, a director.<BR>2 A master, an owner.<BR>3 A sage, one who is perfect in the principles and practice of the Vedānta.<BR>mf. (-री-रिणी)<BR>(In law) The possessor of a right or title, as, धनाधिकारी heir to property; संस्काराधिकारी one who has a right to the essential ceremonies of the Hindu religion.<BR>E.<BR>अधिकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृत|अधिकृतः
अधिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Superintended, guided.<BR>2 Claimed or held as a right.<BR>3 Set over, superintendent.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A superintendent in general.<BR>2 Inspector of receipts and disbursements, an auditor of public accompts.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रम|अधिक्रमः
अधिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Invasion, assailing.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, and क्रम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्रमण|अधिक्रमणं
अधिक्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Invading, assailing, overrunning.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and क्रमण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिकृति|अधिकृतिः
अधिकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A possession, a right.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and कृति doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षिप्त|अधिक्षिप्तः
अधिक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Censured, reviled, detracted from.<BR>2 Sent, dispatched.<BR>3 Placed, fixed.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and क्षिप्त participle of क्षिप to send or throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिक्षेप|अधिक्षेपः
अधिक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Detraction, censure.<BR>2 Sending, despatching.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगत
अधिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Obtained.<BR>2 Gone through or over, lit. or fig. as read, studied.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम|अधिगमः
अधिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Obtaining, attaining, acquiring.<BR>2 Going through or over, lit. or fig.<BR>3 Overpassing, overflowing: also अधिगमन n. (-नं) &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and गम or गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिगम्य
अधिगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Unattainable, not to be reached or acquired. So अधिगमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) and अधिगन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं).<BR>E.<BR>अधिगम with यत्, अनीयर or तव्य participial affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिजिह्व|अधिजिह्वः
अधिजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A tumor on the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिज्योतिष
अधिज्योतिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The luminous parts of the creation.<BR>E.<BR>अधि supreme, ज्योतिष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधित्यका
अधित्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Land on the upper part of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, above, and त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदन्त|अधिदंतः|अधिदन्तः
अधिदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A tooth growing over another.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेव|अधिदेवः
अधिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A supreme or superior deity.<BR>2 A tutelary deity.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदेवता
अधिदेवता<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A tutelary or presiding divinity.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and देवता a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिदैव|अधिदैवं
अधिदैव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The ruling deity, the active principle in creation: also अधिदैवतं.<BR>2 The collective body of gods, and superhuman beings.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and दैव divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप|अधिपः
अधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 An owner, a lord or master.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and प who preserves, from पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपति|अधिपतिः
अधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A master, an owner, a ruler.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रज
अधिप्रज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Continuation of the world by procreation.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and प्रजा progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभू
अधिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A master, a ruler.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and भू who is from भू to be, affix विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=022" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूत|अधिभूतं
अधिभूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>An essential element of matter, perishable matter, that of which the presence involves eventual dissolution.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, and भ्रूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमन्थ|अधिमंथः|अधिमन्थः
अधिमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>Acute pains in the balls of the eyes, with pain and swelling of one side of the head.<BR>E.<BR>अधि over, मन्य what agitates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांस|अधिमांसः
अधिमांस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Fleshy excrescences on the eye, cancer of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसक|अधिमांसकः
अधिमांसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Inflammation of the tonsils.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and मांस flesh, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमात्र
अधिमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A knowledge of the properties of the letters forming the word for the Hindu triad ओम्.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and मात्र the whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमास|अधिमासः
अधिमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An intercalary month, formed of the aggregate days omitted in reckoning the lunar year.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथ|अधिरथः
अधिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्
अधिराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A supreme king, an emperor. So अधिराज m. (-जः)<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and राज् राजन a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्य|अधिराज्यं
अधिराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Empire, supreme sway.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and राज्य kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्यभाज्
अधिराज्यभाज्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>An emperor, a paramount sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>अधिराज्य, and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढ
अधिरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Elevated, exalted, surmounting.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and रूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोपित
अधिरोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Placed over, lit. or fig.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and रोपित raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोह|अधिरोहः
अधिरोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Surmounting, overtopping, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and रोह mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहणी
अधिरोहणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A ladder, a pair of steps.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and रुह to mount, with ल्युट् affix, and fem. ङीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहिन्
अधिरोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-हि-हिणी-हि)<BR>Who rises on or above.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A ladder, a staircase.<BR>E.<BR>अधिरोह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिलोक
अधिलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The universe, the material world.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवचन|अधिवचनं
अधिवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A name, an appellation.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवास|अधिवासः
अधिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A house, an abode.<BR>2 Place, situation.<BR>3 Continuance, perseverance.<BR>4 Perfuming the person, &c.<BR>5 A neighbour.<BR>6 Neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and वस to dwell, with घञ् affix; or पास to fumigate, with अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासन|अधिवासनं
अधिवासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Perfuming or scenting the person, &c.<BR>2 Abiding, staying.<BR>3 A religious ceremony; touching a vessel containing perfumes, flowers, and other things previously presented to an idol, or offering perfumes, &c. to idols, as a preliminary ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and वास to fumigate, ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासिता
अधिवासिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Residence, staying or abiding in one place.<BR>E.<BR>अधिवास, with ता affix, and इट augment; also with त्व, अधिवासित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविद्या
अधिविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>The collective means and end of acquiring knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविन्ना
अधिविन्ना<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>A wife whose husband has subsequently married others; a superseded wife.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and विन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेत्तृ
अधिवेत्तृ<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>A man marrying other than his first wife.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before विद to obtain, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदन|अधिवेदनं
अधिवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marrying again, whilst a former wife is living.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before विद to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदनीया
अधिवेदनीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A wife deserving or proper to be superseded.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before विद to obtain, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रय|अधिश्रयः
अधिश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A place, a receptacle.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before श्रि to serve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयणी
अधिश्रयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A furnace or fire-place.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and श्रिङ to cook, ल्युट् affix, and fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रित
अधिश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Placed, deposited, received, included.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, before श्रि to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठान|अधिष्ठानं
अधिष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abiding, resting.<BR>2 Site, situation.<BR>3 Prescribed rule, fixed practice.<BR>5 A town.<BR>6 A wheel.<BR>4 Dignity.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, श्या to stand, and ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठातृ
अधिष्ठातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Governing, directing, fixing.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A ruler, a governor, a director.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before स्था to stay, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठित
अधिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fixed, determined, established; literally or figuratively, as a house or a practice.<BR>2 Supervised, overlooked.<BR>3 Guarded, surrounded.<BR>4 Appointed.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and स्थित stationed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीकार|अधीकारः
अधीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Superintendence, authority, &c. See अधिकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीत|अधीतः
अधीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Read, read through.<BR>E.<BR>the participial deriv. from अधी to read over, or study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतवेद
अधीतवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A Brahman, who has read the Vedas; a student who has finished his course of study.<BR>E.<BR>अधीत, and वेद the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीति|अधीतिः
अधीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Study, perusal.<BR>E.<BR>अधी to read, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिन्
अधीतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>A scholar, one who has finished his studies.<BR>E.<BR>अधीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीन|अधीनः
अधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Docile.<BR>2 Dependant.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and इन a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीनता
अधीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Subjection, dependance, slavery: so अधीनत्व (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीयान|अधीयानः
अधीयान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A student, one going over or reading the Vedas, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before इ to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीर|अधीरः
अधीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Confused, perplexed.<BR>2 Unsteady, (lit. or met.)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 An offended, cross or capricious mistress or wife.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and धीर firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीरता
अधीरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fickleness, unsteadiness; also अधीरत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश|अधीशः
अधीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A master, a lord.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश्वर|अधीश्वरः
अधीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An emperor, a king paramount over all the neighbouring princes.<BR>E.<BR>अधि superior, and ईश्वर a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुना
अधुना<BR>ind.<BR>Now, at present.<BR>E.<BR>इदस् this, irregularly formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुनातन|अधुनातनं
अधुनातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Of or belonging to the present.<BR>E.<BR>अधुना, and द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृत|अधृतः
अधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unheld, undetained.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृति|अधृतिः
अधृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Laxity, want of firm hold.<BR>2 Want of steadiness or firmness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धृति holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अधृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ashamed, modest, humble.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धृष्ट proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्टता
अधृष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Modesty, diffidence: also अधृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=023" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्य|अधृष्यः
अधृष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Proud, vain.<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and धृष to be proud; than whom nought is prouder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधेय
अधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be held or taken.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धा to have, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य|अधैर्य्यः
अधैर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Unsteady, feeble, irresolute.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Instability, want of firmness.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, धैर्य्य firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोंशुक|अधोंशुकं
अधोऽंशुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A lower garment.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् beneath, and अंशुक clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षज|अधोक्षजः
अधोक्षज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अधस, अक्ष an organ of sense, and ज who is produced; being produced by, or produced to, such as have subdued or cast down their passions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगत
अधोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Descended, gone down.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् down, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगति|अधोगतिः
अधोगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Going downwards, lit. or fig. descent, degradation. Also अधोगमः and अधोगमनं.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् and गति, &c. going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोगामिन्
अधोगामिन्<BR>n. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Descending, going downwards.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोघण्टा
अधोघण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>A plant, (Acheranthes aspera.) See अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and घटि to hurt, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोङ्ग
अधोङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 The anus.<BR>2 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोजिह्विका
अधोजिह्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The uvula or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् below, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोदृष्टि|अधोदृष्टिः
अधोदृष्टि<BR>mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि)<BR>Downcast, one who looks down.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोपर
अधोपर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The anus.<BR>2 Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोबन्धन
अधोबन्धन<BR>n. (नं)<BR>An under girth or strap.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभव
अधोभव<BR>n. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Placed below, inferior.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभाग|अधोभागः
अधोभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The bottom, the lowest part.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभागहर
अधोभागहर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Purging.<BR>E.<BR>अधोभाग the lower part (of the body,) हर what affects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोभुवन|अधोभुवनं
अधोभुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The regions below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् beneath, and भुवन a world; the world below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमर्म्मन्|अधोमर्मन्
अधोमर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and मर्म्मम् a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोमुख|अधोमुखः
अधोमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>1 Down-looked, looking downwards.<BR>2 Inverted, turned upside down.<BR>3 Headlong.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A plant, (Premna esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोयन्त्र
अधोयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A still, or the lower of two vessels luted together for distilling, sublimation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and यन्त्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोलम्व
अधोलम्व<BR>m. (-म्वः)<BR>A perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>अधस् below, लम्व a straight line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोलोक
अधोलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The regions below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवदन
अधोवदन<BR>n. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Down-looked: see अधोमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवश|अधोवशः
अधोवश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Bottom of a thing.<BR>2 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and वश dependance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोवायु|अधोवायुः
अधोवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The vital air that passes downwards.<BR>E.<BR>अधस्, and वायु air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोस्रपित्त
अधोस्रपित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Discharge of blood from the anus, urethra, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधम्, अस्रपित plethora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्ष|अध्यक्षः
अध्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Perceptible, present to the senses.<BR>2 Superintending, presiding over.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A superintendent in general, one of receipts and disbursements.<BR>2 A plant, (a species of Mimusops.) See क्षीरिका.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अक्ष to pervade, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षता
अध्यक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Superintendence: also अध्यक्षत्व. n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षर|अध्यक्षरं
अध्यक्षर<BR>n. (रं)<BR>The mysterious word Om.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अक्षर letter: above all others in importance or in place; being often put at the head of various writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यग्नि
अध्यग्नि<BR>ind.<BR>Gifts made to a woman at the time of her marriage.<BR>E.<BR>अधि near, over, &c. and अग्नि fire, being presented at the time that burnt offerings are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यण्डा|अध्यंडा
अध्यण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>अधि, अम to be diseased, and ड affix; superior to disease. See अव्यंगा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यय|अध्ययः
अध्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A lecture, a chapter or section.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before इक् to go, अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययन|अध्ययनं
अध्ययन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Study, reading, especially of the sacred books; one of the six duties of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, इङ् to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसाय|अध्यवसायः
अध्यवसाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Effort, exertion, determined application.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अव before षो to destroy, with the affixes घञ् and यक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायित
अध्यवसायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undertaken, attempted, as a difficult task.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अव before षो, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायिन्
अध्यवसायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Resolute, determined.<BR>E.<BR>अध्यवसाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशन|अध्यशनं
अध्यशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating too often, taking food before that previously eaten is digested.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्त|अध्यस्तं
अध्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Substituted.<BR>2 Placed over.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अस्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्थि
अध्यस्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>Bony exfoliation or deposit.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मन्
अध्यात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 The soul, individuated spirit, or that which belongs to and presides over the body.<BR>2 The supreme spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मिक
अध्यात्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Spiritual, relating to the supreme spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अध्यात्मन् and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मदृश्
अध्यात्मदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A holy sage, one who knows the nature of inherent spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अध्यात्मन, and दृश् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मरति
अध्यात्मरति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An anchorite, one who diligently meditates on the supreme spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अध्यात्मन्, and रति pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापक|अध्यापकः
अध्यापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A teacher, one who instructs in the sacred books.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and इङ् to go, in the causal form, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापन|अध्यापनं
अध्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Instructing, teaching the sacred books; one of the six duties of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, इङ to go, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापित
अध्यापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taught.<BR>E.<BR>अधीङ and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The section, or division of a book.<BR>2 A chapter or lecture of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, इङ to go, and घञ् aff. proper to be gone through or read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारूढ|अध्यारूढः
अध्यारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Mounted on, riding upon.<BR>2 Exceeding, very much.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and आङ before रुह to become manifest, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोप|अध्यारोपः
अध्यारोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=024" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपण|अध्यारोपणं
अध्यारोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Fixing in or upon.<BR>2 Transferring.<BR>3 Attaching erroneously the predicates of one object to another, as of eternity to matter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before रुह to grow, causal form ल्युट् affix, also with घञ् affix अध्यारोपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोह
अध्यारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Mounting or ascending.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and आङ before रुह to rise, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोहण
अध्यारोहण<BR>n. (-ण)<BR>Ascending, mounting on or upon.<BR>E.<BR>अधि and आङ before रुह to rise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिक|अध्यावाहनिकं
अध्यावाहनिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A woman's marriage portion, a dowry of such property as has descended to her lineally.<BR>E.<BR>अधि and आङ before वह to convey, ल्युट् affix, and ठक added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास|अध्यासः
अध्यास<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Inhabiting as chief, residing in, presiding over or ruling.<BR>2 Sitting on or upon.<BR>3 Transferring.<BR>4 Attributing erroneously the nature of one thing to another, as of eternity to matter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before, आस sit, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासित
अध्यासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seated in or on.<BR>2 Presiding over.<BR>3 Inhabited.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before, आस to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासीन
अध्यासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Seated in or on.<BR>2 Placed or presiding over.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरण|अध्याहरणं
अध्याहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>2 Reasoning, discussing.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, आङ prefixed to हृञ to convey, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहार|अध्याहारः
अध्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Adding a word or words to complete a sentence, supplying an ellipsis.<BR>2 Reasoning, argument.<BR>E.<BR>See अध्याहरण, घञ् being the aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहार्य्य|अध्याहार्य
अध्याहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Investigable.<BR>2 Requiring an ellipsis to be supplied.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and आङ before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहृत
अध्याहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Supplied as an ellipsis.<BR>2 Argued, discussed.<BR>E.<BR>अधि and आङ before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inhabited, settled.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before वस to dwell, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट्र|अध्युष्ट्रः
अध्युष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A litter drawn or carried by a camel.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and उष्ट्र a camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्यूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Very prosperous, thriving.<BR>2 Much.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A superseded wife, one whose husband has married others.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, and ऊढ borne, from वह to bear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतृ
अध्येतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>A student, reading, studying.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before इङ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषणा
अध्येषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Request, solicitation.<BR>2 Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>अधि, इष to wish, and ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अध्रुव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Unstable, unfixed, uncertain, transient, perishable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ध्रुव fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वग|अध्वगः
अध्वग<BR>mf. (-गः-गा)<BR>A traveller.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A name of the river Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes, from गम, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगमन
अध्वगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Journeying, travelling.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगामिन्
अध्वगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Travelling, a traveller.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वगभोग्य|अध्वगभोग्यः
अध्वगभोग्य<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>अध्वग a traveller, and भोग्य to be enjoyed by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्
अध्वन्<BR>m. (-ध्वा)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 Fixing, placing.<BR>3 Time.<BR>4 Assault.<BR>5 Correcting viscidity, dilution of the phlegm and marrow.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go constantly, क्वनिप् affix; ध substituted for त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीन|अध्वनीनः
अध्वनीन<BR>mf. (-नः-ना)<BR>A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्य|अध्वन्यः
अध्वन्य<BR>mf. (-न्यः-न्या)<BR>A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर|अध्वरः
अध्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sacrifice.<BR>2 A Vasu, or a kind of demigod.<BR>3 Intent, attentive, careful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ध्वृ^1 to bend or make crooked, and अच् affix; or अध्व a road, and र from रा to give; leading to heaven.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: cf. WIL, MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरथ|अध्वरथः
अध्वरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A travelling carriage or cart.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन् a road, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्य्यु<BR>m. (-र्य्युः)<BR>A Brahman versed in the Yajurveda.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वर a sacrifice, क्यच् and उ affix, अ being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वशल्य|अध्वशल्यः
अध्वशल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.) See अपमार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वन्, and शल्य a stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्त|अध्वांतं|अध्वान्तः
अध्वान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Gloom, twilight.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ध्यान्त darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वान्तशात्रव|अध्वान्तशात्रवः
अध्वान्तशात्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.) See पत्रोर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ध्वान्त darkness, शावव inimical; blossoming in the shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन|अनः
अन<BR>(घ) r. 2d cl. (अनिति) Also of 4th cl. (ङ) (अन्यते)<BR>To breathe, to live See अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंश
अनंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Portionless, not entitled to a share or portion.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंशुमत्फला
अनंशुमत्फला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plantain, (Musa sapientum.) See अंशुमत्फला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Inferior, low. See अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष|अनक्षः
अनक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-का-क्षं)<BR>Blind, eyeless.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अक्षि the eye, the final dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षर|अनक्षरं
अनक्षर<BR>n. (-र)<BR>1 Blamable discourse, what is unfit to be uttered.<BR>2 Abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षि
अनक्षि<BR>mfn. (-क्षिः-क्षिः-क्षि)<BR>Having bad eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगार|अनगारः
अनगार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A saint, an anchorite.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अगार a house; living in woods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नि|अनग्निः
अनग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A Brahman who has not maintained his household fire.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघ|अनघः
अनघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>1 Clean, clear.<BR>2 Pure, sinless.<BR>2 Handsome, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अघ fault, faultless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्ग|अनंग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR>m. (-हृ)<BR>A name of KĀMA, the Hindu deity of love.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Heaven, aether or the atmosphere.<BR>2 The mind or faculty of reasoning.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अङ्ग body; as applicable to KĀMA, it alludes to his having been reduced to ashes, by the eye of ŚIVA, for having disturbed his devotions, and rendered him enamoured of PĀRVATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गक|अनंगकं|अनङ्गकं
अनङ्गक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The mind or faculty of reasoning.<BR>E.<BR>अनङ्ग, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनङ्गासुहृद्
अनङ्गासुहृद्<BR>m. (-हृद or -हृत्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अनङ्ग KĀMA, अ neg. and सुहृद् a friend, the foe of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनच्छ|अनच्छः
अनच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Turbid, muddy.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अच्छ clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनञ्जन|अनंजन|अनञ्जनं
अनञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The sky, atmosphere, aether.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्ज to go, with the neg. prefix अन्, and affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह्
अनडुह्<BR>m. (-ड्वान्)<BR>A bull or ox.<BR>f. (-डुही or -ड्वाही)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>अनस् a cart, वह to bear, and क्विप् affix, with ड inserted: after अनस्, व is changed to उ in the mas., optionally in the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=025" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणु|अनणुः
अनणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>Small grain.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अणु an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनत
अनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Erect, not bowed down.<BR>2 Proud, haughty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतता
अनतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Erectness, stiffness.<BR>2 Pride. also अनतत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रम
अनतिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Moderation, mediocrity, equality, not over. stepping certain limits, not surpassing certain qualities, &c.<BR>2 Propriety, decorum.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अतिक्रम exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रम्य
अनतिक्रम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Not having transgressed, &c.<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्य)<BR>Incapable of being transgressed or exceeded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अतिक्रम्य having surpassed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिक्रान्त
अनतिक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Unsurpassed, unexceeded.<BR>2 Untransgressed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अतिक्रान्त surpassed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनतिरिक्त
अनतिरिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Equal, not exceeded in quantity or quality.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आंतक्त more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकार|अनधिकारः
अनधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Absence of right, claim, interest or concern.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिकार right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारचर्च्चा|अनधिकारचर्चा
अनधिकारचर्च्चा<BR>f. (-र्च्चा)<BR>Officiousness, meddling with other people's business.<BR>E.<BR>अनधिकार, and चर्च्चा investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारिन्
अनधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A non-heir, one who has no right or claim.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिकारिन् an heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकृत
अनधिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uninherited, unclaimed.<BR>2 Not set over, or appointed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिकृत claimed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगत|अनधिगतः
अनधिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not acquired.<BR>2 Not learnt or studied.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिगत gone over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगम
अनधिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Non-acquirement.<BR>2 Non-perusal.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिगम obtaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगम्य
अनधिगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Unattainable.<BR>2 Incapable of being known.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिगम्य to be attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिष्ठित
अनधिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Absent, not present.<BR>2 Not placed over, not appointed.<BR>3 Not ordered or enjoined.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधिष्ठित placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीन|अनधीनः
अनधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Independent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यक्ष|अनध्यक्षः
अनध्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Imperceptible, unperceived, absent. See अप्रत्यक्ष.<BR>2 Having no superintendent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अध्यक्ष perceptible, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्याय|अनध्यायः
अनध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Intermission of study.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अध्याय reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यायदिवस
अनध्यायदिवस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A day on which it is improper to study.<BR>E.<BR>अनध्याय, and दिबस a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुज्ञात
अननुज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Denied, refused, not assented to.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अनुज्ञात assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त|अनंत|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अनन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Eternal, endless.<BR>2 Unbounded, illimitable.<BR>3 Infinite, innumerable.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 BALADEVA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 The chief of the Nāgas or serpent race, that inhabit the infernal regions: the couch and constant attendant of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 The king of serpents, confounded with VĀSUKI. See वासुकि.<BR>5 The fourteenth of the Jaina Tīrthakaras or deified Saints: also called अनन्तजित्.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A name of PĀRVATĪ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A synonym of several plants, (as Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>4 A kind of potherb. See विशल्या.<BR>5 Bent grass, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR>6 Another plant, (Echites frutescens, Rox.) See श्यामा. Or according to others, (Asclepias psoudosarsa, Rox.) See शारीवा.<BR>7 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia citrina.)<BR>9 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>9 Another plant, (Menispermum glabrum.) See गुडुची.<BR>10 Long pepper. See कणा.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Sky or atmosphere, aether.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तक|अनंतक
अनन्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Endless, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तचतुर्दशी|अनन्तचतुर्द्दशी
अनन्तचतुर्दशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The fourteenth lunation of the light half of Bhadra, when ANANTA is worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and चतुर्दशी the fourteenth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तजित्
अनन्तजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The fourteenth of the twenty-four Jaina deified Saints: also called अनन्त.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त endless, and जित् who conquers, who gains eternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तता
अनन्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Eternity: also अनन्तत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अनन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्ततीर्थकृत्
अनन्ततीर्थकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The fourteenth Jaina Saint, also अनन्त, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त endless, तीर्थ pilgrimage or virtue, and कृत् who has made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तमूल|अनन्तमूलः
अनन्तमूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Periploca Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तर|अनंतर|अनन्तरं
अनन्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Next, immediately following.<BR>2 Next of kin or in succession.<BR>3 Close, compact.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Extreme propinquity.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अन्तर between; having nothing intermediate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरज|अनन्तरजः
अनन्तरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born of the next in order; as of a Kṣatriya woman, by a Brahman; of a Vaiśya woman, by a Kṣatriya.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्तर, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तराशि|अनन्तराशिः
अनन्तराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>In arithmetic; infinite quantity.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त endless, राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तरूप
अनन्तरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Multiform.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवात|अनन्तवातः
अनन्तवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Rigidity or paralysis of the muscles of the face and neck.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तविजय|अनन्तविजयः
अनन्तविजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The shell of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and बिजय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तवीर्य्य|अनन्तवीर्य|अनन्तवीर्यः|अनन्तवीर्य्यः
अनन्तवीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The twenty third Jaina Tīrthakara of a future age.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त endless, and वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तव्रत|अनन्तव्रतं
अनन्तव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A ceremony performed in honour of VIṢṆU, on the day of the full moon in Bhādra.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त, and व्रत a religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्तशीर्षा
अनन्तशीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>The wife of VĀSUKI, the king of serpents.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त many, and शीर्ष a head; many headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्त्य|अनंत्य
अनन्त्य<BR>mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>Infinite, unbounded, eternal.<BR>n. (-त्य)<BR>1 Immortality.<BR>2 Eternity.<BR>3 Infinity.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्त्य final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अनन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 One, sole, without any other.<BR>2 Same, identical.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगति|अनन्यगतिः
अनन्यगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Having but one refuge.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>One only refuge or asylum.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्य, and गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यगतिक|अनन्यगतिकः
अनन्यगतिक<BR>mfn. (कः-का-कं)<BR>Having one refuge or hope alone.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यज|अनन्यजः
अनन्यज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य. other, and ज born; produced only in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यता
अनन्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Singleness.<BR>2 Identity.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्य, and ता or त्व affix; also अनन्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=026" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यपूर्व्व|अनन्यपूर्व|अनन्यपूर्वः
अनन्यपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Intact, virgin, never in the prior possession of another.<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A virgin, a girl not previously wedded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य another, पूर्व्व prior; also with कन् added अनन्यपूर्ष्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यभव
अनन्यभव<BR>mfn. (वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced or effected by one particular person or thing.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्य, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यमनस्
अनन्यमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यमनस्क
अनन्यमनस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Intent, attentive, having the mind fixed on one subject, not absent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्यमनस् or अन्यसनस्क thinking of some thing else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यवृत्ति|अनन्यवृत्तिः
अनन्यवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Closely attentive, having the mind fixed on one object.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य other, वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यहृत
अनन्यहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not stolen or taken, safe.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य another, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यहार्य्य
अनन्यहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Incapable of being taken or stolen.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्य another, हार्य्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वित
अनन्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconnected with, irrelevant.<BR>2 Devoid of, not possessing.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकरण|अनपकरणं
अनपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Non-requital, not retaliating.<BR>2 Non-resumption.<BR>3 Not doing ill.<BR>E.<BR>अन् before अपकरण evil doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकर्म्म
अनपकर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Non-retaliation.<BR>2 Non-resumption, (of a thing given or paid, &c.)<BR>3 Abstaining from evil.<BR>E.<BR>अन् before अपकर्म्म; also अनपाकर्म्म, अनपक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकार|अनपकारः
अनपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Harmlessness, freedom from hatred and malice.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपकार evil doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकारिन्
अनपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Innecuous.<BR>E.<BR>अनपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपक्रिया
अनपक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Non-requital, non-retaliation.<BR>2 Non-acquittance (as of debt, &c.)<BR>3 Non-resumption.<BR>4 Abstaining from offence or evil.<BR>E.<BR>अन् before अपक्रिया offence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपचित
अनपचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dishonoured, disregarded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपचित honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्य
अनपत्य<BR>mfn. (-कः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Childless, having no progeny: so अनपत्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं).<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपर
अनपर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपर another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराध|अनपराधः
अनपराध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Innocence.<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Innocent, sinless.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराधिन्
अनपराधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Innocent, sinless.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपराधिन् offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपाय|अनपायः
अनपाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undiminished, unceasing.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Permanence, absence of loss or diminution.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपायिन्
अनपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Firm, constant, durable, imperishable.<BR>2 Increasing.<BR>E.<BR>अनपाय permanence, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्ष|अनपेक्षं
अनपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Disregarding, unheeding.<BR>f. (क्षा)<BR>Carelessness, indifference, disregard.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. अपेक्षा regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्षित
अनपेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unheeded, disregarded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अपेक्षित regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेत
अनपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Present, not passed or gone.<BR>2 Possessed of, not devoid of.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. अपेत gone away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिमत
अनभिमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disagreeable, unpleasant, disastrous, unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिमत liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिज्ञ|अनभिज्ञः
अनभिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञ)<BR>Unwise, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिज्ञ wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिभव
अनभिभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Freedom from obstruction or defeat.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिभव defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिभूत
अनभिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unsubdued, unsurpassed.<BR>2 Unobstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिभूत subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलाष|अनभिलाषः
अनभिलाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Indifference, absence of desire.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिलाष desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलाषिन्
अनभिलाषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-वि)<BR>Indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अनभिलाष, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिव्यक्त
अनभिव्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Indistinct, dim.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिव्यक्त clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिष्वङ्ग|अनभिष्वंग
अनभिष्वङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Detachment, disconnection, freedom from affection or attachment.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अभिष्वङ्ग connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनम|अनमः
अनम<BR>mfn. (-मः)<BR>A Brahman, one who does not salute a Brahman, making obeisance to the gods only, and returning salutations with his blessing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and नम who salutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमस्य
अनमस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Unworthy of being saluted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नमस्य to be saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनय|अनयः
अनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Fate.<BR>2 Ill-luck, bad-fortune.<BR>3 Calamity, distress.<BR>4 Vice, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अय good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनयङ्गत|अनयंगत
अनयङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fallen into misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>अनय, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्गल|अनर्गलं
अनर्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अर्गल a bolt or bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्य
अनर्घ्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ध्यः-र्ध्या-र्ध्यं)<BR>Invaluable, priceless, not to be bought.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्य्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्यत्व
अनर्घ्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Absence of price or cost, invaluableness; also अनर्ध्यता.<BR>E.<BR>त्व or ता added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्च्चित|अनर्चित
अनर्च्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unworshipped, unreverenced, disrespected.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्च्चित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ|अनर्थः
अनर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Unmeaning, fruitless, nonsensical.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्थ use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थक|अनर्थकं
अनर्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unmeaning, idle, fruitless.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Unmeaning or nonsensical discourse.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्थ meaning, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह
अनर्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Unfit, unworthy, unsuitable.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अर्ह fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल|अनलं|अनलः
अनल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>2 One of the eight Vasus or demigods^1 so called.<BR>3 Bile.<BR>4 A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica and rosea.)<BR>E.<BR>अन् to be, and कलच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलप्रिया
अनलप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The wife of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>अनल, and प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलम्
अनलम्<BR>ind.<BR>Insufficient, unequal, unable, not enough.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अलम् enough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलि|अनलिः
अनलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A plant, (Æschynomene grandiflora.) See अगस्तिद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवगीत
अनवगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Excellent, good, uncensured.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अघगीत disparaged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवग्रह
अनवग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Resistless, not to be obstructed or impeded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवग्रह obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्य
अनवद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Blameless, irreproachable.<BR>2 Unobjectionable, allowable.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवद्य censurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधान|अनवधानं
अनवधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Careless, inattentive.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inadvertence, inattention, carelessness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधानता
अनवधानता<BR>f. (ता)<BR>Inadvertence, inattention.<BR>E.<BR>ता affix, subjoined to the preceding; or with त्व, अनवधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवर|अनवरः
अनवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Equal or superior, not younger nor inferior.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवर inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=027" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरत|अनवरतं
अनवरत<BR>adj. mfn. or adv. n. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eternal, eternally, continually.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवरत stopped, ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरार्द्ध
अनवरार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवरार्द्ध inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलम्व
अनवलम्व<BR>mfn. (-म्वः-म्वा-म्वं)<BR>Without support or dependance.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवलम्व support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसर|अनवसरः
अनवसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Occupied, busy, having no leisure.<BR>2 Unseasonable, inopportune.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Want of leisure or opportunity.<BR>2 Unseasonableness, inopportuneness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवसर leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्कर|अनवस्करं
अनवस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Clean.<BR>E.<BR>अन् priv. and अवस्कर dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थ
अनवस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Unstable, unsteady.<BR>2 Incontinent.<BR>f. (स्था)<BR>1 Instability, absence of fixed state or condition. Uncertainty, doubt.<BR>3 Incontinence, dissoluteness.<BR>4 (In logic,) the abstract nature of a thing, independent of its existence.<BR>E.<BR>अम् neg. अवस्था condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थान|अनवस्थानः
अनवस्थान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unsteady, mutable, variable, not stationary.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Instability.<BR>2 Wrong situation or direction.<BR>3 Misconduct.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Wind.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवस्थान fixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थित
अनवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unfixed, unsteady, unstable, inconstant.<BR>2 Loose, abandoned, violating moral and legal restraint.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अवस्थित steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थिति|अनवस्थितिः
अनवस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Unsteadiness, instability.<BR>2 Dissoluteness, profligacy.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अवस्थिति stability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवाप्त
अनवाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Unobtained.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. अवाप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशन|अनशनं
अनशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>One who fasts.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fast, fasting.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वर|अनश्वरं
अनश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Eternal, imperishable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and नश्वर transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्
अनस्<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>1 A cart.<BR>2 Boiled rice.<BR>3 A mother.<BR>4 Birth.<BR>5 Life, breath.<BR>E.<BR>अन् to live, and असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूय
अनसूय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not envious.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 The wife of the sage ATRI.<BR>2 Exemption from envy.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. असूया envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अनसूयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unenvious.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. असूया, and कन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयु
अनसूयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Free from envy.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. असूय to envy, उस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कार|अनहंकार
अनहङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Absence of pride, humility.<BR>2 The absence of the pride of individuality: one of the elements of creation, according to the Vedānta system.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अहङ्कार pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कारिन्|अनहंकारिन्
अनहङ्कारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रणी-रि)<BR>Philosophical, humble, not proud, not selfish.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. अहङ्कारिन् proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहङ्कृति|अनहंकृति|अनहङ्कृतिः
अनहङ्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Content, satisfaction, the absence of care or vanity.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and अहङ्कृति pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकार
अनाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Shapeless, without form.<BR>E.<BR>अट् neg. आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाल|अनाकालः
अनाकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Scarcity, famine.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आङ before काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकालभृत|अनाकालभृतः
अनाकालभृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A slave, one who has given himself to slavery, in a season of scarcity, for support.<BR>E.<BR>अनाकाल, and भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अनाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unperplexed, collected, composed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आकुल perplexed, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रान्त|अनाक्रांत
अनाक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Unsurpassed, unsubdued.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A sort of prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini, WILD.) See कण्ठकारी.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आक्रान्त surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षारित
अनाक्षारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not calumniated, free from reproach or censure.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आक्षारित censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागत|अनागतं
अनागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not come, not arrived: (of a person, absent;) future, (of time.)<BR>2 Unknown, undistinguished.<BR>3 Not acquired, learned or obtained.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आगत come, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतार्तवा|अनागतार्त्तवा
अनागतार्तवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A young girl, one not arrived at puberty.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आगत arrived, and आर्तव from ऋतु the menstrual flux, who has not menstruated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अनागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Non-arrival of person or time.<BR>2 Non-acquisition.<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Not arrived, not present.<BR>2 Not having or obtaining.<BR>3 Not scriptural.<BR>4 Not having vouchers or deeds.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आगम arrival, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम्य
अनागम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Unapproachable, inaccessible.<BR>2 Unobtainable.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आगम्य to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचरण
अनाचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Improper or immoral conduct.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आचरण moral rule or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार|अनाचारः
अनाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Immoral, ill behaved, indecent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Impropriety, violation of moral or civil rule or institute.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आचार moral rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचारिन्
अनाचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Immoral, indecorous, indecent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आचारिन् decent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाढ्य
अनाढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>Poor, without wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आढ्य rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अनातप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Shade, shadow.<BR>2 Coolness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आतप heat, moral or physical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अनातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Well, vigorous, free from sickness or pain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. आतुर diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मनीन
अनात्मनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ता-नं)<BR>Disinterested, liberal, not regarding self alone.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आत्मनीन selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अनाथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Without a master or protector, without a husband, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नाथ master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अनादर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादि|अनादिः
अनादि<BR>mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि)<BR>Eternal, without any beginning, unborn, uncreate.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादित्व|अनादित्वं
अनादित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Eternity, exemption from commencement or birth. Also अनादिता.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिष्ट
अनादिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Denied, refused, dissented.<BR>2 Not directed, advised or commanded.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आदिष्ट directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादीनव
अनादीनव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Pure, faultless.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आदीनव faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अनादृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespected, despised.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आदृत respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेय
अनादेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Inadmissable, unacceptable, not to be taken or received.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आदेय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्य
अनाधृष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Unconquerable, indomitable.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आधृष्य to be tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापन्न
अनापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Unobtained, unattained.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आपन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अनाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Unskilful, unapt.<BR>2 Uneffected, unobtained.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आप्त fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=028" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामक|अनामकं|अनामकः
अनामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Nameless, noteless.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The intercalary month.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Piles or hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अ bad, नामक from नामन् a name, with कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The ring finger. See अनामिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अनामय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Health.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिका
अनामिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The ring finger.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and नामिका deriv. of नामन् a name, having no other name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत
अनायत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unchecked, unrestrained.<BR>2 Close, continuous, unseparated.<BR>3 Unextended, having no length.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आयत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Independent, uncontrolled.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आयत्त dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्तवृत्तिता
अनायत्तवृत्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Independence, self subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>अनायत्त, and वृत्ति or वृत्तिता business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Exemption from pain or difficulty, facility, ease.<BR>2 Absence of exertion, idleness, neglect.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आयास effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायासकृत|अनायासकृतं
अनायासकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done readily or easily.<BR>2 In medicine, prepared extemporaneously, simply decocted, (medicine or drugs.)<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आयास effort, pains, and कृत made, made without trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Crookedness, moral or physical.<BR>2 Disease.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आर्जव straightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत<BR>adj. mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) adv. n. (-तं)<BR>Eternal, eternally.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आ prefixed to रम to be pleased, क्त affixed; having no rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारम्भ|अनारंभः|अनारम्भः
अनारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Defect of commencement, being without a beginning.<BR>2 Non-commencement, not attempting or undertaking.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्य
अनारोग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Sickness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आरोग्य health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्यकर
अनारोग्यकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Unwholesome, unhealthy, causing sickness.<BR>E.<BR>अनारोग्य, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्य|अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Unworthy, inferior, bad, vile.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आर्य्य respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यक|अनार्यक|अनार्यकं|अनार्य्यकं
अनार्य्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Agallochum or aloe wood, (Aquila agallocha, Rox.) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यज|अनार्यज|अनार्य्यजं
अनार्य्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Of vile or unworthy origin.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Agallochum or aloe wood, (Aquila agallocha.) See अगुरु.<BR>E.<BR>अन् priv. आर्य्य respectable, and ज produced; the perfume being brought from the country of Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यता|अनार्यता
अनार्य्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Vileness, unworthiness, baseness; also अनार्य्यत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अनार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य्यतिक्त|अनार्यतिक्त|अनार्यतिक्तः|अनार्य्यतिक्तः
अनार्य्यतिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A medicinal plant, a kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अनार्य्य inferior, and तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालम्ब|अनालंब|अनालम्बः
अनालम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्वः-म्वा-म्वं)<BR>Unsupported, without stay or support.<BR>E.<BR>अन् gen. आलम्व support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालाप|अनालापः
अनालाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Silent, taciturn.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Taciturnity.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आलाप conversing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालोचित|अनालोचितः
अनालोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unseen, unbeheld.<BR>2 Unweighed, unconsidered, rash, imprudent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आलोचित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविल|अनाविलः
अनाविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Clear, clean, pure.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आविल turbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत|अनावृतः
अनावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uncovered, undressed.<BR>2 Open, uninclosed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्त
अनावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Not stirred or turned round.<BR>2 Not retreating.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, and आवृत्त whirled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृष्टि|अनावृष्टिः
अनावृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Drought.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आ before वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्य|अनाश्यः
अनाश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Indestructible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नाश्य to be destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रय|अनाश्रयः
अनाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Detachment, absence of attachment or dependance.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रित
अनाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Detached, disengaged, unconcerned in or unconnected with.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आश्रित dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्वस्
अनाश्वस्<BR>mfn. (-श्वान्-शुषी-श्वत्)<BR>Fasting, not eating.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आश्वस् eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादित
अनासादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not occurred, not having happened, non-existent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आसादित effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासिक|अनासिकः
अनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्था
अनास्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Disrespect.<BR>2 Want of fixity or condition.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आस्था station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहत|अनाहतं|अनाहतः
अनाहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unhurt, unbeaten, unwounded, intact.<BR>2 New and unbleached, (as cloth.)<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The fourth of the mystical Cakras or circles of the body.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and आहत beaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार|अनाहारः
अनाहार<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 Abstinence, starvation.<BR>2 Non-production.<BR>3 Non-seizure.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आहार food, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहारिन्
अनाहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Not seizing.<BR>2 Fasting.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, and आहारिन् who takes food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार्य्य|अनाहार्य
अनाहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Not to be seized or taken, not producible.<BR>2 Not to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आहार्य्य to be taken, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहुत
अनाहुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uncalled, unbidden: also अनाहूत.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. आहुत called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिक्षु|अनिक्षुः
अनिक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A sort of long grass or reed, (Saccharum spontaneum).<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and इक्षु sugar-cane; not it, but it's like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्ण|अनिगीर्णः|अनिगीर्ण्ण
अनिगीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-णं)<BR>Unuttered, unsaid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निगीर्ण uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रह|अनिग्रहः
अनिग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-क्षं)<BR>Unrestrained, unconfined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छ
अनिच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Undesirous, averse, indifferent: so अनिच्छक.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, and इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छा
अनिच्छा<BR>f. (-छा)<BR>Indifference, absence of wish or desire.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. इच्छा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिछु|अनिच्छु|अनिच्छुः
अनिछु<BR>mfn. (-छुः-छुः-छु)<BR>1 Disliking, not wishing.<BR>2 Indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. इच्छु who wishes: also अनिच्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अनित्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Transient, not everlasting.<BR>2 Occasional, incidental.<BR>3 Irregular, unusual.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नित्य constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यक्रिया
अनित्यक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>An occasional act of worship, sacrifice for a special purpose.<BR>E.<BR>अनित्य occasional, not constant, and क्रिया rite, also अनित्यकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यता
अनित्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Transient or limited existence: also अनित्यत्व.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्यसम|अनित्यसमः
अनित्यसम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Arguing by illustration, not by logical rule.<BR>E.<BR>अनित्य unusual, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिदान
अनिदान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निदान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद्र
अनिद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Awake, sleepless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=029" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्दित|अनिन्दितः
अनिन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pious, virtuous, free, unreproachable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and निन्दित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन्द्य
अनिन्द्य<BR>mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्य)<BR>Faultless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निन्द्य blamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपुण|अनिपुणः
अनिपुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unskilled, unlearned, not conversant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निपुण clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबद्ध
अनिबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unproduced, unseized.<BR>2 Unasked.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निवद्ध attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृत
अनिभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unsteady (as the mind), agitated.<BR>2 Tremulous, moving.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निभृत held firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिष|अनिमिषं|अनिमिषः
अनिमिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A god.<BR>2 A fish.<BR>3 A person whose eyes are fixed, (as in disease, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and निमिष what twinkles; the eyes being always fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषाचार्य्य|अनिमिषाचार्य|अनिमिषाचार्यः|अनिमिषाचार्य्यः
अनिमिषाचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>अनिमिष a deity, and आचार्य्य a teacher; the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A fish.<BR>3 A demon.<BR>4 A spirit or ghost.<BR>5 A person whose eyes are fixed. See अनिमिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियत|अनियतं
अनियत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Transitory, perishable.<BR>2 Unrestrained.<BR>3 Undefined, unprescribed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नियत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियम|अनियमः
अनियम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Uncertainty, doubt.<BR>2 Absence of moral or religious obligation.<BR>3 Indecorous or improper conduct.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undetermined, undefined, unprovided for, by any rule or law.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नियम fixed observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिराकृत|अनिराकृतः
अनिराकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unchecked, unobstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निराकृत opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्ध|अनिरुद्धं|अनिरुद्धः
अनिरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary.<BR>2 Self willed, ungovernable, headstrong.<BR>3 Unobstructed, unrestrained.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>The son of PRADYUMNA, a form of KĀMA, and husband of UṢĀ.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>The rope for fastening cattle.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निरुद्ध restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धपथ|अनिरुद्धपथं
अनिरुद्धपथ<BR>n. (-थ)<BR>1 The atmosphere, aether.<BR>2 An unobstructed path.<BR>E.<BR>अनिरुद्ध unobstructed, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्धभाविनी
अनिरुद्धभाविनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A proper name. See उषा.<BR>E.<BR>अनिरुद्ध, and भाविनी a wife; the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णय|अनिर्णयः
अनिर्णय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्णय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णीत
अनिर्णीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unascertained, undetermined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्णीत ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णेय
अनिर्णेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undecidable, incapable of being decided. अ<BR>E.<BR>neg. निर्णेय decidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दिष्ट
अनिर्दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Unexplained, undefined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्दिष्ट explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश|अनिर्देशः
अनिर्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Absence of demonstration or direction.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्दिश instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्द्धारित
अनिर्द्धारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unascertained, undetermined, undefined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्द्धारित defined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्भर
अनिर्भर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Little, slight, light.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्भर bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्म्मल|अनिर्मल|अनिर्म्मलः
अनिर्म्मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Dirty, foul. अ<BR>E.<BR>neg. निर्म्मल clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्माल्या|अनिर्म्माल्या
अनिर्माल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A plant, (Medicago esculenta, Rox.) See पृका.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, निर् out from, and माल्य from माला a necklace; not used in garlands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीय|अनिर्व्वचनीयः
अनिर्वचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be mentioned or described, indescribable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्वचनीय describable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्वाह|अनिर्वाह|अनिर्वाहः|अनिर्व्वाहः
अनिर्व्वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Incoherence, want of connexion or consistency.<BR>2 Want of means of subsistence.<BR>3 Incompleteness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्व्वाह connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्विण्ण|अनिर्विण्ण|अनिर्व्विण्णः
अनिर्व्विण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Disgusted.<BR>2 Poor, needy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्व्विण्ण satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्विद|अनिर्विद
अनिर्व्विद<BR>mfn. (-वित्)<BR>Free from pain or trouble.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्व्विद what annoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्वृत|अनिर्वृत
अनिर्व्वृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Discontented.<BR>2 Unquiet discomposed.<BR>3 Unaccomplished, unfulfilled.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्व्वृत effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्व्वृति|अनिर्वृति|अनिर्वृतिः
अनिर्व्वृति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>1 Poverty.<BR>2 Discontent.<BR>3 Incompleteness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निर्व्वृति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिल|अनिलः
अनिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Air or wind, considered also as a deity.<BR>2 A subordinate deity, forty-nine of whom form a class, ANILAS or winds.<BR>2 One of another class of demigods or Vasus.<BR>4 Wind, as one of the humors of the body.<BR>5 Rheumatism, paralysis, or any affection referred to disorder of the wind.<BR>E.<BR>अन to breathe, इलट् aff.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The fifteenth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion. See स्वाति.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल and the fem. termination: the wind being the ruling deity of the constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलघ्नक|अनिलघ्नकः
अनिलघ्नक<BR>m.<BR>A large tree, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, घ्न what removes, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलपर्य्यय|अनिलपर्यय
अनिलपर्य्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Pain and swelling of the eyelids and outer parts of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, and पर्य्यय pervasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलसख|अनिलसखः
अनिलसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, and सखि a friend, the friend of the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलात्मज|अनिलात्मजः
अनिलात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of the wind, HANUMAN or BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलामय|अनिलामयः
अनिलामय<BR>m. (यः-)<BR>1 Flatulence.<BR>2 Morbid affection of the wind, rheumatism, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलाशिन्
अनिलाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिणी-शि)<BR>Fasting, lit. feeding on the wind.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोचित
अनिलोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconsidered, inconsiderate, imprudent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निलोचित regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोडित
अनिलोडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconsidered, ill judged, undiscriminated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निलोडित revolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवारित
अनिवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unchecked, unimpeded, unopposed, unforbidden.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निवारित checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश|अनिशं
अनिश<BR>n. (-शः)<BR>Eternally, eternal, (not employed as an adjective.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and निश from निशा night; having no night or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश्चित|अनिश्चितः
अनिश्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unascertained, not certain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निश्चित ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ट|अनिष्टः
अनिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Unwished, undesirable, bad, unlucky.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A plant, (Sida alba.)<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ठा
अनिष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>Unsteadfastness, unsteadiness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निष्ठा fixedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्णात|अनिष्णातः
अनिष्णात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unskilful, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निष्णात clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पन्न|अनिष्पन्नः
अनिष्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निष्यन्न completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषिद्ध
अनिषिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Unprohibited, unforbidden.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निषिद्ध prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिसर्ग
अनिसर्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>Unnaturally elated or depressed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निसर्ग natural condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्ण
अनिस्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Unanswered, unrefuted.<BR>2 Not set aside or got over.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. निस्तीर्ण replied to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीक|अनीकं|अनीकः
अनीक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 An army, forces.<BR>2 War, combat.<BR>E.<BR>अन् to live, and ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=030" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकस्थ|अनीकस्थः
अनीकस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 An armed or royal guard, a centinel.<BR>2 A warrior, a combatant.<BR>3 The trainer of an elephant, an elephant driver.<BR>4 A mark, a sign, a signal.<BR>5 A military drum.<BR>E.<BR>अनीक battle, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकिनी
अनीकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 An army, a host, forces.<BR>2 A certain force; one-tenth of an Akṣauhiṇī, containing two thousand, one hundred and eighty-seven elephants, and as many cars, six thousand, five hundred and sixty-seven horse, and ten thousand, nine hundred and thirty-five foot.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अनीक an army, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीच
अनीच<BR>mfn. (चः-चा-च)<BR>Decent, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नीच low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचानुवर्त्तिन्|अनीचानुवर्तिन्
अनीचानुवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Not keeping low or improper company.<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A faithful lover or husband.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नीच low, अनुवर्त्तिन् following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीचदर्शिन्
अनीचदर्शिन्<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>A Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नीच low, दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीति|अनीतिः
अनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Impropriety, immorality.<BR>2 Impolicy, ill conduct.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. नाति good conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीदृश
अनीदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Unlike, dissimilar.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ईदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश|अनीशः
अनीश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>One who has not a lord or superior.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वर
अनीश्वर<BR>mfn. (रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Without a superior.<BR>2 Unchecked, uncontrolled.<BR>3 Without power, powerless, unable.<BR>4 Atheist.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ईश्वर a supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरता
अनीश्वरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Absence of a supreme ruler.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to the last: also अनीश्वरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वरवादिन्
अनीश्वरवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An atheist, one who denies a supreme ruler of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>अनीश्वर, and वादिन् who asserts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीह|अनीहः
अनीह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Careless, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहा
अनीहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Indifference, apathy, disinclination.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहित
अनीहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disagreeable, displeasing, unwished.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Displeasure.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, and ईहित desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु<BR>ind.<BR>A preposition and prefix, implying<BR>1 After.<BR>2 Like, in same manner.<BR>3 Under, inferior to.<BR>4 Along, lengthwise.<BR>5 With, together with.<BR>6 In part of.<BR>7 Severally, each, by each.<BR>8 Near to.<BR>9 In regard to.<BR>10 To, out to, (calling.)<BR>11 Orderly, methodical.<BR>As अनुकर्त्तुं to act like; अनुगन्तुं to follow; अनुकमितुं to proceed in order; अनुशयितुं to repent, &c.; also, अनुरूपं according to the form; अनुविष्णु according to VIṢṆU; अनुगं गं upon or along the Ganges. See also the following words.<BR>E.<BR>अन् to live, and ज aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-क)<BR>Lustful, libidinous.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and क from कम to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथन|अनुकथनं
अनुकथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Discourse, conversation.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and कथन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्पा|अनुकंपा
अनुकम्पा<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>Tenderness, compassion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before कपि to tremble, and affix अच्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकम्प्य|अनुकंप्य|अनुकम्प्यः
अनुकम्प्य<BR>mfn. (-म्प्यः-म्प्या-म्प्यं)<BR>1 Swift, expeditious.<BR>2 Pitiable, worthy of tenderness or compassion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before कपि to tremble, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरण|अनुकरणं
अनुकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Imitation, making or doing any thing like or in imitation of another, following an example.<BR>2 Resemblance, similarity.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्म्मन्|अनुकर्मन्
अनुकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>2 A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्ष|अनुकर्षः
अनुकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 The bottom of a carriage.<BR>2 Invoking, summoning by incantation.<BR>3 Attraction, drawing.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before कृष to drag or furrow, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षण|अनुकर्षणं
अनुकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Invoking, summoning by incantations.<BR>2 Attracting, attraction.<BR>3 Including a subsequent in a preceding rule.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and कृष to draw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षन्
अनुकर्षन्<BR>m. (-र्षा)<BR>The bottom of a carriage. See अनुकर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकल्प|अनुकल्पः
अनुकल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 An alternative, a substitute.<BR>2 A secondary, subsidiary or succedaneous injunction; as, instead of Kuśa grass use Dūrbbā.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and कल्प a principal precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामम्
अनुकामम्<BR>ind.<BR>According to wish or inclination.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामीन|अनुकामीनः
अनुकामीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 One who goes as he lists.<BR>2 One who acts as he pleases.<BR>E.<BR>अनुकामं and ईन, for गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकार|अनुकारः
अनुकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>2 Resemblance.<BR>E.<BR>अनु like, and कृञ् to do, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारिन्
अनुकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रणी-रि)<BR>Imitating, an imitator.<BR>E.<BR>अनुकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूल|अनुकूलः
अनुकूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Friendly, well disposed to, favourable or conformable to.<BR>m. (-ल)<BR>A faithful husband.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Croton polyandrum.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Favour, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and कूल race, family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलता
अनुकूलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Concord, good will, consent.<BR>E.<BR>अनुकूल, and ता affix; also with त्व, अनुकूलत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृत
अनुकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Copied, imitated, made like or done in like manner.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रकच
अनुक्रकच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Serrated, dentated.<BR>E.<BR>अनु like, क्रकत्र a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम|अनुक्रमः
अनुक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Order, method.<BR>E.<BR>अनु methodically, and क्रम to go, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमण|अनुक्रमणं
अनुक्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Proceeding methodically or in order.<BR>2 Following.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and कसण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणिका
अनुक्रमणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A table or chapter of contents.<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रान्त
अनुक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Done methodically, passed over, read, &c. in due order.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and क्रान्त gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रिया
अनुक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Imitation, doing any thing subsequently or in like manner.<BR>2 A subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रोश|अनुक्रोशः
अनुक्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Tenderness, compassion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, क्रुश to bewail, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षण|अनुक्षणं
अनुक्षण<BR>n. adv. (-णं)<BR>Momentarily, perpetually.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and क्षण a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग|अनुगः
अनुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Following.<BR>2 A follower, a servant.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A husband, a master.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगत|अनुगतः
अनुगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Followed, literally or figuratively, as by a dependant, &c.<BR>2 Following, a follower or a dependant.<BR>3 Acquired, obtained.<BR>4 Determined, defined.<BR>E.<BR>अन, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम|अनुगमः
अनुगम<BR>m. (मः)<BR>1 Following, going after in life or death.<BR>2 Imitating, approaching.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमन|अनुगमनं
अनुगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going after, following.<BR>2 Dying after, as of a widow. See अनुमरण.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=031" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम्य
अनुगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Worthy of being followed or imitated.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गम्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगवीन|अनुगवीनः
अनुगवीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गवीन belonging to kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामिन्
अनुगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 A companion, a follower.<BR>2 One who goes behind or after.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after or with, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुण|अनुगुणः
अनुगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-ण)<BR>According or suitable to, according to merit or property.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगृहीत
अनुगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Favoured, obliged.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and गृहीत^1 taken.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्र
अनुग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Calm, gentle, not violent.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, neg. उग्र fierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रह|अनुग्रहः
अनुग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Favour; conferring benefits, promoting good, and preventing ill.<BR>E.<BR>अनु afterwards, ग्रह to take, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राहिन्
अनुग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Gracious, favourable.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर|अनुचरः
अनुचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A companion, a follower.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female companion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with or after, and चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचारिन्
अनुचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Following, attending.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचित
अनुचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Improper, wrong.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्ता|अनुचिंता
अनुचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Thinking of, meditating upon, recalling, recollecting.<BR>E.<BR>अनु subsequent, चिन्ता thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिन्तित
अनुचिन्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Recollected, recalled, thought of.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and चिन्तित thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्च
अनुच्च<BR>mfn. (-च्चः-च्चा-च्चं)<BR>Low, not high, humble.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. उच्च high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिष्ट|अनुच्छिष्टः
अनुच्छिष्ट<BR>mfn. (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pure, purified by austerity and devotion.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and उच्छिष्ट rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज|अनुजं|अनुजः
अनुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born after, later, younger.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A younger brother.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A younger sister.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्मन्
अनुजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Younger, junior.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजात|अनुजातः
अनुजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>After-born, later, younger.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A younger brother.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A younger sister.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्झित
अनुज्झित<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undiminished, unimpaired, not left or lost.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उज्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविन्
अनुजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Servant, dependant.<BR>2 A companion, a follower.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after or with, and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 An order or command.<BR>2 Assent.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, ज्ञा to know, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञात
अनुज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ordered, directed, instructed.<BR>2 Assented to, permitted, allowed.<BR>3 Accepted.<BR>4 Acknowledged, recognised.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापक|अनुज्ञापकः
अनुज्ञापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who commands or enjoins.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and ज्ञापक who makes known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्त
अनुतप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Heated.<BR>2 Filled with regret or repentance.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनुतर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Fare, freight.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and तर what crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्ष|अनुतर्षः
अनुतर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 A drinking vessel, one used to drink spirituous liquors from. See अनुतर्षण.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and तष, from तृष to thirst, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षण|अनुतर्षणं
अनुतर्षण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>1 A vessel from which spirituous liquor is drunk.<BR>2 Distributing liquor.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before तृष to be thirsty, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुताप|अनुतापः
अनुताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Repentance.<BR>2 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>अनु afterwards, and ताप heat, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापिन्
अनुतापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Penitent, regretting.<BR>E.<BR>अनुताप and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्क
अनुत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Free from regret, possessed of self-complacency.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उत्क sorry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्कर्ष
अनुत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Inferiority.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उत्कर्ष superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Chief, principal, best.<BR>2 Worse, inferior, not best.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तर|अनुत्तरं
अनुत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Chief, principal.<BR>2 Best, excellent.<BR>3 Unable to answer, silent.<BR>4 Fixed, firm.<BR>5 Low, inferior.<BR>6 South, southern.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A reply which is incoherent or evasive, and is therefore held to be no answer.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and उत्तर subsequent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तान
अनुत्तान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lying with the face to the ground.<BR>E.<BR>अन neg. उत्तान sleeping, supine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्ति|अनुत्पत्तिः
अनुत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Failure.<BR>2 Non-production.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उत्पत्ति production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पन्न
अनुत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Uneffected, unaccomplished.<BR>2 Unborn, unproduced.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उत्पन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदग्र|अनुदग्रः
अनुदग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Very lofty.<BR>2 Not lofty, low.<BR>E.<BR>अन्, neg. उदग्र lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर
अनुदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Thin, lank.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्त|अनुदात्तः
अनुदात्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Unaccented.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>One of the three accents to be observed in reading the Vedas, the grave accent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उत् high, and आत्त pronounced, from दा to give, with आङ prefixed, to speak, and क्त affixed: pronouncing the vowels in a low and full tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Liberal, munificent.<BR>2 Niggardly, mean.<BR>3 Adhered to or followed by a wife.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उदार liberal, or अनु, and दार wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
अनुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unrisen.<BR>2 Unsaid, unuttered.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उदित risen or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिन|अनुदिनं
अनुदिन<BR>adv. n. (-नं)<BR>Daily.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धत
अनुद्धत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unsurpassed, unequalled.<BR>2 Unopposed.<BR>3 Humble.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्वत proud, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धरण|अनुद्धरणं
अनुद्धरण<BR>m. (-ण)<BR>1 Non-removal.<BR>2 Not offering.<BR>3 Not establishing or proving.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्धरण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धार|अनुद्धारः
अनुद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Non-partition, not taking a share.<BR>2 Non-removal.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्धार partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृत
अनुद्धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Non-removed, not taken away.<BR>2 Uninjured, undestroyed.<BR>3 Unoffered.<BR>4 Undivided, unpartitioned.<BR>5 Unestablished, unproved.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्धृत removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यत
अनुद्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inactive, idle, destitute of perseverance.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्यत active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योग|अनुद्योगः
अनुद्योग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Absence of exertion or effort, laziness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्योग effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योगिन्
अनुद्योगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Lazy, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अनुद्याम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रुत|अनुद्रुतं
अनुद्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Followed, pursued.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A measure of time in music, half a Druta, or one-fourth of a Mātra or time taken to articulate a short vowel.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and द्रुत gone, escaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वाह|अनुद्वाहः
अनुद्वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Celibacy.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्वाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=032" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्विग्न
अनुद्विग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Easy, free from apprehension or perplexity.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्विग्न anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वेग|अनुद्वेगः
अनुद्वेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Free from anxiety.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Freedom from anxiety.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उद्वेग anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावन|अनुधावनं
अनुधावन<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Chasing, pursuit, running after.<BR>2 Pursuit of any object, as of a mistress, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and धावन running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावित
अनुधावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>Pursued, run after, literally or figuratively.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and धावित run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Salutation, courtesy, civility, shewing respect or adoration to a guest or a deity.<BR>2 Regulation of conduct, discipline, tuition.<BR>E.<BR>अनु^1 and नय, from णीञ्^2 to guide or lead, and अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयिन्
अनुनयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Courteous, humble.<BR>E.<BR>अनुनय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनाद|अनुनादः
अनुनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound, consequent sound, vibration, echo.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and नाद noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिक
अनुनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Nasal, uttered through the nose.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनीत
अनुनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Trained, disciplined.<BR>2 Obtained, acquired.<BR>3 Taught.<BR>4 Respected.<BR>5 Pleased, pacified, appeased.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and नीत brought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्मत्त
अनुन्मत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Sane, sober, not wild, not mad: so अनुन्माद.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उन्मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप
अनुप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Watery, marshy; more usually अनूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकारिन्
अनुपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Not assisting, neglecting, ungrateful.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपकारित assisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकृत
अनुपकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unassisted.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपकृत assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतन|अनुपतनं
अनुपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Falling on or upon.<BR>2 Following.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and पतन falling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतित
अनुपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fallen, descended.<BR>2 Followed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिष्ट
अनुपदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Untaught, uninstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपदिष्ट advised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदम्
अनुपदम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Following.<BR>2 Step by step.<BR>3 Upon the foot.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A burthen, a word or passage repeated.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिन्
अनुपदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A searcher, an inquirer, one who follows or seeks for.<BR>E.<BR>अनुपदम् following, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदीना
अनुपदीना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A boot, a buskin.<BR>E.<BR>अनुपद upon the foot, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यस्त
अनुपन्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Undetermined, not established.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपन्यस्त fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यास|अनुपन्यासः
अनुपन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Failure of proof or determination, uncertainty, doubt.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपन्यास ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपत्ति|अनुपपत्तिः
अनुपपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Not supporting an assertion by good argument, inconclusive argumentation.<BR>2 Non-completion, not effecting or accomplishing, failure.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपपत्ति demonstration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपन्न
अनुपपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Not done, unaccomplished, uneffected.<BR>2 Unproved, undemonstrated.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपपन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रपन्न
अनुप्रपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Following, conforming to.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and प्रपन्न done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपभुक्त
अनुपभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unenjoyed, unpossessed.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपभुक्त enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपम|अनुपमः
अनुपम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Excellent, best.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The female elephant of the south-east, or of the north-east.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and उपमा resemblance; above comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमेय
अनुपमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Incomparable: so अनुपमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपमित compared, or उपमेय comparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयुक्त
अनुपयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Useless, unnecessary, unserviceable.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपयुक्त serviceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयोग|अनुपयोगः
अनुपयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Unserviceableness, uselessness.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपयोग utility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलक्षित
अनुपलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unmarked, undiscriminated.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपलक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्ध
अनुपलब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Unperceived, unascertained.<BR>2 Unobtained.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपलब्ध obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपशय|अनुपशयः
अनुपशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Any aggravating thing or circumstance, (in medicine) what increases the disease.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपशय a palliative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कृत
अनुपस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undressed, unprepared.<BR>2 Unfinished, unpolished.<BR>3 Unrequited.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपस्कृत finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थान|अनुपस्थानं
अनुपस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Absence.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपस्थान vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापन|अनुपस्थापनं
अनुपस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not producing, not offering, not placing, not having ready or at hand.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उप near, स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापित
अनुपस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>Not ready, not at hand, not offered or produced.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपस्थापित placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थायिन्
अनुपस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Absent, distant.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपस्थायिन् near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थिति|अनुपस्थितिः
अनुपस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Absence.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उपस्थिति vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपात|अनुपातः
अनुपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Falling subsequently upon, alighting or descending upon in succession.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 Following.<BR>4 A degree of latitude opposite to one given, the antoeci.<BR>5 Proportion, (in arithmetic.)<BR>6 Arithmetical progression.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and पात falling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातक|अनुपातकं
अनुपातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A heinous crime, as, falsehood, fraud, theft, adultery, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and पातक crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपान|अनुपानं
अनुपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fluid vehicle in medicine; drink taken with or after medicine.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after or with, and पान a drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपार्श्व
अनुपार्श्व<BR>mfn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वा-र्श्वं)<BR>Lateral.<BR>E.<BR>अनु by or upon, पार्श्व the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्त
अनुप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Obtained, attained, arrived at.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुष्प|अनुपुष्पः
अनुपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>E.<BR>अनु before पुष्प to put forth flowers, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्व|अनुपूर्व|अनुपूर्वं
अनुपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Regular, orderly, successively, from the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्वशस्|अनुपूर्वशस्
अनुपूर्व्वशस्<BR>ind.<BR>In regular order or succession, from the first, from above downwards.<BR>E.<BR>अनुपूर्व्व and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्त
अनुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Unsown, (as seed.)<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उप्त sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्तशस्य
अनुप्तशस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Fallow, meadow, (ground, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. उप्त sown, शस्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रस्थ
अनुप्रस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Latitudinal.<BR>E.<BR>अनु neg. according to, प्रस्थ extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रास|अनुप्रासः
अनुप्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Alliteration, repetition of similar letters, syllables and words.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and प्र before अस् to be, affix चञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लव|अनुप्लवः
अनुप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A companion or follower.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, प्लु to go, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=033" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबद्ध
अनुबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound to, connected with.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध|अनुबंधः|अनुबन्धः
अनुबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 The inseparable adjunct or sign of any thing, the indication of guilt, symptom of disease, &c.<BR>2 An element of language, root, affix, &c.<BR>3 An indicatory letter not sounded or dropped in composition, but marking some peculiarity in inflecting the word to which it is attached; for instance, an indicatory इ, denotes that verbs require the insertion of a nasal before their final consonant.<BR>4 A child or pupil, who imitates an example set by the parent or preceptor.<BR>5 A child or infant in general.<BR>6 Commencement, beginning.<BR>7 Binding, confining.<BR>8 Any thing small or little, a part, a small part.<BR>9 The connexion between the agent and the cause or motive.<BR>10 Circumstance, case.<BR>11 The junction of fractions.<BR>12 A secondary or symptomatic affection, one supervening on the principal disease.<BR>f. (-न्धी)<BR>1 Hickup.<BR>2 Thirst.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and बन्ध to bind or confine, with घञ् affix; and in the fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्धिन्|अनुबंधिन्
अनुबन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Connected with, attached.<BR>E.<BR>अनुवन्ध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबन्ध्य|अनुबंध्य
अनुबन्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं)<BR>Principal, primary, what may receive an adjunct, as a root, a disease, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and बन्ध्य to be attached to or by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोध|अनुबोधः
अनुबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Reviving the scent of a faded perfume.<BR>2 Replacing perfumes removed by bathing, &c.<BR>3 An after-thought.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and बुघ understand, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधित
अनुबोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Informed or convinced by reflection.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and बोधित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभव|अनुभवः
अनुभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Conclusive judgment, understanding, impression, the exercise of the intellect, independent of memory; also अनुभूति.<BR>2 Result, consequence.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, भू to be, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाव|अनुभावः
अनुभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Indication of passion, by look or gesture.<BR>2 Dignity, authority, consequence.<BR>3 Firm opinion, belief, knowledge.<BR>4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and भाव the essence or being; according to the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाविन्
अनुभाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Judging, knowing, understanding.<BR>2 Indicative of passion or feeling.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and भाविन् perceiving, or अनुभाव and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूत
अनुभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Understood, judged, apprehended.<BR>2 Resulted, followed as a consequence.<BR>3 Perceiving, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूति|अनुभूतिः
अनुभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Judgment; knowledge, from four sources, perception, inference, comparison and verbal information; or any source except memory.<BR>2 Dignity, consequence.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत|अनुमतः
अनुमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Accepted, assented to.<BR>2 Agreeable, pleasant.<BR>3 Loved, beloved.<BR>4 Concurred with, being of one opinion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमति|अनुमतिः
अनुमति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Order or command.<BR>2 Assent, permission.<BR>3 A fifteenth day of the moon's age, on which she rises one digit less than full.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with, before मन to respect, and क्तिन् affix; in the last acceptation, because offerings made to the manes on this day are especially accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्तृ|अनुमंतृ
अनुमन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Consenting to, concurring in, permitting.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मन to mind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरण|अनुमरणं
अनुमरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Dying with or following in death; the term usually denotes the cremation of a Hindu widow, whose husband's corpse is not on the spot, and with part of whose dress she, therefore, ascends the pile: this is prohibited to Brahman women. It is also synonymous with सहमरण burning with the body.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with or after, and मरण dying: dying with her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Inference (in logic,) drawing a conclusion from given premises.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after or according to, and मा from माङ to measure, affix अङ् and टाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमान|अनुमानं
अनुमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See अनुमा.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मा to measure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमानोक्ति|अनुमानोक्तिः
अनुमानोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Reasoning, logic.<BR>E.<BR>अनुमान, and उक्ति saying; speaking from inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमित
अनुमित<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inferred.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमिति|अनुमितिः
अनुमिति<BR>f. (तिः-)<BR>Inference, conclusion from given premises.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मिति measuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमृता
अनुमृता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The woman who burns with a part of her husband's dress.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मृता deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमेय
अनुमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Inferable.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मेय to be measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदन|अनुमोदनं
अनुमोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pleasing.<BR>2 Assent, acceptance.<BR>3 Sympathetic joy.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, with मोदन rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदित|अनुमोदितं
अनुमोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased, delighted.<BR>2 Agreeable, acceptable.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and मोदित pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात
अनुयात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Followed, pursued.<BR>2 Practised.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायित्व
अनुयायित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Succession.<BR>2 Subsequence.<BR>E.<BR>अनुयायिन्, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायिन्
अनुयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Following, consequent upon.<BR>2 A follower, a dependant or attendant.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्त|अनुयुक्तः
अनुयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Asked, inquired.<BR>2 Reprehended, censured.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोक्तृ
अनुयोक्तृ<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A hired teacher.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and योक्तृ who joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोग|अनुयोगः
अनुयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A question.<BR>2 Asking, solicitation.<BR>3 Censure, reproof.<BR>4 Religious meditation, spiritual union.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगकृत्
अनुयोगकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>An Ācārya or spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>अनुयोग, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगिन्
अनुयोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Reproving; or a reprover.<BR>2 What combines or unites.<BR>3 Connected or combined with, situated in or on.<BR>E.<BR>अनुयोग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोजन|अनुयोजनं
अनुयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A question.<BR>E.<BR>See अनुयोग; the affix being ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोज्य|अनुयोज्यं|अनुयोज्यः
अनुयोज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Bad, censurable.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and योज्य to be joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्त|अनुरक्तः
अनुरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Fond of, attached to, liking, esteeming, loving.<BR>2 Pleased.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रक्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्ति|अनुरक्तिः
अनुरक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Affection, love.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रक्ति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जक|अनुरंजक
अनुरञ्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Gratifying, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रञ्जक what pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जन|अनुरंजनं|अनुरञ्जनं
अनुरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Loving, being attached to.<BR>2 Pleasing, giving delight to.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रञ्जन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=034" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरञ्जित|अनुरंजित
अनुरञ्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased, delighted.<BR>2 Inspired with affection.<BR>E.<BR>अनु. and रञ्जित pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरत|अनुरतः
अनुरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fond of, attached to.<BR>2 Beloved.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रत attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरति|अनुरतिः
अनुरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Love, regard, esteem, attachment.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with, रम to play, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरस|अनुरसः
अनुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 (In poetry) a subordinate feeling or passion.<BR>2 (In medicine) a secondary flavour, as a little sweetness in a sour fruit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराग|अनुरागः
अनुराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Attachment, love.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with, and रञ्ज to stain or colour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागवत्|अनुरागवन्त्
अनुरागवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Loving, affectionate, in love with.<BR>E.<BR>अनुराग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिणी
अनुरागिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>One of the personifications of musical notes.<BR>E.<BR>अनु subsequent, रागिणी a musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिन्
अनुरागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Passion, impassioned, loving, in love.<BR>E.<BR>अनुराग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराधा
अनुराधा<BR>f. (धा)<BR>The seventeenth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, designated by a row of oblations; (stars in Libra.)<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and राध to accomplish, अन् affix, and टाप् for the fem; an auspicious sign for any thing to be undertaken in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुद्ध
अनुरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Soothed, pacified.<BR>2 Checked, opposed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रुद्ध opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूप|अनुरूपः
अनुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Like, resembling.<BR>2 Fit, suitable.<BR>2 According to.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Conformity.<BR>2 Assistance.<BR>3 Mediation, friendly interposition.<BR>4 Hindrance, check.<BR>E.<BR>अनु like, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपचेष्ट
अनुरूपचेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Endeavouring to act becomingly.<BR>E.<BR>अनुरूप, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोध|अनुरोधः
अनुरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The accomplishing of a desired object for another person, obligingness, service.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and रुध to confine, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधक
अनुरोधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Complying with, complaisant.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, रुध with, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधिन्
अनुरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>1 Compliant, complaisant.<BR>2 Adverse.<BR>E.<BR>अनुरोध obliging, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलाप|अनुलापः
अनुलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Tautology, repetition.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लप to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलिप्त
अनुलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Smeared, anointed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेप|अनुलेपः
अनुलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Unction, anointing.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लेप anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपक
अनुलेपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Anointing, who or what anoints.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लेपक who anoints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपन|अनुलेपनं
अनुलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Anointing the body with unguents.<BR>2 Unguent so used.<BR>3 Oily or emollient application.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लेपन anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपिन्
अनुलेपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Anointing the body with unguents.<BR>E.<BR>अनुलोम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोम|अनुलोमः
अनुलोम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Regular, successive, with the hair or grain.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and लोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमज|अनुलोमजः
अनुलोमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced or born in due gradation; applied especially to the mixed tribes; as the offspring of a Brahman man and Kṣatriya woman, a Kṣatriya man and Vaiśya woman, and so on. See प्रतिलोमज.<BR>E.<BR>अनुलोमन, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमन|अनुलोमनं
अनुलोमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>(In medicine) Following the natural course or direction.<BR>E.<BR>अनुलोम used as a nominal verb, and ल्यूट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवचन|अनुवचनं
अनुवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Concordance, conformity to or concurrence with a previous text or authority.<BR>2 Subsidiary or similar doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवत्सर|अनुवत्सरं|अनुवत्सरः
अनुवत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्त्तन|अनुवर्तन|अनुवर्तनं|अनुवर्त्तनं
अनुवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Obliging or serving another.<BR>2 Consequence, result.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वर्त्तन profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक|अनुवाकः
अनुवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A chapter of the Vedas, a subdivision or section.<BR>2 A compilation from the Rich, or Yajur Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, वच to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक्या
अनुवाक्या<BR>f. (-क्या)<BR>A prayer or formula from the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वाक्या a formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद|अनुवादः
अनुवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Abuse, reviling.<BR>2 Tautology, repetition.<BR>3 Conformity to what has been previously said or explained.<BR>E.<BR>अनु low, or after, and वाद from वद to speak, with धञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादक
अनुवादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Consenting to, replying.<BR>2 Conformable to, concurrent, corroborative.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वादक what says.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादत्व
अनुवादत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Consent, conformity, concurrence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व or ता added to अनुवादत्व; also अनुवादता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादिन्
अनुवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Consenting to, concurring with, conformable to. अनुवाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be conformable or correspondent to.<BR>n. (द्यं)<BR>The subject of a predicate.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before वद to speak, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवारम्
अनुवारम्<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वार time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास|अनुवासः
अनुवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Scenting, perfuming.<BR>2 An oily enema.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वास to perfume, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासन|अनुवासनं
अनुवासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Affection, attachment.<BR>2 Perfuming the clothes, especially dipping the ends of the cloth in perfumes.<BR>3 Perfuming, scenting in general.<BR>4 An oily enema.<BR>5 Administering oily enemata.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, वास to fumigate, and ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासित
अनुवासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Scented, perfumed.<BR>2 Fumigated.<BR>3 Prepared or administered as an enema.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, वास to fumigate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास्य
अनुवास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 To be scented or fumigated.<BR>2 Requiring an enema.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, वास and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Variegated, ornamented.<BR>2 Obstructed, checked.<BR>3 Full of, abounding in.<BR>4 Set (as a jewel.)<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and विद्ध penetrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधायिन्
अनुविधायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Conformable, compliant, obedient, attentive to.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and विधायिन् observing rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्ति|अनुवृत्तिः
अनुवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Complaisance, obliging or serving another. See अनुरोध.<BR>2 A subsequent or supplementary rule, completing what a preceding one has left to be explained.<BR>3 Imitating, doing or acting in like manner.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, वृत to serve, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेल्लित
अनुवेल्लित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Bandaging, securing with bandages, &c. (in surgery.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रजन|अनुव्रजनं
अनुव्रजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Complimentary attendance on a departing guest, following him to a given distance; also अनुव्रज्या.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, व्रजन or व्रज्या going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशय|अनुशयः
अनुशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Repentance, regret.<BR>2 Ancient enmity.<BR>3 Hatred, resentment.<BR>4 Attachment to or pursuance of any object. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=36" target="_blank">Page36</a>]<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 A disease of the feet, a boil or abscess on the upper part.<BR>2 A pimple on the head.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, शीङ्^1 to sleep, and अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=035" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयितव्य
अनुशयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be repented or regretted.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before शीङ्^1 and तव्य affix; also अनुशयनीय, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Devotedly attached to, faithful, adoring.<BR>2 Repentant, penitent, sorry for.<BR>E.<BR>अनुशय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशर|अनुशरः
अनुशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a sort of demon.<BR>E.<BR>अनु repeatedly, शृ to injure, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशस्त्र|अनुशस्त्रं
अनुशस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A supplementary or subsidiary weapon or instrument.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासक
अनुशासक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Ruling or one who governs or directs.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शासक what governs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासन|अनुशासनं
अनुशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Command, order, precept, law.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शासन ruling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासित
अनुशासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Directed, governed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शासित् governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासितृ
अनुशासितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Ruling, governing, commanding, directing, a ruler, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शासितृ who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्ति|अनुशास्तिः
अनुशास्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>Order, command, precept.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शास्ति order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्तृ
अनुशास्तृ<BR>m. (-स्ता)<BR>A governor, director, teacher.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शास्तृ who directs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलन|अनुशीलनं
अनुशीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Repeated and devoted service.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, शीलन behaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिष्ट
अनुशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Taught, revealed.<BR>2 Done conformably to law, &c.<BR>3 Nearly completed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, शिष्ट taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुचिका
अनुशुचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Any ceremony enjoined by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोक|अनुशोकः
अनुशोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sorrow, repentance, regret.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचक
अनुशोचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Grieving, one who repents.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and शोचक who sorrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचन|अनुशोचनं
अनुशोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sorrow, repentance.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, शृच to grieve, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचित
अनुशोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Regretted, repented of.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, शुच to sorrow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्ग|अनुषंग|अनुषंगः|अनुषङ्गः
अनुषङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Tenderness, compassion.<BR>2 Conjunction, coalition, connexion of word with word, or effects with causes.<BR>3 Necessary consequence, the connexion of a subsequent with a previous act.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and षंज to embrace, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिक|अनुषंगिक
अनुषङ्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Consequent, following as a necessary result.<BR>2 Connected with, adhering to, inherent, concomitant.<BR>E.<BR>अनुषङ्ग, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषङ्गिन्|अनुषंगिन्
अनुषङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्की-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Addicted or attached to.<BR>2 Embracing.<BR>3 Connected with.<BR>4 Common, prevailing.<BR>E.<BR>अनुषङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषञ्जन|अनुषंजनं
अनुषञ्जन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Connection with what follows, concord.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, षञ्ज to embrace, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषिक्त
अनुषिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Re-watered or sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and षिक्त sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषेचन
अनुषेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Watering or sprinkling over again.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and षिच to sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ्<BR>f. (-ष्टुप्)<BR>1 A measure of verse, the stanza consisting four lines of eight syllables each, or three lines of eight, twelve, and twelve, making, in either case, thirty-two.<BR>2 A name of SARASVATI.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and ष्टुभ् to stop, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ण|अनुष्णं|अनुष्णः
अनुष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>1 Lazy, sluggish.<BR>2 Cold, chilly.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and उष्ण warm, alert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातव्य
अनुष्ठातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be done or accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, स्था to stay or be, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातृ
अनुष्ठातृ<BR>m. (-ता-)<BR>The undertaker of any work.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, स्था to stay, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठान|अनुष्ठानं
अनुष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Commencement or course of proceeding.<BR>2 Fixing, establishing, proof.<BR>3 Propriety, fitness.<BR>4 Doing or engaging in any thing.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठित
अनुष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Effected, accomplished.<BR>2 Done, practised.<BR>3 Followed, observed.<BR>4 Appointed.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठेय
अनुष्ठेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be proved or established, demonstrable.<BR>2 To be effected or accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before स्था to stay, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धान|अनुसंधान|अनुसंधानं|अनुसन्धानं
अनुसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inquiry, investigation, searching.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and सम् before धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धानिन्|अनुसंधानिन्
अनुसन्धानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Investigating, searching; so अनुसन्धायिन्<BR>E.<BR>अनुसन्धान and इनि affix, or अनु and सम् before धा, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसन्धेय|अनुसंधेय
अनुसन्धेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Investigable, worthy of inquiry or scrutiny.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and सम् before धा to have, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसरण|अनुसरणं
अनुसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Custom, habit, usage.<BR>2 Conformity to, consequence of.<BR>3 Following, going after.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before सृ to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसार|अनुसारः
अनुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Custom, usage.<BR>2 Nature, natural state or condition of any thing.<BR>3 Prevalence, currency.<BR>4 Received or established authority, especially of codes of law.<BR>5 Conformity to usage, &c.<BR>6 Consequence, result.<BR>E.<BR>अन according to, सृ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसारिन्
अनुसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Following.<BR>2 According with or to.<BR>E.<BR>अनुसार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसूचक
अनुसूचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Indicative of, pointing out.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before षूच to point out, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्मृति|अनुस्मृतिः
अनुस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Cherished recollection, recalling some idea to the exclusion of all others.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before स्मृति memory. Also अनुस्मरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुस्वार|अनुस्वारः
अनुस्वार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The nasal letter (.) or dot above the line.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, स्वर to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार|अनुहारः
अनुहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>2 Resemblance.<BR>E.<BR>अनु like, हृञ to convey, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुहार्य्य|अनुहार्य|अनुहार्यः
अनुहार्य्य<BR>m.<BR>Monthly obsequies.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक|अनूकं|अनूकः
अनूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A former state of existence.<BR>n. (-क)<BR>1 Race, family.<BR>2 Disposition, temperament.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, उच to associate, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूचान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Well-behaved.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A learned Brahman; one versed in the Vedas and Vedāṅgas.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and वच to speak: the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूच्च
अनूच्च<BR>mfn. (च्चः-च्चा-च्चं)<BR>Short, low.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and ऊच्च tall, high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूढ|अनूढः
अनूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Unmarried.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूदित
अनूदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unuttered.<BR>E.<BR>अन् before ऊदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=036" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूद्य|अनूद्यं
अनूद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Not to be addressed or spoken to.<BR>2 To be spoken to afterwards or in reply to.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A spiritual teacher, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ before वद, to speak, यत् affix form irregular, it is improper to address a Guru, &c. by name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनून|अनूनं
अनून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Whole, entire.<BR>2 Not less, not inferior.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ऊन to diminish, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूनक|अनूनकं
अनूनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् affixed to अनून.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूप|अनूपं|अनूपः
अनूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Watery, wet.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>अनु near or with, and आप् water; ऊ is substituted for आ, and अच् is added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूपज|अनूपजं
अनूपज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>अनूप, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरु|अनूरुः
अनूरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Thighless.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The charioteer of the sun, the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>अन् priv. and ऊरु a thigh; being represented without legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूरुसारथि|अनूरुसारथिः
अनूरुसारथि<BR>m. (-स्थिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अनूरु, and सारथि a charioteer, whose coachman is ANŪRU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृजु|अनृजुः
अनृजु<BR>mfn. (-जुः-जुः-जु)<BR>Wicked, perverse, crooked, not straight, physically or morally.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and ऋजु straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृण
अनृण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Free from debt.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ऋण debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृणिन्
अनृणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Unindebted, free from debt.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ऋणिन्^1 a debtor.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृत|अनृतं
अनृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Falsehood.<BR>2 Agriculture.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. and ऋत truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनृतवादिन्
अनृतवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking falsely, lying, a liar.<BR>E.<BR>अनृत, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेक|अनेकं
अनेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Many, much, not one.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेककाल
अनेककाल<BR>adv. n. (-लं)<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकज|अनेकजः
अनेकज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bird, born more than once; or in the shell, and upon being hatched.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक more than one, and ज what is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकता
अनेकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Muchness, manifold condition; also अनेकत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकाकार
अनेकाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Multiform.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकप|अनेकपः
अनेकप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक various, from अन् neg. एक one, and प from पा who drinks, who drinks with his trunk, and with his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकरूप|अनेकरूपः
अनेकरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Multiform.<BR>2 Of various kinds or sorts.<BR>3 Fickle, of variable mind.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकविध
अनेकविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Various, of many kinds, in different ways.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकश|अनेकशः
अनेकश<BR>ind.<BR>By large numbers or quantities.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेकधा
अनेकधा<BR>ind.<BR>In various ways.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेडमूक|अनेडमूकः
अनेडमूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Deaf and dumb.<BR>2 Wicked, fraudulent.<BR>E.<BR>अन् here implying similarity, ण्ड deaf, and मूक dumb. See एडमूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेनस्
अनेनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Blameless, sinless.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. एनस् fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेव
अनेव<BR>ind.<BR>Otherwise, or.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. एव so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनेहस्
अनेहस्<BR>m. (-हाः)<BR>Time.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. हन to kill or hurt, एहच् substitute, and असि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैक्य|अनैक्यं
अनैक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>1 Plurality, the existence of many.<BR>2 Want of union, anarchy.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्त|अनैकांत
अनैकान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Variable, unsteady.<BR>2 (In logic) Occasional, as a cause not invariably attended by the same effects.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, अन्त end, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनैकान्तिक|अनैकांतिक
अनैकान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unsteady, variable, having many objects or purposes.<BR>E.<BR>अनेक, अन्त end, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनो
अनो<BR>ind.<BR>No, not; also नो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोकह|अनोकहः
अनोकह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>अनस् a cart, उक going, and ह what injures; from हन with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनोदित
अनोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unquestioned, unaddressed, not spoken to.<BR>E.<BR>अन् neg. ओदित spoken to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःकरण|अन्तःकरणं
अन्तःकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The internal and spiritual part of man, the seat of thought and feeling, the mind, the heart, the conscience, the soul.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and करण an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःपुर|अन्तःपुरं
अन्तःपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The female apartments.<BR>2 A queen.<BR>3 A palace.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and पुर a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रकृति|अन्तःप्रकृतिः
अन्तःप्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The heart, the soul, the internal nature or constitution of man.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and प्रकृति nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःप्रज्ञ
अन्तःप्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Acquainted with the heart, knowing one's self.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and प्रज्ञा knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशरीर
अन्तःशरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The internal and spiritual part of man, the conscience, the soul.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, शरीर the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःशल्य
अन्तःशल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Having some extraneous body, (a wound, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and शल्य a thorn, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसंज्ञा
अन्तःसंज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Internal consciousness.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and संज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःसत्त्वा
अन्तःसत्त्वा<BR>f. (-त्त्वा)<BR>1 A pregnant woman.<BR>2 Marking nut, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and सत्त्वा having life or being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तःस्वेद|अन्तःस्वेदः
अन्तःस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and स्वद warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त|अंत|अन्तं|अन्तः
अन्त<BR>mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>1 End, term.<BR>2 Final, ultimate, (continuing M. N. even with a fem. noun).<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Near.<BR>2 Handsome.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 A boundary, a limit.<BR>3 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>4 A limb, a member.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Nature, disposition.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तक|अंतक|अन्तकः
अन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त death, and क affix of agency. YAMA is the king or angel of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकर
अन्तकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Causing death, mortal, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तकाल|अन्तकालः
अन्तकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Time of death, death.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त end, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तग|अन्तगः
अन्तग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Dead, departed.<BR>2 Traversing, crossing, going to the end.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ततस्
अन्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 From the end, from the term.<BR>2 Similarly, like.<BR>3 In part.<BR>4 Lastly, finally.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्|अंतर्
अन्तर्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Within, between, amongst.<BR>2 To the end.<BR>3 Certainly, very well, a particle of assent.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त end, रा to receive, and क्रिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर|अंतर|अन्तरं
अन्तर<BR>(noun and adverb) n. (-रं)<BR>1 Interval, intermediate space.<BR>2 Period, term.<BR>3 Clothing.<BR>4 Covering.<BR>5 Difference.<BR>6 Sake, behalf.<BR>7 A hole or rent.<BR>8 Own, the self.<BR>9 Without, except.<BR>10 Without, outside.<BR>11 Opportune time.<BR>12 Midst, the midst.<BR>13 The supreme soul.<BR>14 Like, similar.<BR>15 Other.<BR>16 (In arithmetic) Remainder, difference.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त end, and र from रा to obtain, and क aff. In consulting the meanings of this word, it is to be recollected, that vocables which are adverbs in English, are often nouns of the neuter gender in Sanscrit; this word is also a pronoun, in the 3d and 10th acceptations. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=38" target="_blank">Page38</a>] when the latter means, without, or out of, any thing but a house or town: the whole of the interpretations may be referred to the ideas of, within and without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=037" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरङ्ग|अन्तरंग|अन्तरङ्गः
अन्तरङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Own, belonging to.<BR>2 Internal, interior.<BR>3 Of kin.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरतम|अंतरतम|अन्तरतमः
अन्तरतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)<BR>1 Immediate, intimate, internal.<BR>2 Like, analogous.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A congenial letter, one of the same class.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर inner, and डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरज्ञ
अन्तरज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Prudent, provident, foreseeing.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर midst, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरप्रभव|अन्तरप्रभवः
अन्तरप्रभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Of mixed origin or caste.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर different, प्रभव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरस्थ
अन्तरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Internal, inward.<BR>2 Separate, apart.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरा|अंतरा
अन्तरा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Without, except.<BR>2 In the middle, among, amidst.<BR>3 Near at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरात्मन्
अन्तरात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 The soul, the inherent spirit.<BR>2 The internal feelings, the heart or mind.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरापत्या
अन्तरापत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराय|अंतरायः|अन्तरायः
अन्तराय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Obstacle, impediment.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर between, इण to go, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तराल|अंतरालं|अन्तरालं
अन्तराल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>Included space: also अन्तरालक.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तरा in the midst, ला to obtain, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरिक्ष|अंतरिक्षं|अन्तरिक्षं
अन्तरिक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The sky or atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर within, and ऋक्ष a star; in which are the stars: or ईक्ष to see; seen by the world; the word is properly written with the long vowel, as अन्तरीक्ष, but the short is substituted in poetry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरित|अंतरित|अन्तरितं
अन्तरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead, departed, concealed, lost.<BR>2 Separated, detached.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Remainder, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीक्ष|अंतरीक्षं|अन्तरीक्षं
अन्तरीक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 Sky, heaven.<BR>2 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>see अन्तरिक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीप|अन्तरीपं|अंतरीपः|अन्तरीपः
अन्तरीप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>An island.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर in the midst of, and आप water; आ changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरीय|अंतरीयं|अन्तरीयं
अन्तरीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A lower garment.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर inner, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरे|अंतरे
अन्तरे<BR>ind.<BR>Amidst, among, between.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् with इण् to go, and विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तरेण|अंतरेण
अन्तरेण<BR>ind.<BR>1 Except, without.<BR>2 Amidst, between.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, इण to go, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गडु
अन्तर्गडु<BR>mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डु)<BR>Unprofitable, vain, idle.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर amidst, गडु to drop or distil, and उ affix: what runs to waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गत|अंतर्गत|अन्तर्गतं
अन्तर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Forgotten.<BR>2 Intermediate, interposed.<BR>3 Inner, internal, within.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and गत gone, part. past. of गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्गृह|अन्तर्गृहं
अन्तर्गृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>An inner apartment.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्जठर|अन्तर्जठरं
अन्तर्जठर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The stomach.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and जठर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्ज्वलन|अन्तर्ज्वलनः
अन्तर्ज्वलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Internal heat, inflammation.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and ज्वस्तन burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्जात
अन्तर्जात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inborn, inbred, innate.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दहन
अन्तर्दहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The distillation of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दाह|अन्तर्दाहः
अन्तर्दाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Internal heat, or fever.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्दुष्ट
अन्तर्दुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्ट)<BR>Internally bad, wicked, vile.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and दुष्ट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्वार|अन्तर्द्वारं
अन्तर्द्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A private door within the house.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धा
अन्तर्द्धा<BR>f. (-र्द्धा)<BR>Disappearance, concealment, covering.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर within, धा to have or hold, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धान
अन्तर्द्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Concealment, disappearance.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्द्धि
अन्तर्द्धि<BR>f. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्ध्यान
अन्तर्ध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Profound inward meditation.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and ध्यान meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भव|अंतर्भव
अन्तर्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Inward, internal, generated internally.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भाव|अंतर्भावः|अन्तर्भावः
अन्तर्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Internal or inherent nature or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भावना|अंतर्भावना
अन्तर्भावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Inward meditation or anxiety.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and भावना meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्भूत|अंतर्भूत|अन्तर्भूतः
अन्तर्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Internal, inner, being within.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्मनस्
अन्तर्मनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Sad, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यमन
अन्तर्यमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inward restraint, mental controul.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and यमन restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्यामिन्
अन्तर्यामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Checking or regulating the internal feelings.<BR>2 Heart-searching or pervading.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 The soul.<BR>2 Providence, the Supreme Spirit, as regulating and guiding mankind.<BR>3 Conscience.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and यामिन् who stops or refrains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्लम्ब|अन्तर्लम्बः
अन्तर्लम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>An acute angular triangle.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and लम्व the perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वंशिक|अन्तर्वंशिकः
अन्तर्वंशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Superintendent of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, वंश a race, and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वत्नी|अन्तर्व्वत्नी
अन्तर्वत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, मतुप् possessive affix, with an irregular formation of the fem. In the Vedas अन्तर्व्वती occurs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वमि|अन्तर्वमिः|अन्तर्व्वमिः
अन्तर्वमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>Flatulence, indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and वमि vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वर्त्तिन्|अन्तर्वर्तिन्
अन्तर्वर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Internal, included.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and वर्त्तिन् what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्व्वाणि|अन्तर्वाणि|अन्तर्व्वाणिः
अन्तर्व्वाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Skilled in sacred sciences.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and वाणि speech: containing the essence of all knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वासस्
अन्तर्वासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>An inner garment.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and वासस् clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्विगाहन|अन्तर्व्विगाहनं
अन्तर्विगाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Entrance, entering.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and वि before, गाह to agitate, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेग|अन्तर्वेगः
अन्तर्वेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Internal uneasiness or anxiety.<BR>2 Inward fever.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and वेग agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेदी|अन्तर्व्वेदी
अन्तर्वेदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The name of a country.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् between, and वेदी level earth. The Doab or district beween the Gaṅgā and Yamunā rivers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्वेश्मन्
अन्तर्वेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>The inner apartments, the interior of a building.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हास|अन्तर्हासः
अन्तर्हास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Laughing inwardly.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Self-satisfaction, conceit.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् inner, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=038" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तर्हित|अंतर्हित|अन्तर्हितं
अन्तर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Concealed, covered, hidden, disappeared.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् within, and धा to hold with क्त affix; हि substituted for धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवत्|अंतवत्|अन्तवन्त्
अन्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Finite, having a term or end.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तवासिन्
अन्तवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A pupil. See अन्तेवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तशय्या
अन्तशय्या<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 A bed or mat on the ground.<BR>3 The place for burial or burning.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त end, and शय्या a sleeping place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तावसायिन्
अन्तावसायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A barber.<BR>2 A man of a low tribe or cast, the offspring of a Niṣāda woman by a Caṇḍāla, whose business is to attend in places where dead bodies are burned.<BR>3 The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त the end, अव and षो to cut, who pares the nails, &c. or षै to decay, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ति|अंति|अन्तिः
अन्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>An elder sister, (in theatrical language).<BR>ind.<BR>Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिक|अंतिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अन्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An elder sister, (in theatrical language). See अत्तिका.<BR>2 A fire-place. See अन्दिका.<BR>3 A plant, (Echites scholaris.) See सप्तला.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Vicinity.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त the end, and कन् affix, इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकतम|अन्तिकतमः
अन्तिकतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)<BR>Very near.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तिक, and डतम superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकता
अन्तिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Nearness, vicinity, contiguity: also अन्तिकत्वं.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तिक with, ता or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिकाश्रय|अन्तिकाश्रयः
अन्तिकाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Contiguous support, (as that given by a tree to a creeper, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तिक, and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तिम|अंतिम|अन्तिमः
अन्तिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Final, ultimate, last.<BR>2 Very near.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त, and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्तेवासिन्
अन्तेवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 A pupil.<BR>2 A Caṇḍāla, or man of a low cast.<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Final, ultimate.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त in the locative case, near or final; वस to abide, and णिनि affix: who dwells near his teacher, &c. See अन्तवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्य|अंत्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अन्त्य<BR>mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>1 Last, ultimate.<BR>2 Inferior, low.<BR>m. (-न्त्यः)<BR>1 A man of low caste.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.) See मुस्ता.<BR>n. (-न्त्यं)<BR>A measure of number, two Sāgaras, a very large number.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यकर्म्मन्|अन्त्यकर्मन्
अन्त्यकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Funeral rites.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य, and कर्म्मन् act; also अन्त्यक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यज|अन्त्यजः
अन्त्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Younger, latest born.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A Śūdra or man of the fourth tribe.<BR>2 A man of one of seven inferior tribes; a washerman, currier, mimic, Varūra, fisherman, Meda or attendant on women, and mountaineer or forester.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य inferior, and ज who is born: born from the feet of BRAHMĀ; also अन्त्यजात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजन्मन्
अन्त्यजन्मन्<BR>mf. (-न्मा)<BR>A man or woman of the Śūdra or fourth tribe, &c., see the last.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यजातीय
अन्त्यजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sprung from the last or lowest class.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य last, जाति class, affix छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यभ|अन्त्यभं
अन्त्यभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 The sign Pisces.<BR>2 The asterism Revatī.<BR>2 The last star or constellation.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य last, and भ a constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यवर्ण|अन्त्यवर्णः|अन्त्यवर्ण्ण
अन्त्यवर्ण<BR>mf. (-र्णः-र्णा)<BR>A man or woman of the fourth tribe.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य, and वर्ण a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्यावसायिन्
अन्त्यावसायिन्<BR>mf. (-यी-यिनी)<BR>A man or woman of low caste, especially one of seven classes: a Caṇḍāla, a Śvapaca or executioner, a Kṣattā or insect hunter, a charioteer, a bard, and a Vaideha or attendant on women.<BR>2 A man or a woman of a particular caste living by the chase. See अन्तावसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्येष्टि|अन्त्येष्टिः
अन्त्येष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A funeral sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्येष्टिक्रिया
अन्त्येष्टिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Obsequies.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्येष्टि, and क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्र|अंत्रं|अन्त्रं
अन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>An entrail.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, and त्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रकूज|अन्त्रकूजः
अन्त्रकूज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Grumbling of the bowels, borborygmi.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्र, and कूज murmuring: also अन्त्रकूजनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्रवृद्धि|अन्त्रवृद्धिः
अन्त्रवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Inguinal hernia, rupture.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्र, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्त्राद|अन्त्रादः
अन्त्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A worm, ascarides, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्र, and द्यद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दिका|अंदिका
अन्दिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दु|अंदुः|अन्दुः
अन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>See अन्दू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दुक|अन्दुकः
अन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A ring or chain worn on the ancle.<BR>2 The chain for an elephant's feet.<BR>E.<BR>अदि to bind, कु affix, and कन् final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दू
अन्दू<BR>f. (-न्दूः)<BR>1 An ornament worn round the ancles.<BR>2 The chain for an elephant's feet.<BR>3 A chain, a fetter, a bond or tie.<BR>E.<BR>अदि to bind, and कू Uṇādi aff. or with कु affix अन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दूक|अन्दूकः
अन्दूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The chain for an elephant's feet. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्दोल
अन्दोल<BR>(त) r. 10th cl. (अन्दोलयति)<BR>To agitate, to swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध<BR>(त) r. 10th cl. (अन्धयति)<BR>To be or become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध|अंध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Blind.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>2 Water.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध to be blind, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धक|अंधक|अन्धकः
अन्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Blind.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The name of a country, apparently Behar.<BR>2 The name of a king.<BR>3 Of a Muni.<BR>4 Of an Asura.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध to be blind, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकरिपु|अन्धकरिपुः
अन्धकरिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA, the enemy of the demon ANDHAKA.<BR>E.<BR>अन्धक a demon so named, and रिपु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकार|अन्धकारः
अन्धकार<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध blind, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकासुहृद
अन्धकासुहृद<BR>m. (-द)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अन्धक, and असुहृद् the enemy. See अन्धकरिपु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धकूप|अन्धकूपः
अन्धकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A blind well.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध, and कूप a well: one of which the mouth is hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतमस|अन्धतमसं
अन्धतमस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Great darkness.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध to make blind, and तमस darkness: also written अन्धतामसं, अ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धता
अन्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Blindness. Also n. अन्धत्व.<BR>E.<BR>ता or त्व added to अन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धतामिश्र|अन्धतामिश्रः
अन्धतामिश्र<BR>n. (-श्रं)<BR>1 A division of Tartarus, the second of the twenty-one hells.<BR>2 The doctrine of annihilation after death.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध blind, great, and तामिश्र darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषा
अन्धमूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A small covered crucible, with a hole in the side.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध, and मूषा a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धमूषिका
अन्धमूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a grass. See देवताड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धस्|अंधस्
अन्धस्<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, नम् inserted, and असुन् Uṇādi affix, द changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धालजी
अन्धालजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>A blind boil, one that does not suppurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धाहि|अन्धाहिः
अन्धाहि<BR>mf. (हिः-हिः)<BR>A kind of fish, vulg. kūñciyā; a species of eel?<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध blind, and अहि a snake: from its form and the smallness of its eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धिका|अंधिका
अन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 Gambling.<BR>3 A small kind of mustard. See सर्षप.<BR>4 A woman.<BR>5 A disease of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध dark or blind, and कन् affix in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=039" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीकृत
अन्धीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made or become blind.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध, and कृत made, च्ची augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धीभूत
अन्धीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become blind.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध, and भूत become, च्ची augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धु|अंधुः|अन्धुः
अन्धु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>A well.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and तुक् Uṇādi affix; घ is substituted for त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्धुल|अंधुलः|अन्धुलः
अन्धुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa sirisa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अंध्रः|अन्ध्रः
अन्ध्र<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>A hunter, one who lives by killing game; a man of low caste, the offspring of a Vaideha father and Kārāvara mother; not allowed to reside within a village or town.<BR>2 A country, modern Telangana; also आन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्न|अन्नं|अन्नः
अन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 Boiled rice.<BR>2 Food in general.<BR>3 Corn.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, and क्त affix of the part. past. त becoming न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकाल|अन्नकालः
अन्नकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Meal time, proper hour for eating.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकोष्ठ
अन्नकोष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A cupboard, a granary.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and कोष्ठ or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नकोष्ठक|अन्नकोष्ठकः
अन्नकोष्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A granary, a cupboard.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न food, कोष्ठक a repository.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नगन्धि|अन्नगन्धिः
अन्नगन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>Dysentery, diarrhoea.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न food, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नज
अन्नज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Springing from or occasioned by food.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नजल
अन्नजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Support, subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and जल water, meat and drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद
अन्नद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who gives food.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदातृ
अन्नदातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>One who gives food, a charitable man.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and दातृ donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नदान
अन्नदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The giving of rice or food, the maintenance of a person.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नद्वेष|अन्नद्वेषः
अन्नद्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Want of appetite, dislike of food.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and द्वेष dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपरिवर्त्त|अन्नपरिवर्त
अन्नपरिवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Change of diet.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and परिवर्त्त revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्णा|अन्नपूर्ण्णा
अन्नपूर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and पूर्ण who fills with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नपूर्व्वा|अन्नपूर्वा
अन्नपूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नप्राशन|अन्नप्राशनं
अन्नप्राशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A religious ceremony, in which after presenting oblations to fire, a little rice is, for the first time, put into the child's mouth; it should take place between the fifth and eighth month.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and प्राशन feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नब्रह्म
अन्नब्रह्म<BR>n. (-ह्म)<BR>The deification of food, considering it in the light of BRAHMA, as the pervader and supporter of existence.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and ब्रह्म the Supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नभूमि
अन्नभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>A large collection of food.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and भूमि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Composed of food, containing food.<BR>2 Derived or made from food.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमयकोष|अन्नमयकोषः
अन्नमयकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The gross material body, that which is sustained by food.<BR>E.<BR>अन्नमय, and कोष sheath, (of the spirit.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमल|अन्नमलं
अन्नमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Spirituous liquor, the excrement or ferment of rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and मल foecula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नरस|अन्नरसः
अन्नरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Chyle.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नलिप्सा
अन्नलिप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Hunger, craving.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and लिप्सा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नवाहिस्रोतस्
अन्नवाहिस्रोतस्<BR>n. (-तः)<BR>The oesophagus.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and वाहि what conveys, स्रोतस् canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नविकार|अन्नविकारः
अन्नविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The seminal secretion.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and विकार change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नशेष|अन्नशेषः
अन्नशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Leavings, offal.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाद|अन्नादः
अन्नाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Feeding, eating.<BR>2 The partaker or eater of another's food.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नायिन्
अन्नायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Hungry; desiring food.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न nominal verb to want food, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नाहारिन्
अन्नाहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Eating, feeding.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न, and आहारिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यत्)<BR>1 Other, different.<BR>2 Unlike.<BR>E.<BR>अन to live, and यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्
अन्यत्<BR>ind.<BR>Otherwise.<BR>E.<BR>See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यगामिन्
अन्यगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Adulterous.<BR>2 Going to another (place, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्य another (husband or wife), गामिन् who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यच्च
अन्यच्च<BR>ind.<BR>1 Again, moreover.<BR>2 On the contrary.<BR>E.<BR>अन्यत्, and च and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यज
अन्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born of another (family, &c.) of a different origin.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यजन्मन्
अन्यजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Another birth, being born again, the metempsychosis.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतम|अन्यतमः
अन्यतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मत्)<BR>1 Either, any, any one of many.<BR>2 Different, distinct from many.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतर|अन्यतरः
अन्यतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रत्)<BR>1 Other, different.<BR>2 Either of two.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य other, and डतर affix; applied to words that refer to but two things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरेद्युस्
अन्यतरेद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>Either of two days.<BR>E.<BR>अन्यतर, and एद्युस् affix, derived from द्युस् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्
अन्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Elsewhere.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र<BR>ind.<BR>1 Elsewhere, in another place.<BR>2 Except, unless, without.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Otherwise, in a different manner.<BR>2 Inaccurately, untruly.<BR>3 Badly.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and थाल् affix, referring to manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथाख्याति|अन्यथाख्यातिः
अन्यथाख्याति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>Erroneous conception of spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अन्यथा and ख्याति declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथात्व
अन्यथात्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>An opposite or different state of the case.<BR>E.<BR>अन्यथा and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथासिद्धि|अन्यथासिद्धिः
अन्यथासिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Disproving a cause or argument, by giving it a different effect or application, coming to a different conclusion from the same premises.<BR>E.<BR>अन्यथा otherwise, and सिद्ध्रि proving, establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा<BR>ind.<BR>Another time.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and दा affix, referring to time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपुष्ट|अन्यपुष्टः
अन्यपुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The koil or Indian cuckoo, supposed to be reared by the crow.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यपूर्व्वा|अन्यपूर्वा
अन्यपूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A girl previously promised or betrothed to one and married to another.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृत्
अन्यभृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य another, and भृत् who nourishes: the crow is supposed to sit upon the eggs of the kokila: from भृ root, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यभृत|अन्यभृतः
अन्यभृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and भृत nourished, from भृ with part. affix क्त; this bird, like the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=41" target="_blank">Page41</a>] English cuckoo, being supposed to leave its eggs in the nests of other birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=040" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्
अन्यमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>1 Fickle-minded.<BR>2 Absent.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमनस्क|अन्यमनस्कः
अन्यमनस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>1 Absent, thinking of something else.<BR>2 Fickle, versatile.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and मनस्क minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यमानस
अन्यमानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Fickle-minded, otherwise minded.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and मानस mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवर्द्धित
अन्यवर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-सः-ता-सं)<BR>Brought up by a stranger, fostered.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and वर्द्धित part. past. of वृध् to grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यवादिन्
अन्यवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking inconsistently; (in law) prevaricating or a prevaricator.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य otherwise, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यशाख|अन्यशाखः
अन्यशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>An apostate.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य another, शाखा a branch or sect, or with कन् affix अन्यशाखकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश्
अन्यादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Of another kind, like another.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, दृश to see, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश|अन्यादृशः
अन्यादृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याधीन
अन्याधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Subject to others, dependant.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Impropriety, indecorum.<BR>2 Irregularity, disorder.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. न्याय propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अन्यायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Unjust, unreasonable.<BR>2 Indecorous.<BR>3 Illogical.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. न्यायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायवृत्त
अन्यायवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्त-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Following evil courses.<BR>E.<BR>अन्याय improper, ष्टत्त practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्य|अन्याय्यः
अन्याय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Improper, indecorous, unbecoming, unfit.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. न्याय्य right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यासक्त
अन्यासक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Absent, intent on something else.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and आसक्त intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Complete, entire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and न्यून defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्
अन्येद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>Another day.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and एद्युस् affix, from द्युस् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युस्क
अन्येद्युस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Daily, diurnal, occurring every other day.<BR>m. (-स्कः)<BR>A quotidian fever.<BR>E.<BR>अन्येद्युस् and कत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योत्पन्न
अन्योत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Begotten by another, the progeny of another than the reputed parent or husband.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योदर्य्य|अन्योदर्य|अन्योदर्यः|अन्योदर्य्यः
अन्योदर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A stepmother's son.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य, and उदर belly, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Mutual.<BR>E.<BR>अन्य repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यकलह
अन्योन्यकलह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Mutual quarrel.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and कलह strife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यघात
अन्योन्यघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Mutual conflict, striking, wounding or killing one another.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and घात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यभेद|अन्योन्यभेदः
अन्योन्यभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Mutual aversion or enmity.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and भद difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्यापहृत
अन्योन्यापहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken or secreted from one another, taken severally.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and अपहृत removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याभाव|अन्योन्याभावः
अन्योन्याभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Mutual negation, relative difference.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्याश्रय|अन्योन्याश्रयः
अन्योन्याश्रय<BR>m. (यः)<BR>Mutual or reciprocal connexion or dependance.<BR>E.<BR>अन्योन्य, and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्ष|अन्वक्षः
अन्वक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Following.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वञ्च्|अन्वंच्
अन्वञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-न्वङ्-नूची-न्वक्)<BR>Following.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, अञ्च to go, and क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Race, lineage, succession.<BR>2 Connexion, acquaintance, intercourse.<BR>3 The natural order or connexion of words in a sentence or stanza.<BR>3 The logical connexion of cause and effect, or proposition and conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, इण to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयज्ञ|अन्वयज्ञः
अन्वयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A genealogist.<BR>E.<BR>अन्वय, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Following, agreeing with.<BR>2 Belonging to race or family.<BR>E.<BR>अन्वय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववाय|अन्ववायः
अन्ववाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Race, lineage.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, अव prefixed to इण to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A Śrāddha or funeral ceremony performed on the ninth day of the months Pauṣa, Māgha, Phālguna, or Āśvina. It is the maternal Śrāddha for those who preserve the sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and अष्टका the eighth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहम्
अन्वहम्<BR>ind.<BR>Every day, daily.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचय|अन्वाचयः
अन्वाचय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Connecting, uniting.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and आङ् before चि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधि|अन्वाधिः
अन्वाधि<BR>f. (-घिः)<BR>1 A bail or deposit to be delivered to a third person.<BR>2 Repentance.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, and आधि a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेय|अन्वाधेयं
अन्वाधेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Property presented after marriage to the wife by her husband's family.<BR>E.<BR>अनु subsequently, and आधेय to be taken or received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतन
अन्वायतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Latitudinal.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and आयतन breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहण|अन्वारोहणं
अन्वारोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Mounting the funeral pile after or with the body of the husband.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and आरोहण ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासन|अन्वासनं
अन्वासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An unctuous or cooling enema.<BR>2 Service.<BR>3 Regret, affliction.<BR>4 A place where work is done, a manufactory, a house of industry.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, आस to sit, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 The monthly Śrāddha, or funeral repast in honour of the manes, held on the day of new moon; it should be, according to Menu, of meat eaten after the presentation of a piṇḍa or ball of rice.<BR>2 The monthly obsequies performed during the first year after the death of a parent.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and आहार्य्य to be taken or eaten; from हृ with आङ् prefixed, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्य्यक|अन्वाहार्यक|अन्वाहार्य्यकं
अन्वाहार्य्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Daily, diurnal.<BR>E.<BR>अन्वह daily, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Deposited with a person to be delivered ultimately to another.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, and आहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Joined, connected with.<BR>2 Having as an essential or inherent part, possessed of, possessing.<BR>3 Connected as in grammar, or construction.<BR>E.<BR>अनु with, and इत gone, part. of इण; also अन्वीत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्ट|अन्विष्टः
अन्विष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Sought.<BR>E.<BR>अनु after, and इष desire, with the part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीत|अन्वीतः
अन्वीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Joined, connected with. See अन्वित.<BR>E.<BR>अन with, and ईत from ई to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषण|अन्वेषणं
अन्वेषण<BR>fn. (-णा-णं)<BR>1 Research, investigation of duty by reasoning.<BR>2 Research, enquiry in general.<BR>E.<BR>अनु, इष to desire, and ल्यु aff. and in the fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषित|अन्वेषितः
अन्वेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sought.<BR>E.<BR>the part. past. of इष, with अनु prefixed, and इ inserted before क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=041" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषिन्
अन्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Seeking, inquiring after.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before, इष to wish, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष्टृ
अन्वेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>An enquirer, a searcher.<BR>E.<BR>अनु before इष, and तृच् affix of agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपःसान्त
अपःसान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The offering or performance of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप्<BR>f. pl. only, (आपः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, and क्विप् Uṇādi affix; the vowel of the radical becomes short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and preposition implying<BR>1 Inferiority, (below, worse.)<BR>2 Privation, (from.)<BR>3 Separation, (away from.)<BR>4 Contrariety, (against, opposite to.)<BR>5 Difference, (from.)<BR>6 Dishonesty.<BR>7 Exultation: as अपकृष्टुं to revile, अपहर्त्तुं to take away, अपकर्त्तुं to do wrong, अपवक्तुं to contradict, अपकीर्त्ति infamy, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and प from पा to preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरण|अपकरणं
अपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Acting improperly, doing wrong.<BR>2 Ill treating, offending, injuring.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अपकर्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ)<BR>Injurious, offensive, hostile, inimical, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अप before कृ to do, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्म्मन्|अपकर्मन्
अपकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>2 Oppression, violence.<BR>3 Laziness, incompetence.<BR>4 Any impure or degrading act or rite.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलङ्क|अपकलंक|अपकलंकः|अपकलङ्कः
अपकलङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्क)<BR>An indelible disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कलङ्क a stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्ष|अपकर्षः
अपकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Pulling down, bringing low, lowering, depressing.<BR>2 Inferiority, infamy, degradation. So अपकर्षण n. (णं.)<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कृष to attract, घञ् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकार|अपकारः
अपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Injury, offence, wrong, mischief.<BR>2 Wickedness.<BR>3 Tyranny, oppression.<BR>4 Hatred, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>अप ill, and कार what does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अपकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-क)<BR>Injuring, pernicious.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कृ to do, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारगीर्
अपकारगीर्<BR>f. (-गीः)<BR>Reproach and menace.<BR>E.<BR>अपकार hatred, and गीर् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Offensive, oppressive.<BR>2 Wicked, doing ill.<BR>3 Mischievous, malicious.<BR>4 Inimical.<BR>E.<BR>अपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारार्थिन्
अपकारार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Malicious, malevolent.<BR>E.<BR>अपकार and अर्थिन् who aims at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकीर्ति|अपकीर्तिः|अपकीर्त्ति
अपकीर्ति<BR>f. (-र्तिः)<BR>Infamy, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत
अपकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done wrong, maliciously, offensively, or wickedly committed.<BR>2 Who does wrong.<BR>3 Ill treated.<BR>4 Observed or practised as a degrading or impure act, as servile duties, funereal rites, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृति|अपकृतिः
अपकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Oppression, wrong, injury.<BR>2 Enmity, opposition.<BR>3 Any degrading or impure act or rite.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, कृ to do, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Low, vile, inferior.<BR>2 Perplexed, distressed.<BR>3 Depressed, lowered, brought down.<BR>E.<BR>part. past. of कृष, with अप prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्टता
अपकृष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Inferiority, vileness. So अपकृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ति|अपक्तिः
अपक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Immaturity.<BR>2 Indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पक्ति ripeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Unripe, immature.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्वता
अपक्वता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Immaturity.<BR>E.<BR>अपक्व, and तल् affix: also with त्व, अपक्वत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम|अपक्रमः
अपक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Flight, retreat.<BR>2 Passing off or away.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, and क्रम to go, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमण|अपक्रमणं
अपक्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Retiring, passing off or away.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Oppression, offence.<BR>2 Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>3 Any impure act or rite.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and क्रिया action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोश|अपक्रोशः
अपक्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Reviling, abusing.<BR>E.<BR>अप against, क्रुश to call out, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ष
अपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Adverse, opposed to, not of the same side or party.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पक्ष a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षता
अपक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Opposition, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>अपक्ष, and तल् affix: or with त्व affix अपक्षत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगत|अपगतः
अपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead, deceased.<BR>2 Gone, departed, remote, gone off.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम|अपगमः
अपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Departure, separation, death.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and गम to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगा
अपगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>अप down, below, or अप् water, and thence the sea; and गा what goes downward or into the sea; also आपगा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघन|अपघनः
अपघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A limb or member.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and घन from हन् to kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघात|अपघातः
अपघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Striking or cutting off, killing.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and घात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिन्
अपघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Murderous, killing.<BR>E.<BR>अपघात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचय|अपचयः
अपचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Loss, privation.<BR>2 Respect, obeisance.<BR>E.<BR>अप opposite to, and चय from चि to collect, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायित|अपचायितः
अपचायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Saluted, reverenced.<BR>E.<BR>अप here implying much or highly; and चायित part. past. of चाय to reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचार|अपचारः
अपचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Impropriety, defect, wickedness.<BR>2 Observing unwholesome or improper regimen.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, त्तर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wicked, bad, one who acts wickedly.<BR>E.<BR>अपचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित|अपचितः
अपचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Saluted, honoured.<BR>2 Diminished, expended, wasted.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, चाय to reverence, or चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचिति|अपचितिः
अपचिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Loss.<BR>2 Expense.<BR>3 Annihilation.<BR>4 Worship, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, चाय or चि, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपची
अपची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>1 Enlargement of the glands of the neck, &c.<BR>2 Any indolent tumor.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पच to ripen, अङ् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचीयमान
अपचीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wasting, perishing, departing.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, चि to collect, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचेतृ
अपचेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A spendthrift.<BR>E.<BR>अप, चि to collect, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Shadowless, having no shadow, as a deity or celestial being.<BR>2 Having a bad or unlucky shadow.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>An unlucky shadow, a phantom.<BR>E.<BR>अप priv. छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपञ्चीकृत|अपंचीकृत|अपंचीकृतं|अपञ्चीकृतं
अपञ्चीकृत<BR>n. (तं)<BR>Simple elementary substance, not compounded of the five gross elements.<BR>E.<BR>neg. पञ्च five, कृत made, च्ची augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटान्तर|अपटांतर|अपटान्तरं
अपटान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Adjoining, contiguous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पट a screen, and अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=042" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A screen or wall of cloth, especially the kenāt or screen surrounding a tent.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and पट to go, with fem, termination ङीप्; preventing admission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटीक्षेप|अपटीक्षेपः
अपटीक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Precipitate entrance on the stage, indicating hurry and agitation: also read अपटाक्षेप.<BR>E.<BR>अपटी curtain, and क्षेप tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटु|अपटुः
अपटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-ट्वी-टु)<BR>1 Sick, diseased.<BR>2 Awkward, not clever, uncouth.<BR>3 Ineloquent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटुकरण
अपटुकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A defect in any of the senses.<BR>E.<BR>अपटु, and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्डित|अपंडित
अपण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unlearned, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पण्डित learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतन्त्रक|अपतंत्रकः|अपतन्त्रकः
अपतन्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Spasmodic contraction of the body, emprosthotonos.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, तन्त्र will, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पण|अपतर्पणं
अपतर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Fasting, (in sickness.)<BR>E.<BR>अप bad, and तर्पण satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानक|अपतानकः
अपतानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Spasmodic contraction: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>अप down, तन to spread, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्य|अपत्यं
अपत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Offspring, male or female.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वत to fall, and यत् affix; the family being upheld by them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यदा
अपत्यदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A midwife.<BR>E.<BR>अपत्य offspring, and दा fem. deriv. who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यपथ|अपत्यपथः
अपत्यपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>अपत्य, and पथ the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यविक्रयिन्
अपत्यविक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A father who receives a gratuity from his son-in-law, a seller of his offspring.<BR>E.<BR>अपत्य, and विक्रयिन् who sells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यशत्रु|अपत्यशत्रुः
अपत्यशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>अपत्य offspring, and शत्रु an enemy. The crab being said to perish on producing young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप|अपत्रपः
अपत्रप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Bashful, modest.<BR>2 Immodest.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 Bashfulness.<BR>2 Want of shame, immodesty.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपिष्णु|अपत्रपिष्णुः
अपत्रपिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Bashful.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, त्रप to be ashamed, and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>The absence of a road.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and पथ for पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथिन्
अपथिन्<BR>m. (-न्था)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अपथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>1 Unsuitable, inconsistent.<BR>2 (In medicine) Contra-indicated, unfit as food or drink in particular complaints.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पथ्य suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा or -दी-दं)<BR>1 Footless, having no feet.<BR>2 Having no place, no station.<BR>adv. n. (-दं)<BR>Unseasonably, inopportunely.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A reptile.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान|अपदानं
अपदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Approved occupation.<BR>2 Work well or completely done.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, दा to give, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानक|अपदानकं
अपदानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the above.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदान्तर|अपदान्तरः
अपदान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Adjoining, contiguous.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Proximity, close, contiguity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पद a foot, and अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदार्थ|अपदार्थः
अपदार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>Nonentity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पदार्थ a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश|अपदिशं
अपदिश<BR>n. or ind. (-शं)<BR>Intermediate space, half a point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and दिश to shew, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश्य
अपदिश्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Dispersing, going or having gone to various quarters.<BR>2 Having shewn or stated.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, दिश to show, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेवता
अपदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An evil spirit, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and देवता a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश|अपदेशः
अपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Evasion, prevarication.<BR>2 Disguise by dress, &c.<BR>3 Place, quarter.<BR>4 A butt or mark.<BR>5 Cause.<BR>6 Fame, reputation.<BR>7 A contrivance, a pretence, a pretext.<BR>E.<BR>अप ill, badly, &c. and दिश to shew, with धञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्य|अपद्रव्यं
अपद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 An impurity, any bad thing.<BR>2 Alloy, adulteration.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंस|अपध्वंसः
अपध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Degradation, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसज|अपध्वंसजः
अपध्वंसज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A man of a mixed or impure cast.<BR>E.<BR>अपध्वंस and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Cursed, reviled.<BR>2 Abandoned.<BR>3 Pounded.<BR>E.<BR>अप implying contempt, &c. part. past. of ध्वस to go, also अवध्वस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यान|अपध्यानं
अपध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Evil thoughts, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and ध्यान meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयन|अपनयनं
अपनयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Taking away, withdrawing, removing.<BR>2 Destroying.<BR>3 Dying.<BR>4 Acquittance of a debt or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, णी to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीत
अपनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken away, removed.<BR>2 Paid, discharged.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीय
अपनीय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken away.<BR>2 Having discharged.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, णी to take, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्ति|अपनुत्तिः
अपनुत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Removing, taking or sending away.<BR>E.<BR>अप, नुद to send, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोद|अपनोदः
अपनोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Removing, taking away.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and नुद to send, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनोदन|अपनोदनं
अपनोदन<BR>n. (नं)<BR>1 Removing, destroying.<BR>2 Expiating.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, नुद to send, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अपपात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Of low caste, using separate vessels.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A separate vessel, one from which no one else will eat.<BR>E.<BR>अप apart, पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्रित|अपपात्रितः
अपपात्रित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A person who has lost caste, one with whom his kindred will not eat or drink, from a common pātra or vessel.<BR>E.<BR>अपपात्र, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभी
अपभी<BR>mfn. (-भीः-भीः-भि)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, भी fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश|अपभ्रंशः
अपभ्रंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Ungrammatical language.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, भ्रंश to fall, and अच् affix; also अपभ्रंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपम|अपमः
अपम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Declination, (in astronomy.)<BR>E.<BR>अप, मा to measure, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान|अपमानं|अपमानः
अपमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अप reverse, and मन to respect, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानित
अपमानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespect, disgraced.<BR>E.<BR>अपमान disgrace, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमान्य
अपमान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Disreputable, dishonourable.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, मन to mind, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित
अपमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Neglected in dress or person, unadorned.<BR>2 Disrespected, disgraced.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्यक|अपमित्यकं
अपमित्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Debt.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, मि to throw, and त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्यु|अपमृत्युः
अपमृत्यु<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>Sudden death, dying of some casualty, not of sickness or decay.<BR>E.<BR>अप, मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अपयशस्<BR>n. (-शः)<BR>Disgrace, infamy.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=043" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्कर
अपयशस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Disgraceful, occasioning infamy.<BR>E.<BR>अपयशस्, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयान|अपयानं
अपयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Retreat, flight.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Other.<BR>2 Opposite, contrary.<BR>3 Posterior, (in place or time.)<BR>4 Similar, same.<BR>5 Friendly, not adverse.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The hind quarter of an elephant.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The womb.<BR>2 Suppressed menstruation in pregnancy.<BR>3 The west.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and पर from पृ to nourish or fill, and अच् affix; or अ neg. and पर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरञ्च
अपरञ्च<BR>ind.<BR>Again, moreover.<BR>E.<BR>च the particle added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्व|अपरत्वं
अपरत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Opposition, contrariety.<BR>2 Posteriorly, (in place or time); also अपरता f. (-ता.)<BR>E.<BR>त्व or तल् added to अपर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरति|अपरतिः
अपरति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Stopping, ceasing.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, रम to please, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपररात्र|अपररात्रः
अपररात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The end of the night, the last watch.<BR>E.<BR>अपर the end, रात्र from रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरलोक|अपरलोकः
अपरलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Another world, paradise.<BR>E.<BR>अपर, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरव|अपरवः
अपरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Contest, dispute.<BR>2 Discord.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवक्त्र
अपरवक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>A kind of metre of four lines, having every two lines the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवोज्झित
अपरवोज्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undisturbed, undisputed.<BR>E.<BR>अपरव, and उज्झित^1 free from.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर<BR>adj. mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) or adv. n. (-रं)<BR>1 Continued, uninterrupted.<BR>2 Continually, (applied to action.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and परस्पर mutual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराङ्मुख|अपराङ्मुखः
अपराङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Not having the head downwards or reverted.<BR>2 Presenting a firm front in battle or danger.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पराङ्मुख reverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconquered, unsurpassed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A sage.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A name applied to several plants.<BR>2 (Clitoria ternatea,) see गिरिकर्णी.<BR>3 Aeschynomene sesban, see जया and,<BR>4 Another plant, see अशनपर्णी.<BR>5 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>6 A species of the शर्करी metre of four lines, with fourteen syllables in each line.<BR>7 The north-east quarter.<BR>E.<BR>अपर another, अ neg. and जित conquered, excelled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजेय
अपराजेय<BR>mfn. (यः-या-यं)<BR>Unconquerable, invincible.<BR>E.<BR>अपर, and अजेय unconquerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अपराद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Criminal, guilty.<BR>2 Erring.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, राघ to accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धपृषत्क|अपराद्धपृषत्कः
अपराद्धपृषत्क<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>An archer or arrow always missing the butt.<BR>E.<BR>अपराद्ध erring, and पृषत्क an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धृ
अपराद्धृ<BR>mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ)<BR>Offending an offender.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, राध, with तृच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध|अपराधः
अपराध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Offence, transgression, fault.<BR>E.<BR>अप badly, and राध to accomplish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधित
अपराधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Criminated, condemned.<BR>E.<BR>अपराध and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिता
अपराधिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Criminality, guilt. So अपराधित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to अपराध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अपराधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Offending, culpable, criminal.<BR>E.<BR>अपराध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधीन
अपराधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Independent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पराधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्ण|अपराह्णः
अपराह्ण<BR>m. (-ह्लः)<BR>Afternoon, the last watch of the day.<BR>E.<BR>अपर last, and अह्ण for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराह्णतन|अपराह्णतनं
अपराह्णतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging to or produced in the close of the day, also अपराह्लेतन.<BR>E.<BR>अपराह्ल the end of a day, with द्यु, or द्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिकलित|अपरिकलितः
अपरिकलित<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unknown.<BR>2 Unseen.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिकलित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्लिन्न
अपरिक्लिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Dry, not moist, not liquid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिक्लिन्न moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिगत
अपरिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unknown, unobtained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिगत obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Non-acceptance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्राह्य
अपरिग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्मं)<BR>Unfit or improper to be accepted, not to be taken.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचयिन्
अपरिचयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Without acquaintance.<BR>2 Misanthropic.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिचयिन् acquainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचित
अपरिचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unacquainted with, unknown to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिचित known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचेय
अपरिचेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unsociable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिचेय to be combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छद
अपरिच्छद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Absence of clothing, nudity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छन्न|अपरिच्छन्नं
अपरिच्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Uncovered, unclothed. So अपरिच्छादित. mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छन्न or परिच्छादित clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छिन्न|अपरिच्छिन्नं
अपरिच्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Continuous, connected without interval.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छिन्न intersected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेद|अपरिच्छेदः
अपरिच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Want of arrangement or order.<BR>2 Want of distinction or division.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छेद section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेदित
अपरिच्छेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unarranged, not distinguished or divided.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिच्छेदित intersected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणयन
अपरिणयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Celibacy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिणयन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणीता
अपरिणीता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An unmarried woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिणीत married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपक्व|अपरिपक्वं
अपरिपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्व)<BR>Not quite mature.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिपक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपाटि
अपरिपाटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>Want of order, disarrangement.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिपाटि order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपूत
अपरिपूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unripe, immature, imperfect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg परिपूत perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमाण
अपरिमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Without measure, immense, immeasurable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिमाण measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमित|अपरिमितं
अपरिमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unmeasured.<BR>2 Unlimited, unbounded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिमित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमेय
अपरिमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unbounded, illimitable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिमेय measurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिम्लान|अपरिम्लानः
अपरिम्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Pure, clean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिम्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवाद्य
अपरिवाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Not to be reprimanded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिवाद्य to be reproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवृत
अपरिवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uninclosed, unsurrounded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिष्टत surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कार|अपरिष्कारः
अपरिष्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Coarseness, rudeness, want of polish or finish, moral or physical.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिष्कार polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=044" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कृत|अपरिष्कृतं
अपरिष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Coarse, rude, unpolished, unadorned, morally or physically.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिष्कृत finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसर|अपरिसरः
अपरिसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Distant, not contiguous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिसर near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहरणीय
अपरिहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be abandoned or lost.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिहृ to leave, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहार्य्य|अपरिहार्य|अपरिहार्य्यं
अपरिहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Not to be avoided, inevitable.<BR>2 Not to be abandoned.<BR>3 Not to be degraded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परिहृ to leave, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षित
अपरीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Untried, unproved.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. परीक्षित tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अपरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>Ugly, deformed, ill-looking, ill-made, monstrous.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Monstrosity, deformity.<BR>E.<BR>अप bad, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्ण
अपर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Leafless.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, and पर्ण a leaf: the goddess not having even leaves for food, during her performance of religious austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्य्याप्त|अपर्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्तं
अपर्य्याप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Unlimited, unbounded.<BR>2 Incompetent, unable, insufficient.<BR>3 Incomplete, not enough.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पर्य्याप्त extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्य्याय|अपर्याय|अपर्यायः
अपर्य्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Want of order or method.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पर्य्याय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल|अपलं
अपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pin or bolt.<BR>E.<BR>अप below, and ला to take, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाप|अपलापः
अपलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Denial or concealment of knowledge, evasion.<BR>2 Affection, regard.<BR>3 Concealing, hiding.<BR>E.<BR>अप away or kindly, and लप to speak, घञ् affix; also अपलपन n. (-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापिन्
अपलापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>One who denies or evades.<BR>E.<BR>अपलाप and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिका
अपलाषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Thirst.<BR>E.<BR>अप, लष to desire, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवन|अपवनं
अपवन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Without air, sheltered from wind.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A garden, a grove.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and वन a wood, or अ neg. पवन wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरक|अपवरकः
अपवरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An inner apartment, the lying-in chamber.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृञ to hide or choose, अच् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरण|अपवरणं
अपवरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Covering, screening.<BR>2 A garment, a mantle.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृ to screen, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Final beatitude, the delivery of the soul from the body, and exemption from farther transmigration.<BR>2 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>3 The fruit or consequences of any completed act.<BR>4 The completion of any act.<BR>5 Any act brought to a conclusion.<BR>6 End, completion.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, वृज to forsake, घञ् affix, and ग substituted for ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्गद
अपवर्गद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Conferring final beatitude.<BR>E.<BR>अपवर्ग, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जन|अपवर्जनं|अपवर्ज्जन|अपवर्ज्जनं
अपवर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift or donation.<BR>2 Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR>3 Abandoning, abandonment.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृज to forsake, and ल्युट् aff. See अपवर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ज्जित|अपवर्जित
अपवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, quitted, got rid of, given or cast away.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, वृज to forsake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त्त|अपवर्त|अपवर्तः
अपवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Taking away.<BR>2 A common measure in algebra.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, वृत्त being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त्तन|अपवर्तन|अपवर्तनं
अपवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Agitating, shaking.<BR>2 Taking away, removal, resumption.<BR>3 Transferring, removing from one place to another.<BR>4 Abbreviation, abridging.<BR>5 Division by a common measure, reduction of a fraction to its lowest terms.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाद|अपवादः
अपवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Censure, blame.<BR>2 An order, a command.<BR>3 Difference, distinction, exception.<BR>4 Contradiction, opposition, denial.<BR>E.<BR>अप implying aversion, and वाद speech, from वद with घञ्; also अववाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादक
अपवादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Censuring, accusing.<BR>2 Opposing, objecting to.<BR>3 Excepting, excluding.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वद to speak, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादित
अपवादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Accused, censured.<BR>2 Opposed, objected to.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वद to speak, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादिन्
अपवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Accusing, defaming.<BR>2 Opposing, objecting to.<BR>E.<BR>अपवाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारण|अपवारणं
अपवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disappearance, concealment, covering.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृञ् to hide, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारित|अपवारितं
अपवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, concealed, disappeared.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृञ् to hide, क्त affix, and the vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवार्य्य|अपवार्य
अपवार्य्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 (In theatrical language,) Apart, aside.<BR>2 Having concealed.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृञ् to hide, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाह|अपवाहः
अपवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An inference or deduction.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वह to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवित्र|अपवित्रं
अपवित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Impure, unclean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पवित्र pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवित्रता
अपवित्रता<BR>f.<BR>Impurity, uncleanness. So अपवित्रत्व n.<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Rejected, dismissed, removed.<BR>2 Thrown, sent.<BR>3 Broken to pieces.<BR>E.<BR>अप before ट्यध to strike, क्त the part. affix, and the semivowel changed to its corresponding vowel इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्धपुत्र|अपविद्धपुत्रः
अपविद्धपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A son rejected by his natural parents, and adopted by a stranger; one of the twelve objects of filiation in Hindu law.<BR>E.<BR>अपविद्ध as before, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविषा
अपविषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A species of grass, (Kyllingia monocephala.)<BR>E.<BR>अप, and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्त
अपवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Reversed, inverted, overturned.<BR>2 Deprived of.<BR>3 Uncovered.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and वृत्त established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेध|अपवेधः
अपवेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Piercing any thing in the wrong direction.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and वेध perforating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्यय|अपव्ययः
अपव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Prodigality.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययमान
अपव्ययमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Squandering.<BR>2 Denying a debt.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, व्यय expenditure, used as a verb, शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययिन्
अपव्ययिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Squandering, wasting, prodigal.<BR>E.<BR>अपव्यय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशङ्क|अपशंक
अपशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearless, having no fear or hesitation.<BR>adv. n. (-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearlessly.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and शङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशद|अपशदः
अपशद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A low man. See अपसद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशब्द|अपशब्दः
अपशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>1 Ungrammatical language.<BR>2 Common or vulgar speech, any form of language not Sanscrit.<BR>E.<BR>अप bad, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुच्
अपशुच्<BR>m. (-शुक्)<BR>The soul.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and शुच् sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>E.<BR>अप, and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ट
अपष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>The end or point of the hook for driving an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अप before ष्टे to surround, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=045" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्टम
अपष्टम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The point of the hook by which elephants are driven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु<BR>m. (-ष्टुः)<BR>Time.<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठुः-ष्ठुः-ष्ठु)<BR>1 Contrary, opposite.<BR>2 Left, (not right.)<BR>ind.<BR>1 Well, properly.<BR>2 Handsomely.<BR>3 Contrary, perversely.<BR>E.<BR>अप badly, स्थ what stays, with कु Uṇādi affix; स्थ becomes ष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुर|अपष्ठुरं
अपष्ठुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opposite, contrary.<BR>E.<BR>अपष्ठु contrary, and र from रा to obtain, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुल|अपष्ठुलं
अपष्ठुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Opposite, contrary.<BR>E.<BR>as before, ल substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्
अपस्<BR>n. (-पः)<BR>Sacrificing.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, असुन् Uṇādi aff.; the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसद|अपसदः
अपसद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A low man, an outcaste; it especially applies to the children of six degrading connexions, or of a Brāhmaṇa with the women of the three lower classes; of a Kṣatriya with women of two, the Vaiśya and Śūdra; and of a Vaiśya with one of a lower class or a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>अप low, सद to abide, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर|अपसरः
अपसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The removal of any thing from one place to another.<BR>E.<BR>अप before सृ to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्जन|अपसर्जनं|अपसर्ज्जन|अपसर्ज्जनं
अपसर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A gift or donation.<BR>2 Killing.<BR>3 Final emancipation.<BR>4 Abandonment.<BR>E.<BR>अप before सृज to leave, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरण|अपसरणं
अपसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going out, egress.<BR>E.<BR>अप before सरणं going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A secret emissary or agent, a spy. So अपसर्पक m. (-कः)<BR>E.<BR>अप bad, &c. सर्प who goes; from सृप with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसलवि
अपसलवि<BR>ind.<BR>The space between the thumb and the forefinger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अपसव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Opposite, contrary.<BR>2 Right, (not left.)<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>The space between the thumb and the forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and सव्य left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यक
अपसव्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the above.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसार|अपसारः
अपसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Egress, passage for going forth.<BR>2 Going out or away.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, सार a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारित
अपसारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone out, got out, escaped, fled.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, सारित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कर|अपस्करः
अपस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Any part of a carriage.<BR>2 The anus.<BR>3 Faeces.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and कर from कृष to furrow, or कृ to do; स is inserted for the sake of euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नात|अपस्नातः
अपस्नात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bathed or bathing after mourning, or upon the death of a connexion.<BR>2 Bathed after death, (the corpse,) preparatory to other ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and स्नात bathed, from ष्णा, and क्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नान|अपस्नानं
अपस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Funereal bathing, upon the death of a connexion, after mourning, &c.<BR>2 Impure bathing, or bathing in water with which a person has previously washed.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पश
अपस्पश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Being without spies or emissaries.<BR>2 Wanting the introduction or explanation, (grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>अप with स्पश a spy, or अ and पस्पश the first section of the Bhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मार|अपस्मारः
अपस्मार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Epilepsy, falling sickness.<BR>E.<BR>अप privation, स्मृ to remember, and घञ् affix; loss of memory or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारिन्
अपस्मारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Epileptic, convulsed.<BR>E.<BR>इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहत
अपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and उत killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरण|अपहरणं
अपहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking away, carrying off, stealing, &c.<BR>2 Taking back, resuming.<BR>E.<BR>अप before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरणीय
अपहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be taken away, carried off, stolen, &c.<BR>2 To be taken back or resumed.<BR>E.<BR>अप before हृ to take, अनीयर affix; also अपहर्त्तव्य, and अपहार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्त|अपहस्तः
अपहस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Taking away or off.<BR>2 Stealing, plundering.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तित
अपहस्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lost, gone, parted with or deprived of.<BR>E.<BR>अप, हस्त the hand, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानि|अपहानिः
अपहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Exception, exclusion.<BR>2 Quitting, leaving.<BR>3 Leaving off, stopping.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and हानि abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहाय
अपहाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having left or abandoned.<BR>2 Except, excepting.<BR>E.<BR>अप before हा to abandon, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहार|अपहारः
अपहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Loss.<BR>2 Taking away.<BR>3 Theft, stealing.<BR>4 Secreting.<BR>5 Spending another person's property.<BR>E.<BR>अप before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारक|अपहारकः
अपहारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who takes away, seizing, taking a thief.<BR>E.<BR>अपहृ to take away, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारिन्
अपहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>One who takes away, who seizes, steals, &c. a plunderer, a thief.<BR>E.<BR>अपहृ to steal, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहास|अपहासः
अपहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Silly or causeless laughter.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृत
अपहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken away, carried off, stolen, &c.<BR>2 Taken back, resumed.<BR>E.<BR>अप before हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नव|अपह्नवः
अपह्नव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>2 Affection.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, ह्नङ to conceal, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुत
अपह्नुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Concealed, denied.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, ह्नु and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुति|अपह्नुतिः
अपह्नुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Denial, or concealment of knowledge.<BR>2 A figure of rhetoric, applying a description or simile to other than its obvious application.<BR>E.<BR>अपह्नङ and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नोतृ
अपह्नोतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्रणी-नृ)<BR>One who conceals or denies.<BR>E.<BR>अपह्लुङ् and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक|अपाकः
अपाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Immature, raw, undressed or unripe.<BR>2 Undigested.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Immaturity.<BR>2 Indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पाक ripeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरण|अपाकरणं
अपाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Payment, liquidation.<BR>2 Removal, abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आङ् before कृ to make, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकशाक|अपाकशाकं
अपाकशाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>अपाक indigestion, and शाक herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृत
अपाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken away, removed, destroyed, void of.<BR>2 Paid.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आ before कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृति|अपाकृतिः
अपाकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Removal, taking away.<BR>2 Change of form or condition.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आ before कृति doing, or अप with आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Present, perceptible.<BR>E.<BR>अप before, and अक्ष an organ of sense, or अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त|अपांक्त
अपाङ्क्त<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्तः-ङ्क्ता-ङ्क्तं)<BR>1 Not in a line or row.<BR>2 Not in the same degree or class, unworthy, inadmissible into society, excluded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पंक्ति a line, अण् affix; also similar derivatives as अपांक्तय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्तेय|अपांक्तेय
अपाङ्क्तेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-य)<BR>1 Not in a line or row.<BR>2 Not in the same degree or order of society.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पङ्क्ति a line, ढक aff. see अपाङ्कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=046" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्क्त्योपहत
अपाङ्क्त्योपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Defiled or contaminated by the presence of impure or improper persons.<BR>E.<BR>अपाङ्क्त्य excluded, उपहत affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्ग|अपांग|अपाङ्गः
अपाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 The outer corner of the eye.<BR>2 A sectarial mark or circlet on the forehead.<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Maimed, crippled.<BR>E.<BR>अए before अगि to go, and अच् affix, or अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गक|अपांगक|अपाङ्गकः
अपाङ्गक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Maimed, mutilated.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>2 The outer angle of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>अप before अङ्ग the body, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाङ्गदर्शन|अपांगदर्शन|अपाङ्गदर्शनं
अपाङ्गदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A side glance, a leer, a wink.<BR>E.<BR>अपाङ्ग the corner of the eye, and दर्शन looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्
अपाच् or अपाञ्च्<BR>mfn. (अपाङ् अपाची अपाक्)<BR>South, southern.<BR>E.<BR>See अवाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्य|अपाच्यं
अपाच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 Southern, southerly.<BR>2 Not to be ripened or digested.<BR>E.<BR>अपाच्, and यत् affix or अ neg. पाच्य to be ripened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाचीन|अपाचीनं
अपाचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 South, southern.<BR>2 Opposite.<BR>E.<BR>अपाच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाठव
अपाठव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Awkwardness, inelegance.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and पाटब strength, cleverness, &c. see पटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिग्रहण
अपाणिग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Celibacy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पाणिग्रहण taking the hand, as in marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्र|अपात्रं
अपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A worthless or common utensil.<BR>2 An inferior or worthless person.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रीकरण|अपात्रीकरणं
अपात्रीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Acting unbecomingly, doing degrading offices, as for a Brāhmaṇa to receive wealth improperly acquired; to trade, to serve a Śūdra, and to utter an untruth.<BR>2 Excommunication, disqualification.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पात्र a vessel, कररं making, च्ची augment; disqualifying a person from eating out of the same vessel as another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादान|अपादानं
अपादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Removal, ablation, the sense of the fifth or ablative case.<BR>2 Taking away.<BR>E.<BR>अप from, आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान|अपानं|अपानः
अपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The anus.<BR>2 A fart, one of the five vital airs.<BR>E.<BR>अप below, अन to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्नाथ|अपांनाथ|अपांनाथः
अपान्नाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अपाम् of water, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्निधि|अपांनिधि|अपांनिधिः
अपान्निधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अपां of water, निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाप|अपापः
अपाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Sinless, virtuous, pure. So अपापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि).<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and पाप sin or पापिन् sinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्ग|अपामार्गः
अपामार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>अप, मृज to clean, with आङ् prefixed, and घञ् affix; the ashes are used in washing linen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाम्पति|अपांपति|अपांपतिः|अपाम्पतिः
अपाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The ocean. A name of VARUṆA. See अप्पति.<BR>E.<BR>अपाम् genitive case of अप water, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाम्पित्त|अपांपित्त|अपांपित्तं|अपाम्पित्तं
अपाम्पित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>अपाम् of water, and पित्त bile; drying it up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाय|अपायः
अपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Destruction, annihilation.<BR>2 Separation, disunion.<BR>3 Loss, injury.<BR>4 Departure, going away.<BR>5 Retreat, flight.<BR>E.<BR>अप away, अय going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Going away, departing, perishing.<BR>E.<BR>अपाय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The opposite bank of a river.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unbounded, boundless, interminable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पार shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारक
अपारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Incompetent, impotent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पारक who gets through or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थ
अपार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Useless, unprofitable.<BR>2 Unmeaning.<BR>E.<BR>अप without, अर्थ object, also with कन् added अपार्थक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थकरण
अपार्थकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A false plea in a law suit.<BR>E.<BR>अपार्थ, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावर्त्तन|अपावर्तन|अपावर्तनं
अपावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Turning away or from.<BR>2 Retreat, repulse.<BR>3 Returning.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आङ् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत|अपावृतं
अपावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR>2 Covered, concealed.<BR>3 Surrounded, inclosed.<BR>4 Opened.<BR>5 Driven away.<BR>adv. (-र)<BR>Immoderately, unreservedly.<BR>E.<BR>अप priv. वृञ to hide, with आङ prefixed, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृति|अपावृतिः
अपावृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Enclosing, surrounding.<BR>2 Covering, screening.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आङ् before वृ to hide, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्ति|अपावृत्तिः
अपावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Retreat, repulse.<BR>2 Returning.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आङ् before वृत to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्त|अपावृत्तं
अपावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Rolling on the ground, (as a horse.)<BR>2 Uncovered.<BR>3 Driven back or to the rear, repelled.<BR>E.<BR>अप before वृत to stand, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रय|अपाश्रयः
अपाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An awning spread over a court or yard.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Helpless, destitute.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and आश्रथ protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासङ्ग|अपासंग|अपासंगः|अपासङ्गः
अपासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A quiver; also उपासङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासन|अपासनं
अपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Quitting, foregoing, discarding.<BR>2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>अप, अस to be, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासरण|अपासरणं
अपासरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Departing, departure, removal.<BR>E.<BR>अप and आङ्. before सृ to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासित
अपासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrown or cut down, injured, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>अप with अस to throw, क्त affix and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासृत
अपासृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, departed, gone away.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and आङ् before सृ to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्त|अपास्तं
अपास्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Thrown off, set aside.<BR>2 Driven away, expelled.<BR>3 Discarded, abandoned.<BR>4 Disregarded, contemned.<BR>E.<BR>अप and अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्य
अपास्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having quitted or left.<BR>2 Having thrown away.<BR>3 Disregarding.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and अस to throw, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपि
अपि<BR>ind.<BR>A preposition and particle corresponding to even, though, yet, assuredly, &c. and implying<BR>1 Interrogation.<BR>2 Earnest interrogation or enquiry.<BR>3 Doubt.<BR>4 Possibility.<BR>5 Reproof; and,<BR>6 Conjunction.<BR>7 It is often an expletive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and पि to go, with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिगीर्ण|अपिगीर्णं
अपिगीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Praised.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before, गीर्ण part. past., irregularly formed from गॄ to sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच
अपिच<BR>ind.<BR>Moreover, also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच्छल
अपिच्छल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Clear, free from sediment or soil.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पिच्छल muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितु
अपितु<BR>ind.<BR>If, if indeed, yet, but yet.<BR>E.<BR>अपि, and तु but, and, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितृक
अपितृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the next.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पितृ a father, कव् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्र्य
अपित्र्य<BR>mfn. (-त्र्यः-त्र्या-त्र्यं)<BR>Uninherited, acquired, not ancestral or paternal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पितृ a father, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधान|अपिधानं
अपिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Covering, concealment, disappearance.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before धा to have or hold, and ल्युट् aff. See पिधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिनद्ध|अपिनद्धं
अपिनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Clothed, accoutred.<BR>E.<BR>अपि, and नद्ध part. past. of नह to bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशुन
अपिशुन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Upright, honest.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पिशुन dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=047" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीडन
अपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gentleness, kindness, giving pain to nothing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पीडन paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीनस|अपीनसं|अपीनसः
अपीनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Dryness of the nose, want of the pituitary secretion and loss of smell, cold.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पीनस the mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीव्य|अपीव्यं
अपीव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Very handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुच्छ
अपुच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Tailless.<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia sisu.) See शिंशपा.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्य
अपुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Wicked, bad.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and पुण्य virtuous. So अपुण्यशील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्यकृत्
अपुण्यकृत्<BR>mfn. (-त्)<BR>Acting wickedly, wicked, bad.<BR>E.<BR>कृत् who does, with अपुण्य. So अपुण्यवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्र|अपुत्रः
अपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रं)<BR>A man who has no son.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुत्र a son, also with कन added, अपुत्रकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनरावृत्ति|अपुनरावृत्तिः
अपुनरावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Final exemption from life.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुनरावृत्ति renewed practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनर्भव|अपुनर्भवः
अपुनर्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Final beatitude, exemption of the soul from further transmigration.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुनर् again, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुराण
अपुराण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Modern, new. So अपुरातन.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुराण old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुरुष
अपुरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Unmanly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्ट
अपुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Lean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्प|अपुष्पः
अपुष्प<BR>mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पा-ष्पं)<BR>Not flowering.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पुष्प a flower. So अपुष्पक and अपुष्पित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्पफलद|अपुष्पफलदः
अपुष्पफलद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Any tree which bears fruit without flowering, as the jack tree.<BR>E.<BR>अपुष्प, फल fruit, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजक
अपूजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Irreligious, irreverent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूजक a worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजा
अपूजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Irreverence, disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजित
अपूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contemned, disregarded, not reverenced or worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूजित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूत
अपूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Impure.<BR>2 Not having received the invocatory rite.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूत pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप|अपूपः
अपूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Cake of flour, meal, &c.<BR>2 Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>पूय to split with अ neg. prefixed; प affixed, and य dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप्य|अपूप्यः
अपूप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>Flour, meal.<BR>E.<BR>अपूप a cake, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरणी
अपूरणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ण
अपूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Incomplete, not full or entire.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fraction.<BR>2 An incomplete number.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूर्ण full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकाल|अपूर्णकालः
अपूर्णकाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Premature.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Incomplete time.<BR>E.<BR>अपूर्ण, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णकालज
अपूर्णकालज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Abortive, born before the proper time.<BR>E.<BR>अपूर्ण, and काल time, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्णता
अपूर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Incompleteness.<BR>E.<BR>अपूर्ण and तल् affix; also with त्व, अपूर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व|अपूर्वः|अपूर्व्वं
अपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>1 Wonderful, extraordinary.<BR>2 Unprecedented, unpreceded.<BR>3 Excellent, not exceeded.<BR>4 Not easterly.<BR>n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>The remote or unforeseen consequence of an act, as heaven of religious rites, a consequence not immediately preceded by its cause.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्ववत्|अपूर्ववत्
अपूर्व्ववत्<BR>ind.<BR>Singularly, unlike any thing else.<BR>E.<BR>अपूर्व्व and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृक्त|अपृक्तः
अपृक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unmixed, uncombined.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>(In grammar) an affix of a single letter.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पृक्त combined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथक्
अपृथक्<BR>ind.<BR>With, together with, collectively.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, पृथक severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृष्ट
अपृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Unasked, unaddressed, not spoken to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पृष्ट asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षक
अपेक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Expecting.<BR>E.<BR>अप before ईक्ष to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणीय|अपेक्षणीयं
अपेक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be regarded or considered.<BR>2 Desirable.<BR>E.<BR>अप before ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षा
अपेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Expectation, hope.<BR>2 Regard, reference, consideration.<BR>3 Connexion of cause and effect.<BR>4 Absolute connexion, as of an individual with its species.<BR>5 Necessity, need, occasion.<BR>E.<BR>अप, ईक्ष to see, अङ and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षाबुद्धि|अपेक्षाबुद्धिः
अपेक्षाबुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Clearness of understanding, the faculty of arranging and methodising a variety of considerations.<BR>E.<BR>अपेक्षा, and बुद्धि intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षित
अपेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Regarded, considered, referred to.<BR>2 Wished, hoped.<BR>3 Connected.<BR>E.<BR>अप, ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितव्य
अपेक्षितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be regarded or considered.<BR>2 Desirable, estimable.<BR>E.<BR>अप and ईक्ष to see, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षिन्
अपेक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>1 Expecting, hoping, an expectant.<BR>2 Looking to.<BR>E.<BR>अपेक्षा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्य
अपेक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 To be regarded or considered.<BR>2 To be wished or desired.<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered, having, or with, regard or reference to.<BR>E.<BR>अप, ईक्ष to see, यत् or य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेत
अपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, departed.<BR>2 Lost.<BR>3 Open, apart.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेशल
अपेशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Inexpert.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पेशल clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपैशुन
अपैशुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Integrity, honesty, uprightness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पैशुन roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगण्ड|अपोगंडः|अपोगण्डः
अपोगण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Deformed, having a limb too many or too few, &c.<BR>2 Flaccid.<BR>3 A child or infant.<BR>4 Timid, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>अप before गम to go, affix ड, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Removed, carried off.<BR>2 Lost, deprived of, taken away.<BR>3 Discussed, established by argument.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and ऊढ borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिका
अपोदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra or lucida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह|अपोहः
अपोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The removal of doubt by the exercise of the reasoning faculty.<BR>2 Reasoning, arguing.<BR>E.<BR>अप reverse, ऊह to reason, and घञ् affix; opposed to doubt or deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहन|अपोहनं
अपोहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reasoning, exercise of reason.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and ऊह to reason, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहित
अपोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Removed, taken away.<BR>2 Lost, deprived of.<BR>3 Established by reason.<BR>E.<BR>अप, and वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुष
अपौरुष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Unmanliness, cowardice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. पौरुष manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तस्
अप्तस्<BR>n. (-प्तः)<BR>Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, असुन् affix, and त inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु<BR>m. (-प्तुः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 A limb or member.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, and तुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्
अप्नस्<BR>n. (-प्नः)<BR>Water, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, असुन् affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पति|अप्पतिः
अप्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>अप् water, and पति lord; regent of the water, also अपांपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पित्त|अप्पित्तं
अप्पित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Fine.<BR>E.<BR>अप water, पित्त bile; see अपाम्पित्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=048" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्युत
अप्युत<BR>ind.<BR>Also, indeed.<BR>E.<BR>अपि, and उत or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकट|अप्रकटः
अप्रकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Unmanifested, unapparent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकट evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकम्प|अप्रकंप
अप्रकम्प<BR>mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>1 Unshaken, literally or figuratively, firm, steady.<BR>2 Unanswered, unrefuted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकम्पता
अप्रकम्पता<BR>n. (-ता)<BR>1 Firmness, stability.<BR>2 Unanswerableness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding, also with त्व, अप्रकम्पत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकर्षित
अप्रकर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not exceeded, not more than.<BR>2 Unsurpassed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकर्षित bettered, exceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश|अप्रकाशः
अप्रकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Hidden, private, not public or displayed, not manifest or evident.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकाश light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशित
अप्रकाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not manifested, undivulged, unrevealed, not evident or public.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकाशित manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृत|अप्रकृतः
अप्रकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unusual, uncommon, occasional or incidental to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्र before कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृति|अप्रकृतिः
अप्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Accidental property or nature, not the inherent or inseparable property.<BR>2 Spiritual being.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकृति nature or matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृष्ट|अप्रकृष्टः
अप्रकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Low, vile.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रकृष्ट excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रखर|अप्रखरः
अप्रखर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Dull, obtuse.<BR>2 Bland, mild.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रखर sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगल्भ
अप्रगल्भ<BR>mfn. (-ल्मः-ल्मा-ल्मं)<BR>Modest, unassuming.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रगल्भ arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगुण|अप्रगुणः
अप्रगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Confounded, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रगुण direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचुर
अप्रचुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Little, few.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रचुर much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचोदित
अप्रचोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undesired, not bidden or commanded.<BR>2 Undeclared, not said.<BR>3 Not promised.<BR>4 Unasked, declared.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रचोदित directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्युत
अप्रच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Observing, following, not fallen or deviating from.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रच्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रज
अप्रज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Childless, without progeny.<BR>2 Unpeopled, destitute of subjects.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रजा offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजात
अप्रजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Childless.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A barren woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रजात generated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणीत
अप्रणीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconsecrated, profane, common.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रणीत sacred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणोद्य
अप्रणोद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Not to be turned away.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रणोद्य to be dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतर्क्य
अप्रतर्क्य<BR>mfn. (-र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं)<BR>Not to be discussed, incomprehensible by reason.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतर्क्य to be investigated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रताप|अप्रतापः
अप्रताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Meanness, want of dignity.<BR>2 Dulness, want of brilliancy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रताप splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर|अप्रतिकरः
अप्रतिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Trusted, confidential.<BR>2 One who does not requite or retaliate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रति again, कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकार|अप्रतिकारः
अप्रतिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Non-requital, non-acquittal.<BR>2 Non-retaliation.<BR>3 Not remedying.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Helpless, defenceless.<BR>2 Irremediable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिकार rendering again or the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राह्य
अप्रतिग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Not to be taken, unacceptable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिघ
अप्रतिघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Favourable, friendly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिघ adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपण्य
अप्रतिपण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Not to be bartered or exchanged.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, प्रति again, पण्य to be sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपत्ति|अप्रतिपत्तिः
अप्रतिपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Non-ascertainment.<BR>2 Non-performance, failure.<BR>3 Neglecting. disregard.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिपत्ति effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपन्न
अप्रतिपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Unascertained.<BR>2 Unaccomplished.<BR>3 Neglected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिपन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभ|अप्रतिभः
अप्रतिभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Modest, bashful.<BR>2 Confounded, perplexed.<BR>3 Unreflected, (as an image.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिभा light, reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिम
अप्रतिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Unequalled, incomparable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिमा similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्न|अप्रतियत्नः
अप्रतियत्न<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>Natural or spontaneous state or condition.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतियत्न fabrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्नपूर्व्व|अप्रतियत्नपूर्व
अप्रतियत्नपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Natural, not made or artificial.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतियत्न fabrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबन्ध|अप्रतिबंध
अप्रतिबन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>1 Unobstructed, undisputed.<BR>2 Absolute, direct, (as inheritance,) not collateral or presumptive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिबन्ध obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं|अप्रतिरथः
अप्रतिरथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 A march or procession.<BR>2 The Sāma Veda.<BR>3 Auspicious, well, right.<BR>m. (थः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रति against, रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूप
अप्रतिरूप<BR>mfn. (पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>Unequalled, incomparable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रति against, रूप kind, form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूपकथा
अप्रतिरूपकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Unanswerable or incomparable discourse.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रतिरूप, and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकारित
अप्रतिकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिकारित hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिविधान
अप्रतिविधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Natural, unartificial.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिविधान fabrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठ|अप्रतिष्ठः
अप्रतिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Infamous, disreputable.<BR>2 Thrown away, unprofitable.<BR>3 Undecided, fluctuating.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिष्ठा credit, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठित|अप्रतिष्ठितः
अप्रतिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unconsecrated.<BR>2 Obscure, uncelebrated.<BR>3 Unsettled, unfixed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिष्ठित celebrated &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिषिद्ध
अप्रतिषिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Unprohibited, unforbidden.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिषिद्ध forbidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहत
अप्रतिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unaffected, uninjured, unimpaired.<BR>2 Not disappointed.<BR>3 Unobstructed, uninterrupted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतिहत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीकार
अप्रतीकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Unresisting, defenceless.<BR>2 Irremediable.<BR>m. (रः)<BR>1 Non-retaliation.<BR>2 Want of remedy or relief.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतीकार counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीति|अप्रतीतिः
अप्रतीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Mistrust, want of confidence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतीति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतुल|अप्रतुलं|अप्रतुलः
अप्रतुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Necessity, want.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रतुल sufficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्ष|अप्रत्यक्षः
अप्रत्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Invisible, imperceptible, not present.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रत्यक्ष present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यय|अप्रत्ययः
अप्रत्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Doubt, distrust, disbelief.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रत्यय trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्ययिन्
अप्रत्ययिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Doubtful, mistrusting, sceptical.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रत्यय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्याख्यात
अप्रत्याख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Assented to, uncontradicted, unrefuted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रत्याख्यात denied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=049" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्याख्येय
अप्रत्याख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be contradicted, undeniable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रत्याख्येय deniable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रथित
अप्रथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unpublished.<BR>2 Unnoted, unknown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रथित celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधान|अप्रधानं
अप्रधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Subordinate, secondary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रधान principal: (always neuter.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधानता
अप्रधानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Inferiority, subordination.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also with त्व, अप्रधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रबल
अप्रबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Weak, inefficacious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रबल potent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभ
अप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Dull, obscure.<BR>2 Mean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रभा radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभूत
अप्रभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Insufficient, inadequate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्र before भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमत्त|अप्रमत्तः
अप्रमत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Careful, attentive, vigilant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रमत्त careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाद|अप्रमादः
अप्रमाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Care, vigilance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रमाद carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमादिन्
अप्रमादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Careful, cautious, steady.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रमाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमित
अप्रमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unbounded, unmeasured.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रमित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेय
अप्रमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unbounded, immeasurable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रमेय measurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्न|अप्रयत्नः
अप्रयत्न<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>Indifference, laziness.<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Indifferent, apathetic, making no effort.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रयत्न energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रलम्व
अप्रलम्व<BR>mfn. (-म्वः-म्वा-म्वं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रलम्ब slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवत्तक
अप्रवत्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Abstaining from action, inert.<BR>2 Not exciting to action.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रवर्त्तक what excites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्त्तन|अप्रवर्तन|अप्रवर्तनं
अप्रवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Refraining from, not engaging in.<BR>2 Not exciting to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्र before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीण
अप्रवीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unskilful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रवीण skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृत्ति|अप्रवृत्तिः
अप्रवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Abstaining from action, inertion.<BR>2 Nonexcitement.<BR>3 (In Medicine) Suppression of the natural evacuations, constipation, ischury, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रवृत्ति active exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशक्त
अप्रशक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Moderate, temperate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रशक्त intent or fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशक्ति
अप्रशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Moderation.<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Moderate, temperate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रशक्ति addiction to any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Bad, worthless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रशस्त excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्न|अप्रसन्नं
अप्रसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Turbid, muddy.<BR>2 Displeased, dissatisfied, unfavourable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रसन्न pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद|अप्रसादः
अप्रसाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Disfavour, disapprobation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रसाद favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाद्य
अप्रसाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Not to be propitiated.<BR>2 Unappeasable, implacable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्र before षद to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्ध|अप्रसिद्धं
अप्रसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unusual, uncommon.<BR>2 Uncelebrated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रसिद्ध famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसूत
अप्रसूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not having offspring, barren, childless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रसूत bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uncommenced, not begun.<BR>2 Unconnected with, unattached to.<BR>3 Uncommon, unusual.<BR>4 Unpraised, not celebrated.<BR>5 Confounded, not prompt.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्र before ष्टु to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहत|अप्रहतं
अप्रहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unhurt, intact.<BR>2 Untilled, waste, fallow.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रहत broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकृत
अप्राकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Special, particular, not common or generic.<BR>2 Not vulgar, (especially as dialect or speech.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राकृत common, vulgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राग्र्य|अप्राग्र्यं
अप्राग्र्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं)<BR>Secondary, subordinate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राग्र्य principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राचीन|अप्राचीनं
अप्राचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Modern, recent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राचीन old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञ
अप्राज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Unlearned, ignorant.<BR>2 Unconscious, unwitting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राज्ञता
अप्राज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Unconsciousness.<BR>2 Ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also with त्व, अप्राज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राण|अप्राणः
अप्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Lifeless, inanimate.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Death.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राणिन्
अप्राणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Lifeless, inanimate.<BR>E.<BR>अप्राण and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्त|अप्राप्तः
अप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Unobtained.<BR>2 Unarrived.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राप्त acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तकाल
अप्राप्तकाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Inopportune, out of season.<BR>2 Under age.<BR>E.<BR>अप्राप्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तव्यवहार
अप्राप्तव्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A minor.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Under age, not of years to engage in law or public business.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राप्त attained, व्यवहार legal affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्ति|अप्राप्तिः
अप्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Non-attainment, non-acquisition.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राप्ति acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राथ
अप्राथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Unobtainable, unattainable.<BR>ind.<BR>Not having obtained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्राथ future or past part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाणिक|अप्रामाणिकः
अप्रामाणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unauthentic, unauthoritative.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रामाणिक of authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाण्य|अप्रामाण्यं
अप्रामाण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Absence, or insufficiency of proof or authority.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रामाण्य proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रावृत
अप्रावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uncovered, unclothed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रावृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Disliked, disagreeable.<BR>2 Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A foe, an enemy.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A sort of skeat fish, (Silurus pungentissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियकर
अप्रियकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR>2 Disagreeable.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रिय, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियम्वद
अप्रियम्वद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who speaks harshly or unkindly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रियम्वद kind spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रियवादिन्
अप्रियवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking unkindly.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रिय, and वादिन् who speaks; also अप्रियभाषिन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीति|अप्रीतिः
अप्रीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Dislike, aversion.<BR>2 Unfriendliness, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रीति love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीतिकर
अप्रीतिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Unkind, adverse.<BR>2 Disagreeable, offensive.<BR>E.<BR>अप्रीति and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेमन्
अप्रेमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Dislike, aversion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रेमन् affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढ
अप्रौढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Timid, gentle.<BR>2 Immature.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>An unmarried girl, or one very recently married, and not come to womanhood.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. प्रोढ arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस्<BR>f. plur. always (-राः)<BR>The nymphs of Svarga, attendants on INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अप water, सृ to go, and असि Uṇādi affix: or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=51" target="_blank">Page51</a>] अप्स in the waters, and रस flavour: from their fondness for bathing, or from their being produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=050" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरा
अप्सरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>An Apsarā or heavenly nymph.<BR>E.<BR>अप and सृ as before, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Unfruitful, barren.<BR>2 Vain, unproductive.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The aloe plant, (Aloes perfoliata.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Flacoartia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलता
अफलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Barrenness, unprofitableness.<BR>E.<BR>अफल with तल् affix; also अफलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफलाकाङ्क्षिन्|अफलाकांक्षिन्
अफलाकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>Disinterested, indifferent, not looking to beneficial consequences.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. फल fruit, and आकाङ्क्षिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल्गु
अफल्गु<BR>mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)<BR>Productive, profitable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. फल्गु worthless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफुल्ल
अफुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Unblown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. फुल्ल flowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Opium.<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Frothless, without scum or foam.<BR>E.<BR>अ dim. and फेन froth; the word in the first sense is, no doubt, of modern date and foreign introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब
अब<BR>r. 1st cl. with an indicatory इ, अबि (अंबते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unmeaning or nonsensical discourse.<BR>2 Unbound, at liberty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and बद्ध bound, connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धक|अबद्धकं
अबद्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, वुन् being added, which leaves क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धमुख|अबद्धमुखः
अबद्धमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Foulmouthed, scurrilous.<BR>E.<BR>अबद्ध unbound, and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध
अबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Not killing.<BR>f. (धा)<BR>The segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वध what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्य|अबध्यं
अबध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Unmeaning or nonsensical, (as discourse.)<BR>2 Sacred, not to be put to death.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बन्ध to bind, or बध to kill, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्यभाव
अबध्यभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Immunity, sacredness of character, as that of an embassador.<BR>E.<BR>अबध्य, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्धुर
अबन्धुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unlovely, displeasing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बन्धुर handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबन्ध्य|अबन्ध्यः
अबन्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं)<BR>Fruitful, productive, not barren.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and बन्ध्य bound, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Weak, feeble, infirm.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Tapia cratoeva.) see बरुण.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अबाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Unobstructed, unrestrained.<BR>2 Free from pain.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>2 Indistinctness, perplexity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and बाध to oppose, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाधक
अबाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Not obstructing or opposing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बाधक what opposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध्य
अबाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Improper to be pained or opposed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बाध to oppose, यत् part. affix, also with अनीयर् and तव्य, अबाधनीय and अबाधितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबान्धव|अबांधव
अबान्धव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Having no relation or kindred, lone, unacknowledged, unowned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बन्धु kindred, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धि|अबुद्धिः
अबुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Ignorance.<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Ignorant, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिमत्|अबुद्धिमन्त्
अबुद्धिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Unwise, ignorant, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बुद्धिमत् wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध
अबुध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Stupid, foolish. a fool.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बुध wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Ignorance, stupidity.<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Ignorant, stupid.<BR>2 Puzzled, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधगम्य
अबोधगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Incomprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बोध knowledge, गम्य to be attained by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधनीय
अबोधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Unintelligible.<BR>2 Not to be awakened or aroused.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. बोधनीय to be understood, &c. also अबोधितव्य and अबोध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ज|अब्जः
अब्ज<BR>m. (-ब्जः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A kind of tree, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>3 The physician of the gods. See धन्वन्तरि.<BR>mn. (-ब्जः-ब्जं)<BR>A conch.<BR>n. (-ब्जं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A large number, a million of millions.<BR>E.<BR>अव् for अप् water, and ज who is born; from the situation of the things named, or their production at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जज|अब्जजः
अब्जज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज a lotus, and ज born; BRAHMĀ, being said to have sprung at the creation from the lotus, which arose from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जनयन
अब्जनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having fine eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जनेत्र
अब्जनेत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Having fine eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज and नेत्र eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जदृश्
अब्जदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Lotus-eyed, having large fine eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज, and दृश् eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जभोग|अब्जभोगः
अब्जभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The root of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जयोनि|अब्जयोनिः
अब्जयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज, and योनि the vulva; see अब्जज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जवाहन|अब्जवाहनः
अब्जवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज the moon, and वाहन a vehicle: carrying or wearing the moon on his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जहस्त|अब्जहस्तः
अब्जहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज a lotus, and हस्त a hand: SŪRYA is represented holding this flower in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनी
अब्जिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>अब्ज and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनीपति|अब्जिनीपतिः
अब्जिनीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अब्जिनी, and पति a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्द|अब्दः
अब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A year.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>4 The name of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अप् water, प changed to ब, and द what gives; or अब to preserve, &c. and दन् Uṇādi affix; hence the word is also written अब्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दशत
अब्दशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A century.<BR>E.<BR>अब्द, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दसहस
अब्दसहस<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A thousand years.<BR>E.<BR>अब्द, सहस a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दार्द्ध
अब्दार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>A half year.<BR>E.<BR>अब्द, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दिक
अब्दिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Annual, yearly.<BR>E.<BR>अब्द and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दुर्ग|अब्दुर्गः
अब्दुर्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A fortress surrounded by a moat or lake.<BR>E.<BR>अप् water, and दुर्ग fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धि|अब्धिः
अब्धि<BR>m. (-ब्धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अब् substituted for अप् water; धि from धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिकफ|अब्धिकफः
अब्धिकफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and कफ phlegm; being considered as the froth of the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिज|अब्धिजः
अब्धिज<BR>m. du. (-जौ)<BR>The two sons of SŪRYA, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Wine.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and ज born: the former are more usually termed the sons of AŚVINI, see आश्विनेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिद्वीपा
अब्धिद्वीपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and द्वीप in the fem. form; an island surrounded by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिनगरी
अब्धिनगरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A name of Dvārakā, the capital of KṚṢṆA, see द्वारका.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and नगरी a city: the ocean-city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिनवनीतक|अब्धिनवनीतकः
अब्धिनवनीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, नवनीत fresh butter, and क affix; produced by churning the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=051" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिमण्डूकी
अब्धिमण्डूकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि the ocean, and मण्डूकी a female frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिशयन|अब्धिशयनः
अब्धिशयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and शयन sleeping; sleeping on the ocean at the periods of the destruction and renovation of the world, having the serpent ANANTA for his couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ध्यग्नि|अब्ध्यग्निः
अब्ध्यग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>अब्धि, and अग्नि fire. see और्व्वस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्ष|अब्भक्षः
अब्भक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>अब for अप् water, and भक्ष to eat: living upon water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्र|अब्भ्रं
अब्भ्र<BR>m. (-ब्भ्रः)<BR>The ocean. see अभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्रि|अब्भ्रिः
अब्भ्रि<BR>n. (-ब्भ्रिः)<BR>1 A baling vessel.<BR>2 An iron hoe.<BR>3 A stick tipped or shod with iron. see अभ्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मचर्य्य|अब्रह्मचर्य
अब्रह्मचर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Incontinence.<BR>2 Coition.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ब्रह्मचर्य्य the duty of the religious student, i. e. chastity; also with कन् added अब्रह्मचर्य्यक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मण्य|अब्रह्मण्यं
अब्रह्मण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Sacred, not to be killed, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>अ not, ब्रह्मण्य proper for a Brahman, i. e. death; also अब्राह्मण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ
अभ<BR>r. 1st cl. with an indicatory इ, अभि (अंभते)<BR>To sound, (not generally admitted.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्त
अभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Not believing, not attached to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तच्छन्द
अभक्तच्छन्द<BR>m. (न्दः)<BR>Want of appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्त food, छन्द inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तरुच्
अभक्तरुच्<BR>f. (-रुक्)<BR>Want of appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्त food, रुच् inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ति|अभक्तिः
अभक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Incredulity, unbelief, want of devotion to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तिमत्
अभक्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Unbelieving, undevoted to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्तिमत् believing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्षण|अभक्षणं
अभक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Abstaining from, not eating any thing.<BR>2 Fasting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्य|अभक्ष्यं
अभक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Not to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भक्ष्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्यत्व
अभक्ष्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Unfitness as food.<BR>E.<BR>अभक्ष्य and त्व affix; also अभक्ष्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग्न
अभग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Entire, unbroken.<BR>2 Uninterrupted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभङ्गुर|अभंगुर
अभङ्गुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Unbroken, entire.<BR>2 Undisturbed, uninterrupted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भङ्गुर what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभय|अभयं|अभयः
अभय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Absence or removal of fear.<BR>2 The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia citrina.)<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and भय fear; the plant removing the dread of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयडिण्डिम|अभयडिंडिम|अभयडिण्डिमः
अभयडिण्डिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A war-drum.<BR>E.<BR>अभय, and डिण्डिम a drum: inspiring courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयद|अभयदः
अभयद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A protector, a defender.<BR>mfn. (दः-दा-दं)<BR>Removing fear or danger.<BR>E.<BR>अभय fearlessness, द who gives; also with प्र prefix अभयप्रद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदक्षिणा
अभयदक्षिणा<BR>f. (णा)<BR>Promise or present of protection from danger<BR>E.<BR>अभय, and दक्षिणा a gift to a Brahman, which, in this case he may receive from even a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयदान
अभयदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Assurance of safety or protection.<BR>E.<BR>अभय and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयप्रद
अभयप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who grants safety.<BR>E.<BR>अभय fearlessness, प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयप्रदान
अभयप्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Assurance of safety, protection.<BR>E.<BR>अभय, and प्रदान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयवाच्
अभयवाच्<BR>f. (-वाक्)<BR>Assurance of safety, encouragement.<BR>E.<BR>अभय, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव|अभवः
अभव<BR>m. (वः)<BR>1 End of the world, liberation from the world.<BR>2 Non-existence.<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Non-existent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवितव्य
अभवितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What is not to be, what will not be.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भवितव्य to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवितव्यता
अभवितव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fate, predestined non-occurrence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भवितव्य what is to be, तल् affix; also अभवितव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव्य
अभव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Not to be, not predestined.<BR>2 Improper, what ought not to be.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भव्य what is to be, also अभवनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग
अभाग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Not sharing or dividing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भाग a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग्य
अभाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Unfortunate, wretched.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भाग्य fortunate. So अभाग्यवत् (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव|अभावः
अभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Non-existence, annihilation.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 (In logic) Negation of two kinds, संसर्गाभाव universal negation, and अन्योन्याभाव relative or mutual negation.<BR>4 (In rhetoric) Absence of the essential parts of poetical description of character, want of the properties or temperaments.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. भाव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावना
अभावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Absence of judgment or right perception.<BR>2 Absence of religious meditation or contemplation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भावना perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावनीय|अभावनीयः
अभावनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be contemplated or inferred, uninferrible, inconceivable, unintelligible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भावनीय to be perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाविन्
अभाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 What is not to be, what will not be.<BR>2 Void of temperament or natural disposition.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भाविन् future, or having disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाषण|अभाषणं
अभाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Silence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभि
अभि<BR>ind.<BR>A preposition and particle implying,<BR>1 Superiority in place, rank, or power, (over, upon, against, above);<BR>2 Proximity, (near);<BR>3 Separation, (severally);<BR>4 Wish, desire:<BR>5 Conjunction, particularizing, (to, with respect to.) Thus अभिक्रमितुं to overpower; अभिगन्तुं to approach; अभिख्यातुं to speak to; अभिभव disgrace; अभिलाष desire; अभ्यग्निं on the fire, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भा to shine, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक|अभिकः
अभिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Lustful, libidinous.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and क from कम to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षा|अभिकांक्षा
अभिकाङ्क्षा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and काङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षित
अभिकाङ्क्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and काङ्क्षित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाङ्क्षिन्|अभिकांक्षिन्
अभिकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and काङ्क्षिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम|अभिक्रमः
अभिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Assault, attack, invasion.<BR>2 Mounting, ascending.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before or beyond, क्रम to go, and घञ् affix; see अतिक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>1 A name or appellation.<BR>2 Calling, addressing.<BR>3 Beauty.<BR>4 Fame, glory.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, ख्या to speak, अङ् affix, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=052" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगत
अभिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Approached.<BR>E.<BR>अभि near to, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम|अभिगमः
अभिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Approach, proximity.<BR>E.<BR>अभि to, गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमन|अभिगमनं
अभिगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Approaching, going near to.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभिगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Approaching.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रस्त|अभिग्रस्तः
अभिग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Overcome, subdued.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रह|अभिग्रहः
अभिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Attack, onset.<BR>2 Challenge, going to fight.<BR>3 Plundering, robbing.<BR>4 Celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before, in presence of, ग्रह to take, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहण|अभिग्रहणं
अभिग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Robbing, seizing any thing in presence of the owner.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before ग्रह to take, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघर्षण|अभिघर्षणं
अभिघर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>2 Possession by an evil spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before घृष to pound, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Striking, wounding, beating.<BR>2 Touching, contact.<BR>3 Pain, infliction, torture.<BR>4 Remedy, removal.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The combination of the fourth letter of any class with any of the other three preceding it.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before हन to strike, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातिन्
अभिघातिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>An enemy.<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Hostile, an assailant.<BR>2 Inflicting injury.<BR>3 Remedial.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before हन to strike or kill, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघार|अभिघारः
अभिघार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, घृ to scatter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचर|अभिचरः
अभिचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>अभि after, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचार|अभिचारः
अभिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Magic for a malevolent purpose, the spells and diagrams of the Atharva Veda and some of the Tantras, supposed to produce mental aberration, love, hatred, loss of feeling or paralysis, and death.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before चर to go, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारमन्त्र|अभिचारमन्त्रः
अभिचारमन्त्र<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>A formula or prayer for working a charm, an incantation.<BR>E.<BR>अभिचार, and मन्त्र a formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिक
अभिचारिक<BR>m. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Magical, magician, relating to spells or magic.<BR>E.<BR>अभिचार and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारित
अभिचारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inchanted, charmed.<BR>E.<BR>अभिचार and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिन्
अभिचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Magical, done by magic.<BR>2 Magician or one employing spells, a conjuror, a witch, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अभिचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचैद्य
अभिचैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR>E.<BR>अभि over, चैद्य the people of Cedi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजन|अभिजनः
अभिजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Family, race.<BR>2 Native country.<BR>3 The head or ornament of a family.<BR>4 Fame, notoriety.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before जन who is born, from जन to be born, घञ् affix, the vowel remaining short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजात|अभिजातः
अभिजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Noble, well born.<BR>2 Wise, learned.<BR>3 Fit, proper.<BR>4 Handsome.<BR>5 Respectable.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजित्
अभिजित्<BR>f. (-जित्)<BR>1 One of the Nakṣatras or lunar asterisms.<BR>2 The eighth muhūrtta or hour.<BR>2 An expiatory sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and जित् what conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञ|अभिज्ञः
अभिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Skilful, clever.<BR>2 One who knows or understands.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and ज्ञ who knows, from ज्ञा to know, क affix leaving अ; आ is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञात
अभिज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Detected, discovered.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञान|अभिज्ञानं
अभिज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A mark, a spot or stain.<BR>2 A sign, a token.<BR>3 Ascertaining, knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before ज्ञा to know, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्त
अभितप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Scorched, burnt.<BR>2 Afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and तप्त burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितस्
अभितस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Quickly.<BR>2 Entirely.<BR>3 Before, in presence of.<BR>4 On both sides.<BR>5 Near.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताप|अभितापः
अभिताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Extreme heat.<BR>2 Agitation, affliction, emotion.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रोह|अभिद्रोहः
अभिद्रोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Oppression, cruelty.<BR>2 Abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and द्रोह violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A name, an appellation.<BR>2 (In logic,) the power or sense of a word.<BR>3 The chief or common acceptation of a word.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before धा to have, क affix and टाप् fem.: what any thing is obtained by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधान|अभिधानं
अभिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A name, an appellation.<BR>2 Speaking, speech.<BR>3 A vocabulary, a dictionary.<BR>E.<BR>as before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिक
अभिधायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Denominative, relating to.<BR>E.<BR>अभिधायिन् with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायिन्
अभिधायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यौ-यिनी-यि)<BR>Denominative, appellative.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before धा to have, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावन|अभिधावनं
अभिधावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pursuit, chase.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and धावन running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधित्सा
अभिधित्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Direction, injunction.<BR>2 Desire, wish.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before धा to have, desiderative form, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेय|अभिधेयं
अभिधेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A name or appellation.<BR>2 A significant word.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be named or mentioned.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before धा, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेयरहित
अभिधेयरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unmeaning, nonsensical, having no sense nor meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अभिधेय, and रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्या
अभिध्या<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>1 Coveting another's property.<BR>2 Desire, longing for in general.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, ध्ये to think, and अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यान|अभिध्यानं
अभिध्यान<BR>n. (नं)<BR>1 Coveting, desiring, longing for.<BR>2 Meditation, profound thought.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before ध्यै to think of, ल्युट् affix, or ध्यान contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनद्ध
अभिनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound, tied round, fastened on or upon.<BR>E.<BR>अभि over, नद्ध tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दन|अभिनंदनं|अभिनन्दनः
अभिनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The fourth Jaina Tīrthakara or deified saint.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Delighting, rejoicing.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before नदि to please, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दा
अभिनन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Wish, expectation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and नदि to please, affix अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनन्दित
अभिनन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delighted, made happy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and नन्दित pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनय|अभिनयः
अभिनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Indication of a passion or purpose by look, gesture, &c.<BR>2 Acting, dramatic personification.<BR>3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>4 Civility, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, णीञ्^1 to guide, and अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: Cf WIL and WIL1819 णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनव|अभिनवः
अभिनव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 New.<BR>2 Young.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनवोद्भिद्
अभिनवोद्भिद्<BR>m. (-द् or -त्)<BR>A germin, a new bud.<BR>E.<BR>अभिनव new, and उद्भिद् produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्म्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्तः
अभिनिर्म्मुक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>One asleep at sun-set.<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Left, quitted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि always, निर्म्मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=053" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्याण|अभिनिर्याणं|अभिनिर्य्याण
अभिनिर्याण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Invasion, march of an assailant, or march in general.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निर् prefixed to या to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्वृत्ति|अभिनिर्वृत्तिः
अभिनिर्वृत्ति<BR>(-त्तिः)<BR>Accession of disease.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निर्वृत्ति inaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्ट
अभिनिविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Conversant or familiar with, studied in.<BR>2 Attentive, engrossed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेश|अभिनिवेशः
अभिनिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Intentness, application, perseverance, determination to effect a purpose, or attain an object.<BR>2 Tenacity.<BR>3 Study.<BR>4 Ignorant fear causing death.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and नि before विश to enter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रमण|अभिनिष्क्रमणं
अभिनिष्क्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going forth or out, issuing, exit.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and निर् before क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रान्त
अभिनिष्क्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Gone out or forth.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निष्क्रान्त gone out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पतन|अभिनिष्पतनं
अभिनिष्पतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sallying, issuing, going forth.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before निष्पतन going out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्ति|अभिनिष्पत्तिः
अभिनिष्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>End, termination.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निष्पत्ति discontinuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पन्न
अभिनिष्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Finished, completed^1.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and निष्पन्न done.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्ठान|अभिनिष्ठानः
अभिनिष्ठान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The soft aspirate.<BR>2 A letter of the alphabet.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and नि before ष्ठा to stay or stand, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीत|अभिनीतः
अभिनीत<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fit, proper.<BR>2 Friendly, kind.<BR>3 Highly finished, or ornamented.<BR>4 Patient.<BR>5 Impatient.<BR>6 Passionate.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and णीञ्^1 to guide or obtain, क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: Cf WIL and WIL1819 णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीति|अभिनीतिः
अभिनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Friendship, civility, kindness.<BR>2 Gesture, expressive gesticulation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and नीति conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेय
अभिनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be represented dramatically.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before नी to guide, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतृ
अभिनेतृ<BR>mf. (ता-त्री-)<BR>An actor, an actress.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before नी to guide, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्न
अभिन्न<BR>mfn. (न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Same, identical.<BR>2 One, undivided.<BR>3 Unchanged, unaltered.<BR>4 Uncut, unbroken.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>An integer, a whole number.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भिन्न other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्नता
अभिन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Identity, wholeness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, or with त्व, अभिन्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपन्न|अभिपन्नः
अभिपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Guilty.<BR>2 Unfortunate, calamitous.<BR>3 Subdued.<BR>4 Flown, fugitive.<BR>5 Seeking refuge.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before पद to go, in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणय|अभिप्रणयः
अभिप्रणय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Propitiation.<BR>2 Affection, favour.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and प्र before णी, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणीत
अभिप्रणीत<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Invoked, propitiated.<BR>2 Consecrated.<BR>3 Brought, attracted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and प्र before णी to conduct, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राय|अभिप्रायः
अभिप्राय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Meaning, intention, wish, purpose.<BR>2 Meaning, a sentence, sense.<BR>3 The main purport of a book.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and प्रिञ् to satisfy, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत|अभिप्रेतं
अभिप्रेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Meant, intended.<BR>2 Wished.<BR>3 Wishing, desirous, ambitious of, pretending to.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and प्र before इण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत्य
अभिप्रेत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Intending, meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and प्र before इण to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रोक्षण|अभिप्रोक्षणं
अभिप्रोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sprinkling, affusion.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and प्रोक्षण sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लुत
अभिप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Overflowed, overrun, filled with.<BR>2 Attacked or affected by, labouring under.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभव|अभिभवः
अभिभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Defeat, subjugation.<BR>2 Humiliation, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अभि implying inferiority, and भव being; from भू to be, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवन|अभिभवनं
अभिभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Overpowering, overcoming.<BR>2 Being overpowered.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, भू to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूत|अभिभूतः
अभिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Humbled, surpassed, defeated, subdued.<BR>2 Ignorant.<BR>3 Overcome with feelings or wants, with passion, with hunger, &c.<BR>4 Injured, aggrieved.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and भूत been, being; part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Disrespect, disgrace, humiliation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before भू to be, and क्तिन् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>2 Agreed, accepted.<BR>3 Admitted, assented to.<BR>E.<BR>अभि over, मत thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतता
अभिमतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Desire, love.<BR>2 Agreeableness, desirableness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, अभिमतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभिमन्त्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Calling to, addressing, inviting.<BR>2 Counselling.<BR>3 Consecrating any thing by a special formula.<BR>E.<BR>अभि in presence, मन्त्र to speak, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्त्रित
अभिमन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Charmed, consecrated, had a certain formula pronounced over it.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, मन्त्र to charm, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्तृ|अभिमंतृ
अभिमन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A counsellor, a monitor.<BR>2 Conscience.<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Who or what admonishes or advises.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मन to mind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्थ|अभिमंथः|अभिमन्थः
अभिमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>Ophthalmia, disease of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मन्थ to agitate, घञ् affix; also read अधिमन्थः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्यु|अभिमन्युः
अभिमन्यु<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>The son of ARJUNA by SUBHADRĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मन wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर|अभिमरः
अभिमर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 War, combat.<BR>3 Binding, confinement.<BR>4 Treachery, danger from one's own party or friends.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before मर from मृ to die, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द|अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>2 Devastation of a country, &c. by an enemy.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मृद् to tread down, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शन|अभिमर्शनं
अभिमर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Touching, rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before मृश to rub, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्षण|अभिमर्षणं
अभिमर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sprinkling upon or over.<BR>2 Licking the lips as an indication of guilt or prevarication.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मृष to sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाति|अभिमातिः
अभिमाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, and सा to measure, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमान|अभिमानः
अभिमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Pride, haughtiness.<BR>2 Knowledge.<BR>3 Affection.<BR>4 Injury, hurting, killing.<BR>5 Requesting.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मन to know, with घञ् affix, or मी to injure, and ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानता
अभिमानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last: also अभिमानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानवत्|अभिमानवन्त्
अभिमानवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Pride.<BR>E.<BR>मतुप् poss. affix; added to अभिमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानित|अभिमानितं
अभिमानित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मन to know, in the causal form, and क्त aff.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>अभिमानिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=054" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>अभिमान and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाय|अभिमायः
अभिमाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Subdued, reduced, broken or worn down.<BR>2 Stupid, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before माया ignorance, illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>Present.<BR>2 Near to, in front of.<BR>n. adv. (-खं)<BR>In front or presence of.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखता
अभिमुखता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Presence, proximity.<BR>E.<BR>अभिमुख, and तल् affix or with त्व, अभिमुखत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृष्ट
अभिमृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Touched, rubbed, brought or passed close.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and मृष्ट rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियाति|अभियातिः
अभियाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, या to go, with अति affix, see अभियातिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियातिन्
अभियातिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, यत् to strive, and णिनि affix, see अभिघातिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्त|अभियुक्तः
अभियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Attacked by an enemy, assaulted, assailed.<BR>2 Diligent, intent.<BR>3 Said, spoken.<BR>4 Blamed, rebuked.<BR>5 (In law) Charged, prosecuted, defendant.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियुक्तता
अभियुक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Diligence, application.<BR>2 Accusation, prosecution.<BR>E.<BR>अभियुक्त and तल् affix; also with त्व, अभियुक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तव्य
अभियोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Blamable, to be reproved or rebuked.<BR>2 To be prevented or prohibited.<BR>3 To be prosecuted, indictable.<BR>4 To be pursued diligently.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before युज to join, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोक्तृ
अभियोक्तृ<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A plaintiff, an accuser.<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>One who assails another in any way.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before युज to join, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोग|अभियोगः
अभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Attack, assault.<BR>2 Challenging to fight.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>4 Energetic effort, exertion, perseverance.<BR>5 Reprimand, reproof.<BR>5 Prohibition, prevention.<BR>7 Contact, conjunction.<BR>8 (In law) A plaint, a charge, an accusation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, युज to joint, and घञ् affix, ज being changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभियोगिन्
अभियोगिन्<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>A plaintiff, a prosecutor.<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>One who assails another in any way.<BR>E.<BR>अभियोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षा
अभिरक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Universal protection, wide benevolence.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and रक्षा preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षित
अभिरक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Guarded, preserved, kept.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and रक्षित preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरक्षितृ
अभिरक्षितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A guardian.<BR>2 A controller.<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what keeps or preserves.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, रक्षितृ who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरत
अभिरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased or contented with, satisfied.<BR>2 Performing, practising, engaged in, attentive to.<BR>E.<BR>अभिरम to sport, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरति|अभिरतिः
अभिरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Pleasure, delight.<BR>2 Practice, occupation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and रति pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराद्ध
अभिराद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Propitiated, (by penance, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and राद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिराम|अभिरामः
अभिराम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before रम to sport, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरामता
अभिरामता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Beauty, splendour.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last: also अभिरामत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरुचि|अभिरुचिः
अभिरुचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>1 Ambition, desire of fame.<BR>2 Desire in general.<BR>3 Taste, relish.<BR>4 Splendour.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and रुचि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिरूप|अभिरूपः
अभिरूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A learned Brahman, a Paṇḍita.<BR>2 A name of KĀMA.<BR>3 Of the moon.<BR>4 Of ŚIVA.<BR>5 Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>1 Learned.<BR>2 Pleasing.<BR>3 Handsome.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before रूप to have form, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषणीय
अभिलषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Desirable.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before लष to wish, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलषित
अभिलषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Desired, wished.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Desire.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before लष with क्त part. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाप|अभिलापः
अभिलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Speech, speaking.<BR>2 Declaration of the object of a vow or religious obligation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before लप to speak, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाव|अभिलावः
अभिलाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Reaping.<BR>2 Cutting.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and लूञ्^1 to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाष|अभिलाषः
अभिलाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and लष to like, घञ् aff; also अभिलास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषिन्
अभिलाषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Wishing, desiring.<BR>E.<BR>अभिलाष and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलाषुक|अभिलाषुकः
अभिलाषुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Covetous, greedy.<BR>2 Desirous, wishing.<BR>E.<BR>अभिलष to desire, उकन् affix, and the antepen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलास|अभिलासः
अभिलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>See अभिलाष; the root being लष, or लस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलिखित
अभिलिखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inserted in writing.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and लिखित written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिलेखन
अभिलेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Writing or inscribing.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and लेखन writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवन्दन|अभिवंदनं
अभिवन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Saluting respectfully.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before वदि to praise, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद|अभिवादः
अभिवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Reverential salutation.<BR>2 Opprobrious, or unfriendly speech, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, or adverse, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादक|अभिवादकः
अभिवादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Civil, polite.<BR>2 Uncivil, abusive.<BR>E.<BR>अभि to, or against, वादक who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवादन|अभिवादनं
अभिवादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Respectful salutation, a bow or prostration; including sometimes the name or title of the person so addressed, and followed by the declaration of the person's own name. Salutation of a superior or elder, by a junior or inferior, and especially of the teacher by his disciple. In general it is merely lifting the joined hands to the forehead, and saying, अहममिवादये I salute.<BR>E.<BR>अभि in presence of, and वादन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाद्य|अभिवाद्यः
अभिवाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be saluted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and वाद्य to be addressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिवाह्य
अभिवाह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 Presentation, offering.<BR>2 Conveyance, transmission.<BR>E.<BR>अभि to, बाह्य to be borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिविनीत
अभिविनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pious, pure, devout.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and विनीत well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्यक्त
अभिव्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Plain, distinct, evident, manifest.<BR>2 Declared, revealed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and व्यक्त plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याप्ति|अभिव्याप्तिः
अभिव्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Co-extending, pervading, omnipresence.<BR>E.<BR>अभि every where, and व्याप्ति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिव्याहार|अभिव्याहारः
अभिव्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An articulate and significant word or phrase.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and व्याहार speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशङ्कित|अभिशंकित
अभिशङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Frightened, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and शङ्कित alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=055" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपन|अभिशपनं
अभिशपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>False accusation, calumny. See अभिशाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशप्त|अभिशप्तः
अभिशप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Falsely accused, calumniated.<BR>2 Cursed, accursed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before शप with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसन|अभिशंसनं
अभिशंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calumny, abuse, calumniating, abusing.<BR>E.<BR>अभि reverse, शंस to praise, affix; ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>2 Defamed, infamous.<BR>3 Sinful, wicked.<BR>4 Asked, wanted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि- implying opposition, शस to praise, and affix of the part. past. क्त; the nasal being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तक
अभिशस्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Calumniating, a calumniator.<BR>E.<BR>अभिशस्त, and कृ to make, affix अच् or ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ताङ्क
अभिशस्ताङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A brand, a mark of infamy on a criminal.<BR>E.<BR>अभिशस्त infamous, अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्ति|अभिशस्तिः
अभिशस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>1 Calumny, scandal, defamation.<BR>2 Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before शंस to praise or ask, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दित
अभिशब्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Declared, announced.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and शब्दित sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशाप|अभिशापः
अभिशाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 False accusation, calumny.<BR>2 Charge, accusation.<BR>3 Suffering from anger or passion.<BR>4 Curse, imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and शप to curse or swear, affix घञ्; or with ल्युट् affix अधिशपन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापन|अभिशापनं
अभिशापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pronouncing a curse or malediction.<BR>E.<BR>अभि with शप causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषङ्ग|अभिषंग|अभिषंगः|अभिषङ्गः
अभिषङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Curse or imprecation.<BR>2 An oath.<BR>3 Defeat.<BR>4 False accusation, calumny.<BR>5 Association, company, connexion.<BR>6 Embracing.<BR>7 Possession by evil spirits.<BR>8 Accession of passion.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, along with, &c. षञ्ज to embrace, to unite, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषव|अभिषवं|अभिषवः
अभिषव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Religious bathing, ablution preparatory to religious rites.<BR>2 Sacrifice.<BR>3 Bathing in general.<BR>4 Drinking the juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR>5 Ferment, yeast, any substance producing vinous fermentation.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sour gruel. See काञ्जिका.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सु to mix, to stir, अप् affix; and स is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवण|अभिषवणं
अभिषवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Bathing, ablution.<BR>2 Sacrificing, &c. See अभिषव.<BR>E.<BR>as before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषह्य
अभिषह्य<BR>ind.<BR>Insolently, violently, by force.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, षह to bear, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषिक्त
अभिषिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>2 Anointed, installed, inaugurated, enthroned.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सिच् to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुत|अभिषुतं
अभिषुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Sour gruel. See काञ्जिका.<BR>2 The juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सु to mix, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक|अभिषेकः
अभिषेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Bathing, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सिच to sprinkle, and घञ् affix; the word is often used for initiation, royal unction, &c. sprinkling with the water of the Ganges, or water in which various articles have been immersed, being an essential part of the rites: also for a religious ceremony, including the presentation of a variety of articles, fruits, gems, &c. along with water or fluid substances, for the bathing of the deity to whom worship is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकशाला
अभिषेकशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The hall of coronation.<BR>E.<BR>अभिषेक, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचन|अभिषेचनं
अभिषेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Initiation, inauguration.<BR>2 Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before षिच् to sprinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणन|अभिषेणनं
अभिषेणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>March to repel an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि against, सेना an army, used as a verb, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टुत|अभिष्टुतं
अभिष्टुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before स्तु to praise, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्द|अभिष्यंदः|अभिष्यन्दः
अभिष्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Great increase or enlargement.<BR>2 Oozing or flowing.<BR>3 Weakness of, or running at the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before स्यन्द to ooze or drop as a liquid, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिन्|अभिष्यंदिन्
अभिष्यन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>1 Oozing, trickling.<BR>2 Having weak eyes.<BR>3 Causing defluxions or serous effusion.<BR>E.<BR>अभिष्यन्द and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यन्दिरमण|अभिष्यन्दिरमणं
अभिष्यन्दिरमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A suburb, a smaller city appended to a larger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंहित
अभिसंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Attached to, interested, following any object eagerly.<BR>2 Agreed, contracted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सम् before धा to have, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्ताप|अभिसंताप|अभिसंतापः|अभिसन्तापः
अभिसन्ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>अभि much, and सन्ताप pain, heat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्धान|अभिसंधान|अभिसंधानं|अभिसन्धानं
अभिसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cheating, deceiving.<BR>2 Attachment or interest in any object.<BR>3 Special agreement.<BR>4 Making peace or alliance.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सम् before धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसन्धि|अभिसंधि|अभिसंधिः|अभिसन्धिः
अभिसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>1 Cheating, deceit.<BR>2 Purpose, object.<BR>3 Special agreement.<BR>4 Making peace or alliance.<BR>5 Joint junction.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सन्धि agreement, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसम्पात|अभिसंपात|अभिसंपातः|अभिसम्पातः
अभिसम्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Curse, imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सम्पात going or falling; from पत to fall, with सं prefix, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर|अभिसरः
अभिसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A companion, a follower.<BR>E.<BR>अभि after or near, and सर who goes; from सृ to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसम्बन्ध|अभिसंबन्ध|अभिसंबंधः|अभिसंबन्धः
अभिसम्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Relation, connexion.<BR>2 Sexual connexion.<BR>3 Contact, conjunction.<BR>E.<BR>अभि intensitive, सम्वन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभिसर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Killing. See अतिसर्ज्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायम
अभिसायम<BR>ind.<BR>About evening, at sunset.<BR>E.<BR>अभि towards, साव evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसार|अभिसारः
अभिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Strength.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 A companion, a follower.<BR>4 The instrument or agent.<BR>5 An assignation, an appointment.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सृ to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारण|अभिसारणं
अभिसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Coming to or near, visiting, attending, following.<BR>2 Importuning, haunting.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सारण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभिसारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman who makes or keeps an assignation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before सृ to go, वुन affix which leaves क, and टाप् fem. do. also अभिसारिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिन्
अभिसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Going to or near to, visiting, attending.<BR>2 Going to an appointment or assignation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and सारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहत
अभिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Humbled, subdued, broken down.<BR>2 Killed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and हत part. past. of हन to kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहार|अभिहारः
अभिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Robbing, seizing any thing in the owner's presence.<BR>2 A brisk attack.<BR>3 Arming, taking up arms.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before हृ to take, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken, said, declared.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before धा to have, the part. affix क्त, and हि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितत्व
अभिहितत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Text, authority, declaration.<BR>E.<BR>अभिहित said, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=056" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A poet.<BR>2 A husband.<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Lustful, libidinous.<BR>2 Anxious, desirous.<BR>3 Cruel.<BR>4 Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before क, from कम to desire: the इ being made long irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्ण|अभीक्ष्णं
अभीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Repeated, frequent.<BR>2 Constant, perpetual.<BR>ind. (क्ष्णम्)<BR>1 Repeatedly, again and again.<BR>2 Perpetually, constantly.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before क्ष्णा to whet, डम् affix, and the इ of अभि made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अभीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भीत afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीति|अभीतिः
अभीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fearlessness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भीति fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सित|अभीप्सितं
अभीप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, आप to obtain, in the desiderative form, and क्त affix, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सु
अभीप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before ईप्सु wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीम|अभीमः
अभीम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Causing no fear or terror, unterrific. So अभीषण and अभीष्म and अभैरव.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भीम fearful, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pride.<BR>E.<BR>See अभिमान, the इ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीर|अभीरः
अभीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and ईर to send, अच् affix; also अभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of BHAIRAVA.<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.) See शतमूली.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भीरु timid: as applied to the plant, not fearful of breaking, from the number of its roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुपत्री
अभीरुपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A plant. See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलु
अभीलु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>अभीरु, र being changed to ल. Also अभीलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशु|अभीशुः
अभीशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 A rein.<BR>f. (-शुः)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before अशू to pervade, उ affix, derivative irregular, See अभीषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषङ्ग|अभीषंग|अभीषङ्गः
अभीषङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Curse, imprecation. See अभिषङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>as before, the इ being here long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषु|अभीषुः
अभीषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 A rein.<BR>3 Love, lust.<BR>4 Passion.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before इष to desire, and उ affix or अश to pervade, &c. whence, अभिशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषुमत्|अभीषुमन्त्
अभीषुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Splendid, brilliant.<BR>2 Enamoured, amorous.<BR>E.<BR>अभीषु and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A perfume. See रेणुका.<BR>E.<BR>अभि repeatedly, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Uneaten.<BR>2 Unenjoyed, unused, unexpended.<BR>3 One who has not eaten.<BR>4 One who has not enjoyed or possessed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Straight, not bent.<BR>2 Well, free from disease.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भुग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज
अभुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Armless, maimed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भुज the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Non-existent, absent, what is not or has not been.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमि|अभूमिः
अभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Want of place of refuge or support, destitution, privation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूयिष्ठ
अभूयिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Few, scanty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भूयिष्ठ many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूरि
अभूरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Few, some, several.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भूरि many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूषित
अभूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unadorned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भूषित adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृशम्
अभृशम्<BR>ind.<BR>A little, a few.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भृशम् much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Identity, absence of difference or distinction.<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Alike, identical.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भेद distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अभेद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>A diamond.<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Hard, solid, not to be broken or divided.<BR>2 Not to be pierced, indivisible.<BR>3 Impenetrable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and भेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्यता
अभेद्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Indivisibility.<BR>2 Impenetrability.<BR>3 Inseparability.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also with त्व, अभेद्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तव्य
अभोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Not to be used or enjoyed.<BR>2 Not to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भुज to eat, &c. तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तृ
अभोक्तृ<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>An abstemious person.<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>Not enjoying, not using.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोक्तृ who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग|अभोगः
अभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Non-enjoyment, not making use of.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोग्य
अभोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Not to be used or enjoyed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोग्य to be used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजन|अभोजनं
अभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Abstinence, fasting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजनीय
अभोजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Not to be eaten.<BR>2 Not to be used.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोजनीय to be eaten, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजिन्
अभोजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Fasting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Impure, prohibited as food, not to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भोज्य to be eaten, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यक्त
अभ्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Oiled, anointed.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अञ्ज to anoint, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंग|अभ्यंगः|अभ्यङ्गः
अभ्यङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Rubbing the body with unctuous substances; smearing the body with oil, inunction.<BR>2 Unguent, liniment, oily application.<BR>3 Applying collyrium to the eyes.<BR>4 Sediment of oil, cake.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अञ्ज to anoint, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यञ्जन|अभ्यंजन|अभ्यंजनं|अभ्यञ्जनं
अभ्यञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Oil.<BR>2 Smearing the body with oil, inunction; see the preceding.<BR>3 Applying collyrium to the eyelashes, decorating the hair, &c. or any personal embellishment.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, अञ्ज to anoint, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-क्रं)<BR>Exceeding, surpassing (in number, power, or kind, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधीन
अभ्यधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dependant.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 Order, command.<BR>2 Assent, permission. Also अभ्यनुज्ञानं<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अनुज्ञा order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Included space.<BR>2 Inner part, middle.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अन्तर within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यन्तरायाम|अभ्यन्तरायामः
अभ्यन्तरायाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Curvature of the spine by spasm; emprosthotonos^1.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्यन्तर middle, and आयाम length.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञात
अभ्यनुज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ordered.<BR>2 Permitted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अनु before ज्ञा to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित|अभ्यमितः
अभ्यमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, अम to be sick, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीण|अभ्यमित्रीणः
अभ्यमित्रीण<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A soldier who faces the enemy valiantly.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before, or against, अमित्र an enemy, and ख affix; the affix being छ or यत्, the word is also written अभ्यमित्रीय or अभ्यमित्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्च्चन|अभ्यर्चन|अभ्यर्चनं
अभ्यर्च्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worship, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before अर्च्च to worship, affix ल्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्च्चा|अभ्यर्चा
अभ्यर्च्चा<BR>f. (-र्च्चा)<BR>Respect, worship.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अर्च्च reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं|अभ्यर्ण्ण
अभ्यर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>E.<BR>अभि near, and अर्ण irr. part. past. of अर्द to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थना
अभ्यर्थना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Petition, request.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before अर्थ to ask, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=057" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थित
अभ्यर्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Asked, invited.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अर्थित asked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हित
अभ्यर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fit, proper, becoming.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अर्हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकर्षण|अभ्यवकर्षणं
अभ्यवकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Extraction, drawing out.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and अव prefixed to कृष to draw furrows, affix ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कंदः|अभ्यवस्कन्दः
अभ्यवस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>2 Facing an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अव before स्कन्द to go, affix घञ्; also with ल्युट् affix, अभ्यवस्कन्दनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरण|अभ्यवहरणं
अभ्यवहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अव before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार|अभ्यवहारः
अभ्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अव before हृ to convey, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृत|अभ्यवहृतं
अभ्यवहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and अव before हृ to convey, and the part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसन|अभ्यसनं
अभ्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Frequent repetition, use, exercise, especially of the memory, learning by rote.<BR>E.<BR>अभि frequently, अस to throw or send, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्यसूय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Angry, vexed.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Detraction. Also असूया.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before असूया envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Detracting, a detractor, a calumniator.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before असूय to envy or detract, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्य
अभ्यस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>To be studied. Also अभ्यसनीयं.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before अस to throw, affix य or अनीयर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Exercised, practised.<BR>2 Learnt by heart.<BR>3 Repeated as the radical syllable of a verb.<BR>E.<BR>अभि frequently, अस to throw or send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकाङ्क्षित|अभ्याकांक्षित|अभ्याकांक्षितं|अभ्याकाङ्क्षितं
अभ्याकाङ्क्षित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A groundless complaint, a false accusation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आकाङ्क्षित desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यान|अभ्याख्यानं
अभ्याख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A false accusation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आख्यान saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A guest, a visitor.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Arrived.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम|अभ्यागमः
अभ्यागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Striking, killing.<BR>3 Enmity.<BR>4 Vicinity.<BR>5 Rising, getting up.<BR>6 Coming, arrival, visit.<BR>E.<BR>अभि near, or before, &c. गम to go, with आ prefixed, and अच् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमन|अभ्यागमनं
अभ्यागमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Arrival, visitation.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आगमन coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिक|अभ्यागारिकः
अभ्यागारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Diligent in supporting a family.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before आगार a house, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघात|अभ्याघातः
अभ्याघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Assault, attack.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आघात assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादान|अभ्यादानं
अभ्यादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Beginning, commencement.<BR>2 First beginning.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यान्त|अभ्यांत
अभ्यान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before अम to be sick, and the affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यापात|अभ्यापातः
अभ्यापात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Calamity, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and आङ् before पत to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्द्द|अभ्यामर्द|अभ्यामर्दः
अभ्यामर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and आ before मृद to tread down, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Constant repetition. See अभ्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Practice, exercise.<BR>2 Learning by rote.<BR>3 Practising archery.<BR>4 (In arithmetic,) Multiplication.<BR>5 (In grammar,) The reduplicate syllable of a verb.<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before, अस to go, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासता
अभ्यासता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Constant practice, use, habit.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्यास and तल् affix, also with त्व, अभ्यासत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासयोग|अभ्यासयोगः
अभ्यासयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The practice of frequent and repeated contemplation on any deity or abstract spirit, repeated recollection, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्यास, and योग religious exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासादन|अभ्यासादनं
अभ्यासादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Striking so as to disable an enemy.<BR>2 Facing an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and आङ् before सद to go, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासिन्
अभ्यासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Practising, exercising, repeating.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्यास and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार|अभ्याहारः
अभ्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Robbery. See अभिहार.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and आङ् before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार्य्य|अभ्याहार्य
अभ्याहार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>An eatable.<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Eatable, to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and आहार्य्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षण|अभ्युक्षणं
अभ्युक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उक्ष to moisten, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्ष्य
अभ्युक्ष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उक्ष to moisten, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थान|अभ्युत्थानं
अभ्युत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Fame, reputation.<BR>2 Rising from off a seat, &c. Rise.<BR>3 Elevation.<BR>4 Sun-rise.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उत् before स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थित
अभ्युत्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Risen, arisen.<BR>2 Elevated, exalted.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उत्थित lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Prosperity, increase.<BR>2 Accident, occurrence.<BR>3 A festival, any religious celebration.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उदय rise, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरण|अभ्युदाहरणं
अभ्युदाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An example or illustration of a thing by its reverse.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उदाहरण example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
अभ्युदित<BR>m. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Asleep at sun-rise.<BR>2 Celebrated as a festival.<BR>3 Risen, (as the sun.)<BR>4 Elevated, exalted.<BR>5 Arisen, happened.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, उत् up, and इत gone; part. past. of इण to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदीरित
अभ्युदीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrown over or upon.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उत् before ईरित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यत
अभ्युद्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought or given unsolicited.<BR>E.<BR>अभि towards, उद्यत exerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्धृत
अभ्युद्धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken up, delivered.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उद्धृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगत|अभ्युपगतः
अभ्युपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed, assented.<BR>2 Gone near to, approached, arrived at.<BR>3 Inferred, probable.<BR>4 Similar, analogous.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, उप over, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम|अभ्युपगमः
अभ्युपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A promise, an agreement, a contract.<BR>2 Approaching, going near to.<BR>3 Probable ascertainment.<BR>4 Analogy, affinity.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप implying association or vicinity, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमित|अभ्युपगमितः
अभ्युपगमित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A slave for a fixed term.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Obtained by assent or free will.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्युपगम and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्ति|अभ्युपपत्तिः
अभ्युपपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Favour, affection.<BR>2 Defence, protection.<BR>3 Agreement, assent.<BR>4 Impregnation of a woman, as of a brother's widow, as an act of duty.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप before पत to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपन्न
अभ्युपपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Agreeing to.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप before पद to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाय|अभ्युपायः
अभ्युपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An agreement, a promise, an engagement.<BR>2 A means, an expedient.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप before इण to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=058" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायन|अभ्युपायनं
अभ्युपायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bribe, an inducement.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप before इण to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत|अभ्युपेतं
अभ्युपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Contracted, promised, agreed.<BR>2 Approached.<BR>E.<BR>अभि and उप before इण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत्याशुश्रूषा
अभ्युपेत्याशुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A head or title of law, disputes between master and servant.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्युपेत्य having engaged, अ neg. शुषूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युष|अभ्युषः
अभ्युष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Grain, &c. half dressed, slightly scorched, or parched so as to be eaten from the hand.<BR>2 Bread.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before, उष to burn, क affix; the vowel may be made also long, which gives अभ्यूष, or may be changed to ओ, and form अभ्योष; some consider the root to be ऊष, to be sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषित|अभ्युषितः
अभ्युषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dwelling with.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before वस to dwell, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युह
अभ्युह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Discussion, reasoning.<BR>2 Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, and उह to reason, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युह्य
अभ्युह्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having concluded or inferred, having reasoned.<BR>2 Having supplied as an ellipsis.<BR>E.<BR>अभि, उह to reason, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूष|अभ्यूषः
अभ्यूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>See अभ्युष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योष|अभ्योषः
अभ्योष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>See अभ्युष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र<BR>r. 1st cl. (अभ्रति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Wind.<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Cloud-touching, cloud-sweeping.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud, लिह to lick, खश aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र|अभ्रं
अभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>1 The sky or atmosphere.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>4 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र to go, or अप् water, and भृ to have, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रक|अभ्रकं
अभ्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The mineral substance called talc.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र the same, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रङ्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र the sky, कष to plough, and खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाच|अभ्रपिशाचः
अभ्रपिशाच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A name of RĀHU, the descending node personified.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र the sky, and पिशाच a goblin; from the mischief he does to the moon, as the cause of its eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपिशाचक|अभ्रपिशाचकः
अभ्रपिशाचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रपुष्प|अभ्रपुष्पं|अभ्रपुष्पः
अभ्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A kind of tree or cane. See वेतस.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud and पुष्प a flower; flowering in the cloudy or rainy season.<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>as before; put forth as a flower from the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम|अभ्रमः
अभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Steadiness, composure.<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Steady, clear, not blundering.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भ्रम confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमातङ्ग|अभ्रमातंग|अभ्रमातङ्गः
अभ्रमातङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud, and मातङ्ग an elephant. The cloud-elephant, or that of the cloud-compelling king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमाला
अभ्रमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A line or succession of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमु|अभ्रमुः
अभ्रमु<BR>f. (-मुः)<BR>The female elephant of the east.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भ्रम to wander, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुप्रिय|अभ्रमुप्रियः
अभ्रमुप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The male elephant of the east, also INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्रमु, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुवल्लभ|अभ्रमुवल्लभः
अभ्रमुवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्रमु, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ररोह|अभ्ररोहं
अभ्ररोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud, रोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृक
अभ्रातृक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>Brotherless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भ्रातृ a brother, कन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्त|अभ्रांत|अभ्रान्तः
अभ्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Clear, composed, unperplexed, not mistaken or in error.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भ्रान्त misled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रान्ति|अभ्रांतिः|अभ्रान्तिः
अभ्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Absence of perplexity or error.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. भ्रान्ति error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाश|अभ्रावकाशः
अभ्रावकाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Fall of rain.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र cloud, अवकाश occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रावकाशिक
अभ्रावकाशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Exposed to the rain.<BR>E.<BR>अभावकाश and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रि|अभ्रिः
अभ्रि<BR>f. (-भ्रिः)<BR>A wooden scraper or shovel for cleaning a boat.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र to go, and इन् affix, also अभ्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिय|अभ्रियः
अभ्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to or produced from clouds.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud, and इय affix, or technically घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रेष|अभ्रेषः
अभ्रेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Fitness, propriety.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and भ्रेष impropriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रोत्थ|अभ्रोत्थं|अभ्रोत्थः
अभ्रोत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>INDRA'S thunder-bolt.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्र a cloud, उत् before स्था to stand, to rise up, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम<BR>r. 1st cl. (अमति)<BR>1 To go, to go to or towards.<BR>2 To serve or honour.<BR>3 To sound.<BR>10th cl. (अमयति)<BR>To afflict with sickness or pain from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम<BR>ind. (-अम्)<BR>1 Quickly.<BR>2 Little.<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Unripe, (as fruit, &c.)<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Sickness.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go or to be sick. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल|अमंगल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
अमङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Inauspicious, unlucky, evil.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Inauspiciousness, ill luck.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The castor oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मङ्गल auspicious: the wood has no sap, and is useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमङ्गल्य|अमंगल्य|अमङ्गल्यः
अमङ्गल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Inauspicious, unlucky, productive of evil.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मङ्गल्य auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्ड|अमंड|अमण्डः
अमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The castor oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मडि to adorn, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमण्डित
अमण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unadorned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मण्डित adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत|अमतः
अमत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 Time.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, and अतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अमति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A cheat, a rogue.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Unconsciousness, ignorance, absence of knowledge or intention.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and अति Uṇādi affix, or अ neg. मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिपूर्व्व|अमतिपूर्व
अमतिपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Unconscious, unintentional.<BR>E.<BR>अमति ignorance, पूर्व्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्त
अमत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Sober, not inebriated.<BR>2 Sane, not mad.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मत्त crazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
अमत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel, a utensil.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, अत्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्सर|अमत्सरः
अमत्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unenvious, charitable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मत्सर envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनि|अमनिः
अमनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्तव्य
अमन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Not to be regarded, inadmissible, unknowable. Also अमननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं).<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्तव्य or मननीय to be regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अमनुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Unmanly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनुष्य a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्यन्ता
अमनुष्यन्ता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unmanliness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last: also with त्व, अप्तनुष्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोगत
अमनोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unthought of, unknown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनोगत thought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोज्ञ
अमनोज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Disagreeable, disliked.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनोज्ञ agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=059" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोनीत
अमनोनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Disapproved.<BR>2 Reprobate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनस् the mind, नीत led.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोग|अमनोयोगः
अमनोयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Inattention.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनोयोग attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोयोगिन्
अमनोयोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Inattentive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनोयोगिन् attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनोहर
अमनोहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Disagreeable, displeasing, unattractive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनोहर pleasant. So अमनोरम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) and अमनोहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्र|अमंत्र
अमन्त्र<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>Unentitled to, or unaccompanied by holy texts, as a Śūdra, a female, certain ceremonies, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्त्र a text of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्त्रक|अमंत्रक
अमन्त्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unentitled to, or unaccompanied by holy texts.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्त्र a text, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्द|अमंद|अमन्दः
अमन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A tree. (E. अम sickness, and द from दो to cut, or destroy.)<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>1 Fierce, violent.<BR>2 Active.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्द tardy or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>One of the Jaina saints of a future age.<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Devoid of all selfish or worldly attachment or desire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मम mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममता
अममता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Disinterestedness, indifference.<BR>E.<BR>अमम and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममत्व|अममत्वं
अममत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Disinterestedness, philosophy, stoicism.<BR>E.<BR>अमम and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A deity, an immortal.<BR>2 A plant, (Heliotropium indicum.) See अस्थिसंहार.<BR>3 Also, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.)<BR>4 Quicksilver.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The residence of INDRA.<BR>2 A house post.<BR>3 The womb.<BR>4 The umbilical cord.<BR>5 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.) See गुडूची.<BR>6 Bent grass, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Immortal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मर what dies, from मृ and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणीय
अमरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>What cannot die, immortal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मरणीय perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणीयता
अमरणीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Immortality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also अमरणीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरता
अमरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Immortality.<BR>E.<BR>अमर and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरत्व|अमरत्वं
अमरत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Immortality.<BR>E.<BR>अमर and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरदारु|अमरदारुः
अमरदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>Name of a tree, (Pinus longifolius.)<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and दारु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरद्विज|अमरद्विजः
अमरद्विज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Brahman who lives by attending a temple or idol.<BR>E.<BR>अमर a god, and द्विज a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपति|अमरपतिः
अमरपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and पति lord; also similar compounds, as अमराधिपतिः, अमरेशः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपुष्प|अमरपुष्पः
अमरपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and पुष्प a flower; also with कन् added, अमरपुष्पकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरपुष्पिका
अमरपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of anise, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>अमर perpetual, and पुष्पिका having flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरभर्तृ|अमरभर्त्तृ
अमरभर्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and भर्तृ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोक|अमरलोकः
अमरलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Heaven, the abode of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरलोकता
अमरलोकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Heaven.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अमरलोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरस्त्री
अमरस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>An Apsarā, or nymph of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and स्त्री a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमराङ्गना
अमराङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and अङ्गना a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमराद्रि|अमराद्रिः
अमराद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>Mount Sumeru or Meru.<BR>E.<BR>अमर a deity, and अद्रि a mountain; being the residence of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरापगा
अमरापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The heavenly Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and अपगा river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The capital of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अमर a deity, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुत
अमरुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Calm, without wind.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मरुत wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरेश|अमरेशः
अमरेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>INDRA the king of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरेश्वर|अमरेश्वरः
अमरेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अमर, and ईश्वर chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अमर्त्य<BR>m. (-र्त्यः)<BR>A deity.<BR>mfn. (-र्त्यः-र्त्या-र्त्यं)<BR>Immortal, divine.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मृ to die, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्यभुवन|अमर्त्यभुवनं
अमर्त्यभुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The heaven of INDRA, or Svarga, a kind of Mohammedan paradise.<BR>E.<BR>अमर्त्य a deity, and भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्द्दित|अमर्दित
अमर्द्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unthreshed, unsubdued, not trodden down.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मर्द्दित trampled on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्य्यादा|अमर्यादा
अमर्य्यादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Impropriety of conduct.<BR>2 Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मर्य्यादा limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अमर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Anger, passion.<BR>2 Impatience, impetuosity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मृष to bear with, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अमर्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Passionate, wrathful.<BR>E.<BR>as before, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षवत्
अमर्षवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Hasty, impetuous, impatient.<BR>2 Wrathful, passionate.<BR>E.<BR>अमर्ष and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षिन्
अमर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-षिणी-र्षि)<BR>1 Passionate, wrathful.<BR>2 Impetuous.<BR>E.<BR>अमर्ष and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Talc.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMI.<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>3 The umbilical cord.<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Clean, pure.<BR>2 White.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलपतत्रिन्
अमलपतत्रिन्<BR>mf. (-त्री-त्रिणी)<BR>The wild goose.<BR>E.<BR>अमल white or grey, and पतत्रिन् a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अमलिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Clean, pure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मलिन dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस|अमसः
अमस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 Stupidity.<BR>3 Disease.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, or be sick, and अस Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसृण
अमसृण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Harsh, hard.<BR>2 Violent, intense.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मसृण soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तक
अमस्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Headless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मस्तक the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांस|अमांसः
अमांस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Feeble, thin.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मांस flesh. Also अमांसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा<BR>ind.<BR>1 With, together with.<BR>2 Near.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Day of conjunction or new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. माङ् to measure, क्विप् affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृक
अमातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Motherless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मातृ a mother, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्य|अमात्यः
अमात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A minister, a counsellor.<BR>E.<BR>अमा near, त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्र|अमात्रः
अमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>1 Not whole or entire.<BR>2 Not elementary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मात्र whole, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रवत्त्व
अमात्रवत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>1 Spirit, spiritual essence.<BR>2 Deficiency, defect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मात्रवत् like elementary, त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानन|अमाननं
अमानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन to mind, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानव
अमानव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Not human, animal.<BR>2 Superhuman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मानव mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानस्य|अमानस्यं
अमानस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Pain. See आमनस्य.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मनस् the mind, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=060" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिता
अमानिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Modesty, humility.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अमानिन्, also with त्व, अमानित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Humble, modest.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मान pride, इनि affix. Also अमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अमानुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Not human, animal, superhuman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मानुष human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्य
अमानुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्यी-ष्यं)<BR>Superhuman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मानुष्य human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमान्य|अमान्यः
अमान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>To be disrespected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मान्य to be respected. Also अमाननीय and अमानितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामसी
अमामसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमा with, मस to measure, अच् affix, and ङीप् fem. do or with घञ् affix; अमामासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसी
अमावसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमा with, and वस to abide, अच् affix; being with, or in the same quarter as the sun; also अमावासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्य
अमावास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Produced in the day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमावास्या and अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्यक
अमावास्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Produced on the day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमावास्या and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्या
अमावास्या<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Day of conjunction or new moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमा with, (the sun and moon,) वस to abide, ण्यत् affix: or with the penult. vowel short, अमावस्या; also अमावसी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अमाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 True, wise.<BR>2 Sincere, guileless, free from error or deceit.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Absence of delusion, knowledge of the truth.<BR>2 Sincerity, honesty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. माया deceit, delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिक|अमायिकः
अमायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>True, real, honest, void of trick or guile.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मायिक deceptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिन्
अमायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यी)<BR>Acting without illusion or deceit.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मायिन् deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ग|अमार्गः
अमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Want of a road.<BR>mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>Without a road.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्गित
अमार्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unsought, not hunted after.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मार्गित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ज्जित|अमार्जित
अमार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uncleansed.<BR>2 Unadorned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मार्ज्जित cleaned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unmeasured, boundless, infinite.<BR>2 Neglected, unpolished, unclean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमितौजस्
अमितौजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Mighty, all-powerful, almighty.<BR>E.<BR>अमित boundless, ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्र|अमित्रः
अमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An enemy, an adversary.<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Unfriendly, hostile.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, and इत्र Uṇādi affix, or अ neg. and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन्
अमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>अम sickness, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्र
अमिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Unmixed, unmixing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मिश्र mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रणीय
अमिश्रणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यां-यं)<BR>Immiscible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मिश्रणीय to be mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रित
अमिश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unmixed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मिश्रित mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Luxury.<BR>2 Honesty, simplicity.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, इषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीमांसा
अमीमांसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Absence of reasoning or investigation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मीमांसा investigation by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीव|अमीवं|अमीवः
अमीव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A certain person or thing, any thing or person referred to without a name.<BR>E.<BR>अमु for अदस् this, and वज added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्त|अमुक्तं
अमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Not loosed, not let go.<BR>2 Not liberated from birth and death.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A weapon that is always grasped to be used, as a knife, &c. See मुक्तामुक्त, यन्त्रामुक्त, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तहस्त
अमुक्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Sparing, frugal, prudent.<BR>E.<BR>अमुक्त not loosed, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्ति|अमुक्तिः
अमुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Confinement, want of freedom or liberty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मुक्ति liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुख्य
अमुख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Inferior, ordinary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मुख्य principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतस्
अमुतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Hence, from this.<BR>E.<BR>अमु for अदस् and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र<BR>ind.<BR>In the next life.<BR>E.<BR>अमु from अदस् this or that, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रत्य
अमुत्रत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Belonging to a future state, being of the next world.<BR>E.<BR>अमुत्र and त्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यपुत्र|अमुष्यपुत्रः
अमुष्यपुत्र<BR>mf. (-त्रः-त्री)<BR>1 Of a good family, of known origin.<BR>2 The son or daughter of such a one.<BR>E.<BR>अमुष्य the irr. gen. of अदस् this, and पुत्र a son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्यायण
अमुष्यायण<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>1 Of respectable birth, of known origin.<BR>2 The offspring of such a one, of a certain person, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अमुष्य as in the last, and फक् affix, also आमुष्यायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश्
अमूदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Of such form or kind.<BR>E.<BR>अमू for अदस् this, and क्किप् affix; also अमूदृश and अमूदृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश|अमूदृशः
अमूदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Of such a form or kind.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृक्ष
अमूदृक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Such, like, of such form or kind.<BR>E.<BR>see अमूदृश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Formless, shapeless, unembodied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मूर्त्ति form; the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त्ति|अमूर्ति|अमूर्तिः
अमूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Shapelessness, absence of shape or form.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having no root. Also अमूलक<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant. See अग्निशिखा.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Invaluable, not to be purchased.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणाल|अमृणालं
अमृणाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, used in India for taties or screens against the hot winds, commonly called Kas kas, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>अ like, as it were, and मृणाल a fibrous root; also मृणाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The food of the gods, Ambrosia or Nectar.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Butter, rice, &c. the residue of a sacrifice.<BR>4 Oiled butter or ghee.<BR>5 Unsolicited alms.<BR>6 Boiled rice.<BR>7 Food.<BR>8 Wealth, property.<BR>9 Gold.<BR>10 Buttermilk.<BR>11 Any thing sweet, a sweetmeat.<BR>12 Milk.<BR>13 Poison.<BR>14 A drug or medicament.<BR>15 Quicksilver.<BR>16 Final emancipation.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A god, an immortal.<BR>2 DHANVANTARI, the physician of the gods.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>2 The yellow sort, (Terminalia citrina.)<BR>3 Another plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>4 Long pepper.<BR>5 Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>6 Spirituous liquor. It also occurs amongst the synonyms of several plants besides those enumerated.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Beloved, desired.<BR>2 Beautiful.<BR>3 Immortal, imperishable. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=62" target="_blank">Page62</a>]<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मृङ to die, and क्त affix; what is immortal, or what makes so; what supports life, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=061" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतकुण्ड
अमृतकुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A vessel of nectar.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत and कुण्ड a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतता
अमृतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Immortality.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत and तल् affix; also with त्व, अमृतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृततरङ्गिणी|अमृततरंगिणी
अमृततरङ्गिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and तरङ्गिणी a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतदीधिति|अमृतदीधितिः
अमृतदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत ambrosia, and दीधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतद्रव|अमृतद्रवः
अमृतद्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Shedding ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and द्रव dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतधार
अमृतधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Shedding or distilling ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and धारा a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतप|अमृतपः
अमृतप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Drinking ambrosia.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतरस|अमृतरसः
अमृतरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Nectar, ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतवर्ष
अमृतवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A fall of ambrosia from heaven.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतवल्ली
अमृतवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A species of moonseed, (Menispermum glabrum.) See गुडूची.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and वल्ली a pedicle; the plant flourishing for a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसारज|अमृतसारजः
अमृतसारज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Raw sugar, molasses.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत ambrosia, सार essence, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसू
अमृतसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>The moon, as the producer of ambrosia.<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A Mātṛ or a divine mother.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत the ambrosia, and सू who brings forth; from सूड् to bear, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतस्रुत्
अमृतस्रुत्<BR>mfn. (-स्रुत्)<BR>Shedding ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, स्रु to distil, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतसोदर|अमृतसोदरः
अमृतसोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and सोदर brother: born with nectar at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतान्धस्
अमृतान्धस्<BR>m. (-न्धाः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and अन्धस् food; whose food is ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताफल|अमृताफलं|अमृताफलः
अमृताफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The fruit of the Trichosanthes.<BR>E.<BR>अमृता, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताशन|अमृताशनः
अमृताशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>as before, अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतासङ्ग|अमृतासङ्गं|अमृतासङ्गः
अमृतासङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A collyrium, extracted from the Amomum anthoriza. See कर्परी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताहरण|अमृताहरणः
अमृताहरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, हृ to convey, with आङ् prefixed, and ल्युट् affix; GARUḌA having upon one occasion stolen the Amṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतोत्पन्ना
अमृतोत्पन्ना<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>A fly.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतोद्भव|अमृतोद्भवं
अमृतोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A kind of collyrium. See अमृतासङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>अमृत, and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्ति
अमृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>A drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्यु|अमृत्युः
अमृत्यु<BR>f. (-त्युः)<BR>Immortality.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेघ
अमेघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Cloudless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मेघ a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेधस्
अमेधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>A fool, an idiot.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मेध to understand, and अमुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अमेध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Impure, foul.<BR>n. (-ध्यंः)<BR>Faeces, excrement.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and मेध्य pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यत्व
अमेध्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Foulness, filthiness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अमेध्य, also with तल, अमेध्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्ययुक्त
अमेध्ययुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Filthy, foul.<BR>E.<BR>अमेध्य, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलिप्त
अमेध्यलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Smeared with ordure, foul, defiled.<BR>E.<BR>अमेध्य, and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्यलेप|अमेध्यलेपः
अमेध्यलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Smearing with ordure.<BR>E.<BR>अमेध्य, and लेप plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्याक्त
अमेध्याक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Soiled by ordure.<BR>E.<BR>अमेध्य, and अक्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेय
अमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Immense, immeasurable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मेय to be measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेयात्मन्
अमेयात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Magnanimous, possessing extraordinary powers of mind.<BR>E.<BR>अमेय, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्ष|अमोक्षः
अमोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 Bondage, confinement.<BR>2 Confinement to life.<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Unliberated, unloosed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मोक्ष liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Productive, fruitful, not vain or barren.<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>1 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 A plant of which the seed is used as a vermifuge, (Erycibe paniculata, Rox.) See बिडङ्ग.<BR>3 Yellow myrobalan. See हरीतकी.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, मोघ vain, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचन|अमोचनं
अमोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Non-liberation, not loosing or letting go.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मोचन loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचित
अमोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Confined, not liberated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मोचित loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब|अंब|अंबः|अम्बः
अम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (अंबति)<BR>To move, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बक|अंबक|अंबकं|अम्बकं
अम्बक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Copper.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ब to go, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बर|अंबर|अंबरं|अम्बरं|अम्बरः
अम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The sky or atmosphere.<BR>2 Clothes, apparel.<BR>3 A perfume, (Ambergris.)<BR>4 Cotton.<BR>5 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ब to go, and अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरयुग
अम्बरयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The two principal female garments, or upper and lower cloths or mantles.<BR>E.<BR>अम्वर, and युगं a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरान्त|अंबरान्त|अम्बरान्तः
अम्बरान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The horizon.<BR>2 The end of a garment.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बर, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरिष|अम्बरिषं
अम्बरिष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>A frying pan. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बरीष|अंबरीष|अंबरीषं|अम्बरीषं|अम्बरीषः
अम्बरीष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>1 A frying pan.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Also of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A young animal, a colt, a boy.<BR>4 The name of a king of the solar race, celebrated as a worshipper of VIṢṆU.<BR>5 A division of hell.<BR>6 The sun.<BR>7 Repentance.<BR>8 A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>अबि to sound, and ईषन् Uṇādi affix, but irregularly formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अंबष्ठः|अम्बष्ठः
अम्बष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 The name of a country, stated to be in the eastern division of India, and supposed by Mr. WILFORD, to be the abode of the AMBASTOE of Arrian.<BR>2 The offspring of a man of the Brahman, and a woman of the Vaiśya tribe, a man of the medical cast.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 A sort of jasmin, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>2 A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.) See बनतिक्तिका.<BR>3 Woodsorrel, (Oxalis corniculata, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बा a mother, स्था to stand, and क affix, what cherishes-like a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बष्ठकी|अंबष्ठकी
अम्बष्ठकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A creeper, (Cissampelos hexandra.) Also अम्बष्ठा and अम्बष्ठिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बा|अंबा
अम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 The same, (in theatrical language.)<BR>3 A name of DURGĀ. See अम्बिका.<BR>E.<BR>अबि to sound, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बालिका|अंबालिका
अम्बालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 The mother of PĀṆḌU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिका|अंबिका
अम्बिका<BR>f. (का)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>3 The mother of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>4 One of the female domestic deities of the Jainas.<BR>5 A medicinal plant. See कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बा a mother, and कन् affix; like a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=062" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेय|अंबिकेय|अंबिकेयः|अम्बिकेयः
अम्बिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 GAṆEŚA, or KĀRTTIKEYA, both sons of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 A name of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बिका as above; and ढक affix, implying family decent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बिकेयक|अंबिकेयकः|अम्बिकेयकः
अम्बिकेयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बु|अंबु
अम्बु<BR>n. (-म्बु)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>अबि to sound, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकणा
अम्बुकणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकण्ठक
अम्बुकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The short-nosed alligator.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु water, and कण्ठक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकिरात|अम्बुकिरातः
अम्बुकिरात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An alligator.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and किरात a savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकीश|अम्बुकीशः
अम्बुकीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A porpoise, especially of the kind common in the Ganges, (Delphinus gangeticus, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and कीश, the water-monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुकूर्म्म|अम्बुकूर्म|अम्बुकूर्मः|अम्बुकूर्म्मः
अम्बुकूर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>A porpoise, especially the gangetic.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and कूर्म्म a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचर
अम्बुचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Aquatical.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and चर what moves in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचामर|अम्बुचामरं
अम्बुचामर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.) See शैवाल.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and चामर the Indian chowrie; the water-chowrie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुचारिन्
अम्बुचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Aquatical, as a fish, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुज|अम्बुजं|अम्बुजः
अम्बुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant, (Eugenia acutangula.) See हिज्जल.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A lotus, (Nymphaea nelumbo.)<BR>2 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatic, water-born.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and ज what is produced; water-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुजन्मन्
अम्बुजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and जन्म birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुताल|अम्बुतालः
अम्बुताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Vallisneria. See अम्बुचामर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुद|अम्बुदः
अम्बुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Shedding or giving water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुधि|अम्बुधिः
अम्बुधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and धि what possesses; from धाञ् with कि affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुनिधि|अम्बुनिधिः
अम्बुनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुप|अम्बुपः
अम्बुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia tora, or alata.)<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Drinking or imbibing water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and प what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुपत्रा
अम्बुपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A fragrant grass, (perhaps a Cyperus.) See उच्चटा.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुपद्धति|अम्बुपद्धतिः
अम्बुपद्धति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Current, stream, flow of water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and पद्धति distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुप्रसादन|अम्बुप्रसादनं
अम्बुप्रसादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The clearing nut tree, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु water, प्रसद to cleanse, घञ affix. The nuts of this plant are generally used in India, for purifying water: they are rubbed upon the inner surface of the vessel, and occasion the precipitation of the impurities of the fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुभृत्
अम्बुभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 A grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and भृत् what nourishes, from भृञ् with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमत्|अंबुमत्|अम्बुमन्त्
अम्बुमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The side of a river, or a bank, a shore.<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Watery, having or containing water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ब and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमात्रज|अम्बुमात्रजः
अम्बुमात्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु water, मात्र all, every kind, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुमुच्
अम्बुमुच्<BR>m. (-मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and मुच् what lets go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुर|अम्बुरः
अम्बुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The lower limb of a door frame, the threshold.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and राज to shine, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुराशि|अम्बुराशिः
अम्बुराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुरुह|अम्बुरुहः
अम्बुरुह<BR>m. (-रुहः)<BR>1 Any aquatic plant.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and रुह् what grows on or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुरोहिणी
अम्बुरोहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and रोहिन् what grows, or rises on or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाची
अम्बुवाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>Four days in Āṣārha, the 10th to the 13th of the dark fortnight, when the earth is supposed to be unclean, and agriculture is prohibited.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and वाच् speech, with ङीष added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवासी
अम्बुवासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवासिनी
अम्बुवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु before वस to abide, णिनि and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाह|अम्बुवाहः
अम्बुवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 The cyperus.<BR>3 A water carrier.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु water, and वाह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवाहिन्
अम्बुवाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Carrying or conveying water.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A wooden baling vessel.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, and वाहिन् what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुवेतस|अम्बुवेतसः
अम्बुवेतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A kind of cane or reed growing in water. See वेतस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुसर्पिणी
अम्बुसर्पिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु before सृप् to go, णिनि affix; and डीष् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असादन
असादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The nut of the Strychnos. See अम्बुप्रसादन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बुसेचनी
अम्बुसेचनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A vessel used for baling water out of a boat.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु, षिच् to sprinkle, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्बूकृत|अंबूकृत|अम्बूकृतं
अम्बूकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sputtered, (speech, discourse.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्बु water, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ब्ल|अम्ब्लः
अम्ब्ल<BR>m. (-म्ब्लः)<BR>Sourness.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ब to go, and क्ल Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्|अंभस्
अम्भस्<BR>n. (-म्भः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>अप् water, before असुन Uṇādi affix; नुम् is inserted, and प becomes भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्स्थ
अम्भस्स्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्स्थः-स्स्था-स्स्थं)<BR>1 What holds or contains water.<BR>2 Abiding in water.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस् and स्थ what abides or where it abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भस्सू
अम्भस्सू<BR>m. (-स्सूः)<BR>Smoke, cloudiness.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस् water, and सू what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोज|अम्भोजं|अम्भोजः
अम्भोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatic, water-born.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजजनि
अम्भोजजनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>BRAHMĀ, being born secondarily from a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भोज, and जनि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजयोनि|अम्भोजयोनिः
अम्भोजयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भोज, and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोजिनी|अंभोजिनी
अम्भोजिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers, or a place where they abound.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भोज a lotus, णिनि and डीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोद|अम्भोदः
अम्भोद<BR>m.<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधर|अम्भोधरः
अम्भोधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस् water, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोधि|अम्भोधिः
अम्भोधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and धि what possesses, from धा with the affix. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोनिधि|अम्भोनिधिः
अम्भोनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोराशि|अम्भोराशिः
अम्भोराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्भोरुह|अम्भोरुहं
अम्भोरुह<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस्, and रुह what rises or grows, from रुह with अच् affix; also with क्किप् affix. अम्भोरुह nom. (रुट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्मय|अम्मयं
अम्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Watery, formed from, or consisting of water, (as froth, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अप् water, and मयट् affix; म is changed to प, and the fem. takes ङीप्^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=063" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्र|अम्रः
अम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>n. (-म्रं)<BR>A mango.<BR>E.<BR>अम to eat, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रात|अम्रातः
अम्रात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A species of spondias or hog plum, (Spondias mangifera).<BR>E.<BR>अम्र the mango, and अत to go, अच् affix; resembling that fruit, also अम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रातक|अम्रातकः
अम्रातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ल|अम्लं|अम्लः
अम्ल<BR>mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं)<BR>Sour, acid.<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>Sourness, acidity.<BR>f. (-म्ली)<BR>Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sour curds.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, क्ल Uṇādi affix, and ङीप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लता
अम्लता<BR>f.<BR>Sourness.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल and तल् affix, also with त्व aff. अम्लत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लक|अम्लकः
अम्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Artocarpus lacucha.) See लकुच.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल sourness, and क affix; having a sour taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लकेशर|अम्लकेशरः
अम्लकेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The citron.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and केशर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लपनस|अम्लपनसः
अम्लपनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लपित्त
अम्लपित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Acidity of stomach.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and पित्त bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लफल|अम्लफलं|अम्लफलः
अम्लफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fruit.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लरस|अम्लरसः
अम्लरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Sour, having a sour taste.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Sourness, acidity.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोणिका
अम्ललोणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Wood sorrel, (Oxalis corniculata,) also अम्ललोणी and अम्ललोलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोणी
अम्ललोणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ललोलिका
अम्ललोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See अम्ललोणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवर्ग|अम्लवर्गः
अम्लवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A class of plants with acid leaves or fruit, as the lime, orange, pomegranate, tamarind, wood apple, sorrel, Lakucha, Spondias and others.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवाडव
अम्लवाडव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>See अम्रात above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवातक
अम्लवातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवेतस|अम्लवेतसः
अम्लवेतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A kind of dock or sorrel. (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल sour, and वेतस a kind of reed; sour grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवासुक
अम्लवासुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लवृक्ष|अम्लवृक्षं|अम्लवृक्षः
अम्लवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लशाक|अम्लशाकं|अम्लशाकः
अम्लशाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius,) commonly used as a potherb.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लसार|अम्लसारं|अम्लसारः
अम्लसार<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>Rice water after fermentation.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The lime.<BR>2 A sort of sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लाक्त
अम्लाक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Acidulated.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and अक्त mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लान|अम्लानः
अम्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Clean, clear.<BR>2 Bright, unclouded.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Globe amaranth, (Gomphrena globosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and म्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानि|अम्लानिः
अम्लानि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>1 Vigorous.<BR>2 Unfading.<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Vigour.<BR>2 Freshness, verdure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. म्लानि soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानिन्
अम्लानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Clean, clear.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. म्लानिन् soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिका
अम्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The tamarind tree.<BR>2 Wood sorrel, (Oxalis corniculata.)<BR>3 A sour taste in the mouth, acidity of stomach.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल sour, कन् and टाप् affixes; इ being substituted for अ; also अम्लीका and आम्लका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लीका
अम्लीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लोद्गार|अम्लोद्गारः
अम्लोद्गार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sour eructation.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल, and उद्गार bringing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय<BR>r. 1st cl. (अयते)<BR>To go, to go to or towards.<BR>With प्रति<BR>to believe, to rely on. A preposition containing र substitutes ल before this root, as प्र and पर make प्लायते, पलायते to fly, to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Good luck, favourable fortune.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, and अच् affix; happiness proceeding by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञ|अयज्ञः
अयज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Not offering sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञक
अयज्ञक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unfit for sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यज्ञक sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञिय
अयज्ञिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not sacrificial, common, profane.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यज्ञिय sacrificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयतिन्
अयतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Incontinent, of unsubdued appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यतिन् self-restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्न|अयत्नः
अयत्न<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>Absence of effort or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यत्व effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नकारिन्
अयत्नकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Idle, indifferent, making no exertion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यत्न effort, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नकृत
अयत्नकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spontaneous, readily or easily produced.<BR>E.<BR>अयत्न, and कृत done. So अयत्नभूत (-तः-ता-तं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्नवत्
अयत्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Idle, inactive, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यत्नघत् active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथा
अयथा<BR>ind.<BR>Unsuitably, unfitly, inconsistently, incongruously.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and यथा as, (it should be.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथातथ
अयथातथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Unprofitable, useless, vain.<BR>2 Unfit, unsuitable, incompatible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यथा as, तथा so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथातथ्य
अयथातथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Unprofitableness, unsuitableness, incompatibility.<BR>E.<BR>अयथातथ and ष्यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथार्थ
अयथार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Not according to the sense or object, incongruous, nonsensical, unmeaning.<BR>2 Improper, unfitting.<BR>3 False, untrue.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यथा as, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथावत्
अयथावत्<BR>ind.<BR>Inaccurately, erroneously.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यथा as, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथाबलम्
अयथाबलम्<BR>ind.<BR>Unsuitably, imperfectly.<BR>E.<BR>अयथा, and वल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथाशास्त्रकारिन्
अयथाशास्त्रकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Irreligious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यथा according to, शास्त्र scripture, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथेष्ट
अयथेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Insufficient, not enough.<BR>2 Disliked, disapproved of.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यथेष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A road, a path.<BR>2 The half year, that is, the sun's road north and south of the equator. See उत्तरायण, &c.<BR>3 The equinoctial and solstitial points.<BR>4 A Śāstra or inspired writing.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनकाल|अयनकालः
अयनकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The interval between the equinoxes.<BR>E.<BR>अयन, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनभाग|अयनभागः
अयनभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>See अयनांश.<BR>E.<BR>अयन, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयनांश|अयनांशः
अयनांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The arc between the vernal equinoctial point, and the beginning of the fixed zodiac or first point in Aries.<BR>E.<BR>अयन, and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन्त्रित|अयंत्रित|अयन्त्रितः
अयन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unrestrained, self-willed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यन्त्रित restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयवत्|अयवन्त्
अयवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Lucky, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>अय and मतुप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्
अयशस्<BR>mfn. (-शाः-शाः-शः)<BR>Infamous.<BR>n. (-शः)<BR>Infamy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=064" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्कर
अयशस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Disgraceful, degrading.<BR>E.<BR>अयशस् and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्य
अयशस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Infamous. So अयशस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि).<BR>E.<BR>अयशस् and य or विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्
अयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>Iron.<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>A name of VAHNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, and असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कान्त|अयस्कान्तः
अयस्कान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A precious stone, the loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>अयस् and कान्त beautiful, implying a gem, after this word and others, as सूर्य्यकान्त, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कार
अयस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The upper part of the thigh.<BR>2 A blacksmith.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and कार an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्कुम्भ
अयस्कुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>An iron pot or boiler.<BR>E.<BR>अयस् and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचक|अयाचकः
अयाचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who does not ask or solicit.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. याचक who solicits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचित|अयाचितं|अयाचितः
अयाचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unasked, unsolicited.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint, also उपवर्ष.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and याचित asked, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाज्य
अयाज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Outcaste, degraded, not competent to offer sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. याज्य to be sacrificed; by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातपूर्व्व|अयातपूर्व
अयातपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-ब्वो-र्व्वं)<BR>Following, subsequent to, succeeding.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यातपूर्व्व preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थिक
अयाथार्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Improper, unjust.<BR>2 Absurd, incongruous.<BR>E.<BR>अयथार्थ and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थ्य|अयाथार्थ्यं
अयाथार्थ्य<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>1 Impropriety, unfitness.<BR>2 Absurdity, nonsense.<BR>E.<BR>अयथार्थ and य्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयान|अयानं
अयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Natural disposition or temperament.<BR>2 Halt, stop.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and या to go, ल्युट् affix; what never departs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानय|अयानयं|अयानयः
अयानय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानयीन|अयानयीनः
अयानयीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Produced in, or brought from Ayānaya.<BR>E.<BR>अयानय and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावक
अयावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unstained with lac-dye, naturally red.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. यावक of lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयि
अयि<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of encouragement, and asking; also a vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>इ to go, and इन् affix, by which one goes; what leads or calls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्च्छद
अयुक्च्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.) See सप्तपर्णः.<BR>E.<BR>अयुज् separate, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्त|अयुक्तं
अयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Separate, disjoined.<BR>2 Improper.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्ति|अयुक्तिः
अयुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Disunion, separation.<BR>2 Unreasonableness, want of conformity to correct principles or to analogy.<BR>3 Impropriety, unfitness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युक्ति union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग
अयुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Single, separate.<BR>2 Odd.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगपत्
अयुगपत्<BR>ind.<BR>Gradually, seriatim, not at once.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युगपत् at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगल
अयुगल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Single.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युगल a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगार्च्चिष्
अयुगार्च्चिष्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>अयुग uneven, (seven) अर्च्चिष् ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्म
अयुग्म<BR>mfn. (-ग्मः-ग्मा-ग्मं)<BR>1 Separate, divided, single.<BR>2 Odd, uneven.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, युग्म a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्मछद|अयुग्मच्छद|अयुग्मच्छदः
अयुग्मछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युग्म double, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अयुज्<BR>mfn. (-युक)<BR>1 Separate, single.<BR>2 Odd, uneven.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युज् what joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disjoined, detached.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Ten thousand.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and यत joined, counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Peace, absence of war.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये<BR>ind.<BR>Oh! ah! &c. an interjection of<BR>1 Recollection.<BR>2 Fatigue;<BR>3 Fear;<BR>4 Passion; and<BR>5 Calling.<BR>E.<BR>इ to go, एच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Separation, disjunction.<BR>2 A widower, an absent lover or husband.<BR>3 Unfitness, unsuitableness.<BR>4 Medical treatment, counter to the symptoms.<BR>5 Consistent treatment, non-mixture of opposite qualities.<BR>6 Dislike, aversion to any thing.<BR>7 Vigorous effort, exertion.<BR>8 An iron hammer.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and योग union; or अयस् iron, and ग what goes, or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगव|अयोगवः
अयोगव<BR>mf. (-वः-वा-वी)<BR>The offspring of a Śūdra man, and Vaiśya woman.<BR>E.<BR>अयोग disjoined, and व from बा to go; being one of the lowest castes or tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगुड|अयोगुडः
अयोगुड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A chalybeate pill, one made of some preparation of iron.<BR>2 An iron ball.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and गुड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्य
अयोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>1 Unfit, unsuitable.<BR>2 Useless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. योग्य fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्यता
अयोग्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Unfitness, unsuitableness, incongruity, impropriety. अयोग्य and तल् affix; also अयोग्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्र|अयोग्रं
अयोग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>1 A pestle for cleaning grain.<BR>2 A mace of club tipped with iron.<BR>3 A hammer, a forge hammer.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and अग्र the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोघन|अयोघनः
अयोघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A hammer, a forge hammer.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and घन what strikes, from हन् to kill or strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजन
अयोजन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Disunion, separation, distinctness.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, योजन uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोदत्
अयोदत्<BR>mfn. (-दत्-दती-दत्)<BR>Iron-toothed.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्य
अयोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Not to be warred against.<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>The capital of RĀMA, Ayodhya, the modern Oude.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. युद्ध to make war, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिज|अयोनिजः
अयोनिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Generated equivocally, not born from the womb.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. योनि the womb, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमय
अयोमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of iron.<BR>E.<BR>अयस् and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमल|अयोमलं
अयोमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Rust of iron.<BR>E.<BR>अयस, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमुख|अयोमुखः
अयोमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Tipped or pointed with iron.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A kind of goblin with an iron face.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and मुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोहृदय
अयोहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Stern, unrelenting, iron-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>अयस्, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Swift, speedy.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The spoke or radius of a wheel.<BR>adv.<BR>Swiftly.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A Jaina division of time, the sixth of an Avasarpiṇī or Utsarpiṇī. See अवसर्पिणी, &c.<BR>2 The eighteenth Jaina Tīrthakara, or deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक|अरकः
अरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.) See शैवाल.<BR>E.<BR>अर what goes, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षित
अरक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not preserved, not kept.<BR>3 Unprotected, undefended.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रक्षित kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरग्वघ
अरग्वघ<BR>m. (घः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.) See आरग्वघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघट्ट|अरघट्टः
अरघट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 A machine for raising water from a well.<BR>2 A deep well.<BR>E.<BR>अर quickly, and घट्ट to move, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरघदृक
अरघदृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wheel for drawing water with.<BR>2 A deep or large well.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=065" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरङ्गर|अरंगर|अरंगरः
अरङ्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Factitious or made up poison.<BR>E.<BR>अरम् quick, and गर poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अरजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>1 Free from the quality of passion.<BR>2 Free from desire, &c.<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A young girl.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रजस् the menstrual flux, or passion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरटु|अरटुः
अरटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.) See अरलु.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणि|अरणिः
अरणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णी)<BR>Wood used for kindling a fire, exciting it by attrition.<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 The plant of which especially the wood is used for this purpose, (Premna spinosa, &c). See गणिकारिका.<BR>2 A flint.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्य|अरण्यं|अरण्यः
अरण्य<BR>nf. (-ण्यः-णी)<BR>A forest.<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>Kayaphal, a drug so named. See कट्फल.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and अन्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकदली
अरण्यकदली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The wood or wild plantain.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and कदली the plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकार्प्पासी|अरण्यकार्पासी
अरण्यकार्प्पासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and कार्प्पासी cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यचटक|अरण्यचटकः
अरण्यचटक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A wood sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यज
अरण्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced or born in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and ज born; also similar compounds, as अरण्यजात, अरण्योत्पन्न, अरण्यभव, अरण्यसम्भव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यजार्द्रका
अरण्यजार्द्रका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Wild ginger.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्यज, and आर्द्रका ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यधान्य|अरण्यधान्यं
अरण्यधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Wild rice.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यमक्षिका
अरण्यमक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The gad fly.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यरक्षक|अरण्यरक्षकः
अरण्यरक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Keeper of a forest, superintendent of a forest district.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and रक्षक who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवायस|अरण्यवायसः
अरण्यवायस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and वायस a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवास|अरण्यवासः
अरण्यवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A hermitage.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य a wood, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यवासिन्
अरण्यवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A hermit, an anchorite.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and वासिन who resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यशालि|अरण्यशालिः
अरण्यशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Wild rice.<BR>E.<BR>अरेण्य, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यशूकर
अरण्यशूकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The wild hog.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and शूकर a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यश्वन्
अरण्यश्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा)<BR>A wolf.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and श्वन् a dog, the forest dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्याध्यक्ष|अरण्याध्यक्षः
अरण्याध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Keeper or ranger of the forests, a headman or superintendent of a forest district, an officer in the old Hindu government.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A large forest.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य, आनुक and ङीष aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dull, languid, apathetic.<BR>2 Disgusted, discontented.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रत interested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरतत्रप|अरतत्रपः
अरतत्रप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रत copulation, and त्रप ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Dull, languid.<BR>2 Discontented, unhappy.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Anger, passion.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Dissatisfaction, discontent.<BR>2 Dulness, languor.<BR>3 Absence of pleasure, pain.<BR>4 Anxiety, distress.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and रति pleasure, or ऋ to go, and अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्नि|अरत्निः
अरत्नि<BR>m. (-त्निः)<BR>1 A cubit of the middle length, from the elbow to the tip of the little finger.<BR>2 The elbow.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and कत्नि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम|अरमः
अरम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Low, inferior. See अवम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम्य
अरम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Disagreeable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रम्य pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर|अररं|अररः
अरर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 A door.<BR>2 A covering, a sheathe.<BR>3 The sheathe of the shoot of a bamboo.<BR>E.<BR>अर, from ऋ to go, and अरण Uṇādi affix, ङीष् in the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररि|अररिः
अररि<BR>mn. (-रिः-रि)<BR>A door.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and अरिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररु|अररुः
अररु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, अरु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररे
अररे<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle, expressing haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरलु|अरलुः
अरलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.) See शोनाक.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, अरु affix, and र is changed to ल, also अरटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरव
अरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Silent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्द|अरविंदं|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>1 A lotus, (Nymphaea nelumbo.)<BR>2 Copper.<BR>E.<BR>अर quickly, and विन्द to obtain, श affix; with reference to the lotus, as of quick growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दनाभि|अरविन्दनाभिः
अरविन्दनाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अरविन्द, and नाभि the navel, from which sprung the lotus that bore BRAHMĀ at the creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविन्दिनी|अरविंदिनी
अरविन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>अरविन्द, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Insipid, tasteless.<BR>2 Dull, flat, (as a composition.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अरसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Unfeeling, dull, devoid of taste.<BR>2 Flavourless, insipid, liter. or fig.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रसिक flavoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहित
अरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having, possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रहित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Cool, unimpassioned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिन्
अरागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Cool, unimpassioned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रागिन् impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Anarchical, having no king or governor.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. राजन् a king, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराति|अरातिः
अराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and रा to give, with ति affix; who does not give pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिभङ्ग|अरातिभंग|अरातिभङ्गः
अरातिभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>Defeat or destruction of a foe.<BR>E.<BR>अराति, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Crooked.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Resin.<BR>2 An elephant in rut.<BR>3 A bent or crooked, arm.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A modest woman.<BR>2 A disloyal or unchaste one.<BR>E.<BR>अर what goes, आ before ला to take or give, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 A wheel.<BR>3 A species of Khadira or Mimosa.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, अच् affix, and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिकुल
अरिकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Family of an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and कुल family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Not entitled to a share of the property, a non-heir.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रिक्थभाज a co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिता
अरिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Enmity, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>अरि and तल् affix, also with त्व, अरित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A rudder.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिनन्दन
अरिनन्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Gratifying an enemy, affording triumph to an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and नन्दन what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिन्दम|अरिंदम|अरिन्दमः
अरिन्दम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Conquering, victorious.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and दम to tame, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिपुर
अरिपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An enemy's town or country.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमित्र
अरिमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An ally or friend of an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिमेद|अरिमेदः
अरिमेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A fetid Mimosa, (M. Farnesiana.)<BR>E.<BR>अरि an enemy, and मेद what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=066" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिराष्ट्र
अरिराष्ट्र<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रंः)<BR>An enemy's country.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and राष्ट्र a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिलोक
अरिलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hostile tribe or an enemy's country.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and लोक a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष|अरिषं|अरिषः
अरिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Disease arising from meat and drink.<BR>2 A stream of water from the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria, &c.)<BR>2 Garlick.<BR>3 The Nimb tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR>4 A crow.<BR>5 A heron.<BR>6 The name of an Asura or infernal spirit.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 A woman's apartment, the lying-in chamber.<BR>2 Good fortune, happiness.<BR>3 Bad or ill luck, misfortune.<BR>4 Buttermilk.<BR>5 Vinous spirit.<BR>6 Sign or symptom of approaching death.<BR>7 A portent, some natural phenomenon considered as indicating calamity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and रिष्ट bad or good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टक|अरिष्टकः
अरिष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and रिष्ट affliction, क affix; relieving sickness, &c. See the preceding, of which it may have all the meanings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टताति|अरिष्टतातिः
अरिष्टताति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Auspicious, making fortunate or happy.<BR>E.<BR>अरिष्ट, तन to spread, and डाति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टदुष्टधी
अरिष्टदुष्टधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Apprehensive of death, alarmed at its approach.<BR>E.<BR>अरिष्ट sign of death, टुष्ठ disturbed, and धी understanding, mind; whose is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टनेमि|अरिष्टनेमिः
अरिष्टनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The twenty-second of the twenty-four Jaina Tīrthakaras or saints. Also नेमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टसूदन|अरिष्टसूदनः
अरिष्टसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अरिष्ट the Asura so named, and सूदन who destroys; having killed the demon ARIṢṬA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टानक
अरिष्टानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Consternation, defeat.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and स्थानक being in place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिहंसक
अरिहंसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An avenger.<BR>E.<BR>अरि, and हिंसक who injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुग्न
अरुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Healthy, well.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुग्न sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचि|अरुचिः
अरुचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>1 Aversion, dislike.<BR>2 Want of appetite, disrelish, disgust.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुचि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिर
अरुचिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Disagreeable, disgusting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुचिर agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्य
अरुच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Disagreeable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुच्य to be liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज्
अरुज्<BR>mfn. (-रुक् or -रुग्)<BR>Sound, healthy, free from disease.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुज् sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of the sun.<BR>2 Also of his charioteer, or the dawn personified as the son of KAŚYAPA by VINATĀ.<BR>3 The colour of the dawn, dark red, or the mixture of red and black.<BR>4 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>5 The redness of sun-set.<BR>6 A kind of leprosy, with red spots and insensibility of the skin.<BR>7 A dumb man.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 A plant, (Betula.) See अतिविषा.<BR>2 Madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>3 Another plant, commonly Tëori. See त्रिष्टत्.<BR>4 A black kind of the same.<BR>5 Colocynth or bitter apple.<BR>6 The plant that yields the red and black berry from which the jeweller's weight, the Ratti, is derived. See गुञ्जा.<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Tawny, dark red, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and उनन Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणकमल|अरुणकमलं
अरुणकमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and कमल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणलोचन|अरुणलोचनः
अरुणलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणसारथि|अरुणसारथिः
अरुणसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and सारथि a charioteer; whose charioteer is ARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणाग्रज|अरुणाग्रजः
अरुणाग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and अग्रज first born; having ARUṆA as his elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणात्मज|अरुणात्मजः
अरुणात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of JAṬĀYU, a fabulous bird: said by some to be the son of ARUṆA, but more generally of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and आत्मज the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणावरज|अरुणावरजः
अरुणावरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, अवर after, and ज born; the younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणित
अरुणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reddened.<BR>2 Dyed red, impurpled.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणिमन्
अरुणिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Redness.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणीकृत
अरुणीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reddened, turning or become red.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण, and कृत made, च्ची augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोदय|अरुणोदयः
अरुणोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Break of day, dawn, the period preceding sunset.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण dawn, उदय rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणोपल|अरुणोपलः
अरुणोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>अरुण dark red, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुदित
अरुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unwept, unlamented.<BR>2 Not weeping.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुदित wept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुद्ध
अरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Free, unobstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुद|अरुंतुद|अरुन्तुदः
अरुन्तुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Sharp, corrosive.<BR>2 Acrimonious, sharp, sour. (as disposition.)<BR>E.<BR>अरुस् a sore, and तुद what torments, from तुद and खश affix; the final of अरुस् is dropped, and नुम inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्तुदत्व
अरुन्तुदत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Infliction of pain.<BR>2 Acrimoniousness, causticity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last. Also अरुन्तुदता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धती|अरुंधती
अरुन्धती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The daughter of KĀRDDAMA and wife of VASIṢṬHA, one of the seven Ṛṣis; she is also one of the Pleiades.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुध to confine, तन् and ङीप् affixes; who does not confine or hinder good works. ARUNDHATĪ is considered as a pattern of conjugal excellence, and is invoked at the marriage ceremony by the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीजानि|अरुन्धतीजानिः
अरुन्धतीजानि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>VAŚIṢṬHA, one of the seven Ṛṣis or saints, and stars in the great bear.<BR>E.<BR>अरुन्धती and जानि from जाया a wife; whose wife is ARUNDHATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुन्धतीनाथ|अरुन्धतीनाथः
अरुन्धतीनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of VASIṢṬHA, as above.<BR>E.<BR>अरुन्धती and नाथ a lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुश
अरुश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Smooth, liter. or fig.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुश rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्क|अरुष्कः
अरुष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>The marking-nut plant, see the next word.<BR>E.<BR>अरुस् a sore, and क what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्कर|अरुष्करं|अरुष्करः
अरुष्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Corrosive, caustic, acrid.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The marking-nut plant, (Semecarpius anacardium.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The nut.<BR>E.<BR>अरुस् a sore, कृ to make, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्ट
अरुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Calm, not angry.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रुष्ट angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुस्
अरुस्<BR>mfn. (-रुः)<BR>A sore or wound.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>ind.<BR>A joint.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and उसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुसिका
अरुसिका<BR>f. (का)<BR>Eruptions on the scalp, with acute pain.<BR>E.<BR>अरुस् a sore, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>1 Formless, shapeless.<BR>2 Ugly, ill formed, misshapen.<BR>3 Dissimilar, unlike.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रूप beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपक
अरूपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Literal, without figure or metaphor.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रूपक figurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपता
अरूपता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Ugliness.<BR>2 Shapelessness.<BR>3 Dissimilarity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अरूप, also अरूपत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=067" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपवत्|अरूपवन्त्
अरूपवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Ugly, shapeless.<BR>E.<BR>अरूप and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूष|अरूषः
अरूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, ऊषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरे
अरे<BR>ind.<BR>Interjection of calling to inferiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेरे
अरेरे<BR>ind.<BR>1 Interjection of calling to inferiors.<BR>2 Also of calling angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोक|अरोकः
अरोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Obscured, dimmed, darkened.<BR>E.<BR>रुच् to be light, घञ् affix; अ neg. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोकदत्|अरोकदन्त्
अरोकदत्<BR>mfn. (-दत्-दती-दत्)<BR>Having black or discoloured teeth.<BR>E.<BR>अरोक, and दत् for दन्त a tooth, also अरोकदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोकदन्त|अरोकदंत
अरोकदन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Having bad teeth; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग|अरोगः
अरोग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Well, healthy, free from disease.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Health.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिता
अरोगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Health.<BR>E.<BR>अरोगिन् well, तल् affix, or with त्व अरोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिन्
अरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Well, in health.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोगिन् sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचक|अरोचकः
अरोचक<BR>f. (-कः)<BR>Indigestion, loss of appetite.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोचक digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचिष्णु
अरोचिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Disagreeable.<BR>2 Dark.<BR>3 Ugly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोचिष्णु splendid, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोदन
अरोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not weeping.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोदन weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोध्य
अरोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Unobstructed, unobstructable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोध्य to be hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोपण
अरोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Not planting or fixing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोपण setting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोष|अरोषः
अरोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Calmness, gentleness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरौद्र
अरौद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>Not formidable or fierce.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रोद्र formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (अर्कयति)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>2 To heat or warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Crystal.<BR>3 Swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea.)<BR>4 Copper.<BR>5 A name of INDRA.<BR>6 A Paṇḍita or learned man.<BR>7 An elder brother.<BR>8 Sunday.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship or respect, क Uṇādi affix, and the च is dropped; what is worshipped or respected: or अर्क to heat, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कज|अर्कजः
अर्कज<BR>du. m. (-जौ)<BR>The two sons of SŪRYA and AŚVINĪ, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, and ज who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कतनय|अर्कतनयः
अर्कतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of SŪRYA or the sun, applicable to YAMA, to SANI, to the Munis VAIVASVATA and SĀVARṆI, to REVANTA, and to KARṆA.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The daughter of the sun, applied to the river goddesses YAMUNĀ and TAPATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and तनय a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कत्विष्
अर्कत्विष्<BR>f. (-त्विट्)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 The light of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and त्विष् radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कदिन
अर्कदिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A solar day.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and दिन a day: also अर्कदिवसं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कनन्दन|अर्कनन्दनः
अर्कनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>YAMA, &c. see अर्कतनय.<BR>E.<BR>as before, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपत्र|अर्कपत्रः
अर्कपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea.)<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A kind of birth wort, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the swallow wort, and पत्र a leaf: the leaves of the two plants being similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपर्ण|अर्कपर्णः|अर्क्कपर्ण
अर्कपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea, or Calotropis.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपादप|अर्कपादपः
अर्कपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Nimb tree, (Nimba or Melia azadirachta.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कपुष्पिका
अर्कपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, vulgarly Arkahuli, (Cleome pentaphylla). Also अर्कपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कबन्धु|अर्कबन्धुः
अर्कबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA, the founder of the BAUDDHA sect of Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, and बन्धु a kinsman, being of the Sūrya Van's, or line of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कबान्धव|अर्कबान्धवः
अर्कबान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, बान्धव a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कमण्डल
अर्कमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The disc of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कमूला
अर्कमूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Birthwort. See अर्कपत्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्करेतोज|अर्करेतोजः
अर्करेतोज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>REVANTA the son of SŪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, रेतस् the semen, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कवर्ष|अर्कवर्षः
अर्कवर्ष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A solar year.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and वर्ष a year; also अर्कवत्सर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कव्रत|अर्कव्रतं|अर्कव्रतः
अर्कव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Levying taxes, subjecting the people to heavy imposts, drawing their wealth as the sun evaporizes water.<BR>2 Periodical worship of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कसूनु|अर्कसूनुः
अर्कसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and सूनु a son: the son of SŪRYA. See अर्कतनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कसोदर|अर्कसोदरः
अर्कसोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, सोदर kinsman, from स with, and उदर womb; from their being alike engaged in maintaining the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कांश|अर्कांशः
अर्कांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A digit or twelfth of the sun's disc.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्काश्मन्
अर्काश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>1 A crystal lens. See सूर्य्यकान्त.<BR>2 A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्काहू
अर्काहू<BR>m. (-हूः)<BR>Swallow wort.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and अक्व appellation: bearing all the synonyms of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्केन्दुसङ्गम|अर्केन्दुसंगम|अर्केन्दुसंगमः
अर्केन्दुसङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The instant of conjunction of the sun and moon.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, इन्दु the moon, and सङ्गम union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कोपल|अर्कोपलः
अर्कोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sun-stone.<BR>2 A ruby.<BR>3 A crystal lens.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल|अर्गलं|अर्गलः
अर्गल<BR>nf. (-लः-ला or -ली)<BR>A wooden bolt or pin for fastening a door.<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A surge or billow.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ज to gain, कलच् affix, ज becomes ग, and the fem. takes both टाप् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small door pin, a bolt.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन affix, टाप् for the fem. and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्घति)<BR>To hurt or injure.<BR>r. 10th cl. (अर्घयति)<BR>To cost, to be worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ|अर्घः
अर्घ<BR>m. (र्घः)<BR>1 Price, cost.<BR>2 Mode of worship or reverence.<BR>3 An oblation of various ingredients to a god or Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ to cost, or अर्हं to worship, ह being changed to घ, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घदान
अर्घदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Presentation of a respectful offering.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घबलाबल
अर्घबलाबल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Rate of price, proper price.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ, and बल strength, अबल weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घसंख्यापन
अर्घसंख्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fixing the price of commodities, appraising, assize.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ, and संख्यापन fixing together with: it is the act of the king or ruler, in concert with the traders, and should be done once a week or once a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=068" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घार्ह
अर्घार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Worthy of or requiring a respectful offering, a superior.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घीश|अर्घीशः
अर्घीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ oblation, and ईश lord: the lord of offerings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य<BR>mfn. (-र्घ्यः-र्घ्या-र्घ्यं)<BR>Venerable, deserving worship.<BR>n. (-र्घ्यं)<BR>A respectful oblation to gods or venerable men, of rice, dūrbbā grass, flowers, &c. with water, and of water only in a small boat-shaped vessel.<BR>n. (-र्घ्यं)<BR>Wild honey.<BR>E.<BR>अर्घ, and य or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च|अर्च्च
अर्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्चति) Also 1st and 10th cls. (अर्चति-ते अर्चयति-ते)<BR>To worship, to honour or treat with respect: with सम् prefixed, to worship. This root and its derivatives are also read अर्च्च, &c. doubling the consonant after र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A worshipper, one who worships.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चना|अर्च्चना
अर्चना<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>An article of worship.<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Worship, the homage paid to deities and to superiors.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship, युच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनीय
अर्चनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च, and अनीयर् affix, also अर्च्य and अर्चयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा<BR>f. (-र्चा)<BR>1 Worship, see अर्चना.<BR>2 An image.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship, अच् affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चि|अर्चिः|अर्च्चिः
अर्चि<BR>f. (-र्चिः)<BR>Flame.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चित|अर्च्चितः
अर्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Worshipped, respected, saluted.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मत्|अर्चिष्मन्त्
अर्चिष्मत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मती-ष्मत्)<BR>Brilliant, resplendent.<BR>m. (-ष्मान्)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अर्चिस् flame, and मतुप poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्चिस्|अर्चिस्
अर्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्चिः)<BR>1 Flame.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>3 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship, and इसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्य
अर्च्य<BR>mfn. (-र्च्यः-र्च्या-र्च्यं)<BR>Reverend, respectable, worshipful.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च to worship, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज|अर्ज्ज
अर्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्जति)<BR>To earn, to gain or acquire, (commonly used with उप prefixed.)<BR>10th cl. (अर्जयति)<BR>1 The same, and:<BR>2 To work or manufacture.<BR>3 To make or prepare. This root and its derivatives are also read अर्ज्ज, &c. doubling the consonant after र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>An acquirer, one who gains or acquires.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Basil, the white sort, (Ocymum villosum.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्ज to gain, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जन|अर्जनं|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gain, acquisition of wealth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ज, and ल्युट् affix, also written अर्ज्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जित
अर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gained, acquired.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ज to gain, क्त affix, also written अर्ज्जित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The third of the Pāṇḍavas, the son of INDRA and friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 The name of a king with a thousand arms. See कार्त्तवीर्य्य.<BR>3 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>4 A peacock.<BR>5 The only son of his mother.<BR>6 White, (the colour.)<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>1 Grass.<BR>2 Slight inflammation of the conjunctiva or white of the eye.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 UṢĀ, the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>3 The Karatoya river in the north of Bengal.<BR>4 A procuress, a bawd.<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>White.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ज to gain, उनन् Uṇādi affix, fem. ङीप्^1, also read अर्ज्जुन.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनक|अर्जुनकः
अर्जुनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Belonging to ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्जुन and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनतस्
अर्जुनतस्<BR>ind.<BR>On the side or party of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्जुन and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनच्छवि|अर्जुनछवि
अर्जुनच्छवि<BR>mfn. (-विः-विः-वि)<BR>White, of a white colour.<BR>E.<BR>अर्जुन white, and छवि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनध्वज|अर्जुनध्वजः|अर्ज्जुनध्वजः
अर्जुनध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>अर्जुन, and ध्वज a banner, being ARJUNA'S symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनोपम|अर्जुनोपमः|अर्ज्जुनोपम|अर्ज्जुनोपमः
अर्जुनोपम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The teak tree, (Tectona grandis.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्जुन a tree, &c. उपम like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ण|अर्णः
अर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The teak tree.<BR>2 A letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णस् water, व affix, and स is dropped: the ण in this and similar words is optionally doubled, as अर्ण्णव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवज|अर्णवजः|अर्ण्णवज
अर्णवज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Sea-born, marine.<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>Cuttle fish.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवमन्दिर|अर्णवमन्दिरः
अर्णवमन्दिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>VARUṆA, regent of the water.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णव the ocean, and मन्दिर a house; whose dwelling is the deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवपोत|अर्णवपोतः
अर्णवपोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A boat or ship.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णव, and पोत a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णवयान
अर्णवयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A boat or ship.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णव, and यान vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्
अर्णस्<BR>n. (-र्णः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, असुन् Uṇādi affix, and नट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोद|अर्णोदः|अर्ण्णोद
अर्णोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णोभव|अर्णोभवः|अर्ण्णोभव
अर्णोभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A shell.<BR>E.<BR>अर्णस्, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तगल|अर्तगल|अर्तगलः|अर्त्तगलः
अर्त्तगल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Blue barleria, (B. caerulea.)<BR>E.<BR>आर्त्त exhausted, and गल to drop, the आ is made short, also आर्तगल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तन|अर्तन|अर्त्तनं
अर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Censure, reproach, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>ऋति to blame, a sautra root, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्ति|अर्ति|अर्तिः|अर्त्तिः
अर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 The end of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द to hurt, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तिक
अर्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Diseased, pained.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of cake.<BR>E.<BR>अर्त्ति pain, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्त्तिका|अर्तिका
अर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An elder sister, (in theatrical language.) See अत्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ<BR>r. 10th cl. (अर्थयते sometimes -ति)<BR>To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ|अर्थः
अर्थ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Rich.<BR>2 Learned.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 Wealth, property, substance.<BR>2 Meaning, signification.<BR>3 Thing.<BR>4 Fruit, consequence.<BR>5 Prohibition.<BR>6 A material substance or object of sense.<BR>7 Cause, origin.<BR>8 Request, asking, begging.<BR>9 Kind, sort, manner.<BR>10 Well, well being.<BR>11 (In law) A suit, an action.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and थन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकर
अर्थकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Producing or yielding wealth, what enriches.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and कर what makes, also similar compounds, as अर्थकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं,) अर्थकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) and अर्थजनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं,) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थकाम
अर्थकाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Avarice, desire of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थगरीयस्
अर्थगरीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Significant, meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ with गुरु heavy, ईयसुन superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थघ्न
अर्थघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Wasteful, extravagant.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and घ्न who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थज्ञ
अर्थज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Wise, discriminating, understanding the various significations of a word, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ meaning, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतस्
अर्थतस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to the sense.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to अर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतत्त्व
अर्थतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>Truth, the real object, nature or cause of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=069" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थद
अर्थद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Liberal, munificent.<BR>2 Compliant, favourable.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ wealth or object, and द who or what gives. Also similar compounds, as अर्थदायक, अर्थदायिन् and अर्थदातृ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थदूषण
अर्थदूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Waste, prodigality, extravagance.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and दूषण spoiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Begging, asking.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ to ask, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपति|अर्थपतिः
अर्थपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 KUVERA, the Hindu PLUTUS.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ wealth, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थपर
अर्थपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Intent on gaining wealth.<BR>2 Parsimonious, niggardly.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्रयोग|अर्थप्रयोगः
अर्थप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Application of wealth, as to trade, usury, &c.<BR>2 The profession of usury.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थप्राप्ति
अर्थप्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Acquisition of wealth.<BR>2 Attainment of an object.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and प्राप्ति gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभृत
अर्थभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A servant who has high wages.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and भृत maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थभेद|अर्थभेदः
अर्थभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Distinction, difference of meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ meaning, and भेद dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलाभ|अर्थलाभः
अर्थलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Acquisition of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and लाभ acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलुब्ध
अर्थलुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Greedy of wealth, covetous, niggardly.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and लुब्ध desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलेश
अर्थलेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A little wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थलोभ|अर्थलोभः
अर्थलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Avarice, desire of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Wealthy, rich.<BR>2 Significant, having sense or meaning.<BR>3 Designed, intentional, having an object.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवाद|अर्थवादः
अर्थवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>2 Declaration of purpose or object, speech or expression having a certain object, as स्तुत्यर्थवादः speech implying praise, निन्दार्थवादः speech implying censure.<BR>3 Amplification.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ substance, thing, and वाद speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविज्ञान|अर्थविज्ञानं
अर्थविज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>One of the six exercises of the understanding, the comprehension of meanings.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ meaning, import, and विज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थविद्
अर्थविद्<BR>mfn. (-वित् or -विद्)<BR>Sagacious, sensible, wise.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवृद्धि|अर्थवृद्धिः
अर्थवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Accumulation of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवैकल्प
अर्थवैकल्प<BR>n. (-ल्पं)<BR>Prevarication, evasion, deviation from truth, perversion or disguise of fact.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ object, वैकल्प alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्यय|अर्थव्ययः
अर्थव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and व्यय expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थव्ययज्ञ|अर्थव्ययज्ञः
अर्थव्ययज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Liberal in giving and using.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ wealth, व्यय expense, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशास्त्र|अर्थशास्त्रं
अर्थशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>The science of polity or moral and political government.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ possession, property, and शास्त्र institutes of a science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थशौच
अर्थशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Honesty.<BR>2 Acquisition of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ purpose or wealth, शौच purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंग्रह
अर्थसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Accumulation of wealth.<BR>2 A treasure.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and संग्रह a collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसंस्थान
अर्थसंस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Accumulation of wealth.<BR>2 A treasury.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and संस्थान assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसञ्चय|अर्थसंचय|अर्थसंचयः
अर्थसञ्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Accumulation of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and सञ्चय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसम्बन्ध|अर्थसंबन्ध|अर्थसंबन्धः
अर्थसम्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Connexion of the sense with the word or sentence.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्ध
अर्थसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Effected by wealth.<BR>2 Successful, one whose aim is accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थसिद्धि|अर्थसिद्धिः
अर्थसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Success.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहर
अर्थहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Inheriting or taking wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and हर who takes. So अर्थहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थहीन
अर्थहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Poor.<BR>2 Failing, disappointed.<BR>3 Unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and हीन wanting. So अर्थशून्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं).<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and शून्य empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थागम|अर्थागमः
अर्थागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Receipt or collection of property.<BR>2 Acquisition of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ wealth, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकार|अर्थाधिकारः
अर्थाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Stewardship, treasurership, charge of money or property.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थाधिकारिन्
अर्थाधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A treasurer, a paymaster.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and अधिकारिन् superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तर
अर्थान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Difference of meaning or purport.<BR>2 Another or second sense.<BR>3 Opposite or antithetical meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्तरन्यास
अर्थान्तरन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Antithesis.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थान्तर, and न्यास position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थान्वित
अर्थान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rich.<BR>2 Significant.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ wealth, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापत्ति|अर्थापत्तिः
अर्थापत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 A figure of speech, a quibble, the use of one word in a double sense.<BR>2 An inference from circumstances.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and आपत्ति gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थार्थिन्
अर्थार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 One who solicits wealth.<BR>2 One endeavouring to gain any object.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and अर्थिन who seeks or solicits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिक|अर्थिकः
अर्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crier, a watchman, a minstrel, a servant whose duty it is to announce by song or music, fixed periods of the day, or those of getting up and of repose, &c.<BR>2 A beggar, a solicitor.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थि a rich man, and क from के to call or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित
अर्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Asked, begged, sought.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिता
अर्थिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Asking, begging. Also n. (-त्वं)<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to अर्थिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 One who asks or begs for any thing.<BR>2 One who seeks to effect or gain a purpose or object.<BR>m. (-र्थी)<BR>1 A servant.<BR>2 A follower, a companion or partisan.<BR>3 A plaintiff, a prosecutor.<BR>4 A beggar, a petitioner.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ asking, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोपार्ज्जन|अर्थोपार्जन
अर्थोपार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acquiring wealth.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and उपार्ज्जन acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थोष्मन्
अर्थोष्मन्<BR>n. (-ष्म)<BR>Wealth, the condition of being wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ, and उष्मन् warmth. So, anglice, a warm man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य<BR>mfn. (-र्थ्यः-र्थ्या-र्थ्यं)<BR>1 Intelligent, wise.<BR>2 Wealthy.<BR>3 Right, proper.<BR>4 Fit to be asked or sought.<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द|अर्द्द
अर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्दति)<BR>1 To ask or beg.<BR>2 To go.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (अर्दति-ते अर्दयति-ते)<BR>To kill or to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दना|अर्द्दना
अर्दना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Begging, asking.<BR>2 Giving pain.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>4 Going.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द to ask, &c. युच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=070" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनि|अर्दनिः
अर्दनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Asking, begging.<BR>3 Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द to pain, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दित|अर्दितं|अर्द्दित|अर्द्दितः
अर्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Asked, requested, begged.<BR>2 Killed, injured.<BR>3 Pained, afflicted.<BR>4 Gone.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A disease, Hemiplegia, paralysis of the muscles on one side of the face and neck.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द to go, to ask, &c. affix, क्त and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्ध
अर्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>Half, halved.<BR>m. (-र्द्धं)<BR>A part.<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>A half.<BR>E.<BR>ऋध to increase, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धकृत
अर्द्धकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Halved, divided equally.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धखार
अर्द्धखार<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>A measure, half a khārī.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धं, and खारी a measure so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धगङ्गा
अर्द्धगङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The Kāverī river, in the peninsula.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध half, and गङ्गा the Ganges; being a sacred stream, having half the virtues of the great Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धगुच्छ
अर्द्धगुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A necklace of twenty-four strings.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and गुच्छ a bundle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्र
अर्द्धचन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A crescent or half moon.<BR>2 The hand bent into a semicircle or the shape of a claw, as for the purpose of seizing or clutching any thing.<BR>3 The semicircular marks on a peacock's tail.<BR>4 An arrow, with a head like a crescent.<BR>5 The semicircular scratch of the finger nail.<BR>f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>A plant, vulgarly Teori, the black kind.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध half, and चन्द्र moon, or with कन् added अर्द्धचन्द्रकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्राकार
अर्द्धचन्द्राकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Of the shape of the half moon.<BR>m. (रः)<BR>A meniscus.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्र, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचन्द्राकृति
अर्द्धचन्द्राकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Half mooned, of a crescent-shape, convex and concave.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A meniscus.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धचन्द्र, and आकृति shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धचोलक
अर्द्धचोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A short bodice.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and चोलक a bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धजाह्नवी
अर्द्धजाह्नवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The Kāverī river. See अर्द्धगङ्ग, जाह्नवी being the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धधार
अर्द्धधार<BR>n. (रं)<BR>A knife or lancet with a single edge, the blade two inches long, the heft six.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and धारा an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनारीश
अर्द्धनारीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, नारी a woman, and ईश master; one of the forms of ŚIVA, to which this name applies, being half male and half female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनाव
अर्द्धनाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A boat's half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and नाव, from नौ a boat, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धनिशा
अर्द्धनिशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपण
अर्द्धपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Half a Paṇa.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and पण a measure of four Kākiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपारावत
अर्द्धपारावत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A pigeon, (with a spotted or painted throat.)<BR>2 The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and पारावत a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धपुलायित
अर्द्धपुलायित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A half gallop, a canter.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and पुलायित a gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धप्रहर
अर्द्धप्रहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Half a watch, a period of an hour and a half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and प्रहर a watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभाग
अर्द्धभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभाज्
अर्द्धभाज्<BR>mf. (भाक्)<BR>Taking or sharing half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध half, and भाज who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभागिक
अर्द्धभागिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Taking or sharing half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धभाग a half, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धभागिन्
अर्द्धभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Sharing or taking half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धभाग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धमाणव
अर्द्धमाणव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A necklace of twelve strings. Also अर्द्धमाणवक.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and माणव one of twenty-four strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धयाम
अर्द्धयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Half a watch, an hour and a half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and याम a watch, also अर्द्धयामक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धरथ
अर्द्धरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A warrior, who fights on a car with another.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and रथ a car, having half a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धरात्र
अर्द्धरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 Midnight.<BR>2 The period from two and a half to three and a half watches of the night.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and रात्र night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धर्च
अर्द्धर्च<BR>mn. (-र्चः-र्चं)<BR>Half a verse of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and ऋच् a verse of a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धवीक्षण
अर्द्धवीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A side look, a glance, a leer.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and वीक्षण looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धशत
अर्द्धशत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fifty.<BR>2 One hundred and fifty.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and शत a hundred, in the second sense it is more usually सार्द्ध शत, &c. So अर्द्धपञ्चाशत्, अर्द्धसहस्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धशन
अर्द्धशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Half a meal.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and अशन eating, also अर्द्धाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धसफर
अर्द्धसफर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small fish, (Cyprinus sophore, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and सफर another fish, to which it is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धसीरिन्
अर्द्धसीरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A cultivator, a ploughman who takes half the crop for his labour.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and सीर a plough, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धहार
अर्द्धहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A necklace of sixty-four strings.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and हार a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धांश
अर्द्धांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धांशिन्
अर्द्धांशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Sharing a half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धांश and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धाङ्ग
अर्द्धाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Half the body.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धार्द्ध
अर्द्धार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>Sharing equally.<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A quarter.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धावभेदक
अर्द्धावभेदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Pain of half the head, hemicrania.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Dividing in equal parts.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and अवभेदक cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धाशन
अर्द्धाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Half a meal. Also अर्द्धशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धासन
अर्द्धासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Exemption from censure.<BR>2 Greeting kindly or with respect, placing on the same seat.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and आस to remain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धिक
अर्द्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Measuring a half.<BR>2 Relating to a half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध and टिठन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धिन्
अर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिणी-र्द्धि)<BR>Entitled to or sharing a half.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धेन्दु
अर्द्धेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A half moon or crescent.<BR>2 The impression of a finger nail.<BR>3 The hand expanded in a semicircular form like a claw.<BR>4 An arrow with a crescent-shaped head.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धे, and इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोक्त
अर्द्धोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Half uttered, said imperfectly or indistinctly.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोक्ति
अर्द्धोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Speaking indistinctly or incompletely, broken or interrupted speech.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोदित
अर्द्धोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Half risen.<BR>2 Half uttered.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and उदित risen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्धोरुक
अर्द्धोरुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A short petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, and उरु the thigh, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पण|अर्पणं
अर्पण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Delivering, entrusting.<BR>2 Placing in or upon.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, in the causal form, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=071" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पणीय
अर्पणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be delivered, deliverable.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, causal form, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पित
अर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Delivered, consigned.<BR>2 Placed in or upon.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, in the causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पितकर
अर्पितकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Extending or giving the hand.<BR>2 Married.<BR>E.<BR>अर्पित, and कर the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पिस|अर्पिसः
अर्पिस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The heart.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, in the causal form अर्प, and इसन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्प्य
अर्प्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be delivered, consignable.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, causal form, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्ब|अर्ब
अर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्ब्बति)<BR>1 To go, to go to towards.<BR>2 To kill or hurt. See अर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्बुद|अर्बुद|अर्बुदं|अर्बुदः|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्ब्बुद<BR>mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>1 Ophthalmia.<BR>2 A hundred millions.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The name of a mountain in the west of India, commonly Abū, a place of pilgrimage, especially to the Jains.<BR>2 An indolent swelling.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ब to injure, उदच् affix; the root and derivative are also written with the dental letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ<BR>mfn. (-र्भः-र्भा-र्भं)<BR>Destitute of splendour.<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 A child, a pupil.<BR>2 Dew.<BR>3 Herbs.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and भन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A child, the young of any animal.<BR>2 A fool, an idiot.<BR>3 Small, minute.<BR>4 Emaciated.<BR>5 Like, similar.<BR>E.<BR>ऋध to grow, वुन् Uṇādi affix, and भ substituted for ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्म|अर्म|अर्मं|अर्मः|अर्म्मं
अर्म्म<BR>mn. (-र्मः-र्मं)<BR>A disease of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and मन Uṇādi affix, also read अर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्मण|अर्मण|अर्मणं|अर्म्मणः
अर्म्मण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A measure of one Droṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्म्मन्|अर्मन्
अर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>A disease of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्य|अर्य|अर्यः|अर्य्यः
अर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Excellent.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A master.<BR>2 A man of the third tribe, the Vaiśya.<BR>f. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A woman of the third tribe.<BR>2 The wife of a Vaiśya.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, यत् affix, and टाप् or ङीप् for the fem.; ङीष् is affixed, when the word is fem. with reference to the male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्यमन्|अर्यमन्
अर्य्यमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A class of the Manes or deified progenitors.<BR>3 The asclepias plant.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, कनिन् Uṇādi affix, and माङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्यर्य्याणी
अर्य्यर्य्याणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A multitude of women of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य्याणी|अर्याणी
अर्य्याणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A woman of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR>E.<BR>अर्य्य, ङीप् affix, and आनुक inserted. See अर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्व|अर्व
अर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्व्वति)<BR>To kill or hurt, also written अर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वट|अर्वट|अर्वटं
अर्व्वट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Ashes.<BR>E.<BR>अर्व्व or अर्ब्ब to injure, hence the word may be also written अर्ब्बट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वन्|अर्वन्
अर्व्वन्<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वा-र्व्वती-र्व्वत्)<BR>Low, inferior, vile.<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>3 A short span.<BR>f. (-र्वती)<BR>1 A mare.<BR>2 A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and वनिप् Uṇādi affix; it is sometimes derived from अर्ब्ब to go, and is then written अर्ब्बन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाच्|अर्वाच्
अर्व्वाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाङ्-वाची-वाक्)<BR>Following, subsequent.<BR>ind. (वाच् or वाक्)<BR>1 After, in time.<BR>2 Behind, in place.<BR>3 Near.<BR>E.<BR>अवर behind, अञ्च to go, and क्विप् affix; the formation is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाचीन|अर्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीनः
अर्व्वाचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Reverse, contrary.<BR>2 Recent, modern.<BR>E.<BR>अर्व्वाच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्वाचीनत्व
अर्व्वाचीनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>State of reverse.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, अर्व्वाचीनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्श|अर्शं|अर्शः
अर्श<BR>n. (-र्शं)<BR>Hoemorrhoids, piles. Also अर्शस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस्
अर्शस्<BR>n. (-र्शः)<BR>Hoemorrhoids, piles.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, असुन् Uṇādi affix, and शुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस|अर्शसः
अर्शस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Afflicted with hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अर्शस् and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शसान|अर्शसानः
अर्शसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, शानच् affix, and शुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शिन्
अर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Afflicted with hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोघ्न|अर्शोघ्नः
अर्शोघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>Destroying the hoemorrhoids.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्शस्, and घ्न what destroys, from हन to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोग
अर्शोरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The piles or hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अर्शस, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोगयुत
अर्शोरोगयुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Afflicted with hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अर्शोरोग, and युत affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोरोगिन्
अर्शोरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Having hoemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>अर्शोरोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शोहित|अर्शोहितः
अर्शोहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The marking-nut plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्शस्, and हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्सस्
अर्सस्<BR>m. (-र्सः)<BR>Hoemorrhoids. See अर्शस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्हति)<BR>1 To worship or honour.<BR>2 To be fit or worthy: in the first sense it is also r. 10th cl. (अर्हयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>1 Proper, fit, becoming.<BR>2 Deserving, entitled to, worthy.<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>f. (-र्हा)<BR>Worship.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ह to worship, to be fit, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हण|अर्हणं
अर्हण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Worship, adoration, respect, courtesy, treating with veneration or respect.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ह to worship, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्|अर्हन्त्
अर्हत्<BR>mfn. (-न्-न्ती-त्)<BR>1 Venerable, respectable.<BR>2 Praised, celebrated.<BR>m. (-न्)<BR>1 A Jina or Jaina saint and teacher.<BR>2 A Jain or follower of the doctrines of Jina.<BR>3 A religious mendicant of that sect.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ह to worship, &c. and शतृ affix, of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्तम
अर्हत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Best, most worthy.<BR>E.<BR>अर्हन् respectable, डतम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्तर
अर्हत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>More worthy, better.<BR>E.<BR>अर्हत् and डत्तर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हन्त|अर्हंत|अर्हन्तः
अर्हन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A Saugata or follower of the doctrines of Buddha.<BR>2 A religious mendicant of the same sect.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अर्ह to worship, &c. and अन्त irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हित|अर्हितः
अर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Saluted, honoured, worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>अह to worship, &c. and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्य
अर्ह्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable, right, fit.<BR>E.<BR>अह and यत् affix: also with अनीयर affix, अर्हणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल|अलं
अल<BR>r. 1st cl. also read अलं (अलति-ते)<BR>1 To adorn.<BR>2 To be competent or able.<BR>3 To prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल|अलं
अल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The sting in the tail of the scorpion.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक|अलकं|अलकः
अलक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A curl.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mad dog. See अलर्क.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Alakā, the capital of KUVERA.<BR>2 A young girl from eight to ten years of age.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. वुन् affix, and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकनन्दा
अलकनन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>1 A young girl from eight to ten years old.<BR>2 A river, the Alakanandā, a stream that runs from the Himālaya mountains, and falls into the Ganges near Srīnagar. It is also a name of the terrestrial Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>अलका, and नन्दा who delights, the final of the first dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=072" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकप्रभा
अलकप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The capital of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>अलका and प्रभा what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकप्रिय|अलकप्रियः
अलकप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकसंहति|अलकसंहतिः
अलकसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Rows of curls.<BR>E.<BR>अलक, and संहति collection. So अलकावली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकाधिप|अलकाधिपः
अलकाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>अलका the city, and अधिप a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकाधिपति|अलकाधिपतिः
अलकाधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>लका, and अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकान्त|अलकान्तः
अलकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A ringlet, the end of a curl.<BR>E.<BR>अलक, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्त|अलक्तः
अलक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>Lac, the red animal dye so called.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. रक्त red, र being changed to ल; than what nothing is redder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तक|अलक्तकः
अलक्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lac, the dye; see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तरस|अलक्तरसः
अलक्तरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Liquefied lac dye.<BR>E.<BR>अलक्त, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षण|अलक्षणं
अलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Unfortunate, ill fated, having no good marks on the person.<BR>2 Undefined.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The absence of auspicious marks.<BR>2 Misfortune.<BR>3 The want of any predicate or definition.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षित
अलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unmarked, having no particular mark.<BR>2 Unobserved, unseen.<BR>3 Undefined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्मी
अलक्ष्मी<BR>f. (-क्ष्मीः)<BR>Misfortune, poverty.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and लक्ष्मी fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्य
अलक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Undistinguishable, undefinable. So अलक्षणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलगर्द|अलगर्दः|अलगर्द्द
अलगर्द<BR>m. (-र्दः)<BR>1 The black variety of the Cobra de Capello, (Coluber naga.)<BR>2 A large black leech.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लग to be with or near, and क्विप् affix अलक; again अर्द to go, and अच् affix; not trailing its whole length upon the ground: also अलगर्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलग्न
अलग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Not joined or connected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लग्न attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघु
अलघु<BR>mfn. (-घुः-घुः-घ्वी-घु)<BR>1 Heavy, weighty.<BR>2 Serious, solemn.<BR>3 Violent, intense.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लघु light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघुप्रतिज्ञ
अलघुप्रतिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Solemnly pledged or promised.<BR>E.<BR>अलघु, and प्रतिज्ञा agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघूपल|अलघूपलः
अलघूपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A rock.<BR>E.<BR>अलघु, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघूष्मन्
अलघूष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>Intense heat.<BR>E.<BR>अलघु, and उष्मन् heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करण|अलंकरण|अलंकरणं|अलङ्करणं
अलङ्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ornament, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् ornament, and करण what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्करिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णुः|अलङ्करिष्णुः
अलङ्करिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Ornamented.<BR>2 Fond of ornament.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् ornament, कर from कृ, and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्तृ|अलंकर्तृ|अलङ्कर्त्तृ
अलङ्कर्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्ता-र्त्री-र्तृ)<BR>Ornamented, ornamenting.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् as before, and कर्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कर्म्मीण|अलङ्कर्मीण|अलंकर्मीण|अलङ्कर्म्मीणः
अलङ्कर्म्मीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Competent to an act, skilful, clever.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् able, fit for, कर्म्म act, business, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कार|अलंकार|अलंकारः|अलङ्कारः
अलङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Ornament (of dress), trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR>2 (Of language,) A figure or rhetorical expression.<BR>3 The art of composition.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् ornament, कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कारहीन|अलंकारहीन
अलङ्कारहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unadorned.<BR>E.<BR>अलङ्कार, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्क्रिया|अलंक्रिया
अलङ्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Adorning, ornamenting.<BR>E.<BR>अलस्, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्कृत|अलंकृत|अलङ्कृतः
अलङ्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ornamented, adorned, lit. or fig.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् as before, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घन|अलंघन|अलंघनं
अलङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Not transgressing.<BR>2 Not passing over or beyond.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लङ्घन crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घनीय|अलंघनीय
अलङ्घनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Impassable, not to be crossed.<BR>2 Venerable, inviolable, not to be transgressed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लङ्घनीय to be passed, also अलङ्घ्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घनीयता|अलंघनीयता
अलङ्घनीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The state of not being passable.<BR>2 Inviolability, respectability.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also अलङ्घमीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घ्य|अलंघ्य
अलङ्घ्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्घ्यः-ङ्घ्या-ङ्घ्यं)<BR>1 Inviolable.<BR>2 Impassable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लङ्घ्य to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलङ्घ्यता
अलङ्घ्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Impassability, inaccessibility.<BR>2 Superiority.<BR>3 Authoritative or absolute rule.<BR>E.<BR>अलङ्घ्य not to be crossed or transgressed, तल् affix, also अलङ्घ्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज्ज
अलज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Shameless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लज्जा shame. So अलज्जित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलजी
अलजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>Inflammation of the eye, at the edge of the cornea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलञ्जर|अलंजरः|अलञ्जरः
अलञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An earthen water jar.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् able, and जॄ to decay, also अलिञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलति|अलतिः
अलति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A kind of song.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् ornament, and अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्तराम्|अलंतराम्
अलन्तराम्<BR>ind.<BR>Quite enough, amply sufficient.<BR>E.<BR>अलं and तराम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलब्ध
अलब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Unobtained.<BR>E.<BR>अ and लब्ध attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलन्धूम|अलंधूम|अलन्धूमः
अलन्धूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A great smoke.<BR>E.<BR>अलम् much, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलभ्य
अलभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>Unattainable, unobtainable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लभ्य to be got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्
अलम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Ornament.<BR>2 Enough, abundance.<BR>3 Able, adequate or equal to.<BR>4 Prohibition, no, not.<BR>5 Unnecessary, no need of.<BR>It is chiefly used in composition, as अलञ्जीविकः having enough for subsistence; अलन्दत्वा refusing to give; इत्यलम् enough; अलङ्कार ornament, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. and अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्पुरुषीण|अलंपुरुषीण|अलम्पुरुषीणः
अलम्पुरुषीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Fit for a man, becoming a man.<BR>E.<BR>अलन्, पुरुष a man, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्बुष|अलंबुष|अलंबुषः|अलम्बुषः
अलम्बुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>2 Vomiting, sickness.<BR>3 The name of a Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 One of the Apsarasas or nymphs of Svarga.<BR>2 Madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>3 A sort of sensitive plant.<BR>4 A barrier, a line or any thing not to be crossed.<BR>E.<BR>अलम्, and बुस to injure, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलय|अलयः
अलय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Houseless, homeless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and लय place of refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्क|अलर्कः
अलर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 White swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea alba.)<BR>2 A mad dog or one rendered furious.<BR>3 A fabulous animal, like a hog with eight legs.<BR>4 An Asura changed to such an animal. Also अलर्क्क.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. क्विप् affix, and अर्क to inflame or heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलले
अलले<BR>ind.<BR>A word of no import, occurring in the dialect or gibberish of Piśācas, a class of imps or goblins, when they are introduced in plays, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवाल|अलवालं
अलवाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A basin for water at the root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लू to cut, and आल affix; also आलवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवालक|अलवालकं
अलवालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस|अलसः
अलस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Lazy, idle, indolent.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Swelling of the feet in elephantiasis.<BR>2 Chaps between the toes.<BR>3 Name [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=74" target="_blank">Page74</a>] of a tree.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A creeping plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and लस to work, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=073" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसक|अलसकः
अलसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Indolent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Flatulence, Tympanitis, intumescence of the abdomen, with constipation and wind.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसता
अलसता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Idleness.<BR>E.<BR>अलस and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसत्व
अलसत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Idleness.<BR>E.<BR>अलस and त्वं aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसेक्षणा
अलसेक्षणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A woman with languishing looks.<BR>E.<BR>अलस idle, and ईक्षणा looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलात|अलातं|अलातः
अलात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A fire brand, whether burning or extinguished.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ला to take, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबु|अलाबुः
अलाबु<BR>f. (-बुः)<BR>A long gourd. See the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबू
अलाबू<BR>f. (-बूः)<BR>The bottle gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaris.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लब to sink, ऊ Uṇādi affix; म् is dropped, and the preceding vowel lengthened: what does not sink in water; floats, &c. are made of this gourd, especially when hollowed: also अलाबु and आलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबूकट
अलाबूकट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The down of the gourd.<BR>E.<BR>अलाबू and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाभ|अलाभः
अलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Non-acquirement, not getting.<BR>2 Loss.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलार|अलारं
अलार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A door.<BR>E.<BR>अल able, and ऋ to go, अच् affix; by which one may go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास|अलासः
अलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Inflammation and abscess at the root of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लास saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलि|अलिः
अलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 A scorpion.<BR>3 The sign Scorpio.<BR>4 A crow.<BR>5 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>6 Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>अल to be able, &c. and इण Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिक|अलिकं
अलिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. and इकन् affix; also अलीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिकुल
अलिकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A flight or a number of bees.<BR>E.<BR>अलि, and कुल a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिगर्द्ध
अलिगर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A snake, the black Cobra.<BR>E.<BR>अलि, and गर्द्ध to sound, affix अच्; hissing like the scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिङ्गिन्|अलिंगिन्
अलिङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>An impostor, a pretended ascetic or student, one wearing the usual marks, as the frontal marks, skin, staff, &c. without belonging in reality to a religious order.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लिङ्ग sectarial mark, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिजिह्वा
अलिजिह्वा<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The uvula or soft palate. Also अलिजिह्विका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिञ्जर|अलिंजर|अलिंजरः|अलिञ्जरः
अलिञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An earthen water jar.<BR>E.<BR>अलिम् strength, acc. of अलि and जॄ to waste, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्
अलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 A scorpion.<BR>E.<BR>अल a sting, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्द|अलिंदः|अलिन्दः
अलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A terrace before a house.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. and किन्दच् affix; also आलिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपक|अलिपकः
अलिपक<BR>m. (कः)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 A scorpion.<BR>3 A dog. Also read अलिम्पक and अलिमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपिज्ञ
अलिपिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Ignorant of reading and writing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लिपि writing, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्रिय|अलिप्रियं|अलिप्रियः
अलिप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The red lotus, (Nymphoea rubra.)<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>अलि a bee, and प्रिय beloved, the object of the bee's affections: the lotus especially is so described by the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्सा
अलिप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Freedom from desire or cupidity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and लिप्सा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिमक|अलिमकः
अलिमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A large black bee.<BR>4 The filaments of the lotus.<BR>5 A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>अलि from अल to adorn, मकच् affix; also अलिपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिमाला
अलिमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A flight of bees.<BR>E.<BR>अलि, and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिम्पक|अलिंपक
अलिम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bee.<BR>2 The Kokila.<BR>3 A dog.<BR>4 The filaments of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लिपि to smear, वुन् affix; also read अलिवकः and अलिम्बकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिविराव|अलिविरावः
अलिविराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The hum of bees.<BR>E.<BR>अलि, and विराव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिविरुत
अलिविरुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The song or hum of the bee.<BR>E.<BR>अलि, and विरुत sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक|अलीकं
अलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 False.<BR>2 Unpleasing.<BR>3 Small, little.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Falsehood, untruth.<BR>2 Any thing displeasing.<BR>3 Heaven.<BR>4 The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, &c. and कीकच Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकता
अलीकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Falsehood, vanity: also अलीकत्व.<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकमत्स्य|अलीकमत्स्यः
अलीकमत्स्य<BR>m. (-त्स्यः)<BR>A cake of beans fried with Sesamum oil.<BR>E.<BR>अलीक unreal, मत्स्य fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलु|अलुः
अलु<BR>f. (-लुः)<BR>A small water pot.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and उच् affix, र becomes ल; also आलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुब्ध|अलुब्धः
अलुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Moderate, content, not covetous.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलून
अलून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Uncut, unshorn.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अले
अले<BR>ind.<BR>An unmeaning word in the dialect of the demons or Piśācas, when they are introduced in plays, &c. also अलले.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेले
अलेले<BR>ind.<BR>See the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेश
अलेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Much, large.<BR>adv. n. (-शं)<BR>Not at all.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लेश small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेशैज
अलेशैज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Firm, steady.<BR>E.<BR>अलेश not at all, एज what shakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकन|अलोकनं
अलोकन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disappearance, invisibility.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोकन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकनीय
अलोकनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोकनीय visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकित
अलोकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unseen.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोकित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभ|अलोभः
अलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Moderation, content, absence of cupidity.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभिन्
अलोभिन्<BR>mfn. (-भी-भिनी-भि)<BR>Not wanting or desiring any thing, free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and लोभिन् desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोल
अलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Firm, steady, tranquil, unagitated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोल moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलु
अलोलु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Indifferent to sensual objects.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोल to desire, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुप
अलोलुप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लोलुप libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुत्व
अलोलुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Indifference to sensual objects.<BR>E.<BR>अलोलु and त्व affix: also अलोलुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोहित|अलोहितं
अलोहित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौकिक|अलौकिकः
अलौकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Supernatural, not relating, to this world.<BR>2 Not common, not current in the world.<BR>3 Indifferent to the world, unworldly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लौकिक mundane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्क|अल्कः
अल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कं)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A member of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्प|अल्पं|अल्पः
अल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>1 Little, small.<BR>2 Inferior, low.<BR>E.<BR>अल to be able, &c. प affix or with कन् added अल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=074" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पक|अल्पकः
अल्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Small, minute.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पकेशी
अल्पकेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The root of sweet flag.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प small, and केशी having filaments, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पगन्ध|अल्पगन्धं
अल्पगन्ध<BR>n. (न्धं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पज्ञ
अल्पज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Ignorant, shallow, superficial.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पतनु|अल्पतनुः
अल्पतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Small, short, thing, pigmy, having a little body.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and तनु the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पता
अल्पता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Smallness, minuteness.<BR>2 Inferiority, insignificance.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and तल् affix, or with त्व, अल्पत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पदक्षिण
अल्पदक्षिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Defective in presents, (any ceremony, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and दक्षिणा gift to Brahmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पधन
अल्पधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of little wealth, not affluent.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and घन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पधी
अल्पधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Ignorant, foolish, of little sense.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पपत्र|अल्पपत्रः
अल्पपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A species of the Tulasi.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पपद्म|अल्पपद्मं
अल्पपद्म<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प small, and पद्म lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रभाव
अल्पप्रभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Insignificant, of little weight or consequence.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and प्रभाव authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रमाण|अल्पप्रमाणः
अल्पप्रमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Of little authority.<BR>2 Of little weight or measure.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and प्रमाण authority, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पप्रमाणक|अल्पप्रमाणकः
अल्पप्रमाणक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Credulous, resting on little evidence.<BR>2 Of little weight or authority.<BR>3 Of short measure.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Common cucumber, (Cucumis sativus.)<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and प्रमाण authority, &c. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबल
अल्पबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Feeble, of little strength.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and वल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबाध
अल्पबाध<BR>m. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Causing little annoyance or inconvenience.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पबुद्धि
अल्पबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Ignorant, silly, unwise.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमात्र
अल्पमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A little, a little only.<BR>2 A short time, a few moments.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमारिष|अल्पमारिषः
अल्पमारिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of amaranth, (Amaranthus polygamus.)<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, मृष to hurt, and इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमूर्त्ति|अल्पमूर्ति|अल्पमूर्तिः
अल्पमूर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति)<BR>Small, diminutive.<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A small figure or object.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पमेधस्
अल्पमेधस्<BR>mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः)<BR>Ignorant, silly, of little understanding.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and मेधस् apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पवयस्
अल्पवयस्<BR>mfn. (-याः-याः-यः)<BR>Young, of few years.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and वयस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पवादिन्
अल्पवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Taciturn: also अल्पभाषिन्.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and वादिन् or भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पविषय
अल्पविषय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Meaning or directing a little.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पविद्य
अल्पविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Ill taught, uneducated, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशक्ति
अल्पशक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Weak, feeble.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशस
अल्पशस<BR>ind.<BR>1 A little.<BR>2 To a few.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पसरस्
अल्पसरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A basin, a small pond, one which is shallow or dry in the hot season.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and सरस् a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाकाङ्क्षिन्|अल्पाकांक्षिन्
अल्पाकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि^1)<BR>Contented, satisfied with little.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and आकाङ्क्षिन् who desires.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: nom. sgn. of 'xin' is `xI`.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पायुस्
अल्पायुस्<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-युः)<BR>1 Short lived.<BR>2 Young, of few years.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and आयस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाल्प
अल्पाल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>1 Very little, minute.<BR>2 Grandual, little at a time.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाहार|अल्पाहारः
अल्पाहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Moderate, abstemious.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Moderation, abstinence.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पाहारिन्
अल्पाहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Abstemious, moderate.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and आहारिन् who feeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पिष्ठ|अल्पिष्ठः
अल्पिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Least, smallest, very small.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and इष्ठच् affix of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीकृत
अल्पीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reduced, comminuted, made little or few.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and कृत with च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीभूत
अल्पीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reduced, diminished, become little or few.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प, and भूत become, च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीयस्
अल्पीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very small.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प and ईयसुन् affix. Also अल्पिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पोन
अल्पोन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Defective, not quite finished, not wholly entire.<BR>E.<BR>अल्प a little, ऊन less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्ला
अल्ला<BR>f. (-ल्ला)<BR>A mother, in dramatic language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव<BR>r. 1st cl. (अवति)<BR>1 To keep, protect or defend.<BR>2 To please. (The following meanings, although found in lists of roots, are rarely used:)<BR>3 To move.<BR>4 To excite affection or be lovely.<BR>5 To satisfy.<BR>6 To know or apprehend.<BR>7 To enter.<BR>8 To be near.<BR>9 To own, to have a right.<BR>10 To obey.<BR>11 To act.<BR>12 To desire.<BR>13 To shine or be splendid.<BR>14 To obtain.<BR>15 To embrace.<BR>16 To kill or hurt.<BR>17 To take.<BR>18 To be.<BR>19 To grow.<BR>In place of 9, 17, and 18 as above, some read:<BR>9 To be able. .²17 To burn, and .²18 To divide or share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव<BR>ind.<BR>A preposition and prefix to words, corresponding to off, from, down from, out, away, &c. and implying;<BR>1 Diminution.<BR>2 Depreciation.<BR>3 Diffusion.<BR>4 Support, resting.<BR>5 Commanding.<BR>6 Purifying, correcting.<BR>7 Knowledge.<BR>8 Disrespect.<BR>9 Nourishing.<BR>As<BR>अवगन्तुं<BR>To go away;<BR>अवज्ञातुं<BR>To disrespect;<BR>अवतरितुं<BR>To come down, to descend;<BR>अवस्थातुं<BR>To remain in or on;<BR>अवहर्त्तुं<BR>To take off or away;<BR>also<BR>अवमः<BR>a low man;<BR>अवाक्<BR>reverse, behind;<BR>अवकोकिलः<BR>a koïl with a bad voice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकट|अवकटं
अवकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Opposite, contrary.<BR>2 Backwards.<BR>3 Downwards.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Opposition, contrariety, reverse.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, and कठच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकम्पित
अवकम्पित<BR>m.<BR>A Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and कम्पित shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर|अवकरः
अवकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Dust or sweepings.<BR>E.<BR>अव spreading, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्त्तन|अवकर्तन|अवकर्तनं
अवकर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Excision, cutting off.<BR>E.<BR>अव and कर्त्तन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षण|अवकर्षणं
अवकर्षण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Taking or pulling out, extraction, expulsion.<BR>2 Pulling, dragging.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and कर्षण pulling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen.<BR>E.<BR>अव and कलित part. past. of कल to sound, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश|अवकाशः
अवकाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Leisure, opportunity.<BR>2 Interval, space.<BR>3 An open or wide space.<BR>4 A receptacle, a repository, a place in which any thing is kept.<BR>5 A place, a spot, a situation.<BR>E.<BR>अव between, &c. काश to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=075" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Coarsely pounded.<BR>2 Scattered.<BR>3 Disregarded, violated.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying separation, कॄ to scatter in the irregular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्णिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि)<BR>Violating a vow or engagement to be chaste, abstemious, &c.<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>The religious student who has committed an act of incontinency.<BR>E.<BR>अव before, कॄ to scatter, क्त the part. past., and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिव्रत
अवकीर्णिव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Penance for an act of incontinency.<BR>E.<BR>अवकीर्णिन् and व्रत religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुञ्चन|अवकुंचन|अवकुंचनं
अवकुञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bending, curving, flexure, contraction.<BR>E.<BR>अव and कुञ्चन curving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटार|अवकुटारं
अवकुटार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Opposite, contrary.<BR>2 Backwards.<BR>3 Downwards.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Reverse, contrariety.<BR>E.<BR>अव and कुटार aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुट्टित
अवकुट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Vexed.<BR>2 Inflamed.<BR>3 Cut off.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and कुट्ट to heat, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठन|अवकुंठनं
अवकुण्ठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Investing, surrounding.<BR>2 Attracting.<BR>E.<BR>अव, before कुठ to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुण्ठित|अवकुंठित
अवकुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Affected.<BR>2 Surrounded, attracted.<BR>E.<BR>अव before कुठ to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्ट|अवकृष्टः
अवकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Expelled, turned out.<BR>2 Removed, sent away, drawn aside.<BR>3 Extracted.<BR>4 Pulled.<BR>5 Inferior, low.<BR>6 Degraded, outcaste.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A servant who performs the lowest office, a sweeper, a waterman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अव out of, and कृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्य
अवकृष्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having drawn out or extracted.<BR>2 Having drawn together or contracted.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and कृष to draw, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेशिन्
अवकेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Barren.<BR>E.<BR>अव privative, केश properly hair, in this instance fruit, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्तव्य|अवक्तव्यं
अवक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Not to be said, improper.<BR>2 Indescribable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वक्तव्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्र
अवक्र<BR>mfn. (-क्रः-क्रा-क्रं)<BR>1 Straight.<BR>2 Upright, honest.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वक्र crooked liter. and metaph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रन्दन|अवक्रंदनं
अवक्रन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Weeping aloud.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्रन्दन crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रय|अवक्रयः
अवक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Price.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रान्ति|अवक्रांतिः|अवक्रान्तिः
अवक्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Descent, descending.<BR>2 Approaching, going near to.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्रान्ति passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रिया
अवक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Neglect, omission, non-performance of prescribed acts.<BR>E.<BR>अव priv. क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुष्ट
अवक्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Sounded ill or badly.<BR>2 Reviled, abused.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्रुष्ट sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रोश|अवक्रोशः
अवक्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A disagreeable noise.<BR>2 A curse, an imprecation.<BR>3 Abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अव and क्रुश to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेद|अवक्लेदः
अवक्लेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Ichor, malignant or fetid discharge.<BR>2 Trickling, descent of moisture.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्लेद what wets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदन|अवक्लेदनं
अवक्लेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trickling, falling as dew or moisture.<BR>E.<BR>अव and क्लेदन wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वण|अवक्वणः
अवक्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A discord, a false note.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्वण a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वाथ|अवक्वाथः
अवक्वाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Imperfect digestion or decoction.<BR>E.<BR>अव and क्वाथ a decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षय|अवक्षयः
अवक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Loss, waste, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्षय waste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्त
अवक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Said sarcastically, imputed, insinuated.<BR>2 Ill thrown.<BR>3 Thrown down.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्षिप्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षीण
अवक्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Emaciated, wasted.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्षीण wasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षुत|अवक्षुतं
अवक्षुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sneezed upon.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्षुत sneezed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेप|अवक्षेपः
अवक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Sarcasm, irony.<BR>3 Throwing wrong or improperly.<BR>3 Throwing down.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगणित|अवगणितं
अवगणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disregarded, despised.<BR>E.<BR>अव, गण to count or reckon in the past. part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगण्ड|अवगंडः|अवगण्डः
अवगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A boil or pimple upon the face.<BR>E.<BR>अव, गडि to affect the cheek, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगत|अवगतं
अवगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Gone, gone off or away.<BR>3 Assented, promised.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying knowledge, and गत part. past. of गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगति|अवगतिः
अवगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Knowledge in general.<BR>2 Departure, removal.<BR>E.<BR>अव, गम to go, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगथ|अवगथः
अवगथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Bathing or bathed early in the morning.<BR>E.<BR>अव, ग from गम to go, and थक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगदित|अवगदितः
अवगदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unsaid, unuttered.<BR>E.<BR>अव reverse, गदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगन्तव्य
अवगन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Meant, intended to be known or understood.<BR>2 To be quitted. So अवगम्य.<BR>E.<BR>अव and गन्तव्य to be gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगम|अवगमः
अवगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Knowledge, certainty.<BR>2 Removal, departure.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढ
अवगाढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Immersed, plunged, bathed.<BR>2 Deep.<BR>E.<BR>अवगाह and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढवत्
अवगाढवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Bathing, plunging, diving.<BR>E.<BR>अवगाढ and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाद|अवगादः
अवगाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A small wooden bason for baling water out of a boat.<BR>E.<BR>अव for अप water, ग from गम to go, and आदक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह|अवगाहः
अवगाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Bathing.<BR>2 Bathing place, bath.<BR>E.<BR>अब before, गाह to agitate: also वगाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहन|अवगाहनं
अवगाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bathing.<BR>E.<BR>अवगाह and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहित
अवगाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bathed, immersed.<BR>E.<BR>अवगाह, and क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reproached, abused, censured.<BR>2 Wicked, vile.<BR>3 Sung depreciatingly, satirised in song.<BR>4 Sung badly.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Reproach, blame.<BR>2 Satire in song.<BR>3 Bad singing.<BR>E.<BR>अव bad, &c. गीत sounded, sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठन|अवगुंठनं|अवगुण्ठनं
अवगुण्ठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A veil.<BR>2 Sweeping.<BR>3 Hiding, veiling.<BR>E.<BR>गुठि to enclose, with अव prefixed, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठिका|अवगुंठिका
अवगुण्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with वुन् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्ठित|अवगुंठित|अवगुण्ठितं
अवगुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Concealed, covered, veiled, screened.<BR>E.<BR>अवगुठ to enclose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुण्डित|अवगुंडित
अवगुण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pounded, ground, pulverulent.<BR>E.<BR>अव prefixed to गुण्डित pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगोरण|अवगोरणं
अवगोरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Assailing with weapons, assaulting with intent to kill.<BR>E.<BR>अव, गुर् or गूर् to assault, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह|अवग्रहः
अवग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking, acceptance.<BR>2 Taking off or away, seizure.<BR>3 Disrespect.<BR>4 Drought.<BR>5 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>6 An elephant's forehead.<BR>7 A herd of elephants.<BR>8 Nature, original temperament.<BR>9 A sort of knowledge, a false idea.<BR>10 An imprecation or term of abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अव before, ग्रह to take or seize, अप् affix: also अवग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=076" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहण|अवग्रहणं
अवग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>2 Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव, ग्रह to take, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्राह|अवग्राहः
अवग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An imprecation or term of abuse, as अवग्राहस्ते स्यात्, may disappointment befall you.<BR>2 Drought.<BR>3 Disgrace, discomfiture: see अवग्रह.<BR>E.<BR>as before, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृह्य
अवगृह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>An inflection, an inflective termination.<BR>E.<BR>अव before ग्रह to take, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्ट|अवघट्टः
अवघट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A hole in the ground, a cave, a cavern.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, low, घट्ट to move, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षण|अवघर्षणं
अवघर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rubbing, scrubbing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षित
अवघर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rubbed, scrubbed.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घर्षित rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघात|अवघातः
अवघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Threshing corn, by bruising it with a wooden pestle in a mortar of the same material.<BR>2 Sudden or violent death.<BR>3 Strinking, killing.<BR>4 A violent or fatal blow.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घात struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातिन्
अवघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Striking, killing.<BR>E.<BR>अव before हन to strike, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघुष्ट
अवघुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Proclaimed, denounced.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घुष्ट cried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्ण|अवघूर्णः
अवघूर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A whirling round.<BR>2 A whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>अव before घूर्ण to roll round, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णन|अवघूर्णनं|अवघूर्ण्णन
अवघूर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rolling or whirling round.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घूर्णन rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णित
अवघूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Whirled round.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घूर्णित whirled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषण|अवघोषणं
अवघोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Crying, proclaiming, denouncing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and घोषण proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन
अवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Silence, not speaking.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वचन word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीय
अवचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be spoken, improper.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वचनीय to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीयता
अवचनीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Impropriety of speech.<BR>E.<BR>अवचनीय and तल् affix; also अवचनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचय|अवचयः
अवचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gathering, especially flowers, fruits, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and चय collecting; also अवचाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचस्कर|अवचस्करः
अवचस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Silent, not speaking.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वच speech, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार्य्य|अवचार्य
अवचार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be cast down.<BR>2 To be given.<BR>3 To be put on or applied.<BR>E.<BR>अव, चर to go, causal form, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूड|अवचूडः
अवचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The crest or ornamented top of a standard, hanging downwards.<BR>E.<BR>अव, चूडा a crest; also अवचूडक and अवचूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णन|अवचूर्णनं|अवचूर्ण्णन
अवचूर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pounding, grinding, reducing to powder.<BR>2 Sprinkling absorbent powders on sores.<BR>E.<BR>अव, चूर्ण to pound, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णित|अवचूर्णितं|अवचूर्ण्णित
अवचूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Coarsely pounded.<BR>E.<BR>अव, चूर्ण to pound, in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूल|अवचूलः
अवचूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The ornamented head of a standard, when the ornaments, streamers, peacockś tails, &c. hang downward.<BR>2 A chowri.<BR>E.<BR>अव inferior, and चूडा crest, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलक|अवचूलकं|अवचूलकः
अवचूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A chowri or brush formed of a cow's tail, peacock's feathers, &c. for fanning off lies.<BR>E.<BR>कन् affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छात
अवच्छात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Emaciated by abstinence.<BR>2 Reaped.<BR>3 Cut off.<BR>E.<BR>अव before छो to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिन्न|अवच्छिन्नं
अवच्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Cut off.<BR>2 Divided, separated, detached.<BR>3 In logic, predicated. i. e. separated from every thing else by the properties especially predicated of any thing.<BR>4 Bounded.<BR>E.<BR>अव affix, छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरित|अवच्छुरितं|अवछुरित
अवच्छुरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A horse laugh.<BR>E.<BR>अव, छुर to cut or split, and the affix of the part. past.: what splits, (one's sides).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरितक|अवच्छुरितकं
अवच्छुरितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A horse laugh.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding word, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेद|अवच्छेदः
अवच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A predicate, the property of a thing by which it is distinguished from every other.<BR>3 A part, a portion.<BR>3 A boundary, a barrier.<BR>4 Amputation, excision.<BR>E.<BR>अव off, छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदक|अवच्छेदकं|अवच्छेदकः
अवच्छेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Peculiar, distinguishing, that which separates.<BR>2 Bounding, separating one thing from another.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A predicate, a property.<BR>2 A barrier, a boundary.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदन|अवच्छेदनं
अवच्छेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>2 Separating, dividing.<BR>3 Discriminating, distinguishing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and छेदन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदावच्छेद|अवच्छेदावच्छेदः
अवच्छेदावच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Generalising, removing distinctions.<BR>E.<BR>अवछेद a distinction, and cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजनित
अवजनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Born.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and जनित born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजय|अवजयः
अवजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Overcoming, victory.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and जय conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजित
अवजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Conquered.<BR>2 Contemned, disregarded.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव, ज्ञा to know, अङ् affix, and टाप for the fem.; also अवज्ञता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञात|अवज्ञातं
अवज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespected.<BR>E.<BR>अव, ज्ञात part. past. of ज्ञा to know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञान|अवज्ञानं
अवज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrepect.<BR>E.<BR>अव before ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञेय
अवज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Contemptible, disreputable, to be treated with disrespect: so अवज्ञातव्य.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and ज्ञा to know, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञोपहत
अवज्ञोपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Degraded, humiliated.<BR>E.<BR>अवज्ञा, and उपहत wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट|अवटः
अवट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A hole, a vacuity.<BR>2 A hole in the ground, a chasm, a pit.<BR>3 Any depressed part of the body, a cavity, a fosse, a sinus.<BR>4 A well.<BR>5 A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटङ्क
अवटङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A mart; also अवटङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटि|अवटिः
अवटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>1 A hole in the ground.<BR>2 In anatomy, a sinus. a hollow, a cavity.<BR>E.<BR>as before, अटिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying lowness, flatness, and टीटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटु|अवटुः
अवटु<BR>f. (-टः)<BR>1 The back of the neck.<BR>2 A hole in the ground.<BR>2 A well.<BR>4 The name of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, and टीक to go, irregular affix डु; or अ neg. वट to surround, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुज|अवटुजः
अवटुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A hind curl, the hair on the back of the head.<BR>E.<BR>अवटु, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडीन|अवडीनं
अवडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The flight of a bird, or a particular act of such flight; flying down.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, &c. and डीन flying: see प्रडीन, उड्डीन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=077" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंस|अवतंसं|अवतंसः
अवतंस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>1 An ear-ring.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>E.<BR>अव, तसि a Sautra root to adorn, अच्, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसित
अवतंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Having an ear-ring.<BR>2 Crested.<BR>E.<BR>अवतंस and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतति|अवततिः
अवतति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Stretching, extending.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and तन to spread, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतमस|अवतमसं
अवतमस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Slight darkness, obscurity.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying deficiency, and तमस् darkness, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरण|अवतरणं
अवतरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Descending, alighting.<BR>2 Crossing.<BR>3 Translating.<BR>4 Quoting, citing.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, तॄ to cross, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतान|अवतानः
अवतान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Stretching, extension.<BR>E.<BR>अव before तन to stretch, affix ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतार|अवतारः
अवतार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Descent, especially of a deity from heaven; the appearance of any deity upon earth, but more particularly the incarnations of VIṢṆU in ten principal forms which are well known, viz. .²1 The fish. .²2 The tortoise. .²3 The boar. .²4 The man-lion. .²5 The dwarf. .²6 and .²7 The two RĀMAS. .²8 KṚṢṆA. .²9 BUDDHA. And .²10 KALKI. A pious or distinguished person, in the language of respect or flattery, is also called an Avatāra, a descent or incarnation of the deity.<BR>2 A Tīrtha or sacred place.<BR>3 Translation, translating.<BR>3 Descent.<BR>4 Crossing.<BR>E.<BR>अव before, तॄ to cross, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारण|अवतारणं
अवतारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Possession by an evil spirit.<BR>2 The ends or border of a garment.<BR>3 Worship, adoration.<BR>4 Taking out.<BR>E.<BR>अव, तॄ to pass, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारित
अवतारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken off or out, laid down or aside.<BR>2 Descended.<BR>E.<BR>अव and तॄ causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्ण|अवतीर्णः|अवतीर्ण्ण
अवतीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Descended, alighted.<BR>2 Crossed, passed over.<BR>3 Translated.<BR>E.<BR>अव and तॄ with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतोका
अवतोका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow miscarrying from accident.<BR>E.<BR>अव, implying censure, and तोक offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदंश|अवदंशः
अवदंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A relish, or what excites thirst.<BR>E.<BR>अव, दंश to bite, to be pungent, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदत्त
अवदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Given away.<BR>2 Finished, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अव before दा to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Yellow.<BR>3 Clean, clear.<BR>4 Beautiful.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>White, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>अव, दै to cleanse, क्त affix of the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदातक
अवदातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>As above.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>White.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान|अवदानं
अवदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Approved occupation.<BR>2 An act accomplished.<BR>3 Achievement, a great or glorious act.<BR>4 Breaking, dividing.<BR>5 The root of a fragrant grass; see अवदाह.<BR>6 An oblation.<BR>E.<BR>अव, दै to cleanse, to purify, or दा to give, and ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारण|अवदारणं
अवदारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A spade or hoe.<BR>2 Tearing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, दॄ to tear or rend, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारित
अवदारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Torn, rent.<BR>E.<BR>अव before दॄ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाह|अवदाहं|अवदाहः
अवदाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum).<BR>E.<BR>अब reverse, and दाह heat, burning, heat-preventing, from its being used in Tātis or screens, placed before doors, &c. and kept constantly wet: the air passing through these, blows into a room cool and refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहेष्ट|अवदाहेष्टं
अवदाहेष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहेष्टकापथ|अवदाहेष्टकापथं
अवदाहेष्टकापथ<BR>n. (-थ)<BR>See अवदाह. See also इष्टकापथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्ण|अवदीर्णं
अवदीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Melted, fused, liquefied.<BR>2 Torn, rent, sundered.<BR>E.<BR>अव, दॄ to separate, irregular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदून
अवदून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Regretted.<BR>E.<BR>अव, दु to be sorry, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदोह|अवदोहः
अवदोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>अव, दुह to milk, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Low, inferior.<BR>2 Disagreeable, disliked.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Sin, vice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वद to speak, and यत् affix of the part. future; not to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्रङ्क
अवद्रङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A market or fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधातव्य
अवधातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be attended to, deserving attention and care. So अबधानीय and अवधेय.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धा to have, तव्य, अनीयर or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधान|अवधानं
अवधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Attention, attentiveness, intentness.<BR>2 Care, carefulness.<BR>E.<BR>अव, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानता
अवधानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Attentiveness.<BR>E.<BR>अवधान attention, तल् added, also with त्व, अवधानत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारण|अवधारणं
अवधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Determining, certainty, ascertainment.<BR>2 Emphasis.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धृ to hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणीय
अवधारणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धृ to hold, causal form, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारित|अवधारितः
अवधारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Certain, known, ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धृ to hold, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधार्य्य|अवधार्य|अवधार्य्यः
अवधार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be ascertained or known.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धृ to hold, causal form, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावन|अवधावनं
अवधावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Running after, pursuing.<BR>2 Taking, seizure.<BR>3 Cleaning.<BR>E.<BR>अव, धाव to run, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावनीय
अवधावनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be run after.<BR>2 To be seized.<BR>E.<BR>अव after, धाव to run, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावित
अवधावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Chased, pursued.<BR>2 Cleaned.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धाव to run, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधि|अवधिः
अवधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 Limit, division.<BR>2 Period, time.<BR>3 A hole, a pit.<BR>4 Agreement, engagement.<BR>5 Conclusion, termination.<BR>6 Attention, application.<BR>7 Care.<BR>E.<BR>अव, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिता
अवधिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Limit, limitation.<BR>E.<BR>अवधि with तल् affix; also with त्व, अवधित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीर
अवधीर<BR>r. 10th cl. (अवधीरयति)<BR>To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरण|अवधीरणं
अवधीरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Treating with disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अवधीर and ल्युट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरित
अवधीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespected, disregarded.<BR>E.<BR>अवधीर and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूत|अवधूतः
अवधूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Compelled.<BR>2 Discarded.<BR>3 Shaken, removed, tossed.<BR>4 Trodden upon.<BR>5 Separated from worldly feeling and obligation.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and धूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूनन|अवधूननं
अवधूनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Shaking, causing to shake.<BR>2 Expelling.<BR>3 Being in agitation, trembling.<BR>4 Trampling on, treading on.<BR>E.<BR>अव before धूनन shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंस|अवध्वंसः
अवध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Censure, blame.<BR>2 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>3 Pounding, grinding.<BR>E.<BR>अव before ध्वंस to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वस्त|अवध्वस्तः
अवध्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Pounded coarsely.<BR>2 Abandoned.<BR>3 Censured.<BR>E.<BR>अव separate, &c. ध्वस to go, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन|अवनं
अवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Satisfaction, (given or received.)<BR>2 Preserving, protecting.<BR>3 Kindness.<BR>4 Speed.<BR>5 Going.<BR>6 Obtaining.<BR>7 Asking.<BR>8 Seizing.<BR>9 Killing.<BR>10 Strength, power.<BR>11 Increase.<BR>12 Existence, being.<BR>13 Doing.<BR>14 Desire.<BR>15 Beautifying, adorning. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=79" target="_blank">Page79</a>]<BR>16 Embracing.<BR>17 Bearing.<BR>18 Entrance.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, to preserve, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=078" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनत|अवनतं
अवनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, नम to bow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनति|अवनतिः
अवनति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Bowing, stooping.<BR>2 Setting.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and नति bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनद्ध|अवनद्धं
अवनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound on, tied, fastened.<BR>n. (-द्वः)<BR>A drum: see आनद्ध.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and नद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनय|अवनयः
अवनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Causing to descend, throwing down.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, नय for नाय causing to get: see अवनाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाट|अवनाटः
अवनाट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>अव flatness, नाटच् affix, in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाम|अवनामः
अवनाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Causing to bend, bending, bowing.<BR>E.<BR>अव before नम to bow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामक
अवनामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What depresses or causes to bow or bend.<BR>E.<BR>अव and नम in the causal, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामिन्
अवनामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Bending or bowing down.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and नामिन् what bends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाय|अवनायः
अवनाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Causing to descend, throwing down, precipitating.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, णीञ्^1 to obtain, in the causal form, घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: Cf WIL and WIL1819 णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनायक
अवनायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Causing to descend.<BR>E.<BR>अव before नी to obtain, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाह|अवनाहः
अवनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Binding, girding, putting on.<BR>E.<BR>अव before नह to bind, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनि|अवनिः
अवनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, अनि Uṇādi affix; it is also written अवनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपति|अवनिपतिः
अवनिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>अवनि, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिपाल|अवनिपालः
अवनिपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>अवनि, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिरुह
अवनिरुह<BR>m. (रुट)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>अवनि, and रुह् what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिष्ठीवन|अवनिष्ठीवनं
अवनिष्ठीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spitting upon.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and निष्ठीवन spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनी
अवनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The earth: see अवनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीपति|अवनीपतिः
अवनीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>अवनी the earth, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीश|अवनीशः
अवनीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>अवनी and ईश् lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनीश्वर|अवनीश्वरः
अवनीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king, an emperor.<BR>E.<BR>अवनी, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेजन|अवनेजनं
अवनेजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Washing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and नेजन ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ति|अवंति|अवंतिः|अवन्तिः
अवन्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 The name of a city, the modern Oujein.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, Uṇādi affix झिच्; the derivative is irregular. Avanti, is one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus, to die at which secures eternal happiness: the word is also written अवन्ती and अवन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्तिसोम|अवन्तिसोमं|अवन्तिसोमः
अवन्तिसोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Sour gruel, prepared from the fermentation of rice water.<BR>E.<BR>अवन्ति the city, षू to produce, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन्ती|अवंती
अवन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A city: see अवन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपतन|अवपतनं
अवपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Alighting, descending.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, पतन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपन्न
अवपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Alighted, descended.<BR>2 Fallen on or into.<BR>3 Thrown down.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and पन्न gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात|अवपातः
अवपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A hole or pit for catching game in.<BR>2 Descent, descending.<BR>E.<BR>अव below, पत to go or fall, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातन|अवपातनं
अवपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Felling, knocking or cutting down.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, पातन causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपालित
अवपालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Neglected, not protected.<BR>E.<BR>अव, before पालित protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड|अवपीडः
अवपीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A sternutatory, any drug producing sneezing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, पीड to pain, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबधा
अवबधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and बध what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोध|अवबोधः
अवबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Judgment, discrimination, knowledge.<BR>2 Waking, being awake.<BR>3 Teaching.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधक|अवबोधकः
अवबोधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A teacher.<BR>2 An awakener.<BR>E.<BR>अव before बुध to be wise, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधकत्व
अवबोधकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Instruction, guidance, explanation.<BR>E.<BR>अवबोधक who teaches, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभास|अवभासः
अवभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and भास light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासित
अवभासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Illumined, lighted, radiant.<BR>2 Evident, manifest.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and भासित splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासिन्
अवभासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Shining, bright.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The outer skin or cuticle.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and भासिन् what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभिन्न
अवभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Broken, pierced, divided.<BR>E.<BR>अव affix, भिन्न cut or broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुग्न
अवभुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Contracted, bent.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and भुग्न bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथ|अवभृथः
अवभृथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A supplementary sacrifice made to atone for any defects in a principal and preceding one.<BR>2 Bathing after a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>अव भृ to screen, क्थन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथस्नान
अवभृथस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bathing after any sacrifice or ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>अवभृथ as before, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रट|अवभ्रटः
अवभ्रट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>अव and भ्रटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवम|अवमं|अवमः
अवम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Low, vile, inferior, base.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A lunar day, exactly coinciding with a solar one.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, &c. अम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमत|अवमतं
अवमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Despised, disregarded, contemned.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying contempt, and मत known, minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमताङ्कुश|अवमतांकुश|अवमताङ्कुशः
अवमताङ्कुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A restive elephant, or one in rut.<BR>E.<BR>अवमत disregarded, and अङ्कुश the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमति|अवमतिः
अवमति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A master, an owner.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Aversion, dislike.<BR>2 Disregard, contempt.<BR>E.<BR>अव, मन to heed, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तव्य|अवमंतव्य
अवमन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be contemned, to be treated with disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मन and तव्य affix. So अवमन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्तृ|अवमंतृ
अवमन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Proud, contemptuous, disrespectful.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मन, with तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्द्द|अवमर्द|अवमर्दः
अवमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 Devastation, inflicting pain or punishment on an enemy, by laying his country waste, &c.<BR>2 Giving pain.<BR>E.<BR>अव, मृद to tread down, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षण|अवमर्षणं
अवमर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Intolerance, impatience.<BR>2 Effacing, obliterating.<BR>3 Banishing from recollection.<BR>E.<BR>अव away, &c. मृष to endure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान|अवमानः
अवमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मान् respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानता
अवमानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Dishonourableness.<BR>2 Contempt.<BR>E.<BR>तल added to the last; also with त्व, अवमानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानना
अवमानना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मन to mind, युच् affix and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमाननीय
अवमाननीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be disrespected, to be contemned^1.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मन, with अनीयर् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानित|अवमानितः
अवमानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespected, despised.<BR>E.<BR>अव before the part. past. of मन to respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=079" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिता
अवमानिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Disrespectfulness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अवमानिन्; also with त्व, अवमानित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिन्
अवमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Behaving disrespectfully, contemning, despising.<BR>E.<BR>अवमान and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान्य|अवमान्यः
अवमान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>To be treated with disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मन with ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूत्रयत्
अवमूत्रयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Urining upon.<BR>E.<BR>अव on, मूत्र nominal v. to make water, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्द्धशय
अवमूर्द्धशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Prostrate.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, मूर्द्धन् the forehead, शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमोचन|अवमोचनं
अवमोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Letting forth, emitting.<BR>2 Setting at liberty.<BR>E.<BR>अव before मुच to set free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयव|अवयवः
अवयव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A limb, a member.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>3 Division of a logical argument or syllogism.<BR>E.<BR>अव, यु to join, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयविन्
अवयविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Limbed, having limbs.<BR>2 Having portions or subdivisions.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A syllogism, a logical argument.<BR>E.<BR>अवयव and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर|अवरं|अवरः
अवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Posterior, hinder, last.<BR>2 Younger.<BR>3 Inferior.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The hind thigh of an elephant.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वर preferable; not the best, or than which nothing is better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरज|अवरजः
अवरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Younger, junior.<BR>2 Inferior, of low birth.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A younger brother.<BR>E.<BR>अवर after, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरत|अवरतः
अवरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stopped, ceased, desisted from.<BR>E.<BR>अव, रम to sport, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतस्
अवरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Hinder, posterior.<BR>E.<BR>अवर and अतसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरति|अवरतिः
अवरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Stopping, ceasing, cessation, end.<BR>E.<BR>अव bad, &c. रम to play, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्ण|अवरवर्णः
अवरवर्ण<BR>mf. (-र्णः-र्णा or -र्णी)<BR>A Śūdra, a man or woman of the fourth tribe.<BR>E.<BR>अवर last, and वर्ण a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरवर्णक|अवरवर्णकः
अवरवर्णक<BR>mf. (-र्णकः-र्णिका)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to अवरबर्ण, also अवरबर्णज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरव्रत|अवरव्रतः
अवरव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वर best, than what nought is better, and ब्रत worship: whose worship is of the first importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरस्तात्
अवरस्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>Hinder, posterior.<BR>E.<BR>अवर and अस्तात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्द्ध
अवरार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>The last half.<BR>E.<BR>अवर and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरार्द्ध्य|अवरार्द्ध्यः
अवरार्द्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-र्द्ध्यः-र्द्ध्या-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>Belonging to the last half.<BR>E.<BR>यत् affix to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरीण|अवरीणं
अवरीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Censured, blamed.<BR>E.<BR>अव, री to flow, the irregular part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुग्ण
अवरुग्ण<BR>mfn. (-ग्णः-ग्णा-ग्णं)<BR>Broken, torn.<BR>2 Diseased.<BR>E.<BR>अव, before रुज to be sick, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्ध
अवरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Checked, stopped, hindered.<BR>2 Shut up or in, inclosed.<BR>3 Secluded, as in a haram.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and रुद्ध hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूढ
अवरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Descended, alighted.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, रुह to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोध|अवरोधः
अवरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 The seraglio of a palace, the queen's apartment.<BR>2 A queen.<BR>3 A palace.<BR>4 A covering.<BR>5 Hindrance, obstruction.<BR>6 A fence, a pen, an inclosure, confinement.<BR>7 Restraint.<BR>E.<BR>अव, रुध to inclose or shut up, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधक|अवरोधकः
अवरोधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What impedes or obstructs.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A guard.<BR>f. (-धिका)<BR>A female of the haram.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A barrier, a fence.<BR>E.<BR>अव before रोधक what opposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधन|अवरोधनं
अवरोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The inner or women's apartments in a royal palace.<BR>2 Hindering, obstructing.<BR>4 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>E.<BR>अव, रुध to enclose, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधायन
अवरोधायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A seraglio.<BR>E.<BR>अवरोध hindrance, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Obstructive, impeding.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A guard of the queen's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>अवरोध with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिन्
अवरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिणी-धि)<BR>Obstructing.<BR>E.<BR>अवरोध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपण|अवरोपणं
अवरोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking away, depriving, diminishing.<BR>2 Descending.<BR>3 Setting, (as of the sun.)<BR>E.<BR>अव affix, and रोपण placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपित
अवरोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Deprived of, curtailed, diminished, lost.<BR>E.<BR>अव aff. रोपित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोह|अवरोहः
अवरोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Mounting, ascending.<BR>2 Descent, passing from or over.<BR>3 The growth of a creeping plant or vine.<BR>4 A pendant branch, one that strikes fresh root into the earth, as those of the Indian fig tree.<BR>5 Heaven or Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>अव up or down, &c. रुह to mount, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहण|अवरोहणं
अवरोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Alighting, descending.<BR>3 Mounting.<BR>E.<BR>अव before रुह to mount, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिन्
अवरोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 What descends.<BR>2 What ascends.<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>अवरोह a branch, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णीं-र्णं)<BR>1 Colourless.<BR>2 Bad, low, destitute of good qualities.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Censure, blame.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वर्ण praise, colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्त्तमान|अवर्तमान
अवर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Non-existent.<BR>2 Not present.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वर्त्तमान existing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्द्धमान
अवर्द्धमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Not increasing, not growing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वर्द्धमान increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः) or attributively, mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>White: see वलक्ष.<BR>E.<BR>अव and लक्ष to mark, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्न|अवलग्नः
अवलग्न<BR>mn. (-ग्नः-ग्नं)<BR>The waist.<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Placed contiguously, impressed, attached, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लग्न part. past. of लग to be near or with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्ब|अवलंबः|अवलम्बः
अवलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 Asylum, dependance, support.<BR>2 Depending, hanging on or from.<BR>3 A prop, a stay.<BR>4 A suspender.<BR>5 A perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>अव before लवि to go, &c. अच् affix; also अवलम्बनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बन|अवलंबनं|अवलम्बनं
अवलम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Depending upon, dependance.<BR>2 Hanging on or from.<BR>3 A prop.<BR>E.<BR>अव before लवि and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बित|अवलंबित|अवलम्बितं
अवलम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Quick, expeditious.<BR>2 Alighting, descending.<BR>3 Protected, cherished.<BR>4 Hanging on or upon, suspended from, clinging to.<BR>5 Depending upon, trusting to, supported by.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and the part. past. of लवि to go, to fall, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलम्बिन्|अवलंबिन्
अवलम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>Depending on.<BR>E.<BR>अवलम्ब and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्त|अवलिप्तः
अवलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Anointed, plastered, smeared.<BR>2 Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>अव before लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=080" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्तता
अवलिप्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Unction.<BR>E.<BR>अवलिप्त plastered, smeared, and तल् affix; also with त्व, अवलिप्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढ|अवलीढं
अवलीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Licked.<BR>2 Devoured, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लीढ licked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीला
अवलीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Sport, play.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लीला sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुञ्चन|अवलुंचन|अवलुंचनं
अवलुञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tearing, tearing or cutting off.<BR>E.<BR>अव, लुच to separate, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठन|अवलुंठनं|अवलुण्ठनं
अवलुण्ठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rolling on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लुण्ठन rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुण्ठित
अवलुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rolled on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लुण्ठित rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलून
अवलून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Cut off.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेप|अवलेपः
अवलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Pride.<BR>2 Smearing, anointing.<BR>4 Ornament.<BR>4 Union, association.<BR>E.<BR>अव, लिप to smear, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपन|अवलेपनं
अवलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Daring, proud or arrogant purpose.<BR>2 Anointing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, लिप and ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह|अवलेहः
अवलेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An extract, an electuary, confection.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लेह licking, what is to be licked with the tongue, not masticated or drank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहन|अवलेहनं
अवलेहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Licking with the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लेहन licking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेह्य
अवलेह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Thick, viscid.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लेह्य to be licked with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक|अवलोकः
अवलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लोकृ to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकन|अवलोकनं
अवलोकन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>अव, लोकृ to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकित|अवलोकितं|अवलोकितः
अवलोकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and the part. past. of लोक to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुज|अवल्गुजः
अवल्गुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica): see सोमराजी.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वल्गु handsome, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववाद|अववादः
अववाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A command, an order.<BR>2 Censure, reproach.<BR>3 Trust, confidence.<BR>E.<BR>अव implying disrespect, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Independent, unsubjected, unrestrained.<BR>2 Necessary, certain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशक्थिका
अवशक्थिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cloth tied round the legs and knees of a person sitting on his hams: see अवसक्थिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्ट|अवशिष्टः
अवशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Left, rest, remainder.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीन|अवशीनः
अवशीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A scorpion.<BR>E.<BR>अव before श्यै to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीभूत
अवशीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unrestrained, independent.<BR>2 Uninfluenced by magic.<BR>E.<BR>अवश and भूत been, with च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेष|अवशेषः
अवशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Leavings, remainder.<BR>2 End, close, termination.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अवश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Untameable, ungovernable.<BR>ind. (-श्यः)<BR>Certainly, necessarily.<BR>E.<BR>अव, श्ये to go, डम् affix; irregularly formed: it occurs in composition with or without the nasal, as अवश्यङ्कारी who does what is necessary, अवश्यपाच्यः to be necessarily cooked, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वश to subdue, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अवश्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Necessary, inevitable, indispensable.<BR>E.<BR>अवश्य and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकता
अवश्यकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Necessity, obligation.<BR>2 Certainty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अवश्यक; also अवश्यकत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>A fog or mist.<BR>E.<BR>अव, श्यै to go, ड affix and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्याय|अवश्यायः
अवश्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Frost.<BR>2 Pride.<BR>E.<BR>अव, श्यै to go, and यङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्कयणी
अवष्कयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A cow that bears a calf after a long interval: see वष्कयणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अवष्टब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Near.<BR>2 Protected, supported.<BR>3 Surpassed, overcome.<BR>4 Bound, tied.<BR>5 Opposed.<BR>6 Wrapped up, enfolded.<BR>7 Hanging from or upon.<BR>8 Stopped, stayed.<BR>9 Paralysed.<BR>E.<BR>अव, लभि to stop, to stand, in the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टभ्य
अवष्टभ्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Leaning upon, holding.<BR>2 Stopping, arresting.<BR>E.<BR>अव before लभि to stop, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भन|अवष्टंभनं
अवष्टम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Supporting, protecting.<BR>2 A pillar, a post.<BR>3 Stopping, staying.<BR>4 Paralysing.<BR>E.<BR>अव before स्तभि to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भः
अवष्टम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Commencement, beginning.<BR>3 A post or pillar.<BR>4 Excellence.<BR>5 Impediment.<BR>6 Support, stay.<BR>7 Paralysis.<BR>E.<BR>अव, स्तभि to stay or stop, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वाण|अवष्वाणं|अवष्वाणः
अवष्वाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>अव, स्वन to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस|अवसं|अवसः
अवस<BR>ind. (-वस)<BR>Without, on the outside.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Preserving, protecting, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, &c. असच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्त
अवसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Attached to or by, in contact with.<BR>2 Engaged or eager.<BR>3 Bound^1 round, begirt.<BR>4 Placed or thrown upon.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and सक्त joined.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्तिका
अवसक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wrapper, a girth or band.<BR>E.<BR>अव about, सक्त joined, कन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A wrapper, a mantle.<BR>2 A cloth drawn round the knees and legs of a person sitting on his hams.<BR>E.<BR>अव round, सक्थि the thigh, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसज्जन|अवसज्जनं
अवसज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Embracing, clinging.<BR>E.<BR>अव before सज्ज to embrace, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ|अवसथः
अवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A village.<BR>2 A college, a school.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. चस to dwell, and अथच् affix; than which there is no other or better abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्य|अवसथ्यः
अवसथ्य<BR>m. (-थ्यः)<BR>A college, a school.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अवसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Melancholy, dispirited, unhappy.<BR>2 Ended, terminated.<BR>3 Languid, enervated.<BR>4 Separated.<BR>5 Bowed, bent.<BR>6 Non-suited.<BR>E.<BR>अव before सन to faint, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नता
अवसन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Low spirits, affliction.<BR>2 Termination, completion.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अवसन्न; also with त्व affix अवसन्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर|अवसरः
अवसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Occasion, opportunity.<BR>2 Rain, raining.<BR>3 Consultation in private.<BR>4 A year.<BR>5 A moment.<BR>E.<BR>अव, सृ to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्ग|अवसर्गः
अवसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Following one's own inclinations.<BR>E.<BR>अव, सृज to create, घञ् affix; ज becomes ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्प|अवसर्पः
अवसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary: see अपसर्प.<BR>E.<BR>अव सृप to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिणी
अवसर्पिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A Jaina division of time; ten Crores of Crores of Sāgaras or oceans of years.<BR>E.<BR>अव, सृप to go, णिनि and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसव्य|अवसव्यं
अवसव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Right, (not left.)<BR>E.<BR>अव reverse, सव्य left; also अपसव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाद|अवसादः
अवसाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Lassitude, want of energy or spirit, especially as proceeding from doubtful or unsuccessful love.<BR>2 Exhaustion, fatigue.<BR>3 In law, badness of a cause.<BR>4 End, termination.<BR>E.<BR>अव, षद to go, to sink, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=081" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Exhausting, wearisome.<BR>2 Ending, finishing.<BR>E.<BR>अव before षद to go, &c. causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादन|अवसादनं
अवसादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Finishing.<BR>2 An escharotic.<BR>3 Removing proud flesh by escharotic applications.<BR>E.<BR>अव before षद to go, a ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादित
अवसादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Languid, exhausted, faint.<BR>E.<BR>अव, षद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान|अवसानं
अवसान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Conclusion, termination, cessation.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 Boundary, limit.<BR>4 In grammar, disjunction of letters.<BR>E.<BR>अव, षो to finish, ल्युट् affix; ओ is changed to आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसाय|अवसायः
अवसाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 End, conclusion.<BR>2 Termination, completion.<BR>3 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>अव, षो to finish, affix ण, and युक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसारण
अवसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Removing, causing to move.<BR>E.<BR>अव before सृ to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
अवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ended, terminated.<BR>2 Finished, completed.<BR>3 Known, understood.<BR>4 Stored, (as grain, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अव, षो to finish, and क्त part. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेक|अवसेकः
अवसेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>अव, षिच to sprinkle, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकिम|अवसेकिमः
अवसेकिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A kind of cake, pulse ground and fried with oil or butter.<BR>E.<BR>अव, सेकृ to sprinkle, इमच् affix; what is sprinkled with oil, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेचन|अवसेचनं
अवसेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>2 Bleeding.<BR>E.<BR>अव before षिच to sprinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेय
अवसेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be destroyed, destructible.<BR>E.<BR>अव before षो to destroy, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्द|अवस्कंदः|अवस्कन्दः
अवस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A camp.<BR>2 Assault, attack, storm.<BR>3 Bathing.<BR>4 Going down, descending.<BR>E.<BR>अव against, &c. स्कन्द to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दन|अवस्कंदनं|अवस्कन्दनं
अवस्कन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Attacking, assaulting, storm.<BR>2 Bathing.<BR>3 Descending.<BR>E.<BR>अव before स्कन्दन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कन्दित|अवस्कंदित
अवस्कन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Attacked.<BR>2 Bathed, bathing.<BR>3 Gone down.<BR>E.<BR>अव, स्कन्द to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कर|अवस्करः
अवस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A privity, a part to be concealed.<BR>2 Ordure, faeces.<BR>3 Dirt.<BR>4 Sweepings.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, away, &c. क to throw, अप् affix, स prefixed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्करक|अवस्करकः
अवस्करक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sweeper.<BR>2 A brush, broom, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अवस्कर and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तात्
अवस्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Posterior, latter.<BR>2 Finally.<BR>E.<BR>अव and स्तात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तार|अवस्तारः
अवस्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A screen or wall of cloth surrounding a tent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अव round, स्तृ to spread, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तु
अवस्तु<BR>n. (-स्तु)<BR>Insubstantiality, the unreality of matter.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. वस्तु thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्तुता
अवस्तुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Insubstantiality, unreality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, अवस्तुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्था
अवस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>State, condition, situation, circumstance of age or position.<BR>E.<BR>अव, स्था to stand or stay, अङ् and टाप affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थाचतुष्टय|अवस्थाचतुष्टयं
अवस्थाचतुष्टय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The periods of human life, viz. childhood, youth, manhood, and old age.<BR>E.<BR>अवस्था, and चतुष्टय four-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थाद्वय
अवस्थाद्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Two states of life, viz. happiness or misery.<BR>E.<BR>अवस्था, and द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थान|अवस्थानं
अवस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Situation, station, abode, place or period of abiding or staying.<BR>E.<BR>अव before स्था to stay, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापन|अवस्थापनं
अवस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fixing, settling.<BR>E.<BR>अव, स्था to stay, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थापित
अवस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fixed.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थायिन्
अवस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Staying, residing in.<BR>E.<BR>अव before स्था to stay, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थित|अवस्थितः
अवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Occupying place or period, abiding, residing, remaining firm or fixed, &c.<BR>2 Firm of purpose, steady.<BR>3 Engaged in, prosecuting, following.<BR>E.<BR>अव before स्था to stay, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्थिति|अवस्थितिः
अवस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Abiding.<BR>2 A residence.<BR>3 Following, practising.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहत
अवहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bruised, beaten.<BR>2 Threshed, winnowed.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहरण|अवहरणं
अवहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Redeeming, taking back.<BR>2 Fining, mulcting.<BR>3 Taking away, stealing, plundering.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्त|अवहस्तः
अवहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The back of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>अव reverse, &c. and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार|अवहारः
अवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A shark.<BR>2 A water elephant.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 Truce, suspension or cessation of gambling, fighting, &c.<BR>5 Summoning, inviting.<BR>6 Any approximatable object, fit or able to be brought near.<BR>7 Apostacy, abandoning a sect or cast.<BR>8 Re-delivery.<BR>E.<BR>अव, हृ to take or convey, घञ् or ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारक|अवहारकः
अवहारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who stops fighting, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shark, a marine monster.<BR>E.<BR>अवहार, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार्य्य|अवहार्य|अवहार्य्यः
अवहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Recoverable, redeemable.<BR>2 Finable, punishable.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and हार्य्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहालिका
अवहालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wall, a bound hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित|अवहितं
अवहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, celebrated.<BR>2 Done with care.<BR>3 Careful.<BR>4 Attentive.<BR>E.<BR>अव, धा to have or hold, part. affix क्त; ध becomes ह and इट् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्थ|अवहित्थं
अवहित्थ<BR>nf. (-त्थं-त्था)<BR>Dissimulation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वहिर् outer, स्था stand; an irregular form: what does not shew outwardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृत
अवहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken off, back, or away, seized, stolen.<BR>2 Fined.<BR>E.<BR>अव off, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेल|अवहेलं|अवहेलः
अवहेल<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अव, हेड to despise, घञ् affix; ड becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलन|अवहेलनं
अवहेलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>as अवहेल, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलित|अवहेलितं
अवहेलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disrespected.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अवहेल and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्पुष्पी
अवाक्पुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, (Pimpinella Anisum.)<BR>E.<BR>अवाक् downwards, and पुष्पी having flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्शिरस्
अवाक्शिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-राः)<BR>Having the head downwards.<BR>E.<BR>अवाक् down, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्ष|अवाक्षः
अवाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Who protects or defends, a guardian, a keeper.<BR>E.<BR>अव under, and अक्षि the eye, अ final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्र|अवाग्रं
अवाग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Stooping, bending, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>अव reverse, and अग्र front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाङ्मुख|अवाङ्मुखं|अवाङ्मुखः
अवाङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Downlooked, headlong.<BR>E.<BR>अवाच् and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Dumb.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् or अवाञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-वाड्-वाची-वाक्)<BR>1 Downlooked, headlong.<BR>2 South.<BR>ind. (-वाक्)<BR>1 South, southern.<BR>2 Downwards.<BR>f. (-वाची)<BR>1 The south quarter.<BR>2 The lower regions.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, downwards, अञ्च् to go, क्विप् affix; the south being considered as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=082" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचीन|अवाचीनं
अवाचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 South, southern.<BR>3 Downlooked, headlong.<BR>3 Descended, gone down.<BR>E.<BR>अवाच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 Vile, bad.<BR>2 Improper to be uttered.<BR>3 Southern, southerly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वाच्य to be spoken, or अवाच् and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यता
अवाच्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Reproach, calumny.<BR>2 Impropriety.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, अवाच्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्यदेश|अवाच्यदेशः
अवाच्यदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>अवाच्य not to be named, देश a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाज्ज्ञान
अवाज्ज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अवाच, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवादिन्
अवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>One who does not speak, who does not dispute, who does not bring an action, peaceable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वादिन् who speaks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
अवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dried, dry, (fruit.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वान dry: than which nothing is drier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्तर|अवांतर|अवान्तरं
अवान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Included, involved.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and अन्तर inner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापित
अवापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unsown, (as grain,) planted.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and वापित sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्त
अवाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Received, got, obtained.<BR>E.<BR>अव before आप to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तवत्
अवाप्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Receiving, obtaining, taking.<BR>2 Entertaining, (as a belief.)<BR>E.<BR>अवाप to get, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्ति|अवाप्तिः
अवाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Obtaining, getting, receiving.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and आप to attain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Unattainable, unobtainable.<BR>ind.<BR>Having obtained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वाप्य procurable, or अव before आप to obtain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार|अवारं|अवारः
अवार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The near bank of a river.<BR>E.<BR>अव down, ऋ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपार|अवारपारः
अवारपार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>अवार the near and पार the opposite bank; embanked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारपारीण|अवारपारीणः
अवारपारीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Crossing a river.<BR>E.<BR>अवारपार both banks, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारिका
अवारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Coriander seed; also अवरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारित|अवारितं
अवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>2 Innumerable.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and वारित hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारितव्य
अवारितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Not to be impeded.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and वारितव्य to be hindered; also अवारणीय and अवार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारीण|अवारीणः
अवारीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Crossing a river.<BR>E.<BR>अवार and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य्य|अवार्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Unrestrainable, irresistible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वार्य्य to be hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावट|अवावटः
अवावट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The son of a woman by any other man than her first husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावन्
अवावन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>ओण to take away, वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवासस्
अवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Naked.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. वासस् clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तव|अवास्तवं
अवास्तव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Unsubstantial, unreal.<BR>2 Unfounded, irrational, (as an argument.)<BR>E.<BR>अ, and वास्तव substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तविक
अवास्तविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Insubstantial, unreal.<BR>2 Unfounded, (as an argument.)<BR>E.<BR>अ, वास्तविक substantial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A sheep.<BR>4 A master.<BR>5 A blanket.<BR>6 A rat.<BR>7 A wall or enclosure.<BR>8 Air, wind.<BR>9 The shawl goat.<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>A woman in her courses; also अवी.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, to preserve, &c. इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक|अविकं|अविकः
अविक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A diamond.<BR>E.<BR>अवि the sun, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकच
अविकच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Closed, shut.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकच open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकचित
अविकचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unblown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकचित blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकट|अविकटः
अविकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A flock of sheep.<BR>E.<BR>अवि a sheep, कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकथ
अविकथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Not boasting, not talking vainly or idly.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विकथा boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकथन
अविकथन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>One who does not boast.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not boasting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकथन talking idly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल
अविकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Entire, perfect, unimpaired.<BR>2 Regular, orderly, consistent.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विकल defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्प|अविकल्पः
अविकल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>Positive act or precept, absence of doubt or alternative.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकल्प alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार|अविकारः
अविकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Immutable, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकार change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार्य्य|अविकार्य
अविकार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Immutable, unchangeable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकार्य्य liable to change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृत
अविकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unchanged, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विकृत changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रम|अविक्रमः
अविक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Powerless, feeble.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Cowardice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रय
अविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Want of sale.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रान्त|अविक्रांत
अविक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Unsurpassed.<BR>2 Feeble, powerless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वि before क्रम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रीत
अविक्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unsold.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्रीत sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रेय
अविक्रेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unsaleable, not to be sold.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्रेय to be sold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लम|अविक्लमः
अविक्लम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Vigour, freshness, absence of fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्लम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लव
अविक्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Calm, composed, firm.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्लव confounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लान्त
अविक्लान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Unwearied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्लान्त wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षत
अविक्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Entire, undiminished.<BR>2 Unhurt.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्षत wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप्त
अविक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Attentive, composed.<BR>2 Retained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्षिप्त tossed, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षोभ
अविक्षोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Quiet, quiescence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्षोभ agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षोभित
अविक्षोभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tranquil, undisturbed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विक्षोभित agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगत
अविगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Retained, present, unseparated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विगत gone away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगम|अविगमः
अविगम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Unseparated, unremoved.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Presence, inherence, association, non-separation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विगम separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगर्हित
अविगर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unreproached.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विगर्हित reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगीत|अविगीतं
अविगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unreproached.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विगीत censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगुण
अविगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Compatible, consistent with, not contrary to.<BR>2 Worthy, good.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वि without, गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्न|अविग्नः
अविग्न<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>A fruit tree, commonly Caronda, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विज to fear, part. past., irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्रह|अविग्रहः
अविग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विग्रह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=083" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्न
अविघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>Unimpeded, uninterrupted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विघ्न obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचक्षण
अविचक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unlearned, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विचक्षण learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचार|अविचारः
अविचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Undiscriminating, ill-judging, unwise.<BR>2 Prompt, unhesitating.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Want of judgment or discrimination, error, folly.<BR>2 Promptitude.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विचार discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारित|अविचारितः
अविचारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ill-judged or investigated, unconsidered.<BR>2 Determined, certain, clear, not requiring deliberation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विचारित discussed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचालित
अविचालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Victorious, triumphant.<BR>2 Unmoved.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विचालित shaken, resisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्युत
अविच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undeviated from, observed, followed.<BR>2 Eternal, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विच्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविछिन्न|अविच्छिन्न|अविच्छिन्नं
अविछिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Unseparated, undivided.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विछिन्न cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविछेद|अविच्छेद|अविच्छेदः
अविछेद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Entire, whole, undivided.<BR>2 Uninterrupted.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Entireness.<BR>2 Connexion, continuity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विछेद separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजातीय
अविजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of the same species.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विजातीय of a different kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञ|अविज्ञः
अविज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Clumsy, stupid.<BR>2 Ignorant, untaught.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विज्ञ wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञता
अविज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ignorance, fully.<BR>E.<BR>अविज्ञ, and तल् affix; also अविज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञात
अविज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unknown.<BR>2 Undistinguished.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञेय|अविज्ञेयं|अविज्ञेयः
अविज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undiscernible, not to be recognised or known.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विज्ञेय to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविडीन|अविडीनं
अविडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A direct flight.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विडीन flying deviously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित|अवितं
अवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Preserved, protected.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, क्त affix of part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथ|अवितथं
अवितथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>True.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Truth.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and वितथ untrue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्त
अवित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Unknown.<BR>2 Poor.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वित्त known, or wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यज|अवित्यजं|अवित्यजः
अवित्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथ्य
अविथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>Fit for or suited to a sheep.<BR>E.<BR>अवि and थ्यन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदग्ध
अविदग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Unlearned.<BR>2 Stupid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विदग्ध clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदाहिन्
अविदाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Imperfectly digested, producing heartburn.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वि free from, दाहिन् what burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदित|अविदितः
अविदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unknown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विदित known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूर
अविदूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Near, contiguous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विदूर distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूरतस्
अविदूरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Near, not far off.<BR>E.<BR>अविदूर and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूस|अविदूसं
अविदूस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The milk of a ewe.<BR>E.<BR>अवि and दूस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्धकर्णा
अविद्धकर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विद्ध broken, divided, and कर्ण the ear; the leaf being compared to the ear; also अविद्धकर्णी and विद्धकर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्य|अविद्यः
अविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Foolish, unwise.<BR>2 Not relating to knowledge.<BR>f. (द्या)<BR>1 Ignorance.<BR>2 Spiritual ignorance.<BR>3 Illusion.<BR>4 Personified illusion or Māyā.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्यमान|अविद्यमानः
अविद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Non-existent.<BR>2 Not present, absent.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विद्यमान being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्वस्
अविद्वस्<BR>mfn. (-द्वान्-टुषी-द्वः)<BR>Unwise, unlearned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विद्वस् learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधान
अविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Irregularity, deviation from or absence of fixed rule.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विधान rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधानतस्
अविधानतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Irregularly.<BR>E.<BR>अविधान and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधि|अविधिः
अविधि<BR>mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>Irregular, void of or contrary to rule.<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Irregularity.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविन|अविनः
अविन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sacrificer, one who makes a sacrifice or causes it to be made.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, इनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनय|अविनयः
अविनय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Indecorous, ill-behaved^1.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Indecorum, impropriety, fault.<BR>2 Incivility, disrespect.<BR>3 Offence, crime.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विनय modest behaviour.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनश्वर|अविनश्वरः
अविनश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Indestructible: so अविनाश्य.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विनश्वर destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाभाव|अविनाभावः
अविनाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Inherent and essential character.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विना without, भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिगम|अविनिगमः
अविनिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An illogical conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विनिगम accurate deduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिवर्त्तिन्|अविनिवर्तिन्
अविनिवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिणी-र्त्ति)<BR>Holding on, advancing, one who does not turn back.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विनिवर्त्तिन् who retreats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिर्मोक
अविनिर्मोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Without an exception.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विनिर्मोक exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीत|अविनीतः
अविनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Misbehaving, acting ill or improperly, wicked, vile.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An unchaste or disloyal woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विनीत virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्ष
अविपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Unopposed, having no adversary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपक्ष an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपट|अविपटः
अविपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Wollen cloth.<BR>E.<BR>अवि a sheep, and पटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपद्
अविपद्<BR>f. (-पत्)<BR>Prosperity, ease.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपद् misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपन्न
अविपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>2 Not soiled or contaminated, pure, clean.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपन्न destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपश्चिद्
अविपश्चिद्<BR>mfn. (-श्चित्)<BR>Unwise, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपश्चिद् learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपाक|अविपाकः
अविपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Immaturity.<BR>2 Not suffering the consequence of actions in a former life.<BR>3 Indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपुल
अविपुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Small, insignificant, slender.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विपुल large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्रकृष्ट
अविप्रकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Near, not remote.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विप्रकृष्ट remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्लुत
अविप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undeviating, following or observing steadily.<BR>2 Observed, unviolated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विप्लुत transgressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविफल
अविफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fruitful, productive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विफल unfruitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविफुल्ल
अविफुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Unblown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विफुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभक्त|अविभक्तः
अविभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Undivided, unpartitioned.<BR>2 Joint, unseparated, (as coparceners.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभक्त divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाग|अविभागः
अविभाग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Unportioned, unpartitioned.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Undivided inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=084" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभागिन्
अविभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 One who does not share.<BR>2 Not sharing, not dividing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभागिन् who divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्य|अविभाज्यं
अविभाज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Not to be divided, not to be partitioned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभाज्य particle^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्यत्व
अविभाज्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Indivisibility, unfitness for partition.<BR>E.<BR>अविभाज्य and त्व affix; also with तल्, अविभाज्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावन|अविभावनं
अविभावन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Disappearance, imperceptibility.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभावन perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनीय
अविभावनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Imperceptible, undistinguishable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विभावनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमरीस|अविमरीसं
अविमरीस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The milk of a ewe.<BR>E.<BR>अवि and मरीसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमल
अविमल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Foul, turbid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विमल clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्त|अविमुक्तं|अविमुक्तः
अविमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unloosed, not quitted.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A name of Benares.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and विमुक्त loosed: the last is never to be lost view of by those seeking salvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्तेश्वर|अविमुक्तेश्वरः
अविमुक्तेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A celebrated Śiva Liṅga, at Benares.<BR>E.<BR>अविमुक्त, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियुक्त
अवियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Undivided, conjoined.<BR>2 Not separated or absent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वियुक्त disjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोग|अवियोगः
अवियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Conjunction, association.<BR>2 Presence, not being parted or absent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वियोग disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरक्त
अविरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Interested in, attached to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरक्त unattached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरत|अविरतं
अविरत<BR>adj. mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eternal, continual, uninterrupted.<BR>2 Abandoned, or<BR>adv. n. (-तं)<BR>Eternal, continual.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरत, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरल|अविरलं
अविरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Coarse, gross, substantial.<BR>2 Close, contiguous.<BR>3 Uninterrupted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and विरल fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराम|अविरामः
अविराम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Continuous, uninterrupted.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Continuance, Uninterrupted succession.<BR>n. adv. (-मं)<BR>Uninterruptedly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विराम rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरुद्ध
अविरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>2 Allowed, permitted, proper.<BR>3 Compatible, consistent with.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरुद्ध hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेचन|अविरेचनं
अविरेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Constipating, stopping dejection.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरेचन purging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेच्य
अविरेच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Improper to be purged.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरेच्य to be purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोध|अविरोधः
अविरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Absence of impediment.<BR>2 Assent, concurrence, non-opposition.<BR>3 Consistency, compatibility.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरोध hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोधित
अविरोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unimpeded, unobstructed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विरोधित hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घन|अविलंघनं
अविलङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not exceeding, not trespassing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विलङ्घन trespassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलङ्घनीय|अविलंघनीय
अविलङ्घनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Prescribed, fixed, not to be transgressed or exceeded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विलङ्घनीय to be passed over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्ब|अविलंब|अविलम्बः
अविलम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>Prompt, quick, without delay.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विलम्ब delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बन|अविलम्बनं
अविलम्बन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Quick, expeditious: also अविलम्बित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बित|अविलंबित|अविलम्बितं|अविलम्बितः
अविलम्बित<BR>mfn. adj. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>Quickly, expeditiously.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and विलम्बित slow, tedious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलम्बितक्रम
अविलम्बितक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Going quickly, a swift pace.<BR>E.<BR>अविलम्बित and क्रम motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविला
अविला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sheep, a ewe.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विल to break, अच् and टाप् affixes; not able to wound, &c. having no horns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलास|अविलासः
अविलास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Faithful, constant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विलास sport, caprice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवक्षित
अविवक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unasserted, undeclared.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विवक्षित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाद|अविवादः
अविवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Concurrence, consent, non-disagreement.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादिन्
अविवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Quiet, peaceable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विवादिन् contentious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहित|अविवाहितः
अविवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unmarried.<BR>E.<BR>अ and विवाहित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहिन्
अविवाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Interdicted as to marriage.<BR>2 Not relating to marriage.<BR>3 Single, not marrying.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विवाहिन् marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविविक्त
अविविक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Uninvestigated, undiscriminated.<BR>2 Indiscriminate, confounded.<BR>3 Common, public.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विविक्त discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेक|अविवेकः
अविवेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Ignorance, absence of discrimination or judgment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and विवेक discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकता
अविवेकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Inconsiderateness, imprudence, want of judgment.<BR>E.<BR>अविवेक and तल् added: also अविवेकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकिन्
अविवेकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Ignorant, undiscriminating, defective in judgment, superficial, short sighted.<BR>E.<BR>अविवेक as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचक|अविवेचकः
अविवेचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Ignorant, undiscriminating.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विवेचक who judges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेचना
अविवेचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Want of judgment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विवेचन discriminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्का
अविशङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>Unapprehensiveness, confidence, certainty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विशङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशङ्कित|अविशंकित
अविशङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Confiding, trusting, unapprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विशङ्कित alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशुद्ध
अविशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pure, clear, free from fault or defect.<BR>2 Valid, perfect, unimpeached.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विशुद्ध faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेष|अविशेषः
अविशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Uniform, alike, without any difference.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Equality, uniformity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विशेष variation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेषज्ञ
अविशेषज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Indiscriminating, not perceiving the difference in things.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विशेष, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रान्त|अविश्रांत|अविश्रान्तः
अविश्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Unwearied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विश्रान्त tired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वस्त|अविश्वस्तः
अविश्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Suspected, doubted, not trusted.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and विश्वस्त trusted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वास|अविश्वासः
अविश्वास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Mistrusted.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Suspicion, mistrust.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विश्वास trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासा
अविश्वासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A cow calving after long intervals.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विश्वास trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासिन्
अविश्वासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Mistrustful, unbelieving.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विश्वासिन् who trusts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष|अविषः
अविष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Anti-venomous, antidote, not poisonous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and विष poison.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The ocean, sky.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 Heaven.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, &c. टिषच Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=085" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषक्त
अविषक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unchecked, unopposed, unimpeded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विषक्त restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषय|अविषयः
अविषय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Unperceived, invisible.<BR>2 Insensible, disregarding objects of sense.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Disappearance, absence.<BR>2 Disregard of objects of sense.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विषय an object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्
अविस्<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>An extender or enlarger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसर्गिन्
अविसर्गिन्<BR>mfn. (र्गी-र्गिणी-र्गि)<BR>Adhering to, retaining, not quitting.<BR>m. (-र्गी)<BR>A continued fever.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विसर्गिन quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसोढ|अविसोढं
अविसोढ<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>Ewe's milk.<BR>E.<BR>अवि and सोढ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तृत
अविस्तृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compact, compressed, close.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विस्तृत spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्ट|अविस्पष्टं
अविस्पष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Obscure, not clear or plain.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Indistinct speech.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विस्पष्ट plain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्मरण
अविस्मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Remembering, not forgetting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विस्मरण forgetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्मृति
अविस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Remembering, recollection.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विस्मृति forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहित
अविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Undone, uneffected.<BR>2 Unprescribed, not directed or ruled.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विहित established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्नल
अविह्नल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Calm, composed, unagitated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विह्नल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवी
अवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A woman in her courses: see अवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीक्षण
अवीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Not regarding, not looking at.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वीक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीक्षित
अवीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unseen, unbeheld.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वीक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचि|अवीचिः
अवीचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A hell.<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Waveless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वीचि a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचिमय|अवीचिमयः
अवीचिमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A hell, the place of punishment for liars.<BR>E.<BR>अवीचि without waves, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीज|अवीजः
अवीज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Seedless.<BR>n. (जं)<BR>Bad seed.<BR>2 Absence of seed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजक
अवीजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Seedless.<BR>E.<BR>अवीज and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर|अवीरः
अवीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Weak, impotent, helpless.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A woman who has neither husband nor son.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वीर strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत
अवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unselected.<BR>2 Uncovered.<BR>3 Unprotected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वृत chosen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत्ति|अवृत्तिः
अवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Inadequate support, absence of subsistence or allowance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथा
अवृथा<BR>ind.<BR>Successfully, profitably.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, वृथा vainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथार्थ
अवृथार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Succeeding, gaining one's object.<BR>E.<BR>अवृथा not in vain, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृद्धिक
अवृद्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Not bearing interest.<BR>2 Not augmentative.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वृद्धि increase, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षण|अवेक्षणं
अवेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Seeing.<BR>2 Attention, observation.<BR>E.<BR>अव and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षमाण
अवेक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Inspecting, examining.<BR>E.<BR>अव, ईक्ष to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षा
अवेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Attention, observation.<BR>2 Seeing, looking at.<BR>3 Agreement, engagement.<BR>E.<BR>अव upon or to, ईक्ष to see, अ affix, and टाप् feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षित|अवेक्षितं
अवेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, regarded.<BR>E.<BR>अव before ईक्ष and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदयान
अवेदयान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Not enquiring or ascertaining.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विद to know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविद्
अवेदविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>A Brahman who has not studied the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वेद and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदविहित
अवेदविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unscriptural, not enjoined in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वेद and विहित declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्य|अवेद्यः
अवेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 Unascertainable, secret, not to be known.<BR>2 Not to be pained or hurt.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वेद्य to be hurt or known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेल|अवेलः
अवेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Chewed betel.<BR>E.<BR>अव and इला speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैध|अवैधं
अवैध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>Irregular, heterodox, contrary or not conformable to rule.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. विधि rule, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोद|अवोदं|अवोदः
अवोद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Wet, moist.<BR>E.<BR>अव ill, उन्द to moisten, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्द
अव्द<BR>m. (-व्दः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A year.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, दन् Uṇādi affix, see अब्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं|अव्यक्तः
अव्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Indistinct, unapparent, invisible, imperceptible.<BR>2 In algebra, unknown as quantity or number.<BR>m. (क्त)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 KANDARPA or CUPID.<BR>4 A fool.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 The Supreme Being or universal spirit.<BR>2 Any invisible principle according to the Sāṃkhya philosophy.<BR>3 The soul.<BR>4 Nature, temperament.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यक्त evident, distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तक्रिया
अव्यक्तक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Algebraic calculation.<BR>2 Any act of an indistinct character or aim.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यक्त and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराग|अव्यक्तरागः
अव्यक्तराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Dark-red, the colour of the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यक्त indistinct, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तराशि|अव्यक्तराशिः
अव्यक्तराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>An unknown number or indistinct quantity, (in algebra.)<BR>E.<BR>अव्यक्त and राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्तसाम्य
अव्यक्तसाम्य<BR>n. (म्यं)<BR>Equation of unknown quantities.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यक्त and साम्य equality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्र
अव्यग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Steady, cool, deliberate.<BR>2 Indifferent, undisturbed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यग्र hurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्ग|अव्यंग|अव्यङ्गः
अव्यङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Plain, not figurative.<BR>2 Perfect, not mutilated.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. वि priv. and अङ्ग the body, or व्यङ्ग figure of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यङ्गाङ्ग
अव्यङ्गाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Well made, symmetrical, perfect, entire.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यङ्ग not defective, अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यञ्जन|अव्यंजन|अव्यञ्जनः
अव्यञ्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Indistinct.<BR>2 Plain, not figurative.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An animal without horns, though of an age to have them. अ neg. व्यञ्जन a mark or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यण्डा|अव्यंडा
अव्यण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A plant, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिकीर्ण|अव्यतिकीर्ण्ण
अव्यतिकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Distinct, specific, separate, unmixed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यतिकीर्ण confounded, mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ|अव्यथः
अव्यथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Free from pain.<BR>2 Merciful, not inflicting pain.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A snake.<BR>f. (-था)<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>2 Another plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.) See पद्मचारिणी.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथि|अव्यथिः
अव्यथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>A horse, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg, व्यथ to pain, and इन् affix; who does not tire in war, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिधी
अव्यथिधी<BR>m. (-धीः)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिन्
अव्यथिन्<BR>mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>Free from pain.<BR>2 Not inflicting pain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यथा pain, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=086" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिष|अव्यथिषः
अव्यथिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यथ to suffer pain, and टिषच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ्य|अव्यथ्यः
अव्यथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>1 Free from pain.<BR>2 Not paining, not giving pain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यथ to feel pain, and क्यप् affix irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचार|अव्यभिचारः
अव्यभिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Steadiness, consistency, constancy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg व्यभिचार irregularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारिन्
अव्यभिचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Constant.<BR>2 Virtuous, moral.<BR>3 Steady, permanent, faithful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यभिचारिन् variable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यय|अव्ययं|अव्ययः
अव्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Economical, parsimonious.<BR>2 Unexpended, unwasted.<BR>3 Imperishable, immutable, eternal.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>An indeclinable word, a particle.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and व्यय expenditure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययात्मन्
अव्ययात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Eternal, imperishable.<BR>m. (त्मा)<BR>Soul, spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यय undecayed, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययीभाव|अव्ययीभावः
अव्ययीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Imperishableness.<BR>2 An indeclinable compound.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यय and भाव disposition, with च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यर्थ|अव्यर्थः
अव्यर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Profitable, fruitful.<BR>2 Effectual, efficacious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यर्थ useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यलीक
अव्यलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>True, veracious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यलीक false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधान
अव्यवधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Close, contiguous.<BR>2 Careless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवधान any thing interposed, or carefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधानता
अव्यवधानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Contiguity.<BR>2 Carelessness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to with the last; also with त्व, अव्यवधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसाय|अव्यवसायः
अव्यवसाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Negligence, inactivity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवसाय employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायवत्|अव्यवसायवन्त्
अव्यवसायवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Negligent, remiss in practice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवसाय practice, profession, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवसायिन्
अव्यवसायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Negligent, inactive, remiss.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवसाय business, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्था
अव्यवस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Irregularity, deviation from established rule.<BR>2 Incorrect legal opinion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवस्था law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थित|अव्यवस्थितः
अव्यवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not conformable to law or practice.<BR>2 Unacquainted with the law or custom.<BR>3 Ill regulated.<BR>4 Displaced, disordered.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and व्यवस्थित ordained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहार्य्य|अव्यवहार्य|अव्यवहार्य्यं
अव्यवहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Unactionable, not to be discussed in law.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवहार्य्य actionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहित|अव्यवहितं
अव्यवहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Adjoining, contiguous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and व्यवहित divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहृत|अव्यवहृतः
अव्यवहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not determined or investigated by law.<BR>2 Not spoken.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यवहृत tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसन
अव्यसन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Moral, correct, free from vice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यसन evil practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसनिन्
अव्यसनिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Free from evil practices, steady, correct.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यसन evil practices, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यस्त
अव्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Simple, undecomposed.<BR>2 Undispersed, collected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यस्त scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकुल
अव्याकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Calm, firm, composed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याकुल flurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकृत
अव्याकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undecomposed, simple.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Elementary substance from which all things were created, considered as one with the substance of BRAHMA.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याकृत separated, decomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्या
अव्याख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>Obscurity, want of clearness or explanation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. आख्या explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यात
अव्याख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unexplained, obscure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याख्यात explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यान|अव्याख्यानं
अव्याख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Absence of explicitness, want of explanation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याख्यान explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्येय
अव्याख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Unintelligible, inexplicable.<BR>2 Easy, not requiring to be explained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याख्येय to be explained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याज|अव्याजं|अव्याजः
अव्याज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Absence of fraud, simplicity, honesty.<BR>E.<BR>अ, and व्याज disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापक
अव्यापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Special, individual, peculiar.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यापक generick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापकत्व
अव्यापकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Speciality, individuality, non-comprehensiveness or generalization.<BR>E.<BR>अव्यापक special, and त्व affix; also अव्यापकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापार|अव्यापारः
अव्यापार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Inexpert, inexperienced.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Business not practised or understood.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, व्यापार business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापित्व
अव्यापित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Speciality, non-generalization.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यापिन् what pervades, त्व affix; also अव्यापिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापिन्
अव्यापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>1 Special, individual.<BR>2 Limited, partial, not comprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यापिन् pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्त
अव्याप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Peculiar, individual, limited.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याप्त diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्य|अव्याप्यं
अव्याप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Peculiar, not to be extended generally.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याप्य to be extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्यष्टत्ति
अव्याप्यष्टत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः)<BR>In logic, A category of individual application, and influenced by place and time, as pain, pleasure, love, hatred, virtue, vice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याप्य diffusive, general, and वृत्ति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायाम|अव्यायामः
अव्यायाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Absence of lassitude or fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यायाम exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यावर्त्तन|अव्यावर्तन
अव्यावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Not returning, not coming back, not circulating.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्यावर्त्तन returning, revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहत|अव्याहतं
अव्याहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unresisted, unimpeded.<BR>2 Not disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याहत baffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहित
अव्याहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undisputed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्याहित disputed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रण
अव्रण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Sound, unhurt, unscarred.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्रण a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत
अव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not observing religious rites or obligations, uninitiated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. व्रत a vow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश
अश<BR>r. 5th cl. (ऊ.) अशू (अश्नुते)<BR>1 To pervade or occupy.<BR>2 To heap or crowd.<BR>r. 9th cl. (अश्नाति)<BR>To eat, to eat hungrily.<BR>With प्र prefixed,<BR>to begin to eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्त|अशक्तं
अशक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unable, incompetent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शक्त able, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्तता
अशक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Weakness, inability.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, अशक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्ति|अशक्तिः
अशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Inability, incapability, weakness, impotence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्य|अशक्यं
अशक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>1 Impossible, impracticable.<BR>2 Not to be made.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शक्य possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्क|अशंक
अशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>1 Fearless, undaunted.<BR>2 Secure, certain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=087" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशङ्कित|अशंकित
अशङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Certain, undoubted.<BR>2 Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शङ्कित alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशठ
अशठ<BR>mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>Virtuous, good.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शठ wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रु|अशत्रुः
अशत्रु<BR>mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु)<BR>Friendly.<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A name of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and शत्रु an enemy; who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन|अशनं|अशनः
अशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, (Pentaptera tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Eating: also असन.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनपर्णी
अशनपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant: also असनपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनाया
अशनाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>अशन food, क्यच् affix, अ and टाप् added, and the penultimate made long: wishing for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायित|अशनायितं
अशनायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungry.<BR>E.<BR>as before इतच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनि|अशनिः
अशनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, अनि Uṇādi affix; what eats or consumes rocks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीर|अशरीरः
अशरीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Bodiless, incorporeal.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरिन्
अशरीरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Incorporeal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शरीरिन् embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशर्म्मन्|अशर्मन्
अशर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Pain, affliction.<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Unhappy, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>शर्म्मन् happiness, &c. with the priv. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशान्त|अशांत
अशान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Restless, anxious, unresigned.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शान्त tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशान्ति
अशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Anxiety, restlessness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शान्ति tranquillity. So अशान्तता f. (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाम्य
अशाम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Unappeasable, not to be pacified.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शम to appease, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशारीरिक
अशारीरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Not relating to or endowed with body.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शरीरिक bodily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाश्चत
अशाश्चत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perishable, transient, temporary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शाश्वत eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासन
अशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Want of government, anarchy, disorder.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शासन governing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासनीय
अशासनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Ungovernable: so अशास्य.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शासनीय or शास्य to be ruled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासित
अशासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ungoverned, undisciplined.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शासित governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्र
अशास्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Not conform able to sacred authority, heterodox, unscriptural.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शास्त्र scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रीय
अशास्त्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not conformable to sacred authority, heterodox, immoral, irreligious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शास्त्रीय scriptural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिक्षित|अशिक्षितं
अशिक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Untaught, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिक्षित taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित|अशितं
अशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितङ्गवीन|अशितंगवीन|अशितङ्गवीनं
अशितङ्गवीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Formerly grazed by cattle, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अशित eaten, and गवीन relating to cattle; also आशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित्र|अशित्रः
अशित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>अशू to pervade, इत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिथिल
अशिथिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Firm, tight, hard.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिथिल loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिर|अशिरं|अशिरः
अशिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of the sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A goblin or demon.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The wife of a goblin.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A diamond.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, and इर affix; what eats sacrifices, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्
अशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Headless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरःस्नान
अशिरःस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bathing the body with exception of the head.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिरस् the head, स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिव|अशिवः
अशिव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Unlucky, unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिव propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिवी
अशिवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A female demon or goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्विका
अशिश्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the following.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to अशिश्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिश्वी
अशिश्वी<BR>f. (-श्वी)<BR>A childless woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. शिशु a child, and ङीप् fem. affix; उ becomes व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ट
अशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ill regulated, ill behaved, rude, barbarous, profligate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शिष्ट regulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्टता
अशिष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rudeness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, अशिष्टत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्टाचार
अशिष्टाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rudeness, profligacy.<BR>E.<BR>अशिष्ट, and आचार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अशीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Warm, hot.<BR>E.<BR>अ not, शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतकर|अशीतकरः
अशीतकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शीत cold, and कर a ray, and similar compounds, as अशीतदीधिति, अशीतमरीचि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीति|अशीतिः
अशीति<BR>f. sing. always. (-तिः)<BR>Eighty.<BR>du. (-तीः)<BR>Two eighties.<BR>pl. (-तयः)<BR>Many eighties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिक
अशीतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Octagenarian, of eighty years of age, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अशीति and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीर्ण
अशीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Undecayed, unimpaired.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शीर्ण decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशील
अशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Ill behaved, vulgar, offensive.<BR>2 Indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शील polite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुष्क
अशुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Green, fresh, moist.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचि|अशुचिः
अशुचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>1 Impurity.<BR>2 Disgrace, degradation.<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Foul, impure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शुचि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचित्व
अशुचित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Impurity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अशुचि; also अशुचिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्ध|अशुद्धं
अशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Impure.<BR>2 Inaccurate.<BR>3 Unknown, unascertained.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धवासक|अशुद्धवासकः
अशुद्धवासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vagrant, a suspicious character.<BR>E.<BR>अशुद्ध unknown, वास abode, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धि|अशुद्धिः
अशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Impurity.<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Impure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभ|अशुभं
अशुभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Misfortune.<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. शुभ good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुश्रूषा
अशुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Inattention, neglect of service or respect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशृत|अशृतं
अशृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unripe.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and शृत ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेष|अशेषं|अशेषः
अशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Entire, all, the whole.<BR>2 Infinite, endless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषतस्
अशेषतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Entirely, wholly.<BR>E.<BR>अशेष whole, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोक|अशोकं|अशोकः
अशोक<BR>m. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Cheerful, not sorrowful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, commonly Aśoka, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, see कटुकी.<BR>2 One of the female domestic deities of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोकरोहिणी
अशोकरोहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A medicinal plant, see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>अशोक, and रोहिणी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोकारि|अशोकारिः
अशोकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A tree, (Nauclea Cadamba): see कदम्ब.<BR>E.<BR>अशोक, and अरि an enemy: choking the Aśoca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोच|अशोचः
अशोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>Content, tranquillity, the absence of care or vanity.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. शोच sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=088" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोच्य|अशोच्यं
अशोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Not to be sorrowed for.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शोच्य to be regretted; also अशोचनीय and अशोचितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधन
अशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Uncleanness.<BR>2 Inaccuracy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शोधन cleaning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधित
अशोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unclean, uncleansed.<BR>2 Inaccurate, unrevised, uncorrected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शोधित purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोष्य
अशोष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Not to be dried up.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शौष्य to be dried up; so अशोषणीय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौच|अशौचं
अशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Foulness, impurity.<BR>2 Legal impurity, contamination, defilement contracted by the death of a relation, the commission of prohibited acts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शौच purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौचत्व
अशौचत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Impure or abandoned nature or disposition.<BR>2 Defilement, contamination.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अशौच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौर्प्य
अशौर्प्य<BR>n. (-र्प्यं)<BR>Want of heroism, cowardice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. शौर्य्यं valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्म|अश्मः
अश्म<BR>m. (-श्मः)<BR>1 A mountain, a rock.<BR>2 A cloud, (in the language of the Vedas): see अश्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मकुट्ट|अश्मकुट्टः
अश्मकुट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः-ट्टा-ट्टं)<BR>Who or what breaks with a stone.<BR>2 Bruised or broken by stones.<BR>E.<BR>अश्म and कुट्ठ what bruises or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मकुट्टक|अश्मकुट्टकः
अश्मकुट्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-क्रं)<BR>Breaking or bruising any thing with a stone.<BR>E.<BR>अश्म and कुदृक who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मगर्भ|अश्मगर्भः
अश्मगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, and गर्भ the womb; the primary stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मगर्भज|अश्मगर्भजं|अश्मगर्भजः
अश्मगर्भज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>अश्म and गर्म्भ before ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मज|अश्मजं|अश्मजः
अश्मज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Red chalk.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, &c. and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मजतुक|अश्मजतुकं
अश्मजतुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>अश्म and जतुक lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मदारण|अश्मदारणः
अश्मदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An axe or crow for breaking stones, &c.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Splitting stones or rocks.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, &c. द to split, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
अश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>A stone or rock.<BR>E.<BR>अश to spread, &c. मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्त|अश्मंत|अश्मन्तं|अश्मन्तः
अश्मन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Unbounded, unlimited.<BR>2 Inauspicious, unlucky.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 A fire-place.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 A field, a plain.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, &c. and अन्त the end; it is also written अश्वन्त and अस्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्तक|अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मन्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A fire-place.<BR>2 A shade for a lamp.<BR>3 A species of oxalis.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मपुष्प|अश्मपुष्पं
अश्मपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Benzoin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, and षुष्प a flower: supposed to exude from rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभाल|अश्मभालं
अश्मभाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A mortar of stone or iron.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, and भाल the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभिद्
अश्मभिद्<BR>m. (-द्)<BR>The name of a plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन a stone, and भिद् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मभेद|अश्मभेदः
अश्मभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, अश्मन् and भेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ममय
अश्ममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or consisting of stone, stony.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A mineral.<BR>E.<BR>अश्म and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मयोनि|अश्मयोनिः
अश्मयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>see अश्मगर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मर|अश्मरः
अश्मर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Stony, rocky, appertaining to stone or rock.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरी
अश्मरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Strangury.<BR>2 Stone or gravel, (the disease.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्मर stony, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरीघ्न|अश्मरीघ्नः
अश्मरीघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A tree, (Tapia cratoeva.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्मरी gravel, and घ्न what destroys; a lithonthriptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरीहर|अश्मरीहरः
अश्मरीहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>see the last word, हर from हृ to carry away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मसार|अश्मसारः
अश्मसार<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, and सार essence, &c. the hardest stone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मान्तक
अश्मान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, from the fibres of which the girdle of a Brahman may be made; also अश्मन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मीर|अश्मीरं|अश्मीरः
अश्मीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Stone or gravel, (the disease.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् a stone, ईर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्र|अश्रं|अश्रः
अश्र<BR>n. (-श्रं)<BR>1 A tear.<BR>2 Blood.<BR>E.<BR>अश्रू to spread, &c. and र affix: see अश्रु and अस्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्ध
अश्रद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Unbelieving.<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>Unbelief.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रद्धा faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धधान
अश्रद्धधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unbelieving, incredulous, having no faith.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रद्धधान believing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धेय|अश्रद्धेयं
अश्रद्धेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Incredible, not to be believed.<BR>E.<BR>अ and श्रद्धेय worthy of faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रप|अश्रपः
अश्रप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A fiend, a cannibal.<BR>E.<BR>अश्र blood, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रवण|अश्रवणः
अश्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Deafness, loss of hearing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रवण hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रम|अश्रमः
अश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Freshness, freedom from fatigue.<BR>2 Laziness, want of exertion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राद्ध|अश्राद्धः
अश्राद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Not performing exequial rites, not entitled to them, not belonging or relating to them.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>Nonperformance of exequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्राद्ध funereal ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रान्त|अश्रांत|अश्रान्तं|अश्रान्तः
अश्रान्त<BR>adv. n. (-न्तं) adj. mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Eternal, continual.<BR>2 Unwearied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and श्रान्त wearied, part. past. of श्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रि|अश्रिः
अश्रि<BR>f. (-श्रिः)<BR>1 The edge of a sword.<BR>2 A corner, the angle of a room or house.<BR>E.<BR>श्रिञ to serve, आङ् prefixed, आ becomes अ; also अश्री and आश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीक
अश्रीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unlucky, unpropitious.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्री fortune, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीमत्|अश्रीमन्त्
अश्रीमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Inglorious, unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रीमत् fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रील
अश्रील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unlucky, unprosperous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्री prosperity, ला to have, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रु
अश्रु<BR>n. (-श्रु)<BR>A tear.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रि to serve, डुन् Uṇādi affix; it is also written अश्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुत|अश्रुतं
अश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unheard.<BR>2 Not directed by or contrary to the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अ and श्रुत heard, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुनाली
अश्रुनाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Fistula lacrymalis.<BR>E.<BR>अश्रु and नाली a channel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुपात|अश्रुपातः
अश्रुपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A flow of tears.<BR>E.<BR>अश्रु, and पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेयस्
अश्रेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Worthless, useless, unprofitable, bad.<BR>2 Inferior, worse.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रेयस् excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेष्ठ
अश्रेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठ)<BR>1 Inferior, worse.<BR>2 Bad, vile.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रोत्रिय
अश्रोत्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Brahman who has not read the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्रोत्रिय a learned Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघ्य
अश्लाघ्य<BR>mfn. (-घ्यः-घ्या-घ्यं)<BR>Worthless, undeserving of honour or praise.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्लाघ्य to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघनीय
अश्लाघनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undeserving of honour or praise, base, mean, worthless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्लाघनीय to be praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=089" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लीक
अश्लीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unlucky, unpropitious.<BR>E.<BR>as अश्रीक, the र being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लील
अश्लील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Coarse, vulgar.<BR>2 Abusive, blackguard.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Rustic language.<BR>2 Untruth.<BR>3 Low abuse.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्लील elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषा
अश्लेषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 The ninth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, containing five stars.<BR>2 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and श्लष union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषाभव|अश्लेषाभवः
अश्लेषाभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of KETU or the dragon's head: see केतु.<BR>E.<BR>अश्लेषा the asterism, and भव born, born under the sign Aśleṣā; or अश्लेषा disjunction, and भव produced; as KETU was formed of the lower extremities which had been sundered by VIṢṆU from RĀHU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषाभू
अश्लेषाभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A name of KETU.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding, भू to be born, with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व|अश्वः
अश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A set or cast of men horse-like in strength.<BR>(-श्वौ)<BR>A horse and a mare.<BR>f. (-श्वा)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>अश to pervade, क्वन Uṇādi affix, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वक|अश्वकः
अश्वक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Horse-like, acting like a horse, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bad horse, a hack.<BR>2 A stray horse, one whose owner is not known.<BR>3 Any horse.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and कन् added in different senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकन्दिका
अश्वकन्दिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकर्ण|अश्वकर्णः|अश्वकर्ण्ण
अश्वकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A timber tree, commonly Sākva or Śāl, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व a horse, and कर्ण an ear, the leaves being compared to the ears of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकर्णक|अश्वकर्णकः
अश्वकर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Śāl-tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to अश्वकर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वकिनी
अश्वकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The first Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वक a horse, इनि and ङीप् affixes: see अश्विनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वखुर|अश्वखुरः
अश्वखुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A horse's hoof.<BR>2 A perfume, apparently a dried shell-fish: see नखी.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>A plant, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and खुर his hoof: which the perfume and leaves of the plant are supposed to resemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगन्धा
अश्वगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, and गन्ध smell; having the smell of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगोयुग|अश्वगोयुगं|अश्वगोयुगः
अश्वगोयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A pair of horses.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and गोयुगच् affix implying a pair, a brace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वगोष्ठ|अश्वगोष्ठं
अश्वगोष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A stable.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, and गोष्ठ abode, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वग्रीव|अश्वग्रीवः
अश्वग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The name of a demon, more commonly named Hayagrīva.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and ग्रीवा a neck; horse-necked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वघ्न|अश्वघ्नः
अश्वघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Oleander, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and घ्न what kills or hurts, from हन; horse-destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वचिकित्सक|अश्वचिकित्सकः
अश्वचिकित्सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A farrier.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and चिकित्सक who heals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वचिकित्सा
अश्वचिकित्सा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Farriery.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and चिकित्सा medical treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वतर|अश्वतरः
अश्वतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Swift, speedy.<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A mule.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent race, inhabiting the regions under the earth.<BR>2 A Gandharba or celestial quirister.<BR>3 A male calf.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and तर from तृ to pass, to go, affix अप्; or ष्टरच् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थ|अश्वत्थः
अश्वत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>1 The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiousa.)<BR>2 The fruit of the tree.<BR>3 The time at which it bears.<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>Day of fullmoon.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्व a future period, and थ from स्था to remain; of less duration than the Vaṭa or Indian fig; there are several other etymologies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थक|अश्वत्थकः
अश्वत्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>To be given, to be done, &c. when the Aśvattha tree bears.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The petals of the Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वत्थ and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वत्थामन्
अश्वत्थामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The name of a saint and warrior, the son of DROṆA.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, स्था to stand or stay, and मनिन् affix; the story is that at his birth he made a noise like a horse; also with a final vowel अश्वत्थाम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वदंष्ट्रा
अश्वदंष्ट्रा<BR>f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>A plant, (Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वन्त|अश्वंत|अश्वन्तं|अश्वन्तः
अश्वन्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 Termination, limit.<BR>3 A fire-place.<BR>4 A field.<BR>5 Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>E.<BR>अशु vital air, अन्त end; also अश्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वपाल|अश्वपालः
अश्वपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A groom.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, and पाल who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वबाल|अश्वबालः
अश्वबाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>2 Horse hair.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and बाल a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वभा
अश्वभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमहिषिका
अश्वमहिषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The natural enmity of a horse and a buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, महिष a buffalo, वुन् affix of enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमार|अश्वमारः
अश्वमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Oleander, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and मार what kills; the plant is conceived to be deleterious to the horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमारक|अश्वमारकः
अश्वमारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमाल|अश्वमालः
अश्वमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमुख|अश्वमुखः
अश्वमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A Kinnara or celestial quirister.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and मुख a face; this kind of demigod being represented with a horse's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेध|अश्वमेधः
अश्वमेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The actual or emblematic sacrifice of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and मेध sacrifice; this sacrifice is one of the highest order, and performed a hundred times, entitles the sacrificer to the dominion of Svarga or paradise: it appears to have been originally typical; the horse, and other animals being simply bound during the performance of certain ceremonies; the actual sacrifice is an introduction of a later period. See As. R. Vol. viii. p. 442, COLEBROOKE on the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेधिक|अश्वमेधिकः
अश्वमेधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse fit for the sacrifice called Aśvamedha.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वमेध as above, कन् added, and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वमेधीय|अश्वमेधीयः
अश्वमेधीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A horse fit for an Aśvamedha.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वमेध and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वयुज्
अश्वयुज्<BR>f. (-युक्)<BR>The first lunar mansion: see अश्विनी.<BR>m. (-युक् or -युजः)<BR>The month Aśvin, (Sept.-Oct.) see आश्वयुज.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, युज to join, affix क्विप्; also with अ added in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वरक्ष|अश्वरक्षः
अश्वरक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The keeper or rider of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and रक्ष who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वलाल
अश्वलाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of snake.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and लाल spittle, whose foam is like that of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वलोमन्
अश्वलोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>2 Horse hair.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववक्त्र|अश्ववक्त्रः
अश्ववक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A chorister of Svarga, a Kinnara or Gandharba.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and वक्त्र face, horse-faced: these demigods being so represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववडव|अश्ववडवं
अश्ववडव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A stud of horses and mares.<BR>m. du. or plu. only. (-वौ-वाः)<BR>1 A horse and a mare.<BR>2 Horses and mares.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and वडवा a mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=090" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववह|अश्ववहः
अश्ववह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horseman.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and वह what bears; whom a horse carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववार|अश्ववारः
अश्ववार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A horseman.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and वृञ to nourish, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववारण|अश्ववारणः
अश्ववारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The Gayal, a sort of ox, (Bos gavoeus.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, वृ to skreen or hide, in the causal form, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वविद्
अश्वविद्<BR>m. (-वित्)<BR>1 A name of NALA, a king and hero of several poems.<BR>2 A jockey.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ववैद्य|अश्ववैद्यः
अश्ववैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A farrier, a horse doctor.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and वैद्य physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशाला
अश्वशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A stable.<BR>3 A riding house.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशाव|अश्वशावः
अश्वशाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A foal, a colt.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and शाव young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वशृगालिका
अश्वशृगालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The natural enmity between a horse and a jackall.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and शृगाल a jackall, affix वुन् implying hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वषङ्गव
अश्वषङ्गव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A set of six horses.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and षङ्गवच् a set of six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसादिन्
अश्वसादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A horseman, a rider, a horse-soldier.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and सादिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसारथ्य
अश्वसारथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Management of horses and cars, coachmanship, charioteership.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and सारथि a driver, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसेन|अश्वसेनः
अश्वसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A proper name, a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वसेननृपनन्दन|अश्वसेननृपनन्दनः
अश्वसेननृपनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A king and saint; also SANATKUMĀRA.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वसेन a proper name, नृप a king, and नन्दन a son: the son of the king AŚVASENA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तन
अश्वस्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Of to-day, not of or for to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. श्वस् to-morrow, द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तनिक
अश्वस्तनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Not of or for to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वस्तन and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वहारक|अश्वहारकः
अश्वहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse stealer.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and हारक who takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वहृदय
अश्वहृदय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Horsemanship.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and हृदम heart, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारि|अश्वारिः
अश्वारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारूढ|अश्वारूढः
अश्वारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mounted, set on horseback.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारोह|अश्वारोहः
अश्वारोह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Riding or carried on a horse.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horseman.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant; also Aśvagandhā, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and आरोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वावरोहक|अश्वावरोहकः
अश्वावरोहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, अव on, &c. रोहक what grows; growing to the length of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वारोहिन्
अश्वारोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Mounted or riding on horseback.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and आरोहिन् what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विक
अश्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Drawn by horses, carried by horses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and ष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन्<BR>m. du. (-नौ)<BR>The twin sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी and अण् affix, the fem. termination is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनी
अश्विनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The first of the twenty-eight Nakṣatras or constellations in the moon's path, hence considered its mansions.<BR>2 In mythology, a nymph, the asterism personified.<BR>3 The wife of SŪRYA, who concealed herself in the form of a mare.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व a horse, इन् and ङीप् affix; the symbol of the Nakṣatra is a horse's head, figured by three stars in the head of ARIES.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीकुमार
अश्विनीकुमार<BR>m. du. (-रो)<BR>The twin sons of SŪRYA the sun, by his wife SAṂJÑĀ transformed to a mare; they are endowed with perpetual youth and beauty, and are the physicians of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी the wife of SŪRYA, and कुमार a youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीपुत्र
अश्विनीपुत्र<BR>m. du. (-त्रौ)<BR>The Aśvins: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनीसुत
अश्विनीसुत<BR>m. du. (-ता)<BR>The twin sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विसालोक्य
अश्विसालोक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>The heaven or station of the Aśvins, to which the giver of a horse is raised.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विन् and सालोक्य interview.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीन|अश्वीनः
अश्वीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Distant a day's journey for a horse, more usually आश्वीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीय|अश्वीयं|अश्वीयः
अश्वीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a horse.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A number of horses.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वोरस
अश्वोरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Broad chested.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and उरस् the breast, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष
अष<BR>r. 1st cl. (असति-ते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To take or receive.<BR>3 To shine: see अस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीण|अषडक्षीणः
अषडक्षीण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A secret.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. षट six, अक्षि an eye, and ख affix; what is not seen by six eyes, that is, known or determined by two persons to the exclusion of a third.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढ|अषाढः
अषाढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Produced or occurring in the month Āṣārha.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>1 The month Āṣāḍha, commencing with the sun's entrance into Gemini, (June-July.)<BR>2 A student's staff.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A name common to the twentieth and twenty-first lunar mansion: see पूर्ष्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR>E.<BR>see आषाढ, the initial being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढक|अषाढकः
अषाढक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Āṣāḍha; also आषाढक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Eight.<BR>2 Eighth.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The eight sections of PĀṆINI'S Grammar.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The formulae of the Rig Veda as collected into eight portions, thence called Aṣṭakas.<BR>2 One acquainted with PĀṆINI'S rules or the formulae of the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to अष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकर्ण|अष्टकर्णः
अष्टकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and कर्ण an ear; eight-eared, being four-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टका
अष्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Worship of the manes or progenitors performed on certain days.<BR>2 The eighth day of three months on which the progenitors are worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, and तकन् affix; vegetables, flesh, and cake, being severally offered upon these occasions, and the Brahmins feasted; in this sense it is also अष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकाङ्ग|अष्टकांग|अष्टकाङ्गं|अष्टकाङ्गः
अष्टकाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A kind of board or cloth for playing with dice on.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टक eight, and अङ्ग body, having eight divisions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकोण|अष्टकोणः
अष्टकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An octagon.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and कोण angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगाध्
अष्टगाध्<BR>m. (-ट् or -त्)<BR>1 A fabulous animal supposed to have eight legs: see शरभ.<BR>2 A spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगव
अष्टगव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A flock of eight cows.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and गव kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टगुण
अष्टगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Eight fold.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, गुण number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिक्पाल
अष्टदिक्पाल<BR>m. plu. (-लाः)<BR>The regents of the cardinal points, as INDRA of the East; VAHNI of the S. E.; YAMA of the South; NAIRṚTA of the S. W.; VARUṆA of the West; MARUT of the N. W.; KUVERA of the North; and ĪŚA of the N. E.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टदिश् the eight points, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=091" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टदिश्
अष्टदिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्)<BR>The eight cardinal points of the compass collectively.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and दिश् quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टधा<BR>ind.<BR>Eight fold, eight times.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधातु|अष्टधातुः
अष्टधातु<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>The eight metals collectively, as, gold, silver, copper, tin, lead, brass, iron and steel.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन्<BR>mfn. plu. only (अष्ट or अष्टौ)<BR>Eight.<BR>E.<BR>असू to pervade, कनिन Uṇādi affix, and तुद् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टपाद|अष्टपादः
अष्टपाद<BR>m. (-पात् or -पाद्)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 A fabulous animal with eight legs: see शरभ.<BR>(-दः)<BR>A kind of spider with a small body and long legs.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टी
अष्टी<BR>f. (-ष्टी)<BR>A metre consisting of four lines, and having sixteen syllables in each; there are nine species of it.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टन् eight, ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Eighth.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 The eighth day of the fortnight.<BR>2 A medicinal plant: see क्षीरकाकोली, the last of a class of eight medicinal plants: see अष्टवर्ग.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टन् with डट् affix and मट augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमङ्गल|अष्टमंगल|अष्टमङ्गलं|अष्टमङ्गलः
अष्टमङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A horse with a white face, tail, mane, breast, and hoofs.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A collection of eight lucky things to be assembled on certain occasions, as at a coronation, &c. as a lion, a bull, an elephant, a water jar, a fan, a flag, a trumpet, and a lamp; or a Brahman, a cow, fire, gold, ghee, the sun, water, and a king.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमांश|अष्टमांशः
अष्टमांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An eighth.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टम and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमान|अष्टमानं
अष्टमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A measure, one Kuḍava.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमिका
अष्टमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A weight of four tolas.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टम eight, कन् added fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्त्ति|अष्टमूर्ति|अष्टमूर्तिः|अष्टमूर्त्तिः
अष्टमूर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and मूर्त्ति form: evident in the earth, water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमूर्त्तिधर|अष्टमूर्तिधर
अष्टमूर्त्तिधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टमूर्त्ति an assemblage of eight forms, and धर who has, being identical with the five elements and with the mind, individuality and crude matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टलोहक|अष्टलोहकं
अष्टलोहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A class of eight metals: gold, silver, copper, tin, lead, and iron of three sorts, including steel.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, लोहक metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टवर्ग|अष्टवर्गः
अष्टवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A class of eight principal medicaments, they are mostly the roots of plants from the hills, which have not been determined, and are named: Ṛṣabha, Jīvaka, Meda, Mahāmeda, Ṛddhi, Vṛddhi, Kākolī and Kṣīrakākolī.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टविध
अष्टविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Eight fold, of eight kinds.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टश्रवस्
अष्टश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and श्रवस् an ear; eight-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाकपाल|अष्टाकपालः
अष्टाकपाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Prepared in eight pans.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sacrifice in which ghee is offered in eight vessels.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and कपाल the convexity of a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टागव
अष्टागव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A car or wain, one drawn by eight oxen.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and गो a cow, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्ग|अष्टांग
अष्टाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Eight parts of the body, the hands, breast, forehead, eyes, throat and middle of the back; or four first, with the knees and feet; or these six, with the words and mind.<BR>2 Any whole consisting of eight parts or members.<BR>3 The eight parts of a court, or the law, the judge, assessors, scribe and astrologer, gold, fire and water.<BR>3 A die, dice.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गनय
अष्टाङ्गनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>See the above.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टाङ्ग and नय taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गपात|अष्टांगपात
अष्टाङ्गपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Prostration as in reverence.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टाङ्ग eight members, and पात falling, touching the ground^1 with the hands, knees, and feet, forehead and breast.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गप्रणाम|अष्टांगप्रणाम
अष्टाङ्गप्रणाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Profound reverence, prostration with the hands, feet, thighs, breast, eyes, head, words and mind.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टाङ्ग and प्रणाम bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टाङ्गार्घ्य|अष्टाङ्गार्घ्यः
अष्टाङ्गार्घ्य<BR>m. (-र्घ्यः)<BR>An offering of eight articles, water, milk, Kusa grass, curds, ghee rice, barley and mustard: or honey, red oleander flowers, and sandal, are substituted for the three last.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, अङ्ग member, अर्घ्य offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टादशन्<BR>mfn. plu. only (-दश)<BR>Eighteen.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापद|अष्टापदं|अष्टापदः
अष्टापद<BR>mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>1 A kind of chequered cloth or board for drafts, dice, &c.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 A fabulous animal with eight legs, the Śarabha.<BR>3 The mountain Kailāsa or abode of KUVERA.<BR>4 A worm.<BR>5 A pin or bolt.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A wild sort of jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट eight, and पद a quarter, place, foot, &c. अ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापदपत्र
अष्टापदपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>gold leaf, a sheet of gold.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टापद and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टापाद
अष्टापाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Quartered by eight, having eight for the root.<BR>E.<BR>अष्टन् and पाद a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टारचक्रवत्|अष्टारचक्रवन्त्
अष्टारचक्रवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A Jaina saint and ruler.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट, अर a period, and चक्रवत् a ruler; such for eight Aras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्र|अष्टास्रः
अष्टास्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>An octagon.<BR>E.<BR>अष्ट and अस्र angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टास्रय
अष्टास्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Octangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठि|अष्ठिः
अष्ठि<BR>f. (-ष्ठिः)<BR>A kernel, a stone.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्था to remain, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A round pebble or stone.<BR>2 A globular swelling below the navel, produced by wind.<BR>3 Contusion.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि a bone, ला to bring, (to resemble,) क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीवत्|अष्ठीवन्त्
अष्ठीवत्<BR>mn. (-वान्-वत्)<BR>The knee.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि a bone, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीलिका
अष्ठीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pebble.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयम|असंयमः
असंयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Absence of check or restraint, especially of the senses.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संयम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयोग|असंयोगः
असंयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Absence of union or connection.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संयोग connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंलग्न
असंलग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Disjoined, detached, separate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मम् with लग्न connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंविदान
असंविदान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Ignorant, unwise.<BR>2 Not promising or contracting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सं before विद् to know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत
असंवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uncovered, exposed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
असंशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Free from doubt, certain.<BR>n. adv. (-यं)<BR>Certainly, verily.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
असंश्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Out of hearing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सं with श्रव hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसक्त
असंसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Indifferent to, not attached to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम् with सक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=092" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृष्ट
असंसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unmixed with.<BR>2 Separate, not living in common.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संसृष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृत|असंस्कृतः
असंस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Not perfect, unpolished, rude, common.<BR>2 Unintiated, not having gone through the proper rites of caste, state, sex or age.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संस्कृत perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्तुत
असंस्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unknown, unacquainted, not known as acquaintances.<BR>2 Not friends.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संस्तुत known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थान|असंस्थानं
असंस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Want, destitution.<BR>2 Disorder, confusion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मंस्थान station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थित
असंस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Disordered, irregular, not arranged or arrayed.<BR>2 Not collected or assembled.<BR>3 Destitute.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संस्थित placed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थिति|असंस्थितिः
असंस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>See असंस्थान.<BR>E.<BR>as before, स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहत|असंहतः
असंहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Scattered, loose, straggling, uncompressed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A form of array, loose or open order of troops.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संहत compact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहार्य्य|असंहार्य
असंहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Irresistible, insuperable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. संहार्य्य to be repelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस
अस<BR>(ञ) r. 1st cl. (असति-ते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To take or receive.<BR>3 To shine.<BR>(ल) r. 2d cl. (अस्ति)<BR>To be.<BR>(य, उ, इर) r. 4th cl. (अस्यति-ते)<BR>To throw or direct.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>to sit down:<BR>with अप,<BR>to quit or abandon:<BR>with नि,<BR>to deposit:<BR>with निर्,<BR>to expel:<BR>with परि and उप,<BR>to sit around:<BR>with प्र,<BR>to throw away, to reject, to confute:<BR>with वि,<BR>to divide:<BR>with वि and आङ्,<BR>to class, to arrange:<BR>with सम and नि,<BR>to abandon the world:<BR>with सम,<BR>to collect, to combine or compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकल
असकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Part, not all, unentire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सकल all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
असकृत्<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly, again and again.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सकृत् once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृद्गर्भवास|असकृद्गर्भवासः
असकृद्गर्भवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Repeated birth.<BR>E.<BR>असकृत् repeatedly, गर्भ the womb, वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
असक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Detached, disunited.<BR>2 Not interested in, indifferent to, unattached to.<BR>3 Detached from worldly feelings and passions.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सक्त united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्थ
असक्थ<BR>mfn. (-क्थः-क्था-क्थं)<BR>Without thighs.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सक्थि a thigh, अच् affix; also without the affix, असक्थि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखिन्
असखिन्<BR>m. (-खा)<BR>An enemy, an adversary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सखिन् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असगोत्र
असगोत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Of a different family.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स with गोत्र family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्प|असंकल्प
असङ्कल्प<BR>mn. (-ल्पः-ल्पं)<BR>1 Sincerity.<BR>2 Absence of predetermination.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्कल्प will, vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कल्पित|असंकल्पित|असङ्कल्पितः
असङ्कल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not purposed, not resolved or determined on.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्कल्पित purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कसुक|असंकसुक
असङ्कसुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Firm, steady.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्कसुक mutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कीर्ण|असंकीर्ण
असङ्कीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Uncompounded, uncollected, unmixed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मङ्कीर्ण collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्कुल|असंकुल|असंकुलः|असङ्कुलः
असङ्कुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Clear, open, broad.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A broad road.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सङ्कुल crowded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्केत
असङ्केत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not appointed, not agreed upon.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्केत an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्य|असंख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
असङ्ख्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्य)<BR>Innumerable, exceedingly numerous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सङ्ख्य to be numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्यता|असंख्यता
असङ्ख्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Innumerability, immensity, infinity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; or with त्व, असङ्ख्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्यात|असंख्यात|असंख्यातं
असङ्ख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uncounted.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्ख्यात numbered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येय|असंख्येयः
असङ्ख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Innumerable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्ख्येय to be counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्ग|असंग|असंगः
असङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्का-ङ्गं)<BR>Solitary, unassociated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्ग with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गत|असंगत
असङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uneven, unequal.<BR>2 Unattached.<BR>3 Unpreferred, disesteemed.<BR>4 Improbable, inconsistent.<BR>5 Unaccompanied, unassociated with.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्गत connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गति|असंगति|असंगतिः
असङ्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Improbability, incongruity.<BR>2 Not associating with.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्गति congruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असङ्गम|असंगम|असंगमः
असङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Separation, disunion.<BR>2 Inequality.<BR>3 Incongruity.<BR>4 Not associating with.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्गम union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असच्छास्त्र
असच्छास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Heretical or heterodox doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>असत् untrue, शास्त्र a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्जन|असज्जनः
असज्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wicked or contemptible person.<BR>E.<BR>असत् bad, जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असज्ञ
असज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Insensible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सज्ञा sign of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्|असन्त्
असत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>1 Non-existent, not being.<BR>2 Untrue, unreal.<BR>3 Bad, vile.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सत् being, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतायी
असतायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>असत् bad, ङीप् affix, and आय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असती
असती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सती virtuous, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतीसुत|असतीसुतः
असतीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A bastard.<BR>E.<BR>असती and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्म्मन्|असत्कर्मन्
असत्कर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Wicked.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>असत and कर्म्म act; also असत्कार्य्य, असत्क्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत
असत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ill done, done from improper motives, or in an unbecoming manner.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सत् good, कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्ता
असत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>1 Non-existence.<BR>2 Untruth.<BR>3 Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and तल् added; also with त्व, असत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पथ|असत्पथः
असत्पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A bad road.<BR>2 Evil practice or doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सत् good, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्परिग्रह|असत्परिग्रहः
असत्परिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Receiving unfit presents, or from improper persons.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and परिग्रह acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्पुत्र|असत्पुत्रः
असत्पुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A childless man.<BR>2 A wicked or disreputable son.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
असत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 False, untrue.<BR>2 Lying, a liar.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Untruth.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यवादिन्
असत्यवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>A liar, speaking falsely, giving false evidence.<BR>E.<BR>असत्य and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्ध|असत्यसंध
असत्यसन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Treacherous, base, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>असत्य untrue, सन्धि combination, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्यसन्निभ
असत्यसन्निभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Improbable, unlikely. असत्य and सन्निभ like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्संसर्ग|असत्संसर्गः
असत्संसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Evil company.<BR>E.<BR>असत् wicked, and संसर्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्
असद्<BR>m. (-द् or -त्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदध्येतृ
असदध्येतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A heterodox student.<BR>E.<BR>असत् untrue, bad, अधि before इङ् to go, to read or study, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचार|असदाचारः
असदाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wicked, following evil practices.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Evil practice.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=093" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदाचारिन्
असदाचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wicked, vile, one who follows bad or heterodox practices.<BR>E.<BR>असदाचार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
असदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Unlike, dissimilar.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सदृश् like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्ग्रह|असद्ग्रहः
असद्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Caprice, idle or childish desire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सत् good, wise, &c. and ग्रह what is taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्भाव|असद्भावः
असद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 An evil temperament or disposition.<BR>2 Nonexistence.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्वृत्ति|असद्वृत्तिः
असद्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Low or degrading occupation or profession.<BR>2 Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>असत् wicked, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहार|असद्व्यवहारः
असद्व्यवहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Following evil practices.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Evil practices.<BR>E.<BR>असत् and व्यवहार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्व्यवहारिन्
असद्व्यवहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Following evil courses.<BR>E.<BR>असद्व्यवहार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन|असनं|असनः
असन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Throwing, sending.<BR>E.<BR>अस to expel (disease), to send, to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनपर्णी
असनपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>The name of a plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>असन and पर्ण a leaf; having leaves like the Asana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तति|असंतति|असन्ततिः
असन्तति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Childless.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Want of posterity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्तति descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तान|असंतान|असन्तानः
असन्तान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Childless, having no posterity.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Want of posterity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्तान progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तुष्ट|असंतुष्ट|असन्तुष्टः
असन्तुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Displeased.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्तोष|असंतोष|असंतोषः
असन्तोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Displeasure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. मन्तोष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिग्ध|असंदिग्ध
असन्दिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Undoubted, unsuspected.<BR>2 Certain, confident.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्दिग्ध doubted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्दिष्ट
असन्दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unapprised.<BR>2 Uncommunicated.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्दिष्ट informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धान|असंधान
असन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Want of an aim or object.<BR>2 Disjunction.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्धान holding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धि|असंधि|असंधिः
असन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>Want of union or connection.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्धित|असंधित
असन्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Untied, unbound, at liberty, loose.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्धित tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्नद्ध|असंनद्ध|असन्नद्धः
असन्नद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Affecting knowledge, conceited as a Paṇḍita or teacher.<BR>3 Proud.<BR>4 Unarmed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम with, &c. नद्ध the part. past. of नह to bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकर्ष|असंनिकर्ष|असंनिकर्षः
असन्निकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Non-perception of objects, not bringing them to the mind.<BR>2 Remoteness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्निकर्ष attraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निकृष्ट|असंनिकृष्ट
असन्निकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Unperceived, undistinguished.<BR>2 Remote, not near.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्निकृष्ट drawn near to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निधि|असंनिधि|असंनिधिः
असन्निधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Absence, distance.<BR>2 Confidence, absence of doubt.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्निधि proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्निहित|असंनिहित
असन्निहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Far, not near.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्निहित placed near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्मान|असन्मानं
असन्मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Disrespect.<BR>2 Impropriety.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सन्मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिण्ड|असपिंड
असपिण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Unconnected by obsequial offerings.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सपिण्ड offering a common cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असभ्य|असभ्यः
असभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>1 Unfit for an assembly.<BR>2 Vulgar, low.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सभ्य belonging to a company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
असम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Unequalled, individual, without a fellow or equal.<BR>2 Uneven, unequal either in surface or number.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A name of Buddha or a Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सम like, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमक्ष
असमक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Absent, not present or visible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समक्ष before the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
असमग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Part, partial, incomplete, unentire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समग्र all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमञ्जस|असमंजस|असमञ्जसं
असमञ्जस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Unequal, unlike.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Unconformity, disparity, difference.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समञ्जस equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमय|असमयः
असमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Unseasonableness.<BR>2 Unfit or unfavourable time.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समय season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिकारण|असमवायिकारणं
असमवायिकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>(In logic,) Incidental cause, as the simple conjunction of two different objects.<BR>E.<BR>असमवायि and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
असमवायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Accidental, not inherent and inseparable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समवाय intimate union, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
असमर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Unable, incompetent.<BR>2 Feeble, weak.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समर्थ able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पण
असमर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Non-delivery, not committing or intrusting any thing to another.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्पित
असमर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unconsigned, unintrusted, undelivered.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समर्पित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्त
असमस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Separate, several, uncollected, uncompounded.<BR>2 Incomplete, imperfect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समस्त assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
असमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Different.<BR>2 Unlike.<BR>3 Unequal.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समान same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमापित
असमापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unfinished, unaccomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समापित completed, simple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्त|असमाप्तं
असमाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Unfinished, incomplete.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समाप्त finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्ति
असमाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Incompleteness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समाप्ति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावर्त्तक|असमावर्तक|असमावर्तकः
असमावर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A religious student, whose studies are not completed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समावर्त्तक who compleats his course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार|असमाहारः
असमाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Non-recovery of any thing.<BR>2 Disjunction, disconnection.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम् and आङ् before हृ to take, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार्य्य|असमाहार्य
असमाहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Irrecoverable.<BR>2 Not to be combined or united.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम and आङ् before हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्य
असमीक्ष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Not having considered.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समीक्ष्य having seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्यकारिन्
असमीक्ष्यकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Acting inconsiderately.<BR>E.<BR>अस मीक्ष्य and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीचीन
असमीचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Improper, incorrect.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समीचीन proper, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमृद्धि|असमृद्धिः
असमृद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Unfortunate.<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Non-increase.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. समृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पत्ति|असंपत्ति|असंपत्तिः
असम्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Ill luck, non-increase.<BR>2 Non-accomplishment, failure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्पत्ति prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पन्न|असंपन्न
असम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Uneffected, unaccomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्पन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्क|असंपर्क
असम्पर्क<BR>mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>Destitute of connexion or relation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्पर्क connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पर्कीय
असम्पर्कीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unconnected with, not belonging to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्पर्कीय related to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=094" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्पूर्ण|असंपूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण्ण
असम्पूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Incomplete, not entire.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्पूर्ण complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बद्ध|असंबद्ध|असम्बद्धं
असम्बद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unconnected, unmeaning, incoherent, (discourse, &c.)<BR>2 Improper, wrong.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम् with, and बध to bind, affix of the part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बन्ध|असंबंध|असंबन्ध|असंबन्धः
असम्बन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Unconnected, not relating or belonging to.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्बन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्बाध|असंबाध
असम्बाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Open, accessible.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>A species of the Śarkarī metre.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्बाध contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भव|असंभव|असंभवः
असम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Improbable, unlikely, inconsistent.<BR>2 Non-existent.<BR>nf. (-वं-वा)<BR>1 Any extraordinary event.<BR>2 Nonexistence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावना|असंभावना
असम्भावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Difficulty or impossibility of conceiving or comprehending.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भावना conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भावनीय|असंभावनीय
असम्भावनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Inconceivable, incomprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भावनीय conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भूत|असंभूत
असम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>Unproduced.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भोग|असंभोग
असम्भोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Non-enjoyment, not using or enjoying.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रम|असंभ्रमः
असम्भ्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Cool, composed.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Calmness, steadiness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्भ्रम flurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मत|असंमत|असंमतः|असम्मतः
असम्मत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dissentient, differing from.<BR>2 Averse, contrary.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सं with, मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मति|असंमति|असंमतिः
असम्मति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Dissent, difference of opinion.<BR>2 Dislike, aversion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम् with, मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मान|असंमान|असम्मानं|असंमानः
असम्मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disrespect, disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम् with, मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मूढ|असंमूढ
असम्मूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Clear-seeing, judging well, cool, calm.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्मूढ beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्मोह|असंमोह|असंमोहः
असम्मोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Steadiness, calmness, composure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्मोह fascination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यक्कारिन्
असम्यक्कारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Inexpert, incompetent.<BR>2 Ill conducted, profligate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्यक् properly, कारिन् who does any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यञ्च्|असम्यंच्
असम्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-म्यङ्-मीची-म्यक्)<BR>1 Improper, incorrect.<BR>2 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सम्यञ्च् right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असरु|असरुः
असरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The name of a medicinal plant, vulg. Kukūrsoṅga, (Conyza lacera.)<BR>E.<BR>अस to reject or be rejected, अरु affix; thrown away from its bad smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असल|असलं
असल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 Arms.<BR>3 A mantra.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असवर्ण|असवर्ण्ण
असवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Of a different caste.<BR>2 Of a different colour.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सवर्ण of one caste, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह
असह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Impatient, intolerant, not enduring.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहन|असहनः
असहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unable to endure.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Intolerance, impatience.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सह to bear ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनीय
असहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unbearable, insufferable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सहनीय to be borne; also असहित्तव्य and असह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहमान
असहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Impatient, not bearing, not enduring.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सहमान bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहाय
असहाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Lonely, solitary, friendless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सहाय an associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहायता
असहायता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Loneliness, solitude, the life of a hermit.<BR>2 Friendlessness, being without a friend or patron.<BR>E.<BR>असहाय and तल् affix; also असहायत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहित
असहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unassociated, unaccompanied.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सहित accompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णु
असहिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Impatient, unenduring.<BR>E.<BR>अ and सहिष्णु bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह्य|असह्यः
असह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Intolerable, unbearable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सह्य to be borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षात्
असाक्षात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>2 Not present.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साक्षात् before one's eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिक
असाक्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unattested, unwitnessed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साक्षिन् a witness, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिन्
असाक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>Incompetent as evidence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्ष्य|असाक्ष्यं
असाक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Want of evidence, sufficient evidence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साक्ष्य testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असात्म्य
असात्म्य<BR>mfn. (-त्म्यः-त्म्या-त्म्यं)<BR>Unwholesome, disagreeing with, (as food, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सात्म्य suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधन
असाधन<BR>mfn. (-तः-ना-नं)<BR>Without means.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Non-accomplishment.<BR>2 Not proving or establishing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and साधन implement or means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधनीय
असाधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Unaccomplishable, not to be effected or completed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साधनीय to be effected; also असाध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारण|असाधारणं|असाधारणः
असाधारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Special, specific, not common.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Speciality, species.<BR>2 Special property.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साधारण common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधित
असाधित<BR>mfn. (-तः)<BR>Unaccomplished.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साधित accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधु
असाधु<BR>mfn. (-धुः-धुः-ध्वी-धु)<BR>Wicked, bad.<BR>f. (-ध्वी)<BR>An unchaste wife.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साधु virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुता
असाधुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>असाधु and तल् affix; or with त्व, असाधुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधुवृत्ता
असाधुवृत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>असाधु impurity, and वृत्त professed or practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्य|असाध्यं
असाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Not to be effected, not proper or able to be accomplished.<BR>2 Incurable, irremediable.<BR>3 Not susceptible of proof.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साध्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असान्द्र|असान्द्रं
असान्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं)<BR>Fine, delicate but with interstices.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and सान्द्र coarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामयिक
असामयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unseasonable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ससय time, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्य
असामान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Peculiar, not common.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Peculiar or special property.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सामान्य common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्प्रतम्|असांप्रतम्
असाम्प्रतम्<BR>ind.<BR>Unfitly, improperly, inopportunely.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and साम्प्रतं fitly, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्य|असाम्यं
असाम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Difference, dissimilarity.<BR>2 Unsuitableness, (in medicine or diet,) unwholesomeness.<BR>3 Disagreeableness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साम्य sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असार|असारं|असारः
असार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Sapless, pithless.<BR>2 Vain, unprofitable.<BR>3 Weak, feeble.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The castor oil tree.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. and सार juice, sap, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असावधान
असावधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Careless, inadvertent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सावधान careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=095" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असावधानता
असावधानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Carelessness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, or with त्व, असावधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहस|असाहसं
असाहस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Gentleness, absence of violence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसिक
असाहसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Gentle, peaceable, not violent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साहसिक violent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहाय्य
असाहाय्य<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>Want of assistance or co-operation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. साहाय्य alliance, friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असि|असिः
असि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar.<BR>E.<BR>अस to cast, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक|असिकं
असिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The part of the face between the under lip and the chin.<BR>E.<BR>अस to throw, to shine, &c. and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्निका
असिक्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman servant: see असिक्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्नी
असिक्नी<BR>f. (-क्नी)<BR>1 A girl attending upon the inner or women's apartments.<BR>2 A river.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सित white, because her hair is not whitened by age: क्न is substituted for त, and the affix is ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिगण्ड|असिगण्डः
असिगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A small pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Black or dark blue.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Black, (the colour.)<BR>2 A name of the planet Saturn.<BR>3 The dark fortnight of a lunar month.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सित white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताभ्रशेखर|असिताभ्रशेखरः
असिताभ्रशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Jaina or Buddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>असित black, अभ्र a cloud, and शेखर a crest: cloud-crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताम्बुरुह
असिताम्बुरुह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>असित black or dark blue, and अम्बुरुह a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितार्च्चिस्|असितार्चिस्
असितार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>A name of VAHNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>असित dark, smoky, अर्च्चिस् a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिताश्मन्
असिताश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>1 The lapis lazuli.<BR>2 Any black or dark blue stone.<BR>E.<BR>असित black, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितोत्पल|असितोत्पलं
असितोत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>असित and उत्पल lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असितोपल
असितोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>असित blue, उपल stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्र|असिदंष्ट्रः
असिदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A marine monster, the Makara, considered as the emblem of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>असि and दंष्ट्र a tooth: swordtoothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदंष्ट्रक|असिदंष्ट्रकः
असिदंष्ट्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिदन्त|असिदंत|असिदन्तः
असिदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A crocodile: see मकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधारा
असिधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The edge of a sword.<BR>E.<BR>असि and धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
असिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Unripe.<BR>2 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>3 Unaccomplished, uneffected.<BR>4 Unproven.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सिद्ध perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धि|असिद्धिः
असिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Failure, imperfect or incomplete accomplishment.<BR>2 (In logic,) Want of proof, conclusion not warranted by the premises.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधाव|असिधावः
असिधाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An armourer, a furbisher, a sword or tool cleaner.<BR>E.<BR>असि and धाव who polishes; धाव to clean, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधावक|असिधावकः
असिधावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनु|असिधेनुः
असिधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>असि and धेनु a bow; the sword-like bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिधेनुका
असिधेनुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्र|असिपत्रः
असिपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 The sugar cane.<BR>2 A hell paved with swords.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A sheathe, a scabbard.<BR>2 The blade of a sword.<BR>E.<BR>असि and पत्र a leaf; sharp as a sword, or enclosing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रक|असिपत्रकः
असिपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपत्रवन|असिपत्रवनं
असिपत्रवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A hell where the trees have leaves as sharp as swords.<BR>E.<BR>असि and पत्र a leaf, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुच्छक|असिपुच्छकः
असिपुच्छक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus gangeticus, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>असि, पुच्छ a tail, and कन् affix; sword tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्रिका
असिपुत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Aknife.<BR>E.<BR>असि and पुत्रिका a daughter, an infant sword; from its smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिपुत्री
असिपुत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिमेद|असिमेदः
असिमेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A fetid Mimosa: see विट्खदिर.<BR>E.<BR>असि and मेद marrow, essence; the plant being described with many thorns, and a decoction of it being demulcent^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिहेति|असिहेतिः
असिहेति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A swordsman or soldier armed with a sword.<BR>E.<BR>असि and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असु|असुः
असु<BR>m. pl. always, (असवः)<BR>The five vital breaths or airs of the body.<BR>n. (-सु)<BR>1 Reflexion, thought, or the heart as the seat of it.<BR>2 Affliction.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, &c. and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुकर
असुकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult, arduous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुकर easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुक्षण|असुक्षणं
असुक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>See असूक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
असुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Sorrow, pain, affliction, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखावह
असुखावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Producing unhappiness.<BR>E.<BR>असुख and आवह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखिन्
असुखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>Unhappy, sorrowful, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>असुख and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदय
असुखोदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Causing or ending in unhappiness.<BR>E.<BR>असुख and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखोदर्क
असुखोदर्क<BR>mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>Productive of or ending in unhappiness.<BR>E.<BR>असुख and उदर्क subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुगम
असुगम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult of attainment or accomplishment, hard, unattainable.<BR>2 Difficult to be understood.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सु easily, गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Childless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुत a son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुधारण|असुधारणं
असुधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Life, existence.<BR>E.<BR>असु vital air, and धारण possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुनिरस
असुनिरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Disagreeable, unpleasant, offensive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुनिरस agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्दर
असुन्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Plain, ugly.<BR>2 Improper, unbecoming.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुन्दर handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुभृत्
असुभृत्<BR>mfn. (-मृत्)<BR>Living, alive.<BR>E.<BR>असु and भृत् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुमत्|असुमन्त्
असुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Living, breathing.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>Life, the principle of vitality, the portion of spirit connected with the attributes of existence.<BR>E.<BR>असु vital air, and मतुप् posses. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>An Asura or demon: the Asuras are children of DITI by KAŚYAPA; they are demons of the first order, and in perpetual hostility with the gods.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 A zodiacal sign.<BR>3 A prostitute.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Black mustard, (Sinapis ramosa.)<BR>2 The wife of an Asura.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सुर a deity; or अस् to send, to cast, &c. and उरन् Uṇādi affix, टाप् and ङीप् for the fem.; or अ neg. and सुरा spirituous liquor, personified as a damsel produced at the churning of the ocean, who was rejected by the demons and received by the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=096" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष
असुरक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Perishable, volatile, transitory.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सु easy, रक्षा preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरक्ष्य
असुरक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Difficult of retention or preservation.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सु easily, रक्ष्य to be kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुररिपु|असुररिपुः
असुररिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>असुर and रिपु an enemy, the foe of the Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसा
असुरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A sort of basil, (Ocymum pilosum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुराह्व|असुराह्वं
असुराह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>Bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>असुर and आह्वा a name: named after an Asura; struck at seasons of worship, and deterring his approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्क्षण|असुर्क्षणं
असुर्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>See असूर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
असुलभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुस्तभ easily got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसम|असुसमः
असुसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Dearly beloved.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A lover.<BR>E.<BR>असु life, सम equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुस्थ|असुस्थः
असुस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Unwell, uncomfortable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुस्थ well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
असुहृद्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सुहृत् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक
असूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Calumnious, scandalous, detracting, depreciating.<BR>E.<BR>असूञ् to calumniate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्षण|असूक्षणं
असूक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>अ implying modification, सूर्क्ष to disrespect, affix ल्युट्, the र is rejected; it is also written असुक्षण and असूर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्ष्म
असूक्ष्म<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)<BR>Large, thick, gross.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सूक्ष्म fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूति|असूतिः
असूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Non-production, obstruction, removal.<BR>2 Barrenness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सूति bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयन|असूयनं
असूयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Calumny, detraction.<BR>E.<BR>असूय to detract from, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Calumny, detraction.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The wife of the sage ATRI.<BR>E.<BR>असूञ् to detract from, a nominal root, and यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयु|असूयुः
असूयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Calumny.<BR>E.<BR>असूय to calumniate, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्क्षण
असूर्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>See असूक्षण; it is also written असुर्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्य्यम्पश्या|असूर्यम्पश्या|असूर्यंपश्या
असूर्य्यम्पश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>The wife of a king or a great man.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सूर्य्य the sun, and पश्या who sees; who never sees the sun; being shut up in the Zenana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्कर|असृक्करः
असृक्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The juice or essence of the body, lymph, serum, &c.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् blood, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्प|असृक्पः
असृक्प<BR>mf. (-क्पः-क्पा)<BR>A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin of malicious propensities.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् blood, and प who drinks: these demons eat flesh, human or animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्पात|असृक्पातः
असृक्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Drops of blood, as from a wound.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्श्राव
असृक्श्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Bleeding, letting blood.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and आब causing to flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृक्श्राविन्
असृक्श्राविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Bleeding, who or what takes away blood.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and श्राविन् what causes to flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्दरा
असृग्दरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Irregular or excessive menstruation, menorrhagia.<BR>E.<BR>अतृज्, दृ to tear, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धरा
असृग्धरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The skin.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and धरा what contains: blood-containing; also असृग्धारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्धारा
असृग्धारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The skin.<BR>2 A stream of blood.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and धारा a stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्वहा
असृग्वहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A blood vessel.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृग्विमोक्षण
असृग्विमोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Bleeding.<BR>E.<BR>असृज् and विमाक्षण letting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज्<BR>n. (-सृक्)<BR>Blood.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सृज् to create, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाट|असृपाटः
असृपाट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A stream of blood.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सृप to go, काटः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्ट
असृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Uncreated.<BR>2 Undistributed, not presented.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सृष्ट created, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचनक|असेचनकं
असेचनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Charming, lovely.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सेचव satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवन
असेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Disregarding, neglecting.<BR>2 Avoiding, shunning.<BR>3 Disobedience, inattention.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सेवन service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवा
असेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 Avoiding, not following or practising.<BR>2 Disregard.<BR>3 Disobedience.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सेवा service: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
असेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Neglected, unattended to, disobeyed.<BR>2 Abstained from, disused.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सेवित served, used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेव्य
असेव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Not to be served or attended to.<BR>2 Not to be used or practised, not to be eaten, drank, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सेव्य to be followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौन्दर्य्य|असौन्दर्य
असौन्दर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Ugliness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सौन्दर्य्य beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्य
असौम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Ugly, unlovely.<BR>2 Disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सौम्य pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्यस्वर|असौम्यस्वरः
असौम्यस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having a bad or croaking voice.<BR>E.<BR>असौम्य disagreeable, and स्वर a note or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्टव
असौष्टव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Ugliness, deformity.<BR>2 Demerit, worthlessness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सौष्टव beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्न
अस्कन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Permanent, durable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्कद to flow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अस्खलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Firm, permanent, unshaken, unyielding.<BR>2 Not slipping or fallen.<BR>3 Undeviating.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्खलित slipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त<BR>Sautra root. 10th cl. (अस्तयति)<BR>To obscure or eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Thrown, cast.<BR>2 Sent, dispatched.<BR>3 Set, obscured.<BR>4 Removed, set aside.<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>1 The western mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to set.<BR>2 Sun-set.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>Death, end.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त to obscure or eclipse, अच् affix, or अस to throw, &c. and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तक|अस्तकः
अस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Beatitude, eternal felicity.<BR>E.<BR>अस्तम् disappearance, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगत
अस्तगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set, as the sun.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तगिरि|अस्तगिरिः
अस्तगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The western mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अस्तब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Unconfounded.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्तब्ध astounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्धत्व
अस्तब्धत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Self-possession, not being confused or confounded.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तम्
अस्तम्<BR>ind.<BR>Disappearance, setting, vanishing.<BR>E.<BR>अस to send or cast, तम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमती
अस्तमती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum): see सालपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>अस्तम् the mountain, and अत to go, अच् and ङीप् affixes; abounding in the west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमयन
अस्तमयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disappearance, setting.<BR>E.<BR>अस्तम्, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमित
अस्तमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set, (as the sun.)<BR>E.<BR>अस्तम् and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तवत्
अस्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Obstructed, hindered, opposed.<BR>2 Set.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त thrown, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=097" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तव्यस्त
अस्तव्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Confused, disordered, irrelevant.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त and व्यस्त scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तसङ्ख्य|अस्तसंख्य
अस्तसङ्ख्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्यं)<BR>Innumerable.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त gone, सङ्ख्या number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताघ|अस्ताघः
अस्ताघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Very deep: see अस्थाघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताचल|अस्ताचलः
अस्ताचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The western mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताद्रि|अस्ताद्रिः
अस्ताद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The western mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तावलम्बन|अस्तावलंबन
अस्तावलम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The resting of a heavenly body on the western part of the horizon.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त and अवलम्बन depending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तावलम्बिन्
अस्तावलम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>Setting as the sun, on the point of setting.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त and अवलम्बिन् impending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ति|अस्तिः
अस्ति<BR>ind.<BR>Now being, existent, present.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, and क्तिन affix, or the third person sing present tense, it is, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिनास्ति
अस्तिनास्ति<BR>ind.<BR>1 Doubtful.<BR>2 Partly true and partly not.<BR>E.<BR>अस्ति and नास्ति it is not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिनास्तित्व
अस्तिनास्तित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Uncertain or doubtful existence.<BR>2 Partial existence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also अस्ति नास्तिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिमत्|अस्तिमन्त्
अस्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Wealthy, opulent.<BR>E.<BR>अस्ति what is, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्तु<BR>ind.<BR>Be it so, let it be, implying assent, also reluctance and pain.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, तुम् affix or the third person sing. imperative used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुत
अस्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Not praised.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्तुत praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेन
अस्तेन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Honesty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्तेन theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेय|अस्तेयं
अस्तेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Honesty.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्तेय theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्यान|अस्त्यानं
अस्त्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reproach, blame.<BR>E.<BR>अ deteriorative, and स्त्ये to sound, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्र|अस्त्रं
अस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 A weapon in general.<BR>2 A sword.<BR>3 A bow.<BR>4 A missile weapon.<BR>E.<BR>अस to throw, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकण्ठक
अस्त्रकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and कण्ठक a thorn, a thorn-like weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रकारक|अस्त्रकारकः
अस्त्रकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An armourer.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and कारक who makes: so अस्त्रकारः and अस्त्रकारिन् m. (-री.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सक|अस्त्रचिकित्सकः
अस्त्रचिकित्सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A surgeon.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and च्चिकित्सक healing; who uses instruments as means of cure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रचिकित्सा
अस्त्रचिकित्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Surgery.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र a knife, a lancet, and चिकित्सा healing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रजीव|अस्त्रजीवः
अस्त्रजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A soldier, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र a weapon, and जीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रधारिन्
अस्त्रधारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A soldier.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and धारिन् who bears; so अस्त्रधारक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रनिवारण
अस्त्रनिवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Guarding off a blow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and निवारण guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रमार्ज्ज|अस्त्रमार्ज|अस्त्रमार्ज्जः
अस्त्रमार्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>An armourer, a sword or tool cleaner.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and मार्ज्ज who cleans, from मृज and अण् affix; also अस्त्रमार्ज्जक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रयुद्ध
अस्त्रयुद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>Fighting with weapons.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and युद्ध battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रविद्या
अस्त्रविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>The military science.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रवेद|अस्त्रवेदः
अस्त्रवेद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The science of arms and war.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र a weapon, and वेद a Veda or scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रसायक|अस्त्रसायकः
अस्त्रसायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र, षो to destroy, वुन affix; what destroys all other weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रहीन
अस्त्रहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unarmed, defenceless.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रागार|अस्त्रागारं|अस्त्रागारः
अस्त्रागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An arsenal, an armoury.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राघात|अस्त्राघातः
अस्त्राघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A wound, a cut.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्राहत
अस्त्राहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck, wounded, killed.<BR>E.<BR>अस्त्र and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रीक
अस्त्रीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having no female.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्त्री female, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाग|अस्थागं
अस्थाग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Very deep.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्था to stand, with क्विप् affix, and ग from गम to go; where there is no proceeding to an end; it is also written अस्ताग, अस्थाघ, अस्थान and अस्थार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाघ|अस्थाघं|अस्थाघः
अस्थाघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with घ, from हन to kill or hurt, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अस्थान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>See अस्थाग.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A place where there is no firm footing.<BR>adv.<BR>Unsuitably, unseasonably.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. end, स्थान stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाने
अस्थाने<BR>ind.<BR>Unseasonably, inopportunely.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्थाने in place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाय|अस्थायं|अस्थायः
अस्थाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>See अस्थाग; also अस्थाव and अस्थास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Perishable, transient.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्थायिन् staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थार|अस्थारं|अस्थारः
अस्थार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>See अस्थाग.<BR>E.<BR>अस्था as above, and र from रा to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थावर|अस्थावरं
अस्थावर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Moveable, moving, not fixed.<BR>2 (In law) Personal, (as property) money, cattle, &c. opposed to land.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्थावर stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>A bone.<BR>E.<BR>अस to throw, &c. and क्थिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिक
अस्थिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bone.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिकृत्
अस्थिकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि a bone, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिज|अस्थिजः
अस्थिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and ज what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिज्ञ
अस्थिज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and ज्ञ what knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिति|अस्थितिः
अस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Want of place or condition, want of firm continuance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितुण्ड|अस्थितुंड|अस्थितुण्डः
अस्थितुण्ड<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डा)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and तुण्ड a mouth; whose mouth or beak is of bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थितोद|अस्थितोदः
अस्थितोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Pain in the bones.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and तोद torturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित्वच्
अस्थित्वच्<BR>f. (-त्वक्)<BR>The periosteum.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and त्वच् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिधन्वन्
अस्थिधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि, धनु a bow, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिपञ्जर|अस्थिपंजर|अस्थिपञ्जरः
अस्थिपञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A skeleton.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and पञ्जर a cage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभक्ष|अस्थिभक्षः
अस्थिभक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभङ्ग|अस्थिभंग|अस्थिभङ्गः
अस्थिभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Fracture.<BR>2 A plant of supposed efficacy in fractures, (Cissus quadrangularis.)<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभुज्
अस्थिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि a bone, भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेद|अस्थिभेदः
अस्थिभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Fracturing, breaking or wounding a bone.<BR>2 A sort of bone, a bone.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and भेद breaking, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिभेदक|अस्थिभेदकः
अस्थिभेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A bone-breaker, who or what breaks bones.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and भेदक what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=098" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमत्|अस्थिमन्त्
अस्थिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Having bones, vertebrated, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमाला
अस्थिमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A necklace of bones.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमालिन्
अस्थिमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि a bone, माला a garland, इनि affix; ŚIVA is commonly represented with a necklace of skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अस्थिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Trembling, shaken, unsteady.<BR>2 Uncertain, unascertained.<BR>3 Unworthy of confidence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्थिर firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिरता
अस्थिरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unsteadiness, fickleness, mutability.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थिर and तल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिरत्व
अस्थिरत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Unsteadiness, mutability.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थिर and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिवत्
अस्थिवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Bony, osseous.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिविग्रह|अस्थिविग्रहः
अस्थिविग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of BHṚṄGI, one of ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and विग्रह a part, &c. who carries ŚIVA'S decorations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिशोष|अस्थिशोषः
अस्थिशोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Dryness and decay of the bones.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and शोष drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहार|अस्थिसंहारः
अस्थिसंहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, a species of turnsole^1, (Heliotropium indicum): see हस्तिशुण्डी.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and सं before हृ to take, to collect, seize, &c. (it is an ingredient in philtres, &c.) अण aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसंहारक|अस्थिसंहारकः
अस्थिसंहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The adjutant bird.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and संहारक who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसञ्चय|अस्थिसंचय|अस्थिसंचयः
अस्थिसञ्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Collecting the bones or their ashes after burning a corpse.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and सञ्चय assemblage; also अस्थिसञ्चायनं^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसन्धि|अस्थिसंधि|अस्थिसन्धिः
अस्थिसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>1 A joint, an articulation.<BR>2 Uniting of a broken bone.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and सन्धि connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसमर्पण
अस्थिसमर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throwing the bones of a dead body into the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and समर्पण consigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिसार|अस्थिसारः
अस्थिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि bone, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिस्थूण|अस्थिस्थूणः
अस्थिस्थूण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The body, or that of which the bones are the supporters.<BR>E.<BR>अस्थि and स्थूण a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूल
अस्थूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Small, delicate.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्थूल gross.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अस्थैर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Instability, unsteadiness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्थैर्य्य steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्ध
अस्निग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Harsh, hard, dry.<BR>2 Harsh, unkind.<BR>E.<BR>अ and स्निग्ध unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेह|अस्नेहः
अस्नेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Harsh, unkind.<BR>2 Harsh, hard, dry.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Unkindness, want of affection.<BR>2 Absence of oiliness.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्नेह affection, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्श|अस्पर्शः
अस्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>What does not touch or is not touched.<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Not touching, non-contact.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पर्श contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शन|अस्पर्शनं
अस्पर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Non-contact, avoiding the contact of any thing or person, especially of one who is impure.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पर्शन touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शनीय
अस्पर्शनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Impure, not to be touched.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पर्शनीय to be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शित
अस्पर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Untouched.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पर्शित touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अस्पष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Indistinct.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्पष्ट clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृश्य
अस्पृश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Not to be touched.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पृश्य tangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्ट
अस्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Untouched.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टि|अस्पृष्टिः
अस्पृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Not touching, avoiding contact. अ neg. स्पृष्टि touching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृह
अस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Undesirous, content, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृहनीय
अस्पृहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undesirable.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्पृहनीय desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुट|अस्फुटं
अस्फुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Indistinct speech.<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Indistinct, obscure.<BR>2 Invisible.<BR>3 Unblown.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्फुट open, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटफल
अस्फुटफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Indistinct result.<BR>2 (In Geometry,) Gross area of a triangle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अस्फुट and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुटवाच्
अस्फुटवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Lisping, speaking indistinctly.<BR>E.<BR>अस्फट and वाच् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद्<BR>First person pronoun, (अहं)<BR>I.<BR>(आवां)<BR>We two.<BR>(वयं)<BR>We.<BR>E.<BR>अस to be, and मदिक् Uṇādi affix: the inflexions of this pronoun are very irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Our, ours.<BR>E.<BR>अस्मद् I, and छ affix in the sense of the second case plur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मन्त|अस्मंतं|अस्मन्तं
अस्मन्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>A furnace or fire-place: see अश्मन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरण|अस्मरणं
अस्मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Forgetfulness, forgetting.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्मरण remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरणीय
अस्मरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be recollected.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्मरणीय to be remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मार्त्त|अस्मार्त
अस्मार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Immemorial, not within memory.<BR>2 Illegal, not according to law.<BR>3 Not belonging to the Hindu institutes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्मार्त्त relating to law, &c. from स्मृति with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृत
अस्मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Forgotten.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्मृत remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृति|अस्मृतिः
अस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Want of memory, forgetfulness.<BR>2 Not being part of the institutes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्मृति memory or code of law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्व|अस्वः
अस्व<BR>mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>Not one's own.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वक
अस्वक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Not one's own, belonging to another.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वकीय
अस्वकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not one's own, belonging to another.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वकीय own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छ
अस्वच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Opake, not clear.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वच्छ clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छन्द|अस्वच्छंद|अस्वच्छन्दः
अस्वच्छन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>1 Docile.<BR>2 Dependant.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. स्व own, and च्छन्द intention; not self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वजाति
अस्वजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Of a different caste.<BR>2 Of a different species.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्व own, जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वतन्त्र|अस्वतंत्र|अस्वतन्त्रः
अस्वतन्त्र<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>1 Docile, humble.<BR>2 Dependant, subject.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वतन्त्र self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वत्व|अस्वत्वं
अस्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Want of claim or right to any thing, having no indefeasible property in it, absence of ownership.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्व own, with त्व affix: also with तल, अस्वत्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वन्त|अस्वंत|अस्वन्तः
अस्वन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Ending ill, leading to or having an unfavourable close.<BR>2 Approaching the end of life.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A fire-place: see अश्वन्त.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and सु good, or असु breath, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्न|अस्वप्नः
अस्वप्न<BR>m. (-प्नः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्वप्न sleep; who never sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभाव|अस्वभावः
अस्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Unnatural or unusual character or temperament.<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Of a different nature.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=099" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having a bad or croaking voice.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and स्वर a note or the voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरूप
अस्वरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Essentially different or unlike.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वरूप of one nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अस्वर्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्म्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>Not leading to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वर्ग्यं paradisiacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अस्वस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Unwell, indisposed.<BR>2 Unfortunate, badly off.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वस्थ being well or happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वादु
अस्वादु<BR>mfn. (-दुः-दुः-दु)<BR>Tasteless, insipid.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वादु sapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाध्याय|अस्वाध्यायः
अस्वाध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A Brahman who has not made his studies, who has not read the Vedas previous to his investiture.<BR>2 Interruption or interval of study, prohibited on certain days of the moon, at eclipses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्व own, and अध्याय a lecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिक|अस्वामिकं
अस्वामिक<BR>m. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unowned, unclaimed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वामिन् a master, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अस्वामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Having no right or title to anything, not being master of it.<BR>2 That which has no master or owner.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वामिन् a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिविक्रय|अस्वामिविक्रयः
अस्वामिविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sale without ownership.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वामिन् a master, &c. विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्य|अस्वाम्यं
अस्वाम्य<BR>n. (-भ्यं)<BR>Absence of right or title to property.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वाम्य ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वार्थ
अस्वार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Not for one's self.<BR>2 Not for a proper object.<BR>3 Having a different meaning.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्व own, अर्थ end or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वास्थ्य|अस्वास्थ्यं
अस्वास्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>Indisposition, discomfort, indigence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वास्थ्य well-being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकार
अस्वीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Dissent, non-acquiescence.<BR>E.<BR>neg. स्वीकार promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वीकृत
अस्वीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dissented from, refused, not promised.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वीकृत promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वेद
अस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Suppressed perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्र|अस्रं|अस्रः
अस्र<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>1 A corner, an angle.<BR>2 Hair.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>3 A tear.<BR>E.<BR>अस to cast or throw, &c. affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रकण्ठ|अस्रकंठ|अस्रकण्ठः
अस्रकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>अस्र and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रज|अस्रजं
अस्रज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>अस्र blood, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रजित्
अस्रजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A plant, commonly Kabātabentu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रप|अस्रपः
अस्रप<BR>mf. (-पः-पा)<BR>A Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>अस्र blood, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रपित्त
अस्रपित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Plethora, haemorrhage^1, epistaxis, involuntary discharge of blood from the mouth, nostrils, anus, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अस्र and पित्त bile: both humors being supposed to be affected.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रमातृका
अस्रमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Chyle, chyme.<BR>E.<BR>अस्र blood, मातृ the parent, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ररोधिनी
अस्ररोधिनी<BR>f.<BR>A plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रार्ज्जक|अस्रार्जक|अस्रार्जकः|अस्रार्ज्जकः
अस्रार्ज्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The white Tulasi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रि|अस्रिः
अस्रि<BR>f. (-स्रिः)<BR>Ten millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रु
अस्रु<BR>n. (-स्रु)<BR>A tear.<BR>E.<BR>अस to cast or reject, and रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रुव
अस्रुव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A granulation, (of flesh.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. स्रु to distil, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह<BR>r. 5th cl. (अहति)<BR>To pervade or occupy.<BR>(इ.) अहि r. 1st cl. (अंहते)<BR>To go or move;<BR>also 10th cl. (अंहयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and interjection implying,<BR>1 Commendation.<BR>2 Rejecting, sending.<BR>3 Deviation from custom, (improperly).<BR>4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ह from हन to hurt, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Proud.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् I, and युस् affix: self-opinioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःपति|अहःपतिः
अहःपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहःशेष|अहःशेषः
अहःशेष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Evening.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कार|अहंकार|अहङ्कारः
अहङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Pride.<BR>2 Individuality, sense of self.<BR>3 One of the elements of creation, consciousness, individualization.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् I, and कार what makes; thinking highly of one's self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारबत्
अहङ्कारबत्<BR>mfn. (-बान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Proud.<BR>E.<BR>अहंङ्कार pride, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कारिन्|अहंकारिन्
अहङ्कारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Proud, self-important.<BR>E.<BR>अहंङ्कार and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृत|अहंकृत
अहङ्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Proud.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् I, and कृत made: see अहंकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहङ्कृति|अहंकृति|अहङ्कृतिः
अहङ्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Pride.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् and कृति action: see अहङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unhurt, uninjured, not struck or killed.<BR>2 Unblemished, unsoiled.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>New clothes.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and हत hurt, part. past. of हन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन्<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A day.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हा to leave, and कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहननीथ
अहननीथ<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be killed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हननीथ to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्तव्य
अहन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Not to be killed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हन्तव्य to be killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहमहमिका
अहमहमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Military vaunting.<BR>2 Assertion or conceit of superiority, boasting, egotism.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् I, reiterated, क and टाप् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्पूर्व्विका|अहम्पूर्विका|अहंपूर्विका
अहम्पूर्व्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Emulative onset, the running forward of soldiers with emulation.<BR>2 Conceit, vaunting.<BR>E.<BR>अहं I, पूर्ब्व first; affixes as in the last; I will be foremost, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्मति|अहंमति|अहम्मतिः
अहम्मति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Spiritual ignorance.<BR>2 Conceit.<BR>3 Self-love.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् and मति understanding; self-love, or worldly mindedness, opposed to abstract meditation on the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरणीय
अहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Not to be taken away.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हरणीय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरह|अहरहः
अहरह<BR>ind.<BR>Daily, day by day.<BR>E.<BR>अहम् repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्गण|अहर्गणः
अहर्गण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A month.<BR>2 Any calculated term.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, and गण a number or class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्निशम्
अहर्निशम्<BR>ind.<BR>Day and night.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् day, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्पति|अहर्पतिः
अहर्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and पति a master; also अहः, पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्बान्धव|अहर्बान्धवः|अहर्ब्बान्धवः
अहर्बान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and बान्धब a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मणि|अहर्मणिः|अहर्म्मणिः
अहर्मणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्मुख|अहर्मुखं
अहर्मुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Morning, the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and मुख the commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल
अहल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unploughed, unfurrowed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हस्ति a furrow, अच् affix: also with the final unchanged, अहलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहल्य|अहल्यः
अहल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Unploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 The name of an Apsaras or heavenly courtezan.<BR>2 The wife of GAUTAMA, a saint and philosopher.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हल to plough, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=100" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्ष
अहर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Unhappy, gloomy, sorrowful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हर्ष happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर्षित
अहर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unhappy, sorrowful.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हर्षित rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहवनीय
अहवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Not to be offered, not fit or proper to be sacrificed.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हबनीय to be offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्कर|अहस्करः
अहस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहस्पति|अहस्पतिः
अहस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Swallow wort.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहह
अहह<BR>ind.<BR>A particle or interjection, as ah! aha! &c. implying:<BR>1 Surprise:<BR>2 Fatigue:<BR>3 Pain:<BR>4 Pleasure:<BR>5 Calling.<BR>E.<BR>अह from अहम् I, and ह from हा to abandon: self or pride-abandonment; also अहहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहहा
अहहा<BR>ind.<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्य|अहार्य|अहार्यः|अहार्य्यं|अहार्य्यः
अहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Not to be stolen or taken away.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and हार्य्य future part. of हृञ् to take or convey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहार्य्यत्व|अहार्यत्व
अहार्य्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Security, not being liable to be stolen or taken away.<BR>E.<BR>अहार्य्य and त्व affix; also अहार्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहि|अहिः
अहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>1 A snake or serpent.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A traveller.<BR>4 Lead.<BR>5 The name of a demon: see वृत्रासुर.<BR>6 A name of RĀHU, the ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed to हन to hurt, इन् Uṇādi affix; injuring all or every thing, the आ of आङ् is made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसक
अहिंसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Harmless, innocuous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हिंसक mischievous; so अहिंस्र and अहिंस्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसा
अहिंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Harmlessness, doing injury to nothing, one of the cardinal virtues of most Hindu sects, but particularly of the Bauddhas and Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हिंसा hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंसित
अहिंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uninjured.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हिंसित hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिंस्र|अहिंस्रः
अहिंस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>Innocuous, innocent, harmless.<BR>f. (-स्रा)<BR>The name of a plant, commonly Kurkavali: see कर्कटा.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and हिंस्रा injurious: than which there is none more so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिका
अहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and हा to go or abandon, ङिक and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिकान्त|अहिकांत|अहिकान्तः
अहिकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a serpent, and कान्त beloved; snakes being supposed to feed upon air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिच्छत्र|अहिच्छत्रः
अहिच्छत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 The name of a country.<BR>2 A milky or thorny plant: see मेषशृङ्गी.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Sugar.<BR>2 A city.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, and छत्र a parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिजित्
अहिजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 Also of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and जित् who conquers, from जि with क्विप् affix; subduing a demon in the form of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहित|अहितः
अहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hostile, inimical.<BR>2 Hurtful, prejudicial.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Food, &c. contra indicated in a disease.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and हित friendly, fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितकारिन्
अहितकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Adverse, inimical, acting unkindly.<BR>E.<BR>अहित unkind, कारिन् acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितमनस्
अहितमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Hating, adverse, inimical.<BR>E.<BR>अहित and मनस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहितुण्डिक|अहितुंडिक|अहितुण्डिकः
अहितुण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake-catcher or exhibiter.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and तुण्ड face, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिद्विष्
अहिद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>4 An ichneumon.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and द्विष who hates, from द्विष् to hate, with क्विप् affix; serpent-hater or enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनकुलिका
अहिनकुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The natural enmity subsisting between a snake and an ichneumon.<BR>E.<BR>अहि, नकुल a mungoose, बुन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिनिम्माक
अहिनिम्माक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The slough of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and निर्म्मोक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपति|अहिपतिः
अहिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of ŚEṢA, the sovereign of the snakes; also of VĀSUKI and others.<BR>2 Any large serpent.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, and पति lord; also similar compounds, as अहिनाथः, अहीन्द्रः, अहीशः, अहीश्वरः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिपुत्रक|अहिपुत्रकः
अहिपुत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of boat.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and पुत्रक a son, resembling a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिफेन|अहिफेनं|अहिफेनः
अहिफेन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Opium.<BR>2 The saliva or venom of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, and फेन foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्न|अहिब्रध्नः
अहिब्रध्न<BR>m. (-ध्नः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of the demigods called RUDRAS.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and ब्रधि to bind, नक् Uṇādi affix; having his neck bound with snakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिब्रध्नदेवता
अहिब्रध्नदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The twenty-sixth constellation.<BR>E.<BR>अहिब्रध्न and देवता presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभय|अहिभयं
अहिभय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Mistrust or apprehension of treachery.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and भय fear; fear of a lurking snake as it were.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिभुज्
अहिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>1 GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>अहि and भुज who eats, from भुज and क्विप् affix; snake-eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिमांशु|अहिमांशुः
अहिमांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हिम cold, and अंशु a ray; also similar compounds, as अहिमकर, अहिमरुचि, अहिमतेजस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहिविद्विष्
अहिविद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>1 GARUḌA.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake or VṚTRĀSURA, and विद्विष् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Possessed of, not deprived of.<BR>2 Not outcaste or vile.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हीन deprived of.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A large snake, a serpent.<BR>2 A particular sacrifice, one lasting twelve days.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, and इन superior, or अहन् a day, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीनवादिन्
अहीनवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A witness who is not unit to give evidence.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हीनबादी a defective witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहीरणि|अहीरणिः
अहीरणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A kind of snake, said to be two-headed.<BR>E.<BR>अहि, इर to move, and अणि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहुत|अहुतः
अहुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unoffered, unsacrificed.<BR>2 Uncalled, unsummoned.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Religious meditation and prayer, considered as one of the five great sacraments.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हु to sacrifice, or ह्वे to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहे
अहे<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying.<BR>1 Rejection.<BR>2 Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतु|अहेतुः
अहेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Absence of cause or reason.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुक
अहेतुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हेतुक having cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुता
अहेतुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Absence of cause or necessity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अहेतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेतुत्व
अहेतुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Absence of reason or cause.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to अहेतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहेरु|अहेरुः
अहेरु<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus): see शतमूली.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हि to go, and रु affix; immoveable; alluding to the number of its roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहो
अहो<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and interjection of,<BR>1 Reproach, (fie!)<BR>2 Compassion.<BR>3 Regret, (ah! oh!)<BR>4 Calling, (ho! hola!)<BR>5 Praise, flattery, approbation.<BR>6 Fatigue, weariness.<BR>7 Surprise, (ah!) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">Page102</a>]<BR>8 Doubt, deliberation, (either, or.)<BR>9 Contempt, sneering.<BR>10 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. हा to go, and डो aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=101" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोरात्र|अहोरात्रः
अहोरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A day of twenty-four hours or thirty Muhūrtas, from sun-rise to sun-rise.<BR>n. or ind. (-त्रम्)<BR>Day and night, continually, always.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोबत
अहोबत<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of calling;<BR>2 Of compassion;<BR>3 Of fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहोही
अहोही<BR>ind.<BR>In a variegated or wonderful manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्नाय
अह्नाय<BR>ind.<BR>Soon, instantly.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ह्नाय from ह्नु to take away or secrete, with घञ् affix, and य substituted for the ब to which the radical त is changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्रीक|अह्रीकः
अह्रीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. and ह्रीक bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्वला
अह्वला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The marking nut plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. ह्वे to emulate, and डल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ<BR>The second letter of the alphabet, corresponding to A long, as in far, and written in the Roman character A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of reminiscence. (ah! oh!)<BR>2 A conjunction disjunctive, (but.)<BR>3 A particle of compassion, (ah! alas!)<BR>4 A conjunction copulative, (and.) This particle remains unaltered in orthography even before vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ or आङ्<BR>A particle, and prefix to words, implying;<BR>1 Diminution, (a little.)<BR>2 Limit, inceptive, (from, from thence, or that time.)<BR>3 Limit conclusive, (until, unto, as far as.)<BR>4 Prefixed to verbs it extends or reverses their meaning, as रुह to rise, आरुह to ascend, to mount, and गम to go, आगम to come.<BR>5 In composition with nouns it forms indeclinables, either crude, as आजानु to the knee, or with the terminations of the objective or ablative case, as आसमुद्रं or आसमद्रात् as far as to the ocean.<BR>6 A particle of menace or of pain, (ah! alas!) this is more correctly written आस्.<BR>E.<BR>आप् to pervade, to obtain, and डाङ affix, प is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ<BR>m. (-आः)<BR>A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आ
आ<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of assent, yes, verily.<BR>E.<BR>अस to go, क्विप् affix, अ becomes आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पन|आकंपन
आकम्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कपि to tremble, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्पित|आकंपित|आकम्पितं
आकम्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed, कपि to shake, and क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकम्प्र|आकंप्र
आकम्प्र<BR>mfn. (-म्प्रः-म्प्रा-म्प्रं)<BR>Trembling, shaking, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कपि to shake; रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर|आकरः
आकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mine.<BR>2 A multitude.<BR>3 Best, excellent.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed, कृ to make, &c. अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिन्
आकरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Mineral, produced in a mine, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आकर and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णन|आकर्णनं
आकर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कर्ण to hear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्णित
आकर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heard.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् कर्ण to hear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्ष|आकर्षः
आकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Pulling, hauling^1.<BR>2 Pulling to or towards, dragging, attracting.<BR>3 Attraction, fascination.<BR>4 Magnetic attraction.<BR>5 A magnet, a loadstone.<BR>6 A dice or die.<BR>7 Playing with dice.<BR>8 A board for such a game.<BR>9 Drawing the bow.<BR>10 An organ of sense.<BR>11 Spasm.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कृष to draw or make furrows, घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षक|आकर्षकः
आकर्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Attractive, what draws or attracts.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A magnet or loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>आकर्ष attraction, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Pulling, drawing, attracting.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A crooked stick, for pulling down fruit, &c.<BR>2 Any instrument for pulling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृष to pull, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिक
आकर्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Magnetic, attractive.<BR>E.<BR>आकर्ष and ष्ठल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षित
आकर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drawn, attracted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृष to draw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिन्
आकर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>Attractive.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A rod with a hook at the end to pull down the boughs of trees, for the purpose of gathering the fruit.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृष to draw, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलन|आकलनं
आकलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Counting, reckoning.<BR>3 Confinement, binding.<BR>4 Laying hold of.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कल to count, sound, &c. and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकलित
आकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Counted, reckoned.<BR>2 Seized, held, bound.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्ग before कल to count, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्प|आकल्पः
आकल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 Ornament, decoration.<BR>2 Encreasing, adding to, improving.<BR>3 Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृप to be able, to be weak, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकल्पक|आकल्पकः
आकल्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Remembering with regret, missing.<BR>2 Fainting, loss of sense or perception.<BR>4 Darkness.<BR>4 A knot or joint.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कल्प from कृप to be able, to be weak, &c. and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकष|आकषः
आकष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A touchstone.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कष to injure, and अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषक
आकषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Touching, assaying.<BR>E.<BR>वुन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकषिक
आकषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Touching, testing.<BR>E.<BR>आकष and ष्ठल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकस्मिक|आकस्मिकं
आकस्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sudden, unexpected, causeless.<BR>E.<BR>अक स्मात् and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षत्
आकाङ्क्षत्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षन्-ङ्क्ष-अन्ती-ङ्क्षत्)<BR>1 Wishing, expecting.<BR>2 Looking at, to, or towards.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before काङ्क्षि to desire, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षनीय
आकाङ्क्षनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Desirable, to be desired or expected.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before काक्षि to desire, अनीयर् affix; also आकाङ्क्षितब्य (-ब्यः-ब्या-ब्यं) and आकाङ्ख्य (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्यं) with तब्य or यत् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षा|आकांक्षा
आकाङ्क्षा<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षा)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Purpose, intention.<BR>3 Looking at, to, or towards.<BR>4 Enquiry, asking.<BR>5 The presence of a word in a sentence indispensable to the sense.<BR>6 The significancy of a word.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed to काक्षि to desire, अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षित|आकांक्षित
आकाङ्क्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>2 Asked, enquired.<BR>3 Regarded, looked at.<BR>4 Wanted, necessary.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before काङ्क्षि to desire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाङ्क्षिन्|आकांक्षिन्
आकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>1 Wishing, wishful.<BR>2 Asking, enquiring, expectant.<BR>E.<BR>आकाङ्क्षा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाय|आकायः
आकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A funeral pile.<BR>2 Abode, residence.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चि to collect, घञ् affix, च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकार|आकारः
आकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Hint, sign, token.<BR>2 Form.<BR>3 The letter आ.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कृ to make, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=102" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगुप्ति|आकारगुप्तिः
आकारगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Dissimulation.<BR>E.<BR>आकार and गुप्ति concealment, suppressing all sign or indication of the feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारगोपन|आकारगोपनं
आकारगोपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारण|आकारणं
आकारण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Calling, a call or summons.<BR>E.<BR>आङ, कृ to make or do in the causal form, and ल्यु affix, fem. affix टाप्; sometimes written आकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवत्|आकारवन्त्
आकारवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Symmetrical, handsome, well formed.<BR>E.<BR>आकार form, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारित
आकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Called, summoned.<BR>2 Stipulated, agreed.<BR>3 Demanded, exacted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृ to make, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिक|आकालिकं
आकालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Momentary, instantaneous.<BR>2 Unseasonable, improper with respect to time.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. काल time, ठक् affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकालिकत्व
आकालिकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Unseasonableness, suddenness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाश|आकाशं|आकाशः
आकाश<BR>mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>1 The fifth element, aether, the sky or atmosphere.<BR>2 Brahma as identical with aether.<BR>3 Space, vacuity.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and काशृ to shine, घञ् affix; every where shining; Ākāśa is the subtle and ethereal^1 fluid, supposed to fill and pervade the universe, and to be the peculiar vehicle of life and sound.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशकक्षा
आकाशकक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>The horizon.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and कक्षा girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशज
आकाशज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in the sky.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशजननिन्
आकाशजननिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>A loop-hole, a casement, an embrasure.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and जनविन् what generates, giving air and light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशदीप|आकाशदीपः
आकाशदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A lamp or torch lighted in honour of LAKṢMI or VIṢṆU, and elevated on a pole in the open air at the Dewali festival, in the month Kartik.<BR>2 A beacon, a lanthorn on a pole.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and दीप a lamp; also आकाशप्रदीपः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशभाषित
आकाशभाषित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Speaking outside or off the stage, or a suppositious speech, which is replied to as if it had been spoken, (in dramatic language.)<BR>3 A voice or sound in the air.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and भाषित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमण्डल
आकाशमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The celestial sphere.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमांसी
आकाशमांसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A plant, small Jaṭāmāṃsī, (Valeriana Jatamansi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशमूली
आकाशमूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and मूली having roots; having its root in air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशयान
आकाशयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A heavenly car, one moving through the air.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and यान vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशरक्षिन्
आकाशरक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A warder, a watchman on the outer battlements.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and रक्षिन् a guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवर्त्मन्
आकाशवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>The atmosphere, the firmament, the air.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवल्ली
आकाशवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A sort of creeper, a parasite, (Cassyta filiformis.)<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशवाणी
आकाशवाणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A voice from heaven.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशसलिल|आकाशसलिलं
आकाशसलिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Rain.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and सलिल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशस्थ
आकाशस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Abiding in the sky.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशीय
आकाशीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Atmospherical. Also आकाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशे
आकाशे<BR>ind.<BR>In the air, a stage direction, implying something said by or to a person out of sight.<BR>E.<BR>7th case of आकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकाशेश|आकाशेशः
आकाशेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 INDRA, as ruler of the firmament.<BR>2 (In law) A helpless person, as a child, a woman, a pauper or invalid.<BR>E.<BR>आकाश and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकिञ्चन|आकिंचन|आकिंचनं|आकिञ्चनं
आकिञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Poverty.<BR>E.<BR>अकिञ्चन poor, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्ण|आकीर्णं|आकीर्ण्ण
आकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Filled, overspread.<BR>2 Crowded.<BR>3 Impervious.<BR>4 Spread.<BR>5 Scattered.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कॄ to scatter, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्णता
आकीर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Fulness.<BR>2 Crowd, multitude.<BR>E.<BR>आकीर्ण filled, तल् affix; also आकीर्णत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चन|आकुंचनं|आकुञ्चनं
आकुञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Compression, contraction, shrinking.<BR>2 Collecting, heaping.<BR>3 Curving, flexure.<BR>4 Contortion.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कुचि to contract, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुञ्चित
आकुञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bent, contracted.<BR>2 Twisted, contorted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कुचि to contract, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुण्ठित
आकुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Confounded, abashed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कुण्ठित abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Confounded, confused, flurried.<BR>2 Confused (in order), disordered.<BR>3 Incoherent, contradictory.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कुल to accumulate, and क affix; not self-possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलत्व|आकुलत्वं
आकुलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Confusion, perplexity, bewilderment.<BR>E.<BR>आकुल and त्व affix; also with तल् affix आकुलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलित
आकुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bewildered, flurried, agitated.<BR>2 Distressed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कुल, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीकृत
आकुलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bewildered, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>आकुल and कृत made with च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुष्ठ
आकुष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Expelled, extracted.<BR>E.<BR>आकुष to extract, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूत|आकूतं
आकूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Meaning, intention.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, कूङ to cry, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृति|आकृतिः
आकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Form, figure.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 Tribe, species.<BR>4 A metre: a stanza of four lines, with twenty-two syllables to each line.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृ to make or do, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिच्छत्रा
आकृतिच्छत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्ट|आकृष्टं
आकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Pulled, drawn.<BR>2 Attracted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृष to drag, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्यमाण
आकृष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Drawing, attracting.<BR>E.<BR>आकृष to draw, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टवत्
आकृष्टवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Pulling, dragging, pulling up or out.<BR>2 Pulling to, attracting.<BR>3 Charming, fascinating.<BR>E.<BR>आकृष्ट and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टि|आकृष्टिः
आकृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Pulling, dragging.<BR>2 Drawing, attraction.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before कृष to drag, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकोकेर|आकोकेरः
आकोकेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The constellation Capricornus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकौशल
आकौशल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Inexpertness, want of skill or practice.<BR>E.<BR>अकुशल unskilful, affix अण् and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्द|आक्रंदः|आक्रन्दः
आक्रन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Who checks or restrains.<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Crying, crying out.<BR>2 Calling.<BR>3 Weeping, sobbing.<BR>4 Sound.<BR>5 Violence.<BR>6 Furious or violent combat.<BR>7 A friend.<BR>8 A brother.<BR>9 A king, a lord.<BR>10 A usurper.<BR>11 A king who [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">Page104</a>] prevents an ally from aiding another.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्रन्द to cry, to sound, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=103" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रन्दिक|आक्रंदिक
आक्रन्दिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Going where sounds of distress are heard.<BR>E.<BR>आक्रन्द and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रम|आक्रमः
आक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going over or beyond.<BR>2 Surpassing.<BR>3 Spreading over or upon.<BR>4 Overloading.<BR>5 Attaining, overcoming, obtaining.<BR>6 Invading, attacking, falling upon.<BR>7 Might, valour.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रम to go, to mount, ascend, surpass, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमण|आक्रमणं
आक्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going over or beyond.<BR>2 Overpowering, subduing.<BR>3 Spreading or extending over or upon.<BR>4 Attacking, marching against, invading.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमणीय
आक्रमणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be attacked.<BR>2 To be surpassed or overcome.<BR>3 To be seized.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रम to go, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्त|आक्रांत|आक्रान्तः
आक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Surpassed, surmounted.<BR>2 Overcome, overrun.<BR>3 Pained, distressed.<BR>4 Accompanied, attended.<BR>5 Overspread.<BR>6 Obtained, possessed.<BR>7 Agitated or overcome by, as a feeling.<BR>E.<BR>आक्रम to mount, surpass, &c. and part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रान्ति|आक्रांतिः|आक्रान्तिः
आक्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Going over or beyond.<BR>2 Overpowering.<BR>3 Might, valour.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रम to go, affix क्तिन्: see आक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रामक|आक्रामकः
आक्रामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Invading, assailing<BR>2 Overrunning.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रम to go, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड|आक्रीडः
आक्रीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A royal garden.<BR>2 Sport, pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्रीड to play, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडन|आक्रीडनं
आक्रीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sporting, taking pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>आक्रीड to sport, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडिन्
आक्रीडिन्<BR>mfn. (-डी-डिनी-डि)<BR>Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>आक्रीड to play, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुष्ट
आक्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Cursed.<BR>2 Accused, calumniated.<BR>3 Abused.<BR>4 Vociferated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रश to call, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोश|आक्रोशः
आक्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Abuse, censuring, a curse or oath.<BR>2 Vociferousness, calling aloud.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्रुश to call, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशक|आक्रोशकः
आक्रोशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Abusing, abusive.<BR>2 Vociferous.<BR>E.<BR>आक्रुश to call, वुञ्^1 aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशन|आक्रोशनं
आक्रोशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Curse, imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्रुश to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशनीय
आक्रोशनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be accursed, censurable, reprovable.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्रुश to cry, अनीयर् affix; also आक्रुश्य and आक्रोशितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षद्यूतिक
आक्षद्यूतिक<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Effected or completed by gambling.<BR>E.<BR>आक्षद्यूत and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपण|आक्षपणं
आक्षपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Fasting, or purification by fasting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्षप to endure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाटिक|आक्षपाटिकः
आक्षपाटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a law suit, पट to go, causal form, उक affix; also आक्षपाटिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाद|आक्षपादः
आक्षपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A logician.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष dispute, पाद a division, अण affix; also अक्षपाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षार|आक्षारः
आक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Accusation, calumny.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्षर to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारण|आक्षारणं
आक्षारण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Calumnious accusation.<BR>2 Abuse, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्षर to go, with युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारित|आक्षारितं
आक्षारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>2 Accused of adultery or fornication.<BR>3 Falsely accused, of such crimes in particular.<BR>4 Guilty, criminal.<BR>5 Reviled, abused.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्षर to go, part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिक|आक्षिकः
आक्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating or belonging to a die, to gambling, &c.<BR>2 Won at dice.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree. (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A gambling debt, money lost at play.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष a die, &c. and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिकपण|आक्षिकपणः
आक्षिकपण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A stake, a wager, a bet.<BR>E.<BR>आक्षिक and पण a wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिपत्
आक्षिपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पती-पत्)<BR>1 Excelling, so as to reproach or put to shame others.<BR>2 Reviling, abusing.<BR>3 Tossing.<BR>4 Sending.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्षिप् to throw, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्त
आक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Cast, thrown, tossed.<BR>2 Thrown down or away.<BR>3 Borne, carried.<BR>4 Reviled, abused, blamed, ridiculed.<BR>5 Equal or equivalent to.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्षिप to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीब|आक्षीबः
आक्षीब<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>A plant, (Morunga guilandina and hyperanthera): see अक्षीब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेप|आक्षेपः
आक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Throw, toss.<BR>2 Abuse, reviling.<BR>3 Censure, blame, reproach.<BR>4 Attraction.<BR>5 A figure in rhetoric, (irony.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, क्षिप to throw or send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपक|आक्षेपकः
आक्षेपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Convulsion, spasm.<BR>3 A detractor, a calumniator or accuser.<BR>4 A thrower.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before क्षिप to toss, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षैत्रज्ञ
आक्षैत्रज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Spiritual ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. क्षेत्रज्ञ wise, and ष्यञ affix, the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोट|आक्षोटः
आक्षोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A tree, (see पीलु,) growing in mountains: in Hindi, the corresponding name implies the walnut: see अक्षोट and आक्षोड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोड|आक्षोडः
आक्षोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A kind of Pilu, a tree so named, (Careya arborea): see अक्षोड, अक्षोट and पीलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोद
आक्षोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A Brahman of the Ṛkṣoda mountain.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्षोद and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोदन|आक्षोदनं
आक्षोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख|आखः
आख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A spade, a hoe.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण्डल|आखंडलः|आखण्डलः
आखण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and खण्ड to break, अलच् affix; mountain-breaking, foe-destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखन|आखनः
आखन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A spade.<BR>3 A digger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिक|आखनिकः
आखनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>3 A hog.<BR>4 A spade.<BR>5 A digger, a ditcher, a miner.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, and इकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकवक
आखनिकवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spade.<BR>2 A digger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, before खन to dig, इकविक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखर|आखरः
आखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A spade.<BR>2 A digger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, डर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखात|आखातं|आखातः
आखात<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>A natural pond: see अखात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखान|आखानः
आखान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A spade.<BR>2 A digger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखु|आखुः
आखु<BR>m. (-खुः)<BR>1 A rat, a mouse.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 A sort of tree: see देबताड.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खन to dig, and कु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुकर्णी
आखुकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>The name of a plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>आखु a mouse, and कर्ण an ear; the leaves are compared to the ears of a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुग|आखुगः
आखुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>आखु a rat, and ग who goes; GAṆEŚA is represented riding on a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=104" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुघात|आखुघातः
आखुघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Śūdra or man of low cast and profession, lit. a rat-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and घात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपर्णिका
आखुपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see आखुकर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपर्णी
आखुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुपाषाण|आखुपाषाणः
आखुपाषाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of mineral, a loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and पाषाण a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुभुज्
आखुभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुरथ|आखुरथः
आखुरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and रथ a carriage; whose vehicle is a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुविषहा
आखुविषहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A kind of grass: (Andropogon serratum.)<BR>E.<BR>आखु, बिष venom, and हा what destroys; considered as a remedy for the bite of a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखूत्थ|आखूत्थः
आखूत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>The rising up or coming of rats, a swarm of rats.<BR>E.<BR>आखु and उत्थ from उत् and स्था with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेट|आखेटः
आखेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Chase, hunting.<BR>2 Terror, fright.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, खिट to alarm, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटक|आखेटकः
आखेटक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Hunting, a hunter.<BR>2 Frightening, frightful.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Hunting.<BR>E.<BR>आखेट and कन् pleonastic affix; or आङ् with खिट and खुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटशीर्षक|आखेटशीर्षकं
आखेटशीर्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A cavern, a mine.<BR>E.<BR>आखेट terrifying, and शीर्ष the head or principal, क affix: very gloomy and terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिक|आखेटिकः
आखेटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Who or what hunts.<BR>2 Terrible, frightful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hound.<BR>2 A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>आखेट chase, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखोट|आखोटः
आखोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The walnut tree.<BR>E.<BR>see अक्षोट, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>A name or appellation.<BR>E.<BR>ख्या to say, आङ् prefixed, अङ् and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, spoken.<BR>2 Called, declared.<BR>3 Made known.<BR>4 Inflected, declined, conjugated.<BR>E.<BR>part. past. of आख्या to say, to speak, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यान|आख्यानं
आख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A tale, a legend.<BR>2 Saying, declaring.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ख्या to tell, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आख्यायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A messenger, a teller, an announcer or relater.<BR>f. (-यिका)<BR>A tale, a true or probable story.<BR>E.<BR>आख्या to say, ण्वुल् affix, यत्; inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be said.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ख्या to say, affix यत्; also आख्यातब्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Arrived, come.<BR>2 Received, obtained.<BR>3 Living or residing in.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत्य
आगत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having arrived.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तब्य
आगन्तब्य<BR>mfn. (-ब्यः-ब्या-ब्यं)<BR>What will come, what is likely to arrive.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and गम to go, तब्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तु|आगंतु|आगन्तुः
आगन्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>1 Coming, arriving.<BR>2 Incidental, adventitious.<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 A guest.<BR>2 A stranger, a new comer.<BR>3 An accident, any accidental hurt or wound.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, to come, तु affix; म becomes न; also आगान्तु and आगन्तुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगन्तुक|आगंतुक|आगन्तुकं
आगन्तुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Incidental, adventitious, (as pleasure, pain, ornament, &c.)<BR>2 Stray.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A stranger, a new comer.<BR>2 A guest.<BR>E.<BR>आगन्तु and कन् affix, what comes and goes; what is not inseparably inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम|आगमं|आगमः
आगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Arrival, coming, approach.<BR>2 A Śāstra or work on sacred science in general, supposed to be of divine origin. A Tantra or any work inculcating the mystical worship of SIVA and ŚAKTI.<BR>4 A grammatical augment, a syllable or letter inserted in any part of the radical word.<BR>5 Record, title deed, legal title, a voucher or written testimony, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ before गम to go, to come, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमन|आगमनं
आगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Arriving, coming.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनिरपेक्ष
आगमनिरपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Independent of a written voucher or title.<BR>E.<BR>आगम and निरपेक्षा disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमय्य
आगमय्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having explored or discovered.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमरहित
आगमरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Devoid of a written title or voucher.<BR>2 Without a Śāstra.<BR>E.<BR>आगम and रहित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमसापेक्ष
आगमसापेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>With or supported by legal vouchers.<BR>E.<BR>आगम and सापेक्ष regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमापायिन्
आगमापायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Transient, of short duration.<BR>E.<BR>आगम and अपायिन् separating, going at the time of arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमित|आगमितं
आगमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Read over, perused, studied.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed to गम in the causal form; participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्य
आगम्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 To be approached, accessible.<BR>2 To be acquired.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम with यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस्<BR>n. (-गः)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Transgression, offence, fault.<BR>E.<BR>आग substituted for इण to go, असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Very deep: see अगाध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगान्तु|आगान्तुः
आगान्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>A guest: see आगन्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Arriving, coming.<BR>2 Future.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before गम to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगार|आगारं
आगार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A house, a dwelling: see अगार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाह|आगारदाहः
आगारदाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Arson, setting a house on fire.<BR>E.<BR>आगार and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारदाहिन्
आगारदाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>An incendiary.<BR>E.<BR>आगारदाह arson, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर्<BR>f. (-गूः)<BR>An agreement: see आगू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरब
आगुरब<BR>mfn. (-बः-बी-बं)<BR>1 Consisting of or containing Agallochum.<BR>2 Very heavy.<BR>E.<BR>अगुरु and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगू
आगू<BR>f. (-गूः)<BR>1 An agreement.<BR>E.<BR>आगम to come, डू affix, or आङ् prefixed to गू to come and क्विन् affix; also आगुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र<BR>n. (-ध्रं)<BR>The place where a sacrificial fire is kindled.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire, and इन्ध to kindle; see अग्नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to fire or its deity.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 The name of a city, (Devikote, on the Coromandel Coast.)<BR>2 Blood.<BR>3 Ghee or boiled butter.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTI.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 The wife of AGNI.<BR>2 The southeast quarter, of which AGNI is the regent.<BR>E.<BR>अग्नि fire or its deity, ढक् affix which leaves ण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह|आग्रहः
आग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Favour, patronage.<BR>2 Seizing, taking.<BR>3 Surpassing, surmounting.<BR>4 Power, ability.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ग्रह to take, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायण|आग्रहायणः
आग्रहायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A month so called, the first of the Hindu year according to some systems, (November-December.)<BR>E.<BR>अप beginning, and हायन a year; also अग्रहायण, the अ being unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिक|आग्रहायणिकः
आग्रहायणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Āgrahāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रहायण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणी
आग्रहायणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The name of a constellation consisting of three stars, one of which is λ Orionis, figured by an antelope's [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">Page106</a>] head, hence also मृगशिरस्.<BR>2 The day of full moon in the month Āgrahāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>अग्रहायण and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=105" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायण
आग्रायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A sacrifice offered when the new rice or wheat ripens.<BR>E.<BR>अग्र chief, अयन coming, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रायणेष्टि
आग्रायणेष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A particular ceremony: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>आग्रायण and इष्टि a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टक|आघट्टकः
आघट्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (the red sort of Achyranthes.)<BR>2 A rubber, what effects friction.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घदृ and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टन
आघट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Friction, rubbing, contact.<BR>2 Shaking.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घदृ to move, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टित
आघट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Touched, rubbed.<BR>2 Shaken.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घदृ to move, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्ष|आघर्षः
आघर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Rubbing, friction.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घृष to rub, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षण|आघर्षणं
आघर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rubbing, friction.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A brush, a rubber.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घृष to rub, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षित
आघर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rubbed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घृष, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाट|आघाटः
आघाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A limit, a boundary.<BR>2 A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, घट to endeavour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघात|आघातः
आघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Killing, striking.<BR>2 A blow, a wound.<BR>3 A slaughter-house, a place for killing animals or victims.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, हन to kill or injure, in the participial form; घ is substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातन|आघातनं
आघातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Striking, killing.<BR>2 A slaughter-house.<BR>E.<BR>आहन्, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघार|आघारः
आघार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Ghee or boiled butter.<BR>2 Sprinkling.<BR>3 Sprinkling ghee at certain sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, घृ to sprinkle, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णन|आघूर्णनं
आघूर्णन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Rolling, tossing.<BR>2 Whirling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घूर्ण to roll, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णित|आघूर्णितं
आघूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rolled, rolling.<BR>2 Whirled round.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घूर to roll, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषण|आघोषणं
आघोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A crying or proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before घुष to sound, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्नत्
आघ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नन्ती-घ्नत्)<BR>Striking, beating.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हन to kill, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राण|आघ्राणं
आघ्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Smelling.<BR>2 Satisfaction, satiety.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, घ्रा to smell, युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रात|आघ्रातः
आघ्रात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Smelled, scented.<BR>2 Surmounted, surpassed.<BR>3 Satisfied, satiated.<BR>E.<BR>क्त participial affix after आघ्रा to smell, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्क्षी|आंक्षी
आङ्क्षी<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षी)<BR>A musical instrument, a tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्ग|आंग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Bodily, corporeal.<BR>2 Having limbs or parts, or relating to them.<BR>3 Relating to the inferior persons of a drama, to a portion of the Vedas, &c.: see अङ्ग.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A soft delicate form or body.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग a body, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गार|आंगार|आंगारं|आङ्गारं
आङ्गार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A multitude of firebrands.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गार a torch, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गक|आंगक|आङ्गकः
आङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ruler of the country Aṅga.<BR>2 An inhabitant of the same.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिक|आंगिक|आङ्गिकः
आङ्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Bodily, corporeal.<BR>2 Gesticulated, expressed by bodily action, (dramatic sentiment, passion, &c. exhibited by attitude, gesture, &c.)<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A player on a tabor or drum.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्ग the body, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गिरस|आंगिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आङ्गिरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI, preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गिरस् a saint so named, patronymic affix अण्; AṄGIRAS being the father of VṚHASPATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आङ्गुलिक
आङ्गुलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Like a finger.<BR>E.<BR>अङ्गुली and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षमाण
आचक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Saying, declaring.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चक्ष to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षुस्
आचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A learned man, a Paṇḍita.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चक्ष to speak, उमि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुर्य्य|आचतुर्य
आचतुर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR>E.<BR>अचतुर and यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम|आचमः
आचम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Rincing the mouth: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमन|आचमनं
आचमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rincing the mouth, sipping water before religious ceremonies, meals, &c. from the palm of the hand, and spitting it out again; the ceremony also includes touching the body in various parts.<BR>2 Gargling the throat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चमु to eat, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनक|आचमनकं|आचमनकः
आचमनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spitting pot.<BR>E.<BR>आचमन, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीय|आचमनीयं
आचमनीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Water for rincing the mouth.<BR>2 A gargle.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चम to eat, affix अनीयर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्य
आचम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having rinced the mouth, having sipped and ejected a little water.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चम to eat, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण|आचरणं
आचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Following, observing, usage, practice.<BR>2 An instituted rite or rule of conduct.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणीय
आचरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Right, proper, what is to be followed or observed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरत्
आचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रन्)<BR>Following, practising, observing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरित|आचरितं
आचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Observed, practised, either as a rite or usuage.<BR>2 Usual, customary.<BR>2 Enjoined, fixed by rule.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्य्य|आचर्य
आचर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be gone to or approached.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचान्त|आचांत|आचान्तः
आचान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Sipped and ejected, (as water.)<BR>2 One who has rinced his mouth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चम to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम|आचामः
आचाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Sipping water, rincing the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चम to eat, affix घज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्य
आचाम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Rincing the mouth, &c.<BR>2 Water so used.<BR>3 A gargle.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चम to eat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार|आचारः
आचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An established rule of conduct, an ordinance, an institute, a precept.<BR>2 Custom, practice, usage.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारबर्ज्जित
आचारबर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Irregular, out of rule.<BR>2 Outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>आचार an institute, and बर्ज्जित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारहीन
आचारहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Outcaste, void of decent or established practices.<BR>E.<BR>आचार and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिक
आचारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Conformable to rule or practice.<BR>2 Prescriptive, authorised.<BR>E.<BR>आचार and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिन्
आचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Following established rites or practice.<BR>E.<BR>आचार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्य|आचार्य|आचार्यः|आचार्य्यः
आचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A spiritual guide or teacher; he who invests the student with the sacrificial thread, and instructs him in the Vedas, the law of sacrifice, and religious mysteries.<BR>2 A name of DROṆA, the teacher of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A spiritual [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">Page107</a>] preceptress.<BR>f. (-र्य्यानी)<BR>The wife of an Ācārya or holy teacher.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चर to go, ण्यत् affix, in the fem. टाप् or ङीप् with आनुक inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=106" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्यत्व|आचार्यत्व|आचार्यत्वं
आचार्य्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The office or proficiency of a holy teacher.<BR>E.<BR>आचार्य्य and त्व affix; also with तल्, आचार्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्यमिश्र|आचार्यमिश्र
आचार्य्यमिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Venerable, honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्य्योपासन|आचार्योपासन
आचार्य्योपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Waiting upon or serving the spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>आचार्य्य and उपासना worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित|आचितं|आचितः
आचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heaped, accumulated.<BR>2 Covered.<BR>3 Spread, diffused.<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 A measure of ten Bharas.<BR>2 A cart load.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and the past participle of चिञ् to collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिक
आचितिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Holding an Ācita.<BR>E.<BR>आचित and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितीन
आचितीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Holding or equal to an Ācita.<BR>E.<BR>आचित and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचूषण|आचूषणं
आचूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Suction.<BR>2 Application of cupping glasses or horns to the skin, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चूष to suck, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छ|आछ
आच्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ.) आच्छि (आञ्छति)<BR>To lengthen or stretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छन्न|आच्छन्नं
आच्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Covered.<BR>2 Clothed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before च्छद to cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाक|आच्छाकः
आच्छाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Morinda tinctoria.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद|आच्छादः|आछाद
आच्छाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Cloth, clothes.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, छद to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादन|आच्छादनं|आछादन
आच्छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cloth, clothes.<BR>2 Covering, disappearance.<BR>3 A covering, a sheath, mantle, cloak, &c.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादित|आच्छादितं
आच्छादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered.<BR>2 Clothed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before छद to cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाद्य
आच्छाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be covered or clothed.<BR>ind.<BR>Having clothed or put. on.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before छद to cover, causal form, यत् or ल्यप् affix; also आच्छादनीय and आच्छादितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छिन्न
आच्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Cut, cut off.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before छिद to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरित|आच्छुरितं|आछुरित
आच्छुरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A horse laugh.<BR>2 Making a noise with the finger nails by rubbing them on one another.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, छुर to cut, क्त affix; also आच्छुरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरितक|आच्छुरितकं|आछुरितक
आच्छुरितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेद|आच्छेदः
आच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Cutting, cutting off, excision.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before छिद to cut, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदन|आच्छेदनं
आच्छेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Excision.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, छिद to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोदन|आच्छोदनं|आछोदन
आच्छोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hunting, the chase.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, चुद to command, with ल्युट् affix, च becomes छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज|आजं|आजः
आज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Oiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, अज to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजक|आजकं
आजक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flock of goats.<BR>E.<BR>अज a goat, and बञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजकार|आजकारः
आजकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA'S bull.<BR>E.<BR>आज from अज to go, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजगव|आजगवं
आजगव<BR>n. (-बं)<BR>The bow of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>see अजकाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानेय|आजानेयः
आजानेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A horse of a good breed.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, घञ् affix, आज going; आनेय to be taken: who carries the rider through all opposition, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजि|आजिः
आजि<BR>f. (-जिः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Level ground.<BR>3 An instant.<BR>4 Abuse, reviling.<BR>5 Going.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, इन् Uṇādi affix, and आङ् prefixed or अज with इण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिक्रिया
आजिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Fighting, making war.<BR>E.<BR>आजि and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिगीषु
आजिगीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Ambitious, desirous to excel or overcome.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before जि to conquer, in the desiderative form, affix उस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिग्रह
आजिग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>What takes or seizes.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ग्रह to take, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव|आजीवः
आजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, जीव to live, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवन|आजीवनं
आजीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Livelihood.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before जीव to live, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवनार्थ
आजीवनार्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>Means of livelihood or subsistence, business, profession.<BR>E.<BR>आजीवन and अर्थ means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्य
आजीव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Habitable, fertile.<BR>2 To be practised as a means of living.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before जीव्य to be lived, in or by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजुर्
आजुर्<BR>f. (-जूः)<BR>Working without wages.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, जुर् to become old, क्विप् affix; also आजू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजू
आजू<BR>f. (-जूः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, जु to be quick, क्विप् affix, and the final lengthened; or जन to be born, and डू aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्त|आज्ञप्तः
आज्ञप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Ordered, commanded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञप causal of ज्ञा and क्त affix; also आज्ञापित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्ति|आज्ञप्तिः
आज्ञप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Order, command.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञा to know, with क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>An order, a command.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ज्ञा to know, and अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकर|आज्ञाकरः
आज्ञाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Obeying, obedient, performing an order.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकरण
आज्ञाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Obedience, execution of orders.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाकारिन्
आज्ञाकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Obedient, ministrant, one who obeys or executes orders.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाचक्र|आज्ञाचक्रं
आज्ञाचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>A mystical circle or diagram, one of six described by the Tantras.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञात
आज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ordered, commanded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञा to know, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुयायिन्
आज्ञानुयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Obeying or executing orders, obedient.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा, अनु according to, यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुवर्त्तिन्|आज्ञानुवर्तिन्
आज्ञानुवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Obeying or executing orders.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा, अनु according to, and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानुसारिन्
आज्ञानुसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Obedient, obeying or executing orders.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा, अनु according to, सारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापक|आज्ञापकः
आज्ञापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Giving orders, a commander, commanding.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञा to know, causal form, वुन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापत्र|आज्ञापत्रं
आज्ञापत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An edict, a written order.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and पत्र a page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापन|आज्ञापनं
आज्ञापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Ordering, commanding.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ज्ञा to know, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाप्रतिघात|आज्ञाप्रतिघातः
आज्ञाप्रतिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Disobedience, rebellion.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and प्रति घात rebelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञाभङ्ग|आज्ञाभंग|आज्ञाभङ्गः
आज्ञाभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Disobedience, insubordination, disloyalty.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञावह
आज्ञावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Obedient, subject, ministrant.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and वह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञासम्पादिन्|आज्ञासंपादिन्
आज्ञासम्पादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Obedient, submissive.<BR>E.<BR>आज्ञा and सम्पादिन् who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यप
आज्यप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A Pitṛ or progenitor of a class of Pitṛs who are the sons of PULASTYA, and the ancestors of the Vaiśya order.<BR>E.<BR>आज्य ghee, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=107" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यभास
आज्यभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Offering ghee at certain ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>आज्य and भास what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्चन|आंचनं
आञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Partial extraction of thorns or arrows and the like from the body. आङ् before अञ्च to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जनेय|आंजनेयः|आञ्जनेयः
आञ्जनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of the monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जना the mother of HANUMĀN, and ढक् patronymic affix which leaves एय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आञ्जिनेय|आंजिनेयः|आञ्जिनेयः
आञ्जिनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An insect, a kind of lizard.<BR>E.<BR>अञ्जन antimony, ढक् affix, and इट् inserted; from the blue tint of the animal's back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविक|आटविकः
आटविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wood-man.<BR>E.<BR>अटवी a wood, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटरूष|आटरूषः
आटरूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A tree, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>see अटरुष, the अ being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटि|आटिः
आटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>The Śarāli, a bird so called, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अट to go, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकन|आटीकनं
आटीकन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The leaping motion of a calf.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् prefixed to टीक to go, ल्युट् affix; also written आटीकर and आटीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकर|आटीकरः
आटीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>आटीक leaping, and र who gets or uses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोप|आटोपः
आटोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Pride.<BR>2 Flatulence, borborygmi.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before टुप a Sautra root, to be proud, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बर|आडंबरः|आडम्बरः
आडम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Charge sounded by musical instruments.<BR>2 The roaring of elephants.<BR>3 A drum used in battle.<BR>4 Commencement.<BR>5 The eyelid.<BR>6 Pride, arrogance.<BR>7 Anger, passion.<BR>8 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Rubbing and moulding the body.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दम to tame or subdue, बरच् affix; द is changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडम्बरिन्|आडंबरिन्
आडम्बरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>आडम्बर and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडि|आडिः
आडि<BR>f. (-डिः)<BR>A bird, the Śarāli, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, अड to go, इन् affix; also आटि, आडिका and आटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडू
आडू<BR>m. (-डूः)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. अण to sound, ड and ऊ Uṇādi affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढक|आढकं|आढकः
आढक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-का-कं)<BR>A measure of grain equal to four Prasthas, or containing nearly 7 lbs. 11 oz. avoirdupois: in Bengal an Araka is equal to two mans or 164 lbs. avds.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A kind of pulse, (Cytisus cajan.)<BR>2 A fragrant earth: see तुबरी.<BR>E.<BR>आङ, ढोक to go, irregularly अच, fem. ङीप्^1, or टाप with इक inserted.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकिक|आढकिकः
आढकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Sown with an ĀḌhaka of seed, (a field, &c.)<BR>2 Holding or containing the same.<BR>E.<BR>आढक the measure, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकीन|आढकीनः
आढकीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>आढक, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>1 Opulent, wealthy, rich.<BR>2 Abounding in, productive.<BR>3 Having, being possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ध्ये to consider, to meditate, क irregular aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यङ्करण|आढ्यंकरण
आढ्यङ्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Enriching, or the means of enriching, wealth, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>आढ्य and ख्युन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यचर
आढ्यचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Formerly opulent.<BR>E.<BR>आध्य and चरट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यम्भविष्णु|आढ्यंभविष्णु
आढ्यम्भविष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Becoming rich or eminent.<BR>E.<BR>आढ्य and भी to be, खिष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यम्भावुक|आढ्यंभावुक
आढ्यम्भावुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Becoming rich or eminent.<BR>E.<BR>आढ्य and भू to be, with खुकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणक|आणकः
आणक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Low, inferior: see अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवीन|आणवीनं
आणवीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bearing or fit to bear panic.<BR>E.<BR>अणु panic, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणि|आणिः
आणि<BR>mf. (-णिः)<BR>1 The edge of a sword.<BR>2 The pin of the axle of a cart.<BR>3 A limit, a boundary.<BR>E.<BR>अन to sound, इन् affix, the pen. long; also अणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्ड|आंड|आण्डः
आण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A multitude of eggs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अण्ड and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आण्डीर|आंडीर
आण्डीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having many eggs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आण्ड and ईरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतङ्क|आतंक|आतंकः|आतङ्कः
आतङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 Fear, apprehension.<BR>2 Disease, sickness.<BR>3 Affliction, pain.<BR>4 Fever.<BR>5 The sound of a drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तकि to live in distress, घञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतञ्चन|आतंचनं|आतञ्चनं
आतञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calcining, adding a powder or flux to metals in fusion.<BR>2 The flux so used.<BR>3 Casting any thing into another to effect some change, as butter-milk into fresh milk to turn it.<BR>4 Casting away, destroying.<BR>5 Danger, calamity, as a pestilence or epidemic.<BR>6 Speed, velocity.<BR>7 Gratifying, satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तञ्चु to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतत
आतत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spread, extended.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before तन to spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिता
आततायिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Stealing, persecuting, murdering, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>आततायिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व affix, आततायित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>A felon, a thief, a murderer, incendiary, ravisher, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आतत extended, every where, ई to go, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन|आतनं
आतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sight, view.<BR>2 Spreading, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before तन to spread, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आतप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Sunshine.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तप to heat, to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्र|आतपत्रं
आतपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A large umbrella of silk or leaves, used in the east as a parasol.<BR>E.<BR>आतप sun-shine, त्र what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपत्रक|आतपत्रकं
आतपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A small umbrella, a mat or basket carried on the head as one.<BR>E.<BR>आतपत्र a parasol, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवारण|आतपवारणं
आतपवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A Catta or Indian parasol.<BR>E.<BR>आतप sun-shine, and वारण preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपशुष्क
आतपशुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Dried in the sun, evaporated by the solar heat.<BR>E.<BR>आतप and शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपाभाव|आतपाभावः
आतपाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Shade.<BR>E.<BR>आतप and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर|आतरः
आतर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fare, freight.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तृ to cross or pass over, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतर्पण|आतर्पणं
आतर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Satisfying, satisfaction.<BR>2 Whitening the wall or floor or seat on festival occasions.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तृप to satisfy or to be satisfied, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिन्
आतापिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A kite.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतायिन्
आतायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A kite.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ताय to spread, णिनि affix; it is also read आतापिन्, from तप to be warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतार|आतारः
आतार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fare, freight.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तृ to cross, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आति|आतिः
आति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 Going.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, इण् affix: or Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Proper for a guest.<BR>2 Hispitable, attentive to a guest.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि a guest, and ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>1 Proper for a guest.<BR>2 Hospitable, attentive to a guest.<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Hospitality.<BR>m. (-थ्यः)<BR>A guest.<BR>E.<BR>अतिथि and ज्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरेक्य|आतिरेक्यं
आतिरेक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Excess, superfluity.<BR>E.<BR>अतिरेक exceeding, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=108" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिशय्य|आतिशय्यं
आतिशय्य<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>Excess, quantity.<BR>E.<BR>अतिशय much, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतु|आतुः
आतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तृ to cross, and डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतुर|आतुरः
आतुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Diseased.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before तुर to hasten, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतृप्य|आतृप्यं|आतृप्यः
आतृप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Satisfiable, to be satisfied.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>The custard apple tree, (Annona reticulata.)<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>The fruit.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before तृप to satisfy, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतोद्य|आतोद्यं
आतोद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, तुद to torment, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्त
आत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Taken, accepted.<BR>2 Assumed.<BR>3 Attracted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगन्ध|आत्तगन्धः
आत्तगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>1 Humbled, degraded.<BR>2 Perfumed.<BR>E.<BR>आत्त taken, and गन्ध pride; whose pride is taken down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्तगर्व्व|आत्तगर्व|आत्तगर्व्वः
आत्तगर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Humbled, &c. see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकर्म्मन्|आत्मकर्मन्
आत्मकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>One's own act.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मकृत
आत्मकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Self-executed, done of one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगुप्ता
आत्मगुप्ता<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>A plant, Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, गुप्त hidden; self-preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मग्राहिन्
आत्मग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Selfish, greedy, taking care of one's self, appropriating, taking for one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and ग्राहिन् who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघात|आत्मघातः
आत्मघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Suicide.<BR>2 Heresy, schism.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघातिन्
आत्मघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 A suicide.<BR>2 A heretic, a schismatic, one who disregards the moral or religious institutions of the code.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and घातिन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मघोष|आत्मघोषः
आत्मघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन्, घुषि to sound, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज|आत्मजः
आत्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A son.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 The understanding.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् the body or soul, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मजन्मन्
आत्मजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञ|आत्मज्ञः
आत्मज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A sage, one who knows his own nature and that of spirit. आत्मन् and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मज्ञान
आत्मज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spiritual knowledge, true wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मगत|आत्मगतं
आत्मगत<BR>ind. (-तं)<BR>Apart, to one's self, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्व
आत्मतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The nature of spirit.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and तत्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मतत्वज्ञ
आत्मतत्वज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A sage, especially one versed in the Vedānta doctrines.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मतत्व and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मता
आत्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Identity with self.<BR>2 Spirituality.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and तल् affix; also with त्व affix आत्मत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मत्यागिन्
आत्मत्यागिन्<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>1 A suicide.<BR>2 A heretic, an unbeliever.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and त्यागिन् who deserts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्श|आत्मदर्शः
आत्मदर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and दर्श sight, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मदर्शन
आत्मदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge of man's real nature, spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मद्रोहिन्
आत्मद्रोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Self-tormenting, fretful, miserable.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and द्रोहिन् who torments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मन्
आत्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 The soul.<BR>2 The natural temperament or disposition.<BR>3 BRAHM, the supreme deity and soul of the universe, or more usually in this sense परमात्मा.<BR>4 Life, spirit, the vivifying soul in opposition to the sentient; commonly also जीवात्मा.<BR>5 Body.<BR>6 Care, effort, pains.<BR>7 Firmness.<BR>8 The understanding, the intellect.<BR>9 The mind or faculty of reason.<BR>10 The sun.<BR>11 Fire.<BR>12 Wind, air.<BR>13 A son.<BR>14 The self, the abstract individual.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, अत to go, मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनीन|आत्मनीनं|आत्मनीनः
आत्मनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Existent, sentient.<BR>2 Appropriate, good for, fit for.<BR>3 Suitable, (as diet, &c.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A wife's brother.<BR>3 A jester.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मनेपद|आत्मनेपदं
आत्मनेपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The middle voice, the proper form of the verb.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मने to one's self, पद inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबन्धु|आत्मबन्धुः
आत्मबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>One's own kinsman, a first cousin or father's sister's son, mother's brother's son, mother's sister's son.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् own, and बन्धु relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबुद्धि
आत्मबुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Self-knowledge.<BR>2 One's own knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and बुद्धि knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मबोध|आत्मबोधः
आत्मबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Spiritual instruction.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and बोध causing to know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभाव|आत्मभावः
आत्मभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Proper or peculiar nature.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् own, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभू
आत्मभू<BR>mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु)<BR>Self-born, self-existent.<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Of KĀMADEVA.<BR>3 Of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 And of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मभूत|आत्मभूतः
आत्मभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Self-produced.<BR>2 Own, peculiar, belonging to.<BR>3 Attached to, faithful.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममानिन्
आत्ममानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Respecting one's self, decorous, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and मानिन् respecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ममूली
आत्ममूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi): see दुरालभा.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मम्भरि|आत्मंभरि|आत्मम्भरिः
आत्मम्भरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Selfish, greedy.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and भरि who nourishes, from भृ to nourish, with खि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयाजिन्
आत्मयाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A wise or learned man, one who studies his own nature and that of the soul.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and याजिन् who worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मयोनि|आत्मयोनिः
आत्मयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Of ŚIVA.<BR>3 Of VIṢṆU, and:<BR>4 Of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and योनि the place of birth: see आत्मभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मलोमन्
आत्मलोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>1 The beard.<BR>2 The hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्|आत्मवन्त्
आत्मवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्|आत्मवन्त्
आत्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Prudent, considerate.<BR>3 Selfpossessed, composed, calm.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवत्ता
आत्मवत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>1 Self-resemblance.<BR>2 Proportion, analogy.<BR>3 Prudence, self-regard.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवश|आत्मवशः
आत्मवश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Subjection of the mind, self-controul, self-government.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्
आत्मविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>1 A sensible man, one who knows himself.<BR>2 A wise man, a sage, one who knows the nature of the soul or spirit.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविद्या
आत्मविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मविवृद्धि|आत्मविवृद्धिः
आत्मविवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Self-advantage.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and विवृद्धि encrease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवीर|आत्मवीरः
आत्मवीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Existent, sentient.<BR>2 Appropriate, good for one's self.<BR>3 Suitable, (as diet, &c.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A wife's brother.<BR>2 A jester.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and बीर heroic, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=109" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मवृत्ति|आत्मवृत्तिः
आत्मवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Practising one's duties or occupation.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशक्ति|आत्मशक्तिः
आत्मशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Inherent or own power.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मशुद्धि|आत्मशुद्धिः
आत्मशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Self-purification.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मश्लाघा
आत्मश्लाघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>Boasting.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and श्लाघा praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसंयम|आत्मसंयमः
आत्मसंयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Self-restraint, stoicism.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and संयम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसन्देह|आत्मसंदेह|आत्मसंदेहः
आत्मसन्देह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Internal doubt.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and सन्देह doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसम्भव|आत्मसंभव|आत्मसंभवः
आत्मसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्
आत्मसात्<BR>ind.<BR>One's own.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and सात् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसात्कृत
आत्मसात्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Appropriated, made one's own.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मसात् and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मसिद्धि|आत्मसिद्धिः
आत्मसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Self-advantage.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महत्या
आत्महत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Suicide, self-destruction.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महन्
आत्महन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>1 A suicide, a self-murderer.<BR>2 A heretic, an unbeliever.<BR>3 A priest in a temple, a servant or attendant upon an idol.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and हन् who kills or destroys, self-destroying; the priest subsisting by appropriating to himself offerings to deities, for which future punishment is assigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महनन
आत्महनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Suicide.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and हनन killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्महित
आत्महित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Beneficial to one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and हित good for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मादिष्ट|आत्मादिष्टः
आत्मादिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Self-counselled.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A treaty dictated by the party wishing it himself.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and आदिष्ट directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माधीन|आत्माधीनः
आत्माधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sentient, existent.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A wife's brother.<BR>2 A censorious man.<BR>3 A son.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मापहारक|आत्मापहारकः
आत्मापहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An impostor, one who pretends to belong to a higher class than his own.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and अपहारक a plunderer: who steals himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मार्थ
आत्मार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>For one's own sake, for the sake of one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and अर्थं object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माशिन्
आत्माशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन्, अश to eat, णिनि affix; supposed to eat its young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्माश्रय|आत्माश्रयः
आत्माश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Self-dependance.<BR>2 Innate idea, abstract knowledge, independant of the thing to be known.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मीय|आत्मीयः
आत्मीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Cognate, related, of kin.<BR>2 Own.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोदय|आत्मोदयः
आत्मोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Self-advantage or elevation.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपम|आत्मोपमः
आत्मोपम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Like one's self.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and उपम resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोपजीविन्
आत्मोपजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 A public performer, actor, singer, dancer, &c.<BR>2 A day labourer.<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् self, उपजीविन् who subsists: who lives by his own exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्मोद्भव|आत्मोद्भवः
आत्मोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced from one's self.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A son.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>आत्मन् and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यन्तिक|आत्यंतिक
आत्यन्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Supreme.<BR>2 Excessive, abundant.<BR>3 Infinite.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यन्त exceeding, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्ययिक
आत्ययिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Ill-omened, unpropitious.<BR>2 Destructive.<BR>3 Disastrous.<BR>4 Distressing, painful.<BR>E.<BR>अत्यय destruction. ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्यूह|आत्यूहः
आत्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A gallinule: see दात्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्रेय|आत्रेयः
आत्रेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni or saint, the son of ATRI, applicable to DATTA, DURVĀSAS, and SOMA.<BR>2 An essential humor or juice of the body.<BR>f. (-यिका or -यी)<BR>A woman during her courses.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 The name of a river in the north of Bengal.<BR>2 The wife of ATRI.<BR>3 Any woman of the Brahmanical order.<BR>E.<BR>अत्रि a saint so called, ढक् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्व्वण|आथर्वण|आथर्वणः|आथर्व्वणं|आथर्व्वणः
आथर्व्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A family priest.<BR>2 A Brahman versed in the Atharvan Veda.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A collection of prayers, &c. delivered by ATHARVAN, a sage.<BR>2 A private apartment in which, after a sacrifice, the sacrificer receives absolution from the officiating Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>अथर्व्वण a Veda, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आथर्व्वणिक|आथर्वणिक|आथर्वणिकः
आथर्व्वणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman who has studied the Atharva Veda.<BR>E.<BR>अथर्व्वण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदत्त
आदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Taken, received.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आददान
आददान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Taking, accepting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, affix शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदधान
आदधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर|आदरः
आदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Respect, reverence.<BR>2 Commencement, beginning.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दृ to have, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदरणीय
आदरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Venerable, respectable.<BR>2 To be attended to.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृ to have, आनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्त्तव्य|आदर्तव्य
आदर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be respected or regarded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् ट्ट and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्य्य|आदर्य|आदर्य्यः
आदर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृ to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्श|आदर्शः
आदर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 A mirror.<BR>2 A commentary.<BR>3 The original manuscript from which a copy is taken.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दृशि to see, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शन|आदर्शनं
आदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Showing, making apparent or seen.<BR>2 A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृश to see, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदर्शित
आदर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shewn, made apparent.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृश to see, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदान|आदानं
आदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Taking, receipt, acceptance.<BR>2 A horse's trappings.<BR>3 A symptom.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant: see हस्तिघोषा.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् reversing the sense, and दा to give, ल्युट् affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदाय|आदायः
आदाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदायचर
आदायचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who goes away after taking any thing.<BR>E.<BR>आदाय, चर to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदि|आदिः
आदि<BR>m. only. (-दिः)<BR>1 First, prior.<BR>2 First, pre-eminent.<BR>ind.<BR>(In composition,) Other, et-cetera, as स्वादि the affix सु et-cetera.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर|आदिकरः
आदिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>BRAHMĀ, the creator.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकर्त्तृ|आदिकर्तृ
आदिकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>BRAHMĀ, as the creator.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकवि|आदिकविः
आदिकवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A name of VĀLMĪKI, the first mortal poet.<BR>E.<BR>आदि the first, and कवि a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिकारण|आदिकारणं
आदिकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A primary cause.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and कारण a cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=110" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितस्
आदितस्<BR>ind.<BR>From the first, from the beginning.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदितेय|आदितेयः
आदितेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A deity, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>अदिति the mother of the gods, and ढक् derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्य|आदित्यः
आदित्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A deity in general.<BR>2 A deity of a particular class; the ĀDITYAS are twelve in number, they are forms of SŪRYA or the sun, and appear to represent him as distinct in each month of the year.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>अदिति the mother of the gods, and घञ् derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यपुष्पिका
आदित्यपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red swallow wort.<BR>E.<BR>आदित्य the sun, and पुष्पिका having a flower, the flower of the sun, from its red colour: see अर्कपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यमण्डल
आदित्यमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The disc or orb of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>आदित्य and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्यसूनु|आदित्यसूनुः
आदित्यसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A name of SUGRĪVA, a monkey king;<BR>2 of YAMA;<BR>3 of SANI or SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>आदित्य the sun, and सूनु a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्व|आदित्वं
आदित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Priority, precedence.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and त्व added; also आदिता with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सिता
आदित्सिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wish to seize.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदित्सु
आदित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing to take or have.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, desiderative form, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिदेव|आदिदेवः
आदिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Name of VIṢṆU or NĀRĀYAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>आदि the first, and देव a god, the first god, the creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिपुरुष|आदिपुरुषः
आदिपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The first male, usually applied to VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>आदि the first, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिभूत|आदिभूतः
आदिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>First born or existent.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>BRAHMA.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिम|आदिमं
आदिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>First, prior.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and डिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिराज|आदिराजः
आदिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The name of a king; also पृथु.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and राजन् a king, the first king; he was a form of VIṢṆU, and husband of Pṛthvī or the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिवराह|आदिवराहः
आदिवराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and वराह a boar; the first boar, alluding to VIṢṆU'S avatāra, or incarnation in that form; also similar compounds, as आदिशूकरः, आद्यकोलः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्ट|आदिष्टं|आदिष्टः
आदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Commanded, directed.<BR>2 Appointed.<BR>3 Advised, enjoined.<BR>4 Said.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Fragments or leavings of a meal.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिश to point or shew, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदिष्टिन्
आदिष्टिन्<BR>m. (-ष्टी)<BR>1 A student, a Brahman in the first order.<BR>2 A penitent, one engaged in any expiatory rite.<BR>E.<BR>आदिष्ट what is instructed, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीनव|आदीनवं|आदीनवः
आदीनव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Distress, pain, uneasiness.<BR>2 Fault, transgression.<BR>3 An inflictor of distress.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दीङ् to decay, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपन|आदीपनं
आदीपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Whitening the wall, floor, or seat, &c. upon festival occasions.<BR>2 Embellishing.<BR>3 Inflaming, exciting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दीप to beautify, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदीपित
आदीपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Illuminated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दीप to inflame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत|आदृतः
आदृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Respectful.<BR>2 Respected, honoured, worshipped.<BR>3 Zealous, diligent.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृञ्^1 to have, and क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदृत्य|आदृत्यः
आदृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दृ to have, क्यप् affix; तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेय
आदेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Receivable, leviable, what may be taken or received.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेवक
आदेवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>One who sports or plays.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिन to sport, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेश|आदेशः
आदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An order, a command.<BR>2 Advice, instruction.<BR>3 (In grammar,) A substitute;<BR>4 (In astrology,) Event, result, consequence of stellar conjunctions, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिश to point or shew, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेशिन्
आदेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A commander, a director.<BR>2 An astrologer, a fortune teller.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिश to point or shew, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आदेष्टृ
आदेष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 An adviser, a director, a commander.<BR>2 An employer of priests.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिश to shew, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्य|आद्यं|आद्यः
आद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 First, initial.<BR>2 Edible, what is to be or may be eaten.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Grain.<BR>2 Food.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>आदि and ण्यत् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यकवि|आद्यकविः
आद्यकवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>A name of VĀLMĪKI, author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>आद्य first, and कवि a poet, being the first who wrote Sansscrit verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्त
आद्यन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>From the beginning to the end.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Beginning and end, first and last.<BR>E.<BR>आदि first, and अन्त last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यन्तवत्|आद्यन्तवन्त्
आद्यन्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Finite, having beginning and end.<BR>E.<BR>आदि beginning, अन्त end, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यमाषक|आद्यमाषकः
आद्यमाषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Māṣa, a weight equal to five Gunja or Ratti seeds, about 17(1/2) grains troy.<BR>E.<BR>आद्य and माषक a Māṣa, the primary Māṣa; also माष and मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यवीज|आद्यवीजं
आद्यवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A primary cause.<BR>E.<BR>आद्य and वीज seed, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्यून|आद्यूनः
आद्यून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Shamelessly voracious.<BR>2 Without the beginning.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, दिव to play or enjoy in the part. past., or आदि first, and ऊन minus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आद्योपान्त|आद्योपान्तं
आद्योपान्त<BR>adv. (-न्तं)<BR>From first to last.<BR>E.<BR>आद्य and उप near, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधमन|आधमनं
आधमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्म्मिक|आधर्मिक
आधर्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Unjust, unrighteous.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धर्म्म virtue, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षण|आधर्षणं
आधर्षण<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Conviction, (of crime or of error.)<BR>2 Sentence, refutation.<BR>2 Injuring, annoying.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धृष to be bold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधर्षत
आधर्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Convicted, sentenced.<BR>2 Refuted, disproved.<BR>3 Injured, aggrieved.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धृष to be bold, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधान|आधानं
आधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Taking, having.<BR>2 Receiving, recovering.<BR>3 A ceremony performed with consecrated fire.<BR>4 A pledge, a deposit.<BR>5 A surety.<BR>6 A ceremony performed previous to conception: see गर्भाधान.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, धा to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधानिक|आधानिकं|आधानिकः
आधानिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A ceremony performed after cohabitation to procure or favour conception.<BR>E.<BR>आधान and ठक् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाय|आधायः
आधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having deposited or placed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधार|आधारः
आधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Support, prop, stay.<BR>2 Receptacle.<BR>3 Comprehension, location, the sense of the ablative in or on.<BR>4 A dike, a canal.<BR>5 A basin round the foot of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and धृ to hold or contain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=111" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधाराधेयभाव|आधाराधेयभावः
आधाराधेयभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The influence or action of the support or recipient upon the thing received or supported.<BR>E.<BR>आधार support, &c. आधेय what is to be held, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधि|आधिः
आधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 Mental agony, anxiety.<BR>2 Expectation.<BR>3 Definition.<BR>4 A pledge, a pawn, a mortgage.<BR>5 Location, fixing, site, &c.<BR>6 Engagement.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ध्यै to reflect, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिक्य|आधिक्यं
आधिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Excess.<BR>E.<BR>अधिक more, ष्यज aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिज
आधिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by pain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आधि pain, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिज्ञ|आधिज्ञः
आधिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Crooked.<BR>2 Pained, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>आधि pain, &c. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारण्य|आधिकारण्यं
आधिकारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Possession.<BR>2 Location.<BR>E.<BR>अधिकरण्य, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिकारिक
आधिकारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Supreme, superior, relating or belonging to any thing or person of importance or sway.<BR>2 Official, relating to any office or duty.<BR>E.<BR>अधिकार and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधित्व|आधित्वं
आधित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Nature or circumstance of a pledge.<BR>E.<BR>आधि and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधित्वोपाधि
आधित्वोपाधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The object or purpose with which a pledge is given, the conditions or terms of a mortgage.<BR>E.<BR>आधित्व and उपाधि condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिदैविक|आधिदैविकं
आधिदैविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to, a tutelary or presiding deity.<BR>E.<BR>अधिदैव and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिपत्य|आधिपत्यं
आधिपत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Power, supremacy, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>अधिपति a lord or master, &c. व्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभोग|आधिभोगः
आधिभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Usufruct, enjoyment or use of a deposit, use of a horse, cow, &c. pledged.<BR>E.<BR>आधि a pledge, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिभौतिक|आधिभौतिकं
आधिभौतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Elementary, derived or produced from the primitive elements.<BR>E.<BR>अधिभूत a material cause, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिमन्यव|आधिमन्यवः
आधिमन्यव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Feverish heat or burning.<BR>E.<BR>आधि and मन्यु distress, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिराज्य|आधिराज्यं
आधिराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Supreme sway, royalty, royal government.<BR>E.<BR>अधिराज and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधिवेदनिक|आधिवेदनिकं
आधिवेदनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Property, &c. given to a first wife upon marrying a second.<BR>E.<BR>अधि before विद to know, and ल्युट् affix, अधिवेदन, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकरण|आधीकरणं
आधीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Pledging, mortgaging.<BR>2 A pledge.<BR>E.<BR>आधि and करण making, &c. with च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत
आधीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pledged, pawned, mortgaged.<BR>E.<BR>आधि and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधीकृत्य
आधीकृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having pledged.<BR>E.<BR>आधि with कृत्य having done, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुत|आधुतः
आधुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धु or धू to tremble, affix क्त; it is also long, आधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधुनिक|आधुनिकः
आधुनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>New, recent, of the present moment.<BR>E.<BR>अधुना now, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूत|आधूतः
आधूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, agitated, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधूर्य्य|आधूर्य
आधूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Weakness, infirmity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. धुर्य्य to be borne, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधृत
आधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contained, supported.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before धृ to have, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधेय|आधेयं
आधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Placed, deposited or to be deposited.<BR>2 To be received or supported.<BR>3 To be pledged or mortgaged.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, धा to have or hold, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आधोरण|आधोरणः
आधोरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The rider or driver of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् धोर to move well, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मात|आध्मातः
आध्मात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sounded, sounding.<BR>2 Inflated.<BR>3 Burnt.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Flatulence, borborygmi, swelling of the abdomen with noise.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ध्मा to blow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्मान|आध्मानं
आध्मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Blowing, inflation.<BR>2 A bellows.<BR>3 Intumescence, swelling of the belly, dropsy.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ध्मा to blow, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्या
आध्या<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>Recollection, remembering especially with regret.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ध्यै to reflect, अच् affix, and ठाप् fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यात्मिक|आध्यात्मिकं
आध्यात्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the supreme spirit, spiritual, holy.<BR>E.<BR>अध्यात्म the soul, and ठङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यान|आध्यानं
आध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Remembering, pensive or sorrowful recollection, dwelling or meditating upon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ध्यै to consider, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्यापक|आध्यापकः
आध्यापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A teacher, a scriptural preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, prefixed to the causal of अधी to peruse, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्युपभोग
आध्युपभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Usufruct of a pledge.<BR>E.<BR>आधि and उपभोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आध्वर्य्यव|आध्वर्यव
आध्वर्य्यव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Belonging, to the officiating priest.<BR>E.<BR>अध्वर्य्यु and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन|आनः
आन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Breath inspired.<BR>E.<BR>अन् to be, अण् affix; existing by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक|आनकः
आनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A large military drum, beaten at one end.<BR>2 A double drum.<BR>3 A small drum or tabor.<BR>4 A thunder-cloud. or a cloud to which the noise of the thunder is ascribed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, अन to sound, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकटुन्दुभि
आनकटुन्दुभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A name of VASUDEVA the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>अनकदुन्दभ the parent of VASUDEVA, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनकदुन्दुभि|आनकदुन्दुभिः
आनकदुन्दुभि<BR>mf. (-भिः-भी)<BR>A large drum beaten at one end, a large dhol, a kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>आनक what sounds, and दुन्दुभि a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनक्य
आनक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>Name of a Muni or sage: see काण्डिल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनत|आनतः
आनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR>2 Pacified, conciliated.<BR>3 Humbled.<BR>4 Submissive, obedient.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नम to bow or bend, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनति|आनतिः
आनति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनद्ध|आनद्धं|आनद्धः
आनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Bound, tied.<BR>2 Costive.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>1 A drum in general: also अवनद्ध.<BR>2 Dressing, putting on clothes or ornaments.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, नह to bind, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन|आननं
आनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The mouth, (and by syncope) the face.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अन to live or breathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्तर्य्य|आनन्तर्य|आनंतर्यं
आनन्तर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Proximity, absence of interval.<BR>2 Immediate consequence or succession.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्तर and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्त्य|आनंत्यं
आनन्त्य<BR>n. (-न्त्यं)<BR>1 Infinity.<BR>2 Immortality, future happiness.<BR>E.<BR>अनन्त endless, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्द|आनंदः|आनन्दः
आनन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Happiness, joy.<BR>2 BALARĀMA according to the Jain system of many KṚṢṆAS and many BALARĀMAS.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>GOD, Supreme Spirit, according to the Vedānta.<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">Page113</a>] plant, vulgarly Ākanpāta.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, नदि to be or make happy घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=112" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दथु|आनंदथु|आनन्दथुः
आनन्दथु<BR>mfn. (-थुः-थुः-थु)<BR>Happy, joyful.<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Happiness, joy.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, नदि, to be happy, and अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दद
आनन्दद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Exhilarating, delighting: so आनन्दकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्ददत्त|आनन्ददत्तः
आनन्ददत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दन|आनंदन|आनन्दनं
आनन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Civility, courtesy, the treatment of a friend or guest at meeting and parting.<BR>2 Delighting, making happy.<BR>3 What gives or occasions delight.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नदि to make happy, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दपट|आनन्दपटं|आनन्दपटः
आनन्दपट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Bridal clothes.<BR>E.<BR>आनन्द making happy, and पट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दप्रभव|आनन्दप्रभवं|आनन्दप्रभवः
आनन्दप्रभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The seminal fluid.<BR>E.<BR>आनन्द pleasure, and प्रभव what is manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमय|आनंदमय|आनन्दमयः
आनन्दमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Blissful, made up or consisting of happiness.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>आनन्द and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दमयकोष|आनन्दमयकोषः
आनन्दमयकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The innermost case of the body, or causal frame enshrining the soul.<BR>E.<BR>आनन्दमय and कोष sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दानन्दन
आनन्दानन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दि|आनंदिः|आनन्दिः
आनन्दि<BR>m. (-न्दिः)<BR>Happiness, pleasure; also आनन्दी f. (-न्दी.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, नदि to be happy, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दित|आनन्दितः
आनन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Happy, rejoiced, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नदि, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनन्दिन्|आनंदिन्
आनन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>Happy, joyful.<BR>E.<BR>आनन्द and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनमित
आनमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, bowed down.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नम with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनम्र
आनम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>Bowing, stooping, bent, bowed down.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नम to bow, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनय|आनयः
आनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Bringing.<BR>2 Investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, णीञ् to obtain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनयन|आनयनं
आनयन<BR>n. (नं)<BR>1 Bringing.<BR>2 Investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी to get, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त्त|आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्तः
आनर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 A country on the north of the Malabar Coast.<BR>2 A stage, a theatre.<BR>3 War.<BR>4 Water.<BR>5 An inhabitant of Ānarta.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before नृत् to dance, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्थक्य|आनर्थक्यं
आनर्थक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>1 Unfitness, impropriety.<BR>2 Uselessness, unprofitableness.<BR>E.<BR>अनर्थ unprofitable, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय|आनायः
आनाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A net.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णीञ् to obtain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाय्य|आनाय्यः
आनाय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>To be brought.<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>Consecrated fire, taken from the household fire, and placed on the south side.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी to obtain, ण्यत् affix: deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनाह|आनाहः
आनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Epistasis, suppression of urine, or constipation.<BR>2 Length, especially of cloth.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, नह to bind, affix घञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिल|आनिलः
आनिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Name of HANUMĀN and BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल and अण् patronymic affix; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनिलि|आनिलिः
आनिलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 A name of the monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>2 BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल the wind, patronymic affix इञ; HANUMĀN and BHĪMA being the sons of ANILA or the wind.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A name of SVĀTI, the fifteenth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>अनिल and अण् affix fem. ङीप्; ANILA being the ruling deity of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीत
आनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken.<BR>2 Brought.<BR>3 Obtained.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनीय
आनीय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Having brought.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनील|आनीलः
आनील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Darkish.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A black horse.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् diminutive, and नील black or dark blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुकूल्य|आनुकूल्यं
आनुकूल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Favour, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>अनुकूल favourable, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुगत्य|आनुगत्यं
आनुगत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Acquaintance, familiarity.<BR>E.<BR>अनुगत followed, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुग्रामिक
आनुग्रामिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>About or belonging to the village, rustic, rural, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनुग्राम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपदिक
आनुपदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Following, pursuing, tracking.<BR>E.<BR>अनुपद and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुपूर्व्व|आनुपूर्व|आनुपूर्वं
आनुपूर्व्व<BR>nf. (-र्व्वं-र्व्वी)<BR>1 Order, series, succession.<BR>2 (In law) Direct order of the castes. (In logic) A conclusion, regularly or syllogistically deduced.<BR>E.<BR>अनु subsequent, पूर्व्व first, अण् affix; also आनुपूर्व्व्य and आनुपूर्व्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुमानिक|आनुमानिकः
आनुमानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Inferrable, inferred, subject to inference, derived from inference, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनुमान inference, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुरक्ति|आनुरक्तिः
आनुरक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Passion, affection.<BR>E.<BR>अनुरक्ति the same, the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोम्य
आनुलोम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Direct order, regular series or succession.<BR>E.<BR>अनुलोम direct, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुलोमिक
आनुलोमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Regular, orderly, in due course or series.<BR>E.<BR>आनुलोम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुविधित्सा
आनुविधित्सा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Ingratitude.<BR>E.<BR>अनु and वि before धा, to have, desiderative form, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनुषङ्गिक|आनुषंगिक
आनुषङ्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Proportionate, like, analogous, relative.<BR>2 Necessary, (as result, consequence.)<BR>3 Connected, concomitant with, adherent, inherent.<BR>4 (In grammar) Elliptical, including or agreeing with words not comprised in the sentence.<BR>E.<BR>अनुषङ्ग relation or connexion, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूप|आनूपः
आनूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Any animal frequenting marshy places, as a buffalo, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अनूप marshy ground, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनूपमांस
आनूपमांस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Flesh or meat of animals frequenting marshes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आनूप and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृण्य|आनृण्यं
आनृण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Acquittance of debt or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>अनृणी out of debt, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनृशंस्य|आनृशंस्यं
आनृशंस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 Mildness.<BR>2 Cruelty.<BR>E.<BR>अनृशंस mild, and यञ् affix, or आङ् intensitive, and नृशंस्य cruelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेतव्य
आनेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be brought or taken.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनेय
आनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taken or brought.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before णी to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैपुण|आनैपुणं
आनैपुण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Clumsiness, stupidity.<BR>E.<BR>अनिपुण not dexterous, अण् affix; and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनैश्वर्य्य|आनैश्वर्य|आनैश्वर्यं
आनैश्वर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Absence of power or supremacy.<BR>E.<BR>अनैश्वर्य्य the same, and the initial optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Gone.<BR>E.<BR>अम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त|आंत
आन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>Final, terminal, relating to the end.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्गणिक|आंतर्गणिक
आन्तर्गणिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Included, comprehended, (in a class or troop.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर् and गण a class, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तरीक्ष|आंतरीक्ष|आन्तरीक्षं
आन्तरीक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Heavenly, celestial, produced in the sky.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The firmament.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तरीक्ष the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तर्वेश्मिक
आन्तर्वेश्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Produced or occuring within a house.<BR>E.<BR>अन्तर्वेश्मन् and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=113" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्तिका|आंतिका
आन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An elder sister: see अन्तिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्त्रिक|आंत्रिक|आन्त्रिकः
आन्त्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Visceral, relating to the bowels.<BR>E.<BR>अन्त्र an entrail, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल|आंदोलः|आन्दोलः
आन्दोल<BR>r. 10th cl. (त) आन्दोलयति<BR>To swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोल|आंदोलः|आन्दोलः
आन्दोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Swinging.<BR>E.<BR>आन्दोल and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलन|आंदोलनं|आन्दोलनं
आन्दोलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Swinging.<BR>2 A swing.<BR>3 Trembling, oscillation.<BR>E.<BR>आन्दोल to swing, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्दोलित|आन्दोलितं
आन्दोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Swung, shaken.<BR>E.<BR>participle past of आन्दोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धस|आंधसः|आन्धसः
आन्धस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The scum of boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>अन्धस and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्धसिक|आंधसिकः|आन्धसिकः
आन्धसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>अन्धस् boiled rice, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्न
आन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्नी-न्नं)<BR>1 Fed, having food.<BR>2 Relating to food, derived from it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अन्न and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्ध्र|आंध्र|आन्ध्रः
आन्ध्र<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>A native of Telangana.<BR>E.<BR>अन्ध्र country, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वयिक|आन्वयिकः
आन्वयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of a good family, well born.<BR>2 Orderly, according to order or arrangement.<BR>E.<BR>अन्वय race, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आन्वीक्षिकी
आन्वीक्षिकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Logical philosophy, metaphysics.<BR>E.<BR>अनु according to, ईक्ष to see, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप<BR>r. 1st, 5th & 10th cls. (ऌ.) आपॢ (आपति, आप्नोति or -नुते and आपयति)<BR>1 To pervade or occupy.<BR>2 To obtain, to gain.<BR>In the first sense it is usually employed with वि prefixed, and in the second with अव or प्र;<BR>also with अभि andवि prefixed,<BR>to spread from one place to another;<BR>with परि and वि or सं and वि,<BR>to obtain completely;<BR>with सं and प्र,<BR>to meet with, light upon or fall into;<BR>with उप, सं and प्र,<BR>to arrive at, to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप|आपः
आप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>One of the eight demigods called Vasus.<BR>E.<BR>आप् to obtain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपकर
आपकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Offensive, mischievous, unfriendly.<BR>E.<BR>अपकर offence, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्व|आपक्वं
आपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>1 Half baked, crude, raw.<BR>2 Nearly ripe, not quite ripe.<BR>3 Undressed, what is eaten without further preparation, (as bread, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ् diminutive, पक्व dressed, cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river, a stream.<BR>E.<BR>आप् a quantity of water, the ocean, and गा fem. derivative from गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपण|आपणः
आपण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A market.<BR>2 A shop.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and पण to trade, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणिक|आपणिकः
आपणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mercantile, relating to traffic, to a market, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A merchant, a dealer, a shop-keeper.<BR>2 Tax on markets or shops.<BR>3 Assize, market rate.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् पणि to negociate, इकण् Uṇādi affix; or आपण and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतन|आपतनं
आपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Coming, approaching.<BR>2 Descending, alighting.<BR>3 Happening.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पत to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिक|आपतिकः
आपतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Accidental, unforeseen, sent from heaven.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hawk, a falcon.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पत to go, to fall, इकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतित
आपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Happened, befallen.<BR>2 Alighted, descended.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पत to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्काल|आपत्कालः
आपत्काल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Season of distress.<BR>E.<BR>आपद् and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्कालिक
आपत्कालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-का-कं)<BR>Occurring in a time of calamity, belonging to it.<BR>E.<BR>आपत्काल and ठक or ञिठ्^1 aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्ति|आपत्तिः
आपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>2 Obtaining, procuring.<BR>3 Fault, transgression.<BR>2 Remonstrance, expostulation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पद to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्प्राप्त|आपत्प्राप्तः
आपत्प्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Unfortunate, unhappy, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>आपद् misfortune, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद्<BR>f. (पद्-पत्)<BR>Misfortune, calamity.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पद to go, क्किप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्ग्रस्त
आपद्ग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Unfortunate, unhappy, in misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>आपद् and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्धर्म्म|आपद्धर्म|आपद्धर्मः
आपद्धर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>Practice or profession other than that proper to caste, but allowable in time of distress.<BR>E.<BR>आपद and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदा
आपदा<BR>fn. (-दा-दं)<BR>Misfortune, calamity.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पद to go, अङ् and टाप्; also आपद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन|आपनं
आपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Obtaining.<BR>2 Pepper.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनिक|आपनिकः
आपनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An emerald.<BR>2 A barbarian.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पन to praise, and इकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्न|आपन्नः
आपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Unfortunate, afflicted.<BR>2 Gained, obtained, acquired.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पद to go, क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्नसत्व
आपन्नसत्व<BR>mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>Impregnated, pregnant.<BR>f. (-त्वा)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>आपन्न obtained, सत्व thing, substance, टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यक|आपमित्यकं
आपमित्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Property, &c. obtained by barter.<BR>E.<BR>अपमित्य having changed, ककन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपराह्निक
आपराह्निक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Occurring in the afternoon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अपराह्न and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपव|आपवः
आपव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of VASIṢṬHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्
आपस्<BR>n. (-पः)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्कार|आपस्कारं
आपस्कार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The root or extremity of the trunk or body.<BR>E.<BR>अपस्कर filth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्तम्व|आपस्तम्वः
आपस्तम्व<BR>m. (-म्वः)<BR>The name of a sage and legislator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाक|आपाकः
आपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A potter's kiln.<BR>2 A baking oven.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पच् to bake, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाण्डुर
आपाण्डुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Slightly pale, palish.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् dimin. पाण्डुर pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Throwing down, causing to descend.<BR>2 Falling, descending.<BR>3 The instant, the current moment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् पत to go, to fall, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाततस्
आपाततस्<BR>ind.<BR>Immediately, instantly.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपान|आपानं
आपान<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tavern, a liquor shop, a place for drinking in society.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पा to drink, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपालि|आपालिः
आपालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A louse.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, पल to go, इन् affix; the penultimate irregularly long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The twentieth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आपीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Squeezing, compressing.<BR>2 Giving pain, hurting.<BR>3 A chaplet tied on the crown of the head.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पीड to pain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडन|आपीडनं
आपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Squeezing, compressing, tying or drawing tightly.<BR>2 Embracing, clasping.<BR>3 Giving pain, hurting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पीड to pain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आपीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Squeezed, compressed.<BR>3 Bound tightly.<BR>3 Embraced.<BR>4 Hurt.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पीडित pressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आपीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Drank up.<BR>2 Very yellow.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A pyritic mineral.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पीत drank or yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Stout, fat.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A well.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An udder.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and पीन fat, large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिक|आपूपिकं|आपूपिकः
आपूपिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 A baker.<BR>2 A confectioner.<BR>3 One who eats cakes, one for whom they are good, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of cakes.<BR>E.<BR>अपप a cake, ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=114" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूप्य|आपूप्यः
आपूप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>Flour, meal.<BR>E.<BR>अपूप a cake, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्त्ति|आपूर्ति|आपूर्तिः|आपूर्त्तिः
आपूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Filling.<BR>2 Satisfaction, fulness.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पूर्त्ति fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूष|आपूषं
आपूष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आपृच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>Conversation, speaking to or with.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, प्रच्छ to ask, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Trusted, confidential.<BR>2 Gained, obtained.<BR>3 True.<BR>4 Apt, fit.<BR>5 A friend.<BR>6 Appointed.<BR>7 Authentic.<BR>8 Accused, prosecuted.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>A twisted band or lock of hair.<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>1 Quotient.<BR>2 Equation of a degree.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तकारिन्
आप्तकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A trusty agent, a confidential servant.<BR>E.<BR>आप्त trusted, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्व्व|आप्तगर्व|आप्तगर्व्वः
आप्तगर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>आप्त and गर्ब्ब pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तगर्भा
आप्तगर्भा<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>आप्त and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तवचन
आप्तवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A received text, an authority.<BR>E.<BR>आप्त and वचन text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्ति|आप्तिः
आप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Gain, acquisition.<BR>2 Binding, joining.<BR>3 Connexion, relation.<BR>4 Fitness, aptitude.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तोक्ति|आप्तोक्तिः
आप्तोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 An augment or affix, (in grammar.)<BR>2 A word of received acceptation, and established by usage only.<BR>E.<BR>आप्त received, उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्प
आप्प<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>The sign Aquarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>1 Watery, consisting of water, as froth, &c.<BR>2 Obtainable, to be obtained.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>A plant, a kind of costus.<BR>E.<BR>अप water, यञ् affix; or आप to get, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यान
आप्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Stout, robust.<BR>2 Fat.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्फाय to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>2 Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>3 Advancing.<BR>4 Corpulency, growing or being fat or stout.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्फाय to increase, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायित|आप्यायितः
आप्यायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased.<BR>2 Satisfied.<BR>3 Increased, improved.<BR>4 Stout, fat.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्फाय to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छन|आप्रच्छनं
आप्रच्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Civility upon receiving or parting with a visitor, welcome, adieu, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, प्रच्छ to ask, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपद|आप्रपदं
आप्रपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A dress reaching to the feet.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and प्र before पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीन|आप्रपदीनं
आप्रपदीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>A dress reaching from the shoulders to the feet.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and प्र prefixed to पद a foot, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीनक
आप्रपदीनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लव|आप्लवः
आप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Bathing.<BR>2 Sprinkling with water.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, प्लु to swim, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवन|आप्लवनं
आप्लवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sprinkling with water.<BR>2 Bathing. आङ् before प्लु to swim, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवव्रतिन्
आप्लवव्रतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>An initiated householder, one who has passed through the first order, that of the Brahmacārī, and is admitted into the second.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before प्लव bathing, व्रतिन् performer of a व्रत, or religious obligation; bathing being part of the prescribed ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव|आप्लावः
आप्लाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Bathing.<BR>2 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>3 A submerging.<BR>4 A flood, an inundation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, प्लुङ् to swim, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लावित
आप्लावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inundated, overflowed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before प्लु to bathe, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लाव्य
आप्लाव्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having wetted or sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before प्लु to swim, ध्यण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत|आप्लुतः
आप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bathed.<BR>2 Wetted, sprinkled.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An initiated householder: see आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Bathing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, प्लुङ् to bathe, affix of the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुतव्रतिन्
आप्लुतव्रतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>See आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR>E.<BR>आप्लत bathed, &c. as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत्य
आप्लुत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having bathed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before प्लु to bathe, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वन्
आप्वन्<BR>m. (-प्वा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, वुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्ध|आबद्धः
आबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Tied, bound.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 A binding.<BR>2 A yoke.<BR>3 Ornament.<BR>4 Affection.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before बन्ध to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबन्ध|आबंधः|आबन्धः
आबन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Bound or tied firmly.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 The tie of a yoke, that which fastens the ox to the yoke, or the latter to the plough.<BR>2 Affection.<BR>3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>4 A tie or bond.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाधा
आबाधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुत्त|आबुत्तः
आबुत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A sister's husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, क्विप्, उत् and तन् to stretch, ड affix, प is changed to ब; according to another etymology the word is आवुत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबोधन|आबोधनं
आबोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Knowledge, understanding.<BR>2 Instructing, informing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, बुध to know, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरण|आभरणं
आभरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Ornament, decoration, as jewels, &c.<BR>2 Nourishing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, भृञ् to fill or nourish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Splendour.<BR>3 Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before भा to shine, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाति|आभातिः
आभाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Shade.<BR>2 Light.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before भा to shine, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष|आभाषः
आभाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Introduction, preface.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before भाष to speak, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषण|आभाषणं
आभाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Addressing, speaking to.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, भाष to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास|आभासः
आभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Reflexion.<BR>3 Intention, purpose.<BR>4 (In logic) Fallacy, semblance of a reason, an argument that is erroneous though plausible: it is classed as of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before भास shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्वर|आभास्वरः
आभास्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A demigod, of a class consisting of sixty-four.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, भास to shine, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजन|आभिजनः
आभिजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Loftiness of birth.<BR>E.<BR>अभिजन family, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्य|आभिजात्यं
आभिजात्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Birth, family, rank.<BR>2 Learning.<BR>E.<BR>अभिजाति family, &c. यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधा
आभिधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>अभिधा a compound root, to name, अङ् and टाप् affixes, and आङ् prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधातक|आभिधातकं
आभिधातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, क्त and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयक
आभिधानीयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a name or word.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The property of a name, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अभिधानीय and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्य|आभिमुख्यं
आभिमुख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Presence, being in front of or face to face.<BR>E.<BR>अभिमुख and ष्यञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिक
आभिहारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Taken by force or fraud.<BR>E.<BR>अभिहार seizure, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण|आभीक्ष्णं
आभीक्ष्ण<BR>adj. mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं) or adv. n. (-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Much, exceeding.<BR>3 Eternal, eternally.<BR>E.<BR>अभीक्ष्न frequent, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=115" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीर|आभीरः
आभीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cowherd, sprung from a Brahman and female of the medical tribe or the Ambaṣṭha.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A cowherd's wife, or a woman of that tribe.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, अभि and ईर to send, affix अच् and fem. ङीष्, or without the first prefix अभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्लि|आभीरपल्लिः
आभीरपल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>a station of herdsmen, a village inhabited by them only, an abode of cowherds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आभीर a cowherd, and पल्लि a house, a village, &c. also with the final long पल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरपल्ली
आभीरपल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Formidable, fearful.<BR>2 Suffering pain.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Bodily pain.<BR>E.<BR>अभि before इल to sleep, क affix; अ is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभेरी
आभेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or modes of music, femininely personified.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, भेरी a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोग|आभोगः
आभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Completion, fulness.<BR>2 Enjoyment.<BR>3 Effort, pains.<BR>4 The expanded hood of the Cobra capella, used by VARUṆA as his umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, भुज to eat, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Resulting from practice, practising, repeating.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्यास and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
आभ्युदयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to prosperity, &c.<BR>2 High, exalted.<BR>3 Important.<BR>n. (-क)<BR>A Śrāddha or offering to ancestors on occasions of rejoicing.<BR>E.<BR>अभ्युदय elevation. prosperity, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Raw, undressed, unripe.<BR>2 Unbaked, unannealed.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Constipation, passing hard and unhealthy excretions.<BR>3 Grain freed from the chaff.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमकुम्भ|आमकुम्भः
आमकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A water jar of unbaked clay.<BR>E.<BR>आम and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमगन्धि
आमगन्धि<BR>n. (-न्धि)<BR>A bad and cadaverous smell, like that of raw meat or a burning corpse.<BR>E.<BR>आम raw, &c. and गन्धि smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमण्ड|आमंडः|आमण्डः
आमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The castor oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् dim. मडि to adorn, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्य|आमनस्यं
आमनस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Pain.<BR>E.<BR>अ priv. मनस् the mind, यत् affix and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रण|आमंत्रणं|आमन्त्रणं
आमन्त्रण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Calling or calling to.<BR>2 Courtesy, welcome, adieu, &c.<BR>3 Inviting, invitation.<BR>4 Interrogation.<BR>5 The vocative case.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, मत्रि to consult, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रयितृ|आमंत्रयितृ
आमन्त्रयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Asking, inviting, calling.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>An inviter, an entertainer, especially of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मन्त्रि to counsel, causal form, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमन्त्रित|आमंत्रित
आमन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Invited, summoned, called.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, मत्रि to consult, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमपीनस
आमपीनस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Running at the nose, defluxion.<BR>E.<BR>आम and पीनस pituitary excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आममांस
आममांस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Raw flesh.<BR>E.<BR>आम and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आममांसाशिन्
आममांसाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A cannibal.<BR>E.<BR>आममांस and आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमय|आमयं|आमयः
आमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A grass, (Costus.)<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, घञ् affix; आम, and य, from या to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Sick, diseased.<BR>2 Affected with indigestion, dyspeptic.<BR>E.<BR>आमय, अव to go, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयावित्व
आमयावित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Dyspepsia, indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>आमयाविन् and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरक्त
आमरक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>Dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>आम and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणान्तिक|आमरणांतिक
आमरणान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Lasting for life, continuing till death.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मरण dying, and अन्त end, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरस|आमरसः
आमरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Imperfect chyme.<BR>E.<BR>आम and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्श|आमर्शः
आमर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Advice, counsel.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मृश to advise, affix घ्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्ष|आमर्षः
आमर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Wrath or rage.<BR>2 Impatience.<BR>E.<BR>अ before मृष to bear, affix घञ्, the prefix made long: also अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षण|आमर्षणं
आमर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rubbing, wiping.<BR>2 Anger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मृष to rub, &c. युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलक|आमलकं|आमलकः
आमलक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Another plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The fruit of the myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and मल to hold, वुन् affix, fem. ङीष् having all medicinal virtues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमवात|आमवातः
आमवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Constipation or torpor of the bowels, with flatulence and intumescence.<BR>E.<BR>आम and वात wind, the wind being supposed to be chiefly affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमशूल|आमशूलः
आमशूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cholic, pain arising from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमातिसार|आमातिसारः
आमातिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Dysentery, the excretion being mixed with hard and foetid matter.<BR>E.<BR>आम and अतिसार dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमात्य|आमात्यः
आमात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A minister, a counseller, an adviser.<BR>2 A general.<BR>E.<BR>see अमाव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाद्
आमाद्<BR>mfn. (-मात्)<BR>Eating raw food.<BR>E.<BR>आम, अद to eat, ञिट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्य|आमानस्यं
आमानस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Pain.<BR>E.<BR>see आमनस्य, the antepen. being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमान्न|आमान्नं
आमान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Undressed rice.<BR>E.<BR>आम and अन्न boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमालक|आमालकः
आमालक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Land near a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्य
आमावास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Occurring on the day of conjunction, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अमावास्य and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमाशय|आमाशयः
आमाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The stomach.<BR>E.<BR>आम hardness of the faeces, &c. and आशय a station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षा
आमिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Curd of two milk whey.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, मिष to sprinkle, सक् affix; also आमीक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्ष्य|आमिक्ष्यं
आमिक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Made of curds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आमिक्षा and यत् affix; also with छ, आमिक्षीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष|आमिषं
आमिष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Enjoyment.<BR>3 An object of enjoyment, a pleasing or beautiful object, &c.<BR>4 A bribe.<BR>5 Coveting, longing for.<BR>6 Form.<BR>7 Lust, desire.<BR>8 Food.<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, to go, ष्टिसच् Uṇādi affix and the antepen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषप्रिय|आमिषप्रियः
आमिषप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Carnivorous, fond of flesh meat.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>आमिष flesh, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषभुज्
आमिषभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Carnivorous.<BR>E.<BR>आमिष and भुज् what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषाशिन्
आमिषाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Carnivorous, eating flesh and fish.<BR>E.<BR>आमिष flesh, अश to eat, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्त|आमुक्तः
आमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Loosed, let go.<BR>2 Discharged, cast, shot.<BR>3 Put on as clothes or armour.<BR>4 Dressed, accoutred.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, मुच् to release, unbind, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्ति|आमुक्तिः
आमुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Liberation, being let loose.<BR>2 Final liberation.<BR>ind. (-क्ति)<BR>To the end of existence.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and मुक्ति liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुख|आमुखं
आमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Prelude, prologue.<BR>2 Commencement.<BR>ind.<BR>To the face.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मुख face or beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुप|आमुपः
आमुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A thorny kind of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायण|आमुष्यायणः
आमुष्यायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Of an illustrious family, well born, well descended.<BR>E.<BR>अमुष्य the genitive of अदस् this, and कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=116" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमूल|आमूलं
आमूल<BR>adv. n. (-लं)<BR>To the root, by the root, entirely, radically.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् particle, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृष्ट
आमृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Wiped, rubbed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मृज to wipe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचन|आमोचनं
आमोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Loosing, liberating.<BR>2 Emitting, shedding, letting forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मुच to liberate, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A fragrancy, a diffusive perfume.<BR>2 Strong smell.<BR>3 Pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, मुद to be pleased, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदन|आमोदनं
आमोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Delighting, rejoicing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मुद to please, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदित|आमोदितः
आमोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased, delighted.<BR>2 Fragrant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मुद with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
आमोदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दनी-दि)<BR>1 Fragrant.<BR>2 Happy, delighted.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A perfume for the mouth, made up in the form of a pill or bolus of camphor, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आमोद and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषिन्
आमोषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>A thief, who or what steals.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before मुष to steal, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नाय|आम्नायः
आम्नाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A Veda, or the Vedas in the aggregate.<BR>2 Received doctrine, traditional and right.<BR>3 Traditional usuage, family or national customs.<BR>4 Advice, instruction in past and present usage.<BR>5 A Tantra.<BR>6 An element of being. a property of substance.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, म्ना to learn, to remember, घञ् and युक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायसारिन्
आम्नायसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Pious, observing the Vedas and national customs.<BR>E.<BR>आम्नाय and सारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्बिकेय|आंबिकेयः|आम्बिकेयः
आम्बिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>2 Also of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>अम्बिका the mother of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA or a name of DURGĀ, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्भसिक|आंभसिक|आम्भसिकः
आम्भसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Aquatic.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>अम्भस् water, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्र|आम्रः
आम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>अम to be sick, रक् Uṇādi affix, and अ made आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रपेशी
आम्रपेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A piece of dried mango.<BR>E.<BR>आम्र and पेशी a piece of flesh, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रमय
आम्रमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of mangoes, (sauce, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>आम्र and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रात|आम्रातः
आम्रात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>आम्र the mango, and अत to go, the affix अच्; the fruit resembling the mango: also आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातक|आम्रातकः
आम्रातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कब् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रावर्त्त|आम्रावर्त|आम्रावर्त्तः
आम्रावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Inspissated mango juice.<BR>E.<BR>आम्र and आवर्त्त stirring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडन|आम्रेडनं
आम्रेडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tautology, reiteration of words or sounds.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before म्रेड to be mad, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडित|आम्रेडितं
आम्रेडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reiterated, repeated.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Repetition of a sound or word.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, म्रेडृ to be mad, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ल|आम्लः
आम्ल<BR>mfn. (-म्लः-म्ली-म्लं)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sourness, acidity.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल sour, with आङ् prefixed, or अम्ल sour and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लवेतस|आम्लवेतसः
आम्लवेतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>आम्ल sourness, and वेतस a cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लिका
आम्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The tamarind tree.<BR>2 Sourness in the mouth, acidity of the stomach: see अम्लिका.<BR>E.<BR>आम्ल sour, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लीका
आम्लीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>अम्ल and ठक् affix, the pen. made long: otherwise अम्लिका, as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आय|आयः
आय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Income, revenue.<BR>2 Gain, profit.<BR>3 The guard of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before या to obtain, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिक|आयःशूलिकः
आयःशूलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Active, diligent, indefatigable.<BR>E.<BR>अयस् iron, शूल a sharp weapon, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Coming, approaching.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before इण to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत|आयतः
आयत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Long.<BR>2 Diffuse, prolix.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An oblong figure, (in geometry.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before यम to cease, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतच्छदा
आयतच्छदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The plantain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>आयत long, and छद a leaf, long-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतस्तू
आयतस्तू<BR>m. (-स्तूः)<BR>A panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>आयत diffuse, ष्टू to praise, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतार्द्ध
आयतार्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>(In geometry,) half an oblong.<BR>E.<BR>आयत and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतन|आयतनं
आयतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abode, house.<BR>2 An altar, also a shed for sacrifices.<BR>3 A ground plot, the site of a house, &c.<BR>4 The cause of disease.<BR>E.<BR>आयत nominal root, to lengthen, affix ल्युट्; extending from the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयताक्षी
आयताक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A woman with large eyes or long eyelids.<BR>E.<BR>आयत and अक्षि the eye, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतायति|आयतायतिः
आयतायति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Long continuance, remote futurity.<BR>E.<BR>आयत and आयति future time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयति|आयतिः
आयति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Future time.<BR>2 Majesty, dignity.<BR>3 Restraint of mind.<BR>4 Length.<BR>5 Meeting, junction.<BR>6 Obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, यम to cease, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिमत्
आयतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Long, extended.<BR>2 Stately, dignified.<BR>3 Self-restrained.<BR>E.<BR>आयति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतेक्षण
आयतेक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Long-eyed, having large eyes.<BR>E.<BR>आयत and ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्त|आयत्तः
आयत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Docile, tractable, dependant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, यम to restrain, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तता
आयत्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Docility, tractableness, humility.<BR>E.<BR>आयत्त and तल् affix of the abstract; also with त्व, आयत्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्ति|आयत्तिः
आयत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 A day.<BR>2 Affection.<BR>3 Subjection, subjecting.<BR>4 A boundary, a limit.<BR>5 Power, strength.<BR>6 Continuance in the right way, steadiness of conduct.<BR>7 Sleeping.<BR>8 Length.<BR>9 Majesty, dignity.<BR>10 Future time.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, यति to endeavour, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथातथ्य|आयथातथ्यं
आयथातथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Unfitness, unsuitableness, incompatibility.<BR>E.<BR>अयथातथ and घ्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्य
आयम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having restrained or suppressed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before यम to restrain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयव्यय
आयव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Receipt and disbursement, income and expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>आय and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयल्लक|आयल्लकं|आयल्लकः
आयल्लक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Missing, regretting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>1 Of iron, iron.<BR>2 Armed with an iron weapon.<BR>3 Zealous.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Armour for the body, a breast-plate, a coat of mail.<BR>E.<BR>अयस् iron, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आयस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Sharpened, whetted.<BR>2 Thrown, cast, sent.<BR>3 Pained, distressed.<BR>4 Vexed, angry.<BR>5 Hurt, killed.<BR>6 Managed or effected with difficulty.<BR>7 Labouring, toiling, making effort or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, यस to endeavour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=117" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयागभूत
आयागभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Obtained by sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before याग sacrifice, भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाचित
आयाचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Urgently requested or desired.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before याच to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयात|आयातं
आयात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Come.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयान|आयानं
आयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The natural temperament or disposition.<BR>2 Coming, arrival.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, या to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाम|आयामः
आयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Length, either in space or time.<BR>2 Breadth, (in mensuration.)<BR>3 Restraint, restraining.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before यम to cease, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामिन्
आयामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Long in space or time.<BR>2 One who restrains.<BR>E.<BR>आयाम and इनि affix or आङ् before यम and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयास|आयासः
आयास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Fatigue, weariness.<BR>2 Effort, exertion.<BR>3 Trouble, labour.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before यस to endeavour, to make exertion, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आयासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Making exertion, active, laborious.<BR>2 Exhausted by labour, wearied.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, यस to endeavour, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुःशेष|आयुःशेषः
आयुःशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>End of life, death.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयु|आयुः
आयु<BR>mn. (-युः-यु)<BR>Age, duration of life.<BR>E.<BR>अय to go, Uṇādi affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्त|आयुक्तः
आयुक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A minister, an agent or deputy.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, युज to join, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध|आयुधं|आयुधः
आयुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A weapon in general.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, युध to fight, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधधर्म्मिणी|आयुधधर्मिणी
आयुधधर्म्मिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Aeschynomene sesban): see जयन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>आयुध a weapon, and धर्म्मिणी possessing virtue: having the virtues of a weapon against disease, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधागार|आयुधागारं
आयुधागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An arsenal, an armoury.<BR>E.<BR>आयुध and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to arms.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A soldier, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>आयुध a weapon, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to or connected with weapons.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>आयुध and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्द्रव्य|आयुर्द्रव्यं
आयुर्द्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A medicament.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् life, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेद|आयुर्वेदः|आयुर्व्वेदः
आयुर्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The science of medicine.<BR>2 The collective writings of authority on medicine, or medical Śāstra.<BR>E.<BR>आयस् life, and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदमय
आयुर्वेदमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Acquainted with medical science.<BR>E.<BR>आयुर्वेद and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुर्वेदिन्
आयुर्वेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Belonging to medicine, of the medical profession, medical, medicinal, &c.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A practiser of physic, a physician or surgeon.<BR>E.<BR>आयुर्वेद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्मत्|आयुष्मन्त्
आयुष्मत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मती-ष्मत्)<BR>1 Alive, living.<BR>2 Long lived.<BR>m. (-ष्मान्)<BR>One of the twenty-seven Yogas or divisions of the ecliptic.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् age, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्टोम|आयुष्टोमः
आयुष्टोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sacrifice to obtain longevity.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् and ष्टोम a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Vital, preservative of life, for the sake of life, relating or belonging to it.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Age, duration of life.<BR>E.<BR>इ to go, उसि Uṇādi affix, the pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्कर|आयुस्करः
आयुस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Promoting longevity, supporting life.<BR>E.<BR>आयुस् and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आये
आये<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of calling, expressive of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोग|आयोगः
आयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Presenting or offering flowers, perfumes, &c.<BR>2 Action, the performance of an act.<BR>3 A shore or bank.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, युज to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगव|आयोगवः
आयोगव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A man of a mixed tribe sprung from a Śūdra man and Vaiśya woman; his business is carpentry, &c.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A woman of the tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजन|आयोजनं
आयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR>2 Taking, seizing.<BR>3 Collecting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before युज to join, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजित
आयोजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Collected together.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before युज to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधन|आयोधनं
आयोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 War, battle, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, युध to make war, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर|आरं|आरः
आर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 The planet SATURN.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 An angle, a corner.<BR>2 End, extremity.<BR>3 Brass.<BR>4 Oxide of iron.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A shoe-maker's awl or knife.<BR>2 A probe.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकूट|आरकूटः
आरकूट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>आर what goes, and कूट a heap; composed of various materials.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Preserved, defended.<BR>2 Proper or worthy to be preserved, &c.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 Protection, guard, preservation.<BR>2 The junction of the frontal sinuses of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रक्ष to preserve, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षक|आरक्षकः
आरक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what guards or protects.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A watchman, a patrole.<BR>2 A village or police magistrate.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रक्ष to preserve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्वध|आरग्वधः
आरग्वध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रुज् sickness, बध what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्ट|आरट्टः
आरट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>The name of a country, north-west of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्टज|आरट्टजः
आरट्टज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A horse from the Āraṭṭa country.<BR>E.<BR>आरट्ट and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणि|आरणिः
आरणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>An eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्यी-ण्यं)<BR>Forest, wild, forest-born, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अरण्य a wood, अण् affix of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Forest, wild, forest-born or produced.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A forester, an inhabitant of the woods.<BR>E.<BR>आरण्य and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यपशु|आरण्यपशुः
आरण्यपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A wild or forest animal, as a buffalo, a monkey, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आरण्य forest, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यराशि|आरण्यराशिः
आरण्यराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The sign LEO.<BR>E.<BR>आरण्य a forest beast, and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरति|आरतिः
आरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Stopping, ceasing.<BR>2 Waving lights before an image.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रम to play, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनाल|आरनालं
आरनाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sour gruel made from the fermentation of boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>आर what goes, from ऋ to go, and नाल smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनालक|आरनालकं
आरनालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्ध|आरब्धं
आरब्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Begun, commenced.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रभि to commence, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभट|आरभटः
आरभट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी)<BR>Boldness, confidence.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A branch of the dramatic art, the machinery of the drama, the representation of magical incantations, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आर quickly, भट to nourish, अच् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभमाण
आरभमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Beginning, beginning resolutely with a determination to finish.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before राभि to commence, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=118" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्भ|आरंभः|आरम्भः
आरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>2 Haste, speed.<BR>3 Effort, exertion.<BR>4 Pride.<BR>5 Killing, slaughter.<BR>6 An introduction, a prologue, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ, रभि to commence, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्य
आरभ्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having begun, beginning from.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रभि to commence, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रु to sound, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्य|आरस्यं
आरस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Insipidity, want of flavour or spirit.<BR>E.<BR>अरस and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराग्र|आराग्रं
आराग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The edge of a semicircular arrow head.<BR>E.<BR>आर what goes, and अग्र edge, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्
आरात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Near.<BR>2 Distant, far from.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रा to get, आत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराति|आरातिः
आराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रा to take or receive, आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातीय
आरातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Remote.<BR>E.<BR>आरात् and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्रिक|आरात्रिकं
आरात्रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Waving lamps at night before an image.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रात्रि night, कन added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधक
आराधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what worships, a worshipper.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before राध and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधन|आराधनं
आराधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Accomplishment.<BR>2 Acquirement, attainment.<BR>3 Gratifying, propitiating.<BR>4 Worshipping.<BR>5 Cooking.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Service.<BR>(-नी)<BR>Worship, adoration, propitiation of the deities.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, राध to finish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनीय
आराधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be worshipped or adored.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before राध to finish, अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य and य, आराधितव्य and आराध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधित
आराधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Worshipped, honoured, reverenced.<BR>2 Propitiated, pleased.<BR>3 Accomplished, effected.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before राध to finish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्यमान
आराध्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being worshipped, receiving worship, &c.<BR>2 Being in course of fulfilment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before राध and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराम|आरामः
आराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A garden, a grove.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रम to please, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरालिक|आरालिकः
आरालिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>अराल crooked, ठक् affix; always bending over the dishes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराव|आरावः
आराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रु to sound, affix घञ्; also आरव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The name of a tree, (Lagerstroemia regina.)<BR>2 A crab.<BR>3 A hog.<BR>4 A pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, उण् affix, the pen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुक|आरुकः
आरुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A drug brought from the hills, of cooling properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षु
आरुरुक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Desirous to rise or ascend, to advance, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to rise, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरू
आरू<BR>mfn. (-रूः-रूः-रु)<BR>Of a tawny colour.<BR>m. (-रूः)<BR>Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, ऊ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढ|आरूढः
आरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Mounted, ascended, risen.<BR>2 Raised up, elevated on high.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढवत्|आरूढवन्त्
आरूढवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Mounting, rising.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to mount, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवत|आरेवतं|आरेवतः
आरेवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रेव, आरेव trust, तन् to stretch, ड affix; inspiring confidence during sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्य|आरोग्यं
आरोग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Health.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् reverse, रुज to be sick, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोढृ
आरोढृ<BR>mfn. (-ढा-ढ्री-ढृ)<BR>Who or what mounts or rides, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to mount, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोप|आरोपः
आरोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Placing in or on.<BR>2 Assigning or attributing to.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to mount, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपण|आरोपणं
आरोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Trusting, delivering.<BR>2 Placing or fixing in or on.<BR>3 Elevating.<BR>4 Planting.<BR>5 The bending of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to ascend, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपित|आरोपितं
आरोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deposited, intrusted.<BR>2 Placed, fixed.<BR>3 Made.<BR>4 Raised, elevated.<BR>5 Consecrated.<BR>6 Accidental, adventitious.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रुह to ascend, causal form, part. past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोह|आरोहः
आरोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Length.<BR>2 A woman's waist.<BR>3 Ascent, rising. creeping up.<BR>4 Mounting, riding.<BR>5 The rider of a horse or elephant.<BR>6 Weight.<BR>7 A measure.<BR>8 The buttocks.<BR>9 A mine.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रुह to rise, to mount, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहक|आरोहकः
आरोहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Lifting or raising up.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहण|आरोहणं
आरोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rising, ascending.<BR>2 The rising or growing of new shoots.<BR>3 A ladder, a staircase.<BR>4 Riding on.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, रुह, to ascend, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहिन्
आरोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>One who mounts or rides.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before रुह to mount, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्कि|आर्किः
आर्कि<BR>m. (-र्किः)<BR>A son of the sun, as SANI and the rest.<BR>E.<BR>अर्क the sun, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्ष|आर्क्षः
आर्क्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्क्षः-र्क्षी-र्क्षं)<BR>Stellar, regulated by the stars or constellations.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्ष and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षवर्ष|आर्क्षवर्षः
आर्क्षवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A stellar year, or revolution of a constellation.<BR>E.<BR>आर्क्ष and बर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गल|आर्गलः
आर्गल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>A bolt or bar: see अर्गल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ग्वध|आर्ग्वधः
आर्ग्वध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and बध to destroy or prevent, deriv. irr: see आरग्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घा
आर्घा<BR>f. (-र्घा)<BR>A sort of yellow bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घ्य|आर्घ्यं
आर्घ्य<BR>n. (-र्घ्यं)<BR>Wild honey.<BR>E.<BR>आर्घा and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च्च|आर्च
आर्च्च<BR>mfn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्ची-र्च्चं)<BR>1 Devout, worshipping.<BR>2 Relating to the Ṛc or Ṛk Veda.<BR>E.<BR>अर्च्चा worship, and ण affix or ऋच् and अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च्चिक|आर्चिक
आर्च्चिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the Rig Veda, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच् and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जव|आर्जवं
आर्जव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Straightness.<BR>2 Rectitude, propriety of act or observance.<BR>3 Sincerity.<BR>E.<BR>ऋञ् straight, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्त|आर्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Pained, afflicted.<BR>2 Disturbed, confounded.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत to hate, to move, participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तगल|आर्तगल|आर्तगलः|आर्त्तगलः
आर्त्तगल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, blue Barleria, (Barleria coerulea.)<BR>E.<BR>आर्त्त pained, गल to eat, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तनाद|आर्तनाद|आर्तनादः
आर्त्तनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cry of pain.<BR>E.<BR>आर्त्त and नाद sound. So आर्त्तस्वर m. (-रः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्तव|आर्तव|आर्तवः|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्त्तव<BR>mfn. (वः-वा or -वी-वं)<BR>1 Menstrual, relating to or produced by this discharge.<BR>2 Seasonable, produced in season.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The menstrual discharge.<BR>2 A flower.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु the menses, or a season, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्ति|आर्ति|आर्तिः|आर्त्तिः
आर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Sickness.<BR>3 The end of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ऋत to move, क्तिन् affix; also अर्त्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्त्विज्य
आर्त्त्विज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>The office of a sacrificing priest.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत्विज् a priest, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्त्यपहरण
आर्त्त्यपहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Consoling or relieving distress, pain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आर्त्ति and अपहरण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=119" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थिक
आर्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Wise.<BR>2 Rich.<BR>3 Significant.<BR>E.<BR>अर्थ and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्र|आर्द्रं
आर्द्र<BR>mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं)<BR>1 Wet, moist, damp.<BR>2 Fresh, not dry.<BR>3 Loose, flaccid.<BR>4 Tender, soft.<BR>f. (र्द्रा)<BR>The sixth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>अद to go, रक् Uṇādi affix, and the pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रक|आर्द्रकं
आर्द्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Ginger in the undried state.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्र moist, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रकाष्ठ
आर्द्रकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Green wood, timber not dry.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्र and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रता
आर्द्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Moisture, wetness.<BR>2 Tenderness, softness.<BR>3 Freshness, greenness.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्र and तल् affix; also आद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रनयन
आर्द्रनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Weeping, suffused with tears.<BR>E.<BR>आद्र and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रमाषा
आर्द्रमाषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्र moist, and माष a sort of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रशाक|आर्द्रशाकं
आर्द्रशाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्र and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रालुब्धक|आर्द्रालुब्धकः
आर्द्रालुब्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The dragon's tail or descending node.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्रा the lunar mansion, and लुब्धक who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धद्रौणिक
आर्द्धद्रौणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought with half a Droṇa, containing it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध, द्रोण a measure, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धधातुक
आर्द्धधातुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a part of a verb, (the inflexions of six tenses.)<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध and धातु a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धप्रस्थिक
आर्द्धप्रस्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought, &c. with half a Prastha.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्धप्रस्थ a measure, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धमासिक
आर्द्धमासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Lasting, &c. for half a month.<BR>2 Observing or practising (Continence, &c.) for a fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>आर्द्धमास and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्धिक
आर्द्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Sharing half, an equal partner.<BR>2 Relating to half.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who ploughs the ground for half the crop.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्ध half, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्य|आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्यः
आर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Of a good family.<BR>2 Respectable, venerable.<BR>3 Apposite, proper.<BR>4 To be sought or obtained.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A master, an owner.<BR>2 A name of BUDDHA.<BR>3 A friend.<BR>f. (-र्य्यां)<BR>1 A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 A kind of metre, measured by feet, each foot being equal to four short syllables, or two long and two short; there are seven and a half feet in each verse of the couplet, equal to thirty and to twenty-seven syllabic instants: the regular form consists of alternate long and short verses, but it admits of eighty principal variations.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, ण्यत् affix; also अर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यक|आर्यक|आर्यकः|आर्य्यकं|आर्य्यकः
आर्य्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A grandfather.<BR>2 Any respectable man.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The vessel, &c. used in sacrifices made to the manes.<BR>f. (आर्य्यका or आर्य्यिका)<BR>A respectable woman.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य respectable, &c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यगृह्य|आर्यगृह्य
आर्य्यगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Decorous, respectable, right.<BR>E.<BR>आय्य and गृह्य to be accepted by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यपुत्र|आर्यपुत्र|आर्यपुत्रः|आर्य्यपुत्त्रः
आर्य्यपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR>2 The son of a spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य a respectable person and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यप्राय|आर्यप्राय
आर्य्यप्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Abounding with respectable persons.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य and प्राय quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्र|आर्यमिश्रः|आर्य्यमिश्रः
आर्य्यमिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Distinguished, respectable.<BR>m. (-श्रः)<BR>A gentleman, a man of consequence.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य and मिश्र mixed, joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यरूप|आर्यरूप
आर्य्यरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>A hypocrite, an impostor.<BR>E.<BR>आय्य and रूप semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यलिङ्गिन्|आर्यलिङ्गिन्
आर्य्यलिङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>A hypocrite, an impostor; a Śūdra, wearing the dress of a Brahman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य and लिङ्गिन् who bears insignia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यवृत्त|आर्यवृत्त
आर्य्यवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Good, pious, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>आय्य and वृत्त practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यवेश|आर्यवेश
आर्य्यवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Well clothed, fine.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्य and वेश vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यागीति|आर्यागीति
आर्य्यागीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A variety of the Āryā metre, containing eight equal feet or thirty-two syllabic instants in each verse of the couplet.<BR>E.<BR>आर्य्यां and गीति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य्यावर्त्त|आर्यावर्त|आर्यावर्तः|आर्यावर्त्त|आर्य्यावर्त्तः
आर्य्यावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>The holy land, the country extending from the eastern to the western sea, and bounded on the north and south, by the Himāla and Vindhya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>आय्य venerable, आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्व्वाक्|आर्वाक्
आर्व्वाक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 After, afterwards.<BR>2 Behind.<BR>E.<BR>अर्व्वाक् and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष|आर्षः
आर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं)<BR>Relating or belonging to or derived from a Ṛṣi.<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A form of marriage, the father of the bride receiving one or two pair of kine from the bridegroom.<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The Vedas.<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>One of the orders of the metres of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभि|आर्षभिः
आर्षभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A name of BHARATA, emperor of India.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषभ excellent, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ्य|आर्षभ्यः
आर्षभ्य<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>A steer fit to be let loose.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषभ an ox, ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेय
आर्षेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Relating or belonging to or derived from a Ṛṣi.<BR>2 Venerable, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि a sage, ढक् affix; also आर्ष and आर्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षोढा
आर्षोढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A wife married according to the Ārṣa form.<BR>E.<BR>आर्ष and ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत|आर्हतः
आर्हत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Jaina, a follower of the doctrines of a Jina or Arhat.<BR>E.<BR>अर्हत् a Jina, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत्य|आर्हत्यं
आर्हत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं-न्ती)<BR>The quality or practice of an Arhat or Jain saint.<BR>E.<BR>अर्हत् ष्यञ् affix fem. ङीष् with the nasal inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आल|आलं|आलः
आल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Large, extensive.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, in the causal form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलगर्द्द|आलगर्द|आलगर्दः|आलगर्द्दः
आलगर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A species of Cobra.<BR>E.<BR>see अलगर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
आलभ्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having received or obtained.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लभि to gain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ|आलंभः|आलम्भः
आलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Slaughter, killing.<BR>2 Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लभि to kill, affix धञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्भ्य
आलम्भ्य<BR>mfn. (म्भ्यः-म्भ्या-म्भ्यं)<BR>1 Fit or proper to be killed.<BR>2 Obtainable, to be obtained.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लभि with ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्ब|आलंब|आलम्बः
आलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A receptacle. a prop, an asylum or support.<BR>2 Depending on or from.<BR>3 A perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लम्बि to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बन|आलंबनं|आलम्बनं
आलम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Depending on or resting upon, hanging from.<BR>2 The natural and necessary connexion of feeling with the cause by which it is excited.<BR>3 Supporting, sustaining.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and लवि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बित|आलंबित
आलम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pendant, suspended, hanging from or on.<BR>2 Supported, upheld.<BR>3 Protected.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लवि to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=120" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलम्बिन्|आलंबिन्
आलम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>1 Depending on or from, hanging from, &c.<BR>2 Supporting, maintaining.<BR>E.<BR>आलम्ब support, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलय|आलयं|आलयः
आलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A house, a dwelling, a receptacle, an asylum.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लीङ् to enfold, धञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवण्य|आलवण्यं
आलवण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Ugliness.<BR>2 Insipidity.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. लवण handsome, affix यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवाल|आलवालं
आलवाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A basin for water round the root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लू to cut or dig, and आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस|आलसः
आलस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Idle, slothful, lazy.<BR>E.<BR>अलस idle, अण् affix: see अलस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्य|आलस्यं|आलस्यः
आलस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-सी-स्यं)<BR>Idle, slothful, apathetic.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Idleness, sloth.<BR>E.<BR>अलस idle, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलात|आलातं
आलात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A firebrand, a coal burning or extinguished.<BR>E.<BR>अलात and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलान|आलानं
आलान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>2 The rope that ties him.<BR>3 A fetter, a tie.<BR>4 Tying, binding.<BR>5 A rope or string.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ला to take, आला to tie or fasten, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप|आलापः
आलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Speaking to, addressing, conversation.<BR>2 Enumeration of the questions in an arithmetical or algebraic sum.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लप to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापन
आलापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Speaking to, conversing with.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लप to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनीय
आलापनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be said or spoken.<BR>2 To be spoken to or addressed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लप to speak, अनीयर् affix; also आलाप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिन्
आलापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Who speaks or converses.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लप to speak, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबु|आलाबुः
आलाबु<BR>f. (-बुः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd: also आलाबू, अलाबु and अलाबू, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलावर्त्त|आलावर्त|आलावर्तं|आलावर्त्तं
आलावर्त्त<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>A fan made of cloth.<BR>E.<BR>आल orpiment, and आवर्त्त abode: stained or painted with some such substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलास्य|आलास्यः
आलास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>आल wide, large, and आस्य a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलि|आलिः
आलि<BR>mfn. sub. (-लिः-लिः) or ली-लि<BR>1 Pure, honest, sincere.<BR>2 Useless, idle, unmeaning.<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>1 A woman's female friend.<BR>2 A row or range, a continuous line.<BR>3 A ridge or mound of earth, crossing ditches, dividing fields, &c.<BR>4 A line, a race or family.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>2 A bee: see अलि.<BR>E.<BR>अल to adorn, to be able, &c. affix इण and the pen. made long; also आली, affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गन|आलिंगन|आलिंगनं|आलिङ्गनं
आलिङ्गन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिगि to approach, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गित|आलिंगित|आलिङ्गितः
आलिङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Embraced.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिगि to approach, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्गिन्|आलिंगिन्
आलिङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>Embracing.<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A small drum shaped like a barley corn, and carried upon the breast.<BR>E.<BR>आलिङ्ग an embrace, and इनि affix; also आलिङ्गी fem. ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिङ्ग्य|आलिंग्य|आलिङ्ग्यः
आलिङ्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्ग्यः-ङ्ग्या-ङ्ग्यं)<BR>To be embraced.<BR>m. (-ङ्ग्यः)<BR>A small drum: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>आलिङ्ग and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिञ्जर|आलिंजर|आलिंजरः|आलिञ्जरः
आलिञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large clay water jar.<BR>E.<BR>अलिञ्जर a jar. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्
आलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A scorpion.<BR>E.<BR>see. आलि, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्द|आलिंद|आलिंदः|आलिन्दः
आलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A terrace before a house.<BR>2 A raised place or terrace for sleeping upon.<BR>E.<BR>अलिन्द the same, and अण् affix: see अलिन्द, also आलिन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप्त
आलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Smeared, plastered, anointed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिप to smear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिम्पन|आलिंपनं|आलिम्पनं
आलिम्पन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Whitening or painting the floor, wall, &c. on festival occasions. आङ्, लिपि to plaster, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A female friend.<BR>2 A row or range.<BR>3 A field, boundary or mound: see आलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढ|आलीढं
आलीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Licked.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>An attitude in shooting, the right knee advanced, the left leg retracted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लिह to lick, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढक|आलीढकं
आलीढक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The frolicking of a calf. Sometimes written आढीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीन
आलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Melted, fused.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ली to melt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीनक|आलीनकं
आलीनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>आलीन and affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलु|आलुः
आलु<BR>f. (-लुः)<BR>A pitcher, a small water jar.<BR>mn. (-लुः-लु)<BR>1 An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum); in the modern dialects this name is applied to the yam, potatoe, &c.<BR>2 A raft, a float.<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and उण् affix, आरु what goes, (in the earth, water, &c.) the initial is lengthened, and र is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुक|आलुकं|आलुकः
आलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A name of the chief of the Nāgas or serpent race: see शेष.<BR>2 An esculent root: see आलु.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलून
आलून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Cut, cut off.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लून cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखन|आलेखनं|आलेखनः
आलेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Writing.<BR>2 Painting.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A brush, a pencil.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिख to write, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्य|आलेख्यं
आलेख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>1 To be written.<BR>2 To be delineated or painted.<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>1 A painting.<BR>2 A writing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिख to write, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्यशेष|आलेख्यशेषः
आलेख्यशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>E.<BR>आलेख्य painting. writing, and शेष final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेप|आलेपः
आलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Smearing, plastering, anointing.<BR>2 Liniment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लिपि to anoint, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेपन
आलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Smearing, plastering.<BR>2 Liniment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, before लिप to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोक|आलोकः
आलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>2 Light.<BR>3 Flattery, complimentary language, panegyric.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लोकृ to see, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकन|आलोकनं
आलोकन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लोकृ to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकित
आलोकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लोक to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचक
आलोचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The faculty of vision or the cause of sight.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लोच and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचन|आलोचनं
आलोचन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लोच to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचित
आलोचित<BR>mf. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, beheld.<BR>2 Considered.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लोच to see, क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोच्य
आलोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>To be seen thought of or considered; also आलोचनीय.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, लोच to see, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडन|आलोडनं
आलोडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Mixing, blending.<BR>2 Strirring, shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and लुड to stir, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=121" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडित
आलोडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mixed, blended.<BR>2 Shaken, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लुड to stir, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोल|आलोलः
आलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Shaken, agitated.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Trembling, agitation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लुड to shake, affix घञ, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोलित
आलोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before लुल to shake, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवनेय|आवनेयः
आवनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>अवनी the earth, ढक् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवन्त्य|आवंत्य|आवन्त्यः
आवन्त्य<BR>m. (-न्त्यः)<BR>1 The offspring of a degraded Brahman.<BR>2 An inhabitant, &c. of Avanti or Ougein.<BR>E.<BR>अवन्ती and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपन|आवपनं
आवपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Any vessel.<BR>2 Weaving.<BR>3 Sowing seed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् वप to sow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A cover, a veil, what covers or conceals.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृ with वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Covering.<BR>2 A covering, a garment.<BR>3 A shield.<BR>4 An outer bar or a fence, a wall.<BR>5 An obstruction.<BR>6 Mental blindness.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वृ to skreen, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरणशक्ति|आवरणशक्तिः
आवरणशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>The power of illusion, that which veils the real nature of things.<BR>E.<BR>आवरण and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्त|आवर्त|आवर्तः|आवर्त्तं|आवर्त्तः
आवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Revolving, turning round.<BR>2 A whirlpool.<BR>3 A lock of hair that curls backwards, especially on a horse.<BR>4 Deliberation, revolving.<BR>5 A mineral substance, pyrites, marcasite.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वृत to choose, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तका
आवर्त्तका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A revolution, a whirl.<BR>2 A whirlpool.<BR>3 A curl of hair, especially on a horse.<BR>4 Revolution of the mind from the influence of the senses.<BR>5 The depression above the frontal ridge or over the eyebrows.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The name of a creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तन|आवर्तन|आवर्तनः|आवर्त्तनं
आवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Turning, turning round.<BR>2 Churning.<BR>3 Stirring any thing in fusion.<BR>4 Melting metals together, alligation.<BR>5 The time when shadows are cast in an opposite direction.<BR>6 Repeating, doing over again.<BR>7 Study, practising.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A crucible.<BR>E.<BR>आवर्त्त, ल्युट् affix; and ङीप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तनमणि|आवर्तनमणि|आवर्त्तनमणिः
आवर्त्तनमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A gem of a secondary order, commonly Rājāvartta.<BR>E.<BR>आवर्त्तन the same, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तनीय|आवर्तनीय
आवर्त्तनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be whirled or turned round.<BR>2 To be reversed.<BR>3 To be repeated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृत to be, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तमान|आवर्तमान
आवर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Advancing, proceeding.<BR>2 Revolving, going round.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृत to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्त्तिन्|आवर्तिन्
आवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>What whirls or turns upon itself.<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A horse having curls of hair on various parts of his body: it is considered as a lucky mark.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>आबर्त्त and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्हित|आवर्हितः
आवर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eradicated, plucked up by the roots.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वर्ह to hurt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलि|आवलिः
आवलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 A row, a range, a continuous line.<BR>2 A series, dynasty, a lineage.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वल to move, इन् affix; also आवली, taking ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्य
आवल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Weakness.<BR>E.<BR>अवल weak, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्य|आवश्यं
आवश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Necessity, inevitable act or conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>अवश्य and अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यक|आवश्यकं
आवश्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Necessity, inevitable act or conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>अवश्य certain, affixes अण् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकत्व|आवश्यकत्वं
आवश्यकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Necessity, inevitability.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to आवश्य, also with तल्, आवश्यकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ|आवसथं|आवसथः
आवसथ<BR>mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 A fire temple or place where sacrificial fire is preserved.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A treatise on the poetical metre called Ārya. (आर्य्याकोषः) see आर्य्या.<BR>2 A particular religious observance.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वस to dwell, अथ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथिक|आवसथिकः
आवसथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Inhabiting a house, household, domestic.<BR>E.<BR>आवसथ and ष्ठल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्य|आवसथ्यः
आवसथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>आवसथ and ञ्य added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसित|आवसितं
आवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stored, (as grain.)<BR>2 Winnowed.<BR>3 Ripe, full grown.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and अब reverse, and षो to destroy, participial affix क्त; also अवसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह|आवहः
आवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>What bears or conveys.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>One of the seven winds.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वह to bear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहत्
आवहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Obtaining, receiving.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वह to hear, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहमान|आवहमानं
आवहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Followed, succeeded, come in succession.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वह to hear, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहित
आवहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rooted up, extirpated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवात्
आवात्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वान्ती-वात्)<BR>Blowing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वा to blow, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाधा
आवाधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Distress.<BR>3 Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वाधा the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाप|आवापः
आवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A basin for water round the root of tree.<BR>2 A bracelet.<BR>3 Hostile purpose, intention of going to war, (as a king.)<BR>4 Throwing, casting, directing.<BR>5 Sowing seed.<BR>6 Throwing additional ingredients into any compound, (in pharmacy, &c.) in course of preparation.<BR>7 Mixing, inserting.<BR>8 Uneven ground.<BR>9 A vessel.<BR>10 Principal sacrifice with fire.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वप to sow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापक|आवापकः
आवापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bracelet of gold, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापन|आवापनं
आवापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A loom, an implement for weaving.<BR>2 A reel or frame for winding thread.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वप to weave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारि|आवारिः
आवारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A shop, a stall.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृ to nourish, in the causal form, इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवार्य्य|आवार्य
आवार्य्य<BR>ind.<BR>Covering, hiding, concealing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृ to screen, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाल|आवालं
आवाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A basin for water round the foot of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वल to move, घञ् affix; also आलवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाल्य|आवाल्यं
आवाल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Age or time ending with infancy.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् unto, बाल्य childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवास|आवासः
आवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A house, a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वस to dwell, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहन|आवाहनं
आवाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calling.<BR>2 Inviting.<BR>3 Offering oblations with fire.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A particular position of the hands or the palms put together, and the thumbs put at the root of the ring finger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वक्त to bear, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहित
आवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Invoked, invited.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वह to bear, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविक|आविकः
आविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Woollen, &c. or any thing relating to or derived from a sheep.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A blanket, woollen cloth.<BR>E.<BR>अवि a sheep, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविकसौत्रिक
आविकसौत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of woollen thread.<BR>E.<BR>आविक and सूत्र a thread, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=122" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविग्न|आविग्नः
आविग्न<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>A small fruit tree, vulgarly Caronda, (Carissa carondas.) also अविग्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pierced, wounded.<BR>2 Crooked.<BR>3 Cast, thrown, sent.<BR>4 Disappointed.<BR>5 Stupid, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before व्यध to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्धकर्णी
आविद्धकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णीं)<BR>A plant, (Aknidhi): also आविद्धकर्णिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविध|आविधः
आविध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>An awl, a drill, a kind of gimblet worked by a string.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, व्यध to pierce, घञ् or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भाव|आविर्भावः
आविर्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Manifestation, presence, becoming visible.<BR>E.<BR>आविस् manifestly, and भाव condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भूत|आविर्भूतः
आविर्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Appeared, manifest, become visible.<BR>E.<BR>आविस् and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविल
आविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Foul, turbid.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, विल to break, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्करण|आविष्करणं
आविष्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Manifestation, making visible.<BR>E.<BR>आविस् an करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कार|आविष्कारः
आविष्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Becoming or making visible.<BR>E.<BR>आविस् and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कृत|आविष्कृतः
आविष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made or become visible, evident, manifest.<BR>E.<BR>आविस् apparent, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्ट|आविष्टः
आविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Entered.<BR>2 Possessed, (by a demon, &c.)<BR>3 Possessed, engrossed, (by any sentiment or feeling.)<BR>E.<BR>आविश to enter, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्
आविस्<BR>ind.<BR>Manifest, evident.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, उङ् to sound, इर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवी
आवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Pain of child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीत
आवीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Passed, gone.<BR>2 Placed, hung.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The sacrificial cord worn in any particular manner.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वीत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीतिन्
आवीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A Brahman who wears the cord in any particular manner.<BR>E.<BR>इनि added to the last: see प्राचीनावीतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवूक
आवूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A father, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, ऊकन् affix, and the initial lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत्<BR>f. (-वृत्)<BR>Order, method.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृत to choose, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत|आवृतः
आवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Enclosed, surrounded, (by a ditch, wall, &c.)<BR>2 Covered, screened.<BR>3 Invested, inclosed, involved.<BR>4 Spread, overspread, overcast.<BR>5 Filled with, abounding with.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A man of mixed origin, the son of a Brahman, by a woman of the Ugra caste.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वृ to nourish, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्त|आवृत्तः
आवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Whirled, stirred, turned round.<BR>2 Reverted, averted.<BR>3 Retreated, fled.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्ति|आवृत्तिः
आवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Reversion, turning back or from.<BR>2 Flight, retreat.<BR>3 Revolving, going round.<BR>4 Wordly existence, the revolution of births.<BR>5 Use, employment, application.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वृत, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेग|आवेगः
आवेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Hurry, haste.<BR>2 Flurry, agitation.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विज to be alarmed, घञ् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदक|आवेदकः
आवेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who makes known.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An appellant, a suitor.<BR>2 An informer.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विद to know, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदन|आवेदनं
आवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Representing, addressing or apprising respectfully.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and वेदन informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदित|आवेदितः
आवेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made known, communicated, represented.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विद to know, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्य
आवेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be represented or made known.<BR>ind.<BR>Having made known.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विद् to know, causal form, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्यमान
आवेद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Stating, representing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विद to know, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेश|आवेशः
आवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Entrance, entering.<BR>2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>3 Indistinctness of idea, apoplectic or epileptic giddiness.<BR>4 Absorption of the faculties in one wish or idea, devotedness to an object.<BR>5 Demoniac frenzy, possession, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विश to enter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशन|आवेशनं
आवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Entrance, entering.<BR>2 A house in which work is carried on, a workshop, a manufactory, &c.<BR>3 Possession by devils, &c.<BR>4 Passion, fury.<BR>5 The disk of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, विश to enter, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिक|आवेशिकः
आवेशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 A guest, a visiter.<BR>2 Entering into.<BR>3 Own, peculiar, unparticipated.<BR>4 Inherent.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, विश to enter, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टक|आवेष्टकः
आवेष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wall, a fence, an enclosure.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, वेष्ट to surround, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टन|आवेष्टनं
आवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wrapping round, binding, tying.<BR>2 A wrapper, an envelope, a bandage.<BR>3 An inclosure.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वेष्ट to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टित
आवेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, enveloped, inclosed, bound or tied.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before वेष्ट to inclose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसन|आशंसनं
आशंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Expecting, wishing.<BR>2 Declaring, asserting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शसि to wish, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसा
आशंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Speech, declaration.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, शसि to desire, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसित
आशंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, expected.<BR>2 Declared, said.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शसि to desire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसितृ
आशंसितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Wishing, desiring.<BR>2 Asserting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, शसि to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसु|आशंसुः
आशंसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Wishing, desiring.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, शसि to wish, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्त|आशक्तः
आशक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Able, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् and शक्त able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्ति|आशक्तिः
आशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Power, ability, might.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कनीय|आशंकनीय
आशङ्कनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be doubted, questionable.<BR>2 To be apprehended.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शकि to doubt, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्का|आशंका
आशङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>1 Fear, apprehension.<BR>2 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, शकि to doubt, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कान्वित
आशङ्कान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Afraid.<BR>2 Doubting, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>आशङ्का and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशङ्कित|आशंकित
आशङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Feared, dreaded.<BR>2 Doubted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शकि to doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशन|आशनः
आशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.) see असन and आसन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशय|आशयः
आशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Meaning, intention.<BR>2 Free will or pleasure.<BR>3 A asylum, an abode or retreat.<BR>4 A receptacle, a recipient.<BR>5 Any recipient or containing vessel or viscus of the body, as रक्ताशय the heart, आमाशय the stomach, &c.<BR>6 The stomach in particular.<BR>7 The mind.<BR>8 Property, possessions.<BR>9 A miser, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">Page124</a>] niggard.<BR>10 Virtue and vice.<BR>11 Fate, fortune.<BR>12 The Jack, a kind of bread-fruit tree.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, शीङ् to rest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=123" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयाश|आशयाशः
आशयाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of fire: see आश्रयास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयितृ
आशयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Feeding, a feeder, one who gives food.<BR>2 Protecting, a protector.<BR>3 Recipient, a receiver.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, causal form, affix शतृ or आङ् before शीङ् to rest, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशर|आशरः
आशर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 An imp, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शृ to injure, अप् affix; also आशिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशल|आशलः
आशल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree: see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशव|आशवं
आशव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A spirit distilled from molasses: see आसव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशा
आशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 Hope, desire.<BR>2 Length.<BR>3 A quarter, a region.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अशू to expand, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाढ|आशाढः
आशाढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>1 The month Āśāḍha, (June-July.)<BR>2 A staff of Palāśa wood carried by ascetics.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>The name of two of the lunar mansions: see पूर्व्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशान्वित
आशान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having hope.<BR>E.<BR>आशा and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाप्राप्त
आशाप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Successful, possessing the object hoped for.<BR>E.<BR>आशा and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाबन्ध|आशाबन्धः
आशाबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Confidence, trust, expectation.<BR>2 A spider's web.<BR>E.<BR>आशा hope, &c. and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाभङ्ग|आशाभंग|आशाभङ्गः
आशाभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Disappointment.<BR>E.<BR>आशा and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावत्|आशावन्त्
आशावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Hoping, having hope.<BR>E.<BR>आशा and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाहीन
आशाहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Desponding, despairing.<BR>E.<BR>आशा and हीन destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिञ्जित|आशिंजित
आशिञ्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tinkling, applied to the ornaments worn on the hands and feet.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शिजि to tinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अश to eat, affix क्त; also अशित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितङ्गवीन|आशितंगवीन|आशितङ्गवीनं
आशितङ्गवीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Formerly grazed by cattle.<BR>E.<BR>आशित eaten, गवीन irregular derivative of गो a cow, and खश् affix; also अशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितम्भव|आशितंभव|आशितम्भवं
आशितम्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Food, victuals.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Satisfaction, satiety.<BR>E.<BR>आशित and भव produced by, from भू and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितृ
आशितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Voracious, gluttonous, eating excessively.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, and तृच् affix, इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर|आशिरः
आशिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A goblin or imp.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अश to eat, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
आशिस्<BR>f. (-शीः)<BR>1 Blessing, benediction, bestowing or wishing a blessing upon others.<BR>2 A serpent's fang.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before शास to rule, क्विप् affix, and आ is changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी<BR>f. (-शीः)<BR>1 Wishing or bestowing a blessing.<BR>2 A serpent's fang.<BR>3 A kind of venom, the venom of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before अश to eat, अच् and ङीप् affixes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वचन
आशीर्वचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A blessing, a benediction.<BR>E.<BR>आशिस् and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीर्वाद|आशीर्वादः|आशीर्व्वादः
आशीर्वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A blessing, a benediction.<BR>E.<BR>आशिस् and वाद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशीविष|आशीविषः
आशीविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>आशी a fang, and विष poison; in whose fang is venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु<BR>mfn. (-शुः-शुः-शु)<BR>Going quickly, fleet, fast.<BR>mn. (-शुः-शु)<BR>Rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR>n. adv. (-शु)<BR>Quick, quickly.<BR>E.<BR>अशू to pervade, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुकारिन्
आशुकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Doing any thing quickly, smart, active.<BR>2 (In medicine) Operating speedily.<BR>E.<BR>आशु and कारिन् what acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुग|आशुगः
आशुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going or moving quickly, swift, fleet.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The wind.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>आशु quick, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुपत्री
आशुपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A tree which yields frankincense, (Boswellia serrata). see शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुव्रीहि|आशुव्रीहिः
आशुव्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>Rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>आशु quick, and व्रीहि rice; that is, of rapid growth; also आशु. so आशुधान्य n. (-न्यं) and other compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणि|आशुशुक्षणिः
आशुशुक्षणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Wind, air.<BR>E.<BR>आशु before शुष to dry in the reiterative form, and अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशेकुटिन्
आशेकुटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौच|आशौचं
आशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Impurity.<BR>E.<BR>अशुचि impure, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्यं
आश्चर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Astonishing, wonderful.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>Surprise, astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before चर to go, deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य्यत्व|आश्चर्यत्व|आश्चर्यत्वं
आश्चर्य्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Wonderfulness.<BR>2 Wonder, astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>आश्चर्य्य and त्व; or with ता, आश्चर्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतन
आश्चोतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Aspersion, sprinkling.<BR>2 Applying ghee, &c. to the eyelids.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्चुत to sprinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्म|आश्मः
आश्म<BR>mfn. (-श्मः-श्मा-श्मं)<BR>Stony, made of stone, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् stone, and अण् affix: with the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मन|आश्मनः
आश्मन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Made of stone, stony, stone.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् and अञ aff.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् stone, अण् affix: immoveable as a stone, having no legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मिक
आश्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of stone, consisting of stone, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अश्मन् and ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
आश्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dried partially, consolidated, coagulated.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् dimin. श्यान dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रम|आश्रमं|आश्रमः
आश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A religious order, of which there are four kinds referable to the different periods of life, 1st, that of the student or Brahmacārī; 2d, that of the householder or Gṛhastha; 3d, that of the anchorite or Vānaprastha; and 4th, that of the beggar or Bhikṣu: see ब्रह्मचारी, &c.<BR>2 A college, a school.<BR>3 A hermitage, the abode of retired saints or sages.<BR>4 A wood or thicket.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्रम to perform religious austerities, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमगुरु|आश्रमगुरुः
आश्रमगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The head of a religious order, a preceptor, a principal.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रम a convent, and गुरु senior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमधर्म्म|आश्रमधर्म|आश्रमधर्मः
आश्रमधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The special duty or duties of each order of life.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रम and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिक|आश्रमिकः
आश्रमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to one of the four orders, see आश्रम.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रम as above, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिन्
आश्रमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>1 Belonging to one of the four orders.<BR>3 Belonging to a hermitage, a hermit, an anchorite, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रम and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रय|आश्रयः
आश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Being inclined or addicted to, following, practising.<BR>2 A recipient, the person or thing in which any quality or article is inherent, retained or received.<BR>3 An asylum, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">Page125</a>] place of refuge.<BR>4 A patron, a protector.<BR>5 Having recourse to a protector or asylum.<BR>6 A dwelling.<BR>7 Contiguity, vicinity.<BR>8 Source, origin.<BR>9 A plea, an excuse.<BR>10 Appropriate act, one consistent with the character of the agent.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्री to serve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=124" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयण
आश्रयण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Refuge, asylum, means of protection or security. आङ् before श्रि to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणीय
आश्रयणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be had recourse to.<BR>2 To be practised or followed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्रि to serve, affix अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयभूत
आश्रयभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protecting, supporting, one who is the refuge of any other.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रय and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयाश|आश्रयाशः
आश्रयाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>A forfeiter of an asylum, one who by misconduct, &c. loses patronage or protection.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR>E.<BR>आश्रय a house, &c. अश to eat, or consume, and अण् affix: similar compounds occur frequently, as आश्रयध्वंसिन्, आश्रयभुज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Compliant, obedient.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A promise, an engagement.<BR>2 Distress, fatigue.<BR>3 Fault, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, श्रु to hear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि<BR>f. (-श्रिः)<BR>The edge of a sword: see अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Inhabiting, dwelling in, resorting to as a retreat or asylum.<BR>2 Following, practising, observing.<BR>3 Using, employing, having recourse to.<BR>4 Receiving any thing, as an inherent or integral part.<BR>5 Taking one's station at or on, as at a window or a seat, &c.<BR>6 A dependant.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्रि to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित्य
आश्रित्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having sought or obtained an asylum.<BR>2 Having recourse to, employing, practising.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्रि to serve, ल्यप् affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत|आश्रुतः
आश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed.<BR>2 Heard.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्रु to hear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्ट
आश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Embraced.<BR>2 Embracing, who or what embraces.<BR>3 Connected, interwoven, blended.<BR>4 Attaching to, joining, who or what adheres to.<BR>5 Invested, spread.<BR>6 Connected as a consequence, deduced, concluded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्लिष to fold, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेष|आश्लेषः
आश्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Embracing, an embrace.<BR>2 Site of any act.<BR>3 Intimate connexion.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, श्लिष to fold, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्व|आश्वं
आश्व<BR>mfn. (-श्वः-श्वी-श्वं)<BR>Relating to a horse, drawn by horses, equestrian, &c.<BR>n. (-श्वं)<BR>1 A number of horses.<BR>2 A chariot drawn by horses.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व a horse, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थ|आश्वत्थं
आश्वत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>The fruit of the holy fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वत्थ and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थिक
आश्वत्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to or produced by the Aśvattha tree.<BR>2 Flowering of the Aśvattha (the time when.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्वत्थ and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुज|आश्वयुजः
आश्वयुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जी-जं)<BR>Belonging to or occurring in the same month of Āśvina.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The month Āśvina. (September-October.)<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>The day of full moon in Āśvina.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वयुज the first lunar mansion, affix अण् and fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वरथ
आश्वरथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-थी-थं)<BR>Belonging to a chariot.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वरथ and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A farrier, a groom.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व, लक्षण a mark, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायन|आश्वलायनः
आश्वलायन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>The name of a sage and legislator, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अश्वलायन and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसत्
आश्वसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Breathing, alive.<BR>2 Recovering, reviving.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वसित
आश्वसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Encouraged, cheered, consoled.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास|आश्वासः
आश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Completion, cessation.<BR>2 A chapter or section, the division of a book.<BR>3 A probable story.<BR>4 Breathing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, श्वस to breathe, to live, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासक|आश्वासकः
आश्वासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Clothing.<BR>mfn. (-कः-सिका-कं)<BR>Consoling, comforting.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासन|आश्वासनं
आश्वासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Consoling, encouraging, reviving.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासित
आश्वासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Encouraged, comforted.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वास्य
आश्वास्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having recovered or revived.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before श्वस to breathe, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Equestrian, cavalier, relating to a horse, drawn by horses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The month Āśvina, (September-October.)<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी the constellation, अण् deriv. affix: when the moon is in Āśvinī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>A day's journey for a horse.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व a horse, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेय|आश्विनेयः
आश्विनेय<BR>m. du. (-यौ)<BR>The two twin sons of AŚVINĪ, by SŪRYA, and physicians of Svarga; one of them is named NĀSATYA, the other DASRA: or the patronymic may be used in the singular to designate either one of them.<BR>E.<BR>अश्विनी and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीय|आश्वीयं
आश्वीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A number of horses.<BR>E.<BR>अश्व a horse, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढ|आषाढः
आषाढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>1 The name of a month, (June-July.)<BR>2 A staff of the wood of the Palāśa, carried by an ascetic in the month Āṣāḍha.<BR>3 The Malaya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>आषाढा the constellation, and अण् affix.<BR>f. (-ढी)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Āṣāḍha.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>The twenty-first and twenty-second lunar mansion; it is most commonly compounded with पूर्व्व^1 and उत्तरः see पूर्व्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सह to bear, अण् and टाप् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढक|आषाढकः
आषाढक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Āṣāḍha: see the preceding, also अषाढक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढभव|आषाढभवः
आषाढभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced in the month Āṣāḍha.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>आषाढ the month, and भव produced, from भू and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढाभू
आषाढाभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>आषाढा the sign, and भू produced, from भू to be, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्र|आष्ट्रं
आष्ट्र<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Æther, the sky or atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>अस to throw, to send, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस<BR>r. 2d cl. (आस्ते or आसते^1)<BR>1 To sit.<BR>2 To be present.<BR>3 To be or exist.<BR>With अधि prefixed.<BR>1 To inhabit, to dwell in.<BR>2 To sit over or upon.<BR>3 To mistake or err by taking one thing for another from similarity of appearance.<BR>With अभि,<BR>to sit or apply to, to study, to learn.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To leave, to abandon.<BR>2 To shake, agitate, &c. (as wind.)<BR>With उप,<BR>to worship, to do homage.<BR>With निर्,<BR>to expel.<BR>With प्र and निर्,<BR>to reject, to refute, to invalidate.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: cf mw, pwg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=125" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस्<BR>ind. (आः)<BR>An interjection, ah! oh! &c. implying,<BR>1 Recollection.<BR>2 Anger.<BR>3 Menace.<BR>4 Pain.<BR>5 Affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस|आसः
आस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>अस to send or throw, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Zealously following or pursuing, intent or attached strongly to.<BR>2 Trusting to, confiding in.<BR>3 Eternal.<BR>adv. n. (-क्तं)<BR>Eternally.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षञ्ज to embrace, to move, participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचित्त
आसक्तचित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Of a fixed mind, intent on, devoted to, absorbed in.<BR>E.<BR>आसक्त and चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तचेतस्
आसक्तचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ता-ताः-तः)<BR>Having the mind fixed or intent on any object.<BR>E.<BR>आसक्त and चेतस् the understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तमनस्
आसक्तमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Having the mind fixed upon any object.<BR>E.<BR>आसक्त and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्ति|आसक्तिः
आसक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Attachment to one object or pursuit, diligence, application.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षञ्ज to embrace, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्ग|आसंग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Attachment to any object.<BR>2 Association, connexion.<BR>3 Proximity, contact.<BR>adv. n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Eternally.<BR>adj. mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Eternal.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् always, षञ्ज to move, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गत्य|आसंगत्य|आसंगत्यं
आसङ्गत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Detachment, disunion.<BR>E.<BR>अ neg. सङ्गति union, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसङ्गिनी|आसंगिनी
आसङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A whirlwind.<BR>E.<BR>आसङ्ग eternal, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसज्जन
आसज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Putting on dress, armour, ornaments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षज्ज to dress, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसज्ज्य
आसज्ज्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having put on.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षज्ज to dress, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्ति|आसत्तिः
आसत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Intimate union, meeting, junction.<BR>2 Gain, profit, acquirement.<BR>3 In logic, connexion or relation between two or more proximate terms and the sense they convey.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षद to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन|आसनं|आसनः
आसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A stool, a seat.<BR>2 Maintaining a post against an enemy.<BR>3 The withers of an elephant, the part where the driver sits.<BR>4 Halting, stopping.<BR>5 Sitting in some peculiar posture, as in the custom of devotees, &c. eighty-four kinds are enumerated: see पद्मासन, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Pentapheca tomentosa.) also असन<BR>f. (-ना-नी)<BR>Stay, abiding, sitting.<BR>(-नी)<BR>1 A shop, a stall.<BR>2 A small seat, a stool.<BR>E.<BR>आस to abide, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्द|आसंदः|आसन्दः
आसन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी)<BR>A small couch or oblong chair, having the seat made of basket work.<BR>E.<BR>आस sitting, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A setting sun.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षद to go, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्नकाल|आसन्नकालः
आसन्नकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Hour of death.<BR>E.<BR>आसन्न and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Rum, spirit distilled from sugar or molasses.<BR>2 Spirituous liquor in general.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षूञ्^1 to be generated, and अप् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवद्रु|आसवद्रुः
आसवद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The palmyra tree.<BR>E.<BR>आसव spirit, and द्रु a tree; the juice of the palmyra upon fermenting affording a spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादन|आसादनं
आसादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Obtaining, attaining.<BR>2 Accomplishing.<BR>3 Going to or toward.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षद to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादित|आसादितः
आसादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Obtained.<BR>2 Reached, gone to.<BR>3 Spread, extended, overspread.<BR>4 Effected, completed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षद to go, in the causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
आसाद्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having attained or reached.<BR>2 Having obtained.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षद to go, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाधन|आसाधनं
आसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Accomplishment, attainment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षाध to succeed, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसार|आसारः
आसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hard shower.<BR>2 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>3 The army of an ally, or of a king whose dominions are separated by other intervening states.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, सृ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाव्य
आसाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be born.<BR>E.<BR>षु to bear, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A swordsman.<BR>E.<BR>असि a sword, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक|आसिकः
आसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who sits.<BR>E.<BR>आस to sit, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिक्त
आसिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before विच to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसित
आसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sat down.<BR>2 Who sits or is seated.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Place of abode, a city.<BR>2 A seat.<BR>E.<BR>आस to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिद्ध
आसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Accomplished, effected.<BR>2 Put under restraint: see आसेध.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षिध to go, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीन|आसीनः
आसीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sitting, seated.<BR>E.<BR>आस to sit, शानच् affix, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीनप्रचलायित|आसीनप्रचलायितं
आसीनप्रचलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Nodding, rocking as seated, falling asleep.<BR>E.<BR>आसीन and प्रचलायित set in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुति|आसुतिः
आसुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Distilling, distillation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षूञ्^1 to produce, affix क्तिन्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुतीबल
आसुतीबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sacrificer at the full and change of the moon.<BR>2 A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>आसुति and बलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Infernal, demoniac, belonging or relating to the Asuras.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An Asura or demon.<BR>2 A form of marriage, in which the bridegroom gives to the bride, her father and paternal kinsmen, as much as he can afford.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Black salt.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A division of medicine, surgery, curing by cutting with instruments, applying the actual cautery, &c.<BR>2 Mustard.<BR>E.<BR>असुर a demon, अण् and in the fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक|आसेकः
आसेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षिच to sprinkle, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आसेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sprinkling.<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Beloved, desired.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षिच to sprinkle, ल्युट् affix; also आसेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचनक|आसेचनकः
आसेचनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, षिच to sprinkle, ल्युट् and कन् aff. also असेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेद्धृ
आसेद्धृ<BR>m. (-द्धा)<BR>One who confines or arrests another.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षिध to go, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध|आसेधः
आसेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Arrest, legal restraint of four kinds; कालामेधः limit of time, स्थानामेधः confinement to a place, प्रवासासेधः prohibition against removal or departure, कर्म्मासेधः restriction from employment.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षिध to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेध्य
आसेध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>To be interrupted, prohibited or restrained.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before षिध to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दन|आस्कंदनं|आस्कन्दनं
आस्कन्दन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Going, going to, approaching.<BR>2 Effacing, destroying.<BR>3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>4 War, battle.<BR>5 Drying.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्कन्द to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दित|आस्कंदितं|आस्कन्दितं
आस्कन्दित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The walk of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>आङ, स्कन्द to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कन्दितक|आस्कंदितकं|आस्कन्दितकं
आस्कन्दितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तर|आस्तरः
आस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A covering, a coverlet, a blanket thrown over the back of a horse or elephant.<BR>2 Spreading clothes, &c.<BR>3 A carpet, a bed.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्तृञ् to spread, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=126" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आस्तरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A carpet, a rug, a quilt, bed clothes.<BR>2 A bed.<BR>3 A layer of sacred grass spread out at a sacrifice.<BR>4 An elephant's housings, a painted cloth or blanket worn on his back.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>E.<BR>अस्ति who is, and वुञ् affix; from an expression of his father, (he is in the womb,) pronouncing his conception to have taken place before there were any external indications of it.<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A believer, pious, faithful.<BR>E.<BR>अस्ति as before, saying that there is a GOD, &c. in opposition to the नास्तिक an atheist, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकता
आस्तिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Belief in GOD.<BR>E.<BR>आस्तिक and तल् affix; also with त्व affix आस्तिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकार्थद|आस्तिकार्थदः
आस्तिकार्थद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A name of a king, also called JANAMEJAYA.<BR>E.<BR>आस्तिक the Muni, अर्थ a request, and द who gives or grants; having at his request spared the Nāga, TAKṢAKA, from the destruction to which he had devoted the race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक|आस्तीकः
आस्तीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint, the son of JARATKĀRU, also a Muni: see आस्तिक.<BR>E.<BR>अस्ति and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीकजननी
आस्तीकजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of JARATKĀRU, a saint.<BR>E.<BR>आस्तीक as above, and जननी a mother, the mother of that saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक्य
आस्तीक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Belief in Providence and a future world.<BR>E.<BR>आस्तिक a believer, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीर्ण|आस्तीर्ण्ण
आस्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Spread, strewed, scattered.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्तॄ to spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृत
आस्तृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread.<BR>2 Covered.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्तृ to spread, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Prop, stay, place or means of abiding.<BR>2 An assembly.<BR>3 Effort, pains, care.<BR>4 Consideration, regard.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्था to stay, to stand, आङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थान|आस्थानं
आस्थान<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>An assembly.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Place, site.<BR>2 Staying, abiding.<BR>3 Pains, care.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्था to stay or stand, ल्युट् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थापन|आस्थापनं
आस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Placing, fixing, causing to stay or remain.<BR>2 An enema of oil, ghee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्था to stay, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थित
आस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stayed, dwelt, abiding, abode.<BR>2 Applied to, having recourse to.<BR>3 Occupied, engrossed by, engaged in.<BR>4 Spread, overspread.<BR>5 Obtained.<BR>6 Observing, adhering to, following, practising.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्था and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पद|आस्पदं
आस्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Business, affair.<BR>2 Office, rank, station.<BR>3 Dignity.<BR>4 Authority.<BR>5 Place, site.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before पद to go, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पन्दन|आस्पन्दनं
आस्पन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trembling, throbbing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्पदि to shake, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्द्धा
आस्पर्द्धा<BR>f. (-र्द्धा)<BR>Emulation, rivalry.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्पर्द्ध to vie with, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्द्धिन्
आस्पर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>Emulous.<BR>E.<BR>आस्पर्द्धा and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फाल|आस्फालः
आस्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Striking, rubbing, causing to move gently.<BR>2 Flapping, clapping.<BR>3 The flapping motion of an elephant's ear.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्फल to move, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालन|आस्फालनं
आस्फालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Rubbing, stirring, moving gently.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्फल to move, causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालित
आस्फालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Struck gently, rubbed, touched, stirred.<BR>2 Flapped, clapped, struck together.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्फल to move, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुजित्
आस्फुजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of ŚUKRA, regent of the planet VENUS, and teacher of the Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोट|आस्फोटः
आस्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A plant, (Swallow wort.)<BR>2 The sound of striking on the arms, as made by combatants, wrestlers, &c.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A wild variety of jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्फुट् to expand, and अच् affix; also आस्फोत^1 and आस्फोता.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटक|आस्फोटकः
आस्फोटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Careya arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्फुट् to blow, &c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटन|आस्फोटनं
आस्फोटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Blowing, expanding.<BR>2 Contracting, closing.<BR>3 Slapping the arms, or the noise made by it.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A gimlet or auger.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्फुट to blow or expand, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोत|आस्फोतः
आस्फोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>2 Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR>3 A kind of echites or savanna flower, (E. dichotoma, Rox.)<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A wild variety of jasmin.<BR>2 Clitoria ternatea.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्फुट to blow or expend, अच् affix and ट changed to त; or स्फै to encrease, with क्त affix, and आ converted to ओ; also sometimes आस्फोट and आस्फोटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 The face.<BR>2 The mouth.<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the mouth or face.<BR>E.<BR>अस to throw or direct, and ण्यत् affix, or आङ् before स्यन्द to go, and ड affix; to which food goes or is directed.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Stay, abiding, resting.<BR>E.<BR>आस to sit, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यपत्र|आस्यपत्रं
आस्यपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>आस्य a face, and पत्र a leaf; this flower is commonly compared to a beautiful face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलाङ्गल|आस्यलांगल|आस्यलाङ्गलः
आस्यलाङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A hog, a boar.<BR>E.<BR>आस्प and लाङ्गल a plough; whose face is as it were a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यलोमन्
आस्यलोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The beard.<BR>E.<BR>आस्य and लामन् hair; the hair of the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यासव|आस्यासवः
आस्यासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Spittle, saliva.<BR>E.<BR>आस्य the mouth, आसव liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रप|आस्रपः
आस्रप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The nineteenth lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>आस्रप a Rākṣasa or goblin, and अण् aff. one of this race being the deity of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रव|आस्रवः
आस्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Distress, pain, affliction.<BR>2 Flow, running, discharge.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्रु to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राव|आस्रावः
आस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Pain, affliction.<BR>2 Flow, issue, running, discharge.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्। स्रु to ooze, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वनित
आस्वनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, स्वन to sound, क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वान्त
आस्वान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Sounded.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before स्वन to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद|आस्वादः
आस्वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Tasting, eating.<BR>2 Enjoying.<BR>2 Flavour.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ष्वद to taste, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादन|आस्वादनं
आस्वादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tasting, eating.<BR>2 Enjoying.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ष्वद and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादित
आस्वादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tasted.<BR>2 Enjoyed, possessed.<BR>3 Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ष्वद to taste, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection, aha! ah! implying,<BR>1 Casting, sending.<BR>2 Severity, reproof.<BR>3 Commanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहक|आहकः
आहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A disease of the nose, inflammation of the Schneiderian membrane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत|आहतं|आहतः
आहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Struck, beaten.<BR>2 Injured, killed.<BR>3 Multiplied.<BR>4 Known, understood.<BR>5 Uttered falsely.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Old. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">Page128</a>] cloth or raiment.<BR>2 New cloth or clothes.<BR>3 Assertion of an impossibility.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A drum.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, हन to hurt or injure, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=127" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतलक्षण|आहतलक्षणः
आहतलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Noted for good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>आहत known, and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर|आहरः
आहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Breath inspired, inspiration.<BR>2 Taking, seizing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरण|आहरणं
आहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>2 Causing, inducing.<BR>3 Extracting, removing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्त्तृ|आहर्तृ
आहर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>One who takes or seizes.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>(In law,) A copy-holder.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
आहव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Sacrificing.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हु to sacrifice or ह्वेञ्^1 to call, and अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवन|आहवनं
आहवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sacrifice, offering sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हु to sacrifice, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीय|आहवनीयः
आहवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be offered as an oblation.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A consecrated fire taken from the householder's perpetual fire, and prepared for receiving oblations.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, हु to offer oblations, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयक|आहवनीयकः
आहवनीयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Fit for a burnt offering.<BR>m. (कः)<BR>A consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार|आहारः
आहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Taking, conveying.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, हृ to convey, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारसम्भव|आहारसंभव|आहारसंभवः|आहारसम्भवः
आहारसम्भव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>The juice of the body, chyle, lymph, serum, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आहार food, and सम्भव what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारार्थिन्
आहारार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Begging or seeking for food.<BR>E.<BR>आहार and अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य्य|आहार्य|आहार्यः|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Adventitious, accessory^1, incidental.<BR>2 To be taken or seized.<BR>3 To be eaten.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The ornamentative part of the drama, the dress, decorations, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृञ् to convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य्यशोभा|आहार्यशोभा
आहार्य्यशोभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Adventitious beauty, beauty not natural but the effect of pain, ornaments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आहार्य्य incidental, and शाभा splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
आहाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 Calling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ह्वे to call, घञ् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिक|आहिकः
आहिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A name of the inspired grammarian PĀṆINI.<BR>2 The descending node.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, or the constellation Aśleṣā, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिण्डिक|आहिंडिकः|आहिण्डिकः
आहिण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of mixed origin, the son of a Niṣada father and Vaidehī^1 mother, employed as a watchman on the outside of jails, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260430.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहित|आहितः
आहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed, deposited.<BR>2 Entertained, felt.<BR>3 Comprising, containing.<BR>4 Made, done.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, धा to have or hold, part. affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितलक्षण|आहितलक्षणः
आहितलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Noted for good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>see अहतलक्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितव्यथ
आहितव्यथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Pained, grieved.<BR>E.<BR>आहित felt, व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितस्वन
आहितस्वन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Noisy, uttering or making sound.<BR>E.<BR>आहित made, स्वन a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताङ्क|आहितांक
आहिताङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Marked, spotted, stained.<BR>E.<BR>आहित made, अङ्क a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिताग्नि|आहिताग्निः
आहिताग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A Brahman who has preserved a sacred fire kept alive perpetually in a family, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आहित placed, and अग्नि a fire; by whom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितुण्डिक|आहितुंडिकः|आहितुण्डिकः
आहितुण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler, a snake-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, तुण्ड a mouth, and ठक् affix; playing with the mouth of a snake: the poisonous fangs being extracted, the snakes are suffered to bite their exhibitors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुत|आहुतं
आहुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The nourishment of all created beings, considered as one of the five sacraments or principal sacrifices of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, हु to offer oblations, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुति|आहुतिः
आहुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Offering oblations with fire to the deities.<BR>2 Any solemn rite accompanied with oblations.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुल्य|आहुल्यं
आहुल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>A leguminous shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूत|आहूतं|आहूतः
आहूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Called, summoned, invoked, invited.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ह्वे to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतप्रपलायिन्
आहूतप्रपलायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A defendant or witness absconding, or not appearing when summoned.<BR>E.<BR>आहूत and प्रपलायिन् who runs away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूति|आहूतिः
आहूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Calling.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वे to call, affix क्तिन्; ए is dropped, and व is changed to its analogous vowel उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृत
आहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought, taken collected.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृव्य
आहृव्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken or received, having brought.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहेय|आहेयं
आहेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Belonging, or relating to a snake.<BR>E.<BR>अहि a snake, and ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहो
आहो<BR>ind.<BR>1 An interjection of doubt;<BR>2 Of asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोपुरुषिका
आहोपुरुषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Boasting, military vaunting.<BR>E.<BR>आहो, पुरूष a man, and affix कन्; doubting another's manhood, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहोस्वित्
आहोस्वित्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying doubt.<BR>E.<BR>आहो and स्वित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्न|आह्नः
आह्न<BR>n. (-ह्नं)<BR>Many days.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निक|आह्निकं
आह्निक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Daily, diurnal, of or belonging to a day.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Constant occupation, daily work.<BR>2 The division or section of a book.<BR>3 Food.<BR>E.<BR>अहन् a day, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निकाचार
आह्निकाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Daily observance, the prayers and practices necessary for bodily and mental purification.<BR>E.<BR>आह्निक and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लाद|आह्लादः
आह्लाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Joy, delight.<BR>E.<BR>आङ् before ह्लद to be pleased, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादित|आह्लादितः
आह्लादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delighted, rejoiced.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्लद to be delighted, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्व
आह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A crier, who or what calls.<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>1 A name, an appellation.<BR>2 A call, a summons.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वे to call, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वय|आह्वयः
आह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name or appellation.<BR>2 A lawsuit arising from a dispute about games with animals, as cockfighting, &c.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वेञ्^1 to call, अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वान|आह्वानं
आह्वान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calling, a call or summons.<BR>2 Legal summons.<BR>3 A name, an appellation.<BR>4 Invocation, invitation.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वेञ्^1 to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानदर्शन
आह्वानदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Day of trial.<BR>E.<BR>आह्वान summons, and दर्शन seeing, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वाय|आह्वायः
आह्वाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name<BR>2 A summons.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वे to call, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायक|आह्वायकः
आह्वायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A messenger, a courier.<BR>E.<BR>आङ्, ह्वे to call, ण्वुल् aff. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">Page129</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=128" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ<BR>The third vowel of the alphabet, corresponding to I short, and pronounced as that letter in kill, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ<BR>m. (-इः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection<BR>1 Of anger.<BR>2 Of calling.<BR>3 Of sorrow or distress.<BR>4 Of compassion.<BR>E.<BR>इ to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ<BR>r. 1st cl. (अयति)<BR>To go, to go to or towards:<BR>with उत् prefixed,<BR>to rise or ascend, as the sun, &c.<BR>with अभि and उत्<BR>the same, or to rise in the world, to prosper. (ङ) इङ् and अधि always prefixed अधीङ<BR>r. 2nd cl. (अधीते)<BR>To study, to learn, to read over or through.<BR>(क) इक and अधि prefixed r. 2nd cl. (अध्येति)<BR>To remember, to think of.<BR>(ण) इण् r. 2nd cl. (एति)<BR>To go. This root takes many prefixes, implying<BR>with अति,<BR>1 to surpass, to surmount.<BR>2 To pass, to spend time or to elapse as time.<BR>With अनु,<BR>1 To go after, to follow.<BR>2 To go like, to imitate in going.<BR>3 To succeed.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To obtain, to get.<BR>2 To proceed, to go on.<BR>3 To go.<BR>4 To approach.<BR>5 To serve or worship.<BR>With अप<BR>1 To go away, to depart.<BR>2 To perish.<BR>With अभि and उप,<BR>To arrive.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To receive.<BR>2 To aid or assist.<BR>3 To approach or go near to.<BR>With निर्,<BR>to go forth or out from.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>1 To trust, to confide.<BR>2 To follow, to be added or subjoined to.<BR>3 (In the passive verb,) To become evident or manifest.<BR>With वि,<BR>To expend, to waste, to depart.<BR>With सम and उप,<BR>To obtain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कट|इक्कटः
इक्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A kind of reed: see इत्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षव
इक्षव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षु|इक्षुः
इक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इष to desire, and क्सु affix or ईक्ष to see, असुन् affix and ई made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुकाण्ड|इक्षुकाण्डः
इक्षुकाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A species of sugar cane, (Saccharum munja, Rox.) see मुञ्ज.<BR>2 A sort of grass, (Kās,) (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>3 The stem or cane of the Saccharum officinale, the sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुगन्धा
इक्षुगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>2 Barleria longifolia, (this and its synonyms are also applied to Capparis spinosa and Tribulus lanuginosus: see कोकिलाक्ष and गोक्षुरक.)<BR>3 Convolvulus paniculatus: भूमिकुष्माण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and गन्ध smell; having the odor of the sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुगन्धिका
इक्षुगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Convolvulus paniculatus.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुतुल्या
इक्षुतुल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A species of grass or reed.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and तुल्या like, like sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुदण्ड|इक्षुदण्डः
इक्षुदण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>The stem or cane of the Saccharum officinale, the sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and दण्ड a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुदर्भा
इक्षुदर्भा<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>A kind of grass; also वंशमूल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुनेत्र|इक्षुनेत्रं
इक्षुनेत्र<BR>(-त्रं)<BR>A kind of tree.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and नेत्र an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुपत्र|इक्षुपत्रः
इक्षुपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A species of grain, Jowar, (Panicum spicatum).<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुप्र|इक्षुप्रः
इक्षुप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुबालिका
इक्षुबालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of reed: see इक्ष्वालिका.<BR>2 Saccharum spontaneum.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and बालिका an infant; a young sugar cane, from its smaller size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुभक्षिका
इक्षुभक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A meal of sugar or molasses.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु, भक्ष to eat, ण्वुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमती
इक्षुमती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The name of a river in Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and मतुप् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमूल|इक्षुमूलं
इक्षुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A sort of tree; also इक्षुनेत्र.<BR>2 The root of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमेह|इक्षुमेहः
इक्षुमेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Diabetes, or D. mellitus.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and मेह urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुमेहिन्
इक्षुमेहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Diabetic.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षुमेह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुयन्त्र|इक्षुयंत्र
इक्षुयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A sugar mill.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and यन्त्र a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुयोनि|इक्षुयोनिः
इक्षुयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The common sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुर|इक्षुरः
इक्षुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Sugar cane.<BR>2 Barleria longifolia or Tribulus lanuginosus.<BR>3 Saccharum spontaneum.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु sugar, and र what gives, from रा and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरक|इक्षुरकः
इक्षुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Saccharum spontaneum.<BR>2 Barleria longifolia: see the preceding, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरस|इक्षुरसः
इक्षुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The juice of the sugar cane.<BR>2 Molasses, unrefined sugar.<BR>3 A sort of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरसक्वाथ|इक्षुरसक्वाथः
इक्षुरसक्वाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Raw or unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षुरस and क्वाथ a decoction, the boiled or inspissated juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरसोद|इक्षुरसोदः
इक्षुरसोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of syrup.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षुरस and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुवाटिका
इक्षुवाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of sugar cane, the common yellow cane; also इक्षुवाटी; see पुण्ड्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुविकार|इक्षुविकारः
इक्षुविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Sugar, molasses.<BR>2 Any sweetmeat.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and विकार change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुवेष्टन|इक्षुवेष्टनः
इक्षुवेष्टन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुशाकट|इक्षुशाकटं
इक्षुशाकट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A field of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and शाकट a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुशाकिन|इक्षुशाकिनं
इक्षुशाकिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A field of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and शाकिन a field in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुसार|इक्षुसारः
इक्षुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Molasses, raw or unrefined sugar.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and सार essence, the essence of the sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वाकु|इक्ष्वाकुः
इक्ष्वाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>The son of the Menu VAIVASVATA, the son of SŪRYA or the sun, and first prince of the solar dynasty: he reigned at Ayodhya in the commencement of the second Yuga or age.<BR>f. (-कुः)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and अक to obtain, and कु or उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वालिक|इक्ष्वालिकः
इक्ष्वालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Another sort, (Saccharum fuscum); the native pens are made from its stem.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु and आलिका for आली a line; it grows like the sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इख
इख<BR>r. 1st cl. (एखति) and (इ) इखि (इंखति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इग
इग<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) इगि (इंगति)<BR>1 To go, to go to or towards.<BR>2 To move or agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्ग|इंग|इङ्गं|इङ्गः
इङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Moveable, locomotive.<BR>2 Surprising, wonderful.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A hint or sign, an indication of sentiment by gesture, &c.<BR>2 Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>इगि to go, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गित|इंगित|इङ्गितं
इङ्गित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Hint, sign, gesture.<BR>2 Going, motion.<BR>3 Intention, purpose.<BR>E.<BR>इगि to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गितज्ञ|इंगितज्ञ
इङ्गितज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Understanding signs.<BR>E.<BR>इङ्गित and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुद|इंगुद|इंगुदः|इङ्गुदः
इङ्गुद<BR>mf. (-दः-दी)<BR>The name of a plant, commonly Iṅguä.<BR>E.<BR>इङ्गु going, and द what gives; the pen. अ is changed to उ. and the fem. affix is ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इङ्गुल|इंगुलः|इङ्गुलः
इङ्गुल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, द being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=129" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-क)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Demand, the sum sought.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा wish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्व
इच्छत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Desire, wishfulness.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा and त्व affix; also with तल, इच्छता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छन्
इच्छन्<BR>mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छंती-च्छत्)<BR>Wishing, wishful, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>इष to desire, affixes श and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छानिवृत्ति|इच्छानिवृत्तिः
इच्छानिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Suppression of desire.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा and निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छान्वित
इच्छान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having desire, wishing, wishful.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छावत्|इच्छावन्त्
इच्छावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wishing, wishful, desirous.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A woman desirous of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा, मतुप् poss. affix, and ङीप् fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छावसु|इच्छावसुः
इच्छावसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा and वसु wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छु|इच्छुः
इच्छु<BR>mfn. (-च्छुः-च्छुः-च्छु)<BR>Wishing, desiring.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, and उस् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छुक|इच्छुकः
इच्छुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, or इच्छ and उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्जल|इज्जलः
इज्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small tree growing in wet and saline soil, or on low grounds near the sea, (Barringtonia acutangula.) see हिज्जल.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, क्किप् affix, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्य|इज्यः
इज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>A teacher.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, the teacher or Guru of the gods.<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 A gift, a donation.<BR>2 Sacrificing, making offerings to the gods or manes.<BR>3 Worship, reverence.<BR>4 Meeting, union.<BR>5 A cow.<BR>6 A bawd or procuress.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, &c. क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्याशील|इज्याशीलः
इज्याशील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A frequent sacrificer.<BR>E.<BR>इज्या sacrifice, and शील to be frequent, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इञ्चाक|इंचाकः|इञ्चाकः
इञ्चाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shrimp or prawn.<BR>E.<BR>इ love, चक to satisfy, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट|इटः
इट<BR>r. 1st cl. (एटति)<BR>To go, to go to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्चर|इट्चरः
इट्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull or steer allowed to go at liberty.<BR>E.<BR>इष् to wish, क्विप् affix, and चर who goes, going at will; also इड्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 The wife of BUDDHA, daughter of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A cow.<BR>4 Speed.<BR>5 A tubular vessel, one of the principal channels of the vital spirit, that which is on the right side of the body.<BR>6 Heaven.<BR>7 The goddess of speech.<BR>E.<BR>इल to direct or send, क affix, and टाप् fem. ल and ड are interchangeable: see इला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाचिका
इडाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>इडा the earth, चर to go, and ड्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिका
इडिका<BR>f. (का)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>इल to direct, and वुन् affix; ल becomes ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिक्क|इडिक्कः
इडिक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>इडिक् an imitative sound, and क who utters, from कै, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्वर|इड्वरः
इड्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull fit to be let at liberty.<BR>E.<BR>इष् to wish, affix क्विप्, and वृ to choose, अप् affix: see इट्चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्यीन्थ
इण्यीन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इण्वीन्दु
इण्वीन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A tree, (Trochis aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतःइतस्
इतःइतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Here here, come here.<BR>E.<BR>इतस् repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्
इत्<BR>ind.<BR>A grammatical term, implying a letter in the inflective particles that is to be rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत|इतः
इत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Remembered.<BR>3 Obtained.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Other, different.<BR>2 Low, vile.<BR>E.<BR>इ desire, तृ to pass over, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरथा
इतरथा<BR>ind.<BR>In another manner, otherwise, differently.<BR>E.<BR>था added to इतर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतर|इतरेतरं
इतरेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Mutual, one with another. Respective, several.<BR>E.<BR>इतर repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतरकाम्या
इतरेतरकाम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>Respective or several fancies or inclinations.<BR>E.<BR>इतरेतर and काम्य to be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेतराश्रय
इतरेतराश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Affecting or concerning mutually.<BR>E.<BR>इतरेतर and आश्रय object or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेद्युस्
इतरेद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>Another or different day.<BR>E.<BR>इतर and एद्यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Hence, from hence.<BR>E.<BR>irr. deriv. from इदम् this, with तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्ततस्
इतस्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>Here and there, hither and thither.<BR>E.<BR>इतस् hence, ततस् thence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतश्चेतस्
इतश्चेतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Hither and thither.<BR>E.<BR>इतस् repeated, with च and, inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying,<BR>1 Cause, (thus, therefore.)<BR>2 Manifestation, (lo! behold!)<BR>3 Something additional, (et cetera.)<BR>4 The meanings of एव, (so thus, even, in this manner)<BR>5 Conclusion, enough, (finis.)<BR>6 Reference, (so says, this is, &c.) It also implies,<BR>7 Order, arrangement, specific or distinctive, and<BR>8 Identity (of this or similar form.)<BR>9 A grammatical copulative, indicating a preceding sound or sense, to be again intended.<BR>E.<BR>इ to go, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकथ|इतिकथं
इतिकथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Unworthy of trust, not fit to be credited.<BR>2 Wicked, lost.<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Unmeaning or nonsensical discourse.<BR>E.<BR>इति this, so, and कथा a saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्त्तव्य|इतिकर्तव्य
इतिकर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What is proper or necessary to be done.<BR>E.<BR>इति so, कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिकर्त्तव्यता|इतिकर्तव्यता
इतिकर्त्तव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Proper and right measures.<BR>E.<BR>इतिकर्त्तव्य with तल् added, or with त्व, इतिकर्त्तव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिह
इतिह<BR>ind.<BR>Traditional instruction, advice, &c. mutually imparted.<BR>E.<BR>इति so, thus, and ह tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहास|इतिहासः
इतिहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>History, traditional accounts of former events, heroic history, as the Mahābhārata and Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>इतिह traditional instruction, अस to be, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्कठ
इत्कठ<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>A kind of reed or grass; also वहूमूल.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and कठ to go, उ is changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्किला
इत्किला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A perfume: see रोचना.<BR>E.<BR>इत obtained, and किल to play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्
इत्थम्<BR>ind.<BR>Thus.<BR>E.<BR>इदम् this, deriv. irr. with थमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थम्भूत|इत्थंभूत
इत्थम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become thus or in such manner.<BR>E.<BR>इत्यम् and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्य|इत्यः
इत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be gone to or towards.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>a litter, a palankeen.<BR>E.<BR>इत् to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्यादि
इत्यादि<BR>ind.<BR>Et cetera, and so forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Low, vile.<BR>2 Cruel, harsh.<BR>3 A traveller.<BR>4 Poor, indigent.<BR>5 Going, moving, what goes.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>इत and क्वरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद|इदं
इद<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) इदि (इन्दति)<BR>To have supreme power and superhuman faculties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=130" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदम्
इदम्<BR>pron. mfn. (अयं इयं इदं)<BR>This.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द to have power, कमिन् Uṇādi affix, and the radical न rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंकार्य्या|इदङ्कार्या|इदंकार्या|इदङ्कार्य्या
इदंकार्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi?)<BR>E.<BR>इदम् this, and कार्य्य business; applied to this and that use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीन्तन|इदानींतन|इदानीन्तनं
इदानीन्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Present, momentary, of the present moment.<BR>E.<BR>इदानीम् and द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीम्
इदानीम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Now, at present.<BR>2 An expletive, affecting however slightly the sense.<BR>E.<BR>irr. deriv. from इदम् this, with दानीम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदावत्सर|इदावत्सरः
इदावत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year, one of the five sorts of years in which gifts of clothes and food are productive of great rewards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Lighted, alight.<BR>2 Shining, glowing, blazing.<BR>3 Clean, clear, bright.<BR>4 Wonderful.<BR>5 Obeyed, unresisted.<BR>n. (-द्ध)<BR>1 Sunshine, light, heat.<BR>E.<BR>इन्ध to shine, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म<BR>n. (-ध्मं)<BR>Fuel.<BR>E.<BR>इन्धी to kindle, to burn, मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मप्रव्रञ्चन
इध्मप्रव्रञ्चन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>A hatchet, an axe.<BR>E.<BR>इध्म and प्रव्रच्चन what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन|इनः
इन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A master, a lord.<BR>3 A king.<BR>4 The asterism Hasta.<BR>E.<BR>इण् to go, नक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनसभ
इनसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A royal court or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>इन and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दम्बर|इंदंबरं|इन्दम्बरं
इन्दम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The blue lotus, (Nymphaea coerulea.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्दं from इदि to possess great power, and वर what chooses, preeminent above other flowers: see इन्दीवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिन्दिर|इंदिंदिरः|इन्दिन्दिरः
इन्दिन्दिर<BR>m. (रः)<BR>A large bee.<BR>E.<BR>इदि to possess great power, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरा|इंदिरा
इन्दिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>इदि as above, and रा who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरालय|इन्दिरालयं
इन्दिरालय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The lotus, (Nymphaea lotus.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्दिरा LAKṢMĪ, and आलय an abode; this goddess issued at the creation from the petals of the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिरावर|इन्दिरावरं
इन्दिरावर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दिरा the goddess, and वर what is best; a flower beloved by LAKṢMĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दिवर|इंदिवर|इंदिवरं|इन्दिवरं
इन्दिवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The blue lotus, (Nymphaea coerulea.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्दि for इन्दिरा q. v. the rest as in the preceding; also इन्दीवर and इन्दीवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवर|इंदीवर|इंदीवरं|इन्दीवरं
इन्दीवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus).<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दीवार|इन्दीवारं|इंदीवारः|इन्दीवारः
इन्दीवार<BR>n. (रं)<BR>See इन्दिवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दु|इंदुः|इन्दुः
इन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to wet or moisten; उ Uṇādi affix, and the initial changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकमल|इन्दुकमलं
इन्दुकमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु the moon, and कमल the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकला
इन्दुकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A digit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and कला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकलिका
इन्दुकलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Ketakī flower.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and कलिका a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुकान्त|इन्दुकान्तः
इन्दुकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The lunar gem, the moon-stone.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and कान्त a master or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजनक|इन्दुजनकः
इन्दुजनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and जनक a parent; the moon was produced amongst other things at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुजा
इन्दुजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The Narmadā or commonly Nerbudda river in the Dekhin.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and जा born; the daughter of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुदल|इन्दुदलः
इन्दुदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A portion of the moon, a digit, a crescent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुपुत्र|इन्दुपुत्रः
इन्दुपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A name of BUDHA, regent, of the planet MERCURY.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and पुत्र the son: the son of CANDRA or the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुभृत्
इन्दुभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and भृत् who nourishes; ŚIVA wears a half moon on his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमण्डल
इन्दुमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The orb or disc of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुमती|इंदुमती
इन्दुमती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 Day of full moon.<BR>2 Name of a princess married to AJA the son of RAGHU.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and मतुप् poss. affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुर
इन्दुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to moisten, उरच् affix, the initial is changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरत्न|इन्दुरत्नं
इन्दुरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुरेखा
इन्दुरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A digit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलेखा
इन्दुलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A digit of the moon.<BR>2 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>3 The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>4 A kind of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen): see यमानिका.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुलोहक|इन्दुलोहकं
इन्दुलोहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and लोह iron, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुवल्ली
इन्दुवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्दुव्रत|इन्दुव्रतं
इन्दुव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A religious observance depending on the age of the moon; diminishing the quantity of food by a certain portion daily, for a fortnight or a month, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु and व्रत a religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्र|इंद्रः|इन्द्रः
इन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 The deity presiding over Svarga or the Hindu paradise, and the secondary divinities; he is also regent of the east quarter, and is more particularly the deity of the atmosphere, corresponding in many respects with the Grecian JOVE.<BR>2 The Supreme Being, (according to the Vedānta,) or the deity INDRA in that capacity.<BR>3 Supremacy, supreme power or authority.<BR>4 An Āditya, one of the twelve demigods so called.<BR>5 One of the Yogas, or divisions of a circle on the plane of the ecliptic.<BR>6 The human or animal soul, the portion of spirit residing in the body.<BR>7 Night.<BR>8 A plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica, &c.) see कुटज.<BR>9 An organ of sense.<BR>10 (In composition) Best, excellent.<BR>11 The 14th lunation of the month Jyeṣṭha.<BR>12 One of the nine divisions of Jambu Dvīpa, or the known continent.<BR>f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>1 The name of a plant, (Marjoram?) see फणिम्भक.<BR>2 The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>इदि to possess supreme power, and रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रक|इंद्रकं|इन्द्रकं
इन्द्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An assembly-room, a hall.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र excellent, and क what sounds, from कै and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकील|इन्द्रकीलः
इन्द्रकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Mandara, a fabulous mountain with which the ocean was churned.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकुञ्जर|इन्द्रकुञ्जरः
इन्द्रकुञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रकोष|इन्द्रकोषः
इन्द्रकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A platform, a scaffold.<BR>2 A projection of the roof of a house, forming a kind of balcony or terrace.<BR>3 A pin or bracket projecting from the wall.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, and कोष a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रगोप|इन्द्रगोपः
इन्द्रगोप<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>An insect, (Coccinella of various kinds.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, गो light, and प from पा who nourishes or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=131" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रछन्दस्|इन्द्रच्छन्दस्
इन्द्रछन्दस्<BR>n. (-न्दः)<BR>A necklace of a thousand strings.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, and छन्दस् a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजाल|इन्द्रजालं
इन्द्रजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Conjuring, juggling.<BR>2 Deception, cheating.<BR>3 Trick or stratagem in war.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र an organ of sense, and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजालिक|इन्द्रजालिकः
इन्द्रजालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 A juggler, a conjuror.<BR>2 Deceptive, unreal.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रजाल illusion, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजित्
इन्द्रजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and जित् who conquers: the conqueror of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रजिद्विजयिन्
इन्द्रजिद्विजयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>LAKṢMAṆA, the brother of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रजित् and विजयिन् a victor, the conqueror of INDRAJIT.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रतूल|इन्द्रतूलं
इन्द्रतूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A flock of cotton, a flocculent seed, &c. blown about in the air.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and तूल cotton: INDRA'S cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रतूलक|इन्द्रतूलकं
इन्द्रतूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रदारु|इन्द्रदारुः
इन्द्रदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tree, (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and दारु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रद्रु|इन्द्रद्रुः
इन्द्रद्रु<BR>n. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and द्रु a tree; a staff of which is fit to carry the banner of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रद्रुम|इन्द्रद्रुमः
इन्द्रद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रनील|इन्द्रनीलः
इन्द्रनील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रनीलक|इन्द्रनीलकः
इन्द्रनीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुष्पा
इन्द्रपुष्पा<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A medicinal plant; also अग्निजिह्वा.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and पुष्पा a flower: also इन्द्रपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रपुरोहिता
इन्द्रपुरोहिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The asterism Puṣya.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and पुरोहिता priest, INDRA presiding over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रस्थ|इंद्रप्रस्थ|इन्द्रप्रस्थं
इन्द्रप्रस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>Ancient Dehli.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र the deity, and प्रस्थ who presides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रप्रहरण|इन्द्रप्रहरणं
इन्द्रप्रहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and प्रहरण a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रभेषज|इन्द्रभेषजं
इन्द्रभेषज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Dried ginger.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, and भेषज medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमहकामुक|इन्द्रमहकामुकः
इन्द्रमहकामुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, मह a sacrifice, and कामुक desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रमूल
इन्द्रमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A flock of cotton: see इन्द्रतूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रयव|इन्द्रयवः
इन्द्रयव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>The seed of the Wrightea antidysenterica.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र the plant, and यव seed: it is used medicinally in cases of diarrhoea, dysentery, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्त|इन्द्रलुप्तं|इन्द्रलुप्तः
इन्द्रलुप्त<BR>mn. (-प्तः-प्तं)<BR>Morbid baldness, falling of the hair of the head: according to some authorities, loss of beard.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, लुप्त lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलुप्तक|इन्द्रलुप्तकं
इन्द्रलुप्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोक|इन्द्रलोकः
इन्द्रलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Svarga or paradise, the heaven of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रलोकेश|इन्द्रलोकेशः
इन्द्रलोकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 A guest, hospitality to whom secures paradise.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रलोक and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणिका
इन्द्रवारुणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Colocynth, a wild bitter gourd, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवारुणी
इन्द्रवारुणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and वरुण the two deities so called, affixes अण् and ङीप्; the favourite plant of INDRA and VARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृक्ष|इन्द्रवृक्षः
इन्द्रवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A kind of fir: see देवदारु.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र for any god, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रव्रत
इन्द्रव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the duties of a king, to distribute gratification, as INDRA pours down rain.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रवृद्धा
इन्द्रवृद्धा<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>A sore, an ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रशक्ति|इन्द्रशक्तिः
इन्द्रशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>INDRĀṆĪ, the wife or personified energy of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसावर्णि|इन्द्रसावर्णिः
इन्द्रसावर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>The last of the fourteen Manus.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and सावर्णि the son of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुत|इन्द्रसुतः
इन्द्रसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The monkey king BĀLĪ.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and सुत a son; the son of INDRA: the epithet is also applied to ARJUNA and JAYANTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरस|इन्द्रसुरसः
इन्द्रसुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A shrub, the leaves of which are used in discutient applications, (Vitex negundo); also सिन्दुवार.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र best, सु good, and रस juice; whose juice is excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसुरिस|इन्द्रसुरिसः
इन्द्रसुरिस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, the pen. being changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रसूनु|इन्द्रसूनुः
इन्द्रसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The son of INDRA: see इन्द्रसुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राग्निधूम|इन्द्राग्निधूमः
इन्द्राग्निधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणिका|इंद्राणिका
इन्द्राणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Vitex negundo: see इन्द्रसुरस.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राणी|इंद्राणी
इन्द्राणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The wife of INDRA.<BR>2 A plant, (Vitex negundo): see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, ङीष् affix, and आनुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रानुज|इन्द्रानुजः
इन्द्रानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and अनुज younger born: the younger brother of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रायुध|इन्द्रायुधं|इन्द्रायुधः
इन्द्रायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The rainbow.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>A kind of leech of various tints on the back.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and आयुध a weapon; INDRA'S weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रारि|इन्द्रारिः
इन्द्रारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An Asura or demon.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रावरज|इन्द्रावरजः
इन्द्रावरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and अवरज after-born: the younger brother of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्राशन|इन्द्राशनः
इन्द्राशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Hemp, dried and chewed.<BR>2 The shrub which bears the seed used as jeweller's weight, (Abrus precatorius).<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and अशन food: the food of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रासन
इन्द्रासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The throne of INDRA.<BR>2 Any throne.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and असन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रिय|इंद्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 An organ of sense divided into three classes, Jñānendriyas, Karmendriyas, and Antarindriyas, or organs of perception and action, and the internal organs; the first are the eye, ear, nose, tongue, and skin; the second, the organ of speech or larynx, hand, foot, anus, and parts of generation; the last are, Manas the mind or organ of thought; Buddhi the organ of apprehension; Ahaṅkāra the organ of selfishness; and Citta the heart or organ of feeling.<BR>2 Semen virile.<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Done, seen, given, &c. by INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र the soul or self, and इयच् affix, deriv. irr. what is with difficulty restrained by the soul, or इन्द्र the deity, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियगोचर|इन्द्रियगोचरः
इन्द्रियगोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Perceptible, capable of being ascertained by the senses.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and गोचर perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियग्राम|इन्द्रियग्रामः
इन्द्रियग्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The senses or organs of sense collectively.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and ग्राम here, assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियज्ञान
इन्द्रियज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The faculty of perception, sense, consciousness.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियनिग्रह|इन्द्रियनिग्रहः
इन्द्रियनिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Restraining the organs of sense.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबुद्धि|इन्द्रियबुद्धिः
इन्द्रियबुद्धि<BR>f. (द्धिः)<BR>Perception, the exercise of any sense, the faculty of any organ.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and बुद्धि knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=132" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियबोधन
इन्द्रियबोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any excitement of sense, an object of perception, a stimulus, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and बोधन waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियवर्ग|इन्द्रियवर्गः
इन्द्रियवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The organs of sense collectively.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति|इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्तिः
इन्द्रियविप्रतिपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Erroneous or vicious perception.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and विप्रतिपत्ति perversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियस्वाप|इन्द्रियस्वापः
इन्द्रियस्वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Unconsciousness, insensibility.<BR>2 The end of the world.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and स्वाप sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियागोचर
इन्द्रियागोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Imperceptible.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and अगोचर imperceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियायतन|इन्द्रियायतनं
इन्द्रियायतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and आयतन a mansion: the residence of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियार्थ|इन्द्रियार्थः
इन्द्रियार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>An object of sense, as sound, smell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रियासङ्ग|इन्द्रियासङ्गः
इन्द्रियासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Stoicism, philosophy, detachment from sensual objects.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय and असङ्ग detachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्द्रेज्य|इन्द्रेज्यः
इन्द्रेज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>The name of VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र and इज्य to be worshipped; venerable to the deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्ध|इंध|इन्धः
इन्ध<BR>r. 7th cl. (ई and ञि) ञिइन्धी (इन्धे)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्धन|इंधन|इन्धनं
इन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fuel; wood, grass, &c. used for that purpose.<BR>E.<BR>इन्ध to kindle, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वका
इन्वका<BR>f. plu. (-काः)<BR>Stars in the head of Orion.<BR>E.<BR>इवि to please, क्वुन् affix: see इल्वला and इल्वका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) इभि (इम्भयते)<BR>To collect or accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ|इभः
इभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 Best (in composition.)<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, भन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभकणा
इभकणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant with an aromatic seed, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>E.<BR>इभ an elephant, and कणा pepper; being considered by Hindu writers, as a large species of pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभदन्ता
इभदन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A plant: see नागदन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and दन्त a tooth: this and similar names are given, from its supposed resemblance to an elephant's tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभनिमीलिका
इभनिमीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Smartness, shrewdness, wittiness.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and निभनिमीलिका winking; winking knowingly like an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपालक|इभपालकः
इभपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The driver or keeper of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>इभ, पालक a nourisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभपोटा
इभपोटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A young elephant, a cub.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and पोटा any young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभमाचल|इभमाचलः
इभमाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>इभ an elephant, in the second case, आ and चल who attacks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभयुवति|इभयुवतिः
इभयुवति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An elephant's cub.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and युवति young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभाख्य|इभाख्यः
इभाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea): see नागकेशर.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and आख्या an appellation; named from the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभोषणा
इभोषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A kind of aromatic plant: see इभकणा.<BR>E.<BR>इभ and उषणा pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>Wealthy, opulent.<BR>f. (-भ्या)<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>2 The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>इभ an elephant; here also implying excellence, and यत् affix of appropriation or fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्|इयन्त्
इयत्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यती-यत्)<BR>So much, thus much.<BR>E.<BR>इदम् this, and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्ता
इयत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Fixed measure or quantity, so much.<BR>E.<BR>इयत् and तल् affix; also with त्व, इयत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरण|इरणं
इरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Desert.<BR>2 Salt or barren, (soil.)<BR>E.<BR>see इराण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरम्मद|इरंमद|इरम्मदः
इरम्मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A flash of lightning, or the fire attending the fall of a thunderbolt.<BR>2 Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>इरा water, here also watery clouds, and मद what plays or shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Speech.<BR>4 The goddess of speech, &c.<BR>5 Ardent spirits.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, and रन् Uṇādi affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराचर|इराचरं
इराचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Hail.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Earth-born, terrestrial.<BR>2 Aquatic.<BR>E.<BR>इरा water, &c. and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इराज|इराजः
इराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KANDARPA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>इरा water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावत्|इरावन्त्
इरावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 A king.<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Watery, having or yielding water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इरा and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावेल्लिका
इरावेल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Pimples or pustules on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण|इरिणं|इरिणः
इरिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A desert, an inhospitable region.<BR>2 Salt or barren soil.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, इनन् Uṇādi affix, and the initial changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिमेद|इरिमेदः
इरिमेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A fetid mimosa: see विट्खदिर.<BR>E.<BR>see अरिमेद, अ being changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरु
इरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>Seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरेश|इरेशः
इरेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A king, a sovereign.<BR>3 VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>इरा SARASVATĪ, &c. and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वारु|इर्वारु|इर्वारुः|इर्व्वारुः
इर्व्वारु<BR>mf. (-रुः-रुः)<BR>1 A cucumber, (Cumumis utilatissimus, Rox.)<BR>2 Another kind, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR>E.<BR>इरु a seed, and आरु what goes to or gets, from ऋ and उण् affix, or आलु, र becoming ल; also written इर्व्वालु, ईर्व्वारु, उर्व्वारु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वारुशुक्तिका|इर्वारुशुक्तिका
इर्व्वारुशुक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of melon; commonly Sphuti or Sphut, (Cucumis momordica.)<BR>E.<BR>इर्व्वारु and शुक्तिका an oyster-shaped cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्व्वालु|इर्वालु|इर्व्वालुः
इर्व्वालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>See इर्व्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल
इल<BR>r. 6th cl. (इलति)<BR>1 To sleep.<BR>2 To go.<BR>3 To throw, send or direct: in this last sense, it is also r. 10th cl. (एलयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलविला
इलविला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The mother of KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The wife of BUDDHA, and daughter of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A cow.<BR>4 Speech.<BR>E.<BR>इल to send, क and टाप् affixes; also इडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलागोल
इलागोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The earth, the globe.<BR>E.<BR>इला and गोल a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलातल
इलातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The fourth place in the circle^1 of the zodiac.<BR>2 The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>इला and तल below.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलावृत|इलावृतं
इलावृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the nine Varṣas or divisions of the known world, comprehending the highest and most centrical part of the old continent.<BR>E.<BR>इला the earth, and आवृत chosen: the fairest part of the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिका
इलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>इल to go, कन् and टाप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इली
इली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A cudgel, a stick shaped like a sword or a short sword: see ईली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीश|इलीशः
इलीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A fish, commonly the Hilsa or Sable, (Clupea alosa.)<BR>E.<BR>इल to go, (in the water,) and ईश chief, principal. The fish being one of high flavour, and very abundant at certain seasons, it is generally eaten both by the natives of Bengal, and by Europeans residing there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लल|इल्ललः
इल्लल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>इल to go, and अल who is able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लिश|इल्लिशः
इल्लिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The Hilsa fish: see इलीश; also ईल्लीश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=133" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वका
इल्वका<BR>f. plu. (-काः)<BR>Stars in Orion's head: see इल्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वड
इल्वड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वल|इल्वलः
इल्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The name of a demon.<BR>2 Of a fish.<BR>f. plu. (-लाः)<BR>Stars in Orion's head.<BR>E.<BR>इल to send or go, and वल Uṇādi affix; the last is also written इल्वका ut sup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) इवि (इंवति)<BR>1 To pervade.<BR>2 (According to some,) to please.<BR>3 To be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव<BR>ind.<BR>So, even, as, like, in the same manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इशीका
इशीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An elephant's eye-ball: see इषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष|इषः
इष<BR>r. 4th cl. (इष्यति)<BR>To go.<BR>r. 6th cl. (इच्छति)<BR>1 To wish, to desire.<BR>2 To accept, to receive.<BR>With अभि,<BR>to desire:<BR>with प्रति,<BR>to engage, to promise.<BR>r. 9th cl. (इष्णाति)<BR>To repeat an act, to do any thing again and again.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>to search after, to investigate or enquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष|इषः
इष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The month Āśvina, (September-October.)<BR>E.<BR>इष to go, क affix; also ईष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिका
इषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An elephant's eye-ball.<BR>2 A painter's brush, &c. also इषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिर|इषिरः
इषिर<BR>m. (रः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>इष to go, किरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीका
इषीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An elephant's eye-ball.<BR>2 A painter's brush, &c. also इषिका.<BR>3 A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>इष to go, ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषु|इषुः
इषु<BR>mf. (-षुः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A versed sine.<BR>E.<BR>इष to go, and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधर|इषुधरः
इषुधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An archer.<BR>E.<BR>इषु and धर who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधि|इषुधिः
इषुधि<BR>mf. (-धिः)<BR>A quiver.<BR>E.<BR>इषु and धि what holds, from धा root, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
इष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>2 Cherished, beloved.<BR>3 Worshipped, reverenced, respected.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A lover, a husband.<BR>2 The Castor-oil tree.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 An act of sacrifice, an oblation, &c.<BR>2 An essential ceremony, as ablution, investiture, &c.<BR>ind. (-ष्टम)<BR>Voluntarily.<BR>E.<BR>इष to desire, or इष substituted for यज to sacrifice, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकर्म्मन्|इष्टकर्मन्
इष्टकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>(In arithmetic,) Rule of supposition, operation with an assumed number.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट wished, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A brick; also इष्टिका.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, तकक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकान्यास|इष्टकान्यासः
इष्टकान्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Laying the foundation of a house.<BR>E.<BR>इष्टका and न्यास order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकापथ|इष्टकापथं|इष्टकापथः
इष्टकापथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum).<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट wished, and कापथ a bad road, growing in or preferring unfrequented places: this word is sometimes divided, कापथ being one name, and इष्ट added to अवदाह, another name: see अवदाहेष्ट and अवदाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टकाराशि|इष्टकाराशिः
इष्टकाराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>A pile of bricks.<BR>E.<BR>इष्टका and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टगन्ध|इष्टगन्धं|इष्टगन्धः
इष्टगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Fragrant, any fragrant substance.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Sand.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and गन्ध a smell; of a desirable odor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टतम
इष्टतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Beloved, best beloved, dearest, most desired.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टतर
इष्टतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dearer, more dear, more desired.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टत्व
इष्टत्व<BR>n. (त्वं)<BR>1 Desirableness.<BR>2 Reverence, &c. also इष्टता.<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to इष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेव|इष्टदेवः
इष्टदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A tutelary deity, one particularly worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टदेवता
इष्टदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A person's chosen or tutelary divinity.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्त्त|इष्टापूर्त|इष्टापूर्तं|इष्टापूर्त्तं
इष्टापूर्त्त<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>Any religious duty, a oblation, sacrifice, penance, holy study, digging a well, planting a tree, &c.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट a sacrifice, and पूर्त्त liberal act, religiously considered; आङ् prefixed to the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टार्थोद्युक्त|इष्टार्थोद्युक्तः
इष्टार्थोद्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Zealously active, diligent for a desired object.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट wished, अर्थ intention, and उद्युक्त diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टि|इष्टिः
इष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 A sacrifice, any sacrificial rite.<BR>3 A compendious verse easily committed to memory.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, or इष substituted for यज, to sacrifice; affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A brick.<BR>E.<BR>more usually इष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिन्
इष्टिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्टी-ष्टिनी-ष्टि)<BR>Who wishes or desires, desirous, wishing.<BR>E.<BR>इष्ट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिपच|इष्टिपचः
इष्टिपच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A demon.<BR>E.<BR>इष्टि a sacrifice or oblation, and पच who digests: stealing oblations to the deities, and eating them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिमुष्
इष्टिमुष्<BR>m. (-मुट्)<BR>A demon.<BR>E.<BR>इष्टि an oblation, and मुष् who steals; from मुष root, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टु|इष्टुः
इष्टु<BR>f. (-ष्टुः)<BR>Desire, wish.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, तु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट्वा
इष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having sacrificed or worshipped.<BR>2 Having wished.<BR>E.<BR>इष with क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR>2 Spring.<BR>E.<BR>इष to desire, and मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्य|इष्यं|इष्यः
इष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>The spring season.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, and क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्व|इष्वः
इष्व<BR>m. (-ष्वः)<BR>A spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वास|इष्वासं|इष्वासः
इष्वास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>A thrower of arrows.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 An archer, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>इषु an arrow, and आस who throws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस्<BR>ind. (-इः)<BR>An interjection of anger, pain, or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह<BR>ind.<BR>1 Here, in this place.<BR>2 Now, at this time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहकाल|इहकालः
इहकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>This life.<BR>E.<BR>इह and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलोक|इहलोकः
इहलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>This life, this world.<BR>E.<BR>इह and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहामूत्र
इहामूत्र<BR>ind.<BR>Here and there, in this world and in the next.<BR>E.<BR>इह here, अमूत्र there or in that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई<BR>The fourth letter of the alphabet, corresponding to I long, having the sound of ee in feel, and distinguished by an accent from the former, as ī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई<BR>m. (-ईः)<BR>A name of KANDARPA.<BR>f. (ईः)<BR>A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Anger.<BR>3 Consciousness or perception.<BR>4 Consideration.<BR>5 Compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई<BR>r. 2nd cl. (एति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To pervade.<BR>3 To conceive or become pregnant.<BR>4 To desire.<BR>5 To throw or direct.<BR>6 To eat.<BR>This root is not generally admitted, though it occurs in composition, as with उत्<BR>(उदीते)<BR>To appear.<BR>r. 4th cl. (ङ) ईङ (ईयते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष
ईक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ईक्षते)<BR>To see. It most usually occurs compounded with one or other of the prepositions, as<BR>with अप,<BR>to expect;<BR>with अभि,<BR>to gaze at;<BR>with अव,<BR>to inspect;<BR>with उत् or उप,<BR>to expect or await;<BR>with उप,<BR>to abandon;<BR>with निर्,<BR>to see; [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">Page135</a>]<BR>with परि,<BR>to try, to test, to assay;<BR>with प्र,<BR>to see, to resemble, or look like;<BR>with वि,<BR>to inspect;<BR>with प्रति,<BR>1 to look for, to expect.<BR>2 to venerate;<BR>with सम,<BR>to compare, to contrast, to select;<BR>with प्रति and उत्,<BR>to look up at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=134" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षण|ईक्षणं
ईक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 An eye.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिका
ईक्षणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female fortune-teller.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्षण seeing, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षमाण
ईक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Looking at, surveying.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्ष to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षित
ईक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्ष and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख
ईख<BR>r. 1st cl. (ईखति)<BR>To go; also (इ) ईखि (ईखति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज
ईज<BR>r. 1st cl. (ङ) (ईजते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To blame or censure; also (इञ) ईजिञ् (ईंजति-ते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड
ईड<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ईट्टे) also 10th cl. (ईडयति)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडण
ईडण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Praising.<BR>E.<BR>ईड and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Praise.<BR>E.<BR>ईड to praise. क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडित|ईडितः
ईडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, commended.<BR>E.<BR>ईड to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्य
ईड्य<BR>mfn. (-ड्यः-ड्या-ड्यं)<BR>To be praised, to be glorified.<BR>E.<BR>ईड to praise, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईढ
ईढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईत
ईत<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) ईति (ईंतति)<BR>To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईत
ईत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone.<BR>E.<BR>ई to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Calamity of season, as drought, excessive rain, rats, foreign invasion, &c.<BR>2 Travelling in foreign countries, sojourning.<BR>3 An affray.<BR>E.<BR>ईङ to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Such.<BR>E.<BR>ई for इदम् this, दृश to see, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश्
ईदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Such, so like.<BR>E.<BR>ई for इदम् this, दृश with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश|ईदृशः
ईदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Such, so like.<BR>E.<BR>as the last, with कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सन
ईप्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Desiring, wishing to obtain.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, desiderative form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desirous, wishing to get or obtain.<BR>E.<BR>आप to obtain, desiderative form, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर|ईरः
ईर<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ईर्त्ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To shake.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (ईरति, ईरयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To throw or direct, to drive or force on;<BR>with उत् prefixed,<BR>to say or speak:<BR>with प्र,<BR>to send, to make to go;<BR>with सम्,<BR>to go like the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईयिवस्
ईयिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वस्)<BR>1 Gone, having gone.<BR>2 Having obtained.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, क्वसु aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Desert.<BR>2 Saline and barren (soil.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, and इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, dispatched.<BR>2 Said, uttered.<BR>3 Gone.<BR>4 Made.<BR>E.<BR>ईर to send, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिताकूत
ईरिताकूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Declared purpose or intention.<BR>E.<BR>ईरित and आकूत purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य
ईर्क्ष्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (ईर्क्ष्यति)<BR>To envy, to feel impatient at another's prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म्म|ईर्म|ईर्मः
ईर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>A sore or wound.<BR>E.<BR>ईर to send, and मक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य्या|ईर्या
ईर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>ईर to go, affix क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्व्वारु|ईर्वारु|ईर्वारुः|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्व्वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus); also ईर्व्वालु and इर्व्वारु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Impatience, envy of another's success; more properly read ईर्ष्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्षालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Impatient of another's success, envious.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्षा and आलुच् affix: see ईर्घ्यालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षित
ईर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Envied.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Envy.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्षा and इतच् affix, or ईर्ष with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (ईर्ष्यति)<BR>To envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं)<BR>Envious, envying.<BR>f. (-र्ष्या)<BR>1 Envy or impatience of another's success.<BR>2 Spite, malice.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्ष्य to envy, and अच् and टाप् affixes; also, but according to the best writers, inaccurately written ईर्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Envious, envying.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्ष्यं and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यमान
ईर्ष्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Envying, envious.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्ष्य and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्यालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Envious.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्ष्य and आलुच् affix; also written ईर्षालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यावश
ईर्ष्यावश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Being overcome with envy.<BR>E.<BR>ईष्या and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यिन्
ईर्ष्यिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्ष्यी-र्ष्यिणी-र्ष्यि)<BR>Envious, spiteful.<BR>E.<BR>ईर्ष्या and इनि affix. So ईर्ष्यावत् (-वान्-वती-वत्) and ईर्ष्यामय (-यः-यी-यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलि|ईलिः
ईलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>See ईली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलित|ईलितः
ईलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised.<BR>E.<BR>इड to praise, affix क्त, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईली
ईली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A weapon, sometimes considered as a cudgel, and sometimes as a short sword, or a stick shaped like a sword.<BR>E.<BR>ईर to go, &c. क and ङीप् affixes, and र changed to ल; see इली; also ईलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ङ) ईशङ् (ईष्टे)<BR>To possess power, property, or authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Also of the same deity as regent of the north-east quarter.<BR>3 A ruler, a master.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The shaft of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>ईश to rule, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशसखि
ईशसखि<BR>m. (-खा)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>ईश ŚIVA, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशादन्त|ईशादन्तः
ईशादन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 An elephant with large tusks.<BR>2 The tusk of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>ईशा and दन्त a tooth; whose tooth is of the size of a plough-shaft, or the tooth which is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Also of the same as regent of the north-east quarter.<BR>3 One of the Rudras.<BR>4 The sun as a form of ŚIVA.<BR>mf. (-नः-नी)<BR>The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum).<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Light, splendor.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ईश a master, &c. and आनच् affix, and fem. ङीष्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिता
ईशिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Superiority, supremacy, one of the eight attributes of divinity.<BR>E.<BR>ईश a master, and तल् abstract affix; also ईशित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितृ
ईशितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A master, an owner or proprietor.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>ईश to rule, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशित्व|ईशित्वं
ईशित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>See ईशिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The supreme ruler of the universe, GOD; it is therefore applied to all the different divinities, but mostly designates ŚIVA, in mythological and popular acceptation. According to the Sāṃkhyas, Īśvara is the liberated spirit; finite, according to KAPILA; in finite, according to PATAÑJALI. In the Nyāya system, Īśvara is also a finite spirit endowed with attributes. In the Vedānta, Īśvara is infinite and universal spirit, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">Page136</a>] the cause and substance of creation.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA, especially in a compound, when the form of the deity implied is a Liṅga, as, Viśveśvara, Someśvara, Rāmeśvara, &c.<BR>3 KĀMADEVA.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 An owner, a proprietor, a chief or head.<BR>2 Able, competent.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 Of LAKṢMĪ, or of any other of the Śaktis or female energies of the deities.<BR>E.<BR>ईश to rule, and वरट् or वरच् affix, consequently ङीप् or टाप् for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=135" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरभाव|ईश्वरभावः
ईश्वरभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Royal or imperial nature.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वर a sovereign, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरसभ
ईश्वरसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A royal court or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वर and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वराधीन
ईश्वराधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Subject to a king, dependant, on A master or on GOD, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वर, अधि over, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वराधीनता
ईश्वराधीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dependance upon GOD, subjection to a ruler.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वराधीन and तल् added; also with त्व, ईश्वराधीनत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ङ) ईषङ (ईषते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To kill or hurt.<BR>3 To see.<BR>4 To give.<BR>(उ.) ईषु (ईषति)<BR>To glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष|ईषः
ईष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The month Aśvin: see इष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषज्जल
ईषज्जल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Shallow water, a little water.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत्<BR>ind.<BR>A little.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to go, अत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्कर|ईषत्करः
ईषत्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Diminutive, delicate.<BR>2 Doing little.<BR>3 What little is done to or made of.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् a little, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पान
ईषत्पान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>What is little drank or drank little of.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and पान drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्प्रलम्भ
ईषत्प्रलम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>What is little gained of.<BR>E.<BR>इषत् and प्रलम्भ profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदुष्ण|ईषदुष्णं
ईषदुष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Tepid, slightly warm.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्गुण
ईषद्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Of little merit.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पाण्डु|ईषत्पाण्डुः
ईषत्पाण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A pale or light brown colour.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् a little, and पाण्डु pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्पुरुष|ईषत्पुरुषः
ईषत्पुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A mean man.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषदून
ईषदून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Not quite complete or entire.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and ऊन less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्दर्शन
ईषद्दर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A glance at, a slight inspection.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्धास|ईषद्धासः
ईषद्धास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A smile.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् a little, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषद्रक्त|ईषद्रक्तः
ईषद्रक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Of a pale red (colour.)<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and रक्त red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषन्निमय
ईषन्निमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Exchanged for a little.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and निमय barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषल्लभ
ईषल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>What little is or can be gained of.<BR>E.<BR>ईषत् and लभ what gets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The pole or shaft of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to go, affixes क and टाप्; also ईशा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादण्ड|ईषादण्डः
ईषादण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The handle of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>ईषा the staff, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषादन्त|ईषादन्तः
ईषादन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An elephant with a large tusk or tooth.<BR>E.<BR>ईषा and दन्त a tooth: see ईशादन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An elephant's eye-ball: see इषीका.<BR>2 A painter's brush, &c. see ईषीका.<BR>3 A weapon, a dart or arrow.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to hurt, किकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिर|ईषिरः
ईषिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to injure, and किरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A painter's brush, a fibrous stick used as one.<BR>2 An ingot mould.<BR>3 A dipping-rod, or something cast into a crucible to examine if the metal it contains is in fusion: see ईषिका.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to go, ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA.<BR>2 Spring: see इष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह|ईहः
ईह<BR>r. 1st cl. (-ङ) ईहङ् (ईहते)<BR>To endeavour, to aim or attempt.<BR>With सम् prefixed,<BR>to wish, to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहमान
ईहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Performing, undertaking.<BR>E.<BR>ईह to make effort, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>ईह to desire. अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहातस्
ईहातस्<BR>ind.<BR>Diligently, energetically, by or with labour or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>तसि substituted for the regular case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहामृग|ईहामृगः
ईहामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A wolf.<BR>2 A division of the drama.<BR>E.<BR>ईहा wish, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहार्थिन्
ईहार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 Aiming at any object.<BR>2 Seeking wealth.<BR>E.<BR>ईह to seek, अर्थ wealth, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहावृक|ईहावृकः
ईहावृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wolf.<BR>E.<BR>ईहा and वृक a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहित
ईहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sought, attempted, made effort for.<BR>2 Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>ईह to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ<BR>The third short vowel of the Sanskrit alphabet, corresponding to the letter U, and pronounced as that is in the word full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) उङ (उवते)<BR>To sound, to make a particular sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection,<BR>1 of assent;<BR>2 calling;<BR>3 of compassion;<BR>4 anger; and<BR>5 of command.<BR>6 An expletive.<BR>m. (-उः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Of BRAHMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकनाह|उकनाहः
उकनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of a red and yellow, or red and black colour, a bay or chesnut horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकुण|उकुणः
उकुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bug. also उत्कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A sentence.<BR>nf. (-क्तं-क्ता)<BR>A stanza of four lines with one syllabic instant, one long or two short syllables in each.<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Spoken, said.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, affix क्त and व changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तवत्|उक्तवन्त्
उक्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Said, was saying.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, क्तवतु affix of the past part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तवाक्य
उक्तवाक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>One who has borne testimony or given an opinion.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>A dictum, a decree.<BR>E.<BR>उक्त and वाक्य dictum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्ति<BR>f. (क्तिः)<BR>Speech, speaking.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्तोपसंहार|उक्तोपसंहारः
उक्तोपसंहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Any brief or compendious phrase or description.<BR>E.<BR>उक्त what is said, उपसंहार compendiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त्वा
उक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having spoken or said.<BR>E.<BR>वच् to speak, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ|उक्थं|उक्थः
उक्थ<BR>n. (-क्थं)<BR>The second or Sāma Veda.<BR>f. (-क्था)<BR>A kind of metre, a stanza of four lines of one syllable each, the syllable may be one long or two short in quantity.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, and थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष<BR>r. 1st. cl. (उक्षति)<BR>1 To sprinkle or wet.<BR>2 To clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Cleansed, washed.<BR>2 Wet, moist.<BR>E.<BR>उक्ष to wet, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=136" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षतर|उक्षतरः
उक्षतर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large bull or ox.<BR>E.<BR>उक्षन् an ox, and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन्<BR>m. (-क्षा)<BR>An ox or bull.<BR>E.<BR>उक्ष to sprinkle, and कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षाल|उक्षालः
उक्षाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Swift.<BR>2 Excellent.<BR>3 Terrible.<BR>4 High.<BR>5 Much.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
उक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>2 Cleansed, perfumed.<BR>E.<BR>उक्ष to wet, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख|उखः
उख<BR>r. 1st cl. (ओखति) (इ) उखि (उंखति)<BR>1 To go, to move or approach.<BR>2 To dry, to wither.<BR>3 To adorn. The first retains the diphthong with a prefix ending in अ, as प्र and ओखति make प्रोखति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखर्व्वल|उखर्वल|उखर्वलः|उखर्व्वलः
उखर्व्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of grass, a sort of Andropogon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखल|उखलः
उखल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of grass, a sort of Andropogon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखा
उखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A pot or saucepan, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उख to go, क affix, and टाप्, also उघा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्य|उख्यं|उख्यः
उख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Boiled, dressed in a pot, (flesh, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उखा a pot, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Angry, wrathful.<BR>2 Hot, sharp, pungent, acrid.<BR>3 Formidable, terrible.<BR>4 Cruel, fierce, savage.<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of a mixed tribe, from a Kṣatriya father and Śūdra mother: the employment of this caste, according to MANU, is the killing or catching of animals that live in holes, as a snake-catcher, &c.; according to the Tantras, the Ugra is an encomiast or bard.<BR>3 A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera, &c.)<BR>4 A class of asterisms, Maghā, Bharaṇi, Pūrvaphalgunī, Pūrvāṣāḍhā, Pūrvabhadrapada.<BR>5 A name of Malabar.<BR>f. (-ग्रा)<BR>1 Orris root.<BR>2 A medicinal plant.<BR>3 An Ugra woman.<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>Wrath, anger.<BR>E.<BR>उच to accumulate, रन् Uṇādi affix, च is changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रकर्म्मन्|उग्रकर्मन्
उग्रकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Fierce, violent, cruel.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रकाण्ड|उग्रकाण्डः
उग्रकाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A sort of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>उग्र and काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रगन्ध|उग्रगंध|उग्रगन्धं|उग्रगन्धः
उग्रगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Strong smelling.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A plant, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2 Garlic.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 Common carraway, (Carum carui, &c.) see अजमोदा.<BR>2 Orris root.<BR>3 A medicinal plant.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र violent, &c. and गन्ध scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रगन्धिन्
उग्रगन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Strong smelling.<BR>E.<BR>उग्रगन्ध and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रचय|उग्रचयः
उग्रचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Desire.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र fierce, चय a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रत्व|उग्रत्वं
उग्रत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Violence, passionateness.<BR>2 Pungency, acrimony.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र angry, and त्व; also with तल् affix. उग्रता f. (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रदण्ड
उग्रदण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Relentless, remorseless.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रधन्वन्
उग्रधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र fierce, and धन्वन् a bowyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रनासिक|उग्रनासिकः
उग्रनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Large-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र formidable, and नासिका a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रम्पश्य|उग्रंपश्य
उग्रम्पश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>1 Frightful, hideous, fierce looking.<BR>2 Malignant, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र fierce, पश्य looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रशेखरा
उग्रशेखरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of GAṄGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र ŚIVA, and शेखरा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रसेन|उग्रसेनः
उग्रसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The name of a prince, the father of DEVAKĪ and KAṂSA, and king of Mathurā.<BR>2 The name of another prince, the son of PARIKṢIT.<BR>E.<BR>उग्र fierce, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रसेनज|उग्रसेनजः
उग्रसेनज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KAṂSA, the uncle and enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उग्रसेन and ज born; also उग्रमेनतनयः, उग्रसेनपुत्रः, उग्रसेनसुतः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उङ्कुण|उंकुणः|उङ्कुणः
उङ्कुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bug: see उत्कुण.<BR>E.<BR>उ fear, and कुण a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच
उच<BR>r. 4th cl. (उच्यति)<BR>To be conglomerate, to be gathered or assembled together, to unite or associate with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proper, suitable, convenient.<BR>2 Receivable, fit or right to be taken.<BR>3 Known, understood.<BR>4 Intrusted, deposited.<BR>5 Measured, adjusted, accurate.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, and कितच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्च|उच्चं|उच्चः
उच्च<BR>mfn. (-च्चः-च्चा-च्चं)<BR>High, tall.<BR>m. (-च्चः)<BR>The apex of the orbit of a planet.<BR>E.<BR>उत् upwards, चि to gather, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकैस्
उच्चकैस्<BR>ind.<BR>Excessively lofty, tall, loud, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च high, कैस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चघन|उच्चघनं
उच्चघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Laughter in the mind not expressed in the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटा
उच्चटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Habit, usage.<BR>3 A kind of garlic.<BR>4 A species of grass, (a cyperus.)<BR>5 A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>6 A sort of sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and चट to injure, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चण्ड|उच्चंड|उच्चण्डः
उच्चण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Quick, expeditious.<BR>2 Passionate, violent.<BR>E.<BR>उत् implying excess, चडि to be angry, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतम
उच्चतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Highest.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतर
उच्चतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Higher, more lofty.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चतरु|उच्चतरुः
उच्चतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The cocoanut tree.<BR>2 Any lofty tree.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चता
उच्चता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Height; also n. (-त्वं).<BR>E.<BR>तल् or त्व added to उच्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चताल|उच्चतालं|उच्चतालः
उच्चताल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Music and dancing at feasts, drinking parties, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च high sounding, and ताल tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेव|उच्चदेवः
उच्चदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च high, above, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चदेवता
उच्चदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Time personified, Chronos.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च high, and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चन्द्र|उच्चंद्र|उच्चंद्रः|उच्चन्द्रः
उच्चन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The end of the night, the last watch of the night.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. and चन्द्र the moon; moonset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चभाषण
उच्चभाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Speaking loud.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च and भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चमान
उच्चमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>To be said.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चय|उच्चयः
उच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The knot of the string or of the cloth which fastens the lower garments round the loins tied in front.<BR>2 The opposite leg of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, above, चि to gather, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरण|उच्चरणं
उच्चरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Uttering, articulating.<BR>2 Going up or out.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चर to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरित
उच्चरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uttered, articulated.<BR>2 Gone up or out.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चर to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल|उच्चलं
उच्चल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The mind, the understanding.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, and चल what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलन|उच्चलनं
उच्चलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going off or out.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चल to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चललाटा
उच्चललाटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A woman with a high or projecting forehead.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च high, and ललाट a forehead; also उच्चललाटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलित
उच्चलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone up or out.<BR>2 Winnowed.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चल to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटन|उच्चाटनं|उच्चाटनः
उच्चाटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eradicating as a plant.<BR>2 Ruining, (as an individual.)<BR>3 Causing a person's ruin by magical incantations.<BR>E.<BR>उच्च up, and अटन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=137" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार|उच्चारः
उच्चार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Foeces, excrement.<BR>2 Pronunciation, utterance.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, चर to go, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारण|उच्चारणं
उच्चारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Articulating, enunciation.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चर to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणज्ञ|उच्चारणज्ञः
उच्चारणज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A linguist, one skilled in languages or sounds.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चारण and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणस्थान
उच्चारणस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The part of the throat, &c. whence certain sounds, as nasals, gutturals, and the like proceed.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चारण and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणार्थ
उच्चारणार्थ<BR>mfn. (-थ-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Necessary for pronunciation, a superfluous letter, &c. उच्चारण and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारित
उच्चारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pronounced, uttered, articulated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before चर to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य्य|उच्चार्य
उच्चार्य्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having spoken or uttered.<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be spoken, to be pronounced.<BR>E.<BR>उद before चर to go, causal form, affix ल्यप् or यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चार्य्यमाण|उच्चार्यमाण
उच्चार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being uttered or pronounced.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चर, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चावच|उच्चावचः
उच्चावच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>1 Various, multiform.<BR>2 Uneven, irregular, undulating.<BR>3 High and low.<BR>E.<BR>उदक् upper, and अवाक् lower, great and small, &c.; the compound is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिकीर्षा
उच्चिकीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Desire or wish to collect.<BR>E.<BR>उद before चि to collect, desiderative form, अ and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिङ्गट|उच्चिंगटः|उच्चिङ्गटः
उच्चिङ्गट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A sort of cricket.<BR>2 A passionate man.<BR>E.<BR>उत् like, and चिङ्गट a shrimp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूल|उच्चूलः
उच्चूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The flag or pennon of a banner.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, and चूड to be high; ल is substituted for ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःश्रवस्
उच्चैःश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>The horse of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चैस् high, and श्रवस् an ear, long-eared; it is sometimes written with a final vowel, nom. (-सः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैःस्वर|उच्चैःस्वरः
उच्चैःस्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A loud sound or voice.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चैस् and स्वर sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैर्घुष्ट|उच्चैर्घुष्टं
उच्चैर्घुष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Making a loud noise, clamour.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चैस् high, loud, and घुष्ट sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्
उच्चैस्<BR>ind.<BR>High, loud, great, much, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, चि to collect, डैसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तम
उच्चैस्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Very high, tall or lofty.<BR>2 Very loud.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चैस् and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तमाम्
उच्चैस्तमाम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Loudly, aloud.<BR>2 On high, high.<BR>E.<BR>आसु added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तर|उच्चैस्तरं
उच्चैस्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Loftier.<BR>2 Louder.<BR>E.<BR>उच्चैस् and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ|उछ
उच्छ<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (इ.) उच्छि (उञ्छति)<BR>1 To glean.<BR>2 To gather little by little.<BR>(ई.) उच्छी (उच्छति) or usually with वि prefixed, (व्युच्छति)<BR>1 To end or terminate, to leave off.<BR>2 To finish or conclude.<BR>3 To pass or quit.<BR>4 To bind.<BR>With प्र,<BR>to wipe off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छन्न|उच्छन्नं
उच्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Destroyed.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>Peace obtained by ceding valuable lands.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before षद to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलत्|उच्छलन्त्
उच्छलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लंती-लत्)<BR>Going or moving on or against.<BR>E.<BR>उद, शल to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलन|उच्छलनं
उच्छलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going upon.<BR>2 Having over, or above, or against.<BR>E.<BR>उद before शल, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छादन|उच्छादनं
उच्छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning with perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, छद to cover, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छालित
उच्छालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Waved, waved above.<BR>2 Gone, went.<BR>3 Shaken.<BR>E.<BR>उद and शल to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्|उच्छास्त्रवर्तिन्
उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Transgressing, deviating from the ritual.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before शास्त्र scripture, वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिख
उच्छिख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 Flaming, blazing up.<BR>2 Radiant.<BR>3 High crested.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, शिखा a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिङ्घन|उच्छिंघनं
उच्छिङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Breathing through the nostrils, snuffing, snoring.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and शिघि to smell, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिद्य
उच्छिद्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having cut off, destroyed, killed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before छिद to cut, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिन्न|उच्छिन्नः
उच्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Cut, cut off or cut.<BR>2 Destroyed, killed.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिलीन्ध्र|उच्छिलींध्र
उच्छिलीन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and शिलीन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्ट|उच्छिष्टं
उच्छिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Left, rejected as food; (i. e. spit out of the mouth, or orts, crumbs, fragments, &c.)<BR>2 Left, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, शिष to leave as a residue, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टभोजन|उच्छिष्टभोजनः
उच्छिष्टभोजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 One who eats another's leavings.<BR>2 The attendant upon an idol, whose food is the leavings of the deities.<BR>E.<BR>उच्छिष्ट orts, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टभोजिन्
उच्छिष्टभोजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Who eats the remains of a meal.<BR>E.<BR>उच्छिष्ट and भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टमोदन|उच्छिष्टमोदनं
उच्छिष्टमोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Wax.<BR>E.<BR>उच्छिष्ट and मोदन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्टान्न
उच्छिष्टान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Leaving, offal.<BR>E.<BR>उच्छिष्ट and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छीर्षक|उच्छीर्षकं
उच्छीर्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pillow.<BR>E.<BR>उत् upon, and शीर्षक the head: on which rests the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छुष्क
उच्छुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Dry, dried up, withered.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before शुष्क dried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूडा
उच्छूडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>The head of a banner or part above the flag with erect ornaments.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, छूडा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छून|उच्छूनं
उच्छून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Swollen, turgid.<BR>2 Lofty, high.<BR>3 Fat, bulky.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, श्वि to increase, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृङ्खल|उच्छृंखल|उच्छृङ्खलं
उच्छृङ्खल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Unrestrained, perverse, self-willed.<BR>2 Irregular, desultory, unmethodical.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. and शृङ्क्षला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेद|उच्छेदः
उच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Cutting off or out.<BR>2 Destroying, destruction.<BR>3 Cutting short, putting an end to.<BR>4 Excision.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and छिद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेषण|उच्छेषणं
उच्छेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rest, remainder.<BR>2 Leavings.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and शेषण remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोषण
उच्छोषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>What dries up or withers.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Drying up, parching.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रय|उच्छ्रयः
उच्छ्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Height, elevation of a tree, mountain, &c.<BR>2 Rising of a planet, &c.<BR>3 Upright side of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, श्रिञ् to serve, च्यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्राय|उच्छ्रायः
उच्छ्राय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before श्रि to serve, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायिन्
उच्छ्रायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>High raised, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>उच्छ्राय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रित|उच्छ्रितं
उच्छ्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 High, tall.<BR>2 Lifted up, raised.<BR>4 Prosperous, advancing, increasing, rising.<BR>5 Left, abandoned.<BR>6 Increased in size or bulk, grown.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, श्रिञ् to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रिति|उच्छ्रितिः
उच्छ्रिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Height, elevation.<BR>2 The upright side of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before श्रि to serve, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रेय
उच्छ्रेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>High, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before श्रि to serve, यत् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=138" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूसन
उच्छूसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breathing.<BR>2 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before श्वस to breathe, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूसित
उच्छूसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blown, expanded.<BR>2 Breathed, inspired.<BR>3 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, &c. श्वसित breathed, blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूस
उच्छूस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Breath, breathing, inspiration.<BR>2 A sigh.<BR>3 Consolation, encouragement.<BR>4 Division of a book.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and श्वस to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयनी
उज्जयनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Ujjayanī or Oujein, a city so called in Mālava, formerly the capital of VIKRAMĀDITYA. It is one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus, and the first meridian of their geographers: the modern Oujein is about a mile south of the ancient city.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, जयनी victorious or place of victory; from the military character of its people; also अवन्ती and उज्जयिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयन्त|उज्जयन्तः
उज्जयन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The name of a mountain, part of the chain in the west of India, part of the Vindhya range: see रैवत.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. and जयन्ति a banner, or जयन्त the son of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयिनी
उज्जयिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The city Oujein.<BR>E.<BR>see उज्जयनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जासन|उज्जासनं
उज्जासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>उत्। जस to kill, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जिहीर्षा
उज्जिहीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Wishing to take or seize.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before हृ to take, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृम्भ|उज्जृंभ|उज्जृम्भं|उज्जृम्भः
उज्जृम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>1 Blown, expanded.<BR>2 Open, apart.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and जृभि to gape, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृम्भित|उज्जृंभित|उज्जृम्भितं
उज्जृम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blown, expanded.<BR>2 Opened, stretched.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, जृभि to yawn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वल|उज्ज्वलं|उज्ज्वलः
उज्ज्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Luminous, splendid, light.<BR>2 Lovely, beautiful.<BR>3 Clean, clear.<BR>4 Blown, expanded.<BR>5 Burning, blazing.<BR>m. (लः)<BR>Love, passion.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, ज्वल् to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलता
उज्ज्वलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Splendour, radiance.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, उज्ज्वलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलन|उज्ज्वलनं
उज्ज्वलन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Burning or shining.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before ज्वल to shine, affs. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलित
उज्ज्वलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lighted, shining, flaming, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before ज्वल to shine, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छ|उञ्छं|उंछः|उञ्छः
उञ्छ<BR>n. (-ञ्छं)<BR>Gathering grains.<BR>E.<BR>उछि to glean, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छन|उंछनं|उञ्छनं
उञ्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gathering grains of corn in market places, &c. gleaning.<BR>E.<BR>उछि to glean, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छवृत्ति
उञ्छवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>A gleaner, one who lives by gleaning.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्छ and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छशिल|उञ्छशिलं
उञ्छशिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Gleaning corn or grains.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्छ gathering grain, and शिल gleaning corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्छशील|उञ्छशीलः
उञ्छशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>One who lives by leaning, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्छ and शील who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्झ
उञ्झ<BR>r. 6th cl. (उञ्झति)<BR>To quit or abandon. This is some. times read उद्झ्.<BR>With प्र,<BR>to escape or avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्झ
उञ्झ<BR>m. (-ञ्झः)<BR>Abandoning, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्झ and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्झित
उञ्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left, abandoned.<BR>2 Left off, discontinued.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्झ to leave, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उञ्झितृ
उञ्झितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what leaves.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्झ and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उट|उटं|उटः
उट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Leaves, grass, &c. used in making huts, thatches, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उटज|उटजः
उटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A hut made of leaves, the residence of hermits or saints.<BR>2 A house in general.<BR>E.<BR>उट thatch, &c. and ज made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उठ
उठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ओठति)<BR>To strike or knock down; also ऊठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडु|उडुः
उडु<BR>fn. (-डुः-डु)<BR>A lunar mansion or constellation in the moon's path.<BR>n. (-डु)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, डीङ् to go or fly, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुप|उडुपः
उडुप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A raft or float.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>उडु as above, and प from पा to preserve, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुपति|उडुपतिः
उडुपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>उडु and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुपथ|उडुपथः
उडुपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The firmament.<BR>E.<BR>उडु a constellation, and पथ a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुम्बर|उडुंबर|उडुम्बरं|उडुंबरः|उडुम्बरः
उडुम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>2 The threshold of a house.<BR>3 A eunuch.<BR>4 A species of leprosy with coppery spots.<BR>5 A kind of worm, supposed to be generated in the blood, and to produce leprosy.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 A Karṣa, a measure of two Tolas.<BR>E.<BR>उडु a constellation in the second case, वृ to screen, and अप् affix; it is also written उडुम्बर and उटुम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुम्बरपर्णी
उडुम्बरपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>The name of a plant: see दन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>उडुम्बर and पर्ण a leaf: whose leaves are of the color of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडूप|उडूपः
उडूप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The moon: see उडुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डयन|उड्डयनं
उड्डयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flying, soaring.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before डी to fly, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डामर|उड्डामरं
उड्डामर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Excellent, respectable, of rank or consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीन|उड्डीनं
उड्डीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flown up, flying up.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Flying as a bird.<BR>2 Flying up, soaring.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and डी to fly, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीयमान|उड्डीयमानः
उड्डीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flying, soaring, who flies or soars.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, डी to fly, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीश|उड्डीशः
उड्डीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A work so called, containing charms and incantations.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and डी to fly, Uṇādi affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उण्डेरक|उंडेरक|उंडेरकः|उण्डेरकः
उण्डेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ball of flour, a roll, a loaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उण्डेरकस्रज्
उण्डेरकस्रज्<BR>f. (-स्रक्)<BR>A string of rolls, balls of meal or flour upon a string.<BR>E.<BR>उण्डेरक and स्रज a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उढ्र
उढ्र<BR>m. (-ढ्रः)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 The China rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्
उत्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of,<BR>1 asking, (how, what?)<BR>2 of deliberation, (either, or);<BR>3 of extreme doubt, (hey! what!)<BR>4 Up, above. on, upon; see उद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sewn, woven.<BR>E.<BR>ऊय to sew, affix क्त.<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of,<BR>1 doubt, (what!)<BR>2 of interrogation^1, (what, how?)<BR>3 Of connection, (also, and);<BR>4 of deliberation, (either, or.)<BR>5 It is also an expletive.<BR>E.<BR>ऊङ to sound, क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्य|उतथ्यः
उतथ्य<BR>m. (-थ्यः)<BR>The name of a Muni, son of AṄGIRAS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्यानुज|उतथ्यानुजः
उतथ्यानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of the planet Jupiter.<BR>E.<BR>उतथ्य and अनुज younger born; the younger brother of UTATHYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्यानुजन्मन्
उतथ्यानुजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>VṚHASPATI: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उताहो
उताहो<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying,<BR>1 deliberation, (either, or);<BR>2 asking, (how, what?)<BR>E.<BR>उत् and आहो meaning as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उताहोस्वित्
उताहोस्वित्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of doubt or deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क|उत्कः
उत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>1 Regretting, sad, sorrowful.<BR>2 Absent, thinking of something else.<BR>3 Wishing for, desirous of.<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>Opportunity, occasion.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, away, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कट|उत्कटं|उत्कटः
उत्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>2 Drunk, mad, furious.<BR>3 Proud, haughty.<BR>4 Uneven.<BR>5 Difficult.<BR>6 Superior, high.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Intoxication, pride.<BR>2 An elephant in rut.<BR>3 Sara [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">Page140</a>] grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 Woody cassia or its bark.<BR>2 Sarsaparilla.<BR>E.<BR>उत् high, great, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=139" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कटुकासन|उत्कटुकासनं
उत्कटुकासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sitting on the hams, squatting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठा|उत्कंठा
उत्कण्ठा<BR>f. (-ण्ठा)<BR>Regretting, missing any thing or person.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, कठि to be sad, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कण्ठित|उत्कंठित|उत्कण्ठितं
उत्कण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Regretting, wishing or sorrowing for, distressed, sorrowful.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman whose husband or lover is absent.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, कठि to be sad, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कता
उत्कता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A plant with aromatic seeds, (Pothos officinalis, Rox.) see गजपिप्पली.<BR>2 Regretting, sorrowing for.<BR>E.<BR>उत्क regretting, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कन्धरं|उत्कन्धर|उत्कंधर
उत्कन्धरं<BR>ind.<BR>Bending back the neck.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, कन्धर the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर|उत्करः
उत्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 What lifts or raises.<BR>2 What piles or heaps, what makes up.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A heap, a pile, a stack, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and कर what makes, from कृ and ट or अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करिका
उत्करिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of sweetmeat made with milk, treacle, and ghee.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कर and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करीय
उत्करीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a heap, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कर and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्त्तन|उत्कर्तन|उत्कर्तनं
उत्कर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cutting over or on.<BR>2 Cutting to pieces.<BR>3 Cutting off.<BR>E.<BR>उद् कृत to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्ष|उत्कर्षः
उत्कर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>1 Superior, eminent.<BR>2 Much, excessive.<BR>3 Attractive, drawing.<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Excellence, eminence.<BR>2 Excess.<BR>3 Increase.<BR>4 Pulling, pulling up or to.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, कृष to mark, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कल|उत्कलं|उत्कलः
उत्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A porter, one who travels with a burden or load.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A country in the south of India, part of Orissa.<BR>2 A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and कल to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलिका
उत्कलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Regretting, missing any thing or person.<BR>2 A bud, an unblown flower.<BR>3 A wave.<BR>4 Wanton sportfulness, dalliance.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, कल to go, वुन and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलित|उत्कलितः
उत्कलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Regretting, grieving for.<BR>2 Prosperous, rising, increasing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and कल to go or count; part. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्काका
उत्काका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow calving every year.<BR>E.<BR>उत्क regretting, and अक to go, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कार|उत्कारः
उत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Winnowing corn.<BR>2 Piling it up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and कॄ to scatter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारिका
उत्कारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A poultice.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before कृ to make, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कासन|उत्कासनं
उत्कासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hemming, clearing the throat of mucus.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and कासन coughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुञ्चिता|उत्कुंचिता
उत्कुञ्चिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Kalonji, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, कुञ्च to go crookedly, क्त affix, or with वुन् affix उत्कुञ्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्त्तन|उत्कीर्तन|उत्कीर्तनं
उत्कीर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Praising, celebrating.<BR>2 Crying, proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before कीर्त्त to praise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्त्तित|उत्कीर्तित
उत्कीर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Praised, renowned.<BR>2 Proclaimed, promulgated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् aloud, कीर्त्त to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुट|उत्कुटं
उत्कुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Sleeping with the head erect.<BR>E.<BR>उत् neg. and कुट to be crooked, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुण|उत्कुणः
उत्कुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>उत् high, loud, and कुण to call, क affix; also उङ्कुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूट|उत्कूटं|उत्कूटः
उत्कूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An umbrella or parasol.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. कूट to heat, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूलित
उत्कूलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought to the bank or shore.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, कूल a bank, nominative verb, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृति|उत्कृतिः
उत्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Cutting up.<BR>2 A form of metre, a stanza of four lines of twenty-six syllables each.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and कृति another metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृत्य
उत्कृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having cut out, off, or up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before कृत to cut, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृत्यमान
उत्कृत्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being cut to pieces.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before कृत to cut, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्ट|उत्कृष्टं
उत्कृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Excellent, eminent.<BR>2 Superior, best.<BR>3 Much, most, excessive.<BR>4 Drawn, attracted.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before कृष to drag, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टता
उत्कृष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Excellence, superiority, eminence.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कृष्ट with तल् added; also with त्व, उत्कृष्टत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टभूम|उत्कृष्टभूमः
उत्कृष्टभूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A good soil.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कृष्ट excellent, and भूमि earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टवेदन
उत्कृष्टवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The best or most respectable form of marriage.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कृ and वेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोच|उत्कोचः
उत्कोच<BR>mf. (-चः-चा)<BR>A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, कुच to be crooked, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचक|उत्कोचकः
उत्कोचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The receiver of a bribe.<BR>2 A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, कुच् to be crooked, वुन् affix or कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रम|उत्क्रमः
उत्क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going up or out.<BR>2 Progressive increase.<BR>3 Going astray, acting improperly, deviation, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्रम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमण|उत्क्रमणं
उत्क्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going up or out.<BR>2 Surpassing, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्रम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्त|उत्क्रांत
उत्क्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Passed, surpassed, gone over or beyond.<BR>2 Gone forth or out.<BR>3 Trespassing, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्रम to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रान्तिन्|उत्क्रांतिन्
उत्क्रान्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिनी-न्ति)<BR>Passing, passing away, gone, departed.<BR>E.<BR>उत्क्रान्त and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्राम|उत्क्रामः
उत्क्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Opposition, contrariety.<BR>2 Going, going above, surpassing.<BR>3 Going from or out.<BR>4 Deviating from propriety, transgressing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् out, क्रम to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रामत्
उत्क्रामत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>1 Going over or above, surpassing.<BR>2 Going out.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्रम to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्ट
उत्क्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Crying, speaking out or aloud, (who or what does so.)<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Crying out, calling, exclaiming.<BR>2 Conversation.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, क्रुश to cry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोश|उत्क्रोशः
उत्क्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An osprey.<BR>2 Clamour, proclamation.<BR>E.<BR>उन् loud, कुश to cry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेद|उत्क्लेदः
उत्क्लेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Nausea, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and क्लेद moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेश|उत्क्लेशः
उत्क्लेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Nausea, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्लेश distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्त|उत्क्षिप्तः
उत्क्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Thrown upwards, tossed.<BR>2 Thrown out, ejected.<BR>3 Vomited.<BR>4 Rejected, dismissed.<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura metel and fastuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and क्षिप्त thrown; in the last sense it alludes to the intoxicating qualities of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तिका
उत्क्षिप्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An ornament in the shape of a crescent worn in the upper part of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, क्षिप to send, affix क्तिन्; to which कन् and टाप् are then added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेप|उत्क्षेपः
उत्क्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Throwing or tossing up.<BR>2 Throwing away.<BR>3 Sending, dispatching.<BR>4 Bringing up, vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्षिपि to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=140" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपक|उत्क्षेपकः
उत्क्षेपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Throwing, a thrower, what or who elevates or raises.<BR>2 Who sends or orders.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stealer of clothes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before क्षिप to throw, ण्वुस्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपण|उत्क्षेपणं
उत्क्षेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A fan.<BR>2 A kind of basket or bowl used for cleaning corn.<BR>3 Throwing upwards, tossing.<BR>4 Sending, sending away.<BR>5 Vomiting.<BR>6 Taking up.<BR>7 A measure of sixteen Paṇas.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, क्षिप to throw or send, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खला
उत्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, खल to gather, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खात|उत्खातं
उत्खात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR>2 Destroyed, annihilated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, खन to dig, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त|उत्तं
उत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Wet, moistened.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to wet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंस|उत्तंसः
उत्तंस<BR>mn. (-सः)<BR>1 An earring.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, and तसि a Sautra root, to ornament, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्त|उत्तप्तं|उत्तप्तः
उत्तप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Burnt, seared.<BR>2 Bathed, washed.<BR>3 Anxious, excited.<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>Dried flesh.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, or in the last sense priv. and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम|उत्तमः
उत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Chief, principal, first, best.<BR>2 Greatest, highest.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The third Menu, son of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>2 The best kind of lover or hero.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 An excellent woman: one who is handsome, healthy, and affectionate.<BR>2 A plant. (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, तम to desire, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमपुरुष|उत्तमपुरुषः
उत्तमपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The first person, (in grammer.)<BR>2 An excellent man.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमफलिनी
उत्तमफलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Asclepias rosea, Rox.) see टुन्धिका.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम best, फल fruit, इनि affix, and ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्ण|उत्तमर्णः
उत्तमर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>A creditor.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम chief, and ऋण a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्णिक
उत्तमर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A creditor.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम, ऋण a debt, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमर्णिन्
उत्तमर्णिन्<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>A creditor.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम, ऋण a debt, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमलाभ|उत्तमलाभः
उत्तमलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Great profit, a double return.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसंग्रह
उत्तमसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Intriguing with another man's wife, addressing her privately, casting amorous looks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमसाहस|उत्तमसाहसः
उत्तमसाहस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 The highest of the three fixed mulcts or fines; a fine of 1,000 or of 80,000 Paṇas.<BR>2 Capital punishment, branding, banishment, confiscation, mutilation and death.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम the best or greatest, साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाङ्ग|उत्तमांग|उत्तमाङ्गं
उत्तमाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम chief, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमार्द्ध्य
उत्तमार्द्ध्य<BR>n. (-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>The best half.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम, अर्द्ध half, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाह|उत्तमाहः
उत्तमाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A fine day, a lucky day.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम best, अहन a day, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमोपपद
उत्तमोपपद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Best, good.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम and उपपद secondary term, to whom or what the best term is applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमौजस्
उत्तमौजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A proper name, one of the warriors of the Mahābhārata.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्भन|उत्तंभन|उत्तंभनं
उत्तम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Upholding, supporting, staying.<BR>2 Stopping, arresting.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before ष्टभि to stop, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्भित
उत्तम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Upheld, supported.<BR>2 Stopped, arrested.<BR>3 Erect, (as the hair of the head,) standing on end.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before ष्टभि to stop, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
उत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Superior, high, lofty.<BR>2 Northern.<BR>3 Best, excellent.<BR>4 (In composition) Fit, appertaining to.<BR>5 Subsequent, posterior.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 An answer, a reply.<BR>2 (In law) A defence, a rejoinder.<BR>3 A consequence, a result.<BR>4 Remainder, difference, (in arithmetic.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of VIRĀṬA.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The wife of ABHIMANYU, the son of ARJUNA.<BR>2 The north.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, and तर from तृ to pass, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकाल|उत्तरकालः
उत्तरकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Future time.<BR>2 Time reckoned from full moon to full moon.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकुरु|उत्तरकुरुः
उत्तरकुरु<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>Uttarakuru, the country about the north pole.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर northern, and कुरु the northern part of the globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरकोशला
उत्तरकोशला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The city Ayodhyā, the modern Oude.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर north, कोशला a district so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरक्रिया
उत्तरक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Obsequial ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर last, क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंग|उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्गं
उत्तरङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Flooded, inundated, washed under by waves.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A wooden arch surmounting the door frame.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर above, ग what goes, affix खश्; or उत् and तरङ्ग a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज
उत्तरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born subsequently or afterwards, posterity.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरज्या
उत्तरज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>The versed sine of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and ज्या an arc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरण|उत्तरणं
उत्तरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Crossing, rivers, &c.<BR>2 Coming forth or out of, (especially water,) landing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् over, तरण passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्
उत्तरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Crossing, going over.<BR>2 Coming out of (water.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तृ to cross, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतस्
उत्तरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Northward.<BR>2 Afterwards.<BR>3 Behind.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and अतसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्र
उत्तरत्र<BR>ind.<BR>1 After, subsequent.<BR>2 Northward.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदायक
उत्तरदायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Replying, answering.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and दायक a giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरदिश्
उत्तरदिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्)<BR>The north quarter.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and दिश् region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरधेय
उत्तरधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be done subsequently.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर afterwards, धि to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपक्ष|उत्तरपक्षः
उत्तरपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A demonstrated truth, a direct conclusion.<BR>2 Course of argument, according to established truths.<BR>3 Second part of an argument, reply, refutation.<BR>4 The minor proposition in a syllogism.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, and पक्ष subject of an inference; also adding. क, उत्तरपक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपक्षता
उत्तरपक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Conclusion, demonstration.<BR>2 Replication, reply.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, उत्तरपक्षत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपद
उत्तरपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The last member of a compound word.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and पद word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपदिक
उत्तरपदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the last word or term.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तरपद and ठक् affix; also with छ added उत्तरपदकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपाद|उत्तरपादः
उत्तरपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A division of legal practice, that part which relates to the reply or defence.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर a reply, and पाद a quarter; four divisions being admitted in every suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरपुरुष|उत्तरपुरुषः
उत्तरपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>(In grammar,) The third person.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर last, and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरप्रच्छद|उत्तरप्रच्छदः
उत्तरप्रच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A coverlid, a quilt.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and प्रच्छद what covers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरफाल्गुनी
उत्तरफाल्गुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The twelfth lunar mansion containing two stars, figured by a bed.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, and फाल्गुनी or फल्गुनी an asterism; hence it also occurs उत्तरफल्गुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=141" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरभाद्रपद्
उत्तरभाद्रपद्<BR>f. (-द्)<BR>The twenty-seventh lunar mansion, figured by a couch, and comprehending two stars, of which one is α Andromedae.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, and भाद्रपद properly the constellation; also with a final vowel, उत्तरभाद्रपद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरमात्र
उत्तरमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Any reply, some reply.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तररहित
उत्तररहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unable to reply, having no answer.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and रहित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरलक्षण
उत्तरलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The indication of an actual reply.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवस्ति
उत्तरवस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>A small syringe, a urethra injection pipe.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर best, वस्ति syringe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरवादिन्
उत्तरवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A defendant, a replicant. उत्तर a reply, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसंज्ञित
उत्तरसंज्ञित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Designated in the reply, (a witness, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and संज्ञित named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाक्षिन्
उत्तरसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>Witness for the defence.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर reply, and साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरसाधक|उत्तरसाधकः
उत्तरसाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Befriending, assisting, a help, a friend.<BR>2 Who or what establishes a reply.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and साधक what accomplishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरा
उत्तरा<BR>ind.<BR>North, northerly, northward.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and आच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्
उत्तरात्<BR>ind.<BR>Northward.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधर
उत्तराधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Superior and inferior, higher and lower.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर upper, अधर lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकार|उत्तराधिकारः
उत्तराधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Right to property, &c. in succession to another person, heirship, inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and अधिकार right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकारिन्
उत्तराधिकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>An heir, a claimant, subsequent to the death, &c. of the original owner.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तराधिकार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराधिकारिता
उत्तराधिकारिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Right of succession.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to उत्तराधिकारिन्; also with त्व, उत्तराधिकारित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरापथ
उत्तरापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The north, a northern road or direction.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and पथिन् a road, the final of उत्तर lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराभास|उत्तराभासः
उत्तराभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A false, indirect, or prevaricating reply, (in law.)<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर a defence, and आभास what resembles: apparently a defence, but not so in fact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराभासता
उत्तराभासता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Inadequacy of a reply, the semblance without the reality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, उत्तराभासत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरायण|उत्तरायणं
उत्तरायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The period of the sun's progress to the north of the equator, the summer solstice.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर the north, and अयन going, progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशा
उत्तराशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The north.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and आशा region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशाढा
उत्तराशाढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>One of the lunar mansions, see उत्तराषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराशापति|उत्तराशापतिः
उत्तराशापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर, आशा a quarter, and पति a master; regent of the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराषाढा
उत्तराषाढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>The twenty-first of the lunar mansions, figured by an elephant's tooth or a bed, and containing two stars, one of which is β in Sagittarius.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, and आषाढा the constellation; to distinguish it from asterism twentieth: see पूर्व्वाषाढा and आषाढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरासङ्ग|उत्तरासंग|उत्तरासङ्गः
उत्तरासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>An upper and outer garment.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर upper, आङ् prefixed to षञ्ज to surround, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहि
उत्तराहि<BR>ind.<BR>Northerly, from the north, implying distance.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर and आहिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीय|उत्तरीयं
उत्तरीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An upper or outer garment.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर upper, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेण
उत्तरेण<BR>ind.<BR>Northward, posterior, subsequent.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर with एनप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेद्युस्
उत्तरेद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>A subsequent day, a day following to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर subsequent, and एद्यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरोत्तर
उत्तरोत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>More and more, further and further. &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A rejoinder, a reply to an answer.<BR>2 Excess, exceeding quantity or degree.<BR>3 Succession, gradation, descending.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Shallow.<BR>2 Sleeping supinely or with the face upwards.<BR>3 Upright.<BR>4 Concave.<BR>E.<BR>उत् upwards, तन to stretch, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानक|उत्तानकः
उत्तानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of grass, (a cyperus): see उच्चटा.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, तन to spread, वुज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपाद|उत्तानपादः
उत्तानपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A prince, son of SVAYAMBHU the Manu.<BR>2 One of the stars of the little bear, (β Ursi minoris.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानपादज|उत्तानपादजः
उत्तानपादज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of DHRUVA.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तानपाद, ज born: the son of UTTĀNAPĀDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानशय|उत्तानशयः
उत्तानशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>One who sleeps with the face upwards.<BR>mf. (-यः-या)<BR>An infant.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तान and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताप|उत्तापः
उत्ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Great heat.<BR>2 Affliction, distress.<BR>3 Anxiety, excitement.<BR>4 Effort, energy.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तप to be hot, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापित
उत्तापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heated, made hot.<BR>2 Pained, distressed.<BR>3 Roused, excited.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तप to be hot, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार|उत्तारः
उत्तार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>2 Passing away, instability.<BR>3 Ejecting, getting rid. of.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, and तार who passes, from तृ and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारिन्
उत्तारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Unsteady, changing, shaking.<BR>2 Sick.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, तृ to go, णिनि affix; or उत्तार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार्य्य|उत्तार्य
उत्तार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be ejected, to be thrown up by vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, तृ to pass, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताल|उत्तालः
उत्ताल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Best, excellent.<BR>2 Arduous, difficult.<BR>3 Formidable.<BR>4 Swift, speedy.<BR>5 Lofty, tall.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An ape.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तल् to fix, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तिष्ठामान
उत्तिष्ठामान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Getting up, rising.<BR>2 Increasing, augmenting.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before स्था to stay शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीरम्
उत्तीरम्<BR>ind.<BR>On the bank, ashore.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीर्ण|उत्तीर्णं|उत्तीर्ण्ण
उत्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Crossed, traversed.<BR>2 Loosed, liberated.<BR>3 Thrown off.<BR>E.<BR>उत् over, तीर्ण crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुङ्ग|उत्तुंग|उत्तुङ्गः
उत्तुङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>High, lofty, tall.<BR>E.<BR>उत् very, and तुङ्ग high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुङ्गता
उत्तुङ्गता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, or with त्व, उत्तुङ्गत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुण्डित|उत्तुंडितं
उत्तुण्डित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The head of a thorn, &c. which has entered the skin.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तुडि to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुष|उत्तुषः
उत्तुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Fried grain.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. and तुष husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजन|उत्तेजनं
उत्तेजन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Sending, dispatching.<BR>2 urging, driving.<BR>3 Whetting, sharpening, polishing.<BR>4 Exciting, animating.<BR>5 An inspiring or exciting speech.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and तेजन giving light or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजित|उत्तेजितं
उत्तेजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, dispatched.<BR>2 Animated, excited.<BR>3 Whetted, sharpened, polished.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Moving in the longe, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">Page143</a>] sidling, one of a horse's five paces.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, निज to sharpen, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=142" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेरित|उत्तेरितं
उत्तेरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A horse's walk, one of his five paces in Hindu jockeyship.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, तृ to pass, क्त irr. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलन|उत्तोलनं
उत्तोलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Lifting up, raising, elevating.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and तोलन weighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलित
उत्तोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Raised, lifted up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before तुल to be equal, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यक्त|उत्त्यक्तः
उत्त्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Abandoned, left.<BR>2 Thrown, tossed.<BR>3 Free from passion or affection.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and उत्त्यक्त abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्याग|उत्त्यागः
उत्त्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Abandonment, quitting.<BR>2 Throwing, throwing, up.<BR>3 Secession from worldly feelings.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and त्याग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रास
उत्त्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, and त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थ|उत्थः
उत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>Standing or being up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and स्था to stay, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थान|उत्थानं
उत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Effort, exertion.<BR>2 Manhood, manly exertion.<BR>3 An army.<BR>4 War, battle.<BR>5 A book.<BR>6 Joy, pleasure.<BR>7 Rising, getting up.<BR>8 A court yard.<BR>9 A shed where sacrifices are made.<BR>10 A term, a limit.<BR>11 Evacuating by stool, &c.<BR>12 Business of a family or realm, as the care of subjects or dependants.<BR>13 Reflexion.<BR>14 Proximate cause of disease.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, स्था to stand, and ल्युट् affix, स is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थानैकादशी
उत्थानैकादशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The eleventh lunation of the light half of Kārttika or Agrahāyaṇa, when VIṢṆU rises from his sleep.<BR>E.<BR>उत्थान rising, एकादशी eleventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापक|उत्थापकः
उत्थापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Lifting, causing to get up, who or what raises, &c.<BR>2 Exciting, animating.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before स्था to stay, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापन|उत्थापनं
उत्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Raising, elevating.<BR>2 Causing to rise or get up.<BR>3 Exciting, instigating.<BR>4 (In arithmetic) Substitution of a value.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and स्था causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापित
उत्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, lifted up, elevated.<BR>2 Made to get up, aroused from a seat, a bed, &c.<BR>3 Instigated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and स्था causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाप्य
उत्थाप्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having raised or caused to rise.<BR>2 Having roused or instigated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before स्था to stay, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाय
उत्थाय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having risen (from a seat, &c.)<BR>2 Having risen (in rank, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् before स्था to stand, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थित|उत्थितं
उत्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Endeavouring, striving.<BR>3 Happened, occurring.<BR>4 Increasing, advancing, rising.<BR>5 High, risen or rising as from a seat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, स्था to stay, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थिताङ्गुलि|उत्थितांगुलि|उत्थिताङ्गुलिः
उत्थिताङ्गुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>E.<BR>उत्थित increased, and अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थिति|उत्थितिः
उत्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Elevation, rising up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत|उत्पतः
उत्पत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 Going upwards, or up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and पत who goes, from पत to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतन|उत्पतनं
उत्पतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, पत to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतितृ
उत्पतितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Jumping up, rising, going upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पत to rise, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतित
उत्पतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Risen, ascended.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, पत to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतिष्णु|उत्पतिष्णुः
उत्पतिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Rising, jumping up.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पत and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्ति|उत्पत्तिः
उत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Producing as an effect or result, giving rise to or generating as a consequence.<BR>3 Production in general.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, पत to go, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिप्रयोग|उत्पत्तिप्रयोगः
उत्पत्तिप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Purport, meaning.<BR>2 Production by the joint operation of cause and effect.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पत्ति and प्रयोग act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जक|उत्पत्तिव्यंजक|उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जकः
उत्पत्तिव्यञ्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A type of birth, (as investiture.)<BR>E.<BR>उत्पत्ति and व्यञ्जक figurative indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथ|उत्पथः
उत्पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Error, bad way, evil.<BR>E.<BR>उत् from, पथ for पषिन a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथम्
उत्पथम्<BR>ind.<BR>Astray, on the wrong road.<BR>E.<BR>उत् from, पथिन a path, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्न|उत्पन्नः
उत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Known, ascertained.<BR>3 Risen, gone up.<BR>4 Acquired, gained.<BR>5 Effected, accomplished.<BR>6 Occurred, happened.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, पद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्नतन्तु
उत्पन्नतन्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>Having progeny.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पन्न and तन्तु line; descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पल|उत्पलं|उत्पलः
उत्पल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Thin.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A blue lotus, (Nymphaea caerulea.)<BR>2 A plant, (a Costus): see कुष्ठ.<BR>3 A water lily in general.<BR>4 A flower in general.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A kind of cake made with unwinnowed corn.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, पल to go or grow, अच् affix, and fem. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलगन्धिक|उत्पलगन्धिकं
उत्पलगन्धिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A species of sandal of the colour of brass, and very fragrant.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल the lotus, गन्ध a smell, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलचक्षुस्
उत्पलचक्षुस्<BR>mfn. (-क्षूः-क्षूः-क्षूः)<BR>Lotus-eyed, fine-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलपत्र|उत्पलपत्रं
उत्पलपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The leaf of the lotus.<BR>2 The impression of a female nail.<BR>3 The Tilaka or mark on the forehead, made with sandal, &c. by the Hindus.<BR>4 A broad bladed knife or lancet.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल a lotus, and पत्र a leaf; similarly shaped, &c. also कन् added उत्पलपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलशारिवा
उत्पलशारिवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल a flower, शारिवा irregular deriv. of शृ to harm: whose flower injures or destroys, (disease.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलाभ
उत्पलाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Lotus-like, resembling a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल and आङ् before भा to shine, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलिनी
उत्पलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पल a lotus, इनि affix, and ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवन|उत्पवनं
उत्पवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Straining liquids before using for domestic or religious purposes.<BR>2 Sprinkling ghee or other fluids on the sacrificial fire, with two blades of Kusa grass, the ends of which are held in either hand, and the centre dipped into the liquid, which is then dropped upon the fire.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, &c. पुङ् to purify, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पश्य|उत्पश्यः
उत्पश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Looking up or upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and ग्रश्य looking, irr. formative, from दृश to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाट|उत्पाटः
उत्पाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Pulling up by the roots.<BR>2 Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, पट to go, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटन|उत्पाटनं
उत्पाटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eradicating, pulling up by the roots.<BR>2 Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पट to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=143" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटित|उत्पाटितं
उत्पाटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, or out, पट to go, in the causal form, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिन्
उत्पाटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>Eradicating, extirpating.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पाट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पात|उत्पातः
उत्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A portent, some natural prodigy or phoenomenon.<BR>2 Any public calamity, as an eclipse, a meteor, an earthquake, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् accidentally, पत to happen, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातवात|उत्पातवातः
उत्पातवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पात a portent, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादक|उत्पादकः
उत्पादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A producer, a generator.<BR>2 What gives origin or production to, causative.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fabulous animal with eight legs: written also उत्यातकः.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Origin, cause.<BR>f. (-दिका)<BR>1 A white ant, (termes.)<BR>2 A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR>3 Also, Basella (rubra or lucida).<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, पद a foot, or पद to go, in the causal, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादन|उत्पादनं
उत्पादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Producing, generating, begetting.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पद to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादशयन|उत्पादशयनः
उत्पादशयन<BR>mfn. (-नः)<BR>The Francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>उत् upon, पाद a foot, शयन sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादित
उत्पादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Produced, effected.<BR>2 Generated, begotten.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पद to go, causal form क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाद्य
उत्पाद्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having begotten.<BR>2 Having produced, having inspired.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पद to go, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाली
उत्पाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Health.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before, पल to preserve, अञ् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाव|उत्पावः
उत्पाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Purifying ghee, &c. see उत्पवन.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पू to make pure, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जर|उत्पिंजर
उत्पिञ्जर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Uncaged, unconfined.<BR>E.<BR>उत् out of, पिञ्चर a cage; also उत्पिञ्जल, ल being substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिञ्जल|उत्पिंजल|उत्पिञ्जलः
उत्पिञ्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Confounded, confused.<BR>2 Uncaged.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पित्सु
उत्पित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Desirous of going, going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before पत to go, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्ट
उत्पिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ground, rubbed.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A disease, a grating of the bones of the joints upon each other.<BR>E.<BR>उत and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड|उत्पीडः
उत्पीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>Froth.<BR>E.<BR>उत् on, पीड to go, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासन|उत्प्रासनं
उत्प्रासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Ridicule, derision.<BR>2 Hurling, throwing afar.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and प्र before अस to throw, affix ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षा
उत्प्रेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Indifference, carelessness.<BR>2 Ironical comparison.<BR>3 Comparison in general, poetical or rhetorical.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and प्र prefixed to ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवन|उत्प्लवनं
उत्प्लवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Taking up oil or ghee when it has been defiled in any way, by dipping a blade of Kusa grass into it, and dropping it from them upon the fire.<BR>2 Jumping, springing upon.<BR>E.<BR>उत् over, प्लवन jumping, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवा
उत्प्लवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>उत् over, प्लु to go, अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुत
उत्प्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Jumped upon, approached suddenly.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लुव्य
उत्प्लुव्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sprung or jumped upon.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before प्लु to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल|उत्फलं
उत्फल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Excellent fruit.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फाल|उत्फालः
उत्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A jump, a leap.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and स्फुल to move, affix घञ् the vowel and final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्ल|उत्फुल्लः
उत्फुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>1 Blown, as a flower.<BR>2 Swollen, encreased in bulk.<BR>3 Sleeping supinely.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and फुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स|उत्सः
उत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>A fountain, a spring.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to wet, and स Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्ग|उत्संग|उत्संगः|उत्सङ्गः
उत्सङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The haunch or part above the hip.<BR>2 The acclivity or slope of a hill.<BR>3 Association, union.<BR>4 Embrace.<BR>5 The bottom or deep part of an ulcer.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, षञ्ज to embrace, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गित|उत्संगित
उत्सङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Associated, combined, joined.<BR>E.<BR>उत् षञ्ज before to be joined with, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सङ्गिन्|उत्संगिन्
उत्सङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>Associating or combining with, an associate, a partner.<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>An ulcer, a deep sore.<BR>f. (-ङ्गिनी)<BR>Pimples on the inner edge of the eyelids.<BR>E.<BR>उत्युङ्ग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्न
उत्सन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Destroyed. overturned.<BR>2 Decayed, in ruins.<BR>3 Risen, increased.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before षद to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्ग|उत्सर्गः
उत्सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>2 Resigning, retiring from.<BR>3 Giving, donation.<BR>4 Any precept or rule.<BR>5 Presentation of any thing promised to a god or Brahman, with suitable ceremonies.<BR>6 A particular ceremony preparatory to a course of the Vedas.<BR>7 Dejection, excretion, voiding by stool, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृज to quit, to leave, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्जन|उत्सर्जनं
उत्सर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Abandoning, leaving, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृज to leave, and ल्युट् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिणी
उत्सर्पिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A Jaina division of time, a long period described as 10 crores of crores of oceans of years; this period alternates with one of similar duration: see अवसर्पिणी.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, सृप to go, णिनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्प|उत्सर्प|उत्सर्पः
उत्सर्प्प<BR>m. (-र्प्पः)<BR>1 Going or gliding upwards.<BR>2 Swelling, heaving.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृप to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्पण|उत्सर्पण|उत्सर्पणं
उत्सर्प्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Gliding upward.<BR>2 Swelling, heaving.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृप to go gently, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्पित|उत्सर्पित
उत्सर्प्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heaving, heaved, undulating.<BR>2 Gliding or going upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृप to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्प्पिन्|उत्सर्पिन्
उत्सर्प्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्प्पी-र्प्पिणी-र्प्पि)<BR>1 What glides upwards.<BR>2 Rising gently, heaving, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सर्प्प and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्य्या|उत्सर्या
उत्सर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A cow fit to take the bull.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, सृ to go, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सव|उत्सवः
उत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A festival, a jubilee.<BR>2 Height, elevation.<BR>3 Impatience.<BR>4 Wish.<BR>5 Passion, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, षू to bear, to bring forth, affix अच्; happiness, &c. is produced by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादन|उत्सादनं
उत्सादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going up, ascending, rising.<BR>2 Raising, elevating.<BR>3 Destroying, overturning.<BR>4 Cleaning the person with perfumes.<BR>5 Rubbing or chafing the limbs.<BR>6 Ploughing a field twice or thoroughly.<BR>7 Healing a sore, causing it to fill up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, षद to destroy, in the causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीय
उत्सादनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be gone up or ascended.<BR>2 To be effected.<BR>3 To be destroyed.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Any application to a sore producing granulations.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before षद to go, causal form, affix अनीयर्; also उत्सादितव्य and उत्साद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादित|उत्सादितं
उत्सादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Risen, ascended.<BR>2 Raised, elevated.<BR>3 Destroyed.<BR>4 Cleansed, purified with oil, perfumes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>as above, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारक|उत्सारकः
उत्सारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>2 A guard, a guardian.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, सृ to go, in the causal, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=144" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारण|उत्सारणं
उत्सारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Removing, keeping at a distance.<BR>2 Moving, causing to move.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, सृ to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साह|उत्साहः
उत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Effort, perseverance, strenuous and continued exertion.<BR>2 A thread.<BR>3 Happiness.<BR>4 Firmness, fortitude.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, सह to bear, to be able, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवत्|उत्साहवन्त्
उत्साहवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Active, energetic, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>उत्साह and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहवर्द्धन
उत्साहवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Heroism.<BR>E.<BR>उत्साह exertion, and वर्द्धन increasing, from वृध and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहसम्पन्न|उत्साहसंपन्न
उत्साहसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Active, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>उत्साह and सम्पन्न effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहिन्
उत्साहिन्<BR>mf. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Active, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>उत्साह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिक्त|उत्सिक्तः
उत्सिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Haughty, proud, rude.<BR>2 Elevated, raised.<BR>3 Enlarged, increased.<BR>4 Sprinkled.<BR>5 Disordered, disturbed (in mind, &c.)<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A king's wrestler.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, षिच to sprinkle, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्यमान|उत्सिच्यमानः
उत्सिच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Augmenting, growing.<BR>2 Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, षिच to sprinkle, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुक|उत्सुकः
उत्सुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Zealously active, making exertions for a gratifying object.<BR>2 Regretting, missing, sorrowing for.<BR>3 Fond of, attached to.<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, सु to produce, क्विप् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकता
उत्सुकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sorrow, regret.<BR>2 Attachment, affection.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सुक and तल् affix; also with त्व, affix उत्सुकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूत्र
उत्सूत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>1 Loose, detached, unstrung.<BR>2 Irregular, out of rule.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सूत्र a thread, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूर|उत्सूरः
उत्सूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Evening, twilight.<BR>E.<BR>उत् priv. सूर the sun; sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्य
उत्सृज्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having quitted.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before सृज to leave, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्ट|उत्सृष्टः
उत्सृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Left, abandoned.<BR>2 Given, presented.<BR>3 Cast into or upon.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and सृज to leave, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टपशु
उत्सृष्टपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A bull set at liberty upon particular occasions, as a marriage, &c. and allowed to go about at will.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सृष्ट loosed, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेक|उत्सेकः
उत्सेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Increase, enlargement.<BR>2 Pride, haughtiness.<BR>3 Casting water, &c. on any thing, sprinkling.<BR>4 Flying out or up, foaming or spouting over, showering.<BR>E.<BR>उत् on, षिच् to sprinkle, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेचन|उत्सेचनं
उत्सेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Showering or spouting upwards.<BR>2 Boiling or foaming over.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and सेचन sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेध|उत्सेधः
उत्सेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Height, elevation.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 Fatness, obesity.<BR>4 Intumescence.<BR>5 Thickness.<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, षिध to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मय|उत्स्मयः
उत्स्मय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A smile.<BR>E.<BR>उत् and स्मय a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् or उत्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix to words implying,<BR>1 Superiority in degree; (over, above.)<BR>2 In place, (Over, above, on, upon.)<BR>3 Pride;<BR>4 Publicity;<BR>5 Power;<BR>6 Separation, disjunction, (off, from, out of);<BR>7 Emancipation;<BR>8 Binding;<BR>9 Helplessness, weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद|उदं
उद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to wet, deriv. irr.: see उदक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्
उदक्<BR>ind.<BR>Northern, upper, subsequent: see उदच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक|उदकं
उदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to wet, deriv. irr.; this is sometimes considered as two words, उद and क, each having the same meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकक्रिया
उदकक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Presentation of water to ancestors as far as the fourteenth degree.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and क्रिया rite; so उदकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकद|उदकदः
उदकद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>A giver of water, yielding water, offering water to the manes, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An heir, a near kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and द who gives; also उदकदातृ and उदकदायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकदान
उदकदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift of water, especially to the manes, as a religious or obsequial rite.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकदायिन्
उदकदायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Giving water.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>An heir or kinsman, one who presents libations of water.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and दायिन् who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकपूर्व्वकम्|उदकपूर्वकम्
उदकपूर्व्वकम्<BR>ind.<BR>Pouring water on the hand as preparatory to or confirmatory of a gift or promise.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and पूर्व्वक prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकप्रतीकाश
उदकप्रतीकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Watery, fluid like water.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and प्रतीकाश what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकमेह|उदकमेहः
उदकमेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A variety of Diabetes, passing watery urine.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and मेह urining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकशाक
उदकशाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Any aquatic herb.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकस्पर्श|उदकस्पर्शः
उदकस्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Touching different parts of the body with water.<BR>2 Touching water in confirmation of a promise, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and स्पर्श touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकाधार|उदकाधारः
उदकाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A reservoir, a cistern, a well, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकार्थिन्
उदकार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Thirsty, desirous of water.<BR>E.<BR>उदक and अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकीर्य्य|उदकीर्य|उदकीर्यः|उदकीर्य्यः
उदकीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A plant, (Galedupa arborea, &c.) see करञ्जक.<BR>E.<BR>उद water, and कॄ to scatter, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकुम्भ|उदकुंभ|उदकुम्भः
उदकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A water jar.<BR>E.<BR>उद and कुम्भ a jar; also उदककुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकोदञ्जन|उदकोदंजन|उदकोदञ्जनः
उदकोदञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A water jar.<BR>E.<BR>उकक and उदञ्चन what goes up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकोदर
उदकोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Dropsy.<BR>E.<BR>उदक् and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्त
उदक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Gone up, risen, ascended.<BR>E.<BR>उद before अञ्च to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्या
उदक्या<BR>f. (-क्या)<BR>A woman in her courses.<BR>E.<BR>उदक water, and यत् affix of fitness: requiring water for purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदगद्रि|उदगद्रिः
उदगद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The Himālaya mountains on the north of Hindustan.<BR>E.<BR>उदक north, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदगयन|उदगयनं
उदगयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The sun's progress north of the equator: see उत्तरायण.<BR>E.<BR>उदक् north, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्भूम|उदग्भूमः
उदग्भूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Good soil.<BR>E.<BR>उदक् north, भूमि earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्भूमि|उदग्भूमिः
उदग्भूमि<BR>m. (मिः)<BR>Fertile soil: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्र|उदग्रं
उदग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 High, tall.<BR>2 Large, vast.<BR>3 Projecting.<BR>4 Pointing upwards.<BR>5 Fierce, intense.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, and अग्र end, point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्रदत्|उदग्रदन्त्
उदग्रदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Large toothed.<BR>m. (-दन्)<BR>An elephant with a large tusk.<BR>E.<BR>उदग्र large, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदङ्मुख
उदङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खा-खं)<BR>Facing the north.<BR>E.<BR>उदच् and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदच्
उदच् or उदञ्च्<BR>mfn. (उदङ् उदीची उदक्)<BR>1 North, northern.<BR>2 Upper, upwards.<BR>3 Subsequent, posterior.<BR>f. (-दीची)<BR>The north.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, अञ्च to go, affix क्विप्; the neuter is used as a particle: see उदक्; the noun is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदज|उदजः
उदज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatic, watery, produced in or by water.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Driving cattle.<BR>E.<BR>उद water, and ज born, or उद् up, and अज to go, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=145" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चन|उदंचन|उदंचनं|उदञ्चनं
उदञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A lid or cover.<BR>2 Directing or throwing upwards.<BR>3 Rising, ascending.<BR>E.<BR>उद above, अञ्च to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदञ्चित|उदञ्चितं
उदञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thrown up, tossed.<BR>2 Worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, अञ्च to go or worship, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदण्डपाल|उदंडपाल|उदंडपालः|उदण्डपालः
उदण्डपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of fish.<BR>2 A sort of snake.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, अण्ड an egg, and पाल what nourishes; laying many eggs at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधि|उदधिः
उदधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A water jar.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>उद् water, and धि having, from धा, with कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिक्रम्
उदधिक्रम्<BR>m. (-क्राः)<BR>A voyager, a mariner.<BR>E.<BR>उदधि, क्रम to go, विट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिमल|उदधिमलः
उदधिमल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>उदधि and मल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिमेखला
उदधिमेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>उदधि and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिसुता
उदधिसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 Dvārakā, the capital of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उदधि the ocean, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्त|उदंत|उदन्तः
उदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A pure and virtuous man.<BR>2 Tidings, intelligence.<BR>3 One who gets a livelihood by a trade, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् disjunctive, and अन्त end, term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तक|उदंतक|उदंतकः|उदन्तकः
उदन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>News, tidings, intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्तिका|उदंतिका
उदन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Satisfaction, satiety.<BR>E.<BR>उद् complete, अन्त end, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्या
उदन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>Thirst.<BR>E.<BR>उदक् water, क्यच् affix, the final क is changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्वत्|उदन्वन्त्
उदन्वत्<BR>m. (-न्वान्)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>उद् water, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपात्र
उदपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A water cup, a ewer.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपान|उदपानं|उदपानः
उदपान<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 A well.<BR>E.<BR>उद् water, पा to drink, and ल्युट् affix; the place where water is drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदपेष
उदपेष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A paste, any thing ground with water.<BR>E.<BR>उद and पेष grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदभार|उदभारः
उदभार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A water carrier.<BR>E.<BR>उद and भार a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदमन्थ|उदमन्थः
उदमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>Barley water.<BR>E.<BR>उद and मन्थ scum; also, उदकमन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदमेघ|उदमेघः
उदमेघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A watery cloud.<BR>E.<BR>उद and मेघ a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The rising of the sun and planets in general.<BR>2 The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR>3 Rising, ascending.<BR>4 Light, splendor.<BR>5 Prosperity, good fortune.<BR>6 Creation, the rising of the world.<BR>7 (In law) Income.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, इण to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयन|उदयनं|उदयनः
उदयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rising, ascending.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of AGASTYA: see अगस्त्य.<BR>2 The name of a sovereign, king of Kauśāmbī, and hero of the Vāsavadattā, a dramatic poem; also, of part of the Vṛhat Kathā.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, इण to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयपर्व्वत|उदयपर्वत|उदयपर्वतः
उदयपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The eastern mountain behind which the sun rises.<BR>E.<BR>उदप and पर्ब्वत a mountain; also similar compounds, as उदयगिरिः, उदयशैलः, उदयाचलः, उदयाद्रिः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयिन्
उदयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Rising, ascending.<BR>2 Prosperous, flourishing.<BR>E.<BR>उदय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर|उदरं|उदरः
उदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The belly.<BR>2 War.<BR>3 Any morbid abdominal affection, as liver, spleen, &c.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Enlargement of the abdomen from dropsy or flatulency.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, ऋ to go, अप् affix; what goes up or swells with food, slaughter, &c. or उद् prefixed to दृ to burst, and अच् or अल् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरक
उदरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Rubbing the belly, &c.<BR>2 Abdominal.<BR>E.<BR>उदर and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरग्रन्थि|उदरग्रन्थिः
उदरग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>The spleen, (the disease; a chronic affection of this organ not uncommon in India.)<BR>E.<BR>उदर abdomen, and ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरत्राण|उदरत्राणं
उदरत्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A cuirass, armour covering the front.<BR>2 A girth, a belly band.<BR>E.<BR>उदर the belly, and त्राण what preserves: see उदरस्त्राण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरथि|उदरथिः
उदरथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>उद् freely, ऋ to go, and अथिर् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरपिशाच|उदरपिशाचः
उदरपिशाच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>A glutton, voracious, one who devours every thing, flesh, fish, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उदर and पिशाच a demon, who is a devil for his belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरम्भरि|उदरंभरि|उदरम्भरिः
उदरम्भरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Selfishly voracious, gluttonous.<BR>E.<BR>उदर, भृ to nourish, इन् affix, and मुम् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरशय|उदरशयः
उदरशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sleeping on the face or belly.<BR>E.<BR>उदर and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरामय|उदरामयः
उदरामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Dysentery, diarrhoea^1.<BR>E.<BR>उदर the belly, and आमय sickness.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावर्त्त|उदरावर्त|उदरावर्तः|उदरावर्त्तः
उदरावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>The navel.<BR>E.<BR>उदर and आवर्त्त whirl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरावेष्ट|उदरावेष्टः
उदरावेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Tape worm.<BR>E.<BR>उदर and आवेष्ट what surrounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिन्
उदरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Fat, corpulent.<BR>2 Abdominal.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>उदर the belly, इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिल|उदरिलः
उदरिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fat, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>उदर to belly, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्क|उदर्कः
उदर्क<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Future or remote consequence.<BR>2 Future time.<BR>3 A plant, (Vangueria spinosa): see मदन.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, ऋच् to praise, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्च्चिस्|उदर्चिस्
उदर्च्चिस्<BR>mfn. (-र्च्चिः-र्च्चिः-र्च्चि)<BR>Luminous and ascending.<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>1 A name of VAHNI or fire.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 KANDARPA.<BR>E.<BR>उद upwards, and अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्द|उदर्दः|उदर्द्द
उदर्द<BR>m. (-र्दः)<BR>Erysipelas.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, अर्द to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्द्ध
उदर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>Scarlet fever.<BR>E.<BR>उद and ऋध to increase, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदलावणिक|उदलावणिकः
उदलावणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Salted, prepared with brine.<BR>E.<BR>उद water, लवण salt, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवज्र|उदवज्रः
उदवज्र<BR>m. (-ज्रः)<BR>A thunderbolt of water, a water spout.<BR>E.<BR>उद and वज्र a thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसित|उदवसितं
उदवसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>उद water, and वसित covered, defended, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवास|उदवासः
उदवास<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 A house in the margin of a stream or pond.<BR>2 A marine grotto, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and वास a bode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवाहन
उदवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 Any water vessel.<BR>E.<BR>उद and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदविन्दु
उदविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>उद and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्वित्
उदश्वित्<BR>n. (-श्वित्)<BR>Buttermilk, with an equal proportion of water.<BR>E.<BR>उद water, श्वि to increase, affixes क्विप् and तुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्त
उदस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Cast, thrown.<BR>2 Expelled, cast out.<BR>3 Cast up.<BR>4 Humbled, shamed.<BR>5 Scattered.<BR>6 Removed.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्थाली
उदस्थाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A caldron, a kettle.<BR>E.<BR>उद and स्थाली a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्य
उदस्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken pains, made an effort, &c.<BR>2 Having thrown, having cast up or tossed.<BR>3 Having scattered.<BR>4 Having expelled.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before अस to be or throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=146" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदहार|उदहारः
उदहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A water carrier.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and हार who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाज|उदाजः
उदाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Commanding, directing bodies of men.<BR>E.<BR>उद before अज to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Generous, gentle and bountiful.<BR>2 Giving, a donor.<BR>3 Great, illustrious.<BR>4 Dear, beloved.<BR>5 Accented.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 The acute accent, a high or sharp tone.<BR>2 Gift, donation.<BR>3 A musical instrument, a large drum.<BR>4 An ornament, (in rhetoric.)<BR>E.<BR>उद high, up, and आत्त pronounced, sounded; or from दा, to give or have, with आङ् prefixed, affix क्तः see अनुदात्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उदान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 One of the five vital airs, that which rises up the throat and passes into the head.<BR>2 The navel.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>4 An eye-lash.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, आङ् prefixed to अण् to breathe, to be, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Generous, liberal, munificent.<BR>2 Great.<BR>3 Unperplexed.<BR>4 Gentle.<BR>5 Upright, honest, sincere.<BR>6 Eloquent.<BR>7 Proper, right.<BR>E.<BR>उद् well, आङ् prefixed to ऋ to go, and अप् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारचेतस्
उदारचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>High-minded, magnanimous.<BR>E.<BR>उदार and चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारधी
उदारधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Wise, sagacious, noble-minded.<BR>E.<BR>उदार and धी Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावत्सर|उदावत्सरः
उदावत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year, one of the five sorts of years astrologically considered.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and आङ् before वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावर्त्त|उदावर्त|उदावर्तः|उदावर्त्तः
उदावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A disease of the bowels, iliac passion.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Difficult menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>उद् upper, आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Throwing or directing upwards.<BR>2 Elevation, being above or over.<BR>3 A stoic, a philosopher.<BR>4 Stoicism.<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Indifferent, unconcerned, apathetic.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and आस who casts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासितृ
उदासितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्रै-तृ)<BR>Indifferent, disregarding, void of concern or affection.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before आस to cast, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उदासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Indifferent, disregarding.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A stoic, a philosopher, one who has no passion nor affection for any thing: in popular acceptation, a religious mendicant in general, or one of a particular order.<BR>E.<BR>उदास and इमि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन<BR>mfn. (नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Indifferent, free from affection. (In law) One not involved in the dispute.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A stranger, a neutral, a common acquaintance, a person neither a friend nor a foe.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A spy, an emissary.<BR>2 A doorkeeper.<BR>3 A superintendent.<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set over.<BR>E.<BR>उद् over, आङ् before स्था to stay, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरण|उदाहरणं
उदाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 An example or illustration, an apposite argument, one of five modes of logical reasoning.<BR>2 Declaring, saying.<BR>E.<BR>उद् over, आङ् before हृ to convey, and ल्युट् affix, or with घञ् affix उदाहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहार|उदाहारः
उदाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृत
उदाहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Called, named, entitled.<BR>2 Said.<BR>3 Illustrated.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and आङ् before हृ to take, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, spoken.<BR>2 Bound, tied.<BR>3 Risen, ascended.<BR>4 Grown, augmented.<BR>5 Born, produced.<BR>6 Incurred, experienced.<BR>7 High, tall, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, and क्त affix; or उद् up, and इत gone, past part. of इण to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितोदित|उदितोदितः
उदितोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well acquainted with the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>उदित said, (by law and religion,) and उदित risen, &c. eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षण|उदीक्षणं
उदीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>2 Looking up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्य
उदीक्ष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having seen.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and ईक्ष to see, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचि
उदीचि<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The north: see उदच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Northern.<BR>E.<BR>उदच north, खः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>The country to the north and west of the river Sarasvatī, the northern region.<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>A perfume: see वाला.<BR>E.<BR>उदीची the north, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरण|उदीरणं
उदीरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, out, ईर to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरित
उदीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, uttered.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and ईर to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्ण|उदीर्णः
उदीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Generous, great, excellent.<BR>2 Intense.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, ऋ to go, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्णवेग
उदीर्णवेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Impetuous (as a torrent), violent.<BR>E.<BR>उदीर्ण and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य्य|उदीर्य
उदीर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be spoken.<BR>E.<BR>उद before ईर to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्य्यमाण|उदीर्यमाण
उदीर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Speaking.<BR>2 Spoken.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before ईर to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बर|उदुंबर|उदुम्बरं|उदुंबरः|उदुम्बरः
उदुम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR>2 A kind of leprosy.<BR>3 A threshold.<BR>4 A eunuch.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Copper; see उडुम्बर, it is also written ऊडुम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुम्बरपर्णी|उदुम्बरपर्ण्णी
उदुम्बरपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant: see दन्तिका; also उडुम्बरपर्णी and ऊडुम्बरपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूखल|उदूखलं
उदूखल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A gum-resin, Bdellium.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 A wooden mortar used for freeing rice from the husk, by pounding it with a pestle.<BR>2 Any mortar.<BR>E.<BR>उदू for उद् up, and खल what goes, affix अच्; also उडूखल and उलूखल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूढ|उदूढः
उदूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Married.<BR>2 Coarse, gross, heavy.<BR>3 Material, substantial.<BR>4 Much, exceeding.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, वह to bear, and क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजय
उदेजय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Shaking, making tremble.<BR>E.<BR>उद before एज to tremble, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग
उद्ग<BR>r. 6th cl. (उद्गति)<BR>To cast off or quit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गत|उद्गतं
उद्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Risen, ascended.<BR>2 Vomited, cast up.<BR>3 Departed, gone.<BR>4 Proceeded forth or from.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गता
उद्गता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A stanza of four lines, with ten syllables in the three first, and thirteen in the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गतासु
उद्गतासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Deceased, dead.<BR>E.<BR>उद्गत gone, असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गति|उद्गतिः
उद्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>2 Bringing up, vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गम|उद्गमः
उद्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>2 Bringing up, vomiting; also उद्गमनं.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, गम or गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीय|उद्गमनीयं
उद्गमनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be gone up, or ascended.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A pair of bleached clothes.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, गम to go, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाढ|उद्गाढं
उद्गाढ<BR>n. adv. (-ढं) or adj. mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>उद् excess, and गाढ much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=147" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A reciter of the prayers, &c. of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and गातृ who sings, (the prayers being chaunted,) from गै to sing, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाथा
उद्गाथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>A variety of the Arya measure, the same as the Gīti, a stanza of four lines containing alternately 12 and 18 instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गार|उद्गारः
उद्गार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>2 Ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>4 Speaking in the throat.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, गॄ to vomit, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गिरण|उद्गिरणं
उद्गिरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>2 Ejecting any thing, as saliva, &c. from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before गॄ to vomit, ल्युट् affix; also उद्गारणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीति|उद्गीतिः
उद्गीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A variety of the Arya metre, a verse of four lines containing 12, 15--12, and 14 feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीथ|उद्गीथः
उद्गीथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A portion of the Sāma Veda.<BR>2 Designation of the triliteral name of God.<BR>3 Chaunting the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, aloud, गै to sing, and थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गुर्ण
उद्गुर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Raised, lifted, held up.<BR>2 Erected.<BR>3 Excited.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, गुर to make effort, irr. participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रह|उद्ग्रहः
उद्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking up.<BR>2 An object that may be accomplished by religious or other acts.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before ग्रह to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रहण|उद्ग्रहणं
उद्ग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking up, lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उद and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राह|उद्ग्राहः
उद्ग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking up.<BR>2 Replying in argument.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, ग्रह to take, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहित|उद्ग्राहितः
उद्ग्राहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Excellent, exalted.<BR>2 Bound, tied.<BR>3 Seized.<BR>4 Deposited, delivered.<BR>5 Taken or lifted up.<BR>5 Recalled, remembered.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and ग्राहित taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घ|उद्घः
उद्घ<BR>m. (-द्घः)<BR>Excellence, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>उद much, घण to shine, affix ड or उद before हन to strike, अप् aff. and the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घन|उद्घनः
उद्घन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A carpenter's work-bench, a plank on which he works.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, हन to injure, अप् affix, ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टन|उद्घट्टनं
उद्घट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Opening, opening up as a lid.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and घट्टन fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टित
उद्घट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Opened, unlocked.<BR>E.<BR>उद up, and घट्टित fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घर्षण|उद्घर्षणं
उद्घर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Rubbing, rubbing up.<BR>2 Rubbing the skin with hard substances, as vitrified brick, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and घर्षण friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घस|उद्घसं
उद्घस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>उद, घस substituted, for अद to eat, affix अप्; what is eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाट|उद्घाटः
उद्घाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A watch or guard house.<BR>E.<BR>उद up, घट to endeavour, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटक|उद्घाटकं|उद्घाटकः
उद्घाटक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A key.<BR>2 A bucket, &c. see the next.<BR>3 An opener, the instrument or agent of opening any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटन|उद्घाटनं
उद्घाटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The rope and bucket of a well, a leather bucket used for drawing water.<BR>2 Opening, unlocking.<BR>3 An opener, the instrument or means of opening, a key, &c.<BR>4 Hosting, raising, lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उद up, घट^1 to strive, affix ल्युट्; also with वुञ् affix उद्घाटक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 307,308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटित|उद्घाटितः
उद्घाटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done with effort, exerted.<BR>2 Opened.<BR>3 Raised, hoisted or lifted up.<BR>E.<BR>उद much, घट to exert, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटितज्ञ|उद्घाटितज्ञः
उद्घाटितज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Wise, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, घट to endeavour, affix क्त, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटिताङ्ग
उद्घाटिताङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Intelligent.<BR>2 Naked.<BR>E.<BR>उद्घाटित and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घात|उद्घातः
उद्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>3 A club, a mallet.<BR>4 Striking, wounding, inflicting a hurt.<BR>5 A wound, a blow.<BR>6 The division of a book, a chapter, a section.<BR>7 Breathing through the nostrils as a religious exercise.<BR>8 Slipping, tripping.<BR>9 High, tall.<BR>E.<BR>उद before हन to kill or destroy, and घञ् affix, त is substituted for न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ज
उद्ज<BR>r. 6th cl. (उज्जति)<BR>To be straight: see उज्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्झ
उद्झ<BR>r. 6th cl.<BR>See उञ्झ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्ट
उद्घुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Sounded out.<BR>E.<BR>उद before घुष् to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंश|उद्दंशः
उद्दंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, and दंश who bites, from दशि and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्ड|उद्दंड|उद्दण्डः
उद्दण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Raised on a staff or pole.<BR>E.<BR>उद and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दण्डपाल|उद्दंडपाल|उद्दण्डपालः
उद्दण्डपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of snake.<BR>2 A kind of fish.<BR>3 A punisher, whether king or magistrate.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, दण्डपाल a punisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दन्तुर|उद्दंतुर|उद्दन्तुरः
उद्दन्तुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 High, tall.<BR>2 Terrific, formidable.<BR>3 Large toothed.<BR>E.<BR>उद high, long, and दन्तुर large toothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दान|उद्दानं
उद्दान<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Binding, confinement.<BR>2 Taming, subduing.<BR>3 A fire place.<BR>4 Submarine fire.<BR>5 The middle, the waist.<BR>6 The entrance of the sun into a sign of the zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>उद reverse, and दा to give, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दान्त|उद्दांत
उद्दान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Energetic.<BR>2 Humble.<BR>3 Elevated.<BR>4 Vomited by an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>उद and दान्त tamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाम|उद्दामः
उद्दाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Set free, unbound.<BR>2 Unconstrained, self-willed.<BR>2 Large, great.<BR>4 Proud, haughty.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उद priv. दम to tame, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाल|उद्दालः
उद्दाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant, (Cordia myxa or latifolia.)<BR>2 A kind of grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>उद high, large दल to pierce, affix घञ्; also उद्दालक, क being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दित|उद्दितः
उद्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>E.<BR>उद up, दो to cut, and क्त affix; also उदित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिन|उद्दिनं
उद्दिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Mid-day.<BR>2 Every day.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्य
उद्दिश्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having shewn or explained.<BR>2 Stipulating for, demanding.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, दिश to show, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिष्ट
उद्दिष्ट<BR>mf. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Mentioned, particularised, described.<BR>2 Promised.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before दिश to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप|उद्दीपः
उद्दीप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A gummy and resinous substance, Bdellium.<BR>m. (पः)<BR>1 Inflaming, lighting.<BR>2 An inflamer.<BR>3 Animating, or who or what animates.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, दीप to shine, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपक|उद्दीपकः
उद्दीपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Exciting, inflaming, rendering more intense.<BR>2 Lighting, setting alight.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and दीपक what lights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपन|उद्दीपनं
उद्दीपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Exciting, inflaming a passion.<BR>2 Illuminating.<BR>3 Burning of a body, &c.<BR>4 Any aggravating thing or circumstance, calculated to give poignancy to feeling or passion.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, दीप to inflame, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपमान
उद्दीपमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lighting up, brightening, becoming light.<BR>E.<BR>उद before दीप and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्त|उद्दीप्तः
उद्दीप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Lighted, set on fire or alight.<BR>2 Inflamed, aggravated, as passion.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and दीप्त lighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=148" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्र|उद्दीप्रं|उद्दीप्रः
उद्दीप्र<BR>n. (-प्रं)<BR>Bdellium.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before दीप to shine, रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश|उद्देशः
उद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Illustration, explanation, exemplification.<BR>2 Search, enquiry.<BR>3 Stipulation, bargain.<BR>4 An object, a motive.<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Relative to.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and देश showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशक|उद्देशकः
उद्देशक<BR>mf. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What explains or shows, illustrative, explanatory.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An illustration, an example.<BR>2 An illustrator.<BR>3 A guide.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before दिश to show, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्य|उद्देश्यः
उद्देश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>To be illustrated or explained.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, दिश to show, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देहिका
उद्देहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The white ant, termes; also उत्यादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योत|उद्द्योतः
उद्द्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, द्युत to shine, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्राव|उद्द्रावः
उद्द्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Flight, retreat.<BR>2 Going upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, द्रु to run, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्रुत
उद्द्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>1 Fled, retreated, run away.<BR>2 Ascended, gone up or upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and द्रुत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धत|उद्धतं|उद्धतः
उद्धत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rude, ill behaved.<BR>2 Haughty, vain, puffed up.<BR>3 Raised, elevated.<BR>4 Excited, intense.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A king's wrestler.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, हन to hurt or injure, affix क्त; ह becomes घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्क
उद्धतमनस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Haughty, proud, high minded.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धत raised, मनस्क minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतमनस्कत्व|उद्धतमनस्कत्वं
उद्धतमनस्कत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धत, मनस्क having a mind, and त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धति|उद्धतिः
उद्धति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Pride, haughtiness.<BR>2 Elevation.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before हन to strike, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धम|उद्धमः
उद्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Who or what blows.<BR>m. (मः)<BR>1 Breathing hard, panting.<BR>2 Blowing, sounding.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before ध्मा to blow, affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धय
उद्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who or what drinks.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before धे to drink, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्त्तृ|उद्धर्तृ
उद्धर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्ती-र्त्तृ)<BR>1 Who raises or lifts up.<BR>2 A sharer, a coheir.<BR>3 Who recovers property.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before हृ to take, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरण|उद्धरणं
उद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Raising or lifting any thing.<BR>2 Eradicating a tree, &c.<BR>3 Exterminating, destroying.<BR>4 Taking a part or share.<BR>5 Vomiting, bringing up.<BR>6 Final emancipation.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, हृ to take, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरणीय
उद्धरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be raised up.<BR>2 To be given up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before हरणीय to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्ष|उद्धर्षः
उद्धर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 A festival, especially religious.<BR>2 Great joy.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, हर्ष happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षण|उद्धर्षणं
उद्धर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Erection of the hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, हृष to be happy, and ल्युट् affix; occasioned by great pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धव|उद्धवः
उद्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A festival, a holiday.<BR>2 Sacrificial fire.<BR>3 The name of a person, the friend and councillor of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उद् reverse, धु to feel pain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान|उद्धानं|उद्धानः
उद्धान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Gone up, ascended.<BR>2 Vomited.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A furnace or fire place.<BR>E.<BR>उद, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान्त|उद्धांत|उद्धान्तः
उद्धान्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Vomited.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An elephant out of rut.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and ध्मा to breathe or blow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धार|उद्धारं|उद्धारः
उद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Raising, elevating, lifting up.<BR>2 Debt, especially a debt not bearing interest.<BR>3 A portion, a share.<BR>4 A deduction, a part to be set aside.<BR>5 Recovering property.<BR>6 Extracting, quoting.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fire place.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडूची.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, धृ to have, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारक
उद्धारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what raises or lifts.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before हृ to take, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारण|उद्धारणं
उद्धारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Raising, elevating.<BR>2 Sharing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before धृ to have, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारविभाग|उद्धारविभागः
उद्धारविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Partition, division of shares.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धार and विभाग dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धुर
उद्धुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Heavy.<BR>2 Thick, gross.<BR>3 Firm.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and धुर a burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूत
उद्धूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken off, fallen from or off.<BR>2 Tossed up, scattered above.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and धूत trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूषण|उद्धूषणं
उद्धूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, धूष to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृत|उद्धृतः
उद्धृत<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, drawn up, as water from a well, &c.<BR>2 Pulled up or out, eradicated or broken off.<BR>3 Lifted up.<BR>4 Raised, elevated.<BR>5 Thrown up or upwards.<BR>6 Vomited.<BR>7 Separated, set apart.<BR>8 Divided, partitioned.<BR>9 Recovered.<BR>10 Uncovered.<BR>11 Dispersed, scattered.<BR>12 Extracted, selected, taken from or out of.<BR>13 Holding, containing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, धृ to take, and क्त. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतोद्धार
उद्धृतोद्धार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 One who has received his share.<BR>2 That from which a share has been deducted.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धृत and उद्धार a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्य|उद्ध्यः
उद्ध्य<BR>m. (-द्ध्यः)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>उञ्झ to go, क्यप् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्यान
उद्ध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A furnace or fire place.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, ध्मा to blow, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बन्धन|उद्बंधन
उद्बन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tying up, hanging.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and वन्धन tying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बाहु
उद्बाहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-ह्वी-हु)<BR>1 Having the arms lifted up.<BR>2 Having the trunk upraised (as an elephant.)<BR>E.<BR>उद् and वाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुद्ध|उद्बुद्धः
उद्बुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Blown, budded.<BR>2 Reminded, made to think of or recalled.<BR>3 Awaked.<BR>E.<BR>उद् forth, up, and वुद्ध known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुद्धसंस्कार|उद्बुद्धसंस्कारः
उद्बुद्धसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Association of ideas recalling any thing to remembrance.<BR>E.<BR>उद्वद्ध and संस्कार faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोध|उद्बोधः
उद्बोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Incipient knowledge.<BR>2 Awaking.<BR>3 Reminding.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and बोध knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधक|उद्बोधकः
उद्बोधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Discovering, exhibiting.<BR>2 What reminds, or calls to remembrance.<BR>E.<BR>उद and बोधक making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधन|उद्बोधनं
उद्बोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Recalling, reminding.<BR>2 Awaking, arousing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before बुध to know, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भट|उद्भटः
उद्भट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Excellent.<BR>2 Exalted, magnanimous.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A tortoise.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>उद् lofty, भट to desire, and अच् affix; high-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भव|उद्भवः
उद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>उद् forth, भू to be or become, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवकर
उद्भवकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Productive.<BR>E.<BR>उद्भव, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भाव|उद्भावः
उद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Production, generation.<BR>2 Magnanimity.<BR>E.<BR>उद् भाव causing to be, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावन|उद्भावनं
उद्भावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Inattention, neglect, disregard.<BR>2 Saying, speaking.<BR>E.<BR>उद् away or up, भावन observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावित
उद्भावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Neglected, disregarded.<BR>2 Said, declared.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and भावित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=149" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भास|उद्भासः
उद्भास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Radiance, splendor.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and भास shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासयन्
उद्भासयन्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Lighting up, irradiating.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before भास to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासित
उद्भासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Lighted up, illuminated, splendid.<BR>2 Ornamented, graced, beautified.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before भास to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिज|उद्भिजः
उद्भिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिज्ज|उद्भिज्जं|उद्भिज्जः
उद्भिज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Sprouting, germinating, (as a vegetable.)<BR>E.<BR>उद्भिद a vegetable, and ज produced; also उद्भिज one ज being dropped; also उद्भिद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद्
उद्भिद्<BR>mfn. (-द्भिद् or -द्भित्)<BR>Sprouting, germinating.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, भिद to break or burst, affix क्विप्, or with क affix उद्भिद (-दः-दा-दं.)<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Culinary salt.<BR>E.<BR>उद् forth, भिद to break, and क affix; breaking from the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद|उद्भिदं
उद्भिद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Sprouting, &c. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिन्न
उद्भिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Opened, burst.<BR>2 Budded.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूत|उद्भूतः
उद्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Lofty, literally or figuratively.<BR>3 Visible, perceptible, present.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before भू to be, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतरूप|उद्भूतरूपं
उद्भूतरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Visible shape or form.<BR>E.<BR>उद्भूत and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रम|उद्भ्रमः
उद्भ्रम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Regret.<BR>2 Whirling, flourishing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, भ्रम to wander, धञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रान्त|उद्भ्रांत|उद्भ्रान्तं
उद्भ्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Agitated, bewildered, distressed.<BR>3 Whirled, flourished, waved (as a sword).<BR>E.<BR>उद् and भ्रान्त revolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्य|उद्यः
उद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>उद् water, and य what goes, from या to go, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत|उद्यतं|उद्यतः
उद्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, held up.<BR>2 Active, persevering, labouring diligently and incessantly.<BR>3 Trained, exercised, disciplined.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A section, a chapter, the division of a book.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before यम to cease, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम|उद्यमः
उद्यम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Strenuous and continued effort, exertion, perseverance.<BR>2 Taking or lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् reverse, यम to cease, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमिन्
उद्यमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Persevering, active, making effort.<BR>E.<BR>उद्यम and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम्य
उद्यम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Requiring exertion.<BR>ind.<BR>Having lifted or taken up.<BR>2 Having made exertion.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before यम to cease, यत् and ल्यप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यान|उद्यानं|उद्यानः
उद्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A garden.<BR>2 A royal garden, a park.<BR>3 Going forth, exit.<BR>4 Purpose, motive.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, या to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानपाल|उद्यानपालः
उद्यानपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gardener.<BR>2 The master or owner of a garden.<BR>E.<BR>उद्यान and पाल who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्याव|उद्यावः
उद्याव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Mixing, joining.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before यु to mix, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्युक्त|उद्युक्तः
उद्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Zealously active, labouring for some desired end.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, युज to join, क्त affix; also उद्यत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योग|उद्योगः
उद्योग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Exertion, perseverance, strenuous and continued endeavour.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, युज to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योगिन्
उद्योगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Active, laborious, persevering, one who makes effort.<BR>E.<BR>उद्योग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्र|उद्रः
उद्र<BR>(-द्रः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>उन्दी to wet, and रक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रङ्ग|उद्रंगः|उद्रङ्गः
उद्रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>An imaginary city, one floating in the air.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, and द्रङ्ग a town, one द rejected; also read उद्रङ्क, see हरिश्वन्द्रपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रथ|उद्रथः
उद्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The pin of the axle of a carriage.<BR>3 A cook.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्राव|उद्रावः
उद्राव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>A loud noise.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before रु to cry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रिक्त|उद्रिक्तं
उद्रिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Distinct, evident.<BR>2 Increased, augmented.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, रिच् to flow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रुज
उद्रुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Destroying, breaking down.<BR>E.<BR>उद् on, रुज to injure, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रेक|उद्रेकः
उद्रेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Commencement.<BR>2 Increase.<BR>3 Excess.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, रिच to flow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वत्सर|उद्वत्सरः
उद्वत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वमन|उद्वमनं
उद्वमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Vomiting, bringing up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and वमन vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्त|उद्वर्त|उद्वर्तः|उद्वर्त्तः
उद्वर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Abundant, plentiful.<BR>2 Left over.<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A remainder, a surplus.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तक|उद्वर्तक|उद्वर्तकः
उद्वर्त्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Rubbing and cleaning the body, (who or what does so.)<BR>2 Causing increase.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>(In algebra,) An assumed quantity.<BR>E.<BR>उद् over, वृत to be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तन|उद्वर्तन|उद्वर्तनं|उद्वर्त्तनं
उद्वर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going up, rising, ascending.<BR>2 Grinding, pounding.<BR>3 Rubbing or kneading the body.<BR>4 Rubbing and cleaning it with fragrant unguents.<BR>5 Unguents used for that purpose, or to relieve pains in the limbs, &c.<BR>6 Rising, (figuratively) prosperity, elevation.<BR>7 Misbehaving.<BR>8 Springing up of plants or grain, &c.<BR>9 Drawing out metal, laminating, wire drawing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and वर्त्तन abiding, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त्तित|उद्वर्तित
उद्वर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Perfumed, scented.<BR>2 Risen, elevated.<BR>3 Sprung up.<BR>4 Drawn out.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्द्धन
उद्वर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sly or suppressed laugh.<BR>E.<BR>उद् priv. वृद्ध to increase, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्हित|उद्वर्हितः
उद्वर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, drawn or lifted up.<BR>2 Eradicated.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, and वर्हित injured; also उद्वाहित, from वाह to endeavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वह|उद्वहः
उद्वह<BR>mf. (-हः-हा)<BR>A son or a daughter.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The vital air that conveys nourishment, &c. upwards.<BR>2 A chief, a leader, the head of a family or force.<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Who or what takes up or away.<BR>2 Best, most eminent.<BR>E.<BR>उद् further, वह what bears; carrying on one's name, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वहत्
उद्वहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>1 Upholding, supporting, bearing, containing.<BR>2 Having, possessing, assuming.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before वह to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वान|उद्वानः
उद्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Vomited.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, वम to vomit, क्त affix: see उद्वान्त and उद्वान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वान्त|उद्वांत|उद्वान्तं|उद्वान्तः
उद्वान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Vomited.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An elephant out of rut.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, वम to vomit, affix क्त, deriv. irr. see उद्वान्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाप|उद्वापः
उद्वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>(In logic,) non-existence of a subsequent consequent on the absence of an antecedent.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before वप to sow, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वास|उद्वासः
उद्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Abandoning, letting loose or free.<BR>2 Exile.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् away, वस to abide, causal form, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वासन|उद्वासनं
उद्वासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Quitting, abandoning.<BR>2 Expelling, banishing.<BR>3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>उत् forth, out, वस to abide, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाह|उद्वाहः
उद्वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, वह to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=150" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहकर्म्मन्|उद्वाहकर्मन्
उद्वाहकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>The marriage ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>उद्वाह and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहन|उद्वाहनं
उद्वाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Marriage.<BR>2 Ploughing a field twice.<BR>3 Anxiety, anxious regret.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The small shell used as a coin, a Cowri.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, वाह to endeavour, ल्युट् affix, and ङीष् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिक|उद्वाहिकः
उद्वाहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Relating to marriage, matrimonial.<BR>E.<BR>उद्वाह marriage, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहित|उद्वाहितः
उद्वाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, lifted or pulled up, &c.<BR>2 Eradicated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before वह to bear, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिन्
उद्वाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 What raises or draws up.<BR>2 Who or what marries, relating to marriage.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A rope.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, वाह to endeavour, णिनि and ङीष् affixes, or उद्वाह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्न|उद्विग्नः
उद्विग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Sorrowful, anxious, grieving for an absent lover, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, विज to shake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्नमनस्
उद्विग्नमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Sorrowful, depressed in spirits, anxious, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>उद्विग्न and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्षण|उद्वीक्षणं
उद्वीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Looking up or upwards.<BR>2 Seeing, looking at.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and वि before ईक्ष to see, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्त|उद्वृत्तः
उद्वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Raised, elevated.<BR>2 Exalted, prosperous.<BR>3 Unrestrained, ill behaved.<BR>4 Vomited.<BR>5 Left, as a remainder.<BR>E.<BR>उत् above, and वृत्त placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेग|उद्वेगं|उद्वेगः
उद्वेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 One going swiftly, a runner, a courier, &c.<BR>2 Steady, composed, tranquil.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Regret.<BR>2 Fear.<BR>3 Anxiety, agitation.<BR>4 Distress occasioned by separation from a beloved object.<BR>5 Admiration, astonishment.<BR>6 Ascending, mounting, going up or upwards.<BR>7 An ascetic whose arms, by long habit, continue always raised above his head.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The fruit of the Areca Catechu, the betel nut.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, विज to fear, to shake, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेगिन्
उद्वेगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Suffering distress, anxious, unhappy.<BR>E.<BR>उद्वेग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजक
उद्वेजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Distressing, annoying, what causes pain or sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before विज to fear, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजन|उद्वेजनं
उद्वेजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Anxiety, distress, regret, sorrowing for one absent.<BR>2 Corporal infliction, mutilation, torture.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before विज to shake, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजनकर
उद्वेजनकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Inflicting pain, punishing, torturing.<BR>2 Painful.<BR>E.<BR>उद्वेजन and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजित
उद्वेजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Garieved, pained, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before विज to fear, causal. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्ट|उद्वेष्टः
उद्वेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>What surrounds, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 Investing a town, besieging or surrounding it.<BR>2 Capturing, taking.<BR>3 Surounding, enclosing.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before वेष्ट to surround, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टन
उद्वेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Surrounding.<BR>2 An enclosure.<BR>3 Pain in the buttocks.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before वेष्ट to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टित
उद्वेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, invested, enclosed.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before वेष्ट to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उधस
उधस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>An udder: see ऊधस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उध्य
उध्य<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>Name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उध्रस्
उध्रस्<BR>r. 9th cl. (उध्रस्नाति) r. 10th cl. (उध्रामयति)<BR>1 To glean or gather by little at a time.<BR>2 To throw or cast upwards. The initial उ is considered^1 by some as an indicatory letter, the root being then ध्रस; q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्द
उन्द<BR>r. 7th cl. (ई,) उन्दी (उनत्ति)<BR>1 To wet or moisten.<BR>2 To be or become wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दर
उन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दुर|उंदुर|उंदुरः|उन्दुरः
उन्दुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rat: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्दुरु|उंदुरु|उंदुरुः|उन्दुरुः
उन्दुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>उन्दी to wet, and उरु affix; it is also written उन्दरु, उन्दर, as above, and उन्दुरु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्न|उन्नः
उन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Wet, moist.<BR>2 Kind, humane.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to be moist, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नत|उन्नतः
उन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 High, tall.<BR>2 Raised, held or lifted up.<BR>3 Plump, full.<BR>4 Great, eminent.<BR>E.<BR>उत् high, नत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतनाभि|उन्नतनाभिः
उन्नतनाभि<BR>mfn. (-भिः-भिः-भि)<BR>Corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>उन्नत high, and नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतशिरस्
उन्नतशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Holding up the head, carrying the head high.<BR>E.<BR>उन्नत and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतानत|उन्नतानतं
उन्नतानत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uneven, undulating, wavy.<BR>E.<BR>उन्नत high, and आनत low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नति|उन्नतिः
उन्नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Increase, advancement, prosperity.<BR>2 Rising, ascending.<BR>3 The wife of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, नम to bend, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतीश|उन्नतीशः
उन्नतीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>उन्नति and ईष husband: the husband of UNNATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्ध
उन्नद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Swelled, increased.<BR>2 Tied upon or over.<BR>3 Unbound.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before नह to bind, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमन|उन्नमनं
उन्नमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Raising, lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before नम to bow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमित|उन्नमितः
उन्नमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Raised, elevated, lifted or pulled up.<BR>2 Heightened, increased.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before नम to bow, क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमय्य
उन्नमय्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having raised.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before नम to bow, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्र
उन्नम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>Lofty, high, elevated.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before नम to bow, रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्नय<BR>m. (-यं)<BR>1 Raising, elevating, hoisting.<BR>2 Analogy, resemblance.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, नी to obtain, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयन|उन्नयनं
उन्नयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Deliberation, discussion, logic, reasoning.<BR>2 Inference.<BR>3 Raising, elevating, lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, नी to obtain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नस
उन्नस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Having a prominent nose.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, नस for नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाम|उन्नामः
उन्नाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Raising, lifting up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and नम to bow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाय|उन्नायः
उन्नाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Raising.<BR>E.<BR>see उन्नय, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायक
उन्नायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What raises.<BR>2 What leads to an inference or conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before नी to get, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाह|उन्नाहं|उन्नाहः
उन्नाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Sour gruel made from the fermentation of rice.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and नह to bind, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्र|उन्निद्रः
उन्निद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Awake.<BR>2 Blown, expanded as a flower.<BR>E.<BR>उद् priv. and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्मत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Insane, frantic, mad.<BR>2 Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 The thorn apple, (Datura metel and fastuosa.)<BR>2 A plant, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>उत् much, मत्त drunk or mad: applied to the plants, it alludes to their deleterious properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तता
उन्मत्तता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Insanity, intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also उन्मत्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=151" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद|उन्मदः
उन्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Mad, furious, extravagant, intoxicated.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Insanity, either morbid or as the effect or temporary excitement, intoxication, ecstasy^1.<BR>E.<BR>उत् very, मद to be mad, अच् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदिष्णु|उन्मदिष्णुः
उन्मदिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Mad, insane, crazed.<BR>2 Intoxicated.<BR>3 In rut, (as an elephant.)<BR>E.<BR>उन्मद to be mad, इष्णुच् attributive. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उन्मनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Regretting, missing, sorrowing for a lost or departed friend, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उत् up, upset, disturbed, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थ|उन्मंथ|उन्मंथः|उन्मन्थः
उन्मन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Agitation.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before, मथि to kill, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थक|उन्मंथक|उन्मन्थकः
उन्मन्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What moves or stirs.<BR>2 Throbbing, beating.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Inflammation of the outer ear.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before मथि to hurt, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थन|उन्मंथन|उन्मंथनं
उन्मन्थन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Shaking, agitating.<BR>2 Hurting, killing.<BR>3 Probing, stirring a weapon, &c. lodged in the body.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before मथि to hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मन्थित
उन्मन्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Moved, agitated, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and मन्थित agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथ|उन्माथः
उन्माथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A snare or trap.<BR>2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 A killer, a slaughterer.<BR>4 Pride, disdain.<BR>E.<BR>उत्, मथ to agitate, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माद|उन्मादः
उन्माद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Mad, insane, extravagant.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Madness, extravagance.<BR>2 (In medicine,) Mania.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, मद to be mad, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादन|उन्मादनः
उन्मादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Maddening, exciting, intoxicating.<BR>2 One of five arrows borne by KĀMADEVA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>उत् before मद to be mad or intoxicated, causal form, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादवत्|उन्मादवन्त्
उन्मादवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Mad, insane, wild, extravagant.<BR>E.<BR>उन्माद madness, &c. and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादिन्
उन्मादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Mad, intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>उन्माद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मान|उन्मानं|उन्मानः
उन्मान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A measure of size or quantity.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and मा to measure, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्ग|उन्मार्गः
उन्मार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A wrong road.<BR>2 Improper conduct, an evil course, error.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and मार्ग way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगत
उन्मार्गगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Erred, erring, going wrong.<BR>E.<BR>उन्मार्ग and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगमन
उन्मार्गगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going a wrong road.<BR>2 Following evil courses.<BR>E.<BR>उन्मार्ग and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गगामिन्
उन्मार्गगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Going wrong, erring, following evil courses.<BR>2 Taking a wrong road.<BR>E.<BR>उन्मार्ग and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मित
उन्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Meted, measured.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषत्
उन्मिषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Opening the eye, drawing up the eyelid, looking at, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before मिष to scatter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषित|उन्मिषितः
उन्मिषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opened, (as the eye.)<BR>2 Blown as a flower.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, मिष to scatter, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलन|उन्मीलनं
उन्मीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Winking, twinkling of the eye.<BR>2 Blowing, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and मील to twinkle, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलित|उन्मीलितः
उन्मीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opened, (as the eyes.)<BR>2 Blown as a flower.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, मील to wink, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुख|उन्मुखः
उन्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Looking upwards.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुद्र|उन्मुद्रः
उन्मुद्र<BR>mfn. (द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Blown as a flower.<BR>2 Unsealed, opened.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, open, and मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलित|उन्मूलितं
उन्मूलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eradicated, pulled up by the roots.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, मूल nominal verb, to take root, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृष्ट
उन्मृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Worn off, blotted out.<BR>E.<BR>उद् out, मृष्ट rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेदा
उन्मेदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Corpulency, fatness.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, मिद to anoint, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेष|उन्मेषं|उन्मेषः
उन्मेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Winking, twinkling of the eyelids, the upward motion.<BR>2 Opening the eye, looking at.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, मिष to scatter, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप
उप<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix to verbs and other words implying,<BR>1 Excess, (over, above, &c.);<BR>2 Vicinity or assemblage, (near, by the side of, with, together with);<BR>3 Inferiority, (lesser, secondary, &c.);<BR>4 Likeness, resemblance;<BR>5 Disease, extinction;<BR>6 Ornament;<BR>7 Command;<BR>8 Reproof;<BR>9 Astonishing;<BR>10 Giving;<BR>11 Killing;<BR>12 Diffusion;<BR>13 Wish, desire;<BR>14 Effort, exertion, &c. as उपर्कत्तुं, to assist; उपगन्तुं to approach; उपदेष्टं to advise; उपलब्धुं to revile; उपस्थातुं to worship; also उपपुराणं. an inferior or minor Purāṇa, उपकुम्भं near the water pot, उपगङ्गं upon the Ganges, उपकान्तं near or with a lover, उपाग्नि in the vicinity of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकण्ठ|उपकंठ|उपकण्ठं|उपकण्ठः
उपकण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>n. (-ण्ठं)<BR>1 Space near a village or its boundary.<BR>2 One of a horse's paces, his walk.<BR>ind. (-ण्ठं)<BR>Upon the neck, near the throat.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, कण्ठ the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरण|उपकरणं
उपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Apparatus, paraphernalia, as the vessels and offerings at a sacrifice.<BR>2 Implements, machines.<BR>3 The insignia of royalty.<BR>4 Sauces, condiments.<BR>5 Helping, assisting.<BR>6 Object of art or science, fabricating, composing, &c.<BR>7 Means of subsistence, any thing supporting life.<BR>E.<BR>उप implying command or help, कृ to make, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णम्
उपकर्णम्<BR>ind.<BR>Close to the ear, into the ear, (whispered, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उप near, कर्ण् the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्त्तृ|उपकर्तृ
उपकर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Assisting, befriending, one who helps or befriends.<BR>E.<BR>उप before कृ to do, affix तृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पन|उपकल्पनं
उपकल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Preparing articles of food, medicine, &c.<BR>2 Fabricating, making.<BR>3 Substituting.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कल्पन making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पित
उपकल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Prepared, made.<BR>2 Secondary, substituted.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कल्पित prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार|उपकारः
उपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Favour, protection, help, assistance.<BR>2 Use, advantage.<BR>3 A flower, &c. full blown.<BR>4 Garlands suspended, at gateways, as an embellishment on festivals.<BR>E.<BR>उप near or over, कृ to make, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारक
उपकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A friend, a protector, one who befriends.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कृ to do, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारकत्व
उपकारकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Protection, assistance.<BR>E.<BR>उपकारक and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारपर
उपकारपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Beneficent, diligent in doing good.<BR>E.<BR>उपकार and पर diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिका
उपकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A protectress, a governess.<BR>2 A palace, a caravansera.<BR>3 A kind of cake.<BR>E.<BR>उपकारी as below, &c. कन् affix, and the fem. form, or the fem. of उपकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिता
उपकारिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Aid, succour, protection.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to उपकारिन्; also with त्व, उपकारित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=152" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिन्
उपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Helping, assisting, a benefactor.<BR>2 Subsidiary, subservient.<BR>E.<BR>उपकार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारी
उपकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A palace, a caravansera.<BR>E.<BR>उपकार aid, asylum, affixes अण and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार्य्य|उपकार्य|उपकार्य्यः
उपकार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Deserving assistance or favour.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 A king's house, a palace, a caravansera.<BR>2 A tent.<BR>E.<BR>उपकार aid, &c. and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चि|उपकुंचिः|उपकुञ्चिः
उपकुञ्चि<BR>f. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>A plant, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>उप very, कुञ्च to be small, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुञ्चिका|उपकुंचिका
उपकुञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>2 A sort of fennel flower, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वुन् affixed to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुम्भ|उपकुंभ|उपकुम्भं
उपकुम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Solitary, lonely, retired.<BR>n. or ind. (-म्भं)<BR>Near the water jar.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुल्या
उपकुल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A canal, a trench, a ditch.<BR>2 Long pepper, (Piper longum.)<BR>E.<BR>उप near, कुल to accumulate, and क्यप् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुश|उपकुशः
उपकुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Gum-boil.<BR>E.<BR>उप before कुश to enclose, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपजलाशय|उपकूपजलाशयः
उपकूपजलाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A trough near a well for watering cattle.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, कूप a well, and जलाशय a place for water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृत
उपकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Benefited, assisted.<BR>2 Done kindly or beneficently, rendered as assistance.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A favour, a benefit.<BR>E.<BR>उप before कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृति|उपकृतिः
उपकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Aid, assistance, kindness.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कृ to do, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रन्तृ|उपक्रंतृ
उपक्रन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Beginning, one who begins.<BR>E.<BR>उप before क्रम to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रम|उपक्रमः
उपक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Deliberate commencement or undertaking; providing means, and anticipating consequences.<BR>2 A beginning in general.<BR>3 A particular ceremony preparatory to reading the Vedas.<BR>4 A stratagem.<BR>5 A means, an expedient.<BR>6 Trying the fidelity, &c. of a counsellor or friend.<BR>7 Valor.<BR>8 Practice of medicine, physicking.<BR>9 Flight, retreat.<BR>10 Approach.<BR>E.<BR>उप over, &c. क्रम to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणीय
उपक्रमणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Necessary, to be commenced or undertaken.<BR>2 To be gone to or near.<BR>E.<BR>उप before क्रम to go, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमितृ
उपक्रमितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>One who begins, &c. see उपक्रम.<BR>E.<BR>उप before क्रम to go, तृच् affix, with इट augment; also उपक्रत्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोश|उपक्रोशः
उपक्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Censure, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>उप reproach, inferiority, क्रुश to cry, to sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोष्टृ
उपक्रोष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 An ass.<BR>2 A reviler, a reprover.<BR>E.<BR>उप implying censure, क्रुश to cry, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्त
उपकॢप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Consecrated, dedicated, prepared or set apart for use.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कॢप्त made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्वण|उपक्वणं|उपक्वणः
उपक्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sound of a lute.<BR>E.<BR>उप well, क्वण to sound, affix अपे or with घञ् affix उपक्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षय|उपक्षयः
उपक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Loss.<BR>E.<BR>उप before क्षि to lose, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेप|उपक्षेपः
उपक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Poetical or figurative style or composition.<BR>E.<BR>उप and क्षिप to throw, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगण|उपगणः
उपगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A small number, less than a troop or number.<BR>E.<BR>उप and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगत|उपगतः
उपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed.<BR>2 Near, approached, gone to.<BR>2 Feeling, suffering, entertaining.<BR>3 Becoming, being, become.<BR>5 Having, obtained.<BR>E.<BR>उप with, गत gone, part. past. of गम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगतवत
उपगतवत<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Going to, gone to.<BR>2 Feeling, suffering, (as sorrow, &c.)<BR>3 Promising.<BR>4 Possessing.<BR>E.<BR>उप before गम to go, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगन्ध|उपगंधः|उपगन्धः
उपगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Perfume.<BR>E.<BR>उप and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगम|उपगमः
उपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Agreement, promise.<BR>2 Approach, approximation.<BR>3 Suffering, feeling.<BR>4 Acquaintance, society, intercourse.<BR>5 Getting, having, obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, गम to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरि|उपगिरिः
उपगिरि<BR>ind.<BR>Near a mountain; also with टच् added उपगिरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीत
उपगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Celebrated, proclaimed, sung, (by bards, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उप and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीति|उपगीतिः
उपगीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A variety of the Arya metre, a stanza of four lines, containing 12--15 and 12--15 syllabic instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीय
उपगीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be sung.<BR>ind.<BR>Having sung.<BR>E.<BR>उप before गै to sing, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूढ
उपगूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Hidden, concealed.<BR>2 Lulled, suppressed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before गुह to hide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूहन|उपगूहनं
उपगूहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An embrace, embracing.<BR>2 Astonishment, surprise.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, गुह to hide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रह|उपग्रहः
उपग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A prisoner, a man or animal in confinement.<BR>2 Favour, encouragement.<BR>3 Assistance.<BR>4 Peace purchased by the cession of every thing.<BR>5 Seizure.<BR>6 The presiding spirit or cause directing a planet's motion.<BR>7 A minor planet or any heavenly body of a secondary kind, as a comet, a meteor, a falling star, &c.<BR>8 A heap of kusa grass.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, ग्रह to take, अप् affix or ग्रह a planet, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहण|उपग्रहणं
उपग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>2 Holy study, reading the Vedas after initiation.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, ग्रह to take, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राह्य|उपग्राह्यः
उपग्राह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A present, an offering to a king or great man, a Nezer.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, &c. ग्रह to take, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघात|उपघातः
उपघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Disease, sickness.<BR>2 Touch, contact, especially with an intent to injure.<BR>3 Personal violence, assault.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, हन to injure, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघ्न|उपघ्नः
उपघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 Contiguous support.<BR>2 Support, stay, protection.<BR>3 What rests upon or is supported by.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, हन to destroy, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्र|उपचक्रः
उपचक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A variety of the ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>उप minor, and चक्र the Cakra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचतुर
उपचतुर<BR>m. plu. (-राः)<BR>Almost four.<BR>E.<BR>उप and चतुर four.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचय|उपचयः
उपचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Quantity, heap.<BR>2 Elevation.<BR>3 Prosperity.<BR>4 Excess.<BR>5 The third, sixth, tenth, and eleventh degrees from the first of a zodiacal sign.<BR>E.<BR>उप above, चि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचरित|उपचरितं
उपचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Served, adored.<BR>E.<BR>उप near or with, चर to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्य्य|उपचर्य
उपचर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be served or waited on.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 Service, attendance.<BR>2 Practice of medicine, physicking.<BR>E.<BR>उप implying help, चर to go, क्यप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचाय्य|उपचाय्यः
उपचाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A place for holding sacrificial fire, a hearth, an altar.<BR>E.<BR>उप, चिञ् to collect, ण्यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार|उपचारः
उपचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Service, attendance.<BR>2 Physicking, the practice of medicine.<BR>3 Practice, profession, usage.<BR>4 A present, a bribe.<BR>5 Presenting delicacies or necessaries, water, betel. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">Page154</a>] &c.<BR>6 Tending the sick, nursing.<BR>7 Solicitation, request.<BR>8 Incomplete, act, one in progress.<BR>9 A form of speech, a phrase that leaves something to be inferred, ellipsis, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप well. much, &c. चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=153" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारकरण
उपचारकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Offering presents, especially of perfumes. flowers, &c. attention, service.<BR>E.<BR>उपचार and करण making; also उपचारकर्म्मन्, उपचारक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारपर
उपचारपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Waiting upon, serving diligently.<BR>E.<BR>उपचार service, and पर diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्य्य|उपचार्य|उपचार्यः|उपचार्य्यः
उपचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>Practice of medicine.<BR>E.<BR>उप, चर in the causal form, and ण्यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित|उपचितः
उपचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Collected, assembled.<BR>2 Heaped.<BR>3 Thriving, increasing.<BR>4 Burnt.<BR>5 Plaistered, smeared.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, and चित collected, from चिञ् to gather, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित्रा
उपचित्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata, Rox.) see मूषिकपर्णी<BR>E.<BR>उप much, चित्र variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचूलन|उपचूलनं
उपचूलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Heathing, burning.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, चूर to burn, affix ल्युट्, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचेय
उपचेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be collected or heaped up.<BR>E.<BR>उप before चि to gather, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपछन्न|उपच्छन्न
उपछन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Secret, concealed.<BR>E.<BR>उप and छद to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजात
उपजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Produced, engendered, aroused.<BR>E.<BR>उप and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजाति|उपजातिः
उपजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A metre or stanza of four lines, with eleven syllables in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजाप|उपजापः
उपजाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Disunion, separation.<BR>2 Treason, treachery.<BR>E.<BR>उप separation, जप to meditate, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापक
उपजापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A mischief-maker, one who foments quarrels.<BR>2 A traitor, treacherous.<BR>E.<BR>उप before जप to meditate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्वा
उपजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>1 A kind of insect.<BR>2 The uvula or soft palate.<BR>3 Enlargement of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>उप privation or similitude, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्विका
उपजिह्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A species of insect.<BR>2 The soft palate: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवक
उपजीवक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Act, object.<BR>2 Means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>उप before जीव to live, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविका
उपजीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Subsistence, livelihood.<BR>E.<BR>उप and जीविका the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवन|उपजीवनं
उपजीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Subsistence, means of living.<BR>E.<BR>उप and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविन्
उपजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Dependant, living by or on.<BR>E.<BR>उप and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्य|उपजीव्यः
उपजीव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Affording a livelihood.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Cause.<BR>E.<BR>उप before जीव to live, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषम्
उपजोषम्<BR>ind.<BR>An expression indicative of joy.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, जुष to be kind, and अम् affix; also उपयोषम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Untaught knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, with ज्ञा knowledge, from ज्ञा to know, अङ्, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौकन|उपढौकनं
उपढौकन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A respectful offering or present, a Nezer.<BR>E.<BR>उप and ढौकन seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्त
उपतप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Heated, parched.<BR>2 Distressed, pained.<BR>E.<BR>उप and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्तृ
उपतप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>1 Morbid heat.<BR>2 Any cause of heat, burning or inflammation.<BR>E.<BR>उप excess, तप to heat, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपताप|उपतापः
उपताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Disease.<BR>2 Haste, hurry.<BR>3 Heat, heatedness.<BR>4 Pain.<BR>5 Misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, तप to heat, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापिन्
उपतापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>1 Inflaming, exciting.<BR>2 Heating.<BR>3 Suffering heat or pain.<BR>4 Sick.<BR>E.<BR>उपताप and इनि affix, or उप before तप with णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्यका
उपत्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Land near the foot of a hill or mountain.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, त्यकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंश|उपदंशः
उपदंश<BR>n. (-शः)<BR>1 A relish, or something to promote drinking.<BR>2 The venereal disease, chancre.<BR>3 Biting, stinging.<BR>4 A tree, the scraped root of which is used for horse-radish, (Morunga hyperanthera).<BR>E.<BR>उप much, &c. दंश biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उपदर्शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A doorkeeper.<BR>2 A guide.<BR>E.<BR>उप and दर्शक who shews.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शित
उपदर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perceived, distinguished.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दर्शित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A present, an offering to a king or great man, &c. a Nezer.<BR>E.<BR>उप, दा a gift, from दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानक|उपदानकं
उपदानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A present, &c. see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>उप implying help, &c. दान a gift, and क affix: a gift which is for the purpose of procuring favour or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्य
उपदिश्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having advised or instructed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्ट|उपदिष्टः
उपदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Instructed, advised.<BR>2 Initiated.<BR>3 Specified, particularised.<BR>4 Assigned as a plea or reason.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Council, advice.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदी
उपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A parasitic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उपदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A minor divinity, as a Yakṣa, Gandharba, Apsaras, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेश|उपदेशः
उपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Advice, information, instruction.<BR>3 Plea, pretext.<BR>4 Specification.<BR>5 Initiation, communication of the initiatory Mantra or formula.<BR>6 (In grammar,) An elementary term.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उपदेशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Giving instruction, instructing, instructive.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An instructor, a guide, specially a spiritual guide.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशन|उपदेशनं
उपदेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Advising, instructing.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशिन्
उपदेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Advising, an adviser.<BR>E.<BR>उपदेश advice, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टव्य
उपदेष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be advised, (fit, proper, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उप before दिश to shew, तव्य affix; also उपदेश्य, उपदेशनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उपदेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>One who points out, who orders or advises.<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>A Guru, a spiritual guide.<BR>E.<BR>उप prefixed to दिश to shew, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेह|उपदेहः
उपदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Liniment, ointment.<BR>2 A minor or secondary body.<BR>E.<BR>उप and दिह plaster, or देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेहिका
उपदेहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of insect.<BR>E.<BR>उप with, &c. देह the body, affixes कन् and टाप्; also उत्पादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रव|उपद्रवः
उपद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Tyranny, oppression.<BR>2 National distress, whether the act of the seasons or the king, famine, exaction, &c.<BR>3 National commotion, rebellion.<BR>4 Violence.<BR>5 A supervenient [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">Page155</a>] disease, one brought one whilst a person labours under another.<BR>E.<BR>उप, द्रु to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=154" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रविन्
उपद्रविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Tyrannical.<BR>2 Violent, factious.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A tyrant, an oppressor.<BR>2 A rebel.<BR>E.<BR>उपद्रव and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रष्टृ
उपद्रष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Supervisor, inspector, overseeing, overlooking.<BR>E.<BR>उप before दृश to see, तृच् affix, the vowel changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुत
उपद्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tyrannized over, oppressed, visited by calamities, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप before द्रु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म|उपधर्मः|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 A heretic, a schismatic.<BR>2 A minor or inferior duty.<BR>E.<BR>उप and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A false pretence.<BR>2 Trial or test of honesty, &c. of four kinds, of loyalty, disinterestedness, continence, and courage.<BR>3 A penultimate letter.<BR>E.<BR>उप, धा having, from धा, to have, with अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातु|उपधातुः
उपधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 An inferior mineral, a semi-metal: seven are specified; pyrites, sulphate of copper, talc, antimony, red orpiment, yellow orpiment, and calx of brass.<BR>2 Secondary secretion, as the milk, menses, adeps, sweat, teeth, hair, and lymph.<BR>E.<BR>उप minor, and धातु mineral, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उपधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A pillow.<BR>2 Kindness, affection.<BR>3 Poison.<BR>4 Religious observance or obligation.<BR>5 Excellence, excellent quality.<BR>6 Resting or placing upon.<BR>E.<BR>उप, धा to have or hold, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A pillow.<BR>E.<BR>उपधान a pillow, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाय
उपधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having placed or rested upon.<BR>E.<BR>उप before धा to hold, ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाशुचि
उपधाशुचि<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Approved, tried, of approved loyalty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उपधा and शुचि pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधि|उपधिः
उपधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 Fraud, circumvention.<BR>2 The wheel of a carriage.<BR>3 Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>उप, धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिक|उपधिकः
उपधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cheat, a knave, especially one who extorts money by threats.<BR>2 Fraud.<BR>E.<BR>उपधि and कृ to make, ड aff. or कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Being at the point of death.<BR>2 Suffering extreme pain.<BR>E.<BR>उप near or much, धूपित pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृति|उपधृतिः
उपधृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, धृ to have, क्तिन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Approached, approximate, near, (either in time or place.)<BR>E.<BR>उप near, नम to bow, affix क्तः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनय|उपनयः
उपनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The initiation of the three first classes; investiture with a peculiar thread or cord worn over the left shoulder, and under the right: the cord of the Brahman is of cotton, Munja, or Kusa grass; of the Kṣatriya, of Śaṇa or flax; and of the Vaiśya, of wool: the youths should be invested, respectively, from eight to sixteen, from eleven to twenty-two, and from twelve to twenty-four years of age.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Attaining, gaining.<BR>2 Bringing to.<BR>E.<BR>उप over, णीञ्^1 to obtain, अच् affix; also with घञ् affix उपनाय, and with ल्युट् affix उपनयन.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: Cf WIL and WIL1819 णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयन|उपनयनं
उपनयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before affix ल्युट्; also with अण् added उपनायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाय|उपनायः
उपनाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>See उपनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाह|उपनाहः
उपनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A plaster, an unguent applied to a wound or sore.<BR>2 The tie of a lute, the lower part of the tail piece where the wires are fixed.<BR>3 Inflammation of the ciliary glands, stye.<BR>E.<BR>उप, नह to bind, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहन|उपनाहनं
उपनाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Unction, anointing, plastering.<BR>E.<BR>उप before नह to tie, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेप|उपनिक्षेपः
उपनिक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A deposit, sealed or in a cover, so that the contents are unknown.<BR>E.<BR>उप and निक्षेप the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधान|उपनिधानं
उपनिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A deposit: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधि|उपनिधिः
उपनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A deposit, a pledge, property put into the care of a creditor, friend, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before धा to have, कि affix; in law this word ordinarily implies more especially a sealed or enclosed deposit, but according to some, it is any article entrusted to a friend which he may use whilst in his keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद्
उपनिषद्<BR>f. (-षत् or -षत्)<BR>1 A portion of the religious writings of the Hindus; the theological part, and the Vedānta or argumentative part of the Vedas, either detached from or comprised in the principal work.<BR>2 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>3 Truth as the principle of divine being.<BR>4 A neighbouring mansion.<BR>5 A lonely place.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि prefixed to षद to go, affix क्विप्; in which abide the essential parts of religion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं|उपनिष्करः
उपनिष्कर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A street.<BR>2 A principal or royal road.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before कृ to make, affix अप्, and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमण|उपनिष्क्रमणं
उपनिष्क्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A main or royal road.<BR>2 An instituted observance or Saṃskāra, taking a child in the fourth month of its age into the open air.<BR>3 Going forth.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before क्रम to go, affix ल्युट्, and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिहित
उपनिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deposited with, entrusted to.<BR>2 Placed near to.<BR>3 Offered, presented.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before धा to have, क्ति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीत|उपनीतः
उपनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Brought near to, approximated.<BR>2 Obtained, attained.<BR>3 Citing, adducing.<BR>4 Presented.<BR>5 Known.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The youth invested with the characteristic string: see उपनय.<BR>E.<BR>उप before नी to obtain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीय
उपनीय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having brought.<BR>2 Having invested.<BR>E.<BR>उप before नी to bring, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनुन्न
उपनुन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Sent or dispatched.<BR>2 Wafted, driven, (by the wind.)<BR>E.<BR>उप before नुद to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्त
उपन्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Pledged, deposited.<BR>2 Given, communicated.<BR>3 Brought forward, (as an example, &c.) adduced.<BR>4 Placed near to, or in, or upon.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि before अस to throw, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यास|उपन्यासः
उपन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A pledge, a pawn, a hostage.<BR>2 An exordium or introduction.<BR>3 A precept, a law.<BR>4 Giving, imparting.<BR>5 Juxtaposition.<BR>6 A suggestion, a hint.<BR>E.<BR>उप and नि prefixed to अस, to throw or send, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यास्य
उपन्यास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>To be pleaded.<BR>E.<BR>उप and न्यास्य to be adduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपति|उपपतिः
उपपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A paramour, a gallant.<BR>E.<BR>उप in place of, पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्ति|उपपत्तिः
उपपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Association, connexion.<BR>3 Fitness, propriety.<BR>4 Cessation, end.<BR>5 Possessing, having. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">Page156</a>]<BR>6 Ascertained or demonstrated conclusion.<BR>7 Cause, reason.<BR>8 Effecting, doing.<BR>9 Religious abstraction.<BR>10 (In arithmetic or geometry,) Proof, demonstration.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=155" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिमत्|उपपत्तिमन्त्
उपपत्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Right, fit, reasonable, proper.<BR>2 United, associated.<BR>E.<BR>उपपत्ति and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपद|उपपदं
उपपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Small, diminutive.<BR>2 The subsidiary term in a compound word.<BR>3 The first member of a compound word.<BR>4 An aptote, a word sometimes used as an adverb and sometimes as an inflected noun.<BR>5 A secondary noun in a sentence in conjunction or apposition.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद a foot, or an inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्न
उपपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Manifested.<BR>2 Fit, suited to the occasion, adequate.<BR>3 Done, shewn, proved, effected.<BR>4 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>5 Produced from or by.<BR>6 Physicked, cured.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातक|उपपातकं
उपपातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A great crime, as killing a cow, selling a daughter, atheism, &c; it is considered as criminality in the second or third degree, and is of various kinds: see महापातक.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, and पातक a crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकिन्
उपपातकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A sinner in any but the first degree.<BR>E.<BR>उपपातक and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादन|उपपादनं
उपपादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Effecting, doing.<BR>2 Giving, delivering, presenting.<BR>3 Proving or establishing by argument.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद to go, causal. form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादित
उपपादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done, effected.<BR>2 Given, delivered, presented.<BR>3 Proved, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Shod.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A superhuman being, a god, a demon, &c.<BR>2 Hell.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पद to go, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपाप|उपपापं
उपपाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A heinous crime, as killing a cow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप excess, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपालित
उपपालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protected, nurtured.<BR>E.<BR>उप and पालित protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडन|उपपीडनं
उपपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pain, agony, torture.<BR>2 Inflicting pain.<BR>3 Devastating, laying waste.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पीड to give pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपीडित
उपपीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tortured, pained, distressed.<BR>2 Devastated.<BR>E.<BR>उप before पीड to give pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुर|उपपुरं
उपपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>a suburb.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुराण|उपपुराणं
उपपुराण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A Purāṇa, one not included in the eighteen principal: a similar number is reckoned, or<BR>1 Ādi.<BR>2 Nṛsiṃha.<BR>3 Vāyu.<BR>4 Śivadharma.<BR>5 Durvasa.<BR>6 Nārada.<BR>7 Nandikeśvara.<BR>8 Uśanas.<BR>9 Kapila.<BR>10 Varuṇa.<BR>11 Sāmba.<BR>12 Kālikā.<BR>13 Maheśvara.<BR>14 Padma.<BR>15 Deva.<BR>16 Parāśara.<BR>17 Mārīca.<BR>18 Bhāskara.<BR>E.<BR>उप minor, पुराण a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपुष्पिका
उपपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Yawing, gaping.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, पुष्प to flower, to open as a flower, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्रदान|उपप्रदानं
उपप्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>उप for assistance, प्रदा to give, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लव|उपप्लवः
उपप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Rāhu, the ascending node.<BR>2 A portent or natural phaenomenon so considered.<BR>3 An affray or assault, a conflict without weapons.<BR>4 Eclipse.<BR>5 Misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>उप over &c. प्न to go, अप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपप्लुत
उपप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Distressed, pained.<BR>2 Harassed (by Rāhu, &c.) eclipsed.<BR>3 Assailed, beset.<BR>4 Marked by prodigies.<BR>5 Wet, moistened.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Morbid sensibility of the uterus.<BR>E.<BR>उप before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुक्त
उपभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Used, enjoyed, possessed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before भुज to enjoy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभुञ्जान
उपभुञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Using, enjoying.<BR>E.<BR>उप before भुज to enjoy, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभृत्
उपभृत्<BR>f. (-भृत्)<BR>A cup of a round shape, made of the wood of the banian tree, and used in sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>उप, भृ to fill, क्विप् and तुक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग|उपभोगः
उपभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>2 Enjoyment, use.<BR>3 Cohabitation.<BR>4 Use, usufruct.<BR>E.<BR>उप excess, भुज् to eat, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपभोग्य
उपभोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>To be used, to be enjoyed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before भुज् to enjoy, य affix; also उपभोजनीय and उपभोक्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्द्द|उपमर्द|उपमर्दः
उपमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 Reproach, abuse.<BR>2 Refuting a charge.<BR>E.<BR>उप, मृद to tread down, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमर्दक|उपमर्दकः|उपमर्द्दक
उपमर्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The refuting of a charge.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपम
उपम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Like, (but used only in composition.)<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Resemblance, a resemblance as a picture, an image, &c.<BR>2 A simile.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, मा to measure, affixes, अङ् and टाप्; also with ल्युट् affix, उपमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमातृ
उपमातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>An image maker, a portrait painter.<BR>E.<BR>उप before मा to measure, तृच् affix.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A wet nurse.<BR>2 A near female relative.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमान|उपमानं
उपमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See उपमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमित
उपमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compared.<BR>E.<BR>उप and मा to measure, क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमिति|उपमितिः
उपमिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Resemblance, comparison, a likeness, a picture, image, &c.<BR>2 Analogy.<BR>3 Knowledge of things derived from analogy or resemblances.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, मा to measure, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेत|उपमेतः
उपमेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compared with.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Śāl, a timber tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>उपम like, इत gone: high as a mountain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेय
उपमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be compared with or to.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The subject of a comparison, as the face is of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>उप before मा to measure, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपमेयोपमा
उपमेयोपमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The resemblance of any object to that compared with it, as of the moon to a beautiful face.<BR>E.<BR>उपमेय and उपमा likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्तृ|उपयंतृ
उपयन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>A husband, a master.<BR>E.<BR>उप, यम to cease, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयन्त्र|उपयंत्र|उपयंत्रं
उपयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 A small instrument or implement.<BR>2 An application of a similar nature, as actual cautery, escharotics, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप and यन्त्र instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयम|उपयमः
उपयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>उप and यम to stop, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचक|उपयाचकः
उपयाचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A present solicitor, one who asks or begs.<BR>E.<BR>उप before याच to beg, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाचित|उपयाचितं
उपयाचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Requested, solicited.<BR>2 Offered, especially to the deities to render them propitious.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, याच to ask or beg, affix क्त, or with कन् added उपयाचितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयाम|उपयामः
उपयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>उप, यम to refrain, affix घञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=156" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुक्त|उपयुक्तः
उपयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Proper, right.<BR>2 Adapted to, suitable, appropriate, useful.<BR>3 Touched by.<BR>4 Taken.<BR>5 Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>उप before युज to join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयुञ्जान
उपयुञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Taking, appropriating, attaching.<BR>E.<BR>उप before युजि to join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोग|उपयोगः
उपयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Good conduct, observing established practices.<BR>2 Any act tending to effect a desired object.<BR>3 Fitness, suitableness.<BR>4 Service, utility.<BR>5 Use, application.<BR>6 Contact, proximity.<BR>7 Administration of medicines.<BR>3 Preparation of them.<BR>E.<BR>उप before युज to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिता
उपयोगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Fitness, suitableness.<BR>2 Usefulness.<BR>2 Occasion, need.<BR>4 Favour, propitiousness.<BR>E.<BR>उपयोगिन् and तल् affix, or with त्व, उपयोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोगिन्
उपयोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Appropriate, suitable.<BR>2 Conducive or contributing to, serviceable, useful.<BR>3 Favourable, propitious.<BR>4 Touching, in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>उपयोग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपयोषम्
उपयोषम्<BR>ind.<BR>A word expressing great pleasure: see उपजोषम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्त|उपरक्तः
उपरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Afflicted with pain or calamity.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>1 Eclipsed, (the sun or moon.)<BR>2 Rāhu, (the ascending node.)<BR>E.<BR>उप implying distress, रञ्ज to colour, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरक्षण|उपरक्षणं
उपरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A guard, an outpost.<BR>E.<BR>उप, रक्ष to defend or protect, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरचित
उपरचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made, prepared.<BR>E.<BR>उप and रचित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरत|उपरतः
उपरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stopped, ceased.<BR>2 Dead.<BR>E.<BR>उप before रम to please, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरतस्पृह|उपरतस्पृहः
उपरतस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Void of desire.<BR>E.<BR>उपरत and स्पृह desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरति|उपरतिः
उपरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Stopping, ceasing.<BR>2 Refraining from sensual enjoyment.<BR>3 Abstaining from prescribed acts.<BR>4 Great or exquisite pleasure.<BR>5 Death.<BR>E.<BR>उप reverse or excess, रम to please, क्तिन् affix; also with घञ् affix उपरम or उपराम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरम|उपरमः
उपरम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरमण|उपरमणं
उपरमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Abstaining from ceremonial acts or from the pleasures of sense, &c.<BR>2 Ceasing, discontinuance.<BR>E.<BR>उप before रम to please, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरस|उपरसः
उपरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A secondary mineral, as red chalk. bitumen, &c.<BR>2 A secondary passion.<BR>3 A subordinate flavour.<BR>E.<BR>उप minor, रस flavour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराग|उपरागः
उपराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>2 Rāhu or the ascending node.<BR>3 Calamity, affliction.<BR>4 Misbehaviour, ill conduct.<BR>5 Reproach, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>उप, रञ्ज to colour, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपराम|उपरामः
उपराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Stopping, ceasing: see उपरति.<BR>E.<BR>उप, रम to please, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरि
उपरि<BR>ind.<BR>On, upon, above.<BR>E.<BR>उप and रि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिगत
उपरिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone up, ascended.<BR>E.<BR>उपरि and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिचित
उपरिचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Piled over or above.<BR>E.<BR>उपरि and चित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिज
उपरिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>High, elevated, produced above.<BR>E.<BR>उपरि and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरिष्टात्
उपरिष्टात्<BR>ind.<BR>Up, above.<BR>E.<BR>उप and रिष्टातिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरुद्ध|उपरुद्धः
उपरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Obstructed, impeded.<BR>2 Covered, spread.<BR>3 Favoured, protected.<BR>E.<BR>उप and रुद्ध checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोध|उपरोधः
उपरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Impediment, opposition, check, refusal.<BR>2 Favour, protection.<BR>3 Surrounding, blockading.<BR>4 Binding, tying.<BR>5 Taking hold of.<BR>E.<BR>उप before रुध to hinder, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपरोधक|उपरोधकं
उपरोधक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An inner room, a private apartment.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, रुध to enclose, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपर्य्युपरि
उपर्य्युपरि<BR>ind.<BR>1 Over, upon, above, what is above.<BR>2 Near, neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>उपरि repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपल|उपलः
उपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A rock or stone, a precious stone or jewel.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Refined or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, ला to give or take; affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्ष्य|उपलक्ष्यः
उपलक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Inferable.<BR>m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>1 A prop, a stay, a support, an asylum.<BR>2 An inference.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, लक्ष्य to be marked or sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षण|उपलक्षणं
उपलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Designating or implying any analogous object where only one is specified, using a term in a generic sense.<BR>2 Metaphorical or elliptical expression.<BR>E.<BR>उप comprehensive, लक्षण a mark or designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलक्षित
उपलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Comprehended, included, implied, understood.<BR>E.<BR>उप before, लक्ष to designate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्ध
उपलब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Obtained, received.<BR>2 Understood, known.<BR>3 Perceived.<BR>E.<BR>उप before लभ to get, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धार्था
उपलब्धार्था<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>A tale, a true or probable story.<BR>E.<BR>उपलब्ध understood, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलब्धि|उपलब्धिः
उपलब्धि<BR>f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>1 Mind, understanding.<BR>2 Knowledge, especially religious.<BR>3 Gain, acquisition.<BR>4 Perceptibility, appearance.<BR>E.<BR>उप, लभ to obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भ|उपलंभ|उपलंभः|उपलम्भः
उपलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Apprehension, conception, comprehension otherwise than from memory.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, लभि to obtain, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलभ्य
उपलभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>1 To be obtained.<BR>2 To be understood.<BR>ind.<BR>Having observed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before लभ to get, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलम्भ्य|उपलम्भ्यः
उपलम्भ्य<BR>mfn. (-म्भ्यः-म्भ्या-म्भ्यं)<BR>Commendable, praiseworthy, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>उप before लभ to get, ण्यत् affix, and म augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलालिका
उपलालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिङ्ग|उपलिंग|उपलिंगं|उपलिङ्गं
उपलिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A portent, a natural phaenomenon considered as announcing evil.<BR>E.<BR>उप over, लिगि to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्त
उपलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Smeared, plastered.<BR>E.<BR>उप and लिप्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलिप्सित
उपलिप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wishing to take or seize.<BR>E.<BR>उप before लभ to gain, desider. form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेप|उपलेपः
उपलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Plastering, smearing, anointing.<BR>E.<BR>उप, लिप to smear, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपलेपन|उपलेपनं
उपलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Smearing, plastering with cow dung, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप, लिप to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवन|उपवनं
उपवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A garden, a grove.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्णन|उपवर्णनं
उपवर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Minute description.<BR>E.<BR>उप and वर्णन describing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्त्तन|उपवर्तन|उपवर्तनं|उपवर्त्तनं
उपवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A country inhabited or not.<BR>2 An uninhabited country.<BR>3 A division, a district or Pergana.<BR>4 A kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>उप, वृत to abide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ष|उपवर्षः
उपवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>The name of a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवर्ह|उपवर्हः
उपवर्ह<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>A pillow.<BR>E.<BR>उप over, वर्ह to excel, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवसथ|उपवसथः
उपवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>उप, वस to abide, थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवस्त|उपवस्तं
उपवस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>A fast, fasting.<BR>E.<BR>उप, वस to abide, क्त affix; or with घञ् affix उपवास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=157" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवास|उपवासः
उपवास<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>1 A fast, fasting: when observed as a religious act, it comprises abstinence from all sensual gratification, from perfumes, flowers, unguents, ornaments, betel, music and dancing, &c.<BR>2 A fire altar.<BR>E.<BR>उप before वस to abide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवासिन्
उपवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Fasting, one who observes a fast.<BR>E.<BR>उपवास and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाहन|उपवाहनं
उपवाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Carrying, bringing back.<BR>E.<BR>उप and वाहन bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवाह्य|उपवाह्यः
उपवाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>1 A king's elephant.<BR>2 Any royal vehicle.<BR>E.<BR>उप above, वह to bear, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविद्या
उपविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Profane science, inferior sort of knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>उप and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष|उपविषं|उपविषः
उपविष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Factitious poison.<BR>2 A narcotic, any deleterious drug, as opium, Datura, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, विष poison.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, Atis.<BR>E.<BR>उप reverse, and विष poison: an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपविष्ट|उपविष्टः
उपविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Seated, sitting.<BR>2 Arrived, entered.<BR>E.<BR>उप upon, विष्ट placed, entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीत|उपवीतं
उपवीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The thread or cord worn by the three first classes of Hindus, over the left shoulder and under the right.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, वी to shine, affix क्त; see उपनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवीतिन्
उपवीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>The Brahman who wears the string in the usual manner, or on the left shoulder and under the right arm.<BR>E.<BR>उपवीत and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवृंहित
उपवृंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Collected from, possessed of.<BR>E.<BR>उप and वृंहित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेद|उपवेदः
उपवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A minor Veda, or which four are reckoned, treating of the military art, medicine, music, and mechanics.<BR>E.<BR>उप and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेश|उपवेशः
उपवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Sitting, resting.<BR>2 A seat.<BR>3 Voiding by stool.<BR>E.<BR>उप before विश to enter, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेशन|उपवेशनं
उपवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sitting, resting.<BR>2 Voiding by stool.<BR>E.<BR>उप before विश to enter, active or causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपवेश्य
उपवेश्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having seated or caused to sit.<BR>E.<BR>उप before विश to enter, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपव्याघ्र|उपव्याघ्रः
उपव्याघ्र<BR>m. (-घ्रः)<BR>The hunting leopard.<BR>E.<BR>उप and व्याघ्र a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशम|उपशमः
उपशम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Tranquillity, calmness, patience.<BR>2 Intermission, cessation, relaxation.<BR>E.<BR>उप much, शम to be tranquil, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशय|उपशयः
उपशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Productive of happiness or rest.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Ascertainment of disease or diagnosis by the effect of certain articles of food or medicine.<BR>2 Allaying disease by diet, regimen, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप before शी to sleep, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशल्य|उपशल्यं|उपशल्यः
उपशल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>A space near a village.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, शल to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्त|उपशांत
उपशान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Calm, tranquil.<BR>2 Appeased, pacified.<BR>3 Diminished, intermitted.<BR>E.<BR>उप before शम to be tranquil, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्ति|उपशांति|उपशांतिः|उपशान्तिः
उपशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Tranquillity, calm.<BR>2 Appeasing, allaying.<BR>3 Cessation, intermission, remission.<BR>E.<BR>उप before शम to be quiet, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशान्तिन्|उपशांतिन्
उपशान्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिनी-न्ति)<BR>Tranquil, calm, appeased, tame.<BR>(-न्ती)<BR>A tame elephant.<BR>E.<BR>उपशान्त and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशाय|उपशायः
उपशाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Watching and sleeping alternately.<BR>E.<BR>उप alternately, -शी to sleep, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिता
उपशायिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Tranquillizing, calming.<BR>2 Secondary means of cure, as diet, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उपशायिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व, उपशायित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशायिन्
उपशायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Allaying, tranquillizing, what calms, &c.<BR>2 (In medicine,) Composing, narcotic.<BR>E.<BR>उप before शी to sleep, causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपशोभित
उपशोभित<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>Adorned.<BR>E.<BR>उप and शोभित beautified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुत|उपश्रुतं
उपश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Promised, agreed.<BR>E.<BR>उप with श्रु to hear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपश्रुति|उपश्रुतिः
उपश्रुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Promise, assent.<BR>2 Judicial astrology, aspect of the stars, fortune-telling.<BR>E.<BR>उप above, श्रु to hear, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंक्षेप
उपसंक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An abstract or compendium.<BR>E.<BR>उप and संक्षेप abridgement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंख्यान
उपसंख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>(In grammar,) A substitute in form or sense, a consignificant term or affix.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, संख्या to number, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्रह
उपसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Obeisance, civil address, respectful salutation of a person by name.<BR>2 Taking, holding.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, सम् with, ग्रह to take, affix घञ्, or with ल्युट् affix उपसंग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंग्राह्य
उपसंग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 Respectable, venerable.<BR>2 To be saluted reverentially.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सं before ग्रह to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंगृह्य
उपसंगृह्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken, holding.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सं before ग्रह to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंव्यान|उपसंव्यानं
उपसंव्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A lower garment.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सं before व्येञ् to cover, ल्युट् affix; what covers the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहरण|उपसंहरणं
उपसंहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Refusing, withholding.<BR>2 Excluding.<BR>3 Taking away.<BR>4 Attacking, invading.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् before हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहरत्
उपसंहरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Taking away.<BR>2 Refusing, excepting.<BR>3 Going against, invading.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सं before हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहार|उपसंहारः
उपसंहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Witholding, refusing.<BR>2 Taking away.<BR>3 Excepting, excluding.<BR>4 Destruction, death, end.<BR>5 Collection, assemblage.<BR>6 A compendium.<BR>7 Brevity, conciseness.<BR>8 Attacking, invasion.<BR>9 (In logic,) Refutation.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृत
उपसंहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Withheld, denied, refused.<BR>2 Excepted.<BR>3 Compressed, comprehended, excluded.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसंहृति|उपसंहृतिः
उपसंहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A compound expressive of various meanings.<BR>2 Comprehension.<BR>3 Seizing, taking.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् before हृ to take, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसत्ति|उपसत्तिः
उपसत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Meeting, union.<BR>2 Service.<BR>3 Gift, donation.<BR>E.<BR>उप with, षद to go, &c. क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसद|उपसदः
उपसद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who goes near to.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Approach.<BR>E.<BR>उप and षद to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसदन|उपसदनं
उपसदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A neighbouring abode, a neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, and सदन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्ध्यम्|उपसंध्यम्
उपसन्ध्यम्<BR>ind.<BR>Near evening.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, सन्ध्या evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्न|उपसन्नः
उपसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Approached, approximate.<BR>E.<BR>उप over, षद to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसन्नता
उपसन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Proximity, approach.<BR>E.<BR>उपसन्न and तल् affix; also उपसन्नत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=158" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसमाधान|उपसमाधानं
उपसमाधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Placing, putting in or on.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् with आङ् before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसम्पन्न|उपसंपन्न|उपसम्पन्नः
उपसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Dressed, cooked.<BR>2 Immolated, sacrificed, (as a victim, &c.)<BR>3 Dead, deceased.<BR>4 Gained, obtained.<BR>5 Enough, sufficient.<BR>6 Perfected, finished.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सम् prefixed to पद to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर|उपसरः
उपसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 The first pregnancy or impregnation of a cow, &c.<BR>2 Who or what approaches.<BR>E.<BR>उप, सृ to go, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्ग|उपसर्गः
उपसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A portent, a natural phaenomenon supposed to announce future evil, an eclipse, &c.<BR>2 A particle prefixed to roots, &c. a preposition.<BR>3 A disease, possession by an evil spirit.<BR>4 Change occasioned by any disease.<BR>5 A disease brought on whilst a person labours under another.<BR>6 Indication or symptom of death.<BR>E.<BR>उप near or with, सृज to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जन|उपसर्जनं|उपसर्ज्जन|उपसर्ज्जनं
उपसर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A representative, a substitute, any person or thing subordinate or subsidiary.<BR>2 Portent, eclipse.<BR>3 Approaching.<BR>E.<BR>उप inferior, सृज to go, ल्युट् affix. In the first sense, though used as an attributive, it is always neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पण|उपसर्पणं
उपसर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Approaching, advancing to.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, सृप to to, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्य्या|उपसर्या
उपसर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A cow, (fit for the bull.)<BR>E.<BR>उप, सृ to go, यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसार्य्य|उपसार्य|उपसार्य्यः
उपसार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be approached or gone to.<BR>E.<BR>उप, सृ to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसुन्द|उपसुंदः|उपसुन्दः
उपसुन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The name of a demon.<BR>E.<BR>उप, and सुन्द another demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसूर्य्यक|उपसूर्यक|उपसूर्यकं|उपसूर्यकः|उपसूर्य्यकं
उपसूर्य्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, or with, सूर्य्य the sun, कन् affix of identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृत्य
उपसृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having approached.<BR>E.<BR>उप before सृ to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Attended by or accompanied with, jointed. attached, connected, to or with.<BR>2 Eclipsed, (as the sun or moon.)<BR>3 Seized by, possessed by, (evil demons, &c.)<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Coition, copulation.<BR>E.<BR>उप, सृज to create, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवन|उपसेवनं
उपसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Addiction to.<BR>E.<BR>उप and सेव to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कर|उपस्करः
उपस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A condiment, a spice or seasoning, mustard, pepper, &c.<BR>2 An article of household use, as a broom, a basket, &c.<BR>3 Blame, censure.<BR>E.<BR>उप complete, and कर what makes, स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृत
उपस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blamed, censured.<BR>E.<BR>उप and कृत made, स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तम्भ|उपस्तंभ|उपस्तंभः|उपस्तम्भः
उपस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Support of life, as food, sleep, and government of the passions.<BR>E.<BR>उप and स्तभि to stop, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्त्री
उपस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A concubine.<BR>E.<BR>उप and स्त्री a female, a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उपस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 The male or female organs of generation.<BR>2 The haunch or hip.<BR>3 The anus.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, and स्थ what is or stays, ड affix after स्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थपत्र|उपस्थपत्रः
उपस्थपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Indian fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थनिग्रह|उपस्थनिग्रहः
उपस्थनिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Continence.<BR>E.<BR>उपस्थ an organ of generation, and निग्रह restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थातृ
उपस्थातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>उप, स्था to remain, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थान|उपस्थानं
उपस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Proximity, nearness.<BR>2 Obtaining, getting.<BR>3 An assembly.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, स्था to stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानीय
उपस्थानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be stayed with or near.<BR>2 What ought to be near or with.<BR>E.<BR>उप, स्था to stay, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापक
उपस्थापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Placing or bringing near to.<BR>2 Explaining, teaching, a teacher.<BR>3 Causing to obtain.<BR>E.<BR>उप before स्था to be, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापन|उपस्थापनं
उपस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Placing near.<BR>2 Attendance, service.<BR>E.<BR>उप and स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापयितव्य
उपस्थापयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be placed near.<BR>E.<BR>उप before स्था to stay, causal form, तव्य affix; also उपस्थापनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापित
उपस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed near to.<BR>2 Attended.<BR>E.<BR>उप before स्था to stay, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थाय
उपस्थाय<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having approached.<BR>2 Having brought near to or assembled.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, and स्था to stay, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायिन्
उपस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Standing near, being present.<BR>E.<BR>उप before स्था to stay, णिनि affix, युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थित|उपस्थितः
उपस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Approached, arrived.<BR>2 Staying by or near to.<BR>3 Caused, occasioned.<BR>4 Got, received.<BR>5 Felt.<BR>6 Clean, cleansed.<BR>7 Done, accomplished.<BR>8 Known.<BR>E.<BR>उप, स्था to stay, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थिति|उपस्थितिः
उपस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Proximity.<BR>2 Obtaining, getting.<BR>3 Effecting, accomplishing.<BR>4 Arrival.<BR>5 Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>उप before स्था to be, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्श|उपस्पर्शः
उपस्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Touching, contact.<BR>2 Bathing, ablution.<BR>3 Rincing the mouth, sipping water and ejecting it.<BR>E.<BR>उप like, स्पर्श touch, from स्पृश to touch, and अच् affix; or with ल्युट् affix, उपस्पर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शन|उपस्पर्शनं
उपस्पर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृष्ट
उपस्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Touched.<BR>2 Sipped.<BR>E.<BR>उप and स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वत्व|उपस्वत्वं
उपस्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Revenue, profit, what is derived from land or other capital.<BR>E.<BR>उप and खत्व ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत|उपहतः
उपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Destroyed.<BR>2 Injured, impaired, evilly affected by.<BR>3 Struck by lightning, &c.<BR>4 Pained, hurt.<BR>5 Impure.<BR>6 Infected, polluted, vitiated.<BR>E.<BR>उप and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतदृश्
उपहतदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Dazzled, blinded.<BR>E.<BR>उपहत struck, दृश the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतात्मन्
उपहतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्मं)<BR>Agitated, affected as by passion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उपहत and आत्मन् the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरण|उपहरणं
उपहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Offering gifts to superiors.<BR>2 Presenting victims.<BR>3 Distributing or serving out food.<BR>4 Taking, seizing.<BR>E.<BR>उप and हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्त्तव्य|उपहर्तव्य
उपहर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be offered as a victim.<BR>2 To be presented.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हृ to take, तव्य affix; also उपहरणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहर्त्तृ|उपहर्तृ
उपहर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Offering victims, serving out food, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव|उपहवः
उपहव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Calling to.<BR>2 Summoning, invoking.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हृ to call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उपहसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Laughter, laughing.<BR>E.<BR>उप up, हसित laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहार|उपहारः
उपहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A complimentary gift, a present to a superior, &c.<BR>2 A victim, an offering to a deity.<BR>3 Tribute, indemnification, presents as the price of peace.<BR>4 Food distributed to guests, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप, हृ to convey, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिन्
उपहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Giving, presenting.<BR>2 Sacrificing.<BR>E.<BR>उपहार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=159" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालक|उपहालकः
उपहालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a country, part of the peninsula: see कुन्तल.<BR>E.<BR>उप, हाल a king so named, affix कः, the country over which HĀLA reigned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास|उपहासः
उपहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Ridicule, laughing at any one.<BR>E.<BR>उप and हस to laugh, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्य
उपहास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Ridiculous, laughable.<BR>E.<BR>उप and हास्य to be laughed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उपहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed, deposited, placed in or upon.<BR>2 Laid aside.<BR>3 Joined.<BR>4 Mixed.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हा to quit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूय
उपहूय<BR>ind.<BR>Having called or addressed.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, ह्वे to call, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृत
उपहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken, collected, gathered.<BR>2 Offered, presented.<BR>3 Immolated, offered as a victim.<BR>4 Served out as food.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वर|उपह्वरं|उपह्वरः
उपह्वर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Solitary, private.<BR>2 Near.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A car, a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>उप, ह्वृ to bend, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>Muttering prayers, reciting them in a low voice so as not to be overheard.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Solitary, private.<BR>2 Secretly, in a whisper.<BR>E.<BR>उप, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरण|उपाकरणं
उपाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Performance of a preparatory rite before reading the Vedas.<BR>2 Immolation, sacrifice of an animal duly consecrated.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् prefixed to कृ to do, affix, ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्म्मन्|उपाकर्मन्
उपाकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Preparation.<BR>1 A ceremony performed before reading the Vedas.<BR>2 Beginning to read the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding, the affix being मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Attended with evil omens, disastrous, calamitous.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A victim slain or to be slain.<BR>2 A portent, a phaenomenon announcing calamity.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यान|उपाख्यानं
उपाख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A tale, a narrative.<BR>2 Telling, narration.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आख्यान a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागत
उपागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Suffering, feeling.<BR>2 Promised.<BR>3 Approached, arrived.<BR>4 Occurred, happened.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before गम to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम|उपागमः
उपागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Promise, agreement.<BR>2 Approach.<BR>3 Occurrence, arrival.<BR>4 Feeling, suffering.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, आङ् before गम to come, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहण|उपाग्रहणं
उपाग्रहण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>Reading the Vedas after initiation.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before ग्रह to take, ल्युट् affix: see उपाकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाङ्ग|उपांग|उपांगः|उपाङ्गः
उपाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The sectarial mark made with Sandal, &c. on the forehead.<BR>2 Any minor limb or member.<BR>3 Secondary portion of science.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाञ्जन|उपांजन|उपांजनं
उपाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Plastering the ground with cow dung, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अञ्जन anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्त|उपात्तं|उपात्तः
उपात्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Taken, received, gained, got.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>An elephant out of rut.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, आत्त taken, seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तरंहस्
उपात्तरंहस्<BR>mfn. (-हाः-हाः-हः)<BR>Quick, fleet.<BR>E.<BR>उपात्त acquired, रंहस् speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्तशास्त्र
उपात्तशास्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Armed, taking up arms.<BR>E.<BR>उपात्त and शास्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्यय|उपात्ययः
उपात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Neglect or disobedience of ordinances or customs.<BR>2 Disorder or disorderly behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अति prefixed to इण to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादान|उपादानं
उपादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Taking away, abduction, taking.<BR>2 Abstraction, restraining the organs of sense and perception.<BR>3 Cause, motive.<BR>4 Immediate or proximate cause.<BR>5 The formal or distinct form, the material cause.<BR>6 A double meaning, an expression conveying a sense besides that which appears intended.<BR>7 Saying, speaking.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, आदा to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानकारण
उपादानकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A proximate cause.<BR>E.<BR>उपादान and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिका
उपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella lucida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादेय|उपादेयः
उपादेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Acceptable, admissible, to be taken or received.<BR>2 Excellent, admirable.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधि|उपाधिः
उपाधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 Virtuous reflection.<BR>2 A discriminative or distinguishing property, an attribute.<BR>3 Deception, disguise. (In the Vedānta this is especially applied to certain natural forms or properties, considered as disguises of the spirit.)<BR>4 A title, a discriminative appellation, a nickname.<BR>5 Careful or diligent for the support of a family, (always masculine, though with a feminine or neuter substantive.)<BR>6 A purpose, an occasion, an object.<BR>7 (In logic,) A special cause for a general effect.<BR>3 (In rhetoric,) The natural character of species, quality, or action.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before धा to have, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्याय|उपाध्यायः
उपाध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A spiritual preceptor.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A female preceptor.<BR>(-यी or -यानी)<BR>The wife of a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अधि before इण to go, घञ् affix, for the fem. टाप् affix in the first instance, in the second ङीष् with or without आनुक inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह्
उपानह्<BR>f. (-नत्)<BR>A shoe.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before नह to bind, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त|उपांत|उपान्तः
उपान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Near.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The angle of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्तिक|उपांतिक
उपान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Near, proximate, neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>उपान्त and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपान्त्य|उपांत्य|उपान्त्यः
उपान्त्य<BR>m. (-न्त्यः)<BR>The corner of the eye.<BR>n. (-न्त्यं)<BR>Vicinity.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अन्त्य end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाय|उपायः
उपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A means, an expedient, a way.<BR>2 A means of success against an enemy; four are usually enumerated as, sowing dissension, chastisement, conciliation and gifts.<BR>3 Approaching, approach.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before इण to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायज्ञ
उपायज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Fertile in expedients, contriving, providing for.<BR>E.<BR>उपाय and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A present, a complimentary or respectful gift.<BR>2 Approaching, going near to.<BR>3 Engaging in a religious observance.<BR>E.<BR>उप, अय to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिन्
उपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Expert in the use of means.<BR>E.<BR>उपाय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाययोग|उपाययोगः
उपाययोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Application of means, or combination of expedients.<BR>E.<BR>उपाय and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्जन|उपार्जन|उपार्जनं|उपार्ज्जनं
उपार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acquiring property, earning.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अर्ज्जन gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्जित|उपार्जित
उपार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gained, acquired, earned.<BR>E.<BR>उप and अर्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारत
उपारत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Engaged in, occupied by.<BR>2 Frequenting, resorting to.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before रम to sport, क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=160" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम|उपारमः
उपारम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Engaging in.<BR>2 Going to or in.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before रम to sport, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालब्ध
उपालब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Reproached, reviled.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before लभि to hurt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालम्भ|उपालंभ|उपालंभः|उपालम्भः
उपालम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Abuse, reviling.<BR>2 Deferring, delaying.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ्, लभि to injure, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावर्त्तन|उपावर्तन|उपावर्तनं
उपावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Turning round, revolving.<BR>2 Ceasing.<BR>3 Turning back, returning.<BR>4 Approaching.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्त|उपावृत्तः
उपावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Rolling on the ground.<BR>2 Ceased, ceasing, refraining.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A horse rolling himself on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before वृत to be, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रय|उपाश्रयः
उपाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Asylum, support.<BR>2 Reliance, dependance upon.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before श्री to serve, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रित
उपाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Supporting, (literally or figuratively,) bearing, holding, protecting.<BR>2 Relying or depending upon.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, and आश्रित giving support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासक|उपासकः
उपासक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Worshipping, a worshipper.<BR>2 Serving, a servant.<BR>3 A Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>उप before अस to be, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासङ्ग|उपासंग|उपासंगः|उपासङ्गः
उपासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A quiver.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before षञ्ज to embrace, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासन|उपासनं
उपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Archery.<BR>2 Service.<BR>3 A seat.<BR>4 Assembling.<BR>5 Injuring, hurting.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Worship, adoration.<BR>E.<BR>उप, आस to sit, or आङ् before उस to throw or send, affix युच् and fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासित|उपासितः
उपासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Served, honoured, worshipped.<BR>2 Serving, paying worship or service.<BR>E.<BR>उप inferiority, आस to sit or remain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासितृ
उपासितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A worshipper.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before आस to sit, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासीन
उपासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Sitting with or near to.<BR>2 Occupying.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्ति|उपास्तिः
उपास्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>Service, especially of a deity, worship.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आस to sit, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्य
उपास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>To be worshipped or served.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having served or worshipped.<BR>2 Having associated or called together.<BR>E.<BR>उप before आस to sit, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्यमान
उपास्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being served or worshipped, receiving homage.<BR>E.<BR>उप before आस to sit, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहित|उपाहितः
उपाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Joined, annexed.<BR>2 Deposited, placed.<BR>3 Put on, worn.<BR>4 Agreed upon, made or done mutually.<BR>(-तः)<BR>A fiery portent, a meteor, a comet.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before धा to have or hold, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहृत
उपाहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Prepared.<BR>2 Taken, seized.<BR>E.<BR>उप and आङ् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षक
उपेक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Disregarding, neglecting, disdaining.<BR>2 Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>उप before ईक्ष to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षण|उपेक्षणं
उपेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Leaving, abandoning.<BR>5 Disregarding, neglecting, disdaining.<BR>E.<BR>उप and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षा
उपेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Trick, deceit, one of the minor expedients in war.<BR>2 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>3 Dissent.<BR>4 Negligence, neglect.<BR>5 Endurance, patience.<BR>6 Contempt, disdain.<BR>E.<BR>उप, ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षित
उपेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disregarded, disesteemed, neglected, disdained.<BR>E.<BR>उप, and ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Endowed with, possessed of, having, possessing.<BR>2 Arrived at, come to, come near to.<BR>3 Invested.<BR>E.<BR>उप and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतृ
उपेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Contriving, a contriver, one who employs expedients.<BR>2 Approaching, going near to.<BR>E.<BR>उप before इण to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्र|उपेंद्र|उपेंद्रः|उपेन्द्रः
उपेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उप after, इन्द्र INDRA: born subsequently to INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेन्द्रवज्रा
उपेन्द्रवज्रा<BR>f. (-ज्रा)<BR>A species of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be sought, to be had recourse to.<BR>2 To be gone to or approached.<BR>3 To be effected by any means.<BR>E.<BR>उप before इण to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयिवस्
उपेयिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वत्)<BR>1 Accompanied or followed by, associated with, united.<BR>2 Obtained, got.<BR>E.<BR>उप near, इण to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेयुस्
उपेयुस्<BR>mfn. (-यूः-यूः-युः)<BR>Arrived at, gone to.<BR>E.<BR>उप before इण to go, उस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Married.<BR>3 Arrayed, arranged.<BR>E.<BR>उप before, वह to bear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोती
उपोती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra or lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>उप much, उद water, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदकी
उपोदकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदिका
उपोदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra or lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>उप and उद water, कन् and टाप् affixes, and इ substituted for the pen. or ई being substituted उपोदीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्घात|उपोद्घातः
उपोद्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A beginning, a thing begun.<BR>2 An introduction, a preface.<BR>3 An example, an apposite argument or illustration.<BR>4 Analysis, the ascertainment of the elements of which a thing consists.<BR>E.<BR>उप before हन to injure, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषण|उपोषणं
उपोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A fast, fasting.<BR>E.<BR>उप, वस to abide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषित|उपोषितं|उपोषितः
उपोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fasted, fasting.<BR>(-तं)<BR>Fast, fasting.<BR>E.<BR>उप before वस to abide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त|उप्तः
उप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Sown, (as seed.)<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तकृष्ट|उप्तकृष्टं
उप्तकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ploughed after sowing.<BR>E.<BR>उप्त and कृष्ट ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्ति|उप्तिः
उप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Sowing seeds.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तिविद्
उप्तिविद्<BR>m. (-वित् or -विद्)<BR>An agriculturist.<BR>E.<BR>उप्ति and विद who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्तिम
उप्तिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Sown, cultivated.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, क्त्रि affix, and मम् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज
उब्ज<BR>r. 6th cl. (उब्जति)<BR>To be straight:<BR>with नि prefixed,<BR>(न्युब्जति)<BR>To be crooked: this root is also written उब्ज and उद्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ<BR>r. 6th cl. (उभति)<BR>To fill; also उम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ<BR>pron. m. and dual only, (उभौ)<BR>Both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभय|उभयं|उभयः
उभय<BR>pron. (sing. and plu. only,) (-यः-ये)<BR>Both.<BR>E.<BR>उभ and य from या to obtain, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतस्
उभयतस्<BR>ind.<BR>On both sides.<BR>E.<BR>उभय both, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोदत्|उभयतोदन्त्
उभयतोदत्<BR>mf. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Having a double row of teeth, (man, animal, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उभयतस् and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतोमुख
उभयतोमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Looking either way, two-faced.<BR>E.<BR>उमयतस् and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयत्र
उभयत्र<BR>ind.<BR>In both places, on both sides.<BR>E.<BR>उभय and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=161" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयथा
उभयथा<BR>ind.<BR>In both ways.<BR>E.<BR>उभय and थाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयद्युस्
उभयद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>Both days, the day past and to come.<BR>E.<BR>उभय both, द्युस् affix; or with एद्युस् affix, उभयेद्युस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयभागहर
उभयभागहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Applicable to two purposes.<BR>2 Taking two shares or parts.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A medicine that acts in two ways, as an emetic and a purge.<BR>E.<BR>उभय, भाग a part, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयवेतन
उभयवेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Serving two masters, being in the pay of both.<BR>E.<BR>उभय and वेतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयसम्भव|उभयसंभव|उभयसंभवः
उभयसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A dilemma.<BR>E.<BR>उभय both, (conclusions,) सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयानुमत
उभयानुमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Agreed to or accepted mutually, or on both sides.<BR>E.<BR>उभय and अनुमत assented to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयार्थम्
उभयार्थम्<BR>ind.<BR>For a double object, (as for prosperity in earth and happiness in heaven.)<BR>E.<BR>उभय and अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्
उम्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection,<BR>1 Of anger.<BR>2 Interrogation.<BR>3 Promise or assent; and<BR>4 Of cordiality or pacification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम|उमः
उम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A city, a town.<BR>2 A wharf, a landing place.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ or DURGĀ.<BR>2 Light, splendor.<BR>3 Fame, reputation.<BR>4 Turmeric.<BR>5 Flax, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>6 Quiet, tranquillity.<BR>E.<BR>उ particle of calling, and मा prohibition: i. e. “Practise not austerities,” the exclamation addressed to DURGĀ by her mother: in the other senses it may be derived from मा to measure, or मा lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमाकट|उमाकटः
उमाकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The cluster of flax.<BR>E.<BR>उमा flax, कच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमागुरु|उमागुरुः
उमागुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The mountain Himālaya.<BR>E.<BR>उमा the goddess, and गुरु a spiritual teacher: in mythology the personified mountain is the father of UMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमापति|उमापतिः
उमापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>उमा and पति master; the husband of UMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमावन|उमावनं
उमावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A name of Vanapura or Devī Koṭa, (Devi Cote.)<BR>E.<BR>उमा and वन a grove; the residence of UMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमासुत|उमासुतः
उमासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>उमा and सुत a son, the son of PĀRVATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमेश|उमेशः
उमेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A title of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>उमा and ईश a lord: see उमापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्भ
उम्भ<BR>r. 6th cl. (प) (उम्भति)<BR>To fill; also उभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्य|उम्यं
उम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>A field of linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>E.<BR>उमा flax, and यत् affix; also औमीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्वर
उम्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The upper-timber of a door frame.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, above, वृ to screen, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्वी
उम्वी<BR>f. (-म्वी)<BR>The stalks of wheat or barley friend over a fire of wet grass, considered as a tonic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःक्षत
उरःक्षत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Injury of the lungs, breaking a blood vessel, consumption.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् and क्षत lesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःस्थल
उरःस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The breast, the bosom.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरःसूत्रिका
उरःसूत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pearl necklace.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, सूत्र a thread, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर|उरः
उर<BR>Sautra root. (उरति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरग|उरगः
उरग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, and ग who goes, from गम to go, affix ड; also उरङ्ग and उरङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगस्थान|उरगस्थानं
उरगस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The infernal regions below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>उरग and स्थान a place or country; the abode of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगारि|उरगारिः
उरगारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A large crane.<BR>E.<BR>उरग a snake, and अरि the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगाशन|उरगाशनः
उरगाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The gigantic crane.<BR>E.<BR>उरग and अशन food; whose food is of serpents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगेन्द्र|उरगेन्द्रः
उरगेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The king of snakes, ŚEṢA or VĀSUKI.<BR>E.<BR>उरग and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरङ्ग|उरंग|उरंगः|उरङ्गः
उरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A snake, a serpent: see उरग, the affix being खच्; also उरङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरण|उरणः
उरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A ram.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A ewe.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, क्यु affix, leaving ण, and उ substituted for the antepenultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणाक्ष|उरणाक्षः
उरणाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Cassia, (Alata).<BR>E.<BR>उरण ram, अक्ष an eye: the flower being so compared: क being added, also उरणाक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणाख्य|उरणाख्यः
उरणाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>Cassia: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>उरण and आख्या a name; named from the ram; also उरणाख्यक, क being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरभ्र|उरभ्रः
उरभ्र<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>उरु much, भ्रम to wander, ड affix, and the final of उरु dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररी
उररी<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying,<BR>1 Assent.<BR>2 Expansion: (it chiefly occurs in composition.)<BR>E.<BR>वे to weave, ररीक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकार|उररीकारः
उररीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A promise, an agreement.<BR>E.<BR>उररी, कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकृत|उररीकृतः
उररीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed.<BR>2 Spread, diffused.<BR>E.<BR>उररी and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरश्छद|उरश्छदः
उरश्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, and छद a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्
उरस्<BR>mfn. (उराः-उराः-उरः)<BR>Best, excellent.<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The breast, the bosom.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, Uṇādi affix असुन्, the pen. changed to उ; also उर a Sautra root, to go, and असुन् as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिज|उरसिजः
उरसिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, in the 7th case, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिरुह|उरसिरुहः
उरसिरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>उरसि on the breast, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिल|उरसिलः
उरसिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Broad-chested, having a full or broad breast.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्कट|उरस्कटः
उरस्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The sacrificial thread hung round the neck and upon the breast, as it is sometimes worn.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, कट to encompass, अल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्तस्
उरस्तस्<BR>ind.<BR>From the breast.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्त्राण|उरस्त्राणं
उरस्त्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Mail, the breastplate or cuirass.<BR>E.<BR>उरस्, त्रै to preserve, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्य|उरस्यः
उरस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>From the breast.<BR>mf. (-स्यः-स्या)<BR>A legitimate son or daughter, that is, one born from a married couple of the same tribe or cast.<BR>E.<BR>उरस the breast, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्वत्|उरस्वन्त्
उरस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>Broad-chested, full-breasted, strong.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उराह|उराहः
उराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of a pale colour, with dark legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरी
उरी<BR>ind.<BR>A particle, implying, (especially in composition,)<BR>1 Promise, assent.<BR>2 Expansion; also उररी and ऊरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकार
उरीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Promise.<BR>2 Extension.<BR>E.<BR>उरी, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=162" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकृत|उरीकृतः
उरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised.<BR>2 Expanded, spread.<BR>E.<BR>उरी and कृत made; also उररीकृत and ऊरीकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरु|उरुः
उरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Much, excessive.<BR>3 Long.<BR>4 Valuable, precious.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णु to cover, कु Uṇādi affix; ऊ is made short, and ण dropped by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुकाल|उरुकालः
उरुकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A creeper, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR>E.<BR>उरु and काल time, of long growth; also with कन् added उरुकालकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुगाय|उरुगायः
उरुगाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>उरग a snake, इ to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुतर
उरुतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Greater, larger.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुतम
उरुतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Greatest.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and तमप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुताप|उरुतापः
उरुताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Great heat. उरु much, ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुत्व|उरुत्वं
उरुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Magnitude, vastness.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and त्व affix; also उरुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुमार्ग|उरुमार्गः
उरुमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A long road.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and मार्गं a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुरी
उरुरी<BR>ind.<BR>A particle, of,<BR>1 Assent.<BR>2 Expansion: see उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवुक|उरुवुकः
उरुवुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The castor-oil tree, (Palma christi or Ricinus communis).<BR>E.<BR>उरु great or much, (disease,) वै to wither or dry, affix उक deriv. irr. or with ऊक affix उरुवूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवूक|उरुवूकः
उरुवूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुव्यचस्
उरुव्यचस्<BR>m. (-चाः)<BR>A malignant sprite, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>उरु much, व्यच to deceive, असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुसत्त्व
उरुसत्त्व<BR>mfn. (-त्त्वः-त्त्वा-त्त्वं)<BR>Magnanimous, of a lofty nature.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and सत्त्व disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुहार|उरुहारः
उरुहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A valuable necklace.<BR>E.<BR>उरु and हार a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोगामिन्
उरोगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Creeping, crawling, going on the belly as a reptile.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोग्रह|उरोग्रहः
उरोग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Pain of the chest, pleurisy.<BR>E.<BR>उरस and ग्रह what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोघात|उरोघातः
उरोघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Striking or beating the breast.<BR>2 Pain in the chest.<BR>E.<BR>उरस and घात a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरोज|उरोजः
उरोज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the breast, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्ज्जित|उर्जित|उर्ज्जितं
उर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, left.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ज्ज to abandon, क्त affix, and the vowel substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णनाभ|उर्णनाभः|उर्ण्णनाभ
उर्णनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>उर्ण wool, नाभि a navel, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णा
उर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>1 Wool, felt, the hair of camels, &c.<BR>2 A circle of hair between the eye-brows.<BR>E.<BR>उर्णु to cover, ड affix; the word is properly ऊर्णा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द|उर्द्द
उर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (उर्दते)<BR>1 To measure.<BR>2 To play.<BR>3 To be easy or cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्र|उर्द्रः
उर्द्र<BR>m. (-र्द्रः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>उर्द to play, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्व|उर्व
उर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई,) उर्वी (उर्वति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वट|उर्वट|उर्वटः|उर्व्वटः
उर्व्वट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>उरु much, and अट to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वरा|उर्वरा
उर्व्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Fertile soil, yielding every kind of crop.<BR>2 Land in general.<BR>E.<BR>उरू much, ऋ to go, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशी|उर्वशी
उर्व्वशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The name of one of the courtezans of Svarga or INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>उरु great, वश to tame, अच् and ङीष् affixes; also उर्व्वसी and ऊर्व्वसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशीरमण|उर्वशीरमण|उर्वशीरमणः|उर्व्वशीरमणः
उर्व्वशीरमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The name of AILA or PURŪRAVAS, the second king of the line of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>उर्व्वशी, and रमण the gallant or husband of the Apsaras URVAŚĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वशीवल्लभ|उर्वशीवल्लभ|उर्वशीवल्लभः|उर्व्वशीवल्लभः
उर्व्वशीवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A name of AILA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, वल्लभ a friend, a lover, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वारु|उर्वारु|उर्वारुः|उर्व्वारुः
उर्व्वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (cucumis^1 utilatissimus): see इर्व्वारु.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वी|उर्वी
उर्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>उरु great, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वीधर|उर्वीधर|उर्वीधरः
उर्व्वीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 The serpent ŚEṢA.<BR>E.<BR>उर्व्वी the earth, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्वीरुह|उर्वीरुह|उर्वीरुहः
उर्व्वीरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>उर्व्वी and रुह what grows on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल|उलः
उल<BR>Sautra root, (उलति)<BR>to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलप|उलपः
उलप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 A creeping plant, a spreading creeper.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A kind of grass or reed, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>वल to be strong, अपच् affix; also उलुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलिन्द|उलिंदः|उलिन्दः
उलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The name of a country.<BR>E.<BR>उल to burn, किन्दच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुप|उलुपः
उलुप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A spreading creeper.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A reed, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>वल to be strong, उपच् affix; also उलप and उलूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुपिन्
उलुपिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A porpoise, or fish resembling it.<BR>E.<BR>उ for उत् up, लुप to disturb, &c. णिनि affix; also उलूपिन्, ऊलुपिन्, उल्लुपिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूक|उलूकं|उलूकः
उलूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An owl.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>3 One of the heroes of the Mahābhārata.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>वल to be strong, ऊकः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखल|उलूखलं|उलूखलः
उलूखल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A wooden mortar used for cleaning rice.<BR>2 Bdellium, a gummy substance.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, up ख empty, and ल what takes: or उदू for उद्, and खल what goes; द is changed to लः see उदूखल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलिक
उलूखलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Pounded in a mortar, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>उलूखल and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलक|उलूखलकं
उलूखलक<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of Bdellium, a gummy substance, or the plant which produces it.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूत|उलूतः
उलूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A large snake, the Boa.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, लू to cut, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूप
उलूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A spreading creeper.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A sort of grass.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A nymph of Pātāla married to ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>see उलुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूपिन्
उलूपिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A porpoise, or fish resembling it: see उलुपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्का
उल्का<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>1 A firebrand.<BR>2 Fire falling from heaven, a meteor, &c.<BR>3 Flame.<BR>4 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, कक् Uṇādi affix, ल substituted for ष; or the root is a Sautra root, उल to burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्कामुख|उल्कामुखः
उल्कामुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A ghost or goblin, with a face of fire, who eats what is vomited, and who was a negligent Brahman in his lifetime.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A fox.<BR>E.<BR>उल्का a flame, मुख a mouth, ङीष् affix; the latter from the redness of his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्मुक|उल्मुकं|उल्मुकः
उल्मुक<BR>(-कः)<BR>1 A firebrand, wood burning or burnt as charcoal.<BR>2 The name of a prince.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, मुक Uṇādi affix, घ is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लकसन|उल्लकसनं
उल्लकसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Horripilation, erection of the hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, लष to injure, ल्युट् affix, and क inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लग्न
उल्लग्न<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>The Lagna of any particular place.<BR>E.<BR>उत् over, लग्न the entrance of the sun into a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घन|उल्लंघन|उल्लंघनं|उल्लङ्घनं
उल्लङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Leaping or passing over or beyond.<BR>2 Exceeding, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लघि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घित|उल्लंघित
उल्लङ्घित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Passed over or beyond, jumped across.<BR>2 Exceeded, transgressed.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लघि to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घ्य|उल्लंघ्य
उल्लङ्घ्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्घ्यः-ङ्घ्या-ङ्घ्यं)<BR>1 To be crossed, to be passed over or beyond.<BR>2 To be disregarded or neglected.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लघि to go, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=163" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लङ्घितशासन|उल्लंघितशासन
उल्लङ्घितशासन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Refractory, rebellious, disobedient.<BR>E.<BR>उल्लङ्घित and शासन order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लल|उल्ललः
उल्लल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, लल to tremble, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललत्
उल्ललत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>2 Moving irregularly or convulsively.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लल to tremble, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललित|उल्ललितः
उल्ललित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, लल to tremble, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस
उल्लस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Bright, shining.<BR>2 Sporting, merry, happy.<BR>3 Going out, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लस to shine, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसत्
उल्लसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Brilliant, shining.<BR>2 Sporting, wantoning.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लस to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसता
उल्लसता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Splendor, brilliancy.<BR>2 Mirth, happiness.<BR>3 Going forth, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>उल्लस what shines, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसित
उल्लसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bright, splendid, shining.<BR>2 Happy.<BR>3 Ejected, brought to the top or surface.<BR>4 Drawn up.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लस to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाघ|उल्लाघः
उल्लाघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>1 Recovered from sickness, convalescent.<BR>2 Dextrous, clever, intelligent.<BR>3 Pure.<BR>4 Happy, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, लाघ to be able, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाप|उल्लापः
उल्लाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Change of voice in grief, sickness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उद् implying alteration, लप to speak, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लास|उल्लासः
उल्लास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Joy, happiness.<BR>2 Light, splendor.<BR>3 Increase.<BR>4 The division of a book, a chapter, a section.<BR>E.<BR>उद् much, लस to shine, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासित
उल्लासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delighted, rejoicing.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लस to shine, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखत्
उल्लिखत्<BR>mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्)<BR>1 Painting, writing.<BR>2 Making lines or streaks, above or on high.<BR>3 Scratching, scraping.<BR>4 Bearing, raising.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लिख to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखित|उल्लिखितः
उल्लिखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thrown up, tossed.<BR>2 Pared, made thin.<BR>3 Scraped, scratched.<BR>4 Painted, delineated.<BR>5 Written over or above.<BR>E.<BR>उद् and लिखित written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिङ्गित|उल्लिंगित
उल्लिङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Discriminated, distinguished, known.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, before लिगि to mark, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुञ्चन|उल्लुंचन|उल्लुंचनं
उल्लुञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Plucking out hair.<BR>2 Cutting the hair.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, लिचि to cut, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेख|उल्लेखः
उल्लेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 Utterance, pronunciation.<BR>2 Speaking.<BR>E.<BR>उद् before लिख to write, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखन|उल्लेखनं
उल्लेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Raising up, elevating.<BR>2 Vomiting.<BR>3 Digging.<BR>4 Scraping, paring.<BR>5 Uttering, utterance.<BR>6 Writing, painting.<BR>E.<BR>उद्, लिखि to write, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोच|उल्लोचः
उल्लोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>An awning, a canopy.<BR>E.<BR>उद् above, लोच to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोल|उल्लोलः
उल्लोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A surge, a large wave or billow.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, लोड to be furious, अच् affix, and ड becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्व|उल्वं
उल्व<BR>n. (-ल्वः)<BR>1 The womb.<BR>2 The embryo.<BR>3 The membranes investing the foetus.<BR>4 A cavity.<BR>E.<BR>उच to accumulate, कन् Uṇādi affix, and च becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्वण|उल्वणं
उल्वण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Apparent, evident.<BR>2 Much, exceeding.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An excess of either of the humors of the body, bile, phlegm or wind.<BR>E.<BR>उद् up, ल्वी to join, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उव्ज
उव्ज<BR>r. 6th cl. (उव्जति)<BR>To be straight: see उब्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशत्|उशन्त्
उशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शती-शत्)<BR>Inauspicious, (as discourse.)<BR>E.<BR>उव to burn, शतृ part. affix; also उषत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशनस्
उशनस्<BR>m. (-नाः)<BR>A name of ŚUKRA, regent of the planet Venus.<BR>E.<BR>वस to wish, कनसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशिज्
उशिज्<BR>m. (-शिक्)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Ghee or boiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>वस to wish, Uṇādi affix इज्, and व changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशी
उशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>वश to wish, ई Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीनर|उशीनरः
उशीनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The name of a country, (Candahar.)<BR>2 A king, the father of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>उशी desire, नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उशीर|उशीरं|उशीरः
उशीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum).<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of grass, a small sort of Saccharum.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire, ईरन् Uṇādi affix; also with कन् added उशीरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
उष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ओषति)<BR>To burn. (उ,) उषु (ओषति). To kill or injure: with प्र prefixed, this root makes प्रोषति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष|उषं|उषः
उष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Early morning, dawn, day-break.<BR>2 A libidinous man.<BR>3 Bdellium.<BR>4 Saline earth.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 Burning, scorching.<BR>3 A proper name, the wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>4 Night.<BR>5 A pot; also उखा.<BR>ind.<BR>The end of night or day-break.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, क affix and fem. do. टाप्; the affix of the particle is का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषण|उषणं
उषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Long pepper.<BR>2 Chai, (Piper chavya.)<BR>3 Dried ginger.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, कनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषत्|उषन्त्
उषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षती-षत्)<BR>Inauspicious, (as discourse): see उशत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषप|उषपः
उषप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>उप to burn, पच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषर्बुध|उषर्बुधः
उषर्बुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>उषस् dawn, बुध to know, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्
उषस्<BR>n. (-षः)<BR>1 The dawn, morning.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The end of the day. twilight.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, असि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषस्य
उषस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Belonging to the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>उषस् and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषाकल|उषाकलः
उषाकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>उषा dawn, कल to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषापति|उषापतिः
उषापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of ANIRUDDHA, the son of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>उषा and पति a lord, a master: the husband of UṢĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषारमण|उषारमणः
उषारमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>ANIRUDDHA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>उषा and रमण a husband, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित|उषितः
उषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stale.<BR>2 Burnt.<BR>3 Quick, expeditious.<BR>4 Fixed, remaining in or on.<BR>5 Inhabited, dwelt.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, or वस to abide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषितङ्गवीन|उषितंगवीन|उषितङ्गवीनः
उषितङ्गवीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Formerly inhabited by cattle.<BR>E.<BR>उषित inhabited, गवीन appertaining to cattle, from गो with खश् affix: see अशितङ्गवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषित्वा
उषित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having resided in.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषीर|उषीरं|उषीरः
उषीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire, ईरन affix, श becomes षः see उशीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उषेश|उषेशः
उषेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>उषा and ईश lord, husband: see उषापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्य
उष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Fit to be dressed in a pot, or boiled, (meat, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उषा a pot, यत् affix; also उख्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्र|उष्ट्रः
उष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A cart, a vehicle of burthen.<BR>f. (-ष्ट्री or -ष्ट्रिका)<BR>An earthen vessel.<BR>2 A she camel.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, and ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi affix, fem. ङीष्, or ठाप् with इक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रकाण्डी
उष्ट्रकाण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A flower of a red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रक्रोशिन्
उष्ट्रक्रोशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Making a noise like a camel.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र and क्रुश to cry, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=164" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रगोयुग
उष्ट्रगोयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A pair of camels.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र and गोयुग a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रग्रीव|उष्ट्रग्रीवः
उष्ट्रग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Hemorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र and ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रधूसरपुच्छिका
उष्ट्रधूसरपुच्छिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रपादिका
उष्ट्रपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Arabian jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र and पाद a foot: from the shape of its flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रयान
उष्ट्रयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A camel litter, a vehicle drawn or borne by camels.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ट्रशिरोधर|उष्ट्रशिरोधरं|उष्ट्रशिरोधरः
उष्ट्रशिरोधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Piles, hemorrhoids, bleeding piles.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र a camel, शिरस् head, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्ण|उष्णः
उष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>1 Hot, warm.<BR>2 Pungent, acrid.<BR>3 Sharp, active.<BR>4 Impetuous, warm, passionate.<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>1 The hot season, (June and July.)<BR>2 Heat, warmth.<BR>3 Sunshine.<BR>4 An onion.<BR>5 A sigh.<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>1 Consumption.<BR>2 Bile.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, णक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णक|उष्णकः
उष्णक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Sharp, smart, active.<BR>2 Suffering pain.<BR>3 Bent, inclining, stooping.<BR>4 Warming, heating.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The hot season, two months about June and July.<BR>2 Revolving, turning round.<BR>E.<BR>वुन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णता
उष्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Heat, warmth.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to उष्ण; also with त्व, उष्णत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णनदी
उष्णनदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The river of hell.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण hot, नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णरश्मि|उष्णरश्मिः
उष्णरश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवारण|उष्णवारणः
उष्णवारण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>An umbrella or parasol, a Catta.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण heat, and वृ to screen, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवाष्प
उष्णवाष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 Hot vapour, steam.<BR>2 Tears.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and वाष्प vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णवीर्य्य|उष्णवीर्य|उष्णवीर्यः|उष्णवीर्य्यः
उष्णवीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 The gangetic porpoise.<BR>2 Any hot or pungent substance.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण heat, वीर्य्य power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णांशु|उष्णांशुः
उष्णांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णागम|उष्णागमः
उष्णागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The hot season, consisting of two months, about June and July.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण heat, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णाभिगम|उष्णाभिगमः
उष्णाभिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The hot season, as above.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and अभिगम approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णालु
उष्णालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Suffering from heat.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and आलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णासह|उष्णासहः
उष्णासह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The cold season.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण warmth, असह intolerant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिका
उष्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Rice gruel.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण warm (rice,) वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णिह्
उष्णिह्<BR>f. (-ष्णिक्)<BR>A verse of four lines, each line being of seven syllables: it is used chiefly in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>उत् prefixed to ष्णिह to be unctuous or bland, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीष|उष्णीषं|उष्णीषः
उष्णीष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>1 A turban.<BR>2 A diadem.<BR>3 A distinguishing cognate mark.<BR>4 The curly hair with which a Buddha is born, and which indicates his future sanctity.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण heat, ईष to oppose or injure, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णीषधारिन्
उष्णीषधारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Turbaned.<BR>E.<BR>उष्णीष and धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णोदक|उष्णोदकं
उष्णोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Warm or hot water.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्णोपगम|उष्णोपगमः
उष्णोपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The hot season, summer.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण, उपगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्म|उष्मं|उष्मः
उष्म<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 The hot season, (June and July.)<BR>2 Spring, (April and May.)<BR>3 Heat.<BR>4 Anger, warmth of temper.<BR>5 Ardor, eagerness.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, मक् affix; also with कन् affix उष्मक, also उष्ण and उष्णक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मन्
उष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>1 The hot season.<BR>2 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मपा
उष्मपा<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>A heavenly spirit of an inferior order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मभास्
उष्मभास्<BR>m. (-भाः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>उष्म and भास् what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मस्वेद|उष्मस्वेदः
उष्मस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A vapour bath.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ण and स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उष्मागम|उष्मागमः
उष्मागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The hot season: see उष्णागम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्र|उस्रः
उस्र<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>f. (-स्रा)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 A plant, (Anthericum tuberosum, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उस्रधन्वन्
उस्रधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उह
उह<BR>r. 1st cl. (इर) उहिर् (ओहति) or (इ) उहि (उंहति)<BR>1 To hurt or give pain.<BR>2 To kill, to destroy.<BR>With वि and अप prefixed,<BR>to destroy, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उहान|उहानः
उहान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ<BR>The sixth vowel of the Sanscrit alphabet, corresponding to U long, and having the sound of that letter in the word rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊ
ऊ<BR>ind.<BR>1 An incipient particle.<BR>2 An interjection of compassion.<BR>3 Of regard.<BR>m. (ऊः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, क्विप् affix, व becomes ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढ|ऊढः
ऊढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Married.<BR>2 Carried as a load or burthen.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A bride, a wife espoused according to the ritual.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊढकङ्कट|ऊढकंकट|ऊढकङ्कटः
ऊढकङ्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Armed, mailed.<BR>E.<BR>ऊढ borne, कङ्कट armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊत|ऊतं
ऊत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Woven.<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to weave, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊति|ऊतिः
ऊति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Preserving, protecting.<BR>2 Sewing, weaving.<BR>3 Distilling.<BR>4 Speed.<BR>5 Sport, play.<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to weave, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधन्य|ऊधन्यं
ऊधन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Produced from the udder, milk, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऊधस, यत् affix, and न substituted for स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्
ऊधस्<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>An udder.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, असि affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊधस्य|ऊधस्यं
ऊधस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>ऊधस् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊन|ऊनं
ऊन<BR>r. 10th cl. (न) ऊनत् (ऊनयति)<BR>1 To deduct or lessen.<BR>2 To mete out in small quantities.<BR>3 To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊन|ऊनं
ऊन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Less in number, size or degree, as fewer, smaller, inferior, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऊन to deduct, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊम|ऊमं|ऊमः
ऊम<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of,<BR>1 Interrogation.<BR>2 Anger.<BR>3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>4 Arrogance.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A city.<BR>E.<BR>अव to preserve, &c. मन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊय
ऊय<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई) ऊयी (ऊयते)<BR>To sew, to weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊररी
ऊररी<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of assent.<BR>3 Of expansion.<BR>E.<BR>ऊय to sew, &c. ररोक affix: see उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरव्य|ऊरव्यः
ऊरव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A man of the third cast or tribe, the merchant or husbandman, the Vaiśya.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु a thigh, and यत् affix; being born from the thighs of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरी
ऊरी<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of,<BR>1 Assent.<BR>2 Of expansion: see उरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरीकृत|ऊरीकृतः
ऊरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised.<BR>2 Expanded.<BR>E.<BR>उरी and कृत made: see उरीकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरु|ऊरुः
ऊरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The thigh.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णु to cover, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=165" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुग्लानि|ऊरुग्लानिः
ऊरुग्लानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Weakness of the thigh.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and ग्लानि debility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुज|ऊरुजः
ऊरुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Vaiśya or man of the third tribe.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and ज born; from the thigh of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुदध्र
ऊरुदध्र<BR>mfn. (-ध्नः-ध्नी-ध्नं)<BR>As high as the thigh.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and दध्नच् affix; also ऊरुद्वयस and ऊरुमात्र, with द्वयसच् and मात्रच् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुपर्व्वन्|ऊरुपर्वन्
ऊरुपर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>The knee.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुरी
ऊरुरी<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of,<BR>1 Promise.<BR>2 Of expansion: see ऊररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊरुस्तम्भ|ऊरुस्तम्भः
ऊरुस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Paralysis of the lower extremities.<BR>2 Rheumatism of the thigh.<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>The plantain tree.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्
ऊर्ज्<BR>f. (-ऊर्क्)<BR>Strength, vigour.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज to be strong, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज|ऊर्जः|ऊर्ज्ज|ऊर्ज्जं|ऊर्ज्जः
ऊर्ज<BR>r. 10th cl. (ऊर्जयति)<BR>1 To be strong.<BR>2 To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज|ऊर्जः|ऊर्ज्ज|ऊर्ज्जं|ऊर्ज्जः
ऊर्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः)<BR>1 The month Kārttika, (Oct.-Nov.)<BR>2 Effort, exertion.<BR>3 Power, strength.<BR>4 Breath, breathing.<BR>5 Procreative power.<BR>n. (-र्जं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज to live, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्जस्वत्|ऊर्जस्वत्|ऊर्जस्वन्त्
ऊर्ज्जस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>Strong, vigorous.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज्ज and मतुप् affix, with स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्वल|ऊर्ज्जस्वलः
ऊर्जस्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज strength, वलच् affix, and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्जस्विन्
ऊर्जस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Very strong.<BR>n. (-स्वि)<BR>Speaking of any thing with disdain, (a figure of rhetoric.)<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज and विनि affix, स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्जित|ऊर्जित
ऊर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Powerful, mighty, great, excellent.<BR>2 Exceeding, much.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज्ज to be strong, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्ज्जिताश्रय|ऊर्जिताश्रय
ऊर्ज्जिताश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Spirited, magnanimous.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज्जित great, आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णनाभ|ऊर्णनाभः|ऊर्ण्णनाभ
ऊर्णनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ण wool, नाभि the navel, ड affix; also ऊर्णनाभि, the final being retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णा
ऊर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>1 Wool, felt, &c. the hair of sheep, deer, camels, &c.<BR>2 A circle of the hair between the eye-brows, considered as a token of greatness.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णु to cover, ड and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णामय|ऊर्ण्णामय
ऊर्णामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Wollen, made of wool.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णा and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णायु|ऊर्णायुः|ऊर्ण्णायु
ऊर्णायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A woollen blanket.<BR>2 A ram.<BR>3 A spider.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णा wool, युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णु|ऊर्ण्णु
ऊर्णु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ञ) ऊर्णुज (ऊर्णौति ऊर्णोति or ऊर्णुते)<BR>To cover, hide, conceal, &c. with प्र prefixed प्रोर्णौति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्णुत
ऊर्णुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णु and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्दर|ऊर्दर|ऊर्दरं|ऊर्दरः|ऊर्द्दरः
ऊर्द्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hero, a champion.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa, a goblin or fiend.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्ज to be strong. दरल् Uṇādi affix; ज is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध
ऊर्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>1 Above, upper.<BR>2 High, elevated.<BR>3 Abandoned: see ऊर्द्ध्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्धक
ऊर्द्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of drum: see ऊर्द्ध्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्व
ऊर्द्ध्व<BR>mfn. (-ऊर्द्ध्वः-ऊर्द्ध्वा-ऊर्द्ध्वं)<BR>1 Above, superior, upper.<BR>2 High.<BR>3 Abandoned.<BR>4 After, subsequent.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर् substituted for उद् above, हा to leave, and ड्व affix, or with ड only ऊर्द्ध्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वक
ऊर्द्ध्वक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of drum.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व or ऊर्द्ध्व up, and क what sounds; from its making a loud noise, or being elevated in playing; also ऊर्द्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वकाय
ऊर्द्ध्वकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The upper part of the body.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वग
ऊर्द्ध्वग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going up or above; ascending, hovering.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and ग what goes; also ऊर्द्ध्वगामिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगत
ऊर्द्ध्वगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone up, risen, ascended.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगति
ऊर्द्ध्वगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Ascent, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगपुर
ऊर्द्ध्वगपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA, who with his subjects is supposed to be suspended in the atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्वग going above, and पुर a city: see हरिश्चन्द्रपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वगम
ऊर्द्ध्वगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Upward motion of any kind.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and गम going; also ऊर्द्ध्वगति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वचरण
ऊर्द्ध्वचरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Supine, heels upwards.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and चरण the foot; also ऊर्द्ध्वपाद, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वजानु
ऊर्द्ध्वजानु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>1 Thick-kneed, long-shanked.<BR>2 Sitting on the hams.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व high, large, जानु the knee, and with कन् added ऊर्द्ध्वजानुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञ
ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Thick-kneed: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and ज्ञ substituted for जानु; also ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञु
ऊर्द्ध्वज्ञु<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वत्व
ऊर्द्ध्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Height, elevation.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to ऊर्द्ध्व; also with तल्, ऊर्द्ध्वता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वदृष्टि
ऊर्द्ध्वदृष्टि<BR>mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि)<BR>Looking up or upwards.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वदेव
ऊर्द्ध्वदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व superior, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वन्दम
ऊर्द्ध्वन्दम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Exalted, elevated.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व upper, दम to tame, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपातन
ऊर्द्ध्वपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Causing to ascend.<BR>2 Sublimation.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and पातन causing to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपात्र
ऊर्द्ध्वपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A sacrificial vessel.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपाद
ऊर्द्ध्वपाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Heels upwards.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A fabulous animal with eight legs.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व superior, exceeding, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वपुण्ड्र
ऊर्द्ध्वपुण्ड्र<BR>m. (-ण्ड्रः)<BR>A perpendicular line on the forehead made with Sandal, &c. a Vaiṣṇava mark.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, पुण्ड्र a similar mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वबाहु
ऊर्द्ध्वबाहु<BR>n. (-हुः)<BR>An ascetic, one who holds his arms above his head constantly till they are fixed in that position.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and वाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वरेतस्
ऊर्द्ध्वरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Of BHĪṢMA.<BR>3 A description of saint, one who lives in perpetual chastity.<BR>E.<BR>उर्द्ध्व up, above, and रेतस् semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वलिङ्ग
ऊर्द्ध्वलिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and लिङ्ग the generative organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वलोक
ऊर्द्ध्वलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Svarga, the heaven of INDRA or paradise.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व, and लोक a world: the world above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववर्त्मन्
ऊर्द्ध्ववर्त्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The atmosphere, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, and वर्त्मन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववायु
ऊर्द्ध्ववायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The wind in the upper part of the body.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्ववृत
ऊर्द्ध्ववृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Put on, above or over the head.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and वृत worn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वशोधन
ऊर्द्ध्वशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and शोधन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वस्थ
ऊर्द्ध्वस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Above, superior, placed on high; also ऊर्द्ध्वस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वस्थिति
ऊर्द्ध्वस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A horse's back, the part where the rider sits.<BR>2 Elevation, superiority.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, and स्थिति being, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=166" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्द्ध्वासित
ऊर्द्ध्वासित<BR>m. (तः)<BR>The name of a vegetable, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध्व above, आसित thrown: raised above other fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मि|ऊर्मि|ऊर्मिः|ऊर्म्मिः
ऊर्म्मि<BR>mf. (-र्म्मिः) or f. only, (-र्म्मी)<BR>1 A wave.<BR>2 A current, the flowing of water.<BR>3 A fold or plait in a garment.<BR>4 Light, manifestation.<BR>5 Speed, velocity.<BR>6 Mental suffering, distress, uneasiness.<BR>7 Pain.<BR>8 Missing, regretting.<BR>9 Human infirmity, as grief, illusion, hunger, thirst, decay, death.<BR>10 Association.<BR>11 Number, quantity.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, मि Uṇādi affix, ऊ substituted for the initial letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिका|ऊर्मिका
ऊर्म्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A finger ring.<BR>2 A plait or fold in a garment.<BR>3 A wave.<BR>4 Regret, sorrowing for any thing lost.<BR>5 The buzzing of a bee.<BR>E.<BR>as the preceding, कन्, &c. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमत्|ऊर्मिमत्|ऊर्मिमन्त्
ऊर्म्मिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Crooked.<BR>2 Wavy, billowy.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्म्मि a wave, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमता
ऊर्म्मिमता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Undulation.<BR>2 Crookedness.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्म्मिमत् and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्म्मिमालिन्|ऊर्मिमालिन्
ऊर्म्मिमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्म्मि, माला a necklace, and इनि affix; whose necklace is the surge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वरा|ऊर्वरा
ऊर्व्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Fertile soil, land bearing any and every crop: see उर्व्वरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वष्ठीवत्
ऊर्व्वष्ठीवत्<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>The thigh and knee.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरु and अष्ठीवत् the knee pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्वसी
ऊर्व्वसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A nymph of Svarga: see उर्व्वशी. Also written ऊर्व्वशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्व्व्यङ्ग|ऊर्व्यङ्ग|ऊर्व्यंगं|ऊर्व्यङ्गं
ऊर्व्व्यङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्व्वी for उर्व्वी the earth, and अङ्ग body: earth-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊर्षा
ऊर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratum): see देवताडक.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to rain, अङ् and टाप् affixes, व changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलूक|ऊलूकः
ऊलूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>वल to be strong, and ऊक affix; व becomes ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊलूपिन्
ऊलूपिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A porpoise: see उलुपिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष|ऊषं|ऊषः
ऊष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊषति)<BR>To be diseased or disordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊष|ऊषं|ऊषः
ऊष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Salt ground, soil impregnated with saline particles.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>ऊष to be or make sick, क affix, fem. टाप्: see उषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषक|ऊषकं
ऊषक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषण|ऊषणं|ऊषणः
ऊषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Long pepper: see उषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषर|ऊषरः
ऊषर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A spot with saline soil.<BR>E.<BR>ऊस such soil, रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊषवत्|ऊषवन्त्
ऊषवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Consisting of saline soil, (a place, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>ऊष and poss. affix मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
ऊह<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊहते)<BR>To reason, to apprehend and infer:<BR>with प्र and वि,<BR>to intermit;<BR>with वि,<BR>to array in order of battle;<BR>with सम् prefixed,<BR>(समूहति or -ते)<BR>to assemble or be assembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह|ऊहः
ऊह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Reasoning.<BR>2 Completing a defective sentence or verse, supplying an ellipsis.<BR>E.<BR>ऊह to deliberate, घञ् affix, or with ल्युट् affix, ऊहन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहन|ऊहनं
ऊहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reasoning, inferring, concluding.<BR>E.<BR>ऊह and ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहनी
ऊहनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A broom.<BR>E.<BR>वह to carry, ल्युट् and ङीष् affixes; व is changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊहिन्
ऊहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Who or what reasons.<BR>2 Who or what assembles.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>An assemblage, a collection.<BR>E.<BR>ऊह reasoning, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऊह्य
ऊह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be investigated, to be supplied.<BR>E.<BR>ऊह to reason, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ<BR>The seventh vowel of the Sanscrit alphabet, and peculiar to it. It corresponds in sound with RI, in merrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ<BR>f. (आ)<BR>A name of ADITI, the mother of the gods.<BR>ind.<BR>1 An expression of abuse.<BR>2 An articulate sound.<BR>3 An expression of laughter.<BR>4 A sound inarticulate or reiterated as in stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋ
ऋ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋच्छति)<BR>1 To go, to approach.<BR>2 To gain, to acquire; (the radical is changed to ऋछ before an initial mute श.)<BR>r. 3rd cl. (ईयर्त्ति)<BR>To go; (some confine this root to the Vedas.)<BR>r. 5th cl. (ऋणोति)<BR>To kill, to injure; also रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थ|ऋक्थं
ऋक्थ<BR>m. (-क्थं)<BR>1 Wealth, possessions, property.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच to praise, थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थग्रहण
ऋक्थग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Receiving or inheriting property.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थग्राह|ऋक्थग्राहः
ऋक्थग्राह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Who inherits or takes property.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Inheriting or receiving property.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and ग्रह to take, with घञ् affix; also with णिनि, ऋक्थग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थजात
ऋक्थजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Accumulated, added, (as property.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थभाग|ऋक्थभागः
ऋक्थभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Division of property, inheritance, partition.<BR>2 A share.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and भाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थभागिन्
ऋक्थभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>An heir, a coheir, inheriting or sharing property.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थहर
ऋक्थहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>An heir, a coheir.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्थहारिन्
ऋक्थहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>An heir, inheriting or sharing property.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्थ and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्शत
ऋक्शत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A hundred texts.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच् a prayer, and शत a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्संहिता
ऋक्संहिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The collection of the prayers and hymns of the Ṛk Veda.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच् and संहिता compendium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष<BR>r. 5th cl. (ऋक्ष्णोति)<BR>To kill, to hurt or seek to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्ष|ऋक्षं|ऋक्षः
ऋक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Pierced, cut, divided.<BR>mn. (-क्षः-क्षं)<BR>A star, a constellation.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A mountain in the peninsula, the temporary residence of RĀMA.<BR>2 A bear.<BR>3 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, Uṇādi affix स, the radical final then becomes क, and स becomes ष; and क and ष form the compound letter क्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षगन्धा
ऋक्षगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 A kind of potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>2 Another sort, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्ष a bear, and गन्ध smell, smelling like a bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षगन्धिका
ऋक्षगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Convolvulus paniculatus, the pale sort): see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षर|ऋक्षरं|ऋक्षरः
ऋक्षर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A shower, a stream.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A family priest.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, and सर Uṇādi affix: see the derivation of ऋक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षविभावन
ऋक्षविभावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Observing or seeing the stars.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्ष and विभावन noticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षेश|ऋक्षेशः
ऋक्षेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>ऋक्ष a star, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋक्षेष्टि|ऋक्षेष्टिः
ऋक्षेष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Offering worship to the planets and stars.<BR>E.<BR>ऋल and इष्टि worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्वेद|ऋग्वेदः
ऋग्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The Ṛc or Ṛk Veda, the first of the four Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच् and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=167" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋग्वेदविद्
ऋग्वेदविद्<BR>m. (-वित् or -विद्)<BR>A Brahman familiar with the Ṛk Veda.<BR>E.<BR>ऋग्वेद and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच
ऋच<BR>r. 6th cl. (ऋचति)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>2 To cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्
ऋच्<BR>f. (ऋक्)<BR>1 Ṛk or Ṛg Veda, one of the four principal religious books of the Hindus.<BR>2 A stanza of a prayer or hymn of the Rig Veda.<BR>3 A mantra, a magical invocation, a mystical prayer.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच to praise, affix क्विप्, celebrating the praises of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋचीष|ऋचीषं|ऋचीषः
ऋचीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A frying pan.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>ऋज to fry, ईषन् affix, च substituted for ज; also ऋजीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छ
ऋच्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (ऋच्छति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To fail in faculties.<BR>3 To become hard or stiff, to congeal.<BR>4 To incur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋच्छरा
ऋच्छरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A harlot, a courtezan.<BR>E.<BR>ऋच्छ to go, अर Uṇādi affix, and टाप् for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज
ऋज<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्जते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To stand or be firm.<BR>3 To be strong.<BR>4 To acquire, to gain or earn.<BR>5 To live.<BR>With a prefix ending in अ, the radical vowel is changed to आर, as in the pass. voice,<BR>(प्रार्ज्यते.)<BR>(इ) ऋजि (ऋजते)<BR>To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीक|ऋजीकः
ऋजीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>ऋज and कीकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजीष|ऋजीषं
ऋजीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 A frying pan.<BR>2 A hell.<BR>E.<BR>ऋज to fry, ईषन् Uṇādi affix: see ऋचीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजु
ऋजु<BR>mfn. (-जुः-जुः-जु)<BR>1 Straight.<BR>2 Straight metaphorically, as in morals, upright, honest.<BR>E.<BR>ऋज to go, affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजुकाय|ऋजुकायः
ऋजुकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of the saint KAŚYAPA.<BR>E.<BR>ऋजु straight, काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजुता
ऋजुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Uprightness, sincerity.<BR>2 Straightness.<BR>E.<BR>ऋजु with तल् affix; also with त्व, ऋजुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूकरण
ऋजूकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Straightening.<BR>E.<BR>ऋजु and करण making; the vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋजूकृत
ऋजूकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made straight.<BR>E.<BR>ऋजू and कृत made; the vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋज्र|ऋज्रः
ऋज्र<BR>m. (-ज्रः)<BR>A leader.<BR>E.<BR>ऋज to go, रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋञ्जसान|ऋंजसान|ऋञ्जसानः
ऋञ्जसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>ऋजि to go, शानच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋण|ऋणं
ऋण<BR>r. 8th cl. (उ) ऋणु (अर्णोति or अर्णुते, ऋणोति or -णुते)<BR>To go; according to some it is ऋन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋण|ऋणं
ऋण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Debt.<BR>2 A fort, a strong hold.<BR>3 (In algebra,) Negative quantity, minus.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणकर्त्तृ|ऋणकर्तृ
ऋणकर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Getting into debt, indebted.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रस्त
ऋणग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Indebted, involved in debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्रह|ऋणग्रहः
ऋणग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Borrowing.<BR>2 A borrower.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and ग्र taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणग्राहिन्
ऋणग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Borrowing, a borrower.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदातृ
ऋणदातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>One who pays a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and दातृ who gives. Also ऋणद (-दः-दा-दं) and ऋणदायिन् (-यी-यिनी-यि.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणदान
ऋणदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Payment of debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमत्कुण|ऋणमत्कुणः
ऋणमत्कुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A security, a bail.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण debt, मत्कुण an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमार्गण|ऋणमार्गणः
ऋणमार्गण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A security.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण, मृग to cleanse, in the causal, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमुक्ति|ऋणमुक्तिः
ऋणमुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Discharge of a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and मुक्ति emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणमोक्ष|ऋणमोक्षः
ऋणमोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Paying a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and मोक्ष release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणवत्|ऋणवन्त्
ऋणवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Owing, in debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणशोधन
ऋणशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Payment or discharge of a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण an शोधन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणादान|ऋणादानं
ऋणादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Recovery of a debt, receipt of money, &c. lent It is one of the eighteen titles or subjects of judicial procedure.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and आदान receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणान्तक|ऋणान्तकः
ऋणान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण, अन्त end, and क affix of agency: being the patron of debtors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापनयन
ऋणापनयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Discharge of a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and अपनयन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापनोदन|ऋणापनोदनं
ऋणापनोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Payment of a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and अपनोदन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणापाकरण
ऋणापाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Paying off a debt.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and अपाकरण acquittance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिक|ऋणिकः
ऋणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण debt, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणिन्
ऋणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णीनी-णि)<BR>1 Indebted.<BR>2 Of or belonging to debt.<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋणोद्ग्रहण
ऋणोद्ग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Recovering a debt in any way from the creditor, by friendly or legal proceedings, by stratagem, or by arrest.<BR>E.<BR>ऋण and उद्ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत<BR>r. 6th cl. (ऋतति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To have power.<BR>3 To domineer.<BR>4 To hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत|ऋतं|ऋतः
ऋत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Enlightened, luminous.<BR>3 Wonshipped, respected.<BR>4 True.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Gleaning.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Truth.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतधामन्
ऋतधामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत luminous, धाम abode; whose residence is brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतव्य
ऋतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Seasonable, in season, relating to a season.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋति|ऋतिः
ऋति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Prosperity, felicity.<BR>2 A road, a way.<BR>3 Abus censure, reproach.<BR>4 Envy, emulation.<BR>5 Going, motion.<BR>6 I fortune.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतिङ्कर|ऋतिंकर
ऋतिङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Propitious, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>ऋति and क what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतीया
ऋतीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Censure, reproach, (according to some,)<BR>2 Shame.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत sautra root, to abuse, ईयच् affix, fem. ठाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतु|ऋतुः
ऋतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 A season, (the Hindu year is divided into ar seasons, each consisting of two months.)<BR>2 The menstrual evacuation.<BR>3 The time favourable for procreation, or sixteen days in each month.<BR>4 A month.<BR>5 A kind of collyrium.<BR>6 Light.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुकाल|ऋतुकालः
ऋतुकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The duration of a season.<BR>2 The period menstruation.<BR>3 The period favourable for procreation, sixteen days in each month.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुगण|ऋतुगणः
ऋतुगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The seasons collectively.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and गण class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुपर्य्याय|ऋतुपर्याय|ऋतुपर्यायः
ऋतुपर्य्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The revolution of the seasons.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु an पर्य्याय revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुप्राप्त|ऋतुप्राप्तः
ऋतुप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Fruitful, fertile, &c. productive in due season^1.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु season, and प्राप्त attained.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66. note: scan error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुमती
ऋतुमती<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु, मतुप् a.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुवृत्ति|ऋतुवृत्तिः
ऋतुवृत्ति<BR>m. (त्तिः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु a season, वृत्ति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुराज|ऋतुराजः
ऋतुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Spring.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=168" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुलिङ्ग|ऋतुलिंग
ऋतुलिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A sign of the season.<BR>2 A symptom of menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and लिङ्ग a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसन्धि|ऋतुसंधि|ऋतुसन्धिः
ऋतुसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>The interval or junction between two seasons: the last seven days of one season and the first seven of the next.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुसात्म्य
ऋतुसात्म्य<BR>n. (-त्म्यं)<BR>Diet, &c. suited to the season.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and सात्म्य suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्नाता
ऋतुस्नाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman who has bathed after menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and स्नाता bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतुस्नान|ऋतुस्नानं
ऋतुस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bathing after menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋते
ऋते<BR>ind.<BR>Besides, except.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत Sautra root, to except, के aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋतोक्ति
ऋतोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Speaking truth.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्वन्त|ऋत्वन्तः
ऋत्वन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The close of a season.<BR>2 The termination of menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु and अन्त term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋत्विज्
ऋत्विज्<BR>m. (-त्विक्)<BR>1 A domestic chaplain, a family priest.<BR>E.<BR>ऋतु a season, यज to worship, affix क्विन् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्ध|ऋद्धं|ऋद्धः
ऋद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Prosperous, thriving, rising, &c.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>1 Stored grain.<BR>2 A demonstrated conclusion, a distinct result.<BR>E.<BR>ऋध to grow, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धि|ऋद्धिः
ऋद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 A medicinal plant; also सिद्धि.<BR>2 Increase, growth.<BR>3 Fortune, prosperity.<BR>4 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>ऋध to grow, &c. क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋद्धिमत्|ऋद्धिमन्त्
ऋद्धिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Rich, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>ऋद्भि and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋध
ऋध<BR>r. 4th cl. (उ) ऋधु (ऋध्यति)<BR>To increase, to grow, to flourish, to prosper.<BR>r. 5th cl. (ऋध्नीति)<BR>1 To increase, &c.<BR>2 To augment or make increase.<BR>3 To please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋफ
ऋफ<BR>r. 6th cl. (ऋफति)<BR>To injure, to kill; also रिफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभु|ऋभुः
ऋभु<BR>m. (-भुः)<BR>1 A deity, a divinity.<BR>2 A divinity of a particular order.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ the mother of the gods, भू to be, डु affix; also रिभु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्ष|ऋभुक्षः
ऋभुक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>3 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>ऋभु a deity, क्षि to waste, to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋभुक्षिन्
ऋभुक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>ऋभुक्ष paradise, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋम्फ
ऋम्फ<BR>r. 6th cl. (ऋम्फति)<BR>To injure, to kill; also रिम्फ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋश्य|ऋश्यः
ऋश्य<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>The painted or white footed antelope.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, क्यप् affix; also ऋष्य and रिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष
ऋष<BR>r. 1st cl. (अर्षति)<BR>To take, to receive, to choose.<BR>(ई) ऋषी r. 6th cl. (ऋषति)<BR>To go, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभ|ऋषभः
ऋषभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 (In composition,) best, excellent.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>3 A dried plant, one of the eight principal medicaments.<BR>4 The second of the seven notes of the Hindu gamut; in abbreviation, Ri.<BR>5 The first of the twenty-four principal. Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>6 The hollow of the ear.<BR>7 The name of a mountain.<BR>8 A crocodile's tail.<BR>9 A boar's tail.<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>1 A masculine woman, a woman with a beard, &c.<BR>2 A widow.<BR>3 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, अभच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषभध्वज|ऋषभध्वजः
ऋषभध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषभ and ध्वज a sign: he whose symbol is a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषि|ऋषिः
ऋषि<BR>m. (-षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi or sanctified personage so called: there are seven orders of these saints, as the Śrutarṣi, Kāṇḍarṣi, Paramarṣi, Maharṣi, Rājarṣi, Brahmarṣi and Devarṣi: the uncompounded name is especially applied to seven sages, of the Brahmarṣi order, cotemporary with each MANU; those of the present Manvantara, are MARĪCI, ATRI, AṄGIRAS, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU and VASIṢṬHA: the names of each series differ: those specified also form, in astronomy, the asterism of the greater bear: the Ṛṣi of a Mantra or mystic prayer in the Vedas, is the saint by whom it is supposed to have been remembered or recited.<BR>2 A Veda.<BR>3 A ray of light.<BR>4 A saint or sanctified sage in general.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The wife of A Ṛṣi.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, इन् Uṇādi affix fem. affix ङीष्; who goes beyond the limits of earthly life and wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिकुल्या
ऋषिकुल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि a saint, कुल्या an artificial canal; a canal made by the saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिगण
ऋषिगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A company or number of sages.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि and गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गल|ऋषिजाङ्गलः
ऋषिजाङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिजाङ्गलिकी
ऋषिजाङ्गलिकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus): see वृद्धताडक.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि and जाङ्गलिक a dealer in antidotes, affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषिप्रोक्ता
ऋषिप्रोक्ता<BR>f. (-क्ताः)<BR>A plant: see माषपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि, प्रोक्त mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषियज्ञ|ऋषियज्ञः
ऋषियज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>The study of Scripture.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि a sage, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋषीवह
ऋषीवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Bearing or conveying a Ṛṣi.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि and वह what bears, the final made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्टि|ऋष्टिः
ऋष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A sword.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्य|ऋष्यः
ऋष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>The painted or white footed antelope.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>A sort of leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष to go, क्यप् affix: also ऋश्य and रिश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यकेतु|ऋष्यकेतुः
ऋष्यकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A name of ANIRUDDHA the son of KANDARPA.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष्य and केतु a sign; having a deer for his symbol: some read this दिश्वकेतु, and others ऋश्यकेतु, ऋष्यकेतन, रिष्यकेतु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगता
ऋष्यगता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि and अ before गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यगन्धा
ऋष्यगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus): see वृद्धताडक.<BR>E.<BR>ऋषि, अ priv. and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यजिह्व
ऋष्यजिह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>A sort of leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष्य the deer and जिह्वा the tongue; to which the blotches are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यप्रोक्ता
ऋष्यप्रोक्ता<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>1 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>2 Asparagus racemosus.<BR>3 Sida, (cordifolia and rhombifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>see ऋषिप्रोक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यमूक|ऋष्यमूकः
ऋष्यमूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountain in the Dekhin, the temporary abode of RĀMA with the monkey chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>E.<BR>ऋष्य a deer, मूक dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऋष्यशृङ्ग|ऋष्यशृङ्गः
ऋष्यशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The name of a holy sage celebrated in the first book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ<BR>The long vowel corresponding to the short one preceding, and having the sound of RI long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ<BR>r. 9th cl. (गि) ॠणोति<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॠ
ॠ<BR>f. (री)<BR>1 The mother of the gods.<BR>2 Also of the demons.<BR>3 Recollection.<BR>m. (आ)<BR>1 A name of BHAIRAVA.<BR>2 An Asura or demon.<BR>3 The breast.<BR>4 Motion, going.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Incipient particle.<BR>2 An interjection of compassion.<BR>3 Of reproach.<BR>4 Of terror.<BR>5 A mystical letter used in the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=169" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ<BR>The ninth vowel of the Nāgarī Alphabet, having the power of Lri, but more usually considered to be expressed by Li as in Lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऌ
ऌ<BR>aptote.<BR>1 The divine nature.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>ind.<BR>A mystical letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ<BR>The long vowel corresponding to the preceding short one, Ḹ of Ḷ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ॡ
ॡ<BR>aptote.<BR>1 A divine female.<BR>2 The female nature.<BR>3 A mother.<BR>m. (-ॡः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ॡः)<BR>1 The mother of the demons.<BR>2 The mother of the all-bestowing cow.<BR>ind.<BR>A mystical letter used once or repeatedly in many Mantras or mystical formulae. The letter ॠ and ऌ are employed in the same manner: they have apparently no signification, but are personified and invested with marvellous properties in the Tantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए<BR>The eleventh vowel of the alphabet, corresponding to the letter E as pronounced in most languages except the English, and having the sound of A in amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ए
ए<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of,<BR>1 Remembering, (ha.)<BR>2 Censure or contempt.<BR>3 Compassion, (ah!)<BR>4 Addressing, (eh! hey.)<BR>5 Calling, (hey, ho.)<BR>(-एः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एक|एकं|एकः
एक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 One.<BR>2 Alone, solitary.<BR>3 Other, different.<BR>4 Chief, pre-eminent.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, Uṇādi affix कन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकऋक्थिन्
एकऋक्थिन्<BR>m. (-क्थी)<BR>A coheir.<BR>E.<BR>एक one (father), ऋक्थिन् heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकक|एककः
एकक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Alone, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककर
एककर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Making one.<BR>2 One-handed.<BR>3 Onerayed.<BR>E.<BR>एक and कर making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककार्य्य|एककार्य
एककार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Performing the same office, answering the same end.<BR>E.<BR>एक and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककाल|एककालः
एककाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>One or the same time.<BR>E.<BR>एक and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककालभोजन
एककालभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating but one meal in any given time.<BR>E.<BR>एककाल and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककालीन
एककालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Coeval, cotemporary.<BR>E.<BR>एक and कालीन relating to time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एककुण्डल|एककुण्डलः
एककुण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>2 An epithet of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>एक and कुण्डल an ear-ring: wearing it in one ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकक्षीर
एकक्षीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The milk of one (nurse, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>एक and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकगुरु|एकगुरुः
एकगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A spiritual brother, pupil of the same preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>एक and गुरु a religious preceptor; also with कन् added एकगुरुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकग्रामीण
एकग्रामीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Of the same town or village.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, ग्रामीण villager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचक्र|एकचक्रं|एकचक्रः
एकचक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>The name of a city: see हरिगृह.<BR>E.<BR>एक, चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचर|एकचरः
एकचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Solitary, alone.<BR>2 Having one follower.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>E.<BR>एक् alone, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचारिन्
एकचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Going alone or with one follower only.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A follower of BUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकचित्त
एकचित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Thinking of one thing only, intent upon, absorbed in.<BR>2 Of one mind, agreeing, concurring.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, चित्त the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजन्मन्
एकजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>एक best or one, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजात
एकजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Of one parentage, born of the same parents.<BR>E.<BR>एक and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकजाति|एकजातिः
एकजाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Of the same caste.<BR>2 Once born.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, and जाति birth or caste: not being regenerated by investiture, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकज्या
एकज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 The chord of an arc.<BR>2 Sine of 30° or of the radius.<BR>E.<BR>एक and ज्या a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतम|एकतमः
एकतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>One of many.<BR>E.<BR>एक and डतमच् affix of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतर|एकतरः
एकतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Either, one of two.<BR>2 Other, different.<BR>E.<BR>एक and डतरच् affix of the comparative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतस्
एकतस्<BR>ind.<BR>On one side, on one part.<BR>E.<BR>एक and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकता
एकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unity, oneness.<BR>E.<BR>एक and तल् affix, or with त्व aff. एकत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतान|एकतानः
एकतान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Closely attentive, having the mind fixed on one only object.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Musical unison: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>एक, तन to stretch or spread, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकताल|एकतालः
एकताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Harmony, unison, the accurate adjustment of song, dance, and instrumental music.<BR>(-ली)<BR>An instrument for heating time, any instrument having but one note.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, uniform, and ताल musical measure or time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकतीर्थिन्
एकतीर्थिन्<BR>m. (-र्थी)<BR>A spiritual brother, an associate in religious offices or objects.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, the same, तीर्थ place of pilgrimage, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकत्र
एकत्र<BR>ind.<BR>Together, in one, in one place.<BR>E.<BR>एक and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदंष्ट्र|एकदंष्ट्रः
एकदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>एक and दंष्ट्र a tooth, single toothed or tusked; the fellow being broken off in a scuffle by KĀRTTIKEYA, or according to another legend by PARAŚURĀMA; also एकदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदन्त|एकदंत|एकदन्तः
एकदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>एक and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदा
एकदा<BR>ind.<BR>At the same time, at once.<BR>E.<BR>एक and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदुःखसुख
एकदुःखसुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Sympathizing, having the same joy and sorrows.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and दुःख pain, सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदृश्
एकदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>1 A name of MAHĀDEVA<BR>2 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>एक and दृश् an eye: ŚIVA is termed one-eyed from the eye in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदेश|एकदेशः
एकदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A part, a portion, a division.<BR>E.<BR>एक and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकदेह|एकदेहः
एकदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Elegantly formed.<BR>2 Single bodied.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR>E.<BR>एक best or one, and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधा
एकधा<BR>ind.<BR>In one way.<BR>E.<BR>एक and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुर्
एकधुर्<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>A particular burthen or conveyance.<BR>E.<BR>एक an धुर् a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुर|एकधुरः
एकधुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cattle for special burthen, fit for but or kind of labour.<BR>E.<BR>see एकधुरीण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=170" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुरावह|एकधुरावहः
एकधुरावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>एक, धुर burthen, and वह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकधुरीण|एकधुरीणः
एकधुरीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Cattle of special burthen.<BR>E.<BR>एक, धुर a burthen, ख affix which leaves ईण, or with अ affix forming एकधुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकनट|एकनटः
एकनट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The principal actor in a drama, the manager.<BR>E.<BR>एक chief, and नट an actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकनाथ|एकनाथः
एकनाथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Having one master.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Sole master or lord.<BR>E.<BR>एक and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपक्ष|एकपक्षः
एकपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>An associate, a firm ally or partisan.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, पक्ष part; of the same side or party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपत्नी
एकपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>1 A faithful wife, one devoted to her husband.<BR>2 The wife of a man who has no other wives.<BR>E.<BR>एक one or excellent, पति a husband, न substituted for the final, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपत्रिका
एकपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, white basil.<BR>E.<BR>एक and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपद|एकपदं|एकपदः
एकपद<BR>adv. n. (-दं)<BR>Then, at that time, at once.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A single inflection of a verb or noun.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A road, a path or way.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, पद a foot, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपरि
एकपरि<BR>ind.<BR>One over, a term at dice.<BR>E.<BR>एक and परि over, against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपात
एकपात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sudden, rapid, coming suddenly or at once.<BR>E.<BR>एक and पात falling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपाद्
एकपाद्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>एक best, and पाद् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिङ्ग|एकपिंग|एकपिङ्गः
एकपिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, and पिङ्ग tawny: having a yellow mark in the place of one of his eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिङ्गल|एकपिंगल|एकपिङ्गलः
एकपिङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिण्ड|एकपिंड
एकपिण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Related, near of kin, united by the offering of the funeral cake.<BR>E.<BR>एक and पिण्ड a funeral cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकपिण्डता
एकपिण्डता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Connexion by the funeral cake, consanguinity.<BR>E.<BR>एकपिण्ड and तल् affix; also with त्व, एकपिण्डत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकफल
एकफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having one or a principal result or object.<BR>E.<BR>एक and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्त
एकभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Attached to a common master.<BR>2 Worshipping one deity.<BR>3 Eating together.<BR>4 Eating but one meal, (a day.)<BR>E.<BR>एक and भक्त attached to, or भक्त food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्तव्रत|एकभक्तव्रतं
एकभक्तव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Eating but once a day as a religious obligation.<BR>E.<BR>एक, भक्त food, व्रत vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभक्ति
एकभक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>1 Of one faith.<BR>2 Believing in one deity.<BR>E.<BR>एक and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभाव|एकभावः
एकभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Of a simple or single nature or temperament.<BR>E.<BR>एक and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभुक्त
एकभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Eating but one meal, (a day, &c.)<BR>2 Eating together.<BR>E.<BR>एक and भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकभोजन
एकभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating in common, feeding together.<BR>2 Eating one meal a day, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एक and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमुख
एकमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>1 Having one chief or head.<BR>2 One faced.<BR>E.<BR>एक and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकमूला
एकमूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>2 Flax, (Linum.)<BR>E.<BR>एक and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकयष्टिका
एकयष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A single string of flowers, pearls, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एक and यष्टिका a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकयोनि
एकयोनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Uterine, of the same mother.<BR>E.<BR>एक and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरज|एकरजः
एकरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant, (Verbesina scandens): see भृङ्गराज.<BR>E.<BR>एक excellent, and रजस् farina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरस|एकरसः
एकरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Of one flavour.<BR>E.<BR>एक and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरात्र|एकरात्रः
एकरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>One night, a night.<BR>E.<BR>एक and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकरात्रिक
एकरात्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>For a night, of a night.<BR>E.<BR>एक and रात्रि night, with ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकराशि|एकराशिः
एकराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>A heap, a crowd.<BR>E.<BR>एक and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकराशिभूत
एकराशिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heaped or collected together.<BR>E.<BR>एकराशि and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकल|एकलः
एकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Alone, solitary; a various reading of एकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकलिङ्ग|एकलिंग|एकलिङ्गं|एकलिङ्गः
एकलिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 A place or district in which for five Cos there is but one Phallus.<BR>E.<BR>एक one or best, लिङ्ग a mark, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवद्भाव
एकवद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An aggregate of many, as in grammar, the formation of a compound noun of several nouns.<BR>E.<BR>एक, वत् like, भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्ण|एकवर्णः
एकवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Of one caste or tribe.<BR>2 Of one colour.<BR>3 Of one quality.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>One unknown quantity, (in algebra.)<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>Beating time, marking musical measure by clapping the hands, or the instrument which does so, a castanet: see एकताली.<BR>E.<BR>एक, वर्ण a quality, a note, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्णसमीकरण
एकवर्णसमीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Uniliteral equation.<BR>E.<BR>एकवर्णं and समीकरण equation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवर्षिका
एकवर्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A heifer one year old.<BR>E.<BR>एक, वर्ष a year, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवाद|एकवादः
एकवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A musical instrument, a kind of drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>एक principal, वाद sound: high-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवीर|एकवीरः
एकवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A chief warrior.<BR>E.<BR>एक and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवृक्ष|एकवृक्षः
एकवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A desert place, in which but one tree is seen for four Cos.<BR>E.<BR>एक and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकवेणी
एकवेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A single braid of hair.<BR>2 A woman whose hair is tied in one braid.<BR>E.<BR>एक and वेणी a tress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशफ|एकशफः
एकशफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 Any animal whose hoof is not cloven.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, uniform, and शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरण
एकशरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>One only hope or refuge, especially applied to a deity.<BR>E.<BR>एक and शरण protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीर
एकशरीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Consanguineous, of one body or blood.<BR>2 Of one or the same body.<BR>E.<BR>एक, शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरान्वय
एकशरीरान्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Consanguineous descent.<BR>E.<BR>एकशरीर and अन्वय lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरारम्भ
एकशरीरारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Commencement of consanguinity by the union of father and mother.<BR>E.<BR>एकशरीर and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरावयव
एकशरीरावयव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A descendant in a right line, a kinsman by blood.<BR>E.<BR>एकशरीर and अवयव a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशरीरावयवत्व
एकशरीरावयवत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Consanguineous descent or connexion.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशाख|एकशाखः
एकशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A Brahman of the same branch or school.<BR>E.<BR>एक and शाखा a branch, (of the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकशृङ्ग|एकशृंग|एकशृङ्गः
एकशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A title of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A unicorn, a rhinoceros, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एक and शृङ्ग a mark or horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसर्ग|एकसर्गः
एकसर्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>Closely attentive, having the mind intent upon one object.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, and सृज to create, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसूत्र|एकसूत्रः
एकसूत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A small double drum, played by a string and ball attached to the body of it: see वृषाङ्कज.<BR>E.<BR>एक and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=171" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकसूनु
एकसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>An only son.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and सूनु a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकस्थ
एकस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Collected, assembled, conjoined, in one site or place.<BR>E.<BR>एक and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकस्थान
एकस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>One place, the same place.<BR>E.<BR>एक and स्थान place, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकहायनी
एकहायनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A heifer one year old.<BR>E.<BR>एक, हायन a year, affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाकिन्
एकाकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Alone, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>एक and आकिनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाक्ष|एकाक्षः
एकाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाक्षर
एकाक्षर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A monosyllable, especially the sacred monosyllable Om.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्र|एकाग्रः
एकाग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Intent, closely attentive, fixed on one object.<BR>2 Undisturbed, unperplexed.<BR>3 Known, celebrated.<BR>4 Single-pointed.<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>The whole of a long line which is subdivided.<BR>E.<BR>एक and ग्र chief, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्रता
एकाग्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Close and undisturbed attention.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, एकाग्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाग्र्य|एकाग्र्यः
एकाग्र्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं)<BR>Closely attentive: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>एक, अग्र्य chief, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाङ्ग|एकांग|एकाङ्गं|एकाङ्गः
एकाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>एक best pre-eminent, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकादश
एकादश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Eleven, eleventh.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The eleventh day of the half month: it is especially sacred to VIṢṆU, and fasting on it is most efficacious.<BR>E.<BR>एकादशन् eleven, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकादशन्
एकादशन्<BR>plur. mfn. (-श)<BR>Eleven.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, दशन् ten, with आङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकानंशा
एकानंशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>अंश a part, with the neg. pref. and एक preeminent: chief and undivided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकानुदिष्ट
एकानुदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Left, as a funeral feast, one who has recently partaken of it.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, (ancestor,) अनु after, दिष्ट shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्त|एकान्तं|एकान्तः
एकान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Excessive.<BR>2 Solitary, lonely, retired.<BR>3 Aside, apart.<BR>adv. n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>2 Apart.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तकरुण
एकान्तकरुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Very compassionate, weakly charitable.<BR>E.<BR>एकान्त and करुण charitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्ततस्
एकान्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Alone, apart, privately.<BR>2 Much, exceedingly.<BR>E.<BR>एकान्त and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तर|एकान्तरः
एकान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Next but one.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकान्तस्थित
एकान्तस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Staying alone or apart.<BR>E.<BR>एकान्त and स्थित staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाब्दा
एकाब्दा<BR>f. (-ब्दा)<BR>A heifer one year old.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकायन|एकायनः
एकायन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Closely attentive, intent.<BR>E.<BR>एक, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकायनगत|एकायनगतः
एकायनगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>एकायन and गत being, having gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकावली
एकावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A single string of beads, flowers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एक and आवली a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकार्थ|एकार्थः
एकार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Having one sense or meaning.<BR>2 Having one or the same object.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाश्रितगुण|एकाश्रितगुणः
एकाश्रितगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A simple attribute or predicate, as form, taste, smell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, आश्रित invested, गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाष्टी
एकाष्टी<BR>f. (-ष्टी)<BR>A pod or seed of cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाष्टील
एकाष्टील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant: see वकपुष्प; the flowers are sacred to ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>एक best, अष्टि seed, and ल what gives or takes, from ला with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाह|एकाहः
एकाह<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>The period of one day.<BR>E.<BR>एक and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकाहगम
एकाहगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A day's journey.<BR>E.<BR>एकाह and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीभाव|एकीभावः
एकीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Common nature or property.<BR>E.<BR>एक with च्चि augment, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकीय|एकीयः
एकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>A companion, a partisan or associate.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, and छण affix, also एकपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकैक
एकैक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Singly, one by one.<BR>E.<BR>एक repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकैकशस्
एकैकशस्<BR>ind.<BR>One by one, severally, seriatim.<BR>E.<BR>एक repeated, with शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकोद्दिष्ट|एकोद्दिष्टं
एकोद्दिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>The Śrāddha or funeral rite offered to one person only.<BR>E.<BR>एक and उद्दिष्ट addressed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकोशिका
एकोशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra): see एकाष्टील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एकौघभूत
एकौघभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heaped, crowded together.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, ओघ quantity, भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एज
एज<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) एजृ (एजते)<BR>To shine.<BR>(एजति)<BR>To quake or tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजन|एजनं
एजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>एज and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजयत्
एजयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Causing to shake or tremble.<BR>E.<BR>एज to shake, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजित
एजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>एज to shake, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितव्य
एजितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be shaken.<BR>E.<BR>एज and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एजितृ
एजितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>एज and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एठ
एठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (एठते)<BR>To annoy, to resist or oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एड|एडः
एड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Deaf.<BR>E.<BR>ईड to praise, आङ् prefixed, अच् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडक|एडकः
एडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A ram.<BR>2 A wild goat.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A ewe.<BR>E.<BR>ईल to go, ण्वुल् affix; and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडगज|एडगजः
एडगज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A medicinal plant, used for the cure of ringworms, (Cassia tora.)<BR>E.<BR>एड a sheep, गज to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडमूक|एडमूकः
एडमूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Deaf and dumb.<BR>2 Wicked, perverse.<BR>E.<BR>एड deaf, and भूक dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एडुक|एडुकं|एडुकः
एडुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A building constructed of rubbish, bones, &c.<BR>2 A wall enclosing bones, a tomb, &c.<BR>3 A building of hard substances resembling bones.<BR>E.<BR>ईड to throw or send, deriv. irr.; also एडूक and ण्डोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एण|एणः
एण<BR>mf. (-णः-णी)<BR>A kind of deer or antelope, described as being of a black colour, with beautiful eyes, and short legs.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणक|एणकः
एणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of deer or antelope: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to एण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणतिलक|एणतिलकः
एणतिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>एण an antelope, and तिलक the sectarial mark; a deer being fancifully visible in the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणभृत्
एणभृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>एण and भृत् who nourishes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एणाजिन
एणाजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A deer skin.<BR>E.<BR>एण and अजिन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत|एतं|एतः
एत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or -ती तं)<BR>Of a variegated colour.<BR>(-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Arrived, come.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A deer or antelope.<BR>2 A variegated colour.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, तन् affix; when signifying colour, the fem. affix is either टाप् or ङीप्, and before the latter, त is changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=172" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतद्
एतद्<BR>pron. mfn. (एषः एषा एतद् or एतत्)<BR>This.<BR>E.<BR>एत derived from इण to go, and तद् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतन|एतनः
एतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Expiration, breathing out, discharging air from the lungs.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, तनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतर्हि
एतर्हि<BR>ind.<BR>Now, at this time.<BR>E.<BR>एत substituted for इदम्, and र्हिल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतश|एतशः
एतश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, and तशः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतशस्
एतशस्<BR>m. (-शाः)<BR>A Brahman or man of the first class.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, तशस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतादृश्
एतादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Such, such like.<BR>E.<BR>एतद् this, दृश् to see, क्किप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतादृश
एतादृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Such, such like.<BR>E.<BR>एतद् this, दृश to see, कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एतावत्|एतावन्त्
एतावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>So many, so much, so far.<BR>ind. (-वत)<BR>So far, thus far, so much, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एतद्, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एत्य
एत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having gone to or approached.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध|एधः
एध<BR>r. 1st cl. (एधते)<BR>To grow or increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एध|एधः
एध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Fuel, as wood, grass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>एध to increase, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधतु|एधतुः
एधतु<BR>mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु)<BR>Increased, grown.<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Man.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>एध to increase, तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधनीय
एधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be enlarged or increased.<BR>E.<BR>एध to grow, and अनीयर् affix; also एधितव्य and एध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधस्
एधस्<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>Fuel: see एध.<BR>E.<BR>एध to grow, Uṇādi affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधित|एधितः
एधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Increased, grown.<BR>E.<BR>एध to increase, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एधितृ
एधितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Increasing, growing, enlarging.<BR>E.<BR>एध to grown, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्
एनस्<BR>n. (-एनः)<BR>1 Sin, fault, offence.<BR>2 Censure, blame.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, असुन् Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एनस्विन्
एनस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Sinful, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>एनस्, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरका
एरका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of grass of emollient and diluent properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरङ्ग|एरंगः|एरङ्गः
एरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A kind of fish; also एलङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्ड|एरंडः|एरण्डः
एरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The castor-oil plant, (Palma christi or Ricinus communis).<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>इर to go, &c. आङ् prefixed, अण्डच् affix, fem. affix ङीष्; also with कन् added एरण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डक|एरंडकः|एरण्डकः
एरण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Palma christi: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डपत्रिका
एरण्डपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti.<BR>E.<BR>एरण्ड, and पत्र leaf, having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एरण्डफला
एरण्डफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>एरण्ड, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एर्वारु|एर्वारुः|एर्व्वारुः
एर्वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>see ईर्व्वारु^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: 'r' missing; b/v unclear print.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलक|एलकः
एलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ram: see एडक.<BR>E.<BR>ड and ल being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलङ्ग|एलंगः|एलङ्गः
एलङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Cyprinus marginatus, BUC.) also एरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालु
एलवालु<BR>n. (-लु)<BR>The name of a perfume: see the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलवालुक
एलवालुक<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A granular substance apparently vegetable, of a reddish brown colour, and used as a drug and as a perfume.<BR>E.<BR>एला cardamoms, वल to breathe, उण् affix, and कन् added, or without कन्, एलवालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलविल|एलविलः
एलविल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of KUVERA: see ऐलविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एला
एला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Cardamoms, the seed of the Eletteria cardamomum, or Alpinia Cardamomum: it applies to both the large and small cardamom, but most commonly to the former.<BR>E.<BR>इल to send, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलापत्र|एलापत्रः
एलापत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>One of the chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलापर्णी|एलापर्ण्णी
एलापर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>एल cardamoms, and पर्ण a leaf, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एलीका
एलीका<BR>f. (का)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>एला, and ईकन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एव|एवं|एवः
एव<BR>mfn. (-एवः-एवा-एवं)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>ind.<BR>As, like, &c.: see एवम्.<BR>E.<BR>इण् to go, Uṇādi affix वन्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्
एवम्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying,<BR>1 Likeness, (as, so, like.)<BR>2 Assent, (yes, verily.)<BR>3 Sameness of manner, (thus, in this way.)<BR>4 Certainly, (indeed, assuredly, even so.)<BR>5 Command, (so, thus, &c.)<BR>6 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>इण to go, वम् affix; also एव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्भूत|एवंभूत
एवम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>So, such, in such manner.<BR>E.<BR>एवम्, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एवम्विध
एवम्विध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Such, in such form or manner, of such a kind.<BR>E.<BR>एवम्, and विध sort, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष|एषः
एष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) एषृ (एषते)<BR>To go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषण|एषणः
एषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A goldsmith's balance, assay scales.<BR>2 An iron or steel probe.<BR>E.<BR>एष to go, ल्युट् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणिका
एषणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A goldsmith's balance.<BR>E.<BR>as before, with कन् and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषणीय
एषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be desired, desirable.<BR>2 To be aimed at.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, affix अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषा
एषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Desire.<BR>E.<BR>इष to wish, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एषितृ
एषितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्टृ
एष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्र)<BR>1 Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>ईष to wish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ<BR>The twelfth vowel of the Nagarī alphabet, or more properly a diphthong; corresponding in sound to Ei in heighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of,<BR>1 Remembering, (aye, ha.)<BR>2 Calling, summoning, (hola, ho, heigh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐ
ऐ<BR>m. (-ऐः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकध्य|ऐकध्यं
ऐकध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Singleness of time or occurrence.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and ध्यमुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकमत्य|ऐकमत्यं
ऐकमत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Consent, concurrence, sameness of doctrine or opinion.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, मत minded, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकशफ
ऐकशफ<BR>mfn. (-फः-फी-फं)<BR>Produced by or belonging to animals with single hoofs.<BR>E.<BR>एकशफ, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकागारिक|ऐकागारिकः
ऐकागारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 A thief, a robber.<BR>2 The possessor of one residence.<BR>E.<BR>एक one, अगार a house, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाग्र्य|ऐकाग्र्यं
ऐकाग्र्य<BR>n. (-ग्र्यं)<BR>Intentness. of one object.<BR>E.<BR>एकाग्र, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकान्यिक|ऐकान्यिकः
ऐकान्यिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who commits a single error in reading.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and अन्य other, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाहिक|ऐकाहिकं
ऐकाहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ephemeral, quotidian, of one day, of the same day.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and अहन a day, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्य|ऐक्यं
ऐक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>1 Unity, oneness.<BR>2 A whole of various parts, an aggregate, a total.<BR>E.<BR>एक, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षव|ऐक्षवं
ऐक्षव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Sugar, sugary, produced from or relating to the sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु sugar cane, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुक|ऐक्षुकः
ऐक्षुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A carrier of sugar canes.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्ष, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=173" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्षुभारिक
ऐक्षुभारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Carrying sugar canes.<BR>E.<BR>इक्षु, and भार a load, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाक|ऐक्ष्वाकः
ऐक्ष्वाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of the family of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्षाकु, and अञ् affix, the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्ष्वाकव
ऐक्ष्वाकव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Of the family of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>E.<BR>ईक्ष्वाकु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐङ्गुद|ऐंगुद|ऐङ्गुदं
ऐङ्गुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The fruit of the plant called Iṅguda.<BR>E.<BR>इङ्गुद the plant, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐच्छिक
ऐच्छिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Optional, voluntary, at will.<BR>E.<BR>इच्छा wish, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐडुक|ऐडुकं
ऐडुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A wall, &c. of bones and rubbish: see एडुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐण|ऐणं
ऐण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Belonging to a male antelope.<BR>E.<BR>एण an antelope, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणिक|ऐणिकः
ऐणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a deer, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>E.<BR>एण, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐणेय|ऐणेयं|ऐणेयः
ऐणेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Appertaining to a doe or the female antelope.<BR>E.<BR>एणी a doe, affix ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयोपनिषद्
ऐतरेयोपनिषद्<BR>f. (-षद् or षत्)<BR>One of the Upaniṣads of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिक|ऐतिहासिकः
ऐतिहासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Historical.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A historian.<BR>E.<BR>इतिहास a story, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिह्य|ऐतिह्यं
ऐतिह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>Traditional instruction.<BR>E.<BR>इतिहा tradition, ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्दव|ऐंदव|ऐन्दवं|ऐन्दवः
ऐन्दव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Lunar.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The asterism Mṛgaśiras.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>इन्दु the moon, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्र|ऐंद्र|ऐन्द्रं|ऐन्द्रः
ऐन्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं)<BR>Sacred, or relating to the god INDRA.<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A name of the monkey king BĀLĪ.<BR>2 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>1 The wife of INDRA.<BR>2 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3 Misfortune, misery, (personified.) The name of a plant, a kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>5 The constellation Jyeṣṭha.<BR>6 The east quarter, of which INDRA is regent.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रजालिक|ऐंद्रजालिक|ऐन्द्रजालिकः
ऐन्द्रजालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Deceptive, illusory.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रजाल deception, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक|ऐंद्रलुप्तिक|ऐन्द्रलुप्तिकः
ऐन्द्रलुप्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Afflicted with falling of the hair or morbid baldness.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रलुप्त falling of the hair, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्राग्न|ऐंद्राग्न
ऐन्द्राग्न<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>A ceremony, &c. addressed to INDRA and AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, and अग्नि, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रायुध
ऐन्द्रायुध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>Relating to INDRA'S bow or the rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रायुध, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रावरुण
ऐन्द्रावरुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Sacred to INDRA and VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, and वरुण with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रि|ऐंद्रिः|ऐन्द्रिः
ऐन्द्रि<BR>m. (-न्द्रिः)<BR>1 The patronymick of JAYANTA the son of INDRA.<BR>2 A name of the monkey BĀLĪ.<BR>3 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>4 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्र, इञ् patronymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्द्रियक|ऐंद्रियक|ऐन्द्रियकं
ऐन्द्रियक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Perceptible, perceived, present.<BR>2 Of or belonging to the sense.<BR>E.<BR>इन्द्रिय an organ of sense, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावण|ऐरावणः
ऐरावण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>इरावत् the ocean, अण affix of descent; ocean-born: न is changed irregularly to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावत|ऐरावतं|ऐरावतः
ऐरावत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 INDRA'S elephant.<BR>2 The same, considered as the elephant of the north quarter.<BR>3 An orange.<BR>4 A fruit, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR>5 A serpent, one of the chiefs of the Nāga or serpent race, inhabiting the infernal regions.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 A particular kind of it.<BR>3 The female of INDRA'S elephant.<BR>4 The Rāvī river in the Pañjāb.<BR>n. (-त)<BR>INDRA'S bow unbent, the rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>इरावत् water-having; that is, the ocean, a cloud, &c. अण् affix implying origin or descent; born from the ocean, (the elephant,) proceeding from watery clouds, (lightning, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरिण|ऐरिणं
ऐरिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Fossil or rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>इरिन् earthy, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरेय|ऐरेयं
ऐरेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>इरा wine, ढक् affix: see मैरेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐल|ऐलः
ऐल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a king, also PURŪRAVAS.<BR>E.<BR>इला the wife of BUDDHA, अण् patronymick affix; the son of ILĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवालुक|ऐलवालुकः
ऐलवालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A perfume: see एलवालुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविल|ऐलविलः
ऐलविल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A title of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>इलविला the wife of PULASTYA, and the paternal grand-mother of the deity, affix अण; also ऐडविल, ऐडविड, एलविल, &c. ल and ड being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलेय|ऐलेयं|ऐलेयः
ऐलेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A perfume: see एलवालुक.<BR>E.<BR>एला cardamoms, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश
ऐश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Divine.<BR>2 Regal.<BR>E.<BR>ईश, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशानी
ऐशानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The north-east quarter.<BR>E.<BR>ईशान ŚIVA, as regent of the north-east, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशिक|ऐशिकः
ऐशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Divine, heavenly.<BR>2 Regal, royal.<BR>E.<BR>ईश, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर
ऐश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Divine, relating to god, &c.<BR>2 Royal, supreme.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वर, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर्य्य|ऐश्वर्य|ऐश्वर्यं|ऐश्वर्य्यं
ऐश्वर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Super-human power, the divine faculties of omnipresence, omnipotence, invisibility, &c.<BR>2 Supremacy, dominion, sway, power, might.<BR>E.<BR>ईश्वर a master, a deity, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्
ऐषमस्<BR>ind.<BR>The present year.<BR>E.<BR>इदम् this, समसण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्त्य|ऐषमस्त्यः
ऐषमस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>Of or belonging to the present year.<BR>E.<BR>ऐषमस, and त्यय affix; or with द्यु affix, ऐषमस्तन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिक
ऐष्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR>E.<BR>इष्टि a sacrifice, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक|ऐष्टिकपौर्तिक
ऐष्टिकपौर्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ceremonial and meritorious, (any act, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>इष्टापूर्त्तं any pious act, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहलौकिक
ऐहलौकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of this world, terrestrial, sublunary.<BR>E.<BR>इह here, लोक world, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिक|ऐहिकं
ऐहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Worldly, local, of this world, of this place.<BR>E.<BR>ईह here, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ<BR>The vowel O, and the thirteenth of the Nāgarī alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ<BR>ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle, (oh.)<BR>2 An interjection of calling, (ho, hola.)<BR>3 Of reminiscence, (ho, ah.)<BR>4 Of compassionating, (ah, oh.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ<BR>m. (-औः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओं
ॐ<BR>ind.<BR>The mystical monosyllable Om: see ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक|ओकं|ओकः
ओक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 An asylum, a refuge: see ओकम्.<BR>3 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>उच to assemble, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकण|ओकणः
ओकण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bug; also ओकणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकस्
ओकस्<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>1 An asylum, a place of refuge.<BR>2 A house.<BR>E.<BR>उच to collect, असुन Uṇādi affix, च becomes क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुल|ओकुलः
ओकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cake of flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकोदनी
ओकोदनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्कणी
ओक्कणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=174" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख
ओख<BR>r. 1st. cl (ऋ) ओखृ (ओखति and with a prefix, as प्र, प्रोखति.)<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>2 To adorn.<BR>3 To be able or competent, to suffice.<BR>4 To refuse or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघ|ओघः
ओघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A heap or quantity, flock or multitude.<BR>2 A stream, a torrent, a rapid flow of water, an inundation.<BR>3 Quick time in music.<BR>4 Tradition.<BR>5 Advice, instruction.<BR>E.<BR>उच to collect, घञ् affix, and च is changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओङ्कार|ओंकार|ओंकारः|ओङ्कारः
ओङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The mysterious name of the deity: see ओम्.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A Bauddha Śakti, or female personification of divine energy.<BR>E.<BR>ओम, and कार affix implying a letter, the compound letter ओ; otherwise ओम्, signifying assent, and कार who makes; what complies with our wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज<BR>(त) r. 1st cl. (ओजति)<BR>1 To live, to have the vital faculties and organs.<BR>2 To be strong or able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>See the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 Light, splendor.<BR>2 Manifestation, appearance.<BR>3 Strength.<BR>4 Support, stay.<BR>5 Metallic lustre.<BR>6 Vitality, the principle of vital warmth and action diffused throughout the body.<BR>7 Virility, the generative faculty.<BR>8 A form of style, elaborate style, abounding with compounds.<BR>9 (In astrology,) Each alternate sign of the zodiac, first, third, fifth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ओज to live, and असुन् affix; or with अच् affix ओज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्विन्
ओजस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Mighty, powerful, strong.<BR>2 Splendid, bright.<BR>E.<BR>आजस्, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडक
ओडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A musical mode, which omits two of the notes of the scale, Ri and Pa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडिका
ओडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडी
ओडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्र|ओड्रः
ओड्र<BR>m. (-ड्रः)<BR>1 The China rose, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>2 The name of a country, the northern part of Orissa.<BR>E.<BR>उड to embrace. रक affix, and उ is changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रपुष्प|ओड्रपुष्पं
ओड्रपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>The China rose, the plant or its flower.<BR>E.<BR>ओड्र China rose, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण
ओण<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) ओणृ (ओणति)<BR>To remove, to take away or abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतु|ओतुः
ओतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, &c. and तु Uṇādi affix, the radical is changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदन|ओदनं|ओदनः
ओदन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>Boiled rice.<BR>f. (-निका-नी)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia, &c.) see वला.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to be wet, ल्युट् Uṇādi affix, and न dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्म|ओद्मः
ओद्म<BR>m. (-द्मः)<BR>Wetting, moistening.<BR>E.<BR>उन्द to be wet, मम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 The mystic name of the deity, prefacing all the prayers and most of the writings of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>अ a name of VIṢṆU, उ ŚIVA, and म of BRAHMA; it therefore implies the Indian triad, and expresses the three in one.<BR>2 A particle of command or injunction.<BR>3 Of assent, (verily, amen.)<BR>4 Of auspiciousness.<BR>5 Of removal, (away, hence,) and,<BR>6 It is an inceptive particle.<BR>E.<BR>अव to go, to preserve, &c. मन् Uṇādi affix, the radical being converted into ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल|ओलं|ओलः
ओल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Wet, damp; also ओण.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>E.<BR>वल or वल्ल to destroy, (complaints, especially hoemorrhoids.) अच् affix, व changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलड
ओलड<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (इ) ओलडि (ओलण्डति or ओलण्डयति.)<BR>To dart or throw up:<BR>some consider the initial vowel to be indicatory, and make the root लडि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष|ओषं|ओषः
ओष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Burning, combustion.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषण|ओषणः
ओषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Pungency, pungent taste or flavour.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A potherb, commonly Pūrya.<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, and ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधि|ओषधिः
ओषधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>An annual plant or herb, one that dies after becoming ripe.<BR>E.<BR>ओष heat, and धा to have, कि affix; or with ङीष्, ओषधी; or with इञ् affix, औषधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधी
ओषधी<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>An annual plant or deciduous herb: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधीपति|ओषधीपतिः
ओषधीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>ओषधी and पति lord: presiding over annual plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधीश|ओषधीशः
ओषधीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding; ईश meaning lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ|ओष्ठः
ओष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The lip, especially the upper, &c. du.<BR>m. (ओष्ठौ or ओष्ठाधरौ)<BR>The lips: see अधर.<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>A creeper, bearing a red flower, to which the lip is commonly compared, (Bryonia grandis.)<BR>E.<BR>उष to burn, थन् Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्: see विम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठपल्लव|ओष्ठपल्लवः
ओष्ठपल्लव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A lip or the lips.<BR>E.<BR>ओष्ठ and पल्लव a new shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठरोग|ओष्ठरोगः
ओष्ठरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Any morbid affection of the lips.<BR>E.<BR>ओष्ठ and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठोपमफला
ओष्ठोपमफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The creeper, (Bryonia grandis): see ओष्ठी.<BR>E.<BR>ओष्ठ a lip, उपम like, फल a flower, अच् and टाप् affixes; whose flower resembles a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ<BR>The diphthong Au or Ou, having the same sound as in Our, and considered as the fourteenth vowel of the Nāgarī alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of,<BR>1 Calling, (ho! hola.)<BR>2 Of addressing, (the vocative particle oh.)<BR>3 A particle of prohibition, and<BR>4 Of asseveration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ<BR>m. (-औः)<BR>The serpent ANANTA.<BR>f. (-औः)<BR>The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ<BR>ind.<BR>The mystical prefix proper for Śūdras: see ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थक
औक्थक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman acquainted with the Uktha portion of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>उक्था, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्ष|औक्षं
औक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Relating to an ox, derived from one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उक्षन्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्षक|औक्षकं
औक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A herd of oxen.<BR>E.<BR>उक्ष an ox, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औख्य|औख्यं
औख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Boiled or dressed in a pot.<BR>E.<BR>उखा a cauldron, a saucepan, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औचित्य|औचित्यं
औचित्य<BR>nf. (-त्यं-ती)<BR>Propriety, aptness, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>उचित proper, ष्यञ् affix in the abstract sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औजसिक|औजसिकः
औजसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hero.<BR>E.<BR>ओजस् strength, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुपिक|औडुपिकः
औडुपिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A passenger, one going in a raft or boat.<BR>E.<BR>उडुप, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औडुम्बर|औडुंबर|औडुम्बरं|औडुम्बरः
औडुम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Coppery, made of copper, &c.<BR>2 Made of the wood of the Uḍumbara fig tree.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of YAMA the regent of death.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A kind of leprosy.<BR>2 Copper.<BR>E.<BR>उडुम्बर, and अण affix: see उडुम्बर, उदुम्बर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औड्र|औड्रः
औड्र<BR>m. (-ड्रः)<BR>An Uriya, an inhabitant of Urisa.<BR>E.<BR>ओड्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्कर्ष्य|औत्कर्ष्यं
औत्कर्ष्य<BR>n. (-र्ष्यं)<BR>Excellence, superiority.<BR>E.<BR>उत्कर्ष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तमि|औत्तमिः
औत्तमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The third MANU.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तम, and इञ् patron. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=175" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तरपथिक
औत्तरपथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Going or coming in a northerly direction.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तर, पथ for पथिन् a road, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्तानपादि|औत्तानपादिः
औत्तानपादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>A name of DHRUVA, in mythology the son of UTTĀNAPĀDA, and grandson of the first MANU; in astronomy, the polar star, or the north pole itself.<BR>E.<BR>उत्तानपाद, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्पातिक
औत्पातिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Portentous, calamitous.<BR>E.<BR>उत्पात, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सङ्गिक|औत्संगिक
औत्सङ्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Carried or placed upon the hip or flank.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सङ्ग, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सर्गिक|औत्सर्गिकः
औत्सर्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Omitting, leaving.<BR>2 Terminative, completing^1, relating or belonging to a final ceremony, by which the rite is dismissed.<BR>3 Natural, inherent.<BR>4 Derivative, produced from or of, directly and naturally.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सर्ग abandoned, and ठञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औत्सुक्य|औत्सुक्यं
औत्सुक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Anxiety, perturbation, regret.<BR>E.<BR>उत्सुक anxious, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदक
औदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Watery, aquatic, of or belonging to water.<BR>E.<BR>उदक, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदनिक|औदनिकः
औदनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>ओदन boiled rice, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदरिक|औदरिकः
औदरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Selfishly voracious.<BR>E.<BR>उदर the belly, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदश्वित|औदश्वितं
औदश्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Made of buttermilk, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Buttermilk with an equal proportion of water.<BR>E.<BR>उदश्वित the same, and अण् affix; or with कस् added औदश्वित्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदार्य्य|औदार्य|औदार्यं|औदार्य्यं
औदार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Magnanimity, generosity, greatness.<BR>E.<BR>उदार liberal, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औदास्य|औदास्यं
औदास्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Philosophy, stoicism, indifference.<BR>E.<BR>उदास, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्दालक|औद्दालकं
औद्दालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bitter and acrid substance like honey, said to be found in the nest of the white ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धत्य|औद्धत्यं
औद्धत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Arrogance, disdain.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धत haughty, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धारिक
औद्धारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Heritable, portionable, belonging to a share or portion.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A portion or inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धार a share, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्धाहिक
औद्धाहिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A gift made to a woman at her marriage.<BR>E.<BR>उद्धाहिक, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्भिज्ज|औद्भिज्जं
औद्भिज्ज<BR>n. (-ज्जं)<BR>Fossil salt.<BR>E.<BR>उद्भिज् the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औद्भिद|औद्भिदं
औद्भिद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Rock or Sambher salt.<BR>E.<BR>उद्भिद्, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपकार्य्या|औपकार्या
औपकार्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A booth, a residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपगवक|औपगवकं
औपगवक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of the descendants of Upagu.<BR>E.<BR>औपगव the patronymic of उपगु, and वुन् aggregate aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपग्रस्तिक|औपग्रस्तिकः
औपग्रस्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eclipse, or the sun or moon in eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>उपग्रस्त an eclipse, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपग्रहिक|औपग्रहिकः
औपग्रहिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eclipse, or the sun or moon in eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>उपग्रह an eclipse, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपजानुक
औपजानुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Upon or near the knees.<BR>E.<BR>उपजानु, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपधेय
औपधेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The wheel of a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>उपधि, and ढञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनायनिक
औपनायनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the rite of investiture.<BR>E.<BR>उपनयन, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनिधिक|औपनिधिकं
औपनिधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a deposit.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A deposit, the thing pledged or deposited.<BR>E.<BR>उपनिधि, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपनिषद|औपनिषदः
औपनिषद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Scriptural, theological.<BR>E.<BR>उपनिषद, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपम्य|औपम्यं
औपम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Resemblance, similitude.<BR>E.<BR>उपमा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपयिक|औपयिकः
औपयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Right, fit, proper.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A means, an expedient.<BR>E.<BR>उपाय an expedient, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपरिष्ट
औपरिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं)<BR>Being or produced above.<BR>E.<BR>उपरिष्ट, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपरोधिक|औपरोधिकः
औपरोधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Proceeding from or relating to kindness or favour.<BR>2 Opposing, impeding, connected with or relating to a check or hindrance.<BR>E.<BR>उपरोध, and ठक् affix.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A staff of the wood of a particular tree, (the Pīlu.)<BR>E.<BR>उपरोध willingness to oblige, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपल
औपल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Stony, of stone.<BR>E.<BR>उपल, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपवस्त|औपवस्तं
औपवस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>Fasting, a fast.<BR>E.<BR>उपवस्त, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपवाह्य|औपवाह्यः
औपवाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Drawn for pleasure, (a carriage.)<BR>E.<BR>उपवह a conveyance, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपसर्गिक|औपसर्गिकः
औपसर्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Portentous.<BR>2 Prepositive, connected with a preposition.<BR>3 Relating to change, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Irregular action of the humors of the body, producing cold sweats, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उपसर्ग a portent, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपस्थ्य|औपस्थ्यं
औपस्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>Cohabitation, sexual enjoyment.<BR>E.<BR>उपस्थ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपाध्यायक
औपाध्यायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Preceptral, of or relating to a spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>उपाध्याय, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपानह्य
औपानह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be tied or bound on (grass, leather, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उपानह, and ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औपासन|औपासनः
औपासन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Devotional, holy, connected with or belonging to worship or service.<BR>E.<BR>उपासना, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औम
औम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Flaxen, made of flax, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उमा, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औमक
औमक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Flaxen, made of flax, &c.<BR>E.<BR>उमा, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औमीन|औमीनं
औमीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flax, (a field of, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>उमा flax, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरग|औरगं
औरग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गी-गं)<BR>Serpent, serpentine, relating or belonging to a snake.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The constellation Aśleṣā.<BR>E.<BR>उरग a snake, and अण् affix; a serpent is the regent of this constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्र|औरभ्रः
औरभ्र<BR>mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्री-भ्रं)<BR>Belonging to, &c. a sheep.<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>A coarse woollen blanket.<BR>n. (-भ्र)<BR>1 Mutton, the flesh of sheep.<BR>2 Woollen cloth.<BR>E.<BR>उरभ्र a sheep, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्रक|औरभ्रकं
औरभ्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flock of sheep.<BR>E.<BR>उरभ्र, and वुञ् affix of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरभ्रिक|औरभ्रिकः
औरभ्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to, produced by, &c. sheep.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shepherd.<BR>E.<BR>उरभ्र a sheep, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस|औरसः
औरस<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>A legitimate child, i. e. by a wife of the same tribe.<BR>E.<BR>उरस् the best, and अण् affix; the best of the twelve sons; also उरस्य and औरस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औरस्य|औरस्यः
औरस्य<BR>mf. (-स्यः-सी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्ण|और्ण्ण
और्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Woollen (cloth, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णा wool, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्णक|और्ण्णक
और्णक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of wool, woollen, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्णा, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्द्धदेहिक
और्द्धदेहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Obsequial, funeral.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Obsequies of a deceased person; whatever is given or performed on a person's decease, as burning, offering cakes, giving [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">Page177</a>] alms, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्ध or ऊर्द्ध्व above, देह the body, and ठक् affix; hence also और्द्ध्वदेहिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=176" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्द्धश्रोतसिक
और्द्धश्रोतसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A Śaiva or adherent of that doctrine^1, which gives ŚIVA the pre-eminence in the Hindu triad.<BR>E.<BR>ऊर्द्धश्रोतस् a name of ŚIVA, viz. above whom or in whose head is the river, (-श्रोतस्) (the Ganges,) and ठक् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्व|और्व|और्वः|और्व्वं|और्व्वः
और्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>उर्व्व a saint so named, from whose thighs sprang a being of flame, which was received by the ocean; the affix is अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्वशेय|और्वशेय|और्वशेयः|और्व्वशेयः
और्व्वशेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>उर्व्वशी the celestial courtezan, and ठक् affix; his birth being ascribed indirectly to this lady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

और्व्वानल|और्वानल
और्व्वानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>और्व्व, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक|औलूकं
औलूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flock of owls.<BR>E.<BR>उलूक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूक्य|औलूक्यः
औलूक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>A follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>उलूक an owl, and ष्यञ् affix, like an owl: this etymology, and perhaps the word, owes its origin probably to controversial animosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औलूखल
औलूखल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Ground or pounded in a mortar.<BR>E.<BR>उलूखल, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशनस
औशनस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The code, &c. of UŚANAS.<BR>E.<BR>उशनस्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीर|औशीरं|औशीरः
औशीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 The cow's tail used as a fan, the Chowri.<BR>2 A stick, or, according to some, the stick which serves as a handle to the preceding.<BR>3 A bed.<BR>4 A seat, a chair or stool.<BR>5 The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>उशीर the root of the Andropogon muricatum, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषण|औषणं
औषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Pungency.<BR>E.<BR>उषण pepper, &c. अण affix; also उषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषध|औषधं
औषध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>A medicament, a drug, any herb, mineral, &c. used in medicine.<BR>E.<BR>औषधि an annual plant, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधि|औषधिः
औषधि<BR>n. (-धिः)<BR>A deciduous plant, an annual as grass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>see औषधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीय
औषधीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Medicinal.<BR>E.<BR>औषध, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषर|औषरं
औषर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Fossile salt.<BR>2 Iron stone.<BR>E.<BR>ऊषरा desert soil, अण् affix; also with कन् added औषरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस
औषस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Early, matutinal.<BR>E.<BR>उषस् the dawn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिक
औषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Early, morning, &c. with the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>उषा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्र
औष्ट्र<BR>mfn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Derived from or relating to a camel.<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>The camel genus or species.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A herd of camels.<BR>E.<BR>उष्ट्र a camel, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्य|औष्म्यं
औष्म्य<BR>n. (-ष्म्यं)<BR>Heat, warmth.<BR>E.<BR>उष्म, warm, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क<BR>The first consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, and the first of the guttural letters, corresponding to K or C in can, designated by the latter in Sir WM. JONES'S system, but in this work by the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क<BR>m. (कः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 Of KĀMADEVA.<BR>4 Of fire.<BR>5 Air or wind.<BR>6 A title of YAMA.<BR>7 The sun.<BR>8 The soul.<BR>9 A clever or dexterous man.<BR>10 A king, a prince.<BR>11 A knot or joint.<BR>12 A peacock.<BR>13 The mind.<BR>14 The body.<BR>15 Time.<BR>16 Wealth, property.<BR>17 Sound.<BR>18 Light, splendor.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>4 Hair.<BR>5 A head of hair.<BR>pron. mfn. (कः का किम्)<BR>Who or what: see किम्.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, or कच to shine, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्य
कंय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Happy.<BR>E.<BR>कं happiness, यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्यु
कंय्यु<BR>mfn. (-य्युः-य्युः-य्यु)<BR>Happy, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>कं, and युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंश|कंशः
कंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A goblet: see कंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस|कंसं|कंसः
कंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A proper name; KAṂSA king of Mathura the uncle and enemy of KṚṢṆA, by whom he was slain; as the foe of the deity, he is considered an Asura or demon.<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>1 A goblet, a drinking vessel; also कंश and कांस्य.<BR>2 A metal, tutanag or white copper; also bell metal.<BR>3 A measure.<BR>E.<BR>कमु to desire, सः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसक|कंसकं
कंसक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mineral substance, (a salt of iron?) used as an application to the eyes: see पुष्पकासीस.<BR>E.<BR>कंस, and क affix of similarity; of similar white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकार|कंसकारः
कंसकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A worker in pewter or white brass.<BR>E.<BR>कंस and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसजित्
कंसजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A title of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कंस, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसहन्
कंसहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हन् from हन, to kill; the destroyer of KAṂSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसाराति|कंसारातिः
कंसाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>KṚṢṆA, or VIṢṆU in that character.<BR>E.<BR>कंस, and अराति an enemy, the foe of KAṂSA; hence also कंसारि and other similar epithets: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारि|कंसारिः
कंसारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसास्थि
कंसास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>Tutanag, white copper, any alloy of tin and copper.<BR>E.<BR>कंस white metal, and अस्थि bone, fig. substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of bellmetal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कंस, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit for or relating to a cup.<BR>E.<BR>कंस, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसोद्भवा
कंसोद्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A fragrant earth: see तुवरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक
कक<BR>r. 1st cl. (ककते)<BR>1 To be proud.<BR>3 To be unsteady.<BR>4 To be thirsty.<BR>(इ) ककि (कंकते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख
कक्ख<BR>r. 1st cl. (कक्खति)<BR>To laugh. to laugh, at or deride: see कख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककन्द|ककंदः|ककन्दः
ककन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>कनी to shine, affix द, and the initial repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जलः
ककुञ्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bird, the Cātaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुत्स्थ|ककुत्स्थः
ककुत्स्थ<BR>m. (-त्स्थः)<BR>A prince, the grandson of IKṢVĀKU, and ancestor of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>ककुद् an emblem of royalty, and स्थ who resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद्<BR>f. (-त्) or ककुद mn. (-दः-दं)<BR>1 The hump on the shoulders of the Indian bull.<BR>2 An ensign or symbol of royalty, as the white parasol, &c.<BR>3 Chief, pre-eminent.<BR>4 The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>क happiness, कु to sound, affixes क्विप् and तुक्; त becomes द; or with a final vowel, taking an additional affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्मत्<BR>m. (-द्मान्)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>f. (-द्मती)<BR>The hip and loins.<BR>E.<BR>ककुद् a bull's hump, &c. affix मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिकन्या
ककुद्मिकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>ककुद्मिन् a mountain, कन्या a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-द्मी-द्मिनी-द्मि)<BR>1 Peaked.<BR>2 Humped.<BR>m. (-द्मी)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>ककुद, and मिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुन्दर|ककुंदर|ककुंदरं|ककुन्दरं
ककुन्दर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The cavities of the loins: see कुकुन्दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ्<BR>f. (-प्)<BR>1 Space, region or quarter, as east, west, &c.<BR>2 Beauty, splendor.<BR>3 Unornamented hair, or the hair hanging [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">Page178</a>] down as a tail.<BR>4 A wreath of Champaka flowers.<BR>5 A Rāgiṇī or personified mode of music.<BR>6 A Śāstra or sacred treatise.<BR>E.<BR>क wind, स्कुभ to spread, क्विप् affix and the स is dropped; or कक to be proud, उभ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=177" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna, Rox.)<BR>2 A part of a lute, the belly, a wooden vessel covered with leather placed under its neck to render the sound deeper, or a crooked piece of wood at the end of the lute.<BR>3 One of the Rāgas or personified musical modes.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Space, region, quarter: see ककुभ्.<BR>2 One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR>E.<BR>ककुभ् space, and अच् affix; or क wind, स्कुभ spread, क affix and स rejected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभादनी
ककुभादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of perfume: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुक|ककेरुकः
ककेरुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A worm in the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क
कक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (कक्कति)<BR>To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोल|कक्कोलः
कक्कोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A perfume, a plant bearing a berry, the inner part of which is a waxy and aromatic substance.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The berry, possibly the fruit of the Cocculus Indicus.<BR>E.<BR>कक to be proud, with क्विप् affix, कुल to accumulate, अच् affix; also with कन् added कक्कोलक (-कः-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख
कक्ख<BR>(ए) r. 1st cl. (कक्खति)<BR>To laugh, to laugh at, to deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Hard, solid.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>कक्ख to deride, अटन् affix, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्; also खक्खट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटपत्रक|कक्खटपत्रकः
कक्खटपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant of the fibres of which a kind of rope is made, (Corchorus olitorius, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कक्खट hard, पत्र a leaf, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्व
कक्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (कक्वति)<BR>To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष|कक्षः
कक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The armpit.<BR>2 A spreading creeper, a climbing plant.<BR>3 Grass.<BR>4 Dry grass.<BR>5 A wood, a forest.<BR>6 A forest of dead trees, a dry wood.<BR>7 A private or inner chamber or part of a house.<BR>8 Sin.<BR>9 A buffalo.<BR>10 The side or flank.<BR>11 (In astronomy,) The orbit of a planet, or the circle anciently termed a deferent.<BR>12 A gate.<BR>13 The beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)<BR>1 A wall.<BR>2 The end of the lower garment, which after the cloth is carried round the body, is brought up behind, and tucked into the waistband.<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 An elephant's rope, the string round his neck, also his girth.<BR>2 A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>3 An enclosure, a part or division of an edifice.<BR>4 A part of a car.<BR>5 Objection or reply in argument.<BR>6 Similarity, parity.<BR>7 Emulation, rivalship.<BR>8 The jeweller's weight, the Ratti.<BR>9 Painful boils in the armpit, side, shoulder, &c.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A constellation, a star: see कक्ष्या, कच्छ, काञ्चि, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt or kill, स Uṇādi affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षरुहा
कक्षरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>E.<BR>कक्ष an enclosure, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षशाय|कक्षशायः
कक्षशाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>कक्ष an inner room, शाय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षान्तर|कक्षांतर
कक्षान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The inner or private apartment.<BR>E.<BR>कक्ष and अन्तर interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षापट|कक्षापटः
कक्षापट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A cloth passed between the legs to cover the privities.<BR>E.<BR>कक्षा a girdle, and पट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावत्|कक्षावन्त्
कक्षावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>कक्षा a reply, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षावेक्षक|कक्षावेक्षकः
कक्षावेक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A doorkeeper.<BR>2 A guard of the queen's apartments.<BR>3 Keeper of a royal garden.<BR>4 A painter.<BR>5 A poet.<BR>6 A debauchee.<BR>7 Eagerness of feeling, strength of sentiment.<BR>E.<BR>कक्षा an enclosure, and अबेक्ष to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षोत्था
कक्षोत्था<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>The cup or receptacle of a balance.<BR>f. (-क्ष्या)<BR>1 The girth of an elephant, of rope or leather.<BR>2 A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>3 The enclosure of an edifice; that is, either the wall, &c. so enclosing, or the court or chamber constituting the enclosure.<BR>4 The inner apartment of a palace.<BR>5 Similarity.<BR>6 Effort, exertion.<BR>7 An upper garment.<BR>8 A shrub, yielding the black and red berry, that serves as a jeweller's weight; the Ratti or Gunja, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>कक्ष the flank, &c. यत् affix; see कक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख
कख<BR>r. 1st cl. (ए) कखे (कखति)<BR>To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also कक्ख and खक्ख q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>An enclosure, a division of a large building: see कक्ष्या.<BR>E.<BR>कख to deride, यत् affix, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग
कग<BR>r. 1st cl. (ए) कगे (कगति)<BR>To perform any action: the meaning of this root is not given in many lists, from its application being indefinitely various.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्क|कंक|कंकः|कङ्कः
कङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A heron.<BR>2 YAMA or death.<BR>3 A false or pretended Brahman.<BR>4 A title of YUDHIṢṬHIRA, from his assuming the disguise of a Brahman.<BR>5 A man of the second or military tribe.<BR>6 One of the eighteen division of the continent.<BR>7 The brother of KAṂSA.<BR>8 A kind of mango.<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>1 A daughter of UGRASENA.<BR>2 A sort of sandal.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कट|कंकट|कंकटः|कङ्कटः
कङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Mail, defensive armour.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, Uṇādi affix अटन्, and with कन् added कङ्कटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कटेरी
कङ्कटेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Turmerick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कण|कंकण|कंकणं|कङ्कणं|कंकणः|कङ्कणः
कङ्कण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 A bracelet or ornament of the wrist.<BR>2 A string or ribbon tied round the wrist.<BR>3 An ornament or trinket.<BR>4 A crest.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small bell or tinkling ornament; also किङ्किणी and कङ्कणीका.<BR>E.<BR>कं happily, agreeably, कण to sound, or the reiterative form of कण and अच् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कणीका|कंकणीका
कङ्कणीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See कङ्कणी.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound in the reiterative form, and ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत|कंकत|कंकतं|कङ्कतं|कंकतः|कङ्कतः
कङ्कत<BR>mfn. (-तः-तिका or -ती-तं)<BR>A comb, an instrument for cleaning the hair.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, अतच् affix, fem. ङीष्, or कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोट|कङ्कत्रोटः
कङ्कत्रोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A kind of fish commonly Kankila, (Esox Cancila, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क a heron, and त्रोटि, the throat; whose long snout resembles the beak of a heron; also कङ्कत्रोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कत्रोटि|कङ्कत्रोटिः
कङ्कत्रोटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A kind of fish: see the preceding; also जलसूचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कपत्र|कंकपत्र|कङ्कपत्रः
कङ्कपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क, and पत्र leaf, (feather.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमाला
कङ्कमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Beating time by clapping the hands: see करताली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कमुख|कंकमुख|कङ्कमुखः
कङ्कमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A pair of tongs.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>A sort of forceps.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क, and मुख the mouth; heron-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कर|कंकर|कङ्करं|कङ्करः
कङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Vile, bad.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Buttermilk mixed with water. see कञ्जर.<BR>E.<BR>क implying bad, or कं water, कर what does or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=178" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्करोल|कंकरोलः|कङ्करोलः
कङ्करोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small tree, (Alangium hexapetalum): see निकोचक; the word in the dialects Kāṅkarol is applied to a species of gourd, (Momordica mixta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कलोद्य
कङ्कलोद्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>A kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कशत्रु|कङ्कशत्रुः
कङ्कशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum): see शालपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क a heron, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कशाय|कंकशाय|कङ्कशायः
कङ्कशाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क a heron, and शाय sleeping, sleeping like a heron, from शीङ्^1 and घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्का|कंका
कङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>Scent of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्काल|कंकाल|कंकालं|कंकालः|कङ्कालः
कङ्काल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The skeleton.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, कालच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कालमालिन्|कंकालमालिन्
कङ्कालमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A title of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्काल, माला, a necklace, and इनि affix; whose necklace is formed of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कु|कंकुः|कङ्कुः
कङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>1 The brother of KAṂSA.<BR>2 A sort of Panic: see कङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्कुष्ट
कङ्कुष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A medicinal earth, described as of two colours, one of a silvery and one of a gold colour, or one of a light and one of a dark yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केरु|कंकेरुः|कङ्केरुः
कङ्केरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A kind of crow.<BR>E.<BR>कङ्क an imitative sound, ईर to send, to utter, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केलि|कंकेलि|कङ्केलिः
कङ्केलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The Asoka tree, (Jonesia asoca); also कङ्केल्लि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्ल|कंकेल्लः|कङ्केल्लः
कङ्केल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Chenopodium esculentum, Rox.) see वास्तुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्केल्लि|कंकेल्लिः|कङ्केल्लिः
कङ्केल्लि<BR>m. (-ल्लिः)<BR>A tree, (Jonesia asoca, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्ख|कंखं|कङ्खं
कङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>Enjoyment, fruition.<BR>E.<BR>कखि to deride, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गु|कंगु|कङ्गुः
कङ्गु<BR>f. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>A kind of Panick seed, (Panicum Italicum); several varieties of it are cultivated, and form articles of food for the poor.<BR>E.<BR>क water, अगि to go, कु affix; also with ऊङ् affix कङ्गू, and with कन् added कङ्गुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुनी
कङ्गुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of Panick: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुनीपत्रा
कङ्गुनीपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कङ्गुल|कंगुल|कंगुलः|कङ्गुलः
कङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच|कचः
कच<BR>r. 1st cl. (कचते)<BR>1 To bind.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>3 To sound.<BR>(इ) कचि r. 1st cl. (कञ्चते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To bind; also काचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच|कचः
कच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 The hair.<BR>2 A proper name, the son of VṚHASPATI.<BR>3 Binding or a binding.<BR>3 A cicatrix, a dry or healed sore.<BR>5 A cloud.<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>2 Beauty, brilliance.<BR>E.<BR>कच to bind, &c. अच् affix, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गन|कचंगन|कचंगनं|कचङ्गनं
कचङ्गन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A free market, a place of sale that pays no duty or custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचङ्गल|कचंगल|कचंगलः|कचङ्गलः
कचङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>कच a cloud, अङ्ग the body, and ल what takes or receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचप|कचपं|कचपः
कचप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Grass.<BR>2 A leaf.<BR>E.<BR>कच a cloud, and प what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचपक्ष|कचपक्षः
कचपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Much or ornamented hair.<BR>E.<BR>कच hair, and पक्ष, in this combination, abundance; similar compounds are made with पाश and हस्त, कचपाश, कचहस्त; also with केश hair, as केशपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचपाश|कचपाशः
कचपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचमाल|कचमालः
कचमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>कच a cloud, and माला a necklace, ड affix; also खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचरिपुफला
कचरिपुफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Śami tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचहस्त|कचहस्तः
कचहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>See कचपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाकु|कचाकुः
कचाकु<BR>mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>1 Ill disposed, wicked.<BR>2 Intolerable, difficult to be borne.<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाचित
कचाचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having long or dishevelled hair.<BR>E.<BR>कच, and अचित not gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचाटुर|कचाटुरः
कचाटुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कचु|कचुः
कचु<BR>f. (-चुः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia and other kinds, many of which are cultivated for food): see कच्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चट|कच्चटं
कच्चट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>An aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चर|कच्चरं
कच्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Dirty, foul.<BR>2 Soiled, spoiled by dirt.<BR>3 Vile, wicked, bad.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Buttermilk diluted with water.<BR>E.<BR>कुत् bad, vile, चर what goes or is, from चर with अच् affix; कत् is substituted for कत्, and the त changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्चित्
कच्चित्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle implying wish or desire, (may it be so); also introducing a kind enquiry, (I hope that it is so, &c.)<BR>2 A particle implying an alternative, whether, whether or not.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छ|कच्छं|कच्छः
कच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>Contiguous to water, (land, &c.)<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 Marshy ground, a marsh, a morass.<BR>2 Ground bordering water or watery soil, as the bank of a river, the margin of a lake or tank, a mound or causeway, &c.<BR>3 Level land skirting mountains.<BR>4 A tree, the timber of which is used for making furniture, &c. commonly Tūn, (Cedrela Tunna, Rox.)<BR>5 Another tree, (Hibiscus Populneoides.)<BR>6 A part of a boat.<BR>mf. (-च्छः-च्छा)<BR>The hem of a garment tucked into the waistband: see कक्ष.<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>1 A plant, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.) see वाराही.<BR>2 A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>क water, छो to cut or break, क affix; or कच to bind, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छटिका
कच्छटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The end or hem of a lower garment or cloth gathered up behind, and tucked into the waistband; also कक्षा and कच्छाटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छप|कच्छपः
कच्छप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>2 One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or treasures.<BR>3 An attitude in wrestling.<BR>4 A flat kind of still.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>1 A female tortoise, also a small one.<BR>2 A kind of lute, also the lute of SARASVATĪ.<BR>3 A cutaneous disease, wart or blotch.<BR>E.<BR>कच्छ a morass, and प who cherishes, who inhabits watery places: the lute, &c. are so named from being similar in shape to the tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छपिका
कच्छपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pimple, a blotch or wart.<BR>2 A wart accompanying gonorrhoea.<BR>E.<BR>कच्छप a tortoise, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छभू
कच्छभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>Marshy ground, a swamp, a morass.<BR>E.<BR>कच्छ, and भू land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छरुहा
कच्छरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A kind of grass, Dūrvā or Dūb, (Agrostis linearis, Lin., Panicus dactilon, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कच्छ marshy ground, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छाटिका
कच्छाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See कच्छटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छान्त|कच्छांत|कच्छान्तः
कच्छान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The border of a lake or stream.<BR>E.<BR>कच्छ, and अन्त term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छु|कच्छुः
कच्छु<BR>f. (-च्छुः)<BR>Itch, formation of watery pustules on the hands, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, उ affix; also कच्छू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुघ्नी
कच्छुघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A vegetable, (Trichosanthes.)<BR>E.<BR>कच्छु, and ध्नी what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छुर|कच्छुरः
कच्छुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Scabby, itchy.<BR>2 Unchaste, libidinous.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A plant, (a species of Hedysarum?)<BR>2 Cowach, (Dolichos carpopogon.)<BR>3 Another plant: see शठी.<BR>E.<BR>कच्छ itch or scab, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=179" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छू
कच्छू<BR>f. (-च्छूः)<BR>Scab or itch.<BR>E.<BR>कष to injure, ऊ Uṇādi affix, and छ substituted for ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छूमती
कच्छूमती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Cowach, (Dolichos carpopogon.)<BR>E.<BR>चच्छू itch, and मतुप् affix; producing an itching upon application to the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्छोटिका
कच्छोटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The fastening of the lower garment: see कच्छटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कच्वी
कच्वी<BR>f. (-च्ची)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia and other kinds, several of which are cultivated for food); also written कचु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज<BR>r. 1st cl. (कजति)<BR>To be disturbed or confused with joy, pride, or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज|कजं
कज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Watery, aquatic, produced in or by water.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्जल|कज्जलं|कज्जलः
कज्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Lampblack, considered as a collyrium, being applied upon the eyelashes or eyelids, medicinally or ornamentatively; also sulphuret of lead or antimony, when so used.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Sulphuret of mercury, Æthiop's mineral.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>A kind of fish, (Cyprinus atratus,) or any kind peculiar to stagnant waters, whence the name.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, and जल water or juice, as the moisture of the collyrium, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वल|कज्ज्वलं
कज्ज्वल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Lampblack, especially considered as an application to the eyes: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कत bad, and ज्वल flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वलध्वज
कज्ज्वलध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>कज्ज्वल, and ध्वज a sign; also कज्जलध्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कज्ज्वलरोचक
कज्ज्वलरोचक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>The wooden stand or tripod on which the lamp is placed, a candlestick.<BR>E.<BR>कज्ज्वल and रुच to shine; affixes घञ् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चट|कञ्चटं|कञ्चटः
कञ्चट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant: see लाङ्गली, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Another species of the same, (Commelina Bengalensis.)<BR>E.<BR>कं water, and चट to divide; alluding to the habits of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चड|कञ्चडः
कञ्चड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A plant, (Commelina Bengalensis): see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चार|कंचार|कंचारः|कञ्चारः
कञ्चार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>कं heaven, and चर to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चिका|कंचिका
कञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The branch of a bamboo.<BR>2 A small boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुक|कंचुक|कंचुकः|कञ्चुकः
कञ्चुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The skin of a snake.<BR>2 Armour, mail.<BR>3 A bodice or jacket.<BR>4 Cloth, clothes.<BR>5 A kind of drawers or short breeches.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The name of a plant.<BR>E.<BR>कचि to bind or shine, affix उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकालु|कंचुकालु|कंचुकालुः|कञ्चुकालुः
कञ्चुकालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>कञ्चुक a serpent's skin, and आलुक poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुकिन्|कंचुकिन्
कञ्चुकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>2 A libidinous man, a debauchee.<BR>3 A serpent.<BR>4 Agallochum.<BR>5 Barley.<BR>6 A sort of pulse, (Chenna.)<BR>E.<BR>कञ्चुक armour, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्चुलिका|कंचुलिका
कञ्चुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bodice or jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्ज|कंज|कञ्जं|कंजः|कञ्जः
कञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>Produced in or from water.<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The hair.<BR>n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>1 Nectar, the food of the immortals.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कं happiness, water, &c. and ज what is born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जक|कंजक|कंजकः|कञ्जकः
कञ्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of bird, the Mayana: see कञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जज|कंजज|कञ्जजः
कञ्जज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कञ्ज a lotus, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जन|कंजन|कंजनः|कञ्जनः
कञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The Mayana or Maina, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR>2 A name of KANDARPA, the deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>कचि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जर|कंजर|कंजरः|कञ्जरः
कञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 The belly.<BR>4 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कञ्ज a lotus, &c. ऋ to hate or injure, अच or घञ् affix कञ्जार, the pen. made short; also derived by some from कजि, a Sautra root, to produce or grow, and अर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जल|कंजल|कंजलः|कञ्जलः
कञ्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Maina: see कञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जार|कंजार|कंजारः|कञ्जारः
कञ्जार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Muni or holy sage.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ, &c. see कञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कञ्जिका|कंजिका
कञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica): see ब्रह्मयष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट|कटः
कट<BR>r. 1st cl. (कटति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To live with difficulty.<BR>(इ) कटि (कण्टति)<BR>To go.<BR>(ए) कटे (कटति)<BR>1 To rain.<BR>2 To encompass, to cover or screen.<BR>(ई) कटी (कटति)<BR>To go or approach:<BR>with प्र prefixed,<BR>verb 10th cl. (प्रकटयति)<BR>To appear, to become apparent or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट|कटः
कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>An agent in any action.<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>1 The hip.<BR>2 The hollow above the hip or the loins, also the hip and loins.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The temples of the elephant.<BR>2 A mat.<BR>3 A twist of straw or grass.<BR>4 A screen of the same.<BR>5 A corpse.<BR>6 A time or season.<BR>7 Much, excessive.<BR>8 Grass.<BR>9 A place where dead bodies are burnt or buried, a place of sepulture.<BR>10 A hearse, a bier, a bed, &c. used for conveying a dead body.<BR>11 An annual plant.<BR>12 A thin piece of wood, a plank.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>कट to rain or encompass, अच् affix, fem. ङीष्; also कटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटक|कटकं|कटकः
कटक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The side or ridge of a hill or mountain.<BR>2 Table land.<BR>3 Sea salt.<BR>4 A ring placed as an ornament upon an elephant's tusk.<BR>5 A bracelet of gold, shell, &c.<BR>6 A zone.<BR>7 A royal metropolis.<BR>8 A city or town.<BR>9 A village.<BR>10 A house or dwelling.<BR>11 A camp.<BR>12 An army.<BR>13 A circle.<BR>14 A wheel.<BR>E.<BR>कट to encompass, कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटकिन्
कटकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>कटक land on a hill, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटकोल|कटकोलः
कटकोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A spitting vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटखादक|कटखादकं|कटखादकः
कटखादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>An eater, one who eats voraciously.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A glass vessel, a tumbler or bowl.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 A jackall.<BR>E.<BR>कट much, or a corpse, खाद to eat, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटङ्कट|कटंकट|कटंकटः|कटङ्कटः
कटङ्कट<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>कट a mat, &c. कट who goes, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटङ्कटेरी|कटंकटेरी
कटङ्कटेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>2 Yellow saunders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटन|कटनं
कटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Roof or thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटपूटन
कटपूटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A kind of goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटप्रू
कटप्रू<BR>m. (-प्रूः)<BR>1 A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR>2 A kind of demigod, one of the class of Vidyādharas.<BR>3 A Rākṣasa, an imp or demon.<BR>4 Gambling, playing with dice.<BR>5 A worm.<BR>E.<BR>कट much, प्र to go, क्विप् affix, and the final is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटप्रोथ|कटप्रोथः
कटप्रोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The buttocks: see कटिप्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटभङ्ग|कटभंग|कटभङ्गः
कटभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Gleaning, plucking or gathering corn by the hand.<BR>2 Royal misfortune, as deposure, defeat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कट, &c. भञ्ज to break, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटभी
कटभी<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>1 A plant, (Heartpea, Cardiaspermum halicacabum.)<BR>2 Another creeper, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>E.<BR>कट to encompass, and भज to serve, ड and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटमालिनी
कटमालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Wine or any vinous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्ब|कटंबः|कटम्बः
कटम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, and अम्ब Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=180" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्बरा
कटम्बरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>कट to surround, अच् affix; what invests the body, as sickness; वृ to screen or defend, मुम् inserted, and अच् and टाप् affixes; also कटम्भरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटम्भरा|कटंभरा
कटम्भरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A plant, (Poederia fetida.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant, कटुकीः see the preceding.<BR>3 A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR>4 A female elephant.<BR>5 Red arsenic.<BR>6 A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides): see मुर्व्वा.<BR>7 Hog-weed.<BR>E.<BR>as before, भृ to nourish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटव्रण|कटव्रणः
कटव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of BHĪMASENA, one of the five Pāṇḍava brothers.<BR>E.<BR>कट much, व्रण who wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटशर्करा
कटशर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant: see गाङ्गेष्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटस्थल
कटस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The hip and loins.<BR>2 An elephant's temples.<BR>E.<BR>कट, and स्थल place; also कटभू, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाकु|कटाकुः
कटाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, काकु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाक्ष|कटाक्षः
कटाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A leer, a glance or side look.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाक्षावेक्षण
कटाक्षावेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Casting lewd or amorous glances, ogling.<BR>E.<BR>कटाक्ष a leer, and अवेक्षण looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाग्नि|कटाग्निः
कटाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 A fire of grass or straw.<BR>2 Straw, &c. investing a criminal who is to be burnt and set on fire.<BR>E.<BR>कठ, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटायन|कटायनं
कटायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटार|कटारः
कटार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A libidinous man, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटाह|कटाहः
कटाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A shallow boiler for oil or butter.<BR>2 A frying pan.<BR>3 A winnowing basket.<BR>4 A turtle's shell.<BR>5 A young buffalo whose horns are just appearing.<BR>6 A Dvīpa or division of the known continent, so called.<BR>7 Hell, the infernal regions.<BR>8 A well.<BR>E.<BR>कट much, &c. हन to destroy, with आङ् prefixed, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटि|कटिः
कटि<BR>mf. (-टिः-टी)<BR>1 The hip.<BR>2 The buttocks.<BR>3 An elephant's cheek.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, कि affix, fem. ङीष्; see कट and कटिप्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटितट
कटितट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The loins, the hip.<BR>E.<BR>कटि, and तट shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटित्र|कटित्रं
कटित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 An ornament of small bells worn round the loins.<BR>2 A cloth so worn.<BR>3 Armour for the hip and loins.<BR>E.<BR>कटि the hip, and त्र what preserves, from त्रै with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिदेश|कटिदेशः
कटिदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The loins.<BR>E.<BR>कटि and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिन्
कटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>1 Matted, screened.<BR>2 Loined, having handsome loins, &c.<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कट an elephant's temples, &c. इनि pos. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिप्रोथ|कटिप्रोथः
कटिप्रोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The buttocks.<BR>E.<BR>कटि the hip or loins, and प्रोथ to be equal to; also written कटप्रोथ, कटीप्रोथ, and severally कटि and प्रोथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिरोहक|कटिरोहकः
कटिरोहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The rider of an elephant, as distinct from the driver, the person that sits upon the loins.<BR>E.<BR>कटि the loins, रुह to mount, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिल्लक|कटिल्लकः
कटिल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of the balsam apple, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, &c. इल्ल affix कन् added; also कठिल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिशीर्षक|कटिशीर्षकः
कटिशीर्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The hip and loins, or the hollow above the hip.<BR>E.<BR>कटि, शीर्ष the head or superior part, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिशृङ्खला|कटिशृंखला
कटिशृङ्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A girdle of small bells.<BR>E.<BR>कटि the loins, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटिसूत्र|कटिसूत्रं
कटिसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A female zone or waist-band.<BR>E.<BR>कटि the loins, and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटी
कटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>See कटि and कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीतल|कटीतलः
कटीतल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A crooked sword, a sabre or scymitar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीर|कटीरं|कटीरः
कटीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 The cavity of the loins, or the iliac regions.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mons veneris.<BR>2 A cave.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, and ईरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटीरक|कटीरकं|कटीरकः
कटीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The posteriors.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटु|कटुः
कटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः or -ट्वी-टु)<BR>1 Pungent.<BR>2 Envious.<BR>3 Fierce, impetuous, hot.<BR>4 Fragrant.<BR>5 Bad scented, ill smelling.<BR>6 Displeasing, disagreeable.<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 Pungency or a pungent taste.<BR>2 A flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 A sort of gourd, (Trichosanthes.)<BR>n. (-टु)<BR>1 An improper action, an act which ought not to have been done.<BR>2 Blaming, reviling, scandal.<BR>f. (-टुः)<BR>1 The name of a medicinal plant; also कटुका and कटुकी.<BR>2 A plant which bears a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>3 Mustard.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, &c. and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुक|कटुकं|कटुकः
कटुक<BR>m. (-कः-की)<BR>1 A plant, the bark and seed of which have an acrid and bitter taste, and are used in medicine for worms, dysentery, &c. (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>2 Gigantic swallow wort, (Colotropis gigantea.)<BR>3 A fragrant kind of grass.<BR>4 Mustard.<BR>5 A gourd: see पटोल.<BR>f. (-का or -की)<BR>A medicinal plant, used as a sedative and laxative; also कटुरोहिणी.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A compound of three pungent substances, as black pepper, long pepper, and dry ginger: see त्रिकटु.<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकन्द|कटुकन्दः
कटुकन्द<BR>mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>1 A plant, (Morunga guilandina, and Hyperanthera.)<BR>2 Ginger, the fresh root or the plant.<BR>3 Garlic.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and कन्द a root; having a pungent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकालावु|कटुकालावुः
कटुकालावु<BR>m. (-वुः)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>कटुक pungent and acrid, अलावु a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकीट|कटुकीटः
कटुकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A gnat or musquito.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुकीटक|कटुकीटकः
कटुकीटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gnat or musquito.<BR>E.<BR>कटु fierce, and कीटक a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुक्वाण|कटुक्वाणः
कटुक्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bird, jacana, (Parra goensis.)<BR>E.<BR>कटु disagreeable, क्वाण sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुग्रन्थि|कटुग्रन्थिः
कटुग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>Ginger, the root.<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, and ग्रन्थि joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुच्छद|कटुच्छदः
कटुच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a plant; also तगर.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and छद a leaf: having a pungent leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुता
कटुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Pungency, sharpness.<BR>2 Testiness, irritability.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and तल् affix; also with त्व, कटुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुतिक्तिका
कटुतिक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and तिक्त bitter, कन् affix with the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुतुम्बी
कटुतुम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, here meaning bitterly so, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुत्रय|कटुत्रयं
कटुत्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The aggregate of three spices, ginger, and long and black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुनिष्प्लाव|कटुनिष्प्लावः
कटुनिष्प्लाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Grain not inundated.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and निष्प्लाव, non-inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुपत्र|कटुपत्रः
कटुपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Oldenlandia biflora.)<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुफल|कटुफलः
कटुफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुभङ्ग|कटुभङ्गः
कटुभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुभद्र|कटुभद्रं|कटुभद्रः
कटुभद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>Ginger either fresh or dry.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=181" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुर|कटुरं|कटुरः
कटुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and रा to give, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुरव|कटुरवः
कटुरव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुरोहिणी
कटुरोहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, and रोहिणी that grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुवार्त्ताकी|कटुवार्ताकी
कटुवार्त्ताकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A variety of solanum.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and वार्त्ताकी the egg plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुवीजा
कटुवीजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटुस्नेह|कटुस्नेहः
कटुस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The mustard seed plant, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and स्नेह oily substance: yielding a pungent oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटूत्कट|कटूत्कटं
कटूत्कट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>कटु, and उत्कट best, and with कन् added कटूत्कटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोरा
कटोरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A shallow cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोल|कटोलः
कटोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A man of an inferior and degraded tribe, a Caṇḍāla, a Pariah, &c.<BR>2 A pungent flavour.<BR>E.<BR>कट to go, ओलच् Uṇādi affix; also कटोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कटोलवीणा
कटोलवीणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A kind of lute played by the common people.<BR>E.<BR>कटोल a Caṇḍāla, and वीणा a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्टार|कट्टारः
कट्टार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A weapon, a dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्फल|कट्फलः
कट्फल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small tree found in the north-west of Hindustan, the bark and seeds of which are used in medicine, and as aromatics; the fruit also is eaten; the common name is Kayaphal.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A plant, (Gmelina arborea, Rox.)<BR>2 The egg plant, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कट् instead of कटु acrid, and फल fruit, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वङ्ग|कट्वङ्गः
कट्वङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>2 A name of DILĪPA a king of Ayodhya.<BR>E.<BR>कटु pungent, &c. अङ्ग bark, body, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कट्वर|कट्वरं
कट्वर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Sauce, condiment.<BR>2 Buttermilk.<BR>3 The skim or whey of curds.<BR>E.<BR>कट to rain, &c. वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (कठति)<BR>To live in distress.<BR>(इ) कठि r. 1st and 10th cls. (कण्ठति-ते कण्ठयति)<BR>1 To grieve.<BR>2 To recollect.<BR>With उद् prefixed,<BR>to regret or miss, to lament, to bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठ|कठः
कठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>2 A note or simple sound.<BR>3 A portion of the Yajur Veda.<BR>4 A Mantra or mystical prayer.<BR>5 A Brahman.<BR>6 A Brahman versed in the Vedas, especially in the Rig Veda.<BR>7 A student of the same.<BR>8 Trouble, distress.<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>The wife of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>कठ to be confused, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठधूर्त्त|कठधूर्त|कठधूर्तः
कठधूर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A BRAHMAN skilled in the Kaṭha branch of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>कठ, and धूर्त्त cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठमर्द्द|कठमर्द|कठमर्दः|कठमर्द्दः
कठमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कठ distress, मर्द्द who dissipates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठर|कठरः
कठर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hard.<BR>E.<BR>कठ trouble, and र from रा to take or give, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठश्रोत्रिय|कठश्रोत्रियः
कठश्रोत्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A BRAHMAN who has studied the Kaṭha portion of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>कठ, and श्रोत्रिय a BRAHMAN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाध्यापक|कठाध्यापकः
कठाध्यापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A teacher of the Kaṭha portion of the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>कठ, and अध्यापक a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठाहक|कठाहकः
कठाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिका
कठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Chalk.<BR>2 The Tulasi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिञ्जर|कठिंजरः|कठिञ्जरः
कठिञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant worshipped by the Hindus, commonly Tulsi, (Ocymum sanctum, or sacred basil.)<BR>E.<BR>कठिन hard, and जृ to destroy, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिन|कठिनं|कठिनः
कठिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Hard, solid.<BR>2 Unkind, severe.<BR>3 Paralysed, rendered stiff or rigid.<BR>4 Difficult, obscure.<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>An earthen vessel.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A sweetmeat made with refined sugar.<BR>(-नी or निका)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>कठ to be confounded, and इनच् Uṇādi affix, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनता
कठिनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Firmness, hardness.<BR>2 Severity.<BR>3 Difficulty, obscurity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कठिनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनपृष्ठ|कठिनपृष्ठः
कठिनपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>कठिन, and पृष्ठ back; also कठिनपृष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनहृदय
कठिनहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Hardhearted, cruel, unkind.<BR>E.<BR>कठिन, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिनान्तःकरण
कठिनान्तःकरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Harsh, cruel, severe.<BR>E.<BR>कठिन, and अन्तःकरण disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिल्ल|कठिल्लः
कठिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A plant, (Momordica charantia): see कटिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठिल्लक|कठिल्लकः
कठिल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant: see the preceding.<BR>2 A name of Tulasi or holy basil.<BR>3 Hogweed.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding: see कटिल्ल and कटिल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठेर|कठेरः
कठेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A needy or distressed man, a pauper.<BR>E.<BR>कठ to be distressed, and एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठेरु
कठेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Indian Plutus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोर|कठोरः
कठोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Hard, solid.<BR>2 Severe, cruel.<BR>3 Full, complete, full-grown.<BR>4 Full, (as the moon.)<BR>E.<BR>कठ to be distressed, &c. आरन् Uṇādi affix; also कठोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोरता
कठोरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Hardness, firmness.<BR>2 Severity, rigor.<BR>E.<BR>तल्, added to the preceding; also कठोरत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कठोल|कठोलः
कठोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>See कठोर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड|कडः
कड<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (कडति)<BR>To be confused or disturbed by pleasure or pain, to be proud or mad, (the roots differ in some of the inflections.)<BR>(इ) कडि r. 1st cl. (कण्डते)<BR>The same as the preceding;<BR>also r. 1st and 10th cls. (कण्डति, कण्डयति)<BR>1 To break off a part, to tear, to separate or detach.<BR>2 To remove the chaff or husk of grain, &c.<BR>3 To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड|कडः
कड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Ignorant, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>कड to be perplexed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडक|कडकं
कडक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sea salt obtained by evaporation.<BR>E.<BR>कड to separate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्कर|कडंकर|कडंकरः|कडङ्करः
कडङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Straw, the stalks of various sorts of pulse, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कड made, कृ to make, खच् affix; also कडङ्गर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्करीय|कडंकरीय
कडङ्करीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be fed with straw.<BR>E.<BR>कडङ्कर, and छ affix; also with यत्, कडङ्कर्प्य; and from कडङ्ग, कडङ्गरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्ग|कडंगः|कडङ्गः
कडङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A spirituous liquor, a kind of rum.<BR>E.<BR>कड to be intoxicated, अङ्ग aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडङ्गर|कडंगर|कडंगरः|कडङ्गरः
कडङ्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Straw, chaff.<BR>E.<BR>कड, रक affix, अङ्गच् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडत्र|कडत्रं
कडत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel.<BR>E.<BR>गड to distil, अत्रन् Uṇādi affix, and क substituted for ग; also कलत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडम्ब|कडंब|कडंबः|कडम्बः
कडम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 The stalk of a potherb.<BR>2 The end or point.<BR>E.<BR>कड to separate, &c. अम्बच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडम्बी
कडम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus repens): see कलम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडार|कडारः
कडार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Tawny.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>2 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>कड to be confused, आरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कडितुल|कडितुलः
कडितुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar, a sacrificial knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कड्ड
कड्ड<BR>r. 1st cl. (कड्डति)<BR>To be rough, to be harsh or severe: the pen. is originally द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण<BR>(म) r. 1st cl. (कणति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To cry as in distress.<BR>(ऋ) कण r. 1st cl. (कणति)<BR>To go or approach.<BR>r. 10th cl. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">Page183</a>] (कणयति)<BR>To wink, to cover or close the eye with the lids or lashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=182" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण|कणः
कण<BR>mf. (-णः-णी or -णिका)<BR>1 Small, minute.<BR>2 An atom, a minute particle.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An eye of corn.<BR>2 The spark or facet of a gem.<BR>3 A spark of fire.<BR>4 A drop of water, &c.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Cummin seed.<BR>2 Long pepper.<BR>3 A kind of fly, (कुम्भीरमक्षिका) the crocodile fly?<BR>E.<BR>कण to contract, अच् affix fem. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणजीर|कणजीरः
कणजीर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A white kind of cummin seed.<BR>E.<BR>कण small, and जीर cummin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणजीरक|कणजीरकं
कणजीरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Small cummin seed.<BR>E.<BR>कण minute, and जीरक cummin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणभक्षक|कणभक्षकः
कणभक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>कण pepper, and भक्षक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणलाभ|कणलाभः
कणलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाटीन|कणाटीनः
कणाटीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>कण little, अट to go, and ईनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाटीर|कणाटीरः
कणाटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wagtail; also कणाटीरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणाद|कणादः
कणाद<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni, also called Kaśyapa: the author of the Vaiśeṣika philosophy.<BR>2 A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>कण a little, and अद to eat, referring to the abstemiousness of the saint; or आदा to take, alluding to the proverbial dishonesty of the artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिक|कणिकः
कणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A small particle, as a crystal, an eye of corn, &c.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>3 Whirling round a set of lamps at sacrificial ceremonies.<BR>4 The heart of wheat, commonly Suji, sharps or semoule.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An atom, a small particle.<BR>2 Small, minute: see कण.<BR>3 A plant, (Premna spinosa): see गणिकारिका.<BR>4 A kind of rice.<BR>E.<BR>कण small, वुन् affix, and इट् inserted, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणित|कणितं
कणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A cry or sound uttered through pain.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणिश|कणिशं|कणिशः
कणिश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>An ear or spike of corn.<BR>E.<BR>कण small, &c. affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीक|कणीकं|कणीकः
कणीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Small, diminutive.<BR>E.<BR>कण to be small, ईकन् Uṇādi affix; it is also written कनीक, and कणिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीचि|कणीचिः
कणीचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>1 A creeper in flower.<BR>2 A cart.<BR>3 The Abrus precatorius.<BR>E.<BR>कण to wink, ईचि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणीयस्
कणीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very small.<BR>2 Young, younger.<BR>E.<BR>कण small, and ईयसुन् superlative affix; also कनीयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कणेर|कणेरः
कणेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Cascaria ovata, &c.)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A courtezan.<BR>2 A she-elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कण to go, एर affix, or with एरु affix अणेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टक|कंटक|कंटकं|कंटकः|कण्टकः
कण्टक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A thorn.<BR>2 A paltry foe.<BR>3 A fish bone.<BR>4 Horripilation, or the erection of the hair of the body.<BR>5 Any annoyance or source of vexation.<BR>6 A term in the Nyāya philosophy, implying refutation of argument, detection of error, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A workshop, a manufactory.<BR>2 Fault, defect.<BR>3 The point of a pin or needle.<BR>4 A fish or marine monster, the symbol of KĀMADEVA: see मकर.<BR>5 A bamboo.<BR>E.<BR>कटि to divide, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकद्रुम|कंटकद्रुम|कण्टकद्रुमः
कण्टकद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The Śālmali or silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and द्रम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकफल|कंटकफल|कण्टकफलः
कण्टकफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The Jaka or bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>2 Another plant: see गोक्षुर.<BR>3 The castor oil tree.<BR>4 The Datura.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक a spike, and फल fruit; the term is applicable to any plant, the fruit of which is invested with a hairy or thorny coat; also कण्टकिफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकभुज्|कंटकभुज्
कण्टकभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and भुज who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकमर्द्दन|कण्टकमर्दन
कण्टकमर्द्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 What treads down or extracts thorns.<BR>2 What bridles or suppresses disturbances, annoyances, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Beating down thorns.<BR>2 Suppressing disturbances, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and मर्द्दन trampling on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकश्रेणी
कण्टकश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A porcupine.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and श्रेणी a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकागार|कण्टकागारः
कण्टकागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A porcupine.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकारिका|कंटकारिका
कण्टकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक a thorn, ऋ to go, अण् affix, कन् added with the feminine termination; also कण्टकारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकारी
कण्टकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A prickly nightshade: see the preceding.<BR>2 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>3 Another plant, commonly Buïñchi, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाल|कंटकालः|कण्टकालः
कण्टकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The bread-fruit tree or Jaka: see कण्टकफल.<BR>2 A species of the coral tree, (Erythrina Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक a thorn, आला to take, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाशन|कंटकाशन|कण्टकाशनः
कण्टकाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and अशन food; whose food is of thorns, thistles, &c.; also कण्टकभुज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकाष्ठील|कण्टकाष्ठीलः
कण्टकाष्ठील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of fish, one which has many bones.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, अस्थि a bone, and ईलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिज
कण्टकिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Produced from a fish.<BR>2 Borne by the mimosa tree.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टकिन. and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिन्|कंटकिन्
कण्टकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>1 Thorny, prickly.<BR>2 Vexatious, annoying.<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>3 A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>4 A bamboo.<BR>5 The jujube.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक a thorn or small bone, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिफल|कंटकिफल|कण्टकिफलः
कण्टकिफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Indian bread fruit tree or Jaka, (Artocarpus integrifolia): see कण्टकफल; also कण्टकीफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकिल|कंटकिल|कंटकिलः|कण्टकिलः
कण्टकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A thorny kind of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकीफल|कण्टकीफलः
कण्टकीफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See कण्टकिफल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टकोद्धरण
कण्टकोद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Weeding, extracting thorns, &c.<BR>2 Removing annoyances.<BR>3 Extirpating thieves, rogues, &c. or all national or public nuisances.<BR>E.<BR>कण्टक, and उद्धरण extracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टपत्र|कण्टपत्रः
कण्टपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A plant, commonly Buïñchi, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.) and कण्टपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टफल
कण्टफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The jack tree.<BR>2 The Datura plant.<BR>3 The castor oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ट for कण्टक a thorn or spike, फल fruit: see कण्टकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टल|कंटलः|कण्टलः
कण्टल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Babul, a tree yielding a species of gum arabic, (Acacia Arabica.) the branches are prickly, whence the name.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ट for कण्टक a thorn, and ल from ला to take or have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टाकारिन्
कण्टाकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The jack tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्टाफल|कण्टाफलः
कण्टाफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Jaca or Jack tree: see कण्टकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ|कंठ|कंठं|कंठः|कण्ठः
कण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा) or -ण्ठी-ण्ठं<BR>1 The throat.<BR>2 Sound, especially guttural sound.<BR>3 Near, proximate.<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>2 The space of an inch from the edge of the hole in which sacrificial fire is deposited.<BR>f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>1 A rope or leather round the neck of a horse.<BR>2 A necklace, a collar.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, ठ Uṇādi affix, fem. Affix. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=183" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठकूणिका|कंठकूणिका
कण्ठकूणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Vīṇā or Indian lute.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ the throat, कूण to sound, and ठक् affix; sounding like the larynx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठग
कण्ठग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Extending to the throat or swallow.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठतलासिका
कण्ठतलासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The leather or rope passing round the neck of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीडक|कंठनीडक|कण्ठनीडकः
कण्ठनीडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठनीलक|कंठनीलक|कण्ठनीलकः
कण्ठनीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A torch, a whisp of lighted straw, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठपाशक|कंठपाशक|कण्ठपाशकः
कण्ठपाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A halter.<BR>2 A rope passing round an elephant's neck.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and पाशक a fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठभूषा|कंठभूषा
कण्ठभूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A collar or short necklace.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ the throat, and भूषा an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठमणि|कंठमणि|कण्ठमणिः
कण्ठमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A jewel worn on the throat.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलग्न
कण्ठलग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Fastened or suspended round the throat.<BR>2 Clinging to, embracing.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and लग्न attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठलता
कण्ठलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A collar.<BR>2 A horse's halter.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठसज्जन|कंठसज्जन
कण्ठसज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hanging on or round the throat.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and सज्जन equipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठस्थ
कण्ठस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Sticking in the throat.<BR>2 Being in or upon the throat.<BR>3 Guttural.<BR>4 Having by rote, ready to repeat.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठागत
कण्ठागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Come in to the throat, (breath, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाग्नि|कण्ठाग्निः
कण्ठाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and अग्नि fire, and figuratively digestive faculty; digesting in the throat or gizzard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठाल|कंठाल|कंठालः|कण्ठालः
कण्ठाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A boat.<BR>2 A hoe, a spade.<BR>3 War.<BR>4 An esculent root, (Arum.)<BR>5 A camel.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A churning vessel.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ the throat, अल to ornament, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठावसक्त
कण्ठावसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Embracing, clinging to the neck.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ, and अवसक्त fastened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठिका|कंठिका
कण्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A necklace of one string or row.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठी and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठीरव|कंठीरव|कण्ठीरवः
कण्ठीरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 An elephant in rut.<BR>3 A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ the throat, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठेकाल|कंठेकाल|कंठेकालः|कण्ठेकालः
कण्ठेकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठे in the throat, काल black, black-necked; see नीलकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ठ्य|कंठ्य|कण्ठ्यः
कण्ठ्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठ्यः-ण्ठ्या-ण्ठ्यं)<BR>Guttural, belonging to the throat, pronounced from the throat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कण्ठ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डन|कंडन|कंडनं|कण्डनं
कण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Threshing, separating the chaff from grain.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A wooden bowl or mortar, in which the cleaning or threshing of grain is performed.<BR>E.<BR>कडि to divide, ल्युट् affix, fem. do. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डरा|कंडरा
कण्डरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A principal vessel of the body, a large artery, vein, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कडि to divide, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डु|कंडु|कंडुः|कण्डुः
कण्डु<BR>f. (-ण्डुः)<BR>1 The itch, itching.<BR>2 Scratching: see कण्डू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डुरा
कण्डुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Cowach: see कण्डूरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डू|कंडू
कण्डू<BR>n. (ञ्) कण्डूञ् Sautra root, (कण्डूयति-ते^1)<BR>1 To itch.<BR>2 To scratch.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161202. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 303. note: 3rd sing. atmaneapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डू|कंडू
कण्डू<BR>f. (-ण्डूः)<BR>1 The itch, itching.<BR>2 Scratching.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डूञ् to itch, affix क्विप्; also with the final short, कण्डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूकरी
कण्डूकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू itching, and कर what makes, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूघ्न|कण्डूघ्नः
कण्डूघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Cassia, (fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूति|कंडूति|कंडूतिः|कण्डूतिः
कण्डूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Itching, the itch.<BR>2 Scratching.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू and क्तिन् affix; also कण्डू, कण्डूयन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयत्
कण्डूयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यती-यत्)<BR>Scratching, rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू to itch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयन|कंडूयन|कण्डूयनं
कण्डूयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Itching.<BR>2 Scratching; also कण्डूया and कण्डू.<BR>E.<BR>as before, affixes यक् and ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूयनक|कंडूयनक|कण्डूयनकः
कण्डूयनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tickler, one who tickles or scratches.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डूयन^1 and क who makes.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूया|कंडूया
कण्डूया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Itching.<BR>2 Scratching.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू to itch, affixes यक् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूरा|कंडूरा
कण्डूरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू itching, and रा what makes, from रा to take or give, affixes क and टाप; alluding to the irritating property of the leaves of this plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डूल|कंडूल|कण्डूलः
कण्डूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Itchy, having the itch.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A esculent root, (Arum.)<BR>E.<BR>कण्डू and ला to have, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोल|कंडोल|कंडोलः|कण्डोलः
कण्डोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A basket, a safe, any place in which provisions are kept.<BR>2 A camel.<BR>E.<BR>कडि to divide, ओलच् Uṇādi affix; also with कन् added कण्डोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलक|कंडोलकः|कण्डोलकः
कण्डोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A safe, a store room: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोलवीणा
कण्डोलवीणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A vulgar lute.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डोल here implying a Cāṇḍāla, and वीणा the Vīṇā or Indian lute; also कटोलवीणा and कण्डोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्डोली|कंडोली
कण्डोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्ड्वोघ|कण्ड्वोघः
कण्ड्वोघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A caterpillar.<BR>E.<BR>कण्डु itching, and ओघ an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कण्व|कण्वं|कण्वः
कण्व<BR>m. (-ण्वः)<BR>The name of a celebrated Muni or saint.<BR>n. (-ण्वं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, क्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत|कतः
कत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>2 The clearing nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, अत Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतक|कतकः
कतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum); one of the seeds of this plant being rubbed upon the inside of the water jars used in Bengal, occasions a precipitation of the earthy particles diffused through the water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतम
कतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Which, (of many.)<BR>E.<BR>किम् and डतमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतमाल|कतमालः
कतमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of AGNI or fire; this word is perhaps a corruption: see कचमाल and खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतर
कतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Which, (of two,) whether.<BR>E.<BR>किम् and डतरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कति
कति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 How many.<BR>2 How much.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, and डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिचित्
कतिचित्<BR>ind.<BR>1 In any way, in some way.<BR>2 For some time.<BR>E.<BR>कति how many, and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिथ
कतिथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>What, how much.<BR>E.<BR>थुक् added to कति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपय|कतिपयः
कतिपय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 How many.<BR>2 A certain number, so many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिपयथ
कतिपयथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>What, how much.<BR>E.<BR>थक् added to कतिपयथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कतिविध
कतिविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Of how many sorts.<BR>2 Of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>कति, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तृण|कत्तृणं
कत्तृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Cākuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्तोय|कत्तोयं
कत्तोय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Wine or vinous spirit.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, and तोय water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्थ
कत्थ<BR>r. 1st cl. (कत्थते)<BR>1 To praise or celebrate.<BR>2 To flatter or coax.<BR>3 To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=184" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्र
कत्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (कत्रयति)<BR>To loosen, to slacken, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कत्सवर|कत्सवरं
कत्सवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The shoulder, the shoulder blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ|कथं
कथ<BR>r. 10th cl. (कथयति)<BR>To speak, to tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथक|कथकः
कथक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A narrator, a relator, one who recites a story, or who publicly reads and expounds the Purāṇas, &c.<BR>2 One who speaks or tells.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>The speaker of a prologue or a monologue.<BR>2 A professional story teller.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to speak, to relate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथिक|कथंकथिक|कथङ्कथिकः
कथङ्कथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>An interrogant, one who asks or questions.<BR>E.<BR>कथम् how, कथ to speak, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथिकता|कथंकथिकता
कथङ्कथिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A question, asking, enquiring.<BR>E.<BR>तल् affix of the abstract added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथङ्कथित
कथङ्कथित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An interrogant, one who questions.<BR>E.<BR>कथम् how, कथित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथञ्चन
कथञ्चन<BR>ind.<BR>In some way, in any way, by any means.<BR>E.<BR>कथम् and चन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथञ्चित्
कथञ्चित्<BR>ind.<BR>In any way, by some means or other.<BR>E.<BR>कथम् and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन|कथनं
कथन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Talkative.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Saying, narrating, relating.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to say, &c. युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथनीय
कथनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be said, to be told or declared.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to tell, अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य, कथितव्य, and with यत्, कथ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथन्ता|कथंता
कथन्ता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Enquiry, question, demand.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to speak, भश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथम्
कथम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of interrogation, (how, what.)<BR>2 Also implying mode, (how, in what manner.)<BR>3 A particle of amazement or surprise.<BR>4 Of pleasure.<BR>5 Of abuse.<BR>6 Of interrogation, implying doubt.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, and थमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथा
कथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>A feigned story, a tale or fable.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to tell, &c. अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथानुराग|कथानुरागः
कथानुराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Attention, taking pleasure in a discourse.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and अनुराग inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रबन्ध|कथाप्रबंध|कथाप्रबन्धः
कथाप्रबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A narrative, a tale, a fiction.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and प्रबन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्रसङ्ग|कथाप्रसंग|कथाप्रसङ्गः
कथाप्रसङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Talkative, talking much and foolishly.<BR>2 Half-witted, foolish.<BR>3 A conjuror, a dealer in antidotes, &c.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Talking, conversation, speaking to or with.<BR>2 Rumour, report.<BR>E.<BR>कथा a fable, and प्रसङ्ग who relates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाप्राण|कथाप्राणः
कथाप्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An actor, the speaker of a prologue or monologue, the introducer or a drama.<BR>2 A professed story teller.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and प्राण life, livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथायोग|कथायोगः
कथायोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Conversation, talk, discourse.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and योग uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथारम्भ|कथारंभ|कथारम्भः
कथारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Narration, narrative, story telling.<BR>2 Beginning of a story.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and आरम्भ beginning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथाविरक्त
कथाविरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Reserved, taciturn, disliking conversation.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and विरक्त disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथासंग्रह
कथासंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A collection of tales or fables.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and संग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथिक|कथिकः
कथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A story teller by profession, a narrator, a relator.<BR>E.<BR>कथा a tale, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथित|कथितः
कथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, told, related.<BR>E.<BR>कथ to tell, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथितपद
कथितपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Repetition, tautology.<BR>E.<BR>कथित said, पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोद्घात|कथोद्घातः
कथोद्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The opening of a drama, by the character that first enters overhearing and repeating the last words of the prelude.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and उद्घात beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपकथन
कथोपकथन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Conversation, conference.<BR>2 Narration.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and उपकथन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथोपाख्यान
कथोपाख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Narration, narrative, relation, telling a story.<BR>E.<BR>कथा, and उपाख्यान telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कथ्य
कथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>To be spoken or said.<BR>E.<BR>कथ and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद<BR>or (-इ.) कदि r. 1st cl. (कदते and कन्दते)<BR>1 To be confused, to suffer mentally, to grieve.<BR>2 To confound.<BR>3 To kill or hurt;<BR>also कदि, (कंदति)<BR>1 To call.<BR>2 To cry or shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद|कदः
कद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक|कदकं|कदकः
कदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An awning.<BR>E.<BR>कद a cloud, and क what makes; yielding a shade as a cloud; also fem. कदका and कदकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदक्षर|कदक्षरं
कदक्षर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A bad letter.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदध्वन्
कदध्वन्<BR>m. (-ध्वा)<BR>A bad road.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, and अध्वन a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन|कदनं
कदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, destroying.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>3 War.<BR>E.<BR>कद to kill or injure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदन्न|कदन्नं
कदन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Bad food.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्ब|कदंब|कदम्बं|कदंबः|कदम्बः
कदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Kadamba (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>2 The mustard seed plant, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR>3 A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratum): see देवताडक.<BR>4 Turmeric.<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A multitude, an assemblage or collection.<BR>E.<BR>कद to confound, &c. अम्बच् Uṇādi affix; also with कन् added कदम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बक|कदंबक|कदम्बकं|कदंबकः|कदम्बकः
कदम्बक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बद|कदंबदः|कदम्बदः
कदम्बद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Mustard seed plant: it seems to be a variety of reading for कदम्बक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बपुष्पी
कदम्बपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, the flowers, of which resemble those of the Kadamba, commonly called Muṇḍīrī.<BR>E.<BR>कदम्ब, and पुष्प a flower, fem. affix ङीष्; also with टाप्, कदम्बपुष्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बवायु|कदंबवायु|कदम्बवायुः
कदम्बवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A fragrant breeze.<BR>E.<BR>कदम्ब the plant, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदम्बानिल|कदंबानिल|कदम्बानिलः
कदम्बानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A fragrant breeze.<BR>2 Spring.<BR>E.<BR>कदम्ब, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर|कदरं|कदरः
कदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A white sort of mimosa.<BR>2 A corn, a callosity.<BR>3 A saw.<BR>4 An iron goad for an elephant.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Coagulated milk.<BR>E.<BR>क water, &c. दृ to tear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थ|कदर्थः
कदर्थ<BR>(-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Useless.<BR>2 Unmeaning.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत्, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थित
कदर्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Despised, disdained, rejected.<BR>2 Rendered useless.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, अर्थित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्थीकृत
कदर्थीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Despised, disdained.<BR>2 Rendered useless and unavailing.<BR>E.<BR>कदर्थ and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य्य|कदर्य|कदर्यः|कदर्य्यः
कदर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Avaricious, miserly.<BR>2 Little, insignificant, mean.<BR>3 Bad, disagreeable.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A miser.<BR>E.<BR>कत् bad, vile, and अर्य्य possessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदर्य्यत्व|कदर्यत्व
कदर्य्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Avarice.<BR>2 Insignificance.<BR>3 Badness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, कदर्य्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदल|कदलः
कदल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>1 The plaintain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Pistia stratiotes): see पृष्णी.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The silk cotton tree;<BR>also (-ली-लिका)<BR>1 A kind of deer, the hide of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">Page186</a>] which is used as a seat, &c.<BR>2 A flag, a banner.<BR>3 A flag carried by an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>क water, air, &c. दल to pierce, to divide, &c. affix अच्, and टाप् or ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=185" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलक|कदलकः
कदलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The plaintain or banana tree: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to कदल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदलीक्षता
कदलीक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A sort of cucumber.<BR>2 A fine woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदश्व|कदश्वः
कदश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A hack, a bad horse.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत्, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदा
कदा<BR>ind.<BR>When, at what time.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, दा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाकार|कदाकारः
कदाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Ill formed, ugly.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत्, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाख्य|कदाख्यं
कदाख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>A plant, commonly Kurh or Kudh, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>कत् bad, आख्या name, ill named: having a bad name or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचन
कदाचन<BR>ind.<BR>Sometime or other, ever; नकदाचन never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचार|कदाचारः
कदाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wicked, abandoned, following evil practices.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत्, आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदाचित्
कदाचित्<BR>ind.<BR>Sometimes, at sometime or other, ever; नकदाचित् never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदापि
कदापि<BR>ind.<BR>Sometimes, now and then.<BR>E.<BR>कदा when, अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कदुष्ण|कदुष्णं
कदुष्ण<BR>mfn. (ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Tepid, warm.<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>Warmth, gentle warmth.<BR>E.<BR>कत् instead of कुत् bad, inferior, उष्ण heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रु|कद्रुः
कद्रु<BR>mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>Tawny.<BR>f. (-द्रुः)<BR>The wife of KAŚYAPA the saint, and mother of the Nāgas or the serpent race, inhabiting the regions below the earth.<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>कभ to desire, डु affix, and र inserted; the final of the radical is irregularly changed to द; fem. affix ऊञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुपुत्र|कद्रुपुत्रः
कद्रुपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A serpent.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्र a son, joined to the preceding; also other compounds of similar import, as कद्रुसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्रुसुत|कद्रुसुतः
कद्रुसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A serpent: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कद्वद|कद्वदः
कद्वद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Speaking ill, inaccurately, indistinctly, &c.<BR>2 Vile, base, contemptible.<BR>E.<BR>कत् for कुत् bad, and वद who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन
कन<BR>(इ ञि) ञिकनी r. 1st cl. (कनति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To desire or love.<BR>3 To go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनक|कनकं|कनकः
कनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The name of a tree which bears red flowers, (Butea frondosa): see पलाश.<BR>2 Thorn apple, (Datura metel, &c)<BR>3 Another plant, (Mesua ferrea): see नागकेशर.<BR>4 Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.) see काञ्चनाल.<BR>5 A black sort of agallochum.<BR>6 A shrub yielding a yellow fragrant flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, अक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकक्षार|कनकक्षारः
कनकक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and क्षार flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकटङ्क|कनकटंक|कनकटङ्कः
कनकटङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A golden hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and टङ्क a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकदण्डक|कनकदंडक
कनकदण्डक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The royal parasol.<BR>E.<BR>कनक gold, दण्ड a staff, and कन् affix; golden-sticked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकपराग|कनकपरागः
कनकपराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Gold dust.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and पराग pollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकपल|कनकपलः
कनकपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Pala, a weight of gold and silver equal to sixteen Māṣas, or about 280 grains troy: see पल.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and पल a Pala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकभङ्ग|कनकभङ्गः
कनकभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A piece of gold.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, भङ्ग what is broken off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकमय
कनकमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Golden, consisting or made of gold.<BR>E.<BR>कनक and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकरस|कनकरसः
कनकरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकलोद्भव|कनकलोद्भवः
कनकलोद्भव<BR>m. (-द्भः)<BR>Resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकसूत्र
कनकसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A gold cord.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and सूत्र string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकस्थली
कनकस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A gold mine, golden soil.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाचल|कनकाचलः
कनकाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and अचल a mountain; the golden mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाध्यक्ष|कनकाध्यक्षः
कनकाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The treasurer or superintendant of the gold.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and अध्यक्ष a superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकालुका
कनकालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A golden jar or vase.<BR>E.<BR>कनक, आलु a water jar, कन् and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनकाह्व|कनकाह्वं|कनकाह्वः
कनकाह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A tree with golden or yellow blossoms, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>कनक, and आह्वा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनन|कननः
कनन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठ|कनिष्ठः
कनिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Small, little.<BR>2 Younger, younger born.<BR>3 Young.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>The little finger.<BR>E.<BR>कन् to shine, &c. and इष्ठच् affix, or कण small, the ण being changed, or कन substituted for युवन् and अल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनिष्ठता
कनिष्ठता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The state of being younger or smaller.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कनिष्ठत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनी
कनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A girl, a maiden.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीक
कनीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Very small: see कणिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीचि|कनीचिः
कनीचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>1 A creeping plant which bears flowers.<BR>2 The Gunja, a shrub bearing a red and black berry, (Abrus precatorios.)<BR>3 A cart.<BR>E.<BR>कनी to shine, ईचि Uṇādi affix; also according to some कणीचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीनक|कनीनकः
कनीनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The caruncula lacrymalis.<BR>f. (-निका)<BR>1 The pupil of the eye.<BR>2 The little finger.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, ईकन् affix, कन added; also with ङीष् only कनीनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीनी
कनीनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The little finger.<BR>2 The pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस्
कनीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very young, youngest.<BR>2 Very small, least.<BR>3 Younger born, a younger brother or sister.<BR>E.<BR>कण small, ईयसुन् affix, the ण being changed; or कन to shine, &c.: or कन substituted for युवन् and अल्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनीयस|कनीयसं
कनीयस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, ईयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनेर
कनेर<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>2 A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्त|कंत
कन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Happy.<BR>E.<BR>कं and त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्ति
कन्ति<BR>mfn. (-न्तिः-न्तिः-न्ति)<BR>Happy.<BR>E.<BR>कम् and ति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्तु|कंतु|कन्तुः
कन्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>Happy.<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA, the deity of love.<BR>2 The heart, as the seat or faculty of perception and feeling.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, तु Uṇādi affix; or कं and तु possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्था|कंथा
कन्था<BR>f. (-न्था)<BR>1 A rag, a patched cloth or garment, a quilt of grass.<BR>2 A wall: this word in composition may be used as neuter, if the compound imply a town in the province of Usināra, as सोसिमकन्थं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थाधारण|कंथाधारण
कन्थाधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Wearing a garment of patch-work, the practice of some Yogis.<BR>E.<BR>कन्था, and धारण wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्थाधारिन्|कंथाधारिन्
कन्थाधारिन्<BR>mf. (-री)<BR>A Yogi, a religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>कन्था, and धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्द|कंद|कंदं|कन्दं|कंदः|कन्दः
कन्द<BR>mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>1 A bulbous or tuberous root.<BR>2 One of an esculent sort, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR>3 Garlic.<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An affection of the feminine organ, considered as a fleshy excrescence, but apparently prolapsus uteri.<BR>E.<BR>कदि to wet, &c. अच् affix, or कं water, and दा to give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=186" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दट|कंदट|कन्दटं
कन्दट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The white esculent water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दमूल|कंदमूल|कन्दमूलं
कन्दमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A radish.<BR>E.<BR>कन्द, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर|कंदर|कंदरं|कन्दरं|कंदरः|कन्दरः
कन्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>1 An artificial or natural cave.<BR>2 A glen, a defile, a valley.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hook for driving an elephant with.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>क water, or the head, and दृ to divide, to pierce, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दराकर|कंदराकर|कन्दराकरः
कन्दराकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>कन्दर a cave, आकर having, making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दराल|कन्दरालः
कन्दराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>2 A species of fig tree, (Ficus venosa): see प्लक्ष.<BR>3 The walnut tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन्दरा a cave, and लक्ष् affix; growing in desolate places: also with कन् added, कन्दरालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दरालक|कन्दरालकः
कन्दरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of fig tree: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्प|कंदर्प|कंदर्पः|कन्दर्पः
कन्दर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A name of the deity KĀMA, the CUPID of the Hindu mythology.<BR>E.<BR>कं BRAHMĀ, दर्प to inflame, अच् affix; the inflamer even of the first of the gods; corresponding in this respect with his Grecian prototype.<BR>f. (-र्पा)<BR>One of the presiding female deities of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पकूप|कंदर्पकूप|कन्दर्पकूपः
कन्दर्पकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पज्वर|कंदर्पज्वर|कन्दर्पज्वरः
कन्दर्पज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Passion, desire.<BR>E.<BR>कन्दर्प, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दर्पमुषल|कंदर्पमुषल|कन्दर्पमुषलः
कन्दर्पमुषल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दल|कंदल|कंदलं|कन्दलं|कंदलः|कन्दलः
कन्दल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 The cheek, or the cheek and temple.<BR>2 A portent, a natural phoenomenon supposed to announce evil.<BR>3 A new shoot or spring.<BR>4 A low minute tone.<BR>5 Reproach, censure.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A species of deer of which the hide is used.<BR>2 A sort of tree, the banana: see कदली.<BR>3 A flag.<BR>E.<BR>कन्द a root, &c. and ल from ला to take, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलित|कंदलित
कन्दलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Budden, blown.<BR>2 Put forth, emitted.<BR>E.<BR>कन्दल a bud, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दलीकुसुम|कंदलीकुसुम|कन्दलीकुसुमं
कन्दलीकुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दवर्द्धन
कन्दवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An esculent root.<BR>E.<BR>कन्द, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दशूरण|कन्दशूरणः
कन्दशूरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sort of Arum, (A. campanulatum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्द, and शूरण the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दसंज्ञ
कन्दसंज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Prolapsus uteri, see कन्द.<BR>E.<BR>कन्द a root, and संज्ञा a name, affix ड; every संज्ञा or name for a bulbous root, being a term for this complaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दसार|कंदसार|कन्दसारं
कन्दसार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The garden or grove of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दालु|कन्दालुः
कन्दालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>An esculent root, a sort of Arum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दिन्|कंदिन्
कन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>Having a bulbous root.<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>A sort of Arum, (A. campanulatum, or any similar bulb.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्द and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दु|कंदुः|कन्दुः
कन्दु<BR>mfn. (-न्दुः-न्दुः-न्दु)<BR>1 A boiler, a saucepan or other cooking utensil of iron.<BR>2 An oven or vessel serving for one.<BR>E.<BR>स्कन्द to go, उ Uṇādi affix, and the initial स rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुक|कंदुक|कंदुकं|कंदुकः|कन्दुकः
कन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ball of wood or pith for playing with.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A germ.<BR>E.<BR>कदि to cry, to call, &c. उ affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दुपक्व|कन्दुपक्वं
कन्दुपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Parched, roasted, (as grain,) fried, &c. dressed without water.<BR>E.<BR>कन्दु, and पक्व dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोट|कंदोट|कन्दोटं|कंदोटः|कन्दोटः
कन्दोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The white esculent water lily.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्दोत|कंदोतः|कन्दोतः
कन्दोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्ध|कंध|कंधः|कन्धः
कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>कं water, and ध from धा to have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धर|कंधर|कंधरः|कन्धरः
कन्धर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>The neck.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>कं water or the head, and धर having, from धृञ्, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्धि|कंधि|कंधिः|कन्धिः
कन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>The neck.<BR>E.<BR>क water or the head, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्न|कन्नं
कन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Fainting, falling in a fit or state of insensibility: in some copies this word is read कल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A girl, a maiden.<BR>2 A daughter.<BR>3 The Socotrine aloe, (Aloes perfoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्या A girl, कन् pleonastic affix, fem. affix, टाप्: see कन्या and कन्याका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकाछल|कन्यकाच्छल|कन्यकाच्छलः
कन्यकाछल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Beguiling a maiden, seduction, betrayal.<BR>E.<BR>कन्यका, and छल deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकाजात|कन्यकाजातः
कन्यकाजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The son of an unmarried woman.<BR>E.<BR>कन्यका, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यकापति|कन्यकापतिः
कन्यकापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A daughter's husband.<BR>E.<BR>कन्यका, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यस|कन्यसः
कन्यस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A younger brother.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The little finger: see कनिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्या
कन्या<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>1 A girl nine years old, a virgin.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 The sign of the zodiac, Virgo.<BR>4 The socotrine aloe (Aloe perfoliata.)<BR>6 Large cardamoms.<BR>6 A species of metre of four lines, with four syllables in each.<BR>7 A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, Uṇādi affix यक्, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याका
कन्याका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A young girl or virgin: see कन्या and कन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याकुब्ज|कन्याकुब्जः
कन्याकुब्ज<BR>m. (-ब्जः)<BR>Kanyākubja or Kinnoge, an ancient city of great note, in the north of Hindustan, known to classical geography as Canogyza: the name also applies to its dependencies or the surrounding district; also कान्यकुब्ज.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या a girl, and कुब्ज round-shouldered, crooked; the etymology alludes to a legend relating to the one hundred daughters of KUŚANĀBHA the king of this city, who were all rendered crooked by Vāyu, for non-compliance with his licentious desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याग्रहण
कन्याग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking a girl in marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याट|कन्याटः
कन्याट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The middle of a house; the inner or private apartments.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या a girl, अट to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादान|कन्यादानं
कन्यादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Giving a girl in marriage.<BR>2 Receiving the same.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and दान gift, or आदान acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादातृ
कन्यादातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father, one who gives a girl in marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and दातृ donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादूषक|कन्यादूषकः
कन्यादूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A violator or defiler of a virgin.<BR>2 A calumniator of a girl.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and टूषक who defiles; also कन्यादूषिन् (-षी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादूषण
कन्यादूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Defiling a virgin.<BR>2 Calumniating a girl.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and दूषण spoiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यादोष|कन्यादोषः
कन्यादोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A blemish in a virgin, disease, bad repute, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापति|कन्यापतिः
कन्यापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A daughter's husband: see कन्यकापति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापाल|कन्यापालः
कन्यापाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A dealer in slave girls.<BR>2 The father of a daughter.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यापुत्र|कन्यापुत्रः
कन्यापुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The offspring of an unmarried daughter.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याप्रदान
कन्याप्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving a daughter in marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and प्रदान a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=187" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याराम|कन्यारामः
कन्याराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या a girl, रम to please, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यावेदिन्
कन्यावेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A son-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याशुल्क
कन्याशुल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>The purchase money of a maiden, money given to the bride's father.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and शुल्क tax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यासमुद्भव
कन्यासमुद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The son of an unmarried girl.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and समुद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्याहरण
कन्याहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Carrying off a girl, rape, ravishment.<BR>E.<BR>कन्या, and हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यिका
कन्यिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A young girl, a virgin: see कन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्युष|कन्युषं
कन्युष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The hand below the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप
कप<BR>(इ) कपि r. 1st cl. (कंपते)<BR>To shake, to tremble:<BR>with अनु prefixed,<BR>to feel tenderness or compassion, to pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपट|कपटं|कपटः
कपट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>Fraud, deceit, cheating, circumvention.<BR>E.<BR>क. BRAHMĀ, पट to go, अच् affix; what extends even to BRAHMĀ; or क the head, and पट a covering, screening the head as it were.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A measure equal to the capacity of the hollows of the two hands joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटता
कपटता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Deceitfulness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to कपट्; also with त्व, कपटत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटप्रबन्ध|कपटप्रबंध|कपटप्रबन्धः
कपटप्रबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Fraud, trick, fraudulent plot or contrivance.<BR>E.<BR>कपट, and प्रबन्ध procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटलेख्य
कपटलेख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>A forged document, a false or fraudulent statement.<BR>E.<BR>कपट, and लेख्य a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटवेश|कपटवेशः
कपटवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Masked, disguised, assuming a false dress or appearance.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Disguise.<BR>E.<BR>कपट, and वेश costume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटवेशिन्
कपटवेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Disguised, in masquerade.<BR>E.<BR>कपटवेश and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिक|कपटिकः
कपटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A rogue, a cheat, fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>कपट and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिन्
कपटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest, a cheat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कपट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्द|कपर्द|कपर्दः|कपर्द्दः
कपर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 The braided hair of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A small shell used as a coin, a Cowri.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>क water, (that of the Ganges,) पृ in the deriv. form, nourishing, and द from दा to give; or क happiness, &c. which will apply to both senses; also with कन् added कपर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्दक|कपर्दक|कपर्दकः|कपर्द्दकः
कपर्द्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्द्दिन्|कपर्दिन्
कपर्द्दिन्<BR>m. (-र्द्दी)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कपर्द्द his braided hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाट|कपाटं|कपाटः
कपाट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>A door, the leaf or pannel of a door.<BR>E.<BR>क the head or wind, पट to go, अण् affix; also कबाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटघ्न
कपाटघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A thief, a house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>कपाट, and घ्न who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटसन्धि|कपाटसंधि|कपाटसंधिः
कपाटसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>1 The junction of the leaves of a door.<BR>2 A mode of multiplying, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>कपाट, and सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाल|कपालं|कपालः
कपाल<BR>m. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 The skull, the cranium.<BR>2 Either half of a water jar.<BR>3 Any flat bone.<BR>4 A beggar's bowl.<BR>5 Multitude, assemblage, collection.<BR>6 A species of leprosy.<BR>7 A treaty of peace on equal terms.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to tremble, and कालन् Uṇādi affix; or क the head, and पाल what cherishes or protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालनालिका
कपालनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of pin or spindle for winding cotton, thread, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालभृत्
कपालभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल a skull, and भृत् who cherishes; being represented with a necklace of skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालसन्धि|कपालसंधि|कपालसंधिः
कपालसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>Treaty of peace on equal terms.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल, and सन्धि peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिका
कपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The tartar of the teeth.<BR>2 A potsherd.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिन्
कपालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A title of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A man of low caste, from a Brahman mother and fisherman father.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल a skull, इनि affix; and ङीष् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपि|कपिः
कपि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>1 An ape or monkey.<BR>2 The monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>3 A title of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>4 Incense, storax or impure benzoin.<BR>5 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>6 A kind of Bonduc or Bonducella.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to tremble, इ Uṇādi affix, the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकच्छु|कपिकच्छुः
कपिकच्छु<BR>f. (-च्छुः)<BR>Cowach, (Dolichos carpopogon.)<BR>E.<BR>कपि a monkey, and कच्छु itching; also with final vowel long कपिकच्छू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकच्छुरा
कपिकच्छुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Cowach: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिकन्दुक|कपिकन्दुकं
कपिकन्दुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The skull, the cranium.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and कन्दुक a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिचूत|कपिचूतः
कपिचूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree, (Spondias mangifera): see आम्रातक.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and चूत the mango tree, the monkey's mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिज|कपिजः
कपिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born of a monkey, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Incense, benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिञ्जल|कपिंजल|कपिंजलः|कपिञ्जलः
कपिञ्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A bird, the francoline partridge.<BR>2 The Chataka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपितैल|कपितैलं
कपितैल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>Benzoin or storax.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थ|कपित्थः
कपित्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>The elephant or wood apple, (Feronia elephantum.)<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and त्थ from स्था to stay or abide; the residence of apes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थपर्णी
कपित्थपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, commonly कपित्थानी, the leaves of which are compared to those of the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थानी
कपित्थानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थास्य|कपित्थास्यः
कपित्थास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A kind of monkey.<BR>E.<BR>कपित्थ, and आस्य a face; having a roundish face, in shape like the wood apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिध्वज|कपिध्वजः
कपिध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कपि a monkey, and ध्वज a sign; having a monkey as his symbol, his ensign or arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिनामन्
कपिनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Incense: see कपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रभा
कपिप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Cowach: see कपिकच्छु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रभु|कपिप्रभुः
कपिप्रभु<BR>m. (-भुः)<BR>A name of the first RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and प्रभु master; general of the monkey force with which he invaded Laṅkā or Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिप्रिय|कपिप्रियः
कपिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>E.<BR>कपि and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिरथ|कपिरथः
कपिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A title of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कपि and रथ a car; having been carried by his monkies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल|कपिलः
कपिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Tawny.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 KAPILA, a celebrated Muni or saint, the founder of the Sāṃkhya system of philosophy: the son of KĀRDDAMA by DEVAHŪTI, and according to some, an avatāra of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A title of AGNI the deity of fire.<BR>3 A dog.<BR>5 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The female elephant of the south-east.<BR>2 A kind of Sisu, or timber tree so [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">Page189</a>] called: see शिंशपा.<BR>3 A sort of perfume: see रेणुका.<BR>4 The aloe plant.<BR>5 A fabulous cow, celebrated in the Purāṇas.<BR>5 The common leech.<BR>E.<BR>कभ to desire, इलच् Uṇādi affix, and प substituted for म; or कपि a monkey, and ल to take, &c. being of such a colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=188" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्युति|कपिलद्युतिः
कपिलद्युति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of SŪRYA or the sun.<BR>E.<BR>कपिल, and द्युति light; being of a dull red or tawny hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्राक्षा
कपिलद्राक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>The brown or tawny grape.<BR>E.<BR>कपिल, and द्राक्षा a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलद्रुम|कपिलद्रुमः
कपिलद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The name of a perfume or sweet scented wood: see काक्षी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलधारा
कपिलधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 A holy place, a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलाश्व|कपिलाश्वः
कपिलाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A title of the god INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>कपिल tawny, and अश्व horse; such being the colour of INDRA'S steed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिलोह|कपिलोहं
कपिलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>कपि for कपिल brown, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल्लिका
कपिल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, which bears a seed resembling pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिवक्त्र|कपिवक्त्रः
कपिवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A name of NĀRADA, a saint and philosopher, and friend of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and वक्त्र a face; the saint having a face like a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिवल्ली
कपिवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and वल्ली a pedicle; that being invested with a downy coat, resembling the hair of an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिश|कपिशः
कपिश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Brown, of a brown colour.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Brown, (the colour,) a compound of black and yellow.<BR>2 Incense, styrax or coarse benzoin.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A spirit, a sort of rum.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The mother of the demons called Piśācas.<BR>E.<BR>कपि an ape, and शः affix; of the colour of an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशाञ्जन|कपिशाञ्जनः
कपिशाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A title of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशायन|कपिशायनः
कपिशायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A sort of spirit or rum.<BR>E.<BR>कपिशा, affix फक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशापुत्र
कपिशापुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A Piśāca, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>कपिशा the mother of these beings, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशित
कपिशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Embrowned, made brown or dusky red.<BR>E.<BR>कपिश and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीका
कपिशीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>कपिश, and ईकन् affix: see कपिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीर्ष|कपिशीर्षं
कपिशीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षः)<BR>The upper part or coping of a wall.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and शीर्ष the head; a monkey's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीर्षक|कपिशीर्षकं
कपिशीर्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Vermilion, the red sulphuret of mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिस्थल
कपिस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A place frequented by monkies.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीकच्छु|कपीकच्छुः
कपीकच्छु<BR>f. (-च्छुः)<BR>Cowach: see कपिकच्छु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीज्य|कपीज्यः
कपीज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A plant, (a species of mimusops): see क्षीरिका.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and इज्य respected, liked: a favourite plant with the monkies; also कपीज्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीतन|कपीतनः
कपीतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A tree bearing an acid fruit, (Spondias mangifera): see आम्रातक.<BR>2 Another tree, (Hibiscus populneoides): see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR>3 A species of Mimosa, (Mimosa sirisha, Rox.)<BR>4 The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>5 The betel nut tree, (Areca faufel or Catechu.)<BR>6 The name of another plant, (Crataeva marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>कपि an ape, and तन what spreads; sheltering or feeding monkies; the vowel is made long irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीन्द्र|कपींद्र|कपीन्द्रः
कपीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A name of the celebrated monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>2 Also of SUGRĪVA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and इन्द्र the chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुष्टिका
कपुष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A patch of hair on each side of the head.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, पुष्टि cherishing, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुच्छल|कपुच्छलं
कपुच्छल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Hair hanging down to the ground.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, पुच्छ a tail, and ल what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोत|कपोतः
कपोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A dove or pigeon, especially the spotted necked pigeon.<BR>2 A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>कब to tinge, to be of various hues, आतच् Uṇādi affix, ब changed to प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतक|कपोतकं|कपोतकः
कपोतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Antimony.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत, and कन् affix, implying resemblance, (in colour.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतचरणा
कपोतचरणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A perfume: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतपालिका
कपोतपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A dove cot, an aviary or pigeon house.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत a bird, &c. पाल to nourish, and वुन् affix, fem. termination टाप्; also with the affixes अण and ङीप्, कपोतपाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतपाली
कपोतपाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतसार|कपोतसारं
कपोतसार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Antimony.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोताङ्घ्रि|कपोतांघ्रि|कपोताङ्घ्रिः
कपोताङ्घ्रि<BR>f. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>A perfume: see नली.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत, and अङ्घ्रि a foot; of a red colour, like the claw of a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोताभ|कपोताभः
कपोताभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A pale or dirty white colour.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत, and आङ् before भा to shine, affix ड; of the colour of a pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतारि|कपोतारिः
कपोतारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A hawk, a falcon.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतिका
कपोतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A done.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत a pigeon, कन् affix fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोल|कपोलः
कपोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cheek.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The forepart of the knee, the knee-cap or pan.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to quiver, and ओलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलकाष|कपोलकाषः
कपोलकाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The elephant's temples and cheeks.<BR>E.<BR>कपोल, and काष a touchstone; being of the like dark colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलभित्ति|कपोलभित्तिः
कपोलभित्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>The temples and cheek, the upper part of the face.<BR>E.<BR>कपोल, and भित्ति a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलराग|कपोलरागः
कपोलराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Colour or flush in the cheek.<BR>E.<BR>कपोल, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलफलक|कपोलफलकः
कपोलफलक<BR>f. (-कः)<BR>The cheek.<BR>E.<BR>कपोल, and फलक a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप्याख्य|कप्याख्यः
कप्याख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>Incense.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and आख्या aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफ|कफः
कफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>1 Phlegm, one of the three humours of the body.<BR>2 Watery froth or foam in general.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and फल to bud or flower, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफकर
कफकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Producing phlegm.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफकूर्च्चिका|कफकूर्चिका
कफकूर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Saliva, spittle.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and कूर्च्चिका cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफघ्न
कफघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing phlegm, antiphlegmatic, (an epithet of many plants, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफणि|कफणिः
कफणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>The elbow.<BR>E.<BR>क pleasure, फण to go, इन् and ङीष् affixes; also कफोणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफनाशन
कफनाशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Antiphlegmatic.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफवर्द्धक
कफवर्द्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Exciting phlegm.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and वर्द्धक what increases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफवर्द्धन
कफवर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Exciting phlegm.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a plant; also पिण्डीतगर.<BR>E.<BR>कफ phlegm, वृध to augment, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफारि|कफारिः
कफारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफिन्
कफिन्<BR>mfn. (-फी-फिनी-फी)<BR>Phlegmatic.<BR>m. (-फी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कफ and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=189" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफेलू
कफेलू<BR>mfn. (-लूः-लूः-लु)<BR>Phlegmatic, causing or exciting phlegm.<BR>E.<BR>कफ, लू from ला to take or give, and कू Uṇādi affix; the deriv. is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफोणि|कफोणिः
कफोणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>The elbow.<BR>E.<BR>क pleasure, स्फुर् to go, &c. इन् and ङीष् affixes; the form is irregular: see कफणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कब
कब<BR>(ऋ) कबृ r. 1st cl. (कबते)<BR>1 To colour, to tinge with various hues.<BR>2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्ध|कबंध|कबंधं|कबन्धं|कबंधः|कबन्धः
कबन्ध<BR>mn. (-न्धः-न्धं)<BR>A headless trunk, especially retaining vitality.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Water.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A name of RĀHU.<BR>2 Also of a demon destroyed by RĀMA.<BR>3 The belly.<BR>E.<BR>कं the head, and बध to injure, to lop, affix अच्; also कं water, and बन्ध binding, attaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबन्धता
कबन्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Headlessness, decapitation.<BR>E.<BR>कबन्ध and तल् affix; also with त्व, कबन्धत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबित्थ|कबित्थः
कबित्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबिल|कबिलः
कबिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Tawny, (of such a hue.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Tawny, (the colour): see कपिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम
कम<BR>(उ) कमु r. 1st cl. (कामयति)<BR>To desire: this root is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 The head.<BR>2 Happiness or happily.<BR>4 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमठ|कमठं|कमठः
कमठ<BR>mn. (-ठः-ठं)<BR>1 A water jar, especially one made of a hollow gourd or cocoanut, and used by ascetics.<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>2 A bamboo.<BR>3 The name of a Daitya or demon.<BR>4 A porcupine.<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>A female tortoise, a small one.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, &c. अठः Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमण्डलु|कमंडलु|कमंडलुः|कमण्डलुः
कमण्डलु<BR>mn. (-लुः-लु)<BR>An earthen or wooden water pot, used by the ascetic and religious student.<BR>2 The waved-leaf fig tree: see प्लक्ष.<BR>E.<BR>क BRAHMĀ or water, and मण्ड ornament or essence, ल from ला to get or give, and डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन|कमनं|कमनः
कमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Libidinous, desirous.<BR>2 Beautiful, desirable.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 KĀMA or love.<BR>3 A tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, affix युच् or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनच्छद|कमनच्छदः|कमनछद
कमनच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>कमन beautiful, and च्छद plumage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीय|कमनीयं
कमनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Pleasing, beautiful, desirable.<BR>E.<BR>कम and अनीयर् affix of the future participle, to be desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीयता
कमनीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Loveliness, beauty.<BR>2 Desirableness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, or with त्व, कमनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन्ध|कमन्धं
कमन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Water. see कबन्ध; also according to some, this is an orthographical compound, of कं and अन्ध, both synonyms of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमर|कमरः
कमर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Desirous, lustful.<BR>E.<BR>कम and अरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमल|कमलं|कमलः
कमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum or Nymphaea nelumbo.)<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Copper.<BR>4 A medicament, a drug.<BR>5 The bladder.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A species of deer.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 An excellent woman.<BR>E.<BR>कम् water, and अल what adorns, or कम to desire, with कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलच्छद
कमलच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A heron: see कङ्क.<BR>2 Petal of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कमल, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलाकर|कमलाकरः
कमलाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lake &c. where lotuses abound.<BR>E.<BR>कमल, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलासन|कमलासनः
कमलासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An epithet of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कमल a lotus, and आसन seat or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलिनी
कमलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A number of lotus flowers, or a place abounding with them.<BR>E.<BR>कमल, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलोत्तर|कमलोत्तरं
कमलोत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>E.<BR>कमल, and उत्तर best, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमा
कमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Beauty, radiance.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमितृ
कमितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Lustful, desirous, cupidinous.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, तृच् affix; and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प|कंप|कंपः|कम्पः
कम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Tremour, trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to shake, and अच् affix; also कम्पन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पन|कंपन|कम्पनं|कम्पनः
कम्पन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Trembling, unsteady, shaken.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trembling, quivering.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The dewy season. (Nov.-Dec.)<BR>E.<BR>कपि to tremble, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पमान
कम्पमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Trembling.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पलक्ष्मन्|कंपलक्ष्मन्
कम्पलक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>कम्प trembling, and लक्ष्मन् mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पाक|कंपाक|कंपाकः|कम्पाकः
कम्पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Wind, air.<BR>E.<BR>काकुन् affixed to कपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पान्वित
कम्पान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Trembling, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>कम्प, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पित|कंपित|कम्पितं
कम्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaking, shaken, trembling.<BR>(-तं)<BR>Trembling, a trembling, a tremor.<BR>E.<BR>कपि and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्पिल|कम्पिलः
कम्पिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant: see रोचनी: see काम्पिल्ल; also कम्पिल्ल and कम्पील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्प्र|कंप्र
कम्प्र<BR>mfn. (-म्प्रः-म्प्रा-म्प्रं)<BR>Trembling, shaken.<BR>E.<BR>कपि, and रः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्ब
कम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (-कम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बर|कंबर|कम्बरः
कम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Variegated.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Variegated, (the colour.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बल|कंबल|कम्बलं|कंबलः|कम्बलः
कम्बल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A blanket.<BR>2 A chief of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR>3 A small worm.<BR>4 A dewlap.<BR>5 An upper cloth or garment.<BR>6 A sort of deer.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, कलः Uṇādi affix, and ब inserted; or कम् the head, water, &c. and बल to be strong, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलकारक
कम्बलकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Woollen cloth manufacturer.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बल, and कारक who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बलवाह्यक|कंबलवाह्यक
कम्बलवाह्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of carriage, covered with a coarse blanket or woollen cloth, and drawn by oxen.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बल and बह to bear, affixes ण्यत् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बालायिन्
कम्बालायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A sort of kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बि|कंबिः|कम्बिः
कम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बिः)<BR>1 A ladle or spoon.<BR>2 A shoot, a branch or joint of a bamboo.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, बिन् affix, or with ङीष् added, कम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बु|कंबु|कम्बुः
कम्बु<BR>mfn. (-म्बुः-म्बू-म्बु)<BR>Speckled, variegated.<BR>mn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)<BR>1 A conch, a shell.<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>1 A bracelet, a ring.<BR>2 A bivalve shell.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 The neck.<BR>5 A vein or tubular vessel of the body, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कम्ब to go, उ affix, or कम to desire; the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बुक|कंबुकः|कम्बुकः
कम्बुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A mean person.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A conch.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बुग्रीवा|कंबुग्रीवा
कम्बुग्रीवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A neck marked with three lines like a shell, and considered to be indicative of exalted fortune.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बु a shell, and ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बू|कंबू
कम्बू<BR>mfn. (-म्बूः-म्बू-म्बु)<BR>A thief, a plunderer.<BR>m. (-म्बूः)<BR>A bracelet.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, ऊ Uṇādi affix, and बुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्बोज|कंबोज|कंबोजः|कम्बोजः
कम्बोज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The name of a country in the north of India, Camboja or Camboya.<BR>2 A kind of shell.<BR>3 A description of elephant: see काम्बोज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=190" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भारी
कम्भारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>कम water, भार a burthen, ङीष् affix; also गम्भारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्भु|कंभु
कम्भु<BR>n. (-म्भु)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>कं water, भू produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्र|कम्रः
कम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>1 Desirous, cupidinous.<BR>2 Beautiful, desirable.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयस्था
कयस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Kākoli: also कायस्था, or more accurately, perhaps, वयस्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Who or what does, makes or causes, as किङ्करः A servant, who does any thing; भयङ्करः frightful, what causes fear; उपकरः who gives aid; अपकरः who does ill, &c.<BR>m. (रः)<BR>1 A ray of light, a sun or moonbeam.<BR>2 Royal revenue, toll, tax, impost, &c.<BR>3 The hand.<BR>4 Hail.<BR>5 An elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, &c. ट or अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करक|करकं|करकः
करक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>Hail.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The water pot of the student or ascetic.<BR>2 The shell of the cocoanut hollowed to form a vessel.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The pomegranate tree.<BR>2 Toll, tax.<BR>3 A particular sort of bird.<BR>4 A plant, (Galedupa arborea, &c.) see करञ्च.<BR>5 A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, or कृ to injure, &c. and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकण्ठक
करकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The finger nail. कर the hand, and कण्ठक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकमल
करकमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The hand, especially of a lover, a mistress, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and कमल a lotus; also similar compounds, as करपद्मं, करपङ्कज, करपल्लव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकलश|करकलशः
करकलश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The hand hollowed to receive water.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and कलश a ewer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकाम्भस्|करकांभस्
करकाम्भस्<BR>m. (-म्भाः)<BR>The cocoanut tree, (Cocos nucifera.)<BR>E.<BR>करक the shell, and अम्भस् the water, the nut containing a serous fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकुद्मल
करकुद्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and कुद्मल a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकोष|करकोषः
करकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The hollow of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and कोष receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्रह|करग्रहः
करग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Marriage.<BR>2 Levying or gathering a tax.<BR>3 A tax gatherer.<BR>4 Taking the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and ग्रह taking: one part of the ceremony of marriage is the placing of the right hand of the bride with the palm uppermost, in the right hand of the bridegroom; also करग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्रहण
करग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Levying or gathering a tax.<BR>2 Taking the hand.<BR>3 Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करग्राहिन्
करग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>1 Levying a tax.<BR>2 Taking the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करघर्षण|करघर्षणः
करघर्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The churning stick.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rubbing the hands together.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and घर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करघर्षिन्
करघर्षिन्<BR>m. (-र्षी)<BR>The churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, घृष to rub, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्क|करंक|करंकः|करङ्कः
करङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 A cocoanut hollowed so as to form a cup or vessel.<BR>3 Any bone of the body.<BR>4 A kind of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to send or throw, &c. अंक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्कशालि|करङ्कशालिः
करङ्कशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करङ्गण
करङ्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A market or fair.<BR>E.<BR>कर tax, and गण collection, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करच्छद|करच्छदः
करच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The teak tree.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and च्छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करज|करजं|करजः
करज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in or from a hand, a ray, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A finger nail.<BR>2 The name of a timber tree, commonly Karanja, (Galendupa arborea, Rox.)<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A perfume, commonly Nakhi, resembling a nail in appearance.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and ज produced; or कं pleasure, रञ्ज to colour, &c. अच affix: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करजाल
करजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pencil of rays, a stream of light.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and जाल multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करञ्ज|करंज|करंजः|करञ्जः
करञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>The name of a plant, commonly Karanja, (Galedupa arborea, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, and रञ्ज to colour, अच् affix: see करज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करञ्जक|करञ्जकः
करञ्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Karanja: see the preceding.<BR>2 Another plant, (Verbesina scandens, Rox.) see भृङ्गराज.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the foregoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करट|करटः
करट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 An elephant's cheek.<BR>3 Safflower or carthamus.<BR>4 A man of a low or degraded profession.<BR>5 The first Śrāddha or ceremony performed in honour of a deceased relation.<BR>6 An atheist, an unbeliever, an oppugner of the doctrines of the Vedas.<BR>7 A musical instrument, (Castanets?)<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A cow difficult to be milked.<BR>E.<BR>क pleasure, &c. रट to sound, and अच् affix; or कृ to do, and अटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटक|करटकः
करटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटिन्
करटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करट and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटु|करटुः
करटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>The numidian crane.<BR>E.<BR>कर् for कुत् bad, अट to go, and डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण|करणं|करणः
करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 An instrument or means of action.<BR>2 Making, doing.<BR>3 Action, act.<BR>4 Cause, motive.<BR>5 Business, occupation, as trade, &c.<BR>6 An organ of sense.<BR>7 The body.<BR>8 The mind or heart.<BR>9 A field.<BR>10 Grain.<BR>11 The posture, abstinence, &c. of an ascetic.<BR>12 Copulation, (seu modus coeundi.)<BR>13 The usage or practice of the writer caste.<BR>14 Acting, dramatic action.<BR>15 Song, singing.<BR>16 The particular business of any tribe or cast.<BR>17 Plaistering, spreading any thing with the hand.<BR>18 A Karaṇa, an astrological division of time; the Karaṇas are eleven: 7 moveable and 4 fixed, and two are equal to a lunar day; or the time during which the moon's motion from the sun amounts to 6°.<BR>19 (In grammar) The instrumental case, or noun in that case.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A man of a mixed class, the son of a Śūdra woman by a Vaiśya; or, according to some, of an outcast Kṣetriya, by a Kṣetriya female; the occupation of this class is writing, accounts, &c. a writer, a scribe.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A woman of the same caste.<BR>2 (In arithmetic, &c.) A surd or irrational quantity.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, to act, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणत्राण|करणत्राणं
करणत्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>करण an organ of sense, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणत्व
करणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Instrumentality, mediate agency.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणनियम
करणनियम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Suppression or restraint of the organs of sense.<BR>E.<BR>करण, and नियम restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणि
करणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>Doing, making, effecting.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, अनि affix; also with कन added करणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणीय|करणीयं
करणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be done or made.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करणीसुता
करणीसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An adopted daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=191" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण्ड|करंड|करंडः|करण्डः
करण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A basket or covered box of bamboo wicker work.<BR>2 A bee-hive, a honey-comb.<BR>3 A sword.<BR>4 A sort of duck.<BR>5 An aquatic weed, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, अण्डन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण्डिन्|करंडिन्
करण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>A fish in general.<BR>E.<BR>करण्ड Vallisneria, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतल|करतलः
करतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The palm of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and तल lower part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतलधृत
करतलधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Held in the hand.<BR>E.<BR>करतल, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतलस्थ
करतलस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Held in the hand, what is in or under the hand.<BR>E.<BR>करतल, and स्थ what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करताल|करतालं|करतालः
करताल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>1 A musical instrument, a cymbal.<BR>2 Beating time by clapping the hands.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, ताल musical time, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करतोया
करतोया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The Karatoyā river, a river in the north-east of Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and तोय water: at the wedding of ŚIVA and PĀRVATĪ, the water which had been poured into the hand of the former, constituted, upon its being thrown on the ground, the source of this river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करद
करद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Subject to tax or duty.<BR>2 Tributary.<BR>3 Who gives his hand, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करदक्ष
करदक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Handy, dexterous, ready. कर, and दक्ष clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करदीकृत
करदीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subjugated, made tributary.<BR>E.<BR>करद, and कृत made with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करधृत
करधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Held, supported by the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करनिहित
करनिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Held in the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and निहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्र|करपत्रं
करपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A saw.<BR>2 Splashing water about while bathing, playing or gamboling in water.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पत्र a leaf; being in the hand as a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्रवत्|करपत्त्रवन्त्|करपत्रवन्त्
करपत्रवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The palmyra tree, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR>E.<BR>करपत्र a saw, and मतुप् affix, the spatha being compared to a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपत्रिका
करपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Playing with water, gamboling in it, splashing it about; also करपत्र, करपात्र and करपत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपर्ण|करपर्णः|करपर्ण्ण
करपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A species of castor oil tree.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपल्लव|करपल्लवः
करपल्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपात्र|करपात्रं
करपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The hand hollowed so as to hold any thing.<BR>2 The throwing of water in sport.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पात्र a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपाल|करपालः
करपाल<BR>(-लः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and पल protecting, or with बल to be strong, करबाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपालिका
करपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A cudgel, a short club or wooden sword.<BR>2 A sword or one edged knife.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, पाल to nourish, ण्वुल् affix, and the fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपुट|करपुटः
करपुट<BR>m. (-टं)<BR>Joining the palms of the hands to shew respect.<BR>2 The hands joined and hollowed to receive anything.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पुट् a bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करपृष्ठ
करपृष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Back of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करप्रचेय
करप्रचेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be held, to be taken hold of.<BR>2 To be collected by taxes.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and प्रचेय to be accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करप्राप्त
करप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Held in hand, got, secured.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करबाल|करबालः
करबाल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>1 A finger nail.<BR>2 A sword, a scymitar: see करपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करबालिका
करबालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small sword, &c. see करपालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभ|करभः
करभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 The metacarpus, the hand from the wrist to the root of the fingers.<BR>2 A young camel or any young animal.<BR>3 A young elephant.<BR>4 A perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>A she camel.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to reject, अभच Uṇādi affix: see कलभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभप्रिया
करभप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, a sort of Hedysarum.<BR>E.<BR>करभ, and प्रिय fond of; folder for camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभिन्
करभिन्<BR>m. (-भी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करभ and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभीर|करभीरः
करभीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>करभ a young animal, and ईर who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभूषण|करभूषणं
करभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A bracelet, an ornament worn round the wrist.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and भूषण an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमट्ट|करमट्टः
करमट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>The betel nut tree: see गुवका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमरिन्
करमरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A prisoner, a captive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमर्द्द|करमर्द|करमर्दः|करमर्द्दः
करमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A small tree bearing an acid fruit, commonly Karonda or Karinda, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and मृद to destroy, अण् affix; what is plucked by the hand; also with कन् affix, करमर्द्दक and fem. with ङीष् affix करमर्द्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमर्द्दक|करमर्दक|करमर्दकः|करमर्द्दकः
करमर्द्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमाल|करमालः
करमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Smoke, probably an error or corruption for खतमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमाला
करमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The hand used as a rosary, the joints of the fingers corresponding to the beads.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and माला a rosary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमुक्त|करमुक्तं
करमुक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A missile weapon, but thrown by the hand, a dart, a javelin, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराग्रपल्लव
कराग्रपल्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>कर and अग्र to the point, पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्ब|करंब|करंबः|करम्बः
करम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled.<BR>2 Set, inlaid.<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>Flour or meal mixed with curds: see करम्भ.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, अम्बच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्बित|करंबित|करम्बितः
करम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Intermingled, mixed, blended, &c.<BR>2 Pounded, reduced to grains or dust.<BR>2 Set, inlaid.<BR>E.<BR>करम्ब and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करम्भ|करंभ|करंभः|करम्भः
करम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A cake, flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and रभि to send, &c. अच् affix, also with कन् added करम्भक; also with रवि to sound, &c. करम्ब, &c. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कररुद्ध
कररुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Stopped by the hand, held tight or fast.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and रुद्व stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कररुह|कररुहः
कररुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and रुह to grow, to rise, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करर्द्धि|करर्द्धिः
करर्द्धि<BR>m. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>A small musical instrument used for marking time, (a castanet,) or clapping the hands together for that purpose.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, ऋद्धि property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवालिका
करवालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small club, &c. see करबालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवी
करवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The leaf of the Asafoetida plant, Hingupatri: see कवरी and कारवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवीर|करवीरः
करवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A fragrant plant, (Oleander or Nerium odorum.)<BR>2 The name of a demon.<BR>3 A sword or scymitar.<BR>4 A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">Page193</a>] cemetery, a place for burning or interring the dead.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>(-री)<BR>1 A name of ADITI, the mother of the gods.<BR>2 A good cow.<BR>3 A woman who has borne a son, a mother.<BR>E.<BR>कर here said to mean a root, वीर to become evident, and अच् affix, or कर hand, वि prefixed to ईर to go, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=192" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करवीरक|करवीरकः
करवीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sword.<BR>2 A poison, the poisonous root of the Oleander.<BR>3 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशाखा
करशाखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A finger.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशीकर|करशीकरः
करशीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Water expelled by an elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>कर his trunk, and शीकर drizzling rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशूक|करशूकः
करशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, and शूक the beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करशोथ|करशोथः
करशोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>OEdematous swelling of the hands.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and शोथ swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करहाट|करहाटः
करहाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR>2 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, and रह to abandon, करह a lotus, अट what goes, or by what it goes; or कर the hand, हट to illuminate or adorn, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करहाटक|करहाटकः
करहाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराघात|कराघातः
कराघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A thump, a blow with the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करामर्द्द|करामर्द|करामर्दः|करामर्द्दः
करामर्द्द^1<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Carissa carondas): see करमर्द्द.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराम्बुक|कराम्बुकः
कराम्बुक^1<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta, Rox.) see कृष्णपाक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260425. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराम्लक|कराम्लकः
कराम्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Carissa carondas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करायिका
करायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird, a small kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करारोट|करारोटः
करारोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A finger ring.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, रुट to shine, with आङ् prefixed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराल|करालं|करालः
कराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Great, large.<BR>2 High, lofty.<BR>3 Formidable, terrible.<BR>4 Having projecting teeth.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Rosin, pitch, or a mixture of oil and the resin of the Śāl tree.<BR>n. (लं)<BR>A dark kind of Tulasī or Basil.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kind of swallow wort, commonly Ananta-mul, (Hemisdemus Indicus). see शारिवा.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>One of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>कर the hand, &c. ला with आङ् prefixed to take, and क affix; or कर, and अल to be able, &c. affix अण्, fem. do टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालक|करालकः
करालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of Basil, the dark kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालकर
करालकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Having a large trunk, (an elephant.)<BR>2 Having a powerful arm or hand.<BR>E.<BR>कराल, and कर a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालम्ब|करालंब|करालम्बः
करालम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>One who stretches out his hand to support or pick up another, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and अलम्ब what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालम्बन
करालम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Extending the hand, taking by the hand, helping, sustaining.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and आलम्बन supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालवदन
करालवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of hideous aspect, ugly, frightful.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A form or emanation of DURGA.<BR>E.<BR>कराल, and वदन countenance; also करालानन, करालमुखः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालिक|करालिकः
करालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालित
करालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Afraid of, alarmed by or at.<BR>2 Rendered formidable.<BR>3 Magnified.<BR>E.<BR>कराल and इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकणवल्ली
करिकणवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A species of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>E.<BR>करिकण elephant-pepper, वल्ली a vine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकुम्भ|करिकुंभ|करिकुम्भः
करिकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The frontal globe of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and कुम्भ the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिकुसुम्भ|करिकुसुम्भः
करिकुसुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A fragrant powder prepared from the flowers of the Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea); also करिकुसुम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिगर्ज्जित|करिगर्जित|करिगर्ज्जितं
करिगर्ज्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The roaring of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>करिन् an elephant, and गर्ज्जित sounding, thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिचर्म्मन्|करिचर्मन्
करिचर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>An elephant's hide.<BR>E.<BR>करिन्, and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिज|करिजः
करिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A young elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करि an elephant, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिदन्त|करिदंत|करिदन्तः
करिदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 An elephant's tusk.<BR>2 Ivory.<BR>E.<BR>करिन् and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिदारक|करिदारकः
करिदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>करि an elephant, दृ to tear or rend, ण्वुल affix; or with युच् affix करिदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिन्
करिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कर the proboscis of this animal, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिनासिका
करिनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिपिप्पली
करिपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant bearing a pungent fruit, (Pothos officinalis, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>करि, and पिप्पली long-pepper; Elephantpepper; considered by native writers as a large species of that condiment; also गजपिप्पली, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिपोत|करिपोतः
करिपोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A young elephant, one under ten years old.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and पोत a young animal; also करिशावक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिबन्ध|करिबंध|करिबन्धः
करिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिमाचल|करिमाचलः
करिमाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>करि, मा splendor, and चल to go; the lion being considered as the natural enemy and destroyer of the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिमुख|करिमुखः
करिमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A title of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and मुख a face: this deity being represented with an elephant's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करियादस्
करियादस्<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>A water elephant, a hippopotamus.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and यादस् any aquatic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिर|करिरः
करिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The shoot of a bamboo: see करीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिशावक|करिशावकः
करिशावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A young elephant under five years old; according to some, also until ten years.<BR>E.<BR>see करिपोत, शावक meaning a young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्ठ
करिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Doing much.<BR>E.<BR>कर who does, इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यत्|करिष्यन्त्
करिष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Doing, (with a future sense,) about to do.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, शतृ affix of the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिष्यमाण
करिष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>About to do, going to do.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, शानच् affix of the future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीन्द्र|करींद्र|करीन्द्रः
करीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A large, or a war or state elephant.<BR>2 INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करि, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीयस्
करीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Who does much.<BR>E.<BR>कर who does, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीर|करीरः
करीर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The shoot of a bamboo; also करिर.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A thorny plant, described as growing in desarts, and fed upon by camels, commonly Karit, (Capparis aphylla, Rox.)<BR>2 A water jar.<BR>f. (-रा or री)<BR>1 The root of an elephant's tusk.<BR>2 A cricket, a small grasshopper, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to injure, to throw. or send, &c. and ईरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरिका
करीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The root of an elephant's tusk: see करीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीष|करीषं|करीषः
करीष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>Dry cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to throw, send, &c. and ईषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषङ्कषा|करीषंकषा
करीषङ्कषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A strong wind, a gale.<BR>E.<BR>करीष, कष to disturb, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=193" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषाग्नि|करीषाग्निः
करीषाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A fire of dry cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>करीष, and अग्नि fire; this substance is very generally used as fuel in Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुण|करुणः
करुण<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>Tenderness, pity, compassion, the feeling or sentiment.<BR>adv. (-णं)<BR>Pitifully, in distress.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Sorrow, affliction, one of the eight sentiments.<BR>2 The name of a fruit tree, the pamplemousse^1, (Citrus decumana.)<BR>3 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to send or cast, उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणात्मक
करुणात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Compassionate, tender-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा आत्म self, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणापर|करुणापरः
करुणापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Compassionate, tender.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा, and पर excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणामल्ली
करुणामल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Double jasmin: see नवमल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणामय
करुणामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Gentle, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणार्द्र
करुणार्द्र<BR>mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्र)<BR>Tender-hearted, soft, sensitive.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा, and आर्द्र moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणाविप्रलम्भ
करुणाविप्रलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Grief of separation with the uncertainty of meeting again, fears occurring in absence.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा sorrow, and विप्रलम्भ separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणावेदिता
करुणावेदिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Charitableness, kindliness.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा, वेदिन् who knows, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेट|करेटः
करेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and इट to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटव्या
करेटव्या<BR>f. (व्या)<BR>The numidian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटु|करेटुः
करेटु<BR>mf. (-टुः)<BR>The numidian crane.<BR>E.<BR>क for कुत् bad, or क water, and रेट to sound, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणु|करेणुः
करेणु<BR>mf. (-णुः)<BR>A male or female elephant.<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A plant: see कर्णिकार.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, &c. ण्णु Uṇādi affix; also with a final long vowel, करेणू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुभू
करेणुभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint; also पालकाप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुवर्य्य|करेणुवर्य
करेणुवर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A large or powerful elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करेणु, and वर्य्य excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुसुत|करेणुसुतः
करेणुसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणू
करेणू<BR>mf. (-णूः)<BR>A male or female elephant: see करेणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेनर|करेनरः
करेनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Benzoin or storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोट|करोटं
करोट<BR>mf. (-टः or टी)<BR>The bones of the head, the scull.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, रुट to oppose, to defend, &c. affixes अच् and इन् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोत्कर
करोत्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bundle of rags.<BR>2 A heavy tax.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and उत्कर plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोदक
करोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water held in, or poured into the hand.<BR>E.<BR>कर, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क|कर्कः
कर्क<BR>mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Good, excellent.<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 A white horse.<BR>2 A mirror.<BR>3 A water jar.<BR>4 A crab.<BR>5 A sign of the zodiac, (Cancer.)<BR>6 Fire.<BR>7 A long gourd.<BR>8 Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, &c. कः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कचिर्भिटी
कर्कचिर्भिटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A small cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>कर्क, and चिर्भिटी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कट|कर्कटः
कर्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A crab.<BR>2 The sign of the zodiac, (Cancer.)<BR>3 A kind of bird, the numidian crane.<BR>4 A long gourd: see तुम्बी.<BR>5 The fibrous root of the lotus.<BR>6 The curved end of the beam of a balance, to which the strings supporting the scale are attached.<BR>7 A compass.<BR>8 The radius of a circle.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A plant, commonly Kurkavali, (Momordica mixta.)<BR>(-टी)<BR>1 A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus, Rox.)<BR>2 The fruit of the silk cotton tree.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>4 A water jar.<BR>E.<BR>कर्क a Sautra root, to laugh or smile, and अटन् affix, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटक|कर्कटकः
कर्कटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटशृङ्गिका
कर्कटशृङ्गिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Kāṅkarasriṅgī: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटशृङ्गी
कर्कटशृङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant, the fruit of which is compared to the claw or feelers or a crab, the horn of a goat, &c. see अजशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कट, शृङ्ग a horn, इनि and ङीष् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटाख्या
कर्कटाख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कट, and आख्या an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटि|कर्कटिः
कर्कटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus): see कर्कट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटु|कर्कटुः
कर्कटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>The numidian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कन्धु|कर्कंधु|कर्कंधुः|कर्कन्धुः
कर्कन्धु<BR>mf. (-न्धुः-न्धूः)<BR>A tree, the jujube: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कन्धू|कर्कंधू
कर्कन्धू<BR>mf. (-न्धूः)<BR>The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्क excellent, धा to have, and कु Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ऊञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कर|कर्करं|कर्करः
कर्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hard, firm.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Stone, limestone. especially the nodule found in Bengal under the name of Kankar.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mirror.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A small water jar.<BR>E.<BR>कर्क beauty, from कर्क to smile, र from रा to give, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराक्ष|कर्कराक्षः
कर्कराक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कर a mirror, and अक्ष an eye: bright-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराङ्ग|कर्करांग|कर्कराङ्गः
कर्कराङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कर firm, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटु|कर्कराटुः
कर्कराटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A glance, a side look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटुक|कर्कराटुकः
कर्कराटुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The numidian crane: see कर्करेटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करान्धक
कर्करान्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A blind well, one of which the mouth is overgrown with grass, &c. so as to be hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराल|कर्करालः
कर्कराल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A curl, a ringlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करी
कर्करी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A water jar with a spout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करीका
कर्करीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small water jar.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, in the reiterative form, and ईकः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेट|कर्करेटं
कर्करेट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The hand curved as a claw or half moon, for the purpose of grasping any thing.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कर hard, firm, इट to go, to be, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करेटु|कर्करेटुः
कर्करेटु<BR>mf. (-टुः)<BR>The numidian crane: see करेटु.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कश hard, &c. रेट to sound, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कश|कर्कशः
कर्कश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Violent.<BR>2 Hard.<BR>3 Intangible.<BR>4 Cruel.<BR>5 Unfeeling, unmerciful.<BR>6 Harsh, unkind.<BR>7 Miserly.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Sunda rocani, (Crinum?)<BR>2 A kind of cassia, (Cassia esculenta.)<BR>3 Sugar cane.<BR>4 A sword, a scymitar.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>Wild jujube; also कर्क्कशिका.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to injure, विच् affix, कश with the same meaning, and अच्, highly injurious: or कर्क्क a Sautra root, and शः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशच्छद|कर्कशच्छदः
कर्कशच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>2 A kind of gourd, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्कश hard, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशदल|कर्कशदलः
कर्कशदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gourd, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कशवाक्य|कर्कशवाक्यं
कर्कशवाक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Harsh or contumelious speech.<BR>E.<BR>कर्श, and वाक्य speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कसार|कर्कसारं
कर्कसार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR>E.<BR>कर्क, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारु|कर्कारुः
कर्कारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR>E.<BR>कव white, ऋ to go, or to be, उण् affix; also कर्कारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=194" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कारुक|कर्कारुकः
कर्कारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क्कि|कर्कि|कर्किः
कर्क्कि<BR>m. (-र्क्किः)<BR>The sign Cancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क्केतर
कर्क्केतर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of gem or precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोट|कर्कोटः
कर्कोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>One of the principal serpents or Nāgas of Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोटक|कर्कोटकः
कर्कोटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Ægle marmelos): see मालूर.<BR>2 A Nāga or serpent: see the preceding.<BR>3 A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia); in this sense; also कर्कोटिका.<BR>5 Sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कोटकी
कर्कोटकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, a Ghosha with yellow flowers: see घोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्घ
कर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (कर्घति)<BR>To go, to move. Probably a variant misreading for 'karba'^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260702. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/283.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूर|कर्चूरः|कर्च्चूरं|कर्च्चूरः
कर्चूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Curcuma reclinata, Rox.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gold: see कर्बूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्चूरक|कर्चूरकः|कर्च्चूरकः
कर्चूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet): see कर्बूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ज|कर्ज्ज
कर्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (कर्जति)<BR>To pain or make uneasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण<BR>r. 10th cl. (कर्णयति)<BR>To pierce or bore:<BR>with the prefix आङ्, समा, (सम् and आङ्) or उप,<BR>to hear or listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ण|कर्णः|कर्ण्ण
कर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 KARṆA a prince, sovereign of Aṅgadeśa, and elder brother, by the mother's side, to the Pāṇḍu princes, being the son of SŪRYA by KUNTĪ, before her marriage with PĀṆḌU.<BR>3 The helm or rudder of a vessel.<BR>4 (In prosody,) A spondee, a foot of two long syllables.<BR>5 (In geometry,) The hypothenuse of a triangle, or the diagonal of a tetragon.<BR>6 A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>7 A kind of swallow wort, (Colotropis gigantea.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण to hear, घञ् affix; or कृ do, &c. न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकण्डु|कर्णकण्डुः
कर्णकण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>Itching of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and कण्डु itching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णकीटी
कर्णकीटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 An insect or worm with many feet, and of a reddish colour, (Julus cornifex.)<BR>2 A small centipede.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण the ear, and कीट an insect, being supposed to attack the ear especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णक्ष्वेड|कर्णक्ष्वेडः|कर्ण्णक्ष्वेड
कर्णक्ष्वेड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>An affection of the ear, a roaring or constant noise in it.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and क्ष्वेड a buzzing in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग
कर्णग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Hanging on the ear, next to the ear.<BR>2 Extending to the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगूथ|कर्णगूथं|कर्णगूथः
कर्णगूथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The wax of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and गूथ foeces, excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णगोचर
कर्णगोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Capable of being heard, perceptible to the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and गोचर perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग्राह|कर्णग्राहः
कर्णग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A helmsman.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and ग्राह who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णग्राहवत्|कर्णग्राहवन्त्
कर्णग्राहवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a helmsman.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णग्राह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णछिद्र|कर्णच्छिद्र
कर्णछिद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>The outer auditory passage.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and छिद्र hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजप|कर्णजपः
कर्णजप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An informer.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and जप who whispers; also कर्णेजप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलूका
कर्णजलूका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An insect, (Julus.)<BR>2 A small centipede: see कर्णकीटी.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण; and जलूका a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलौकस्
कर्णजलौकस्<BR>f. (-काः)<BR>A worm: see the preceding; also कर्णजलौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजलौका
कर्णजलौका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of insect, (Julus cornifex, &c.)<BR>2 A small centipede; also कर्णजलौकस् and कर्णजलूका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजाह|कर्णजाहं|कर्ण्णजाह
कर्णजाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The root of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and जाह affix in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णजित्
कर्णजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A title of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and जित् conqueror; KARṆA. having taken the part of the Kurus, was killed by ARJUNA in the great battle between them and the Pāṇḍus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णताल|कर्णतालः|कर्ण्णताल
कर्णताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The flapping of an elephant's ears.<BR>E.<BR>कण, and ताल tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णदर्पण|कर्णदर्पणः|कर्ण्णदर्पण
कर्णदर्पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An ear-ring, an ornament of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and दर्पण a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णदुन्दुभि|कर्णदुन्दुभिः|कर्ण्णदुन्दुभि
कर्णदुन्दुभि<BR>f. (-भिः)<BR>A kind of worm: see कर्णकीटी.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and दुन्दुभि a sort of drum; making a noise in the ear like a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णधार|कर्णधारः|कर्ण्णधार
कर्णधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pilot, a helmsman.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण the helm, धृञ् to have or hold, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णनाद|कर्ण्णनाद
कर्णनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Ringing in the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णन्दु
कर्णन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>A woman's ear-ring: see कर्णान्दु and कर्णेन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपाक|कर्णपाकः|कर्ण्णपाक
कर्णपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Inflammation of the outer ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and पाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपाली|कर्ण्णपाली
कर्णपाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>An ornament of the ear, a garland or string of jewels pendent from it.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and पाल to cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपुर|कर्ण्णपुर
कर्णपुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The capital of KARṆA, the ancient name of Bhāgalpur.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and पुर city; also कर्णपुर् f. (-पूः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपूर|कर्णपूरः|कर्ण्णपूर
कर्णपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>2 The blue lotus.<BR>3 An ear-ring.<BR>4 The Asoka tree.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and पूर to make full, to complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णपूरक|कर्णपूरकः|कर्ण्णपूरक
कर्णपूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्णपूर an ear-ring, and कन् resembling, like the large round drop or pendant of a Hindustani ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णप्रतिनाह|कर्णप्रतिनाहः|कर्ण्णप्रतिनाह
कर्णप्रतिनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A disease of the ear, suppression of the excretion or wax, which is supposed to have dissolved and pass by the nose and mouth.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and प्रतिनाह suppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णफल|कर्णफलः|कर्ण्णफल
कर्णफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Ophiocephalus kurrawey.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमद्गुर
कर्णमद्गुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus unitus.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and मद्गुर a sheat fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमल|कर्णमलं|कर्ण्णमल
कर्णमल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The excretion or wax of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कण, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमुकुर|कर्णमुकुरः
कर्णमुकुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An ornament of the ear.<BR>2 An ear-ring.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and मुकुर a mirror; reflecting its beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णमोटी|कर्ण्णमोटी
कर्णमोटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A name of DEVĪ or DURGĀ in one of her forms or incarnations.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण the ear, मुठ to rub, घञ् and ङीप् affixes; this is sometimes written कर्णमोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णलतिका
कर्णलतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The lobe of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, लता a creeping plant, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवंश|कर्णवंशः|कर्ण्णवंश
कर्णवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An elevated platform.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and वंश a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवत्|कर्णवन्त्
कर्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having ears.<BR>2 Long eared.<BR>3 Having a helm.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवर्जित|कर्णवर्जितः|कर्णवर्ज्जितः|कर्ण्णवर्ज्जित
कर्णवर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Earless.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and वर्जित deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णविद्रधि
कर्णविद्रधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Ulceration of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and विद्रधि a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेध|कर्णवेधः|कर्ण्णवेध
कर्णवेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Boring the ears: as a religious ceremony it is performed where there are three sons, to prevent one of them from dying.<BR>2 Piercing the ear in general.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and वेध piercing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनिका
कर्णवेधनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An instrument for perforating the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, विध to pierce, ल्युट् and ङीष् affixes, with कन् added, and the fem. termination टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=195" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेधनी
कर्णवेधनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टक|कर्णवेष्टकं
कर्णवेष्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An ear-ring: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णवेष्टन|कर्णवेष्टनं
कर्णवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An ear-ring.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशष्कुली|कर्ण्णशष्कुली
कर्णशष्कुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The outer part of the ear, the cartilage and depressions leading to the auditory passage.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and शष्कुल the hollows of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णशूल|कर्णशूलः|कर्ण्णशूल
कर्णशूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Ear-ache.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and शूल pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णश्रव|कर्ण्णश्रव
कर्णश्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Audible, loud.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and श्रव hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णसंस्राव|कर्णसंस्रावः|कर्ण्णसंस्राव
कर्णसंस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Discharge of pus from the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and संस्राव suppuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णस्राव
कर्णस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Discharge of ichorous matter from the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and स्राव running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णस्फोटा|कर्ण्णस्फोटा
कर्णस्फोटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and स्फोट a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णाट|कर्णाटः
कर्णाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A country, Karṇāṭa, whence the modern Karnatic: the name however was anciently applied to the central districts of the peninsula, including Mysūr.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of the musical modes, the bride of the Rāga MĀLAVA.<BR>2 A plant.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण the ear, a prince, &c. and अट to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णानुज|कर्णानुजः
कर्णानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of Yudhiṣṭhira, the elder brother of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and अनुज younger born; the younger brother of KARṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्तिक|कर्णांतिक
कर्णान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Near or close to the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and अन्तिक near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्दु|कर्णांदु|कर्णान्दुः
कर्णान्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 An ornament of the ear.<BR>2 An ear-ring: see the next, and कर्णेन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णान्दू|कर्णांदू
कर्णान्दू<BR>f. (-न्दूः)<BR>An ornament of the ear, an ear-ring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and अन्दू a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णारा
कर्णारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>An instrument for perforating the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण the ear, ऋ to go, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णारि|कर्णारिः
कर्णारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णालङ्कार|कर्णालंकार
कर्णालङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ear-ring, an ornament of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण and अलङ्कार ornament; also कर्णालङ्किया, कर्णालङ्कृति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णास्फाल|कर्णास्फालः
कर्णास्फाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The flapping of an elephant's ear.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and आस्फाल with the same import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिक|कर्णिकः
कर्णिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Having large or long ears.<BR>2 Having ears.<BR>3 Having a helm.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A steersman.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An ear-ring or ornament of the ear.<BR>2 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>3 The middle finger.<BR>4 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>5 A fruit stalk.<BR>6 A pen or small brush.<BR>7 A plant, (Premna spinosa, &c.) see अग्निमन्थ.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णं the ear, &c. इक affix; or कन् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकाचल|कर्णिकाचलः|कर्ण्णिकाचल
कर्णिकाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The fabulous mountain Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णिका the seed vessel of a lotus, and अचल a mountain, Meru being in the centre of the world, the divisions of which are delineated as the leaves of a lotus; also other compounds, as कर्णिकाद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकार|कर्णिकारः|कर्ण्णिकार
कर्णिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The name of a tree, commonly Kaniyar, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR>2 A sort of Cassia, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>3 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णिका an ornament of the ear, ऋ to go, अण् affix; also with कन् added कर्णिकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिकिन्
कर्णिकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णिका the tip of his trunk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिन्
कर्णिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि)<BR>1 Having an ear, relating to the ear, &c.<BR>2 Long eared.<BR>3 Barbed, (as an arrow.)<BR>4 Having a helm.<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>1 The name of a mountain, one of the seven principal ranges of the mountains, dividing the universe.<BR>2 The side of the neck, the part near the ear.<BR>3 A steersman.<BR>f. (-णिनी)<BR>A disease of the uterus, prolapsus or polypus uteri.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णिल
कर्णिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Long eared.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीरथ|कर्णीरथः|कर्ण्णीरथ
कर्णीरथ<BR>mf. (-थः-था)<BR>A covered car, or according to some, a litter for the conveyance of women, &c. borne on men's shoulders.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णी the part near the ear, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णीसुत|कर्णीसुतः|कर्ण्णीसुत
कर्णीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of KAṂSA the enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णी the mother of this prince, and मुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेजप|कर्णेजपः
कर्णेजप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>An informer, a tale bearer.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णे in the ear, and जप to recite in a low voice, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्णेन्दु|कर्णेन्दुः|कर्ण्णेन्दु
कर्णेन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A semicircular ornament of the ear.<BR>2 An earring.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and इन्दु the moon, a crescent, &c. see कर्णान्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्त|कर्त|कर्तः|कर्त्तः
कर्त्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (कर्त्तयति)<BR>To slacken or unloose, to remove; also कत्र and कर्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तन|कर्तन|कर्त्तनं
कर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cutting, cutting off or in pieces.<BR>2 Spinning cotton or thread.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Scissors.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तरिका|कर्तरिका
कर्त्तरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A knife.<BR>2 A small sword or cutlass.<BR>3 A hunter's knife or sword, a couteau de chasse.<BR>4 A scissors.<BR>E.<BR>कर्त्तरी, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तरी|कर्तरी
कर्त्तरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A scissors or shears.<BR>2 A knife.<BR>3 A small sword or cutlass.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, अरन् affix, and ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तव्य|कर्तव्य|कर्त्तव्यं|कर्त्तव्यः
कर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be done or made.<BR>2 What ought to be done.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तव्यता|कर्तव्यता
कर्त्तव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Necessity, obligation, propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>कत्तव्य, and तल् affix; also with त्व affix कर्त्तव्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तित|कर्तित
कर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut, cut off.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तिष्यत्|कर्तिष्यत्
कर्त्तिष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Intending or wishing to cut.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, शतृ affix of the future participle; also कर्त्तिष्यमाण (-णः-णा-णं) with शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तुकाम|कर्तुकाम
कर्त्तुकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Desirous or intending to do.<BR>E.<BR>कत्तुम् to do, काम desire, the final of the first rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृ|कर्तृ
कर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्ती-र्त्तृ)<BR>1 An agent, a doer, a maker, one who makes or does.<BR>2 One who practices what he knows.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 (In grammar,) The active noun, the nominative case.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, and तृच् affix: it may also be read कर्त्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृक|कर्तृक
कर्त्तृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>An agent, one who does any thing.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृकत्व|कर्तृकत्व
कर्त्तृकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Agency, action.<BR>E.<BR>कर्त्तृक and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृका|कर्तृका
कर्त्तृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small sword.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, कृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृत्व|कर्तृत्व|कर्तृत्वं
कर्त्तृत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Agency, the act or property of an agent.<BR>E.<BR>कर्त्तृ, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix कर्त्तृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्य|कर्तृवाच्यः
कर्त्तृवाच्य<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>(In grammar,) The active voice.<BR>E.<BR>कर्त्तृ agent, and वाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्र|कर्त्रं
कर्त्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (कर्त्रयति)<BR>To unloose, to remove: see कर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्त्री
कर्त्री<BR>f. (-र्त्री)<BR>A scissors.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, तृच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (कर्दति)<BR>To grumble, as the bowels; to caw as a crow; or to make any such noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्द|कर्दः|कर्द्द|कर्द्दः
कर्द<BR>m. (-र्दः)<BR>Mud, clay.<BR>E.<BR>कर्द to sound ill, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=196" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दट|कर्दटः|कर्द्दट|कर्द्दटः
कर्दट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The fibrous root of the lotus.<BR>2 Mud, dirt.<BR>2 Any aquatic weed, as Vallisneria, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्द mud, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दन|कर्दनं|कर्द्दन|कर्द्दनं
कर्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Grumbling of the bowels, borborygmi.<BR>E.<BR>कर्द to make such a noise, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दम|कर्दमः|कर्द्दम|कर्द्दमं|कर्द्दमः
कर्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Mud, mire, clay.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>3 A Prajāpati, the son of BRAHMĀ by CHĀYĀ, and he father of Kapila: (this personage appears to be an innovation in Hindu mythology.)<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>A plant.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>कर्द to sound badly, and अम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्दमाटक|कर्दमाटकः|कर्द्दमाटक|कर्द्दमाटकः
कर्दमाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A receptacle for filth, a sewer, a necessary.<BR>E.<BR>कर्दम filth, अट to go, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पट|कर्पटं|कर्पटः
कर्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Old and patched or ragged garments.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, and अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटधारिन्
कर्पटधारिन्<BR>m. (री)<BR>A religious mendicant, a Fakir, a beggar in patched or ragged clothes, or sometimes with merely a cloth to cover the privities.<BR>E.<BR>कर्पट as above, धृ to have, and णिनि affix; also कर्पटिक and कर्पटिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटिक|कर्पटिकः|कर्प्पटिक
कर्पटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पटिन्
कर्पटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>See कर्पटधारिन्. This and the two preceding words may also be used in three genders, meaning, beggar in general, or any one in beggarly raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पर|कर्परः
कर्पर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The skull, the cranium.<BR>2 An iron saucepan or frying pan.<BR>3 A kind of weapon.<BR>4 The Glomerous fig tree: see उडुम्बर.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A collyrium extracted from the Amomum authorhiza, Rox.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराल|कर्परालः
कर्पराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, described as a Pīlu growing in the hills.<BR>E.<BR>कर्पर the skull, &c. and अल to adorn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पराश
कर्पराश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Sand, gravel, a sandy soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्परिकातुत्थ|कर्परिकातुत्थं
कर्परिकातुत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>A collyrium extracted from the Amomum authorhiza: see कर्परा.<BR>E.<BR>कर्परिका for कर्परी, and तुत्थ any collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पास|कर्पासं|कर्पासः
कर्पास<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>Cotton.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The cotton tree; also कार्पासी.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, &c. पास Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूर|कर्पूरं|कर्पूरः
कर्पूर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, ऊरः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरक|कर्पूरकः
कर्पूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet, Rox.) see कर्ब्बूरक and कचूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरतिलका
कर्पूरतिलका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>One of DURGĀ'S female attendants or confidantes: see जया.<BR>E.<BR>कर्पूर camphor, and तिलक the sectarial spot on the forehead; having the Tilaka of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्प्पूरतैल|कर्पूरतैल|कर्पूरतैलं
कर्प्पूरतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Camphor liniment.<BR>E.<BR>कर्प्पूर, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्प्पूरनालिका|कर्पूरनालिका
कर्प्पूरनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Rice dressed with spices, camphor and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्प्पूरमणि|कर्पूरमणि|कर्पूरमणिः
कर्प्पूरमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A white mineral used medicinally.<BR>E.<BR>कर्प्पूर, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्फर|कर्फरः
कर्फर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब|कर्ब्ब
कर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (कर्बति)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बर
कर्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>See कर्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुदार|कर्ब्बुदारः
कर्बुदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mountain ebony: see कोबिदार.<BR>2 Blue barleria: see नीलझिण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुर|कर्बुरः|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Variegated, of a spotted or variegated color.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 A sort of basil, (Ocymum gratissimum): see वर्वरा.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Datura, (the fruit.)<BR>(-रः)<BR>1 A demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>2 A variegated colour.<BR>3 A plant, (Curcuma reclinata, Rox.) see शठी.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>5 Rice growing amidst inundation.<BR>E.<BR>कब to tinge or dye, उरच् Uṇādi affix and र inserted, or कर्ब to go, &c. and उरन् affix, also long, कर्बुर; it is also often read with the dental ब, but perhaps erroneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूर|कर्बूरः|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बूर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Gold.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A species of curcuma, (C. reclinata, Rox.)<BR>2 Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>3 A demon.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A leech.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Yellow orpiment, see कर्बुर and कर्बूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूरक|कर्ब्बूरकः
कर्बूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding: also कचूरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब्बूरित|कर्बूरित
कर्ब्बूरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Variegated, many coloured.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ब्बूर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्म|कर्म
कर्म्म<BR>mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं)<BR>Act, action; see कर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकर|कर्मकर|कर्मकरः|कर्म्मकरः
कर्म्मकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 A hired laborer.<BR>2 A servant of any kind, (as a pupil, &c.) not a slave.<BR>3 An agent, any one who does work or business.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides): see मूर्व्वा.<BR>2 Bryonia grandis: see निम्बिका.<BR>3 A female servant or slave.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म work, act, and कर who does or performs; also कर्म्मकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकार|कर्मकार|कर्मकारः|कर्म्मकारः
कर्म्मकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 A worker, one who does any business, an artisan, a mechanic.<BR>2 One who performs any act.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blacksmith, one of the progeny of the divine artist VIŚVAKARMA.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म an act, कृञ् to perform, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकारक|कर्मकारक
कर्म्मकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who does any work, one who performs any act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and कारक who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकारिन्|कर्मकारिन्
कर्म्मकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Working, doing any work, who performs any act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and कारिन् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकार्म्मुक|कर्मकार्मुक|कर्मकार्मुकः
कर्म्मकार्म्मुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A strong bow.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म used to action, कार्म्मुक a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकीलक|कर्मकीलक|कर्मकीलकः|कर्म्मकीलकः
कर्म्मकीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकृत्|कर्मकृत्
कर्म्मकृत्<BR>mfn. (-त)<BR>1 Having done work.<BR>2 A workman, an artisan.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मकृतवत्|कर्मकृतवत्
कर्म्मकृतवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The director of a religious rite, the reciter of the Mantras or formula.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and कृतवत् doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मक्षम|कर्मक्षम|कर्म्मक्षमः
कर्म्मक्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Competent to an act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and क्षम to be patient, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मचेष्टा|कर्मचेष्टा
कर्म्मचेष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Active exertion, action.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मचोदना|कर्मचोदना
कर्म्मचोदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The object of acts, the inducement, to ritual acts, or the combination of knowledge, the thing to be known, and the person who acquires knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and चोदना impelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मज|कर्मज|कर्मजः|कर्म्मजः
कर्म्मज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Resulting from or produced by any act, especially religious or moral, or unrighteous or immoral actions.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The Kali-yug or fourth and present age of the world, the age of iniquity.<BR>2 The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मजगुण|कर्मजगुण|कर्म्मजगुणः
कर्म्मजगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A predicate or property resulting from human acts, as separation, reunion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मज, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मज्ञ|कर्मज्ञ
कर्म्मज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Skilled in any work.<BR>2 Acquainted with religious rites.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मठ|कर्मठ|कर्मठः|कर्म्मठः
कर्म्मठ<BR>mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>1 Finishing carefully.<BR>2 Accomplishing any rite.<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>The director and performer of a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and ठच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=197" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मणिवाच्य
कर्म्मणिवाच्य<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>The passive voice, (in grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मणि in the act or object, and वाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मण्य|कर्मण्य|कर्म्मण्यः
कर्म्मण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Proper to any act, suitable to or fit for it.<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>Wages, hire.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Energy, activity.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मन् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मण्यभुज्|कर्मण्यभुज्
कर्म्मण्यभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Working for hire.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मण्य wages, and भुज to eat, affix क्विप्: see भरण्यभुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मत्याग|कर्मत्याग|कर्मत्यागः
कर्म्मत्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Abandonment of worldly duties or ceremonial rites.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and त्याग abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मत्व|कर्मत्व
कर्म्मत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Acts, action, the active discharge of the duties and functions of life.<BR>2 Any act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and त्व affix; also with तल्, कर्म्मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मदुष्ट|कर्मदुष्ट
कर्म्मदुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Following wicked or degrading practices, immoral, disreputable.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and दुष्ट defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मदोष|कर्मदोष|कर्मदोषः
कर्म्मदोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Error, blunder.<BR>2 Sin, vice.<BR>3 The evil consequence of human acts.<BR>4 Discreditable conduct or business.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मध्वंस|कर्मध्वंस|कर्मध्वंसः
कर्म्मध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Loss of benefits arising from religious acts.<BR>2 Destruction of any work.<BR>3 Disappointment.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मन्|कर्मन्
कर्म्मन्<BR>mn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Action in general.<BR>2 The object of an action.<BR>3 The subject of action in grammar, considered of three kinds, प्राप्य or व्याप्य when it is simple, as ग्रामं गच्छति he goes to the village; सूर्य्यं पश्यति he sees the sun; विकार्य्य when change of form is implied, as सुवर्णं कुण्डलं^1 करोति gold forms the ear-ring; and निर्वर्त्य when some new product is evolved, as कटं करोति he makes a mat; पुत्रं प्रसूते she bears a son.<BR>4 The objective noun.<BR>5 Action specific, moral duty, the obligation imposed by peculiarities of tribe, occupation, &c.<BR>6 Natural, active property, as maturity, of heat; support, of earth; dispersion, of wind, &c.<BR>7 Religious action, as sacrifice, ablution, &c. especially as originating in the hope of future recompense, and as opposed to speculative religion or knowledge of spirit.<BR>8 (In Logic,) Substantial action or motion of five kinds, upwards, downwards, extension, contraction, and going in general.<BR>9 Action or act involving retribution or reward, virtue, vice, &c.<BR>10 Fate, the certain consequence of previous acts.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, मनिन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161202. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मनिष्ठ|कर्मनिष्ठ
कर्म्मनिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Engaged in active duties.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A Brahman who performs sacrifices, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and निष्ठ who stays in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मन्दिन्|कर्मन्दिन्|कर्मंदिन्
कर्म्मन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>The beggar, the religious mendicant, the member of the fourth order; see आश्रम, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म work, अन्द to abandon, or कर्म्मन्द the name of a saint, the founder of the sect, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मफल|कर्मफल|कर्म्मफलं
कर्म्मफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Pain, pleasure, &c. considered as the consequence or fruit of human actions.<BR>2 The name of a fruit: see कर्म्मरङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मफलोदय|कर्मफलोदय
कर्म्मफलोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The occurrence of consequences.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मफल, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मबन्धन|कर्मबन्धन|कर्मबंधन
कर्म्मबन्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bound by acts.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Confinement to repeated existence, as the consequence of acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मभू|कर्मभू
कर्म्मभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>Tilled or cultivated ground.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and भू earth, ground, &c. it may also mean the same as the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मभूमि|कर्मभूमि|कर्मभूमिः|कर्म्मभूमिः
कर्म्मभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Aryavarta or the central part of India, Bharata Varṣa, the whole of India, or any similar place considered as holy land.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and भूमि earth: where men perform the ceremonies of the Hindu faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्ममूल|कर्ममूल|कर्म्ममूलं
कर्म्ममूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Kuśa or sacrificial grass; see कुश.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and मूल a root: it being used in many religious and essential Karmas or sacred rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मयुग|कर्मयुग|कर्म्मयुगं
कर्म्मयुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The fourth and present age of the world, the iron age, the Kali-yug: see कलि, and above, कर्म्मज.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and युग a Yuga or age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मयोग|कर्मयोग|कर्मयोगः|कर्म्मयोगः
कर्म्मयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Performance of worldly functions or duties.<BR>2 The same, considered as equivalent to a religious duty.<BR>3 Active exertion, industry.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and योग union or observances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मरङ्ग|कर्मरङ्ग|कर्म्मरङ्गः
कर्म्मरङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A plant bearing an acid fruit, (Averhoa carambola.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मरी|कर्मरी
कर्म्मरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The manna of the bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवज्र|कर्मवज्र|कर्मवज्रः|कर्म्मवज्रः
कर्म्मवज्र<BR>m. (-ज्रः)<BR>A Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and वज्र the thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवश|कर्मवश|कर्मवशः
कर्म्मवश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The necessary influence of acts.<BR>2 Fate, considered as the inevitable consequence of actions done in a former life.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मवाटी|कर्मवाटी
कर्म्मवाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A lunar day, or the 30th division of a lunar month.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and वाटी a road, &c. regulating all ceremonies and observances, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविघ्न|कर्मविघ्न
कर्म्मविघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Impediment, obstruction.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and विघ्न hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविधि|कर्मविधि
कर्म्मविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Rule of action, observance, practice.<BR>2 Mode of conducting any ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and विधि precept; also कर्म्मविधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविपर्य्यय|कर्मविपर्यय
कर्म्मविपर्य्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Succession of office or employment, revolving or alternating duty.<BR>2 Contrariety or reverse of any act or business.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and विपर्य्यय contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविपाक|कर्मविपाक|कर्म्मविपाकः
कर्म्मविपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Future reward or punishment, the consequence of human acts in a subsequent birth.<BR>2 A work on this subject, explaining expiatory rites to be performed in cases of disease, &c. supposed to be the punishment of offences in a previous existence.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and विपाक, maturity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मविशेष|कर्मविशेष
कर्म्मविशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Variety of act or actions.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशील|कर्मशील|कर्म्मशीलः
कर्म्मशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Assiduous, laborious.<BR>2 One who perseveres in his duties without looking forward to their reward.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and शील attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशुद्ध|कर्मशुद्ध
कर्म्मशुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Approved occupation.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and शुद्ध pure, correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशूर|कर्मशूर|कर्म्मशूरः
कर्म्मशूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Assiduous, laborious.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and शूर dexterous, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मशौच|कर्मशौच
कर्म्मशौच<BR>m. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Humility.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म and शौच purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसंग्रह|कर्मसङ्ग्रह
कर्म्मसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Collective acts, comprising the act, its performance, and the performer.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and संग्रह assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसचिव|कर्मसचिव|कर्मसचिवः|कर्म्मसचिवः
कर्म्मसचिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A minister, a subordinate one employed upon active duties, as a judge, a deputy, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and सचिव an adviser, a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=198" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्मसन्न्यासिक|कर्मसंन्यासिकः|कर्म्मसंन्यासिक|कर्म्मसन्न्यासिकः
कर्म्मसन्न्यासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ascetic, a religious person who has withdrawn from the world.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and सन्न्यासिक a Sannyāsī or religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसमाधि
कर्म्मसमाधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Devotion, abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and समाधि abstraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसम्भव|कर्मसम्भव
कर्म्मसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced by, or the consequence of acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसाक्षिन्|कर्मसाक्षिन्
कर्म्मसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and साक्षिन् an evidence; who beholds all deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसाधन|कर्मसाधन
कर्म्मसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Implement, means.<BR>2 Articles essential to the performance of a religious act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and साधन means of effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मसिद्धि|कर्मसिद्धि|कर्मसिद्धिः
कर्म्मसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Success, accomplishment.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्महेतु|कर्महेतु
कर्म्महेतु<BR>mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु)<BR>Arising from acts, caused by acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and हेतु cause; also with कन् added कर्म्महेतुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्माङ्ग|कर्माङ्ग|कर्मांग
कर्म्माङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Part or progress of any act.<BR>2 Part of a sacrificial rite.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मात्मन्|कर्मात्मन्
कर्म्मात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Endowed with principles of action, active, acting.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुबन्ध|कर्मानुबन्ध
कर्म्मानुबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Connexion with or dependance upon acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुबन्ध attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुबन्धिन्|कर्मानुबन्धिन्
कर्म्मानुबन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Connected or confined by works.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुबन्धिन् what connects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुरूप|कर्मानुरूप
कर्म्मानुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 According to action or act.<BR>2 According to function or duty.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुरूप according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुरूपतस्|कर्मानुरूपतस्
कर्म्मानुरूपतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Conformably to act, function, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुष्ठान|कर्मानुष्ठान
कर्म्मानुष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Practising one's duties, discharging peculiar functions.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुष्ठान following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुसार|कर्मानुसार|कर्मानुसारः
कर्म्मानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Consequence of or conformity to acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुसार consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुसारतस्|कर्मानुसारतस्
कर्म्मानुसारतस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to one's deeds.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुसार conformity, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मानुस्थायिन्
कर्म्मानुस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Practising duties, performing rites, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अनुस्थायिन् following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्त|कर्मान्त|कर्मांत|कर्मान्तः|कर्म्मान्तः
कर्म्मान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Tilled or cultivated land.<BR>2 The end or abandonment of ritual acts.<BR>3 The end of any task or act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अन्त an end or limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्तर|कर्मान्तर|कर्मांतर
कर्म्मान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Difference or contrariety of action, re-action.<BR>2 Penance, expiation.<BR>3 Suspense, interval of action.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अन्तर difference, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मान्तिक|कर्मान्तिक|कर्मांतिक|कर्मान्तिकः
कर्म्मान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Final, completing.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A servant, one who finishes work.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मान्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्माभिधायक|कर्माभिधायक
कर्म्माभिधायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Enjoining, or prescribing duties or acts.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अभिधायक what shows; also कर्म्माभिधायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मार|कर्मार|कर्मारः|कर्म्मारः
कर्म्मार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An artificer, a mechanic, a blacksmith, a brazier, a carpenter, &c.<BR>2 A bamboo.<BR>3 An acid fruit: see कर्म्मरङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, ऋ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मारम्भ|कर्मारम्भ
कर्म्मारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्मः)<BR>Commencement of any act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मार्ह|कर्मार्ह|कर्मार्हः|कर्म्मार्हः
कर्म्मार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>1 Fit for work, able to do any thing.<BR>2 Suitable to any rite, &c.<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मिन्|कर्मिन्
कर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>1 Busy, active, engaged in any work.<BR>2 Belonging or relating to any act.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मिष्ठ|कर्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठः
कर्म्मिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Active, assiduous, diligent.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मीर|कर्मीर|कर्म्मीरः
कर्म्मीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Variegated: see किर्म्मीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मीरक|कर्मीरक
कर्म्मीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मेन्द्रिय|कर्मेन्द्रिय|कर्मेंद्रिय|कर्म्मेन्द्रियं
कर्म्मेन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An organ of action; five are reckoned, the hand, the foot, the larynx or organ of the voice, the organ of generation, and that of fœculent excretion.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोदार|कर्मोदार
कर्म्मोदार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Any honourable or valiant act, magnanimity, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and उदार lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोद्युक्त|कर्मोद्युक्त
कर्म्मोद्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Actively labouring, busily engaged.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and उद्युक्त exerting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्म्मोद्योग|कर्मोद्योग
कर्म्मोद्योग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Engaging actively in any work.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म, and उद्योग effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्व|कर्व्वः
कर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (कर्वति)<BR>To be proud, to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्व|कर्व|कर्वः|कर्व्वः
कर्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>1 Love, desire.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to injure, and व Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वट|कर्वट|कर्वटः|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्व्वट<BR>m. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 The capital of a district, (of two or four hundred villages,) in a pleasant site and of handsome construction, a market town, &c.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A city.<BR>E.<BR>कर्व to be proud, and अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्वर|कर्वर|कर्वरः
कर्व्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A demon or imp.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 The leaf of the asafoetida plant: see हिङ्गुपत्री.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to injure, क्करच् Uṇādi affix; if derived from कर्व्व to go, &c. this word is read कर्व्वर, but such a reading is probably inaccurate: see कर्व्वर, also कर्व्वुर; it is sometimes considered as a various reading of this last, meaning, variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ष|कर्षः
कर्ष<BR>mn. (-र्षः-र्षं)<BR>A weight of gold or silver, a Karṣa equal to sixteen Māṣas; this, according to the ancient division of five Rattis to the Māṣa, would make the Karṣa equal to about 176 grains troy; in common use, eight Rattis are given to the Māṣa, and the Karṣa is therefore about 280 grains troy: see मास and रक्तिक.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Drawing, dragging, pulling.<BR>2 Ploughing.<BR>3 Attracting.<BR>4 Beleric myrobalan: see विभीतक.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A cultivator of the soil, one who lives by tillage.<BR>2 What draws or drags.<BR>3 Attractive, what attracts.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Ploughing, cultivating the ground.<BR>2 Pulling. dragging.<BR>3 Attracting.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणि|कर्षणिः
कर्षणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>A dishonest woman.<BR>E.<BR>कृष and अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणीय
कर्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be drawn or pulled.<BR>2 To be attracted, to be conciliated or won.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, with अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षफल|कर्षफलः
कर्षफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्ष the same, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षयत्
कर्षयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Dragging, pulling.<BR>2 Attracting.<BR>3 Harassing, annoying.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to attract, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षाह्व
कर्षाह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>A Tola, a weight of sixteen Māṣas.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ष, and आह्वा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षित
कर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Drawn.<BR>2 Attracted.<BR>3 Ploughed.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to draw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=199" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-षि)<BR>1 What pulls or draws.<BR>2 What ploughs or furrows.<BR>3 Attractive, what attracts.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A medicinal sort of moon plant: see क्षीरिणी.<BR>2 The bit of a bridle.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, &c. णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षू
कर्षू<BR>m. (-र्षूः)<BR>1 A fire of dried cowdung.<BR>2 Agriculture, cultivating, cultivation.<BR>3 Livelihood.<BR>f. (-र्षूः)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 A canal.<BR>3 A shallow trench for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, &c. Uṇādi affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि<BR>ind.<BR>When, at what time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हिचित्
कर्हिचित्<BR>ind.<BR>Sometimes, occasionally, ever; नकर्हिचित् never.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल<BR>r. 1st cl. (कलति)<BR>To sound.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (कलति, कालयति)<BR>To throw or cast, to send;<BR>also 1st and 10th cls. (कलति, कलयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To count or reckon:<BR>with आङ् prefixed,<BR>1 To take.<BR>2 To bind or tie;<BR>with परि,<BR>To keep in mind, to think or remember;<BR>with वि,<BR>To maim, to separate a part, to make defective;<BR>with सम,<BR>To sum up, to add.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Crude, undigested.<BR>2 Weak.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A low or soft tone, as humming, buzzing, &c.<BR>2 The Śāl tree.<BR>3 In poetry, time equal to four mātras or instants.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A small part of any thing.<BR>2 A digit or one sixteenth of the moon's diameter.<BR>3 A division of time, equal to thirty Kāṣas or about eight seconds.<BR>4 The 60th part of one thirtieth of a zodiacal sign, a minute of a degree.<BR>5 Interest on a capital.<BR>6 Any practical art, mechanical or fine, sixty-four such are enumerated, as carpentering, architecture, jewellery, farriery, acting, dancing, music, medicine, poetry, &c.<BR>7 The menstrual discharge.<BR>8 A boat.<BR>9 Fraud, deceit.<BR>E.<BR>कल to sound, to count, &c. (-अच्) affix; or क pleasure, and ल what gives, from ला to bring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलक|कलकः
कलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of fish: see शकुल.<BR>2 Name of a species of prose composition.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकण्ठ|कलकंठ|कलकण्ठः
कलकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A low murmuring tone.<BR>2 The Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A dove, a pigeon.<BR>4 A goose.<BR>E.<BR>कल a low tone, and कण्ठ the throat; in whose throat it is made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकल|कलकलः
कलकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A confused noise, the murmuring or buzz of a crowd.<BR>2 Resin, pitch, the resin of the Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>कल to sound, as above; the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकूजिका
कलकूजिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wanton, a lascivious woman.<BR>E.<BR>कल, and कूज to coo, affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलघोष|कलघोषः
कलघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>कल, घुष to sound, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्क|कलंक|कलंकः|कलङ्कः
कलङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A spot or mark.<BR>2 Defamation, abuse.<BR>3 The rust of iron.<BR>E.<BR>क BRAHMĀ, water, &c. लकि to deface, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्ककर
कलङ्ककर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Censorious, calumniating, defaming.<BR>2 Spotting, staining.<BR>E.<BR>कलङ्क, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्ककला
कलङ्ककला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A digit of the moon in shadow.<BR>E.<BR>कलङ्क, and कला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कमय
कलङ्कमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Spotted, stained.<BR>2 Calumniated, defamed.<BR>E.<BR>कलङ्क and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कष|कलंकष|कलंकषः|कलङ्कषः
कलङ्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A lion.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A musical instrument: see करताली.<BR>E.<BR>कल a murmuring sound, and कष to make a sound, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कित|कलंकित
कलङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spotted, soiled, stained.<BR>2 Calumniated, defamed.<BR>E.<BR>कलङ्क, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्किन्
कलङ्किन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्की-ङ्किनी-ङ्कि)<BR>1 Soiled, stained.<BR>2 Disgraced, reviled.<BR>3 Rusty.<BR>E.<BR>कलङ्क, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलङ्कुर|कलंकुर|कलंकुरः|कलङ्कुरः
कलङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>कल a sound, and कुर to emit sound, क affix, and the termination of the 2nd case retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलञ्ज|कलंज|कलंजः|कलञ्जः
कलञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>An animal struck with a poisoned weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलट|कलटं
कलट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The that of a house; other works read this कुटक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलता
कलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Melody, music.<BR>E.<BR>कल, and तल् affix; also with त्व, कलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्र|कलत्रं
कलत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The hip and loins.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>3 A royal citadel, a strong hold or fastness.<BR>E.<BR>गड to distil, &c. अत्रच् affix, क is substituted for ग, and ड and ल are interchangeable: see कडत्र; or कल weak, feeble, and त्र, from त्रै to preserve, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधूत|कलधूतं
कलधूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Silver: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौत|कलधौतं
कलधौत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Silver.<BR>3 A low or pleasing tone; also कलधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलधौतलिपि
कलधौतलिपि<BR>f. (-पिः)<BR>1 A streak of gold.<BR>2 Illumination of a manuscript with gold.<BR>E.<BR>कलधौत, and लिपि writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलध्वनि|कलध्वनिः
कलध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 The turtle dove.<BR>2 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>4 A low sweet tone.<BR>E.<BR>कल, and ध्वनि a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A spot, a stain.<BR>2 An offence, fault, defect.<BR>3 Murmuring, sounding.<BR>4 An embryo or the first vestige of the foetus.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of cane.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Subjection, submission.<BR>2 Chattering, talking.<BR>3 Shedding, emitting.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दर|कलंदरः|कलन्दरः
कलन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man of a mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन्दिका|कलंदिका
कलन्दिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Knowledge, intelligence, wisdom in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभ|कलभः
कलभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A young elephant: see कल.<BR>2 The Datura plant.<BR>E.<BR>कल to cast, अभच् Uṇādi affix; or according to some authorities कृ to cast, अभच् affix, making करभ, and र is then changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम|कलमः
कलम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Rice which is sown in May and June, and ripens in December or January; a white rice growing in deep water: see शालि.<BR>2 A pen, a reed for writing with.<BR>3 A thief, a rogue.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. and अमः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्ब|कलंब|कलंबः|कलम्बः
कलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 The stalk of a potherb.<BR>3 The Kadamba, (Nauclea cadamba): see कदम्ब.<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>Calumba root, (Menispermum calumba.)<BR>f. (-म्बी) or m. and f. (-म्बः-म्बी)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Convolvulus repens, &c.) see कडम्बी.<BR>E.<BR>कड to delight, अम्बच् affix, ल substituted for ड, fem. affix ङीष्; also कलम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बिका|कलंबिका
कलम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A potherb: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to कलम्बी.<BR>2 The nape of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, and लबि to be, to rest, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बुट|कलंबुट|कलम्बुटं
कलम्बुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलम्बू
कलम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>A potherb: see कलम्बी the fem. affix being ऊञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलयत्
कलयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Computing, calculating.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=200" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलरव|कलरवः
कलरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A dove, a pigeon.<BR>2 The Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A low or pleasing tone, a humming, buzzing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कल a low tone, and रव what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलल|कललं|कललः
कलल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>The womb, the uterus; according to some, the embryo one month after conception.<BR>E.<BR>कल to reckon, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललज|कललजः
कललज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Resin, the extract of the Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललजोद्भव|कललजोद्भवः
कललजोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>कललज, and उद्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविंकः|कलविङ्कः
कलविङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A sparrow.<BR>2 A plant, (Echites antidysenterica): see कलिङ्कक.<BR>3 A spot, a stain.<BR>4 A white Chowri.<BR>E.<BR>कल a low tone, chirping, &c. वकि to go, &c. अच् affix, the deriv. is irr; also कलविङ्कक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलश|कलशः
कलश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>An earthen water pot; also कलस, कलशि, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क water, लश to labour, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशि|कलशिः
कलशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>1 A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR>2 A water jar.<BR>E.<BR>क water, लश to labour, &c. कि affix; also कलशी and कलसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशी
कलशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A plant.<BR>2 A water jar: see the preceding, and कलश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलस|कलसः
कलस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>A water jar: see कलश.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A measure, a Droṇa: see द्रोण.<BR>2 A rounded pinnacle or ball on the top of a temple.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A plant: see कलशि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसि|कलसिः
कलसि<BR>f. (-सिः)<BR>See कलशि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसीसुत|कलसीसुतः
कलसीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA: see घटोद्भव and अगस्त्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसोदधि|कलसोदधिः
कलसोदधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>कलस, and उदधि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलस्वर
कलस्वर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A low musical sound.<BR>E.<BR>कल, and स्वर a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलह|कलहं|कलहः
कलह<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Strife, contention.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The sheath of a sword, a scabbard.<BR>2 A road, a way.<BR>3 Deceit, falsehood.<BR>4 Violence without murderous weapons, abuse, beating, kicking, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कल a pleasing sound, and ह what destroys, from हन with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहंस|कलहंसः
कलहंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A drake, or according to some, a teal.<BR>2 A gander.<BR>3 Another bird, (Gallinula porphyria.)<BR>4 BRAHM or the Supreme Being.<BR>5 An emperor.<BR>6 A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>कल pleasing sound, and हंस a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहकार|कलहकारः
कलहकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Contending with, fighting.<BR>2 Quarrelsome, turbulent.<BR>E.<BR>कलह, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहकारिन्
कलहकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Assailing, contending or fighting with.<BR>2 Quarrelsome, fractions, turbulent.<BR>E.<BR>कलह, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहनाशन|कलहनाशनः
कलहनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Febrifuge nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहप्रिय|कलहप्रियः
कलहप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Quarrelsome.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>NĀRADA.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The Maina, a bird.<BR>E.<BR>कलह, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहान्तरिता|कलहांतरिता
कलहान्तरिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An appeased wife, one who has been angry and is sorry for it.<BR>E.<BR>कलह strife, अन्तरित covered, &c. fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहापहृत
कलहापहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken by force.<BR>E.<BR>कलह, and अपहृत taken away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकुल
कलाकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकुशल
कलाकुशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Skilled in the elegant arts; singing, dancing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कला, and कुशल clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाकेलि|कलाकेलिः
कलाकेलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Gay, frolicsome, wanton.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A name of KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>कला deceit, and केलि who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाङ्कुर|कलांकुर|कलांकुरः|कलाङ्कुरः
कलाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A crane.<BR>2 A name of KAṂSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाचिका
कलाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The fore arm, the arm below the elbow; also कलाची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाची
कलाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाद|कलादः
कलाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A goldsmith: see कणाद.<BR>E.<BR>कला an art, and दा to give, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानिधि|कलानिधिः
कलानिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कला a digit, निधि a treasure; containing many digits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलानुनादिन्
कलानुनादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A bee, but particularly one of a very large kind.<BR>2 A sparrow.<BR>3 The Cātaka, a bird so called.<BR>E.<BR>कल a buzz, &c. अनुनद to sound, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलान्तर|कलांतर|कलान्तरं
कलान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Interest, profit.<BR>E.<BR>कला a part, अन्तर over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाप|कलापः
कलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 An ornament in general.<BR>2 A zone, a string of bells worn by women round the wrist.<BR>3 A peacock's tail.<BR>4 Assemblage, multitude.<BR>5 A quiver.<BR>6 The moon.<BR>7 A clever and intelligent man.<BR>8 The name of a grammar of the Sanscrit language, ascribed to the god KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>9 A village where the destroyer KALKI is to be born.<BR>10 A poem written in one metre.<BR>E.<BR>कला an art, a division of time, &c. आप to obtain, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापक|कलापकं|कलापकः
कलापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A rope on an elephant's neck.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A number of verses in one metre.<BR>2 A series of four stanzas on one subject.<BR>3 A loan to be repaid when the peacocks spread their tails.<BR>E.<BR>कलाप and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापिन्
कलापिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 The Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 Waved leaf fig tree.<BR>4 The author of the Kalāpa grammar.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A species of cyperus.<BR>E.<BR>कलाप a peacock's tail, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापूर्ण|कलापूर्णः|कलापूर्ण्ण
कलापूर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कला a digit, and पूर्ण filled, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाभृत्
कलाभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 An artist, a mechanic, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कला a digit, &c. and भृत् who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलामक|कलामकः
कलामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of rice ripening in the cold season: see कलम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाम्बि|कलांबिः|कलाम्बिः
कलाम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बिः)<BR>Lending, a loan: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाम्बिका
कलाम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lending, a loan.<BR>E.<BR>कल a part, and अम्ब to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाय|कलायः
कलाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The name of various leguminous seeds, chiefly of the order Phaseolus, particular kinds of pulse or vetches.<BR>E.<BR>क wind, ला to bring or give, and युक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायखञ्ज
कलायखञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>One who trembles and totters as he walks.<BR>E.<BR>कलाय, and खञ्ज a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायन|कलायनः
कलायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tumbler, a dancer, but especially one who dances or walks on a sharp edge, as the edge of a sword, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कला a part, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलालाप|कलालापः
कलालाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A bee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कल buzz, and आलाप speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलावत्|कलावन्त्
कलावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A name of Candra or the moon.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A celestial lute or Vīṇā.<BR>2 The mother of RĀDHĀ.<BR>3 An Apsaras.<BR>4 A mystical ceremony, initiation of the Tāntrika student, in which the goddess DURGĀ is supposed to be transferred from the water jar to the body of the novice.<BR>E.<BR>कला a digit, or कल a sweet tone, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=201" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविक|कलाविकः
कलाविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविकल|कलाविकलः
कलाविकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sparrow: see कलविङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाहक|कलाहकः
कलाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A musical instrument; also काहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलि|कलिः
कलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 The fourth age of the world, according to the Hindus; the iron age, or that of vice: the commencement of the Kali-yug or age, is placed 3,101 years anterior to the Christian aera, so that in A. D. 1830, the Kali year is 4,931, the number of its years is 432,000, at the expiration of which, the world is to be destroyed.<BR>2 The age personified.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>4 Strife, dissension.<BR>5 An arrow.<BR>6 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>An unblown flower: see कलिका.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count or reckon, इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिक|कलिकः
कलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A curlew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An unblown flower.<BR>2 The bottom or peg of a lute.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, इन् affix कलि, and with ङीष्, कली as above; again, कन् pleonastic affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकापूर्व्व|कलिकापूर्व|कलिकापूर्व्वं
कलिकापूर्व्व<BR>n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>Acts leading to future consequences, not connected with those of a previous birth.<BR>E.<BR>कलिका a bud, अपूर्व्व not preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकार|कलिकारः
कलिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A plant bearing a nut, which is used as a febrifuge, (Grey bonduc): see पूर्तिकरञ्ज.<BR>2 The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>3 Another bird, a small one with a yellow head, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR>4 A name of NĀRADA.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A poisonous plant: see लाङ्गली.<BR>E.<BR>कलि strife, &c. कृञ् to make, affix अण्; also with कन् added कलिकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकारक|कलिकारकः
कलिकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Grey bonduc; also कलिमारक.<BR>2 The name of NĀRADA a divine sage, and great mischief maker: see कलिकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्ग|कलिंग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The febrifuge nut plant, (Caesalpinia bonduccella.)<BR>2 The fork-tailed shrike, (Lanius forficatus, Lath.)<BR>2 The name of a country; the name Kaliṅga is applied in the Purāṇas to several places, but it especially signifies a district on the Coromandel coast, extending from below Cuttack to the vicinity of Madras, in this sense, like some other names of countries, it is usually confined to the plural number, (-ङ्गाः) confounding the place with the people inhabiting it.<BR>nf. (-ङ्गं-ङ्गा)<BR>A medicinal seed, that of Echites antidysenterica.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 A woman of a good shape.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum): see त्रिवृत्.<BR>E.<BR>कलि strife, &c. ग from गम to go, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिङ्गक|कलिङ्गकः
कलिङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The seed of the Coraiya, (Echites antidysenterica): see इन्द्रयव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिञ्ज|कलिंज|कलिंजः|कलिञ्जः
कलिञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>A mat, a screen of grass, a tāti, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gained, acquired.<BR>2 Known, understood.<BR>3 Numbered, reckoned.<BR>4 Separated, divided.<BR>4 Made, done.<BR>6 Held, laid hold of.<BR>7 Sounded indistinctly, buzzed, murmured, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिद्रुम|कलिद्रुमः
कलिद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica,) also कलि, the tree of strife; being supposed to be the favorite haunt of imps or goblins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्द|कलिंद|कलिंदः|कलिन्दः
कलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>कलि strife, दा to give, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दकन्या|कलिंदकन्या
कलिन्दकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>The Yamunā.<BR>E.<BR>कलिन्द the sun or a mountain, कन्या daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दनन्दिनी|कलिंदनंदिनी
कलिन्दनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Yamunā or Jumna river.<BR>E.<BR>कलिन्द the name of a mountain, part of the Himālaya range, and नन्दिनी a daughter; the source of the river being in the mountain Kalinda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिन्दशैलजाता
कलिन्दशैलजाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The Yamunā river: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कलिन्दशैल the mountain, and जाता born; also कलिन्दसू, कालिन्दी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिप्रिय|कलिप्रियः
कलिप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Quarrelsome, mischievous, mischief making.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A monkey, an ape.<BR>2 NĀRADA.<BR>E.<BR>कलि strife, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिमारक|कलिमारकः
कलिमारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Bonduccella): see पूतिकरञ्ज.<BR>E.<BR>कलि strife, मृ to destroy or remove, affixes अण् and कन्; some copies read कलिकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलियुग|कलियुगं
कलियुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The Kali, the present or iron age: see कलि.<BR>E.<BR>कलि, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिल|कलिलः
कलिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Impervious, impenetrable.<BR>2 Mixed, blended.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिवृक्ष|कलिवृक्षः
कलिवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुक्क|कलुक्कः
कलुक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A musical instrument; a cymbal.<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>1 A tavern.<BR>2 A meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुष|कलुषं|कलुषः
कलुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Turbid, foul, muddy.<BR>2 Wicked, bad.<BR>mf. (-षः-षी)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Wrath.<BR>E.<BR>कल to go, &c. उषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषत्व
कलुषत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Foulness, turbidness.<BR>2 Opacity.<BR>3 Agitation, trouble, anger.<BR>E.<BR>कलुष foul, &c. त्व affix; also with तल्, कलुषता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषयोनि
कलुषयोनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Of impure origin.<BR>E.<BR>कलुष, and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषित
कलुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Defiled, contaminated.<BR>2 Foul, impure.<BR>3 Wicked.<BR>E.<BR>कलुष and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषिन्
कलुषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>1 Foul, impure.<BR>2 Depraved, wicked.<BR>3 Defiled.<BR>E.<BR>कलुष and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवर|कलेवरं|कलेवरः
कलेवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>कल semen, and वर best; formed from the seminal fluid; the termination of the ablative is retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलोत्ताल
कलोत्ताल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>High, sharp.<BR>E.<BR>कल, and उत्ताल loud, high sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क<BR>mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्का-ल्कं)<BR>Sinful, wicked.<BR>mn. (-ल्कः-ल्कं)<BR>1 Sediment, the deposit of oil, ghee, &c.<BR>2 Dirt, filth.<BR>3 Ordure, faeces.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>5 Hypocrisy.<BR>6 Pride.<BR>7 The beleric myrobalan.<BR>8 The wax of the ear.<BR>9 Levigated powder.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. कः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कफल|कल्कफलः
कल्कफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The pomegranate plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कि|कल्किः
कल्कि<BR>m. (-ल्किः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU, in his future capacity of destroyer of the world, the tenth and last Avatāra or descent of the deity, in the four ages or Kalpa.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्किन्
कल्किन्<BR>mfn. (-ल्की-ल्किनी-ल्कि)<BR>1 Foul, turbid, having sediment.<BR>2 Dirty.<BR>3 Wicked.<BR>m. (-ल्की)<BR>The last descent of VIṢṆU; see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कल्क and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प|कल्पः
कल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>In composition; Like, but with a degree of inferiority.<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 A Śāstra or sacred work; one of the six Vedāṅgas, and comprehending the description of religious rites.<BR>2 A day and night of BRAHMĀ, a period of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">Page203</a>] 4,320,000,000 solar-sydereal-years or years of mortals, measuring the duration of the world, and as many, the interval of its annihilation.<BR>3 A destruction of the world.<BR>4 A sacred precept, practice prescribed by the Vedas for effecting certain consequences.<BR>5 Propriety, fitness.<BR>6 Optionality, alternative, doubt.<BR>7 Resolve, purpose, any act of determination.<BR>8 One of the trees of INDRA'S paradise or Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to be able, घः affix, ऋ is changed to अल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=202" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पक|कल्पकः
कल्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to cut, बुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पक्षय|कल्पक्षयः
कल्पक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The destruction of all things, the end of the world.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पद्रुम|कल्पद्रुमः
कल्पद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A fabulous tree, one granting every thing desired.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प purpose, and द्रुम a tree; also कल्पद्रु, कल्पवृक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पन|कल्पनं
कल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cutting.<BR>2 Making, manufacturing.<BR>3 Making as a poem or tale, inventing, composing.<BR>nf. (नं-ना)<BR>1 Inference.<BR>2 Invention, fabrication.<BR>3 Caparisoning or decorating an elephant.<BR>(-नी)<BR>A scissors or shears.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, &c. ल्यु or ल्युट् affixes, and consequently टाप् or ङीप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनीय
कल्पनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be made or contrived.<BR>2 To be substituted or supplied.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, अनीयर् affix; also कल्प्य and कल्पितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पवायु
कल्पवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The wind that is to blow at the end of all things.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पवृक्ष|कल्पवृक्षः
कल्पवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>One of the fabulous trees of INDRA'S heaven; a tree which yields whatever may be desired.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प purpose, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पादि|कल्पादिः
कल्पादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>The beginning of a Kalpa, the renovation of all things.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प, and आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्त|कल्पांत|कल्पान्तः
कल्पान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The destruction of the world, the end of the Kalpa, or four ages of its existence.<BR>E.<BR>कल्प the period, and अन्त the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पान्तस्थायिन्|कल्पांतस्थायिन्
कल्पान्तस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Lasting, permanent.<BR>E.<BR>कल्पान्त, and स्थायिन् what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पित|कल्पितः
कल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made, fabricated, artificial.<BR>2 Composed, invented.<BR>3 Arranged, put in order.<BR>4 Prepared at once, put together extempore.<BR>5 Brought, conducted.<BR>6 Inferred.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant armed or caparisoned for war.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पितार्धं
कल्पितार्धं<BR>mfn. (-र्धः-र्धा-र्धं)<BR>One for whom or what a respectful offering is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>कल्पित made, and अर्ध an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प्य
कल्प्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्प्यः-ल्प्या-ल्प्यं)<BR>1 To be made or contrived.<BR>2 To be substituted.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मष|कल्मषं|कल्मषः
कल्मष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Dirty, foul.<BR>m. (-षं)<BR>A kind of hell, a division of the infernal regions.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 The hand below the wrist.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म virtuous or pious action, षो to destroy and क affix; the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माष|कल्माषः
कल्माष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा or षी-षं)<BR>Of a mixed or variegated colour.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A variegated colour.<BR>2 A mixture of black and white.<BR>3 Black.<BR>4 A demon or goblin.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The spotted cow of Jamadagni, the giver of all desires.<BR>E.<BR>कल to go, &c. क्विप् affix, कल्, मष to injure, अण् affix माष; what injures or triumphs over other colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषकण्ठ|कल्माषकंठ|कल्माषकण्ठः
कल्माषकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कल्माष black, and कण्ठ throat; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माषपाद|कल्माषपादः
कल्माषपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a king, also SAUDĀSA, transformed to a Rākṣasa by VASIṢṬHA.<BR>E.<BR>कल्माष, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Ready, prepared, armed.<BR>2 Healthy, free from sickness.<BR>3 Clever, dexterous.<BR>4 Deaf and dumb.<BR>5 Auspicious, (speech or discourse.)<BR>6 Counselling, monitory.<BR>7 Sound, perfect, free from mental or bodily imperfections.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 The dawn or break of day.<BR>2 Yesterday.<BR>3 Tomorrow.<BR>nf. (-ल्यं-ल्या)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>2 Congratulation, good wishes, annunciation of good tidings.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>Emblic myrobalan: see हरीतकी.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, &c. यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यजग्धि|कल्यजग्धिः
कल्यजग्धि<BR>f. (-ग्धिः)<BR>The morning meal, breakfast.<BR>E.<BR>कल्य dawn, and जग्धि eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यत्व|कल्यत्वं
कल्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Health.<BR>2 Recovery, convalescence.<BR>E.<BR>कल्य being well, and त्व affix of the abstract; also कल्यता with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यपाल|कल्यपालः
कल्यपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>कल्य vinous liquor, and पाल who nourishes; also with कन् added, कल्यपालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यवर्त्त|कल्यवर्त|कल्यवर्तः|कल्यवर्त्तः
कल्यवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Breakfast.<BR>E.<BR>कल्य, and वर्त्त, from वृत to be or abide, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Happy, well, right, prosperous, lucky.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 A leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Good fortune, happiness, prosperity.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>कल्य, healthy, &c. अ to be, to sound, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकर
कल्याणकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious, conferring good fortune, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणकृत्
कल्याणकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>1 Virtuous, good.<BR>2 Propitious, lucky.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणचार
कल्याणचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Following virtuous courses.<BR>2 Lucky, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, चर to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणधर्म्मन्|कल्याणधर्मन्
कल्याणधर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Good, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, धर्म्म duty, अनिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणपञ्चमीक
कल्याणपञ्चमीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fortnight which has the fifth lunation lucky.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, पञ्चमी the fifth, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवचन
कल्याणवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Friendly speech, good wishes.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणवीज|कल्याणवीजः
कल्याणवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Ervum hirsutum.)<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणाचार
कल्याणाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Virtuous, following good practices.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and आचार rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिका
कल्याणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याणी and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिन्
कल्याणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>1 Happy, lucky, prosperous.<BR>2 Auspicious, propitious.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्यापाल|कल्यापालः
कल्यापाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>कल्या spirituous liquor, and पाल who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्युष
कल्युष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (कल्लते)<BR>1 To sound ill or indistinctly.<BR>2 To sound.<BR>3 To be mute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Deaf.<BR>E.<BR>कल्ल to sound indistinctly, affix अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लत्व|कल्लत्वं
कल्लत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Indistinct articulation, hoarseness.<BR>2 Deafness.<BR>E.<BR>कल्ल to sound indistinctly, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix कल्लता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लि
कल्लि<BR>ind.<BR>To-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोल|कल्लोलः
कल्लोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>An enemy, hostile, inimical.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A surge, a billow.<BR>2 Joy, happiness, pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>कल्ल to sound, ओलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=203" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव
कव<BR>(ऋ) कवृ r. 1st cl. (कवते)<BR>1 To describe, (as a poet.)<BR>2 To paint, to picture; also कब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवक|कवकं|कवकः
कवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A mouthful.<BR>2 A fungus, a mushroom, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, अक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवच|कवचं|कवचः
कवच<BR>mn. (-चः-चं)<BR>1 Armour, mail.<BR>2 A drum used in battle, a kettle drum.<BR>3 An amulet, a charm.<BR>4 A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides): see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR>5 The mystical syllable Hum, forming part of a Mantra, and considered as a preservative like armour; it is also inscribed on a Birch leaf, &c. and worn as an amulet; being carried about the person as a charm: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, अच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचपत्र|कवचपत्रं|कवचपत्रः
कवचपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The Birch tree, commonly Bhojpatra: see भूर्जपत्र.<BR>E.<BR>कवच an amulet, and पत्र a leaf: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचहर|कवचहरः
कवचहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Wearing armour or amulets.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A boy, a child.<BR>E.<BR>कवच, and हृ to take, अच् or ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवटी
कवटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A door: see कवाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवयी
कवयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A kind of flat fish, commonly Kavay or Kay; remarkable for going by land from one spot to another, (Coiuscoboius, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कवर<BR>sub. mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A braid or fillet of hair.<BR>adj. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled, blended.<BR>2 Set, inlaid.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 Salt.<BR>2 Sourness or acidity.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>(-री)<BR>The leaf of the asafoetida plant, Hingupatri.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, &c. वृ to screen, अच् affix, fem. do. टाप् or ङीष्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरकी
कवरकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A captive, a prisoner: see वन्दी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभार|कवरीभारः
कवरीभार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fine head of hair.<BR>E.<BR>कवरी, and भार a load; also कवरीभर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरीभृत्
कवरीभृत्<BR>mfn. (भृत्)<BR>Wearing a fillet of hair.<BR>E.<BR>कवरी, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवल|कवलं|कवलः
कवल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A mouthful.<BR>2 A kind of fish, commonly Baliya.<BR>3 An astringent wash for cleaning the mouth, a gargle.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, water, &c. and वल to be strong, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A piece of cloth over a sore, a bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>कवल nominal verb, to eat, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवस|कवसः
कवस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, and अस Uṇādi affix; also कवच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट<BR>sub. mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>A door, the leaf or pannel of the door.<BR>E.<BR>क wind, air, वट to exclude, and अण् affix; also कपाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाटवक्र|कवाटवक्रं
कवाटवक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>A plant, commonly Kapāta ventu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवार|कवारं
कवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A bird, (Tantalus falcinellus, BUC.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, वर to prefer, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि<BR>mfn. (-विः-विः or -वी-वि)<BR>Learned, wise.<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>1 A poet.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 ŚUKRA, the regent of the planet Venus, and preceptor of the demons.<BR>4 A name of VĀLMĪKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa, the inventor of poesy.<BR>5 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-विः-वी)<BR>The bit of a bridle, or the reins altogether; also कविका.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, to celebrate, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविक|कविकं|कविकः
कविक<BR>nf. (-कं-का)<BR>The bit of a bridle, or the reins altogether.<BR>(-का)<BR>A sort of fish, the Kay.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविज्येष्ठ|कविज्येष्ठः
कविज्येष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A name of VĀLMĪKI, author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>कवि a poet, and ज्येष्ठ elder or superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविता
कविता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Poesy, poetical style or composition.<BR>2 A poem.<BR>E.<BR>कवि, and तल affix; also with त्व affix, कवित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवितावेदिन्
कवितावेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Wise, learned, a genius, a poet.<BR>E.<BR>कविता poetry, &c. वेदिन् who understands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविय|कवियं
कविय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>The bit of a bridle, or the reins.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, affix यः see कवि and कविक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविरामायण|कविरामायणः
कविरामायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of VĀLMĪKI.<BR>E.<BR>कवि a poet, &c. and रामायण the epic poem so called; the poet of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविलाशिका
कविलाशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A musical instrument, a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविवाल्मीकि|कविवाल्मीकिः
कविवाल्मीकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>The poet VĀLMĪKI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीय|कवीयं
कवीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The bit of a bridle, or the reins.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, छ affix; also कविय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवेल|कवेलं
कवेल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>क water, विल to send, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
कवोष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Slightly warm, tepid.<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>A slight warmth.<BR>E.<BR>कु indifferent, and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्य|कव्यं|कव्यः
कव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>An oblation or offering of food to deceased ancestors.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound or praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवाल|कव्यवालः
कव्यवाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A class of the manes or deified ancestors.<BR>E.<BR>कव्य an offering to the manes, वा occasionally, and ल who receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यवाहन
कव्यवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>कव्य, and वाहन vehicle; also कव्यवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश|कशः
कश<BR>r. 1st cl. (कशति-ते)<BR>To kill, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशा
कशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 A whip.<BR>2 Whipping, flogging.<BR>E.<BR>कश to hurt, अच् and टाप् affixes; also कष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशात्रय
कशात्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Three modes of whipping (a horse), good, bad, and middling.<BR>E.<BR>कषा, and त्रयम् three-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशार्ह|कशार्हः
कशार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Deserving a whipping.<BR>E.<BR>कशा a whip, and अर्ह to be fit or proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Clothing. du.<BR>m. (-पूः)<BR>Food and clothing.<BR>E.<BR>कश to injure, to remove, (pain, hunger, &c.) पु affix, the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशेरु<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>The back bone.<BR>f. (-रूः)<BR>A kind of grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>One of the nine divisions of Jambu Dvīpa.<BR>E.<BR>क sound, शृ to harm, ऊ or उ Uṇādi affix, and एरङ् substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुक|कशेरुकं|कशेरुकः
कशेरुक<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The back bone.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुस्
कशेरुस्<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>A grass, (Scirpus kysoor): see कशेरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्चन
कश्चन<BR>ind.<BR>Some body, a certain person; the first member of the compound is declinable, as कश्चन, कस्यचन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्चित्
कश्चित्<BR>ind.<BR>Some body, some one, a certain one: the first member of the compound is declinable, as कश्चित्, कस्मैचित् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Foul, dirty.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Fainting, syncope.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कश to go, क्मलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीर|कश्मीरः
कश्मीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a country, Kāṣmir.<BR>E.<BR>कश to go, ईरन् Uṇādi affix, and मुद inserted: see काश्मीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरजन्मन्
कश्मीरजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>Saffron: see काश्मीरजन्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Deserving a whipping.<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>2 A horse's flank.<BR>E.<BR>कश to beat, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यप|कश्यपः
कश्यप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni or deified sage, the son of MARĪCI, and father of the gods, demons, animals, fishes, reptiles, &c. by the seventeen daughters of DAKṢA.<BR>2 A kind of deer.<BR>3 A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपनन्दन|कश्यपनन्दनः
कश्यपनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कश्यप, and नन्दन a son, the son of KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=204" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष<BR>r. 1st cl. (कषति) 10th cl. (कषयुति)<BR>1 To injure, to hurt, to destroy, to kill.<BR>2 To try, to test: with नि, to try metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The touchstone.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A whip; also कशा.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, to test or try, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Unripe, immature.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Touch or test of gold by the touchstone.<BR>2 Rubbing, marking.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषपाषाण|कषपाषाणः
कषपाषाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A touchstone.<BR>E.<BR>कष and पाषाण a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाकु|कषाकुः
कषाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>कष to injure, आकु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाघात
कषाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A cut, a stroke with a whip.<BR>E.<BR>कषा and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाय|कषायः
कषाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Astringent.<BR>2 Fragrant.<BR>3 Red, dull red.<BR>4 Brown, of a colour composed of red and yellow.<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>1 An astringent flavour or taste.<BR>2 A decoction or infusion.<BR>3 Gum, resin, extract, exudation from a tree, &c.<BR>4 Plastering, anointing.<BR>5 Colouring or perfuming the person.<BR>6 Attachment to worldly objects.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>2 Passion, emotion.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, a small sort of Hedysarum.<BR>E.<BR>कष to injure, आय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायकृत्
कषायकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>Red. Lodh, a tree the bark of which is used in dyeing.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय red, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायचित्र
कषायचित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Dyed or stained of a dull red colour.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय, and चित्र painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायन्वित
कषायन्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Astringent, harsh.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायित
कषायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Prepared for dyeing or colouring.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय nominal verb, to astringe, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायिन्
कषायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Yielding a resinous exudation.<BR>2 Astringent.<BR>3 Dyed of a red colour.<BR>4 Worldly minded.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>The Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषि|कषिः
कषि<BR>mfn. (-षिः-षिः-षि)<BR>Injurious, mischievous.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषिका
कषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, and इकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषित
कषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hurt, injured.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषेरुका
कषेरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The back bone, the spine: see कशेरुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्ट|कष्टं|कष्टः
कष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Pained, suffering pain.<BR>2 Impervious, impenetrable.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Bodily pain or uneasiness.<BR>ind. (-ष्टं)<BR>An exclamation of regret or sorrow, ah, alas!<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, participial affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टकर
कष्टकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Giving pain or trouble.<BR>E.<BR>कष्ट, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टकारक|कष्टकारकः
कष्टकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Causing trouble or annoyance.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The world.<BR>E.<BR>कष्ट pain, and कारक the maker, the cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टश्रित
कष्टश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suffering pain or misfortune, undergoing hardships, performing penance.<BR>E.<BR>कष्ट and श्रित subjected to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टस्थान|कष्टस्थानं
कष्टस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bad or disagreeable place or site.<BR>E.<BR>कष्ट, and स्थान place, situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टि|कष्टिः
कष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Test, trial.<BR>2 Pain, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>कष to hurt, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस|कसः
कस<BR>r. 1st cl. (कसति)<BR>To move, to go or approach:<BR>with वि prefixed,<BR>to open or expand as a flower, to blow.<BR>(इ) कसि r. 2nd cl. (कंस्ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To command.<BR>3 To destroy: this root is also read by some authorities, कस (कस्ते) or कशि (कंष्टे.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस|कसः
कस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A touchstone: see कष.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A whip: see कशा and कषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसनोत्पाटन|कसनोत्पाटनः
कसनोत्पाटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, (Justicia, &c.) see वासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसिपु|कसिपुः
कसिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>Food, boiled rice: see कशिपु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरु|कसेरुः
कसेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A sort of grass: see कशेरु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुका
कसेरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of grass.<BR>2 The back bone: see कशेरुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तीर|कस्तीरं
कस्तीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>कस् to go, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तुरिका
कस्तुरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Musk; also कस्तूरी and कस्तूरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरीमल्लिका
कस्तूरी-मल्लिका^1<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The musk bag.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20250526. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिका
कस्तूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See कस्तूरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिकाण्डज
कस्तूरिकाण्डज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरी
कस्तूरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Musk, the animal perfume so called, as brought from Kashmir, Napal, and western Asam or Butan, the latter is said to be the best.<BR>2 A plant, (Hibiscus abelmoschus.)<BR>3 Another plant, (Amaryllis zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>कस to go, and तूरच् affix; its scent going or spreading; the deriv. is irr.; also कन् being added, कस्तूरिका and कस्तुरिका as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्मल|कस्मलं
कस्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Fainting, syncope.<BR>2 Sin: see कश्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्वर
कस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what goes or moves.<BR>E.<BR>कस to go, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हार|कल्हारं
कल्हार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The white esculent water lily, (Nymphaea lotus.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, हार a necklace or ornament, and ल irregularly inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्व|कह्वः
कह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, ह्वेञ् to call, &c. ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांसीय|कांसीयं
कांसीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>White copper: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्य|कांस्यं|कांस्यः
कांस्य<BR>mn. (-स्यः-स्यं)<BR>A goblet, a drinking vessel.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 White copper or brass, queen's-metal, any amalgam of zinc and copper.<BR>2 A musical instrument, a sort of gong or plate of bell-metal struck with a stick or rod.<BR>3 A measure: see कंस, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कसि to injure, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यक|कांस्यकं
कांस्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यकार|कांस्यकारः
कांस्यकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A brazier, a pewterer, a worker in white or bell-metal.<BR>E.<BR>कांस्य, and कार a workman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यनील|कांस्यनीलः
कांस्यनील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Blue vitriol considered as a collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>कांस्य bell-metal, and नील blue or black; also written occasionally कांश्यनील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक|काकं|काकः
काक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 A plant, (Ardisia solanacea?)<BR>3 A lame man, a cripple, one whose legs are wanting or useless.<BR>4 One of the divisions of the world or Dvīpas.<BR>5 A measure.<BR>6 Washing the head, bathing by dipping the head only into the water.<BR>7 A sectarial mark, the Tilaka?<BR>8 Shameless, arrogant.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Modus coeundi.<BR>2 A multitude or assemblage of crows.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An appellation of several plants, as,<BR>1 The common Bakapuṣpa: see वक.<BR>2 Kakjhangi, (Leea hirta); also in this sense काकी;<BR>3 A medicinal plant, vulg. Kākoli;<BR>4 The Ratti or Gunja, (Abrus precatorius);<BR>5 Opposite leaved fig tree: see उडुम्बर;<BR>6 A potherb, (Solanum Indicum, &c.) see काकमाची.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, Uṇādi affix कन्; or क for कु bad, ill, and अक to go, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काककङ्गु|काककङ्गुः
काककङ्गु<BR>f. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>A kind of panick, (P. miliaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and कङ्ग another species of the same grass; the Kaṅgu of the crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=205" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काककला
काककला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Leea hirta): see काकजङ्घा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकघ्नी
काकघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A tree, said to be a large kind of Karanja, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and घ्नी what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्चा|काकचिंचा
काकचिञ्चा<BR>f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>The shrub which yields the red and black berry, used in India as a jeweller's weight, (Abrus precatorius): see गुञ्जा.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and चिञ्चा extremity; the point being as black as a crow; also काकचिञ्चि and काकचिञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्चि|काकचिञ्चिः
काकचिञ्चि<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकचिञ्ची
काकचिञ्ची<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>See काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकछद|काकच्छद|काकच्छदः
काकछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A wagtail.<BR>2 Side locks of the head of hair.<BR>E.<BR>काक a crow, and छद plumage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकछर्द्दि|काकच्छर्दि|काकच्छर्द्दि
काकछर्द्दि<BR>m. (-र्द्दिः)<BR>1 A wagtail.<BR>2 What is ejected by a crow.<BR>E.<BR>काक and छर्द्दि vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकजङ्घा|काकजंघा
काकजङ्घा<BR>f. (-ङ्घा)<BR>A plant, (Leea hirta, Rox. Catalogue; elsewhere described as Leea aequata.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and जङ्गा a thigh; compared to a crow's leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकजम्बु|काकजम्बुः
काकजम्बु<BR>f. (-म्बुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bhuinjamb, (Ardisia solanacea): see भूमिजम्बु; also काकजम्बू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकण|काकणं
काकण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A leprosy with black and red spots, considered incurable.<BR>E.<BR>काक the Gunja berry, deriv. irr. also with कन्, affix काकणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणन्तिका
काकणन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Abrus precatorius: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकता
काकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The state or nature of a crow.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and तल् affix; also काकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीय
काकतालीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Accidental, unexpected, opportune.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and ताली the fruit of the palm: it alludes to a story of the fruit of the palm falling in the way of a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालीयवत्
काकतालीयवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Suddenly, opportunely.<BR>E.<BR>काकतालीय, and वत् like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतालुकिन्
काकतालुकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Contemptible, vile.<BR>E.<BR>काक, तालु palate, कन् affix of similitude, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतिक्ता
काकतिक्ता<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>The Gunja plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतिन्दुक|काकतिन्दुकः
काकतिन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and तिन्दुक ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतुण्ड|काकतुण्डः
काकतुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A dark sort of Agallochum: see कालागुरु.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 The Gunja plant.<BR>2 A sort of brass.<BR>3 A tree, commonly Kuwa dorī.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and तुण्ड face; of the colour of a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकतुण्डिका
काकतुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Gunja plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकध्वज|काकध्वजः
काकध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Submarine fire, a personage in Hindu mythology: see और्व्व.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and ध्वज a banner, whose symbol is a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनाशा
काकनाशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A plant, commonly Vakapushpa: see वकपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनासा
काकनासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A plant: see काकजङ्गा; also काकनासिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकनासिका
काकनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Leea hirta.)<BR>2 Red Tëori.<BR>E.<BR>काक a crow, and नासिका a nose; the root being fancifully compared to the beak of the bird; also काकनासा and काकनासिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकन्दी
काकन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>Emblick myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपक्ष|काकपक्षः
काकपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The side locks of the head of hair; three or five on each side left when the head is first shaved, and which may be allowed to remain, especially in persons of the military cast.<BR>E.<BR>काक and पक्ष a feather, a wing, a crow's wing; the word is also used as an epithet of a warrior, a name of RĀMA, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपीलु|काकपीलुः
काकपीलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A kind of ebony: see काकतिन्दुक; also with कन् added काकपीलुकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपुच्छ|काकपुच्छः
काकपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and पुच्छ a tail; crow-tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकपुष्ट|काकपुष्टः
काकपुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The Koil or Kokil, as before.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and पुष्ट nourished; this bird, like the English cuckoo, being said to leave its eggs in the nests of other birds, as in that of the crow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकफल|काकफलः
काकफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Nimb tree.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकबन्ध्या
काकबन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>A woman that bears only one child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकभीरु|काकभीरुः
काकभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>An owl. काक, and भीरु fearful; afraid of the crows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमद्गु|काकमद्गुः
काकमद्गु<BR>m. (-द्गुः)<BR>A water hen, a gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and मद्गु another kind of bird, a Shag; resembling a crow in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमर्द्द|काकमर्द|काकमर्दः|काकमर्द्दः
काकमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>The colocynth or bitter apple.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and मर्द्दक destroying; the fruit of which destroys crows; also काकमर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमाचिका
काकमाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see the next word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमाची
काकमाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>An esculent vegetable, commonly Gūrkamai, (Solanum Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, मच to respect, &c. अण् and ङीष् affixes; also with कन् and टाप् added, काकमाचिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकमुद्गा
काकमुद्गा<BR>f. (-द्गा)<BR>A plant, commonly Mugani, according to some, a wild kind of bean.<BR>E.<BR>काक and मुद्ग Moong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकयव|काकयवः
काकयव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Barren corn, the ear of which has no grain.<BR>E.<BR>काक and यव barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Naked.<BR>2 Timid, fearful.<BR>2 Poor, indigent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Fraud, deceit.<BR>2 An owl.<BR>3 A henpecked husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुहा
काकरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A parasite plant, (Epidendrum tesseloides, &c.) see वन्दा.<BR>E.<BR>काक and रुह what mounts; on which crows rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकल|काकलं|काकलः
काकल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A jewel worn upon the neck.<BR>f. (-लिः or -ली)<BR>A low and sweet tone, the song of a bird, &c.<BR>E.<BR>का instead of कु diminutive, कल to sound, इन् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलक|काकलकः
काकलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ornament of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीद्राक्षा
काकलीद्राक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A grape with a very small stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीरव|काकलीरवः
काकलीरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Kokila.<BR>E.<BR>काकली a sweet tone, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकशब्द
काकशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>The cawing of a crow.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकशीर्ष|काकशीर्षः
काकशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A tree, commonly Vakapushpa: (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and शीर्ष a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकस्त्री
काकस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाङ्गा
काकाङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A plant, (Leea aequata.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and अङ्ग form, body, टाप् affix; or with ङीष् affix, काकाङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाङ्गी
काकाङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाञ्ची
काकाञ्ची<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>1 A plant, (Leea aequata.)<BR>2 An esculent vegetable, (Solanum Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, अञ्च to go, अच् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकादनी
काकादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Gunja plant: see काकचिञ्चा.<BR>E.<BR>काक, अदन food, ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकार
काकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Scattering water.<BR>E.<BR>क water, क, to scatter; with आङ् prefixed, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकारि|काकारिः
काकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An own.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and अरि a foe; whose enemy is the crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=206" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकाल|काकालः
काकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and अल to be able, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणी
काकिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A cubit, the fourth part of a Daṇḍa or short pole.<BR>2 The quarter of a Paṇa, a weight, or a tale of shells equal to twenty Cowries.<BR>3 A quarter of a Māṣa, a weight of silver or gold.<BR>4 A Ratti or small seed used as a weight.<BR>5 A Cowri or shell used as a coin.<BR>E.<BR>कक to be unsteady, ल्युट् and ङीप् affixes; deriv. irr; also the dental न being substituted, काकिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिनी
काकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिल|काकिलः
काकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The central jewel in a necklace, &c. see काकल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकु|काकुः
काकु<BR>f. (-कुः)<BR>1 Change of voice in fear, grief, &c.<BR>2 Muttering, murmuring.<BR>3 The tongue.<BR>E.<BR>कक to deride, उण् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थ|काकुत्स्थः
काकुत्स्थ<BR>m. (-त्स्थः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>2 The name of a sovereign, also Purañjaya.<BR>E.<BR>ककुट् preeminent, अण् affix, and स्थ who stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुद|काकुदं
काकुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The palate.<BR>E.<BR>ककुद् the head, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकेक्षु|काकेक्षुः
काकेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>काक, and इक्षु sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकेन्दु|काकेन्दुः
काकेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A species of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोचिक|काकोचिकः
काकोचिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of fish, commonly Caouchi; also काकोचि. (Cyprinus cachius, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोडुम्बर|काकोडुम्बरः
काकोडुम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Opposite leaved fig tree, (Ficus oppositifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोडुम्बरिका
काकोडुम्बरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>काक, and उडुम्बर glomerous fig, कन् affix, and the feminine termination; also काकोदुम्बरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोदर|काकोदरः
काकोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>काक going ill or tortuously, (derived from का for कु, and अक to go,) and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोल|काकोलं|काकोलः
काकोल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A poisonous substance of a black colour, or the colour of a raven, whence its name; possibly the berry of the Cocculus Indicus.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A division of the infernal regions or hell.<BR>(-लः)<BR>1 A raven.<BR>2 A potter.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>4 A boar.<BR>5 A drug; as follows.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The name of a vegetable substance used in medicine, described as sweet and cooling, allaying fever, removing phlegm, &c.; it is said to be a root brought from Nepal or Morung.<BR>E.<BR>काक to be unsteady, &c. and ओलच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोलूकिका
काकोलूकिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The natural enmity of the owl and crow.<BR>E.<BR>काक a crow, उलूक an owl, वुन् affix, implying enmity in this and similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्ष|काक्षः
काक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) काक्षि (कांक्षति)<BR>To desire; it is most frequently used with आङ् prefixed, in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्ष|काक्षः
काक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Frowning, looking scornfully or in displeasure.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A glance, a wink or leer.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A frown, a look of displeasure.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु diminutive, or depreciative, and अक्षि the eye.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>1 A sort of trefoil, (Cytisus cajan.)<BR>2 A perfume, a fragrant kind of earth.<BR>E.<BR>कक्ष a creeping plant, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षीव|काक्षीवः
काक्षीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant, (Morunga hyperanthera, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु diminutive, and क्षीव to be intoxicated: see अक्षीव; also with कन् added काक्षीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काग|कागः
काग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A crow: (in the dialects, a raven.)<BR>E.<BR>का an imitative sound, and ग who sings, from गै with ड or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षत्
काङ्क्षत्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षन्-ङ्क्ष-न्ती-ङ्क्षत्)<BR>Wishing, desiring, hoping.<BR>E.<BR>काक्षि to desire, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षा|कांक्षा
काङ्क्षा<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षा)<BR>Wish, inclination, desire.<BR>E.<BR>काक्षि to wish, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षित|कांक्षित
काङ्क्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>काक्षि to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्क्षोरु|कांक्षोरुः|काङ्क्षोरुः
काङ्क्षोरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काङ्गा
काङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Orris root.<BR>E.<BR>का bad, crooked, and अङ्ग body, shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) काचि (काचते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काच|काचं|काचः
काच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 Alkaline ashes, any salt of potash or soda in a glassy or crystalline state.<BR>2 Crystal, quartz or glass, considered as a natural production, and used as a jewel or ornament.<BR>3 A loop, a swinging shelf, a string so contrived as to hold or support burthens, &c. A disease of the eyes, affection of the optic nerve or gutta serena.<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Alkaline salt, black salt.<BR>2 Wax.<BR>E.<BR>कच to shine or bind, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचक|काचकः
काचक<BR>(-कः)<BR>1 A stone.<BR>2 Alkaline ashes, &c. see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचकूपी
काचकूपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A glass bottle.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and कूपी bottle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचघटी
काचघटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A glass ewer.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and घटी a small jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An enclosure, a string or tape which ties a parcel or bundle or papers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कच to tie, ल्युट् affix; also with कन् added काचनक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन<BR>ind.<BR>Some one, any one, (applied to feminine objects,) the first member is declinable.<BR>E.<BR>का fem. of किम, चन added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनक|काचनकं
काचनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A binding or rope for binding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to काचन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनकिन्
काचनकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A writing, a written paper.<BR>E.<BR>काचनक a binding, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचभाजन|काचभाजनं
काचभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A vessel of glass or crystal, a cup, a goblet, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमणि|काचमणिः
काचमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Crystal, quartz.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचमल|काचमलं
काचमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Black salt or soda: see काचलवण.<BR>E.<BR>काच glass, and मल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचलवण|काचलवणं
काचलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Black salt, a medicinal salt, prepared by calcining fossile salt and the fruit of the emblic myrobalan together. It consists chiefly or muriate of soda, with a small quantity of iron, lime and sulphur, and is a tonic aperient.<BR>E.<BR>काच alkaline ashes, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचवकयन्त्र
काचवकयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A glass retort.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and वकयन्त्र a retort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचसम्भव|काचसंभव|काचसम्भवं
काचसम्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Black salt: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचसौवर्च्चल|काचसौवर्चल|काचसौवर्चलं
काचसौवर्च्चल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Black salt: see काचलवण.<BR>E.<BR>काच, and सौवर्च्चल salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचस्थाली
काचस्थाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>काच glass, and स्थाली a goblet, &c. to which its colour is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिघ|काचिघः
काचिघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A legume.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>3 Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित्
काचित्<BR>ind.<BR>Some one, any one, (a female person or object,) the first member is declinable, as काञ्चित्, &c.<BR>E.<BR>का fem. of किम् and चित् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित|काचितं
काचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suspended by a swing or in a loop.<BR>E.<BR>काच a nominal root, to hang by a loop or in a swing, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=207" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिम|काचिमः
काचिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree considered as sacred, one growing near a temple, and an object or religious veneration or worship, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चन|कांचन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
काञ्चन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Golden, of gold.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 A filament of the lotus.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR>2 A tree bearing a yellow fragrant flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>3 Another plant, (Mesua ferrea): see नागकेसर.<BR>4 Glomerous fig tree: see उदुम्बर.<BR>5 Common thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>2 A yellow pigment.<BR>E.<BR>कचि to shine, &c. ल्युट् affix, the radical vowel lengthened; this etymology gives the meaning gold, the others refer to their colour, &c. in which they resemble the metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनक|काञ्चनकं|कांचनकः|काञ्चनकः
काञ्चनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Mountain ebony, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन gold, &c. and कन् affix, implying resemblance or identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनकन्दर|कांचनकंदर|काञ्चनकन्दरः
काञ्चनकन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A gold mine.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and कन्दर a cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनकारिणी
काञ्चनकारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus): see शतमूली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनगिरि|कांचनगिरि|काञ्चनगिरिः
काञ्चनगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Mount Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>काच्चन, and गिरि a mountain; the golden mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनचय
काञ्चनचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A heap of gold.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and चय assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनभू|कांचनभू
काञ्चनभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>1 Gold dust.<BR>2 A golden or yellow soil.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and भू soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनमय
काञ्चनमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Golden.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनवप्र
काञ्चनवप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>A hill or mound of gold.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and वप्र a mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनसन्धि|काञ्चनसंधि|कांचनसंधि|काञ्चनसन्धिः
काञ्चनसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>A treaty of friendship between two parties on equal terms.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन, and सन्धि alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनाल|कांचनाल|कांचनालः|काञ्चनालः
काञ्चनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>काञ्चन gold, and अल to be able or like; some copies read काञ्चनार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चनीया
काञ्चनीया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A yellow pigment, commonly Gorocanā.<BR>E.<BR>काचि to shine, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चि|कांचि|कांचिः|काञ्चिः
काञ्चि<BR>f. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>See काञ्ची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चिक|कांचिकं|काञ्चिकं
काञ्चिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sour gruel: see काञ्जिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्ची|कांची
काञ्ची<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>1 A woman's zone or girdle.<BR>2 The name of an ancient city situated in the peninsula, and one of the seven sacred cities of the Hindus.<BR>3 A plant, (Abrus precatorious): see गुञ्चा.<BR>E.<BR>काचि to bind or shine, इन or ङीष् affixes; whence also काञ्चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्चीपद|कांचीपद|काञ्चीपदं
काञ्चीपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Mons veneris, the pubic region.<BR>E.<BR>काञ्ची the zone, and पद place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काञ्जिक|कांजिक|कांजिकं|काञ्जिकं
काञ्जिक<BR>nf. (-कः-का)<BR>Sour gruel, the water of boiled rice in a state of spontaneous fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>क water, अञ्ज to go, &c. and affix इक; also the vowel being lengthened काञ्जीक, or without the final, काञ्जी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठ|काठः
काठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A stone, a rock.<BR>E.<BR>कठ to be hard, &c. अण् affix; also with कन् added, काठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठक
काठक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>According to the Kaṭha portion of the vedas.<BR>E.<BR>कठ, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन|काठिनं|काठिनः
काठिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The date fruit.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Hardness.<BR>2 Sternness.<BR>E.<BR>कठिन and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काठिन्य|काठिन्यं
काठिन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Hardness.<BR>2 Difficulty, obscurity.<BR>3 Sternness, severity.<BR>E.<BR>कठिन hard, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण|काणः
काण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>One-eyed, monoculous.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणूक|काणूकः
काणूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, &c. and ऊकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेय|काणेयः
काणेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>काण, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काणेर|काणेरः
काणेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>One-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>काण, and द्रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्ड|कांड|कांडं|काण्डं|कांडः|काण्डः
काण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 A stalk or stem.<BR>2 The part of the trunk of a tree whence the branches proceed.<BR>3 A cluster, a clump.<BR>4 An arrow.<BR>5 Opportunity, season.<BR>6 Water.<BR>7 A kind of reed, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>8 A multitude, a heap, a quantity.<BR>9 A horse.<BR>10 A chapter, a section.<BR>11 The part in a sacrifice appropriated to different objects, as the gods or manes.<BR>12 A long bone, a bone of the extremities.<BR>13 Praise, flattery.<BR>14 Private, privacy.<BR>15 Low, vile, bad.<BR>16 Sinful, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>कन to shine, &c. डः Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डकाण्डक|काण्डकाण्डकः
काण्डकाण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of grass.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डकार|कांडकार|काण्डकारं|काण्डकारः
काण्डकार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The betle nut, the fruit of the areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डगोचर|कांडगोचर|काण्डगोचरः
काण्डगोचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड a stem or stalk, and गोचर an object of sense: it is fired from a stock like the arrow of the cross bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डणी
काण्डणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, commonly Rāmadūtī: see सूक्ष्मपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डतिक्तक|काण्डतिक्तकः
काण्डतिक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड the stem, and तिक्त sharp, bitter, कन् added to this and similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डनील|काण्डनीलः
काण्डनील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant with an astringent bark, commonly Lodh.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपट|कांडपट|काण्डपटः
काण्डपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An outer tent, a screen surrounding a tent.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड a stem, &c. and पट a cloth; also with कन् added काण्डपटकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपुष्प|काण्डपुष्पं
काण्डपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पः)<BR>A small fragrant flower, commonly Dona, (Artemisia.)<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड the stem, and पुष्प flower; flowering from the stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डपृष्ठ|कांडपृष्ठ|काण्डपृष्ठं|काण्डपृष्ठः
काण्डपृष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Of the military profession, a soldier.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 The husband of a Vaiśya female.<BR>2 An adopted or any other than the natural son.<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>The bow of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड an arrow, and पृष्ठ the back: see काण्डस्पृष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डभग्न
काण्डभग्न<BR>n. (-ग्नं)<BR>A fracture of either of the extremities.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड, and भग्न breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डरुहा
काण्डरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड the stem of a tree, and रुहा what ascends; hence it appears to be a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डर्षि|काण्डर्षिः
काण्डर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi or divine saint of a peculiar class; Jaimini and others who teach a particular Kāṇḍa or section of Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड a section, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डवत्|कांडवत्|काण्डवन्त्
काण्डवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Armed with an arrow, an archer.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड an arrow, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डसन्धि|कांडसंधि|काण्डसंधि|काण्डसन्धिः
काण्डसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>A knot, a joint in the stem of a tree, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड a stem, and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डस्पृष्ट|कांडस्पृष्ट|काण्डस्पृष्टः
काण्डस्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Of the military profession, living by arms, a soldier.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड an arrow, &c. स्पृश to touch, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डहीन|काण्डहीनं
काण्डहीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fragrant grass, a sort of cyperus: see भद्रमुस्तक.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड a stem, and हीन deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डीर|कांडीर|कांडीरः|काण्डीरः
काण्डीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Armed with an arrow, an archer.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A creeping plant, commonly Kāṇḍa Bel, (Momordica charantia.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">Page209</a>]<BR>2 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith): see मञ्जिष्ठा.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड an arrow, a stem, &c. and ईरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=208" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काण्डेक्षु|काण्डेक्षुः
काण्डेक्षु<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>1 A plant, (Barleria longifolia.)<BR>2 A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum): see काश.<BR>E.<BR>काण्ड, and ईक्षु sugar cane; having a similar stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातर|कातरः
कातर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Confused, perplexed, disordered.<BR>2 Timid, gentle.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large kind of fish, commonly Kātala, (Cyprinus catla, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>का a little or badly, and तर what crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातरता
कातरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Timidity, agitation.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to कातर; also with त्व, कातरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातल|कातलः
कातल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a fish, commonly Kātala, (Cyprinus catla, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>see कातर, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कातीय|कातीयः
कातीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name of KĀTYĀYANA.<BR>2 A pupil of the same.<BR>E.<BR>कात्यायन with फक् affix and the middle syllable dropped; also कात्यायनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्त्रयक
कात्त्रयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Produced from any bad triad.<BR>E.<BR>कत्त्रय, and ढकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्य|कात्यः
कात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>The name of a saint; also कात्यायन.<BR>E.<BR>कत a proper name, and यञ् affix implying descent or lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायन|कात्यायनः
कात्यायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The name of a celebrated lawgiver and divine sage.<BR>2 An appellation of VARARUCI a poet.<BR>E.<BR>कात्य, and फक् pleonastic affix.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A middle-aged widow.<BR>E.<BR>ङीष् added to कात्यायन; the daughter of the saint KĀTYĀYANA, (DURGĀ,) or resembling the wife of a sage in dress and austerity, (the widow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कात्यायनीय|कात्यायनीयः
कात्यायनीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A pupil of KĀTYĀYANA.<BR>E.<BR>कात्यायन, and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काथिक|काथिकः
काथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a story, told in it, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A narrator.<BR>E.<BR>कथा and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्ब|कादंब|कादंबः|कादम्बः
कादम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>1 A tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>2 A drake, or, according to some, a teal.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī: see कदम्बपुष्प.<BR>E.<BR>अण् added to कदम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बक|कादंबकः|कादम्बकः
कादम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर|कादंबर|कादंबरं|कादम्बरं|कादम्बरः
कादम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The surface or skim of coagulated milk.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the Kadamba.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Wine, spirituous liquor in general.<BR>2 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>3 The female Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR>4 The female of another bird, (Turdus salica, BUC.)<BR>E.<BR>कदम्ब the Kadamba flower, र what gains or gets, from रा, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बरीवीज|कादम्बरीवीजं
कादम्बरीवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Ferment, yeast, whatever occasions fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>कादम्बरी, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बर्य्य|कादम्बर्य|कादम्बर्य्यः
कादम्बर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The Kādamba tree: see कादम्ब.<BR>E.<BR>कादम्बरी a spirit, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादम्बिनी|कादंबिनी
कादम्बिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A long line of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>कादम्ब the Kādamba flower, इनि and ङीप्^1 affixes, implying a multitude; the clouds being compared he large white flowers of the Nauclea cadamba.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कादाचित्क|कादाचित्कं
कादाचित्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्की-त्कं)<BR>Produced sometimes, occasional, incidental.<BR>E.<BR>कदाचित् sometimes, with कन् added, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काद्रवेय|काद्रवेयः
काद्रवेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Nāga or serpent of the race that is supposed to people the lower regions.<BR>E.<BR>कद्रु the mother of these beings, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानक|कानकं
कानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The seed of the croton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानन|काननं
कानन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>1 A forest, a grove.<BR>2 The face of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 A house.<BR>E.<BR>कनि to shine, in the causal form, and ल्युट् affix, or क BRAHMĀ, and आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काननारि|काननारिः
काननारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The Śami or Śain tree, (Mimosa albida): see समी.<BR>E.<BR>कानन, and अरि enemy; injurious to a wood; being a thorny tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कानीन|कानीनः
कानीन<BR>mf. (-नः-नी)<BR>The son or daughter of a young and unmarried woman.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VYĀSA.<BR>2 Also of KARṆA, (being both born of mothers who were unmarried.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्या a virgin or young girl, changed to कनीन् and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्त|कांत|कान्तं|कान्तः
कान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>2 Lovely, beautiful.<BR>3 Dear, beloved.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A husband.<BR>4 Spring.<BR>5 A precious stone; in which case it is compounded with सूर्य्य, चन्द्र or अयस्, as सूर्य्यकान्त a crystal lens, &c.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A wife, a mistress, any beloved or lovely woman.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Priyangu: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>3 A grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तता
कान्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Loveliness, beauty, splendor.<BR>E.<BR>कान्त pleasing, &c. तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपक्षिन्|कांतपक्षिन्
कान्तपक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>कान्त beautiful, पक्षिन् a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तपुष्प|कान्तपुष्पः
कान्तपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Mountain ebony, &c. (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>E.<BR>कान्त, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तलक|कान्तलकः
कान्तलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, the wood of which something resembles mahogany, commonly Toon, (Cedrela tunna, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कान्त, beauty, and र what gives, कन् added, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद|कांतांघ्रिदोहद|कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहदः
कान्ताङ्घ्रिदोहद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A tree, commonly Aśoka, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>E.<BR>कान्ता a woman, अङ्ग्नि a foot, and दोहद desire; the tree being supposed to blossom upon coming in contact with the foot of a handsome female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ताचरणदोहद|कान्ताचरणदोहदः
कान्ताचरणदोहद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The tree Aśoka: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तायस|कांतायस|कान्तायसं
कान्तायस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Iron stone: see अयस्कान्त.<BR>E.<BR>कान्त, and अयस् iron, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तार|कांतार|कांतारं|कान्तारं|कांतारः|कान्तारः
कान्तार<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 A bad or difficult road.<BR>2 A wood, a forest.<BR>3 A hole, a cavity.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A red variety of the sugar cane.<BR>2 A bamboo.<BR>3 Mountain ebony.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A symptom or symptomatic disease.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>कान् for कञ्चित् any one, here meaning no one, तृ to go, in the causal form, अच् affix; allowing none to pass; or क pleasure, &c. अन्त end, and ऋ to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारक|कांतारकः|कान्तारकः
कान्तारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>कान्त good, excellent, (juice,) ऋ to go, to gain, अण् and कन् affixes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तारग
कान्तारग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Who or what goes into or in a wood.<BR>E.<BR>कान्तार, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्ति|कांति|कांतिः|कान्तिः
कान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Beauty, splendor, light.<BR>2 Female beauty.<BR>3 Wish, desire.<BR>4 A lovely or desirable woman.<BR>5 Personal decoration or embellishment.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire or be desired, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिकर|कांतिकर
कान्तिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Beautifying, illumining, making handsome or splendid.<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिद|कांतिद|कान्तिदं
कान्तिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Beautifying, illuminating.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति light, splendor, &c. and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=209" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिदायक|कांतिदायक|कान्तिदायकं
कान्तिदायक<BR>mfn. (-यकः-यिका-यकं)<BR>Beautifying, adorning.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of Curcuma, from the root of which a yellow die is pared, (C. Zanthorhiza.)<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति beauty, &c. दायक distributor, giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिभृत्|कांतिभृत्
कान्तिभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>1 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>2 Bright, shining.<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति, and भृत् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिमत्|कांतिमत्|कान्तिमन्त्
कान्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Splendid.<BR>2 Beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्तिहर
कान्तिहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Dimming, dulling, making dull or ugly.<BR>E.<BR>कान्ति, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दव|कांदव|कांदवं
कान्दव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Roasted or baked, (in an iron pan or oven, as bread, cakes, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्दु and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दविक|कांदविक|कांदविकः|कान्दविकः
कान्दविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A baker.<BR>E.<BR>कान्दव baked bread, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्दिशीक|कांदिशीक|कान्दिशीकः
कान्दिशीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Flying, running away, put to flight.<BR>E.<BR>कदि to fear, घञ् and इन् affixed, कन्दि; शीक to go, to ooze, घञ् affix, कन्दिशीक; and again, अण् affix, कान्दिशीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यकुञ्ज
कान्यकुञ्ज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A country, the modern Kanouj; also कन्यकुब्ज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कान्यजा
कान्यजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Nali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापटिक|कापटिकः
कापटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Wicked, bad, perverse.<BR>2 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A student, a scholar.<BR>2 A flatterer, a parasite.<BR>E.<BR>कपट fraud, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापट्य|कापट्यं
कापट्य<BR>n. (-ट्यं)<BR>Wickedness, fraud, dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>कपट, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापथ|कापथः
कापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A bad road.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु bad, vile, and पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापाल|कापालं|कापालः
कापाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Cranial, relating to the skull.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापालिक|कापालिकः
कापालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the skull.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A worshipper of ŚIVA of the left-hand order, characterised by carrying a half of the skull as a cup, drinking spirituous liquors, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कपाल, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिल|कापिलः
कापिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Of a tawny colour.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A follower of the Sāṃkhya system of philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>कपिल the founder of the school, and अण् affix.<BR>2 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonastic, added to कपिल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिश|कापिशं
कापिश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A spirituous liquor, wine.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A country.<BR>E.<BR>कपिश brown, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशायन|कापिशायनं
कापिशायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A kind of vinous liquor.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Honey.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>कपिश brown, or कापिशी a country, and ष्फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापिशेय|कापिशेयः
कापिशेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Piśāca, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>कपिश, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुष|कापुरुषः
कापुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A mean contemptible man, a coward, a wretch.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु bad, vile, पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापुरुषत्व
कापुरुषत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Meanness, cowardliness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the preceding: also with तल्, कापुरुषता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापेय|कापेयं|कापेयः
कापेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Belonging to or relating to a monkey.<BR>E.<BR>कपि a monkey, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोत|कापोतं|कापोतः
कापोत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Of a dirty white colour.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Natron, fossile alkali.<BR>2 Antimony, considered as a collyrium or application to the eyes.<BR>3 A pale or dirty white colour.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A flock of pigeons.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत a pigeon, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कापोताञ्जन|कापोतांजन|कापोताञ्जनं
कापोताञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Antimony, especially considered as a collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>कपोत a pigeon, and अञ्जन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकर|काप्यकरः
काप्यकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A penitent, one who acknowledges his faults.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु bad, आप्य having obtained, and कर who does; from कृ and अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काप्यकार|काप्यकारः
काप्यकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Avowal or confession of sin.<BR>2 A penitent, one who confesses a crime.<BR>E.<BR>as before, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काफल|काफलः
काफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bitter seed: see कट्फल.<BR>E.<BR>का bad, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम|कामं|कामः
काम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 KĀMA the Hindu Cupid or deity of love.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 BALARĀMA the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>4 The mango tree.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Love, desire.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 An object of desire.<BR>3 Willingly, voluntarily.<BR>4 A particle of assent or agreement: see कामम्.<BR>ind.<BR>(in composition,) Following one's own desire, as कामवाद speaking what one lists; कामभक्ष eating whatever one likes; कामचार doing whatever one chooses; in law, a child previous to the imposition of the characteristic cord is all these.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकला
कामकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>RATI the wife of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and कला a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकामिन्
कामकामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Following the dictates of passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and कामिन् desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकार|कामकारः
कामकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Following one's inclinations.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Desire, the operation or influence of desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and कार act, who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकारतस्
कामकारतस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to one's desires, following one's inclinations, indulging desire.<BR>E.<BR>कामकार and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकूट|कामकूटः
कामकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The paramour of a harlot, a cully.<BR>2 Wanton caresses, harlotry.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and कूट a peak or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामकेलि|कामकेलिः
कामकेलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Libidinous, wanton.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 Copulation.<BR>2 Amorous sport.<BR>E.<BR>काम love desire, केलि play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामग
कामग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Acting as one pleases.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगामिन्
कामगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going as one lists.<BR>E.<BR>काम the wish, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामगुण|कामगुणः
कामगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Passion, affection.<BR>2 An object of sense.<BR>3 Completion, satiety, perfect enjoyment.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and गुण a quality or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामङ्गामिन्|कामंगामिन्
कामङ्गामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going as one lists.<BR>E.<BR>कामं at will, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचार|कामचारः
कामचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Following one's own pleasure, unchecked, unrestrained.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Following one's own wishes or pleasure, sensuality, selfishness.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and चार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारतस्
कामचारतस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to one's own inclinations.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामचारिन्
कामचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Desirous, libidinous.<BR>2 Self-willed.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A sparrow. A name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and चारिन् who goes, from चर with णिनि affix; also with ण्वुल् affix, कामचारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामज|कामजः
कामज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced or caused by passion or desire.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and ज born; also कामजनित, कामोत्पन्न, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=210" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजान|कामजानः
कामजान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and जान what produces, from जन in the causal form, and घञ् affix; also read कामजनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामजाल
कामजाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See कामताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामठ
कामठ<BR>(-ठः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>कमठ the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामतस्
कामतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Willingly, consentingly.<BR>2 Passionately.<BR>E.<BR>काम and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामताल|कामतालः
कामताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Kokila, or Koïl, the Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and ताल a musical strain; the song of the Koïl being poetically considered as an incentive to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामद|कामदः
कामद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Giving what is wished, granting one's desires.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A fabulous cow, the cow of plenty.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुघा
कामदुघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>The cow of plenty.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and दुह to yield milk, affix कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदुह्
कामदुह्<BR>f. (-धुक्)<BR>1 The cow of plenty.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and दुह to give milk, क्विस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामदूती
कामदूती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 The female koïl.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and दूती a messenger; also कामदूति and कामदूतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामध्वंसिन्
कामध्वंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>काम CUPID, and ध्वंसिन् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन|कामनः
कामन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lustful, libidinous, desirous.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामन्धमिन्|कामंधमिन्
कामन्धमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A brazier.<BR>E.<BR>काम willingly, ध्मा to blow, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपत्नी
कामपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A name of RATI.<BR>E.<BR>काम KANDARPA, and पत्नी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामपाल|कामपालः
कामपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>काम KĀMA, and पाल who cherishes; being by one legend the paternal uncle of that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामप्रद|कामप्रदः
कामप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Granting what is desired.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and प्रद what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामबद्ध
कामबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound by love.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>A wood.<BR>E.<BR>काम and बद्ध tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभक्ष
कामभक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Eating any thing or every thing.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामभक्ष्य
कामभक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Eating any thing.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and भक्ष्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामम्
कामम्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle,<BR>1 Of reluctant assent, (well, very well.)<BR>2 Of assent, (willingly, readily.)<BR>3 Of agreement, (very well, so be it.)<BR>4 Of contempt or invidious remark.<BR>5 Agreeably to desire, following the inclination: see काम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममह|काममहः
काममह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>E.<BR>काम the deity, and मह worship; a festival in honour of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काममालिन्
काममालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामयितृ
कामयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, in the causal form, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूप|कामरूपः
कामरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>1 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>2 Taking any or every shape at will.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A district lying east of Bengal, the western portion of Asam.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and रूप form or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूपिन्
कामरूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>1 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>2 Taking any shape at will.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>1 A Vidyādhara, a kind of subordinate deity.<BR>2 A pole cat.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, will, रूप form, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरेखा
कामरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A harlot, a courtezan.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामल|कामलः
कामल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Libidinous, cupidinous.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A complaint, jaundice, excessive secretion or obstruction of bile.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Spring.<BR>2 A dry and sterile soil.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, ला to bring, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलता
कामलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Membrum virile.<BR>2 A plant, (Ipomaea quamoclit.)<BR>E.<BR>काम, and लता creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामलोल
कामलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Overcome with desire or passion.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and लोल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवल्लभ|कामवल्लभः
कामवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>2 Spring.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and वल्लभ friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवाद
कामवाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Saying any thing at pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामविहन्तृ|कामविहंतृ
कामविहन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Disappointing, preventing.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and विहन्तृ^1 who destroys.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृत्त
कामवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Licentious, dissipated, debauched.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and वृत्त practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृद्धि|कामवृद्धिः
कामवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 A shrub, commonly Kāmaja, of supposed aphrodisial properties.<BR>2 Increase of passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामवृन्ता
कामवृन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>काम, and वृन्ता a flower stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामशर|कामशरः
कामशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The shaft of KĀMADEVA.<BR>2 The mango.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and शर an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसंयोग|कामसंयोगः
कामसंयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Attainment of desired objects.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसख|कामसखः
कामसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 Spring.<BR>2 The mango.<BR>E.<BR>काम and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामसुत|कामसुतः
कामसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and सुत a son; also similar compounds, as कामपुत्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामहैतुक
कामहैतुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of one's own accord.<BR>E.<BR>काम, हेतु cause, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाग्नि|कामाग्निः
कामाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Passion, lust, violent desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्कुश|कामांकुश|कामाङ्कुशः
कामाङ्कुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A finger nail.<BR>2 Membrum virile.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अङ्कुश shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाङ्ग|कामांग|कामाङ्गः
कामाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अङ्ग the body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामातुर|कामातुरः
कामातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>In love, affected by love or desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आतुर diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मन्
कामात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>1 Licentious, libidinous.<BR>2 Desiring, wishing for.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामात्मता
कामात्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Passion, lust.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>कामात्म and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिष्ठित
कामाधिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Influenced or overcome by love.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अधिष्ठित placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामाधिकार|कामाधिकारः
कामाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The influence of passion or desire.<BR>2 The aspiration of the will.<BR>3 The part of the Śāstra which relates to human wishes or desires.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामानल|कामानलः
कामानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Passion, lust, violent desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामान्ध|कामांध|कामान्धः
कामान्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo. काम, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=211" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुध|कामायुधः
कामायुध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>An arrow of KĀMADEVA.<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Membrum virile.<BR>2 The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामायुस्
कामायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आयुस् life; existing at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारण्य|कामारण्यं
कामारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A handsome grove or wood.<BR>E.<BR>काम desirable, and अरण्य a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामारि|कामारिः
कामारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A mineral substance used in medicine, a sort of pyrites: see विटमाक्षिक.<BR>E.<BR>काम love, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामार्त्त|कामार्त|कामार्त्तः
कामार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>In love, afflicted by love or passion.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामालु|कामालुः
कामालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A red sort of mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसाय|कामावसायः
कामावसाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Coldness, stoicism, mortification or suppression of the passions.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अवसाय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायिता
कामावसायिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The power of suppressing desire, self-denial or mortification.<BR>E.<BR>कामावसायिन् and तल् affix, or with त्व, कामावसायित्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायितृ
कामावसायितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what suppresses or destroys passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and अवसायितृ destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामावसायिन्
कामावसायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Destructive of love or desire, one who suppresses desire, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कामावसाय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्त
कामासक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Impassioned, in love, overcome with desire or passion.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आसक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामासक्ति
कामासक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Passion, desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and आसक्ति attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामि|कामिः
कामि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A libidinous man, a lecher.<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>A name of RATI the wife of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, कि affix; the pen. becomes long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिक|कामिकः
कामिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of wild duck.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिता
कामिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Love, desire.<BR>E.<BR>कामिन् and तल् affix; also with त्व, कामित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिन्
कामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Impassioned, fond, loving, wanton.<BR>2 Cupidinous, desirous.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A lover, an uxorious husband.<BR>3 The ruddy goose.<BR>4 A pigeon.<BR>5 A sparrow.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A loving or affectionate woman.<BR>2 A timid woman.<BR>3 A woman in general.<BR>4 Spirituous liquor.<BR>5 A climbing plant.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामिनीश|कामिनीशः
कामिनीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A plant, (Morunga guilandina, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामील|कामीलः
कामील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of betel, commonly रामगुवाक.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, ईलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामुक|कामुकः
कामुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Cupidinous, desirous, lustful, libidinous.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, Aśoka, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>2 A creeping plant, (Gaertnera racemosa.)<BR>3 A sparrow.<BR>4 A bow.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman desirous of wealth, food, &c.<BR>(-की)<BR>A woman libidinous or lustful.<BR>E.<BR>कम to desire, उकञ् affix, fem. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदक|कामोदकं
कामोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Oblation of water to deceased friends, &c. exclusive of those for whom it is directed by law.<BR>E.<BR>काम will, and उदक water; being given according to the inclination of the giver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोदा
कामोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A Rāgiṇī, one of the female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामोपहत
कामोपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Overcome with passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम, and उपहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल|कांपिलः|काम्पिलः
काम्पिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A country believed to be situated in the north of India: see काम्पिल्ल, &c.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The capital city of that region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्य|काम्पिल्यः
काम्पिल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>1 A perfume, commonly Sunda Rocani.<BR>2 A country: see the preceding; also काम्पिल्ल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्ल|कांपिल्ल|कांपिल्लः|काम्पिल्लः
काम्पिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 Sunda Rocani, a perfume and drug so called.<BR>2 The name of a country said to be in the north-west of India.<BR>E.<BR>कपि to tremble or shake, इल्ल affix; also काम्पिल or काम्पील, काम्पिल्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पिल्लका
काम्पिल्लका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्पील|काम्पीलः
काम्पील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See काम्पिल and काम्पिल्ल; also काम्पीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बल|कांबल|कांबलः|काम्बलः
काम्बल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Clothed with a blanket, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A car covered with a woollen cloth or blanket.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बल a blanket, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बलिक|काम्बलिकः
काम्बलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Gruel, barley water, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बविक|कांबविक|कांबविकः|काम्बविकः
काम्बविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dealer in shells, a vender of ornaments made of them, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बु a shell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बुका
काम्बुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Physalis flexuosa): see अश्वगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्बोज|कांबोज|कांबोजः|काम्बोजः
काम्बोज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A native of Kāmboja, a foreign race going like the Yavanas, with the whole of the head shaved, one of the tribes originally Kṣatriya, but degraded by omission of the essential rites.<BR>2 A horse of the breed of Kamboya or Kamboja.<BR>3 A white mimosa.<BR>4 A tree, commonly Punnag, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Maṣāni: see माषपर्णी.<BR>2 A white mimosa, as above.<BR>3 The Gunja plant.<BR>E.<BR>कम्बोज Kamboja or Kamboya, a country in the north of India, अण and ङीष् affix: the plants, &c. being supposed indigenous to that district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्य|काम्यं
काम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Agreeable, desirable, amiable.<BR>2 Performed through the desire of some advantage, (a religious ceremony, &c.)<BR>2 Optional, supererogatory, performed for some particular object, and opposed to the नित्यकर्म्म or fixed and indispensable observance.<BR>4 Relating to desire, will, &c.<BR>5 Done through lust or passion.<BR>E.<BR>काम desire, love, &c. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यगिर्
काम्यगिर्<BR>f. (-गीः)<BR>A pleasing sound, an agreeable speech or song.<BR>E.<BR>काम्य, and गिर् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यत्व
काम्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Supererogation, will, pleasure.<BR>2 Love, desire.<BR>E.<BR>काम्य, and त्व affix; also with तल्, काम्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यदान|काम्यदानं
काम्यदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An acceptable or desirable gift.<BR>2 A voluntary gift.<BR>E.<BR>काम्य, and दान a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्यमरण
काम्यमरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Voluntary death, suicide.<BR>E.<BR>काम्य, and मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्याभिप्राय|काम्याभिप्रायः
काम्याभिप्राय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The purpose of deriving benefit from any act.<BR>E.<BR>काम्य, and अभिप्राय intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काम्ल
काम्ल<BR>mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं)<BR>Slightly acid, acidulous.<BR>E.<BR>का dimin. अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय|कायं|कायः
काय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>The body.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Part of the hand sacred to the creator; the root of the little finger.<BR>2 Clarified butter or any oblation to BRAHMĀ.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 One of the eight modes of marriage, the same as प्राजापत्य.<BR>2 Assemblage, collection.<BR>3 A butt or mark, an object to be hit or attained.<BR>4 Natural temperament of any thing or being.<BR>5 A house, a habitation.<BR>6 Principal, capital.<BR>E.<BR>क a name of BRAHMĀ, and अण् deriv. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">Page213</a>] affix, इ is added to क, and अय is substituted for the short vowel; proceeding from or relating to BRAHMĀ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=212" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक
कायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Belonging to the body.<BR>E.<BR>काय, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायक्लेश|कायक्लेशः
कायक्लेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Bodily suffering, toil or pain.<BR>E.<BR>काय, and क्लेश distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायचिकित्सा
कायचिकित्सा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Treatment of disease, administering medicines.<BR>E.<BR>काय, and चिकित्सा remedying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायबलन
कायबलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>काय the body, and बलन protecting; from बल to be strong, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायमान|कायमानं
कायमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A hut of grass or thatch.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायस्थ|कायस्थः
कायस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 The Supreme Being.<BR>2 A caste or tribe, or man of that tribe; the Kayeth or writer caste, proceeding from a Kṣatriya father and Śūdra mother.<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan: see हरीतकी.<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>3 A drug, commonly Kākoli.<BR>4 A woman of the Kayeth caste.<BR>(-स्थी)<BR>The wife of a Kayeth or scribe.<BR>E.<BR>काय the body or house, and स्थ who stays, or resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायाग्नि|कायाग्निः
कायाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The digestive faculty.<BR>E.<BR>काय, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिक|कायिकः
कायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Corporeal, relating to the body.<BR>E.<BR>काय the body, and कन् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कायिकाष्टद्धि
कायिकाष्टद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Interest arising from service drawn from the body of an animal, (as a cow, &c.) pledged; or according to some, interest of which the payment does not affect the principal.<BR>E.<BR>कायिका corporal, &c. वृद्धि interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार|कारः
कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what does any act, (but used chiefly in composition with other words); the agent, a maker or doer; as कुम्भकार a potter, a maker of earthen vessels. स्वर्णकार a goldsmith, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Act, action.<BR>2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>3 Certainty.<BR>4 Effort, exertion.<BR>5 Religious austerity.<BR>6 A heap of snow, or a mountain covered with it.<BR>7 Tax, toll, royal revenue.<BR>8 A master, a lord.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A prison.<BR>2 Binding, confinement.<BR>3 A female messenger.<BR>4 The part of a lute below the neck.<BR>5 A female worker in gold, (हेमकारिका?)<BR>6 Pain, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to make, to do, with घञ् or अण् affix, in the latter case the fem. affix is ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारक|कारकं|कारकः
कारक<BR>mfn. (-रकः-रिका-रकं)<BR>An agent, acting, doing, who or what does, acts, makes, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A noun of action.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Action, especially in grammar.<BR>2 That part of grammar comprising all nouns which imply the agent, object, instrument, &c. or any thing except the simple and radical idea; it also includes the use and government of the cases or syntax.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, and ण्वुल् affix of agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकर
कारकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Working, doing work, acting as agent.<BR>E.<BR>कार, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकहेतु|कारकहेतुः
कारकहेतु<BR>m.^1 (-तुः)<BR>Efficient or active cause.<BR>E.<BR>कारक what produces, हेतु cause.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260624. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारकुक्षीय|कारकुक्षीयः
कारकुक्षीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The name of a country, that of king SALVA; or plu. (-याः) The people of that country.<BR>E.<BR>कार a snowy mountain, कुक्ष the flank, and छ affix; being on the skirts of the Himāla ridge in the north-west of Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारज
कारज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जी-जं)<BR>Of or relating to the finger nail.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A young elephant.<BR>E.<BR>करज a nail, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण|कारणं
कारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Cause, motive, origin, principle: in logic, cause is of three kinds; Samavāyi, inherent or direct; Asamavāyi, proximate or indirect; and Nimitta, instrumental or incidental.<BR>2 Action, agency.<BR>3 Killing, injuring.<BR>4 An organ of sense.<BR>5 An instrument or means.<BR>6 An element, elementary matter.<BR>7 A deity, as the remote or proximate cause of creation.<BR>8 A number of scribes.<BR>9 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>10 A sort of song, &c. see करण.<BR>11 The origin of a story (of a play or poem.)<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Pain, agony.<BR>2 Casting into hell.<BR>3 An astronomical period.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do or act, in the causal form, and युच् or ल्युट् affix, or करण and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणकारण
कारणकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A primary cause.<BR>2 An elementary cause, an atom.<BR>E.<BR>कारण repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगुण|कारणगुणः
कारणगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An elementary or causal property.<BR>E.<BR>कारण, and गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणगुणोद्भवगुण|कारणगुणोद्भवगुणः
कारणगुणोद्भवगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A secondary or derivative property, as form, taste, smell, &c. produced by combinations of elementary or causal particles.<BR>E.<BR>कारणगुण, and उद्भवगुण produced property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणत्व
कारणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Causality, causation.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to कारण, and त्व affix, or with तल्, कारणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणमाला
कारणमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A series or chain of events.<BR>E.<BR>कारण, and माला a wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणवादिन्
कारणवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A complainant, a plaintiff.<BR>E.<BR>कारण the cause, and वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणशरीर|कारणशरीरं
कारणशरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The inner rudiment of the body or causal frame, the seat of the soul.<BR>E.<BR>कारण, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणाभाव
कारणाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Absence of cause.<BR>E.<BR>कारण, and अभाव nonentity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणिक|कारणिकः
कारणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Investigating, trying, ascertaining the cause.<BR>2 Causal, causative.<BR>E.<BR>कारण action, and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारणोत्तर|कारणोत्तरं
कारणोत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Special plea, denial of the cause of complaint, admission of the charge generally, but denial of the issue; as to a demand of debt, acknowledgment that it was incurred, but assertion that the loan has been repaid, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कारण् the cause, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव|कारंडव|कारंडवः|कारण्डवः
कारण्डव<BR>mf. (-वः-वी)<BR>A sort of duck.<BR>E.<BR>करण्ड Vallisneria, अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारण्डव्यूह|कारण्डव्यूहः
कारण्डव्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A Buddha or sanctified being according to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>कारण्ड the same, वै to go, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारन्धमिन्|कारंधमिन्
कारन्धमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 A brazier, a worker in mixed or white metal.<BR>2 A mineralogist, an assayer.<BR>E.<BR>कारं work, and घमिन् who blows; from ध्मा to blow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारम्भा|कारंभा
कारम्भा<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>A plant bearing a fragrant seed, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु bad, आरम्भ beginning; very diminutive while young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारमिहिका
कारमिहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयत्
कारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Causing to do, conferring any power or authority to do, &c. कृ to do, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयमाण
कारयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Doing what is appointed, carrying into effect what has been ordered.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारयितृ
कारयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Causing to act or do.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, causal form, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=213" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारव|कारवः
कारव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>क्वा an imitative sound, रव who sounds.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A kind of Anise, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>3 The asafoetida plant or its leaf, Hiṅguparṇī.<BR>4 A kind of fennel, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>5 A small gourd.<BR>E.<BR>क water, आङ् before रु to go, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्ल|कारवेल्लं|कारवेल्लः
कारवेल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>कार certainty, and वेल्ल what goes; also with कन् added कारवल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारवेल्लक|कारवेल्लकः
कारवेल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कर|कारस्करः
कारस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A medicinal plant.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>कार toll, revenue, and कर what makes; स is inserted in this sense, for the sake of euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारस्कराटिका
कारस्कराटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A centipede or worm resembling it, (Julus.)<BR>E.<BR>कारस्कर a tree, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागार|कारागारं
कारागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A gaol, a place of confinement.<BR>E.<BR>कारा confinement, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारागुप्त|कारागुप्तः
कारागुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Captive, imprisoned, confined, a prisoner.<BR>E.<BR>कारा confinement, and गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारायिका
कारायिका<BR>n. (-का)<BR>A female crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावर|कारावरः
कारावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man of a mixed and low caste, a man born of a Niṣāda father and Vaidehī^1 mother, employed in working in leather or hides.<BR>E.<BR>कार, and अवर low.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260430.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारावेश्मन्
कारावेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>A prison, a gaol.<BR>E.<BR>कारा confinement, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारि|कारिः
कारि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>An artist, an artificer.<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>Action, act, agency.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ to do, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिका
कारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An actress, a dancing woman.<BR>2 Action, agency.<BR>3 Comment, gloss.<BR>4 An art, a profession.<BR>5 Sharp pain.<BR>6 Interest at any stipulated rate.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, and वुन् affix, fem. termination टाप्, and इ substituted for the penultimate vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारित|कारितः
कारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused to be made or done, brought about, effected.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Stipulated interest; also कारिका, and कारितावृद्धि.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, in the causal form, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारितवत्
कारितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Making, doing.<BR>2 Calling, appointing.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारिन्
कारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>An actor, acting, doing.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारीष|कारीषं
कारीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A great quantity of dried cow-dung.<BR>E.<BR>करीष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारु|कारुः
कारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>1 An artist, an artificer, an agent, a maker, a doer.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of VIŚVAKARMA, the artist of the gods.<BR>2 An art, a science.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, and उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुक|कारुकः
कारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An artisan, an artificer.<BR>E.<BR>कारु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुचौर|कारुचौरः
कारुचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One who commits burglary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुज|कारुजः
कारुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A piece of mechanism, any product of manufacture.<BR>2 An ant hill, a hillock.<BR>3 A young elephant.<BR>4 Sesamum growing spontaneously.<BR>5 A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>6 Froth, foam.<BR>7 Red orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>कारु an art or artist, and ज what is born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुणिक|कारुणिकः
कारुणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Compassionate, tender, kind.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा compassion, and ठफ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्डी|कारुंडी
कारुण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A leech; also कारुण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारुण्य|कारुण्यं
कारुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Compassion, tenderness.<BR>E.<BR>करुणा compassion, &c. ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूष
कारूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The offspring of the degraded or outcaste Vaiśya tribe.<BR>2 A country; plu.<BR>m. (-षाः)<BR>Its inhabitants; also वृहद्गृहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारूहस्त
कारूहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The hand of the artisan or artificer.<BR>E.<BR>कारू, and हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तम|कारोत्तमः
कारोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Yeast, barm, froth.<BR>E.<BR>कार action, and उत्तम first, best, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कारोत्तर|कारोत्तरः
कारोत्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Barm, yeast: see the preceding.<BR>2 A well.<BR>E.<BR>as before, उत्तर best, instead of उत्तम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कण|कार्कण
कार्क्कण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Done by or relating to a pheasant.<BR>E.<BR>कृकणा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कवाकव|कार्कवाकव
कार्क्कवाकव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Produced or done by a cock, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृकबाकु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्कश्य|कार्कश्यं|कार्क्कश्य
कार्कश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>1 Hardness, firmness, solidity.<BR>2 Sternness, inflexibility.<BR>E.<BR>कर्कश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्क्कीक|कार्कीक
कार्क्कीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Like a white horse.<BR>E.<BR>कर्क, and ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ण|कार्णः|कार्ण्ण
कार्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Relating to the ear, auricular, &c.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>An earring.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णछिद्रक|कार्णच्छिद्रक
कार्णछिद्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः)<BR>A sort of well.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णछिद the opening of the ear, कन् affix of similitude, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्णवेष्टकिक
कार्णवेष्टकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ornamented with ear-rings.<BR>E.<BR>कर्णवेष्टक, and ठक् affix; also read कार्णवेष्टनिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तवीर्य्य|कार्तवीर्य|कार्तवीर्यः|कार्त्तवीर्य्यः
कार्त्तवीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 The name of a king; also called ARJUNA, killed by PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>2 The name of one of the Jaina cakravartīs or emperors of the world.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्तवीर्य्य the father of this prince, अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तस्वर|कार्तस्वर|कार्तस्वरं|कार्त्तस्वरं
कार्त्तस्वर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Thorn apple.<BR>E.<BR>कृतस्वर a kind of mine, and अण् affix, implying production: or कृतस्वर a reader of the Vedas, (from कत made, and स्वर a sound); to whom gold is given as a reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तान्तिक|कार्तान्तिक|कार्तांतिक|कार्तांतिकः|कार्तान्तिकः|कार्त्तान्तिकः
कार्त्तान्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>कृतान्त fortune, luck, and ठक् affix; acquainted with the fates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिक|कार्तिक|कार्तिकः|कार्त्तिकः
कार्त्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The month Kartik, (October-November,) when the moon is full near the Pleiades.<BR>2 The deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्तिका the Pleiades, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकिक|कार्तिकिक|कार्त्तिकिकः
कार्त्तिकिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding, ठक् affix added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकेय|कार्तिकेय|कार्तिकेयः|कार्त्तिकेयः
कार्त्तिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA, the deity of war and son of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्तिका the personified Pleiades, and ढक् affix: according to the legend, having been fostered and brought up by the nymphs so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकेयप्रसू|कार्तिकेयप्रसू
कार्त्तिकेयप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कार्त्तिकेय, and प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्तिकोत्सव|कार्तिकोत्सव|कार्त्तिकोत्सवः
कार्त्तिकोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Kārttika, a festival.<BR>E.<BR>कार्त्तिक the month, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न
कार्त्स्न<BR>n. (-र्त्स्नं)<BR>The whole, all, entire.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्स्न, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्त्स्न्य|कार्त्स्न्यं
कार्त्स्न्य<BR>n. (-र्त्स्न्यं)<BR>The whole, all entire.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्स्न, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्द्दम|कार्दम
कार्द्दम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Made of mud, filled with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कर्द्दम and अण् affix; also with ठक्, कार्द्दमिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पट|कार्पटः
कार्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Lac, the animal dye.<BR>2 A petitioner, A suitor, one who begs for employment, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पटिक|कार्पटिकः
कार्पटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A parasite.<BR>2 A pilgrim, one who spends his life in pilgrimage, or who subsists by carrying water from holy rivers.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, अटन affix, ठञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पण्य|कार्पण्यं
कार्पण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Poverty, indigence.<BR>2 Poorness of spirit, weakness, imbecility.<BR>E.<BR>कृपण poor, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=214" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पास|कार्पासं|कार्पासः
कार्पास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Made of cotton, cottony, &c.<BR>nf. (-सं-सी)<BR>1 The cotton plant, (Gossypium hirsutum.)<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Cotton cloth, &c.<BR>2 Paper.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, to do, पास Uṇādi affix, the vowel of the radical being lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासनासिका
कार्पासनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A spindle.<BR>E.<BR>कार्पास, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासास्थि
कार्पासास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थिः)<BR>The seed of the cotton plant.<BR>E.<BR>कार्पास, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्पासिक
कार्पासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of or from cotton.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The cotton plant: see कार्पास.<BR>E.<BR>कार्यास, and ठञ् affix; or कार्प्पास with कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्म|कार्म|कार्म्मः
कार्म्म<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी-र्म्मं)<BR>Laborious, industrious, occupied.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म an act, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मण|कार्मण|कार्म्मणं
कार्म्मण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Finishing a work, doing it well or completely.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Magic, performing any thing by means of magical incantations.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्मन् work, act, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मणत्व|कार्मणत्व
कार्म्मणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Magic, fascination.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मिक|कार्मिक|कार्म्मिकः
कार्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Manufactured, made.<BR>2 Worked, embroidered, intermixed with coloured thread, (cloth, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म work, art, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मुक|कार्मुक|कार्म्मुकं|कार्म्मुकः
कार्म्मुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Finishing a work, doing it well or completely.<BR>nm. (-कं-कः)<BR>A bamboo.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>कर्म्म act, action, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्म्मुकभृत्|कार्मुकभृत्
कार्म्मुकभृत्<BR>m. (भृत्)<BR>A soldier, an archer.<BR>E.<BR>कार्म्मक, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्य|कार्य|कार्य्यं
कार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be done.<BR>2 What ought to be done, fit, right.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Cause, origin.<BR>2 Motive, object.<BR>3 Effect, result of a cause.<BR>4 Affair, business.<BR>5 Lawsuit, dispute.<BR>6 The denouement of a drama.<BR>7 In grammar, an adjunct, either as an affix, augment or substitute.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकारण|कार्यकारण
कार्य्यकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Cause of a special or incidental kind, originating in some act or occasion.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकारणतस्|कार्यकारणतस्
कार्य्यकारणतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Incidentally, from some special cause.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्यकारण, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकाल|कार्यकाल|कार्यकालः
कार्य्यकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Time for action, appointed time, season, opportunity.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यकुशल|कार्यकुशल|कार्य्यकुशलः
कार्य्यकुशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Finishing a work, doing it well or completely.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य business, and कुशल prosperous, successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यक्षम|कार्यक्षम
कार्य्यक्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Competent, fit, able.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and क्षम able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यगुरुता|कार्यगुरुता
कार्य्यगुरुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Necessity or importance of any act.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and गुरुता weight; also कार्य्यगुरुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यचिन्तक|कार्यचिन्तक|कार्यचिंतक|कार्यचिन्तकः
कार्य्यचिन्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Prudent, considerate, cautious.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and चिन्तक who reflects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यचिन्ता|कार्यचिन्ता
कार्य्यचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Prudence, caution, consideration.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and चिन्ता reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यतस्|कार्यतस्
कार्य्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Consequently, necessarily, actually.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य act, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यदर्शन|कार्यदर्शन
कार्य्यदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inspection, supervision.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यनिर्णय|कार्यनिर्णय|कार्यनिर्णयः
कार्य्यनिर्णय<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 Judgment, ascertainment of the fact.<BR>2 Settlement of an affair.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य affair, cause, and निर्णय ascertainment; also कार्य्यविनिर्णय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यपुट|कार्यपुट|कार्यपुटः|कार्य्यपुटः
कार्य्यपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An impudent or shameless fellow.<BR>2 An idler, one who follows unprofitable pursuits.<BR>3 A madman, a crazy or hair-brained man.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य object, cause, &c. पुट to rub, to destroy, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यप्रद्वेष|कार्यप्रद्वेष|कार्यप्रद्वेषः|कार्य्यप्रद्वेषः
कार्य्यप्रद्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Idleness.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and प्रद्वेष aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यभाजन|कार्यभाजन
कार्य्यभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any one engaged in active life, one fit for business or conducting affairs.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and भाजन a vessel; also कार्य्यपात्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्|कार्यवत्|कार्यवन्त्
कार्य्यवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Actually, according to act or motive.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्|कार्यवत्|कार्यवन्त्
कार्य्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Engaged in business.<BR>2 Having a cause or motive.<BR>3 Doing one's duty.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवत्ता|कार्यवत्ता
कार्य्यवत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Act, action.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्यवत् and तल् affix; also कार्य्यवत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवश|कार्यवश
कार्य्यवश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Necessary consequence.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य cause, and वश subjection to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यवस्तु|कार्यवस्तु
कार्य्यवस्तु<BR>n. (-न्तु)<BR>End, object.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and वस्तु thing, what is to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यविपत्ति|कार्यविपत्ति|कार्यविपत्तिः
कार्य्यविपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Failure, reverse, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and विपत्ति misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यशेष|कार्यशेष|कार्यशेषः
कार्य्यशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The completion of a business or affair begun.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and शेष rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसन्देह|कार्यसन्देह
कार्य्यसन्देह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Embarrassment, difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and सन्देह doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसागर|कार्यसागर
कार्य्यसागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Business, heavy business, weighty affairs.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and सागर ocean; also similar compounds, as कार्य्याब्धि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसाधक|कार्यसाधक
कार्य्यसाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Accomplishing any object.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and साधक what compleats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसाधन
कार्य्यसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Means of effecting any object, instrument, implement, aid.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and साधन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यसिद्धि|कार्यसिद्धि|कार्यसिद्धिः
कार्य्यसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Accomplishment, success, fulfilment of any object or purpose.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and सिद्धि success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यहन्तृ|कार्यहन्तृ|कार्यहंतृ
कार्य्यहन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Foiling, counteracting, opposing all one's aims.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and हन्तृ who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्याक्षम|कार्याक्षम
कार्य्याक्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Unfit, incompetent, unable.<BR>E.<BR>काय्य, and अक्षम unable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यान्त|कार्यान्त
कार्य्यान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The end of a business.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थ|कार्यार्थ|कार्यार्थः
कार्य्यार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 An object or purpose.<BR>2 Application for employment.<BR>n. or adv. (-र्थं)<BR>1 For the sake of any particular object.<BR>2 To perform any work or duty.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थसिद्धि|कार्यार्थसिद्धि
कार्य्यार्थसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>The accomplishment of any object or purpose.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्यार्थ, and सिद्धि fulfilment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यार्थिन्|कार्यार्थिन्
कार्य्यार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 Having an object or purpose.<BR>2 Applying for employment.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्यार्थ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यिक|कार्यिक
कार्य्यिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having business, transacting business.<BR>2 Seeking employment, &c.<BR>3 Engaged in a suit at law.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्यिन्|कार्यिन्
कार्य्यिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यी-र्य्यिनी-र्य्यि)<BR>1 Seeking for employment.<BR>2 One who transacts business, active, assiduous.<BR>3 Having an object.<BR>4 A party to a suit, either as plaintiff or defendant.<BR>5 Requiring an affix, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्येक्षण|कार्येक्षण
कार्य्येक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Superintendence of public affairs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्योद्धार|कार्योद्धार|कार्योद्धारः
कार्य्योद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Discharge of any duty, performance of any act.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and उद्धार extrication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=215" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काय्याद्युक्त
काय्याद्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Engaged in any business, intent upon any object.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and उद्युक्त active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्य्योद्योग|कार्योद्योग|कार्योद्योगः
कार्य्योद्योग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Active engagement in any business.<BR>E.<BR>कार्य्य, and उद्योग exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्शनव
कार्शनव<BR>mfn. (-बः-वी-वं)<BR>Fiery, hot, glaring, relating to fire.<BR>E.<BR>कृशानु fire, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्य|कार्श्यं|कार्श्यः
कार्श्य<BR>m. (-र्श्यः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta): see कार्श्य.<BR>n. (-र्ष्यं)<BR>Thinness, emaciation.<BR>E.<BR>कृश thin, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्श्मरी
कार्श्मरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, commonly Gambhari: see काश्मरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षक|कार्षकः
कार्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to draw furrows, क्वुन् Uṇādi affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापण|कार्षापणं|कार्षापणः
कार्षापण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>A weight or measure of different values, as synonymous with Karṣa; it is of gold, weighing sixteen Māṣas, or about 176 grains; of silver, it is in value sixteen Paṇas of kowries, or in tale 1280 commonly termed a Kāhan: of copper it weighs eighty Rattis, or the same as of gold, about 176 grains; according to some, it is the same as a Pan of kowries, or in tale eighty.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Money, gold and silver.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ष a Karṣa of silver, आपण custom, habit, and the vowel of कर्ष lengthened; also with कन् added कार्षापणकः see कर्षपण and कार्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणवर
कार्षापणवर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The Karṣa of the lowest value.<BR>E.<BR>कार्षापण, and अवर low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षापणिक
कार्षापणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought, &c. with a Karṣa.<BR>E.<BR>कार्षापण, and टिठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षि|कार्षिः
कार्षि<BR>f. (-र्षिः)<BR>1 Ploughing, cultivation.<BR>2 Drawing, attracting.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to draw, इन affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्षिक|कार्षिकः
कार्षिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A weight: see the preceding.<BR>2 A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>कर्ष a measure, ploughing, &c. and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्ण
कार्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-र्ष्णी-र्ष्णं)<BR>1 Black.<BR>2 Of or belonging to the black antelope.<BR>m. (-र्ष्णः)<BR>The black antelope.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णायस
कार्ष्णायस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Made of black iron.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्णायस, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्णि|कार्ष्णिः
कार्ष्णि<BR>m. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण the deity KṚṢṆA, and इञ् affix; the son of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्य|कार्ष्यः
कार्ष्य<BR>m. (-र्ष्यः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष to make furrows, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कार्ष्यवण
कार्ष्यवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A forest of Śāl trees.<BR>E.<BR>कार्ष्य, and वन a wood, the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल<BR>r. 10th cl. (कालयति)<BR>To count time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल|कालं|कालः
काल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Black, of a dark colour, dark blue especially, which is usually confounded with black.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>3 A black colour.<BR>4 Death.<BR>5 A form of ŚIVA.<BR>6 The planet Saturn.<BR>7 The Koïl.<BR>8 Cassia fistula.<BR>9 Resin.<BR>10 A plant, a red kind of plumbago.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 A black agallochum: see कालीयक.<BR>3 A vegetable poison, perhaps the fruit of the Cocculus Indicus.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Indigo, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>2 A black sort of Tëori.<BR>5 Calonji, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>4 Madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>(-ला or -ली)<BR>A name of the goddess DURGĀ the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>(-ली)<BR>1 The wife of ŚANTANU a king.<BR>2 One of the Mātṛs or divine mothers.<BR>3 A female deity of the Bauddhas.<BR>4 A row or succession of clouds.<BR>5 Ink or blacking.<BR>6 A worm or animalcule generated in the acetous fermentation of milk.<BR>7 Abuse, censure, defamation.<BR>8 Night.<BR>9 Trumpet flower. (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>10 One of the seven tongues or flames of fire.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count or reckon, &c. in the causal form, अच affix, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक|कालकं|कालकः
कालक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Black, dark coloured.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A freckle, a mark.<BR>2 A water snake.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The mother of a class of Asuras.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The liver.<BR>E.<BR>कल to reckon, (good or bad fortune,) वुञ् affix; or काल black, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकण्ठ|कालकंठ|कालकण्ठः
कालकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A water fowl, a gallinule.<BR>3 A sparrow.<BR>4 A peacock.<BR>5 A wagtail.<BR>6 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa): see असन.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and कण्ट the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकण्ठक|कालकण्ठकः
कालकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकचु
कालकचु<BR>f. (-चुः)<BR>A sort of Arum, (A. colocasia.)<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and कचु Arum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकन्दक|कालकन्दकः
कालकन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A water snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकर्णिका
कालकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Misfortune, misery; also कालकर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकलाय|कालकलायः
कालकलाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR>E.<BR>काल black, कलाय pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकरण
कालकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Appointing a time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकल्प
कालकल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Like death, fatal, deadly.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and कल्प like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकस्तूरी
कालकस्तूरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus abelmoschus.)<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and कस्तूरी musk; the seeds having a smell of musk when rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकारित
कालकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Effected or brought about by or in time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and कारित occasioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकील|कालकीलः
कालकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A confused or mingled sound, a tumult; also कालकीलक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुण्ठ|कालकुंठ|कालकुण्ठः
कालकुण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and कुण्ठ confusing, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकुष्ठ|कालकुष्ठः
कालकुष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A sort of earth from the mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूट|कालकूटं|कालकूटः
कालकूट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>A kind of poison.<BR>E.<BR>काल YAMA, कूठ to destroy, अप् affix; destroying even the regent of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकूटङ्कट
कालकूटङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कालकूट poison, and कट who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकृत्
कालकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and कृत् who makes; who marks the time; also कालकृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालकृत|कालकृतः
कालकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fixed, appointed, (as to time.)<BR>2 Lent or deposited by a giver.<BR>3 Produced or effected by time.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The sun: see the preceding.<BR>2 Time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालक्षेप|कालक्षेपः
कालक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Spending or passing time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and क्षेप throwing away; also कालक्षेपन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालखञ्जन|कालखंजन|कालखञ्जनं
कालखञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The liver.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and खजि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालखण्ड|कालखंड|कालखण्डं
कालखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>The liver.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and स्वण्ट part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालगन्ध
कालगन्ध<BR>m. (न्धः)<BR>Kind of Cobra de copella: see अलगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालग्रन्थि|कालग्रंथि|कालग्रन्थिः
कालग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and ग्रन्थि a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालङ्कत|कालङ्कतः
कालङ्कत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालचक्र|कालचक्रं|कालचक्रः
कालचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 A cycle, a given revolution of time.<BR>2 A period according to the Jainas, of twelve Aras: see अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालञ्जर|कालंजर|कालंजरः|कालञ्जरः
कालञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The name of a rock in Bundelkhand, the modern Kallinjer.<BR>3 The adjacent country [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">Page217</a>]<BR>4 An assembly or collection of religious mendicants; Kallinjer is one of the places at which such assemblies meet, being enumerated in the Vedas amongst the Tapasyasthānas, or spots adapted to practices of austere devotion.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>An appellation of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>काल in the second case, time or death, and जर who makes old, or causes to decay; irregularly deduced from the causal of जॄ to become old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=216" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालज्ञ|कालज्ञः
कालज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>One who knows times or seasons.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 An astrologer.<BR>2 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालदण्ड|कालदंड|कालदण्डः
कालदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The staff of death, death.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and दण्ड staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालधर्म्म|कालधर्म|कालधर्मः|कालधर्म्मः
कालधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Influence of time, seasonableness, effects proper to the time or season.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and धर्म्म virtue, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनियोग|कालनियोगः
कालनियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Fate, destiny.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and नियोग will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनिर्य्यास|कालनिर्यास|कालनिर्यासः|कालनिर्य्यासः
कालनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A fragrant and resinous substance, Bdellium: see गुग्गुल.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and निर्य्यास an extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमि|कालनेमिः
कालनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A demon, the son of HIRAṆYAKAŚIPU.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa described in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिन्
कालनेमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A demon: see कालनेमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिरिपु|कालनेमिरिपुः
कालनेमिरिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>An epithet of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कालनेमि the name of a demon who undertook to destroy the deity in his youth, and रिपु the foe: see similar names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेमिहन्
कालनेमिहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कालनेमि, and हन who kills or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालनेम्यरि|कालनेम्यरिः
कालनेम्यरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>See कालनेमिरिपु.<BR>E.<BR>as above, अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपक्व
कालपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Spontaneously ripened.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and पक्व matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपर्ण|कालपर्णः|कालपर्ण्ण
कालपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A tree bearing dark coloured leaves, (Tabernae montana coronaria,) commonly Tagara: see तगर.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपरिवास|कालपरिवासः
कालपरिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Standing for a time, (as to get stale or fermented, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>काल, and परिवास abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपाश|कालपाशः
कालपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The noose of YAMA or death.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and पाश a noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपुरुष|कालपुरुषः
कालपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 One of YAMA'S attendants or ministers.<BR>2 An astrological figure of a man, with the positions of the constellations, &c. inscribed on different parts of the body for the purpose of predicting his fortunes; also कालनर, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालपृष्ठ|कालपृष्ठं|कालपृष्ठः
कालपृष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>1 The bow of KARṆA.<BR>2 A bow in general.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 The black antelope.<BR>2 A heron.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and पृष्ठ the back; black-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालप्रभात|कालप्रभातं
कालप्रभात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The sultry season, autumn, the two months following the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and प्रभात shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालप्ररूढ
कालप्ररूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Over-blown, over-ripe.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and प्ररूढ blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालबलन
कालबलन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>काल death, and बलन strengthening, defending; perhaps a wrong reading for कायबलन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमान|कालमानः
कालमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Black Tulasi; also read कालमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमुष्कक|कालमुष्ककः
कालमुष्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेशिका
कालमेशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>2 A black sort of Tëori, a plant so called, a species of convolvulus: see कालमेषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेशी
कालमेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>See कालमेषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेषिका
कालमेषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Bengal madder.<BR>2 Black Tëori: see त्रिवृता.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, मिष to possess, अन् and ङीष् affixes, and कन् added; or without this affix, कालमेषी; also being derived from मिश to sound, कालमेशिका and कालमेशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालमेषी
कालमेषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>2 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith): see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयवन|कालयवनः
कालयवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An Asura, an enemy of KṚṢṆA, destroyed by him by stratagem.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, यवन a Yavana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालयाप|कालयापः
कालयाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Procrastination, putting off, delaying.<BR>2 Passing away time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and या to go, causal form, घञ् affix; also with ल्युट्, कालयापनं; also यापः and यापनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालरात्रि|कालरात्रिः
कालरात्रि<BR>m. (-त्रिः)<BR>1 A particular night, one which occurs on the 7th day of the 7th month of every 77th year; after such a period of life, a man is exempt from attention to the usual ordinances.<BR>2 The last night of a Kalpa.<BR>3 A dark night.<BR>4 A form of Śakti or DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, time, and रात्रि a night: see भीमरथी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललवण|काललवणं
काललवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A factitious and purgative salt, commonly Bitlaven or Bitnoben.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काललोह
काललोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and लौह a metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृक्ष
कालवृक्ष<BR>(-क्षः)<BR>A kind of vetch: see कलिवृन्त.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, वृक्ष tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृद्धि|कालवृद्धिः
कालवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Periodical interest, payable, monthly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and वृद्धि interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवृन्त|कालवृन्तः
कालवृन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A kind of vetch, (Dolichos biflorus.)<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>Trumpet flower.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and वृन्त stalk: see कुलत्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालवेला
कालवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A season at which any act is improper, half a watch in every day.<BR>E.<BR>काल and बेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशाक
कालशाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of potherb.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालशेय|कालशेयं
कालशेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>कलशी a jar, and ढक् affix; produced in a jar or pitcher by churning; also कालसेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसंरोध|कालसंरोधः
कालसंरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Lapse of a long period of time.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, संरोध impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसदृश
कालसदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Opportune, seasonable.<BR>2 Deathlike.<BR>E.<BR>काल and सदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसम्पन्न|कालसंपन्न
कालसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Dated, bearing a date.<BR>2 Effected by time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and सम्पन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसर्प|कालसर्पः
कालसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>The black and most deadly variety of the cobra, (Coluber naga.)<BR>E.<BR>कास्त black, and सर्प a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसार|कालसारं|कालसारः
कालसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The black antelope.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसूत्र|कालसूत्रं
कालसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>One of the twenty-one hells.<BR>E.<BR>काल from कल to count, a reckoning, and सूत्र a thread, a rule; also with कन added कालसूत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालसेय|कालसेयं
कालसेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Buttermilk: see कालशेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालस्कन्ध|कालस्कंध|कालस्कन्धः
कालस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A sort of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon, Rox.)<BR>2 The Tamāla, a tree bearing dark blossoms.<BR>3 Another plant: see जीवक.<BR>4 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>काल black and स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाकृष्ट
कालाकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Led to death or destruction, drawn to or by one's fate.<BR>2 Produced or brought about by time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and आकृष्ट attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=217" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाक्षरिक|कालाक्षरिकः
कालाक्षरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A scholar, a pupil.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, अक्षर a letter, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालागुरु
कालागुरु<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>A black kind of aloe wood or agallochum: see अगुरु.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and अगुरु agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाग्नि|कालाग्निः
कालाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The fire that is to destroy the world.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाञ्जनी
कालाञ्जनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A small shrub, used as a purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालात्यय|कालात्ययः
कालात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Loss or destruction by lapse of time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अत्यय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुनादिन्
कालानुनादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 A sparrow.<BR>3 The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>काल season, and अनुनादिन् who sings or sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसारक|कालानुसारकं|कालानुसारकः
कालानुसारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A tree, commonly Tagara.<BR>2 Yellow Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अनुसार being like or conforming to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसारि|कालानुसारिः
कालानुसारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 Benzoin or benjamin.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, अनुसार resembling, being, and कि affix; also कालानुसार्य्य the affix being यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालानुसार्य्य|कालानुसार्य|कालानुसार्यः|कालानुसार्य्यं
कालानुसार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Gum benjamin or benzoin.<BR>2 A yellow fragrant wood from which a perfume is prepared.<BR>3 A timber tree, commonly Sisu: see शिंशपा.<BR>4 A tree, commonly Tagara.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding; also with कन्, added कालानुसार्य्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तक|कालांतक|कालान्तकः
कालान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>YAMA, death.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तर|कालांतर
कालान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Interval, intermediate time.<BR>2 Period, process of time.<BR>2 A former or another time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अन्तर between, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तरविष|कालांतरविष|कालान्तरविषः
कालान्तरविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A poisonous animal, venomous only when enraged or alarmed, as a rat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, अन्तर after or at, and विष poison; having venom only at times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालान्तरावृत्त
कालान्तरावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Hidden or concealed by time.<BR>E.<BR>कालान्तर, and आवृत्त covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाप|कालापः
कालाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A serpent's hood.<BR>2 A demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>3 A student of the Kalāpa grammar.<BR>E.<BR>कलाप, and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालायस|कालायसं
कालायस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अयस् iron, टच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालावधि|कालावधिः
कालावधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A fixed or appointed time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालाशौच
कालाशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Season of mourning or impurity.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and अशौच impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिक|कालिकं|कालिकः
कालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to time.<BR>2 Seasonable.<BR>3 Of long standing.<BR>4 Of a dark colour, black, blackish, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The curlew.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A black kind of Sandal: see कालीयक.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Cloudiness, a multitude or succession of clouds.<BR>2 A dark cloud threatening rain.<BR>3 A fog or mist, &c.<BR>4 The goddess GAURĪ.<BR>5 A terrific goddess, a form of CAṆḌĪ or DURGĀ.<BR>6 A female singer of Svarga.<BR>7 Blackness, a black colour.<BR>8 A fault or flaw in gold, &c.<BR>9 Spirituous liquor.<BR>10 A plant: see वृश्चिकपत्र.<BR>11 A kind of potherb.<BR>12 The branch of a cucumber plant.<BR>13 Spikenard.<BR>14 A line of hair extending to the navel.<BR>15 A female crow.<BR>16 Price of a commodity on credit, or a price to be paid at a fixed period, or by instalments.<BR>17 Periodical interest paid by the month, &c.<BR>18 An animalcule formed by the fermentation of milk.<BR>19 Ink or blacking.<BR>20 A small bird, commonly Śyāma.<BR>21 A medicinal plant: see काकोलि.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, &c. ठक् or कन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिकता
कालिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Time, date, season.<BR>E.<BR>कालिक, and तल् affix; also with त्व, कालिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिङ्ग|कालिंग|कालिङ्गं|कालिङ्गः
कालिङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Produced in or belonging to the Kaliṅga country.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>3 A species of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>4 A sort of iron.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A gourd or cucumber.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The water melon.<BR>E.<BR>कलिङ्ग a country, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदास|कालिदासः
कालिदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The name of a celebrated poet, author of Śakuntalā, Vikramorvaśī, the Megha Dūta, the Raghu Vaṃśa, the Nalodaya and other poems: he was one of nine poets or gems of VIKRAMĀDITYA'S court, and is supposed to have flourished in the century preceding the Christian aera; the name is however applied to more persons than one, and seems, in some measure, to have been used as an honorary title; the works attributed to this author are amongst the most elegant compositions in the Sanskrit language.<BR>E.<BR>काली the goddess DURGĀ, and दास a slave, the final of काली being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदासक|कालिदासकः
कालिदासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The poet KĀLIDĀSA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to कालिदास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिनी
कालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>One of the lunar mansions: see आर्द्रा.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, affixes इनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दक|कालिन्दकं
कालिन्दक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The water melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दी|कालिंदी
कालिन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>The YAMUNĀ or JUMNA river.<BR>E.<BR>कलिन्द a mountain, part of the Himāla range, and the seat of the river's source, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीकर्षण|कालिंदीकर्षण|कालिन्दीकर्षणः
कालिन्दीकर्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कालिन्दी the YAMUNĀ, and कर्षण the plougher; having diverted the stream into a new and devious channel, marked out by his ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीभेदन|कालिंदीभेदन|कालिन्दीभेदनः
कालिन्दीभेदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कालिन्दी, and भिद् to break, affix ल्युट्: see the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसू|कालिंदीसू
कालिन्दीसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The wife of SŪRYA and mother of YAMUNĀ the personified river.<BR>E.<BR>कालिन्दी, and सू who bears, from सू to bear children, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिन्दीसोदर|कालिंदीसोदर|कालिन्दीसोदरः
कालिन्दीसोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>कालिन्दी, and सोदर brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिमन्
कालिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Blackness.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिय|कालियः
कालिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to time, &c.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A serpent destroyed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीक|कालीकः
कालीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A curlew, a sort of heron: see कालिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीची
कालीची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The court of judgment of YAMA, regent and judge of the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीतनय|कालीतनयः
कालीतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>काली the goddess, and तनय a son: i. e. a favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीन
कालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Timely, seasonable, relating to time.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीय|कालीयं
कालीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to time, to blackness, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A dark kind of Sandal, or perhaps of Agallochum: see कालीयक.<BR>E.<BR>काल black, and छः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालीयक|कालीयकं|कालीयकः
कालीयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A yellow fragrant wood, perhaps a species of aloe wood.<BR>2 A dark kind of Sandal wood.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of turmeric, (Curcuma zanthorhiza): see दारुहरिद्रा.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, of a black or blackish hue; also कालीय, कालेय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालुष्य|कालुष्यं
कालुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Foulness, dirtiness, turbidness, opacity.<BR>E.<BR>कालष, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=218" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेय|कालेयं|कालेयः
कालेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Belonging to the Kali age, &c.<BR>2 Dark coloured.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A yellow fragrant wood: see कालीयक and कालीयक.<BR>2 The liver.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The name of a demon or imp.<BR>E.<BR>काल or कलि, and ढक् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालेयक|कालेयकं|कालेयकः
कालेयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of curcuma, (C. zanthorhiza, Rox.) see कालीयक.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोत्पादित
कालोत्पादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Produced in due season.<BR>E.<BR>काल, उत्पादित engendered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालोप्त
कालोप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Sown in due season.<BR>E.<BR>काल, and उप्त sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्प|काल्पः
काल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पी-ल्पं)<BR>1 Preceptive, ritual.<BR>2 Relating to a Kalpa or period so called.<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>E.<BR>कल्प a precept, and अण् affix; the plant forms a part of oblations offered upon certain occasions to fire; also with कन् added काल्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पक|काल्पकः
काल्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary: see the preceding; also काल्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्पनिक|काल्पनिकः
काल्पनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Artificial, fabricated.<BR>2 Fictitious, invented.<BR>E.<BR>कल्पना, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्य|काल्यं
काल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Timely, seasonable.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Dawn, daybreak, see कल्य.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A cow fit for the bull.<BR>2 Pleasant or auspicious discourse: see कल्या.<BR>E.<BR>काल time, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्यक|काल्यकः
काल्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary: see कल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काल्याणिनेय
काल्याणिनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sprung from a virtuous or fortunate woman.<BR>E.<BR>कल्याणी, and ढक् affix, इनञ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावचिक|कावचिकं
कावचिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to armour, armorial.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of men in armour.<BR>E.<BR>कवच armour, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावरुक
कावरुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fearful, henpecked.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावाद
कावाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Indistinct sound.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु bad, वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावार|कावारं
कावार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>An umbrella, a Catta, especially one without a stick, and worn like a broad brimmed hat.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, and आबार what covers or protects, from वृ to skreen, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावृक|कावृकः
कावृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A gallinaceous fowl.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR>3 A small singing bird, (Loxia philippensis^1): see पीतमस्तक.<BR>E.<BR>क water, or क for कु bad, आङ्, before वृ to cover, and कक् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कावेर|कावेरं
कावेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Saffron, (Crocus sativus.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A river in the Dekhin, the Kāverī.<BR>2 A courtezan, a harlot.<BR>3 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>कव to colour, एरक affix, and the radical vowel made long, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्य|काव्यं|काव्यः
काव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A name of ŚUKRĀCĀRYA, the preceptor of the demons.<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>1 Understanding, intelligence.<BR>2 A female fiend: see पूतना.<BR>3 A Pitṛ of a particular order, the son of KAVI or ŚUKRA.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A poem, poetical composition.<BR>E.<BR>कवि a poet, &c. ञ्यत् derivative or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काव्यचौर|काव्यचौरः
काव्यचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plagiarist.<BR>E.<BR>काव्य a poem, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश<BR>(ऋ) काशृ r. 1st cl. (काशते) also (उ, ऋ) (उकाशृ) r. 4th cl. (काश्यते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>With निर् prefixed,<BR>To expel.<BR>2 To hide or obscure;<BR>with प्र,<BR>To make or become manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश|काशं|काशः
काश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Cough, catarrh: see कास.<BR>2 Sneezing.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>1 A species of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>2 Irritation in the throat.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>Kāśi or Benares, the holy city so called.<BR>(-शी or -शा)<BR>Saccharum spontaneum, as above.<BR>E.<BR>कश to sound, in the causal form, अच् affix; or काश to shine, अच्, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशक|काशकः
काशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of long grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशमर्द्द|काशमर्द|काशमर्द्दः
काशमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>See कासमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशाल्मलि|काशाल्मलिः
काशाल्मलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A kind of silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>का bad, inferior, and शाल्मलि the Simul tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशि|काशिः
काशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>Kāśi, a celebrated city and place of pilgrimage, the modern Benares.<BR>E.<BR>काश to shine, to be beautiful or renowned, and इन् Uṇādi affix; also काशीः see काश and काशिका, काशिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिका
काशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Kāśi or Benares: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिकाप्रिय|काशिकाप्रियः
काशिकाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of DHANVANTARI, as king of Benares.<BR>E.<BR>काशिका the city Kāśi, and प्रिय a friend; also काशिराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिन्
काशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 Having a cold or cough.<BR>2 Shining, brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>काश cough, and इनि affix, or काश to shine, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिराज|काशिराजः
काशिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of DHANVANTARI or DIVODĀSA, a king of Benares, and an author of medical works; he is often confounded with his celestial namesake, the physician of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>काशि the city, and राज a king or ruler; also काशीराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशिल
काशिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Made of kās grass, abounding with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काश, and इल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीनाथ|काशीनाथः
काशीनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>काशी Kāśi or Benares, and नाथ lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीराज|काशीराजः
काशीराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>DIVODĀSA: see काशिराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशीश|काशीशं
काशीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 DIVODĀSA, or any king of Benares.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Sulphate of iron.<BR>E.<BR>काशी, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काशूकार
काशूकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The betel nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मरी
काश्मरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, commonly Gambhāri, (Gmelina arborea, Rox.) see गम्भारी.<BR>E.<BR>काश to shine, and अर affix, formative irr.; also कार्श्मरी and काश्मर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मर्य्य|काश्मर्य|काश्मर्यः|काश्मर्य्यः
काश्मर्य्य<BR>mn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्यं)<BR>Gambhāri, a plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>यत् added to काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीर|काश्मीरं|काश्मीरः
काश्मीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A plant with a tuberous root, a sort of costus, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>2 A country, Kashmir, or in the plu. (-राः) its inhabitants.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A tree, (Ficus elastica.)<BR>E.<BR>कश्मीर Kashmir, and अण् affix; produced in that place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरज|काश्मीरजं
काश्मीरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A costus.<BR>2 Saffron: see कश्मीर.<BR>f. (-जः)<BR>Atis or Betula: see अतिबिषा.<BR>E.<BR>काश्मीर and ज born; produced in Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्मीरजन्मन्
काश्मीरजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>काश्मीर, and जन्मन् birth; produced in Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्य|काश्यं
काश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यप|काश्यपं|काश्यपः
काश्यप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The name of a saint; also called KAṆĀDA, the son of KAŚYAPA.<BR>2 A name of ARUṆA: see the next.<BR>3 A sort of deer.<BR>4 A tribe of Brahmans pretending to descend from KAŚYAPA.<BR>E.<BR>कश्यप a saint, and अण् affix of descent.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>काश्य spirituous liquor, and प from पा to drink or cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपि|काश्यपिः
काश्यपि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>1 A name of ARUṆA.<BR>2 A name of GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कश्यप the saint, and इञ् affix of descent, being both sons of KAŚYAPA.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>as before; alluding to a legend from the Purāṇas, in which [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">Page220</a>] PARAŚURĀMA, after the destruction of the Kṣatriya race, and performance of an Aśvamedha, presented the sovereignty of the world to his Guru, KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=219" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्यपेय|काश्यपेयः
काश्यपेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>कश्यप the saint, and ढक् affix of descent, the son of KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काश्वरी
काश्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant: see काश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काषाय
काषाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Red, dyed of a reddish colour.<BR>E.<BR>कषाय, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठ|काष्ठं
काष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Wood.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 A quarter or region of the world, space, tract.<BR>2 Place, site.<BR>3 Limit, boundary.<BR>4 A measure of time, the thirtieth part of a Kalā, or eighteen twinklings of the eye.<BR>5 Excellence, superiority.<BR>6 A plant, (Curcuma zanthorhiza, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>काश to shine, Uṇādi affix क्यन्, श changed to ष, and थ after ष becomes ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठक|काष्ठकं
काष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Aloe wood or agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकदली
काष्ठकदली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The wild plantain.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and कदली a plantain; the fruit being hard and woody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकीट|काष्ठकीटः
काष्ठकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small insect or worm found in decayed wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकुट्ट|काष्ठकुट्टः
काष्ठकुट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A bird, a sort of woodpecker, (Picus Bengalensis.)<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and कुट्ट to cut, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठकुद्दाल|काष्ठकुद्दालः
काष्ठकुद्दाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of wooden shovel or scraper used for baling water out of a boat, or for scraping and cleaning its bottom, &c.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and कुद्दाल shovel; also with the first vowel long कूद्दाल, काष्ठकूद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठखण्ड
काष्ठखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A stick, a spar, a piece of wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and खण्ड piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतक्ष्
काष्ठतक्ष्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and तक्ष to cut or pare, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतक्षक|काष्ठतक्षकः
काष्ठतक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A carpenter: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठतन्तु|काष्ठतंतु|काष्ठतन्तुः
काष्ठतन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A small worm that is found in timber.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and तन्तु what spreads, from तन with तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठदारु|काष्ठदारुः
काष्ठदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Deodar tree, (Uvaria longifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठद्रु|काष्ठद्रुः
काष्ठद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमठी
काष्ठमठी<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>A funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and मठी a pile, an edifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमय
काष्ठमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Wooden, made of wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठमल्ल|काष्ठमल्लः
काष्ठमल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A bier, a plank, &c. on which dead bodies are carried.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ wood, and मल्ल a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलेखक|काष्ठलेखकः
काष्ठलेखक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small worm found in wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and लेखक who writes or inscribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठलोहिन्
काष्ठलोहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A club, a short cudgel, especially if armed with iron.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, लौह iron, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठवत्|काष्ठवन्त्
काष्ठवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having wood for fuel, &c.<BR>ind.<BR>Like a piece of wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठागार|काष्ठागारः
काष्ठागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wooden house or enclosure.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी|काष्ठांबुवाहिनी
काष्ठाम्बुवाहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A wooden bucket or baling vessel: see अम्बुवाहिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठिन्
काष्ठिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>1 Of wood, wooden.<BR>2 Having wood.<BR>E.<BR>काष्ठ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काष्ठीला
काष्ठीला<BR>m. (-ला)<BR>A large kind of Colotropis.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plantain: see रम्भा.<BR>E.<BR>का for कु small, अस्थि bone or stalk, and ला to get or possess; क and टाप् affix; having a stem which is good for nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
कास<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) कासृ (कासते)<BR>1 To make a bad sound, or one indicating disease; to cough.<BR>2 To shine: see काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कास|कासः
कास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Cough, catarrh.<BR>2 A species of reed or long grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>3 Morunga, (Hyperanthera, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>कास to cough, to make an unpleasant sound, अच् affix; also काश to shine, &c. see काश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासकुण्ठ|कासकुंठ|कासकुण्ठः
कासकुण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>Afflicted with cough.<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासघ्न|कासघ्नः
कासघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing or alleviating cough, pectoral.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A sort of prickly nightshade: see कण्ठकारी.<BR>E.<BR>कास catarrh, and घ्न from हन् to kill, removing cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासनाशिनी
कासनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A thorny plant: see कर्कटशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>कास catarrh, and नाशिनी removing, remedying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासुन्दीवटिका
कासुन्दीवटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An acid drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासमर्द्द|कासमर्द|कासमर्दः|कासमर्द्दः
कासमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 A plant, (Cassia or Senna esculenta.)<BR>2 An acid preparation, a mixture of tamarinds and mustard.<BR>E.<BR>काश or काश cough, and मर्द्द what destroys; also काशमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासमर्द्दन|कासमर्दन|कासमर्द्दनः
कासमर्द्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासर|कासरः
कासर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and आङ् prefixed to सृ to go, affix अप्; who frequents water, this animal being partial to marshy places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासार|कासारं|कासारः
कासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pond, a pool.<BR>E.<BR>क water, सृ to go, आङ् prefix, and घञ् affix, or कास to shine, आरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासारि|कासारिः
कासारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia esculenta): see कासमर्द्द.<BR>E.<BR>कास cough, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासालु|कासालुः
कासालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>An esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासीस|कासीसं
कासीस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Green vitriol, green sulphate of iron.<BR>E.<BR>कास to go, ईसण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासू
कासू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 Indistinct speech.<BR>2 Speech in general.<BR>3 Understanding.<BR>4 Devotion.<BR>5 Light, lustre.<BR>6 A sort of spear or lance.<BR>E.<BR>कस to go, to shine, or कास to make a bad sound, क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कासूतरी
कासूतरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A short spear, a javelin.<BR>E.<BR>कासू, and ष्टरच् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहका
काहका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A musical instrument: see काहला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहल|काहलं|काहलः
काहल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Dry, withered.<BR>2 Mischievous.<BR>3 Large, excessive.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 One of the Apsarasas or courtezans of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>2 The sound of any tube, pipe or musical instrument.<BR>(-ला)<BR>A young woman.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A horn, either a cow horn, or an instrument of that shape.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A cock.<BR>2 Sound in general.<BR>3 A cat.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Indistinct speech.<BR>adv.<BR>Much, excessively.<BR>E.<BR>क pleasure, the head, &c. हल to plough or divide, with आङ् prefixed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काहलापुष्प|काहलापुष्पः
काहलापुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कि
कि<BR>r. 3rd cl. (चिकेति)<BR>To know: with निर् prefixed, to attain certainly, to ascertain positively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किं
किं<BR>See किम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशारु|किंशारुः
किंशारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The beard of corn.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A heron.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, or sometimes, शृ to injure, &c. रुण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशुक|किंशुकः
किंशुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree bearing beautiful red blossoms, and hence often alluded to by the poets, (Butea frondosa); also पलाश. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">Page221</a>]<BR>E.<BR>किं what, something, शुक a parrot; its red flowers being of the colour of a parrot's beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=220" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किंशुलुक|किंशुलुकः
किंशुलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of the Kiṃśuka: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकि|किकिः
किकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>A blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>कि an imitative sound; the word being repeated: or कै to emit a sound, and कि affix; also किकीदीवि, किकी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकिदिवि|किकिदिविः
किकिदिवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>किकि an imitative sound, and दिव to play, कि affix; also in other forms किकि, किकिदिव, किकिदीवि, किकीदिवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकीदिव|किकीदिवः
किकीदिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किकीदीवि|किकीदीविः
किकीदीवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>See किकिदिवि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किखि|किखिः
किखि<BR>m. (-खिः)<BR>A monkey, an ape.<BR>f. (-खिः)<BR>A small jackal, a fox.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, डिखि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्कर|किंकर|किङ्करः
किङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>किं what or something, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किणि
किङ्किणि<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>1 A girdle of small bells, or any tinkling ornament.<BR>2 An acid sort of grape.<BR>E.<BR>किं some, and किण an imitative sound, affix क, with इन् or ङीष् fem. affix; also with कन् added किङ्किणीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किर|किंकिर|किङ्किरं|किंकिरः|किङ्किरः
किङ्किर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Indian cuckoo, the Koïl or Kokila.<BR>2 A large black bee.<BR>3 A horse.<BR>4 KĀMADEVA.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Blood.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The frontal sinus of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>किं something, कॄ to scatter, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किरात|किंकिरात|किंकिरातः|किङ्किरातः
किङ्किरात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>2 A parrot.<BR>3 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>4 A tree, (Jonesia asoka.)<BR>5 A species of barleria: see भिण्ठी.<BR>E.<BR>किङ्कर as above, and अत who goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किङ्किरिन्
किङ्किरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A plant, commonly Buïñci, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्च|किंच
किञ्च<BR>ind.<BR>1 An inceptive or continuative particle, (moreover, further, again.)<BR>3 A particle of comprehension.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, च and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चन|किंचन|किञ्चनः
किञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A species of the Palāśa or Butea frondosa.<BR>ind.<BR>Somewhat, something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चनता|किंचनता
किञ्चनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Somewhat, something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चित्|किंचित्
किञ्चित्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Something, somewhat.<BR>2 A part, a little.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, चित to think, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चिलिक|किंचिलिकः|किञ्चिलिकः
किञ्चिलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्चुलुक|किञ्चुलुकः
किञ्चुलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A worm.<BR>E.<BR>किञ्चित् a little, and चल to go, or चुल to be high, वुन् affix, deriv. irr.; it is sometimes written किञ्चिलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्ज|किंज|किंजं|किञ्जं
किञ्ज<BR>n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>The filament of a lotus: see किञ्जल्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्जल्क|किंजल्क|किञ्जल्कं|किंजल्कः|किञ्जल्कः
किञ्जल्क<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The filament of a lotus: see किञ्जल्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किञ्जल्क|किंजल्क|किञ्जल्कं|किंजल्कः|किञ्जल्कः
किञ्जल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>The filament of a lotus, great numbers of which surround the pericarp.<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>The flower of the Mesua ferrea.<BR>E.<BR>किञ्चित् somewhat, जक to hide or cover, क affix, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट
किट<BR>r. 1st cl. (केटति)<BR>1 To go or approach.<BR>2 To alarm or terrify.<BR>3 To dread, to fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटि|किटिः
किटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>किट to go, and कि affix; also किटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किटिभ|किटिभः
किटिभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>किटि a hog, भ who resembles, from भा to shine, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्ट|किट्टं
किट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Excrement, excretion, dirt.<BR>E.<BR>किट to go, here implying to go out of, (the body, &c.) and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टवर्जित|किट्टवर्ज्जित|किट्टवर्ज्जितं
किट्टवर्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Semen virile.<BR>E.<BR>किट्ट dirt, &c. यर्जित deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किट्टाल|किट्टालः
किट्टाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A copper vessel.<BR>2 Scoria, rust of iron, &c.<BR>E.<BR>किट्ट dirt, अल to be able, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण|किणः
किण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A wart, a mole.<BR>2 A scar.<BR>3 A corn, a callosity.<BR>4 An insect found in wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किणि|किणिः
किणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>A tree, (Achyranthes aspera): see अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>किण् a scar, and कि affix; making scars; that is cicatrizing wounds, sores, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किणिही
किणिही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>Achyranthes aspera.<BR>E.<BR>किणि a sore, and ह what removes, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किण्व|किण्वं|किण्वः
किण्व<BR>mn. (-ण्वः-ण्वं)<BR>Ferment, a drug or seed used to produce fermentation, in the manufacture of spirits from sugar, bassia, &c.<BR>n. (-ण्वं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कण to sound, &c. क्वन् Uṇādi affix, and the इ irregularly inserted: see कण्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कित
कित<BR>r. 1st cl. (चिकित्सति)<BR>1 To cure, to administer remedies, to practise physic.<BR>2 To remove, to destroy.<BR>3 To chastise.<BR>4 (Usually with वि prefixed,) To doubt; this root is regular.<BR>r. 3rd cl. (चिकेति)<BR>To know.<BR>r. 10th cl. (केतयति)<BR>1 To dwell.<BR>2 To desire; some authorities make it a regular root of the 1st cl. in these senses, and others deny its admitting of any conjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कितव|कितवः
कितव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 A gamester, a gambler.<BR>2 A cheat, cheating, fraudulent.<BR>3 Mad, crazy.<BR>4 Mischievous, malicious.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>2 A kind of perfume, commonly Rocanā.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, तव yours, (what is your stake or wager?) he who asks such a question, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तनु|किंतनु|किन्तनुः
किन्तनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>An insect described as having eight legs and a very slender body, a species of spider.<BR>E.<BR>किं for किञ्चित् a little, and तनु the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तमाम्|किंतमाम्
किन्तमाम्<BR>ind.<BR>Whether, either of any.<BR>E.<BR>किं, and तरप् with आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तराम्|किंतराम्
किन्तराम्<BR>ind.<BR>Whether, either of two.<BR>E.<BR>किं, and तरप् with आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तु|किंतु
किन्तु<BR>ind.<BR>1 But.<BR>2 Moreover, further.<BR>E.<BR>A compound particle of किं and तु disjunctive particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्तुघ्न|किंतुघ्न|किन्तुघ्नः
किन्तुघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>One of the eleven periods called Karaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्धिन्|किंधिन्
किन्धिन्<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>A horse: see किल्किन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नर|किंनर|किन्नरः
किन्नर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A demigod attached to the service of KUVERA, a celestial quirister or musician.<BR>2 A kind of follower or attendant on a Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female Kinnara, or chorister.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, used contemptuously, (what kind of) नर a man: the Kinnara having, with the human figure, the head of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नरेश|किंनरेश|किन्नरेशः
किन्नरेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>किन्नर a Kinnara, and ईश master, lord; also other similar compounds, as किन्नरेश्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किन्नु|किंनु
किन्नु<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of interrogation, (what?)<BR>2 Doubt, (how, what?)<BR>3 Comparison, (thus, as, like, how much less.)<BR>4 Conjunction, (again, further.)<BR>5 Place, location, and<BR>6 Agency.<BR>E.<BR>किम्, and नु conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्
किम्<BR>ind. (किम् or किं)<BR>1 What, how.<BR>2 Either, or; a particle of doubt or interrogation.<BR>3 A particle of contempt.<BR>The relative pronoun. mfn. (-कः-का-किं)<BR>What, who, which, expressing,<BR>1 Doubt.<BR>2 Interrogation.<BR>3 Disdain.<BR>4 Reproach, (as [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">Page222</a>] in English, Who are you, &c.)<BR>5 Kind, sort.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, डिमि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=221" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमर्थम्
किमर्थम्<BR>ind.<BR>What for, wherefore, why.<BR>E.<BR>किम्, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमु
किमु<BR>ind.<BR>Either, or, whether, implying doubt or discrimination: see किम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किमुत
किमुत<BR>ind.<BR>1 Either, or, whether, implying.<BR>2 Doubt or discrimination.<BR>3 Much, exceeding; a particle of magnitude or quantity.<BR>4 An interrogative, how, what, &c. see किम्.<BR>E.<BR>किम् and the particle उत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पच|किंपच|किम्पचः
किम्पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Miserly, avaricious.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, (nothing,) पच who cooks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पचान|किंपचान|किम्पचानः
किम्पचान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Miserly, niggardly, avaricious.<BR>E.<BR>किं what, used contemptuously, पच to cook, and शानच् affix, or with अच् only, किम्पचः see मितम्पच, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पाक|किंपाक|किम्पाकः
किम्पाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Mother-led, infantine, childish.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cucurbitaceous plant, (Trichosanthes palmata; also Cucumis colocynthus.)<BR>E.<BR>किं depreciative, and पाक what is ripe or mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुष|किंपुरुष|किम्पुरुषः
किम्पुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A heavenly musician: see किन्नर.<BR>2 A division of the universe, one of the nine Khaṇḍas or portions into which the world is divided, and described as the country between the Himācala and Hemakūṭa mountains.<BR>3 A despicable or low man.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, contemptuously, and पुरुष a man; also with the first vowel of that word lengthened, किम्पूरुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पुरुषेश्वर|किंपुरुषेश्वर|किम्पुरुषेश्वरः
किम्पुरुषेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An epithet of KUVERA: see किन्नरेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्पूरुष|किंपूरुष|किम्पूरुषं
किम्पूरुष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The division of the world, called by this name: see किम्पुरुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्भरा|किंभरा
किम्भरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Nali: see नली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्भूत|किंभूत
किम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) or n. only, (-तं)<BR>How, in what manner or degree, like what.<BR>E.<BR>किम्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्वत्
किम्वत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Poor, mean, insignificant.<BR>E.<BR>किं a little, मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्वदन्ति
किम्वदन्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Rumour, report.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, वद to say, and झिच् Uṇādi affix, or with झच् and ङीष् affixes किम्वदन्ती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किम्वा
किम्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Or, else, moreover.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, वा or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियत्|कियन्त्
कियत्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यती-यत्)<BR>1 How much, how many.<BR>ind. (यत्)<BR>1 A little.<BR>2 How much, used chiefly in composition; as कियत्काल how long, for a short time; कियदवधि or कियत्यर्य्यन्तं how far, or for a little way.<BR>E.<BR>किम् and वतुप् affix, and य is substituted for the व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियदेतिका
कियदेतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Effort, vigorous and persevering exertions.<BR>E.<BR>कियत् used contemptuously, and इति from इदम् this, affix ठक्; (how great a task is this, that it should not be effected, &c.) इह here, being employed in place of इति, the word is written कियदेहिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियद्दूर
कियद्दूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>For a short distance, a little way.<BR>E.<BR>कियत, and दूर far.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कियाह|कियाहः
कियाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of a red or bay colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर|किरः
किर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, क affix; also किरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरक|किरकः
किरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A scribe.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरण|किरणः
किरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A ray of light, a sun or moon beam.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>क to scatter, (light,) and क्यु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणमय
किरणमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Radiant, bright, refulgent.<BR>E.<BR>किरण and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरणमालिन्
किरणमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>किरण, माला a garland, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरत्
किरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Scattering, spreading.<BR>2 Lighting, shedding light.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरात|किरातः
किरात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A savage, one of the barbarous tribes who inhabit woods and mountains and live by the chase, the Kirrhadoe of Arrian.<BR>2 ŚIVA as a mountaineer opposed to ARJUNA, the account of which is the subject of the poem, the Kirātārjunīya.<BR>3 A kind of gentian: see किराततिक्त.<BR>4 A pigmy, a dwarf.<BR>5 A groom, a horseman.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The river GAṄGES or its goddess.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 A bawd, a procuress.<BR>4 The celestial GAṄGES or river of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, (speech, &c.) and अत who goes; also किरातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराततिक्त|किराततिक्तः
किराततिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR>E.<BR>किरात a savage, तिक्त pungent, bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराताशिन्
किराताशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A name of GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>किरात a pigmy, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किराति|किरातिः
किराति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A name of the GAṄGES.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, (sound, &c.) to make a murmuring noise, अत who goes, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरातिनी
किरातिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Indian spikenard; see जटामांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरि|किरिः
किरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, (dirt, &c.) and इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरिटि|किरिटिः
किरिटि<BR>n. (-टिः)<BR>The fruit of the marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीट|किरीटं|किरीटः
किरीट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>A crest, a diadem.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, (pearls, &c.) and कीटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटधारण
किरीटधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Wearing a tiara, assuming the crown.<BR>E.<BR>किरीट, and धारण bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटधारिन्
किरीटधारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Crowned, having a tiara.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>किरीट, and धारिन् who wears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किरीटिन्
किरीटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>Crested, crowned.<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>1 A king.<BR>9 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>किरीट a crest, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मी|किर्मी
किर्म्मी<BR>f. (-र्म्मी)<BR>The Palāśa tree: see पलाश.<BR>2 A hall, a building, an apartment.<BR>3 An image of gold.<BR>4 A figure of iron.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, मन् and ङीप् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीर|किर्मीर|किर्मीरः|किर्म्मीरः
किर्म्मीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Variegated.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The orange tree.<BR>2 The name of a Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>3 A variegated colour.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, ईरन् affix; and मुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरजित्|किर्मीरजित्
किर्म्मीरजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of BHĪMASENA one of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>किर्म्मीर a demon, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरत्वच्|किर्मीरत्वच्
किर्म्मीरत्वच्<BR>f. (-त्वक्)<BR>The orange tree.<BR>E.<BR>किर्म्मीर variegated, and त्वच् bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरभिद्
किर्म्मीरभिद्<BR>m. (-भित् or -भिद्)<BR>A name of BHĪMA: see किर्म्मीरजित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किर्म्मीरसूदन|किर्मीरसूदन|किर्मीरसूदनः|किर्म्मीरसूदनः
किर्म्मीरसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of BHĪMA: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल<BR>r. 6th cl. (किलति)<BR>1 To be or become white.<BR>2 To play.<BR>r. 10th cl. (केलयति)<BR>To send, to throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल|किलः
किल<BR>ind.<BR>An aptote signifying,<BR>1 News, (so said, so reported.)<BR>2 Likelihood, (probably, possibly.)<BR>3 Conciliatory expression.<BR>4 Assertion, certainty, (indeed, verily, assuredly.)<BR>5 Falsehood, inaccuracy.<BR>E.<BR>किल to send or order, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिञ्चित|किलकिंचित|किलकिञ्चितं
किलकिञ्चित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Amorous agitation, weeping, laughing, being angry, being pleased, &c. in the society of a lover.<BR>E.<BR>किल play, sport, किं what, some, and चित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=222" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलकिला
किलकिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Sound expressing joy, or the expression of pleasure by any sound or cry.<BR>E.<BR>किल play, sport, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाट|किलाटः
किलाट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>Inspissated milk, curds or coagulated milk; it may be applied to cheese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलाटिन्
किलाटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलास|किलासं
किलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A blotch, a scab.<BR>2 A white leprous spot.<BR>E.<BR>किल to play, affix क; आस from आस to reject or throw, with अच् affix; or अस to be, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासघ्न|किलासघ्नः
किलासघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A sort of gourd, (Momordica mixta): see काकरोल.<BR>E.<BR>किलास a blotch, and घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलासिन्
किलासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Having blotches.<BR>E.<BR>किलास, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्च|किलिञ्चं
किलिञ्च<BR>mn. (-ञ्चः-ञ्चं)<BR>A thin plank: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्ज|किलिंज|किलिंजं|किलिञ्जः
किलिञ्ज<BR>mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>1 A thin plank of green wood.<BR>2 A mat: see the next; also read किलिञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिञ्जक|किलिंजकः|किलिञ्जकः
किलिञ्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mat.<BR>2 A screen or twist of grass or straw.<BR>E.<BR>किल to be white, इ added किलि, ज what overcomes, from जि with ड affix, and वुन् added; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किलिम|किलिमं
किलिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, a kind of fir or pine, (Pinus deodar.)<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Resin, the extract of the pine.<BR>E.<BR>किल to cast, किमन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विन्
किल्विन्<BR>m. (-ल्वी)<BR>A horse; read also किन्धिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विष|किल्विषं
किल्विष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Fault, offence.<BR>3 Disease, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>किल to play or sport, टिषच् Uṇādi affix, and वुक inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किल्विषिन्
किल्विषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Wicked, culpable, criminal.<BR>E.<BR>किल्विष, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशल|किशलं
किशल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A sprout, a shoot: see किसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलय|किशलयं|किशलयः
किशलय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>A young shoot: see किसलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशलयतल्प
किशलयतल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>A bed of young leaves, &c.<BR>E.<BR>किशलय, and तल्प a couch; also किशलयशय्या, किशलयशयनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किशोर|किशोरः
किशोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Young, infantine.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A colt.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 Benjamin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR>4 A youth, a lad, one from his birth to the end of his fifteenth year: a minor in law अजातव्यवहारः becoming, after his fifteenth year, subject to suits at law or जातव्यवहार.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, used contemptuously, शृ to go, and ओरन् Uṇādi affix; also कन् added किशोरकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्क
किष्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (किष्कयते)<BR>To kill, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध|किष्किंध|किष्किंधः|किष्किन्धः
किष्किन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A mountain in the south of India, in Mysore, the residence of the monkey prince BĀLĪ.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A cave in the mountain; also किष्किन्ध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्य|किष्किंध्य|किष्किंध्यः|किष्किन्ध्यः
किष्किन्ध्य<BR>m. (-न्ध्यः)<BR>The mountain Kiṣkindhya, situated in the peninsula in the northern part of Mysore, near the sources of the Pampā river, the territory of BĀLĪ the monkey, from whom it was conquered by RĀMA, and transferred to SUGRĪVA, another monkey chief.<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>A cave in the mountain of Kiṣkindhya, the peculiar residence of BĀLĪ; also किष्किन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्किन्ध्याधिप|किष्किन्ध्याधिपः
किष्किन्ध्याधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of BĀLĪ, a monkey king slain by RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>किष्किन्ध्य, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कु|किष्कुः
किष्कु<BR>mfn. (-ष्कुः-ष्कुः-ष्कु)<BR>Vile, bad, contemptible.<BR>mf. (-ष्कुः)<BR>1 A cubit.<BR>2 A span.<BR>3 The fore-arm.<BR>E.<BR>कै to sound, डिष्कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किष्कुपर्व्वन्|किष्कुपर्वन्
किष्कुपर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 Sugar cane.<BR>2 A bamboo.<BR>3 A reed, (Arundo tibialis.)<BR>E.<BR>किष्कु a span or cubit, and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसल|किसलं|किसलः
किसल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A sprout or shoot, the extremity of a branch bearing new leaves.<BR>E.<BR>किं diminutive, सल to go, अच affix; also किशल and किसलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

किसलय|किसलयं|किसलयः
किसलय<BR>m. (-यः-यं)<BR>A sprout, a young shoot: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, affix कयञ्; also किशलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकट|कीकटः
कीकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>1 Miserly, avaricious.<BR>2 Poor, needy.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A country, (Behar); or<BR>m. plu. (-टाः)<BR>its inhabitants.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>ककि to go, अटच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकस|कीकसं|कीकसः
कीकस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Hard, firm.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>A bone.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A worm, an insect.<BR>E.<BR>की derived from किम् what, a depreciating particle, before कस to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकसास्य|कीकसास्यः
कीकसास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>कीकस a bone, and आस्य face or mouth; alluding to the osseous structure of the beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीकि|कीकिः
कीकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>A blue jay: see किकि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचक|कीचकः
कीचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bamboo whistling or rattling in the wind.<BR>2 Any hollow bamboo.<BR>3 A reed.<BR>4 A Daitya or infernal demon so named.<BR>5 A particular Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>6 A kind of tree.<BR>7 A prince, the son of KEKAYA.<BR>E.<BR>चीक to touch, to sound, वुन् Uṇādi affix, and the radical consonants transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकजित्
कीचकजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>कीचक a goblin, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकनिसूदन|कीचकनिसूदनः
कीचकनिसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BHĪMA: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीचकभिद्
कीचकभिद्<BR>m. (-भित्)<BR>See the two words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट<BR>r. 11th cl. (कीटयति)<BR>1 To tinge or colour.<BR>2 To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीट|कीटः
कीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A worm, an insect.<BR>E.<BR>कीट to colour or dye, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटक|कीटकः
कीटक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Harsh, hard, unfeeling.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A worm, an insect.<BR>2 A bard, a panegyrist, descended from a Kṣatriya father and Vaiśya mother.<BR>E.<BR>कीट a worm, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटघ्न|कीटघ्नः
कीटघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>कीट a worm, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटज
कीटज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Silk.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Lac, an animal dye of a red colour.<BR>E.<BR>कीट a worm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटपक्षोद्भव
कीटपक्षोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The change from the chrysalis or larva to the butterfly.<BR>E.<BR>कीट, पक्ष a wing, and उद्भव evolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीटपादिका
कीटपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीदृश्
कीदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Who or what like.<BR>E.<BR>किम् what, दृश to see, and क्विन् affix; also with कञ् affix; कीदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीनाश|कीनाशः
कीनाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 A labourer or cultivator of the soil.<BR>2 Small, little.<BR>3 Covetous, niggardly.<BR>4 A slayer of cattle.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA.<BR>2 A particular monkey.<BR>E.<BR>की for का or कु bad, vile, नाश who destroys, the causal form of नश to destroy, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर|कीरं|कीरः
कीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A parrot.<BR>2 Kashmir.<BR>m. plu. (-राः)<BR>The people of Kashmir.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>की bad, vile, ईर to send or order, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरक|कीरकः
कीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A Buddha.<BR>3 Obtaining, gaining.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरेष्ट|कीरेष्टः
कीरेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A tree, a species of mountain Pīlu: see अक्षोड.<BR>2 The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>कीर a parrot, and इष्ट wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्ण|कीर्णः|कीर्ण्ण
कीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Covered, secreted, hidden.<BR>2 Scattered, thrown, cast.<BR>3 Injured, hurt.<BR>4 Full.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, affix क्त, formation irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्णि|कीर्णिः|कीर्ण्णि
कीर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 Scattering, throwing.<BR>2 Covering, concealing.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तन|कीर्तन|कीर्तनं|कीर्त्तनं
कीर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Saying, telling.<BR>2 Repeating.<BR>3 Celebrating, praising.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Fame, glory.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to praise or celebrate, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=223" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तयत्|कीर्तयत्
कीर्त्तयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Praising, celebrating.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to praise, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्ति|कीर्ति|कीर्तिः|कीर्त्तिः
कीर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Fame, renown, glory.<BR>2 Favour, approbation.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>4 Light, lustre.<BR>5 Mud, dirt.<BR>6 Diffusing, expansion.<BR>7 One of the Mātṛkās or personified divine energies of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to celebrate, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिकर|कीर्तिकर
कीर्त्तिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Conferring fame.<BR>E.<BR>कीर्त्ति, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तित|कीर्तित|कीर्त्तितः
कीर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, asserted.<BR>2 Known, notorious.<BR>3 Celebrated, praised.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to celebrate, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिभाज्|कीर्तिभाज्
कीर्त्तिभाज्<BR>mfn. (भाक्)<BR>Celebrated, famous.<BR>m. (-भाक्)<BR>A name of DROṆĀCĀRYA, the military preceptor of the PĀṆḌUS and KURUS.<BR>E.<BR>कीर्त्ति fame, and भाज to serve or honour, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिमत्|कीर्तिमत्|कीर्तिमन्त्
कीर्त्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Praised, famous, celebrated.<BR>n. (-मान्)<BR>The elder brother of VASUDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>कीर्त्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्तिशेष|कीर्तिशेष|कीर्तिशेषः|कीर्त्तिशेषः
कीर्त्तिशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>कीर्त्ति fame, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्त्त्य
कीर्त्त्य<BR>mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>To be praised or celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to praise, क्यप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्म्मी|कीर्मी
कीर्म्मी<BR>f. (-र्म्मी)<BR>A house for straw; also हेमपुत्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्य्यमाण|कीर्यमाण
कीर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Covered, bestrewed.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, passive form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील|कीलः
कील<BR>r. 10th cl. (कीलयति)<BR>To bind, to fasten, to stake, to pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील|कीलः
कील<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>1 Flame, lambent flame.<BR>2 Small, minute.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A stake, a pin, a bolt, a wedge, &c.<BR>9 A lance, a pike.<BR>2 A gnomon.<BR>4 A weapon.<BR>5 A post, a pillar.<BR>6 The elbow.<BR>7 A blow or punch with the elbow.<BR>8 A blow, a thump; (in the three last senses some make this also fem.)<BR>9 A post in a cow-house: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कील to bind, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलक|कीलकः
कीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pillar for cows, &c. to rub themselves against, or one to which they are tied.<BR>2 A pin, a bolt, a wedge.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलसंस्पर्श|कीलसंस्पर्शः
कीलसंस्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>A plant, the fruit of which yields a turpentinous substance that has been used in India as pitch, &c. commonly Gab; (Embryopteris glutinifera, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कील a bolt, सम् with, and स्पर्श touch, the fruit being invested with a hard coat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलाल|कीलालं|कीलालः
कीलाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Blood.<BR>3 Amṛta, the food of the gods.<BR>4 Honey.<BR>E.<BR>कील flame, and अल what opposes, &c. or कील a stake, &c. and अल what adorns; from अल् with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलालधि|कीलालधिः
कीलालधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>कीलाल water, and धि what contains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलालप|कीलालपः
कीलालप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a sort of goblin or imp.<BR>E.<BR>कीलाल blood, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलित|कीलितः
कीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bound, tied, confined.<BR>2 Pierced, transfixed.<BR>3 Staked, impaled.<BR>4 Pinned, fastened by a stake, &c.<BR>5 Set up as a stake or pole.<BR>E.<BR>कील to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीश|कीशः
कीश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Naked.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A monkey, an ape.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>क air, water, &c., ईश who has power over, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीशपर्ण|कीशपर्णः|कीशपर्ण्ण
कीशपर्ण<BR>mf. (-र्णः-र्णी)<BR>A tree, (Achyranthes aspera): see अपामार्गः also कीशपर्णक. m. (कः)<BR>E.<BR>कीश a monkey, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु<BR>r. 1st cl. (ङ) कुङ् (कवते) r. 2nd cl. (टु) टुकु (कौति) r. 6th cl. (शिं) कुशि (कुवते) r. 9th cl. (ञ) कुञ (कुनाति कुनीते.)<BR>1 To sound, to sound indistinctly, to moan, to groan.<BR>2 To cry as a bird, to coo, to hum as a bee, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु<BR>f. (-कुः)<BR>The earth.<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of depreciation, and implying,<BR>1 Sin, guilt.<BR>2 Reproach, contempt.<BR>3 Diminution, littleness.<BR>4 Prevention, hindrance, as कुपथ a bad road, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, क्विप् affix, or कुङ to sound, with the affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक
कुक<BR>r. 1st cl. (कोकते)<BR>To take, to accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक
कुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Taking, accepting.<BR>E.<BR>कुक and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकभ|कुकभं
कुकभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर|कुकरः
कुकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Having a crooked or withered arm.<BR>2 Wicked, acting wickedly.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and कर the hand; or कृ to do, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर्म्मन्|कुकर्मन्
कुकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Wicked, bad.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Wickedness, depravity, villainy.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकर्म्मकारिन्|कुकर्मकारिन्
कुकर्म्मकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wicked, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>कुकर्म्म, and कारिन् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकील|कुकीलः
कुकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>कु earth, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुद|कुकुदः
कुकुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who gives a girl, decorated with fit ornaments and with the prescribed ceremonies, in marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to take, and द who gives: see कूकुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुन्दर|कुकुंदर|कुकुन्दरं|कुकुंदरः|कुकुन्दरः
कुकुन्दर<BR>n. (-रं) or n. du. (-रे)<BR>The cavities of the loins.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्दर a hollow, a cave, from कु the earth, and दृ to rend or tear, कु bad, vile, prefixed; it is also written ककुन्दर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुभा
कुकुभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>One of the female personifications of music or Rāgiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुर|कुकुरः
कुकुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A branch of the Yadu race: see कुक्कुर.<BR>3 A plant and perfume: see ग्रन्थपर्णी.<BR>m. plu. (-राः)<BR>A country: see दशार्ह.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to take, उरच् Uṇādi affix; also कुक्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुराधिनाथ
कुकुराधिनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कुकुर a Yadu, and अधिनाथ chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूणक
कुकूणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Weakness of the eyes in infants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूल|कुकूलं|कुकूलः
कुकूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A hole filled with stakes.<BR>2 Conflagration of chaff.<BR>3 Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and कूल a bank, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकृत्य
कुकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Wickedness, evil.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and कृत्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकोल|कुकोलं
कुकोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The jujube: see कोलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुट|कुक्कुटः
कुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A cock.<BR>2 A wild cock.<BR>3 The offspring of a Śūdra or man of the fourth caste, by a Caṇḍāla woman.<BR>4 A whisp of lighted straw, a firebrand.<BR>5 A spark of fire.<BR>f. (-टिः or -टी)<BR>Hypocrisy, interested observance of religious duties.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A hen.<BR>2 A small house lizard.<BR>3 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>E.<BR>कुक् taking, from कुक with क्विप् affix, and कुट to cut or scratch, with क affix; scratching up the earth, &c. or कु bad, कुट to cut, &c. and क inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटक|कुक्कुटकः
कुक्कुटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cock.<BR>2 A wild cock.<BR>3 A man of a mixed caste, one sprung from a Śūdra and the female of a barbarian.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटमण्डप|कुक्कुटमण्डपः
कुक्कुटमण्डप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A place where final emancipation may be attained; also मुक्तिमण्डप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटमस्तक|कुक्कुटमस्तकं|कुक्कुटमस्तकः
कुक्कुटमस्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुट, and मस्तक head; to what the flower may be compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटव्रत|कुक्कुटव्रतं
कुक्कुटव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A religious observation, (worship of ŚIVA,) on the seventh of the light fortnight of Bhadra, by women, especially [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">Page225</a>] for the sake of obtaining offspring.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुट a fowl, and व्रत religious rite; alluding to the fruitfulness of the hen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=224" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटशिख|कुक्कुटशिखः
कुक्कुटशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुट a cock, and शिख a crest; cockscomb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाण्ड
कुक्कुटाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A fowl's egg.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुटी, and अण्ड an egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाभ|कुक्कुटाभः
कुक्कुटाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A kind of snake, compared to a fowl, in some respects, perhaps from having a crest or comb.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुट a cock, and आभ who is or resembles, from भा to shine, prefix आङ् and affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटाहि|कुक्कुटाहिः
कुक्कुटाहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A kind of snake: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुभ|कुक्कुभः
कुक्कुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A wild cock, (Phasianus gallus.)<BR>2 Varnish, oiling or oily gloss; also कुक्कुभक. m. (-कः)<BR>E.<BR>कुक् imitative sound, कु to utter sound, and भक् irr. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुर|कुक्कुरं|कुक्कुरः
कुक्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A dog.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A vegetable perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla: see ग्रंथिपर्णी.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to take, उरन् Uṇādi affix, and क inserted; also कुकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुवाच्
कुक्कुवाच्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>A sort of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्ष|कुक्षः
कुक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The belly.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to extract, and सः affix; by which the foeces are excreted; also कुक्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षि|कुक्षिः
कुक्षि<BR>m. (-क्षिः)<BR>The belly, the cavity of the abdomen.<BR>E.<BR>कुषि to extract, and क्मि affix; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिम्भरि|कुक्षिंभरि|कुक्षिम्भरिः
कुक्षिम्भरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Voracious, gluttonous, filling or pampering the belly.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्षि the belly, भृ to nourish, affix स्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिरन्ध्र|कुक्षिरन्ध्रः
कुक्षिरन्ध्र<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>A reed.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्षि, and रब्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुख्याति
कुख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Evil report, infamy.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुम|कुंकुम|कुंकुमं|कुङ्कुमं
कुङ्कुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Saffron, (Crocus sativus.)<BR>E.<BR>कुकि to take, and उमक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमताम्र
कुङ्कुमताम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>Red, coppery red.<BR>E.<BR>कुङ्कुम, and ताम्र copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमरेणु
कुङ्कुमरेणु<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>The dust or pollen of saffron.<BR>E.<BR>कुङ्कम, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमाक्त
कुङ्कुमाक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Dyed or stained with saffron, orange, yellow.<BR>E.<BR>कुङ्कुम, and अक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमाक्त
कुङ्कुमाक्त<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Marked with saffron, dyed or stained of an orange colour.<BR>E.<BR>कुङ्कुम, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुङ्कुमारुण
कुङ्कुमारुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Red, ruddy.<BR>E.<BR>कुङ्गुम, and अरुण purple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच|कुचः
कुच<BR>r. 1st cl. (कोचति)<BR>1 To sound high, to utter a loud, shrill cry, as a bird.<BR>2 To go.<BR>3 To polish.<BR>4 To touch.<BR>5 To furrow or mark with lines.<BR>6 To be crooked.<BR>7 To write.<BR>8 To oppose.<BR>9 To contend.<BR>10 To be restricted or confined, to contract.<BR>r. 6th cl. (शि) शिकुच. (कुचति) or with सं prefixed, (संकोचति or संकुचति)<BR>1 To straiten, to narrow or contract.<BR>2 To be straitened, to shrink, to contract.<BR>With उत्<BR>to bribe;<BR>with वि and आ,<BR>to expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच|कुचः
कुच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A breast, a pap.<BR>E.<BR>कुच to bind or confine, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचकुम्भ|कुचकुम्भः
कुचकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>कुच, and कुम्भ vase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचण्डिका
कुचण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides): see मूर्व्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचतट
कुचतट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>कुच, and तट bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचतटाग्र
कुचतटाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>कुचतट, and अग्र tip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचन्दन
कुचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santolinus.)<BR>2 Sappan or log wood: see पत्राङ्ग.<BR>3 Saffron.<BR>4 A leguminous plant, (Adenanthera pavonina.)<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, inferior, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचफल|कुचफलः
कुचफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>कुच, and फल fruit of the shape of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचर|कुचरः
कुचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Censorious, detracting.<BR>2 Following evil practices, low, vile, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचर्य्या|कुचर्या
कुचर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Impropriety, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, चर्य्या practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचाग्र|कुचाग्रं
कुचाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>कुच a breast, and अग्र point, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचाङ्गेरी
कुचाङ्गेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha): see चाङ्गेरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचिक|कुचिकः
कुचिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A kind of fish, in shape like an eel, commonly Kunchiya, (Unibranchapertura Cuchiya, Ham.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचित
कुचित<BR>mf. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Closed, contracted.<BR>2 Measured.<BR>E.<BR>कुच to contract, कितच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचेल|कुचेलः
कुचेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Ill clothed, dressed in dirty or tattered garments.<BR>f. (-लः-ली)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra): see विद्धकर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and चेला a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच्छ|कुच्छं
कुच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>The white water lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज|कुजः
कुज<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) कुजु (कोजति)<BR>1 To steal or rob.<BR>(इ) कुजि (कुञ्जति)<BR>To sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज|कुजः
कुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 A demon; also called Naraka.<BR>3 A tree.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 Of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and ज born, earth-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भल|कुजंभलः|कुजम्भलः
कुजम्भल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A housebreaker; also कुजम्भिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुजम्भिल|कुजंभिल|कुजंभिलः|कुजम्भिलः
कुजम्भिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A thief, a housebreaker; also कुजम्भल and कुजम्भर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्जिश|कुज्जिशः
कुज्जिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झटि|कुज्झटिः
कुज्झटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>A fog or mist.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and झट to be entangled, affix कि; also कुञ्झटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुज्झटिका
कुज्झटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fog or mist: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्च
कुञ्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) कुञ्चु (कुंचति)<BR>1 To go, to go to or towards.<BR>2 To move crookedly.<BR>3 To make crooked.<BR>4 To be crooked.<BR>5 To lessen, to make small.<BR>6 To be or become small, to shrink as a substance.<BR>7 To contract or draw in, (as the thoughts.) Some read this root कुचि, but needlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चन|कुंचन|कुंचनं|कुञ्चनं
कुञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Curving, bending.<BR>2 Contracting.<BR>3 Contraction of the eyelids.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्च to go crookedly, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चि|कुंचि|कुंचिः|कुञ्चिः
कुञ्चि<BR>f. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>A measure of quantity equal to eight handfuls.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्च to be curved, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चिका|कुंचिका
कुञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant bearing a red and black seed, used as a weight, (Abrus precatorius): see गुञ्जा.<BR>2 The branch or shoot of a bamboo.<BR>3 A plant bearing a pungent seed, (Nigella Indica): see कृष्णजीरक.<BR>4 A fish, commonly Cunchiya, in shape like an eel and eaten as one, (Unibranchapertura cunchiya.)<BR>5 A key.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्च to go crookedly, &c. क्वुन् affix, with the fem. termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्चित|कुंचित|कुञ्चितं
कुञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Crooked, curved, bent.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्च to go crookedly, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्ज|कुंज|कुंजं|कुंजः|कुञ्जः
कुञ्ज<BR>mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>1 A place overgrown with creeping plants, a bower, an arbour.<BR>2 An elephant's tusk or ivory.<BR>3 The lower jaw.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and ज produced, म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जकुटीर|कुंजकुटीर|कुञ्जकुटीरः
कुञ्जकुटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bower, an arbour.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्ज, and कुटीर a small house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जर|कुंजर|कुंजरः|कुञ्जरः
कुञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 (In composition,) Preeminent, as पुरुषकुञ्जर an excellent man.<BR>3 Hair.<BR>4 A country.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>(-रा)<BR>1 A plant, (Bignonia suave-olens.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">Page226</a>]<BR>2 A shrub, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्ज a tusk, an arbour, &c. and र what forms or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=225" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जरपिप्पली
कुञ्जरपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant described as bearing a fruit which resembles long pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जराराति|कुंजराराति|कुञ्जरारातिः
कुञ्जराराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The Śarabha, a fabulous animal.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्जर an elephant, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जरालुक|कुञ्जरालुकं
कुञ्जरालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A species of esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जराशन|कुंजराशन|कुञ्जराशनः
कुञ्जराशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्जर an elephant, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जल|कुंजलं|कुञ्जलं
कुञ्जल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sour gruel: see काञ्जिक.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and जल water, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुञ्जिका
कुञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Kalonji, (Nigella Indica): see कुञ्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट<BR>(शि) r. 6th cl. (कुटति)<BR>1 To make crooked.<BR>2 To be or become crooked.<BR>3 To be dishonest, to cheat or deceive.<BR>(इ) कुटि (कुण्टति)<BR>1 To be stopped or obstructed, to be prevented from moving.<BR>2 To confound or disorder from pain or grief: see कुडि<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुटयते कोटयति)<BR>1 To cut: see त्रुट.<BR>2 To heat: see कुट्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट|कुटं|कुटः
कुट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 A water pot.<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A house; also कुटि.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A fort, a strong hold.<BR>2 A tree: see कुठ.<BR>6 A hammer, a mallet for breaking small stones.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A kind of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>2 A bawd, a procuress or go-between.<BR>3 A nosegay, a bundle or tuft of flowers or vegetables.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ to go crookedly, &c. कः aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्क|कुटंक|कुटंकः|कुटङ्कः
कुटङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A roof, a thatch.<BR>E.<BR>कुट a house, in the third case, and क what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटङ्गक|कुटंगक|कुटंगकः|कुटङ्गकः
कुटङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An arbour formed by creeping plants overrunning a tree.<BR>2 A roof or thatch.<BR>3 A house, a small house, a hut or cottage: see कुटुङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटच|कुटचः
कुटच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>Coraya: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटज|कुटजः
कुटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Coraya, (Echites antidysenterica, Rox.) the seeds are used as a vermifuge: see इन्द्रयव.<BR>2 A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>3 Also of DROṆA a sage and warrior: see द्रोण.<BR>E.<BR>कूट a mountain peak, and ज what is produced; the vowel of कूट being made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटन्नक
कुटन्नक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant grass: see मुस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटन्नट|कुटन्नटं|कुटन्नटः
कुटन्नट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>कुटन् being crooked, नट to dance or wave, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटप|कुटपः
कुटप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A saint, a divine sage or Muni.<BR>2 A garden or grove near a house.<BR>3 A measure of grain, &c. see कुडप.<BR>(-पं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कुट a house, and प what nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटर|कुटरं|कुटरः
कुटर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A post round which the string passes that works the churning stick: see कुठर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटरु|कुटरुः
कुटरु<BR>n. (-रु)<BR>A tent, a house of cloth or canvas.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, अरु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटरुणा
कुटरुणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटल|कुटलं
कुटल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A roof, a thatch: see कुटङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटहारिका
कुटहारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female slave or servant.<BR>E.<BR>कुट a water pot, and हारिका who carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटि|कुटिः
कुटि<BR>mf. (-टिः-टिः or -टी)<BR>A house.<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 Curvature, a curve.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिचर|कुटिचरः
कुटिचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>कुटि a curve, चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटित|कुटितं
कुटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Crooked, bent.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be curved, इतः Uṇādi affix; also कुटिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटितृ
कुटितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Being bent.<BR>2 Acting dishonestly.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिर|कुटिरं
कुटिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A hut, a cottage.<BR>E.<BR>कुटि a house, रा to be like, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिल|कुटिलं
कुटिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Crooked, bent.<BR>2 Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Tin.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The name of a river, the Kuṭilā river, according to some, a name of the SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, किलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलगामिन्
कुटिलगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Tortuous, going crookedly.<BR>E.<BR>कुटिल, and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलता
कुटिलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Crookedness.<BR>2 Guile, dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>कुटिल and तस्र् affix; also with त्व, कुटिलत्वं. n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटिलिका
कुटिलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A blacksmith's forge.<BR>2 Crouching, coming stealthily as a hunter on his prey.<BR>E.<BR>कुटिल, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीचक|कुटीचकः
कुटीचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who lives at his son's expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीचर|कुटीचरः
कुटीचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ascetic of a particular order, one who consigns the care of his family to his son, and remains at home engaged solely in devotion.<BR>E.<BR>कुटी a house, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटीर|कुटीरं|कुटीरः
कुटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small house, a hut, a hovel.<BR>E.<BR>कुटी a house, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुङ्कक
कुटुङ्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An arbour or bower, formed of creeping plants.<BR>2 A thatch, a roof.<BR>3 A hut, a cottage.<BR>4 A creeper winding round a tree.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, क affix, कुट and अङ्ग the body, with कन् added; the form is irr.; also कुटङ्कक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्ब|कुटुंब|कुटुंबं|कुटुम्बः
कुटुम्ब<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुटुम्बयते)<BR>To support a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्ब|कुटुंब|कुटुंबं|कुटुम्बः
कुटुम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A name.<BR>2 A kinsman, a relation by descent.<BR>3 A connexion, a relation by the mother's side by marriage, &c.<BR>4 Offspring, progeny.<BR>5 Family, race.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब to support a family, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बक|कुटुंबक|कुटुंबकं
कुटुम्बक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Being of one family.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A family, a kindred.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बव्यापृत|कुटुंबव्यापृत|कुटुम्बव्यापृतः
कुटुम्बव्यापृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A provident and attentive father of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब kindred, and व्यापृत one who manages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बिता
कुटुम्बिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Family connexion or union, living as one family.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्बिन्, and तल् affix; also with त्व, कुटिम्बित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बिन्|कुटुंबिन्
कुटुम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>1 A peasant, a cultivator of the soil.<BR>2 One who supports or has a family.<BR>m. (-म्बी)<BR>A householder, a pater-familias.<BR>f. (-म्बिनी)<BR>1 The wife of a householder and mother of a family, a matron.<BR>2 A small shrub used in medicine, a kind of moon plant: see क्षीरिणी.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब kindred, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बार्थ
कुटुम्बार्थ<BR>n. adj. (-र्थं)<BR>For the support or on account of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटुम्बौकस्
कुटुम्बौकस्<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>Apartments, &c. appropriated to the accommodation of relations, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब kindred, and ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुटेर
कुटेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hut, a cottage.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्ट|कुट्टः
कुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुट्टयति)<BR>1 To cut, to divide.<BR>2 To grind or pound.<BR>3 To censure.<BR>1st cl. (कुट्टति) 10th cl. (कुट्टयति)<BR>To heat, some make this root कुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टक|कुट्टकः
कुट्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What cuts.<BR>2 What pounds or grinds.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A power in arithmetic or algebra, a quantity such, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">Page227</a>] that a given number being multiplied by it, and the product added to a given quantity, the sum may be divisible without remainder by a given divisor.<BR>2 A kingfisher.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट to pound, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=226" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टकव्यवहार
कुट्टकव्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>That branch of arithmetic which treats of the Kuṭṭaka: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्टक, and व्यवहार practice; also कुट्टकाध्याय or chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टन|कुट्टनं
कुट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pounding, grinding, cutting, dividing.<BR>2 Abusing.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bawd, a procuress, a go-between.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट to cut, ल्युट् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टमित|कुट्टमितं
कुट्टमित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the ten graces of women, affected repulse of a lover's caresses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टाक
कुट्टाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>What cuts or divides.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट to cut, षाकन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टार|कुट्टारं|कुट्टारः
कुट्टार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Pleasure.<BR>2 A blanket.<BR>adv.<BR>Only, merely. (केवले) This word is also written कुट्टीर and कुठार, but perhaps inaccurately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिन्
कुट्टिन्<BR>mfn. (-ट्टी-ट्टिनी-टि)<BR>What cuts or pounds.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bawd, a procures.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट cutting, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिम|कुट्टिमः
कुट्टिम<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>1 A jewel mine.<BR>2 Ground smoothed and plastered.<BR>3 Ground prepared for the site of a mansion.<BR>4 A hut, a cottage.<BR>5 The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट to cut or pierce, and इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टिहारिका
कुट्टिहारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female servant, a slave: see कुटहारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्टीर|कुट्टीरः
कुट्टीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain: see कुट्टार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुट्मल
कुट्मल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>An opening bud.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of the hells in which sinners are punished, where they are bound with ropes.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be curved, and क्मलच् Uṇādi affix, or कल affix, with मुट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठ|कुठः
कुठ<BR>(इ,) कुठि 1st cl. (कुण्ठति)<BR>To be idle.<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुण्ठयति)<BR>To surround; अप् is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठ|कुठः
कुठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and स्था to abide, ड affix; earth-abiding; the deriv. is irregular, and is sometimes written कुट, derived from कुट to be crooked, to bend or wave, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठर|कुठरः
कुठर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The post round which the string of the churning stick winds: see कुटर.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to surround, करन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाकु|कुठाकुः
कुठाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>A bird; the woodpecker.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ for कुट to cut, and आकुः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाटङ्क|कुठाटंकः|कुठाटङ्कः
कुठाटङ्क<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ a tree, आङ् prefixed to टकि to bind, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठार|कुठारः
कुठार<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>1 An axe.<BR>2 A sort of hoe or spade.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ a tree, and ऋ to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारिका
कुठारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small one or adze; also a similarly shaped instrument used in surgery for scarification.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारु|कुठारुः
कुठारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A monkey, an ape.<BR>3 An armourer.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ a tree, ऋ to go, affix ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठि|कुठिः
कुठि<BR>m. (-ठिः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ to surround, and इः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठिक|कुठिकः
कुठिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of costus, commonly, Cuṭh, (Costus speciosus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेर|कुठेरः
कुठेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of fire.<BR>2 Tulasi or basil: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ to surround, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरक|कुठेरकः
कुठेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Holy basil, (Ocimum sanctum): see पणास.<BR>2 A white sort of the same, (Ocimum gratissimum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरज|कुठेरजः
कुठेरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A white species of basil; also कुठेरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरु|कुठेरुः
कुठेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The wind of a fan or Chowrie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड
कुड<BR>(शि) r. 6th cl. (कुडति)<BR>1 To play or act as a child, to trifle.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>3 To heap.<BR>(इ,) कुडि r. 1st cl. (कुंडति)<BR>1 To confound or disorder with grief or pain.<BR>2 To form, to make.<BR>(कुण्डते)<BR>To burn, to heat.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुंडति कुण्डयति)<BR>To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडप|कुडपः
कुडप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A measure: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडव|कुडवः
कुडव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A measure of grain, wood, iron, &c. the fourth part of a Prastha, described by some as a vessel four fingers wide, and as many deep, and containing twelve Prakṛtis or handfuls: it is also said to contain thirteen and a half cubic Aṅgulas; or to be a finger and a half deep, and three fingers each length and breadth. In medicine it is equal to two Prakṛtis or thirty-two Tolakas.<BR>E.<BR>कुड to heap, कवन् affix; also कुडप and कुटप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडि|कुडिः
कुडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>कुड to burn, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिका
कुडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An earthen or wooden water pot used by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिश|कुडिशः
कुडिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A fish, commonly Kūrci, (Cyprinus curchius, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडुप|कुडुपः
कुडुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The clasp or fastening of a necklace or bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मल|कुड्मलः
कुड्मल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A new bud: see कुट्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मलित
कुड्मलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Budded, blossomed.<BR>2 Cheerful, smiling, (as the countenance.)<BR>E.<BR>कुद्मल and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्य|कुड्यं
कुड्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>1 A wall.<BR>2 Anointing, plastering.<BR>3 Eagerness, curiosity.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, and ड्यन् affix, or कुड to heap, &c. and क्यप् affix; also कूड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यक|कुड्यकं
कुड्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A wall: see the preceding, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यच्छेदिन्
कुड्यच्छेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A thief, a housebreaker.<BR>E.<BR>कुड्य a wall, and छेदिन् who cuts or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यच्छेद्य|कुड्यच्छेद्यं|कुड्यच्छेद्यः
कुड्यच्छेद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>An opening, a hole in a wall, a breach.<BR>E.<BR>कुड्य a wall, and छेट्ट्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यमत्स्य|कुड्यमत्स्यः
कुड्यमत्स्य<BR>mf. (-त्स्यः-त्स्यी)<BR>A house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>कुड्य a wall, and मत्स्य a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण
कुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (कुणति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To cherish, to support or aid with gifts, &c.<BR>3 To be in pain.<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुणयति)<BR>1 To converse with, to speak to or address.<BR>2 To counsel or advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणप|कुणपः
कुणप<BR>mn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Foul smelling, stinking.<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 A dead body, a corpse.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A stink, a foul smell.<BR>2 A spear.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A small bird, a kind of Maina or Sārika: see विट्सारिका.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, कपन् affix, व is changed to its congener उ; sound proceeding from the corpse, &c. by the escape of the vital air, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणाल|कुणालः
कुणाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a country.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, कालन् Uṇādi affix, व becomes उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणि|कुणिः
कुणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A cripple with a crooked or withered arm, or without a hand or finger; कूणि.<BR>2 The Tūn tree, (Cedrela tunna); also तुणि.<BR>3 A whitlow.<BR>E.<BR>कुण to sound, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणिन्द|कुणिन्दः
कुणिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Sound, sounding.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, किन्दच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्टक|कुंटक|कुण्टकः
कुण्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fat, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>कुटि to be crooked, क्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=227" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठ|कुंठ|कुण्ठः
कुण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>1 Indolent, lazy, slow.<BR>2 Stupid, foolish, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>कुठि to be slothful, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठक|कुंठक|कुंठकः|कुण्ठकः
कुण्ठक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A fool, stupid, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ठित|कुंठित|कुण्ठितः
कुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Grasped, held.<BR>2 Encircled.<BR>3 Stupid.<BR>E.<BR>कुठि and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A son born in adultery, the son of a woman by another man than her husband, while the husband is alive.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 A hole in the ground for receiving and preserving consecrated fire.<BR>2 A pool, a well, a spring or basin of water, especially consecrated to some holy purpose or person.<BR>2 A measure.<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी)<BR>A pitcher.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A student's water-pot, made of a hollow cocoanut, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुडि to preserve, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डकीट|कुंडकीट|कुण्डकीटः
कुण्डकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A follower of the Cārvāka doctrine, or the tenets of those sects who deny the authority of the Vedas.<BR>2 The son of a woman of the Brahminical tribe born in adultery, particularly with a man of an inferior caste.<BR>3 A keeper of concubines, a man who has female slaves.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड a pool, &c. and कीट a worm, a reptile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डकील|कुंडकील|कुण्डकीलः
कुण्डकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A low, vile man: see नागर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डगोल|कुंडगोल
कुण्डगोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sour rice gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डगोलक|कुंडगोलक|कुण्डगोलकं
कुण्डगोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sour rice gruel: see काञ्जिक.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड a pitcher, गुड to preserve, ण्वुल् affix, ड is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डङ्ग|कुण्डङ्गः
कुण्डङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>An arbour, a bower.<BR>E.<BR>कुडि to preserve, अङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डपाय्य|कुण्डपाय्यः
कुण्डपाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A sacrifice, an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड, and पाय्य to be imbibed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डल|कुंडल|कुंडलं|कुण्डलं|कुंडलः|कुण्डलः
कुण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 An earring.<BR>2 A bracelet.<BR>3 A fetter, a tie, a collar.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Mountain ebony: see काञ्चन.<BR>2 Gurūci, a plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडूची.<BR>3 Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>कुडि to preserve, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलधारण
कुण्डलधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Wearing earrings.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्डल, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलधारिन्
कुण्डलधारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wearing earrings.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्डल, and धारिन् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डलिन्|कुंडलिन्
कुण्डलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having an earring.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A name of VARUṆA regent of the water.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>4 The spotted or painted deer.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A Śakti or form of DURGĀ, worshipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>2 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>3 Curds boiled with Ghee and spices.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्डल an earring, and इनि affix; the rings on the snake, the eyes in the peacock's tail, &c., being compared to this ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डाशिन्|कुंडाशिन्
कुण्डाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A pander, a pimp.<BR>2 One who is supported by a bastard.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड, अश to eat, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिका|कुंडिका
कुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A student's waterpot, the Kamandalu.<BR>2 A pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड a pitcher, &c. कन् added with the fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन|कुंडिन|कुंडिनं|कुण्डिनं|कुण्डिनः
कुण्डिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A city; also Vidarbhā, the capital of Vidarbha the father-in-law of Nala Rājā, apparently the modern Condavir.<BR>m. plur. (-नाः)<BR>The people of Kundina.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>कुडि to preserve, इनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डिन्|कुंडिन्
कुण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>A bastard: see कुण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>कुण्ड and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्डीर|कुंडीर|कुण्डीरः
कुण्डीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Able, powerful.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतनु|कुतनुः
कुतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु)<BR>Deformed.<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, vile, and तनु body, this deity being of a monstrous appearance, having three legs and but eight teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतप|कुतपः
कुतप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Slightly hot, mild, tepid.<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 The eighth Muhūrta or portion of the day, from the last Daṇḍa of the second watch to the first of the third or about noon; an eligible time for the performance of sacrifices to the manes.<BR>2 A daughter's son.<BR>3 A musical instrument.<BR>4 A sort of blanket made of the hair of the mountain goat.<BR>5 Sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A twice born man, one of the three first classes.<BR>4 A guest.<BR>5 A sister's son.<BR>6 An ox.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and तप what warms, or कु diminutive, and तप heat; the sun being on the decline, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतपसप्तक
कुतपसप्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A Śrāddha in which seven constituents occur, noon, a horn platter, a Nepal blanket, silver, sacrificial grass, sesamum and kine.<BR>E.<BR>कुतप, and सप्तक sevenfold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतश्चन्
कुतश्चन्<BR>ind.<BR>Anywhere, somewhere.<BR>E.<BR>चन added to कुतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतश्चित्
कुतश्चित्<BR>ind.<BR>Somewhere or other.<BR>E.<BR>चित् added to कुतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Implying interrogation,<BR>1 How, what.<BR>2 How, in what way, how should it be thus, &c. implying denial or concealment of knowledge.<BR>3 Whence, from what place.<BR>E.<BR>कु for किम् what, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>Whence come, how happened.<BR>E.<BR>त्यप् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुक|कुतुकं
कुतुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>2 Desire, inclination.<BR>3 Curiosity.<BR>E.<BR>कुत a particular sound, कै to emit sound, ड affix; also कौतुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुप|कुतुपं|कुतुपः
कुतुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A small leathern oil bottle.<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>The eighth hour of the day: see कुतप.<BR>E.<BR>कुतू as below, and उपच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतू
कुतू<BR>f. (-तूः)<BR>A leathern oil bottle.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and तन to spread, डु affix, and the final lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूणक|कुतूणकः
कुतूणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Weakness of the eyes in infants; also read कुकूणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Excellent, best, praised, celebrated.<BR>3 Surprising, wonderful.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Eagerness, vehemence, impetuosity.<BR>2 Desire, inclination.<BR>3 Curiosity.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, तूल to send forth, क affix, and ह inserted; or कुतू an oil bottle, and हल to make lines or furrows; or कु the earth, and तुद to vex or tease; the etymologies however are all fanciful; the word is also written कौतूहल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहलिन्
कुतूहलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Curious, inquisitive.<BR>2 Eager, impatient.<BR>E.<BR>कुतूहल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतृण|कुतृणं
कुतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An aquatic plant, water house-leek, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र<BR>ind.<BR>Where, wherein, in what place.<BR>E.<BR>कु substituted for किं what, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रचित्
कुत्रचित्<BR>ind.<BR>Somewhere.<BR>E.<BR>चित् added to कुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रापि
कुत्रापि<BR>ind.<BR>Wherever, somewhere.<BR>E.<BR>कुत्र, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स
कुत्स<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुत्सयते-ति)<BR>To despise, to abuse, to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सन|कुत्सनं
कुत्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Abuse, contempt, reproach, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>कुत्स to revile, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सला
कुत्सला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The indigo plant: see नीली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Reproach, contempt, censure.<BR>E.<BR>कुत्स to despise, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सावादिन्
कुत्सावादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Censorious, abusive.<BR>E.<BR>कुत्स, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=228" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Low, vile, contemptible, contemned, reviled, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>E.<BR>कुत्स to reproach, &c., and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ<BR>r. 4th cl. (-कुथ्यति)<BR>To stink.<BR>r. 9th cl. (कुथ्नाति)<BR>1 To be distressed: see कुन्थ.<BR>(इ) कुथि r. 1st cl. (कुंथति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To afflict, to give pain.<BR>3 To be afflicted, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ|कुथं|कुथः
कुथ<BR>mf. (-थः-था)<BR>A painted or variegated cloth or blanket, serving as an elephant's housings.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Sacrificial or Kusa grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>E.<BR>कुथ to be connected, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद
कुद<BR>r. 10th cl. (ऋ) कुदृ (कोदयति)<BR>To lie, to speak falsely: see कुद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुदाल|कुदालः
कुदाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Mountain ebony.<BR>2 A kind of spade: see कुद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुदृष्टि|कुदृष्टिः
कुदृष्टि<BR>mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि)<BR>Having bad eyes.<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Heterodox doctrine, as that of the Sāṃkhyas, &c.<BR>2 Weak sight.<BR>3 Evil eye.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दल
कुद्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दार|कुद्दारः
कुद्दार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>See the next; sometimes also written कुदार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्दाल|कुद्दालः
कुद्दाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.) also काञ्चन.<BR>2 A kind of spade or hoe.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and दल to divide, with उत् prefixed, and अण् affix, or with दॄ to divide, कुद्दार; also कुदाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्मल|कुद्मलं|कुद्मलः
कुद्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An opening bud: see कुड्मल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्य|कुद्यं
कुद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>A wall: see कुद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्र
कुद्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) कुद्रि (कुंद्रयति)<BR>To speak falsely, to lie: some read this root कुदृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्रङ्ग|कुद्रंग|कुद्रंगः|कुद्रङ्गः
कुद्रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A dwelling raised on a platform or scaffold. It is sometimes written कुद्रङ्क.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and द्रङ्ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुद्रव|कुद्रवः
कुद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A kind of grass, the grain of which is eaten by the poor, (Paspalum scrobiculatum); also कोद्रव.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and द्रु to be fixed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुध्र|कुध्रः
कुध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, ध्रु to be fixed, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनख|कुनखः
कुनख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Having ugly nails.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>A disease of the nails.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and नख a nail; also with इनि added, कुनखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनखिन्
कुनखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>Having bad or diseased nails.<BR>E.<BR>कुनख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनट|कुनटः
कुनट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of trumpet flower.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 Red arsenic.<BR>2 Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and नट to dance, to be; also कुलटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनलिन्
कुनलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, नल a stalk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनाभि|कुनाभिः
कुनाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>1 A whirlwind.<BR>2 KUVERA'S aggregate treasure: see निधि.<BR>E.<BR>कु the world, and नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनाशक|कुनाशकः
कुनाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Javāsa: see यवास.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and नाशक what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुनीति
कुनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Impolicy, misgovernment.<BR>2 Ill conduct, misbehaviour.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्त|कुंत|कुंतः|कुन्तः
कुन्त<BR>mf. (-न्तः-न्ती)<BR>1 A bearded dart, a lance.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A species of grain, (Coix barbata, Rox.)<BR>2 A small animal, an insect.<BR>3 Passionateness.<BR>f. (-न्तिः or -न्ती)<BR>1 The wife of PĀṆḌU, and mother of the three elder PĀṆḌAVA princes by as many gods.<BR>2 The gum olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>3 Bdellium, a fragrant resin.<BR>4 The wife of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and अन्त end, destroying ill, enemies, &c. or क the head, and उन्द to give pain, त substituted for द, fem. affix इन् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तल|कुंतल|कुंतलः|कुन्तलः
कुन्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Hair.<BR>2 A drinking cup.<BR>3 Barley.<BR>4 A plough.<BR>5 The name of a country in the north-west of the peninsula.<BR>m. plu. (-लाः)<BR>The people of that country, the inhabitants of Kuntala.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्त a dart, and ला to bring or gain, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्तलिका|कुंतलिका
कुन्तलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A butter-knife or scoop.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्तल a cup, &c. and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थ
कुन्थ<BR>r. 9th cl. (कुथ्नाति)<BR>1 To cling to, to twine round or be connected with.<BR>2 To be distressed.<BR>3 To suffer pain, want, &c.: see कुथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्थु|कुन्थुः
कुन्थु<BR>m. (-न्थुः)<BR>1 The seventeenth of the Jinas or deified Jaina saints.<BR>2 One of the Jaina emperors of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्द|कुंद|कुंदं|कुंदः|कुन्दः
कुन्द<BR>mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>A kind of jasmin, (J. multiflorum or pubescens.)<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A turner's lathe.<BR>2 Olibanum, the resin of the Boswellia thurifera: see कुन्दरु.<BR>3 One of KUVERA'S nine treasures.<BR>4 The Nerium plant.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, दन Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted, or कु the earth, उन्द to hurt, and अण् affix; also with कन् added कुन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दम|कुंदम|कुंदमः|कुन्दमः
कुन्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, (animals, as mice,) and दम who tames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दर|कुंदरः|कुन्दरः
कुन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दिनी|कुंदिनी
कुन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्द the jasmin, and इनि affix, fem. affix ङीप्; an assemblage like that of Kunda flowers, from the similar whiteness of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दु|कुंदु|कुंदुः|कुन्दुः
कुन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>Frankincense or olibanum: see कुन्दुरु.<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A rat, a mouse.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and दृ to tear or divide, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुर|कुन्दुरः
कुन्दुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Olibanum: see कुन्दुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुरु|कुन्दुरुः
कुन्दुरु<BR>mf. (-रुः)<BR>The resin of the Boswellia thurifera, gum olibanum or frankincense.<BR>E.<BR>क BRAHMĀ, उन्द to moisten, (to bedew with incense in sacrifice,) रु affix, उक् inserted.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A rat: see कुन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुन्दुरुक|कुन्दुरुकः
कुन्दुरुक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>The olibanum tree, commonly Salaī or Salae, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The gum.<BR>E.<BR>कन् possessive or pleonastic added to कुन्दुरु, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप|कुपः
कुप<BR>(इर) कुपिर r. 4th cl. (कुप्यति)<BR>To be angry, to be flushed with wrath.<BR>With प्र,<BR>to be very much enraged.<BR>r. 10th cl. (कोपयति)<BR>1 To shine: see कूप.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>(इ) कुपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुंपति कुंपयति)<BR>1 To spread.<BR>2 To remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपङ्क
कुपङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A slough, a heap of filth and mud.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, पङ्क mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपत
कुपत<BR>ind.<BR>Excellently. Wrong reading for kūpat.^1<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260701. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ|कुपथः
कुपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 A bad road.<BR>2 Immorality, profligacy.<BR>3 Heterodox doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and पथिन् a road; also कापथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथगामिन्
कुपथगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Wicked, going in a bad or wrong road.<BR>E.<BR>कुपथ, and गामिन् who goes; also कुपथग, कुपथचर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपथ्य
कुपथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>1 Relating to a bad road, literally or figuratively.<BR>2 Counter-indicated, improper, unwholesome, (as regimen, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कु and पथ्य proper, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपाणि|कुपाणिः
कुपाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Crooked-handed, having a deformed or maimed hand.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपित
कुपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Incensed, angry, offended.<BR>E.<BR>कुप to be angry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=229" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितवायु|कुपितवायुः
कुपितवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Flatulence or hypochondria.<BR>E.<BR>कुपित, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपितान्तक
कुपितान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Imminent or threatening death.<BR>E.<BR>कुपित, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनिन्
कुपिनिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>कुपिनी a net, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिनी
कुपिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of net or snare, for catching small fish, made of bamboos or rushes.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to cover or conceal, इनि and ङीष् affixes; ग is changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपिन्द|कुपिंद|कुपिंदः|कुपिन्दः
कुपिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>E.<BR>कुप or कुय to spread out, किन्दच् Uṇādi affix; also कुयिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपीलु|कुपीलुः
कुपीलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A sort of ebony tree.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, पीलु a tree, so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुत्र|कुपुत्रः
कुपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A son of an inferior degree, as one adopted, &c.<BR>2 A disobedient or wicked son.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपुरुष|कुपुरुषः
कुपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A low or vile man.<BR>2 A poltroon^1.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and पुरुष a man.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुपूय|कुपूयः
कुपूय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Inferior, low, vile.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and पूय to divide, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्य|कुप्यं
कुप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Base metal, copper, brass, &c. or any metal except gold and silver.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to conceal or preserve, क्यप् affix; ग is changed irregularly to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्यशाला
कुप्यशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A braziery, a foundery, a place where metallic vessels, &c. are made or sold.<BR>E.<BR>कुप्य base metal, शाला a dwelling, a shop, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्रिय|कुप्रियः
कुप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Low, vile, last, worst.<BR>E.<BR>कु reverse, and प्रिय beloved; disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुप्लव|कुप्लवः
कुप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A weak or frail raft or float.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and प्लव a raft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब
कुब<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (इ) कुबि (कुम्बति-कुम्बयति)<BR>To cover, to hide, to clothe, to screen, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुबेर|कुबेरः
कुबेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The deity KUVERA: see कुवेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्ज|कुब्जः
कुब्ज<BR>mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं)<BR>Humpbacked, crooked.<BR>m. (-ब्जः)<BR>1 A tree, (Achyranthes aspera): see अपामार्ग.<BR>2 A scymitar.<BR>3 A sort of fish, (Bola cuja, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, or कु ill, badly, and उज to be straight, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जक|कुब्जकः
कुब्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Humpbacked.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa): see वारिकण्टक.<BR>E.<BR>क water, and उब्ज to be straight, affix अच्, and कन् added, or कुब्ज and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्जकण्टक|कुब्जकण्टकः
कुब्जकण्टक<BR>m. (कः)<BR>A white mimosa.<BR>E.<BR>कुब्ज, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्र|कुब्रं
कुब्र<BR>n. (-ब्रं)<BR>1 A forest.<BR>2 A hole for sacrificial fire.<BR>3 An earring.<BR>4 A thread.<BR>5 A cart.<BR>E.<BR>कुबि to hide, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुब्रह्म|कुब्रह्मः
कुब्रह्म<BR>m. (-ह्मः)<BR>A degraded or contemptible Brahman, one who officiates for Śūdras.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, ब्रह्मन् a Brahman, टच् affix; also retaining the final, कुब्रह्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुभ
कुभ<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) कुभि (कुम्भयति)<BR>To cover, to clothe, to veil or hide: see कुब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुमारयति)<BR>To play, especially as a child; also कुमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमार|कुमारं|कुमारः
कुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A boy, one under five years of age.<BR>2 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>3 A prince, the heir apparent, and who is associated to the empire, (in theatrical language.)<BR>4 A horseman, a cavalier.<BR>5 A parrot.<BR>6 One of the attendants on the twenty-four Jinas, and also a sanctified character amongst the Jaina sect.<BR>7 A tree, (Tapia crataeva): see वरुण.<BR>8 A name of the Sindhu river or Indus.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Pure gold.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A young girl, one from ten to twelve years old, a virgin; or in the Tantras any virgin to the age of sixteen, or as long as menstruation has not commenced.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 The central part of the universe according to Hindu geography, Jambu Dvīpa or India.<BR>4 The most southerly of the nine portions of the known continent, or of Jambu Dvīpa, the southern extremity of the peninsula, whence Cape Comorin or Kumāri.<BR>5 The name of a river flowing from the mountain Sactiman.<BR>6 A plant, (Clitoria ternatea): see अपराजिता.<BR>7 Double jasmin.<BR>8 The aloe tree, (Aloes perfoliata): see घृतकुमारी.<BR>9 The Śyāmā, a bird so named.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार to play as a child, affix अच् fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारक|कुमारकः
कुमारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A boy, a lad.<BR>2 A tree: see वरुण.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारघातिन्
कुमारघातिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>The slayer of a child.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार, हन to kill, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारपाल|कुमारपालः
कुमारपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of Rājā SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>2 Name of a king of Guzerat.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार a child, and पाल a cherisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारभृत्या
कुमारभृत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Care of a pregnant or lying-in woman, midwifery.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार a child, and भृत्या cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारयु|कुमारयुः
कुमारयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A prince.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार a prince, या to go or be, and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारवाहिन्
कुमारवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार KĀRTTIKEYA, and वाहिन् what bears; this god being usually represented riding on a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारसू
कुमारसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A name of GAṄGĀ, the river goddess.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार the god KĀRTTIKEYA, and सू a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमारिका
कुमारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A girl from ten to twelve years old, or generally a virgin.<BR>2 Double jasmin.<BR>3 A division of the known continent.<BR>4 Large cardamoms.<BR>5 An insect, (Sphex Asiatica): see कुमारी, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमाल
कुमाल<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुमालयति)<BR>To play as a child, &c.: see कुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमालक|कुमालकः
कुमालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a district, part of Malva: also termed Sauvīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्
कुमुद्<BR>mfn. (-त् or द्)<BR>1 Niggardly, avaricious.<BR>2 Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>n. (-त् or -द्)<BR>1 The esculent white water lily.<BR>2 The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, or bad, vile, मुद to be pleased, and क्विप् affix; also कुमुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद|कुमुदं|कुमुदः
कुमुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 The white esculent water lily, (Nymphaea esculenta.)<BR>2 The red lotus, (N. rubra.)<BR>3 Silver.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The elephant of the south-west quarter.<BR>2 One of the monkey heroes of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>3 One of the Nāga or serpent race.<BR>4 A Dānava or infernal deity.<BR>5 Camphor.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>2 A tree, (Gmelina arborea): see गम्भारी.<BR>(-दी)<BR>A medicinal and aromatic shrub, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, &c. मुद to be pleased, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदबान्धव|कुमुदबांधव|कुमुदबान्धवः
कुमुदबान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद a lotus, and बान्धव the friend; the white esculent lotus expanding its petals during the night, and closing them in the day time; hence other similar appellations of the moon, as कुमुदवन्धु, कुमुदप्रिय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदवती
कुमुदवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A place abounding in water lilies, &c. see कुमुद्धती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=230" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदाकर|कुमुदाकरः
कुमुदाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A number of water lilies or place abounding with them.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद, and आकर a mine; also कुमुदवनं, कुमुदिनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदावास|कुमुदावासः
कुमुदावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A pool abounding in lotuses.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद, and आवास a residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिक
कुमुदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Abounding with water lilies.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद, and ठच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिका
कुमुदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small tree, the seeds of which are aromatic, commonly Kāyaphal: see कुमुदी, and कट्फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनी
कुमुदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A place abounding in lotuses, &c. see कुमुद्धती.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद, इनि and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदिनीपति|कुमुदिनीपतिः
कुमुदिनीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुदिनी, and पति lord: see कुमुदबान्धव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुदेश|कुमुदेशः
कुमुदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The moon: see कुमुदबान्धव.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद, and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमुद्वत्|कुमुद्वन्त्
कुमुद्वत्<BR>mfn. (-द्वान्-द्वती-द्वत्)<BR>A place abounding in the flowers of the Nymphaea esculenta.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The same.<BR>2 A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR>3 The flexible stalk of a water lily.<BR>4 A sort of water lily, (Menyanthes Indica or cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद the water lily, and मतुप् poss. affix, or वति affix of comparison, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमेरु|कुमेरुः
कुमेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The southern hemisphere or pole, the region of the demons and Titans.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and मेरु the mountain where the gods reside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुमोदक|कुमोदकः
कुमोदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, मुद to delight, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्प|कुम्पः
कुम्प<BR>mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>Crooked-armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्बा|कुंबा
कुम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>An enclosure round a place of sacrifice, to prevent profane intrusion.<BR>E.<BR>कुवि to cover, to screen or conceal, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भ|कुंभ|कुम्भं|कुंभः|कुम्भः
कुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A small water jar.<BR>2 The frontal globe on the upper part of the forehead of an elephant; there are two of these projections, which swell in the rutting season.<BR>3 A sign of the zodiac, (Aquarius.)<BR>4 A proper name, the nephew of Rāvaṇa considered as a Rākṣasa or demon.<BR>5 The paramour of a harlot, a bully, a flash or fancy man.<BR>6 A religious exercise, closing the nostrils and mouth, so as to suspend breathing.<BR>7 A measure of grain equal to twenty Droṇas, a little more than three bushels and three gallons, or a Comb: some make it two Droṇas or sixty-four Seers.<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 A fragrant resin or the plant which bears it, (Bdellium.)<BR>2 A plant commonly Teöri: see त्रिवृत्.<BR>f. (-म्भी)<BR>1 A pot, an earthen cooking vessel, a small jar.<BR>2 Kāyaphal, a small tree, the seeds of which are used in medicine: see कट्फल.<BR>3 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>4 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>(-म्भा)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, or base, vile, &c. उम्भ to fill, and अण् or अच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भक|कुंभक|कुंभकः|कुम्भकः
कुम्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Stopping the breath by shutting the mouth and closing both nostrils with the fingers of the right hand.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकर्ण|कुम्भकर्णः
कुम्भकर्ण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The gigantic brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकामला
कुम्भकामला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A bilious affection, a sort of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकार|कुंभकार|कुम्भकारः
कुम्भकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A potter.<BR>2 A kind of wild fowl.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A mineral substance, used as an application to strengthen the eyes and beautify the eye lashes.<BR>2 Red arsenic.<BR>3 The wife of a potter.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ a jar, &c. and कार what makes, from कृ to make, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भकारक
कुम्भकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A potter.<BR>f. (-रिका)<BR>1 Collyrium.<BR>2 A woman of the potter caste.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भतुम्बी
कुम्भतुम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>A large round gourd.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भदासी|कुंभदासी
कुम्भदासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ a bully, and दासी a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भपदी
कुम्भपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A woman with an enlarged leg.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and पद् for पाद a foot, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भपाद
कुम्भपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A man with an enlarged leg.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भयोनि|कुंभयोनि|कुम्भयोनिः
कुम्भयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A name of AGASTYA, a saint so called.<BR>2 Also of VAŚIṢṬHA; and,<BR>3 Of DROṆA, the military preceptor of the Kurus and Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ a jar, and यानि a womb; born in a water jar, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भला
कुम्भला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, the flowers of which are compared to those of the Nauclea cadamba: see मुण्डिरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भशाला
कुम्भशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A pottery, a potter's kiln.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ a jar, and शाला a hall, a shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भसन्धि|कुम्भसंधि|कुंभसंधि|कुम्भसन्धिः
कुम्भसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>The hollow on the top of an elephant's head, between the frontal globes.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ the frontal globe, and सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भसम्भव|कुम्भसंभव|कुंभसंभव|कुम्भसंभवः|कुम्भसम्भवः
कुम्भसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The saint AGASTYA: see अगस्त्य.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ a jar, and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भाण्ड|कुम्भाण्डः
कुम्भाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A minister of the Asura, BĀṆA.<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी)<BR>A pumpkin gourd: see कुष्माण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिका|कुंभिका
कुम्भिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>2 Trumpet flower.<BR>3 A disease of the eyes, hordeolum or stye.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भी as above, and कन् affix, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिन्|कुंभिन्
कुम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>1 Having a water jar.<BR>2 Shaped like a water jar, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and इनि affix.<BR>m. (-म्भी)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A crocodile.<BR>3 A fish.<BR>4 A plant bearing a fragrant resin, Bdellium.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिनीवीज|कुम्भिनीवीजं
कुम्भिनीवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The croton nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिमद|कुंभिमद|कुम्भिमदः
कुम्भिमद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples at certain seasons.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भि, and मद the exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भिल|कुंभिल|कुंभिलः|कुम्भिलः
कुम्भिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 A plagiarist, a paraphrast.<BR>3 A wife's brother.<BR>4 A fish, the gilt-head.<BR>5 A child begotten at undue seasons, or of an imperfect impregnation.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ as above, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीक|कुंभीक|कुंभीकः|कुम्भीकः
कुम्भीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, the bark of which furnishes a yellow dye, (Rottleria tinctoria): see पुन्नाग.<BR>2 An aquatic plant.<BR>3 An affection of the eyes, hordeolum or stye: see कुम्भिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीधान्य
कुम्भीधान्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>Grain stored in jars sufficient, according to some, for six days, or to others for one year's consumption.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भ, and धान्य grain, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीधान्यक|कुम्भीधान्यकः
कुम्भीधान्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A householder, preserving grain in store for six days, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीनस|कुंभीनस|कुम्भीनसः
कुम्भीनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A large, and venomous snake.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The mother of LAVANA, a Rākṣasa or fiend.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भी a pitcher, and नस derived from नासा the nose; having wide nostrils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीपाक|कुंभीपाक|कुम्भीपाकः
कुम्भीपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भी a pot, and पाक what cooks: in which the wicked are baked like potterś vessels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=231" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीर|कुंभीर|कुंभीरः|कुम्भीरः
कुम्भीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The crocodile of the Ganges, the long nosed alligator.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भी an elephant, and ईर what resembles; or कुम्भी a fish, and र who seizes, from रा to take or gain: or ल from ला, whence also कुम्भील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीरमक्षिका
कुम्भीरमक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of fly or aquatic insect.<BR>E.<BR>कुम्भीर a crocodile, and मक्षिका a fly, the crocodile fly, alluding, perhaps, to its size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भील|कुंभील|कुंभीलः|कुम्भीलः
कुम्भील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A crocodile: see कुम्भीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुम्भीवीज|कुम्भीवीजं
कुम्भीवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The nut of the croton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर
कुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (कुरति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरका
कुरका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्कर|कुरंकर|कुरंकरः|कुरङ्करः
कुरङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>कुर to sound, क aff., a sound, and कर what makes; also कुरङ्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्ग|कुरंग|कुरंगः|कुरङ्गः
कुरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A deer, an antelope.<BR>E.<BR>कुर to sound, अङ्गच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गक|कुरंगकः|कुरङ्गकः
कुरङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गनयना|कुरंगनयना
कुरङ्गनयना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुरङ्ग, and नयना the eye, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरङ्गम|कुरंगम|कुरंगमः|कुरङ्गमः
कुरङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A deer, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरचिल्ल|कुरचिल्लः
कुरचिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरट|कुरटः
कुरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A currier, a leather-seller, a shoe-maker.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, रट to speak, अच् affix; being described as a man of low occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्टक|कुरंटक|कुरंटकः|कुरण्टकः
कुरण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Yellow amaranth.<BR>2 Yellow barleria: see कुरुण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्ड|कुरंड|कुरंडः|कुरण्डः
कुरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Enlargement of the testicles or rather of the scrotum, including inguinal hernia, hydrocele, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, ill, रम to play, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरण्डक|कुरंडकः|कुरण्डकः
कुरण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Yellow amaranth: see करुण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरर|कुररः
कुरर<BR>f. (-रः-रा)<BR>An osprey; also another species of eagle.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sheep, an ewe.<BR>2 A female osprey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुररीगण|कुररीगणः
कुररीगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A flight of ospreys.<BR>E.<BR>कुररी, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरल|कुरलः
कुरल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A curl, a lock of hair.<BR>2 An osprey, see कुरुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरव|कुरवः
कुरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Having a bad voice.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A bad or harsh sound.<BR>2 Red or yellow amaranth: see कुरवक.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad or ill, and रव what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरवक|कुरवकः
कुरवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having a bad voice, making a disagreeable sound.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A purple sort of Jhinti or Barleria.<BR>2 A crimson species of amaranth.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, रव to sound, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरस|कुरसः
कुरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Bad-juiced, of bad essence.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A wild creeping plant, a species of hieracium: see गोजिह्वा.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुराल|कुरालः
कुराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A light bay horse, with black legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरी
कुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरीर|कुरीरं
कुरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, ईरन् Uṇādi affix, उद् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरु|कुरुः
कुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 Kuru or Uttara Kuru, the most northerly of the four Mahā Dvīpas, or principal divisions of the known world; by other systems it is considered as one of nine divisions or Varṣas of the same; in both cases it is the country beyond the northern-most range of mountains, extending to the frozen ocean.<BR>2 A proper name, son of AGNĪDHRA, and grandson of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>3 A proper name, a prince of the lunar race, son of SAṂVARAṆA by TAPATĪ; sovereign of the north-west of India or the country about Dehli, and ancestor of both PĀṆḌU and DHṚTARĀṢṬRA; the patronymic however derived from his name is most usually applied to the sons of the latter.<BR>4 A holy place: see कुरुक्षेत्र.<BR>5 Boiled rice.<BR>6 Pricklynightshade: see कण्टकारिका.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, कु affix, and ऋ becomes उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुकन्दक|कुरुकन्दकं
कुरुकन्दक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>Horseradish, (Raphanus sativus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुक्षेत्र|कुरुक्षेत्रं
कुरुक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The country near Dehli, the scene of the great battle between the Kurus and Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु the Kuru race, and क्षेत्र a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुक्षेत्रीयोग|कुरुक्षेत्रीयोगः
कुरुक्षेत्रीयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A solar day, in the course of which three lunar days, three asterisms and three Yogas occur.<BR>E.<BR>कुरुक्षेत्र, and योम conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुण्ट|कुरुंट|कुरुंटः|कुरुण्टः
कुरुण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>1 Yellow amaranth.<BR>2 Yellow Barleria.<BR>f. (-ण्टी)<BR>1 A doll, a puppet.<BR>2 The wife of a Brahman or teacher.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, रुटि to shine, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुण्टक|कुरुंटकः|कुरुण्टकः
कुरुण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Yellow or white amaranth.<BR>2 A yellow species of Barleria, (B. prionitis.)<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, रुटि to shine, &c. ण्वुल् affix; also कुरण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुम्ब|कुरुंबं|कुरुम्बं
कुरुम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A large species of orange.<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>Trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुराज्
कुरुराज्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A name of DURYODHANA.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु the Kuru race, राज to shine, and क्विप् affix; the Kuru chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुरी
कुरुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of bird with a warbling note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुल|कुरुलः
कुरुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A curl or lock of hair, especially on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुवक|कुरुवकः
कुरुवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The crimson amaranth.<BR>2 A purple species of Barleria.<BR>3 Also a yellow kind.<BR>E.<BR>कु a little, रु to sound, क्वुन् affix, and उवङ् substituted for उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविन्द|कुरुविंद|कुरुविंदं|कुरुविन्दं|कुरुविंदः|कुरुविन्दः
कुरुविन्द<BR>mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>2 A kind of barley: see कल्माष.<BR>3 A ruby: see कुरुविल्ल.<BR>4 Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु Kurudeśa, विन्द to gain, and शः affix; found in that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविन्दक
कुरुविन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of Dolichos biflorus, a wild variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविल्ल|कुरुविल्लः
कुरुविल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A ruby; also कुरुविल्व, and कुरुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविल्व|कुरुविल्वः
कुरुविल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A ruby; also कुरुविन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुविस्त|कुरुविस्तः
कुरुविस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A Pala of gold, a weight of gold equal to about 700 Troy grains.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु the country, and विस्त, abundant; abounding in Kurudeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूप
कुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Ugly, ill made, deformed.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Ugliness.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूपता
कुरूपता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ugliness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also कुरूपत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूपिन्
कुरूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Ugly, ill made, frightful, deformed.<BR>E.<BR>कुरूप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरूप्य|कुरूप्यं
कुरूप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>कु base, रूप्य silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्क्कुर|कुर्कुर|कुर्कुरः
कुर्क्कुर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A dog or bitch.<BR>E.<BR>कुर् instead of कु bad, prefixed to कु to sound, and रक् affix: see कुक्कुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्द|कुर्द्द
कुर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (कूर्दते or कुर्दते)<BR>To play; also कूर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्द्दन|कुर्दन|कुर्द्दनं
कुर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Play, playing, sport: see कूर्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्पर|कुर्परः
कुर्पर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The knee.<BR>2 The elbow; also कूर्पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्पास|कुर्पासः
कुर्पास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A sort of bodice or jacket: see कूर्पास; also with कन् added कुर्पासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वाण|कुर्वाण
कुर्व्वाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Doing, making.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वत्|कुर्वत्|कुर्वन्त्
कुर्व्वत्<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वन्ती-र्व्वत)<BR>1 Doing, acting, an agent.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=232" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुर्व्वत्रूप
कुर्व्वत्रूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Cause according to the Cārvākas.<BR>E.<BR>कुर्व्वत्, and रुप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल<BR>r. 1st cl. (कोलति)<BR>1 To accumulate.<BR>2 To be of kin, to act as of kin.<BR>3 To flow homogeneously.<BR>4 To count.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>to be attentive;<BR>with वि and आङ्<BR>to be bewildered, flurried or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल|कुलं|कुलः
कुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Family, race, tribe or caste.<BR>2 A herd, a flock, &c. of animals of the same species.<BR>3 An inhabited country.<BR>4 A house, an abode.<BR>5 The body.<BR>6 The front or fore part.<BR>7 A blue stone: see कुलत्थ.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An artist of celebrated descent.<BR>f. (-लिः or -ली)<BR>A prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारी, &c.<BR>(-ली)<BR>A wife's elder sister.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, क affix, or कुङ् to sound, and लक् affix, or कु the earth, and ल who takes or possesses, from ला with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक|कुलकं|कुलकः
कुलक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Of a good family, of eminent birth.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A species of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.) see काकेन्दु.<BR>2 An artist of eminent birth.<BR>3 An ant or mole hill.<BR>4 A green snake.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A sort of gourd, (Trichosanthes diaeca.)<BR>2 The connexion of several stanzas, protraction of the government of the noun or verb through several verses, contrary to the practice of closing the sense with each verse.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, or कुल race, and क who sounds, declares, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलकन्या
कुलकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A girl of good family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and कन्या a maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलकर्म्मन्|कुलकर्मन्
कुलकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The proper duty of a race or family, any observance customarily held by one.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and कर्म्म act; also कुलक्रिया and कुलकार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्क|कुलक्कः
कुलक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>Beating time in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलक्षय|कुलक्षयः
कुलक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Decay or disappearance of a family.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>कुल the body, and क्षय injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलगिरि|कुलगिरिः
कुलगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A mountain, any one of the seven principal mountains of Bhārata Varṣa.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and गिरि mountain: see कुलाचल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलङ्गी
कुलङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A thorny plant: see कर्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलज|कुलजः
कुलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Well-born, of a good family.<BR>2 Ancestral, hereditary.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and ज born; also कुलजात, कुलोत्पन्न, and similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलञ्ज|कुलञ्जः
कुलञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलञ्जन|कुलञ्जनः
कुलञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An aromatic plant, (Alpinia galanga); also कुलञ्ज and गन्धमूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलट|कुलटः
कुलट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Any son except the one begotten, as one adopted, bought, &c.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and अट who goes, deriv. irr.; by whom the family honour is injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलटापति
कुलटापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The husband of an unchaste woman, a cuckold.<BR>E.<BR>कुलटा, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलटी
कुलटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलतिथि|कुलतिथिः
कुलतिथि<BR>mf. (-थिः)<BR>The fourth, eighth, twelfth, or fourteenth lunar day.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and तिथि a lunation, respectable days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलतिलक|कुलतिलकः
कुलतिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The chief of a family, one who does honour to a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and तिलक frontal mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थ|कुलत्थः
कुलत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>A kind of pulse, (Dolichos biflorus.)<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>1 A blue stone used in medicine, and applied as a collyrium to the eyes; also as an astringent to sores, &c.<BR>2 A wild kind of Dolichos.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a bank, and स्था to stand or stay, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलत्थिका
कुलत्थिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A blue stone used as a collyrium, &c.<BR>2 A sort of vetch, considered as a wild sort of the Dolichos biflorus.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding, कन् added to कुलत्थ in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधर्म्म|कुलधर्म|कुलधर्मः|कुलधर्म्मः
कुलधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Practice or observance peculiar to a tribe or family, peculiar duty of caste or race.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलधारक|कुलधारकः
कुलधारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a race, and धृ to hold, in the causal form, वुन् affix; upholding a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनक्षत्र|कुलनक्षत्रं
कुलनक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Any propitious asterism.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनायिका
कुलनायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A girl who is worshipped at the celebration of the orgies of the left hand Śāktas.<BR>E.<BR>कुल society, and नायिका a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनारी
कुलनारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A woman of good family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and नारी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनाश|कुलनाशः
कुलनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A reprobate, an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a family, नाश who hurts or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलनिन्दा
कुलनिन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Family disgrace.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and निन्दा reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपति|कुलपतिः
कुलपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Head or chief of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a family, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपर्व्वत|कुलपर्वत|कुलपर्वतः
कुलपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A principal mountain of India, any one of seven so considered: see कुलाचल.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and पर्ब्वत a mountain; also similar compounds, as कुलगिरि, कुलशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपांसुला
कुलपांसुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालक|कुलपालकं
कुलपालक<BR>mfn. (-लकः-लिका-लकं)<BR>Nourishing or providing for a family.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of orange.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a race, &c. पाल to nourish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालि|कुलपालिः
कुलपालि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A chaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and पाल who nourishes, इन् fem. affix; also कुलपालिका and कुलपाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलपालिका
कुलपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See कुलपालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलबधू
कुलबधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>A virtuous or respectable woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and बधू a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलभृत्या
कुलभृत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A midwife, a nurse.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, and भृत्या a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलभ्रष्ट
कुलभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Expelled from a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and भ्रष्ट fallen from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलमर्य्यादा|कुलमर्यादा
कुलमर्य्यादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Family honour or respectability.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and मर्य्यादा propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलमित्र
कुलमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रं)<BR>A friend of the family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलम्भर|कुलंभर|कुलंभरः|कुलम्भरः
कुलम्भर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief: see कुजम्भल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलयोषित्
कुलयोषित्<BR>f. (-त्)<BR>A virtuous woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and योषित् a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलवार|कुलवारः
कुलवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Tuesday or Friday.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलविप्र|कुलविप्रः
कुलविप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>The family priest.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and विप्र a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलव्यापिन्
कुलव्यापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Attaching or applicable to tribe or caste.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and व्यापिन् prevailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलश्रेष्ठिन्
कुलश्रेष्ठिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>1 An artificer or artist of eminent birth.<BR>2 Well-born, of good family.<BR>3 Eminent in a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and श्रेष्ठ best, poss. affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसङ्ख्या|कुलसंख्या
कुलसङ्ख्या<BR>f. (-ङ्ख्या)<BR>Ranking or being reckoned as a family, family respectability.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and सङ्ख्या enumeration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=233" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसन्तति|कुलसंतति|कुलसंततिः
कुलसन्तति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Posterity, descendants.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and सन्तति continuance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसन्निधि|कुलसंनिधि|कुलसन्निधिः
कुलसन्निधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Kindred, relations.<BR>2 Presence of witnesses.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and सन्निधि proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसम्भव|कुलसंभव|कुलसम्भवः
कुलसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Sprung from family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and सम्भव born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलसौरभ|कुलसौरभं
कुलसौरभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A plant, commonly Marüa: see मरुवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलस्थिति|कुलस्थितिः
कुलस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Antiquity or prosperity of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and स्थिति duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलस्त्री
कुलस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>1 A chaste woman.<BR>2 A woman of a good family, a respectable woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a family, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलहण्डक|कुलहंडकः|कुलहण्डकः
कुलहण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eddy: see कूलहण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुल
कुलाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of mixed origin of a mixed character.<BR>E.<BR>कुल propitious, and आकुल bewildered, or कुल with a neg. prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलतिथि|कुलाकुलतिथिः
कुलाकुलतिथि<BR>mf. (-थिः)<BR>The second, sixth or tenth lunar days.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाकुल, and तिथि a lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलनक्षत्र|कुलाकुलनक्षत्रं
कुलाकुलनक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An asterism of mixed character, as Vāruṇī, Ārdrā, Mūla and Abhijit.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाकुल, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाकुलवार|कुलाकुलवारः
कुलाकुलवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wednesday.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाकुल, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाक्षुता
कुलाक्षुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचल|कुलाचलः
कुलाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A mountain, one of a class of seven principal mountains, which are supposed to exist in each Varṣa or division of a continent: those of Bhārata Varṣa or India are Mahendra, Malaya, Sahya, Śuktimān, Ṛkṣa, Vindhya, and Pāripātra.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a race, and अचल a mountain; also कुलाद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचार|कुलाचारः
कुलाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The proper duty or practice of a caste or family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाचार्य्य|कुलाचार्य|कुलाचार्यः|कुलाचार्य्यः
कुलाचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A family priest.<BR>2 A genealogist.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and आचार्य्य teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाट|कुलाटः
कुलाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small fish.<BR>E.<BR>कुल for कूल a bank, and अट who goes; burrowing in the sand and mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाधारक|कुलाधारकः
कुलाधारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>see कुलधारक, आङ् being here inserted signifying extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभि|कुलाभिः
कुलाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभिमान|कुलाभिमानः
कुलाभिमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pride of birth, family pride.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and अभिमान pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाभिमानिन्
कुलाभिमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Proud of birth or of family descent.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and अमिमानिन् proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाय|कुलायं|कुलायः
कुलाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A nest.<BR>2 A place, a spot in general.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, and अय to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलाय|कुलायनिलायः
कुलायनिलाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sitting in a nest, brooding.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाय, and निलाय abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलायिन्
कुलायनिलायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Brooding, hatching, (as a bird.)<BR>E.<BR>कुलाय, and निलायिन् who abides in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायनिलायिता
कुलायनिलायिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The act or condition of hatching, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायस्थ|कुलायस्थः
कुलायस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाय a nest, and स्थ who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलायिका
कुलायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An aviary.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाय a nest, and कन् affix in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाल|कुलालः
कुलाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A potter.<BR>2 A wild cock.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A species of blue stone^1, applied as a collyrium to the eyes.<BR>2 The wife of a potter.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, and कालन Uṇādi affix, or कुल family, अल to adorn, &c. अण् and ङीप् or ङीष् affs.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलालम्बिन्|कुलालंबिन्
कुलालम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>Supporting or maintaining a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and आलम्बिन् what upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलालिका
कुलालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An aviary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाह|कुलाहः
कुलाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse of a light brown colour, with black knees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाहल|कुलाहलः
कुलाहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small tree, (Conyza terebinthina.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलाहक|कुलाहकः
कुलाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chamelion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलि|कुलिः
कुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A hand.<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A prickly nightshade: see कुल.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, &c. कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिक|कुलिकः
कुलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Of a good family, well-born.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One of the eight chiefs of the Nāgas or serpent race, described as having a half moon on the top of his head, and being of a monkey hue.<BR>2 An artist or artificer of eminent birth.<BR>3 A thorny plant, (Ruellia longifolia.)<BR>4 The chief or headman of a tribe or caste.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, &c. कन् affix, and इ substituted for अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिकवेला
कुलिकवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Certain portions of each day, on which it is improper to begin any business.<BR>E.<BR>कुलिक, and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिङ्ग|कुलिंग|कुलिंगः|कुलिङ्गः
कुलिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike; also कलिङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिङ्गक|कुलिङ्गकः
कुलिङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिर|कुलिरं|कुलिरः
कुलिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crab; also कुलीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिश|कुलिशं|कुलिशः
कुलिश<BR>mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>1 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>2 A kind of fish.<BR>E.<BR>कुलि for कुल a bank, and श what rests, from शीङ्^1 to sleep. &c. and क aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशभृत्
कुलिशभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>कुलिश, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशाङ्कुशा
कुलिशाङ्कुशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A kind of female deity.<BR>E.<BR>कुलिश the thunderbolt, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलिशासन|कुलिशासनः
कुलिशासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of Śākya, a Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीन|कुलीनः
कुलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Well-born, of high or eminent descent, of a good family.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A horse of a good breed.<BR>2 A Brahman of one of the twenty-two Rārhiya divisions of the five principal tribes, as established by Balāl Sen king of Beṅgal.<BR>3 A worshipper of ŚAKTI, according to the left hand ritual: see कौलीन.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a family, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनक|कुलीनकः
कुलीनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Of a good family.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of wild kidney bean.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनता
कुलीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Birth, rank, family respectability.<BR>E.<BR>कुलीन, and तल् affix; also with त्व, कुलीनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीनस|कुलीनसं
कुलीनस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीर|कुलीरः
कुलीर<BR>mf. (-रः-रं)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, and ईरन् affix; also कुलिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीरशृङ्गी
कुलीरशृङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant: see कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीराद्
कुलीराद्<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>A young crab.<BR>E.<BR>कुलीर a crab, and अद to eat, affix क्विप्; destroying its parent; the old crab being supposed to perish on producing young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलीश|कुलीशं|कुलीशः
कुलीश<BR>mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt: see कुलिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलुक|कुलुकं
कुलुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The fur or foulness of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, and उक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलुक्कगुञ्जा|कुलुक्कगुंजा
कुलुक्कगुञ्जा<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>A firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलेश्वर|कुलेश्वरः
कुलेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The chief of a family or race.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a race, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=234" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्कट|कुलोत्कटः
कुलोत्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>High-born.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A horse of a good breed.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, and उत्कट eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्कर्ष
कुलोत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Family respectability.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उत्कर्ष excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्गत
कुलोद्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Of good family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उद्गत exalted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोत्पन्न
कुलोत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Of a good family, well-born.<BR>2 Family, belonging to, inherited by, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्भव
कुलोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Well-born, of good family.<BR>2 Produced in a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उद्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्भूत
कुलोद्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well-born, of family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उद्भूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलोद्वह|कुलोद्वहः
कुलोद्वह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A chief, a leader, the head of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुल, and उद्वह who upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्फ|कुल्फं|कुल्फः
कुल्फ<BR>mn. (-ल्फः-ल्फं)<BR>A disease.<BR>m. (-ल्फः)<BR>The ancle; also गुल्फ.<BR>E.<BR>कल to count, फ Uṇādi affix, and उ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्मल|कुल्मलं
कुल्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to extract, क्मलन् Uṇādi affix, and ष changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्माष|कुल्माषं|कुल्माषः
कुल्माष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>Sour gruel prepared by the spontaneous fermentation of the water of boiled rice.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Half ripe barley.<BR>2 Forced rice.<BR>3 A sort of Phaseolus: see राजमाष.<BR>4 A species of Dolichos, (D. biflorus.) see यावक.<BR>5 A disease.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A dish consisting of half boiled rice, with pulse, &c. commonly Khicri.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a class or race, मष or मस to hurt or kill, अण् affix; hence the word is also written कुल्मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्माषाभिसुत
कुल्माषाभिसुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sour gruel. see कुल्मास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्मास|कुल्मासं
कुल्मास<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>See कुल्माष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्य|कुल्यं|कुल्यः
कुल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Of a good family, well-born, well descended.<BR>2 Of or relating to a family or race.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A counsellor.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 A canal, a channel for irrigation.<BR>3 A ditch, a dyke or trench.<BR>4 A drug or medicinal plant, (Celtis orientalis): see जीवन्ती.<BR>5 A chaste or virtuous woman.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 A bone.<BR>2 A measure of eight Droṇas: see द्रोण.<BR>3 A winnowing basket.<BR>4 Flesh.<BR>5 Friendly inquiry after family affairs or domestic accidents, condolence, congratulation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, and यत् affix, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुल्वक|कुल्वकं
कुल्वक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>Fur upon the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव|कुवं
कुव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A water lily, a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवङ्ग|कुवंग|कुवङ्गं|कुवङ्गः
कुवङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, and वङ्ग tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवच|कुवचः
कुवच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Abusive, censorious, detracting.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, वच to speak, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवज्रक|कुवज्रकं
कुवज्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Crystal, a stone resembling a diamond.<BR>E.<BR>कु inferior, वज्र the diamond, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवद
कुवद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Censorious.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, वद to speak, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवर|कुवरः
कुवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An astringent taste: see तुवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवल|कुवलं
कुवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>1 The jujube, the tree.<BR>2 The fruit.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A water lily.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and वल to cover, affix अच्; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलय|कुवलयं
कुवलय<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 Any water lily.<BR>2 The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, वल to cover, and कयन् affix; also कुवल, and कुव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलयिनी
कुवलयिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A place abounding in water lilies.<BR>E.<BR>कुवलय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवलाश्व|कुवलाश्वः
कुवलाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A proper name of a king; also घुन्धुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाद|कुवादः
कुवाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Detracting, censorious.<BR>E.<BR>कु evil, वद to speak, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवाहुल|कुवाहुलः
कुवाहुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविन्द|कुविंद|कुविंदः|कुविन्दः
कुविन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>E.<BR>कुप to spread, किन्दच् Uṇādi affix, and प changed to व; also कुपिन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुविवाह|कुविवाहः
कुविवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A degrading or improper marriage.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवृत्तिकृत्
कुवृत्तिकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A plant, (Caesalpinia bonduccella): see पूतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेणी
कुवेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A fish basket.<BR>2 An ill braided tress of hair.<BR>3 A woman with her hair ill braided.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, वेण to go, घञ् affix, and ङीष् fem. affix; also with टाप् or इन् affixed, कुवेणा and कुवेणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेर|कुवेरः
कुवेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Deformed, monstrous.<BR>2 Slow, lazy.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA the son of VISRAVAS by IḌAVIḌĀ, the chief of the Yakṣas, god of wealth and regent of the north.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, and वेर body, alluding to the deformity of the god, who is represented as having three legs and but eight teeth.<BR>2 The Tūn tree: see नन्दिवृक्ष.<BR>3 One of the attendants of a Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>as above, or कुवि to cover, &c. and एरच् Uṇādi affix; in this case the word may be read कुबेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेरक|कुवेरकः
कुवेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Tūn tree, (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराक्षी
कुवेराक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>कुवेर, and अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराचल|कुवेराचलः
कुवेराचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mount Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>कुवेर, and अचल a mountain; the capital of KUVERA, being situated in Kailāsa, which is supposed to be in the Himālaya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेराद्रि|कुवेराद्रिः
कुवेराद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as above, अद्रि being a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुवेल|कुवेलं
कुवेल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Any water lily.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, बेल to shake, अच् affix: see कुवलय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुव्र
कुव्र<BR>n. (-व्रं)<BR>A forest or wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश|कुशं|कुशः
कुश<BR>(इर) कुशिर r. 4th cl. (कुश्यति)<BR>1 To embrace, to enfold.<BR>2 To take out or from.<BR>(इः) कुशि r. 1st and 10th cl. (कुंशति कुंशयति)<BR>To shine: see कुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुश|कुशं|कुशः
कुश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Wicked, depraved.<BR>2 Mad, inebriate.<BR>mn. (-शः-श)<BR>A species of grass used in many solemn and religious observances, hence called sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The yoke of a plough.<BR>2 A proper name, one of the sons of RĀMA.<BR>3 One of the great Dvīpas or divisions of the universe, surrounded by the sea of spirituous liquor.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 A rope.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Maükāṭha.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Water.<BR>(-शी)<BR>1 A ploughshare.<BR>2 Wrought iron.<BR>mf. (-शः-शी)<BR>A bridle, a horse's head rope.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, शीङ्^1 to sleep or rest, and ड affix, or कु bad, and शो to destroy, again कुश to embrace or to enfold, and क aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशनामन्
कुशनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशय|कुशयः
कुशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A drinking vessel, a cup, a goblet.<BR>E.<BR>कुश to extract, and अय Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशपुष्प|कुशपुष्पं
कुशपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशल|कुशलं|कुशलः
कुशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right.<BR>2 Expert, skilful.<BR>3 Clever.<BR>4 Eloquent.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Adequacy, ability.<BR>2 Virtue, virtuous action.<BR>3 Well-being, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, and शल to go, affix अच्; also कुषल and कुसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=235" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलता
कुशलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Cleverness, ability.<BR>2 Eloquence.<BR>3 Wellbeing.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कुशलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलप्रश्न|कुशलप्रश्नः
कुशलप्रश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>Salutation, greeting, friendly inquiry respecting a person's health or welfare.<BR>E.<BR>कुशल well-being, and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलव
कुशलव<BR>du. m. (-वौ)<BR>The two sons of RĀMA, or KUŚA and LAVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलबुद्धि
कुशलबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Wise, able, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>कुशल, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलिन्
कुशलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Auspicious, favourable.<BR>2 Virtuous, good.<BR>3 Happy, prosperous.<BR>4 Clever.<BR>E.<BR>कुशल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशवारि
कुशवारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Water in which Kusa grass has been boiled.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and वारि water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशलव
कुशलव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A bundle of Kuśa grass.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and स्तव a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशस्थल|कुशस्थलं
कुशस्थल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>The country of Kanyakubja or Kanouj.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The residence of KṚṢṆA: see द्वारका.<BR>2 A name of Oujein or Avanti during the Tretā Yuga or second age.<BR>E.<BR>कुश sacred grass, and स्थल place; abounding in Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाकर|कुशाकरः
कुशाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the grass, &c. आकर a mine; the sacrificial fire being made upon a tuft of this grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाक्ष|कुशाक्षः
कुशाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A monkey, an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्र
कुशाग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Sharp, shrewd, intelligent.<BR>m. (-ग्रं)<BR>The sharp point of the Kusa grass.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रबुद्धि
कुशाग्रबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Sharp, shrewd, intelligent.<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Shrewdness, subtlety.<BR>E.<BR>कुशाग्र, and बुद्धि understanding; also similar compounds, कुशाग्रधी, कुशाग्रीयमति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रीय
कुशाग्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Subtile, penetrating: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the grass, अग्र point, and छ, affix; implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाग्रीयमति|कुशाग्रीयमतिः
कुशाग्रीयमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Inspecting minutely, subtile, sharp sighted, intelligent, possessing mental acumen.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the grass, अग्रीय point, and मति mind; also other similar compounds, as कुशाग्रीयधी, कुशाग्रीयबुद्धि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाङ्गुरीय|कुशांगुरीय
कुशाङ्गुरीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A ring of Kusa grass, worn at religious ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and अङ्गुरीय a ring; also कुशाङ्गुरीयकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशाल्मलि|कुशाल्मलिः
कुशाल्मलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>E.<BR>कु, and शाल्मलि silk cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशारणि|कुशारणिः
कुशारणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The name of a sage celebrated for his irascibility: see दुर्व्वास.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the grass, and अरणि wood whose attrition produces fire; using Kusa for this purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशासन
कुशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A seat of Kuśa grass.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिंशपा
कुशिंशपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A kind of Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu).<BR>E.<BR>कु inferior, and शिंशपा the Sisu tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिक|कुशिकः
कुशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Muni or divine sage so named, the father of JAMADAGNI.<BR>2 A ploughshare.<BR>3 The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>4 Beleric myrobalan: see विभीतक.<BR>5 The sediment of oil.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the grass, &c. इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशित|कुशितं
कुशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mixed, combined with water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुश or कुष to embrace, to mix, and इतच् Uṇādi affix; hence also कुषित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशिन्
कुशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A name of VĀLMĪKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>कुश the son of RĀMA, affix इनि; the poem is supposed to be recited by KUSA and LAVA, the sons of the hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीद|कुशीदं
कुशीद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 The profession of usury.<BR>2 Red saunders: see कुमीद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशील
कुशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Ill-behaved. rude, wicked.<BR>2 Evil disposed, ill-tempered.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and शील temper, conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीलता
कुशीलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Misbehaviour, misconduct.<BR>2 Bad disposition, ill-temper.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, कुशीलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीलव|कुशीलवः
कुशीलव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>1 An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR>2 A bard, a herald.<BR>3 A newsmonger.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, शील practice, and वः affix, from वा to go, &c. with क affix, du. m. (-वौ) The two sons of RĀMA: see कुशलव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशीवश|कुशीवशः
कुशीवश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of VĀLMĪKI: see कुशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूल|कुशूलः
कुशूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A granary, a cupboard, a place in which rice or other grain is kept.<BR>2 Conflagration of chaff.<BR>E.<BR>कुश to enfold, कूल affix; also कुसूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूलधान्य
कुशूलधान्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>Grain stored for three year's consumption.<BR>E.<BR>कुशूल, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशूलधान्यक|कुशूलधान्यकः
कुशूलधान्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A householder, &c. who has three year's grain in store.<BR>E.<BR>कुशूलधान्य, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशेशय|कुशेशयं|कुशेशयः
कुशेशय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A lotus in general.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A tree, commonly Kaniyār: see कर्णिकार.<BR>2 The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>कुश water, in the seventh case, शीङ्^1 to sleep or rest, with the affix अच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशेशयकर
कुशेशयकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशोत्तर
कुशोत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having, or being covered with grass.<BR>E.<BR>कुश and उत्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशोदक
कुशोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water in which Kusa grass has been infused.<BR>E.<BR>कुश, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष
कुष<BR>r. 9th cl. (कुष्णाति)<BR>1 To expel, to force or draw out, to extract<BR>2 To test, to assay.<BR>3 To shine.<BR>With अव,<BR>to prove, to display;<BR>with निर्,<BR>to extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषल|कुषलः
कुषल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>Clever, expert, skilful: see कुशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषाकु|कुषाकुः
कुषाकु<BR>mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु)<BR>1 Burning, scorching, inflaming.<BR>2 Wicked, detestable.<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 A monkey.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to shine, काकु Uṇādi affix; also कुषाकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित्
कुषित्<BR>ind.<BR>Excellently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषित|कुषितः
कुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mixed with water, &c. see कुशित.<BR>n. (-त)<BR>Happy, well, right, fortunate, auspicious, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुषीद|कुषीदं
कुषीद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Indifferent, apathetic, inert.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Usury: see कुसीद.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, षद to move, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठ|कुष्ठं|कुष्ठः
कुष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Leprosy, of which eighteen varieties are enumerated, seven great or severe, and eleven of minor importance.<BR>2 A plant, a kind of costus, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>3 A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to extract, and क्थन् Uṇādi affix, or कु bad, ill, and स्थ being, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठघ्न|कुष्ठघ्नः
कुष्ठघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Hiyāvali: see हितावली.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 An esculent root, (Solanum Indicum.) see काकमाची.<BR>2 Opposite leaved fig tree; also काकोडुम्बरिका.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ the leprosy, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठनाशन|कुष्ठनाशनः
कुष्ठनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 White mustard.<BR>2 A sort of yam: see वाराही.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ the leprosy, and नाशन what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठनाशिनी
कुष्ठनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, commonly Hākuca, (Psoralia corylifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>as above: see कुष्ठनाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठल|कुष्ठलं
कुष्ठल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A bad place or spot.<BR>2 The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, or the earth, and स्थल place; स becomes ष, and थ is then changed to ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=236" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठसूदन|कुष्ठसूदनः
कुष्ठसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The cassia tree, (C. fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ, and सूदन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठहृत्
कुष्ठहृत्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>Catechu, (Mimosa catechu): see खदिर.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ leprosy, and हृत् what takes away, from हृ to convey, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठहन्तृ
कुष्ठहन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>A large esculent root, described as possessed of medicinal virtue in leprosy, and other cutaneous affections, (Arum campanulatum): see हस्तिकन्द.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ leprosy, and हन्तृ what kills or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठारि|कुष्ठारिः
कुष्ठारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A fetid mimosa, (M. Farnesiana.)<BR>2 The Khayar or Catechu: (M. catechu.)<BR>3 A kind of Aristolochia: see अर्कपत्र.<BR>4 A sort of gourd, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>5 Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ the leprosy, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्ठिन्
कुष्ठिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>Leprous, a leper, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुष्ठ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्मल|कुष्मलं
कुष्मल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cutting, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to extract, and क्मलन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्ड|कुष्मांड|कुष्मांडः|कुष्माण्डः
कुष्माण्ड<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डा or -ण्डी)<BR>A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo).<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 One of a class of demigods attached to ŚIVA.<BR>2 State of the womb in gestation.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A drug.<BR>3 A religious ceremony, a certain rite performed as a penance or expiation; also कुष्माण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुष्माण्डक|कुष्मांडक|कुष्मांडकः|कुष्माण्डकः
कुष्माण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, उष्म heat, अन् to exist or be, ड affix, and the vowel irregularly short, कन् added; also कुष्माण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस
कुस<BR>(इर) कुसिर r. 4th cl. (कुस्यति)<BR>To embrace.<BR>(इ) कुसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (कुंसति कुंसयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसरित्
कुसरित्<BR>f. (-रित्)<BR>A shallow stream.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, सरित् a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसल|कुसलं
कुसल<BR>adv. n. (-लं)<BR>Well, happy, &c. see कुशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसित|कुसितः
कुसित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An inhabited country.<BR>E.<BR>कुस to shine, and इत Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीतायी
कुसीतायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The wife of a money-lender: see कुसीदायी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीद|कुसीदं|कुसीदः
कुसीद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Usury, the profession of usury.<BR>2 Any loan or thing lent to be repaid with interest.<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 A money-lender.<BR>2 Slothful, inert.<BR>E.<BR>कुस to embrace, ईद Uṇādi affix; or कु bad, and षद to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदपथ|कुसीदपथः
कुसीदपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Usury, usurious interest, any exceeding five per cent.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद, and पथ for पथिन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदवृद्धि|कुसीदवृद्धिः
कुसीदवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Interest on money.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदायी
कुसीदायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The wife of a usurer.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद a usurer, ऐ substituted for its final, and ङीष् affix; also कुसीतायी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसीदिक|कुसीदिकः
कुसीदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>One who follows the profession of usury.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद usury, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम|कुसुमं|कुसुमः
कुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A flower in general.<BR>2 Fruit.<BR>3 The menstrual discharge.<BR>4 Ophthalmia, disease of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>कुस to shine, उम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमकार्म्मुक|कुसुमकार्मुक|कुसुमकार्मुकः
कुसुमकार्म्मुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and कार्म्मुक a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमचित
कुसुमचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heaped with flowers.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and चित gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमपुर|कुसुमपुरं
कुसुमपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A city, the vicinity of the modern Patna: see पाटलिपुत्र.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम a flower, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुममध्य|कुसुममध्यं
कुसुममध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>The name of a tree, bearing a large acid fruit, (Dilenia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम a flower, and मध्य the centre; the flower blossoming from the fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमयत्
कुसुमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Producing flowers, causing to flower.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम nom. verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमवत्|कुसुमवन्त्
कुसुमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>In flower, flowering.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A female during menstruation.<BR>2 A town: see कुसुमपुर.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमस्तवक|कुसुमस्तवकः
कुसुमस्तवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A collection of flowers, a garland, a nosegay.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and लवक a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाकर|कुसुमाकरः
कुसुमाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Spring, the vernal season.<BR>2 A quantity of flowers or place abounding with them, a parterre, a garden.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाञ्जन|कुसुमांजन|कुसुमाञ्जनं
कुसुमाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The calx of brass, used as a collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम a flower, and अञ्जन application to the eyes; resembling a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमात्मक|कुसुमात्मकं
कुसुमात्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and आत्मक self; the essential part of the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाधिप|कुसुमाधिपः
कुसुमाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Campa, a tree which bears a yellow fragrant flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम a flower, and अधिप a king; royal amongst flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाधिराज्
कुसुमाधिराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमायुध|कुसुमायुधः
कुसुमायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम a flower, and आयुध a weapon: his shafts being tipped with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमाल|कुसुमालः
कुसुमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमावचाय|कुसुमावचायः
कुसुमावचाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gathering flowers.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and अवचाय, gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमावतंसक
कुसुमावतंसक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A chaplet, a crown of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and अवतंसक a tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमासव|कुसुमासवं
कुसुमासव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Honey.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमित
कुसुमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Flowered, budded, in flower.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमितलता
कुसुमितलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of the Dhṛti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुमेषु|कुसुमेषुः
कुसुमेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>A name of the god KĀMA.<BR>n. (-षु)<BR>The bow of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम, and इषु an arrow; whose shafts are flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसुम्भ|कुसुंभ|कुसुंभं|कुसुम्भं|कुसुंभः|कुसुम्भः
कुसुम्भ<BR>n. (-म्भं)<BR>1 Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>2 Gold.<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The water pot of the student and Sannyāsī.<BR>E.<BR>कुस to shine, and उम्भः Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसू
कुसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>An earthworm.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, सू produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसूल|कुसूलः
कुसूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A granary, &c. see कुशूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुसृति|कुसृतिः
कुसृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Wickedness, depravity.<BR>2 Conjuring, slight-ofhand, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, सृ to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुभ|कुस्तुभः
कुस्तुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, ष्टुभ to stop, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बरी
कुस्तुम्बरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A pungent seed used in condiments, coriander: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्तुम्बुरु|कुस्तुम्बुरुः
कुस्तुम्बुरु<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>Coriander, a pungent seed.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, vile, तुवि to take, उरु affix, deriv. irr.; also कुस्तुम्बरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्वप्न
कुस्वप्न<BR>m. (-प्नः)<BR>A bad dream, nightmare.<BR>E.<BR>कु, and स्वप्न a vision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुस्म
कुस्म<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुस्मयति)<BR>1 To smile improperly or blamably.<BR>2 To see mentally, to perceive, to imagine: this is considered by some as a denominative, and to be classed improperly amongst the roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
कुह<BR>r. 10th cl. (कुहयते)<BR>1 To surprise, to astonish, to excite wonder.<BR>2 To cheat, to impose upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुह|कुहः
कुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A medicinal drug: see कटुकी.<BR>ind.<BR>Where, whither, used in the Vedas in place of कुत्र.<BR>E.<BR>कु vile, and हा to leave, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहक|कुहकं|कुहकः
कुहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A cheat, a rogue, a juggler.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Juggling, deception, slight-of-hand, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुह to astonish, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=237" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहककार
कुहककार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Juggling, conjuring, cheating.<BR>E.<BR>कुहक, and कार who makes; also कुहककारक and कुहककारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकचकित
कुहकचकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suspicious, cautious, wary.<BR>E.<BR>कुहक, and चकित fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकजीविन्
कुहकजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living by slight-of-hand, a conjuror, a cheat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुहक deception, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकवृत्ति|कुहकवृत्तिः
कुहकवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Juggling, conjuring, slight-of-hand.<BR>2 Hypocrisy.<BR>E.<BR>कुहक, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकस्वन|कुहकस्वनः
कुहकस्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wild cock.<BR>E.<BR>कुहक deception, and खन who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहकस्वर|कुहकस्वरः
कुहकस्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wild cock: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहन|कुहनं|कुहनः
कुहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Envious.<BR>2 Hypocritical.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A rat.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Hypocrisy, assumed and sanctity, the interested performance of religious austerities.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A small earthen vessel.<BR>2 A glass vessel.<BR>E.<BR>कुह to surprise, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहनिका
कुहनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hypocrisy: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कुहन, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहर|कुहरं|कुहरः
कुहर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A cavity, a hollow.<BR>2 A hole, a rent, &c.<BR>3 The ear.<BR>4 A guttural sound.<BR>5 The throat or larynx.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of snake.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, &c. and हर what takes, &c. from हृ with the affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहरित|कुहरितं
कुहरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The song, or cry of the Kokila, the Indian cuckoo.<BR>2 Vox congressus in coitu.<BR>3 A sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>कुहर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहलि|कुहलिः
कुहलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A Pān, the leaf of the Piper betel, with small pieces of the Areca nut, and Catechu and a little lime, which are chewed and eaten by the Oriental nations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहु|कुहुः
कुहु<BR>f. (-हुः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहू
कुहू<BR>f. (-हूः)<BR>1 New moon; the first day of the first quarter on which the moon rises invisible.<BR>2 The cry of the Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>कुह to astonish, ऊः affix, or with कु affix कुहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूक
कुहूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूकण्ठ|कुहूकंठ|कुहूकण्ठः
कुहूकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>कुहू the Kokila's cry, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूपाल
कुहूपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूमुख|कुहूमुखः
कुहूमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The Kokila: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूरव|कुहूरवः
कुहूरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Kokila.<BR>E.<BR>कुहू, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहूल|कुहूलं
कुहूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pit, filled with stakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेडिका
कुहेडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fog, a mist, haze, haziness.<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, हेड to surround, वुन् affix; also कुहेलिक and कुहेडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेडी
कुहेडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>See the preceding: also कुहेली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुहेलिका
कुहेलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Fog, mist: see कुहेडिका, ल being changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू<BR>r. 6th cl. (ङ) कूङ (कुवते)<BR>To sound, especially as if in pain, to moan, to groan, &c.<BR>(ञ) कूञ् r. 9th cl. (कुनानि-नीते)<BR>To sound, &c. as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कू
कू<BR>f. (-कूः)<BR>A female Piśāca or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>कू to sound, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूकुद|कूकुदः
कूकुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who gives a girl in marriage with due ceremony, and suitable decorations.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to take, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूच|कूचः
कूच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A breast, a female breast, especially that of a young or unmarried woman: see कुच.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A painting brush or pencil.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, चट Uṇādi affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूचिका
कूचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small brush or hair pencil.<BR>E.<BR>कुच to be curved, and क्वुन् affix, with the fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूज|कूजः
कूज<BR>r. 1st cl. (कूजति)<BR>To make any inarticulate sound, to utter a cry as a bird, to coo as a pigeon, to caw as a crow, &c.<BR>With परि prefixed,<BR>to moan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजत्
कूजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>Cooing.<BR>E.<BR>कूज to coo, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजन|कूजनं
कूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cooing, moaning, uttering an inarticulate sound.<BR>E.<BR>कूज and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूजित|कूजितं
कूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cooed, uttered inarticulately.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The cry of a bird, cooing.<BR>E.<BR>कूज to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट|कूटः
कूट<BR>r. 10th cl. (कूटयते)<BR>1 To avoid or decline giving, to not give.<BR>2 To render indistinct or unintelligible, to muddle or render confused or foul.<BR>(कूटयति)<BR>1 To give pain.<BR>2 To burn.<BR>3 To call or invite, to counsel or advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूट|कूटः
कूट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A house, a dwelling: see कुट.<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>2 A water-jar.<BR>3 A heap of grain, &c.<BR>4 Uniform and elementary substance.<BR>5 A hammer, a mallet.<BR>6 A ploughshare.<BR>7 The body of a plough.<BR>8 A trap for catching deer.<BR>9 A concealed weapon, as a dagger in a wooden case, a sword-cane, &c.<BR>10 Illusion.<BR>11 Fraud, trick, deceit.<BR>12 Untruth, falsehood, (or attributively,) false, untrue.<BR>13 Vile, low.<BR>14 An ox whose horns are broken.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The name of a saint, also named AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>कूट to confuse, to withhold, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटक|कूटकं|कूटकः
कूटक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unfair, fraudulent.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A ploughshare.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A braid or tress of hair.<BR>2 A perfume: see मुरा.<BR>E.<BR>कूट to cut, and क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकार|कूटकारः
कूटकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A rogue.<BR>2 A cheat, a false witness.<BR>E.<BR>कूट, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकारक|कूटकारकः
कूटकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A false witness.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>कूट, and कारक who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटकृत्
कूटकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A Kāyastha or man of the writer cast.<BR>E.<BR>कूट illusion, &c. and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटज|कूटजः
कूटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कुटज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटता
कूटता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Falsehood, fraud.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to कूट; also with त्व, कूटत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटपर्व्व|कूटपर्व|कूटपर्वः
कूटपर्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>Fever occurring in an elephant from vitiation of the three humors; also read कूटपूर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटपाकल|कूटपाकलः
कूटपाकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A bilious fever in an elephant.<BR>2 A potter's kiln.<BR>E.<BR>कूट a heap, and पाक what ripens, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटयन्त्र|कूटयंत्र|कूटयन्त्रं
कूटयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A trap or snare for deer, birds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कूट a trap, and यन्त्र an implement; also simply कूट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशाल्मलि|कूटशाल्मलिः
कूटशाल्मलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A species of the Simul silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>कूट false, and शाल्मलि the Simul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटशासन
कूटशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A forged or false grant or decree.<BR>E.<BR>कूट, and शासन a grant, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटसाक्षिन्
कूटसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A false witness.<BR>E.<BR>कूट falsehood, and साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटस्थ|कूटस्थं|कूटस्थः
कूटस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Uniform, perpetually and universally the same, as spirit, elementary matter, aether, &c.<BR>n. (-स्थं)<BR>1 The soul.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, a species of dried shell fish, commonly Nakhi.<BR>E.<BR>कूट fixed, and स्थ what remains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटस्वर्ण
कूटस्वर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Alloyed or counterfeit gold. कूट, and स्वर्ण gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=238" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटाक्ष|कूटाक्षः
कूटाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Loaded or false dice.<BR>E.<BR>कूट, and अक्ष a die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटागार|कूटागारं
कूटागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An upper room, an apartment on the top of a house.<BR>E.<BR>कूट a peak, आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूटार्थभाषिता
कूटार्थभाषिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A tale, a story, a fiction.<BR>E.<BR>कूट false, अर्थ meaning, and भाषिता spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड
कूड<BR>r. 6th cl. (कूडति)<BR>1 To be or become firm or solid.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>3 To graze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूड्य|कूड्यं
कूड्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>A wall: see कुड्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूण
कूण<BR>r. 10th cl. (कूणयते-ति)<BR>To contract or close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणि|कूणिः
कूणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः णिः-णि)<BR>Crooked-armed, having a curved or withered arm: see कुणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणिका
कूणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The horn of any animal.<BR>2 The peg of a lute.<BR>E.<BR>कूण to sound or be crooked, वुन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूणित
कूणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contracted, shut, closed.<BR>E.<BR>कूण to contract, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूदर|कूदरः
कूदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The offspring of a Brahman woman by a Ṛṣi, begotten during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूद्दाल|कूद्दालः
कूद्दाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mountain ebony: see कुद्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कून
कून<BR>r. 10th cl. (कूनयति)<BR>To contract or close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप|कूपः
कूप<BR>r. 10th cl. (कूपयति)<BR>1 To be weak.<BR>2 To weaken: see कुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूप|कूपः
कूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A well.<BR>2 A hole, a hollow.<BR>3 A mast.<BR>4 A tree or rock in the midst of a river.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>1 A small well.<BR>2 The navel.<BR>3 A flask, a bottle.<BR>E.<BR>कु to sound, (frogs croaking in a well, &c.) and प Uṇādi affix: the vowel is made long; also कूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपक|कूपकः
कूपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The mast of a vessel.<BR>2 A stake, &c. to which a boat is moored.<BR>3 A leather oil vessel.<BR>4 The hollow below the loins.<BR>5 A funeral pile.<BR>6 A well.<BR>7 A temporary well, a hole dug for water in the dry bed of a rivulet.<BR>8 A tree or rock in the middle of a stream.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपमण्डूक
कूपमण्डूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A frog in a well, applied to a person of no enterprise, one who never leaves his home.<BR>E.<BR>कूप, and मण्डूक a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपाङ्ग|कूपांग|कूपाङ्गः
कूपाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Horripilation, erection of the hairs of the body.<BR>E.<BR>कूप a well, and अङ्ग the body; some copies read कूपाङ्क, from अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपार|कूपारः
कूपार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean; also कूवार, and अकूपार, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूपिका
कूपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A stone or rock in the middle of a stream: see कूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूम|कूमं
कूम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A lake, a pool, a pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर|कूरं|कूरः
कूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्च|कूर्च|कूर्चं|कूर्चः|कूर्च्चं|कूर्च्चः
कूर्च्च<BR>mn. (-र्च्चः-र्च्चं)<BR>1 The upper part of the nose, the part between the eye-brows.<BR>2 The beard.<BR>3 Deceit, fraud, circumvention.<BR>4 Hard, solid.<BR>5 The tip of the thumb and middle finger brought in contact, as to pinch, &c.<BR>6 A handful of Kusa grass or peacock's feathers.<BR>7 A bunch, a bundle, as of grass, &c.<BR>8 A brush of the same.<BR>9 The head.<BR>10 False praise, unmerited commendation, either of one's self or another person, boasting, flattery.<BR>11 Hypocrisy.<BR>12 The mystic syllable Hum.<BR>E.<BR>कूर to sound, चङ् affix, or कृ to do, उर्च्च affix or कूर्च्च Sautra root, to praise, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चक|कूर्चक|कूर्चकः
कूर्च्चक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A brush for cleaning the teeth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशिरस्|कूर्चशिरस्
कूर्च्चशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The heel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशीर्ष|कूर्चशीर्ष|कूर्चशीर्षः|कूर्च्चशीर्षः
कूर्च्चशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A drug, commonly Jivaka, one of the eight principal medicaments.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्च्च the beard, &c. and शीर्ष the head; being bearded: or from कूर्च्च praise, and शिर्ष chief; commendable amongst medicines; also with कन् added कूर्च्चशीर्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चशेखर|कूर्चशेखर|कूर्चशेखरः|कूर्च्चशेखरः
कूर्च्चशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The cocoa nut tree.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्च्च a bunch, and शेखर summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्च्चिका|कूर्चिका
कूर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Inspissated milk.<BR>2 A key.<BR>3 A bud, a blossom.<BR>4 A painting brush or pencil.<BR>5 A needle.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्च्च to praise, &c. वुन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्द|कूर्द्द
कूर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (कूर्दते)<BR>To play: see कुर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्दन|कूर्दनं|कूर्द्दन|कूर्द्दनं
कूर्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Playing, sport, pastime.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A festival in honour of KĀMADEVA, held on the day of full moon, in the month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्द to play, ल्युट् affix, fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्प|कूर्प|कूर्पं|कूर्पः
कूर्प्प<BR>n. (-र्प्पं)<BR>The space between the eye-brows.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, &c. deriv. irr.: see कूर्च्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पर|कूर्पर|कूर्परः
कूर्प्पर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>1 The elbow.<BR>2 The knee.<BR>E.<BR>कुर to sound, with क्विप् affix कुर, पर from पृ to nourish, the first vowel is made long; sometimes also कुर्पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पास|कूर्पास|कूर्पासः
कूर्प्पास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A cuirass or quilted jacket worn as armour: see कूर्प्पासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्प्पासक|कूर्पासक|कूर्पासकः
कूर्प्पासक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A bodice, a jacket with short sleeves worn next the body, by women especially.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्पर the elbow, आस to abide, घञ् affix, and र dropped, कूर्प्पास, see the preceding; again, कन् pleonastic affix added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्म|कूर्म|कूर्मः|कूर्म्मः
कूर्म्म<BR>mf. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी)<BR>1 A tortoise, a turtle.<BR>2 The descent of VIṢṆU as a tortoise to support the mountain Mandāra at the churning of the ocean.<BR>3 A peculiar gesticulation with the fingers.<BR>E.<BR>कु implying reverse, ऊर्म्मी speed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मचक्र|कूर्मचक्र|कूर्म्मचक्रं
कूर्म्मचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>An astrological diagram.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्म्म, and चक्र circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मपृष्ठ|कूर्मपृष्ठ|कूर्म्मपृष्ठः
कूर्म्मपृष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 Globe amaranth, (Gomphrena globosa.)<BR>2 The back or shell of a tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्म्म a tortoise, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मपृष्ठक|कूर्मपृष्ठक|कूर्म्मपृष्ठकं
कूर्म्मपृष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The cover of a dish, a lid.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूर्म्मराज|कूर्मराज|कूर्मराजः|कूर्म्मराजः
कूर्म्मराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The king of turtles, the tortoise supposed to uphold the world.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्म्म tortoise, and राज a king, from राजन् with टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल|कूलं
कूल<BR>r. 1st cl. (कूलति)<BR>To cover, to hide, to screen, to enclose: with अनु prefixed, to protect, to be kind to, as to a follower or dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूल|कूलं
कूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A bank, a shore.<BR>2 A heap, a mound.<BR>3 A pond or pool.<BR>4 The rear of an army.<BR>E.<BR>कूल to cover, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलक|कूलकं|कूलकः
कूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An anthill.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A mound of earth, a heap, a pile.<BR>2 A bank, a dyke.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलङ्कष|कूलंकष|कूलंकषः|कूलङ्कषः
कूलङ्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The ocean, the sea.<BR>2 The stream or current of a river.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>कूल a bank, कष to injure, affix स्वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलचर
कूलचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Frequenting the banks of rivers, grazing there, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कूल, चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलभू
कूलभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A bank, the land upon the bank or shore.<BR>E.<BR>कूल, and भू earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्रुज
कूलमुद्रुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Breaking down banks (as a river, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कूल, रुज to make sick, with उत् pre. and खश aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=239" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलमुद्वह
कूलमुद्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Carrying away the banks, (a river, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कूल, वह to bear, उत् pre. खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलवती
कूलवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>कूल a bank, and मतुप् poss. affix, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलहण्डक|कूलहंडक|कूलहण्डकः
कूलहण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eddy.<BR>E.<BR>कूल a bank, and हुडि to collect, वुन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूलिका
कूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Base or bottom part of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवर|कूवरः
कूवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Beautiful, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The pole of a carriage or wood to which the yoke is fixed.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A humpbacked man.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A carriage covered with a cloth or blanket.<BR>E.<BR>कू to sound, and वर from वृ to cherish, with अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूवरिन्
कूवरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A carriage.<BR>E.<BR>कूवर the pole, इनि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्ड|कूष्मांड|कूष्मांडः|कूष्माण्डः
कूष्माण्ड<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी)<BR>A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita pepo.)<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of sprite or imp, of which there exists a Gaṇa or class.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ; also कुम्माण्ड and कूष्माण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूष्माण्डक|कूष्माण्डकः
कूष्माण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd: see कूष्माण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, उष्म warm, and अण्ड an egg, here put for seed, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहना
कूहना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Hypocrisy, affectation of religious zeal or austerity: see कुहना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कूहा
कूहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A fog, a mist.<BR>E.<BR>कुह to astonish, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृ
कृ<BR>r. 5th cl. (ञ्) कृञ् (कृणोति कृणुते)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>(डु, ञ,) डुकृञ् r. 8th cl. (करोति कुरुते)<BR>To do, to make, to perform any kind of action:<BR>this root admits most of the prepositions and a variety of significations; it is also active or deponent, according to its prefix and import; as,<BR>.²1 With अति,<BR>(अतिकुरुते)<BR>To exceed, to do more.<BR>.²2 With अधि,<BR>(अधिकुरुते)<BR>a To surpass or overcome. .²b To superintend, to govern. .²c To hold of right. .²d To bear patiently. .²e To refrain from.<BR>.²3 With अनु<BR>(अनुकरोति)<BR>To copy, to imitate, to act like or after.<BR>.²4 With अप<BR>(अपकुरुते)<BR>a To wrong, to injure. .²b To do evil.<BR>.²5 With आङ्<BR>(आकुरुते)<BR>a To call. .²b To take shape or form.<BR>.²6 With उत्<BR>(उत्कुरुते)<BR>a To kill or hurt dangerously. .²b To collect, to assemble.<BR>.²7 With उद् and आङ्<BR>(उदाकुरुते)<BR>To reproach.<BR>.²8 With उप<BR>(उपकुरुते)<BR>To befriend, to serve or assist.<BR>.²9 With उप, and स inserted<BR>(उपस्कुरुते, or उपस्करोति)<BR>To alter.<BR>(उपस्करोति)<BR>a To polish, to adorn. .²b To assemble. .²c To reply.<BR>.²10 With तिरस्<BR>(तिरस्करोति)<BR>To abuse, to revile.<BR>.²11 With दुर्<BR>(दुष्करोति)<BR>To do evil.<BR>.²12 With निर् and आङ्<BR>(निराकुरुते)<BR>a To make light of, to contemn. .²b To expel. .²c To annihilate.<BR>.²13 With परि, and स inserted<BR>(परिष्करोति)<BR>To polish, to refine, to make elegant or perfect.<BR>.²14 With पर and आङ्<BR>(पराकरोति)<BR>To act well.<BR>.²15 With प्र<BR>(प्रकुरुते)<BR>a To begin. .²b To do any thing quickly. .²c To serve. .²d To allot, to portion. .²e To violate. .²f To chaunt, to recite.<BR>.²16 With प्रति<BR>(प्रतिकुरुते)<BR>a To counteract. .²b To retaliate. .²c To remedy.<BR>.²17 With प्रति and उप<BR>(प्रत्युपकुरुते)<BR>To requite, to return a kindness;<BR>.²18with वि<BR>(विकुरुते)<BR>a To utter, to sound. .²b To seek, to strive for.<BR>(विकरोति)<BR>a To alter, to change in form. .²b To disturb or agitate.<BR>.²19 With वि and आङ्<BR>(व्याकुरुते)<BR>a To explain, to expound. .²b To make manifest or public.<BR>.²20 With सम<BR>(संस्करोति)<BR>a To polish, to perfect. .²b To assemble, to bring together.<BR>.²21 With सु<BR>(सुकरोति)<BR>To do well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृक|कृकः
कृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The throat, the larynx.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, and क्वुन् affix, what makes or produces sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकण|कृकणः
कृकण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A kind of partridge, commonly Kaër, (Perdix sylvatica.)<BR>2 A worm.<BR>E.<BR>कृक the throat, and अण् to sound, affix अच्, the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकणीय
कृकणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a partridge.<BR>E.<BR>कृकण and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकर|कृकरः
कृकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of the five vital airs, that which assists in digestion.<BR>3 A kind of partridge: see कृकण.<BR>4 A sort of pepper, (P. chavya.)<BR>5 The oleander tree.<BR>E.<BR>कृक the throat, and र what gets or receives; or कृ imitative sound, and कर what makes, from कृ to make or do, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलाश|कृकलाशः
कृकलाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकलास|कृकलासः
कृकलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>E.<BR>कृक the throat, and लस to play, &c. affix अण्; also कृकलाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकु|कृकवाकुः
कृकवाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 A cock, a gallinaceous fowl.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>3 A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>E.<BR>कृक the throat, वच् to speak, Uṇādi affix ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकवाकुध्वज|कृकवाकुध्वजः
कृकवाकुध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>कृकवाकु a peacock, and ध्वज a standard or symbol; the peacock is the vehicle and standard of SKANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकाटिका
कृकाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The back of the neck.<BR>2 The raised and straight part of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>कृक the throat, अट to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृकुलास
कृकुलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon: see कृकलास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रं|कृच्छ्रः|कृछ्र
कृच्छ्र<BR>mfn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रा-च्छ्रं)<BR>1 Attended with pain, painful.<BR>2 Wicked, sinful.<BR>mn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रं)<BR>Bodily pain.<BR>2 Penance, expiation.<BR>3 Sin.<BR>4 Difficulty, labour, trouble.<BR>5 A kind of religious penance, according to some, the same as the Prājāpatya: (see प्राजापत्य); according to others, as the Sāntapana: (see सान्तपनं)<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, रक् Uṇādi affix, and छ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रगत
कृच्छ्रगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Embarrassed, distressed.<BR>2 Pained, suffering pain.<BR>E.<BR>कृच्छ्र, and गत gone to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्र|कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्रः
कृच्छ्रातिकृच्छ्र<BR>m. (-च्छ्रः)<BR>A kind of penance, taking no sustenance but water for three, nine, twelve, or twenty-one days.<BR>E.<BR>कृच्छ्र one kind of penance, and अतिकृच्छ्र another; the substance of both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृच्छ्रार्द्ध|कृच्छ्रार्द्धः
कृच्छ्रार्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>An inferior penance lasting six days.<BR>E.<BR>कृच्छ्र, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृड
कृड<BR>r. 6th cl. (कृडति)<BR>1 To be thick or coarse, to be gross, to be solid.<BR>2 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृणु|कृणुः
कृणु<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do or make, क्रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत<BR>(ई,) कृती r. 6th cl. (कृन्तति)<BR>To cut, to divide.<BR>r. 7th cl. (कृणति)<BR>To surround, to encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत|कृतं
कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done, made, performed.<BR>2 Injured, hurt.<BR>3 Fit, proper.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The first of the four ages of the world, the Satya yug.<BR>2 Fruit, consequence.<BR>adv.<BR>1 Enough, sufficient.<BR>2 Enough, completely finished.<BR>3 Enough, have done, no more.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, to injure, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक|कृतकं|कृतकः
कृतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Artificial, factitious, made, not produced spontaneously.<BR>2 Assumed, simulated, not natural.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Factitious salt, produced by boiling and evaporating from saline soils.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut or divide, Uṇādi affix अक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकपट
कृतकपट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Deceiving, beguiling, fraudulent.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and कपट deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्त्तव्य|कृतकर्तव्य
कृतकर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Having done or discharged, or being done, (a duty.) कृत done, कर्त्तव्य what was to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=240" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकर्म्मन्|कृतकर्मन्
कृतकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Skilful, clever, able.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकार्य्य|कृतकार्य
कृतकार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>See कृतकृत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकाल|कृतकालः
कृतकाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fixed, settled as to time.<BR>2 Sent or deposited, &c. for a certain time.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकूर्च्छक
कृतकूर्च्छक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Tied up as a small bundle or brush.<BR>E.<BR>कृतकूर्च्छ a bundle, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्य|कृतकृत्यः
कृतकृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Having done or discharged any thing to be done.<BR>2 Having accomplished or attained any object.<BR>3 Contented, satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, and कृत्य what was to be done; also कृतकर्त्तव्य, कृतकार्य्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकृत्यता
कृतकृत्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Success, attainment, accomplishment, the full discharge of any duty or realisation of any object.<BR>E.<BR>कृतकृत्य, and तल् affix; also with त्व affix, कृतकृत्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकोटि|कृतकोटिः
कृतकोटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>1 A name of the saint KAŚYAPA.<BR>2 A name of UPAVARṢA, another divine sage.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, कोटि excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतकोप
कृतकोप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Angry, indignant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and कोप anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रय|कृतक्रयः
कृतक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A purchaser, a buyer.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and क्रय purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रिय|कृतक्रियः
कृतक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Having finished or completed any thing in which one was engaged.<BR>2 Having attained any end or accomplished any object.<BR>3 Having fulfilled one's duty.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, क्रिया work, duty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतक्रुध
कृतक्रुध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Angry, resentful.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and क्रुधा wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघातयत्न
कृतघातयत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Assaulting, attacking, one who tries to kill.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, घात a blow, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्न|कृतघ्नः
कृतघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>1 Ungrateful, not acknowledging former good offices.<BR>2 Defeating or rendering vain all previous measures.<BR>E.<BR>कृत what has been done, and घ्न killing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतघ्नता
कृतघ्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ingratitude.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कृतघ्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतचूड|कृतचूडः
कृतचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A boy on whom the ceremony of tonsure has been performed.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and चूडा a crest, a lock of hair being left on the top of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतजन्मन्
कृतजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Generated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञ|कृतज्ञः
कृतज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Grateful, remembering former aid or favours.<BR>2 Observant of propriety, correct in conduct.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>कृत what is done, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतज्ञता
कृतज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Gratitude.<BR>E.<BR>कृतज्ञ, and तल् affix; also कृतज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृततीर्थ
कृततीर्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 A guide to holy places, &c. one who frequents them.<BR>2 A councillor, one fertile in expedients.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, तीर्थ pilgrimage, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतत्व
कृतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The being done or effected.<BR>E.<BR>त्व, added to कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदार
कृतदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A married man.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and दार a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतदास|कृतदासः
कृतदास<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>A self-engaged servant, a hired servant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, (spontaneously,) and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतधी
कृतधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>1 Prudent, considerate.<BR>2 Learned, educated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतध्वंस
कृतध्वंस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Defeated, overpowered.<BR>2 Injured, destroyed.<BR>3 Recollecting past transactions.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतध्वस्त
कृतध्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Lost after being once possessed or acquired.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, gained, ध्वस्त destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनाशक
कृतनाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ungrateful.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and नाशक who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिर्णेजन|कृतनिर्णेजनः
कृतनिर्णेजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A penitent, one who has performed penance or made expiation.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and निर्णेजन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतनिश्चय
कृतनिश्चय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Confident, sure, certain.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and निश्चय certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपुङ्ख|कृतपुंख|कृतपुङ्खः
कृतपुङ्ख<BR>mfn. (ङ्खः-ङ्खा-ङ्खं)<BR>Skilled in archery.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, made, पुङ्ख the feather of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्व्व|कृतपूर्व
कृतपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Done formerly or precedingly.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्व्वनाशन|कृतपूर्वनाशन
कृतपूर्व्वनाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Ingratitude, forgetting past services.<BR>E.<BR>कृतपूर्व्व, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपूर्व्विन्|कृतपूर्विन्
कृतपूर्व्विन्<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वी-र्व्विणी-र्व्वि)<BR>One by whom any thing was done in time past.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, पूर्व्व formerly, इनि affix of agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतपौरुष
कृतपौरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Behaving gallantly.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and पौरुष manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रणाम
कृतप्रणाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Saluting, making or having made obeisance.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and प्रणाम salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतप्रयत्न
कृतप्रयत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Active, industrious, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and प्रयत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतफल|कृतफलं
कृतफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Successful, fruitful.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Result, consequence of an act.<BR>2 A poisonous substance: see कृक्वोल.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबाहु
कृतबाहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु)<BR>Laying hand upon, touching.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and बाहु the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतबुद्धि
कृतबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Informed of one's duty, having acquired knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतभय
कृतभय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Alarmed, apprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमङ्गल
कृतमङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Blessed, consecrated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमन्यु
कृतमन्यु<BR>mfn. (-न्युः-न्युः-न्यु)<BR>Angry, offended, indignant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and मन्यु anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमाल|कृतमालः
कृतमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, माल a garland, garlands being made of its flowers; also आरग्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतमुख|कृतमुखः
कृतमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Skilled, clever, conversant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, and मुख chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरव
कृतरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Sounding, singing.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and रव a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरुच्
कृतरुच्<BR>mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>Splendid, brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and रुच् light; also कृतरुचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतरुष
कृतरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Angry, displeased.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and रुषा wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतलक्षण|कृतलक्षणः
कृतलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Excellent, amiable, &c. noted for good qualities.<BR>2 Defined, discriminated.<BR>3 Marked, stamped.<BR>4 Branded.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, लक्षण a mark, a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवत्|कृतवन्त्
कृतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Making, was making, made.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवाप|कृतवापः
कृतवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A penitent who has shaven his head and chin.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and वाप tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविक्रिय
कृतविक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Altered, changed.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and विक्रिय change; also कृतविकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविद्य
कृतविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Scientific, a philosopher.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=241" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतविस्मय
कृतविस्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Surpassing, astonishing.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and वित्पय wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेतन|कृतवेतनः
कृतवेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Hired as a servant or labourer.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, appointed, and वतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेदिन्
कृतवेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Grateful.<BR>2 Knowing, observant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेधन
कृतवेधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, a sort of Ghosha with white flowers: see घोष^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 307,308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेपथु
कृतवेपथु<BR>mfn. (-थुः-थुः-थु)<BR>Trembling.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and वेपथु trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतवेश
कृतवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Decorating, adorning.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and वेश dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतव्यलीक
कृतव्यलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Annoyed, vexed, irritated. कृत, and व्यलीक pain, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशक्ति
कृतशक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Putting forth one's strength or courage.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशोभ
कृतशोभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Splendid, brilliant.<BR>2 Beautiful, beautified.<BR>3 Dexterous, handy.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and शोभा splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतशौच
कृतशौच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Purified, cleansed, freed from the natural dejections, released from conventional defilement, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and शाच purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतश्रम|कृतश्रमः
कृतश्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Laborious, assiduous, persevering, painstaking, making great or continuous exertions.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसङ्केत|कृतसंकेत
कृतसङ्केत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Making an agreement or appointment.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and सङ्केत agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंसर्ग
कृतसंसर्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>Approximate, united.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and संसर्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसंस्कार
कृतसंस्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Initiated, having undergone all the purificatory ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and संस्कार rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसज्ञ
कृतसज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Distinguished by appropriate marks, devices, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and सज्ञा a signal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसन्निधान|कृतसंनिधान
कृतसन्निधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Contracted, approximated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and सन्निधान proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसम्बन्ध
कृतसम्बन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Connected, allied.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and सम्बन्ध alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतसापत्निका
कृतसापत्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose husband has taken another wife.<BR>E.<BR>कृक made, स with, together with, पत्नी a wife, affix कन्: or derived from सापत्नक, कृतसापत्नका; also कृतसापत्नी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतस्थिति
कृतस्थिति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Abiding, staying, taking up an abode in or with.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतस्वस्त्ययन
कृतस्वस्त्ययन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Recommended to the protection of gods previous to any journey or undertaking.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, स्वस्त्ययन benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतहस्त|कृतहस्तः
कृतहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Skilled in archery.<BR>2 Clever, skilful, dexterous.<BR>E.<BR>कृत exercised, हस्त the hand; also कृतहस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताकृत|कृताकृतः
कृताकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done in part, not completed.<BR>2 Committed and omitted.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अकृत undone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागम
कृतागम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Advanced, proficient.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतागस्
कृतागस्<BR>mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः)<BR>Criminal, offending, in fault.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, अगस् crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताग्निकार्य्य|कृताग्निकार्य
कृताग्निकार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A Brahman who has offered the usual oblations with fire.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अग्निकार्य्य fire-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताङ्क|कृतांक|कृताङ्कः
कृताङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>1 Marked.<BR>2 Numbered.<BR>3 Branded.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलि|कृतांजलि|कृताञ्जलिः
कृताञ्जलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>One who joins the palms of the hands, making such a sign of reverence or solicitation, reverent, respectful.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A shrub used in medicine, also in magical potions, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, अञ्जलि the hand joined, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताञ्जलिपुट
कृताञ्जलिपुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Joining the palms of the hands for the purpose of doing obeisance, also for holding water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अञ्जलिपुट the palms joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतात्मन्
कृतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Subdued, tranquil, of a self-governed spirit.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानति
कृतानति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Bending, bowed, paying homage or respect.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आनति bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुकूल्य
कृतानुकूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Kind, favouring, compliant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, आनुकूल्य favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुव्याध
कृतानुव्याध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Mixed, combined, united.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अनुव्याध mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतानुसार|कृतानुसारः
कृतानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Established practice, usage, custom, rate.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अनुसार custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्त|कृतांत|कृतान्तः
कृतान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA, son of SŪRYA, and regent of the dead, or death personified.<BR>2 Destiny, that is, the inevitable result of actions done in a past existence.<BR>3 A demonstrated conclusion, proved or established doctrine.<BR>4 Sinful or inauspicious action.<BR>5 Saturday, which is considered as an unlucky day.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A perfume: see रेणुका.<BR>E.<BR>कृत act, (actum) done, अन्त end, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्तक
कृतान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतान्तजनक|कृतांतजनक|कृतान्तजनकः
कृतान्तजनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>कृतान्त YAMA, and जनक progenitor; being the father of YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापकार
कृतापकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Injured, wronged.<BR>2 Discomfited, overpowered.<BR>3 Doing wrong, offending.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अपकार offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापदान
कृतापदान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Completing a task, effecting an object.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अपदान accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतापराध
कृतापराध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Guilty, culpable, an offender.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताभिषेक|कृताभिषेकः
कृताभिषेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>2 Inaugurated.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A prince, &c. who has been inaugurated.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अभिषेक sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थ|कृतार्थः
कृतार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Successful, having attained an end, having accomplished a purpose or desire.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थता
कृतार्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Success, fruitfulness, accomplishment of an object.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also कृतार्थत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थीकृत
कृतार्थीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rendered successful.<BR>E.<BR>कृतार्थ, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतार्थीभूत
कृतार्थीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become successful.<BR>E.<BR>कृतार्थ, and भूत been, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतालय|कृतालयः
कृतालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>कृत made, आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधान
कृतावधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Careful, cautious, prudent, attentive.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावधि
कृतावधि<BR>mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>1 Fixed, appointed, agreed upon.<BR>2 Bounded, limited.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अवधि term, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावमर्ष
कृतावमर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>1 Disregarding, effacing from recollection.<BR>2 Intolerant.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अवमर्ष impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=242" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावशक्थिक|कृतावशक्थिकः
कृतावशक्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Seated on the hams with the knees tied together, or the hips and knees surrounded by a cloth.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अवशक्थिका the cloth so used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावस्थ
कृतावस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Summoned, called.<BR>2 Made present.<BR>3 Fixed, settled.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अवस्था condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतावास
कृतावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A lodging, a temporary accommodation, an apartment.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताशन
कृताशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Feeding upon.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्कन्दन
कृतास्कन्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Assailing, attacking.<BR>2 Effacing from recollection.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आस्कन्दन going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्त्र
कृतास्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Armed.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अस्त्र weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतास्पद
कृतास्पद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Governed, ruled.<BR>2 Supporting, rested upon by any thing.<BR>3 Residing in or on, taking one's abode.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आस्पद place, rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताहक
कृताहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having performed the daily ceremonies, or devotions.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, अहन् a day, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृताह्वान
कृताह्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Summoned, called.<BR>2 Challenged.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and आह्वान calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृति|कृतिः
कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Act, action, acting, doing, &c.<BR>2 Injuring, hurt, hurting.<BR>3 A sort of metre, a stanza of four lines, with twenty syllables in each.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, to injure, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिकर|कृतिकरः
कृतिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृति injuring, कृ to do, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतिन्
कृतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Wise, learned.<BR>2 Clever, skilful.<BR>3 Good, virtuous.<BR>4 Pure, pious.<BR>5 Following, obeying, doing what is enjoined.<BR>E.<BR>कृत done, performed, इनि affix; by whom proper acts are done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृते
कृते<BR>ind.<BR>For, on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतेर्ष्य
कृतेर्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं)<BR>Envious, jealous.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and ईर्ष्या envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोच्चैस्
कृतोच्चैस्<BR>ind.<BR>Raised on high.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उच्चैस्^1 high.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोदक
कृतोदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having performed ablutions.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोद्वाह
कृतोद्वाह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Performing penance by standing with uplifted hands.<BR>2 Married.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उद्वाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपकार
कृतोपकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Assisted, befriended.<BR>2 Friendly, giving aid.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उपकार help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपनयन
कृतोपनयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The student invested with the sacrificial cord.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उपनयन investiture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृतोपभोग
कृतोपभोग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Used, enjoyed.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and उपभोग use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्त|कृत्तं
कृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Cut, divided.<BR>2 Desired, sought, wished for.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्ति|कृत्तिः
कृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 The hide upon which the religious student sits, sleeps, &c. usually the skin of an antelope.<BR>2 The skin.<BR>3 The bark of the Bhojpatra, used for writing upon, for making hooka snakes, &c.<BR>4 One of the lunar mansions: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिका
कृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The third of the lunar mansions, or constellations in the moon's path, consisting of six stars, and corresponding to the Pleiades.<BR>2 (In mythology,) a nymph; one of six, the nurses of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, क्तिन् and कन् affixes; the figure of the asterism is a razor or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकाभव|कृत्तिकाभवः
कृत्तिकाभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्तिका the constellation, and मव who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिकासुत|कृत्तिकासुतः
कृत्तिकासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of SKANDA or KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्तिका, and सुत the son; the nymphs so named being his foster mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवास|कृत्तिवासः
कृत्तिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>ŚIVA: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्तिवासस्
कृत्तिवासस्<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An appellation of MAHĀDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्ति a skin or hide, and वासस् clothes; clothes with a tiger^1's skin; also कृत्तिवास.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्नु|कृत्नुः
कृत्नु<BR>mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु)<BR>An artist, an artificer or mechanic.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, कत्नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्य|कृत्यं|कृत्यः
कृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 To be done or performed.<BR>2 To be rendered murderous or mischievous, hired as an assassin, seduced from allegiance or alliance, hostile through covetousness, &c.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 Action, act.<BR>2 A female deity, to whom sacrifices are offered for destructive and magical purposes.<BR>3 Magic.<BR>4 A pestilence.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Motive, cause.<BR>2 The class of affixes in grammar forming nouns corresponding to gerunds and supines, chiefly with a passive signification, but sometimes active, and sometimes abstract nouns.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to injure, to divide, &c. क्यप् or यत् affixed, or कृत to injure, वुन् affix, and य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यक
कृत्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यज्ञ
कृत्यज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Learned, wise, who knows what is to be done.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्य, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यवर्त्मन्
कृत्यवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>The right way, the manner in which any object is to be effected.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्य, and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविद्
कृत्यविद्<BR>mf. (-विद्)<BR>Learned, wise, who knows what is to be done.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्य, and विद who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्यविधि|कृत्यविधिः
कृत्यविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>The way to do any thing, a rule or precept.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्य, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिम|कृत्रिमं|कृत्रिमः
कृत्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Made, factitious, artificial, the reverse of what is naturally or spontaneously produced.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Incense, olibanum.<BR>2 An adopted son, used for कृत्रिमपुत्र.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A kind of salt, the common Bit Noben or Bit Lavan,<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, क्त्रि Uṇādi affix, and मम् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमधूप|कृत्रिमधूपः
कृत्रिमधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A compound perfume, containing ten or eighteen ingredients.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्रिम artificial, and धूप resin; also with कन् added कृत्रिमधूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिमपुत्र|कृत्रिमपुत्त्रः|कृत्रिमपुत्रः
कृत्रिमपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An adopted son; one of the twelve kinds recognized in law, the son made.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्रिम, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्रिममित्र|कृत्रिममित्रः
कृत्रिममित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An acquired friend; one on whom benefits have been conferred, or from whom they have been received.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्रिम made, and मित्र a friend; also similar compounds in this or other senses, कृत्रिमशत्रु an acquired enemy, कृत्रिमौदसीन one who is indifferent to benefits or injuries, neither an acquired friend nor foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्वा
कृत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having done, made, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स|कृत्सं|कृत्सः
कृत्स<BR>n. (-त्सं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Entire, whole.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to surround, and स Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्न|कृत्स्नं|कृत्स्नः
कृत्स्न<BR>mfn. (-त्स्नः-त्स्ना-त्स्नं)<BR>All, whole, entire.<BR>n. (-त्स्नं)<BR>Water.<BR>2 The flank or hip.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to encompass, क्स्न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नविद्
कृत्स्नविद्<BR>mfn. (-वित् or -विद्)<BR>Omniscient, acquainted with all things.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्स्न all, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृत्स्नशस्
कृत्स्नशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Wholly, entirely, altogether.<BR>E.<BR>कृत्स्न, and शम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=243" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदर|कृदरं|कृदरः
कृदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A granary, a cupboard, &c. for holding corn, grain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to contain, Uṇādi affix अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृदन्त
कृदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A noun formed by the application of the affixes termed कृत् to the root.<BR>E.<BR>कृत, and अन्त a final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तत्र|कृंतत्र|कृंतत्रं|कृन्तत्रं
कृन्तत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A plough.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to divide or cut, कत्रन् Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तन|कृंतन|कृंतनं|कृन्तनं
कृन्तन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Cutting.<BR>E.<BR>कृति to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृन्तनिका
कृन्तनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A knife.<BR>2 The edge of a knife.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप<BR>(ऊ, ऌ) ऊकृपॢ r. 1st cl. (कल्पते)<BR>To be able.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (कल्पति, कल्पयति)<BR>1 To think or imagine.<BR>2 To mix.<BR>3 To paint or colour.<BR>r. 1st cl. (कृपति)<BR>To have pity or mercy^1.<BR>r. 10th cl. (कृपयति)<BR>To be weak. In the first roots ल ॡ is substituted for ऋ.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृप|कृपः
कृप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The name of a sage, the brother-in-law of DROṆA.<BR>2 A name of VYĀSA, the compiler of the Vedas and Purāṇas.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>Tenderness, compassionateness.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The wife of the sage DROṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, &c. अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपण|कृपणः
कृपण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Miserly, avaricious.<BR>2 Low, vile.<BR>3 Poor, feeble, miserable, pitiable.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A worm.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, क्वुन् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाण|कृपाणः
कृपाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar or sacrificial knife.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A knife.<BR>2 A shears or scissors^1.<BR>4 A dagger.<BR>E.<BR>कृपा mercy, नुद to destroy, ड aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणक|कृपाणकः
कृपाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to कृपाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाणिका
कृपाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to कृपाण, and the fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाद्वैत|कृपाद्वैतः
कृपाद्वैत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the Buddhas or deified saints of the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>कृपा compassion, and अद्वैत not second; unequalled for tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपालु|कृपालुः
कृपालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Compassionate, tender.<BR>E.<BR>कृपा tenderness, आलुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपामय
कृपामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Compassionate: so कृपावत् (-वान्-वती-वत्) कृपान्वित (-तः-ता-तं) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपाहीन
कृपाहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unfeeling, unkind, hardhearted.<BR>E.<BR>कृपा, हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीट|कृपीटं
कृपीट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 The belly.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A wood, a forest.<BR>4 Wood, timber.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, कीटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीटपाल|कृपीटपालः
कृपीटपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A rudder or large oar used as one.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>कृपीट water, पाल what preserves, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीटयोनि|कृपीटयोनिः
कृपीटयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>कृपीट water, योनि source, place of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीपति|कृपीपतिः
कृपीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of DROṆĀCĀRYA.<BR>E.<BR>कृपी the wife of the sage, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृपीपुत्र
कृपीपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>AŚVATTHĀMA a sage, the son of KṚPĪ and DROṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृपी, and पुत्र a son, or with other synonyms of a son, as कृपीसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृब
कृब<BR>r. 1st cl. or 5th cl. (इ,) कृवि (कृणोति)<BR>1 To kill, to hurt or injure in any way.<BR>2 To act, to do.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR>4 To be in pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमि|कृमिः
कृमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A worm, an insect in general.<BR>2 Lac, the red dye, which is in fact an insect.<BR>5 An Asura or demon.<BR>4 One subject to worms.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, इन् Uṇādi affix, and the corresponding vowel substituted for र; also किमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकण्टक|कृमिकण्टकं
कृमिकण्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A plant used in medicine: see बिडङ्ग.<BR>2 Opposite leaved fig tree.<BR>3 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata): see मूषिकपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, and कण्टक a thorn, a foe; also क्रिमिकण्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकर्ण|कृमिकर्णः|कृमिकर्ण्ण
कृमिकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Worms or lice generating in the external ear.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिकोशोत्थ
कृमिकोशोत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>Silken, silk.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, कोश a ball, and उत्थ what comes or rises from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिग्रन्थि|कृमिग्रन्थिः
कृमिग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>Insects generated at the roots of the eyelashes.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and ग्रन्थि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिघ्न|कृमिघ्नः
कृमिघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Vermifuge, anthelmintic.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 A shrub used in medicine, as an anthelmintic, commonly Bireṅg, (Erycibe paniculata, Rox.) see बिडङ्ग.<BR>2 The onion.<BR>3 The root of the jujube.<BR>4 The marking nut plant.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, हन् to kill, and टक् affix; also क्रिमिघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिज|कृमिजं
कृमिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Agallochum: see क्रिमिज.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Lac, a red dye so called.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि an insect, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिदन्तक|कृमिदन्तकः
कृमिदन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Toothache with decay of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and दन्त a tooth, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिन्
कृमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Affected with worms.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिरिपु|कृमिरिपुः
कृमिरिपु<BR>n. (-पुः)<BR>An anthelmintic plant: see कृमिघ्न.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and रिपु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिल
कृमिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having worms, wormy.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A fruitful woman, one bearing many children.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, and ला to receive, to get, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशङ्ख|कृमिशंख|कृमिशङ्खः
कृमिशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>The fish of the conch.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशुक्ति|कृमिशुक्तिः
कृमिशुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>An oyster.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि an insect, and शुक्ति oyster-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिशैल|कृमिशैलः
कृमिशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An ant or mole hill.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि a worm, and शैल a hill; also with कन् added, कृमिशैलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमिहर
कृमिहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Anthelmintic, vermifuge.<BR>E.<BR>कृमि, and हर what removes; so कृमिहन्तृ (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृमीलक|कृमीलकः
कृमीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wild sort of kidney bean: see बनमुद्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवि|कृविः
कृवि<BR>r. 5th cl. (कृविणीति)<BR>To want to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृवि|कृविः
कृवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>A loom.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make, (cloth,) and क्विन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश<BR>r. 4th cl. (इर) कृशिर (कृश्यति)<BR>To make thin or small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृश|कृशः
कृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Small, thin, little, minute.<BR>2 Thin, spare, emaciated.<BR>3 Weak, feeble.<BR>E.<BR>कृश to pare or make thin, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशता
कृशता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Leanness, thinness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, कृशत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशर|कृशरः
कृशर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>1 A dish composed of milk, sesamum, and rice.<BR>2 Rice and pease boiled together with a few spices, commonly Khichree; also कृसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशला
कृशला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>कृश minute, ल what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाकु
कृशाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 Heating.<BR>2 Grieving.<BR>E.<BR>कृश to make small, and काकु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाक्ष|कृशाक्षः
कृशाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>कृश, अक्षि eye, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाङ्ग|कृशाङ्गः
कृशाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Spare, thin, emaciate.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A woman with a slender shape.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Priyangu: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>कृश thin, अङ्ग the body, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=244" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानु|कृशानुः
कृशानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A name of fire.<BR>2 A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>कृश to make thin, आनुक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशानुरेतस्
कृशानुरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>कृशानु fire, and रेतस् semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्व
कृशाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The name of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृशाश्विन्
कृशाश्विन्<BR>m. (-श्वी)<BR>A dancer, an actor, a tumbler.<BR>E.<BR>कृशाश्व the name of a saint, the author of directions to players, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष
कृष<BR>r. 1st cl. (आ) औकृश (कर्षति) and 6th cl. (कृषति-ते)<BR>1 To draw or make furrows.<BR>2 To plough.<BR>With अप,<BR>1 To draw down.<BR>2 To debase.<BR>3 To disregard.<BR>With अव,<BR>1 To draw out or off.<BR>2 To disregard or contemn.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To attract, to draw to.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To raise, to draw up.<BR>2 To raise, to excite, to make high, proud, loud, &c.<BR>With सम,<BR>To draw together.<BR>With सम and नि,<BR>To bring near or close to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषक|कृषकः
कृषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What or who makes furrows or ploughs.<BR>2 Attractive, attrahent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ploughshare.<BR>2 A husbandman, a peasant.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, &c. Uṇādi affix, क्वुन्; also कृषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाण|कृषाणः
कृषाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A husbandman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषाणु|कृषाणुः
कृषाणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A name of fire: see कृशानु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषि|कृषिः
कृषि<BR>f. (-षिः)<BR>1 Husbandry, agriculture.<BR>2 Ploughing, cultivating the soil, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, इक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिक|कृषिकः
कृषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ploughshare.<BR>2 A husbandman, a cultivator.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, Uṇādi affix किकन्; also कृषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिजीविन्
कृषिजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A cultivator, a farmer.<BR>E.<BR>कृषि, and नीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषिफल
कृषिफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Agricultural produce or profit.<BR>E.<BR>कृषि, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृषीबल
कृषीबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>One who lives by agriculture, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>कृषि agriculture, वलच् affix, and इ made ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्कर|कृष्करः
कृष्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An appellation of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ट|कृष्टं
कृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ploughed or tilled, a field, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपच्य|कृष्टपच्यः
कृष्टपच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Sown in ripening after ploughing, (rice, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ट ploughed, पच to ripen, and क्यप् affix; in some places the grain is sown without previous ploughing, whence it is called अकृष्टपच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टपाक्य|कृष्टपाक्यं
कृष्टपाक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Sown or rather ripening after ploughing: see कृष्टपच्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्टि|कृष्टिः
कृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A teacher, a learned man or Paṇḍita.<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Ploughing, cultivating the soil.<BR>2 Attracting, drawing.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, to trace, ति or क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णंश्रित
कृष्णंश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Devoted to Kṛṣṇa.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्णं second case, श्रित serving; also कृष्णश्रित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्ण|कृष्णं|कृष्णः
कृष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Black or dark blue.<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>1 Black, the colour, or dark blue, which is often confounded with it by the Hindus.<BR>2 KṚṢṆA, the most celebrated form of VIṢṆU, or rather VIṢṆU himself; he is distinct from the ten Avatāras or incarnations, being identified with the deity.<BR>3 VYĀSA, a sage, the compiler of the Vedas.<BR>4 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>5 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>6 A crow.<BR>7 A fruit, Karonda or Karinda, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>8 The dark half of the lunar month from full to new moon.<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>1 Black pepper.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>3 Blue vitriol.<BR>4 Black agallochum.<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>1 A name of DRAUPADĪ wife of the PĀṆḌAVAS.<BR>2 The indigo plant.<BR>3 Long pepper.<BR>4 A grape.<BR>5 A drug, commonly Kakoli.<BR>6 Kalonji, (Nigella Indica): see कृष्णजीरक.<BR>7 Black mustard, (the name is applied to other vegetable substances of a dark colour.)<BR>8 The Kṛṣṇā river in the Dekhin.<BR>9 A black leech, considered poisonous.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to attract, as the minds of men, &c. नक् Uṇādi affix; (this is applied to KṚṢṆA, &c.) else, कृष to tinge, affix the same; again कृष्ण black, &c. and अच् affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकन्द|कृष्णकंद|कृष्णकन्दं
कृष्णकन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The red lotus, (Nymphaea rubra.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and कन्द stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकर्म्मन्|कृष्णकर्मन्
कृष्णकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Criminal, guilty.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Making black.<BR>2 Cauterising.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and कर्म्मन् action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकाक|कृष्णकाकः
कृष्णकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकाष्ठ|कृष्णकाष्ठं
कृष्णकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A black variety of agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकेलि|कृष्णकेलिः
कृष्णकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A plant, (Mirabilis jalapa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णकोहल|कृष्णकोहलः
कृष्णकोहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gamester, a gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचतुर्द्दशी|कृष्णचतुर्दशी
कृष्णचतुर्द्दशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The fourteenth day in the dark half of a month.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण dark, चतुर्द्दशी fourteen; it is the day preceding new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचर|कृष्णचरः
कृष्णचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Formerly or in a former existence, KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and चरट् affix, implying former state of being; also कृष्णरुप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचूडा
कृष्णचूडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>A shrub, (Poinciana pulcherrima.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णचूर्ण|कृष्णचूर्णं|कृष्णचूर्ण्ण
कृष्णचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Rust of iron, iron filings.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and चूर्णं powder, dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णजटा
कृष्णजटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Indian spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, जटा twisted hair, to which its entangled stalks are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णजीरक|कृष्णजीरकः
कृष्णजीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Kalonji, a plant having a small black seed, which is used for medical and culinary purposes, (Nigella Indica, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and जीरक cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णता
कृष्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Blackness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to कृष्ण; with त्व, कृष्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णताम्र|कृष्णताम्रं
कृष्णताम्र<BR>n. (-म्रं)<BR>A kind of Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and तास्र copper, of a dusky copper hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णतार|कृष्णतारः
कृष्णतार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A deer, an antelope.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and तार the pupil of the eye, black-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णत्रिवृता
कृष्णत्रिवृता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, black Teöri: see चिवृता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णदशन
कृष्णदशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having bad or discoloured teeth.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and दशन a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णदेह|कृष्णदेहः
कृष्णदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Black-bodied.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णद्वैपायन|कृष्णद्वैपायनः
कृष्णद्वैपायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VYĀSA, the compiler of the Vedas, and Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>a compound of two other names of the sage: see कृष्ण, and द्वैपायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णधत्तूर
कृष्णधत्तूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A dark species of Datura or thorn apple, (Datura fastuosa): see घत्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपक्ष|कृष्णपक्षः
कृष्णपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The dark half of a month, the fifteen days during which the moon is in the wane.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण dark, and पक्ष fortnight or half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=245" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपाक|कृष्णपाकः
कृष्णपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree bearing a small fruit, which, when ripe, is of a black colour, commonly Karinda or Karonda, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and पाक what is ripe, from पच to ripen, to cook, and घञ् affix; also कृष्णफल, and कृष्णपाकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपाकफल|कृष्णपाकफलः
कृष्णपाकफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Karonda: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, added to कृष्णपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिङ्गला
कृष्णपिङ्गला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and पिङ्गल tawny; being of such of such a colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिण्डीतक|कृष्णपिण्डीतकः
कृष्णपिण्डीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dark kind of Māyana, (Vangueria spinosa).<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and पिण्डीतक the Mayan or Mayana tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिण्डीर|कृष्णपिण्डीरः
कृष्णपिण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A dark kind of Mayan: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपिपीली
कृष्णपिपीली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The black ant.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and पिपील ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णपुष्प|कृष्णपुष्पः
कृष्णपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A black kind of Datūra.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>Another plant: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णफल|कृष्णफलः
कृष्णफल<BR>(-लः)<BR>A fruit tree, the Karinda: see कृष्णपाक.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica): see सोमराजी.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णफलपाक|कृष्णफलपाकः
कृष्णफलपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fruit: see the preceding; also कृष्णपाकफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभूमि
कृष्णभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>A country with a dark soil, one of mould, blue clay, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and भूमि earth; also with a final अ, कृष्णभूमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभूमिजा
कृष्णभूमिजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A species of grass, described as a nourishing food for cattle.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्णभूमि black earth, and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णभेदी
कृष्णभेदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, hence, dirt or excrement, and भेदी what breaks, or dissipates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमुद्ग|कृष्णमुद्गः
कृष्णमुद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, मुद्ग phaseolus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमृत्
कृष्णमृत्<BR>f. (-मृत्)<BR>A country with a soil of a dark colour.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and मृत् earth: see कृष्णभूमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णमृत्तिका
कृष्णमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णरुप्य
कृष्णरुप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Formerly KṚṢṆA: see कृष्णचर.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and रुप्य affix, implying past state of being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलवण|कृष्णलवणं
कृष्णलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A factitious salt, either that prepared by evaporation from saline soil, or the medicinal kind, called Bit Loben or Bit Noben, a muriate of soda with a proportion of sulphur and iron.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णल|कृष्णलः
कृष्णल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Ratti, a weight, the berry so used; or an artificial weight derived from it, the berry averaging about 1¼ grain, the weight 2(3/16) grains.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A shrub bearing a small black and red berry, the Ratti or Gunja: see गुञ्जा.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण blackness, and ल what gets, from ला to obtain, affix ड and fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलक|कृष्णलकः
कृष्णलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Ratti, the jeweller's weight, the fifth of a Māṣa.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलोह|कृष्णलोहं|कृष्णलोहः
कृष्णलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण what attracts, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णलोहित|कृष्णलोहितः
कृष्णलोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Of a purple colour.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and लोहित red; of which two colours purple is supposed to consist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवक्त्र|कृष्णवक्त्रः
कृष्णवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>The black faced monkey.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and वक्त्र the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवर्ण|कृष्णवर्णः|कृष्णवर्ण्ण
कृष्णवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Black or dark blue.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>The colour black.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवर्त्मन्
कृष्णवर्त्मन्<BR>m. (-र्त्ना)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 RĀHU or the personified ascending node.<BR>3 A low man, an outcaste, a profligate, a blackguard.<BR>4 The marking nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and वर्त्मन् a path or way; whose way is darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवल्ली
कृष्णवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A plant, a dark kind of Babul, (Ocymum pilosum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवानर|कृष्णवानरः
कृष्णवानर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A black monkey.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and वानर an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवीज|कृष्णवीजं|कृष्णवीजः
कृष्णवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A red variety of the Morunga: see रक्तशीग्र.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and वीज the seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवृन्ता
कृष्णवृन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 A leguminous plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and वृन्त foot-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णवृन्तिका
कृष्णवृन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Gmelina arborea): see गम्भारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशार|कृष्णशारः
कृष्णशार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The black antelope: see कृष्णसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशालि|कृष्णशालिः
कृष्णशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of rice of a dark colour.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशिम्बी
कृष्णशिम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Dolichos virosus.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and शिम्बी a Dolichos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णशृङ्ग|कृष्णशृंग|कृष्णशृङ्गः
कृष्णशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and शृङ्ग a horn, black, horned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णश्रित
कृष्णश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Worshipping or devoted to KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and श्रित attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसख|कृष्णसखः
कृष्णसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A friend or follower of KṚṢṆA, especially ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and सखि a friend, टच् affix in this class of compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसखि
कृष्णसखि<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>Cummin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसर्प
कृष्णसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A black snake.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसर्षप|कृष्णसर्षपः
कृष्णसर्षप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and सर्षप mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसार|कृष्णसारः
कृष्णसार<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>A timber tree, Sisū, (Dalbergia Sisu, Rox.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The black antelope.<BR>2 Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>2 A thorny plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसारङ्ग|कृष्णसारङ्गः
कृष्णसारङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The black antelope.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and सारङ्ग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णसारथि|कृष्णसारथिः
कृष्णसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and सारथि charioteer; driven by KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णस्कन्ध|कृष्णस्कन्धः
कृष्णस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A tree which bears black blossoms, the Tamāla tree.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and स्कन्ध the shoulder: see कालस्कन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णागुरु
कृष्णागुरु<BR>n. (-रु)<BR>Agallochum or aloe wood, the black variety.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and अगुरु aloe wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाचल|कृष्णाचलः
कृष्णाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Raivata, part of the western portion of the Vindhya chain; it is also one of the nine principal mountains that separate the same divisions or Varṣas of the known world.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णानदी
कृष्णानदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The name of a river, possibly the Kistṇa in the Dekin.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and नदी a river, the river of KṚṢṆA; also other analogous names, as कृष्णसमुद्भवा, कृष्णवेण्या, कृष्णगङ्गा, &c.; also कृष्णा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णामिष|कृष्णामिषं
कृष्णामिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and आमिप flesh, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णायस|कृष्णायसं
कृष्णायस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Iron, crude or black iron.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and अयस iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णार्च्चिस्|कृष्णार्चिस्
कृष्णार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=246" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णार्जक|कृष्णार्जकः
कृष्णार्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A black species of basil: see कृष्णवल्ली.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and अर्जक basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णावास|कृष्णावासः
कृष्णावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण the deity, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णाश्रित|कृष्णाश्रितः
कृष्णाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Devoted to or the votary of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and आश्रित attached or devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिका
कृष्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, कन् affix, the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णिमन्
कृष्णिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Blackness.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीकरण|कृष्णीकरणं
कृष्णीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Blackening, making black.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्णं, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीकृत
कृष्णीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blackened, made black.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णीभूत
कृष्णीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Being or become black, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण, भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृष्णेक्षु|कृष्णेक्षुः
कृष्णेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>कृष्ण black, and इक्षु sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कृसर|कृसरः
कृसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A dish consisting of sesamum and grain.<BR>2 A mixture of rice and peas with a few spices.<BR>E.<BR>कॄ to scatter, सरः Uṇādi affix; also कृशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄ
कॄ<BR>r. 6th cl. (किरति)<BR>To throw, to scatter.<BR>r. 9th cl. (कृणति) or (गि, ञ्) गिकॄञ् (कृणाति-कृणीते)<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR>r. 10th cl. (कारयते)<BR>To know.<BR>.²1 With अप prefixed<BR>a To draw furrows, to make lines. .²b To disperse.<BR>.²2 With अव,<BR>To throw, to cast.<BR>.²3 With आङ्,<BR>To fill up, to cover over.<BR>.²4 With प्रति,<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR>.²5 With वि,<BR>To throw, to caste, to send, to scatter widely.<BR>.²6 With सम,<BR>To gather, to collect.<BR>.²7 With अभि, in the passive voice,<BR>to be upset, overcome or overwhelmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॄत
कॄत<BR>r. 10th cl. (कीर्त्तयति)<BR>To celebrate, to glorify, to render renowned or notorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्त|कॢप्तः
कॢप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Made, formed.<BR>2 Fixed, appointed.<BR>3 Ascertained, determined.<BR>4 Cut, pared, shorn.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, &c. affix क्ल, and the augment इट् omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तकीला
कॢप्तकीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Title deed, lease of a house, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कॢप्त fixed, कील a bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तधूप|कॢप्तधूपः
कॢप्तधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Frankincense, olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>कॢप्त made, धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कॢप्तिक|कॢप्तिकः
कॢप्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Bought, purchased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकय|केकयः
केकय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A prince of the solar race.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The daughter of the preceding, and one of the wives of DAŚARATHA: the mother of BHARATA: see केकेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकर|केकरः
केकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>के in the head, कृ to make, टच् affix; also compounded with अक्ष an eye, as केकराक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकल
केकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केका
केका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The cry of a peacock.<BR>E.<BR>के an imitative sound, and क what sounds, from के to sound, affixes ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकाबल|केकाबलः
केकाबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>केका his cry, and बलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकिन्
केकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>केका the cry of the bird, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकेयी
केकेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>One of DAŚARATHA'S three wives, the mother of BHARATA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचन
केचन<BR>ind.<BR>Some, some or certain persons.<BR>E.<BR>के plural of किम्, and चन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचित
केचित<BR>ind.<BR>Some, some persons.<BR>E.<BR>see the last; चिति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केचुक|केचुकं
केचुक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia): see कचु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केणिका
केणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>किण to cover (a Sautra root), ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केत|केतः
केत<BR>r. 10th cl. (केतयति)<BR>1 To call or invite.<BR>2 To counsel or advise; some authorities substitute सङ्केत for this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केत|केतः
केत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A house, an abode.<BR>E.<BR>कित to abide, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतक|केतकः
केतक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>किति to abide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतन|केतनं
केतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A flag, a banner.<BR>2 Business, indispensable act.<BR>3 Invitation.<BR>4 A spot or mark, a sign, a symbol.<BR>5 A house, an abode.<BR>6 Place, site, situation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कित to abide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतित
केतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Called, summoned.<BR>2 Dwelt, inhabited.<BR>E.<BR>केत to call, or कित to dwell, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतु|केतुः
केतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>KETU the dragon's tail or descending node; in astronomy, the ninth of the planets; in mythology, a demon: the body of SAIṂHIKEYA severed from the head (RĀHU), by VIṢṆU, at the churning of the ocean, but immortal, by having tasted the Amṛta.<BR>2 A banner, a flag.<BR>3 A mark, a sign, a symbol, &c.<BR>4 Light.<BR>5 A comet, a falling star, &c.<BR>6 Disease.<BR>7 A pigmy race inhabiting Kusa Dvīpa, the progeny of JAIMINI.<BR>E.<BR>चाय to worship, तु Uṇādi affix, कि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुतारा
केतुतारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A comet.<BR>E.<BR>केतु, and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुभ|केतुभः
केतुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>केतु the plant, and भ what resembles it in darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुमाल|केतुमालं|केतुमालः
केतुमाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of nine great divisions of the known world, the western portion or Varṣa of Jambu Dvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुयष्टि|केतुयष्टिः
केतुयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A flag-staff.<BR>E.<BR>केतु, and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुरत्न|केतुरत्नं
केतुरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>केतु, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केतुवसन
केतुवसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A flag.<BR>E.<BR>केतु a standard, and वसन cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदर|केदरः
केदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a plant.<BR>E.<BR>क the earth or the head, दृ to divide, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदार|केदारः
केदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A field, a meadow, a plain.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 A particular place, the modern Kedār, part of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>5 A basin for water round the root of a tree.<BR>6 A bed in a garden or field.<BR>E.<BR>क water, earth, &c. दृ to tear or rend, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केदारखण्ड|केदारखंड
केदारखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A small dyke or mound, earth raised to keep out water.<BR>E.<BR>केदार, and खण्ड a portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनार|केनारः
केनार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 The temples, the upper part of the cheek.<BR>3 A joint.<BR>4 A division of hell, a hell like a potter's kiln.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, &c. मृ to guide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केनिपात|केनिपातः
केनिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The helm, a rudder, a large oar used as one.<BR>E.<BR>क water, निपात who goes or falls; also केनिपातक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दु|केन्दुः
केन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A sort of ebony, (Diospyros tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>क the earth, इन्द to moisten, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्दुक|केन्दुकः
केन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of ebony, that yields a species of tar, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केन्द्र|केंद्र|केंद्रं|केन्द्रं
केन्द्र<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>1 The centre of a circle.<BR>2 The argument of an equation.<BR>3 The distance of a planet from the first point of its orbit in the fourth, seventh, or tenth degree. It is variously applied in combination, as पतनकेन्द्रं argument of the latitude; द्वितीयकेन्द्रं the distance of the higher apsis form a planet in any point of its orbit; शीघ्रकेन्द्रं commutation, the distance of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">Page248</a>] the sun from a superior planet or of an inferior planet from the sun; मन्दकेन्द्रं argument of anomaly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=247" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केप
केप<BR>(ऋ) केपृ r. 1st cl. (केपते)<BR>1 To shake or tremble.<BR>2 To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केयूर|केयूरं|केयूरः
केयूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A bracelet worn on the upper arm.<BR>E.<BR>क the head, here implying the head of the arm, यु to join, ऊर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरल|केरलः
केरल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The appellation of a country, Keraladeś or the modern Malabar.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Astronomical science.<BR>2 An astronomical Śāstra or treatise.<BR>2 A Horā or period of time equal to about one hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केल
केल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊ) केलु (केलति)<BR>1 To shake.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलक|केलकः
केलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dancer, a tumbler, one who walks or dances on the edge of a sword.<BR>E.<BR>किल to sport, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलास|केलासः
केलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>के in water, लस to shine, अंण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलि|केलिः
केलि<BR>mf. (-लिः लिः or -ली)<BR>Play, sport, pastime, amusement.<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>किल to sport, Uṇādi affix इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिक|केलिकः
केलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sportive, sporting.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Asoka tree.<BR>E.<BR>केलि and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकला
केलिकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The Vīṇā or lute of SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 Amorous or sportive accents or address.<BR>3 Sportive skill, wantonness.<BR>E.<BR>केलि sport, कल to sound, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकिल|केलिकिलः
केलिकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>One of ŚIVA'S attendant demigods.<BR>2 The confidential companion of the hero of a drama, in general a sort of buffoon.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A name of RATI, the wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>केलि sport, किल who plays, from किल to sport, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकीर्ण|केलिकीर्णः|केलिकीर्ण्ण
केलिकीर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकुञ्चिका|केलिकुंचिका
केलिकुञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wife's younger sister.<BR>E.<BR>केलि play, कुचि to be crooked, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिकोष|केलिकोषः
केलिकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An actor, a dancer or tumbler: see केलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिगृह
केलिगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A pleasure house, a private apartment.<BR>E.<BR>केलि sport, and गृह a house; also कलिनिकेतन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिनागर|केलिनागरः
केलिनागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sensualist, an enjoyer of worldly pleasures.<BR>E.<BR>केलि sport, and नागर a libertine, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिपर
केलिपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wanton, sportive.<BR>E.<BR>केलि, and पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिमुख|केलिमुखः
केलिमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Pastime, sport.<BR>E.<BR>केलि play, and मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिवृक्ष|केलिवृक्षः
केलिवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A species of the Kadamba, commonly Keli-Kadamba, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>केलि sport, and वृक्ष a tree; being abundant in the scene of KṚṢṆA'S sports with the Gopīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिशयन
केलिशयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A couch, a sofa.<BR>E.<BR>केलि, and शयन a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिशुषि|केलिशुषिः
केलिशुषि<BR>f. (-षिः)<BR>The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केलिसचिव|केलिसचिवः
केलिसचिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Minister of the sports, master of the revels.<BR>E.<BR>केलि play, सचिव a counsellor, a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केव
केव<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) केवृ (केवते)<BR>To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवर्त्त|केवर्त|केवर्तः|केवर्त्तः
केवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A fisherman: see कैवर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवल|केवलं|केवलः
केवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला or -ली-लं)<BR>1 One, alone, only.<BR>2 All, entire, whole.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An envious or selfish man.<BR>n. adv. (-लं)<BR>1 Absolutely, certainly.<BR>2 Only, alone.<BR>Subst.<BR>3 A species of knowledge, that of the unity of spirit.<BR>E.<BR>केव to sprinkle, कल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलज्ञानिन्
केवलज्ञानिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>One of the Jaina saints of the last age.<BR>E.<BR>केवल unity, and ज्ञानिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलद्रव्य|केवलद्रव्यं
केवलद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>केवल one, only, द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलवैयाकरण
केवलवैयाकरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A grammarian, a mere grammarian, one not versed in any other science.<BR>E.<BR>केवल only, and वैयाकरण a grammarian; also similar compounds, as केवलनैयायिक a mere logician, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केवलिन्
केवलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>One, only, alone.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A Jaina who has acquired holy knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>केषल one, इनि affix; a unitarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केविका
केविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a flower, commonly Keber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केश|केशः
केश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Hair.<BR>2 A name of VARUṆA.<BR>3 A kind of perfume: see वाला.<BR>4 The name of a demon.<BR>5 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>2 The indigo plant.<BR>3 Indian spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to bind, अण् affix, and ल rejected; or क the head, and ईश to rule, affix अच्; again, क water or happiness, and ईश the lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशक|केशकः
केशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Skilful in dressing hair, taking pains with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकलाप|केशकलापः
केशकलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A quantity of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, and कलाप in this compound implying quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकार|केशकारः
केशकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and कार what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशकीट|केशकीटः
केशकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A louse.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशगर्ब्भ
केशगर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>1 A braid of hair.<BR>2 Varuṇa.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and गर्भ origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशगर्ब्भक
केशगर्ब्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A braid or tress of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, and गर्ब्भक a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशगृहीत
केशगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pulled or seized by the hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and गृहीत seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशग्रह|केशग्रहः
केशग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Pulling the hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and ग्रह seizing; also केशग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशघ्न|केशघ्नं
केशघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Morbid baldness, falling of the hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश the hair, and घ्न what destroys, from हन् to injure, affix टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशच्छिद्
केशच्छिद्<BR>m. (-च्छित् or -च्छिद्)<BR>A barber, a hair-dresser.<BR>E.<BR>केश the hair, छिद् to cut, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशट|केशटः
केशट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A goat.<BR>3 A louse.<BR>5 A brother.<BR>5 One of KĀMA'S arrows.<BR>6 A tree, commonly Sonapat, (शोणक.)<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, अट to go, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशधृत्
केशधृत्<BR>m. (-धृत्)<BR>The root of sweet flag.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, धृ to hold, affix, क्विप्; resembling hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपक्ष|केशपक्षः
केशपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Much or ornamented hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, पक्ष quantity, in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपङ्क्ति
केशपङ्क्ति<BR>f. (-ङ्क्तिः)<BR>1 A row or line of hair.<BR>2 A quantity of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and पंक्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपर्णी|केशपर्ण्णी
केशपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera); also अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशपाश|केशपाशः
केशपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Much or ornamented hair.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A lock of hair on the top of the head.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, पाश quantity, in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशभू
केशभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमार्जक|केशमार्जकं|केशमार्ज्जक
केशमार्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A comb.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, मृज to clean, ण्वुल् affix; also केशमार्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमार्जन|केशमार्जनं|केशमार्ज्जन
केशमार्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A comb.<BR>2 Cleaning the hair.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=248" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशमुष्टि|केशमुष्टिः
केशमुष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 A large species of Nimb tree.<BR>2 A handful of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and मुष्टि the fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशर|केशरं|केशरः
केशर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The filament of a lotus or of any vegetable.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>2 A tree bearing a white strong smelling flower, (Mimusops elengi): see वकुल.<BR>3 A shrub used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria); also पुन्नाग.<BR>4 A lion's mane.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>क water, &c. in the seventh case के, शृ to go, अप् affix; also with सृ to go केसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशरञ्जन|केशरञ्जनः
केशरञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant: see भृङ्गराज, (Verbesina prostrata).<BR>E.<BR>केश the hair, and रञ्जन what colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशराज|केशराजः
केशराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A species of Bhringariva: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, राज to shine, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशराम्ल|केशराम्लः
केशराम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>A citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशरिन्
केशरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 A plant used in dying: see पुन्नाग.<BR>4 Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>5 The citron tree.<BR>E.<BR>केशर a mane, a filament, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशव|केशवः
केशव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Having much or handsome hair.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Punnag: see पुन्नाग.<BR>E.<BR>क BRAHMA, and ईश ŚIVA, व who goes, &c. from वा with ड affix; again केश hair, व who possesses; fine-haired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवत्|केशवन्त्
केशवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a fine head of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवभक्ति
केशवभक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Devotion to KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>केशव, and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवायुध|केशवायुधः
केशवायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>2 Any weapon of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>केशव KṚṢṆA, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवालय|केशवालयः
केशवालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>केशव KṚṢṆA, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवावाल
केशवावाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवावास|केशवावासः
केशवावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशवेश|केशवेशः
केशवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A tress or fillet of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, and बेश ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशहल
केशहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Much or ornamented hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, and हल here implying much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशाकेशि
केशाकेशि<BR>n. (-शि)<BR>Pulling the hair mutually, hair to hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, repeated, affix इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्त|केशांत|केशान्तः
केशान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Cutting off the hair finally as a religious ceremony, performed upon Brahmans at sixteen years of age; Kṣatriyas at twenty-two; and Vaiśyas at twenty-four.<BR>2 The tip or end of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशान्तिक
केशान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Extending to the hair.<BR>2 Relating to the ceremony of final tonsure.<BR>E.<BR>केशान्त, and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशारि|केशारिः
केशारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A tree, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशावमर्षण
केशावमर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Pulling the hair, especially amorously, playing with it, rubbing it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>केश the hair, अव implying improperly, and मर्षण rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिक|केशिकः
केशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Having fine or luxuriant hair.<BR>2 Relating to the hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिन्
केशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Having fine hair.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 The name of a Daitya or demon killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A lion.<BR>f. (-शिनी)<BR>1 A kind of grass, (Andropogon aculeatum.)<BR>2 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिसूदन|केशिसूदनः
केशिसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>केशि a demon, सूदन destroyer; also similar compounds, as केशिहन्, कशिनिसूदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशिहन्
केशिहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केशोच्चय|केशोच्चयः
केशोच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Much or handsome hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, उच्चय heap, abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसर|केसरं|केसरः
केसर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>A filament.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 The mane of a horse or lion, &c., see केशर.<BR>4 A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>5 A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Sulphate of iron.<BR>3 The flower of the Nagesar.<BR>E.<BR>के on the head, सृ to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरवर|केसरवरं
केसरवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>केसर, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसराम्ल|केसराम्लः
केसराम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>A citron.<BR>E.<BR>केसर, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिन्
केसरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 A plant used in dying: see पुन्नाग.<BR>4 Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>5 A monkey the father of HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>केसर a filament, a mane, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केसरिसुत|केसरिसुतः
केसरिसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The monkey HANUMAN.<BR>E.<BR>केसरि, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कै
कै<BR>r. 1st cl. (कायति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैकेयी
कैकेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, and the mother of BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>केकय a king, father of this lady, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैङ्कर्य्य|कैङ्कर्य|कैंकर्यं|कैङ्कर्य्यं
कैङ्कर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Service, servitude.<BR>E.<BR>किङ्कर^1 a servant, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161202. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभ|कैटभः
कैटभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A demon slain by VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कैटभ a demon in whose death the goddess was instrumental, by having at the prayers of BRAHMĀ roused VIṢṆU from his slumbers, during which two demons, Kaitabha and Madhu, were about to demolish BRAHMĀ; also कैटभी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभजित्
कैटभजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कैटभ the name of an Asura killed by the deity, and जित् who conquers; also similar compounds, as कैटभहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटभारि|कैटभारिः
कैटभारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU: see कैटभजित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैटर्य्य|कैटर्य|कैटर्यः|कैटर्य्यः
कैटर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A plant used in medicine, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>2 The Nimb tree.<BR>3 Mayana, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कैटर from किट to fear, and रा to cause, alarming by its pungency; pleonastic affix ष्यञ्; also कैडर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतव|कैतवं|कैतवः
कैतव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery.<BR>2 Gambling.<BR>3 The lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>कितव a cheat, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतवप्रयोग|कैतवप्रयोगः
कैतवप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A trick, a device.<BR>E.<BR>कैतव, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैतववाद|कैतववादः
कैतववाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Evasion, falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>कैतव, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार|कैदारं|कैदारः
कैदार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Belonging to a field, a meadow, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rice, corn.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A multitude of fields.<BR>E.<BR>केदार a field, and अण् affix; also केदारक, and कैदारिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदारक|कैदारकं
कैदारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of fields.<BR>E.<BR>केदार, and वुञ् affix; also with ठञ् affix कैदारिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैदार्य्य|कैदार्य|कैदार्य्यं
कैदार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ष्यः-री-र्य्यं)<BR>Belonging to a field, &c.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A number of fields.<BR>E.<BR>केदार, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरव|कैरवं|कैरवः
कैरव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The white esculent water-lily.<BR>2 Fraud, trick.<BR>E.<BR>केरव here said to mean, a goose, from के in water, and रु to sound, with अप् affix; again, अण् affix, liked by the geese; or किरव a cheat, &c. or कैरव a lotus, and अण् affix, implying identity or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविणी
कैरविणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A place abounding in lotus flowers, or an assemblage of lotuses.<BR>E.<BR>कैरव a white lotus, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरविन्
कैरविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कैरवी moonlight, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=249" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैराटक|कैराटकः
कैराटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of poison, one of the fixed kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैरात|कैरातं|कैरातः
कैरात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A sort of gentian, commonly Cherayta, (Gentiana cherayta, Rox.)<BR>2 A kind of Sandal.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A strong man.<BR>E.<BR>किरात gentian, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैल|कैलं
कैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sport, pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>केलि, and अञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलास|कैलासः
कैलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The mountain Kailāsa, the fabulous residence of KUVERA, and favourite haunt of ŚIVA; it is placed by the Hindus amongst the Himālaya mountains, and the name is given to one of the loftiest peaks lying on the north of the Mānasa lake.<BR>E.<BR>कैलास crystal, and the affix अण् implying nature or consistence; or कैल pleasure, आस to abide, affix घञ्; the place where beings reside in bliss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासनिकेतन|कैलासनिकेतनः
कैलासनिकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>कैलास, and निकेतन dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैलासौकस्
कैलासौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>कैलास the mountain, औकस् abode; whose abode is mount Kailāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्त|कैवर्त|कैवर्तः|कैवर्त्तः
कैवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A fisherman born of a prostitute by a Kṣatriya, or of an Ayogava female by a Niṣāda father.<BR>f. (-र्त्ती)<BR>The wife of a fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>क water, in the seventh case, के and वर्त्त who abides, केवर्त्त a fish, अण् affix, implying enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तक|कैवर्तक|कैवर्तकः
कैवर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तमुस्त|कैवर्तमुस्त|कैवर्त्तमुस्तं
कैवर्त्तमुस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तमुस्तक|कैवर्तमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तमुस्तकं
कैवर्त्तमुस्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant grass: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवर्त्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्तिमुस्तक|कैवर्त्तिमुस्तकं
कैवर्त्तिमुस्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant kind of grass, (Cyperus rotundus).<BR>E.<BR>कैवर्त्त as above, water-abiding, and मुस्तक cyperus; also कैवर्त्तीमुस्तक, कैवर्त्तंमुस्त, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैवल्य|कैवल्यं
कैवल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ली-ल्यं)<BR>Sole, only.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Eternal emancipation, future happiness.<BR>2 Exclusiveness, individuality.<BR>E.<BR>केवल alone, free from all fetters, व्यञ् affix of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशिक|कैशिकं|कैशिकः
कैशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Love, passion, lust.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>One of the four varieties of dramatic style, the graceful style, suited especially to the passion of love.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A quantity of hair, the head of hair.<BR>E.<BR>केशिक having much hair, &c. affix अण्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैशोर|कैशोरं
कैशोर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Youth, boyhood, from the age of ten to that of fifteen.<BR>E.<BR>किशोर a child, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कैश्य|कैश्यं
कैश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>A head of hair, much or ornamented hair.<BR>E.<BR>केश hair, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोक|कोकः
कोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wolf.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR>3 A frog.<BR>4 A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>5 The wild date tree.<BR>6 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to seize or take, or क water, उक to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकड|कोकडः
कोकड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>An animal said to be a kind of deer, of a brown colour, with a bushy tail, and lurking in holes, perhaps a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकदेव|कोकदेवः
कोकदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनद|कोकनदं
कोकनद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 The red lotus.<BR>2 The red water lily.<BR>E.<BR>कोक a goose, and नद to sound, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकनदच्छवि|कोकनदच्छविः
कोकनदच्छवि<BR>mfn. (-विः-विः-वि)<BR>Red, the colour, or of that colour.<BR>E.<BR>कोकनद the red lotus, and छवि light, splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकबन्धु|कोकबन्धुः
कोकबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>कोक the ruddy goose, and बन्धु a friend: see चक्रवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकाह|कोकाहः
कोकाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A white horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिल|कोकिलः
कोकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The Kokila or Koïl, the black or Indian cuckoo, (Cuculus Indicus.)<BR>2 A firebrand, a lighted coal.<BR>E.<BR>कुक to seize, (the heart,) and इलच् affix: the Kokila makes a prominent figure in Hindu poetry, and is supposed, by his musical cry, to inspire pleasing and tender emotions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलनयन|कोकिलनयनः
कोकिलनयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant bearing a dark black flower, (Capparis spinosa); it is also applied to Barleria longifolia.<BR>E.<BR>कोकिल the Koil, and नयन an eye, to which the flower is compared; also other similar compounds, as कोकिलाक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलाक्ष|कोकिलाक्षः
कोकिलाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A shrub: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कोकिल, and अक्ष the eye, or with कन् added, कोकिलाक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलावास|कोकिलावासः
कोकिलावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>कोकिल, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलेक्षु|कोकिलेक्षुः
कोकिलेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The black variety of sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>कोकिल, and इक्षु sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोकिलोत्सव|कोकिलोत्सवः
कोकिलोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>कोकिल, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोच|कोचः
कोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A man of degraded caste, the offspring of a fisherman by a female of the butcher tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कण|कोंकण|कोङ्कणं|कोंकणः|कोङ्कणः
कोङ्कण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The name of a country, Konkan, in the peninsula.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A kind of weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोङ्कणासुत|कोंकणासुत|कोङ्कणासुतः
कोङ्कणासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कोङ्कणा the mother of the hero, or the woman of Konkan, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोजागर|कोजागरः
कोजागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The day of full-moon in the month Aśvin, (September-October.)<BR>E.<BR>कः who, जागर wakeful; who is awake, the call of LAKṢMĪ, who, descending on this night, promised wealth to all that were awake: hence the night is spent in festivity, and games of chance in honour of the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट|कोटः
कोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A fort, a strong hold.<BR>2 A shed, a hut.<BR>3 Crookedness, curvature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटक|कोटकः
कोटक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Who or what curves or bends.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thatcher, a builder of huts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटर|कोटरं|कोटरः
कोटर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The hollow of a tree.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A naked woman: see कोटवी.<BR>E.<BR>कोट and र, from रा to get, to possess, with the affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटरावण|कोटरावणं
कोटरावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A wood in which there are hollow trees.<BR>E.<BR>कोटर the hollow of a tree, and वन a wood; by special rules, the final vowel of the first word is made long, and न in the second is changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटवी
कोटवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A naked woman.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कोट crookedness, and वा to get or receive, क and ङीष् affixes; also कोट्टवी, and कोटरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटि|कोटिः
कोटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>1 The edge or point of a sword.<BR>2 The end of a bow.<BR>3 A number, a Krore or ten millions.<BR>4 Eminence, excellence.<BR>5 The upright side of a triangle.<BR>6 The complement of an are to 90°.<BR>7 A plant, Piring or Asparac, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, and इण् Uṇādi affix; also कोटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिक|कोटिकः
कोटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An insect., coccinella of various kinds; this is most usually read कोटिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिजित्
कोटिजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of the poet KĀLIDĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>केटि a crore, (of competitors,) and जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिज्या
कोटिज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>The cosine of an angle, in a right angled triangle.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि, and ज्या a sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिपात्र|कोटिपात्रः
कोटिपात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A rudder or large oar used as one.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि an edge, and पात्र a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=250" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिर|कोटिरः
कोटिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An ichneumon, (Viverra ichneumon.)<BR>2 An insect, coccinella of various kinds: see इन्द्रगोप.<BR>3 A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि excellence, and र what possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिवर्ष|कोटिवर्षं
कोटिवर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The name of a city, Vāṇapura or Devikote, on the Koromandel coast.<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>A plant used as a medicinal vegetable, (Medicago esculenta): see पिडिङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि excellence, वर्ष what diffuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिश|कोटिशः
कोटिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि an edge, शो to cut or pare, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटिशस्
कोटिशस्<BR>ind.<BR>In multitudes, by millions.<BR>E.<BR>कोटि, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटी
कोटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 The edge or point of a sword.<BR>2 A medicinal plant, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR>3 A Krore, &c.: see कोटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीर|कोटीरः
कोटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Long entangled hair.<BR>2 A crest, a diadem.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be crooked, इरन् affix and the radical vowel converted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीवर्ष|कोटीवर्षं
कोटीवर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>A name of Vāṇapura.<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Piring, a plant: see कोटिवर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोटीश|कोटीशः
कोटीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A harrow: see कोटिश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्ट|कोट्टं|कोट्टः
कोट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः-ट्टं)<BR>A fort, a castle, a strong hold.<BR>E.<BR>कुट्ट to cut or divide, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवी
कोट्टवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A naked woman.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 The mother of Vāṇa, an asura: see कोटवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टवीपुर|कोट्टवीपुरं
कोट्टवीपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Vanapur or Devicotta.<BR>E.<BR>कोट्टवी the mother of Vāṇa, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोट्टार|कोट्टारः
कोट्टार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A well.<BR>2 The stairs of a pond.<BR>3 A fortified town, a strong hold.<BR>4 A libertine.<BR>E.<BR>कोट्ट a fort, &c. ऋ to go, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोठ|कोठः
कोठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 A species of leprosy with large round spots.<BR>2 Ringworm, impetigo.<BR>E.<BR>कुठ to surround, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोण|कोणः
कोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A corner, an angle.<BR>2 The quill or bow of a lute, a fiddle stick, &c.<BR>3 A drum stick.<BR>4 A sort of stringed musical instrument.<BR>5 The sharp edge of a sword.<BR>6 A stick, a staff, a club.<BR>7 A name of Maṅgala, the planet MARS.<BR>8 A name of the planet SATURN.<BR>9 An intermediate point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>कुण to sound, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणकुण|कोणकुणः
कोणकुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>कुण to cut, affix क, added to कोण the edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोणि|कोणिः
कोणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Having a crooked arm: see कुणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोथ|कोथः
कोथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Afflicted with pain.<BR>2 Churned.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Inflammation, and ulceration of the angles of the eyelids.<BR>2 Gangrene.<BR>3 Churning.<BR>E.<BR>कुथ to afflict or be afflicted, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोदण्ड|कोदंड|कोदंडं|कोदण्डं|कोदंडः|कोदण्डः
कोदण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>A bow.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 An eyebrow.<BR>2 The name of a country.<BR>E.<BR>कुण to sound, अण्ड Uṇādi affix, &c. दन् inserted; the final radical consonant is rejected; otherwise, कुद to speak false, अण्डच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोद्रव|कोद्रवः
कोद्रव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A species of grain eaten by the poorer people, (Paspalum kora.)<BR>E.<BR>क wind, उद्रव to go, affix अच्; sown by the wind, or growing wild in many places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोप|कोपः
कोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Wrath, rage.<BR>2 Morbid irritation or disorder of the humours.<BR>E.<BR>कुप to be angry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपक्रम|कोपक्रमं|कोपक्रमः
कोपक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An angry or passionate man.<BR>E.<BR>कोप rage, and क्रम who goes or has.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The creation by BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>क BRAHMĀ, and उपक्रम order, method; also similar compounds, as कोपज्ञ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपज्वलित
कोपज्वलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Enraged, inflamed with wrath.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and ज्वलित inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपदीप्त
कोपदीप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Incensed, inflamed with anger.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and दीप्त shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपन|कोपनः
कोपन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Passionate, wrathful.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A passionate woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुप to be angry, युच् affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपपद
कोपपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Appearance of anger, pretended wrath.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवत्|कोपवन्त्
कोपवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Passionate, angry.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपवेग|कोपवेगः
कोपवेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Violence, impetuosity of passion.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपाकुल
कोपाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Furious, enraged.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and आकुल bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपित
कोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Angry, enraged.<BR>E.<BR>कोप, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोपिन्
कोपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Angry, passionate, wrathful.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A bird called the water-pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>कुप to be angry, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमल|कोमलं|कोमलः
कोमल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Soft, bland.<BR>2 Soft, low, sweet.<BR>3 Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant: see क्षीरिका.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>कुट to be curved, कल Uṇādi affix, and मुट् inserted, formative irregular; or कम to desire, कलच् affix, and उ inserted with conversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलक|कोमलकं
कोमलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कोमल soft, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलगीत
कोमलगीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A pleasing song.<BR>E.<BR>कोमल, and गीत a song; also with कन् added, कोमलगीतकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमलता
कोमलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Softness, tenderness, agreeableness; also with त्व, कोमलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोमासिका
कोमासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A budding fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टि|कोयष्टिः
कोयष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>The lapwing: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोयष्टिक|कोयष्टिकः
कोयष्टिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The lapwing.<BR>E.<BR>क water, यष्टि a line or row, कन् added, deriv, irr.; also कोयष्टि. These birds are found in the vicinity of marshes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोर|कोरः
कोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Union with little or no motion, as that of the fingers with one another, amphiarthrosis.<BR>2 A bud.<BR>E.<BR>कुर sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरक|कोरकं|कोरकः
कोरक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A bud, an unblown flower.<BR>2 A species of perfume, commonly Chor.<BR>3 Another perfume, a berry containing a resinous and fragrant substance: see कक्कोलक.<BR>4 The fibres of the stalk of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कुर to sound, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरङ्गी
कोरङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>E.<BR>कुर to sound, अङ्गच् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरदूष|कोरदूषः
कोरदूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>कोर a bud, दूष to change, अण् affix; also कन् being added, कोरदूषक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोरित
कोरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pounded, ground, comminuted.<BR>2 Budded, sprouted.<BR>E.<BR>कोर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोल|कोलं|कोलः
कोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A raft, a float.<BR>3 The haunch, the hip or flank.<BR>4 Embracing, an embrace.<BR>5 The planet Śani or SATURN.<BR>6 Plumbago, (Zeylanica, &c.)<BR>7 A country, Kaliṅga, the modern seacoast from Cuttak to Madras.<BR>8 A kind of weapon.<BR>9 An outcaste, one of a tribe degraded by SAGARA [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">Page252</a>] from the military order.<BR>10 A man of a mixed caste.<BR>11 A barbarian, a Kol, people inhabiting the hills and forests in central India.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>2 The weight of one Tola.<BR>3 Black pepper.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>1 The jujube tree.<BR>2 Long pepper.<BR>3 A kind of pepper, (Piper chavya, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=251" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलक|कोलकं|कोलकः
कोलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A kind of perfume: see कक्कोलक.<BR>2 Long pepper.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Cordia myxta.)<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलदल|कोलदलं
कोलदल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A kind of perfume: see नखी.<BR>E.<BR>कोल the jujube, दल a leaf; having a similar leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलनासिका
कोलनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant? also वङ्किनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलपुच्छ|कोलपुच्छः
कोलपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>कोल a hog, पुच्छ a tail; hog-tailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलमूल|कोलमूलं
कोलमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>कोल, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलम्बक|कोलंबक|कोलंबकः|कोलम्बकः
कोलम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The body of a lute, the whole of it except the strings.<BR>E.<BR>कुल to accumulate, अम्बच् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलवल्ली
कोलवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A plant, with a pungent fruit resembling pepper: see गजपिप्पली (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>E.<BR>कोल a hog, वल्ली a creeper; resembling a hog's bristle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाञ्च|कोलांच|कोलाञ्चः
कोलाञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A name of Kaliṅga, the Coromandel coast, from Cuttak to Madras; according to some, it is in Gangetic Hindustan, with Kanouj for the capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलाहल|कोलाहलं|कोलाहलः
कोलाहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A loud and confused sound, an uproar, a great and indistinct noise.<BR>E.<BR>कोल accumulation, from कुल, with घञ्; again, हल to make or plough, आङ् prefixed, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोलि|कोलिः
कोलि<BR>f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>The jujube tree, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>E.<BR>see कोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविद|कोविदः
कोविद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>को who sounds or teaches, (the Shasters,) विद divine knowledge, from विद to know, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोविदार|कोविदारं|कोविदारः
कोविदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A species of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth, दॄ to tear or divide, with वि prefixed, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोश|कोशं|कोशः
कोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An egg.<BR>2 Wrought or unwrought gold or silver plate, jewellery.<BR>3 An ordeal, &c.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A shoe, a sandal.<BR>2 The beard of corn.<BR>E.<BR>कुश or कुष to issue, घञ् affix, fem. affix ङीष्; see कोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशकार|कोशकारः
कोशकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sugar cane; also कोषकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशफल|कोशफलं
कोशफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A berry containing a waxy and fragrant substance: see कक्कोल.<BR>E.<BR>कोश an egg, फल fruit; the berry being egg-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशल|कोशलः
कोशल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>1 A name of the city Ayodhya (Oude), or the neighbouring district.<BR>2 The name of a prince.<BR>E.<BR>कुश to shine, अल Uṇādi affix; also कोषल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलात्मजा
कोशलात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The wife of DAŚARATHA the mother of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कोशल the name of a king, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशवासिन्
कोशवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Wrapped up in a sheathe or shell, &c.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 A shelled animal.<BR>2 A chrysalis or pupa.<BR>E.<BR>कोश, and वासिन् what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशस्थ|कोशस्थः
कोशस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Sheathed, enveloped in a sheathe, a shell, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 Any shelled insect or animal, as a snail, &c.<BR>2 A pupa or chrysalis.<BR>3 The silk worm in its cocoon.<BR>E.<BR>कोश, and स्थ what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशलिक|कोशलिकं
कोशलिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>कोश or कोष wealth, and ल what takes, ठक् affix; also कोषलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशाङ्ग|कोशाङ्गं
कोशाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A kind of reed or grass, commonly Ikāda.<BR>E.<BR>कोश or कोष a sheathe, and अङ्ग body; also कोषाङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातक|कोशातकः
कोशातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hair.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Several sorts of cucurbitaceous plants: see कोषातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशातकिन्
कोशातकिन्<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 Trade, business.<BR>2 A trader, a merchant.<BR>3 Submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष|कोषं|कोषः
कोष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>1 A bud.<BR>2 A sheathe, a scabbard, &c.<BR>3 A coat, a surrounding cover, any investing sheathe.<BR>4 Judicial trial by oath or ordeal, or by fire, water, poison, the balance, heated balls of iron, boiling oil, &c. attesting a deity, and touching or drinking water three times in which some idol has been washed.<BR>5 Gold or silver, wrought or unwrought, as plate, jewellery, &c.<BR>6 Wealth.<BR>7 Accumulated wealth, treasure.<BR>8 A treasury, the apartment where money or plate is kept.<BR>9 A sacrificial vessel or any drinking vessel.<BR>10 The vulva, the womb.<BR>11 The penis.<BR>12 A testicle or the scrotum.<BR>13 An egg.<BR>14 (In composition,) A ball or globe, as सूत्रकीष a ball of thread, नेत्रकोष the eyeball, &c.<BR>15 The inner part of the Jack-fruit or its like.<BR>16 A nutmeg.<BR>17 A dictionary or vocabulary.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A shoe, a sandal.<BR>2 The beard of corn: see कोश.<BR>E.<BR>कुश or कुष to issue, affix घञ्; hence the word is optionally कोष or कोश; the meanings may be mostly resolved into, that from which something issues or evolves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषक|कोषकः
कोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An egg.<BR>2 A testicle.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषकार|कोषकारः
कोषकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Sugar cane, or a variety.<BR>2 The silk worm, or the insect while in its cocoon.<BR>3 A chrysalis, or (pupa.)<BR>E.<BR>कोश a sheathe, and कार what makes; also कोशकार or with कन् added कोशकारक and कोशकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषग्रहण
कोषग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Undergoing an ordeal.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and ग्रहण taking; also कोशग्रहणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषचञ्चु|कोषचंचु|कोषचञ्चुः
कोषचञ्चु<BR>m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a sheathe, &c. and चञ्चु a beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषनायक
कोषनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Indian Plutus.<BR>2 A treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and नायक chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषफल|कोषफलं|कोषफलः
कोषफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A berry having a fragrant pulp: see कक्वोल.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of creeping plant: see घोषक.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of Ghoṣa with yellow flowers.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a sheathe, and फल fruit; also कोशफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषभूत
कोषभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Treasured, stored, accumulated.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषला
कोषला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The country south of Ayodhya (Oude), or Ayodhya itself: see कोशला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषवत्
कोषवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Rich, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषवृद्धि|कोषवृद्धिः
कोषवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Swelled testicle, enlargement of the scrotum, from hernia or hydrocele, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a testicle, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषशायिका
कोषशायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a scabbard, and शी to sleep, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषशुद्धि
कोषशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Purification by ordeal.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and शुद्धि purity; also कोशशृद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=252" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषहीन
कोषहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor, without treasure.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषांश
कोषांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Part of a treasure, a portion of a person's wealth.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषातक|कोषातकः
कोषातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hair.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A small species of cucumber, (Trichosanthes diaeca.)<BR>2 A cucurbitaceous plant, commonly called Turai, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR>3 Another kind, (L. pentangula.)<BR>4 A kind of creeper: see घोष.<BR>5 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera); also अपामार्ग.<BR>6 Night.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a sheathe, &c. अत to go, affixes क्वुन् and ङीष्; also कोशातक and कोषातकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषाध्यक्ष
कोषाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A treasurer.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषापहरण
कोषापहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Carrying off treasure.<BR>E.<BR>कोष, and अपहरण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोषिन्
कोषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>कोष a sheathe, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठ|कोष्ठः
कोष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Own.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 A granary, a place in which grain is kept.<BR>2 A treasury.<BR>3 An apartment.<BR>4 Any viscus, as the heart, lungs, stomach, bowels, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुष to issue, थन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठक|कोष्ठकः
कोष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A granary.<BR>2 A treasury.<BR>3 A brick trough for watering cattle at.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठपाल|कोष्ठपालः
कोष्ठपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A municipal officer, a constable.<BR>2 A watch, a guard.<BR>3 A storekeeper, a treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>कोष्ठ the granary, &c. and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठागार
कोष्ठागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A store.<BR>2 A treasury.<BR>E.<BR>कोष्ठ, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ठाग्नि|कोष्ठाग्निः
कोष्ठाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The digestive faculty, the gastric juice.<BR>E.<BR>कोष्ठ stomach, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोष्ण|कोष्णं
कोष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Warm, moderately warm, tepid.<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>Warmth.<BR>E.<BR>का diminutive, and उष्ण warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहल|कोहलः
कोहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The name of a saint or Muni, the inventor or first preceptor of the drama.<BR>2 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>3 A sort of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकृत्य|कौकृत्यं
कौकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>2 Repentance.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, कृत्या action, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिक|कौक्कुटिकः
कौक्कुटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hypocrite.<BR>2 A kind of mendicant, one who does not look far before him, or who proceeds with his eyes fixed upon the ground, for fear of treading upon insects, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्कुटी hypocrisy, or a small part, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिकन्दल|कौक्कुटिकन्दलः
कौक्कुटिकन्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A species of snake, the Boä or Bor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्ष
कौक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Abdominal, ventral.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्षि the belly, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेयक|कौक्षेयकः
कौक्षेयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar.<BR>E.<BR>कुक्षि the belly, and ढकञ् affix; in any other sense the affix is अण्, making कौक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्क|कौंक|कौंकः|कौङ्कः
कौङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The country, the Konkan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौङ्किण|कौङ्किणः
कौङ्किण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The district of Konkan in the peninsula: see कोङ्कण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्च|कौञ्चः
कौञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>The name of a mountain, part of the Himāla range: see क्रौञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौञ्जायनी
कौञ्जायनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The wife of a Brahman or any venerable personage.<BR>2 A female descendant of Kuñja.<BR>E.<BR>कुञ्ज, and फक् affix, fem. affix ङीष्; this word may be masculine, कौञ्जायन m. (-नः) meaning a male descendant of Kuñja; also कैञ्जायन्य formed from कुञ्ज by च्यञ् affix m. sing. (-न्यः) sense; also plur. (-नाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौट|कौटः
कौट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>1 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>2 Snared, wired.<BR>3 Domestic, homely, home-born, home-bred.<BR>4 Independent.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Fraud, falsehood.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A medicinal shrub, &c. कुटज.<BR>E.<BR>कूट fraud, or कुटि a house, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटकिक|कौटकिकः
कौटकिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender of the flesh of birds or beasts, a poacher, a butcher, &c.; also कौटिक.<BR>E.<BR>कूट or कूटक a snare, a trap, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटज|कौटजः
कौटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A medicinal shrub, (Echites antidysenterica): see कुटज.<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonastic affix to कुटज the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटतक्ष|कौटतक्षः
कौटतक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An independent carpenter, one who works at home on his own account, and not for the village or the corporation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कौट domestic, and तक्ष a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटल्य|कौटल्यः
कौटल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>The name of a saint; also called Vātsyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्षिन्
कौटसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A false witness.<BR>E.<BR>कौट fraud, साक्षिन् a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटसाक्ष्य
कौटसाक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>False evidence.<BR>E.<BR>कौट, and साक्ष्य testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिक|कौटिकः
कौटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>2 Relating to a snare or trap.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who kills animals, and sells their flesh for his own subsistence, a hunter, a poacher, a mountaineer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कूट a trap for catching birds, &c. affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिलिक|कौटिलिकः
कौटिलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hunter.<BR>2 A blacksmith.<BR>E.<BR>कुटिलिका derived from कुटिल crooked, said to mean a forge, or the stooping approach of a hunter on his prey, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्य|कौटिल्यं|कौटिल्यः
कौटिल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Crookedness.<BR>2 Dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>कुटिल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुम्बिक|कौटुंबिक|कौटुम्बिकः
कौटुम्बिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The father or master of a family.<BR>E.<BR>कुटुम्ब, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौडविक|कौडविकं
कौडविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sown with a certain measure, (a Kuḍava) of grain; (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कुडव a measure, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणप|कौणपः
कौणप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>कुणप a corpse, and अण् affix; these beings are supposed to eat human flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपदन्त|कौणपदंत|कौणपदन्तः
कौणपदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A name of BHĪṢMA uncle of the Pāṇḍus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्डिन्य|कौण्डिन्यः
कौण्डिन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>The name of a Muni or divine sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्य|कौण्यं
कौण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Being maimed, being handless.<BR>E.<BR>कुणि a cripple, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुक|कौतुकं
कौतुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Eagerness, vehemence, impatience.<BR>2 Joy, pleasure, happiness.<BR>3 Sport, pastime.<BR>4 A festival, festivity.<BR>5 Wish, inclination.<BR>6 Curiosity.<BR>7 Kind or friendly greeting, civility, salutation.<BR>8 The marriage thread or ring.<BR>9 The enjoyment of public diversions.<BR>10 Song, dance, shew or spectacle.<BR>11 Season of enjoyment.<BR>E.<BR>कुतुक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहल|कौतूहलं
कौतूहल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>2 Curiosity.<BR>E.<BR>कुतूहल and अण् pleonastic affix; also with ष्यञ् affix, कौतूहल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहलान्वित
कौतूहलान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eager, vehement.<BR>2 Curious.<BR>E.<BR>कौतूहल^1, and अन्वित having.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161202. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौदालिक|कौदालिकः
कौदालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of a mixed caste, the son of a fisherman by a woman of the washerman caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रविक|कौद्रविकं
कौद्रविक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रवीण|कौद्रवीणं
कौद्रवीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>A field, &c. of a particular grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>कोद्रव a species of grain, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्य|कौनख्यं
कौनख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Ugliness of the nails.<BR>E.<BR>कुनख, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्यादिक
कौनख्यादिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Neglect of personal decoration.<BR>E.<BR>कु bad, नखी a nail, आदि etcetera, कन् added, and अण् affix; allowing the nails to grow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=253" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तिक|कौंतिक|कौंतिकः|कौन्तिकः
कौन्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spearman, a soldier armed with a spear.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्त a spear, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्ती
कौन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्ति here said to mean a country, affixes अण् and ङीष्; produced in that district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्तेय|कौंतेय|कौंतेयः|कौन्तेयः
कौन्तेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Either of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्ती, and ढक् affix, son of KUNTĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौन्द
कौन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी-न्दं)<BR>Relating to the jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>कुन्द, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप|कौपं
कौप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Water of a well.<BR>E.<BR>कूप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपीन|कौपीनं
कौपीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A small piece of cloth worn over the privities.<BR>2 A privity, a privy part.<BR>3 A wrong or improper at.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कूप a well, &c. खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपोदकी
कौपोदकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The mace of KṚṢṆA: see कौमोदकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमार|कौमारं
कौमार<BR>mfn. adj. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Maiden, virgin.<BR>2 Juvenile.<BR>3 Soft, tender.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the seven Mātṛs, the divine mothers or personified energies of the gods; the energy or Śakti of KUMĀRA or KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Youth, childhood, from birth to the age of five.<BR>2 Maidenhood to the age of sixteen.<BR>E.<BR>कुमार a youth, and अञ् aff.; or कुमार the deity KĀRTTIKEYA, अण् and ङीष् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुद|कौमुदः
कौमुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The month Kartik, (Oct.-Nov.)<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 A festival.<BR>3 A festival in honour of KĀRTTIKEYA, held on the full moon of the month Kartik.<BR>4 Day of full moon in the month Aśvin.<BR>5 The same in the month Kartik.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुद a white lotus, अण् and ङीष् affixes, कौमुदी moonlight, equally white or brilliant; the other senses come from this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदिक
कौमुदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a water lily, abounding with them, &c. कुमुद, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीका
कौमुदीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A companion and confidant of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीचार|कौमुदीचारः
कौमुदीचार<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Day of full moon in the month of Aśvin.<BR>E.<BR>कौमुदी a festival, and चार what proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीपति|कौमुदीपतिः
कौमुदीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>कौमुदी moonlight, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदीवृक्ष|कौमुदीवृक्षः
कौमुदीवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>the stick or stand of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>कौमुदी here light in general, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदकी
कौमोदकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The club or mace of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कुमुदक what gives the earth pleasure, here said to be VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, affixes अण् and ङीष्; also कौमुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव|कौरवः
कौरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Kaurava, a descendant of KURU.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु, and अण् affix; also with वुञ् affix कौरवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्य|कौरव्यः
कौरव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>An ancestor or descendant of KURU.<BR>E.<BR>कुरु, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्म्म|कौर्म|कौर्मः
कौर्म्म<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Relating to a tortoise.<BR>2 Acting as a tortoise.<BR>3 Belonging or relating to the Avatar of VIṢṆU, as a tortoise, as the Kaurmma or Kūrma Purāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>कूर्म्म, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्प्य|कौर्प्यः
कौर्प्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The sign Scorpio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल|कौलः
कौल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Of a good family, well-born.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A worshipper of Śakti according to the left hand ritual.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The doctrine and practices of the left hand Śāktas.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a family, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेय|कौलकेयः
कौलकेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Of a good family, well-born.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of an unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>कुलक family, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटिनेय|कौलटिनेयः
कौलटिनेय<BR>mf. (-यः-यी)<BR>1 The son or daughter of a female beg gar.<BR>2 A bastard.<BR>E.<BR>कुलटा a female beggar, ढक् affix, and इनञ् inserted; also without the augment कौलटेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेय|कौलटेयः
कौलटेय<BR>mf. (-यः-यी)<BR>1 The child of a female beggar.<BR>2 A bastard, the child of an unchaste wife: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेर|कौलटेरः
कौलटेर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>A bastard son or daughter of a disloyal wife.<BR>2 The child of a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>कुलटा an unchaste woman, द्रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलत्थ
कौलत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्थी-त्थं)<BR>Made, prepared, consisting of a kind of vetch.<BR>E.<BR>कुलत्थ Dolichos biflorus, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलत्थीन|कौलत्थीनं
कौलत्थीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>A field, &c. of Dolichos biflorus.<BR>E.<BR>कुलत्थ, and खञ् affix; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलव|कौलवः
कौलव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>One of the astrological periods called Karaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालक
कौलालक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made by a potter.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Earthenware, porcelain.<BR>E.<BR>कुलाल, and वुज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिक|कौलिकः
कौलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ancestral, heritable in the family, belonging to it, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A heretic, an impostor.<BR>2 A weaver.<BR>3 A follower of the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR>E.<BR>कुल race, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन|कौलीनं|कौलीनः
कौलीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 High birth, family descent.<BR>2 Rumor, report.<BR>3 Evil report, detraction.<BR>4 Combat of animals, of birds, snakes, &c.<BR>5 Cock-fighting, &c. contention of animals as a species of gambling.<BR>6 A privity, a privy part.<BR>7 An improper act.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The son of a female beggar.<BR>2 A follower of the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR>E.<BR>कुलीन of a good family, affix श्वण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेय|कौलेयः
कौलेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Of a good family, well-born.<BR>2 Of the left hand Śākta sect.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयक|कौलेयकः
कौलेयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of good parentage.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, ढकञ् affix.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>कुल a house, affix as before; a domestic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्माषीण|कौल्माषीणं
कौल्माषीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>A field, &c. fit for or sown with a kind of bean.<BR>E.<BR>कुल्माष q. v. and खञ् affix; also with अञ् affix, कौल्माष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्य|कौल्यः
कौल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Of good family or parentage.<BR>2 Of the left hand Śākta sect.<BR>E.<BR>कुल family, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवल|कौवलं
कौवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The jujube tree: see कुवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेर|कौवेरं
कौवेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Relating or referable to KUVERA.<BR>2 Situated in the north.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The Śakti or female energy of KUVERA.<BR>2 The north quarter.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of costus, (C. speciosus): see कुष्ठ.<BR>E.<BR>कुवेर the deity, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Silk, silken.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Kanyakubja or Kanouj.,the ancient city so called.<BR>E.<BR>कोश, and अण् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल|कौशलं
कौशल<BR>mf. (-लं-ली)<BR>1 Greeting, salutation, friendly inquiry.<BR>2 A respectful present, a Nazr.<BR>3 Happiness, welfare, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुशल good fortune, well-being, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिका
कौशलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A present, a respectful gift or offering.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलेय|कौशलेयः
कौशलेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कौशल्या the wife of DAŚARATHA, ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्य|कौशल्यं
कौशल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Good fortune, well-being, &c.<BR>2 Cleverness, talent.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>The mother of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कुशल and यञ् affix, or कोशल a name of the father of this princess, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यानन्दन|कौशल्यानन्दनः
कौशल्यानन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दन a son, and कौशल्या RĀMA'S mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=254" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यायनि|कौशल्यायनिः
कौशल्यायनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>RĀMA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कौशल्या, and फिञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बर
कौशाम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Silk cloth.<BR>E.<BR>कौश, and अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशाम्बी|कौशांबी
कौशाम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>The name of an ancient city on the Ganges in the lower part of the Doab, in the vicinity of Kurrah; also वत्सपत्तन.<BR>E.<BR>कुशाम्ब a proper name, (the founder,) अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
कौशिक<BR>(-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Silk, silken.<BR>2 Of the family of Kuśika, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A fragrant substance, (Bdellium.)<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 A snake-catcher.<BR>5 An ichneumon, (Viverra ichneumon.)<BR>6 A title of VIŚVAMITRA.<BR>7 One skilled in dictionaries.<BR>8 A dictionary compiler.<BR>9 Love, the passion.<BR>10 The marrow.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A river in Behar, the Kosi or Koosa.<BR>2 A name of the goddess DURGA.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silk.<BR>E.<BR>कोश a sheathe, &c. ठक् affix, and ङीप् for the feminine; also कौषिक, and कौषिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकप्रिय|कौशिकप्रियः
कौशिकप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>कौशिक the sage VIŚVAMITRA, and प्रिय a friend or favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकफल|कौशिकफलः
कौशिकफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>कौशिक the saint VIŚVAMITRA, and फल fruit, being said to have been created by the sage in his progress to make a human being in rivalry to BRAHMĀ, the nut being the first rudiment of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिका
कौशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A drinking vessel, a cup or goblet.<BR>E.<BR>कुश to surround or contain, affixes ण्वुल् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकात्मज|कौशिकात्मजः
कौशिकात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>कौशिक INDRĀ, and आत्मज a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकायुध|कौशिकायुधं
कौशिकायुध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>The rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>कौशिक INDRĀ, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकाराति|कौशिकारातिः
कौशिकाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>कौशिक an owl, and अराति an enemy; also कौशिकारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशितकी
कौशितकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>कुश to retract, (wrath,) इतक and ङीष् affixes; this lady being an anti-xantippe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीलव्य
कौशीलव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>The profession of an actor, a dancer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कुशीलव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Silken, of silk.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Silk.<BR>2 A silk petticoat or trowsers, a woman's lower garment of silk.<BR>E.<BR>कोश or कोष the cocoon, and ढक affix; also कौषेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषिक|कौषिकः
कौषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of INDRA, &c.: see above, काशिक.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>DURGĀ, &c.: see कौशिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषेय|कौषेयं
कौषेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Silken: see कौशेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद
कौसीद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Usurious.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद्य|कौसीद्यं
कौसीद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Sloth, indolence.<BR>2 The practice of usury.<BR>E.<BR>कुसीद usury, &c. affix यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम|कौसुमं
कौसुम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Flowering.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम्भ|कौसुंभ|कौसुम्भः
कौसुम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भी-म्भं)<BR>Dyed with safflower, orange, red.<BR>E.<BR>कुसुम्भ safflower, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसृतिक|कौसृतिकः
कौसृतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A juggler, a conjuror.<BR>E.<BR>कुसृति wickedness, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभ|कौस्तुभः
कौस्तुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The jewel of KṚṢṆA suspended on his breast.<BR>E.<BR>कुस्तुभ a name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभलक्षक
कौस्तुभलक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभवक्षस्
कौस्तुभवक्षस्<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कौस्तभ the jewel, and वक्षस् the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नथ
क्नथ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्नथति क्नथयति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नस
क्नस<BR>(उ) क्नसु r. 4th cl. (क्नस्यति)<BR>1 To be crooked, (in mind or body.)<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(इ,) क्नसि r. 10th cl. (क्नंसयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नु
क्नु<BR>r. 9th cl. (ञ्) क्नुञ् (क्नुनाति-नीते)<BR>To sound; also क्नू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नू
क्नू<BR>r. 9th cl. (ञ्) क्नूञ् (क्ननाति-नीते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूय
क्नूय<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई) क्नूया (क्नूयते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To be wet.<BR>3 To stink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूयितृ
क्नूयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>What stinks, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्नूय, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्मर
क्मर<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्भरति)<BR>To be crooked in person, to be crooked in mind, to be fraudulent or crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकच|क्रकचः
क्रकच<BR>mn. (-चः-चं)<BR>1 A saw.<BR>2 A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>The Ketaki: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>क्र an imitative sound, कच to emit sound, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचच्छद|क्रकचच्छदः
क्रकचच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A plant with a strong smelling flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रकच a saw, and छद a leaf; having serrated leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपाद्
क्रकचपाद्<BR>m. (-पाद् or -पात्)<BR>A chameleon, a lizard.<BR>E.<BR>क्रकच a saw, पाद् a foot, saw-footed, or with a final vowel, क्रकचपाद m. (-दः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचपृष्ठी
क्रकचपृष्ठी<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>A small fish with numerous small spines in the back, (Coius cobojius, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रकच a saw, and पृष्ठ the back, saw-backed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकण|क्रकणः
क्रकण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of partridge, commonly Kayar; also कृकण and क्रकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकर|क्रकरः
क्रकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of partridge, called Kaër, (Perdix sylvatica); also कृकर.<BR>2 A thorny plant, vulgarly Karil: see करीर.<BR>3 A saw.<BR>4 A poor man.<BR>E.<BR>क्र an imitative sound, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतु|क्रतुः
क्रतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Sacrifice, offering, worship.<BR>2 An Aśvamedha, the sacrifice.<BR>3 The name of a Muni, one of the seven principal Ṛṣis or saints, the offspring of BRAHMĀ, married to Kriyā, and the father of the 60,000 Bālikhilyas.<BR>4 One of the ten VIŚVADEVAS.<BR>E.<BR>कृञ् to do, क्तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुच्छद
क्रतुच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A Jina.<BR>2 One skilled in sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुतुल्य
क्रतुतुल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Equal to an Aśvamedha in merit.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and तुल्य equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्रुह्
क्रतुद्रुह्<BR>m. (-द्रुक् or -द्रुग्-द्रुट् or -द्रुड्)<BR>An Asura, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु sacrifice, and द्रुह who hates, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुद्विष्
क्रतुद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>A Daitya or demon.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु a sacrifice, and द्विष who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुध्वंसिन्
क्रतुध्वंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु a sacrifice, ध्वसि to destroy, affix णिनि, the destroyer of DAKṢA'S sacrifice: see दक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपशु|क्रतुपशुः
क्रतुपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A horse, especially such a one as is fit for an Aśvamedha.<BR>E.<BR>क्रत sacrifice, and पशु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुपुरुष|क्रतुपुरुषः
क्रतुपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and पुरुष man or male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुफल
क्रतुफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The reward of a sacrifice, the object for which it is performed.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुभुज्
क्रतुभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A god, a deity.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु sacrifice, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुराज|क्रतुराजः
क्रतुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A particular sacrifice, the Rājasūya: one performed by a monarch who has subdued all the princes of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">Page256</a>] word.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु sacrifice, and राज a king; a royal or preeminent ceremony: see राजसूय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=255" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुविक्रयिन्
क्रतुविक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A Brahman who sells to another the possible benefits of a sacrifice which he has performed.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and विक्रयिन् who sells; also क्रतुविक्रायकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुसिद्धि
क्रतुसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Completion of a sacrifice, attainment of the object for which it is performed.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतूत्तम|क्रतूत्तमः
क्रतूत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The Rājasūya sacrifice: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>क्रतु, and उत्तम best: the pre-eminent sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ
क्रथ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्रथयति-ते and क्राथयति-ते)<BR>To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्रथयति)<BR>To amuse, to delight repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथन|क्रथनं
क्रथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Slaughter, killing.<BR>2 Snoring, stertor.<BR>E.<BR>क्रथ to kill, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथनक|क्रथनकं
क्रथनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A white sort of Agallochum: see अगुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रद
क्रद<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्रदते) or (इ) क्रदि (क्रन्दति)<BR>1 To confound, to confuse.<BR>2 To grieve, to be confused;<BR>also (क्रन्दति)<BR>1 To call, to cry out.<BR>2 To weep, to shed tears: see क्रन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्तृ
क्रन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Going, who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्द|क्रंदः|क्रन्दः
क्रन्द<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. generally used with आङ् prefixed, आक्रन्द (आक्रन्दति आक्रन्दयति)<BR>1 To weep, to shed tears.<BR>2 To call continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दन|क्रंदन|क्रन्दनं|क्रंदनः|क्रन्दनः
क्रन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cat.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Weeping, lamenting, sobbing.<BR>2 Crying out, calling.<BR>3 Mutual daring or defiance, challenging, braving.<BR>E.<BR>क्रदि to cry out, to call, sob, &c. affix ल्युट्; also with क्र affix क्रन्दित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रन्दित|क्रंदित|क्रन्दितं
क्रन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wept.<BR>2 Called or cried out.<BR>n. (-तं.)<BR>1 Weeping.<BR>2 Calling.<BR>3 Mutual daring: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>क्रन्द to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप
क्रप<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्रपते)<BR>1 To compassionate, to pity.<BR>2 To go or move: see कृप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम|क्रमः
क्रम<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) क्रमु (क्रामति क्राम्यति or क्रम्यति)<BR>To go, to walk, to step:<BR>(in the following senses it is optionally deponent): (क्रमते क्रम्यते)<BR>1 To proceed uninterruptedly.<BR>2 To grow or increase.<BR>3 To preserve.<BR>It is also active or deponent according to various prefixes and in various senses, as,<BR>with अति<BR>(अतिक्रामति)<BR>1 To go over or beyond, to leap over.<BR>2 To transgress, to pass beyond the bounds of virtue.<BR>With अनु<BR>(अनुक्रमते)<BR>To proceed regularly or in order.<BR>With अभि<BR>(अभिक्रामति)<BR>1 To overcome, to surpass.<BR>2 To assail.<BR>With अप<BR>(अपक्रमते)<BR>To go away, to depart.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>(आक्रमते)<BR>To rise as the sun, &c.<BR>or (आक्रामति)<BR>To rise, to mount, to overcome.<BR>With उत्,<BR>(उत्क्रामति)<BR>To transgress.<BR>With उप,<BR>(उपक्रामति)<BR>To depart.<BR>(उपक्रमते)<BR>To begin.<BR>With निर्,<BR>(निष्क्रामति)<BR>To go forth.<BR>With पर and आङ्<BR>(पराक्रमति)<BR>To display valour, to surpass or overcome.<BR>With प्र,<BR>(प्रक्रामति)<BR>To depart, to go or approach.<BR>(प्रक्रमते)<BR>To begin.<BR>With परि,<BR>(परिक्रामति)<BR>To wander about, to ramble.<BR>With वि,<BR>(विक्रामति)<BR>1 To overcome.<BR>2 To mount or ascend.<BR>(विक्रमते)<BR>To pace, to proceed by steps, to move with the feet.<BR>With वि and आङ्<BR>(व्याक्रमते)<BR>To transgress.<BR>With सम्,<BR>(संक्रामति)<BR>to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम|क्रमः
क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 A sacred precept or practice prescribed by the Vedas.<BR>3 Order, method.<BR>4 Power, strength.<BR>5 Overcoming, surpassing, subduing, &c.<BR>6 A foot.<BR>7 Uninterrupted progress.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमक|क्रमकः
क्रमक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Orderly, methodical.<BR>2 Proceeding, going.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A student who goes through a regular course of study, one who proceeds methodically. क्रम to go, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमज्या
क्रमज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>(In astronomy,) The sine of a planet's declination.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम going, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमण|क्रमणः
क्रमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A foot.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमतस्
क्रमतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Gradually, successively, in order.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रममाण
क्रममाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमयोग|क्रमयोगः
क्रमयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Successive or methodical practice.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमशस्
क्रमशस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Gradually, by degrees.<BR>2 Regularly, seriatim.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमागत|क्रमागतं
क्रमागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Descended to or inherited lineally, what comes from one's ancestors in regular succession.<BR>2 Arrived in due course or succession.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमागतत्व
क्रमागतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Hereditary succession or possession.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमायात|क्रमायातः
क्रमायात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proceeding in regular order.<BR>2 Descended lineally, (estate, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रम order, and आयात come, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमि|क्रमिः
क्रमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A worm: see क्रिमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमितृ
क्रमितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Going, who or what goes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, तृच् affix, with इट augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमु|क्रमुः
क्रमु<BR>m. (-मुः)<BR>The betel nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu); also क्रमुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुक|क्रमुकः
क्रमुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The areca or betel nut, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>2 A kind of tree, a red sort of Lodh: see लाघ्र.<BR>3 A kind of fragrant grass: see भद्रमुस्तक.<BR>4 The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR>5 The fruit of the cotton tree.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The areca tree.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, उक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुकफल|क्रमुकफलं
क्रमुकफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The areca nut.<BR>E.<BR>क्रमुक, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेल|क्रमेलः
क्रमेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A camel: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेलक|क्रमेलकः
क्रमेलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, एलप Uṇādi affix, and कन् added; or क्रम order, इल to go, क affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमोद्वेग|क्रमोद्वेगः
क्रमोद्वेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An ox.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम a foot, उद्वेग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय|क्रयः
क्रय<BR>m. (यः)<BR>Buying, purchase.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयक्रीत
क्रयक्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bought, purchased.<BR>E.<BR>क्रय, and क्रीत bought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयलेख्य|क्रयलेख्यं
क्रयलेख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Deed of sale, conveyance, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्रय, and लेख्य writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रय|क्रयविक्रयः
क्रयविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Trade, traffic, buying and selling.<BR>E.<BR>क्रय purchase, विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रयानुशय|क्रयविक्रयानुशयः
क्रयविक्रयानुशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Rescission of sale, a title of civil judicature.<BR>E.<BR>क्रयविक्रय, and अनुशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयविक्रयिक|क्रयविक्रयिकः
क्रयविक्रयिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A trader or merchant, a dealer.<BR>E.<BR>क्रय buying, विक्रय sale, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयशीर्ष|क्रयशीर्षं
क्रयशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>The coping of a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयारोह|क्रयारोहः
क्रयारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A market, a fair.<BR>E.<BR>क्रय purchase, and रुह to rise, आङ् prefix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=256" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिक|क्रयिकः
क्रयिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A trader, a dealer.<BR>2 A purchaser, a buyer.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, Uṇādi affix इकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिन्
क्रयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>A buyer or purchaser.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय्य|क्रय्यं
क्रय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Purchasable.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, यत् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्य|क्रव्यं
क्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Raw flesh.<BR>E.<BR>कृप to be able, यत् affix, and प changed to ब; the latter becomes dental before य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यघातन|क्रव्यघातनः
क्रव्यघातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>क्रव्य flesh, and घातन killing for its flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यभुज्
क्रव्यभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Carnivorous.<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>क्रव्य, भुज who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याद्
क्रव्याद्<BR>m. or mfn. (-व्याद् or -व्यात्)<BR>1 An imp or goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>2 A flesh-eater.<BR>3 A beast of prey, a carnivorous animal.<BR>E.<BR>क्रव्य flesh, अद् to eat, विद् affix, or with अण् affix, क्रव्याद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याद|क्रव्यादः
क्रव्याद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>An eater of flesh or meat, carnivorous.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 A hawk.<BR>4 Funeral fire.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्याशिन्
क्रव्याशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Carnivorous.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A demon, an anthropophagus.<BR>E.<BR>क्रव्य, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राकचिक|क्राकचिकः
क्राकचिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sawyer.<BR>E.<BR>क्रकच्, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्त|क्रांत|क्रान्तः
क्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Overcome, surpassed.<BR>2 Attacking, invading, gone to or against.<BR>3 Spread, extended.<BR>4 Going, going over or across.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 (In astronomy,) Declination.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>An astrological element, the conjunction of any planet with the moon.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्ति|क्रांति|क्रांतिः|क्रान्तिः
क्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 Overcoming, surpassing.<BR>3 The sun's course on the globe, the ecliptic.<BR>4 Declination of a planet.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिकक्ष|क्रांतिकक्ष|क्रान्तिकक्षः
क्रान्तिकक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The ecliptic.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and कक्ष girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिज्या
क्रान्तिज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>Sine of the declination.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिपात|क्रांतिपात|क्रान्तिपातः
क्रान्तिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The nodes of the ecliptic, or the equinoctial points.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and पात going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिपातगति
क्रान्तिपातगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Motion of the nodes of the ecliptic, precession of the equinox.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्तिपात, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिभाग|क्रान्तिभागः
क्रान्तिभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Declination of a point of the ecliptic.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and भाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिमण्डल|क्रांतिमंडल
क्रान्तिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The ecliptic.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तिवलय|क्रांतिवलय|क्रान्तिवलयः
क्रान्तिवलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The space within the tropics.<BR>E.<BR>क्रान्ति, and वलय bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रान्तु|क्रांतुः|क्रान्तुः
क्रान्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, वुन् Uṇādi affix, and the pen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रामत्
क्रामत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>1 Going, proceeding over or through.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायक|क्रायकः
क्रायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A buyer or purchaser.<BR>2 A dealer, a trader. क्री to buy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमि|क्रिमिः
क्रिमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A worm, an insect.<BR>2 Lac, which is the accumulation of an insect.<BR>3 A worm in the intestines.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, इन् Uṇādi affix, and इट् inserted; also कृमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिकण्टक|क्रिमिकण्टकं
क्रिमिकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Bireng: see कृमिकण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिघ्न|क्रिमिघ्नः
क्रिमिघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Vermifuge, anthelmintic.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>An anthelmintic shrub: see कृमिघ्न.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Somraj, (Serratula or Conyza anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>कृमि or क्रिमि a worm, and घ्न what kills: see कृमिघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिज|क्रिमिजं
क्रिमिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Aguru or aloe wood: see अगुरु.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The red dye called Lac.<BR>E.<BR>-क्रिमि a worm, and ज born; also कृमिज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशत्रु|क्रिमिशत्रुः
क्रिमिशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रिमि a worm, and शत्रु an enemy; the leaves yield, by expression, an acrid anthelmintic juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशात्रव|क्रिमिशात्रवः
क्रिमिशात्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A fetid mimosa, (M. farnesiana.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रिमि a worm, and शात्रव inimical: an anthelmintic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिशैल|क्रिमिशैलः
क्रिमिशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An ant hill.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिमि a worm, and शेल a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिय|क्रियः
क्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The sign Aries.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियमाण
क्रियमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Doing, making, engaged in.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिया
क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 An act, action, acting.<BR>2 Means, expedient.<BR>3 Beginning, undertaking.<BR>4 Atonement.<BR>5 Study.<BR>6 Worship.<BR>7 Disquisition.<BR>8 Bodily action.<BR>9 Remedying, physical treatment or practice.<BR>10 Instrument, implement.<BR>11 A religious or initiatory ceremony.<BR>12 Obsequies, rites performed immediately after death.<BR>12 Purificatory rites, as ablution, &c.<BR>14 Judicial investigation, by human means, as witnesses, documents, &c. or by superhuman or ordeals of various kinds.<BR>15 In grammar, a verb of two kinds, सकर्म्मक्रिया active or अकर्म्मक्रिया intransitive.<BR>16 A noun of action.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to act, to do, श affix, fem. do. टाप्; the above meanings may be all resolved into the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाकर
क्रियाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाकार|क्रियाकारः
क्रियाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>One who does any act, an agent, a performer.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A student, a novice, a tyro.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया study, and कर or कार, who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाद्वेषिन्
क्रियाद्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Opposed or averse to any act.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>One of the five kinds of witnesses, he whose testimony is hurtful to the cause.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया a suit, and द्वेषिन् injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियानिर्देश|क्रियानिर्देशः|क्रियानिर्द्देश
क्रियानिर्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Evidence.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and निर्देश proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियानुरूप
क्रियानुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Conformably to the act, according to the action.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and अनुरूप like to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापटु
क्रियापटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु)<BR>Clever, dexterous.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापर
क्रियापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Attentive to or diligent in the performance of their duties.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and पर engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापवर्ग|क्रियापवर्गः
क्रियापवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 End of an affair.<BR>2 Liberation from ceremonial acts.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and अपवर्ग end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियापाद|क्रियापादः
क्रियापाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The third division of a suit at law, the proof or rejoinder of the plaintiff.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिवा an affair, and पाद a fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाप्रसङ्ग|क्रियाप्रसंग
क्रियाप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Course of proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and प्रसङ्ग procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाफल
क्रियाफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Result or consequence of acts.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाभ्युपगम|क्रियाभ्युपगमः
क्रियाभ्युपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Special compact or agreement.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया business, अभि and उप prefixed to गम to go, affix अच्; going through with any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियालोप|क्रियालोपः
क्रियालोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Discontinuance or loss of any of the essential ceremonies of the Hindu religion.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and लोप loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=257" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावत्|क्रियावन्त्
क्रियावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Engaged in business.<BR>2 Understanding business, fit for it, possessed of worldly knowledge.<BR>2 Celebrating religious rites.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावश|क्रियावशः
क्रियावश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Subject to the influence of acts.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Necessity, necessary influence of acts done or to be done.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावसन्न|क्रियावसन्नः
क्रियावसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>One who loses his cause in a lawsuit.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया affair, अवसन्न ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावादिन्
क्रियावादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A plaintiff.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया affair, and वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाविधि|क्रियाविधिः
क्रियाविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Conduct of affairs.<BR>2 Mode of performing any rite.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियाविधिज्ञ
क्रियाविधिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Conversant with business.<BR>2 Understanding the ritual, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्रियाविधि, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियासमभिहार|क्रियासमभिहारः
क्रियासमभिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Repetition of any act, doing any thing repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया, and समभिहार repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियेन्द्रिय|क्रियेंद्रिय|क्रियेन्द्रियं
क्रियेन्द्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An organ of action, as the hand, foot, voice, organ of generation and that of excretion.<BR>E.<BR>क्रिया acting, and इन्द्रिय an organ; also कर्म्मेंन्द्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
क्री<BR>(डु, ङ्,) डुक्रीङ् r. 9th cl. (क्रीणाति क्रीणीते)<BR>To buy, to barter or exchange;<BR>with वि prefixed,<BR>to sell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) क्रीडृ (क्रीडति)<BR>To play, to sport;<BR>with अनु, अव, आङ्, परि, or सम् prefixed, it is deponent,<BR>as अनुक्रीडते, &c. unless अनु requires the accusative case, and the compound with सम् implies inarticulate sound, as तमनुक्रीडति सा she plays with him, संक्रीडति चक्रं the wheel creaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा)<BR>1 Sport, play, pastime, pleasure, amusement.<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 Playing, as a ball, &c.<BR>2 Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीड to play, अ affix, and fem. do. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडन|क्रीडनं
क्रीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Play, sport, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीड to play, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडत्
क्रीडत्<BR>mfn. (-डन्-डन्ती-डत्)<BR>Playing, gamboling, sporting.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीड, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडमान
क्रीडमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीड, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडाकूत
क्रीडाकूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sportive or wanton purpose or desire.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा, and आकूत wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडाकोप|क्रीडाकोपः
क्रीडाकोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Assumed anger, anger in sport.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा, and कोप anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडारत्न|क्रीडारत्नं
क्रीडारत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडारथ|क्रीडारथः
क्रीडारथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A car, a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा sport, pleasure, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडावत्
क्रीडावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sporting, sportive.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडासरस्
क्रीडासरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A reservoir, a basin.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीडा pleasure, सरस् a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीत|क्रीतः
क्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bought, purchased.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A son, one of the twelve kinds acknowledged by the ancient Hindu law; he who is purchased from his natural parents.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतक|क्रीतकः
क्रीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A son bought from his natural parents, and adopted as male issue; also क्रीत and क्रीतपुत्त्रः see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतानुशय|क्रीतानुशयः
क्रीतानुशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Returning a purchase upon the seller, admissible in some cases by law.<BR>E.<BR>क्रीत bought, अनुशय repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च<BR>(उ) क्रुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (क्रुञ्चति)<BR>1 To go, to approach to wards or arrive at.<BR>2 To move crookedly.<BR>3 To be crooked.<BR>4 To curve or make crooked.<BR>5 To become small, to shrink.<BR>6 To make small, to lessen; also कुञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च्|क्रुंच्
क्रुञ्च्<BR>mf. (क्रुङ् क्रुञ्चा)<BR>A curlew.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुञ्च to go crookedly, affix क्विन्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A name of the mountain Krouncha.<BR>f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>A kind of Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुञ्च to be crooked, affixes क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुड
क्रुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (क्रुडति)<BR>To sink.<BR>2 To be childish.<BR>3 To eat.<BR>4 To be thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुद्ध|क्रुद्धः
क्रुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Angry, wrathful.<BR>2 Fierce, cruel.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Anger.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुध to be angry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध
क्रुध<BR>(औ, ऌ) औक्रुधॢ r. 4th cl. (क्रुध्यति)<BR>To be wrathful, to be flushed with anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्
क्रुध्<BR>f. (क्रुत्) or (-क्रुद्)<BR>Anger, passion.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुध to be angry, affix क्विप्; also with अङ् and टाप् affixes, क्रुधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुधा
क्रुधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Anger: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्यत्
क्रुध्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्)<BR>Being angry.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुध, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुन्थ
क्रुन्थ<BR>r. 9th cl. (क्रुथ्नाति)<BR>1 To be connected with, to cling or adhere to.<BR>2 To be distressed, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश
क्रुश<BR>r. 1st cl. (-क्रोशति)<BR>1 To call.<BR>2 To cry, to weep.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To feel for, to sympathise with.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To revile, to abuse or censure.<BR>With उप,<BR>To reproach.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To cry aloud, to shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्वन्
क्रुश्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा)<BR>A jackall.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुश to cry or howl, Uṇādi affix क्वनिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुष्ट|क्रुष्टं
क्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Wept, cried.<BR>2 Cried aloud, bawled.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Weeping, sobbing.<BR>2 Noise, sound.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुश to weep, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर|क्रूरः
क्रूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Cruel, pitiless.<BR>2 Hard, harsh.<BR>3 Hard, solid.<BR>4 Mischievous, destructive.<BR>5 Formidable, terrible.<BR>6 Hot, sharp.<BR>7 Disagreeable.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An odd sign of the zodiac, as the first, third, fifth, &c. which are of malignant influences.<BR>2 A hawk.<BR>3 A heron.<BR>4 Red oleander.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, रक् Uṇādi affix, and क्रू substituted for कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरकर्म्मन्|क्रूरकर्मन्
क्रूरकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Fierce, cruel, unrelenting.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरकोष्ठ
क्रूरकोष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>Torpid or costive bowels unaffected by strong purgatives.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर, and कोष्ठ the alimentary canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरगन्ध|क्रूरगंध|क्रूरगन्धः
क्रूरगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरचरित
क्रूरचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cruel, ferocious, addicted to cruel practices.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर, and चरित who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरता
क्रूरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Cruelty, fierceness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्रूरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरदृश्
क्रूरदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Mischievous, villainous.<BR>2 Evil-eyed.<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A name of the planet Śani or Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर cruel, &c. and दृश who sees, from दृश to see, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरराविन्
क्रूरराविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर formidable, राविन् who cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरलोचन|क्रूरलोचनः
क्रूरलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर evil, and लाचन an eye; of an evil or inauspicious aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूरव
क्रूरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A jackall.<BR>2 Any thing bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूराकृति|क्रूराकृतिः
क्रूराकृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA the ruler of Laṅkā.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर evil, and आकृति figure, form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूराचार
क्रूराचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Following barbarous or savage practices.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=258" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर्च्च|क्रूर्च
क्रूर्च्च<BR>mn. (-र्चः-र्चं)<BR>The beard: see कूर्च्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणि|क्रेणिः
क्रेणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Buying, purchase.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, णि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतव्य|क्रेतव्यं
क्रेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Purchasable.<BR>E.<BR>future participle of क्री to buy, affix तव्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतृ
क्रेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A purchaser, a buyer. क्री to buy, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेय|क्रेयं
क्रेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Purchasable.<BR>E.<BR>क्री to buy, affix यत्; to be bought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्च|क्रोंच|क्रोंचः|क्रोञ्चः
क्रोञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A mountain: see क्रौञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्चपदा
क्रोञ्चपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A species of metre of four lines, and twenty-five syllables in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोञ्चदारण
क्रोञ्चदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोञ्च or क्रौञ्च a mountain, and दारण the render or tearer; also क्रौञ्चदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोड|क्रोडं|क्रोडः
क्रोड<BR>nf. (-डं-डा)<BR>1 The breast, the chest.<BR>2 The haunch, the flank, the hollow above the hip.<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A name of Śani or Saturn.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुड to be thick, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडपर्णी|क्रोडपर्ण्णी
क्रोडपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडपाद|क्रोडपादः
क्रोडपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोड the breast, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडाङ्क|क्रोडांक|क्रोडाङ्कः
क्रोडाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडाङ्गि
क्रोडाङ्गि<BR>m. (-ङ्गिः)<BR>A turtle or tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोड and अङ्गि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकरण|क्रोडीकरणं
क्रोडीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोड breast or side, करण making, and च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकृति|क्रोडीकृतिः
क्रोडीकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Embracing, mutual embrace.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding; कृति making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोथ|क्रोथः
क्रोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Killing, slaying.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुथ to kill or hurt, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोध|क्रोधः
क्रोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Anger, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुध to be angry, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधज|क्रोधजः
क्रोधज<BR>mf. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Proceeding from or engendered by wrath; it especially applies to eight vices, hatred, envy, oppression, violence, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध passion, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधन|क्रोधनः
क्रोधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Passionate, angry, wrathful.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A passionate woman, a vixen.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुध to be angry, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधनीय
क्रोधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Provocative.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An injury.<BR>E.<BR>क्नुध to be angry, (on account of,) अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधमय
क्रोधमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Angry, passionate.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधमूर्च्छित
क्रोधमूर्च्छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Passionate, angry, overcome with rage.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Cor.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध wrath, and मूर्च्छित confused, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधवर्जित|क्रोधवर्ज्जित
क्रोधवर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Free from wrath, mild, calm.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध, and वर्जित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधवश
क्रोधवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Passionate, violent.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध, and वश subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधिन्
क्रोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Angry, passionate.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध angry, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधोज्झित
क्रोधोज्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Calm, composed, free from wrath.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोध, and उज्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोश|क्रोशः
क्रोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A measure of distance, a league, a Koś, containing 4000 cubits; some double this, and make the Koś 8000 cubits.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुश to call, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशत्
क्रोशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Crying, calling out. क्रुश to cry, शत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशताल|क्रोशतालः
क्रोशताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large or double drum.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोश a Koś, and ताल a tune; whose sound may be heard for a league.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशध्वनि|क्रोशध्वनिः
क्रोशध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A large drum.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोश, and ध्वनि sound: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशयुग|क्रोशयुगं
क्रोशयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A measure of two Koś 4000 yards, or about 2½ miles; this seems to correspond to the modern Koś, but the standard varies.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोश a Koś, and युग a pair; also गव्यूति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टु
क्रोष्टु<BR>mf. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री)<BR>A jackall.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुश to cry or call, and तुन् affix; the noun declined in many cases like nouns in ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका
क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Chaculiya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.) or according to some, Ramvāsac, a different plant: see क्रोष्टुविन्ना.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोष्टु a jackall, कन् affix, and पुच्छिका tail; the flower being compared to the tail of the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुकमेखला
क्रोष्टुकमेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The plant Cāculiya; see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुपुच्छिका
क्रोष्टुपुच्छिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See क्रोष्टुकपुच्छिका: also क्रोष्टुपुच्छी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टुविन्ना
क्रोष्टुविन्ना<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>The name of a plant, either Chaculiya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.) or a different plant called Ramvāsac.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोष्टु a jackall, and विन्न known; known by being compared to the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टेक्षु|क्रोष्टेक्षुः
क्रोष्टेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The white sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोष्ट, and इक्षु cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्ट्री
क्रोष्ट्री<BR>f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>1 The black or white Bhuincaönra, (Convolvulus paniculatus): see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR>2 Cāculiya: see क्रोष्टुविन्ना.<BR>3 A she jackall: see क्रोष्टु.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुश to cry, affix ष्ट्रन् and fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्च|क्रौंच|क्रौंचः|क्रौञ्चः
क्रौञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>1 A kind of heron, (Ardea jaculator, BUC.)<BR>2 One of the Dvīpas or principal divisions of the world, surrounded by the sea of curds.<BR>3 A mountain, part of the Himāla range, situated in the eastern part of the chain on the north of Asam.<BR>4 A Jaina emblem, the figure of the curlew, used as a symbol.<BR>5 The name of a demon.<BR>f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>The female of the curlew.<BR>E.<BR>क्रुञ्च to go crookedly, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चदारण|क्रौंचदारण|क्रौञ्चदारणः
क्रौञ्चदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>क्रौञ्च the name of a mountain; also of an Asura, and दारण the tearer or destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चादन|क्रौंचादन|क्रौञ्चादनं
क्रौञ्चादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Long pepper.<BR>2 The fibres of the stalk of the lotus.<BR>3 An esculent root, commonly Ghenchu.<BR>4 An aquatic plant, commonly Ciñcāta.<BR>E.<BR>क्रौञ्च the heron, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चाराति|क्रौंचाराति|क्रौञ्चारातिः
क्रौञ्चाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA. क्रौञ्च the Asura, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौञ्चारि|क्रौंचारि|क्रौञ्चारिः
क्रौञ्चारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 The deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 The hero and Avatāra PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>क्रौञ्च the Asura or the mountain, and अरि a foe: RĀMA is said to have made with his arrows a pass or defile through the Krauncha mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौर्य्य|क्रौर्य|क्रौर्यं
क्रौर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Cruelty, fierceness, passion.<BR>E.<BR>क्रूर cruel, &c. य्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौशशतिक|क्रौशशतिकः
क्रौशशतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who goes a hundred Koś or leagues.<BR>E.<BR>क्रोश a Koś, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लथ
क्लथ<BR>(म) r. 1st cl. (क्लथति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लद
क्लद<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्लदते) or (इ) क्लदि (क्लंदते)<BR>1 To be confused, to grieve.<BR>2 To confound;<BR>also क्लदि (क्लंदति)<BR>1 To call.<BR>2 To shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लप
क्लप<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्लापयति)<BR>To speak, to speak barbarously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम<BR>(उ, भ, ञि, इर) क्लमु r. 4th cl. (क्लाम्यति)<BR>To be fatigued, to be weary or exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम|क्लमः
क्लम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Fatigue, weariness, exhaustion.<BR>E.<BR>क्लम to be weary, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथ|क्लमथः
क्लमथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Fatigue, exhaustion.<BR>E.<BR>क्लम to be weary, Uṇādi affix अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=259" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमित्व
क्लमित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Exhaustion, languor, fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>क्लमिन्, and त्व affix; also with तल्, क्लमिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमिन्
क्लमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Weary, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>क्लम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लव
क्लव<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्लवते)<BR>To fear, to be afraid: वि is usually prefixed in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्त|क्लांत|क्लान्तः
क्लान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता न्तं)<BR>1 Wearied.<BR>2 Depressed in spirits or exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>क्लम to be weary, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तमनस्
क्लान्तमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Low spirited, languid, melancholy.<BR>E.<BR>क्लान्त, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्ति|क्लांति|क्लांतिः|क्लान्तिः
क्लान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Fatigue, weariness.<BR>E.<BR>क्लम to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तिच्छिद्|क्लांतिच्छिद्
क्लान्तिच्छिद्<BR>mfn. (-च्छित् or च्छिद्)<BR>Relieving fatigue, refreshing, invigorating.<BR>E.<BR>क्लान्ति, and च्छिद् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लान्तिच्छेद
क्लान्तिच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Refreshing, restoring, removing fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>क्लान्ति, and च्छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिद
क्लिद<BR>(इ) क्लिदि r. 1st cl. (क्लिंदते-ति)<BR>To bewail, to lament, to weep.<BR>(ऊ, इर); इर क्लिदू r. 4th cl. (क्लिद्युति)<BR>To be or become wet, damp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्न|क्लिन्नं
क्लिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Wet, moistened.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be or become wet, irr. participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्नवर्त्मन्
क्लिन्नवर्त्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>Excess of the lachrymal discharge, watering of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिन्न, and वर्त्मन् the eyelid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्नाक्ष|क्लिन्नाक्षः
क्लिन्नाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Blear-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिन्न wet, and अक्ष the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिश
क्लिश<BR>(उ) क्लिशु r. 4th cl. (क्लिश्यते)<BR>1 To suffer distress.<BR>2 To inflict or cause distress;<BR>(ऊ,) क्लिशू r. 9th cl. (क्लिश्नाति)<BR>1 To oppose.<BR>2 To afflict, to distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशित|क्लिशितः
क्लिशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distrest, afflicted, wearied.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to be distrest, &c. affix क्त with इद inserted; also without इट् क्लिष्ट^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: missing space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशितवत्
क्लिशितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Suffering pain or distress.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्ट|क्लिष्टः
क्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Distrest, afflicted, &c.<BR>2 Inconsistent, contradictory.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to be distrest, &c. affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टि|क्लिष्टिः
क्लिष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Calamity, distress.<BR>2 Service.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to afflict, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतक
क्लीतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Liquorice, (Glycirrhiza glabra?)<BR>E.<BR>क्लीव to be weak, affix क्त, व being dropped; क्लीत weakness, कल to remove, and ल dropped by affixing ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीतकिका
क्लीतकिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The indigo plant, (Indigofera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>क्रीतक traffic, कन् pleonastic, the fem. form; र is changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब|क्लीबः
क्लीब<BR>(ऋ) क्लीबृ r. 1st cl. (क्लीबते)<BR>1 To be impotent.<BR>2 To be timorous, to be modest or unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव<BR>(ऋ) क्लीबृ r. 1st cl. (क्लीवते)<BR>1 To be impotent.<BR>2 To be timid or modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Weak, impotent.<BR>2 Idle, slothful.<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 The neuter gender.<BR>2 A eunuch.<BR>E.<BR>क्लीव to be weak or timid, affix क; also read क्लीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेद|क्लेदः
क्लेद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Wetness, dampness, moisture, &c.<BR>2 Running, discharge from a sore.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be wet, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदक|क्लेदकः
क्लेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Wetting, moistening, making wet or moist.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Phlegm in the stomach, excess of saliva.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be wet, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन्
क्लेदन्<BR>m. (-दा)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be damp, कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन|क्लेदनः
क्लेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wetting, moistening.<BR>2 Oozing, trickling.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humor.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be moist, ल्यट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदु|क्लेदुः
क्लेदु<BR>m. (-दुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Complication of disorders.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be wet or damp, उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्लेशते)<BR>1 To speak articulately.<BR>2 To distress.<BR>3 To impede or obstruct.<BR>4 To kill, to strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश|क्लेशः
क्लेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Pain, affliction or distress.<BR>2 Pain from disease, anguish.<BR>3 Worldly occupation, care, trouble.<BR>4 Wrath, anger.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to suffer or inflict pain, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशक
क्लेशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Giving pain, annoying, afflicting.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशप्रहाण
क्लेशप्रहाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Termination of distress, especially of worldly cares, passions, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्लेश, and प्रहाण destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशापह|क्लेशापहः
क्लेशापह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Consolatory, consoling.<BR>2 Palliative, allaying pain.<BR>m. (हः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>क्लेश, and अपह what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशित|क्लेशितः
क्लेशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिश to suffer pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैतकिक|क्लैतकिकं
क्लैतकिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Wine, spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>क्लीतक liquorice, ठक् affix; a fermented liquor being prepared from this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैव्य|क्लैव्यं
क्लैव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Absence of virility, impotence.<BR>2 The neuter gender.<BR>2 Unmanliness, cowardice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्लीव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोमन्
क्लोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The bladder.<BR>E.<BR>क्लु to go, कनिन् affix; also with a final vowel; क्लोम n. (-मं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्व
क्व<BR>ind.<BR>Where, in what place or degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वङ्गु|क्वङ्गुः
क्वङ्गु<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>A sort of Panick: see कङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वचित्
क्वचित्<BR>ind.<BR>Somewhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण|क्वणः
क्वण<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्वणति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण|क्वणः
क्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The sound or tone of any musical instrument.<BR>2 Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, अप् affix; also क्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणत्
क्वणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्^1)<BR>Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण, and शतृ aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणन|क्वणनं|क्वणनः
क्वणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The sound of any musical instrument.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A small earthen pot or boiler.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणित|क्वणितं
क्वणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, twanged.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वत्य
क्वत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Of or belonging to where or what place.<BR>E.<BR>त्यप् added to क्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ|क्वथः
क्वथ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ए,) क्वथे (क्वथति)<BR>To decoct, to boil, to prepare by heat, to digest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथन|क्वथनं
क्वथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Boiling, decocting.<BR>E.<BR>क्वथ to boil, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथित|क्वथितः
क्वथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Boiled, decocted, stewed, digested.<BR>E.<BR>क्वथ to decoct, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाण|क्वाणः
क्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sound of musical instruments.<BR>E.<BR>क्वण to sound, affix घञ्: see क्वण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथ|क्वाथः
क्वाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A decoction, any solution or infusion prepared with a continued and gentle heat.<BR>2 Pain, sorrow.<BR>3 Calamity, distress.<BR>4 The mixture of the materials for a decoction.<BR>E.<BR>क्वथ to decoct, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथोद्भव|क्वाथोद्भवं|क्वाथोद्भवः
क्वाथोद्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Blue vitriol used as a collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>क्वाथ, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वेल
क्वेल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊ) क्वेलू (क्वेलति)<BR>To shake or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष|क्षः
क्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A destruction of the world.<BR>2 A demon, a goblin.<BR>3 The third incarnation of VIṢṆU, the Narasiṃha Avatāra.<BR>4 Lightning.<BR>5 A field.<BR>6 A peasant, a husbandman.<BR>7 Loss, disappearance.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि or क्षै to waste, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षज
क्षज<BR>(म, ष) r. 1st cl. (क्षजते)<BR>1 To go or approach.<BR>2 To give.<BR>(इ, ष, म) क्षजि r. 1st cl. (क्षञ्जते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To give.<BR>r. 1st and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">Page261</a>] 10th cls. (इ) क्षजि (क्षञ्जति क्षञ्जयति)<BR>To live in distress, to live in pain or want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=260" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण|क्षणं|क्षणः
क्षण<BR>(उ) क्षणु r. 8th cl. (क्षणति क्षणुते)<BR>To kill, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण|क्षणं|क्षणः
क्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A measure of time, equal to thirty Kalās or four minutes.<BR>2 A moment.<BR>3 A festival.<BR>4 Vacation from work, state of being unemployed.<BR>5 Leisure, opportunity.<BR>6 A certain day of the fortnight, as the full, change, &c. see पर्वन्.<BR>7 Dependence, servitude.<BR>8 The centre, the middle.<BR>n. adv. (-णं)<BR>For a moment.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण to injure, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणक्षेप|क्षणक्षेपः
क्षणक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A short delay.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and क्षेप throwing (away).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतु|क्षणतुः
क्षणतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A wound or sore.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण to hurt, अतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणद|क्षणदं|क्षणदः
क्षणद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Water.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण leisure, a moment, &c. and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदाचर
क्षणदाचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Nocturnal, nightwalker.<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A fiend, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>क्षणदा night, and चर who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदान्ध्य|क्षणदांध्य
क्षणदान्ध्य<BR>n. (-न्ध्यं)<BR>Night blindness, nyctalopsis.<BR>E.<BR>क्षणदा, and आन्ध्य blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणदृष्ट
क्षणदृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Momentarily visible, seen for an instant.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणद्युति|क्षणद्युतिः
क्षणद्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षंण, and द्युति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणन|क्षणनं
क्षणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण to hurt, to kill, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनिश्वास|क्षणनिश्वासः
क्षणनिश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A porpoise, the Gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण a moment, and निश्वास breath, breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणप्रकाश
क्षणप्रकाश<BR>f. (-शः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and प्रकाश manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणप्रभ
क्षणप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Gleaming, flashing.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण a moment, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभङ्गुर|क्षणभंगुर|क्षणभङ्गुरः
क्षणभङ्गुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Transient, frail, perishable.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and भङ्गुर breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणभूत
क्षणभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Momentary, short-lived.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणमात्र
क्षणमात्र<BR>adv. n. (-त्रं)<BR>Momentary, but for a moment.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणरामिन्
क्षणरामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण a moment, and रम to play, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणविध्वंसिन्
क्षणविध्वंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Transient, frail.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and विध्वंसिन् what is destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणान्तर
क्षणान्तर<BR>adv. n. (-रं)<BR>A minute afterwards, the next moment.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिक|क्षणिकः
क्षणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Momentary, transient.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण a moment, affix कन् or ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिन्
क्षणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Momentary, transient.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत|क्षतं
क्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hit, hurt, wounded, &c.<BR>2 Broken, torn, rent.<BR>3 Trodden or broken down.<BR>4 Impaired, diminished.<BR>5 Destroyed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A wound, a sore, a hurt.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण to hurt, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतघ्न|क्षतघ्नः
क्षतघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The name of a plant, (Conyza lacera.)<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Lac, the animal dye.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत a wound, and घ्न what destroys or removes; from हन to kill, affix टक्, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतज|क्षतजं
क्षतज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 Pus, matter.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत a wound, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षततेजस्
क्षततेजस्<BR>mfn. (-जः-जाः-जं)<BR>Dimmed, obscured, (as light or power.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षत, and तेजस् splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतविक्षत
क्षतविक्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mangled, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत, and विक्षत wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतविध्वंसिन्
क्षतविध्वंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A sort of potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus): see ष्टद्धदार.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत a wound, &c. ध्वंसि to attack, with वि prefix, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतवृत्ति|क्षतवृत्तिः
क्षतवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Destitution, being without the means of support, living on what one can get.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत, and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतव्रत|क्षतव्रतः
क्षतव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A violator of a vow or religious engagement.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत broken, and व्रत a religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतहर|क्षतहरं
क्षतहर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Agallochum or aloe wood: see अगुरु.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत a wound, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतारि
क्षतारि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत struck, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षति|क्षतिः
क्षति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A wound.<BR>E.<BR>क्षण to hurt, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतौजस्
क्षतौजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Weakened, reduced, impaired.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत, and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ)<BR>Occupied, engaged in work.<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>1 A charioteer, a coachman.<BR>2 A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>3 The son of a Śūdra by a Kṣatriya woman, whose employment is catching animals that live in holes.<BR>4 The son of a female slave.<BR>5 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>6 The son of a Śūdra man and Vaiśya woman.<BR>E.<BR>क्षद a Sautra root, to screen or defend, to join or mix, Uṇādi affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्र
क्षत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A man of the second or military and regal class.<BR>n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>क्षद Sautra root, to divide or eat, Uṇādi affix त्र; this word and its derivatives are commonly, for the sake of convenience, written with one त, क्षत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रधर्म्म
क्षत्त्रधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The duty of a Kṣatriya, bravery, military conduct.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्त्र, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रधर्म्मानुग
क्षत्त्रधर्म्मानुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Following or observing the duty of a soldier.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्त्रधर्म्म, and अनुग who follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रबन्धु
क्षत्त्रबन्धु<BR>mfn. (-न्धुः-न्धू or न्धुः-न्धु)<BR>1 A mere Kṣatriya, a certain Kṣatriya.<BR>2 A Kṣatriya, one of the military tribe: see ब्रह्मबन्धु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रिन्
क्षत्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्त्री)<BR>A man of the military class.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रिय
क्षत्त्रिय<BR>mf. (-यः-या or -याणी)<BR>A man or woman of the second or military tribe.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The wife of a Kṣatriya.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्त्र, affix घ, fem. टाप् or ङीष्, in one form, with आनुक inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रियजाति
क्षत्त्रियजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The military tribe or caste.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्त्रिय, and जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रियधर्म्म
क्षत्त्रियधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The duty or occupation of the warrior tribe, war, government, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्त्रिय, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्त्रियप्राय
क्षत्त्रियप्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Full of or abounding with the military tribe.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्रिय, and प्राय most.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद
क्षद<BR>Sautra r. 1st cl. (क्षदति)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To pull to pieces, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदत्
क्षदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Dividing, tearing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षद to eat, &c., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदन|क्षदनं
क्षदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Tearing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षद to eat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तव्य|क्षंतव्य
क्षन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be endured, to be suffered or submitted to patiently.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=261" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्तृ|क्षंतृ
क्षन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Patient, resigned.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, to be patient, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप|क्षपः
क्षप<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्षपयति)<BR>1 To send, to throw, to cast, to direct, &c.<BR>2 To bear patiently.<BR>(इ) क्षपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (क्षम्पति क्षम्पयति)<BR>1 To bear patiently, to endure.<BR>3 To compassionate.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण|क्षपणः
क्षपण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Shameless, impudent.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Defilement, impurity.<BR>E.<BR>क्षप to throw away (shame,) affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणक|क्षपणकः
क्षपणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Buddha.<BR>2 A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>3 A Jaina mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 An oar.<BR>2 A net: see क्षेपणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्यु|क्षपण्युः
क्षपण्यु<BR>m. (-ण्युः)<BR>Offence, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>क्षप to bear, अण्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपयत्
क्षपयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Bearing patiently, enduring.<BR>2 Casting, sending.<BR>E.<BR>क्षप to send, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>क्षप to send or reject, अ affix, and टाप् fem. do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाकर|क्षपाकरः
क्षपाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा night, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाघन|क्षपाघनः
क्षपाघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dark cloud or clouds of night.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा, and घन a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाचर|क्षपाचरः
क्षपाचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fiend, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाट|क्षपाटः
क्षपाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा night, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपानाथ|क्षपानाथः
क्षपानाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपान्त
क्षपान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपाह
क्षपाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A day and night.<BR>E.<BR>क्षपा, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपित
क्षपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Submitted to, borne, endured.<BR>2 Sent, cast, directed.<BR>E.<BR>क्षप, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम<BR>(उ, ष, ञि) ञिक्षमुष r. 1st cl. (क्षमते)<BR>To bear or endure.<BR>(उ, इर, भ) इरक्षमुभ r. 4th cl. (क्षम्यति)<BR>To bear or endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Patient, resigned, enduring.<BR>2 Refraining from, forbearing.<BR>2 Able, adequate.<BR>4 Benevolent, friendly.<BR>5 Fit, appropriate, suitable, proper.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Patience.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 Night.<BR>4 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम as above, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमान्वित
क्षमान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Patient, enduring.<BR>2 Forgiving.<BR>E.<BR>क्षमा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापर
क्षमापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Patient, forbearing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षमा, पर practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमाभुज्
क्षमाभुज्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>Patient.<BR>m. (-क)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>क्षमा, the earth, &c. and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमायुक्त
क्षमायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षमा, and युक्त joined with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमावत्|क्षमावन्त्
क्षमावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षमा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितृ
क्षमितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमिन्
क्षमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Patient.<BR>2 Capable, able.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
क्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Loss, waste, destruction, removal, &c.<BR>2 A destruction of the universe.<BR>3 Consumption, Phthisis pulmonalis.<BR>4 A house, an abode.<BR>5 Sickness in general.<BR>6 Decay, wasting away.<BR>7 In algebra, negative quantity, minus.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste or destroy, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकर
क्षयकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Destroying, terminating.<BR>2 Liberating from existence.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकाल|क्षयकालः
क्षयकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The end of all things, the period of destruction.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयकास|क्षयकासः
क्षयकास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A consumptive or phthisical cough.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and कास cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथु|क्षयथुः
क्षयथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Cough, consumption.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, अथुच् affix; some copies read this क्षवथु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयनाशिनी
क्षयनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Celtis Orientalis): see जीवन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय consumption, and नाशिनी what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयपक्ष|क्षयपक्षः
क्षयपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The dark fortnight, that of the moon's wane.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and पक्ष half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयवायु|क्षयवायुः
क्षयवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The wind that is to blow at the end of the world.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and वायु wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षययुक्ति|क्षययुक्तिः
क्षययुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Necessity or opportunity of destroying.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and युक्ति fitness; also क्षययोग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोग|क्षयरोगः
क्षयरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Consumption.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोगित्व
क्षयरोगित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Consumption.<BR>E.<BR>क्षयरोगिन्, and त्व affix; also with तल् क्षयरोगिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयरोगिन्
क्षयरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Consumptive, hectic.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and रोगिन् diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयसम्पद्|क्षयसंपद्
क्षयसम्पद्<BR>f. (-त् or -द्)<BR>Total loss, ruin, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and सम्पद् increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिन्
क्षयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Wasting, decaying.<BR>2 Consumptive.<BR>E.<BR>क्षय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिष्णु
क्षयिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Wasting, decaying, perishing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to perish, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षरति)<BR>1 To drop or let fall.<BR>2 To distil, to ooze, to trickle.<BR>With सं,<BR>To flow.<BR>With आ,<BR>r. of the 10th cl. (आक्षारयति)<BR>To accuse, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 Trickling, oozing.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर to drop, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरज|क्षरजः
क्षरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by distillation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर, and ज born; also क्षरेज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरण|क्षरणं
क्षरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Trickling, running.<BR>2 Distilling, dropping.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरत्
क्षरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Trickling, oozing, running.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर to trickle, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरपत्रा
क्षरपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>The Droṇapuṣpa plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरभाव
क्षरभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Mutable, dissoluble.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर flowing, भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरित
क्षरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Oozed, trickling, dropped, flowing, liquefied.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरिन्
क्षरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Dropping, flowing, trickling.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर water, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरेज
क्षरेज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by distilling, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर in the seventh case, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल
क्षल<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षलति)<BR>1 To shake.<BR>2 To move, (some consider this as interchangeable with क्षर.)<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्षलयति)<BR>To purify, to cleanse or make clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षव|क्षवः
क्षव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Sneezing.<BR>2 Cough, catarrh.<BR>3 A species of Mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sneeze, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवकृत्
क्षवकृत्<BR>mfn. (-त्)<BR>Sneezing, coughing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षव, and कृत who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षविका
क्षविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of rice.<BR>2 A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथु|क्षवथुः
क्षवथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 Cough, catarrh.<BR>2 Sneezing.<BR>3 Irritation of the throat, sore throat.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sneeze, &c. अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=262" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्त्र
क्षात्त्र<BR>mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the military tribe.<BR>E.<BR>क्षत्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्त|क्षांत|क्षान्तः
क्षान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्ति|क्षांति|क्षांतिः|क्षान्तिः
क्षान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Patience, forbearance, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to be patient, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षान्तु|क्षांतु|क्षान्तुः
क्षान्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, Uṇādi affix तुन्; the vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Slender, slim, emaciated.<BR>2 Weak, infirm.<BR>E.<BR>क्षै to waste, affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामता
क्षामता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Slenderness.<BR>2 Thinness, emaciation.<BR>3 Debility.<BR>E.<BR>क्षाम, and तल् affix: also with त्व, क्षामत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामास्य|क्षामास्यं
क्षामास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Improper regimen, diet, &c. Contra-indicated in disease.<BR>E.<BR>क्षाम debilitating, and आस्य to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Glass.<BR>2 Juice, essence.<BR>3 Molasses, treacle.<BR>4 Salt.<BR>5 Ashes.<BR>6 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>7 Borax, borate of soda.<BR>8 Alkali, either soda or potash.<BR>9 Caustic alkali, one species of cautery.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A factitious or medicinal salt, commonly black salt: see कृष्णलवण.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर to drop, or distil, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारक|क्षारकः
क्षारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A blossom, a new blown flower.<BR>2 A cage or basket for birds or fish.<BR>3 A washerman.<BR>4 Juice, essence.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर to fall or drop, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारकर्म्मन्|क्षारकर्मन्
क्षारकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Applying caustic alkali (lapis infernalis) to proud flesh, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारण|क्षारणं
क्षारण<BR>nf. (-णं-णः)<BR>Accusing, calumniating.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Distilling.<BR>2 Converting to alkali or ashes.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार to drop, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारदला
क्षारदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारद्रु|क्षारद्रुः
क्षारद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, commonly Ghantaparali: see घण्टापाटलि; also क्षारवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारपत्र|क्षारपत्रः
क्षारपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षार juice, and पत्र a leaf; also क्षारपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारमध्य|क्षारमध्यः
क्षारमध्य<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>A shrub, (Achyranthes aspera); also अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार alkali, and मध्य middle; its alkaline ashes make it useful in washing clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारमृत्तिका
क्षारमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Saline soil, especially an impure sulphate of soda.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार, salt, and मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाररस|क्षाररसः
क्षाररस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A salt or alkaline flavour.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारवृक्ष|क्षारवृक्षः
क्षारवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Any tree yielding abundant potash, as the plantain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारषट्क|क्षारषट्कं
क्षारषट्क<BR>n. (-ट्कं)<BR>Six kinds of trees distinguished by their juice, as the Butea frondosa, Grislea tomentosa, Achyranthes aspera, Cowach, Ghaṇṭāpārali, Coraya.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार, and षट्क six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाराच्छ|क्षाराच्छं
क्षाराच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>Sea-salt.<BR>E.<BR>क्षार salt, and अच्छ clear, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारिका
क्षारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारित|क्षारितः
क्षारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Guilty.<BR>2 Calumniated, falsely accused, specially of adultery.<BR>3 Accused of crime.<BR>4 Distilled from saline matter, strained through alkaline ashes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षर to go or fall, in the causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालन|क्षालनं
क्षालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Washing, sprinkling, cleaning with water.<BR>E.<BR>क्षाल to wash, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनीय
क्षालनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be washed, to be cleaned with water.<BR>E.<BR>क्षल, and अनीयर् affix; also with तव्य and यत्, क्षालितव्य and क्षाल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालयत्
क्षालयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Washing, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>क्षल् to wash, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालित|क्षालितं
क्षालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cleared, cleaned, washed.<BR>E.<BR>क्षाल to cleanse, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षयति-ते)<BR>1 To wane or decrease.<BR>2 To diminish, to disappear, to waste, to perish.<BR>3 To rule or possess with unlimited power.<BR>r. 5th cl. (क्षिणोति)<BR>To hurt or injure, to wound or kill.<BR>r. 6th cl. (क्षियति)<BR>1 To dwell.<BR>2 To go or approach.<BR>(ष) क्षिष r. 9th cl. (क्षिणाति)<BR>To injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि<BR>f. (-क्षिः)<BR>Residence, abode.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>3 Waste, loss, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to decrease, &c. कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिण
क्षिण<BR>(उ) क्षिणु r. 8th cl. (क्षिणोति or क्षिणुते or क्षेणोति-णते)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित|क्षितः
क्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wasted, decayed.<BR>2 Poor, miserable.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, affix क्त; also क्षिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिति|क्षितिः
क्षिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 An abode, a dwelling, a house.<BR>3 Loss, destruction, wane.<BR>4 The period of the destruction of the universe.<BR>5 A perfume, commonly called Rocana.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, to dwell, &c. क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिकण|क्षितिकणः
क्षितिकण<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>Dust.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति the earth, and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिक्षम|क्षितिक्षमः
क्षितिक्षम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa khayar.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and क्षम able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिक्षित्
क्षितिक्षित्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and क्षि to dwell, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिखण्ड
क्षितिखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A clod or lump of earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and खण्ड earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिज|क्षितिजं|क्षितिजः
क्षितिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Earth-born, produced of or in the earth.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Mars.<BR>2 The demon NARAKA.<BR>3 An earth-worm.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिजन्तु|क्षितिजन्तुः
क्षितिजन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितितल
क्षितितल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The region below the earth.<BR>2 The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and तल beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिधर|क्षितिधरः
क्षितिधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति the earth, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिधारिन्
क्षितिधारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Carrying soil or earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and धारिन् bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिनाग|क्षितिनागः
क्षितिनाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and नाग a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिप|क्षितिपः
क्षितिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and प who protects; also क्षितिपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपति|क्षितिपतिः
क्षितिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपाल|क्षितिपालः
क्षितिपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिपीठ
क्षितिपीठ<BR>n. (-ठं)<BR>The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिप्रतिष्ठ
क्षितिप्रतिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Dwelling on the earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and प्रतिष्ठ established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिभृत्
क्षितिभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A prince, a king.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and भृत् who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिमण्डल|क्षितिमंडल
क्षितिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The earth, the globe.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिरुह|क्षितिरुहः
क्षितिरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति the earth, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिवर्द्धन
क्षितिवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A corpse.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति the earth, and वर्द्धन what increases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=263" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिसुत|क्षितिसुतः
क्षितिसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of the demon NARAKA, also of<BR>2 Mars.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीश|क्षितीशः
क्षितीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and ईश a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितीश्वर|क्षितीश्वरः
क्षितीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति, and ईश्वर a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्यदिति|क्षित्यदितिः
क्षित्यदिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिति the earth, and अदिति the mother of the gods; the terrestrial parent of divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्वन्
क्षित्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to go, Uṇādi affix, क्वनिप्, त inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिद
क्षिद<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षेदति)<BR>To utter an inarticulate sound, to moan as in grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप<BR>(औ) औक्षिप r. 4th cl. (क्षिप्यति) (ञ, आ) औक्षिपञ् r. 6th cl. (क्षिपति-ते)<BR>To throw or cast, to direct or send.<BR>With अधि prefixed,<BR>To abuse, to censure or reproach.<BR>With अव,<BR>To throw down.<BR>With आङ्.<BR>1 To attract.<BR>2 To ridicule.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To raise up, &c.<BR>With नि,<BR>To place, to deposit.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To throw far or violently.<BR>With वि,<BR>To scatter, to disperse.<BR>With वि and नि,<BR>To deliver over, to resign, to leave.<BR>With सम and आङ्,<BR>To remove, to send away.<BR>With सम्.<BR>1 To abridge, to compress or contract.<BR>2 To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Throwing, casting.<BR>2 Reviling.<BR>3 One who throws, &c.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 Sending, casting, throwing, &c.<BR>2 Night. see क्षपा.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपक|क्षिपकः
क्षिपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A warrior, a fighter.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप throwing or directing, (darts, &c.) क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण|क्षिपणं
क्षिपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sending, dismissing, throwing, casting, &c.<BR>2 Reviling, abusing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, &c. affix ल्युट्, the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणि|क्षिपणिः
क्षिपणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A missile weapon.<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>An oar.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw or cast, Uṇādi affix अणि, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणु|क्षिपणुः
क्षिपणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw or send, to waft, Uṇādi affix अनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण्यु|क्षिपण्युः
क्षिपण्यु<BR>mfn. (-ण्युः-ण्युः-ण्यु)<BR>1 Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>2 Diffusive, what may be sent or scattered.<BR>m. (-ण्युः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 Spring, the season of spring.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to send, &c. कन्युच् Uṇādi affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपत्
क्षिपत्<BR>mfn. (-पत्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>1 Throwing, casting.<BR>2 A busing, reproaching.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्नु|क्षिप्नुः
क्षिप्नु<BR>mfn. (-प्नुः-प्नुः-प्नु)<BR>Obstructive, throwing obstacles in the way; also क्षिप्णु.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to cast, &c. क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्त|क्षिप्तः
क्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Thrown, cast.<BR>2 Sent, despatched.<BR>3 Dismissed.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>Night; also क्षिपा and क्षपा.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्तदेह
क्षिप्तदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Prostrate, lying down.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्त, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्ति|क्षिप्तिः
क्षिप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Throwing.<BR>2 Sending, ordering.<BR>3 Solving a riddle, explaining or understanding a hidden meaning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यत्
क्षिप्यत्<BR>mfn. (-प्यन्-पन्ती-प्यत्)<BR>1 Throwing.<BR>2 Sending.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप 4th cl. to send, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्यमाण
क्षिप्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Tossing, throwing.<BR>2 Casting aside, throwing off.<BR>3 Sending, directing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्र|क्षिप्रं
क्षिप्र<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं)<BR>Quickly, speedily, quick, swift.<BR>adv. n. (-प्रं)<BR>Quickly.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्त to send or despatch, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्रपाकिन्
क्षिप्रपाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A kind of tree, (Hibiscus populneoides): see गर्द्धभाण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्र quick, and पाकिन् what ripens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिया
क्षिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Loss, waste, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, अङ्, and टाप् affixes, इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिव
क्षिव<BR>(उ) क्षिवु r. 4th cl. (क्षीव्यति)<BR>To eject from the mouth, to vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षी
क्षी<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षयति-ते)<BR>To hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीज
क्षीज<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षीजति)<BR>To sound inarticulately, to sigh or groan as in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीजन|क्षीजनं
क्षीजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The whistling of hollow reeds or bamboos.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीज to sound inarticulately, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Thin, emaciated, feeble.<BR>2 Thin, slender.<BR>3 Wasted, diminished, worn away, expended.<BR>4 Destroyed. lost.<BR>5 Injured, broken, torn.<BR>6 Subdued, suppressed.<BR>7 Poor, miserable.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणता
क्षीणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Slenderness, delicacy.<BR>2 Thinness, emaciation.<BR>3 Diminution, decay.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्षीणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणपाप
क्षीणपाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Purified, having suffered the consequences of sin.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणपुण्य
क्षीणपुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>1 Abandoned.<BR>2 Having enjoyed the fruits of virtue, and being doomed by another birth to labour for more.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and पुण्य virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणमध्य
क्षीणमध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Slender-waisted.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवत्
क्षीणवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wasted, decayed.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to waste, and क्ततवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवासिन्
क्षीणवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Inhabiting a destructible house.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A dove or pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and वासिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणविक्रान्त|क्षीणविक्रांत
क्षीणविक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Cowed, deprived of courage or prowess.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and विक्रान्त valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणवृत्ति
क्षीणवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Out of employ, out of bread, having no maintenance.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण lost, and वृत्तिं practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणशक्ति
क्षीणशक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Weak, feeble, impotent.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and शक्ति vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणाज्यकर्म्मन्|क्षीणाज्यकर्मन्
क्षीणाज्यकर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A Bauddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीणाष्टकर्म्मन्|क्षीणाष्टकर्मन्
क्षीणाष्टकर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A Jina, an inspired teacher according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीण, and अष्टकर्म्मन् eight natural acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब<BR>(ऋ) क्षीवृ r. 1st cl. (क्षीबते)<BR>To be intoxicated, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब<BR>mfn. (-बः-बा-बं)<BR>Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीब to be drunk, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीबता
क्षीबता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्षीवत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीयमाण
क्षीयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Perishing, wasting away.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to perish, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीर|क्षीरः
क्षीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A small shrub (Asclepia rosea); also दुग्धिका.<BR>2 A tree, a species of Mimosa, (M. kauki, Rox.) also क्षीरिका.<BR>3 Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR>4 Euphorbia; several kinds, particularly, E. hirta. E. thymifolia, and E. chamæsyce.<BR>E.<BR>घस to eat, ईरन् Uṇādi affix; the fem. nouns are derived from क्षीर milk, the plants yielding a milky juice or sap, upon expression or incision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकण्ठ|क्षीरकंठ|क्षीरकण्ठः
क्षीरकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>An infant, a young child.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and कण्ठ throat; also with कन् added क्षीरकण्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=264" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकन्दा
क्षीरकन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>A kind of potherb, black Bhuincaönra, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर water, and कन्द root: having a watery root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकाकोलिका
क्षीरकाकोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A drug, and one of the eight principal medicaments of the Hindus; it is a root from the Himālaya.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and काकोली a drug, कन् added; yielding, when fresh, a milky juice; also क्षीरकाकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकाकोली
क्षीरकाकोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरकीट|क्षीरकीटः
क्षीरकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An insect or animalcule generated by the fermentation of milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरज|क्षीरजं
क्षीरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Coagulated or curdled milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरद
क्षीरद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>What gives or yields milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरदल|क्षीरदलः
क्षीरदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and दल leaf; the leaves, &c. yielding, on expression or incision, a milky juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरनीर|क्षीरनीरं
क्षीरनीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Embracing, embrace.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, milk, and नीर water; mixing like milk and water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरप|क्षीरपः
क्षीरप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Drinking milk, who or what drinks it.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपर्णी
क्षीरपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>See क्षीरदल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपाण|क्षीरपाणं|क्षीरपाणः
क्षीरपाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Drinking milk; also क्षीरपान.<BR>m. plu. (-णाः)<BR>The name of a people, the milk-drinkers.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and पान drink; in the second sense, न is changed always to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपायिन्
क्षीरपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Drinking milk, sucking, &c.<BR>2 Drinking or imbibing water repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरपायिण्
क्षीरपायिण्<BR>m. plu. (-यिणः)<BR>The people called Usinaras, the milk-drinkers.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, पा to drink, णिनि affix, य inserted, and न final changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरमोचक
क्षीरमोचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरमोरट|क्षीरमोरटः
क्षीरमोरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, a kind of Murva: see मूर्व्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरयष्टिक
क्षीरयष्टिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A dish of liquorice and^1 milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and यष्टिक made of liquorice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरवल्ली
क्षीरवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The dark Bhuincaönra, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर water, and वल्ली pedicle: see क्षीरकन्दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविकृति|क्षीरविकृतिः
क्षीरविकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Inspissated milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and विकृति change of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविदारिका
क्षीरविदारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The dark Bhuincaönra; also क्षीरविदारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरविदारी
क्षीरविदारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The white or black Bhuincaönra, (Convolvulus paniculatus): see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर water, and विदारी the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरवृक्ष|क्षीरवृक्षः
क्षीरवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata); also उडुम्बर.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and वृक्ष a tree, the leaves and bark yielding a white milky juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरशर|क्षीरशरः
क्षीरशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Cream, the surface or skim of milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and शर what goes over or on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरशुक्ल|क्षीरशुक्लः
क्षीरशुक्ल<BR>m. (-क्लः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa, Rox.)<BR>f. (-क्ला)<BR>The pale Bhuincaönra: see भूमिकुष्माण्डक.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and शुक्त white; as milk, the fruit, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरसार|क्षीरसारः
क्षीरसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Butter.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरस्फटिक|क्षीरस्फटिकः
क्षीरस्फटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A precious stone, described as a milky crystal, (opal or cat's eye?)<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराद|क्षीरादः
क्षीराद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An infant at the breast.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and अद who feeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धि|क्षीराब्धिः
क्षीराब्धि<BR>m. (-ब्धिः)<BR>The sea of milk, one of the seven seas surrounding as many worlds.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and अब्धि the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धिज|क्षीराब्धिजं|क्षीराब्धिजः
क्षीराब्धिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The moon.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Sea salt.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीरब्धि the sea of milk, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराब्धितनया
क्षीराब्धितनया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीराब्धि the sea of milk, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरान्नाद
क्षीरान्नाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An infant both fed and suckled.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर, and अन्न food, अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराविका
क्षीराविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of Asclepias: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरावी
क्षीरावी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A sort of Asclepias, (A. rosea, Rox.); also दुग्धिका.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk or milky juice, अव to contain, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीराह्व|क्षीराह्वः
क्षीराह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>The Saral, a kind of pine.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and आह्व what is named; or it may mean that the tree is also named simply क्षीर, that which yields a milky juice or sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिका
क्षीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A tree bearing an edible fruit, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.)<BR>2 A potherb, Bhuincaönra, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिणी
क्षीरिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A milch-cow.<BR>2 A tree bearing an edible fruit, (Mimusops kauki.)<BR>3 A medicinal kind of the moon plant or acid Asclepias.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and इनि affix, alluding to its juice, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिन्
क्षीरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Milky, yielding milk.<BR>2 Having milk.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A sort of Mimusops: see क्षीरिका.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरेयी
क्षीरेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>An oblation of milk, rice, and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोद|क्षीरोदः
क्षीरोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, and उद water; it also implies the sea in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोदतनया
क्षीरोदतनया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीरोद the sea of milk, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरोदनन्दन|क्षीरोदनन्दनः
क्षीरोदनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीरोद the ocean in general, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव|क्षीवः
क्षीव<BR>(उ) क्षीवु r. 1st cl. (क्षीवति)<BR>1 To spit or sputter, to eject from the mouth.<BR>2 To be drunk: see क्षिव, also क्षीब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव|क्षीवः
क्षीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीव, and क्त affix; also क्षीब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीवता
क्षीवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Drunkenness, intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, क्षीवत्वं; also क्षीवता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षु|क्षुः
क्षु<BR>(टु) टुक्षु r. 2d cl. (क्षौति)<BR>To sneeze, to make any such sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण|क्षुणः
क्षुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The soap berry plant, (Sapindus saponaria.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to bruise, डुण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Bruised, pounded.<BR>2 Exercised, practised, skilful.<BR>3 One versed in sacred science, but described as unable to explain or teach it.<BR>4 Defeated, overcome.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to bruise, &c. affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्
क्षुत्<BR>f. (-क्षुत्)<BR>1 Sneezing; also क्षुत.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष to sneeze, affix क्विप्, तुक् is added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत|क्षुतं|क्षुतः
क्षुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sneezed, sneezing.<BR>mf. (-तः-ता)<BR>1 Sneezing.<BR>2 Cough.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sneeze, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुतवत्
क्षुतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sneezing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sneeze, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुताभिजनन|क्षुताभिजननः
क्षुताभिजनन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुत sneezing, and अभिजनन what produces; also क्षुधाभिजनन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=265" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्करी
क्षुत्करी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुत् sneezing, करी making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्तृष्णोपपीडित
क्षुत्तृष्णोपपीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungry and thirsty.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध् with तृष्णा thirst, and उपपीडित distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्पिपासित
क्षुत्पिपासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungry and thirsty.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध्, and पिपासा thirst, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्प्रतीकार
क्षुत्प्रतीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Allaying hunger, eating.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध्, and प्रतीकार counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद|क्षुदः
क्षुद<BR>(ञ, इर, औ) औ क्षुदिर r. 7th cl. (क्षुणत्ति क्षुत्ते)<BR>To pound, to bruise, to reduce to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्र|क्षुद्रः
क्षुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Small, little.<BR>2 Mean, low.<BR>3 Mean, niggardly, avaricious.<BR>4 Cruel.<BR>5 Poor, indigent.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 A woman maimed or crippled, wanting a limb, &c.<BR>2 A dancing girl.<BR>2 A whore, a harlot.<BR>4 A fly.<BR>5 A bee or wasp.<BR>6 A gnat, &c.<BR>7 A prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारी.<BR>8 The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>9 Sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to bruise or pound, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रकम्बु|क्षुद्रकंबु|क्षुद्रकम्बुः
क्षुद्रकम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>A small shell.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and कम्बु a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रघण्टिका|क्षुद्रघंटिका
क्षुद्रघण्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tinkling ornament, a girdle of small bells, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, घण्टा a clock or bell, affix कन्, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रचूड|क्षुद्रचूडः
क्षुद्रचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A kind of small bird.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and चूडा a crest, small crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रजन्तु|क्षुद्रजंतु|क्षुद्रजन्तुः
क्षुद्रजन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 Any small animal.<BR>2 A kind of worm, (Julus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रजीर|क्षुद्रजीरः
क्षुद्रजीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Small cummin.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and जीर cummin seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रता
क्षुद्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Smallness, minuteness.<BR>2 Inferiority, insignificance, meanness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to क्षुद्र; also with त्व, क्षुद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रदंशिका
क्षुद्रदंशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small gadfly.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and दंशिका a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रदंशी
क्षुद्रदंशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A small gadfly.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and दंशी a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रनासिक|क्षुद्रनासिकः
क्षुद्रनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having a little nose.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रपत्रा
क्षुद्रपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>Wood-sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and पत्र a leaf, small-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रफलक|क्षुद्रफलकः
क्षुद्रफलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Celtis orientalis): see जीवन.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and फल fruit, कन् added, bearing a small fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रफला
क्षुद्रफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Ardisia solanacea.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रबुद्धि|क्षुद्रबुद्धिः
क्षुद्रबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Simple, silly, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and वुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्ररोग|क्षुद्ररोगः
क्षुद्ररोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A minor disease, one of little importance.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रवंशा
क्षुद्रवंशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A plant, (Dioscorea): see वराहक्रात्त्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रशङ्ख|क्षुद्रशंख|क्षुद्रशङ्खः
क्षुद्रशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>A small shell.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रशीर्ष|क्षुद्रशीर्षः
क्षुद्रशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A tree, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and शीर्ष the head, having a small head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रसहा
क्षुद्रसहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, commonly Mugāi: see मुद्गपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रहिङ्गुलिका
क्षुद्रहिङ्गुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.) a small species.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, and हिङ्गुली the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रहिङ्गुली
क्षुद्रहिङ्गुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसङ्घात|क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसंघात|क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसंघातः
क्षुद्राण्डमत्स्यसङ्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Small fry.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, अण्ड an egg, मत्स्य a fish, and सङ्घात a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राम्लपनस|क्षुद्राम्लपनसः
क्षुद्राम्लपनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha): see लकुच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्राम्ला
क्षुद्राम्ला<BR>f. (-म्ला)<BR>Wood-sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and अम्ल sour; a small and acid plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध
क्षुध<BR>(ऋ औ) औक्षुधृ r. 4th cl. (क्षुध्यति)<BR>To be hungry, to hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध्
क्षुध्<BR>f. (-क्षुत् or -क्षुद्)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध to be hungry, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधा
क्षुधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध to be hungry, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाकर
क्षुधाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Causing hunger, improving the appetite.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाध्वंस
क्षुधाध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Allaying hunger.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा, and ध्वंस destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधापीडित
क्षुधापीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungry, starving.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा, and पीडित pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाभिजनन|क्षुधाभिजननः
क्षुधाभिजनन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Black mustard.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा hunger, and अभिजनन causing, promoting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधार्त्त|क्षुधार्त|क्षुधार्त्तः
क्षुधार्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Hungry, hungered.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधाशान्ति
क्षुधाशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Satisfaction, satiety, allaying hunger.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुधा, and शान्ति appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधित|क्षुधितः
क्षुधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungered, hungry.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध to be hungry, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधुन|क्षुधुनः
क्षुधुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A savage, a barbarian.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुध to be hungry, Uṇādi affix उनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुप|क्षुपः
क्षुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A small tree, one with short branches and roots, a bush, a shrub.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sound, aff. प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुब्ध|क्षुब्धः
क्षुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्ध)<BR>1 Agitated, tossed, stirred.<BR>2 Agitated mentally, anxious, disturbed.<BR>m. (-ब्धः)<BR>The churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुभ to stir, to agitate, affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ|क्षुभः
क्षुभ<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षोभति)<BR>1 To be confused or agitated.<BR>2 To stir or disturb.<BR>r. 4th cl. and 9th cl. (क्षुभ्यति and क्षुभ्नाति)<BR>To shake, to tremble, to be unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभित|क्षुभितः
क्षुभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Frightened, alarmed, afraid.<BR>2 Agitated, tossed, set in motion.<BR>3 Agitated mentally, disturbed, anxious.<BR>4 Angry, enraged.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुभ to shake, to be agitated, to stir, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुमा
क्षुमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Linseed, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>2 A sort of flax, Bengal San.<BR>3 The indigo plant.<BR>4 A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to sound, affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर|क्षुरः
क्षुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (क्षुरति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To scratch, to make lines or furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर|क्षुरः
क्षुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A razor.<BR>2 A plant, (Barleria longifolia.)<BR>3 Also Tribulus lanuginosus: see गोक्षुर.<BR>4 A horse's hoof; also खुर.<BR>5 The hoof of a cow, &c.<BR>6 The foot of a bedstead.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर to scratch or cut, Uṇādi affix रन्, and the final consonant rejected; also खुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरक|क्षुरकः
क्षुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Tila.<BR>2 Barleria longifolia.<BR>3 Tribulus lanuginosus.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर to scratch, &c. क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरप्र|क्षुरप्रः
क्षुरप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>1 A kind of arrow, one with a horse shoe head.<BR>2 A sort of hoe or weeding spade.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर a hoof, and प्रथ to go, ड affix; also खुरप्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरभाण्ड|क्षुरभांड|क्षुरभाण्डं
क्षुरभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A razor case.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरमर्द्दिन्|क्षुरमर्दिन्
क्षुरमर्द्दिन्<BR>m. (-र्द्दी)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर a razor, and मृद to destroy, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिणी
क्षुरिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A kind of yam: see वराहक्रान्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिन्
क्षुरिन्<BR>mf. (-री-रिणी)<BR>A male or female barber.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर a razor, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्ल|क्षुल्लः
क्षुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Little, small.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to pound, affix क्विप्, क्षुद powder, dust, ल from ला to get, to be, affix ड; also खुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लक|क्षुल्लकः
क्षुल्लक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Little, small.<BR>2 Hard.<BR>3 Poor, indigent.<BR>4 Low, vile.<BR>5 Wicked, malicious, abandoned.<BR>6 Young. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">Page267</a>] youngest.<BR>7 Pained, distressed.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small shell.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुल्ल as above, and कन् added; also खुल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=266" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लतात|क्षुल्लतातः
क्षुल्लतात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लतातक|क्षुल्लतातकः
क्षुल्लतातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A paternal uncle.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुल्ल youngest, and तात a father, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुवत्
क्षुवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sneezing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेड
क्षेड<BR>r. 10th cl. (क्षेडयति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेड
क्षेड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Disease in the ear.<BR>2 Poison.<BR>3 Sound: see क्ष्वेड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेडित
क्षेडित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Roar of a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्र|क्षेत्रं
क्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A field.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 A wife.<BR>4 A pure or sacred spot, a place of pilgrimage, as Benares, &c.<BR>5 Plane figure, geometry.<BR>6 A diagram.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to dwell, &c. affix ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रकर|क्षेत्रकरः
क्षेत्रकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Making a field, cultivating it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रज|क्षेत्रजः
क्षेत्रज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Produced in a field, (as corn, &c.)<BR>2 Born of the body, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A son, the offspring of the wife by a kinsman or person duly appointed to procreate issue to the husband.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र wife, and ज born, born of the wife only; this is one of the twelve kinds of issue acknowledged by the old Hindu law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रज्ञ|क्षेत्रज्ञः
क्षेत्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Clever, dexterous, skilful.<BR>2 A husbandman, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 The soul, the emanation of divinity residing in the body.<BR>2 A libertine, a whore-monger.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र a field, the body, &c. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रपति|क्षेत्रपतिः
क्षेत्रपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A landowner, a farmer, the master of a field.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रभूमि|क्षेत्रभूमिः
क्षेत्रभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Cultivated land.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रविद्
क्षेत्रविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>1 A sage, one who possesses spiritual knowledge.<BR>2 A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रराशि|क्षेत्रराशिः
क्षेत्रराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>Figurate quantity.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and राशि number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रसीमा
क्षेत्रसीमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The boundaries of a meadow or field, or holy place.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and सीमा limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्राजीव|क्षेत्राजीवः
क्षेत्राजीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>A cultivator, a peasant.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र a field, and जीव who lives, with आङ् prefixed; who gets a livelihood by the labours of the field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रामलकी
क्षेत्रामलकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, commonly Bhūmyāmalakī, (Flacourtia cataphracta, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिक|क्षेत्रिकः
क्षेत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having a field, relating to a field, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A farmer, a cultivator.<BR>2 A husband.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिन्
क्षेत्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>Owning or having a field, cultivating it, &c.<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A cultivator, a husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र a field, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिय|क्षेत्रियं|क्षेत्रियः
क्षेत्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Meadow grass, herbage, pasturage.<BR>3 Physicking. operating.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An adulterer.<BR>2 A medicament, what is fit to be administered in medicine.<BR>3 An incurable disease.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र a field, the body, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेद
क्षेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sorrowing, moaning.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to moan, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप|क्षेपः
क्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Sending, dismissing.<BR>2 Throwing, casting.<BR>3 Pride, haughtiness.<BR>4 Delay, dilatoriness.<BR>5 Disrespect, contempt.<BR>6 Passing away time.<BR>7 Abuse, reviling.<BR>8 A clump of flowers, &c.<BR>9 (In arithmetic, &c.) Additive quantity, addendum.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपक|क्षेपकः
क्षेपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Who or what throws or sends.<BR>2 Abusing, disrespectful.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपण|क्षेपणं
क्षेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sending, directing.<BR>2 Throwing, casting.<BR>3 Passing away time.<BR>4 Abusing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणि|क्षेपणिः
क्षेपणि<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>1 An oar.<BR>2 A net, a fishing net.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to cast or throw, अण and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिमन्
क्षेपिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Great velocity.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्र quick, and इमनिच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिष्ठ|क्षेपिष्ठः
क्षेपिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very quick, quickest.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्र quick, and इष्ठन् superlative affix, र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपीयस्
क्षेपीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very quick.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप्र, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्तृ
क्षेप्तृ<BR>mfn. (-प्ता-प्ती-प्तृ)<BR>Who or what throws, sends, orders, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षिप to throw, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम|क्षेमं|क्षेमः
क्षेम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Happy, well, prosperous, right, &c.<BR>mn. (-भः-मं)<BR>1 Happiness, well being.<BR>2 Preserving, protecting, keeping what is acquired.<BR>3 Final emancipation or eternal happiness.<BR>4 The proper term of civil address to a Vaiśya, as क्षेममस्ति, क्षेमं भवतु, Is it well, or may it be well, &c.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>क्षि to remove, and मन् Uṇādi affix; what removes or destroys sorrow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमक|क्षेमकः
क्षेमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A perfume, commonly Cor.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to क्षेम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमकर|क्षेमकरः
क्षेमकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Propitious, conferring happiness or good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम, and कृ to make, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमकार|क्षेमकारः
क्षेमकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness or good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम happiness, and कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमङ्कर|क्षेमंकर|क्षेमङ्करः
क्षेमङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Propitious, &c.: see the preceding.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The Brahmani kite or Coromandel eagle, which is considered as a bird of good omen, (Falco ponticerianus.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम, and कृ to make, with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमवत्|क्षेमवन्त्
क्षेमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Happy, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमाफला
क्षेमाफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Opposite leaved fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम auspicious, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम्य|क्षेम्यं|क्षेम्यः
क्षेम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Luckly, prosperous, thriving.<BR>2 Healthy, salubrious.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेम, and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेव
क्षेव<BR>(उ) क्षेवु r. 1st cl. (क्षेवति)<BR>To spit, to eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षै
क्षै<BR>r. 1st cl. (क्षायति)<BR>To wane, to waste or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्र|क्षैत्रं
क्षैत्र<BR>n. (त्रं)<BR>A multitude of fields, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्र a field, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञ|क्षैत्रज्ञं
क्षैत्रज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञ्यं)<BR>Spirituality, the nature of the soul.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्रज्ञ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञ्य|क्षैत्रज्ञ्यं
क्षैत्रज्ञ्य<BR>n. (-ज्ञ्यां)<BR>Spirituality, the nature of the soul, the knowledge of it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>क्षेत्रज्ञ, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैरेयी
क्षैरेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>Milk and rice, or any preparation of milk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षीर milk, affix ढञ्, fem. affix ङीप्; some copies read this word क्षीरेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोड|क्षोडः
क्षोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The post to which an elephant is bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोजन
क्षोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sound of the flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोणि|क्षोणिः
क्षोणि<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष to sound, अणि affix, fem. affix optionally ङीप्; also क्षौणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद|क्षोदः
क्षोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Powder, pulverized substance.<BR>2 A piece, a small piece or particle.<BR>3 The stone or slab on which any thing is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">Page268</a>] ground or powdered, a mortar, &c.<BR>3 Dust.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to bruise^1 or pound, affix घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=267" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदारज
क्षोदारज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Ground, pulverized.<BR>E.<BR>क्षोद, and रज for रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदित|क्षोदितं
क्षोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pounded, ground, comminuted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Powder, dust, substance pulverized or ground.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद to bruise or pound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिमन्
क्षोदिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Minuteness, exceeding smallness or inferiority.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, &c. Affix इमनिच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिष्ठ|क्षोदिष्ठः
क्षोदिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Finely pounded or levigated, very small or minute.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र small, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative, र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदीयस्
क्षोदीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very fine or small.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र, and इयसुन् affix of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ|क्षोभः
क्षोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Agitation, emotion.<BR>2 Shaking, trembling, tossing.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुभ to be agitated, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोम|क्षोमं|क्षोमः
क्षोम<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>A room on the top of a house: see क्षौम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Wove silk.<BR>E.<BR>क्षु to make a sound, Uṇādi affix मन्; also क्षौम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणि|क्षौणिः
क्षौणि<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षोणि the earth, and अण् pleonastic, with इन् or ङीप् fem. terminations added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणीप्राचीर|क्षौणीप्राचीरः
क्षौणीप्राचीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>क्षौणी the earth, and प्राचीर an enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्र|क्षौद्रं|क्षौद्रः
क्षौद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 Honey.<BR>2 Water.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्रा a fly, &c. affix अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रक्य|क्षौद्रक्यं
क्षौद्रक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-की-क्यं)<BR>Small, minute.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुद्र Small, ञ्यट् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौम|क्षौमं|क्षौमः
क्षौम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Linen, made of linen, covered with it, &c.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>Linen or flax, (Linum usitatissimum.)<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>1 An airy room on the top of a house.<BR>2 An apartment on the top of a hall.<BR>3 The back of an edifice.<BR>4 A fortified place in front of a building.<BR>5 A building of a particular form.<BR>6 Wove silk:<BR>7 Linen cloth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षोम q. v. अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौमक|क्षौमकः
क्षौमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cor, a species of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौर|क्षौरं
क्षौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Shaving the head.<BR>2 Shaving in general.<BR>(-री)<BR>A razor.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर a razor, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरिक|क्षौरिकः
क्षौरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>क्षुर a razor, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णु
क्ष्णु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (क्ष्णोति or with सम्) prefixed (संक्ष्णुते)<BR>To whet, to sharpen.<BR>(क्ष्णोते)<BR>To take away, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णुत|क्ष्णुतः
क्ष्णुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Whetted, sharpened.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्णु to whet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मा
क्ष्मा<BR>f. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्षम to bear, Uṇādi affix अच्, and the penultimate dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मातल|क्ष्मातलं
क्ष्मातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्मा, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माभुज्
क्ष्माभुज्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्मा, and भुक् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माभृत्
क्ष्माभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 A king, a prince.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्मा the earth, and भृत् who nourishes, from भृ, affix क्विप्, तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माय
क्ष्माय<BR>(ई) क्ष्मायी r. 1st cl. (क्ष्मायते)<BR>To shake, to make tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायित|क्ष्मायितः
क्ष्मायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्माय, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मायितृ
क्ष्मायितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्माय, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मील
क्ष्मील<BR>r. 1st cl. (-क्ष्मीलति)<BR>To wink or twinkle, to close as the eye lids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विण्ण|क्ष्विण्णः
क्ष्विण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Sounded.<BR>2 Soft, unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्विद to sound, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विद
क्ष्विद<BR>(ञि, आ) ञिक्ष्विदा r. 1st cl. (क्ष्वेदति)<BR>To sound inarticulately.<BR>r. 4th cl. (क्षिद्यति)<BR>1 To be unctuous, to be soft or bland.<BR>2 To liberate, to free: some consider these roots as more properly read क्ष्विड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेड|क्ष्वेडं|क्ष्वेडः
क्ष्वेड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>1 Crooked, bent.<BR>2 Wicked, depraved.<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Venom, poison.<BR>2 Sound, noise.<BR>3 Tingling or buzzing in the ear, from hardening of the wax, &c.<BR>4 Ghosha, with yellow flowers; see घोष.<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>1 The flower of the Ghosha plant.<BR>2 The fruit of a red kind of swallow wort.<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 A war whoop, a battle cry.<BR>2 A bamboo rod or stake.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्विद to sound inarticulately, to be soft or bland, &c. affix घ, and ड substituted for द, or क्ष्वेल to shake, &c. अच् affix, and स्व changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडित|क्ष्वेडितं|क्ष्वेडितः
क्ष्वेडित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A battle cry, a war whoop.<BR>E.<BR>क्ष्विद to sound inarticulately, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेल
क्ष्वेल<BR>(ऋ) क्ष्वेऌ r. 1st cl. (क्ष्वेलति)<BR>1 To shake, to tremble.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख<BR>The second consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, being the aspirate of the preceding; it is written in the Roman character Kh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख|खं|खः
ख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Heaven.<BR>2 Sky or ether.<BR>3 An organ of sense.<BR>4 Knowledge.<BR>5 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>6 Vacuity.<BR>7 A dot, a cypher.<BR>8 A city, a field.<BR>9 Action.<BR>10 Auspiciousness.<BR>11 Talc.<BR>12 The tenth constellation from any given one, or the sun's entrance into it.<BR>13 Brahma the supreme spirit.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A name of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, to penetrate, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खकुन्तल|खकुंतल|खकुन्तलः
खकुन्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>ख ether, कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खक्ख
खक्ख<BR>r. 1st cl. (खक्खति)<BR>To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also कख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खक्खट|खक्खटः
खक्खट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Hard, solid: see कक्खट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खखोल्क|खखोल्कः
खखोल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and खोल्क a meteor, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खग|खगः
खग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A planet.<BR>5 A deity.<BR>6 Air, wind.<BR>7 A grasshopper.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, &c. and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगपति|खगपतिः
खगपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird, and पति lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगम|खगमः
खगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>ख and गम what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगवक्त्र|खगवक्त्रः
खगवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A tree, commonly Lakucha, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird, and वक्त्र face, bird-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगवती
खगवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगशत्रु|खगशत्रुः
खगशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Chakuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगस्थान
खगस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The hollow of a tree.<BR>2 A bird's nest.<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगान्तक|खगांतक|खगान्तकः
खगान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hawk, a falcon.<BR>E.<BR>खग, and अन्तक destroyer^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगासन|खगासनः
खगासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The eastern mountain over which the sun rises.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>खग a bird or the sun, and आसन seat or place of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेन्द्र|खगेंद्र|खगेन्द्रः
खगेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>खग, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेन्द्रध्वज|खगेन्द्रध्वजः
खगेन्द्रध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>खगेन्द्र, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगेश्वर|खगेश्वरः
खगेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>GARUḌA the bird of VIṢṆU; also खगेश.<BR>E.<BR>खग, and ईश्वर king of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोड
खगोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=268" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोल|खगोलः
खगोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The vault or circle of the heavens, the planisphere.<BR>2 The same represented artificially, the armillary sphere.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and गोल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खगोलविद्या
खगोलविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Astronomy.<BR>E.<BR>खगोल, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खङ्कर|खंकर|खंकरः|खङ्करः
खङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A curl, a lock of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खच
खच<BR>r. 1st cl. (खचति) also r. 9th cl. (खन्नाति)<BR>1 To be past birth.<BR>2 To cause prosperity.<BR>3 To purify.<BR>r. 10th cl. (खचयति)<BR>To fasten, to bind, to set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचमस|खचमसः
खचमस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, चम to eat, and अस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचर|खचरः
खचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Moving in the sky, flying in the air.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An aerial spirit.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>4 A demon.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>6 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and चर who goes, from चर to go, affix ट; see also खेचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खचित|खचितं
खचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mixed, blended, inlaid.<BR>2 Joined, combined.<BR>E.<BR>खच to fasten, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज|खजः
खज<BR>r. 1st cl. (खजति)<BR>To churn or agitate.<BR>(इ,) खजि (खञ्जति)<BR>To limp, to halt, to walk lame or ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज|खजः
खज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A ladle, a spoon.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 Churning, stirring.<BR>2 Killing, destroying.<BR>3 The palm with the fingers extended.<BR>E.<BR>खज to agitate, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजक|खजकः
खजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The churning stick.<BR>f. (-जिका)<BR>A ladle or spoon.<BR>E.<BR>खज to churn or agitate, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजप|खजपं
खजप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>खज to stir or agitate, Uṇādi affix अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजल|खजलं
खजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Frost, hoar-frost.<BR>2 Dew, rain.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजाक|खजाकः
खजाक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A spoon, a ladle.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>खज to agitate, and आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खजित्
खजित्<BR>m. (जित्)<BR>A Buddha, one of seven teachers or saints of the Buddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and जित् who subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खज्योतिस्
खज्योतिस्<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A fire-fly.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्ज|खंज|खञ्जः
खञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>Lame, crippled, limping.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>A species of metre, a stanza of two lines, one of thirty-two, the other of thirty feet.<BR>E.<BR>खजि to limp or go lame, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जक|खंजक|खञ्जकः
खञ्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Lame, limping.<BR>E.<BR>खजि to limp, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जखेट|खंजखेट|खञ्जखेटः
खञ्जखेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A wag-tail.<BR>E.<BR>खञ्ज lame, and खेट who moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जखेल|खंजखेल|खञ्जखेलः
खञ्जखेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wag-tail.<BR>E.<BR>खञ्ज lame, and खेल who moves, from खेल to move, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जन|खंजन|खञ्जनं|खंजनः|खञ्जनः
खञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A small bird, the wag-tail, (Motacilla alba.)<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A small kind of wag-tail.<BR>2 Mustard.<BR>n. (-र्नं)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>खजि to go lamely, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनरत|खंजनरत|खञ्जनरतं
खञ्जनरत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The cohabitation of saints.<BR>E.<BR>खञ्जन a wag-tail, and रत cohabitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनाकृति|खञ्जनाकृतिः
खञ्जनाकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A sort of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जनिका|खंजनिका
खञ्जनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खञ्जरीट|खंजरीट|खंजरीटः|खञ्जरीटः
खञ्जरीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A wag-tail.<BR>E.<BR>खञ्ज lame, ऋ to go, कीटन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट|खटः
खट<BR>r. 1st cl. (खटति)<BR>To desire, to wish, to seek or inquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट|खटः
खट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Grass.<BR>2 Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humor.<BR>3 A blind well.<BR>4 An axe, a hatchet.<BR>5 A closed or doubled fist, as for striking.<BR>6 A plough.<BR>7 A fragrant kind of grass: see कत्तृण.<BR>E.<BR>खट to seek, to wish, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटक|खटकः
खटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A go-between, a man whose business it is to negociate marriages: see घटक.<BR>2 The doubled fist of wrestlers or boxers.<BR>E.<BR>खट to seek, to wish, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटकामुख|खटकामुखं|खटकामुखः
खटकामुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A man in the attitude of shooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटखादक|खटखादकः
खटखादक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An eater.<BR>2 A glass vessel.<BR>3 A jackal.<BR>4 An animal.<BR>5 A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिक|खटिकः
खटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The fist, the hand closed.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Chalk.<BR>2 The external opening of the ear.<BR>3 A fragrant grass: (Andropogon muricatus.)<BR>E.<BR>खट to seek or wish, वुन् affix, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटिनी
खटिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>खट to seek, इनि affix, fem. affix ङीष्; also कठिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खटी
खटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>खट to seek, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्ट
खट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (खट्टयति)<BR>To cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टन|खट्टनः
खट्टन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dwarfish, short of stature.<BR>E.<BR>खट्ट to cover or hide, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टा
खट्टा<BR>f. (-ट्टा)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>E.<BR>खट्ट to screen, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टाश|खट्टाशः
खट्टाश<BR>mf. (-शः-शी)<BR>The civet or zebet cat, (Viverra zibetha.)<BR>E.<BR>खट्टा the grass, and अश who eats; also खट्टास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टास|खट्टासः
खट्टास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The civet: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टि|खट्टिः
खट्टि<BR>m. (-ट्टिः)<BR>A bier, the bed on which the corpse is carried to the pile; also खट्टी.<BR>E.<BR>खट्ट to screen, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टिक|खट्टिकः
खट्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A hunter, a fowler, one who lives by killing and selling game.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A small bedstead, a cot.<BR>2 A bier or bed on which the corpse is carried.<BR>E.<BR>खट्ट to screen, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्टेरक|खट्टेरकः
खट्टेरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Dwarf, dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वा
खट्वा<BR>f. (-ट्वा)<BR>1 A bedstead, a cot, a couch.<BR>2 A hammock, a swing.<BR>E.<BR>खट्ट to hide, Uṇādi affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्ग|खट्वांग|खट्वाङ्गं|खट्वाङ्गः
खट्वाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A king of the solar line.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Part of a bed.<BR>2 A club or staff with a skull at the top of it, considered as a weapon of ŚIVA, and carried by penitents and Yogis.<BR>3 Wood from a funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>खट्वा a cot, and अङ्क body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्गभृत्
खट्वाङ्गभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA. खट्वाङ्ग one of his weapons, भृत् who maintains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वाङ्गिन्|खट्वांगिन्
खट्वाङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>खट्वाङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्वारूढ|खट्वारूढः
खट्वारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Low, vile, abandoned, iniquitous.<BR>2 Erring, going wrong.<BR>3 Stupid, silly.<BR>4 Laid or lying on a bed.<BR>E.<BR>खट्वा a bed, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खट्विका
खट्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small bedstead.<BR>E.<BR>खट्वा a bedstead, and कन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड|खडं|खडः
खड<BR>r. 10th cl. (खाडयति) also (इ,) खडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (खण्डति खण्डयति) and (इ ङ) खडिङ् r. 1st cl. (खण्डते)<BR>To divide, to tear, to break off a part or piece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड|खडं|खडः
खड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Breaking, dividing.<BR>2 Buttermilk boiled with acid vegetables and spices.<BR>3 A small grass.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>खड to break, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडक्किका
खडक्किका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A private or back door, a small or venetian door or window.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडिका
खडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>खड to break, affix वुन् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खडु|खडुः
खडु<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>A bier.<BR>E.<BR>खड to break, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्ग|खड्गं|खड्गः
खड्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>2 A rhinoceros horn.<BR>3 A sword, a scimitar.<BR>4 A large sacrificial knife.<BR>5 One of the Buddhas or Bauddha saints.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>खड to tear or rend, Uṇādi affix गन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=269" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गकोष|खड्गकोषः
खड्गकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A creeping plant, (Scirpus maximus.)<BR>2 A scabbard, a sheathe.<BR>E.<BR>खङ्ग a sword, and कोष a sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गचर्म्मधर|खड्गचर्मधर
खड्गचर्म्मधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A soldier armed with a sword and shield.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and चर्म्म a shield, धर who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गट|खड्गटः
खड्गट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A large kind of Kās, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग the rhinoceros, and अट who goes; these animals being usually found amongst high grass or reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गधर|खड्गधरः
खड्गधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A swordsman.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गधेनु|खड्गधेनुः
खड्गधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>1 A small knife.<BR>2 A female rhinoceros.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a sword, &c. धेनु a cow, used here as a diminutive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपत्र|खड्गपत्रः
खड्गपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The name of a creeper, (Scirpus maximus.)<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The blade of a sword.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a sword, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपाणि
खड्गपाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Holding a sword.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपात्र
खड्गपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel of buffalo's horn.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपिधान|खड्गपिधानं
खड्गपिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A scabbard, a sheathe.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a sword, and पिधान a sheathe; also with कन् added, खड्गपिधानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गपुत्त्रिका
खड्गपुत्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A knife, a small sword.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and पुत्त्रिका infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गप्रहार|खड्गप्रहारः
खड्गप्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sword cut.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and प्रहार a stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गमांस
खड्गमांस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Buffalo-beef.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गलेखा
खड्गलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A row of sabres.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गराट
खड्गराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A shield.<BR>2 One who observes a peculiar religious obligation, rubbing the feet backwards and forwards on the edge of a sword made red hot, this is a penance peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a sword, रट to speak, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाघात|खड्गाघातः
खड्गाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sword cut.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाधार|खड्गाधारः
खड्गाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sheathe, a scabbard.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and आधार what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गाभिहत
खड्गाभिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut or struck with a sword.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and अभिहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गामिष
खड्गामिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Buffalo's flesh.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग, and आमिष flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिक|खड्गिकः
खड्गिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The cream or froth of buffalo's milk.<BR>2 A vender of flesh meat.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a sword, &c. affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिन्
खड्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ड्गी-ड्गिनी-ड्गि)<BR>Armed with a sword.<BR>m. (-ड्गी)<BR>1 A rhinoceros.<BR>2 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a horn, &c. affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गिमार|खड्गिमारः
खड्गिमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of creeper: see खड्गकोष.<BR>E.<BR>खड्गि a rhinoceros, and मार what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खड्गीक|खड्गीकं
खड्गीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sickle, a scythe.<BR>E.<BR>खड्ग a scymitar, and ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड|खंड|खण्डं|खण्डः
खण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 A piece, a part, a fragment, a portion.<BR>2 A chapter, a section.<BR>3 A term in an equation.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A flaw in a jewel.<BR>2 Treacle or molasses partially dried or candied.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 A sort of sugar cane.<BR>2 Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>खडि to break, and घञ् affix, or खन to tear, affix ड, and न changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डक|खंडक|खण्डकः
खण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Pared or clipped finger nails.<BR>2 A part, a piece.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड to tear, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकर्ण|खण्डकर्णः
खण्डकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Sweet potatoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकथा|खंडकथा
खण्डकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>A tale or story divided into sections.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a section, and कथा a story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकालु
खण्डकालु<BR>n. (-लु)<BR>An esculent root, sweet potatoe: also खण्डकालुक. n. (-कं)<BR>E.<BR>खण्डक a portion, and आलु any esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डकाव्य|खंडकाव्य
खण्डकाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A poem interspersed with prose.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and काव्य a poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डज|खंडज|खण्डजः
खण्डज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Treacle, molasses.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and ज what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डधारा|खंडधारा
खण्डधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Shears, scissors.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a part, and धृ to have or hold, in the causal form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डन|खंडन|खण्डनं
खण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breaking, dividing, cutting, reducing to pieces.<BR>2 Destroying, annihilating.<BR>3 Refuting, (in argument.)<BR>4 Rebellion, opposition.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड to break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डनरत
खण्डनरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Destructive, skilful in cutting or destroying.<BR>E.<BR>खण्डन, and रत engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डनीय|खंडनीय
खण्डनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Brittle, fragile.<BR>2 Refutable.<BR>4 Destructible, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खडि, and अनीयर् affix; also खण्ड्य, and खण्डितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपत्र
खण्डपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रं)<BR>A bundle of various leaves.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपरशु|खंडपरशु|खण्डपरशुः
खण्डपरशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a part, and परशु a hatchet; cutting his foes to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपर्शु|खंडपर्शु|खण्डपर्शुः
खण्डपर्शु<BR>m. (-र्शुः)<BR>1 A name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 Rāhu, the personified ascending node.<BR>5 A spreader of unguents, fragrant powders, &c.<BR>5 A drug, commonly Candāmalaki.<BR>6 An elephant with a broken tusk.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a part, and पर्शु an axe; whose axe or arms cut every thing to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डपाल|खंडपाल|खण्डपालः
खण्डपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A confectioner, a seller of sweetmeats.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड molasses, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डप्रलय|खंडप्रलय|खण्डप्रलयः
खण्डप्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Partial destruction of the universe, the destruction of the division of the terrestrial world.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डमण्डल|खंडमंडल
खण्डमण्डल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Gibbous, not full or round.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A segment of a circle, part of a circle or an incomplete sphere.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डमोदक|खंडमोदक|खण्डमोदकः
खण्डमोदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Granulated sugar.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and मोदक a sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डलवण|खंडलवण|खण्डलवणं
खण्डलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डशस्|खंडशस्
खण्डशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Piece-meal, in or by pieces.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डसर|खण्डसरः
खण्डसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Granulated sugar.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड, and सर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डाभ्र|खंडाभ्र|खण्डाभ्रं
खण्डाभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>1 Scattered clouds.<BR>2 A bite, the impression of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a part, and अभ्र a cloud, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डाली|खंडाली
खण्डाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A measure for oil.<BR>2 A pond.<BR>3 A woman whose husband has been guilty of infidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिक|खंडिकः|खण्डिकः
खण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Pease.<BR>2 The armpit.<BR>E.<BR>खडि to break, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डित|खंडित|खण्डितं
खण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut, torn, broken in pieces.<BR>2 Destroyed.<BR>3 Broken as allegiance, disobeyed against, rebelled.<BR>4 Refuted, controverted.<BR>5 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>6 Disappointed.<BR>7 Betrayed, abandoned, (as a lover.)<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman whose husband or lover has been guilty of infidelity.<BR>E.<BR>खडि to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डितव्य
खण्डितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be broken, what may or ought to be broken, confuted, destroyed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खडि, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डितविग्रह|खंडितविग्रह
खण्डितविग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Maimed, mutilated.<BR>E.<BR>खण्डित, and विग्रह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिताशंस
खण्डिताशंस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Disappointed, foiled, frustrated.<BR>E.<BR>खण्डित, and आशंसा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डिन्|खंडिन्
खण्डिन्<BR>mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि)<BR>1 In pieces or parts, divided, comminuted, &c.<BR>2 Consisting of pieces or parts.<BR>m. (-ण्ड)<BR>A wild [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">Page271</a>] kind of kidney bean: see वनमद्ग.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a portion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=270" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्डीर|खण्डीरः
खण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of kidney bean: see पीतमुद्ग.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड a part, ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खण्ड्य|खंड्य
खण्ड्य<BR>mfn. (ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं)<BR>What may or ought to be broken, &c. see खण्डितव्य.<BR>E.<BR>खडि, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खतमाल|खतमालः
खतमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Smoke.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, तमाल a tree with dark blossoms; the etherial Tamāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद
खद<BR>r. 1st cl. (खदति)<BR>1 To be steady or firm.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR>3 To eat.<BR>r. 10th cl. (खदयति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिका
खदिका<BR>m. (-का)<BR>Fried or parched grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिर|खदिरः
खदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tree, the resin of which is used in medicine, Khayar, Terra japonica or catechu, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>खद to hurt, Uṇādi affix इरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिरपत्री
खदिरपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The sensitive plant.<BR>E.<BR>खदिर, and पत्र a leaf, affix ङीप्; also with कन् added खदिरपत्रिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदिरोपम|खदिरोपमं
खदिरोपम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The Babul, (Acacia Arabica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदूरक
खदूरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A dwarf.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and दूर afar, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खदूरवासिनी
खदूरवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>One of the female deities or Śaktis of the Buddhas.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, दूर ill, and वासिनी who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद्योत|खद्योतः
खद्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A fire-fly.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and द्योत what is luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खद्योतन|खद्योतनः
खद्योतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and द्युत to shine, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खधूप|खधूपः
खधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A rocket, a fire work.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खन
खन<BR>(उ,) खनु r. 1st cl. (खनति-ते)<BR>1 To dig or delve.<BR>2 To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनक|खनकः
खनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Tearing, dividing.<BR>2 Digging, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A rat.<BR>2 A housebreaker.<BR>3 A miner.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनत्
खनत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>Digging.<BR>E.<BR>खन, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनि|खनिः
खनि<BR>f. (-निः or -नी)<BR>A mine, especially of precious stones; when used in composition with आकर, more commonly a mine of the precious metals.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, इन् affix, and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनितृ
खनितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what digs or delves, a digger, a ditcher, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खनित्र|खनित्रं
खनित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A spade or hoe.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, इत्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खपुर|खपुरं|खपुरः
खपुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The betel tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>3 Garlic.<BR>4 Flatulence.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A water jar.<BR>2 A city in the sky, the city of HARIŚCANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>ख the heavens, &c. पृ to nourish, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खभ्रान्ति|खभ्रांति|खभ्रान्तिः
खभ्रान्ति<BR>m. (न्तिः)<BR>A kite.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, भ्रम to roam, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमणि|खमणिः
खमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमीलन|खमीलनं
खमीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Lassitude, weariness, sleepiness.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, and मीलन twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूर्त्ति|खमूर्ति|खमूर्तिः
खमूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A celestial appearance or person.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूर्त्तिमत्|खमूर्तिमत्|खमूर्तिमन्त्
खमूर्त्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Having a divine or celestial person or form.<BR>E.<BR>खमूर्त्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खमूलि|खमूलिः
खमूलि<BR>f. (-लिः or -ली or -लिका)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes).<BR>E.<BR>ख ether, मूल a root, affixes इन् or ङीष्; also खमूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खम्ब
खम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (खम्बति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर|खरं|खरः
खर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Hot.<BR>2 Sharp, pungent.<BR>3 Sharp, sharp-edged, cutting.<BR>4 Cruel, harsh.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Heat.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An ass.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa, the brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>3 A Daitya or demon in general.<BR>4 A sort of prickly nightshade.<BR>5 A crow.<BR>6 A heron.<BR>7 An osprey.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>E.<BR>ख an organ of sense, and रा to get or give, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरकुटि
खरकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः or टी)<BR>A barber's shop.<BR>E.<BR>खर heat, and कुटि a dwelling; also written खरकुट्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरकोण|खरकोणः
खरकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>खर heat, कुण to sound, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरक्वाण|खरक्वाणः
खरक्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The francoline partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगन्धनिभा
खरगन्धनिभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगृह|खरगृहं
खरगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>An ass's stable.<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरगेह|खरगेहं
खरगेह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A stable for asses.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and गेह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरग्रह|खरग्रहः
खरग्रह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A stable for asses.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and ग्रह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरघातन|खरघातनः
खरघातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, commonly Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, and घातन mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरच्छद|खरच्छदः
खरच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A kind of reed or grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>2 Also another kind, commonly Okera.<BR>E.<BR>खर warm, sharp, छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरणस्
खरणस्<BR>mfn. (-णाः-णाः-णः)<BR>Sharp-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>खर sharp, नस् from नासिका a nose; also with a final vowel खरणस (-सः-सा-सं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदण्ड|खरदंड|खरदण्डं
खरदण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A lotus, (Nymphaea lotus.)<BR>E.<BR>खर sharp, and दण्ड stick or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदला
खरदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Opposite leaved fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>खर hot, दल leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरदूषण|खरदूषणः
खरदूषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, and दूषण hurting; by its narcotic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरध्वंसिन्
खरध्वंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>खर an imp or goblin so called, and ध्वंसिन् the destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरनाद|खरनादः
खरनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The braying of an ass.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and नाद noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरनादिन्
खरनादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Braying as an ass.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of perfume: see रेणुका.<BR>E.<BR>खरनाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपत्र|खरपत्रः
खरपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A red sort of Tulasi or basil.<BR>2 The teak tree, (Tectona grandis.)<BR>E.<BR>खर hot, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपत्रक|खरपत्रकः
खरपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant: see तिलक.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to खरपत्र hot leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपात्र|खरपात्रं
खरपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An iron pot or vessel.<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, and पात्र a vessel; fit for such an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपादाद्य
खरपादाद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>The elephant or wood apple, (Feronia elephantium): see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपाल|खरपालः
खरपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wooden vessel.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and पाल what cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरपुष्प|खरपुष्पः
खरपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, commonly Marüa: see मरुवक.<BR>f. (-ष्पा or ष्पिका)<BR>A kind of Tulasi, (Ocymum gratissimum); also वर्वर.<BR>E.<BR>खर sharp, hot, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरप्रिय|खरप्रियः
खरप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>खर hot, and प्रिय fond, dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरमञ्जरी
खरमञ्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera): see अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>खर sharp, pungent, and मञ्जरी a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरयान
खरयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A vehicle drawn by asses.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरलोमन्
खरलोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>One of the chiefs of the Nāga or serpent race inhabiting hell.<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, and लोमन् hair of the body; having the skin of an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=271" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरवल्लिका
खरवल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Gorakṣa Cākuliya, (Hedysarum lagopodiodes.)<BR>E.<BR>खर hot, sharp, वल्लिका a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरशब्द|खरशब्दः
खरशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>1 An osprey.<BR>2 The braying of an ass.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरशाल
खरशाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Born or produced in an ass's stall.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An ass's stable or stall.<BR>E.<BR>खर, and शाला a hall; in the first sense the final is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरसोल्ल
खरसोल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>An iron vessel; also read खरसोनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरांशु|खरांशुः
खरांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>खर hot, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरागरी
खरागरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus); also देवताड.<BR>E.<BR>खर venom, गृ to take, with आङ् prefixed, अच् and ङीष् affixes; antivenomous, an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरालक
खरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An iron arrow; also खरालिक. m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खराश्वा
खराश्वा<BR>f. (-श्वा)<BR>A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>खर an ass, अश to be eaten, and व and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरिका
खरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Musk in powder.<BR>E.<BR>खर, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरिन्धय|खरिंधय
खरिन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Drinking ass's milk.<BR>E.<BR>खरी, and धे to drink, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खरु|खरुः
खरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः or -रूः-रु)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Desirous of improper or prohibited things.<BR>3 A fool, foolish, idiotic^1.<BR>4 Harsh, cruel.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 A tooth.<BR>4 Pride.<BR>5 Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR>6 White, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, &c. Uṇādi affix कु, and र substituted for the final.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब|खर्ब्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब<BR>r. 10th cl. (खर्ब्वति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज|खर्ज्ज
खर्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्जति)<BR>1 To worship, to treat with respect or courtesy.<BR>2 To pain or make uneasy.<BR>3 To cleanse or make clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्जिका|खर्ज्जिका
खर्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A relish, a provocative to drinking.<BR>E.<BR>खर्ज to pain, and वुन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जुर|खर्जुर|खर्जुरं|खर्ज्जुरं
खर्ज्जुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Silver: see खर्ज्जूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जू|खर्जू
खर्ज्जू<BR>f. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>1 Cutaneous eruption, itch, scab, &c.<BR>2 A worm, an insect.<BR>E.<BR>खर्जि to give pain, Uṇādi affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जूर|खर्जूर|खर्जूरः|खर्ज्जूरं|खर्ज्जूरः
खर्ज्जूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 The fruit of the date.<BR>3 Yellow orpiment.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The date tree, (Phoenix sylvestris.)<BR>2 A scorpion.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The wild date tree.<BR>E.<BR>खर्ज to give pain, &c. Uṇādi affix ऊर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ज्जूररस|खर्जूररस|खर्जूररसः
खर्ज्जूररस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The juice or extract of the wild date, Tāri, used to leaven bread, and as an intoxicating liquor, when in a state of spontaneous fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>खर्ज्जूर, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्द|खर्द्द
खर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्दति)<BR>To bite, to sting, to sting venomously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्प्पर|खर्पर|खर्परः
खर्प्पर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A kind of collyrium or application to the eyes: see कर्पर.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 A beggar's bowl or dish.<BR>4 The half of a skull.<BR>5 An umbrella or parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्द्ध
खर्द्ध<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्घति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्पराल
खर्पराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant: see कन्दराल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्प्परीतूत्थ
खर्प्परीतूत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>A sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब|खर्ब्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्बंति)<BR>To go, to move to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्ब|खर्ब|खर्ब्बः
खर्ब्ब<BR>mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्बं)<BR>A dwarf, short, low, of little size or stature.<BR>m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>One of KUVERA'S nine Nidhis or treasures.<BR>n. (-र्ब्बं)<BR>A large number, ten million-millions.<BR>E.<BR>खर्ब्ब or खर्व्व to be small, to go, to move, affix अच्; also खर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्ब्बशाख|खर्बशाख|खर्ब्बशाखः
खर्ब्बशाख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Small, short, dwarfish.<BR>E.<BR>खर्ब्ब short, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्म्म|खर्म|खर्म्मः
खर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Virility, manliness.<BR>2 Wovesilk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्व्व|खर्व|खर्वः|खर्व्वः
खर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्व्वति)<BR>To be proud, or haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्व्व|खर्व|खर्वः|खर्व्वः
खर्व्व<BR>mfn. (र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>A dwarf, &c.: see खर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खर्व्वट|खर्वट|खर्वटं|खर्वटः|खर्व्वटः
खर्व्वट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 The capital of a district of four hundred villages, a market or country town.<BR>2 A village at the foot of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>खर्व्व being proud, and अट what goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल|खलं|खलः
खल<BR>r. 1st cl. (खर्लति)<BR>1 To gather.<BR>2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल|खलं|खलः
खल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Low, vile, base.<BR>2 Low, inferior.<BR>3 Cruel, mischievous, mischief-making.<BR>4 Bad, wicked.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Earth, mould or soil.<BR>2 Place, site.<BR>3 Sediment, deposit of oil, &c.<BR>4 A granary, a threshing floor.<BR>5 A mill.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A tree with black blossoms: see तमाल.<BR>3 The Datura plant.<BR>E.<BR>खल to gather, (misfortune, &c.) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलता
खलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Wickedness, villainy.<BR>2 Filthiness.<BR>E.<BR>खल, and तल् affix; also with त्व affix खलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलति|खलतिः
खलति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः or -ती-ति)<BR>Bald, baldheaded.<BR>E.<BR>स्खल to fall, Uṇādi affix अतच, इ inserted, and स rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलपू
खलपू<BR>mf. (-पूः)<BR>A sweeper, a cleaner, Mehter or Ferash.<BR>E.<BR>खल place, and पू who cleans, from पूञ् to cleanse or purify, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलप्रीति
खलप्रीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The friendship or favour of wicked or low persons.<BR>E.<BR>खल, and प्रीति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलमूर्त्ति|खलमूर्ति|खलमूर्त्तिः
खलमूर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>खल place, and मूर्त्ति form; taking the form of the place it lies in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलसंसर्ग|खलसंसर्गः
खलसंसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Associating with bad company.<BR>E.<BR>खल, संसर्ग associating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलाधारा
खलाधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>खल the sediment of oil, and आधार having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलि|खलिः
खलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Sediment of oil or oil-cake.<BR>E.<BR>खल to gather, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिन्
खलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having sediment, &c.<BR>f. (नी)<BR>1 A multitude of threshing floors.<BR>2 A plant, (Anthericum tuberosum.)<BR>E.<BR>खल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिन|खलिनं|खलिनः
खलिन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>The bit of a bridle: see खलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलिश|खलिशः
खलिश<BR>mf. (-शः-शा)<BR>A kind of fish, (Trichopodus colisa, HAM.) also खलेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलीकार|खलीकारः
खलीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mischief, evil.<BR>2 Leaving or reducing to sediment.<BR>E.<BR>खल mischievous, and कार who makes; च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलीन|खलीनं|खलीनः
खलीन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>The bit of a bridle.<BR>E.<BR>ख the mouth, and लीन what is fixed; also the vowel being made short खलिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलु
खलु<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of prohibition.<BR>2 An expletive.<BR>3 An expression of endearment or conciliation.<BR>4 An expression indicating inquiry.<BR>5 An expression of asseveration or ascertainment, (certainly, indeed.)<BR>6 Only, merely.<BR>E.<BR>खल to gather, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलुज्
खलुज्<BR>m. (-लुक्)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>ख the sky, लुक् dropped, lost, from लुज to efface, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलुरेष|खलुरेषः
खलुरेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of wild animal; also खलुरेषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलूरिका
खलूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A parade, a place for military exercise.<BR>E.<BR>खडि to break, ऊरच् affix, ड changed to ल, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेधानी
खलेधानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The post of a threshing floor, round which the oxen pass who tread out the grain; also खलेवाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेबाली
खलेबाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A post: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>खल a threshing floor in the seventh case, and बाली what is firm, a post, &c. from बल to be strong, अण् and ङीष affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=272" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेश|खलेशः
खलेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A kind of fish, (commonly Trichopodus colisa, HAM.) see खलिश.<BR>E.<BR>खले in dirt, and श from शी to sleep; burrowing in the mud of the banks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलेशय|खलेशयः
खलेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Khaliśa fish: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, शी, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खलोक्ति|खलोक्तिः
खलोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Abuse, low or wicked language.<BR>E.<BR>खल, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्या
खल्या<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Fit for oil cake, for a threshing floor, &c.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A multitude of threshing floors.<BR>E.<BR>खल a threshing floor, affix क्यप् यत् or य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्ल|खल्लः
खल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 A kind of cloth or clothes, leather garments.<BR>2 A canal, a cut, a creek, a trench, a deep hole.<BR>3 The Cātaka, a kind of cuckoo.<BR>4 Leather.<BR>5 A leather water bag.<BR>6 A mill, a stone or vessel for grinding drugs, &c.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Shooting pain in the extremities.<BR>E.<BR>खल collecting, &c. and ल what gets; also खल्लक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लिका
खल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A frying pan.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लिट|खल्लिटः
खल्लिट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Bald, morbidly troubled with falling of the hair; also खल्लीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्लीट|खल्लीटः
खल्लीट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Becoming morbidly bald: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्वट
खल्वट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A severe cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खल्विका
खल्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A frying pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खव
खव<BR>r. 9th cl. (खौनाति)<BR>1 To be past birth.<BR>2 To cause or procure prosperity.<BR>3 To produce purity, to purify.<BR>4 To produce or manifest wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवल्ली
खवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A parasitic plant.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and वल्ली a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवारि
खवारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Rain water, dew, vapour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and वारि water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खवाष्प
खवाष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Snow, hoar frost, dew.<BR>E.<BR>ख sky, and वाष्प vapour or tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खश|खशः
खश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A mountainous country to the north of India.<BR>2 A native of that country, considered as a degraded Kṣatriya.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशय
खशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Resting or dwelling in the air.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशरीर
खशरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A celestial or immortal body.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशरीरिन्
खशरीरिन्<BR>m. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Of a heavenly body.<BR>E.<BR>खशरीर, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खशेट|खशेटः
खशेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The Khaliśa, a kind of fish: see खलेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खश्वास|खश्वासः
खश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>ख the atmosphere, and श्वास breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खष
खष<BR>r. 1st cl. (खषति)<BR>To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खष्प|खष्पं|खष्पः
खष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Anger, passion.<BR>2 Violence, oppression.<BR>E.<BR>खन to hurt, to dig, प Uṇādi affix, न changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस|खसः
खस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Itch, scab.<BR>2 A man of a country or tribe considered to be a degraded Kṣatriya: the Khasas inhabit the mountains surrounding Kashmir.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The mother of the imps or goblins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसगन्ध
खसगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A plant, commonly Kṣīrakañcuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसम|खसमः
खसम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and सम equal, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसम्भव|खसंभव
खसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced in the sky, aerial, ethereal.<BR>E.<BR>ख. and सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसर्पण|खसर्पणः
खसर्पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>One of the Buddhas or Buddha saints.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Gliding through the air.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and सर्पण who goes to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खसात्मज|खसात्मजः
खसात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>खसा the mother of these beings, आत्मज a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्तनी
खस्तनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>ख ether, स्तन a breast, affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्खस|खस्खसः
खस्खस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The poppy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्खसरस|खस्खसरसः
खस्खसरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Poppy juice, opium.<BR>E.<BR>खस्खस, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खस्फटिक
खस्फटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Crystal, the sun gem.<BR>2 The moon gem: see सूर्य्यकान्त, and चन्द्रकान्त.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खहर
खहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>(In arithmetic.) A fraction having a cypher for its denominator.<BR>E.<BR>ख a cypher, हर divisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाजिक|खाजिकः
खाजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fried or parched grain.<BR>E.<BR>खज to go, &c. affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाट|खाटः
खाट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>1 A bier, a cot or bedstead on which dead bodies are conveyed to the pile.<BR>E.<BR>खट to screen, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाटि|खाटिः
खाटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>1 Caprice, whim.<BR>2 A scar.<BR>3 A bier.<BR>E.<BR>खट to screen, &c. इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाटिका
खाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bier: see खाट; also खाटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डव|खांडव|खाण्डवं|खांडवः|खाण्डवः
खाण्डव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A wood, sacred to INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाण्डिक|खांडिक|खांडिकः|खाण्डिकः
खाण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A confectioner, a seller of sweetmeats.<BR>E.<BR>खण्ड molasses or coarse sugar, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खात|खातं
खात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dug, excavated.<BR>2 Torn, rent.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A square or oblong pond.<BR>2 Any excavation.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, affix क्त, and the pen. lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खातक|खातकं|खातकः
खातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A delver, a digger.<BR>2 A debtor; more correctly खादक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A moat, a ditch.<BR>E.<BR>खात a pond, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खातभू
खातभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A moat, a ditch.<BR>E.<BR>खात a pond, भू earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खात्र|खात्रं
खात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A square or large pond.<BR>2 A spade, a hoe.<BR>3 A wood.<BR>4 A thread.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाद|खादः
खाद<BR>(ऋ) खादृ r. 1st cl. (खादति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादक|खादकः
खादक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A borrower, a user, (in law,) literally, an eater.<BR>2 A feeder, one who eats or feeds.<BR>E.<BR>खाद to eat, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादन|खादनं|खादनः
खादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>खाद to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादनीय
खादनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Edible, to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>खाद and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादित|खादितं
खादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>खाद to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादितवत्
खादितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Eating, feeding.<BR>E.<BR>खाद and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादितव्य
खादितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be eaten, what may be or must be eaten, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खाद, and तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादिर|खादिरः
खादिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Derived from the Khayar tree.<BR>2 Made of its wood.<BR>E.<BR>खदिर, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादिरसार|खादिरसारः
खादिरसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Catechu, the resinous extract of the Mimosa catechu.<BR>E.<BR>खादिर, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खादुक|खादुकः
खादुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mischievous, injurious, malignant.<BR>E.<BR>खाद to eat, उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाद्य|खाद्यं
खाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Edible, to be eaten, what is to be or may be eaten.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>खाद to eat, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानि|खानिः
खानि<BR>mf. (-निः-नी)<BR>A mine.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, इञ् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=273" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानिक|खानिकं|खानिकः
खानिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An opening or hole in a wall, a breach.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानिल|खानिलः
खानिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A housebreaker.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, इलच् affix, deriv. irr.; this is sometimes read खानिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खानोदक|खानोदकः
खानोदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>खान rending, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खापगा
खापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A name of GAṄGĀ or the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, and अपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खार|खारः
खार<BR>mf. (-रः-रिः or -री)<BR>A Khāri, a measure of grain containing sixteen Droṇas, or about three bushels: it is also reckoned at three or four Droṇas; also at five Gonis, which is considered equal to 512 Sers.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A scar.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारिम्पच|खारिंपच|खारिम्पचः
खारिम्पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Cooking a Khāri, by measure (a vessel, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>खारी as above, पच to cook, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारीक|खारीकं
खारीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A field, &c. equal to or sown with a Khāri of grain.<BR>E.<BR>खारी the measure, and इकन् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खारीवाप|खारीवापः
खारीवाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>A field sown with a Khāri of grain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खारी, and वाप sowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खालित्य
खालित्य<BR>n. (-त्य)<BR>Morbid baldness.<BR>E.<BR>खलति, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाशि
खाशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>Name of a country to the east of Bengal: the Cossya hills; also खाशिक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खाश्मरी
खाश्मरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant: see कश्मरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिखि|खिखिः
खिखि<BR>f. (-खिः)<BR>A fox; also in some copies, किखि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिङ्खिर|खिंखिर|खिंखिरः|खिङ्खिरः
खिङ्खिर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>A fox.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of ŚIVA'S weapons.<BR>2 A kind of perfume, commonly Hāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिट
खिट<BR>r. 1st cl. (खेटति)<BR>1 To terrify, to alarm or surprise.<BR>2 To be terrified, to fear or dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद
खिद<BR>r. 4th and 7th cls. (खिद्यते and खिंते)<BR>To be distrest, to suffer pain or misery.<BR>(औ, प) औखिदप् r. 6th cl. (खिन्दति)<BR>To afflict or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिदिर|खिदिरः
खिदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>2 An ascetic, a penitent.<BR>3 A pauper.<BR>E.<BR>खिद to suffer pain, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्यमान|खिद्यमानः
खिद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Suffering pain or distress.<BR>E.<BR>खिद, with शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिद्र|खिद्रः
खिद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 Disease, sickness.<BR>2 A pauper, a poor man.<BR>E.<BR>खिद, to be in pain, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिन्न|खिन्नः
खिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Distrest, suffering pain or uneasiness.<BR>2 Wearied, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>खिद to be in pain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खिल|खिलं|खिलः
खिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Waste or unploughed land.<BR>2 Empty. vacant.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A compendium, a compilation, especially of hymns and prayers.<BR>E.<BR>ख vacuity, &c. ल what gets or possesses, affix ड, and इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खु
खु<BR>(ङ) खुङ् r. 1st cl. (खुवते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुङ्गाह|खुंगाह|खुंगाहः|खुङ्गाहः
खुङ्गाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A black horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुज
खुज<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) खुजु (खुजति)<BR>To steal or rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुञ्जाक
खुञ्जाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of grass: see देवताडक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुड
खुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (खुडति)<BR>To cover.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cl. (खोडति खोडयति) also (इ,) खुडि r. 1st and 10th cl. (खुण्डति, खुण्डयति)<BR>To break in pieces, to sunder, to divide, tear, rend, &c.<BR>(इङ्) खुडिङ् r. 1st cl. (खुण्डते)<BR>To limp, to be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर|खुरः
खुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (खुरति)<BR>To cut, to scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर|खुरः
खुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hoof, a horse's hoof, &c.<BR>2 A razor.<BR>3 The foot of a bedstead; also क्षुर.<BR>4 A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi, apparently a dried shell fish, and of the shape of a hoof.<BR>E.<BR>खुर to cut, रन् Uṇādi affix, the radical र is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरक|खुरकः
खुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Tilā.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरक्षेप|खुरक्षेपः
खुरक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A kick, kicking.<BR>E.<BR>खुर, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरणस्
खुरणस्<BR>mfn. (-णाः-णाः-णः)<BR>Flat-nosed, having a nose like a horse's hoof.<BR>E.<BR>खुर a hoof, and नस् deriv. of नासिका a nose; also with a final vowel खुरणस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरपदवी
खुरपदवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A horse's foot marks.<BR>E.<BR>खुर, and पदवी vestige.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरप्र|खुरप्रः
खुरप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>An arrow with a semicircular head: see क्षुरप्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरली
खुरली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Military exercise, practising archery, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खुर to cut, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराक|खुराकः
खुराक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An animal in general.<BR>E.<BR>खुर to cut, and आक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराघात|खुराघातः
खुराघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A kick.<BR>E.<BR>खुर, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुराभिघात
खुराभिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A kick.<BR>2 Kicking, pawing, (as a horse.)<BR>E.<BR>खुर, and अभिघात, striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरालक|खुरालकः
खुरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>E.<BR>खुर a razor, and अल what is able, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुरालिक|खुरालिकः
खुरालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A barber's case.<BR>2 An iron arrow.<BR>3 A pillow.<BR>E.<BR>खुर a razor, &c. अल to be equal to, affix ठक्; some read this खरालक, but to all appearance erroneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुर्द|खुर्द्द
खुर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (खुर्दते or खूर्दते)<BR>To play, to sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्ल|खुल्लं
खुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Small, little, low, mean, &c.<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>A kind of perfume: see खुर.<BR>E.<BR>खुद to divide, &c. and ल from ला to get, the radical द becomes ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लक|खुल्लकः
खुल्लक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Low, vile.<BR>2 Little, small.<BR>2 Poor, indigent.<BR>4 Cruel, harsh.<BR>4 Wicked, mischievous, malignant: see क्षुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लतात|खुल्लतातः
खुल्लतात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A father's younger brother; also क्षुल्लतात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खुल्लम|खुल्लमः
खुल्लम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खूर्द|खूर्द्द
खूर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (खूर्दते)<BR>To play: see खुर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेखीरक|खेखीरकः
खेखीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hollow or sounding reed, or cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेगमन|खेगमनः
खेगमन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>खे in the air, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेचर|खेचरः
खेचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Aerial, moving in the air.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A Vidyādhara or kind of demigod.<BR>3 Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>खे in heaven, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेट|खेटं|खेटः
खेट<BR>r. 1st cl. (खेटति)<BR>To alarm.<BR>r. 10th cl. (खेटयति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेट|खेटं|खेटः
खेट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Vile, bad, low.<BR>2 Armed, having a weapon or weapons.<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>Hunting, the chase; also आखेट.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A shield.<BR>2 A village, the residence of peasants or farmers.<BR>3 A small town, half the Pura or town.<BR>4 The club of BALARĀMA.<BR>5 Phlegm, the phlegmatic or watery humour.<BR>6 The ascending node or RĀHU.<BR>7 A horse.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Grass.<BR>E.<BR>खिट to terrify, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटक|खेटकः
खेटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A village, the residence of agricultural peasants.<BR>2 A shield.<BR>3 The club of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>खिट to terrify, &c. अच् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटिताल|खेटितालः
खेटिताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A minstrel, a family bard or piper, whose business it is to awaken the Laird, with music and singing.<BR>E.<BR>खेटि derived from खिट to disturb, and ताल tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेटिन्
खेटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>A lecher, a libertine.<BR>E.<BR>खेट sport, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेड
खेड<BR>r. 10th cl. (खेडयति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेडिताल
खेडिताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A minstrel: see खेटिताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=274" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेद|खेदः
खेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Sorrow, affliction, distress.<BR>2 Lassitude, depression.<BR>3 Pain.<BR>4 Poverty.<BR>E.<BR>खिद to be distrest, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदन|खेदनं
खेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदान्वित
खेदान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distressed, pained.<BR>E.<BR>खेद, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदित
खेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Annoyed, harassed.<BR>2 Afflicted, distressed, pained.<BR>E.<BR>खिद to give pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेदिनी
खेदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia): see असनपर्णी.<BR>2 A creeper, a creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>खिद to be distrest, affixes णिनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेय|खेयं
खेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be dug.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A ditch, a moat.<BR>E.<BR>खत to dig, affix क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेल
खेल<BR>(ऋ) खेऌ r. 1st cl. (खेलति)<BR>To shake, to tremble, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेलन|खेलनं
खेलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Play, sport, pastime.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A piece or man at drafts, chess, &c.<BR>E.<BR>खेल to shake or move, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेला
खेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Play, pastime, sport.<BR>E.<BR>खेल to shake, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेलि|खेलिः
खेलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 A song, a hymn.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A bird.<BR>5 Any animal.<BR>E.<BR>खेल to shake, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेव
खेव<BR>(ऋ) खेवृ r. 1st cl. (खेवते)<BR>To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खेसर|खेसरः
खेसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mule.<BR>E.<BR>खे in air, सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खै
खै<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्वायति)<BR>1 To be firm or steady.<BR>2 To kill, to injure or hurt.<BR>3 To dig.<BR>4 To mourn, to sorrow for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोङ्काह|खोङ्काहः
खोङ्काह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A white and brown horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोट
खोट<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) खोदृ (खोटति)<BR>To be lame or lamed.<BR>r. 10th cl. (खोटयति)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोटि|खोटिः
खोटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>A cunning or scheming woman; also read खोरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोटी
खोटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>The gum olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोड|खोडः
खोड<BR>(ऋ) खोडृ r. 1st cl. (खोडति)<BR>To be or become lame.<BR>r. 10th cl. (खोडयति)<BR>To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोड|खोडः
खोड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Lame, limping.<BR>E.<BR>खोड to be lame, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोडकशीर्ष
खोडकशीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The arched roof of a house, the coping of a wall, &c. also खोडकशीर्षकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोर|खोरः
खोर<BR>(ऋ) खोरृ r. 1st cl. (खोरति)<BR>To be lame, to be prevented from moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोर|खोरः
खोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Lame.<BR>E.<BR>खोर to be lame, affix अच्; also खोड, and खोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल|खोलः
खोल<BR>(ऋ) खोऌ r. 1st cl. (खोलति)<BR>To be lame, to limp, to be prevented from moving. खोड, खोर, &c. are conceived by some authorities to be mere variations in the form of this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल|खोलः
खोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Lame.<BR>E.<BR>खोल to be lame, affix अच्; also खोर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोलक|खोलकः
खोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A helmet, armour for the head.<BR>2 A pot, a saucepan.<BR>3 An ant hill.<BR>4 The shell of the betel nut.<BR>E.<BR>खुड to cover, affix ण्वुल्, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोलि|खोलिः
खोलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल्क|खोल्कः
खोल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>1 A meteor.<BR>2 A planet.<BR>E.<BR>ख, and उल्का torch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

खोल्मुक|खोल्मुकः
खोल्मुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>ख heaven, उल्मुक^1 a hot coal.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: Print unclear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्या
ख्या<BR>r. 2nd cl. (ख्याति)<BR>1 To relate, to recount, to say or tell.<BR>2 To celebrate, to make known.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>To shine or be glorious.<BR>With आ,<BR>To be famous.<BR>With वि,<BR>To celebrate.<BR>With सु,<BR>To be approved.<BR>With कु,<BR>To be infamous.<BR>With प्रति and आ,<BR>To reject, to refuse.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To count, to reckon.<BR>With सं and आ,<BR>To denominate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यात|ख्यातः
ख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Famous, celebrated, notorious.<BR>E.<BR>ख्या to relate, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यातगर्हण|ख्यातगर्हणः
ख्यातगर्हण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Notoriously vile, infamous.<BR>E.<BR>ख्यात famous, गर्हण abuse; also ख्यातगर्हित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यातगर्हित|ख्यातगर्हितः
ख्यातगर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Infamous: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्याति|ख्यातिः
ख्याति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>ख्या to tell, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यापक
ख्यापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Declaring, making known, one who tells or declares.<BR>2 One who confesses.<BR>E.<BR>ख्या to say, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ख्यापन|ख्यापनं
ख्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Declaring, divulging.<BR>2 Saying, avowing.<BR>3 Confessing.<BR>4 Explaining.<BR>E.<BR>ख्या causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग|गं|गः
ग<BR>The third consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, the letter G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग|गं|गः
ग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Who or what goes, used chiefly in composition: as अधगः a traveller, who goes a road; अपगा what goes down, (a river, &c.)<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A name of the deity GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A Gandharba or celestial musician.<BR>f. (गा)<BR>A song.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Song, singing.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go or गै to sing, affix ड, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगण|गगणं
गगण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sky, atmosphere, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, Uṇādi affix, युच्, and the radical final changed to ग; the word and its derivatives are also sometimes read गगन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणध्वज
गगणध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>गगण the sky, and ध्वज a standard or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणाध्वग
गगणाध्वग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A planet.<BR>3 A heavenly spirit.<BR>E.<BR>गगण the sky, अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणपुष्प
गगणपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A flower in the sky, i. e. an impossibility.<BR>E.<BR>गगण and पुष्प a flower; also गगणकुसुम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणविहारिन्
गगणविहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Sporting in heaven.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A heavenly luminary.<BR>3 A divinity or celestial being.<BR>E.<BR>गगण, and विहारिन् who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणसद्
गगणसद्<BR>mf. (-सत् or सद्)<BR>Going in the air.<BR>m. (-सद्)<BR>A celestial being.<BR>E.<BR>गगण, and षद to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणस्थ
गगणस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Situated in the sky.<BR>E.<BR>गगण, and स्थ what stays in; also गगणस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणस्पर्शन
गगणस्पर्शन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>गगण, and स्पर्शन who touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणाग्र
गगणाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The highest heavens, the summit or highest part of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>गगण, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणेचर
गगणेचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A planet.<BR>2 An asterism.<BR>3 A heavenly spirit.<BR>E.<BR>गगणे in the sky, चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गगणोल्मुक
गगणोल्मुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The planet Mars.<BR>E.<BR>गगण the sky, and उल्मका, a torch or coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गग्घ
गग्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (गग्घति)<BR>To laugh, to laugh at or deride: see घग्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गा|गंगा
गङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The river Ganges, or its personification as a goddess.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, Uṇādi affix गन्, or गां the accusative of गो the earth, and ग who goes, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाका|गंगाका
गङ्गाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The river Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also read गङ्गका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=275" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाक्षेत्र|गंगाक्षेत्र
गङ्गाक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The river Ganges, and two Kos on either of its banks.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and क्षेत्र holy place; all dying within such limits going to heaven, whatever their crimes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाचिल्ली|गंगाचिल्ली
गङ्गाचिल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The black headed gull, (Larus ridibundus.)<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the Ganges, and चिल्ली a kite, considered by the Hindus as a species of that bird; the Gangetic kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाज|गंगाज|गङ्गाजः
गङ्गाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>2 A name of the deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the river goddess, and ज born; the son of GAṄGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाजल
गङ्गाजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The water of the Gaṅgā.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाटेय|गङ्गाटेयः
गङ्गाटेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Going in or to the Ganges.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A shrimp or prawn; also गलाविल.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the river, and अट् to go, अच् affix, गङ्गाट, and ढक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाद्वार|गंगाद्वार
गङ्गाद्वार<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The place where the Gaṅgā enters the plains; also Haridvār.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and द्वार gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गातीर
गङ्गातीर<BR>m. (-रं)<BR>The bank of the Gaṅgā.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाधर|गंगाधर|गङ्गाधरः
गङ्गाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the Ganges, and धर who possesses or receives; according to the legend, the Ganges in its descent first alighted on the head of ŚIVA, and continued for some period entangled in his hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गापार
गङ्गापार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The bank of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा and पार the bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गापुत्र|गंगापुत्र|गङ्गापुत्रः
गङ्गापुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 BHĪṢMA.<BR>2 A man of a mixed and vile caste, employed to remove dead bodies.<BR>3 A Brahman who conducts the ceremonies of pilgrimage at some places on the Ganges, especially at Benares,<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and पुत्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गामध्य|गंगामध्य
गङ्गामध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>The bed or stream of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and मध्य centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गाम्बु|गंगांबु
गङ्गाम्बु<BR>n. (-म्बु)<BR>1 Pure rain water, such as falls in Aśvin.<BR>2 Ganges water.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गायात्रा|गंगायात्रा
गङ्गायात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Pilgrimage to the Gaṅgā.<BR>2 Carrying a sick person to the river side to die there.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गासुत|गंगासुत|गङ्गासुतः
गङ्गासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 A name of the hero BHĪṢMA: see गङ्गाज.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and सुत a son; the son of GAṄGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गिका|गंगिका
गङ्गिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, and कन् affix fem. form; also गङ्गका, and गङ्गाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गङ्गीभूत|गंगीभूत
गङ्गीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become as the Ganges, as sacred, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गा, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गच्छ|गच्छः
गच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, and स Uṇādi affix, what goes or grows; also अगच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गच्छत्
गच्छत्<BR>mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छन्ती-च्छत्)<BR>Going.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गज|गजः
गज<BR>r. 1st cl. (गजति)<BR>To be drunk, to be confused or inebriated:<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (गजति गजयति) also (इ) गजि r. 1st cl. (गञ्जति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गज|गजः
गज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A measure of length, the Gaz, a yard, a measure of two cubits.<BR>3 A mound of earth sloping on both sides, on which a house may be erected.<BR>4 A small hole in the ground for a fire, over which to prepare medicines.<BR>E.<BR>गज to sound, to roar, affix अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजकन्द|गजकंद|गजकन्दः
गजकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A large esculent root, a sort of arum.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजकूर्म्माशिन्|गजकूर्माशिन्
गजकूर्म्माशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A name of GARUḌA the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, कूर्म्म a tortoise, and अशिन् who eats; alluding to a legend of his swallowing both animals whilst engaged in a contest with each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजचिर्भट
गजचिर्भट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजच्छाया
गजच्छाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A portion of time proper for a Śrāddha.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजढक्का
गजढक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A kettle drum carried on an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and ढक्का a large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजता
गजता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A multitude of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदघ्न|गजदघ्नः
गजदघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>As high or tall as an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and दघ्नच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदन्त|गजदंत|गजदन्तः
गजदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 Ivory, the elephant's tooth.<BR>3 A bracket or pin projecting from the wall.<BR>E.<BR>गज a elephant, and दन्त a tooth; GAṆEŚA is represented with an elephant's head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजदान|गजदानं
गजदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The liquor exuding from an elephant's temples.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and दान the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजद्वयस|गजद्वयसः
गजद्वयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>As high as an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and द्वयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपति|गजपतिः
गजपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A large state elephant.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपिप्पली
गजपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant bearing a seed which resembles pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and पिप्पली long pepper; considered to be a large species of pepper: see similar names, as करिपिप्पली, इभकणा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपुङ्गव|गजपुंगव|गजपुङ्गवः
गजपुङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A large and excellent elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and पुङ्गव implying eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजपुट|गजपुटः
गजपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small hollow for a fire, over which to prepare medical decoctions, extracts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and पुट a hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजप्रिया
गजप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The gum olibanum tree, (Boswellia serrata).<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and प्रिय beloved; also वल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजबन्धनी|गजबंधनी
गजबन्धनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A post to which an elephant is bound.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजभक्षक|गजभक्षकः
गजभक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The sacred fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and भक्षक eater; the young branches of the Pipal being the elephant's favourite food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजभक्षा
गजभक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>The gum olibanum tree: see गजप्रिय.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and भक्षा food; also गजभक्ष्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमण्डलिका|गजमंडलिका
गजमण्डलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A ring or circle of elephants surrounding a car, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गज, मण्डल a circle, कन् affix fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमाचल|गजमाचलः
गजमाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, मा fortune, and चल what goes; the destroyer of the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमात्र|गजमात्रः
गजमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>As tall as an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमुक्ता
गजमुक्ता<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A pearl, supposed to be found in the head of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and मुक्ता a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजमोटन|गजमोटनः
गजमोटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, मुट to run away, in the causal form, affix ल्युट्; or with मुच to go, गजमोचन as it is sometimes read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजयूथ
गजयूथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A herd of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and यूथ a herd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजवदन|गजवदनः
गजवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA, who is represented always with the head of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and वदन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजव्रज|गजव्रजः
गजव्रज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Who walks like an elephant.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A troop of elephants.<BR>2 The pace of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and व्रज a number or going, who goes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=276" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजसाह्वय|गजसाह्वयं
गजसाह्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A famous city, Hastinapur the capital of the KURUS.<BR>E.<BR>गज, स for सम् with, and आह्वय an appellation; named from its elephants; also गजाह्व, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाग्रणी
गजाग्रणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and अग्रणी preeminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाजीव|गजाजीवः
गजाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An elephant keeper or driver.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and आजीव who lives; who gets his livelihood by elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजानन|गजाननः
गजानन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The deity GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and आनन a face; see गजवदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजारि|गजारिः
गजारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A particular tree.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजारूढ
गजारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mounted or riding on an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाशन|गजाशनः
गजाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The religious fig tree.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>2 The gum olibanum tree.<BR>3 The root of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and अशन food; the food of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजास्य|गजास्यः
गजास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>GAṆEŚA: see गजानन.<BR>E.<BR>गज an elephant, and आस्य a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाह्व|गजाह्वं
गजाह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>The city Hastinapur.<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A plant: see गजपिप्पली.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and आह्वा a name: see गजसाह्वय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजाह्वय|गजाह्वयं
गजाह्वय<BR>n. (-य)<BR>Hastinapur, the ancient Dehli: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजेन्द्र|गजेंद्र|गजेन्द्रः
गजेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A large and excellent elephant.<BR>2 INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गजोषणा
गजोषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A sort of pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR>E.<BR>गज, and उषणा pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गञ्ज|गंज|गंजः|गञ्जः
गञ्ज<BR>mfn. subst. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>A mine, a jewel mine.<BR>mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>1 A cow-house or station of cowherds.<BR>2 A treasury, a jewel room, the place where plate, &c. is preserved.<BR>3 A mart, a place where grain, &c. is stored for sale.<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>1 A tavern.<BR>2 A drinking vessel.<BR>3 A hut, a hovel, the abode of low people.<BR>4 The Gunja or Ratti, (Abrus precatorius): see गुञ्जा.<BR>E.<BR>गजि to sound, अच् affix; fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गञ्जिका|गंजिका
गञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tavern.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड|गडः
गड<BR>r. 1st cl. (गडति)<BR>To distil or drop, to run as a liquid; also, गल.<BR>(इ) गडि r. 1st cl. (गण्डति)<BR>To affect the cheek, to be rough as the cheek, (obsolete.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड|गडः
गड<BR>m. (-ड)<BR>1 A kind of fish, the young of the Ophiocephalus lata, HAM.<BR>2 Another species, (Cyprinus garra. HAM.) see गल.<BR>3 An impediment, an obstacle.<BR>4 A screen, a covering, a fence.<BR>5 A moat, a ditch.<BR>6 A country, part of Malva, Gerha or Gera Mendela.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडक|गडकः
गडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of fish: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, affix क्वुन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडयन्त|गडयंत|गडयंतः|गडयन्तः
गडयन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop (water), Uṇādi affix झच् and अय substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडलवण|गडलवणं
गडलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rock or fossile salt, especially that found in the district of Sāmbher in the province of Ajmere.<BR>E.<BR>गड a country, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडि|गडिः
गडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>1 A steer.<BR>2 A lazy ox.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडु|गडुः
गडु<BR>mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डु)<BR>Crooked, humpbacked, &c.<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>1 A hump on the back.<BR>2 Goitre or Bronchocele.<BR>3 A humpbacked man.<BR>4 A javelin, a spear.<BR>5 An earth-worm.<BR>6 A water pot.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुक|गडुकः
गडुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A water pot.<BR>2 A finger ring.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुकण्ठ
गडुकण्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठी-ण्ठं)<BR>Having a goitre.<BR>E.<BR>गडु, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुर|गडुरः
गडुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Crooked, bent, humpbacked.<BR>E.<BR>गडु a hump, and र substituted for ल: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडुल|गडुलः
गडुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Crooked, humpbacked.<BR>E.<BR>गडु hump, and लच् affix; also गडुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडेर|गडेरः
गडेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop (water), and एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडोत्थ|गडोत्थं
गडोत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>Fossile salt.<BR>E.<BR>गड the country, and उत्थ produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गडोल|गडोलः
गडोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A mouthful.<BR>2 Raw sugar.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, ओलच् Uṇādi affix; also गण्डोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डरिका
गड्डरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sudden rush of water of which the source is unknown.<BR>2 A single ewe preceding a flock of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डुक|गड्डुकः
गड्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A golden vase.<BR>E.<BR>गड to sprinkle, डुक Uṇādi affix; also गड्डूक and occasionally गडुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गड्डूक|गड्डूकः
गड्डूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A golden water vessel: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण|गणः
गण<BR>r. 10th cl. (गणयति)<BR>To count, to reckon up by number, to calculate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण|गणः
गण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A flock, a multitude, a troop, a tribe or class, &c.<BR>2 A body of troops equal to three Gulmas, or twenty-seven chariots and as many elephants, eighty-one horses, and 135 foot.<BR>3 Troops of inferior deities considered as ŚIVA'S attendants, and under the especial superintendence of GAṆEŚA.<BR>4 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>5 A number, (in arithmetic.)<BR>6 A kind of perfume, commonly Cor.<BR>7 A sect in philosophy or religion.<BR>8 A conjugation, a class of radicals.<BR>9 Series of asterisms which are classed under three heads, human, infernal, and divine.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count or reckon, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणक|गणकः
गणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An astrologer, a calculator of nativities, &c.<BR>2 An arithmetician.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The wife of an astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>गण to calculate, affix क्वुन्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणकार|गणकारः
गणकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>2 A classifier, one who arranges into classes.<BR>E.<BR>गण a troop, and कार who forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणचक्रक|गणचक्रकं
गणचक्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A dinner in common by a party of virtuous men.<BR>E.<BR>गण a number, चक्र a wheel or circle, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणता
गणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Classification.<BR>2 Multitude, assemblage.<BR>3 Following a party or faction.<BR>4 Arithmetic.<BR>E.<BR>गण a class, तल् affix; also with त्व, गणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदीक्षा
गणदीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Initiation of a particular kind in which GAṆEŚA is especially worshipped.<BR>2 Initiation of a number or class.<BR>3 Performance of religious rites for a number of persons.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and दीक्षा a religious rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदीक्षिन्
गणदीक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>1 A priest who officiates for various castes and people.<BR>2 One who has been initiated into the worship of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गण, दीक्षा a rite, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणदेवता
गणदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A deity of a class, as an Āditya, a Vasu, a Rudra, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणद्रव्य|गणद्रव्यं
गणद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Public property, common stock.<BR>2 A variety of articles.<BR>E.<BR>गण a class, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणधर|गणधरः
गणधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The head of a class or number, the teacher of a school.<BR>2 A title of the first disciples of the Jina Mahāvīra.<BR>E.<BR>गण a class, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणन|गणनं
गणन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Counting, enumerating.<BR>2 Arithmetic.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=277" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनाथ|गणनाथः
गणनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनायक|गणनायकः
गणनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>f. (-यिका)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and नायक a leader: see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणनीय|गणनीयं
गणनीय<BR>mfn. (-य-यी-यं)<BR>1 Numerable, to be counted or reckoned.<BR>2 To be classed.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपति|गणपतिः
गणपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and पति lord: see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपर्व्वत|गणपर्वत|गणपर्व्वतः
गणपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The fabulous mountain Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>गण ŚIVA'S attendant demigods, and पर्ब्वत a mountain; this mountain being the residence of the Kinnaras, Yakṣas, and other subordinate deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणपीठक|गणपीठकं
गणपीठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The breast or bosom.<BR>E.<BR>गण the aggregate, (of qualities,) and पीठक a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरात्र|गणरात्रं
गणरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A multitude of nights.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and रात्र night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरूप|गणरूपः
गणरूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Swallow wort, (Calotropis gigantea); also अर्क.<BR>E.<BR>गण a number, and रूप form, multiform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणरूपिन्
गणरूपिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>Swallow wort, the white sort: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणवतीसुत|गणवतीसुतः
गणवतीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The name of a sage and physician; also called DHANVANTARI or KĀŚIRĀJA.<BR>E.<BR>गणवती a proper name, and सुत a son, the son of GAṆAVATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणहासक|गणहासकः
गणहासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cor, a species of perfume.<BR>E.<BR>गण many, and हासक what causes to smile, what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाग्रणी
गणाग्रणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गण the troops of deities, and अग्रणी principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाचल|गणाचलः
गणाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and अचल a mountain, the residence of the GAṆAS or troops of demigods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाधिप|गणाधिपः
गणाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A title of ŚIVA.<BR>3 The chief of a troop of soldiers, of a class of disciples, of a body of men or animals, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and अधिप master; also गणाधिपति, and other similar epithets: see गणेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणान्न
गणान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>A mess, food prepared for a number of persons in common.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणाभ्यन्तर|गणाभ्यंतर|गणाभ्यन्तरः
गणाभ्यन्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>One of a troop or number.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A member of a religious convent or association.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and अभ्यन्तर included.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणि|गणिः
गणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>Counting, enumerating.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिका
गणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A courtezan, a harlot.<BR>2 A sort of jasmin, (J. auriculatum.)<BR>3 A tree, commonly Ganiyari, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>4 A female elephant.<BR>5 Counting, enumerating.<BR>E.<BR>गण to reckon, &c. ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिकारिका
गणिकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a small tree with a very fetid leaf, commonly called Ganiyāri, the wood of which is used in attrition, for the purpose of producing flame, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to गणिकारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिकारी
गणिकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The name of a tree: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणित|गणितं
गणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Numbered, counted, reckoned, calculated.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The science of computation, comprising arithmetic, algebra, and geometry, distinguished as पाटीगणितं, वीजगणितं and रेखागणितं.<BR>2 Calculating, numbering.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणितव्य
गणितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be counted or numbered.<BR>2 To be calculated.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणिपिटका
गणिपिटका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A division of science peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणीभूत
गणीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Included in any class or troop^1.<BR>2 Calculated.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and भूत become, with च्चि augment.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेय|गणेयः
गणेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Numberable, calculable, what may be reckoned or counted.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, and यत् affix, form irr. see गण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेरु|गणेरुः
गणेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Pterospermum acerifolium, &c.) see कर्णिकार<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>1 A harlot, a whore.<BR>2 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गण a number, ईर to go, &c. affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेरुका
गणेरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेश|गणेशः
गणेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 GAṆEŚA the son of ŚIVA and PĀRVATĪ; he is the deity of wisdom, and remover of obstacles, whence in the commencement of all undertakings, the opening of all compositions, &c. he receives the reverential homage of the Hindus. He is represented as a short fat man, with the head of an elephant; and the present appellation, with other similar compounds, alludes to his office as chief of the various classes of subordinate gods, who are regarded as ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR>E.<BR>गण a troop or class (of deities attendant upon ŚIVA), and ईश lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशकुसुम|गणेशकुसुमं
गणेशकुसुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A shrub, Oleander with red flowers.<BR>E.<BR>गणेश, and कुसुम a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशपूजा
गणेशपूजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Worship of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>गणेश, and पृजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणेशभूषण|गणेशभूषणं
गणेशभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>गणेश, and भूषण ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गणोत्साह|गणोत्साहः
गणोत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>E.<BR>गण a herd, and उत्साह toil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्ड|गंड|गंडः|गण्डः
गण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A cheek, the whole side of the face including the temple.<BR>2 An elephant's temple or cheek.<BR>3 A boil, a pimple.<BR>4 A mark, a spot.<BR>5 A bubble.<BR>6 A knot.<BR>7 A rhinoceros: (see गण्डक.)<BR>8 Part of a horse's trappings, a stud or button fixed as an ornament upon the harness.<BR>9 A hero.<BR>10 The abrupt interchange of question and answer, as one of the characteristics of the dramatic composition called Vīthi.<BR>11 The tenth Yoga, or one of the twenty-seven portions of a circle on the plane of the ecliptic: see योग.<BR>12 An astronomical period.<BR>E.<BR>गडि to affect the cheek, अच् affix, or गम to go, ड Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डक|गंडक|गंडकः|गण्डकः
गण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A rhinoceros.<BR>2 A mode of reckoning by fours.<BR>3 An obstacle or impediment.<BR>4 Separation, disjunction.<BR>5 Astrological science or a part of it.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The name of a river in the north of India, the Gandaki.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lump, a ball.<BR>E.<BR>गडि to affect the cheek, &c. ण्वुल् affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकारी
गण्डकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a boil, and कारी what occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकाली
गण्डकाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>See the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a knot, and काली black; black with many joints and knots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकुसुम|गंडकुसुम|गण्डकुसुमं
गण्डकुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The juice that exudes from the elephant's temples in time of rut.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड an elephant's temples, and कुसुम a flower, from its supposed fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डकूप|गंडकूप|गण्डकूपः
गण्डकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डगात्र|गण्डगात्रं
गण्डगात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A fruit, custard apple, (Annona squamosa.)<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a boil, and गात्र a body; the inside being compared to purulent pustules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डफलक|गंडफलक
गण्डफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The cheek.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड, and फलक a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डमाला|गंडमाला
गण्डमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Inflammation of the glands of the neck, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a boil, and माला a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=278" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डमालिन्
गण्डमालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having the glands of the neck inflamed.<BR>E.<BR>इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डशैल|गंडशैल|गण्डशैलः
गण्डशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A rock or rocky fragment fallen from a height, thrown down by an earthquake, a storm, &c.<BR>2 The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a cheek, and शैल a rock, the cheek of the mountain, or in the second instance, vice-versa, the mountain as it were of the cheek or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डस्थल|गंडस्थल
गण्डस्थल<BR>nf. (-लः-ली)<BR>The cheek.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डाङ्ग|गंडांग|गण्डाङ्गः
गण्डाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a stud, and अङ्ग a body: from the studded appearance of his hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डाली|गंडाली
गण्डाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A bent grass with white blossoms, a white sort of Dūrvā, (Agrostis linearis.)<BR>E.<BR>गण्ड a boil, अल to be adequate to or fit for, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डि|गंडि|गंडिः|गण्डिः
गण्डि<BR>m. (-ण्डिः)<BR>1 Goitre or Bronchocele.<BR>2 The trunk of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>गडि to affect the cheek, &c. Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डीर|गंडीर|गंडीरः|गण्डीरः
गण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A kind of potherb, described as growing in watery ground, and according to some, a species of cucumber.<BR>2 A hero, a champion.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A milky plant, (Euphorbia.)<BR>E.<BR>गडि to affect a part, &c. इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डु|गंडु|गंडुः|गण्डुः
गण्डु<BR>mf. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A pillow.<BR>f. (-ण्डूः)<BR>A knot or joint.<BR>E.<BR>गडि to support the cheek, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूपद|गंडूपद|गण्डूपदः
गण्डूपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A small or female worm.<BR>E.<BR>गण्डू a knot, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूपदभव|गंडूपदभव|गण्डूपदभवं
गण्डूपदभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>गण्डूपद a worm, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डूष|गंडूष|गंडूषः|गण्डूषः
गण्डूष<BR>mf. (-षः-षा)<BR>1 A mouthful.<BR>2 A handful.<BR>3 A handful of water, water, &c. held in the hollowed palm of the hand for rincing the mouth, &c.<BR>4 Filling the mouth, rincing it, &c.<BR>5 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, ऊषण् Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्डोल|गंडोल|गंडोलः|गण्डोलः
गण्डोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Raw sugar.<BR>2 A mouthful.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, or गडि to affect the cheek, ओलच् affix; also गडोल.<BR>E.<BR>गल to court, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गण्य|गण्यं
गण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>To be counted or calculated.<BR>E.<BR>गण to count, affix of the future participle यत्; also irregularly गणेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत|गतं
गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Known, understood.<BR>3 Obtained, gained.<BR>4 Lost.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Going, motion.<BR>2 Any thing past or done, an event.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, in the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतकाल
गतकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Time past.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतक्लम
गतक्लम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Rested, refreshed.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and क्लम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतचेतन
गतचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Senseless, swooned.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and चेतना consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतज्वर
गतज्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Well, recovered, free from fever or sickness^1.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and ज्वर fever.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गततोयद
गततोयद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Cloudless, cleared up, fair.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and तोयद a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतप्रत्यागत
गतप्रत्यागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Returned, come back again after having gone away.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and प्रत्य, गत come back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतदिन
गतदिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Yesterday.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and दिन day; also गतदिवसं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतधृति
गतधृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Agitated, discomposed, unsteady.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and धृति firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतनासिक|गतनासिकः
गतनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>गत gone, lost, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतमाय
गतमाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Reformed, without deceit.<BR>2 Cruel without compassion.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and माया deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतलक्ष्मीक
गतलक्ष्मीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unfortunate, suffering losses; so गतदीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवत्
गतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Going, passing.<BR>2 Obtaining.<BR>3 Falling into.<BR>4 Feeling, entertaining.<BR>E.<BR>गम, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतवित्त
गतवित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Beggared, impoverished.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and वित्त wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतविभव
गतविभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and विभव wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतव्यथ
गतव्यथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Free from pain.<BR>2 Unanxious.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and व्यथ pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतशैशव
गतशैशव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Grown up, above eight years of age. गत, and शैशव infancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसङ्कल्प|गतसंकल्प
गतसङ्कल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Bereft of sense, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and सङ्कल्प purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसङ्ग
गतसङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Detached from, dissevered.<BR>2 Adverse or indifferent to.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and सङ्ग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसत्व
गतसत्व<BR>mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>1 Base.<BR>2 Lifeless, dead, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and सत्व being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतसन्नक|गतसन्नकः
गतसन्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An elephant out of rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गताक्ष
गताक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Blind, sightless.<BR>E.<BR>गत gone, and अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतागत|गतागतं
गतागत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The flight of a bird backward and forward.<BR>2 Going and coming, reiterated motion in general.<BR>E.<BR>गत going, आगत coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतानुगतिक
गतानुगतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Following, imitating, imitative, doing as others do.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and अनुगतिक who goes after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतायुस्
गतायुस्<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>1 Very old, infirm, decrepid, decayed.<BR>2 Dead.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्त्तवा|गतार्तवा
गतार्त्तवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A woman past child bearing.<BR>2 A barren woman.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and आर्त्तवा a woman menstruating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतार्थ
गतार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Unmeaning, nonsensical.<BR>2 Poor.<BR>3 Void of an object.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and अर्थ sense, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतासु
गतासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Dead, expired.<BR>E.<BR>गत, and असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गति|गतिः
गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Going, moving, motion in general.<BR>2 March, procession.<BR>3 A road, a way, a path.<BR>4 A period of life, as age, youth, &c.<BR>5 An expedient^1, a means of success.<BR>6 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>7 A sinus, a fistular sore.<BR>8 Worldly vanity or wickedness.<BR>9 Course of events, fate, fortune.<BR>10 Resource, refuge, asylum.<BR>11 The diurnal motion of a planet in its orbit.<BR>12 State, mode of existence.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, affix क्तिन.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिक|गतिकं
गतिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 Refuge, asylum.<BR>3 Course.<BR>4 Condition.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गतिला
गतिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The name of a river, the Gatilā.<BR>2 Mutual separation.<BR>E.<BR>गप्त to go, इल Uṇādi affix, and त substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्वर|गत्वरः
गत्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going, moving, locomotive.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, affix क्वरप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्वा
गत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having gone, gone to or attained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गत्यून
गत्यून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Impassable, difficult of access.<BR>2 Desert.<BR>3 Helpless.<BR>E.<BR>गति, and ऊन् defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद|गदं|गदः
गद<BR>r. 10 cl. (गदति)<BR>1 To speak articulately.<BR>2 To be sick.<BR>r. 10th cl. (गदयति)<BR>To thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=279" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद|गदं|गदः
गद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Disease, sickness.<BR>2 Speech, speaking.<BR>2 GADA the younger brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A mace, a club.<BR>2 Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>गद to speak, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदयित्नु|गदयित्नुः
गदयित्नु<BR>mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु)<BR>1 Loquacious, talkative, talking much or idly.<BR>2 Libidinous, lustful, desirous.<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>A name of KANDARPA, the deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>गद to speak, Uṇādi affix इत्नुच्, and अय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाख्य|गदाख्यं
गदाख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>A kind of Costus, (C. speciosus): see कुष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदागद
गदागद<BR>m. (always dual -दौ)<BR>The two physicians of Svarga, the sons of AŚVINĪ by SŪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>गद disease in general, and अगद health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाग्रज|गदाग्रजः
गदाग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>गद, and अग्रज an elder brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाधर|गदाधरः
गदाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>गदा a club, and धर who holds; KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU is represented holding a mace in one of his hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाभृत्
गदाभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A mace or club bearer.<BR>3 One who fights with a mace.<BR>E.<BR>गदा a club, and भृत् who nourishes: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाम्बर|गदांबर|गदाम्बरः
गदाम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>गद sound, अम्बर the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाराति|गदारातिः
गदाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>गद, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदाहू
गदाहू<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>A kind of grass, (Costus speciosus): see कुष्ठ.<BR>E.<BR>गद disease, and आह्वा a name; named by many of the same terms as disease: see व्याधि, &c.; also गदाख्य, गदाह्वय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदित|गदितः
गदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken, said.<BR>E.<BR>गद to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदितवत्
गदितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Saying, speaking, having spoken.<BR>E.<BR>गद, and क्तततु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गदिन्
गदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A mace bearer.<BR>3 One armed with a club.<BR>4 A sick man.<BR>E.<BR>गदा a mace, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गद|गद्गदः
गद्गद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Indistinct or convulsive utterance, as sobbing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गद to speak, क्विप् affix, root repeated with अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदध्वनि|गद्गदध्वनिः
गद्गदध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Low inarticulate expression of joy or grief.<BR>E.<BR>गद्गद inarticulate utterance, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदपद
गद्गदपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Inarticulate speech. गद्गद, and पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्गदवाच्
गद्गदवाच्<BR>f. (-बाक्)<BR>Inarticulate or convulsive speech, interrupted by sobbing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गद्गद, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्य|गद्यं
गद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be spoken or uttered.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Prose.<BR>E.<BR>गद to speak, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गद्यानक|गद्यानकं|गद्यानकः
गद्यानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A weight either of sixty-four or forty-eight Rattis; also read गद्यालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तव्य|गंतव्य
गन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be gone, to be gone to or attained.<BR>E.<BR>गम, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तु|गंतुः|गन्तुः
गन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A traveller, a way-farer.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, Uṇādi affix तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्तृ|गंतृ
गन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Who or what goes or moves.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्त्री|गंत्री
गन्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>A cart or car drawn by oxen.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, ष्ट्रन् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्त्रीरथ|गंत्रीरथ|गन्त्रीरथः
गन्त्रीरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A cart.<BR>E.<BR>गन्त्री a carriage drawn by oxen, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्ध|गंध|गन्धं|गंधः|गन्धः
गन्ध<BR>r. 10th cl. (गन्धयते)<BR>1 To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>2 To move, to go.<BR>3 To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्ध|गंध|गन्धं|गंधः|गन्धः
गन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Smell, odour.<BR>2 A perfume, a fragrance or fragrant substance.<BR>3 A diffusive fragrance.<BR>4 Sulphur.<BR>5 Connexion, relationship.<BR>6 A neighbour.<BR>7 A plant, (Morunga hyperanthera, &c.)<BR>8 Pride, arrogance.<BR>9 Small, diminutive, a little, a small quantity, &c.<BR>10 Pounded Sandal.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>The bud of the Champaca flower, (Michelia Champaca.)<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Aloe-wood.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध to hurt, to move, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धक|गंधक|गंधकः|गन्धकः
गन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sulphur.<BR>2 The morunga tree, (M. hyperanthera, &c.) see शोभाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकारिका|गंधकारिका
गन्धकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female artisan, living in the house of another woman.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध perfume, and कारिका who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकालिका|गंधकालिका
गन्धकालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकाली|गंधकाली
गन्धकाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The mother of the poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध perfume, कल to make, affixes अण् and ङीप् having a strong scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकाष्ठ|गंधकाष्ठ|गन्धकाष्ठं
गन्धकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A fragrant wood, as Sandal, aloewood, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and काष्ठ timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धकुटी|गंधकुटी
गन्धकुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A kind of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, &c. कुटी abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धखेड|गन्धखेडं
गन्धखेड<BR>n. (-डः)<BR>A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and खेड grass; also with कन् added गन्धखेडकं: see गन्धतृण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धगज|गंधगज|गन्धगजः
गन्धगज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An elephant of the best kind.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध odour, गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धगुण|गंधगुण
गन्धगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having the property of odour.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धघ्राण|गंधघ्राण
गन्धघ्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Smelling any odour.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and घ्राण smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धचेलिका|गंधचेलिका
गन्धचेलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध fragrance, चेलि clothes, affix कन्; being used for scenting clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धजात|गन्धजातं
गन्धजात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and जात produced; fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धज्ञा|गंधज्ञा
गन्धज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध scent, and ज्ञा who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धतूर्य्य|गन्धतूर्य|गंधतूर्य|गन्धतूर्य्यं
गन्धतूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A musical instrument, one of a loud sound used in battle: (a drum or trumpet.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध pride, and तूर्य्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धतृण|गन्धतृणं
गन्धतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धत्वच्
गन्धत्वच्<BR>f. (-त्वक्)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध and त्वच् skin, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धद्विप|गंधद्विप|गन्धद्विपः
गन्धद्विप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An elephant of the best class, supposed to emit a particular smell at all times.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and द्विप an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धधूलि|गंधधूलि|गन्धधूलिः
गन्धधूलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Musk, the fragrant secretion of the musk-deer.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध fragrant, and धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धन|गंधन|गंधनं|गन्धनं
गन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Continued effort, perseverance.<BR>2 Injury, hurting, killing.<BR>3 Intimation, information.<BR>4 Manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध to hurt, to move, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनकुल|गंधनकुल|गन्धनकुलः
गन्धनकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The musk-rat of Bengal, (Sorex moschata.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध scented, and नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनाकुली
गन्धनाकुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, possibly the serpent Ophioxylon: see रास्ना.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smelling, and नाकुली the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनामन्
गन्धनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A fragrant kind of basil.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध fragrance, and नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनाली|गंधनाली
गन्धनाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध scent, and नाली a tubular canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=280" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धनिलया|गंधनिलया
गन्धनिलया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Double jasmin, (J. Zambac floribus multiplicatis.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and निलय a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपत्र|गन्धपत्रः
गन्धपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A white sort of basil, (Ocymum gratissimum): see श्वेतपर्णास.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A sort of zedoary.<BR>(-त्रा)<BR>Ajwaen, (Ligusticam ajwaen.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपलाशिका|गंधपलाशिका
गन्धपलाशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध small, पलाश a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपलाशी|गंधपलाशी
गन्धपलाशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and पलाश a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपाषाण|गंधपाषाण|गन्धपाषाणः
गन्धपाषाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smelling, and पाषाण a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपिशात्रिका
गन्धपिशात्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The smell of incense, diffusive incense.<BR>E.<BR>गम्म smell, पिशाचिका female demon; imp-like, from its dark colour or cloudy nature; or attracting demons by its fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपीता
गन्धपीता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of zedoary.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and पीत yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धपुष्प|गंधपुष्प|गन्धपुष्पः
गन्धपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A kind of cane, (Calamus roatang.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Alangium hexapetalum): see अङ्कोट.<BR>3 Sebesten, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>1 The indigo plant.<BR>2 Ganiyāri, (Premna spinosa, &c.) see गणिकारी.<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Flowers and Sandal presented together at seasons of worship.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and पुष्प flower; having odoriferous flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धफल|गन्धफलः
गन्धफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>2 The Bel, (Ægle crataeva.)<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>1 A plant bearing a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>2 The gum olibanum tree.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The blossom of the Champaca: see चम्पक.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and फल a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धबन्धु|गंधबंधु|गन्धबन्धुः
गन्धबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध a smell, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धभद्रा
गन्धभद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A creeper commonly Gandhabhādali or Ghandali, (Poederia fetida?)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धभाण्ड|गन्धभाण्डः
गन्धभाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides): see गर्द्धभाण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमांसी
गन्धमांसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A kind of Indian spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमातृ|गंधमातृ
गन्धमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध scent, and मातृ the mother; the property of fragrance residing in the earth or earthy atoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमादन|गंधमादन|गन्धमादनं|गन्धमादनः
गन्धमादन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>The name of a particular mountain, forming the division between Ilāvṛtta and Bhadrāśva or to the east of Meru.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 Sulphur.<BR>3 The name of one of the monkey chiefs.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Spirituous liquor; also in some books read गन्धमादिनी.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, मद to inebriate in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमादिन्
गन्धमादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Strong scented, of intoxicating odour.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Lac.<BR>2 A sort of perfume.<BR>3 Wine or spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and मादिन् what intoxicates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमार्जार|गंधमार्जार|गन्धमार्जारः|गन्धमार्ज्जार|गन्धमार्ज्जारः
गन्धमार्जार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The civet-cat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and मार्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमालिनी
गन्धमालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Murā, a perfume so called.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, माला a necklace, affixes इनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमुण्ड|गन्धमुण्डः
गन्धमुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A creeper, (Hibiscus populneoides); also गन्थभाण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूल|गन्धमूलः
गन्धमूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant with a fragrant and tuberous root, one of the Scitaminea, (Alpinia galanga): see कुलञ्जन.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>1 A species of Curcuma, (C. reclinata, Rox.)<BR>2 The olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and मूल a root, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्; also with कन् affix गन्धमूलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूलक|गन्धमूलकः
गन्धमूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of Curcuma; also गन्धमूली: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमूषिक|गंधमूषिक|गन्धमूषिकः
गन्धमूषिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>The musk-rat or shrew, (Sorex moschata); also in the fem. गन्धमृषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमृग|गंधमृग|गन्धमृगः
गन्धमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The civet-cat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and मृग a deer; the name also may be applied to the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमोदन|गंधमोदन|गन्धमोदनः
गन्धमोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and मोदन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमैथुन|गंधमैथुन|गन्धमैथुनः
गन्धमैथुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and मैथुन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धमोहिनी|गंधमोहिनी
गन्धमोहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Champaca flower.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and मोहिनी delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धरस|गन्धरसः
गन्धरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and रस essence; also रसगन्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धराज|गंधराज|गन्धराजं|गन्धराजः
गन्धराज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 Any sweet smelling flower.<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>1 A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi: see नखी.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and राज what excels, from राज to shine, affix अच्; fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्ब
गन्धर्ब्ब<BR>m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>1 A Gandharba or celestial musician; these demigods inhabit INDRA'S heaven, and form the orchestra at all the banquets of the principal deities.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 A kind of deer; according to some authorities, the musk-deer.<BR>4 The soul after death, and previous to its being born again, corresponding, in some respects, to the western notion of ghosts.<BR>5 A singer in general.<BR>6 The Koïl or black cuckoo.<BR>7 The sun.<BR>8 A sage, a pious man.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, injury, &c. अर्ब्ब to go, affix अच्, the अ final of गन्ध is rejected; the root is also sometimes written with the dental letter अर्व्व, when the compound will be गन्धर्व्व; the best authorities however write it with the final labial letter ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बविद्या
गन्धर्ब्बविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Music, dancing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गन्धर्ब्ब, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बविवाह
गन्धर्ब्बविवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marriage by mutual consent, without any ceremonies, allowable between persons of the second class.<BR>E.<BR>गन्धर्ब्ब, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बवेद
गन्धर्ब्बवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The science of music considered as a branch of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>गन्धर्ब्ब, and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धर्ब्बहस्त
गन्धर्ब्बहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The castor-oil tree, (Palma christi or Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्धर्ब्ब a deer, and हस्त hand or foot; the leaves being compared to the foot of the deer; also with कन् added गन्धर्ब्बहस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धलोलुपा|गंधलोलुपा
गन्धलोलुपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A fly or gnat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, &c. लोलुप unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवणिज्
गन्धवणिज्<BR>m. (-णिक्)<BR>A perfumer, a dealer in perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and वणिज a dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवत्|गंधवत्|गन्धवन्त्
गन्धवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Scented, smelling, odoriferous.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The name of a city.<BR>3 Wine or vinous liquor.<BR>4 A kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR>5 The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>6 A wild species of Ajväen: see यमानी.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, मतुप् poss. affix fem. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवल्कल|गन्धवल्कलं
गन्धवल्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Cassia bark.<BR>2 Sarsaparilla.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवल्लरी
गन्धवल्लरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant; also सहदेवी.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and वल्लर a pedicle, or with वल्ली the same, गन्धवल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवह|गंधवह|गन्धवहः
गन्धवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Smelling, fragrant, &c.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The wind.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and वह what conveys, from वह to bear, &c., and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=281" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवाह|गंधवाह|गन्धवाहः
गन्धवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The wind.<BR>2 A deer, the musk-deer.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, वह to convey, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धविह्वल|गंधविह्वल|गन्धविह्वलः
गन्धविह्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धवृक्ष|गंधवृक्ष|गन्धवृक्षः
गन्धवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध perfume, and वृक्ष a tree, yielding a fragrant resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धव्याकुल|गंधव्याकुल|गन्धव्याकुलं
गन्धव्याकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A perfume, a fragrant berry: see कक्कोल.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and व्याकुल disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशटी
गन्धशटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A sort of Curcuma: see शटी.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and शटी the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशालि|गन्धशालिः
गन्धशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sweet smelling kind of rice.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशुण्डिनी|गंधशुंडिनी
गन्धशुण्डिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The musk-rat or shrew.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and शुण्डिनी a rat; also गन्धाशुण्डिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धशेखर|गंधशेखर|गन्धशेखरः
गन्धशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and शेखर chief, a principal perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसार|गंधसार|गन्धसारः
गन्धसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and सार essence, the essence of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसूयी
गन्धसूयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The musk shrew or small musk-rat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and सू to produce, affixes युक् and ङीप्; also sometimes read गन्धसुखी, from गन्ध and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धसोम|गंधसोम|गन्धसोमं
गन्धसोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The white esculent water lily.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and सोम the moon; opening its petals at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धहारिका|गंधहारिका
गन्धहारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female artisan working in another person's house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाखु|गंधाखु|गन्धाखुः
गन्धाखु<BR>m. (-खुः)<BR>A musk-rat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and आखु a rat: see गन्धसूयी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाजीव|गंधाजीव|गन्धाजीवः
गन्धाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A vender of perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and आजीव who gets a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाढ्य|गंधाढ्य|गन्धाढ्यं|गन्धाढ्यः
गन्धाढ्य<BR>m. (-ढ्यः)<BR>The orange tree.<BR>f. (-ढ्या)<BR>A plant: see गन्धाली.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and आढ्य wealth, rich in odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धापकर्षण|गंधापकर्षण
गन्धापकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Removing any smell.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and अपकर्षण taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाला
गन्धाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, commonly Jiyati, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाली|गंधाली
गन्धाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Gandhali or Gandbhadalīya, a plant, (Paederia fetida.)<BR>2 A wasp: see गन्धोली.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and आली a line, a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाश्मन्|गंधाश्मन्
गन्धाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धाष्टक|गंधाष्टक|गन्धाष्टकं
गन्धाष्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A class of eight fragrant articles used in worship, &c. as a Sandal, agallochum, camphor, saffron, valerian, and some fragrant grasses.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and अष्टक eight collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिक|गंधिक|गन्धिकः
गन्धिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and ठक् affix; also गन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धिन्|गंधिन्
गन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Smelling, odoriferous.<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>1 A bug; also the flying bug.<BR>2 A tree, (Xanthophyllum virens.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of perfume: see Mura.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smelling, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोतु|गन्धोतुः
गन्धोतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The civet-cat.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and ओतु a cat; also गन्धौतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोत्तमा|गंधोत्तमा
गन्धोत्तमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध odour, and उत्तम excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोपजीविन्|गंधोपजीविन्
गन्धोपजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A perfumer.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध, and उपजीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गन्धोलि|गन्धोलिः
गन्धोलि<BR>f. (-लिः or -ली)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (C. reclinata, Rox.)<BR>(-ली)<BR>1 A wasp.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध to smell or injure, ओलच affix, इन् or ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभलि
गभलि<BR>mf. (-स्तिः)<BR>A ray of light, a sun or moon-beam.<BR>m. (-स्तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>A name of SVĀHĀ the wife of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>ग for गो the heaven, भस to shine, and क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिमत्|गभस्तिमन्त्
गभस्तिमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The sun.<BR>n. (-मत्)<BR>One of the seven divisions of Pātāla or regions below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>गभस्ति a ray of light, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभस्तिहस्त|गभस्तिहस्तः
गभस्तिहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>गभस्ति a ray, and हस्त a hand; wielding the sun-beams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीर|गभीरं
गभीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Deep.<BR>2 Thick, impervious, (as a forest.)<BR>3 Profound, sagacious.<BR>4 Deep in sound, hollow-toned.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, भ substituted for the final, ईरन् Uṇādi affix; also with नुम् inserted गम्भीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरध्वनि
गभीरध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 Deep sound.<BR>2 A low note or tone.<BR>E.<BR>गभीर, and ध्वनि sound; also गभीरनाद, गभीरशब्द, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभीरिका
गभीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A large drum.<BR>2 A gong.<BR>E.<BR>गभीर deep, (as sound,) कन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गभोलिक|गभोलिकः
गभोलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small round pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम|गमः
गम<BR>(औ, ऌ) औगसॢ r. 1st cl. (गच्छति)<BR>1 To go, to move or approach.<BR>2 To arrive at, to accomplish or attain.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To follow, to imitate.<BR>With आङ्<BR>(आगच्छति)<BR>1 To come, to arrive.<BR>2 To go to or unto.<BR>(आगमयते)<BR>To wait, to delay.<BR>With अधि,<BR>1 To obtain, to gain or acquire.<BR>2 To go over, as a book or set of rules, to peruse, to learn.<BR>3 To pass over, to omit.<BR>With अप,<BR>To go back or away, to separate.<BR>With अव,<BR>To know, to understand.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To approach, to go near to.<BR>2 To go up, to rise.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To produce.<BR>2 To go near.<BR>3 To consent to.<BR>With उप and आङ्,<BR>To approach.<BR>With दुर्,<BR>To go with difficulty.<BR>With नि,<BR>To acquire knowledge.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To go forth or out.<BR>With परि and उत्,<BR>To rise as from a seat, &c.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To surround.<BR>2 To go away.<BR>With प्रति and आङ्,<BR>To return or arrive at.<BR>With वि,<BR>To go against as an enemy.<BR>With सम्,<BR>(संगच्छते)<BR>1 To go with, to accompany.<BR>2 To meet, to encounter.<BR>(संगच्छति)<BR>To go to, (in a transitive sense.)<BR>With सम and आङ्<BR>To meet, to unite.<BR>With सम and उप,<BR>To submit to, to yield.<BR>With सु,<BR>1 To go easily or well.<BR>2 To arrive at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम|गमः
गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 March, especially the march of an assailant.<BR>3 A road.<BR>4 A game played with dice and men, as backgammon, &c.<BR>5 Acting inconsiderately, looking at any thing hastily and superficially.<BR>6 Reading lightly, hasty or careless perusal^1, running over a book, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, घञ् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमकारित्व|गमकारित्वं
गमकारित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Rashness, inconsiderateness.<BR>E.<BR>गम as above, कारिन् who does or acts, and त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमथ|गमथः
गमथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, अथ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमन|गमनं
गमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going in general.<BR>2 March in general, or the march of an assailant.<BR>3 Cohabitation.<BR>4 Obtaining, attaining.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go or move, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनार्ह
गमनार्ह<BR>m. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>To be sought, fit, suitable, desirable.<BR>E.<BR>गमत, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमनीय
गमनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 What may be gone to or reached, attainable, accessible.<BR>2 What ought to be followed, to be practised or observed.<BR>E.<BR>गम, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=282" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमयत्
गमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Causing or making to go.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमागम|गमागमः
गमागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Going and coming.<BR>E.<BR>गम, and आगम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमित
गमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused to go, sent, brought, reduced, driven to, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गमिन्
गमिन्<BR>m. (-भी)<BR>A passenger.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, इनि Uṇādi affix, otherwise with णिनि affix, गामिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्ब
गम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (गम्बति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भारी|गंभारी
गम्भारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The name of a tree, commonly called by the same name Gambhāri, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>क water, भृ to nourish, affixes अण् and ङीष्, क is changed to ग and into the second case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीर|गंभीर|गम्भीरं|गम्भीरः
गम्भीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Deep, (as water, but applied metaphorically to sound, intellect, &c. as in English.)<BR>2 Dull, slow.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Mantra or magical incantation written in prose in the Rig Veda.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>3 The citron.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Hiccup, violent singultus.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, ईरन् Uṇādi affix, म changed to भ, and नुम् inserted: see गभीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरता
गम्भीरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Depth, (of water.)<BR>2 Depth of thought, profoundness.<BR>3 Depth of sound.<BR>E.<BR>गम्भीर, and तल् affix; also गम्भीरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरनाद
गम्भीरनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A deep or hollow sound, thundering, roaring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गम्भीर, and नाद sound; also similar compounds, as गम्भीरध्वनि, गम्भीरशव्य; also with गभीर, गभीरनाद, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरवेदिन्|गंभीरवेदिन्
गम्भीरवेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A restive elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गम्भीर dull, and विद to know, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्भीरार्थ
गम्भीरार्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>Profound sense or meaning.<BR>E.<BR>गम्भीर, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्य|गम्यं|गम्यः
गम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Attainable, accessible.<BR>2 To be gone, to be gone to.<BR>3 Perceptible.<BR>4 Desirable, suitable, fit.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्यता
गम्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Accessibility.<BR>2 Perceptibility.<BR>3 Being capable of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, गन्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गम्यमान|गम्यमानः
गम्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>To be gone, to be traversed, to be gone to, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, passive v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गय|गयः
गय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A species of ox, the Gayal or Bos Gavoeus.<BR>2 The name of a royal or military saint.<BR>3 The name of an Asura.<BR>4 One of the monkey chiefs of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Gaya, a city in Behār still so called, and a place of pilgrimage; the capital of the saint of the same name; it was made holy by the benediction of VIṢṆU, who granted its sanctity to the piety of Gaya the Rājarṣi; or according to another legend to Gaya the Asura, who was overwhelmed here by the deities with rocks; sacrifices should be offered once at least in the life of every Hindu to his progenitors at Gaya.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, डय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर|गरं|गरः
गर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 Poison.<BR>2 An antidote.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>2 The fifth of the eleven Karaṇas.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Swallowing.<BR>(-री)<BR>A species of grass, (Andropogon serratus); also गरागरी.<BR>E.<BR>गर to hurt, and अच् affix, or गृ to wet or sprinkle, or again गॄ to swallow, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरघ्न|गरघ्नः
गरघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>1 Antidote, an antidote.<BR>2 Sanative, healthy.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A species of Basil.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A fish (the young of the Ophiocephalus lata, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>गर, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरण|गरणं
गरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Wetting, sprinkling.<BR>2 Swallowing.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to wet, or गृ to swallow, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरद|गरदं|गरदः
गरद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 A poisoner, poisoning.<BR>2 Unwholesome, occasioning sickness.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Poison.<BR>E.<BR>गर poison, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरब्रत
गरब्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>गर sprinkling, (of rain,) and ब्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरभ|गरभः
गरभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The foetus or embryo: see गर्भ.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to drop, &c. अभच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरल|गरलं|गरलः
गरल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The venom of a snake or venom in general.<BR>2 A bundle of grass, or hay.<BR>3 Measure in general.<BR>E.<BR>गर poison, &c. and ल what gets or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरलिन्
गरलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Venomous, poisonous.<BR>E.<BR>गरल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरागरी
गरागरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus): see खरा and गरी; also अगरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरात्मक|गरात्मकं
गरात्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The seed of the Śobhāñjana or Morunga.<BR>E.<BR>गर poison, and आत्मक nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गराधिका
गराधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lac, the animal red dye so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरिमन्
गरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Weight, heaviness.<BR>2 Venerableness.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरिष्ठ|गरिष्ठः
गरिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Heaviest, excessively heavy.<BR>2 Very venerable.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु heavy, इष्ठच् superlative affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरीयस्
गरीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Heaviest, very heavy.<BR>2 Highly venerable.<BR>3 Worst.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, affix ईयसुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुड|गरुडः
गरुड<BR>m. (डः)<BR>The bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU; he is generally represented as a being something between a man and a bird, and considered as sovereign of the feathered race; he is the son of KAŚYAPA and VINATĀ, and younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>गरुत् a wing, डी to fly, affix ड, and the त of the noun dropped, who flies like a bird, or गृ to moisten, and उडच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडध्वज|गरुडध्वजः
गरुडध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>गरुड, and ध्वज a symbol; whose symbol is GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडरुत
गरुडरुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of metre having four lines to the stanza, and sixteen syllables to each line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाग्रज|गरुडाग्रजः
गरुडाग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>गरुड, and अग्रज elder born; the elder brother of GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाङ्कित|गरुडांकित|गरुडाङ्कितं
गरुडाङ्कित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>गरुड GARUḌA, and अङ्किय marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडाश्मन्
गरुडाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>गरुड, and अश्मान् a stone: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुडोत्तीर्ण|गरुडोत्तीर्णं|गरुडोत्तीर्ण्ण
गरुडोत्तीर्ण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The emerald.<BR>E.<BR>गरुत, and उत्तीर्ण passed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुत्
गरुत्<BR>m. (-रुत्)<BR>A wing.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to moisten, and उति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुत्मत्|गरुत्मन्त्
गरुत्मत्<BR>m. (-त्मान्)<BR>1 The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>गरुत् a wing, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गरुद्योधिन्
गरुद्योधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A quail.<BR>E.<BR>गरुत् a wing, and योधिन् who fights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ग|गर्गः
गर्ग<BR>m. (-र्ग)<BR>One of the ten principal Munis or saints, a son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (गर्गी)<BR>Wife of GARGA.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to sprinkle, ग Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गर|गर्गरः
गर्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora, HAM)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A churn.<BR>2 A water vessel, a guglet.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ग an imitative sound, a guggling, and र what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गाट|गर्गाटः
गर्गाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=283" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्गीय
गर्गीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>A descendant of GARGA.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ग, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्घ
गर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (गर्घति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज|गर्जः|गर्ज्ज|गर्ज्जं
गर्ज<BR>r. 10th cl. (गर्जयति)<BR>To sound.<BR>r. 1st cl. (गर्जति)<BR>To emit a deep or full sound, to sound as distant thunder, to roar as a lion, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज|गर्जः|गर्ज्ज|गर्ज्जं
गर्ज<BR>n. (-र्जं)<BR>1 The roaring of elephants.<BR>2 The grumbling of clouds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to roar or growl, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जक|गर्जकः|गर्ज्जक|गर्ज्जकः
गर्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fish, commonly Gajar.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to grumble, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जन|गर्जनं|गर्ज्जन|गर्ज्जनं
गर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>2 Passion, wrath.<BR>3 Excessive indignation.<BR>4 Reproach, menace.<BR>5 War, battle, conflict.<BR>6 The grumbling of clouds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to grumble or roar, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जनीय
गर्जनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be sounded or roared.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to sound, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जर|गर्ज्जर|गर्ज्जरं
गर्जर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जि|गर्जिः|गर्ज्जिः
गर्जि<BR>m. (-र्जिः)<BR>The muttering of clouds or distant thunder.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to sound as thunder, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्जित|गर्जितः|गर्ज्जितं
गर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, roared, bellowed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant in rut.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The muttering of clouds or rolling of distant thunder.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to roar, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ज्य
गर्ज्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ज्यः-र्ज्या-र्ज्यं)<BR>To be roared or sounded.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ज to sound, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्त्त|गर्त|गर्तं|गर्तः|गर्त्तः
गर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 A hole in general.<BR>2 The hollow of the loins.<BR>3 The name of a country; also त्रिगर्त्त, in the north-west of India.<BR>4 A kind of disease.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to drop, Uṇādi affix तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्त्तिका|गर्तिका
गर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A weaver's workshop.<BR>E.<BR>गर्त्त a hole, affix ठन्, the weaver sits at his loom with his feet in a hollow or hole below. the level of the floor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द|गर्द्द
गर्द<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (गर्दति गर्दंयति)<BR>To sound, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभ|गर्दभ|गर्दभः|गर्द्दभं|गर्द्दभः
गर्द्दभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Smell, odour.<BR>2 An ass.<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>1 A she-ass.<BR>2 An insect, a kind of beetle springing from cow dung.<BR>3 A disease of the skin, eruption of round, red, and painful spots; also गर्दभिका.<BR>4 A creeper, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्द to sound, Uṇādi affix अभच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाजिन
गर्द्दभाजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The skin or hide of an ass.<BR>E.<BR>गर्द्दभ, and अजिन a skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभशाक|गर्दभशाक|गर्द्दभशाकः
गर्द्दभशाक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A plant, (Ovieda verticellata.)<BR>E.<BR>गर्द्दभ an ass, and शाक a vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाण्ड|गर्दभाण्ड|गर्दभांड|गर्दभाण्डः|गर्द्दभाण्डः
गर्द्दभाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of tree, commonly Pārspīpal, (Hibiscus populneoides)<BR>E.<BR>गर्द्दभ smell, अम to go, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभाह्वय|गर्दभाह्वय|गर्द्दभाह्वयः
गर्द्दभाह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्द्दभ smell, and आह्वय an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्दभिका|गर्दभिका
गर्द्दभिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cutaneous disease, a blotch, an eruption.<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form added to गर्द्धभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्ध
गर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>1 Eagerness, greediness.<BR>2 The Pārspīpal: see गर्द्धभाण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to desire, to be greedy, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्धन
गर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Covetous, greedy.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to be greedy, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्द्धिन्
गर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>Greedy, covetous.<BR>E.<BR>गर्द्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ध|गर्द्धः|गर्धः
गर्ध<BR>r. 10th cl. (गर्धयति)<BR>To desire or covet: see गृध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्ब|गर्ब|गर्ब्बः
गर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (गर्ब्बति)<BR>To move, to go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्ब|गर्ब|गर्ब्बः
गर्ब्ब<BR>m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>Pride, haughtiness.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ब्ब to be proud, अच् affix; also read गर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ब्भ
गर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>A foetus, &c.: see the next.<BR>f. (-र्ब्भा)<BR>Interval of time, division of time or place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भ|गर्भः
गर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 A foetus or embryo.<BR>2 A child.<BR>3 The belly.<BR>4 The inside, the middle.<BR>5 Joining, union.<BR>6 The rough coat of the fruit of the Jaka.<BR>7 An inner apartment, a lying-in chamber.<BR>8 Any interior chamber, the adytum of a temple, &c.<BR>9 The bed of the Ganges, when the river is fullest; that is, on the fourteenth day of the dark half of the month Bhādra, or in the height of the rains; as high as the river flows at this period, so far extends the Garbha, after which the Tīra or proper bank begins, and extends for 150 cubits; this space is holy ground.<BR>10 The calyx of the lotus. The interior or inner part of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to drop, or गॄ to swallow, Uṇādi affix भन्; also read गर्ब्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भक|गर्भकं|गर्भकः
गर्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chaplet of flowers, &c. worn in the hair.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A period of a day and two nights.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भकर|गर्भकरः
गर्भकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Impregnating, fecundatory, procreative, producing impregnation.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Nagelia putranjiva.)<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भकोश|गर्भकोशः
गर्भकोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The uterus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and कोश sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भगृह
गर्भगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>1 An inner chamber.<BR>2 A lying-in chamber.<BR>3 The sanctuary or adytum of a temple.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भग्रहण
गर्भग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Conception, impregnation.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भघातिन्
गर्भघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Producing abortion.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and घातिन् what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भचलन
गर्भचलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Quickening, motion of the foetus in utero.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and चलन moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भच्युत
गर्भच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bearing a child.<BR>2 Miscarrying.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ and च्युत falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भच्युति|गर्भच्युतिः
गर्भच्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Birth, delivery.<BR>2 Miscarriage.<BR>E.<BR>गर्म, and च्युति falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भण्ड|गर्भंड|गर्भंडः|गर्भण्डः
गर्भण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Enlargement of the navel.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the belly, and अण्ड an egg, the penultimate made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भद|गर्भदः
गर्भद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Impregnating, procreative.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A tree, (Nagelia putranjiva.)<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A shrub so called.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ a foetus, and द what gives, with reference to the supposed virtue of the plant; also गर्भदातृ (-ता-त्री-तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भद्रुह्
गर्भद्रुह्<BR>mfn. (-द्रुक् or द्रुट्)<BR>Causing abortion.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and द्रुह what injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भधारण
गर्भधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Impregnation, gestation.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and धारण holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भनाडी
गर्भनाडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>The umbilical cord.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and नाडी a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपरिस्रव|गर्भपरिस्रवः
गर्भपरिस्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Secundines.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and परिस्रव what exudes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपाकिन्
गर्भपाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>Rice ripening after two months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातक|गर्भपातकः
गर्भपातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Producing abortion.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A red kind of morunga.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the foetus, पत to fall, in the causal form, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातन|गर्भपातनः
गर्भपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Producing abortion.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Any plant or drug supposed to have that effect.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and पातन causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपातिन्
गर्भपातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Producing abortion.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of potherb: see विशल्या.<BR>E.<BR>as in the last, affixes णिनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=284" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भपोषण
गर्भपोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Gestation.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and पोषण nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भरूप|गर्भरूपः
गर्भरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>A child, an infant.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ an embryo, and रूप form; also गर्भरूपकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भवती
गर्भवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A pregnant female.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ a foetus, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भशङ्कु|गर्भशंकु|गर्भशङ्कुः
गर्भशङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A kind of vectis or instrument for extracting the dead foetus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and शङ्क, a probe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भशय्या
गर्भशय्या<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>The uterus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and शय्या a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्थ
गर्भस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Situated in the womb.<BR>2 Centrical, internal, within the centre of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and स्थ what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्राव|गर्भस्रावः
गर्भस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Abortion, miscarriage.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the embryo, and स्राव expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भस्राविन्
गर्भस्राविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Producing or occasioning abortion.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and स्राविन् what causes to issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भागार|गर्भागारं
गर्भागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 An inner and private room, the female apartments, the lying-in chamber.<BR>2 The sanctuary of a temple, the chamber where the object of worship is placed.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the foetus, and आगार an abode, hence it is also applied to the womb: see गर्भाशय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाधान|गर्भाधानं
गर्भाधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A ceremony performed prior to conception.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the embryo, and आधान taking, being supposed conducive to future impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाशय|गर्भाशयः
गर्भाशय<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>The womb, the uterus.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the embryo, and आशय asylum or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भाष्टम|गर्भाष्टमः
गर्भाष्टम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The eighth month of uterine gestation.<BR>2 The eighth year reckoning from conception.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the foetus, and अष्टम eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिणी
गर्भिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A pregnant woman.<BR>2 A plant, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ embryo, and इनि poss. affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भिण्यवेक्षण|गर्भिण्यवेक्षणं
गर्भिण्यवेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Midwifery, attendance and care of pregnant women and new born infants.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भिणी, and अवेक्षण care, looking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्भोपघातिनी
गर्भोपघातिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A cow (or female), miscarrying from going unseasonably.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ the foetus, उप intensitive prefix, हन to destroy, affixes णिनि and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्म्मुटिका|गर्मुटिका
गर्म्मुटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A species of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्म्मुत्|गर्मुत्
गर्म्मुत्<BR>f. (-म्मुत्)<BR>1 A kind of grass.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 A reed.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, &c. Uṇādi affix उति, and म inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्व|गर्व|गर्वः|गर्व्वः
गर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (गर्व्वति)<BR>To be proud or haughty;<BR>also (ङ) गर्व्वङ् r. 10th cl. (गर्व्वयते)<BR>To grow proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्व|गर्व|गर्वः|गर्व्वः
गर्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>गर्व्व to be proud, affix अच् or गॄ swallow, &c. and व Uṇādi affix; this word is sometimes written गर्ब्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वर|गर्वर
गर्व्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Proud, haughty, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to reject, &c. Uṇādi affix स्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वाट|गर्वाट|गर्वाटः|गर्व्वाटः
गर्व्वाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A watchman, a doorkeeper, a sort of village constable, a headborough or beadle.<BR>E.<BR>गर्व्व pride, अट to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्व्वित|गर्वित|गर्व्वितः
गर्व्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>2 Conceited.<BR>E.<BR>गर्व्व pride, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह
गर्ह<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (गर्हति-ते गर्हयति)<BR>To blame, to censure, to despise or contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हण|गर्हणं
गर्हण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Censuring, censure, blame, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ह to reprove, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हणीय
गर्हणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Censurable, contemptible, vile, bad.<BR>E.<BR>गह to abuse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हा
गर्हा<BR>f. (-र्हा)<BR>Abuse, censure, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ह to revile, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्हित|गर्हितं
गर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blamed, censured.<BR>2 Contemned, despised.<BR>3 Bad, vile.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ह to blame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्य|गर्ह्यः
गर्ह्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं)<BR>Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ह to abuse, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गर्ह्यवादिन्
गर्ह्यवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking ill, speaking vilely or inaccurately.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ह्य vile, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल|गलः
गल<BR>r. 1st cl. (गलति)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To ooze;<BR>also (ङ्) गलङ् r. 10th cl. (गलयते)<BR>To drop, to ooze or distil.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>To fall, to fall down or off;<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To go, to approach.<BR>2 To bear or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल|गलः
गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The throat.<BR>2 The resin of the Sal tree.<BR>3 A reed, a large kind of the Saccharum cylindricum.<BR>4 A rope.<BR>5 A musical instrument.<BR>6 A kind of fish, a small kind of cyprinus, a subgenus of that class, (Cyprinus garra, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>गल to eat, to drop, &c. affix अच्, or गॄ to swallow, with अच्, गर, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलक|गलकः
गलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of fish.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलकम्बल|गलकंबल|गलकम्बलः
गलकम्बल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bull's dewlap.<BR>E.<BR>गल the neck, and कम्बल a soft substance as a blanket, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलगण्ड|गलगंड|गलगण्डः
गलगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Inflammation, enlargement of the glands of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and गण्ड a swelling or boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलग्रह|गलग्रहः
गलग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A sauce of fish ground up with salt, pepper, Ghee, &c.<BR>2 A day on which a course of study is commenced, but immediately preceding a day on which study is prohibited.<BR>3 The fourth lunation of the dark fortnight, the seventh, eighth, and ninth, the thirteenth and three days following.<BR>4 Seizing any one by the throat, throttling, choking^1.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and ग्रह what takes, &c.; also गलग्रहण.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलत्
गलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Falling, dropping.<BR>2 Oozing, trickling, flowing.<BR>3 Melting.<BR>E.<BR>गल to flow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन|गलनं
गलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Melting, fusing.<BR>2 Trickling, dropping, oozing.<BR>3 Falling down or off.<BR>4 Leaking.<BR>E.<BR>गल to drop, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलनीय
गलनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fusible, liquefiable, to be melted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गल to melt, अनीयर् affix; also गलितव्य and गल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलन्तिका|गलंतिका
गलन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A small pitcher.<BR>2 A small water jar with a small hole in the bottom, from which the water drops upon a Liṅga or Tulasi plant, placed beneath.<BR>E.<BR>गड to drop, affix झच्, गडन्ति; कन् in the fem. form added, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलमेखला
गलमेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A thread worn round the neck, a necklace.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलव्रत|गलव्रतः
गलव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, व्रत holy observance; also the same as गरव्रत q. v. ल being substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलशुण्डिका|गलशुंडिका
गलशुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The uvula or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and शुण्डिका the elephant's trunk, resembling it in being a pendulous, roundish, and fleshy substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलस्तनी
गलस्तनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A she goat.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and लन the breast; some species of the Bengal goat have small fleshy processes, resembling nipples depending from the throat; also गलेस्तनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलहस्त|गलहस्तः
गलहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>Throttling.<BR>E.<BR>गल, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=285" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाङ्कुर|गलांकुर|गलाङ्कुरः
गलाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A disease of the throat, inflammation of the fauces, and enlargement of the tonsils.<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, and अङ्कुर a new sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलाविल
गलाविल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A prawn or shrimp: see गङ्गाटेय. Some books read this गलानिल, and others गलानिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलि|गलिः
गलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A strong and lazy ox.<BR>E.<BR>गल to eat, and इन् affix; who is good for nothing but eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलित|गलितः
गलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fallen, dropped.<BR>2 Liquefied, melted.<BR>3 Distilled, oozing, flowing.<BR>4 Decayed, impaired.<BR>5 Lost, deprived.<BR>6 Untied, loosed.<BR>E.<BR>गल to drop, to ooze, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितकुष्ठ
गलितकुष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Advanced and incurable leprosy, when the fingers and toes fall off.<BR>E.<BR>गलित, and कुष्ठ leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितदन्त
गलितदन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Toothless.<BR>E.<BR>गलित, and दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनख
गलितनख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>Having no nails.<BR>E.<BR>गलित, and नख the nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलितनयन
गलितनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Blind.<BR>E.<BR>गलित, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेगण्ड|गलेगंड|गलेगंडः|गलेगण्डः
गलेगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of bird, (the Adjutant or Ardea argala.)<BR>E.<BR>गल the throat, in the seventh case, and गण्ड a boil; alluding to a pendulous fleshy purse hanging from the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलेस्तनी
गलेस्तनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A she goat: see गलस्तनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गलू
गलू<BR>m. (-लूः)<BR>A sort of gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ<BR>r. 1st cl. (गल्भते)<BR>To be bold or confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्भ
गल्भ<BR>mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं)<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>2 Confident, bold, audacious.<BR>E.<BR>गल्भ to be proud, &c. अच् affix, more commonly प्रगल्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्या
गल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A multitude of throats.<BR>2 A quantity of a kind of grass, or ropes made of it.<BR>E.<BR>गल a throat, &c. य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ल|गल्लः
गल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>The cheek.<BR>E.<BR>गल to eat, and ल affix; from ला to get or receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्लचातुरी
गल्लचातुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A small round pillow to put underneath the cheek.<BR>E.<BR>गल्ल the cheek, and चातुर a pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्वर्क|गल्वर्कः
गल्वर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 A goblet, a vessel for drinking spirituous liquor.<BR>2 Lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>गल to drop, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गल्ह
गल्ह<BR>r. 1st cl. (गल्हते)<BR>To blame, to censure or despise: see गर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवय|गवयः
गवय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A species of ox, the Gayal, erroneously classed by Hindu writers amongst the kinds of deer, (Bos gavaeus.)<BR>2 A monkey chief: the son of VAIVASVATA.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The female Gayal.<BR>E.<BR>गु to sound, and अय affix, form irregular; or गो a cow, and य from या to obtain, affix ड, resembling a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवराज|गवराजः
गवराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, affix अण्, गव relating to a cow, and राजन् king, chief; the more direct compound makes गोराज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवल|गवलं|गवलः
गवल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wild buffalo.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Buffalo's horn.<BR>E.<BR>गु to sound, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्ष|गवाक्षः
गवाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 An air hole, a loop hole, a round window, a bull's eye, &c.<BR>2 A monkey chief; one of the sons of VAIVASVATA.<BR>E.<BR>गो a ray of light, अक्ष to spread, affix घञ्, or गो an ox, and अक्ष an eye; ox-eyed.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>2 A plant, (Clitoria ternatea): see अपराजिता.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, अक्ष to spread, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाक्षजाल
गवाक्षजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A lattice, a jealousie, trellis-work^1.<BR>E.<BR>गवाक्ष, and जाल a net.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाची
गवाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A fish, (Macrognathus pancalus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवादन|गवादनं
गवादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pasture or meadow grass.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A hay rack, a trough for holding grass out of which cattle feed.<BR>2 A species of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus, or, according to some, C. coloquintida.)<BR>3 A plant, (Clitoria ternatea): see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, अदन food, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवालूक|गवालूकः
गवालूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Gayal, (Bos gavaeus): see गवय.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, लोक to see, with आङ् prefixed, deriv. irr; in appearance a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाशन|गवाशनः
गवाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>गव, and अशन who eats, eating beef.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाषिका
गवाषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lac, the dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवाह्निक
गवाह्निक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A day's feed for a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and अह्निक daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवीश्वर|गवीश्वरः
गवीश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Owner of kine.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, ईश्वर a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेडु|गवेडुः
गवेडु<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>f. (-डुः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Coix barbata.)<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow or the earth, ण्ड to preserve, उ affix, or with कन् added गवेडुका; also गवेधु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेधु|गवेधुः
गवेधु<BR>f. (-धुः)<BR>Coix barbata: see the preceding; also with कन् added गवेधुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेरुक|गवेरुकं
गवेरुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>गो light or colour, ईर to send, affix वुन्, and the penultimate changed to उ irregularly; also read गवेधुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेशका
गवेशका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेष|गवेषः
गवेष<BR>r. 10th cl. (गवेषयति)<BR>1 To seek, to hunt for, to search or inquire.<BR>2 To make an effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषण|गवेषणं
गवेषण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Research, inquiry after any thing, (physical or philosophical, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>गवेष to inquire, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवेषित|गवेषितं
गवेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sought, inquired for.<BR>E.<BR>गवेष to search or hunt, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गवोद्घ|गवोद्घः
गवोद्घ<BR>m. (-द्घः)<BR>An excellent cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and उद्घ implying excellence; the compound remains masculine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्य|गव्यं
गव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 (Of or belonging to a cow, as milk, curds, &c.)<BR>2 Proper or fit for cattle.<BR>nf. (-व्यं-व्या)<BR>A bowstring.<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>1 A multitude of cows.<BR>2 A measure of two Kos: see गव्यूति.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A colouring substance, a yellow pigment or dye.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, &c. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूत|गव्यूतं
गव्यूत<BR>nf. (-तं)<BR>1 A Kos, a measure of length equal to 4000 cubits.<BR>2 A measure of two Kos: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गव्यूति|गव्यूतिः
गव्यूति<BR>mf. (-तिः)<BR>A measure of two Kos, a league measured by 2000 Dands or fathoms.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, यु to join, क्तिन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह<BR>r. 10th cl. (गहयति)<BR>To be thick or impervious as a forest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह
गह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A cave.<BR>2 A forest.<BR>E.<BR>गह to be impervious, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहन|गहनं|गहनः
गहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Impervious, inaccessible.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A wood, a thicket.<BR>2 A cave.<BR>3 Pain, distress.<BR>E.<BR>गाह to tremble, &c. affix युच्, and the radical vowel made short; or गह to be thick, affix as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गहीय
गहीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to a cave or a thicket, deep, difficult of access, impervious.<BR>E.<BR>गह a thicket, छ^1 aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गह्वर|गह्वरं|गह्वरः
गह्वर<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>A cave, a cavern, a grotto, a recess in a rock or mountain, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A thicket, a wood.<BR>2 Hypocrisy.<BR>3 Weeping, crying, but not violently.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An arbour, a bower.<BR>E.<BR>गाह to be agitated, and ष्वरच् Uṇādi affix, the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=286" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा<BR>r. 1st cl. (ङ) गाङ् (गाते)<BR>To go, to go to or towards.<BR>r. 3rd cl. but restricted to the Vedas (जगाति)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गा
गा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A verse or metrical composition.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, क and टाप् affix: see ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्ग|गांग|गाङ्गं|गाङ्गः
गाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the river Ganges.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the GAṄGĀ, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गट|गांगट|गांगटः|गाङ्गटः
गाङ्गट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A prawn or shrimp.<BR>E.<BR>गाङ्ग relating to the Ganges, and अट what goes, form irr.; also गाङ्गाट or with कन् affix गाङ्गटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गटेय|गांगटेय|गांगटेयः|गाङ्गटेयः
गाङ्गटेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A shrimp or prawn.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा, अट to go, and ढक् affix; also गङ्गाटेय, and गाङ्काट, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गायनि|गांगायनि|गांगायनिः|गाङ्गायनिः
गाङ्गायनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>2 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the personified river, (as the wife of ŚANTANU, in the first instance, and mother of the hero; and in the second, as the receiver of KĀRTTIKEYA the son of ŚIVA, from AGNI, the god of fire,) and फिञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेय|गांगेय|गाङ्गेयं|गाङ्गेयः
गाङ्गेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 BHĪṢMA.<BR>2 KĀRTTIKEYA: see the preceding.<BR>3 The Hilsa or Illias fish, (Clupanodon ilisha, HAM.)<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A grass: see कशेरु.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>गङ्गा the Ganges, ढक् affix of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेरुकी
गाङ्गेरुकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides, but it is variously described.)<BR>E.<BR>गाङ्ग Ganges water, ईर to go or grow, उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गेष्ठी
गाङ्गेष्ठी<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>A plant, (Guilandina bonducella.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाङ्गौघ
गाङ्गौघ<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>The current of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>गाङ्ग Gangetic, and ओघ heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाञ्जिकाय|गांजिकाय|गांजिकायः|गाञ्जिकायः
गाञ्जिकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढ|गाढं
गाढ<BR>adv. n. (-ढं) adj. mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Excessive, much, very much, heavy, oppressive, &c.<BR>2 Firm, strong.<BR>3 Hard.<BR>4 Close.<BR>E.<BR>गाह to agitate, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढता
गाढता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Firmness, hardness.<BR>2 Excess.<BR>E.<BR>गाढ, and तल् affix; also with त्व, गाढत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाढमुष्ठि
गाढमुष्ठि<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठिः-ष्ठिः-ष्ठि)<BR>Miserly, niggard, avaricious, closefisted.<BR>m. (-ष्ठिः)<BR>A scymitar, a large sacrificial knife.<BR>E.<BR>गाढ heavy or close, and मुष्ठि gripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत
गाणपत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Relating to GAṆEŚA, or the leader of a troop, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गणपति, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणपत्य|गाणपत्यः
गाणपत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-ती-त्यं)<BR>Relating to GAṆAPATI or GAṆEŚA.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A worshipper of him.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Worship of him.<BR>2 Chieftainship, presidency.<BR>E.<BR>गणपति, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाणिक्य|गाणिक्यं
गाणिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>An assembly of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>गणिका a whore, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डिव|गांडिव|गांडिवं|गांडिवः|गाण्डिवः
गाण्डिव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 The bow of ARJUNA.<BR>2 Any bow; also गाण्डीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीव|गांडीव|गांडीवं|गांडीवः|गाण्डीवः
गाण्डीव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 The bow of ARJUNA.<BR>2 Any bow.<BR>E.<BR>गाण्डि what affects the cheek, from गण्ड with इञ् affix, then व added, and इ final lengthened; or continuing short, गाण्डिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाण्डीविन्|गांडीविन्
गाण्डीविन्<BR>m. (-बी)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>गाण्डीव ARJUNA'S bow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातु|गातुः
गातु<BR>mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु)<BR>Angry, wrathful.<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 A Gandharba or celestial quirister.<BR>2 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A large black bee.<BR>4 A singer.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, Uṇādi affix तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गातृ
गातृ<BR>mf. (-ता-त्री)<BR>A male or female singer.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्र|गात्रं
गात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 The fore quarter of an elephant.<BR>3 A limb, a member.<BR>E.<BR>गभ to go, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi affix, the radical final is rejected, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रभङ्गा
गात्रभङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>गात्र the body, and भङ्गा what breaks or hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रमार्जनी|गात्रमार्ज्जनी
गात्रमार्जनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A towel.<BR>E.<BR>गात्र, and मार्जनी a wiper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रसङ्कोचिन्|गात्रसंकोचिन्
गात्रसङ्कोचिन्<BR>m. (-ची)<BR>The pole-cat, (Viverra putorius.)<BR>E.<BR>गात्र the body, and सङ्कोचिन् who draws up or contracts in order to spring upon prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रसम्प्लव|गात्रसंप्लव|गात्रसंप्लवः
गात्रसम्प्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A small bird, the diver.<BR>E.<BR>गात्र the body, and सम्प्लव who plunges, from सम् entirely, प्लुङ् to go, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रानुलेपनी
गात्रानुलेपनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Fragrant unguents, &c. smeared upon the body, perfume for the person.<BR>E.<BR>गात्र the body, अनु upon, लिप to plaster or smear, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गात्रोत्सादन
गात्रोत्सादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning the person with perfumes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गात्र, and उत्सादन cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथक|गाथकः
गाथक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A musician, a singer.<BR>2 A chaunter of the Purāṇas or sacred poems.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, स्थकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथा
गाथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>1 A verse, a stanza.<BR>2 Metre, rhythm.<BR>3 A song, a chaunt or verse to be chaunted or sung.<BR>4 Prākṛta or any language not Sanscrit.<BR>6 The same as the Arya Metre, in which the verse contains sixty syllabic instants, variously arranged.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, थन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथाकार|गाथाकारः
गाथाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A singer, a reciter.<BR>E.<BR>गाथा, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाथिक|गाथिकः
गाथिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who recites Gāthas, verses or hymns.<BR>E.<BR>गाथा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध|गाधः
गाध<BR>(ऋ) गाधृ r. 1st cl. (गधते)<BR>1 To stand, to stay, to remain.<BR>2 To seek, to search or inquire for.<BR>3 To compile, string or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाध|गाधः
गाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Not very deep.<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Place, site.<BR>2 Desire of gain, cupidity, covetousness.<BR>3 Bottom, soundings.<BR>E.<BR>गाध to stand, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधि|गाधिः
गाधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The name of a king, sovereign of Kanyakubja, father of VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिज|गाधिजः
गाधिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of the celebrated saint VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR>E.<BR>गाधि as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिपुर|गाधिपुरं
गाधिपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Kanyakubja the ancient Kanouj.<BR>E.<BR>गाधि a proper name, and पुर a city; the capital of GĀDHI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधिभू
गाधिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The saint VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR>E.<BR>गाधि, and भू born, the son of GĀDHI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाधेय|गाधेयः
गाधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR>E.<BR>गाधि, and ढक् patronymick affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान|गानं
गान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Singing, song in general, or a song.<BR>2 Sound.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानिनी
गानिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Orris root.<BR>E.<BR>गान song, इनि and ङीप् affixes; supposed to be of use in clearing the voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गानीय
गानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Musical.<BR>E.<BR>गान and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्तु|गांतुः|गान्तुः
गान्तु<BR>mfn. (-न्तुः-न्तुः-न्तु)<BR>A goer, a traveller, one who goes or moves.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, Uṇādi affix तु, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्त्री|गांत्री
गान्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>A carriage drawn by oxen.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, ष्ट्रन् affix, fem. do. ङीष्, and the pen. made long; also गन्त्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=287" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिनी|गांदिनी
गान्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The river Ganges, or the goddess GAṄGĀ.<BR>2 The mother of AKRŪRA.<BR>E.<BR>गो paradise, in the accusative case, द who gives, इनि, and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्दिनीसुत|गांदिनीसुत|गान्दिनीसुतः
गान्दिनीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪṢMA, &c.<BR>2 AKRŪRA.<BR>E.<BR>गान्दिनी GAṄGĀ, and सुत a son: see गङ्गासुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धर्ब्ब
गान्धर्ब्ब<BR>mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बी-र्ब्बं-)<BR>Relating or belonging to a Gandharba.<BR>m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>A heavenly quirister: see गन्धर्ब्ब.<BR>n. (-र्ब्बं)<BR>1 Song, singing.<BR>2 A form of marriage, that which requires only mutual and amorous agreement.<BR>E.<BR>गन्धर्ब्ब a Gandharba, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धार|गांधार|गान्धारं|गांधारः|गान्धारः
गान्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of the seven primary notes of music.<BR>2 Minium or red lead.<BR>3 A country, (Kandahar, between the north of India and Persia.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The wife of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA, mother of DURYODHANA.<BR>2 One of the tutelary female deities of the Jainas.<BR>3 A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>4 Prickly nightshade.<BR>E.<BR>गान्ध the aggregate of गन्ध smell, &c. ऋ to go, and अण् affix; the note being said to be produced by pure and fragrant breath, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धारेय|गांधारेय|गांधारेयः|गान्धारेयः
गान्धारेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of DURYODHANA, the son of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>गान्धारी the name of the mother of this chief, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गान्धिक|गांधिक|गांधिकः|गान्धिकः
गान्धिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A scribe, a clerk.<BR>2 A vender of perfumes, a perfumer.<BR>3 A kind of worm, having a strong fetid smell.<BR>E.<BR>गन्ध smell, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गामुक|गामुकः
गामुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं)<BR>Going, locomotive.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाम्भीर्य्य|गाम्भीर्य|गांभीर्य|गांभीर्यं|गाम्भीर्य्यं
गाम्भीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Depth, (of water, sound, &c.)<BR>2 The deep sound of the voice of a Jaina saint, like distant thunder or the muttering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>गम्भीर deep, affix ष्यञ् or ज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायक|गायकः
गायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Singing, one who sings.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A singer.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्
गायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Singing.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्रिन्
गायत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A tree that yields the resin formerly called Terra Japonica, (Mimosa catechu); also गायत्री fem. noun, as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायत्री
गायत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A measure of verse in the Vedas, a stanza usually of twenty-four syllables, variously arranged, but most commonly in three lines.<BR>2 A sacred verse from the Vedas to be recited only mentally; this is usually personified and considered as a goddess, the wife of BRAHMĀ; the metaphorical mother of the three first classes, in their capacity of twice born, investiture with the sacred and distinguishing string, &c. being regarded as a new birth; there is but one Gāyatrī of the Vedas, but according to the system of the Tāntrikas, a number of mystical verses are called Gāyatrīs; each deity has one in particular.<BR>3 A kind of mimosa, (M. catechu): see the preceding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गायन् who sings, and त्रै to preserve, affixes क and ङीष्; this applies especially to the mystical verse, the repetition of which is necessary for salvation; the word is also written गायत्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गायन|गायनः
गायन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Singing, a singer.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A singer.<BR>2 A chatterer, a gossip.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Singing.<BR>2 Professing or practising singing as a livelihood.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारित्र|गारित्रं
गारित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Rice, grain, corn.<BR>E.<BR>ग to swallow, Uṇādi affix णित्रन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुड|गारुडं|गारुडः
गारुड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A Mantra or charm against poison.<BR>3 An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>गरुड the vehicle of VIṢṆU, and अण् affix; of or relating to GARUḌA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडिक|गारुडिकः
गारुडिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A charmer, a dealer in antidotes.<BR>E.<BR>गारुड the mantra of GARUḌA, or a charm against venom, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुडी
गारुडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>Hog-weed, (Boerhavia diffusa alata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गारुत्मत्
गारुत्मत्<BR>n. (-त्)<BR>The emerald.<BR>E.<BR>गरुत्मत् GARUḌA, and अण् affix; derived from or relating to GARUḌA; the gem is supposed to be generated from his voided phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्ग|गार्ग|गार्गः
गार्ग्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्गः-र्ग्गी-र्ग्गं)<BR>Descended from the age GARGA.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ग्ग, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गक|गार्गकः|गार्ग्गक
गार्गक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of the descendants of the saint GARGA.<BR>E.<BR>गार्ग a descendant of GARGA, and वुञ् affix of multitude; also with ठञ्, गार्गिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्गीपुत्रकायनि|गार्ग्गीपुत्रकायनि
गार्गीपुत्रकायनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A descendant of the son of GĀRGĪ.<BR>E.<BR>गार्गी the wife of the saint GARGA, पुत्र a son, and फिञ् affix, कुक् augment; also without the augment गार्ग्गीपुत्रायनि, or with इञ् affix, गार्ग्गीपुत्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्ग्ग्य
गार्ग्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्ग्यः-र्ग्ग्यी-र्ग्ग्यं)<BR>Descended from GARGA, son, daughter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गर्ग्ग, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध
गार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं)<BR>1 Derived from a vulture.<BR>2 Greedy.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 Desire, greediness, cupidity.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>गृध greedy, affix अण् or गृध्र with अण् affix, and र rejected optionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्धपक्ष
गार्द्धपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>गार्द्ध, and पक्ष a wing; formed with vulture's feathers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्धपत्र
गार्द्धपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>as before, पत्र a leaf, a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध्य
गार्द्ध्य<BR>n. (-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>1 Greediness.<BR>2 Desire.<BR>E.<BR>गृध greedy, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्ध
गार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं)<BR>Derived from a vulture.<BR>E.<BR>गृध्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्द्धपक्ष
गार्द्धपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>गार्द्ध, and पक्ष a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भ
गार्भ<BR>mfn. (-र्भः-र्भी-र्भं)<BR>1 Uterine, fœtal.<BR>2 Relating to conception, (any act or ceremony, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>गर्भ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिक
गार्भिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Foetal, uterine.<BR>2 Relating to or connected with gestation or the foetus in utero.<BR>E.<BR>गभ, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण|गार्भिणं
गार्भिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A number of pregnant women.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भिणी a pregnant woman, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्भिण्य|गार्भिण्यं
गार्भिण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>An assembly of pregnant women.<BR>E.<BR>गर्भिणी as above, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हपत्य|गार्हपत्यः
गार्हपत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A sacred fire perpetually maintained by a householder, received from his father, and transmitted to his descendants, and from which fires for sacrificial purposes are lighted.<BR>E.<BR>गृहपति a householder, (from गृह a house, and पति master,) and ज्य referential aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गार्हस्थ्य|गार्हस्थ्यं
गार्हस्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>The order or estate of a householder.<BR>E.<BR>गृहस्थ, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाल|गालः
गाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Flowing, liquefying.<BR>2 Flowing, dropping.<BR>3 A flux.<BR>E.<BR>गल to flow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालन|गालनं
गालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Straining fluids.<BR>2 Fusing, liquefying, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गल् to flow, causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालव|गालवः
गालव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A tree, the bark of which is used in dying, Lodh, (Symplocus racemosa, Rox.)<BR>2 A pale species of the same: see लोध्र.<BR>3 A kind of ebony; also केन्दुक, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>4 A particular Muni or saint, a disciple of VIŚVĀMITRA. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">Page289</a>]<BR>E.<BR>गाल flux, and ब what prevents; referring to the astringent qualities of the Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=288" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालि|गालिः
गालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A curse, execration or imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>गल in the causal form, to cause to drop, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालित|गालितः
गालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Melted, fused.<BR>2 Strained.<BR>3 Distilled, dropped.<BR>E.<BR>गल to drop, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालिन्
गालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Fusing, liquefying.<BR>2 Distilling.<BR>3 Abusive, abusing.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A particular gesticulation or Madrā.<BR>E.<BR>गल to flow, causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गालोड्य|गालोड्यं
गालोड्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>The seed of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाह|गाहः
गाह<BR>(ऊ) गाहू r. 1st cl. (गाहते)<BR>1 To churn, to stir or agitate.<BR>2 To penetrate.<BR>3 To destroy.<BR>With अव or वि prefixed,<BR>To bathe, to perform ablutions.<BR>With वि,<BR>To shake, to agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहित
गाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, trembling.<BR>2 Destroyed.<BR>3 Plunged into, immersed.<BR>E.<BR>गाह to agitate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गाहितृ
गाहितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Shaking, agitating.<BR>2 Destroying, a destroyer.<BR>3 One who plunges into water, bathes, dives, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गाह to agitate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिर्
गिर्<BR>f. (-गीः)<BR>1 Speech, speaking.<BR>2 A name of SARASVATĪ the goddess of speech.<BR>3 Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to sound, affix क्विप्, ॠ is changed to इर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरण
गिरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Swallowing.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरा
गिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Speech.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to sound, क, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरि|गिरिः
गिरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Venerable, respectable, worshipful.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A mountain, a hill.<BR>2 A wooden ball with which children play.<BR>3 A disease of the eyes.<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 Swallowing.<BR>2 A small rat, a mouse.<BR>3 A title given to one order of the Dāsnāmī Gosains.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, &c. इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकण्टक|गिरिकंटक|गिरिकण्टकः
गिरिकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and कण्टक a thorn, tearing or splitting rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकदम्ब|गिरिकदंब|गिरिकदम्बः
गिरिकदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A species of Kadamba, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and कदम्ब the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकन्दर|गिरिकंदर|गिरिकन्दरः
गिरिकन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cave, a cavern.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and कन्दर a cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकदली
गिरिकदली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A species of plantain growing in hilly countries.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and कदली a plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकर्णिका|गिरिकर्ण्णिका
गिरिकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and कर्ण an ear, affixes कन् and टाप्; the mountain-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकर्णी|गिरिकर्ण्णी
गिरिकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Javāsa, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>2 A different plant, (Clitoria ternatea): see अपराजिता.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mouse, and कर्णी an ear, affix ङीष्, the mouse-earleaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिका
गिरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small rat, a mouse.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to गिरि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिकाण|गिरिकाणः
गिरिकाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A blind or one-eyed man, one blind from a particular disease.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि as above, and काण one-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिगुड|गिरिगुडः
गिरिगुड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A ball for playing with.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and गुड, each meaning the same thing, a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिज|गिरिजं|गिरिजः
गिरिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Mountain-born, mountaineer, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The Mahwa tree, (Bassia.)<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ, as the daughter of the personified HIMĀLA mountain.<BR>2 The Shaddock or pamplemouse^1, (Citrus decumana.)<BR>3 A plant considered as a white species of Rasnā: see रास्ना.<BR>4 The hill plantain.<BR>5 Jasmine.<BR>6 A pebble, a small stone.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Talc.<BR>2 Benzoin or gum benjamin; it is also confounded with styrax, another gum resin.<BR>3 Bitumen.<BR>4 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and ज born.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिजामल|गिरिजामलं
गिरिजामल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Talc.<BR>E.<BR>गिरिज mountain-born, and अमल clear, clean; also गिरिज, and अमल severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिज्वर|गिरिज्वरः
गिरिज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and ज्वर what burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरित|गिरितः
गिरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Swallowed.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, affix क्त; also गिलित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिदुर्ग
गिरिदुर्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A hill fort or any strong hold amongst mountains.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and दुर्ग a place of difficult access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिधातु|गिरिधातुः
गिरिधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिध्वज
गिरिध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and ध्वज a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिपुष्पक|गिरिपुष्पकं
गिरिपुष्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and पुष्प a flower; कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिपृष्ठ|गिरिपृष्ठः
गिरिपृष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>The top of a hill.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिप्रिय
गिरिप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fond of or frequenting mountains.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The Yak.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमल्लिका
गिरिमल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Echites antidysenterica): see कुटज.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and मल्ली a jasmin, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमान|गिरिमानः
गिरिमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A large and powerful elephant.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and मान measure, like a mountain in bulk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिभिद्
गिरिभिद्<BR>m. (-भित्)<BR>A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and भिद् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिभू
गिरिभू<BR>mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु)<BR>Mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A small stone.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमृत्
गिरिमृत्<BR>f. (-मृत्)<BR>1 Red chalk.<BR>2 Mountain-soil.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and मृत् clay, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमृद्भव|गिरिमृद्भवं
गिरिमृद्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>गिरिमृत्, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिमेद|गिरिमेदः
गिरिमेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A foetid mimosa.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and मेद filth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरियक|गिरियकः
गिरियक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ball for playing with.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a ball, घ pleonastic affix, and कन् added; also गिरियाक the pen, being lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरियाक|गिरियाकः
गिरियाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ball: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिवासिन्
गिरिवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Living in the mountains, being or produced in them.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A large kind of Arum.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and वासिन् what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिश|गिरिशः
गिरिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and शीङ्^1 to sleep, affix ड; inhabiting mount Kailāsa, or frequenting the Himāla range.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: Wil1819 also shows Y. But under SI, only 'N' appears..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिशालिनी
गिरिशालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and शालिनी what grows in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिशृङ्ग|गिरिशृंग|गिरिशृङ्गः
गिरिशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 The peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mount, and शृङ्ग a peak, alluding to his bulk, or गिरि the mountain Kailāsa, and शृङ्ग chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसार|गिरिसारः
गिरिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Malaya mountains, situated in the south of India.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>3 Tin.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरिसुता
गिरिसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि Himālaya, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिरीश|गिरीशः
गिरीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of Himāla, the snowy mountains on the north of Hindustan, or the range personified.<BR>3 A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, (or in the last meaning, गिर् speech,) and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=289" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिल|गिलः
गिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Who or what swallows.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The citron.<BR>2 Swallowing.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, affix क, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलग्राह|गिलग्राहः
गिलग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A shark.<BR>E.<BR>गिल, and ग्राह who seizes, who swallows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलत्|गिलन्त्
गिलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Swallowing, eating, devouring.<BR>E.<BR>गै to swallow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलन|गिलनं
गिलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Swallowing; also गिरण.<BR>E.<BR>as before; र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलि|गिलिः
गिलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 Swallowing.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>see गिरि, र being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिलित|गिलितं
गिलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Swallowed.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, affix क्त, गिरित, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गिष्ण|गिष्णः
गिष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>1 A Brahman versed in the Sāma Veda, a chanter of that Veda, which is always to be so recited.<BR>2 An actor, a professional singer.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, डिष्ण Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीत|गीतं
गीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sung, chaunted, sounded, &c.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A name often applied to books, as the Śiva Gītā, Rāma Gītā, Gītā Govinda, Bhagavad Gītā, which last is also often called Gītā only.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Singing, song either general or particular.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to sing, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीतमोदिन्
गीतमोदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A Kinnara or celestial chorister.<BR>E.<BR>गीत song or singing, and मोदिन् who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीति|गीतिः
गीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Song, singing.<BR>2 A kind of poetical metre, a form of the Ārya metre, in which the stanza consists of four lines of twelve and eighteen syllabic instants alternately.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीरथ|गीरथः
गीरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>गी speech, and रथ a car, the conveyer of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्ण|गीर्णः|गीर्ण्ण
गीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Praised.<BR>2 Swallowed.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow or make known, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्णि|गीर्णिः|गीर्ण्णि
गीर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 Swallowing.<BR>2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>3 Praise, applause.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्देवी
गीर्देवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>गी speech, and देवी a goddess, the goddess of language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीर्व्वाण|गीर्वाण|गीर्वाणः|गीर्व्वाणः
गीर्व्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A deity, a god.<BR>E.<BR>गीः speech, and वाण an arrow or weapon in general, whose fiat or word is his weapon; or गी with वन to desire, affix अन्, desiring hymns, prayers, &c. it is also written गीर्ब्बाण^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: alternate form of gIrvvARa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गीष्पति|गीष्पतिः
गीष्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER and preceptor of the gods.<BR>2 A Paṇḍita or learned teacher.<BR>E.<BR>गिर् speech, in the nominative case, गीः and पति master, Visarga becomes स and स is here changed irregularly to ष; the compound however is sometimes written differently, thus गीःपति, गीर्पति or गीस्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गु
गु<BR>(ओ, शि) r. 6th cl. (गुवति)<BR>To stool, to void excrement.<BR>(ङ) गुङ् r. 1st cl. (गवते)<BR>To sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुल|गुग्गुलः
गुग्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gum resin: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुग्गुलु|गुग्गुलुः
गुग्गुलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>1 A fragrant gum resin, Bdellium or the exudation of the Amyris agallochum.<BR>2 A species of morunga, (M. hyperanthera.)<BR>E.<BR>गुज् (here said to mean) disease, and गुड to perfume, affixes क and उ, ड changed to ल; also गुग्गुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छ|गुच्छः|गुछ
गुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 A cluster of blossoms.<BR>2 A clump of grass.<BR>3 A necklace of thirty-two strings.<BR>4 A pearl necklace.<BR>5 A peacock's plumage or bundle of peacock's feathers.<BR>6 A bundle.<BR>f. (-च्छी)<BR>A species of Bonduc: see करञ्ज.<BR>E.<BR>गु to sound, छ affix, or गुध to play, and च्छक् affix, where bees, &c. sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छक|गुच्छकं|गुच्छकः
गुच्छक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cluster of blossoms.<BR>2 A clump of grass.<BR>3 A kind of necklace.<BR>4 A peacock's plumage, a bundle of peacock's feathers.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also गुत्सक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छपत्र|गुच्छपत्रः
गुच्छपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>गुच्छ a cluster, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छफला
गुच्छफला<BR>m. (-ला)<BR>1 The plaintain.<BR>2 The vine.<BR>E.<BR>गुच्छ a cluster, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छार्द्ध
गुच्छार्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A necklace of thirty-four strings.<BR>E.<BR>गुच्छ a large necklace, and अर्द्ध a part; also गुत्सार्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुच्छाल|गुच्छालः
गुच्छाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A species of grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>E.<BR>गुच्छ, and अल to be fit for, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुज
गुज<BR>r. 1st cl. (गोजति) or (शि) r. 6th cl. (गुजति) or (इ) गुजि r. 1st cl. (गुञ्जति)<BR>To sound, to sound inarticulately, to buzz, to hum, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुज्जरी
गुज्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs, perhaps more correctly गुर्ज्जरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्ज|गुंज|गुंजः|गुञ्जः
गुञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>1 A small shrub, (Abrus precatorius,) bearing a red and black berry, which forms the smallest of the jeweller's weights.<BR>2 The berry which averages about 1(5/16) grains troy, or the artificial weight called by this name, weighing about 2(3/16) grains: see रक्तिका, &c.<BR>3 A kettle drum.<BR>4 A low murmuring sound.<BR>5 A tavern.<BR>6 Reflection, meditation.<BR>E.<BR>गुजि to sound, affix क; where the bees buzz.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जकृत्|गुंजकृत्
गुञ्जकृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>गुञ्ज a low tone, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जत्
गुञ्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्)<BR>Buzzing, humming, making a low murmuring sound.<BR>E.<BR>गुजि to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जन|गुंजन|गुंजनं|गुञ्जनं
गुञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sounding low and deep, as buzzing, murmuring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुजि to sound, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जिका|गुंजिका
गुञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Ratti or Gunja seed, considered as equal to three barley corns: see गुञ्जा.<BR>E.<BR>गुञ्जा, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुञ्जित|गुंजित|गुंजितं|गुञ्जितं
गुञ्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uttered in a low tone, murmured, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sounding, murmuring, buzzing.<BR>E.<BR>गुजि, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुटिका
गुटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pill, a bolus, any small globe or ball.<BR>2 A small pustule.<BR>3 The cocoon of the silk worm.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to surround, affix क्वुन्, ड changed to ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुठ
गुठ<BR>(इ) गुठि r. 10th cl. (गुण्ठयति)<BR>To surround, to envelope or enclose: with अव, to veil, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुड|गुडः
गुड<BR>(शि) r. 6th cl. (गुडति)<BR>To defend, to guard or preserve.<BR>(इ) गुडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (गुण्डति गुण्डयति)<BR>1 To surround, to enclose.<BR>2 To pound, to grind, to reduce to powder.<BR>3 (According to some authorities,) To preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुड|गुडः
गुड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Round, globular.<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A globe or ball.<BR>2 Treacle, molasses, the first thickening of the juice of the cane by boiling.<BR>3 An elephant's trappings or armour.<BR>4 A mouthful.<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 A plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli^1): see स्नुही.<BR>2 Powder, pounded substance.<BR>E.<BR>गुङ् to sound, affix ड.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडक|गुडकः
गुडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A conserve, a drug prepared with treacle.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Treacle.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडकरी
गुडकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडची
गुडची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडुची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडतृण|गुडतृणं
गुडतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>गुड raw sugar, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=290" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडत्वच्
गुडत्वच्<BR>n. (-त्वक्)<BR>The aromatic bark of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>गुड sugar, and त्वच् skin, bark, sweet-bark; also गुडत्वच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडत्वच|गुडत्वचं
गुडत्वच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Mace.<BR>2 Cassia bark.<BR>E.<BR>गुड sugar, sweet as sugar, त्वच् bark, and अच् added in this form of the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडदारु|गुडदारुः
गुडदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>Sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>गुड raw sugar, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडधेनु|गुडधेनुः
गुडधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>Sugar piled up for distribution at certain religious rites.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडपिष्ट
गुडपिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A sort of sweetmeat, flour or rice and sugar, ground and boiled together.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडपुष्प|गुडपुष्पः
गुडपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A kind of bassia, (B. latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>गुड sugar, and पुष्प flower; the flowers being full of saccharine matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडफल|गुडफलः
गुडफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, commonly Pilu, (Careya arborea, &c.): see पीलु.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and फल fruit, the fruit yielding Gur or saccharine matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडमिश्र
गुडमिश्र<BR>n. (-श्रं)<BR>A sort of cake or sweetmeat, flour or rice and coarse sugar ground and boiled together.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडमूल|गुडमूलः
गुडमूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of amaranth, (A. polygamus); also अल्पमारिष.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and मूल root; having a root as sweet as Gur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडल|गुडलं
गुडल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A spirituous liquor distilled from molasses, a sort of rum.<BR>E.<BR>गुड sugar, and ल what requires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडशर्क्करा|गुडशर्करा
गुडशर्क्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Sugar, refined sugar.<BR>E.<BR>गुड molasses, and शर्क्करा sugar or sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडशिग्रु|गुडशिग्रुः
गुडशिग्रु<BR>m. (-ग्रुः)<BR>A red sort of morunga: see शोभाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>गुड sugar, शिग्रु morunga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाका
गुडाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाकेश|गुडाकेशः
गुडाकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A title of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>गुडा Euphorbia, and केश the hair; the hair forming matted locks, resembling in shape the leaves of the Euphorbia: again, गुडाका sloth, and ईश paramount; subduing indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडाशय|गुडाशयः
गुडाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A mountain Pilu: see गुडफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडिका
गुडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pill, a bolus.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to be round, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडुची
गुडुची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडूची
गुडूची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A creeper, commonly called Guricha, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>गुड to preserve, (from disease,) ऊचट् affix; also with the pen. vowel short गुडुची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडेर|गुडेरः
गुडेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mouthful.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to surround, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडेरक|गुडेरकः
गुडेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mouthful.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to preserve, एरक् affix, and कन् added; also गुडेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडोद्भवा
गुडोद्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Sugar.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुडौदन
गुडौदन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Boiled rice and coarse sugar.<BR>E.<BR>गुड, and ओदन rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण|गुणः
गुण<BR>r. 10th cl. (गुणयति)<BR>1 To invite.<BR>2 To advise.<BR>3 To multiply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण|गुणः
गुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A quality, attribute, or property in general.<BR>2 A property of all created things; three are particularized, the Sattva, Raja, and Tama, or principles of truth or existence, passion or foulness, and darkness or ignorance.<BR>3 A means of defence, one of six expedients in government, as, peace, war, a march, a halt, a stratagem, and recourse to protection: see सन्धि, &c.<BR>4 Form, shape, &c. or property of the body.<BR>5 Knowledge, ignorance, &c. or quality of the mind.<BR>6 Heroism, valor, &c.<BR>7 White, black, &c. or the attributes of color.<BR>8 An organ of sense.<BR>9 A string in general.<BR>10 A bow-string.<BR>11 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>12 A cook.<BR>13 A name of BHĪMA.<BR>14 Secondary, subordinate.<BR>15 Excellence, merit, freedom from fault or blemish.<BR>16 (In arithmetic,) The given coefficient of any number.<BR>17 (In geometry,) The chord of an are.<BR>18 (In grammar,) The substitution of e, o, ar and al for i, u, ṛ, ḷ.<BR>19 (In rhetoric,) Consistency of plan, elegance of expression, &c. as the merits of a composition.<BR>20 In composition with numerals, multiplication, as द्विगुण twice, त्रिगुण thrice.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant of the fibres of which bow-strings are made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to address or advise, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणक|गुणकः
गुणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A numerator, a reckoner.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) The multiplier.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to count, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणकार|गुणकारः
गुणकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who counts, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and कार who makes; BHĪMA performed the duties of a cook at the time all the Pāṇḍava princes became servants to VIRĀṬA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणगान
गुणगान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Panegyric, praise.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and गान singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणग्रहण
गुणग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Acknowledging or appreciating merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणग्राहिन्
गुणग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Who judges or appreciates good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and ग्राहिन् who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणगृह्य
गुणगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 Suited to good qualities.<BR>2 Admiring or attached to merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and गृह्य to be caught by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणघातिन्
गुणघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>A detractor, a calumniator, envious, censorious.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and घातिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणज्ञ|गुणज्ञः
गुणज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>One who knows how to appreciate men or things, knowing or judging of their merits.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणतस
गुणतस<BR>ind.<BR>1 According to property or quality.<BR>2 According to desert.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणता
गुणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Excellence, the possession of good qualities.<BR>2 Substantiality, possession of attributes or qualities in general.<BR>3 Multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and तल् affix; also with त्व, affix गुणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणत्रय
गुणत्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The three properties of nature; purity, passion, and darkness.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and त्रय triple; also गुणत्रितयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणदोषपरीक्षण
गुणदोषपरीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Test or investigation of merits and faults.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, दोष fault, परीक्षण trying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणधर्म्म|गुणधर्म|गुणधर्मः
गुणधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The virtue incident to the possession of certain qualities, as clemency is the virtue of royalty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुण a property, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणन|गुणनं
गुणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Describing, relating qualities.<BR>2 Enumerating.<BR>3 Multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to number, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनिका
गुणनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Dance, the science or profession of dancing, acting, &c.<BR>2 Determining the reading of a manuscript, &c.<BR>3 A cypher.<BR>4 The prologue or introduction to a drama.<BR>5 A necklace.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to गुणनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनी
गुणनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Examining books, studying, collating, and correcting copies, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to advise, affix ल्युट्, and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणनीय|गुणनीयः
गुणनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be advised.<BR>2 To be multiplied.<BR>3 To be enumerated.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Practice, practising any thing, but especially science or study.<BR>m. (-यं)<BR>The multiplicand.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to advise, &c. अनीवर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणपूग
गुणपूग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Great merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and पूग a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=291" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणप्रकर्ष|गुणप्रकर्षः
गुणप्रकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Great merit, excellence.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and प्रकर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणप्रिय
गुणप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Attached to merit, fond of excellence.<BR>E.<BR>गण, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणभ्रंश|गुणभ्रंशः
गुणभ्रंश<BR>mfn. (-शः)<BR>The loss of all good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण good property, and भ्रंश fall, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणमय
गुणमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Endowed with or consisting of properties.<BR>2 Possessed of merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणमहत्
गुणमहत्<BR>n. (-हत्)<BR>Great merit, superior qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and महत् great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणयुक्त
गुणयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Having virtues or properties.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलक्षण
गुणलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Mark or indication of internal property.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलयनिका
गुणलयनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>गुण rope, ली to bind, ल्युट् and ङीप् affix, with कन् added; also गुणलयनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणलुब्ध
गुणलुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Desirous of merit, attached to excellence.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and लुब्ध covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्|गुणवन्त्
गुणवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Possessing attributes.<BR>2 Endowed with good qualities.<BR>3 Tied, bound, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुण quality, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्तम
गुणवत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Excellent.<BR>E.<BR>गुणवत् and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्तर
गुणवत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Excellent.<BR>E.<BR>गुणवत् and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवत्ता
गुणवत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Excellence.<BR>E.<BR>गुणवत् and तल् affix; also with त्व, गुणवत्त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवाचक|गुणवाचकः
गुणवाचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An adjective or attributive noun.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and वाचक a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवैशेष्य
गुणवैशेष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Preeminence of merit or of any property.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and वैशेष्य superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणवृक्षक|गुणवृक्षकः
गुणवृक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mast.<BR>E.<BR>गुण a rope, and वृक्ष a tree, कन् affix of similitude; also गुणवृक्षः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणश्लाघा
गुणश्लाघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>Praise, encomium.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and श्लाघा praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसम्पद्|गुणसंपद्
गुणसम्पद्<BR>f. (-पत् or पद्)<BR>Great merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and सम्पद् wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसङ्ग|गुणसंग|गुणसंगः
गुणसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Association with properties or qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and सङ्ग combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसङ्ग्रह|गुणसंग्रह|गुणसंग्रहः
गुणसङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A collection of merits or properties.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and सङ्ग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणसागर|गुणसागरः
गुणसागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Endowed with all good qualities.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A form of BUDDHA, a Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>गुण excellence, and सागर the ocean; an ocean of desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणस्तुति|गुणस्तुतिः
गुणस्तुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Panegyric, encomium.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणहीन
गुणहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Void of merit.<BR>2 Free from properties.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाकर|गुणाकरः
गुणाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Possessing all excellences.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>गुण attribute, especially good, and आकर a mine; a mine of merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणातीत|गुणातीतः
गुणातीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Freed from or beyond all properties.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणानुरोध|गुणानुरोधः
गुणानुरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Conformity or suitableness to good qualities, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अनुरोध concurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणान्तर
गुणान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Species or sort of merit.<BR>2 Variety of property or quality.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणान्वित
गुणान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having attributes or qualities.<BR>2 Excellent, good, endowed with virtues.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणापवाद|गुणापवादः
गुणापवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Detraction.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अपवाद reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाभास
गुणाभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Semblance of qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and आभास appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणाश्रय
गुणाश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Virtuous, excellent, able, endowed with good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिगण
गुणिगण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>A number of virtuous persons.<BR>E.<BR>गुणिन्, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणित|गुणितः
गुणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Multiplied, (arithmetically.)<BR>2 Collected, heaped together.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to advise, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिद्वैध
गुणिद्वैध<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>Equality of merit on two sides.<BR>E.<BR>गुणिन्, and द्वैध duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणिन्
गुणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Endowed with good qualities.<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>गुण a quality, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणीभूत|गुणीभूतः
गुणीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made secondary or subordinate.<BR>2 Invested with attributes, &c.<BR>3 Varied according to its qualities.<BR>4 Having a certain force or application, (a word, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and भृत become, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणेश्वर|गुणेश्वरः
गुणेश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Having good qualities, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a mountain, according to some, Citrakūṭa or Comptah in Bundelcund.<BR>E.<BR>गुण qualities, and ईश्वर master or possessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कर्ष|गुणोत्कर्षः
गुणोत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Excellence, endowment with superior qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and उत्कर्ष abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कीर्त्तन|गुणोत्कीर्तन|गुणोत्कीर्त्तनं
गुणोत्कीर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Panegyric, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and उत्कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोत्कृष्ट
गुणोत्कृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Superior in merit or in good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and उत्कृष्ट best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणोपेत
गुणोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Endowed with good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुणौघ|गुणौघः
गुणौघ<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>Superior or abundant merit.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and ओघ heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्ठित|गुंठित|गुण्ठितः
गुण्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pounded, ground, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>2 Covered with, surrounded.<BR>E.<BR>गुठि to surround, &c. affix क्त; also गुण्डित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्ड|गुंडः|गुण्डः
गुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डक|गुंडक|गुंडकः|गुण्डकः
गुण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Dust, powder.<BR>2 Dirty meal.<BR>3 An oil vessel.<BR>4 A low tone.<BR>E.<BR>गुडि to surround, &c. affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डिक|गुंडिक|गुंडिकः|गुण्डिकः
गुण्डिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>Flour, powder, meal.<BR>E.<BR>गुडि to pound, वुन् affix, and इ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डिचा
गुण्डिचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>The name of the place where the car of JAGANNĀTHA stays for a week at the Ratha Yātrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्डित|गुंडित|गुण्डितः
गुण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pounded, ground.<BR>2 Covered with dust.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to grind or pound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुण्य
गुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>1 To be enumerated.<BR>2 To be described as qualities, to be praised.<BR>3 To be multiplied, the multiplicand.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to count, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्स|गुत्सः
गुत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>1 A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>2 A clump of grass.<BR>3 A necklace of thirty-six strings.<BR>4 A perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>5 A bundle.<BR>E.<BR>गुध to enclose or surround, Uṇādi affix स; also गुत्सक, गुच्छ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सक|गुत्सकः
गुत्सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A nosegay, a cluster of blossoms.<BR>2 A chowri, a cow tail.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also गुच्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=292" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सपुष्प
गुत्सपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris): see सप्तपर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>गुत्स, and पुष्प a flower; bearing its flowers in clusters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुत्सार्द्ध
गुत्सार्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A necklace or garland of twenty-four strings.<BR>E.<BR>गुत्स a large garland, and अर्द्ध a part; also गुच्छार्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद|गुदं
गुद<BR>r. 1st cl. (गोदति)<BR>To play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद|गुदं
गुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>गुद to play, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदकील|गुदकीलः
गुदकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Piles.<BR>E.<BR>गुद the anus, कील a pin or bolt; also with कन् added गुदकीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदग्रह|गुदग्रहः
गुदग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Constipation, flatulence, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुद the anus, and ग्रह what takes or affects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदभ्रंश|गुदभ्रंशः
गुदभ्रंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Prolapsus ani.<BR>E.<BR>गुद, and भ्रंश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदाङ्कुर|गुदांकुर|गुदाङ्कुरः
गुदाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Piles.<BR>E.<BR>गुद the anus, and अङ्कुर a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद्र
गुद्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) गुद्रि (गुंद्रयति)<BR>To lie, to speak falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुध
गुध<BR>r. 1st cl. (गोधते)<BR>To play.<BR>r. 4th cl. (गोध्यति)<BR>To surround, to encompass.<BR>r. 9th cl. (गोध्नाति)<BR>To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधित
गुधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, inclosed.<BR>E.<BR>गुध to surround, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधेर|गुधेरः
गुधेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A protector, a defender.<BR>E.<BR>गुध to invest, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्दल|गुंदल|गुंदलः|गुन्दलः
गुन्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The sound of a small oblong drum.<BR>E.<BR>गुद to play, अलच् affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्दाल|गुंदाल|गुंदालः|गुन्दालः
गुन्दाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of bird, (a sort of pheasant?)<BR>2 The bartavelle: see चकोर.<BR>E.<BR>गुन्द्रा a kind of grass, and ल what takes or eats, र rejected; also read गुन्द्राल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्द्र|गुंद्रः|गुन्द्रः
गुन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A kind of grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus pertenuis; also C. rotundus.)<BR>2 A plant bearing a fragrant seed; also प्रियङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>गुद to play, affix रक्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुन्द्राल|गुंद्राल|गुंद्रालः|गुन्द्रालः
गुन्द्राल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of bird: see गुन्दाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप
गुप<BR>r. 1st cl. (जुगुप्सते)<BR>1 To conceal, to hide.<BR>2 To censure, to blame or despise, (this root takes सन् irregularly.)<BR>(उ) गुपू r. 1st cl. (गोपयति)<BR>To guard or protect.<BR>(इर) गुपिर r. 4th cl. (गुप्यति)<BR>1 To be confused or disturbed.<BR>2 To disturb or perplex.<BR>गुप r. 10th cl. (गोपयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुपिल|गुपिलः
गुपिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to protect, Uṇādi affix इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्त|गुप्तं|गुप्तः
गुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Preserved, protected.<BR>2 Hidden, concealed, secret.<BR>3 Joined, combined.<BR>4 Invisible, withdrawn from sight.<BR>n. adv. (-प्तं)<BR>Privately, secretly.<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>An appellation forming especially the second member of the name of a Vaiśya or man of the third class.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>1 Cowach.<BR>2 A woman who hides from her lover's endearments.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to defend, &c. affix ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तगति|गुप्तगतिः
गुप्तगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A spy or secret emissary.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Going privately or secretly.<BR>E.<BR>गुप्त and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तचर|गुप्तचरः
गुप्तचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what goes secretly.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>गुप्त, and चर who goes, or चरट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्ति|गुप्तिः
गुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Concealing, hiding, concealment.<BR>2 Preserving, protecting.<BR>3 Restraint, check.<BR>4 A hole in the ground, a cavern, a sink, a cellar, &c. (a place of concealment.)<BR>5 A prison.<BR>6 The well or lower deck of a boat.<BR>7 Digging a hole in the ground.<BR>8 Fortification.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to hide, &c. affix क्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफ
गुफ<BR>r. 6th cl. (गुफति)<BR>To string as a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफित|गुफितः
गुफित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strung, tied on a string.<BR>2 Arranged in order.<BR>E.<BR>गुफ to string, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुंफः|गुम्फः
गुम्फ<BR>r. 6th cl. (गुम्फति)<BR>To string together as a garland, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुंफः|गुम्फः
गुम्फ<BR>m. (-म्फः)<BR>1 Tying, stringing as a garland, &c.<BR>2 A bracelet.<BR>3 A whisker, a mustachio.<BR>E.<BR>गुम्फ to tie or string, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुम्फित|गुंफित|गुम्फितः
गुम्फित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tied, strung.<BR>2 Arranged, placed in order.<BR>E.<BR>गुम्फ to tie, affix क्त; also गुफित, and ग्रन्थित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर
गुर<BR>r. 1st cl. (गोरति) r. 6th cl. (ई) गुरी (गुरते)<BR>To make an effort or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरण|गुरणं
गुरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Effort, perseverance, great or continued exertion.<BR>E.<BR>गुर to make an effort, affix ल्युट्; also गोरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरु|गुरुः
गुरु<BR>mfn. (-गुरुः गुर्व्वी गुरु)<BR>1 Heavy, weighty.<BR>2 Great, (large or eminent.)<BR>2 Difficult, arduous.<BR>4 Important.<BR>5 Much, excessive.<BR>6 Best, excellent.<BR>7 Venerable, respectable.<BR>8 Dear, valuable, highly prized.<BR>9 Accented long, (as a foot or vowel.)<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>The long vowel, a sound equal to two Mātras or simple sounds.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A spiritual parent, from whom the youth receives the initiatory Mantra or prayer, and who conducts the ceremonies necessary at various seasons of infancy and youth, up to the period of investiture with the characteristic thread or string; this person may be the natural parent or the religious preceptor.<BR>2 A religious teacher, one who explains the law and religion to his pupil, instructs him in the Śāstras, &c.<BR>3 A name of VṚHASPATI, who is considered as the Guru or preceptor of the gods.<BR>4 A father or any venerable male relation.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to sound or speak, &c. Uṇādi affix कु, and उ substituted for ऋ; declaring the mode of performing the rites, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकार्य्य|गुरुकार्य
गुरुकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 A serious or momentous affair.<BR>2 The business or office of a spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु as above, and कार्य्य business, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुकोप
गुरुकोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Violent wrath.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु much, and कोप anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुक्रम|गुरुक्रमः
गुरुक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Traditionary instruction.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु a teacher, and क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुगत
गुरुगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Being with or belonging to a spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुघ्न|गुरुघ्नः
गुरुघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Destroying a spiritual parent.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>White mustard.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and घ्न who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुजन|गुरुजनः
गुरुजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An elder, a venerable person.<BR>2 The elders of a family, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुण्टक|गुरुण्टकः
गुरुण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of bird, a sort of peacock: see नीलमयूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पग|गुरुतल्पगः
गुरुतल्पग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A violator of his teacher's bed.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु as above, तल्प a bed, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पव्रत
गुरुतल्पव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Penance for intercourse with the wife of a Guru.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, तल्प a bed, (defiling, &c. understood,) and व्रत penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतल्पिन्
गुरुतल्पिन्<BR>m. (-ल्पी)<BR>One who has criminal intercourse with his teacher's wife.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, तल्प a bed, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुताप
गुरुताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Excessive heat.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुत्व|गुरुत्वं
गुरुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Sacredness, venerableness, respectability.<BR>2 Greatness, magnitude.<BR>3 Weight, heaviness.<BR>4 Burden, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and त्व affix; also with तल्, गुरुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुप्रमोद
गुरुप्रमोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Happiness, delight.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and प्रमोद pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुरत्न|गुरुरत्नं
गुरुरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A topaz.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु valuable, रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुदैवत|गुरुदैवतः
गुरुदैवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The eighth lunar constellation; also पुष्य.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु and देवता deity, affix अण्; VṚHASPATI is the ruling deity of the constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=293" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुपत्र|गुरुपत्रं
गुरुपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Tin.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and पत्र leaf; heavy or abundant in leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुमर्द्दल|गुरुमर्दल|गुरुमर्दलः
गुरुमर्द्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु heavy or large, and मर्द्दल a small drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवत्
गुरुवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like a Guru, as a Guru.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and बति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवद्वृत्ति
गुरुवद्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Behaving to any one with as much respect as to a sacred teacher.<BR>E.<BR>गुरुवत्, and वृति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुवर्च्चोघ्न|गुरुवर्चोघ्न|गुरुवर्चोघ्नः|गुरुवर्च्चोघ्नः
गुरुवर्च्चोघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु much, वर्च्चम् heat, and घ्न what removes; of cooling properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुशिंशपा
गुरुशिंशपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia sisu): see शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुशुश्रूषा
गुरुशुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Service of a Guru.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and शुश्रूषा; also गुरुपूजा, गुरुसेवा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुसारा
गुरुसारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>See शिंशपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुस्थिर
गुरुस्थिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very firm.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and स्थिर steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुहन्
गुरुहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>The murderer of his Guru or spiritual parent.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and हन् who kills, from हन with क्विप् affix; this is the most heinous of all criminals, according to Hindu notions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्ज्जर|गुर्जर|गुर्जरः|गुर्ज्जरः
गुर्ज्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a district, Gurjara or Guzerat.<BR>m. plu. (-राः)<BR>The people of Guzerat.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्द|गुर्द्द
गुर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (गुर्दते or गूर्दते)<BR>To play.<BR>r. 10th cl. (गूर्दयति)<BR>1 To dwell or inhabit.<BR>2 To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व|गुर्व्व
गुर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई) गुर्वी (गुर्वति)<BR>To endeavor, to aim or strive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वर्थम्|गुर्वर्थम्
गुर्व्वर्थम्<BR>ind.<BR>For or on account of a Guru.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वङ्गना|गुर्वङ्गना
गुर्व्वङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The wife of a Guru.<BR>2 Any woman entitled to great respect.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, and अङ्गना a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्विणी|गुर्विणी
गुर्व्विणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>गर्व्व to be proud, Uṇādi affix इनच् and ङीष् fem. affix, उ substituted for the radical अ; also गर्भिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्वी|गुर्वी
गुर्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>1 A pregnant woman.<BR>2 The wife of a Guru or spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु heavy, &c. and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल|गुलः
गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Raw or unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli): see स्नुहि.<BR>(-ली)<BR>1 A pill, a bolus, any small globular substance.<BR>2 Small pox.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to surround, &c. affixes क and टाप्, or ङीष्, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलञ्चकन्द|गुलञ्चकन्दः
गुलञ्चकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>An esculent root, commonly कुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिका
गुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small ball.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to गुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिकाक्रीडा
गुलिकाक्रीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Playing with a ball, bat and ball, golf, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुलिका, and क्रीडा play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुच्छ|गुलुच्छः|गुलुछ
गुलुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A cluster of blossoms; also गुलुञ्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुञ्छ|गुलुंछ|गुलुंछः|गुलुञ्छः
गुलुञ्छ<BR>m. (-ञ्छः)<BR>A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to preserve, affix क्विप्, and ड changed to ल, and उच्छ or इच्छि to gather or glean, affix क; also with कन् added गुलुञ्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्फ|गुल्फः
गुल्फ<BR>m. (-ल्फः)<BR>The ancle.<BR>E.<BR>गल to go, affix फक्, and उ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्म|गुल्मं|गुल्मः
गुल्म<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>1 The division of an army, a body of troops, consisting of nine platoons, or nine elephants, nine chariots, twenty-seven horse, and forty-five foot.<BR>2 The spleen.<BR>3 A shrub, a bush.<BR>4 A clump of grass, &c.<BR>5 A fort, an intrenchment.<BR>6 Disciplining an army, keeping it in a posture of defence.<BR>7 A wharf or stairs, a Ghat.<BR>8 A disease; according to some, a chronic enlargement of the spleen, but as variously situated it is any glandular enlargement in the abdomen, as that of the mesenteric gland, &c. so as to be perceived externally.<BR>f. (-ल्मी)<BR>1 A tent.<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan; also आमलकी.<BR>3 Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>4 A cluster or clump of trees, a multitude of thickets.<BR>5 A kind of plant, commonly Kurkavali.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to surround, मक् affix, ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मकेतु|गुल्मकेतुः
गुल्मकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A small sort of cane or reed.<BR>E.<BR>गुल्म, and केतु banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्ममूल|गुल्ममूलं
गुल्ममूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>गुल्म, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मिन्
गुल्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-ल्मी-ल्मिनी-ल्मि)<BR>1 Composed of different divisions, (a force, &c.)<BR>2 Growing, &c. in a clump or cluster.<BR>3 Having the spleen affected by it.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A spreading creeper or any creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>गुल्म a clump, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्य|गुल्यः
गुल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>Sweetness, a sweet or saccharine taste.<BR>E.<BR>गुड molasses, and क्यप् affix; ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुवाक|गुवाकः
गुवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The betelnut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>गु to stool, affix आक, and उ converted to अव irregularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह|गुहः
गुह<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊ) गुहू (गुहति)<BR>To cover, to cover as with clothes, to wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह|गुहः
गुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A swift horse.<BR>4 The name of a Niṣāda, ruler of Sringavera, the friend of RĀMA.<BR>5 A name or title proper to persons of the writer caste.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A cave, a cavern.<BR>2 A pit, a hole in the ground.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Cākuliya: see सिंहपुच्छी.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to conceal, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहागृह
गुहागृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A cavern.<BR>E.<BR>गुहा, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहामुख
गुहामुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Wide mouthed, open mouthed.<BR>E.<BR>गुहा, and मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहाशय|गुहाशयः
गुहाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 Any animal or man living in caverns.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>गुहा a cave, and आशय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिन|गुहिनं
गुहिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A wood, a thicket.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to hide, इनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिल|गुहिलं
गुहिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Wealth, property.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to hide, &c. इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहेर|गुहेरः
गुहेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An ironsmith.<BR>2 A guardian, a preserver.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to cover, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्य|गुह्यं|गुह्यः
गुह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 Secret, solitary, retired.<BR>2 Private, concealable, to be kept hidden or secret.<BR>3 Mysterious, mystical.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>1 A tortoise.<BR>2 Hypocrisy.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 A privity, an organ of generation, &c.<BR>2 The anus.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to cover, क्यप् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यक|गुह्यकः
गुह्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of demigod attendant upon KUVERA the deity of wealth, and guardian of his treasures.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to preserve or conceal, affix क्वुन् and य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यकेश्वर|गुह्यकेश्वरः
गुह्यकेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of KUVERA the Hindu PLUTUS.<BR>E.<BR>गुह्यक a demigod, (see the preceding,) and ईश्वर lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यगुरु|गुह्यगुरुः
गुह्यगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>गुह्य secret, and गुरु a master; ŚIVA being considered as the teacher, especially of the Tantras, or Hindu mystic and magical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यदीपक|गुह्यदीपकः
गुह्यदीपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The fire fly.<BR>E.<BR>गुह्य a solitary place, and दीपक the illuminer; from दीप to light or inflame, and क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यनिष्यन्द|गुह्यनिष्यंद|गुह्यनिष्यन्दः
गुह्यनिष्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Urine.<BR>E.<BR>गुह्य, and निष्यन्द what flows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यभाषित|गुह्यभाषितं
गुह्यभाषित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A Mantra, a mystical prayer or incantation.<BR>2 A secret.<BR>E.<BR>गुह्य secret, and भाषित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गू
गू<BR>(ओ) ओगू r. 6th cl. (गुवति)<BR>To void by stool; also with a short vowel, गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=294" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढ|गूढं|गूढः
गूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Hidden, concealed.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>1 A solitary or private place.<BR>2 A private part.<BR>3 A mystery.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to hide, affix क्त, deriv. irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढचार
गूढचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>One who goes about privately.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A secret emissary.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ, and चार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढचारिन्
गूढचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A secret emissary, a spy.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढज|गूढजः
गूढज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of a concealed birth; born privately of a woman whose husband is absent, the real father being unknown; this is one of the twelve forms particularized in Hindu law.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ hidden, and ज born; also compounded with पुत्त्र a son, गूढजपुत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढनीड|गूढनीडः
गूढनीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>गूड secret, and नीड a nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपथ|गूढपथः
गूढपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Mind, intellect.<BR>2 A bye-path, a hidden way.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ secret, and पथ a road; whose path is unperceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपाद्
गूढपाद्<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ hidden, and पाद a foot, the final vowel rejected; also being retained गूढपाद nom. (-दः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढपुरुष|गूढपुरुषः
गूढपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary, a disguised agent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ concealed, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढभाषित
गूढभाषित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Secret intelligence, private communication.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ secure, and भाषित what is said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढमार्ग|गूढमार्गः
गूढमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A subterraneous passage, a defile, a bye-road, or secret way.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ concealed, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढमैथुन|गूढमैथुनः
गूढमैथुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ secret, and मैथुन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढवर्च्चस्|गूढवर्चस्
गूढवर्च्चस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चाः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ hidden, and वर्च्चस light, warmth; perhaps an idea is implied analogous to that of cold blooded animals: some explain it वर्च्चस् foeces, whose excrement is unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढसाक्षिन्
गूढसाक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A concealed witness, one placed by the plaintiff, so as to overhear what has been said by the defendant.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ^1, and साक्षिन् a witness.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढाङ्ग|गूढांग|गूढाङ्गः
गूढाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ, and अङ्ग body, hidden in his shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढाङ्घ्रि|गूढांघ्रि|गूढाङ्घ्रिः
गूढाङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ, and अङ्घ्रि foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढोत्पन्न|गूढोत्पन्नः
गूढोत्पन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>The son of concealed birth: see गूढज.<BR>E.<BR>गूढ privately, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूथ|गूथं|गूथः
गूथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Foeces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>गू to void by stool, and थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूथलक्त|गूथलक्तः
गूथलक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A small bird, considered to be a species of the Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>गूथ ordure, and लक्त marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गून|गूनः
गून<BR>m. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Voided, (as ordure.)<BR>E.<BR>गू to stool, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर
गूर<BR>r. 10th cl. (गूरयते)<BR>1 To strive, to endeavor, to make an effort or exertion.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>(ई) गूरी r. 4th cl. (गूर्यते)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, as to wound, to kill, &c.<BR>2 To be decayed or old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूरण|गूरणं
गूरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>गूर to strive, affix ल्युट्; also गुरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्द|गूर्दः|गूर्द्द
गूर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (गूर्दते)<BR>To play.<BR>r. 10 cl. (गूर्दयति)<BR>1 To dwell or inhabit.<BR>2 To invite; these roots are both written more usually with the short vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूवाक|गूवाकः
गूवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The betelnut tree: see गुवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूषणा
गूषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The eye in a peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहमान
गूहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Hiding, concealing.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to hide, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहयित्वा
गूहयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having concealed, hidden, disguised.<BR>E.<BR>गुह to hide, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृ
गृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (गरति)<BR>To sprinkle, to moisten or wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृज
गृज<BR>r. 1st cl. (गर्जति) also (इ,) गृजि (गृञ्जति)<BR>To sound, to roar, to grumble, &c. also गर्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृञ्जन|गृंजन|गृञ्जनं|गृंजनः|गृञ्जनः
गृञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Poisoned flesh, the meat of an animal destroyed by poison.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Garlic, or a small variety of it of a red colour.<BR>2 A turnip.<BR>3 The tops of hemp chewed as an inebriating substance, the Gāñja.<BR>E.<BR>गृजि to sound, and ल्युट् affix; applied to the latter as causing eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृणत्
गृणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>1 Speaking.<BR>2 Praising, flattering.<BR>E.<BR>ग to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृण्डीव|गृंडीव|गृंडीवः|गृण्डीवः
गृण्डीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An animal of prey, considered as a large kind of jackal.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to sound, and डीव affix; deriv. irr.; also sometimes short गृण्डिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृत्स|गृत्सः
गृत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>A name of KANDARPA.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to be desirous, and स Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध
गृध<BR>r. 4th cl. (उ,) गृधु (गृध्यति)<BR>To covet, to desire greedily, to be greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृधु|गृधुः
गृधु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>1 The deity KĀMA or love.<BR>2 A libidinous man.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to desire, कु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृधू
गृधू<BR>m. (-धूः)<BR>1 Understanding.<BR>2 Air voided downwards.<BR>3 Bad, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>गृध, and कू Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्नु|गृध्नुः
गृध्नु<BR>mfn. (-ध्नुः-ध्नुः-ध्नु)<BR>Covetous, cupidinous, greedy.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to be greedy, क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्नुता
गृध्नुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Covetousness, greediness, extreme and illiberal desire.<BR>E.<BR>गृध्नु greedy, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्र|गृध्रः
गृध्र<BR>mfn. (-ध्रः-ध्रा-ध्रं)<BR>Desirous, greedy, covetous.<BR>m. (-घ्रः)<BR>A vulture.<BR>E.<BR>गृध to desire, and क्रन् Uṇādi affix; it may also be written गृद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रनखी
गृध्रनखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>1 The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>2 A wild kind of the same, (Zizyphus nepeca.)<BR>E.<BR>गृध्र a vulture, and नख nail, having thorns like a vulture's claws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रराज|गृध्रराजः
गृध्रराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of JAṬĀYU.<BR>E.<BR>गृध्र, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृध्रसी
गृध्रसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 Lumbago.<BR>2 Rheumatism affecting the loins.<BR>E.<BR>गृध desire, सो to destroy, ड and ङीप् affixes; also sometimes written ग्रध्रसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृष्टि|गृष्टिः
गृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 A cow that has had one calf.<BR>2 A yam.<BR>3 The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>E.<BR>घृष to grind, affix क्तिन्, and घ changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह|गृहं|गृहः
गृह<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऊ,) गृहू (गर्हते) also r. 10th cl. (गृहयते)<BR>To take, to seize, to receive or accept; also ग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह|गृहं|गृहः
गृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>1 A house, a mansion, a habitation in general.<BR>2 A wife: (in these senses the plural is always masculine, गृहाः).<BR>3 A name, an appellation.<BR>E.<BR>गृह to receive or take, (grain, goods, &c.) affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकच्छप|गृहकच्छपः
गृहकच्छप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A small flat oblong stone, used for grinding condiments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and कच्छप a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकन्या
गृहकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>The aloe, (Aloes perfoliata); also घृतकुमारी, कुमारी, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and कन्या a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकपोतक|गृहकपोतकः
गृहकपोतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pigeon, a tame or domestic pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and कपोतक a dove or pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकरण
गृहकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Household affairs.<BR>2 House building.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=295" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकारक|गृहकारकः
गृहकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A house builder.<BR>2 A thatcher.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and कारक who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकारिन्
गृहकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A kind of wasp.<BR>2 A house builder.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and कारिन् who makes, building a nest or house of clay, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहकार्य्य|गृहकार्य
गृहकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Household affairs.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and कार्य्य business; also गृहकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहगोधा
गृहगोधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>A small house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and गोधा or गोधिका an iguana; hence also गृहगोधिका, or ध being changed to ल, गृहगोलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहगोलिका
गृहगोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lizard: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहचटक
गृहचटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A house sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहछिद्र|गृहच्छिद्र
गृहछिद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 Private or family afflictions or troubles.<BR>2 A breach in a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and छिद्र a hole; also गृहरग्ध्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहज
गृहज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born in the house.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A slave born in the house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and ज born; also गृहजात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहणी
गृहणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Rice water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहतटी
गृहतटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A terrace in front of a house, a threshold.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहदास|गृहदासः
गृहदास<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>A domestic slave.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहदीप्ति|गृहदीप्तिः
गृहदीप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>A virtuous woman.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and दीप्ति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहद्वार
गृहद्वार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The door of a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहद्रुम|गृहद्रुमः
गृहद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A plant commonly Medhasriṅgi: see मेढशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, द्रुम a tree, growing near dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहनाशन|गृहनाशनः
गृहनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and नाशन who injures; defacing the walls of a house by building in and about it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहनीड|गृहनीडः
गृहनीड<BR>m. (डः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and नीड a nest, who builds his nest in human dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहपति|गृहपतिः
गृहपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A householder, a man of the second class, or who after having finished his studies is married and settled.<BR>2 A householder of particular merit, giving alms, and performing all the prescribed ceremonies, &c.<BR>3 Maintenance of a sacred and perpetual fire.<BR>4 Virtue, especially of a householder, as hospitality, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and पति lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहपोतक|गृहपोतकः
गृहपोतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The site of a habitation, the ground on which it stands, and which is attached to it.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and पोत a young animal, affix कन्, the rudiments of the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलि|गृहबलिः
गृहबलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Offering of the reliques of a meal, or sacrifice to the spirits of the air, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and वलि offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलिप्रिय|गृहबलिप्रियः
गृहबलिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A kind of crane, the Vaca.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, बलि food offered in oblation, and प्रिय fond of: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहबलिभुज्
गृहबलिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>1 A sparrow.<BR>2 A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>3 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house or a wife, बलि grain, &c. used in oblations, or any edible grain, and भुज् who eats; that is, who eats the food of his female, or the fragments of offerings fallen in or about the house; also गृहवलिप्रिय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभङ्ग|गृहभंग|गृहभङ्गः
गृहभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 An exile, one who is driven from his house.<BR>2 Family decay.<BR>3 Breaking down or into a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभञ्जन
गृहभञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breaking down or destroying a house.<BR>2 Causing the ruin or decay of a family.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and भञ्जन breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहभूमि|गृहभूमिः
गृहभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>The site of a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and भूमि ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमणि|गृहमणिः
गृहमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमाचिका
गृहमाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bat.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and माचिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमृग|गृहमृगः
गृहमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहमेधिन्
गृहमेधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A householder.<BR>f. (-धिनी)<BR>1 A housewife, the wife of a householder.<BR>2 Natural sense or intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, मेध to understand, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहयाप्य
गृहयाप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>The householder, the master of a house or family.<BR>E.<BR>गृह to take, आप्य Uṇādi affix, and अय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहयालु|गृहयालुः
गृहयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Disposed to seize or take.<BR>E.<BR>गृह to take, अय inserted, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहरन्ध्र
गृहरन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>1 Private or family affairs, especially of an unpleasing nature.<BR>2 A breach in the wall of a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and रन्ध्र a hole; also गृहछिद्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहवाटिका
गृहवाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A garden or grove near a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, वट to surround, affix ण्वुल्, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहव्यापार
गृहव्यापार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Household affairs, domestic economy.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and व्यापार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्तम्भ
गृहस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The pillar of a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थ|गृहस्थः
गृहस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A householder, the man of the second class, or he who, after having finished his studies, and been invested with the sacred thread, performs the duties of the master of a house, and father of a family.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and स्थ who stays or abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थधर्म्म|गृहस्थधर्म
गृहस्थधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The practice or duty of a householder.<BR>E.<BR>गृहस्थ, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थाश्रम
गृहस्थाश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The order of householder.<BR>E.<BR>गृहस्थ, and आश्रम order of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहस्थूण|गृहस्थूणं
गृहस्थूण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The pillar of a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and स्थूण a prop or pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाक्ष|गृहाक्षः
गृहाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A loophole, an eyelet hole, a round or oblong window.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and अक्ष for अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहागत|गृहागतः
गृहागत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A guest.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and आगत come to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाधिप|गृहाधिपः
गृहाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Gṛhastha or householder: see गृहस्थ.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and अधिप a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाभिपालिन्
गृहाभिपालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Watching, taking care of the house.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A watchman.<BR>E.<BR>गृह and अभि before पाल to protect, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाम्ल|गृहाम्लं
गृहाम्ल<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sour gruel, made from the fermentation of rice water.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and अम्ल sour, the domestic acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहायणिक
गृहायणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A householder.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, फिञ् derivative affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाराम|गृहारामः
गृहाराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A garden, a grove, &c. near a house.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and आराम a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहालिका
गृहालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small lizard.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, आलि a scorpion, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहावग्रहणी
गृहावग्रहणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The threshold, a raised ground or a terrace in front of the door.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and अव prefixed to ग्रह to take, affixes ल्युट् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहावस्थित
गृहावस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dwelling or living in a house.<BR>2 Lying in any place.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and अवस्थित placed or situated in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाशया
गृहाशया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The betel tree, (Piper betel.)<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, &c. आशय an asylum, growing near dwellings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहाश्मन्
गृहाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>A flat oblong stone, upon which condiments are ground together.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=296" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहिणी
गृहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहिन्
गृहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A householder.<BR>E.<BR>गृह a house, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत|गृहीतं
गृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken, attached, seized, caught.<BR>2 Obtained.<BR>3 Known, understood.<BR>4 Promised, agreed.<BR>5 Learnt, acquired.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, affix क्त, र charged to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतविद्य
गृहीतविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Versed in science, learned, studied.<BR>E.<BR>गृहीत, and विद्या learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतदिश्
गृहीतदिश्<BR>mfn. (-दिक्)<BR>Flown, escaped, retreated.<BR>E.<BR>गृहीत seized, and दिश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतवेतन
गृहीतवेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Paid, remunerated.<BR>E.<BR>गृहीत, and वेतन wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीतृ
गृहीतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Taking, disposed to seize or take.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to seize, affix तृच्, and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहीत्वा
गृहीत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोपकरण
गृहोपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Any domestic utensil.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and उपकरण instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोत्पात|गृहोत्पातः
गृहोत्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A domestic nuisance, as vermin, &c.<BR>2 Family misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>गृह, and उत्पात calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृहोलिका
गृहोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>गृह to take, and उल and कन् affixes: see गृहगोधिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्णत्
गृह्णत्<BR>mfn. (-ह्णन्-ह्णन्ती-ह्णत्)<BR>Taking, seizing, accepting, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्य|गृह्यं|गृह्यः
गृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 Dependant, subservient.<BR>2 A partisan of or belonging to a side or party.<BR>3 To be taken or seized.<BR>4 To be trusted to, to be relied on.<BR>5 To be acknowledged or admitted, to be adopted as faith or belief.<BR>6 Domestic, of or belonging to a house.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A tame or domesticated animal.<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 The name of a book, containing directions for religious rites, a section or component treatise of the Sāma Veda, by GOBHILA and others; which contains rules for the performance of domestic and other ceremonies: the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A suburb, a village adjoining to a city, or a small village attached to a larger.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह or गृह to take, affix क्यप्; or गृह a house, यत् affix; also with कन् added गृह्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यक|गृह्यकः
गृह्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Dependent, docile, not following one's own inclinations.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tame or domesticated animal, whether a bird or beast, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गृह for ग्रह to take, क्यप् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यगुरु
गृह्यगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>गृह्य, and गुरु a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गृह्यसूत्र
गृह्यसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A precept of the Gṛhya or ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>गृह्य, and सूत्र a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गॄ
गॄ<BR>r. 6th cl. (गिरति or गिलति)<BR>To swallow, to eat.<BR>r. 9th cl. (गृणाति)<BR>To sound, to sound intelligibly or articulately, to speak.<BR>r. 10th cl. (गीरयते)<BR>1 To know.<BR>2 To make known, to teach:<BR>With निर् or उत् prefixed,<BR>To reject, to vomit.<BR>With सम् and उत्,<BR>1 To throw up.<BR>2 To cry aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डु|गेण्डुः
गेण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A ball for playing with.<BR>E.<BR>गा to go, affix इण्डु, or with कन् added गेण्डुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेण्डुक|गेंडुक|गेंडुकः|गेण्डुकः
गेण्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ball; also गेण्डूक, the penultimate being made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेप
गेप<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) गेपृ (गेपते)<BR>1 To shake or tremble.<BR>2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेय|गेयं|गेयः
गेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 A singer.<BR>2 A song or chaunt, what is to be sung or chaunted.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Song, singing.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेव
गेव<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) गेवृ (गेवते)<BR>To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष
गेष<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) गेषृ (गेषते)<BR>To seek, to search, to investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्ण|गेष्णः
गेष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>1 A professional singer, an actor, a mime, &c.<BR>2 A chaunter of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, and इष्णच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेष्णु|गेष्णुः
गेष्णु<BR>m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>1 A singer.<BR>2 An actor.<BR>3 A chaunter of the Sāma Veda: see गेष्ण.<BR>E.<BR>गै to sing, and इष्णुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेह|गेहं
गेह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A house, a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>ग a name of GAṆEŚA, इह to desire, affix घञ्; that deity being usually invoked upon laying the foundations of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहनर्द्दिन्
गेहनर्द्दिन्<BR>m. (-र्द्दी)<BR>A lazy or effeminate man, a cotquean.<BR>E.<BR>गेह a house, and नर्द्दिन् who makes a noise: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहशूर
गेहशूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A slothful and trifling man, one who is unfit for concerns beyond those of the house, a cotquean, a house-hero.<BR>E.<BR>गेह a house, and शूर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गेहिन्
गेहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Having a house, a householder, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गेह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गै
गै<BR>r. 1st cl. (गायति)<BR>To sound, to sing.<BR>With उद् or प्र prefixed;<BR>(उद्गायति प्रगायति)<BR>To sing, to chaunt, to sing out or aloud.<BR>(उद्गीयते प्रगीयते)<BR>To be sung or chaunted.<BR>With वि<BR>(विगायति)<BR>To assert repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैर
गैर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरिक|गैरिकं|गैरिकः
गैरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mountain, mountain-born or produced.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Red chalk, or as sometimes applied, red orpiment.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गैरेय|गैरेयं
गैरेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Mountain, mountaineer, mountain-born.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Bitumen.<BR>2 Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>गिरि a mountain, affix ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गो
गो<BR>m. (-गौः)<BR>1 Heaven, Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>3 A ray of light.<BR>4 The thunderbolt.<BR>5 The moon.<BR>6 The sun.<BR>7 A kind of sacrifice, the sacrifice of a cow.<BR>8 The moment of the sun's entering Taurus.<BR>mn. (-गौः-गु)<BR>1 The hair of the body.<BR>2 Water: (in the last sense some confine it to the mas. plu. गावः and according to others, it is neuter in several other senses.)<BR>f. (-गौः)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 The eye.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 A quarter, as the east, west, &c.<BR>5 Speech; also identified with the goddess of speech, SARASVATĪ.<BR>6 The earth.<BR>7 A mother.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, and डो Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकण्टक|गोकंटक|गोकण्टकः
गोकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The name of a plant: see गोखुर.<BR>2 The print of a cow's hoof or spot so marked.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth or a cow, &c. and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकर्ण|गोकर्णः
गोकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A span from the tip of the thumb to that of the little finger.<BR>2 A kind of deer, (the Nīlgau?)<BR>3 A mule.<BR>4 A class of demigods.<BR>5 A kind of snake.<BR>6 A snake in general.<BR>7 A place of pilgrimage on the Malabar coast.<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides): see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and कर्ण an ear, having ears like a cow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिराटिका
गोकिराटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird, considered as one kind of the common Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, and किर a hog, अट who goes, with कन् added in the fem. form; resembling a hog, feeding on ordure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=297" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकिल|गोकिलः
गोकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plough.<BR>2 A pestle.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, and किल to go, affix क; also गोकील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकील|गोकीलः
गोकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A pestle.<BR>2 A plough.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुल|गोकुलं
गोकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A herd of kine, a multitude of cattle.<BR>2 A cowhouse or station.<BR>3 A village or tract on the Jumna, the residence of NANDA and of KṚṢṆA during his youth.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and कुल an assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकुलिक|गोकुलिकः
गोकुलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Squint-eyed.<BR>2 One who gives help to a cow in the mud.<BR>E.<BR>गो the eye, &c. and कुल to accumulate, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोकृत|गोकृतं
गोकृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुर|गोक्षुरः
गोक्षुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a plant; also Gokhura, (Ruellia longifolia, Rox. it is also applied in Bengal to Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A cow's hoof.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and क्षुर a hoof, the thorns getting between the hoofs of cattle; also with कन् added गोक्षुरक, and with खुर a hoof, गोखुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोक्षुरक|गोक्षुरकः
गोक्षुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोखुर|गोखुरः
गोखुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>See गोक्षुर; also गोखुरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोयुग|गोगोयुगं
गोगोयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A pair of oxen.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and गोयुग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगोष्ठ|गोगोष्ठं
गोगोष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A cattle shed.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and गोष्ठ a shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोगृष्टि|गोगृष्टिः
गोगृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A cow that has had one calf.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and गृष्टि q. v. the same as the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रन्थि|गोग्रंथि|गोग्रन्थिः
गोग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>1 Dried cow-dung.<BR>2 A station for cows, a cowyard or house, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, ग्रन्थ to arrange, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रह|गोग्रहः
गोग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Spoil, booty, capture of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and ग्रह seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोग्रास|गोग्रासः
गोग्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The ceremony of presenting grass to the cow when making atonement.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and ग्रास a mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघ्न|गोघ्नः
गोघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Who or what kills kine.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A guest.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and घ्न what kills, from हन् with टक् affix; a cow being killed on the arrival of the latter, or being presented to him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोघृत|गोघृतं
गोघृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Rain.<BR>2 Ghee made from cow's milk.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, घृत what sprinkles, from घृ to sprinkle or wet, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर|गोचरः
गोचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An object of sense, as sound, shape, colour, &c.<BR>2 A country, a district.<BR>3 The house or mansion of a planet, or its presence in any sign which is that of a person's nativity.<BR>4 Pasturage.<BR>E.<BR>गो an organ of sense, &c. and चर what goes, from चर to go, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचर्म्मन्|गोचर्मन्
गोचर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 A cow's hide.<BR>2 A hide of land, 300 feet long, by 10 broad: it is also defined as that extent of land, the crop of which will support a man for a year.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोचारक|गोचारकः
गोचारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>गो, चर to go, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोछाल|गोच्छाल|गोच्छालः
गोछाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The palm of the hand with the fingers extended, &c. see अलम्बुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजल|गोजलं
गोजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cow's urine.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजागरिक|गोजागरिकं|गोजागरिकः
गोजागरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A prickly nightshade.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Happy, fortunate, auspicious.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, जागृ to wake or to be awake, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोजिह्वा
गोजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A potherb growing wild, (Elephantophus scaber.)<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and जिह्वा a tongue: the leaves being so compared; also with कन् added गोजिह्वका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडु
गोडु<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>A lump of flesh on the navel.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to be sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोडुम्ब|गोडुंब|गोडुंबः|गोडुम्बः
गोडुम्ब<BR>mf. (-म्बः-म्बा)<BR>The water melon.<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, लुवि to hurt, affix अच्, and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोणी
गोणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Torn or ragged clothes.<BR>2 A sack.<BR>3 The measure of a Droṇa.<BR>E.<BR>गुण to reckon, affixes अच् and ङीष्, the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोण्ड|गोंड|गोंडः|गोण्डः
गोण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>A person with a prominent navel.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A man of a low tribe, a mountaineer, especially inhabiting the eastern portion of the Vindhya range, between the Nerbudda and Kṛṣṇa, giving name to the province of Gondwana.<BR>2 A prominent navel, or a lump of flesh on the navel, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गुडि to enclose, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतम|गोतमः
गोतम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The name of a sage; also गौतम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतमान्वय|गोतमान्वयः
गोतमान्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of ŚĀKYA or ŚĀKYA MUNI, a Bauddha sage.<BR>E.<BR>गोतम a sage, and अन्वय lineage; the descendant of GOTAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोतल्लज|गोतल्लजः
गोतल्लज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An excellent cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, तल्लज implying excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्र|गोत्रं|गोत्रः
गोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Family, race, lineage, kin.<BR>2 A name, an appellation.<BR>3 A forest.<BR>4 A field.<BR>5 A Catta, an umbrella or parasol.<BR>6 A road.<BR>7 Knowledge of futurity, inspiration.<BR>8 A genus, a class or species.<BR>9 A caste, a tribe or subdivision of it into families, as in that of the Brahman; twenty-four Gotras are reckoned, supposed to be sprung from and named after celebrated teachers, as ŚĀṆḌILYA, KAŚYAPA, GAUTAMA, BHĀRADVĀJA, &c.<BR>10 Increase.<BR>11 Wealth.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A herd of kine.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>गु to sound, and त्र Uṇādi affix, or गो the earth, &c. and त्र what preserves, from त्रै with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रज|गोत्रजः
गोत्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A relation: in law, the term is nearly equivalent to the Gentile of Roman law, and is applied to kindred of the same general family, who are connected by offerings of food and water, and stands opposed to the Bandhu or cognate kin, who do not partake in the offerings to the common ancestors: see बन्धु.<BR>E.<BR>गोत्र as above, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्रभिद्
गोत्रभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद् or भित्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>गोत्र a mountain, and भिद् who splits, (with his thunderbolt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोत्ररिक्थ
गोत्ररिक्थ<BR>n. (-क्थं)<BR>Patrimony, inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>गोत्र, and रिक्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोद|गोदः
गोद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what gives a cow.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The brain.<BR>E.<BR>गो light or a cow, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदन्त|गोदंत|गोदन्तं
गोदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>2 A cow's tooth.<BR>3 A fossile substance of a white colour, apparently an earthy salt.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and दन्त a tooth, a cow's tooth, from its similar hardness, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदा
गोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The Godāvarī river.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, and द who gives: see गोदावरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदान
गोदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and दान gift; also गोप्रदान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदारण|गोदारणं
गोदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A plough.<BR>2 A spade or hoe.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, and दारण what cuts or tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=298" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदावरी
गोदावरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The name of a river in the peninsula, the Godāvarī.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, and द what gives, गोद and आवृ to cover or conceal; affixes अप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदुग्ध
गोदुग्ध<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>Cow's milk.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदुह्
गोदुह्<BR>m. (-धुक्)<BR>A cowherd, a milkman.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, दुह to milk, and क्विप् affix; also with क affix गोदुह, nom. (-हः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोदोहनी
गोदोहनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A milk pail.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and दुह to milk, with ल्युट् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोद्रव|गोद्रवः
गोद्रव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Cow's urine.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and द्रव what runs from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधन|गोधनं|गोधनः
गोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A herd of cows, a multitude or number of cattle, especially if considered as property.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A large headed arrow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधा
गोधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A leathern fence worn by archers on the left arm, to prevent its being injured by the bowstring.<BR>2 An iguana, either the Gosamp or the alligator.<BR>E.<BR>गुध to surround, affixes अङ् and टाप्; see गोधिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधापदिका
गोधापदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cissus pedata.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधापदी
गोधापदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>E.<BR>गोधा, and पद for पाद a foot, affix ङीष्, the root being compared to an alligator's foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधि|गोधिः
गोधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The forehead.<BR>2 The Gangetic alligator.<BR>3 An iguana.<BR>E.<BR>गो the eye or water, and धा to possess, with कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधिका
गोधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The Gangetic alligator.<BR>2 The iguana.<BR>E.<BR>कन् with the fem. form added to गोधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधिकात्मज|गोधिकात्मजः
गोधिकात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The iguana.<BR>E.<BR>गोधा an alligator, and आत्मज offspring, here used to imply diminution: so गोधिकापुत्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधुम|गोधुमः
गोधुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Wheat: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूम|गोधूमः
गोधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Wheat.<BR>2 The orange.<BR>3 The name of a drug.<BR>E.<BR>गुध to surround, and ऊम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूमचूर्ण|गोधूमचूर्णं
गोधूमचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्लं)<BR>Wheat flour.<BR>E.<BR>गोधूम, and चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूमसम्भव|गोधूमसंभव|गोधूमसम्भवं
गोधूमसम्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sour paste.<BR>E.<BR>गोधूम, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधूलि|गोधूलिः
गोधूलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A period of the day, in the hot season when the sun is half risen; in the cold and dewy seasons, when the sun is full but mild; and in the three other seasons, sunset.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधेनु|गोधेनुः
गोधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A milch cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and धेनु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोधेर|गोधेरः
गोधेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A guardian, a protector, a preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनन्दी|गोनंदी
गोनन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>The female of the Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, नदि to be happy, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनर्द|गोनर्दः|गोनर्द्द|गोनर्द्दं|गोनर्द्दः
गोनर्द<BR>m. (-र्दः)<BR>The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>n. (-र्दं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>गो water, नर्द to sound, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनर्द्दीय|गोनर्दीय|गोनर्दीयः|गोनर्द्दीयः
गोनर्द्दीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of the saint PATAÑJALI, the founder of the Yoga philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>गो heaven, नर्द्दीय to be sounded or celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनस|गोनसः
गोनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A large kind of snake, by some considered to be the same with the Boa or Bor.<BR>2 A kind of gem.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and नस a nose, cow-nosed; also गोनास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनाथ|गोनाथः
गोनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 A herdsman.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and नाथ master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनास|गोनासं|गोनासः
गोनास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A snake: see गोनास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोनिष्यन्द|गोनिष्यंद|गोनिष्यन्दः
गोनिष्यन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>Cow's urine.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and निष्यन्द what oozes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप|गोपः
गोप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 A helper, a friend or patron.<BR>2 A preserver, a cherisher.<BR>3 Who or what hides or conceals.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Superintendent of a district.<BR>2 The head of a cowpen.<BR>3 A herdsman, a cowherd, a milkman by caste and occupation.<BR>4 A king.<BR>5 Myrrh: see गोपरस.<BR>f. (-पा or -पी)<BR>A plant, (Echites frutescens).<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A milkwoman, a female cowherd.<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>1 A cowherd's wife, but especially applied to those of Vṛndāvana, the companions and objects of KṚṢṆA'S juvenile sports, and who are considered sometimes as holy or celestial personages.<BR>2 A protectress.<BR>3 Nature, elementary nature.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, &c. and प what preserves; also in some senses गुप to hide, to protect, &c. affix घञ्, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपक|गोपकः
गोपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>One who guards or protects.<BR>(-कः)<BR>1 Myrrh.<BR>2 The superintendant of a district.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपकन्या
गोपकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>1 The daughter of a cowherd.<BR>2 A nymph of Vṛndāvana.<BR>3 A medicinal plant.<BR>E.<BR>गोप, and कन्या a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपघोण्टा
गोपघोण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>A wild sort of jujube, (Zizyphus nepeca.)<BR>E.<BR>गोप a cowherd, and घोण्टा the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपति|गोपतिः
गोपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Of INDRA.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A king.<BR>5 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, &c. and पति lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपतिचाप
गोपतिचाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>गोपति INDRA, and चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपदल|गोपदलः
गोपदल<BR>m. (लः)<BR>The areca tree.<BR>E.<BR>गोप preserving, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपन|गोपनं
गोपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Protecting, guarding.<BR>2 Concealment, hiding.<BR>3 Reviling, abuse.<BR>4 Flurry, hurry, alarm.<BR>5 Light, lustre.<BR>6 The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to hide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनीय|गोपनीयं
गोपनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Secret, mysterious, to be concealed or hidden.<BR>2 To be preserved or protected.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to hide, &c. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपबधू
गोपबधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>1 The wife of a cowherd.<BR>2 A plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa.)<BR>E.<BR>गोप, and वधू a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपबधूटी
गोपबधूटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>The youthful wife of a cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपभद्र|गोपभद्रं
गोपभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The fibrous root of a waterlily.<BR>E.<BR>गोप a cowherd, and भद्र lucky, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपभद्रिका
गोपभद्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a tree: see गम्भारी.<BR>E.<BR>गोप a preserver, and भद्र auspicious, and कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपरस|गोपरसः
गोपरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>गोप secret, and रस juice, exuding in a manner or place unknown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपवल्ली
गोपवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens): see श्यामलता.<BR>2 Another plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa.)<BR>E.<BR>गोप a cowherd, and वल्ली a pedicle, being used in medicines for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाटविक
गोपाटविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and पाटविक clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपानसी
गोपानसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 The wood of a thatch.<BR>2 A crooked beam which supports it.<BR>3 The bamboo frame work on which it rests.<BR>E.<BR>गोप preserving, affixes नसट् and ङीष्, आ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायक
गोपायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A preserver, a cherisher, one who guards or protects.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to preserve, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायित|गोपायितं
गोपायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Preserved, protected, cherished.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to protect, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाल|गोपालः
गोपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A cowherd.<BR>3 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, &c. and पाल who preserves or protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालक|गोपालकः
गोपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A cow keeper or protector.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow or the earth, पाल् to cherish, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=299" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपालिका
गोपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of worm.<BR>2 A female cowherd: see गोपालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपाष्टमी
गोपाष्टमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The eighth lunation of the light half of Kārttika, on which KṚṢṆA became a cowherd; cows are to be worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>गोप, and अष्टमी the eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिन्
गोपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>A protector, one who preserves or protects.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>2 A cowherd's wife.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to preserve, णिनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिका
गोपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female cowherd, &c.: see गोपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिल|गोपिलः
गोपिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>One who preserves or protects.<BR>E.<BR>गुप, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपीचन्दन
गोपीचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A species of white clay, said to be brought from Dvārakā, and used by the worshippers of VIṢṆU to smear their faces with.<BR>E.<BR>गोपी, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपीथ|गोपीथं|गोपीथः
गोपीथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Preserving, protecting.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>A holy place, a place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>गोप preserving, and थक् Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुच्छ|गोपुच्छः
गोपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 A cowtail.<BR>2 A sort of necklace, one of four or thirty-four strings.<BR>3 A sort of monkey.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and पुच्छ a tail, resembling or possessing a cow's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुटा
गोपुटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुटिक|गोपुटिकं
गोपुटिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A temple or edifice consecrated to ŚIVA'S bull.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and पट to enclose, affix इकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुर|गोपुरं
गोपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A town gate.<BR>2 A gate in general.<BR>3 The ornamented gateway of a temple.<BR>4 A kind of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>गुप to preserve, and ऊरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपुरीष|गोपुरीषं
गोपुरीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and पुरीष dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपेन्द्र|गोपेंद्र|गोपेन्द्रः
गोपेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>गोप a cowherd, and इन्द्र lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपेश|गोपेशः
गोपेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚĀKYA MUNI, a Buddha.<BR>2 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A chief herdsman, the keeper or owner of kine.<BR>4 A name of NANDA.<BR>E.<BR>गोप a cowherd, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्तृ
गोप्तृ<BR>mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ)<BR>A preserver, a protector, one who defends or cherishes.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to preserve, &c. affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्य|गोप्यः
गोप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>1 To be cherished or preserved.<BR>2 To be kept secret or hidden.<BR>3 To be kept, to be taken care of.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>1 A slave.<BR>2 The son of a female slave.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to preserve, &c. ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्यक|गोप्यकः
गोप्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A servant or slave.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्याधि|गोप्याधिः
गोप्याधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>A pledge, that is not to be used, but to be carefully preserved.<BR>E.<BR>गोप्य to be preserved, and आधि a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्रकाण्ड|गोप्रकांड|गोप्रकाण्डं
गोप्रकाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>An excellent cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and प्रकाण्ड excellent; the compound is always neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्रचार|गोप्रचारः
गोप्रचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Pasturage ground.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and प्रचार going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोफणा
गोफणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A sling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोबध
गोबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Killing a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोबाल|गोबालः
गोबाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The hair of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and बाल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोभण्डीर|गोभण्डीरः
गोभण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A water fowl.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, भडि to sound, affix ईरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोम
गोम<BR>r. 10th cl. (गोमयति)<BR>To smear, to anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमक्षिका
गोमक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A gadfly.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and मक्षिका a fly: stinging cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमण्डल|गोमंडल
गोमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The earth, the globe.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमत्|गोमन्त्
गोमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Possessing herds, rich in cattle.<BR>f. (-मती)<BR>The name of a river, the Goomtī, in the province of Oude.<BR>2 A prayer or formula of the Vedas, to be repeated during expiation for killing a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow or water, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमतल्लिका
गोमतल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tractable and good cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, मतल्लिका excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमध्यमध्य
गोमध्यमध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्वं)<BR>Slender in the waist.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, &c. मध्य middle: repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमन्त|गोमन्तः
गोमन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The name of a mountain.<BR>2 An owner of cattle.<BR>3 A herd of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, मन to mind, झच्^1 aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमय|गोमयं|गोमयः
गोमय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>1 Cowdung.<BR>2 The property or nature of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and मयट् affix of relation or comprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयछत्र|गोमयच्छत्र|गोमयच्छत्रं
गोमयछत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A mushroom, a fungus.<BR>E.<BR>गोमय cowdung, and छत्र a Catta or parasol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयछविका
गोमयछविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of fungus or mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>कन् and the fem. form added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयप्रिय|गोमयप्रियं
गोमयप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A sort of grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>E.<BR>गोमय cowdung, and प्रिय favourable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयोत्था
गोमयोत्था<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>A kind of beetle found in cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गोमय cowdung, and उत्थ what rises or is generated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमयोद्भव|गोमयोद्भवः
गोमयोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Cassia fistula.<BR>E.<BR>गोमय, and उद्भव born, produced, requiring manure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमायु|गोमायुः
गोमायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A jackall.<BR>2 A kind of Gandharba or celestial musician.<BR>3 The bile or bilious humor of the cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो sound, &c. मा to measure, and उण् Uṇādi affix, य inserted, or गो a cow, and मायु bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिथुन
गोमिथुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A pair of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and मिथुन a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिन्
गोमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Rich in herds, &c.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 The owner of cattle.<BR>2 A jackall.<BR>3 A worshipper.<BR>4 An attendant on a Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, &c. मिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमिल
गोमिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Name of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमीन|गोमीनः
गोमीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of fish, the bull-fish.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and मीन a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमुख|गोमुखं|गोमुखः
गोमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 A house built unevenly or crookedly, viz. with angles, projections, &c.<BR>2 A kind of musical instrument, (a sort of horn or trumpet?)<BR>3 Spreading unguents, plastering, smearing.<BR>4 A hole in a wall made by thieves, &c a breach.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A shark.<BR>2 A kind of Yakṣa; according to the Jainas, a demigod subservient to their deified saints.<BR>nf. (-खं-खी)<BR>A cloth-bag, containing a rosary into which the hand is thrust to count the beads.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>The chasm in the Himālaya mountains through which the Ganges flows, erroneously conceived by the Hindus to be of the shape of a cow's mouth.<BR>2 A river in Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and मुख face, having the face of a cow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूढ
गोमूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Stupid as an ox.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and मूढ foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्र|गोमूत्रं
गोमूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Cow's urine.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and मूत्र urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमूत्रिका
गोमूत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of grass, described as growing in corn fields, of a reddish colour, and eaten by cattle, commonly Tāmbāda (तांवड.)<BR>2 A verse the second half of which repeats nearly all the syllables of the first.<BR>3 A form of calculation.<BR>E.<BR>गो, मूत्र urine, कन् affix; operating on cows as a diuretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेद|गोमेदः
गोमेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A yellow gem: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=300" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेदक|गोमेदकं|गोमेदकः
गोमेदक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A gem or precious stone brought from the Himālaya and Indus, described as of four sorts, white, pale yellow, red, and dark blue, perhaps varieties of agate.<BR>2 A kind of poison: see काकोल.<BR>3 Smearing the body with unguents.<BR>E.<BR>गो the eye, मिद to anoint, &c. affix घञ् and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेदसन्निभ|गोमेदसंनिभ|गोमेदसन्निभः
गोमेदसन्निभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Chalcedony or opal.<BR>E.<BR>गोमेद, and सन्निभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोमेध|गोमेधः
गोमेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The offering or sacrifice of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and मेध sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयान
गोयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A cart.<BR>2 A carriage drawn by oxen.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and आत a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोयुग
गोयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A yoke of oxen.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्ष|गोरक्षः
गोरक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>A cow-keeper, the cherisher or preserver of kine.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The orange.<BR>2 Keeping or tending cattle.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A small shrub.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and रक्ष who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षक
गोरक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cow keeper, one who tends cattle.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षजम्बू
गोरक्षजम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>1 Wheat.<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides); also गाङ्गेरुकौ.<BR>3 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>E.<BR>गोरक्ष, and जम्बू a rose-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षण
गोरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Tending or taking charge of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and रक्षण protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्षतण्डुला
गोरक्षतण्डुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>गोरक्ष cow-preserving, and तण्डुल grain, used in medicines for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरक्ष्य
गोरक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Tending cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and रक्ष्य to be preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरङ्कु|गोरंकु|गोरङ्कुः
गोरङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>1 A waterfowl.<BR>2 A prisoner, a person or animal confined.<BR>3 A naked man, a mendicant, &c. wandering about without clothes.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, sky, &c. रङ्कु a kind of deer: as it were, the water deer, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरण|गोरणं
गोरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>गुर to make effort, affix ल्युट्; also गुरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरस|गोरसः
गोरस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>1 Milk.<BR>2 Curdled or coagulated milk.<BR>3 Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरसज|गोरसजं
गोरसज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Buttermilk.<BR>2 Curds.<BR>E.<BR>गोरस, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोराज|गोराजः
गोराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and राजन् a king, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोराटी
गोराटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A small bird, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>गो speech, रट to utter, affix घञ्, feminine affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरुत|गोरुतं
गोरुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A measure of distance equal to two Cros or Cos: see गव्यूति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरोच|गोरोचं
गोरोच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and रोच what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोरोचना
गोरोचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A bright yellow pigment prepared from the urine of a cow, or vomited in the shape of scibulæ by the animal; or according to some, found in the head of a cow; it is employed in painting and dying, and is of especial virtue in marking the foreheads of the Hindus with the Tilaka or sectarial mark; it is also used in medicine as a sedative, tonic, and anthelmintic remedy, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, रुचि to shine, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोर्द्द|गोर्द|गोर्दः|गोर्द्दं
गोर्द्द<BR>n. (-र्द्दं)<BR>The brain.<BR>E.<BR>गुर to endeavor, and दन affix; also गोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोल|गोलं|गोलः
गोल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A circle, a ball, any thing round or globular.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A widow's bastard.<BR>2 Myrrh.<BR>3 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>4 A globe, celestial or terrestrial.<BR>5 Conjunction of planets, or the presence of several in one sign.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A globe, a sphere, a Mandala.<BR>2 A wooden ball with which children play.<BR>3 A woman's female friend.<BR>4 The Godāvarī river.<BR>5 A large water jar.<BR>6 Ink.<BR>7 Red arsenic.<BR>8 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>गो heaven, water, &c. and ल what gets or receives; again, गुड to be round, &c. affix घञ् and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलक|गोलकं|गोलकः
गोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wooden ball for playing with, or any thing globular, a sphere, a globe, &c.<BR>2 A widow's bastard.<BR>3 A water jar.<BR>4 Gum myrrh.<BR>5 Pease.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The heaven of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलाङ्गुल|गोलांगुल|गोलाङ्गुलः
गोलाङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of monkey, described as of a black colour, and having a tail like a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and लाङ्गुल a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलाध्याय|गोलाध्यायः
गोलाध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The division of mathematical science which treats of the spheres, spherics.<BR>E.<BR>गोल the globe, and अध्याय chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलास|गोलासः
गोलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A mushroom, a kind of fungus springing from cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलिह|गोलिहः
गोलिह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and लिह to lick, affix क; upon which kine graze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलीढ|गोलीढः
गोलीढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and लिह as above, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोक|गोलोकं|गोलोकः
गोलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The heaven of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोमिका
गोलोमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of small shrub.<BR>E.<BR>गोलोमन् cow's hair, कन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोलोमी
गोलोमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 A kind of bent grass, with white blossoms; also श्वेतदूर्व्वा.<BR>2 Root of sweet flag.<BR>3 Orris root.<BR>4 A whore, a harlot.<BR>5 A small shrub.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, &c. and लोमन् hair, the hair of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवन्दनी
गोवन्दनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant bearing a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>गो the earth, and वन्दनी praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवर्द्धन
गोवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A celebrated hill in Vindrāvan or the country about Mathura; it was upheld by KṚṢṆA upon one finger, to shelter the cowherds from a storm excited by INDRA, as a test of the former's divinity.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and वर्द्धन encreasing; pasturing cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवर्द्धनधर
गोवर्द्धनधर<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>गोवर्द्धन Govardhana, and धर who upholds: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवशा
गोवशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A barren cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and वशा barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविन्द|गोविंद|गोविन्दः
गोविन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 One of the most usual appellations of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU in that form.<BR>2 A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER.<BR>2 A cowkeeper, one who protects, cherishes or owns cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो language, here the language of the Vedas especially, and विन्द who knows, from विद to know, with श affix; also गो heaven, a cow, विद to obtain, by whom heaven is obtained, or who obtains felicity by protecting kine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोविष्
गोविष्<BR>f. (-विद्)<BR>Cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and विष् ordure; also गोविष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृन्द|गोवृंद|गोवृन्दं
गोवृन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>1 Property in cattle, possession of flocks and herds.<BR>2 A herd, a drove of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and वृन्द a heap, a multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=301" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृन्दारक|गोवृंदारक|गोवृन्दारकः
गोवृन्दारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A capital cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and वृन्दारक affix of pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोवृष|गोवृषः
गोवृष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and वृष best, pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोव्रज|गोव्रजः
गोव्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A station for cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो and व्रज a pen, a fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशकृत्
गोशकृत्<BR>n. (-कृत्)<BR>Cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and शकृत् ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशाल|गोशालं
गोशाल<BR>mfn. sub. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A cowhouse.<BR>adj.<BR>Born in a cowhouse.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशीर्ष|गोशीर्षं|गोशीर्षः
गोशीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>1 A kind of Sandal, described as of the colour of brass, and of great fragrance.<BR>2 The head of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and शीर्ष the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशीर्षक|गोशीर्षकः
गोशीर्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant; also called Droṇapuṣpī.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to गोशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोशृङ्ग|गोशृङ्गः
गोशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A tree; also Berbera.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The horn of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं|गोष्ठः
गोष्ठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (गोष्ठते)<BR>To assemble, to collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठ|गोष्ठं|गोष्ठः
गोष्ठ<BR>mn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठं)<BR>1 A cowpen, a fold for cattle, any place where animals are kept.<BR>2 A station of cowherds.<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1 An assembly, a meeting.<BR>2 Conversation, discourse, dialogue, dispute.<BR>3 Family connexions, but especially the dependant or junior branches.<BR>4 A dramatic composition in one act.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and ष्ठ from स्था to stay, with क affix; here meaning the place of abiding, or गोष्ठ to assemble, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठवेदिका
गोष्ठवेदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A mound or altar in a cowpen.<BR>E.<BR>गोष्ठ, and वेदिका a mound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठश्व|गोष्ठश्वः
गोष्ठश्व<BR>mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं)<BR>Malignant, censorious, envious: especially applied to a person who stays at home, and slanders his neighbours.<BR>E.<BR>गोष्ठ a cowpen, in the first case used for abode in general, and श्वि to increase, affix ड, who magnifies himself in his own house.<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A horse in a cowpen.<BR>E.<BR>गोष्ठ, and अश्व a horse, the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठाष्टमी
गोष्ठाष्टमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>A particular holiday: see गोपाष्टमी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्ठीपति|गोष्ठीपतिः
गोष्ठीपति<BR>m. (-ति)<BR>1 The chief person in assembly, a president.<BR>2 The master of a family.<BR>E.<BR>गोष्ठी, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोष्पद|गोष्पदं
गोष्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 A spot frequented by kine.<BR>2 A measure, as much as a cow's footstep will hold.<BR>3 The mark or impression of a cow's foot.<BR>4 A cow's foot or hoof.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and पद for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस|गोसः
गोस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Gum myrrh.<BR>2 The last watch of the night, early morning or day-break.<BR>E.<BR>गो water, dew, and षो to destroy, to absorb, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसंख्य
गोसंख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A herdsman, a cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and सम् prefixed to ख्या to count, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसगृह
गोसगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The inner part of a house, an inner or sleeping room, a bedchamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसङ्ग|गोसंग|गोसङ्गः
गोसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and सङ्ग meeting, junction; the herd assembling at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसदृक्ष|गोसदृक्षः
गोसदृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Gayal, (Bos gavæus.)<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and सदृक्ष like, from सदृश with स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसन्दाय|गोसंदाय|गोसन्दायः
गोसन्दाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>One who gives a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, दा to give, with सम् prefixed, युक् augment, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसम्भव|गोसंभव
गोसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced from or by a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसर्ग|गोसर्गः
गोसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and सर्ग going forth, the cattle then going forth to pasture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसव|गोसवः
गोसव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sacrifice of a cow, one of the grand sacrifices of the Hindus in former times, and not permitted in the present or Kali age: see गोमेध.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and सव sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोसशश|गोसशशः
गोसशश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Myrrh: see गोस and शश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्तन|गोस्तनः
गोस्तन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The udder of a cow.<BR>2 A garland consisting of four or of thirty-four strings.<BR>3 A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay, &c.<BR>f. (-ना or नी)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and लन a breast, full or clustering like the udder of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्थान|गोस्थानं
गोस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A cowpen, a station for cattle.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and स्थान a place; also with कन् added गोस्थानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्थानक|गोस्थानकं
गोस्थानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोस्वामिन्
गोस्वामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 The master or possessor of herds.<BR>2 A holy man, a religious personage and teacher; in common language, a Gosain.<BR>E.<BR>गो kine, or an organ of sense, and स्वामिन् a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहत्या
गोहत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Killing a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and हत्या murder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहन्न|गोहन्नं
गोहन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>गो and हन्न ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहरीतकी
गोहरीतकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Vilva or Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहित|गोहितः
गोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proper or fit for cattle.<BR>2 Cherishing or protecting kine.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A creeping plant; also घोषा.<BR>2 The Bel tree.<BR>E.<BR>गो a cow, and हित suitable, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोहिर|गोहिरं
गोहिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The heel.<BR>E.<BR>गूह to cover, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोह्य|गोह्यं
गोह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be covered or concealed.<BR>2 To be kept secret.<BR>E.<BR>गूह to cover, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौञ्जिक|गौंजिक|गौंजिकः|गौञ्जिकः
गौञ्जिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>गुञ्जा the small weight especially used by goldsmiths, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौड|गौडः
गौड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The district of Gaur, the central part of Bengal, extending from Bang to Bhuvaneswar in Orissa: the ruins of its capital, called by the same name, are still extensive.<BR>m. plu. (-डाः)<BR>The inhabitants of Gaur.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>1 Rum or spirit distilled from Gur or molasses.<BR>2 One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>3 A style of poetry, the bold and spirited style.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to surround, or गुड raw sugar, and अण् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौडिक|गौडिकं|गौडिकः
गौडिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or relating to Gur or molasses.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rum.<BR>E.<BR>गुड as above, affix of relation ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौण|गौणः
गौण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 Having qualities or attributes.<BR>2 Relating to multiplication or enumeration.<BR>3 Secondary, subordinate.<BR>4 Secondary as applied to the month, reckoned from fullmoon to full moon.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौणिक
गौणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having qualities, relating to or connected with them.<BR>E.<BR>गुण, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौतम|गौतमः
गौतम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The name of a saint or sage and founder of the Nyāya philosophy.<BR>2 A legislator of the same name.<BR>3 A name of ŚĀKYA Muni, the original Buddha or founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>4 A name of the first pupil of the last Jina.<BR>5 Name of a tribe or family of Brahmans descended from GOTAMA.<BR>6 A poison, one of the fixed kinds, or mineral, vegetable, &c.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A female Rākṣasa or goblin.<BR>3 A yellow dye: see गोरोचना.<BR>4 The Godāvarī river.<BR>E.<BR>गोतम a sage, and अण् patronymic^1 affix, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधार|गौधारः
गौधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An iguana.<BR>E.<BR>गोधा an alligator, and आरक् affix of descent; considered as the offspring of the alligator, on account of its smaller size, and similar shape; also गौधेय and गाधेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=302" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधेय|गौधेयः
गौधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An iguana.<BR>E.<BR>गोधा, and ढक् affix: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौधेर|गौधेरः
गौधेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An iguana.<BR>E.<BR>गौधा, and द्रक् affix: see गौधार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौपुच्छिक
गौपुच्छिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or belonging to a cow's tail, bought for a cow's tail, &c.<BR>E.<BR>गो, and पुच्छ a tail, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौर|गौरं|गौरः
गौर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Yellow.<BR>3 Pale red: (or it may be used as a noun substantive mas. to imply either of these colours.)<BR>4 Clean, cleansed, pure.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 White mustard.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A tree, (Grislea tomentosa): see धव.<BR>4 A name of CAITANYA.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The filament of a lotus.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 Saffron.<BR>f. (-रा or री)<BR>1 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>(-री)<BR>2 A young girl, eight years old.<BR>3 Any young girl prior to menstruation, a maid, a virgin.<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>5 The wife of the deity VARUṆA.<BR>6 The earth.<BR>7 Turmeric.<BR>8 A yellow die called Gorocanā.<BR>9 A plant: see रोचनी.<BR>10 A plant bearing a fragrant seed: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>11 One of the female energies or Śaktis of the Bauddhas.<BR>12 A white kind of Dūrbbā or bent grass.<BR>13 Arabian jasmin.<BR>14 Sacred basil or Tulasi.<BR>15 One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>E.<BR>गुड to sound, and रन् Uṇādi affix, the deriv. is irregular; also गुरी to endeavour, घञ् affix, and derivative irr.; upon whom or what the mind exerts itself; again, गौर white, pure, &c. affix ङीष्, that which is white or brilliant, &c. which applies to the virgin, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरचन्द्र|गौरचन्द्रः
गौरचन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of the saint CAITANYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरव|गौरवं
गौरव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Reputation, respectability, venerableness or weight.<BR>2 Physical weight, heaviness.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु heavy, respectable, &c. and अण् affix, implying condition of being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरवित|गौरवितः
गौरवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Venerable, respectable.<BR>E.<BR>गौरव, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरवेरित
गौरवेरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, famed, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>गौरव fame, and ईरित declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरशाक|गौरशाकः
गौरशाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of bassia; also धूमल.<BR>E.<BR>गौर pale white, and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरसर्षप|गौरसर्षपः
गौरसर्षप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 White mustard.<BR>2 The white mustard seed considered as a measure of weight.<BR>E.<BR>गौर white, and सर्षप mustard; also गौर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौराङ्ग|गौराङ्गः
गौराङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A name of CAITANYA.<BR>E.<BR>गौर pale, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरार्द्रक|गौरार्द्रकः
गौरार्द्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of poison.<BR>E.<BR>गौर white, and आर्द्रक ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरास्य|गौरास्यः
गौरास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A black monkey with a white face.<BR>E.<BR>गौर, and आस्थ face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिका
गौरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A virgin, a young girl, one eight years old, or in whom menstruation has not commenced.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी as above, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरिल|गौरिलः
गौरिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 White mustard.<BR>2 Iron or steel filings or dust.<BR>E.<BR>गौर pale white, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीज|गौरीजं|गौरीजः
गौरीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA or GAṆEŚA.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Tale.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपट्ट|गौरीपट्टः
गौरीपट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>The horizontal plate of the Liṅga, typical of the female organ.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी, and पट्ट a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपति
गौरीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीपुत्त्र
गौरीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A name of the deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी the goddess, and पुत्र a son, the son of GAURĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरीललित|गौरीललितं
गौरीललित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>गौरी the goddess, or a young girl, and ललित loved, liked; this being used as a dye to stain the clothes of women, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौरुतल्पिक|गौरुतल्पिकः
गौरुतल्पिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A violator of the bed of a Guru.<BR>E.<BR>गुरु, तल्प a bed, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौलक्षणिक|गौलक्षणिकः
गौलक्षणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who distinguishes the good marks of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>गो, लक्षण a mark, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौल्य|गौल्यं
गौल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौशतिक|गौशतिकः
गौशतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One possessing a hundred cows.<BR>E.<BR>गौ, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौष्ठीन|गौष्ठीनं
गौष्ठीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The site of an old and abandoned cowpen.<BR>E.<BR>गाष्ठ a cowpen, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौसहस्रिक
गौसहस्रिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who has a thousand cows.<BR>E.<BR>गो, सहस्र a thousand, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथ
ग्रथ<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) ग्रथि (ग्रन्थते)<BR>1 To be crooked.<BR>2 To be crooked metaphorically, to be wicked.<BR>2 To curve, to bend or make crooked.<BR>3 To string together, to arrange.<BR>r. 10th cl. (ग्रन्थयति)<BR>To bind or tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रथित|ग्रथितं
ग्रथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strung, tied together or in order.<BR>2 Collected.<BR>3 Arranged, classed.<BR>4 Overcome.<BR>5 Hurt, injured.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रथि to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थ|ग्रंथ|ग्रंथः|ग्रन्थः
ग्रन्थ<BR>r. 1st, 9th and 10th cls. (ग्रन्थति ग्रथ्नाति ग्रन्थयति)<BR>To string, to tie together, to connect or arrange in a regular series.<BR>With उद् prefixed,<BR>To untie, to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थ|ग्रंथ|ग्रंथः|ग्रन्थः
ग्रन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 Stringing or tying together, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>2 Wealth, property.<BR>3 A book or composition in prose or verse.<BR>4 A metre or measure of thirty-two syllables.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ to dispose or arrange, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकर्त्तृ|ग्रन्थकर्तृ
ग्रन्थकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>An author.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ, and कर्त्तृ maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकार|ग्रंथकार
ग्रन्थकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An author.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थकुटी|ग्रंथकुटी
ग्रन्थकुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>An office, a study, a library.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ a book, and कुटी a house or room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थन|ग्रंथन|ग्रंथनं|ग्रन्थनं
ग्रन्थन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Arranging, stringing, tying or connecting together either as a chaplet or a book.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ to arrange, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थविस्तर|ग्रंथविस्तर|ग्रन्थविस्तरः
ग्रन्थविस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A voluminous work.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ, and विस्तर extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थि|ग्रंथि|ग्रंथिः|ग्रन्थिः
ग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>1 The joint or knot of a reed or cane, &c.<BR>2 A tie, the knot of a cord, &c.<BR>3 A joint or articulation of the body.<BR>4 A plant, commonly Ganṭhiāla: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>5 Crookedness, distortion.<BR>6 A complaint, knotting of the vessels as in varicocele, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ to connect, &c. Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिक|ग्रंथिक|ग्रन्थिकं|ग्रंथिकः|ग्रन्थिकः
ग्रन्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An astrologer, a fortune teller.<BR>2 The youngest of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>3 A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The root of long pepper.<BR>2 A kind of resin, Bdellium.<BR>3 A perfume: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, or ग्रन्थ a book, &c. and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थित|ग्रंथित|ग्रन्थितं
ग्रन्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Strung, tied.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ to tie, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिदूर्व्वा|ग्रन्थिदूर्वा
ग्रन्थिदूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A species of Dūrvā grass.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि, and दूर्व्वा Panicum dactylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिन्|ग्रंथिन्
ग्रन्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्थी-न्थिनी-न्थि)<BR>1 Bookish, read, learned.<BR>2 Relating or belonging to a book, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिपर्ण|ग्रंथिपर्ण|ग्रन्थिपर्णं|ग्रन्थिपर्णः
ग्रन्थिपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A plant, and according to some authorities a perfume, commonly called Ganṭhiāla.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थ a knot, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=303" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिबन्धन|ग्रंथिबंधन
ग्रन्थिबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tying a knot.<BR>2 A ligament.<BR>3 Tying together the garments of the bride and bridegroom at the marriage ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिमत्|ग्रंथिमत्|ग्रन्थिमन्त्
ग्रन्थिमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A plant, (Heliotropium indicum); also अस्थिसंहार.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि knot, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिमूल|ग्रन्थिमूलं
ग्रन्थिमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Garlic.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि, a knot, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिल|ग्रंथिल|ग्रन्थिलं|ग्रन्थिलः
ग्रन्थिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Knotted, knotty, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Buïñci (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>2 Karīr, a thorny plant, (Capparis): see करीर.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Green or undried ginger.<BR>2 Root of long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि a knot, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिवर्हिन्
ग्रन्थिवर्हिन्<BR>m. (-र्ही)<BR>A plant: see ग्रन्थिपर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि a knot, वर्ह to cover, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थिहर|ग्रंथिहर|ग्रन्थिहरः
ग्रन्थिहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रन्थि a knot, and हर who removes; who unites the knots of business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रन्थीक|ग्रन्थीकं
ग्रन्थीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of long pepper: see ग्रन्थिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस
ग्रस<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) ग्रसु (ग्रसते)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To swallow, to devour.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (ग्रसति ग्रासयति)<BR>To take, to seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसन|ग्रसनं
ग्रसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Swallowing, eating.<BR>2 Taking, seizing.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसमान
ग्रसमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Swallowing, devouring.<BR>2 Receiving or listening to any thing eagerly.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to eat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रसिष्णु
ग्रसिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Eating, taking food.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to eat, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्त|ग्रस्तं
ग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Inarticulately pronounced, slurred, uttered with the omission of a letter or syllable.<BR>2 Eaten.<BR>3 Taken, seized.<BR>4 Affected by.<BR>5 Commenced as an eclipse, eclipsed.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रस्तास्त
ग्रस्तास्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Commenced and ended as an eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस्त seized, अस्त set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह|ग्रहः
ग्रह<BR>r. 1st, and 10th cls. (ग्रहति ग्रहयति) r. 9th cl. (ऊ) ग्रहू (गृह्णाति गृह्णीते)<BR>1 To take, to seize, to receive or accept.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To favour, to shew kindness to.<BR>With अव,<BR>To oppose.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To deposit, to trust.<BR>With उप,<BR>To provide.<BR>2 To favour.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To take, to arrest.<BR>2 To punish.<BR>3 To restrain.<BR>With परि,<BR>To lay hold of, to seize.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>1 To assent to, to receive as a precept or truth.<BR>2 To embrace, to enfold, to comprehend or contain.<BR>3 To subdue.<BR>4 To accept.<BR>With वि,<BR>To quarrel, to fight.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To collect, to assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रह|ग्रहः
ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking, whether by seizure or acceptance.<BR>2 An eclipse or seizure of the sun or moon, by RĀHU, &c.<BR>3 A planet.<BR>4 The place of a planet in the fixed zodiac.<BR>5 A moveable point in the heavens.<BR>6 A name of RĀHU, or the ascending node.<BR>7 An imp, one of a particular class, beginning with PŪTANĀ, supposed especially to seize upon young children, producing convulsions.<BR>8 Effort in battle.<BR>9 Tenacity, perseverance.<BR>10 Purpose, design.<BR>11 Favor, patronage.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, &c. affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहकल्लोल|ग्रहकल्लोलः
ग्रहकल्लोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and कल्लोल an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहगण
ग्रहगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The planets taken collectively.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहण|ग्रहणं
ग्रहण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>A prisoner, captive, confined.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, seizure.<BR>2 Receiving, acceptance.<BR>3 Assent, agreement.<BR>4 Respect.<BR>5 The hand.<BR>6 An eclipse.<BR>7 Comprehension, the taking or receiving of instruction, or the acquirement of any science.<BR>8 Sound.<BR>9 An organ of sense.<BR>10 In grammar, Exception.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणान्त|ग्रहणान्तः
ग्रहणान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Close of study, acquirement of science, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रहण taking, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणान्तिक
ग्रहणान्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Termination of holy study.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रहण, and अन्तिक final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणि|ग्रहणिः
ग्रहणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 Diarrhoea, dysentery.<BR>2 The vessels diffusing vital warmth.<BR>3 The small intestines, that part of the alimentary canal where the bile assists digestion.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to seize, अनि Uṇādi affix; also with ङीष् added ग्रहणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीरुज्
ग्रहणीरुज्<BR>f. (-रुक्)<BR>Diarrhoea, dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रहणी the same (as above), and रुज् sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीय
ग्रहणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taken, to be seized, accepted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहणीहर|ग्रहणीहरं
ग्रहणीहर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रहणी diarrhoea, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनायक|ग्रहनायकः
ग्रहनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The planet Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and नायक a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनाश|ग्रहनाशः
ग्रहनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह taking, and नाश injury, producing pain in the bowels, &c. also ग्रहनाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहनेमि|ग्रहनेमिः
ग्रहनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and नेमि the circumference of a wheel, from its shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपति|ग्रहपतिः
ग्रहपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपीडा
ग्रहपीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>The influence of an unpropitious planet.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपुष|ग्रहपुषः
ग्रहपुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and पुष to cherish, affix क; cherishing the planets with his light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहपूजा
ग्रहपूजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Worship of the sun and the other planets.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयाग|ग्रहयागः
ग्रहयाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Worship of or offering to the planets.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and याग sacrifice; also ग्रहयज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहयालु
ग्रहयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Taking, receiving.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, आलुच् affix, अय inserted; also गृहयालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहराज|ग्रहराजः
ग्रहराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 The planet Jupiter or its regent.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह a planet, and राज a king, a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहविप्र|ग्रहविप्रः
ग्रहविप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and विप्र a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाधार|ग्रहाधारः
ग्रहाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The constellation DHRUVA or the polar star.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह planet, and आधार asylum; the star remaining fixed amidst the planetary movements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाधीन
ग्रहाधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Subject to planetary influence.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह, and अधीन dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहामय|ग्रहामयः
ग्रहामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Epilepsy, convulsions, demoniac possession which the complaint is supposed to be.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह an imp, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहाशिन्
ग्रहाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris): see ग्रहनाश.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह taking, and अश here meaning to hurt, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतव्य
ग्रहीतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be taken or accepted.<BR>2 To be learned or acquired.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, तव्य affix, and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रहीतृ
ग्रहीतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Taking, disposed to take.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, तृच् affix, and ई inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम|ग्रामः
ग्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A village, a hamlet, an inhabited and unfortified place in the midst of fields and meadow land, where men of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">Page305</a>] the servile class mostly reside, and where agriculture thrives.<BR>2 A scale in music.<BR>3 (In composition.) A multitude.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, affix घञ् and deriv. irr. or ग्रस to eat, Uṇādi affix मन् and आच् substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=304" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामकुक्कुट|ग्रामकुक्कुटः
ग्रामकुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A tame or domestic cock.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामकूट|ग्रामकूटः
ग्रामकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A man of the fourth tribe, a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, and कूट a number, the crowd or population of the village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामग
ग्रामग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Who or what goes to a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and गम to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामगमिन्
ग्रामगमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going in or to a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and गमिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामगृह्य
ग्रामगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Being or remaining outside the village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and गृह्य to be taken out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामघात|ग्रामघातः
ग्रामघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Plundering a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and धात attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामङ्गमिन्
ग्रामङ्गमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Who or what goes to a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम in the 2d case, गमिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामज
ग्रामज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Village, rustic, village-born or produced.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and ज born; also ग्रामजात, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामणी
ग्रामणी<BR>mfn. (-णीः-णीः-णि)<BR>1 Best, excellent.<BR>2 Chief, pre-eminent, superintendent.<BR>3 One who only thinks of enjoyment.<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>A barber.<BR>f. (-णीः)<BR>1 A whore, a harlot.<BR>2 A female peasant or villager.<BR>3 The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, नी to get or obtain, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामणीपुत्र
ग्रामणीपुत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The son of a whore, a bastard.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रामणी, and पुत्र a son; also read ग्रामणिपुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामतक्ष|ग्रामतक्षः
ग्रामतक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The village carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, and तक्ष carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामतस्
ग्रामतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From the village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामता
ग्रामता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A multitude of villages.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and तल् affix of multitude; also ग्रामत्वं with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामदशेश
ग्रामदशेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The head of ten villages.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, दश ten, and ईश chief; also ग्रामद शाधिपति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामभृत|ग्रामभृतः
ग्रामभृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The village messenger or servant.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and भृत supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममद्गुरिका
ग्राममद्गुरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of fish, (Silurus singio, HAM.)<BR>2 A riot, a fray, a village war, (ग्रामयुद्ध.)<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and मद्गुर a fish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममुख|ग्राममुखः
ग्राममुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A market town, a fair, a market.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, and मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राममृग|ग्राममृगः
ग्राममृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and मृग a deer, the village deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामयाजक|ग्रामयाजकः
ग्रामयाजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The village priest, one who conducts the ceremonies for any or all classes, and is consequently considered as a degraded Brahman; it also applies to the attendant of an idol.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, यज to sacrifice, in the causal form, affix वुन्; also with णिनि affix ग्रामयाजिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामलुण्टन
ग्रामलुण्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Plundering or pillaging a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and लुण्टन robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवास|ग्रामवासः
ग्रामवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A villager.<BR>2 Living in a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and वास abode; also ग्रामेवास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामवासिन्
ग्रामवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A villager.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and वासिन् who inhabits; also ग्रामेवासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामविशेष|ग्रामविशेषः
ग्रामविशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Variety of the scales in music.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामशत
ग्रामशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A hundred villages, a province.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामशतेश
ग्रामशतेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The governor of a province.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, शत and ईश chief; also ग्रामशताधिपति, ग्रामशताध्यक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसङ्कर|ग्रामसंकर|ग्रामसंकरः
ग्रामसङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The common sewer or drain of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and सङ्कर a narrow place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामसङ्घ|ग्रामसंघ|ग्रामसंघः
ग्रामसङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>A village corporation, a municipality.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and सङ्घ an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामस्थ|ग्रामस्थः
ग्रामस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Being or residing in a village, belonging to it, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामहासक|ग्रामहासकः
ग्रामहासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sister's husband.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, and हास who delights, from हस to laugh, &c. and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधान|ग्रामाधानं
ग्रामाधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hunting.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, and आधान what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधिकृत|ग्रामाधिकृतः
ग्रामाधिकृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The head man or chief of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and अधिकृत set over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाधिपति|ग्रामाधिपतिः
ग्रामाधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Chief or head of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and अधिपति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामाध्यक्ष|ग्रामाध्यक्षः
ग्रामाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Superintendent or chief of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and अध्यक्ष superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामान्त|ग्रामांत|ग्रामान्तं|ग्रामान्तः
ग्रामान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Space near a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and अन्त a boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामान्तीय
ग्रामान्तीय<BR>m. (-यं)<BR>Space near a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and अन्त end, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिक|ग्रामिकः
ग्रामिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Village, rude, rustic.<BR>2 Chromatic.<BR>m. (कः)<BR>1 The headman of a village.<BR>2 A village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामिन्
ग्रामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Village, villager.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>The headman of a village.<BR>f. (-मिनी)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम a village, इनि and ङीष् affixes; also ग्रामीणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीण|ग्रामीणः
ग्रामीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 A villager, a rustic.<BR>2 Produced in or peculiar to a village.<BR>3 Vulgar, rude.<BR>4 Chromatic.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामीय|ग्रामीयः
ग्रामीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to a village, produced in or derived from it.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A villager.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and छ affix; also with कन् added ग्रामीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेय
ग्रामेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>A villager, rustic, village-born, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and ढक् affix; also with कन् added ग्रामेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेवास
ग्रामेवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A villager.<BR>2 A village abode.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रामे seventh case, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेवासिन्
ग्रामेवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रामे seventh case, वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेश|ग्रामेशः
ग्रामेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The headman of a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and ईश a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रामेश्वर|ग्रामेश्वरः
ग्रामेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The headman or ruler over a village.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and ईश्वर a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्य|ग्राम्यः
ग्राम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Village-born, produced in or relating to a village.<BR>2 Vulgar, rude, rustic.<BR>3 Relating to a musical scale.<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>A hog, a tame or a village hog.<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Rustic or homely speech.<BR>2 The Prākṛta and the other dialects of India, except the Sanscrit.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकर्क्कटी|ग्राम्यकर्कटी
ग्राम्यकर्क्कटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A pumpkin gourd.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य village, and कक्कट gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=305" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकन्द|ग्राम्यकन्दः
ग्राम्यकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A common species of Arum.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यकुङ्कुम|ग्राम्यकुंकुम|ग्राम्यकुङ्कुमं
ग्राम्यकुङ्कुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A yellow dye, safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and कुङ्कुम saffron, village saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यधर्म्म|ग्राम्यधर्म|ग्राम्यधर्मः|ग्राम्यधर्म्मः
ग्राम्यधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and धर्म्म virtue, village virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमद्गुरिका
ग्राम्यमद्गुरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of fish, (Silurus singio, HAM.) ग्राममद्गुरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमांस
ग्राम्यमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Meat of tame animals.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य rural, and मांस fresh^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यमृग|ग्राम्यमृगः
ग्राम्यमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and मृग a deer, the village deer; also ग्राममृग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यराशि|ग्राम्यराशिः
ग्राम्यराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>A name of several of the signs of the zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्यशूकर|ग्राम्यशूकरः
ग्राम्यशूकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A village hog, a tame hog, a pig.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and शूकर a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राम्याश्व|ग्राम्याश्वः
ग्राम्याश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राम्य, and अश्व a horse, the village horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रावन्
ग्रावन्<BR>mfn. (-वा-वा-व)<BR>Hard, solid.<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>1 A stone or rock.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to seize, वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रास|ग्रासः
ग्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A mouthful or a quantity equivalent to a mouthful, a lump of rice, &c. of the size of a peacock's egg.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to eat, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रासाच्छादन
ग्रासाच्छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bare subsistence, food and clothing.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रास, and आच्छादन covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह|ग्राहं|ग्राहः
ग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking, either by seizure or acceptance.<BR>2 A shark; according to some, the Gangetic alligator, (Lacerta Gangetica); according to others, the water elephant, (the hippopotamus?)<BR>3 Any large fish or marine animal.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, affix घञ् or ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहक|ग्राहकः
ग्राहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>One who takes or seizes, one who accepts or receives.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hawk, a falcon.<BR>2 A police officer, a constable, a bailiff.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहवत्|ग्राहवन्त्
ग्राहवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Containing or abounding with alligators.<BR>E.<BR>ग्राह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राहिन्
ग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>1 Taking, seizing, accepting, who or what takes.<BR>2 Astringent, binding, constipating.<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>1 A sedative, a narcotic.<BR>2 The elephant or wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small kind of Javāsa, perhaps a species of Hedysarum.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्राह्य|ग्राह्यः
ग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be seized, to be taken, to be accepted.<BR>2 To be accepted as a rule or law, to be acknowledged or assented to.<BR>3 To be attached to or obeyed.<BR>4 To be admitted in evidence, &c.<BR>5 To be apprehended or arrested.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीवा
ग्रीवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 The neck.<BR>2 The back part of the neck, the nape, the tendon of the Trapezium muscle.<BR>E.<BR>गॄ to swallow, वन् Uṇādi affix, ईट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीविन्
ग्रीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Long-necked, handsome-necked.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीवा a neck, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्म|ग्रीष्मः
ग्रीष्म<BR>mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मा-ष्मं)<BR>Hot, warm.<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 The hot season, comprehending two months, about June-July.<BR>2 Heat, warmth.<BR>f. (-ष्मी)<BR>Jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रस to take, &c. मक् Uṇādi affix, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मज
ग्रीष्मज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Produced by heat.<BR>2 Produced in the hot season.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A kind of fruit, (Annona reticulata.)<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म the hot season, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मभव
ग्रीष्मभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced by heat or in the hot season.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Double jasmin: see नवमल्ली.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म the hot season, and भव being, flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक|ग्रीष्मसुन्दरकः
ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Chironia centauroides; it is also applied to Pharnaceum mollugo.)<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म the hot season, and सुन्दर handsome, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्महास|ग्रीष्महासं
ग्रीष्महास<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The flocculent seeds, down, &c. blown about in the air.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म the hot season, and हास a smile, considered, from their white colour, as the smiles of the season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रीष्मोद्भव
ग्रीष्मोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced by heat or in the hot season.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Double jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म, and उद्भब produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रुच
ग्रुच<BR>(इर उ) इर ग्रुचु r. 1st cl. (ग्रोचति)<BR>To steal or rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैव|ग्रैवं
ग्रैव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Belonging to the neck, &c.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 A necklace, a close necklace or collar.<BR>2 A chain worn round the neck of an elephant, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीवा the necklace, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेय|ग्रैवेयं
ग्रैवेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Belonging to the neck.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A collar, a necklace.<BR>2 A chain on the neck of an elephant or horse.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीवा, and ढक् affix; also ग्रैवेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैवेयक|ग्रैवेयकं
ग्रैवेयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A collar, an ornament for the neck.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीवा, and ढकञ् affix: see ग्रै and ग्रैवेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्रैष्म
ग्रैष्म<BR>mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मी-ष्मं)<BR>Belonging or relating to, or produced by heat or the hot season.<BR>f. (-ष्मी)<BR>Double jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रीष्म the hot season, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लपित
ग्लपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Distressed, pained.<BR>2 Exhausted, overpowered.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लै to be weary, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस
ग्लस<BR>(उ) ग्लसु r. 1st cl. (ग्लसते)<BR>To eat: see ग्रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लस्त|ग्लस्तः
ग्लस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लस to eat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह|ग्लहः
ग्लह<BR>(उ) ग्लहु r. 1st and 10th cl. (ग्लहति-यति)<BR>To take, to receive or accept: see ग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लह|ग्लहः
ग्लह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Gaming, playing with dice.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लह to take, &c. affix अच्, or it is derived irregularly from ग्रह, with अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लान|ग्लानः
ग्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wearied, languid, feeble, exhausted by fatigue, disease, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लै to be feeble, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लानि|ग्लानिः
ग्लानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Langour, lassitude, fatigue of body or depression of mind.<BR>E.<BR>ग्ला or ग्लै to be weary, Uṇādi affix नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लायत्
ग्लायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Being exhausted, languid, faint, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लै to be weary, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लास्नु|ग्लास्नुः
ग्लास्नु<BR>mfn. (-स्नुः-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>Exhausted by disease or fatigue, wearied, languid.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लै to be weak, affix स्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुच
ग्लुच<BR>(इर उ) इर ग्लुचु r. 1st cl. (ग्लोचति)<BR>1 To steal, to rob.<BR>2 To go: see ग्रुच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लुञ्च
ग्लुञ्च<BR>(इर उ) इर ग्लुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (ग्लुञ्चति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेप
ग्लेप<BR>(ऋ) ग्लेपृ r. 1st cl. (ग्लेपते)<BR>1 To be poor or dependant.<BR>2 To shake, to tremble.<BR>3 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेय|ग्लेयः
ग्लेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be made weary or exhausted, exhaustible, fatigable^1.<BR>E.<BR>ग्ला or ग्लै to be weary, affix यत्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेव
ग्लेव<BR>(ऋ) ग्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (ग्लेवते)<BR>To serve, to worship, to gratify by service or devotedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लेष
ग्लेष<BR>(ऋ) ग्लेषृ r. 1st cl. (ग्लेषते)<BR>To inquire, to search, to investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लै
ग्लै<BR>r. 1st cl. (ग्लायति)<BR>1 To be languid or weary, to be exhausted, faded, &c.<BR>2 To yawn: this root is sometimes considered [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">Page307</a>] to be ग्ला, making ग्लायति as above, and in the causal form ग्लपयति or ग्लापयति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=306" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौतृ
ग्लौतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Wearied, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>ग्लै to be weary, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ग्लौ
ग्लौ<BR>m. (-ग्लौः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>ग्ला to be weary, Uṇādi affix डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ<BR>The fourth consonant of the Sanskrit alphabet, being the aspirate of the preceding letter, and corresponding to Gh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ|घः
घ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A bell.<BR>2 A rattling or gurgling sound.<BR>f. (घा)<BR>1 A tinkling ornament worn by women round the waist.<BR>2 Striking, killing.<BR>3 Wetting, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, affix ड, and घ substituted for the radical letter, or the same affix, with घृ to sprinkle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घग्घ
घग्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (घग्घति)<BR>To laugh, to laugh at or deride; also घघ and गग्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घघ
घघ<BR>r. 1st cl. (घघति)<BR>To laugh or to laugh at: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट|घटः
घट<BR>r. 1st cl. (घटते)<BR>To act, to strive or endeavour.<BR>r. 10th cl. (घाटयति)<BR>1 To unite or to put together.<BR>2 To injure or kill.<BR>3 To shine.<BR>(इ) घटि, r. 10th cl. (घण्टयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट|घटः
घट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A large earthen water jar.<BR>2 The sign Aquarius.<BR>3 A measure: see कुम्भ.<BR>4 An elephant's frontal sinus.<BR>5 Suspending the breath as a religious exercise.<BR>6 A man who makes effort or exertion.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>1 A troop of elephants assembled for martial purposes.<BR>2 Effort, endeavour.<BR>3 An assembly.<BR>4 A number, a collection, an assemblage.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 The Gharī or Indian clock, a plate of iron or mixed metal on which the hours are struck.<BR>2 A small water jar, a ewer.<BR>E.<BR>घट to endeavour, &c. affixes अच् or अङ्, and fem. affix टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटक|घटकः
घटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree that produces fruit without apparent flowers.<BR>2 A match-maker, an agent who ascertains or invents genealogies, and negociates matrimonial alliances.<BR>3 A genealogist.<BR>E.<BR>घट to endeavour, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटग्रह|घटग्रहः
घटग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Who or what takes a water pot.<BR>E.<BR>घट, and ग्रह to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटदासी
घटदासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A bawd or procuress.<BR>E.<BR>घट effort, and दासी a slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटन|घटनं
घटन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Effort, exertion.<BR>2 Assembling, bringing together.<BR>3 Joining, mixing.<BR>4 Occurring.<BR>E.<BR>घट to strive, &c. affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटयोनि|घटयोनिः
घटयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The saint AGASTYA. घट a water jar, and योनि place of birth; the saint being born from a water jar: see कुम्भसम्भव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटराज|घटराजः
घटराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A large water jar of baked clay.<BR>E.<BR>घट a jar, and राज king, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटस्थापन
घटस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Placing a water pot as a type of DURGĀ, an essential part of various Tāntrika ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>घट, and स्थापन placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटाटोप|घटाटोपः
घटाटोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A covering for a carriage or any article of furniture.<BR>E.<BR>घट, and आटोप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिक|घटिकं|घटिकः
घटिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The posteriors^1.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The ancle; also घुटिका^2.<BR>2 A Muhūrta or thirtieth part of a day and night.<BR>3 A Daṇḍa or period of twenty-four minutes.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A waterman.<BR>E.<BR>घटी a clock, &c. affixes कन् and टाप् for the feminine; otherwise घट a jar, and ठन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161211. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 307,308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटित
घटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Devised, attempted.<BR>2 Made of.<BR>3 In contact with, contiguous, joined.<BR>E.<BR>घट^1 to make effort, क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: Gawita is 'kta' of root Gawa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्धम|घटिंधम|घटिंधमः
घटिन्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Who blows or sounds in a jar.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A potter.<BR>E.<BR>घटी, and ध्मा to blow, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटिन्धय|घटिंधय
घटिन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who drinks a Ghaṭī, (in measure.)<BR>E.<BR>घटी, and धे to drink, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीकार|घटीकारः
घटीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A potter.<BR>E.<BR>घट, कार who makes, with च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीग्रह
घटीग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Who or what takes a small jar, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घटी, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटीयन्त्र|घटीयंत्र|घटीयन्त्रं
घटीयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>The rope and bucket of a well, or any machine for raising water.<BR>E.<BR>घट effort, and यन्त्र machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोत्कच|घटोत्कचः
घटोत्कच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The son of BHĪMA by the Rākṣasī, named HIḌIMBĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोत्कचान्तक|घटोत्कचान्तकः
घटोत्कचान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of KARṆA, natural brother to the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>घटोत्कच a proper name, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटोद्भव|घटोद्भवः
घटोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sage AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>घट a jar, and उद्भव born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट|घट्टः
घट्ट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (घट्टते घट्टयति)<BR>To move.<BR>With परि prefixed,<BR>To spread or diffuse.<BR>With वि,<BR>To rub gently, to scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्ट|घट्टः
घट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A Ghat, a quay or landing place, steps on the side of a river, &c. leading to the water's edge.<BR>f. (-ट्टी)<BR>A small or inferior landing place, private stairs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घट्ट to go, affix अच्, and with ङीष् affix, implying diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टना
घट्टना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 Practice, business, means of living.<BR>3 Rubbing or striking together.<BR>E.<BR>घट्ट to go, affix युच्, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घट्टजीविन्
घट्टजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>An attendant at a landing place, who takes care of the clothes of the bathers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घट्ट, and जीविन् who subsists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण
घण<BR>(उ,) घणु r. 8th cl. (घणुति or घणुते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ट|घंट|घण्टः
घण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A sort of sauce, vegetables made into a pulp with water, turmeric, mustard seeds and capsicums.<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>1 A bell; also a plate of iron or mixed metal struck as a bell.<BR>2 A plant: see घण्टापाटली.<BR>E.<BR>हन to strike, ट affix, fem. टाप्, and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाक|घण्टाकः
घण्टाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant: see घण्टापाटली.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; some copies read घण्टीक and घाण्टीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाकर्ण|घण्टाकर्णः|घण्टाकर्ण्ण
घण्टाकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>One of ŚIVA'S attendants, who is supposed to preside over cutaneous complaints, and is worshipped for exemption from them in the month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and कर्ण an ear; having ears as broad as a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाताड|घंटाताड|घण्टाताडः
घण्टाताड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A bellman, one who strikes a bell or Gharī.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and ताड who beats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाताडन
घण्टाताडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Striking a bell.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and ताडन beating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टानाद|घंटानाद|घण्टानादः
घण्टानाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sound of a bell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and माद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टापथ|घंटापथ|घण्टापथः
घण्टापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The chief road through a village, a highway.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा a bell, and पथि a road, affix अ; the bell-road, or that by which elephants, &c. decorated with tinkling ornaments^1, proceed.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=307" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टापाटली
घण्टापाटली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant commonly called by the similar name Ghaṇṭāpārali, a species of the trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा a bell, &c. and पाटली the trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टावाद्य
घण्टावाद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>The sound of a clock.<BR>E.<BR>घण्ठा, and वाद्य playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टावीज
घण्टावीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The croton nut.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टारवा
घण्टारवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Crotolaria of various species.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and रव sound; the seed rattling within the husk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टाशब्द|घंटाशब्द|घण्टाशब्दं|घण्टाशब्दः
घण्टाशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दं)<BR>1 Bellmetal.<BR>2 The sound of a bell.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टास्वन
घण्टास्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sound of a bell or clock.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टिका|घंटिका
घण्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The uvula or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>घण्ठा a bell, and कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टु|घंटुः|घण्टुः
घण्टु<BR>m. (-ण्टुः)<BR>1 A string of bells tied on an elephant's chest, &c. by way of ornament.<BR>2 Heat, light, &c. घण to shine, Uṇādi affix टु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्टेश्वर|घण्टेश्वरः
घण्टेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A minor deity, the son of MARS.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा, and ईश्रर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घण्ड|घंडः|घण्डः
घण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घन|घनं|घनः
घन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Material, solid.<BR>2 Coarse, gross.<BR>3 Compact.<BR>4 Hard, firm.<BR>5 Full, plump.<BR>6 Impenetrable.<BR>7 Viscid, thick, inspissated.<BR>8 Deep, (as sound.)<BR>9 Very, much.<BR>10 Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>11 A Permanent, eternal.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An iron club.<BR>3 The body.<BR>4 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>5 A number, an assemblage or quantity.<BR>6 Extension, diffusion.<BR>7 Hardness.<BR>8 Solidity, substance, matter.<BR>9 The cube of a number, (in arithmetic.)<BR>10 A solid, (in geometry.)<BR>11 Phlegm.<BR>12 Talc.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A cymbal, a bell, a Gong, &c. any brazen or composite metallic instrument, which is struck as a clock, &c.<BR>2 A mode of dancing, neither quick nor slow.<BR>3 Iron.<BR>4 Skin, rind, bark, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हन to strike or be struck, affix अप्, and ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनकफ|घनकफः
घनकफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनकाल|घनकालः
घनकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनगोलक|घनगोलकः
घनगोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An alloy of gold and silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनघनौघ
घनघनौघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A gathering of dark clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन thick, close, घनौघ cumulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनचय
घनचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A collection of clouds, cumulus.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and चय a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनजम्बाल|घनजंबाल|घनजम्बालः
घनजम्बाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A quantity of mire, a slough.<BR>E.<BR>घन much, a heap, and जम्बाल mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनजाल
घनजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A gathering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and जाल multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनज्वाला
घनज्वाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Lightning, a flash of lightning.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनताल|घनतालः
घनताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bird: see घनतोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनतिमिर
घनतिमिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The darkness of clouds.<BR>2 Great darkness.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and तिमिर dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनत्व
घनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Firmness, compactness.<BR>2 Thickness, coarseness, solidity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to घन; also with तल्, घनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनतोल|घनतोलः
घनतोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and तुल to be equal, affix घञ्; who soars to the clouds in the rainy season, which, according to the fable, is the only time when he gets water to drink; some books have घनताल from ताल tune, or sound; whose music is (from) the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनध्वनि|घनध्वनिः
घनध्वनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Roaring, who or what makes such a sound.<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A deep and loud tone, a roar.<BR>2 The muttering of thunder clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घननाभि|घननाभिः
घननाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and नाभि the navel or centre; smoke being supposed to be a principal ingredient in clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घननीहार|घननीहारः
घननीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Thick falling frost or snow.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and नीहार hoar frost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपदवी
घनपदवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The sky.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and पदवी station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपयोधर
घनपयोधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A firm breast.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and पयोधर the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपल्लव
घनपल्लव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga): see शोमाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>घन abundance, and पल्लव a shoot or sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनपाषण्ड|घनपाषंड|घनपाषण्डः
घनपाषण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and पाषण्ड a sectary; this bird is supposed to delight in cloudy and rainy weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनफल|घनफलः
घनफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The contents of a solid, (in Geometry.)<BR>E.<BR>घन, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनमूल|घनमूलं|घनमूलः
घनमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cube root, (in Arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>घन, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनरव|घनरवः
घनरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The roaring of clouds, thunder.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनरस|घनरसः
घनरस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>Water.<BR>m. (-स)<BR>1 Camphor.<BR>2 Extract, decoction, &c.<BR>3 A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>4 Thick or inspissated juice.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud or a heap, and रस juice, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवर्त्मन्
घनवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>The sky.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and वर्त्मन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवल्लिका
घनवल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and वल्लिका a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवल्ली
घनवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>चन, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवात|घनवातः
घनवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the regions of hell.<BR>E.<BR>घन much, and वात wind; the region of storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवास|घनवासः
घनवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd.<BR>E.<BR>घन a long time, and वास abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवाहन|घनवाहनः
घनवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and वाहन a vehicle; who rides in the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनवीथि|घनवीथिः
घनवीथि<BR>f. (-थिः)<BR>A line of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and वीथि a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनशब्द|घनशब्दः
घनशब्द<BR>m. (ब्दः)<BR>The noise of clouds, thunder.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनश्याम|घनश्यामः
घनश्याम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Black, deep black, as that of heavy clouds.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 RĀMA.<BR>2 KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and श्याम black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसंवृत्ति|घनसंवृत्तिः
घनसंवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Profound secrecy.<BR>E.<BR>घन impenetrable, संवृत्ति secret purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनस्वन|घनस्वनः
घनस्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Low thunder, the muttering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसमय|घनसमयः
घनसमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, समय time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनसार|घनसारः
घनसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Camphor.<BR>2 Mercury, or some peculiar form of it.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 A kind of tree.<BR>E.<BR>घन firm, &c. and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाकर|घनाकरः
घनाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and आकर a mine or place of producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाघन|घनाघनः
घनाघन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Mischievous, cruel.<BR>2 Even, uniform, without spaces or interstices.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">Page309</a>]<BR>2 A vicious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>3 A rainy cloud.<BR>4 Mutual collision.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A vegetable, (Solanum Indicum); also काकमाची.<BR>E.<BR>घन as above, reiterated and the final of the first made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=308" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनात्यय|घनात्ययः
घनात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The season succeeding the rains, autumn.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and अत्यय disappearance, departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनान्त|घनान्तः
घनान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Autumn, the end of the rains.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनामय|घनामयः
घनामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The date tree, (Elate sylvestris.)<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and आमय sickness, pining in the rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनामल|घनामलः
घनामल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Chenopodium album): see वास्तूक.<BR>E.<BR>घन much, and अमल clear, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाम्बु|घनांबु
घनाम्बु<BR>n. (-म्बु^1)<BR>Rain.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and अम्बु water.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनारुण
घनारुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Deep red.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and अरुण red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनारुद्ध
घनारुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Overcast, overspread with clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and आरुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनावरुद्ध
घनावरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Overcast, overspread with clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and अवरुद्ध impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनाश्रय|घनाश्रयः
घनाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Æther, the atmosphere or heaven.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनीकृत
घनीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hardened, compacted, made solid or firm.<BR>2 Congealed, thickened.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोदधि|घनोदधिः
घनोदधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A division of hell.<BR>E.<BR>घन viscid, and उदधि an ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोपल|घनोपलः
घनोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>घन a cloud, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनोपरुद्ध
घनोपरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Clouded, overcast.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and उपरुद्ध obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घनौघ|घनौघः
घनौघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A gathering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>घन, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घम्ब
घम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (घम्बयति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घट|घर्घटः
घर्घट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A kind of fish, (Pimelodus gagora or P. tengara, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>घर् an imitative sound, and घट to endeavour, affix अच्; who makes such a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घर|घर्घरः
घर्घर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>One of the tones or notes in music.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The pass of a mountain.<BR>2 A door, a gate.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 The name of a river, the Gogra or Ghogra.<BR>5 Sound.<BR>6 Laughter, mirth.<BR>7 A fire of straw or chaff.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>A girdle of small bells or tinkling ornaments worn by women.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A kind of lute.<BR>E.<BR>घर्घ here said to imply an inarticulate sound, gurgling, &c. and रा to give or take, affix डः also with कन् added घर्घरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरारव
घर्घरारव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A tinkling sound, the sound of small bells.<BR>E.<BR>घर्घरा, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घरिका
घर्घरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An ornament of small bells worn by women, horses, &c.<BR>2 The bow or stick of a viol, &c.<BR>3 A sort of musical instrument.<BR>4 Fried grain.<BR>5 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>घर्घरी as above, and कन् added fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्घूघा
घर्घूघा<BR>m. (-घा)<BR>1 A sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ब|घर्ब्ब
घर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (घर्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्म|घर्म|घर्मः|घर्म्मः
घर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Heat.<BR>2 The hot season.<BR>3 Sunshine.<BR>4 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>घृ to sprinkle, and मक् Uṇādi affix; what sprinkles the limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मचर्च्चिका|घर्मचर्चिका|घर्म्मचर्चिका
घर्म्मचर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Eruptions from suppressed perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>घम्म, and चर्च्चिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मद्युति|घर्मद्युति|घर्मद्युतिः
घर्म्मद्युति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and द्युति splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मपयस्|घर्मपयस्
घर्म्मपयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>2 Warm water.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and पयस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मरश्मि|घर्मरश्मि
घर्म्मरश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Heat, radiance.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मविचर्च्चिका|घर्मविचर्चिका
घर्म्मविचर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cutaneous eruptions or pimples from suppressed perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and विचर्च्चिका pustular eruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मान्त|घर्मान्त|घर्मांत|घर्मान्तः|घर्म्मान्तः
घर्म्मान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मान्तकामुकी|घर्मान्तकामुकी
घर्म्मान्तकामुकी<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A small white bird; a kind of crane.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्मान्त, and कामुकी who wishes for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मार्त्त|घर्मार्त
घर्म्मार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Suffering from heat.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and आर्त्त pained by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्माम्बु|घर्माम्बु|घर्मांबु
घर्म्माम्बु<BR>n. (-म्बु)<BR>1 Perspiration, sweat.<BR>2 Warm water.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and अम्वु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्म्मोदक|घर्मोदक
घर्म्मोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Perspiration.<BR>2 Warm water.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्ष|घर्षः
घर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Rubbing, friction.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to rub, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षण|घर्षणं
घर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Grinding, pounding.<BR>2 Rubbing, friction.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to grind, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षणाल|घर्षणालः
घर्षणाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wooden roller or pestle for grinding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घर्षण rubbing, and अल what is fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घर्षित
घर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed.<BR>2 Ground.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to rub, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घष
घष<BR>(इ) घषि r. 1st cl. (घंषते)<BR>To render handsome or brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस|घसः
घस<BR>(आ ऌ,) औघसॢ^1 r. 1st cl. (घसति)<BR>To eat: this root is in many tenses a substitute for अद, and is itself imperfect in others.<BR>(इ,) घसि r. 1st cl. (घंसते)<BR>To sprinkle or drop; this root is not generally admitted.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: root with anubandhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घसि|घसिः
घसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>घस to eat, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्मर|घस्मरः
घस्मर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Gluttonous, voracious.<BR>E.<BR>घस to eat, क्भरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घस्र|घस्रं|घस्रः
घस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>A day.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>घस to eat, and रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाट|घाटः
घाट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>The nape or back of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>घट to unite, affix अच्; the radical is of the 10th class of roots, whence the penultimate is long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाटिका
घाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The nape of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाण्टिक|घांटिक|घांटिकः|घाण्टिकः
घाण्टिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bard, who sings in chorus, but especially in honour of the gods, and rings a bell in presence of their images.<BR>2 Datura fastuosa.<BR>E.<BR>घण्टा a bell, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात|घातः
घात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Striking, wounding, killing.<BR>2 A bruise, a blow.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 Product (of a sum in multiplication.)<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, घञ् affix, and the radical letters changed respectively to घ and त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातक|घातकः
घातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A murderer, a maimer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हन as above, with ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातन|घातनं|घातनः
घातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A murderer, a killer.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Striking.<BR>3 Immolating victims.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, युन् affix, and घात substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातयत्
घातयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Striking, hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातव्य
घातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be killed, what may be or ought to be killed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, तव्य affix, and घा substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=309" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातस्थान
घातस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A slaughter house.<BR>2 A place of execution.<BR>E.<BR>घात, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घाति|घातिः
घाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Catching or killing birds, fowling.<BR>2 Killing in general.<BR>3 Striking.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill or hurt, affix इञ्, and the radical changed: see घात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातिन्
घातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Murderous, felonious, who or what strikes or kills.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातिपक्षिन्
घातिपक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A hawk or falcon.<BR>E.<BR>घाति fowling, and पक्षिन् a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घातुक|घातुकः
घातुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>2 Cruel, savage, violent, ferocious.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, changed to घत, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घात्य|घात्यं
घात्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Proper or fit to be killed.<BR>E.<BR>हन, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार|घारः
घार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>E.<BR>घृ to sprinkle, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घार्त्तिक|घार्तिक|घार्तिकः|घार्त्तिकः
घार्त्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Pulse ground and fried with clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घास|घासः
घास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Meadow or pasture grass.<BR>E.<BR>घस to eat, घञ् affix; what is eaten by animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घासि|घासिः
घासि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>घस to devour, and इन Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घिण
घिण<BR>r. 1st cl. (इ) घिणि (घिण्णते)<BR>To take, to seize or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
घु<BR>r. 1st cl. (घवते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घु|घुः
घु<BR>m. (-घुः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>घु to sound, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट|घुटः
घुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (घोटते)<BR>1 To come back, to return.<BR>2 To barter or exchange.<BR>r. 6th cl. (घुटति)<BR>1 To strike again or retaliate, to resist or oppose.<BR>2 To prevent.<BR>3 To protect or preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुट|घुटः
घुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The ancle.<BR>E.<BR>घुट to resist, and क affix; also घुटि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुटि|घुटिः
घुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>The ancle.<BR>E.<BR>घुट to resist, affix कि, and ङीप् may be added; also with कन् added घुटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुटिक|घुटिकः
घुटिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>The ancle, &c. see घुट and घुटि; also घुण्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण|घुणः
घुण<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (घोणति घुणति)<BR>To roll, to whirl, to turn round.<BR>(इ) घुणि r. 1st cl. (घुणते)<BR>To take or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण|घुणः
घुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An insect that is found in timber.<BR>2 The pangolin or armadillo.<BR>E.<BR>घुण to turn round, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ट|घुंट|घुंटः|घुण्टः
घुण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>The ancle.<BR>E.<BR>घुट to resist, affix क and नुम् inserted; also with कन् added घुण्टक, or without the augment घुट &c. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्टिक|घुंटिकं|घुण्टिकं
घुण्टिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Cowdung found in thickets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुण्ड|घुंड|घुंडः|घुण्डः
घुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>घुण to roll, Uṇādi affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर
घुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (घुरति)<BR>1 To be frightful or terrible.<BR>2 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर
घुर<BR>(ई) घुरी r. 4th cl. (घुर्य्यते)<BR>1 To be ignorant.<BR>2 To inquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुर्घुर|घुर्घुरः
घुर्घुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of worm burrowing in the skin, guinea worm, Dracunculus.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The mole cricket.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Growling, as of dog or cat.<BR>E.<BR>घुर् imitative sound, and घुर to sound, with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष
घुष<BR>(इ) घुषि r. 1st cl. (घुषते)<BR>To render beautiful or brilliant.<BR>(इर) घुषिर r. 1st cl. (घोषति)<BR>To do any act except manifest sentiment by sound.<BR>r. 10th cl. (घोषयति)<BR>1 To manifest sentiment or thought by sound, to speak, to affirm, to declare or proclaim.<BR>2 To make various sounds.<BR>3 To praise.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>To weep incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुषित|घुषितं
घुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Manifested by sound, proclaimed.<BR>E.<BR>घुष as above, affix क्त, इट् augment; also घुष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट|घुष्टं
घुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Sounded, proclaimed.<BR>E.<BR>घुष to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्टन्न
घुष्टन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Food given away by proclamation.<BR>E.<BR>घुष्ठ, and अङ्ग food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुष्ट्र|घुष्ट्रं
घुष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A car, a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घुसृण|घुसृणं
घुसृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>घुषि to beautify, ऋणच्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूक|घूकः
घूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>घू an imitative sound, and क who sounds, from कै with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूकारि|घूकारिः
घूकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>घूक an owl, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर
घूर<BR>(इ) घूरी r. 4th cl. (घूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR>2 To become old, to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण|घूर्णः|घूर्ण्ण
घूर्ण<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (घूर्णते, घूर्णति)<BR>To roll, to whirl, to turn round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण|घूर्णः|घूर्ण्ण
घूर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A kind of potherb, (Chironia centauroides): see ग्रीष्मसुन्दरक.<BR>2 Turning round, whirling, rolling, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण to roll, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णन|घूर्णनं|घूर्ण्णन
घूर्णन<BR>n. (-र्नं)<BR>Revolving, whirling, turning round.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण to whirl, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णायमान|घूर्णायमानः|घूर्ण्णायमान
घूर्णायमान<BR>m. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Whirling, revolving, rolling, tossing.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णि|घूर्णिः|घूर्ण्णि
घूर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>Rolling, revolving, going round or over.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण, and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्णित|घूर्णितः|घूर्ण्णित
घूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rolling, turning, tossing.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण to turn round, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घूर्ण्यमान|घूर्ण्यमानः
घूर्ण्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Agitated, set in motion, made to go round.<BR>E.<BR>घूर्ण to revolve, pass. voice, शानच् affix; also घूर्णमान middle voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृ
घृ<BR>r. 1st, 3d and 10th cls. (घरति जिघर्त्ति and घरयति)<BR>1 To sprinkle, to wet or moisten.<BR>2 To drop or distil.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृण|घृणः
घृण<BR>(उ,) घृणु 8th cl. (घर्णोति घणुते)<BR>To shine.<BR>(इ) घृणि r. 1st cl. (घृणते)<BR>To take or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणा
घृणा<BR>(-णा)<BR>1 Reproach, blame, censure, &c.<BR>2 Compassion, tenderness, pity.<BR>E.<BR>घृण to shine, अङ् and टाप् affixes, or घृ to sprinkle, with णक् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणावास|घृणावासः
घृणावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणि|घृणिः
घृणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A ray of the sun or moon.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>घृण to shine, affix इन्; or घृ to sprinkle, Uṇādi नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणित
घृणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abused, hated.<BR>2 Pitied.<BR>E.<BR>घृणा pity, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृणिन्
घृणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>1 Censorious, abusive.<BR>2 Compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>घृणा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृत|घृतः
घृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>2 Illumined.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Ghee, clarified butter, or butter which has been boiled gently, and allowed to cool: it is then used for culinary and religious purposes, and is highly esteemed by the Hindus.<BR>2 Water.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The name of a tree: see घृतमण्डा.<BR>E.<BR>घृ to sprinkle, Uṇādi affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतकुमारी
घृतकुमारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The aloe, (Aloes perfoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, to which the extract is compared, and कुमारी a virgin, which the plant is supposed to resemble in delicacy and elegance; also घृतकुमारिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतकुम्भ
घृतकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A jar of ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतदीधिति|घृतदीधितिः
घृतदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The deity of fire.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, and दीधिति light; offerings to fire, always comprehending clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपशु|घृतपशुः
घृतपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>Ghee made into or supposed to resemble an animal to be offered at a sacrifice or eaten at a meal, for which it is substituted.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=310" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपूर|घृतपूरः
घृतपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sweetmeat composed of flour, milk, cocoanut and ghee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, and पूर what is full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतपूर्णक|घृतपूर्णकः|घृतपूर्ण्णक
घृतपूर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Galedupa arborea, &c.): see करञ्ज.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, and पूर्ण full, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्राश|घृतप्राशः
घृतप्राश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Swallowing ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and प्राश eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्राशन
घृतप्राशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tasting or swallowing ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and प्राशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतप्लुत
घृतप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sprinkled or smeared with ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत and प्लुत bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतमण्डा
घृतमण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A tree; also वायसोली.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and मण्ड scum; the scum of its infusion resembling ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतलोलीकृत
घृतलोलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mixed with ghee, steeped in it or wet with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, लोल desirous, कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतवर|घृतवरः
घृतवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sweetmeat, or flour, &c. baked with ghee and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and वर what excels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतविक्रयिन्
घृतविक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A vender of ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, विक्रय to sell, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतस्पृश्
घृतस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Who or what touches ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, स्पृश to touch, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताक्त
घृताक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Smeared with ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and अक्त smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताची
घृताची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>One of the Apsaras or courtezans of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, अञ्च to worship, क्विप् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताचीगर्भ्भसम्भवा|घृताचीगर्भसम्भवा|घृताचीगर्भसंभवा
घृताचीगर्भ्भसम्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>घृताची, गर्म्भ the womb, and सम्भव born from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताभ्यक्त
घृताभ्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Smeared or anointed with ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and अभ्यक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृताह्व|घृताह्वः
घृताह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, and आहूआ an appellation, named from ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतेली
घृतेली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>घृत ghee, इर to go, घञ् affix, र changed to ल, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतोद|घृतोदः
घृतोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of ghee surrounding Kusa Dvīpa.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृतोदङ्क|घृतोदङ्कः
घृतोदङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A leather vessel holding ghee.<BR>E.<BR>घृत, उद up, अञ्च to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष
घृष<BR>(उ) घृषु r. 1st cl. (घर्षति)<BR>To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्ट|घृष्टः
घृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Ground, rubbed, pounded.<BR>2 Frayed, grazed, rubbed off.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्टि|घृष्टिः
घृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A hog; also गृष्टि.<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Varāhakrāntī, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR>2 Grinding, pounding.<BR>3 Emulation, contest.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to grind, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्टिला
घृष्टिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant: see पृश्निपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घृष्वि|घृष्विः
घृष्वि<BR>m. (-ष्विः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>घृष to rub, Uṇādi affix क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घेञ्चुलिका
घेञ्चुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum orinense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोङ्घ|घोंघः|घोङ्घः
घोङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>Intermediate space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोट|घोटः
घोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A horse: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोटक|घोटकः
घोटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse.<BR>f. (-टिका)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>घुट to strike again, (to spurn the ground,) अच् and कन् affixes, or without the latter affix घोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणा
घोणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The nose.<BR>2 The nose or nostrils of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>घुण to roll, to turn, and अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोणिन्
घोणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>घोणा nose or snout, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोण्टा|घोंटा
घोण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>1 The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>2 The betel-nut tree: see गुवाक.<BR>3 A timber tree, (Schrebera swietenioides^1.)<BR>E.<BR>घुट to resist, affix अच्, and नुम् inserted.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोनस|घोनसः
घोनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A large kind of snake.<BR>E.<BR>घा for गो a cow, and नस a nose, see गोनस; according to others the word is घोणस, from घुण to roll, and असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर<BR>r. 1st cl. (घोरति)<BR>To go as a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोर|घोरं|घोरः
घोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Frightful, horrible, terrific.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Night.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Horror, horribleness.<BR>2 Poison.<BR>E.<BR>घुर to be frightful, affix अच्; or घुर substituted for हन to injure or kill, and अच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरदर्शन|घोरदर्शनः
घोरदर्शन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Terrific, of horrid or frightful appearance.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>घोर as above, and दर्शन sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरपुष्प|घोरपुष्पं
घोरपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पः)<BR>Bellmetal.<BR>E.<BR>घोर, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासन|घोररासनः
घोररासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A jackall.<BR>E.<BR>घोर frightful, and रासन cry or sound, from रास to sound, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररासिन्
घोररासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A jackall.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररूप|घोररूपः
घोररूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Frightful, hideous.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A hideous appearance.<BR>E.<BR>घोर, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोररूपिन्
घोररूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>Frightful, horrible, hideous.<BR>E.<BR>घोररूप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोरसङ्काश|घोरसंकाश
घोरसङ्काश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Dreadful, horrible.<BR>E.<BR>घोर, and सङ्काश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोराकृति
घोराकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Frightful, hideous, of horrible aspect or form.<BR>E.<BR>घोर, and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोल|घोलं|घोलः
घोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>घुर substituted for हन to strike, (i. e. with the churn,) and अच् affix, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोष|घोषं|घोषः
घोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A station of herdsman.<BR>2 A herdsman.<BR>3 A creeping plant, commonly called by the same name Ghoṣa, and bearing white or yellow flowers, (Luffa pentandra and acutangula.)<BR>4 Bellmetal, tutenague, &c.<BR>5 Low thunder or the muttering of clouds.<BR>6 Sound.<BR>7 A proclamation.<BR>8 A gnat, a musquito.<BR>9 A term proper for the name of a Kāyastha.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa): see मघुरिका.<BR>E.<BR>घुसि to shine, to sound, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषक|घोषकः
घोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cryer, a proclaimer.<BR>2 Ghoṣa, described as a creeping plant, (Luffa pentangula, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषकाकृति|घोषकाकृतिः
घोषकाकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A plant commonly called Hātīghoṣa, and perhaps a species of the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>घोषक Ghoṣa, and आकृति shape, appearance, of similar appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषण|घोषणं
घोषण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Speaking loud, making a great noise.<BR>2 Crying, proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>घुष to sound, affixes युच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषयित्नु|घोषयित्नुः
घोषयित्नु<BR>m. (-त्नु)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A captive.<BR>4 A cryer, a herald.<BR>E.<BR>घोष sound, &c. इत्नुच् affix, and य inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घोषवती
घोषवती<BR>f. (-तीः)<BR>A lute, a Vīṇā.<BR>E.<BR>घोष sound, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घौर
घौर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Horror, horribleness.<BR>E.<BR>घोर, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्नत्|घ्नन्त्
घ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नन्ती-घ्नत्)<BR>Striking, beating, hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>हन to strike, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रति
घ्रति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रा
घ्रा<BR>r. 1st cl. (जिघ्रति)<BR>To smell, to receive smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राण|घ्राणं|घ्राणः
घ्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Smelled.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The nose.<BR>2 Smell, odour.<BR>3 Smelling.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणतर्पण|घ्राणतर्पणः
घ्राणतर्पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Fragrance, odour, a fragrance, a perfume.<BR>E.<BR>घ्राण the smell, and तर्पण what satisfies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=311" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राणदुःखदा
घ्राणदुःखदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Sneezing.<BR>E.<BR>घ्राण, and दुःखदा paining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात|घ्रातः
घ्रात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smelled.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्रात्वा
घ्रात्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having smelled.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घ्राति|घ्रातिः
घ्राति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 The nose.<BR>2 Smelling.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ<BR>The fifth consonant of the Sanskrit alphabet, and the nasal of the first class; the sound of this letter corresponds with that of the nasal N in Song, &c. or in the French word bon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङ|ङः
ङ<BR>m. (ङः)<BR>1 An object of sense.<BR>2 Desire, wish for any sensual object.<BR>E.<BR>ङु to sound, affix ङ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ङु
ङु<BR>(ङु) r. 1st cl. (ङवते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च<BR>The twentieth letter of the alphabet, and first of the second or palatial class of consonants, having the sound of Ch in church.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च|चः
च<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>1 Seedless.<BR>2 Vile, base.<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 A tortoise.<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and conjunction copulative or disjunctive, corresponding to<BR>1 And.<BR>2 Also.<BR>3 Moreover.<BR>4 Mutually.<BR>5 Equally.<BR>6 Otherwise.<BR>7 For, on account of.<BR>8 But, &c.<BR>9 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, or चि to collect, &c. ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक
चक<BR>r. 1st cl. (चकते)<BR>To repel, to resist.<BR>(चकति-ते)<BR>To be satiate or satisfied.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकास
चकास<BR>(ऋ) चकासृ r. 2nd cl. (चकास्ति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासयत्
चकासयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Beautifying, illuminating.<BR>E.<BR>चकास to shine, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकासित
चकासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Illuminated, shining, splendid, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>चकास, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकित|चकितं
चकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Timid, fearful.<BR>2 Frightened at, afraid of.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Timidity, groundless alarm.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of the Aṣṭi metre.<BR>E.<BR>चक to repel, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोर|चकोरः
चकोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The bartavelle or Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa or Tetrao rufus.)<BR>E.<BR>चक to be satisfied, ओरन् Uṇādi affix; also with कन् added चकोरक; what is satisfied with the moonbeams, upon which the bird is fabulously said to subsist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरक|चकोरकः
चकोरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Greek partridge: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चकोरदृश्
चकोरदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Fine-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>चकोर and दृश the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्क
चक्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (चक्कयति)<BR>To give or inflict pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्नस|चक्नसः
चक्नस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Crookedness.<BR>2 Dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>क्नस to be crooked, अप् affix, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्र|चक्रं|चक्रः
चक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>1 The ruddy or Brahmani goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 An army, a host.<BR>2 A realm, a region.<BR>3 A multitude, a heap.<BR>4 A wheel.<BR>5 A potter's wheel.<BR>6 An oil mill, &c.<BR>7 A discus or sharp circular missile weapon.<BR>8 A whirlpool.<BR>9 A province, a number of villages, a district.<BR>10 A form of military array, a circular position.<BR>11 A diagram of various sorts for calculating nativities or foretelling events.<BR>12 A ring, circle or depression of the body for mystical, astrological or cheiromantic purposes; six such are enumerated, or Mūlādhāra the parts about the pubis, above that is the Svādhiṣṭhānam or umbilical region, and above that the Maṇipūram or pit of the stomach or epigastrium, Anāhatam is the root of the nose, Viśuddham the hollow between the frontal sinuses, and the Ājñākhyam the fontenelle or union of the coronal and sagittal sutures; various faculties and divinities are supposed to be present in these hollows.<BR>13 A cycle, a cycle of years.<BR>14 (In Astronomy,) A sphere or circle, as राशिचक्रं the zodiac; प्राक् चक्रं an epicycle.<BR>15 The horizon.<BR>16 The spiral marks of the Śālagrāma or ammonite.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do or make, with the reduplicate initial letter, affix क, or चक to repel, &c. with रक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रक|चक्रकः
चक्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A logical form or proposition, arguing in a circle.<BR>E.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रकारक|चक्रकारकं
चक्रकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of perfume, apparently a dried shellfish: see नखी.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a heap, and कारक what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रकुल्या
चक्रकुल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A species of fern, commonly Cākuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रगण्डु|चक्रगंडु|चक्रगण्डुः
चक्रगण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A round pillow.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and गण्डु a pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रगुच्छ|चक्रगुच्छः
चक्रगुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and गुच्छ a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रजीवक|चक्रजीवकः
चक्रजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A potter.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and जीवक who lives by; also चक्रजीविन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रदंष्ट्र|चक्रदंष्ट्रः
चक्रदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and दंष्ट्र a tusk, having a curved tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रधर|चक्रधरः
चक्रधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having a wheel, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A village or common tumbler or juggler.<BR>2 One who holds a wheel, a discus, &c.<BR>3 The manager or owner of many villages.<BR>4 A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, who is represented as holding a discus in one hand.<BR>5 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, &c. and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रनामन्
चक्रनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A pyritic ore of iron: see माक्षिक.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, &c. and नामन् appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपद्माट|चक्रपद्माटः
चक्रपद्माट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Cassia tora: see चक्रमर्द्दक.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, पद्म a lotus, and अट what goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपर्णी|चक्रपर्ण्णी
चक्रपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant commonly Cākuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and पर्ण a leaf, the leaves being nearly round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाणि|चक्रपाणिः
चक्रपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and पाणि the hand, being always represented with a discus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाद|चक्रपादः
चक्रपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A carriage.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and पाद a foot; also चक्रपादक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रपाल|चक्रपालः
चक्रपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Superintendent of a province.<BR>2 One who carries a discus.<BR>3 A circle.<BR>4 The horizon.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and पाल who or what protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रफल|चक्रफलं
चक्रफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A missile weapon, a kind of discus.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and फल fruit, bearing a discus as it were for fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रबान्धव|चक्रबांधव|चक्रबान्धवः
चक्रबान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र the ruddy goose, and बान्धव a friend; these birds being supposed to couple only in the day time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभृत्
चक्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a discus, and भृत् who cherishes: see चक्रपाणि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रभेदिनी
चक्रभेदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र the ruddy goose, and भेदिनी what divides, (male and female); these birds being condemned, according to the Hindus, to be separated at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=312" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमण्डलिन्|चक्रमंडलिन्
चक्रमण्डलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and मण्डल a circumference, implying either that the body of the snake, or the spots on the body may be compared to a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्द|चक्रमर्द|चक्रमर्द्दः
चक्रमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>Cassia tora.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, here meaning figuratively a large leprous spot, and मर्द्दं what cleanses or removes, from मृद with अच् added; or with वुन् affix चक्रमर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमर्द्दक|चक्रमर्दक|चक्रमर्द्दकः
चक्रमर्द्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रमुख|चक्रमुखः
चक्रमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a discus, and मुख face; cutting the ground as it were with a sharp weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रयान|चक्रयानं
चक्रयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any wheel carriage.<BR>E.<BR>क्षक्र a wheel, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ररद|चक्ररदः
चक्ररद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A hog, a boar.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and रद a tooth or tusk: see चक्रमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रलक्षणा
चक्रलक्षणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडूची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रला
चक्रला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Kyllinga monocephala.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and ल what gets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Circular, being in a ring or circle.<BR>2 Armed with a discus.<BR>3 Wheeled, &c.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 The proprietor of an oil mill, or any one in which seeds are bruised.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 An emperor.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवत्|चक्रवन्त्
चक्रवत्<BR>ind.<BR>In rotation, going round or revolving like a wheel.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिन्|चक्रवर्तिन्
चक्रवर्त्तिन्<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>An emperor, a sovereign of the world, the ruler of a Cakra or country described as extending from sea to sea; twelve princes beginning with Bharata are especially considered as Cakravartīs.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a reign, and वृत to abide, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवर्त्तिनी|चक्रवर्तिनी
चक्रवर्त्तिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A fragrant plant, commonly Cakāvat.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a heap, and वर्त्तिन् what abides or grows, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाक|चक्रवाकः
चक्रवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The ruddy goose, commonly called in India, the Brahmany duck or goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र an imitative sound, and वाक speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाट|चक्रवाटः
चक्रवाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Limit, boundary.<BR>2 A lamp stand.<BR>3 Engaging in any action.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and वट to surround, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाड|चक्रवाडं
चक्रवाड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>See चक्रवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवात|चक्रवातः
चक्रवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a circle, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवाल|चक्रवालं|चक्रवालः
चक्रवाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A range of mountains supposed to encircle the earth, and to be the limit of light and darkness.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The sensible horizon.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a region, वल to encompass, and अण् affix; girding the world; or वाड to emerge, &c. affix अच्, what emerges (from darkness), in the shape of a wheel; ड changed to ल; also चक्रवाड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रव्यूह|चक्रव्यूहः
चक्रव्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The circular array of troops.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र and व्यूह array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रवृद्धि|चक्रवृद्धिः
चक्रवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Compound interest.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रश्रेणी
चक्रश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant bearing a crooked fruit: see अजशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and श्रेणी a line or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसंज्ञ
चक्रसंज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and सज्ञा a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रसम्बर
चक्रसम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a Bauddha deity; also हेरम्ब.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a discus, and सम्बर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रहस्त|चक्रहस्तः
चक्रहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र, and हस्त hand: holding a discus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्की|चक्रांकी
चक्राङ्की<BR>f. (-ङ्की)<BR>A wild goose.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a number, and अकि to go, affixes अच् and ङीप्, flying in large flocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राङ्ग|चक्रांग|चक्राङ्गः
चक्राङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A gander.<BR>2 A carriage.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A goose.<BR>2 A drug: see कटुकि.<BR>3 A potherb, (Hilancha repens): see हिलमोचिका.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, &c. and अङ्ग a limb or the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राट|चक्राटः
चक्राट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A juggler, a snake-catcher, one who exhibits snakes and pretends to cure their bites.<BR>2 A knave, a cheat, a rogue.<BR>3 A gold coin or certain weight of gold, a Dīnāra.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a number of villages, and अट who goes, i. e. a vagabond, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राण|चक्राणः
चक्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Doing.<BR>2 Done.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, कानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्राधिवासिन्
चक्राधिवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>The orange tree.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a heap, and अधिवस to abide, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रावर्त्त|चक्रावर्त|चक्रावर्तः|चक्रावर्त्तः
चक्रावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Turning round, whirling or rotatory motion.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रि|चक्रिः
चक्रि<BR>m. (-क्रिः)<BR>An agent, a maker, a doer.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, कि affix, the root reduplicate and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिका
चक्रिका<BR>f. (का)<BR>The knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रिन्
चक्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्री-क्रिणी-क्रि)<BR>1 Having or holding a discus, &c.<BR>2 Wheeled, having a wheel.<BR>3 Circular.<BR>m. (-क्री)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A potter.<BR>3 The ruddy goose.<BR>4 A snake.<BR>5 An informer.<BR>6 A tumbler, one who exhibits tricks with a discus or a wheel.<BR>7 An oil grinder.<BR>8 An emperor, a Cakravartī: see चक्रवर्त्तिन्.<BR>9 One who rides in a carriage.<BR>10 A crow.<BR>11 An ass.<BR>12 Cassia, (the tree.)<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, &c. and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रीवत्|चक्रीवन्त्
चक्रीवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 An ass.<BR>2 The name of a king.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a wheel, वतु affix, and deriv. irr. rolling over like a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रु|चक्रुः
चक्रु<BR>m. (-क्रुः)<BR>An agent, a maker, a doer.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to make or do, with the reduplicate initial, and कु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्रेश्वरी
चक्रेश्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female deity peculiar to the Jainas, one of their Vidyā Devis or goddesses of wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र the universe, and ईश्वरी mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्ष
चक्ष<BR>(इङ्) चक्षिङ् r. 2nd cl. (चष्टे)<BR>1 To speak, to tell.<BR>2 To see; (in this sense आङ् is usually prefixed)<BR>3 To eat. ख्या or क्श are substituted for the radical letters in several tenses of this verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षण|चक्षणं
चक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Eating a relish to promote drinking.<BR>2 Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>चक्ष to speak, to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षस्
चक्षस्<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>1 A name of VṚHASPATI the preceptor of the gods.<BR>2 A spiritual teacher, an instructor in sacred science.<BR>E.<BR>चक्ष to speak, affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुःश्रवस्
चक्षुःश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस् an eye, and श्रवस् an ear; whose eyes are ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुर्दान
चक्षुर्दान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The ceremony of anointing the eyes of the image at the time of consecration.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस्, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुर्विषय|चक्षुर्विषयः
चक्षुर्विषय<BR>m. (-यः-यं)<BR>1 Presence, sight.<BR>2 An object of sight, any visible object.<BR>3 Visibility.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस्, and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष्मान्
चक्षुष्मान्<BR>mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्)<BR>1 Having eyes, seeing.<BR>2 Having fine eyes.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुष्य|चक्षुष्यं|चक्षुष्यः
चक्षुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>1 Beautiful, pleasing or well looking.<BR>2 Fit or agreeable for the eyes.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>1 A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>2 A plant: see पुण्डराक.<BR>3 A collyrium or application to the eyes, extracted from the Amomum anthorhiza. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">Page314</a>]<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>1 A blue stone, or according to some, the calx of brass used as collyrium.<BR>2 A pleasing or interesting woman.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस् the eye, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=313" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षुस्
चक्षुस्<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>The eye.<BR>E.<BR>चक्ष to speak, and उसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चक्षूरोग|चक्षूरोगः
चक्षूरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Ophthalmia.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुस्, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चघ
चघ<BR>r. 5th cl. (चघ्नोति)<BR>To smite or slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्कुर|चंकुर|चङ्कुरं|चंकुरः|चङ्कुरः
चङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A car, a carriage.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Any vehicle.<BR>E.<BR>चकि a sautra root, to wonder, and उरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमण|चंक्रमण|चंक्रमणं|चङ्क्रमणं
चङ्क्रमण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Who or what goes slowly or crookedly.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going, proceeding, going tortuously or slowly.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, युच् affix, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमा|चंक्रमा
चङ्क्रमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Going tortuously or slowly.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, root repeated, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्क्रमावत्
चङ्क्रमावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Who or what moves slowly or crookedly.<BR>E.<BR>चङ्क्रमा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चङ्ग|चंग|चङ्गः
चङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>2 Dexterous, clever.<BR>3 Sound, healthy.<BR>E.<BR>चं the moon, and ग what goes; what resembles the moon in beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चचेण्डा
चचेण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A creeper, commonly Cicirā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्च|चंच|चंचः|चञ्चः
चञ्च<BR>(उ) चञ्चु r. 1st cl. (चञ्चति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्
चञ्चत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 Unsteady, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्च to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चत्क|चंचत्क
चञ्चत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Trembling, moving.<BR>E.<BR>क्षञ्चत् the present participle of चञ्च as above, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चरी|चंचरी
चञ्चरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चरीक|चंचरीक|चंचरीकः|चञ्चरीकः
चञ्चरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, reduplicated, नुम् inserted, ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चल|चंचल|चञ्चलं|चञ्चलः
चञ्चल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Trembling, shaking, moving, unsteady.<BR>2 Fickle, inconsiderate, inconstant, (unsteady, metaphorically.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The wind.<BR>2 A lecher, a libertine, a lover.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 LAKṢMĪ or the goddess of fortune.<BR>3 Longpepper.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, in the reiterative form, नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चलत्व
चञ्चलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Fickleness, inconstancy, unsteadiness.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चल, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix चञ्चलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चलहृदय
चञ्चलहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Capricious, fickle, false hearted.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चल, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चा|चंचा
चञ्चा<BR>f. (-च्चा)<BR>1 A mat, a stool, &c. made of reeds or basket work.<BR>2 A puppet of grass or reeds, a man of straw.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्च to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चु|चंचु|चञ्चुः
चञ्चु<BR>f. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>A beak; also चञ्च.<BR>m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>1 The castor oil plant.<BR>2 A kind of potherb.<BR>3 A deer.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चु to go, to eat, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुका|चंचुका
चञ्चुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A beak.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुभृत्|चंचुभृत्
चञ्चुभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चु a beak, and भृत् who possesses; also other similar compounds as चञ्चुमत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुमत्|चंचुमत्|चञ्चुमन्त्
चञ्चुमत्<BR>mf. (-मान्-मती)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चु a beak, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुर|चंचुर|चञ्चुरः
चञ्चुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Expert in, conversant with.<BR>2 Going to repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, intensitive form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चुसूचि|चंचुसूचि|चञ्चुसूचिः
चञ्चुसूचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>The tailor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.)<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चु a beak, and सूचि a needle; having a sharp-pointed beak; also with कन् added, चञ्चुसूचिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चू|चंचू
चञ्चू<BR>f. (-ञ्चूः)<BR>A beak: see चञ्चु, the affix being ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चञ्चूर्य्यमाण|चञ्चूर्यमाण
चञ्चूर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Following evil practices, behaving ill, addicted to wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, intensitive form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चट
चट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cl. (चटति चाटषति)<BR>1 To break, to pierce<BR>2 To kill, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटक|चटकः
चटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A hen-sparrow.<BR>2 A young hen-sparrow.<BR>3 The root of long pepper: see चटकाशिरस and चटिका.<BR>E.<BR>चट to break, वुन् affix; breaking corn, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटकाशिरस्
चटकाशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The root of long pepper: see चटिकाशिरस्; also mas. चटकाशिर (-राः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटिका
चटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The root of long pepper.<BR>2 A sparrow: see चटका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटिकाशिरस्
चटिकाशिरस्<BR>mn. (-राः-रः)<BR>The root of long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>चटका a sparrow, and शिरस् a head; resembling in colour the head of a sparrow; in other forms चटका, चटिका, शिरस् and चटकाशिरस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटु|चटुः
चटु<BR>mn. (-टुः-टु)<BR>1 Scream, screech.<BR>2 Kind or agreeable discourse.<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 The belly.<BR>2 A posture of devotion amongst ascetics.<BR>E.<BR>चट to break, &c. Uṇādi affix उ; also चाटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुल|चटुलः
चटुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Tremulous, trembling.<BR>2 Shaking, moving.<BR>3 Beautiful.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>चट to hurt, to break, and उलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुलालस
चटुलालस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Pleased with or desirous of flattery.<BR>E.<BR>चटु, and लालस desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चटुलोल
चटुलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Tremulous and beautiful, beautiful as a soft swimming eye, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चटु beautiful, and लोल shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चड
चड<BR>(इ,) चडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (चण्डते and चण्डति, चण्डयति)<BR>To be angry, to be wrathful or passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण|चणः
चण<BR>r. 1st cl. (चणति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To sound.<BR>3 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणक|चणकः
चणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Chick-pea, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>2 The name of a sage.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Linseed.<BR>E.<BR>चण to be given, affix अच् and कन् added; what is given to horses, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकात्मज|चणकात्मजः
चणकात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The name of a sage; also called VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>E.<BR>चणक, and आत्मज born; the son of CAṆAKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकाम्लक|चणकाम्लकं
चणकाम्लक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Pease with salt.<BR>E.<BR>चणक, and अम्ल acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चणकाम्लवार्
चणकाम्लवार्<BR>n. (-र्)<BR>Water drops on the leaves of the Cicer.<BR>E.<BR>चणकाम्ल, and बार् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्ड|चंड|चण्डं|चण्डः
चण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Fierce, violent, passionate.<BR>2 Hot, warm.<BR>2 Pungent, acrid.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The tamarind tree.<BR>2 A messenger of YAMA.<BR>3 A Daitya, a demon.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 A perfume, commonly Cor.<BR>2 A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>3 The name of a river in the east of Bengal.<BR>4 A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>f. (-ण्डा-ण्डी)<BR>A name of the goddess DURGĀ, applied especially to her incarnation for the purpose of destroying Mahiṣāsura; this exploit forms the subject of a section of the Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa, and is particularly celebrated in Bengal at the Durgā Pūja, or festival held in honour of the goddess, towards the close of the year, (Oct.-Nov.)<BR>(-ण्डी)<BR>1 A passionate woman.<BR>2 A mischievous or furious woman.<BR>3 A species of the Atijagatī verse.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 Heat, warmth.<BR>2 Passion, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>चडि to be wrathful, ड Uṇādi affix, and टा or ङीप् affixes of the feminine gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डता
चण्डता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Warmth, pungency.<BR>2 Warmth of temper, passionateness.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड angry, and तल् abstract affix; also with त्व, चण्डत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=314" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डनायिका
चण्डनायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>2 One of the eight Nāyikās.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड a demon, and नायिका mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डरुद्रिका
चण्डरुद्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Knowledge of mystical nature, acquired by worship of the Nāyikās.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड, and रुद्र ŚIVA, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डवत्|चंडवत्
चण्डवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Passionate, violent, warm.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A name or form of DURGĀ.<BR>2 One of her attendants.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड anger, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डात|चंडात|चंडातः|चण्डातः
चण्डात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A fragrant plant, (Nerium odorum); also प्रतीहास.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड heat, and अत to go or be, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डातक|चंडातक|चंडातकं|चण्डातकं|चंडातकः|चण्डातकः
चण्डातक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A short petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>चण्डा an angry woman, अत to go, and वुन् affix; it being described as the garb of women of some consequence, and therefore privileged to give themselves airs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डाल|चंडाल|चण्डालः
चण्डाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An outcaste, a Cāṇḍāla, the generic name for a man of the lowest of the mixed tribes, born from a Śūdra father and Brahman mother.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड angry, and अल able, or चण्ड to be angry, and आलञ् Uṇādi affix; proper to execute all vile or barbarous acts; also चाण्डाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डालवल्लकी|चंडालवल्लकी
चण्डालवल्लकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A common or vulgar lute.<BR>E.<BR>चण्डाल an outcaste, and वल्लकी a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डालिका|चंडालिका
चण्डालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A common lute.<BR>2 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3 A plant.<BR>E.<BR>चण्डाल, and इकन् affix; or चण्ड a demon, &c. आली a line or troop, and कन् affix; hence also चण्डालीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डांशु|चंडांशु|चण्डांशुः
चण्डांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>चण्ड hot, अंशु ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिका|चंडिका
चण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>कण् added to चण्डी q. v. also चण्डा and चण्डी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डिल|चंडिल|चंडिलः|चण्डिलः
चण्डिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A barber.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 A kind of potherb: see बास्तूक.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>चडि to be wrathful, or to cause wrath, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डी|चंडी
चण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>DURGĀ. see चण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डीकुसुम|चण्डीकुसुमः
चण्डीकुसुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Red oleander.<BR>E.<BR>चण्डी, and कुसुम a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चण्डु|चंडुः|चण्डुः
चण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>1 A rat.<BR>2 A small monkey, (Simia erythroea.)<BR>E.<BR>चडि to be passionate, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत
चत<BR>(ए) चते r. 1st cl. (चतति-ते)<BR>To ask, to beg, to solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुः|चतु
चतुः<BR>ind.<BR>Four times: see चतुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःशाल|चतुःशालं
चतुःशाल<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A square formed by four houses.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, शाला a hall or house: the compound takes the neuter gender or the feminine, with टाप् affix; also with कन् added चतुःशालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुःषष्टि|चतुःषष्टिः
चतुःषष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 The number sixty-four.<BR>2 The Rig Veda.<BR>3 Art or science collectively, supposed to comprise sixty-four branches.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and षष्टि sixty; before ष, र becomes Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्
चतुर्<BR>mfn. plu. only, (चत्वारः चतस्र चत्वारि)<BR>Four:<BR>in composition, and the last member of a compound, the numeral is inflected in all the numbers; thus प्रियचतुर् Who has four favorites, makes masc. and fem. (sing.) प्रियचत्वा (du.) त्वारौ (plu.) त्वारः and n. (sing.) प्रियचतुः (du.) चत्वारी (plu.) चत्वारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर|चतुरः
चतुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Dexterous, ingenious, clever.<BR>2 Visible, perceptible.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A round pillow, one for the cheek.<BR>3 An elephant stable.<BR>E.<BR>चत to ask, Uṇādi affix उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्ग|चतुरंग|चतुरङ्गं
चतुरङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 An entire army, comprising elephants, cars, horse and foot.<BR>2 A sort of chess.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गवल
चतुरङ्गवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An entire army: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>चतुरङ्ग, and बल an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गसैन्य
चतुरङ्गसैन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>An entire army: see चतुरङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>चतुरङ्ग, and सैन्य an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गिन्
चतुरङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>Having four parts or members.<BR>f. (-ङ्गिनी)<BR>An army.<BR>E.<BR>चतुरङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरङ्गुल|चतुरङ्गुलः
चतुरङ्गुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Four fingers, (long, &c.)<BR>m. (लः)<BR>A kind of Cassia, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and अङ्गुली a finger; the leaves being four fingers in length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरस्र|चतुरस्रः
चतुरस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>Four cornered, quadrangular.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A square.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and अस्र a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुरानन|चतुराननः
चतुरानन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and आनन face; fourfaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्गति|चतुर्गतिः
चतुर्गति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four (feet), and गति motion; a quadruped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्गुण
चतुर्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Four times, four-fold.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and गुण multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थ|चतुर्थः
चतुर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था or -र्थी-र्थं)<BR>Fourth.<BR>f. (-र्थी)<BR>The fourth lunation.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, थुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थकाल
चतुर्थकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fourth season, implying especially the evening of every second day of a person's fasting.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्थ, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थफल
चतुर्थफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>(In Astronomy,) The second inequality or equation of a planet.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्थ, and फल quotient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थांश|चतुर्थांशः
चतुर्थांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A quarter, a fourth part.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्थ, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्थिका
चतुर्थिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A Pala.<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form added to चतुर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दत्|चतुर्दन्त्
चतुर्दत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Four toothed.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, दतृ substituted for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दन्त|चतुर्दंत|चतुर्दन्तः|चतुर्द्दन्त|चतुर्द्दन्तः
चतुर्दन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्दश|चतुर्द्दश
चतुर्दश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Fourteen.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The fourteenth lunation.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्दश, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्द्दशन्|चतुर्दशन्
चतुर्द्दशन्<BR>mfn. plur. (-दश)<BR>Fourteen.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्द्दोल|चतुर्दोल|चतुर्दोलः|चतुर्द्दोलं
चतुर्द्दोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A royal litter.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, (supporters,) दोल a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्द्धा
चतुर्द्धा<BR>ind.<BR>Four times, four-fold.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भद्र|चतुर्भद्रं
चतुर्भद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>The aggregate of four objects of human wishes, viz. virtue, love, wealth, and final beatitude.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, and भद्र fortunate, auspicious: see चतुर्व्वर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भाग|चतुर्भागः
चतुर्भाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Fourth part.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and भाग a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्भुज|चतुर्भुजः
चतुर्भुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 An equilateral tetragon.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्म्मुख|चतुर्मुख|चतुर्मुखः|चतुर्म्मुखः
चतुर्म्मुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 The deity BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A preparation of mercury.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and मुख a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्युग|चतुर्युगं
चतुर्युग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The aggregate of the four Yugas or ages of the Hindus, a Mahāyuga or 4,320,000 years.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वक्त्र|चतुर्वक्त्रः|चतुर्व्वक्त्रः
चतुर्वक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and वक्त्र a face: see चतुर्मुख and other synonymous compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वर्ग|चतुर्वर्गः|चतुर्व्वर्गः
चतुर्वर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 The four objects of human pursuit collectively: see चतुर्भद्र.<BR>2 Any assemblage of four things.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and वर्ग class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्वर्ण|चतुर्वर्णः
चतुर्वर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The four classes of Hindus.<BR>2 Four principal colours.<BR>3 Four letters.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=315" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्विद्य|चतुर्व्विद्यः
चतुर्विद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A priest who has studied the four Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, विद्या knowledge; also चतुर्वेद, and with अण् added चातुर्वेद्य and चातुर्वैद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुर्विध
चतुर्विध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of four sorts or kinds, in four ways.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुल|चतुलः
चतुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Depositing, placing, fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुश्शाला
चतुश्शाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A square of four houses, or a court inclosed by four buildings.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्क|चतुष्कं
चतुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Four.<BR>f. (-ष्की)<BR>1 A large four-sided pond or tank.<BR>2 A bed or musquito curtain.<BR>3 A necklace of four strings.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, कन् affix, and र is changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्कोण|चतुष्कोणः
चतुष्कोण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Square, quadrangular.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A square, a tetragon.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्टय|चतुष्टयं
चतुष्टय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Four.<BR>2 Four-fold.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A square.<BR>2 The centre of a circle.<BR>3 The aggregate of four.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, and तयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पथ|चतुष्पथं|चतुष्पथः
चतुष्पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>A place where four roads meet.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and पथि a road, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पद|चतुष्पदः
चतुष्पद<BR>nf. (-दं-दी)<BR>Verse, a metre of stanzas especially consisting of four Padas or lines.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An animal with four legs, a quadruped.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and पद for पाद a foot; also read चतुष्पाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाटी
चतुष्पाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four (the four quarters), and पाटी what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाठी
चतुष्पाठी<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>A school for Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, (the Vedas,) पाठ perusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाणि|चतुष्पाणिः
चतुष्पाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and पाणि a hand; the four-handed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुष्पाद्
चतुष्पाद्<BR>mfn. (-पात्)<BR>1 A quadruped.<BR>2 A whole of four parts or quarters.<BR>2 A judicial procedure, consisting of four processes, plea, defence, rejoinder, and sentence.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्, and पाद् a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुस्सम|चतुस्समं
चतुस्सम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>An unguent of four ingredients, Sandal, agallochum, saffron, and musk.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर् four, and सम equal, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चतुस्रिंशज्जातकज्ञ
चतुस्रिंशज्जातकज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A Buddha, a Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>चतुस्रिंशत् thirty-four, जातक species, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वर|चत्वरं
चत्वर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A levelled spot of ground prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>2 A court yard.<BR>E.<BR>चत to ask, Uṇādi affix वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चत्वाल|चत्वालः
चत्वाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A hole in the ground, &c. prepared for oblation with fire.<BR>2 The womb.<BR>3 Kusa grass.<BR>E.<BR>चत to ask, वालच् affix, or with वालञ् affix, चात्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चद
चद<BR>r. 1st cl. (ए) चदे (चदति-ते)<BR>To ask or beg, to solicit.<BR>(इ) चदि (चंदति)<BR>1 To gladden.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चदिर|चदिरः
चदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>चद to shine, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन
चन<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चनति चानयति)<BR>To hurt, to injure in any manner, to wound or kill, &c.<BR>2 To believe, to confide.<BR>3 To make a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन
चन<BR>ind.<BR>A particle affixed to certain words, giving them an indefinite signification, as कदा when, कदाचन some when, at sometime, कः who कञ्चन some one: see चित्.<BR>E.<BR>चन to sound, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चनस्
चनस्<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>Food.<BR>E.<BR>च, असुन् Uṇādi affix, and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द|चंद|चंदः|चन्दः
चन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>चदि to shine, affix अच्: see चन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दक|चंदकः|चन्दकः
चन्दक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Pleasing, joy-inspiring.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Moonlight.<BR>3 A small silvery fish, of a genus allied to the Zeus, (Canda, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>चदि to shine, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दकपुष्प
चन्दकपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रक, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दन|चंदन|चंदनं|चन्दनं|चंदनः|चन्दनः
चन्दन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>Sandal, (Sirium myrtifolium); it implies either the tree, the wood, or the unctuous preparations of the wood, held in high estimation as perfumes.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Red Sandal wood: see रक्रचन्दन.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A kind of ape.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>चदि to gladden, to delight, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दनाचल|चंदनाचल|चन्दनाचलः
चन्दनाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Malaya mountain, part of the southern range of the Ghāts, where Sandal wood is procured.<BR>E.<BR>चन्दन and अचल a hill, the Sandal hill; also similar names, as चन्दनाद्रि, चन्दनपर्वत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्दिर|चंदिर|चंदिरः|चन्दिरः
चन्दिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>चदि to shine, &c. Uṇādi affix किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्र|चंद्र|चन्द्रं|चन्द्रः
चन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 The moon considered as a planet or a deity.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 Gold.<BR>5 A plant, (Crinum): see रोचनी.<BR>6 (In composition) Pre-eminent, (as पुरुषचन्द्र an eminent man, a chief, a moon of men.)<BR>7 The eye in the peacock's tail.<BR>8 One of the eighteen minor Dvīpas or divisions of the known continent.<BR>9 The mark of the soft aspirate.<BR>10 A pearl with a red tinge.<BR>11 Any thing giving pleasure.<BR>f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>1 An awning, a canopy.<BR>2 Small cardamoms: see एला.<BR>E.<BR>चदि to shine, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रक|चंद्रक|चन्द्रकं|चंद्रकः|चन्द्रकः
चन्द्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A ring, a circle, (like the moon.)<BR>3 The eye in a peacock's tail.<BR>4 A finger nail.<BR>5 A fish, (Canda, HAM.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकवत्|चंद्रकवत्|चन्द्रकवन्त्
चन्द्रकवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रक the mark in his tail, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकला|चंद्रकला
चन्द्रकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A digit, or one-sixteenth of the moon's orb; each is personified as a female divinity, and worshipped in some Tāntrika ceremonies.<BR>2 A small drum.<BR>3 A fish commonly called Vacā or Bacā, (Pimelodus vacha, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and कला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकान्त|चंद्रकांत|चन्द्रकान्तं|चन्द्रकान्तः
चन्द्रकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A fabulous gem, the moon-stone, supposed to be formed of the congelation of the rays of the moon; a kind of crystal may perhaps be meant.<BR>mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 The white water lily.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The wife of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and कान्त splendid or beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रकिन्|चंद्रकिन्
चन्द्रकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रक the eye of the peacock's tail, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगुप्त|चन्द्रगुप्तः
चन्द्रगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>1 The registrar of YAMA'S court.<BR>2 SANDROKOPTUS king of Pāṭaliputra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोल|चंद्रगोल|चन्द्रगोलः
चन्द्रगोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The orb or sphere of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and गोल a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोलस्थ
चन्द्रगोलस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A deceased and deified progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रगोल, and स्थ who stays or abides; an inhabitant of the lunar sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रगोलिका|चंद्रगोलिका
चन्द्रगोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रगोल the lunar orb, and कन् affix; derived from the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रचञ्चल
चन्द्रचञ्चल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A small fish, (Canda, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and चञ्चल trembling, quivering, and glistering like the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=316" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रदार|चंद्रदार
चन्द्रदार<BR>plu. m. (-राः)<BR>The twenty-seven lunar mansions, which, in mythology, are so many nymphs, daughters of DAKṢA, and wedded to CANDRA, or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and दार a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रनिभ
चन्द्रनिभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Like the moon, bright, handsome.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and निभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रभागा|चंद्रभागा
चन्द्रभागा<BR>f. (-गा-गी)<BR>The name of a river, the Chinab, one of the five streams of the Punjab.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रभाग the name of a mountain, part of the Himāla range, where the river is said to have its source, affix of derivation अण्, hence also it may be read चान्द्रभागा-गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रप्रभ|चन्द्रप्रभः
चन्द्रप्रभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The eighth^1 Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 A compound of various drugs used in jaundice, piles, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and प्रभा light.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमणि|चंद्रमणि|चन्द्रमणिः
चन्द्रमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The Candrakānta or moon-gem: see चन्द्रकान्त.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमण्डल|चन्द्रमण्डलं
चन्द्रमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The orb or disc of the moon, the lunar sphere.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमस्|चंद्रमस्
चन्द्रमस्<BR>m. (-माः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र camphor, मा to mete or measure, and असि Uṇādi affix; rendering all objects white like camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रमौलि|चंद्रमौलि|चन्द्रमौलिः
चन्द्रमौलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and मौलि a crest; this deity being represented with a half moon on his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्ररेखा|चंद्ररेखा
चन्द्ररेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A digit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्ररेणु|चंद्ररेणु|चन्द्ररेणुः
चन्द्ररेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A plagiarist, a poetical thief, (काव्यचौर.)<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलेखा|चंद्रलेखा
चन्द्रलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A plant, (Serrantula anthelmintica): see सोमराजी.<BR>2 A digit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and लेखा a line or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलोक|चंद्रलोक|चन्द्रलोकः
चन्द्रलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The sphere or heaven of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रलौह|चंद्रलौह
चन्द्रलौह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and लौह metal; also चन्द्रलौहकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवंश|चंद्रवंश|चन्द्रवंशः
चन्द्रवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The race of the moon, the second great branch of the Kṣatriya or royal dynasties, derived from the moon, through BUDHA his son, and Purūravas his son.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and वंश race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवंशिन्
चन्द्रवंशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A member of the lunar dynasty.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रवंश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवल्लरी
चन्द्रवल्लरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A kind of asclepias, (A. acida): see सोमलता.<BR>2 Rue: see ब्राह्मी.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and वल्लरी a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रवाला
चन्द्रवाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र camphor, and वाला a child, a diminutive term in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रविहङ्गम|चन्द्रविहंगम|चन्द्रविहंगमः|चन्द्रविहङ्गमः
चन्द्रविहङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A kind of crane.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, (as white,) and विहङ्गम a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रव्रत|चंद्रव्रत|चन्द्रव्रतं
चन्द्रव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A regal property or virtue.<BR>2 A kind of penance: see चान्द्रायण.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशाला|चंद्रशाला
चन्द्रशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 An upper room, an apartment on the house top.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशालिका|चंद्रशालिका
चन्द्रशालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A room on the top of a house.<BR>E.<BR>कन् affixed to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रशेखर|चंद्रशेखर|चन्द्रशेखरः
चन्द्रशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The name of a mountain; one so called is amongst the hills of Aracan.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and शेखर a crest; whose^1 crest is the moon.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसंज्ञ
चन्द्रसंज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and संज्ञा a name: having all the synonyms of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसम्भव|चन्द्रसंभव|चन्द्रसंभवः
चन्द्रसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Budha, the planet MERCURY.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसम्भवा|चन्द्रसंभवा
चन्द्रसम्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रसालोक्य|चंद्रसालोक्य
चन्द्रसालोक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Attainment of the lunar heaven.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and सालोक्य domicile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रहास|चंद्रहास|चन्द्रहासं|चन्द्रहासः
चन्द्रहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A scimitar.<BR>2 The sword of RĀVAṆA.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Moon plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and हास what derides; outvieing the moon in brightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्राकृति
चन्द्राकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Moon-shaped, like the moon, (in roundness, whiteness, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रातप|चंद्रातप|चन्द्रातपः
चन्द्रातप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 An awning.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and आतप shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रार्द्ध
चन्द्रार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>A half moon, a crescent.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रापीड|चंद्रापीड|चन्द्रापीडः
चन्द्रापीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and आपीड a chaplet; who has the moon like a chaplet amidst his hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्राभास|चंद्राभास|चन्द्राभासः
चन्द्राभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A false moon, an appearance like the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र, and आभास resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिका|चंद्रिका
चन्द्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 A small fish, commonly Cāndā, (Canda of var. species, HAM.)<BR>3 Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकाद्राव|चंद्रिकाद्राव|चन्द्रिकाद्रावः
चन्द्रिकाद्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The moon-stone.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रिका, and द्राव what fuses; liquefying in moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकापायिन्|चंद्रिकापायिन्
चन्द्रिकापायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>The Cakora or hill partridge.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रिका, and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिकाम्बुज|चंद्रिकांबुज|चन्द्रिकाम्बुजं
चन्द्रिकाम्बुज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रिका, and अम्बुज a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रिल|चंद्रिल|चंद्रिलः|चन्द्रिलः
चन्द्रिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A barber.<BR>3 A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon or weapon, &c. bright as the moon, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रोदय|चंद्रोदय|चन्द्रोदयः
चन्द्रोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An awning, a cloth or sheet spread over the large open courts of Hindu houses, upon festival occasions.<BR>2 Moon-rise.<BR>3 A mercurial preparation used in medicine.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and उदय rising, (of a planet, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चन्द्रोपल|चंद्रोपल|चन्द्रोपलः
चन्द्रोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Moon-gem: see चन्द्रकान्त.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चप
चप<BR>r. 1st cl. (चपति)<BR>To caress, to coax, to soothe or console.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चपयति)<BR>To grind or pound.<BR>(इ) चपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (चम्पति चम्पयति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपट|चपटः
चपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The palm with extended fingers: see चपेट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपल|चपलं|चपलः
चपल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Trembling, tremulous, shaking.<BR>2 Wavering, unsteady.<BR>3 Inconsiderately criminal.<BR>4 Swift, expeditious; (also in this sense, or swiftly, adv. n. -लं)<BR>5 Momentary, instantaneous.<BR>6 Agitated violently, overcome with alarm, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>2 A kind of stone.<BR>3 A fish.<BR>4 A thief.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ or fortune.<BR>2 Lightning.<BR>3 A whore.<BR>4 Long pepper.<BR>5 The tongue.<BR>6 Spirituous liquor.<BR>7 A species of the Aryā metre.<BR>E.<BR>चप to go, affix अलच्, or चुप to move, Uṇādi affix कल and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलता
चपलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Moving, trembling.<BR>2 Fickleness, inconstancy.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last, also with त्व, चपलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=317" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपलात्मक
चपलात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Of a fickle or inconstant nature.<BR>E.<BR>चपल, आत्म self, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेट|चपेटः
चपेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>E.<BR>चप to go, affix अच्, चप trembling, and इट् what goes or is, from इट् with क affix; also चपट and चर्पट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेटाघात
चपेटाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A slap with the open hand.<BR>E.<BR>चपेट, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चपेटिका
चपेटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A slap with the open hand.<BR>E.<BR>चपेट, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम|चमः
चम<BR>(उ) चमु r. 1st and 5th cls. (चमति चम्नोति)<BR>To eat, to drink, to take any thing into the mouth, as food, whether solid or liquid.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>(आचामति)<BR>To sip as water.<BR>With वि,<BR>(विचमति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्करण|चमत्करणं
चमत्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Astonishing, producing wonder or surprise.<BR>2 Festival, spectacle.<BR>4 High poetical composition.<BR>E.<BR>चमत् a sound of surprise, and करण making; also चमत्कार and चमत्कृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कार|चमत्कारः
चमत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Astonishment, surprise.<BR>2 Show, spectacle.<BR>3 Row, riot, festive or angry turbulence.<BR>4 Elaborate style or high poetical composition.<BR>5 The name of a tree: see अपामार्ग.<BR>E.<BR>चमत् a sound of surprise, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कारिन्
चमत्कारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Uunsual, surprising, astonishing.<BR>E.<BR>चमत्कार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कृत
चमत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surprised, astonished.<BR>E.<BR>चमत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमत्कृति|चमत्कृतिः
चमत्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Display, spectacle, &c.: see चमत्करण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमर|चमरं|चमरः
चमर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A Chowri or long brush, most usually made of the tail-hairs of the Yak or Bos Grunniens, and employed to whisk off insects, flies, &c.<BR>2 The name of a demon.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A compound pedicle.<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A kind of deer, or rather the Bos Grunniens, erroneously classed by the Hindu writers amongst the deer.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat or be eaten, अर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमरपुच्छ|चमरपुच्छः
चमरपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A small animal with a bushy tail; a squirrel.<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>A Chowri.<BR>E.<BR>चमर, and पुच्छ tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमरिक|चमरिकः
चमरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A species of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>E.<BR>चमर a Chowri, and ठक् affix, growing in clusters, resembling a Chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमस|चमसं|चमसः
चमस<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>1 A vessel used at sacrifices for drinking the juice of the acid asclepias, a kind of ladle or spoon.<BR>2 A cake made of barley, rice, or lentils ground to meal.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Khetpāpara, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>4 A sweetmeat, or flour, sesamum, &c. mixed up with sugar into a kind of cake, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat, असच् Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमू
चमू<BR>f. (-मूः)<BR>1 An army.<BR>2 A squadron, a division of an army consisting of 129 elephants, as many cars, 2187 horse, and 3685 foot.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat or destroy, (the enemy,) and ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूचर|चमूचरः
चमूचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A soldier, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>चमू, and चर who marches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूपति|चमूपतिः
चमूपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A general of division, any general.<BR>E.<BR>चमू, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चमूरु|चमूरुः
चमूरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A kind of deer.<BR>E.<BR>चम to be eaten, ऊरच् affix, and उ final added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प|चंपः|चम्पः
चम्प<BR>r. 1st cl. (-चम्पति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्प|चंपः|चम्पः
चम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>The capital of KARṆA, the modern Bhāgalpur, or a place in its vicinity.<BR>E.<BR>चपि to go, &c., अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पक|चंपक|चम्पकं|चंपकः|चम्पकः
चम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree bearing a yellow fragrant flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2 A division of the jack fruit.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The flower of the Campa.<BR>2 A variety of the banana or plantain, (the fruit.)<BR>E.<BR>चपि to shine, &c. affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकालु|चंपकालु|चंपकालुः|चम्पकालुः
चम्पकालु<BR>(-लुः)<BR>The Jāka or Indian bread fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>चम्पक as above, and आलुच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पकोष|चम्पकोषः
चम्पकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The Jāka: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पाधिप|चम्पाधिपः
चम्पाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of KARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चम्पा the city, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पापुरी
चम्पापुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The city Campā: see चम्पा.<BR>E.<BR>चम्पा, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पालु|चंपालु|चंपालुः|चम्पालुः
चम्पालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>The Jāka: see चम्पकालु.<BR>E.<BR>चम्प for चम्पक, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पावती|चंपावती
चम्पावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The district of Campā or Bhāgalpur.<BR>E.<BR>चम्प the ebony tree, and मतुप् poss. affix, abounding in such trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पू|चंपू
चम्पू<BR>f. (-म्पूः)<BR>A work in which the same subject is continued through alternations in the composition of prose and verse.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat or be eaten, ऊ affix, and प inserted; what is relished by persons of taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पेश|चम्पेशः
चम्पेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>KARṆA the natural brother of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>चम्पा the city Campā, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्पोपलक्षित|चम्पोपलक्षितः
चम्पोपलक्षित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The district of Campā or Bhāgalpur, or<BR>m. plu. (-ताः)<BR>The inhabitants.<BR>E.<BR>चम्प the ebony, and उपलक्षित designated: see चम्पावती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चम्ब
चम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (चम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय<BR>r. 1st cl. (चयते)<BR>To go to or towards, to go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चय|चयः
चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An assemblage, a multitude.<BR>2 A heap, a collection.<BR>3 A mound of earth, raised to form the foundation of a building.<BR>4 A rampart or mound of earth raised from the ditch of a fort.<BR>5 The gate of a fort.<BR>6 Any edifice.<BR>7 A seat, a stool.<BR>8 A cover, a covering.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, aff. अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयन|चयनं
चयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Collecting, gathering.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयनीय
चयनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be collected or gathered.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर<BR>r. 1st cl. (चरति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>3 To behave or act, (in this sense आङ् is usually prefixed);<BR>With अति and आङ् prefixed,<BR>To transgress, to go astray.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To deceive, to betray.<BR>2 To conjure.<BR>3 To attend.<BR>With अनु.<BR>1 To follow, to attend.<BR>2 To imitate.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>1 To practise a duty.<BR>With उत्,<BR>(उच्चरते)<BR>1 To transgress.<BR>2 To expel.<BR>(उच्चरति)<BR>To go up, to rise.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To approach.<BR>2 To worship.<BR>With परि,<BR>To serve.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To prevail as a custom.<BR>2 To declare, to manifest.<BR>With वि and अभि,<BR>To go astray, to act wickedly.<BR>With सम्<BR>(सञ्चरते)<BR>1 To ride upon.<BR>(सञ्चरति)<BR>To accompany.<BR>With सम and आङ्,<BR>1 To perform.<BR>2 To announce.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चारयति)<BR>1 To doubt.<BR>2 To be free from doubt.<BR>With वि prefixed,<BR>To discuss, to dispute, to reason upon or respecting any doubtful points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं)<BR>1 Moveable, locomotive.<BR>2 Trembling, shaking, unsteady.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>2 The planet Mars.<BR>3 A game played with dice and men, similar to backgammon.<BR>4 A wagtail.<BR>5 A cowri.<BR>6 The seventh Karaṇa, (in Astrology.)<BR>7 The Karaṇas collectively.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, affix अच् or टच्, and in the latter case the fem. affix is ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=318" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरक|चरकः
चरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The author of a treatise upon medicine: applied also to the work.<BR>2 A spy or secret emissary, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, Uṇādi affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरट|चरटः
चरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A wagtail; also चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण|चरणं|चरणः
चरण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 The root of a tree.<BR>3 A race, a family.<BR>4 A portion of the Vedas.<BR>5 Fixed or instituted observances.<BR>6 The peculiarity of condition or conduct implied by the English affix hood, as manhood, priesthood, &c.<BR>7 The fourth part of a stanza.<BR>8 (In Prosody,) A dactyl.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Wandering, roaming, going round or about.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणकिशलय
चरणकिशलय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The foot of a lover, a deity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and किशलय lotus filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणगत
चरणगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fallen at one's feet, prostrate.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणग्रन्थि|चरणग्रंथि|चरणग्रन्थिः
चरणग्रन्थि<BR>f. (-न्थिः)<BR>The ancle.<BR>E.<BR>चरण the foot, and ग्रन्थि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपतन
चरणपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Prostration, falling at the feet.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and पतन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपतित
चरणपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Prostrate, fallen at the feet.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणपात|चरणपातः
चरणपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Tread, trampling, foot-fall.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणयुग
चरणयुग<BR>m. (-गं)<BR>1 Both the feet.<BR>2 Two lines of a stanza.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणसेवा
चरणसेवा<BR>f. (-बा)<BR>Service, devotion.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणार्द्ध
चरणार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>1 The half of the foot.<BR>2 Half of the fourth of a stanza.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणानमित
चरणानमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Trodden down, bent or bowed under the feet.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and आनमित bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणाभरण
चरणाभरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An ornament on the feet.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and आभरण ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणामृत
चरणामृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The water in which the feet of a venerable Brahman or teacher have been washed.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and अमृत nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणायुध|चरणायुधः
चरणायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>चरण the foot, and आयुध a weapon, whose foot is his weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणारविन्द|चरणारविंद
चरणारविन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The foot (of a deity, a lover, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and अरविन्द a lotus; also many similar compounds, as चरणपद्मं, चरणकमल, चरणनलिनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणास्कन्दन|चरणास्कंदन
चरणास्कन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trampling, treading on.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and आस्कन्दन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणोदक
चरणोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water in which the feet of a venerable Brahman or spiritual teacher have been washed.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणोपग
चरणोपग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>In contact with the feet, at the feet.<BR>E.<BR>चरण, and उपग approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरत्
चरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Going, going to.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरपुष्ट|चरपुष्टः
चरपुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A mediator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरम|चरमः
चरम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Last, ultimate, final.<BR>2 West, western. चर to go, अम Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमक्ष्माभृत्
चरमक्ष्माभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>The western mountain behind which the sun is supposed to set.<BR>E.<BR>चरम western, and क्ष्माभृत् a mountain; also चरमाचल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमाचल|चरमाचलः
चरमाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरमाद्रि|चरमाद्रिः
चरमाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>See चरमक्ष्माभृत्; also other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चराचर|चराचरं|चराचरः
चराचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Moveable, locomotive.<BR>2 Shaking, trembling, unsteady.<BR>3 Wished, desired.<BR>4 Moveable and immoveable.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The world.<BR>2 Sky, atmosphere.<BR>3 Heaven, paradise.<BR>4 The aggregate of all things, whether inanimate or animate.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, affix अच, and the derivative reiterated, आङ् inserted; or चर what goes, and अचर what does not go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरि|चरिः
चरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An animal in general.<BR>E.<BR>चर locomotive, and इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित|चरितं
चरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, gone to, attained.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Fixed institute, proper or peculiar observance: see चरण.<BR>2 Story, adventures.<BR>3 Practice, behaviour.<BR>4 Nature.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितव्य
चरितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be followed or observed.<BR>E.<BR>चर, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितार्थ|चरितार्थः
चरितार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Effected, accomplished.<BR>2 Successful.<BR>E.<BR>चरित, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितगुणत्व
चरितगुणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Accompaniment, assistance.<BR>2 Meritorious conduct.<BR>E.<BR>चरित, and गुणत्व faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्र|चरित्रं
चरित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Instituted and peculiar observance or conduct.<BR>2 Story, adventures.<BR>3 Practice, habit, behaviour.<BR>4 Nature, disposition.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, इत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्रबन्धक|चरित्रबन्धकः
चरित्रबन्धक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A friendly pledge, one of unequal value to the loan.<BR>E.<BR>चरित्र, and बन्धक a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरिष्णु|चरिष्णुः
चरिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Moveable, locomotive.<BR>2 Wandering about.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, and इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरीत्र|चरीत्रं
चरीत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Practice, conduct, behaviour: see चरित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरु|चरुः
चरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 An oblation of rice, barley, and pulse, boiled with butter and milk for presentation to the gods or manes.<BR>2 The vessel in which such an oblation is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>चर to eat, उण् Uṇādi affix, what the gods feed upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुव्रण|चरुव्रणः
चरुव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of cake.<BR>E.<BR>चर to eat, उ affix, edible, and व्रण what is ground or pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुश्रपण
चरुश्रपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sprinkling an oblation of milk and ghee.<BR>E.<BR>चरु and श्रपण scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुस्थाली
चरुस्थाली<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The vessel in which an oblation is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>चरु, and स्थाली a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्घ
चर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (चर्घत्ति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च|चर्चः|चर्च्च
चर्च<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (चर्चति)<BR>1 To speak or say.<BR>2 To abuse, to reprove, to censure or condemn.<BR>3 To injure or hurt.<BR>4 To inquire.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चर्चयति)<BR>To read over, to peruse carefully, to study; also read चर्च्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरी|चर्च्चरी
चर्चरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A festival, festive sport.<BR>2 A kind of song.<BR>3 Striking the hands to beat time.<BR>4 Curled or woolly hair.<BR>5 Musical symphony or, the recitation of scholars.<BR>6 The noise made at festivals, &c.<BR>7 Flattery, dishonest praise.<BR>E.<BR>चर्च to speak or say, to sound, &c. रल and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरीक|चर्चरीकः|चर्च्चरीकः
चर्चरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A form of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A potherb.<BR>3 Decorating or curling the hair.<BR>E.<BR>चर्चरी noise, &c. and क who utters, from कै to sound, affix ड; some authorities substitute बर्चरीक for this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=319" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चा|चर्च्चा
चर्चा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>1 Reflexion, consideration, the exercise of judgment or deliberation.<BR>2 Cleaning the person with fragrant unguents.<BR>3 Inquiry, investigation.<BR>4 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>चर्च to read, &c. affixes अङ् and टाप्; also चर्चिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिका|चर्च्चिका
चर्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ or CĀMUṆḌĀ.<BR>2 Cleaning the person with perfumes.<BR>3 Deliberation, inquiry.<BR>E.<BR>चर्च to ask, affix ण्वुल्; also चर्चा as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चित|चर्च्चितं
चर्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Perfumed, anointed, smeared with sandal, &c.<BR>2 Sought, desired.<BR>3 Inquired into or after, investigated.<BR>E.<BR>चर्चा smearing, &c. and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च्च|चर्च|चर्चः
चर्च्च<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्च्चते चर्च्चयते)<BR>1 To speak, to tell.<BR>2 To reprove.<BR>3 To study: see चर्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्त्त्य
चर्त्त्य<BR>mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>1 To be hurt or injured.<BR>2 To be strung or tied in order.<BR>E.<BR>चृत to hurt, &c. and क्यप् affix, form special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पट|चर्पटः
चर्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The open palm of the hand with fingers extended.<BR>2 A plant, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>3 A quantity of bubbles or specks, (स्फारविपुल.)<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A thin cake or biscuit of flour.<BR>E.<BR>चर्प a Sautra root, to be low or flat, affix अटच्; also चपट and चपेट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ब|चर्ब्ब
चर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (चर्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्भट|चर्भटः
चर्भट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus): see इर्व्वारु.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>The noise of merriment or festivity: see चर्च्चरी.<BR>E.<BR>चारु agreeable sound, and भट what makes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्म|चर्म|चर्मं|चर्म्मं
चर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>A shield: see चर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकरण|चर्मकरण
चर्म्मकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Working in skins or leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकषा|चर्मकषा
चर्म्मकषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, commonly called by a similar name Carmakaṣā or Carmaghās.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म the skin, and कष what injures; also चर्म्मकसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकार|चर्मकार|चर्मकारः|चर्म्मकारः
चर्म्मकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The shoe-maker, a currier or worker in leather, the offspring of a Caṇḍāla woman by a man of the fisherman caste, or of a Vaideha female by a Niṣada.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The plant Carmaghās: see the preceding.<BR>2 The wife of a Carmakāra.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म skin or leather, and कार who does or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकारक|चर्मकारक|चर्मकारकः
चर्म्मकारक<BR>m.<BR>A worker in leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and कारक making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकारिन्|चर्मकारिन्
चर्म्मकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A currier, a worker in hides or leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकार्य्य|चर्मकार्य
चर्म्मकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Working in leather or skins.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and कार्य्य business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकील|चर्मकील|चर्मकीलः|चर्म्मकीलः
चर्म्मकील<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A wart.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and कील a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मकृत्|चर्मकृत्
चर्म्मकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A shoe-maker: see चर्म्मकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मचटका|चर्मचटका
चर्म्मचटका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bat.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, and चटका a sparrow, the leather-winged sparrow; also चर्म्मचटिका, चर्म्मचटी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मचटी|चर्मचटी
चर्म्मचटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A bat.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, and चट who hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मज|चर्मज|चर्म्मजं
चर्म्मज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by or from the skin.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Hair.<BR>2 Blood.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मण्वती|चर्मण्वती
चर्म्मण्वती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A river that runs across Bundelkhand into the Ganges, the modern Chambal.<BR>2 The plaintain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्मन् skin, and मतुप् poss. affix; न is changed to ण; it may also be dropped, and the word be written चर्म्मवती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मतरङ्ग|चर्मतरङ्ग|चर्मतरङ्गः|चर्म्मतरङ्गः
चर्म्मतरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A wrinkle, a fold of skin.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and तरङ्ग a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मदण्ड|चर्मदण्ड|चर्मदंड|चर्मदण्डः|चर्म्मदण्डः
चर्म्मदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A whip.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म a leather (thong), and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मदूषिका|चर्मदूषिका
चर्म्मदूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Leprosy.<BR>2 Cutaneous disease.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and दूष to vitiate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मन्|चर्मन्
चर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Skin, hide, bark, &c.<BR>2 A shield.<BR>3 A student's hide, usually that of an antelope.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, to obstruct, Uṇādi affix मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मनासिका|चर्मनासिका
चर्म्मनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A whip.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and नासिका the nose or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपट्टिका|चर्मपट्टिका
चर्म्मपट्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A piece or strap of leather, for playing upon with dice, a leather backgammon board, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and पट्टिका a fillet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपत्रा|चर्मपत्रा|चर्म्मपत्त्रा
चर्म्मपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A bat, the small house-bat.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, and पत्र a wing, the fem. form implies diminutiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मपादुका|चर्मपादुका
चर्म्मपादुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leather shoe.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and पादुका a slipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मप्रभेदिका|चर्मप्रभेदिका
चर्म्मप्रभेदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shoe-maker's awl.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, भिद to pierce, with प्र prefixed, and वुन् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मप्रसेवक|चर्मप्रसेवक|चर्मप्रसेवकः|चर्म्मप्रसेवकः
चर्म्मप्रसेवक<BR>mf. (-वकः-विका)<BR>A bellows.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, सिव to sew, प्र prefix, and वुन् affix; what is sewn or made of leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मबन्ध|चर्मबन्ध|चर्मबंध|चर्मबन्धः
चर्म्मबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A leather band or strap.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and बन्ध band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्ममय|चर्ममय
चर्म्ममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Leather, made of leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्ममुण्डा|चर्ममुण्डा|चर्ममुंडा
चर्म्ममुण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A form of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म a shield, and मुण्ड a bald head; whose head is round like a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मयष्टि|चर्मयष्टि|चर्मयष्टिः
चर्म्मयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A whip.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मरु|चर्मरु|चर्मरुः|चर्म्मरुः
चर्म्मरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A shoe-maker, a worker in leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, and रु to make a noise, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मसम्भवा|चर्मसम्भवा|चर्मसंभवा
चर्म्मसम्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Cardamoms: see एला.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म skin, and सम्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मसार|चर्मसार|चर्मसारः|चर्म्मसारः
चर्म्मसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Lymph, serum.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्माच्छादित|चर्माच्छादित
चर्म्माच्छादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered with skin.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and आच्छादित covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मावकर्त्तन|चर्मावकर्तन|चर्मावकर्त्तन
चर्म्मावकर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Working in leather or skins.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and अवकर्त्तन cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मावकर्त्तिन्|चर्मावकर्तिन्|चर्मावकर्त्तिन्
चर्म्मावकर्त्तिन्<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A worker in leather or skins, a man of the lowest caste.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and अवकर्त्तिन् who cuts off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मावनद्ध|चर्मावनद्ध
चर्म्मावनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Covered with skin.<BR>2 Tied with leather, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and अवनद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मावृत|चर्मावृत
चर्म्मावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered with skin or leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and आवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्माम्भस्|चर्माम्भस्|चर्मांभस्
चर्म्माम्भस्<BR>n. (-म्भः)<BR>Lymph, serum.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मार|चर्मार|चर्मारः|चर्म्मारः
चर्म्मार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A worker in leather.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and ऋ to go, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्म्मिन्|चर्मिन्
चर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>1 Having a hide or skin.<BR>2 Leather, made of leather, &c.<BR>m. (-र्म्मी)<BR>1 A soldier armed with a shield, a shield bearer.<BR>2 A tree of which the bark is used for writing upon, &c. see भूर्ज, a sort of birch.<BR>3 One of ŚIVA'S doorkeepers: see भृङ्गरीट.<BR>4 A plantain.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म skin, a shield, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्य्य|चर्य
चर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be gone, (in or by.)<BR>nf. (-र्य्यं-र्य्या)<BR>1 Perseverance in religious austerities.<BR>2 Due and regular observance of all rites or customs.<BR>3 Following the rules of studentship.<BR>4 Going.<BR>5 Eating.<BR>6 Practice, usage.<BR>7 Behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, and यत् or ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व|चर्व्व
चर्व<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्वति चर्व्वयति)<BR>To eat, to chew, to masticate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=320" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वण|चर्वण|चर्वणं|चर्व्वणं
चर्व्वण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Chewing, masticating.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व्व to chew, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वन्|चर्वन्
चर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>Striking with the flat of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, affix वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वित|चर्वित|चर्व्वितं
चर्व्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Chewed.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व्व to eat, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्वितपात्र|चर्वितपात्र
चर्व्वितपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A spitting pot.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व्वित chewed, (pān or tobacco,) पात्र a vessel; also चर्व्वितपात्रकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्व्य|चर्व्य|चर्व्व्यं
चर्व्व्य<BR>mfn. (-र्व्व्यः-र्व्व्या-र्व्व्यं)<BR>To be chewed.<BR>n. (-र्व्व्यं)<BR>Solid food, requiring mastication.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व्व to chew, यत् affix; also चर्व्वणीय, चर्व्वितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्षणि|चर्षणिः
चर्षणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल<BR>r. 1st cl. (चलति)<BR>To tremble, to shake or totter.<BR>r. 6th cl. (चलति)<BR>To sport, to play, to frolic or wanton.<BR>r. 10th cl. (-चालयति)<BR>To cherish, to foster.<BR>(चालयति, चलयति)<BR>To shake, to cause to shake.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To fall as from a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Trembling, tremulous, unfixed or unsteady.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Trembling, shaking.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The goddess of fortune, LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 Lightning.<BR>3 Incense.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix अच्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलकर्ण|चलकर्णः
चलकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The true distance of a planet from the earth<BR>E.<BR>चल, and कर्ण hypothenuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचञ्चु|चलचंचु|चलचञ्चुः
चलचञ्चु<BR>m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>The Greek partridge: see चकोर.<BR>E.<BR>चल tremulous, and चञ्चु a beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचित्त
चलचित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Fickle, inconstant.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Fickleness, mutability.<BR>E.<BR>चल, and चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलचित्तता
चलचित्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fickleness, unsteadiness, inconstancy.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last: also with त्व, चलचित्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्
चलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्पद
चलत्पद<BR>n. adv. (-दं)<BR>Moving, walking.<BR>E.<BR>चलत्, and पद a step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलत्पूर्णिमा|चलत्पूर्ण्णिमा
चलत्पूर्णिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A small fish, (Canda, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>चलत् trembling, and पूर्णिमा full moon, being of a white, glistering colour, like that of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलदङ्ग|चलदङ्गः
चलदङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A fish, a sort of gilt-head.<BR>E.<BR>चलत् trembling, and अङ्ग body; also with कन् added चलदङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलदल|चलदलः
चलदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The holy fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>चल shaking, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलद्विष|चलद्विषः
चलद्विष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The Kokila or cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलन|चलनं|चलनः
चलन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>1 Who or what goes or moves.<BR>2 Trembling, tremulous, shaking.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 A deer, an antelope.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A short petticoat worn by common women.<BR>2 The tye of an elephant.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wandering, roaming.<BR>2 Trembling, shaking.<BR>3 Going.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलनक|चलनकं|चलनकः
चलनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A short petticoat worn by women of some rank.<BR>E.<BR>चलन, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलमान
चलमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Going, moving, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलस्
चलस्<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>Wood sorrel: see अम्ल.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलसन्धि|चलसंधि|चलसन्धिः
चलसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>Moveable articulation of the bones, Diarthrosis.<BR>E.<BR>चल, and सन्धि a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलाचल|चलाचलः
चलाचल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Tremulous, unsteady, unfixed.<BR>2 Moveable and stationary.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix अच्, deriv. reiterated, and the first final vowel made long, or चल, and अचल immoveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलि|चलिः
चलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A cover, a wrapper, a surtout: see निचोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलित|चलितं
चलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>2 Gone, departed.<BR>3 Went, proceeded.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलु|चलुः
चलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A handful of water, water taken up in the hollowed palm of the hand for rincing the mouth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलुक|चलुकः
चलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The hand hollowed as for holding a little water, &c.<BR>2 A small pot, a gallipot, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A handful of water: see चलु.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, उकच affix: see चुलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलेन्द्रिय|चलेंद्रिय
चलेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sensitive, sensual, not having subdued senses or passions.<BR>E.<BR>चल, and इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चवि|चविः
चवि<BR>f. (-विः-वी)<BR>The pepper plant or a kind of it.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व to eat, इन् affix; also sometimes ङीष्, deriv. irr.; also चव्य and चविका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चविक|चविकं
चविक<BR>mf. (-कः-का or की)<BR>A plant that yields a sort of long pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>E.<BR>चर्व to eat, and क्वुन् affix. र rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चव्य|चव्यं
चव्य<BR>nf. (-व्यं-व्या)<BR>A variety of pepper, (Piper chavya, Rox.)<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>Orris root.<BR>E.<BR>चर्व to be eaten, ण्यत् affix, and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष
चष<BR>r. 1st cl. (चषति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR>(चषति-ते)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषक|चषकं|चषकः
चषक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A vessel for drinking spirits with, a wine glass, &c.<BR>2 Any drinking vessel.<BR>3 Spirituous liquor.<BR>4 Honey.<BR>E.<BR>चष to eat, क्वुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषति|चषतिः
चषति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Decay, infirmity.<BR>E.<BR>कृष to plough, ति Uṇādi affix, and च substituted for the radical initials.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषाल|चषालः
चषाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A wooden ring on the top of a sacrificial post.<BR>2 An iron ring at the base of the post.<BR>3 A hive.<BR>E.<BR>चष to eat, &c. आलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चह
चह<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चहति चहयति)<BR>1 To be wicked, to commit wickedness.<BR>2 To cheat.<BR>3 To be proud, &c.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चहयति)<BR>To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिक|चाक्रिकः
चाक्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Circular.<BR>2 Belonging to a wheel or discus.<BR>3 Relating to a company or circle.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A chorister, a bard who chaunts in chorus the praises of kings. heroes, gods, &c.<BR>2 An oil maker.<BR>3 A coachman, a driver.<BR>E.<BR>चक्र a multitude, &c. and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्षुष|चाक्षुषं|चाक्षुषः
चाक्षुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Visible, perceptible, seen.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The sixth Manu.<BR>E.<BR>चक्षुष the eye, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्ग|चांग|चांगः|चाङ्गः
चाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Whiteness or beauty of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>चङ्ग handsome, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाङ्गेरी
चाङ्गेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Wood sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>चाङ्ग as above, and इर to send or cause, affixes अच् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाचलि
चाचलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Moving much or repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, intens. form, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाञ्चल्य|चांचल्य|चांचल्यं|चाञ्चल्यं
चाञ्चल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Tremulousness, unsteadiness.<BR>2 Transitoriness.<BR>E.<BR>चञ्चल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाट|चाटः
चाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A cheat, a rogue, a peculator, one who makes away with money, &c. entrusted to him.<BR>E.<BR>चट to injure, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटकैर|चाटकैरः
चाटकैर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A young sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>चटक a sparrow, and ऐरक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटु|चाटुः
चाटु<BR>mn. (-टुः-टु)<BR>1 Pleasing or grateful discourse.<BR>2 Distinct speech.<BR>3 Flattery.<BR>E.<BR>चट to break, (anger,) Uṇādi affix ञुन्; also चटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुकार
चाटुकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Speaking agreeably or kindly.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A flatterer.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=321" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुपटु|चाटुपटुः
चाटुपटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A jester, a buffoon.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु agreeable speech, and पटु clever; also चाटुवटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुलोल|चाटुलोलः
चाटुलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Elegantly tremulous.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु for चटु beautiful, and लोल trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुवटु|चाटुवटुः
चाटुवटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A jester.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु wit, and वटु who utters: see चाटुपटु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुशत
चाटुशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Repeated coaxing or intreaty.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटूक्ति|चाटूक्तिः
चाटूक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Agreeable language.<BR>3 Flattery.<BR>E.<BR>चाटु agreeable speech, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणकीन|चाणकीनं
चाणकीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fit for or sown with the chickpea, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>चणक chickpea, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणक्य|चाणक्यः
चाणक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>1 A name of the sage VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>2 Name of a Brahman, the reputed author of a work on polity, and minister of CANDRAGUPTA.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>The work of Cāṇakya, detached stanzas original or compiled, on morals and polity.<BR>E.<BR>चणक a saint, and यञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूर|चाणूरः
चाणूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wrestler in the service of KAṂSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूरसूदन|चाणूरसूदनः
चाणूरसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चाणूर, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डाल|चांडाल|चांडालः|चाण्डालः
चाण्डाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of an impure or degraded tribe, a Caṇḍāla, a Pariah, an outcaste.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A woman of the same tribe.<BR>E.<BR>चडि to be angry, Uṇādi affix आलञ्, and according to some अण् added; also चण्डाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाण्डालिका|चांडालिका
चाण्डालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A vulgar lute.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 A kind of herb: see चण्डालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातक|चातकः
चातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird, a kind of cuckoo, (Cuculus melano-leucus.)<BR>E.<BR>चत to beg, affix ण्वुल्; begging water from the clouds, the supposed sole source of the fluid which this bird drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातकानन्दन|चातकानंदन|चातकानन्दनः
चातकानन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>चातक, and आनन्दन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर|चातुरः
चातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Perceptible, visible.<BR>2 Speaking well or amiably.<BR>3 Driving, one who drives, a driver, a charioteer, &c.<BR>4 Clever, able, ingenious.<BR>5 Relating to four.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Dexterity, ability, cleverness.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small round pillow for resting the cheek upon.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A carriage, a cart holding four people.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर dexterous, or चतुर् four, अण् affix; also with कन् added चातुरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक|चातुरकः
चातुरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रम्य|चातुराश्रम्यं
चातुराश्रम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>The aggregate of the four orders of student, householder, mendicant and ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, आश्रम order, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरिक|चातुरिकः
चातुरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A charioteer, a coachman.<BR>E.<BR>चातुर a carriage, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थक|चातुर्थकः
चातुर्थक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A quartan ague.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्थ, अण् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्म्मास|चातुर्मास
चातुर्म्मास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Produced in four months.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्म्मास, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास्य|चातुर्मास्यं|चातुर्म्मास्य|चातुर्म्मास्यं
चातुर्मास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>A sacrifice performed every four months.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, and मास a month, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्य्य|चातुर्य|चातुर्यं
चातुर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Dexterity, cleverness.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वर्ण्य|चातुर्व्वर्ण्यं
चातुर्वर्ण्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ण्यः-र्ण्या-र्ण्यं)<BR>Suited to the four tribes, belonging to them, &c.<BR>n. (-र्ण्यं)<BR>The aggregate of the four original castes, the Brāhmaṇa, Kṣatriya, Vaiśya and Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, and वर्ण a class, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विध्य|चातुर्विध्यं
चातुर्विध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Four kinds collectively.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर्विध, and ञ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वैद्य|चातुर्व्वैद्यः
चातुर्वैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A priest, &c. versed in the four Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, वेद a Veda, and ष्यञ् affix; it is also derived from विद्या knowledge, and is optionally as here given, or चातुर्विद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होतृक
चातुर्होतृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Performed by four priests, read or sacrificed by, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर, होतृ a priest, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वाल|चात्वालं|चात्वालः
चात्वाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A hollow made in the ground to receive a burnt offering.<BR>3 Any hole in the ground.<BR>E.<BR>चत to ask, (to solicit the gods,) and वालञ् Uṇādi affix; also चत्वाल, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्दनिक|चांदनिक
चान्दनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of or derived from Sandal, perfumed with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चन्दन, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्र|चांद्र|चान्द्रं|चान्द्रः
चान्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्री-न्द्रं)<BR>Lunar, relating to the moon, regulated by it, &c.<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 The Candrakānta or moon-gem.<BR>2 A month, a lunar month.<BR>3 The light fortnight or half month, during which the moon is on the increase.<BR>n. (-न्द्रं)<BR>The Cāndrāyaṇa observance: see चान्द्रायण.<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and अण् affix of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रक|चांद्रक|चांद्रकं|चान्द्रकं
चान्द्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fresh ginger.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रभागा|चांद्रभागा
चान्द्रभागा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river, the Chinab: see चन्द्रभागा; also चान्द्रभागी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमस|चांद्रमस|चान्द्रमसं|चान्द्रमसः
चान्द्रमस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Lunar, relating or belonging to the moon, &c.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The constellation Mṛgaśiras; stars in Orion.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रमस् the moon, and अण् affix; the moon being its ruling deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमसायन|चांद्रमसायनः|चान्द्रमसायनः
चान्द्रमसायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA, regent of Mercury, and son of CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्रमस the moon, फक् affix; or with फिञ् affix चान्द्रमसायनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रमास|चांद्रमास|चान्द्रमासः
चान्द्रमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A lunar month, from new moon to new moon, when it is called Mukhya, and from full moon to full moon, when it is termed Gauna.<BR>E.<BR>चान्द्र lunar, मास month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायण|चांद्रायण|चांद्रायणं|चान्द्रायणं
चान्द्रायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A religious or expiatory observance, regulated by the moon's age; diminishing the daily consumption of food every day, by one mouthful, for the dark half of the month beginning with fifteen at the full moon, until it is reduced to one, at the new moon, and then increasing it in like manner during the fortnight of the moon's increase: there are other forms of this penance.<BR>E.<BR>चन्द्र the moon, and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायणव्रत
चान्द्रायणव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The penance called Cāndrāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>चान्द्रायण as before, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चान्द्रायणविधान
चान्द्रायणविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The penance called Cāndrāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>चान्द्रायण as before, and विधान rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाप|चापं|चापः
चाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 (In Geometry,) An arc or portion of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>चप to cast, (arrows,) affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापपट|चापपटः
चापपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A tree, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.) see प्रियाल.<BR>E.<BR>चाप a bow, and पट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल|चापलं
चापल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Unsteadiness, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>2 Transitoriness.<BR>E.<BR>चपल trembling, अण् affix; also with यञ् affix चापल्य. n. (-ल्यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापलाश्रय
चापलाश्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Unsteadiness, transitoriness.<BR>E.<BR>चापल, and आश्रय support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल्य|चापल्यं
चापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Unsteadiness: see चापल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाबुका
चाबुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small circular pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामर|चामरं|चामरः
चामर<BR>nf. (-रं-रा or री-रं)<BR>A Chowri, the tail of the Bos grunniens, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">Page323</a>] used to whisk off flies, also as an emblem or insignia of princely rank.<BR>E.<BR>चमर the Yak or Bos grunniens, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=322" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरपुष्प|चामरपुष्पः
चामरपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>2 A kind of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>3 The mango tree.<BR>4 A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>चामर a Chowri, and पुष्प a flower; whose flowers grow in clusters like the Indian Chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरपुष्पक|चामरपुष्पकः
चामरपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of grass: see काश.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिन्
चामरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>चामर a Chowri, and इनि affix, either alluding to his bushy tail, or the custom of whisking off flies, &c. from the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामीकर|चामीकरं
चामीकर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>चमीकर, said to mean a kind of mine, and अण् affix implying production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामुण्डा|चामुंडा
चामुण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 One of the Mātṛkās.<BR>E.<BR>च the moon, and मुण्ड the head; having a head like the moon; or चा for चण्ड the name of a demon, and मुण्ड the skull; having seized the decapitated head of the demon: in either case the deriv. is irregular: see चर्म्ममुण्डा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पिला|चांपिला
चाम्पिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्पेय|चांपेय|चांपेयः|चाम्पेयः
चाम्पेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Nagesar, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>चम्पा the district, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्य|चाम्यं
चाम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Food, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाय
चाय<BR>(ऋ) चायृ r. 1st cl. (चायति-ते)<BR>1 To worship, to revere.<BR>2 To discern, to perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार|चारं|चारः
चार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>3 Binding, a binding, a fetter, &c.<BR>4 A prison, a house of confinement.<BR>5 A kind of tree, the Piyal, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.) see प्रियाल.<BR>6 Wandering about, travelling.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A factitious poison.<BR>E.<BR>चर going, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारक|चारकः
चारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A groom, a horseman, a cavalier.<BR>2 A binding, a fetter.<BR>3 An associate, a companion.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, in the causal form, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारकाण्ड
चारकाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Ascenscional difference, (in Astronomy.)<BR>E.<BR>चार, and काण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचक्षुस्
चारचक्षुस्<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>Espionage.<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>One (a king, &c.) who employs spies.<BR>E.<BR>चार, and चक्षुस् eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचण
चारचण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Graceful in gait or motion.<BR>E.<BR>चार and चणप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारचुञ्चु
चारचुञ्चु<BR>mfn. (-ञ्चुः-ञ्चुः-ञ्च)<BR>Remarkable in walking, of graceful carriage.<BR>E.<BR>चार, and चुञ्चुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारज्या
चारज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>The sine of the ascensional^1 difference.<BR>E.<BR>चार and ज्या a sine.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारटी
चारटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A plant: see पद्मचारिणी.<BR>E.<BR>चर in the causal, what makes go or disperses, (disease,) अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारण|चारणः
चारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A dancer, a mime.<BR>2 An actor of note.<BR>3 A reader of scripture.<BR>4 A panegyrist of the gods.<BR>5 A bard, a herald.<BR>E.<BR>चर in the causal, to cause to go, to diffuse, (fame, &c.) and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारणदारा
चारणदारा<BR>f. plur. (-राः)<BR>Female dancers, actresses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चारण and दारा wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारपथ|चारपथः
चारपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A meeting of two roads.<BR>E.<BR>चार a passenger, and पथिन् a road, ष affix, which leaves अ final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारभट|चारभटः
चारभट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A hero, a chief or warrior.<BR>E.<BR>चार diffusion, (of praise, &c.) and भट who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारयित्वा
चारयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having enjoined or prescribed, having caused to observe.<BR>2 Having made to go.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारवायु|चारवायुः
चारवायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Summer-air, zephyr.<BR>E.<BR>चार causing to go, and वायु air or wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारान्तरित|चारांतरित|चारान्तरितः
चारान्तरित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A secret emissary or spy.<BR>E.<BR>चार, and अन्तरित concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिका
चारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित
चारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Caused to go.<BR>2 Distilled.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिवाच्
चारिवाच्<BR>f. (-क्)<BR>A plant: see कर्क्कटशृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र|चारित्रं
चारित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Peculiar observance or practice, peculiarity of customs or condition: see चरण.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, नित्रन् Uṇādi affix; also चरित्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्र्य
चारित्र्य<BR>n. (-त्र्यं)<BR>Becoming practices, moral conduct or instituted observance.<BR>E.<BR>चरित्र, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारु|चारुः
चारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>Beautiful, elegant.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, Uṇādi affix ञुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुक|चारुकः
चारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The seed of the Sara cane.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुगर्भ|चारुगर्भः
चारुगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A son of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and गर्भ asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुगुप्त|चारुगुप्तः
चारुगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A son of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and गुप्त preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुता
चारुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Loveliness, beauty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to चारु; also with त्व added चारुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुदेष्ण|चारुदेष्णः
चारुदेष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>The son of KṚṢṆA by RUKMIṆĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुधामन्
चारुधामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A plant: see शठी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुधारा
चारुधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of SACI the wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>चारु beautiful, and धारा fame, splendor, &c. some authorities read चारुधामा, from चारु, and धामन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुफला
चारुफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>चारु beautiful, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुमत्|चारुमन्त्
चारुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Lovely, beautiful.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The daughter of KṚṢṆA by RUKMIṆĪ.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुलोचन|चारुलोचनः
चारुलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deer.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman with fine eyes.<BR>E.<BR>चारु beautiful, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुवर्द्धना
चारुवर्द्धना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुवाहु
चारुवाहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>One of KṚṢṆA'S sons.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and वाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुव्रता
चारुव्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A female who observes a month of fasting.<BR>E.<BR>चारु elegant, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुशिला
चारुशिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A jewel, a gem.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and शिला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुशील
चारुशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Lovely, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारुहासिन्
चारुहासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Smiling sweetly.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and हासिन् laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारेक्षण|चारेक्षणः
चारेक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A statesman, a minister or king.<BR>E.<BR>चार a spy, and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्च्चिक्य|चार्चिक्य|चार्चिक्यं|चार्च्चिक्यं
चार्च्चिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Perfuming the person, smearing it with Sandal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर्च to beautify, ण्वुल् affix, and ष्यञ् added: see चर्चिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म्म|चार्म|चार्म्मः
चार्म्म<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मी-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Covered with leather, (a car, &c.)<BR>2 Defended by a hide or skin.<BR>3 Shielded, having a shield.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म leather, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=323" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म्मण|चार्मण|चार्म्मणं
चार्म्मण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A multitude of hides, of shields, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्मन् a hide, &c. and अण् affix of aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म्मिक|चार्मिक
चार्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Leather, made of leather.<BR>2 Belonging to the skin, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्म, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म्मिण|चार्मिण|चार्मिणं|चार्म्मिणं
चार्म्मिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A number of men armed with shields.<BR>E.<BR>चर्म्मिन् a shield bearer, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वङ्गी|चार्वङ्गी|चार्वंगी
चार्व्वङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A beauty.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वाक|चार्वाक|चार्वाकः|चार्व्वाकः
चार्व्वाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sophist, a philosopher; one acquainted with the doctrines of the schools, a sceptic in many matters of Hindu faith, and considered by the orthodox as an atheist or materialist.<BR>E.<BR>चारु good, beautiful, and वाक discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वाघाट|चार्वाघाट
चार्व्वाघाट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Destructive of beauty.<BR>E.<BR>चारु, and हन to destroy, affix घञ् and घट substituted for the radicals; also with घत, चार्व्वाघात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्व्वी|चार्वी
चार्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>1 A beautiful woman, a beauty.<BR>2 The wife of KUVERA.<BR>3 Understanding, intellect.<BR>4 Moonlight.<BR>5 Light, splendor.<BR>E.<BR>चारु beautiful, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाल|चालः
चाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The thatch or roof of a house.<BR>2 The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालक|चालकः
चालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A restive elephant.<BR>E.<BR>चल to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालन|चालनं
चालन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A sieve, a strainer.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Causing to move or go.<BR>2 Muscular action.<BR>E.<BR>चल in the causal, to make go, (grain, &c. through its pores,) ल्युट् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाष|चाषः
चाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The blue jay, (Coracias Indica.)<BR>2 A kingfisher, (according to some.)<BR>E.<BR>चष to injure, (fish, &c.) affix घञ्; also चास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चास|चासः
चास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The blue jay.<BR>2 Sugar cane: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चि
चि<BR>(ञ) चिञ् r. 1st, 5th and 10th cls. (चयति-ते चिनोति चययति or चपयति)<BR>To collect, to gather together, to heap, to assemble, to accumulate, &c.<BR>With अप,<BR>To lose, to squander.<BR>With उप or सम्,<BR>To collect or acquire.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To determine.<BR>With वि and निर,<BR>To determine exactly.<BR>(ईर ण) ईरचिण् r. 1st cl. (चयति)<BR>To injure, (peculiar to the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकरिषु
चिकरिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous to cast or throw.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to throw, desiderative form उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकर्त्तिषु|चिकर्तिषु
चिकर्त्तिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desiring or intending to cut or cut off.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to cut, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सक|चिकित्सकः
चिकित्सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A physician, a practiser in medicine.<BR>E.<BR>कित, to cure, affix ण्वुल्, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सन|चिकित्सनं
चिकित्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Healing, practising medicine.<BR>E.<BR>कित to relieve, reiterative form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सा
चिकित्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>The practice of medicine, healing, curing, administering or applying remedies.<BR>E.<BR>कित to relieve, (disease,) in the reduplicate form, affixes अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सित|चिकित्सितं
चिकित्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Remedied, healed, physicked, cured.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Healing, remedying.<BR>E.<BR>कित, &c.: see the preceding, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिन|चिकिनः
चिकिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>नि preposition, इनच् affix in this sense, and नि changed to चिक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिल|चिकिलः
चिकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mud, mire.<BR>E.<BR>चिक to obstruct, इलच् affix deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षत्|चिकीर्षन्त्
चिकीर्षत्<BR>mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षती-र्षत्)<BR>Wishing, purposing, meaning to do.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षा
चिकीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Desire to do any thing.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, in the desiderative form, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षित
चिकीर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, designed, purposed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Purpose, intention.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षु|चिकीर्षुः
चिकीर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>Desirous to do any thing.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, reiterated, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकुर|चिकुरः
चिकुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Rashly criminal, inconsiderately guilty, punishing or injuring others without consideration.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Hair.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>4 A musk rat.<BR>5 A kind of bird.<BR>6 A kind of tree.<BR>E.<BR>चि imitative sound, and कुर to utter, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकुरपाश|चिकुरपाशः
चिकुरपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Abundance of hair.<BR>E.<BR>पाश affix in this sense: see कचपाश; also with other affixes चिकुरपक्ष, and चिकुरहस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकूर|चिकूरः
चिकूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Hair.<BR>E.<BR>see चिकुर; the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क|चिक्कः
चिक्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (चिक्कयति)<BR>To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क|चिक्कः
चिक्क<BR>mfn. (-क्कः-क्की-क्कं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A musk rat.<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A mouse.<BR>E.<BR>चिक् imitative sound, and क who utters, from कै with ड affix; or चिक्क to give pain, and क affix; or in the last sense, नि preposition changed to चिक्, and कच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कण|चिक्कणं|चिक्कणः
चिक्कण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Unctuous, greasy.<BR>2 Bland, emollient.<BR>3 Smooth, glossy.<BR>4 Slippery.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The betel-nut tree.<BR>nf. (-णं-णा or णी)<BR>1 The betel-nut.<BR>2 A good cow.<BR>E.<BR>चित to think of, Uṇādi affix कन्, the final of the radical changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कणता
चिक्कणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Smoothness, greasiness, oiliness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, चिक्कणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कस|चिक्कसः
चिक्कस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Barley meal.<BR>E.<BR>चिक्क to give pain, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्किण
चिक्किण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Unctuous, greasy.<BR>2 Bland, emollient.<BR>3 Glossy, shining, smooth.<BR>4 Slippery.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>An excellent cow: see चिक्कण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्रंसा
चिक्रंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Wish to go or to approach.<BR>E.<BR>क्रम to go, desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्लिद|चिक्लिदं|चिक्लिदः
चिक्लिद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Moisture, freshness.<BR>E.<BR>क्लिद to be wet, क affix, root redup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिङ्गेट
चिङ्गेट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A shrimp or prawn.<BR>E.<BR>चिङ्ग, handsome, and अट what goes, the radical vowel changed; also चिङ्गडः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचिण्ड|चिचिंडः|चिचिण्डः
चिचिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A sort of gourd, commonly Chichinda, (Trichosanthes anguinæ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचीषत्
चिचीषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Wishing to gather or collect.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चा|चिंचा
चिञ्चा<BR>f. (-ञ्चा)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>चम to eat, affix क्विप्, and the radical vowel changed, चिम् then, चर to go, with ड affix, and the fem. form; what becomes edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चाटक
चिञ्चाटक<BR>mfn. (-कः)<BR>A sort of grass, commonly Ceñcrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चाम्ल|चिञ्चाम्लं|चिञ्चाम्लः
चिञ्चाम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>An acid potherb, (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>चिञ्चा, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिञ्चासार|चिञ्चासारः
चिञ्चासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of potherb, (Rumex vesicatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>चिञ्चा, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिट
चिट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चेटति चेटयति)<BR>1 To be another's messenger or servant.<BR>2 To order as a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित<BR>(ई) चिती r. 1st cl. (चेतति) चित r. 10th cl. (चेतयति-ते) also (इ) चिति r. 10th cl. (चिन्तयनि)<BR>To think or reflect on, to be sensible or rational, to weigh, to remember, to consider, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=324" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
चित्<BR>f. (चित्)<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and affix to words giving them an indefinite signification, as कश्चित् some one, कस्यचित् of some one, &c. see चन.<BR>E.<BR>चित् to remember, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered, veiled, concealed.<BR>2 Collected, accumulated.<BR>3 Piled, heaped.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A funeral pile.<BR>2 A heap, an assemblage.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, &c. affix क्त; also चिति and चिती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिताग्नि|चिताग्निः
चिताग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The funeral fire.<BR>E.<BR>चिता the pile, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिताचूडक|चिताचूडकं
चिताचूडक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mark where a funeral pile has been, a mausoleum, a monument, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चिता a pile, and चूडक a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिति|चितिः
चिति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>Collecting, gathering.<BR>(-तिः-ती)<BR>1 A funeral pile.<BR>2 A heap, a quantity.<BR>3 A pile, a stack.<BR>4 An oblong with quadrangular sides.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, affix क्तिन्, and optionally ङीष् is added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितिका
चितिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small chain worn as an ornament round the loins.<BR>E.<BR>चित to think of, इकन् affix, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्कार
चित्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cry, a scream.<BR>E.<BR>चित् imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्कारशब्द
चित्कारशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>A cry, a scream.<BR>E.<BR>चित्कार the same, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्त|चित्तं
चित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>The mind or faculty of reasoning, the heart considered as the seat of intellect.<BR>E.<BR>चित to consider, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तकलित
चित्तकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Anticipated, expected, calculated.<BR>2 Known.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and कलित computed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तजन्मन्
चित्तजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>Love.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तनिर्वृत्ति
चित्तनिर्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Contentment, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and निर्वृत्ति repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तप्रशम|चित्तप्रशमः
चित्तप्रशम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Tranquil, content.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and प्रशम calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तप्रसन्नता
चित्तप्रसन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Happiness, gaiety, joy.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त the heart, प्रसन्नता happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तराग|चित्तरागः
चित्तराग<BR>mn. (-गः-गं)<BR>Passion, desire.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवत्|चित्तवन्त्
चित्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Kind-hearted, amiable.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविकार|चित्तविकारः
चित्तविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Change of thoughts or feelings.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and विकार alteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविकारिन्
चित्तविकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Changing a person's character or feeling.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and विकारिन् causing change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविप्लव|चित्तविप्लवः
चित्तविप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Madness, insanity.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त the mind, and विप्लव affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तविभ्रम|चित्तविभ्रमः
चित्तविभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Madness, derangement.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त as above, and विभ्रम wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवृत्ति|चित्तवृत्तिः
चित्तवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Inward purpose, feeling, emotion.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and वृत्ति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवेदना
चित्तवेदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Anxiety, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभव
चित्तभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Felt, perceived, being in the thoughts.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभू
चित्तभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>Love.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तभेद|चित्तभेदः
चित्तभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Inconsistency, contrariety of purpose or will.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and भेद difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसङ्ख्य|चित्तसंख्य
चित्तसङ्ख्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्या-ङ्ख्यं)<BR>Pervading the heart, penetrating, knowing the thoughts.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and सङ्ख्य what enumerates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसमुन्नति|चित्तसमुन्नतिः
चित्तसमुन्नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Pride, arrogance, hauteur, haughtiness.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त the mind, समुन्नति elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तसंहति
चित्तसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A multitude of thoughts, minds or emotions.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तहृत्
चित्तहृत्<BR>mfn. (-हृत्)<BR>Winning, fascinating.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and हृत् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तहारिन्
चित्तहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Beautiful, agreeable, fascinating.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and हारिन् what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तापहारिन्
चित्तापहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Captivating, attractive.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and अपहारिन् what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ताभोग|चित्ताभोगः
चित्ताभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Consciousness of pleasure or pain, the attention of the mind to its own sensations.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त the mind, and आभोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तासङ्ग|चित्तासंग|चित्तासङ्गः
चित्तासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Love, attachment, affection.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and आसङ्ग devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तैक्य
चित्तैक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Harmony, agreement, unanimity.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and ऐक्य identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तोन्नति|चित्तोन्नतिः
चित्तोन्नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Pride, &c. see चित्तसमुन्नति.<BR>E.<BR>चित्त, and उन्नति elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्य|चित्यं|चित्यः
चित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>A monument, or any mark of the site of a funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>चिता a pile, and क्यप् affix.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A funeral pile.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, ण्यत् affix, and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्याधिरोहण
चित्याधिरोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Burning with a husband's corpse.<BR>E.<BR>चित्या and अधिरोहण ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्यारोहण
चित्यारोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ascending the funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>चिति, and आरोहण mounting; also चितारोहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (चित्रयति)<BR>1 To paint, to delineate, to colour with various colours, &c.<BR>2 To wonder.<BR>3 To cause wonder or be wonderful.<BR>4 To see a rare or wonderful sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>1 Variegated, spotted, speckled.<BR>2 Wonderful, surprising.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 A plant: see मूषिकपर्णी.<BR>2 A kind of cucumber: see गोडुम्वा.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Danti: see दन्तिका.<BR>4 A name of SUBHADRĀ, the sister of JAGANNĀTHA.<BR>5 A star in the virgin's spike.<BR>6 A kind of snake.<BR>7 The name of a river.<BR>8 Illusion, worldly unreality.<BR>9 The name of a nymph of Svarga.<BR>10 A form of metre.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Wonder, surprise.<BR>2 Painting, delineation, writing, &c.<BR>3 Sky, heaven.<BR>4 A circular ornament, a sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>5 White or spotted leprosy.<BR>6 Facetious conversation, conundrums, riddles, &c.<BR>7 Writing or arrangement of verses in mathematical or other fanciful figures.<BR>mn. (-त्रः-त्रं)<BR>Variegated colour.<BR>E.<BR>चि to accumulate, Uṇādi affix क्ति, or चित् the mind, and त्र what preserves, from त्रै with क affix, and the duplicate त rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रक|चित्रकं|चित्रकः
चित्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Cīta or small hunting leopard.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>3 The castor oil plant.<BR>4 A medicinal plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A mark made with Sandal, &c. on the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकण्ठ|चित्रकंठ|चित्रकण्ठः
चित्रकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, speckled, and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर|चित्रकरः
चित्रकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र colouring, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकम्बल|चित्रकंबल|चित्रकम्बलः
चित्रकम्बल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A painted cloth used as an elephant's housings, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and कम्बल a blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर्म्मन्|चित्रकर्मन्
चित्रकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>1 Astonishing, surprising, working [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">Page326</a>] wonders.<BR>2 Painting, variegating.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 A magician.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>3 A tree, (Dalbergia ougeiniensis.)<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Painting, or a painting.<BR>2 Magic.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and कर्म्मन् function.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=325" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकर्म्मविद्|चित्रकर्मविद्
चित्रकर्म्मविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>1 A painter.<BR>2 A magician.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रकर्म्म, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकाय|चित्रकायः
चित्रकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 A Chita.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र speckled, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकार|चित्रकारः
चित्रकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकूट|चित्रकूटः
चित्रकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The name of a mountain in Bundelkhand, the modern Compteh, and first habitation of RĀMA in his exile.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र wonderful, and कूट peak; it is an epithet of many hills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकृत्
चित्रकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>1 A painter.<BR>2 A tree, (Dalbergia ougieniensis.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रकोल|चित्रकोलः
चित्रकोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of lizard.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र speckled, and क्रोड haunch, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगत
चित्रगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Painted, delineated, represented in a picture.<BR>2 Coloured, variegated.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगन्ध|चित्रगंध|चित्रगन्धं
चित्रगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगुप्त|चित्रगुप्तः
चित्रगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA, or rather one of the fourteen YAMAS.<BR>2 YAMA'S registrar, who records the vices and virtues of mankind.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र wonderful, and गुप्त preserving; or चित्र writing, and गुप्त as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रगो
चित्रगो<BR>mfn. (-गौः-गौः-गु)<BR>Having a brindled cow.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रजल्प|चित्रजल्पः
चित्रजल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>Talking incoherently.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and जल्प prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रतण्डुल|चित्रतण्डुलं
चित्रतण्डुल<BR>mfn. subst. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A medicinal plant, said to possess anthelmintic virtues: see विडङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र wonderful, and तण्डुल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रतल
चित्रतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Painted or variegated on the surface, (as a floor, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रत्वच्
चित्रत्वच्<BR>m. (-त्वक्)<BR>The birch or Bhurja tree.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and त्वच् bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रदण्डक|चित्रदंडक|चित्रदण्डकः
चित्रदण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The cotton plant.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and दण्डक stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रनेत्रा
चित्रनेत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A small bird, the Maina of the dialects.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, and नेत्र an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपक्ष|चित्रपक्षः
चित्रपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and पक्ष a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपत्रिका
चित्रपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a plant, commonly कपित्थानी.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र wonderful, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपदक्रम
चित्रपदक्रम<BR>adv. ind. or n. (-मं)<BR>At a good pace.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, पद a step, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपदा
चित्रपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>2 A kind of metre.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and पद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपर्णिका
चित्रपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Cākuliya, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR>2 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to चित्रपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपर्णी|चित्रपर्ण्णी
चित्रपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 Cākuliya.<BR>2 Madder; also चित्रपर्णिका.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र writing or painting, and पर्ण leaf; the leaves being as it were painted: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपादा
चित्रपादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The Maina, a small bird so called.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र speckled, and पाद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपिच्छक|चित्रपिच्छकः
चित्रपिच्छक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and पिच्छ the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपुङ्ख|चित्रपुंख|चित्रपुङ्खः
चित्रपुङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र wonderful, and पुङ्ख shaft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रपृष्ठ|चित्रपृष्ठः
चित्रपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र speckled, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रफल|चित्रफलः
चित्रफल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of fish, (Mystus chitala, HAM.)<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>1 Egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>2 Prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>3 Gourds of various sorts.<BR>4 A fish, (Mystus karpirat, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रफलक|चित्रफलकः
चित्रफलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, and फलक a scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रभानु|चित्रभानुः
चित्रभानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A name of BHAIRAVA, a form of ŚIVA.<BR>4 The marking-nut plant.<BR>5 Gigantic swallow wort.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, and भानु light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रमृग|चित्रमृगः
चित्रमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The spotted antelope.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रमेखल|चित्रमेखलः
चित्रमेखल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र spotted, and मेखला a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रयोधिन्
चित्रयोधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>1 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>2 A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>4 Any hero.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and योधिन् a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्ररथ|चित्ररथः
चित्ररथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The chief of the Gandharbas or choristers of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र painted, and रथ a car; lord of the painted car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रल|चित्रलः
चित्रल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Variegated or spotted.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A variegated colour.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र painting, and ल what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलेखा
चित्रलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A portrait, a picture.<BR>2 An Apsaras and friend of UṢĀ.<BR>3 A form of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलिखित
चित्रलिखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Represented, delineated, (as in a picture.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and लिखित drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रलोचना
चित्रलोचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The Maina, a small bird so called.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवदाल|चित्रवदालः
चित्रवदाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sheat fish, (Silurus pelorius.)<BR>E.<BR>वित्र variegated, and वदाल a sheat fish, the epithet being a pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवल्लिक|चित्रवल्लिकः
चित्रवल्लिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sheat fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रवृत्ति
चित्रवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Astonishing act or effort.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिज|चित्रशिखंडिज|चित्रशिखण्डिजः
चित्रशिखण्डिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रशिखण्डी one of the seven Ṛṣis, and ज born; being the son of AṄGIRAS; also similar compounds, as चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिन
चित्रशिखण्डिन<BR>m. plu. (-ण्डिनः)<BR>The seven sages or Ṛṣis, but especially as represented in the seven principal stars of the great bear; these sages are MARĪCI, ATRI, AṄGIRAS, PULAHA, PULASTYA, KRATU, and VASIṢṬHA.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र surprising, शिखण्ड a crest, and इनि affix; sing. nom. case, शिखण्डिन् (-ण्डी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत
चित्रशिखण्डिप्रसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रशिखण्डि, and प्रसुत born: see चित्रशिखण्डिज; there are other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रश्री
चित्रश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>Great beauty, or the loveliness of variegated colours.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and श्री beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसंस्थ
चित्रसंस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Pictured, painted.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and संस्थ fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसर्प|चित्रसर्पः
चित्रसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A large speckled snake.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रसेन|चित्रसेनः
चित्रसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One of the judges or recorders of hell.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राक्षी
चित्राक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>The Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, अक्ष an eye, fem. affix ङीष्, implying diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्ग|चित्रांग|चित्राङ्गं|चित्राङ्गः
चित्राङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Painted, spotted, striped, (the body.)<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>2 A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>2 Vermilion.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 Madder.<BR>2 A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">Page327</a>] worm, (Julus cornifex.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र spotted or painted, &c. अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=326" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्गद|चित्राङ्गदः
चित्राङ्गद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A king, the predecessor of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA and PĀṆḌU, and son of ŚANTANU.<BR>2 A judge and recorder in hell.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, अङ्ग body, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राङ्गदसू
चित्राङ्गदसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>चित्राङ्गद the name of a king, uterine brother of VYĀSA, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्राटीर|चित्राटीरः
चित्राटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The forehead spotted with the blood of a goat, slain in the worship of the demon GHAṆṬĀKARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र spotted, &c. and अट to go or be, and ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रान्न
चित्रान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Rice dressed with coloured condiments.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रापूप|चित्रापूपः
चित्रापूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A cake.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र speckled, and आपूप a cake, a plum-cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रायस|चित्रायसं
चित्रायस<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Steel.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र, and अयस् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिक|चित्रिकः
चित्रिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Chaitra or Cheyt, (March-April.)<BR>E.<BR>चित्र the star, and ठन् affix; also ऐत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रित
चित्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Painted.<BR>2 Spotted, striped.<BR>3 Variegated.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र to paint, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिन्
चित्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>1 Variegated.<BR>2 Wonderful.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>One of the four kinds in which women are classed.<BR>E.<BR>वित्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीयमाण
चित्रीयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Astonishing, surprising, causing wonder or astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र with क्यच्, or used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रेश|चित्रेशः
चित्रेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र the star, and ईंश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रोक्ति|चित्रोक्तिः
चित्रोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 A voice from heaven, that of an invisible speaker.<BR>2 A marvellous tale.<BR>3 Agreeable or eloquent discourse.<BR>E.<BR>चि miraculous, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रौदन|चित्रौदनं|चित्रौदनः
चित्रौदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Boiled rice coloured with turmeric, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चित्र variegated, and ओदन boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिदात्मन्
चिदात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The intellectual soul, spirit.<BR>E.<BR>चित, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिद्रूप|चिद्रूपः
चिद्रूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Amiable, good-hearted.<BR>2 Wise, intelligent, of liberal or expansive mind.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>The Supreme Being, as identifiable with intellect or understanding.<BR>E.<BR>चित् mind, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयत्
चिन्तयत्<BR>mfn. (-यत्-यती-यत्)<BR>Reflecting, considering.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तनीय
चिन्तनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be considered or thought.<BR>2 To be comprehended.<BR>3 To be meditated on.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to reflect, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयितव्य
चिन्तयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be considered, to be reflected on.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, (10th cl.) तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तयित्वा
चिन्तयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having thought or considered.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, (10th cl.) क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्ता|चिंता
चिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Reflexion, consideration, recollection.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to reflect, affixes अङ् and ठाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्ताकुल|चिंताकुल
चिन्ताकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Disturbed in thought or distracted by any idea.<BR>E.<BR>चिन्ता, and आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तापर|चिंतापर
चिन्तापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Thoughtful, anxious.<BR>E.<BR>चिन्ता, and पर engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तामणि|चिंतामणि|चिन्तामणिः
चिन्तामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A fabulous gem, supposed to yield its possessor whatever may be required.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिन्ता reflexion, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तायान
चिन्तायान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Reflecting, considering, meditating.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तावत्|चिन्तावन्त्
चिन्तावत्<BR>mfn. (-बान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Thinking, thoughtful.<BR>E.<BR>चिन्ता, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तावेश्मन्|चिंतावेश्मन्
चिन्तावेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>Council house or room.<BR>E.<BR>चिन्ता reflexion, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिडी|चिंतिडी
चिन्तिडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>irregularly changed from तिन्तिडी, q. v. also चिन्तिडीका, कन् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तित|चिंतित|चिन्तितं
चिन्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thought, considered.<BR>2 Reflecting, considering.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Reflexion: see चिन्ता.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिति|चिंतिति|चिंतितिः|चिन्तितिः
चिन्तिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Consideration, reflexion.<BR>E.<BR>चिति to think, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तिया|चिंतिया
चिन्तिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Reflexion, consideration, thinking.<BR>E.<BR>चिति, and इय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्तोक्ति
चिन्तोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Midnight cry or alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्त्य|चिंत्य
चिन्त्य<BR>mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>1 To be considered.<BR>2 To be appreciated or conceived.<BR>3 To be thought of or meditated upon.<BR>E.<BR>चित् to think, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्न|चिन्नः
चिन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Panicum miliaceum,) a various reading of चीन, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्वत्
चिन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्)<BR>Gathering, collecting.<BR>E.<BR>चि to gather, (5th cl.) शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिट|चिपिटः
चिपिट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>नि preposition, पिटञ् affix in this sense, and नि changed to चि.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Rice or grain flattened.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to flatten, क affix, the derivative reduplicated, and च substituted for the radical; also with कन् added चिपिटक; also the pen. becoming उ, चिपुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिटक|चिपिटकः
चिपिटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपुट|चिपुटः
चिपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>See चिपिट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिप्य
चिप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>A whitlow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिमि|चिमिः
चिमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A parrot.<BR>2 A plant, from the fibres of which coarse cloth and rope are made: see पट्ट.<BR>E.<BR>चि imitative sound, and मि to utter, affix क्विप्, with कन् added, चिमिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिमिक|चिमिकः
चिमिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A parrot: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकारिन्
चिरकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Dilatory, tedious, slow.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकाल|चिरकालः
चिरकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A long period.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकालपालित
चिरकालपालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protected for a long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिरकास्त, and पालित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरकालोपार्जित
चिरकालोपार्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Accumulated slowly or after a long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिरकाल, and उपार्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरक्रिय|चिरक्रियः
चिरक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dilatory, tedious, slow.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and क्रिया business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरगत
चिरगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Long absent, a long time gone.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरचेष्टित
चिरचेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Long sought for, of rare occurrence.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and चेष्टित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरजीवक|चिरजीवकः
चिरजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree: see जीवक.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and जीवक lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरजीविन्
चिरजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Long-lived.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 The Jivaka: see the preceding.<BR>4 An [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">Page328</a>] epithet applied especially to eight chiefs or saints, viz. MĀRKAṆḌEYA, AŚVATTHĀMA, BĀLĪ, VYĀSA, HANUMĀN, VIBHĪṢAṆA, KṚPA, and PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>चिर for चिरम् long, and जीविन् living or lived; also चिरञ्जीविन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=327" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरञ्जीविन्|चिरंजीविन्
चिरञ्जीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Long-lived.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरण्टी|चिरंटी
चिरण्टी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A woman married or single, who continues to reside after maturity in her father's house.<BR>2 A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>चिरम् long or late, and अट to go, (from home,) affix अच्, and deriv. irr.; also चिरिण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरतिक्त|चिरतिक्तः
चिरतिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरत्न|चिरत्नः
चिरत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्नी-त्नं)<BR>Old, ancient, what has been or lasted long.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and त्न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरदिवसं
चिरदिवसं<BR>ind.<BR>For a long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and दिवस a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरनिविष्ट
चिरनिविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Long rested, long abided.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and निविष्ट rested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरन्तन|चिरंतन|चिरन्तनः
चिरन्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Old, ancient, antiquated, long lasting.<BR>E.<BR>चिरम् long, and द्यु affix, with तुद augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरम्
चिरम्<BR>ind.<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर to injure, and क affix: this word, and others evidently derived from it, are now considered as particles, and have accordingly appropriate, though strained, etymologies; the derivatives however corresponding with the inflections of the singular number of nouns masculine or neuter, it may have been originally an imperfect noun of the 1st declension, thus; nom. चिरः or चिरं, acc. चिरं, 1st abl. चिरेण, dat. चिराय, 2nd abl. चिरात्, gen. चिरस्य, 3rd abl. चिरे; see these words severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरप्रवासिन्
चिरप्रवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Dwelling a long time abroad.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and प्रवासिन् who is away from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरमित्र
चिरमित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An old friend.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरमेहिन्
चिरमेहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>चिर a long time, and मिह to sprinkle or urine, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरम्भण|चिरम्भणः
चिरम्भण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kite.<BR>E.<BR>चि imitative cry, and रभि to commence, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिररात्र|चिररात्रं
चिररात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A period of very many nights, a long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and रात्र a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिररात्राय
चिररात्राय<BR>ind.<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिररात्र as above, and अय to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरलब्ध
चिरलब्ध<BR>(-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Obtained after a long time, (as a son in old age.)<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरविल्व|चिरविल्वः
चिरविल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>The name of a plant: see करज.<BR>E.<BR>चिर a long time, विल to divide, and व affix; also चिरिविल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरसूता
चिरसूता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A cow that has borne many calves.<BR>E.<BR>चिर for a long time, and सूता prolific; also चिरसूतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरसेवक|चिरसेवकः
चिरसेवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An old servant.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and सेवक who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थ
चिरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Long continuing, enduring, lasting.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and स्थ what is; also चिरस्थायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थायिन्
चिरस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Of long continuance.<BR>E.<BR>चिर for चिर्, and स्थायिन् what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्थित
चिरस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Long enduring, lasting or remaining for a long time.<BR>2 Left behind for a long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and स्थित stayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरस्य
चिरस्य<BR>ind.<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर a long time, अस to be, affix ण्यत्: see चिरम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराटिका
चिराटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hogweed, the white sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरातिक्त|चिरातिक्तः
चिरातिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A sort of gentian: see चिरतिक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराद्
चिराद्<BR>m. (-रात्)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>ind.<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर for a long time, and अद् who eats, from अद with क्विप् affix: or चिर and आजि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराय
चिराय<BR>ind.<BR>A long time.<BR>E.<BR>चिर a long time, and अय to go, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरायुस्
चिरायुस्<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Long-lived.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A deity, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>चिर long, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरारोध|चिरारोधः
चिरारोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Blockade.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and आरोध obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिराश्रित
चिराश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Long maintained or protected.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and आश्रित supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरि|चिरिः
चिरि<BR>r. 5th cl. (चिरिणोति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरि|चिरिः
चिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>चि imitative cry, and रा to utter, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिण्ठी
चिरिण्ठी<BR>f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>1 A woman staying in her father's house.<BR>2 A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>irregularly derived from चिरि to hurt: see चिरण्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिविल्व|चिरिविल्वः
चिरिविल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A tree: see चिरविल्व.<BR>E.<BR>चिरि a parrot, and विख to break, affix व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरु|चिरुः
चिरु<BR>n. (-रु)<BR>The shoulder joint.<BR>E.<BR>चिर to hurt, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरे
चिरे<BR>ind.<BR>A long time: see चिरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरेण
चिरेण<BR>ind.<BR>A long time: see चिरम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरोज्झित
चिरोज्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Long since abandoned or left.<BR>E.<BR>चिर, and उञ्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिर्भिटी
चिर्भिटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल
चिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (चिलति)<BR>To put on clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिलमीलिका
चिलमीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A necklace.<BR>2 A firefly.<BR>3 Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>चिर a long time, and र changed to ल, मील to twinkle or glister, with क्वुन् affix; and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिलिचिम|चिलिचिमः
चिलिचिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A kind of sprat, (Clupea cultrata, B. MSS ?)<BR>2 A kind of prawn, (according to some.)<BR>E.<BR>चिल to sport or play, affix कि, चिलि and reiterated, चिलिचि sport, pastime, मा to mete, to find, क affix, finding sport in marshy places amongst reeds, &c.; this word has various forms, being read as above, and चिलिचीम, चिलिमीनक, चिलीचिम, चिलिचिमि, चिलीम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (-चिल्लति)<BR>1 To be loose, to be slack or flaccid.<BR>2 To indicate one's meaning.<BR>3 To act wantonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्ल|चिल्लः
चिल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ली-ल्लं)<BR>Blear-eyed.<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 The Bengal kite, (Falco cheela, Lath.)<BR>2 A bleared or sore eye.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A potherb, said to be a small kind of Chenopodium: see वास्तूक.<BR>2 A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>चिल्ल to be flaccid or loose, affix अच्: see चुल्ल, or नि preposition, लच् in the second sense, and चिल् substituted for नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लका
चिल्लका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket: see चीलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लभक्ष्या
चिल्लभक्ष्या<BR>f. (क्ष्या)<BR>A vegetable perfume: see हट्टविलाशिनी.<BR>E.<BR>चिल्ल a kite, and भक्ष्य eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिल्लाभ|चिल्लाभः
चिल्लाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A petty thief, a shoplifter, a pick-pocket, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चिल्ल a kite, and आभ resembling, from भा to shine, with आङ् prefix and ड affix, pouncing on his prize like a kite on its prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=328" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवि|चिविः
चिवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The chin.<BR>E.<BR>चीव to take, कि affix, and the radical vowel shortened: see चिवु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिविट|चिविटः
चिविट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Flattened grain. A various reading of चिपिट, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवु|चिवुः
चिवु<BR>m. (-वुः)<BR>The chin: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवुक|चिवुकं|चिवुकः
चिवुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The chin.<BR>E.<BR>चीव to take or cover, कु affix, and कन् added; also चिवु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्न|चिह्नं
चिह्न<BR>Sautra root. 10th cl. (चिह्नयति)<BR>To mark, to spot, to stamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्न|चिह्नं
चिह्न<BR>n. (-ह्नं)<BR>1 A mark of any kind, a spot, stain, sign, symbol, &c.<BR>2 A banner, a standard.<BR>3 A symptom.<BR>E.<BR>चह to pound, affix नक्, and the radical vowel changed to इ, or चिह्न to mark, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नकारिन्
चिह्नकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Spotting, marking.<BR>2 Hideous, frightful.<BR>3 Striking, killing.<BR>E.<BR>चिह्न, and कारिन् who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नधारिणी
चिह्नधारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>चिह्न a mark, and धारिणी possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नित|चिह्नितः
चिह्नित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Marked, spotted, stained, stamped.<BR>2 Designated.<BR>3 Known.<BR>E.<BR>चिह्न to mark, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीक
चीक<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चीकति चीकयति)<BR>1 To be patient, to suffer or endure.<BR>2 To be impatient.<BR>3 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीन|चीनं|चीनः
चीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A kind of deer.<BR>2 A sort of panic, (Panicum miliaceum.)<BR>3 A country, China.<BR>4 A sort of cloth.<BR>5 A thread.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A banner, (perhaps made of deer skin.)<BR>2 Lead.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, नक् affix, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनक|चीनकः
चीनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of panic, (P. miliaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनकर्प्पूर|चीनकर्पूर|चीनकर्पूरः
चीनकर्प्पूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>चीन, and कर्पूर the same; the best is from China.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनज|चीनजं
चीनज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Steel.<BR>E.<BR>चीन, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनपिष्ठ
चीनपिष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 Minium or red-lead.<BR>2 Lead.<BR>E.<BR>चीन China, and पिष्ठ cake; brought in lumps from the hills on the northwest of Bengal, and between it and China.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनवङ्ग|चीनवंग|चीनवङ्गं
चीनवङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Lead, or more probably tutenague.<BR>E.<BR>चीन, and वङ्ग zinc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनांशुक
चीनांशुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>China cloth, silk.<BR>E.<BR>चीन, and अंशुक cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीब्
चीब्<BR>(ऋ) चीवृ r. 1st cl. (चीबति)<BR>To take: see चीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीभ
चीभ<BR>(ऋ) चीभृ r. 1st cl. (चीभते)<BR>To coax, to commend, to flatter.<BR>2 To appropriate praise, to boast, &c.: some authorities substitute वीभृ for this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीय
चीय<BR>(ऋ) चीयृ r. 1st cl. (चीयति-ते)<BR>1 To take, to receive.<BR>2 To wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर|चीरं
चीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Cloth, clothes.<BR>2 A rag, old and torn cloth.<BR>3 Bark, rind.<BR>4 A crest.<BR>5 A kind of garland.<BR>6 Lead.<BR>7 A line, a stroke.<BR>8 Writing.<BR>9 The dress of a Bauddha priest.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A cricket.<BR>2 The ends or hem of a garment.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, Uṇādi affix रक्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरवासस्
चीरवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Clothed in tatters.<BR>E.<BR>चीर, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरि|चीरिः
चीरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>An eye cloth, a veil covering the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>चिर to hurt, and कि affix; the radical vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरिका
चीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to चीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर्ण|चीर्णं|चीर्ण्ण
चीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Conversant, learned.<BR>2 Split, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर्णपर्ण|चीर्णपर्णः|चीर्ण्णपर्ण्ण
चीर्णपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The Nimb: see निम्ब.<BR>2 The date tree, (Elate sylvestris.)<BR>E.<BR>चीर्ण divided, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीलिका
चीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>चीरी imitative cry, and क who utters; also चिल्लका and झिल्लका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीव
चीव<BR>r. 10th cl. (चीवयति)<BR>To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>(-ऋ,) चीवृ r. 1st cl. (चीवति-ते)<BR>1 To take.<BR>2 To wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवर|चीवरं
चीवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The tattered dress of a Bauddha mendicant, or of any mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, &c. and स्वरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरिन्
चीवरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A Bauddha or Jaina mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>चीवर a beggar's dress, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्क|चुक्कं
चुक्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (चुक्कयति)<BR>To inflict or suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्कार|चुक्कारः
चुक्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The roaring of a lion.<BR>E.<BR>चुक्क pain, derived from चुक्क, with अच् affix, ऋ in the causal, to occasion, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्र|चुक्रं|चुक्रः
चुक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>1 Sorrel.<BR>2 Sourness.<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 Acid seasoning.<BR>2 Vinegar made by the acetous fermentation of grain.<BR>f. (-क्रा or क्री)<BR>1 Indian sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>2 Hogplum.<BR>3 The tamarind.<BR>E.<BR>चक to satisfy, Uṇādi affix रक्, and the radical vowel changed to उ; also with कन्, चुक्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रिका
चुक्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Indian sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचि|चुचिः
चुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>The female breast or bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचुक|चुचुकं|चुचुकः
चुचुक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>चुष to such, and क affix, deriv. irr. or चुचु imitative sound, (such as a child makes in sucking,) and क what sounds; also चुचूक and चूचुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचू
चुचू<BR>m. (-चूः)<BR>A potherb, (Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुच्य
चुच्य<BR>(ई) चुच्यी r. 1st cl. (चोच्यति)<BR>1 To distil, to drop.<BR>2 To bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुञ्चु|चुंचु|चुञ्चुः
चुञ्चु<BR>m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>1 The musk rat or shrew.<BR>2 A mixed caste, born of a Brahman father by a Vaideha female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुञ्चुरी|चुंचुरी
चुञ्चुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A game, a kind of hazard played with tamarind seeds in place of dice.<BR>E.<BR>चुञ्च substituted for चिञ्चा the tamarind, and र from रा to get or give, affixes ड and ङीष्, or with ल affix चुञ्चुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट
चुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (चोटति) and 10th cl. (चोटयति)<BR>To wane, to become small, low or shallow.<BR>r. 6th and 10th cls. (चुटति चोटति)<BR>To cut, to pierce or divide;<BR>(इ,) चुटि r. 1st cl. (चुंटति)<BR>To become low or shallow.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चुण्टति^1 चुण्टयति)<BR>To cut, &c.; also चुट्ट and चुड.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्ट
चुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (चुट्टयति)<BR>1 To become small, low or shallow, as a river, &c.<BR>2 To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड
चुड<BR>(इ) चुडि r. 1st cl. (चुण्डति)<BR>To become small, low or shallow.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चुण्डयति)<BR>To cut, to pierce or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्ड
चुड्ड<BR>r. 1st cl. (चुड्डति)<BR>1 To hint one's meaning.<BR>2 To dally, to wanton, to coquet, &c.<BR>3 To act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण
चुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (चुणति)<BR>To cut, to pierce or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्टा|चुंटा
चुण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>A small well or reservoir near a well.<BR>E.<BR>चुडि to be low or shallow, affixes अङ् and टाप्; also चुड्डी, the fem. affix being ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्टी
चुण्टी<BR>f. (-ण्टी)<BR>A small well: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत|चुतः
चुत<BR>(इर) चुतिर r. 1st cl. (चोतति)<BR>To wet, to be wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत|चुतः
चुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>चुत to be moist, affix क; also च्युत and चुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुति|चुतिः
चुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>चुत to be wet, क्तिन् affix; also च्यति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुद
चुद<BR>r. 10th cl. (चोदयति)<BR>1 To send, to direct, to throw or cast.<BR>2 To ask or interrogate.<BR>(इर, इ) इर चुदि r. 1st cl. (चुन्दति-ते)<BR>To sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=329" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुन्दी|चुंदी
चुन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>A procuress, a bawd.<BR>E.<BR>चुद to inquire, affixes क and ङीष्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुप
चुप<BR>r. 1st cl. (चोपति)<BR>To move slowly, to creep or steal along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुब
चुब<BR>(इ,) चुबि r. 1st cl. (चुम्बति) or implying reciprocity, (चुम्बते)<BR>To kiss.<BR>r. 10th cl. (चुम्बयति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुब्र|चुब्रं
चुब्र<BR>n. (-ब्रं)<BR>The face.<BR>E.<BR>चुव to kiss, रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बक|चुंबक|चुंबकः|चुम्बकः
चुम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kisser, a lecher.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 The loadstone.<BR>4 A general scholar, one who knows parts in a variety of books.<BR>5 The upper part or middle of a balance.<BR>E.<BR>चुबि to kiss, affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बत्
चुम्बत्<BR>mfn. (म्बन्-म्बन्ती-म्बत्)<BR>Kissing.<BR>E.<BR>चुवि to kiss, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बन|चुंबन|चुंबनं|चुम्बनं
चुम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Kissing.<BR>2 A kiss.<BR>E.<BR>चुबि to kiss, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बनदान
चुम्बनदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Kissing.<BR>E.<BR>चुम्बन, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बित|चुंबित
चुम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kissed.<BR>E.<BR>चुवि to kiss, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुम्बितवत्
चुम्बितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Kissing.<BR>E.<BR>चुवि, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुर
चुर<BR>r. 10th cl. (चोरयति)<BR>To steal, to rob:<BR>according to some it is also r. 1st cl. (चोरति.)<BR>This root gives its name to the 10th class, which is thence called चुरादि;<BR>(ई) चुरी r. 4th cl. (चूर्य्यते)<BR>To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरा
चुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Theft, stealing.<BR>E.<BR>चुर to steal, affix क, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरी
चुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A small well.<BR>E.<BR>चु, ट to be shallow, affixes क and ङीष्; ट changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल
चुल<BR>r. 10th cl. (चोलयति)<BR>1 To rise, to increase.<BR>2 To raise, to elevate.<BR>2 To dip or dive into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुक|चुलुकं|चुलुकः
चुलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Mud, mire.<BR>2 A small vessel or pot, a gallipot, &c.<BR>3 The hand hollowed to hold water.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water in which pulse has been steeped.<BR>E.<BR>चुल to dip into, affix क्वुन्: see चलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुकिन्
चुलुकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>चुलुक mud, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्प|चुलुंप|चुलुंपः|चुलुम्पः
चुलुम्प<BR>r. 1st cl. (चुलम्पति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To disappear, to be lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्प|चुलुंप|चुलुंपः|चुलुम्पः
चुलुम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Fondling or nursing children, &c.<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>A she goat.<BR>E.<BR>चुलुम्प to cut, अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुम्पिन्
चुलुम्पिन्<BR>m. (-म्पी)<BR>The gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>चुलुम्प to cut, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल|चुल्लः
चुल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (चुल्लति)<BR>1 To manifest one's meaning.<BR>2 To dally, to wanton or coquet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल|चुल्लः
चुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Blear-eyed.<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A blear eye.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A chimney, a fire place.<BR>2 A funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>चुल्ल to indicate meaning, affix अच्; or नि preposition, लच् affix implying moisture of the eyes, and चुल् substituted for नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लक|चुल्लकः
चुल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The palm of the hand hollowed as if to hold water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लकी
चुल्लकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A porpoise.<BR>2 A water pot.<BR>3 The opposite bank of a river.<BR>E.<BR>चुल्ल to dally, (in the water,) क्वुन् affix, and fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लि|चुल्लिः
चुल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>A fire place, a chimney.<BR>E.<BR>चुल्ल to manifest meaning, and इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुस्त|चुस्तं|चुस्तः
चुस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Fried meat.<BR>2 Chaff, rind.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूचुक|चूचुकं
चूचुक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A nipple.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, and deriv. irr.; or चूचु imitative sound, (in sucking,) and क what makes; also चुचुक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडक|चूडकः
चूडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A well.<BR>E.<BR>चुड to become shallow, affix क्वुन् and the vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडा
चूडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 A single lock of hair left on the crown of the head at the ceremony of tonsure.<BR>2 A peacock's crest.<BR>3 Any crest, plume, diadem, &c.<BR>4 The head.<BR>5 Top, summit.<BR>6 An upper house, a room on the top of a house, &c.<BR>7 A kind of bracelet.<BR>8 A small well.<BR>9 Tonsure; more commonly चूडाकरणं.<BR>E.<BR>चूल to elevate, अङ् and टाप् affixes, ल changed to ड, and the vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाकरण|चूडाकरणं
चूडाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Shaving the head all but one lock, considered as a religious, and purificatory rite; it should be performed in the first or third year.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाकर्म्मन्|चूडाकर्मन्
चूडाकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The rite of tonsure: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा, and कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडामणि|चूडामणिः
चूडामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A jewel worn in a crest or a diadem.<BR>2 The Gunja, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>चूडा a crest, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाल|चूडालं
चूडाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Crested, having a lock of hair on the crown of the head, &c.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kind of grass, (Kyllinga monocephala.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा a crest, and ल what has, from ला with ड affix, or लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडालक्षण
चूडालक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Tonsure.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडावत्|चूडावन्त्
चूडावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत)<BR>Crested, having a lock of hair, &c. on the top of the head.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा a crest, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूण
चूण<BR>r. 10th cl. (चूणयति)<BR>To contract, to close or shrink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूत|चूतः
चूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The mango, (Manjifera Indica.)<BR>2 The anus.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to drink, affix क्त, deriv. irr., or चुत to be moist, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूतक|चूतकः
चूतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The mango.<BR>2 A small or shallow well.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूति|चूतिः
चूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The anus: see चुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर
चूर<BR>(इ,) चूरी r. 1st cl. (चूर्य्यते)<BR>To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण<BR>r. 1st cl. (चूर्णयति)<BR>1 To contract, to shrink, to close as an eye, to wink.<BR>2 To throw, to send or direct.<BR>3 To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्ण<BR>mn. (-र्णः-र्णं)<BR>1 Powder, any pulverulent or minute division of substance.<BR>2 Chalk, lime.<BR>3 Aromatic powder, pounded Sandal, &c.<BR>4 Pounded camphor.<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A Cowri, the shell used as a coin.<BR>2 Selection of an unanswerable argument.<BR>3 A river in Bengal.<BR>4 The red powder scattered at the Holi festival.<BR>5 Dust: see चूर्णि.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण to pound, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णक|चूर्णकं|चूर्णकः
चूर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Grain fried and pounded.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Expounding in prose the purport of a foregoing verse, an order or interpretation or prose not abounding in compound words.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णकार|चूर्णकारः
चूर्णकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lime-burner^1, a maker of lime.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण, and कार who makes.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णकुन्तल|चूर्णकुंतल|चूर्णकुन्तलः
चूर्णकुन्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lock of hair, a curl or curling hair.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण what contracts, and कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णखण्ड|चूर्णखंड|चूर्णखण्डं|चूर्णखण्डः
चूर्णखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Pebble, gravel, hardened fragments of earth or brick; limestone nodule, commonly known in India by the name of Concar.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण dust, and खण्ड fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णता
चूर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pulverulence, comminution, the state of dust or powder.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण with तल् affix; also त्व, चूर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णपारद|चूर्णपारदः
चूर्णपारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्णं, and पारद quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णमुष्टि|चूर्णमुष्टिः
चूर्णमुष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A handful of perfume or powder.<BR>E.<BR>चर्ण, and मुष्टि handful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=330" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णि|चूर्णिः
चूर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>A sum of 100 Cowries, the small shells used as coin.<BR>2 A selection or picking out of an unanswerable argument.<BR>2 The grammar of PATAÑJALA, a comment on PĀṆINI'S grammar.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, to pass, (current,) नि Uṇādi affix, and ऊ substituted for the radical vowel, or चूर्ण to direct, &c. affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिका
चूर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Fried and ground rice.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण to pound, वुन् affix, and the feminine form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिकृत्
चूर्णिकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>An annotator, commentator, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्णि selecting, picking out, (meanings or corroborative passages,) and कृत who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णित
चूर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ground, pounded, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>3 Squeezed, smashed.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण to pound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिन्
चूर्णिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-र्णिनी-र्णि)<BR>Made or mixed up with any thing powdered or pounded.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण powder, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीकृत
चूर्णीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reduced to dust or powder, pounded, beaten to pieces.<BR>E.<BR>चूर्ण, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्त्ति|चूर्ति|चूर्तिः
चूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Going.<BR>E.<BR>चर to go, क्तिन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूला
चूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 An upper room, a room on the top of a house.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>E.<BR>चुल to rise, affixes अङ् and टाप्: see चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिका
चूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The root of an elephant's ear.<BR>2 The body of a drama, the inferior personages of the drama collectively.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Flour cakes fried with ghee.<BR>E.<BR>चूल to be or make high, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष
चूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (चूषति)<BR>To drink or suck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषा
चूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Sucking.<BR>2 A leathern girth.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to drink, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्य|चूष्यं
चूष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>To be drunk or sucked.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Any thing that can be eaten by sucking.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृत
चृत<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्त्तति-चर्त्तयति)<BR>To light, to kindle.<BR>(ई) चृती r. 6th cl. (-चृतति)<BR>1 To hurt, to wound or kill.<BR>2 To tie or connect together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृप
चृप<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (चर्पति, चर्पयति)<BR>To light or kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेक्रिय
चेक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who does much or often, active, industrious.<BR>E.<BR>कृ to do, intens. form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेट|चेटः
चेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A servant, a slave.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A female servant.<BR>E.<BR>चिट to serve, affix अण्, also with कन् added चेटक. f. चेटिका; also चेड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटक|चेटकः
चेटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A slave.<BR>2 A gallant: see the last.<BR>3 A servant, a minister, one who fulfils an appointed duty.<BR>E.<BR>चिट to serve, ण्वुल affix, or चेट with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेड|चेडः
चेड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A servant.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>A female servant or slave.<BR>E.<BR>चिट to serve, अण् affix, and ट changed to ड; also चेट, &c. as above, and चेडक, चेडिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेत्
चेत्<BR>ind.<BR>If.<BR>E.<BR>चित to think, to consider, affix विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतक
चेतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Suggesting, causing to think.<BR>2 What thinks or feels, sentient.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>E.<BR>चित to consider, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतन|चेतनः
चेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Alive, living, feeling.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Soul, self.<BR>2 A man.<BR>3 A living and sentient being.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Understanding, intelligence, wisdom, reflection.<BR>E.<BR>चित to reflect, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनावत्|चेतनावन्त्
चेतनावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Living, sentient.<BR>E.<BR>चेतना, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतय
चेतय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>A living and sentient being.<BR>E.<BR>चित to think, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतयमान
चेतयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sentient, reflecting, conscious.<BR>E.<BR>चित to think, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतव्य
चेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be collected, to be gathered.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस्<BR>n. (-तः)<BR>Mind, intellect, the faculty of reasoning or understanding.<BR>E.<BR>चित to consider, Uṇādi affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतोभू
चेतोभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>Love.<BR>E.<BR>चेतस्, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदार
चेदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lizard, a chamelion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदि|चेदिः
चेदि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>The name of a country, perhaps the modern Chandail.<BR>m. plu. (-दयः)<BR>The inhabitants of Cedi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिपति|चेदिपतिः
चेदिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A VASU named UPACARA.<BR>2 A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR>E.<BR>चेदि, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिराज|चेदिराजः
चेदिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA a king killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चेदि the country, and राज a king; also चेदिपति, चेदिराज्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेय
चेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be gathered or collected.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल<BR>(ऋ) चेलृ r. 1st cl. (चेलति)<BR>1 To shake or tremble.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल|चेलं
चेल<BR>mfn. sub. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Cloth, clothes, raiment.<BR>adj.<BR>Vile, wicked, bad.<BR>E.<BR>चिल to wear, affix अग्; also चेलक and चैल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलप्रक्षालक|चेलप्रक्षालकः
चेलप्रक्षालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>चेल, and प्रक्षालक who washes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलाल|चेलालः
चेलाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलिका
चेलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A corset, a boddice.<BR>E.<BR>चेल clothes, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलीम
चेलीम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A small kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्ल
चेल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (चेल्लति)<BR>1 To think.<BR>2 To go: this root is not usually admitted: see चेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेवी
चेवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट|चेष्टं
चेष्ट<BR>r. 1st cl. (चेष्टते)<BR>To act or perform functions, duties, &c. to strive, to endeavour, to be busy or follow any particular avocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टन|चेष्टनं
चेष्टन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Making effort, who or what acts or attempts any act.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्ट, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टमान
चेष्टमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Active, moving.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्ट to exert, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टा
चेष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Effort, exertion, bodily effort.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्ट to act, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टानिरूपण
चेष्टानिरूपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Observing a person's actions.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्टा, and निरूपण investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टानाश|चेष्टानाशः
चेष्टानाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The end of the world.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्टा, and नाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टित|चेष्टितं
चेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Exerted, done with effort.<BR>2 Done.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 Bodily act or function.<BR>3 Action, behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>चेष्ट to act, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्य|चैतन्यं|चैतन्यः
चैतन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Soul, spirit, the deity considered as the essence of all being.<BR>2 Sense, consciousness.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A modern reformer of the Vaiṣṇava faith, considered in Bengal as an Avatāra of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>चेतन intellect, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A sacred tree, a religious fig tree, &c. growing in a village or near it, and held in veneration by the villagers.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 A place of sacrifice or religious worship, an altar, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">Page332</a>] shed kept for sacrifices, &c.<BR>2 A religious building peculiar to the Jainas, a Jaina temple.<BR>3 A Jaina or Bauddha image, &c.<BR>4 A monument, a tombstone, a column, &c. erected in memory of some deceased person, or on the site of a funeral pile.<BR>5 A pile of stones forming a landmark or boundary.<BR>E.<BR>चि to collect, deriv. irr.; or चित to consider, affix क्यप्, चित्य, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=331" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यद्रु|चैत्यद्रुः
चैत्यद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>1 The religious fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>2 A large tree in a village.<BR>E.<BR>चैत्य as above, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यद्रुम|चैत्यद्रुमः
चैत्यद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A large tree in a village.<BR>E.<BR>चैत्य as above, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यमुख|चैत्यमुखः
चैत्यमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A student's water pot.<BR>E.<BR>चैत्य place of sacrifice, and मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्यवृक्ष|चैत्यवृक्षः
चैत्यवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The religious fig tree.<BR>2 A large tree in a village.<BR>E.<BR>चैत्य, and वृक्ष a tree: see चैत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्र|चैत्रं|चैत्रः
चैत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 The month Chaitra or Cheyt, (March-April.)<BR>2 One of the ranges of mountains dividing the continent into portions or Varṣas: see वर्ष.<BR>3 A Bauddha or Jaina religious mendicant.<BR>4 The son of BUDHA by CITRĀ.<BR>n. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A monument erected to the dead, a column or block of wood, a tree, &c. so considered.<BR>2 A small temple.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रा the star, or चित्र wonderful, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रक|चैत्रकः
चैत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also चैत्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ|चैत्ररथं
चैत्ररथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>The garden of the deity KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>चित्ररथ a Gandharba in charge of the garden, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रावली
चैत्रावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The day of full moon in Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>चैत्र the month, and आवली a line, a series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रि|चैत्रिः
चैत्रि<BR>m. (-त्रिः)<BR>The month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रा, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिक|चैत्रिकः
चैत्रिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रा the asterism, or lunar mansion for this month, and ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिन्
चैत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>The month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>चित्रा, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैद्य|चैद्यः
चैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA an adversary of KṚṢṆA, the son of DAMAGHOṢA, and sovereign of Cedi or Chandail.<BR>m. plu. (-द्याः)<BR>The inhabitants of Cedi.<BR>E.<BR>चेदि the country so called, and ज्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैल|चैलः
चैल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>1 Cloth, of cloth.<BR>2 Bred in clothes, (insects or lice, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>चेल cloth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलाशक|चैलाशकः
चैलाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eater of lice, (a goblin so designated.)<BR>E.<BR>चैल an insect found in clothes, and अशक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोक्ष|चोक्षः
चोक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Sung.<BR>2 Pure, clean.<BR>3 Clever, dexterous.<BR>4 Pleasing, delightful, beautiful.<BR>5 Sharp, pungent, keen, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, affix ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोच|चोचं
चोच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Bark, rind.<BR>2 Skin.<BR>3 Cassia bark.<BR>4 Half eaten fruit of the palm.<BR>5 A banana or plaintain: see मोचा.<BR>6 A cocoanut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोचक|चोचकं|चोचकः
चोचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bark, rind.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोटी
चोटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>चुट to be small, affixes अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोड|चोडः
चोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A bodice or jacket.<BR>2 A country: see चोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदना
चोदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A precept, a sacred ordinance or commandment.<BR>2 Sending, commanding, directing, &c.<BR>3 Enjoining, ordaining.<BR>4 Casting, throwing.<BR>E.<BR>चुद to command, &c. affixes ल्यु and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदनागुड|चोदनागुडः
चोदनागुड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A ball for playing with.<BR>E.<BR>चेदना directing or throwing, and गुड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदित
चोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Informed, apprised.<BR>2 Ordered, directed.<BR>3 Appointed.<BR>4 Urged, impelled.<BR>5 Thrown, cast.<BR>E.<BR>चुद to direct, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोद्य|चोद्यं|चोद्यः
चोद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be sent, thrown, or directed.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Surprise, astonishment, wonderful or astonishing.<BR>2 Asking, an asking, a question, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चुद to send, to command, &c. affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोपन|चोपनं
चोपन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Moving, moving slowly.<BR>E.<BR>चुप to move, affix युच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोर|चोरः
चोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A thief, a robber.<BR>2 A perfume called commonly by the same name.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant: see चोरपुष्पी.<BR>E.<BR>चुर to steal, affix अच; also with कन added चोरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरकण्टक
चोरकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of grass, commonly Corkānta, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>चोर, and कण्टक a thorn: the seeds clinging to the feet and clothes of those who walk amongst it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरपुष्पी
चोरपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>चोर a thief, and पुष्प a flower, fem. affix ङीष्: see the last; also with कन् added चोरपुष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरिका
चोरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Theft, robbery: see चौरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोल|चोलः
चोल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>A short jacket, a bodice.<BR>m. (-लः) or m. plu. (-लाः)<BR>A country, the modern Tanjore, the name is also supposed to apply to a part of Birbhum, in Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>चुल to be high or to elevate, affix अच, and ल being changed to ड, चोड ut sup. or चोल a proper name, that of the king of the country applied to the country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलक|चोलकं|चोलकः
चोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A breastplate, a cuirass.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bark, rind.<BR>E.<BR>चुल to elevate, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलकिन्
चोलकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 The shoot of the bambu.<BR>2 The wrist.<BR>3 The orange.<BR>4 A cuirassier, a soldier armed with a breastplate.<BR>E.<BR>चोलक armour, rind, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलोण्डुक|चोलोंडुक|चोलोंडुकः|चोलोण्डुकः
चोलोण्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A diadem, a fillet for the head, a turban or tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष|चोषः
चोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Suction, sucking.<BR>2 Burning, (of the skin,) inflammation.<BR>3 Drying up.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोषण|चोषणं
चोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sucking, suction.<BR>E.<BR>चूष to suck, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोस्क|चोस्कः
चोस्क<BR>m. (-स्कः)<BR>A horse of a particular and good breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष|चौक्षं
चौक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Agreeable, pleasant.<BR>E.<BR>चोक्ष the same, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौड
चौड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डी-डं)<BR>1 Crested, relating to a crest.<BR>2 Relating to tonsure.<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>Tonsure.<BR>E.<BR>चूडा a crest, &c. and अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौडकर्म्मन्|चौडकर्मन्
चौडकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The rite of tonsure.<BR>E.<BR>चौड, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर|चौरः
चौर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>1 A thief, a robber, a pilferer.<BR>2 A plant: see चोरपुष्पी.<BR>3 A perfume.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Stealing, theft.<BR>E.<BR>चोर a thief, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरतस्
चौरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From theft.<BR>E.<BR>चौर, and तसि for the sign of the fifth case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरहृत
चौरहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stolen, robbed.<BR>E.<BR>चौर, and हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरापहृत
चौरापहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Carried off, stolen.<BR>E.<BR>चौर, and अपहृत taken away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरिका
चौरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Theft, robbing.<BR>E.<BR>चोर a thief, वुञ् affix, optionally चोरिका; or चौरी theft, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्य्य|चौर्य|चौर्यं|चौर्य्यं
चौर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Theft, robbing.<BR>E.<BR>चोर a thief, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=332" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्य्यार्ज्जित|चौर्यार्जित
चौर्य्यार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Acquired by plunder or robbery.<BR>E.<BR>चौर्य्य, and अर्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौल
चौल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Relating to a crest or top-knot, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चूला for चूडा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौलकर्म्मन्|चौलकर्मन्
चौलकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The ceremony of tonsure, cutting off all the hair from the head of a child three years old, except one lock on the crown.<BR>E.<BR>चौल or चौड relating to the चूडा or crest, and कर्म्मन् work, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौलुक्य|चौलुक्यः
चौलुक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>One of the Rājarṣis or royal saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवन|च्यवनं|च्यवनः
च्यवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Oozing, trickling, flowing.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a ṚṢI.<BR>E.<BR>च्यु to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु<BR>(ङ) च्युङ् r. 1st cl. (च्यवते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To flow, to drop.<BR>r. 10th cl. (च्यावयति)<BR>1 To laugh.<BR>2 To bear or suffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत<BR>(इर) च्युतिर r. 1st cl. (च्योतति)<BR>To wet thoroughly, to moisten^1 a little, to sprinkle, to drop, to exude.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fallen, dropped, oozed out, &c.<BR>2 Fallen, from or off.<BR>3 Deviated from, erred, strayed.<BR>4 Broken, disordered.<BR>5 Lost.<BR>E.<BR>च्यु to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युताचार
च्युताचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Deviating from duty.<BR>E.<BR>च्युत, and आचार rite, usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युताधिकार
च्युताधिकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dismissed, (from an office, &c.) deprived of, (as a right.)<BR>E.<BR>च्युत lost, and अधिकार function.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युतोत्साह
च्युतोत्साह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Spent, exhausted, incapable of effort.<BR>E.<BR>च्युत, and उत्साह exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युति|च्युतिः
च्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Dropping, dripping, oozing.<BR>2 Falling, falling from.<BR>3 Deviating from.<BR>4 The vulva.<BR>5 The anus.<BR>E.<BR>च्यु to fall, &c. affix क्तिन्; also with ङीष्, च्युती; again with the radical vowel protracted च्यूति &c.; and without the semivowel च्युति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युप|च्युपः
च्युप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The face.<BR>E.<BR>च्यु to laugh, प Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस
च्युस<BR>r. 10th cl. (च्चोसयति)<BR>1 To laugh.<BR>2 To bear.<BR>3 To loose.<BR>4 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योत|च्योतं
च्योत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sprinkling, pouring or dropping forth, falling as an unctuous substance, oozing, trickling, &c.<BR>E.<BR>च्युत to wet or moisten, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योत्न
च्योत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्नी-त्नं)<BR>1 A mover, a goer, one who moves or goes.<BR>2 Oviparous.<BR>3 Abandoned, wicked, void of virtue or purity.<BR>E.<BR>च्यु to go, Uṇādi affix त्नण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ<BR>The aspirated letter corresponding to the preceding, and expressed by Ch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ<BR>mfn. (छः-छा-छं)<BR>1 Pure, clean.<BR>2 Trembling, tremulous, unsteady.<BR>m. (छः)<BR>1 Cutting, dividing.<BR>2 A part, a fragment.<BR>f. (-छा)<BR>1 Covering, concealing.<BR>2 An infant, a child, any young animal.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, or छद to cover, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छग|छगः
छग<BR>mf. (-गः-गा)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, गक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगण|छगणं|छगणः
छगण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>Dried cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>छ a fragment, and गण assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगल|छगलं|छगलः
छगल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A goat.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>A she goat.<BR>2 A kind of convolvulus (C. argenteus), or more probably (C. pes-capræ): see ऋक्षगन्धा.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Blue cloth or raiment.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut or tear, Uṇādi affixes कल and गुट्, or ग substituted for क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलक|छगलकः
छगलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलाङ्घ्री
छगलाङ्घ्री<BR>f. (-ङ्घ्री)<BR>A kind of convolvulus, (C. pes-caprae): see छगला.<BR>E.<BR>छगल a goat, and अङ्घ्रि a foot; also छगलान्त्री, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलाण्डी
छगलाण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलान्त्री
छगलान्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>A kind of convolvulus: see छगलाङ्घ्री.<BR>E.<BR>छगल a goat, and अन्त्र a gut, an entrail; with कन् added, छगलान्त्रिका; also छगलाङ्घी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>1 Light, lustre, splendor.<BR>2 Assemblage, quantity, number.<BR>3 A straight or continuous mark or line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाफल|छटाफलः
छटाफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A palmyra tree.<BR>E.<BR>छटा a line, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटाभा
छटाभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>छटा a streak, and भा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्र|छत्त्रं|छत्त्रः|छत्रं|छत्रः
छत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A parasol, an umbrella, the Indian catta.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>2 A pungent seed, coriander.<BR>3 A mushroom.<BR>4 Anise.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, and ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi affix; hence the word and its derivatives are also written with a double त, छत्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रक|छत्त्रकः|छत्रकः
छत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A king-fisher.<BR>2 A mushroom.<BR>3 A shrub, commonly Kuliyā-khāra.<BR>4 A small vaulted temple, in honour of a deity.<BR>5 A beehive of a conical or umbrella form.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रचक्र|छत्त्रचक्रं
छत्रचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>An astrological diagram.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधार|छत्त्रधारः|छत्रधारः
छत्रधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Bearing a parasol, having or possessing one.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, and धर who has or holds, affix अण्; also छत्रधर, छत्रधारक, and छत्रधारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रधारण
छत्रधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Carrying a catta.<BR>2 The carrying of one as a type of authority.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रपत्र|छत्त्रपत्त्रं|छत्त्रपत्त्रः|छत्त्रपत्र
छत्रपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, and पत्र a leaf, umbrella-leaved; also छत्रपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रभङ्ग|छत्त्रभङ्गः|छत्रभंग|छत्रभङ्गः
छत्रभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Widowhood.<BR>2 Wilfulness, independence.<BR>3 Subversion of dominion, loss of empire, deposition, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छत a parasol, and भङ्ग a breaking; in the first two senses छत्र is used metaphorically, for any cover or defence, as a husband, &c.; in the last it is used by synecdoche, a parasol being one of the ensigns of royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्राक|छत्त्राकं|छत्त्राकः|छत्राकः
छत्राक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, commonly Rāsnā: see रास्ना.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र a parasol, and अक to go, to resemble; affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रातिछत्र|छत्रातिच्छत्र|छत्त्रातिच्छत्त्रः
छत्रातिछत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A fragrant grass, described as growing in marshy ground.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र a mushroom, and अतिछत्र surpassing an umbrella, i. e. more like a catta, than even a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिका
छत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, कन् affix of resemblance, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिन्
छत्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>Bearing a parasol or umbrella.<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्वर|छत्वरः
छत्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 A bower, an arbour.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, स्वरच् Uṇādi affix, and त substituted for द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (छदति-ते and छदयति, or more commonly छादयति.)<BR>1 To cover, to clothe, to veil, to hide, or remove from view: (आङ् is usually prefixed to the root in these senses.)<BR>2 To march.<BR>(इ) छदि r. 1st cl. (छंदति)<BR>To live or breathe, to be or make strong;<BR>also r. 1st and 10th cls. (छन्दति छंदयति)<BR>To cover, &c. as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद|छदः
छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 A wing.<BR>3 A plant: see ग्रन्थिपर्णी.<BR>4 A tree bearing dark blossoms: see तमाल.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, &c. aff. घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=333" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदन|छदनं
छदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 A wing.<BR>3 A covering, a sheathe, a scabbard.<BR>4 Cassia.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover or hide, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदपत्र|छदपत्त्रः|छदपत्रः
छदपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A tree, (Symplocos racemosa, Rox.) see भूर्य्य<BR>E.<BR>छद a cover or skin, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिस्
छदिस्<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>The thatch or roof of a house.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, इसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मतापस|छद्मतापसः
छद्मतापस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A religious hypocrite, a false brother.<BR>E.<BR>छद्म disguise, and तापस an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>1 Trick, deceit.<BR>2 Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>3 Plea, pretext.<BR>4 Masquerade, disguise of person, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छद a cloak, a covering, and मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मवेशिन्
छद्मवेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>Being in disguise, a player.<BR>E.<BR>छद्म and वेशिन् who wears a dress, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्वर
छद्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 An arbour or bower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्च्छन्
छन्च्छन्<BR>ind.<BR>An imitative sound, expressive of sobbing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्द|छंद|छन्दः
छन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Solitary, secret, private.<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Meaning, intention, purport, opinion.<BR>2 Subjection.<BR>3 Poison.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, affix घञ्: see छन्दस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दपातन|छन्दपातनः
छन्दपातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A hypocrite, a pretended and false ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>छन्द subjection, (of all human beings,) and पातन obtaining, from पत to go, affix ल्युट्; also छन्दकपातन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्|छंदस्
छन्दस्<BR>n. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Poetical metre of every kind, but it is also applicable particularly to the metre of the Vedas.<BR>2 Meaning, purport, object, intention.<BR>3 Wish, desire.<BR>4 The Vedas or scripture.<BR>5 Wilfulness, independence, uncontrolled or unrestrained conduct.<BR>E.<BR>चदि to gladden, &c. and असुन् Uṇādi affix, च is changed to छ; also in some senses with a final vowel छन्द, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्कृत|छंदस्कृत
छन्दस्कृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A holy verse.<BR>E.<BR>छन्दस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दस्य|छंदस्य
छन्दस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Made or done at will or according to one's wish.<BR>E.<BR>छन्दस् inclination, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोग|छंदोग|छन्दोगः
छन्दोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A reciter, or chanter of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>छन्दस् the metre of the Vedas, and ग who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्दोनुवृत्त
छन्दोनुवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Humouring, indulgence.<BR>E.<BR>छन्दस् will, and अनुवृत्त conforming to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Private, secret.<BR>2 Solitary.<BR>3 Covered.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छप
छप<BR>(इ) छपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (छम्पति छम्पयति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम
छम<BR>(उ) छमु r. 1st cl. (छमति)<BR>To eat: see चमु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमण्ड|छमंड|छमंडः|छमण्डः
छमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 An orphan, a fatherless son.<BR>2 A lad who has no kinsmen.<BR>E.<BR>छम to eat, अण्डच् Uṇādi affix; also छेमण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द|छर्दः|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्द<BR>r. 10th cl. (छर्दयति)<BR>To vomit, to be sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द|छर्दः|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्द<BR>nf. (-र्दं-र्दी)<BR>Vomiting, sickness, reaching.<BR>E.<BR>छर्द to vomit, affix अच्; also with the affixes ल्युट् and इन्, छर्दन्, छर्दि, &c. ut infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दन|छर्दनं|छर्दनः|छर्द्दन|छर्द्दनं
छर्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Vomiting, reaching, sickness.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The Nimb tree: see निम्ब.<BR>2 The Rākṣasa, ALAMBUṢA.<BR>E.<BR>कृद to be or make sick, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दि|छर्दिः|छर्द्दि|छर्द्दिः
छर्दि<BR>f. (-र्दिः)<BR>Vomiting: see छर्द.<BR>E.<BR>छृद to be sick, इन् Uṇādi affix; also with ङीष् added छर्दी, and with a further addition of कन्, छर्दिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द्दिघ्न|छर्दिघ्न|छर्द्दिघ्नः
छर्द्दिघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The Nimb tree.<BR>E.<BR>छर्द्दि, and घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिकारिपु|छर्द्दिकारिपुः
छर्दिकारिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>छर्दिका vomiting, and रिपु enemy, anti-emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
छर्दिस्<BR>f. (-र्दिः)<BR>Vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>छृद to be sick, Uṇādi affix इसि; also छर्दि and छर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्ष
छर्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (छर्षति-ते)<BR>To kill, to wound, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल|छलं|छलः
छल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Wickedness.<BR>2 Fraud, circumvention, trick, stratagem.<BR>3 Design, device.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, कलच् affix, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलन|छलनं
छलन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Tricking, deceiving.<BR>E.<BR>छल nominal verb, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलनापर
छलनापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cunning, crafty, deceitful.<BR>E.<BR>छलना, and पर addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलयत्
छलयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Deceiving, cheating.<BR>E.<BR>छल nom. verb to cheat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिन्
छलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A cheat.<BR>E.<BR>छल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लि|छल्लिः
छल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>Skin, bark, rind, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छद a cover, ला to give or get; with affix कि, द becomes ल; also with ङीप् added छल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्ली
छल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 Skin, bark, rind, &c.<BR>2 Offspring, posterity.<BR>3 A spreading creeper.<BR>4 A kind of flower.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छवि|छविः
छवि<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>1 Beauty, splendor, brilliance.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>छो to divide, (darkness, &c.) इन् affix, and the deriv. irr. or क्विन् Uṇādi affix; also with ङीष् added छवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छा
छा<BR>f. (छा)<BR>A young animal.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, डा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग<BR>f. (-गः)<BR>A goat.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>A she goat.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, Uṇādi affix गण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागण|छागणः
छागण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fire of dried cowdung.<BR>E.<BR>अण् affix of relation, added to छगण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागभोजिन्
छागभोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A wolf.<BR>E.<BR>छाग, and भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागरथ|छागरथः
छागरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>AGNI or the deity of fire.<BR>E.<BR>छाग a goat, and रथ a car or any vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A goat: see छगल; also with कन् added छागलक.<BR>2 A proper name, the son of CHAGALA or ATRI.<BR>E.<BR>छगल and अण affix; also with इञ् aff. छागलि or कन् added छागलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागलान्त्री
छागलान्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>A plant, (Convolvulus pes-capræ): see छगलान्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागवाहन|छागवाहनः
छागवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of AGNI or the deity of fire.<BR>E.<BR>छाग a goat, and वाहन a vehicle, the goat-borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागिका
छागिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A she goat.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to छागी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut, divided.<BR>2 Thin, feeble, emaciated.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, affix क्त; also छित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्र|छात्त्रः|छात्रं|छात्रः
छात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A scholar, a pupil, a disciple, a tyro or novice.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Honey.<BR>E.<BR>छत्र an umbrella, a screen or cover, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रक|छात्रकं
छात्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Honey in the comb or hive.<BR>E.<BR>छत्रक a hive, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रगण्ड|छात्रगंड|छात्रगण्डः
छात्रगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>An indifferent scholar in poetical composition; one citing imperfect portions only of a verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रदर्शन|छात्रदर्शनं
छात्रदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Oiled butter prepared from milk one day old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद|छादं
छाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A thatch, a roof.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादन|छादनं|छादनः
छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Covering.<BR>2 A covering, a screen, &c.<BR>3 Hiding, concealing.<BR>4 A leaf.<BR>E.<BR>छद to cover, affix ल्यु, and the vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादित|छादितः
छादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut, divided.<BR>2 Covered.<BR>3 Hidden, concealed.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, or छद to cover, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A rogue, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>छद्मन् knavery, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दस|छांदस|छान्दसः
छान्दस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Relating to poetical metre, to the Vedas, &c.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A priest conversant with scripture.<BR>E.<BR>छन्दस्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=334" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छान्दोग्य|छान्दोग्यं
छान्दोग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>1 The doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>2 A celebrated Upaniṣad of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>छान्दस् belonging to the Vedas, ग who goes, and क्य affix of habitude or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाया
छाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Shade.<BR>2 Shadow, reflected image.<BR>3 The wife of the sun.<BR>4 Beauty, splendor, lustre.<BR>5 Light.<BR>6 Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>7 A bribe.<BR>8 A straight or continuous line.<BR>9 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>10 Darkness, obscurity.<BR>11 The shadow of a Gnomon, especially as indicative of the position of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, (to cut off the light, &c.) and य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाकर|छायाकरः
छायाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Shading, shadowing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A catta or umbrella bearer.<BR>2 A species of metre.<BR>E.<BR>छाया shade, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातनय|छायातनयः
छायातनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>छाया the wife of SŪRYA, and तनय a son; also similar compounds, as छायात्मज, छायासुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायातरु|छायातरुः
छायातरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A large tree, one that gives shade or shelter.<BR>E.<BR>छाया, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायात्मज|छायात्मजः
छायात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>SATURN: see छायातनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायापथ|छायापथः
छायापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Æther, the Ākāśa or firmament.<BR>E.<BR>छाया light, and पथ a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायाभृत्
छायाभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>छाया light, and भृत् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामय
छायामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Reflected.<BR>2 Casting a shadow.<BR>E.<BR>छाया, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामित्र|छायामित्रं
छायामित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A catta or parasol.<BR>E.<BR>छाया shade, and मित्र friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामृगधर|छायामृगधरः
छायामृगधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>छाया an image, मृग a deer, and धर who possesses; also छायाधर, and मृगधर severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायासुत|छायासुतः
छायासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>SATURN: see छायातनय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छि|छिः
छि<BR>m. (-छिः)<BR>Abuse, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कण
छिक्कण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sneezing.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small plant, (Artemisia sternutatoria).<BR>E.<BR>छिक्क nominal verb, to sneeze, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्का
छिक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>Sneezing.<BR>E.<BR>छिक् imitative sound, and क what utters, from कै with ड and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्कक
छिक्कक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Sternutatory.<BR>2 Sneezing.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Artemisia sternutatoria.)<BR>E.<BR>छिक्क nominal verb, to sneeze, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित|छितं
छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut, divided.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, affix क्त, deriv irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्ति|छित्तिः
छित्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Cutting, division.<BR>2 A plant, (Galedupa arborea): see करज.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्त्वर
छित्त्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Roguish, fraudulent, knavish, a knave.<BR>2 Hostile, inimical, a foe.<BR>3 Cutting or fit for cutting, (a weapon, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, स्वरच् Uṇādi affix, and त optionally substituted for the radical final, otherwise छिद्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्त्वा
छित्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having cut or divided.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद
छिद<BR>(औ, इर) औछिदिर r. 7th cl. (छिनत्ति छिंत्ते)<BR>To divided, to split, to cut, &c. With the prefix आङ्, To seize, to lay hold of. With the prefix उत, To slay or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद्<BR>mfn. (-द् or त्)<BR>Cutting, destroying, who or what cuts.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदक|छिदकं
छिदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut or split, affix क्वन्; also छिदिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदा
छिदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Cutting, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>छिद, as above, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदि|छिदिः
छिदि<BR>f. (-दिः)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, इ Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिर|छिदिरः
छिदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A rope, a cord.<BR>3 A sword.<BR>4 An axe, a hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Cutting, dividing, what cuts or divides.<BR>2 A knave.<BR>3 Hostile, a foe.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, and कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (छिद्रयति)<BR>1 To pierce, to bore, to perforate, to make openings or holes.<BR>2 To perforate the ear for rings, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 A hole, a vacuity, a perforation, &c.<BR>2 Fault, defect, flaw, (moral or physical.)<BR>3 A weak side.<BR>4 Infirmity.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to pierce, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रकर्ण
छिद्रकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Having the ears pierced.<BR>E.<BR>छिद्र, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रानुसारिन्
छिद्रानुसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Looking out for faults or flaws.<BR>E.<BR>छिद्र, and अनुसारिन् who pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्तर्|छिद्रांतर्
छिद्रान्तर्<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A reed.<BR>E.<BR>छिद्र, and अन्तर् within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रान्वेषिन्
छिद्रान्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Seeking for faults, malicious.<BR>E.<BR>छिद्र, and अन्वेषिन् searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रित|छिद्रितः
छिद्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perforated, pierced, having holes or openings.<BR>E.<BR>छिद्र to pierce, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्वर
छिद्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>See छित्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्न|छिन्नं
छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Cut, divided.<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>1 A whore, a harlot.<BR>2 A tree: see गुडूची.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नक
छिन्नक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Cut a little, incised, not cut off.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to छिन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नकर्ण
छिन्नकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Having the ears cut off.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नकेश
छिन्नकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Shorn, shaven.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and केश the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नधन्वन्
छिन्नधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>A warrior whose bow has been cut or broken by his enemy's arrow.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ननासिक
छिन्ननासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Noseless, having had the nose cut off.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्ननास्य
छिन्ननास्य<BR>mfn. (स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Having the rope that passes through the nose of a draft ox broken.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and नास्य the nose-rein.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नबन्धन
छिन्नबन्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Loosed, liberated.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नभिन्न
छिन्नभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Cut up, destroyed, scattered.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नमस्त
छिन्नमस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Decapitated.<BR>f. (-स्ता)<BR>A form of DURGĀ without her head.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and मस्त the head; also with कन् added छिन्नभस्तक, छिन्नमस्तका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नरुहा
छिन्नरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A tree, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडूची.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न cut, and रुहा what grows; growing again after being cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नवत्
छिन्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having cut or cut off.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नवेशिका
छिन्नवेशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Akaindhi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न what is cut, (a wound,) and विश to enter, वुन् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्नसंशय
छिन्नसंशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Confirmed, confident, free from doubt.<BR>E.<BR>छिन्न, and संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुछुन्दरी|छुच्छुन्दरी
छुछुन्दरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The musk rat or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=335" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुट
छुट<BR>r. 6th and 10th cls. (छोटति छोटयति)<BR>To cut; also चुट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड
छुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (छुडति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुद्र|छुद्रं
छुद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 Retaliating, returning, remedying.<BR>2 A ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप|छुपः
छुप<BR>(औ) ओछुप r. 6th cl. (छुपति)<BR>To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप|छुपः
छुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A small tree, a shrub, a bush.<BR>2 Touch, touching.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>4 War, combat.<BR>E.<BR>छुप to touch, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुर
छुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (छुरति)<BR>To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरा
छुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Lime.<BR>E.<BR>छुर to cut, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरिका
छुरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>छुर to cut, क्वुन् affix, and the fem. form; also with क, and ङीष् affixes, छुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरित|छुरितं
छुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut.<BR>2 Inlaid, set, coated, spread.<BR>3 Blended, intermingled.<BR>E.<BR>छुर to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरितोदर
छुरितोदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Pierced, transpierced.<BR>2 Run through the belly.<BR>E.<BR>छुरित, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरी
छुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A knife: see छुरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृद
छृद<BR>(उ and इर) उछृदिर r. 7th cl. (छृणत्ति छृंत्ते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To vomit.<BR>3 To play.<BR>(ई) छृदी r. 1st and 10th cls. (छर्दति छर्दयति)<BR>To light, to kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृप
छृप<BR>(ई) छृपी r. 1st and 10th cls. (छर्पति छर्पयति)<BR>To light, to inflame or kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेक|छेकः
छेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Tame, domesticated, as a bird or beast.<BR>2 Citizen, town-bred, rakish, buckish, smart, trained in the acuteness and vice of towns.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, affix ईकन, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेकोक्ति|छेकोक्तिः
छेकोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Indirect speech, insinuation, double entendre, hint, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छेक city-bred, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तव्य
छेत्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cut, to be cut off, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तृ
छेत्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ)<BR>1 Who or what cuts.<BR>2 Solving, resolving, (doubts, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद<BR>r. 10th cl. (छेदयति)<BR>To cut, to cover, to divide, but especially into two parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद|छेदः
छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Cutting, dividing.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>3 Solving, dissipating, (as doubt.)<BR>4 The denominator of a fraction.<BR>5 The divisor.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदकर|छेदकरः
छेदकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Cutting.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wood-cutter.<BR>E.<BR>छेद, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदन|छेदनं
छेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cutting, dividing.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदनीय|छेदनीयः
छेदनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be cut or divided.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदि|छेदिः
छेदि<BR>mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि)<BR>Cutting, dividing, a cutter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदित|छेदितं
छेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut, divided.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदितव्य
छेदितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cut or divided.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद्य
छेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be cut or divided.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Amputation, excision^1.<BR>E.<BR>छिद to cut, यत् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेमण्ड|छेमंड|छेमंडः|छेमण्डः
छेमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A fatherless son: see छमण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेलु|छेलुः
छेलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Conyza anthelmintica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छैदिक|छैदिकः
छैदिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ratan, a cane.<BR>E.<BR>छेद cutting, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छो
छो<BR>r. 4th cl. (छ्यति^1)<BR>To cut, to mow, to reap, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिका
छोटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Snapping the thumb and fore finger together.<BR>E.<BR>छुट to touch, वुद aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिन्
छोटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>छो to cut, उटिन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोरण|छोरणं
छोरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Abandoning, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>छुर to cut, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोलङ्ग|छोलंगः|छोलङ्गः
छोलङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A citron, a lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ्यु
छ्यु<BR>r. 1th cl. (छ्यवते)<BR>To go, to move or approach: see च्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज<BR>The third letter of the second class of consonants, corresponding to the letter J in jet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज<BR>mfn. (जः जा जं)<BR>1 Speedy, swift.<BR>2 Eaten.<BR>3 Victorious, triumphant, conquering or a conqueror.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 Birth, production.<BR>4 A parent, a progenitor.<BR>5 Poison.<BR>6 Enjoyment.<BR>7 Light, lustre.<BR>8 Speed.<BR>9 An imp, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>जन to bear or be born, जि to conquer, or other roots, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जकुट|जकुटं|जकुटः
जकुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The Malaya mountain.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष
जक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (जक्षति 3rd plu. जक्षति)<BR>1 To eat.<BR>2 To laugh.<BR>(इ) जक्षि (जंक्षते)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षण|जक्षणं
जक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>जक्ष to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षि|जक्षिः
जक्षि<BR>f. (-क्षिः)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>जक्ष to eat, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षिवस्
जक्षिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-क्षुषी-वत्)<BR>Eating, who eats.<BR>E.<BR>जक्ष to eat, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्म|जक्ष्मः
जक्ष्म<BR>m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR>Consumption, decline: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्मन्
जक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Consumption, phthisis.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष to worship, and मनिन् affix; ज is substituted for the semivowel; also यक्ष्मन्, and with a final vowel जक्ष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगच्चक्षुस्
जगच्चक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्
जगत्<BR>mfn. (-गन्-गती-गत्)<BR>Moveable, loco-motive, transitory.<BR>nf. (-त्-ती)<BR>The world, the universe.<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 People, mankind.<BR>3 A sort of metre, a stanza of forty-eight syllables variously disposed so as to form thirty varieties.<BR>4 A field of Jambu flowers.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, Uṇādi affix अति, जग substituted for the root, and ङीप् fem. affix, or गम as before, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीधर|जगतीधरः
जगतीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>जगती, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीपति|जगतीपतिः
जगतीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>जगती, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीपाल
जगतीपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>जगती, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगतीरुह
जगतीरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>जगती, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्कर्त्तृ|जगत्कर्तृ
जगत्कर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and कर्त्तृ a maker, the creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्कृत्स्न
जगत्कृत्स्न<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The universe.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and कृत्स्न whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्क्षय
जगत्क्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The destruction of the world.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and क्षय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्त्रय
जगत्त्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The three worlds, or heaven, earth, and hell.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्पति|जगत्पतिः
जगत्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्प्राण|जगत्प्राणः
जगत्प्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and प्राण breath or being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्समग्र
जगत्समग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The universe.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and समग्र whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्सर्व्व|जगत्सर्व
जगत्सर्व्व<BR>n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>The whole world.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and सर्व्व whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्साक्षिन्
जगत्साक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and साक्षिन, witness, spectator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्स्रष्टृ
जगत्स्रष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>The creator of the world, BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and स्रष्ट creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=336" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदन्त
जगदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The end of the world.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदम्बा|जगदंबा
जगदम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and अम्बा mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदात्मक
जगदात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Identical with the world.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and आत्मक same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदात्मन्
जगदात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The supreme spirit.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and आत्मन् the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदाधार|जगदाधारः
जगदाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A stay or supporter of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the world, and आधार support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदीश|जगदीशः
जगदीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An epithet of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदेकपावन
जगदेकपावन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Purifying or sanctifying the world.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, एक chief, and पावन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्गौरी
जगद्गौरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A name of MANASĀDEVĪ, the deified wife of the sage JARATKĀRU, and sister to the Nāgas or serpent race.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the world, and गौरी the goddess GAURĪ; a terrestrial GAURĪ; her relationship to the snake breed is supposed to give her an influence over them, which is implored frequently by the Hindus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्घातिन्
जगद्घातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Destroying the world, destructive, hostile to mankind.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and घातिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्धात्री
जगद्धात्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and घात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्वल
जगद्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and वल surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्योनि|जगद्योनिः
जगद्योनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and योनि womb, or place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्वहा
जगद्वहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्विनाश|जगद्विनाशः
जगद्विनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The expiration of a Yuga or period of the world's existence.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the world, and विनाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगनु|जगनुः
जगनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 Fire or its deity.<BR>2 An animal or insect.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथ|जगन्नाथः
जगन्नाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A form of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जगत् the universe, and नाथ lord; a peculiar and celebrated idol of this name is worshipped on the Coromandel coast, in Orissa, and pilgrimages are made to the shrine of JAGANNĀTHA from all parts of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथक्षेत्र
जगन्नाथक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The shrine of JAGANNĀTHA and surrounding district.<BR>E.<BR>जगन्नाथ, and क्षेत्र holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्निवास|जगन्निवासः
जगन्निवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Worldly existence.<BR>2 A deity, as VIṢṆU, in whom the world exists.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नु|जगन्नुः
जगन्नु<BR>m. (-न्नुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 An animal.<BR>E.<BR>जगत्, and नु to send, कु affix; also जगनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्मातृ
जगन्मातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जमत्, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्वस्
जगन्वस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-नुषी-न्वत्)<BR>Who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, वसु affix, root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगर|जगरः
जगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to awaken, अच् affix, deriv. irr.; also जागर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगल|जगलः
जगल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR>2 Armour: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>गल to ooze, अच् affix, and the root reduplicated; otherwise ल interchanged with रः see जगर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्ध|जग्धं
जग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>Food.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, affix क्त, and जग्ध substituted for the regular form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्धि|जग्धिः
जग्धि<BR>f. (-ग्धिः)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Eating, together or in company.<BR>3 Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, क्तिन् affix, and जग्धि substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि<BR>m. (-ग्मिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, कि affix, root reiterated, and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मिवस्
जग्मिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-ग्मुषी-वत्)<BR>Who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, वसु affix, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन|जघनं
जघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Mons veneris.<BR>2 The hip and loins.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill or hurt, जवन substituted for the radical, and अच Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनकूपक
जघनकूपक<BR>m. du. (-कौ)<BR>The hollows of the loins of a handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>जघन the loins, and कूपक a well or pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनचपला
जघनचपला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A woman active as in dancing.<BR>2 A species of the Aryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनेफला
जघनेफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Opposite leaved fig tree, (Ficus oppositi-folia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>जघन the haunch, &c. here put for the stem, and फल fruit; growing round the stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्य|जघन्यः
जघन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 Last, hindmost.<BR>2 Low, vile, base.<BR>3 Worst, vilest, lowest.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>The penis.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A Śūdra or man of the fourth tribe.<BR>E.<BR>जघन the loins, &c. and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्थ
जघन्यगुणवृत्तिस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Vile, addicted to low pursuits.<BR>E.<BR>जघन्य vile, गुण quality, वृत्ति practice, and स्थ standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्यज|जघन्यजः
जघन्यज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A Śūdra.<BR>2 A younger brother or younger born.<BR>E.<BR>जघन्य last, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्वस्
जघन्वस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-नुषी-न्वत्)<BR>Who or what kills.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, वसु affix, root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नि|जघ्निः
जघ्नि<BR>m. (-घ्निः)<BR>A sharp or offensive weapon.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, affix कि, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नु|जघ्नुः
जघ्नु<BR>mfn. (-घ्नुः-घ्नुः-घ्नु)<BR>Striking, beating, injuring, one who does so.<BR>E.<BR>हन to hurt or kill, कु affix, and the radical reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्मिवस्
जघ्मिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-घ्मुषी-वत्)<BR>Killing, who or what kills.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, वसु affix, root repeated, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गपूग
जङ्गपूग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Wickedness, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गम|जंगम|जङ्गमः
जङ्गम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Locomotive, moveable, that which has motion as opposed to that which is stationary.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, affix अच्, and the radical reduplicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गमकुटी|जंगमकुटी
जङ्गमकुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A parasol, a catta or umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गम moveable, and कुटी a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गल|जंगल|जङ्गलं|जङ्गलः
जङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Desert, solitary, waste, jungle, wild, &c.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्ग for जङ्गम moveable, and ल what brings or takes, i. e. appertaining to moveable beings, as beasts, birds, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गाल|जंगाल|जंगालः|जङ्गालः
जङ्गाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A land mark, a limit, a boundary, a ridge of earth running along the edge of a field for collecting water, and forming a passage over it.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्ग locomotion, and ल what makes, आङ् prefixed, with the sense of limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्गुल|जंगुल|जंगुलं
जङ्गुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Poison, venom.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गु locomotive, (an animal,) and ल what destroys, from लु to cut, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घा|जंघा
जङ्घा<BR>f. (-ङ्घा)<BR>The leg.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, जङ्घ substituted for the radical, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाकारिक|जंघाकारिक|जङ्घाकारिकः
जङ्घाकारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A courier, a runner, an express.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्घा a leg, and कर a toll, affix ठन; who levies a toll by his legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाचाण
जङ्घाचाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Cuisses or greaves.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्घा the leg, and त्राण what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जङ्घाल|जंघाल|जङ्घालः
जङ्घाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Quick, rapid, going quickly.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A courier.<BR>2 A deer, an antelope.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्घा the leg, and अल able, stout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज|जजं|जजः
जज<BR>r. 1st cl. (जजति) also (इ) जजि (जंजति)<BR>To fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=337" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज|जजं|जजः
जज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>जज to fight, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जजौजस्
जजौजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Prowess, valour.<BR>E.<BR>जज, and ओजस् power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जञ्जपूक|जंजपूक|जञ्जपूकः
जञ्जपूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Muttering repeatedly.<BR>2 Muttering evil prayers or charms.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ascetic, a devotee, one who does so.<BR>E.<BR>जप to mutter, reiterative form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट
जट<BR>r. 1st cl. (जटति)<BR>To clot, to be entangled, as hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटा
जटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>1 The hair matted as worn by the god ŚIVA, and by ascetics; the long hairs occasionally clotted together, and brought over the head so as to project like a horn from the forehead, at other times allowed to fall carelessly over the back and shoulders.<BR>2 The root of a tree, a fibrous root.<BR>3 Spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR>4 A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>5 Cowach.<BR>6 Hedysarum, various species.<BR>E.<BR>जट to entangle, अच् affix; or जन to be produced, टन् Uṇādi affix, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाजूट|जटाजूटः
जटाजूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A quantity of clotted hair.<BR>2 ŚIVA'S hair.<BR>E.<BR>जटा, and जूट the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाज्वाल|जटाज्वालः
जटाज्वाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>जटा entangled hair, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाटङ्क|जटाटंक|जटाटङ्कः
जटाटङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>जटा as above, टकि to bind, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाटीर|जटाटीरः
जटाटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>जटा as above, अट to go, and ईरन् affix; some copies read जटाचीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाधर|जटाधरः
जटाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>3 Any mendicant wearing the braid of hair.<BR>E.<BR>जटा entangled hair, and धर possessor; also with धारिन्, जटाधारिन् (-री.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटामांसी
जटामांसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>E.<BR>जटा, entangled hair or root, and मांसी the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायु|जटायुः
जटायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A fabulous bird, the son of ARUṆA, killed by RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 Bdellium.<BR>E.<BR>जटा accumulation, आयु or आयुस् life; long-lived; hence also जटायुस् m. (-युः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाल|जटालः
जटाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Wearing clotted hair.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>2 Zedoary.<BR>3 Bdellium.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Spikenard: see जटामांसी.<BR>E.<BR>जटा as above, and लच् affix of possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटावत्|जटावन्त्
जटावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having clotted hair.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansie.)<BR>E.<BR>जटा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटि|जटिः
जटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>1 Waved-leaf fig tree, (F. venosa): see जटिन.<BR>2 Assemblage, multitude.<BR>2 Clotted hair: see जटा.<BR>E.<BR>जट to collect, affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिन्
जटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>Having clotted hair.<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>Wavedleaf fig tree: see जटि.<BR>E.<BR>जटा as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिल|जटिलः
जटिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having any clotted or entangled hair.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lion.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Indian spikenard.<BR>2 Long pepper.<BR>3 Orris.<BR>E.<BR>जटा, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटी
जटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Waved-leaf fig tree: see जटि.<BR>E.<BR>जट to entangle, इ Uṇādi affix, and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटुल|जटुलः
जटुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A freckle, a mark.<BR>E.<BR>जट to accumulate, उलच् affix; also जडुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठर|जठरं|जठरः
जठर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Hard, firm.<BR>2 Bound, tied.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The belly.<BR>E.<BR>जम to eat, अर Uṇādi affix, and ठच् substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरज्वाला
जठरज्वाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Belly-ache, colic, enteritis.<BR>E.<BR>जठर, and ज्वाला burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरनुद्
जठरनुद्<BR>m. (-नुत्)<BR>Cassia fistula.<BR>E.<BR>जठर the belly, and नुद् a laxative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरयन्त्रणा|जठरयंत्रणा
जठरयन्त्रणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Pain endured by the child before birth.<BR>E.<BR>जठर, and यन्त्रणा punishing; for misdeeds in a preceding birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरयातना
जठरयातना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Pain of the child in the womb: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>जठर, and यातना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरव्यथा
जठरव्यथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Colic.<BR>E.<BR>जठर, and व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरस्थ
जठरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Being in the belly.<BR>2 Being in the womb.<BR>E.<BR>जठर, and स्थ what stays; also जठरस्थित, and जठरस्थायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरामय|जठरामयः
जठरामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Dropsy, water in the abdomen.<BR>E.<BR>जठर the belly, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जड|जडं|जडः
जड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>1 Cold, frigid, chilly.<BR>2 Stupid, apathetic, idiotic.<BR>3 Dumb.<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>1 Water: see जल.<BR>2 Lead.<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Cowach.<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Cold, frost, winter.<BR>2 Idiocy, fatuity, stupidity.<BR>3 Dulness, apathy, sluggishness of mind or body.<BR>E.<BR>जल to heap or accumulate, affix अच्, and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडक्रिय|जडक्रियः
जडक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dilatory, working slowly.<BR>E.<BR>जड apathetic, and क्रिया business, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडता
जडता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Coldness, chilliness.<BR>2 Apathy, stupidity.<BR>3 Stupefaction, despair.<BR>E.<BR>जड, as above, and तल् affix of the abstract; also with त्व, जडत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडिमन्
जडिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Stupefaction, insensibility.<BR>2 Stupidity, dulness.<BR>3 Frigidity.<BR>E.<BR>जड cold, &c. इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीकृत
जडीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Paralysed, rendered cold, torpid or insensible, confounded.<BR>E.<BR>जड, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीभूत
जडीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stupefied, paralysed, become torpid, dull, or insensible.<BR>E.<BR>जड, and भूत been, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडुल|जडुलः
जडुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A freckle, a mark.<BR>E.<BR>जल to accumulate, उलच् affix, and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतु|जतुः
जतु<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>Lac, a red dye or animal pigment, analogous to cochineal.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, उ Uṇādi affix, and न changed to त; also with कन् added जतुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुक|जतुकं
जतुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Lac: see the last.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Chakawat:<BR>2 A bat; also जतूका.<BR>3 A fragrant substance.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुकृत्
जतुकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A fragrant substance: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>जतु lac, and कृत what makes or affords; the lac insect building its nest in this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुनी
जतुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुपुत्त्रक
जतुपुत्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man at chess or backgammon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जतु lac, and पुत्त्रक as it were, a son, being coloured with lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुमणि|जतुमणिः
जतुमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A mole, a natural mark on the body.<BR>E.<BR>जतु, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुरस|जतुरसः
जतुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Lac, the dye.<BR>E.<BR>जतु, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतूका
जतूका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A fragrant substance.<BR>2 A bat.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, ऊकच् affix, and न changed to त; also with the pen. short जतुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्रु
जत्रु<BR>n. (-त्रु)<BR>The collar bone, the clavicle.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born. Uṇādi affix रु, and न changed to त; also with कन added जत्रुक n. (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्वश्मक|जत्वश्मकं
जत्वश्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>जतु, and अश्म a stone, कन् affix, like a stone of lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन<BR>r. 3rd cl. but peculiar to the Vedas (जजन्ति); also (ई) जनी r. 4th cl. (जायते)<BR>1 To be born or produced.<BR>r. 10th cl. (जनयति)<BR>To generate or beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=338" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन|जनः
जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Man, individually or collectively, a man, mankind.<BR>2 The universe.<BR>3 A division of the universe or Loka, the residence of deified mortals: see जनलोक.<BR>4 A low man, a wretch.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A mother, &c. see जनि.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A father, a progenitor.<BR>2 The name of a king, sovereign of Mithilā, and father of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकता
जनकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The property of generation, productiveness, paternity.<BR>E.<BR>जनक, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जनकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनकात्मजा
जनकात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ the wife of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>जनक as above, and आत्मजा daughter; also similar compounds, as जनकतनया, जनकसुता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनङ्गम|जनंगम|जनंगमः
जनङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Caṇḍāla, a man of a low or degraded tribe.<BR>E.<BR>जन a mean man, and गम to go, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनता
जनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Mankind, a number of men.<BR>2 Manhood.<BR>3 Generation, birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन a man, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनत्रा
जनत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>An umbrella or parasol.<BR>E.<BR>जन the person, and त्रा saving; from sun and rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Family, race, lineage.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 Tenderness, compassion.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Chakawat; also जननि and जनी.<BR>4 A bat.<BR>5 Arabian jasmin.<BR>6 Valerian.<BR>mf. (-नः-नी)<BR>A parent, a progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>जन to bear or be born, affix ल्युट्, and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननि|जननिः
जननि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 A fragrant plant: see the preceding.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, affix अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनपद|जनपदः
जनपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Any inhabited country.<BR>2 Man, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and पद going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रवाद|जनप्रवादः
जनप्रवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Rumour, report.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and प्रवाद speech, from वद to speak, with प्र prefixed, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनप्रिय|जनप्रियः
जनप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Agreeable to mankind.<BR>2 Philanthropic.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Coriander seed.<BR>2 A tree, (Morunga hyperanthera.)<BR>E.<BR>जन, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमेजय|जनमेजयः
जनमेजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The name of a king, son and successor to PARĪKṢIT.<BR>2 A son of PURU.<BR>E.<BR>जन in the second case, the world, एजृ to shine, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयत्
जनयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Begetting, engendering, producing.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Generating, begetting, producing, who or what does so.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father, a progenitor.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>जन in the causal form, to give birth, to engender, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनरव|जनरवः
जनरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Rumour, report.<BR>2 Calumny, scandal.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनलोक|जनलोकः
जनलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One of the seven Lokas or divisions of the world, the fifth, next above MAHARLOKA, where the sons of BRAHMĀ, and other pious men, reside.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनवल्लभ|जनवल्लभः
जनवल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Kind to or fond of mankind.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and वल्लभ a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनवाद|जनवादः
जनवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>News, rumour, report.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and वाद speech: see जनप्रवाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनश्रुति|जनश्रुतिः
जनश्रुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>News, tidings, intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>जन mankind, and श्रुति that which is heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्थान|जनस्थानं
जनस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The forest Daṇḍaka, (in the Dekhin,) the eastern part of it.<BR>E.<BR>जन a world, and स्थान a place; the resort of a world of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाचार|जनाचारः
जनाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Propriety, decorum, good conduct.<BR>E.<BR>जन mankind, and आचार moral observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनातिग
जनातिग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Superior, superhuman.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and अतिग going beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाधिनाथ|जनाधिनाथः
जनाधिनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and अधिनाथ supreme lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाव्
जनाव्<BR>m. (-नौः)<BR>A preserver or protector of mankind.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and अव to preserve, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्त|जनांत|जनान्तः
जनान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A district, an inhabited country.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and अन्त boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनान्तिक|जनांतिक
जनान्तिक<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>Secret communication, whispering, speaking aside, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and अन्तिक near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनार्द्दन|जनार्दन|जनार्दनः|जनार्द्दनः
जनार्द्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जन mankind, and अर्द्दन worshipping; whom men worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाशन|जनाशनः
जनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wolf.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनाश्रय|जनाश्रयः
जनाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A temporary hall.<BR>E.<BR>जन man, and आश्रय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनि|जनिः
जनि<BR>f. (-निः or -नी)<BR>1 A woman in general.<BR>2 A mother.<BR>3 Birth, production.<BR>4 The wife of a son, or brother's son, &c.<BR>5 A fragrant plant; see जतूका.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born or to bear, Uṇādi affix इन्, and optionally ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिक
जनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Producing.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman, a wife, a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित|जनितं
जनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Engendered, begotten.<BR>2 Occasioned, occurring, produced.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितस्वन
जनितस्वन<BR>m. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sounding, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>जनित, स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितृ
जनितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, (from whom,) तृच् affix; and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनितोद्यम
जनितोद्यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Vigorous, energetic, making exertion.<BR>E.<BR>जनित, and उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनित्व|जनित्वः
जनित्व<BR>m. (-त्वः)<BR>A father.<BR>f. (-त्वा)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, (from whom,) and इत्व Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनिमन्
जनिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Birth, engenderment.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, इमन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनीन
जनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Appropriate, good for, suitable.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनु|जनुः
जनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>Birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, उ Uṇādi affix; also with ऊ affix जनू, f. (-नूः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनुस्
जनुस्<BR>n. (-नुः)<BR>Birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनेष्ट|जनेष्टः
जनेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Desired or prized by mankind.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनोदाहरण|जनोदाहरणं
जनोदाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Fame, glory.<BR>E.<BR>जन mankind, and उदाहरण pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनौघ|जनौघः
जनौघ<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>A multitude, a mob.<BR>E.<BR>जन, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तु|जंतु|जंतुः|जन्तुः
जन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>Any animal, any being endowed with animal life; it is more usually applied however to beings of the lowest organization.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुकम्बु|जंतुकंबु|जन्तुकम्बुः
जन्तुकम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>A shell, a snail's shell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जन्तु, and कम्बु a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुका|जंतुका
जन्तुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lac.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to जन्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=339" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुघ्न|जन्तुघ्नं|जन्तुघ्नः
जन्तुघ्न<BR>nf. (-घ्नं-घ्नी)<BR>1 A plant, and vermifuge: see विडङ्ग.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A citron.<BR>E.<BR>जन्तु an animal, (a worm,) and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुनाशन|जन्तुनाशनं
जन्तुनाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR>E.<BR>जन्तु, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुफल|जंतुफल|जन्तुफलः
जन्तुफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR>E.<BR>जन्तु an animal, and फल a leaf; its leaves swarm with insects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्तुला
जन्तुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>जन्तु an animal or insect, and ला what gets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्म|जन्मं
जन्म<BR>mn. (-न्मः-न्मं)<BR>Birth: see जन्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मकील|जन्मकीलः
जन्मकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म birth, and कील the stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मद|जन्मदः
जन्मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A father.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म birth, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मन्
जन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, and मनिन् Uṇādi affix, or with a final vowel जन्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मनक्षत्र
जन्मनक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The planet or constellation under which a person is born.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मभूमि|जन्मभूमिः
जन्मभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Native country, birthplace.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवत्|जन्मवन्त्
जन्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Mortal, living.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवर्त्मन्
जन्मवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म birth, and वर्त्मन् path or way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मवैलक्षण्य
जन्मवैलक्षण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Acting contrary to one's origin, unbecoming one's birth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and वैलक्षण्य inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मशोधन
जन्मशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acquitting the obligations derived from birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and शोधन wiping away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मसाफल्य
जन्मसाफल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Attainment of the object or end of existence.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and साफल्य fruitfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्तर|जन्मांतर|जन्मान्तरं
जन्मान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The other world.<BR>2 Regeneration, another birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मान्ध|जन्मांध|जन्मान्धः
जन्मान्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Blind from birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्माष्टमी
जन्माष्टमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The eighth lunation or dark half of Bhadra, the birth day of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म, and अष्टमी eighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मिन्
जन्मिन्<BR>m. (-न्मी)<BR>An animal, an existent being.<BR>E.<BR>जन्म birth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्मेजय|जन्मेजयः
जन्मेजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The name of a prince: see जनमेजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्य|जन्यं|जन्यः
जन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 To be born or produced.<BR>2 Fit for or favourable to men.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 A father. The friend, attendant, or companion of a bridegroom.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>The friend of a mother.<BR>2 The relation or companion of a bride, a bridesmaid, &c.<BR>3 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>4 Affection.<BR>5 A mother.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 War, combat.<BR>2 Rumour, report.<BR>3 A market, a fair.<BR>4 A portent, one occurring at birth.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, &c. affix यत्, or Uṇādi affix युक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्यु|जन्युः
जन्यु<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>1 An animal, an existent and sentient being.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 Fire or Agni.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, &c. Uṇādi affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप<BR>r. 1st cl. (जपति)<BR>1 To speak, to say or tell.<BR>2 To meditate, to speak internally, to say to one's self.<BR>With उप prefixed,<BR>To divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप|जपः
जप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Muttering prayers, repeating inaudibly passages from the scriptures, charms, names of a deity, counting silently the beads of a rosary, &c.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The China rose, the flower or plant; also जवा.<BR>E.<BR>जप to repeat inaudibly, affix अप्; the flower is a sacred object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपन|जपनं
जपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inaudible repetition of prayers, &c.: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>जप as before, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपनीय
जपनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be meditated on, to be repeated inaudibly.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपपरायण|जपपरायणः
जपपरायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Devoted to religious meditation, engaged in muttering prayers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जप as above, and परायण adhering or attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपमाला
जपमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A rosary.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and माला a string of beads, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपयज्ञ|जपयज्ञः
जपयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Muttering prayers as a religious rite or sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित्वा
जपित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having repeated inaudibly.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and क्त्वा affix, इट inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जपित
जपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Repeated inaudibly.<BR>E.<BR>जप to mutter prayers, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्त्वा
जप्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having repeated inaudibly.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and क्त्वा affix: see जपित्वा; the omission of इट् is unusual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जप्य|जप्यः
जप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be repeated inaudibly, to be said over repeatedly, (a prayer, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>जप, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जभ्
जभ्<BR>r. 1st cl. (जभति-ते) also (इ) जभि r. 1st cl. (जम्भति-ते)<BR>1 To gape or yawn.<BR>2 To copulate.<BR>r. 10th cl. (जम्भयते)<BR>To destroy, to efface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम
जम<BR>(उ) जमु r. 1st cl. (जमति)<BR>To eat; also चम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्
जम्<BR>ind.<BR>A wife. It is used in composition: see जम्पती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमदग्नि|जमदग्निः
जमदग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A Muni, the father of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जमन|जमनं
जमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>जम to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्पती|जंपती
जम्पती<BR>m. du. (-ती)<BR>Husband and wife.<BR>E.<BR>जं for जाया a wife, and पति a husband: see दम्पती, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बाल|जंबाल|जंबालः|जम्बालः
जम्बाल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Mud, clay.<BR>2 An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria,) &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, बल to move, affix अण्, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बालिनी|जंबालिनी
जम्बालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>जम्बाल mud, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बिर|जम्बिरः
जम्बिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lime: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बीर|जंबीर|जंबीरः|जम्बीरः
जम्बीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Common lime, (Citrus acida); the name seems to be applied to more than one species.<BR>2 A plant, called by some a sort of basil, with small leaves; also जम्भीर, and जम्बिर.<BR>E.<BR>जम to eat, ईरन् affix, and बुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बु|जंबु|जम्बुः
जम्बु<BR>mn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)<BR>1 Jambu Dvīpa, said to be so named from the Jambu tree abounding in it, and implying, according to the Purāṇas, the central division of the world, or the known world: according to the Bauddhas, it is confined to India.<BR>2 A fabulous river, said to flow from the mountain Meru.<BR>f. (-म्बुः)<BR>A fruit tree, the rose apple, (Eugenia OK^1); also applied to every species of Eugenia.<BR>fn. (-म्बुः-म्बु)<BR>The fruit.<BR>E.<BR>जम to eat, बुक् augment, and कु or कू Uṇādi affix; hence it is also written जम्बूः.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुक|जंबुक|जंबुकः|जम्बुकः
जम्बुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A jackall.<BR>2 The deity of water, VARUṆA.<BR>3 A low man.<BR>4 The rose apple.<BR>E.<BR>जम to eat, affix उकच् and वुक् augment, eating flesh, &c. or जम्बु as above, and कन् added; the affix also being ऊकच्, जम्बूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुद्वीप|जंबुद्वीप|जम्बुद्वीपः
जम्बुद्वीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>One of the divisions of the world.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप a continent, added to जम्बु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बुमत्|जम्बुमन्त्
जम्बुमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>1 A monkey.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>f. (-मती)<BR>An Apsarā or heavenly nymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=340" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बू|जंबू
जम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>See जम्बु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूक|जंबूक|जंबूकः|जम्बूकः
जम्बूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>See जम्बुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूल|जंबूल|जम्बूलः
जम्बूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>2 The rose apple.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Jokes addressed to the bridegroom by his female relatives and friends.<BR>E.<BR>जम्बू as above, and ल what gets or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्बूलमालिका
जम्बूलमालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Compliments or jokes addressed to the bride and bridegroom.<BR>E.<BR>जम्बूल, and मालिका a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भ|जंभ|जंभः|जम्भः
जम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 The lime.<BR>3 Food, victuals.<BR>4 The chin.<BR>5 A quiver.<BR>6 A part, a portion.<BR>7 The name of a demon.<BR>E.<BR>जभि to destroy, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भक|जंभक|जम्भकः
जम्भक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Who or what yawns, opens, expands, &c.<BR>2 Who or what kills or destroys.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lime or citron.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Yawning.<BR>E.<BR>जभि to yawn, &c. ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भद्विष्|जंभद्विष्
जम्भद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A demon.<BR>E.<BR>जम्भ a demon, and द्विष् a foe; also similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भभेदिन्|जंभभेदिन्
जम्भभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>जम्भ as above, and भेदिन् destroying: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भर|जंभर|जंभरः|जम्भरः
जम्भर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>see the next, ल being changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भल|जंभलः|जम्भलः
जम्भल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A lime or citron.<BR>2 A Jina or deified Jaina saint.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A female Rākṣasī, the worship of whom is supposed to procure for women procreation.<BR>E.<BR>जभि to destroy, (sickness, sin, &c.) कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भारि|जंभारि|जम्भारिः
जम्भारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>2 Fire or its deity.<BR>3 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>जम्भ the demon, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भिन्|जंभिन्
जम्भिन्<BR>m. (-म्भी)<BR>A lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>जभि to destroy, (disease,) affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जम्भीर|जंभीर|जंभीरः|जम्भीरः
जम्भीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The lime or citron, apparently of more than one species.<BR>2 A plant, considered to be a kind of basil with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>जभि to destroy, (sickness,) ईरन् affix, and नुम् augment; also जम्बीर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय|जयः
जय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Conquest, victory, triumph.<BR>2 A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>3 A proper name, the son of INDRA.<BR>4 One of VIṢṆU'S doorkeepers.<BR>5 The name of a king; also विजयनन्दन.<BR>6 A kind of Mūṅg or bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 One of her female companions.<BR>3 The 3rd, 8th, or 13th lunar day of either half month.<BR>4 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>5 A plant: see जयन्ती.<BR>6 A tree, commonly Ganiyari, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>7 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>8 A banner, a flag.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, affixes अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयकोलाहल|जयकोलाहलः
जयकोलाहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of dice.<BR>2 Shouts of victory.<BR>E.<BR>जय victory, कोलाहल a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयगर्व्व|जयगर्व
जयगर्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>Pride of conquest, exultation.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्|जयन्त्
जयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Conquering, excelling.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयढक्का
जयढक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A large kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and ढक्का a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदत्त|जयदत्तः
जयदत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>The son of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>जय victory, दत्त given, to whom victory is given by his enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयद्रथ|जयद्रथः
जयद्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A chief in the army of DURYODHANA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन|जयनं
जयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Armour for cavalry, elephants, &c.<BR>2 Conquering, subduing.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>INDRA'S daughter.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, affixes ल्युट् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनयुज्
जयनयुज्<BR>mfn. (-युक्)<BR>1 Caparisoned, (as a war horse.)<BR>2 Victorious.<BR>E.<BR>जयन, and युज् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयन्त|जयंत|जयंतः|जयन्तः
जयन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A hero and demigod, the son of INDRA.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 A name of BHĪMA.<BR>(-न्ती)<BR>1 A tree, (Aeschynomene sesban.)<BR>2 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3 The daughter of INDRA.<BR>4 A flag, a banner.<BR>5 A particular combination in astronomy, or the rising of the asterism ROHIṆĪ at midnight, on the 8th of the dark half of Śrāvaṇa, or in fact on the birth day of KṚṢṆA, which is then particularly sacred.<BR>6 Blades of barley planted at the commencement of the Daśaharā, and plucked at its close.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, Uṇādi affix झच्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपत्र|जयपत्रं
जयपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Record of victory or triumph; in law, the sealed and written award of the judge in favour of either party; in historical tradition, the label on the brow of a horse turned loose for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>जय conquest, and पत्र a leaf; also with वन added जयपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपाल|जयपालः
जयपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMA.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A king, a sovereign; (it is also the appellation of several celebrated Hindu princes.)<BR>4 A tree, (Croton tiglium.)<BR>E.<BR>जय victory, पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयध्वनि
जयध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Shout of victory.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयपुत्रक|जयपुत्रकः
जयपुत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयमङ्गल|जयमंगल|जयमङ्गलः
जयमङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The royal elephant.<BR>E.<BR>जय victory, and मङ्गल good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जययज्ञ|जययज्ञः
जययज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>The Aśvamedha or sacrifice of a horse, as a mark of dominion.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवह
जयवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Conferring victory.<BR>2 Victorious.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयवाहिनी
जयवाहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>जय conquest, and वाहिनी who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशब्द|जयशब्दः
जयशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>A shout or song of victory, or the exclamation Jaya Jaya repeated like the Io of the Greeks, as जयजयदेवहरे &c.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयशील
जयशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and शील possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयश्री
जयश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>Victory, glory.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and श्री splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयान्तराय
जयान्तराय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An impediment or hindrance to victory.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and अन्तराय obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयारव
जयारव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Io or song of victory: see जयशब्द.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and आरव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयावह
जयावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Victorious.<BR>2 Conferring victory.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and आवह what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Victorious.<BR>E.<BR>जय victory, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयोद्धुर
जयोद्धुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Victorious, conquering.<BR>E.<BR>जय, and उद्धुर firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Able to conquer, victorious.<BR>E.<BR>जि to subdue, affix यत्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्यता
जय्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Victory, success, ability to conquer.<BR>E.<BR>जय्य, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जय्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरठ|जरठः
जरठ<BR>mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>1 Hard, solid.<BR>2 Hard-hearted, harsh, cruel.<BR>3 Pale, yellowish-white.<BR>4 Old, decayed, infirm. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">Page342</a>]<BR>5 Bent, bowed down, drooping.<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Decrepitude.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to become old or decayed, Uṇādi affix अठ, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=341" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण|जरणं|जरणः
जरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Old, infirm, decayed.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Cuminseed.<BR>2 A plant yielding a pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>3 A sort of salt, (Bit-lobon or Bit-lavaṇa.)<BR>4 Old age, becoming old and infirm.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to become old, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरण्ड|जरंड|जरण्डः
जरण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Old, decayed.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to be old, अण्डच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्|जरन्त्
जरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रती-रत्)<BR>1 Old, ancient, advanced in years.<BR>2 Infirm, decayed.<BR>m. (-रन्)<BR>An old man.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>An old woman.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to be or become old, participial affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारु|जरत्कारुः
जरत्कारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A celebrated Muni or sage so named.<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>The wife of JARATKĀRU, the snake goddess MANASĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जरत् being old, and कारु a maker; a practiser of austerities in old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरत्कारुप्रिया
जरत्कारुप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The goddess MANASĀ, exercising a peculiar power over serpents, as the sister of VĀSUKI, the Nāga.<BR>E.<BR>जरत्कारु as above, and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरद्गव|जरद्गवः
जरद्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An old ox.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>An old cow.<BR>E.<BR>जरत् old, गो a cow, affix टच्, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरन्त|जरंत|जरन्तः
जरन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 An old man.<BR>E.<BR>जृ to be or become old, Uṇādi affix झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरसान|जरसानः
जरसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to grow old, असानच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरा
जरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Decrepitude, the general relaxation and debility consequent upon old age, or old age itself.<BR>2 A tree, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.)<BR>3 A female demon or Rākṣasī.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to grow old, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरातुर|जरातुरः
जरातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Infirm, decrepid, debilitated, old.<BR>E.<BR>जरा infirmity, and आतुर diseased, affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापरिणत
जरापरिणत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stooping, bent down with age or infirmity.<BR>E.<BR>जरा, and परिणत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरापुष्ट|जरापुष्टः
जरापुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A proper name: see जरासन्ध.<BR>E.<BR>जरा a female Rākṣasī, and पुष्ट fostered; assisted at his birth by a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जराभीरु|जराभीरुः
जराभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>Love or the deity KĀMA^1.<BR>E.<BR>जरा decrepitude, and भीरु formidable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260619. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायणि|जरायणिः
जरायणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sovereign JARĀSANDHA.<BR>E.<BR>जरा the Rākṣasī, फिञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायु|जरायुः
जरायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The womb, the uterus.<BR>E.<BR>जरा infirmity, इण् to obtain, Uṇādi affix उण्; also with a final स, जरायुस्. m. (-युः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरायुज|जरायुजः
जरायुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Viviparous, born from the womb, as man and other animals.<BR>E.<BR>जरायु the womb, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासन्ध|जरासंध|जरासन्धः
जरासन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A proper name, a celebrated king and warrior, sovereign of Magadha, father-in-law to KAṂSA, and foe to KṚṢṆA; he was slain in single combat by BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>जरा a female demon, and सन्ध connection, union; he was born in two halves, which were put together by the Rākṣasī JARĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरासन्धजित्|जरासंधजित्
जरासन्धजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>BHĪMASENA, the third of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>जरासन्ध, and जित् conqueror: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरिन्
जरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>2 Infirm, decayed.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An old man.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to become old, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जरुथ
जरुथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Skinniness, flesh flaccid with old age.<BR>E.<BR>ज to become old, उथन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च|जर्च्च
जर्च<BR>r. 6th cl. (जर्चति)<BR>1 To say, to speak.<BR>2 To reprove, to abuse or blame.<BR>3 To threaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्च्छ
जर्च्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (जर्च्छति)<BR>To say, to blame: see जर्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज|जर्ज्ज
जर्ज<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (जर्जति)<BR>1 To say.<BR>2 To blame, to reprove.<BR>3 To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जर|जर्ज्जरः
जर्जर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Old, infirm.<BR>2 Split, broken.<BR>3 Wounded, hurt.<BR>4 Divided in parts or pieces.<BR>5 Perforated.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 INDRA'S banner or emblem.<BR>2 Benzoin.<BR>3 An aquatic plant, (Utricularia fasciculata.)<BR>E.<BR>जर्ज to hurt, and अर affix; or जॄ to grow old, affix अच्, the radical repeated, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्जरीक|जर्ज्जरीकः
जर्जरीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Ragged, perforated, full of holes.<BR>2 Old, decayed.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ज्जरीकृत|जर्जरीकृत
जर्ज्जरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wounded, disabled.<BR>E.<BR>जर्जर, and कृत made, च्चि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्झ
जर्झ<BR>r. 6th cl. (जर्झति)<BR>1 To say or speak.<BR>2 To blame.<BR>3 To threaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्ण|जर्णः
जर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Old, decayed.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to grow old, न Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्तिल|जर्तिल|जर्तिलः|जर्त्तिलः
जर्त्तिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sesamum growing wild.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be produced, and तिल sesamum, deriv. irr.; also read जर्हिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्तु|जर्तु|जर्तुः|जर्त्तुः
जर्त्तु<BR>m. (-र्त्तुः)<BR>1 The vulva.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, तु Uṇādi affix, and र inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्हिल|जर्हिलः
जर्हिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Wild sesamum: see जर्त्तिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जर्त्स
जर्त्स<BR>r. 6th cl. (जर्त्सति)<BR>1 To say or speak.<BR>2 To blame, to censure, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल<BR>r. 1st cl. (जलति)<BR>1 To be sharp.<BR>2 To be wealthy.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (जलति जालयति)<BR>To cover, to hide or veil; to cover also as with a net, to encompass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल|जलं|जलः
जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Cold, stupid, apathetic, idiotic, &c.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A kind of perfume: see ह्रीवेर.<BR>3 The uterus of a cow.<BR>4 Frigidity, (moral, mental, or physical.)<BR>E.<BR>जल to hide, to encompass, &c. affix अच्; also ल being changed to its congener ड, जड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक|जलकं
जलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A conch, a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकण्टक|जलकंटक|जलकण्टकः
जलकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>2 A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकपि|जलकपिः
जलकपि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>The gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and कपि an ape, the water-ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकर|जलकरः
जलकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Making or shedding water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rent or tax derived from water, for fisheries, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and कर tax or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकरङ्क|जलकरंक|जलकरङ्कः
जलकरङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A cocoanut.<BR>2 A shell or conch.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 A wave.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and करङ्क a cup or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकल्क|जलकल्कः
जलकल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>Mud, mire.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and कल्क sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाक|जलकाकः
जलकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The diver.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and काक a crow; the water-crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाङ्क्ष|जलकांक्ष|जलकाङ्क्षः
जलकाङ्क्ष<BR>m. (-ङ्क्षः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and काङ्क्ष desirous, from काक्षि with अच् affix; also with इनि affix, ut infra^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकाङ्क्षिन्|जलकांक्षिन्
जलकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिनी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>Desirous of water, fond of water.<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and काङ्क्षिन् wishing: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकान्तार|जलकांतार|जलकान्तारः
जलकान्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>जलकान्त the water-gem, the ocean, and अर who goes or rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=342" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकिराट|जलकिराटः
जलकिराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A shark, or according to some, a large alligator.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, किर a hog, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुक्कुटी
जलकुक्कुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>The black-headed gull: see गङ्गाचिल्ली.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and कुक्कुटी a fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुक्कुभ|जलकुक्कुभः
जलकुक्कुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A sort of aquatic bird.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and कुक्कुभ a wild fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुन्तल|जलकुंतल|जलकुन्तलः
जलकुन्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकुब्जक
जलकुब्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, कुब्ज to be crooked, affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकूपी
जलकूपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>1 A whirlpool.<BR>2 A pond, a pool.<BR>3 A spring, a well.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, कूप a well, ङीष् affix of diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकूर्म्म|जलकूर्म|जलकूर्मः|जलकूर्म्मः
जलकूर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and कूर्म्म a tortoise, a water tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक्रिया
जलक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A funeral ceremony, presenting water to the manes of the deceased.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and क्रिया ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलकेश|जलकेशः
जलकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and केश hair; spreading over the water like dishevelled hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलक्रीडा
जलक्रीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Sporting or gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure or amusement.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and क्रीडा pastime, play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलगुल्म|जलगुल्मः
जलगुल्म<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>1 A whirlpool.<BR>2 A turtle, a tortoise.<BR>2 A piece of water, a lake.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and गुल्म a lump like the spleen, or a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलङ्ग|जलंग|जलङ्गः
जलङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Aquatic, frequenting or going to water.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The colocynth.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलङ्गम|जलंगम|जलङ्गमः
जलङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Caṇḍāla, an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and गम who goes; who goes to fish for his subsistence; also जनङ्गम q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलचर|जलचरः
जलचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Aquativ, amphibious, going in or into water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलचारिन्
जलचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Aquatic, living in or frequenting water.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and चर to go, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलज|जलजं|जलजः
जलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Water-born, aquatic.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 Any aquatic animal.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A shell.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A plant; said to be a sort of bassia growing in or near water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्तु|जलजंतु|जलजन्तुः
जलजन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A fish, or any marine, aquatic, or amphibious animal.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and जन्तु animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्तुका|जलजंतुका
जलजन्तुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>कन्, and टाप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजन्मन्
जलजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलजिह्व|जलजिह्वः
जलजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>जल cold, and जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलडिम्ब|जलडिम्बः
जलडिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and डिम्ब a young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलतरङ्ग|जलतरंग|जलतरङ्गः
जलतरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A wave.<BR>2 A metal cup with water, so as to produce a harmonic note like a musical glass.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and तरङ्ग a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलतापिक|जलतापिकः
जलतापिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Hilsa or sable fish, (Clupanodon ilisha, HAM.)<BR>2 Another kind of fish, commonly Caöuchi, (Cyprinus cachius, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, तप to inflame, ठक affix; also with णिनि affix जलतापिन् m. (-पी) The Hilsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलताल|जलतालः
जलताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Ilīśa or Hilsa fish: see the last<BR>E.<BR>जल water, तल to abide, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलत्रा
जलत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>An umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>जल rain, and त्रा defending, from त्रै, with ड and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलद|जलदः
जलद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Giving or shedding water.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदपङ्क्ति
जलदपङ्क्ति<BR>f. (-ङ्क्तिः)<BR>A line or succession of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>जलद, and पङ्क्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदसंहति
जलदसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Cloudiness, gathering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>जलद, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदागम|जलदागमः
जलदागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>जलद, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदान
जलदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदाभ
जलदाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Dark, black.<BR>E.<BR>जलद a cloud, and आभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलदाशन|जलदाशनः
जलदाशन<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>जलद a cloud, and अशन imbibing, from अश to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधर|जलधरः
जलधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Holding or having water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 A grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and धर containing, possessing, from धृ with अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधरमाला
जलधरमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A row of clouds.<BR>2 A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>जलधर, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधि|जलधिः
जलधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A large number, (a hundred lacs of crores).<BR>E.<BR>जल water, धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधिगा
जलधिगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>जलधि the sea, गा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलधिजा
जलधिजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>जलधि, and जा produced, the ocean-born; appearing at the churning of the ocean, amongst the fourteen precious things recovered from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनकुल|जलनकुलः
जलनकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and नकुल an ichneumon; the water-ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिधि|जलनिधिः
जलनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and निधि a nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिर्गम|जलनिर्गमः
जलनिर्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A drain, a water-course, a pipe along a wall or building for carrying off water, a waterfall, the descent of a spring, &c. into a river below.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, निर्गम transit or passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनिवह
जलनिवह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A quantity of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and निवह a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलनीली
जलनीली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Vallisneria.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and नीली a blue dye or indigo; imparting its own tinge to the stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलन्धर|जलंधर|जलन्धरः
जलन्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An Asura sprung from ŚIVA, and adopted by the ocean.<BR>E.<BR>जलं, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपटल
जलपटल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A quantity of water.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and पटल a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपति|जलपतिः
जलपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 VARUṆA, the deity presiding over the watery element, the Hindu Neptune.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and पति lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपात्र
जलपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A drinking vessel.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and पात्र vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपान
जलपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Drinking water: in Bengal, refreshment, luncheon.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपित्त|जलपित्तं
जलपित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and पित्त bile; being as adust to water as bile is to the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपिप्पली
जलपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia, &c.) see जलभू.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and पिप्पली long-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलपृष्ठजा
जलपृष्ठजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, पृष्ठ back or surface, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=343" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्राय|जलप्रायं
जलप्राय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A country abounding with water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and प्राय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्रिय|जलप्रियः
जलप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fond of water, frequenting water.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>2 A fish.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्लव|जलप्लवः
जलप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and प्लव who goes or swims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलप्लावन
जलप्लावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An inundation, a deluge.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and प्लावन overflowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबन्धक|जलबन्धकः
जलबन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dam, a dike, rocks or stones impeding a current.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and बन्धक confining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबन्धु|जलबंधु|जलबन्धुः
जलबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलबुद्वुद
जलबुद्वुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A bubble of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and बुद्वुद a bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलब्रह्मी
जलब्रह्मी<BR>f. (-ह्मी)<BR>A kind of potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ब्रह्मी an asclepias.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलभू
जलभू<BR>mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु)<BR>Aquatic, produced in or by water.<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia or bengalensis): see कञ्चट.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and भू being or born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमक्षिका
जलमक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A water insect.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमद्गु|जलमद्गुः
जलमद्गु<BR>m. (-द्गुः)<BR>A kingfisher.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मद्गु another bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमसि|जलमसिः
जलमसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मसि ink; composed as it were of ink and water, alluding to its dark colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमार्ग|जलमार्गः
जलमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A drain or issue from a pond, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and मार्ग a road, a watercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमार्जार|जलमार्जारः|जलमार्ज्जार
जलमार्जार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and मार्ज्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमुच्
जलमुच्<BR>m. (-मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मुच् from मुच् to set free, affix क्विप्, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमूर्त्ति|जलमूर्ति|जलमूर्तिः|जलमूर्त्तिः
जलमूर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मूर्त्ति form; of whom one form is water; implying his omnipresence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमूर्त्तिका|जलमूर्तिका
जलमूर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मूर्त्ति form, with कन् added; a form or condition of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलमोद|जलमोदं
जलमोद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and मोद what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलम्बल
जलम्बल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A stream.<BR>2 Collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्र|जलयंत्र
जलयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A waterwork, a machine for raising water, &c., any contrivance connected with that element.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and यन्त्र a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलयन्त्रगृह|जलयंत्रगृह
जलयन्त्रगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A house or fabric erected in the midst of water, or subterraneous apartments constructed in the bank of a river, for retiring to in the hot season; a summer house, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जलयन्त्र a waterwork, and गृह a house; also similar compounds, as जलयत्त्रनिकेतन, जलयन्त्रमन्दिरं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरङ्क|जलरङ्कः
जलरङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and रङ्क miserly, greedy of water; feeding on small fish chiefly, and therefore haunting swamps, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरङ्कु|जलरंकु|जलरङ्कुः
जलरङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and रङ्कु a sort of deer; the water-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरञ्ज|जलरञ्जः
जलरञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>The Vaka, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, रजि to be fond of, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरण्ड|जलरंड|जलरण्डः
जलरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A whirlpool.<BR>2 A drop or a thin sprinkling of water.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and लडि to tremble, to play, &c. affix अच, and ल becomes र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरस|जलरसः
जलरस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Salt.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and रस taste, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलराशि|जलराशिः
जलराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>A piece of water, a quantity of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरुह्
जलरुह्<BR>m. (-रुट्)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, रुह to mount, affix क्विप्; also with क affix, जलरुह n. (-हं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलरूप|जलरूपः
जलरूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The fish of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जललता
जललता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A wave, a billow.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवरण्ट|जलवरण्टः
जलवरण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A watery pustule, a sort of watery pox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवल्कल|जलवल्कलः
जलवल्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and वल्कक bark, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवायस|जलवायसः
जलवायस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bird, the diver.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and वायस a crow, the water-crow; also जलकाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवालक|जलवालकः
जलवालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Vindhya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, वाड to dive, and ण्वुल् affix; ड changed to ल; alluding to the many streams that rise in this range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवालिका
जलवालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and वालिका offspring, engendered at the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवाह|जलवाहः
जलवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A water carrier.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and वह to bear, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवाहन|जलवाहनः
जलवाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flowing of water.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A watercourse, an aqueduct.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and वाहन bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविडाल|जलविडालः
जलविडाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and विडाल a cat; the water-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविन्दु
जलविन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविल्व|जलविल्वः
जलविल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>1 A crab.<BR>2 A tortoise.<BR>3 A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and विल्व a particular tree and fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलविषुव|जलविषुवं
जलविषुव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The autumnal equinox, the moment of the sun's entering Libra.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and विषुव equinox; the watery equinox, occurring near the close of the annual rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलवृश्चिक|जलवृश्चिकः
जलवृश्चिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A prawn or shrimp.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, वृश्चिक a scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलव्यध|जलव्यधः
जलव्यध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A kind of fish, (Esox cancila, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and व्यध to pierce, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलव्याल|जलव्यालः
जलव्याल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A water-snake.<BR>2 A marine monster.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and व्याल a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशय|जलशयः
जलशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and शय who sleeps; he is supposed to sleep, borne by his serpent couch above the ocean, during the four months of the periodical rains in India; also during the intervals of the submersion of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशयन|जलशयनः
जलशयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, शि to sleep, affix ल्यु, see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशायिन्
जलशायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शायिन् who sleeps: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशुक्ति|जलशुक्तिः
जलशुक्ति<BR>m. (-क्तिः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शुक्ति an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशुचि
जलशुचि<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>Bathed, washed.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शुचि cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशूक|जलशूकं
जलशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Vallisneria.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शूक the beard of corn, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलशूकर|जलशूकरः
जलशूकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शूकर a hog, the water-hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसंसर्ग
जलसंसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Mixture with water, dilution.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and संसग combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=344" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसर्पिणी
जलसर्पिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, सृप to go or creep, affix णिनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलसूचि|जलसूचिः
जलसूचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>1 A fish, a small sort of pike, (Esox cancila, HAM.)<BR>2 The gangetic porpoise.<BR>3 A heron.<BR>4 An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and सूचि a needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलस्थ
जलस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Being or abiding in water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलह|जलहं
जलह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A small water (or summer) house.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and हा to quit, affix डः see जलयन्त्रगृह, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलहास|जलहासः
जलहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone, considered as the indurated foam of the sea; also जलहासक.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and हास laugh, smile; alluding to its white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाकर|जलाकरः
जलाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A piece of water, a spring, a fountain.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाका
जलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अक to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाक्षी
जलाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अक्ष the eye, affix ङीष्: see जलपिप्पली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाखु|जलाखुः
जलाखु<BR>m. (-खुः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आखु a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाञ्चल|जलांचल|जलाञ्चलं
जलाञ्चल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A natural water-course or channel.<BR>2 A plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अञ्चल end of a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाञ्जलि|जलांजलि|जलाञ्जलिः
जलाञ्जलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A handful of water, or water held in the palms of the hand, as presented in oblation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अञ्जलि salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाटन|जलाटनः
जलाटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A heron.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, अट to go, affixes ल्युट् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाढ्य
जलाढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>Watery, marshy.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आद्य rich, abounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाण्टक|जलांटक|जलाण्टकः
जलाण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shark, or according to some a large alligator, &c.: see ग्राह.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, अटि to go, क्वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाण्डक|जलाण्डकं
जलाण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Small fry.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, अण्ड an egg, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलात्मिका
जलात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A leech.<BR>2 A well.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आत्मा being, existence, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलादर्श
जलादर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Water reflecting any object, a watery mirror.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आदर्श a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाधार|जलाधारः
जलाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pond, a lake, a reservoir, any piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आधार a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाधिदैवत|जलाधिदैवतः
जलाधिदैवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The asterism Pūrvāṣāḍhā.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, अधि over, and दैवत divinity; the possessor of divine supremacy over the element of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलानुसार
जलानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Going or acting like water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अनुसार agreeing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाभिषेक
जलाभिषेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sprinkling with water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अभिषेक aspersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाम्बिका|जलांबिका
जलाम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A well.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अम्बिका a mother; bearing water as it were in its womb: the word is sometimes read जलात्मिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलायुका
जलायुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, अय to go, उकच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्णव|जलार्णवः
जलार्णव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The rainy season.<BR>2 The sea of fresh water.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and अर्णव a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्थिन्
जलार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिणी-र्थि)<BR>Thirsty, desirous of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and अर्थिन् desirous of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलार्द्र|जलार्द्रः
जलार्द्र<BR>mfn. subst. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं)<BR>Wet cloth or clothes.<BR>adj.<BR>Wet, charged with aqueous moisture.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and आर्द्र damp, moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालुका
जलालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, आलुच् affix, and कन् added; also जलायुका and जलालोका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलालोका
जलालोका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, आलोकृ to look or see, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलावर्त्त|जलावर्त|जलावर्तः|जलावर्त्तः
जलावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and आवर्त्त turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाविल
जलाविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Stained or spotted with water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आविल muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलावुका
जलावुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाशय|जलाशयं|जलाशयः
जलाशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Stupid, dull, cold, apathetic.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A pond, a tank, a lake, a reservoir or any piece of water.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and आशय an abode or receptacle, or जल for जड cold, and आशय disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाशायिन्
जलाशायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Lying or sleeping in water as a penance.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and शी to sleep or lie, with आङ् prefixed, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाश्रय|जलाश्रयः
जलाश्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A piece of water, a pond, a lake.<BR>2 A water-house.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आश्रय refuge, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाष्ठीला
जलाष्ठीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A large square pond.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, स्था to abide, with आङ् prefixed, and अच् and ङीष् affixs. जलाष्ठी and लच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाह्वय|जलाह्वयं
जलाह्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलिका
जलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and ठक् affix: see जलौका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलुका
जलुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जस to set free, (blood,) उक or ऊक Uṇādi affix, and स changed to ल; hence also, जलूका f. (-का) also जलौका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेचर|जलेचरः
जलेचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Aquatic, living in or frequenting water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 Any kind of water fowl.<BR>E.<BR>जले in water, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेच्छया
जलेच्छया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेजात|जलेजातं
जलेजात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>जले the seventh case, in water, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेन्द्र|जलेंद्र|जलेन्द्रः
जलेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>2 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>3 The ocean of fresh water.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and इन्द्र a ruler or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेन्धन|जलेंधन|जलेन्धनः
जलेन्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and इन्धन् inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेवाह|जलेवाहः
जलेवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A diver, (by caste or business.)<BR>E.<BR>जले, and वाह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेशय|जलेशयः
जलेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>जले in the seventh case, in water, and शय who sleeps or abides, from शीङ्^1 to sleep, affix घ.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेश्वर|जलेश्वरः
जलेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of the deity of water, VARUṆA.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोका
जलोका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, and ओक a house; also जलौका, जलौकस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोकिका
जलोकिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोच्छ्वास|जलोच्छ्वासः
जलोच्छ्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A drain or channel, made on purpose for carrying off an excess of water, or such a channel made naturally by the overflow of a river, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, उत् up, and श्वास breath, breathing forth or expiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=345" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोदर|जलोदरं
जलोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Dropsy.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोद्भव
जलोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Aquatic, marine, born of or in water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोरगी
जलोरगी<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल water, उरग a snake, diminutive affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौकस्
जलौकस्<BR>f. (-काः)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ओकस् house; also जलौकस with a final vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौकस|जलौकसः
जलौकस<BR>mfn. sub. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>as before: see जलौकस्, अच् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौका
जलौका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding; also जलोका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलौघ
जलौघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A quantity of water.<BR>E.<BR>जल, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प<BR>r. 1st cl. (जल्पति)<BR>1 To speak articulately, to say or tell.<BR>2 To prattle, to talk much or idly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प|जल्पः
जल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 Dissention, wrangling.<BR>2 Prate, babble.<BR>3 (In Logic,) Refutation of an adversary's arguments, and assertion of one's own.<BR>E.<BR>जल्प to speak, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पक
जल्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A chatterer, one who talks much or idly.<BR>E.<BR>जल्प to prate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पन|जल्पनं
जल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Talking, saying.<BR>2 Chattering, prattling.<BR>E.<BR>जल्प, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पाक|जल्पाकः
जल्पाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>A chatterer, talking much and foolishly, or improperly.<BR>E.<BR>जल्प to talk idly, षाकन् affix; also जल्पक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पित|जल्पितं
जल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, told, spoken.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Talking, babbling, gossiping.<BR>E.<BR>जल्प to talk, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव<BR>(इ) जवि r. 10th. cl. (जंवयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Swift, quick, expeditious.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 A runner, an express.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The China rose, (Hibiscus rosa sinensis); also जपा.<BR>E.<BR>जु to move quickly, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
जवन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>Quick, fleet.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A courser, a fleet horse.<BR>2 A country, Ionia or Greece: see यवन.<BR>3 A native of that country.<BR>4 A sort of deer.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Speed, velocity.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A screen surrounding a tent, a Kenāt.<BR>2 A drug.<BR>E.<BR>जु to be quick, affix ल्युट् or युच्, and fem. ङीष् or टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनाल|जवनालं
जवनाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of grain, (Andropogon bicolor): see यवनाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिका
जवनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A wall or screen of cloth surrounding a tent, an outer tent, &c.<BR>2 A curtain, a screen in general.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to जवनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस|जवसं|जवसः
जवस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Meadow or pasture grass.<BR>E.<BR>जु to grow quick, असच् affix: see यवस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवादि
जवादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>A perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवाधिक|जवाधिकः
जवाधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Very quick.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fleet horse, a courser.<BR>E.<BR>जव speed, and अधिक exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवानिल|जवानिलः
जवानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gale, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>जव fleet, अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवापुष्प|जवापुष्पं
जवापुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The China rose, the plant or its flower.<BR>E.<BR>जवा as above, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन्
जविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Quick or fleet, expeditious.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>जव speed, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष
जष<BR>r. 1st cl. (जषति)<BR>To kill, to wound, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस
जस<BR>(इर उ) इर् जसु r. 4th cl. (जस्यति)<BR>To liberate, to set free, to let loose.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (जसति जासयति)<BR>1 To kill or injure.<BR>2 To slight or disregard, to treat irreverently.<BR>3 To strike, to punish with blows.<BR>(इ) जसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (जंसति जंसयति)<BR>To preserve, to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुरि|जसुरिः
जसुरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>जस to kill or hurt, Uṇādi affix उरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहक|जहकः
जहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Abandoning, who leaves or abandons.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A child.<BR>3 The slough of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, or abandon, कन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्
जहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Leaving, quitting, foregoing.<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्स्वार्था
जहत्स्वार्था<BR>f. (-र्था)<BR>The use of a word in a sense different from its ordinary one.<BR>E.<BR>जहत्, and स्वार्थ own meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहा
जहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī; also कदम्बपुष्पी, &c.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon ड, affixes and टाप्; shedding its leaves in spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहानक|जहानकः
जहानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The period of the total destruction of the world.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, शानच् affix, and कन् added; also इ being substituted for the vowel of reduplication, जिहानक as it is sometimes read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नु|जह्नुः
जह्नु<BR>m. (-ह्नुः)<BR>1 The name of a king or saint, son of KURU: see the next.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>हा to abandon, (the world for devotion,) नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नुतनया
जह्नुतनया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>जह्नु, and तनया the daughter; the river in its course disturbed the devotions of the saint JAHNU, upon which he drank up its waters; having released them at the intercession of BHAGĪRATHA, he is thus considered as the parent of the stream: see जाह्नवी; also जह्नुसुता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर|जागरः
जागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Waking, awake.<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>Waking, wakefulness, vigilance, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Mail, armour.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरण|जागरणं
जागरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Waking, watchfulness.<BR>2 Keeping watch, sitting up at night as part of a religious ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to be awake, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरितृ
जागरितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Wakeful, awake, vigilant.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिन्
जागरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wakeful, awake.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरूक|जागरूकः
जागरूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Wakeful, waking, watchful.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, ऊक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्त्ति|जागर्ति|जागर्तिः|जागर्त्तिः
जागर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Waking, vigilance.<BR>2 Keeping watch.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्य्या|जागर्या
जागर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Wakefulness, waking, watching.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ as above, यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागुड|जागुडं|जागुडः
जागुड<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृ
जागृ<BR>r. 2nd cl. (जागर्त्ति)<BR>To wake, to be awake or watchful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृवि|जागृविः
जागृवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, Uṇādi affix क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रत्
जाग्रत्<BR>mfn. (-ग्रन्-ग्रती-ग्रत्)<BR>Watching, being awake.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, Uṇādi affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रिया
जाग्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Waking, watching.<BR>E.<BR>जागृ to wake, यत् affix, ऋ changed to its congener रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गल|जांगल|जाङ्गलं|जाङ्गलः
जाङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>1 Rural, picturesque, diversified with hill, vale, wood, and water, (country.)<BR>2 Wild, jaṅgala, barbarous, savage.<BR>3 Wild, (not tame, as an animal, &c.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Game, the flesh of deer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गल a wilderness, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=346" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गलि|जांगलिः|जाङ्गलिः
जाङ्गलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A snake-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गल a wilderness, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुल|जांगुल|जांगुलं|जाङ्गुलं
जाङ्गुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Poison, venom.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Knowledge of poisons, the possession of charms or drugs, and employment of them as antidotes.<BR>2 A potherb, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गुल poison, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलि|जांगुलि|जांगुलिः|जाङ्गुलिः
जाङ्गुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A snake-catcher, a dealer in antidotes.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गुल, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्गुलिक|जांगुलिक|जांगुलिकः|जाङ्गुलिकः
जाङ्गुलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake-catcher, a snake doctor, one who pretends, chiefly by charms, to cure the bite of snakes or other venomous animals, a dealer in antidotes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्गुल poison, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घनी
जाङ्घनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The thigh.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्घा the leg, affixes अण् and ङीष्, नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाङ्घिक|जांघिक|जाङ्घिकः
जाङ्घिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the leg.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A courier, a running footman, an express.<BR>2 A camel.<BR>E.<BR>जङ्घा a leg, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजिन्
जाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A warrior, a combatant.<BR>E.<BR>जज to fight, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाज्वल्यमान|जाज्वल्यमानः
जाज्वल्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shining, flaming, blazing.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to burn, intensitive form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाटलि|जाटलिः
जाटलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia suave-olens); a various reading for पाटलि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्य|जाड्यं
जाड्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>1 Coldness, apathy.<BR>2 Folly, stupidity, dulness or coldness of intellect.<BR>3 Coldness, frigidity.<BR>E.<BR>जड cold, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, engendered.<BR>2 A child, offspring.<BR>3 Apparent, manifest.<BR>4 Produced, caused, occasioned.<BR>5 Felt, entertained.<BR>6 Inspired with, affected by.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Kind, sort, class, species.<BR>2 Multitude, collection.<BR>3 Individuality, specific condition.<BR>4 Birth, production.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Born.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mendicant.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Astrological calculation of a nativity.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकध्वनि|जातकध्वनिः
जातकध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातकर्म्म
जातकर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>1 A ceremony performed, when the navel string is divided, touching the infant's tongue thrice with ghee, with appropriate prayers, &c.<BR>2 Delivery, &c. of a new-born infant.<BR>E.<BR>जात born, and कर्म्म rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातदन्त
जातदन्त<BR>mf. (-न्तः-न्ती)<BR>A child that has got a tooth.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातप्रत्यय
जातप्रत्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Confiding, believing, inspired with confidence.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and प्रत्यय trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमर्ष
जातमर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Enraged, vexed, angry.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and मष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातमात्र
जातमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>What is just born, or merely born<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>As soon as born, the instant of birth.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातरूप|जातरूपं
जातरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Embodied, assuming shape or form<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>जात produced, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातवेदस्
जातवेदस्<BR>m. (-दाः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>जात born, वेद a Veda, असि Uṇādi affix; or जात kind, sort, and विद to know, or comprehend, affix as before: one legend makes the Vedas to have issued from the mouth of AGNI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातश्रम
जातश्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Wearied, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातस्पृह
जातस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Desirous, wishing for.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and स्पृहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातहार्द्द|जातहार्द
जातहार्द्द<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दः-र्द्दी-र्द्दं)<BR>Becoming attached to or fond of.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and हार्द्द affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातागस्
जातागस्<BR>mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः)<BR>Offending, sinning, committing any fault.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and आगस् sin; also जातापराध, जातदोष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातापत्या
जातापत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A mother, a woman who has borne a child.<BR>E.<BR>जात born, (by whom,) अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाताश्रु
जाताश्रु<BR>mfn. (-श्रुः-श्रुः-श्रु)<BR>Weeping, shedding tears.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and अश्रु a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाति|जातिः
जाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Kind, sort, species, class, tribe.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Lineage, race, family.<BR>4 A fire place, a chimney.<BR>5 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>6 A plant: see काम्पिल्ल.<BR>7 A kind of poetical metre.<BR>8 A rhetorical ornament.<BR>9 (In Arithmetic,) Assimilation, as विशेषजाति assimilation of the difference, शेषजाति of the remainder.<BR>10 Proximate cause or occurrence of disease, &c.<BR>f. (-तिः or -ती)<BR>1 Great flowered jasmin, (J. grandiflorum.)<BR>2 Mace, nutmeg.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The flower of the jasmin.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, affix क्तिच्, and occasionally ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिकोश|जातिकोशं|जातिकोशः
जातिकोश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Nutmeg.<BR>E.<BR>जाति or जाती mace, and कोश or कोष sheathe; hence also जातिकोष, जातीकोश or जातीकोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातित्व
जातित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Distinction or nature of caste or tribe.<BR>2 Special or generic property.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to जाति; also with तल्, जातिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिधर्म्म|जातिधर्म|जातिधर्मः
जातिधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 The duty of caste, as sacred study of the Brahman, battle of the Kṣatriya, &c.<BR>2 Generic or specific property.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिफल|जातिफलं
जातिफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Nutmeg.<BR>E.<BR>जाति or जाती mace, and फल fruit; also जातीफल; also जातिकोष, जाति or जाती, and जातिपुष्पं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंश|जातिभ्रंशः
जातिभ्रंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Loss of caste.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and भ्रंश injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिभ्रंशकर|जातिभ्रंशकरं
जातिभ्रंशकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Forbidden, improper, causing loss of caste.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Doing any act prohibited to a particular caste.<BR>E.<BR>जातिभ्रंश, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमात्र
जातिमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Species, genus.<BR>2 Caste only, not the performance of its especial duties.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिलक्षण
जातिलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Specific or generic distinction or characteristic.<BR>2 Mark of tribe or caste.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैर|जातिवैरं
जातिवैर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Innate or instinctive hostility.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and वैर enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिवैलक्षण्य
जातिवैलक्षण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Inconsistency, incompatibility, conduct or quality at variance with tribe or species.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and वैलक्षण्य inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्वभाव|जातिस्वभावः
जातिस्वभाव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>Specific or generic character or nature.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिस्मर
जातिस्मर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>One who recollects his condition in a former life.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and स्मर who remembers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिहीन
जातिहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Outcaste, void of caste.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीपत्री
जातीपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>Mace.<BR>E.<BR>जाती, and पत्री a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=347" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
जातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to any species, belonging to any tribe or order, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीरस|जातीरसं
जातीरस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Gem myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>जाती nutmeg, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Sometimes, occasionally.<BR>2 A particle of prohibition.<BR>3 Of doubt.<BR>4 Of contempt or abuse.<BR>E.<BR>जै to waste or decay, तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुक|जातुकं
जातुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>जतुक the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुधान|जातुधानः
जातुधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>जातु sometimes, धान possessing, from धा with ल्युट् or युच्; otherwise यातुधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Made, &c. of lac, any artificial form or condition of it.<BR>E.<BR>जतु lac, अण् affix, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातेष्टि|जातेष्टिः
जातेष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Rites performed at birth.<BR>E.<BR>जात, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातोक्ष|जातोक्षः
जातोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A bullock.<BR>E.<BR>जात born, उक्ष an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Well-born, legitimate, born of parents of the same caste.<BR>2 Best, excellent.<BR>3 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>4 Rectangular.<BR>E.<BR>जाति family, &c. यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्यन्तर
जात्यन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Interval of difference of caste.<BR>E.<BR>जाति, and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्यन्ध|जात्यंध|जात्यन्धः
जात्यन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Born blind.<BR>E.<BR>जाति birth, अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकी
जानकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>जनक the father of this lady. affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानत्
जानत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>Knowing, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानन
जानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Knowing, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, तङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपद|जानपदः
जानपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Man, mankind.<BR>2 An inhabited country.<BR>E.<BR>जनपद the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The knee.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be produced, (walking, motion,) ञुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुफलक
जानुफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The knee pan or patella.<BR>E.<BR>जानु, and फलक a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानुसन्धि|जानुसंधि|जानुसन्धिः
जानुसन्धि<BR>f. (-न्धिः)<BR>The knee joint.<BR>E.<BR>जानु, and सन्धि articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप|जापः
जाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Muttering prayers or beads, reciting passages of the Vedas, &c. inaudibly.<BR>E.<BR>जप to mutter, &c. affix घञ्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Muttering prayers, one who does so.<BR>E.<BR>जप, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापन|जापनं
जापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Declining, rejection, dissent.<BR>2 Dismissing, completing, finishing.<BR>E.<BR>जप to speak, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्य
जाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be muttered, &c.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>The muttering of prayers, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबाल|जाबालः
जाबाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A goatherd.<BR>2 The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>अजा a goat, and पाल who cherishes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालि|जाबालिः
जाबालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The name of a Muni, one of the original teachers of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>जवल, and इञ् patronymic affix; also with अण्, जाबाल as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्य|जामदग्न्यः
जामदग्न्य<BR>m. (-ग्न्यः)<BR>A name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>जमदग्नि a Muni so named, and यञ् patronymick affix; the son of the saint JAMADAGNI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A daughter's husband, a son-in-law.<BR>2 A husband, a lord or master.<BR>3 A friend.<BR>4 The sunflower, (Helianthus annuus.)<BR>E.<BR>जा for जाया a wife, मा to take, तृच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि<BR>f. (-मिः or मी)<BR>1 A virtuous and respectable woman.<BR>2 A sister, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जै to decline or decay, affix मि; or जम to eat, affix अण्, ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेय|जामेयः
जामेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sister's son.<BR>E.<BR>जामि a sister, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बव|जांबव|जांबवं|जाम्बवं
जाम्बव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The rose apple, the fruit.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>जम्बु the tree, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बवौष्ठ
जाम्बवौष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A cauterising needle or probe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बबत्
जाम्बबत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A fabulous bear, father-in-law to KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>जाम्ब the Jambu tree, and मतुप् affix; also जाम्बुवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनद|जांबूनद|जांबूनदं|जाम्बूनदं
जाम्बूनद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>जम्बुनदी a river flowing from mount Sumeru, the Indian Pactolus, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाम्बूनदमय
जाम्बूनदमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Golden, made of gold.<BR>E.<BR>जाम्बूनद and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायक|जायकं
जायक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>E.<BR>जि to excel (all perfumes), and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायमान
जायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being born, coming into life.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A wife, one wedded according to the perfect ritual.<BR>E.<BR>जन to be born, affix यक्; in whom a man is again born, that is to say, he is re-born in his children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाघ्न|जायाघ्नः
जायाघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 A murderer of his wife.<BR>2 A mole or mark on the body, indicative of the death of a wife.<BR>E.<BR>जाया, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायाजीव|जायाजीवः
जायाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An actor, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>जाया a wife, and जीव who gets a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायात्व
जायात्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The character or attributes of a wife.<BR>E.<BR>जाया, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायानुजीविन्
जायानुजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 An actor, a dancer, a mine, &c.<BR>2 A kind of crane, the Vaka (Ardea nivea.)<BR>3 A needy man, a pauper.<BR>4 The husband of a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>जाया a wife, अनु like or with, and जीविन् who gets a livelihood; who is supported by his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायापती
जायापती<BR>m. du. (-ती)<BR>Husband and wife.<BR>E.<BR>जाया a wife, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायु|जायुः
जायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A medicine, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>जि to subdue, (disease,) Uṇādi affix उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जार|जारः
जार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A paramour, a gallant.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to grow infirm, घञ् affix of agency, fem. ङीष्; weakening the affection of wives to their husbands, or diminishing the force of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारज|जारजः
जारज<BR>mf. (-जः-जा)<BR>An adulterine, the child of a woman by her gallant.<BR>E.<BR>जार as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारजात|जारजातः
जारजात<BR>mf. (-तः-ता)<BR>An adulterine.<BR>E.<BR>जार, and जात born; also with कन् added, जारजातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारण|जारणं
जारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Calcining or oxydizing metals.<BR>2 A condiment, a digester.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to decay, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारभरा
जारभरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>An adulteress.<BR>E.<BR>जार, and भरा who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारुत्थ
जारुत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>A sacrifice, thrice worshipping the sun in his southern declination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल|जालं|जालः
जाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A net.<BR>2 A window, a lattice, an eyelet or loophole.<BR>3 A multitude, an assemblage.<BR>4 An unblown flower.<BR>5 Pride, arrogance.<BR>6 Magick, conjuring, illusion, super-natural [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">Page349</a>] deception.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The Kadamba tree.<BR>2 The young fruit of a gourd or cucumber.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A small cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca, Rox.)<BR>2 Any medicament or drug.<BR>E.<BR>जल to encompass, to hide or screen, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=348" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालक|जालकं|जालकः
जालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A bud, a germ. An unblown flower.<BR>3 A nest.<BR>4 A net.<BR>5 Pride.<BR>6 A plantain, the fruit.<BR>7 Multitude, assemblage.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A window, a lattice, a loop or eyelethole.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>1 Armour, chain armour.<BR>2 A kind of cloth or raiment, woollen cloth.<BR>3 A leech.<BR>4 A window.<BR>5 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>जाल, and कन् added, or जल to enclose, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकारक|जालकारकः
जालकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 A net-maker.<BR>E.<BR>जाल a net, cobweb, and कारक a fabricator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sheep, an ewe.<BR>E.<BR>जालक woollen cloth, इनि and ङीष् affis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगणिका
जालगणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A churning vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालगर्द्दभ|जालगर्दभ|जालगर्दभः|जालगर्द्दभः
जालगर्द्दभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A dull spreading pimple or boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालन्धर|जालंधर|जालंधरः|जालन्धरः
जालन्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a country situated in the northwest of India, apparently part of Lahore, and perhaps the modern Jallindhar.<BR>m. plu. (-रः)<BR>The inhabitants of Jālandhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालपाद्
जालपाद्<BR>m. (-त् or द्)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>जाल a net, and पाद a foot; web-footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालप्राया
जालप्राया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Armour, iron network, or chain armour.<BR>E.<BR>जाल a net, and प्राय resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालबद्ध
जालबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Caught in a net, snared.<BR>E.<BR>जाल, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिक|जालिकः
जालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 A cheat, a rogue, a vagabond, a conjuror or juggler.<BR>2 One who employs nets, &c. for a livelihood.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 A fisherman.<BR>3 A hunter using nets.<BR>E.<BR>जाल a net, &c. affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिन्
जालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Having a net.<BR>2 Having a window.<BR>3 Illusory, deceptive.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A fisherman.<BR>2 A hunter using nets.<BR>3 A juggler.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A painting room.<BR>E.<BR>जाल a net, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म<BR>mfn. (-ल्मः-ल्मा-ल्मं)<BR>1 Cruel, harsh, severe.<BR>2 Inconsiderate, rash, acting without thinking.<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>A low man, one of a degraded tribe or business.<BR>E.<BR>जल to screen or hide, affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाषक|जाषकं
जाषक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>E.<BR>जष to hurt, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहक|जाहकः
जाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 A pole-cat.<BR>3 A bed, a cot.<BR>4 A leech.<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, affix ण्वुल्; radical initial doubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवी
जाह्नवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>GAṄGĀ or the Ganges personified.<BR>E.<BR>जह्नु a saint, अण् affix of descent, fem. affix ङीष्, the daughter of JAHNU: see जह्नुतनया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि<BR>r. 1st cl. (जयति)<BR>1 To excel, to be pre-eminent, to surpass.<BR>2 To conquer, to reduce or overcome.<BR>With वि or परा prefixed,<BR>(विजयते पराजयते)<BR>To overcome, to conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि<BR>mfn. (-जिः-जिः-जि)<BR>Victorious, conquering, a victor.<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>A demon.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगत्नु|जिगत्नुः
जिगत्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>Breath, life.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, to depart, इत्नुच् Uṇādi affix, and the radical repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषत्
जिगमिषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Wishing or endeavouring to go.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषा
जिगमिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Wish to go or move.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, desider. form अङ्, and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगमिषु
जिगमिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to go.<BR>E.<BR>गम to go, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगरिषु
जिगरिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to take, to lay hold of, to take away.<BR>E.<BR>गृ to seize, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Emulation, wish to excel or overcome.<BR>2 Eminence.<BR>3 Usage, profession or habit of life.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, in the desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Striving to overcome, vieing or contending with.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer; desiderative form, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सत्
जिघत्सत्<BR>mfn. (-त्सन्-त्सन्ती-त्सत्)<BR>Wishing to eat.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सा
जिघत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>अद to eat, in the desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सु|जिघत्सुः
जिघत्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Hungry.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसा
जिघांसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Wish or intention to kill.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसु|जिघांसुः
जिघांसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Mischievous, murderous, seeking to hurt or kill.<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, &c. in the desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसत्
जिघांसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Wishing to kill, murderous, felonious.<BR>E.<BR>हन to kill, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसियस्
जिघांसियस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very desirous or determined to kill.<BR>E.<BR>जिघांस, and इयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षत्
जिघृक्षत्<BR>mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्)<BR>Desirous to take, greedy, avaricious.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, desiderative form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षा
जिघृक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Greediness, covetousness, wish to seize or take.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षु
जिघृक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to seize or take.<BR>E.<BR>ग्रह to take, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्र|जिघ्रः
जिघ्र<BR>mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्रा-घ्रं)<BR>Smelling, who smells.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, श affix, root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्रत्
जिघ्रत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्रन्-घ्रती-घ्रत्)<BR>Smelling.<BR>E.<BR>घ्रा to smell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्गशल्य
जिङ्गशल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa catechu): see जिह्मशल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिङ्घि
जिङ्घि<BR>f. (-ङ्घिः or ङ्घी)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>इङ्ग going, from इगि to go, &c. added to जि to excel, fem. affix ङीष्; excelling all other plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीविषु
जिजीविषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous of life.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिजीषत्
जिजीषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Wishing or striving to overcome, emulous, ambitious, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, desiderative form, -शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञापयिषु
जिज्ञापयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing or seeking to inform.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञः to know, desiderative form of the causal. उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासमान
जिज्ञासमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Inquiring, investigating.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, desiderative form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासा
जिज्ञासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Asking, inquiring.<BR>2 Search, investigation.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, desider. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासित|जिज्ञासितः
जिज्ञासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Asked, inquired, sought.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, desid. form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासु|जिज्ञासुः
जिज्ञासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Inquiring, inquisitive.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=349" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्
जित्<BR>mfn. (-जित्)<BR>Who or what conquers or surpasses.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conquered, subdued, surpassed, overcome.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the attendants upon a Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशि|जितकाशिः
जितकाशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The fist doubled.<BR>E.<BR>जित conquered, काश to shine, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितकाशिन्
जितकाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Victorious.<BR>E.<BR>जित conquered, and काशिन् who shines, from काशृ, with णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितक्रोध|जितक्रोधः
जितक्रोध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of subdued passion, not to be provoked or made angry.<BR>E.<BR>जित, and क्रोध wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितनेमि|जितनेमिः
जितनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A staff made of the wood of the religious fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>जित excelled, (by which,) and नेमि circumference of a wheel, (of any other wood.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितशत्रु|जितशत्रुः
जितशत्रु<BR>mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>The father of AJITA, the 2nd Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>जित, and शत्रु a foe: see other similar compounds, as जितामित्र, जितारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितश्रम
जितश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>One who is free from worldly cares, a stoic^1.<BR>E.<BR>जित, and श्रम fatigue, exertion.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताक्षर|जिताक्षरः
जिताक्षर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Reading well or readily.<BR>E.<BR>जित mastered, and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितात्मन्
जितात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Self-subdued, void of passion.<BR>E.<BR>जित, and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितामित्र|जितामित्रः
जितामित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Triumphing, victorious over an enemy.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>जित subdued, by whom, and अमित्र a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितारि|जितारिः
जितारि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>2 The father of SAMBHAVA, the third of the Jaina pontiffs of this age.<BR>3 A conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>जित conquered, (by whom,) and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिताहव|जिताहवः
जिताहव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>E.<BR>जित conquered, and आहव war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रिय|जितेंद्रिय|जितेन्द्रियः
जितेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Having subdued the senses, calm, unmoved.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An ascetic, a sage, one who has completely subdued his passions.<BR>E.<BR>जित subdued, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितेन्द्रियत्व
जितेन्द्रियत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Continence, subjugation of the senses or passions.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्तम|जित्तमः
जित्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Most victorious, first of the victors.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The constellation, Gemini.<BR>E.<BR>जित, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्य|जित्यः
जित्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Conquerable, vincible.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A ploughshare.<BR>E.<BR>जि to excel, क्यप् affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वर|जित्वरः
जित्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The city of Benares.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, क्वरप् affix, तुक् inserted, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वा
जित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having conquered or excelled.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>(-नः)<BR>1 A Jina, the generic name of the personage peculiar to the Jaina sect, who is ranked by them as superior to the gods of the other sects: a saint and teacher: twenty-four Jinas are supposed to flourish in an Avasarpiṇī or Jaina age, and their writers enumerate those of the ages past, present, and to come.<BR>2 A Buddha; a generic term applied to the chief saints of the Bauddha sect, in the same manner as to those of the Jainas.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A very old man.<BR>5 A sage, one who is omniscient.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, नक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनयोनि|जिनयोनिः
जिनयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>अजिन the skin of a deer, and योनि a place of production; the initial of the first word rejected; also अजिनयोनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनसद्मन्
जिनसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>A Jaina temple.<BR>E.<BR>जिन a Jina, and सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिनेन्द्र|जिनेंद्र|जिनेन्द्रः
जिनेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A Jaina or Jina saint.<BR>E.<BR>जिन a Jaina teacher, and इन्द्र a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम
जिम<BR>(उ) जिमु r. 1st cl. (जेमते)<BR>To eat: see जम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
जिरि<BR>r. 5th cl. but restricted to the Vedas (जिरिणोति)<BR>To injure, wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव
जिव<BR>(इ) जिवि r. 1st cl. (जिम्वति)<BR>1 To please, to delight or charm.<BR>2 To be pleased or charmed.<BR>3 To loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवाजिव|जिवाजिवः
जिवाजिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A pleasant: see जीवंजीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवि
जिवि<BR>r. 5th cl. (जिविनोति)<BR>To seek to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रि|जिव्रिः
जिव्रि<BR>m. (-व्रिः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to decay, Uṇādi affix क्रिन्, and व substituted for the conversion of ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष
जिष<BR>(उ) जिषु r. 1st cl. (जेषति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्णु|जिष्णुः
जिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 An epithet of INDRA.<BR>2 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, कस्रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Going, going to, attaining, obtaining.<BR>2 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>हा to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहानक|जिहानकः
जिहानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The destruction of the world: see जहानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षा
जिहीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Wish to take or seize.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, desiderative form, चङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहीर्षु
जिहीर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>Wishing to take, seizing, carrying off.<BR>E.<BR>हृ to take, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म<BR>mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं)<BR>1 Crooked.<BR>2 Dishonest.<BR>3 Slow, lazy.<BR>m. (-ह्मः)<BR>A tree, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>E.<BR>हा to quit, (a straight line,) मन् Uṇādi affix, and the root reduplicated, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मग|जिह्मगः
जिह्मग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going tortuously or lazily.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्म as above, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मता
जिह्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Crookedness, curvature.<BR>2 Dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>तल added to जिह्म; also with त्व, जिह्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्ममोहन|जिह्ममोहनः
जिह्ममोहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्म slowly, and मोहन copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मशल्य|जिह्मशल्यः
जिह्मशल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>The Khadira, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>जिह्म crooked, शल्य a dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मित
जिह्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bent, bowed, curved.<BR>2 Turned away.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्म, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्व|जिह्वं|जिह्वः
जिह्व<BR>mf. (-हूः-ह्वा)<BR>The tongue.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick, Uṇādi affix वन्, and the initial changed to ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वल|जिह्वलः
जिह्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Greedy.<BR>E.<BR>जिहू the tongue, ल to take, क affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाग्र
जिह्वाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The tip of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वानिर्लेखन|जिह्वानिर्लेखनं
जिह्वानिर्लेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Scraping the tongue.<BR>2 A tongue-scraper.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and निर्लेखन scraping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाप|जिह्वापः
जिह्वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>3 A tiger.<BR>4 The hunting leopard.<BR>5 A bear.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा the tongue, and प who drinks, who laps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामल|जिह्वामलं
जिह्वामल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fur of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and मल dirt, excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=350" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूल
जिह्वामूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वामूलीय|जिह्वामूलीयः
जिह्वामूलीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A character substituted for the Visarga, as हरिन्काम्य, and with a like sound.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वामूल, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वारद|जिह्वारदः
जिह्वारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and रद a tooth; whose tooth, (i. e. beak,) is like a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वालिह्
जिह्वालिह्<BR>m. (-लिट्)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and लिह् who licks or laps, from लिह with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वास्वाद|जिह्वास्वादः
जिह्वास्वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Licking, lapping.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा the tongue, and आस्वाद eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वाशत
जिह्वाशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A hundred tongues.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and शत a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वोल्लेखन
जिह्वोल्लेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Scraping the tongue.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A tongue-scraper, made of a thin piece of wood of the Mimusops Kauki or other trees.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्वा, and उल्लेखन scraping; also in the second sense, with कन् added, जिह्वोल्लेखनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन<BR>mf. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Old, aged.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या to become old, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूत|जीमूतः
जीमूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>4 A name of INDRA.<BR>5 A nourisher, a sustainer.<BR>6 A plant: see घोषक.<BR>7 A species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>E.<BR>जि to excel or surpass, Uṇādi affix तन्, and मूट् augment, or जी for जीव life, and मूत who urines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतकुट
जीमूतकुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small hill near a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>जीमूत a mountain, and कुट a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहन|जीमूतवाहनः
जीमूतवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 The author of a celebrated work on inheritance.<BR>E.<BR>जीमूत a cloud, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतवाहिन्
जीमूतवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>जीमूत a cloud, and वह to bear, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Cumin seed.<BR>2 A sacrificial knife or sword, a scymitar.<BR>3 A sort of panic seed: see अणु.<BR>E.<BR>जु to go, or grow quickly, रक् Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरक|जीरकः
जीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cumin seed.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>2 Withered, decayed.<BR>3 Digested.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 An old man.<BR>2 Cumin seed.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Benjamin.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to become old or decayed, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णज्वर|जीर्णज्वरः
जीर्णज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fever of some continuance and diminished intensity.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णता
जीर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Old age.<BR>2 Infirmity, decay.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and तल् affix; also with त्व, जीर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णदारु|जीर्णदारुः
जीर्णदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argentaceus.)<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णपर्ण्ण|जीर्णपर्ण|जीर्णपर्णः
जीर्णपर्ण्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The Kadamba: see कदम्बक.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A withered leaf.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण old, withered, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवज्र|जीर्णवज्रं
जीर्णवज्र<BR>n. (-ज्रं)<BR>A gem, said to be a sort of diamond.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण decayed, वज्र diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवत्
जीर्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Old, decayed.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to grow old, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवस्त्र|जीर्णवस्त्रं
जीर्णवस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>Old, worn or tattered raiment.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण old, and वस्त्र cloth or clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णवाटिका
जीर्णवाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A ruined mansion.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and वाटिका a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णव्रध्नक
जीर्णव्रध्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण old, and व्रध्न a root, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णि|जीर्णिः
जीर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 Old age, infirmity, decay.<BR>2 Digestion.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to become old, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्यान
जीर्णोद्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A neglected garden.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्धार|जीर्णोद्धारः
जीर्णोद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Repairing, renewal, repairs.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and उद्धार lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णोद्धृत
जीर्णोद्धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Repaired, renewed.<BR>E.<BR>जीर्ण, and उद्धृत lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्वि|जीर्विः
जीर्वि<BR>m. (-र्विः)<BR>1 An axe.<BR>2 A cart.<BR>3 The body.<BR>E.<BR>जॄ to decay, Uṇādi affix क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव<BR>(ऋ) जीवृ r. 1st cl. (जीवति)<BR>To live.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To use or enjoy, to get a living.<BR>With उप,<BR>To be dependant on for a living.<BR>With सं or प्र,<BR>To live agreeably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Life, existence.<BR>mf. (-वः-वा)<BR>1 Livelihood, profession, specific occupation.<BR>2 A tree: see जीवन्ती.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The sentient soul, the emanation of the deity, which is incorporated with the animal body, and gives it life, motion, and sensation; hence also called जीवात्मन्; it is opposed to that abstract state of the soul परमात्मन् in which by meditating upon its own divine nature and origin, the spirit is set at liberty from human feelings and passions.<BR>2 A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>3 A name of the prince KARṆA.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A bow string.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 The tinkling of metallic ornaments.<BR>4 Orris root.<BR>5 (In Geometry,) The chord of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, affix घञ् or क, and fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A servant, a slave, one who gets a livelihood by service.<BR>2 A snake-catcher, one whose business is catching snakes, curing their bites, &c.<BR>3 An usurer, or one who lives by lending money at high interest.<BR>4 A mendicant or one who lives by begging.<BR>5 One whose life is prolonged by blessings.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa): see असन.<BR>2 A medicinal plant, commonly called by the same name Jīvaka, and considered as one of the eight principal drugs, classed together under the name अष्टवर्ग.<BR>3 An animal, any being endowed with life.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, affix ण्वुल् or वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवग्राह|जीवग्राहः
जीवग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A prisoner, one taken alive.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and ग्राह capture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवजीव|जीवजीवः
जीवजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A kind of bird, supposed to be a sort of pheasant: see जीवञ्जीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवञ्जीव|जीवंजीव|जीवञ्जीवः
जीवञ्जीव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 A kind of bird, supposed to be a pheasant.<BR>5 The Cakora or Greek partridge.<BR>3 A kind of tree.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, and जीव who lives, from जीव with खच् affix, long-lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्|जीवन्त्
जीवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Living, alive.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्तोका
जीवत्तोका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose children are living.<BR>E.<BR>जीवत् living, and तोक offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्पति|जीवत्पतिः
जीवत्पति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A wife whose husband is alive.<BR>E.<BR>जीवत् living, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्पितृक|जीवत्पितृकः
जीवत्पितृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A son whose father is alive.<BR>E.<BR>जीवत्, and पितृ a father, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious.<BR>2 Long-lived.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Virtue, piety.<BR>2 Life, existence.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 A peacock.<BR>5 A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, अथ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=351" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवद|जीवदः
जीवद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Life-giving, who or what gives life.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A physician, a practitioner of medicine.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, and द in the first sense, from दा to give, in the second, from दो to destroy, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवधन|जीवधनं
जीवधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Living property, live-stock, wealth in flocks and herds.<BR>E.<BR>जीव alive, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Jiuti, (Odina wodier.)<BR>2 A son.<BR>3 A living being, an animal.<BR>f. (-ना or गी)<BR>A plant, commonly Jiyati: see जीवन्ती.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Jasmin.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Life, existence.<BR>2 Livelihood, profession.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 Butter of new or one day-old milk.<BR>5 Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, affix ल्यु or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनक|जीवनकं
जीवनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Food, especially boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनविडम्बन
जीवनविडम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disappointment of all hopes, living in vain.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन, and विडम्वन frustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनयोनि|जीवनयोनिः
जीवनयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Communication of vitality with body.<BR>E.<BR>जीवम, and योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनहेतु|जीवनहेतुः
जीवनहेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>End or object of life, the cause of living.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनाघात|जीवनाघातं
जीवनाघात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Poison.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन life, and आघात destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनान्त|जीवनांत|जीवनान्तः
जीवनान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Death.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनावास|जीवनावासः
जीवनावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>VARUṆA, regent of water.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन water, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीय|जीवनीयं
जीवनीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Water.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Jiyati: see जीवन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन life, छ affix; being friendly or necessary to existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनोपाय|जीवनोपायः
जीवनोपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Livelihood, means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन and उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनौषध|जीवनौषधं
जीवनौषध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>A drug to revive the dead.<BR>E.<BR>जीवन living, and औषध a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्त|जीवंत|जीवन्तः
जीवन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>Living, existent.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Life, existence.<BR>2 A medicament, a drug.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 The name of a tree, commonly Jiyati, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>2 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गुडूची.<BR>3 The Śami or Sāen tree, (Mimosa albida.)<BR>4 A parasite plant.<BR>5 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, affix झच्; fem. affix ङीप्; also with कन् added जीवन्तिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्तिक|जीवंतिक|जीवंतिकः|जीवन्तिकः
जीवन्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fowler, a bird-catcher: see जीवान्तक.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A parasite plant, (Epidendron tesseloides,) and other species.<BR>3 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>3 A kind of potherb.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्त|जीवन्मुक्तः
जीवन्मुक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A man purified by knowledge of BRAHMA, and exonerated whilst living from future birth, and all ritual ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>जीवत्, and मुक्त freed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन्मुक्ति|जीवन्मुक्तिः
जीवन्मुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Acquirement of spiritual knowledge, and consequent liberation from future birth, and ritual acts.<BR>E.<BR>जीवत्, and मुक्ति liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवपुत्रक
जीवपुत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, commonly Ingua.<BR>2 A different plant bearing seeds which are used in rosaries, commonly Jiyaputa, (Nageia putranjiva.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवबध
जीवबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Destruction of living beings.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवमन्दिर|जीवमंदिर|जीवमन्दिरं
जीवमन्दिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, and मन्दिर mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवभूत
जीवभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Alive, endowed with life.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवलोक|जीवलोकः
जीवलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The world, the habitation of living beings.<BR>2 Mankind.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाधन
जीवसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rice, grain.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and साधन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसाफल्य
जीवसाफल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Realisation of all one's wishes.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and साफल्य fruitfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवसू
जीवसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of living offspring.<BR>E.<BR>जीव living, and सू bringing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवस्थान|जीवस्थानं
जीवस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A joint, an articulation.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाजीवाधार|जीवाजीवाधारः
जीवाजीवाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The material and visible world.<BR>E.<BR>जीव animate, and अजीव inanimate, आधार a support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवातु|जीवातुः
जीवातु<BR>mn. (-तुः-तु)<BR>1 A drug for reanimating the dead.<BR>2 Boiled rice, food.<BR>3 Life, existence.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, आतु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवात्मन्
जीवात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The vital principle or spirit; that spiritual essence which renders bodies susceptible of motion or sensation.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, and आत्मन् soul or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाधार|जीवाधारः
जीवाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The world.<BR>E.<BR>जीव an animal, and आधार support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवान्तक|जीवांतक|जीवान्तकः
जीवान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>2 A destroyer of life, a slayer, a murderer.<BR>E.<BR>जीव a living being, and अन्तक a destroyer; also sometimes written जीवन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवाश
जीवाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Hoping for life.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Hope of living.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविका
जीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Livelihood, profession or occupation by which a subsistence is obtained.<BR>2 A tree: see जीवन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>जीव to live, ण्वुल् and टाप् affixes: see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविकापन्न
जीविकापन्न<BR>mf. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Having obtained subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>जीविका, and आपन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविकाप्राप्त
जीविकाप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Having obtained as a livelihood.<BR>E.<BR>जीविका, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवित|जीवितं
जीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Living, alive, existent.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Living, life, existence.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितकाल|जीवितकालः
जीवितकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Period or duration of life, a life.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित existence, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितज्ञा
जीवितज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>An artery, a vessel of the body.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित, and ज्ञा what knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be lived, to be kept alive.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Casting away life.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितसंशय|जीवितसंशयः
जीवितसंशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Fear of death.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित, and संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितहारिन्
जीवितहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Destroying life.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित, and हारिन् what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविताशा
जीविताशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Love of life.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितेश|जीवितेशः
जीवितेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Ruling life, master of being, (applicable to objects either of reverence or affection.)<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA, regent of death.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 A lover, a husband.<BR>5 Lord or master of existence.<BR>6 A drug to revive the dead.<BR>E.<BR>जीवित life, and ईश lord, ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवोत्सर्ग|जीवोत्सर्गः
जीवोत्सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Abandonment of life, voluntary death.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and उत्सर्ग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविन्
जीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Alive, living, animate, a living being.<BR>E.<BR>जीव, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=352" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जु
जु<BR>r. 1st cl. (जवति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To move quickly, to go rapidly.<BR>(ङ) जुङ् r. 1st cl. (जवते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुट|जुकुटः
जुकुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The Malaya range of mountains.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुग
जुग<BR>(इ) जिगि r. 1st cl. (जुंगति)<BR>1 To except, to exclude.<BR>2 To quit or abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सन|जुगुप्सनं
जुगुप्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Censure, abuse, reproach, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to censure, affix ल्युट्, or with अङ् and टाप् affixes जुगुप्सा; the root is always inflected in this sense, in the desiderative form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सा
जुगुप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Censure, &c. see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सित
जुगुप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reviled, blamed, censured, abused.<BR>E.<BR>गुप to censure, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्ग|जुङ्गः
जुङ्ग<BR>mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>E.<BR>जुगि to quit, affix घञ्, removing all blemishes; also with कन् added जुङ्गक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुङ्गित|जुंगित|जुङ्गितः
जुङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Outcaste, deserted, injured, abandoned.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A man of a degraded caste, a Caṇḍāla, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जुगि to abandon, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटक|जुटकं
जुटक<BR>nf. (-टकं-टिका)<BR>1 The matted hair of ŚIVA or of ascetics.<BR>2 Any knot or fillet of hair.<BR>E.<BR>जट to collect, affix वुन्, and उ or ऊ inserted: see जटा; also जूट, जूटक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुड
जुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (जुडति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To bind.<BR>3 To join, as in making or mending.<BR>r. 10th cl. (जोडयति)<BR>1 To send, to cast or throw, to direct.<BR>2 To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुत
जुत<BR>(ऋ) जुतृ r. 1st cl. (जोतते)<BR>To shine, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुन
जुन<BR>r. 6th cl. (जुनति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर्<BR>f. (-जूः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 Motion in general.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर to make haste, affix क्विप्, and उठ् substituted for ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुल
जुल<BR>r. 10th cl. (जोलयति)<BR>To reduce to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्व|जुर्व्व
जुर्व<BR>(इ) जुर्वी r. 1st cl. (जूर्वति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष
जुष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (जुषति जोषयति)<BR>1 To reason, to think, to conceive or imagine, to investigate or examine.<BR>2 To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>3 To like.<BR>(ञि ई) ञि जुषी r. 6th cl. (जुषते)<BR>To please, to gratify, to give satisfaction or delight, to serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्कक|जुष्ककः
जुष्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The water of boiled pulse, pease soup, porridge, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please or satisfy, क affix, and deriv. irr. see जूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Served, obliged, worshipped, gratified by service.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>The crumbs or remnants of a meal or its leavings.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्य|जुष्यः
जुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>To be served or worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवत्
जुहुवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवान|जुहुवानः
जुहुवान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 A hard hearted man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहू
जुहू<BR>f. (-हूः)<BR>A wooden vessel, of the shape of a semicircle or crescent, used at sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, Uṇādi affix क्विप्, the root reiterated, and the final made long; also remaining short जुहु. f. (-हुः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवत्|जुहूवन्त्
जुहूवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>Fire, or the deity AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>जुह्व a sacrificial vessel, and मतुप् possessing; being the medium of (burnt) offerings; also जुहुवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूराण|जुहूराणः
जुहूराण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Fire or its deity.<BR>3 An officiating priest.<BR>E.<BR>हूर्च्छ to be crooked, to abandon, &c. Uṇādi affix आनच्; the root is reiterated, and the final छ rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुह्वत्
जुह्वत्<BR>mfn. (-ह्वन्-ह्वती-ह्वत्)<BR>Sacrifice, offering oblations.<BR>E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू<BR>f. (-जूः)<BR>1 Æther, heaven.<BR>2 A name of the goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>3 A female demon or goblin.<BR>4 Speed, expedition, velocity.<BR>5 Going, motion.<BR>E.<BR>जु to go swiftly, affix क्विप्, and the final lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूट|जूटः
जूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The matted hair of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The clotted hair of an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>जट to collect, affix अच्, ऊ inserted: see जटा; also with कन् added जूटक. n. (-कं) And with a short vowel जुटक q. v.; it is also used compounded with जटा in the same sense, as जटाजूट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूति|जूतिः
जूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 Going, proceeding, moving.<BR>E.<BR>जु to go swiftly, affix क्तिन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर
जूर<BR>(ई) जूरी r. 4th cl. (जूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, to world or kill.<BR>2 To be decayed, to decay or grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णाह्वय|जूर्णाह्वयः
जूर्णाह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Andropogon sorghum): see देवधान्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
जूर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 Speed.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 Fever.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर to be feverish, Uṇādi affix नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्त्ति|जूर्ति|जूर्तिः|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Fever, feverish or morbid heat.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर to be feverish, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्व्व
जूर्व्व<BR>(-ई) जूर्व्वी (जूर्व्वति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष|जूषं|जूषः
जूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (जूषति-ते)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष|जूषं|जूषः
जूष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The water of boiled pulse, pease soup, porridge, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to satisfy, affix क, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषण|जूषणं
जूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A plant, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>जष to hurt, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (जरति)<BR>To make short or low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृभ
जृभ<BR>(ई) जृभी r. 1st cl. (जर्भते) or more commonly r. 1st cl. (इ) जृभि (जृम्भते^1)<BR>To gape, to yawn.<BR>r. 10th cl. (जृम्भयति)<BR>To fear, to dread.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभं|जृंभः|जृम्भः
जृम्भ<BR>mfn. sub. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>2 Expansion, stretching, expanding.<BR>3 Swelling, a puffing or blowing up.<BR>4 Blowing blossoming.<BR>E.<BR>जृभि to gape, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भक|जृंभकः|जृम्भकः
जृम्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A subordinate deity.<BR>2 A yawner.<BR>E.<BR>जृभि, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भण|जृंभण|जृम्भणं
जृम्भण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>2 Blowing.<BR>E.<BR>जृभि to yawn, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भमाण
जृम्भमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Yawning, gaping.<BR>2 Opening, blowing.<BR>E.<BR>जृभि to open, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भावत्|जृम्भावन्त्
जृम्भावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Yawning, gaping.<BR>E.<BR>जृम्भा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिका|जृंभिका
जृम्भिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Gaping, yawning.<BR>E.<BR>जृम्भि, and क्वुन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भित|जृंभित|जृम्भितं
जृम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opened, expanded.<BR>2 Enlarged.<BR>3 Done, exerted.<BR>4 Opened, (as a flower,) blown.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>2 Swelling, expansion.<BR>3 Bursting, opening.<BR>4 Wish, active wish or search for.<BR>E.<BR>जृभि to gape, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृम्भिन्
जृम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>1 Who or what yawns or gapes.<BR>2 Expanding, blossoming.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of Mimosa, (M. octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>जृम्भ bursting, budding, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ<BR>r. 1st cl. (जरति) 4th cl. (जोर्य्यते) 9th cl. (जृणाति) and 10th cl. (जारयति)<BR>To grow old, to be or become old or decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतव्य
जेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be conquered or overcome, to be surpassed or excelled.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=353" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतृ
जेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Victorious, triumphant.<BR>2 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A victor, a conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्ताक|जेंताक|जेंताकः|जेन्ताकः
जेन्ताक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dry hot bath, or heated chamber for inducing perspiration in rheumatism, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमन|जेमनं
जेमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Food, victuals.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>जमु to eat, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेय|जेयः
जेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Conquerable, fit or subject to be conquered.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष
जेष<BR>(ऋ) जेषृ r. 1st cl. (जेषते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेह
जेह<BR>(ऋ) जेहृ r. 1st cl. (जेहते)<BR>To resolve, to attempt resolutely, to endeavour diligently or perseveringly.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जै
जै<BR>r. 1st cl. (जायति)<BR>To wane or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्र|जैत्रं|जैत्रः
जैत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A conqueror, a victor.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A tree, (Aeschynomene sesban.)<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer or excel, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्ररथ|जैत्ररथः
जैत्ररथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A hero, a victor, a conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>जैत्र victorious, and रथ a car; whose chariot is triumphant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैन|जैनः
जैन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Jaina, a follower of the principles of a Jina or teacher of heterodox notions, the chief of which are, the supremacy of certain religious pontiffs over the gods of the Hindus, a denial of the divine authority of the Vedas, and a disregard of the distinction of castes.<BR>E.<BR>जिन a Jina, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैपाल|जैपालः
जैपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Croton tiglium): see जयपाल, the diphthong being considered as a substitute for the semivowel and vowels of the first members of the compound; it is most probably a corruption borrowed from the dialects in which such a substitution is common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनि|जैमिनिः
जैमिनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The name of a celebrated saint and philosopher, the pupil of VYĀSA, and founder of the Uttara Mīmāṃsā school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Long-lived.<BR>2 Thin, spare.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A drug, a medicament.<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 A son.<BR>E.<BR>जीव life, आतृकन् Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैष्णव
जैष्णव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Relating to a conqueror, to ARJUNA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जिष्णु as above, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्य|जैह्म्यं
जैह्म्य<BR>n. (-ह्म्यं)<BR>Crookedness, moral or physical.<BR>E.<BR>जिह्म crooked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गक|जोंगकं|जोङ्गकं
जोङ्गक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>जुगि to remove, ण्वुल् affix; dissipating bad smells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोङ्गट|जोंगट|जोंगटः|जोङ्गटः
जोङ्गट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Longing for, wishing earnestly or eagerly.<BR>E.<BR>जुगि to abandon, (all objects save that desired,) and अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोटिङ्ग|जोटिंग|जोटिंगः|जोटिङ्गः
जोटिङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A devotee, an ascetic, who subjects himself to the severest penances.<BR>E.<BR>जूट the braided hair of ŚIVA, ग who goes, from गम to go, the form is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोन्ताला
जोन्ताला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kind of grain: see देवधान्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोष|जोषं|जोषः
जोष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Happiness, felicity, pleasure, enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A woman: see योषा; also जोषित्, जोषिता, &c.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to delight, affix घञ्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषम्
जोषम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Silently.<BR>2 In happiness, delightedly at ease, &c.<BR>3 Well, excellently.<BR>4 Excessively, beyond bounds.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please or be pleased, affix अम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिका
जोषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bud, a germ.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please, affix वुन्, and fem. form; some copies have more accurately perhaps कोषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषित्
जोषित्<BR>f. (-षित्)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to delight, affix इति; also योषित्, जोषिता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिता
जोषिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>जुष to please, affix क्त; also योषित, योषिता, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ<BR>A compound letter, considered to be composed of ज and ज्ञ; it is usually expressed by jn or gn, but its peculiar nasal sound is not well conveyed by any combination of the Roman alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ<BR>mfn. (ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Who or what knows.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A wise and learned man; it especially applies to one possessed of sacred learning, and religious knowledge.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 Buddha, first of the line of the moon, and regent of the planet MERCURY.<BR>5 The planet MARS or its regent.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, to possess knowledge, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप
ज्ञप<BR>r. 10th cl. (ज्ञापयति)<BR>1 To know.<BR>2 To cause to be known: see ज्ञा.<BR>3 To whet or sharpen.<BR>4 To beat.<BR>5 To please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञपित|ज्ञपितः
ज्ञपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taught, expounded, made known.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञप to make known, affix क्त, इट् optionally inserted, otherwise ज्ञप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्त|ज्ञप्तः
ज्ञप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Made known: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्ति|ज्ञप्तिः
ज्ञप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Understanding, comprehension, the exercise of the intellectual faculty.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञप to make known, affix क्तिन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
ज्ञा<BR>r. 9th cl. (जानाति जानीते)<BR>To know, to understand.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>1 To assent or conform^1 to.<BR>2 To acknowledge.<BR>With अप,<BR>To conceal.<BR>With अव,<BR>To disrespect, to despise.<BR>With उप,<BR>To deny knowledge of any thing.<BR>With परि,<BR>To ascertain.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To know well.<BR>With प्रति or सम्,<BR>To assent, to admit, to agree, to promise.<BR>With प्रति and अभि,<BR>To recognise.<BR>With वि,<BR>To discriminate, to know.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To recollect or possess the power of knowing. (In combination, it usually takes the deponent form, as अनुजानीते, अपजानीते, &c.)<BR>r. 10th cl. (ज्ञापयति)<BR>To command, to direct; आङ् is usually prefixed in this sense.<BR>r. 1st cl. but occurring in the form of the causal, (ज्ञपयति)<BR>1 To slay.<BR>2 To gratify or please.<BR>3 To exhibit.<BR>4 To sharpen.<BR>5 To praise. In these senses the root is, in general, combined with a prefix.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात|ज्ञातं
ज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Known, comprehended, understood fully.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातव्य|ज्ञातव्यं
ज्ञातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be known or understood.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातसिद्धान्त|ज्ञातसिद्धांत|ज्ञातसिद्धान्तः
ज्ञातसिद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A man completely versed in any science or Śāstra.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञात what is known, and सिद्धान्त completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातान्वय|ज्ञातान्वयः
ज्ञातान्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of Varddhamāna, the last Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञात known, and अन्वय lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाति|ज्ञातिः
ज्ञाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A father.<BR>2 A kinsman in general.<BR>3 A distant kinsman, one who does not participate in the oblations of food or water offered to deceased ancestors.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, affix क्तिन्; who is known, an acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिकर्म्मन्|ज्ञातिकर्मन्
ज्ञातिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Duty of kindred.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञाति, and कम्म act; also ज्ञातिकार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=354" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातित्व
ज्ञातित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Relationship, kin.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to ज्ञाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातृ
ज्ञातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Knowing, wise, intelligent, who or what knows.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, तृच् active aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातेय|ज्ञातेयं
ज्ञातेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Relationship, affinity.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञाति a kinsman, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात्वा
ज्ञात्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having known.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञान|ज्ञानं
ज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Knowledge in general.<BR>2 Knowledge of a specific and religious kind, that which is derived from meditation, and the study of philosophy, which teaches man the divine nature and origin of his immaterial part, with the unreality of corporal enjoyments or worldly forms, and which, separating him during life from terrestrial objects, secures him, after death, a final emancipation from existence, and reunion with the universal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानगम्य
ज्ञानगम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>Attainable by knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and गम्य attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानचक्षुस्
ज्ञानचक्षुस्<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>Intellect, intellectual vision.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतपस्
ज्ञानतपस्<BR>n. (-पः)<BR>Cultivation of sacred knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and तपस् religious austerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतस्
ज्ञानतस्<BR>ind.<BR>By or through knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदर्पण|ज्ञानदर्पणः
ज्ञानदर्पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>One of the Jaina saints.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान true knowledge, and दर्पण a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानदीप
ज्ञानदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Knowledge, the lamp of knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाननिष्ठ
ज्ञाननिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Cultivating spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and निष्ठ engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपर
ज्ञानपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Versed in spiritual wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and पर attentive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानपूर्व्व|ज्ञानपूर्व
ज्ञानपूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>Preceded by the acquirement of divine wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and पूर्व्व prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमय|ज्ञानमयः
ज्ञानमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Consisting of knowledge, made up of it.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमुद्र
ज्ञानमुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Having the impress of wisdom, wise, making wise.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमूल
ज्ञानमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Founded on spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानलक्षण
ज्ञानलक्षण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Indication, sign, means of knowing or inferring.<BR>2 (In Logic,) Sign or proof of knowledge, or subsequent derived from antecedent knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानवत्|ज्ञानवन्त्
ज्ञानवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wise, especially in spiritual things.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानविज्ञान
ज्ञानविज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sacred and profane knowledge.<BR>2 The Vedas and their subordinate parts, as medicine, war, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and विज्ञान miscellaneous knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानानुत्पाद|ज्ञानानुत्पादः
ज्ञानानुत्पाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Folly, ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and अनुत्पाद nonproduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानावस्थित
ज्ञानावस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Occupied by wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and अवस्थित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिन्
ज्ञानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>1 Wise, intelligent.<BR>2 Knowing, who or what knows.<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>1 An astrologer, a fortuneteller, a man prescient of future events.<BR>2 A sage, one possessing religious wisdom or Jñāna (ज्ञान) as above.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान knowledge, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानेन्द्रिय|ज्ञानेंद्रिय|ज्ञानेन्द्रियं
ज्ञानेन्द्रिय<BR>m. (-यं)<BR>An organ of perception or consciousness, the skin, tongue, eye, ear and intellect.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञान, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापक|ज्ञापकः
ज्ञापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Making or causing to know.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An instructor.<BR>2 A commander, a master.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापन|ज्ञापनं
ज्ञापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Making known, apprising, informing.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञाप्ति|ज्ञाप्तिः
ज्ञाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Making known, informing.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा to know, causal form, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञेय|ज्ञेयं
ज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be known, what may be or ought to be known.<BR>E.<BR>ज्ञा, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यका
ज्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The chord of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या<BR>r. 9th cl. (जिनाति)<BR>To decay, to be or become old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A bowstring.<BR>4 The chord of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या to become old, to decay, affixes अङ्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्याघोष
ज्याघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Twang of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानि|ज्यानिः
ज्यानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Old age, decay, infirmity.<BR>2 Abandoning, quitting, leaving.<BR>3 A river, a stream.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या to decay, &c. Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस्
ज्यायस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very old.<BR>2 Very excellent, best.<BR>3 Elder, elder born.<BR>4 In law, one independent and answerable for his own conduct.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या to be old, इयसुन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यु
ज्यु<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्यवते)<BR>To go or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युत
ज्युत<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) ज्युतृ (ज्योतते); also (इर) ज्युतिर r. 1st cl. (ज्योतति)<BR>To shine. see द्युत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठ|ज्येष्ठः
ज्येष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Best, most excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>2 Very old, oldest.<BR>3 Elder, elder born.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 One of the asterisms considered as lunar mansions; the eighteenth, comprising three stars, of which one is a Scorpionis, figured by a ring or earring.<BR>2 The middle finger.<BR>3 Misfortune, personified as a goddess.<BR>4 The Ganges.<BR>(-ष्ठा or ष्ठी)<BR>A small house lizard.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The month Jyaiṣṭha or Jeyte, (May-June.)<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Age, oldness.<BR>E.<BR>ज्या to decay, to grow infirm or old, affix इष्ठन्, fem. affixes. टाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठता
ज्येष्ठता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Seniority.<BR>2 Superiority.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and तल् affix; also ज्येष्ठत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठतात|ज्येष्ठतातः
ज्येष्ठतात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A father's elder brother.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ elder born, and तात a father; the usual order of composition is here irregularly inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठभार्य्या|ज्येष्ठभार्या
ज्येष्ठभार्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 An elder brother's wife.<BR>2 The elder or chief wife.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and भार्य्या a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवर्ण|ज्येष्ठवर्णः
ज्येष्ठवर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ elder born or best, and वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठवृत्ति|ज्येष्ठवृत्तिः
ज्येष्ठवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>The duties of age or seniority.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठावाप्य
ज्येष्ठावाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be obtained by virtue or seniority, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and आवाप्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठश्वश्रू
ज्येष्ठश्वश्रू<BR>f. (-श्रूः)<BR>A wife's elder sister.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ elder, श्वश्रू motherin-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=355" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठसामन्
ज्येष्ठसामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>1 A portion of the Sāma Veda.<BR>2 A religious rite of which its perusal is a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठांश|ज्येष्ठांशः
ज्येष्ठांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The elder brother's share.<BR>2 The best share.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूलीय|ज्येष्ठामूलीयः
ज्येष्ठामूलीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The month Jyeṣṭha.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठा the constellation, (as above,) मूल root, origin, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाम्बु|ज्येष्ठांबु
ज्येष्ठाम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>The scum of boiled rice, or water in which grain has been washed.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाश्रम|ज्येष्ठाश्रमः
ज्येष्ठाश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The order of the householder.<BR>2 A householder.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ, and आश्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठाश्रमिन्
ज्येष्ठाश्रमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A householder, a man of the second order.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठ best, आश्रम order, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ|ज्यैष्ठः
ज्यैष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The month Jyaiṣṭha or Jyeṣṭha or Jeyte, (May-June.)<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1 The day of full moon in Jyeṣṭha.<BR>2 A house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>ज्यैष्ठा the mansion or asterism which the moon is in this month, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठसामन्
ज्यैष्ठसामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A Brahman versed in that portion of the Sāma Veda called Jyeṣṭha Sāma.<BR>E.<BR>ज्येष्ठसामन् as above, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठिनेय
ज्यैष्ठिनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Born of the elder or principal wife.<BR>E.<BR>ज्यैष्ठा, and ढक् affix, इनङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ्य|ज्यैष्ठ्यं
ज्यैष्ठ्य<BR>n. (-ष्ठ्यं)<BR>Seniority, age.<BR>E.<BR>ज्यैष्ट, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यो
ज्यो<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्यवते)<BR>1 To advise or instruct.<BR>2 To order.<BR>3 To observe a vow or any religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिःशास्त्र
ज्योतिःशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>The science of Astronomy.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and शास्त्र a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिरिङ्ग|ज्योतिरिंग|ज्योतिरिङ्गः
ज्योतिरिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A fire fly.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, इगि to go, affix क; also with युच् affix, ज्योतिरिङ्गण n. (-णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्गण|ज्योतिर्गणः
ज्योतिर्गण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The heavenly bodies collectively.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिम् a planet, and गण a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्
ज्योतिर्विद्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>An astrologer, an arithmetician.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्विद्या
ज्योतिर्विद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>The science of computation, from arithmetic to astronomy and astrology.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्वीज|ज्योतिर्व्वीजं
ज्योतिर्वीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A fire fly.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिश्चक्र|ज्योतिश्चक्रं
ज्योतिश्चक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 The zodiac.<BR>2 The lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् planet, and चक्र a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं|ज्योतिषः
ज्योतिष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Astrological, astronomical, relating to the heavenly bodies.<BR>mf. (-षः-षी)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Mathematical, astronomical, and astrological science, astronomy, astrology.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>A star, a planet, an asterism.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, especially of the heavenly bodies, affix अण्, fem. ङीष्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषिक|ज्योतिषिकः
ज्योतिषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astrologer: see ज्यौतिषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्क|ज्योतिष्कः
ज्योतिष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>1 A planetary or heavenly body; the generic term for the sun, the moon, a planet, an asterism, a star: the word in the m. plu. (-ष्काः) implies all these five.<BR>2 A tree, the wood of which is used to produce fire by attrition: see गणिकारिका.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Heart-pea: see ज्योतिष्मती.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, and क what makes, from कृ, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कल्प
ज्योतिष्कल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Blazing, radiant, like flame or fire.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and कल्प affix, implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्टोम|ज्योतिष्टोमः
ज्योतिष्टोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A particular sacrifice at which sixteen officiating priests are required.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, and स्तोम a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्मत्|ज्योतिष्मन्त्
ज्योतिष्मत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-मती)<BR>Heart-pea, (Halicacabum cardiospermum.)<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light or splendor, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस्<BR>n. (-तिः)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 A star.<BR>3 The pupil of the eye.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत् to shine, to be or give light, इसिन् Uṇādi affix, and ज substituted for the radical initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्सात्
ज्योतिस्सात्<BR>ind.<BR>In flame or fire.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस्, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतीरथ|ज्योतीरथः
ज्योतीरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The pole star, or in mythology DHRUVA, the son of UTTĀNAPĀDA.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् a star, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्ना
ज्योत्स्ना<BR>f. (-त्स्ना)<BR>1 Moonlight.<BR>2 A moonlight night.<BR>3 A small cucumber: see ज्योत्स्नी.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् light, त affix, and the penultimate rejected deriv. irr. fem. affix टाप्; also with ङीप्^1, ज्योत्स्नी q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नाप्रिय|ज्योत्स्नाप्रियः
ज्योत्स्नाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Cakora or Greek partridge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योत्स्ना moonlight, and प्रिय fond of; this bird is said to feed upon the moonbeams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नावृक्ष|ज्योत्स्नावृक्षः
ज्योत्स्नावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The tripod or tree of a lampstand, a candlestick.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योत्स्ना moonlight, (put for lamp-light,) and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नी
ज्योत्स्नी<BR>f. (-त्स्नी)<BR>1 A moonlight night.<BR>2 A small cucumber, (Trichosanthes diæca); it is also applied to Luffa acutangula, &c.<BR>3 A kind of perfume: see रेणुका.<BR>E.<BR>see ज्योत्स्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौतिषिक|ज्यौतिषिकः
ज्यौतिषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योतिस् a star, affix टक्; also the vowel being unchanged optionally, ज्योतिषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्न|ज्यौत्स्नः
ज्यौत्स्न<BR>mfn. (-त्स्नः-त्स्नी-त्स्नं)<BR>Light, especially with moonlight, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योत्स्ना^1 moonlight, अण् affix: see ज्यौत्स्नी^2 and ज्यौत्स्निका^3.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: cf. WIL1819.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: cf. WIL1819.<BR>[3] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: cf. WIL1819.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्निका
ज्यौत्स्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योत्स्नी and कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्नी
ज्यौत्स्नी<BR>f. (-त्स्नी)<BR>A moonlight night, or a night on which the moon is full.<BR>2 A kind of cucumber: see ज्यौत्स्ना.<BR>E.<BR>ज्योत्ली as above, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
ज्रि<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्रियति)<BR>1 To conquer, to reduce.<BR>2 To be conquered or reduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्री
ज्री<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्रिणाति) r. 1st and 10th cls. (ज्रयति-ज्राययति)<BR>To grow old, to be or become old or decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्वरति)<BR>To be diseased, to be feverish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fever, intermitting or continued.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर to be feverish, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरघ्न|ज्वरघ्नः
ज्वरघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Anti-febrile, febrifuge.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>2 A potherb, (Chenopocium album.)<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरनाशक
ज्वरनाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Febrifuge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर, and नाशक what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरहन्तृ
ज्वरहन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Febrifuge.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर, and हन्तृ what destroys; ज्वरहन् (-च्चा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वराग्नि|ज्वराग्निः
ज्वराग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Feverish heat, or the hot paroxysm of fever.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर fever, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरान्तक|ज्वरान्तकः
ज्वरान्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Febrifuge.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of Nimb from Nepal.<BR>2 Cassia fistula.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर, and अन्तक what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरापहा
ज्वरापहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर fever, अपहा removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरित|ज्वरितः
ज्वरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Febrile, feverish, affected with fever.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर to be feverish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरिन्
ज्वरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Febrile, feverish, fevered.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वर, and इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=356" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ज्वलति,) or with a prefix, r. 10th cl. (प्रज्वलयति)<BR>To shine, to blaze, to flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Blazing, shining.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Flame, blaze, light.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल, to blaze, affix अच्; also ज्वाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलका
ज्वलका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Flame.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to blaze, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलत्|ज्वलन्त्
ज्वलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Burning, blazing.<BR>2 Shining, radiant, brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to burn, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन|ज्वलनः
ज्वलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Burning, blazing.<BR>2 The fire.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>AGNI, or fire.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to blaze, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलनाश्मन्
ज्वलनाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>The sun-stone.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वलन, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन्मणि
ज्वलन्मणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Blazing with jewels.<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A brilliant gem.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वलत्, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलयत्
ज्वलयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Burning, blazing.<BR>2 Radiant.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to burn, r. 10th cl. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलित|ज्वलितः
ज्वलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Burnt.<BR>2 Blazing, flaming.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to flame, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलितनयन
ज्वलितनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fiery-eyed, looking angrily or fiercely.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वलित, and नयन the eye; also ज्वलितचक्षुस्, ज्वलितनेत्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलिन्
ज्वलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Burning, flaming.<BR>2 Shining.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वाल|ज्वालः
ज्वाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Burning, blazing.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>Flame, blaze.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Burnt rice.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वल to blaze, affix अण्, fem. affix टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालाग्नि
ज्वालाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Flame.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वाल, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालाजिहू
ज्वालाजिहू<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>AGNI, or fire.<BR>E.<BR>जाला, and जिह्वा a tongue; whose tongue is flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालामुखी
ज्वालामुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A place where subterraneous fires break forth; an object of veneration to the Hindus: a celebrated Jvālāmukhī exists in Lahore, to which pilgrimages are made; the soil abounding with carburetted hydrogen, which takes fire upon coming in contact with the external air; otherwise vents being made, a light is applied to the orifice, and flame being kindled, is fed by the stream of gas that escapes. The tongue of PĀRVATĪ is said to have fallen at this place.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वाला flame, and मुख chief, principal, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालिन्
ज्वालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Flaming, blazing.<BR>E.<BR>ज्वाला, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ<BR>The ninth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet; the aspirate of the preceding letter, and corresponding in power to Jh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ<BR>mfn. (झः झा झं)<BR>1 Asleep, sleeping.<BR>2 Lost, destroyed.<BR>m. (झः)<BR>1 A name of VṚHASPATI, preceptor of the gods.<BR>2 A name of the chief of the Daityas or demons.<BR>3 Sound, or a sort of sound like the splashing of water, or the clashing of cymbals, jangling, clanging, &c.<BR>4 High wind.<BR>5 A stray, a thing lost or mislaid.<BR>6 Playing a tune, beating time.<BR>f. (झा)<BR>The descent of a cascade, a water fall.<BR>E.<BR>झट to collect, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झङ्कार|झंकार|झंकारः|झङ्कारः
झङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A low inarticulate sound, as the buzzing of bees, &c.<BR>E.<BR>झं, and कार a making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झन|झंझन|झंझनं
झञ्झन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An indistinct noise, like the jangling of metal ornaments, a ringing, a rattling, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झा|झंझा
झञ्झा<BR>f. (-ञ्झा)<BR>1 Wind, wind and rain, a hurricane, a gale.<BR>2 A sharp clanging sound, jangling.<BR>3 Raining in large drops.<BR>4 A stray, any thing lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्झानिल|झंझानिल|झञ्झानिलः
झञ्झानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Wind with rain, a high wind in the rainy season, a typhoon or the sort of tempest frequent during the south-west monsoon.<BR>E.<BR>झञ्झा heavy rain, and अनिल wind; also झञ्झामरुत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झञ्भ्कावात
झञ्भ्कावात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Wind with rain, a storm, a squall.<BR>E.<BR>झञ्झा heavy rain, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झट
झट<BR>r. 1st cl. (झटति)<BR>To clot, to be entangled, (as hair): see जट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटा
झटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>झट to be entangled, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटि|झटिः
झटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A small tree, a shrub, a bush.<BR>E.<BR>झट to be entangled, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटिति
झटिति<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly, speedily, instantly.<BR>E.<BR>झटि entangling, confusing, affix क्तिच्; also जटिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झनत्कार|झनत्कारः
झनत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The clanging of metallic ornaments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>झनत् imitative sound, &c. कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम
झम<BR>(उ) झमु r. 1st cl. (झमति)<BR>To eat: see जमु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्प|झंप|झंपः|झम्पः
झम्प<BR>mf. (-म्पः-म्पा)<BR>Jumping, springing, plunging.<BR>E.<BR>झं imitative sound, and पत to fall, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पाक|झंपाक|झंपाकः|झम्पाकः
झम्पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A monkey or ape.<BR>E.<BR>झम्प, and अक to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पारु|झंपारु|झंपारुः|झम्पारुः
झम्पारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A monkey, an ape.<BR>E.<BR>झम्प plunging, and ऋ to go, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पाशिन्
झम्पाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A kingfisher.<BR>E.<BR>झम्प plunging, and अश to eat, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झम्पिन्|झंपिन्
झम्पिन्<BR>m. (-म्पी)<BR>A monkey, an ape.<BR>E.<BR>झम्प springing, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर|झरः
झर<BR>m. (-रः) f. (-रा or -रिः-री)<BR>A cascade, a water-fall.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>झॄ to waste or decay, affix अप्, fem. affix टाप्, इन् or ङीष्; also निर्झर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्च|झर्च्च
झर्च<BR>r. 6th cl. (झर्चति)<BR>1 To say.<BR>2 To blame; to abuse or menace; also झर्छ, झर्ज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्छ
झर्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (झर्छति)<BR>1 To say.<BR>2 To blame, to abuse or menace; also झर्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्ज
झर्ज<BR>r. 6th cl. (झर्जति)<BR>1 To say, to speak.<BR>2 To censure, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झ
झर्झ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (झर्झति झर्झयति)<BR>1 To speak or say.<BR>2 To censure or reprove.<BR>r. 1st cl. (झर्झति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झर|झर्झरः
झर्झर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A sort of drum.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Kali yug, the present Yug or age of the world.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A whore.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sound as of splashing or dropping.<BR>E.<BR>झर्झ an imitative sound like that of water splashing, &c. and र what makes, from रा with ड affix, or झर्झ to censure, and अरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरक|झर्झरकः
झर्झरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Kali yug.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झर्झरीक|झर्झरीकः
झर्झरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 A country.<BR>3 A picture.<BR>E.<BR>झर्झ to injure or destroy, ईकन् affix, and र inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलञ्झला
झलञ्झला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The flapping of an elephant's ears, of loose breasts, &c. the word is considered as merely imitative of the noise made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलरी
झलरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A sort of drum.<BR>2 A curl.<BR>E.<BR>झल imitative sound, र from रा to get or make, affix ड and ङीप्; also झल्लरी and झल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झला
झला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 Sunshine, splendour, brilliant or glistering light.<BR>3 A cricket; also झाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झलि|झलिः
झलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>The areca nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=357" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्ल|झल्लः
झल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A prize fighter, a cudgel player, a man of a tribe following such a profession; one of the degraded classes, being sprung from the outcaste Kṣatriya.<BR>E.<BR>जल to surround or embrace, ल added, and ज changed to झ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लक|झल्लकं
झल्लक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Cymbals.<BR>E.<BR>झल्ल imitative sound, a clash, and क what emits, from कै to sound, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लकण्ठ|झल्लकंठ|झल्लकंठः|झल्लकण्ठः
झल्लकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>झल्ल imitative sound, and कण्ठ a throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लरी
झल्लरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A sort of drum.<BR>2 A curl, a lock of hair: see झलरी.<BR>3 A ball, &c. of perfumed substances used for cleaning the hair.<BR>4 Moisture.<BR>5 Purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लिका
झल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Light, splendour, lustre.<BR>2 A rag or cloth used for applying colour or perfumes.<BR>3 Dirt brought off the body by rubbing it with perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्ली
झल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A kind of drum: see झलरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झल्लोल|झल्लोलः
झल्लोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A ball or protuberance at the lower end of a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष|झषं|झषः
झष<BR>r. 1st cl. (-झषति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR>2 To take.<BR>3 To put on, to wear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झष|झषं|झषः
झष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 The sign Pisces.<BR>3 Heat, warmth.<BR>4 A forest, a thicket.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Waste land.<BR>E.<BR>झष to injure, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषकेतन|झषकेतनः
झषकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KANDARPA.<BR>E.<BR>झष a fish, and केतन a banner, who bears a fish on his banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषाङ्क|झषांक|झषाङ्कः
झषाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A name of ANIRUDDHA, the son of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>झष a fish, and अङ्क a mark or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषाशन|झषाशनः
झषाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>झष fish, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झषोदरी
झषोदरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A proper name, the mother of the poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>झष a fish, and उदर the belly: born from the belly of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झांकृत
झांकृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A tinkling ornament worn on the toes or the feet.<BR>E.<BR>झां a jangling or jingling, and कृत made (by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाट|झाटः
झाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with creepers.<BR>2 A wood, a thicket.<BR>3 Cleaning sores or wounds.<BR>f. (-टा-टी)<BR>1 Jasmine.<BR>3 A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta): see झाट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A wood, a thicket.<BR>E.<BR>झट to be entangled, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटल|झाटलः
झाटल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of flower: see घण्टापाटलि.<BR>E.<BR>झाट a thicket. or bower, ला to make, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटास्त्रक|झाटास्त्रकः
झाटास्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The water melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाटीका
झाटीका<BR>(-का)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झामक|झामकं
झामक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A burnt or vitrified brick.<BR>E.<BR>झम to eat, affix ण्वुल, being fed upon by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झामर|झामरः
झामर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small whetstone, used chiefly by housewives for sharpening their spindles, needles, &c.<BR>E.<BR>झाम eating, wearing away, from झम to eat, affix घञ्, and र what gets, from रा with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झार्झर|झार्झरः
झार्झर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A tabor player, a drummer.<BR>E.<BR>झर्झर a cymbal, affix अण्; also with ठक् affix झार्झरिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झालरी
झालरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>झलरी the same, अण् pleonastic, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झाला
झाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>See झला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झालि|झालिः
झालि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of sour or unripe mangoes, fried with salt, mustard and asafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झावु|झावुः
झावु<BR>m. (-वुः)<BR>A tree, (Tamarix Indica); also with कन् added झावुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>and with a long final vowel झावू.<BR>m. (-वूः)<BR>the words are considered as irregular or foreign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिङ्गाक|झिङ्गाकं
झिङ्गाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिङ्गिनी|झिंगिनी
झिङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A torch, a firebrand.<BR>2 A sort of cucumber, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिज्जी
झिज्जी<BR>f. (-ज्जी)<BR>A cricket: see झिल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिञ्जिम
झिञ्जिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A forest on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिण्टी|झिंटी
झिण्टी<BR>f. (-ण्टी)<BR>A shrub, (Barleria cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>झि imitative sound, रट to utter, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिरी
झिरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>झि imitative of the cricket's chirp, रा to make, affixes ड and ङीष्; also झिल्ली; also झिरिका, कन् being added; also इ pen. being made long झिरीका, or changed to उ, झिरुका; the first vowel also being lengthened झीरिका, and झीरुका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिरुका
झिरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लि|झिल्लिः
झिल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>1 Cymbals.<BR>2 A cricket.<BR>3 Membrane: see झिल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लिका
झिल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A cricket.<BR>2 The light of sunshine, strong light, splendour.<BR>3 Dirt taken off the body in rubbing it with perfumes.<BR>4 A cloth or rag used for applying colour, unguents, &c.<BR>5 A cricket's cry.<BR>6 Membrane, thin skin, parchment.<BR>E.<BR>झिल्ल for चिल्ल imitative sound, expressing the cricket's chirp, and ङीष् being added झिल्ली, and कन् again added झिल्लिका; also with the penultimate long झिल्लीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्ली
झिल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A cricket.<BR>2 Sunshine, light, lustre.<BR>3 The wick of a lamp.<BR>4 A cloth or rag for applying unguents, colour, &c.<BR>5 A musical instrument, cymbals.<BR>6 Membrane.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झिल्लीकण्ठ|झिल्लीकंठ|झिल्लीकण्ठः
झिल्लीकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>झिल्ली a cricket, and कण्ठ the throat; chirping as it were in the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झीरिका
झीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket: see झिरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झीरुका
झीरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket: see झिरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झु|झुः
झु<BR>r. 1st cl. (झवते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झुण्ट|झुंट|झुंटः|झुण्टः
झुण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A shrub, a bush.<BR>E.<BR>झट to be entangled, affix अच्, नुम् augment, and the vowel changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूणि|झूणिः
झूणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 A kind of betel nut.<BR>2 Heavenly annunciation of misfortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूमेरि
झूमेरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs, or modes of music personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झूष
झूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (झूषति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झॄ
झॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (भृणाति) (ष) झॄष् r. 1st cl. (झीर्य्यति)<BR>To grow old, to become infirm with age, &c. to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झोड|झोडः
झोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The betel nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ्यु
झ्यु<BR>r. 1st cl. (झ्यवते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ञ|ञः
ञ<BR>The nasal attached to the class of palatal letters, having something like the sound of N in the French word Singe, and expressed by that letter accented N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ञ|ञः
ञ<BR>m. (ञः)<BR>1 A name of ŚUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR>2 An ox.<BR>3 A heretic, an apostate.<BR>4 Singing.<BR>5 Jingling or inarticulate sound. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">Page359</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=358" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट|टं|टः
ट<BR>The 11th consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, and first of the 3rd class or cerebrals. It corresponds in sound to the letter T pronounced far back in the mouth, or as in true, and is expressed in the roman character by the accented letter T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट|टं|टः
ट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Sound, or a particular sound, like the twang of a bow strong.<BR>2 A dwarf.<BR>3 A quarter, a fourth.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A hollowed cocoanut.<BR>f. (टा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 An oath, confirming an assertion by ordeal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>टक to bind, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टक
टक<BR>(इ) टकि r. 1st and 10th cls. (टङ्कति टङ्कयति)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टक्कदेशीय|टक्कदेशीयः
टक्कदेशीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टगर|टगरः
टगर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Borax.<BR>2 Wanton play or sport.<BR>3 Wandering of the mind, confusion, perplexity.<BR>4 An object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्क|टंक|टंकं|टंकः|टङ्कः
टङ्क<BR>mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>1 A kind of elephant or wood apple. नीलकपित्थ.<BR>2 Borax.<BR>3 A spade or hoe.<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A hatchet or stone cutter's chisel.<BR>2 A sword, a scimitar, a sacrificial hatchet or knife.<BR>3 A scabbard, a sword-sheath.<BR>4 Anger, wrath.<BR>5 A weight (of silver) equal to four māṣas.<BR>6 A coin.<BR>7 Pride, arrogance.<BR>8 A cleft, a chasm.<BR>9 A peak.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 The leg.<BR>2 The edge or side of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>टकि to bind, affix अच्; or ट imitative, कै to emit sound, affix ड, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कक|टंकक|टंककः|टङ्ककः
टङ्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stamped coin, especially of silver.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to टङ्क a weight of silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ककपति|टंककपति|टङ्ककपतिः
टङ्ककपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The master of a mint or superintendent of the silver coin.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्कक, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ककशाला|टंककशाला
टङ्ककशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A mint.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्कक, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कटीक|टंकटीकः|टङ्कटीकः
टङ्कटीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्क an axe, and टीक who has, from टीक to go or get, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कण|टंकण|टंकणं|टङ्कणः
टङ्कण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Borax.<BR>2 Binding, tying.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्क to bind, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कपति|टङ्कपतिः
टङ्कपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The master of the mint.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्क a weight of silver put for a coin, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कशाला
टङ्कशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A mint.<BR>E.<BR>टङ्क see the last, and शाला a house or hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कानक|टङ्कानकः
टङ्कानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The mulberry, (Morus Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्कार|टंकार|टंकारः|टङ्कारः
टङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Surprise, wonder.<BR>2 Fame, notoriety.<BR>3 The twang of a bow string.<BR>E.<BR>टकि to bind, &c. affix आरक्; or ट twang, in the second case, कृ to make, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्ग|टंग|टंगं|टंगः|टङ्गः
टङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A spade or hoe.<BR>2 An axe.<BR>3 The leg.<BR>4 Borax.<BR>5 A weight of four māṣas.<BR>E.<BR>टकि to bind, affix अच्, क changed to गः otherwise टङ्क as above; also with ल्युट् affix, टङ्गन n. (-नं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टङ्गिनी
टङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टनी
टट्टनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>टट्ट imitative sound, and न what makes, from नी, affixes ड and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टरी
टट्टरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A joke, a jest.<BR>2 A kettle drum.<BR>3 Any musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>टट्ट imitative sound, and र what makes, from रा, with ड and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टट्टुर|टट्टुरः
टट्टुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sound of a drum.<BR>E.<BR>टट्टु imitative sound, tattoo, and र what gets or has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टल|टलः
टल<BR>r. 1st cl. (टलति)<BR>To be confused, to be disturbed by fear, anxiety, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टलन|टलनं
टलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Anxiety, perturbation.<BR>E.<BR>टल to be disturbed, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टाङ्कर|टांकर|टांकरः|टाङ्करः
टाङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blackguard, a lecher, a libertine.<BR>E.<BR>टां an oath, and कर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टार|टारः
टार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A catamite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिक
टिक<BR>(ऋ) टिकृ r. 1st cl. (टेकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिटिभक|टिटिभकः
टिटिभक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिट्टिभ|टिट्टिभः
टिट्टिभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A bird, (Parra jacana or goensis.)<BR>E.<BR>टिट्टि imitative sound, भास to utter, affix ड; also with कन् added, टिट्टिभक; also टिटिभक, टिठिभक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिण्डिश|टिण्डिशः
टिण्डिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिप
टिप<BR>r. 10th cl. (टेपयति)<BR>To direct, to send, to throw or cast: the act of throwing being considered analogous to that of sending or ordering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टिप्पनी
टिप्पनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A gloss, a comment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टीक
टीक<BR>(ऋ) टीकृ r. 1st cl. (टीकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टीका
टीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A commentary.<BR>E.<BR>टीक to go, affix अङ् and टाप्; by which the sense of the text proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टु|टुः
टु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A Proteus, a changer of shapes at will.<BR>3 KĀMA^1 or love.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260619. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टुण्ठुक
टुण्ठुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Low, little, vile.<BR>2 Cruel, harsh.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>2 A black species of catechu.<BR>3 A small bird, (Silvia sutoria.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknidhi: see टङ्गिनी.<BR>E.<BR>टुण्ठु imitative sound, and क what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेपन|टेपनं
टेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sending.<BR>2 Throwing.<BR>E.<BR>टिप to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेर
टेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टेरक|टेरकः
टेरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टौक
टौक<BR>m. (ऋ) टौकृ r. 1st cl. (टौकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ट्वल
ट्वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ट्वलति)<BR>To be disturbed or confused: see टल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठ|ठः
ठ<BR>The aspirate of the preceding letter, corresponding to Ṭh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठ|ठः
ठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>3 A circle, a globe.<BR>4 A cypher.<BR>5 An object of sense.<BR>6 A loud noise.<BR>7 An idol, a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठक्कुर|ठक्कुरः
ठक्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An idol, a deity, an object of reverence or worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ठठम्
ठठम्<BR>ind.<BR>An imitative sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड<BR>The third letter of the cerebral class of consonants, having the sound of D, pronounced far back in the head: it is often confounded in pronounciation with a hard R, or L, sounded as in the Northumbrian bur; it is written in the Roman character D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड|डः
ड<BR>m. (डः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Fear.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>4 Submarine fire.<BR>5 A kind of drum or tabor.<BR>f. (डा)<BR>1 A kind of female imp or goblin.<BR>2 A basket, &c. carried by a sling: see डलक.<BR>E.<BR>डप to collect, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डङ्गरी
डङ्गरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of gourd; also read डङ्गारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डप
डप<BR>r. 10th cl. (डापयति) (इ) डपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डम्पति डम्पयति)<BR>To collect, to accumulate, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=359" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डब
डब<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) डबि (डम्बयति)<BR>To throw, to send, to order.<BR>With वि prefixed,<BR>to deceive, to disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डभ
डभ<BR>(इ) डभि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डम्भति डम्भयति-ते)<BR>To collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम|डमः
डम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A man of a low caste, employed to clear away filth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमर|डमरं|डमरः
डमर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>1 An affray, a conflict without weapons.<BR>2 Terrifying an enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>3 Petty or predatory warfare, war carried on by detachments or by villages, one in which kings are not engaged.<BR>4 Rout, riot.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Flight, running away through fear.<BR>E.<BR>डम् imitative sound, and अर what occasions, from ऋ to go, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरु|डमरुः
डमरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A musical instrument, a sort of small drum, shaped like an hour glass, and held in one hand.<BR>2 Any thing surprising, any strange occurrence, &c.<BR>E.<BR>डम् imitative sound, ऋ to go or get, कु affix, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयन|डयनं
डयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A car or litter carried upon menś shoulders, a Palanquin, a Dūli.<BR>2 Flying in the air, the flight of a bird.<BR>E.<BR>डी to fly, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डलक|डलकं
डलक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A sling, a basket, a dūlī carried on menś shoulders by means of a stick and ropes like the beam and strings of a balance; presents of fruit, sweetmeats, &c. are usually sent in this manner; also read डल्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डहु|डहुः
डहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>A tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, affix कु, and the deriv. irr.; also with कू affix डहू, m. (-हूः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाकिनी
डाकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of female imp or evil being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डामर|डामरः
डामर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Affray, conflict without weapons, &c. see डमर.<BR>2 Rout, uproar, the bustle and the confusion of festivity or strife.<BR>3 Any surprising thing, sight or occurrence.<BR>4 A name common to six Tantras, as the Śivaḍāmara, Yogaḍāmara, Durgāḍāmara, &c.<BR>E.<BR>डमर q. v. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डालिम|डालिमः
डालिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A pomegranate: see दाडिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहल|डाहलः
डाहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a country; also Tripura: see त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहुक|डाहुकः
डाहुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>दह to consume, (disease,) उकञ् affix, the flesh being considered medicinal: the radical initial is changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिक्करी
डिक्करी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिङ्गर|डिंगर|डिंगरः|डिङ्गरः
डिङ्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Throwing, sending.<BR>2 A fat man.<BR>3 A servent, a slave.<BR>4 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>5 A low or depraved man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिम|डिंडिम|डिंडिमः|डिण्डिमः
डिण्डिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A musical instrument, a kind of small drum or tabor.<BR>2 A plant, bearing a small fruit, (Carissa carandas): see कृष्णपाक.<BR>E.<BR>डिण्डि imitative sound, a din, and म what emits, from मि, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिर|डिंडिर|डिंडिरः|डिण्डिरः
डिण्डिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone, considered to be the foam of the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिण्डिरमोदक|डिण्डिरमोदकं
डिण्डिरमोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिप
डिप<BR>r. 4th cl. (इर) डिपिर (डिप्यति) r. 6th cl. (डिपति) and r. 10th cl. (डेपयति)<BR>To throw, to cast, to send or order, to direct: see टिप.<BR>r. 10th cl. (डेपयति-ते) also (इ) डिपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डिम्पति) and (डिम्पयति-ते)<BR>To collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिब
डिब<BR>r. 10th cl. (इ) डिबि (डिम्बयति)<BR>To cast, to throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिभ
डिभ<BR>(इ) डिभि r. 1st and 10th cls. (डिम्भति and डिम्भयति-ते)<BR>To collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम|डिमः
डिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A dramatic entertainment, dramatic exhibition of battle or siege, such as the Tripuradāha, in which the destruction of the three cities of TRIPURA by ŚIVA is dramatised.<BR>E.<BR>डिम्ब affray, &c. deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्ब|डिंब|डिम्बं|डिंबः|डिम्बः
डिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 Affray, assault, conflict without weapons, mutual defiance, petty and predatory war, &c. see डमर.<BR>2 Sound or noise occasioned by terror.<BR>3 An egg.<BR>4 A chrysalis.<BR>5 The bladder.<BR>6 The spleen.<BR>7 The uterus.<BR>8 Fear, terror.<BR>9 Any young animal.<BR>10 A globe or ball.<BR>E.<BR>डी to fly, derive irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्बाहव|डिंबाहव|डिम्बाहवः
डिम्बाहव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Petty warfare, affray, skirmish, riot, &c.<BR>E.<BR>डिम्ब as above, and आहव war, battle; also डिम्बयुद्ध, and other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्बिका|डिंबिका
डिम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bubble.<BR>2 A kind of waterfly.<BR>3 A libidinous woman.<BR>E.<BR>डिम्ब the bladder, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भ|डिंभ|डिंभः|डिम्भः
डिम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Any young animal.<BR>2 A fool, an idiot, a blockhead.<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>An infant.<BR>E.<BR>डिभि to collect, affix अच्; कन् being added; also डिम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्भचक्र|डिम्भचक्रं
डिम्भचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>A diagram for telling fortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डी
डी<BR>(ङ) डीङ् r. 1st and 4th cls. (डयते डीयते)<BR>1 To fly, to pass through the air.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>To fly down, to alight.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To fly up, to soar.<BR>With परि,<BR>To fly round.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To fly well or swiftly.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To fly well or in flocks.<BR>With सम् and उत्,<BR>To fly up by degrees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीन|डीनं
डीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flying, the flight of a bird.<BR>E.<BR>डी to fly, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीनडीनक|डीनडीनकं
डीनडीनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Flying reiteratedly.<BR>E.<BR>डीन flying, reduplicated, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीनावडीन|डीनावडीनं
डीनावडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Flying up and down.<BR>2 Flying ill.<BR>E.<BR>डीन, and अवडीन alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डु|डुण्डुः
डुण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A kind of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डुभ|डुंडुभ|डुंडुभः|डुण्डुभः
डुण्डुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A kind of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR>E.<BR>डुण्डु, and भ from भा to shine or resemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुण्डुल|डुंडुलः|डुण्डुलः
डुण्डुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुन्दुक|डुंदुकः|डुन्दुकः
डुन्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gallinule: see डाहुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलि|डुलिः
डुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 A small turtle.<BR>2 A female turtle: see दुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलिका
डुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird resembling a wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोर|डोरं|डोरः
डोर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fillet of thread or cord tied round the arm or wrist; it is also applied to the string tying a packet or parcel; also with कन added डोरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ<BR>The aspirate of the preceding letter corresponding to Ḍh: the use of this as an initial letter is very limited, and several of the words in which it occurs can scarely be regarded as pure Sanscrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढ|ढः
ढ<BR>m. (ढः)<BR>1 A large drum.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>3 A dog's tail.<BR>4 Sound.<BR>5 A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्क|ढक्कः
ढक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>1 A city or district, Dhacca or Dacca.<BR>2 Coveting, disappearance.<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A large or double drum, a Ḍhāk.<BR>E.<BR>ढक् imitative sound, and क what utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्कारी
ढक्कारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The goddess TĀRIṆĪ, a Tāntrika form of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढामरा
ढामरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढाल|ढालं
ढाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढालिन्
ढालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A warrior armed with a shield, a shield-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुढ
ढुढ<BR>(इ) ढढि Sautra root, (ढुण्ढति)<BR>To search, to seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=360" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढन|ढुंढनं
ढुण्ढन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Seeking, investigating.<BR>E.<BR>ढुढि to search, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढि|ढुंढि|ढुंढिः|ढुण्ढिः
ढुण्ढि<BR>m. (-ण्ढिः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>ढुढि to seek, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुण्ढित
ढुण्ढित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sought, inquired.<BR>E.<BR>ढुढि to seek, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढोल|ढोलः
ढोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Dhol or large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौक
ढौक<BR>(ऋ) ढौकृ r. 1st cl. (ढौकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौकन|ढौकनं
ढौकन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>ढौक to go, ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण<BR>The nasal Ṇ belonging to the third or cerebral class of consonants; in derivation and inflection this is usually changed to न or the dental N, and hence the derivatives from the following radicals occur under that letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ण|णः
ण<BR>m. (णः)<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>2 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 Vindudeva, said to be a Jaina deity.<BR>5 An ornament.<BR>6 A water or summer house.<BR>7 One without good qualities.<BR>8 A kind of sound, the sound of negation.<BR>9 Gift, giving.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णक्ष
णक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (नक्षति, or with प्र prefixed प्रणक्षति)<BR>To go, to move, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णख
णख<BR>r. 1st cl. (नखति) also (इ) णखि r. 1st cl. (नंखति)<BR>To go, to move; also नख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णट
णट<BR>r. 1st cl. (नटति प्रणटति)<BR>1 To dance.<BR>2 To dance as an actor, to gesticulate, to act; also नट.<BR>3 To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णद
णद<BR>r. 1st cl. (नदति प्रणदति)<BR>To sound inarticulately, to roar as a river or a wild beast, to ring as a bell, &c.<BR>r. 10th cl. (नादयति)<BR>1 To speak or tell, to shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णभ
णभ<BR>r. 1st cl. (नभते प्रणभते) 4th cl. (नभ्यति) and 9th cl. (नभ्नाति)<BR>1 To kill, to injure.<BR>2 To be annihilated, to cease to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णम
णम<BR>r. 1st cl. (नमति)<BR>1 To salute with reverence or respect.<BR>2 To bow or bend, to bow down in homage or worship.<BR>3 To sound.<BR>With अव or आङ् or सम् prefixed,<BR>To bend down, to decline.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To bow, to salute.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To lift up, to raise, to make straight or erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णय
णय<BR>r. 1st cl. (नयते प्रणयते)<BR>1 To go, to move or approach.<BR>2 To preserve, to protect, to defend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णर्द|णर्द्द
णर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (नर्दति प्रणर्दति)<BR>To sound; also नर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णल
णल<BR>r. 1st cl. (नलति प्रणलति)<BR>1 To smell.<BR>2 To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णश
णश<BR>r. 4th cl. (ऊ) णशू (नश्यति)<BR>To disappear, to cease to be, to perish, to be annihilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णस
णस<BR>r. 1st cl. (नसते प्रणसते)<BR>1 To be crooked, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>2 To bend, to make curved or crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णह
णह<BR>r. 4th cl. (औ) औनह (नह्यति नह्यते)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR>With सभ prefixed,<BR>(सन्नाहति)<BR>To arm, to put on mail or military accoutrements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णास
णास<BR>(ऋ) णासृ r. 1st cl. (नासते प्रणासते)<BR>To sound in a particular manner, to snore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिक्ष
णिक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (निक्षति प्रणिक्षति)<BR>To kill: the change of the ण after a preposition is optional in the derivatives of this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिज
णिज<BR>(इ) णिजि r. 2nd cl. (निंक्ते प्रणिंक्ते)<BR>To cleanse.<BR>(औ, इर) औणिजिर r. 3rd cl. (नेनेक्ति नेनिक्ते)<BR>1 To nurture, to cherish or maintain.<BR>2 To purify, to cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिद
णिद<BR>(इ) णिदि r. 1st cl. (निन्दति-ते प्रणिन्दति) also (ऋ) णिदृ r. 1st cl. (नेदति-ते प्रणेदति)<BR>1 To abuse, to censure, to reproach, to reprove or revile, to despise or condemn, &c. (The second root means also)<BR>2 To approach, to come near. The change of ण after a preposition is optional in the derivatives of the first of these roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिल
णिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (निलति)<BR>1 To misunderstand, to comprehend ill or imperfectly.<BR>2 To be thick or impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिव
णिव<BR>(इ) णिवि r. 1st cl. (निन्वति प्रणिन्वति)<BR>To wet, to moisten, to sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिश
णिश<BR>r. 1st cl. (नेशति प्रणेशति)<BR>To meditate profoundly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिष
णिष<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) णिषु (नेषति)<BR>To sprinkle, to shed as water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णिस
णिस<BR>(इ) णिसि r. 2nd cl. (निंस्ते प्रणिंस्ते)<BR>To kiss: the change of ण after a preposition is optional in the derivatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णी
णी<BR>(ञ) णीञ् r. 1st cl. (नयति-ते)<BR>1 To conduct, to drive or guide, to cause progressive conveyance.<BR>2 To obtain, to get.<BR>The root is inflected as the deponent verb, implying.<BR>1 Instruction, as नयते शास्त्रे he instructs in the Śāstra;<BR>2 Worshipping, विष्णुंनयते he worships VIṢṆU;<BR>also with prepositions in the sense of;<BR>1 Paying, भृत्यमुपनयते he pays the hire;<BR>2 Paying as a debt, ऋणम्विनयते he discharges the debt;<BR>3 Casting or lifting up, दण्डमुन्नयते he lifts up the stick;<BR>4 Giving, द्रव्यम्बिनयते he gives the things; and<BR>5 Brahmanical Investiture, पुत्त्रमुपनयते he invests his son with the thread:<BR>it is also deponent, governing an incorporeal object existing in the agent, as<BR>क्रोधम्विनयते<BR>he suppresses wrath;<BR>if the object is not in the agent the verb is active, as<BR>गुरोःक्रोधम्विनयति^1<BR>he appeases his teacher's anger;<BR>as also if the object is corporal,<BR>as गण्डं विनयति he turns away the cheek.<BR>The root occurs with many prefixes, and in a great variety of meanings;<BR>.²1 With अनु,<BR>a To ask, to entreat. .²b To make like or resembling. .²c To favour.<BR>.²2 With अप,<BR>a To take away, to remove. .²b To attract.<BR>.²3 With अभि,<BR>a To indicate by signs. .²b To be kind or civil to.<BR>.²4 With आङ्,<BR>To bring.<BR>.²5 With उत्,<BR>To raise up.<BR>.²6 With उप,<BR>To approach, to go near to, (see also above.)<BR>.²7 With दुर्,<BR>To act or behave wickedly.<BR>.²8 With निर्,<BR>a To get or obtain. .²b To ascertain, to determine.<BR>.²9 With परि,<BR>a To marry. .²b To take cognizance of.<BR>.²10 With प्र,<BR>a To punish. .²b To love.<BR>.²11 With वि,<BR>a To take away, to make remote or distant. .²b To be humble or modest.<BR>.²12 With वि and अप,<BR>To remove, to dispel, to disperse.<BR>.²13 With वि and निर्,<BR>To decide by law.<BR>.²14 With सम्,<BR>a To collect. .²b To discharge.<BR>.²15 With सम् and अनु,<BR>To intreat.<BR>.²16 With सम and आङ्,<BR>To assemble, to collect, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: ktoDam -> kroDam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णील
णील<BR>r. 1st cl. (नीलति प्रणीलति)<BR>1 To be blue.<BR>2 To make or dye blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णीव
णीव<BR>r. 1st cl. (नीवति प्रणीबति)<BR>To be large or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णु
णु<BR>r. 3rd cl. (नौति प्रणौति)<BR>To praise.<BR>With आङ् prefixed<BR>(आनुते)<BR>To utter a cry of regret.<BR>r. 6th cl. (नवति)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णुद
णुद<BR>r. 6th cl. (औ) औणुद (नुदति नुदते)<BR>1 To cast, to command, to direct, to throw or send; the act of ordering being considered analogous to that of throwing.<BR>2 To go or proceed.<BR>With अप,<BR>To remove.<BR>With निर्,<BR>1 To throw out.<BR>2 To confess, to acknowledge.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be happy.<BR>With सं in the causal<BR>To drive, (as horses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णू
णू<BR>r. 6th cl. (नुवति)<BR>To praise; also ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णेद
णेद<BR>(ऋ) णेदृ r. 1st cl. (नेदति-ते)<BR>1 To censure, to despise.<BR>2 To approach or come near: see णिद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णेष
णेष<BR>(ऋ) णेषृ r. 1st cl. (नेषते)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=361" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त<BR>The first consonant of the fourth or dental class, corresponding to the letter T, in tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त|तं|तः
त<BR>m. (तः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 Nectar, the food of the immortals.<BR>3 An outcaste, a barbarian or Mleccha.<BR>4 The flank, the hip or haunch.<BR>5 A tail.<BR>6 The womb.<BR>7 A wicked man.<BR>8 A tree.<BR>9 A jewel.<BR>10 A Buddha.<BR>n. (तं)<BR>1 Passing, crossing.<BR>2 Virtue, sanctity.<BR>E.<BR>तृ to cross, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक<BR>r. 1st cl. (तकति)<BR>1 To laugh at or deride.<BR>2 To bear.<BR>With वि and अति prefixed, and implying reciprocity<BR>(ष्यतितकते)<BR>To retort a laugh.<BR>(इ) तकि r. 1st cl. (तङ्कति)<BR>To live in distress, to be in poverty or pain.<BR>(तंकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>That.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, कन् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकिल|तकिलः
तकिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or cheat.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A medicament, a drug.<BR>E.<BR>तक to deride, affix इलच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्य|तक्यः
तक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>1 Laughable, ridiculous.<BR>2 To be borne or endured.<BR>E.<BR>तक to laugh, यत् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्र|तक्रं
तक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>Buttermilk with a fourth part water.<BR>E.<BR>तक to bear (sickness), Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्रकूर्च्चिका|तक्रकूर्चिका
तक्रकूर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Inspissated buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>तक्र, and कूर्च्चिका inspissated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्रमांस|तक्रमांसं
तक्रमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Meat fried with ghee, turmeric and asafœtida, &c. eaten with buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>तक्र, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्राट|तक्राटः
तक्राट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A churning-stick.<BR>E.<BR>तक्र buttermilk, and अट what goes or is, (from it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष
तक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (तक्षति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To skin or peel.<BR>(ऊ) तक्षू r. 1st cl. (तक्ष्णोति)<BR>To pare, to plane, to make thin, to cut off, to chip or slice;<BR>used in any other sense, this root takes the regular form only, whether simple or compound, as with सम् prefixed,<BR>To censure, (सन्तक्षति,) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षक|तक्षकः
तक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A carpenter.<BR>2 The Sūtradhāra, the manager and chief actor in the prelude of a drama.<BR>3 One of the principal Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR>4 The divine artist, VIŚVAKARMA.<BR>5 The name of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष to chip, to peel or plane, &c. affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षण|तक्षणं
तक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Paring, peeling, planing, &c.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A carpenter's adze.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष to plane or pare, affix ल्युट् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षन्
तक्षन्<BR>m. (-क्षा)<BR>A carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष to pare, Uṇādi affix कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षशिला
तक्षशिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The name of a city, the Taxila of Ptolemy, in the Punjab.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष paring, शिला stone, built of hewn stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तग
तग<BR>(इ) तगि r. 1st cl. (तंगति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To quake, to shake or tremble.<BR>3 To trip, to stumble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगर|तगरं|तगरः
तगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A shrub, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>2 A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>3 Another plant, commonly Tagaramūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगरपादिका
तगरपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant; also Tagaramūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तङ्क|तंक|तंकः|तङ्कः
तङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 An axe, a crow, a stonecutter's chisel: see तङ्क.<BR>2 Grief upon separation from a beloved object.<BR>3 Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>तकि to be in distress, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तज्ज
तज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Immediate, instantaneous.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, (that moment,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्च
तञ्च<BR>(उ) तञ्चु r. 1st cl. (तञ्चति)<BR>To go.<BR>(ऊ) तञ्चू r. 7th cl. (तनक्ति)<BR>To shrink or contract; also तञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तञ्ज
तञ्ज<BR>(उ) तञ्जू r. 7th cl. (तनक्ति)<BR>To shrink or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट|तटं|तटः
तट<BR>r. 1st cl. (तटति)<BR>To be elevated or high, to rise.<BR>r. 10th cl. (ताटयति)<BR>To beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट|तटं|तटः
तट<BR>mfn. sub. (-टः-टा-टी-टं)<BR>A shore or bank.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A field.<BR>E.<BR>तट to rise or be high, affix अच्, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटस्थ|तटस्थं|तटस्थः
तटस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Indifferent, alien, neuter.<BR>2 Situated on the bank or shore.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>An indifferent person, one neither a friend nor a foe.<BR>n. (-स्थं)<BR>That property which is distinct from the nature of any thing, yet is the faculty by which it is known: in other words, spiritual essence unconnected with bodily wants or passions.<BR>E.<BR>तट a bank, a height, and स्थ who stands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाक|तटाकं|तटाकः
तटाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pond deep enough for the lotus and other aquatic flowers.<BR>E.<BR>तट a bank, and अक to go, affix अच्; also तडाक; also ताटाक and तटीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटिनी
तटिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>तट a bank, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तड
तड<BR>r. 10th cl. (ताडयति)<BR>1 To beat, to strike.<BR>2 To shine:<BR>(इ) तडि r. 1st cl. (तण्डते)<BR>To strike or beat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडग|तडगः
तडग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A pond, a tank: see तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाक|तडाकः
तडाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pond or pool, one deep enough for the lotus, &c.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bank, a shore.<BR>2 A blow.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, Uṇādi affix आक; also तटाक and तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाग|तडागं|तडागः
तडाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A pond, a pool, deep enough for the growth of the lotus, &c. see the preceding.<BR>2 A trap for catching deer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, affix आग, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाघात|तडाघातः
तडाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A blow from an elephant's uplifted trunk.<BR>E.<BR>तडा a beating, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्
तडित्<BR>f. (-डित्)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>तड to strike or beat, Uṇādi affix इति; striking the earth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्वत्|तडित्वन्त्
तडित्वत्<BR>mfn. (-त्वान्-त्वती-त्वत्)<BR>Lightening, emitting lightning, flashing.<BR>m. (-त्वान्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>तडित्, lightning, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडिल्लता
तडिल्लता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Forked lightning.<BR>E.<BR>तडित्, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डक|तंडक|तंडकः|तण्डकः
तण्डक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Complete performance or preparation.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wag-tail.<BR>2 Froth, foam.<BR>3 The trunk of a tree.<BR>4 The upright post of a house.<BR>5 A compound word.<BR>6 A juggler, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>तडि to beat or kill, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डु|तण्डुः
तण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>One of ŚIVA'S doorkeepers, and one of the original teachers of the arts of dancing and mimicry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुरीण|तंडुरीणः|तण्डुरीणः
तण्डुरीण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A worm, an insect.<BR>2 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>3 The water in which rice has been soaked or steeped.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल rice, &c. ख affix, and ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुल|तंडुल|तंडुलः|तण्डुलः
तण्डुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Grain after threshing and winnowing, especially rice.<BR>2 A vermifuge plant: see विडङ्ग.<BR>3 A potherb, a sort of Amaranth, (A. polygonoides.)<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, Uṇādi affix उल, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलाम्बु
तण्डुलाम्बु<BR>f. (-म्बुः)<BR>Rice water or gruel.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीक|तण्डुलीकः
तण्डुलीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of Amaranth.<BR>E.<BR>ईकन् added to the preceding; also तण्डुलीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलीय|तण्डुलीयः
तण्डुलीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A kind of Amaranth, (A. polygonoides.)<BR>2 Viraṅga, a vermifuge.<BR>3 A mineral, iron pyrites.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल grain, (to which the seeds, &c. are compared,) and छ affix; also तण्डुलीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलु|तण्डुलुः
तण्डुलु<BR>f. (-लुः)<BR>A plant of which the seeds are used as a vermifuge: see विडङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>तडि to beat, affix उलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=362" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलेर|तण्डुलेरः
तण्डुलेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of Amaranth: see तण्डुलीय, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल, and एरक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलोदक|तण्डुलोदकं
तण्डुलोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water in which rice has been boiled, rice gruel.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तण्डुलौघ|तण्डुलौघः
तण्डुलौघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A prickly sort of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR>2 A heap of grain.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डुल grain, &c. or (as derived from तडि to beat, to tear,) a thorn, ओघ a heap or quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्
तत्<BR>ind.<BR>Therefore, thence, the consequent or correlative to यत्.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread or extend, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततःप्रभृति
ततःप्रभृति<BR>ind.<BR>Thenceforth.<BR>E.<BR>ततस्, and प्रभृति the rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread, diffused, expanded.<BR>2 Stretched, extended.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Any stringed musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, &c. क्त affix, or Uṇādi affix तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततचिह्न
ततचिह्न<BR>mfn. (-ह्नः-ह्ना-ह्नं)<BR>Distinctly marked.<BR>E.<BR>तत, and चिह्न a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततपत्री
ततपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The plantain tree.<BR>E.<BR>तत spread, and पत्री a leaf, broad-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम|ततमः
ततम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>That one, (of many.)<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, डतमच् affix of the superlative degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततर|ततरः
ततर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>That one, (of two.)<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, and डतरच् affix of the comparative degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्
ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Therefore, thence, consequently.<BR>2 From that or then.<BR>3 Then, how, (asking.)<BR>4 Then, further, after that, (in continuation.)<BR>5 Afterwards, subsequently.<BR>6 Thither, there.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, affix तसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्ततस्
ततस्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Hither and thither.<BR>2 Then, after that, what next; (asking impatiently.)<BR>E.<BR>ततस् reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्त्य|ततस्त्यं
ततस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>Of or relating to that, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ततस् as above, त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति<BR>mfn. plu. (ततयः ततयः ततीनि)<BR>So many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A line, a row or range.<BR>2 A number, a crowd.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कर
तत्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Obeying, serving, a servant.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्काल|तत्कालः
तत्काल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Present time, time being, or the time when an, act occurs.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्कालधी
तत्कालधी<BR>m. (-धीः)<BR>A man wise or intelligent for the time being, one having presence of mind, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तत्काल time being, and धी understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्रिय|तत्क्रियः
तत्क्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Working without hire or wages.<BR>E.<BR>तत् thence, क्रिया business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्क्षण|तत्क्षणः
तत्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Time present, time being.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, and क्षण moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्व|तत्त्वं
तत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>1 Essential nature, the real nature of the human soul, considered as one and the same with the divine spirit animating the universe: the philosophical etymology of this word best explains its meaning, तद् that, that divine being, and त्व thou, that very God art thou.<BR>2 The Supreme Being, or BRAHMA.<BR>3 Truth, reality, substance, opposed to what is illusory or fallacious.<BR>4 An element or elementary property, differently enumerated in different systems, from the three which are the same with the three Guṇas, to twenty-seven, which include the elements, organs, faculties, matter, spirit, life, and God.<BR>5 A first principle, an axiom.<BR>6 Mind, intellect.<BR>7 Slow time in music.<BR>8 A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>as above, or तद that, thence, &c. affix त्व; the word is properly, therefore, written तत्त्व, but in books one त is commonly rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वज्ञान|तत्त्वज्ञानं
तत्त्वज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge of divine truth.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व as above, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वतस्
तत्त्वतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Truly, accurately, fully.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वन्यास|तत्त्वन्यासः
तत्त्वन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Touching different parts of the body in the worship of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व, and न्यास gesticulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वविद्
तत्त्वविद्<BR>mfn. (-वित्)<BR>Knowing the truth, knowing things as they are.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वावबोध
तत्त्वावबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Knowledge of spirit.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व, and अवबोध ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वाभियोग|तत्त्वाभियोगः
तत्त्वाभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A positive charge or declaration.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्व, and अभियोग accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पर|तत्परः
तत्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Diligent, attending to any thing closely and anxiously.<BR>2 Belonging to a principal object or intent of.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The thirtieth part of the time of the twinkling of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, पर addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्परायण|तत्परायणः
तत्परायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Attached or addicted to some particular thing or person.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, परायण attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पूर्व्व|तत्पूर्व
तत्पूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>Prior, former.<BR>E.<BR>तत्, and पूर्व्व before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्पुरुष|तत्पुरुषः
तत्पुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 That or a certain person.<BR>2 A form of composition, (in Grammar,) usually consisting of two nouns, the first of which was in any case except the nominative or vocative; sometimes the inflection of the case is retained.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, and पुरुष man or person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्फल|तत्फलः
तत्फल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Resulting from any particular act, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The white-water lily.<BR>3 A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र<BR>(इ) तत्रि r. 10th cl. (तन्त्रयति)<BR>1 To spread, to extend or expand.<BR>2 To nourish or support a family, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र<BR>ind.<BR>There, therein, the relative to अत्र.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, त्रल् affix, in lieu of the proper seventh case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रत्य|तत्रत्यः
तत्रत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Produced there or in a certain place.<BR>E.<BR>तत्र, and त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रभवत्|तत्रभवन्त्
तत्रभवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Venerable, respectable, reverend.<BR>E.<BR>तत्र therein, (in all things,) भवत् preeminent: see अत्रभवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्व|तत्वं
तत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>See तत्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा<BR>ind.<BR>1 So, like, correlative to यथा as, &c.<BR>2 Thus, (implying certainty.)<BR>3 So, so be it, (implying assent or promise.)<BR>4 Thus, then, therefore, (or reply.)<BR>5 And, so, in (conjunction.)<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, थाल affix, implying manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथागत|तथागतः
तथागत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Jina or Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>तथा thus, (what really is,) and गत known, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाच
तथाच<BR>ind.<BR>And so, thus, even so.<BR>E.<BR>तथा, with च and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथात्व|तथात्वं
तथात्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Being so; the case or circumstances being admitted to be as stated.<BR>E.<BR>तथा, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथापि
तथापि<BR>ind.<BR>Nevertheless, yet, even.<BR>E.<BR>तथा, and अपि even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाविध
तथाविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of such a sort or kind.<BR>E.<BR>तथा, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाराज|तथाराजः
तथाराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Jina or Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथैव
तथैव<BR>ind.<BR>So, even so, in the same manner.<BR>E.<BR>तथा, and एव thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>True.<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Truth.<BR>E.<BR>तथा thus, (what, is really so,) and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=363" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद्<BR>Relative or third personal pronoun, (सः सा तद्)<BR>He, she, it, that man, that woman, that thing.<BR>E.<BR>तन to extend or spread, Uṇādi affix अदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद
तद<BR>(इ) तदि r. 1st cl. (तन्दते)<BR>To be content or happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदतिपात
तदतिपात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Transgressing, going beyond the bounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदनन्तर
तदनन्तर<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Next, afterwards.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, अनन्तर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदन्त|तदंत
तदन्त<BR>n. adv. (-न्तं)<BR>To that end, just so far.<BR>E.<BR>तद, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्थ
तदर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 On that account, with that object.<BR>2 Having such a meaning.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदर्पण
तदर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A thing returned.<BR>2 Delivering any article.<BR>E.<BR>तद, and अर्पण delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदा
तदा<BR>ind.<BR>Then, at that time.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, दाच affix, implying time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदात्व|तदात्वं
तदात्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Time being, time present.<BR>E.<BR>तदा then, त्व affix of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानीम्
तदानीम्<BR>ind.<BR>Then, at that time.<BR>E.<BR>तद that, दानीम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदाप्रभृति
तदाप्रभृति<BR>ind.<BR>Thenceforward.<BR>E.<BR>तदा, and प्रभृति the rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदामुख|तदामुखं
तदामुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Commencement, beginning.<BR>E.<BR>तदा, and मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीय
तदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>That, that person, that thing.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्दिनम्
तद्दिनम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 In the course of the day.<BR>2 Day by day.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>On a certain day.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धन|तद्धनः
तद्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Miserly, niggardly.<BR>E.<BR>तत् thence, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वत्|तद्वन्त्
तद्वत्<BR>ind.<BR>So, in like manner, the correlative to यद्वत् as.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वला
तद्वला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of arrow.<BR>E.<BR>तत् thence, वल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्विध
तद्विध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>In that manner, in such a manner, of such a kind or sort.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and विध way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्धित|तद्धितः
तद्धित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A derivative noun, as a patronymic or attributive of various kinds, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The formation of such nouns.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, (original noun,) हित what relates to or suits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन|तनः
तन<BR>(उ) तनु r. 8th cl. (तनोति-तनुते)<BR>To expand, to spread, to extend, to diffuse, to dilate, &c. physically or morally.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तनति तानयति)<BR>1 To confide, to believe or have faith in.<BR>2 To aid, to assist.<BR>3 To be harmless.<BR>4 To sound.<BR>5 To pain or afflict with disease.<BR>6 (With a preposition,) To lengthen, to stretch, to expand, &c. as in the 8th cl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनय|तनयः
तनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A male descendant.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 A plant: see चक्रकुल्या.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, (to extend the family or name,) कयन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिष्ठ|तनिष्ठः
तनिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Smaller, less.<BR>2 Minute, delicate, small.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनीयस्
तनीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Smallest, least.<BR>2 Very small or delicate, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तुनु, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः or न्वी or नूः-नु)<BR>1 Small, minute.<BR>2 Delicate, fine, but with interstices.<BR>3 Thin, slender, emaciated.<BR>4 Little.<BR>f. (-नुः-नूः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 The skin.<BR>f. (नुः)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 Point of conjunction, or sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR>f. (-न्वी)<BR>1 A delicate or slender woman.<BR>2 A stanza of four lines, and twenty-four syllables in each: a variety of the Saṃkṛti metre.<BR>E.<BR>तन to stretch or spread, Uṇādi affix उ; also तनू and तनुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुकूप|तनुकूपः
तनुकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A pore of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुच्छद्
तनुच्छद्<BR>mfn. (-छत्)<BR>Covering (the body,) clothing, protecting.<BR>f. (-छत्)<BR>1 Armour.<BR>2 Attire.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and छद to cover, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुज|तनुजः
तनुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A son.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>तनु body, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्र|तनुत्रं
तनुत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>तनु the body, and त्र what preserves; also तनुत्राण (-णं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्रवत्|तनुत्रवन्त्
तनुत्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Armed, defended.<BR>E.<BR>तनुत्र, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुत्याग
तनुत्याग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Niggardly, sparing, letting little go or be spent.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Quitting the body, death.<BR>E.<BR>तवु little or the body, त्याग parting with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुभस्त्रा
तनुभस्त्रा<BR>f. (-स्त्रा)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>तनु the body, and भस्वा a bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमत्|तनुमन्त्
तनुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Embodied, corporeal.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुमध्या
तनुमध्या<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>1 A woman with a slender or elegant waist.<BR>2 A species of the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरस|तनुरसः
तनुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Perspiration, sweat.<BR>E.<BR>तनु the body, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुरुह|तनुरुहं
तनुरुह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The hair or down of the body.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and रुह what grows: also with the final consonant. तनुरुह् n. (-रुट्)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुल|तनुलः
तनुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Spread, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>तनु to spread, उलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवात|तनुवातः
तनुवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A division of hell.<BR>E.<BR>तनु thin, small, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवार
तनुवार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Armour.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, वृ to defend, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुवारभस
तनुवारभस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A warrior, a man in armour.<BR>E.<BR>तनुवार, and भस who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुव्रण|तनुव्रणः
तनुव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A pimple, a pustule, a boil.<BR>E.<BR>तनु slight, and व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्
तनुस्<BR>n. (-नुः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>तन to stretch, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुसञ्चारिणी|तनुसंचारिणी
तनुसञ्चारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A young woman, a girl, one of ten years old.<BR>E.<BR>तनु the body, सञ्चारिणी who makes perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनू
तनू<BR>f. (-नूः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>तन to stretch, affix ऊः see तनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकृत|तनूकृतः
तनूकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pared, made delicate or thin.<BR>E.<BR>तनु thin, कृत made, and उ rendered long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूज|तनूजः
तनूज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A son.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>तनू, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूजनि
तनूजनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>तनू, and जनि birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनून|तनूनः
तनून<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>the wind.<BR>E.<BR>तनु body, ऊन defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनप|तनूनपं
तनूनप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Clarified butter or ghee.<BR>E.<BR>तनु the body, and ऊन deficiency, thinness, spareness of body, and प what cherishes; what fattens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूनपाद्
तनूनपाद्<BR>m. (-पाद् or पात्)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>तनूनप ghee, and अद् who eats, from अद with विच् affix, or तनू the body, न negative, and पा to preserve, deriv. irr. destroying other bodies, or consuming its own support or fuel, and ceasing to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूरुह|तनूरुहं|तनूरुहः
तनूरुह<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>1 The hair of the body.<BR>2 The wing of a bird.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>तनु or तनू the body, and रुह what grows or rises, from रुह with क affix; also तनुरुह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूह्रद|तनूह्रदः
तनूह्रद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The anus, the rectum.<BR>E.<BR>तनू the body, and ह्रद a deep place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्ति|तंतिः|तन्तिः
तन्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Expansion, extension.<BR>E.<BR>तन to stretch, affix क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तु|तंतु|तंतुः|तन्तुः
तन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 A thread.<BR>2 A shark.<BR>3 Offspring, race, descendants.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread or stretch, Uṇādi affix तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=364" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुक|तंतुक|तंतुकः|तन्तुकः
तन्तुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Mustard seed.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A vein or any tubular vessel: see तन्तुभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकाष्ठ|तंतुकाष्ठ|तन्तुकाष्ठं
तन्तुकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A piece of fibrous wood, or a brush used by weavers for cleaning the threads of the woof.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a weaver's thread, and काष्ठ a woof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुकीट|तंतुकीट|तन्तुकीटः
तन्तुकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A silk worm.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुण|तंतुणः|तन्तुणः
तन्तुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A shark.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, तुण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनाग|तंतुनाग|तन्तुनागः
तन्तुनाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A shark.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु, and नाग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुनिर्यास|तंतुनिर्यास|तन्तुनिर्यासः|तन्तुनिर्य्यास
तन्तुनिर्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A palmyra tree.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु thread, and निर्यास exudation, alluding to its stringy or adhesive nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुपर्व्वन्|तन्तुपर्वन्
तन्तुपर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>The full moon of Śrāvaṇa, when KṚṢṆA is invested with the Brahmanical cord.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु, and पर्व्वन् a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुभ|तंतुभ|तन्तुभः
तन्तुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Mustard seed, (Sinapis dichotoma); also sometimes तन्तुका.<BR>2 A calf.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and भा to shine, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुर|तंतुर|तंतुरं|तन्तुरं
तन्तुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुल|तंतुल|तंतुलं|तन्तुलं
तन्तुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The filaments or fibrous root of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and ल what has; also with र, तन्तुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाप|तंतुवाप|तन्तुवापः
तन्तुवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>2 A loom.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, वप to weave, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुवाय|तंतुवाय|तन्तुवायः
तन्तुवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>2 A spider.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, वे to weave, अण् affix; also तन्त्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुविग्रहा|तंतुविग्रहा
तन्तुविग्रहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The banana or plantain.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and विग्रह a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुशाला|तंतुशाला
तन्तुशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A weaver's shop.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु weaving, and शाला a house or hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसन्तत|तन्तुसंतत|तंतुसंतत|तन्तुसन्ततं
तन्तुसन्तत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Wove cloth.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and सन्तत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्तुसार|तंतुसार|तन्तुसारः
तन्तुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The betel-nut^1 tree; also तन्तुसारक.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, and सार pith; having a stringy pith.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्र|तंत्र|तंत्रं|तन्त्रं
तन्त्र<BR>mfn. (न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>Dependant, subservient.<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>1 Any string or rope.<BR>2 The wire or string of a lute.<BR>3 Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>4 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum): see गूडुची.<BR>5 The name of a river.<BR>6 A young woman.<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 A Tantra, a religious treatise teaching peculiar and mystical formulæ and rites for the worship of the deities, or the attainment of superhuman power: it is mostly in the form of a dialogue between ŚIVA and DURGĀ, who are the peculiar gods of the Tāntrikas: there is a great number of these works, and their authority, in many parts of India, seems to have, in a great measure, superseded that of the Vedas: according to one account, a Tantra comprises five subjects, the creation and destruction of the world, the worship of the gods, the attainment of all objects, magical rites for the acquirement of six (superhuman) faculties, and four modes of union with spirit by meditation; a variety of subjects are, however, introduced into many of them, whilst some are limited to a single topic, as the mode of breathing in certain rites, the language of birds, beasts, &c.<BR>2 A branch of the Vedas, that which teaches Mantras or mystical and magical formula.<BR>3 Demonstration, clear and right conclusion.<BR>4 Raiment, vesture.<BR>5 A medicament, a drug.<BR>6 A principal medicament, or perhaps a charm, considered as producing medicinal effects.<BR>7 Providing for a family.<BR>8 A cause, a motive.<BR>9 Cause common to two or more results; the instruments or means of more than one effect.<BR>10 Necessary or indispensable act or provision; the right way of doing any thing.<BR>11 Chief, principal.<BR>12 A royal retinue, a court, a train.<BR>13 An army.<BR>14 A royal property; that of providing for the security and prosperity of the kingdom.<BR>15 A realm, a country.<BR>16 A thread.<BR>17 Subservience, service, dependance.<BR>18 Oath or ordeal.<BR>19 Decorations, hanging with trophies, garlands, &c.<BR>20 Heap, multitude.<BR>21 Wealth.<BR>22 A house.<BR>23 An implement of weaving, a loom.<BR>24 Happiness, felicity.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread or extend, affix ष्ट्रन्; or तत्रि to spread, to support a family, &c. affix क, fem. affix ङीप्; or तत्त्र with ई Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रक|तंत्रक|तन्त्रकं|तंत्रकः|तन्त्रकः
तन्त्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>New and unbleached cloth.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र the loom, and कन् affix, recently from the loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रकाष्ठ|तंत्रकाष्ठ|तन्त्रकाष्ठं
तन्त्रकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A fibrous stick for cleaning the woof, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र weaving, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रता|तंत्रता
तन्त्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Dependance, subservience.<BR>2 The quality or character of a Tantra.<BR>3 Comprehending several rites in one, performance of one ceremony or penance in lieu of a number.<BR>E.<BR>तत्त्र, and तल् added; also with त्व, तन्त्रत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवाप|तंत्रवाप|तन्त्रवापः
तन्त्रवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A weaver.<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A loom.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र a thread, and वप to weave, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रवाय|तंत्रवाय|तन्त्रवायः
तन्त्रवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>2 A spider.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र a thread, a web, and वे to spin or weave, affix घञ्; also तन्त्रवाप, and sometimes तन्द्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिका
तन्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, Guricha.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तन्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिन्|तंत्रिन्
तन्त्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>1 Spun, wove, made of threads.<BR>2 Chorded, having chords or wires, (as an instrument.)<BR>3 A musician.<BR>4 Having a Tantra, following one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्त्रिपालक|तन्त्रिपालकः
तन्त्रिपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of JAYADRATHA.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्रि (derived from तन्त्र any army, with इनि affix,) a general, and पालक who cherishes or aids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रवाय|तन्द्रवायः
तन्द्रवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A weaver: see तन्त्रवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रा|तंद्रा
तन्द्रा<BR>f. (-न्द्रा)<BR>1 Lassitude, exhaustion, weariness, syncope.<BR>2 Sleepiness, sluggishness.<BR>E.<BR>तन्द्रि a Sautra root, to be weary, affixes क and टाप्; also with क्तिन् affix तन्द्रि. f. (-न्द्रिः) and with ङीष् added तन्द्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रालु|तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तन्द्रालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Slothful, sluggish, overcome with sleep or fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>तन्द्र sloth, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तंद्रिः|तन्द्रिः
तन्द्रि<BR>f. (-न्द्रिः)<BR>1 Sleepiness.<BR>2 Lassitude.<BR>3 Fainting, exhaustion: see तन्द्रा.<BR>E.<BR>as above, or तदि Sautra root, to be weary, and क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्रिका|तंद्रिका
तन्द्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sloth, sleepiness.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तन्द्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्द्री|तंद्री
तन्द्री<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>1 Drowsiness.<BR>2 Lassitude: see तन्द्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्नि|तन्निः
तन्नि<BR>f. (-न्निः)<BR>A plant: see चक्रकुल्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मात्र|तन्मात्रं
तन्मात्र<BR>n. sub. (-त्रं)<BR>The archetype or subtile rudiment of elementary matter.<BR>adv.<BR>Merely that.<BR>E.<BR>तद्, and मात्र only, or element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्यतु|तन्यतुः
तन्यतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, यतुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वत्|तन्वन्त्
तन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वत्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्)<BR>Spreading, extending.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप<BR>(औ) तपौ r. 1st cl. (तपति-ते) r. 4th cl. (तप्यति-ते) and r. 10th cl. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">Page366</a>] (तापयति-ते)<BR>1 To heat or be hot, to burn; (hence figuratively,) to suffer mental or bodily pain.<BR>2 To have pre-eminent or superhuman power:<BR>the deponent form only is used when the root with the prefix उत् or वि occurs intransitively, or governs as its object part of the body of the agent, as पाणिं वितपते warms the hand, (उत्तपते वितपते) shines, burns, &c. The root takes the passive form also, when implying religious meditation, as तप्यते तपस्तापसः the devotee revolves religious thoughts.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>(अनुतपते)<BR>To repent, to regret.<BR>With परि or सम्<BR>(परितपति सन्तपति,)<BR>1 To bear or inflict pain, anguish, heat, distress, &c.<BR>2 To be sorrowful, to repent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=365" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकर|तपःकरः
तपःकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The mango fish: see तपस्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःकृश
तपःकृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Emaciated by austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and कृश lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःक्लेशसह|तपःक्लेशसहः
तपःक्लेशसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Patient of austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तपस् austere devotion, क्लश fatigue, and सह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपःस्थली
तपःस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A name of Benāres.<BR>E.<BR>तपस् religious austerities, and स्थल soil, place, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The hot season, summer.<BR>2 Heat, warmth.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपत्|तपन्त्
तपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>1 Heating or warming.<BR>2 Performing penance.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपती
तपती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A name of CHĀYĀ, wife of the sun.<BR>2 Also of the daughter of the sun, or the personified Taptī river, married to SAṂVARAṆA of the Kuru family.<BR>E.<BR>तप heat or the sun, and अत who accompanies, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A division of hell.<BR>3 Heat, burning.<BR>4 Mental distress, pining, grieving.<BR>5 The hot season.<BR>6 The marking nut plant.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Godāvarī river.<BR>E.<BR>तप to inflame, affixes ल्युट् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनकर|तपनकरः
तपनकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A ray, a sun-beam.<BR>E.<BR>तपन, and कर a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनतनय|तपनतनयः
तपनतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KARṆA, &c.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 The Yamunā river.<BR>2 The Tapti.<BR>E.<BR>तपन, the sun, and तनय child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनमणि|तपनमणिः
तपनमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun-stone.<BR>E.<BR>तपन, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनांशु|तपनांशुः
तपनांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A ray of the sun, a sun-beam.<BR>E.<BR>तपन, and अंशु ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनात्मजा
तपनात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 The Godāvarī river.<BR>2 The Yamunā or Jumna river.<BR>E.<BR>तपन the sun, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीय|तपनीयं
तपनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be heated.<BR>2 To be suffered or practised as penance.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, &c. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीयक|तपनीयकं
तपनीयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>तपनीय, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनेष्ट|तपनेष्टं
तपनेष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>तपन, and इष्ट liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस्<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>1 The name of a month, Māgha, (January-February.)<BR>2 The cold or dewy season.<BR>3 The hot season.<BR>n. (-पः)<BR>1 Religious austerity, penance, mortification, the practice of mental or personal self-denial, or the infliction of bodily tortures.<BR>2 A world, the region above the Janaloka, inhabited by saints or devotees after death.<BR>3 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>4 Duty, the special observance of certain things: thus the Tapas of a Brahman is sacred learning; of a Kṣatriya, the protection of subjects; of a Vaiśya, almsgiving to Brahmans; of a Śūdra, the service of the same tribe; and of a Ṛṣi or saint, feeding upon herbs and roots.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat or inflame, affix असुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस|तपसः
तपस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, असच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्तक्ष|तपस्तक्षः
तपस्तक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>तपम् austerity, and तक्ष who pares or makes thin; emaciating himself by his devotions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
तपस्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>1 The month Phālguna, (February-March.) A name of ARJUNA.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>1 Devout austerity, religious penance.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>The flower of the Kunda, (Jasminum pubescens.)<BR>E.<BR>तपस् the cold season, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विन्
तपस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Devout, practising austerities.<BR>2 Poor, wretched, pitiable.<BR>m. (-स्वी)<BR>1 An ascetic, a religious man engaged in the practice of rigorous and devout penance.<BR>2 A name of NĀRADA.<BR>3 A mendicant, a pauper.<BR>4 The mango fish (Polynemus risua.)<BR>f. (-स्विनी)<BR>1 A female devotee, a woman leading a religious life.<BR>2 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>3 Another plant: see कटुरोहिणी.<BR>E.<BR>तपस् religious austerity, the hot season, &c. विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्समाधि
तपस्समाधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The practice of penance.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and समाधि obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्मक
तपात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Practising austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तप, and आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपात्यय|तपात्ययः
तपात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>तप the warm season, and अत्यय destroying; following the hot weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपित|तपितं
तपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heated, burnt.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, affix क्त, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुस्
तपुस्<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, Uṇādi affix उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोधन|तपोधनः
तपोधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A devotee, an ascetic, one who performs religious penance.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A plant: see मुण्डीरी.<BR>E.<BR>तपस् religious austerity, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनुभाव|तपोनुभावः
तपोनुभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The influence of religious penance.<BR>E.<BR>तपस, and अनुभाव authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोनिष्ठ
तपोनिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Performing penance, practising austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and निष्ठ engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमय|तपोमयः
तपोमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Devout, practising austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमूर्त्ति|तपोमूर्ति|तपोमूर्तिः
तपोमूर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोराशि|तपोराशिः
तपोराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवट|तपोवटः
तपोवट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A country, part of central India or holy land.<BR>E.<BR>तपस् religious austerity, and वट what surrounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोवन
तपोवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sacred grove, a place frequented by ascetics.<BR>E.<BR>तपस्, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त|तप्तः
तप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Heated, inflamed, burnt.<BR>2 Scorched by pain or sorrow, distressed, afflicted.<BR>3 Inflamed with anger, incensed.<BR>4 Undergone or performed^1 as penance.<BR>5 Fused, melted.<BR>6 Burnished.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकुम्भ|तप्तकुम्भः
तप्तकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त, and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तकृच्छ्र|तप्तकृच्छ्रः
तप्तकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>A sort of penance, drinking hot water, milk, and ghee for three days each, and inhaling hot air for three days.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त heated, कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्ततपस्
तप्ततपस्<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त, and तपस् penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तपाषाणकुण्ड|तप्तपाषाणकुण्डं
तप्तपाषाणकुण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त, पाषाण a stone, and कुण्ड a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तबालुक|तप्तबालुकः
तप्तबालुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त, and वालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=366" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्तरूपक|तप्तरूपकं
तप्तरूपक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>तप्त, and रूपक silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त्वा
तप्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having heated.<BR>2 Having performed penance.<BR>E.<BR>तप, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्स्यत्
तप्स्यत्<BR>mfn. (-प्स्यन्-प्स्यन्ती-प्स्यत्)<BR>Practising or intending to practise austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तप to perform penance, शतृ affix, future part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःप्रवेश|तमःप्रवेशः
तमःप्रवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Groping in the dark.<BR>2 Mental indistinctness or aberration.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and प्रवेश entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमःस्थित
तमःस्थित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A hell, one of the lowest divisions of hell.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and स्थित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम<BR>(इर उ) इर्तमु r. 4th cl. (ताम्यति)<BR>1 To desire.<BR>2 To be distressed in body or mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The quality of darkness incident to humanity: see तमस्.<BR>mf. (-मः-मा)<BR>A tree bearing black blossoms.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Darkness, gloom.<BR>2 The point of the foot.<BR>f. (-मा-मी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be disturbed, to be fatigued, &c. affixes अच्, and टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमङ्गक|तमंगकः|तमङ्गकः
तमङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The flat and projecting roof of a house, a sort of balcony or terrace.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, अङ्गक affix; pleasant, desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमत|तमतः
तमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Desirous, cupidinous, longing or hankering after.<BR>2 Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, affix अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमप्रभ|तमप्रभः
तमप्रभ<BR>mf. (-भः-भा)<BR>A hell, one of the lowermost divisions of the infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>तम darkness, and प्रभ what is manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमर|तमरं
तमर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be disturbed, affix अरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमराज|तमराजः
तमराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस्<BR>n. (-मः)<BR>1 The third of the qualities incident to the state of humanity, the Tama guṇa, or property of darkness, whence proceed folly, ignorance, mental blindness, worldly delusion, &c.<BR>2 Darkness, gloom.<BR>3 Sin.<BR>4 Sorrow, grief.<BR>mn. (-माः-मः)<BR>Rāhu or the personified ascending node: see राहु.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be disturbed, and असच् Uṇādi affix; that property by which the mind is troubled, the world perplexed, &c.; also तमम् and तम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>2 A city.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>a river, the Tamasā or Tonse.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be disturbed, (daylight, &c.) and असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्कल्प
तमस्कल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Like darkness, black, gloomy.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and कल्प aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्तति|तमस्ततिः
तमस्तति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Great or diffusive darkness.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, and तति a spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्विन्
तमस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Dark, gloomy.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, and विनि affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाल|तमालं|तमालः
तमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sectarial mark made with Sandal, &c. upon the forehead.<BR>2 The name of a tree bearing black blossoms, (Xanthocymus pictorius, Rox.)<BR>3 A sword, a scymitar or large sacrificial knife.<BR>4 A plant: see वरुण.<BR>5 A black kind of Mimosa.<BR>6 The bark of the bambu.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be dark or troubled, Uṇādi affix कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालक|तमालकं|तमालकः
तमालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A sort of potherb, (Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR>2 The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The bark of a bambu.<BR>2 The Tamāla tree: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् pleonasm, or implying some resemblance, added to तमाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालपत्र|तमालपत्रं
तमालपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The Tamāla tree: see तमाल.<BR>2 The Tilaka or sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>3 The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तमाल, and पत्र a leaf: the leaf of the Tamāla, either in fact or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालिका
तमालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A district in Bengal, the modern Tumlook.<BR>E.<BR>तमाल a Tamāla tree, ठन् affix, implying possession; also with an analogous affix इनि, तमालिनी abounding in Tamāla trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमाली
तमाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal plant: see ताम्रवल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमि|तमिः
तमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be weary, इन् affix: see तम and तमी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिन्
तमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Desiring, desirous, wishing.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>The dark half of the month, from the full to the change.<BR>f. (-स्रा)<BR>1 A dark night, or one during the wane of the moon.<BR>2 Great or extensive darkness.<BR>3 The night of new moon.<BR>4 Any night.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>2 Anger, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>तमस darkness, र added, and इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रपक्ष|तमिस्रपक्षः
तमिस्रपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The fortnight of the moon's wane.<BR>E.<BR>तमिस्र, and पक्ष a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोगुण|तमोगुणः
तमोगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The quality of darkness or ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोघ्न|तमोघ्नः
तमोघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 The legislator BUDDHA.<BR>5 VIṢṆU.<BR>6 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, (physical or moral,) and घ्न destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोज्योतिस्
तमोज्योतिस्<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A fire fly.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद्
तमोनुद्<BR>mfn. (-नुद्)<BR>Dispersing darkness.<BR>m. (-नुद् or नुत्)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, नुद to send away or disperse, affix क्विप्; also with क affix तमोनुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोनुद|तमोनुदः
तमोनुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोपह|तमोपहः
तमोपह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Lightening, enlightening, removing darkness physical or moral.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 A name of Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>तमम् darkness, अपह removing, from अप prefixed to हन to kill or destroy, affix ड; also तमोहन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभिद्
तमोभिद्<BR>m. (-भिट् or भित्)<BR>A fire-fly.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, and भिद what penetrates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोभूत
तमोभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dark.<BR>2 Ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमय|तमोमयः
तमोमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Consisting or composed of darkness, derived from it.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमणि|तमोमणिः
तमोमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A fire-fly.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोलिप्ती
तमोलिप्ती<BR>f. (-प्ती)<BR>The district of Tumlook in Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness or sin, and लिप्त soiled, affix ङीष्; a country of which the inhabitants are notoriously depraved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोविकार|तमोविकारः
तमोविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Disease, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>तमस्, and विकार changed, proceeding from the Tama guṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोवृत
तमोवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Overcome with or influenced by rage, fear, &c. or any of the effects of the property of darkness.<BR>2 Obscured, clouded.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् as above, and आवृत surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोहर|तमोहरः
तमोहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Removing darkness, lightening.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् darkness, and हर who removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=367" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्पा
तम्पा<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, अप affix; also प being changed to ब, तम्बा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्ब
तम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (तम्बति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्बा|तंबा
तम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A cow: see तम्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय|तयः
तय<BR>r. 1st cl. (तयते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To guard or preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय|तयः
तय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Who or what protects.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Protection.<BR>E.<BR>तय, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Who or what passes over or beyond.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Passing over, crossing.<BR>2 A float, a raft.<BR>3 A road.<BR>4 A tree.<BR>f. (री)<BR>1 A boat.<BR>2 A club.<BR>3 A clothes basket, a Pitāra.<BR>4 Smoke.<BR>5 A small wooden baling vessel.<BR>6 The end of a garment.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, affix अप्, fem. affix ङीष्; also with इन् affix तरि, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्षु|तरक्षुः
तरक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A hyena.<BR>E.<BR>तर a road, and क्षि to annoy^1, affix डु infesting the road; also with कन् added तरक्षुक. m. (-कः) or with ड affix तरक्ष. m. (-क्षः) but not common.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरंगः|तरङ्गः
तरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A wave.<BR>2 Cloth or clothes.<BR>3 The gallop of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass over or cross, Uṇādi affix अङ्गच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गिणी|तरंगिणी
तरङ्गिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>तरङ्ग a wave, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरङ्गित|तरंगित
तरङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wavy, billowy, tossing with waves.<BR>E.<BR>तरङ्ग, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A raft, a float.<BR>2 Svarga or paradise.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Crossing over, passing, going across.<BR>2 Removing from an inundation.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणि|तरणिः
तरणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>3 A float or raft.<BR>f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>1 A boat. The Socotrine aloe, (A. perfoliata.)<BR>3 A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, Uṇādi affix अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणिपेटक|तरणिपेटकः
तरणिपेटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An oval bowl or bason of wood, for baling a boat.<BR>E.<BR>तरणि, and पेटक a basket, the boat's basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणिरत्न|तरणिरत्नं
तरणिरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्ड|तरंड|तरंडं|तरंडः|तरण्डः
तरण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा or ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>A boat, a vessel.<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 A raft or float, made of bambus, &c. tied together, and sometimes floated upon jars or hollow gourds inverted.<BR>2 The float of a fishing line.<BR>3 An oar.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A country.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, अण्डन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण्डपादा|तरंडपादा
तरण्डपादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>तरण्ड an oar, and पाद a foot, having oars for feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्
तरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Crossing, passing over.<BR>n. (-रत् or रद्)<BR>1 A float or raft.<BR>2 A kind of duck.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, शतृ affix of the active participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरत्सल
तरत्सल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Conflagration of chaff: see तृणाग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरन्त|तरंत|तरंतः|तरन्तः
तरन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A fog.<BR>2 A hard shower, a torrent of rain.<BR>3 The ocean.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरम्बुज|तरम्बुजं
तरम्बुज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A watermelon, (most probably borrowed from the Persian, تربز)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरपण्य|तरपण्यं
तरपण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Fare, freight.<BR>E.<BR>तर passing (a river), and पण्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Trembling, tremulous.<BR>2 Libidinous, lecherous, wanton.<BR>3 Luminous, splendid.<BR>4 Hollow.<BR>5 Liquid, liquefied.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The central gem of a necklace.<BR>2 A necklace.<BR>3 Bottom, depth, lower or under part.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Rice gruel.<BR>2 Wine, vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>3 A bee.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, to go or move, affix कल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलता
तरलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Tremulousness, unsteadiness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, तललत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरललोचना
तरललोचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman with rolling or tremulous eyes.<BR>E.<BR>तरल trembling, and लोचना an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलायित|तरलायितः
तरलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused to tremble, agitated, undulating.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A large wave or surf.<BR>2 Fickleness.<BR>E.<BR>तरल used as a verb, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलित|तरलितं
तरलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>E.<BR>तरल trembling, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवारि|तरवारिः
तरवारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar.<BR>E.<BR>तर passing, वॄ to effect, इञ् affix; making its pass through the enemy, &c. also तरवारिक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 Strength.<BR>3 A bank.<BR>4 A float, a raft.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to go, to go quick, &c. असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस|तरसं
तरस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>तरस् strength, affix अच्; in which there is strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्थान|तरस्थानं
तरस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A landing place, a wharf or stairs.<BR>E.<BR>तर passing, ferrying, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्वत्|तरस्वन्त्
तरस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>1 Quick, swift.<BR>2 Valiant.<BR>E.<BR>तरस्, and वतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्विन्
तरस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Quick, swift.<BR>2 Strong, valiant.<BR>m. (-स्वी)<BR>1 A courier, an express, a runner.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>3 The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>तरस् speed, &c. विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरान्धु|तरांधु|तरांधुः|तरान्धुः
तरान्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A large flat bottomed boat.<BR>E.<BR>तर crossing, अन्धु water; perhaps a various reading of the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरालु|तरालुः
तरालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A flat bottomed boat.<BR>E.<BR>तर passing over, आलुच् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरि|तरिः
तरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 A boat.<BR>2 A clothes basket.<BR>3 The end of a cloth.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, Uṇādi affix इन्; also with ङीष् affix तरी see तर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिक|तरिकः
तरिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ferry-man.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>तरि a boat, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिकिन्
तरिकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A ferry-man.<BR>E.<BR>तरिक a raft, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरित
तरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Carried over or across.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The fore finger.<BR>2 Garlic, or perhaps hemp: see गृञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>त to cross, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिन्
तरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-णि)<BR>Who or what crosses.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>तृ to go, in the causal, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरितृ
तरितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>What crosses, passes or carries over.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A boat, a raft.<BR>E.<BR>तृ to cross, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिरथ|तरिरथः
तरिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>An oar, a paddle.<BR>E.<BR>तरि a boat, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीष|तरीषः
तरीष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 Heaven or paradise.<BR>3 Decorating, ornamenting.<BR>4 A raft, a float.<BR>5 Practice, business, profession.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 The daughter of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross or cause to cross, Uṇādi affix ईषन्; in some of its senses this word and तबिष seem to be confounded: see तबिष and ताविष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
तरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to proceed, Uṇādi affix उ; what goes or grows; or from what flowers and fruits arise, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुकूणि|तरुकूणिः
तरुकूणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and कूण to contract, affix कि; nestling in the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुज
तरुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Borne, produced by a tree, (as a flower, fruit, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुजीवन|तरुजीवनं
तरुजीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=368" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुण|तरुणं|तरुणः
तरुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Young, juvenile.<BR>2 New, fresh, novel.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A young man, one of the virile age.<BR>2 The castor oil plant.<BR>3 Large cumin seed.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A young woman from 16 to 30 years of age; generally however one about the first age.<BR>2 The aloe tree, (A. perfoliata.)<BR>3 A perfume, commonly Chira.<BR>4 A flower, the Indian white rose, (Rosa standulifera.)<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A kind of flower, that of the Achyranthes aspera? (कुजपुष्प.)<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass away, उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणज्वर|तरुणज्वरः
तरुणज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fever that lasts a week.<BR>E.<BR>तरुण, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणदधि
तरुणदधि<BR>n. (-धि)<BR>Curds five days old.<BR>E.<BR>तरुण, and दधि curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणास्थि
तरुणास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>Cartilage, gristle.<BR>E.<BR>तरुण, and अस्थि bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणीगण
तरुणीगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A number of young women.<BR>E.<BR>तरुणी, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणीजन
तरुणीजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>तरुणी, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतल
तरुतल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The part under the branches of a tree, the ground about its root.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतूलिका
तरुतूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The flying fox.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and तूलिका scales, suspended like a balance from the branches of a tree; also read तरुदूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुनख|तरुनखः
तरुनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and नख a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुपङ्क्ति
तरुपङ्क्ति^1<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A row of trees, an avenue.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and पंक्ति a line.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Dhaval Patel on 20151215. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/171. note: Convention error..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुभुज्
तरुभुज्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and भुज what enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुमृग|तरुमृगः
तरुमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A monkey, an ape.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुराग|तरुरागं
तरुराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A bud, a blossom.<BR>2 A new sprout.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, राग delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुविटप
तरुविटप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A branch or sprout.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and विटप a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुराज|तरुराजः
तरुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The palmyra tree.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and राज king, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुरुहा
तरुरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुरोहिणी
तरुरोहिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and रोहिणी what ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुशायिन्
तरुशायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and शीङ्^1 to sleep, with णिनि aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुसार|तरुसारः
तरुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>तरु a tree, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुस्थ
तरुस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Staying or being in a tree.<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>तरु, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरूट|तरूटः
तरूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (तर्कयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>3 To reason, to discuss.<BR>4 To doubt or apprehend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क|तर्कः
तर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 Doubt or disputation, discussion, reasoning.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>4 Cause, motive.<BR>5 The science of reasoning, logic.<BR>6 (In Logic,) Reduction to absurdity, a conclusion opposed to or disproving the premises.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क to infer, to reason, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कक|तर्ककः
तर्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A supplicant, a petitioner, an asker.<BR>2 A logician.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क to reason, and affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कयत्
तर्कयत्<BR>mfn. (-यत्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Expecting, anticipating.<BR>2 Doubting.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क to doubt, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कविद्या
तर्कविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>The science of reasoning or logic.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क as above, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्काभास|तर्काभासः
तर्काभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Apparent reduction to absurdity, or seeming not real, incompatibility of the conclusion with the premises.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क, and आभास fallacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कारी
तर्कारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A tree, (Aeschynomene sesban.)<BR>E.<BR>तर्क reasoning, ऋ to go or affect, affixes अण and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कित
तर्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Doubted, apprehended.<BR>2 Discussed.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क to doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किन्
तर्किन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A logician, a disputant, a follower of the Tarka Śāstra.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किल
तर्किल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Cassia tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कु|तर्कुः
तर्कु<BR>f. (-र्कुः)<BR>A spindle, an iron pin upon which the cotton is first drawn out; it also serves as the distaff, the cotton being next transferred from it to the wheel.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, Uṇādi affix उ, and the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुट|तर्कुटं
तर्कुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Drawing out the cotton upon the distaff or upon the wheel.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A spindle or a distaff: see तर्कु.<BR>E.<BR>कृत to cut, &c. उटच् affix, and the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुपिण्ड|तर्कुपिंड|तर्कुपिण्डः
तर्कुपिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A ball of clay, &c. upon the lower end of the spindle to assist in giving it a rotatory motion.<BR>E.<BR>तर्कु as above, पिण्ड a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुपीठी
तर्कुपीठी<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>A ball at the lower end of a spindle: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>तर्कु a spindle, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुलासक|तर्कुलासकः
तर्कुलासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A concave shell or saucer in which the lower end of the spindle is placed, and whirled round.<BR>E.<BR>तर्कु a spindle, लस to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुशाण|तर्कुशाणः
तर्कुशाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A small whetstone, for sharpening spindles, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तर्कु a spindle, and शाण a whetstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्षु|तर्क्षुः
तर्क्षु<BR>m. (-र्क्षुः)<BR>A hyena.<BR>E.<BR>तर्ज to give pain, affix कु; also तरक्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्ष्य|तर्क्ष्यः
तर्क्ष्य<BR>m. (-र्क्ष्यः)<BR>Nitre, saltpetre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज|तर्ज्ज
तर्ज<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तर्जति-ते तर्जयति)<BR>To blame, to censure, to reprove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्जन|तर्जन|तर्जनं|तर्ज्जनं
तर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Blaming, censuring.<BR>2 Pointing at, in ridicule, or contempt.<BR>3 Putting to shame, surpassing.<BR>4 Wrath, anger.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>तर्ज to abuse, to injure, affixes ल्युट् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्जिक|तर्जिक|तर्ज्जिकः
तर्ज्जिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a country, perhaps to the north-west of India or Bokhara, &c. the country of the Tājiks: also तायिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्जित|तर्जित
तर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blamed, reviled.<BR>2 Shamed, disgraced.<BR>E.<BR>तर्ज to blame, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ण|तर्णः
तर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to go, ण affix; also with कन् added, तर्णक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णक|तर्णकः
तर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A calf: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णि|तर्णिः
तर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 A raft, a float.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, affix णि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्त्तरीक|तर्तरीक|तर्त्तरीकं
तर्त्तरीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A passenger, one who passes or crosses.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A boat, a raft, a vessel.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross over, ईकन् aff. and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द|तर्द्द
तर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (तर्दति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्दू
तर्दू<BR>m. (-र्दूः)<BR>A wooden ladle.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to go, Uṇādi affix उ, and दूट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पण|तर्पणं
तर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Satisfaction given or received; either the act of pleasing, or the state of being pleased.<BR>2 Satiety, fulness.<BR>3 A religious rite, presenting water to the manes of the deceased or to the Pitṛs collectively; also to the gods either generally or individually.<BR>4 Fuel used on sacrificial occasions. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">Page370</a>]<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant; also गुरुस्कन्ध.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to satisfy or be satisfied, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=369" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पणेच्छु|तर्पणेच्छुः
तर्पणेच्छु<BR>mfn. (-च्छुः-च्छुः-च्छु)<BR>Desirous of satisfaction, or of receiving after death the presentation of water called Tarpaṇa.<BR>m. (-च्छुः)<BR>A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>तर्पण as above, इच्छु to wish, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पित
तर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to be pleased, क्त affix, with इट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पिन्
तर्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि)<BR>1 Giving pleasure or satisfaction.<BR>2 Offering oblations to the manes, (who does so.)<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>तृप to give pleasure, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब|तर्ब्ब
तर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (तर्बति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब्बट|तर्बट|तर्बटः
तर्ब्बट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>तर्ब्ब^1 to go, अटन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्म्मन्|तर्मन्
तर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The top or term of the sacrificial post.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass up, and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ष|तर्षः
तर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 The ocean.<BR>4 A raft or float.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix अच्, or तॄ to pass over, and ष Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षण|तर्षणं
तर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Thirst, thirsting: it is also used metaphorically.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षित|तर्षितः
तर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thirsting, athirst, thirsty.<BR>2 Desiring, wishing for.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हि
तर्हि<BR>ind.<BR>Therefore.<BR>E.<BR>तद that, and र्हिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तलति तालयति)<BR>1 To be full or complete.<BR>2 To fix, to found.<BR>3 To establish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल|तलं|तलः
तल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Essential nature, (in composition especially, as महीतलं the earth itself, the very earth.)<BR>2 Depth, bottom, lowness, inferiority of position, the place under or underneath.<BR>3 A wood, a forest.<BR>4 A hole, a pit, a chasm.<BR>5 Cause, origin, motive, the root or seed of events.<BR>6 Sole of the foot.<BR>7 A slap with the hand.<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A leathern fence worn by archers on the left arm.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The palmyra tree.<BR>2 The palm with extended fingers.<BR>3 The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR>4 Pressing the strings of a lute with the left hand.<BR>3 The stand or support of any thing, that which is under or below it.<BR>6 The fore arm.<BR>7 A span.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलक|तलकं|तलकः
तलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A large pond.<BR>E.<BR>तल a hole, a hollow, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलप्रहार|तलप्रहारः
तलप्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A slap or blow with the palm of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>तल the open palm, प्रहार striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवारण|तलवारणं
तलवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A sword.<BR>E.<BR>तल, and वारण opposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलसारक|तलसारकं
तलसारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A martingale.<BR>2 A vessel from which horses are fed.<BR>E.<BR>तल below, सृ to go, in the causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलहृदय|तलहृदयं
तलहृदय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The centre of the sole of the foot.<BR>E.<BR>तल below, and हृदय heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलाची
तलाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A mat, one made of reeds or bamboos.<BR>E.<BR>तल below, अञ्च to go, क्विप् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलातल|तलातलं
तलातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of the seven divisions of the infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>तल below, reiterated, as downadown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिका
तलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A martingale.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
तलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fixed, placed, having a bottom.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Fried meat.<BR>E.<BR>तल to be fixed or to satisfy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन|तलिनं|तलिनः
तलिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Separate, having spaces or interstices.<BR>2 Clear, clean.<BR>3 Small, little.<BR>4 Delicate, thin, spare.<BR>5 Below, situated under or underneath.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bed, a couch or cot.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix or be fixed, Uṇādi affix इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिम|तलिमं
तलिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Ground prepared for the site of a dwelling, &c. see कुट्टिम.<BR>2 A bed, a couch or cot.<BR>3 An awning.<BR>4 A scymitar, a large sacrificial sword or knife.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix, इमन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुन|तलुनः
तलुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A youth.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, उनन् affix, and र changed to लः see तरुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलेक्षण|तलेक्षणः
तलेक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>तल down, and ईक्षण looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलोदरी
तलोदरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A mistress or wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलोदा
तलोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>तल steep, down, उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्क|तल्कं
तल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>A wood, a forest.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix, क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्प|तल्पं|तल्पः
तल्प<BR>mn. (-ल्पः-ल्पं)<BR>1 A bed.<BR>2 An upper story, a room on the top of a house, a turret, a tower or keep.<BR>3 A wife.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix, Uṇādi affix प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पकीट|तल्पकीटः
तल्पकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>तल्प a bed, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पज
तल्पज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Born of a wife, (as a son by an appointed substitute.)<BR>2 Produced in or from a bed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल्प, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पन|तल्पनं
तल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An elephant's back.<BR>2 The exterior muscles of the back.<BR>E.<BR>तल्प a nominal verb, to be as a bed, to be broad, &c. and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्ल|तल्लं|तल्लः
तल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A reservoir, a large pond, a tank or Talao.<BR>f. (-ल्ला)<BR>1 A young woman.<BR>2 A boat.<BR>3 The wife of VARUṆA.<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>A pit, a hole.<BR>E.<BR>तल deep, depth, and ल to be or have, from ला with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लज|तल्लजः
तल्लज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Excellence, happiness; also attributively, Excellent, happy: used in apposition as an epithet, the gender is not changed, as कुमारीतल्लजः an excellent maiden.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, (that which is every thing,) and लज to attain, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लिका
तल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्व|तल्वं
तल्व<BR>n. (-ल्वं)<BR>Scent arising from the rubbing of fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक|तवकः
तवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Thine.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तव the poss. case of त्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक्षीर|तवक्षीरं
तवक्षीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Milk and water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवराज|तवराजः
तवराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sort of sugar prepared from a species of Hedysarum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष|तविषः
तविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 The daughter of INDRA.<BR>3 Strength, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>तव a Sautra root, टिषच् Uṇādi affix; also ताविष and तवीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीष|तवीषः
तवीष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Heaven.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्ट|तष्टः
तष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pared, made thin.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष to pare, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्टृ
तष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 A carpenter.<BR>2 A name of VIŚVAKARMA.<BR>3 One of the twelve Ādityas or suns; also त्वष्टृ.<BR>E.<BR>तक्ष to pare, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस
तस<BR>(इर उ) इरतसु r. 4th cl. (तस्यति)<BR>To throw, to toss, to direct, to send.<BR>(इ) तसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तंसति तंसयति or with अव prefixed अवतंसति अवतंसयति)<BR>To adorn, to dress or decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तसर|तसरः
तसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A shuttle.<BR>E.<BR>तन to stretch, क्मरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्कर|तस्करः
तस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A thief, a robber.<BR>2 The ear.<BR>3 A kind of potherb, (Medicago esculenta.)<BR>3 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa): see मदन.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A passionate woman.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, used depreciatingly, and कर who does, सुट् substituted for the final of तत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=370" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करता
तस्करता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Thievishness, thieving.<BR>2 Hearing, catching by the ear.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, तस्करत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटङ्क|ताटंक|ताटंकः|ताटङ्कः
ताटङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>An ornament of the ear, a large sort of ear-ring: see ताडङ्क and तालपत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटस्थ्य|ताटस्थ्यं
ताटस्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>1 Indifference, disregard, exemption from attachment or aversion.<BR>2 Proximity.<BR>E.<BR>तटस्थ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 Beating, whipping, inflicting bodily chastisement.<BR>2 Sound, noise.<BR>3 A handful of grass, corn, &c. a sheaf.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>5 A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>f. (-डि or डी)<BR>A kind of palm, (Corypha talliera, Rox.) see ताली.<BR>E.<BR>तड to give pain, to beat, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडका
ताडका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female demon, killed by RĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडकाफल|ताडकाफलं
ताडकाफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडङ्क|ताडंक|ताडंकः|ताडङ्कः
ताडङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A kind of ear-ring: see तालपत्र.<BR>E.<BR>तड to shine, अङ्कन् affix; also ड being changed to ट, ताटङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडघ|ताडघः
ताडघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Beating with a whip or with strokes of any kind.<BR>E.<BR>ताड, and घ who strikes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडघात|ताडघातः
ताडघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An artificer who beats or hammers any thing.<BR>E.<BR>ताड, and घात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडन|ताडनं
ताडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Beating, whipping, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A whip.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, अनीयुट् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडनीय
ताडनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be beaten, punishable.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, अनीयर् affix; also ताड्य and ताडयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडपत्र|ताडपत्रं
ताडपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An ornament of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>ताड the Tāla tree, and पत्र a leaf, an earring resembling this: see तालपत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयितृ
ताडयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what beats or strikes.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडयित्वा
ताडयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having beaten.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडित
ताडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck, beaten.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडुल|ताडुलः
ताडुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Beating, who or what beats or strikes.<BR>E.<BR>तड to give pain, उलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्य
ताड्य<BR>mfn. (-ड्यः-ड्या-ड्यं)<BR>To be beaten or chastised, what may or ought to be punished, punishable.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्यमान|ताड्यमानः
ताड्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being beaten or struck.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A musical instrument, which is struck, as a drum, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तड to beat or strike, शाणच् affix, यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|तांडवः|ताण्डवः
ताण्डव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 Dancing, especially with violent gesticulation, and particularly applied to the frantic dance of the god ŚIVA, and his votaries.<BR>2 A sort of grass, (Saccharum procerum.)<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>In prosody, a tribrach or foot of three short syllables.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डु the name of the Muni, by whom the style of dancing was first taught, affix अण्; or तडि to beat, and अव aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवतालिक|ताण्डवतालिकः
ताण्डवतालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of NANDI, one of ŚIVA'S principal attendants.<BR>E.<BR>ताण्डव ŚIVA'S dancing, and तालिक accompanier with music, from ताल tune or time, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डवप्रिय|तांडवप्रिय|ताण्डवप्रियः
ताण्डवप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>ताण्डव dancing, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताण्डि|तांडिः|ताण्डिः
ताण्डि<BR>f. (-ण्डिः)<BR>The science of dancing.<BR>E.<BR>तण्डु the teacher of this art, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात|तातः
तात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Venerable, reverend, respectable.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A father.<BR>2 A term of affection addressed to any person, but especially to a junior or inferior, as हे तात oh! child, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तन to extend, (his race or fame,) क्त affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातगु|तातगुः
तातगु<BR>mfn. (-गुः-गूः-गु)<BR>Paternal, relating or belonging to the father.<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>A paternal uncle.<BR>E.<BR>तात a father, गु who goes or is, from गम to go, with डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातजनयित्री
तातजनयित्री<BR>f. du. always (-त्र्यौ)<BR>Father and mother, parents.<BR>E.<BR>तात father, and जनयित्री mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताततुल्य|ताततुल्यः
ताततुल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A paternal uncle, or the most respectable of the male relations.<BR>E.<BR>तात a father, and तुल्य like, equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातन|तातनः
तातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातल|तातलः
तातल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A fatherly relative, one who may be considered as a father.<BR>2 Sickness, disease.<BR>3 An iron club or spike.<BR>4 Cooking or maturing.<BR>5 Heat, physical or morbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताति|तातिः
ताति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A son.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, (the race,) ञि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to any particular moment of time.<BR>E.<BR>तत्काल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य्य|तात्पर्य|तात्पर्यं|तात्पर्य्यं
तात्पर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Object, purpose, intent, design.<BR>2 Meaning, purport.<BR>2 Explanation.<BR>E.<BR>तत्पर intent, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्य्यार्थ|तात्पर्यार्थ|तात्पर्यार्थः
तात्पर्य्यार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>The meaning or purpose of a sentence.<BR>E.<BR>तात्पर्य्य purpose, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थ्य|तादर्थ्यं
तादर्थ्य<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>1 Sameness or precision of meaning.<BR>2 Identity of object.<BR>E.<BR>तदर्थ, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्य|तादात्म्यं
तादात्म्य<BR>n. (-त्म्यं)<BR>Identity, unity, sameness.<BR>E.<BR>तदात्म same, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृश्
तादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Such like, like him or it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तद् that, दृश to see, affix क्विन्; also with कञ् affix तादृश. mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) or with क्म affix, तादृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान|तानं|तानः
तान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tune.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Expanse, extension.<BR>2 An object of sense.<BR>E.<BR>तन to extend, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानव|तानवं
तानव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Thinness, spareness.<BR>E.<BR>तनु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूर|तानूरः
तानूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, ऊरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त|तांत|तान्तः
तान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Wearied, fatigued, distressed.<BR>2 Languid, languishing.<BR>3 Faded, withered, blighted.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be distressed, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्तव|तांतव
तान्तव<BR>m. (-वं)<BR>Spinning, weaving.<BR>E.<BR>तन्तु a thread, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्र
तान्त्र<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्री-न्त्रं)<BR>1 Stringed, having wires or strings, (as a musical instrument.)<BR>2 Relating to the Tantras, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्त्रिक|तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तान्त्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to the Tāntras, taught by them, following them, &c.<BR>2 Relating to a thread, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A scholar, a man completely versed in any science.<BR>2 A follower of the doctrine taught by the Tantras.<BR>E.<BR>तन्त्र truth, &c. and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तान्दन
तान्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Heat, burning, (moral or physical.)<BR>2 Pain, sorrow, distress.<BR>E.<BR>तप to burn or inflame, affix घञ्<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>A name of the Tapti or Surat river.<BR>2 A name of the Yamunā or Jumna river.<BR>E.<BR>तप the sun, affix of descent इण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Burning, inflaming, heating.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fever, morbid heat.<BR>E.<BR>तप to burn, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्य|तापत्यः
तापत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>तपती, and यञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>What heats or inflames.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 One of KĀMA'S arrows, the inflamer.<BR>3 Sun-shine.<BR>4 Heating, inflaming.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, in the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=371" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Golden, made of gold.<BR>E.<BR>तपनीय, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Performing penance, a practiser of devout austerities, a devotee, an ascetic.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea).<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तपस penance, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसक|तापसकः
तापसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A contemptible devotee, one not long engaged in austerities.<BR>E.<BR>तापस, and कन् depreciative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसतरु|तापसतरुः
तापसतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tree, commonly Ingua or Jiyaputa, (Nagelia putranjiva.)<BR>E.<BR>तापस an ascetic, and तरु a tree; also similar compounds, as तापसद्रुम, तापसवृक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापसप्रिय|तापसप्रियः
तापसप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tree, (Chironjia sapida): see पियाल.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>तापस an ascetic, प्रिय beloved by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापहर
तापहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Cooling, removing heat.<BR>2 Consoling, alleviating distress.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A dish, a sort of soup, of pulse and grain, first fried with ghee and turmeric, and afterwards boiled with salt and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>ताप, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छ|तापिच्छः
तापिच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A tree bearing dark blossoms, the Tamāla: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिञ्छ|तापिञ्छः
तापिञ्छ<BR>m. (-ञ्छः)<BR>The Tamāla tree, (Xanthocymus pictorius.)<BR>E.<BR>तापिन् a person heated, and छद what covers or shelters, ड affix, deriv. irr.; also the final being dropped तापिच्छ, and with जि to conquer or remove तातिञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिञ्ज|तापिञ्जं|तापिञ्जः
तापिञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>The Tamāla tree.<BR>n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>Sulphuret of iron: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापित
तापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Inflamed.<BR>2 Distressed, pained.<BR>E.<BR>तप to inflame, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिन्
तापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Oppressed by heat, morbid, moral or physical; any thing heated or glowing.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>One of the deified saints of the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>तप to heat, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप्य|ताप्यं
ताप्य<BR>mn. (-प्यः-प्यं)<BR>A mineral substance, sulphuret of iron.<BR>E.<BR>तापी the river, and यत् affix; said to be procured from the Tāpi river; also with कन् added ताप्यकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम|तामः
ताम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 An object of terror.<BR>2 Fault, defect, vice.<BR>3 Anxiety, distress.<BR>4 Desire.<BR>E.<BR>तम to be distressed, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामर|तामरं
तामर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>ताम desire, and र from रा to get or have; desirable for drinking, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरस|तामरसं
तामरस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 A lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>2 Copper.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>4 A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>तामर water, सम to abide, and ड affix; or ताम desire, and रस here implying object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलकी
तामलकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta): see भूम्यामलकी.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, to be as it were, or resemble, आमलकी the Āmalaki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामलिप्त|तामलिप्तं
तामलिप्त<BR>nf. (-प्तं-प्ती)<BR>A district in the south of Bengal, commonly Tumlook.<BR>E.<BR>ताम distress, trouble, and लिप्त smeared, affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>1 Affected by or appertaining to the third quality, that of darkness or vice: belonging to it, as a Purāṇa, a system of philosophy, a ceremonial rite, &c.<BR>2 Dark, of or belonging to darkness.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 An incendiary, a malignant and mischievous man, a villain.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 The fourth Manu.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 A dark night.<BR>2 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The quality of darkness.<BR>E.<BR>तमस् the quality of darkness, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसिक|तामसिकं
तामसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Of or belonging to the quality of darkness, derived from it, teaching lessons so characterised, &c.<BR>2 Of or belonging to physical darkness.<BR>E.<BR>तसस्, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्र|तामिस्रं|तामिस्रः
तामिस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>1 Great darkness.<BR>2 A hell, that of deep gloom.<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>Indignation at being disappointed or slighted.<BR>E.<BR>तमिस्र, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूल|तांबूल|तांबूलं|ताम्बूलं
ताम्बूल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>1 Areca, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>2 Betel, (Piper betel,) or its pungent leaf, which together with the areca nut and catechu, and sometimes caustic lime and spices, is eaten very generally by the natives of the east.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The areca nut.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Śaṇa, a plant, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, affix उलच्, and वुक्र् augment, the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलकरङ्क|तांबूलकरंक|ताम्बूलकरङ्कः
ताम्बूलकरङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The Pān-dān or betel-box.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल as above, and करङ्क a hollowed cocoanut, &c. which the Panbox usually resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलद|तांबूलद|ताम्बूलदः
ताम्बूलद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The betel bearer; kings and great men being attended by an officer of this description.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल betel, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलपेटिका|तांबूलपेटिका
ताम्बूलपेटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A betel box.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल, and पेटिका a casket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलराग|ताम्बूलरागः
ताम्बूलराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A kind of pulse, (Ervum lens.)<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल betel, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवल्ली|तांबूलवल्ली
ताम्बूलवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A small plant bearing a pungent leaf, which with the areca nut, a small quantity of caustic lime (or Chunam) and catechu, and occasionally cloves, cardamoms, &c. form the Pan or betel of the Asiatic, (Piper betel.)<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल the same, and वल्ली foot-stalk; also with कन् added ताम्बूलवल्लिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलवाहक|तांबूलवाहक|ताम्बूलवाहकः
ताम्बूलवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A betel bearer, a servant attached to men of rank to prepare the pān, and carry the betel box.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल, and वाहक who carries; also ताम्बूलवाहिन् m. (-ही).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिकः
ताम्बूलिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A seller of betel.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्बूलिन्|तांबूलिन्
ताम्बूलिन्<BR>mf. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Relating or belonging to a Pān, having one, giving one, &c.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The Pān bearer, a servant who prepares and furnishes the Pān.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्बूल as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्यत्
ताम्यत्<BR>mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-भ्यत्)<BR>Distressing, afflicting, annoying.<BR>E.<BR>तम to distress, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्री-म्रं)<BR>Of a coppery red colour.<BR>n. (-म्रं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 A kind of sandal, represented as of a dark red colour, and smelling like a lotus.<BR>3 A dark or coppery red.<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>A leprosy with large red spots.<BR>f. (-म्री)<BR>A copper or metallic cup of prescribed capacity, and perforated by a small hole at the bottom, answering the purpose of an hour glass: it is put into a vessel of water, the water gradually filling it, and the cup sinking, marks the time that has elapsed.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire, Uṇādi affix रक, and the vowel made long; or ताम्र copper, अण् and ङीष् affixes, implying analogy or derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रक|ताम्रकं
ताम्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र as above, and कन् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकर्णी
ताम्रकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A name of the female elephant of the west.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र coppery, and कर्ण ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकार|ताम्रकारः
ताम्रकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A brazier, a copper-smith.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and कार worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=372" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकिलि
ताम्रकिलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A small worm of a red colour.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र red, and किलि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकुट
ताम्रकुट<BR>m. (कः)<BR>A brazier or copper smith.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, कुट to cut, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकुट्टक|ताम्रकुट्टकः
ताम्रकुट्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Tobacco.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and कुट्ट a point: the word is imitative of the foreign original.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकृमि|ताम्रकृमिः
ताम्रकृमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The lady-bird, (Coccinella.)<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र red, and कृमि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रगर्भ|ताम्रगर्भं
ताम्रगर्भ<BR>n. (-र्भं)<BR>Blue vitriol or sulphate of copper.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and गर्भ womb or source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रचूड|ताम्रचूडः
ताम्रचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and चूडा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रतनु
ताम्रतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Having a ruddy or fair complexion, copper-coloured.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपट्ट|ताम्रपट्टं|ताम्रपट्टः
ताम्रपट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>A copper plate, such as Hindu grants of land, &c. are frequently inscribed on.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and पट्ट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपर्णी
ताम्रपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A large pond or lake.<BR>2 The name of a river in the peninsula, and of the district in its vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपत्र|ताम्रपत्रः
ताम्रपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A plate of copper.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A potherb: see जीव.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपाकिन्
ताम्रपाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A tree: see गर्द्दभाण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र red, and पाकिन् ripening, the fruit being of this colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपुष्प|ताम्रपुष्पः
ताम्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A kind of ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>2 A plant, (Kæmpferia rotunda.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens).<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>1 Lythrum fruticosum: see धातृपुष्पिका.<BR>2 Trumpet flower.<BR>3 Red Tëori: see त्रिकृत्.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र coppery red, and पुष्प a flower, bearing red blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रफल|ताम्रफलः
ताम्रफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रफलक
ताम्रफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A copper plate.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and फलक a plank or board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमुख|ताम्रमुखः
ताम्रमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Copper-coloured, fair-complexioned.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A European.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमूला
ताम्रमूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant: see ग्राहिणी.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रमृग
ताम्रमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The red deer.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवर्ण|ताम्रवर्णः
ताम्रवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Red, copper-coloured.<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>The blossom of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवल्ली
ताम्रवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant used as an emollient in affections of the mouth and fauces; also called तमाली, ताली, सूक्ष्मवल्ली, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवीज|ताम्रवीजः
ताम्रवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of vetch: see कुलत्य.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and वीज the seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवृक्ष|ताम्रवृक्षः
ताम्रवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A sort of Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and ष्टक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रवृन्त|ताम्रवृन्तः
ताम्रवृन्त<BR>mf. (-न्तः-न्ता)<BR>A kind of vetch: see कुलत्य.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, or coppery, वृत्त foot-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रशिखिन्
ताम्रशिखिन्<BR>m. (-खी)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, शिखा a crest, and इनि affix: see ताम्रचूड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रसार|ताम्रसारं
ताम्रसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A red kind of Sandal, (Pterospermum santolinum).<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and सार pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राकु|ताम्राकुः
ताम्राकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>One of the eighteen minor divisions of the known continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राक्ष|ताम्राक्षः
ताम्राक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Koil or Kokila, the Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र, and अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्राभ|ताम्राभं
ताम्राभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Red saunders.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रार्द्ध|ताम्रार्द्धं
ताम्रार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>Mixed or bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and अर्द्ध part or half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिक|ताम्रिकः
ताम्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of copper, made of copper, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A brazier, a copper smith.<BR>E.<BR>ताम्र copper, and ठक् affix.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A copper vessel for marking time.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to ताम्री, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय
ताय<BR>(ऋ) तायृ r. 1st cl. (तायते)<BR>1 To spread, to extend, to proceed in a continuous stream or line.<BR>2 To cherish or protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायिक|तायिकः
तायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A country; or plu.<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>Its inhabitants.<BR>E.<BR>ताय to cherish, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार|तारं|तारः
तार<BR>mfn. adj. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 High, as a note in music.<BR>2 Radiant, shining, radiating.<BR>3 Clean, clear.<BR>4 Good, excellent, well flavoured, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A high note or tone in music.<BR>2 Elegance of a pearl.<BR>3 A clear or beautiful pearl.<BR>4 Crossing, passing over, &c.<BR>5 A wire, a chord.<BR>6 The mystic monosyllable Om.<BR>7 A mystical monosyllable in the Tantras.<BR>8 The name of a monkey chief, the son of BĀLĪ.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>mfn. subst. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 The pupil of the eye.<BR>2 A star in general, a planet, an asterism, &c.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A female deity peculiar to the Bauddha sect.<BR>2 The wife of VṚHASPATI.<BR>3 The wife of the monkey king SUGRĪVA.<BR>4 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass or proceed; also in the causal, to cause to pass, and अच् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारक|तारकं|तारकः
तारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 A protector, a preserver.<BR>2 One who causes or enables to pass or go over.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 A Mantra, a formula addressed to Rāma, as Rāmāya namaḥ,<BR>nf. (-कं-का)<BR>1 The pupil of the eye.<BR>2 A star.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A float or raft.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pilot, a helmsman or steersman.<BR>2 The name of a demon or evil spirit destroyed by KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass or cause to pass, and ण्वुल् affix; or कन added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकजित्
तारकजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>तारक a demon, and जित् conqueror: also similar names, as तारकारि, तारकहन्, तारकरिपु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकारि|तारकारिः
तारकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>तारक, and अरि a foe: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकित|तारकितं
तारकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Starry.<BR>E.<BR>तारक a star, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकिन्
तारकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किणी-कि)<BR>Starry.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>तारक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारण|तारणः
तारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Who or what causes or enables to cross.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Carrying or conveying across.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारणि|तारणिः
तारणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass over, अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारतम्य|तारतम्यं
तारतम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 More or less, the state or condition.<BR>2 Dependance of larger numbers on smaller in a progressive series.<BR>E.<BR>तर, and तम affixes of the comparative and superlative degrees, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारनाद
तारनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A loud sound or noise.<BR>E.<BR>तार, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल|तारलः
तारल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Libidinous, dissipated, a lecher.<BR>E.<BR>तरल unsteady, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=373" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारविमला
तारविमला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of mineral said to be of the colour of silver.<BR>E.<BR>तार a star, and विमल pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारशुद्धिकर|तारशुद्धिकरं
तारशुद्धिकर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>तार silver, शुद्धिकर what refines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराधिपति
ताराधिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तारा a star, and अधिपति a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारापथ|तारापथः
तारापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The atmosphere, the firmament, heaven or sky.<BR>E.<BR>तारा a star, and पथ for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारापीड|तारापीडः
तारापीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तार a star, and आपीड a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराभूषा
ताराभूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>तारा, and भूषा ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताराभ्र|ताराभ्रः
ताराभ्र<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>तारा, and अभ्र talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारामण्डल|तारामंडल|तारामण्डलः
तारामण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A large splendid temple.<BR>2 The region of the stars.<BR>E.<BR>तारा a star, and मण्डल a region; shining with gold and jewels as with stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारारि|तारारिः
तारारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A pyritic ore of iron: see विट्माक्षिक.<BR>E.<BR>तारा the pupil of the eye, and अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fare, freight, toll.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A star; also तारका.<BR>2 The juice of the palmyra tree, especially when become a spirit by spontaneous fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>तर fare, ठक् affix, or तारक fem. form, or ताल and कन् added, ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिन्
तारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Enabling or causing to cross or get over.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A goddess peculiar to the Jainas or Bauddhas.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cause to proceed, (life, fortune, &c.) and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारीष
तारीष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The daughter of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>तृ to cross, ईषन् affix, fem. affix ङीष्: see तरीष and तविष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण्य|तारुण्यं
तारुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Youth.<BR>E.<BR>तरुण young, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारेय|तारेयः
तारेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of BĀLĪ, the monkey.<BR>E.<BR>तारा the wife of BALI, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्कव|तार्कव
तार्क्कव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Spun, made with or belonging to a spindle.<BR>E.<BR>तर्कु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्किक|तार्किक|तार्किकः
तार्क्किक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or attached to the science of reasoning or logic.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A philosopher, a sophist, a follower of either of the six schools of Hindu philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>तर्क doubt, disputation, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष|तार्क्षः
तार्क्ष<BR>m. (-र्क्षः)<BR>A name of KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्य|तार्क्ष्यं|तार्क्ष्यः
तार्क्ष्य<BR>m. (-र्क्ष्यः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A name of ARUṆA, or the dawn personified, considered as the elder brother of GARUḌA.<BR>4 A car, a chariot.<BR>5 A snake.<BR>6 Gold.<BR>7 A tree, the Sal, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>n. (-र्क्ष्यं)<BR>A sort of collyrium.<BR>f. (-र्क्ष्यी)<BR>A wild creeper.<BR>E.<BR>तृक्ष to go, घञ् affix तार्क्ष and यत् added; again, तृक्ष or तार्क्षं considered as a name of KAŚYAPA the father of ARUṆA, &c. ष्यञ् or अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यध्वज|तार्क्ष्यध्वजः
तार्क्ष्यध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>तार्क्ष्य GARUḌA, and ध्वज emblem or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यनायक|तार्क्ष्यनायकः
तार्क्ष्यनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>तार्क्ष्य, and नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यशैल|तार्क्ष्यशैलं
तार्क्ष्यशैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A substance prepared from the calx of brass, or from the Amomum anthorrhiza, and used as a medical application to the eyes; see रसाञ्जन.<BR>E.<BR>तार्क्ष्य a collyrium, and शैल derived from शिला a rock or stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्य्य|तार्य
तार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be crossed or carried across, to be ferried over.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Toll, fare, freight.<BR>E.<BR>तृ to cross, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताल|तालं|तालः
ताल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Made of the palm wood.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Beating time in music, musical time or measure.<BR>2 A short span, one measured by the thumb and middle finger.<BR>3 Slapping or clapping the hands together, or against the arms, &c.<BR>4 The open hand with the fingers extended, the palm.<BR>5 A musical instrument of bell metal or brass, (a sort of cymbal,) played with a stick.<BR>6 The hilt of a sword or sacrificial knife, &c.<BR>7 The palmyra tree or fan palm, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR>8 A lock, a bolt.<BR>9 In prosody, a trochee.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The throne of DURGĀ.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment: see हरिताल.<BR>3 The fruit of the palm tree.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A sort of key or pin.<BR>2 A species of the mountain palm, (Corypha taliera, Rox.)<BR>3 A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta): see झटा and अमला.<BR>4 A fragrant earth: see तुवरिका.<BR>5 A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>6 The spirituous juice of the palm, the common Toddy.<BR>E.<BR>तल to fix or तन to spread, affix घञ्; or in the causal form, with अच् affix, fem. affix ङीष्, न changed to ल; otherwise, तड to beat, to overcome, (disease, &c.) अच् and ङीष् affixes, and ड changed to ल; the adjective is derived from the substantive by adding अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालक|तालकं
तालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A bolt, a latch, a kind of lock for fastening a door with.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>3 A fragrant earth.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकाभ|तालकाभः
तालकाभ<BR>adj. mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Green.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Green, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>तालक yellow orpiment, and आभ what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकी
तालकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Toddy, or the fermented exudation of the palm trees.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palmyra, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालजटा
तालजटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>The fibres of the palm tree under the outer bark.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, and जटा matted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालध्वज|तालध्वजः
तालध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The name of a city.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palm, and ध्वज a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपत्र|तालपत्रं
तालपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A hollow cylinder of gold with or without a ring attached to it, thrust through the lobe of the ear, and worn as an ornament.<BR>2 The palm leaf.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palmyra, and पत्र a leaf, pieces of the leaf of this tree being rolled up and used occasionally for the purpose or as a substitute.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A plant: see मूषिकपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>as above; the leaves resembling those of the palm tree, or the palm of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपर्ण|तालपर्णं
तालपर्ण<BR>nf. (-र्णं-र्णी)<BR>1 A kind of vegetable perfume: see मुरा.<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A sort of anise, (Anethum pammorium, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palm, and पर्ण a leaf, palm-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालपुष्पक|तालपुष्पकं
तालपुष्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A medicinal application to the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palmyra, पुष्प a flower, and कन् affix; perhaps prepared from the blossoms of the palmyra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालप्रलम्व
तालप्रलम्व<BR>n. (-म्वं)<BR>The fibres that grow on the cocoanut and other palms, under the outer rind, and from which Coir, a sort of cordage, is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, and प्रलम्व what depends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालभृत्
तालभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>तास्व the palm, and भृत् who retains, (as his banner or symbol): see तालध्वज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालमय
तालमय<BR>mn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of the palm, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालमूली
तालमूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palm, and मूल a root, having a similar root; also with कन् added तालमूलिका f. (-का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=374" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालयन्त्र|तालयंत्र
तालयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 A lock, a lock and key.<BR>2 A small pair of pincers.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, and यन्त्र instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताललक्ष्मन्
ताललक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, and लक्ष्मन् a mark or sign: see तालध्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवृन्त|तालवृंत|तालवृन्तं
तालवृन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A fan.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the palm of the hand, and वृन्त a root-stalk; expanding from the hand like a leaf from its stem; also with कन् added तालवृन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवृन्तक|तालवृन्तकं
तालवृन्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fan, a Pankha: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालवेचनक|तालवेचनकः
तालवेचनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dancer, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>ताल musical tone, विच to observe, ल्यु affix, तालवेचन and कन् pleonasm added; also read तालरेचनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालाख्या
तालाख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>A perfume: see मुरा.<BR>E.<BR>ताल, the palmyra, and आख्या a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालाङ्क|तालांक|तालाङ्कः
तालाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>2 A saw.<BR>3 A book.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>5 A man marked with every fortunate spot or sign, &c.<BR>6 A sort of vegetable.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the tree, and अङ्क mark or emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालावचर|तालावचरः
तालावचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A dancer, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>ताल musical time, अवचर to follow or perform, to affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालि|तालिः
तालि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A kind of palm, (Corypha taliera): see ताली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिक|तालिकः
तालिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>The open palm of the hand.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tie, a seal, a string, &c. binding a letter or parcel of papers.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see तालमूली.<BR>E.<BR>ताल as above, and कन् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालित|तालितं
तालित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Any musical instrument.<BR>2 Dyed or coloured cloth.<BR>3 A string, a tie.<BR>E.<BR>ताल musical time, &c. इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिश|तालिशः
तालिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>ताल to be fixed, इश Uṇādi affix, the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीश|तालीशं
तालीश<BR>n. (शं)<BR>A tree, commonly Tālīśa or its leaf.<BR>E.<BR>ताल the corypha, ईश what resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालीशपत्र|तालीशपत्रं
तालीशपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>2 A tree, Tāliśa or its leaf, which is used in medicine.<BR>E.<BR>तालीश as above, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालु
तालु<BR>n. (-लु)<BR>The palate.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, to go, Uṇādi affix, ञुण्; by which words, &c. proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुका
तालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The palate.<BR>E.<BR>तालु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुजिह्व|तालुजिह्वः
तालुजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>1 The uvula.<BR>2 A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>तालु the palate, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुपुप्पुट|तालुपुप्पुटः
तालुपुप्पुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An indolent swelling of the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूर|तालूरः
तालूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR>E.<BR>तल to be deep, उरन् affix; also read तालुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावक
तावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Thine.<BR>E.<BR>तवक, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावकीन|तावकीनं
तावकीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Thine.<BR>E.<BR>तवक for तव thine, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्|तावन्त्
तावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 So many, as many, as much.<BR>2 All.<BR>ind.<BR>So much, so far, so many, unto, until, the correlative to यावत्.<BR>E.<BR>तत् that, then, and डावत् affix: see यावत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावतिक
तावतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Of so much, worth so much, &c. see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्क
तावत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Of so much, bought for so much, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तावत्; also with इट् inserted तावतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्काल
तावत्काल<BR>adv. n. (-लं)<BR>For so long a period, for such a time.<BR>E.<BR>तावत्, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावद्वयस
तावद्वयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Measuring so much.<BR>E.<BR>तावत्, and द्धयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावन्मात्र
तावन्मात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>So much.<BR>E.<BR>तावत्, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावर|तावरं
तावर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A bow string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताविष|ताविषः
ताविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The daughter of INDRA.<BR>2 A river.<BR>3 The earth.<BR>E.<BR>तव a Sautra root, Uṇādi affix टिषच्; also read तविष, तवीष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावुरि|तावुरिः
तावुरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The constellation Taurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तास्कर्य्य|तास्कर्य|तास्कर्यं
तास्कर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>E.<BR>तस्कर, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक
तिक<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) तिकृ (तेकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR>r. 5th cl. (तिक्नोति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To assail, to assault.<BR>3 To seek to injure or kill: see तिग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्त|तिक्तं|तिक्तः
तिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Bitter.<BR>2 Fragrant.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>1 A bitter taste, bitterness.<BR>2 Fragrance, perfume.<BR>3 A medicinal plant, (Echites antidysenterica.)<BR>4 A tree, (Capparis trifoliata): see वरुण.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>Katuki, a medicinal plant.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen, (the appetite,) affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तक|तिक्तकः
तिक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of gourd, (Trichosanthes diœca, Rox.)<BR>2 A sort of gentian, (G. cherayta.)<BR>3 A dark sort of the Khayar or Mimosa catechu.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तिक्त a bitter; alluding to the taste of these substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तगन्धा
तिक्तगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त fragrant, and गन्ध smell, fem. affix टाप्; also with कन् added, and the fem. form, तिक्तगन्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्ततुम्बी
तिक्ततुम्बी<BR>f. (-म्बी)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त, and तुम्बी a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तदुग्धा
तिक्तदुग्धा<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>A medicinal kind of moon plant: see स्वर्णक्षीरी.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तपत्र|तिक्तपत्रः
तिक्तपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica mixta.)<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तपर्व्वन्|तिक्तपर्वन्
तिक्तपर्व्वन्<BR>f. (-र्व्वां)<BR>1 A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR>2 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>3 Liquorice.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तभद्रक|तिक्तभद्रकः
तिक्तभद्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and भद्रक auspicious, useful in medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तरोहिणिका
तिक्तरोहिणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and रोहिणी the same plant, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तवल्ली
तिक्तवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and वल्ली a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तशाक|तिक्तशाकः
तिक्तशाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Capparis trifoliata): see वरुण.<BR>2 A kind of mimosa: see खदिर.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and शाक an esculent vegetable; also तिक्तशाकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तसार|तिक्तसारं|तिक्तसारः
तिक्तसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of mimosa, (M. catechu): see खदिर<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त bitter, and सार pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तिका
तिक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>तिक्त, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग
तिग<BR>r. 5th cl. (तिग्नोति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To assail.<BR>3 To seek to injure, to attempt to kill, &c. also तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म<BR>mfn. (-ग्मः-ग्मा-ग्मं)<BR>1 Hot.<BR>2 Pungent, acrid.<BR>3 Sharp, (as a weapon.)<BR>4 Passionate, hasty.<BR>n. (-ग्मं)<BR>Heat; also the heat of spices, or pungency.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen, Uṇādi affix मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मता
तिग्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sharpness.<BR>2 Pungency.<BR>3 Heat.<BR>4 Passion, petulance.<BR>E.<BR>तल added to तिग्म; also with त्व, तिग्मत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मरुच्
तिग्मरुच्<BR>mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>1 Bright, shining.<BR>2 Hot.<BR>m. (रुक्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तिग्म, and रुच् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्मांशु|तिग्मांशुः
तिग्मांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तिग्म hot, and अंश्रु a ray; also similar compounds, as तिग्मकर, तिग्मरश्मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=375" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिघ
तिघ<BR>r. 5th cl. (तिघ्नोति)<BR>To strike, to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिङ्गुद
तिङ्गुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a plant: see इङ्गुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिज
तिज<BR>r. 1st cl. (तितिक्षते)<BR>To bear, to endure, to suffer with patience.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तेजते तेजयति)<BR>1 To whet, to sharpen.<BR>2 To shine: see तेज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिजिल|तिजिलः
तिजिल<BR>m. (लः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to shine, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिण्टी
तिण्टी<BR>f. (-ण्टी)<BR>A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितउ|तितउः
तितउ<BR>mn. (-उः-उ)<BR>A sieve, a cribble.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread or scatter, (grain, &c.) डौ Uṇādi affix, and the radical reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षा
तितिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Patience, resignation, sufferance, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to bear, अङ् and टाप् affix, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षित|तितिक्षितः
तितिक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Patient, resigned.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to bear, affix इतच्, and the root reduplicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षु|तितिक्षुः
तितिक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Patient, resigned.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to bear, reduplicated, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिभ|तितिभः
तितिभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>An insect, coccinella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिल|तितिलं
तितिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 One of the seven Karaṇas, or astronomical periods so called.<BR>2 A bowl or bucket.<BR>3 A sort of sweetmeat made of sesamum, ground, and baked with sugar.<BR>E.<BR>तिल to go, affix क, and the radical reiterated: see तैतिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षा
तितीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>1 Wish to cross.<BR>2 Wish to be freed from life.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, desid, form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितीर्षु
तितीर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>1 Desirous of crossing.<BR>2 Desirous of emancipation from existence.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to cross, desid. form, affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिर|तित्तिरः
तित्तिर<BR>m. (रः)<BR>The francoline partridge: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तित्तिरि|तित्तिरिः
तित्तिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 The francoline partridge.<BR>2 The name of a Muni, and one of the early teachers of the Taittiri or Black Yajur Veda.<BR>3 The Yajur Veda, named after its teacher.<BR>E.<BR>तित्ति an imitative sound, रा to make, affix कि; also with क affix तित्तिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथ|तिथः
तिथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 KĀMA or love.<BR>3 Time.<BR>E.<BR>तिथ to inflame, Uṇādi affix थक्, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथि|तिथिः
तिथि<BR>mf. (-थिः-थिः or -थी)<BR>A lunar day, (1/30)th of a whole lunation.<BR>E.<BR>अत to go, to proceed, affix इथिन् and the radical initial rejected; also ङीष् being added तिथी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथिक्षय|तिथिक्षयः
तिथिक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>तिथि, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिथिप्रणी
तिथिप्रणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तिथि a lunar day, प्र before णी to get or obtain, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनाशक|तिनाशकः
तिनाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिनिश|तिनिशः
तिनिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia ougeiniensis.)<BR>E.<BR>अति exceeding, निश to meditate, affix क and the initial of the prefix rejected, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिड|तिंतिड|तिंतिडः|तिन्तिडः
तिन्तिड<BR>mf. (-डः-डी)<BR>The tamarind tree, (Tamarindus Indica.)<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 The name of a demon.<BR>2 Acid seasoning, sour sauce.<BR>3 An inauspicious period, the evil aspect of planets, &c.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be damp or moist, अच् affix, the root reduplicated, and ड substituted for the final म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडिका|तिंतिडिका
तिन्तिडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तिन्तिडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडीक|तिंतिडीक|तिन्तिडीकं|तिंतिडीकः|तिन्तिडीकः
तिन्तिडीक<BR>subst. mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Acid seasoning.<BR>2 The fruit of the tamarind.<BR>E.<BR>तिन्तिड as above, and ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिडीद्यूत
तिन्तिडीद्यूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A kind of game, a sort of odd or even played with tamarind seeds.<BR>E.<BR>तिन्तिडी the tamarind, and द्यूत playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्तिली|तिंतिली
तिन्तिली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The tamarind tree.<BR>E.<BR>see तिन्तिड, ल being substituted for ड; also कन् being added in the usual form, तिन्तिलिका, or retaining the final तिन्तिलीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दु|तिंदु|तिंदुः|तिन्दुः
तिन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A species of ebony, from the fruit of which a kind of resin is obtained, that is used in India as pitch for caulking vessels, &c. (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be wet or moist, affix कु; also with कन् added, तिन्दुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुक|तिंदुक|तिंदुकं|तिन्दुकं|तिंदुकः|तिन्दुकः
तिन्दुक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The resinous fruit of this tree: see the preceding. Also with इ substituted for the final तिन्दुकि.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A Karṣa, the measure.<BR>E.<BR>तिन्दु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिन्दुल|तिंदुल|तिंदुलः|तिन्दुलः
तिन्दुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of ebony: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>लच् added to तिन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिप
तिप<BR>(उ ऋ) उ तिपृ r. 1st cl. (तेपते)<BR>To sprinkle, to distil or drop, to ooze or leak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम
तिम<BR>r. 4th cl. (तिम्यति)<BR>To be or become wet, damp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिम
तिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A fish: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमि|तिमिः
तिमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A whale, or a fabulous fish of an enormous size, said to be one hundred Yojanas long.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>तम to distress, इन् affix, and इ substituted for the radical vowel; otherwise तिम to be wet or watery, affix कि, or with क affix तिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिकोष|तिमिकोषः
तिमिकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>तिमि a fish, as above, and कोष receptacle: also तिमिकोषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिङ्गिल|तिमिंगिल|तिमिंगिलः|तिमिङ्गिलः
तिमिङ्गिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large fabulous fish: see तिमि.<BR>E.<BR>तिमि the fish so called, and गिल who swallows, (from गॄ with क affix, र changed to ल) and मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिङ्गिलगिल|तिमिंगिलगिल|तिमिङ्गिलगिलः
तिमिङ्गिलगिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fabulous fish larger than either of the preceding: see तिमि and तिमिंगिल.<BR>E.<BR>तिमिङ्गिल the fish so called, and गिल who devours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमित|तिमितः
तिमित<BR>mn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wet, moist, moistened, damp.<BR>2 Steady, fixed, unmoved, unshaken.<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be wet or damp, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिर|तिमिरं|तिमिरः
तिमिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>2 Gutta serena, total blindness from affection of the optic nerve.<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be damp, or तम to give pain, किरच् Uṇādi affix, in the latter case इत् is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिररिपु|तिमिररिपुः
तिमिररिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तिमिर darkness, and रिपु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिमिष|तिमिषः
तिमिष<BR>n. (-षः)<BR>1 A kind of pumpkin gourd: see ग्राम्यकर्क्कटी.<BR>2 A watermelon.<BR>E.<BR>तम to desire or be desired, इषच् affix, इत् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरश्चीन
तिरश्चीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sideways, awry, irregular.<BR>E.<BR>तिय्यच् and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्
तिरस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Indirectly, underhandedly, secretly, covertly.<BR>5 Crookedly, awry.<BR>6 A particle of abuse or depreciation.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to go, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्करिणी
तिरस्करिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 An outer tent, a Kenāt, a wall or screen of cloth surrounding the principal tent.<BR>2 A veil.<BR>3 A curtain.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस् secret, and करिणी making; also with the antepen. vowel long, तिरस्कारिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=376" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कार|तिरस्कारः
तिरस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Disrespect, abuse, reproach.<BR>2 Disappearance, concealment.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस् disrespect, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्कृत|तिरस्कृतः
तिरस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reviled, abused, reproached, censured.<BR>2 Veiled, hidden.<BR>3 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरस्क्रिया
तिरस्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Disrespect, contempt, reproach.<BR>2 Disappearance, concealment.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस् disrespect, and क्रिया action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिट
तिरिट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The joint of the sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिम|तिरिमः
तिरिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरिय|तिरियः
तिरिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरीट|तिरीटं|तिरीटः
तिरीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Pale Lodh, a kind of tree: see लोध्र.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A diadem, a tiara.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, कीटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोगत
तिरोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disappeared, vanished, out of sight.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोधान|तिरोधानं
तिरोधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A cover or concealment, a sheath, a veil, a cloth or cloak, any thing which withholds another from sight.<BR>2 Disappearance, the being hidden or the act of hiding or vanishing.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस् concealing, and धान having or holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिरोहित|तिरोहितः
तिरोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, concealed, hidden, removed or withdrawn from sight.<BR>E.<BR>तिरम् covering, धा to have, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यक्|तिर्यक्
तिर्य्यक्<BR>ind.<BR>Crookedly, awry: see तिर्य्यच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यक्स्रोतस्|तिर्यक्स्रोतस्
तिर्य्यक्स्रोतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>An animal, a beast or bird.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यक् crookedly, and स्रोतस् motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्ज|तिर्यग्ज
तिर्य्यग्ज<BR>mfn. (-ग्जः-ग्जा-ग्जं)<BR>Born of an animal or insect.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यच्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्जाति|तिर्यग्जाति|तिर्यग्जातिः
तिर्य्यग्जाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of the brute species, born as an animal.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The brute kind.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यच्, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्यवोदर|तिर्यग्यवोदर
तिर्य्यग्यवोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A barley corn.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यच् curved, यव barley, उदर the interior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्यान|तिर्यग्यान|तिर्यग्यानः|तिर्य्यग्यानः
तिर्य्यग्यान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यक् crookedly, and यान motion, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्योनि|तिर्यग्योनि|तिर्यग्योनिः
तिर्य्यग्योनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Born of or as an animal.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यच्, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यग्योन्यन्वय|तिर्यग्योन्यन्वय
तिर्य्यग्योन्यन्वय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of the brute kind.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The race or kind of animals, birds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तिर्य्यग्योनि, and अन्वय race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिर्य्यच्|तिर्यच्
तिर्य्यच् or तिर्य्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (तिर्य्यङ् तिरञ्ची तिर्य्यक्)<BR>Moving tortuously, going crookedly or awry, (the neuter is also used adverbially: see तिर्य्यक्.)<BR>m. (-र्य्यङ्)<BR>1 An animal, a quadruped.<BR>2 A bird, or any animal moving tortuously.<BR>f. (-र्य्यञ्ची)<BR>The female of an animal, a beast or bird.<BR>E.<BR>तिरस् crookedly, अञ्च to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल<BR>r. 1st cl. (तेलति)<BR>To go.<BR>r. 6th cl. (तिलति) and 10th cl. (तेलयति)<BR>1 To be unctuous or greasy.<BR>2 To oil or anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल|तिलः
तिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant bearing an oily seed; the oil and seed being both much used in Oriental cooking, (Sesamum orientale.)<BR>2 A mole or spot, compared to a seed of sesamum.<BR>3 A small particle or portion.<BR>E.<BR>तिल to be unctuous, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलक|तिलकं|तिलकः
तिलक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Spotted, freckled, a person having moles or spots.<BR>2 Chief, principal.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A mark or marks made with coloured earths or unguents upon the forehead, and between the eye-brows, either as an ornament or a sectarial distinction.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A freckle, a natural mark on the person.<BR>2 A kind of tree, commonly Tila.<BR>3 A sort of horse.<BR>4 A title, especially in composition, implying pre-eminence, as रघुवंशतिलकः the Tilaka of the race of RAGHU, a name of RĀMA.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The bladder.<BR>2 Black Sochal salt, a factitious salt, containing sulphur and iron, &c.<BR>3 A disease, the appearance of dark spots on the skin, unattended with inflammation.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of necklace.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, &c. कन् added, or तिल to go or be unctuous, and क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकट|तिलकटः
तिलकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The farina of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकल्क|तिलकल्कः
तिलकल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>Sesamum ground or bruised.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and कल्क sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकालक|तिलकालकः
तिलकालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A mole, a spot on the body.<BR>2 A man so marked.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum seed, and काल black, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकाश्रय|तिलकाश्रयः
तिलकाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>तिलक, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकिट्ट|तिलकिट्टं
तिलकिट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>The sediment or cake of sesamum after the oil is expressed.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलकिन्
तिलकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>1 Marked with the Tilaka.<BR>2 Freckled, spotted.<BR>E.<BR>तिलक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलचूर्ण|तिलचूर्णं|तिलचूर्ण्ण
तिलचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Sesamum ground or pounded.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलतण्डुलक|तिलतंडुलक|तिलतण्डुलकं
तिलतण्डुलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An embrace, embracing.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and तण्डुल grain, कन् affix, as agreeable as rice mixed with sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलतैल|तिलतैलं
तिलतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sesamum oil.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and तैलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलधेनु|तिलधेनुः
तिलधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>Sesamum made up in the shape of a cow, for the purpose of being presented to Brahmans, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्ण|तिलपर्णं|तिलपर्णः
तिलपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 The leaf of the Tila tree.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णिका
तिलपर्णिका<BR>mfn. (-का)<BR>Red sanders: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तिलपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपर्णी|तिलपर्ण्णी
तिलपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santolinus.)<BR>E.<BR>तिल the sesamum plant, and पर्ण a leaf: see तैलपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिच्चट|तिलपिच्चटं
तिलपिच्चट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A sort of sweetmeat, made chiefly of ground sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपिञ्ज|तिलपिञ्जः
तिलपिञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>Barren sesamum, bearing no blossom, or its seed yielding no oil.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and पिञ्ज affix, in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलपेज|तिलपेजः
तिलपेज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Barren sesamum: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and पेज affix, with this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलमय
तिलमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or composed of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलमयूर|तिलमयूरः
तिलमयूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of peafowl.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and मयूर a peacock: marked with spots resembling the seed of the sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलरस|तिलरसः
तिलरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Sesamum oil.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and रस extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलस्नेह|तिलस्नेहः
तिलस्नेह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Oil, especially from sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and स्नेह grease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलहोम|तिलहोमः
तिलहोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Burnt offering of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and होम burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलापत्या
तिलापत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A plant, bearing a small pungent seed, (Nigella Indica).<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and अपत्य offspring as it were, from the resemblance of the seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=377" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलित्स|तिलित्सः
तिलित्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>A large snake, according to some, the same as the Gokhura, to others the Böa, (Böa constrictor.)<BR>E.<BR>तिलत् here said to imply motion, षो to destroy, and क affix, destroying life or loco-motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलोत्तमा
तिलोत्तमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>One of the courtezans of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>तिल a mole, and उत्तम excellent, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलोदक
तिलोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sesamum seeds and water, as an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिलौदन|तिलौदनं|तिलौदनः
तिलौदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A dish of milk, rice, and sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and ओदन boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्य|तिल्यं
तिल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>A field of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल, with क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्ल
तिल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (तिल्लति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिल्व|तिल्वः
तिल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A pale sort of Lodh: see लोध्र.<BR>E.<BR>तिल to anoint, and व affix; also with कन् added तिल्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठत्|तिष्ठन्त्
तिष्ठत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठन्-ष्ठन्ती-ष्ठत्)<BR>Staying, abiding, standing, being.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to stay, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्ठद्गु|तिष्ठद्गुः
तिष्ठद्गु<BR>n. (-द्गु)<BR>Evening, sun-set, the time which a cow stands to be milked, &c.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to stand, गौ a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्य|तिष्यः
तिष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Auspicious, fortunate, lucky.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>1 The eighth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion, an asterism figured by an arrow, and containing three stars, of which one is δ Cancri.<BR>2 The month Pauṣa, (December-January.)<BR>3 The Kali Yug, the fourth and present age.<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please or delight, affix क्यप्, and इत् substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यक|तिष्यकः
तिष्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Pauṣa: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तिष्य, the moon being then in that asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यपुष्प
तिष्यपुष्प<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>तिष्य auspicious, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिष्यफला
तिष्यफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Emblic myrobalan: see तिष्य.<BR>E.<BR>तिष्य auspicious, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिहन्
तिहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>1 Sickness.<BR>2 Rice.<BR>3 A bow.<BR>4 A good disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक
तीक<BR>(ऋ) तीकृ r. 1st cl. (तिकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्ण|तीक्ष्णं|तीक्ष्णः
तीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Hot, warm.<BR>2 Hot, pungent.<BR>3 Selfdevoted, self-abandoning, committing suicide, &c.<BR>4 Zealous, active, warm.<BR>5 Keen, intelligent.<BR>6 Devout, ascetic, a devotee, a zealot.<BR>7 Sharp, (as a sword.)<BR>n. (-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Heat, warmth.<BR>2 Poison.<BR>3 Iron.<BR>4 War, battle.<BR>5 Plague, pestilence, epidemic destruction.<BR>6 Death, dying.<BR>7 Any weapon.<BR>8 Haste, hurry.<BR>9 Sea salt.<BR>10 The scrotum or testicles.<BR>11 Any metal.<BR>12 Pungency, the heat of pepper, &c.<BR>m. (-क्ष्णः)<BR>Nitre.<BR>f. (-क्ष्णा)<BR>1 Orris root.<BR>2 The cast skin of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen or be sharp, Uṇādi affix क्स्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णक|तीक्ष्णकः
तीक्ष्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The scrotum or the testicles.<BR>2 White mustard.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकण्टक|तीक्ष्णकण्टकः
तीक्ष्णकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकन्द|तीक्ष्णकंद|तीक्ष्णकन्दः
तीक्ष्णकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The onion.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण pungent, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णकर्म्मन्|तीक्ष्णकर्मन्
तीक्ष्णकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Active, zealous.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, keen, and कर्म्मन् conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णगन्ध|तीक्ष्णगन्धः
तीक्ष्णगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Morunga hyperanthera.<BR>2 The gum olibanum tree.<BR>3 Small cardamoms.<BR>4 A tree: see जियती.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Mustard seed.<BR>2 Orris root.<BR>3 Pandanus odoratissimus.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, and गन्ध smell; also with कन् added तीक्ष्णगन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णतण्डुला
तीक्ष्णतण्डुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Long-pepper.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण pungent, and तण्डल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णतैल|तीक्ष्णतैलं
तीक्ष्णतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Resin.<BR>2 The milky juice of the Euphorbia.<BR>3 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण hot, pungent, and तैल oil, unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्र|तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्रः
तीक्ष्णदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, and दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णधार|तीक्ष्णधारः
तीक्ष्णधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Sharp-edged, sharp.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण, and धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णपत्र|तीक्ष्णपत्रः
तीक्ष्णपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण pungent, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णपुष्प|तीक्ष्णपुष्पं
तीक्ष्णपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण pungent, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णफल|तीक्ष्णफलः
तीक्ष्णफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण pungent, and फल fruit, bearing pungent seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णरस|तीक्ष्णरसः
तीक्ष्णरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णशूक|तीक्ष्णशूकः
तीक्ष्णशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण sharp, and शूक awn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णाग्नि|तीक्ष्णाग्निः
तीक्ष्णाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Heartburn, dyspepsia.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण, and अग्नि digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीक्ष्णायस|तीक्ष्णायसं
तीक्ष्णायस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Made of steel, sharp.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Steel.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण, and अयस् iron, टच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीम
तीम<BR>r. 4th cl. (तीम्यति)<BR>To be wet or moist: see तिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर<BR>r. 10th cl. (तीरयति)<BR>To finish or complete, to get through or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर|तीरं|तीरः
तीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A shore, a bank.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Tin.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A kind of arrow.<BR>E.<BR>तीर to get through or over, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरभुक्ति|तीरभुक्तिः
तीरभुक्ति<BR>m. (-क्तिः)<BR>Tirhut, a province in the east of central Hindustan, lying on the north of Behar.<BR>E.<BR>तीर a bank, and भुक्ति here signifying a limit: being bounded on the west and east by the Gandaki and Kauśikī rivers, on the south by the Ganges, and on the north, by the skirts of the Himāla mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीराट
तीराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Lodh: see तिरीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरान्तर
तीरान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The opposite bank or shore.<BR>E.<BR>तीर, and अन्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीरित|तीरितं
तीरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Adjudged, settled, finished.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Completion of any act or affair.<BR>2 Corrupt or improper non-infliction of a sentence.<BR>E.<BR>तीर to get through, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्ण|तीर्णः
तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Crossed, passed over.<BR>2 Spread, expanded.<BR>3 Surpassed, excelled.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्णपदी
तीर्णपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A plant: see तालमूली.<BR>E.<BR>तीर्ण spreading, and पाद foot or root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्णवत्
तीर्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Crossed, having crossed.<BR>E.<BR>त to cross, affix क्तवतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थ|तीर्थं|तीर्थः
तीर्थ<BR>mn. (-र्थः-र्थं)<BR>1 Sacred science, or any of the branches of knowledge esteemed holy.<BR>2 A holy place, any place of pilgrimage, as Benares, &c. but especially particular spots along the course of sacred streams, as the Ganges, &c. and in the vicinity of some piece of water or sacred springs.<BR>3 Any piece of water.<BR>4 A Ghāt or stairs of a landing place.<BR>5 A sacred preceptor, a Guru.<BR>6 Sacrifice.<BR>7 An Avatāra or descent of a deity.<BR>8 A school of philosophy, a Darśana, a sect.<BR>9 A counsellor, an adviser.<BR>10 An expedient, a means of success.<BR>11 The menses.<BR>12 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>13 A vessel.<BR>14 A royal vessel.<BR>15 A Brahman.<BR>16 Ascertainment of disease.<BR>17 Fire.<BR>18 A part of the hand sacred to any [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">Page379</a>] deity, as between the thumb and finger to the manes, the root of the thumb to BRAHMA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass over, थक् Uṇādi affix; by which persons are extricated from sin, difficulty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=378" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकर|तीर्थकरः
तीर्थकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One of the synonyms of a Jina or sanctified teacher of the Jaina sect.<BR>E.<BR>तीर्थ pure, purity, and कर who does or acts; also retaining the nasal तीर्थङ्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थकृत्
तीर्थकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A Jina: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थध्वाङ्क्ष|तीर्थध्वांक्ष|तीर्थध्वाङ्क्षः
तीर्थध्वाङ्क्ष<BR>m. (-ङ्क्षः)<BR>An epithet of contempt, a crow, as it were, at a pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>तीर्थ, and ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थराजी
तीर्थराजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>A name of Benāres.<BR>E.<BR>तीर्थ a holy place, and राजी the queen: the most eminent of the Tīrthas or places of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थवाक|तीर्थवाकः
तीर्थवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A curl of hair.<BR>E.<BR>तीर्थ, and वच to speak, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीर्थसेविन्
तीर्थसेविन्<BR>mf. (-वी-विनी)<BR>1 A pilgrim.<BR>2 A sort of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>तीर्थ, and सेविन् who frequents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव
तीव<BR>r. 1st cl. (-तीवति)<BR>To be large, to be fat or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीवर|तीवरः
तीवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A hunter, one who lives by killing and selling game.<BR>3 A fisherman, one who lives by fishing.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The wife of a hunter.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to go, to pass or cross, ष्वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्र|तीव्रं|तीव्रः
तीव्र<BR>mfn. (-व्रः-व्रा-व्रं)<BR>1 Much, excessive, endless, unbounded, unlimited.<BR>2 Pungent.<BR>3 Hot, warm.<BR>m. (-व्रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-व्रा)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, Katuki.<BR>2 Black mustard.<BR>3 A sort of Dūrvā or bent grass, (गण्डदूर्व्वा)<BR>4 The name of a river in the east of Bengal; also the Caṇḍī or Padmāvatī.<BR>adv. n. (-व्रं)<BR>1 Much, excessively, endless.<BR>2 Violently, fiercely.<BR>subst.<BR>1 A shore, a bank.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>3 Heat.<BR>4 Pungency.<BR>E.<BR>तीव to be large, &c. रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तीव्रवेदना
तीव्रवेदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Agony, excessive pain, the pain of damnation.<BR>E.<BR>तीव्र exceeding, and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (तौति or तवति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To thrive or increase.<BR>3 To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>4 To become full. According to some authorities this is merely a Sautra root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तु
तु<BR>ind.<BR>A particle, implying,<BR>1 Difference, (but, or.)<BR>2 Disjunction, (but, again, further, other.)<BR>3 Connexion, (and, moreover.)<BR>4 Asseveration, (indeed.)<BR>5 An expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुकाक्षीरी
तुकाक्षीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The manna of bambus; also तुगा and सुगाक्षीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगा
तुगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The manna of bambus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुगाक्षीरी
तुगाक्षीरी<BR>f. (री)<BR>Bambu manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्ग|तुंग|तुङ्गः
तुङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 High, elevated, lofty.<BR>2 Chief, principal.<BR>3 Passionate, hot.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 The planet Mercury.<BR>4 The superior apsis or aphelion of a planet.<BR>5 Top, vertex, altitude.<BR>6 The cocoanut tree.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A kind of basil, (Ocymum gratissimum.)<BR>2 Turmerick.<BR>3 Night.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>तुजि to guard, to dwell, to hurt, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गक|तुङ्गकः
तुङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गता
तुङ्गता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Loftiness.<BR>2 Passionateness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to तुङ्ग; also with त्व, तुङ्गत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गभद्र|तुंगभद्र|तुङ्गभद्रः
तुङ्गभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A restive elephant or one in rut.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A river in the Mysur country, the Toombhadra.<BR>E.<BR>तुङ्ग lofty, tall, &c. and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गशेखर|तुंगशेखर|तुङ्गशेखरः
तुङ्गशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>तुङ्ग lofty, and शेखर crest or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गिन्|तुंगिन्
तुङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>High, lofty.<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A planet at the apex of its orbit, or of its position, with regard to others considered astrologically.<BR>E.<BR>तुङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गीपति|तुंगीपति|तुङ्गीपतिः
तुङ्गीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तुङ्गी night, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुङ्गीश|तुंगीश|तुङ्गीशः
तुङ्गीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>तुङ्गी night, or तुङ्ग a mountain, &c. and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छ|तुच्छं|तुच्छः
तुच्छ<BR>mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>1 Void, empty.<BR>2 Small, little.<BR>3 Abandoned, deserted.<BR>4 Low, contemptible.<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>Chaff.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, Uṇādi affix छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छधान्यक|तुच्छधान्यकं|तुच्छधान्यकः
तुच्छधान्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Straw.<BR>E.<BR>तुच्छ, and धान्यक grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुच्छद्रु|तुच्छद्रुः
तुच्छद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The castor oil tree.<BR>E.<BR>तुच्छ empty, pithless, द्रु a tree; having no sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज्
तुज्<BR>m. (तुक्)<BR>Offspring, children.<BR>E.<BR>तुज to guard, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुज|तुजः
तुज<BR>r. 1st cl. (तोजति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR>(इ) तुजि r. 1st cl. (तुञ्जति)<BR>To guard or protect.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुञ्जति तुञ्जयति)<BR>1 To dwell, to abide.<BR>2 To be strong or vigorous.<BR>3 To give.<BR>4 To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>5 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुञ्ज|तुंज
तुञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>Noxious, mischievous.<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>A Daitya, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>तुजि to hurt, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुट
तुट<BR>r. 6th cl. (तुटति)<BR>1 To dispute, to quarrel, to wrangle.<BR>2 To hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुटुम|तुटुमः
तुटुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>तुट to injure, affix उम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड
तुड<BR>(ऋ) तुडृ (तोडति) also (इ) तुडि r. 1st cl. (तुण्डते) also तुड r. 6th cl. (तुडति)<BR>1 To tear, to break or cut, to pull to pieces, to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुड्ड
तुड्ड<BR>r. 1st cl. (तुड्डति)<BR>To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण
तुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (तुणति)<BR>1 To curve, to bend or make crooked.<BR>2 To act fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुणि|तुणिः
तुणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A timber tree: see तुन्न.<BR>E.<BR>तूण to shrink or warp, affix कि, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्ड|तुंड|तुंडं|तुण्डं|तुण्डः
तुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The mouth, the face.<BR>E.<BR>तुडि to tear, (food, &c.) affix अण्, and कन् being added तुण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डकेरी
तुण्डकेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>तुण्डक the mouth, ऋ to go, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डि|तुंडि|तुंडिः|तुण्डिः
तुण्डि<BR>mf. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी)<BR>1 The mouth, the face.<BR>2 A beak.<BR>3 The navel; (also तुन्दि.)<BR>E.<BR>तुडि to break or destroy, Uṇādi affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिका
तुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The navel.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Telakuca.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तुण्डी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेरी|तुंडिकेरी
तुण्डिकेरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The cotton plant.<BR>2 A sort of gourd, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>2 A large boil or swelling on the palate.<BR>E.<BR>तुण्डिका the mouth or beak, ऋ to go, affixes अण् and ङीष्; also with कन् added तुण्डिकेरिका. f. (-का) and with इन् fem. affix तुण्ठिकेरि. f. (-रिः) also तुण्डकेरी and तुण्डिकेशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिकेशी
तुण्डिकेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A sort of gourd, commonly Telakuca: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिभ|तुंडिभ|तुण्डिभः
तुण्डिभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Having a prominent or elevated navel.<BR>E.<BR>तुण्डि the navel, भ affix; also तुन्दिभ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुण्डिल|तुंडिल|तुण्डिलः
तुण्डिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Having a prominent or elevated navel.<BR>2 Speaking harshly or severely.<BR>E.<BR>तुण्डि the navel, and ल affix; also तुन्दिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=379" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ<BR>r. 10th cl. (तुत्थयति)<BR>1 To screen, to veil, to cover.<BR>2 To spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थ|तुत्थं|तुत्थः
तुत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>Fire.<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>1 Indigo.<BR>2 Small cardamoms.<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>1 A collyrium extracted from the Amomum zanthorrhiza.<BR>2 Blue vitriol, sulphate of copper, especially medicinally considered as an Añjana, or application to the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to pain, थक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थक|तुत्थकं
तुत्थक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to तुत्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुत्थाञ्जन|तुत्थांजन|तुत्थाञ्जनं
तुत्थाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Blue vitriol, considered as a medicinal application to the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>तुत्थ the same, and अञ्जन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुद
तुद<BR>(औ) r. 6th cl. (तुदति-ते)<BR>To pain, to wound, to vex or harass, to tease, to torture or torment.<BR>(इ) तुदि r. 1st cl. (तुन्दति)<BR>To search, to seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्द|तुंद|तुंदं|तुन्दं|तुन्दः
तुन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The belly.<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>The navel: see तुण्डि.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to torment, क affix, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दकूपी|तुंदकूपी
तुन्दकूपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The navel.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्द the belly, and कूप a pit, a well, dim. affix ङीष्; also with कन् added तुन्दकूर्पिका, f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दपरिमार्ज|तुंदपरिमार्ज|तुन्दपरिमार्ज्जः
तुन्दपरिमार्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः)<BR>A lazy man, a sloth, a sluggard: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दपरिमृज|तुन्दपरिमृजः
तुन्दपरिमृज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A lazy man, a sluggard.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्द the belly, मृज to rub, with परि prefixed, and क affix; also with the affix घञ्, तुन्दपरिमार्ज as above; passing his whole time in stroking his sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दवत्|तुंदवत्|तुन्दवन्त्
तुन्दवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Corpulent, fat.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्द, and मतुप् aff. also from तुन्दि, तुन्दिवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दि|तुंदि|तुन्दिः
तुन्दि<BR>n. (-न्दि)<BR>The belly.<BR>f. (-न्दिः)<BR>The navel.<BR>m. (-न्दिः)<BR>One of the Gandharbas or quiristers of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to vex or harass, affix इन्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिक|तुंदिक|तुन्दिकः
तुन्दिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having a large or prominent navel, fat, corpulent.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The navel.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्दी the navel, कन् affix, or तुन्द with ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिकर|तुंदिकरः|तुन्दिकरः
तुन्दिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दित|तुंदित|तुन्दितः
तुन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having a large or prominent navel.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्द with इतच् affix; also तुन्दिक, तुन्दिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिन्|तुंदिन्
तुन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>Having a large or prominent navel.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्द with इनि affix; also तुन्दिक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिभ|तुंदिभ|तुन्दिभः
तुन्दिभ.<BR>See तुण्डिभ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्दिल|तुंदिल|तुन्दिलः
तुन्दिल.<BR>See तुण्डिल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्न|तुन्नः
तुन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Tormented, vexed, injured.<BR>2 Cut, broken, cut down, &c.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>Toon or Tuna, a tree of which the wood bears some resemblance to mahogany, and is used for furniture, &c. (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>E.<BR>तुद to vex, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नवाय|तुन्नवायः
तुन्नवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्न cut, (cloth, &c.) and वे to sew, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुन्नसेवनी
तुन्नसेवनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A suture of the skull.<BR>E.<BR>तुन्न cut, and सेवनी a suture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुप
तुप<BR>r. 1st 6th and 10 cls. (तोपति, तुपति, तोपयति) also (इ) तुपि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुम्पति तुम्पयति)<BR>To injure, to hurt or kill; also तुफ, तुम्ब, तुम्प, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुफ
तुफ<BR>r. 1st, 6th and 10th cls. (तोफति तुफति तोफयति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुब
तुब<BR>(इ) तुबि r. 1st and 10th cls. (तुम्बति तुम्बयति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR>r. 10th cl. (तुम्बयति)<BR>To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुभ
तुभ<BR>r. 1st cl. (तोभते) 4th cl. (तुभ्यति) 9th cl. (तुभ्नाति)<BR>To kill, to hurt, to injure in any manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुर|तुमुरः
तुमुर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Mingled combat: see तुमुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुमुल|तुमुलं|तुमुलः
तुमुल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Mingled or tumultuous combat.<BR>2 Uproar, clangour, tumult, tumultuous sound or noise.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>तु a Sautra root, to kill, to injure, &c. मुलक affix; or with the vowel long तुमूल. mn. (-लः-लं) and ल being changed to र, तुमुर as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्प
तुम्प<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (तुम्पति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To be distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्फ
तुम्फ<BR>r. 1st cl. (तुम्फति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्ब|तुंब|तुंबः|तुम्बः
तुम्ब<BR>mf. (-म्बः-म्बा or म्बी)<BR>A long gourd, &c. see तुम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A cow disposed to be milked.<BR>E.<BR>तुबि to destroy, (bile, &c.) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बक|तुम्बकः
तुम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A long gourd.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The gourd.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding: see तुम्बि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बि|तुंबि|तुंबिः|तुम्बिः
तुम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बिः or तुम्बी)<BR>A long gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaris.)<BR>E.<BR>तुबि to destroy, (bile, sickness, &c.) अच् affix; fem. affix इन् or ङीष्; also with कन् added तुम्बिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बीपुष्प|तुम्बीपुष्पं
तुम्बीपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>The flower of the Cucurbita lagenaris.<BR>E.<BR>तुम्बी, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरी
तुम्बुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Coriander.<BR>2 A bitch: see तुम्बुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुम्बुरु|तुंबुरु|तुंबुरुः|तुम्बुरुः
तुम्बुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 One of the Gandharbas or singers of heaven.<BR>2 A celestial inhabitant and attendant upon the sanctified Jaina teachers.<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>तुबि to hurt, &c. उरन् affix; also with the pen. long तुम्बूरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर<BR>r. 3rd cl. (तुतोर्त्ति)<BR>To go quick, to hurry, to make haste; this root is restricted to the Vedas: see त्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर|तुरः
तुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Quick, swift.<BR>E.<BR>तुर to make haste, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरग|तुरगः
तुरग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 The mind.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर speed, velocity, and ग what goes, व changed to उ.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>1 A plant, (Physalis flexuosa): see अश्वगन्ध.<BR>2 A mare.<BR>E.<BR>ङीष् added to तुरग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगगन्धा
तुरगगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>तुरग a horse, and गन्ध small, smelling like a horse; also अश्वगन्ध, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्यक|तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यकं
तुरगब्रह्मचर्य्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Necessary celibacy, leading a life of continence, in consequence merely of being without female society.<BR>E.<BR>तुरग a horse, and ब्रह्मचर्य्यक the practice of a religious student, one of whose duties is continence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरगिन्
तुरगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Equestrian, riding, mounted or carried on a horse.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>A horseman, cavalier, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तुरग a horse, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्ग|तुरंग|तुरंगः|तुरङ्गः
तुरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 The mind, considered as the seat of feeling as well as intellect, the heart.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर speedily, and ग what goes.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A plant: see तुरगी and तुरगगन्धा.<BR>2 A mare.<BR>E.<BR>ङीष् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गक|तुरंगक|तुरंगकः|तुरङ्गकः
तुरङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, a kind of Ghosha, commonly हस्तिघोष.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग a horse, and कन् affix of analogy; coursing through the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गद्विषणी|तुरंगद्विषणी
तुरङ्गद्विषणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A she buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग, and द्विषणी disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गप्रिय|तुरंगप्रिय|तुरङ्गप्रियः
तुरङ्गप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गम|तुरंगम|तुरंगमः|तुरङ्गमः
तुरङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर speed, and गम to go, with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गयायिन्|तुरंगयायिन्
तुरङ्गयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Going on horseback.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=380" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गवक्त्र|तुरंगवक्त्र|तुरङ्गवक्त्रः
तुरङ्गवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A Kinnara or quirister of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग a horse, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गवदन|तुरंगवदन|तुरङ्गवदनः
तुरङ्गवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A celestial quirister.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग a horse, and वदन a face; these beings are described as having the bodies of men, and the heads of horses; also similar compounds, as तुरङ्गानन, तुरङ्गवक्त्र, तुगङ्गास्य, अश्ववक्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गारि|तुरंगारि|तुरङ्गारिः
तुरङ्गारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 Oleander.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग, and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरङ्गिन्|तुरंगिन्
तुरङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A horseman, a rider.<BR>2 A groom.<BR>E.<BR>तुरङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरायण|तुरायणं|तुरायणः
तुरायण<BR>subst. mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Attachment to any object or pursuit.<BR>adj.<BR>Attached to any object or pursuit.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A particular sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर speed, haste, अय to go, affix ल्यु; speeding towards a given end or in a certain cause: see परायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरासाह्
तुरासाह्<BR>m. (-षाट् or षाड्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>तुर for त्वर haste, सह to bear, in the causal form, and क्विप् affix, स being changed to ष in inflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरि|तुरिः
तुरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>See the next; also तुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरी
तुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A brush or a fibrous stick used by weavers to clean and separate the threads of the woof.<BR>2 A painter's brush, &c.: see तुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीय|तुरीयं|तुरीयः
तुरीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fourth, a fourth.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A fourth part, a quarter.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The divine being, or universal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>irr. derived from चतुर् four, with छ affix; also तूर्य्य and तुर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाग
तुरीयभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A fourth part or share.<BR>E.<BR>तुरीय, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयभाज्
तुरीयभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>A sharer of a fourth.<BR>E.<BR>तुरीय, and भाज who divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयवर्ण|तुरीयवर्णः
तुरीयवर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The Śūdra or fourth tribe of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>तुरीय fourth, and वर्ण tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरीयांश
तुरीयांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A fourth part, a quarter share.<BR>E.<BR>तुरीय, and अंश a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुरुष्क|तुरुष्कः
तुरुष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>1 Incense.<BR>2 A country, or<BR>m. plu. (-ष्काः)<BR>Its inhabitants; Turan or Turkestan, the original country of the Turks.<BR>E.<BR>तुर to haste, (into smoke, &c.) affix उस्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्य्य|तुर्य|तुर्य्यः
तुर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Fourth.<BR>E.<BR>irr. derived from चतुर् four, with यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व|तुर्व्व
तुर्व<BR>(इ) तुर्वी r. 1st cl. (तुर्वति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुर्व्वसु|तुर्वसु|तुर्व्वसुः
तुर्व्वसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>One of the sons of YAYĀTI, king of the south and eastern portion of India, reigning over the Mleccha tribes<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल
तुल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (तोलति तुलति तोलयति-ते or irr. तुलयति)<BR>To weigh or measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलयित्वा
तुलयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having weighed, having counterpoised, made equal or like, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसारिणी
तुलसारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलसी
तुलसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A small shrub held in veneration by the Hindus, Tulasi or holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>E.<BR>तुला resemblance, and षो to destroy, affixes ङ and ङीप्; being unparalleled: this plant is said to be a female metamorphosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुला
तुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Measure by weight.<BR>2 A measure or weight of gold and silver, 100 Palas, or about 145 ounces troy.<BR>3 A balance, especially a fine balance, goldsmith's or assay scales.<BR>4 The sign of the zodiac, Libra.<BR>5 Resemblance, likeness, equality, similarity.<BR>6 A vessel.<BR>7 Sloping beams or timbers in the roof of a house.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh or to resemble, affixes क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोटि|तुलाकोटिः
तुलाकोटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>1 An ornament of the feet or toes.<BR>2 A certain weight.<BR>3 A hundred millions.<BR>E.<BR>तुला a balance, कुट to measure, affix अच् and इ or ङीष्; what is valued by weight, &c. or तुला a measure, &c. and कोटि Crore, or million.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाकोश|तुलाकोशः
तुलाकोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A sort of ordeal, in which the accused is tried by being weighed repeatedly in a scale: if he is lighter the second time he is pronounced innocent; if equipoised still, or heavier, he is guilty.<BR>E.<BR>तुला a scale, and कोश ordeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधट|तुलाधटः
तुलाधट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An oar, a paddle.<BR>2 The scale or cup of a balance.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and धट a scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधर|तुलाधरः
तुलाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तुला the sign, and धर who has or possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाधार|तुलाधारः
तुलाधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A trader, a dealer, trafficking, trading.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sign Libra.<BR>2 The string of a balance.<BR>3 The beam.<BR>E.<BR>तुला the scales, &c. आधार what or who supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापरीक्षा
तुलापरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Ordeal by the balance, the weight of the accused being first taken, certain prayers and ceremonies are performed, after which he is weighed again: if lighter, he is innocent; if heavy, or as at first, guilty.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and परीक्षा test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुष|तुलापुरुषः
तुलापुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A person weighed in a balance, or an effigy of him used as a weight.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलापुरुषदान|तुलापुरुषदानं
तुलापुरुषदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift of gold or valuables of the weight of the donor.<BR>E.<BR>तुलापुरुष, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलाप्रग्रह|तुलाप्रग्रहः
तुलाप्रग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The string of a balance.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and प्रग्रह holding; also तुलाप्रग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलामान
तुलामान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Measure by weight.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलावीज|तुलावीजं
तुलावीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The Gunjā or berry of the Abrus precatorius, from which the goldsmith's or jeweller's weight in India is taken; the berry weighs about 1(5/16) grain troy, the factitious weight about 2(3/16).<BR>E.<BR>तुला weight, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलासूत्र
तुलासूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The string of a balance.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलि|तुलिः
तुलि<BR>f. (-लिः or -ली)<BR>1 A fibrous stick or brush used by weavers for cleaning the threads of the woof.<BR>2 A painter's brush, or fibrous stick used for that purpose: see तूलिका.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to resemble, &c. affix क, fem. affix इन् or ङीष्; also with ल changed to र, तुरि, तुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिका
तुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small bird said to resemble the wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलित
तुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made equal or like, equalled, compared.<BR>2 Weighed, counterpoised.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुलिफला
तुलिफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Simul or silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>तुलि for तूलि cotton, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्य|तुल्यः
तुल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Like, resembling, equal or analogous to.<BR>E.<BR>तुला resemblance, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यता
तुल्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Likeness, sameness, equality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, तुल्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यपान|तुल्यपानं
तुल्यपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Drinking together.<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य alike, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यबल
तुल्यबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of equal strength.<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यभावन
तुल्यभावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Combination of like series, (in calculation.)<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and भावनं computing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=381" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यरूप
तुल्यरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>1 Like, similar, analogous.<BR>2 Of like or equal form.<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and रूप nature, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यवृत्ति
तुल्यवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Following the same or similar occupation.<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्यशुद्धि
तुल्यशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Equal subtraction, transposition, (in Arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and शुद्धि subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुल्याकृति
तुल्याकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Alike, of the same form.<BR>E.<BR>तुल्य, and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवर|तुवरः
तुवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Astringent.<BR>2 Beardless.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>An astringent taste.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A fragrant earth.<BR>2 A kind of lentil, (Cytisus cajan): see आढकी.<BR>E.<BR>तु a Sautra root, to remove, (disease, &c.) थ्वरच् and affix ङीष्; also कन् being added, in the fem. form तुवरिका, f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवरोशिम्ब
तुवरोशिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A kind of cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तुवरी the pulse so called, and शिम्ब Cassia tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुवि|तुविः
तुवि<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>A long gourd: see तुम्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष<BR>r. 4th cl. (ञि, औ) ञिऔतुष (तुष्यति)<BR>To be satisfied or content, to be pleased or delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष|तुषः
तुष<BR>mf. (-षः-षा)<BR>1 The husk or chaff of rice, &c.<BR>2 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please or be pleased, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषग्रह|तुषग्रहः
तुषग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Agni or fire.<BR>E.<BR>तुष chaff, and ग्रह who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषसार|तुषसारः
तुषसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Agni or fire.<BR>E.<BR>तुष chaff, and सार who embraces, from सृ to go, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषानल|तुषानलः
तुषानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A conflagration of chaff, or of the husk of corn.<BR>2 A capital punishment, burning; twisting dry straw, &c. round the limbs of a criminal, and setting it on fire.<BR>E.<BR>तुष, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषार|तुषारः
तुषार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cold, frigid, frosty.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Frost.<BR>2 Cold.<BR>3 Thin rain, mist.<BR>4 Ice or snow.<BR>5 The name of a country.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please, Uṇādi affix आरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारकण|तुषारकणः
तुषारकण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A dew drop.<BR>2 An icicle.<BR>3 Hoar frost.<BR>E.<BR>तुषार, and कण a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारकाल|तुषारकालः
तुषारकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Winter, the cold^1 season.<BR>E.<BR>तुषार, and काल time.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषारपात
तुषारपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Thin rain, a sprinkling, a shower.<BR>2 A fall of snow.<BR>E.<BR>तुषार, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषाराद्रि|तुषाराद्रिः
तुषाराद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The Himālaya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>तुषार, and अद्रि a mountain; also similar compounds, as तुषारपर्व्वत, तुषारशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषित|तुषितः
तुषित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Tuṣita, a kind of subordinate deity, one of a class of thirty-six.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुषोदक|तुषोदकं
तुषोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rice gruel.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to satisfy, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट|तुष्टः
तुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pleased, satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to be pleased, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टि|तुष्टिः
तुष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Pleasure, satisfaction, gratification, content.<BR>2 Indifference to every thing but that possessed or obtained.<BR>3 One of the Mātṛs.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिकर
तुष्टिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>तुष्टि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिजनन
तुष्टिजनन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Gratifying, giving or producing satisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>तुष्टि, and जनन birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टिद
तुष्टिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>तुष्टि, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्टु|तुष्टुः
तुष्टु<BR>m. (-ष्टुः)<BR>A jewel worn in the ears.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please, क्तु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुष्ट्वा
तुष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having pleased or gratified.<BR>E.<BR>तुष, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस|तुसः
तुस<BR>r. 1st cl. (तोसति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस|तुसः
तुस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The husk of corn or rice: see तुष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुस्त|तुस्तं
तुस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>Dust.<BR>E.<BR>तुस to sound, affix क्त: see तूस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुह
तुह<BR>(इर) तुहिर r. 1st cl. (तोहति)<BR>To hurt or give pain, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिन|तुहिनं
तुहिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Frost.<BR>2 Moon-light, moonshine.<BR>E.<BR>तुह to give pain, इनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनशैल|तुहिनशैलः
तुहिनशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>तुहिन, and शैल a mountain; also similar compounds, as तुहिनपर्व्वत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनांशु|तुहिनांशुः
तुहिनांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>तुहिन cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनांशुतैल|तुहिनांशुतैलं
तुहिनांशुतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>तुहिनांशु, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तुहिनाद्रि|तुहिनाद्रिः
तुहिनाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>तुहिन, and अद्रि a mountain; also तुहिनशैल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण<BR>r. 1st cl. (तूणयते)<BR>To fill, to fill up.<BR>(तूणयति)<BR>To shrink, to contract, to close as the eye-lids or wink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूण|तूणः
तूण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा or -णी)<BR>A quiver, &c.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Indigo.<BR>E.<BR>तूण to be filled (with arrows, &c.) अच् and टाप् affixes, or घञ् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणक|तूणकं
तूणक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A measure of verse, species of the अतिशर्करी metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणिन्
तूणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Having a quiver, quivered.<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>The Tūn tree.<BR>E.<BR>तूण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूणीर|तूणीरं|तूणीरः
तूणीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A quiver.<BR>E.<BR>तूण to be filled (with arrows), ईरण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूतक|तूतकं
तूतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूनी
तूनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Sharp pain in the perinœum and lower part of the abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्
तूर्<BR>f. (-तूः)<BR>Speed.<BR>m. (-तूः)<BR>A courier.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to make haste, क्विप् affix, and the semivowel changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर|तूरं
तूर<BR>(ई) तूरी r. 4th cl. (तूर्य्यते)<BR>To go quick, to make haste.<BR>2 To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर|तूरं
तूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Any musical instrument.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A trumpet.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to speed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्ण|तूर्णं|तूर्ण्ण
तूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>n. adv. (-र्णं)<BR>Quick, swift, quickly.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to go swiftly, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्णि|तूर्णिः
तूर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity, expedition.<BR>2 Dirt, excrement.<BR>3 A stanza.<BR>4 The mind.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to make haste, Uṇādi affix नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य्य|तूर्य|तूर्यं|तूर्यः|तूर्य्यं
तूर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Fourth: see तुर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Any musical instrument, the genus of which four species are reckoned, as wind instruments, stringed instruments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>चतुर four, यत् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूर्य्यखण्ड|तूर्यखण्ड|तूर्यखण्डः|तूर्य्यखण्डः
तूर्य्यखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A musical instrument, a sort of tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल|तूलं|तूलः
तूल<BR>r. 1st cl. (तूलति)<BR>1 To dismiss, to send forth or turn out.<BR>2 To ascertain quantity or weight; some make this a root of the tenth class (तूलयति-ते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूल|तूलं|तूलः
तूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The mulberry, (Morus Indica.)<BR>2 Æther, the heaven or atmosphere.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>Cotton.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>The wick of a lamp, or cotton twisted into a similar form for applying unguents, &c.<BR>(-ली)<BR>1 Indigo.<BR>2 A weaver's fibrous stick or brush.<BR>3 A painter's brush, &c. see तुली and तुरी; also तूलि.<BR>E.<BR>तूल to dismiss, to send forth, affix घञ्, fem. affixes टाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलक|तूलकं
तूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Cotton.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलकार्म्मुक|तूलकार्मुक|तूलकार्म्मुकं
तूलकार्म्मुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bow which is used for cleaning cotton.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, and कार्म्मुक a bow; also similar compounds, as तूलचाप, तूलधनुः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=382" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलनाली
तूलनाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A thick roll of cotton, from which it is drawn out in spinning.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, नाल a tube, affixes अण् and ङीप्; also with कन् added तूलनालिका, f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलपिचु|तूलपिचुः
तूलपिचु<BR>m. (-चुः)<BR>Cotton.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, and पिचु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलशर्करा
तूलशर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A pod or seed of the plant, any seed yielding a similar substance.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, and शर्करा sand or gravel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलसेचन|तूलसेचनं
तूलसेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spinning.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, सिच to sprinkle, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलि|तूलिः
तूलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A painter's brush, or a fibrous stick used as one, and for other purposes.<BR>E.<BR>तूल to send forth or cut, affix इन्: see तूल and तूली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिका
तूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pencil, a painter's brush, or a stick with a fibrous extremity used as one.<BR>2 A mattress^1 or quilt, a bed, a down or cotton bed.<BR>3 An ingot mould.<BR>4 A rod, &c. dipped into crucibles to try if their contents are in fusion.<BR>5 A wick or twist of cotton either for a lamp or for applying unguents, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तूली as above, and कन् added.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूलिनी
तूलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>तूल cotton, इनि and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूवर|तूवरः
तूवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bull without horns, though of an age to have them.<BR>2 A beardless man.<BR>3 A eunuch.<BR>4 An astringent taste.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A fragrant earth.<BR>E.<BR>तु to injure, ष्वरच् affix, and the vowel optionally long, hence also तुवर and तुवरी; with कन् added तूवरिका and तूवरीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष|तूषः
तूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (तूषति)<BR>1 To satisfy.<BR>2 To be satisfied or happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णींशील|तूष्णींशीलः
तूष्णींशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Silent, taciturn.<BR>E.<BR>तूष्णीम् silent, and शील practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीक|तूष्णीकः
तूष्णीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Silent, taciturn.<BR>E.<BR>तूष्णीम् silent, अकच् affix, and म dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीकाम्
तूष्णीकाम्<BR>ind.<BR>Silent, silently.<BR>E.<BR>तूष्णीम् silent, and काम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीम्
तूष्णीम्<BR>ind.<BR>Silent, silently.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to please or be pleased, affix नीम्, and उ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूष्णीम्भूत|तूष्णींभूत
तूष्णीम्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Silent.<BR>E.<BR>तूष्णीम्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तूस्त|तूस्तं
तूस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Dust.<BR>2 Clotted hair.<BR>3 Sin.<BR>4 An atom, a very thin or delicate substance.<BR>E.<BR>तूस to sound, Uṇādi affix तन्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृक्ष|तृक्षः
तृक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (तृक्षति)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृख|तृखं
तृख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृढ
तृढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Hurt, injured, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>तृह to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण|तृणं
तृण<BR>(उ) तृणु r. 8th cl. (तर्णोति तर्णुते or तृणोति तृणुते)<BR>To eat, especially grass, to graze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण|तृणं
तृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Grass, any gramineous plant.<BR>E.<BR>तृह to hurt, Uṇādi affix क्न, and ह rejected; what is consumed by cattle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकुङ्कुम|तृणकुंकुम|तृणकुङ्कुमं
तृणकुङ्कुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A sort of perfume.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, कुङ्कुम saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकुटी
तृणकुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A hovel, a hut of grass or straw.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and कुटी a small house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकूर्म्म|तृणकूर्म|तृणकूर्म्मः
तृणकूर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>A long gourd, (Cueurbita lagenaria.)<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and कूर्म्म a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणकेतु|तृणकेतुः
तृणकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and केतु a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणगोधा
तृणगोधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A kind of newt.<BR>2 A chameleon.<BR>3 A worm.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and गोधा a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणग्राहिन्
तृणग्राहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>1 Amber, &c. or any gem which being rubbed becomes electrically attractive.<BR>2 Sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and ग्राहिन् what seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणजम्भ
तृणजम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>1 Graminivorous, one whose food is grass.<BR>2 Grass-toothed, having teeth of the colour of grass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and जम्भ food, or a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणजाति|तृणजातिः
तृणजाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The vegetable kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>तृण, and जाति genus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणता
तृणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 The aggregate properties of grass or herbage, gramineousness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् affix of the abstract, added to तृण; also तृणत्व, n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणद्रुम|तृणद्रुमः
तृणद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A palm tree, any of the various species, as the palmyra, cocoanut, date, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and द्रुम a tree; pre-eminent amongst gramineous plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणधान्य|तृणधान्यं
तृणधान्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>Grain growing wild or without cultivation.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and धान्य grain, corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणध्वज|तृणध्वजः
तृणध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and ध्वज a flag or banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणपूली
तृणपूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A mat, a seat made of reeds or basket-work.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, पूल to gather together, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणमणि|तृणमणिः
तृणमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A sort of gem, apparently^1 amber.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and मणि a gem; attracting straws, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणमत्कुण|तृणमत्कुणः
तृणमत्कुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bail or surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणराज|तृणराजः
तृणराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A palmyra tree, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and राजन् a sovereign, टच् affix, leaving a final vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणविस्तर
तृणविस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A heap of grass.<BR>E.<BR>तृण, and विस्तर expanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणशीत|तृणशीतं
तृणशीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and शीत here said to imply abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणशून्य|तृणशून्यं
तृणशून्य<BR>mfn. subst. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>adj.<BR>Free from or devoid of grass.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>The flower of the Ketaki.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, शून्य void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणषट्पद|तृणषट्पदः
तृणषट्पद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and षट्पद् six-foot; an insect haunting meadows, &c. having six feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणस
तृणस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Grassy, made, &c. with grass.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसारा
तृणसारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The plantain or banana.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and सार essence, pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणसिंह|तृणसिंहः
तृणसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणहर्म्म्य
तृणहर्म्म्य<BR>m. (-र्म्म्र्यः)<BR>A hovel, a house or upper-room of grass or straw.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and हर्म्म्र्य a mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाग्नि|तृणाग्निः
तृणाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 Conflagration of chaff.<BR>2 Burning a criminal wrapped up in straw.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and अग्नि fire: see तुषानल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणाञ्जन|तृणांजन|तृणाञ्जनः
तृणाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A chameleon, a lizard.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and अञ्जन a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणेक्षु|तृणेक्षुः
तृणेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A kind of long grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>तृण, and इक्षु sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणोद्भव|तृणोद्भवः
तृणोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Rice, &c. growing wild or without cultivation.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणोल्का
तृणोल्का<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>A firebrand made of a wisp of straw.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and उल्का a firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणौकस्
तृणौकस्<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A hovel, a hut, a house of straw or mats.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृणौषध|तृणौषधं
तृणौषध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>A perfume, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>तृण, and औषध a drug; resembling grass in its appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृण्या
तृण्या<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>A heap or quantity of grass.<BR>E.<BR>तृण grass, यत् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=383" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीय|तृतीयः
तृतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Third.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The third lunation, the third day of the fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, तीय affix, and रि changed to the analogous vowel ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयक
तृतीयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tertian ague.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयकज्वर|तृतीयकज्वरः
तृतीयकज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Tertian ague.<BR>E.<BR>तृतीय, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयप्रकृति|तृतीयप्रकृतिः
तृतीयप्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A eunuch.<BR>2 The neuter gender: see तृतीयाप्रकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाकृत|तृतीयाकृतं
तृतीयाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>तृतीय third, आकृत made, wrought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयाप्रकृति|तृतीयाप्रकृतिः
तृतीयाप्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A eunuch.<BR>2 The neuter gender.<BR>E.<BR>तृतीया the third, and प्रकृति nature; neither male nor female, (whose or which); the compound is more regularly तृतीयप्रकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृतीयिन्
तृतीयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Having a third.<BR>E.<BR>तृतीय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृद
तृद<BR>(औ इर) औतृदिर् r. 7th cl. (तृणत्ति तृन्ते)<BR>1 To kill, to injure.<BR>2 To disregard.<BR>3 To give.<BR>4 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप
तृप<BR>r. 1st cl. (तर्पति) 4th cl. (ञि, उ) ञितृपु (तृप्यति) 5th cl. (तृप्नोति) 6th cl. (तृपति) and 10th cl. (तर्पयति)<BR>1 To please, to satisfy, to content.<BR>2 To be pleased or satisfied, to be content or satiate.<BR>3 (In the 1st and 10th cls.) To light or kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपत्
तृपत्<BR>m. (-पत्)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A parasol.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to please, अति Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृपला
तृपला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A creeper or creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to please, कल Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्त|तृप्तः
तृप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Contented, satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to be pleased, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्तात्मन्
तृप्तात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म्)<BR>Contented, satisfied, tranquil.<BR>E.<BR>तृप्त, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्ति|तृप्तिः
तृप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Satisfaction, content.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to please, or be pleased, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्र|तृप्रः
तृप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to satisfy, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृप्रालु
तृप्रालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Having ghree, but not liking it or not blending with it.<BR>E.<BR>तृप, and आलुच् possessive affix; but in this compound implying also aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफ
तृफ<BR>r. 6th cl. (तृफति)<BR>1 To content, to please.<BR>2 To be pleased or content.<BR>3 To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफला
तृफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The three myrobalans.<BR>E.<BR>तृ for त्रि three, फल a fruit, fem. affix टाप्; also त्रिफला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृफू
तृफू<BR>m. (-फूः)<BR>A serpent in general, the serpent genus.<BR>E.<BR>तृफ to hurt or kill, ऊ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्प
तृम्प<BR>r. 6th cl. (तृम्पति)<BR>1 To content, to please.<BR>2 To be pleased or content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृम्फ
तृम्फ<BR>r. 6th cl. (तृम्फति)<BR>1 To content, to please.<BR>2 To be pleased or content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष
तृष<BR>(ञि आ) ञितृषा r. 4th cl. (तृष्यति)<BR>1 To thirst.<BR>2 To thirst metaphorically, to desire, to long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्
तृष्<BR>f. (तृट्)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Thirst, (metaphorical,) wish, desire, lust.<BR>3 The daughter of KĀMA, the deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix क्विप्; also तृषा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषा
तृषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 The daughter of KĀMA: see the preceding.<BR>4 A plant, (Commelina salicifolia): see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix क and टाप्; also तृष्णा, तर्षा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाभू
तृषाभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>The bladder.<BR>E.<BR>तृषा thirst, and भू being: whence thirst arises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषार्त्त|तृषार्त
तृषार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Affected by desire.<BR>2 Thirsty, athirst.<BR>E.<BR>तृषा, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषाह|तृषाहं
तृषाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Water.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A kind of anise: see मधुरिका.<BR>E.<BR>तृष thirst, आङ् before हन् to destroy or remove, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषित|तृषितः
तृषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thirsty, thirsting, (physically or metaphorically.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Thirst, desire.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृषितोत्तरा
तृषितोत्तरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia): see असनपर्णी.<BR>E.<BR>तृषित thirst, and उत्तर answering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णज्
तृष्णज्<BR>mfn. (-ष्णक्)<BR>Thirsty, (physically or metaphorically,) desiring, longing for, cupidinous.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, न added, तृष्ण and जिङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णा
तृष्णा<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>2 Desire, wish.<BR>E.<BR>तृषं to thirst, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्णाक्षय|तृष्णाक्षयः
तृष्णाक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Content, resignation, patience.<BR>E.<BR>तृष्णा greediness, thirst, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृष्यत्
तृष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यती-ष्यत्)<BR>1 Thirsting, athirst.<BR>2 Desiring.<BR>E.<BR>तृष to thirst, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तृह
तृह<BR>(ऊ) तृहु r. 6th cl. (तृहति) also तृह r. 7th cl. (तृणड्डि)<BR>To kill, to hurt, to injure in any manner.<BR>(इ) तृहि r. 1st cl. (तृंहति)<BR>To grow or increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तॄ
तॄ<BR>r. 1st cl. (तरति)<BR>1 To pass over or across.<BR>2 To pass or float over, to navigate.<BR>3 To float or swim.<BR>4 To overcome, to surpass.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>To descend, as from heaven.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To cross by a boat, &c.<BR>With उत्,<BR>a To pass over or above. .²b To answer. .²c To land, to arrive at the opposite shore.<BR>With दुर्,<BR>To cross with difficulty.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To cross safely, to obtain salvation.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To excel or surpass.<BR>With वि,<BR>a To pass from. .²b To relinquish, to give, to give away, to give alms.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To swim over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ते
ते<BR>ind.<BR>With or by thee.<BR>E.<BR>ते substituted for त्वया, but not to be confounded with the optional inflection of the 4th and 6th cases of युष्मद् thou.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज|तेजः
तेज<BR>r. 1st cl. (तेजति)<BR>To guard, to cherish, to defend or protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेज|तेजः
तेज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Sharpness, pungency.<BR>2 Sharpness of a weapon.<BR>3 Brilliancy.<BR>4 Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen, affix घञ्: see तेजस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजन|तेजनं|तेजनः
तेजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 Enlightening, making splendid or polished.<BR>3 Sharpening.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A plant, (Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>2 Heartpea.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजनक|तेजनकः
तेजनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजपत्र|तेजपत्रं
तेजपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तेज sharp, pungent, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजल|तेजलः
तेजल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>तेज sharpness, ल what gets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजवत्|तेजवन्त्
तेजवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Sharp, pungent.<BR>2 Sharp as a weapon.<BR>3 Bright.<BR>4 Spirited, energetic.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>An aromatic plant, (Pothos officinalis): see गजपिप्पली.<BR>E.<BR>तेज sharpness, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्
तेजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A name of Agni or fire.<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 Splendour, light, lustre.<BR>2 Dignity, consequence.<BR>3 Strength, power.<BR>4 Ardour, spirit, energy.<BR>5 Semen virile.<BR>6 Fresh butter.<BR>7 Impatience, inability to bear or put up with.<BR>8 Gold.<BR>9 Bile, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">Page385</a>] the bilious humour.<BR>10 Marrow, the brain, &c.<BR>11 Fame, glory.<BR>12 Sharpness, (metallic.)<BR>13 Pungency.<BR>14 Heat.<BR>15 Bodily vigour.<BR>16 Vivacity.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen or polish, affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=384" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्कर|तेजस्करं
तेजस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Illuminating, making bright.<BR>2 Sharpening, whetting.<BR>3 Invigorating, tonic.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् light, &c. and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजस्विन्
तेजस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated.<BR>2 Splendid, &c. see the preceding.<BR>f. (-स्विनी)<BR>Heartpea: see ज्योतिष्मती.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् splendour, &c. विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजित|तेजितः
तेजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sharpened, whetted, polished, burnished.<BR>2 Excited, invigorated, stimulated.<BR>E.<BR>तिज to sharpen, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजिष्ठ
तेजिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Very bright or splendid.<BR>2 Vigorous, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस्, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजीयस्
तेजीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very bright, radiant, splendid.<BR>2 Very powerful or vigorous.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस्, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमन्थ
तेजोमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>A tree, (Premna spinosa): see गणिकारी.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् fire, light, and मन्थ friction; the friction of the wood engendering flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोमय
तेजोमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Luminous, brilliant, consisting or made of light.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस्, मयट् made of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोरूप|तेजोरूपं
तेजोरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 The supreme spirit.<BR>2 The nature of light, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् light (divine), रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोवत्|तेजोवन्त्
तेजोवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Pungent.<BR>2 Sharp.<BR>3 Bright.<BR>4 Energetic.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A plant bearing a fruit resembling pepper: see गजपिप्पली.<BR>2 A kind of pepper, (Piper chavya, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् pungency, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेजोवृत्त
तेजोवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Superior brilliancy or power.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस्, and वृत्त being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन<BR>ind.<BR>Therefore, thence, for that reason, on that account, the correlative to येन.<BR>E.<BR>the third case of तद् that, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेन|तेनः
तेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A note or cadence introductory to a song, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त said to mean GAURI and न ŚIVA; whose favour is secured by this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेप
तेप<BR>(ऋ) तेपृ r. 1st cl. (तेपते)<BR>1 To sprinkle, to distil, to ooze or drop.<BR>2 To shake or tremble.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेम|तेमः
तेम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Wet, damp, moisture.<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be wet, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेमन|तेमनं
तेमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wetting, moistening, moisture.<BR>2 A sauce or condiment.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A chimney, a fireplace.<BR>E.<BR>तिम to be or become wet, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेव
तेव<BR>(ऋ) तेवृ r. 1st cl. (तेवते)<BR>1 To play, to sport.<BR>2 To weep or lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तेवन|तेवनं
तेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A garden, a pleasure garden or play-ground.<BR>2 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>E.<BR>तेव to play, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैक्ष्ण्य|तैक्ष्ण्यं
तैक्ष्ण्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्ण्यं)<BR>1 Sharpness.<BR>2 Heat.<BR>3 Pungency.<BR>4 Fierceness, cruelty.<BR>E.<BR>तीक्ष्ण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैजस|तैजसं|तैजसः
तैजस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>1 Of or relating to fire, fiery, splendid.<BR>2 Powerful, vigorous, intense.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>2 Any metal.<BR>3 Intensity.<BR>4 Vigour, energy.<BR>E.<BR>तेजस् brilliance, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैजसावर्त्तिनी|तैजसावर्तिनी
तैजसावर्त्तिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A crucible.<BR>E.<BR>तैजस metal, and आवर्त्तिनी stirring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैतिल|तैतिलं|तैतिलः
तैतिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas.<BR>E.<BR>अण् added to तितिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिर|तैत्तिरं|तैत्तिरः
तैत्तिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A francoline partridge.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A flock of partridges.<BR>E.<BR>तित्तिर, and अण् affix of aggregation or pleonastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीय|तैत्तिरीयः
तैत्तिरीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to the Tittiri portion of the Vedas, as a student, a text, teacher, section of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तित्तिरि the Yajur Veda so called, and छ affix; or तित्तिरि a partridge, affix as before; the texts of this Veda being disgorged by YĀJÑAVALKYA in a tangible form, and picked up by the rest of VAIŚAMPĀYANA'S disciples, who, for the purpose, assumed the shape of partridges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैत्तिरीयक|तैत्तिरीयकः
तैत्तिरीयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A follower of the Tittiri branch of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also इन् being added तैत्तिरीयिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैग्म्य
तैग्म्य<BR>n. (-ग्म्यं)<BR>1 Heat.<BR>2 Sharpness.<BR>3 Pungency.<BR>E.<BR>तिग्म, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैल|तैलं
तैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Oil, expressed oil, prepared from sesamum, mustard, &c.<BR>3 Storax, gum benzoin, incense.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलक|तैलकं
तैलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A small quantity of oil.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and कन् diminutive affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलकार|तैलकारः
तैलकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An oil manufacturer.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलकिट्ट|तैलकिट्टं
तैलकिट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टं)<BR>The oil cake, a cake made of the oily seed, after expression.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलङ्ग|तैलंग|तैलंगः|तैलङ्गः
तैलङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The part of the peninsula south of Orissa to Madras, the modern Carnatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलचौरिका
तैलचौरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, चुर to steal, ण्वुल् affix; it is also sometimes read तैलाचारिका from चर to go, with आङ् prefixed, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलद्रोणी
तैलद्रोणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A bathing tub for an oil bath.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and द्रोणी a bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपक|तैलपकः
तैलपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and पच to digest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपर्णिक|तैलपर्णिकं
तैलपर्णिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>White Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>तिलपर्णी Sandal wood, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपर्णी
तैलपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 Incense.<BR>3 Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and पर्ण a leaf, affix अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपा
तैलपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, and पा who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपायिका
तैलपायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, पा to drink, ण्वुल् affix, and यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलपिपीलिका
तैलपिपीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The small red ant.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and पिपीलिका an ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलमाली
तैलमाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A wick, the cotton of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, माला a necklace, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलम्पात
तैलम्पात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blending with oil, &c.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Oblation to fire.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, पत to go or alight, घञ् affix, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलसाधन|तैलसाधनं
तैलसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fragrant substance, (Civet.)<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, and साधन menstruum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलस्फटिक|तैलस्फटिकः
तैलस्फटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of gem, (Amber.)<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलाटी
तैलाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, and अट to go, affixes अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=385" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलाम्बुका
तैलाम्बुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, अम्बु water or drink, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिक|तैलिकः
तैलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An oilman.<BR>E.<BR>तैल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिन्
तैलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Relating or belonging to oil, oily, &c.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>An oilman, an oil grinder or preparer.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>1 The wick or cotton of a lamp.<BR>2 A kind of insect found in oil.<BR>E.<BR>तैल oil, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलिशाला
तैलिशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An oil mill.<BR>E.<BR>तैलिन् an oilman, and शाला a house or hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैलीन|तैलीनं
तैलीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A field of sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>तिल sesamum, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तैष|तैषः
तैष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The month Pauṣa, (December-January.)<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>Day of full moon in Pauṣa.<BR>E.<BR>तिष्य the constellation, (in which the moon is full in this month,) and अण् affix; य is dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक|तोकं
तोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A child, a son or a daughter, male or female offspring.<BR>E.<BR>तु a Sautra root, to increase, affix क, deriv. irr. also तोककं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोक्म|तोक्मं|तोक्मः
तोक्म<BR>m. (-क्मः)<BR>1 Green or unripe barley.<BR>2 Green, (the colour.)<BR>n. (-क्मं)<BR>1 The wax of the ear.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>तक to deride, म affix, and ओ substituted for the radical vowel; it is also written तोक्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोटक|तोटकं|तोटकः
तोटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A measure of verse, a stanza, each line containing twelve syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोड
तोड<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) तोडृ (तोडति)<BR>To treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्र|तोत्त्रं|तोत्रं
तोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A stick or bambu, with a sharp iron head, used for guiding an elephant.<BR>2 A goad or pike for driving cattle.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to vex, to goad, affix ष्ट्रन्; also तोदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोत्रवेत्र
तोत्रवेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A rod or wand carried by VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>तोत्र a goad, and वेत्र a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोद|तोदः
तोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Pain, anguish, vexation, torture, uneasiness, (either of body or mind.)<BR>2 Sharp, shooting or pricking pain.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to tease^1 or torment, affix घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोदन|तोदनं
तोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A goad: see तोत्र.<BR>2 Pain, affliction from disease, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तुद to give pain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमर|तोमरं|तोमरः
तोमर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 An iron club or crow.<BR>2 A lance.<BR>E.<BR>तु Sautra root, to hurt, affix विच्, तु that which injures, मृ to die, affix अच्, and the vowel of तु changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरग्रह
तोमरग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A warrior armed with a club.<BR>E.<BR>तोमर, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरधर|तोमरधरः
तोमरधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of Agni.<BR>2 A warrior armed with a club.<BR>E.<BR>तोमर an iron club, and धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोमरिका
तोमरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fragrant earth: see तुवरिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोय|तोयं
तोय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>तु to surround, Uṇādi affix कोय or ताय to nourish, अच् affix, and आ changed irregularly to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयकाम|तोयकामः
तोयकाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of cane growing in or near water, (Calamus fasciculatus, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and काम desiring, affecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयकृच्छ्र|तोयकृच्छ्रं|तोयकृच्छ्रः
तोयकृच्छ्र<BR>m. (-च्छ्रः)<BR>A sort of penance, drinking nothing but water for a fixed period.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and कच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयडिम्भ|तोयडिंभ|तोयडिम्भः
तोयडिम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and डिम्भ young; also तायडिम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयद|तोयदः
तोयद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what gives water.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Ghee or oiled butter.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and द yielding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधर|तोयधरः
तोयधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Having or containing water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A fragrant grass: see मुस्तक.<BR>3 A potherb, (Marsilia dentata.)<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and धर possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधि|तोयधिः
तोयधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and धि having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयधिप्रिय|तोयधिप्रियं
तोयधिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>तोयधि the sea, and प्रिय fond of; produced in maritime countries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयनिधि|तोयनिधिः
तोयनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and निधि nest or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयपिप्पली
तोयपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and पिप्पली long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयपुष्पी
तोयपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>Trumpet flower.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and पुष्प a flower; flowering near water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रसादन|तोयप्रसादनं
तोयप्रसादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and प्रसादन clearing, cleansing; the nut being rubbed upon the inside of a water jar, occasions the precipitation of the impurities of the water poured into it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रसादनफल|तोयप्रसादनफलं
तोयप्रसादनफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The clearing nut: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>तोयप्रसादन as above, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयप्रष्ठा
तोयप्रष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>The trumpet flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयवल्ली
तोयवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयशुक्तिका
तोयशुक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An oyster.<BR>E.<BR>तोय, and शुक्तिका an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयसूचक|तोयसूचकः
तोयसूचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, and सूचक a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोयाधिवासिनी
तोयाधिवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Trumpet flower.<BR>E.<BR>तोय water, अधि upon or near, वस to abide, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोरण|तोरणं|तोरणः
तोरण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 The ornamented arch of a door or gateway.<BR>2 An outer door.<BR>3 Decoration of the gate post.<BR>4 A temporary and ornamental arch.<BR>5 A mound or raised mark near a bathing place.<BR>6 A triangle supporting a large balance.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The neck, the throat.<BR>E.<BR>तुर to hasten, affix ल्युट्; by which people pass or go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोल|तोलं|तोलः
तोल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A Tola, a weight of gold or silver: it is stated in books at 16 Māṣas of 5 Rattis or 6½ grains each, and weighs therefore 105 grains troy: in practice it is calculated at 12 Māṣas jeweller's weight, and weighs nearly double, or 210 grains; but actually it is of the same weight as the Sicca or grs. 179 (2/3).<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, affix घञ्; also with ण्वुल् affix तोलक, mn. (-कः-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलन|तोलनं
तोलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Weighing.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोलयित्वा
तोलयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having weighed.<BR>E.<BR>तुल to weigh, causal form, त्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोष|तोषः
तोष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Pleasure, joy, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to be pleased, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तोषित
तोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, appeased.<BR>E.<BR>तुष to be pleased, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक
तौक<BR>(ऋ) तौकृ r. 1st cl. (तौकते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौक्षिक|तौक्षिकः
तौक्षिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sagittarius, the constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौतिक|तौतिकं|तौतिकः
तौतिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The pearl oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्य्य|तौर्य|तौर्यं|तौर्य्यं
तौर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>The sound of musical instruments, harmony, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तूर्य्य an instrument, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौर्य्यत्रिक|तौर्यत्रिक|तौर्य्यत्रिकं
तौर्य्यत्रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Symphony, union of song, dance, and instrumental music.<BR>E.<BR>तौर्य्य as above, त्रि three, कन् affix; triple or threefold melody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौल|तौलं
तौल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A balance.<BR>E.<BR>तुला, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिक|तौलिकः
तौलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>तुलिका a brush, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=386" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौलिकिक|तौलिकिकः
तौलिकिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>तुलिका a brush or pencil, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तौषार|तौषारं
तौषार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Snow.<BR>2 Cold.<BR>E.<BR>तुषार frost, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त|त्यक्तं
त्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Left, resigned, abandoned, deserted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज to quit, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तजीवित
त्यक्तजीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ready to die; willing to run all hazards, having relinquished the expectation of life as men on the forlorn hope.<BR>E.<BR>त्यक्त left, and जीवित life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तवत्
त्यक्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Leaving, abandoning.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज to quit, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तव्य
त्यक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be left, abandoned, excepted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्ताग्नि|त्यक्ताग्निः
त्यक्ताग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A Brahman who has lost his household fire, one who neglects essential ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>त्यक्त, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्तुकाम
त्यक्तुकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Wishing to leave.<BR>E.<BR>त्यक्तु for the infin. त्यक्तुं, and काम desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यक्त्वा
त्यक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having left or abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यज
त्यज<BR>r. 1st cl. (औ) त्यजौ (त्यजति)<BR>To quit, to abandon, to leave or resign, to part from, to give away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजन|त्यजनं
त्यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Leaving, quitting, abandoning.<BR>2 Excepting, exclusion.<BR>3 Giving.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यजनीय
त्यजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be left or abandoned.<BR>2 To be avoided.<BR>3 To be excepted.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यद्
त्यद्<BR>pron. for तद् mfn. (स्यः-स्या-तद्)<BR>That.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज to quit, Uṇādi affix अदि, and the final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याग|त्यागः
त्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Abandoning, leaving, parting from, separation, deserting, &c.<BR>3 A sage, one who separates himself from worldly thoughts.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज to abandon, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागशील
त्यागशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Generous, liberal.<BR>E.<BR>त्याग, and शील addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागशीलता
त्यागशीलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Generosity.<BR>E.<BR>त्यागशील, and तल् affix; also with त्व, त्यागशीलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिता
त्यागिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Liberality, generosity.<BR>E.<BR>त्यागिन्, and तल् affix; also with त्व affix, त्यागित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिन्
त्यागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Who or what leaves, gives, excepts, &c.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>A giver, a donor.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>3 An abandoner, a deserter, but chiefly applied to the religious ascetic, or him who abandons terrestrial objects, thoughts, passions, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्याग as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्यागिम|त्यागिमः
त्यागिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Left, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>त्याग leaving, इमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्याज्य|त्याज्यः
त्याज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>1 To be left or avoided.<BR>2 To be abstained from.<BR>3 To be given.<BR>4 To be excepted.<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Part of an asterism, or its duration considered as unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>त्यज to leave, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रक
त्रक<BR>(इ) त्रकि r. 1st cl. (त्रङ्कते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रख
त्रख<BR>(इ) त्रखि r. 1st cl. (त्रङ्खति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रग
त्रग<BR>(इ) त्रगि r. 1st cl. (त्रङ्गति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रङ्ग|त्रङ्गः
त्रङ्ग<BR>mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA, suspended, it is supposed, in the air.<BR>E.<BR>त्रै to fear, affix क्विप्, and ग what goes; what imparts terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रद
त्रद<BR>(इ) त्रदि r. 1st cl. (त्रन्दति)<BR>1 To act, to perform functions.<BR>2 To endeavour, to strive.<BR>3 To be busy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप
त्रप<BR>(ऊ, ष) त्रपूष् r. 1st cl. (त्रपति)<BR>To be modest, to be ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप
त्रप<BR>mf. (-पः-पा)<BR>Shame, modesty, bashfulness.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 An unchaste woman, (a shame to her family.)<BR>2 Family, race.<BR>3 Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be modest, affix अङ्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपमाण
त्रपमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप्र to be ashamed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाक|त्रपाकः
त्रपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barbarian of a certain description.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be modest, आकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपानिरस्त
त्रपानिरस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Shameless, impudent.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and निरस्त expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपान्वित
त्रपान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Modest, bashful, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाभर
त्रपाभर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Overcome with shame.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and भर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपायुक्त
त्रपायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Bashful, modest.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and युक्त attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपारण्डा|त्रपारंडा
त्रपारण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा shame, लडि to reject, affix अच् and टाप्, and ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपावत्
त्रपावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Modest, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपाहीन
त्रपाहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Immodest, impudent.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपा, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपित
त्रपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Modest, bashful, ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be modest, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपिष्ठ|त्रपिष्ठः
त्रपिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Highly satisfied.<BR>2 Very much ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to please, or त्रपा shame, and इष्ठन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपीयस्
त्रपीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Highly or excessively pleased or content.<BR>2 Very much ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to be pleased, or तृपा and इयसुन् affix of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपु|त्रपुः
त्रपु<BR>n. (-पुः)<BR>1 Tin.<BR>2 Lead.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be modest, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुल|त्रपुलं
त्रपुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>लच् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुष|त्रपुषं
त्रपुष<BR>mf. (-षं-षी)<BR>A cucumber.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be ashamed, &c. उसस् affix, fem. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रपुस्
त्रपुस्<BR>n. (-पुः)<BR>Tin, or according to some, lead: see त्रपु.<BR>E.<BR>त्रप to be ashamed, Uṇādi affix उस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रप्सा
त्रप्सा<BR>n. (-प्स्यं)<BR>Thin or diluted curds.<BR>E.<BR>तृप to be satisfied, deriv. irr.; also without the final य, त्रप्स, n. (-प्सं) also द्रप्स्य and द्रप्सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रय|त्रयं|त्रयः
त्रय<BR>nf. (-यं-यी)<BR>1 The third.<BR>2 (In composition) Three, as गुणत्रयं the three properties.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, टयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयी
त्रयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 The three Vedas collectively, that is, omitting the Atharvan, which not being a text book for the customary religious rites of the Hindus, is considered very commonly rather as an appendix to the other three, than a fourth work of equal authority. A matron, a married woman who has children living.<BR>3 Intellect, understanding.<BR>4 A plant, (Conyza serratula.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, अयप् or टयप् substituted for the final, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीतनु|त्रयीतनुः
त्रयीतनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>त्रयी the three Vedas, and तनु diffusion; celebrated through these sacred books, or because the Sāma Veda, and portions of the other Vedas, are said to have proceeded from the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीधर्म्म|त्रयीधर्म|त्रयीधर्मः|त्रयीधर्म्मः
त्रयीधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Duty enjoined by the Vedas, modes of sacrifice, &c. prescribed by them.<BR>E.<BR>त्रयी the three Vedas, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=387" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयीमुख|त्रयीमुखः
त्रयीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>त्रयी the Vedas, and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदश|त्रयोदशः
त्रयोदश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Thirteenth.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The thirteenth day of the lunar fortnight: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रयोदशन्
त्रयोदशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Thirteen.<BR>E.<BR>त्रयस् for त्रि three, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस|त्रसं|त्रसः
त्रस<BR>(ई) त्रसी r. 1st and 4th cl. (त्रसति त्रस्यति)<BR>1 To fear, to be afraid.<BR>2 To run, to go quickly.<BR>(इ) त्रसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (त्रंसति त्रंसयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>Also त्रस r. 10th cl. (त्रासयति)<BR>1 To hold.<BR>2 To seize or take.<BR>3 To oppose, to prevent or forbid.<BR>4 To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस|त्रसं|त्रसः
त्रस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Moveable, loco-motive.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>A wood, a forest.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसर|त्रसरः
त्रसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A shuttle.<BR>2 Weaving.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to go, affix अरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसरेणु|त्रसरेणुः
त्रसरेणु<BR>mf. (-णुः)<BR>An atom or mote visible in a sunbeam, especially considered as an ideal weight, either of the lowest denomination, or equal to three, or according to some, thirty invisible atoms.<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>A wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस moveable, and रेणु dust; also read त्र्यमरेणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रसुर|त्रसुरः
त्रसुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Timid, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to fear, उरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्त|त्रस्तः
त्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Timid, fearful.<BR>2 Frighted, alarmed.<BR>3 Quick.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to fear, affix क्त; also त्रस्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्तरूप
त्रस्तरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Fearful, terrified.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस्त, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्नु|त्रस्नुः
त्रस्नु<BR>mfn. (-स्नुः-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>Timid, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to fear, क्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रस्यत्
त्रस्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>Fearing, apprehending.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to fear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रा
त्रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (त्राति)<BR>To preserve, &c.: see त्रै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्राण|त्राणं
त्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Preserved, saved, guarded, protected.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Preserving, protection.<BR>2 A plant: see त्रायमाण.<BR>E.<BR>त्रै to preserve, affix क्त and ण optionally substituted for त; also त्रात; again, त्रै to preserve, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रात|त्रातं
त्रात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Preserved, guarded, protected.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Preserving, protection: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रापुष|त्रापुषं
त्रापुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Made of tin.<BR>E.<BR>त्रपुस् tin, affix अण, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायत्
त्रायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Preserving, protecting.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A plant: see the next.<BR>2 A protectress, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्रै to preserve, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रायमाण|त्रायमाणं
त्रायमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>A preserver, preserving.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A medicinal plant.<BR>E.<BR>त्रै to preserve, affix शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रास|त्रासः
त्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Fear, terror.<BR>2 A flaw or defect in a jewel.<BR>E.<BR>त्रस to fear, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासकर
त्रासकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Fearful, alarming.<BR>E.<BR>त्रास, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासदायिन्
त्रासदायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Terrifying, fear-exciting.<BR>E.<BR>त्रास fear, and दायिन् what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रासित
त्रासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Frightened, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रास to fear, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रि|त्रिः
त्रि<BR>plu. only, m. (त्रयः) f. (तिस्रः) n. (त्रीणि)<BR>Three.<BR>subst. m. sing. (त्रिः) plu. (त्रयः)<BR>Three times.<BR>a.<BR>thrice.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to pass, Uṇādi affix क, and त्रि substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंश|त्रिंशः
त्रिंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Thirtieth.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिंशत, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशक|त्रिंशकः
त्रिंशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Thirty collectively, a multitude of thirty.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिंशत thirty, affix क्वुन्^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्
त्रिंशत्<BR>f. sing. (-त्)<BR>Thirty, &c.<BR>(-तौ)<BR>Two thirties.<BR>plu. (-तः)<BR>Many thirties.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिं for त्रि three, and शत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिंशत्पत्र|त्रिंशत्पत्रं
त्रिंशत्पत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The white esculent water lily.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिशत thirty, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिक|त्रिकं
त्रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The lower part of the spine.<BR>2 The aggregate of three, a trine, a triad.<BR>3 The three mystical words to be pronounced in daily prayer.<BR>4 A place where three roads meet.<BR>5 Three spices, three myrobalans, &c. collectively: see त्रिकटु, त्रिफल and the like.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant: see गोक्षुरक.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A triangular frame or bar across the mouth of a well over which passes the rope of the bucket, or to which one end of it is tied to guard against, its slipping.<BR>2 A wooden frame at the mouth of a well, or the upper part of the well.<BR>3 A frame at the bottom of a well, on which the masonry rests.<BR>4 The cover or lid of a well.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुद्
त्रिककुद्<BR>m. (-द् or -त्)<BR>A mountain with three peaks.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, three, and ककुद a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिककुद
त्रिककुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Having three humps or peaks.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and ककुद् a hump, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकट|त्रिकटः
त्रिकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, (Ruellia longifolia,) &c. see गोक्षुरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकटु
त्रिकटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>The aggregate of three spices, viz. black and long pepper, and dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, or three-fold, and कटु pungent, (as a spice.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्ट|त्रिकण्टं|त्रिकण्टः
त्रिकण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>1 A plant, (Ruellia longifolia,) &c. त्रिकट.<BR>2 A sort of Euphorbia.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and कण्ट a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकण्टक|त्रिकण्टकः
त्रिकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of fish, (Silurus.)<BR>2 A plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to त्रिकण्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकाय|त्रिकायः
त्रिकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and काय a body, the three-bodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालज्ञ|त्रिकालज्ञः
त्रिकालज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Omniscient.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A divine sage.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>3 A name of Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect^1.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, काल time, and ज्ञ who knows, acquainted with the past, present, and future; also similar compounds as the next, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालदर्शिन्
त्रिकालदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिणी-शि)<BR>Omniscient.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A Ṛṣi or divine sage.<BR>2 A name of Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, काल time, and दर्शिन् who views: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकालविद्
त्रिकालविद्<BR>mfn. (-विद्-वित्)<BR>Omniscient.<BR>m. (-विद् or -वित्)<BR>A name of Buddha: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as before, विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकुद
त्रिकुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a mountain in the peninsula; it is also applicable to any mountain with three peaks.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Sea salt prepared by evaporation.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, कूट a peak, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकूर्च्चक|त्रिकूर्चक
त्रिकूर्च्चक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of knife with three edges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and कूर्च्चक a bunch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिकोण|त्रिकोणं|त्रिकोणः
त्रिकोण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The vulva.<BR>2 A triangle.<BR>3 Any triangular object.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिख|त्रिखं
त्रिख<BR>(इ) त्रिखि r. 1st cl. (त्रिङ्खति)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिख|त्रिखं
त्रिख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>A cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and ख a cavity or space; also read sometimes तृख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिखद्व
त्रिखद्व<BR>nf. (-द्वं-द्वी)<BR>The aggregate of three beds.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, खद्वा a bed, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगण|त्रिगणः
त्रिगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The aggregate of three human objects, or virtue, wealth, and desire.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and गण a class: see त्रिवर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=388" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगत
त्रिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tripled.<BR>2 Gone or done in three ways.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The expression of different senses by the same word.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्त|त्रिगर्त|त्रिगर्त्तः
त्रिगर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 A country in the north-west division of India, or<BR>m. plu. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Its inhabitants: apparently part of Lahore, said, by Mr. WILFORD, to be the modern Tahora, but differently described in the Koṣas: see जालन्धर and वाह्लीक.<BR>2 A form of calculation, (गणितान्तरे.)<BR>f. (-र्त्ता)<BR>1 A small worm.<BR>2 A lascivious woman, a wanton.<BR>3 A woman in general.<BR>4 A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and गर्त्त a hole, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त्तक|त्रिगर्तक|त्रिगर्त्तकः
त्रिगर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A country, the same as Vāhlika: see वाह्लीक.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुण|त्रिगुणं
त्रिगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)<BR>1 Thrice, three times, triple.<BR>2 Possessing the three Guṇas or properties.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The aggregate of the three qualities incident to human nature.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, गुण a time or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगुणाकृत|त्रिगुणाकृतं
त्रिगुणाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रिगुण three times, and आकृत made, wrought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगूढ
त्रिगूढ<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>The dancing or acting of a man in female attire.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and गूढ concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिचतुर
त्रिचतुर<BR>mfn. plur. (-राः-राः-राणि)<BR>Three or four.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and चतुर four, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिजातक|त्रिजातकं
त्रिजातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Three spices collectively, mace, cardamoms, and cassia leaf.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and जातक species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिज्या
त्रिज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>A radius, a sine of three signs or ninety degrees.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and ज्या a sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिण|त्रिणं
त्रिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Grass, meadow grass.<BR>E.<BR>see तृण, ऋ being changed to रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणता
त्रिणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 The state or abstract property of grass.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिण for तृण grass, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिणाचिकेत|त्रिणाचिकेतः
त्रिणाचिकेत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A portion of the Yajur Veda.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A follower of that branch of the Vedas. It is also sometimes read तृणाचिकेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितक्ष|त्रितक्षं
त्रितक्ष<BR>nf. (-क्षः-क्षी)<BR>An assemblage of three carpenters.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, तक्ष a carpenter, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रितय|त्रितयं
त्रितय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Third.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्ड|त्रिदंड|त्रिदण्डः
त्रिदण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 Three staves collectively.<BR>2 Triple subjection of words, thoughts, and acts; the state of a religious ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, दण्ड a staff, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डधारण
त्रिदण्डधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Carrying three staves tied together, (as done by some mendicants.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदण्ड, and धारण holding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदण्डिन्|त्रिदंडिन्
त्रिदण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A wandering devotee, one who carries three long bambu staves in his right hand.<BR>2 The religious man who has obtained a command over his words, thoughts, and actions, or mind, body, and speech.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and दण्ड a punishment, a staff, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदला
त्रिदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A creeping plant, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A god, a deity, an immortal.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि the third, and दशा state, being, (youth); enjoying perpetual youth; or त्रि three, and दश state, subject as well as mortals to the three conditions, of birth, being, and destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदश|त्रिदशः
त्रिदश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Thirteenth.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The thirteenth day of the fortnight; also त्रयोदश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशदीर्धिका
त्रिदशदीर्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The heavenly Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and दीर्धिका a long pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशन्
त्रिदशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Thirteen.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशनदी
त्रिदशनदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The heavenly Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशपति
त्रिदशपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशबधू
त्रिदशबधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश, and बधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशवनिता
त्रिदशवनिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A nymph of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश, and वनिता a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाङ्कुश|त्रिदशांकुश
त्रिदशाङ्कुश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाचार्य्य|त्रिदशाचार्य
त्रिदशाचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The preceptor of the gods, VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and आचार्य्य a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशायुध|त्रिदशायुधं
त्रिदशायुध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशारि|त्रिदशारिः
त्रिदशारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An Asura or infernal being hostile to the gods, a Titan, a Giant.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशालय|त्रिदशालयः
त्रिदशालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Svarga, INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>2 The mountain Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and आलय an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशावास|त्रिदशावासः
त्रिदशावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a god, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदशाहार|त्रिदशाहारः
त्रिदशाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Amṛta or ambrosia.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश a deity, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदालिका
त्रिदालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिन
त्रिदिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Three days collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिनस्पृश्
त्रिदिनस्पृश्<BR>m. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Conjunction or concurrence of three lunations with one solar day.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदिन, and स्पृश् contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिव|त्रिदिवः
त्रिदिव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 Sky, atmosphere, heaven.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि the three, BRAHMA, VIṢṆU, and ŚIVA, दिव to sport, affix क; the place where these three gods take divine pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवेश|त्रिदिवेशः
त्रिदिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A god, a deity.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदिव heaven, and ईश master or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदिवौकस्
त्रिदिवौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>A god, a celestial.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदिव heaven, and ओकस् asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदृश्
त्रिदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Tri-ocular, three-eyed.<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and दृश् an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोष|त्रिदोषं
त्रिदोष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Disorder of the three humours of the body, vitiation of the bile, blood, and phlegm.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and दोष a fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषघ्न
त्रिदोषघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Correcting the vitiated state of the three humours.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदोष, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिदोषज|त्रिदोषजः
त्रिदोषज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Disease, &c. proceeding from disorder of the three humours of the body<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदोष, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधा
त्रिधा<BR>ind.<BR>In three ways.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधातु|त्रिधातुः
त्रिधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>Three minerals, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and धातु mineral, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिधामन्
त्रिधामन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Having three residences, &c.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 An appellation of ŚIVA.<BR>3 Agni or fire.<BR>4 Death.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three (worlds), and धामन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनयन|त्रिनयनः
त्रिनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Three-eyed, tri-ocular.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and नयन an eye; this deity is represented with a third eye in his forehead; also similar compounds, as त्रिहृश्, त्रिनेत्र, त्र्यक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=389" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्र|त्रिनेत्रः
त्रिनेत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Tri-ocular.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and नेत्र eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिनेत्रचूडामणि|त्रिनेत्रचूडामणिः
त्रिनेत्रचूडामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिनेत्र ŚIVA, त्रूडा a crest and मणि a gem; being worn by that deity as his crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपक्ष
त्रिपक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A period of six weeks.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and पक्ष a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपताक|त्रिपताकं|त्रिपताकः
त्रिपताक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The forehead marked naturally with three horizontal lines.<BR>2 The hand with three fingers erect.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three or three-fold, and पताका a banner, a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपत्र|त्रिपत्रं|त्रिपत्रः
त्रिपत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Three-leaved trefoil.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपत्रक|त्रिपत्रकः
त्रिपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Kiṃśuka tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पत्र a leaf; having three leaves on each stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथ|त्रिपथं
त्रिपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 A place where three roads meet.<BR>2 Three ways or paths.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and पथ a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपथगा
त्रिपथगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपथ three roads, and गा who goes, flowing through earth, heaven, and hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपद
त्रिपद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दी-दं)<BR>1 Three-footed.<BR>2 Having three lines or divisions, (a stanza.)<BR>3 (In Arithmetic,) Trinomial.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 A tripod.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A verse of three lines, as the Gāyatrī.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>1 A creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>2 The girth of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपर्ण|त्रिपर्णः
त्रिपर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Three-leaved trefoil.<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपाद्
त्रिपाद्<BR>m. (-पाद्)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 Fever, (personified.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पाद foot or part; three-footed, alluding to VIṢṆU'S three steps which paced the universe; and the demon of fever is described in the Purāṇas, with three feet, and three heads, alluding probably to its three stages of cold, hot, and sweating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिव
त्रिपिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A long-eared goat.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and पिव who drinks, touching water with both ears as he laps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टप|त्रिपिष्टपं
त्रिपिष्टप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Heaven, Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 Sky, æther.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्टप a world. and त्रि three, or the third; also त्रिविष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपिष्टपसद्
त्रिपिष्टपसद्<BR>m. (-सद्)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपिष्टप heaven, and सद् who goes, from सद् with क्विप् affix; also त्रिविष्टपसद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुट|त्रिपुटः
त्रिपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Pulse, pease of three kinds.<BR>2 A bank or shore.<BR>3 A kind of vetch, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>4 A cubit.<BR>5 A plant, (Ruellia longifolia.)<BR>f. (-टा-टी)<BR>A plant, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>2 Arabian jasmine.<BR>3 A goddess.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पुट skin or coat of a seed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटक|त्रिपुटकः
त्रिपुटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A triangle.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटिन्
त्रिपुटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>The castor oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, पुट the seed vessel, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुटीफल|त्रिपुटीफलः
त्रिपुटीफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The castor oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुटी as above, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्र|त्रिपुंड्र|त्रिपुण्ड्रं
त्रिपुण्ड्र<BR>n. (-ण्ड्रं)<BR>Three curved horizontal marks, made across the forehead with cowdung, ashes, &c.; they are worn especially by the followers of ŚIVA, or ŚAKTI, and are indispensable in proceeding to worship the former.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, triple, and पुण्ड्र a line; also with उन् added त्रिपुण्ड्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुण्ड्रक|त्रिपुण्ड्रकं
त्रिपुण्ड्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>See the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं|त्रिपुरः
त्रिपुर<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>A district, the modern Tipparah, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of an Asura, and king of Tripura.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and पुर a city, the district and dominion of that Asura, consisting of three strong and famous cities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरदहन|त्रिपुरदहनः
त्रिपुरदहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुर the country of Tripura, and दहन burning, consuming; the Asura and his three cities being destroyed by MAHĀDEVA; also similar names, as त्रिपुरजित्, त्रिपुरसूदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरमल्लिका
त्रिपुरमल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal plant, apparently a kind of jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुर Tipperah, and मल्लिका jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरान्तक|त्रिपुरांतक|त्रिपुरान्तकः
त्रिपुरान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुर, and अन्तक ender, destroyer: see त्रिपुरदहन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुष
त्रिपुरुष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Three generations collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरुषागत
त्रिपुरुषागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Enjoyed or inherited through three generations.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुरुष, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपौरुष
त्रिपौरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Relating or belonging to three persons or generations, offered to three, (the funeral cake, &c.) inherited from three, (an estate, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रिपुरुष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुषा
त्रिपुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Black Tëori.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपृष्ठ|त्रिपृष्ठः
त्रिपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A king, and one of the Vāsudevas, or descendants of VASUDEVA, according to the Jains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिफला
त्रिफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The three myrobalans.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, फल fruit, fem. affix टाप्; also with ङीष् affix त्रिफली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिबुलीक
त्रिबुलीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, (the three humors,) बुल to sink, affix कीकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभण्डी
त्रिभण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A plant, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, (ailments, or bile, phlegm, and fever,) भडि to oppose, affix अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभद्र|त्रिभद्रं
त्रिभद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>Copulation, cohabitation.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and भद्र pleasurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुज
त्रिभुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A triangle.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिभुवन|त्रिभुवनं
त्रिभुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Three worlds, or heaven, earth, and hell.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमधु|त्रिमधुः
त्रिमधु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>1 A portion of the Rig Veda.<BR>2 A follower or student of the Tri-madhu section of the Rig Veda.<BR>n. (-धुः)<BR>Ghee, honey, and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and मधु honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमार्ग्गी|त्रिमार्गी
त्रिमार्ग्गी<BR>f. (-र्ग्गी)<BR>The meeting of three roads.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and मार्ग्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुकुट|त्रिमुकुटः
त्रिमुकुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A mountain with three peaks.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and मुकुट a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमुख|त्रिमुखः
त्रिमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Having three faces.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A divine attendant upon a Jaina saint.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A female deity of the Jaina sect.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and मुख a face, three-faced, or त्रि three (worlds), and मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्त्ति|त्रिमूर्ति|त्रिमूर्तिः|त्रिमूर्त्तिः
त्रिमूर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>2 The united form of BRAHMĀ, VIṢṆU, and ŚIVA, or the Hindu trial.<BR>3 One possessing three forms or modes of being.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and मूर्त्ति form, matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिमूर्द्ध
त्रिमूर्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं)<BR>Three-headed.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and मूर्द्धन् the forehead, ष aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियव
त्रियव<BR>n. (-बः)<BR>A Ratti or weight of three barley-corns.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and यव barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियष्टि|त्रियष्टिः
त्रियष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Mollugo pentaphylla.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and यष्टि a line; having three stalks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=390" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामक|त्रियामकं
त्रियामक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्रि the three objects of life, and यामक impeder, from यम, with ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियामा
त्रियामा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The YAMUNĀ or Jumna river.<BR>3 Indigo.<BR>4 Black Tëori, a plant so called.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three (times, or past, present, and future,) या to go, affix मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रियूह|त्रियूहः
त्रियूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A brown or chesnut horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरात्र|त्रिरात्रं|त्रिरात्रः
त्रिरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Three nights collectively, or the duration of three nights.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and रात्रि a night; compounded with a numeral रात्रि substitutes अ for its final, and becomes neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिरेख|त्रिरेखः
त्रिरेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A conch.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and रेखा a line; this shell being marked with three lines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकी
त्रिलोकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The aggregate of the three worlds, or heaven, earth, and hell, collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and लोक a world, and ङीप् affix, with the sense of aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोकेश|त्रिलोकेशः
त्रिलोकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिलोक the three worlds or the universe, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोचन|त्रिलोचनः
त्रिलोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Tri-ocular, three-eyed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A female deity of the Jainas.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and लोचन an eye: see त्रिदृश् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिलोहक|त्रिलोहकं
त्रिलोहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold, silver, and copper.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and लोहक metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्ग|त्रिवर्गः
त्रिवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Three human objects or pursuits, as love, duty, and wealth.<BR>2 Three conditions of a king or state; prosperity, evenness, and decay; or loss, gain, equality, &c.<BR>3 The three qualities of nature, purity, blindness, and depravity.<BR>4 The three myrobalans.<BR>5 The three spices: see त्रिकटु.<BR>6 Propriety, good behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and वर्ग a class; a class or aggregate of three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्गपारीण
त्रिवर्गपारीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having passed through the three conditions, or attained the three objects of life.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवर्ग, and पारीण gone to the opposite shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्णक|त्रिवर्णकं
त्रिवर्णक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The three myrobalans.<BR>2 The three spices.<BR>3 A plant, (Ruellia longifolia): see गोक्षुरक.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, वर्ण a class, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवर्षिका
त्रिवर्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A three years old heifer.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and वर्ष a year, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवली
त्रिवली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Three folds of skin on the abdomen, from obesity.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and वली a wrinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविक्रम|त्रिविक्रमः
त्रिविक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and विक्रम going; crossing over the three worlds in three steps, to the discomfiture of BĀLĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविद्या
त्रिविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Three branches of knowledge, especially that of the three Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविध
त्रिविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>In three ways, of three kinds.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टप|त्रिविष्टपं
त्रिविष्टप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Heaven or paradise.<BR>2 The three worlds, or heaven, earth, and hell: see त्रिपिष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिविष्टपसद्
त्रिविष्टपसद्<BR>m. (-सद)<BR>A deity; also त्रिपिष्टपसद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्
त्रिवृत्<BR>mfn. (-वृत्)<BR>Triple, tri-form, three-fold.<BR>m. (-वृत्)<BR>1 A plant of valuable purgative properties, commonly called Tëori, and distinguished into two species, white and black, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>2 Combining any thing by three.<BR>2 A triple cord, a girdle, &c. of three strings.<BR>3 A kind of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, (three seed vessels,) वृ to cherish, affix क्विप्, and तुक् added; also with टाप् added त्रिवृता (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्करण|त्रिवृत्करणं
त्रिवृत्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Combining earth, water, and fire, in the proportion of half of one with a quarter of each of the others.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवृत्, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवृत्पर्णी
त्रिवृत्पर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A potherb, (Hilancha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवृत् Tëori, and पर्ण a leaf; having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेणी
त्रिवेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A name of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, वेणी a braid of hair: the name is especially applied to the river at Allahabad, where it receives the Jumna, and is supposed to receive under ground the Sarasvatī; it is also that of a village in Bengal, above Hugli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेद|त्रिवेदः
त्रिवेद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The three Vedas collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिवेदिन्
त्रिवेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A Brahman acquainted with three Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवेद्, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कु|त्रिशंकु|त्रिशङ्कुः
त्रिशङ्कु<BR>m. (ङ्कुः)<BR>1 The name of a king of the solar race, famous for attempting to go to heaven in his mortal frame, by the aid of VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>3 A grasshopper.<BR>4 A bird, the Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>5 A fire-fly.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, शङ्कु a dart, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुज|त्रिशंकुज|त्रिशङ्कुजः
त्रिशङ्कुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of HARIŚCANDRA, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिशङ्कु, and ज born, descended from TRIŚAṄKU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन्|त्रिशंकुयाजिन्
त्रिशङ्कुयाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>VIŚVĀMITRA, a celebrated sage and saint.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिशङ्कु the king so named, and याजिन् causing to worship; being the family priest of the monarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशरण|त्रिशरणः
त्रिशरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A Jina, a sanctified teacher of the Jaina sect.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, (the three worlds,) and शरण protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशला
त्रिशला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The mother of VARDDHAMĀNA, the last of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिख|त्रिशिखं|त्रिशिखः
त्रिशिख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Three-crested, three-headed.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 A crest, a tiara with three points.<BR>2 A trident, a three-pronged spear.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The son of RĀVAṆA, a demon with three heads.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशिरस्
त्रिशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Three-headed.<BR>m. (-राः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 Fever personified as a demon with three heads: see त्रिपाद.<BR>3 A son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and शिरस् a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशीर्षक|त्रिशीर्षकं
त्रिशीर्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Three-headed.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A trident, a tri-pointed spear.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and शीर्ष a head, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूल|त्रिशूलं
त्रिशूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A trident, a three-pointed pike or spear, especially the weapon of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three or Tri, and शूल a dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशूलिन्
त्रिशूलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिशूल, and इनि affix, armed with a trident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्ग|त्रिशृंग|त्रिशृङ्गः
त्रिशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः).<BR>1 A hill with three peaks.<BR>2 A triangle.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिशृङ्गिन्
त्रिशृङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of fish, commonly^1 Rohi, (Cyprinus rohita, HAM.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवण
त्रिषवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The three ablutions to be performed in the day, or at dawn, noon, and sun-set.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, सवन bathing; also read त्रिसवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिषवणस्नायिन्
त्रिषवणस्नायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A man performing regularly the prescribed ablutions, morning, noon, and night.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, सवन time or period of ablution, and स्नायिन् who bathes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्टुभ्
त्रिष्टुभ्<BR>f. (-ष्टुप्)<BR>A form of metre, the stanza consisting of four lines of eleven syllables each, or of five lines, one of eleven [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">Page392</a>] and four of eight each, forming altogether forty-four syllables; there are other varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=391" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिष्ठ
त्रिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Situated in three places.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and स्था to be, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसन्ध्य|त्रिसंध्य|त्रिसन्ध्यं
त्रिसन्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या or -न्ध्यी-न्ध्यं)<BR>The three periods of the day, or dawn, noon, and eve.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and सन्ध्य either of the periods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसम|त्रिसमं
त्रिसम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>An aggregate of three like or equal things.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसर|त्रिसरः
त्रिसर<BR>subst. mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A dish of sesamum, rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, three-fold, and सर what is, from सृ to go or get, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसवन|त्रिसवनं
त्रिसवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bathing thrice: see त्रिषवण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसीत्य|त्रिसीत्यं
त्रिसीत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि thrice, and सीत्य ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्ण|त्रिसुपर्णः
त्रिसुपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A portion of the Rig and Yajur Vedas.<BR>2 An observance enjoined by it.<BR>2 A Brahman following it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिसुपर्णिक
त्रिसुपर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Tri Suparṇa Brahman: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिस्रोतस्
त्रिस्रोतस्<BR>f. (-ताः)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 Another river.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and स्रोतस् a river, the river of the three worlds, or one with three channels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहल्य|त्रिहल्यं
त्रिहल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Thrice ploughed, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि thrice, हल्य ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिहायण
त्रिहायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Three years, (old, &c.)<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A threeyears-old heifer.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and हायन a year; also read त्रिहायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुट
त्रुट<BR>r. 4th cl. (त्रुल्यति) r. 6th cl. (त्रुटति) and 10th cl. (त्रोटयति)<BR>To cut, literally or metaphorically; to cut, (wood, &c.) to cut or solve, (difficulties, doubts, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटि|त्रुटिः
त्रुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>1 Cutting, breaking.<BR>2 Loss, destruction.<BR>3 Breaking a promise, &c.<BR>4 Small cardamoms, (Alpinia cardamomum.)<BR>5 A short time, a moment.<BR>6 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>7 (Always feminine, though used attributively,) Little, small.<BR>8 An atom, or a visible atom composed of three subtler elementary particles.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुट to cut or divide, affix कि and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटित
त्रुटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut, broken, divided.<BR>2 Hurt, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुट, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटितवत्
त्रुटितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Chapped, chafed, cut.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुट, and क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुटिवीज|त्रुटिवीजः
त्रुटिवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An esculent root: see कचु.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुटि small, and वीज a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुप
त्रुप<BR>r. 1st cl. (त्रोपति)<BR>To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुफ
त्रुफ<BR>r. 1st cl. (त्रोफति)<BR>To hurt, to kill or injure; also तुफ, तुम्फ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्प
त्रुम्प<BR>r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्पति)<BR>To hurt or injure: see तुप, तुम्प, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रुम्फ
त्रुम्फ<BR>r. 1st cl. (त्रुम्फति)<BR>To kill or injure; also त्रुफ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेता
त्रेता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The second Yug or age of the Hindus, consisting of 1,296,000 years.<BR>2 The three sacred fires collectively, or the southern, household, and sacrificial fires.<BR>E.<BR>त्र preservation, &c. derived from त्रै to preserve, इत obtained, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेताग्नि
त्रेताग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A man who has preserved the three sacred fires.<BR>E.<BR>त्रेता as above, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेतायुग|त्रेतायुगं
त्रेतायुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The second or Tretā age.<BR>E.<BR>त्रेता, and युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रेधा
त्रेधा<BR>ind.<BR>Triple, three-fold, in three ways.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, धा affix, and ए substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रै
त्रै<BR>(ङ) त्रैङ 1st cl. (त्रायते)<BR>To preserve, to protect, to cherish, to defend, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुणिक
त्रैगुणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Giving three times, relating to thrice, three qualities, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिगुण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैगुण्य|त्रैगुण्यं
त्रैगुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 The quality of three Guṇas or properties collectively.<BR>2 A trine, a multiplication by three.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिगुण, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैदशिक
त्रैदशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sacred to the gods, belonging or relating to them.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिदश, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैधम्
त्रैधम्<BR>ind.<BR>In three ways, three-fold.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, धमञ् affix; also ड being added, the word becomes an attributive, and may be inflected in the three genders, त्रैध, mfn. (-धः-धी-धं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैपुर|त्रैपुरः
त्रैपुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Tripura or Tipperah: see त्रिपुर.<BR>E.<BR>अण् added to त्रिपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैराशिक|त्रैराशिकं
त्रैराशिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>(In Arithmetic,) The rule of three: it is of two kinds क्रमत्रैराशिकः Rule of three direct, व्यस्त or विलोमत्रैराशिक Rule of three inverse.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, राशि quantity, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैरूप्य
त्रैरूप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Three ways or forms.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, रूप form, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक्य|त्रैलोक्यं
त्रैलोक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>The three worlds, or heaven, hell, and earth.<BR>E.<BR>वि लोक, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैलोक्यविजया
त्रैलोक्यविजया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A sort of hemp from which an intoxicating infusion, &c. is prepared.<BR>E.<BR>त्रैलोक्य, and विजाय subduing; alluding to its inebriating properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्गिक
त्रैवर्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the three objects of life.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवर्ग, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवर्णिक
त्रैवर्णिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to three castes, the first three.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, वर्ण cast, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवार्षिक
त्रैवार्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Triennial, three years old, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवष three years, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविद्य|त्रैविद्यं|त्रैविद्यः
त्रैविद्य<BR>m. (-ट्यः)<BR>A scholar in the three Vedas, or one who possesses three sciences^1.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>A collection or assembly of learned Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, विद्या knowledge, and अण् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैविध्य|त्रैविध्यं
त्रैविध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Three ways or kinds.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिविध, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैवेदिक
त्रैवेदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Scriptural, enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिवेद, and यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैष्टुभ
त्रैष्टुभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भी-भं)<BR>Relating to or written in the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिष्टुभ्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैस्वर्य्य|त्रैस्वर्य
त्रैस्वर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>The three accents collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and स्वर vowel sound, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रैहायण
त्रैहायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A period or age of three years.<BR>E.<BR>त्रिहायण, and उ, अण् affix; also read त्रैहायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटक|त्रोटकं|त्रोटकः
त्रोटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Angry speech.<BR>2 A minor drama, such as the Vikramorvaśī.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुट to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटकी
त्रोटकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A Rāgiṇī or one of the female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटि|त्रोटिः
त्रोटि<BR>f. (-टिः or टी)<BR>1 The beak or bill of a bird.<BR>2 A bird in general.<BR>3 A kind of pike, (Esox kankila.)<BR>4 A medicinal plant: see कट्फल.<BR>E.<BR>त्रुट to cut, affix अच्, and fem. affix इन् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोटिहस्त|त्रोटिहस्तः
त्रोटिहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>त्रोठि a beak, and हस्त a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रोत्र|त्रोत्रं
त्रोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A goad.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>E.<BR>त्रै to preserve, उत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रौक
त्रौक<BR>(ऋ) त्रौकृ r. 1st cl. (त्रौकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=392" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यंश|त्र्यंशः
त्र्यंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Three-fourths, three shares.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्ष|त्र्यक्षः
त्र्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Tri-ocular.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, अक्षि an eye, अच् substituted for the final: see त्रिदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यक्षर|त्र्यक्षरः
त्र्यक्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A genealogist, the Ghaṭaka or person whose business it is to form alliances.<BR>2 A word, &c. of three letters.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यङ्गट|त्र्यंगट|त्र्यङ्गटं|त्र्यङ्गटः
त्र्यङ्गट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 A sling or three strings like those of a balance, suspended to either end of a pole for the purpose of carrying burthens.<BR>2 A sort of collyrium.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, अङ्ग body, and अट what goes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यञ्जन|त्र्यञ्जनं
त्र्यञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Combination of three, or Kālāñjana, Puṣpāñjana, and Karāñjana collyria.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अञ्जन a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यधिष्ठान|त्र्यधिष्ठानः
त्र्यधिष्ठान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Situate in or affected by three places, (as body, mind, speech.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अधिष्ठान site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यध्वगा
त्र्यध्वगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A name of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, अध्व a road, and ग what goes; going through the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यब्द
त्र्यब्द<BR>n. (-ब्दं)<BR>A period of three years.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बक|त्र्यंबक|त्र्यम्बकः
त्र्यम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, (the three Vedas,) अबि to speak or sound, and कन् added; or त्रि may mean the three letters, अ, उ, म, combined in the mystical word ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यम्बकसस्व
त्र्यम्बकसस्व<BR>m. (-स्वः)<BR>KUVERA the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>त्र्यम्बक ŚIVA, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यवर
त्र्यवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having three inferiors or followers.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अवर inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यसरेणु
त्र्यसरेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A gross atom, one composed of three subtle atoms: see त्रसरेणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यस्र
त्र्यस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A triangle.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यह|त्र्यहः
त्र्यह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Three days collectively.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यहस्पर्श|त्र्यहस्पर्शः
त्र्यहस्पर्श<BR>n. (-र्शं)<BR>Meeting of three lunations in one solar day.<BR>E.<BR>त्र्यह, and स्पर्श contact; also त्र्यहस्पृश, m. (-स्पृक्) and त्र्यहस्पृशं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्यहैहिक|त्र्यहैहिकः
त्र्यहैहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Providing for three days.<BR>E.<BR>त्र्यह, and ऐहिक who makes an effort for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्याहिक|त्र्याहिकः
त्र्याहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Produced or performed, &c. in three days.<BR>2 Quartan (fever.)<BR>E.<BR>त्रि, and आहिक diurnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्र्युषण|त्र्युषणं
त्र्युषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The three spices collectively, or black pepper, long pepper, and dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>त्रि three, and उषण a spice or pungent substance; also with ऊषण the same, त्र्यूषण, n. (-णं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्व|त्वं|त्वः
त्व<BR>mfn. (त्वः त्वा त्वं)<BR>Other, different.<BR>E.<BR>तन to divide or spread, and व substituted for the final letter of the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्कण्डुर|त्वक्कंडुर|त्वक्कण्डुरः
त्वक्कण्डुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sore or wound.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् the skin, कण्डु itching or irritation, and र what excites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्क्षीरा
त्वक्क्षीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The manna of the bambu.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच् the bark of the bambu, and क्षीर milk; also with ङीप् affix, त्वक्क्षीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्छद|त्वक्छदः
त्वक्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A plant, commonly Kshirakanchuki.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् bark, and छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्छेद|त्वक्छेदः
त्वक्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cut, a scratch.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्, and छेद a cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्त्र
त्वक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>Armour.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्, and त्र what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पत्र|त्वक्पत्रं
त्वक्पत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Woody cassia.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A medicinal and vegetable substance: see हिङ्गुपत्री.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् bark, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्परिपुटन
त्वक्परिपुटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Desquamation, pealing of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्, and परिपुटन pealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पुष्प|त्वक्पुष्पं|त्वक्पुष्पः
त्वक्पुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Erection of the hairs of the body, horripilation.<BR>nf. (-ष्पं-ष्पी)<BR>Blotch, scab, cutaneous eruption, &c.<BR>E.<BR>म्बक् the skin, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्पुष्पिका
त्वक्पुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Scab, blotch: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to त्वकपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्सार|त्वक्सारः
त्वक्सार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 Woody cassia.<BR>f. (रा)<BR>Bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् bark, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्सुगन्ध|त्वक्सुगंध|त्वक्सुगन्धः
त्वक्सुगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>An orange.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A perfume, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् skin or rind, and सुगन्ध fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्भेद|त्वग्भेदः
त्वग्भेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A flesh wound, a scratch.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच्, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्भेदक|त्वग्भेदकः
त्वग्भेदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stabber, a scratcher, one who draws blood from the skin.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच्, and भेदक who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वक्ष
त्वक्ष<BR>(ऊ) त्वक्षू r. 1st cl. (त्वक्षति)<BR>1 To pare, to make thin.<BR>2 To be thin.<BR>3 To peel, to skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग
त्वग<BR>(इ) त्वगि r. 1st cl. (त्वंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगङ्कुर|त्वगंकुर|त्वगङ्कुरः
त्वगङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Erection of the hairs of the body.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच् or त्वक् skin, and अङ्कुर a sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगस्थिमात्रशेष
त्वगस्थिमात्रशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Reduced to a skeleton, to mere skin and bone.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच् skin, अस्थि bone, मात्र mere, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वगाक्षीरी
त्वगाक्षीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The manna of the bambu.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् bark, आङ् limitative, and क्षीरी milk, being of a milky colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्गन्ध|त्वग्गंध|त्वग्गन्धः
त्वग्गन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>An orange.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच् rind, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्दोष|त्वग्दोषः
त्वग्दोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वग्रोग|त्वग्रोगः
त्वग्रोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Leprosy.<BR>2 Any cutaneous disease.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच्, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वङ्कार|त्वंकार|त्वंकारः
त्वङ्कार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The expression, ‘thou.’<BR>E.<BR>त्व, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वङ्मय
त्वङ्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of bark or skin.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक् skin, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच|त्वचं
त्वच<BR>r. 6th cl. (त्वचति)<BR>To cover, to clothe, to invest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच्
त्वच्<BR>f. (त्वक्)<BR>1 Skin.<BR>2 Bark, rind, peel, &c.<BR>3 Woody cassia.<BR>E.<BR>तन to spread, to encircle or cover, Uṇādi affix चिक्, and व substituted for the final letters of the radical; also अच being added त्वच and त्वचा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वच|त्वचं
त्वच<BR>nf. (-चं-चा)<BR>1 Skin.<BR>2 Bark, rind.<BR>3 Woody cassia: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचापत्र|त्वचापत्रं
त्वचापत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Woody cassia.<BR>E.<BR>त्वचा bark, and पत्र a leaf; also त्वक्पत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिष्ठ|त्वचिष्ठः
त्वचिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Having abundant skin or bark.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच skin, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative; also with ईयसुन् affix त्वचीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिसार|त्वचिसारः
त्वचिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>त्वचि seventh case of त्वच्, in the bark, and सार strength, pith; also त्वक्सार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वचिसुगन्धा
त्वचिसुगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>त्वचि in the bark, सुगन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वञ्च
त्वञ्च<BR>(उ) तञ्जु r. 1st cl. (त्वञ्चति)<BR>To go, or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्
त्वत्<BR>mfn. (-त्वत्)<BR>Other, different: see त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वत्क
त्वत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Thine, your.<BR>E.<BR>त्वत् thine, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वदीय|त्वदीयं
त्वदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Thine.<BR>E.<BR>त्वत्, from त्वं thou, and छ added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वर
त्वर<BR>(ञि आ) ञित्वरा r. 1st cl. (त्वरते)<BR>To hurry, to make haste, to go or move with speed, to do any thing readily or precipitately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरण|त्वरणं
त्वरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making haste, speed, velocity.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to haste, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरमाण
त्वरमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Hastening, making haste, going speedily.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to be quick, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरा
त्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Haste, speed.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to make haste, affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=393" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरान्वित
त्वरान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Swift, quick.<BR>E.<BR>त्वरा haste, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायण
त्वरायण<BR>mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Adherence, attachment.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to go, with speed, and युच् affix: see तुरायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरायुक्त
त्वरायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Quick, expeditious.<BR>E.<BR>त्वरा, and युक्त having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरि|त्वरिः
त्वरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>Haste, speed.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to make haste, affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरित|त्वरितं
त्वरित<BR>mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Quick, swift, expeditious.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Dispatch, haste.<BR>adv.<BR>Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E.<BR>त्वर to make haste, affix क्त, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरितगति
त्वरितगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Swift motion.<BR>2 A species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>E.<BR>त्वरित, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वरितोदित|त्वरितोदितं
त्वरितोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken fast, hurried.<BR>E.<BR>त्वरित quickly, उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्ट|त्वष्टः
त्वष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pared, made thin.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्ष to make thin, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टि|त्वष्टिः
त्वष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Carpentry.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्ष to plane, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वष्टृ
त्वष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 A carpenter.<BR>2 A name of VIŚVAKARMĀ, the artist of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>त्वक्ष to pare, affix तृच्.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>तिष to shine, Uṇādi affix तृच्, and अ substituted for the radical इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाच
त्वाच<BR>mfn. (-चः-ची-चं)<BR>1 Cuticular, relating to the skin.<BR>2 Contagious, derived from touch.<BR>E.<BR>त्वच्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाचप्रत्यक्ष|त्वाचप्रत्यक्षं
त्वाचप्रत्यक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>Ascertainment of objects by contact.<BR>E.<BR>त्वाच, and प्रत्यक्ष perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वाष्ट्र|त्वाष्ट्रः
त्वाष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>The name of a demon, also called VṚTRĀSURA.<BR>nf. (-ष्ट्रं-ष्ट्री)<BR>One of the lunar mansions, the fourteenth or Citra.<BR>f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>1 A wife of SŪRYA, or the sun; also called SAṂJÑĀ, the daughter of VIŚVAKARMA.<BR>2 A small car.<BR>E.<BR>त्वष्टृ the sun, or a carpenter, अण् affix of relation or descent, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष
त्विष<BR>r. 1st cl. (औ) औत्विष (त्वेषति)<BR>To shine.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विष्
त्विष्<BR>f. (-त्विट्)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Splendour, beauty.<BR>3 Speech.<BR>4 Wish, desire.<BR>5 Custom, practice, usage.<BR>E.<BR>त्विष to shine, affix क्विप्; also with टाप् added त्विषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषा
त्विषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Light: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषाम्पति|त्विषांपति|त्विषाम्पतिः
त्विषाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>त्विषां gen. plu. of तिष् light, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्विषि|त्विषिः
त्विषि<BR>m. (-षिः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>त्विष to shine, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सर
त्सर<BR>r. 1st cl. (त्सरति)<BR>To proceed fraudulently or crookedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्सरु|त्सरुः
त्सरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR>E.<BR>त्सर to go, Uṇādi affix उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ<BR>The seventeenth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, and second of the dental class; the aspirate of the preceding letter, and expressed by Ṭh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थ|थं|थः
थ<BR>n. (थं)<BR>1 Auspiciousness.<BR>2 Fear, terror.<BR>3 Preserving, preservation.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>3 A disease.<BR>E.<BR>स्था to stand, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुड
थुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (थुडति)<BR>To cover, to skreen, to clothe or hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुत्कार|थुत्कारः
थुत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sound made in spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुथु
थुथु<BR>ind.<BR>Imitative sound of spitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुध
थुध<BR>r. 4th cl. (थुध्यति-ते)<BR>To become pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थुर्व|थुर्व्व
थुर्व<BR>(ई) थुर्वी r. 1st cl. (थुर्वति)<BR>To kill, to injure or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

थोडन|थोडनं
थोडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Covering, clothing, wrapping up.<BR>E.<BR>थुड and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द<BR>The third letter of the dental class, and eighteenth consonant in the Nāgarī alphabet, corresponding to the letter D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द|दं|दः
द<BR>n. (दं)<BR>A wife.<BR>nf. (दं दा)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Dividing, cutting, breaking, &c.<BR>f. (दा)<BR>1 Purifying, cleansing.<BR>2 Preserving, cherishing.<BR>3 Repentance.<BR>m. (दः)<BR>1 A donor, a giver.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A gift, a thing given.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, or दो to cut, &c. affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश<BR>r. 1st cl. (दंशति)<BR>To bite, to sting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंश|दंशः
दंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A gadfly.<BR>2 A tooth.<BR>3 Biting, stinging.<BR>4 Armour, mail.<BR>5 Cutting, dividing, tearing.<BR>6 Fault, defect.<BR>7 A joint, a limb.<BR>8 The sting of a snake.<BR>9 Pungency.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A small gadfly.<BR>E.<BR>दंश to bite or sting, affix अच्, diminutive affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशक|दंशकः
दंशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What bites or stings.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gadfly.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशन|दंशनं
दंशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Biting, stinging.<BR>2 Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>दंश to bite, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशभीरु|दंशभीरुः
दंशभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>दंश a gadfly, and भीरु afraid of; also with कन् added, दंशभीरुक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशमूल|दंशमूलः
दंशमूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>दंश biting, and मूल a root; the root of this plant is substituted in Bengal for horseradish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशित|दंशितः
दंशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Armed, mailed.<BR>2 Bitten, stung.<BR>E.<BR>दंश armour, and इतच् affix, or दंश to bite, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंशेर
दंशेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Mischievous, noxious.<BR>E.<BR>दंश to bite or sting, Uṇādi affix एरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रा
दंष्ट्रा<BR>f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>A large tooth, a tusk.<BR>E.<BR>दंश to bite, affix ष्ट्रन्, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिका
दंष्ट्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The beard.<BR>E.<BR>दंष्ट्रा a tooth, इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंष्ट्रिन्
दंष्ट्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रिणी-ष्ट्रि)<BR>1 Biting or wounding with the teeth, (any animal, &c.)<BR>2 Tusked, having tusks or sharp teeth.<BR>3 Carnivorous.<BR>m. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दंष्ट्रा a tooth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंसन|दंसनं
दंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Armour, mail: see दंशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक|दकं
दक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>see उदक, the initial vowel being dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (दक्षते)<BR>1 To grow or increase.<BR>2 To dispatch, to expedite, to do quickly.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR>4 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्ष|दक्षः
दक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Clever, able, dexterous.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A Brahmādika; according to one legend, son of BRAHMĀ, born from the thumb of his right hand, for the purpose of peopling the world: according to another, he is the son of the Munis, called Prācetasas. DAKṢA had sixty daughters, of whom twenty-seven are the nymphs who form the lunar asterisms, and wives of the moon; one of his daughters also was SATI or DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA; and seventeen were married to KAŚYAPA, and were the mothers of all created beings. DAKṢA was on one occasion decapitated by ŚIVA: see दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्; he is sometimes regarded as an Avatāra of BRAHMĀ himself. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">Page395</a>]<BR>2 A Muni and legislator, who flourished in the beginning of the Tretā Yuga.<BR>3 A kind of tree.<BR>4 The bull of ŚIVA.<BR>5 A cock.<BR>6 A scholar, a Paṇḍita.<BR>7 A dexterous or clever man.<BR>8 ŚIVA.<BR>9 A name of Agni of fire.<BR>10 A general lover, one attached to many mistresses.<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष to grow or increase, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=394" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षकन्या
दक्षकन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and कन्या the maiden, the daughter of DAKṢA, who in this case seems to be identified with Himāla, the snowy mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजा
दक्षजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>9 A lunar asterism.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and जा born: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षजापति|दक्षजापतिः
दक्षजापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The deity ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षजा a lunar asterism or DURGĀ, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षता
दक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dexterity, cleverness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to दक्ष; also with त्व, दक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञ
दक्षयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>The sacrifice made by DAKṢA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी
दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षयज्ञ, and विनाशिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षसावर्णि|दक्षसावर्णिः
दक्षसावर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>The ninth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्
दक्षाध्वरध्वंसकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष the Brahmādika, as DAKṢA, अध्वर a sacrifice, ध्वंसकृत् subduer or disturber: DAKṢA having on one occasion made a sacrifice, to which he invited all the gods, except his son-in law ŚIVA, and his wife SATI, the latter went unbid, and being received coolly, threw herself into the fire; an emanation of ŚIVA, proceeded against DAKṢA, and an affray ensued, in which the gods and Ṛṣis were maltreated and dispersed, and DAKṢA decapitated; he was restored to life, and the head of a ram substituted for the one he had lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षाय्य|दक्षाय्यः
दक्षाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>1 The bird of VIṢṆU, Garuḍa.<BR>2 A vulture.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष to hurt, आय्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण|दक्षिणः
दक्षिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Candid, sincere, honest, upright.<BR>2 Right, (not left.)<BR>3 South, southern.<BR>4 Dependent, subject.<BR>5 Clever, able, dexterous.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 A present to Brahmans, upon solemn or sacrificial occasions.<BR>2 The south.<BR>3 Completion of any rite, fixing or establishing any act or place.<BR>4 A form or figure of DURGĀ, in which the right side is said to be advanced.<BR>5 Donation to Brahmans, personified as a goddess, said to be born from KṚṢṆA'S right side.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष to prosper, &c. Uṇādi affix इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणकालिका
दक्षिणकालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A form of DURGĀ worshipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and कालिका a form of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणतस्
दक्षिणतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Southward, southerly.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to दक्षिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपथ
दक्षिणपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 The south.<BR>2 Southern road or course.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणपूर्व्वा|दक्षिणपूर्वा
दक्षिणपूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>The south-east quarter.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण south, and पूर्व्व east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणस्थ|दक्षिणस्थः
दक्षिणस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Upon the right side, to the south, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण as above, and स्थ who stays or abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्नि|दक्षिणाग्निः
दक्षिणाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>One kind of sacred fire, that which is taken from the domestic or consecrated fire, and is placed to the south.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण south, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाग्र
दक्षिणाग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Pointing to the south, having the head or top to the south.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचल|दक्षिणाचलः
दक्षिणाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Malaya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण south, and अचल mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाचार|दक्षिणाचारः
दक्षिणाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A worshipper of Śakti according to the purer or right-hand ritual.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्
दक्षिणात्<BR>ind.<BR>Southward.<BR>E.<BR>the fifth case of दक्षिण, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणात्यय|दक्षिणात्ययः
दक्षिणात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A southern, or an inhabitant of the south.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, अत्यय who goes to or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथ|दक्षिणापथः
दक्षिणापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The south, the southern direction or quarter.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिणा, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणापथजन्मन्
दक्षिणापथजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A southern, or the Andhakas, Guhas, Pulindas, Savaras, Cucukas, and Madrapas, all outcaste or barbarous tribes.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिणापथ, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाप्रवण
दक्षिणाप्रवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Declining, shelving or inclining to the south.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिणा, and प्रवण declivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणामुख|दक्षिणामुखः
दक्षिणामुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Turning the face south wards.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण south, and मुख the face, with आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणायन|दक्षिणायनं
दक्षिणायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The sun's progress south of the equator, the winter solstice.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणारण्य
दक्षिणारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>The peninsula, the great southern forest.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणार्ह|दक्षिणार्हः
दक्षिणार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Meriting a reward.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण a present, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त्त|दक्षिणावर्त|दक्षिणावर्तः
दक्षिणावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A conch shell with the valve opening to the right.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and आवर्त्त a turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणावर्त्तकी|दक्षिणावर्तकी
दक्षिणावर्त्तकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A line of bees.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and आवर्त्तक turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशा
दक्षिणाशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The south.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and आशा quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणाशापति|दक्षिणाशापतिः
दक्षिणाशापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण south, आशा quarter, and पति master or regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणीय|दक्षिणीयः
दक्षिणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Meriting a reward.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण a present or reward, affix च्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेन
दक्षिणेन<BR>ind.<BR>Southward, southerly.<BR>E.<BR>the third case of दक्षिण, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिणेर्म्मन्|दक्षिणेर्मन्
दक्षिणेर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A deer struck by a hunter.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण the right side, and इर्म्म wound, comp. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दक्षिण्य|दक्षिण्यः
दक्षिण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Meriting a reward.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण a present, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध|दग्धं|दग्धः
दग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Burnt, scorched, consumed by fire.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>1 The quarter where the sun is observable.<BR>2 An epithet of certain lunations, on which it is unlucky to do any thing, and religious rites are prohibited.<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धकाक|दग्धकाकः
दग्धकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A raven, or perhaps the carrion crow.<BR>E.<BR>दग्ध burnt, (black,) and काक crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धव्य
दग्धव्य<BR>mfn. (व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be burnt.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धिका
दग्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Scorched rice.<BR>E.<BR>दग्ध burnt, कन् depreciative affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धेष्टका
दग्धेष्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A burnt or vitrified brick.<BR>E.<BR>दग्ध burnt, and इष्टक a brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्धोदर
दग्धोदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hungry, starving.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The appetite, an empty or craving stomach.<BR>E.<BR>दग्ध, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=395" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दग्ध्वा
दग्ध्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having burnt.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दघ
दघ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई) दधि (दंघति)<BR>1 To quit or abandon.<BR>2 To cherish or protect.<BR>r. 5th cl. (दध्नीति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>3 To protect: some consider this root peculiar to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड<BR>r. 10th cl. (दण्डयति)<BR>1 To punish, especially by fine.<BR>2 To fine, to amerce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड|दंड|दंडं|दंडः|दण्डः
दण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>A stick, a staff.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 Punishment, castigation, amercement, imprisonment or putting to death.<BR>2 A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>3 An army.<BR>4 A form of array, a line or column of troops.<BR>5 A long measure, a pole of four cubits.<BR>6 A churning stick.<BR>7 A corner, an angle.<BR>8 A horse.<BR>2 A companion or attendant of the sun.<BR>10 A stem or stick of a tree.<BR>11 Subduing, subjecting.<BR>12 Pride, arrogance.<BR>13 A measure of time, a Daṇḍa, (1/60)th part of the day and night, or twenty-four minutes.<BR>14 Standing upright or erect, being like a staff.<BR>15 A son of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, and ड Uṇādi aff. or दण्ड to punish, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डक|दंडक|दंडकः|दण्डकः
दण्डक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A sort of metre, the stanza of which exceeds twenty-seven syllables, and may extend to 200.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The peninsula of India, from between the Narmadā and Godāvarī rivers to the south, the whole of which, in the days of RĀMA, was a large forest.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff, &c. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डकारण्य
दण्डकारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>The peninsula, the peninsular forest: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>दण्डक, and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डग्रहण|दंडग्रहण
दण्डग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Becoming a mendicant or ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड the staff carried by the mendicant, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डघ्न
दण्डघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A fighter, one who commits personal violence.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, and घ्न who strikes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डजित
दण्डजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suppressed by punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डढक्का|दंडढक्का
दण्डढक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, and ढक्का a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डताम्री
दण्डताम्री<BR>f. (-स्री)<BR>A perforated copper vessel, of given capacity, placed in a vessel of water; when filled with water, it sinks, marking a certain portion of time.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड twenty-four minutes, and ताम्री (q. v.) a copper vessel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डदास|दंडदास|दण्डदासः
दण्डदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A slave, a bondsman, one who has become so as a punishment or for debt.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधर|दंडधर|दण्डधरः
दण्डधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Having a stick or staff.<BR>2 Having authority to punish.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA.<BR>2 A king.<BR>3 A potter.<BR>4 A mendicant carrying a staff.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड punishment, a stick, &c. and धर who holds or possesses; also दण्डधार m. (-रः) दण्डधारिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डधारण
दण्डधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Punishment.<BR>2 Carrying a staff.<BR>3 Following the order of a mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and धारण having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डन|दंडन|दंडनं
दण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Punishing, inflicting punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड to tame, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनायक|दंडनायक|दण्डनायकः
दण्डनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A general, a commander-in-chief.<BR>2 A magistrate, a head police officer.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a column of troops, and नायक a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीति|दंडनीति|दण्डनीतिः
दण्डनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Policy, the system of civil and military administration taught by CĀṆAKYA and others.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड (by) punishment or subjection, नी to get or obtain, and क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीय|दंडनीय
दण्डनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड to punish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डनीयत्व
दण्डनीयत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Demerit, desert of punishment.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to to the last; also with तल्, दण्डनीयता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपांशुल|दंडपांशुल|दण्डपांशुलः
दण्डपांशुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A porter, a warder or doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff, पा to cherish or bear, affix ड, दण्डपः again, अंशुल for अंशल strong, sturdy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाणि|दंडपाणि|दण्डपाणिः
दण्डपाणि<BR>m. (णिः)<BR>1 YAMA.<BR>2 A staffbearer.<BR>3 One of ŚIVA'S attendants worshipped at Benares.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and पाणि a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपातिन्
दण्डपातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Awarding, fining.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and पातिन् causing to alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपारुष्य|दंडपारुष्य|दण्डपारुष्यं
दण्डपारुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 Assault and battery, a title of jurisprudence.<BR>2 Infliction of cruel punishment, one of the seven vices of kings and rulers.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड punishment, पारुष्य severity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाल|दंडपाल|दण्डपालः
दण्डपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A doorkeeper, a porter.<BR>2 A small kind of fish, (Cyprinus danrica, HAM.) see अर्द्धसफर.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff, &c. and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपालक|दंडपालक|दण्डपालकः
दण्डपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of fish: see the preceding, which it is supposed to resemble.<BR>2 A doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>कन् implying likeness, or pleonastic added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डपाशिक|दण्डपाशिकः
दण्डपाशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hangman, an executioner.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and पाश a noose, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डप्रणयन
दण्डप्रणयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Inflicting punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and प्रणयन leading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डभीति
दण्डभीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fear of punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and भीति fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डभृत्|दंडभृत्
दण्डभृत्<BR>mfn. (भृत्)<BR>1 Having a staff or stick.<BR>2 Inflicting punishment.<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A potter.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड the stick or handle of his wheel, and भृत् who possesses or works with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डमानव|दण्डमानवः
दण्डमानव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 An ascetic, one who uses a staff.<BR>2 A leader.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and मानव a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयत्
दण्डयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Punishing, amercing, chastising.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड to punish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयात्रा|दंडयात्रा
दण्डयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Subjection or conquest of a region or quarter.<BR>2 A bridal procession.<BR>3 Procession, moving in state or with attendants.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड punishment, &c. and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयाम|दंडयाम|दण्डयामः
दण्डयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA.<BR>2 The saint AGASTYA.<BR>3 A day.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड punishment, &c. यम to refrain, in the causal form, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डयोग
दण्डयोग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Infliction of punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डलेश
दण्डलेश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A small fine.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवत्|दंडवत्|दण्डवन्त्
दण्डवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Prostrate, falling or lying prostrate.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a strick, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवत्|दंडवत्|दण्डवन्त्
दण्डवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a stick, carrying a staff.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवादिन्|दंडवादिन्
दण्डवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A doorkeeper or a warder.<BR>2 One who threatens another with punishment or castigation.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड castigation, and वद to speak, to threaten, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवालधि
दण्डवालधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, and वालधि a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डवासिन्|दंडवासिन्
दण्डवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 A doorkeeper, a warder, a chamberlain.<BR>2 The magistrate or the head of a village.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff or mace, or punishment, &c. वस to abide, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविकल्प|दण्डविकल्पः
दण्डविकल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>Appropriate punishment or sentence.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and विकल्प alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=396" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविधि|दंडविधि|दण्डविधिः
दण्डविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Criminal law, mode of punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविशेष
दण्डविशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Kind or degree of punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and विशेष sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डविष्कम्भ|दंडविष्कंभ|दण्डविष्कम्भः
दण्डविष्कम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A post or a stake, round which plays the string that works the churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, स्कम्भ to stop, with वि prefixed, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डहस्त|दंडहस्त|दण्डहस्तं|दण्डहस्तः
दण्डहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>1 A staff-bearer.<BR>2 A doorkeeper.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>A tree, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डाजिन|दंडाजिन|दण्डाजिनं
दण्डाजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Deceit, fraud, cheating, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डादण्डि|दंडादंडि
दण्डादण्डि<BR>ind.<BR>Single stick, cudgelling, fighting with sticks or staves.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, repeated, with आ inserted, and इच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डार|दंडार|दंडारः|दण्डारः
दण्डार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A carriage, a vehicle.<BR>2 A potter's wheel.<BR>3 A bow or any instrument for casting arrows or darts.<BR>4 An elephant in rut, a furious or intoxicated elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, ऋ to go, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डाहत|दंडाहत|दण्डाहतं
दण्डाहत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a churning stick, and आहत struck, churned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिक|दंडिक|दंडिकः|दण्डिकः
दण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A mace-bearer, &c. one carrying a stick or staff. A fish, (Cyprinus dankena, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिका|दंडिका
दण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of necklace.<BR>2 A string.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a measure, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डित|दंडित|दण्डितः
दण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Punished, chastised, sentenced, fined.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड to punish, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डिन्|दंडिन्
दण्डिन्<BR>mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि)<BR>Having a staff or stick.<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A doorkeeper, a warder, a porter, a staff or mace-bearer.<BR>2 A name of YAMA.<BR>3 A man of the fourth order or beggar.<BR>4 A mendicant carrying a staff.<BR>5 A mendicant of a particular order, derived from ŚAṂKARĀCĀRYA.<BR>6 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a staff, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्डोत्पला
दण्डोत्पला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A small shrub; also सहदेवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दण्ड्य|दंड्य|दण्ड्यः
दण्ड्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्ड्यः-ण्ड्या-ण्ड्यं)<BR>Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड punishment, and यत् affix implying fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्|दन्त्
दत्<BR>m. (दन्तः दन्तौ दन्तः)<BR>2nd case plu. (दतः) A tooth: see दन्त; the nasal is dropped after the 2nd case.<BR>E.<BR>दम to subdue, affix डत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त|दत्तं|दत्तः
दत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Given, presented, made over, assigned.<BR>2 Preserved, guarded, protected.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 The name of a king.<BR>2 A saint; also दत्तात्रेय.<BR>3 A common surname or title of a man of the Vaiśya or third tribe, at present common to the Kayeth class.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>A gift, a donation.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तक|दत्तकः
दत्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A son given: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तकपुत्त्र
दत्तकपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A son given away by his natural parents, to persons engaging to adopt him; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by the old Hindu law.<BR>E.<BR>दत्तक, and पुत्त्र a son; also simply दत्तक, and sometimes दत्त्रिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तवत्|दत्तवन्त्
दत्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Gave, was giving.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तशुल्का
दत्तशुल्का<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>A bride for whom a sum of money has been paid to her father.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and शुल्क dower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्मन्
दत्तात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Self-given.<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A youth or orphan, who gives himself to persons disposed to take the place of parents.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त given, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तात्रेय|दत्तात्रेयः
दत्तात्रेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sage, the son of ATRI given to him by three deities, BRAHMA, VIṢṆU, and ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and अत्रेय son of ATRI; also दत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादत्त
दत्तादत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given and received.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and आदत्त taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तादर
दत्तादर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Treated with respect.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तानपकर्म्मन्|दत्तानपकर्मन्
दत्तानपकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Nonresumption of gifts.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त a gift, अन for अ, neg. before अपकर्म्मन् resuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तापहृत
दत्तापहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Given and taken again.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and अपहृत taken back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ताप्रदानिक|दत्ताप्रदानिकं
दत्ताप्रदानिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Resumption of gifts; one of the eighteen titles of law.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and अप्रदानिक not giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तावधान
दत्तावधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Attentive.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and अवधान attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तासन
दत्तासन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having a seat given, requested to sit.<BR>E.<BR>दत्त, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्ति|दत्तिः
दत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्रिम
दत्त्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Given.<BR>2 Produced or effected by gifts.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A slave who is given by another.<BR>2 A son given by his parents.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, क्त्रिम aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्तेय|दत्तेयः
दत्तेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The deity INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दत्त्वा
दत्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having given.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद
दद<BR>r. 1st cl. (ददते)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To relinquish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददत्
ददत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Giving.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद
दद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who gives or bestows.<BR>E.<BR>दद to give, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददन|ददनं
ददन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift, giving, donation.<BR>E.<BR>दद to give, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददि
ददि<BR>mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि)<BR>Who or what gives or bestows.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददिवस्
ददिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-दुषी-वः)<BR>Giving, who or what gives.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृत्
ददृत्<BR>mfn. (-दृत्)<BR>Fearful, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to fear, क्विप् affix, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृशिवस्
ददृशिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-शुषी-वः)<BR>Seeing, looking.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, वसु affix, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ददृश्वस्
ददृश्वस्<BR>mfn. (-श्रान्-शुषी-श्वः)<BR>Seeing, looking.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रु|दद्रुः
दद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>Cutaneous and herpetick eruptions; also दद्रूः: or with कन् added दद्रुक, m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुघ्न|दद्रुघ्नः
दद्रुघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A kind of cassia, (C. tora.)<BR>E.<BR>दद्रु herpes, and घ्न, destroying, remedying; also दद्रूघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुण|दद्रुणः
दद्रुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Herpetick, afflicted with herpes.<BR>E.<BR>दद्रु, and न affix; also दद्रूण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रुरोगिन्
दद्रुरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Herpetick, diseased by herpes.<BR>E.<BR>दद्रु herpes, रोग a disease, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रू
दद्रू<BR>m. (-द्रूः)<BR>Herpetick eruptions: see दद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रूघ्न|दद्रूघ्नः
दद्रूघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>See दद्रुघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दद्रूण|दद्रूणः
दद्रूण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>See दद्रुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध
दध<BR>r. 1st cl. (दधते)<BR>1 To hold, to possess or retain.<BR>2 To give, to present, to assign or make over.<BR>(इ) दधि (दन्धति)<BR>To nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध
दध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Who has or possesses.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=397" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधत्
दधत्<BR>mfn. (-धन्-धती-धत्)<BR>Having, holding, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधान
दधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having, holding, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधि
दधि<BR>mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>Holding, having, who or what has or possesses.<BR>n. (-धि)<BR>1 Milk curdled or coagulated spontaneously by heat, or by the addition of buttermilk; it is an article of food of general use, and in high estimation amongst the Hindus, and is considered, medicinally, as the remedy or preventative of most disorders.<BR>2 Resin, turpentine; (all the synonyms are common to these two senses.)<BR>3 A house, an abode.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, किन् affix, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिकूर्च्चिका|दधिकूर्चिका
दधिकूर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A mixture of boiled and coagulated milk, or of water and sour curds.<BR>E.<BR>दधि as above, and कूर्च्चिका inspissated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिचार|दधिचारः
दधिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and चर to move, in the causal form, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिज|दधिजं
दधिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधित्थ|दधित्थः
दधित्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>The wood-apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, स्था to stand or be, affix ड; the root yielding a juice compared to curdled milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिधेनु|दधिधेनुः
दधिधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A quantity of curds given away at any sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिपुष्पिका
दधिपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flower, (Clitorea ternata.)<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and पुष्प a flower, कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिफल|दधिफलः
दधिफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The elephant or wood-apple; also दधित्थ.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and फल fruit, the fruit having the acid taste of Dahī or Dadhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिभाण्ड
दधिभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A vessel for holding curds, a pail.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिमण्ड|दधिमंड|दधिमण्डः
दधिमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Whey.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and मण्ड scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिमण्डोद|दधिमण्डोदः
दधिमण्डोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of curds, or rather of whey.<BR>E.<BR>दधिमण्ड, and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिशोण|दधिशोणः
दधिशोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and शोण crimson; of a colour composed of that of curdled milk and crimson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसक्तु
दधिसक्तु<BR>m. plu. always (-क्तवः)<BR>Barley meal mixed with curds.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and सक्तु the meal of barley, after frying and grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसर
दधिसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The skim of coagulated milk; also सर only.<BR>E.<BR>दधि Dahī, and सर which goes on or upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिसार|दधिसारं|दधिसारः
दधिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and सर essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिस्नेह|दधिस्नेहः
दधिस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Skim of Dahī, or curdled milk whey.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, and स्नेह oily substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधिस्वेद|दधिस्वेदः
दधिस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Buttermilk.<BR>E.<BR>दधि as above, and स्वेद exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच|दधीचः
दधीच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint, famous for having devoted himself to death, that the gods might be armed with his bones in lieu of thunderbolts; they being the only effective weapons against the demon VṚTRA; also दधीचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीचि|दधीचिः
दधीचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A Muni or saint: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधीच्यस्थि
दधीच्यस्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>1 The diamond.<BR>2 The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>दधीचि a saint, and अस्थि a bone; the bones of the saint were converted into thunderbolts, which are of the same substance with the diamond, according to the Hindus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दधृच्
दधृच्<BR>mfn. (-धृक्)<BR>Shameless, impudent.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be vain, affix क्विन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्न|दध्नः
दध्न<BR>m. (-ध्नः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, reiterated, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्याकर|दध्याकरः
दध्याकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sea of curds.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्यानी
दध्यानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>दधि curdled milk, नी with आङ् prefixed, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्याह्व
दध्याह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>The wood-apple.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and आह्वा name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्युत्तर|दध्युत्तरं
दध्युत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The skim of curdled milk, whey.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and उत्तर upper part; also with कन् added, दध्युत्तरक, n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दध्युद|दध्युदः
दध्युद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of curds.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and उद water; that which has curds for water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनु|दनुः
दनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A daughter of DAKṢA, wife of KAŚYAPA, and mother of the demons of Daityas, the Titans of Hindu mythology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुज|दनुजः
दनुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An Asura.<BR>E.<BR>दनु the mother of the giant race, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुजद्विष्
दनुजद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>A god, a deity.<BR>E.<BR>दनुज a demon, and द्धिष् the hater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुजारि
दनुजारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A god, a deity.<BR>E.<BR>दनुज, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दनुसूनु|दनुसूनुः
दनुसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>An Asura or infernal deity.<BR>E.<BR>दनु as above, and सूनु offspring; also similar compounds, as दनुज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त|दंत|दंतः|दन्तः
दन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 The peak of a mountain.<BR>3 The side or ridge of a mountain.<BR>4 An arbour.<BR>5 Ivory, elephant's tooth.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly known by the same name, Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>E.<BR>दम to subdue, तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तक|दंतक|दन्तकः
दन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crooked peak or projection in a rock or mountain.<BR>2 A bracket, a pin or shelf projecting from a wall.<BR>3 A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, added to दन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकर्षण|दंतकर्षण|दन्तकर्षणः
दन्तकर्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The common lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and कर्षण attracting, drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तकाष्ठ|दंतकाष्ठ|दन्तकाष्ठं
दन्तकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A piece of stick, or of the small branch of a tree used as a tooth brush.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तच्छद|दंतच्छद|दन्तच्छदः
दन्तच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and च्छद a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तजात|दंतजात
दन्तजात<BR>mfn.(-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Toothed, having teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तधावन|दंतधावन|दन्तधावनं|दन्तधावनः
दन्तधावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A tooth brush, or a fibrous stick used for cleaning the teeth.<BR>2 Cleaning the teeth.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A tree yielding an astringent resin, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>2 A plant, (Mimusops elengi): see वकुल.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and धाव to clean, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपत्र|दंतपत्र|दन्तपत्रं
दन्तपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An earring.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and पत्र a leaf or plate set with studs, resembling teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपत्रक|दंतपत्रक|दन्तपत्रकं
दन्तपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and पत्र a leaf: the petals or leaves of the flower resembling teeth in colour and shape; this comparison is frequent among the poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपवन|दंतपवन
दन्तपवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A dentifrice, or any thing taken to clean the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and पवन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपुप्पुटक|दन्तपुप्पुटकः
दन्तपुप्पुटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Gum boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=398" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तपुष्प|दंतपुष्प|दन्तपुष्पं
दन्तपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, the flower of which is compared to a tooth, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तफल|दन्तफलं|दन्तफलः
दन्तफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and फल a fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तभाग|दंतभाग|दन्तभागः
दन्तभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An elephant's front or forehead.<BR>2 Part of a tooth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त the tusk, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमल|दंतमल|दन्तमलं
दन्तमल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>The tartar of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमांस|दंतमांस
दन्तमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The gums.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and सांभ flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तमूलिका
दन्तमूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see दन्ती.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and मूल a root, कन् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवस्त्र|दंतवस्त्र|दन्तवस्त्रं
दन्तवस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and वस्त्र a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवासस्|दंतवासस्
दन्तवासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तव्यसन|दंतव्यसन
दन्तव्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fracture or decay of a tusk or tooth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and व्यसन misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तवेष्ट|दन्तवेष्टः
दन्तवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The gums.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and वेष्ट what incloses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशट|दन्तशटः
दन्तशट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A lime: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशठ|दंतशठ|दन्तशठः
दन्तशठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 Elephant or wood-apple: see कपित्थ.<BR>2 Common lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR>2 A plant bearing an acid fruit, (Averhoa carambola.)<BR>4 An orange.<BR>5 Sourness, acidity.<BR>f. (-ठा)<BR>Woodsorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and शठ noxious, bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशर्करा|दंतशर्करा
दन्तशर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Tartar of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त tooth, and शर्करा sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशाण|दंतशाण|दन्तशाणः
दन्तशाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A dentifrice, composed chiefly of the powdered fruit of the chebulic myrobalan, and green sulphate of iron.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and शाण a whetstone; sharpening or polishing the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशिरा
दन्तशिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The gum.<BR>E.<BR>दन्ता, and शिरा a long vein or tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तशुद्धि
दन्तशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Cleaning the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>द्रन्त, and शुद्धि cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तश्लिष्ट
दन्तश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Entangled in or between the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and श्लिष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तसक्त
दन्तसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Touched by the teeth; entangled in or between the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and सक्त in contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तहर्ष|दंतहर्ष|दन्तहर्षः
दन्तहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Tenderness of the teeth; intolerance of any rough, austere, or acid substances.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and हर्ष delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तहर्षक|दंतहर्षक|दन्तहर्षकः
दन्तहर्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and हर्षक delighting, from हृष to please, with वुन् affix; also with युच् affix दन्तहर्षण, m. (-णः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्ताघात|दंताघात|दन्ताघातः
दन्ताघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A bite.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and आघात a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तावल|दंतावल|दंतावलः|दन्तावलः
दन्तावल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, वलच् affix, and the final of दन्त made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तायुध|दंतायुध|दन्तायुधः
दन्तायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth or tusk, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तार्व्वुद
दन्तार्व्वुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A disease of the teeth or gums; gum boil, ulceration of the gums.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and अर्व्वुद a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तालिका|दंतालिका
दन्तालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A horse's bridle.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, अलि a line, affix कन्, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिका
दन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दन्ती; also read दन्तिजा, f. (-जा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिन्|दंतिन्
दन्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्ती-न्तिनी-न्ति)<BR>Toothed, tusked.<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, and इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तिमद|दन्तिमदः
दन्तिमद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The temporal juice of the elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दन्ति and मद the effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तीवीज|दन्तीवीजं
दन्तीवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A strongly purgative nut, the fruit of the croton.<BR>E.<BR>दन्ती, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तुर|दंतुर|दन्तुरः
दन्तुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Having a large or projecting tooth.<BR>2 Waving, undulatory.<BR>3 Rising (a hair), bristling.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, &c. affix उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तोद्भेद|दंतोद्भेद|दन्तोद्भेदः
दन्तोद्भेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Dentition.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and उद्भेद out-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्तोलूखलिक|दन्तोलूखलिकः
दन्तोलूखलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who eats grain without its having been threshed, an anchorite.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त a tooth, उलखल a mortar, and ठक् affix; who winnows with his teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्त्य|दंत्य|दन्त्यः
दन्त्य<BR>mfn. (-न्त्यः-न्त्या-न्त्यं)<BR>Dental, of or belonging to the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दन्त, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दश|दंदश|दंदशः|दन्दशः
दन्दश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>frequentative form of दश to bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्दशूक|दंदशूक|दन्दशूकः
दन्दशूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Mischievous, malignant, venomous.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A snake or serpent.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa, a demon or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>दश to bite, affix ऊक, the radical reiterated, and नुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रम
दन्द्रम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Going slowly or tortuously.<BR>E.<BR>द्रम to go, root redup. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दन्द्रमण
दन्द्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going slowly or tortuously.<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Who or what goes so.<BR>E.<BR>द्रम to go, root redup. युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ|दभः
दभ<BR>r. 10th cl. (दभयति) also दभि (दम्भयति)<BR>To order, to command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दभ्र|दभ्रं|दभ्रः
दभ्र<BR>mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं)<BR>Little, small.<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम<BR>r. 4th cl. (इर, उ) इरदमु (दम्यति)<BR>1 To tame or subject as an enemy, to quiet or pacify, to tranquillize.<BR>2 To be tamed or tranquillized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्
दम्<BR>ind.<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>दम to subject, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम|दमः
दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Punishing, chastisement, punishment.<BR>2 Taming, subduing.<BR>3 Self-command, endurance of the most painful austerities.<BR>4 Self-restraint, subduing the senses, suppressing the appetites, passions, &c.<BR>5 Mud, mire.<BR>6 (In the Vedas,) The hall of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame or subdue, affix अक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमक|दमकः
दमक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A tamer, a subduer.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमघोष|दमघोषः
दमघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A prince of the lunar race, king of Cedi, father of ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमघोषसुत|दमघोषसुतः
दमघोषसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of ŚIŚUPĀLA, a king and enemy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दमघोष a proper name, the father of ŚIŚUPĀLA, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथ|दमथः
दमथ<BR>mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>1 Punishment, punishing, chastising.<BR>2 Selfcontrol, endurance of rigorous austerities.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Taming, subduing.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame or subdue, Uṇādi affix अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमथु|दमथुः
दमथु<BR>mn. (-थुः)<BR>1 Punishment, restraint or subjection of others.<BR>2 Self-denial, subjection of oneself.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमन|दमनं|दमनः
दमन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A hero.<BR>2 A philosopher.<BR>3 A kind of flower, commonly Dona, (Artemisia.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Taming, subduing.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमनीय
दमनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be tamed, subjected, or subdued.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमयत्
दमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Taming, restraining, chastising.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 The wife of NALA.<BR>2 A kind of cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>दम to subdue, participial affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमस्वसृ
दमस्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>DAMAYANTĪ.<BR>E.<BR>द्रम, खसृ sister of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=399" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमित|दमितः
दमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tamed, subdued, patient of every suffering, exaction or privation.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, affix क्त, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमिन्
दमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>A tamer, a dominator.<BR>E.<BR>दम with धिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दमुनस्
दमुनस्<BR>m. (-नाः)<BR>1 A name of Agni or fire.<BR>2 A name of ŚUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame (all things), Uṇādi affix उनसि; also ऊनसि, whence दमुनस्, m. (-नाः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्पति|दंपति
दम्पति<BR>m. du. (-ती)<BR>Husband and wife.<BR>E.<BR>दम् a wife, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ<BR>r. 5th cl. (उ) दम्भु (दभ्नोति)<BR>1 To act deceitfully, to cheat, to impose upon, to trick or deceive.<BR>2 To split or divide.<BR>r. 10th cl. (दम्भयति)<BR>To collect, to gather, to arrange or string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भ|दंभ|दंभः|दम्भः
दम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Deceit, fraud, cheating.<BR>2 Hypocrisy.<BR>3 Sin, wickedness.<BR>4 Arrogance, pride.<BR>E.<BR>दम्भ to deceive, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भिन्|दंभिन्
दम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>1 Hypocritical.<BR>2 Proud.<BR>3 Wicked.<BR>m. (-म्भी)<BR>A hypocrite, an impostor.<BR>E.<BR>दम्भ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्भोलि|दंभोलि|दंभोलिः|दम्भोलिः
दम्भोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>दम्भ to divide or split, affix उलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दम्य|दम्यः
दम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>To be subjected or tamed.<BR>2 To be punished.<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>A steer, a young bullock.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, यत् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय|दयः
दय<BR>(ञि) त्रिदय r. 1st cl. (दयते)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To take.<BR>4 To protect.<BR>5 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दय|दयः
दय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Compassionate, tender-hearted.<BR>mf. (-यः-या)<BR>Tenderness, compassion, clemency.<BR>E.<BR>दय to preserve, affix अङ्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयमान
दयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Preserving, protecting.<BR>E.<BR>दय, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकर|दयाकरः
दयाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Kind, showing compassion.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकूर्च्च|दयाकूर्च|दयाकूर्चः
दयाकूर्च्च<BR>m. (-र्च्चः)<BR>A Buddha, a Bauddha saint, or a form of BUDDHA, the founder of the sect.<BR>E.<BR>दया compassion, and कूर्च्च boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाकृत्
दयाकृत्<BR>mfn. (-त्)<BR>Compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and कृत् doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयान्वित
दयान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compassionate, charitable, kind.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयायुक्त
दयायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Compassionate, benevolent.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाल
दयाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The breaking of a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालु|दयालुः
दयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Tender, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>दया compassion, आलुच् affix; also दयालुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयालुत्व
दयालुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Tenderness, compassionateness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; with तल् दलालुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयावत्|दयावन्त्
दयावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Merciful, tender.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयाशील
दयाशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Kind, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>दया, and शील possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयित|दयितं|दयितः
दयित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Beloved, dear, desired.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A lover.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A wife or mistress.<BR>E.<BR>दय to regard tenderly, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दयिताधीन
दयिताधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Hen-pecked, subject to a wife.<BR>E.<BR>दयिता a wife, and अधीन subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर|दरं|दरः
दर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 Fear, terror.<BR>2 A hole in the ground.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A conch shell.<BR>ind.<BR>A little.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>1 A natural or artificial excavation in a mountain, a cave, a cavern, a grotto, &c.<BR>2 A valley.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide, to dread, &c. affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरणि|दरणिः
दरणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>An eddy, a current.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear (down the banks), affix अणि; some bocks read दारणि, and others आरणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद्
दरद्<BR>f. (-त्)<BR>1 Terror.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A precipice.<BR>4 The heart.<BR>5 A bank or mound.<BR>6 A tribe of barbarians.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide or tear, अदि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरद|दरदं|दरदः
दरद<BR>mf. (-दः-दा)<BR>A country bordering on Kashmir, the mountains about Kashmir and above Peshawer.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Fear, terror.<BR>2 A tribe of barbarians.<BR>E.<BR>अच् added to the former.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरविदलित
दरविदलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Slightly or a little burst or opened.<BR>E.<BR>दर, and विदलित divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरि|दरिः
दरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>A cave: see दर.<BR>E.<BR>दृ to divide, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरित|दरितः
दरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Frightened, terrified.<BR>2 Torn, rent, divided.<BR>E.<BR>दर fear, इतच् affix; or दॄ to divide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्र|दरिद्रः
दरिद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Poor, needy, indigent, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्रा to be poor, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रता
दरिद्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Poverty, indigence.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्र, and तल् affix; also with त्व, दरिद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रा
दरिद्रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (दरिद्राति) 3rd plu. (दरिद्रति)<BR>To be poor or needy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रायक|दरिद्रायकः
दरिद्रायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Poor, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्रा, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रित|दरिद्रितः
दरिद्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Poor, impoverished.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्रा to be poor, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरिद्रितृ
दरिद्रितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Poor, needy.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्रा, and तृच् affix; otherwise with ण्वुल् affix दरिद्रायंक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरीभू
दरीभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A cavern, a hollow.<BR>E.<BR>दरी, and भू a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरीभृत्
दरीभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>दरी a cave, and भृत् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दरोदर|दरोदरं|दरोदरः
दरोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A gamester.<BR>2 A stake.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gambling: see टुरोदर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दर|दर्दरः|दर्द्दरः
दर्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cracked, flawed, slightly broken, (a vessel, &c.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear or break, affix अच्, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दराम्र|दर्दराम्रः|दर्द्दराम्रः
दर्दराम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>A sort of sauce or condiment; also मीनाम्रीण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दरीक|दर्दरीकः|दर्द्दरीकं|दर्द्दरीकः
दर्दरीक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A musical instrument.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A frog.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix रीकन्, and the radical reduplicate; what is struck, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुर|दर्दुरः|दर्द्दुर|दर्द्दुरं|दर्द्दुरः
दर्दुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A sort of musical instrument, a pipe or flute.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A number of villages.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix उरच्, and the radical repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दुरपुट|दर्दुरपुटः
दर्दुरपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The mouth or extremity of a pipe.<BR>E.<BR>दर्दुर, and पुट a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रु|दर्द्रुः
दर्द्रु<BR>m. (-र्द्रुः)<BR>Herpetick eruption: see दर्द्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्दू
दर्दू<BR>m. (-र्दूः)<BR>A cutaneous disease, herpes; also दर्द्रू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रू
दर्द्रू<BR>m. (-र्द्रूः)<BR>Cutaneous eruption, herpes.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्रा to be poor, ऊ Uṇādi affix, the form is irregular: by substituting the short vowel, and omitting the first र, this word and its compounds appear in a variety of forms, as दर्द्रु, दद्रु, दद्रू; also omitting the second र, दर्द, &c. &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रूघ्न
दर्द्रूघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Cassia, (tora); also दद्रघ्न, and दर्द्रूघ्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=400" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रूण|दर्द्रूणः
दर्द्रूण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Diseased with herpes, herpetick; also दर्द्रूण, दर्द्रूण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्द्रुरोगिन्
दर्द्रुरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Herpetick, afflicted with herpes; also दर्द्रूरोगिन्, दद्रुरोगिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्प|दर्पः
दर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Musk.<BR>3 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to be proud, to inflame, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पक|दर्पकः
दर्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What kindles, inflames, or excites.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to inflame, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पण|दर्पणं|दर्पणः
दर्पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A mirror.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Kindling, inflaming.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to excite, to shine, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पध्मात
दर्पध्मात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Puffed up or swelling with pride.<BR>E.<BR>दर्प, and ध्मात inflated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पह
दर्पह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Humbling, humiliating, pride-destroying.<BR>E.<BR>दपौ, and ह what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पारम्भ|दर्पारम्भः
दर्पारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Incipient pride, conceit.<BR>E.<BR>दर्प pride, आरम्भ commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्पोपशान्ति|दर्पोपशान्तिः
दर्पोपशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Conciliating or subduing arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>दर्प, and उपशान्ति allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्ब|दर्ब
दर्ब्ब<BR>m. (-र्ब्बः)<BR>1 A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>2 A mischievous man or animal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बट|दर्बट
दर्ब्बट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A constable, a police officer set over a village, &c.<BR>2 A warder, a doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बरीक
दर्ब्बरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बि|दर्बि
दर्ब्बि<BR>f. (-र्ब्बिः-र्ब्बी)<BR>1 A ladle or spoon.<BR>2 The expanded hood of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix बि; also with ङीप् added दर्ब्बी; some authorities make the final consonant the labial letter व, as दर्ब्बि, दर्ब्बी; also दार्ब्बी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बिक
दर्ब्बिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ladle, a spoon.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb: see दार्ब्बिका.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्ब्बीकर
दर्ब्बीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दर्ब्बी the hood expanded, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भ|दर्भः
दर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 Kuśa or sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>2 A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>3 Another species, (S. cylindricum.)<BR>E.<BR>दृभि to collect, to arrange, affix घञ्; or दॄ to tear, Uṇādi affix भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भट|दर्भटं
दर्भट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A private apartment or house, a retirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्भपत्र|दर्भपत्रः
दर्भपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>दर्भ, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्श|दर्शः
दर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 Day of new moon when it rises invisible.<BR>3 Half monthly sacrifice, performed at the change of the moon, by persons maintaining a perpetual fire.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शक|दर्शकः
दर्शक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what shows, displays, explains, makes clear, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>2 An exhibiter, one who points out or shows any thing.<BR>3 A skilful man, one conversant with any science or art, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शत|दर्शतः
दर्शत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शन|दर्शनं
दर्शन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>2 The eye.<BR>3 A mirror.<BR>4 Showing.<BR>5 Aspect, appearance.<BR>6 Directing, instructing.<BR>7 A dream, a vision.<BR>8 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>9 Knowledge, especially religious.<BR>10 Understanding, intellect.<BR>11 A Śāstra, one of six religious or philosophical systems, the Pātañjala, Sāṃkhya, Vaiśeṣika, Nyāya, Mīmāṃsā, and Vedānta.<BR>12 Sacrifice.<BR>13 Colour.<BR>14 Visiting any sacred shrine, worshipping in the presence of any image.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रतिभू
दर्शनप्रतिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A surety for appearance.<BR>E.<BR>दर्शन, and प्रतिभू a surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनप्रातिभाव्य
दर्शनप्रातिभाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Surety for appearance, bail.<BR>E.<BR>दर्शन, and प्रातिभाव्य surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीय|दर्शनीयः
दर्शनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome, agreeable.<BR>2 Visible, to be seen.<BR>E.<BR>दर्श looking, and छ affix; or दृश to see, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शनीयमानिन्
दर्शनीयमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Vain, conceited, thinking oneself handsome.<BR>E.<BR>दर्शनीय, मन to mind, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयामिनी
दर्शयामिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The night of new moon, on which it rises invisible.<BR>E.<BR>दर्श new moon, and यामिनी night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयितृ
दर्शयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Showing, displaying, who or what shows.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A warder, an usher, a doorkeeper.<BR>2 A show man, a guide, an exhibiter.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, in the causal form, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयित्वा
दर्शयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having shown, having made manifest.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, causal form, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शयिष्यत्
दर्शयिष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Showing, explaining or proposing to shew or explain.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, causal form, शतृ affix, with a future sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शविपद्
दर्शविपद्<BR>m. (-द्)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>दर्श day of new moon, and विपद् trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शित|दर्शितः
दर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Visible, apparent.<BR>2 Shown, displayed.<BR>3 Explained.<BR>4 Seen.<BR>5 Understood.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, in the causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दर्शितवत्|दर्शितवन्त्
दर्शितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having shown, showing, displaying.<BR>2 Explaining, teaching.<BR>E.<BR>दृश causal form, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल<BR>r. 1st cl. (दलति) r. 10th cl. (दालयति)<BR>1 To cut, to divide, to split or pierce.<BR>2 To be cut, &c.<BR>3 To display.<BR>4 To wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल|दलं|दलः
दल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A leaf.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A part, a portion, a fragment.<BR>2 Dividing, tearing, cutting, splitting, &c.<BR>3 A sheath, a scabbard.<BR>4 An adulteration or alloy.<BR>5 A heap or quantity.<BR>6 The leaf of the Tamāla.<BR>7 A half.<BR>E.<BR>दल to divide, to cut, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलकपाट|दलकपाटः
दलकपाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A folded petal or leaf.<BR>E.<BR>दल, and कपाट a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलकोष|दलकोषः
दलकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>E.<BR>दल, a leaf, and कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलत्
दलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Splitting, rending.<BR>2 Being torn or cut.<BR>E.<BR>दल to cut or be pierced, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलद्धृदय
दलद्धृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Broken-hearted, cut to the heart, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दलत्, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलन|दलनं
दलन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Breaking to pieces, cutting, dividing, (who or what does so.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tearing, rending, breaking, pulling to pieces.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A clod or clump of earth or mould.<BR>E.<BR>दल to divide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलनिर्म्मोक|दलनिर्मोक|दलनिर्मोकः|दलनिर्म्मोकः
दलनिर्म्मोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Bhojpatra, a tree of which the bark is used for hookah snakes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दल a leaf, and निर्म्भोक shedding, casting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलप|दलपः
दलप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A sacred or religious institute.<BR>E.<BR>दल to be divided, Uṇādi affix अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=401" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलपुष्पी
दलपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>दल a leaf, and पुष्प a flower; the leaves surrounding the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलसूचि|दलसूचिः
दलसूचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>दल a leaf, and सूचि a needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलस्नसा
दलस्नसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The fibre or vein of a leaf.<BR>E.<BR>दल a leaf, and स्नसा a fibre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाढक|दलाढकः
दलाढक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sesamum growing wild or spontaneously.<BR>2 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>3 A plant commonly Nagesara, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>4 A tree, (Mimosa sirisha^1.)<BR>5 Red chalk.<BR>6 Cuttle fish bone.<BR>7 A moat, a ditch.<BR>8 A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>9 An elephant's ear.<BR>10 The driver of an elephant.<BR>11 A hurricane, a high wind.<BR>E.<BR>दल as above, ढौकृ to go, with आङ् prefixed, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाद्य
दलाद्य<BR>m. (-ढ्यः)<BR>Mud, but mud especially on the banks of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलामल|दलामलं
दलामल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa): see मरुवक.<BR>2 A plant, (Artemisia.)<BR>E.<BR>दल a leaf, and अमल clear, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलाम्ल|दलाम्लं
दलाम्ल<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>दल the leaf, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलि|दलिः
दलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>A clod of clay or mould.<BR>E.<BR>दल to be divided, (by the harrow or plough,) Uṇādi affix इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलिक|दलिकं
दलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Timber, wood.<BR>E.<BR>दल to split, affix इकच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलित|दलितं
दलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blown, full blown, expanded.<BR>2 Broken, split.<BR>3 Cut to pieces.<BR>4 Torn, rent.<BR>5 Scattered, driven apart, divided.<BR>6 Opened, unfolded.<BR>E.<BR>दल to split, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दलेगन्धि|दलेगन्धिः
दलेगन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris): see सप्तपर्ण.<BR>E.<BR>दल in the seventh case दले, in the leaf, and गन्धि fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्भ|दल्भः
दल्भ<BR>m. (-ल्भः)<BR>1 Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>3 The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>4 A wheel.<BR>E.<BR>दल to divide, भ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दल्भि
दल्भि<BR>m. (-ल्भिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>2 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>दल to break or split, Uṇādi affix भि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव<BR>(इ) दवि r. 1st cl. (दन्वति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दव|दवः
दव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A wood on fire, a forest conflagration.<BR>2 A wood, a forest.<BR>3 Fire in general.<BR>4 Heat, (moral or physical.)<BR>E.<BR>दु to agitate, affix अच्; also दाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवथु|दवथुः
दवथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 Anxiety, vexation, distress.<BR>2 Inflammation of the eye, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दु to be agitated, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवयत्
दवयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत)<BR>Removing, making remote, placing at a distance.<BR>E.<BR>दव for दूर used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवाग्नि|दवाग्निः
दवाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A wood on fire, or the conflagration of a forest.<BR>E.<BR>दव a wood, and अग्नि a fire; also दव and दाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दविष्ठ|दविष्ठः
दविष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very remote, very distant.<BR>E.<BR>दूर् far, affix इष्ठन्, and दव substituted for दूर्; also दवीयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दवीयस्
दवीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very remote or distant: see the preceding, the affix being the superlative affix ईयसुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दश
दश<BR>(इ) दशि r. 1st and 10th cls. (दशति दंशयति)<BR>1 To bite or sting.<BR>2 To arm, to put on armour.<BR>3 To see.<BR>r. 10th cl. (दंशयते)<BR>To shine.<BR>With उप,<BR>to be in trouble, to be reduced in circumstances.<BR>With सम्,<BR>to pinch, to nip, to bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशक
दशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Ten.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकण्ठ|दशकंठ|दशकण्ठः
दशकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and कण्ठ a neck; the ten-necked; also similar names, as दशग्रीव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकण्ठजित्|दशकंठजित्
दशकण्ठजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दशकण्ठ RĀVAṆA, and जित् the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकन्धर|दशकंधर|दशकन्धरः
दशकन्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>RĀVAṆA: see दशकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशकामजव्यसन
दशकामजव्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The aggregate of ten vices, proceeding from the quality of desire, viz. hunting, gambling, sleeping during the day, abusiveness, lechery, drunkenness, dancing, singing, playing, and hypocrisy.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, काम desire, ज born, व्यसन calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशगुण
दशगुण<BR>adv. n. (-णं)<BR>Ten times, ten-fold.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and गुण a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्राम
दशग्राम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A district or collection of ten villages.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and ग्राम a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रामपति|दशग्रामपतिः
दशग्रामपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A magistrate or chief of ten villages.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and ग्राम a village, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रामिन्
दशग्रामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 The head man of ten villages.<BR>2 The municipality or corporation of the same.<BR>E.<BR>दशग्राम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशग्रीव|दशग्रीवः
दशग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>RĀVAṆA: see दशकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशति|दशतिः
दशति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशधा
दशधा<BR>ind.<BR>In ten ways.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन्
दशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Ten.<BR>E.<BR>दश to bite, Uṇādi affix अन्, the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशन|दशनं|दशनः
दशन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>A tooth.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The peak of a mountain.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>दंश to bite, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनवासस्
दशनवासस्<BR>n. (-मः)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>दशन a tooth, and वामस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनांशु|दशनांशुः
दशनांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The whiteness or brightness of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दशन, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनाङ्क|दशनांक|दशनाङ्कः
दशनाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A bite, the mark of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>दशन, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनाद्या
दशनाद्या<BR>f. (-ढ्या)<BR>A kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशनोच्छिष्ठ
दशनोच्छिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Toothless.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 Breathing, breathing out, expiration.<BR>2 A lip.<BR>3 Kissing, a kiss.<BR>E.<BR>दशन a tooth, and उच्छिष्ठ expelled, ejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपारमिताधर|दशपारमिताधरः
दशपारमिताधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>दश, पारमिता a particular work or scripture of this sect, धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुर|दशपुरं
दशपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus); see दाशपुर.<BR>2 A district, part of Malva or Bundelkhand.<BR>3 A town or city.<BR>E.<BR>दश for दाश a fisherman, and पुर or पूर to nourish, affix दश; also दश ten, and पुर a city: a district of ten cities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपूर
दशपूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass: see the preceding; also दाशपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशबल|दशबलः
दशबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha teacher.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, (the ten worlds,) बल powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशभूमिग|दशभूमिगः
दशभूमिग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect, or a Buddha, the generic name of the sanctified teachers of that sect.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, भूमि earth, and ग who goes; traversing the ten worlds; also दशभूमीश, m. (-शः) Lord of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशम|दशमः
दशम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Tenth.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 The tenth day of the half month.<BR>2 The tenth or last stage of human life, the last ten years of a century.<BR>E.<BR>दशन् ten, and मट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमहाविद्या
दशमहाविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, (forms, or names,) महा great, and विद्या a name of DURGA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमाल
दशमाल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>A collection of ten garlands.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, माला a garland, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमिन्
दशमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Very old or aged.<BR>E.<BR>दशमी the tenth, (stage of life,) and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीङ्गत|दशमींगत
दशमीङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very old, above ninety.<BR>E.<BR>दशमी, and गत arrived at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=402" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमीस्थ|दशमीस्थः
दशमीस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Impotent.<BR>2 Very old, turned of ninety.<BR>3 Dying, on the point of death.<BR>E.<BR>दशमी the last stage of life, and स्थ who is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुख|दशमुखः
दशमुख<BR>m. (खः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and मुख a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमुखान्तक|दशमुखान्तकः
दशमुखान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दशमुख RĀVAṆA, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशमूल|दशमूलं
दशमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A tonic medicament prepared from the roots of ten plants.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरथ|दशरथः
दशरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A proper name, sovereign of Ayodhya or Oude, and father of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and रथ a car; whose car bore him to the ten quarters of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरात्र|दशरात्रः
दशरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A period of ten days and nights.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशरूपभृत्
दशरूपभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, रूप forms, (Avatars,) and भृत् who assumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशलक्षण
दशलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ten marks or attributes.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशवाजिन्
दशवाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and वाजिन् a horse, whose car is drawn by ten horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशशत
दशशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A thousand.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशसहस्र
दशसहस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A myriad.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशा
दशा<BR>f. (-शा) or m. plu. (-शाः)<BR>1 The ends of a piece of cloth, the end of a garment.<BR>2 A state, a condition, a period or time of life, as youth, age, manhood, &c.<BR>3 The wick of a lamp.<BR>4 The mind or faculty, of understanding.<BR>5 Aspect or position of the planets at birth.<BR>E.<BR>दश to bite, to cut or divide, or be cut or divided, अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्ष|दशाकर्षः
दशाकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दशा a wick, आकर्ष what possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाकर्षिन्
दशाकर्षिन्<BR>m. (-र्षी)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दशा a wick, आङ् before, कृष to make lines, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानन|दशाननः
दशानन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The giant RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशानिक|दशानिकः
दशानिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाफल
दशाफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Result of circumstance or of condition of life.<BR>E.<BR>दशा, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ण|दशार्णः
दशार्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A country, part of central Hindustan, lying on the south-east of the Vindhya mountains.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A river rising in the Vindhya hills, the Dosarene of the ancients.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, ऋण a fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्थिति
दशास्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Condition.<BR>E.<BR>दशा, and स्थिति stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ह|दशार्हः
दशार्ह<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>1 A Buddha or Jina.<BR>2 A country in the south of India, the kingdom of YADU.<BR>m. plu. (-र्हाः)<BR>The Yādavas or people of Daśārha.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and अर्ह proper, worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशावतार|दशावतारः
दशावतार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and अवतार descent; the deity of whom there are ten descents from heaven, for the purpose of protecting or punishing mankind: see अवतार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाविशेष
दशाविशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Existing circumstances, peculiar condition.<BR>E.<BR>दशा, and विशेष sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाश्व|दशाश्वः
दशाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A name of CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and अश्व a horse; driving ten horses in his carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्य|दशास्यः
दशास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and आस्य face, the ten-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशास्यजित्
दशास्यजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दशास्य as above, and जित् the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशाह
दशाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A period of ten days.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेन्द्रिय
दशेन्द्रिय<BR>m. plu. (-याः)<BR>The ten organs of sense and action, viz. the skin, eye, tongue, nose, ear, organ of speech, hand, foot, anus, and pudendum.<BR>E.<BR>दश ten, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशिन्
दशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Having ten of any thing.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>The superintendent of ten villages.<BR>E.<BR>दश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेन्धन|दशेंधन|दशेन्धनः
दशेन्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दशा a wick, and इन्धन fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेर|दशेरः
दशेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mischievous or venomous animal, a beast of prey, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दश to bite, Uṇādi affix एरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशेरक|दशेरकः
दशेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A country destitute of water.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also दशेरुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दष्ट
दष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Bitten.<BR>2 Joining to, in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>दश to bite, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस
दस<BR>(इर्, उ) इरदसु r. 1st cl. (दस्यति)<BR>1 To lose.<BR>2 To throw or direct, to throw up or toss.<BR>r. 10th cl. (दसयते)<BR>To see.<BR>(इ) दसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (दंसति दंसयति)<BR>1 To bite or sing.<BR>2 To see.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दसन|दसनं
दसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Throwing, tossing.<BR>2 Dismissing.<BR>3 Perishing.<BR>E.<BR>दस to lose, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्त
दस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Lost, destroyed.<BR>2 Thrown, tossed.<BR>3 Sent away, dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>दस to lose, &c. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्म|दस्मः
दस्म<BR>m. (-स्मः)<BR>1 A name of fire.<BR>2 A sacrificer, one who employs Brahmans in instituting a religious ceremony.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 A rogue, a knave.<BR>E.<BR>दस to throw or send, मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्यु|दस्युः
दस्यु<BR>m. (-स्युः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>3 An oppressor, a violator, a committer of injustice, &c.<BR>4 A barbarian, an outcaste, or a Hindu who has become so by neglect of the essential rites.<BR>E.<BR>दस to lose or be lost, Uṇādi affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्युह
दस्युह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of BĀLĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्र|दस्रं|दस्रः
दस्र<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>1 Either of the twin sons of AŚVINI, and physicians of Svarga; also collectively m. du. (दस्रौ).<BR>2 An ass.<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>Thin rain, dew, frost.<BR>E.<BR>दस to destroy, (disease, &c.) रक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रदेवता
दस्रदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The lunar constellation AŚVINI.<BR>E.<BR>दस्र a divine physician, and देवता a deity: he being the ruling genius of the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दस्रसू
दस्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A name of SAṂJÑĀ, a wife of the sun, and mother, according to one legend, of the twin physicians of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>दस्र as above, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह
दह<BR>(औ) दहौ r. 1st cl. (दहति)<BR>To burn or reduce to ashes.<BR>(इ) दहि r. 10th cl. (दंहयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहत्
दहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Scorching, burning.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहन|दहनं|दहनः
दहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Burning, combustion.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Fire, or the deity AGNI.<BR>2 A bad man, one of evil dispositions.<BR>3 The marking nut plant.<BR>4 Lead wort, (Plumbago zeylanica, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनकेतन|दहनकेतनं|दहनकेतनः
दहनकेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>दहन fire, and केतन a banner or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनप्रिया
दहनप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of SVĀHĀ, the wife of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>दहन fire, and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनबहुल
दहनबहुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>दहन, and बहुल much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=403" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनाराति|दहनारातिः
दहनाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>दहन, and अराति foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनीय|दहनीयः
दहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be or what may be burnt, combustible.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहनोपल|दहनोपलः
दहनोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Sun-gem, a crystal lens.<BR>E.<BR>दहन fire, and उपल a stone; fire-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दहर|दहरं|दहरः
दहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Thin, small, fine.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A rat, a mouse.<BR>2 A young animal.<BR>3 A younger brother.<BR>4 A child, an infant.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, affix अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्यमान
दह्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Burnt, being burnt.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दह्र|दह्रः
दह्र<BR>m. (ह्रः)<BR>1 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>2 The conflagration of a forest.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दा
दा<BR>(ण) दाण r. 1st cl. (यच्छति, or with सम् prefixed संयच्छते); also (डु ञ्) डुदाञ् r. 3rd cl. (ददाति)<BR>To give, to present.<BR>With आङ् prefixed<BR>(आदत्ते),<BR>To take, to accept or receive.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To give, to give to.<BR>With वि and आङ्,<BR>To open.<BR>With सम and आङ्,<BR>To select.<BR>(प) दाप् r. 2nd cl. (दाति)<BR>To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक|दाकः
दाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A donor, one who makes presents, especially to Brahmans.<BR>2 A sacrificer, one who pays all the expenses of the ceremony, and employs the officiating priests.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षक|दाक्षकं
दाक्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of the descendants of DAKṢA.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायण|दाक्षायणः
दाक्षायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Of or relating to DAKṢA, a descendant, &c.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Gold, or a gold ornament, as an earring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and फञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायणिन्
दाक्षायणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Having gold.<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A Brahman student, wearing gold earrings.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षायण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणी
दाक्षायिणी<BR>f. plu. (-यिण्यः)<BR>The twenty-seven lunar mansions, considered mythologically as the daughters of DAKṢA, and wives of the moon.<BR>f. sing. (-णी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 The nymph and asterism ROHIṆĪ.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Dantī, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>4 A lunar asterism in general.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष the son of BRAHMA, so called, फिञ् affix of descent, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीप
दाक्षायिणीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 CANDRA.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षायिणी, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीपति
दाक्षायिणीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षायिणी an asterism, and पति husband: see the preceding; also similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षायिणीरमण
दाक्षायिणीरमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The moon: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षायिणी, and रमण lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षाय्य|दाक्षाय्यः
दाक्षाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A vulture.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षा to be quick, आय्य affix, and again, अण् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिकन्था
दाक्षिकन्था<BR>f. (-न्था)<BR>A place in the north of India, in the country of Vāhlika or Balkh: see कन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिकन्थीय
दाक्षिकन्थीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Produced or born, &c. in Dākṣikantha; see the last.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षिकन्थ, and छ affix; also similar compounds, as दाक्षिनगरीय, दाक्षिग्रामीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण
दाक्षिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the south, to a gift to Brahmans, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिणात्य|दाक्षिणात्यः
दाक्षिणात्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Southerly, southern, belonging to or produced in the south.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षिण southern, and त्यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षिण्य|दाक्षिण्यं
दाक्षिण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Meriting a reward.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Concord, harmony, agreement.<BR>2 Cleverness. talent.<BR>3 Appeasing or restoring any one offended to good humour.<BR>E.<BR>दक्षिणा a gift, &c. affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षीपुत्त्र
दाक्षीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>The inspired grammarian PĀṆINI.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षी a proper name, the mother of the saint, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्षेय|दाक्षेयः
दाक्षेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of PĀṆINI.<BR>E.<BR>दाक्षी the mother of the Muni, and ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाक्ष्य|दाक्ष्यं
दाक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Cleverness, dexterity, ability.<BR>E.<BR>दक्ष, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडक|दाडकः
दाडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tooth, a tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम|दाडिमः
दाडिम<BR>subst. mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>1 The pomegranate tree, (of mf. the tree, n. the fruit).<BR>2 Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>दल to divide, इमच् affix, the radical vowel made long, and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमपुष्पक|दाडिमपुष्पकः
दाडिमपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>E.<BR>दाडिम as above, पुष्य a flower, and कन् affix of resemblance; bearing flowers like those of the pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमप्रिय|दाडिमप्रियः
दाडिमप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>दाडिम the pomegranate, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिमभक्षण|दाडिमभक्षणः
दाडिमभक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>दाडिम a pomegranate, and भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाडिम्ब|दाडिंब|दाडिंबः|दाडिम्बः
दाडिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>The pomegranate: see दाडिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढा
दाढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>1 A large tooth, a tusk.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 A number, a multitude.<BR>E.<BR>दा to cut, ढ affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाढिका
दाढिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The beard.<BR>E.<BR>दाढा a tooth, and कन् affix, implying propinquity, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्ड|दांड
दाण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>1 Relating to a stick or staff.<BR>2 Relating to punishment, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दण्ड a stick, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डमाथिक
दाण्डमाथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Churning with a straight stick or staff.<BR>E.<BR>दण्डमाथ a churning stick, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाण्डाजिनिक|दांडाजिनिक|दाण्डाजिनिकः
दाण्डाजिनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>दण्डाजिन fraud, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात|दातं
दात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut, divided.<BR>E.<BR>दा to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातव्य
दातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be given, what may or ought to be given.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाति|दातिः
दाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Cutting, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>दा to cut, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दातृ
दातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>A donor, a giver, giving, bestowing.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यूह|दात्यूहः
दात्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A gallinule.<BR>2 The Cātaka, a sort of cuckoo.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>दाति destroying, ऊह to plan or arrange, affix अण्; also दात्यौह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्यौह|दात्यौहः
दात्यौह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Of, relating to, or produced in the vehicle of a demon. (E. दैत्य a demon. बह to bear, affix घञ्, अण् added, and the first vowel changed to आ by especial rule.)<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>see दात्यूह (the radical vowel being optionally changed,) with अण् affix^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्र|दात्रं
दात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A sort of sickle, a large knife or a Dā.<BR>E.<BR>दो to cut, त्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दात्व|दात्वः
दात्व<BR>m. (-त्वः)<BR>A giver, a donor.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, त्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाद|दादः
दाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A gift, a donation.<BR>2 Giving.<BR>E.<BR>दद to give, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादद|दाददः
दादद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A donor, one who gives.<BR>E.<BR>दाद, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दादिन्
दादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Giving.<BR>E.<BR>दद to give, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाधिक|दाधिकं
दाधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of or from Dadhi, or coagulated milk, mixed with it, sprinkled with it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दधि, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=404" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान<BR>(उ) दान r. 1st cl. irr. (दीदांसति-ते)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To straighten or make straight.<BR>3 To be straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान|दानं|दानः
दान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, giving, donation.<BR>2 The fluid that flows from the temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>3 Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>4 Purification.<BR>5 Cutting, dividing.<BR>6 A present, a special gift.<BR>7 Beating, striking.<BR>8 Wild honey.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, or दो to cut, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानकुल्या
दानकुल्या<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>The flow of an elephant's temporal ichor.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and कुल्या a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानधर्म्म|दानधर्म|दानधर्मः|दानधर्म्मः
दानधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Almsgiving, charity.<BR>2 The rules for making donations.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानपति|दानपतिः
दानपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A liberal or munificent man.<BR>2 A name of AKRŪRA, the kinsman of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दान giving, and पति eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानप्रतिभाव्य
दानप्रतिभाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Security for payment of a debt, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and प्रतिभाव्य surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानभिन्न
दानभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Divided or made hostile by bribes.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानयोग्य
दानयोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Fit for or meriting a donation.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and योग्य fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव|दानवः
दानव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A demon, a Titan or giant.<BR>E.<BR>दनु the mother of these beings, and अण् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवज्र|दानवज्रः
दानवज्र<BR>m. (-ज्रः)<BR>A Vaiśya or man of the third tribe.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and वज्र diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवर्षिन्
दानवर्षिन्<BR>m. (-र्षी)<BR>1 An elephant in rut.<BR>2 A liberal man.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and वर्षिन् showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवारि|दानवारिः
दानवारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>दानव a Titan, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानवीर|दानवीरः
दानवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A liberal man.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानव्यत्यास|दानव्यत्यासः
दानव्यत्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Gift under error, as giving to the wrong person, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and व्यत्यास perversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशील|दानशीलः
दानशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Liberal, munificent.<BR>E.<BR>दान giving, शील addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानशौण्ड|दानशौंड|दानशौण्डः
दानशौण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Liberal, bountiful, munificent.<BR>E.<BR>दान a gift, and शौण्ड intoxicated, attached to violently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानिन्
दानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Giving.<BR>E.<BR>दान, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानीय|दानीयः
दानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Worthy of having any thing given, or worthy or fit to be given.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, अनीयर् affix of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दानु|दानुः
दानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A donor, a giver.<BR>2 A victor, a conqueror.<BR>3 Prosperity.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, Uṇādi affix नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्त|दांत|दान्तः
दान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Tamed, subdued, daunted.<BR>2 Bearing patiently privation, austerity, &c.<BR>3 Dental.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A donor, a giver.<BR>2 A well situated about the peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, to pacify, affix क्त, or दन्त a peak, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दान्ति|दांति|दांतिः|दान्तिः
दान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 The patient endurance of religious austerities or privations.<BR>2 Subjection, humiliation.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापयित्वा
दापयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having fined.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, causal form, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापित|दापितः
दापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Condemned, adjudged, (the person.)<BR>2 Assigned, awarded, (the thing.)<BR>3 The person to whom a fine, &c. is awarded or paid.<BR>4 Given, caused to be given.<BR>5 Purified.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, in the causal form, and क्त affix; also दायित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाप्य
दाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be fined, to be made to give or pay.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, causal form, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाभ्य
दाभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>To be ordered, to be governed or ruled.<BR>E.<BR>दभ to order, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
दामन्<BR>nf. (-म-मा)<BR>A string, a cord, a thread or rope.<BR>E.<BR>दो to cut or divide, &c. affix मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन
दामन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating to the Dona or Artemisia flower.<BR>E.<BR>दामन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनपर्व्वन्|दामनपर्वन्
दामनपर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>The fourteenth of the light half of Chaitra, when the Dona flower is worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>दामन, and पर्व्व a holiday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनी
दामनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A string, a rope, especially for typing cattle.<BR>E.<BR>दामन् as above, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामलिप्त|दामलिप्तं
दामलिप्त<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>A country, the modern district of Tumlook.<BR>E.<BR>see तामलिप्त, त being changed to द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामा
दामा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A rope, a string, a cord.<BR>E.<BR>see दामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामाञ्जन|दामांजन
दामाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A foot-rope for horses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दामा, and अञ्ज to go, affix ल्युट्; also दामा, and अञ्चल end, दामाञ्चल, n. (-लं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामोदर|दामोदरः
दामोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A Jina of the past age.<BR>E.<BR>दाम a rope, and उदर a belly; YAŚODHĀ his foster mother having in vain passed the folds of a rope round his body, whilst a child, to keep him in confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाम्भिक|दांभिक|दाम्भिकः
दाम्भिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Hypocritical.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hypocrite.<BR>2 A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>दम्भ, and टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
दाय<BR>(ऋ) दायृ r. 1st cl. (दायते)<BR>To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाय|दायः
दाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 A special gift, as a nuptial present, alms to a student at his initiation, &c.<BR>3 Portion, inheritance.<BR>4 Loss, destruction.<BR>5 Breaking, dividing.<BR>6 A place, a site.<BR>7 Irony.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, in the passive form, affix ण; that which is given; or दो to cut, &c. that which is divided; or दाय to give, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायक|दायकः
दायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Liberal, giving, a donor.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायबन्धु|दायबंधु|दायबन्धुः
दायबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A brother.<BR>E.<BR>दाय portion, बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायभाग|दायभागः
दायभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Partition of heritage, apportioning inheritance, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दाय heritage, and भाग a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायविभाग|दायविभागः
दायविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Portioning or portion of inheritance, division of property amongst different heirs.<BR>E.<BR>दाय heritage, and धिभाग a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायाद|दायादः
दायाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A kinsman, near or remote.<BR>3 An heir.<BR>f. (-दा-दी)<BR>A daughter, an heiress.<BR>E.<BR>दाय a portion, आङ् prefixed to दा to take, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायादव
दायादव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An heir, a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायापवर्त्तन|दायापवर्तन
दायापवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Privation, a forfeiture of property.<BR>E.<BR>दाय, and अपवर्त्तन taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायित|दायितः
दायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Condemned, sentenced.<BR>2 Awarded, adjudged.<BR>3 The person to whom any thing is awarded, &c. see दापित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार|दारः
दार<BR>m. plu. (-राः)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to take, to tear, (a husband,) affix घञ्; also दारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारक|दारकः
दारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A breaker, a tearer.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A child, an infant or young animal.<BR>3 The charioteer of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A village hog.<BR>f. (-रिका)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 A whore.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=405" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारकर्म्मन्|दारकर्मन्
दारकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>दार a wife, and कर्म्मन् a business; also कारकिया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारण|दारणं
दारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The clearing nut plant, (Strychnos potatorum.)<BR>2 Tearing, rending, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारद|दारदः
दारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A sort of poison, one brought from the country named Darad.<BR>2 Quicksilver.<BR>3 Vermilion.<BR>4 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>दारदृ a country, &c. affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारपरिग्रह|दारपरिग्रहः
दारपरिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>दार, and परिग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारव
दारव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Wooden, made of wood.<BR>E.<BR>दारु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारवलिभुज्
दारवलिभुज्<BR>m. (भुक्)<BR>1 The Vaka, a sort of crane.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>2 A sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>दार a wife or female, वलि food, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारसङ्ग्रह|दारसंग्रह|दारसंग्रहः
दारसङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marrying, marriage.<BR>E.<BR>दार, and सङ्ग्नह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारा
दारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A wife: see दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाराधीन
दाराधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dependant upon a wife, subject to her, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दार, and अधीन subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारि|दारिः
दारि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>Cutting, tearing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिकादान
दारिकादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving a daughter in marriage.<BR>E.<BR>दारिका, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारित|दारितः
दारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Torn, divided.<BR>E.<BR>तॄ to tear or divide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र|दारिद्रं
दारिद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>Poverty.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र्य|दारिद्र्यं
दारिद्र्य<BR>n. (-द्र्यं)<BR>Poverty, indigence.<BR>E.<BR>दरिद्र poor, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिन्
दारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A polygamist.<BR>E.<BR>दार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
दारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-र्व्वी-रु)<BR>1 Liberal, munificent, a giver, a donor.<BR>2 An artist.<BR>3 Tearing, rending, a tearer.<BR>mn. (-रः-रु)<BR>Wood, timber.<BR>n. (-रु)<BR>1 A sort of pine, (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>2 Brass.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear or split, Uṇādi affix ञुण्, or दा to give, and रु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुक|दारुकं|दारुकः
दारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A proper name, the charioteer of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear (his foes), affix उकञ्.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pine, (Pinus devadaru).<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुकदली
दारुकदली<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A wild uneatable plantain.<BR>E.<BR>दारु, and कदली a plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुगर्भा
दारुगर्भा<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>A doll, a wooden puppet.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, गर्भ place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुज|दारुजः
दारुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Made of wood, wooden, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of drum.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Horrible, terrific^1, frightful, fearful.<BR>2 Dreadful, shocking.<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>Horror, horribleness.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Lead wort, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear to pieces, Uṇādi affix उनन्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुनिशा
दारुनिशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and निशा turmerick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुपुत्त्रिका
दारुपुत्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wooden doll or puppet.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and पु, त्त्रका an infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुमय
दारुमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of wood, woody, wooden.<BR>E.<BR>दारु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुवह
दारुवह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>What bears or carries timber.<BR>E.<BR>दारु, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुस्त्री
दारुस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A doll.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुहरिद्रा
दारुहरिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A kind of curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and हरिद्रा turmerick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुहस्तक|दारुहस्तकः
दारुहस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wooden ladle.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, हस्त hand, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारोपसङ्ग्रह|दारोपसंग्रह|दारोपसंग्रहः
दारोपसङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marrying, taking a wife.<BR>E.<BR>दार, and उपसङ्ग्नह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्घसत्र|दार्घसत्रः
दार्घसत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Performing a long continued sacrifice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घसत्र a particular sacrifice, अण् affix of relation, and the vowel changed to आ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ढ्य|दार्ढ्यं
दार्ढ्य<BR>n. (-र्ढ्यं)<BR>Hardness, fixedness, stability.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ hard, firm, ष्यञ् affix of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्द्दुर|दार्दुर|दार्दुरं|दार्दुरः|दार्द्दुरं
दार्द्दुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Relating to a cloud, a fog, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A conch, the valve of which opens to the right.<BR>2 Lac.<BR>3 Water.<BR>E.<BR>दर्द्दुर a mountain, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वट|दार्वट|दार्वटं|दार्व्वटं
दार्व्वट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A court or council-house.<BR>E.<BR>दारु timber, and अट to go or be, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वण्ड|दार्वण्ड|दार्वंड|दार्वण्डः|दार्व्वण्डः
दार्व्वण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, and अण्ड an egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वाघाट|दार्वाघाट|दार्वाघाटः|दार्व्वाघाटः
दार्व्वाघाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The woodpecker.<BR>E.<BR>दारु wood, हन to injure, with आङ् prefixed, and अण् affix, घ is substituted for ह, and ट for न in place of त; also with त, दार्व्वाघात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वाघात|दार्वाघात|दार्व्वाघातः
दार्व्वाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The woodpecker: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्विका|दार्विका
दार्व्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of collyrium prepared from an infusion of the Curcuma zanthorrhizon.<BR>2 A sort of potherb: see गोजिह्वा.<BR>E.<BR>दार्व्वी as below, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्विपत्रिका|दार्विपत्रिका
दार्व्विपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Gojihwa, a sort of wild potherb.<BR>E.<BR>दार्व्वी Curcuma, पत्र a leaf, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व्वी|दार्वी
दार्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>1 A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>2 A kind of pine: see देवदारु.<BR>3 Turmerick.<BR>4 Gojihwa, a potherb.<BR>5 A collyrium extracted from an infusion of the Curcuma zanthorrhizon.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear or dissipate (disease), ञुण् affix, fem. affix ङीष्: see दारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्षद|दार्षदः
दार्षद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>1 Ground on a flat stone, (meal, &c.)<BR>2 Stony, of stone, mineral.<BR>E.<BR>दृषद् a stone or slab on which condiments are prepared, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल|दालं|दालः
दाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Wild or unprepared honey.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of grain, (Paspalum frumentaceum.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Colocynth.<BR>E.<BR>दल a sheath, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालन|दालनं
दालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Toothache.<BR>E.<BR>दल to tear, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालब
दालब<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>दल to tear, in the causal form, अच् affix, and ब added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दालिम|दालिमः
दालिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The pomegranate: see दाडिम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाल्मि|दाल्मिः
दाल्मि<BR>m. (-ल्मिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>दल to tear or split, (mountains,) मिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाव|दावः
दाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A forest.<BR>2 A forest on fire.<BR>3 Fire in general.<BR>4 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>टु to go or run, affix अण्: see दव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावाग्नि|दावाग्निः
दावाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>The conflagration of a forest.<BR>E.<BR>दाव a forest, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दावानल|दावानलः
दावानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Fire in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>दाव, and अनल fire: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाविक|दाविकः
दाविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging, relating to, or produced in or near the river Devika or Deva.<BR>E.<BR>देविका the Deva, अण् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश<BR>(ऋ) दाशृ r. 1st cl. (दाशति-ते) 10th cl. (दाशयते)<BR>To give.<BR>5th cl. (दाश्नोति)<BR>To hurt, to injure or kill: see दास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=406" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश|दाशः
दाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A fisherman, the son of a Niṣada by a woman of the Ayogava caste.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A female slave, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दाशृ to give, affix अच्: see दास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशनन्दिनी|दाशनंदिनी
दाशनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA: see दासनन्दिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशपुर|दाशपुरं
दाशपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus): see दशपुर; also दाशपूर, n. (-रं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशरथ|दाशरथः
दाशरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दशरथ the father of RĀMA, and अण् patronymic affix; also with इञ् affix दाशरथि, m. (-थिः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशार्ह|दाशार्हः
दाशार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्ही-र्हं)<BR>Produced in Daśārha, (the country.)<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दशार्ह a country or one of KṚṢṆA'S ancestors, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेय|दाशेयः
दाशेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A servant.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA: see दासेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेर|दाशेरः
दाशेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A servant.<BR>2 A camel: see दासेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाशेरक|दाशेरकः
दाशेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Mālva, the province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्व|दाश्वः
दाश्व<BR>mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं)<BR>Liberal, giving, a donor, a giver.<BR>E.<BR>दाश to give, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाश्वत्
दाश्वत्<BR>mfn. (-श्वन्-श्वती-श्वत्)<BR>Liberal, munificent.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, श्वत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास<BR>(ऋ) दासृ r. 1st cl. (दासति-ते)<BR>To give;<BR>also दाश r. 5th cl. (दास्नोति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill: this and दाश, in the last sense, are restricted by some authorities to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास|दासः
दास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A fisherman.<BR>2 A servant, a slave.<BR>3 A Śūdra or man of the fourth tribe.<BR>4 A Śūdra affix or appellation.<BR>5 A person to whom it is proper to make gifts.<BR>6 A sage, one to whom the proper nature of the soul is known.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 A female servant or slave.<BR>2 The wife of a slave, a fisherman or Śūdra.<BR>3 A harlot.<BR>4 A plant, a sort of Barleria.<BR>E.<BR>दास to give, affix घञ्, to whom wages, &c. are given; also दाश; otherwise, दश or दंश to bite, &c. Uṇādi affix, टन्, and the short vowel and nasal changed to आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासत्व
दासत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Slavery, servitude.<BR>E.<BR>दास, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix, दासता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासनन्दिनी
दासनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of SATYAVATĪ, the mother of the poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>दास a fisherman, and नन्दिनी daughter; also दाशनन्दिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासदासी
दासदासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The female slave of a slave.<BR>E.<BR>दास, and दास the female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासपूर|दासपूरं
दासपूर<BR>m. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>दास a fisherman, and पूर what nourishes, from पृ to nourish, affix क; also दाशपूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासिका
दासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female servant or slave.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दामी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासित
दासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thrown, lost.<BR>2 Lost, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>दस to toss, affix क्त, इट् inserted, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीपुत्त्र
दासीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 The son of a slave.<BR>2 A bastard.<BR>E.<BR>दासी a female slave, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासीसभ|दासीसभं
दासीसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A multitude of female slaves.<BR>E.<BR>दासी a female slave, and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेय|दासेयः
दासेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Born of a slave, &c.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A servant or slave.<BR>2 A fisherman.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>दास as above, affix ढक्; also दाशेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेर|दासेरः
दासेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Born or sprung from a servant or slave.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A servant.<BR>2 A fisherman.<BR>3 A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दास as above, and द्रक् affix; also दाशेर, or with कन् added दासेरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्य|दास्यं
दास्य<BR>n. (-स्य)<BR>Slavery, servitude.<BR>E.<BR>दास a slave, affix ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह|दाहः
दाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Burning, combustion.<BR>2 Morbid heat.<BR>3 Actual or potential cautery.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहक|दाहकः
दाहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Burning, inflammatory.<BR>2 Cauterising, caustic.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहज्वर|दाहज्वरः
दाहज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Inflammatory fever.<BR>E.<BR>दाह, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहन|दाहनं
दाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Burning, reducing to ashes.<BR>2 Cauterising.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहवत्|दाहवन्त्
दाहवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Burning, heated, on fire.<BR>E.<BR>दाह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहसर|दाहसरः
दाहसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A place where dead bodies are burnt.<BR>E.<BR>दाह, and सृ to go or be, affix अप्; also with असुन् affix दाहसरस, n. (रः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाहहरण|दाहहरणं
दाहहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum).<BR>E.<BR>दाह heat, and हरण removing; this root being woven into screens, and kept wet, for the purpose of excluding or tempering the hot winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दाह्य
दाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be burnt, inflammable.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्क|दिक्कः
दिक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A young elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दिक् an imitative sound, and क who utters, some books have धिक्क, and others विक्क in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्कर|दिक्करः
दिक्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Young, juvenile.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>दिक् inflection of दिश place, कर who makes; who is restlessly active, changing place continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पति|दिक्पतिः
दिक्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A regent of a quarter of the universe, as the Sun of the east; Saturn of the west; Mars of the south; Mercury of the north; Venus of the south-east; Rāhu of the south-west; Candra of the north-west; and Jupiter of the north-east.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and पति master: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्पाल|दिक्पालः
दिक्पाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A regent of a quarter of the universe, as INDRA of the east; AGNI of the south-east; YAMA of the south; NAIRṚTA of the south-west; VARUṆA of the west; MARUT of the north-west; KUVERA of the north; ĪŚĀNA of the south-east.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and पाल who protects: this word is applicable to the Dikpatis, (see the last,) as that term is to these also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिक्शूल|दिक्शूलं
दिक्शूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An inauspicious planetary conjunction, as for the Sun and Venus to be in the west, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and शूल a spear or stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्त|दिगंत|दिगन्तः
दिगन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The horizon.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तर|दिगंतर
दिगन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Space, the atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्, and अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगन्तराल
दिगन्तराल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The sky, the atmosphere, space.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्, and अन्तराल interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिगम्बर|दिगंबर|दिगम्बरः
दिगम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Naked, unclad, unclothed.<BR>2 Dressed in, or enveloped by the atmosphere, clouds, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A Bauddha mendicant, wearing coloured clothes, or going naked.<BR>2 Any mendicant not wearing clothes.<BR>3 Darkness.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA, (from his being naked.)<BR>5 A Jain of one great division, which represents the images of their saints, either naked or plainly attired.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A name of DURGĀ. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">Page408</a>]<BR>E.<BR>दिक् inflection of दिश् space, अम्बर vestment; whose only garment is the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=407" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्गज|दिग्गजः
दिग्गज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An elephant of a quarter or point of the compass, one of eight attached to the north, north-east, &c. supporting the globe.<BR>E.<BR>दिश् a quarter, गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्दाह|दिग्दाहः
दिग्दाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Preternatural redness of the horizon, as if on fire.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्ध|दिग्धः
दिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Smeared, anointed.<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>1 A poisoned arrow.<BR>2 A name of fire.<BR>3 Oil, unguent, oily substance.<BR>4 A tale, true or false.<BR>E.<BR>दिह to smear or anoint, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्वासस्
दिग्वासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Naked.<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>दिक् for दिश् space, and बासस् vesture: see दिगम्बर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजय|दिग्विजयः
दिग्विजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Subjugation of an extensive country, either in arms or controversy.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and विजय triumph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विजयक्रम
दिग्विजयक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Invesion, going forth to conquer the world.<BR>E.<BR>द्विग्विजय, and क्रम march.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभाग
दिग्विभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A quarter or point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्, and विभाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्विभावित
दिग्विभावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Famous, celebrated, known in all quarters.<BR>E.<BR>दिक, and विभावित made known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिग्व्यापिन्
दिग्व्यापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Spreading through all space.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्, and व्यापिन् what pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्क|दिङ्कः
दिङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A nit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मण्डल|दिङ्मंडल
दिङ्मण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The circle of the heaven, or any point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>दिश, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्मुख
दिङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Looking to, or facing any point or quarter.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Any part of the heavens.<BR>E.<BR>दिश्, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिङ्नाग|दिङ्नागः
दिङ्नाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An elephant of the quarter: see दिग्गज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित|दितं
दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cut, torn, divided.<BR>E.<BR>दो to cut, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिति|दितिः
दिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 One of the wives of KAŚYAPA, and mother of the Daityas or infernal race, opposed to the gods.<BR>2 Cutting, splitting, dividing.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>दो to cut, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिज|दितिजः
दितिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An Asura, a sort of Titan or giant.<BR>E.<BR>दिति as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दितिसुत|दितिसुतः
दितिसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Titan or giant.<BR>E.<BR>दिति as above, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्य|दित्यः
दित्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A Titan, a demon or giant.<BR>E.<BR>दिति as above, अण् affix; and the vowel unchanged: see दौत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सा
दित्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Desire or purpose to give.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दित्सु
दित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing to give.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, desid. form, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षमाण
दिदृक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Wishing to see.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, desid. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षा
दिदृक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Desire or wish to see.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, desid. form, अङ् and टाप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षु
दिदृक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Desirous of seeing.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदृक्षावत्
दिदृक्षावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wishing to see.<BR>E.<BR>दिदृक्षा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिदेविषत्
दिदेविषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Wishing to play or sport.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्युत्
दिद्युत्<BR>mfn. (-द्युत्)<BR>Shining, blazing, bright.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु to shine, शतृ affix, intens. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिद्योतिषु
दिद्योतिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to shine.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु to shine, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षमाण
दिधक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Wishing to burn.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधक्षयत्
दिधक्षयत्<BR>mfn. (यन्-यन्त्री-यत्)<BR>Desiring to burn.<BR>E.<BR>दह to burn, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधि|दिधिः
दिधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Firmness, stability, fixed state of mind or being.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, affix कि, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषाय्य|दिधिषाय्यः
दिधिषाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A pretended friend, an intimate.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, Uṇādi affix आय्य, the root reduplicated, इट् and षुक augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषु|दिधिषुः
दिधिषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>The second husband of a woman twice married.<BR>f. (-षुः)<BR>A virgin widow remarried.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have (sin), or धिष to be reproached, root reduplicate, affix कु or कू; in the first case, इट् and षुक augments; also दिधिषू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषू
दिधिषू<BR>f. (-षूः)<BR>1 A virgin widow remarried: see the preceding; also दिधीषू.<BR>2 An elder sister unmarried, whose junior is a bride.<BR>m. (-षूः)<BR>1 The husband of a woman married a second time: see दिधीषु.<BR>2 Instability, want of firmness.<BR>E.<BR>दिधि firmness, षो to abandon, कू Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिधिषूपति|दिधिषूपतिः
दिधिषूपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The husband of a woman remarried.<BR>E.<BR>दिधिषू as above, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिन|दिनं|दिनः
दिन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>A day.<BR>E.<BR>दी to waste, नक् affix, and the vowel made short; or दो to destroy, (darkness,) किनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकर|दिनकरः
दिनकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकरात्मजा
दिनकरात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The Yamunā or Jumna river.<BR>E.<BR>दिनकर the sun, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकृत्
दिनकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिन, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनकेशव|दिनकेशवः
दिनकेशव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and केशब hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनज्योतिस्
दिनज्योतिस्<BR>n. (-तिः)<BR>Sunshine, day-light.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनदुःखित|दिनदुःखितः
दिनदुःखित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and दुःखित pained; regretting throughout the day, the approaching nocturnal separation from its female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनप्रणी
दिनप्रणी<BR>m. (-णीः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and प्रणी leading, bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनबल|दिनबलः
दिनबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of certain signs of the zodiac, the fifth to the eighth; also the eleventh and twelfth.<BR>E.<BR>दिन, and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनमणि|दिनमणिः
दिनमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and मणि jewel or gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनमूर्द्धन्
दिनमूर्द्धन्<BR>m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and मूर्द्धन् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनांश|दिनांशः
दिनांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A portion of the day, a watch, an hour, or the three seasons of dawn, noon, and evening.<BR>E.<BR>दिन, and अंश part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनादि|दिनादिः
दिनादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>दिन, and आदि commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनान्त|दिनांत|दिनान्तः
दिनान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Evening, sun-set, close of day.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनान्तक|दिनान्तकः
दिनान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and अन्तक ender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनारम्भ|दिनारंभ|दिनारम्भः
दिनारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Morning.<BR>E.<BR>दिन, and आरम्भ beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=408" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनावसान|दिनावसानं
दिनावसान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Evening, close of day.<BR>E.<BR>दिन day, and अवसान expiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिनिका
दिनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A day's wages, hire for a day or by the day.<BR>E.<BR>दिन a day, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिभ
दिभ<BR>(इ) दिभि r. 10th cl. (दिम्भयति)<BR>To order, to direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्प
दिम्प<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (दिम्पति-ते दिम्पयति-ते)<BR>To order, to command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिम्भ
दिम्भ<BR>r. 10th cl. (दिम्भति)<BR>1 To command, to direct.<BR>2 To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीप|दिलीपः
दिलीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The name of a king and ancestor^1 of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दिली said to be the barbarous name of Hastināpura or the modern Dehli, and प who protects or rules.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीपराज्
दिलीपराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>King DILĪPA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>दिलीप as above, and राज् a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिलीर|दिलीरं
दिलीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव|दिवं
दिव<BR>(उ) दिवु r. 4th cl. (दीव्यति)<BR>1 To play, to sport, to play with, to romp or gambol.<BR>2 To desire, to overcome, to be ambitious of surpassing, &c.<BR>3 To deal, to traffic, to buy or sell.<BR>4 To shine, to be splendid or beautiful.<BR>5 To praise.<BR>9 To be glad, to rejoice.<BR>7 To be mad, to be wild or inflated with pride, passion, &c.<BR>8 To be sleepy or sluggish.<BR>9 To love, to desire.<BR>10 To go.<BR>r. 10th cl. (देवयति)<BR>1 To suffer pain.<BR>2 To ask, to beseech or beg.<BR>3 To move, to go.<BR>(-ति ते)<BR>To lament, to wail, to mourn audibly.<BR>(इ) दिवि r. 1st cl. (दित्वति)<BR>1 To please.<BR>2 To be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्
दिव्<BR>f. (-द्यौः-दिवौ-दिवः)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 Air, sky.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, affix क्विष्, where sport immortals; also दिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव|दिवं
दिव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 Heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR>3 A day.<BR>4 A wood, a thicket.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, to shine, &c. affix कः see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवन्
दिवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>A day.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, Uṇādi affix अन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस|दिवसः
दिवस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>A day.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, कसच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसकर|दिवसकरः
दिवसकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिवस day, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसमुख|दिवसमुखं
दिवसमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>दिवस day, and मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसात्यय
दिवसात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Evening, close of day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवस, and अत्यय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवसावसान
दिवसावसान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Evening, close of day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवस, and अवसान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस्पति|दिवस्पतिः
दिवस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA, the Indian JOVE.<BR>E.<BR>दिवः of day, and पति lord, Divespiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवस्पृथिवी
दिवस्पृथिवी<BR>f. du. (-व्यौ)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>दिव heaven, and पृथिवी earth, स inserted for the sake of euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवा
दिवा<BR>ind.<BR>By day, the day.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, &c. affix का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकर|दिवाकरः
दिवाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 A flower, the sun-flower.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा the day, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकीर्त्ति|दिवाकीर्ति|दिवाकीर्तिः|दिवाकीर्त्तिः
दिवाकीर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 A man of a low or impure caste, a Caṇḍāla.<BR>2 A barber.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा by day, and कीर्त्ति credit, (the barber is not allowed to operate at night,) or दिवा day, अकीर्त्ति disrepute; the Caṇḍāla and owl coming abroad only in the dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाकृत
दिवाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done by day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाचर|दिवाचरः
दिवाचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going about by day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and चर who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाटन|दिवाटनः
दिवाटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा by day, अट to go, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवातन|दिवातनः
दिवातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Daily, diurnal, of or belonging to the day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा by day, ट्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवानिश
दिवानिश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Day and night.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवान्ध|दिवांध|दिवान्धः
दिवान्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Being blind by day.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा by day, and अन्ध dark or blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीत|दिवाभीतः
दिवाभीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An owl.<BR>2 A thief or house-breaker.<BR>3 The white lotus, (कुमुदाकर); perhaps any such flower, the petals of which open at night, and close in the day time.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा day, and भीत afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवाभीति|दिवाभीतिः
दिवाभीति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा by day, and भीति fear: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामणि|दिवामणिः
दिवामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवामध्य|दिवामध्यं
दिवामध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>Mid-day, noon.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and मध्य middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवारात्र
दिवारात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A day and night.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवारात्रि
दिवारात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः)<BR>1 Day or night.<BR>2 A day and night.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवासुप्त
दिवासुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>A sleep by day.<BR>E.<BR>दिवा, and सुप्त asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवि|दिविः
दिवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविज|दिविजः
दिविज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Celestial, heavenly, of heavenly origin.<BR>E.<BR>दिवि in heaven, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविषद्
दिविषद्<BR>m. (-द्)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>दिवि in heaven, सद् to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिविष्ठ|दिविष्ठः
दिविष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Celestial, heavenly, situated in heaven.<BR>E.<BR>दिवि in heaven, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवी
दिवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A sort of insect; also उपजिह्विका.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, क affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोकस्
दिवोकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A kind of cuckoo, the Chataka: see दिवौकस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोदास|दिवोदासः
दिवोदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>DIVODĀSA, a king so named, king of Benares, and founder of the Indian school of medicine.<BR>E.<BR>दिवः of heaven, दास the slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवोद्भव
दिवोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced in heaven.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>दिव heaven, उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिवौकस्
दिवौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>3 A deer.<BR>4 A bee.<BR>5 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दिव heaven, ether, ओकस् a mansion; also with the vowel unaltered दिवोकस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्य|दिव्यं|दिव्यः
दिव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Divine, celestial.<BR>2 Beautiful, agreeable, charming.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>1 Barley.<BR>2 A fragrant resin, (Bdellium.)<BR>3 The divine character or property.<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Cloves.<BR>2 A sort of Sandal.<BR>3 An ordeal.<BR>4 An oath.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु the sky or heaven, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यकारिन्
दिव्यकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>One who undergoes an ordeal.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगन्ध|दिव्यगन्धं|दिव्यगन्धः
दिव्यगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यगायन|दिव्यगायनः
दिव्यगायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Gandharba or singer of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, and गायन a singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यचक्षुस्
दिव्यचक्षुस्<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षु-क्षुः)<BR>1 Beautiful-eyed.<BR>2 Blind.<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>1 A sort of perfume.<BR>2 A monkey.<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>The faculty of seeing what is invisible by the human eye.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, and चक्षुस् an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यदोहद|दिव्यदोहदं
दिव्यदोहद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Fit for an offering or oblation.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, and दोहद wish, that which is the subject of a deity's desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=409" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यधर्म्मिन्|दिव्यधर्मिन्
दिव्यधर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>Virtuous, agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य, and धर्म्मिन् virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यपञ्चामृत|दिव्यपञ्चामृतं
दिव्यपञ्चामृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A mixture of five articles, ghee, curds, milk, butter, and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, पञ्च five, and अमृत ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरत्न|दिव्यरत्नं
दिव्यरत्न<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The fabulous gem Cintāmaṇi.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, and रत्न jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरथ|दिव्यरथः
दिव्यरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The car or vehicle of any deity.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यरस|दिव्यरसः
दिव्यरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यवस्त्र|दिव्यवस्त्रः
दिव्यवस्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>1 Clothed or invested in celestial raiment.<BR>2 Handsomely dressed.<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A plant, commonly Sūryaśobhā, a sort of sun-flower.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, वस्त्र cloth or clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्यादिव्या
दिव्यादिव्या<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>The heroine of a poem, as SĪTĀ, &c. of mixed origin or character, a demigoddess.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, अदिव्य not divine, partaking of both natures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योघ
दिव्योघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A form of ŚIVA, worshipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य, and ओघ heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योदक|दिव्योदकं
दिव्योदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rain water, dew, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य heavenly, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिव्योपपादुक|दिव्योपपादुकः
दिव्योपपादुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Divine, celestial, of heavenly birth or being.<BR>E.<BR>दिव्य divine, पद to go, with उप prefixed, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश|दिशः
दिश<BR>(औ) दिशौ r. 6th cl. (दिशति-ते)<BR>1 To show, to exhibit, to explain or make intelligible.<BR>2 To order, to command, to direct or send.<BR>3 To say, to speak.<BR>4 To give.<BR>With अप prefixed,<BR>To change, to disguise.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>1 To order or command.<BR>2 To show.<BR>3 To summons.<BR>With उद्,<BR>1 To proclaim, to make known or public.<BR>2 To show.<BR>With उप,<BR>To point out (literally or metaphorically), to show, to advise.<BR>With निर्,<BR>1 To speak aloud.<BR>2 To specify, to show.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To appoint, to order.<BR>With प्रति and सम्,<BR>To command, to return, to send back.<BR>With वि and अप,<BR>To plead in excuse, to state as a plea or pretext.<BR>With वि and निर्,<BR>To declare.<BR>With सम्,<BR>1 To exhibit, to show, &c.<BR>2 To communicate as news or information.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To approve, to permit.<BR>With सम and उप,<BR>To point out at a distance, as with the finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्
दिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्-दिशौ-दिशः)<BR>Region, space, quarter, part.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to shew, affix क्विन्; also with टाप् added, दिशा, f. (-शा) or with ङीप्, द्रिशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिशस्
दिशस्<BR>f. (-शाः)<BR>Region, quarter.<BR>E.<BR>दिश, and असुन् affix: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिश्य|दिश्यं
दिश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Situated, bearing, lying in a particular tract or quarter, as पर्व्वदिश्य eastern, bearing east.<BR>E.<BR>दिश् a quarter, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट|दिष्टं|दिष्टः
दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Shown, pointed out.<BR>2 Delineated, described.<BR>3 Counselled, advised, enjoined.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A sort of Curcuma: see दारुहरिद्रा.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Fate, destiny, fortune, good or ill luck.<BR>E.<BR>दिश् to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टान्त|दिष्टांत|दिष्टान्तः
दिष्टान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>दिष्ट fortune, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्टि|दिष्टिः
दिष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>2 A sort of measure.<BR>E.<BR>दिश् to point out, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्ट्या
दिष्ट्या<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation, indicative of joy or auspiciousness, luckily, fortunately.<BR>E.<BR>दिश् pointing out, स्त्यै to sound, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिष्णु|दिष्णुः
दिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Giving, one who gives, a donor.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, इष्णु Uṇādi affix: see देष्णु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दिह
दिह<BR>(औ) दिहौ r. 2nd cl. (दिग्धे)<BR>1 To increase, to augment, to accumulate.<BR>2 To smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी<BR>r. 4th cl. (ओ ङ) ओदीङ (दीयते)<BR>To waste, to diminish, to be reduced, to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दी
दी<BR>f. (दीः)<BR>Wasting, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>दी to waste, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्ष
दीक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (दीक्षति)<BR>1 To be shaved.<BR>2 To perform a sacrifice.<BR>3 To initiate.<BR>4 To teach religious observances.<BR>4 To be self-restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षणीयेष्टि|दीक्षणीयेष्टिः
दीक्षणीयेष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टि)<BR>A particular sacrifice, that preceded by the Dīkṣa: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>दीक्षा as below, छ affix, and इष्टि a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षा
दीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Sacrificing, offering oblations.<BR>2 Worshipping in general.<BR>3 Engaging in a course of austerities.<BR>4 Certain ceremonies preliminary to a sacrifice.<BR>5 Receiving the initiatory Mantra or incantation.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, (knowledge,) and क्षि to destroy, (sin); deriv. irr. or दीक्ष to initiate, &c. affix अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षान्त|दीक्षांत|दीक्षान्तः
दीक्षान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A supplementary sacrifice, one made to atone for any defects in a preceding one.<BR>E.<BR>दिक्षा sacrifice, and अन्त completion, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षित|दीक्षितः
दीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Initiated.<BR>2 Performed, (as the Dīkṣa ceremony.)<BR>3 One by whom the preparatory ceremonies have been observed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An assemblage of priests for peculiar ceremonies, or for any sacrifice.<BR>2 The pupil of an ascetick.<BR>E.<BR>दीक्ष to perform a sacrifice or to be initiated, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीक्षितृ
दीक्षितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A spiritual father, the communicator of the initiatory Mantra or prayer.<BR>E.<BR>दीक्ष to sacrifice, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीद
दीद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>दी, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीदिवि|दीदिविः
दीदिवि<BR>mfn. (-विः-विः-वि)<BR>Risen, ascended.<BR>mn. (-विः-वि)<BR>Boiled rice.<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, Uṇādi affix क्विन्, the radical reduplicate, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधिति|दीधितिः
दीधिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A ray of light, a sun or a moonbeam.<BR>2 Light in general.<BR>E.<BR>दीधी to shine, affix क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीधी
दीधी<BR>(ङ्) दीधीङ्^1 r. 2nd cl. (दीधीते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To play or sport.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: Also, affix Na change to N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीन|दीनं|दीनः
दीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Poor, indigent, needy, distressed.<BR>2 Afraid, frightened, timid.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A mouse or shrew.<BR>E.<BR>दी to waste or decay, affix क्त, deriv. irr. or दी as before, Uṇādi affix नक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनचेतन
दीनचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Distressed, dejected.<BR>E.<BR>दीन, and चेतन feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनमुख
दीनमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Down-cast, of melancholy aspect.<BR>E.<BR>दीन, and मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीनार|दीनारः
दीनार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A gold ornament.<BR>2 A seal.<BR>3 A weight of gold, variously stated as two Kāṣṭhas, one Pala of thirtytwo Reitis, and also as the large Pala or hundred and eight Suvarṇas.<BR>4 A coin, a Dinar.<BR>E.<BR>दीन a pauper, and ऋ to go; what is given to the poor; or दी to waste, Uṇādi affix आरन्, and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=410" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप|दीपः
दीप<BR>r. 4th cl. (ई ऋ) ऋदीपी (दीप्यते)<BR>To shine, to blaze, to be luminous or light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप|दीपः
दीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, affix क or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपक|दीपकं|दीपकः
दीपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Making luminous or beautiful.<BR>2 Kindling, inflaming.<BR>3 Exciting, rendering intense, (a feeling, &c.)<BR>4 Tonic, stimulant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An aromatick seed, (Ligusticum ajväen, Rox.)<BR>2 Small cumin.<BR>3 Celosia cristata.<BR>4 Saffron.<BR>5 A lamp.<BR>6 A falcon.<BR>7 A name of KĀMA.<BR>8 One of the Rāgas or modes of music.<BR>f. (-पिका)<BR>1 One of the Rāgiṇīs, or female personifications of the musical modes.<BR>2 A title of various books, (the illustrator, the illuminator.)<BR>3 Moonlight.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A figure of rhetoric, dilating upon an idea, or accumulation of expressions tending to one object.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, in the causal form, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकिट्ट|दीपकिट्टं
दीपकिट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Lamp black, soot.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and किट्ट sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपकूपी
दीपकूपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>The wick of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपखोरी
दीपखोरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The wick of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप light, खुड to divide, affix अच्, and ड changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपध्वज|दीपध्वजः
दीपध्वज<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>Lamp black, the condensed smoke or soot of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and ध्वज symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपन|दीपनं|दीपनः
दीपन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Inflaming, light or heat-exciting.<BR>2 Tonic, stimulant.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Inflaming, lighting.<BR>2 Stimulating, exciting.<BR>3 A root, commonly Tagara.<BR>4 Saffron.<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>An aromatick seed, (Ligusticum ajväen.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A sort of potherb, commonly Śaliñca, (Achyranthes triandra, Rox.)<BR>2 Celosia cristata.<BR>3 Cassia tora.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, in the causal form, and युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपनीय|दीपनीयः
दीपनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be lighted, to be inflamed.<BR>2 To be excited or stimulated.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An aromatick seed, (Ligusticum ajväen, Rox.)<BR>2 A stimulant drug, as pepper of various kinds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपपादप|दीपपादपः
दीपपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A lampstand, a candlestick.<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपपुष्प|दीपपुष्पः
दीपपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Champac, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>दीप enkindling, (passion,) and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपमाला
दीपमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A row of lamps, an illumination.<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and माला a garland; also दीपमालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपयत्
दीपयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Illuminating, inflaming.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to kindle, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपवृक्ष|दीपवृक्षः
दीपवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The stand or stem of a lamp, a candlestick.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and वृक्ष a tree; also दीपवृक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशिखा
दीपशिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 Lamp black, especially considered as applicable to the eyes, to darken the lashes, &c.<BR>2 The flame of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपशृङ्खला|दीपशृंखला
दीपशृङ्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A row or string of lamps.<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपान्विता
दीपान्विता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A festival: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपाली
दीपाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The day of new moon in the month Aśvin or Kārttika, (September-October,) a festival with nocturnal illuminations in honor of KĀRTTIKEYA; the Divalī, as it is usually termed.<BR>2 A row or range of lamps.<BR>E.<BR>दीप a lamp, and आली a line; also दीपावली the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपित
दीपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Illuminated, irradiated.<BR>2 Excited, inflamed.<BR>3 Manifested.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to kindle, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीपितृ
दीपितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>An illuminator, an enlightener, shining, irradiating.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to kindle, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्त|दीप्तं|दीप्तः
दीप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Luminous, splendid, radiant.<BR>2 Blazing, glowing.<BR>3 Burnt.<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>3 Asafoetida.<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A lime.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>A plant: see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to blaze, to shine, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तक|दीप्तकं|दीप्तकः
दीप्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तजिह्वा
दीप्तजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A fox.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, fiery, and जिह्वा tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तपिङ्गल|दीप्तपिङ्गलः
दीप्तपिङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, and पिङ्गल tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तरस|दीप्तरसः
दीप्तरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोचन|दीप्तलोचनः
दीप्तलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तलोह|दीप्तलोहं
दीप्तलोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताक्ष|दीप्ताक्षः
दीप्ताक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त glowing, and अक्ष the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताग्नि|दीप्ताग्निः
दीप्ताग्नि<BR>mfn. (-ग्निः-ग्निः-ग्नि)<BR>1 Of good digestion.<BR>2 Kindled, fed, (as fire.)<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त excited, and अग्नि fire, or the appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ताङ्ग|दीप्तांग|दीप्ताङ्गः
दीप्ताङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्ति|दीप्तिः
दीप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>3 The swift flight of an arrow.<BR>4 A property of women, extreme loveliness, brilliant beauty.<BR>5 Lac.<BR>6 Bell metal.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तिमत्|दीप्तिमन्त्
दीप्तिमत्<BR>m. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Shining, radiant.<BR>2 Blazing, flaming.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्तोपल|दीप्तोपलः
दीप्तोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The sun-gem, a crystalline lens.<BR>E.<BR>दीप्त shining, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्य|दीप्यः
दीप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>1 To be kindled or inflamed.<BR>2 To be stimulated.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>1 A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>2 An aromatic seed, (Ligusticum ajväen.)<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and यत् affix: see दीप; also with कन् added दीप्यकः see दीपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्यमान
दीप्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shining, radiant, irradiating.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्र|दीप्रः
दीप्र<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्तं)<BR>Light, luminous.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to shine, affix र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीप्रास्त्रधर
दीप्रास्त्रधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Armed with shining weapons; well accoutred.<BR>E.<BR>दीप light, अख arms, धृ to hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घ|दीर्घं|दीर्घः
दीर्घ<BR>mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं)<BR>Long, applied either to space or time.<BR>m. (-र्धः)<BR>1 The Śāl tree.<BR>2 A long vowel.<BR>3 The 5th, 6th, 7th, or 8th sign of the zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide or send, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकण्ठक|दीर्घकंठक|दीर्घकण्ठकः
दीर्घकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of crane, the Vaka, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, कण्ठ throat, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकन्धर|दीर्घकंधर|दीर्घकन्धरः
दीर्घकन्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and कन्धर neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकाल
दीर्घकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A long time, a long period.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकाष्ठ
दीर्घकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A spar, a beam, a long piece of timber.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकील|दीर्घकीलः
दीर्घकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, कील a stem or stake; also with कन्, दीर्घकीलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकेश|दीर्घकेशः
दीर्घकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Long-haired.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकोशिका
दीर्घकोशिका<BR>f. (का)<BR>A cockle; also दीर्घ, कोशी, &c. see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=411" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घकोषिका
दीर्घकोषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockle.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, कोश or कोष a sheath or shell, affix ङीप्, दीर्घकोषी, or दीर्घकोशी and कन् with the fem. form added, दीर्घकोशिका, -षिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घगति|दीर्घगतिः
दीर्घगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घग्रीव|दीर्घग्रीवः
दीर्घग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A kind of curlew.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and ग्रीवा a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घघाटिक|दीर्घघाटिकः
दीर्घघाटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, घाटा the neck, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजङ्गल|दीर्घजङ्गलः
दीर्घजङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of fish, commonly Bhangan.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and जङ्गल desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजङ्घ|दीर्घजंघ|दीर्घजङ्घः
दीर्घजङ्घ<BR>mfn. (-ङ्घः-ङ्घा-ङ्घं)<BR>Long-thighed.<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>1 A crane.<BR>2 A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and जङ्घा a thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजिह्व|दीर्घजिह्वः
दीर्घजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजीव
दीर्घजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Long life.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and जीव life; also दीर्घजीवित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घजीविन्
दीर्घजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living or existing a long time.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतनु
दीर्घतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Tall, long.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतरु|दीर्घतरुः
दीर्घतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Tāla or palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतिमिषा
दीर्घतिमिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A kind of cucumber: see कर्क्कटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घतुण्डा
दीर्घतुण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>The musk shrew.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and तुण्डा a snout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदण्ड|दीर्घदण्डः
दीर्घदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The castor oil tree.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, दण्ड a stick or stem; also with कन् added, दीर्घदण्डकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदर्शिन्
दीर्घदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिणी-र्शि)<BR>Far-seeing, provident, wise.<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>1 A wise or learned man, a seer, a prophet.<BR>2 A vulture.<BR>3 A bean.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, दृश to see, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घदृष्टि|दीर्घदृष्टिः
दीर्घदृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A wise or provident man; also,<BR>mfn.<BR>Wise, provident, far-seeing.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घद्रु|दीर्घद्रुः
दीर्घद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनाद|दीर्घनादः
दीर्घनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A conch shell.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिद्रा
दीर्घनिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Death.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिश्वस्य
दीर्घनिश्वस्य<BR>ind.<BR>Sighing or having sighed deeply.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and निश्वस्य having sighed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घनिश्वास
दीर्घनिश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A long or deep drawn sigh.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and निश्वास a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपक्ष|दीर्घपक्षः
दीर्घपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and पक्ष a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपत्र|दीर्घपत्रः
दीर्घपत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Long-leaved longifolium.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Garlic.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 A sort of Eugenia.<BR>2 A kind of Chakuliya.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपत्रक|दीर्घपत्रकः
दीर्घपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A thorny plant: see करीर.<BR>2 A kind of Bassia growing in marshy places.<BR>3 Garlic.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, पत्र a leaf, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपर्ण
दीर्घपर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Long-leaved longifolium.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपल्लव|दीर्घपल्लवः
दीर्घपल्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वी-वं)<BR>Having long shoots or tendrils.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The Śaṇa plant, (Crotolaria juneca.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपादप|दीर्घपादपः
दीर्घपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The cocoanut tree.<BR>2 The betelnut tree.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपाद्
दीर्घपाद्<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and पाद for पद a foot; also with a final vowel दीर्घपाद m. (-दः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घपृष्ठ|दीर्घपृष्ठः
दीर्घपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घफल|दीर्घफलः
दीर्घफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमारुत|दीर्घमारुतः
दीर्घमारुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, मारुत wind er breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमुख
दीर्घमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Long-faced.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घमूल|दीर्घमूलं|दीर्घमूलः
दीर्घमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>Having a long root.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of Bilva tree.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of sensitive plant.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A creeper, (Echites frutescens): see श्यामलता.<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum); also Śālaparṇī.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरत|दीर्घरतः
दीर्घरत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and रत copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरद|दीर्घरदः
दीर्घरद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरसन|दीर्घरसनः
दीर्घरसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and रसना a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरात्र|दीर्घरात्रं
दीर्घरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A long period.<BR>2 A long night.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घराव
दीर्घराव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Making a long continued noise, yelling, howling.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and राव cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोगिन्
दीर्घरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Being long ill.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and रोगिन् sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोमन्
दीर्घरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, रोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घरोहिषक|दीर्घरोहिषकं
दीर्घरोहिषक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant sort of grass.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and रोहिषक another sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवंश|दीर्घवंशः
दीर्घवंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Having a long staff or stick.<BR>2 Being of an ancient family.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A reed.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and वंश a race, a bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवक्त्र|दीर्घवक्त्रः
दीर्घवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and वक्त्र face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्च्छिका
दीर्घवर्च्छिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An alligator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्ण
दीर्घवर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A long vowel.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and वर्ण a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवर्त्मन्
दीर्घवर्त्मन्<BR>m. (-र्त्मा)<BR>A long road, a long journey.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and वर्त्मन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवृन्त|दीर्घवृन्तः
दीर्घवृन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and वृन्त stalk; with कन् added दीर्घवृन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घवृन्तिका
दीर्घवृन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and वृन्त a stalk, कन् affix, with the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घशाख|दीर्घशाखः
दीर्घशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसक्थ|दीर्घसक्थं
दीर्घसक्थ<BR>mfn. (-क्थः-क्था-क्थं)<BR>Long-thighed.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and सक्थि a thigh, affix अच्; figuratively used, the compound retains its proper final, as दीर्घसक्थि चक्रं a long-spoked wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसत्र|दीर्घसत्रं|दीर्घसत्रः
दीर्घसत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A sort of religious ceremony, one of long continuance.<BR>2 A place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, सत्र sacrifice, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसन्ध्यत्व|दीर्घसंध्यत्व
दीर्घसन्ध्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Long-continued observance of the chief daily rites.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and सन्ध्या the morning, noon, and evening oblation, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसुरत|दीर्घसुरतः
दीर्घसुरत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and सुरत coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्र|दीर्घसूत्रः
दीर्घसूत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Dilatory, slow, tedious.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and सूत्र line or thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रता
दीर्घसूत्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dilatoriness, tediousness.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घसूत्र, and तल् added; also with त्व, दीर्घसूत्रत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घसूत्रिन्
दीर्घसूत्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>Dilatory.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and सूत्रिन् having a line or thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घस्वर
दीर्घस्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A long vowel.<BR>2 A long note, a minim or semibreve.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and स्वर a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घाध्वग|दीर्घाध्वगः
दीर्घाध्वग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>A letter carrier, a messenger, an express.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, अध्वन् a road, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=412" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घाध्वन्
दीर्घाध्वन्<BR>n. (-ध्व)<BR>A long journey.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and अध्वन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घामय
दीर्घामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Long ill.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुध|दीर्घायुधः
दीर्घायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A spear, a javelin.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and आयुध weapon, or one so armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुस्
दीर्घायुस्<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Long-lived.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 The saint MĀRKAṆḌEYA.<BR>2 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>3 A crow.<BR>4 A tree: see जीवक.<BR>n. (-यु)<BR>Long life.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घायुष्य|दीर्घायुष्यः
दीर्घायुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Long-lived.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and आयुष्य lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्घिका
दीर्घिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A large and long pond.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, affix कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीर्ण|दीर्णः
दीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Torn, rent, sundered.<BR>2 Frightened, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to tear, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीवि|दीविः
दीवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>see दिवि and किकीदिवि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीव्यत्|दीव्यन्त्
दीव्यत्<BR>mfn. (-व्यन्-व्यती-व्यत्)<BR>Playing, sporting.<BR>E.<BR>दिव play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दीव्यमान
दीव्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Throwing, darting, shooting.<BR>2 Playing.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दु|दुः
दु<BR>r. 1st cl. (दवति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>(दुनोति) r. 5th cl. (ओ, टु) ओटुटु<BR>1 To be in pain, to burn morally or figuratively.<BR>2 To cause pain, anxiety, &c.<BR>3 To burn, to heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःख|दुःखं
दुःख<BR>r. 10th cl. (दुःखयति)<BR>To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःख|दुःखं
दुःख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Pain, sorrow, affliction, distress, unhappiness.<BR>2 The world.<BR>3 Difficulty, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख to give pain, affix अच्; or दु bad, and ख्या to call; or खन to dig, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखकर
दुःखकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Causing pain.<BR>2 Afflicting, occasioning sorrow or trouble.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखछिन्न|दुःखच्छिन्न
दुःखछिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Cut with difficulty, tough, hard.<BR>2 Afflicted, pained, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and छिन्न cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखछेद्य|दुःखच्छेद्य
दुःखछेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 To be cut with difficulty, tough, hard.<BR>2 To be overcome with difficulty.<BR>3 To be hart or pained by, (affliction, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and छेद्य to be cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखजीविन्
दुःखजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living in pain or distress.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखदग्ध
दुःखदग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Afflicted, pained, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखदोह्या
दुःखदोह्या<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A cow difficult to be milked.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख trouble, दोह्य to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखप्राय
दुःखप्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Full of trouble or pain.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and प्राय abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखबहुल
दुःखबहुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Painful, distressful, abounding with trouble, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and बहुल much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखभागिन्
दुःखभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Suffering pain, having pain as their portion.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखयोग|दुःखयोगः
दुःखयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Occurrence or incidence of trouble, pain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखलभ्य
दुःखलभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>To be obtained or effected with difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and लभ्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंवर्द्धित
दुःखसंवर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reared with trouble and difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुःस्व, and संवर्द्धित raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंयोग
दुःखसंयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Accession or presence of pain, distress, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसंस्थिति
दुःखसंस्थिति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Wretched, poor, miserable.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and संस्थिति condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखसागर|दुःखसागरः
दुःखसागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Deep distress.<BR>2 The world.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and सागर an ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखहन्
दुःखहन्<BR>mfn. (-हा-हा-ह)<BR>Removing pain.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and हन् who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखातीत
दुःखातीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Freed from pain.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखान्वित
दुःखान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pained, afflicted, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखार्त्त|दुःखार्त
दुःखार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Afflicted, pained, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखित|दुःखितः
दुःखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pained, suffering pain.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pain, distress, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख to give pain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखिन्
दुःखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>1 Suffering pain, sorrowing, afflicted.<BR>2 Difficult, painful.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःखोपेत
दुःखोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suffering distress, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुःख, and उपेत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःप्राप
दुःप्राप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्राप obtaining; also दुष्प्राप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःप्राप्य
दुःप्राप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्राप्य obtainable: also दुष्प्राप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशासन|दुःशासनः
दुःशासन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ungovernable, ill managed, intractable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and शासन an edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःशील
दुःशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Ill behaved, reprobate, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and शील behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषमम्
दुःषमम्<BR>ind.<BR>Improperly, unseasonably, unfitly.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, सम् equal to; स changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःषूति
दुःषूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A wicked son.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, सूति progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसन्धान|दुःसंधान
दुःसन्धान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Not coherent, difficult to be united or joined.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and सन्धान uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसम
दुःसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Improper, unseasonable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसह
दुःसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Intolerable, difficult to be borne.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and सह what is borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाधिन्
दुःसाधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A porter, a warder.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, साध to accomplish, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःसाध्य|दुःसाध्यः
दुःसाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Difficult, arduous, not easily accomplished.<BR>2 Incurable or difficult of cure.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, साध to accomplish, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थ|दुःस्थः
दुःस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Poor, ill conditioned, badly situated.<BR>2 Ignorant, unwise, a fool.<BR>3 Suffering pain or affliction, distressed, unhappy.<BR>4 Covetous.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>Pain, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, स्था to be or exist, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्थिति|दुःस्थितिः
दुःस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Unsteadiness, instability.<BR>2 Unhappiness, ill fortune or condition.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, &c. स्थिति staying, state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्पर्श|दुःस्पर्शः
दुःस्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Difficult or unfit to be touched.<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>f. (-र्शा)<BR>A prickly sort of nightshade.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, स्पृश to touch, affix खल्, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुःस्फोट|दुःस्फोटः
दुःस्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of weapon.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, स्फुट to bear, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुकूल|दुकूलं
दुकूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Wove silk.<BR>2 Very fine cloth or raiment.<BR>E.<BR>टु for दुर् ill, कूल to cover, affix क; or दु to heat, to keep hot, उलच् affix, and कू or गू augment, whence also दुगल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुगूल
दुगूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Wove silk: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=413" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्ध|दुग्धः
दुग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Filled, full.<BR>2 Milked.<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>1 Milk.<BR>2 Milking.<BR>f. (-ग्धी)<BR>A medicinal plant; also क्षीरी.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धकूपिका
दुग्धकूपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of cake made of ground rice, and milk, &c. fried with ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धता
दुग्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Milkiness, the nature of milk.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to दुग्ध; also with त्व, दुग्धत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धतालीय|दुग्धतालीयं
दुग्धतालीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Milk and mangoes, mango fool.<BR>2 The froth of milk, syllabub.<BR>3 The skim of milk or cream.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्धता, लीङ् to embrace or adhere, affix छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धपाचन|दुग्धपाचनं
दुग्धपाचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A vessel for boiling milk.<BR>E.<BR>टुग्ध milk, and पाचन cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धपुच्छी
दुग्धपुच्छी<BR>f. (-च्छी)<BR>A plant commonly Dugdhapeya.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध milk, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धफेन|दुग्धफेनः
दुग्धफेन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The froth or skim of milk, syllabub, cream.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A small medicinal shrub, so called.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध milk, फेन froth, foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाक्ष|दुग्धाक्षः
दुग्धाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A sort of stone, (opal?)<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध milk, and अक्ष a die, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाब्धि|दुग्धाब्धिः
दुग्धाब्धि<BR>n. (-ब्धिः)<BR>The sea of milk.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध, and अब्धि sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धाब्धितनया
दुग्धाब्धितनया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of LAKṢMI.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्धाब्धि, and तनया daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिका
दुग्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of Asclepias, (A. rosea, Rox.) (the Hindi derivative Dūdhi, is also applied to Euphorbia hirta and thymifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध milk, and ठन् affix, and the feminine form; the leaves, &c. yielding a milky sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिन्
दुग्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-ग्धी-ग्धिनी-ग्धि)<BR>Milky, having milk.<BR>E.<BR>दुग्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुग्धिनिका
दुग्धिनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant described as a red sort of Apang, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुच्छक|दुच्छकः
दुच्छक<BR>f. (-कः)<BR>A kind of perfume: see मुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुडि|दुडिः
दुडि<BR>f. (-डिः)<BR>A small or female tortoise: see दुलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुण्डुक|दुंडुक|दुण्डुकः
दुण्डुक<BR>mfn. (कः-का-कं)<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest, bad-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुण्डुभ|दुंडुभ|दुंडुभः|दुण्डुभः
दुण्डुभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A kind of snake, one which is described as not venomous^1.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुभ to sink, Uṇādi affix उभ, deriv. irr.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्
दुद्<BR>f. (-दुत् or दुद्)<BR>Anxiety, uneasiness.<BR>E.<BR>दु to give pain, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्द
दुद्द<BR>mfn. (-द्दः-द्दा-द्दं)<BR>1 Giving pain.<BR>2 Wicked.<BR>E.<BR>दुद्, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्यूषु
दुद्यूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to play with or brandish.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, desid. form irr., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुद्रुम|दुद्रुमः
दुद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A green onion.<BR>E.<BR>दु bad, द्रुम tree; onions being prohibited food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुधूषत्
दुधूषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षती-षत्)<BR>Trying to shake.<BR>E.<BR>धु to tremble, desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दम|दुंदम|दुंदमः|दुन्दमः
दुन्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of drum.<BR>E.<BR>दु bad, ill, दम to subdue, affix अच्, नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दु|दुंदु|दुंदुः|दुन्दुः
दुन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A name of VASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A kind of drum.<BR>E.<BR>दु difficult, दस to tame, affix डु, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दुभि|दुंदुभि|दुंदुभिः|दुन्दुभिः
दुन्दुभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>1 A sort of large kettle drum.<BR>2 A name of VARUṆA, regent of the ocean. The name of a Daitya or demon.<BR>3 A pair or couple.<BR>f. (-भिः-भी)<BR>1 A die or dice.<BR>2 Twice three spots on a dice, or a pair of dice, with three spots on each.<BR>E.<BR>दुन्दु imitative sound, and भा to utter, affix कि, or द्यौ heaven, उभ to fill, and deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्दुमार|दुंदुमारः|दुन्दुमारः
दुन्दुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of red worm.<BR>2 The smoke of a house.<BR>3 A cat: other authorities have धुन्धुमार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुन्वत्
दुन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वती-न्वत्)<BR>Afflicting, injuring.<BR>E.<BR>दु to injure, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्
दुर्<BR>ind.<BR>A depreciative particle, implying,<BR>1 Pain, trouble, (bad, difficult, ill.)<BR>2 Inferiority, (bad, vile, contemptible.)<BR>3 Prohibition, (away, hold, forbear.)<BR>It corresponds in general to the English prefixes, in, un, &c. as in infamous, unbearable, and the like.<BR>E.<BR>दो to cut or divide, डुर affix. In composition, the final र is changed to visarga, and this to a sibilant optionally before the two first consonants of each class and the sibilants, as दुःकर, दुष्कर; and दुःसह, दुस्सह; or to र again before any other consonant or vowel, as दुर्ग, दुरतिक्रम &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरक्ष|दुरक्षः
दुरक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A loaded or fraudulent die or dice.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अक्ष a die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरतिक्रम|दुरतिक्रमः
दुरतिक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult to be suppressed or overcome, insuperable, unconquerable.<BR>2 Difficult of performance or accomplishment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अतिक्रम overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरत्यय
दुरत्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Difficult to be passed or overcome.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अत्यय going over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरदृष्ट|दुरदृष्टं
दुरदृष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Bad luck, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अदृष्ट fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरधिगम
दुरधिगम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult to be traversed.<BR>2 Difficult to be read through or studied.<BR>2 Insurmountable, difficult to be overcome.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अधिगम going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्यय
दुरध्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Difficult of attainment or of acquirement.<BR>2 Difficult of perusal.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अध्यय going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरध्व|दुरध्वः
दुरध्व<BR>m. (-ध्वः)<BR>A bad road.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, अध्वन् a road, अच् substituted for the final syllable of the last member of the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरन्त|दुरंत
दुरन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Ending ill, having a bad end.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरपचार
दुरपचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult to be displeased or offended.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अपचार offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरभिग्रह|दुरभिग्रहः
दुरभिग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Difficult to be taken or laid hold of.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and अभिग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक|दुराकः
दुराक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barbarian.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराक्राम
दुराक्राम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult to be passed.<BR>2 Invincible.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आङ् before क्रम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराचार|दुराचारः
दुराचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Wicked, depraved, following evil practices.<BR>2 Disregarding or deviating from established practices.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्य
दुराढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>Poor, not rich.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आढ्य rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्यकर
दुराढ्यकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who does any thing with difficulty though rich.<BR>2 What is done by one not rich.<BR>E.<BR>दुराढ्य, कृ to do, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराढ्यम्भव|दुराढ्यंभव
दुराढ्यम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Proceeding from one not rich. Produced with difficulty by one who is rich.<BR>E.<BR>दुराढ्य, भू to be, खल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरात्मन्
दुरात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Vile, wicked, bad.<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A rascal, a scoundrel, a villain.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=414" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधर्ष|दुराधर्षः
दुराधर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Haughty, intractable.<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Whitemustard.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आधर्ष pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराधि|दुराधिः
दुराधि<BR>mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>Painful, distressing.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आधि affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराप
दुराप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, आप to obtain, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरारोह|दुरारोहः
दुरारोह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Of difficult ascent.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The palm tree.<BR>2 The date tree.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>दुर with difficulty, आरोह to be ascended, from रुह to rise, with आङ् prefixed, affixes अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालभ
दुरालभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Unfit to be touched or taken, difficult of handling.<BR>2 Difficult of attainment.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A prickly plant, commonly Javāsa, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, bad, hardly, लभ to attain, with आङ् prefixed, affix खल, fem. affix टाप्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालम्भा
दुरालम्भा<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>A plant, Javāsa: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>as above, नुम् optionally inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालाप|दुरालापः
दुरालाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Abuse, scurrilous or abusive language.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, आलाप address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरालोक|दुरालोकः
दुरालोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Painfully bright, dazzling, not to be looked at.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Great brightness or splendour.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आलोक seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुराशय
दुराशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Difficult of shelter or asylum.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आशय resting place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरास
दुरास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Difficult to be overcome or expelled.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and आस to sit, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरासद|दुरासदः
दुरासद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Difficult of attainment.<BR>2 Difficult of access.<BR>3 Unequalled, unrivalled.<BR>4 Intolerable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् with difficulty, आङ् implying to or up to, सद to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरित|दुरितं
दुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sinful, wicked.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् vile, bad, इत gone, become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरिष्ठ|दुरिष्ठः
दुरिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very bad, very wicked.<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Great crime, extreme wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, and इष्ठन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरीषणा
दुरीषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Curse, cursing.<BR>2 An evil eye.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ईषणा seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुत्तर
दुरुत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Impassable, difficult to be crossed.<BR>2 Unanswerable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उत्तर going over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुदाहर
दुरुदाहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult to be articulated or pronounced.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उदाहर pronouncing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुद्वह
दुरुद्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Burthensome, unbearable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उद्वह up-bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपक्रम
दुरुपक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult of access or approach.<BR>2 Difficult of cure.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उपक्रम approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपचार
दुरुपचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Difficult of cure.<BR>2 Unmanageable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उपचार implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरुपस्थान
दुरुपस्थान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unapproachable, unattainable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and उपस्थान proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुरोदर|दुरोदरं|दुरोदरः
दुरोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A gamester.<BR>2 A stake.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Playing, gaming.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, reprehensible, उदर contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ग|दुर्गं|दुर्गः
दुर्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्गः-र्गा-र्गं)<BR>1 Difficult of access or approach, inaccessible, impervious, impermeable.<BR>2 Difficult of attainment, unattainable.<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>1 A fort, a strong hold, a Droog or hill fort.<BR>2 A pass, a defile, a difficult or narrow passage over a stream or a mountain, or through a wood, &c.<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The name of an Asura slain by DURGĀ.<BR>f. (-र्गा)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA, and mother of KĀRTTIKEYA, and GAṆEŚA; also called UMĀ, and PĀRVATĪ, &c.: as DURGĀ, she is a goddess of terrific form, and irascible temper, and particularly worshipped at the DURGĀ Pūjā, held in Bengal in the month of Āśvina, or about October.<BR>2 The indigo plant.<BR>3 A creeping shrub, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>4 A singing bird, the Śyāmā.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, with difficulty, गम to go, affix ड; the etymology of the goddess is thus given, दुर् with difficulty, गम to be known; a knowledge of whom is obtained only by the severest austerities; or दुर् bad, गै to sing, who is especially hymned by the wicked; or दुर्ग the Asura slain by the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गकर्म्म
दुर्गकर्म्म<BR>mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं)<BR>Enterprize, difficult undertaking.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गकारक|दुर्गकारकं
दुर्गकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Making difficult or impassable.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग an impervious thicket, and कारक making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गत|दुर्गतः
दुर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Poor, indigent, distressed.<BR>2 Suffering pain or affliction.<BR>E.<BR>दुर ill, गत gone, become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गति|दुर्गतिः
दुर्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Hell.<BR>2 Poverty, indigence.<BR>3 A difficult path or site.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गतिनाशिनी
दुर्गतिनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्गति hell, नाशिनी who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गनिवासिन्
दुर्गनिवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Staying in a stronghold.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and निवासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्ध|दुर्गंध|दुर्गन्धं|दुर्गन्धः
दुर्गन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Ill-smelling, ill-scented.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Any ill-smelling substance.<BR>2 The mango tree.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Socāl salt.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गन्धिन्|दुर्गंधिन्
दुर्गन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Ill-smelling.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्गन्ध a bad smell, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गपुर
दुर्गपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fortified city.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गपुष्पी
दुर्गपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, commonly Keśāpuṣpa.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग with difficulty, पुष्पी a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गम|दुर्गमः
दुर्गम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Inaccessible, difficult of access or approach.<BR>2 Unattainable, difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् with pain or difficulty, गम to go, affix अप्; see दुर्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गमार्ग
दुर्गमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A defile, a difficult pass or way.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गलङ्घन|दुर्गलंघन|दुर्गलङ्घनः
दुर्गलङ्घन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Overcoming difficulties, making way through arduous passages or affairs, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and लङ्घन who traverses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गव्यसन
दुर्गव्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Defect in a citadel, its being ill-guarded, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and व्यसन misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गसञ्चर|दुर्गसंचर|दुर्गसञ्चरः
दुर्गसञ्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Progress or passage through an almost impervious or inaccessible spot.<BR>2 A bridge, &c. or any contrivance for passing a river, a defile, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग a defile, &c. सञ्चर going; also with संचार, दुर्गसंचार m. (-रः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गसम्पद्
दुर्गसम्पद्<BR>f. (-द्-त्)<BR>Essential part of a fortress.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and सम्पद् wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाधिकारिन्
दुर्गाधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The governor of a fort.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and अधिकारिन् who superintends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाध्यक्ष|दुर्गाध्यक्षः
दुर्गाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The governor of a fortress.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and अध्यक्ष supervisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=415" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गानवमी
दुर्गानवमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The ninth of the light half of Kārttika, sacred to DURGA as JAGADDHĀTRĪ.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्गा, and नवमी the ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गावरोध
दुर्गावरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Investing or besieging a fortress.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and अवरोध investing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्गाश्रयण
दुर्गाश्रयण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking refuge in a fortress.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and आश्रयण seeking shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्घोष|दुर्घोषः
दुर्घोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Harsh-voiced, roaring, bellowing.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A bear.<BR>2 A loud or disagreeable cry.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जन|दुर्जनः
दुर्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Bad, wicked, vile.<BR>2 Malicious, mischief-making.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bad man.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, जन a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्जनत्व|दुर्जनत्व
दुर्ज्जनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Wickedness, villainy.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to दुर्ज्जन; also with तल् affix दुर्ज्जनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्जय|दुर्जय|दुर्जयः
दुर्ज्जय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Invincible, difficult to be subdued or overcome.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्जर|दुर्जर
दुर्ज्जर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult of digestion, indigestible.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and जर digesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्जात|दुर्जात|दुर्जातं
दुर्ज्जात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inauspiciously born or produced.<BR>2 Improper.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>2 Disparity, unconformity, impropriety.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्जाति|दुर्जातिः|दुर्ज्जाति
दुर्जाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Vile, wicked.<BR>2 Low, outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ज्ञेय|दुर्ज्ञेयः
दुर्ज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Difficult to be known or understood.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and ज्ञेय to be known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णय|दुर्णयः
दुर्णय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Want of conduct, impropriety, impolicy.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and नय policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीत
दुर्णीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ill-behaved, ill-governed.<BR>2 Impolitic.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Misconduct.<BR>2 Impolicy.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and नीत conducted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्णीति
दुर्णीति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>1 Impolicy.<BR>2 Misconduct.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दम
दुर्दम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Difficult to be subdued.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and दम taming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दर
दुर्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Tearing.<BR>2 Distressing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kind of drug, Ṛṣabha.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and दर what tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्दर्श|दुर्दर्श
दुर्द्दर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Dazzling, painful to the sight.<BR>2 Difficult to be seen or met with.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and दर्श seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्दान्त|दुर्दान्त|दुर्दांत|दुर्दान्तः
दुर्द्दान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Untameable, intractable, difficult to be restrained or disciplined.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Strife, tumult.<BR>2 A calf.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and दान्त daunted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दिन|दुर्द्दिनं
दुर्दिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A dark or cloudy day.<BR>2 Rain, or cloudy and rainy weather.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्दुरुट
दुर्दुरुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An atheist.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् vile, repeated, अट to go or be, affix घञ्, and उ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्दष्ट
दुर्द्दष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Ill seen, (literally or figuratively,) ill-examined, imperfectly investigated.<BR>2 Looked at with an evil eye.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्दैव|दुर्दैव
दुर्द्दैव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Bad luck, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>ठुर्, and दैव fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धरुट
दुर्द्धरुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A pupil who obeys his teacher only after judging of the propriety of obedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रिता
दुर्द्रिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्रुम|दुर्द्रुमः
दुर्द्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A green onion.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, and द्रुम a tree: see दुद्रुम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्द्धर्ष
दुर्द्धर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>1 Difficult of attainment or approach.<BR>2 Haughty, distant.<BR>E.<BR>धर्ष, and दुर् pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्धर|दुर्द्धरः|दुर्धरः
दुर्धर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult to be sustained or borne, troublesome, unbearable.<BR>2 Irresistible, difficult to be restrained.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A division of hell.<BR>2 A kind of drug, commonly Ṛṣabha.<BR>3 The name of an Asura or Titan.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, धर having, possessing; it is also written दुर्द्धैर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामक|दुर्नामकं|दुर्नामकः
दुर्नामक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Hæmorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, नामन् a name, and कन् added: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्नामन्
दुर्नामन्<BR>mf. (-मा-म्नी)<BR>A cockle.<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Piles or hæmorrhoids.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, and नामन् a name, fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्; also in the first sense, with a final vowel दुर्नामा, f. (-मा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निर्ग्रंह्
दुर्निर्ग्रंह्<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Ungovernable, difficult of restraint.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and निर्ग्रंह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्निवार
दुर्निवार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Difficult to be stopped, hindered, contradicted, &c.<BR>2 Invincible, unconquerable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and निवार resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्न्निरीक्ष्य|दुर्निरीक्ष्य
दुर्न्निरीक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Hard to be looked at, as the sun, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and निरीक्ष्य to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्व|दुर्व
दुर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (ई) दुर्व्वी (दूर्व्वति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound, to kill, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ब्बल|दुर्बल|दुर्ब्बलः
दुर्ब्बल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Feeble, thin, emaciated.<BR>2 Weak, impotent.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>One who is circumcised, or whose glans penis is void of prepuce.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् implying depreciation or diminution, and बल strong, potent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्बुद्धि
दुर्बुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Silly, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भक्ष
दुर्भक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>To be eaten with difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and भक्ष eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भगा
दुर्भगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>1 A wife not loved or liked by her husband.<BR>2 A bad or ill tempered woman.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् little or ill, भग affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भर
दुर्भर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Burdensome, troublesome, hard to be supported.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and भर what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भिक्ष|दुर्भिक्षं
दुर्भिक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>Dearth, famine.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and भिक्षा alms; when charity ceases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भाग्य
दुर्भाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Unfortunate, unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and भाग्य fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्भेद्य
दुर्भेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 To be broken with difficulty.<BR>2 Firm, constant, not easily disunited.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and भेद्य to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मति|दुर्मति
दुर्म्मति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Silly, ignorant, simple, a blockhead.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मनस्|दुर्मनस्
दुर्म्मनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Sad, distressed, meditating or thinking sorrowfully.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् distress, मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मर|दुर्मर
दुर्म्मर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dying with difficulty, retentive of life.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Bent grass: see दूर्ब्बा.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् with difficulty, मृ to perish, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मल्लिका|दुर्मल्लिका
दुर्म्मल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A minor drama, a comedy, a farce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मुख|दुर्मुख|दुर्मुखः|दुर्म्मुखः
दुर्म्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>1 Scurrilous, foul-mouthed.<BR>2 Hideous, ugly.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 One of the monkey chiefs.<BR>2 One of the principal Nāgas or serpents.<BR>3 A horse.<BR>3 An Asura.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, मुख mouth or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मूल्य|दुर्मूल्य|दुर्म्मूल्यं
दुर्म्मूल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Any thing of high price or value.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्म्मेधस्|दुर्मेधस्
दुर्म्मेधस्<BR>mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः)<BR>Of little or contemptible understanding, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">Page417</a>] dull, stupid, ignorant, uninformed.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, मेधस् understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=416" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्य्योधन|दुर्योधन|दुर्योधनः|दुर्य्योधनः
दुर्य्योधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The elder of the Kuru princes, and leader in the war against his cousins, the Pāṇḍus and KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् vile, ill, युध to make war, affix युच्; the author and leader of an unjust warfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्योनि
दुर्योनि<BR>mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>Of low or impure origin.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्ल्लभ|दुर्लभ|दुर्लभः
दुर्ल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Difficult of attainment.<BR>2 Excellent, eminent.<BR>3 Dear, beloved.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A plant, (a sort of Hedysarum): see दुरालभा.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A prickly nightshade.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् difficult, लभ to gain, affix खल्, but without any nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वच|दुर्वच|दुर्व्वचं|दुर्व्वचः
दुर्व्वच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>1 Speaking ill or improperly.<BR>2 Speaking in pain.<BR>3 Difficult of utterance or articulation.<BR>4 What ought not to be spoken.<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Abuse, censure.<BR>2 Evil or unlucky speech.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्; वच to speak, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वचस्|दुर्वचस्
दुर्व्वचस्<BR>n. (-चः)<BR>Abuse, bad language.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, वचस्, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वर्ण|दुर्वर्ण|दुर्वर्णः|दुर्व्वर्णं
दुर्व्वर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Of a bad species or class.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Elavāluka: see एलवालुक.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, vile, and वर्ण species; the reduplication of the व is optional in this and the following words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वर्णक|दुर्वर्णक|दुर्व्वर्णकं
दुर्व्वर्णक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् inferior, वर्ण species, कन् pleonasm; inferior as compared with gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वह|दुर्वह
दुर्व्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Difficult to be borne or supported.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वाच्|दुर्वाच्
दुर्व्वाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>An ill speaker, morally or physically.<BR>f. (-वाच्)<BR>Speaking ill, either inelegantly or abusively.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वाच्य|दुर्वाच्य
दुर्व्वाच्य<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>Any unlucky or ill omened speech.<BR>2 Censure, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् improperly, वाच्य to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वाद|दुर्वाद|दुर्वादः|दुर्व्वादः
दुर्व्वाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>One who speaks ill, (grammatically, &c.) or one who utters abusive or unbecoming language.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, bad, वाद speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वार|दुर्वार
दुर्व्वार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Irresistible, not to be prevented or checked.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and वार preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्वासस्|दुर्वासस्
दुर्व्वासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Ill dressed.<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>The name of a Ṛṣi or saint, the son of ATRI, and an incarnation or portion of ŚIVA, famous for his choleric temperament.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्विध|दुर्विध|दुर्व्विधः
दुर्व्विध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 Poor, pauper, indigent.<BR>2 Wicked, malevolent.<BR>3 Foolish, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, विध habit, custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्व्विनीत|दुर्विनीत|दुर्विनीतः|दुर्व्विनीतः
दुर्व्विनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ill mannered, ill trained or behaved.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A restive horse.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् with difficulty, विनीत led, managed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विभाव्य|दुर्व्विभाव्य
दुर्विभाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Incomprehensible, inconceivable.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and विभाव्य to be observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विवाह|दुर्विवाहः|दुर्व्विवाह
दुर्विवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A bad mode or form of marriage.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्विषह|दुर्विषहः|दुर्व्विषह
दुर्विषह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Difficult to be sustained or supported.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and वि before सह to bear, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वृत्त|दुर्व्वृत्तः
दुर्वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Vile, wicked, leading a low or infamous life, following disreputable habits or business, a cheat, a juggler, a rogue, a blackguard, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, वृत to be or abide, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्वृत्ति|दुर्वृत्तिः
दुर्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Leading a disreputable life, following a degrading business, &c.<BR>2 Juggling, fraud.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हन
दुर्हन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>What is killed with difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् before हन to kill, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृद्
दुर्हृद्<BR>mfn. (-द् or त्)<BR>Inimical, ill-disposed^1.<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, हृद् heart.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुर्हृदय|दुर्हृदयः
दुर्हृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Evil-minded, bad-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, ill, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुल
दुल<BR>r. 10th cl. (दोलति)<BR>1 To raise, to throw up.<BR>2 To excite.<BR>3 To shake, to swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुलि|दुलिः
दुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A Muni or saint.<BR>f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>A small or female tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>दुल to throw up, (mud, &c.) affix कि, fem. affix optionally ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर|दुश्चरः
दुश्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Going with trouble or difficulty.<BR>2 Acting ill, behaving wickedly.<BR>3 Unattainable.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bivalve shell.<BR>2 A bear.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, चर to go, अच् or टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चरित
दुश्चरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Misbehaving, abandoned, wicked.<BR>m. (-तं)<BR>Misbehaviour, ill conduct, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and चरित conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चर्म्मन्|दुश्चर्मन्
दुश्चर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A circumcised man, or one whose prepuce is naturally or artificially wanting.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, difficult, चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्चेष्टित
दुश्चेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Misbehaving, doing or designing evil.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Evil purpose or action, misconduct, error.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and चेष्टित exerted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्च्यवन|दुश्च्यवनः
दुश्च्यवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् ill, च्यवन the name of a saint: INDRA having raised his arm to hurl his thunderbolt at Cyavana, had it fixed in that position by the curse of the saint; other etymologies are given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्छद
दुश्छद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Tattered, hardly covered.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुश्शासन
दुश्शासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One of the Kaurava princes.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and शासन government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष
दुष<BR>(इर, जौ) इरदुषौ r. 4th cl. (दुष्यति)<BR>1 To do or act wrong or improperly.<BR>2 To be impure.<BR>With प्र and आङ् prefixed,<BR>To become manifest or apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर|दुष्करं
दुष्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Difficult to be done.<BR>2 One who behaves ill, does wrong, &c. wicked, bad.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Æther, atmosphere.<BR>2 The tree of plenty.<BR>3 Doing any thing with pain or difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, and कर what does, from कृ with खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कर्म्मन्|दुष्कर्मन्
दुष्कर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Wickedness, sin.<BR>2 Any difficult or painful act.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुल
दुष्कुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A low family or race.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कुलीन|दुष्कुलीनः
दुष्कुलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of a low or degraded family.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Chor.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, कुलीन family or species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृत|दुष्कृतं
दुष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done wrong or wickedly.<BR>2 Done with difficulty or pain.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sin, crime, guilt.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् evil, कृत done, committed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=417" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतकर्म्मन्|दुष्कृतकर्मन्
दुष्कृतकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Wicked, reprobate.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्कृत, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतवहिष्कृत
दुष्कृतवहिष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Holy, free from sin.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्कृत, and वहिष्कृत excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्कृतिन्
दुष्कृतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Wicked, an evil doer.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्कृत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रम
दुष्क्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult of access.<BR>2 Going ill or laboriously.<BR>3 Ill arranged, unmethodical.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्क्रीत|दुष्क्रीतं
दुष्क्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dear, bought too dearly or unadvisedly.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, क्रीत purchased: a bad bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ख|दुष्खं
दुष्ख<BR>n. (-ष्खं)<BR>Pain in general: see दुःख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ट|दुष्टं|दुष्टः
दुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Low, vile.<BR>2 Weak, impotent.<BR>3 Wicked, depraved.<BR>4 Spoiled, injured.<BR>5 Violated.<BR>6 Contaminated, degraded.<BR>7 Worthless.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A harlot, a wanton.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A kind of Costus, (C. speciosus): see कुष्ट.<BR>E.<BR>दुष to be corrupt, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचारिन्
दुष्टचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wicked.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट, and चारिन् practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टचेतस्
दुष्टचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>1 Malevolent.<BR>2 Stupid.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट, and चेतस् the heart or mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टता
दुष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Wickedness, badness.<BR>2 Contamination, defilement.<BR>3 Violation.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to दुष्ट; also त्व, दुष्टत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टभाव
दुष्टभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Innately bad.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टभावता
दुष्टभावता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wickedness, innate depravity.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्टभाव, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टमति
दुष्टमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Wicked, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टवृष|दुष्टवृषः
दुष्टवृष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A lazy ox.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट as above, and वृष an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टव्रण|दुष्टव्रणः
दुष्टव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A dull boil or sore, a sinus.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट bad, and व्रण sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्टान्वित
दुष्टान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Defiled, rendered impure.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ट, and possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्ठु|दुष्ठुः
दुष्ठु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Ill, bad.<BR>2 Improperly, incorrectly.<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठुः-ष्ठुः-ष्ठु)<BR>Ill behaved, unprincipled, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>दु ill, स्था to be, affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पत्र|दुष्पत्रः
दुष्पत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Cor, a perfume.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पर्श
दुष्पर्श<BR>mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं)<BR>Not to be touched, unpleasant to the touch.<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji): see दुःस्पर्श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्पान
दुष्पान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Difficult to be drank.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रकृति
दुष्प्रकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of a bad nature or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्रकृति nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्षणी
दुष्प्रधर्षणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>दुर् with difficulty, प्र before धृष to show, to guide, affix ल्युट्; also with णिनि affix दुष्प्रधर्षिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रधर्षा
दुष्प्रधर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarium alhaji.)<BR>2 The date tree.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्र before धृष to guide, affix अङ्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रमय
दुष्प्रमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Immeasurable, difficult to be measured.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्र before मी to measure, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्रलम्भ
दुष्प्रलम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>Difficult of attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्र before लभ to gain, खल् affix, नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप
दुष्प्राप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Difficult of attainment, difficult to be got or reached.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्राप obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्प्राप्य
दुष्प्राप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Remote, unattainable, difficult of approach or attainment.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and प्राप्य obtainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्मन्त|दुष्मन्तः
दुष्मन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A prince of the lunar line, the husband of ŚAKUNTALĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and झ affix, मुम् aug.; also read दुष्यन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुष्यन्त|दुष्यंतः|दुष्यन्तः
दुष्यन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A prince: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>दुष to do wrong, झ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्तर
दुस्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Difficult to be crossed.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and तर crossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्त्यज
दुस्त्यज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Difficult to be relinquished or parted with.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and त्यज abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुस्सथ
दुस्सथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह
दुह<BR>(औ) दुहौ r. 2nd cl. (दोग्धि) 3rd pers. plu. (दुहन्ति)<BR>To milk.<BR>(इर) दुहिर r. 1st cl. (दोहति)<BR>1 To hurt, to afflict, to give pain.<BR>2 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्
दुह्<BR>m. (धुक्)<BR>A milker.<BR>E.<BR>दुह, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहत्
दुहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>1 Relinquishing, parting with.<BR>2 Milking.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहितुःपति|दुहितुःपतिः
दुहितुःपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A son-in-law, a daughter's husband.<BR>E.<BR>दुहितृ a daughter, in the possessive case, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुहितृ
दुहितृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, (the mother,) Uṇādi affix तृच्, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दुह्य|दुह्यं
दुह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be milked, milkable.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, affix क्यप्; also दोह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू<BR>(ओ, ङ) ओदूङ् r. 4th cl. (दूयते)<BR>1 To suffer or be consumed with pain.<BR>2 To inflict pain or anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दू
दू<BR>f. (दूः)<BR>Pain, distress.<BR>E.<BR>दू, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडभ|दूडभः
दूडभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Unfortunate, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>दुर difficult, डम्भ to deceive, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूडाश|दूडाशः
दूडाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Pained, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>दुर bad, painful, दशि to hurt, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूढ्य|दूढ्यः
दूढ्य<BR>mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं)<BR>Bad, vile.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्, and ध्यै to meditate, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूणाश|दूणाशः
दूणाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Destroyed or annihilated with trouble or difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>दुर before, णश to destroy, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत|दूतः
दूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sent, despatched.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A messenger or envoy, a news-carrier.<BR>2 An ambassador.<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>A female messenger, a confidante, a procuress, a go-between, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दु to go, Uṇādi affix क्त, and the vowel made long; or दू to suffer, affix क्त, fem. affix क्तिन् or क्तिच्, and optionally ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतघ्नी
दूतघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A plant, resembling the Kadamba: see कदम्बपुष्पी.<BR>E.<BR>दूत a messenger, घ्नी what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूति|दूतिः
दूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>See दूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूतिका
दूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female messenger, a confidante, &c. see दूत, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दूति; also with the penultimate vowel made long, दूतीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूत्य|दूत्यं
दूत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 An embassy, a message.<BR>2 The abstract state or condition of a message or a messenger.<BR>E.<BR>दूत a messenger, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूद
दूद<BR>mfn. (दः-दा-दं)<BR>Afflicting, harassing.<BR>E.<BR>दू, and द what gives or occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=418" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दून|दूनः
दून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>3 Shaken, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>दू to suffer, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूनवत्
दूनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Being agitated or distressed.<BR>2 Gone, having gone.<BR>E.<BR>दू to be agitated, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूप्र
दूप्र<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं)<BR>Strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर|दूरं
दूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Distant, remote.<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Far, far off.<BR>2 Widely, deeply.<BR>E.<BR>दुर with difficulty, इण् to go, Uṇādi affix रक्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरग
दूरग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Going a far or a long way.<BR>2 Remote.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरगामिन्
दूरगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going far.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>An arrow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरतस्
दूरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Afar, far off, from a distance, from afar.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरता
दूरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Remoteness, distance.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and तल; also with त्व, दूरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शन|दूरदर्शनः
दूरदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Foresight.<BR>2 Long-sightedness.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A vulture.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदर्शिन्
दूरदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Long-sighted, far-seeing, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a learned man, a teacher.<BR>2 A prophet, a seer.<BR>3 A vulture.<BR>E.<BR>दूर far, and दर्शिन् who sees, from दृश to see, with णिनि affix; also with क्विप् affix दूरदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदृश्
दूरदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>1 A learned man.<BR>2 A vulture: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरदृष्टि|दूरदृष्टिः
दूरदृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Long-sightedness.<BR>2 Foresight.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and दृष्टि sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरपातिन्
दूरपातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Far going.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and पातिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरभाज्
दूरभाज्<BR>mfn. (-क् or ज्)<BR>Distant.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and भाज् what shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरभिन्न
दूरभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Struck or wounded deeply.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and भिन्न divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरयायिन्
दूरयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Going far.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and यायिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवस्त्रक
दूरवस्त्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Naked, undressed.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवासिन्
दूरवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Residing in a foreign land, outlandish.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and वासिन् who or what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरविभिन्न
दूरविभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Unconnected by the ties of nature, of a different nature.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and विभिन्न separated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरवेधिन्
दूरवेधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Missile, projectile, (weapons, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>दूर afar, and वेधिन् what pierces or wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरसंस्थ
दूरसंस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Remote, distant.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and संस्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरसंस्थान
दूरसंस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Being or residing at a distance.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and संस्थान site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरस्थ
दूरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Remote, far off.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and स्थ what stays or is; also दूरस्थित, and दूरस्थायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूराप्लाव
दूराप्लाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Jumping far.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and आप्लाव a leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरावस्थित
दूरावस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Standing or being afar off.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and अवस्थित situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीकरण
दूरीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Removing, placing at a distance.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and करण making, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीकृत
दूरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Removed, placed afar off.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरीभूत
दूरीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Remote, far off.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and भूत become, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेत्य
दूरेत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Far, distant.<BR>E.<BR>दूर, and एत्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूरेरितेक्षण|दूरेरितेक्षणः
दूरेरितेक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Squint-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>दूर afar, ईरित sent, and ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्ब्बा|दूर्बा
दूर्ब्बा<BR>f. (-र्ब्बा)<BR>Bent grass, commonly Dūb (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ब्ब to hurt or be hurt, affix अच् or घञ्, fem. affix टाप्; what hurts sin, or is injured by cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्ब्बावण
दूर्ब्बावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A thicket of Dūb grass.<BR>E.<BR>दूर्ब्बा, and वन wood; also with the final unchanged, दूर्ब्बावन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूर्य्य|दूर्य|दूर्यं|दूर्य्यं
दूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Fæces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>दूर far, या to go, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूलास
दूलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूश्य|दूश्यं
दूश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>A tent: see दूष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष
दूष<BR>r. 4th cl. (दूष्यति)<BR>1 To be or become bad.<BR>2 To make bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषक|दूषकः
दूषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Ill, low, contemptible, infamous.<BR>2 Spoiling, corrupting, contaminating, who or what does so.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to be vile, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषण|दूषणः
दूषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, the brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Blame, fault, defect, offence.<BR>2 Spoiling, ruining, vitiating, defiling.<BR>3 Violating, (as a girl.)<BR>4 Breaking, (as an agreement.)<BR>E.<BR>दूष to become vile or wicked, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषणारि|दूषणारिः
दूषणारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>दूषण the brother of RĀVAṆA, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषयाण
दूषयाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Vitiating, defiling, spoiling.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to make bad, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषि|दूषिः
दूषि<BR>f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>The rheum of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to make bad, affix कि or क with डीष् added; also दूषिका and दूषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषिका
दूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The rheum of the eyes.<BR>2 A pencil or painting brush.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to make bad, (the eyes, &c.) affix ण्वुल्, fem. form; also दूषी, दूषि, and दूषीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषित|दूषितः
दूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Calumniated, falsely accused, especially of adultery.<BR>2 Contaminated, corrupted, spoiled.<BR>3 Violated.<BR>4 Blamed, censured.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A girl who has been violated or deflowered.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to become or make bad, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीका
दूषीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The secretion or rheum of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to hurt, (the eyes,) Uṇādi affix ईकन्: see दूषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूषीविष|दूषीविषं
दूषीविष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Poison that may be overcome by drugs or charms, or that does not act upon the system.<BR>E.<BR>दूषी rheum, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दूष्य|दूष्यं|दूष्यः
दूष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Reprehensible, contemptible, vile, bad.<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>An elephant's leathern girth.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 Clothes.<BR>2 A tent.<BR>3 Pus, matter.<BR>E.<BR>दूष to be or become wicked or bad, यत् or ण्यत् affix, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृ
दृ<BR>r. 6th cl. usually with आङ् prefixed (आद्रियते)<BR>To reverence, to revere, to respect.<BR>r. 5th cl. (दृणोति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (दरति दारयति)<BR>To fear, to be afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृंहित
दृंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Grown, increased.<BR>E.<BR>दृहि to increase, क्त affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक|दृकं
दृक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृकाण|दृकाणः
दृकाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A demigod, presiding over the third part of a sign of the zodiac, (in Astrology.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=419" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्कर्ण|दृक्कर्णः
दृक्कर्ण<BR>(-र्णः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दृश् an eye, and कर्ण an ear; whose eyes are his ears; in the opinion of the Hindus, the snake has no visible external ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्काण|दृक्काणः
दृक्काण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>See दृकाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्प्रिया
दृक्प्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Beauty.<BR>2 Splendor.<BR>E.<BR>दृश्, and प्रिय grateful to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृक्श्रुति|दृक्श्रुतिः
दृक्श्रुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दृश an eye, and श्रुति the ear: see दृक्कर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृगध्यक्ष|दृगध्यक्षः
दृगध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>दृश् the sight, त्र्यध्यक्ष ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्गोल|दृग्गोलः
दृग्गोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A small circle on the axis of the earth, within the greater circle of the armillary sphere, and accompanying each planetary circle.<BR>E.<BR>दृश्, and गोल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृग्विष|दृग्विषः
दृग्विष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A serpent or other such venomous reptile.<BR>E.<BR>दृश eye, and विष poison; whose eye is venomous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृङ्मण्डल
दृङ्मण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A small circle within the great circles of the armillary sphere, accompanying each planetary circle or orbit.<BR>E.<BR>दृश, and मण्डल sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृडक|दृडकः
दृडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fire-place, or hole made in the ground for cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढ|दृढं|दृढः
दृढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Much, exceeding; (in this sense it is also an adverb declinable in the neuter gender.)<BR>2 Hard, firm.<BR>3 Able, powerful.<BR>4 Bulky, massive, solid.<BR>5 Strong.<BR>6 Confirmed.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>दृह to increase, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकण्टक|दृढकण्टकः
दृढकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Dhaliākāra.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ much or many, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकाण्ड|दृढकांड|दृढकाण्डं|दृढकाण्डः
दृढकाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and काण्ड a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढकारिन्
दृढकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Persevering, determined.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and कारिन् who does, (any act.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढगात्रिका
दृढगात्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Granulated sugar.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm. गात्र substance, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढग्रन्थि|दृढग्रंथि|दृढग्रन्थिः
दृढग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढता
दृढता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Firmness, hardness.<BR>2 Steadiness.<BR>3 Solidity.<BR>4 Strength.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to दृढ; also with त्व, दृढत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढदंशक|दृढदंशकः
दृढदंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shark.<BR>E.<BR>दृड hard, दंशक a biter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढधन्वन्
दृढधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>A good archer.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढधुर्
दृढधुर्<BR>mfn. (-धूः-धूः-धु)<BR>Strong, able to bear a weight or load.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and धुर् a burthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढनिश्चय
दृढनिश्चय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Certain, confirmed, corroborated, undoubted.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and निश्चय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढफल|दृढफलः
दृढफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ hard, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढबद्ध
दृढबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound or tied tightly.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and वद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढबन्धिनी
दृढबन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firmly, वन्ध to bind, affixes णिनि, and ङीप्; winding closely round a tree or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढभक्ति
दृढभक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Faithful, devoted.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and भक्ति faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढमुष्टि|दृढमुष्टिः
दृढमुष्टि<BR>mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि)<BR>Miserly, niggardly, close-fisted,<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A sword, any weapon with a hilt or handle.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm, and मुष्टि a handle, a fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढमूल|दृढमूलः
दृढमूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ hard, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढलोमन्
दृढलोमन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-मं)<BR>Having coarse hair on the skin.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 A wild hog.<BR>2 Coarse hair, bristles.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm, stiff, and लोमन् the hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढव्रत
दृढव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Observing steadily a religious vow or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसन्धि|दृढसंधि|दृढसन्धिः
दृढसन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>1 Strong knit, well fixed or compact, (the person, &c.)<BR>2 Close, compact, free from interstices.<BR>3 Closely connected or allied.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm, and सन्धि union, a joint, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसूत्रिका
दृढसूत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant from the fibres of which bow strings are made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm, and सूत्र a thread, a fibre, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढसौहृद
दृढसौहृद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Firm in friendship, constant.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and सौहृद friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढस्कन्ध|दृढस्कन्धः
दृढस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A plant, a sort of Mimusops: see क्षीरिका.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ firm, and स्कन्ध stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढाङ्ग|दृढांग|दृढाङ्गं
दृढाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Firm-bodied, hard, strong.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A diamond.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढार्त्ति
दृढार्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 The end of a bow.<BR>2 Great pain.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and अर्त्ति end of a bow, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढाभक्ति
दृढाभक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A faithful mistress or wife.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ fem. form, and भक्ति attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृढायुध|दृढायुधः
दृढायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A hero, one firm in battle.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ, and आयुध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृत|दृतः
दृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Respected, honoured.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Cumin.<BR>E.<BR>दृ to respect, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृति|दृतिः
दृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A bellows.<BR>2 A fish.<BR>3 A skin of leather, or a leather bag for holding water.<BR>4 Skin, hide.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिधारक|दृतिधारकः
दृतिधारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Acanpāta.<BR>E.<BR>दृति a bellows, and धारक having; having leaves compared to a leather bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिहरि|दृतिहरिः
दृतिहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>दृति here said to mean skin in general, and हरि who steals, from हृ with इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृतिहार|दृतिहारः
दृतिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A carrier of skins or bags, a water carrier, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दृति, and हृ to take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृन्भू
दृन्भू<BR>m. (-न्भूः)<BR>1 The thunderbolt.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>f. (-न्भूः)<BR>1 A snake in general.<BR>2 A wheel.<BR>E.<BR>दृभ to fear, Uṇādi affix कू, and नुम् inserted; न being optionally changed to म before भ, the word is also read दृम्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप
दृप<BR>r. 4th cl. (ञि ईर ऊ) ञि ईरदृपु (दृप्यति)<BR>1 To be glad, to rejoice.<BR>2 To be arrogant, to be vain or proud.<BR>r. 6th cl. (दृपति)<BR>To pain, to inflict pain, to torture.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (दर्पति दर्पयति)<BR>To light, to kindle or inflame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्त|दृप्तः
दृप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to be proud, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्यत्
दृप्यत्<BR>mfn. (-प्यन्-प्यती-प्यत्)<BR>Being proud or arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to be proud, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृप्र|दृप्रः
दृप्र<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं)<BR>1 Strong, powerful.<BR>2 Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to be proud, Uṇādi affix रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृफ
दृफ<BR>r. 6th cl. (दृफति)<BR>To pain, to hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृब्ध|दृब्धः
दृब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Strung, tied.<BR>2 Afraid, frightened.<BR>3 Pained, tortured.<BR>E.<BR>दृभ to pain, to string, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृभ
दृभ<BR>(ई) दृभी r. 6th cl. (दृभति)<BR>1 To string, to arrange.<BR>2 To give pain.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (दर्भति दर्भयति)<BR>To fear, to be afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्प
दृम्प<BR>r. 6th cl. (दृम्पति)<BR>To inflict pain, to torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फ
दृम्फ<BR>r. 6th cl. (दृम्फति)<BR>To pain, to torture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=420" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्फू|दृंफू
दृम्फू<BR>f. (-म्फूः)<BR>A snake in general.<BR>E.<BR>दृम्फ to give pain, affix कूः see दृम्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृम्भू
दृम्भू<BR>f. (-म्भूः)<BR>A snake, &c.: see दृम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश
दृश<BR>(औ ईर) औदृशिर r. 1st cl. (पश्यति)<BR>To see.<BR>With उत् prefixed,<BR>1 To see, to observe.<BR>2 To anticipate, to foresee.<BR>3 To doubt, to think doubtingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्
दृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>1 A seer, a looker.<BR>2 Wise, possessed of knowledge.<BR>f. (-दृक्)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix क्विप्; also दृशा and दृशि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशद्
दृशद्<BR>f. (-शद् or शत्)<BR>1 A stone, a rock.<BR>2 A flat stone for grinding condiments upon.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix अदि, augment षुक्, and ष changed to श; the crude form may also be दृषत् or दृषट्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशद्वती
दृशद्वती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The name of a river which forms the eastern boundary of the Āryavarta or holy land of the Hindus, running on the north-east of Delhi.<BR>2 A name of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दृशद् a stone or rock, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशा
दृशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The eye.<BR>E.<BR>see दृश, टाप् being here added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशाकाङ्क्ष्य|दृशाकांक्ष्य|दृशाकाङ्क्ष्यं
दृशाकाङ्क्ष्य<BR>n. (-ङ्क्ष्य)<BR>A lotus, or rather a kind of nelumbium.<BR>E.<BR>दृश the eye, काङ्क्ष्य to desire, with आङ् prefix, and यत् affix; desirable as an object of comparison to the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशान|दृशानं|दृशानः
दृशान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Light.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The name of an Asura; also VIROCANA.<BR>2 A holy or spiritual teacher.<BR>3 A king, a ruler, a protector or cherisher of the world.<BR>4 A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, आनच् Uṇādi affix; by whom or which sight, &c. is enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशि|दृशिः
दृशि<BR>f. (-शिः or शी)<BR>The eye.<BR>2 A Śāstra.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix कि, ङीष् is optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृशोपम|दृशोपमं
दृशोपम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The white lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>E.<BR>दृशा the eye, उपमा resemblance; what resembles the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्य|दृश्यं|दृश्यः
दृश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>1 Visible, to be seen.<BR>2 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>(In Arithmetic,) A given quantity or number.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृश्यत्व
दृश्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Vision, sight.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृषद्
दृषद्<BR>f. (-षद् or षत्)<BR>1 A stone or rock.<BR>2 A flat stone or plate on which spices, &c. are ground.<BR>E.<BR>दॄ to divide, Uṇādi affix अदि, and षुक् augment; also दृशद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्ट|दृष्टं
दृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Seen, visible, apparent.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Obvious danger or calamity.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टकूट
दृष्टकूट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A riddle, an enigma.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्ट seen, कूट trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टदोष
दृष्टदोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Found out, exposed, detected.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्ट, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टरजस्
दृष्टरजस्<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A girl arrived at puberty.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्ट seen, (by whom,) and रजस् the menstrual discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टवत्|दृष्टवन्त्
दृष्टवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Seeing, beholding, having seen.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टान्त|दृष्टांत|दृष्टान्तः
दृष्टान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A science, a Śāstra.<BR>2 An example, an illustration.<BR>3 Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्ट obvious or seen, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टि|दृष्टिः
दृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Sight, seeing.<BR>3 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>4 The sight of the eye, the pupil.<BR>5 Aspect, (of the stars.)<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिकृत्
दृष्टिकृत्<BR>n. (-कृत्)<BR>A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि the eye, कृ to make, here meaning resemble; affix क्विप् and तुक् added; also with क्त affix दृष्टिकृत n. (-तं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिगुण|दृष्टिगुणः
दृष्टिगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A butt, a mark for archers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि the eye, and गुण object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिनिपात
दृष्टिनिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A look, a look at or on.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि, and निपात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपात|दृष्टिपातः
दृष्टिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A look, a glance.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिपूत
दृष्टिपूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kept pure by the sight, i.<BR>E.<BR>watched, that no impropriety is committed, or impurity contracted.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि, and पूत purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिबन्धु|दृष्टिबंधु|दृष्टिबन्धुः
दृष्टिबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A fire-fly.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि sight, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविक्षेप|दृष्टिविक्षेपः
दृष्टिविक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A leer, a side glance.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि the eye, विक्षेप casting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्टिविष|दृष्टिविषः
दृष्टिविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>दृष्टि, and विष poison, venomous in his look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृष्ट्वा
दृष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having seen.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृह
दृह<BR>r. 1st cl. (दर्हति) also (इ) दृहि r. 1st cl. (दृंहति)<BR>To grow, to increase, to prosper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दृहित|दृहितः
दृहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Grown, increased, thriven.<BR>E.<BR>दृह to grow, affix क्त with इट् inserted; also from दृहि, दृहित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दॄ
दॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (दृणाति)<BR>To tear, to rend, to divide or pull to pieces.<BR>r. 1st cl. (दरति)<BR>To fear, to dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दे
दे<BR>(ङ) देङ् r. 1st cl. (दयते)<BR>To preserve, to cherish or protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देदीप्यमान|देदीप्यमानः
देदीप्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shining repeatedly or intensely, glowing, blazing.<BR>E.<BR>दीप to kindle, intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देय|देयं
देय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be given, fit or proper for a gift.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, यत् affix, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव|देवं|देवः
देव<BR>(ऋ) देष्ट r. 1st cl. (देवते)<BR>To sport or play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देव|देवं|देवः
देव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A deity, a god.<BR>2 A king, in poetical language.<BR>3 A husband's brother: see देवृ.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 A fool, a dolt.<BR>6 A child.<BR>7 A man following any particular line or business.<BR>8 A spear-man, a lancer.<BR>9 Emulation, wish to excel or overcome.<BR>10 Sport, play.<BR>11 A term or surname applicable to a Brahman; also to a man of the Kayeth class.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>An organ of sense.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis).<BR>2 A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A goddess, the wife of any deity or divine being.<BR>2 A name very commonly applied to the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3 A queen, one who has been consecrated as well as the king, (in theatrical language chiefly.)<BR>4 A respectful epithet or title applied to a woman of the first class.<BR>5 Worship, reverence.<BR>6 A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>7 Another plant: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, (in heaven, &c.) affix अच्, fem. affix टाप् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवक|देवकः
देवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Who or what sports or plays.<BR>2 Divine, celestial, like a deity.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A proper name, the maternal grandfather of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, ण्वुल् affix; or देव, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकर्द्दम|देवकर्दम|देवकर्द्दमः
देवकर्द्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A fragrant paste of sandal, agallochum, camphor, and safflower.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and कर्द्दम mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकात्मजा
देवकात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>देवक as above, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकार्य्य|देवकार्य
देवकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Worship of, or oblations to the gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and कार्य्य business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=421" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकाष्ठ|देवकाष्ठं
देवकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A kind of pine: (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकिरी
देवकिरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the female personifications of the modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकी
देवकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>DEVAKĪ, the daughter of DEVAKA, wife of VASUDEVA, and mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>देवक, अञ् patronymick affix, fem. affix ङीष्; also with the vowel changed by the affix, दैवकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीनन्दन|देवकीनंदन|देवकीनन्दनः
देवकीनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>देवकी as above, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीय
देवकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Divine, belonging or relating to a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकीसूनु|देवकीसूनुः
देवकीसूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The deity KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>देवकी as above, and सूनु a son; also similar compounds, as देवकीनन्दन, and देवकीपुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुण्ड|देवकुंड
देवकुण्ड<BR>n. (ण्डं)<BR>A natural spring.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and कुण्ड a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुल|देवकुलं
देवकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, and कुल a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवकुसुम|देवकुसुमं
देवकुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and कुसुम a flower; fit for a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखात|देवखातं
देवखात<BR>mfn. (-तं)<BR>1 A cave or hollow among mountains.<BR>2 A natural pond or reservoir.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and खात dug; not the work of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातक|देवखातकं
देवखातक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A natural pond or one in front of a temple.<BR>2 A natural cavern, a grotto.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, खात dug, and कन् affix; dug by divine hands, or in honour of a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवखातविल|देवखातविलं
देवखातविल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A cavern, a chasm.<BR>E.<BR>देवखात, and विल a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगान्धारी
देवगान्धारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs, or female personifications of the modes of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगायन|देवगायनः
देवगायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Gandharba, a celestial quirister.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, and गायन a singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगिरी
देवगिरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगुरु|देवगुरुः
देवगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and गुरु teacher; the preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवगृह|देवगृहं
देवगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>1 A celestial or planetary sphere, the dwelling of the gods.<BR>2 A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देब, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवचिकित्सक
देवचिकित्सक<BR>m. du. (-कौ)<BR>The two sons of AŚVINĪ, and physicians of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, and चिकित्सक a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवच्छन्द|देवच्छंद|देवच्छन्दः
देवच्छन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A garland or necklace of pearls, &c. composed of 100 or 103 strings.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and छदि to cover, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजग्ध|देवजग्धं
देवजग्ध<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and जग्ध eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवजग्धक|देवजग्धकं
देवजग्धक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>कन् pleonastic, added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवट|देवटः
देवट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>An artist, an artisan.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to sport, अटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवट्टी
देवट्टी<BR>f. (-ट्टी)<BR>A sort of gull, (Larus ridibundus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतरु|देवतरुः
देवतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The holy fig tree.<BR>2 A tree of Svarga or paradise, the Mandāra tree.<BR>3 The tree of plenty.<BR>4 Any venerable and ancient tree; usually the place of assembling in a village.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवता
देवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A god, a deity or divine being.<BR>2 Divinity: see देवत्व.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, तल् affix of the abstract: in the first case, अन् added; of whom the attribute is divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतागार|देवतागारः
देवतागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देवता, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताड|देवताडः
देवताड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A kind of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR>2 A name of Rāhu, the personified ascending node.<BR>3 A name of fire.<BR>4 A sort of creeper: see घोषक.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, &c. तड to torment, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताडक|देवताडकः
देवताडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A grass: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to देवताड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताधिप|देवताधिपः
देवताधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>देवता a deity, अधिप ruler or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवताभ्यर्च्चन|देवताभ्यर्चन
देवताभ्यर्च्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worshipping an idol.<BR>E.<BR>देवता, and अभ्यर्च्चन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतायतन
देवतायतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देवता, and आयतन dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवतीर्थ
देवतीर्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>The part of the hand sacred to the gods, the tips of the fingers.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and तीर्थ a shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवत्व|देवत्वं
देवत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Divinity, the abstract attribute of divine being.<BR>2 Identification with a deity, deification.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and त्व abstract affix; also with तल्, देवता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्त|देवदत्तः
देवदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given by the gods, god-given.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 The younger brother of the legislator Buddha.<BR>2 The conch of ARJUNA.<BR>3 One of the vital airs, that which is exhaled in yawning.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and दत्त given; the name is often used in grammatical and other examples, in the place of some one, a certain person, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदत्ताग्रज|देवदत्ताग्रजः
देवदत्ताग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>देवदत्त as above, and अग्रज elder born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदानी
देवदानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of creeper, commonly Hātīghoṣa.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and दान a gift, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदारु|देवदारुः
देवदारु<BR>mn. (-रुः-रु)<BR>A species of pine, (Pinus devadaru); in Bengal it is usually applied to the Uvaria longifolia, and in the Peninsula to another tree, (Erythroxylon sideroxylloides.)<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and दारु timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदासी
देवदासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A courtezan, especially one employed as a dancer, &c. in a temple.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and दासी a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदीप|देवदीपः
देवदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An eye.<BR>E.<BR>देव an organ of sense, and दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदूती
देवदूती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A female messenger of the gods.<BR>2 A sort of plant; also मधुकुक्कुटी.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and दूती a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवदेव|देवदेवः
देवदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>देव god, repeated; god of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवद्रोणी
देवद्रोणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The procession of a deity or idol.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, द्रुण to go, affixes घञ् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवद्र्यञ्च्|देवद्र्यंच्
देवद्र्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्)<BR>Approaching or adoring a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव an idol, अञ्च to go to or to worship, affix क्विप्, and द्रि inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधान्य|देवधान्यं
देवधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>A sort of grain cultivated in many parts of Hindūstan, (Andropogon saccharatus.)<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and धान्य corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवधूप|देवधूपः
देवधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A fragrant resin, (Bdellium,) used in the incense.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन्
देवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>A husband's brother.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, अन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवन|देवनं|देवनः
देवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sport, play, pastime, &c.<BR>2 Emulation, desire to excel or overcome.<BR>3 Affair, business, profession.<BR>4 Gaming.<BR>5 Splendour, lustre, beauty.<BR>6 Light.<BR>7 Praise.<BR>8 Motion.<BR>9 Grief, sorrow.<BR>10 A garden, a play or pleasure ground.<BR>11 A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">Page423</a>] lotus.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A die or dice.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Sport, wanton sport or pastime.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, &c. affix ल्युट्, or युच्, fem. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=422" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनन्दिन्|देवनंदिन्
देवनन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>One of INDRA'S doorkeepers.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and नन्दिन् who pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनल|देवनलः
देवनल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Arundo bengalensis.)<BR>E.<BR>देव, and नल a reed; also read देवानल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनारक
देवनारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A superhuman being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिकाय|देवनिकायः
देवनिकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A heaven, a paradise, the residence of a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and निकाय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दक|देवनिंदक|देवनिन्दकः
देवनिन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A heretic, an unbeliever, a reviler of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and निन्दक a calumniator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिन्दा
देवनिन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Heresy, atheism.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and निन्दा abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवनिर्म्मित|देवनिर्मित
देवनिर्म्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Natural, created.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and निर्म्मित made by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपति|देवपतिः
देवपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपत्नी
देवपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>1 The wife of a deity.<BR>2 Sweet potatoe.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, &c. and पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपथ|देवपथः
देवपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Heaven, the firmament, the celestial path or way.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and पथिन् a road, final affix अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपद
देवपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The royal presence.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and पद for पाद a foot; also देवपाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपर
देवपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Addicted to play.<BR>2 Future, what will be, (predestined, &c.) see दैवपर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपशु|देवपशुः
देवपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>An animal consecrated to a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुत्त्री
देवपुत्त्री<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>A medicinal plant: see पृक्का.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and पुत्त्री a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवपुर्
देवपुर्<BR>f. (-पुः)<BR>The capital of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, and पुर् a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रतिमा
देवप्रतिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>An idol.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and प्रतिमा image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवप्रश्न|देवप्रश्नः
देवप्रश्न<BR>n. (-श्नं)<BR>Astrology, consulting the stars or gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवबल्लभ
देवबल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria, Rox.) see युन्नाग.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and बल्लभ a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्रह्मन्
देवब्रह्मन्<BR>m. (-ह्मा)<BR>A name of the Muni NĀRADA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ; BRAHMĀ amongst the saints and demigods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवब्राह्मण|देवब्राह्मणः
देवब्राह्मण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A venerable Brahman, one esteemed by the deities.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and ब्राह्मण a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभवन|देवभवनं
देवभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The holy fig tree.<BR>2 Paradise.<BR>3 A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and भवन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभाज्
देवभाज्<BR>mfn. (-क् or ग्)<BR>Belonging to a god.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and भाज् what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभू
देवभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 Svarga or paradise.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूति|देवभूतिः
देवभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The Ganges of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and भूति being, abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवभूय|देवभूयं
देवभूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Divinity, godhead.<BR>2 Inferior deification or identification with a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and भूय being, becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमञ्जर
देवमञ्जर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The jewel of KṚṢṆA suspended on his breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमणि|देवमणिः
देवमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The jewel of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A twist of hair on a horse's neck.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृ
देवमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A name of ADITI.<BR>E.<BR>दव, and मातृ a mother; the mother of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमातृक|देवमातृकः
देवमातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Watered by rain, (corn, land, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>देव a cloud, मातृ a mother, and कप् affix; cherished by the clouds as by a parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमानक|देवमानकः
देवमानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The jewel worn by KṚṢṆA: see कौस्तुभ.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, मान respect, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवमास|देवमासः
देवमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The eighth month of pregnancy; also देवमासक.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्
देवयज्<BR>m. (-यक्)<BR>A worshipper of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and यज् to worship, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयजि|देवयजिः
देवयजि<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>1 A worshipper of the gods.<BR>2 A Muni.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and यजि who worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयज्ञ|देवयज्ञः
देवयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>The Homa or burnt sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and यज्ञ sacrifice; the sacrifice appropriated to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयात्रा
देवयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>The procession of a deity or idol, or sacred festival when the images are carried in procession.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयान|देवयानं
देवयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The car or vehicle of a god.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The daughter of ŚUKRA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयितृ
देवयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>देव to play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयु|देवयुः
देवयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>1 Pious, righteous, virtuous.<BR>2 Frequenting holy festivals.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, या to go, Uṇādi affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवयोनि|देवयोनिः
देवयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A superhuman being, a demon or demigod.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर|देवरः
देवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A husband's brother, especially his younger brother.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, &c. affix अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरथ|देवरथः
देवरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The car or vehicle of a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवराज|देवराजः
देवराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, राजन् a king, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरात|देवरातः
देवरात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A sort of crane.<BR>2 The name of a king; also Parikṣit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवरूपिन्
देवरूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>Godlike, of divine form.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and रूप form, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवर्षि|देवर्षिः
देवर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi, a saint of the celestial class, as NĀRADA, ATRI, MARĪCĪ, BHARADVĀJA, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, BHṚGU, VASIṢṬHA, PRACETAS; also BHĀRATA, TUMBURU, KAṆĀDA, and others.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and ऋषि a saint: see ऋषि, and राजर्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवल|देवलः
देवल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An attendant upon an idol; a Brahman of an inferior order, who subsists upon the offerings made to the images which he attends, and who conducts the ceremonies of all sorts of people for hire.<BR>2 A Muni; according to some authorities, a name of NĀRADA; to others, of a different saint, who is also a legislator, the son of ASITA and also named AṢṬAVAKRA.<BR>3 A husband's brother: see देवर.<BR>4 A holy or virtuous man.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, ला to bring, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलक|देवलकः
देवलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The attendant on an idol: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to देवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलता
देवलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Double jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवलोक|देवलोकः
देवलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Heaven or paradise.<BR>2 Any one of the seven superior worlds, from earth to the highest or Satya loka, in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">Page424</a>] opposition to those below the earth.<BR>3 The particular sphere or heaven of any divinity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=423" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववक्त्र|देववक्त्रं
देववक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>Fire or its deity AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and वक्त्र a face, here implying, mouth; the mouth of the gods, eating or consuming the oblations made to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववल्लभ|देववल्लभः
देववल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A tree: see पुन्नाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर
देववर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A superior or supreme deity.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A divine boon or blessing.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववर्द्धकि
देववर्द्धकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>A name of VIŚVAKARMĀ, the divine architect.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, वर्द्धकि a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देववृक्ष|देववृक्षः
देववृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>2 A tree of heaven or paradise.<BR>3 A plant yielding a fragrant resin, (Bdellium.)<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवव्रत|देवव्रतः
देवव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A worshipper of the gods.<BR>2 A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Any obligation or vow of a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and व्रत religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवश्रुत|देवश्रुतः
देवश्रुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A god.<BR>2 A sacred treatise or branch of scripture.<BR>3 A name of NĀRADA.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभा
देवसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>An assembly of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसभ्य|देवसभ्यः
देवसभ्य<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>1 A player, a gambler, a frequenter of clubs or assemblies.<BR>2 An attendant on a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव sport in general, or gambling, सभा an assembly, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसन्ध|देवसंध
देवसन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Divine, relating to a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and सन्ध connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसहा
देवसहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A small shrub: see सहदेवा.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, सह to bear, affix टाप् and अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसात्
देवसात्<BR>ind.<BR>In or on a deity, becoming as a deity, appropriate or offered to one.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसायुजय
देवसायुजय<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>1 Inferior deification, the state or being of the inferior gods.<BR>2 Absorption into or identification with a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a god, स with युज to join or be joined, affix क्विप्, देवसयुज् junction with a deity, ष्यञ् added, implying the state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसृष्टा
देवसृष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and सृष्ट created, made by the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेना
देवसेना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The daughter of INDRA.<BR>2 An army or host of celestials.<BR>E.<BR>देव INDRA or any deity, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवसेनापति|देवसेनापतिः
देवसेनापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of SKANDA.<BR>E.<BR>देवसेना as above, and पति ruler; commander of the hosts of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवस्व|देवस्वं
देवस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>The property applicable to religious purposes, endowments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>देव divine, and स्व wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाजीव|देवाजीवः
देवाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An attendant upon an idol, a low Brahman, subsisting by attendance upon an image, and upon the offerings made to it.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and आजीव who gets a livelihood; also with इनि added देवजीविन् m. (-वी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवात्मन्
देवात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>1 One with or identified with a deity.<BR>2 Belonging to a deity, consecrated, sacred.<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>देव, and आत्मन् the self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवानाम्प्रिय|देवानांप्रिय|देवानाम्प्रियः
देवानाम्प्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A goat.<BR>2 An ascetic, one who relinquishes or abandons the world.<BR>3 A fool, an ideot.<BR>E.<BR>देव in the second case plural, and प्रिय beloved; the beloved of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवान्न
देवान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Rice or food that has been first presented to an idol.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवापि|देवापिः
देवापि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>The son of PRATĪPA, supposed to be still alive, near the Sumeru mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाभीष्ट
देवाभीष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Sacred, dedicated to a deity.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Betel, (Piper betel.)<BR>E.<BR>देव, and अभीष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायतन|देवायतनं
देवायतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and आयतन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवायुध|देवायुधं
देवायुध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>The rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवालय|देवालयः
देवालय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A division of heaven, the residence of the gods.<BR>2 A temple.<BR>E.<BR>देव and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाला
देवाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>One of the female personifications of music.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and अल adapted to, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवार्ह|देवार्हं
देवार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-हं)<BR>Divine, worthy of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवावास|देवावासः
देवावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A temple.<BR>2 The holy fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवाश्व|देवाश्वः
देवाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The horse of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविक
देविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Appertaining to or derived from a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and ठच् affix; also देविय, and देविल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविका
देविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a river, the Sarju or Deva.<BR>E.<BR>देवी, and कन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देविल|देविलः
देविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious, just.<BR>2 Appertaining to a deity: see देविक.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवी
देवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>See देव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवीकोट्ट
देवीकोट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A town, the city of VĀṆA, probably DEVICOTTA, on the Coromandel coast.<BR>E.<BR>देवी a name of DURGĀ, and कोट्ट a house or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवृ
देवृ<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>1 A husband's brother, but especially his younger brother.<BR>2 The husband of a woman previously married.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, Uṇādi affix ऋण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेज्य|देवेज्यः
देवेज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and इज्य a teacher, the Guru or spiritual preceptor of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवेष्ट|देवेष्टः
देवेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Acceptable to the gods, wished for by them.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देवोद्यान|देवोद्यानं
देवोद्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sacred grove, one near a temple or consecrated to a deity.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश|देशः
देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A country, a region, whether inhabited or uninhabited.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>3 Institute, ordinance.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to point, to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशक|देशकः
देशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what shows, points out, describes, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A ruler, a governor.<BR>2 A guide.<BR>3 An instructor.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to command, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकारी
देशकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A mode of music, a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालविद्
देशकालविद्<BR>mfn. (-विद्)<BR>Knowing what is suited to time and place.<BR>E.<BR>देश, काल time, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशकालव्यवस्थित
देशकालव्यवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Regulated by time and place.<BR>E.<BR>देश, काल time, व्यवस्थित determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशदृष्ट
देशदृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Considered locally, judged as to place.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशधर्म्म|देशधर्म|देशधर्मः
देशधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Local law, the law or usage of the country.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and धर्म्म moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशरूप|देशरूपं
देशरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>देश ordinance, रूप form, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशव्यवहार|देशव्यवहारः
देशव्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Local usage, custom of the country.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and व्यवहार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=424" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशान्तर|देशांतर|देशान्तरं
देशान्तर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 A foreign country.<BR>2 Longitude or difference of longitude.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and अन्तर different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशापेक्ष
देशापेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Spying, searching out a land.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and अपेक्ष who inspects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिक|देशिकः
देशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A traveller, a stranger, a sojourner.<BR>2 A Guru or spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>देश a country, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशित
देशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Directed, commanded.<BR>2 Shown.<BR>3 Advised, instructed.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to show, and क्त affix, with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देशिन्
देशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 Of or belonging to a country.<BR>2 Showing, instructing, guiding.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The index or forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to show, affix णिनि or देश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देश्य|देश्यं|देश्यः
देश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>1 What is proper to be proved or ordered.<BR>2 Local.<BR>3 Present at any transaction, on the spot.<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>1 The postulate, the statement or exhibition of a question or argument.<BR>2 The fact or charge to be proved or substantiated.<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>An eyewitness of any thing, one who was on the spot.<BR>E.<BR>दिश to show or command, affix ण्यत्; or देश, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देष्णु|देष्णुः
देष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Difficult of subjection, untameable, intractable, ungovernable.<BR>2 Liberal in giving, a donor.<BR>m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>दा to give, &c. इष्णुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देह|देहं|देहः
देह<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>दिह to collect together, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहकोष|देहकोषः
देहकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The skin.<BR>2 A feather, a wing.<BR>E.<BR>देह body, and कोष a sheath or covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहक्षय|देहक्षयः
देहक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Disease, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, and क्षय a wasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहच्युत
देहच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Separated or detached from the body, (as excrement or the spirit, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>देह, and च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहत्याग|देहत्यागः
देहत्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Voluntary death.<BR>2 Death in general.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and त्याग leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहद|देहदः
देहद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधारक|देहधारकं
देहधारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bone.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, and धारक sustainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधि|देहधिः
देहधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A wing.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, धा to have, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहधृज्
देहधृज्<BR>m. (-धृक्)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, धृज् to pervade, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहभृत्
देहभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>1 Living, being.<BR>2 Embodied, corporeal.<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>Life, vitality.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, भृत् what has or supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहयात्रा
देहयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Food.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, यात्रा proceeding, (to or by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहला
देहला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, ला to seize, affix उ, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहलि|देहलिः
देहलि<BR>f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>1 The threshold of a door, the lower part of the wooden frame of a door, or a raised terrace in front of it.<BR>E.<BR>देह here said to imply plastering of cow-dung, &c. ला to have or get, affix कि or क, and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहसार|देहसारः
देहसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहवत्|देहवन्त्
देहवत्<BR>mfn. (वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Corporeal, inhabiting a body.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहात्मवादिन्
देहात्मवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A Cārvāka, a materialist.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and आत्मन् the soul, and वादिन् who maintains; asserting that the body and soul are one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहावरण
देहावरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Armour.<BR>2 Dress.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and आवरण screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहिका
देहिका<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of insect, (a flea.)<BR>E.<BR>देह the body, affix ठन्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

देहिन्
देहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Corporeal, embodied, having body.<BR>2 Living, a living being.<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>The spirit.<BR>E.<BR>देह, and हनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दै
दै<BR>(प) दैप् r. 1st cl. (दायति)<BR>To purify or cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैतेय|दैतेयः
दैतेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A demon, an Asura, the Titan or giant of Hindu mythology.<BR>E.<BR>दिति the mother of the giants, and ढक् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्य|दैत्यः
दैत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A Daitya or demon: see the preceding.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 A perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>2 A drug: see चण्डा.<BR>3 Spirituous liquor.<BR>4 The wife of a demon.<BR>E.<BR>दिति, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यगुरु|दैत्यगुरुः
दैत्यगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A name of ŚUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य and गुरु a teacher; the spiritual preceptor of the Daityas, or Titans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यदेव|दैत्यदेवः
दैत्यदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of VARUṆA, deity of the waters.<BR>2 Air or wind personified.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य a demon, and देव a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यपुरोधस्
दैत्यपुरोधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>A name of ŚUKRA.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य, and पुरोधस् a family priest: see दैत्यगुरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यपुरोहित
दैत्यपुरोहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of ŚUKRA, regent of Venus.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य, and पुरोहित a family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यमातृ
दैत्यमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A name of DITI, the mother of the Titanic race of Daityas.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य, and मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यमेदजा
दैत्यमेदजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य, मेद marrow, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्ययुग|दैत्ययुगं
दैत्ययुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An age of the demons, consisting of 12,000 divine years, or the sum of the four Yugas or ages of men.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य a demon, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्यारि|दैत्यारिः
दैत्यारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A deity in general.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य, and अरि a foe; the enemy of the Daityas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैत्याहोरात्र|दैत्याहोरात्रं|दैत्याहोरात्रः
दैत्याहोरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A day and night or the demons, being a year of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>दैत्य a demon, अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैन|दैनं
दैन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Diurnal, daily, relating to a day.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Poverty, wretchedness.<BR>E.<BR>दीन or दिन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनन्दिन|दैनंदिन|दैनन्दिनं
दैनन्दिन<BR>mfn. (-तः-नी-नं)<BR>Diurnal, quotidian.<BR>E.<BR>दिनदिन day by day, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनन्दिनप्रलय|दैनंदिनप्रलय|दैनन्दिनप्रलयः
दैनन्दिनप्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Destruction of the world after fifteen years of BRAHMĀ'S age.<BR>E.<BR>दैनन्दिन, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनार|दैनारं
दैनार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Bought with a Dinar, of the value of one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दीनार, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैनिक
दैनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Dirunal, of or relating to a day.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A day's hire or wages.<BR>E.<BR>दिन a day, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैन्य|दैन्यं
दैन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Meanness, covetousness.<BR>2 Poverty, humbleness.<BR>E.<BR>दीन a pauper, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैप|दैपं
दैप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दीप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैर्घ्य|दैर्घ्यं
दैर्घ्य<BR>n. (-र्ध्यं)<BR>Length.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव|दैवं|दैवः
दैव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Of or relating to divinity or a deity, divine, celestial, &c.<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>Destiny, fate, fortune.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The part of the hand sacred to the gods; the tips of the fingers, (some exclude the thumbs.)<BR>2 One of the forms of marriage; the gift of a daughter at a sacrifice to the officiating priest.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A division of medicine, the medical use of charms, prayers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and अञ् affix of reference or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=425" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकर्म्मन्|दैवकर्मन्
दैवकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Burnt-offering, oblations to the gods.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and कर्म्म rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकी
दैवकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>देवक father of the lady, affix of descent अण्, fem. affix ङीष्: see देवकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकीनन्दन|दैवकीनन्दनः
दैवकीनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>दैवकी as above, नन्दन a son; also देवकीनन्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवकोविद
दैवकोविद<BR>mf. (-दः-दा)<BR>A conjuror or fortune-teller.<BR>E.<BR>दैव fortune, and कोविद skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवचिन्तक|दैवचिंतक|दैवचिन्तकः
दैवचिन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fatalist.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and चिन्तक who thinks of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवचिन्ता
दैवचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Fatalism, reliance on fate.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and चिन्ता thinking; also दैवचिन्तनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवज्ञ|दैवज्ञः
दैवज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Prophetic, foretelling, acquainted with fate.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>A female fortune-teller.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवत|दैवतः
दैवत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>1 Of or relating to a god.<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 A god, a deity.<BR>2 An idol.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A number of gods.<BR>E.<BR>देवता a deity, अण् pleonastick or referential affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदीप|दैवदीपः
दैवदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 A heavenly lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and दीप a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवदुर्विपाक|दैवदुर्विपाकः
दैवदुर्विपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hardness of fortune, unpropitiousness^1 of fate.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and दुर्विपाक unfavourableness.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवपर|दैवपरः
दैवपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Fated, willed, predestined.<BR>2 Trusting to fate, a fatalist.<BR>E.<BR>दैव fate, &c. पर after, according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवप्रश्न|दैवप्रश्नः
दैवप्रश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>Astrology, fortune-telling.<BR>E.<BR>दैव fate, &c. प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयुग|दैवयुगं
दैवयुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An age of the gods or immortals: see दैत्ययुग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवयोग|दैवयोगः
दैवयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The occurrence of any unforeseen event, the intervention of destiny.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and योग juncture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलक|दैवलकः
दैवलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The servant or worshipper of an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवलेखक|दैवलेखकः
दैवलेखक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astrologer, a fortune-teller.<BR>E.<BR>दैव fate, लिख to write, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैववाणी
दैववाणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A voice from heaven.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवाकरि|दैवाकरिः
दैवाकरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 YAMA.<BR>2 SATURN.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>YAMUNĀ.<BR>E.<BR>दिवाकर the sun, and इञ patron. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवात्
दैवात्<BR>ind.<BR>By chance, by accident, unavoidably, fatally.<BR>E.<BR>the 5th case of दैव used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवानुरोधिन्
दैवानुरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Subject or obedient to the gods.<BR>E.<BR>दैव divine (will), अनुरोधिन् assenting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवायत्त
दैवायत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Dependant upon destiny.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and आयत्त subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवासुर|दैवासुरं
दैवासुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The natural enmity between the gods and Asuras.<BR>E.<BR>देव, and असुर, with अण् added in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवाहोरात्र|दैवाहोरात्रः
दैवाहोरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A day of the gods, the human year: see दैत्याहोरात्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैविक|दैविकः
दैविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or relating to the gods, divine, deific, &c.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवोढा
दैवोढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A woman married according to the Daiva ritual.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and ऊढा married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैवोपहत
दैवोपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ill-fated, unfortunate, unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>दैव, and उपहत struck by; also with कन्, दैवोपहतकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैव्य|दैव्यं
दैव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Fate, fortune.<BR>E.<BR>देव a deity, and यञ् affix: see दैव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैशिक|दैशिकं|दैशिकः
दैशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Provincial, national, belonging to a country, produced in it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>देश, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिक|दैष्टिकः
दैष्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Fated, predestined.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A predestinarian, a fatalist.<BR>E.<BR>दिष्ट fate, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैष्टिकता
दैष्टिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fatalism, predestinarianism.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to दैष्टिक; also with त्व, दैष्टिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दैहिक|दैहिकं
दैहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Corporeal, bodily.<BR>E.<BR>देहिक, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दो
दो<BR>r. 4th cl. (द्यति)<BR>To cut, to divide: अव is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोग
दोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःशिखर|दोःशिखरं
दोःशिखर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The shoulder.<BR>E.<BR>दोस्, and शिखर crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोःसहस्रभृत्
दोःसहस्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>The name of a king, also called KĀRTAVĪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् an arm, महस्र a thousand, and भृत् possessing; having a thousand arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोग्धृ
दोग्धृ<BR>mfn. (-ग्धा-ग्ध्री-ग्धृ)<BR>1 A milker, who or what milks.<BR>2 What yields milk.<BR>m. (-ग्धा)<BR>1 A poet, a panegyrist, one who writes verses for hire or reward.<BR>2 A calf.<BR>3 A cowherd.<BR>f. (-ग्ध्री)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोदुल्यमान|दोदुल्यमानः
दोदुल्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Swinging or being swung repeatedly or violently.<BR>E.<BR>दुल to swing, intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोध|दोधः
दोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, घञ् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोधक|दोधकः
दोधक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A form of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोधूयमान|दोधूयमानः
दोधूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shaking or trembling violently.<BR>E.<BR>धू to shake, intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोरक|दोरकं|दोरकः
दोरक<BR>mf. (-रकः-रिका)<BR>A string for fastening the wires of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्गडु|दोर्गडुः
दोर्गडु<BR>mfn. (-डुः-डुः-डु)<BR>Crooked-armed, having a crippled or crooked arm.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् an arm, and गडु a cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्ग्रह|दोर्ग्रहः
दोर्ग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Pain in the arm.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् an arm, and ग्रह who takes or uses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्दण्ड|दोर्दंड|दोर्दण्डः
दोर्दण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The arm.<BR>E.<BR>दोस्, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्मध्य|दोर्मध्यं
दोर्मध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>The middle of the arm.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् the arm, and मध्य the centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोर्मूल|दोर्मूलं
दोर्मूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The armpit.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् the arm, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोल|दोलः
दोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Swinging.<BR>2 A festival on the 14th of Phalguna, the swinging of the juvenile KṚṢṆA.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला or ली)<BR>1 A litter, a swinging cot, a dooly.<BR>2 A swing.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>दुल to throw up or toss, to swing, affix अच्; fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलायमान|दोलायमानः
दोलायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Swinging, being swung.<BR>2 Doubting, perplexed, vacillating.<BR>E.<BR>दुल to swing, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोलिका
दोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A swing.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोष|दोषः
दोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Fault, defect, blemish.<BR>2 Sin, offence, transgression.<BR>3 Disorder of the humours of the body, or defect in the functions of bile, circulation, or wind.<BR>4 A calf.<BR>E.<BR>दुष to be defective, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषक|दोषकः
दोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to दोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषकल्पन
दोषकल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reprehending, condemning.<BR>E.<BR>दोष, and कल्पन attributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषग्राहिन्
दोषग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Malicious, malignant, censorious.<BR>E.<BR>दोष a fault, ग्रह to take, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषज्ञ|दोषज्ञः
दोषज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Knowing faults, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a teacher, a sage.<BR>2 A physician.<BR>E.<BR>दोष fault, defect, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषत्रय|दोषत्रयं
दोषत्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Vitiation of the three humours, bile, wind, and phlegm.<BR>2 Any combination of three defects.<BR>E.<BR>दोष, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=426" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषप्रसङ्ग|दोषप्रसंग|दोषप्रसंगः
दोषप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Censure, condemnation.<BR>E.<BR>दोष, and प्रसङ्ग attribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषभाज्
दोषभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Wrong, faulty, doing wrong, being defective or to blame.<BR>E.<BR>दोष, and भाज् who or what shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषवत्|दोषवन्त्
दोषवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Faulty, defective.<BR>2 Wicked.<BR>E.<BR>दोष, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषा
दोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The arm.<BR>ind. (-षा)<BR>1 By night, at night.<BR>2 At the beginning of the night.<BR>E.<BR>दम to tame, डोस् affix, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषाकर|दोषाकरः
दोषाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Defective, faulty.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>दोषा night, and कर a ray; or दोष, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातन|दोषातनः
दोषातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Nocturnal, by night.<BR>E.<BR>दोषा by night, द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषातिलक|दोषातिलकः
दोषातिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दोषा night, and तिलक excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषास्य|दोषास्यः
दोषास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>दोषा night, and आस्य a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिक|दोषिकः
दोषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Faulty, defective, bad.<BR>m. (कः)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>दोष defect, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषिन्
दोषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>1 Faulty, defective.<BR>2 Wicked, bad.<BR>E.<BR>टुष to be defective, affix घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोषैकदृश्
दोषैकदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Malevolent, censorious, discovering defects only.<BR>E.<BR>दोष a fault, एक one, alone, and दृश् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्
दोस्<BR>m. (-दोः)<BR>1 The arm.<BR>2 The side of a triangle, or square, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दम to subdue, affix डोम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्क
दोस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Worn, &c. on the arms.<BR>E.<BR>दोस् the arm, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोस्थ|दोस्थः
दोस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Placed on the arm.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 Play, sport.<BR>2 A player, one who sports or plays.<BR>3 Service.<BR>4 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>दु bad, स्था to stay, ड affix दुस्थ, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह|दोहः
दोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A milk-pail.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>3 Milking.<BR>4 Satisfaction, success.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, &c. affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहज|दोहजं
दोहज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>दोह milking, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहडिका
दोहडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Prākṛta metre, commonly Doha; a stanza of four lines, containing thirteen and eleven syllabic instants alternately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहद|दोहदं|दोहदः
दोहद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 The longing of a pregnant woman, especially as a sign of impregnation.<BR>E.<BR>दोह here said to mean satisfaction, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदलक्षण|दोहदलक्षणं
दोहदलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The fœtus, the embryo, sometimes confounded with the womb.<BR>2 The period of passing from one season of life to another, as from childhood to youth, from youth to manhood.<BR>E.<BR>दोहद longing, and लक्षण a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदवती
दोहदवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A pregnant woman longing for any thing.<BR>E.<BR>दोहद as above, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहदान्विता
दोहदान्विता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A pregnant woman longing for any thing.<BR>E.<BR>दोहद as above, and अन्वित attached or become inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहन|दोहनं
दोहन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A milk vessel, a milk pail.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Milking.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहल|दोहलः
दोहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Longing.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The Asoka tree.<BR>E.<BR>दोह satisfaction, and ल what gets: see दोहद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहलवती
दोहलवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A pregnant woman longing for any thing: see दोहदवती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहापनय|दोहापनयः
दोहापनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>दोह milking, अप below, णी to bring, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहिन्
दोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Milking, a milker.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोहीयस्
दोहीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Yielding a great abundance of milk.<BR>E.<BR>दोह milk, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दोह्य|दोह्यं
दोह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be milked, milkable.<BR>E.<BR>दुह to milk, ण्यत् affix; also दुह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौःसाधिक|दौःसाधिकः
दौःसाधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of head borough or beadle, the superintendent of a village.<BR>2 A doorkeeper, a warder, a porter.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् bad, difficult, साध to accomplish, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौकूल|दौकूलं|दौकूलः
दौकूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Covered with silk, (a car, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>दुकूल wove silk, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौत्य|दौत्यं
दौत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>An embassy or message.<BR>E.<BR>टूत a messenger, affix ष्यञ्: see दूत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौरात्म्य|दौरात्म्यं
दौरात्म्य<BR>n. (-त्म्यं)<BR>Wickedness, depravity.<BR>E.<BR>दुरात्मन् wicked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्गन्धि
दौर्गन्धि<BR>n. (-न्धिः)<BR>Fœtor, bad smell.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्गन्ध ill smelling, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्ग्य|दौर्ग्यं
दौर्ग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Difficulty, inaccessibility.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ग, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्जन्य|दौर्जन्यं|दौर्ज्जन्यं
दौर्जन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Wickedness, depravity, vileness.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ज्जन, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्ब्बल्य|दौर्बल्य|दौर्बल्यं|दौर्ब्बल्यं
दौर्ब्बल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Weakness, debility.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्ब्वल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्भागिणेय
दौर्भागिणेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of a woman disliked by her husband.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The daughter of such a woman.<BR>E.<BR>दर्मगा such a woman, ढक् affix and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्भाग्य|दौर्भाग्यं
दौर्भाग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Ill luck, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>दुर bad, भाग portion, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्मनस्य|दौर्मनस्यं|दौर्म्मनस्यं
दौर्मनस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 Evil disposition or thought.<BR>2 Despair.<BR>3 Affliction, distress.<BR>E.<BR>दुर्मनस्, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्वीण|दौर्वीणं|दौर्व्वीणं
दौर्वीण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The sap or juice of bent grass.<BR>2 A clean leaf.<BR>E.<BR>दूर्ब्बा bent grass, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौर्हृद|दौर्हृदं
दौर्हृद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Wish, desire, but especially the longing of pregnant women.<BR>E.<BR>दुर् pained, हृद the heart, affix अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौलेय|दौलेयः
दौलेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A turtle or tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>दूली a female tortoise, affix ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौल्मि|दौल्मिः
दौल्मि<BR>m. (-ल्मिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौवारिक|दौवारिकः
दौवारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A warder, a porter.<BR>E.<BR>दु bad, वार impediment, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौश्चर्म्म्य
दौश्चर्म्म्य<BR>n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>Paraphymosis, circumcision.<BR>E.<BR>दुश्चर्म्म, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्कुलेय|दौष्कुलेयः
दौष्कुलेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sprung of a bad or low family or race.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्कुल of a bad race, affix ढक्; also दुष्कुलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्ठव|दौष्ठवं
दौष्ठव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Badness, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्ठ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौष्मन्ति|दौष्मंति|दौष्मंतिः|दौष्मन्तिः
दौष्मन्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>A name of BHARAT, the first sole monarch of India.<BR>E.<BR>दुष्मन्त DUṢMANTA, husband of ŚAKUNTALĀ, and father to BHARATA, इञ् affix of descent; it is perhaps preferably read दौष्यन्ति from दुष्यन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दौहित्र|दौहित्रः
दौहित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A daughter's son.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A daughter's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>दुहितृ a daughter, affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावाक्षमा
द्यावाक्षमा<BR>f. always dual, (-मे)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>द्यौ heaven, क्षमा the earth, form irr.; also similar compounds, as द्यावापृथिवी, द्यावाभूमी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावापृथिवी
द्यावापृथिवी<BR>f. always dual, (-व्यौ)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>द्यौ heaven, and पृथिवी the earth: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यावाभूमी
द्यावाभूमी<BR>f. always dual. (-म्यौ)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>द्यौ, and भूमी the earth: see the two words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=427" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यु|द्युः
द्यु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (द्योति)<BR>1 To advance towards or against, to assail.<BR>2 To advance before or in front of, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यु|द्युः
द्यु<BR>m. (द्युः)<BR>A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>n. (द्यु)<BR>1 A day.<BR>2 Heaven, sky, æther.<BR>2 Heaven, paradise.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु to go to or towards, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युक|द्युकः
द्युक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युकारि|द्युकारिः
द्युकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युग|द्युगः
द्युग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युगण|द्युगणः
द्युगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A given term of days, as a month, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु, and गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत
द्युत<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्योतते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युत्
द्युत्<BR>m. (द्युत्)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युति|द्युतिः
द्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Beauty or splendour.<BR>3 A ray of light.<BR>4 Stimulating, exciting.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिकर|द्युतिकरः
द्युतिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Shining, bright.<BR>2 Handsome.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The polar star, or in mythology, the divine sage DHRUVA.<BR>E.<BR>द्युति light, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतित|द्युतितं
द्युतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Enlightened, illuminated, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, affix क्त; also with the vowel changed द्योतित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिमत्|द्युतिमन्त्
द्युतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Resplendent, bright.<BR>E.<BR>द्युति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युतिला
द्युतिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>द्युति beauty, and ला to possess, affix ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिवास|द्युनिवासः
द्युनिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Heavenly abode, heaven.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु, and निवास abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिवासिन्
द्युनिवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 A deity.<BR>2 A pious person.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु, and निवासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युनिश|द्युनिशं
द्युनिश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Day and night.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु a day, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युपति|द्युपतिः
द्युपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु a day or paradise, and पति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमणि|द्युमणिः
द्युमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु a day, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युमयी
द्युमयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The daughter of VIŚVAKARMA, and wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु a day, and मयट् affix of identity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युम्न|द्युम्नं
द्युम्न<BR>n. (-म्नं)<BR>1 Wealth, property, substance.<BR>2 Strength, power.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु day, म्ना to remember or regard, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युवन्
द्युवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Heaven.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु to go, (through the heavens,) Uṇādi affix कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्युषद्
द्युषद्<BR>m. (-षद् or षत्)<BR>1 A god, a deity.<BR>2 A planet.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु heaven, षद to go, affix क्विप्; it is also written द्युषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूत|द्यूतं|द्यूतः
द्यूत<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>Gaming, playing with dice, or any thing not possessing life.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकर|द्यूतकरः
द्यूतकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and कर who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकार|द्यूतकारः
द्यूतकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>2 A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत gaming, and कार who practices; also with कन् added, द्यूतकारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतकृत्
द्यूतकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and कृत् who practices: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतपूर्णिमा
द्यूतपूर्णिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Kārttika, (October-November,) the night of which is spent in games of chance, in honour of the goddess of fortune, LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत gaming, and पूर्णिमा day of full moon; also with अण् pleonastic affix added, and ङीष् fem. affix द्यूतपौर्णिमी, f. (-मी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतप्रतिपत्
द्यूतप्रतिपत्<BR>f. (-पत्)<BR>The first day of the moon's increase in Kartik, when BĀLĪ is to be venerated.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and प्रतिपद् the first lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवीज
द्यूतवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A Cowri, a small shell used as a coin in most parts of India.<BR>E.<BR>द्यत gaming, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतवृत्ति|द्यूतवृत्तिः
द्यूतवृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and वृत्ति subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूतसभा
द्यूतसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A gaming house or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यूताधिकारिन्
द्यूताधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The keeper of a gaming house.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत, and अधिकारिन् who superintends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यून|द्यूनं
द्यून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Playing, sportive.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The seventh sign of the zodiac, reckoning^1 from that which the sun enters.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to play, &c. affix क्त.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यै
द्यै<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्यायति)<BR>To despise, to reprove, to treat or name with contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यै
द्यै<BR>ind.<BR>Fie, for shame.<BR>E.<BR>द्यै, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यो
द्यो<BR>f. (द्यौ)<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 Heaven, sky.<BR>E.<BR>दिव to sport, Uṇādi affix डो; where the gods, &c. sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योत|द्योतः
द्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Sunshine, light, lustre, heat.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतन|द्योतनं|द्योतनः
द्योतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>Bright, shining.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 Making manifest.<BR>3 Illumination.<BR>4 An illumination.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>द्यूत to shine, affix ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतमान
द्योतमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shining, bright, radiant.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतयमान
द्योतयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Enlightening, irradiating.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to shine, causal v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतित|द्योतितं
द्योतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Enlightened, &c.<BR>2 Shining.<BR>E.<BR>द्युत to light, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योतितप्रभ
द्योतितप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Resplendent.<BR>E.<BR>द्योतित, and प्रभा splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योभूमि|द्योभूमिः
द्योभूमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A bird.<BR>f. du. (-मी)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>द्यो heaven, and भूमि the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्योषद्
द्योषद्<BR>m. (-षद्-षत्)<BR>A deity, a celestial.<BR>E.<BR>द्यो heaven, षद् to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्यौत्र|द्यौत्त्रं
द्यौत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Light, splendor.<BR>2 Much or forked lightning.<BR>E.<BR>द्यु for दिव to shine, Uṇādi affix ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रगड|द्रगडः
द्रगड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A kettle drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रङ्खण
द्रङ्खण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A measure or weight, a Tola.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रङ्ग|द्रङ्गः
द्रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A city, a town.<BR>E.<BR>द्रम to go, affix गन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढिमन्
द्रढिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Firmness, hardness, heaviness.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ hard, firm, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रढिष्ठ|द्रढिष्ठः
द्रढिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Hardest, very hard or firm, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दृढ with the superlative affix, इष्ठन् and the liquid substituted for the vowel; also with ईयसुन् affix द्रढीयस् (-यान्-यसी-यः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रप्स|द्रप्सः
द्रप्स<BR>mn. (-प्सः-प्सं)<BR>Thin or diluted curds.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to please, affix स; also त्रप्स and द्रप्सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रप्स्य|द्रप्स्यं
द्रप्स्य<BR>n. (-प्सां)<BR>Thin or diluted curds.<BR>E.<BR>दृप to please, affix स्यः or it is derived from तृप to be satisfied, त being changed to द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रम
द्रम<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्रमति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव|द्रवः
द्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Dropping, oozing.<BR>2 Flowing.<BR>3 Fluid, liquid.<BR>4 Fused, liquefied, melted.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 Flight, retreat.<BR>3 Sport, amusement.<BR>4 Juice, essence, exudation.<BR>5 Fusion, liquefaction.<BR>6 Decoction.<BR>7 Dropping, distilling, trickling.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, to go out of, to drop, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवज|द्रवजः
द्रवज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Treacle.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=428" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवण|द्रवणं
द्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Dropping, exuding.<BR>3 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवत्|द्रवन्त्
द्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>1 Trickling, oozing.<BR>2 Running, flowing.<BR>3 Going.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 A medicinal plant, (Anthericum tuberosum.)<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवत्व|द्रवत्वं
द्रवत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Fluidity, natural or artificial.<BR>2 Distillation.<BR>3 Fusion.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, and त्व affix; also with तल्, द्रवता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवरसा
द्रवरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Lac.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवाधार|द्रवाधारः
द्रवाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small vessel, a receiver.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव juice, distillation, &c. and आधार what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविड|द्रविडः
द्रविड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A man of an outcaste tribe, descended from a degraded Kṣatriya.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविण|द्रविणं
द्रविण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Wealth, property, thing, substance.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 Strength, power.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, इनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणनाशन|द्रविणनाशनः
द्रविणनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>द्रविण strength, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविणोदास्
द्रविणोदास्<BR>m. (-दाः)<BR>AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>द्रविण, and दास् who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीकरण|द्रवीकरणं
द्रवीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Liquefying, melting.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव fluid, करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीकृत
द्रवीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Melted, liquefied.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवीभूत
द्रवीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fluid, liquefied, fused.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रवेतर
द्रवेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hard, solid, congealed.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव, and इतर reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्य|द्रव्यं
द्रव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Fit, proper, right, what is or ought to be.<BR>2 Derived from or relating to a tree.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Wealth, property.<BR>2 Substance, thing, the receptacle or substratum of properties, &c.<BR>3 Elementary substance, nine kinds of which are reckoned: viz. earth, water, fire, air, æther, time, space, soul, and intellect.<BR>4 Brass.<BR>5 A stake, a wager.<BR>6 A drug, a medicament, any thing used in medicine.<BR>7 Anointing, plastering.<BR>8 Lac, the animal dye.<BR>9 Extract, gum, resin, &c. derived from vegetables.<BR>10 Modesty, propriety.<BR>11 Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यक|द्रव्यकः
द्रव्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A carrier or taker of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यप्रयोजन
द्रव्यप्रयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Use or employment of any article.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and प्रयोजन purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यमय
द्रव्यमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Material.<BR>2 Having or holding any thing.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्ययज्ञ
द्रव्ययज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Offering oblations, sacrifice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यवत्|द्रव्यवन्त्
द्रव्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-ववी-वत्)<BR>Rich, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यशुद्धि|द्रव्यशुद्धिः
द्रव्यशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Cleansing or purification of any soiled or defiled article.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसंस्कार|द्रव्यसंस्कारः
द्रव्यसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Consecration of articles for sacrifice.<BR>2 Purification or cleansing of any articles soiled or defiled.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and संस्कार perfectioning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसञ्चय|द्रव्यसंचय
द्रव्यसञ्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Accumulation of property.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and सञ्चय collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यसिद्धि|द्रव्यसिद्धिः
द्रव्यसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Acquirement of wealth.<BR>2 Effecting any thing by wealth.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यहस्त
द्रव्यहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Holding any thing in the hand.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रव्यार्ज्जन|द्रव्यार्जन
द्रव्यार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gain, acquisition, acquiring property.<BR>E.<BR>द्रव्य, and अर्ज्जन acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टव्य
द्रष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be seen, visible, apparent.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, तव्य affix, and ऋ changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रष्टृ
द्रष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what sees, a spectator.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रा
द्रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (द्राति)<BR>1 To fly, to run away.<BR>2 To be ashamed or spoiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्
द्राक्<BR>ind.<BR>Instantly, immediately, soon, shortly.<BR>E.<BR>द्रा to fly, कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्ष
द्राक्ष<BR>(इ) द्राक्षि r. 1st cl. (द्राङ्क्षति)<BR>1 To croke, to caw, &c. as a bird.<BR>2 To desire, to wish or long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राक्षा
द्राक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>द्राक्ष to desire, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राख
द्राख<BR>(ऋ,) द्राखृ^1 r. 1st cl. (द्राखति)<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>2 To adorn.<BR>3 To be able or competent.<BR>4 To prohibit, to prevent.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघ
द्राघ<BR>(ऋ) दाधृ r. 1st cl. (द्राघते)<BR>1 To be able or competent.<BR>2 To stretch, to lengthen.<BR>3 To tire, to be tired or fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिमन्
द्राघिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Length.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and इमनिच् affix, the first syllable changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिमवत्
द्राघिमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Long, lengthy.<BR>E.<BR>द्राघिमन्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघिष्ठ|द्राघिष्ठः
द्राघिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Longest, very long.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ long, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative, and द्राध substituted for दीर्घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राघीयस्
द्राघीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very or exceeding long.<BR>E.<BR>दीर्घ, and ईयसुन् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राड
द्राड<BR>(ऋ) दाघृ r. 1st cl. (द्राडते)<BR>To divide, to split, to pierce, to pull to pieces, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राण|द्राणः
द्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Flown, run away, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to fly, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राप|द्रापः
द्राप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Mud, mire.<BR>2 Heaven, sky.<BR>3 A fool, an idiot.<BR>4 A cowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रामिल|द्रामिलः
द्रामिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Muni CĀṆAKYA.<BR>E.<BR>द्रमिल a proper name, and अण् patronymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राव|द्रावः
द्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Flight, retreat.<BR>2 Speed, going quickly.<BR>3 Flowing, running.<BR>4 Fusion, liquefaction.<BR>5 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावक|द्रावकं|द्रावकः
द्रावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of stone, (a loadstone.)<BR>2 A wit, a wag, a sharp or clever man.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>5 A pursuer, a chaser, one who causes to fly.<BR>6 A sort of Rasa or quality.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to fly, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावकर|द्रावकरं
द्रावकर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A kind of borax.<BR>2 A flux.<BR>E.<BR>द्राव fusion, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावन
द्रावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The clearing nut.<BR>2 Causing to fly or retreat.<BR>3 Fusing.<BR>4 Distilling.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go or retreat, in the causal form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविका
द्राविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Saliva.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to ooze out, ण्वुल् affix, and the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविड|द्राविडः
द्राविड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A country, properly the coast of Coromandel from Madras to Cape Comorin, or the country in which Tamul is spoken.<BR>2 A native of Drāvira or Drāviḍa.<BR>3 A Brahman of Dravira, or rather of the south, five Drāviras being specified, or Drāvira, Karṇāṭa, Gujjerāta, Mahārāṣṭra, and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">Page430</a>] Telanga.<BR>4 A particular number.<BR>5 Zedoary.<BR>E.<BR>द्रविड, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=429" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविडक|द्राविडकं|द्राविडकः
द्राविडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, growing in the country of Drāvira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राविडभूतिक|द्राविडभूतिकः
द्राविडभूतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary.<BR>E.<BR>द्राविड the country, भूत being, affix ठक्: see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रावित
द्रावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Melted, liquefied.<BR>2 Softened, mollified.<BR>3 Driven, chased.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राव्य|द्राव्यं
द्राव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be set in motion, to be put to flight, &c.<BR>2 Fusible, liquefiable, to be made fluid.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्राह
द्राह<BR>(ऋ) द्राह r. 1st cl. (द्राहते)<BR>1 To wake.<BR>2 To deposit, to pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
द्रु<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्रबति)<BR>1 To go, to move, to run.<BR>2 To drop.<BR>3 To distil or ooze.<BR>r. 5th cl. (द्रुनुते द्रुनोति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To pursue, to follow.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To swim, to float, to descend.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To flee.<BR>With उप,<BR>To oppress, to destroy.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To fly, to retreat, to run away.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To smite, to kill.<BR>2 To flee, to run away.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To run together.<BR>With सम् and उप,<BR>To flee.<BR>2 To meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रु|द्रुः
द्रु<BR>m. (द्रुः)<BR>A tree.<BR>f. (द्रुः)<BR>Going, motion.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go (up), to grow, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुकिलिम|द्रुकिलिमं
द्रुकिलिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A tree, a sort of pine: (Pinus devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, किलिम the fir or pine, derived from किल to send or cast, to give out (resin), and किमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुघण|द्रुघणः
द्रुघण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A mace, a millet, an iron weapon made like a carpenter's hammer.<BR>2 An axe, a hatchet.<BR>3 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>4 A plant: see भूमिचम्पक.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, हन to injure or demolish, affix अप्, and घन substituted for the radical; न is usually changed to ण, but the word is also written द्रुघन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुड
द्रुड<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्रुडति)<BR>To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुण|द्रुणं|द्रुणः
द्रुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (द्रुणति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure.<BR>2 To go, to move, to approach.<BR>3 To bind, to make crooked or curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुण|द्रुणं|द्रुणः
द्रुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>2 A bee.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A bow string.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A bow.<BR>2 A sword, a scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुण to injure, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणस|द्रुणसः
द्रुणस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Large-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, and नस for नास a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणह|द्रुणहः
द्रुणह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A scabbard, a sword sheath.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुण a sword, हन to kill or remove, affix ड; the word is also द्रुनह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुणि|द्रुणिः
द्रुणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 An oval water bason of wood or stone, &c. shaped like a boat, and used for pouring water.<BR>2 A bucket, a basket.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A centipede.<BR>2 A small or female tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुण to go, to hurt, affixes कि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुत|द्रुतं|द्रुतः
द्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Quick or swift.<BR>2 Melted, fused.<BR>3 Liquid, fluid.<BR>4 Flown, escaped, run away.<BR>5 Scattered, diffused.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Quick time, (in music,)<BR>adv. n. (-तं)<BR>Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E.<BR>द्र to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुतपद
द्रुतपद<BR>n. subs. (-दं)<BR>A quick pace or step.<BR>adv.<BR>Quickly.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुत, and पद a step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुनख|द्रुनखः
द्रुनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, and नख nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुनह|द्रुनहः
द्रुनह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A scabbard: see द्रुणह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुम|द्रुमः
द्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A tree in general.<BR>2 A tree of Svarga or paradise.<BR>3 A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, म aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमनख|द्रुमनखः
द्रुमनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and नस्व a finger nail: see द्रुनख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमर|द्रुमरः
द्रुमर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, रम to sport, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमव्याधि|द्रुमव्याधिः
द्रुमव्याधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Lac.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम, and व्याधि disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमशीर्ष|द्रुमशीर्षं
द्रुमशीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The upper part of a building or wall.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and शीर्ष a head, resembling the top of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमश्रेष्ठ|द्रुमश्रेष्ठः
द्रुमश्रेष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The palm tree: see ताल.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमामय|द्रुमामयः
द्रुमामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Lac, the animal dye.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and आमत्र sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमारि|द्रुमारिः
द्रुमारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमाश्रय|द्रुमाश्रयः
द्रुमाश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sheltering or dwelling in trees.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुन, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमेश्वर|द्रुमेश्वरः
द्रुमेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The palm tree: see ताल.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुमोत्पल|द्रुमोत्पलः
द्रुमोत्पल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant: see कर्णिकार.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुम a tree, and उत्पल a lotus, to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुवय|द्रुवयं|द्रुवयः
द्रुवय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Measure in general.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, and वय affix, implying measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुसल्लक|द्रुसल्लकः
द्रुसल्लक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Chironjia sapida.)<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a thing or substance, सल्लका the olibanum plant; a resinous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह्
द्रुह्<BR>m. (ध्रुक्)<BR>An injurer.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to hate, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह|द्रुहः
द्रुह<BR>r. 4th cl. (द्रुह्यति)<BR>To bear hatred, to seek to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रह|द्रहः
द्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A son.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to hurt, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुहण|द्रुहणः
द्रुहण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुहिण|द्रुहिणः
द्रुहिण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to injure or hurt, (the wicked,) and इनन् affix, or द्रु a tree, (figuratively the universe,) हन to destroy, इनि affix, destroyer of the world; न changed to ण; also द्रुहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रुह्यत्
द्रुह्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ह्यन्-ह्यन्ती-ह्यत्)<BR>1 Attacking, assailing, defying.<BR>2 Tyrannising over, oppressing.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to hate, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रू
द्रू<BR>r. 9th cl. (ञ्,) द्रूञ् (द्रूणाति द्रूणीते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रू
द्रू<BR>m. (-द्रूः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु to go, क्विप् affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रूघण|द्रूघणः
द्रूघण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 An iron club.<BR>3 A sort of hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>द्रु a tree, हन to strike, affix अप्, घ and ण substituted for ह and न, and the vowel of द्रु made long; also optionally द्रुघण, द्रुघन, and द्रूघन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रूण|द्रूणः
द्रूण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A scorpion; also द्रुण and द्रोण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक
द्रेक<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) देकृ (द्रेकते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To grow or increase.<BR>3 To manifest joy or elevation by noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक्क|द्रेक्कः
द्रेक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>The regent of one-third of a planetary sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रेक्काण|द्रेक्काणः
द्रेक्काण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The regent of one-third of a planetary sign, the Decanus of European astrology, whence the word is probably derived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रै
द्रै<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्रायति)<BR>To sleep; नि is usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोण|द्रोणः
द्रोण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 A measure of capacity, the same as an Āḍhaka: see आढक.<BR>2 A measure of four Āḍhakas.<BR>3 In common use, a measure of thirty-two Seras, or rather more than sixty-four lbs. avoirdupois.<BR>4 The sixteenth part of a Khāri, or forty-eight gallons.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A proper name, the military [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">Page431</a>] preceptor of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>2 A raven, or perhaps the carrion crow.<BR>3 A scorpion: see द्रुण.<BR>4 A large piece of water, one four hundred poles long.<BR>5 One of the principal clouds.<BR>6 A small tree bearing white flowers.<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 Any oval vessel made of wood, stone, &c. in the shape of a boat, and used for holding or pouring out water, as a bathing tub, a baling vessel, a bucket, a watering pot, &c.<BR>2 A trough or rack for feeding cattle.<BR>3 The name of a country.<BR>4 The name of a mountain.<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The indigo plant.<BR>2 The union of two mountains, the valley or chasm between them.<BR>3 A sort of boat, implying the sort of water vessel, probably, described above.<BR>4 A measure of capacity equal^1 to 128 Seras.<BR>E.<BR>द्र to go, न or नि Uṇādi affix, and ङीष् added to either form.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=430" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणकाक|द्रोणकाकः
द्रोणकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण the same, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणकाकल|द्रोणकाकलः
द्रोणकाकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण as above, काकल here said to mean a crow, from का imitative sound, caw, and कल who utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणक्षीरा
द्रोणक्षीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A cow that yields a Droṇa of milk.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण the measure so called, and क्षीरा milk; also other analogous compounds, ut infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणगन्धिका
द्रोणगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see रास्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणघा
द्रोणघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>A cow that yields a Droṇa of milk.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण the measure, दुह to milk, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणदुग्धा
द्रोणदुग्धा<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>A cow that yields a Droṇa of milk.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणदुघा
द्रोणदुघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>See the last.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण, and दुह to milk, affix कप्, and ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणपुष्पी
द्रोणपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, known commonly by the same name; also गोशीर्षक.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण the measure, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणमाना
द्रोणमाना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A cow yielding a Droṇa of milk.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण, and मान a measure: see द्रोणक्षीरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणमुख|द्रोणमुखं
द्रोणमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The capital of a district, the chief of four hundred villages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणम्पच|द्रोणंपच|द्रोणम्पचः
द्रोणम्पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Liberal in entertaining, one who cooks a Droṇa.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण, and पच to cook, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणाचार्य्य|द्रोणाचार्य|द्रोणाचार्यः|द्रोणाचार्य्यः
द्रोणाचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A proper name; Droṇa, the son of BHĀRADVĀJA, and the Ācārya or teacher of the Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण as above, and आचार्य्य a preceptor; also with कन् added द्रोणाचार्य्यक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणिका
द्रोणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोणि the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणीदल|द्रोणीदलः
द्रोणीदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>द्रोणी a water vessel, and दल a leaf, the leaves being boat-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोणीमुख|द्रोणीमुखं
द्रोणीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The principal of four hundred villages: see द्रोणमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोह|द्रोहः
द्रोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Mischief, malice, trespass, injury.<BR>2 Offence, wrong.<BR>3 Rebellion.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to hurt or injure, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहचिन्तन|द्रोहचिंतन|द्रोहचिन्तनं
द्रोहचिन्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Injurious design, malice prepense; the wish, thought, or attempt to injure.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोह as above, and चिन्तन thinking, meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहाट|द्रोहाटः
द्रोहाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A hunter, a deer killer.<BR>2 A sort of metre, the Doha or stanza of Hindi poetry.<BR>3 A religious impostor, a tartuffe, a hypocrite.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोह injury, mischief, and अट who goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रोहिन्
द्रोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>1 Hurting, harming, endeavouring to hurt, malignant, malicious.<BR>2 Rebellious.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुह to seek to hurt, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौणायण
द्रौणायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of AŚVATTHĀMA, son of Droṇa.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण as above, and फक affix; also with फिञ affix द्रौणायणि, or with इञ् affix द्रौणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौणिक|द्रौणिकः
द्रौणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sown with a Droṇa of grain, (fields, &c.)<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A vessel holding a Droṇa by measure.<BR>E.<BR>द्रोण the measure, ठञ् or ठन् affix; also with अण् and ङीष् affix in the last sense द्रौणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रौपदी
द्रौपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A proper name; DRAUPADĪ, the daughter of DRUPADA, king of Pañcāla, and the common wife of the five Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>E.<BR>द्रुपद the father of this lady, and अण and ङीप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द|द्वंद|द्वन्दं|द्वंदः|द्वन्दः
द्वन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A clock or plate on which hours are struck.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>A pair, a couple, (male and female especially): see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्व|द्वंद्व|द्वंद्वं|द्वन्द्वं|द्वन्द्वः
द्वन्द्व<BR>n. (-न्द्वं)<BR>1 A pair, a brace.<BR>2 A couple of animals, or male and female.<BR>3 Union of the sexes or coupling.<BR>4 Strife, dispute.<BR>5 A secret.<BR>m. (-न्द्वः)<BR>1 A form of grammatical combination uniting two or more words in the same case, properly separated by a conjunction, as रामलक्ष्मणौ RĀMA and LAKṢMAṆA; पाणिपादं hand and foot.<BR>2 A sign of the zodiac, (Gemini.)<BR>3 A species of disease, a complication of two disorders, or compound affection of two humours.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, reduplicate, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वचर|द्वंद्वचर|द्वन्द्वचरः
द्वन्द्वचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>द्वग्द्व a couple, and चर who goes; flying in couples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वचारिन्|द्वंद्वचारिन्
द्वन्द्वचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व, and चर to go, affix णिनिः see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वज|द्वंद्वज|द्वन्द्वजः
द्वन्द्वज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-लं)<BR>1 Produced or proceeding from morbid affection of two humours.<BR>2 Proceeding from a pair, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वदुःख|द्वंद्वदुःख
द्वन्द्वदुःख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Pain arising from alternation, as of heat or cold, pleasure or pain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व, and दुःख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वभिन्न|द्वंद्वभिन्न
द्वन्द्वभिन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Separation of the sexes.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वयुद्ध|द्वंद्वयुद्ध
द्वन्द्वयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Single combat.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वन्द्वातीत|द्वंद्वातीत
द्वन्द्वातीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Free from worldly affections.<BR>E.<BR>द्वन्द्व alternation. (of pain and pleasure, &c.) and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वय|द्वयं
द्वय<BR>n. (-यः-यं)<BR>A pair, a couple, two, chiefly used in composition, as पुरुषद्वयं two men.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, टयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वयाग्नि|द्वयाग्निः
द्वयाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वयातिग|द्वयातिगः
द्वयातिग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A saint, a holy or virtuous man.<BR>E.<BR>द्वय a pair, the two bad qualities, passion and ignorance, अति beyond, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थ|द्वाःस्थः
द्वाःस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A warder, a porter.<BR>2 NANDĪ, one of ŚIVA'S doorkeepers.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार् a door, and स्थ who stays; also द्वास्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थित|द्वाःस्थितः
द्वाःस्थित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार् a door, and स्थित staying; also द्वास्थित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वाःस्थितदर्शक|द्वाःस्थितदर्शकः
द्वाःस्थितदर्शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A warder, a porter, a chamberlain.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार् a door, स्थित staying, and दर्शक who shows, who introduces to the prince or great man to whom the mansion belongs; also द्वाःस्थित and दर्शक severally; also द्वाःस्थितदर्शिन्, m. (-र्शी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=431" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वात्रिंशदक्षरिन्
द्वात्रिंशदक्षरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A book or composition.<BR>E.<BR>द्वात्रिंशत thirty-two, अक्षर a letter, a consonant, इनि affix; formed of thirty-two letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेत|द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेतः
द्वात्रिंशल्लक्षणोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having thirty-two auspicious marks, illustrious, great.<BR>E.<BR>द्वात्रिंशत् thirty-two, लक्षण a mark, उपेत possessing, endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादश|द्वादशः
द्वादश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी)<BR>Twelfth.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The twelfth day of the half month.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादशन्, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशक
द्वादशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Consisting of twelve, amounting to twelve, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशकर|द्वादशकरः
द्वादशकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>2 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and कर a hand or ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशन्
द्वादशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Twelve.<BR>E.<BR>द्वा for द्वि two, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशपत्रक|द्वादशपत्रकं
द्वादशपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A particular religious observance.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश, and पत्र leaf or part, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशलोचन|द्वादशलोचनः
द्वादशलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The god KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and लोचन an eye; the twelve-eyed, or six-headed deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशांशु|द्वादशांशुः
द्वादशांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The deity VṚHASPATI, or planet Jupiter, over which he presides.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाक्ष|द्वादशाक्षः
द्वादशाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The god KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 The deity or sage Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and अक्ष an eye: the word is sometimes read in the second sense, द्वादशाख्य m. (-ख्यः) the twelve-named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्र|द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्रः
द्वादशाक्षरमन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A prayer of twelve syllables, especially as addressed to VIṢṆU, or Om, BHAGAVATE, VĀSUDEVĀYA, RĀMĀYA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश, अक्षर a letter, and मन्त्र formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशाङ्गुल|द्वादशांगुल|द्वादशाङ्गुलः
द्वादशाङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A measure of twelve fingers.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश, and अङ्गुल a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशात्मन्
द्वादशात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and आत्मन्, identity; being represented in and identified with the twelve Ādityas, or the sun in each month of the year; also द्वादशात्मक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशायुस्
द्वादशायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, (years,) and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशार्च्चिस्|द्वादशार्चिस्
द्वादशार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, regent of Jupiter, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश twelve, and अर्च्चिस् a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वादशास्र
द्वादशास्र<BR>nf. (-स्रं-स्री)<BR>A parallelopipedon, a dodecagonal figure.<BR>E.<BR>द्वादश, and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वापर|द्वापरं|द्वापरः
द्वापर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The third of the four Yugas or great periods, comprising 864,000 years.<BR>2 The age personified as a god.<BR>3 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>द्वा for द्वि two, पर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार्
द्वार्<BR>f. (-द्वाः)<BR>1 A door, a gate.<BR>2 A means, an expedient, a medium or way by which any thing takes place or is effected.<BR>E.<BR>द्वृ to cover or hold, in the causal form, affix विच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वार|द्वारं
द्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A door, a gate, or rather the door or gateway, a passage, an entrance.<BR>2 A way, a means, a medium or vehicle.<BR>E.<BR>द्वृ to cover, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारक|द्वारकः
द्वारक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>Dvāraka the capital of KṚṢṆA, supposed to have been submerged by the sea, but represented by a small island off the north part of the Malabar coast.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a way, (to salvation,) affix कन्; also द्वारिका, द्वारवती, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारकण्टक|द्वारकंटक|द्वारकण्टकः
द्वारकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A door, a gate, the door itself.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a doorway, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारकेश|द्वारकेशः
द्वारकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वारका as above, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारपाल|द्वारपालः
द्वारपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A warder, a doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and पाल who protects; also with कन् added द्वारपालक, or with the radical finals dropped द्वारप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारपिण्डी|द्वारपिंडी
द्वारपिण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>The threshold of a door.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and पिण्ड a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारयन्त्र|द्वारयंत्र|द्वारयन्त्रं
द्वारयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A lock, a bolt.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and यन्त्र an instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारवती
द्वारवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The city Dvārakā.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and मतुप् poss. affix; also द्वारावती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारवलिभुज्
द्वारवलिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक)<BR>The Vaka, a sort of crane, (Ardea nivea).<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, वलि offal or fragments, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारशाखा
द्वारशाखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The leaf of a door.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and शास्वा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारस्तम्भ|द्वारस्तम्भः
द्वारस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A door-post.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार, and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारस्थ|द्वारस्थः
द्वारस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a gate, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारावती
द्वारावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Dvāraka: see द्वारवती, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारिक|द्वारिकः
द्वारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, and ठक् affix.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Dvāraka, KṚṢṆA'S capital: see द्वारक.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारिन्
द्वारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A porter, a warder, a doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थ|द्वास्थः
द्वास्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार a door, स्थ who stays, and र rejected; also र being changed to Visarga, द्वाःस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थित|द्वास्थितः
द्वास्थित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A doorkeeper.<BR>E.<BR>द्वार, and स्थित who stays; also द्वाःस्थितः see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वास्थितदर्शक|द्वास्थितदर्शकः
द्वास्थितदर्शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A doorkeeper: see द्वाःस्थितदर्शक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वि|द्विः
द्वि<BR>dual only. mf. (-द्वौ) n. (-द्वे)<BR>Two.<BR>m. (-द्विः)<BR>Two, (of times, &c.) it is only used in composition, as अतिद्वि a thing more than two, and inflected like other nouns in इः in composition with other numerals, it is changed to द्वा, as द्वादश twelve, द्वाविंशति twenty-two, द्वात्रिंशत् thirty-two, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विक|द्विकं|द्विकः
द्विक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and क the letter क, as in काक.<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Two.<BR>2 Twice.<BR>3 Two-fold.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, कन् pleonastick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककार|द्विककारः
द्विककार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two or twice, and ककार the letter क, as in काक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विककुद्
द्विककुद्<BR>m. (-दः^1)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and ककुद् a hump.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321. note: kakud and kakudaH are both endings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विकर
द्विकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what makes two of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि and कृ to make, ञच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगु|द्विगुः
द्विगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>A form of grammatical combination, that in which the first member of the compound is a numeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुण|द्विगुणं
द्विगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Twice, two times.<BR>2 Multiplied by two, doubled.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and गुण number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणाकृत|द्विगुणाकृतं
द्विगुणाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Twice ploughed.<BR>E.<BR>द्विगुणा twice, and कृत ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणित
द्विगुणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Doubled, multiplied by two.<BR>2 Folded, double.<BR>3 Invested, enveloped.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and गुण a time, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणीकृत
द्विगुणीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Doubled.<BR>2 Increased.<BR>E.<BR>द्विगुण twice, कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विगुणीभूत
द्विगुणीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Doubled.<BR>2 Augmented.<BR>E.<BR>द्विगुण twice, भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज|द्विजः
द्विज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Twice born.<BR>2 Oviparous.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A man of either of the three first classes, a Brahman, a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">Page433</a>] Kṣatriya or a Vaiśya whose investiture with the characteristick string, at years of puberty, constitutes, religiously and metaphorically, their second birth.<BR>2 Any oviparous animal, as a bird, a snake, a fish, &c. first born in the shell, and in the second instance produced from it.<BR>3 A tooth.<BR>4 Coriander seed.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A sort of perfume; also called Reṇukā.<BR>2 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indicus.)<BR>3 Kundur or gum olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=432" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजकुत्सित|द्विजकुत्सितः
द्विजकुत्सित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a bird, कुत्सित reviled, disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजन्मन्
द्विजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>1 Twice born, regenerate.<BR>2 Oviparous.<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>3 A bird.<BR>4 A man of the three first classes.<BR>5 Any oviparous animal: see द्विज.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि twice, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजदास|द्विजदासः
द्विजदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A Śūdra or man of the fourth and servile tribe.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a man of either of the three first castes, and दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजपति|द्विजपतिः
द्विजपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a Brahman, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजप्रपा
द्विजप्रपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A trough near a well for watering birds, cattle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a bird, &c. and प्र prefixed to पा to drink, affix अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजप्रिय
द्विजप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Acceptable or friendly to a man of the three first classes, or a Brahman especially.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The moonplant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a Brahman, and प्रिय beloved, the acid juice being drank at certain sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजराज|द्विजराजः
द्विजराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The great serpent ANANTA.<BR>3 The bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a snake or bird, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजलिङ्गिन्|द्विजलिंगिन्
द्विजलिङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A Kṣatriya or man of the military tribe.<BR>2 An impostor, a pretended Brahman, wearing the distinguishing mark of that tribe without belonging to it.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज twice born, and लिङ्ग a mark, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजवर्य्य|द्विजवर्य
द्विजवर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>An excellent or superior Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and वर्य्य excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजव्रण|द्विजव्रणः
द्विजव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Gumboil, toothache.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a tooth, व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजब्रुव|द्विजब्रुवः
द्विजब्रुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Brahman by birth only, one not studied or not practising the duties of his caste.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a Brahman, and व्रुव who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजशप्त|द्विजशप्तः
द्विजशप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A sort of pulse; also called Raja-māṣ-kalai and Berbetti, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a Brahman, and शप्त cursed; it is prohibited food on some occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजशुश्रूषा
द्विजशुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Service of the three first classes, especially of the Brahmans, by the fourth.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसत्तम
द्विजसत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A respectable Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and सत्तम best; also द्विजवर, द्विजप्रवर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसेवक|द्विजसेवकः
द्विजसेवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Śūdra or man of the fourth and servile class.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a man of the three first classes, and सेवक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजसेवा
द्विजसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Service of the three first classes, especially of the Brahman by the fourth.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाग्र्य
द्विजाग्र्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A chief or respectable Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and अग्र्य first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाङ्गी
द्विजाङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A medicinal plant; also कटुरोहिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजाति|द्विजातिः
द्विजाति<BR>(-तिः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A man of either of the three first classes.<BR>3 Any oviparous animal, as a bird, a snake, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, जाति birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजानुलोम
द्विजानुलोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The regular order or series of the three first classes.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज, and अनुलोम with the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजायनी
द्विजायनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The characteristick thread or cord which designates the three first classes of the Hindūs.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज twiceborn, फक् affix, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजालय|द्विजालयः
द्विजालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The hollow of a tree.<BR>2 The residence of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज a bird, a Brahman, and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्व|द्विजिह्वः
द्विजिह्व<BR>mfn. (ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>Double-tongued, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 An informer.<BR>3 A rogue, a scoundrel, a bad man.<BR>4 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजिह्वता
द्विजिह्वता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Insincerity, dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विजोत्तम|द्विजोत्तमः
द्विजोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A superior or excellent Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज the twice-born, (three first classes,) and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज्या
द्विज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>The sine or chord of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विज्यामार्ग
द्विज्यामार्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A horizontal line.<BR>E.<BR>द्विज्य, and मार्ग road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विट्सेवा
द्विट्सेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Treachery.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष् a foe, सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विट्सेविन्
द्विट्सेविन्<BR>n. (वी)<BR>A traitor.<BR>E.<BR>द्विट् an enemy, and सेविन् who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विठ|द्विठः
द्विठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Svāhā, the expression used with an oblation to fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितय|द्वितयं
द्वितय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A couple, a pair, two.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीय|द्वितीयं|द्वितीयः
द्वितीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Second.<BR>2 Two.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A son, a second or successor.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A wife, according to the ritual, a woman wedded after the ceremony prescribed by the Vedas, a second self as it were.<BR>2 The second day of the fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and तीय affix, fem. affix टाप्; also with कन् added, द्वितीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयत्व
द्वितीयत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The circumstance or state of second.<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय, and त्व affix: also with तल्, द्वितीयता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयत्रिफला
द्वितीयत्रिफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A set of three fruits, the grape, the date, and the Gambhāri.<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय second, त्रिफल three fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयाकृत|द्वितीयाकृतं
द्वितीयाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Twice ploughed, &c. (a field.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय a second time, and आकृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयाभा
द्वितीयाभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A scitamineous plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhiza.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय second, आभा lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वितीयीक
द्वितीयीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Second.<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय, and ईकक pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वित्र
द्वित्र<BR>mfn. plu. always (-त्रः-त्राः-त्रणि)<BR>Two or three.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and त्र for त्रि three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदत्|द्विदन्त्
द्विदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Two-toothed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, दत् for दन्त a tooth; if marking age or period the compound is द्विदन्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदन्त|द्विदन्तः
द्विदन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>Old enough to have two teeth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि and दन्त a tooth, see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदण्डि|द्विदंडि
द्विदण्डि<BR>ind.<BR>Single stick, quarter staff, as द्विदण्डि प्रहरणं fighting with two sticks.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, दण्ड a staff, इच् affix; also similar compounds, as द्विमुषलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदश
द्विदश<BR>m. plu. (-शाः)<BR>Twenty, two tens.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and दश ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदाम्नी
द्विदाम्नी<BR>f. (-म्नी)<BR>A cow tied with two ropes.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and दामन् a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदेह|द्विदेहः
द्विदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and देह a body; having the head of an elephant, with the figure of a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=433" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विदैवत्या
द्विदैवत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>The constellation Viśākha.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, दैवत a deity, and क्यप् affix; INDRA and AGNI jointly presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधा
द्विधा<BR>ind.<BR>Of two kinds, in two ways.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधाकरण
द्विधाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Dividing into two parts, arranging in two ways, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्विधा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधागति|द्विधागतिः
द्विधागति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>द्विधा of two sorts, गति going; amphibious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधातु|द्विधातुः
द्विधातु<BR>mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु)<BR>Having two natures, two roots, &c.<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two or double, धातु nature: see द्विदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधात्मक|द्विधात्मकं
द्विधात्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A nutmeg.<BR>E.<BR>द्विधा two sorts, and आत्मक being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विधालेख्य|द्विधालेख्यः
द्विधालेख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>To be written in two ways.<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>The marshy date tree.<BR>E.<BR>द्विधा, and लेख्य to be written or described.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनग्नक|द्विनग्नकः
द्विनग्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A circumcised man, one having no prepuce.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, नग्न naked, कन् added; exposed either by want of clothes or skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विनिष्क
द्विनिष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Bought, &c. with two Niṣkas.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and निष्क a measure of value; also द्विनैष्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विप|द्विपः
द्विप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and प who drinks, the elephant imbibing fluids by his trunk, and thence conveying them into his mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपथ|द्विपथं
द्विपथ<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>A place where two roads meet.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, प्रथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपद|द्विपदः
द्विपद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Two-footed.<BR>2 Having two parts.<BR>3 Binomial.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A biped, including four genera, gods, demons, men, and birds.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and पद for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपदराशि|द्विपदराशिः
द्विपदराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>Either of the signs, Gemini, Libra, Aquarius, Virgo, and half of Sagittarius.<BR>E.<BR>द्विपद, and राशि a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपमद|द्विपमदः
द्विपमद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The elephant's temporal juice.<BR>E.<BR>द्विप, and मद the exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपर्ण
द्विपर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Two-leaved, opposite-leaved.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपात्त्व
द्विपात्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The having of two feet, two parts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्विपाद्, and त्व affix; also with तल्, द्विपात्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपाद्
द्विपाद्<BR>mfn. (-पाद् पती पत्)<BR>Biped, two-footed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and पाद् for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपाद्य|द्विपाद्यं|द्विपाद्यः
द्विपाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Bought, &c. with two quarters.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>A double penalty, an amercement of twice the common amount.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, पाद a division, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपायिन्
द्विपायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and पायिन् who drinks: see द्विप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विपृष्ट
द्विपृष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A proper name; also VASUDEVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विप्रतिक
द्विप्रतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought, &c. with two Karṣas.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, प्रति for कार्षापण, and ठन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विबाहु|द्विबाहुः
द्विबाहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-ह्वी-हु)<BR>Two-armed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विभुज|द्विभुजः
द्विभुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Two-armed.<BR>2 An angle or the lines which form it.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and भुज an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमय
द्विमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or consisting of two, (parts of any thing.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमातृज|द्विमातृजः
द्विमातृज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Having two mothers, born in two ways; it may be said of some of the deities, thus GAṆEŚA was the son of PĀRVATĪ, but not born in the usual way, being made of the scurf of her body: see द्वैमातुर.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, मातृ a mother, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुख|द्विमुखः
द्विमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A serpent.<BR>f. (-खः)<BR>1 A small water jar.<BR>2 A leech.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and मुख mouth; double-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुखाहि|द्विमुखाहिः
द्विमुखाहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A sort of serpent, (Amphisbœna.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, मुख face, अहि a snake; the double-headed snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमुखोरग|द्विमुखोरगः
द्विमुखोरग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A sort of snake: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>द्विमुख as above, and उरग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विमूर्द्ध
द्विमूर्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>Two-headed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, मूर्द्धन् the forehead, and यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विर|द्विरः
द्विर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bee: see द्विरेफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरद|द्विरदः
द्विरद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and रद a tooth, having tusks and teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरदान्तक|द्विरदांतक|द्विरदान्तकः
द्विरदान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>द्विरद, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरशन|द्विरशनं
द्विरशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating twice a day.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरसन|द्विरसनः
द्विरसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A snake in general.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, रसना the tongue; double or forky-tongued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरात्र
द्विरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A period of two nights.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विराप|द्विरापः
द्विराप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>द्विर् for द्वि two, आङ् prefixed to पा to drink, affix ड; drinking with the trunk and mouth: see द्विप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुक्त|द्विरुक्तः
द्विरुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Repeated, said twice.<BR>2 Said or told in two ways.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुक्ति|द्विरुक्तिः
द्विरुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Tautology, repetition.<BR>2 Variety of narration, telling any thing in two ways.<BR>3 (In Grammar,) Repetition of a syllable.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरुढा
द्विरुढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A woman who has been twice married.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, उढ a married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरूप|द्विरूपः
द्विरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पी-पं)<BR>1 Of two forms, having a different shape.<BR>2 Spelled or written in two ways.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A word that may be correctly spelled in two ways.<BR>2 Variety of interpretation or reading.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरेफ|द्विरेफः
द्विरेफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, रेफ the letter र; having two rs, in the most common name, भ्रमर, Bhramara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विरेफवृन्द
द्विरेफवृन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>A flight or swarm of bees.<BR>E.<BR>द्विरेफ, and वृन्द a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्ष
द्विवर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं)<BR>Two years old, &c.<BR>(-र्षा)<BR>A cow two years old.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, वर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्षिका
द्विवर्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow two years old.<BR>E.<BR>द्विवर्षा, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवर्षीण|द्विवर्षीणः
द्विवर्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Two years old, two years standing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, वर्ष a year, ख affix; also with ठञ् affix द्विवार्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) when futurity is implied, the first vowel is usually changed, as द्वैवार्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवाहिका
द्विवाहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A swing, a swinging cot, a litter.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, वह to bear, affix ठक्; born usually by two men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविद|द्विविदः
द्विविद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a monkey, slain by RĀMA or VIṢṆU in that incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविदारि
द्विविदारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>द्विविद as above, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विविध
द्विविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of two kinds, in two ways.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विवेशरा
द्विवेशरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A kind of carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशफ|द्विशफः
द्विशफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Any cloven-footed animal.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशस्
द्विशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Two by two, respectively.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=434" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशीर्षक
द्विशीर्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, शीर्ष a head, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशूर्प्प|द्विशूर्प
द्विशूर्प्प<BR>mfn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पी-र्प्पं)<BR>Bought with two winnowing baskets of anything.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and शूर्प्पं a basket; also with ठञ् द्विशौर्प्पिक, mfn. (-कः-की-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विशृङ्गिन्
द्विशृङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of fish, commonly called Marmaka.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष|द्विषः
द्विष<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्विषति) also (औ) औद्विष r. 2nd cl. (द्वेष्टि) plu. (द्विषन्ति)<BR>To hate, to dislike, to be hostile or unfriendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्
द्विष्<BR>mfn. (द्विट्)<BR>Inimical, hostile.<BR>m. (द्विट्)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, affix क्विप्; also with क affix द्विष. m. (-षः) or mfn. (-षः-षा-षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषत्|द्विषन्त्
द्विषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>1 Hating or detesting, hostile.<BR>2 Inimical, unfriendly.<BR>m. (-न्)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, participal aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषतीताप|द्विषतीतापः
द्विषतीताप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Vexing or harassing an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>द्विषत्, and ताप who afflicts, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विषन्तप|द्विषंतप|द्विषन्तपः
द्विषन्तप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Punishing or annoying an enemy, revenging, retaliating.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष an enemy, तप to burn, affix खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्ट|द्विष्टं
द्विष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Hated, disliked.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Copper: see द्व्यष्ट.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विष्ठ|द्विष्ठः
द्विष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Staying in two shapes or places, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and स्थ what is or abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसप्ताह|द्विसप्ताहः
द्विसप्ताह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि twice, सप्त seven, and अह a day, twice seven days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसम
द्विसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Consisting of two equal portions, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, सम equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसमत्रिभुजा
द्विसमत्रिभुजा^1<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>An isosceles triangle.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, सम equal, त्रिभुजा triangle.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160511. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/259. note: triBujA is triangle. So 'BUjA' is misprint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसहस्राक्ष|द्विसहस्राक्षः
द्विसहस्राक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The great serpent, sovereign of the snake race, and the couch of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>द्विसहस्र two thousand, and अक्षि an eye; the two thousand-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विसीत्य|द्विसीत्यं
द्विसीत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Twice ploughed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि twice, सीता a plough, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विस्तन
द्विस्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Two-breasted, two-uddered.<BR>E.<BR>द्धि, and स्तन breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहन्
द्विहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, in two ways, with tusks and teeth, and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहल्य|द्विहल्यं
द्विहल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Twice ploughed.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, हल a plough, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहायन
द्विहायन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Two years old.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A cow two years old.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, हायन a year, affix अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्विहृदया
द्विहृदया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A pregnant woman.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, हृदय a heart; having one of her own and one in the foetus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीन्द्रियग्राह्य|द्वीन्द्रियग्राह्यः
द्वीन्द्रियग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Perceptible by two senses or forms, by sight and touch, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense, ग्राह्य to be seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप|द्वीपं|द्वीपः
द्वीप<BR>mf. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 An island, any land surrounded by water; the word is hence applied to the seven grand divisions of the terrestrial world, each of these being separated from the next, by a peculiar and circumambient ocean: the seven Dvīpas, reckoning from the central one are, Jambu, Kuśa, Plakṣa, Śālmali, Krauncha, Śāka, and Puṣkara: the central Dvīpa, or the known continent, is again portioned into ten divisions, likewise termed Dvīpas: viz. Kuru, Candra, Varuṇa, Saumya, Nāga, Kumārikā, Gabhastimān, Tāmrāpūrna, Kaseru and Indra.<BR>2 A tiger's skin.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, (on both sides,) and आप water, आ dropped, and इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपकर्पूरक
द्वीपकर्पूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>China camphor.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप, and कर्पूर camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपवत्|द्वीपवन्त्
द्वीपवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The ocean.<BR>mf. (-वान्-वती)<BR>A river.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप an island, मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिन्
द्वीपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Island, islander.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 An ounce or panther.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप an island, इनि affix; haunting the small woody islands that abound in the rivers in India, or द्वीप a tiger's spotted skin, derived from द्वि two, इ to go or be, प affix: and इनि as before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीपिशत्रु|द्वीपिशत्रुः
द्वीपिशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>द्वीपिन् a tiger, and शत्रु obnoxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वीप्य|द्वीप्यः
द्वीप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Island, an islander, &c.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>1 A sort of crow.<BR>2 A name of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप, and क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वृ
द्वृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (द्वरति)<BR>1 To accept, to appoint.<BR>2 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेधा
द्वेधा<BR>ind.<BR>In two ways: see द्विघा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष|द्वेषः
द्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Hate, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेषण|द्वेषणं|द्वेषणः
द्वेषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Inimical, hostile.<BR>m. (-णा)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Hate, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, and ल्यु or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेषिन्
द्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Hostile, inimical, adverse, obnoxious.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्टृ
द्वेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Hating, inimical, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्य|द्वेष्यः
द्वेष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Hateful, detestable.<BR>E.<BR>द्विष to hate, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वेष्यता
द्वेष्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Aversion, dislike, detestableness.<BR>E.<BR>द्वेष्य, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुणिक|द्वैगुणिकः
द्वैगुणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A usurer, a money lender.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, गुण number, affix ठक्; who requires cent. per cent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैगुण्य|द्वैगुण्यं
द्वैगुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Duality.<BR>2 The possession of two out of the three qualities.<BR>3 Doubling.<BR>E.<BR>द्विगुण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैजात
द्वैजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Twice born.<BR>E.<BR>द्विजात, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैत|द्वैतं
द्वैत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Duplication, doubling or being doubled.<BR>2 Duality, in philosophy, the assertion of two principles, as the distinctness of life and soul, spirit and matter, god and the universe.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, तल् affix, द्वित double, two-fold, abstract affix अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतवादिन्
द्वैतवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A philosopher who asserts two principles.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैत, and वादिन् who asserts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैतीयीक|द्वैतीयीकः
द्वैतीयीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Second.<BR>E.<BR>द्वितीय second, pleonastick affix अण्, and ईकक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैध|द्वैधं
द्वैध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>Two-fold, of two sorts.<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>1 A double resource, a stratagem, a secondary arrangement or array, a reserve.<BR>2 Contest, dispute, difference.<BR>3 A two-fold form or state.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैधम्, and ड added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधम्
द्वैधम्<BR>ind.<BR>In two ways.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and धमुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकरण
द्वैधीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making two, separating, disuniting.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैध, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीकृत
द्वैधीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Separated.<BR>2 Made into two, sundered.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैध, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभाव|द्वैधीभावः
द्वैधीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Sowing dissension, causing the separation of allies.<BR>2 Dividing into two.<BR>3 The nature or property of being two or distinct.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैध, and भाव property, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=435" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैधीभूत
द्वैधीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Being two, being separated or disunited.<BR>E.<BR>द्वैध, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप|द्वैपः
द्वैप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>1 Made of a tiger's skin.<BR>2 Island, islander.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A car covered or hung with a tiger's skin.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप a tiger's skin, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैपायन|द्वैपायनः
द्वैपायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VYĀSA, the author or compiler of the Vedas and Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप an island, फक् affix; the island-born, the place of his nativity being a small island in the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैप्य|द्वैप्यं
द्वैप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Of or belonging to an island.<BR>E.<BR>द्वीप an island, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमातुर|द्वैमातुरः
द्वैमातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Having two mothers, or the natural mother and a step-mother.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 An epithet of JARĀSANDHA: see जरासन्ध.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, मातृ a mother, अण् affix, उ substituted for the penultimate: see द्विमातृज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैमित्रि
द्वैमित्रि<BR>mfn. (-त्रिः-त्री-त्ति)<BR>Born of two friends, the children, &c.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and मित्र a friend, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैयह्निक
द्वैयह्निक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or belonging to two days.<BR>E.<BR>द्व्यहन्, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरथ|द्वैरथं|द्वैरथः
द्वैरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Single combat in chariots.<BR>E.<BR>द्विरथ two cars, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैरात्रिक
द्वैरात्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or belonging to a period of two nights.<BR>E.<BR>द्विरात्र, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैवर्षिक
द्वैवर्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>After two years, of or belonging to two years to come.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, वर्ष a year, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैविध्य|द्वैविध्यं
द्वैविध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यः)<BR>The state of being two-fold.<BR>E.<BR>द्विविध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वैहायन|द्वैहायनं
द्वैहायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The age of two years.<BR>E.<BR>द्विहायन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यंश
द्व्यंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Two shares.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यक्षर|द्व्यक्षरं|द्व्यक्षरः
द्व्यक्षर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A word of two syllables.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अक्षर a syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यङ्गुल|द्व्यंगुल|द्व्यङ्गुलं
द्व्यङ्गुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Measuring two fingers.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Two fingers.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, अङ्गुलि a finger; if wood is implied, the fem. form is द्व्यङ्गुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यञ्जल|द्व्यञ्जलं
द्व्यञ्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Measuring, &c. two Añjalis.<BR>n. (-लिः)<BR>Two Añjalis collectively.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अञ्जलि a certain measure, टच् affix; also with the final retained द्व्यञ्जलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यणुक|द्व्यणुकं
द्व्यणुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The aggregation of two atoms, the first step in the formation of substances, and when they become perceptible.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अणु an atom, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यन्य|द्व्यन्यः
द्व्यन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Accompanied, &c. by two others.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Two others collectively.<BR>E.<BR>द्धि, and अन्य another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यर्थ|द्व्यर्थः
द्व्यर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Having two senses, meaning two things.<BR>2 Having two objects.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>Two-fold meaning, double-entendre.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यष्ट|द्व्यष्टं
द्व्यष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, (metals; gold and silver,) अश to pervade, affix क्त; mixed as alloy with the fine metals; also the य being interchanged with its congener इ, द्विष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यह|द्व्यहः
द्व्यह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Two days.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि two, and अह a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यहीन
द्व्यहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of or belonging to two days.<BR>E.<BR>द्व्यह, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यात्मक|द्व्यात्मकः
द्व्यात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Comprising two, being two.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sign of the zodiac, Gemini, Virgo, Sagittarius, and Pisces.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and आत्मन् self, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यामुषायण
द्व्यामुषायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A boy who remains heir to his father though adopted by another.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and आमुष्यायण a certain person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्यायुष
द्व्यायुष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Two lives.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and आयुस life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्याहिक|द्व्याहिकः
द्व्याहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Produced, &c. in two days.<BR>E.<BR>द्व्याह, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्व्येकान्तर
द्व्येकान्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having two between, two off.<BR>E.<BR>द्वि, and एकान्तर an interval, च a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध<BR>The aspirated letter corresponding to the preceding, and expressed by Dh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध|धं|धः
ध<BR>m. (धः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A name of KUVERA.<BR>3 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>n. (धं)<BR>Wealth, property.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have or possess, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धक्क
धक्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (धक्कयति)<BR>To destroy or annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धट|धटः
धट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>2 The sign Libra.<BR>3 Ordeal by the balance.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 Old cloth or raiment.<BR>2 A piece of cloth worn over the privities.<BR>E.<BR>धण to sound, and ट substituted for ण, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटक|धटकः
धटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A weight of forty-two Rattis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटिनी
धटिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A cotton tie or string, fastened round the loins.<BR>E.<BR>धट a cloth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धटीदान|धटीदानं
धटीदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving old cloth to a woman after impregnation.<BR>E.<BR>धदी, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धण
धण<BR>r. 1st cl. (घणति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धत्तूर|धत्तूरः
धत्तूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The thorn apple: see धुस्तर.<BR>E.<BR>धेट् to drink, उरच् affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन<BR>r. 1st. cl. (धनति)<BR>To sound.<BR>r. 3rd cl. (दधन्ति)<BR>To bear or produce, (grain, &c.): restricted to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन|धनं
धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Property of any description, thing, substance, wealth.<BR>2 Wealth in cattle, property in herds.<BR>3 A term of endearment.<BR>4 (In Algebra,) The affirmative quantity or plus.<BR>E.<BR>धन to produce, (a crop,) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनकेलि|धनकेलिः
धनकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>KUVERA, the Hindū Plutus; also धनकेलिक.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, and केलि who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनगर्व्वित|धनगर्वित
धनगर्व्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purseproud.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and गर्व्वित arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनच्छू
धनच्छू<BR>f. (-च्छूः)<BR>The Numidian crane.<BR>E.<BR>धन the wealth, (of fields,) and च्छो to destroy, affix डू. Note; as a synonym of करेटव्या this word would seem to mean the bird stated: the name itself is more analogous to the Dhanesa of the dialects or the Indian Buceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनजात
धनजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Springing from wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनञ्जय|धनंजय|धनंजयः|धनञ्जयः
धनञ्जय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The deity of fire.<BR>2 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>3 One of the Nāgas or infernal serpents.<BR>4 One of the five vital airs, that which is supposed to fatten.<BR>5 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, जि to conquer or possess, affix खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनतृष्णा
धनतृष्णा<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>Covetousness.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and तृष्णा thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनद|धनदः
धनद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Beneficent, liberal, who gives away property, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, देङ्^1 to drink, or दा to give, affix क.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदण्ड|धनदंड|धनदण्डः
धनदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Fine, amercement.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदर्प
धनदर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>Pride of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and दर्प pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदानुज|धनदानुजः
धनदानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>धनद KUVERA, and अनुज younger brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=436" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनदायिन्
धनदायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Liberal, munificent.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 The deity of fire.<BR>2 A benefactor, a donor.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, दा to give, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनन्ददा|धनंददा
धनन्ददा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>One of the Śaktis, or female personifications of divine power peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, दद to give, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपति|धनपतिः
धनपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The god of riches, KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, and पति master or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिशाचिका
धनपिशाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Avarice, thirst of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, पिशाचा a she-demon, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनपिशाची
धनपिशाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>Extreme desire of riches, avarice.<BR>E.<BR>see the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनप्रिय
धनप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fond of wealth.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A vegetable, (Ardisia solanacea.)<BR>E.<BR>धन, and प्रिय dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमद|धनमदः
धनमद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Proud, inflated with the pride of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, मद to be intoxicated, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनमूल
धनमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Proceeding from wealth.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Principal, capital.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनलुब्ध
धनलुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Miserly, avaricious, greedy of wealth, mercenary.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and लुब्ध desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनलोभ|धनलोभः
धनलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Desire of wealth, greediness, avarice.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनवत्|धनवन्त्
धनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wealthy, opulent.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>The constellation Dhaniṣṭha.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनव्यय|धनव्ययः
धनव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Expenditure, extravagance.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसम्पत्ति|धनसंपत्ति
धनसम्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Accumulation of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and सम्पत्ति acquirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनसू
धनसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनस्यक|धनस्यकः
धनस्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant: see गोक्षुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहर|धनहरः
धनहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Inheriting, an heir.<BR>2 Stealing, a thief.<BR>3 Taking wealth, &c.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly called Cor.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, हृ to steal, affix अप्, or टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहरिन्
धनहरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>A thief, a pilferer.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहारिन्
धनहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Inheriting, an heir.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनहीन
धनहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor, reduced to poverty.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनागम
धनागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Accession of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनादान
धनादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acceptance of money.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकारिन्
धनाधिकारिन्<BR>mf. (-री-रिणी)<BR>An heir, an heiress.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A treasurer, a collector.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अधिकारिन् having a right to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिकृत
धनाधिकृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अधिकृत placed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाधिप|धनाधिपः
धनाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 A treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>धन riches, and अधिप lord; also similar compounds, धनाधिपति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाध्यक्ष|धनाध्यक्षः
धनाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 A treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनापहार|धनापहारः
धनापहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Fine, amercement.<BR>2 Plunder.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अपहार taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्च्चित|धनार्चित
धनार्च्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wealthy, opulent.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अर्च्चित respected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्ज्जन|धनार्जन
धनार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acquisition of property.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अर्ज्जन acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनार्थिन्
धनार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Seeking for wealth, covetous, miserly.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and अर्थिन् who wants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाशा
धनाशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Thirst of wealth, longing after riches.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, आशा hope, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनाश्री
धनाश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिक|धनिकः
धनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Pious, virtuous, excellent.<BR>2 Rich, opulent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wealthy man.<BR>2 A creditor.<BR>3 A husband.<BR>4 Coriander.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A virtuous or excellent woman.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>3 A young woman.<BR>4 A tree: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिन्
धनिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Wealthy, opulent.<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>1 A rich man.<BR>2 A creditor.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनिष्ठा
धनिष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>The twenty-fourth Nakṣatra or lunar mansion; it comprises four stars, apparently α β γ and δ Delphini, and is figured by a drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>धन to produce, (as corn,) affix अच् and मतुप् added, धनवत् again, इष्ठन् added, and मतुप् rejected, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीका
धनीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, ठक् affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनीयक|धनीयकं
धनीयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Coriander seed.<BR>E.<BR>धन to be produced, (as corn,) affix छ, and कन् added: see धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनु|धनुः
धनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 The sign Sagittarius.<BR>3 A tree: see प्रियाल.<BR>4 A measure of four cubits.<BR>E.<BR>धन here meaning to cast as an arrow, Uṇādi affix उ; also धनुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःकाण्ड|धनुःकांड
धनुःकाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A bow and arrow.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस्, and काण्ड an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःखण्ड|धनुःखंड
धनुःखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A bow, the stick or horns of the bow.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस्, and खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःपट|धनुःपटः
धनुःपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The Piyal tree, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and पट width; bending like a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःशाखा
धनुःशाखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A plant, from the leaves of which a tough thread is extracted, of which bow strings were formerly made: see मूर्व्वा, (Sanseviera zeylanica, Rox. but called by Sir WM. JONES, Aletris hyacinthoides.)<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुःश्रेणी
धनुःश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and श्रेणी a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्गुण|धनुर्गुणः
धनुर्गुण<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>A bow string.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, from which bow strings are made: see the two last.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and गुण a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्द्रुम|धनुर्द्रुमः
धनुर्द्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस्, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धर|धनुर्धरः
धनुर्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An archer, a bowyer, one armed with a bow.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and धर who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्धारिन्
धनुर्धारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An archer, a bowyer.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस्, and धारिन् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्भृत्
धनुर्भृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>An archer.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and भृत् who possesses: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्म्मध्य|धनुर्मध्य|धनुर्मध्यं
धनुर्म्मध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>The middle part of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, मध्य the centre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्म्मार्ग|धनुर्मार्ग|धनुर्मार्गः
धनुर्म्मार्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A curve line.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् an are, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्म्माला|धनुर्माला
धनुर्म्माला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, from the leaves of which bow strings were made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=437" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्य्यास|धनुर्यास|धनुर्य्यासः
धनुर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् for धन्वन् a dry soil, and यास here said to mean effort; also धन्वयास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्लता
धनुर्लता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The moon plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुर्वृक्ष|धनुर्वृक्षः
धनुर्वृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A plant; also called Dhāminiya.<BR>2 A bambu.<BR>3 A measure of four cubits.<BR>4 An are, a portion of the circumference of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्कर|धनुष्करः
धनुष्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bowyer, an archer.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, and कर who makes or practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्पट|धनुष्पटः
धनुष्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A tree: see धनुःपट.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, पट breadth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्पाणि
धनुष्पाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Armed with a bow.<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>An archer.<BR>E.<BR>धमुस्, and पाणि hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुष्मत्|धनुष्मन्त्
धनुष्मत्<BR>m. (-ष्मान्)<BR>An archer, a bowyer.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनुस्
धनुस्<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Armed with a bow.<BR>mn. (-नुः-नु)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 Sagittarius, the sign.<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The Piyal tree, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>धन to produce, (as grain,) to throw forth, (darts, &c.) Uṇādi affix उसि; also with उ affix धनु, and with ऊ affix, धनू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनू
धनू<BR>m. (-नूः)<BR>A bow: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेयक|धनेयकं
धनेयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Coriander: see धन्याक.<BR>E.<BR>धन grain, ढक् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेश|धनेशः
धनेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनेश्वर|धनेश्वरः
धनेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA, the Hindū PLUTUS.<BR>E.<BR>धन wealth, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनैषिन्
धनैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Wishing or claiming property.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A creditor.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and ऐषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धनोपचय
धनोपचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Accumulation of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन, and उपचय assembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्य|धन्यः
धन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 Fortunate, well fated, lucky.<BR>2 Good, virtuous.<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 An infidel, an atheist.<BR>2 A virtuous or fortunate man.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>1 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>2 A nurse.<BR>3 Coriander.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Wealth.<BR>E.<BR>धन to produce, (grain, &c.) or धन wealth, and यत् affix of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्यत्व
धन्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Luck, good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>धन्य, and त्व affix; also with तल् affix धन्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्याक|धन्याकं
धन्याक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A plant, bearing a small pungent seed used by the Hindus as a condiment, (Coriandrum sativum.)<BR>E.<BR>धन to produce, (as grain,) deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्व|धन्वं|धन्वः
धन्व<BR>n. (-न्वं)<BR>A bow: see धन्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वदुर्ग|धन्वदुर्गं
धन्वदुर्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A desart.<BR>E.<BR>धन्व the same, and दुर्ग strong, hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्
धन्वन्<BR>mn. (-न्वा-न्व)<BR>A bow.<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>A country scantily supplied with water, a desart, a waste.<BR>n. (-न्व)<BR>A firm spot, land, ground.<BR>E.<BR>धन्वि Sautra root, to go or move, (by or on which,) and कनिन् Uṇādi affix; also with अच् affix धन्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन|धन्वनः
धन्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly called Dhāminiya or Dhamin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरि|धन्वंतरि|धन्वंतरिः|धन्वन्तरिः
धन्वन्तरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 The physician of the gods, who was produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR>2 A celebrated physician; also काशिराज being the same as the preceding in another existence: he appears to have been the founder of the Hindu medical school.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>5 One of the nine gems of the court of VIKRAMĀDITYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता
धन्वन्तरिग्रस्ता<BR>f. (-स्ता)<BR>A medicinal plant: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>धन्वन्तारि, and ग्रस्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयवास|धन्वयवासः
धन्वयवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>E.<BR>धन्व dry soil, यु to unite, आसच् affix; also with कन् added धन्वयवासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्वयास|धन्वयासः
धन्वयास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant: see the last; also simply यास, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धन्विन्
धन्विन्<BR>m. (-न्वी)<BR>1 An archer, a bow-man.<BR>2 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>3 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>4 A wag, a wit, a sharp or shrewd man.<BR>E.<BR>धन्व a bow, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम|धमः
धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>One who blows a fire or a trumpet.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of the moon.<BR>2 KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A name of Yama.<BR>4 BRAHMA, or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा to blow, affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमक|धमकः
धमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A blacksmith.<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा to blow, (the forge,) कुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमधमा
धमधमा<BR>ind.<BR>Blowing reiteratedly, or the sort of sound made by blowing with a bellows or a trumpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धमन|धमनः
धमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 One who blows a bellows, a trumpet, &c.<BR>2 Cruel.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A reed, (Arundo tibialis or karka.)<BR>2 Blowing, (a wind instrument.)<BR>f. (-निः or -नी)<BR>1 Any tubular vessel of the body, as a vein, a nerve, &c.<BR>2 The neck.<BR>3 Turmerick.<BR>4 A sort of perfume; also हट्टविलासिनी.<BR>E.<BR>धम from ध्मा, to blow, &c. affix युच्, fem. affix इन् or ङीष् or ध्मा as before, Uṇādi affix अनि, and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मल|धम्मलः
धम्मल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The breast ornamented with gold or jewels: see धम्मिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धम्मिल्ल|धम्मिल्लः
धम्मिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>Braided and ornamented hair, tied round the head, and intermixed with flowers, pearls, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धम a Sautra root, to breathe, affix विच्, धम्; मिल to meet, लच् affix, and the two conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धय
धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यी-यं)<BR>Who or what drinks.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A little girl, female infant.<BR>E.<BR>घे to drink, affix श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर|धरः
धर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Who or what has or holds.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A flock of cotton.<BR>3 The tortoise Avatāra.<BR>4 One of the demigods called VASUS.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The uterus or womb.<BR>3 Marrow.<BR>4 A vessel of the body.<BR>5 A golden globe or heap of valuables, representing the earth, and given to Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>धृञ् to have or hold, to contain or support, &c. affix अच्, or ट fem. affix टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरण|धरणं|धरणः
धरण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 Holding, possessing, having.<BR>2 A sort of measure, a weight of ten Palas.<BR>3 A weight of silver, sixteen Māṣas.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The Himāla mountain considered as king of mountains.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A world.<BR>4 A breast, a female breast.<BR>5 Rice.<BR>6 A ridge of land answering the purpose of a bridge, the edge of a river, the skirt of a mountain, a bridge.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The silk cotton tree.<BR>3 A vessel of the body.<BR>4 An esculent root.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, to uphold or support, affix ल्युट्, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणि|धरणिः
धरणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to be contained, (animals, &c.) Uṇādi affix अणि; also धरणी as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिधर|धरणिधरः
धरणिधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>धरणि the earth, and धर who sustains; also धरणिधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणिस्थ
धरणिस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Being or staying on earth.<BR>E.<BR>धरणि, and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीकन्द|धरणीकन्दः
धरणीकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>An esculent root or bulb.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी the earth, कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीकीलक|धरणीकीलकः
धरणीकीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी the earth, कीलक a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=438" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीधर|धरणीधरः
धरणीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A tortoise: see धरणिधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीपूर|धरणीपूरः
धरणीपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी the earth, पूर to surround completely, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीप्लव|धरणीप्लवः
धरणीप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी the earth, and प्लव what swims; in which the earth floats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीश्वर|धरणीश्वरः
धरणीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी, and ईश्वर lord; lord of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरणीसुता
धरणीसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>धरणी the earth, and सुता daughter; the earth-born; being turned up from the soil by a plough, as JANAKA was ploughing a spot to prepare it for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरसंस्थ
धरसंस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Like a mountain, as huge as, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर, and संस्थ what is, or is like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराकदम्ब|धराकदम्बः
धराकदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba); also धराकदम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरात्मज|धरात्मजः
धरात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The planet Mars or its regent.<BR>E.<BR>धरा the earth, and आत्मज son, terræ-filius; also similar compounds, as धरासुत, धरापुत्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराधर|धराधरः
धराधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>धरा the earth, and धर who or what sustains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धराशय
धराशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sleeping on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>धरा, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरामर|धरामरः
धरामर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>धरा, and अमर a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरित्री
धरित्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to contain, (beings,) इत्र Uṇādi affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिमन्
धरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Form, figure, semblance.<BR>2 A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have or hold, Uṇādi affix इमनिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरिममेय
धरिममेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Measurable by weight.<BR>E.<BR>धरिम, and मेय to be measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धरुण|धरुणः
धरुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Heaven, paradise.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 Opinion, conception.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold or uphold, affix उनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्तव्य|धर्तव्य|धर्त्तव्यं
धर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be upheld or supported.<BR>2 To be had or possessed.<BR>3 To be placed or fixed.<BR>4 To be fallen or alighted by.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्तृ|धर्तृ
धर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Who or what has or holds.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्त्त्र
धर्त्त्र<BR>n. (-र्त्त्रं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 Sacrifice.<BR>3 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to contain, Uṇādi affix त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्म|धर्म|धर्मः|धर्म्मः
धर्म्म<BR>mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Virtue, moral and religious merit, according to the law and the Vedas.<BR>2 Usage, practice, the customary observances of caste, sect, &c.<BR>3 Duty, especially that enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>4 Fitness, propriety.<BR>5 Nature, character, proper or natural state or disposition.<BR>6 Innocence, innoxiousness.<BR>7 Resemblance.<BR>8 Any sacrifice.<BR>9 An Upaniṣad or theological portion of a Veda.<BR>10 Any peculiar or prescribed practice or duty; thus, giving, alms, &c. is the dharma of a householder; administering justice, the dharma of a king; piety, that of a Brahman; courage, that of a Kṣatriya, &c.<BR>11 Kind and virtuous speech or discourse.<BR>12 Law.<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 A name of YAMA, ruler of the lower regions, and judge of the dead.<BR>2 A drinker of the juice of the acid asclepias, at certain sacrifices.<BR>3 Virtue personified, born from the right breast of BRAHMĀ.<BR>4 A bow.<BR>5 Associating with the virtuous.<BR>6 The fifteenth of the twenty-four Jaina pontiffs of the present age.<BR>7 A pious or virtuous man.<BR>8 The bull of ŚIVA, a personification or type of virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to maintain or support, &c. Uṇādi affix मन्, what supports all men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकर्म्मन्|धर्मकर्मन्
धर्म्मकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Acting according to some or any indispensable act of piety or duty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकाय|धर्मकाय|धर्मकायः|धर्म्मकायः
धर्म्मकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, and काय body; virtue personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकार्य्य|धर्मकार्य
धर्म्मकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Any indispensable act of religion, &c.<BR>2 Religious or virtuous conduct.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म piety, and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकील|धर्मकील|धर्मकीलः|धर्म्मकीलः
धर्म्मकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An edict, a royal order, decree, or grant.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, कील proper stay; also with कन् added, धर्म्मकीलक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकृत्य|धर्मकृत्य
धर्म्मकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Any moral or religious observance.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and कृत्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकेतु|धर्मकेतु|धर्मकेतुः|धर्म्मकेतुः
धर्म्मकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, केत् an emblem or banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मकोष|धर्मकोष|धर्मकोषः
धर्म्मकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Store or treasure of virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and कोष treasury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मक्रिया|धर्मक्रिया
धर्म्मक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Righteous conduct, acting according to law.<BR>2 Any religious act.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मक्षेत्र|धर्मक्षेत्र|धर्मक्षेत्रः|धर्म्मक्षेत्रं
धर्म्मक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A plain in the north-west of India near Delhi, the scene of the great battle between the Kurus and Pāṇḍus.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A man of piety and virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, holiness, and क्षेत्र a field, literally or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मग्रहण
धर्म्मग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Observance of moral or religious institutes, accepting or following the law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मघ्न|धर्मघ्न
धर्म्मघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Immoral, unlawful, contrary to law or duty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचक्र|धर्मचक्र|धर्मचक्रः|धर्म्मचक्रः
धर्म्मचक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and चक्र a wheel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचक्रभृत्|धर्मचक्रभृत्
धर्म्मचक्रभृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, चक्र a circle, and भृत् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचारिन्|धर्मचारिन्
धर्म्मचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Virtuous, moral, dutiful.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>A virtuous woman, an honest wife.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म duty, चर to follow, affix णिनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचिन्तन|धर्मचिन्तन|धर्मचिंतन|धर्म्मचिन्तनं
धर्म्मचिन्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Virtuous reflection.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and चिन्तन reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिन्ता|धर्मचिंता
धर्म्मचिन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>Virtuous reflection.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and चिन्ता reflection: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मजीवन|धर्मजीवन|धर्मजीवनः
धर्म्मजीवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Brahman who lives according to rule, one who practices the outward acts of the law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञ|धर्मज्ञ|धर्म्मज्ञः
धर्म्मज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Knowing one's duty, conversant with virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मज्ञान|धर्मज्ञान
धर्म्मज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge of moral, legal, and religious duty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मण|धर्मण|धर्म्मणः
धर्म्मण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A sort of tree, commonly Dhāminiya.<BR>2 A kind of large snake, not poisonous, commonly Dhemana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मतस्|धर्मतस्
धर्म्मतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Rightly, justly, righteously.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मत्व|धर्मत्व|धर्मत्वं|धर्म्मत्वं
धर्म्मत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Morality, piety.<BR>2 Inherent nature, peculiar property, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मद्रवी|धर्मद्रवी
धर्म्मद्रवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, द्रु to shed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=439" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मद्रोहिन्|धर्मद्रोहिन्
धर्म्मद्रोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Wicked.<BR>(-ही)<BR>A Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and द्रोहिन् rebellious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मधातु|धर्मधातु|धर्मधातुः|धर्म्मधातुः
धर्म्मधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, धातु essence, root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मध्वजिन्|धर्मध्वजिन्
धर्म्मध्वजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A religious hypocrite or impostor, one who makes a livelihood by assumed devotion.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म piety, ध्वज an emblem, इनि affix; having every outward mark of piety, matted hair, ragged garments, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मनिबन्ध|धर्मनिबन्ध
धर्म्मनिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Piety, virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and निबन्ध attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मनिबन्धिन्|धर्मनिबन्धिन्
धर्म्मनिबन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>Pious, holy, engaged in or conducive to virtue.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, निबन्ध connexion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मनिष्पत्ति|धर्मनिष्पत्ति|धर्मनिष्पत्तिः
धर्म्मनिष्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Duty, moral or religious observance, discharge or fulfilment of duty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and निष्पत्ति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपत्तन|धर्मपत्तन|धर्म्मपत्तनं
धर्म्मपत्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pepper.<BR>2 The name of a district or city.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, पत्तन a city; pepper grows there, whence is said to be its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपत्नी|धर्मपत्नी
धर्म्मपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A man's first wife and of the same class.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and पत्नी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपत्र|धर्मपत्र|धर्म्मपत्रं
धर्म्मपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म sacrifice, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपर|धर्मपर
धर्म्मपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Righteous, pious.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and पर addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपाठक|धर्मपाठक|धर्मपाठकः
धर्म्मपाठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A teacher of law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and पाठक who teaches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मपुत्त्र|धर्मपुत्र|धर्मपुत्रः|धर्म्मपुत्त्रः|धर्म्मपुत्र
धर्म्मपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A name of the Pāṇḍu prince, YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>2 One so considered, as a son for piety or duty; also धर्म्मपुत्त्रक.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म a proper name, and पुत्त्र a son, the son of DHARMA or YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मप्रधान|धर्मप्रधान
धर्म्मप्रधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Eminent in piety.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and प्रधान chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मप्रवक्तृ|धर्मप्रवक्तृ
धर्म्मप्रवक्तृ<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A teacher or expounder of the law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and प्रवक्तृ who explains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मभागिनी|धर्मभागिनी
धर्म्मभागिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A virtuous and amiable wife.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and भागिनी who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मभाणक|धर्मभाणक|धर्मभाणकः|धर्म्मभाणकः
धर्म्मभाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lecturer, a public reader of the Mahābhārata and other sacred works which are read aloud, and explained to large assemblies of Hindūs at particular seasons.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, and भण to utter, to speak, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मभ्रातृ|धर्मभ्रातृ
धर्म्मभ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A fellow religious student.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and भ्रातृ a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मभिक्षुक|धर्मभिक्षुक|धर्मभिक्षुकः
धर्म्मभिक्षुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mendicant Brahman, one who is so, or has become so from meritorious motives.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and भिक्षुक a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्ममय|धर्ममय
धर्म्ममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Moral, righteous, made up or replete with virtue, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्ममूल|धर्ममूल|धर्म्ममूलं
धर्म्ममूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The foundation of Hindū law and religion (the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मयु|धर्मयु|धर्म्मयुः
धर्म्मयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Virtuous, righteous.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, यु to go, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मयुज्|धर्मयुज्
धर्म्मयुज्<BR>mfn. (-युक्)<BR>Righteous, pious, just.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, युज to join, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मराज|धर्मराज|धर्मराजः|धर्म्मराजः
धर्म्मराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A Jina or deified saint, according to the Jaina sect.<BR>2 A name of YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>3 A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>4 Also of ARJUNA.<BR>5 A king in general.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, justice, and राज who shines, affix अच्; or राज from राजन a king; lord of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मरोधिन्|धर्मरोधिन्
धर्म्मरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Illegal, immoral.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and रोधिन् opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मलक्षण|धर्मलक्षण
धर्म्मलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>An essential ingredient in ethics^1 or law, (as place, time, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and लक्षण mark.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मवत्|धर्मवत्|धर्मवन्त्
धर्म्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-बत्)<BR>Virtuous, pious, upright, just.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्मं as above, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मवासर|धर्मवासर|धर्मवासरः|धर्म्मवासरः
धर्म्मवासर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, and वासर a day; peculiar sacrifices being performed on this day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मवाहन|धर्मवाहन|धर्मवाहनः|धर्म्मवाहनः
धर्म्मवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म the bull of this god, virtue typified, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मविद्|धर्मविद्
धर्म्मविद्<BR>mfn. (-द् or -त्)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious, moral.<BR>2 Acquainted with the law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मविधि|धर्मविधि|धर्मविधिः
धर्म्मविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Course of law, legal precepts or injunctions.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and विधि manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मविप्लव|धर्मविप्लव|धर्मविप्लवः
धर्म्मविप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Immorality, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and विप्लव submersion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मविवेचन|धर्मविवेचन
धर्म्मविवेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Judicial investigation.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and विवेचन deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मशाला|धर्मशाला
धर्म्मशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A court of justice, a tribunal.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म justice, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मशास्त्र|धर्मशास्त्र|धर्म्मशास्त्रं
धर्म्मशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>1 The body or code of Hindu law.<BR>2 Any work on the subject.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, and शास्र a treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मशील|धर्मशील|धर्म्मशीलः
धर्म्मशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Virtuous, just, pious.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, शील attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसंहिता|धर्मसंहिता
धर्म्मसंहिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A code of laws, especially the work of some saint or divine person, as MANU, YĀJÑAVALKYA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, and सम् prefixed to धा, to have or possess, affix क्त, fem. affix टाप्; a compilation made for the purpose of teaching and maintaining virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसङ्ग|धर्मसङ्ग|धर्मसंग|धर्मसंगः
धर्म्मसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Virtue.<BR>2 Hypocrisy.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and सङ्ग addiction to, real or seeming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसन्तानसू|धर्मसन्तानसू
धर्म्मसन्तानसू<BR>mfn. (-सूः-सूः-सू)<BR>Virtuous, producing virtuous offspring or actions.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, सन्तान progeny, सू who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसभा|धर्मसभा
धर्म्मसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A tribunal, a court of justice.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म justice, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसाधन|धर्मसाधन
धर्म्मसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any act or virtue essential to a system of duties.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and साधन instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसावर्णि|धर्मसावर्णि|धर्म्मसावर्णिः
धर्म्मसावर्णि<BR>m. (-र्णिः)<BR>The eleventh MANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मसुत|धर्मसुत|धर्म्मसुतः
धर्म्मसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म YAMA, and सुत a son; also धर्म्मसूनु, धर्म्मात्मज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मात्मन्|धर्मात्मन्
धर्म्मात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A saint, a pious or virtuous person.<BR>E.<BR>घर्म्म virtue, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माधर्म्मपरीक्षा|धर्माधर्मपरीक्षा
धर्म्माधर्म्मपरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Ordeal by drawing lots or slips of black and white paper.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, अधर्म्म iniquity, परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माधिकरण|धर्माधिकरण|धर्माधिकरणः|धर्म्माधिकरणं|धर्म्माधिकरणः
धर्म्माधिकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A court of justice.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अधिकरण supervision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माधिकरणिन्|धर्माधिकरणिन्
धर्म्माधिकरणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A judge, a sovereign, an administrator of the law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्माधिकरण, and affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माधिकार|धर्माधिकार|धर्माधिकारः
धर्म्माधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The office of a judge.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माधिकारिन्|धर्माधिकारिन्
धर्म्माधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A judge.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्माधिकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माध्यक्ष|धर्माध्यक्ष|धर्माध्यक्षः|धर्म्माध्यक्षः
धर्म्माध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A magistrate, a judge, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म justice, and अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=440" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मानुष्ठान|धर्मानुष्ठान
धर्म्मानुष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Virtuous or moral conduct, behaviour according to law.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अनुष्ठान act or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मानुसार|धर्मानुसार|धर्मानुसारः
धर्म्मानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Conformity to law or virtue, course or practice of duty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मापेत|धर्मापेत
धर्म्मापेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wicked, immoral, unrighteous.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Immorality, vice.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अपेत deviated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्माभिमनस्|धर्माभिमनस्
धर्म्माभिमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, अभि to or inclined to, मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मारण्य|धर्मारण्य|धर्म्मारण्यं
धर्म्मारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A forest into which DHARMA once retired.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मासन|धर्मासन|धर्म्मासनं
धर्म्मासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The seat of the judge, the bench.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्मं, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मिन्|धर्मिन्
धर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>1 Virtuous, pious, just.<BR>2 Endowed with a peculiar property or faculty.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठ|धर्मिष्ठः
धर्म्मिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very pious or virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मीयस्|धर्मीयस्
धर्म्मीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very pious, moral, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मोपदेश|धर्मोपदेश|धर्मोपदेशः
धर्म्मोपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Moral or religious instruction.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मोपदेशक|धर्मोपदेशक|धर्मोपदेशकः|धर्म्मोपदेशकः
धर्म्मोपदेशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Guru or spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, उप before दिश to show, affix वुन्; pointing out good and evil to his scholars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मोपध|धर्मोपध
धर्म्मोपध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Hypocritical.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and उपधि fraud, अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्मोपेत|धर्मोपेत
धर्म्मोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Virtuous, moral.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्म्य
धर्म्म्य<BR>mfn. (-र्म्म्यः-र्म्म्या-र्म्मां)<BR>1 Conformable or according to justice or morality.<BR>2 Obtainable by virtue or justice.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म as above, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्म्म्यविवाह
धर्म्म्यविवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Legal marriage of five sorts, as the Brāhma, Daiva, Ārṣa, Gandharba, and Prājāpatya.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्मा, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ष|धर्षः
धर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>2 Contumely, overbearing.<BR>3 Impatience.<BR>4 Paralysing, rendering weak or impotent.<BR>5 Injury, wrong.<BR>6 Restraint.<BR>7 Copulation.<BR>8 A eunuch.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be vain, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षक|धर्षकः
धर्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dancer, an actor, a mime.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be vain or presumptuous, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षकारिणी
धर्षकारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A violated virgin.<BR>E.<BR>धर्ष, कृ to act, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षण|धर्षणं
धर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Disrespect, contumely, overbearingness or contempt.<BR>2 Copulation.<BR>3 Arrogance, vanity.<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be arrogant, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षवर
धर्षवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A eunuch superintending the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>धर्ष copulation, वृ to cherish, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षित|धर्षितं
धर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proud, insolent.<BR>2 Unbearing, impatient.<BR>3 Overpowered, smitten.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Copulation, cohabitation.<BR>2 Contumely.<BR>3 Pride.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be vain or impatient, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्षिन्
धर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>1 Proud, arrogant.<BR>2 Cohabiting.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A dishonest or unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>धर्ष cohabitation, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धलण्ड|धलण्डः
धलण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A small tree, commonly called Dhalākara; also धलण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव<BR>(इ,) धवि r. 1st cl. (धन्वति)<BR>To go or move: this is considered sometimes as a Sautra root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धव|धवः
धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A man.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>4 A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>धू to make tremble, (children, &c.) affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवल|धवलः
धवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 A capital ox.<BR>3 The Grislea tomentosa.<BR>4 Camphor.<BR>5 An inferior Rāga or mode of music.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>White pepper.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>A white cow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धाव to be clean or pure, कलच् affix, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलपक्ष|धवलपक्षः
धवलपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A goose.<BR>2 The fortnight of the moon's increase.<BR>E.<BR>धवल, and पक्ष a wing or fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलमृत्तिका
धवलमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>धवल white, मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलित
धवलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White, whitened.<BR>E.<BR>धवल, and इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलीकृत
धवलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White, made white.<BR>E.<BR>धवल, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलीभूत
धवलीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become white.<BR>E.<BR>धवल, and भूत become, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवलोत्पल|धवलोत्पलं
धवलोत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The white esculent water lily.<BR>E.<BR>धवल white, and उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवाणक|धवाणकः
धवाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, (the leaves of trees, &c.) and आणक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धवित्र|धवित्रं
धवित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A Pankhā or fan, made of antelope's skin, and used especially for blowing a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, इच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा<BR>(डु, ञ,) डुधाञ् r. 3rd cl. (दधाति धत्ते)<BR>1 To hold or support.<BR>2 To nurture, to maintain.<BR>3 To give.<BR>4 To have, to possess.<BR>With अनु and सम् prefixed,<BR>To search after.<BR>With अपि,<BR>To cover.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To speak, to speak to or address.<BR>2 To promulgate.<BR>3 To show.<BR>With अभि and सम,<BR>To overcome.<BR>With अव,<BR>1 To be careful.<BR>2 To attend to.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To take, to receive.<BR>With उप and आङ्,<BR>To support.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To uphold.<BR>2 To do, to perform.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To take up or hold up.<BR>2 To place in or upon.<BR>3 To be born or produced.<BR>4 To hold.<BR>With परि,<BR>To assume, to put on, as clothes, &c.<BR>With प्र and नि,<BR>1 To hold or support.<BR>2 To elevate or exalt, to dignify.<BR>3 To admit.<BR>With प्र.<BR>1 To be chief or first.<BR>2 To send.<BR>With प्रति and वि,<BR>To do, to perform.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To do, to execute, to act.<BR>3 To act conformably to religious ordinances, to execute the precepts of the Vedas.<BR>3 To choose, to select.<BR>4 To provide.<BR>5 To order or direct.<BR>6 To promise.<BR>7 To give.<BR>With वि and अव,<BR>To hide, to veil, to conceal.<BR>With सम,<BR>1 To place, to place firmly, to fix.<BR>2 To unite, to combine, to hold together.<BR>3 To shoot at a mark.<BR>With सम and प्र,<BR>To doubt, to discuss;<BR>(also with प्रति and सम्.)<BR>With सम and आङ्,<BR>To instruct, to teach.<BR>With सम and नि,<BR>To place or have near at hand. In the causal<BR>with उप,<BR>To understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धा
धा<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>1 A possessor, a holder, a container, &c.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, affix विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाक|धाकः
धाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An ox.<BR>2 Food.<BR>3 Boiled rice.<BR>4 A post.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have or hold, Uṇādi affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाटी
धाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Advancing towards or confronting an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=441" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाणक|धाणकः
धाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A weight of gold, a coin of that metal, the division of a Dīnāra.<BR>E.<BR>धा to contain, Uṇādi affix आणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातकी
धातकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, affix ण्वुल्, तन् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातु|धातुः
धातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 A principle or humour of the body, as phlegm, wind, and bile.<BR>2 Any constituent part of the body, as blood, flesh, &c.<BR>3 A primary or elementary substance, viz. earth, water, fire, air, and Ākāśa or atmosphere.<BR>4 The property of a primary element, odour, flavour, colour, touch, and sound.<BR>5 An organ of sense.<BR>6 A mineral, a fossil.<BR>7 A metal.<BR>8 A grammatical root; in Sanskrit this radical performs no other office, and cannot be used as a word without undergoing some change.<BR>E.<BR>धा to possess, to contain, (life, substance, &c.) तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुकाशीश
धातुकाशीश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Red sulphate of iron.<BR>E.<BR>धातु mineral, and काशीश the green sulphate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुघ्न|धातुघ्नं
धातुघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Sour gruel, prepared from the fermentation of rice water.<BR>E.<BR>धातु chyle, and घ्न destroying; also similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुनाशन|धातुनाशनं
धातुनाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sour gruel: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>धातु, and नाशन injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुप|धातुपः
धातुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The alimentary juice or chyle.<BR>E.<BR>धातु an essential constituent of the body, and प what cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुपुष्पिका
धातुपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see धातृपुष्पिका; also धातुपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुभृत्
धातुभृत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A robust man.<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Promoting the animal secretions.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a mineral, and भृत् what contains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमाक्षिक|धातुमाक्षिकं
धातुमाक्षिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mineral substance, a sulphuret of iron.<BR>E.<BR>धातु mineral, and माक्षिक the same substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुमारिणी
धातुमारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a metal, मृ to perish, in the causal form, णिनि and ङीप् affixes; the borate of soda is generally used in India as a flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुराजक|धातुराजकं|धातुराजकः
धातुराजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Semen, the seminal fluid.<BR>E.<BR>धातु animal fluid, &c. राज chief, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवल्लभ|धातुवल्लभं
धातुवल्लभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>धातु, and वल्लभ friend, a flux.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवादिन्
धातुवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An assayer, a miner, a mineralogist.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a mineral, वद to speak or describe, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुवैरिन्
धातुवैरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a metal, and वैरिन् an enemy; tarnishing metallic^1 lustre, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातुशेखर|धातुशेखरं
धातुशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Green sulphate of iron, or green vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a mineral, and शेखर crest or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातूपल|धातूपलः
धातूपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>धातु a mineral, and उपला stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृ
धातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A title of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A father, a parent.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A foster-mother, a nurse.<BR>3 The earth.<BR>4 Emblick myrobalan.<BR>mfn. (-ता-ती-तृ)<BR>1 A cherisher, a protector, fostering, nourishing.<BR>2 Having, containing, possessing, a possessor, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, to nourish, &c. affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृपुत्त्र
धातृपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A saint, also called SANATKUMĀRA.<BR>E.<BR>धातृ BRAHMĀ, and पुत्त्र the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धातृपुष्पिका
धातृपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Grislea tomentosa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>धातृ cherishing, पुष्प a flower, ङीष् added, धातृपुष्पी and कन् added; also without the pleonasm, धातृपुष्पी, f. (-ष्पी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रिका
धात्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Emblick myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to धात्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रीपुत्त्र
धात्रीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 An actor.<BR>2 A foster-brother.<BR>E.<BR>धात्री a nurse, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रीफल|धात्रीफलं
धात्रीफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fruit of the emblic myrobalan^1.<BR>E.<BR>धात्री Phyllanthus emblica, and फल fruit.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धात्रेयी
धात्रेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 A sort of confidante, a foster-sister so employed.<BR>2 A wet-nurse.<BR>E.<BR>धातृ a nurse, ढक् affix, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाना
धाना<BR>f. plu. (-नाः)<BR>1 Fried barley or rice. sin.<BR>(-नः)<BR>1 Coriander, (Coriandrum sativum.)<BR>2 Grain fried, and reduced to powder.<BR>3 A bud, a shoot.<BR>E.<BR>धा to nourish, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानाका
धानाका<BR>f. plu. (-काः)<BR>Fried barley or rice.<BR>E.<BR>धाना as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानाचूर्ण|धानाचूर्णं
धानाचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>The meal or flour of fried barley, rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धाना fried grain, चूर्ण powder, dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानी
धानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Coriander.<BR>2 A granary, a receptacle.<BR>3 The site of a habitation.<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>5 What has or contains, used in composition, as राजधानी a royal capital, having the king's presence; मत्स्यधानी a net, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, affix युच्, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्क|धानुष्कः
धानुष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>A bowyer, an archer.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् a bow, ठञ् affix.<BR>f. (-ष्का)<BR>A tree, (Achyranthes aspera).<BR>E.<BR>धनुष्क an archer, अण् affix, and fem. affix टाप्, or धनुस् a bow, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानुष्य|धानुष्यः
धानुष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>धनुस् as above, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धानेय|धानेयं
धानेय<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>Coriander, (Coriandrum sativum.)<BR>E.<BR>धन grain, &c. aff. ढक्; also with कन् added, धानेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्धा|धांधा
धान्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्य|धान्यं
धान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Corn in general, but especially rice, (Oriza sativa.)<BR>2 Coriander.<BR>3 A measure equal to four Sesamum seeds.<BR>E.<BR>धा to nourish (mankind), Uṇādi affix यत्, and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यक|धान्यकं|धान्यकः
धान्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Coriander, (C. sativum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to धान्य; also धन्याक and धान्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकल्क
धान्यकल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>Bran, chaff, straw.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and कल्क dirt or sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यकोष्ठक|धान्यकोष्ठकं
धान्यकोष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A granary, a basket, a cupboard or small shed of matting, &c. for keeping rice.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य rice, कोष्ठ a granary, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यचमस|धान्यचमसः
धान्यचमस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Rice flattened by threshing after it has been steeped, and fried in the husk.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य grain, and चमस a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यधेनु|धान्यधेनुः
धान्यधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A heap of rice to be presented to Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and धेनु a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यमाय|धान्यमायः
धान्यमाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A corn-seller, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य grain, मा to measure, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यराज|धान्यराजः
धान्यराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and राजा king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवत्|धान्यवन्त्
धान्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Abounding in corn, having abundance of it.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवर्द्धन
धान्यवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Lending grain at interest; receiving a usurious return for a loan of seed corn supplied to the peasants.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य corn, वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीज
धान्यवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यवीर|धान्यवीरः
धान्यवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus max.)<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and वीर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यशीर्षक|धान्यशीर्षकं
धान्यशीर्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The ear or spike of corn.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, with शीर्षक the top or head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=442" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यसङ्ग्रह|धान्यसंग्रह
धान्यसङ्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A store or magazine of grain.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and सङ्ग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यसार|धान्यसारः
धान्यसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Grain after threshing.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य corn, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याक|धान्याकं
धान्याक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>अण् added to धन्याक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याचल|धान्याचलः
धान्याचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A pile of grain for presentation to Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याम्ल|धान्याम्लं
धान्याम्ल<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Sour gruel made of the fermentation of rice water.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य rice, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यारि|धान्यारिः
धान्यारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यार्थ|धान्यार्थः
धान्यार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>Wealth in rice or grain.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and अर्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यास्थि
धान्यास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>Grain after threshing.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्योत्तम|धान्योत्तमः
धान्योत्तम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Rice.<BR>E.<BR>धान्य, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 A house, a dwelling.<BR>3 Dignity, consequence, eminence.<BR>4 Spirit, pride, especially martial pride, heroism.<BR>5 Light, splendour, radiance.<BR>6 A ray of light.<BR>7 A place, a spot^1, a country.<BR>8 Birth.<BR>E.<BR>धा to contain, (life, a tenant, &c.) and मनिन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनिधि|धामनिधिः
धामनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>धाम light, निधि a nest or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनी
धामनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Any tubular vessel of the body: see धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामवत्|धामवन्त्
धामवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Splendid, luminous.<BR>2 Eminent, exalted, illustrious.<BR>3 Heroic.<BR>E.<BR>धामन्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामार्ग्गव|धामार्गव|धामार्गवः
धामार्ग्गव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>1 A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>2 A plant, a sort of Ghosha, with white flowers.<BR>E.<BR>धामन् a dwelling, मार्ग a road, ब to go or approach, affix क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय|धायः
धाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Having, possessing, or who has or possesses.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
धायस्<BR>mfn. (-याः-याः-यः)<BR>An upholder.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, &c. असुन् Uṇādi affix; also with a final vowel added, धायस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्य|धाय्यः
धाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A Purohita or family priest.<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>A prayer for exciting fire, upon the addition of fuel.<BR>E.<BR>irregularly derived from धी to contain, with ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Water derived from rain.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of stone.<BR>2 Debt.<BR>3 Slight sprinkling rain.<BR>4 Frost.<BR>5 End, bound, a line or limit.<BR>6 A deep place, a depth.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A horse's pace, as the trot, canter, &c.<BR>2 The van of an army.<BR>3 The sharp edge of a sword or any cutting instrument.<BR>4 The flowing, running, oozing, or distilling, &c. of any liquid, the motion of a fluid, stream, current, &c.<BR>5 Offspring.<BR>6 A leak, a flaw, a hole in a pitcher, &c.<BR>7 Excellence.<BR>8 The wheel of a carriage.<BR>9 A garden wall or fence, a hedge, &c.<BR>10 The edge of a mountain.<BR>11 Quantity, multitude.<BR>12 A heavy shower falling in large drops, or hail.<BR>13 Fame.<BR>14 Likeness.<BR>15 Custom, usage.<BR>16 The capital of BHOJA.<BR>17 Pouring a stream of water upon an image to get rid of a fever.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to fall, to uphold, &c. in the causal form, and अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what holds or contains, a vessel or receptacle of any kind.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A water pot.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Holding, having, keeping, maintaining.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Continuance in rectitude, keeping in the right way.<BR>2 Fortitude, firmness, steadiness, resolution.<BR>3 A particular religious exercise; keeping the mind collected, the breath suspended, and all natural wants restrained; steady, immoveable abstraction.<BR>4 Mental retention, memory.<BR>5 Understanding, intellect.<BR>6 Believing, conviction.<BR>7 Certainty, conclusion.<BR>8 Positive precept or injunction.<BR>9 Debt.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>2 A mystical verse or charm, or collection of such verses, among the Bauddhas.<BR>3 A row or line.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, (purpose, intent, virtue, &c.) affix ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणक|धारणकः
धारणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A debtor.<BR>E.<BR>धारण a debt, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणीय
धारणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be held or retained, to be adhered to.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारय|धारयः
धारय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who or what has or possesses.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, causal form, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयत्
धारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Having, possessing.<BR>2 Acquainted with, versed in.<BR>3 Holding as doctrine, believing, maintaining.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयित्री
धारयित्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to contain, in the causal form, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराकदम्बक
धाराकदम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्कुर|धारांकुर|धाराङ्कुरः
धाराङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Thin rain.<BR>2 Hail.<BR>3 Advancing before an army by way of defiance to an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>धारा rain, and अङ्कुर shoot or sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराङ्ग|धारांग|धाराङ्गः
धाराङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A sword, a scimitar.<BR>2 A place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>धारा the edge of a sword, &c. and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराट|धाराटः
धाराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 A furious elephant.<BR>E.<BR>धारा rain, &c. अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराध्वनि
धाराध्वनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>The sound of falling rain or of the flowing of any fluid.<BR>E.<BR>धारा, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराधर|धाराधरः
धाराधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A sword.<BR>E.<BR>धारा rain or an edge, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारायन्त्र|धारायंत्र
धारायन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A scent bottle, a sprinkling vase or ewer, a sort of censer.<BR>E.<BR>धारा, and यन्त्र an instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावनि|धारावनिः
धारावनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>धारा thin rain, वन to sound, affix इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराविष|धाराविषः
धाराविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A crooked sword, a scimitar, a sabre.<BR>E.<BR>धारा, and विष poison; whose edge is as fatal as venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराश्रु
धाराश्रु<BR>n. (-श्रु)<BR>A flood of tears.<BR>E.<BR>धारा, and अश्रु a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासम्पात|धारासंपात|धारासंपातः|धारासम्पातः
धारासम्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A hard shower, a heavy fall of rain.<BR>E.<BR>धारा rain, सम् implying quantity or accumulation, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारासार|धारासारः
धारासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A heavy fall of rain, a large drop or shower.<BR>E.<BR>धारा, and आसार sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिणी
धारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>E.<BR>धृ, and घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारित
धारित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A horse's trot; also धारितकंः see धौरितकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Having, holding, keeping, possessing.<BR>2 Edged.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A sort of tree: see पीलु.<BR>E.<BR>धारा an edge, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारु|धारुः
धारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Who drinks or sucks, a drinker, a sucker.<BR>E.<BR>धे to drink, रु affix, form special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्त्तराष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>1 A sort of goose, with black legs and bill.<BR>2 A kind of snake.<BR>3 DURYODHANA or any other descendant of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>धृतराष्ट्र the name of a king or a bird, &c. and अण् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=443" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म्मिक|धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिकः
धार्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Virtuous, pious, just.<BR>E.<BR>धर्म्म virtue, affix ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्य|धार्य|धार्य्यं
धार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be born or upheld, to be contained, &c.<BR>2 To be kept or detained.<BR>3 To be determined.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्यमाण|धार्यमाण
धार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being held, maintained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to uphold, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य्यमाणत्व|धार्यमाणत्व
धार्य्यमाणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Property.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट्य|धार्ष्ट्यं
धार्ष्ट्य<BR>n. (-र्ष्ट्यं)<BR>Boldness, confidence, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>धृष्टि bold, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव
धाव<BR>(उ) धावु r. 1st cl. (धावति-ते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To run.<BR>3 To cleanse.<BR>4 To be clean or pure.<BR>With अनु,<BR>1 To know.<BR>2 To run after.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>To approach, to come before.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To alight.<BR>With परि,<BR>To run fast.<BR>With वि,<BR>To shed or sprinkle.<BR>With सम् and उग्र,<BR>To run to meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Running, going, swift, expeditious.<BR>2 Cleaning, what cleans or cleanses.<BR>E.<BR>धाव to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावत्|धावन्त्
धावत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Running, going quickly.<BR>E.<BR>धाव to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावन|धावनं
धावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 Cleansing, purifying.<BR>f. (-निः) or (-नी)<BR>A sort of creeping plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>धाव to go, to cleanse, affix ल्युट् or अनि fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनिका
धावनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A prickly nightshade: see कण्टकारी.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to धावनी, implying similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
धावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Purified, clean, cleansed.<BR>2 Gone, gone or run away.<BR>3 Run to, advanced to or against.<BR>E.<BR>धाव to clean, affix क्त, with इट् augment, or without the augment धौत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>धा to uphold, Uṇādi affix असुन् and षुट् augment; the word is considered as peculiar to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि<BR>r. 6th cl. (धियति)<BR>To have or hold, to keep, to possess.<BR>5th cl. (धिनोति)<BR>1 To satisfy.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of reproach or menace, (fie, shame, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>धक्क to annihilate, डिक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कार|धिक्कारः
धिक्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Disrespect, reproach, censure, contempt.<BR>E.<BR>धिक् fie, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृत|धिक्कृतः
धिक्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cursed.<BR>2 Reproached, reviled, censured, condemned.<BR>E.<BR>धिक् fie, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्क्रिया
धिक्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Reproach.<BR>E.<BR>धिक् fie, and क्रिया making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्पारुष्य
धिक्पारुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Excessive abuse.<BR>E.<BR>धिक्, and पारुष्य violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष
धिक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (धिक्षते)<BR>1 To kindle.<BR>2 To be weary.<BR>3 To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वण|धिग्वणः
धिग्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A man of a low caste sprung from a Brahman, and a female of the tribe called Ayogava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्दण्ड|धिग्दंड|धिग्दण्डः
धिग्दण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Reprimand, censure.<BR>E.<BR>धिक्, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Deceptive, wishing to trick or deceive.<BR>E.<BR>दम्भ to cheat, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धियाम्पति|धियांपति|धियाम्पतिः
धियाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A Jina or Jaina deified saint.<BR>2 The soul.<BR>E.<BR>धी the understanding, in the seventh case, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिव
धिव<BR>(इ,) धिवि r. 1st and 5th cl. (धिनोति)<BR>1 To please, to satisfy.<BR>2 To be pleased or satisfied.<BR>3 To go or approach: this verb takes उ, and substitutes अ for the final, whence its unusual form for the first class, in the instance given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष
धिष<BR>r. 3rd cl. (दिधष्टि)<BR>To emit sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषण|धिषणः
धिषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>2 Any Guru or spiritual preceptor.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The understanding, the intellect.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be presumptuous, Uṇādi affix क्यु, and धिष substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ट्य|धिष्ट्यं|धिष्ट्यः
धिष्ट्य<BR>See धिष्ण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ठ्य
धिष्ठ्य<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य<BR>n. (-ष्ण्यं)<BR>1 A place, a spot, a country.<BR>2 A house.<BR>3 A star, an asterism.<BR>4 Fire.<BR>5 Power, strength.<BR>m. (-ष्ण्यः)<BR>A name of AGNI, the deity of fire.<BR>2 A name of ŚUKRA, regent of VENUS.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be proud or overbearing, deriv. irr.; the word is also written धिष्ट्य or धिष्ठ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी<BR>(ओ ङ) ओ धीङ् r. 4th cl. (धीयते)<BR>1 To contain, to hold.<BR>2 To slight, to disregard or despise.<BR>3 To accomplish.<BR>With अन्तर्,<BR>To disappear, to become invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी<BR>f. (-धीः)<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, affix क्विप्, the final diphthong rejected, and the semi-vowel changed to its congener इ, which becomes long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drank, sucked.<BR>E.<BR>धे to drink, participial affix क्त, and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीति|धीतिः
धीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Thirst.<BR>E.<BR>धे to drink, affix क्तिन्, and the radical vowel changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A virgin, a maiden.<BR>2 Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीन्द्रिय|धींद्रिय|धीन्द्रियं
धीन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An intellectual organ, as the mind, the eye, the ear, the nose, the tongue, and skin.<BR>E.<BR>धी the intellect, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धीमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Sensible, wise, learned.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>धी wisdom, understanding, मतुप् possess. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Wise, sensible, learned.<BR>2 Firm, steady, consistent, determined.<BR>3 Cool, collected.<BR>4 Head-strong, selfwilled, uncontrollable.<BR>5 Lazy, dull, slow.<BR>6 Strong, powerful.<BR>7 Well behaved, decorous, decent.<BR>8 Gentle, steady, (as a breeze.)<BR>9 Deep, (as a sound.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BALI, a celebrated prince.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A drug; also काकोली.<BR>2 A woman who, although jealous of a husband or lover, suppresses all expression of resentment in his presence.<BR>E.<BR>धी understanding, रा to possess, क affix; or धी with ईर to go to, affix अण्; or धी to possess, क्तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरत्व|धीरत्वं
धीरत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Firmness, fortitude.<BR>2 The feminine property of suppressing violent expression of jealousy.<BR>E.<BR>धीर firm, steady, affix त्व; also with तल् affix धीरता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरप्रशान्त|धीरप्रशांत|धीरप्रशान्तः
धीरप्रशान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The hero of a poem or play who unites all good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>धीर, and प्रशान्त calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरललित|धीरललितः
धीरललित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The hero of a poem or play, who is firm and brave, but reckless and inconsiderate.<BR>E.<BR>धीर, and ललित sportive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरस्कन्द
धीरस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>धीर strong, स्कन्द a shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीराधीरा
धीराधीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A mistress or wife, who having cause for jealousy, pursues a middle conduct between the suppression and expression of resentment.<BR>E.<BR>धीरा, and अधीरा joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोदात्त|धीरोदात्तः
धीरोदात्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>The hero of a poem or play whose characteristics are benevolence and fortitude.<BR>E.<BR>धीर, and उदात्त liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=444" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरोद्धत|धीरोद्धतः
धीरोद्धत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The hero of a poem or play who is deficient in magnanimity.<BR>E.<BR>धीर, and उद्धत haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटी
धीलटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>1 A brazier.<BR>2 A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, Uṇādi affix कनिन्, and ऋ changed to ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवर|धीवरः
धीवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A fisherman's wife.<BR>2 A sort of harpoon for catching fish with.<BR>E.<BR>धी to hold or gain, (fish,) Uṇādi affix ष्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीशक्ति|धीशक्तिः
धीशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>An intellectual faculty or power of the understanding, as attention, comprehension, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धी the intellect, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसख|धीसखः
धीसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A counsellor, an adviser, a minister.<BR>2 A tutor or friend.<BR>E.<BR>धी the understanding, and सखि a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीसचिव|धीसचिवः
धीसचिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A counsellor, a minister.<BR>2 A friendly or prudent adviser.<BR>E.<BR>धी the intellect, and सचिव a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु<BR>(ञ) धुञ् r. 7th cl. (धुनोति धुनुते)<BR>To shake, to agitate: see धू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु<BR>f. (धुः)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष
धुक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (धुक्षते)<BR>1 To kindle.<BR>2 To be weary.<BR>3 To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, deserted, left.<BR>2 Shaken, agitated, (as leaves by wind, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुतपाप
धुतपाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Purified from sin.<BR>E.<BR>धुत shaken, पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनन
धुनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, agitation.<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, affix ल्यु; also धूनन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनान
धुनान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनि|धुनिः
धुनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A river; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>धु to go, affix नुक्, fem. affix ङीप्; the affix is sometimes considered as निक्, leaving नि, which makes धुनि ut sup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनीनाथ|धुनीनाथः
धुनीनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>धुनी, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्धुमार|धुंधुमारः|धुन्धुमारः
धुन्धुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The name of a sovereign; also named Kuvalayāśva.<BR>2 An insect, (Coccinella.)<BR>3 The smoke of a house.<BR>4 A house lizard (?)<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke reiterated, ऋ to go, affix अण्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वत्|धुन्वन्त्
धुन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन्वान
धुन्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धु to shake, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर्<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>1 The fore part of a carriage, the pole or the part where the yoke is fixed.<BR>2 Agitation, trembling.<BR>3 Reflection, recollection.<BR>4 A spark of fire.<BR>5 A burthen, a load.<BR>6 A part, a portion.<BR>7 Wealth.<BR>8 A name of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्ब्ब to hurt, affix क्विप्, and व rejected; also with टाप् added, धुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरन्धर|धुरंधर|धुरन्धरः
धुरन्धर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Bearing a burthen.<BR>2 Bearing, (figuratively,) laden with good qualities, heavy duties, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A man of business.<BR>3 A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>धुर् a burthen, and धृ to have, affix खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A burthen, a load.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्व्व to hurt, affixes क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Bearing, (as a burthen.)<BR>2 Charged with, abounding with, (qualities, duties, &c.)<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A man of business.<BR>E.<BR>धुर् a burthen, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Fit for a load, suited to a burthen.<BR>2 Charged with important duties.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A man of business.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य्य|धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Fit for a burthen, adapted to it, &c.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A minister, a charge d'affaires.<BR>3 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>धुर् a burthen, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्व|धुर्व
धुर्व्व<BR>(इ) धुर्व्वी r. 1st cl. (धुर्व्वति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्वह|धुर्वह
धुर्व्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Bearing a load, a burthen.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A minister, a charge d'affaires.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्, and वह who bears; also धुरावह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवका
धुवका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The introductory stanza to a song, forming afterwards the burthen of each verse.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, अक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवन|धुवनः
धुवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A title of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवित्र|धुवित्रं
धुवित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A sort of fan made of deer skin, and used especially to excite a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, इत्र affix; also धवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुर|धुस्तुरः
धुस्तुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura fastuosa): see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तूर|धुस्तूरः
धुस्तूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Thorn apple, (Datura fastuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>धूष to make handsome, affix क्विप्, तूर् to be mischievous, affix क्; elegant but deleterious: the vowels are also both made short, as धुस्तुर, or both remain long, as in धूस्तूर; also written धुत्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू<BR>(ञ) धूञ् r. 5th cl. (धूनोति धूनुते) r. 6th cl. (धूवति) r. 9th cl. (धुनाति धुनीते) r. 1st and 10th cls. (धवति-ते धावयति-ते or धूनयति)<BR>To shake or agitate, to make tremble.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>1 To abandon, to quit.<BR>2 To perceive.<BR>With निर्,<BR>1 To destroy.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR>With वि,<BR>To make tremble or agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूक|धूकः
धूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The air or wind.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 Time.<BR>E.<BR>धु to agitate, कन् Uṇādi affix, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूक्ष
धूक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (धूक्षते)<BR>1 To live.<BR>2 To kindle.<BR>3 To be distrest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, agitated.<BR>2 Reproached, reviled.<BR>3 Abandoned, deserted.<BR>4 Judged, discriminated.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>धू to shake, &c. affix क्त; this root also forms धून with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतकल्मष
धूतकल्मष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Pure, free from sin.<BR>E.<BR>धूत shaken, पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Distressed by heat or thirst.<BR>2 Shaken, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>धू to shake, affix क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनक|धूनकः
धूनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Resin; it is sometimes read धूणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनन|धूननं|धूननः
धूनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धू to shake, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनि|धूनिः
धूनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, affix क्तिन्, and त changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप<BR>r. 1st cl. (धूपायति)<BR>To heat.<BR>r. 10th cl. (धूपयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप|धूपः
धूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Incense, the aromatic vapour that proceeds from the combustion of any fragrant gum or resin, the use of which is authorized by scripture.<BR>E.<BR>धूप to heat, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपन|धूपनं|धूपनः
धूपन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Resin.<BR>2 Incense.<BR>E.<BR>धूप to heat, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपवृक्ष|धूपवृक्षः
धूपवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A species of pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>धूप incense or resin so used, and वृक्ष a tree; also with कन् added, धूपवृक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपाङ्ग|धूपांग|धूपाङ्गः
धूपाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>धूप, and अङ्ग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=445" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपायित|धूपायितः
धूपायित<BR>mn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>2 Incensed, perfumed with incense.<BR>E.<BR>धूप (to heat, &c.) affix क्त, आय inserted, or the passive form with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिका
धूपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Mist, fog.<BR>E.<BR>धूप incense, कन् affix of resemblance, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपित|धूपितः
धूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Suffering pain or fatigue.<BR>2 Scented, perfumed, incensed.<BR>E.<BR>धूप to heat, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम|धूमः
धूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Smoke.<BR>2 A saint.<BR>E.<BR>धूम to agitate, Uṇādi affix क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतन|धूमकेतनः
धूमकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 KETU, the personified descending node.<BR>2 Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमकेतु|धूमकेतुः
धूमकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 A comet or falling-star.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 The personified descending node.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and केतु a mark or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमध्वज|धूमध्वजः
धूमध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and ध्वज a sign or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमप्रभा
धूमप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A division of hell, the hell of smoke.<BR>E.<BR>धूम, and प्रभा what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूममहिषी
धूममहिषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>Fog, mist.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, महिषी a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमयोनि|धूमयोनिः
धूमयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and योनि womb; what is engendered from smoke or vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमल|धूमलः
धूमल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a purple colour.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Purple, a colour compounded of black and red.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and ल what is, being of the hue of smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमसंहति|धूमसंहतिः
धूमसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A cloud or quantity of smoke.<BR>E.<BR>धूम, and संहति collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमसी
धूमसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A cake of pulse steeped in water, and dried in the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाकार
धूमाकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Of the form or appearance of smoke.<BR>E.<BR>धूम, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमाभ|धूमाभः
धूमाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Of a purple colour.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Purple.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and आभ resembling; of a smoky hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमावलि|धूमावलिः
धूमावलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A wreath or cloud of smoke.<BR>E.<BR>धूम, and आवलि a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिका
धूमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Fog, vapour.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोर्णा
धूमोर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>The wife of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, and ऊर्ण wool; of a smoky hue, and woolly-headed, a Caffree Proserpine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमोर्णापति|धूमोर्णापतिः
धूमोर्णापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>YAMA, the ruler of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>धूमोर्णा as above, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्या
धूम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>A quantity of smoke.<BR>E.<BR>धूम with य affix, implying aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्याट|धूम्याटः
धूम्याट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike. धूम्या much smoke, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>Of a purple or smoky colour.<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>Purple; the colour; a compound of red and black.<BR>n. (-म्रं)<BR>Sin, vice, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, रा to get, affix क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रक|धूम्रकः
धूम्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र smoky, कन् affix; of a smoky or tawny hue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रलोचन|धूम्रलोचनः
धूम्रलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र dark, लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्ररुच्
धूम्ररुच्<BR>mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>Of a purple colour.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र, and रुच् to shine, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रवर्ण|धूम्रवर्णः
धूम्रवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Of a smoky hue.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Incense.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>Flame, or one of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र smoky or purplish, and वर्णं colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राक्षि|धूम्राक्षिः
धूम्राक्षि<BR>m. (-क्षिः)<BR>A pearl of a bad colour.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र smoky, अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राट|धूम्राटः
धूम्राट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र smoky, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्राभ|धूम्राभः
धूम्राभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>धूम्र smoky, आभ who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रिका
धूम्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Sisu tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to धूम्र, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूयमान
धूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Agitated, shaken.<BR>E.<BR>धू to shake, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर
धूर<BR>(ई,) धूरी r. 4th cl. (धूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To kill or hurt.<BR>2 To move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्ज्जटि|धूर्जटि|धूर्जटिः
धूर्ज्जटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>धुर् a burthen, and जटि a collection, from जट to collect, and इन् affix; who collects or bears the burthen of the three worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्त|धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Fraudulent, crafty, dishonest, knavish, &c.<BR>2 Mischievous, injurious.<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 A gamester.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 Thorn apple, (Datura.)<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Rust or iron filings.<BR>2 Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्व्व to injure, Uṇādi affix तन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तक|धूर्तक|धूर्तकः|धूर्त्तकः
धूर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>2 A cheat, a rogue, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त crafty, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तकितव|धूर्तकितव|धूर्तकितवः
धूर्त्तकितव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A gamester.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त, and कितव a knave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तकृत्|धूर्तकृत्
धूर्त्तकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Dishonest, a knave, a rogue, a cheat.<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>Thorn apple: see धुस्तूर.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्तं mischievous, and कृत् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तजन्तु|धूर्तजन्तु|धूर्तजंतु|धूर्त्तजन्तुः
धूर्त्तजन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>Man.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त crafty, and जन्तु an animal; the subtlest of all animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तता|धूर्तता
धूर्त्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Knavery, roguery, knavishness.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त, and तल् affix; also with त्व, धूर्त्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तमण्डल|धूर्तमण्डल
धूर्त्तमण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A party of rogues or gamblers.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त a cheat, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त्तमानुषा|धूर्तमानुषा
धूर्त्तमानुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant: see रास्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्धर|धूर्धरः
धूर्धर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Bearing a load or burthen.<BR>2 Managing affairs.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A beast of burthen.<BR>E.<BR>धूर् a burthen, and धर bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्वह|धूर्वह|धूर्वहः|धूर्व्वहः
धूर्व्वह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Bearing a load, who or what does so.<BR>2 Managing affairs.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्वी|धूर्वी
धूर्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>The fore part or pole of a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>धुर्व्व to injure, affix अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलक|धूलकं
धूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलि|धूलिः
धूलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-लिः or -ली)<BR>1 Dust.<BR>2 A number.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, affix लि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिका
धूलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Fog or mist.<BR>E.<BR>धलि dust, कन् affix of resemblance; the dust of the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिकुट्टिम
धूलिकुट्टिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A mound, a rampart.<BR>E.<BR>धूलि dust or earth, and कुट्टिम prepared ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिकेदार|धूलिकेदारः
धूलिकेदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mound, a rampart of earth.<BR>E.<BR>धूलि dust, and केदार a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिगुच्छक|धूलिगुच्छकः
धूलिगुच्छक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The red vegetable powder thrown about at the spring festival called the Holī.<BR>E.<BR>धूलि dust, and गुच्छक a nosegay; also धूलिगुच्छ m. (-च्छः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिध्वज|धूलिध्वजः
धूलिध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>धूलि dust, and ध्वज sign or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलीकदम्ब|धूलीकदम्बः
धूलीकदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A species of the Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR>2 Tila, a plant.<BR>3 A tree: see वरुण (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>E.<BR>धली dust, and वदम्ब Kadamba, whose pollen perhaps resembles that of the Kadamba, or having a similar [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">Page447</a>] quantity of blossoms; also with कन् added धूलीकदम्बक; these words are also written with a short इ, as धूलिकदम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=446" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलीपटल|धूलीपटलः
धूलीपटल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cloud of dust.<BR>E.<BR>धूली, and पटल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूश
धूश<BR>r. 10th cl. (धूशयति)<BR>To make splendid or elegant; also धूष, and धूस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूष
धूष<BR>r. 10th cl. (धूषयति)<BR>To make splendid or elegant; also धूश and धूस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस
धूस<BR>r. 10th cl. (धूसयति)<BR>To embellish, to make splendid or elegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसर|धूसरः
धूसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Grey, of that colour.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Grey, (the colour.)<BR>2 A jackass.<BR>3 An oilman.<BR>4 A camel.<BR>5 A pigeon.<BR>6 Any thing of a grey tint.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female Kinnara or chorister of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>धू to agitate, (the mind,) सर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरछदा|धूसरच्छदा
धूसरछदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A plant commonly Śvetarāsnā.<BR>E.<BR>धूसर grey, and छद a leaf, grey-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्तूर|धूस्तूरः
धूस्तूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The thorn apple, (Datura metel and fastuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>धूस् elegant, and तूर injurious: see धुस्तुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ<BR>(ङ) धृङ् r. 1st cl. (धरते)<BR>To fall.<BR>r. 6th cl. (ध्रियते)<BR>1 To continue, to remain.<BR>2 To have or hold.<BR>(ञ) धृञ् r. 1st cl. (धरति-ते)<BR>To have or hold, to keep, to maintain.<BR>r. 1st cl. (धरति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>r. 10th cl. (धारयति)<BR>To hold.<BR>With अप or निर् prefixed,<BR>To verify, to make sure or certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज
धृज<BR>r. 1st cl. (धर्जति) also (ई) धृजि r. 1st cl. (धृंजति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
धृत्<BR>mfn. (-धृत्)<BR>Who has, holds, possesses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Possessed, held, contained.<BR>2 Cherished, supported.<BR>3 Stood, stayed, standing.<BR>4 Alighted, gone down.<BR>5 Placed.<BR>6 Considered, weighed.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतकार्मुकेषु|धृतकार्म्मुकेषु
धृतकार्मुकेषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Armed with bow and arrow.<BR>E.<BR>धृत, कार्म्मुक a bow, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतपट
धृतपट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Covered or overspread with a cloth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धृत, and पट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतराष्ट्र|धृतराष्ट्रः
धृतराष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A proper name; DHṚTARĀṢṬRA, the father of DURYODHANA, and uncle of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>2 A good king.<BR>3 A Nāga or serpent of the lower regions.<BR>4 A kind of bird, perhaps a sort of goose: see धार्त्तराष्ट्र.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A goose, the female bird only.<BR>E.<BR>धृत possessed, cherished, (by whom,) राष्ट्र a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतवत्|धृतवन्त्
धृतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Held, was holding.<BR>2 Having taken or conveyed.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतहेति
धृतहेति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Armed.<BR>E.<BR>धृत, and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतात्मन्
धृतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Firm, steady, calm, collected.<BR>E.<BR>धृत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृताम्भस्
धृताम्भस्<BR>mfn. (-म्भाः-म्भाः-म्भः)<BR>Full of water.<BR>E.<BR>धृत, and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृति|धृतिः
धृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Sacrifice, offering, religious rite or ceremony.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Holding, having.<BR>2 Steadiness, firmness.<BR>3 One of the astrological Yogas: see योग.<BR>4 Pleasure.<BR>5 Satisfaction, content.<BR>6 Happiness.<BR>7 A metre; a stanza of four lines of eighteen syllables each.<BR>8 The thirteenth Mātṛkā.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to have, &c. affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमत्|धृतिमन्त्
धृतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Firm, steady, calm.<BR>2 Content.<BR>E.<BR>धृति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमुष्
धृतिमुष्<BR>mfn. (मुट्)<BR>Discomposing, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>धृति firmness, and मुष् what steals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>1 Virtue, morality.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>3 The sea.<BR>4 The sky.<BR>5 A clever man.<BR>6 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, क्वनिप् affix, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वरी
धृत्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, क्वरप् affix, and तुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वा
धृत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken or held.<BR>E.<BR>धृ, and क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष
धृष<BR>r. 5th cl. (ञि-आ) ञिधृषा (धृष्णाति)<BR>To be proud, to be confident or presumptuous.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (धर्षति धर्षयति)<BR>To overcome, to overbear, to resist impatiently, to be impatient.<BR>(उ) धृषु r. 1st cl. (धर्षति)<BR>1 To collect.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR>(ङ) धृषङ् r. 10th cl. (धर्षयते)<BR>To neutralise, paralyse or make powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषु|धृषुः
धृषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>1 A clever man.<BR>2 A proud one.<BR>3 A heap.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be confident, Uṇādi affix कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Impudent, confident, bold, shameless.<BR>2 Forward, intrusive, presumptuous.<BR>3 Secured, obtained.<BR>4 Profligate, abandoned.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A faithless husband.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be confident, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज्<BR>mfn. (-ष्णक्)<BR>Confident, impudent, shameless.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be confident, नजिङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णि|धृष्णिः
धृष्णि<BR>m. (-ष्णिः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be arrogant, नि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Confident, bold.<BR>2 Impudent, shameless.<BR>f. (-ष्णुः)<BR>The branch of a bambu.<BR>E.<BR>धृष to be arrogant, affix क्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धॄ
धॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (धृणाति^1)<BR>To be or grow old.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: cf. WIL1819 or MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे<BR>r. 1st cl. (ट्) धेट्^1 (धयति) also (ङ्) धेङ् (धयते)<BR>To drink.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by SergeA on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batche 313. note: Also, wa -> w, Na -> N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेन|धेनः
धेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A male river.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>धे to drink, Uṇādi affix न; what is drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनु|धेनुः
धेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A milch cow, one that has lately calved.<BR>E.<BR>धे to drink, Uṇādi affix नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुक|धेनुकः
धेनुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of an Asura or demon, killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A she-elephant.<BR>2 A milch cow.<BR>E.<BR>धेनु a cow, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकसूदन|धेनुकसूदनः
धेनुकसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>धेनुक a demon, so called, and सूदन the destroyer; also similar compounds, as धेनुकहन्, धेनुकारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकादुग्ध
धेनुकादुग्ध<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>1 Cow's milk.<BR>2 A plant: see चिर्भिट.<BR>E.<BR>धेनुका, and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकारि
धेनुकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A small tree, Nagesara.<BR>E.<BR>धेनुक, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>A cow at the dairy or tied up to be milked.<BR>E.<BR>धेनु a milch cow, यत् affix, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेय
धेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be held.<BR>2 Denominated, called.<BR>E.<BR>धा to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुक|धैनुकं
धैनुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A herd of milch cows.<BR>E.<BR>धेनुका a milch cow, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य्य|धैर्य|धैर्यं|धैर्य्यं
धैर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Steadiness, firmness.<BR>E.<BR>धीर firm, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्य्यकलित|धैर्यकलित
धैर्य्यकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Steady, calm, assuming firmness or composure.<BR>E.<BR>धैर्य्य, and कलित made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत|धैवतः
धैवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The sixth note of the gamut.<BR>E.<BR>धी intellect, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=447" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोड|धोडः
धोड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A sort of snake, commonly Dhora, a kind of watersnake.<BR>E.<BR>धू to make tremble, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर
धोर<BR>(ऋ) धोरृ r. 1st cl. (धोरति)<BR>To move well, to be quick or alert, or to have good paces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरण|धोरणं
धोरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A vehicle in general, any means of conveyance, as a horse, an elephant, a car, &c.<BR>2 A horse's trot.<BR>3 Going well or quickly.<BR>E.<BR>धोर to move well or quickly, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणि|धोरणिः
धोरणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>Tradition.<BR>E.<BR>धोर to proceed, affix अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरित|धोरितं
धोरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A horse's trot.<BR>E.<BR>धोर to go well, affix क्त; also with कन् added, धोरितक n. (-कं) and with अण् again added, धौरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Washed, cleaned, purified.<BR>2 Bright and shining.<BR>3 White.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>धाव to make clean, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकट|धौतकटः
धौतकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A bag of coarse cloth, a sack.<BR>E.<BR>धौत washed, and कट a mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकोषज|धौतकोषजं
धौतकोषज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Bleached or wild silk.<BR>E.<BR>धौत pure or washed, कोष the cocoon, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतकौशेय|धौतकौशेयं
धौतकौशेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Bleached or wild silk.<BR>E.<BR>धौत pure or washed, कोश a cocoon, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतशिल|धौतशिलं
धौतशिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>धौत pure, शिला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौमक|धौमकः
धौमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a district.<BR>E.<BR>धूम smoke, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरितक|धौरितकं
धौरितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A horse's trot: see धोरितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेय|धौरेयः
धौरेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Fit for burthen, capable of taking or bearing it, (either a vehicle or a beast, &c.)<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A beast of burthen.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>धूर् a burthen, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्त्तिक|धौर्तिक|धौर्तिकं|धौर्त्तिकं
धौर्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a cheat, knavish, fraudulent, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>E.<BR>धूर्त्त a cheat, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्य्य|धौर्य|धौर्यं|धौर्य्यं
धौर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A horse's trot.<BR>E.<BR>धोर to go well, affix यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा<BR>r. 1st cl. (धमति)<BR>1 To blow, as a wind instrument, to produce sound by blowing.<BR>2 To blow a fire, to excite fire by blowing.<BR>3 To apply fire.<BR>4 To excite sparks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माकार|ध्माकारः
ध्माकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blacksmith.<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा blowing, from ध्मा to blow, affix क्विप्, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माक्ष
ध्माक्ष<BR>(इ) ध्माक्षि r. 1st cl. (ध्मांक्षति)<BR>1 To desire.<BR>2 To crow or caw: see ध्राक्ष and ध्वाक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माक्ष
ध्माक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 Any aquatic bird.<BR>2 A crow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ध्माक्ष to crow or caw, अच् affix; more usually read ध्वाङ्क्ष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मात
ध्मात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तुं)<BR>1 Inflamed, excited.<BR>2 Blown into or up, inflated.<BR>3 Blown by a bellows, (a fire, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा to blow, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मामन्
ध्मामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Measure.<BR>2 Light.<BR>3 Meditation.<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा to blow or breathe, Uṇādi affix मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मायमान
ध्मायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being melted or refined.<BR>2 Being inflated.<BR>E.<BR>ध्मा to blow, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thought, meditated.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातव्य
ध्यातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be thought or reflected upon.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to think, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Meditation, reflection, but especially that profound and abstract consideration which brings its object fully and undisturbedly before the mind.<BR>2 Mental representation of the personal attributes of the divinity to whom worship is addressed.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानयोग|ध्यानयोगः
ध्यानयोग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The performance of religious abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यान meditation, &c. योग a religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानपर
ध्यानपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Meditating, reflecting.<BR>E.<BR>धान, and पर engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानतत्पर
ध्यानतत्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Reflecting.<BR>E.<BR>धान, and तत्पर absorbed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानीय
ध्यानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be meditated upon.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to think, and अनीथर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Black.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass.<BR>2 A plant, (Artemisia.)<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to think, मक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामन्
ध्यामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Meditation.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Measure.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, and मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याममूर्द्धज
ध्याममूर्द्धज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Having dishevelled hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यायत्
ध्यायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Thinking of, meditating upon.<BR>E.<BR>ध्य to think, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्येय|ध्येयः
ध्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be meditated or pondered.<BR>E.<BR>ध्यै to meditate, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्यायति)<BR>To recollect, to call to mind, to meditate, to think; with the preposition नि, to see, to look, to look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज
ध्रज<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्रजति)<BR>To go;<BR>also (इ) ध्रञ्जि r. 1st cl. (ध्रंजति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण
ध्रण<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्रणति)<BR>To sound, as a drum or other instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस
ध्रस<BR>r. 10th cl. (ध्रसयति)<BR>To throw or toss up.<BR>(उ) उध्रस r. 9th cl. (ध्रस्नाति)<BR>To glean: the root is by some authorities read उध्रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राक्ष
ध्राक्ष<BR>(इ) ध्राक्षि r. 1st cl. (ध्रांक्षति)<BR>1 To utter the sound of birds, or to crow, caw, &c.<BR>2 To desire: see ध्वाक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख
ध्राख<BR>(ऋ) ध्राखृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राखति)<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>2 To adorn.<BR>3 To suffice, to be able or competent.<BR>4 To refuse, to prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ
ध्राघ<BR>(ऋ) ध्राघृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राघते)<BR>To be able on competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राजि|ध्राजिः
ध्राजि<BR>f. (-जिः)<BR>A whirlwind, a gale.<BR>E.<BR>ध्रज to go, इ Uṇādi affix, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड
ध्राड<BR>(ऋ) ध्राडृ r. 1st cl. (ध्राडति)<BR>To divide, to split, to cut or pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राडि|ध्राडिः
ध्राडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>Gathering flowers.<BR>E.<BR>ध्राड to divide, affix इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज
ध्रिज<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्रेजति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रियमाण
ध्रियमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Being held or sustained.<BR>2 Being withheld, checked, suppressed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>धृ to hold, passive v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्रवति) r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>1 To be firm or fixed.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव<BR>r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>1 To stand firm.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Eternal.<BR>2 Fixed, stable, firm.<BR>3 Continual, permanent.<BR>4 Certain, ascertained.<BR>5 Spread, extended.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>4 The polar star or north pole itself; in mythology, personified by DHRUVA, the son of UTTĀNAPĀDA, and grandson of the first MANU.<BR>5 The pole of any great circle, particularly either of the celestial poles.<BR>6 (In Astronomy,) The distance of a planet from the beginning of the sydereal zodiac.<BR>7 Any epoch to which a computation of dates is referred.<BR>8 One of the demigods called VASUS.<BR>9 The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>10 The Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>11 One of the twenty-seven astronomical Yogas, or the Yoga star of the twelfth lunar asterism, supposed to be β Leonis.<BR>12 A sort of bird: see शराटि.<BR>n. (-वं) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">Page449</a>]<BR>1 Ascertainment, certainty.<BR>2 Logie, reasoning, discussion.<BR>3 Heaven.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A sacrificial vase made in the shape of the Indian fig leaf, and of the wood of the Flacourtia sapida.<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>3 A small tree from the fibres of which bow strings are made: see मूर्व्वा.<BR>4 The introductory stanza of a song: it is distinct from the verses of the song, after each of which it is again repeated as a burden or chorus.<BR>5 A virtuous woman.<BR>E.<BR>ध्रु to be fixed, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=448" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवक|ध्रुवकः
ध्रुवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>2 Longitude.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The introductory stanza and burden of a song: see ध्रुवा.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रू
ध्रू<BR>r. 6th cl. (ध्रुवति)<BR>1 To be firm, to stand fast.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक
ध्रेक<BR>(ऋ) ध्रेकृ r. 1st cl. (ध्रेकते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To grow or increase.<BR>3 To be exhilarated or elevated with joy.<BR>4 To manifest elevation or hilarity by noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
ध्रै<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्रायति)<BR>To be satisfied or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव्य|ध्रौव्यं
ध्रौव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Firmness, fixedness.<BR>2 Duration.<BR>E.<BR>ध्रुव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस<BR>(उ) ध्वंसु r. 1st cl. (ध्वंसते)<BR>1 To fall down.<BR>2 To reduce to powder.<BR>3 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस|ध्वंसः
ध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Loss, destruction.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A mote in a sun-beam.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वंस to fall, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Perishing, dying.<BR>2 Loss, destruction.<BR>3 Going.<BR>4 Falling.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वंस to fall down, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसित
ध्वंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Lost, destroyed.<BR>2 Vexed, incensed.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वंस to fall down, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Destructive, destroying.<BR>2 Suffering loss, perishing.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A Pilu tree, said to grow in mountainous districts.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वंस to fall, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्वजति) also (इ) ध्वजि r. 1st cl. (ध्वंजति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज|ध्वजः
ध्वज<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>1 A flag or banner.<BR>2 A mark, a sign or symbol.<BR>3 The penis.<BR>4 The upper part of a skull carried on a stick, as a penance for the murder of a Brahman.<BR>5 A house situated to the east of any object.<BR>6 A flag-staff.<BR>7 (In Prosody,) An Iambic.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A distiller.<BR>2 Pride.<BR>3 Hypocrisy, fraud.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज to go, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजद्रुम|ध्वजद्रुमः
ध्वजद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज a banner, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजप्रहरण|ध्वजप्रहरणः
ध्वजप्रहरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज a flag, and प्रहरण who seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजभङ्ग|ध्वजभङ्गः
ध्वजभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Impotence.<BR>2 Fracture or fall of a banner.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजवत्|ध्वजवन्त्
ध्वजवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a mark or sign.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 An ensign, a standard-bearer.<BR>2 A distiller, a vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>3 A Brahman who having slain another, carries the skull of the murdered man with him to places of pilgrimage by way of penance.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज as above, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजराजिन्
ध्वजराजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Bearing or displaying ensigns.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज, and राज to shine, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजांशुक
ध्वजांशुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flag.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज, and अंशुक a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Having a flag or sign, &c.<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A car or carriage.<BR>4 A snake.<BR>5 A horse.<BR>6 A peacock.<BR>7 A distiller or vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>8 A standard-bearer.<BR>9 An armiger, one having an emblem or sign.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An army.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज symbol, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजीकरण|ध्वजीकरणं
ध्वजीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Raising a standard.<BR>2 Taking an emblem, &c.<BR>3 Making any thing a plea, or setting up as a claim or right.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजोत्थान|ध्वजोत्थानं
ध्वजोत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The twelfth day of the light half of Bhādra, a festival in honour of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वज a flag, and उत्थान elevating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण
ध्वण<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्वणति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन|ध्वनः
ध्वन<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्वनति) r. 10th cl. (ध्वनयति ध्वानयति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन|ध्वनः
ध्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, अच् affix: see ध्वान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनत्
ध्वनत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>Sounding, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनमोदिन्
ध्वनमोदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>The humble bee.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन sound, and मोदिन् who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनयत्|ध्वनयन्त्
ध्वनयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Sounding, resounding, echoing with.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनि|ध्वनिः
ध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 Sound.<BR>2 Figurative or poetical style.<BR>3 The sound of a drum.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, इ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिग्रह|ध्वनिग्रहः
ध्वनिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वनि sound, ग्रह the recipient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनित|ध्वनितः
ध्वनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sounded, making a noise, as a drum, &c.<BR>2 Poetical, figurative, rhetorically expressed.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिनाला
ध्वनिनाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The Vīṇā or lute.<BR>2 A pipe, a fife.<BR>3 A sort of trumpet.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वनि sound, and नाला a hollow tube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिविकार|ध्वनिविकारः
ध्वनिविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Change of voice, through fear, grief, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वनि sound, विकार change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Fallen.<BR>2 Destroyed, perished, lost.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वंस to fall, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाक्ष
ध्वाक्ष<BR>(इ) ध्वाक्षि r. 1st cl. (ध्वांक्षति)<BR>1 To utter a cry peculiar to birds, as to croke, caw, &c.<BR>2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वांक्षः|ध्वाङ्क्षः
ध्वाङ्क्ष<BR>m. (-ङ्क्षः)<BR>1 Any aquatick bird, as a crane, a gull, &c. feeding upon fish.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 One of the Nāgas.<BR>4 A beggar.<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षी)<BR>1 A drug: see काकोली.<BR>2 A female imp or fiend.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष to cry, affix अच्; it and its derivatives may also be read ध्माक्ष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्ट|ध्वांक्षपुष्ट|ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्टः
ध्वाङ्क्षपुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow, and पुष्ट fostered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षराविन्
ध्वाङ्क्षराविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि)<BR>Having a voice like a crow.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow, and रव sound, affix णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षाराति|ध्वांक्षाराति|ध्वाङ्क्षारातिः
ध्वाङ्क्षाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वाङ्क्ष a crow, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वाङ्क्षाली
ध्वाङ्क्षाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal plant: see काकोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान|ध्वानः
ध्वान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वांतं|ध्वान्तं
ध्वान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वन to sound, क्त affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तवित्त|ध्वांतवित्त|ध्वान्तवित्तः
ध्वान्तवित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>The firefly.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वान्त darkness, and वित्त wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तशात्रव|ध्वांतशात्रव|ध्वान्तशात्रवः
ध्वान्तशात्रव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 A sort of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>2 The sun or any luminous body.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वान्त darkness, and शात्रव averse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्ताराति|ध्वान्तारातिः
ध्वान्ताराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sun or any luminous body.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वान्त darkness, and अरानि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वान्तोन्मेष|ध्वांतोन्मेष|ध्वान्तोन्मेषः
ध्वान्तोन्मेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The firefly.<BR>E.<BR>ध्वान्त darkness, and उन्मेष twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (ध्वरति)<BR>1 To bend, to make crooked.<BR>2 To kill.<BR>3 To describe. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">Page450</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=449" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न<BR>The twentieth consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, corresponding with the letter N.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न<BR>mfn. (नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Thin, spare.<BR>2 Vacant, empty.<BR>3 Identical, same, like.<BR>4 Unvexed, unwearied.<BR>5 Undivided, unbroken.<BR>m. (नः)<BR>1 A Bauddha, a follower of Buddha.<BR>2 Binding, tying.<BR>3 One who is praised.<BR>4 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>5 War.<BR>6 Giving, a gift.<BR>7 Good, welfare, prosperity.<BR>8 A jewel.<BR>f. (ना)<BR>1 The navel.<BR>2 A musical instrument.<BR>3 Knowledge.<BR>ind.<BR>1 No, not, a particle of prohibition.<BR>2 A particle of comparison.<BR>3 A particle of negation, annihilation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नी to obtain, or नह to bind, &c., ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नःक्षुद्र|नःक्षुद्रः
नःक्षुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Small-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>नस् the nose, क्षुद्र small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशुक|नंशुकः
नंशुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Injurious, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>नश to destroy, णुकन् Uṇādi affix, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंष्टृ
नंष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>An injurer, injurious, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>नश to destroy, affix तृच्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुट|नकुटं
नकुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुल|नकुलः
नकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Disgraced, rejected from a family or race.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The Bengal mungoose, (Viverra ichneumon.)<BR>2 A proper name, NAKULA, the fourth of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>3 A son.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Silk cotton tree.<BR>2 Indian spikenard.<BR>3 A sort of perfume: see शङ्खिनी.<BR>4 Saffron.<BR>5 The letter ह as used in the Tantras.<BR>E.<BR>न not, कुल race or heap, fem. affix ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेश|नकुलेशः
नकुलेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A Bhairava, an attendant on or emanation from ŚIVA.<BR>2 The letter ह as used mystically in Tantras.<BR>E.<BR>नकुल, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलेष्टा
नकुलेष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A plant: see रास्ना.<BR>E.<BR>नकुल an ichneumon, and इष्ट wished; the mungoose, if wounded in a conflict with a poisonous snake, is supposed to prevent the effects of the venom by the use of this plant; also नकुलेष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क
नक्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (नक्कयति)<BR>To destroy or annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>नज to be ashamed, तन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तक|नक्तकः
नक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Dirty or ragged cloth.<BR>2 A rag, a wiper, a handkerchief, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नज to be ashamed or modest, affix तन्, and कन् added; also लक्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तचारिन्
नक्तचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Going or moving about at night.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 An owl.<BR>3 A goblin.<BR>4 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>नक्त by night, चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तञ्चर|नक्तंचर|नक्तञ्चरः
नक्तञ्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going at night.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A goblin, a demon.<BR>2 A tree, the Bdellium tree: see गुग्गुल.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>नक्तं by night, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तभोजन
नक्तभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Supper.<BR>E.<BR>नक्त night, भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तम्
नक्तम्<BR>ind.<BR>By night, at night.<BR>E.<BR>नज to be ashamed, तन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमाल|नक्तमालः
नक्तमाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Galedupa arborea, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>नक्तम् by night, अल to ornament, आङ् prefix, and अच् affix; blossoming at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तमुखा
नक्तमुखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>नक्तम् by night, उख to produce, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तव्रत|नक्तव्रतं
नक्तव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Fasting by day and eating at night.<BR>2 Any religious rite or obligation observed at night.<BR>E.<BR>नक्त, and व्रत vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्र|नक्रं|नक्रः
नक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>The upper timber of a door-frame.<BR>nf. (-क्रं-क्रा)<BR>The nose.<BR>f. (-क्रा)<BR>A string of bees or wasps.<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A crocodile.<BR>E.<BR>न not, क्रम to go, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्रराज्
नक्रराज्<BR>m. (-राट्) or नक्रराज (-जः)<BR>A shark, but applied also differently: see ग्राह.<BR>E.<BR>नक्र a crocodile, and राज् or राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्र|नक्षत्रं
नक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A star in general.<BR>2 An asterism in the moon's path or lunar mansion, of which twenty-eight, distinct in name, figure, and number of stars, are enumerated; the Paurānic and popular enumeration of those constellations is twenty-seven; Abhijit, the twenty-seventh, being considered as formed of portions of the two contiguous asterisms, and not distinct from them.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>णक्ष to go, Uṇādi affix अत्रन् or क्षद Sautra root, to injure, or क्षर to drop, or क्षी to waste or decay, with the negative prefix, and ष्ट्रन् affix; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रचक्र|नक्षत्रचक्रं
नक्षत्रचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 A particular diagram for astrological calculations.<BR>2 The lunar asterisms collectively.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र, and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रनेमि|नक्षत्रनेमिः
नक्षत्रनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The pole-star.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>The last of the asterisms, Revatī, containing thirtytwo stars.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र a star, and नेमि circumference^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रप|नक्षत्रपः
नक्षत्रप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र, and प who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रमाला
नक्षत्रमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A necklace containing twenty-seven pearls.<BR>2 The table of the asterisms in the moon's path.<BR>3 A kind of dance.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र a constellation, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रेश|नक्षत्रेशः
नक्षत्रेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र an asterism, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख<BR>r. 1st cl. (नखति)<BR>To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख|नखं|नखः
नख<BR>mn. (-खः-खी)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A part, a portion.<BR>nf. (-खं-खी)<BR>A perfume, a dried substance, of a brown colour, and of the shape of a nail; apparently, a dried shell fish, used as a perfume.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A vegetable perfume, different from the one above, though known by the same name, NAKHI.<BR>E.<BR>न privative, ख sense; or नह to bind, ख Uṇādi affix, the radical ह rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखकुट्ट|नखकुट्टः
नखकुट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, and कुट्ट who cuts; barbers in India trim the nails, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखखादिन्
नखखादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Who or what eats with nails or talons.<BR>E.<BR>नस्व, and खादिन् eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखदारण|नखदारणः
नखदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A falcon.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, and दारण tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखपद
नखपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A scratch, the mark of a finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and पद a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखभिन्न
नखभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Torn, or torn off with a nail.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and भिन्न divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखमुच|नखमुचं|नखमुचः
नखमुच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, मुच to let loose, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखम्पच|नखंपच
नखम्पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>What scalds the nail.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and पच to cook, खश aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखर|नखरं|नखरः
नखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A perfume: see नस्वी.<BR>E.<BR>न not, खन to go, and डर affix; or नख a nail, रा to go or be, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरञ्जनी|नखरंजनी
नखरञ्जनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A nail-parer.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and रञ्जनी beautifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरायुध|नखरायुधः
नखरायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 Any beast of prey.<BR>3 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>नखर a nail, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखलेखा
नखलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A scratch.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखविलेख
नखविलेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A scratch.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and विलेखा a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=450" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखविष्किर|नखविष्किरः
नखविष्किर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>What tears or rends, (as a bird of prey, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>नख, and विष्किर what scatters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखव्रण|नखव्रणः
नखव्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A scratch.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and व्रण a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखशङ्ख|नखशंख|नखशङ्खः
नखशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>A small shell.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, शङ्ख a shell, one as small as a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखांशु
नखांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>Elegance of the finger nails.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखाङ्क|नखांक|नखाङ्कं|नखाङ्कः
नखाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A scratch, a mark of the nail.<BR>2 A sort of perfume.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखायुध|नखायुधः
नखायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 A cock.<BR>4 Any beast or bird having talons.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखालि|नखालिः
नखालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A small shell.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, and आलि a line; also नखालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखाशिन्
नखाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>नख a nail, and अशिन् who eats, using its claws in feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखिन्
नखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>Nailed, clawed, having nails or talons.<BR>E.<BR>नख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग|नगः
नग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>न not, गम to go, affix ड, immoveable; or दह to burn, Uṇādi affix ग, ह rejected, and द changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगज|नगजः
नगज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Mountain, mountaineer.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>नग a mountain, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगणा
नगणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum halicacabum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगनन्दिनी|नगनंदिनी
नगनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नग a mountain, and नन्दिनी a daughter, being in one of her characters the daughter of Himāla, the snowy Imaus personified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगपति|नगपतिः
नगपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Himāla, the personified range of snowy mountains dividing India from Tartary, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नग mountain, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगभिद्
नगभिद्<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>1 A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR>2 An axe, a crow.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and भिद् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगभू
नगभू<BR>mfn. (-भूः-भूः-भु)<BR>Mountain, mountaineer.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगमूर्द्धन्
नगमूर्द्धन्<BR>m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>The crest or brow of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and मूर्द्धन् forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगर|नगरं
नगर<BR>mf. (-रं-री)<BR>A town, a city.<BR>E.<BR>नग a tree, or according to some, a mountain, रल् affix; having trees or houses like mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरघात|नगरघातः
नगरघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>नगर a city, and घात who destroys or subverts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरजन|नगरजनः
नगरजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Towns-folk, citizens.<BR>E.<BR>नगर, and जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरस्थ|नगरस्थः
नगरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>City, citizens.<BR>E.<BR>नगर, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरस्वरूपिणी
नगरस्वरूपिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीवक|नगरीवकः
नगरीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>नगरी, and वक a crane, the town-crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरोपान्त|नगरोपांत|नगरोपान्तः
नगरोपान्त<BR>m. (-न्तं)<BR>Suburb, skirts of the town.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and उपान्त vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरौषधि|नगरौषधिः
नगरौषधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>The plantain.<BR>E.<BR>नगर a city, and औषधि a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाटन|नगाटनः
नगाटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>नग a mountain, अट to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाधिप|नगाधिपः
नगाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Himāla: see नगपति.<BR>E.<BR>नग a mountain, and अधिप a lord; also नगाधिराज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगाश्रथ
नगाश्रथ<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Living in or frequenting mountains.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगोच्छ्राय|नगोच्छ्रायः
नगोच्छ्राय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The elevation of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>नग, and उच्छ्राय heighth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगौकस्
नगौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>3 A fabulous animal: see शरभ.<BR>4 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>नग a tree, a mountain, and ओकस् a house or dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Naked.<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>1 A naked mendicant.<BR>2 A Bauddha.<BR>3 A bard.<BR>f. (-ग्ना)<BR>A naked woman.<BR>E.<BR>नज to be ashamed, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नक|नग्नकः
नग्नक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Naked.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नजित्
नग्नजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The name of a king, father of one of KṚṢṆA'S wives.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न Bauddha, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नत्व
नग्नत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Nudity, nakedness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to नग्न; also with तल्, नग्नता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नहू
नग्नहू<BR>mn. (-हूः-हु)<BR>Ferment, a drug used to throw the mixture for spirituous liquor into fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न naked, and ह्वे to call, affix. क्विप्, what is called for by the barefaced, shameless, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नाट|नग्नाटः
नग्नाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A naked man, but especially a kind of religious mendicant, who wanders about without clothes.<BR>2 A Bauddha.<BR>3 A Jain.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न naked, and अट who goes; also with कन् added नग्राटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्निका
नग्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A girl before menstruation or about ten years old.<BR>2 A naked woman.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न naked, कन् added, and the fem. form: see नग्नक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकरण
नग्नीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Stripping, undressing.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकृत
नग्नीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Undressed, stripped, naked.<BR>E.<BR>नग्न, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज
नज<BR>(ओ ई) ओनजी r. 6th cl. (नजते) also (इ, ओ) ओनजि r. 1st cl. (नञ्जते)<BR>To be ashamed, to be modest or bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नञ्
नञ्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of negation, prohibition, &c. (no, not): see अ and न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (नटति नाटयति)<BR>1 To dance, to dance as an actor, to act.<BR>2 To drop or fall.<BR>3 To shake, to move slightly.<BR>4 To injure.<BR>5 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट|नटः
नट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A dancer, a mime, an actor, a Nut, &c. in modern times: in caste, the son of a degraded Kṣatriya by a woman of the second caste.<BR>4 A sort of reed, (Arundo tibialis, or latterly called A. karka, Roxburgh's Catalogue); also नड and नल.<BR>5 A subordinate mode of music.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A sort of shrub, (Cæsalpinia bonduccella.)<BR>(-टी)<BR>1 A medicinal plant: see नली.<BR>2 A whore.<BR>3 A Nach girl, a dancer, an actress.<BR>4 Red arsenick: see नली.<BR>5 A Rāgiṇī.<BR>E.<BR>नट to dance, affix अच्, and टाप् or ङीष्; otherwise, नश to destroy, Uṇādi affix डट, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटन|नटनं
नटन<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>The art or act of dancing, pantomime, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नट to dance, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटनारायण|नटनारायणः
नटनारायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A Rāga or mode of music, according to some, the sixth, or to others, a subdivision of Dīpaka or of Megha.<BR>E.<BR>नट, and नारायण VIṢṆU: the supreme with dancers, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटपर्ण
नटपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटपत्रिका
नटपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The egg-plant (Solanum melongena.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=451" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटमण्डन|नटमंडन|नटमण्डनं|नटमण्डनः
नटमण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>नट an actor, and मण्डन adorning; dying theatrical raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटवर|नटवरः
नटवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A chief dancer or actor.<BR>E.<BR>नट, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटसज्ञक
नटसज्ञक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>2 An actor, a dancer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नट an actor, सज्ञा a name, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटश्रेष्ठ
नटश्रेष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A chief or excellent dancer or actor.<BR>E.<BR>नट, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटान्तिका|नटांतिका
नटान्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Shame, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>नट dancing, and अन्त destroying, affix कन् and टाप्; it is also read नटान्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटेश्वर|नटेश्वरः
नटेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>नट a dancer, and ईश्वर a deity, the god of the dancers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड<BR>r. 1st cl. (नडति)<BR>To be thick or impervious.<BR>r. 10th cl. (नडयति)<BR>To fall off or from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड|नडं|नडः
नड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A sort of reed, (Arundo tibialis, or karka); also नल.<BR>2 A particular tribe whose employment is making a sort of glass bracelets.<BR>E.<BR>नड to be thick, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडकीय|नडकीयः
नडकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Abounding in reeds, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>नड a reed, छ affix, and कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडप्राय|नडप्रायः
नडप्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Abounding in reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड, and प्राय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडमीन|नडमीनः
नडमीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A small fish, a kind of sprat haunting reedy places.<BR>E.<BR>नड a reed, and मीन a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडसंहति|नडसंहतिः
नडसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A quantity of reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड, and संहति assemblage; also any analogous compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडह|नडहः
नडह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Lovely, beautiful, desirable.<BR>E.<BR>नड here said to be mental anxiety, derived from नड to fall off or from, हन to destroy, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्या
नड्या<BR>f. (-ड्या)<BR>A quantity of reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड a reed, affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वत्|नड्वन्त्
नड्वत्<BR>mfn. (-ड्वान्-ड्वती-ड्वत्)<BR>Reedy, abounding in reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वल|नड्वलः
नड्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Reedy, abounding in reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड, and ड्वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वाभू
नड्वाभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A house or hut of reeds.<BR>E.<BR>नड्व, and भू being, with आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत|नतं|नतः
नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bent, bowed, reclining.<BR>2 Crooked, curved.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The are or distance of any planet from the zenith.<BR>3 A plant or its root: see तगर and तगरमूल.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow or bend, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतनाडिका
नतनाडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Any hour of birth, after noon or before midnight.<BR>E.<BR>नत, and नाडिका a period of twenty-four minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतनासिक|नतनासिकः
नतनासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Flat-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>नत bowed, and नासिक the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतभाग
नतभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>(In Astronomy,) Zenith distance.<BR>E.<BR>नत, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतभ्रू
नतभ्रू<BR>mfn. (-भ्रूः-भ्रूः-भ्रू)<BR>Frowning.<BR>E.<BR>नत, and भ्रू the brow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमुख
नतमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Down-faced, looking down.<BR>E.<BR>नत, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतमूर्द्धन्
नतमूर्द्धन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धा-र्द्धा-र्द्ध)<BR>Looking down, hanging down the head.<BR>E.<BR>नत, मूर्द्धन् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतांश|नतांशः
नतांश<BR>m. (-शं)<BR>Zenith distance, (in Astronomy.)<BR>E.<BR>नत, and अंश a degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नताङ्ग
नताङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Bent, curved, bowed, stooping.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>नत, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नति|नतिः
नति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR>2 Curvature, crookedness.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत्यूह|नत्यूहः
नत्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (नदति नादयति)<BR>1 To speak or emit sound.<BR>2 To shine: see खद.<BR>With वि and अनु,<BR>To fill with noise or sound;<BR>(दु इ,) दुनदि r. 1st cl. (नन्दति)<BR>1 To thrive, to be prosperous.<BR>(Usually with आङ् prefixed,)<BR>To be happy, to be pleased or delighted.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>1 To wish for.<BR>2 To acknowledge or confess.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To be thankful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद|नदः
नद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A river, applied only to one of which the personification is male, as the Brahmaputra, Śoṇa, Indus, &c.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A river in general; the common personification of rivers being female.<BR>E.<BR>नद to sound, affix अट्, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदत्|नदन्त्
नदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Sounding, making a sound.<BR>E.<BR>नद to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनदीपति
नदनदीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sea.<BR>E.<BR>नद, and नदी, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनु|नदनुः
नदनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>E.<BR>नद to sound, अनुङ् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकान्त|नदीकांत|नदीकान्तः
नदीकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A sort of tree, (Barringtonia acutangula): see इज्जल.<BR>3 A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A creeper.<BR>2 The rose apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>3 A shrub, (Leea hirta.)<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, कान्त loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकूल
नदीकूल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>The bank or shore of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, कूल a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीकूलप्रिय|नदीकूलप्रियः
नदीकूलप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of reed, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>नदीकूल a river bank, and प्रिय fond of; growing on the banks of rivers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीज|नदीजं|नदीजः
नदीज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatic, water-born.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Antimony.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A sort of tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>2 The marshy date tree.<BR>3 A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीज्ञ
नदीज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>One who knows the course of rivers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नदी, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीतरस्थान|नदीतरस्थानं
नदीतरस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A Ghāt, a landing place, a ferry.<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, तर crossing, and स्थान place; also नदीतरस्थल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीतीर
नदीतीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The bank of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीन|नदीनः
नदीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 The god of water, VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, and इन lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीमातृक|नदीमातृकः
नदीमातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Watered by rivers, (land, rice, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, मातृ a mother, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीरय|नदीरयः
नदीरय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The stream or current of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी, and रय going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवङ्क|नदीवंक|नदीवङ्कः
नदीवङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The bend or arm of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, and वङ्क a bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवेग
नदीवेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The stream or current of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीवेला
नदीवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The current or stream of a river.<BR>E.<BR>नदी, and वेला flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीष्ण|नदीष्णः
नदीष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>1 Bathing, &c. in a river.<BR>2 One who knows rivers, their depth, course, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नदी river, स्ना to bathe, ड affix; and स्न changed to ष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदीसर्ज्ज|नदीसर्ज|नदीसर्जः|नदीसर्ज्जः
नदीसर्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, and सर्ज्ज the Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=452" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदेयी
नदेयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A plant, (Premna herbacea, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>नदी a river, ढक्, affix; also नादेयी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध|नद्धः
नद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Bound, tied.<BR>2 Drawn up, raised.<BR>E.<BR>नह to tye, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्धी
नद्धी<BR>f. (-द्धी)<BR>A leather cord, a thong.<BR>E.<BR>नह to bind, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननान्दृ|ननांदृ
ननान्दृ<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>A husband's sister.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, नन्द to please, ऋत् Uṇādi affix; also the penultimate being made long, ननान्दृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of interrogation, (how, what.)<BR>2 Of affirmation, (certainly.)<BR>3 Of assent.<BR>4 A consolatory and kind expression.<BR>5 A vocative particle, (ho, hola,) or one implying kindness, conciliation, (pray, good friend, &c.)<BR>6 An inceptive particle, implying doubt or dissent, (may be, but, on the other hand.)<BR>7 A responsive particle.<BR>8 A particle of reproach.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, नुद to send or command, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननुच
ननुच<BR>ind.<BR>An inceptive particle, implying doubt, dissent, or contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>ननु as above, and च particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्तव्य
नन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be saluted, to be revered or honoured.<BR>E.<BR>नम to salute, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द|नंद|नंदः|नन्दः
नन्द<BR>mf. (-न्दः-न्दी)<BR>Happiness, pleasure, felicity.<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 One of KUVERA'S nine inestimable gems or treasure.<BR>2 The cowherd NANDA, the foster father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A prince, the son of MAHĀNANDI.<BR>5 A flute, one eleven inches long.<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>1 An earthen water jar.<BR>2 The first, sixth, or eleventh day of the fortnight.<BR>3 Prosperity, increase.<BR>4 A husband's sister.<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>INDRA'S garden.<BR>f. (-न्दा or -न्दी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to be prosperous or happy, affix अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दक|नंदक|नन्दकः
नन्दक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Rejoicing, making happy or delighted.<BR>2 Cherishing or rearing a family.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>2 The sword of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 The foster father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>4 A frog.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to make happy, affix वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकि|नंदकिः|नन्दकिः
नन्दकि<BR>f. (-किः)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to delight, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दकिन्|नंदकिन्
नन्दकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दगोपिता
नन्दगोपिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant: see रास्ना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दथु|नंदथु|नंदथुः|नन्दथुः
नन्दथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Happiness, felicity.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to be happy, affix अथुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन|नंदन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नन्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Delighting, rejoicing, making pleased or happy.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A frog.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>INDRA'S pleasure ground, elysium.<BR>2 A species of the Dhṛti metre.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to be or make happy, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनन्दन|नंदनंदन|नन्दनन्दनः
नन्दनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द, and नन्दन a son; the son of NANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनन्दिनी
नन्दनन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द the cowherd NANDA, and नन्दिनी a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दन्त|नंदंत|नन्दन्तः
नन्दन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A friend.<BR>3 A prince.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to make happy, झच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दनमाला
नन्दनमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A chaplet or garland made by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दन delighting, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयत्
नन्दयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यती-यत)<BR>Making happy, delighting.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to be happy, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दयन्त|नंदयंत|नन्दयन्तः
नन्दयन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>Making happy, rejoicing, delighting.<BR>E.<BR>नदि in the causal form, with झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपाल|नंदपाल|नन्दपालः
नन्दपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द KUVERA'S treasure, and पाल who guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दपुत्री
नन्दपुत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द the cowherd NANDA, and पुत्री a daughter; the goddess becoming incarnate, as the infant daughter of NANDA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दात्मज|नंदात्मज|नन्दात्मजः
नन्दात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द as above, and आत्मज offspring: see नन्दनन्दन; also नन्दपुत्र, नन्दसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दि|नंदि|नंदिः|नन्दिः
नन्दि<BR>mn. (-न्दिः-न्दि)<BR>1 Gambling, gaming.<BR>2 Happiness.<BR>m. (-न्दिः)<BR>1 One of ŚIVA'S principal attendants.<BR>2 The speaker of the prologue or prelude to a drama.<BR>3 One who pronounces a benediction.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to make happy, and इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिक|नंदिक|नंदिकः|नन्दिकः
नन्दिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Tūn, a tree, the wood of which resembles mahogany, and is used for furniture, &c. (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 INDRA'S garden or pleasure ground.<BR>2 An earthen water pot.<BR>3 The first, sixth, or eleventh day of a fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द, with कन् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिकेश्वर|नंदिकेश्वर|नन्दिकेश्वरः
नन्दिकेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of ŚIVA'S chief attendants.<BR>2 An inferior Purāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दिक INDRA'S garden, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिघोष|नंदिघोष|नन्दिघोषः
नन्दिघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The car of ARJUNA.<BR>2 The acclaim or proclamation of a panegyrist or herald.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दि happy, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिन्|नंदिन्
नन्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>Happy, rejoiced, delighted.<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>1 The name of one of ŚIVA'S chamberlains, and chief attendants.<BR>2 The Indian fig tree.<BR>3 Pārspīpal, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>4 The speaker of the prelude or prologue to a drama.<BR>f. (-न्दिनी)<BR>1 A name of the goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 GAṄGĀ, the river goddess.<BR>3 A husband's sister.<BR>4 A fabulous cow, related to the cow of plenty, and the property of the sage VAŚIṢṬHA.<BR>5 The Alakanandā river.<BR>6 The mother of the writer VYĀḌI.<BR>E.<BR>नन्द happiness, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिनीतनय|नन्दिनीतनयः
नन्दिनीतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of VYĀḌI, author of a vocabulary.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दिनी as above, and तनय a son; also similar compounds, as नन्दिनीसुत, नन्दिनीपुत्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवर्द्धन
नन्दिवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 The last day of either half of the month, the full or new moon.<BR>3 A son.<BR>4 A friend.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दि happiness, &c. and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दिवृक्ष|नन्दिवृक्षः
नन्दिवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Tūn tree.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दि pleasure, and वृक्ष a tree: also ङीष् being added to नन्दि, नन्दीवृक्ष; or with कन् added, नन्दिवृक्षक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीट
नन्दीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A bald-headed man.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दि ŚIVA'S bald-headed attendant, and अट who resembles, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीमुखी
नन्दीमुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>Sleep, drowsiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीश|नंदीश|नन्दीशः
नन्दीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of NANDĪ, ŚIVA'S attendant.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 A species of musical rhythm.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दी INDRA'S garden, or नन्दि a proper name, ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीश्वर|नंदीश्वर|नन्दीश्वरः
नन्दीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA, &c.: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दि ŚIVA'S chamberlain, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्दीसरस्
नन्दीसरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A lake or pond in INDRA'S garden.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दी the garden, सरस् a piece of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्द्यावर्त्त|नन्द्यावर्त|नन्द्यावर्तः|नन्द्यावर्त्तः
नन्द्यावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 A sort of temple.<BR>2 A tree, (Tabernæmontana coronaria): see तगर.<BR>3 A peculiar diagram.<BR>E.<BR>नन्दी happiness, आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नन्नम्यमान
नन्नम्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bending or bowing very low.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, intens. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसक|नपुंसकं|नपुंसकः
नपुंसक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A eunuch.<BR>2 An impotent or imbecile man.<BR>3 The neuter gender.<BR>E.<BR>न not, पुंसक a male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=453" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृ
नप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>A grandson.<BR>f. (-प्त्री)<BR>A granddaughter.<BR>E.<BR>न not, पत to fall, तृच् Uṇādi affix; propping or sustaining the family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 The month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>2 Æther, atmosphere.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 A spitting pot.<BR>2 The city of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>नह to bind, affix भ; see नभस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःक्रान्तिन्|नभःक्रांतिन्
नभःक्रान्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ति)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् a cloud, and क्रान्तिन् who goes; whose shape is seen in the clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःप्राण|नभःप्राणः
नभःप्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् atmosphere, and प्राण life or breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसद्
नभःसद्<BR>m. (-सद्)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and सद् who travels, from सद to go, with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःसरित्
नभःसरित्<BR>f. (-रित्)<BR>The celestial Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and सरित् a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थ
नभःस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Celestial, aerial, heavenly, etherial.<BR>E.<BR>नभस्, and स्थ what stays; also नभस्स्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभःस्थित|नभःस्थितः
नभःस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A biding in heaven or in the sky.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A division of the infernal regions, a hell.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् atmosphere, and स्थित a staying; also नभस्स्थित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चक्षुस्
नभश्चक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चमस|नभश्चमसः
नभश्चमस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A variegated cake.<BR>3 Conjuring.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and चमस a sort of ladle, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभश्चर|नभश्चरः
नभश्चर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going in the air or heaven.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A Vidyādhara or demigod so called.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस्<BR>m. (-भाः)<BR>1 The month Śrāvaṇa, (July-August.)<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 The rains, or rainy season.<BR>4 Smell.<BR>5 The fibres in the root of the lotus.<BR>6 A bird.<BR>7 A grey-headed man.<BR>n. (-भः)<BR>Sky, atmosphere, æther or heaven.<BR>E.<BR>नभ to injure, to be annihilated, (at the end of the world,) Uṇādi affix असुन्, or नह to bind, and भ substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस|नभसं|नभसः
नभस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Heaven, sky, &c. see the last.<BR>E.<BR>नभ as above, Uṇādi affix असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभसङ्गम|नभसंगम|नभसंगमः|नभसङ्गमः
नभसङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>नभस heaven, गम to go, affix खच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्तल|नभस्तलं
नभस्तल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>The month Bhādra, (August-September.)<BR>E.<BR>नभस् a cloud or rain, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्वत्|नभस्वन्त्
नभस्वत्<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>नभस्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाक|नभाकं|नभाकः
नभाक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>नभ to injure, आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभि|नभिः
नभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगज|नभोगजः
नभोगज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोगति|नभोगतिः
नभोगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Flying, soaring, going in the air.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोदुह|नभोदुहः
नभोदुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् rain, (-दुह) to milk, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोद्वीप|नभोद्वीपः
नभोद्वीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् rain, द्वीप an island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोधूम|नभोधूमः
नभोधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and भूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोनदी
नभोनदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The celestial Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् heaven, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोमणि|नभोमणिः
नभोमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोम्बुप|नभोंबुप|नभोम्बुपः
नभोऽम्बुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, अम्बु water, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोरजस्
नभोरजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोरेणु|नभोरेणुः
नभोरेणु<BR>f. (-णुः)<BR>Fog, mist, vapour.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and रेणु thin dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलय|नभोलयः
नभोलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>नभस् sky, and लय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभोलिह्
नभोलिह्<BR>mfn. (-लिट्)<BR>Lofty, towering, rising to the clouds.<BR>E.<BR>नभस्, and लिह् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
नभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>Relating to the nave of a wheel, resembling it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नभ for नाभि, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्राज्
नभ्राज्<BR>m. (-भ्राट्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, भ्राज to shine, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम|नमः
नम<BR>r. 1st cl. (नमति)<BR>To bow, to pay obeisance.<BR>r. 10th cl. (नमयति-नामयति)<BR>To bend, to bow: see णम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत्
नमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>Bending, stooping, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत|नमतः
नमत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A master, a lord.<BR>2 An actor, a mime.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow or bend, Uṇādi affix अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमयत्
नमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Bending, directing downward, declining.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow. r. 10th cl. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Gift, present.<BR>2 Bowing, bending, salutation, obeisance.<BR>3 An inarticulate cry.<BR>4 The term used in connexion with the name of a deity in the fifth case to signify veneration, as रामाय नमः salutation, glory or reverence to RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bend, and affix असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस|नमसः
नमस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Agreement, concord.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, affix कसच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसित|नमसितः
नमसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reverenced, respected, worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् bowing, क्यप् affix, and क्त added, य rejected: see नमस्यित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कार|नमस्कारः
नमस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Respectful or reverential address or salutation.<BR>2 A sort of poison.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sensitive plant.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् bowing, and कार making, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्कृत्वा
नमस्कृत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having saluted reverentially.<BR>E.<BR>नमस्, and कृत्वा having made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable, entitled to salutation or civility.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Reverence, respect, worship, adoration.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् respect, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यत्
नमस्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>Saluting reverentially, bowing to, paying adoration.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् nominal verb, to bow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यित|नमस्यितः
नमस्यित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reverenced, respected, worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् respect, affix क्यप्, and the participial affix क्त; also नमसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमित|नमितः
नमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bowed, making salutation or obeisance.<BR>2 Bowed, bent down.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bend, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचि|नमुचिः
नमुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>1 The deity of love.<BR>2 A demon so named.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, मुच to loose, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिसूदन|नमुचिसूदनः
नमुचिसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नमुचि the demon, and सूदन destroyer; also similar names, as नमुचिद्विष्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमेरु|नमेरुः
नमेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The seed of the Elæocarpus.<BR>E.<BR>न not, मेरु the mountain Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमोगुरु|नमोगुरुः
नमोगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>नमस् reverence, and गुरु a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्ब
नम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (नम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>Crooked, curved, bent, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, affix र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रक|नम्रकः
नम्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Bent or bowed, stooping.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रमुख
नम्रमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Looking down, having the head bent.<BR>E.<BR>नम्र, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रमूर्त्ति|नम्रमूर्ति
नम्रमूर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति)<BR>Bending down, stooping, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>नम्र, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=454" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्राङ्ग
नम्राङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Bent, bowed, stooping.<BR>E.<BR>नम्र, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय<BR>r. 1st cl. (-नयते)<BR>To go, to move: see णय and णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Fit, right, proper.<BR>2 Leading, conducting, (who or what does so.)<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Guiding, directing, (literally or figuratively, as in morals, &c.)<BR>2 Polity, civil and military government.<BR>3 The theological part of the Vedas.<BR>4 A sort of dice or men for playing with.<BR>5 A guide, a conductor.<BR>E.<BR>नय to go, affix घञ्, or णी to guide, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयत्
नयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Leading, guiding.<BR>2 Tending or conducing to.<BR>3 Informing, certifying, giving in evidence.<BR>4 Obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>णी to obtain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयन|नयनं
नयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Leading, guiding, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>3 Attaining, obtaining.<BR>4 Bringing.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The pupil of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनवारि
नयनवारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Tears.<BR>E.<BR>नयन, and वारि water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनामोषिन्
नयनामोषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Sight-stealing, blinding.<BR>E.<BR>नयन, and आमोषिन् what steals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोत्सव|नयनोत्सवः
नयनोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A lamp.<BR>2 Any lovely or desired object.<BR>E.<BR>नयन the eye, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनोपान्त|नयनोपांत|नयनोपान्तः
नयनोपान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The outer angle or canthus of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>नयन, and उपान्त extremity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनौषध|नयनौषधं
नयनौषध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Green sulphate of iron, or the salt in a state of partial decomposition by exposure to the atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>नयन the eye, and औषध a medicament, being used as a collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयपीठी
नयपीठी<BR>f. (-ठी)<BR>The board or cloth on which dice or men are played.<BR>E.<BR>नय dice, पीठी a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयप्रयोग|नयप्रयोगः
नयप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Policy, political address.<BR>E.<BR>नय, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयविशारद|नयविशारदः
नयविशारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A politician, a statesman.<BR>E.<BR>नय, and विशारद skilled in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयसिद्धि
नयसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Political success, accomplishing any thing by good management.<BR>E.<BR>नय, and सिद्धि success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर|नरं|नरः
नर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Man, individually or generally.<BR>2 The Eternal, the divine imperishable spirit pervading the universe.<BR>3 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>4 VIṢṆU.<BR>5 A gnomon.<BR>6 A man or piece at chess, draughts, &c.<BR>7 A Muni, an incarnation of VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass, commonly Rāmkapūr.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Woman in general: see नारी.<BR>E.<BR>नृ to lead or guide, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरक|नरकं|नरकः
नरक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Hell, the infernal regions, including a number of places of torture of various descriptions.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a Daitya or demon.<BR>E.<BR>नृ to guide or lead, affix वुन्, whither the wicked are conducted: sometimes read नारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरककुण्ड|नरककुंड|नरककुण्डं
नरककुण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A well or pit in Tartarus, eighty-six such are enumerated.<BR>E.<BR>नरक, and कुण्ड a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकजित्
नरकजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नरक the demon, and जित् subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकदेवता
नरकदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Misfortune, personified as a goddess.<BR>E.<BR>नरक, and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकस्थ
नरकस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Living or being in Tartarus, who or what is there.<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>The river of hell.<BR>E.<BR>नरक hell, स्थ who stays or abides, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकान्तक|नरकांतक|नरकान्तकः
नरकान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नरक hell, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकामय|नरकामयः
नरकामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The soul after death.<BR>E.<BR>नरक hell, and आमव sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकीलक|नरकीलकः
नरकीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The murderer of his spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>नर mankind, and कील a stake, affix कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरङ्ग|नरंग|नरंगं|नरङ्गः
नरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Pimples on the face.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>नृ to guide or lead, Uṇādi affix अङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरदेव|नरदेवः
नरदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A sovereign, a king.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, and देव a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरनारायण|नरनारायणः
नरनारायण<BR>m. dual. (-णौ)<BR>Two sages, incarnations of VIṢṆU, and born again, as KṚṢṆA and ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and नारायण, each severally the name of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरपति|नरपतिः
नरपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a sovereign prince.<BR>E.<BR>नर man, पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरप्रिय|नरप्रियः
नरप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Favourable or friendly to mankind.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरभू
नरभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>Bharata Varṣa, India, or the central part of the known continent.<BR>2 The birth or birthplace of men.<BR>E.<BR>नर man, and भू land; also नरभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमानिनी
नरमानिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman who has a beard.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, मन to regard or think, and णिनि affix; also with कन् affix in the feminine form, नरमानिका; these words are also written नरमालिनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमाला
नरमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A string or girdle of skulls.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमालिनी
नरमालिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman with a beard.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, माला a necklace, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरमेध|नरमेधः
नरमेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A human sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and मेध a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवाहन|नरवाहनः
नरवाहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Borne or carried by men.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरवाहिन्
नरवाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Carried by men, (a vehicle.)<BR>E.<BR>नर, and वाहिन् what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरविष्वण|नरविष्वणः
नरविष्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An imp or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>नर man, and विष्वण who devours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नररूप
नररूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Having the form of man.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>The human form.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नररूपिन्
नररूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>Having the human form.<BR>E.<BR>नररूप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरसिंह|नरसिंहः
नरसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU in his fourth Avatāra or descent, the lion-headed man.<BR>2 A chief, a man of eminence or power.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरहरि|नरहरिः
नरहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VIṢṆU in his fourth Avatar: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and हरि a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधम|नराधमः
नराधम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A low or vile man, a wretch.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and अधम low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधारा
नराधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>नर man, आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराधिप|नराधिपः
नराधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरान्तक|नरांतक|नरान्तकः
नरान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 A Rākṣasa, a son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरायण|नरायणः
नरायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नर man, and अयण going: see नारायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेन्द्र|नरेंद्र|नरेन्द्रः
नरेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A king, an anointed sovereign.<BR>2 A dealer in antidotes, a juggler.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेश|नरेशः
नरेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरेश्वर|नरेश्वरः
नरेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and ईश्वर a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=455" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्कुटक|नर्कुटकं
नर्कुटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तक|नर्तक|नर्तकः|नर्त्तकः
नर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An actor, a mime.<BR>2 A juggler, a dancer, a player of any description.<BR>3 A bard, a herald.<BR>4 An elephant.<BR>5 A reed, (Arundo karka, Rox.)<BR>5 A peacock.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 An actress, female dancer or singing girl.<BR>2 A female elephant.<BR>3 A peahen.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance or act, ष्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तन|नर्तन|नर्तनः|नर्त्तनं
नर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dancing, gesticulating, acting.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तनप्रिय|नर्तनप्रिय|नर्तनप्रियः
नर्त्तनप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>नर्त्तन dancing, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त्तित|नर्तित
नर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Danced, dancing.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्द|नर्द
नर्द्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (नर्द्दति प्रनर्द्दति)<BR>To sound: the radical न is not convertible to ण after a preposition, &c. see णर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दटक|नर्दटक|नर्दटकः|नर्द्दटकं
नर्द्दटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of metre, containing eight feet of various syllabic quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दत्|नर्दत्
नर्द्दत्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दन्-र्द्दन्ती-र्द्दत्)<BR>1 Sounding.<BR>2 Praising aloud, proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>नर्द्द, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दन|नर्दन|नर्दनं
नर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sounding, roaring, making a noise.<BR>2 Celebrating, praising aloud.<BR>E.<BR>नर्द्द to sound, affix ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दनीय|नर्दनीय
नर्द्दनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be sounded.<BR>2 To be celebrated or praised aloud.<BR>E.<BR>नर्द्द sound, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्दित|नर्दित|नर्दितः
नर्द्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sounded, made as a noise.<BR>2 Celebrated, praised aloud.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sound, roar, bellowing.<BR>E.<BR>नर्द्द to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्धटक
नर्द्धटक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A stanza of four parts, having seventeen syllables in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्ब्ब|नर्ब
नर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st. cl. (नर्ब्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मकील|नर्मकील|नर्मकीलः|नर्म्मकीलः
नर्म्मकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म amusement, कील a prop or stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मगर्भ|नर्मगर्भ|नर्मगर्भः
नर्म्मगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A secret lover.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म, and गर्भ source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मट|नर्मट|नर्मटः|नर्म्मटः
नर्म्मट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A potsherd.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म, and अट what goes, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मठ|नर्मठ|नर्मठः|नर्म्मठः
नर्म्मठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 The nipple.<BR>2 A rake, a lecher, a libertine.<BR>3 Sport, amusement.<BR>4 Coition.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म pleasure, स्था to abide, ड affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मद|नर्मद|नर्मदः|नर्म्मदः
नर्म्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Delighting, making happy, giving pleasure.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The associate or companion of a person's sports or amusements.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 The Narmadā river, which rising in the Vindhyā mountains, runs westward to the gulf of Cambay.<BR>2 A plant: see पृक्का.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म pleasure, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मद्युति|नर्मद्युति|नर्मद्युतिः
नर्म्मद्युति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Happy, merry.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Enjoyment of a joke or any amusement.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म, and द्युति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मन्|नर्मन्
नर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Sport, amusement, pastime, diversion.<BR>2 Jest, joke.<BR>3 Wit, humour.<BR>E.<BR>नृ to guide, affix मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मसचिव|नर्मसचिव|नर्मसचिवः
नर्म्मसचिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A companion, an associate, the promoter and partaker of a person's amusements, especially of a prince or man of rank.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्मन्, and सचिव a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मसाचिव्य|नर्मसाचिव्य
नर्म्मसाचिव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Superintendence or provision of a prince's amusements, partaking a person's amusements.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्मसाचिव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मस्फूर्ज्ज|नर्मस्फूर्ज|नर्मस्फूर्जः
नर्म्मस्फूर्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>Happiness or amusement ending in alarm.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म, and स्फूर्ज्ज thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्म्मस्फोट|नर्मस्फोट|नर्मस्फोटः
नर्म्मस्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Slight or inferior amusement.<BR>E.<BR>नर्म्म, and स्फोट opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल<BR>r. 10th cl. (नालयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To bind or confine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल|नलं|नलः
नल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A reed, (Arundo karka, Rox.)<BR>2 The name of a king, son of NIṢADHA, and hero of several poetical works famous amongst the Hindus, especially the poem called Naiṣadha.<BR>3 Another prince, the son of VĪRASENA.<BR>4 A deified progenitor or Pitṛdeva.<BR>5 The name of a monkey chief.<BR>6 A demon.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Red arsenick.<BR>2 A perfume, commonly called by the same name of Nali.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The water lily, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>2 Smell, odour.<BR>E.<BR>नल to shine, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलक|नलकं
नलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bone of either of the extremities, any long bone.<BR>E.<BR>नल a reed, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकिनी
नलकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The knee cap or pan.<BR>E.<BR>नलक as above, and इनि affix; connecting the bones of the lower extremity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकील|नलकीलः
नलकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The knee.<BR>E.<BR>नल a reed, or reed-like bone, and कील a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकूवेर
नलकूवेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>नल a reed, कूवेर a carriage yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलद|नलदं
नलद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 The honey or nectar of a flower.<BR>2 The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>नल here said to mean, fragrance, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलपट्टिका
नलपट्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of mat made with reeds, a coarse mat.<BR>E.<BR>नल a reed, and पट्ट a cloth, कन् affix of similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलमीन|नलमीनः
नलमीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A kind of sprat, or according to some, a shrimp or prawn.<BR>E.<BR>नल a reed, and मीन a fish; frequenting reedy spots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिका
नलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A perfume: see नली.<BR>E.<BR>नली, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिन|नलिनं|नलिनः
नलिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A lotus or water lily, (Nelumbium speciosum, or Nymphaea nelumbo.)<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Indigo.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The Indian crane.<BR>2 A small fruit, Karonda.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>2 A place abounding in lotuses.<BR>3 The flexible stalk of a water lily.<BR>4 A pond in which the lotus grows or may grow.<BR>5 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>6 The fermented and intoxicating juice of the cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>नल to be bright, Uṇādi affix इनच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनीरुह|नलिनीरुहं|नलिनीरुहः
नलिनीरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The fibres of the lotus stalk.<BR>E.<BR>नलिनी, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनेशय|नलिनेशयः
नलिनेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नलिने in a lotus, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्व|नल्वः
नल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A furlong, a distance measured by four hundred cubits.<BR>E.<BR>नल to be as a reed in length, and व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्ववर्त्मगा
नल्ववर्त्मगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The orange tree.<BR>E.<BR>नल्व as above, वर्त्म a road, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>New.<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>Praise, panegyrick, celebration.<BR>E.<BR>नु to praise, &c. affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकारिका
नवकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bride, a woman newly married.<BR>2 A new comment.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and कारिका agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवकास्तिका
नवकास्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A young woman, either one recently married or one in whom menstruation has lately commenced.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, काल time, कन् added with the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवग्रह
नवग्रह<BR>m. plu. (-हाः)<BR>The nine planets, or sun, moon, five planets, and the ascending and descending nodes.<BR>E.<BR>नव for नवन्, and ग्रह a planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवछात्र|नवच्छात्र|नवच्छात्रः
नवछात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A student, a novice.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and छात्र a disciple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=456" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत|नवतः
नवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant's painted or variegated housings.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, तन् to spread, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवता
नवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Novelty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to नव; also with त्व, नवत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवति|नवतिः
नवति<BR>f. (-तिः or -ती)<BR>Ninety.<BR>E.<BR>नव nine, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिका
नवतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A painting brush.<BR>E.<BR>नवति ninety, (hairs,) कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिधा
नवतिधा<BR>ind.<BR>Ninety-fold.<BR>E.<BR>नवति, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिशस्
नवतिशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Ninety by ninety.<BR>E.<BR>नवति, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदल|नवदलं
नवदल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The new leaf of a lotus.<BR>2 Any young leaf.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदीधिति|नवदीधितिः
नवदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Mars, the planet or its deified regent.<BR>E.<BR>नव nine, दीधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदुर्गा
नवदुर्गा<BR>f. (-र्गा)<BR>The nine forms of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and दुर्गा the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवदोला
नवदोला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A litter borne by nine men.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and दोल a litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवद्वार
नवद्वार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having nine doors; an epithet applied to the body, which has nine inlets or outlets, as the nostrils, ears, mouth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवधा
नवधा<BR>ind.<BR>Nine-fold, in nine ways.<BR>E.<BR>नव nine, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन्
नवन्<BR>mfn. always plu. (-व)<BR>Nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनी
नवनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीत|नवनीतं
नवनीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and नीत procured (from milk, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतक|नवनीतकं
नवनीतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनीतधेनु|नवनीतधेनुः
नवनीतधेनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A quantity of butter as a present to Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>नवनीत, and धेनु a milch cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवपल्लव
नवपल्लव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A new shoot or sprout.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवफलिका
नवफलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bride, a newly married woman.<BR>2 A girl in whom menstruation has recently begun.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, फल fruit, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवबधू
नवबधू<BR>n. (-धूः)<BR>A bride, a newly married woman.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and बधु a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम|नवमः
नवम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Ninth.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The ninth day of a lunar half month.<BR>E.<BR>नव nine, and मट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमल्लिका
नवमल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Double jasmine: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवमालिका
नवमालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Double jasmine, (J. Zambac.)<BR>E.<BR>नव excellent, praised, and मालिका or मलिका jasmine: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवयौवना
नवयौवना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A young woman.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and यौवन young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरक्तक
नवरक्तक<BR>f. (-कं)<BR>A newly dyed garment.<BR>E.<BR>नव, रक्त red, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरङ्ग|नवरङ्गं
नवरङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Gift to five and acceptance by four persons of the best Kāyastha families.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and रङ्ग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरत्न|नवरत्नं
नवरत्न<BR>n. (त्नं)<BR>1 Nine precious gems, or a pearl, ruby, topaz, diamond, emerald, lapis lazuli, coral, sapphire, and one called Gomeda.<BR>2 The nine men of letters at the court of VIKRAMĀDITYA, or DHANVANTARI, KṢAPAṆAKA, AMARASIṂHA, SAṄKU, VETĀLABHAṬṬA, GHAṬAKARPARA, KĀLIDĀSA, VARĀHAMIHIRA, and VARARUCI.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and रत्न a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवरात्र|नवरात्रं
नवरात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The period of nine days, from the first of the light half of Aśvin to the ninth; part of the time devoted to the worship of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and रात्र for रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववरिका
नववरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A newly married woman.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, वर a blessing, affix कन् added, fem. affix टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नववस्त्र|नववस्त्रं
नववस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>New cloth.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and वस्त्र cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्
नवशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Nine by nine.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्य
नवशस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Grain of the year's harvest.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and शस्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशस्येष्टि
नवशस्येष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A sacrifice performed on eating the new rice or grain of the year.<BR>E.<BR>नवशस्य, and इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशायक|नवशायकः
नवशायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name given to any of nine inferior classes, the cowherd, gardener, oilman, weaver, confectioner, water-carrier, potter, blacksmith, and barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवश्राद्ध
नवश्राद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>The first series of Śrāddhas collectively, or funeral offerings on the first, third, fifth, seventh, ninth, and eleventh days after a person's demise.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and श्राद्ध obsequial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवसूतिका
नवसूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A milch cow.<BR>2 A woman recently delivered.<BR>E.<BR>नक new, and सूत offspring, and कन् affix, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवांश|नवांशः
नवांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A ninth, a ninth part.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and अंश share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवान्न|नवान्नं
नवान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 New rice or grain.<BR>2 A ceremony observed on first eating the rice, &c. of the last harvest.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाम्बर|नवाम्बरं
नवाम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>New and unbleached cloth.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and अम्बर cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवार्च्चिस्|नवार्चिस्
नवार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>The planet Mars or its deified personification.<BR>E.<BR>नव nine, and अर्च्चिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवाह|नवाहः
नवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A new day.<BR>2 The first day of the fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and अह a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकरण
नवीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Renewing, doing or making anew.<BR>E.<BR>नव, करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकृत
नवीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Renewed, revived, done or made anew.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>New.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, ख pleonasm, and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीभूत
नवीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Renewed, revived.<BR>E.<BR>नव, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवै
नवै<BR>ind.<BR>Not so perhaps, a particle implying doubt.<BR>E.<BR>न not, वै expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोढा
नवोढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>A newly married woman, a bride.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and ऊढा a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवोद्धृत|नवोद्धृतं
नवोद्धृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Fresh butter.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, उद्धृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
नव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>New, recent, young, &c.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>Praise, panegyrick.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशाक|नशाकः
नशाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird, said to be a sort of crow.<BR>E.<BR>णश to destroy, affix आक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नशितृ
नशितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>णश to destroy, affix तृच् with इट् augment, else with a nasal augment नष्टृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्
नश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>Perishing, decaying, wasting, being destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>नश to perish, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्प्रसूतिका
नश्यत्प्रसूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female bearing a dead child.<BR>E.<BR>नश्यत्, प्रसूतिका a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Mischievous, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>णशि to destroy, affix क्वरप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Lost, destroyed, removed, annihilated.<BR>E.<BR>णश to perish, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=457" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचन्द्र|नष्टचन्द्रः
नष्टचन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The moon on the fourth lunation of either half of Bhādra.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and चन्द्र the moon: it is very unlucky to see the moon on these days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेतन
नष्टचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fainted, insensible.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and चेतन conscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्ट
नष्टचेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Insensible, inert.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टचेष्टता
नष्टचेष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fainting, swooning, insensibility, proceeding either from joy or sorrow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट lost, चेष्टता effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टसंस्मृति
नष्टसंस्मृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Unmindful, forgetful.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and संस्मृति recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाग्नि|नष्टाग्निः
नष्टाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>A Brahman or householder who has lost his consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट lost, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टाप्तिसूत्र|नष्टाप्तिसूत्रं
नष्टाप्तिसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Booty, plunder.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट lost, आप्ति gain, and सूत्र thread or chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टार्थ
नष्टार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Reduced, become poor.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and अर्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टेन्दुकला|नष्टेंदुकला
नष्टेन्दुकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The day of new moon when it rises invisible.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and इन्दुकला a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस्<BR>f. (-नाः)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>नस to sound, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसा
नसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The nose: see नासा and नासिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्त|नस्तः
नस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The nose.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>A sternutatory, snuff, &c.<BR>f. (-स्ता)<BR>A hole bored in the septum of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>णस to make crooked, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तित|नस्तितः
नस्तित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ox or any other draft animal, with a string through his nose, the sort of rein usually employed in India.<BR>E.<BR>नस्त as above, the nose, formed into a nominal verb, and क्त added, nozzled or nose-led.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तोत|नस्तोतः
नस्तोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ox led by a string through his nose: see the last; also नस्योत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Nasal, relating or belonging to the nose.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>A sternutatory, snuff.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>नसा the nose, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्योत|नस्योतः
नस्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ox or other animal led by a string through the septum of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नसा the nose, यत् affix of relation or fitness, and ऊत woven: see नस्तित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह
नह<BR>(औ) औनह r. 4th cl. (नह्यति-ते)<BR>To bind: see णह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि<BR>ind.<BR>No, not.<BR>E.<BR>णह to bind or tie, affix इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष|नहुषः
नहुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The name of a Nāga or serpent.<BR>2 The name of a king, one of the lunar race, son of ĀYUS and grandson of PURŪRAVAS.<BR>E.<BR>णह to bind, Uṇādi affix उषन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुषात्मज|नहुषात्मजः
नहुषात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A king, also YAYĀTI.<BR>E.<BR>नहुष as above, आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ना
ना<BR>ind.<BR>No, not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Heaven, paradise, æther, sky, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>न not, with अक derived from क happiness, and the privative अ prefixed, misery; in which there is no unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनाथ|नाकनाथः
नाकनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नाक paradise, and नाथ lord; also with कन् added नाकनाथक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकनायक|नाकनायकः
नाकनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नाक, and नायक a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकवनिता
नाकवनिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A nymph of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>नाक, and वनिता a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकषेधक
नाकषेधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकसद्
नाकसद्<BR>m. (-सत्)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>नाक, and सद् who dwells in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A deity, a god.<BR>E.<BR>नाक heaven, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकु|नाकुः
नाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 An ant or mole hill, a burrow.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A name of a Muni or saint.<BR>E.<BR>न privative, अक to go, affix उ, or नम to be crooked or bowed, Uṇādi affix उ, and नाक substituted for the radical letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुल|नाकुलः
नाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Relating or belonging to an ichneumon.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A plant: the ichneumon plant, a vegetable supposed to furnish the mungoose with an antidote, when bitten in a conflict with a snake, (Serpent ophioxylon?)<BR>2 The root of the Simul tree, (कुक्कुटीकन्द.)<BR>3 A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>E.<BR>नकुल the ichneumon, affixes अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुलान्ध्य
नाकुलान्ध्य<BR>n. (-न्ध्यं)<BR>Weakness of sight.<BR>E.<BR>नाकुल, and अन्ध्य blindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुसद्मन्
नाकुसद्मन्<BR>m. (-द्मा)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>नाकु a mound of earth, सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्र|नाक्षत्रं|नाक्षत्रः
नाक्षत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the lunar asterisms.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A month, one computed by the moon's passage through the twenty-seven mansions, or of thirty days of sixty Gharis each.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्रिक|नाक्षत्रिकः
नाक्षत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the lunar asterisms.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A month of twenty-seven days, each day being the period of the moon's passage through a lunar asterism.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The state or condition to which a person is subjected agreeably to the asterism presiding over his nativity.<BR>E.<BR>नक्षत्र as above, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A Nāga or demigod so called, having a human face, with the tail of a serpent, and the expanded neck of the Koluber Nāga; the race of these beings is said to have sprung from KADRU, the wife of KAŚYAPA, in order to people Pātāla or the regions below the earth.<BR>2 A serpent in general, or especially the spectacle snake, or cobra capella, (Coluber Naga.)<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 A cruel or tyrannical person.<BR>5 A cloud.<BR>6 (In composition,) Pre-eminent.<BR>7 A pin or nail projecting from a wall to hang any thing upon.<BR>8 A small tree, (Mesua ferrea^1.)<BR>9 A sort of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>10 A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>11 One of the airs of the body, that which is expelled by belching.<BR>12 Betle or Pān.<BR>13 The name of a country.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>1 Tin.<BR>2 Lead.<BR>3 One of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas; it is one of those termed invariable, and always corresponds to the last half of Amāvāsyā or new moon.<BR>4 The effects of that period on any thing done or happening during it.<BR>E.<BR>नग a mountain, and अण् affix; living or produced in mountainous regions, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागकेशर|नागकेशरः
नागकेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small tree, commonly Nagesara, (Mesua ferrea).<BR>E.<BR>नाग, and केशर synonyms of the same plant compounded; the word is also written नागकेसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागगर्भ|नागगर्भं
नागगर्भ<BR>n. (-र्भं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>नाग lead, and गर्भ origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागज|नागजं
नागज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by or of a Nāga, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Red lead.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>E.<BR>नाग lead, &c. and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्वा
नागजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa): see शारिवा.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and जिह्वा a tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजिह्विका
नागजिह्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red arsenick.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, जिह्वा a tongue, कन् affix of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागजीवन|नागजीवनं|नागजीवनः
नागजीवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>नाग lead, जीवन proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=458" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्त|नागदंत|नागदन्तः
नागदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Elephant's tooth or ivory; also the tooth of the elephant.<BR>2 A shelf, a pin or bracket projecting from a wall, and used to hang things upon.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A sort of sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>2 A whore.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तक|नागदंतक|नागदन्तकः
नागदन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wooden pin or bracket, projecting from a wall, a shelf.<BR>E.<BR>नागदन्त an elephant's tooth, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदन्तिका
नागदन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly called Rāmadūtī: see विशल्या.<BR>E.<BR>नागदन्ती a plant, and कन् affix of resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागदलोपम|नागदलोपमं
नागदलोपम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of tree, commonly Parusha.<BR>E.<BR>नाग one of the plants so called, दल a leaf, and उपमा resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागद्रु|नागद्रुः
नागद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>Euphorbia.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and द्रु a tree; being used in offerings to the snake goddess MANASĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागनिर्य्यूह|नागनिर्यूह|नागनिर्यूहः|नागनिर्य्यूहः
नागनिर्य्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A large pin or bracket, projecting from a wall like a shelf.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and निर्य्यूह projection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपाश|नागपाशः
नागपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A weapon of VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>2 A sort of noose or knot, used in battle to entangle an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and पाश a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागपुष्प|नागपुष्पः
नागपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A tree used in dyeing, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>2 Nagesara, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>3 The Champaka, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबन्धु|नागबंधु|नागबन्धुः
नागबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and बन्धु friendly, liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागबल|नागबलः
नागबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of BHĪMA.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A creeping plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागभिद्
नागभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद्)<BR>A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and भिद् destroying; the word is sometimes written नागभृत्, from भृत् cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमल्ल|नागमल्लः
नागमल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नाग elephant, and मल्ल a boxer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमातृ
नागमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A name of MANASĀ, a goddess supposed to preside over snakes.<BR>2 Red arsenick.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and मातृ a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागमार|नागमारः
नागमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of potherb; also केशराज.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and मार destroying; considered as an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागयष्टि|नागयष्टिः
नागयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A piece of wood erected in a place dug for water.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and यष्टि a staff; looking like a snake; also नागयष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Clever, sharp, knowing, (as a buck, a blood, a wag, &c.)<BR>2 Town-born or bred, city, citizen.<BR>3 Nameless.<BR>4 Bad, vile.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Dry ginger.<BR>2 A sort of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>3 A form of writing, the Devanāgarī alphabet.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A husband's brother.<BR>9 An orange.<BR>2 A lecturer.<BR>4 Denial of knowledge.<BR>5 Fatigue.<BR>6 Desire of final beatitude.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A sort of Euphorbin.<BR>2 A clever or intriguing woman.<BR>E.<BR>नगर a city, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The orange: see नागरङ्ग.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>3 An artist.<BR>E.<BR>नगर, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक्त|नागरक्तं
नागरक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>नाग mountain, and रक्त red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरङ्ग|नागरंग|नागरङ्गः
नागरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The orange; in India usually applied to the Silhet orange, (Citrus aurantium).<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, रञ्ज to be sick, affix घञ्; on which elephants feed till they become ill; or नाग red lead, and रङ्ग colour, of the colour of red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरमुस्ता
नागरमुस्ता<BR>f. (-स्ता)<BR>A grass, (Cyperus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागराज|नागराजः
नागराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>ANANTA, the chief of the Nāgas.<BR>E.<BR>नाग, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरीट|नागरीटः
नागरीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A libertine, a debauchee, a rake, a blackguard.<BR>E.<BR>नागरी an intriguing woman, अट to accompany, affix अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरुक|नागरुकः
नागरुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The orange: see नागरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेणु|नागरेणुः
नागरेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>नाग, and रेणु oxid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेयक|नागरेयकः
नागरेयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>City, citizen.<BR>E.<BR>नगर a town, and ढकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागलता
नागलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागलोक|नागलोकः
नागलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Nāga regions below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a Nāga, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्लिका
नागवल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The betel plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवल्ली
नागवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The betel plant, (Piper betel.)<BR>E.<BR>नाग the infernal Nāga, and वल्ली a creeper; the creeper of the lower regions; also with कन् added नागवल्लिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवारिक|नागवारिकः
नागवारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Garuḍa, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>3 A royal elephant.<BR>4 An elephant driver or keeper.<BR>5 The chief person in a court or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, वृ to cherish, &c. affix ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीट|नागवीटः
नागवीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A rake: see नागरीट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीथी
नागवीथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>The path of Airāvata, the milky way.<BR>E.<BR>नाग the elephant, वीथी a road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागसम्भव|नागसंभव|नागसम्भवं
नागसम्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Minium or red lead.<BR>E.<BR>नाग lead, and सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागसुगन्धा
नागसुगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>The ichneumon plant: see नाकुली.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and सुगन्ध perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाख्य|नागाख्यः
नागाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A plant: see नागकेसर.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and आख्या a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाङ्ग
नागाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Hastināpura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाञ्चला
नागाञ्चला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A stick or pole driven into a square piece of earth in the centre of a newly dug pond, a boring rod.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and अञ्चला end of a garment; it is also written नागाञ्जना f. (-ना); see नागयष्टि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाधिप|नागाधिपः
नागाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The great serpent ANANTA.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a serpent, and अधिप a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागान्तक|नागांतक|नागान्तकः
नागान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and अन्तक a destroyer; this and similar compounds are also applied to the Ardea Argala, the peacock, and other birds who are natural enemies of the serpent genus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागारूढ
नागारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mounted or riding upon an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>नाग, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाशन|नागाशनः
नागाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Garuḍa: see नागान्तक.<BR>E.<BR>नाग a snake, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागाह्व|नागाह्वं|नागाह्वः
नागाह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>Hastināpura or ancient Delhi.<BR>E.<BR>नाग an elephant, and आह्वा a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोद|नागोदं
नागोद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Armour for the front or the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागोदर|नागोदरं
नागोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A breast-plate, a cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेतु|नाचिकेतुः
नाचिकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट|नाटः
नाट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 Dancing, acting.<BR>2 The Carnatic.<BR>E.<BR>नट to dance, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=459" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटक|नाटकं|नाटकः
नाटक<BR>m. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>An actor, acting, dancing, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A play, a drama: the first of the ten species of dramatic compositions of the first order.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The court of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>नट to act or perform, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकप्रपञ्च|नाटकप्रपञ्चः
नाटकप्रपञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>Course or arrangement of a drama.<BR>E.<BR>नाटक and प्रपञ्च extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीय
नाटकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dramatic.<BR>E.<BR>नाटक, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटाम्र|नाटाम्रः
नाटाम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>The water melon, (Cucurbita citrullus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटार|नाटारः
नाटार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of an actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटिका
नाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A short or light comedy, the first of the Uparūpakas or dramas of the second order.<BR>E.<BR>नट to dance, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेय|नाटेयः
नाटेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of an actress.<BR>E.<BR>नटी, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेर|नाटेरः
नाटेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of an actress or dancing girl.<BR>E.<BR>नटी, an actress, द्रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्य|नाट्यं|नाट्यः
नाट्य<BR>n. (-ट्यं)<BR>The science or art of dancing or acting, or the union of song, dance, and instrumental musick.<BR>E.<BR>नट to dance, affix ण्यत् or ज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यधर्म्मिक
नाट्यधर्म्मिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Rules of dramatic representation.<BR>E.<BR>नाट्य acting, धर्म्म rule, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यप्रिय|नाट्यप्रियः
नाट्यप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>नाट्य dancing, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यशाला
नाट्यशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A theatre, a building for dramatic exhibitions; according to some it should be built near the gate of a palace.<BR>E.<BR>नाट्य, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्योक्ति|नाट्योक्तिः
नाट्योक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Dramatic phraseology.<BR>E.<BR>नाट्य, and उक्ति expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडि|नाडिः
नाडि<BR>f. (-डिः-डी)<BR>1 The stalk or culm of any plant.<BR>2 Any tubular organ of the body, as an artery, a vein, an intestine, &c.<BR>3 The hollow stalk of a lotus, &c.<BR>4 A fistulous sore, a fistula, a sinus.<BR>5 A sort of bent grass.<BR>6 A juggling trick.<BR>7 Deception.<BR>8 An hour of twenty-four minutes.<BR>9 Any pipe or tube.<BR>10 The pulse, either at the hand or feet, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नड to fall off or from, affix अच्, and इ or ङीष्, optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिका
नाडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An Indian hour, or twenty-four minutes.<BR>E.<BR>नाडि the same, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिकेल|नाडिकेलः
नाडिकेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut: see नारिकेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिचीर|नाडिचीरं
नाडिचीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A small reed or tube round which the woof is wound; it is then used as a shuttle.<BR>E.<BR>नाडि a tube, and चीर old cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिन्धम|नाडिंधम|नाडिंधमः|नाडिन्धमः
नाडिन्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Terrifying.<BR>2 Moving the intestines.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>नाडि a tube, a hollow bambu, &c. and धम who blows, from ध्मा, with खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिन्धय|नाडिंधय|नाडिन्धयः
नाडिन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Who or what drinks or sucks through a tube.<BR>E.<BR>नाडि a pipe, धे to drink, affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिपत्र|नाडिपत्रं
नाडिपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रं)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>E.<BR>नाडि a tube, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिमण्डल|नाडिमंडल
नाडिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The celestial equator.<BR>E.<BR>नाडि, and मण्डल a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीकेल|नाडीकेलः
नाडीकेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut: see नाडिकेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीच|नाडीचः
नाडीच<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a tube, चर to go or grow, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीचरण|नाडीचरणः
नाडीचरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a tube, चरण a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीजङ्घ|नाडीजंघ|नाडीजङ्घः
नाडीजङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 The name of a holy teacher or saint.<BR>3 The name of a fabulous crane.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a stalk, and जङ्घा a leg or thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीतरङ्ग|नाडीतरंग|नाडीतरङ्गः
नाडीतरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A sort of poison: see काकोल.<BR>2 An astrologer.<BR>3 A ravisher, a debaucher.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी an Indian hour, and तरङ्ग a wave; also नाडीतरङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीदेह|नाडीदेहः
नाडीदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>BHṚṄGI, one of ŚIVA'S followers.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a tube, and देह the body; as thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीनक्षत्र|नाडीनक्षत्रं
नाडीनक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The planet of a person's nativity.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी, and नक्षत्र an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीविग्रह|नाडीविग्रहः
नाडीविग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of BHṚṄGI, one of ŚIVA'S chief attendants.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a pipe, and विग्रह the body; also नाडीदेह, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीव्रण|नाडीव्रणः
नाडीव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An ulcer.<BR>E.<BR>नाडी a sinus, and व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीस्नेह|नाडीस्नेहः
नाडीस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of BHṚṄGI: see नाडीदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणक|नाणकं
नाणक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A coin, or any thing struck or stamped with an impression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षा
नाणकपरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Assaying.<BR>E.<BR>नाणक, and परीक्षा trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकपरीक्षिन्
नाणकपरीक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>An assayer.<BR>E.<BR>नाणक, and परीक्षिन् who tries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्र|नात्रं|नात्रः
नात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>2 Surprise, wonder.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>2 A sage.<BR>E.<BR>नम to bow, ष्ट्रण् affix, म is dropped, and the short radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ<BR>(ऋ) नाथृ r. 1st cl. (नाथति-ते)<BR>1 To ask or beg.<BR>2 To bless.<BR>3 To destroy.<BR>4 To have wealth or power.<BR>5 To be deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ|नाथः
नाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A master, a lord.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA, especially in the form of a Liṅga; it is usually compounded with some word relating to the legendary history of the Liṅga, as Somanātha, the Liṅga a set up by SOMA, &c.<BR>3 A name adopted by a class of Yogis, as GORAKHNĀTH, &c.<BR>4 A rope passed through the nose of a draft ox.<BR>E.<BR>नाथ to ask, (from whom,) and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवत्|नाथवन्त्
नाथवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Dependant, subservient, subject.<BR>E.<BR>नाथ master, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथहरि|नाथहरिः
नाथहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>An animal bridled by the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नाथ the string, हृ to take, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथहार
नाथहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Taking or carrying a master, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नाथ, हृ to take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद|नादः
नाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Sound in general.<BR>2 A semicircle, used especially as an abbreviation or hieroglyphic^1 in mystical works.<BR>E.<BR>नद to sound, affix घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Who or what sounds.<BR>E.<BR>नद to sound, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Ocean or river-born, marine, aquatick.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Sea salt.<BR>2 Antimony.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 A sort of reed growing usually near water, (Calamus fasciculatus, Rox.)<BR>2 A plant, (Premna herbacea, Rox.)<BR>3 The orange.<BR>4 A tree: see जयन्ती.<BR>5 The China rose.<BR>E.<BR>नद a river or the sea, and ढक् affix, fem. affix ङीप्; also with कन् added, in the fem. form नादेयिका f. (-का)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध
नाध<BR>(ऋ) नाधृ r. 1st cl. (नाधते)<BR>1 To ask or beg.<BR>2 To bless.<BR>3 To destroy.<BR>4 To have wealth or power.<BR>5 To be deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना<BR>ind.<BR>1 Without, except.<BR>2 Many, various.<BR>3 Double or twofold.<BR>E.<BR>नञ् negative, and नाञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=460" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाध्वनि|नानाध्वनिः
नानाध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A musical instrument of more than one tone.<BR>E.<BR>नाना various, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारस
नानारस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Of different flavours.<BR>E.<BR>नाना, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाराग
नानाराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Variegated, of many colours.<BR>E.<BR>नाना, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानारूप|नानारूपः
नानारूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Multiform, various.<BR>E.<BR>नाना various, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानावर्ण|नानावर्णः
नानावर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Variegated, many-coloured.<BR>E.<BR>नाना, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानाविध|नानाविधः
नानाविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>1 In various ways.<BR>2 Of various sorts or kinds.<BR>E.<BR>नाना, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानुष्ठेय|नानुष्ठेयं
नानुष्ठेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Improper, unusual, not right or customary.<BR>E.<BR>न not, अनु according to, ष्ठेय from स्था to be, to be fixed or determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दिकर|नांदिकर|नांदिकरः|नान्दिकरः
नान्दिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The speaker of the prologue to a drama: see नान्दीकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दी|नांदी
नान्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>1 Eulogium of a king, or praise of a deity, recited in benedictory verses at the commencement of a religious ceremony, or the opening of a drama; it most usually signifies the kind of blessing pronounced as a prologue to a Nāṭaka or play.<BR>2 Prosperity, thriving, increase.<BR>E.<BR>नदि to be happy, in the causal form, affix इन्, and ङीष्; delighting the gods, &c. or procuring happiness for mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीक|नांदीकः|नान्दीकः
नान्दीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A post in a door-way, set up for good luck.<BR>E.<BR>नान्दी prosperity, कृ to make, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीकर|नांदीकर|नान्दीकरः
नान्दीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The speaker of the prologue or prelude of a drama.<BR>E.<BR>नान्दी as above, कर who makes; also with the vowel made short, नान्दिकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीपट|नांदीपट|नान्दीपटः
नान्दीपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The lid or cover of a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीमुख|नांदीमुख|नान्दीमुखः
नान्दीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 The lid or cover of a well.<BR>2 The class of male progenitors to whom the Nāndī-mukha Śrāddha is addressed.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A female ancestor sharing in the same.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 A species of the Śarkarī metre.<BR>2 A Śrāddha or funeral obsequies performed on joyous occasions, as initiation, marriage, &c. in which nine balls of meat are offered to the deceased father, paternal grandfather, and great grandfather; to the maternal grandfather, great grandfather, and great great grandfather; and to the mother, paternal grandmother, and paternal great grandmother.<BR>E.<BR>नान्दी good fortune, मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नान्दीवादिन्|नांदीवादिन्
नान्दीवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 The speaker of the prologue or introduction to a drama.<BR>2 A drummer, one who beats a drum at festivals, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नान्दी as above, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापि
नापि<BR>ind.<BR>Not even.<BR>E.<BR>न not, and अपि even.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित|नापितः
नापित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, आप to obtain, (respect,) तन् Uṇādi affix, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितशाला
नापितशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A barber's shop.<BR>E.<BR>नापित, and शाला house; also with कन added in the fem. form, नापितशालिका f. (-का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्य|नापित्यं|नापित्यः
नापित्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>The business of a barber.<BR>E.<BR>नापित, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभक|नाभकः
नाभक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि<BR>f. (-भिः-भी)<BR>1 The nave of a wheel.<BR>2 Musk.<BR>mf. (-भिः and भिः or भी)<BR>The navel.<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>1 An emperor, a sovereign, a lord paramount.<BR>2 A king, a chief.<BR>3 A Kṣatriya or Hindū of the regal and military tribe.<BR>4 The son of PRIYAVRATA.<BR>5 A race, a family.<BR>E.<BR>नह to bind, Uṇādi affix इञि, and भ substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिकण्टक|नाभिकण्टकः
नाभिकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Ruptured or protruded navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि a navel, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगुडक|नाभिगुडकः
नाभिगुडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A prominent or ruptured navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and गुडक a ball or lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिगोलक|नाभिगोलकः
नाभिगोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A prominent or ruptured navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and गोलक a lump or ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिछेदन|नाभिच्छेदन
नाभिछेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Division of the umbilical cord.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and छेदन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिज|नाभिजः
नाभिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि navel, and ज born; BRAHMĀ appearing from the lotus which sprung from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिजन्मन्
नाभिजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि the navel, and जन्मन birth: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाडी
नाभिनाडी<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>The umbilical cord.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and नाडी a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिनाला
नाभिनाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The umbilical cord.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि the navel, and नाला a string, a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिभू
नाभिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and भू born: see नाभिज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिवर्द्धन
नाभिवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Division of the umbilical cord.<BR>2 Umbilical hernia.<BR>3 Corpulency.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभील|नाभीलं
नाभील<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The groin of a woman.<BR>2 A prominent or ruptured navel.<BR>3 Pain.<BR>4 The hollow of the navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि the navel, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>Umbilical, of or relating to the navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि the navel, and यत aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्यावर्त्त|नाभ्यावर्त|नाभ्यावर्तः
नाभ्यावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>The hollow or pit of the navel.<BR>E.<BR>नाभि a navel, आवर्त्त a round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम<BR>ind.<BR>A particle implying,<BR>1 Certainty.<BR>2 Possibility.<BR>3 Anger.<BR>4 Reproach.<BR>5 Consent, promise.<BR>6 Recollection.<BR>7 Surprise.<BR>8 Pretence, &c. as हिमालयो नाम नगाधिपः Himālaya, evidently the king of mountains, इह नाम सीता भविष्यति SĪTĀ will perhaps be here, &c.<BR>E.<BR>णम to call or address, affix ड, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामकरण|नामकरणं
नामकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Naming a child first after birth.<BR>E.<BR>नाम, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामग्रह|नामग्रहः
नामग्रह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Addressing by name.<BR>E.<BR>नाम, and ग्रह taking; also नामग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामद्वादशी
नामद्वादशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A religious ceremony, worshipping DURGĀ daily under one of twelve appellations.<BR>E.<BR>नाम, and द्वादशी twelfth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधेय|नामधेयं
नामधेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A name or appellation.<BR>E.<BR>नाम a name, and धेय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>A name, an appellation.<BR>E.<BR>म्ना to be minded or remembered, मनिन् Uṇādi affix, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामशेष|नामशेषः
नामशेष<BR>m. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Dying, death.<BR>E.<BR>नाम a name, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामापराध|नामापराधः
नामापराध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Abusing a respectable object, as a pious man, a deity by name.<BR>E.<BR>नाम, and अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामित
नामित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, bent down, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>णम to bow, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाय|नायः
नाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Guiding, directing, (morally or physically.)<BR>2 Policy.<BR>3 Obtaining.<BR>4 Means, expedient.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, &c. affix ण or घञ्; also with अच् affix नय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=461" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A guide, a leader, a conductor.<BR>2 A chief, a head, pre-eminent, principal.<BR>3 A general, a commander.<BR>4 The central gem of a necklace.<BR>5 (In Erotick poetry,) The man, the husband or lover.<BR>f. (-यिका)<BR>1 A mistress, a wife, the female in the amatory poetry of the Hindūs.<BR>2 A sort of goddess, an inferior form of DURGĀ, and attendant upon her: there are eight Nāyikās.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायकाधिप|नायकाधिपः
नायकाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king, a sovereign prince.<BR>E.<BR>नायक a chief, and अधिप lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Relating to men, human, mortal, &c.<BR>2 Spiritual.<BR>nf. (-रं-रा)<BR>Water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A calf.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A multitude of men.<BR>E.<BR>नर, and अण् affix or न negative, ऋ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Infernal, hellish.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hell or the infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>नरक hell, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Infernal, being in hell, condemned to or deserving it.<BR>E.<BR>नारक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीट|नारकीटः
नारकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A sort of worm.<BR>2 A deceiver, one who disappoints expectations excited by himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारंगः|नारङ्गः
नारङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The juice of the pepper plant.<BR>2 An animal, one of twins.<BR>3 A catamite.<BR>4 The orange tree.<BR>E.<BR>नार many men, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारद|नारदः
नारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A name of NĀRADA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and one of the ten divine Munis or Ṛṣis; he is a friend of KṚṢṆA, a celebrated legislator, and inventor of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>नार men, and दा to give, (instruction,) ड affix; or नार water, and द who gives; offering sacrifices to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराच|नाराचः
नाराच<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 An iron arrow. (E. नार men, आङ् before चम to eat or consume, affix ड; destroying hosts of men.)<BR>2 A bad or cloudy day.<BR>3 A species of the Dhṛti metre. (E. नार water, आचम to spit, affix ड.)<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A goldsmith's scales, a fine or assay balance.<BR>E.<BR>नाराच an iron arrow, and ङीष् diminutive affix; also with कन् added in the fem. form, नाराचिका f. (-का)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU, but especially considered as the deity who was before all worlds.<BR>2 A sage, the son of DHARMA, a manifestation of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A valiant combatant.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A name of LAKṢMĪ, the goddess of prosperity, and wife of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 GAṄGĀ.<BR>4 A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>नारा the primeval waters, derived from नर the spirit of God, whence they originated, and अयन place of coming or moving; he who moved over the waters before creation: the word has several etymologies, as नर the spirit or soul of the universe, अण् affix, नार appertaining to it, the actions or emotions of the soul, and अयन pervading, influencing; again नार multitudes, mankind, and अयन place: present amongst all men, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणक्षेत्र|नारायणक्षेत्रं
नारायणक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Four cubits on either side of the stream of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>नारायण, and क्षेत्र shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणतैल|नारायणतैलं
नारायणतैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An oil of great reputed efficacy in many complaints, expressed from a variety of plants.<BR>E.<BR>नारायण, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणप्रिय|नारायणप्रियः
नारायणप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Attached to KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>नारायण, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणास्त्र|नारायणास्त्रं
नारायणास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A weapon of undefined form and mystical nature.<BR>E.<BR>नारायण, and अस्त्र weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिक
नारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Watery, aqueous.<BR>2 Spiritual.<BR>E.<BR>नर or नार, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेर|नारिकेरः
नारिकेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The cocoanut: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेल|नारिकेलः
नारिकेल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>नारिक watery (place), ईर to go or grow, affix क, and र optionally changed to ल; also with इन, नारिकेलि, and ड being substituted for र, नाडिकेर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A woman in general, a female.<BR>2 A species of the Madhya metre.<BR>E.<BR>नर a man, अञ् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकवच|नारीकवचः
नारीकवच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A king of the solar line, the son of AŚMAKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीकेल|नारीकेलः
नारीकेल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Fermented liquor made from the water of the cocoanut: see नारिकेल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीच|नारीचं
नारीच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>An esculent root, Arum colocasia: see नाडीच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीतरङ्गक|नारीतरंगक|नारीतरङ्गकः
नारीतरङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>नारी a woman, तरङ्ग capricious, and कन् affix of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीदूषण|नारीदूषणं
नारीदूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A vice or breach of duty in a woman, of which six cases are reckoned, drinking spirits, keeping bad company, quitting a husband, rambling abroad, and sleeping or dwelling in a strange house.<BR>E.<BR>नारी a woman, दूषण defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीप्रसङ्ग|नारीप्रसंग|नारीप्रसंगः
नारीप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Libertinism, lechery.<BR>E.<BR>नारी, and प्रसङ्ग addiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारीयान
नारीयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A litter or other conveyance for women.<BR>E.<BR>नारी, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्य्यङ्ग|नार्यङ्ग|नार्यंग|नार्यंगः|नार्यङ्गः|नार्य्यङ्गः
नार्य्यङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The orange tree; also नागरङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाल|नालं|नालः
नाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला or ली-लं)<BR>1 A hollow or tubular stalk, the stalk of the water lily, &c.<BR>2 Any pipe or tube.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A stalk or culm.<BR>2 An instrument for perforating an elephant's ear.<BR>3 A period of time, a Ghari, twentyfour minutes.<BR>4 Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>5 The pulse.<BR>E.<BR>णल to bind, affix ण, fem. affix टाप्, and ङीष्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालि|नालिः
नालि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>E.<BR>ल interchanged with डः see नाडि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिक|नालिकः
नालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A tubular stalk.<BR>2 An instrument for piercing an elephant's ear.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR>4 A sort of potherb, (Hibiscus cannabinus.)<BR>5 Any plant growing on a hollow stem, as Śaṇa, safflower, a mushroom, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नाली as above, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेर|नालिकेरः
नालिकेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>नल to bind, affix इन, नालि a leaf, &c. क air, wind, and इर what goes; fluttering in the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिजङ्घ|नालिजङ्घः
नालिजङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>A raven or the carrion crow.<BR>E.<BR>नालि a tube, and जङ्घा the leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिता
नालिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीक|नालीकः
नालीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A dart, a javelin, a pike.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>4 The fibrous stalk of the lotus.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>नाली a fibrous stalk, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीकिनी
नालीकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>नालीक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीव्रण|नालीव्रणः
नालीव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fistulous or sinous sore: see नाडीव्रण, ल and ड being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावमिक
नावमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ninth.<BR>E.<BR>नवम and ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=462" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविक|नाविकः
नाविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a vessel, a boat, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The helmsman of a vessel, the steersman, the pilot.<BR>2 A sailor.<BR>E.<BR>नौ a boat, affix ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
नाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Navigable.<BR>2 Belonging to a boat.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Newness, novelty.<BR>E.<BR>नौ a boat or vessel, and यक् affix; or नव new, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश|नाशः
नाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Annihilation, loss, destruction, disappearance.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 Flight, retreat.<BR>4 Abandonment, desertion.<BR>5 (In Arithmetic,) Elimination.<BR>E.<BR>णश to cease to be, affix धञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशन
नाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Destruction, perishing.<BR>E.<BR>णश to perish, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशयत्
नाशयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Destroying, annihilating.<BR>E.<BR>णश to perish, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशित
नाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>नश to perish, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशिन्
नाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 Destructive, destroying, a destroyer.<BR>2 Perishing, being lost or destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>नश to cease to be, in the causal form, affix इनि; or नाश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्टिक|नाष्टिकः
नाष्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to any thing lost.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The owner of any thing lost.<BR>E.<BR>नष्ट, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासत्य
नासत्य<BR>m. du. (-त्यौ)<BR>The two sons of AŚVINĪ, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>The constellation AŚVINĪ.<BR>E.<BR>न not, असत्य impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासा
नासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 The nose.<BR>2 The upper timber of a door.<BR>E.<BR>णस to sound, to stand, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासाछिन्नी|नासाच्छिन्नी
नासाछिन्नी<BR>f. (-न्नी)<BR>A sort of bird; also पूर्णिका.<BR>E.<BR>नासा the nose, छिन्न cut, fem. affix ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासादक्षिणावर्त्त|नासादक्षिणावर्त
नासादक्षिणावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Wearing the nose-ring in the right nostril by women who have money and children.<BR>E.<BR>नासा the nose, दक्षिण the right, and आवर्त्त a turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासादारु|नासादारुः
नासादारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The upper timber of a door: see नासा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासानाह|नासानाहः
नासानाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Thickening of the membrane of the nose, stoppage of the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>नासा, and नाह binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासापरिस्राव|नासापरिस्रावः
नासापरिस्राव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>Running at the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नासा, and परिस्राव flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासारन्ध्र|नासारंध्र
नासारन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>The nostril.<BR>E.<BR>नासा, and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासालु|नासालुः
नासालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Kāyaphal: see कट्फल.<BR>E.<BR>नासा the nose, and लु to cut, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासावंश|नासावंशः
नासावंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The bridge of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नासा, and वंश bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासावामावर्त्त|नासावामावर्त|नासावामावर्तः
नासावामावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>Wearing the nose-ring in the left nostril, a mark of sorrow or distress.<BR>E.<BR>नासा the nose, वाम the left side, आवर्त्त a turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासाशोष
नासाशोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Dryness of the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>नासा, and शोष drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकन्धम|नासिकंधम|नासिकन्धमः
नासिकन्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Blowing or breathing through the nose, snoring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नासिका the nose, ध्मा to blow, &c. affix खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकन्धय|नासिकंधय|नासिकन्धयः
नासिकन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Drinking through the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नासिका, and धेट् to drink, affix खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिका
नासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The nose.<BR>2 The upper timber, or nose as it were, of a door.<BR>3 A name of the nymph Aśvinī.<BR>E.<BR>नासा as above, affix कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकाग्र
नासिकाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The tip of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>नासिका, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकामल|नासिकामलं|नासिकामलः
नासिकामल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The mucus of the nose, snot.<BR>E.<BR>नासिका, and मल excrement; it may also be नासमल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्य|नासिक्यं|नासिक्यः
नासिक्य<BR>m. du. (-क्यौ)<BR>The two sons of Aśvinī.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>नासिका, and यत् affix of identity or descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्यक|नासिक्यकं
नासिक्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासीर|नासीरं
नासीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Advancing or skirmishing in front of an army, leaving the line, and defying the enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The van, or a champion who advances before the line.<BR>E.<BR>णास to sound, affix ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्ति
नास्ति<BR>ind.<BR>Nonexistence, not so, it is not.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, and अस्ति is, third person singular present tense of अस to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक|नास्तिकः
नास्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An atheist, but applied by the orthodox Hindūs, to any one who denies the divine authority of the Vedas, or doubts the legends of the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>नास्ति there is not (a god, &c.) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिकता
नास्तिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Atheism, denial of the deity, of a future state, of the divinity of the Vedas; Bauddhism, heresy, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् abstract affix added to the preceding; also with त्व, नास्तिकत्व, or with यत् affix नास्तिक्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक्य|नास्तिक्यं
नास्तिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Infidelity, atheism.<BR>E.<BR>नास्तिक, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तितद
नास्तितद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तित्व
नास्तित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Nonexistence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to नास्ति; also with तल् affix नास्तिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्य|नास्यं
नास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>The rein of an ox passed through the septum of the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>नासा the nose, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाह|नाहः
नाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Binding, confinement.<BR>2 A trap, a snare for catching deer, &c.<BR>3 Obstruction in any organ or secretion of the body, as costiveness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>णह to bind, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहल|नाहलः
नाहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A man of a barbarous or outcast tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुषि|नाहुषिः
नाहुषि<BR>m. (-षिः)<BR>The name of a king; also YAYĀTI.<BR>E.<BR>नहुष, and इञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकारण
निःकारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Causeless, unfounded.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकासन
निःकासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Expulsion, exile, turning out.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and कस to go, causal form, ल्युट् affix; also निःकाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःकासित|निःकासितः
निःकासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Turned out or forth, expelled, removed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, कस to go, in the causal form, affix क्त; also निष्कासित and निःकाशित and निष्काशित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्रामित|निःक्रामितः
निःक्रामित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expelled, turned out.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् out, क्रामित caused to go, also निष्क्रामित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षत्र
निःक्षत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Having none of the military tribe, (a city &c.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, क्षत्र a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्त
निःक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Thrown or sent away.<BR>2 Spent.<BR>3 Passed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before क्षिप्त to throw, &c. affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्य
निःक्षिप्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having thrown or sent away.<BR>2 Having spent, (as time.)<BR>3 Having wiped away, (as tears,) &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before क्षिप to throw, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षेप|निःक्षेपः
निःक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Throwing, sending, putting away.<BR>2 Spending.<BR>3 Passing, (as time.)<BR>4 Wiping away, (as tears.)<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and क्षिप to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःप्रभ|निःप्रभः
निःप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Gloomy, dark, obscured.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् privative, and प्रभा light; also निष्प्रभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःफल
निःफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fruitless, barren.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. फल fruit, more commonly निष्फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=463" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशंसय
निःशंसय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undoubted.<BR>E.<BR>नि for निर, शंसय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशङ्क
निःशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and शङ्का apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशलाक|निःशलाकः
निःशलाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Solitary, private.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् privative, and शलाका the maina; not even frequented by birds; also निश्शलाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशब्द|निःशब्दः
निःशब्द<BR>mfn. (-ब्दः-ब्दा-ब्दं)<BR>Silent, voiceless.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर्, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशूक|निःशूकः
निःशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Rice without any awn or beard.<BR>E.<BR>नि for निर्, and शूक beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निःशेष<BR>mfn. (षः-षा-षं)<BR>Complete, entire.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् negative, and शेष remainder; also निश्शेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशोध्य|निःशोध्यं
निःशोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Cleansed, cleared, purified.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् implying completion, and शोध्य pure; also निश्शोध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रयणी
निःश्रयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Wooden steps, a ladder, a staircase.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् out, forth, श्रि to go, affix ल्युट्; also with अच् affix, and इनि added, निःश्रयिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणि|निःश्रेणिः
निःश्रेणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 A ladder or staircase, a flight of steps.<BR>2 The wild date tree.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् implying certainty, and श्रणी a line; also निश्श्रेणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयस्
निःश्रेयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 Final beatitude, the release of the soul from the body, and its reunion with the primary and universal spirit.<BR>2 Happiness, welfare.<BR>3 Knowledge, learning.<BR>4 Belief, faith, devotedness.<BR>5 Apprehension, conception.<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>निः for निर् implying eternity or certainty, श्रेयस् best, अच् added; also निश्श्रेयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसन|निःश्वसनं
निःश्वसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sighing, &c.<BR>2 Breathing out.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and श्वसन breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसित
निःश्वसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sighed, sighing.<BR>2 Breathing out.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Expiration.<BR>2 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and श्वस to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वस्य
निःश्वस्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sighed.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and श्वस to breathe, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वास|निःश्वासः
निःश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Breathing out, expiration.<BR>2 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and श्वस to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वासपरम
निःश्वासपरम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Sorrowful, sighing.<BR>E.<BR>निःश्वास, and परम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःषमम्
निःषमम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of reproof, (improperly, unseasonably.)<BR>2 A term of regret, (alas!)<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, सम equal to, र is changed to Visarga, and स becomes ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसङ्ग|निःसंग|निःसंगः|निःसङ्गः
निःसङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Separated, unconnected.<BR>2 Regardless, indifferent, free from attachment or desire.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, सङ्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसंज्ञ
निःसंज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Senseless, insensible.<BR>E.<BR>निर not, संज्ञा sign of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्य
निःसत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>False, untrue.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्यता
निःसत्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Insincerity, falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. सत्यता truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसत्व
निःसत्व<BR>mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>1 Weak, impotent.<BR>2 Insignificant, mean, low.<BR>3 Nonexistent.<BR>4 Insubstantial.<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Insignificance, absence of power or consideration.<BR>2 Nonexistence.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. सत्व substance, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसन्धि|निःसंधि|निःसन्धिः
निःसन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>Firm, well-knit, compact.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, सन्धि junction; the joints of which are not perceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसम्पात|निःसंपात|निःसंपातः|निःसम्पातः
निःसम्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. सम्पात going, from पत to go, with सम् prefix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरण|निःसरणं
निःसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 A means or expedient.<BR>3 Exit, a going forth or out.<BR>4 Final beatitude.<BR>5 The entrance into a house or town, &c. the gate, the gate-way.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth or out, सरण place, means or act of going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निःसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Intolerable, unbearable.<BR>2 Irresistible.<BR>3 Unable to support or bear.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. सह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसहत्व
निःसहत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Inability to bear or support.<BR>2 Impatience, unendurance.<BR>E.<BR>निःसह, and त्व affix; also with तल्, निःसहता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसाध्वस
निःसाध्वस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Bold, fearless.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसार|निःसारः
निःसार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Sapless, pithless.<BR>2 Worthless, vain, insubstantial.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>2 Going forth.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The plantain.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, सार essence, pith; or निर out, सृ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारण|निःसारणं
निःसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going forth or out.<BR>2 The entrance of a house or town, &c. the passage, the road of ingress and egress.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth or out, and सारण place of going: see निःसरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारित|निःसारितः
निःसारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त्तं)<BR>Turned forth or out, expelled, dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, and सारित caused to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसुख
निःसुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 Disagreeable, distressing.<BR>2 Unhappy.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृत
निःसृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and सृ to go, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्नेह|निःस्नेहः
निःस्नेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Dry, not greasy or unctuous.<BR>2 Cold, insensible, unfeeling.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Linseed, (Linum utilitissimum.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, out, and स्नेह oil; whence oil is extracted or expressed, &c. or निर privative, स्नेह oil or affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्पृह
निःस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Free from desire.<BR>2 Disregarding, indifferent to.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. स्पृहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्राव|निःस्रावः
निःस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The moisture or water of boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, and स्राव what is oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्व|निःस्वः
निःस्व<BR>mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, nothing, स्व own property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्वादु
निःस्वादु<BR>mfn. (-दुः-दुः-दु)<BR>Insipid, tasteless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. स्वादु sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि<BR>ind.<BR>1 In, within; on, upon: a particle and prefix.<BR>2 A negative or prohibitive particle.<BR>3 A particle implying certainty, affirmation, proximity, continuance, doubt, intensity, fulness, &c. see the following compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकट|निकटं|निकटः
निकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 Kinless, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and कटच् affix; or नि prefixed to कट to go to or towards, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर|निकरः
निकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A flock or multitude.<BR>2 A heap, a bundle.<BR>3 Pith, sap, essence.<BR>4 Suitable or proper gift.<BR>5 A treasure, especially belonging to KUVERA: see निधि.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or upon, कृ to throw, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षण|निकर्षणं
निकर्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An open space or sort of play-ground in or near a town.<BR>2 A court at the entrance to a house.<BR>3 A neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>नि, with कर्षण ploughing; so prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकष|निकषः
निकष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The touch-stone.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The mother of the imps or goblins.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कष to injure, affix घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषा
निकषा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>2 In the middle, betwixt, between.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कष to hurt, Uṇādi affix आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषात्मज|निकषात्मजः
निकषात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a sort of goblin.<BR>E.<BR>निकषा the mother of the race, and आत्मज a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=464" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकस|निकसः
निकस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A touch-stone: see निकष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाम|निकामं|निकामः
निकाम<BR>n. adv. (-मं)<BR>Voluntarily, willingly, implying certainty.<BR>E.<BR>नि, काम will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय|निकायः
निकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An assemblage of persons performing like duties, a congregation, an audience.<BR>2 A flock, a multitude.<BR>3 A butt, a mark.<BR>4 A house, a habitation.<BR>5 The Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or within, चि to collect, affix घञ्, and क substituted for the radical initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय्य|निकाय्यः
निकाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>as above: see निकाय, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
निकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Opposition, contradiction.<BR>2 Injury, wrong, offence.<BR>3 Wickedness; malice.<BR>4 Abuse, reproach, disrespect.<BR>5 Raising, tossing or lifting up.<BR>6 Piling or winnowing corn.<BR>E.<BR>नि depreciative prefix, कृ to make, or कॄ to throw, affix घञ् or अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारण|निकारणं
निकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कॄ to injure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाष|निकाषः
निकाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before कष to hurt, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकास|निकासः
निकास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Like, (in composition): see नीकास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चक|निकुञ्चकः
निकुञ्चक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A measure of capacity equal to (1/4th) of a Kuḍava.<BR>E.<BR>नि before कुचि to be small, affix क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्चित|निकुञ्चितं
निकुञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contracted.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, and कुञ्चित curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुंजं|निकुञ्जं|निकुंजः|निकुञ्जः
निकुञ्ज<BR>mn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जं)<BR>An arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with creepers.<BR>E.<BR>नि expletive, and कुञ्ज an arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भ|निकुंभ|निकुंभः|निकुम्भः
निकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 The son of KUMBHAKARṆA, the brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 A plant, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>E.<BR>कु the earth भू to be, affix खच्, and नि prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुम्भिला|निकुंभिला
निकुम्भिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A place where offerings with fire are made.<BR>E.<BR>नि before कुम्भ a jar, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरुम्ब|निकुरुंब|निकुरुंबं
निकुरुम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A flock or multitude; also निकुरुम्बक.<BR>E.<BR>नि before कुर to divide or cut, affix अम्बच्, and उ substituted for the penultimate; also read निकुरुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत|निकृतः
निकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dishonest, wicked, perverse.<BR>2 Removed, set aside, dismissed.<BR>3 Tricked, cheated, deceived.<BR>4 Injured, afflicted.<BR>5 Low, base, vile.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कृत to cut, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृति|निकृतिः
निकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Wickedness, dishonesty.<BR>2 Abuse, reproach.<BR>3 Rejection, removal.<BR>4 Poverty, indigence.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कृत to cut, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्ट|निकृष्टः
निकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Outcast, despised, low, vile.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कृष to make furrows, to revile or despise, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेचाय|निकेचायः
निकेचाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Piling or collecting repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चि to gather, reit. v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेत|निकेतः
निकेत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A house, a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, कित to dwell, affix घञ्; also with युच् affix निकेतन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतक|निकेतकः
निकेतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A house, a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to निकेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतन|निकेतनं|निकेतनः
निकेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A house, a habitation.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An onion.<BR>E.<BR>see निकेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोचक|निकोचकः
निकोचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to कुच to be crooked, affix वुन्; also derived from कुठ to surround, निकोठक; also with अण् pleonasm added, निकौचक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वण|निक्वणः
निक्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A musical tone or sound.<BR>2 Any sound.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to क्वण to sound, अप् affix; also with घञ् affix निक्वाण m. (-णः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्ष
निक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (निक्षति)<BR>To kiss: see णिक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षण|निक्षणं
निक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Kissing.<BR>E.<BR>निक्ष to kiss, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षा
निक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A nit.<BR>E.<BR>णिश to meditate, Uṇādi affix स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्त|निक्षिप्तं
निक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Rejected, abandoned, foregone, given or thrown away.<BR>2 Deposited, pawned, pledged.<BR>3 Thrust into, placed in.<BR>4 Sent, sent off or away.<BR>E.<BR>नि implying absolutely or internally, and क्षिप्त thrown away, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिपत्
निक्षिपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>Throwing or placing in or upon.<BR>E.<BR>नि before क्षिप to throw, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप|निक्षेपः
निक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A pledge, a deposit in general, or one which is counted or particularised in presence of the receiver, and left without cover or seal.<BR>2 Abandoning, parting with, throwing away.<BR>3 Sending or putting away.<BR>4 Wiping, drying.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to क्षिप to throw or reject, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्तृ
निक्षेप्तृ<BR>mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ)<BR>Who or what places or deposites.<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>A depositor, a pawner or pledger.<BR>E.<BR>नि before क्षिष to throw, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्ब्ब|निखर्ब|निखर्ब्बं|निखर्ब्बः
निखर्ब्ब<BR>mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्बं)<BR>Dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>n. (-र्ब्बं)<BR>A billion.<BR>E.<BR>नि certainly, verily, खर्ब्ब short, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखात
निखात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dug, dug up, excavated.<BR>2 Fixed in the ground as a stake.<BR>E.<BR>नि before खन to dig, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिल|निखिलं
निखिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>All, entire, complete.<BR>E.<BR>नि negative, खिल defective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगड|निगडः
निगड<BR>mn. (-डः-डं)<BR>An iron chain for the feet, a fetter, but especially the heel chains of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>नि not, गड to drop, (to drop off,) affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडित|निगडितः
निगडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, tied, chained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निगड a chain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगण|निगणः
निगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The smoke of a burnt offering or sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>नि implying certainty, prefixed to गण to estimate, affix क; by which the presence of fire is indicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद|निगदः
निगद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Speech, speaking, discourse.<BR>2 Audible recitation of prayers or charms.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative prefix, गद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदत्
निगदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Speaking, saying, speaking to, addressing.<BR>E.<BR>निगद to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदित
निगदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, spoken.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गद to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदितवत्
निगदितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-नती-वत्)<BR>Speaking, having spoken.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गद to speak, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम|निगमः
निगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A town, a city.<BR>2 A market, a fair.<BR>3 Holy-writ, the Vedas collectively.<BR>4 A road, a market road.<BR>5 Trade, traffick.<BR>6 A camp or caravan of itinerant dealers, as Banjaras, &c.<BR>7 Certainty, assurance.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative prefix, गम to go, affix घ; by which people go, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमन|निगमनं
निगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Certain or logical conclusion, the winding up of a syllogism.<BR>2 Going.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगर|निगरः
निगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Eating, swallowing.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, गॄ to swallow, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरण|निगरणं|निगरणः
निगरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Eating, swallowing.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The throat, the gullet.<BR>2 Smoke of a burnt offering.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to गॄ to swallow, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगाद|निगादः
निगाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Speech, discourse.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गद to speak, affix घञ्; also निगद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=465" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगार|निगारः
निगार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Swallowing.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to गॄ to swallow, affix घञ्; also निगर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगाल|निगालः
निगाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The throat or neck of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गल to eat, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालवत्
निगालवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>निगाल as above, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीत
निगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sung, said.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगु|निगुः
निगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>The mind, the faculty of feeling and reasoning.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmation, गम to go, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढ|निगूढः
निगूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Profound, obscure.<BR>2 Hidden, concealed.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A sort of wild bean: see मुद्ग.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गुह to hide or conceal, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढार्थ
निगूढार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Having a hidden sense or purpose.<BR>E.<BR>निगूढ, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहनीय
निगूहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be hid or concealed.<BR>2 To be protected or defended.<BR>E.<BR>नि before गुह to conceal, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Assailed, attacked.<BR>2 Harassed, spoiled.<BR>3 Seized, arrested.<BR>4 Restrained, subdued, checked.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीति|निगृहीतिः
निगृहीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Restraint, check, &c.: see निग्रह.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्णत्
निगृह्णत्<BR>mfn. (-ह्णन्-ह्णन्ती-ह्णत्)<BR>1 Seizing, taking.<BR>2 Suppressing, restraining.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृह्य
निगृह्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Having restrained or suppressed.<BR>3 Having arrested or confined.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह|निग्रहः
निग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Aversion, disfavour, discouragement, dislike.<BR>2 Abusing, blaming.<BR>3 Binding, confinement, capture, arrest.<BR>4 A binding, a tie.<BR>5 Restraint, subjugation.<BR>6 Suppression, putting down.<BR>7 A boundary, a limit.<BR>8 Administering medicine.<BR>9 Killing.<BR>10 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take or seize, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहण
निग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Subduing, suppression.<BR>2 Defeat.<BR>3 Capture.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहस्थान
निग्रहस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Failure in logical argument.<BR>E.<BR>निग्रह, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राह|निग्राहः
निग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Aversion, &c. used as an imprecation, as निग्राहस्ते भूयात् confusion seize you, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to seize, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ|निघः
निघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A round or circle, a ball, any thing whose height and circumference are equal.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to kill, affix क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघण्टु|निघंटु|निघंटुः|निघण्टुः
निघण्टु<BR>m. (-ण्ठुः)<BR>A vocabulary, a collection of words or names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघस|निघसः
निघस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Food, victuals.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अद to eat, अप् affix, and घस substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघाति|निघातिः
निघाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An iron club or mace.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to kill, इञ् Uṇādi affix, घात substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघानिघ
निघानिघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Of different forms or sizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्ट|निघुष्टं
निघुष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>नि before घुष to sound, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्व|निघृष्वः
निघृष्व<BR>m. (-ष्वः)<BR>1 A hoof.<BR>2 A mule.<BR>3 A boar.<BR>4 A road.<BR>E.<BR>नि before घृष to pound, Uṇādi affix वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्न|निघ्नः
निघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>1 Docile, subservient, domestic^1, dependant.<BR>2 Completing a quotient, (in Arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to injure or do mischief, क aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नत्|निघ्नन्त्
निघ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नन्ती-घ्नत्)<BR>1 Slaying.<BR>2 Destroying, overcoming.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्नान
निघ्नान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Slaying, killing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to kill, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचय|निचयः
निचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Heap, assemblage, collection.<BR>2 Certainty.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चिञ् to collect, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयिन्
निचयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Having or containing a quantity. full of, redolent with, abounding.<BR>E.<BR>निचय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिकी
निचिकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A capital cow: see नैचिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचित|निचितं
निचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Full, filled.<BR>2 Covered, overspread.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चि to collect, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुल|निचुलः
निचुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>2 An upper and outer garment.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चुल to lift up, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलक|निचुलकं
निचुलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A breast-plate, a cuirass.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also निचोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोल|निचोलः
निचोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>A cover, a wrapper, a veil, a surtout.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चुल to lift up, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलक|निचोलकः
निचोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of jacket, but especially a soldier's jacket or a body dress, serving as a cuirass or breast-plate.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to निचोल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छवि|निच्छविः|निछवि
निच्छवि<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>A district, the modern Tirhut.<BR>E.<BR>नि constantly, छवि light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिद्र
निच्छिद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Unimpeached.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. च्छिद्र flaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिवि|निच्छिविः|निछिवि
निच्छिवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>A man of one of the degraded classes, born from the outcast Kṣatriya; the occupation of this caste is apparently public exhibition of tricks, prize-fighting, &c. being classed with the Jhallas, Mallas, and others.<BR>E.<BR>नि privative, छवि light or credit, इ substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छेद|निच्छेदः
निच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>2 (In Arithmetic,) Leaving no common measure.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज|निजं
निज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Own.<BR>2 Perpetual, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>नि implying continuance, and ज what is produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजिघृक्षयत्
निजिघृक्षयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Desirous of making to excel.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ग्रह to take, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निजुह्नूषु
निजुह्नूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to conceal.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्नु to hide, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटल|निटलं
निटल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>नि before टल to be marked, (with frowns, &c.) affix अप् or घञ्, whence it is also निटाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलाक्ष|निटलाक्षः
निटलाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>निटल the forehead, and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडीन|निडीनं
निडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The flight of a bird, or a peculiar mode of flying.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative prefix, and डीन flight, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्डिका
निण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्ब|नितंब|नितंबः|नितम्बः
नितम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A woman's buttocks.<BR>2 The buttocks or posteriors in general, or as it is sometimes applied, the circumference of the hip and loins.<BR>3 The shoulder.<BR>4 The side of a mountain.<BR>5 A bank or shore.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to तम्ब to go, affix अच् or तम to go, with ब aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितम्बिनी|नितंबिनी
नितम्बिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman with large and handsome posteriors.<BR>E.<BR>नितम्ब as above, इनि and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितराम्
नितराम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Always, continually, eternally.<BR>2 Especially, particularly.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, डतरच् comparative affix, and आम् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=466" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितल|नितलं
नितल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>One of the seven divisions of Pātāla or hell.<BR>E.<BR>नि not, (known,) तल depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितान्त|नितांत|नितान्तं
नितान्त<BR>adj. mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Much, excessive.<BR>adv. n. (-न्तं)<BR>Much, excessively.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to तम to desire, affix क्त, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य<BR>mfn. adj. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Eternal, everlasting, continual, perpetual; past, present, and future.<BR>2 Regular, fixed, invariable.<BR>n. adv. (-त्यं)<BR>Always, eternally, continually. sub. Indispensable rite or act.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 The goddess MANASĀ.<BR>3 A Śakti, a form of DURGĀ, or personified energy of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>नि particle implying perpetually, and त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकर्म्मन्|नित्यकर्मन्
नित्यकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Indispensable act or ceremony, as observance of the five great sacrifices, or any daily and necessary rite.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and कर्म्म act; also नित्यक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यकृत्य
नित्यकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Regular and necessary act or ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and कृत्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यगति|नित्यगतिः
नित्यगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य eternal, गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यता
नित्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Perpetuity, eternity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to नित्य; also with त्व, नित्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदा
नित्यदा<BR>ind.<BR>Always, constantly, and eternally.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदान|नित्यदानं
नित्यदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Daily alms.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यनैमित्तिक
नित्यनैमित्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Any act or ceremony which though occasional is of regular recurrence, as Śrāddhas at fixed lunar periods.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and नैमित्तिक occasional; also नित्यनैमित्तिक कर्म्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यप्रलय|नित्यप्रलयः
नित्यप्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The constant loss of living beings.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययुक्त
नित्ययुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Always busy or engaged in.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and युक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्ययौवन
नित्ययौवन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ever or always young.<BR>m. (-ना)<BR>A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य always, and यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशस्
नित्यशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Always, constantly, eternally.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यसम|नित्यसमः
नित्यसम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An erroneous answer, one asserting perpetuity for perishable things.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानध्याय|नित्यानध्यायः
नित्यानध्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A period when the perusal of the Vedas is invariably prohibited, as the day of full moon, new moon, the eighth and fourteenth days of the half month.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य always, अन् negative prefix, अध्याय to be read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यानित्य
नित्यानित्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Eternal and perishable, permanent and temporary, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and अनित्य transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद<BR>(इ) निदि r. 1st cl. (निन्दति)<BR>To reproach, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Poison, venom.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative prefix, दो to destroy, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदत्त
निदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given, given absolutely.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदद्रु|निदद्रुः
निदद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>निद poison, and द्रु tree, a living Upas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An example or illustration.<BR>2 Injunction, precept.<BR>3 Tenour, purport.<BR>4 Authority, text.<BR>E.<BR>नि fully or certainly, दर्शन showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघ|निदाघः
निदाघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 The hot season, (May and June.)<BR>2 Heat, warmth.<BR>3 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, दह to burn, घञ् affix, and घ substituted for ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकर|निदाघकरः
निदाघकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>निदाघ the hot season, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघकाल|निदाघकालः
निदाघकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The hot season, two months previous to the rains, about May and June.<BR>E.<BR>निदाघ, and काल time or season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघसिन्धु|निदाघसिन्धुः
निदाघसिन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A river in the hot weather, one nearly dry.<BR>E.<BR>निदाघ, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदान|निदानं
निदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A first cause, a primary or remote cause.<BR>2 Disappearance, cessation or removal of a first cause.<BR>3 Purification, purity, correctness.<BR>4 Asking for the recompense or objects of austere devotion.<BR>5 End, cessation.<BR>6 A rope for tying a calf.<BR>7 Ascertaining the causes of disease, study of symptoms with a view to trace the remote or proximate causes; hence this word is the name of a division of all works on medicine.<BR>E.<BR>नि always or certainly, दा to give, affix ल्युट्; by which all effects are produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्ध|निदिग्धं
निदिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Smeared, anointed, plastered.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to दिह to smear, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्धिका
निदिग्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासन|निदिध्यासनं
निदिध्यासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Deep and repeated consideration, thinking of or recalling repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ध्यै in the reiterative form, affix ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिष्ट
निदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Ordered, directed.<BR>2 Advised, enjoined.<BR>3 Explained, pointed out.<BR>E.<BR>नि implying certainty, दिश to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदुश
निदुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेश|निदेशः
निदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Order, command, direction, instruction.<BR>2 Speech, speaking, saying, relating.<BR>3 Vicinity, proximity.<BR>4 The word of command.<BR>E.<BR>नि verily, दिश to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिन्
निदेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Showing, directing, pointing out.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A quarter of space.<BR>E.<BR>नि before दिश to show, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेष्टृ
निदेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what shows or points out, explaining, advising, commanding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before दिश to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Sleep, sleepiness, sloth.<BR>E.<BR>णिद to condemn or censure, Uṇādi affix रक्; or द्रै to sleep, affix क्विप्, and नि prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राण|निद्राणः
निद्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Asleep, sleepy, drowsy.<BR>2 Shut up, closed.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा as above, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रात्
निद्रात्<BR>mfn. (-द्रान्-द्रान्ती-द्रात्)<BR>Sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>नि before द्रा to go, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राभङ्ग|निद्राभङ्गः
निद्राभङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Awaked, aroused from sleep.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा, भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रायमान
निद्रायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sleeping, asleep.<BR>E.<BR>नि before द्रै to sleep, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालु|निद्रालुः
निद्रालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Sleeping, sleepy, drowsy, slothful.<BR>f. (-लुः)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly नीली.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रावृक्ष|निद्रावृक्षः
निद्रावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा sleep, and वृक्ष a tree, (whose fruit is sleep.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रासंजनन
निद्रासंजनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Phlegm, phlegmatic^1 humour.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा sleep, and संजनन producing, occasioning.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधन|निधनं|निधनः
निधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor.<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 Race, family.<BR>2 Loss, disappearance, annihilation.<BR>3 Death, dying.<BR>4 The seventh asterism of the lunar mansions, reckoning from that under [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">Page468</a>] which a person is born.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The head of a family.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धन to perish, affix अच्, or नि neg. धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=467" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनकारिन्
निधनकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Destroying, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>निधन, and कारिन् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनता
निधनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Poverty.<BR>E.<BR>निधन, and तल् added; also with त्व, निधनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधान|निधानं
निधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A Nidhi or divine treasure, belonging especially to KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>2 A receptacle, a place or vessel in or on which any thing is collected or deposited.<BR>3 Place of cessation or rest.<BR>4 Property, possessions, wealth.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or on, धा to possess, Uṇādi affix क्युप्: see निधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधापक
निधापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>2 Burnt timber, charcoal.<BR>3 The castor oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधाय
निधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having fixed or placed in or on.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधि|निधिः
निधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or divine treasures, nine of which are enumerated: viz. The Padma, Mahāpadma, Śaṅkha, Makara, Kacchapa, Mukunda, Nanda, Nīla, and Kharba: their nature is not exactly defined, though some of them appear to be precious gems; according to the Tāntrika system, they are personified and worshipped as demigods, attendant either upon KUVERA or upon LAKṢMĪ, the goddess of prosperity.<BR>2 A receptacle, a place of asylum or accumulation, as a treasury, a granary, a nest, &c.; also figuratively, as गुणनिधिः a man who contains or is endowed with all good qualities.<BR>2 A treasure, any sum or quantity of wealth or valuables.<BR>4 A medicinal plant and perfume, commonly Jivaka.<BR>5 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, धा to have, affix कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिनाथ|निधिनाथः
निधिनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>निधि a divine treasure, and नाथ lord; also similar compounds, as निधिप्रभु, निधीश्वर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीयमान
निधीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being in the course of placing, depositing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धा to have, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधीश|निधीशः
निधीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>निधि as above, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवन|निधुवनं
निधुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Coition, copulation.<BR>2 Trembling, agitation.<BR>3 Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>4 Sport, play, pastime.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धू to shake or agitate, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधेय
निधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be placed in or on, to be deposited, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धा to have, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यान|निध्यानं
निध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ध्यै to think, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्वान|निध्वानः
निध्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ध्वन to sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषा
निनीषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Desire to take or lead.<BR>E.<BR>णी to lead, desid. form, affix अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनीषु
निनीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous to take or lead.<BR>E.<BR>णी to lead, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दक|निंदक|निन्दकः
निन्दक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Reproachful, abusive, scurrilous, censorious.<BR>E.<BR>निदि to abuse, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दत्
निन्दत्<BR>mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दन्ती-न्दत्)<BR>Abusing, blaming.<BR>E.<BR>निन्द to blame, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दतल|निन्दतलः
निन्दतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Having a maimed or defective hand: it is also sometimes read निम्नतल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दन|निंदन|निंदनं|निन्दनं
निन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reproach, censure, blame.<BR>E.<BR>णिद to reprove, affix ल्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दा|निंदा
निन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>1 Censure, reproach, reproof, blame, abuse, reviling.<BR>2 Injury, injuring.<BR>3 Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>णिद to abuse, &c. affixes अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दास्तुति|निंदास्तुति|निन्दास्तुतिः
निन्दास्तुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Irony, ironical praise.<BR>E.<BR>निन्दा censure, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनङ्क्षु|निनंक्षु
निनङ्क्षु<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षु)<BR>Wishing to kill.<BR>E.<BR>नि before णश to destroy, desid. v., उ affix, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनद|निनदः
निनद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>नि before नद to sound, affix अप्; also निनाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनयन|निनयनं
निनयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Engaging in performance. नि before णी to lead, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनाद|निनादः
निनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>नि before नद to sound, affix घञ्; also निनद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निनादित
निनादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded.<BR>E.<BR>नि before नद to sound, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दित|निंदित|निन्दितः
निन्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abused, reviled, reproved.<BR>2 Low, despicable, worthy of being reviled.<BR>3 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>णिद to abuse, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्दु|निंदु|निंदुः|निन्दुः
निन्दु<BR>f. (-न्दुः)<BR>A woman bearing a dead child.<BR>E.<BR>णिदि to abuse, affix डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निन्द्य|निंद्य
निन्द्य<BR>mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्यं)<BR>Bad, vile, despicable, reprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>निन्दा, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निप|निपं|निपः
निप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A water jar.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>नि continuative particle, पा to drink, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठ|निपठः
निपठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Reading, studying or lecturing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पठ to read, affix अप्; also with ल्युट्, निपठनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठित
निपठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Read, studied.<BR>E.<BR>नि, पठ to read, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपठिति|निपठितिः
निपठिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Reading, study.<BR>E.<BR>नि, पठ to read, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतत्
निपतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>1 Falling, falling down, prostrating.<BR>2 Alighting.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पत to fall, affix शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतन|निपतनं
निपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Falling.<BR>2 Alighting, descending.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or on, पत to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपतित
निपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fallen, fallen down.<BR>2 Alighted, descended.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or on, पत to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्य
निपत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having fallen down, prostrate.<BR>2 Having alighted.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पत to fall, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपत्या
निपत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 A field of battle.<BR>2 Any plashy or slippery ground.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, पत to fall, affix क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाक|निपाकः
निपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cooking, maturing, ripening.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पच to cook, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपाठ|निपाठः
निपाठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Reading, study of the sacred books, or public perusal of popular poems.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पठ to read, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपात|निपातः
निपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Falling, coming down, alighting.<BR>3 Irregularity, (in Grammar,)<BR>4 A particle, (in ditto.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before पत to go, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातन|निपातनं
निपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Causing to descend or fall, throwing down.<BR>2 Beating, knocking down.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>4 (In Grammar,) Irregularity, exception.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पत to fall, in the causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपातित
निपातित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Beaten down, made to fall or descend.<BR>2 Killed.<BR>3 Irregular, excepted.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पत to fall, causal form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=468" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपान|निपानं
निपान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A through or ditch near a well for watering cattle.<BR>2 A well.<BR>3 Any reservoir of water.<BR>4 A milk pail.<BR>5 Drinking, imbibing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पा to drink, ल्युट् affix; also with कन् added, निपानक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडन|निपीडनं
निपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Squeezing, pressing.<BR>2 Embracing.<BR>3 Hurting, giving pain.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पीड to give pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीडित
निपीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Squeezed, pressed.<BR>2 Embraced.<BR>3 Pained, hurt.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पीड to give pain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीड्य
निपीड्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having pressed or squeezed, having pressed against or upon.<BR>2 Having embraced.<BR>3 Having hurt.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पीड to pain, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीत
निपीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Drank, drank up.<BR>2 Absorbed, imbibed, dried up.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पा to drink, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपीयमान
निपीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being drank.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पा to drink, pass. form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निपुण|निपुणः
निपुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Clever, skilful, conversant.<BR>E.<BR>नि before पुण to be pure, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निफालन
निफालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Seeing, sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबद्ध
निबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Bound, confined.<BR>2 Bound, costive.<BR>3 Fixed upon, fastened to.<BR>4 Checked, restrained.<BR>5 Restricted to.<BR>E.<BR>नि before बध to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्ध|निबंध|निबन्धं|निबंधः|निबन्धः
निबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Epistasis, suppression of urine or constipation.<BR>2 Commentary, explanation of technical rules.<BR>3 The Nimb tree: see निम्ब.<BR>4 Binding, confinement.<BR>5 Intentness on or attachment to.<BR>6 A grant of property, an assignment of cattle or money for support, a corrody.<BR>7 Fixed property, not moveable or fluctuating.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Song, singing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before बधि to bind, affix धञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धदान
निबन्धदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Grant of an assignment, gift of a corrody.<BR>E.<BR>निबन्ध, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धन|निबंधन|निबंधनं|निबन्धनं
निबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cause, motive, origin.<BR>2 Binding, confining.<BR>3 Checking, restraining.<BR>4 Fastening.<BR>5 A grant, an assignment.<BR>6 A commentary.<BR>7 The tie or peg of a lute.<BR>E.<BR>नि before बधि to bind, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धित|निबन्धितः
निबन्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, confined, tied.<BR>E.<BR>नि before बन्ध to bind, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबन्धृ
निबन्धृ<BR>mfn. (-न्धा-न्ध्री-न्धृ)<BR>Who or what ties or binds.<BR>m. (-न्धा)<BR>An author, a commentator.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative, बन्ध to bind, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभ|निभः
निभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Like, resembling, similar.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Fraud, trick, disguise.<BR>2 Light, manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>नि before भा to shine, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभालन|निभालनं
निभालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before भाल to see, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभूत|निभूतं
निभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Past, gone.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative, भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृत|निभृतः
निभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Modest, humble, unassuming.<BR>2 Lonely, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>नि before भृ to cherish, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निभृतम्
निभृतम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Privately, apart.<BR>2 Unobservedly in a corner.<BR>3 Covertly, in disguise or out of sight.<BR>E.<BR>नि before भृ to cherish, affix क्त, and मुट् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम|निमः
निम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A pin, a stake.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, माञ् to plunge or stick, affix ड; stuck in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमग्न
निमग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Plunged in, immersed.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, मस्ज to bathe, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जत्
निमज्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्)<BR>Bathing, plunging in.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मस्ज to bathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जथु|निमज्जथुः
निमज्जथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Sleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, मस्ज to bathe, अथु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमज्जन|निमज्जनं
निमज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bathing.<BR>2 Immersion.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मस्ज to bathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रण|निमंत्रण|निमंत्रणं|निमन्त्रणं
निमन्त्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Summoning, calling.<BR>2 Inviting, invitation.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative, मन्त्रण advising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमन्त्रित
निमन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Summoned, convoked.<BR>2 Invited.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मन्त्र to advise, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमय|निमयः
निमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मि to measure, to mete, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमातव्य
निमातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be exchanged or bartered.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मा to measure, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमि|निमिः
निमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A son of IKṢVĀKU, condemned to reside in the twinkle of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्त|निमित्तं
निमित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>1 Cause, motive, instrumental cause.<BR>2 Mark, sign, spot, trace, token.<BR>3 Omen.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मि to measure, क्त affix; also with कन् added निमित्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तक|निमित्तकं
निमित्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Kissing, a kiss.<BR>2 Cause, &c.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकारण|निमित्तकारणं
निमित्तकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The instrumental cause, the material or the agent, especially the deity considered as the agent in creation.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त the instrumental cause, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तकाल|निमित्तकालः
निमित्तकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Any given or specific time.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तत्व
निमित्तत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Causality, instrumentality.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त, and त्व affix; also with तल्, निमित्तता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तधर्म्म|निमित्तधर्म|निमित्तधर्मः
निमित्तधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Expiation.<BR>2 Any occasional or special penance, rite, or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त, and धर्म्म piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तमात्र
निमित्तमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The mere agent or instrument.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त, and मात्र alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तविद्
निमित्तविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त a mark, (lucky or unlucky,) and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमित्तावृत्ति|निमित्तावृत्तिः
निमित्तावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Dependance upon a special cause or occasion.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त, and आवृत्ति revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिष|निमिषः
निमिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Twinkling of the eye.<BR>2 The twinkling of an eye, considered as a measure of time.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मिष to twinkle, affix क; also with घञ् affix निमेष, or निमि a proper name, षद to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमिषत्
निमिषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Blinking, closing the eyelids.<BR>E.<BR>निमिष to twinkle, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलत्
निमीलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Twinkling, closing, (as the eye.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before मील to disappear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलन|निमीलनं
निमीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>2 Twinkling of the eye, shutting of the eyelids, winking.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मील to disappear, &c. affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलिका
निमीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Fraud, trick, disguise.<BR>2 Twinkling of the eye, winking, blinking.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मील to twinkle, affix वुन् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमीलित
निमीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Closed, (as the eyelid,) twinkled, blinked.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मील to disappear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेय|निमेयः
निमेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मि to measure affix यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=469" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेष|निमेषः
निमेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Twinkling of the eye.<BR>2 A momentary space of time, a twinkling of the eye considered as a measure of time: see निमिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषक|निमेषकः
निमेषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Twinkling of the eye.<BR>2 A firefly.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषकृत्
निमेषकृत्<BR>f. (कृत्)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>निमेष twinkling, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निमेषरुच्
निमेषरुच्<BR>m. (-रुक्)<BR>A firefly.<BR>E.<BR>निमेष a twinkling, रुच् who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्न|निम्नं
निम्न<BR>mfn. (-म्नः-म्ना-म्नं)<BR>Deep, profound, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before म्ना to mind, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नग
निम्नग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Deep, going deep.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>निम्न deep, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नता
निम्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Depth, profundity.<BR>E.<BR>निम्न with तल् affix; also with त्व, निम्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्नोन्नत
निम्नोन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>High and low, up and down.<BR>E.<BR>निम्न, and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्ब|निंब|निंबः|निम्बः
निम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>The Nimb or Neemb tree, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR>E.<BR>निबि to sprinkle, affix अच्; also with कन् added, निम्बकः these words are written with either ब or व, as निम्ब or निम्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्बतरु|निम्बतरुः
निम्बतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens); it is considered as one of the trees of paradise.<BR>E.<BR>निम्ब as above, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निम्बूक|निम्बूकं|निंबूकः|निम्बूकः
निम्बूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The common lime, (Citrus acida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियत|नियतः
नियत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Self-governed, subdued, restrained.<BR>2 Attentive, fixed or intent upon.<BR>3 Constant, permanent.<BR>4 Ascertained, certain, fixed.<BR>5 Inevitable.<BR>6 Positive, definite.<BR>7 Permeable, what may be spread through or over.<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>Always, constantly.<BR>subst.<BR>Elementary or crude matter, the recipient of attributes or properties.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to restrain, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतमानस
नियतमानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Of subdued mind or spirit.<BR>E.<BR>नियत, and मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतात्मन्
नियतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Self-regulated, self-controlled or restrained.<BR>E.<BR>नियत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियताहार
नियताहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Abstemious, moderate.<BR>E.<BR>नियत, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियति|नियतिः
नियति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Destiny, luck, good or bad fortune.<BR>2 A religious duty or obligation.<BR>3 Self-command, self-restraint.<BR>(-ती)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to refrain, affix क्तिन् or क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियतेन्द्रिय|नियतेन्द्रियः
नियतेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of restrained or subdued passions.<BR>E.<BR>नियत controlled, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तव्य
नियन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be restrained, checked, controlled, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to restrain, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्तृ|नियंतृ
नियन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Who or what restrains, governs, or guides.<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A charioteer, a coachman.<BR>2 A ruler, a governor, a master.<BR>3 A punisher.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to restrain, affix तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियन्त्रित|नियंत्रित|नियन्त्रितः
नियन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Checked, restrained, governed, guided.<BR>E.<BR>नि affirmative particle, यम to restrain or check, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम|नियमः
नियम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Agreement, contract, engagement, assent, promise.<BR>2 Any religious observance voluntarily practised, as fasting, watching, pilgrimage, praying, &c.; voluntary penance, meritorious or supererogatory piety.<BR>3 A religious observance or obligation in general.<BR>4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>5 Rule, precept.<BR>6 Usage, practice.<BR>7 Common places in poetry, conventional expression, as notice of the Birch in describing the Himālaya, of the Sandal tree in describing the Malaya mountain, the whiteness of vesture, blackness of hair, the cry of the peacock in the rains, of the Koïl in spring, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to refrain, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमन|नियमनं
नियमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Precept, fixed practice or rule.<BR>2 Binding.<BR>3 Restraining, checking.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to restrain, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमपर
नियमपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Observing fixed rules.<BR>2 Relating to or corroborative of a rule.<BR>E.<BR>नियम, and पर attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियमित|नियमितः
नियमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Regulated, prescribed.<BR>2 Governed, guided.<BR>3 Checked, restrained.<BR>4 Bound, confined.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to check, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियम्य
नियम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having restrained.<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>To be checked or restrained.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to govern, ल्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियातन|नियातनं
नियातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Causing to fall or descend: see निपातन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियाम|नियामः
नियाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Religious act, penance, fasting, &c. especially if an act of supererogation.<BR>2 Restraint.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to restrain, affix घञ्: see नियम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियामक|नियामकः
नियामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Guiding, governing, what regulates or restrains.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A boatman, a sailor; but variously applied to one who rows, who steers, or who keeps a look-out from the mast head.<BR>2 A pilot, a helmsman.<BR>3 A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यम to go or stop, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुक्त|नियुक्तः
नियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Engaged in, applying or attached to.<BR>2 Authorized, called, appointed.<BR>3 Directed, enjoined, commanded.<BR>4 Ascertained.<BR>5 Fastened or attached to.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुञ्जान
नियुञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Authorizing, appointing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुज्य
नियुज्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having joined or attached to.<BR>2 Having put to or harnessed.<BR>E.<BR>नि, युज to join, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुत|नियुतं
नियुत<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 A million.<BR>2 A hundred thousand.<BR>E.<BR>नि before यु to join, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियुद्ध|नियुद्धं
नियुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Close fight, personal struggle.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युद्ध fight, contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोक्तव्य
नियोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be appointed or authorized.<BR>E.<BR>नि, युज to join, affix तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग|नियोगः
नियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 An order or command.<BR>2 Authority, appointment.<BR>3 Occupation, appointed duty.<BR>4 Effort, exertion.<BR>5 Ascertainment, certainty.<BR>6 Incidence, occurrence.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगप्रयोजन
नियोगप्रयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The object of any appointment, authorized act or duty.<BR>E.<BR>नियोग, and प्रयोजन cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगविधि
नियोगविधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The form of appointing to any act or duty.<BR>E.<BR>नियोग, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगार्थ
नियोगार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>The object of an authorized act or appointment.<BR>E.<BR>नियोग, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोगिन्
नियोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Engaged in any pursuit, closely attached to it or engrossed by it.<BR>2 Appointed, authorized, entrusted with authority, &c.<BR>m. (गी)<BR>A minister, a deputy, an agent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नियोग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=470" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोग्य|नियोग्यः
नियोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Fit to be appointed or authorized, able or fit for a duty.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>A master.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजन|नियोजनं
नियोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Ordering, commanding, directing.<BR>2 Uniting, attaching to.<BR>3 Urging, impelling.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजित
नियोजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Entrusted with, appointed to.<BR>2 Directed, ordered.<BR>3 Impelled, urged to, instigated.<BR>4 Joined or attached to.<BR>5 Suited or adapted to, connected with, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, क्त affix, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोजनीय
नियोजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be attached or joined to.<BR>E.<BR>नि, युज to join, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोज्य|नियोज्यः
नियोज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>1 To be attached to.<BR>2 To be appointed to or employed in.<BR>3 To be commanded, instigated, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>नि before युज to join, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नियोद्धृ
नियोद्धृ<BR>m. (-द्धा)<BR>1 A cock.<BR>2 A combatant, a wrestler, a boxer.<BR>E.<BR>नि near, युद्ध to fight, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्
निर्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle and prefix implying certainty, assurance.<BR>2 Negation, privation.<BR>3 Outside, out, without, forth.<BR>E.<BR>नृ to guide, affix क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्ष|निरक्षः
निरक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Having no dice, &c.<BR>2 Having no latitude.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>(In Astronomy,) The terrestrial equator.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अक्ष a die, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरक्षदेश|निरक्षदेशः
निरक्षदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A first meridian, as Laṅkā, a place where the sun is always vertical, and the days and nights are equal.<BR>2 The equatorial region.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, अक्ष latitude, देश a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्कुश|निरंकुश|निरङ्कुशः
निरङ्कुश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Unchecked, uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, अङ्कुश a hook for guiding an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरङ्कुशत्व
निरङ्कुशत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Self-will, wilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the foregoing; also with तल्, निरङ्कशता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरग्नि
निरग्नि<BR>mfn. (-ग्निः-ग्निः-ग्नि)<BR>Having lost or neglected the consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरञ्जन|निरंजन|निरञ्जनः
निरञ्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Void of passion or emotion.<BR>2 Unstained, unblackened.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The Supreme Being.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The day of fullmoon.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. रञ्जन affection; or निर् not, अञ्जन collyrium; figuratively, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत|निरतं
निरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Engaged or interested in.<BR>2 Attached or devoted to.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and रत occupied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरत्यय
निरत्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Faultless, unblamable.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अत्यय fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोश|निरनुक्रोशः
निरनुक्रोश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Hard-hearted, destitute of compassion.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अनुक्रोश pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुक्रोशता
निरनुक्रोशता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Cruelty, hard-heartedness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरनुरोध
निरनुरोध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Unkind, unfavourable.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अनुरोध favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तर|निरंतर|निरन्तरं
निरन्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Coarse, gross, without interstices.<BR>2 Continuous.<BR>3 Uninterrupted, continual.<BR>4 Unbounded.<BR>5 Identical, not different.<BR>6 Unconcealed, not hidden or vanished.<BR>9 Not external, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, अन्तर interval, difference, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तराल|निरंतराल
निरन्तराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Narrow, contracted.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अन्तराल intermediate space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्तराभ्यास|निरंतराभ्यास|निरन्तराभ्यासः
निरन्तराभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Private study, reading to one's self the sacred works.<BR>2 Diligent and uninterrupted pursuit, exercise, practice.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, अन्तर between, अभ्यास practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरन्वय
निरन्वय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Childless, having no family.<BR>2 Unconnected with, not belonging or related to.<BR>3 Done in one's absence, not done openly or visibly.<BR>4 Unmethodical, ill arranged.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अन्वय descent, connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरप
निरप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Destitute of water.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपत्रप|निरपत्रपः
निरपत्रप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Shameless, impudent.<BR>2 Bold, confident.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, अपत्रप shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपराध|निरपराधः
निरपराध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Faultless, blameless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अपराध fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपवर्त्त|निरपवर्त
निरपवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Non-returning or turning back.<BR>2 (In Arithmetic,) Leaving no common measure.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अपवर्त्त returning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपाय
निरपाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Free from destruction or decay, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरपेक्ष|निरपेक्षः
निरपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Independant of, unconnected or unconcerned with.<BR>2 Careless, indifferent, negligent.<BR>3 Without purpose or hope.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अपेक्षा regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरब्भ्र
निरब्भ्र<BR>mfn. (-ब्भ्रः-ब्भ्रा-ब्भ्रं)<BR>Cloudless.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अब्भ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरय|निरयः
निरय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Hell.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, beyond, अय good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्गल|निरर्गलः
निरर्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unobstructed, unrestrained, unimpeded.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, अर्गल a bolt or bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरर्थक|निरर्थकं
निरर्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Vain, fruitless, unprofitable.<BR>2 Unmeaning.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, अर्थं object, end, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरव|निरवः
निरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Loss of voice.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. and रव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवग्रह|निरवग्रहः
निरवग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Self-willed, headstrong, independant, uncontrolled.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अवग्रह control.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवद्य
निरवद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Unobjectionable, unexceptionable.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अवद्य not to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवशेषतस्
निरवशेषतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Fully, particularly, circumstantially.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अवशेषतस् a remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवसाद
निरवसाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Animated, anxious, eager.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अवसाद languor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरवहालिका
निरवहालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fence, a hedge, an outer wall.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, without, and अवहालिका a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरव्यय
निरव्यय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Undecaying, eternal.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अव्यय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरशन|निरशनं
निरशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fasting, going without food.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस|निरसः
निरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Dry.<BR>2 Insipid, tasteless.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Insipidity, want of flavour or passion.<BR>2 Dryness, want of juice.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. रस juice, &c. also निरस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरसन|निरसनं
निरसन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>What removes, expels, subdues, checks, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rejection, denial, contradiction, disallowance.<BR>2 Suppressing, checking.<BR>3 Appeasing.<BR>4 Expelling, ejecting.<BR>5 Spitting, spitting out any thing with sickness or disgust.<BR>6 Killing, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out or forth, अस to throw, affix ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्त|निरस्तः
निरस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Expelled, sent forth or out.<BR>2 Sent, thrown, cast, directed.<BR>3 Thrown off, (as from a horse.)<BR>4 Abandoned, deserted, left.<BR>5 Rejected, disallowed.<BR>6 Shot, (as an arrow.)<BR>7 Uttered rapidly, hurried.<BR>8 Destroyed. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">Page472</a>]<BR>9 Gone, absent, what is not.<BR>10 Suppressed, checked.<BR>11 Torn or taken.<BR>12 Broken, (as an agreement.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् out or forth, अस to throw or send, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=471" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्य
निरस्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having ejected or thrown out.<BR>2 Having expelled, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अस to throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यत्
निरस्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>1 Ejecting, thrown out.<BR>2 Abandoning, neglecting.<BR>3 Expelling.<BR>4 Scattering.<BR>5 Destroying, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, अस to throw, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरस्यमान
निरस्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being suppressed or checked.<BR>2 Being abandoned.<BR>3 Suppressing.<BR>4 Expelling.<BR>5 Scattering, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before अस to throw, either a. or p. voice, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरहङ्कार|निरहंकार
निरहङ्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Humble, free from pride.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. अहङ्कार pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरण|निराकरणं
निराकरण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>1 Obstruction, opposition, contradiction, rejection.<BR>2 Refutation, reply.<BR>3 Holding in no consideration, making light of, contempt, disesteem.<BR>4 Expelling, turning out or away.<BR>5 Throwing out or off.<BR>6 Neglecting the chief sacrificial or religious duties.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative particle, and आङ् before कृ to do or make, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकरिष्णु|निराकरिष्णुः
निराकरिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Obstructive, obstructing.<BR>2 Disdaining, despising.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आङ् before कृ, affix इष्णुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकार|निराकारः
निराकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Devoid of form or figure.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Heaven.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 The divine spirit, God.<BR>5 Reproach, censure.<BR>E.<BR>निर् implying negative or depreciation, and आकार shape, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकुल
निराकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Calm, steady, unperplexed, unconfused.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृत|निराकृतः
निराकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Removed, rejected, set aside.<BR>2 Refuted, replied to.<BR>3 Made light of, contemned, despised.<BR>4 Expelled, turned out.<BR>5 Thrown from or off.<BR>2 Divorced.<BR>E.<BR>निरा, and कृत done, with आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराकृति|निराकृतिः
निराकृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 A person who has not duly gone through a course of study, especially applied however to the religious student, who has not duly read the Vedas.<BR>2 One who neglects the five great religious obligations.<BR>3 Shapeless, formless, viewless.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Rejection, contradiction, opposition, disallowance.<BR>2 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>E.<BR>निरा implying privation or obstruction, कृति making, causing; or निर् privative, and आकृति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराक्रोश
निराक्रोश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Unaccused, unreviled.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आक्रोश exclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरागस्
निरागस्<BR>mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः)<BR>Sinless, faultless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आगस् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराचार|निराचारः
निराचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Lawless, corrupt, barbarian, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, आचार moral ordinance: it is especially applied to those people who have not the ordinances of the Vedas or distinction of Castes, &c. and comprises all, therefore, except Hindūs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरातपा
निरातपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, none, and आतप sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादिष्ट
निरादिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Given, paid, delivered.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and अदिष्ट shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरादेश|निरादेशः
निरादेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Payment, discharge, delivery.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आङ्दिश to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरानन्द
निरानन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Causing no pleasure, undelighting.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरापद्
निरापद्<BR>mfn. (-द् or -त्)<BR>Prosperous, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आपद misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराबाध|निराबाधः
निराबाध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Frivolously or unreally vexatious, (as a cause of complaint.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, आङ् before बाधा pain, annoyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामय|निरामयः
निरामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Well, hale, recovered from sickness.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A wild goat.<BR>2 A hog, a boar.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामालु|निरामालुः
निरामालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>The wood apple: see कपित्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरामिषाशिन्
निरामिषाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 Living without meat.<BR>2 Free from sensual desires.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, आमिष flesh, अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराय|निरायः
निराय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Having no income or profit, yielding none, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आय receipt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायत
निरायत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Contracted, compact.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आयत spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायव्ययवत्
निरायव्ययवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>An idler who lives by clandestine means, has neither income nor expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, आय income, व्यय expense, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायास
निरायास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Not giving trouble, ready, easily attainable.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आयास exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरायुध
निरायुध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Unarmed, defenceless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरालम्ब|निरालंब
निरालम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>Self-supported, not relying on another.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, आलम्ब stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश|निराशः
निराश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Hopeless, despairing.<BR>2 Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आश hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराशिस्
निराशिस्<BR>mfn. (-शिः-शिः-शिः)<BR>Without a blessing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आशिम् blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराश्रय
निराश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Without refuge, destitude.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास|निरासः
निरास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Opposing, rejecting.<BR>2 Dispension.<BR>3 Ejecting, expelling.<BR>4 Removal.<BR>5 Abandonment.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, and आस throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरासन|निरासनं
निरासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rejection, contradiction.<BR>2 Killing, destroying.<BR>3 Spitting out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before अस् to be, &c. with आङ् prefixed, and ल्युट् affix; also निरासन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निराहार|निराहारः
निराहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Fasting through necessity or choice.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरास्पद
निरास्पद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Restless, anxious, unappeasable.<BR>2 Homeless, portionless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. आस्पद station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिङ्गिनी|निरिंगिनी
निरिङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A veil.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative, अङ्ग a hint, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरिन्द्रिय|निरिंद्रिय|निरिन्द्रियः
निरिन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Imperfect, mutilated, maimed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षण|निरीक्षणं
निरीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Looking at, regarding, seeing.<BR>2 Expecting.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षत्
निरीक्षत्<BR>mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्)<BR>1 Looking at, regarding.<BR>2 Expecting, hoping.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and ईक्षत् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षमाण
निरीक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Looking at, regarding.<BR>2 Hoping, expecting.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before ईक्ष to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षा
निरीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Looking at, regarding.<BR>2 Hope, expectation.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्ष्यमाण
निरीक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being regarded or looked at.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and ईक्ष to see, pass, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=472" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीक्षित|निरीक्षितं
निरीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, beheld, looked at.<BR>2 Hoped, expected.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and ईक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीश|निरीशं
निरीश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>The body of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>ईश or ईष the shaft of the plough, and निर् forth or from, prefixed; hence also निरीष n. (-षं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीह|निरीहः
निरीह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Indifferent, unanxious.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. ईह who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरीहता
निरीहता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Indifference, absence of effort or wish to get any thing.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, निरीहत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्त|निरुक्तं
निरुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Said, described.<BR>2 Obscure, obsolete.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 One of the Vedāṅgas or works considered as supplementary to and connected with the Vedas, forming part of scriptural or sacred science: glossarial explanation of obscure terms, especially those occurring in the Vedas.<BR>2 Explanation of the concord or disagreement of letters, &c.<BR>3 Separation or analysis of a derivative or compound word.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative or affirmative prefix, उक्त spoken, said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुक्ति|निरुक्तिः
निरुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 The Vedāṅga or portion of scriptural science, which explains obscure and obsolete terms.<BR>2 Explanation of words: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्यमान
निरुच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being uttered or said.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उच्यमान being spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुच्छास
निरुच्छास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Breathless.<BR>2 Narrow, contracted, crowded.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उच्छास breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्तर
निरुत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Non-plussed, without an answer.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उत्तर an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्साह|निरुत्साहः
निरुत्साह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Indolent, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुत्सुक
निरुत्सुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unanxious, unregretting.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. उत्सुक sorrowing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्ध|निरुद्धः
निरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Stopped, checked, restrained, hindered.<BR>2 Confined, imprisoned.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and रुद्ध hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्धप्रकश|निरुद्धप्रकशः
निरुद्धप्रकश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Stricture of the urethra.<BR>E.<BR>निरुद्ध, and प्रकश what pains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्धशमवृत्ति
निरुद्धशमवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Wearied, tired.<BR>E.<BR>निरुद्ध, and शमवृत्ति repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्द्राव
निरुद्द्राव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Immoveable, undecaying.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उद्द्राव going away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्विग्न
निरुद्विग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Sedate, free from perturbation.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उद्विग्न perturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुद्योग|निरुद्योगः
निरुद्योग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गी-गं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative, उद्योग cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धत्
निरुन्धत्<BR>mfn. (-न्धन्-न्धती-न्धत्)<BR>Hindering, checking, suppressing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रुध to hinder, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुन्धान
निरुन्धान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Hindering, opposing.<BR>2 Preventing, depriving of.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रुध to hinder, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपद्रव|निरुपद्रवः
निरुपद्रव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Free from any national distress or affliction, free from tyranny.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उपद्रव violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपप्लव
निरुपप्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Free from trouble or alarm.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उपप्लव calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपम|निरुपमः
निरुपम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Unequalled, having no resemblance or likeness.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उपमा similitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरुपेक्ष|निरुपेक्षः
निरुपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Honest, free from trick or fraud.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and उपेक्षा trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूढ|निरूढः
निरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Conventional, accepted, (as the meaning of technical words or names in opposition to their etymological sense alone.)<BR>2 Unmarried.<BR>3 Inherent.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>1 The force or application of words, according to their natural or received meanings, (in Rhetoric.)<BR>2 (In Logic,) The implied description of any property in the term designing it, (as of redness in the word red, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>नि affix, and रूढ ascended; or निर् neg. ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपण|निरूपणं
निरूपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 Doubt, discussion, investigation.<BR>3 Ascertaining, determining.<BR>4 Searching, looking for.<BR>E.<BR>नि implying certainty, रूप to have form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपणीय
निरूपणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be discussed, to be investigated.<BR>2 To be sought or looked for.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रूप to have form, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपयत्
निरूपयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यन्)<BR>1 Searching, looking for.<BR>2 Investigating, considering.<BR>E.<BR>नि, रूप to have form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूपित|निरूपितः
निरूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, beheld.<BR>2 Ascertained.<BR>3 Discovered, found.<BR>4 Appointed, deputed, directed to do any thing.<BR>5 Considered, weighed.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रूप to have form, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्य
निरूप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be seen or ascertained.<BR>ind.<BR>Having seen or considered.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रूप to have form, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूप्यत्व
निरूप्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Ascertaining, determining.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, निरूप्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूह|निरूहः
निरूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A complete sentence, one having no ellipsis.<BR>2 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>3 Logick, disputation.<BR>4 An enema, one not of an oily kind.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, and ऊह reasoning, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरूहण|निरूहणं
निरूहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Ascertaining.<BR>2 Administering enemata not of an oily kind.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before ऊह to reason, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरेभ
निरेभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Silent, noiseless.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. रेभ sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरोध|निरोधः
निरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Loss, destruction.<BR>2 Opposition, hindrance, check, restraint, prevention.<BR>3 Aversion, disfavour, dislike.<BR>4 Preserving.<BR>5 Confinement.<BR>E.<BR>नि before रुध to oppose, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृति|निरृतिः
निरृति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Free from violence, tyranny, &c.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A demigod and ruler of the south-west quarter: see नैरृति.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>2 Security, prosperity, immunity from tyranny or violence.<BR>E.<BR>निर् implying reverse, ऋति good fortune, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निरृथ|निरृथः
निरृथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, ऋ to go, Uṇādi affix थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग|निर्गः
निर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Country, region, place or province.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, गम to go, affix ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गत|निर्गतः
निर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone out or forth.<BR>2 Expended, extinct, departed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्ध|निर्गंध|निर्गन्धं
निर्गन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Inodorous, void of fragrance or smell.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्धन|निर्गंधन|निर्गंधनं|निर्गन्धनं
निर्गन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative particle, गन्ध to hurt, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गन्धपुष्पी
निर्गन्धपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>The Simel or silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>निर्गन्ध, पुष्प a flower, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=473" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गम|निर्गमः
निर्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Going forth or out, exit.<BR>2 Total loss or departure.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, and गम going; also निर्गमन and निर्गति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण|निर्गुणः
निर्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Void of all properties.<BR>2 Bad, worthless, having no good qualities.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The Supreme Being, or any deity so considered.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, and गुण a property, an excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुणत्व
निर्गुणत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The state of being free from all qualities, an attribute especially of the Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>निर्गुण, and त्व affix; also with तल्, निर्गुणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गुण्ठी
निर्गुण्ठी<BR>f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>1 A shrub, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>2 Another plant, (नीलशेफालिका.)<BR>3 The root of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth or out, गुठि^1 or गुडि to surround, क affix fem. affix ङीष्; hence also निर्गुण्डी f. (-ण्डा.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: refer to root guWa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्गूढ|निर्गूढः
निर्गूढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>The hollow of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>निर् in, गुह to hide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थ|निर्ग्रंथ|निर्ग्रन्थः
निर्ग्रन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 A saint, a devotee, one who has withdrawn from the world, and lives either as a beggar or a hermit.<BR>2 A religious character wandering about naked.<BR>3 A pauper, a beggar.<BR>4 An ideot, a fool.<BR>5 A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, ग्रन्थ a knot or tie, or figuratively, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थक|निर्ग्रन्थकः
निर्ग्रन्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Unattended, unaccompanied.<BR>2 Abandoned, deserted.<BR>3 Clever, expert, conversant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A religious mendicant.<BR>2 A naked devotee.<BR>3 A gambler.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, ग्रन्थ tie or connexion, affix कन्; also read निर्ग्रन्थिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ग्रन्थन|निर्ग्रंथनं|निर्ग्रन्थनं
निर्ग्रन्थन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, before ग्रन्थ to hurt or kill, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घट|निर्घटं
निर्घट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 A great collection of people, a fair, a market, &c.<BR>2 A free market or wharf, one where no toll is levied.<BR>3 A place where is no quay or stairs.<BR>E.<BR>निर् prefixed to घट to endeavour, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घण्ट|निर्घंट|निर्घंटं|निर्घंटः|निर्घण्टः
निर्घण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A vocabulary, an index.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before घटि to endeavour, aff. अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षण|निर्घर्षणं
निर्घर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rubbing, friction.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before घृष to rub, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घर्षणक
निर्घर्षणक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Rubbing, a rubber.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घात|निर्घातः
निर्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A gust of wind, a hurricane, a whirlwind.<BR>2 The noise of contending vapours in the heavens.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, हन to drive, affix घञ्, घात substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घूरिणी
निर्घूरिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घृण
निर्घृण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Cruel, unmerciful.<BR>2 Shameless, immodest.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. घृणा mercy, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्घोष|निर्घोषः
निर्घोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before घुष to sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ज्जन|निर्जन|निर्ज्जनः
निर्ज्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lonely, unpeopled, unfrequented.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ज्जर|निर्जर|निर्जरं|निर्जरः|निर्ज्जरः
निर्ज्जर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Immortal, imperishable, undecaying.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A deity, an immortal.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Ambrosia, the food of the gods.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A plant: see गुडुची.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Mura.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, जरा decrepitude or decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जल|निर्जलः|निर्ज्जलः
निर्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Dry, desart, void of water.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A desart, a waste.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जित|निर्ज्जितः
निर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Conquered, subdued, overcome.<BR>2 Won, gained.<BR>3 Unconquered.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative or neg. prefix जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जितेन्द्रिय|निर्जितेन्द्रियः
निर्जितेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of subdued passions or feelings.<BR>E.<BR>निर्जित, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जितेन्द्रियग्राम|निर्ज्जितेन्द्रियग्रामः
निर्जितेन्द्रियग्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Muni, a saint.<BR>E.<BR>निर्जितेन्द्रिय, and ग्राम accumulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्जीव|निर्ज्जीवः
निर्जीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Lifeless.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and जीव alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झर|निर्झरं|निर्झरः
निर्झर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A cascade or torrent, the precipitous descent of water from mountains, &c.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A river.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A horse of the sun.<BR>2 A fire of chaff.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before झॄ to waste, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्झरिन्
निर्झरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A mountain.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>निर्झर a waterfall, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णय|निर्णयः
निर्णय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Certainty, positive conclusion.<BR>2 Doubt, discussion, investigation.<BR>3 (In Law,) Sentence, decision.<BR>4 (In the Mīmāṃsā,) The application of a conclusive argument.<BR>5 (In Logic,) Complete ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative prefix, णी to guide, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयन|निर्णयनं
निर्णयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment, positive conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>see निर्णय, with ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयपाद|निर्णयपादः
निर्णयपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sentence, a verdict, (in Law.)<BR>E.<BR>निर्णय, and पाद process.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णर|निर्णरः
निर्णर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One of the horses of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायक
निर्णायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Causing or leading to certainty.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before णी to guide, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायन|निर्णायनं|निर्ण्णायन
निर्णायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Causing certainty.<BR>2 The outer angle of the elephant's eye.<BR>E.<BR>विर्णय certainty, फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिक्त|निर्णिक्तं
निर्णिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before निज to clean, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णीत|निर्णीतं
निर्णीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ascertained, determined.<BR>2 Sentenced, decreed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before णी to get, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेक|निर्णेकः
निर्णेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cleansing, washing, cleaning.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before निज to wash, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजक|निर्णेजकः
निर्णेजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before निज to clean, affix ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृ
निर्णेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Certifying, verifying, leading to certainty, decisive.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A judge.<BR>2 A document, a voucher.<BR>3 A guide.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before णी to lead, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृत्व
निर्णेतृत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Proof, verification.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेय
निर्णेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be ascertained, what is or ought to be determined.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before णी to lead, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दग्ध|निर्दग्ध
निर्द्दग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Burnt, burnt up.<BR>2 Unburnt.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and दग्ध burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दट|निर्द्दटः
निर्दट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Unkind, unfeeling, unmerciful, devoid of pity or charity.<BR>2 Unnecessary.<BR>3 Envious, slanderous, abusive.<BR>4 Mad, intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दो to cut, to hurt, affix अटच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दय|निर्द्दयः
निर्दय<BR>mfn. (-पः-या-यं)<BR>Unkind, unmerciful, cruel, hard-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दया compassion, charity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दर|निर्दर|निर्दरः|निर्द्दरं
निर्द्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Harsh spoken.<BR>2 Shameless.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Much, excessively.<BR>subst. n. (-रं)<BR>Pith, essence.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, दृ to respect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दरि|निर्दरि|निर्दरिः
निर्द्दरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A cave.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दॄ to rend, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दरिवासिन्|निर्दरिवासिन्
निर्द्दरिवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Inhabiting a cave.<BR>E.<BR>निर्द्दरिन्, and वासिन् who abides in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=474" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दशत्|निर्दशत्
निर्द्दशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Biting, consuming.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and दशत् biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दशन
निर्दशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Toothless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. दशन a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहन|निर्द्दहनः
निर्दहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Not burning, not caustic.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marking nut.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affir. or neg. and दहन burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहनी|निर्द्दहनी
निर्दहनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of creeper, from the fibres of which bowstrings are made, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दातृ|निर्दातृ
निर्द्दातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A reaper, a husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दो to cut, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्दारित|निर्दारित
निर्द्दारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Torn, rent.<BR>2 Open, unclosed.<BR>3 Starting, starting, (the eyes.)<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and दारित torn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिग्ध|निर्द्दिग्धः
निर्दिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Stout, lusty.<BR>2 Anointed, smeared.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दिह to heap, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिश्य
निर्दिश्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having shown, explained, enjoined, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दिश to show, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिष्ट|निर्द्दिष्टः
निर्दिष्ट<BR>mfn. (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Described, depicted, pointed out, shown.<BR>2 Ascertained, determined.<BR>3 Ordered, directed.<BR>4 Assigned.<BR>5 Asserted, declared.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दिश to show, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देश|निर्देशः|निर्द्देशः
निर्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Order, command, authoritative instruction or direction.<BR>2 Description, designation.<BR>3 Depicting, pointing out or exhibiting.<BR>4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>5 Saying, telling.<BR>6 Vicinity, proximity.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दिश to show, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देष्टृ
निर्देष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what shows or explains.<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>An authority, a guide.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before दिश to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दोष|निर्द्दोषः
निर्दोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Faultless, without defect or blemish.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative, and दोष defect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्द्वन्द्व|निर्द्वंद्व
निर्द्वन्द्व<BR>mfn. (-न्द्वः-न्द्वा-न्द्वं)<BR>1 Not double.<BR>2 Free from either of two alternatives, neither glad nor sorry, &c.<BR>3 Not acknowledging two principles.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. द्वन्द्व a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धन|निर्धनः
निर्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An old ox.<BR>E.<BR>निर् priv. and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धर्म्म|निर्धर्म|निर्धर्म्मः
निर्धर्म्म<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मा-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Impious, unrighteous, immoral, void of law or religion.<BR>2 Not acknowledging moral or religious institutions, but especially those of the Hindūs.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, धर्म्म virtue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार|निर्धारः
निर्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>2 Particularising individuals according to their degree of merit.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before धृ to hold or have, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारण|निर्धारणं
निर्धारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before धृ to have, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारणीय
निर्धारणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be ascertained.<BR>2 Acting resolutely, irresistible.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affir. or neg. धृ to hold, अनीयर् affix; also निर्धारितव्य, and निर्धार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारित|निर्धारितं
निर्धारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ascertained, determined.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative, धृ to have, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार्य्य|निर्धार्य|निर्धार्य्यं
निर्धार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Acting fearlessly.<BR>2 Active, energetic^1.<BR>3 Ascertainable, to be ascertained or determined.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. or affir. घृ to restrain, affix ण्यत्; it may also be written निर्द्धार्य्य.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धूत|निर्धूतं|निर्धूतः
निर्धूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deserted, rejected.<BR>2 Removed, departed.<BR>3 Broken, divided.<BR>4 Refuted.<BR>5 Thrown out.<BR>6 Suffered, undergone.<BR>7 Destroyed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A man abandoned by his relatives or friends.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before धु to shake, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धौत|निर्धौतं
निर्धौत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Washed.<BR>2 Bright, polished.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and धौत cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नमस्कार
निर्नमस्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Uncourteous.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. नकस्कार salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाथ
निर्नाथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Having no superior, master, protector, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. नाथ a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्नाथता
निर्नाथता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Being without a master.<BR>2 Widowhood.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. नाथता masterhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्निमित्त
निर्निमित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. निमित्त cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बन्ध|निर्बन्ध|निर्बंध|निर्बंधः|निर्बन्धः
निर्ब्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Intent, and pertinacious pursuit of any thing, urgency, importunity.<BR>2 Seizure, laying hold of any thing, literally or figuratively.<BR>3 Caprice, fancy, whim.<BR>E.<BR>रिर् before बन्ध to bind or tie, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बर्हण|निर्बर्हण|निर्ब्बर्हणं
निर्ब्बर्हण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वर्ह to slay, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बल|निर्बल
निर्ब्बल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Weak, feeble, powerless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बुद्धि|निर्ब्बुद्धि
निर्बुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Ignorant, unwise.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. and बुद्धि understanding; also निर्बोध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ब्बैर
निर्ब्बैर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Free from hatred or enmity.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वैर hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भग्न
निर्भग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Broken down.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and भग्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भट|निर्भटः
निर्भट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Hard, firm, compact.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before भट to maintain, affix अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भय|निर्भयः
निर्भय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर|निर्भरं|निर्भरः
निर्भर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>2 Fearless.<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Much, excessively.<BR>subst.<BR>Pith, essence.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before भृ to fill, affix अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सन|निर्भर्त्सनं
निर्भर्त्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wickedness, malignity.<BR>2 Abuse, blame.<BR>3 Lac.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before भर्त्स to abuse, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सित|निर्भर्त्सितं
निर्भर्त्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abused, reviled, despised.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before भर्त्स to abuse, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भाग्य|निर्भाग्यः
निर्भाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Unlucky.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. भाग्य luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिद्य
निर्भिद्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having pierced or penetrated.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before भिद to break, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिन्न
निर्भिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Undistinguished, equal, like.<BR>2 Pierced, divided.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, भिन्न separated or pierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुन्न
निर्भुन्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Straight, flat, not bent.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and भुग्न curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मथ्य|निर्मथ्य
निर्म्मथ्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having discriminated or particularised.<BR>2 Having ground or churned.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मथि to churn, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मद|निर्मद|निर्म्मदः
निर्म्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Sober, quiet, unintoxicated.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An elephant after the frontal juice has ceased to exude, one out of rut.<BR>E.<BR>निर् priv. and मद madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मनुष्य|निर्मनुष्य
निर्म्मनुष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Uninhabited, desolate.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, मनुष्य a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मन्थन|निर्मन्थन|निर्मंथन|निर्मंथनं
निर्म्मन्थन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Separating, distinguishing, discriminating.<BR>2 Churning.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मन्थ to churn, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मन्थ्य|निर्मन्थ्य|निर्मंथ्य
निर्म्मन्थ्य<BR>mfn. (-न्थ्यः-न्थ्या-न्थ्यं)<BR>1 To be rubbed, to be churned, &c.<BR>2 To be distinguished or discriminated.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affir. मन्थ्य to be rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मम|निर्मम
निर्म्मम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Disinterested, claiming or wishing for nothing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and मम mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=475" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्ममत्व|निर्ममत्व
निर्म्ममत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Disregard of worldly interests or possessions.<BR>E.<BR>निर्म्मम, and त्व affix; also निर्म्ममता, with तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मल|निर्मल|निर्म्मलं
निर्म्मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Clear, clean, free from dirt or impurities, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The remains of an offering made to a deity.<BR>2 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>निर् priv. and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मलत्व|निर्मलत्व
निर्म्मलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Purity, cleanness, (physical or moral.)<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, निर्म्मलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्माण|निर्माण|निर्माणं|निर्म्माणं
निर्म्माण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Manufacture, production, making.<BR>2 Pith, marrow, essence.<BR>3 Propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मा to measure, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्माल्य|निर्माल्य|निर्म्माल्यं
निर्म्माल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Clear, clean.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 The remains of an offering presented to a deity.<BR>2 Purity, cleanness, clearness.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A medicinal plant: see पृक्का.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, मल dirt, impurity, affix यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मित|निर्मित|निर्म्मितं
निर्म्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made.<BR>2 Fabricated, artificial.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मा to mete, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मिति|निर्मिति|निर्मितिः|निर्म्मितिः
निर्म्मिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Making, manufacturing, artificial production.<BR>E.<BR>as above: see निर्म्मित, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मुक्त|निर्मुक्त|निर्मुक्तः
निर्म्मुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Loosed, set free, liberated, disjoined, sundered, separated, &c.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A snake who has lately cast his skin.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मुक्त loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मुट|निर्मुट|निर्मुटं|निर्मुटः
निर्म्मुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A tree bearing apparent blossoms.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A rogue.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A large, and free market or fair.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before मुट to press, &c. affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मूल|निर्मूल
निर्म्मूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Baseless, unfounded.<BR>2 Eradicated.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृष्ट
निर्मृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Rubbed out.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and मृष्ट rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्म्मोक|निर्मोक|निर्मोकः|निर्म्मोकः
निर्म्मोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The slough of a snake.<BR>2 Liberating, setting loose or free.<BR>3 Armour, mail.<BR>4 Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, मुच to let loose, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्
निर्यत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Going forth or out, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and यत् going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यन्त्रण|निर्यन्त्रण|निर्यंत्रण|निर्यन्त्रणं
निर्य्यन्त्रण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Self-willed, unrestrained, uncontrolled, independant.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Independence, absence of restraint.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, यन्त्रण restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यन्त्रित|निर्यन्त्रित
निर्य्यन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Self-willed, uncontrolled, unrestrained.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. यन्त्रित restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याण|निर्याणं|निर्य्याण
निर्याण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going forth or out, exit, issue.<BR>2 Eternal emancipation, final beatitude.<BR>3 A rope for tying cattle, a foot-rope.<BR>4 The outer corner of an elephant's eye.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before यम to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यात|निर्यात
निर्य्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone out or forth, departed.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and यात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातन|निर्यातनं|निर्य्यातन
निर्यातन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Revenge.<BR>2 Gift, donation.<BR>3 Delivery of a deposit.<BR>4 Replacing any thing lost.<BR>5 Payment of a debt.<BR>6 Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before यत to endeavour, in the causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यातित|निर्यातित
निर्य्यातित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken away.<BR>2 Retaliated, requited.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, यत to endeavour, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याम|निर्यामः|निर्य्याम
निर्याम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sailor, a boatman.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before यम to refrain, affix घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्याय|निर्याय
निर्य्याय<BR>ind.<BR>Having gone out or departed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, याय having gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यास|निर्यासं|निर्यासः|निर्य्यास
निर्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Extract, decoction, infusion.<BR>2 Any natural exudation of a plant, as gum, milk, extract, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth or out, यस to endeavour, affix घञ्; it is also read निर्य्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्युक्ति|निर्युक्ति
निर्य्युक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Disunion.<BR>2 Unfitness, inappropriateness, impropriety.<BR>3 Want of connexion or government, (in Grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. युक्ति union, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्युक्तिक|निर्युक्तिक|निर्युक्तिकं
निर्य्युक्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Detached, disunited.<BR>2 Unconnected, unmeaning.<BR>3 Inappropriate, improper.<BR>E.<BR>ठक् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्यूह|निर्यूह|निर्यूहः
निर्य्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A chaplet, a crest, an ornament for the head.<BR>2 Extracted juice, or a decoction, &c.<BR>3 A door, a gate.<BR>4 A pin or bracket projecting from a wall to hang or place any thing upon.<BR>5 Wood placed in a wall for doves to build upon.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, out from, युह to go, affix क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्य्योगक्षेम|निर्योगक्षेम
निर्य्योगक्षेम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Free from care or anxiety about property.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. योगक्षेम property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लक्षण|निर्लक्षणः
निर्लक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Unmarked, unnoted, unspotted, &c.<BR>2 Undefined.<BR>E.<BR>निर् priv. and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लज्ज
निर्लज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Impudent, shameless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. लज्जा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लिप्त|निर्लिप्तः
निर्लिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Unsmeared, unanointed.<BR>2 Undefiled, uncontaminated, (by passion, &c.)<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A sage.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. लिप्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेप|निर्लेपः
निर्लेप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Anointed or smeared.<BR>2 Undefiled, (by passion.)<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A sage.<BR>E.<BR>निर् on, लेष plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वचन|निर्वचन|निर्वचनं
निर्व्वचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Silent.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Explanation, declaration.<BR>2 Vocabulary, index.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affir. or neg. वचन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वन|निर्वन
निर्व्वन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bare, open, (a country.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वपण|निर्वपण|निर्व्वपणं
निर्व्वपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Presentation of funeral offerings.<BR>3 Extinguishing, pulling out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वप to go, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वयनी|निर्वयनी
निर्व्वयनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The cast slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वर्णण|निर्वर्णण
निर्व्वर्णण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sight, seeing, looking at, regarding.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वर्ण to class or colour, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्त्तन|निर्वर्तन|निर्वर्तनं|निर्व्वर्त्तन
निर्वर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Leaving off, desisting from.<BR>2 Completing, ending.<BR>3 Limiting to, measuring by.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वर्त्य|निर्वर्त्य
निर्व्वर्त्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having finished, having done.<BR>2 Having ceased.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वृत to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वहण|निर्वहण|निर्वहणं|निर्व्वहणं
निर्व्वहण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 End, completion.<BR>2 Supporting, carrying on, maintaining.<BR>3 The catastrophe of a drama, the conclusion of the fable.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, वह to bear, affix युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाच्य|निर्वाच्य
निर्व्वाच्य<BR>m. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 Unobjectionable, blameless, not to be found fault with or censured.<BR>2 Improper to be said.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वाच्य to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाण|निर्वाण|निर्व्वाणं|निर्व्वाणः
निर्व्वाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Liberated from existence.<BR>2 Dead, deceased.<BR>3 Gone out, extinguished, (as a fire.)<BR>4 Set, as a planet.<BR>5 Immersed, plunged.<BR>6 Having no arrows.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Eternal happiness, emancipation from matter, and re-union with the deity: it is especially employed in this sense by the Bauddhas and Jains, understanding by it perfect and perpetual calm.<BR>2 Setting, disappearing, departure.<BR>3 Refraining, desisting, leaving off, cessation.<BR>4 Union, association, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">Page477</a>] blending, confluence.<BR>5 Bathing or plunging of an elephant.<BR>6 Repose.<BR>7 Vacuity, vacuum or space.<BR>8 Instructing in science.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वाण to blow, &c. affix क्त, deriv. irr. or निर् neg. वाण an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=476" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाणमस्तक|निर्वाणमस्तक|निर्वाणमस्तकः
निर्व्वाणमस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Liberation.<BR>E.<BR>निर्व्वाण, and मस्तक head, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वात|निर्वात|निर्वातः|निर्व्वातः
निर्व्वात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Calm, still, not windy, having ceased to blow.<BR>2 Sheltered from the wind.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A calm.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वात wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाद|निर्वाद|निर्वादः|निर्व्वादः
निर्व्वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Censure, blame, reproach.<BR>2 Rumour, report.<BR>3 Asseveration, affirmation, decision of a controversy.<BR>4 Absence of dispute or railing.<BR>5 Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privat, prefix, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाप|निर्वाप|निर्वापः|निर्व्वापः
निर्व्वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Putting out, as a fire or light.<BR>2 Gifts in honour of a deceased ancestor: see निवाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वापन|निर्वापन
निर्व्वापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Putting out, as a fire or light, extinguishing, quenching.<BR>2 (In medicine,) Refrigerant.<BR>3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>4 Gift, giving.<BR>5 Presenting funeral oblations.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before बप to go, &c. in the causal form, affix ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वापित|निर्वापित
निर्व्वापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Put out, quenched, extinguished.<BR>2 Allayed, cooled.<BR>3 Killed.<BR>4 Offered in oblation.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, वप to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाप्य|निर्वाप्य
निर्व्वाप्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having offered funeral cakes.<BR>2 Having delighted.<BR>3 Having quenched.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वप to sow, affix ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वार्य्य|निर्वार्य|निर्वार्य्य|निर्व्वार्य्यः
निर्व्वार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-य्यं)<BR>1 Acting fearlessly or determinately.<BR>2 Irresistible, not to be opposed or resisted.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, वृ to hinder, affix ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वासन|निर्वासन|निर्वासनं|निर्व्वासनं
निर्व्वासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Hurting, injuring.<BR>3 Banishment, expulsion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, forth, वस to abide, causal form, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वासित|निर्वासित
निर्व्वासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expelled, banished.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, वस to abide, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वास्य|निर्वास्य
निर्व्वास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>To be banished.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, वस to abide, causal form, यत् aff.; also निर्व्वासनीय, निर्व्वासितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाह|निर्वाह|निर्वाहः|निर्व्वाहः
निर्व्वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Accomplishment, completion, end.<BR>2 Carrying on, supporting, maintaining.<BR>3 Providing means.<BR>4 Sufficiency, adequacy.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वह to bear, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाहक|निर्वाहक
निर्व्वाहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Application or connexion of cause and effect.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वह to convey, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वाहण|निर्वाहण|निर्व्वाहणं
निर्व्वाहण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Catastrophe of a drama: see निर्व्वहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्विकल्पक|निर्विकल्पक|निर्व्विकल्पकं
निर्व्विकल्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Knowledge, not depending upon or derived from the senses.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विकल्प alternative, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विकार|निर्विकारः|निर्व्विकार|निर्व्विकारः
निर्विकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unchanged, unaltered, uniform.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विकार change of form or state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विघ्न|निर्व्विघ्न
निर्विघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं)<BR>Unobstructed.<BR>n. subst. (-घ्नं)<BR>Absence of obstruction or impediment.<BR>adv.<BR>Freely, unobstructedly.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. निघ्न obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्णः
निर्विण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Desponding, overcome with fear or sorrow.<BR>2 Humble.<BR>3 Abused, degraded.<BR>4 Fallen away, emaciate with grief.<BR>5 Decayed, impaired.<BR>6 Certain.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, विद to know, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्णचेतस्|निर्व्विण्णचेतस्
निर्विण्णचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Humble, resigned, meek.<BR>E.<BR>निर्व्विण्ण, and चेतस mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विन्ध्या|निर्विंध्या|निर्व्विन्ध्या
निर्विन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>The name of a river that rises in the Vindhya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out of, विन्ध्या the Vindh hills, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवर|निर्व्विवर
निर्विवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Close, contiguous, without interval or interstice.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विवर a space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विवेक|निर्व्विवेक
निर्विवेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Foolish, undiscriminating.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विवेक judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशङ्क|निर्विशंक|निर्व्विशङ्क
निर्विशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted, confident.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विशङ्क fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्विशत्|निर्विशत्
निर्व्विशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>1 Entering in or into.<BR>2 Engaged in.<BR>3 Attaining, obtaining.<BR>4 Marrying.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before विश to enter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विशेष|निर्विशेषः|निर्व्विशेष
निर्विशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Undiscriminating, making no difference.<BR>2 Same, like, indiscriminate.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विषा|निर्व्विषा
निर्विषा<BR>f. (-षा or षी)<BR>A plant, (Curcuma zedoaria.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् opposite, (anti,) विष poison, antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्टः
निर्विष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Attained, arrived at.<BR>2 Obtained, got.<BR>3 Engaged in, occupied by.<BR>4 Staying, being.<BR>5 Married.<BR>6 Earned, gained.<BR>7 Taken, received.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before विश to enter, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्वीज|निर्वीज
निर्व्वीज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Seedless.<BR>2 Impotent.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर|निर्व्वीर|निर्व्वीरं
निर्वीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unheroick, cowardly.<BR>(-रा)<BR>A woman whose husband and children are dead, a childless widow.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, and वीर a hero, a champion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वीर्य्य|निर्वीर्य|निर्व्वीर्य्य
निर्वीर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Tame, feeble, spiritless.<BR>2 Impotent.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ended, terminated.<BR>2 Happy, content.<BR>3 Emancipated.<BR>4 Free from occupation or interest.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and वृ to choose, क्त affix: see निवृत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृति|निर्वृतिः
निर्वृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Final emancipation from existence.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 Happiness.<BR>4 Rest, repose, tranquillity, ceasing or abstaining from.<BR>5 Setting, departure, disappearance.<BR>6 Completion, accomplishment, conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative particle, वृ to choose, affix क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Finished, completely done, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before वृत to be, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ति|निर्वृत्तिः
निर्वृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Destitute, having no occupation.<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Completion, termination, conclusion.<BR>2 Satisfaction.<BR>3 Final beatitude.<BR>4 Approach, advance.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वृत to be, affix क्तिन्, or निर् and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेग
निर्वेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Calm, (as the ocean.)<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and वेग agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेद|निर्वेदः|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Not having the Vedas, infidel, unscriptural.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Humility, self-disparagement.<BR>2 Being neglected or disregarded by others.<BR>3 Indifference, disregard of worldly objects.<BR>E.<BR>निर् depreciative particle, विद to know, affix घञ्, or निर् neg. वेद the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेश|निर्वेशः|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 Enjoyment.<BR>3 Eating.<BR>4 Fainting, swooning, syncope.<BR>5 Attaining, obtaining.<BR>6 Engaged or entering in.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before विश to enter, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टन|निर्वेष्टनं|निर्व्वेष्टनं
निर्वेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A small reed used as a shuttle.<BR>E.<BR>निर् without, वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वैर
निर्वैर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Friendly, without enmity.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. वैर hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथन|निर्व्यथनं
निर्व्यथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm.<BR>2 Exemption from pain.<BR>3 Paining, afflicting.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affix or neg, prefix, and न्यथन fear, dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=477" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यपेक्ष
निर्व्यपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Indifferent to, disregarding.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. व्यपेक्षा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यलीक
निर्व्यलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Undissembling, true.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. व्यलीक false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्याज
निर्व्याज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Without deceit.<BR>2 Without obstruction.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. व्याज deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्व्यूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Abandoned, left, deserted.<BR>2 Finished, completed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before व्यूढ arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरण|निर्हरणं
निर्हरण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking forth or out.<BR>2 Removing entirely.<BR>2 Setting apart.<BR>4 Burning dead bodies, or carrying them out to be burnt.<BR>E.<BR>निर् away, हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हार|निर्हारः
निर्हार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Extracting, drawing out, rooting up, &c.<BR>2 Putting forth or out.<BR>3 Evacuation of any of the natural excrements of the fæces, urine, sweat, &c.<BR>4 Burning, combustion.<BR>5 Giving away, selling, exchanging, &c.<BR>6 Diffusive fragrance.<BR>7 Accumulation of wealth, a hoard, a private purse or hoard.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, हृ to take, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्हारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Taking forth or out.<BR>2 Diffusively fragrant, having a wide spreading odour.<BR>3 Having wealth.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, हृ to take, घिणुन् aff. or निर्हार, affix इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत
निर्हृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken or carried forth or out.<BR>2 Extracted.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृत्य
निर्हृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken forth or out.<BR>2 Having extracted.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हेति
निर्हेति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Unarmed.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्राद|निर्ह्रादः
निर्ह्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound in general.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before ह्रद to sound, affix घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलय|निलयः
निलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A house, a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, ली to embrace, affix घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयन|निलयनं
निलयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Place, dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ली to endeavour, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिता
निलायिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dwelling, domesticality.<BR>E.<BR>निलायिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलायिन्
निलायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ली to embrace, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्प|निलिंप|निलिंपः|निलिम्पः
निलिम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>A deity.<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or on, लिम्प to smear, affix खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिम्पिका|निलिंपिका
निलिम्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीन|निलीनं
निलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Encompassed, surrounded, shut or wrapt up, embraced.<BR>2 Destroyed, perished entirely.<BR>3 Transformed, changed.<BR>4 Fused in or into.<BR>5 Full.<BR>E.<BR>नि in or on, ली to embrace, affix क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवपन|निवपनं
निवपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gifts in honour of deceased ancestors; also निवाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवरा
निवरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A virgin, a girl unmarried.<BR>E.<BR>नि priv. and वर a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्तन|निवर्तन
निवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Returning, turning or coming back.<BR>2 Bringing back.<BR>3 Reforming, repenting.<BR>4 Desisting from.<BR>5 Giving back, returning.<BR>6 Stopping, ceasing.<BR>7 A measure of land 20 rods, or 200 cubits square.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्तयितव्य|निवर्तयितव्य
निवर्त्तयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be restrained, to be hindered or diverted.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वृत to be, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्त्त्य
निवर्त्त्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having desisted or refrained from.<BR>2 Having turned back.<BR>3 Having repented.<BR>4 Having repaid.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ष्टत to be, aff. ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हण
निवर्हण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Killing, destroying.<BR>2 Removing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वर्ह to cover, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्हित
निवर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Killed, destroyed.<BR>2 Removed, taken away.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वर्ह to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसत्
निवसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Dwelling in, inhabiting.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वस to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसति|निवसतिः
निवसति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A house, a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, वस to dwell, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसथ|निवसथः
निवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, वस to dwell, aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसन|निवसनं
निवसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A house, a habitation.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes, raiment.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, वस to dwell or wear, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह|निवहः
निवह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A multitude, a quantity.<BR>2 One of the seven winds.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, वह to gain, घ or अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well armed, accoutred in strong mail.<BR>2 Secure, safe, as in an asylum.<BR>3 Calm, not windy.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An asylum, a dwelling, &c.<BR>2 A calm.<BR>3 Strong armour.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. वात wind, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवातकवच|निवातकवचः
निवातकवच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A demon, the grandson of HIRAṆYAKAŚIPU.<BR>E.<BR>निवात, and कवच a cuirass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाप|निवापः
निवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Gifts in honour of a deceased parent or relative.<BR>2 Offering of water at Śrāddhas, or daily ablution to the manes.<BR>3 Gift, giving in general.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वप to go, to give, &c. aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार|निवारः
निवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Hindering, opposition, impediment.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefix, वॄ to screen, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारण|निवारणं
निवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Hindering, opposing.<BR>2 An impediment.<BR>3 Contemning, holding light or worthless.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefix, वॄ to screen, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारणीय
निवारणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be checked, hindered, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वॄ to screen, aff. अनीयर्; also निवारितव्य and निवार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारयत्
निवारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यत्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Opposing, hindering.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वॄ to screen, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारित|निवारितः
निवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hindered, checked, opposed.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefix, वॄ to screen, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवार्य्यमाण|निवार्यमाण
निवार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>To be opposed or hindered.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वॄ to screen, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवास|निवासः
निवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A house, a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>नि in, वस to abide, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासभूय
निवासभूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Habitation or inhabiting.<BR>E.<BR>निवास, and भूय being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
निवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Dwelling, abiding in, inhabiting.<BR>E.<BR>निवास, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविड|निविडं
निविड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>1 Coarse, large, gross, bulky, without spaces or interstices.<BR>2 Thick, impervious, impenetrable.<BR>3 Crooked-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>नि not, विल an interstice, ल changed to ड; or नि particle, with विलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडीष
निविडीष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Coarse, gross.<BR>2 Crooked-nosed.<BR>E.<BR>see the last; also मि particle, विडीसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविवृत्सत्
निविवृत्सत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्^1)<BR>Wishing to stop or return.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वृत to abide, desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेष|निविशेषः
निविशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Alike, not different.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. विशेष difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्ट|निविष्टं|निविष्टः
निविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Entered, gone in or into.<BR>2 Seated, sitting upon.<BR>3 Situated or placed in or on.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=478" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीत|निवीतं|निवीतः
निवीत<BR>mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A veil, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The Brahminical thread suspended round the neck, in which manner it is worn on some occasions.<BR>E.<BR>नि before व्ये to cover, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतिन्
निवीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A Brahman with the cord suspended round his neck.<BR>E.<BR>निवीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत|निवृतं|निवृतः
निवृत<BR>mfn. adj. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, enclosed, encompassed.<BR>subst.<BR>A veil, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वृ to surround, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृति|निवृतिः
निवृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Covering, enclosing.<BR>E.<BR>नि, वृ to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्त|निवृत्तः
निवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Ceased, stopped.<BR>2 Abstaining from worldly acts, &c.<BR>3 Abstracted from or independant of worldly motives.<BR>3 Desisting from or repenting of any improper conduct.<BR>4 Returned, turned back.<BR>5 Gone, departed.<BR>6 Finished, completed.<BR>E.<BR>नि prohibitory prefix, वृत to be, aff. क्त; see निर्वृत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तकारण|निवृत्तकारणः
निवृत्तकारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Without further cause or motive.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A virtuous man, one uninfluenced by worldly desires.<BR>E.<BR>निवृत्त ceased, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तराग
निवृत्तराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Of subdued appetites or passions.<BR>E.<BR>निवृत्त stopped, राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तवृत्ति
निवृत्तवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>Quitting any practice or occupation.<BR>E.<BR>निवृत्त, and वृत्ति maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तात्मन्
निवृत्तात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 A sage.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>निवृत्त stopped, (from worldly acts, &c.) आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्ति|निवृत्तिः
निवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Cessation, completion, leaving off, rest, repose.<BR>2 Discontinuance of worldly acts, cessation of emotions, separation from the world.<BR>3 Denial, refusal.<BR>4 Abolition, prevention.<BR>5 Returning.<BR>E.<BR>नि negative prefix, वृत to be, aff. क्तिन्: see निर्वृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदन|निवेदनं|निवेदनः
निवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Delivering, giving, entrusting, addressing, (either an article, a message, or a speech.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before विद to know, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदित|निवेदितं
निवेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Given, entrusted, addressed, delivered.<BR>2 Represented, stated, told.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विद to know, aff. क्तः see निवेदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेश|निवेशः
निवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Entrance, entering.<BR>2 Delivering, entrusting, depositing.<BR>3 A camp, a palace, the residence of a king or general.<BR>4 Any dwelling.<BR>5 Military array.<BR>6 Ornament, dress, decoration.<BR>7 Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशन|निवेशनं
निवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Entering, entrance.<BR>2 A house, a habitation.<BR>3 A town or city.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनीय|निवेशनीयः
निवेशनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be entered.<BR>2 To be engaged in.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, अनीयर् aff; also निवेशितव्य and निवेश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशयत्
निवेशयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Sending in or into, causing to enter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, causal form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशित
निवेशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Entered into.<BR>2 Engaged in.<BR>3 Sent, directed.<BR>4 Placed in or upon.<BR>5 Turned to or towards, fixed upon.<BR>E.<BR>नि before विश to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्यूढ|निव्यूढं
निव्यूढ<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>Perseverance, resolution.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and व्यूढ arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश्<BR>f. (-निट्)<BR>Night: see निशा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>The son of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमन|निशमनं
निशमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शम to be quiet, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्य
निशम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Hearing, having heard.<BR>E.<BR>नि, शम to repose, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमयत्
निशमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शम to rest, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमय्य
निशमय्य<BR>ind. (-य्यः)<BR>Having heard.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शमु to repose, ल्यप् aff., and अय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 Turmerick, (Curcuma longa.)<BR>3 Another sort, (C. zanthorrhiza)<BR>E.<BR>नि always, शो to waste or reduce, (mortals,) aff. क; or निश to meditate, aff. क्विप् and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाकर|निशाकरः
निशाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and कर who makes or marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाकेतु|निशाकेतुः
निशाकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and केतु symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशागण|निशागणः
निशागण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A number of nights.<BR>E.<BR>निशा A night, and गण a class, a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचर|निशाचरः
निशाचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Nocturnal, night-walking, what goes or moves about by night.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A Rākṣasa, a fiend, an imp or goblin.<BR>2 A Shakāl.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 A snake.<BR>5 The ruddy goose.<BR>6 A ghost, an evil spirit.<BR>7 A thief.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A woman who goes to an assignation, a harlot, a whore.<BR>2 A she devil, a female fiend.<BR>3 A sort of perfume: see केशिनी.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and चर् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाचर्म्मन्|निशाचर्मन्
निशाचर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and चर्म्मन् skin or hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाजल|निशाजलं
निशाजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Frost, hoar frost.<BR>2 Dew.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाट|निशाटः
निशाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An owl.<BR>2 A demon, a ghost.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and अट who goes; also with ल्यु aff. निशाटन m. (-नः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
निशात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sharpened, polished, whetted, burnished.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शो to cut or pare, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाद|निशादः
निशाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A man of a low caste: see निषाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादत्व
निशादत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The state or condition of a man of low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादर्शिन्
निशादर्शिन्<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादि|निशादिः
निशादि<BR>f. (-दिः)<BR>Evening, twilight.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and आदि beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्त|निशांत|निशान्तं|निशान्तः
निशान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Quiet, tranquil, patient.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 The end of the night, or break of day.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शम to be quiet, aff. क्त; or निशा night, अम to go, aff. क्त; or निशा as before, night, and अन्त end or term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्तनारी
निशान्तनारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female, a housewife.<BR>E.<BR>निशान्त a house, नारी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशान्ध|निशांध
निशान्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Blind at night.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापति|निशापतिः
निशापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशापुष्प|निशापुष्पं
निशापुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Hoar frost.<BR>2 Dew.<BR>3 The white water lily.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाभङ्गा
निशाभङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A plant commonly Dugdhapeya.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामणि|निशामणिः
निशामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामन|निशामनं
निशामन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sight, seeing.<BR>2 Looking at, beholding.<BR>3 Looking at repeatedly.<BR>4 Hearing.<BR>5 A shadow, a reflexion.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शम to quiet, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामृग|निशामृगः
निशामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Shakāl.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाम्य
निशाम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having put out, (as a light.)<BR>2 Having tranquillized.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शम to be quiet, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=479" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारण|निशारणं
निशारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>2 Night combat.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शृ to injure or kill, aff. ल्युट्; or निशा night, and रण war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारत्न|निशारत्नं
निशारत्न<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and रत्न jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुक|निशारुकः
निशारुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An air, a sort of musical composition, played as an accompaniment to dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावृन्द|निशावृन्दं
निशावृन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>A number of nights.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and वृन्द a many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशावेदिन्
निशावेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाहस|निशाहसः
निशाहस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The white water lily.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and हस what smiles; opening its petals at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशाह्वा
निशाह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>Turmerick.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and आह्वा appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशित|निशितं|निशितः
निशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sharpened, whetted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शो to pare, affix क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशिपुष्पा
निशिपुष्पा<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>निशि by night, seventh case of निश्, and पुष्प flower, fem. affix टाप्; also with ङीप् affix निशिपुष्पी, and with कन् added निशिपुष्पिका the night-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ|निशीथः
निशीथ<BR>n. (-थः)<BR>1 Midnight.<BR>2 Night.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, शी to sleep, Uṇādi affix थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनी
निशीथिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>निशीथ as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनीनाथ|निशीथिनीनाथः
निशीथिनीनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>निशीथिनी night, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ्या
निशीथ्या<BR>f. (-थ्या)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>निशीथ midnight, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भ|निशुंभ|निशुंभः|निशुम्भः
निशुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 The name of a giant slain by DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>नि before शुम्भ to hurt or kill, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भन|निशुंभन|निशुंभनं|निशुम्भनं
निशुम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भमर्द्दिनी|निशुम्भमर्दिनी|निशुंभमर्दिनी
निशुम्भमर्द्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>निशुम्भ an Asura or demon so named, and मर्द्दिनी the female destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुम्भिन्
निशुम्भिन्<BR>m. (-म्भी)<BR>An inferior deity of the Bauddhas; also Heramba and Vajraṭīka.<BR>E.<BR>नि not, शुम्भ injuring, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशोपशाय
निशोपशाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Resting at night.<BR>E.<BR>निशा, and उपशाय rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशैत|निशैतः
निशैत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Vaka, a crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>E.<BR>निशा by night, इत gone, to his roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चय|निश्चयः
निश्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment, positive conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative particle, चि to collect, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चल
निश्चल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>Immoveable, still, fixed.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privat. चल what goes or moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चलाङ्ग|निश्चलांग|निश्चलाङ्गः
निश्चलाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Firm, immoveable.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A kind of crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>2 A mountain, a rock.<BR>E.<BR>निश्चल, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायक|निश्चायकः
निश्चायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what ascertains or determines.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before चि to collect, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चारक|निश्चारकं|निश्चारकः
निश्चारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Evacuation by stool.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 Obstinacy, wilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, चर to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित
निश्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Certain, ascertained, determined, concluded.<BR>2 Sentenced, pronounced.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Certainty, conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित्य
निश्चित्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>निर aff. चि to collect, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चिन्त|निश्चिंत|निश्चिन्तः
निश्चिन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Thoughtless, inconsiderate, void of reflexion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. चिन्ता reflexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चीयमान|निश्चीयमानः
निश्चीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being in the course of ascertainment or conclusion, being under investigation.<BR>E.<BR>निर before चि to collect, शानच् aff., यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चुक्कण|निश्चुक्कणं
निश्चुक्कण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A sort of tooth-powder prepared of sulphate of iron, &c. it destroys the tartar, but blackens the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before चुक्क to give pain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चेष्ट|निश्चेष्टः
निश्चेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Powerless, helpless.<BR>2 Incapable of effort.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्रेयस
निश्श्रेयस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Final emancipation: see निःश्रेयस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्रेयसकर
निश्श्रेयसकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Conferring final happiness or emancipation.<BR>E.<BR>निश्श्रेयस, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्वसन
निश्श्वसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breathing out, expiration.<BR>2 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, and श्वसन breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्श्वास
निश्श्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Breath expired, breathing out, expiration.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, and श्वास breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष
निष<BR>(उ) निषु r. 1st cl. (नेषति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्ग|निषंग|निषंगः|निषङ्गः
निषङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A quiver.<BR>2 Union, meeting, association.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सञ्ज to embrace, aff. घञ् a collection of arrows, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गथि|निषंगथि|निषंगथिः|निषङ्गथिः
निषङ्गथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>1 Embracing, an embrace.<BR>2 A bowman.<BR>3 A charioteer.<BR>4 A car.<BR>5 Grass.<BR>6 The shoulder.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सञ्ज to embrace, aff. घ and थिन् Uṇādi aff. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषङ्गिन्|निषंगिन्
निषङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>An archer, a bowman.<BR>E.<BR>निषङ्ग a quiver, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद|निषदः
निषद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A musical note: see निषाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्या
निषद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>1 A market.<BR>2 A small bed.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वर|निषद्वरः
निषद्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Mud, mire.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, Uṇādi aff. ष्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 The name of a mountain or mountainous range, forming one of the principal ranges of the universe, and described as lying immediately south of Hāvrata, and north of the Himāla range.<BR>2 A country in the south-east division of India.<BR>3 The sovereign of Niṣadha.<BR>4 A musical note; also निषाद्र.<BR>5 Hard, solid.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, aff. अच् and द irregularly changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्ण|निषण्णः
निषण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>1 Placed in or on.<BR>2 Gone to.<BR>3 Rested, reclined.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्णक|निषण्णकं
निषण्णक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-खं)<BR>Seating, seated.<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A seat.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषन्नक
निषन्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of potherb, (Marsilea dentata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषाद|निषादः
निषाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The first of the seven musical notes, or more properly the last or highest of the scale.<BR>2 A man of a degraded tribe, or an outcaste, especially the son of a Brahman by a Śūdra woman.<BR>3 A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, aff, घञ्; pervading the mind, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादिन्
निषादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An elephant keeper or driver.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्ध|निषिद्धं
निषिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>नि priv. सिध to complete, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषीदत्
निषीदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>1 Sitting, sitting upon.<BR>2 Standing or resting in or on.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूदन|निषूदनं|निषूदनः
निषूदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=480" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेक|निषेकः
निषेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ceremony performed upon impregnation taking place.<BR>2 Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR>3 Effusion.<BR>4 Seminal effusion.<BR>E.<BR>नि, and षिच to sprinkle, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेदिवस्
निषेदिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-दुषी-वस्)<BR>Sitting, seated on or upon.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सद to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेध|निषेधः
निषेध<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>1 Prohibition, negation.<BR>2 Stop, discontinuance.<BR>3 Contrariety to or deviation from rule, irregularity, exception.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सिध to complete, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवन
निषेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Observance, practice, adherence to.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सेव to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवनीय
निषेवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be served, to be obeyed.<BR>2 To be observed or followed.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सेव to serve, अनीयर् aff.; also निषेवितव्य, and निषेव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवित
निषेवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Observed, practised.<BR>2 Served, obeyed.<BR>3 Frequented through respect.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सेव to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क|निष्कं|निष्कः
निष्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (निष्कयते)<BR>To measure or weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क|निष्कं|निष्कः
निष्क<BR>mn. (-ष्कः-ष्कं)<BR>1 A weight of gold, applied however to different quantities: it is considered as synonymous with the Dīnāra of thirty-two small, or sixteen large Rettīs; with the Karṣa or Suvarṇa of sixteen Māṣas; with the Pala of four or five Suvarṇas; and with the larger Pala or Dināra, which is sometimes reckoned at 108, and other times at 150 Suvarṇas.<BR>2 Gold in general.<BR>3 Any ornament of the breast.<BR>4 An ornament of the neck.<BR>5 A weight of four Māṣas.<BR>6 A weight of silver of four Suvarṇas.<BR>7 A value of sixteen Kahans or Dramyas.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to go, Uṇādi aff. कन्, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्टक|निष्कंटक|निष्कण्टकः
निष्कण्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Without thorns.<BR>2 Free from trouble.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कण्ठ|निष्कण्ठः
निष्कण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A plant, (Capparis trifoliata,) &c.: see वरुणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्म्मन्|निष्कर्मन्
निष्कर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Exempt from or neglecting religious rites, worldly acts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्करुण
निष्करुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Cruel, unpitying, unmerciful.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. करुण compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कल|निष्कलं|निष्कलः
निष्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Waned, diminished.<BR>2 Impotent, seedless, barren.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMA.<BR>3 A fancied personification of BRAHMA, for religious ceremonies.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>A woman past child bearing, in whom menstruation has ceased.<BR>E.<BR>निर् gone, lost, कल a part, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्ष|निष्कर्षः
निष्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before कृष to plough, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काम
निष्काम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Free from wish or desire.<BR>n. adv. (-मं)<BR>Unwillingly.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारण|निष्कारणं
निष्कारण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारुष
निष्कारुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Of a noble race, not degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालक|निष्कालकः
निष्कालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A penitent, shaved and smeared with Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काश|निष्काशः
निष्काश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A portico, a veranda.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and कश to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काशित|निष्काशितः
निष्काशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expelled: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासित|निष्कासितः
निष्कासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expelled, dismissed, turned out.<BR>2 Gone forth or out, issued.<BR>3 Placed, deposited.<BR>4 Placed over, appointed, stationed.<BR>5 Reviled, reproached.<BR>6 Opened out, blown, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, कस to go, in the causal form, aff. क्त, र becomes ष or Visarga: see निःकासित; also निष्काशित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासिन्
निष्कासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Who or what expels.<BR>(-नी)<BR>A female slave not restrained by her master.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, कस to go, causal form, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुट|निष्कुटः
निष्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A grove near a house.<BR>2 A field.<BR>3 A door.<BR>4 The private apartments, the Zenana. (E. निर् without, कुट the house.)<BR>f. (-टा, also टिः or टी)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>निर out, कुट the shell or husk, aff. क, with टाप् fem. aff. or कि with ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुम्भ|निष्कुम्भः
निष्कुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, स्कुम्भ a Sautra root, to spread, aff. अच्; also निःकुम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुषित
निष्कुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expelled, extracted, forced or drawn out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कुष to extract, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुह|निष्कुहः
निष्कुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The hollow of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmative prefix, कुह to astonish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत
निष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Regardless, negligent.<BR>2 Disregarded, thought nothing of.<BR>3 Pardoned.<BR>4 Undone.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृति|निष्कृतिः
निष्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Pardon, absolution.<BR>2 Expiration.<BR>3 Escaping from, avoiding the consequence of any thing.<BR>4 Undoing, doing away.<BR>5 Disregarding, neglecting.<BR>6 Acquittance, compensation, discharge of a debt or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. कृति doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषण|निष्कोषणं
निष्कोषण<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Taking away.<BR>2 Extracting, extirpating.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before कुष to expel, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषितव्य
निष्कोषितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be taken away.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, कुष to expel, तव्य aff.; also निष्कोषणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम|निष्क्रमः
निष्क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Any intellectual faculty, as attention, comprehension, &c.<BR>2 Degradation, baseness, inferiority of tribe, family, &c.<BR>3 Going out, exit.<BR>E.<BR>निर् assuredly or forth, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमण|निष्क्रमणं
निष्क्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going forth or out.<BR>2 Taking a child for the first time out of the house, in the fourth month, considered as an essential ceremony, and accompanied by sacrifice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, क्रमण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम्य
निष्क्रम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Going forth.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, क्रम to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रय|निष्क्रयः
निष्क्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Hire, wages.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before क्री to buy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रान्त|निष्क्रान्तः
निष्क्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Gone out, gone, departed.<BR>E.<BR>निर् out, क्रम to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रिय|निष्क्रियं
निष्क्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Abstaining from ceremonial rites.<BR>2 Idle, unoccupied.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>BRAHMA or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्वाथ|निष्क्वाथः
निष्क्वाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Broth, soup.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before क्वथ to decoct, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्य|निष्ट्यः
निष्ट्य<BR>m. (-ष्ट्यः)<BR>A man of one of the outcast or barbarous tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्त
निष्टप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Well done, dressed or cooked.<BR>2 Burnished, made bright.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ|निष्ठः
निष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Staying, being in, who or what stays or is in or on any thing.<BR>2 Believing, faithful.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 The catastrophe of a drama, the conclusion of a fable.<BR>2 Conclusion in general, end, termination.<BR>3 Disappearance, loss, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">Page482</a>] destruction.<BR>4 Confirmation, completion.<BR>5 Asking, begging.<BR>6 Ordinary and uniform practice or profession.<BR>7 Good conduct, excellence.<BR>8 Religious practice, devout and austere exercise.<BR>9 Faith, belief.<BR>10 Condition, state.<BR>11 Fixed time of life, &c.<BR>12 Trouble, distress, anxiety.<BR>13 The technical term for the past participial affixes क्त and क्तवतु.<BR>E.<BR>नि completely, assuredly, स्था to stay or stop, अङ् and टाप affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=481" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठान|निष्ठानं
निष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sauce, condiment.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्था to stay, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठित|निष्ठितं
निष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Firm, fixed.<BR>2 Certain, ascertained.<BR>3 Engaged in, attached to, devoted to.<BR>4 Staying, being in or on.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीव|निष्ठीवं|निष्ठीवः
निष्ठीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Spitting: see निष्ठेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठीवन|निष्ठीवनं
निष्ठीवन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Spitting, spitting out, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ष्ठिव to eject, aff. ल्युट्; also निष्ठेवन and निष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुर|निष्ठुरं
निष्ठुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Harsh, contumelious, (as speech.)<BR>2 Hard, solid.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्था to be, to be firm, aff. कुरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठुरता
निष्ठुरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Harshness of speech, reviling, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>निष्ठुर, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, निष्ठुरत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूत|निष्ठ्यूतं
निष्ठ्यूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cast, thrown, sent, directed, dispatched.<BR>2 Ejected from the mouth, spit.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ष्ठिव to eject, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ्यूति|निष्ठ्यूतिः
निष्ठ्यूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Spitting, spitting out.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ष्ठिव to eject from the mouth, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेव|निष्ठेवं|निष्ठेवः
निष्ठेव<BR>subst. mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Spitting, spitting out, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ष्ठिव to eject, aff. घञ्; also निष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठेवन|निष्ठेवनं
निष्ठेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spitting.<BR>E.<BR>see the last; also निष्ठीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ण
निष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Skilful, &c. see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्णात|निष्णातः
निष्णात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Skilful, clever, conversant, learned.<BR>2 Perfect, superior, supreme.<BR>3 (In law,) Agreed upon.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्ना to bathe, aff. क्त; also with ड, निष्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पक्व|निष्पक्वं
निष्पक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>Decocted, infused, boiled.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before पक्व ripe or cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पङ्क|निष्पंक
निष्पङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Pure, free from mud or filth.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. पङ्क mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतत्
निष्पतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>Issuing, going forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before पत to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पतन|निष्पतनं
निष्पतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going forth or out, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and पतन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्ति|निष्पत्तिः
निष्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Completion, conclusion, termination, consummation.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Going forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative, पद to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पत्राकृति|निष्पत्राकृतिः
निष्पत्राकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Excessive bodily pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्द|निष्पंद|निष्पन्दः
निष्पन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Motionless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, स्पदि to shake or move, aff. अच्; also निष्पन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पन्न|निष्पन्नः
निष्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Done, finished, concluded, completed.<BR>2 Born, produced.<BR>3 Motionless.<BR>4 Gone forth or out of.<BR>E.<BR>निर् affirmation or negation, and पन्न gone, from पद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पराक्रम
निष्पराक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Weak, destitute of power.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. पराक्रम valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्परिग्रह|निष्परिग्रहः
निष्परिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An ascetic, one who has no family nor dependants.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. परिग्रह dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पादन|निष्पादनं
निष्पादन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Doing, effecting, accomplishing.<BR>2 Concluding.<BR>3 Producing, causing, engendering.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, पद to go, causal form, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पादित|निष्पादितं
निष्पादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done, effected, made, produced.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, पद to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाद्य|निष्पाद्यं
निष्पाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>To be done, to be effected or accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, पद to go, causal form, यत् aff.; also निष्पादनीय and निष्पादयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाद्यमान
निष्पाद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being done or made, in the course of completion.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before पद to go, causal form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पान
निष्पान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Drinking.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पाव|निष्पावः
निष्पाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Certain, indubitable.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Winnowing, cleaning corn, &c.<BR>2 Wind, air.<BR>3 The wind of the winnowing sieve or basket.<BR>4 Straw, chaff.<BR>5 A legume, a pod.<BR>6 A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् before पू to purify, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पिष्ट|निष्पिष्टः
निष्पिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Ground, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>2 Beaten, oppressed.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुत्त्र
निष्पुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः-त्त्रा-त्त्रं)<BR>Sonless.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and पुन्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पुरुष|निष्पुरुषः
निष्पुरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Feminine, neuter, not male.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A eunuch or impotent man.<BR>2 A coward.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रतिभ|निष्प्रतिभः
निष्प्रतिभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Stupid, frigid, dull, apathetic^1, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, प्रतिभ brilliance.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रत्यूह|निष्प्रत्यूहः
निष्प्रत्यूह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Unobstructed, unimpeded.<BR>n. adv. (-हं)<BR>Freely, without hindrance.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. प्रत्यूह obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रभ|निष्प्रभः
निष्प्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Gloomy, dark, obscure.<BR>E.<BR>निर् privative, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रयोजन|निष्प्रयोजनं
निष्प्रयोजन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Causeless, groundless.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative, प्रयोजन motive, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्पृह
निष्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Content, not envying any person, nor coveting any thing.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant; also अमूला and विष्णुघल्लभा.<BR>E.<BR>निर् not, स्पृहा envy, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्प्रवाण|निष्प्रवाणं
निष्प्रवाण<BR>mfn. subst. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>New and unbleached cloth.<BR>E.<BR>निर् gone, प्रकाणी here said to mean the weaver's brush; also निष्प्रवाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) the forms are irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्फल|निष्फलः
निष्फल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Barren, unfruitful.<BR>2 Seedless, impotent.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>A woman past child bearing, one in whom menstruation has ceased: see निष्कल.<BR>E.<BR>निर् priv. and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसम्पात|निसंपात|निसम्पातः
निसम्पात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Midnight; also निःसम्पात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्ग|निसर्गः
निसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 The natural state, nature, peculiar character or condition.<BR>2 Form.<BR>3 Creation.<BR>4 Relinquishment, abandoning.<BR>5 Transfer, barter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सृज to create, or to abandon, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसर्गज
निसर्गज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Cognate, innate.<BR>2 Produced at creation.<BR>E.<BR>निसर्ग, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसिन्धु|निसिन्धुः
निसिन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A shrub, (Vitex negundo); it is also read निसिन्ध, and with कन् added निसुन्धक; the words are considered as barbarous: see सिन्धुवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसूदन|निसूदनं
निसूदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before षद to kill, aff, ल्युट्; also निषूदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृता
निसृता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=482" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्ट|निसृष्टं
निसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Delivered, deposited.<BR>2 Centrical, middle.<BR>E.<BR>नि before सृज to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निसृष्टार्थ|निसृष्टार्थः
निसृष्टार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador: one who decides upon his own discretion, knowing the intentions of both parties.<BR>E.<BR>निसृष्ट deposited, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तनी
निस्तनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A pill, a bolus, a sort of force-meat ball.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्तन a breast, ङीप् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तरण|निस्तरणं
निस्तरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going out or forth.<BR>2 Crossing over or passing.<BR>3 Extraction, getting rid of or free from.<BR>4 Means of success, an expedient, a plan.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before तॄ to cross or pass over, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तब्ध
निस्तब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Paralysed, numbed.<BR>2 Stopped, fixed.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्तम्भ to stop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तर्हण|निस्तर्हणं
निस्तर्हण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before तृह to kill or hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तल|निस्तलं
निस्तल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Round, globular.<BR>2 Trembling, shaking, moving.<BR>3 Down, below.<BR>E.<BR>निर् negative or affirmative, and तल a support or stay; or depth, bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तार|निस्तारः
निस्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Getting over or across.<BR>2 Getting rid of, or away from, extraction, escape.<BR>3 Acquittance, requital.<BR>4 Means, expedient.<BR>5 Final liberation.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and तॄ to cross, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तारवीज
निस्तारवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The cause of final liberation, faith in any deity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निस्तार, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तितीर्षत्
निस्तितीर्षत्<BR>mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षन्ती-र्षत्)<BR>1 Desirous or anxious to cross.<BR>2 Wishing for salvation, or to traverse the world.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before तॄ to cross, desid. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुष
निस्तुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Freed from the chaff, (corn, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. तुष chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषक्षीर|निस्तुषक्षीरः
निस्तुषक्षीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>निस्तुष, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषरत्न|निस्तुषरत्नं
निस्तुषरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>निस्तुष, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तुषित|निस्तुषितं
निस्तुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left, abandoned, deserted.<BR>2 Skinned, peeled.<BR>3 Pared, made thin.<BR>E.<BR>निर् before तुष husk or skin, converted into a nominal verb, and क्त participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्तेजस्
निस्तेजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>1 Dull, obscure.<BR>2 Dull, spiritless.<BR>3 Powerless, impotent.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. तेजस् light, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रंश
निस्त्रंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Fearless, unapprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. त्रशि to fear, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंश|निस्त्रिंशः
निस्त्रिंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Merciless, unfeeling, unpitying.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A scimitar, a sacrificial knife.<BR>E.<BR>निर् forth, त्रिंशत् thirty, ड aff.; being of thirty finger's length, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रिंशधारिन्
निस्त्रिंशधारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A soldier armed with a sword.<BR>E.<BR>निस्त्रिंश, and धारिन् who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्त्रैगुण्य
निस्त्रैगुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Destitute of the qualities, truth, passion, and darkness.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. त्रैगुण्य three qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्नाव|निस्नावः
निस्नाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The remainder of articles, &c. after a sale or market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पन्द|निस्पंद|निस्पन्दः
निस्पन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Still, steady, immoveable.<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Throbbing, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्पद to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्पृह
निस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Content, unenvious.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A plant, (Gloriosa superba.)<BR>2 Contentment.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्यन्द|निस्यंदः|निस्यन्दः
निस्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Trickling, oozing, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्यन्द to ooze, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्राव|निस्रावः
निस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The scum of boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्रु to ooze or drop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वन|निस्वनः
निस्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Sound.<BR>2 Silence.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्वन to sound, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वान|निस्वानः
निस्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>नि before स्वन with घञ् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहत
निहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Killed, slain.<BR>E.<BR>नि affir. हत killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहनन|निहननं
निहनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हनन killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्तृ|निहंतृ
निहन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Murderous, who or what kills.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हन to kill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्यमान
निहन्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Killed.<BR>E.<BR>नि, हन to kill, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहव|निहवः
निहव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Calling, calling to.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्वे to call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहाका
निहाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An iguana or the Gangetic alligator.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हा to quit, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहार|निहारः
निहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Frost, dew: see नीहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहिंसन|निहिंसनं
निहिंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हिंस to kill or hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
निहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deposited, delivered, given, entrusted.<BR>2 Applied to, bestowed upon.<BR>3 Laid, (as dust by rain.)<BR>E.<BR>नि before धा to have, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
निहीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A low man, an outcast.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नव|निह्नवः
निह्नव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Denial or concealment of knowledge, dissimulation, secrecy.<BR>2 Concealment in general.<BR>3 Mistrust, doubt, suspicion.<BR>4 Wickedness.<BR>5 A secret.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्नु to hide or secrete, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नववादिन्
निह्नववादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A defendant or witness who prevaricates or tries to hide the truth.<BR>E.<BR>निह्नव, and वादिन who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवोत्तर
निह्नवोत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An evasive reply or defence.<BR>E.<BR>निह्नव, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुत
निह्नुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Concealed, secreted.<BR>2 Denied, evaded.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्नु to secrete, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुति|निह्नुतिः
निह्नुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Denial or concealment of knowledge, dissimulation, reserve, secrecy.<BR>2 Hiding, concealment.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्नु to secrete, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुवान
निह्नुवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Insinuating, using double entendre.<BR>E.<BR>नि, ह्नु to secrete, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्राद|निह्रादः
निह्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ह्रद to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्रादवत्|निह्रादवन्त्
निह्रादवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sounding, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>निह्राद, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक|नीकः
नीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>णी to gain, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकार|नीकारः
नीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Disrespect, contempt, vilifying, degrading.<BR>E.<BR>नि before कृ to make, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकाश|नीकाशः
नीकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>(In composition,) Like, resembling.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>नि before काश to shine, aff. घञ्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच|नीचः
नीच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>1 Low, (in stature,) short, dwarfish.<BR>2 Low, (in condition,) vile, base, mean.<BR>3 Deep.<BR>E.<BR>न privative, ई good fortune, चि to obtain, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचक|नीचकः
नीचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Low, dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>2 Vile, low.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An excellent cow.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकिन्
नीचकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 The head or top of any thing.<BR>2 The owner of a good cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=483" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकैस्
नीचकैस्<BR>ind.<BR>Low, below, little, vile, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नीचैस् low, अकच् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचग|नीचगं
नीचग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Low, vile, base.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Water.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>नीच low or deep, and ग who is going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचभोज्य|नीचभोज्यः
नीचभोज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>An onion.<BR>E.<BR>नीच a low man, and भोज्य food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचिका
नीचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A good cow; also नीचिकी and नैचिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचैस्
नीचैस्<BR>ind.<BR>Little, small, low.<BR>E.<BR>नि before चि to collect, डैसि aff. and the vowel of नि made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीड|नीडं|नीडः
नीड<BR>mn. (-डः-डं)<BR>1 A nest.<BR>2 A place, a spot.<BR>E.<BR>नि before इङ् to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडज|नीडजः
नीडज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>नीड a nest, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडोद्भव|नीडोद्भवः
नीडोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>नीड a nest, and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
नीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well behaved, correct, modest.<BR>2 Gained, obtained.<BR>3 Led, conducted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Wealth.<BR>2 Corn, grain.<BR>E.<BR>णी to get, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीति|नीतिः
नीति<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 Guiding, directing.<BR>2 Obtaining, acquirement, acquisition.<BR>3 Polity, political science, treating especially of the administration of government, including the practice of morality in private life, both by the sovereign and his subjects.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide or gain, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिकथा
नीतिकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Any work on polity, or good government.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and कथा a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिकुशल
नीतिकुशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Politic, conversant with government and human affairs.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and कुशल able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिघोष|नीतिघोषः
नीतिघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The car of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>नीनि guiding, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिज्ञ
नीतिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Knowing what is right, especially in government, sagacious, politic.<BR>(-ज्ञः)<BR>A statesman, a politician.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिमत्|नीतिमन्त्
नीतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Moral, eminent for royal duties.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिविद्या
नीतिविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Political science.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिशास्त्र
नीतिशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>The science of political ethics, or any work treating of it.<BR>E.<BR>नीति, and शास्त्र a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्त
नीत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given, given away.<BR>E.<BR>नि before, दत्त given, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत्वा
नीत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Having passed or spent.<BR>E.<BR>णी to take, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीथ|नीथः
नीथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A guider, a leader.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, कथन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीध्र|नीध्रं
नीध्र<BR>n. (-ध्रं)<BR>1 The edge of a thatch.<BR>2 A wood.<BR>3 The circumference of a wheel.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>5 The constellation Revatī.<BR>E.<BR>नि before धृ to fall, &c. aff. क, and the vowel of the prefix made long: this is considered as a various reading also of नीब्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीप|नीपः
नीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>2 A species of Ixora, (I. bandhuca, Rox.)<BR>3 A sort of Aśoca or Nil Asoka.<BR>E.<BR>णी to obtain, (pleasure,) and प Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीयमान|नीयमानं
नीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being sought or obtained.<BR>2 Being led or conducted.<BR>3 Being taken or taken away.<BR>E.<BR>नी to obtain, शानच् aff. यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीर|नीरं
नीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Juice, liquor.<BR>E.<BR>नी to obtain, aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरक्त
नीरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्त)<BR>Colourless, faded, having the colour taken out.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. रक्त red or dyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरज|नीरजं|नीरजः
नीरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatick.<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>2 A lotus in general.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, and ज born, or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्
नीरजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>1 Free from dust.<BR>2 Having no pollen, (as a flower.)<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A woman not menstruating.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. रजस् dust, &c. and इ made long before र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजस्व
नीरजस्व<BR>mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>Free from dust.<BR>E.<BR>निर्, and रजस् dust, the इ made long by the dropping of the र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरजीकारित
नीरजीकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cleansed, made free from dust.<BR>E.<BR>नीरजस्, and कारित caused, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरत|नीरतः
नीरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Indifferent, not taking pleasure in.<BR>2 Stopped, staying.<BR>E.<BR>नि neg. रत engaged in, इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरद|नीरदः
नीरद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Toothless.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, द what gives, or नि neg. रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरदिन्
नीरदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Cloudy.<BR>E.<BR>नीरद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरधि|नीरधिः
नीरधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, and धि having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरनिधि|नीरनिधिः
नीरनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरन्ध्र|नीरंध्र|नीरन्ध्रं
नीरन्ध्र<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्रः-न्ध्रा-न्ध्रं)<BR>1 Coarse, thick, gross, without interstices.<BR>2 Entire, having no holes.<BR>3 Imperforate.<BR>E.<BR>नी for निर् negative prefix, रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरस|नीरसः
नीरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Dry, withered, insipid, devoid of taste, &c. morally or physically.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>नी for निर् negative or affirmative prefix, and रस juice, flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराखु|नीराखुः
नीराखु<BR>m. (-खुः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, and आखु a cat; the water-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराजन|नीराजनं
नीराजन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Lustration of arms; a military and religious ceremony held on the 19th of Aśvin, and by kings or generals before taking the field; it is still observed by some Hindū states, under the name of Desahara.<BR>2 Waving lights before an idol; but it may also be performed with a lotus, clean cloth, or the leaves of various sacred plants; prostration is also considered as the fifth kind of this sort of adoration.<BR>E.<BR>निर् completely, राज to shine, aff. युच्; or नीर water, and अजन going, sprinkling the arms, horses, &c. with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरिन्दु|नीरिन्दुः
नीरिन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>नीर water, इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुच्
नीरुच्<BR>mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>Dull, dim, faded.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. रुच् light, and इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज्
नीरुज्<BR>mfn. (-रुक्)<BR>Convalescent, well in health.<BR>E.<BR>नि privative, रुज disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुज|नीरुजं|नीरुजः
नीरुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Convalescent, well.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>नि implying opposition, (anti,) and रुज् disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरुप
नीरुप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Formless, shapeless.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Heaven, æther.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 GOD.<BR>E.<BR>निर् neg. रुप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील|नीलं|नीलः
नील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Blue, dark blue or black.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Black or dark blue, (the colour.)<BR>2 The blue mountain, one of the principal ranges of mountains, dividing the world into nine portions, and lying immediately north of Hāvrata or the central division.<BR>3 One of the monkey chiefs.<BR>4 One of the Nidhis or divine treasures of KUVERA.<BR>5 A gem, (the sapphire.)<BR>6 A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">Page485</a>] name of the Buddha MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR>7 The blue or hill Maina, a bird so called.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Indigo, the dye.<BR>2 A mark, a characteristick mark.<BR>3 A medical plant, apparently distinct form the Indigofera.<BR>4 Blue vitriol.<BR>5 Black salt.<BR>6 Poison.<BR>7 Antimony.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A blue fly.<BR>2 A Rāgiṇī or mode of music, personified as the wife of the Rāga Mallāra.<BR>f. (ली)<BR>1 The indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>2 A complaint of the eyes, a darkening of the pupil.<BR>3 A bruise, a black and blue mark on the skin.<BR>E.<BR>नील to dye or tinge, क aff. or नीली indigo, अन् aff., implying being coloured or stained by it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=484" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलक|नीलकं|नीलकः
नीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Nil Gao or slate coloured antilope, (A. picta.)<BR>2 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Blue steel.<BR>2 Blue vitriol.<BR>3 Black salt.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकण्ठ|नीलकंठ|नीलकण्ठः
नीलकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A gallinule.<BR>3 A sparrow.<BR>4 A wagtail.<BR>5 A peacock.<BR>6 Morunga, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>7 A blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue or black, and कण्ठ the throat; also कालकण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकण्ठाक्ष|नीलकण्ठाक्षं
नीलकण्ठाक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The Eloeocarpus seed.<BR>E.<BR>नीलकण्ठ ŚIVA, and अक्ष seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकमल|नीलकमलं
नीलकमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and कमल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकुरुण्टक
नीलकुरुण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Blue Barleria, (B. cærulea.)<BR>E.<BR>नील, and कुरुण्टक Barleria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलक्रौञ्च|नीलक्रौञ्चः
नीलक्रौञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A sort of curlew or heron.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and क्रौञ्च a heron, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलग्रीव|नीलग्रीवः
नीलग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of MAHĀDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and ग्रीवा neck; the neck of ŚIVA was stained blue by the acrimony of the poison, which, upon its production at the churning of the ocean, he swallowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलङ्गु|नीलंगु|नीलंगुः|नीलङ्गुः
नीलङ्गु<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>1 An insect in general.<BR>2 A sort of worm.<BR>3 A Shakal.<BR>E.<BR>नि before लगि to go, Uṇādi aff. कु, and the इ of नि made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलज|नीलजं
नीलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in the blue mountain, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Blue steel.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलझिण्टी
नीलझिण्टी<BR>f. (-ण्टी)<BR>Blue Barleria.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and भिण्टी Barleria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपङ्क|नीलपंक|नीलपङ्कं|नीलपङ्कः
नीलपङ्क<BR>n. (-ङ्कं)<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>2 Black mud.<BR>E.<BR>नील black, and पङ्क clay or mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपटल
नीलपटल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Very dark or black.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and पटल abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपत्र|नीलपत्रं|नीलपत्रः
नीलपत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Having black or dark blue leaves.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपाचन
नीलपाचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Steeping or maceration of indigo.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and पाचन cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपाचनभाण्ड
नीलपाचनभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>An indigo vat.<BR>E.<BR>नीलपाचन, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपद्म|नीलपद्मं
नीलपद्म<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>The blue lotus, (Nymphæa cærulea.)<BR>E.<BR>नील, and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपिच्छ|नीलपिच्छः
नीलपिच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A falcon.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and पिच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपुष्प|नीलपुष्पं|नीलपुष्पः
नीलपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A sort of Verbesina with blue flowers.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A blue species of Rasan.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपुष्पिका
नीलपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to नीलपुष्पी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलपृष्ठ
नीलपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A sort of fish, commonly called Rohi, (Cyprinus denticulatus.)<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलभ|नीलभः
नीलभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 A bee.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue or black, भा to shine, to show, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमणि|नीलमणिः
नीलमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A gem of a blue colour, the sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमाधव|नीलमाधवः
नीलमाधव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and माधव VIṢṆU, being of a dark colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमीलिक|नीलमीलिकः
नीलमीलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A firefly.<BR>E.<BR>नील black or dark blue, मील to twinkle, aff. टक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलमृत्तिका
नीलमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Iron pyrites.<BR>2 Black mould.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोह|नीललोहं
नीललोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Blue steel.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीललोहित|नीललोहितः
नीललोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purple, of a purple colour.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A mixture of red and blue, purple.<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>A vegetable: see भूमिजम्बु.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue or black, and लोहित red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवर्ण
नीलवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Blue, of a blue colour.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवसन|नीलवसनः
नीलवसन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wearing dark blue or black garments.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The planet Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>नील dark blue, and वसन vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवस्त्र|नीलवस्त्रः
नीलवस्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Dressed in dark blue or black vesture.<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Dark coloured cloth.<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवासस्
नीलवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Dressed in dark blue clothes.<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A name of Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>नील dark blue, वासस् raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलवृष|नीलवृषः
नीलवृष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A dark coloured bull.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and वृष a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाक्ष|नीलाक्षः
नीलाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and अक्ष an eye, having dark blue eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाङ्ग|नीलांग|नीलाङ्गः
नीलाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The Indian crane.<BR>2 The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाङ्गु|नीलांगु|नीलांगुः|नीलाङ्गुः
नीलाङ्गु<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>1 An insect in general.<BR>2 A sort of insect.<BR>3 A Shakāl.<BR>f. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>A gad-fly.<BR>E.<BR>see नीलङ्गु the penultimate being irregularly made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाञ्जन|नीलांजन|नीलाञ्जनं
नीलाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, अञ्जन collyrium, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाञ्जसा|नीलांजसा
नीलाञ्जसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 One of the Apsarasas or courtezans of Svarga.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>3 Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>नील dark, अञ्जस quickly, affs. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाम्बर|नीलांबर|नीलाम्बरं|नीलाम्बरः
नीलाम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dressed in dark blue cloth.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>2 A demon, a goblin.<BR>3 A name of ŚANI or Saturn.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Black or dark blue rainment.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and अम्बर clothing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाम्बुजन्मन्|नीलांबुजन्मन्
नीलाम्बुजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and अम्बुजन्मन् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाभ
नीलाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Blue.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and आभ what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाभ्र|नीलाभ्रः
नीलाभ्र<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>A dark cloud.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and अभ्र cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलाश्मन्
नीलाश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>A blue stone, a sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिका
नीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Nyctanthes tristis); a species with blue flowers.<BR>2 The indigo plant.<BR>3 A slight malady; black and blue marks on the body from bruises, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to नीली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=485" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिनी
नीलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Indigo, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>2 A black species of Tëori.<BR>E.<BR>नील black or dark blue, poss. aff. इनि fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीराग|नीलीरागः
नीलीराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A firm and constant friend.<BR>2 Firm, unalterable attachment, (as that of RĀMA and SĪTĀ.)<BR>3 Dark blue.<BR>E.<BR>नीली indigo, and राग colour; as permanent as the dye of indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीसन्धान|नीलीसंधान
नीलीसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fermentation or maceration of indigo.<BR>E.<BR>नीली, and सन्धान fermentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलीसन्धानभाण्ड|नीलीसंधानभाण्ड
नीलीसन्धानभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>An indigo vat.<BR>E.<BR>नीलीसन्धान, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोत्पल|नीलोत्पलं
नीलोत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A blue lotus, (Nymphæa cærulea.)<BR>E.<BR>नील blue, and उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोत्पलिन्
नीलोत्पलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>One of the Jaina saints or teachers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलोपल|नीलोपलः
नीलोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A blue stone, lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवर|नीवरः
नीवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Trade, traffick.<BR>2 A place, &c. proper for the site of a habitation.<BR>3 A religious mendicant.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Mud.<BR>E.<BR>णी to obtain, &c. ष्वरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवाक|नीवाकः
नीवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Dearth, scarcity.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वच to speak, aff. घञ्; creating alarm and causing conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवार|नीवारः
नीवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rice growing wild or without cultivation.<BR>E.<BR>नि before वृ to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवि|नीविः
नीवि<BR>f. (-विः-वी)<BR>1 Capital, principal, stock.<BR>2 Stake, wager.<BR>3 A cloth round a woman's waist, or the ends of the cloth passed round the loins so as to hold the whole together; on being loosed the lower members are exposed: the tie of drawers worn by women, &c.<BR>4 The outer tie of a packet, in which the offerings of a Śūdra at funeral obsequies are presented.<BR>E.<BR>नि before व्येञ् to cover, Uṇādi aff. इन् and ङीष् optionally added; the इ of नि is made long, and the radical finals rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवृत्
नीवृत्<BR>mfn. (-वृत्)<BR>Any inhabited country.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, वृत to be, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्र|नीव्रं
नीव्र<BR>n. (-व्रं)<BR>1 The edge of a thatch.<BR>2 The circumference of a wheel.<BR>3 A wood.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>5 The constellation Revatī.<BR>E.<BR>नि certainly, वृ to be, aff. क, deriv. irr.; also नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीशार|नीशारः
नीशार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A warm cloth, a blanket.<BR>2 Curtains, musquito curtains.<BR>3 An outer tent or screen. नि before शृ to hurt, &c. aff. घञ्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीहार|नीहारः
नीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Frost, hoar frost.<BR>2 Heavy dew.<BR>E.<BR>नि before हृ to steal or take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle, of interrogation;<BR>2 Of discrimination;<BR>3 of reflexion.<BR>4 Of doubt;<BR>5 Of contempt;<BR>6 Of pretence;<BR>7 Of respect.<BR>8 A particle implying cause or motive: (what, but, how, hum, or, either, &c. will in general express it.)<BR>E.<BR>नुद to go, or नु praise, &c. aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>2 Time.<BR>3 A boat.<BR>4 The nasal mark above the line in neuter nouns, &c.<BR>f. (नुः)<BR>Praise, eulogium, panegyrick.<BR>E.<BR>ण्णु to praise, &c. aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुड
नुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (नुडति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत|नुतं
नुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, commended.<BR>E.<BR>णु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुति|नुतिः
नुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Praise, eulogium, panegyrick.<BR>2 Worship, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>णु to praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत्त|नुत्तः
नुत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Sent, ordered, despatched.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A plant: see लकुच.<BR>E.<BR>णुद to send, aff. क्त; also नुन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुनुत्सु
नुनुत्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Desirous of removing.<BR>E.<BR>णुद to send, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुन्न|नुन्नः
नुन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Sent, thrown, despatched, cast, dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>णुद to send, aff. क्त, form irr.; also नुत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत|नूतः
नूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 New.<BR>2 Praised, eulogized, hymned.<BR>E.<BR>णु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतन|नूतनः
नूतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>New, recent, fresh, young, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नव new, नू substituted for it, and तनप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतनत्व
नूतनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Newness, novelty.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, नूतनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत्न|नूत्नः
नूत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>New.<BR>E.<BR>नू substituted for नव new, त्नप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूद|नूदः
नूद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>णुद to send, क aff. and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूनम्
नूनम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Certainly, assuredly.<BR>2 A particle of doubt or deliberation.<BR>3 A reminiscent particle.<BR>4 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>नू a particle, नम to bow or bend, aff. विच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूपुर|नूपुरं|नूपुरः
नूपुर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>An ornament for the toes and feet.<BR>E.<BR>णु to praise or be praised. aff. क्विप्, नू an ornament, पुर to precede, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ<BR>r. 1st cl. (नरति) 5th cl. (नृणाति)<BR>To lead, to conduct, to guide, physically or morally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ<BR>m. (ना)<BR>1 Man, individually or collectively, a man, mankind.<BR>2 A piece at chess, &c.<BR>3 A gnomon.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide or gain, aff. डृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृकेशरिन्
नृकेशरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The Nṛsiṃha or man-lion Avatar.<BR>E.<BR>नृ, and केशरिन् a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृग|नृगः
नृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The name of a king, the son of IKṢVĀKU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृचक्षस्
नृचक्षस्<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>A demon, a Rākṣasa, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>नृ a man, and चक्षस् an eater; from चक्ष to eat, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृजग्ध
नृजग्ध<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>A man eater, a cannibal, a Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>(by whom,) नृ man, जग्ध is eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत
नृत<BR>(ई) नृती r. 4th cl. (नृत्यति)<BR>To dance, to dance as an actor, to gesticulate, to act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृति|नृतिः
नृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Dancing, the science or practice.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतू
नृतू<BR>m. (-तूः)<BR>1 A dancer, a mime, an actor.<BR>2 Earth.<BR>3 A worm.<BR>4 Length.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, and कू aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्त|नृत्तं
नृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Dancing.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्य|नृत्यं
नृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Dancing, acting, the actor's practice in general.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्यत्
नृत्यत्<BR>mfn. (-त्यन्-त्यन्ती-त्यत्)<BR>Dancing.<BR>E.<BR>नृत to dance, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृदेव|नृदेवः
नृदेव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>नृ, and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृधर्म्मन्|नृधर्मन्
नृधर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Acting as a man, doing a man's duty, &c.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Manly property or duty.<BR>E.<BR>नृ man, धर्म्म virtue, अनिच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृप|नृपः
नृप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>नृ man, पा to protect, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपनीति
नृपनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Royal policy.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, नीति policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपति|नृपतिः
नृपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>नृ man, and पति a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपद्रुम|नृपद्रुमः
नृपद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and द्रम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=486" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपप्रिय|नृपप्रियः
नृपप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A thorny species of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपमन्दिर|नृपमन्दिरं
नृपमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A royal palace.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and मन्दिर a residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपमान
नृपमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Sound of musick, made to give warning to kings when eating or feasting.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलक्ष्मन्
नृपलक्ष्मन्<BR>n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>1 The royal umbrella.<BR>2 Any of the royal insignia.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and लक्ष्मन् a mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलिङ्ग|नृपलिंग
नृपलिङ्ग<BR>n. (ङ्गं)<BR>Any emblem or mark of royalty.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपलिङ्गधर|नृपलिङ्गधरः
नृपलिङ्गधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Assuming the insignia of sovereignty.<BR>2 Taking, (fraudulently,) the emblem or marks of the royal or military caste.<BR>E.<BR>नृपलिङ्ग, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपवल्लभ|नृपवल्लभः
नृपवल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>A king's friend.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A queen.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपसंश्रय
नृपसंश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Service of princes.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and संश्रय dependance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपसभ|नृपसभं
नृपसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 An assembly of princes.<BR>2 A palace.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपांश
नृपांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Revenue, the royal portion; of grain, a sixth, eight, or twelfth; of fruits, &c. a sixth; and of merchandise a fiftieth.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपात्मज
नृपात्मज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Of royal birth.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A prince.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A bitter gourd.<BR>2 A princess.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and आत्मज offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपाध्वर|नृपाध्वरः
नृपाध्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of sacrifice; the Rājasūya, held by a lord paramount, in which all the offices are performed by tributary princes.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, अध्वर a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपाभीर|नृपाभीरं
नृपाभीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Music played at the royal meals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपामय|नृपामयः
नृपामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Consumption.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and आमय disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपावर्त्त|नृपावर्त|नृपावर्त्तं
नृपावर्त्त<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>A kind of gem.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and आवर्त्त what revolves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपासन|नृपासनं
नृपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A throne.<BR>E.<BR>नृप a king, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपोचित|नृपोचितः
नृपोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kingly, princely, suited to a king.<BR>E.<BR>नृप, and उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृयज्ञ|नृयज्ञः
नृयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>नृ a man, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृवराह|नृवराहः
नृवराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The boar incarnation of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>नृ a man, वराह a boar; being delineated with the figure of a man, and the head of the wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंस|नृशंसः
नृशंस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Malicious, wicked, hurtful, injurious, mischievous, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>नृ man, शसि to hurt, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंसवृत्त
नृशंसवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Practising mischief.<BR>E.<BR>नृशंश, add वृत्त engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसिंह|नृसिंहः
नृसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The fourth Avatāra or descent of that deity, in the shape of a man, with the head and claws of a lion.<BR>3 A chief, a noble, a great or illustrious man.<BR>E.<BR>नृ a man, and सिंह a lion; applied in composition, also to signify pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसेन|नृसेनं
नृसेन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>An army of men.<BR>E.<BR>नृ a man, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृसोम|नृसोमः
नृसोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An illustrious or great man, a prince or chief.<BR>E.<BR>नृ mankind, and सोम the moon, here implying superiority or excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृहरि|नृहरिः
नृहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VIṢṆU as the man-lion.<BR>E.<BR>नृ, and हरि a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजक|नेजकः
नेजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>णिज to cleanse, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतव्य
नेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be taken, to be carried or conducted.<BR>E.<BR>णी to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतृ
नेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Leading, conducting, one who guides or leads, &c.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A master, an owner.<BR>2 A guide.<BR>E.<BR>णी to lead, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्र|नेत्रं
नेत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>A leader, a guide, one who guides or leads.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 The root of a tree.<BR>3 Bleached or wove silk.<BR>4 A car, a carriage.<BR>5 The string of a churning rope.<BR>6 An enema pipe.<BR>mn. (-त्रः-त्रं)<BR>Any tubular vessel.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide or gain, Uṇādi aff. ष्ट्रन्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रज
नेत्रज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A tear.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रच्छद|नेत्रच्छदः
नेत्रच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An eyelid.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र the eye, छद to cover, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रपर्य्यन्त|नेत्रपर्यन्त|नेत्रपर्यंत|नेत्रपर्यन्तः|नेत्रपर्य्यन्तः
नेत्रपर्य्यन्त<BR>mfn. (न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>As far as to the eye, up to the eye.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The outer angle of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and पर्य्यन्त limitative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रपिण्ड|नेत्रपिंड|नेत्रपिण्डः
नेत्रपिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 The ball of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र the eye, and पिण्ड a ball of flesh, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रयोनि|नेत्रयोनिः
नेत्रयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र an eye, and योनि the vulva; being covered with marks resembling that organ, through the curse of GAUTAMA, whose wife he had attempted to debauch; the sage afterwards relenting, changed these disgraceful marks on the body of the deity to as many eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्ररञ्जन|नेत्ररंजन|नेत्ररञ्जनं
नेत्ररञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and रञ्जन delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्ररोग|नेत्ररोगः
नेत्ररोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Any disease of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>नेच, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रवस्त्र
नेत्रवस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A veil over the eye.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रामय|नेत्रामयः
नेत्रामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Ophthalmia, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्राम्बु|नेत्रांबु
नेत्राम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>A tear.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र an eye, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रोत्सव|नेत्रोत्सवः
नेत्रोत्सव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Any pleasing or beautiful object.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रौषध|नेत्रौषधं
नेत्रौषध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>1 Green sulphate of iron considered as a collyrium.<BR>2 Collyrium in general.<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>A drug, commonly कोंगा.<BR>E.<BR>नेत्र the eye, and औषध a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदयत्
नेदयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Approximating, bringing near.<BR>E.<BR>नेद for अन्तिक nom. verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठ|नेदिष्ठं
नेदिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Very near.<BR>2 Clever.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>E.<BR>अन्तिक near, इष्ठन् affix of the superlative, and the form irr.; also नेदीयस् with ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदीयस्
नेदीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very near, nearest: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेन्य
नेन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Taking or obtaining frequently.<BR>E.<BR>णी to obtain, frequent. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेप|नेपः
नेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The family priest.<BR>2 Water.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, Uṇādi aff. प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपथ्य|नेपथ्यं
नेपथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>1 A stage, or the part behind the scenes, the tiring room, &c.<BR>2 Ornament, embellishment.<BR>E.<BR>णी to guide, विच् aff. and the vowel changed; ने the eye, or a chief, पथ्य proper, agreeable, grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपाल|नेपालः
नेपाल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>The country of Nepal.<BR>E.<BR>ने a chief: see the last, and पाल cherishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालिका
नेपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>नेपाल, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेम|नेमः
नेम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Time, period, season.<BR>2 Term, boundary, limit.<BR>3 Part, portion.<BR>4 A fence, a boundary wall or hedge.<BR>5 A [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">Page488</a>] hole, a chasm.<BR>6 Fraud, deceit.<BR>7 Acting, dancing.<BR>8 Other, different.<BR>9 Evening.<BR>10 Up, above.<BR>11 A root.<BR>E.<BR>णी to gain, Uṇādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=487" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमि|नेमिः
नेमि<BR>f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>1 The circumference of a wheel.<BR>2 The framework for the rope of a well.<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 The twenty-second Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>2 A sacred place, as Mathura.<BR>mf. (-मिः-मी)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia Oujeiniensis).<BR>E.<BR>णी to gain or go, Uṇādi aff. मि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिचक्र|नेमिचक्रः
नेमिचक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A prince descended from PARĪKṢIT, who is said to have removed the capital of India to Kauśāmbī, after the inundation of Hastinapur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिन्
नेमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>नेमि the circumference of a wheel, इनि aff.; the wood being used for its manufacture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्टृ
नेष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>One of the officiating priests at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>णी to lead or conduct the ceremonies, Uṇādi aff. तृच् and षुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयस
नैःश्रेयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Relating to final emancipation, leading to it, effecting it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निःश्रेयस, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयसिक
नैःश्रेयसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to final emancipation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निःश्रेयस, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्नेह्य
नैःस्नेह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 Dryness, austerity.<BR>2 Coldness, want of feeling or affection.<BR>E.<BR>निःस्नेह, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
नैक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Many, various.<BR>E.<BR>न neg. एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकटिक|नैकटिकः
नैकटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Near, being near.<BR>E.<BR>निकट, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकट्य|नैकट्यं
नैकट्य<BR>n. (-ट्यं)<BR>Proximity, vicinage.<BR>E.<BR>निकट, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकभेद|नैकभेदः
नैकभेद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Various, multiform, manifold.<BR>E.<BR>नैक, and भेद kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकरूप
नैकरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Multiform.<BR>E.<BR>नैक, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकषेय|नैकषेयः
नैकषेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a fiend, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>निकषा the mother of the race, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकृतिक
नैकृतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Morose, harsh spoken.<BR>2 Wicked, bad.<BR>E.<BR>निकृति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगम|नैगमः
नैगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 An Upaniṣad or portion of the Vedas.<BR>2 A sectarian, not a heretic.<BR>2 A trader, a merchant.<BR>4 A citizen, a townsman.<BR>5 Guiding, leading, directing.<BR>6 A road, a way.<BR>E.<BR>निगम a religious obligation, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचिक|नैचिकं
नैचिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The head of an ox.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A capital cow.<BR>E.<BR>नीचैस् low, down, चर to go, ठक् aff. and the radical finals rejected; also नीचिकी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैज|नैजं
नैज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जी-जं)<BR>Own.<BR>E.<BR>निज, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्य|नैत्यं
नैत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Eternity, perpetuity.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यक
नैत्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Always, constant, indispensable.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैत्यिक
नैत्यिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Invariable, constant, perpetual, indispensable.<BR>E.<BR>नित्य, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैद्र
नैद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>Sleepy, somniferous, relating or occurring in sleep.<BR>E.<BR>निद्रा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैधान
नैधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating to a treasure, a nest, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A boundary where some articles^1 are buried and dug up.<BR>E.<BR>निधान a treasure, अण् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपाल|नैपालः
नैपाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Produced in Nepal.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Double jasmine.<BR>2 Red arsenick.<BR>3 Śephālikā, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>4 Indigo.<BR>E.<BR>नेपाल Nepal, अण् and ङीप् affs.; brought from thence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपालिक|नैपालिकं
नैपालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Produced in or brought from Nepal, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>नेपाल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण|नैपुणं
नैपुण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Dexterity, cleverness, skill.<BR>E.<BR>निपुण skilful, aff. अण्; also with ष्यञ् aff., नैपुण्य n. (-ण्यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैपुण्य|नैपुण्यं
नैपुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Dexterity, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिक|नैमित्तिकं|नैमित्तिकः
नैमित्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Occasional.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Occasional, periodical act or rite.<BR>E.<BR>निमित्त cause, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमित्तिककर्म्मन्|नैमित्तिककर्मन्
नैमित्तिककर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>An occasional ceremony, such as should be observed on the birth of a child, &c.<BR>E.<BR>नैमित्तिक, and कर्म्भ act; also नैमित्तिकक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिष
नैमिष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Momentary, transient, in a twinkling.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The name of a forest. see नैमिषारण्य.<BR>E.<BR>निमिष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमिषारण्य|नैमिषारण्यं
नैमिषारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A wood celebrated as the residence of the Ṛṣis, to whom Sauti related the Mahābhārata.<BR>E.<BR>निमिष a twinkling of an eye, in which the sage GAURAMUKHA destroyed a sort of Asuras, and अण् aff. and अरण्य forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैमेय|नैमेयः
नैमेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR>E.<BR>नि before मि to measure, अच् aff. and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयग्रोध|नैयग्रोधं
नैयग्रोध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>The fruit of the Indian fig, &c.<BR>E.<BR>न्यग्रोध the fig tree, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयङ्कव|नैयङ्कवं
नैयङ्कव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Made of the skin, &c. of the deer, called न्यङ्क.<BR>E.<BR>न्यङ्कु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयत्य|नैयत्यं
नैयत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Self-government or subjugation.<BR>E.<BR>नियत, and ष्पञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयमिक
नैयमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>According to rule, regular, enjoined.<BR>E.<BR>नियम, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैयायिक|नैयायिकः
नैयायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A logician, a follower of the Nyāya or logical philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय the Nyāya system, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरन्तर्य्य|नैरन्तर्य|नैरंतर्य|नैरंतर्यं|नैरन्तर्य्यं
नैरन्तर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Compactness, closeness, contiguity.<BR>E.<BR>निरन्तर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैराश्य|नैराश्यं
नैराश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Despair.<BR>E.<BR>निराश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरृत|नैरृतः
नैरृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A demon, a fiend.<BR>2 The ruler of the south-west quarter.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The south-west quarter.<BR>E.<BR>निरृति said to be a proper name, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैरुक्त|नैरुक्तं|नैरुक्तः
नैरुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ती-क्तं)<BR>1 Obsolete, uncommon, belonging to the glossary of the Vedas.<BR>2 Acquainted with the terms of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>निरुक्ति, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्गुण्य|नैर्गुण्यं
नैर्गुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Absence of qualities or properties.<BR>E.<BR>निर्गुण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैर्मल्य|नैर्मल्यं|नैर्म्मल्यं
नैर्मल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Cleanness, purity.<BR>E.<BR>निर्मल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैल्य|नैल्यं
नैल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Blueness, darkness of colour.<BR>E.<BR>नील, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैविड्य|नैविड्यं
नैविड्य<BR>n. (-ड्यं)<BR>1 Thickness, substance.<BR>2 Closeness, compactness.<BR>3 Continued sound.<BR>E.<BR>निविड thick, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेद्य|नैवेद्यं
नैवेद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>An offering of eatable articles presented to a deity, which may afterwards be distributed to his ministers or worshippers, especially when it has been presented to any form of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>निवेद presenting, offering, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैवेशिक|नैवेशिकं
नैवेशिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A present to a Brahman who is a householder, a girl so given, or ornaments with her, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निवेश a house, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश|नैशं
नैश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Nocturnal, relating to the night; or a person, &c. doing any thing by night.<BR>E.<BR>निशा night, and अण् aff.; also with ठञ् aff. नैशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=488" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैश्चित्य|नैश्चित्यं
नैश्चित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Certainty.<BR>2 A fixed festival; as at birth, investiture, marriage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निश्चित, certain, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैषध|नैषधः
नैषध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>Relating to NIṢADHA.<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A name of NALA.<BR>E.<BR>निषध the country so called, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कर्म्म्य
नैष्कर्म्म्य<BR>n. (-र्म्मां)<BR>1 Abstinence or exemption from acts or their consequences.<BR>2 The salvation obtained by abstraction in opposition to that obtained by works.<BR>E.<BR>निष्कर्म्मन्, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कशतिक
नैष्कशतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Worth a hundred Niṣkas, bought with them, &c.<BR>E.<BR>निष्क, and शत a hundred, ठञ् aff.; also with सहस्र a thousand नैष्कसहस्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्किक|नैष्किकः
नैष्किक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought with, made of, &c. a Niṣka.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The mint-master.<BR>E.<BR>निष्क a weight of gold, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्कृतिक
नैष्कृतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Wicked, evil doing, malignant.<BR>E.<BR>निष्कृति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठिक|नैष्ठिकः
नैष्ठिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to state or condition.<BR>2 Belonging to the character or office of a perpetual student.<BR>3 Firm, fixed.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Brahman who continues with his spiritual preceptor, and always remains in the condition of the religious student.<BR>E.<BR>निष्ठा certainty, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैष्ठुर्य्य|नैष्ठुर्य|नैष्ठुर्यं
नैष्ठुर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Severity, cruelty.<BR>E.<BR>निष्ठुर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैसर्गिक|नैसर्गिकः
नैसर्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Natural, innate.<BR>E.<BR>निसर्ग nature, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैस्त्रिंशिक|नैस्त्रिंशिकः
नैस्त्रिंशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A swordsman, a soldier armed with a sword.<BR>E.<BR>निस्त्रिंश a sword, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नो
नो<BR>ind.<BR>No, not.<BR>E.<BR>णुद to command, aff. डो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोधास्
नोधास्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>नु to praise, असि Uṇādi aff. and धुट augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नोपस्थातृ
नोपस्थातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Remote, far off.<BR>E.<BR>न negative, उप near, स्था to be, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौ
नौ<BR>f. (नौः)<BR>A boat, a vessel in general.<BR>E.<BR>नुद to send, Uṇādi aff. डौ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौका
नौका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौकादण्ड|नौकादंड|नौकादण्डः
नौकादण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>An oar, a paddle.<BR>E.<BR>नौका a boat, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौतार्य्य|नौतार्य|नौतार्य्यं
नौतार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>Navigable, to be gone to or traversed in a vessel.<BR>E.<BR>नौ, and तार्य्य to be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नौयायिन्
नौयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>A passenger, a freight, who or what goes in a boat or vessel.<BR>E.<BR>नौ, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्
न्यक्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of abuse or contempt.<BR>E.<BR>the neuter of न्यञ्च् used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्करण|न्यक्करणं
न्यक्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Treating with disrespect or contempt.<BR>E.<BR>न्यक्, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कार|न्यक्कारः
न्यक्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Contempt, disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>न्यङ् little, low, कृ to make, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्कारुका
न्यक्कारुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An insect found in ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यक्ष|न्यक्षं|न्यक्षः
न्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Whole, entire.<BR>2 Low, inferior.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>2 A buffalo.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 A hole.<BR>2 Grass.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अक्ष a die, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्जाति
न्यग्जाति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of mean or inferior race.<BR>E.<BR>न्यक्, and जाति cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्भावन
न्यग्भावन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Contempt.<BR>2 Defiling.<BR>E.<BR>न्धक्, and भावन conceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोध|न्यग्रोधः
न्यग्रोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 The Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>2 A fathom measured by the arms extended.<BR>3 The Śami, (Mimosa albida.)<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>1 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata, Rox.)<BR>2 A medical plant, commonly Mohānā.<BR>E.<BR>न्यक् short, रुध to impede, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला|न्यग्रोधपरिमंडला
न्यग्रोधपरिमण्डला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An elegant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कु|न्यंकु|न्यंकुः|न्यङ्कुः
न्यङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>1 A deer.<BR>2 The name of a saint or Muni.<BR>E.<BR>नि always, अञ्च to go, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्कुभूरुह|न्यङ्कुभूरुहः
न्यङ्कुभूरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>न्यङ्कु a deer, and भूरुह a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यङ्ग|न्यंगः|न्यङ्गः
न्यङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Low abuse.<BR>E.<BR>न्यङ्, and ग what goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्च्|न्यंच्
न्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (न्यङ् नीची न्यक्)<BR>1 Short, dwarfish.<BR>2 Low, vile, contemptible, base.<BR>3 Slow, lazy.<BR>4 Whole, entire.<BR>E.<BR>नि prefixed to अञ्च to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यञ्चित|न्यंचित|न्यञ्चितं
न्यञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thrown or cast down.<BR>E.<BR>नि before, अञ्चित gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यय|न्ययः
न्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Loss, expense, waste, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>नि before इ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यर्ण्ण|न्यर्ण
न्यर्ण्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्ण्णः-र्ण्णा-र्ण्णं)<BR>1 Asked, solicited.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>3 Injured.<BR>E.<BR>नि, अर्द्द to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यसन|न्यसनं
न्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Delivering, giving up.<BR>2 Depositing.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अस to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्त|न्यस्तं
न्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Deposited, consigned, delivered.<BR>2 Placed in or upon.<BR>3 Applied to.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अस to throw or send, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यस्तशस्त्र|न्यस्तशस्त्रः
न्यस्तशस्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Unarmed, defenceless, having laid down or resigned weapons.<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A deified progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>न्यस्त delivered, and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याक्य|न्याक्यं
न्याक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Fried rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याद|न्यादः
न्याद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Eating, feeding.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अद to eat, अण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय|न्यायः
न्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Propriety, fitness.<BR>2 The Nyāya doctrine, logic, logical philosophy.<BR>3 Apposite illustration.<BR>4 A complete argument or syllogism.<BR>5 Policy, good government.<BR>E.<BR>नि certainly, इन् to go, aff घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायता
न्यायता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fitness, propriety.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to न्याय; also with त्व न्यायत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायसारिणी
न्यायसारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A woman acting or judging rightly.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय propriety, सारिणी proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाचार
न्यायाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A virtuous man.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायाधार|न्यायाधारः
न्यायाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An example of virtue or propriety.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय, and आधार what upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यायिन्
न्यायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Right, fit.<BR>2 Logical.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्याय्य|न्याय्यं
न्याय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Right, proper, fit.<BR>E.<BR>न्याय, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यास|न्यासः
न्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A deposit, a pledge.<BR>2 Deserting, abandoning.<BR>3 Delivering, presenting.<BR>4 Mental delivering, consigning or entrusting any thing to the mind.<BR>5 Mental appropriation or assignment of various parts of the body to tutelary divinities, accompanied with certain prayers and gesticulations.<BR>E.<BR>नि before अस to throw or cast away, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यासधारिन्
न्यासधारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The holder of a deposit, a mortgagee.<BR>E.<BR>न्यास, and धारिन् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युङ्ख|न्युंख|न्युङ्खः
न्युङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>1 Six-fold repetition of the triliteral name of God.<BR>2 The Sāma Veda.<BR>3 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>नि before उखि to go, aff. घ; it is also read न्युङ्ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=489" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्ज|न्युब्जं|न्युब्जः
न्युब्ज<BR>mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं)<BR>1 Crooked-backed, hump-backed.<BR>2 Looking downwards.<BR>3 Bent, crooked.<BR>4 Convex.<BR>m. (-ब्जः)<BR>1 Disease, sickness, pain.<BR>2 A sort of ladle made of Kusa grass.<BR>n. (-ब्जं)<BR>1 The fruit of the Kāmaraṅga, (Carambola averrhoa.)<BR>2 A vessel used at Śrāddhas.<BR>E.<BR>न्युब्ज to be crooked, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्युब्जखड्ग|न्युब्जखड्गः
न्युब्जखड्ग<BR>m. (-ड्गः)<BR>A sabre, a crooked sword.<BR>E.<BR>न्युब्ज crooked, and खड्ग a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यून|न्यूनं
न्यून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Blameable, vile, wicked, despicable.<BR>2 Less, deficient, defective.<BR>E.<BR>नि before ऊन less.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनता
न्यूनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Deficiency.<BR>2 Inferiority.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to न्यून also न्यूनत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनधी
न्यूनधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Ignorant, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>न्यून and धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भाव|न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भावः
न्यूनपञ्चाशद्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An ideot.<BR>E.<BR>न्यून, and पञ्चाशत् fifty, भाव property, having but forty-nine properties of human nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाङ्ग|न्यूनांग
न्यूनाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Maimed, mutilated, imperfect.<BR>E.<BR>न्यून, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाधिक
न्यूनाधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unequal, more or less.<BR>E.<BR>न्यून, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनाधिकविभाग
न्यूनाधिकविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Unequal partition.<BR>E.<BR>न्यूनाधिक, and विभाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्यूनेन्द्रिय
न्यूनेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Imperfect, wanting some organ; as blind, deaf, &c.<BR>E.<BR>न्यून, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न्रस्थिमालिन्
न्रस्थिमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>नृ man, अस्थि a bone, माला a necklace, and इनि poss. aff.; ornamented with a garland of human skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प<BR>The twenty-first consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, corresponding to the letter P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प|पं|पः
प<BR>m. (पः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A prince, a ruler.<BR>3 A leaf.<BR>4 Drinking.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, &c. aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्कण|पक्कणः
पक्कण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>The residence of low or outcast tribes.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, कण aff. and क substituted for च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तव्य
पक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be cooked or dressed.<BR>2 To be matured.<BR>3 To be digested.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, &c. तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ति|पक्तिः
पक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Cooking, ripening.<BR>2 Fame, respectability.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तिशूल|पक्तिशूलं
पक्तिशूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Inflammation of the bowels, cholic.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ति, and शूल cholic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्तृ
पक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>Who or what ripens or cooks.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>The digestive faculty.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, &c. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्र|पक्त्रं
पक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>The sacred fire to be maintained perpetually by the householder.<BR>E.<BR>पच to mature, Uṇādi aff. त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्रिम|पक्त्रिमं
पक्त्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Ripe, ripened, matured, cooked.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, &c. aff. क्त्रि and मप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्त्वा
पक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having cooked, dressed, matured, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्व|पक्वं
पक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>1 Mature, dressed, cooked, matured by nature or by art.<BR>2 Fully matured, on the eve of rottenness or decay.<BR>3 Perfect, come to perfection.<BR>4 Able, shrewd, experienced, mature, as the understanding.<BR>5 Grey, (the hair.)<BR>6 Digested.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook or ripen, व substituted for क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वकृत्
पक्वकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Cooking, maturing, who or what does so<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>The Nimb tree.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व ripe, and कृत् what makes; the leaves of the plant are applied to phlegmonoid swellings, to induce suppuration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वकेश
पक्वकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Grey-haired.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व, and केश the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वरस|पक्वरसः
पक्वरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Wine or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व matured, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ववारि
पक्ववारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>1 Rice gruel.<BR>2 Boiling water.<BR>3 Distilled water.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व boiled, वारि water; also read पङ्कवारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वान्न|पक्वान्नं
पक्वान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Dressed food.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वाशय|पक्वाशयः
पक्वाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The abdomen, the stomach.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व, and आशय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्वेष्टका
पक्वेष्टका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A burnt or baked brick.<BR>E.<BR>पक्व, and इष्टका a brick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पक्षति पक्षयति)<BR>1 To take or accept.<BR>2 To take a part or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष|पक्षः
पक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The half of a lunar month or fortnight, comprising fifteen days.<BR>2 A wing; (it is also neuter in this sense.)<BR>3 The feather of an arrow.<BR>4 A partisan.<BR>5 A friend.<BR>6 A side, a flank.<BR>7 An army, forces.<BR>8 A house.<BR>9 An argument, a thesis, a position advanced, doctrine to be maintained.<BR>10 Contradiction, opposition, rejoinder, reply.<BR>11 The subject of an inference.<BR>12 Alternative.<BR>13 A tribe, a class.<BR>14 The ash pit of a fire place.<BR>15 A royal elephant.<BR>16 (In composition with words signifying hair,) Quantity, as केशपक्ष much or abundant hair.<BR>17 A bird.<BR>18 A bracelet.<BR>19 Purity, perfection.<BR>20 A limb, a member.<BR>21 A tail.<BR>22 (In Arithmetic,) Side of an equation in a primary division.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष to take, aff. अच् or पण to transact business, Uṇādi aff. स, and क substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षक|पक्षकः
पक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A private or back door.<BR>2 A side.<BR>3 A sidesman, an associate, a confederate or partisan.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षचर|पक्षचरः
पक्षचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 An attendant, a constant companion.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, &c. चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षज|पक्षजः
पक्षज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in a fortnight, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षजन्मन्
पक्षजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and जन्मन् birth: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षता
पक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The nature or essential character of a proposition.<BR>2 The taking up a side or argument.<BR>3 Maintaining or defending a thesis.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पक्ष; also with त्व, पक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षति|पक्षतिः
पक्षति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 The first day of the half month.<BR>2 The root or insertion of a wing.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, &c. तिन् aff. and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वय
पक्षद्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A month.<BR>2 Both sides of an argument, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and द्वय two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षद्वार|पक्षद्वारं
पक्षद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A private entrance, an inner or back door.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a side, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षधर|पक्षधरः
पक्षधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what has a part or side, a wing, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 A partisan.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a half month, धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपात|पक्षपातः
पक्षपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Adopting a side or an argument whether right or wrong, partisanship.<BR>2 A partisan, an adherent, who or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">Page491</a>] what sides with.<BR>3 The moulting of birds considered to proceed from fever.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and पात who causes to go, or पक्ष a wing, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=490" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिता
पक्षपातिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Adherence, friendship, fellowship.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षपातिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, पक्षपातित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपातिन्
पक्षपातिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A partisan, a friend, an adherent.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षपात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षपालि|पक्षपालिः
पक्षपालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A private or back door.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a side, and पालि a point, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षभाग|पक्षभागः
पक्षभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The side or flank of an elephant.<BR>2 The side in general.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष the side, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षमूल|पक्षमूलं
पक्षमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root or articulation of a wing.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a wing, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवत्|पक्षवन्त्
पक्षवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Winged.<BR>2 Having a side or party.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षवाहन|पक्षवाहनः
पक्षवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a wing, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षविन्दु
पक्षविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a feather, and विन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षस
पक्षस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A wing.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष as above, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षसुन्दर|पक्षसुन्दरः
पक्षसुन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a part, सुन्दर handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाघात|पक्षाघातः
पक्षाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Refutation, confuting.<BR>2 Palsy, hemiplegia.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्त|पक्षांत|पक्षान्तः
पक्षान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The fifteenth and last day of either half month, new or full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षान्तर|पक्षांतर
पक्षान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Another side or part, another view of the argument.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षाभास|पक्षाभासः
पक्षाभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A seeming or fallacious argument.<BR>2 A false plaint.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and आभास semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षालु|पक्षालुः
पक्षालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a wing, आलुच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षावसर|पक्षावसरः
पक्षावसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The last day of either half month, new or full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, and अवसर conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिन्
पक्षिन्<BR>mf. (-क्षी-क्षिणी)<BR>A bird.<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>An arrow.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A night and two days.<BR>2 Day of full moon.<BR>3 A female fiend, also called Pūtanā.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a wing, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिपाणीयशालिका
पक्षिपाणीयशालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A trough for watering birds, cattle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षिन् a bird, पाणीय water, शाला a hall, and कन् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिराज
पक्षिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>King of the birds, usually applied to Garuḍa.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षिन्, and राज for राजा king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिल|पक्षिलः
पक्षिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of the saint VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष to take, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिशावक|पक्षिशावकः
पक्षिशावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A young bird.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षिन्, and शावक a young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिशाला
पक्षिशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A nest, an aviary.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षिन् a bird, शाला a hall or house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिसिंह|पक्षिसिंहः
पक्षिसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षि for पक्षिन् a bird, सिंह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षिस्वामिन्
पक्षिस्वामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>पक्षि, and स्वामिन् lord: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्षोद्ग्राहिन्
पक्षोद्ग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Showing partiality, taking a side.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and उद्ग्राहिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्णु|पक्ष्णुः
पक्ष्णु^1<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णुः-क्ष्णुः-क्ष्णु)<BR>Who or what cooks or matures.<BR>E.<BR>पच to ripen, स्नु aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20160315. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/252. note: 'zn' usually not possible. Confirm MW and other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्मन्
पक्ष्मन्<BR>n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>1 An eye-lash.<BR>2 The filament of a flower.<BR>3 The point of a thread.<BR>4 A wing.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष to take, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पक्ष्य|पक्ष्यः
पक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Produced or occurring in a fortnight.<BR>2 Belonging to a side, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क|पंक|पंकं|पंकः|पङ्कः
पङ्क<BR>mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्कं)<BR>1 Mud, mire, clay.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, aff. घञ् and च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्ककर्व्वट|पङ्ककर्वट|पङ्ककर्वटः|पङ्ककर्व्वटः
पङ्ककर्व्वट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Soft mud, especially such as is left by the retiring of floods, or on the banks of a river, a marsh, a quagmire.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, कर्व्वट the capital of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्ककीर|पंककीर|पङ्ककीरः
पङ्ककीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lap-wing.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and कीर a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कक्रीड|पंकक्रीड|पङ्कक्रीडः
पङ्कक्रीड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Wallowing, sporting in mud.<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A pig.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and क्रीड who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कगडक|पङ्कगडकः
पङ्कगडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small fish, (Macrognathus Pancalus, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and गडक another fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कगति|पङ्कगतिः
पङ्कगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The Pancāl fish: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कग्राह|पंकग्राह|पङ्कग्राहः
पङ्कग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Makara, a marine monster.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and ग्राह a shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कज|पंकज|पङ्कजं|पङ्कजः
पङ्कज<BR>n. (जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कजन्मन्|पंकजन्मन्
पङ्कजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and जन्मन् birth; also पङ्केज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कजिनी|पंकजिनी
पङ्कजिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A pool or pond where the lotus grows, or a place abounding with that flower.<BR>2 The flexible stalk of a water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्गज a lotus, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कण|पंकण|पंकणः|पङ्कणः
पङ्कण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The residence of the lowest and most impure tribes.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कता
पङ्कता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Muddiness, the nature or property of mud.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पङ्क; also with त्व, पङ्कत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कधूम
पङ्कधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>One of the divisions of hell.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कप्रभा
पङ्कप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A hell, the hell of mud or mire.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कभाज्
पङ्कभाज्<BR>mfn. (-क् or -ग्)<BR>Sunk in the mire.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क, and भाज् what shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कभारक
पङ्कभारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Muddy, laden with mud.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क, and भारक burthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कमण्डुक|पंकमंडुक|पङ्कमण्डुकः
पङ्कमण्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mire, मडि to ornament, aff. उक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्करुह्|पंकरुह्
पङ्करुह्<BR>n. (-रुट्)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, रुह to grow, aff. क्विप्; also with क aff. पङ्करुह n. (-हं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कवास|पंकवास|पङ्कवासः
पङ्कवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कशुक्ति|पङ्कशुक्तिः
पङ्कशुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A cockle.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, शुक्ति an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कसूरण
पङ्कसूरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, and सूरण a sort of root; also written पङ्कशूरण, and पङ्कसूरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्कार|पंकार|पंकारः|पङ्कारः
पङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An aquatick plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>2 A bridge or raised bank, forming a path amidst inundated fields.<BR>3 Stairs, steps.<BR>4 An aquatick plant, (Trapa bispinosa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, ऋ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्किल|पंकिल|पङ्किलः
पङ्किल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Muddy, clayey.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A boat, a canoe.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क mud, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्केज|पंकेज|पंकेजं|पङ्केजं
पङ्केज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्के in mud, and ज born; also पङ्कज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्केरुह|पंकेरुह|पङ्केरुहं|पङ्केरुहः
पङ्केरुह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्के in mud, and रुह what grows; also पङ्करुह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्ति|पंक्ति|पंक्तिः|पङ्क्तिः
पङ्क्ति<BR>f. (-ङ्क्तिः-ङ्क्ती)<BR>1 A line, a row or range.<BR>2 A sort of metre, a stanza of four lines, each line consisting of ten syllables.<BR>3 The number ten, (in composition, ut infra.)<BR>4 The earth.<BR>5 Fame, celebrity.<BR>6 Cooking, maturing.<BR>7 Associating with, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">Page492</a>] eating or sitting with, especially with persons of the same caste.<BR>8 A company, a society, an assembly.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, to extend, to make evident, and क्तिन् aff. or पच to cook, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=491" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिग्रीव|पंक्तिग्रीव|पङ्क्तिग्रीवः
पङ्क्तिग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क्ति ten, ग्रीवा a neck; the ten-necked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिचर|पंक्तिचर|पङ्क्तिचरः
पङ्क्तिचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ospray.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्कृ, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिदूषक|पंक्तिदूषक|पङ्क्तिदूषकः
पङ्क्तिदूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An improper person to associate with, an outcast.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्कृ, and दूषक who spoils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिपावन|पंक्तिपावन|पङ्क्तिपावनः
पङ्क्तिपावन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A respectable or eminent person.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्कृ, and पावन who purifies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्क्तिरथ|पंक्तिरथ|पङ्क्तिरथः
पङ्क्तिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>DAŚARATHA, the father of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>पङ्क्ति ten, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गु|पंगु|पङ्गुः
पङ्गु<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गुः-ङ्गुः-ङ्गु)<BR>Lame, crippled, halt, one who has lost his legs, &c.<BR>m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>The planet Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>पण to engage in business, उ aff., and अङ्गु substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुल|पंगुल|पङ्गुलः
पङ्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A horse of a glassy or silvery white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुग्राह|पंगुग्राह|पङ्गुग्राहः
पङ्गुग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>One of the signs of the zodiac: see मकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पङ्गुता
पङ्गुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Deformity, mutilation.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पङ्गु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
पच<BR>(डु, ष्) डुपचष् r. 1st cl. (पचति)<BR>To mature by cooking or ripening, to boil, to dress, to ripen;<BR>(इ) पचि r. 1st and 10th cls. (पंचति-ते पंचयति)<BR>1 To make evident or apparent.<BR>2 To represent, to state fully.<BR>3 To spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच|पचः
पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Who or what cooks, matures, &c.<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>Cooking, maturing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचक|पचकः
पचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्
पचत्<BR>mfn. (-चन्-चन्ती-चत्)<BR>Cooking, ripening.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, participial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत|पचतः
पचत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook or ripen, Uṇādi aff. अतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचतिकल्प|पचतिकल्पं
पचतिकल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) or adv. n. (-ल्पं)<BR>Almost cooked or ripened.<BR>E.<BR>पचति what cooks, and कल्प aff.; implying incompleteness; also in a similar sense पचतिदेश्य and पचतिदेशीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचत्पुट|पचत्पुटः
पचत्पुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A tree, (Hibiscus phæniceus.)<BR>E.<BR>पचत् here said to mean the sun, and पुट to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचन|पचनं|पचनः
पचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नी-नं)<BR>What books or matures, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cooking, dressing, boiling.<BR>2 Maturing.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, aff. युच् or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचमान|पचमानः
पचमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Cooking, in the act of cooking or ripening.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, &c. and शानच् aff., मुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचम्पचा|पचंपचा
पचम्पचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>A species of Curcuma, (C. zanthorhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, reiterated, अच् aff. and मुम् inserted; it is also read पचम्बचा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचा
पचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>Cooking, dressing, maturing, ripening.<BR>E.<BR>पच to dress, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचि|पचिः
पचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Cooking, maturing.<BR>E.<BR>पच to be cooked, (by it,) इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलिम|पचेलिमः
पचेलिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Fit to cook or ripen of itself.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>पच to dress or ripen, केलिमन् aff. of the reflective form, or Uṇādi aff. एलिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलुक|पचेलुकः
पचेलुक<BR>m. (कः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>पच, and एलुक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्छस्
पच्छस्<BR>ind.<BR>Foot by foot, or stanza by stanza.<BR>E.<BR>पत् for पाद, and शश् aff. of several orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पच्यमान|पच्यमानः
पच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being in the act of ripening. cooking &c.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पज्ज|पज्जः
पज्ज<BR>m. (-ज्जः)<BR>A Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>पत् for पाद a foot, and ज born, from the feet of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चक|पंचक|पञ्चकं|पञ्चकः
पञ्चक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Five or relating to five, made of five, bought with five, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Any collection or aggregate of five, a five.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A field of battle.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकपाल|पञ्चकपालः
पञ्चकपाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A particular ceremony in which ghee is offered in five cups.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, कपाल a concave piece of pottery skull-shaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकर्म्मन्|पञ्चकर्मन्|पंचकर्मन्
पञ्चकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Five actions of the body, vomiting, evacuation by bleeding or by stool, diseased excretion of fæces or purging, and blowing the nose.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, कर्म्मन् an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकृत्वस्|पंचकृत्वस्
पञ्चकृत्वस्<BR>ind.<BR>Five times.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and कृत्वसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोण|पंचकोण|पञ्चकोणः
पञ्चकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A pentagon.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and कोण an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोल|पंचकोल|पञ्चकोलं
पञ्चकोल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>The aggregate of five spices, viz. Long pepper, its root, Chai or Piper Cavya, Plumbago, and dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and कोल pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चकोषा
पञ्चकोषा<BR>m. plu. (-षाः)<BR>The five sheathes supposed to invest the soul, or the Annamaya koṣa that supported by food the gross form; the Prāṇamaya koṣa, the organs of action; the Manomaya koṣa, the organs of perception, with the manas or mind; the Vijñānamaya, the same with the Buddhi or intellect; and the Ānandamaya, consisting of the elements of identity and divine wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चखद्व
पञ्चखद्व<BR>nf. (-द्वं-द्वी)<BR>A collection of five beds.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and खद्वा bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगव|पंचगव|पञ्चगवं
पञ्चगव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A collection of five cows.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and गौ a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगवधन|पञ्चगवधनः
पञ्चगवधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having five cows.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चगव, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगव्य|पंचगव्य|पञ्चगव्यं
पञ्चगव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Five articles derived from the cow; milk, curds, clarified butter, cow's urine, and cow-dung.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and गव्य, from गौ a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुण|पंचगुण
पञ्चगुण<BR>mf. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Five times, five-fold.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and गुण multiplying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगुप्त|पंचगुप्त|पञ्चगुप्तः
पञ्चगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>1 A tortoise, a turtle.<BR>2 The atheistical system of the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, (members, &c.) गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चगो
पञ्चगो<BR>mfn. (-गौः-गौः-गु)<BR>Bought with five cows.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचामर|पञ्चचामरं
पञ्चचामर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A form of metre, in which the line contains sixteen syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचीर|पञ्चचीरः
पञ्चचीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Bauddha saint and legislator; also named MAÑJUGHOṢA, apparently the teacher of this doctrine in Nepal.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च spreading, चीर rags.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चचूडा
पञ्चचूडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>One of the nymphs of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and चूडा a top knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजन|पंचजन|पञ्चजनः
पञ्चजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Man in general, a man.<BR>2 The name of a demon, whose bones became the Conch, Pāñcajanya, the shell of KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of five persons.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, (elements,) and जन who is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चजनीन|पंचजनीन|पञ्चजनीनः
पञ्चजनीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An actor, a mimic, a buffoon.<BR>2 The chief of five men.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and जन a man, or पञ्चजन man, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=492" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चज्ञान|पंचज्ञान|पञ्चज्ञानः
पञ्चज्ञान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha sanctified teacher.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, (organs,) and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्|पंचत्
पञ्चत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्चत्)<BR>Five.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतक्ष|पंचतक्ष|पञ्चतक्षं
पञ्चतक्ष<BR>nf. (-क्षं-क्षी)<BR>An assemblage of five carpenters.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and तक्ष a carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतत्व|पंचतत्व
पञ्चतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 The five elements collectively.<BR>2 (In the Tantras,) The five essentials of certain rites; or wine, meat, fish, sexual intercourse, and mystic gesticulations.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and तत्व an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतन्मात्र|पञ्चतन्मात्रं
पञ्चतन्मात्र<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>The five subtile rudiments of the five elements.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and तन्मात्र element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतपस्|पंचतपस्
पञ्चतपस्<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>An ascetic, who, in the hot weather, sits amongst four fires, and has the sun for the fifth.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and तपस् penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतय|पंचतय|पञ्चतयं|पञ्चतयः
पञ्चतय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Having five parts or limbs.<BR>2 Five.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and तयप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चता|पंचता
पञ्चता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Death, dying, i. e. the separation of the five elements of whose aggregate the body consists.<BR>2 The nature or condition of five, the aggregate of five or five times.<BR>3 The five elements collectively, earth, air, fire, water, and Ākāśa.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चतीर्थी
पञ्चतीर्थी<BR>f. (-र्थी)<BR>1 Any five principal places of pilgrimage, especially Viśrānti, Saukara, Naimiṣa, Prayāga, and Puṣkara.<BR>2 Bathing on the day of the equinox.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and तीर्थ a shrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चत्व|पंचत्व|पंचत्वं|पञ्चत्वं
पञ्चत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Death.<BR>2 The state or being of five.<BR>3 The coexistence of the five elements.<BR>3 An aggregate, &c. of five.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and त्व aff.: see पञ्चता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चथु|पंचथु|पंचथुः|पञ्चथुः
पञ्चथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 The Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदश|पंचदश|पञ्चदशः
पञ्चदश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Fifteen or fifteenth.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The fifteenth day of a half month, full or new moon.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, दशन् ten, aff. डत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदशन्|पंचदशन्
पञ्चदशन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-श)<BR>Fifteen.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चदीर्घ|पंचदीर्घ|पञ्चदीर्घं
पञ्चदीर्घ<BR>m. (-र्घः)<BR>Marks on five parts of the body, the arms, eyes, belly, nose, and breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चधा|पंचधा
पञ्चधा<BR>ind.<BR>In five ways, five-fold.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चन् five, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चन्|पंचन्
पञ्चन्<BR>mfn. plu. (-ञ्च)<BR>Five.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, Uṇādi aff. अन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनख|पंचनख|पञ्चनखः
पञ्चनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A tortoise.<BR>3 A tiger.<BR>4 Any animal having five toes or claws.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A lizard.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, नख nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनद|पंचनद|पञ्चनदः
पञ्चनद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The Panjab, or country of five rivers, viz. the Śatadru, Vipāśā, Irāvatī, Candrabhāgā and Vitastā.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, नदी a river, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनिम्ब|पञ्चनिम्बं
पञ्चनिम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>Five parts of the Nimb tree; the flowers, fruit, leaves, bark, and root.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and निम्ब the Nimb, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनी|पंचनी
पञ्चनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A chequered cloth for playing at draughts, chess, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, नी to get, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चनीराजन|पंचनीराजन|पञ्चनीराजनं
पञ्चनीराजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Waving four things before an idol; a lamp, a lotus, cloth, a mango or betel leaf, and then falling prostrate.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and नीराजन presentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपञ्चनख
पञ्चपञ्चनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Five kinds of animals allowed to be killed and eaten, the hare, porcupine, alligator, rhinoceros, and tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and पञ्चनख a five-toed animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपल्लव|पञ्चपल्लवं
पञ्चपल्लव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The aggregate of five sprouts; viz. of the spondias, rose-apple, Bel or marmelos, citron, and wood-apple.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and पल्लव a new shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपर्णी
पञ्चपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A small shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चपाच
पञ्चपाच<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Five plates collectively.<BR>2 A Śrāddha in which offerings are made in five vessels.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्रसाद|पंचप्रसाद
पञ्चप्रसाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A temple with four pinnacles and a steeple.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and प्रसाद a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चप्राण|पंचप्राण
पञ्चप्राण<BR>m. plu. (-णाः)<BR>The five airs supposed to be in the body, and necessary to life.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and प्राण vital air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चबन्ध|पञ्चबन्धः
पञ्चबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A fine equal to the fifth part of any thing lost or stolen.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभद्र|पञ्चभद्रः
पञ्चभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 A horse with five auspicious marks; or spotted on the chest, back, face, and flanks.<BR>2 A sauce or condiment of five vegetables.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and मद्र fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभूत|पंचभूत|पञ्चभूतं
पञ्चभूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The five elements; earth, air, fire, water, Ākāśa.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and भूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चभूतात्मन्
पञ्चभूतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>Man as formed of the five elements.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चभूत, and आत्मन् one with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चम|पंचम|पञ्चमं|पञ्चमः
पञ्चम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>1 Fifth.<BR>2 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>3 Dexterous, clever.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 One of the seven musical notes; the seventh, called Pañcama, from being said to be formed by air drawn from five places; the navel, the breast, the heart, throat, and forehead.<BR>2 One of the Rāgas or modes of music.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the five Pāṇḍus.<BR>2 A chequered cloth for playing at draughts, &c. a chess board.<BR>3 The fifth day of a half month.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चन् five, and डट् aff. with मट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमकार|पंचमकार|पञ्चमकारं
पञ्चमकार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The five essentials of the left hand Tantra ritual; Madya wine, Māṃsa flesh, Matsya fish, Maithuna copulation, Mudrā gesticulation.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and मकार the letter M,; all beginning with that letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमवत्|पञ्चमवन्त्
पञ्चमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having the fifth of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमहायज्ञ|पंचमहायज्ञ
पञ्चमहायज्ञ<BR>m. plu. (-ज्ञाः)<BR>The five great sacraments of the Hindus, or the worship of spirits, progenitors, gods, Vedas, and mankind, by offerings of perfumes and flowers, obsequial rites, oblations with fire, the study of the Vedas, and hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, महा great, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमार|पञ्चमारः
पञ्चमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of BALADEVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमाषिक
पञ्चमाषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of five Māṣas, relating to, worth, amounting to five Māṣas.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, माष a measure of silver, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमास्य|पंचमास्य|पञ्चमास्यः
पञ्चमास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चम the musical note, and आस्य mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमिन्|पंचमिन्
पञ्चमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Being in the fifth year of one's age.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुख|पंचमुख|पञ्चमुखः
पञ्चमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमुद्रा
पञ्चमुद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Five gestures to be made in the usual presentation of offerings to an idol.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and मुद्रा gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूत्र|पञ्चमूत्रं
पञ्चमूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The urine of the cow, goat, sheep, buffalo, and ass.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and मूत्र urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=493" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चमूल|पञ्चमूलं
पञ्चमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The assemblage of five roots, the Bel, Premna longifolia, Cassia, Gmelina arborea, and the Trumpet flower.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A similar aggregate of five roots, considered as the smaller one, viz. Hedysarum gangeticum, H. lagopodioides, Solanum melongena, S. jacquini, and Tribulus lanuginosus.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, मूल a root; the fem. aff. has a diminutive import.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चयज्ञ
पञ्चयज्ञ<BR>m. plu. (-ज्ञाः)<BR>The five rites of a house-keeper: see पञ्चमहायज्ञ.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and यज्ञ a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरत्न|पंचरत्न|पञ्चरत्नं
पञ्चरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A collection of five precious objects; or gold, a diamond, a pearl, a ruby, an amethyst.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चरसा
पञ्चरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, रस flavour, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलक्षण|पंचलक्षण|पञ्चलक्षणं
पञ्चलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A Purāṇa or mythological poem.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and लक्षण a mark; a Purāṇa should comprehend five topics; the creation of worlds, their destruction and renovation, the genealogy of gods and heroes, the reigns of the MANUS, and the actions of their descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलवण|पंचलवण|पञ्चलवणं
पञ्चलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Five kinds of salt.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलाङ्गलक|पञ्चलाङ्गलकं
पञ्चलाङ्गलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gift of land to the extent requiring five ploughs.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, लाङ्गल a plough, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चलोह|पञ्चलोहं
पञ्चलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A metallic alloy containing five metals; copper, brass, tin, lead, and iron.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवक्त्र|पंचवक्त्र|पञ्चवक्त्रः
पञ्चवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवट|पञ्चवटः
पञ्चवट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The Brahminical thread as worn across the breast; also पञ्चावट.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 Five trees, the Indian and holy fig, the Bel, Grislea tomentosa, and Asoka, placed or planted in several quarters; or east, west, north, south and south-east.<BR>2 Part of the great southern forest where the Godāvarī rises.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and वट the Indian fig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवर्ग|पञ्चवर्गः
पञ्चवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A class of five persons or things.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवल्कल|पंचवल्कल|पञ्चवल्कलं
पञ्चवल्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A collection of the bark of five trees, the Indian and the holy fig, the opposite-leaved fig, the wavy-leaved fig, and a sort of reed; other trees are sometimes taken.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and वल्कल a bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चवाण|पंचवाण|पञ्चवाणः
पञ्चवाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>KĀMADEVA, the Indian Cupid.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and वाण an arrow; being armed with five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशर|पंचशर|पञ्चशरः
पञ्चशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and शर an arrow: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशाख|पंचशाख|पञ्चशाखः
पञ्चशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The hand.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, शाखा a branch, the five-fingered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशिख|पंचशिख|पञ्चशिखः
पञ्चशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 The name of a Muni, the son of DHARMA by HIṂSĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च spreading, शिखा a crest or mane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चशैरिषक
पञ्चशैरिषक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The bark of five trees.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and शिरीष Mimosa sirisha, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चष|पंचष
पञ्चष<BR>mfn. plu. (-षाः-षाः-षाणि)<BR>Five or six.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and षष् six, with डच्. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसुगन्धक|पञ्चसुगन्धकं
पञ्चसुगन्धक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The aggregate of five aromatic vegetable substances; cloves, nutmeg, camphor, aloe wood, and Kakkola.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, सुगन्ध fragrance, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चसूना|पंचसूना
पञ्चसूना<BR>m. plu. (-नाः)<BR>The five things in a house by which animal life may be accidentally destroyed; the fire place, the slab on which condiments are ground, the broom, the pestle and mortar, and the waterpot.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and सूना place of slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाग्नि|पंचाग्नि|पञ्चाग्निः
पञ्चाग्नि<BR>n. (-ग्नि)<BR>1 A collection of five fires, amidst which a devotee performs penance during the summer season; or four fires lighted severally to the north, south, east and west, and the sun over head.<BR>2 Five mystic fires, supposed to be present in the body.<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 A householder who maintains five fires, or the domestic one, and one for warming visitors in addition to the other three.<BR>2 One who is acquainted with the doctrine of the five mystic fires.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्ग|पंचांग|पञ्चाङ्गं|पञ्चाङ्गः
पञ्चाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Having five limbs or members, five parts or subdivisions, consisting of five things, &c.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Any aggregate of five parts or five things.<BR>3 Five modes of devotion or silent prayer, burnt offering, libations, bathing idols, and feeding Brahmans.<BR>3 An almanac describing solar days, lunar days, and the periods of asterisms, Yogas and Karaṇas.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A tortoise.<BR>2 A horse: see पञ्चभद्र.<BR>3 Reverence by extending the hands, bending the knees and head, and in speech and look.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गगुप्त|पंचांगगुप्त|पञ्चाङ्गगुप्तः
पञ्चाङ्गगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, अङ्ग limb, and गुप्त hidden; covering his head and legs beneath his shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुल|पंचांगुल|पञ्चाङ्गुलः
पञ्चाङ्गुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>Measuring five fingers.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The castor-oil plant.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, अङ्गुलि a finger, aff. अच्: the leaves having five lobes compared to fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाङ्गुलि|पञ्चाङ्गुलिः
पञ्चाङ्गुलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Having five fingers, or finger-like divisions.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चातपा
पञ्चातपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>Doing penance with five fires, or four fires and the sun.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and आतप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चानन|पंचानन|पञ्चाननः
पञ्चानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Very passionate.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five or spreading, आनन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चामृत|पंचामृत|पञ्चामृतं
पञ्चामृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A mixture of milk, curds, sugar, ghee, and honey.<BR>2 The aggregate of any five drugs of supposed efficacy.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and अमृत ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्नाय|पञ्चाम्नायः
पञ्चाम्नाय<BR>m. plu. (-याः)<BR>Five Śāstras supposed to have proceeded from the five mouths of ŚIVA, constituting the basis of the Tantra ritual.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and आम्नाय a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाम्ल|पञ्चाम्लं
पञ्चाम्ल<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>The aggregate of five acid plants; the jujube, pomegranate, sorrel, spondias, and citron.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चारी
पञ्चारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A chequered cloth for playing draughts upon: see पञ्चाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चार्च्चिस्|पञ्चार्चिस्|पंचार्चिस्
पञ्चार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>The planet Mercury.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, अर्च्चिस् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाल|पंचाल|पञ्चालः
पञ्चाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A country in the north of India.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A chequered cloth for playing at draughts, &c.<BR>2 A doll, a puppet.<BR>3 A style of singing.<BR>E.<BR>पचि to spread, Uṇādi aff. कालच्; also with कन् added पञ्चालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावट|पञ्चावटं|पंचावटः|पञ्चावटः
पञ्चावट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The sacrificial cord, as worn crossed upon the breast, the ends hanging over the shoulders.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च spreading, वट to surround, aff. अच्, आङ् prefixed to the root; also पञ्चवट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चावस्थ|पंचावस्थ|पञ्चावस्थः
पञ्चावस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A corpse.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, (elements,) अवस्था state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चाशत्|पंचाशत्
पञ्चाशत्<BR>f. (-शत्)<BR>Fifty.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, with शत् aff. and आ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चास्य|पंचास्य|पञ्चास्यः
पञ्चास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च spreading, and आस्य a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेन्द्रिय|पंचेंद्रिय|पञ्चेन्द्रियं
पञ्चेन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 The five organs of sense; the eye, ear, nose, tongue, and skin; or those of action, as hands, feet, windpipe, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">Page495</a>] anus, and parts of generation.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=494" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चेषु|पंचेषु|पञ्चेषुः
पञ्चेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>A name of KĀMADEVA, the Hindū Cupid.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च five, इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्चोष्मन्|पंचोष्मन्
पञ्चोष्मन्<BR>m. plu. (-ष्माणः)<BR>The five digestive fires supposed to be in the body.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, and उष्मन् heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जर|पंजर|पंजरं|पञ्जरं|पञ्जरः
पञ्जर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>A skeleton.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A cage, an aviary, a dovecot.<BR>2 The ribs.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 The Kali age.<BR>E.<BR>पजि for पिजि to dwell, &c. Uṇādi aff., अरच्; also पिञ्जर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जराखेट|पंजराखेट|पञ्जराखेटः
पञ्जराखेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of basket or wicker trap in which fish are caught.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्जर a cage, आखेट hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जि|पंजि|पंजिः|पञ्जिः
पञ्जि<BR>f. (-ञ्जिः-ञ्जी)<BR>1 The ball or whisp of cotton from which thread is spun.<BR>2 A journal, a register.<BR>3 An almanack.<BR>E.<BR>पजि for पिजि to touch, &c. aff. इन् and ङीष् optionally added; also पिञ्जि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जिका|पंजिका
पञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The ball or skein of cotton, from which the thread is spun: see the last.<BR>2 A perpetual commentary.<BR>3 A calendar, an almanack.<BR>4 A journal, a register.<BR>5 The register or journal of YAMA, the record of human actions.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to पञ्जि; also पिञ्जिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जिकाकारक|पञ्जिकाकारकः
पञ्जिकाकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A writer, a man of the Kāyastha tribe.<BR>2 An almanack-maker.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्जिका a journal, &c. and कारक. who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पञ्जीकर|पञ्जीकरः
पञ्जीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Kāyastha or scribe.<BR>2 An almanack-maker.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्जी a journal, &c. कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट|पटं|पटः
पट<BR>r. 1st cl. (पटति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पटयति)<BR>1 To string.<BR>2 To surround or encompass.<BR>3 To share, to portion, to distribute.<BR>(पाटयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>With उत् prefixed,<BR>To pluck up, to eradicate, to destroy utterly.<BR>With वि,<BR>To fly, to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट|पटं|पटः
पट<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>1 Fine cloth.<BR>2 Coloured cloth.<BR>3 A leaf or sheet of cloth, &c. on which any figures may be painted.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A kind of tree: see पियाल.<BR>2 Any thing well made or polished.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A particular sort of cloth, coarse thick cloth, canvas.<BR>2 A screen of cloth surrounding a tent, an outer tent.<BR>3 A coloured or chintz garment.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A thatch, a roof.<BR>E.<BR>पट to surround, aff. अच् fem. aff. ङीप्: see पटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटक|पटकः
पटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A camp, an encampment.<BR>E.<BR>पट to surround, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटकार|पटकारः
पटकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, and कार maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटकुटि
पटकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, कुटि a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटच्चर|पटच्चरं|पटच्चरः
पटच्चर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Old cloth.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>पटत् imitative sound, and चर going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटमण्डप|पटमंडप|पटमण्डपः
पटमण्डप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, and मण्डप a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटमय|पटमयं|पटमयः
पटमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of cloth.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A tent, a canvas house.<BR>2 A petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटल|पटलं|पटलः
पटल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A heap, a number, a quantity or multitude.<BR>mf. (-लं-ली)<BR>1 A book.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 A stalk.<BR>nf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A roof, a thatch.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A cover, a coat, an enclosing or surrounding skin or membrane.<BR>2 A place, a spot, a circle or district.<BR>3 A mark on the forehead with Sandal wood.<BR>4 A basket.<BR>5 Train, retinue.<BR>6 A coat of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटलप्रान्त|पटलप्रांत|पटलप्रान्तं|पटलप्रान्तः
पटलप्रान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The edge of a thatch.<BR>E.<BR>पटल a thatch, and प्रान्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवाप|पटवापः
पटवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, and वाप what is woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवास|पटवासः
पटवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A tent.<BR>2 A petticoat.<BR>3 Perfumed powder.<BR>E.<BR>पट cloth, वास abode, or वास to perfume, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवासक|पटवासकः
पटवासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Perfumed powder.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटवेश्मन्
पटवेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पट, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटह|पटहं|पटहः
पटह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>A kettle-drum.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A war-drum, or one used in battle.<BR>2 Injury, killing, slaughter.<BR>3 Tumult.<BR>E.<BR>पट imitative sound, हा to quit or make, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटाक|पटाकः
पटाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flag, a banner.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटालुका
पटालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, आलुच् aff., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटि|पटिः
पटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>1 A kind of cloth.<BR>2 An aquatick plant: see कुम्भिका.<BR>E.<BR>पट to surround, &c. aff. इन्: see पट and पटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटिका
पटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cloth.<BR>E.<BR>वुन् added to पटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटिष्ठ|पटिष्ठः
पटिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very clever.<BR>E.<BR>पटु and irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटीयस्
पटीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very clever or able.<BR>E.<BR>पटु clever, ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटीर|पटीरं|पटीरः
पटीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Sandal-wood.<BR>2 A field.<BR>3 Bambu manna.<BR>4 A radish.<BR>5 The belly.<BR>6 A sieve.<BR>7 Height.<BR>8 Khayar.<BR>9 Rheumatism.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 KANDARPA.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, Uṇādi aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटु|पटुः
पटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-ट्वी-टु)<BR>1 Clever, dexterous, skilful.<BR>2 Diligent.<BR>3 Smart, sharp.<BR>4 Hale, healthy.<BR>5 Warm, hot.<BR>6 Blown, expanded.<BR>7 Cruel, ferocious, unmerciful, unfeeling.<BR>8 Harsh, contumelious, (speech, &c.)<BR>9 Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or cheat.<BR>10 Loquacious, talkative.<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 A small kind of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>2 The leaf of the Trichosanthes.<BR>n. (-टु)<BR>1 Salt.<BR>2 A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>पाट r. 10th cl. to speak, &c. Uṇādi aff. डु, and the radical vowel short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुक|पटुकः
पटुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of gourd.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुकल्प|पटुकल्पः
पटुकल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Not so clever, a little less able, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पटु clever, and कल्प aff. of incompleteness; also in a similar sense पटुदेश्य, and पटुदेशीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुजातीय|पटुजातीयः
पटुजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of a clever sort, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पटु as above, and जातीय aff. of kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुत्व|पटुत्वं
पटुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Cleverness.<BR>2 Eloquence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व, added to पटु; also with तल्, पटुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुपर्णी
पटुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A medicinal sort of moon plant.<BR>E.<BR>पटु a sort of gourd, and पर्ण a leaf, fem. aff. ङीष्^1; also पटुपचक (-कं) and पटुपचिका f. (-का)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटुरूप
पटुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Very clever.<BR>E.<BR>पटु, and रूप here implying much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोटज|पटोटजं
पटोटज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पट, and उटज a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोल|पटोलं|पटोलः
पटोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, commonly Palwal, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of cloth, a kind of chintz.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A small cucumber, either the same as above, (Trichosanthes dioeca,) or another kind, (Luffa acutangula.)<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, in the causal form, aff. ओलच्; removing malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोलक|पटोलकः
पटोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An oyster.<BR>E.<BR>पटोल as above, and कन् aff. of resemblance, compared to the shape of the Trichosanthes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=495" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पटोलिका
पटोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca); it is also applied to Luffa acutangula.<BR>E.<BR>कन् with the fem. form added to पटोली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्ट|पट्टं|पट्टः
पट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 Cloth.<BR>2 Coloured cloth.<BR>3 Wove silk.<BR>4 A turban, &c. or cloth for that purpose.<BR>5 A coloured silk turban.<BR>6 A fillet bound round the head.<BR>7 A bandage, a ligature, a cloth bound round a sore, &c.<BR>8 An upper or outer garment.<BR>9 A plant, commonly called Pāt, (Corchorus olitorius,) from the fibres of the bark of which, called Jute, a coarse sack-cloth and cordage are prepared.<BR>10 A stone for grinding with a mullar.<BR>11 A plate of metal for inscription or engraving.<BR>12 A royal grant or order written on copper, stone, &c.<BR>13 A shield.<BR>14 A place where four roads meet.<BR>15 A chair, a stool.<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>A city, a town, a village, the Pettah probably of the south.<BR>f. (-ट्टा)<BR>1 An ornament of the forehead.<BR>2 Red Lodh.<BR>3 A horse's girth.<BR>E.<BR>पट to surround, क्त aff. and त changed to ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टक|पट्टकः
पट्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cloth, a bandage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टज|पट्टजं
पट्टज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A sort of cloth, probably a kind of canvas or sackcloth.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ठ as above, and ज produced; made from Jute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टन|पट्टनं
पट्टन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A city: see पत्तन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टदेवी
पट्टदेवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A principal queen.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट a fillet or tiara, देवी a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टबन्धन
पट्टबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Crowning, binding the head with a fillet or tiara.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टमहिषी
पट्टमहिषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>A principal queen.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट a fillet or tiara, and महिषी a queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टरङ्ग|पट्टरङ्गं
पट्टरङ्ग<BR>n. (ङ्गं)<BR>A plant used in dying, (Coesalpinia sappan.)<BR>E.<BR>पटृ cloth, and रङ्ग what colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टरञ्जन
पट्टरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sappan wood.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट cloth, and रञ्जन colouring; also with कन् added पट्टरञ्जनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टशाक|पट्टशाकं
पट्टशाक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A sort of potherb, commonly also Nālita or Lalita, (Corchorus capsularis.)<BR>E.<BR>पटृ Corchorus, and शाक potherb; the leaves resembling those of the Pāt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टारोहा
पट्टारोहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A principal queen.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट, and आरोह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिका
पट्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red Lodh.<BR>E.<BR>पट्टी the same, कन् added: again with आख्या a name; it is read also पट्टिकाख्य, mf. (-ख्यः-ख्या)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिन्
पट्टिन्<BR>m. (-ट्टी)<BR>Red Lodh; also पट्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिल|पट्टिलः
पट्टिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Coesalpinia bonduccella.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिलोध्र|पट्टिलोध्रः
पट्टिलोध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A sort of tree, the bark of which is used as an astringent; the red species of the Lodh, (Symplocos racemosa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पट्टी the same plant, लोध्र the Lodh; also with कन् added पट्टिलोध्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टिश|पट्टिशः
पट्टिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A sort of weapon, a kind of axe.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, aff. टिश or टिस; whence it is also read पट्टिस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पट्टोलिका
पट्टोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A title deed, a Paṭṭa, a lease, &c.<BR>2 A written legal opinion.<BR>E.<BR>पट्ट a royal mandate, &c. ओलच् aff., कन् in the fem. form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठ|पठः
पठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (पठति)<BR>To speak articulately, to declaim, to recite or read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठत्
पठत्<BR>mfn. (-ठन्-ठन्ती-ठत्)<BR>Reading, reciting.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, शतृ part. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठन|पठनं
पठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reading, reciting.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठनीय
पठनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Readable, to be read.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठमञ्जरी
पठमञ्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A Rāgiṇī, one of the wives of ŚRĪRĀGA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठि|पठिः
पठि<BR>f. (-ठिः-ठी)<BR>Reading, perusal.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, aff. इन्, ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठित|पठितः
पठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Read, studied.<BR>2 Recited, repeated.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितव्य|पठितव्यं
पठितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be read, what may or ought to be read.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठितृ
पठितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Reading, reciting, a reader.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पठ्यमान
पठ्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being read or recited.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पड
पड<BR>(इ,) पडि r. 1st cl. (पण्डते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cl. (पण्डति पण्डयति)<BR>1 To destroy, to annihilate.<BR>2 To heap together, to accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण|पणः
पण<BR>r. 1st cl. (पणते) also 10th cl. (पणयति)<BR>To negociate, to treat or transact business.<BR>(पणयति)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण|पणः
पण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Measure of account, in cowries or shells, twenty gandas or eighty cowries; also a weight of copper of similar value.<BR>2 Wages or hire.<BR>2 A stake at play, a bet, a wager.<BR>4 Gaming, playing.<BR>5 Playing with dice.<BR>6 Price.<BR>7 Wealth, property.<BR>8 A commodity for sale.<BR>9 Business.<BR>10 A distiller.<BR>11 A house, a dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>पण to do business, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणग्रन्थि|पणग्रंथि|पणग्रन्थिः
पणग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>A fair, a market.<BR>E.<BR>पण a commodity, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणता
पणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The state or condition of a pledge or stake.<BR>2 Price, value.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पण; also with त्व, पणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणन|पणनं
पणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sale, selling.<BR>2 Betting.<BR>E.<BR>पण to do business, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणव|पणवः
पणव<BR>mf. (-वः-वा)<BR>A sort of musical instrument; a small drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>पण business or price, वा to sound, aff. क, it is also प्रणव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणस|पणसः
पणस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A commodity, an article of sale or traffick.<BR>E.<BR>पण to do business, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाङ्गना|पणांगना
पणाङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A prostitute, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>पण price, अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणाया
पणाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Business, affair, transaction, buying and selling, &c.<BR>2 Profits or receipts of trade.<BR>3 A market place.<BR>E.<BR>पण to negociate, in the causal form, अच् and टाप् affs. or पण and अय income, it also occurs mas. (-यः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणायित|पणायितः
पणायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Praised.<BR>2 Transacted.<BR>E.<BR>पण to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणार्पण
पणार्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Agreement, engagement, contract.<BR>E.<BR>पण price, अर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणास्थि
पणास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>The small shell used as coin, a Cowri.<BR>E.<BR>पण business, and अस्थि a bone; also with कन् added पणास्थि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणित|पणितं
पणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Praised.<BR>2 Transacted as business.<BR>E.<BR>पण to praise, aff. क्त; also पणायित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पणितव्य|पणितव्यं
पणितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Vendible, fit or intended for sale.<BR>2 To be transacted, negotiable^1.<BR>3 To be praised.<BR>E.<BR>पण to deal, aff. तव्य.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्ड|पंड|पंडः|पण्डः
पण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 A catamite.<BR>2 A eunuch.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 Wisdom, understanding.<BR>2 Science, learning.<BR>E.<BR>पडि to go, aff. अच्, or पण to deal, Uṇādi aff. ड; also with कन added पण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=496" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डापूर्व्व|पण्डापूर्व|पण्डापूर्व्वं
पण्डापूर्व्व<BR>n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>Non-occurrence of the results of fate or destiny.<BR>E.<BR>पण्ड, and अपूर्व्व unprecedented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डित|पंडित|पण्डितः
पण्डित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A scholar, a teacher, a Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman, or one read in sacred science, and teaching it to his disciples.<BR>2 Incense.<BR>E.<BR>पण्डा learning, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितम्मन्य|पण्डितंमन्य|पंडितंमन्य|पण्डितम्मन्यः
पण्डितम्मन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>An ignorant and vain person, a pedant, one who thinks himself a Paṇḍita or scholar.<BR>E.<BR>पण्डित learned, मन to think, खश aff.; also with णिनि aff. पण्डितमानिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितमानिन्
पण्डितमानिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>An arrogant and ignorant man: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्डितायमान
पण्डितायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Become wise from a state of ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>पण्डित used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्य|पण्यं|पण्यः
पण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>1 To be sold, saleable, vendible.<BR>2 To be praised.<BR>3 To be transacted as business.<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>Heart pea: see पिण्या.<BR>E.<BR>पण to deal, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यफलत्व
पण्यफलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Prosperity in trade, profit.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य, and फलत्व fruitfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यमूल्य
पण्यमूल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>The price of a commodity.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य, and मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथिका
पण्यवीथिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A stall, a shop, a place of sale.<BR>2 A market.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य vendible, and वीथी a shop, &c. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यवीथी
पण्यवीथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>1 A stall, &c.<BR>2 A market: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यशाला
पण्यशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A market.<BR>2 A shop, a ware-room.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य vendible, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यस्त्री
पण्यस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य vendible, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याङ्गना|पण्यांगना
पण्याङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A prostitute, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य to be sold, अङ्गना a woman; also पणाङ्गना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजीव|पण्याजीवः
पण्याजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A trader.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A market, a fair.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य a vendible, and आजीव a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्याजीवक|पण्याजीवकं
पण्याजीवक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A market.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last; also पण्यजीवकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पण्यार्ह
पण्यार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Saleable, vendible.<BR>E.<BR>पण्य, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत|पतं|पतः
पत<BR>(ऌ) पतॢ r. 1st cl. (पतति) r. 10th cl. (पतयति or पातयति)<BR>1 To go, to move, but especially downwards; as, to fall, to descend, to alight.<BR>2 To possess supreme or superhuman power.<BR>r. 4th cl. (पत्यते)<BR>To be rich or powerful.<BR>With अति prefixed,<BR>To excel or surpass.<BR>With अभि or अव,<BR>To descend.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To arrive, to come.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To ascend.<BR>With नि,<BR>To gain or get.<BR>2 To happen.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To abscond.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To go fast.<BR>3 To be valuable.<BR>With प्र and नि,<BR>To fall prostrate, to salute, to worship.<BR>With वि and निर्,<BR>To turn, to turn back.<BR>With सम्,<BR>1 To go with.<BR>2 To gain.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To purify or cleanse.<BR>With सम् and उत्,<BR>To fly.<BR>With सम् and नि,<BR>To go forth or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत|पतं|पतः
पत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished, protected.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Falling, alighting.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, अच् aff. or a various reading of पात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतक|पतकः
पतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Who or what falls, descends, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astronomical table.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, to go, वुन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतग|पतगः
पतग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, Uṇādi aff. अगच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्ग|पतंग|पतङ्गं|पतंगः|पतङ्गः
पतङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A grasshopper.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 A sort of rice.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>2 A kind of Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>पत falling, गम to proceed, aff. खच्; or पत to fall, अङ्गच् Uṇādi aff.; also पतङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गम|पतंगम|पतंगमः|पतङ्गमः
पतङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A grasshopper.<BR>E.<BR>पत, and गम what goes: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतङ्गिका|पतंगिका
पतङ्गिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of bee.<BR>E.<BR>कन् implying resemblance, with the fem. form added to पतङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्चिका|पतंचिका
पतञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतञ्जलि|पतंजलि|पतंजलिः|पतञ्जलिः
पतञ्जलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 The name of a saint or Muni and teacher of the Yoga philosophy, thence called after him PĀTAÑJALA; also the author of the Mahābhāṣya or commentary on PĀṆINI.<BR>2 A name of the poet VARARUCI.<BR>E.<BR>पत falling, अञ्जलि the hands joined as a mark of respect; having fallen from heaven, it is said, in the shape of a small snake, into the hands of the saint PĀṆINI as he was performing this act of reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्|पतन्त्
पतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>Falling, coming down, alighting, &c.<BR>m. (-तन्)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, to alight, participial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्र|पतत्त्रं|पतत्रं
पतत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A wing.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, अचन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रि|पतत्रिः
पतत्रि<BR>m. (-त्रिः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, अत्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिन्
पतत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पतत्र a wing, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतत्रिराज|पतत्रिराजः
पतत्रिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>VIṢṆU'S bird, Garuḍa.<BR>E.<BR>पतत्रिन्, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्ग्रह|पतद्ग्रहः
पतद्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A spitting pot.<BR>2 The reserve of an army.<BR>E.<BR>पतत् what falls, and ग्रह what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतद्भीरु|पतद्भीरुः
पतद्भीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A hawk, a falcon.<BR>E.<BR>पतत्^1 a bird, and भीरु fearful.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321. note: Stray accent in print, coded as a4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतन|पतनं
पतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Who or what goes, falls, descends, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Falling.<BR>2 Alighting, descending.<BR>3 Falling from dignity, virtue, &c.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>5 Going.<BR>6 Substraction.<BR>7 The latitude of a planet.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, युच् or ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतम|पतमः
पतम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 A grasshopper.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, अमच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतयालु|पतयालुः
पतयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Falling, liable or accustomed to fall.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, &c. in the causal form, आलुच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतस|पतसः
पतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A caterpillar.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताका
पताका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A flag or banner.<BR>2 A flagstaff.<BR>3 An emblem carried as an ensign or banner, a symbol, a sign.<BR>4 A mark.<BR>5 An episode, or episodical incident in a drama.<BR>6 Good fortune, auspiciousness.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, आकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पताकिन्
पताकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 An ensign, a standard bearer.<BR>2 A scheme for casting a nativity.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An army.<BR>E.<BR>पताका a flag, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतापत
पतापत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Who or what goes, &c. much or frequently. पत to go, अच् aff. repeated, and आच् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पति|पतिः
पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A master, an owner.<BR>2 A husband.<BR>3 A root.<BR>4 Going, motion.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, Uṇādi aff. डति, or पत to go, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघ्नी
पतिघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 The murderess of her husband.<BR>2 A line on the hand, indicating that a woman will be faithless or treacherous to her husband.<BR>E.<BR>पति a husband, and घ्न who kills, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिघ्नीलक्षण
पतिघ्नीलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sign of a murderess of a husband.<BR>E.<BR>पतिघ्नी, and अक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=497" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित|पतितः
पतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fallen, alighted.<BR>2 Fallen from virtue, wicked, abandoned.<BR>3 Fallen in war, defeated, overthrown.<BR>4 Degraded, outcaste.<BR>5 Gone.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितसावित्रीक|पतितसावित्रीकः
पतितसावित्रीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of the first three classes, whose investiture has not been duly performed.<BR>E.<BR>पतित, and सावित्री the mystical verse, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितेक्षित
पतितेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Looked at by an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>पतित, and ईक्षित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतितोत्पन्न
पतितोत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Born of an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>पतित, and उत्पन्न born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्व|पतित्वं
पतित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The conjugal state.<BR>E.<BR>पति, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतित्वा
पतित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having fallen or fallen down, having alighted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिप्राणा
पतिप्राणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A faithful wife.<BR>E.<BR>पति, and प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिम्वरा
पतिम्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A bride choosing her husband.<BR>2 A pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>पति a husband, वृ to choose, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिवत्नी
पतिवत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A married woman, a wife whose husband is living.<BR>E.<BR>पति a husband, मतुप् aff., fem. form irr., नुक् being inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिव्रता
पतिव्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A good and virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>पति a husband, व्रत a religious obligation; who never violates her marriage vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतिसेवा
पतिसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Devotion to a husband.<BR>E.<BR>पति, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतीयन्ती|पतीयंती
पतीयन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A woman wishing or fit for a husband.<BR>E.<BR>पति, and क्यच् added, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतेर|पतेरः
पतेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Going, moving, one who goes or moves.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 An Arhaka, a measure so called.<BR>3 A hole.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्काषिन्
पत्काषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Pedestrian, going on foot.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A footman, a foot soldier, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत् for पाद foot, कष to injure, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तङ्ग
पत्तङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Red sanders: see पचङ्ग, of which it appears to be a local corruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तन|पत्तनं
पत्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A town, a city.<BR>2 A sort of drum.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, तनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तनवणिज्
पत्तनवणिज्<BR>m. (-णिक्)<BR>A tradesman.<BR>E.<BR>पत्तन a city, वणिज् a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ति|पत्तिः
पत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 A foot soldier.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Going, moving, walking.<BR>2 A company, a platoon, consisting of one chariot, one elephant, three horse, and five foot.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, ति Uṇādi aff. or क्तिन् aff. for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिपङ्क्ति|पत्तिपंक्ति
पत्तिपङ्क्ति<BR>f. (-ङ्क्तिः)<BR>A line of infantry.<BR>E.<BR>पत्ति, and पङ्क्ति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तिसंहति|पत्तिसंहतिः
पत्तिसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A body of troops.<BR>E.<BR>पत्ति, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्तूर|पत्तूरः
पत्तूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, commonly Śaliñca.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Red sanders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्त्र
पत्त्र<BR>n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>Any vehicle or means of conveyance.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, ष्ट्रन् aff.; also पत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्नी
पत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>पति a husband, ङीप् aff., and नुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्न्याट|पत्न्याटः
पत्न्याट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The Haram, the private or women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>पत्नी a wife, आट who goes, from अट, with घञ् affix, and आङ् prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्र|पत्त्रं|पत्रं
पत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 A vehicle in general; as a car, a horse, a camel, &c.<BR>3 The wing of a bird.<BR>4 The feather of an arrow.<BR>5 The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>6 The leaf of a book.<BR>7 Goldleaf, &c. any thin sheet or plate of metal.<BR>nf. (-त्रं-त्री)<BR>A letter, any written document or address.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, ष्ट्रन् aff. and one त rejected; also sometimes पत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रक|पत्रकं
पत्रक<BR>n. (-क)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>3 Staining the person with Sandal, &c. by way of decoration.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकाहला
पत्रकाहला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The noise made by the flapping of wings, or rustling of leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, a wing, &c. and काहल noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रकृच्छ्र|पत्रकृच्छ्रः
पत्रकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>A sort of penance, drinking infusion of any leaves for a given time.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and कृच्छ्र a penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रगुप्त|पत्रगुप्तः
पत्रगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A species of Euphorbia, commonly Teṅkānta Śij.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रङ्ग|पत्रङ्गं
पत्रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santalinus); also पत्राङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रझङ्कार|पत्त्रझङ्कार|पत्रझङ्कारः
पत्रझङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The current of a river: other authorities have in place of this word, पुरसंस्कार, and पत्रसंस्कार, which last appears to be most accurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रणा
पत्रणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Trimming the feathered butt of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>पत the feather of an arrow, णी to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रतण्डुला
पत्रतण्डुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A kind of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रतरु|पत्रतरुः
पत्रतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The foetid Mimosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रदारक|पत्रदारकः
पत्रदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A saw.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, &c. and दॄ to tear, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रनाडिका
पत्रनाडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The fibre or vein of a leaf.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, नाडी a vessel, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपरशु|पत्रपरशुः
पत्रपरशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A small file used by silversmiths, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a sheet of metal, परशु an axe; also with पर्शु the same, पत्रपर्शु (-र्शुः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाल|पत्रपालः
पत्रपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large knife.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A pair of shears or scissors.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, पाल to nourish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपाश्या
पत्रपाश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>An ornament of the forehead, a piece of gold-leaf situate on the forehead, or a painted mark upon it.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, पश to bind, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपिशाचिका
पत्रपिशाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of cap or cover for the head, made of leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, पिशाचिका an imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपुष्प|पत्रपुष्पः
पत्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, a red sort of Tulasī or Basil, (Ocymum pilosum.)<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपुष्पक|पत्रपुष्पकः
पत्रपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of birch, from the bark of which Hukka snakes, &c. are made: see भूर्ज्जपत्र.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and पुष्प a flower, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रबन्ध|पत्रबन्धः
पत्रबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Adorning with leaves, flowers, &c. decorating with nosegays or garlands.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रबाल|पत्रबालः
पत्रबाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An oar, especially a large one used as a rudder.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, बल to be strong, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रभङ्ग|पत्रभंग|पत्रभङ्गः
पत्रभङ्ग<BR>mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी)<BR>Decorating the person by staining it with fragrant pigments of sandal, musk, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, भञ्च to break, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रयौवन|पत्रयौवनं
पत्रयौवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A new leaf, a sprout.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररथ|पत्ररथः
पत्ररथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पच a wing, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्ररञ्जन
पत्ररञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Embellishing a page, illuminating, gilding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रल|पत्रलं
पत्रल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Thin or skim milk.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, रल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रलेखा
पत्रलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>Decoration of the face or person, by means of fragrant pigments, consisting of Sandal, saffron, musk, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=498" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवल्ली
पत्रवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Staining the person with Sandal, &c. by way of ornament.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and वल्ली a creeper; also पत्रावली, पचलेखा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रवाह|पत्रवाहः
पत्रवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 A postman, a letter carrier.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a feather, and बाह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रशिरा
पत्रशिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The vein or fibre of a leaf.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and शिरा a tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रश्रेष्ठ|पत्रश्रेष्ठः
पत्रश्रेष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The Bel tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रसंस्कार
पत्रसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The current of a river.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, संस्कार making perfect: see पत्रझङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रसूचि|पत्रसूचिः
पत्रसूचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and सूचि a needle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रहिम|पत्रहिमं
पत्रहिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Cold, wintry weather.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र here said to mean falling, हिम frost or snow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राख्य|पत्राख्यं
पत्राख्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>The pungent leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and आख्या a name; the leaf, by way of distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्ग|पत्रांग|पत्राङ्गं
पत्राङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Red sanders, (Pterocarpus santolinus.)<BR>2 Red or sappan wood, (Cæsalpinia sappan.)<BR>3 Bhojpatra, a tree so called, a kind of Birch.<BR>4 Another plant: see पद्मक.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राङ्गुलि|पत्रांगुलि|पत्राङ्गुलिः
पत्राङ्गुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Painting the forehead, throat, neck, &c. with coloured Sandal, saffron, or any other fragrant substance.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and अङ्गुलि a finger, being applied with the finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राञ्जन|पत्रांजन|पत्राञ्जनं
पत्राञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Ink or blacking.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, (of a book,) and अञ्चन unction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राढ्य|पत्राढ्यं
पत्राढ्य<BR>n. (-ढ्यं)<BR>1 The root of long pepper.<BR>2 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्राली
पत्राली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Coloured ornamental marks on the face or person.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and आली a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावलि|पत्रावलिः
पत्रावलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 Red chalk.<BR>2 A row of leaves.<BR>3 Decorating the person.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and आवलि a line: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रावली
पत्रावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Drawing lines along the form; staining some parts of the body with coloured and fragrant pigments, as with saffron, Sandal, &c.<BR>2 A mixture of young Aśvattha leaves with barley and honey.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, and आवली a line: see पत्रलेखा, पत्रक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रिका
पत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A leaf, a written leaf or page, a writing, a letter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रिन्
पत्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>1 Winged.<BR>2 Feathered.<BR>3 Having a page or leaf.<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 A falcon.<BR>4 A tree.<BR>5 A mountain.<BR>6 A chariot.<BR>7 A rider in a car or carriage.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A sprout, a shoot.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रपूग
पत्रपूग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A shower of arrows.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and पूग a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोपस्कर|पत्रोपस्करः
पत्रोपस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, उपस्कर a condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोर्ण|पत्रोर्णं|पत्रोर्णः
पत्रोर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Wove silk.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia indica).<BR>E.<BR>पत्र a leaf, ऊर्णा wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्रोल्लास|पत्रोल्लासः
पत्रोल्लास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bud.<BR>E.<BR>पत्र, and उल्लास what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पत्सल|पत्सलं|पत्सलः
पत्सल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, सर Uṇādi aff., र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ|पथः
पथ<BR>r. 1st cl. (पथति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पथयति)<BR>To throw, to cast, to despatch or send;<BR>(इ,) पथि r. 1st and 10th cls. (पन्थति पन्थयति)<BR>To go, to proceed, to travel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ|पथः
पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>पथ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथत्|पथन्त्
पथत्<BR>mfn. (-थन्-थन्ती-थत्)<BR>Going, travelling.<BR>m. (-थन्)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>पथ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिक|पथिकः
पथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Knowing or going on a road.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A traveller, a way-farer.<BR>2 A guide, one who knows the way.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन् a road, वुन् or ष्कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिकसन्तति|पथिकसंतति|पथिकसंततिः|पथिकसन्ततिः
पथिकसन्तति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A line or range of travellers, a cafileh, a caravan.<BR>E.<BR>पथिक a traveller, सन्तति a range; also with संहति assemblage, पथिकसंहति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिद्रुम|पथिद्रुमः
पथिद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of Khayar, (Mimosa alba.)<BR>E.<BR>पथिन् a road, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिन्
पथिन्<BR>m. (-पन्था)<BR>1 A road, a way.<BR>2 Sect, doctrine, path in morals or religion.<BR>3 A division of hell.<BR>E.<BR>पथ to go, इन् Uṇādi aff.; the noun is irregularly inflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिप्रज्ञ
पथिप्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Acquainted with roads.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन्, and प्रज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिल|पथिलः
पथिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A traveller, a way-farer. पथिन् a road, इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथिवाहक|पथिवाहकः
पथिवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>2 A porter, a burthen-carrier.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन् a road, and वाहक who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्य|पथ्यं|पथ्यः
पथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>Proper, fit, suitable, agreeing with, but applied chiefly medically, with respect to diet, regimen, &c.<BR>mf. (-थ्यः-थ्या)<BR>Yellow Myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>E.<BR>पथ to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्यापथ्य|पथ्यापथ्यं
पथ्यापथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>The class of things that are considered beneficial or hurtful in disease.<BR>E.<BR>पथ्य, and अपथ्य improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पथ्याशिन्
पथ्याशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Eating wholesome things.<BR>E.<BR>पथ्य, and आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद|पदं|पदः
पद<BR>r. 4th cl. (औ) पदौ (पद्व्यते) r. 10th cl. (पदयते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>(ए) पदे r. 1st cl. (पदति)<BR>To stand fast.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>1 To know, to understand.<BR>2 To see, to look.<BR>With अनु,<BR>To follow.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>1 To happen, to befall.<BR>2 To gain.<BR>3 To suffer misfortune.<BR>4 To multiply.<BR>5 To produce.<BR>6 To come.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To be born or produced.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To gain.<BR>2 To be born.<BR>3 To be near or connected with.<BR>With उप and सम्,<BR>To offer oblations.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To gain, to acquire.<BR>2 To commence.<BR>With प्र and वि,<BR>To establish, to enact.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>1 To gain.<BR>2 To assent, to agree or promise.<BR>3 To restore.<BR>With वि,<BR>To suffer misfortune or pain.<BR>With वि and आङ्,<BR>To injure or kill.<BR>With वि and उत्,<BR>To discriminate, to analyze.<BR>With सम्,<BR>1 To thrive, to grow or increase.<BR>2 To do, to execute, to perform.<BR>3 To select.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>1 To arrive.<BR>2 To finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्
पद्<BR>m. (-द् or त्)<BR>A foot.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, aff. क्विप्; also पद; or it is considered an irregular substitute for पाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद|पदं|पदः
पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 A footstep, the mark of a foot.<BR>3 A word.<BR>4 An inflected word.<BR>5 A crude word.<BR>6 A connected sentence.<BR>7 Thing.<BR>8 Preservation, defence.<BR>9 Industry, application.<BR>10 Disguise.<BR>11 Place, site.<BR>12 Rank, station, degree.<BR>13 A mark, a spot.<BR>14 A foot or rather line of a stanza.<BR>15 A mode of writing the Vedas, in which the several words are detached from one another.<BR>16 (In Arithmetic,) Any one of a set of numbers the sum of which is required, or the last of the series.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदक|पदकं|पदकः
पदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Brahman knowing the verses of the Vedas.<BR>2 A Niṣka, a weight of gold.<BR>3 An ornament of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>पद a verse, &c. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=499" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदकार|पदकारः
पदकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One who divides or separates compound terms.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदक्रम|पदक्रमः
पदक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Step, pace.<BR>2 Walking.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदग|पदगः
पदग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going with the feet.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A footman, a foot soldier, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पद् or पद a foot, and ग who goes; hence also पद्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदगत
पदगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone on foot.<BR>2 Described or recorded in a line or stanza.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदन
पदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Who or what goes or moves.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदन्यास|पदन्यासः
पदन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Step, pace.<BR>2 Conduct, procedure.<BR>3 Position of the feet in a particular attitude.<BR>4 A plant; also गोक्षुर.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and न्यास gesticulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदपात|पदपातः
पदपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Step, pace, foot-fall, tread.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदभञ्जन|पदभञ्जनं
पदभञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Explanation of obscure or obsolete words.<BR>2 Etymology.<BR>3 Separating the words of a line or sentence.<BR>E.<BR>पद a word, भञ्जन a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदभञ्जिका|पदभंजिका
पदभञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A register, a journal, a calendar or almanack.<BR>E.<BR>पद a mark, &c. भञ्ज to divide, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदवि|पदविः
पदवि<BR>f. (-विः-वी)<BR>1 A road, a path, a way.<BR>2 Station, situation, degree, rank.<BR>3 Place, site.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, अवि aff.; fem. aff. optionally ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदविक्षेप|पदविक्षेपः
पदविक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Step, pace, walking.<BR>2 A horse's paces.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and विक्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदविष्टम्भ|पदविष्टम्भः
पदविष्टम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Tread, step, stamp with the foot.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and विष्टम्भ fixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदष्ठीव|पदष्ठीवं
पदष्ठीव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The feet and knees.<BR>E.<BR>पद् a foot, and अष्ठीवत् the knee, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदसङ्घात|पदसंघात|पदसंघातः
पदसङ्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A writer, an annotator, one who collects or classes words.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and सम् before हन to hurt, अण् aff. also पदसङ्घाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाङ्क|पदांक|पदाङ्कः
पदाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>Foot-mark, vestige.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाजि|पदाजिः
पदाजि<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>A foot soldier.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, अज to go, इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदात|पदातः
पदात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A footman, a pedestrian.<BR>E.<BR>पद foot, अत to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाति|पदातिः
पदाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A footman or foot soldier.<BR>E.<BR>पद foot, अत to go, इन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदातिक|पदातिकः
पदातिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A peon, a footman or foot soldier.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदानुराग|पदानुरागः
पदानुराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A servant.<BR>2 An army.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and अनुराग attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदाम्भोज|पदांभोज
पदाम्भोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The foot of a mistress, or a divinity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and अम्भोज lotus; also similar compounds, पदारविन्द, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदार|पदारः
पदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The dust of the feet.<BR>2 A boat.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, ऋ to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदारविन्द
पदारविन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The foot of a mistress, of a divinity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पद, and अरविन्द a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदार्थ|पदार्थः
पदार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 Thing, substantial or material form of being.<BR>2 A category or predicament in Logic, of which seven are enumerated, viz. substance, quality, action, identity, variety, relation, and annihilation; another enumeration gives sixteen.<BR>3 The meaning of a word or sentence.<BR>E.<BR>पद word, thing, and अथ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदासन|पदासनं
पदासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A footstool.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, आसन a place of sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदिक|पदिकः
पदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Going on foot.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A foot soldier.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The point of the foot.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, aff. ष्ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पदेपदे
पदेपदे<BR>ind.<BR>Continually.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot-step, seventh case, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्ग|पद्गः
पद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A foot soldier.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्धति|पद्धतिः
पद्धति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 A line, a row or range.<BR>3 A ritual, a manual, a work upon any act or ceremony, detailing the mode of its performance, and collecting the texts connected with it.<BR>4 A family name, a surname or title.<BR>E.<BR>पद a foot, हन to strike, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्धिम|पद्धिमं
पद्धिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Coldness of the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पद् for पाद, and हिम frost or cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्म|पद्मं|पद्मः
पद्म<BR>mn. (-द्मः-द्मं)<BR>1 A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum); it is often confounded with the water lily, (Nymphæa.)<BR>2 A form of array.<BR>3 One of KUVERA'S treasures or gems.<BR>4 A large number, ten billions.<BR>5 Coloured marks on the face and trunk of an elephant.<BR>6 A drug, also termed Padmakāṣṭha.<BR>7 Lead.<BR>8 A name given to the six Cakras of the body, or to the mystical faculties present in them.<BR>m. (-द्मः)<BR>1 A Nāga or serpent of the lower regions.<BR>2 One of the twelve Cakravartīs or paramount princes of the Jainas.<BR>3 One of the nine persons termed Śukla Balas by the Jainas.<BR>4 A name of RĀMA.<BR>5 The personified treasure of KUVERA, as worshipped by the Tāntrikas.<BR>f. (-द्मा)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>3 A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>4 A female serpent or Nāga, the goddess MANASĀ, and wife to the sage JARATKĀRU.<BR>5 The mother of the twentieth Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>6 The flower of the Carthamus or safflower.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, (on the water, &c.) Uṇādi aff. मम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मक|पद्मकं
पद्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Coloured marks or spots on the face and trunk of an elephant.<BR>2 A sort of drug, commonly called पद्मकाष्ठ.<BR>3 A kind of leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकर|पद्मकरः
पद्मकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and कर hand, his image always holding a lotus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकाष्ठ|पद्मकाष्ठं
पद्मकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A fragrant wood used in medicine, and described as cooling and tonic.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकिन्
पद्मकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch tree, the bark is used for writing upon, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मकेशर|पद्मकेशरः
पद्मकेशर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The filaments of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and केशर the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मखण्ड|पद्मखंड
पद्मखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A quantity of lotuses, or spot abounding with them.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and खण्ड a portion or district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मगन्ध|पद्मगंध|पद्मगन्धं
पद्मगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Lotus-smelling; smelling like a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and गन्ध smell; also with इ substituted for the final. पद्मगन्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मगर्ब्भ
पद्मगर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and गर्ब्भ womb, born from the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मचारिणी
पद्मचारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small tree, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, चर to resemble, aff. णिनि, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मतन्तु|पद्मतंतु|पद्मतन्तुः
पद्मतन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>The fibrous stalk of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and तन्तु thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मदर्शन|पद्मदर्शनः
पद्मदर्शन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The resin of the Pinus longifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=500" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाभ|पद्मनाभः
पद्मनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 One of the Jinas of a future age.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and नाभि a navel, षच् aff.; also<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाभि|पद्मनाभिः
पद्मनाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>VIṢṆU is thus termed, because the lotus, containing BRAHMĀ, sent to create the world, sprang from his navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मनाल|पद्मनालं
पद्मनाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The stalk of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and नाल a hollow stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपब
पद्मपब<BR>n. (-बं)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and पत्र a leaf; also पद्मपर्ण n. (-र्णं) from पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपाणि|पद्मपाणिः
पद्मपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A Buddha, a Bauddha sanctified teacher.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and पाणि the hand, holding a lotus in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपुष्प|पद्मपुष्पः
पद्मपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A shrub, (Webera corymbosa): see कर्णिकार.<BR>2 A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मप्रभ|पद्मप्रभः
पद्मप्रभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The sixth Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and प्रभ who shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मप्रिया
पद्मप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The wife of the Muni JARATKĀRU.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and प्रिया fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मबन्ध|पद्मबंध|पद्मबन्धः
पद्मबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The arrangement of the words of a verse in a figure representing the leaves of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मबन्धु|पद्मबंधु|पद्मबन्धुः
पद्मबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>1 A bee.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and बन्धु the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मभू
पद्मभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्ममुखी
पद्ममुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A sort of prickly nightshade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मयोनि|पद्मयोनिः
पद्मयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मराग|पद्मरागः
पद्मराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मरेखा
पद्मरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A line of the palm, indicating the possession of great wealth.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a large number, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मलाञ्छन|पद्मलांछन|पद्मलाञ्छनः
पद्मलाञ्छन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>3 A title of TĀRĀ, one of the forms of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, a Catta or parasol shaped like one, a fabulous gem, &c. and लाञ्छन a mark or designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवर्णक|पद्मवर्णकं
पद्मवर्णक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A species of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, वर्ण a colour, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवासा
पद्मवासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and वास abode; abiding at the creation within the petals of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मवीज|पद्मवीजं
पद्मवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The seed of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मस्नुषा
पद्मस्नुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 GAṄGĀ.<BR>2 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>3 GAURĪ or DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and स्नुषा a daughter-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माकर|पद्माकरः
पद्माकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large deep tank or pond; one in which the lotus does or may grow.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माक्ष|पद्माक्षं|पद्माक्षः
पद्माक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The seed of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्माट|पद्माटः
पद्माट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of Cassia, (C. tora.)<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and अट to resemble, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मान्तर|पद्मान्तरः
पद्मान्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Petal of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and अन्तर inside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मालया
पद्मालया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A name of the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and आलय an asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावती
पद्मावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The wife of the sage JARATKĀRU.<BR>2 The name of a river, the main stream of the Ganges, between the Kasimbazar river and the sea.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, मतुप् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्, and the antepen. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावतीप्रिय|पद्मावतीप्रियः
पद्मावतीप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Muni JARATKĀRU.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मावती as above, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मासन|पद्मासनं|पद्मासनः
पद्मासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A posture in religious meditation, sitting with the thighs crossed, one hand resting on the left thigh, the other held up with the thumb upon the heart; the eyes directed to the tip of the nose.<BR>2 A seat or throne made in the shape of a lotus, one especially on which idols are placed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिन्
पद्मिन्<BR>m. (-द्मी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A multitude of lotuses, or place abounding in them.<BR>2 A woman of one of the four classes into which the sex is distinguished; the first and most excellent.<BR>3 A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>4 A pool or pond, especially one deep enough for the growth of the lotus.<BR>5 The fibrous stalk of a lotus.<BR>6 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म coloured marks, &c. or a lotus, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीकान्त|पद्मिनीकांत|पद्मिनीकान्तः
पद्मिनीकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मिनी a lotus, and कान्त beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीखण्ड
पद्मिनीखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A place abounding with lotuses, or a district in which they grow.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मिनी, and खण्ड division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मिनीवल्लभ|पद्मिनीवल्लभः
पद्मिनीवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मिनी a lotus, and बल्लभ a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मेशय|पद्मेशयः
पद्मेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मे in or on a lotus, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोत्तर|पद्मोत्तरः
पद्मोत्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Safflower.<BR>2 A proper name: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म, and उत्तर better.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोत्तरात्मज|पद्मोत्तरात्मजः
पद्मोत्तरात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>One of the Jaina Cakravartīs or emperors.<BR>E.<BR>पद्मोत्तर, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मोद्भव|पद्मोद्भवः
पद्मोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The snake goddess MANASĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पद्म a lotus, and उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्य|पद्यं|पद्यः
पद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्याद्यं)<BR>Hurting or coming in contact with the feet.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Metre, verse.<BR>2 Wickedness, infamy.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A Śūdra.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्र|पद्रः
पद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 A village.<BR>2 The entrance into a village.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्व|पद्वः
पद्व<BR>m. (-द्वः)<BR>1 The abode or world of human beings.<BR>2 A car.<BR>3 A road.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, क्वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्वन्
पद्वन्<BR>m. (-द्वा)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, वनिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन
पन<BR>r. 1st cl. (पनायति)<BR>To praise: this root and पण in the same sense, take आय before the Sārvadhātuka, and some of the Ārddhadhātuka, affixes.<BR>(पनते)<BR>To traffic, to buy and sell: see पण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनस|पनसः
पनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The bread fruit or Jaka tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>2 A thorn.<BR>3 The name of a monkey.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A malady, pustular and phlegmonoid inflammation of the skin or external organs.<BR>2 A she monkey.<BR>3 A female demon.<BR>E.<BR>पन to praise or be praised, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पनसनालिका
पनसनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The bread-fruit or Jack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्थक|पंथक
पन्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Produced in or on the road.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन्, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्न|पन्नं|पन्नः
पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Fallen, gone down or downwards.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>Downward motion, falling, descending.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, aff. क्त, deriv. irr., otherwise पद to go, Uṇādi aff. नन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=501" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नग|पन्नगः
पन्नग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A drug: see पद्मकाष्ठ.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>The snake goddess MANASĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पन्न fallen, ग who goes, or पद् a foot, न not, ग who goes; moving without feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नगाशन|पन्नगाशनः
पन्नगाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पन्नग a snake, and अशन food; the snake-eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नद्धा
पन्नद्धा<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>A leather shoe or boot.<BR>E.<BR>पद् a foot, नह to bind, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पन्नद्धी
पन्नद्धी<BR>f. (-द्धी)<BR>A shoe, a boot.<BR>E.<BR>पद् a foot, नह to bind, aff. ष्ट्रन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपि|पपिः
पपि<BR>mfn. (-पिः-पिः-पि)<BR>Who or what drinks.<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, कि aff. and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपिस्
पपिस्<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, reiterated by special rule, Uṇādi aff. इस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपीति
पपीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Mutual or reciprocal drinking, drinking alike or together.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, in the reiterative form, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पपु|पपुः
पपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A fosterer, a protector.<BR>f. (-पुः)<BR>A nurse, a fostermother.<BR>E.<BR>पा to cherish, कु aff. and the radical consonant repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पम्पा|पंपा
पम्पा<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>The name of a river, in the south of India.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, प Uṇādi aff., मन् inserted, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पय|पयः
पय<BR>r. 1st cl. (पयते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयश्चय|पयश्चयः
पयश्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, चय collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्
पयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>E.<BR>पय to go, असुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस
पयस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् the same, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्प
पयस्प<BR>m. (-स्पः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् milk, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्य|पयस्यं|पयस्यः
पयस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 Made from milk, (curds, butter, cheese, &c.)<BR>2 Relating to or connected with milk or water.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>1 A shrub, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>2 A medicinal kind of moon plant.<BR>3 A drug: see क्षीरकाकोली.<BR>4 Curds of two milk whey.<BR>5 Any plant yielding a milky sap, as the Euphorbia, the Asclepias, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् milk, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्वल|पयस्वलः
पयस्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयस्विनी
पयस्विनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 A milch cow.<BR>3 Night.<BR>4 A she goat.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water or milk, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोगड|पयोगडः
पयोगड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>Hail.<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>An island.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, गड a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोघन|पयोघनः
पयोघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, चन a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोजन्मन्
पयोजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, जन्मन् origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोद|पयोदः
पयोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधर|पयोधरः
पयोधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A woman's breast.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 The sugarcane.<BR>4 The cocoanut.<BR>5 A sort of rush, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>6 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus, &c.) (In Prosody) A scolius.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् milk or water, and धर containing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधस्
पयोधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A piece of water.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, धा to contain, Uṇādi aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधि|पयोधिः
पयोधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, and धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोधिक|पयोधिकं
पयोधिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>पयोधि, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोनिधि|पयोनिधिः
पयोनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, and निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोमुच्
पयोमुच्<BR>m. (-मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, and मुच् what lets go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोर|पयोरः
पयोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>पयस् water, रा to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोराशि|पयोराशिः
पयोराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>पयस्, and राशि a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोव्रत|पयोव्रतः
पयोव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Living upon milk for a month, which with prayer and residence in a cow house, is an expiation for receiving an unsuitable present; offering of milk to VIṢṆU, and subsisting upon it for twelve days; also for one or for three days as a religious act.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् milk, and व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पयोष्णी
पयोष्णी<BR>f. (-ष्णी)<BR>A river that rises in the Vindhya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर|परं|परः
पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Distant, removed, remote.<BR>2 Best, preeminent.<BR>3 Subsequent, after, following.<BR>4 Other, different.<BR>5 Inimical, hostile, estranged, adverse.<BR>6 Addicted to, attached to, engaged in.<BR>7 More, exceeding, as परंशतं more than a hundred, परो लक्षः more than a Lac: these are also considered as distinct compounds, see the next.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 The life of BRAHMĀ.<BR>n. ind. (-रं)<BR>1 Only, alone.<BR>2 After, afterwards.<BR>subst.<BR>1 Final beatitude.<BR>2 (In Logic,) One species of common property, that which comprehends many objects, genus; or it is the same with existence, as the common property of all things.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill, &c. aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःशत|परःशतं
परःशत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>More than a hundred, many.<BR>E.<BR>पर more, and शत a hundred: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःसहस्र|परःसहस्रं
परःसहस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>More than a thousand.<BR>E.<BR>पर more, and सहस्र a thousand: see पर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परःस्वस्
परःस्वस्<BR>ind. (-स्वः)<BR>The day after to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>पर after, स्वस् tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकलत्र
परकलत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Another's wife.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and कलत्र a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकलत्राभिगमन
परकलत्राभिगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Intriguing with another man's wife. adultery.<BR>E.<BR>परकलत्र another's wife, अभिगमन approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परकीय|परकीयं
परकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Another, belonging to another.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The mistress or wife of another, one of the three objects of love, according to the Śṛṅgāra or amatory doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, छ aff., कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परक्षेत्र|परक्षेत्रं
परक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Another man's wife.<BR>2 Another's body.<BR>3 Another's field.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, क्षेच a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्रन्थि|परग्रंथि|परग्रन्थिः
परग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>An articulation, a joint.<BR>E.<BR>पर after, ग्रन्थि a joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परग्लानि|परग्लानिः
परग्लानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Reduction or subjugation of an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and ग्लानि vexing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परछन्द|परच्छन्द|परच्छंद|परच्छन्दः
परछन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Dependant, subservient, subjected.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, छन्द inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परछिद्र|परच्छिद्र|परच्छिद्रं
परछिद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>A fault or defect in another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and छिद्र flaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजात|परजातः
परजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Adopted, fostered, nourished by a stranger.<BR>2 Dependant, servile, subjected.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परजित|परजितः
परजित<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Nourished by a stranger.<BR>2 Conquered, subdued.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and जित conquered, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्ज|परंज|परंजः|परञ्जः
परञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 An oil press.<BR>2 Froth, foam.<BR>3 The blade of a sword or a knife.<BR>4 A sword or scymitar.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>The sound of instruments at a festival.<BR>n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>The sword of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पर in the second case, another, and जि to conquer, aff. ड; some works have परज, and others पराञ्ज in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जन|परंजन|परंजनः|परञ्जनः
परञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, जि to conquer, deriv. irr.; also परञ्जय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परञ्जय|परंजय|परंजयः|परञ्जयः
परञ्जय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>VARUṆA: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=502" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतन्त्र|परतंत्र|परतन्त्रः
परतन्त्र<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>Subservient, obedient, dependant.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, तन्त्र will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतम
परतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Greatest.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and तमप् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतर
परतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Greater, more.<BR>E.<BR>पर more, and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परतस्
परतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Afterwards.<BR>2 Behind.<BR>3 Otherwise, differently.<BR>E.<BR>पर or परा, and अतसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्र|परत्रं
परत्र<BR>ind.<BR>The next world, futurity.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्रभीरु|परत्रभीरुः
परत्रभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A pious man, one standing in awe of futurity.<BR>E.<BR>परच the next world, and भीरु timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परत्व|परत्वं
परत्व<BR>m. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Difference, distinction, separateness.<BR>2 Hostility.<BR>3 (In Logic,) Priority of place or time, proximity, juvenility.<BR>4 The nature of common or generic property.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to पर; also with तल, परता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदार|परदारः
परदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Another's wife.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and दार a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदारगमन
परदारगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Adultery, adulterous intercourse or intrigue.<BR>E.<BR>परदार, and गमन frequenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदाराभिमर्ष
परदाराभिमर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Intriguing with another man's wife.<BR>E.<BR>परदार, and अभिमर्ष contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदारोपसेवन
परदारोपसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Intriguing with another's wife.<BR>E.<BR>परदार, and उपसेवन frequenting; also परदारोपसेवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदुःख|परदुःखं
परदुःख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The pain or sorrow of another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and दुःख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेश|परदेशः
परदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A foreign country.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशिन्
परदेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Foreign, exotic.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A foreigner.<BR>2 One residing abroad.<BR>E.<BR>परदेश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदेशसेविन्
परदेशसेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living abroad, travelling, a traveller.<BR>E.<BR>परदेश, and सेविन् who frequents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परदोषकीर्त्तन
परदोषकीर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Scandal, calumny, censoriousness.<BR>E.<BR>पर, दोष fault, कीर्त्तन proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्वेषिन्
परद्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Hostile, inimical, adverse.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, द्विष to hate, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्रव्य
परद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Another's property.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परद्रोहिन्
परद्रोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Tyrannising over another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and द्रोहिन् injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधन
परधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Another's wealth.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधनास्वादनसुख
परधनास्वादनसुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Feeding luxuriously at another's expense.<BR>E.<BR>परधन, आस्वादन eating, सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परधर्म्म|परधर्म|परधर्मः
परधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Another's duty or business, the occupation of another caste.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परध्यान|परध्यानं
परध्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Intent absorption or abstraction in the subject of meditation.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and ध्यान meditating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परन्तप|परंतप|परंतपः|परन्तपः
परन्तप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Vexing or annoying another, subduing a foe.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, तप to heat or inflame, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपद|परपदं
परपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Eminence, high station.<BR>2 Final felicity.<BR>E.<BR>पर supreme, पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपरिग्रह|परपरिग्रहः
परपरिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The family or dependants of another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and परिग्रह dependants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाक
परपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>What is dressed or cooked by another, another's food.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकनिवृत्त|परपाकनिवृत्तः
परपाकनिवृत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>One who dresses his own food without observing, the expiatory sacrifice for the five Sūnas, or places of destruction to animal life: see पञ्चसूना.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, पाक cooking, and निवृत्त ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरत|परपाकरतः
परपाकरत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One who observes all the due ceremonies preparatory to cooking, but lives upon others.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, पाक cooking, रत constant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपाकरुचि|परपाकरुचिः
परपाकरुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A constant guest at otherś tables.<BR>E.<BR>पर anothers, पाक cooking, and रुचि shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपिण्ड|परपिंड|परपिण्डः
परपिण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Food given by another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and पिण्ड ball of rice or meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपिण्डाद|परपिंडाद|परपिण्डादः
परपिण्डाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Feeding at another's cost.<BR>E.<BR>पर पिण्ड, and आद who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुरुष|परपुरुषः
परपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 Another man.<BR>E.<BR>पर supreme, and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्ट|परपुष्टः
परपुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Fostered, nourished, &c. by a stranger.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR>2 A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, पुष्ट cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपुष्टमहोत्सव|परपुष्टमहोत्सवः
परपुष्टमहोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The mango.<BR>E.<BR>परपुष्ट the cuckoo, महा great, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्व्वा|परपूर्वा
परपूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A woman, formerly married.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (husband,) पूर्व्व prior, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परपूर्व्वापति|परपूर्वापति
परपूर्व्वापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The husband of a woman remarried.<BR>E.<BR>परपूर्व्वा, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रतिनप्तृ
परप्रतिनप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>A great-great-grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पर subsequent, प्रति after, नप्तृ a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रपौच
परप्रपौच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A great-great-grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पर subsequent, प्रपौत्र great-grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परप्रेष्यत्व
परप्रेष्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Servitude, slavery.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and प्रेष्यत्व service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परब्रह्मन्
परब्रह्मन्<BR>n. (-ह्म)<BR>The Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and ब्रह्म the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग|परभागः
परभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Excellence, superior merit, supremacy.<BR>2 Good fortune, prosperity.<BR>3 The last part, residue, remainder.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभाग्य
परभाग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Another's wealth or prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and भाग्य good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभुक्त
परभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Possessed or enjoyed by another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and भुक्त enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूमि
परभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>A foreign or an enemy's country.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूमिष्ठ
परभूमिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Living or being in a foreign or an enemy's country.<BR>E.<BR>परभूमि, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभूषण
परभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Another's ornament.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Peace purchased by ceding the produce of lands.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and भूषण ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत्
परभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (the cuckoo,) and भृत् who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभृत|परभृतः
परभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished or nourished by a stranger, fostered, adopted.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Indian cuckoo, which is supposed to leave its eggs in the nest of the crow to be hatched.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परभेदक
परभेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Destroying or subduing a foe.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and भेदक who breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्
परम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of command.<BR>2 Of dismissal or refusal.<BR>3 Hereafter, afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम|परमः
परम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Best, most excellent.<BR>2 Chief, principal, preceding.<BR>3 First.<BR>ind. (-मं)<BR>1 A term of assent, yes.<BR>2 A term of command.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, मा to mete, aff. ड or डम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=503" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगति|परमगतिः
परमगति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Chief object or refuge, as a god, a protector.<BR>2 Final felicity.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगव|परमगवः
परमगव<BR>mf. (-वः-वी)<BR>An excellent bull or cow.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमगहन
परमगहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Very mysterious or profound.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and गहन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमत|परमतः
परमत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A different opinion or doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and मत thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमपद|परमपदः
परमपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Eminence, high station.<BR>2 Final felicity.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and पद station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमब्रह्मन्
परमब्रह्मन्<BR>n. (-ह्म)<BR>The Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and ब्रह्मन् the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमराज|परमराजः
परमराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A supreme monarch.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and राजन् a king, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्षि|परमर्षिः
परमर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi or divine sage, of a peculiar order or division, comprising the Muni BHELA and others.<BR>E.<BR>परम excellent, and ऋषि a divine sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमर्म्मज्ञ|परमर्मज्ञ
परमर्म्मज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>One who knows another's character or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and मर्म्म a vital point, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमस्वधर्म्मन्|परमस्वधर्मन्
परमस्वधर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A virtuous or pious man, one who attends scrupulously to the proper duties of his tribe or station.<BR>E.<BR>परम best, स्व own, धर्म्म virtue or duty, and अनिच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमहंस|परमहंसः
परमहंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An ascetic, a religious man who has subdued all his senses by abstract meditation.<BR>E.<BR>परम best or first, हंस devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमागति
परमागति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Translation to heaven, final beatitude.<BR>E.<BR>परमा best, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाङ्गना|परमांगना
परमाङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A beautiful woman.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाणु|परमाणुः
परमाणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 An atom, the invisible base of all aggregate bodies; thirty of them are supposed to form a note in a sunbeam; the lowest measure of weight; in Logic, six of them form the first perceptible object.<BR>2 A measure of time, the sun's passage past an atom of matter.<BR>E.<BR>परम first, and अणु an atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाणुङ्गक
परमाणुङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>परमाणु an atom, अङ्ग the body, कप् aff., deriv. irr.; smaller than the smallest; as he is larger than the largest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमात्मन्
परमात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The Supreme Being, considered as the soul of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>परम first, आत्मन् spirit or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमाद्वैत|परमाद्वैतः
परमाद्वैत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pure unitarianism.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>VIṢṆU, the only supreme.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and अद्वैत without duality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमान्न|परमान्नं
परमान्न<BR>n. (-न्न)<BR>An oblation of rice to progenitors or gods, boiled with milk and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>परम best, and अन्न boiled rice; or परम the best, the supreme, (deities, &c.) and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमापम|परमापमः
परमापम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The inclination of a planet's orbit to the ecliptic.<BR>2 The sine of the sun's greatest declination.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and अपम declination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमायुष|परमायुषः
परमायुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A particular tree: see असन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमायुस्
परमायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The longest period of life, either in men or animals.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थ|परमार्थः
परमार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 Truth, fitness.<BR>2 Spiritual knowledge.<BR>3 Any excellent or important aim or object.<BR>4 The best sense.<BR>5 The best kind of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थविद्
परमार्थविद्<BR>m. (-वित्)<BR>A sage, a philosopher, one who knows the truth.<BR>E.<BR>परमार्थ, and विद who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्थविन्द
परमार्थविन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Who or what acquires knowledge of truth, the best kind of wealth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परमार्थ, and विद् to acquire, श aff. and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमावधि
परमावधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Utmost term or limit.<BR>E.<BR>परम, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमार्हत|परमार्हतः
परमार्हत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A king and holy saint, apparently the same as ŚĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>E.<BR>परम excellent, अर्हत a Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमृत्यु|परमृत्युः
परमृत्यु<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and मृत्यु death; having many enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेश्वर|परमेश्वरः
परमेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Supreme Being.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>परम best, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठ|परमेष्ठः
परमेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Supreme, superior.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>E.<BR>परमे, and स्थ who stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परमेष्ठिन्
परमेष्ठिन्<BR>m. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A Jina or deified teacher of the Jaina sect.<BR>3 A kind of Śālagrāma stone.<BR>4 A Guru or spiritual guide.<BR>E.<BR>परमे in the most exalted place, in heaven, स्था to be, Uṇādi aff. निन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पद|परंपदं
परम्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Eternal felicity.<BR>2 The abode of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पर् another, पद degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पर|परंपर|परंपरः|परम्परः
परम्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Successive, proceeding from one to another, from father to son, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of deer.<BR>2 A great-great-grandson.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Race, progeny, lineage.<BR>2 Order, method, continuous arrangement, regular series or succession.<BR>E.<BR>पर subsequent, repeated, and the nasal augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्परतस्
परम्परतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Mutually.<BR>E.<BR>परम्पर and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्पराक|परंपराक|परम्पराकं
परम्पराक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Immolating animals in sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>परम्पर traditionary or successive, and अक going or worshipping; or पर much, पर the best, and अक going, custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परम्परीण|परंपरीण|परम्परीणं
परम्परीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Hereditary, what has come by inheritance or descent.<BR>2 Traditional.<BR>E.<BR>परं another, and पर again, another, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पररु|पररुः
पररु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A potherb, (Eclipta prostrata); also केशराज.<BR>E.<BR>पर much, रुह to grow, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोक|परलोकं|परलोकः
परलोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Heaven, paradise.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परलोकगम|परलोकगमः
परलोकगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, लोक world, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवत्|परवन्त्
परवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Dependant, subject.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवश|परवशः
परवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Subservient, dependant, subject.<BR>3 Deceived.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and वश subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाच्य
परवाच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Reprehensible, blamable.<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>Fault, defect.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and वाच्य to be named, not to be spoken of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परवाणि|परवाणिः
परवाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A judge, a ruler.<BR>2 A year.<BR>3 The peacock on which the god KĀRTTIKEYA rides.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, वा to go, णि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परव्रत|परव्रतः
परव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश|परशं|परशः
परश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A kind of gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशव्य|परशव्यं
परशव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Fit or proper for a hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>परश an axe, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=504" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशु|परशुः
परशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>An axe, a hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, शु to injure, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुधर|परशुधरः
परशुधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A soldier armed with an axe.<BR>2 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 PARAŚURĀMA: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>परशु an axe, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परशुराम|परशुरामः
परशुराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A hero and demigod; the first of the three RĀMAS, and the sixth Avatāra or descent of the deity VIṢṆU; who appeared in the world as the son of the saint JAMADAGNI, for the purpose of repressing the tyranny and punishing the violence of the Kṣatriya, or military tribe; PARAŚURĀMA appears to typify the tribe of Brahmans and their contests with the Kṣetriyas.<BR>E.<BR>परशु an axe, and राम who delights in; also with कन् added, परशुरामक; and with the first member, पर्शु, पर्शुराम, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वध|परश्वधः
परश्वध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>An axe, a hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, an enemy, श्व derived from श्वि to grow or thrive, परश्व the prosperity of a foe, घे to drink, क aff.; what drinks the blood or destroys the life of an enemy; also पारश्वध and परस्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परश्वस्
परश्वस्<BR>ind.<BR>The day after to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>पर after, श्वस् to-morrow; also परःश्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसङ्गत|परसंगत
परसङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Associated with another.<BR>2 Fighting or engaged with another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and सङ्गत gone with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसंज्ञक
परसंज्ञक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The soul.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, संज्ञा name or title, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसम्बन्ध
परसम्बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Relation or connexion with another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and सम्वन्ध connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परसम्बन्धिन्
परसम्बन्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>1 Related to another.<BR>2 Belonging to another.<BR>E.<BR>परसम्वन्ध, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्तात्
परस्तात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Subsequently, afterwards.<BR>2 Behind.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अस्तातिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पर|परस्परं
परस्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Mutual, interchanging.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, repeated; from one to another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परज्ञ|परस्परज्ञः
परस्परज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A friend, an intimate.<BR>E.<BR>परस्पर, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परानुमति
परस्परानुमति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Mutual concurrence or assent.<BR>E.<BR>परस्पर, and अनुमति agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्पराम्
परस्पराम्<BR>ind.<BR>Mutually.<BR>E.<BR>परस्पर, and आम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परोपकार
परस्परोपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mutual assistance.<BR>2 Offensive and defensive alliance.<BR>E.<BR>परस्पर, and उपकार aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्परोपकारिन्
परस्परोपकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 An ally.<BR>2 An associate, a helper.<BR>E.<BR>इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्मैपद|परस्मैपदं
परस्मैपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The transitive or active verb.<BR>E.<BR>परस्मै to another, पद an inflected word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्व
परस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>Another person's property.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वत्व
परस्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Another's right.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and स्वत्व own right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वत्वापादन
परस्वत्वापादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Conferring a right upon another as by gift, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परस्वत्व, and आपादन producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वध|परस्वधः
परस्वध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>An axe: see परश्वध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वादायिन्
परस्वादायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Extortionary, extortioner.<BR>E.<BR>परस्व, and आदायिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परस्वोपजीविक
परस्वोपजीविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Dependant, living on the property of others.<BR>E.<BR>परस्व, and उपजीविक subsisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परहित
परहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Friendly, benevolent.<BR>2 Good or profitable for another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and हित favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परा
परा<BR>ind.<BR>A participle and prefix implying,<BR>1 Supremacy.<BR>2 Liberation.<BR>3 Inverted order.<BR>4 Pride, contumely.<BR>5 Encounter, mutual presence.<BR>6 Excess, exceeding.<BR>7 Overcoming, surpassing.<BR>8 Going.<BR>9 Killing, destroying, injuring.<BR>As पराक्रम superior power or valour; पराजय defeat; पराभव disgrace; परावर्त turning back, &c. see the following.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill, aff. अप् and आ added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्
पराक्<BR>ind.<BR>Crooked, crookedly.<BR>E.<BR>परा away, अच् to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक|पराकः
पराक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A religious obligation of an expiatory kind, fasting for twelve days and nights, and keeping the mind attentive, and organs subdued.<BR>2 A sacrificial sword or scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, अक what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकरण|पराकरणं
पराकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disdaining, disregarding, rejecting.<BR>E.<BR>परा before कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकुर्व्वन्
पराकुर्व्वन्<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वती-र्व्वत्)<BR>Throwing off or aside, rejecting, disdaining.<BR>E.<BR>परा, and कुर्व्वन् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराकृत
पराकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rejected, set aside, thrown off, disdained.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रम|पराक्रमः
पराक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Power, strength.<BR>2 Exertion.<BR>3 Valour, prowess.<BR>4 Going out or forth, exit or issue.<BR>5 Attacking an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>परा supremacy, opposition, &c. and क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराक्रमज्ञ
पराक्रमज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Knowing the power, (of the enemy.)<BR>E.<BR>पराक्रम, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराग|परागः
पराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The pollen or farina of a flower.<BR>2 Dust.<BR>3 Fragrant powder used after bathing.<BR>4 Sandal.<BR>5 The name of a mountain.<BR>6 Fame, celebrity.<BR>7 An eclipse.<BR>8 Following one's own inclinations.<BR>E.<BR>परा implying supremacy, &c. and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागवत्
परागवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Laden with pollen.<BR>E.<BR>पराग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागत
परागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread, expanded.<BR>2 Budded, blown.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and आङ् before गम to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परागिन्
परागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Laden with pollen.<BR>E.<BR>पराग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गद|परांगद|पराङ्गदः
पराङ्गद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (DURGĀ,) अङ्ग form, and द who gives; forming with the goddess a deity, half male and half female; or better, पर an enemy, KĀMADEVA, अङ्ग body, and द who gives; restoring the body of that deity to shape, after having reduced it to ashes in a rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्गव|परांगव|परांगवः|पराङ्गवः
पराङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (river,) अङ्ग substance, water, and व who receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुख|पराङ्मुखः
पराङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Turning away, having the face averted.<BR>E.<BR>पराञ्च, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराङ्मुखता
पराङ्मुखता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Turning away.<BR>E.<BR>पराङ्मुख, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, पराङ्मुखत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचित|पराचितः
पराचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished or fostered by a stranger.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, आचित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराचीन|पराचीनः
पराचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Turned away, having the face averted.<BR>E.<BR>पराञ्च् or पराच् turned away, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजय|पराजयः
पराजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Defeat.<BR>E.<BR>परा implying encounter, contest, and जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजयमाण
पराजयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Overcoming, surpassing, defeating.<BR>E.<BR>पर before जि to conquer, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=505" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराजित|पराजितः
पराजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Conquered, defeated, overcome.<BR>2 Won at dice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परा encounter, and जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्च
पराञ्च or पराच्<BR>mfn. (पराङ् पराची पराक्)<BR>Turned away, inverted, reversed.<BR>E.<BR>परा away, अञ्च to go, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराञ्ज|परांजः|पराञ्जः
पराञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 An oil mill.<BR>2 Froth or foam.<BR>3 The blade of a sword or knife: see परञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्पर|परात्परः
परात्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Superior to the best.<BR>E.<BR>पर in the fifth case, and repeated in the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परात्प्रिय|परात्प्रियः
परात्प्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A kind of reed, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परादन|परादनः
परादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A horse of the Persian breed.<BR>E.<BR>परा exceeding, अदन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधि|पराधिः
पराधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Hunting, the chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिकार
पराधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Another person's office or post.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधिकारचर्च्चा|पराधिकारचर्चा
पराधिकारचर्च्चा<BR>f. (-र्च्चा)<BR>Officiousness, interference with another's concerns.<BR>E.<BR>पराधिकार, and चर्च्चा searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीन|पराधीनः
पराधीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dependant, subject, subservient.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, and अधीन humble, docile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराधीनता
पराधीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Subjection, dependance.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, पराधीनत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परानसा
परानसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The practice of medicine, administering remedies.<BR>E.<BR>परान enemies, (disease,) षो to destroy, aff. ड; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्न|परान्नं|परान्नः
परान्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Living at another's expense.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Food supplied by another.<BR>2 Food dressed or touched by or belonging to another.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परान्नभोजिन्
परान्नभोजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जी)<BR>Living at another's cost.<BR>E.<BR>परान्न, and भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराप|परापं
पराप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>A place, &c. whence water has retired.<BR>E.<BR>पर away, अप water; also परेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापतत्
परापतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>Coming back quickly, returning hastily.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and आङ before पत to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परापर|परापरं|परापरः
परापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Best and worst, prior and posterior, in front and behind, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>(In Logic,) Community of property intermediate between the greatest and smallest numbers: species, as being between genus and individual.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Guru of an intermediate class, a term applied in the Tantras to the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अपर another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभव|पराभवः
पराभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Discomfiting, overcoming.<BR>2 Contempt, disrespect, disgrace.<BR>3 Destruction.<BR>E.<BR>परा disgrace, भू to be, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराभूत|पराभूतः
पराभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Defeated, discomfited, overcome.<BR>2 Degraded, humbled, treated with contempt.<BR>E.<BR>परा disgrace, and भू been, become, from भू with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्श|परामर्शः
परामर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Discrimination, discriminating, distinguishing, judgment.<BR>2 (In Logic,) Drawing conclusions from analogy or experience.<BR>E.<BR>परा implying supremacy, &c. मृश to deliberate, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामर्ष
परामर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Forbearance.<BR>E.<BR>परा, and मृष to bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृत|परामृतं
परामृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Raining.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, अमृत water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परामृष्ट|परामृष्टः
परामृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Weighed, considered, judged.<BR>2 Connected with.<BR>3 Touched or affected by.<BR>4 Borne, endured.<BR>E.<BR>पर and आङ् before मृश to deliberate, or मृष to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायण|परायणं
परायण<BR>mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Adherence to any pursuit, attachment to any object.<BR>2 Dependance upon.<BR>adj.<BR>1 Adhering or attached to.<BR>2 Connected with, depending upon.<BR>3 Wished, desired.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A religious order or division.<BR>E.<BR>पर only, (one object,) अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परायत्त|परायत्तं
परायत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Dependant, subject.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, आयत्त tame, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारि
परारि<BR>ind.<BR>The year before last.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (last,) अरि aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारित्न|परारित्नः
परारित्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Belonging to the year before last.<BR>E.<BR>परारि as above, and त्न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारु|परारुः
परारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>वृ to fill or satisfy, आरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परारुक|परारुकः
परारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stone or rock.<BR>E.<BR>परारु a gourd, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थ|परार्थः
परार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Having another object or sense, &c.<BR>2 Designed or purposed by another.<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>For the sake or good of another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्थवादिन्
परार्थवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Officious, intermeddling.<BR>E.<BR>परार्थ, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्द्ध|परार्द्धं
परार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>1 A great number, a lack of lacks of crores, or a number equal to half the term of BRAHMA'S life, or as many mortal days as are equal to fifty of his years.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परार्द्ध्य|परार्द्ध्यः
परार्द्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-र्द्ध्यः-र्द्ध्या-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>Excellent, chief, principal, best.<BR>n. (-र्द्ध्यं)<BR>An immense or infinite number: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>परा best, अर्द्ध part, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावज्ञा
परावज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Indignity, insult, (received.)<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अवज्ञा disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर
परावर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Before and after, prior and subsequent.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अवर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त|परावर्त|परावर्तः|परावर्त्तः
परावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Retreat, turning back.<BR>2 Exchange, barter.<BR>3 Reversal of a sentence.<BR>4 Restoration.<BR>E.<BR>परा, वृत to be, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त्य
परावर्त्त्य<BR>mfn. (-र्त्त्यः-र्त्त्या-र्त्त्यं)<BR>1 To be turned back.<BR>2 To be exchanged.<BR>3 To be reversed, (as a sentence.)<BR>4 To be given back or restored.<BR>E.<BR>परा, वृत to be, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावर्त्त्यव्यवहार
परावर्त्त्यव्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Appeal, (in law.)<BR>E.<BR>परावर्त्त्य to be reversed, व्यवहार judicial procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराविद्ध|पराविद्धः
पराविद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>पर an enemy, आविद्ध frightened; being a very cowardly deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्त
परावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Fled, retreated, turned back.<BR>2 Turned round, revolved.<BR>3 Exchanged.<BR>4 Reversed, (as a judgment.)<BR>5 Given back, restored.<BR>E.<BR>परा before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परावृत्ति|परावृत्तिः
परावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Returning, retreating, turning back.<BR>2 Revolving.<BR>3 Exchange, barter.<BR>4 Reversion of a judgment.<BR>5 Restoration of property.<BR>E.<BR>परा before वृत to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशर|पराशरः
पराशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The father of the poet. VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, शु to complete, with आङ् prefixed, and अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराशरिन्
पराशरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A beggar, a wandering mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>पराशर the rules of PĀRĀŚARA or VYĀSA, the founder of the tribe, and इनि aff.; also पाराशरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रय|पराश्रयः
पराश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dependant or relying upon another.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Dependance.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=506" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराश्रित
पराश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subject, dependant.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and आश्रित having refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासन|परासनं
परासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>पर an enemy, अस to throw or cast, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासिसिषु
परासिसिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>1 Desirous to throw or send.<BR>2 Wishing to overcome.<BR>E.<BR>पर before अस to throw, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासु|परासुः
परासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Dead, expired.<BR>E.<BR>पर away, remote, असु vital breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परासुता
परासुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Death, extinction.<BR>2 Drowsiness, sleepiness.<BR>E.<BR>परासु, and तल् aff. or with त्व, परासुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्कन्दिन्|परास्कंदिन्
परास्कन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>A thief, a robber.<BR>E.<BR>पर another's property. स्कन्द to steal, with आङ् prefix, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परास्त|परास्तं
परास्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Thrown, tossed.<BR>2 Expelled, turned out.<BR>3 Defeated.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अम to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह|पराहः
पराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The next day.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अह, for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराहत
पराहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Assailed, attacked.<BR>2 Struck.<BR>E.<BR>पर, आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पराह्न
पराह्न<BR>n. (-ह्नं)<BR>The afternoon, the latter part of the day.<BR>E.<BR>पर after, (past,) अह a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परि
परि<BR>A particle and prefix to words implying.<BR>1 Ubiquity, (all round, on every side.)<BR>2 Part, portion.<BR>3 Abandonment, (away.)<BR>4 End, term.<BR>5 Sickness, infirmity.<BR>6 Enforcement, stress, (even, very, great.)<BR>7 Separateness, several distributions, (each by each, &c.)<BR>8 Embracing, encircling, (round, roundabout.)<BR>9 Depreciation, exposure of faults.<BR>10 Homage, respect.<BR>11 Rejection, turning off or away.<BR>12 Ornament.<BR>13 Diffusion, extension.<BR>14 Mark or sign.<BR>15 Sorrow.<BR>16 Cessation, stop, impediment.<BR>17 Truth.<BR>18 An exclamation of pleasure or satisfaction.<BR>As परिकर्त्तुं, to adorn; परिक्षिप्लुं, to abandon; परिछेत्तुं, to divide; परिदेधितुं, to lament; परिक्षिप्लुं, to embrace; परिव्रजितुं, to go about, to wander, &c.: see the following compound nouns.<BR>E.<BR>पृ to complete, to satisfy, aff. इन; in combination with roots forming nouns by घञ्, the इ of परि is sometimes optionally lengthened, as परी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकथा
परिकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>A work of fiction, a tale, a story, the history or adventures of any fabulous person.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying ornament, and कथा a tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकम्प|परिकंप|परिकंपः|परिकम्पः
परिकम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>1 Fear, terror.<BR>2 Trembling.<BR>E.<BR>परि very great, कम्प a trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर|परिकरः
परिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what helps or assists.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bed.<BR>2 Dependants, retinue, train.<BR>3 Multitude, numbers.<BR>4 A firm girth, a waist, a zone or sash.<BR>5 Commencement.<BR>6 Discrimination, judgment.<BR>7 Covert or indirect intimation of wish or purpose.<BR>8 Unusual meaning or expression.<BR>E.<BR>परि round about, कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्त्तन|परिकर्तन|परिकर्तनं
परिकर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cutting, cutting off or round, a circular incision.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and कृत to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्त्तिका|परिकर्तिका
परिकर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sharp shooting pain, especially in the rectum.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and कृत to cut, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्म्मन्|परिकर्मन्
परिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Personal decoration, dressing, painting or perfuming the body.<BR>2 Perfuming the person after bathing.<BR>3 Cleansing, purifying.<BR>4 Arithmetical computation.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A servant, a slave.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying ornament, and कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्म्माष्टक|परिकर्माष्टक
परिकर्म्माष्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The eight rules of arithmetic.<BR>E.<BR>परिकर्म्म, and अष्टक eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्म्मिन्|परिकर्मिन्
परिकर्म्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>Adorning, decorating.<BR>mf. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी)<BR>A slave, a servant.<BR>E.<BR>परिकर्म्म decoration, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पन|परिकल्पनं
परिकल्पन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Contriving, making, inventing.<BR>2 Doing what is necessary, tending, providing food, rest, &c.<BR>3 Dividing.<BR>4 Settling, agreeing upon.<BR>E.<BR>परि, कृप to be able, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पित
परिकल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made, invented.<BR>2 Divided.<BR>3 Tended, waited upon, provided with all necessaries.<BR>4 Settled, agreed.<BR>E.<BR>परि before कृप to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकाङ्क्षित|परिकांक्षित|परिकांक्षितः|परिकाङ्क्षितः
परिकाङ्क्षित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A devotee, a religious ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>परि gone, काङ्क्षा wish, and इतच् aff.; having no earthly desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्ण
परिकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Spread, diffused, scattered around or about.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, कीर्ण scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्त्तन|परिकीर्तन|परिकीर्तनं
परिकीर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Saying, telling.<BR>2 Talking of, boasting.<BR>E.<BR>परि before कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्त्तित|परिकीर्तित
परिकीर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, declared, promulgated.<BR>2 Vaunted or boasted of.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and कीर्त्तत famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकूट|परिकूटं
परिकूट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A barrier, a trench before the gate of a town, forming a sort of covered way.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, कूट a fort or house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकृश
परिकृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Emaciate, thin, wasted.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and कृश thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रम|परिक्रमः
परिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Walking, going.<BR>2 Walking round or about, circumambulating, going about.<BR>3 Roaming, going about.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, around, क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रमसह|परिक्रमसहः
परिक्रमसह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>परिक्रम going about, and सह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रय|परिक्रयः
परिक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Redemption, purchasing or purchasing back.<BR>2 Giving up part of a treasure to preserve the rest.<BR>E.<BR>परि, क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रामत्
परिक्रामत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>Going, going round or about.<BR>E.<BR>परिक्रम to go, round, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रिया
परिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Enclosing, surrounding with a fence or ditch, &c. intrenching.<BR>E.<BR>परि round about, क्रिया making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिश
परिक्लिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Vexation, trouble.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, क्लिश to be vexed, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिष्ट
परिक्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Vexed, annoyed.<BR>E.<BR>परि before क्लिश to be wearied, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षत
परिक्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wounded, abraded, cut, scratched, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before क्षत broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षति|परिक्षतिः
परिक्षति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Wounding, lesion.<BR>E.<BR>परि before क्षति rupture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षय|परिक्षयः
परिक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Waste, decay, dissolution, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>परि before क्षि to waste, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षा
परिक्षा<BR>m. (-क्षा)<BR>Mud, dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षित्
परिक्षित्<BR>m. (-क्षित्)<BR>The name of a king, the son of ABHIMANYU, and grand-son of ARJUNA; see परीक्षित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिपक
परिक्षिपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what scatters, disperses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before क्षिप to throw, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्त|परिक्षिप्तं
परिक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, encircled, intrenched.<BR>2 Scattered, thrown about, diffused.<BR>3 Left, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>परि round about, क्षिप to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=507" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीण
परिक्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Wasted, worn away, decayed.<BR>2 Diminished, decreased.<BR>3 Lost, destroyed.<BR>4 (In Law,) Insolvent.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and क्षीण emaciate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीव
परिक्षीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Drunk.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and क्षीव drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेप|परिक्षेपः
परिक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Scattering, spreading, diffusion.<BR>2 Surrounding.<BR>3 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेपिन्
परिक्षेपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Who or what scatters or distributes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, क्षिप to throw, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखा
परिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A moat, a ditch surrounding a fort, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, खन to dig, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्यात|परिख्यातः
परिख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ख्यात said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्याति|परिख्यातिः
परिख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fame, reputation.<BR>E.<BR>परि on every side, ख्याति notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणित|परिगणितः
परिगणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reckoned, calculated.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and गणित counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगत|परिगतः
परिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Sought, inquired after.<BR>3 Obtained, gained.<BR>4 Forgotten.<BR>5 Diffused, spread.<BR>6 Obstructed, detained.<BR>7 Encircled, encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, &c. and गत gone, become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगम|परिगमः
परिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Surrounding.<BR>2 Seeking for.<BR>3 Knowing, ascertaining.<BR>4 Obtaining.<BR>5 Spreading, extending.<BR>E.<BR>परि before गम to go, अच् aff.; also with ल्युट्, परिगमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमित
परिगमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought, conducted, driven.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and गम to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलित
परिगलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Flowing, fluid.<BR>2 Melted.<BR>E.<BR>परि before गल to ooze, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीत
परिगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Taken, accepted.<BR>2 Assented, consented to.<BR>3 Obeyed.<BR>4 Opposed, checked.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ग्रह to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृह्य
परिगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be taken or accepted.<BR>2 To be regarded.<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>A woman.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Considering, looking upon.<BR>E.<BR>परि encircling, ग्रह to take, aff. यत् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रह|परिग्रहः
परिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Acceptance, taking.<BR>2 Assent, consent.<BR>3 Dependants, a family, a train or retinue.<BR>4 A wife.<BR>5 Root, origin.<BR>6 An oath.<BR>7 The reserve of an army, a corps posted with the general, four hundred yards in the rear of the line: see प्रतिग्रह.<BR>8 Maintaining, observing.<BR>9 Continued possession, continuance.<BR>10 Subjugation, making subservient or subject.<BR>11 Connexion, concern, business or interference with.<BR>12 Comprehension.<BR>13 The sun near the moon's node.<BR>E.<BR>परि intensitive prefix, or round about, &c. and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राह|परिग्राहः
परिग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A mound or place prepared for a burnt offering at a ceremony which requires three or four such places, placed to the north or east, &c. as उत्तरपरिग्राह, पूर्व्वपरिग्राह.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, ग्रह to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्लान
परिग्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wearied out, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>परि intensitive, ग्लान wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघ|परिघः
परिघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A bludgeon, a stick mounted with iron, or an iron club.<BR>2 Killing, striking, destroying.<BR>3 The nineteenth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>4 The pin or bolt of a door.<BR>5 A glass vessel.<BR>6 A pike, a spear.<BR>7 A water jar.<BR>8 The outer door or gate of a palace: see पलिघ.<BR>E.<BR>परि round about, हन to kill, अप् aff., घ substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्टित
परिघट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed repeatedly.<BR>2 Much handled or touched.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and घट्टित rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघात|परिघातः
परिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Killing, striking.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, हन to kill, aff. घञ्, and the root changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातन|परिघातनं|परिघातनः
परिघातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Striking, hurting, killing.<BR>2 A staff or bludgeon armed with iron.<BR>E.<BR>परि before हन to kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघोष|परिघोषः
परिघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Sound.<BR>2 Improper or blameable discourse.<BR>3 The muttering or grumbling of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>परि intensitive or depreciative prefix, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचय|परिचयः
परिचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>2 Accumulation.<BR>3 Meeting with a friend.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, चि to gather, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयनीय
परिचयनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be known.<BR>2 To be collected.<BR>E.<BR>परि before चि to heap, aff. अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर|परिचरः
परिचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A guard, a body-guard.<BR>2 An attendant, a companion, a servant.<BR>3 A commander-in-chief.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्य्या|परिचर्या
परिचर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 Service, dependance.<BR>2 Veneration, worship.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, चर to go, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचाय्य|परिचाय्यः
परिचाय्य<BR>m. (-य्यः)<BR>1 A place for preparing or holding a sacrificial fire.<BR>2 Sacrificial fire in general.<BR>3 Raising the rent or revenue of land.<BR>E.<BR>परि worship, &c. चि to collect, aff. ण्यत, form specifick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारक|परिचारकः
परिचारक<BR>m. (-ऊः)<BR>A servant, an attendant.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, चर to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचार्य्य|परिचार्य|परिचार्य्यः
परिचार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-य्य)<BR>To be served or obeyed, to be worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>परि before चर to go, ण्यत aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचित|परिचितः
परिचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, acquainted with.<BR>2 Heaped, accumulated.<BR>E.<BR>परि before चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचेतव्य
परिचेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्य)<BR>1 To be known, fit or proper to be known as an acquaintance.<BR>2 To be collected together.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and चेतव्य to be gathered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचेय|परिचेयं
परिचेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be collected all round, or from every side.<BR>2 To be known as an acquaintance.<BR>E.<BR>परि before चि to collect, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्युत
परिच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lost, gone, deprived or devoid of.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद|परिच्छदः|परिछद
परिच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Court, train, attendants, retinue.<BR>2 Family, dependants.<BR>3 Goods and chattels, personal property.<BR>4 Dress, paraphernalia.<BR>5 Covering.<BR>6 Clothes.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, छद to cover, aff. (-घ.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्द|परिच्छंद|परिच्छंदः|परिच्छन्दः
परिच्छन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Retinue, train.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, छद to cover, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिछन्न|परिच्छन्न|परिच्छन्नः
परिछन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Covered, clothed.<BR>2 Invested, enclosed.<BR>3 Having a retinue or paraphernalia.<BR>E.<BR>परि before छद to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिछित्ति|परिच्छित्ति|परिच्छित्तिः
परिछित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Partition, separation, &c.: see परिछेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिछिन्न|परिच्छिन्न|परिच्छिन्नः
परिछिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Detached, divided, cut off.<BR>2 Resisted, remedied.<BR>E.<BR>परि before छिद to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिछेद|परिच्छेद|परिच्छेदः
परिछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Segment, division, cutting or severing.<BR>2 Discrimination.<BR>3 Limit, boundary.<BR>4 Obviating, remedying.<BR>5 The division of a book, a section or chapter.<BR>6 Moderation.<BR>E.<BR>परि successively, severally, छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिछेदन|परिच्छेदन|परिच्छेदनं
परिछेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Dividing, division.<BR>2 Discriminating.<BR>3 The division of a book.<BR>4 Laughter, expressive of joy.<BR>E.<BR>परि before छिद to divide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=508" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजन|परिजनः
परिजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Dependants, servants, family, followers.<BR>3 Train, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजल्पित|परिजल्पितं
परिजल्पित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The covert reproaches of a mistress neglected or ill used by her lover.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and जल्पित prattling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञात
परिज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Known, ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञातृ
परिज्ञातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-ची-तृ)<BR>Wise, intelligent, one who has knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ज्ञा to know, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञान|परिज्ञानं
परिज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge, ascertainment, discrimination.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञाय
परिज्ञाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having known or ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and ज्ञाय having known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्मन्
परिज्मन्<BR>m. (-ज्मा)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, जन to be born, Uṇādi aff. मन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्वन्
परिज्वन्<BR>m. (-ज्वा)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, जु to be quick, Uṇādi aff. वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिडीनक|परिडीनकं
परिडीनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The flight of a bird in circles.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, डीन or डीनक flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ripe, mature.<BR>2 Bowed, bent.<BR>3 Aimed at, directed to, inclined to.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An elephant stooping to strike with his tusks.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Capital, stock, wealth accumulated for the sake of profit.<BR>E.<BR>परि before नम to bend or bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणति|परिणतिः
परिणति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Bending, bowing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, नम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणय|परिणयः
परिणय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>परि successively or individually, णी to take, अच् aff.; also with ल्युट् aff. परिणयन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाम|परिणामः
परिणाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Change of form or state.<BR>2 Maturity, fulness, ripeness.<BR>3 End, last stage or state.<BR>E.<BR>परि before नम to bend, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामदर्शिन्
परिणामदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Who looks forward or to the end.<BR>E.<BR>परिणाम, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामनिरोध
परिणामनिरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Human vicissitude; as birth, growth, death, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परिणाम, and निरोध obstruction, (of final felicity.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामपथ्य
परिणामपथ्य<BR>mfn. (-थ्यः-थ्या-थ्यं)<BR>Suited to a future stage or condition.<BR>E.<BR>परिणाम, and पथ्य good for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामशूल|परिणामशूलः
परिणामशूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Flatulence with pain or vomiting after eating, dyspepsia.<BR>E.<BR>परिणाम, and शूल colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाय|परिणायः
परिणाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Leading or taking round.<BR>2 Moving a piece at chess, draughts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, णी to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायक|परिणायकः
परिणायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, णी to take, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाह|परिणाहः
परिणाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Width, breadth.<BR>2 Circumference of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>परि extension, नह to bind, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसक
परिणिंसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what eats of feeds upon.<BR>2 Who or what kisses.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, निसि to kiss, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसा
परिणिंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Kissing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before निसि to kiss, अङ् and टाप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिनंसु
परिणिनंसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Seeking to take or lay hold of.<BR>E.<BR>परि, नश to lose, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीत
परिणीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Married.<BR>E.<BR>परि before णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणेतृ
परिणेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>परि before णी to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितस्
परितस्<BR>ind.<BR>Around, every way, all round.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिताप|परितापः
परिताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Pain, anguish.<BR>2 Sorrow.<BR>3 A division of hell.<BR>4 Heat, warmth.<BR>5 Fear.<BR>6 Trembling.<BR>E.<BR>परि exceeding, ताप burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्ट|परितुष्टः
परितुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pleased, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोष|परितोषः
परितोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Pleasure, satisfaction, delight.<BR>E.<BR>परि entirely, तोष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यक्त
परित्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Void or deprived of, left, quitted, abandoned.<BR>2 Let go, let fly as an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and त्यक्त left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यजन|परित्यजनं
परित्यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Distributing, dispersing.<BR>2 Abandoning.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, त्यज to abandon, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यज्य
परित्यज्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>परि before त्यज to leave, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्याग|परित्यागः
परित्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Abandonment, quitting, desertion.<BR>2 Loss, privation.<BR>E.<BR>परि away, त्याग quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यागिन्
परित्यागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Abandoning, quitting.<BR>E.<BR>परि before त्यज to quit, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्याज्य
परित्याज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>To be left or abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>परि before त्यज to leave, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रस्त
परित्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Afraid.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, चल alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्राण|परित्राणं
परित्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Warding a blow, self-defence.<BR>2 Preserving, protecting.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदर|परिदरः
परिदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sponginess of the gums.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and दर rending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदहन|परिदहनं
परिदहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Scorching, burning.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and दह to burn, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदान|परिदानं
परिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Barter, exchange, returning any thing or its equivalent.<BR>E.<BR>परि reciprocally, दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदाहिन्
परिदाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Hot, scorching.<BR>E.<BR>परि before दह to burn, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवक
परिदेवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what laments or complains.<BR>E.<BR>परि before दिव to play, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवन|परिदेवनं
परिदेवन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Lamentation, complaint, bewailing.<BR>2 Fearing.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying grief, देवन showing, playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवित|परिदेवितं
परिदेवित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Lamentation.<BR>E.<BR>परि before देव to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेविन्
परिदेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Lamenting.<BR>2 Fearing, apprehensive.<BR>E.<BR>परि before दिव to play, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधान|परिधानं
परिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A lower garment.<BR>2 Vesture, clothes.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, round, धान having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाय|परिधायः
परिधाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Retinue, attendants.<BR>2 The posteriors.<BR>3 A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>परि circling, surrounding, धा to have, घञ् aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधि|परिधिः
परिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The circumference of a circle.<BR>2 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>3 The periphery of a wheel.<BR>4 A circle surrounding the globe, a great circle.<BR>5 An epicycle.<BR>6 The branch of the tree to which the victim at a sacrifice is tied.<BR>7 A wooden frame round the hole in which a sacrificial fire is lighted.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिस्थ|परिधिस्थः
परिधिस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A guard, a body-guard.<BR>2 An aide-de-camp, an officer attendant on the king or general.<BR>E.<BR>परिधि around, (the king,) स्थ who stands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूपित
परिधूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perfumed.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and धूपित perfumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्वंस|परिध्वंसः
परिध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Injury, destruction.<BR>2 A man of a mixed caste.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ध्वंस to lose, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=509" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्व्वपन|परिनिर्वपन
परिनिर्व्वपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Distributing, dispensing, giving.<BR>E.<BR>परि and निर् before वप to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्विवप्सा
परिनिर्विवप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Liberality, wish to give.<BR>E.<BR>परि and निर् before वप to give, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्विवप्सु|परिनिर्व्विवप्सु
परिनिर्विवप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desirous of giving.<BR>E.<BR>परि and निर् before वप give, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठित
परिनिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Skilled in, acquainted with.<BR>E.<BR>परि and नि before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिन्यास|परिन्यासः
परिन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Completing the sense of a passage.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and न्यास position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्व
परिपक्व<BR>mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>1 Cooked, dressed.<BR>2 Mature.<BR>3 Shrewd, knowing.<BR>4 Digested.<BR>E.<BR>परि before पक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्वता
परिपक्वता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Being dressed or cooked.<BR>2 Maturity, perfection.<BR>3 Shrewdness.<BR>4 Digestion.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपण|परिपणं
परिपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Capital, principal, stock.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, पण price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणित
परिपणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pledged, plighted, agreed, promised.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and पण to pledge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपदिन्
परिपदिन्<BR>n. (-दी)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>परि against, पद to go, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थक|परिपन्थकः
परिपन्थक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An enemy, an antagonist.<BR>E.<BR>परि opposition, पन्थक who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपन्थिन्|परिपंथिन्
परिपन्थिन्<BR>m. (-न्थी)<BR>1 An enemy, an antagonist.<BR>2 A robber, a highwayman, a bandit.<BR>E.<BR>परि obstacle or opposition, पन्थिन् who goes the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाक|परिपाकः
परिपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Being cooked or dressed.<BR>2 Maturity, perfection.<BR>3 Cleverness, shrewdness.<BR>4 Digestion.<BR>5 The fruit or consequence of actions.<BR>E.<BR>परि before पच to cook or ripen, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाकिन्
परिपाकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Who or what cooks, ripens, digests, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A drug, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, पच to ripen, aff. णिनि, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटि|परिपाटिः
परिपाटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>1 Order, method, arrangement.<BR>2 Arithmetic.<BR>E.<BR>परि several distribution, पाटि proceeding, from पठ to go, in the causal form, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालन|परिपालनं
परिपालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Protecting, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and पालन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालित
परिपालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Protected, cherished.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and पालित protected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपिष्टक|परिपिष्टकं
परिपिष्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपुटन|परिपुटनं
परिपुटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Peeling, desquamation.<BR>E.<BR>परि before पुट to reduce, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपुष्करा
परिपुष्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (C. madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजन|परिपूजनं
परिपूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worshipping, adoring.<BR>E.<BR>परि before पूज to worship, ल्युट् aff.; also परिपूजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूजित
परिपूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Served, worshipped, adored.<BR>E.<BR>परि, पूज to worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूत|परिपूतं
परिपूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pure, purified.<BR>2 Winnowed, threshed, freed from the chaff.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and पूत pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्ण
परिपूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Full, entire, complete.<BR>2 Satisfied, content.<BR>E.<BR>परि quite, पूर्ण full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्णता
परिपूर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Completion, entireness, fulness.<BR>2 Satiety or satisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely. पूर्णता fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपूर्णत्व|परिपूर्णत्वं
परिपूर्णत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Completion, &c.: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and पूर्णत्व fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेल|परिपेलं
परिपेल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>परि extension, पेल to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपेलव|परिपेलवं
परिपेलव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A grass: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>as above, वन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेप्सु
परिप्रेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desiring, seeking.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and प्र before आप to obtain, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेषण|परिप्रेषणं
परिप्रेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Abandoning, leaving, sending or putting away.<BR>E.<BR>परि before प्रेष to send, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्रेषित
परिप्रेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, left, put or sent away.<BR>E.<BR>परि before प्रेष to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लव|परिप्लवं|परिप्लवः
परिप्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>2 Unsteady, restless, moveable.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Bathing, wetting with water, immersing, inundation.<BR>2 Oppression, tyranny.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, प्लव what goes, from प्लु to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिप्लुत|परिप्लुतः
परिप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Immersed, inundated.<BR>2 Wetted, bathed.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>परि every where, प्लु to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्ह|परिबर्हः
परिबर्ह<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>1 Retinue, train.<BR>2 Insignia of royalty.<BR>3 Wealth.<BR>4 Thing, substance.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, or a mark, a sign, बर्ह to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभङ्ग|परिभंग|परिभंगः|परिभङ्गः
परिभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Breaking to pieces, shattering.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभव|परिभवः
परिभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Disrespect, contempt, disgrace.<BR>2 Defeat, discomfiture.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying depreciation, and भव being; also परिभाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवपद
परिभवपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Disgrace, a disgraceful situation.<BR>E.<BR>परिभव, and पद degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवास्पद
परिभवास्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A situation of disgrace or defeat.<BR>E.<BR>परिभव, and आस्पद situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभविन्
परिभविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Treating with contumely or disrespect.<BR>2 Suffering disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भू to be, णिनि aff. der. irr. or परिभव, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाव|परिभावः
परिभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Disrespect: see परिभव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाविन्
परिभाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>1 Irreverent, disrespectful.<BR>2 Putting to shame, surpassing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भू to be, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावुक
परिभावुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Who or what shames or humbles another.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भू to be, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषण|परिभाषणं
परिभाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Reproof, abuse, ridicule, expression of censure or contempt.<BR>2 Addressing, discourse, conversing.<BR>3 Agreement, engagement.<BR>4 Rule, precept.<BR>E.<BR>परि exposure of faults, or mutually, &c., भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषणीय
परिभाषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Reprehensible, liable to or deserving reproof.<BR>2 To be addressed or spoken to.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भाष to speak, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषा
परिभाषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A technicality, a conventional term in any science.<BR>2 (In Grammar,) A maxim given by the ancient grammarians as a summary interpretation of the rules of PĀṆINI.<BR>3 (In Medicine,) Prognosis.<BR>4 Abuse, ridicule.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, and भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषित
परिभाषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said.<BR>2 Formed or used technically.<BR>E.<BR>परि, भाष to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुक्त
परिभुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Enjoyed, possessed.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and भुज to enjoy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूत|परिभूतं
परिभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Treated with contempt or disrespect, disregarded, despised.<BR>E.<BR>परि exposure of fault, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=510" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूय
परिभूय<BR>ind.<BR>Disgracing, shaming, outvieing, having disgraced, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भू to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोक्तृ
परिभोक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्ती-क्तृ)<BR>1 One who uses another's property without leave.<BR>2 Possessing, one who possesses or enjoys.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and भुज to enjoy, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोग|परिभोगः
परिभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Using or living upon another person's property without leave or improperly.<BR>2 Possession, enjoyment.<BR>E.<BR>परि, भुज to enjoy, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रम|परिभ्रमः
परिभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Wandering, going about.<BR>2 Error.<BR>E.<BR>परि before भ्रम to roam, घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट्, परिभ्रमणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रष्ट
परिभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Fallen, degraded, deprived of.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and भ्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डल|परिमंडल|परिमण्डलं|परिमण्डलः
परिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A ball, a globe, a circle.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, and मण्डल a sphere or circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलता
परिमण्डलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rotundity, circularity.<BR>E.<BR>परिमण्डल, and तल् aff.; also परिमण्डलत्वं, with त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमण्डलित
परिमण्डलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rounded, made round or circular.<BR>E.<BR>परिमण्डल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमन्द|परिमंद
परिमन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>1 Little, a little, not much.<BR>2 Slow.<BR>3 Dull.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and मन्द slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्द्दन|परिमर्दन|परिमर्दनं
परिमर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing, grinding.<BR>2 Embracing, pressing.<BR>3 Trampling or destroying.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and मर्द्दन rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमल|परिमलः
परिमल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An exquisite scent, especially arising from the trituration of fragrant substances.<BR>2 The trituration of perfumes.<BR>3 Copulation.<BR>4 A meeting of learned men.<BR>5 Soil, stain, dirt.<BR>E.<BR>परि extension, मल to increase, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलित
परिमलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Soiled, despoiled of freshness or beauty.<BR>2 Perfumed.<BR>E.<BR>परिमल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्श|परिमर्शः
परिमर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>1 Contact, propinquity.<BR>2 Friction.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and मृश to touch, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमर्ष|परिमर्षः
परिमर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Envy, dislike.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृष to bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ग|परिमार्गः
परिमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Friction.<BR>2 Touch.<BR>3 Cleaning, wiping.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृज to clean, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्गितव्य
परिमार्गितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be sought after.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मार्ग to search, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ग्य|परिमार्ग्यं
परिमार्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>1 To be cleaned or cleansed.<BR>2 To be rubbed.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, मृज to clean, ण्यत् aff.; also परिमृज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाण|परिमाणं
परिमाण<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>1 Measure.<BR>2 Measuring.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, and माण measuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाणीय
परिमाणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be measured.<BR>E.<BR>परि, before, मा to measure, अनीयर् aff.; also परिमातव्य and परिमेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमार्ज्जन|परिमार्जन|परिमार्जनं
परिमार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>2 A dish of honey and oil.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, मृज to cleanse, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमित|परिमितं
परिमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Joined.<BR>2 Meted, measured.<BR>3 Regulated.<BR>E.<BR>परि, मा to measure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमितभुज्
परिमितभुज्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>Temperate, abstemious.<BR>E.<BR>परिमित, and भुज् who eats or enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमिताहार
परिमिताहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Eating moderately.<BR>E.<BR>परिमित, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृज्य|परिमृज्यं
परिमृज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>1 To be cleaned.<BR>2 To be touched.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृज to clean, aff. क्यप्; also परिमार्ग्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृदित
परिमृदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed, ground.<BR>2 Embraced, clasped.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृद to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृष्ट
परिमृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Rubbed, touched.<BR>2 Embraced, clasped.<BR>3 Invested.<BR>4 Spread, pervaded.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृष to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमृष्यत्
परिमृष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>1 Envying.<BR>2 Rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मृष to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमेय|परिमेयं
परिमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Measurable, to be measured.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मा to measure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोषिन्
परिमोषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A thief, a robber.<BR>E.<BR>परि every where, मुष to steal, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोहन|परिमोहनं
परिमोहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fascinating, beguiling.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and भोहन fascinating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमोहिन्
परिमोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>What is bewitching, fascinating, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before मुह to be foolish, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिम्लान
परिम्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Soiled, stained.<BR>2 Waned, withered.<BR>3 Diminished, impaired.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Soil.<BR>2 Change of countenance by fear or grief.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and म्लान dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरक्षण|परिरक्षणं
परिरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Guarding, defending, preserving.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरटन
परिरटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Crying, crying aloud.<BR>E.<BR>परि before रट to cry, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरब्ध
परिरब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Embraced.<BR>2 Encircled.<BR>E.<BR>परि before रभ to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरभमाण
परिरभमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and रभ to begin, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरभ्यमाण
परिरभ्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being embraced.<BR>E.<BR>परि every where, रभ to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरम्भ|परिरंभ|परिरंभः|परिरम्भः
परिरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Embrace, embracing.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, रभ to begin, aff. घञ्, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरम्भन
परिरम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before रभ to begin, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिराटिन्
परिराटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>Crying, crying aloud, screaming, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before रट to cry, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिरिप्समान
परिरिप्समान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wishing or trying to embrace.<BR>E.<BR>परिरभि to embrace, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलुप्त
परिलुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Gone, lost.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, लुप्त lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिलुप्तसञ्ज्ञ|परिलुप्तसंज्ञ
परिलुप्तसञ्ज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ञ्ज्ञः-ञ्ज्ञा-ञ्ज्ञं)<BR>Senseless.<BR>E.<BR>परिलुप्त, and सञ्ज्ञा sign of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवत्सर|परिवत्सरः
परिवत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>परि end, वत्सर a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवदन|परिवदनं
परिवदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Reviling, accusing.<BR>2 Crying out, clamouring, screaming.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वद to speak, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्जन|परिवर्जनं|परिवर्ज्जनं
परिवर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Quitting, abandonment.<BR>E.<BR>परि finally, वृज to shun, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्ज्जित|परिवर्जित
परिवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abandoned.<BR>2 Devoid of.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृज to shun, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्त|परिवर्त|परिवर्तः|परिवर्त्तः
परिवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Going or turning back.<BR>2 Turning round, revolving.<BR>3 Flight, retreat, desertion.<BR>4 Exchange, barter.<BR>5 Requital, return.<BR>6 The end of a period of four ages, or destruction of the world.<BR>7 A chapter, a book, a canto, &c.<BR>8 The king of the tortoises, or the tortoise incarnation.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, &c. वृत to be, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तक|परिवर्तक|परिवर्तकं
परिवर्त्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Who or what turns back or round.<BR>2 Who or what requites, exchanges, &c.<BR>3 Leaving off a thing begun for some other object.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वृत to be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तन|परिवर्तन|परिवर्तनं|परिवर्त्तनं
परिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Turning back or round, returning.<BR>2 Turning round, revolving.<BR>3 Barter, exchange.<BR>4 Requital, return. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">Page512</a>]<BR>5 Inverting, taking or putting any thing in a wrong direction.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, &c. वर्त्तन being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=511" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तित|परिवर्तित
परिवर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Turned round, revolved.<BR>2 Returned, retreated.<BR>3 Taken or put on in a wrong direction.<BR>4 Exchanged.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्त्तिन्|परिवर्तिन्
परिवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ति-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>1 Revolving, going round.<BR>2 Returning.<BR>3 Flying, retreating.<BR>4 Exchanging.<BR>5 Requiting, recompensing.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वृत to be, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्द्धन
परिवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Growing, increasing.<BR>2 Rearing, breeding, (as of cattle.)<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्द्धित
परिवर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Increased, augmented.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृद्ध to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्ह|परिवर्हः
परिवर्ह<BR>m. (-र्हः)<BR>1 Train, retinue, dependants.<BR>2 Royal insignia.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, वर्ह to cover, घञ् aff.; also परिबर्ह^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 314. note: cf WIL paribarha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवसथ|परिवसथः
परिवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, वसथ a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाद|परिवादः
परिवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Abuse, reproach, reproof.<BR>2 Charge, accusation.<BR>3 The bow or quill of the lute or fiddle.<BR>E.<BR>परि censure, &c. and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवादक|परिवादकः
परिवादक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An accuser, a plaintiff, a complainant or calumniator.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying censure, वद to speak, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवादिन्
परिवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Who or what reproaches, accuses, &c.<BR>2 Censured, abused.<BR>3 Calling out, crying, screaming.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An accuser, a reprover; (in Law,) a plaintiff.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A lute or a Vīṇā, with seven strings.<BR>E.<BR>परिवाद as above, इनि aff. or परि before वद to speak, धिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाप|परिवापः
परिवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Shaving, shearing.<BR>2 A pool, a pond, a piece of water.<BR>3 Train, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, वप to shave, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवापन|परिवापनं
परिवापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaving, shearing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, वप to cut or shave, causal v. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवापित|परिवापितं
परिवापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaven, shorn.<BR>E.<BR>परिवाप shaving, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवार|परिवारः
परिवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Dependant.<BR>2 Train or retinue.<BR>3 A scabbard, a sheath.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, वृ to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवारता
परिवारता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Subjection, dependance.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to परिवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवारित
परिवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, enclosed or begirt by.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वारित impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवास|परिवासः
परिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Abiding, abode.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वस to dwell, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवासित
परिवासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Respectfully attentive to superiors.<BR>E.<BR>परि respect, वस to abide, aff. क्त, and इट inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाह|परिवाहः
परिवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An inundation, an overflowing, natural or artificial.<BR>2 A water course or a drain to carry off excess of water.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, वह to bear, aff. घञ्; also परीवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाहवत्|परिवाहवन्त्
परिवाहवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A pond or pool.<BR>E.<BR>परिवाह a drain, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवाहित
परिवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drained.<BR>E.<BR>परिवाह, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविण्ण|परिविण्णः
परिविण्ण<BR>m. (-ण्णः)<BR>An unmarried elder brother whose junior is married.<BR>E.<BR>परि before विद to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवित्ति|परिवित्तिः
परिवित्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>An unmarried elder brother, the younger being married and a householder.<BR>E.<BR>परि abandoning, and विद to cover, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविन्दक|परिविंदक|परिविंदकः|परिविन्दकः
परिविन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A younger brother married or become a householder before the elder.<BR>E.<BR>परि, विद to possess, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविन्दत्|परिविंदत्
परिविन्दत्<BR>m. (-न्दन्)<BR>An unmarried elder brother.<BR>E.<BR>परि before विद to know, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविष्ट
परिविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Surrounded, enclosed.<BR>2 Offered, presented.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and विष to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविष्णु
परिविष्णु<BR>ind.<BR>Entirely or every where VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, विष्णु VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविह्वल
परिविह्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Agitated, bewildered.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and विह्वल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिविह्वलता
परिविह्वलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Bewilderment.<BR>E.<BR>परिविह्वल, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवीत
परिवीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, encompassed, invested.<BR>2 Overspread, pervaded.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The bow of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and वी to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहण|परिवृंहणं
परिवृंहण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Augmenting, enlarging, what enlarges or adds to.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An appendix, an additional work or section.<BR>E.<BR>वृहि to increase, with परि prefixed, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहित
परिवृंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Increased, augmented.<BR>2 Improved, thriven.<BR>3 Sounded.<BR>4 Lightened, illuminated.<BR>5 Excited, stimulated.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृहि to augment, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृढ|परिवृढः
परिवृढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A master, an owner, a superior.<BR>E.<BR>परि exceeding, वृह to thrive, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत|परिवृतः
परिवृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>2 Gained or received entirely.<BR>3 Known.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृ to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्त
परिवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Gone round, revolved.<BR>2 Turned back, retreated, retired.<BR>3 Exchanged.<BR>4 Finished, ended.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृत to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्ति|परिवृत्तिः
परिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Exchange, barter.<BR>2 Revolution, return.<BR>3 End, termination.<BR>5 An unmarried elder brother: see परिवित्ति.<BR>4 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>E.<BR>परि mutually, वृत to be, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृत्य
परिवृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having retreated or retired.<BR>2 Having turned round or revolved.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वृत to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृस्ति
परिवृस्ति<BR>m. (-स्तिः)<BR>An elder brother unmarried: see परिवित्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृहित|परिवृहितं
परिवृहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Increased, literally or figuratively, grown, thriven.<BR>2 Making effort, exerted.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, वृह to grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेत्तृ
परिवेत्तृ<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>A younger brother married or become a householder before his elder.<BR>E.<BR>परि abandoning, (the usual practice,) विद to know or possess, (a wife,) तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेदन|परिवेदनं
परिवेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Anguish, pain, misery.<BR>2 Marriage, marrying.<BR>3 Discussion.<BR>4 Gain, acquisition.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Shrewdness, wit.<BR>2 Foresight, prudence.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, विद to know, &c. aff. ल्युट्, or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेदिन्
परिवेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Shrewd, knowing.<BR>2 Suffering pain.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of a younger brother, the elder brother being unmarried.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and विद to know, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेश|परिवेशः
परिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>2 The circumference of a circle.<BR>2 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, विश or विष to encompass, aff. अच्; hence also परिवेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष|परिवेषः
परिवेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Surrounding, encircling.<BR>2 The circumference of a circle.<BR>3 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>4 Distributing rice, &c. to a party, serving up a meal: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेषण|परिवेषणं
परिवेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Surrounding, enclosing.<BR>2 Serving up dinner, distributing food to guests, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, वेषण encompassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=512" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष्टन|परिवेष्टनं
परिवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>2 Circumference.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वेष्ट to surround, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवेष्टित|परिवेष्टितं
परिवेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Enclosed, surrounded, encompassed.<BR>2 Covered, veiled.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, and वेष्टित surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्याध|परिव्याधः
परिव्याध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A tree, (Pterospermum acerifolia.)<BR>2 A sort of reed growing in water, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>परि much, व्याध pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्रज्या
परिव्रज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 Ascetic devotion, religious austerity, abandonment of the world.<BR>2 Leading the life of a mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, व्रज्या religious wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्रढिमन्
परिव्रढिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Masterhood, superiority.<BR>E.<BR>परिवृढ, and इमनिच् aff., ऋ changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज्
परिव्राज्<BR>m. (-ड् or ट्)<BR>The man of the last religious order, the mendicant devotee.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, व्रज to go, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel made long; also with घञ् aff. परिव्राज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज|परिव्राजः
परिव्राज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An ascetic: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राजक|परिव्राजकः
परिव्राजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, व्रज to wander, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिव्राज्य
परिव्राज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>The state or condition of an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>परिव्राज् as above, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशङ्कनीय|परिशङ्कनीयः
परिशङ्कनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be doubted, to be feared or apprehended.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, शकि to doubt, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशाप
परिशाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Cursing, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>परि before शप to curse, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशिष्ट|परिशिष्टं
परिशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Left, remaining.<BR>2 Finished.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A supplement, an appendix.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशुद्ध
परिशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Cleaned.<BR>2 Purified.<BR>3 Discharged, paid.<BR>E.<BR>परि before शुध to be pure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशुष्क|परिशुष्कं
परिशुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>Dry, dried.<BR>n. (-ष्कं)<BR>Meat fried, first with ghee, washed well with warm water, and dressed with spice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, शुष्क dried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशेष|परिशेषः
परिशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Remainder.<BR>2 Completion.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशोध|परिशोधः
परिशोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Cleansing, purifying, correcting.<BR>2 Discharging a debt or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and शोध purifying; also परिशोधनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिशोष|परिशोषः
परिशोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Drying, evaporation.<BR>E.<BR>परि before शुष to be dry, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रम|परिश्रमः
परिश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Labour, trouble, pain.<BR>2 Distress, fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>परि exceeding, श्रम weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रय|परिश्रयः
परिश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An assembly, a meeting.<BR>2 An asylum.<BR>E.<BR>परि, before श्री to serve, &c. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रान्त|परिश्रान्तः
परिश्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Overcome with distress or fatigue, exhausted, wearied.<BR>E.<BR>परि before श्रम to be weary, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रान्ति|परिश्रांति|परिश्रांतिः|परिश्रान्तिः
परिश्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Labour, trouble.<BR>2 Fatigue, exhaustion.<BR>E.<BR>परि before श्रम to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्रुत|परिश्रुतः
परिश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heard.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्लिष्ट
परिश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Embraced, clasped.<BR>E.<BR>परि before श्लिष to embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिश्लेष|परिश्लेषः
परिश्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and श्लेष embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषत्त्व
परिषत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The formation or collection or functions of an assembly.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्
परिषद्<BR>f. (-षद् or -षत्)<BR>An assembly, a meeting, an audience or congregation.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, षद to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद|परिषदः
परिषद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A spectator at a play, one of an assembly or congregation.<BR>E.<BR>परिषद् as above, and अण् aff., whence it is more usually पारिषद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्य|परिषद्यः
परिषद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>One of a party or assembly, a spectator, a guest.<BR>E.<BR>see परिषद, यत् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिषद्वल|परिषद्वलः
परिषद्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An assistant in an assembly, an associate.<BR>2 A spectator, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परिषद as above, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कन्द|परिष्कंद|परिष्कन्दः
परिष्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A foster child, one nourished by a stranger: see परिस्कन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कन्न
परिष्कन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A foster child, or one nourished by a stranger: see परिस्कन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कार|परिष्कारः
परिष्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Decoration, embellishment.<BR>2 Cooking, dressing.<BR>3 Finishing, polishing.<BR>4 Initiation, purification by essential rites.<BR>5 Surrounding.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying ornament, and कार making, स inserted, and changed to ष; also in the same sense परिस्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृत|परिष्कृतः
परिष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Adorned, decorated, embellished.<BR>2 Highly finished or polished.<BR>3 Cooked, dressed.<BR>4 Purified by initiatory^1 rites.<BR>5 Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>परि before कृ to make, aff. क्तः see the last.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृतभूमि|परिष्कृतभूमिः
परिष्कृतभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>An altar, or ground prepared for a sacrifice, or for the victim and the utensils employed.<BR>E.<BR>परिष्कृत, and भूमि ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्कृति|परिष्कृतिः
परिष्कृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Finishing, polishing, &c.: see परिष्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्टोम|परिष्टोमः
परिष्टोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An elephant's coloured housings: see परिस्तोम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्ठल|परिष्ठलं
परिष्ठल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Surrounding place or site.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्वङ्ग|परिष्वंग|परिष्वंगः|परिष्वङ्गः
परिष्वङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ष्वजि to embrace, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिष्वज्य
परिष्वज्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having embraced.<BR>E.<BR>परि, ष्वजि to embrace, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्या|परिसंख्या
परिसङ्ख्या<BR>f. (-ङ्ख्या)<BR>1 Total or complete enumeration or specification, implying exclusion of any other.<BR>2 Reckoning, enumerating.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सङ्ख्य a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्यात|परिसंख्यात
परिसङ्ख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Counted, enumerated.<BR>2 Reckoned up or specified exclusively of any more.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सङ्ख्यात counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसङ्ख्यान|परिसंख्यान|परिसंख्यानं
परिसङ्ख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Exclusive enumeration or specification.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सङ्ख्यान reckoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसभ्य|परिसभ्यः
परिसभ्य<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>An assistant at an assembly.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, सभ्य a fellow guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमापन|परिसमापनं
परिसमापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Finishing entirely.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सम, before आप to get, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमाप्त
परिसमाप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Finished, done entirely.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and समाप्त finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसमाप्ति|परिसमाप्तिः
परिसमाप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Entire completion.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सम before आप to obtain, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर|परिसरः
परिसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Ground on the skirts of a river or mountain, or contiguous to a town, &c.<BR>2 Death, dying.<BR>3 Rule, precept, prescribed mode.<BR>4 Part, place, site.<BR>5 Width, breadth.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, or end, term, &c. सर going, from सृ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्प|परिसर्पः
परिसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>1 Encompassing, surrounding.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 Following, pursuing.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, and सर्प going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=513" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसर्य्या|परिसर्या
परिसर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 Perambulation, wandering round or about.<BR>2 Near approach.<BR>2 Service.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, सृ to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसाधन
परिसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>2 Determining, ascertaining.<BR>E.<BR>परि before साध to accomplish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसार|परिसारः
परिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wandering about.<BR>E.<BR>परि before सृ to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसारिन्
परिसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Wandering.<BR>E.<BR>परि before सृ to go, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसीमन्
परिसीमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Boundary, extreme term or limit.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and सीमन् a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसेधन्
परिसेधन्<BR>mfn. (-धन्-धन्ती-धत्)<BR>Opposing.<BR>E.<BR>परि against, षिघ to effect, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिसेसिचा
परिसेसिचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>Frequent bathing or sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>परि before पिच to sprinkle, frequent. v. (अङ्,) and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्द|परिस्कंद|परिस्कन्दः
परिस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A foster child, one nourished by a stranger.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>Going round or about.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, स्कदि to go, aff. अच्; also स being optionally changed, परिष्कन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्दत्|परिस्कंदत्
परिस्कन्दत्<BR>mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दन्ती-न्दत्)<BR>1 Going round or about.<BR>2 Surrounding, circumambulating.<BR>3 Wandering.<BR>E.<BR>परि, स्कदि to go, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्कन्न|परिस्कन्नः
परिस्कन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A foster or an adopted child.<BR>2 The Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>परि before स्कन्द to go, aff. क्त; also परिष्कन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तृत
परिस्तृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, spread over.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्तृत strewed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्तोम|परिस्तोमः
परिस्तोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An elephant's painted or coloured cloth or housings.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, स्तु to applaud, aff. क्त, irregular form, मन् being substituted for the proper termination; also परिष्टोम when considered as a compound of परि and स्तोम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्थान|परिस्थानं
परिस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Fixedness, solidity.<BR>2 Fortitude, firmness.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्थान place; also परिस्थिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्द|परिस्पंद|परिस्पंदः|परिस्पन्दः
परिस्पन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Beating, throbbing.<BR>2 Decoration of the hair, with flowers, &c.<BR>3 Train, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, स्पन्द to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्दन|परिस्पन्दनं
परिस्पन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Beating, throbbing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before स्पदि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्पन्दमान|परिस्पन्दमानः
परिस्पन्दमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Moving tremulously, being gently agitated, shaking, trembling.<BR>2 Throbbing, beating.<BR>E.<BR>परि before स्पदि to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरण|परिस्फुरणं
परिस्फुरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Glancing, shooting.<BR>2 Budding.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्फुर to expand, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरत्
परिस्फुरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Budding, expanding.<BR>2 Bursting forth.<BR>3 Darting, glancing, moving quickly or suddenly.<BR>4 Gleaming.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्फुर to expand, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्फुरित
परिस्फुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Glancing, gleaming.<BR>2 Opened, expanded.<BR>3 Shot, glanced.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्फुर to expand, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्यन्द|परिस्यंद|परिस्यंदः|परिस्यन्दः
परिस्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Oozing, dropping.<BR>2 Decoration of the hair: see परिस्यन्द.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, स्यन्द to drop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्यन्दन
परिस्यन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dropping, flowing, oozing.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and स्यदि to drop, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रुत्
परिस्रुत्<BR>f. (-स्रुत्)<BR>1 Vinous liquor.<BR>2 Dropping, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>परि before स्रु to distil, aff. क्विप् and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिस्रुत|परिस्रुतः
परिस्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Oozed, trickled, dropped, distilled.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Vinous or distilled liquor.<BR>E.<BR>परि before स्रु to drop or ooze, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरण|परिहरणं
परिहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Seizing, taking.<BR>2 Leaving, abandoning.<BR>3 Avoiding.<BR>4 Disappearing.<BR>5 Refuting, repelling.<BR>E.<BR>परि before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरणीय
परिहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be shunned or avoided.<BR>2 To be taken away.<BR>3 To be confuted.<BR>E.<BR>परि, हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरणीयता
परिहरणीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Disappearance, unattainableness.<BR>2 Refutation.<BR>E.<BR>परिहरणीय to be taken away, तल् abst. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरत्
परिहरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Illuding.<BR>2 Shunning, avoiding.<BR>E.<BR>परि, हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहरमाण
परिहरमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Leaving, quitting.<BR>2 Taking, seizing.<BR>3 Confuting.<BR>E.<BR>परि before हृ to take, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहर्त्तव्य|परिहर्तव्य
परिहर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be shunned or avoided.<BR>2 To be taken away.<BR>3 To be confuted.<BR>E.<BR>परि before हृ to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहार|परिहारः
परिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Disrespect.<BR>2 Seizing, surrounding.<BR>3 Bounty, largess.<BR>4 Any thing or person objectionable.<BR>E.<BR>परि, हृ to take away, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहार्य्य|परिहार्य|परिहार्यः|परिहार्य्यः
परिहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be shunned or avoided.<BR>2 To be taken off or away.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A bracelet: see परिहार्य्य.<BR>E.<BR>परि, हृ to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहास|परिहासः
परिहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Mirth, sport, pastime.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, हस to laugh, aff. घञ्; also परीहास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहासवेदिन्
परिहासवेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A jester, a wag, a wit.<BR>E.<BR>परिहास, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहित
परिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, invested, put on.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and हित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहीण
परिहीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Waned, faded, wasted.<BR>2 Deserted by, deprived of.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and हीण quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिहृत|परिहृतः
परिहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Avoided, quitted.<BR>2 Taken.<BR>E.<BR>परि before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षक|परीक्षकः
परीक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Investigating acutely, trying, examining.<BR>(-कः)<BR>1 An experimenter, an assayer, a prover.<BR>2 An investigator, a judge.<BR>E.<BR>परि well, closely, ईक्ष to look or see, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षण|परीक्षणं
परीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Trial, experiment, examination.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, ईक्ष to see, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षणीय
परीक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be tried or investigated, to be submitted to ordeal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff; also परीक्षितव्य and परीक्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षा
परीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Discrimination, investigation, examination, test, trial, experiment.<BR>2 Trial by ordeal of various kinds: see दिव्य.<BR>E.<BR>परि intensitive prefix, before ईक्ष to see, aff. अङ् and टाप्; looking into any thing or person closely and minutely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षित्
परीक्षित्<BR>m. (-क्षित्)<BR>The grandson of ARJUNA, to whom the Bhāgavata was related.<BR>E.<BR>परि before, क्षि to destroy, क्विप् aff. also with a final vowel परीक्षितः he was destroyed in his mother's womb, but reanimated by KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीक्षित|परीक्षितः
परीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tried, examined, tested, proved.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A prince: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>परि before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणाय|परीणायः
परीणाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Moving a piece at chess, draughts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि before णी to take, aff. घञ्, the vowel of the prefix is optionally made long; also परिणाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीत|परीतं
परीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>2 Circumambulated.<BR>3 Addicted, affected by.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=514" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीतत्
परीतत्<BR>mfn. (-तत्)<BR>Every way spread or extended.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, तन to spread, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix augmented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीत्य
परीत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having passed round or circumambulated.<BR>2 Having encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>परि before इण् to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीधाविन्
परीधाविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>The forty-first year of the Indian cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीभाव|परीभावः
परीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>see परिभाव, the vowel of the prefix being here made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीयमाण
परीयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being penetrated or pervaded by.<BR>E.<BR>परि before इङ् to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीर|परीरं
परीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Fruit.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy, Uṇādi aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीरम्भ|परीरंभ|परीरंभः|परीरम्भः
परीरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>An embrace: see परिरम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवर्त्त|परीवर्त|परीवर्तः|परीवर्त्तः
परीवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Exchange, barter.<BR>2 The royal tortoise: see परिवर्त्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवाद|परीवादः
परीवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Reproof, censure, abuse.<BR>2 The bow or quill of a lute: see परिवाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवार|परीवारः
परीवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sheath of a sword.<BR>2 Dependants, family, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, वृ to cover, aff. घञ्, and the final of परि made long; also परिवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीवाह|परीवाहः
परीवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A drain or channel made to carry off water from a pond that overflows.<BR>2 A natural inundation or overflow.<BR>3 Royal insignia.<BR>4 A sword sheath, a scabbard.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वह to bear, aff. घञ्, and the इ of परि is in consequence optionally long; also परिवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीष्टि|परीष्टिः
परीष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Inquiry, research, especially philosophical.<BR>2 Service.<BR>3 Willingness, readiness.<BR>E.<BR>परि much, इष्टि wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीसार|परीसारः
परीसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Going round or about, wandering, perambulation.<BR>2 Near approach.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीहार|परीहारः
परीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Disrespect.<BR>2 An open space for the pasturage of cattle near a village or town.<BR>3 Remedying or atoning for any improper action.<BR>E.<BR>परि disrespect, हृ to convey, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीहास|परीहासः
परीहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Mirth, sport, amusement.<BR>E.<BR>परि pleasure, हस to laugh, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परु|परुः
परु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A knot or joint in a read.<BR>2 Paradise.<BR>3 The ocean.<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill, aff. उ, also परुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुत्
परुत्<BR>ind.<BR>Last year.<BR>E.<BR>पर prior, उत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुत्न
परुत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Of or belonging to last year.<BR>E.<BR>परुत last year, त्न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुद्वार|परुद्वारः
परुद्वार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुष|परुषं
परुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Harsh, abusive, (speech.)<BR>2 Rough, rugged.<BR>3 Severe, cruel, unkind.<BR>4 Variegated in colour.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Harsh, and contumelious speech, abuse.<BR>2 Yellow Barleria.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A sort of tree, (Xylocarpus granatum.)<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill or satisfy, उषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषवचन
परुषवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Harsh language, reproach, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>परुष, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषवाच्
परुषवाच्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>Harsh spoken.<BR>f. (-क्)<BR>Harsh or contumelious speech.<BR>E.<BR>परुष, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषोक्ति
परुषोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Abusive or harsh language.<BR>E.<BR>परुष, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुषोक्तिक|परुषोक्तिकः
परुषोक्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An abuser, one uttering harsh and scurrilous language.<BR>E.<BR>परुष abuse, and उक्ति speech, aff. कप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परुस्
परुस्<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>The knot or joint of a cane or reed.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to complete, Uṇādi aff. उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परूष|परूषं
परूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The Parush tree: see परुष; also with कन् added परूषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेत|परेतः
परेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead, defunct.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A kind of goblin, a ghost, a spirit.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (world,) इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेतर
परेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Faithful, friendly.<BR>E.<BR>पर an enemy, इतर other, opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेतराज्
परेतराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>परेत a ghost, and राज who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेद्यवि
परेद्यवि<BR>ind.<BR>Next day, to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, एद्यवि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेद्युस्
परेद्युस्<BR>ind. (-द्युः)<BR>Next day.<BR>E.<BR>परे after, द्युस् for दिवस a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेप|परेपं
परेप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Where water is lodged or retired, whence it has, (a place, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पर, and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टि|परेष्टिः
परेष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, इष्टि worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परेष्टुका
परेष्टुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow bearing many calves.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, इप to go, तु aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परैधित|परैधितः
परैधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Nourished by a stranger.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>पर a stranger, एधित nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्ष|परोक्षं|परोक्षः
परोक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Invisible, imperceptible.<BR>2 Absent.<BR>3 Past.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An ascetic, a religious hermit.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Invisibility, absence, secrecy.<BR>2 (In Grammar,) Past time or tense.<BR>E.<BR>पर before उक्ष to sprinkle, aff. क; or पर away, अक्षि the eye, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षभोग|परोक्षभोगः
परोक्षभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Enjoyment or possession of any thing in the absence of the proprietor.<BR>E.<BR>परोक्ष, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षवृत्ति|परोक्षवृत्तिः
परोक्षवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>One who does any thing whilst absent.<BR>E.<BR>परोक्ष, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोक्षार्थ
परोक्षार्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>An absent or invisible object.<BR>E.<BR>परोक्ष, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोत्कर्ष|परोत्कर्षः
परोत्कर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Another's superiority.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उत्कर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोदित
परोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said by an enemy, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Clamour, menace.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकार|परोपकारः
परोपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Charity, benevolence, doing good to others.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, उपकार assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकारिन्
परोपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Benevolent, charitable, good to others.<BR>E.<BR>परोपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपकृत
परोपकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Helped or befriended by another.<BR>2 Brought by another.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उपकृत assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपजाप|परोपजापः
परोपजाप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>The dissension of enemies.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उपजाप dissension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपदेश|परोपदेशः
परोपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Giving advice, counselling, admonishing.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उपदेश instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोपरुद्ध
परोपरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Invested, besieged, blockaded.<BR>E.<BR>पर, and उपरुद्ध surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोवरीण|परोवरीणः
परोवरीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having both superior and inferior, prior and subsequent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, अवर lowest, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परोष्णी
परोष्णी<BR>f. (-ष्णी)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>पर best, उष्णा warmth; it is also written परोष्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्कट|पर्कटः
पर्कट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Regret, anxiety.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्क्कटि|पर्कटि|पर्कटिः
पर्क्कटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>The waved-leaf fig tree, (Ficus infectiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पृच to touch, अटि aff., ङीष् optionally added; also with इन् added पर्क्कटिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्क्कटिन्|पर्कटिन्
पर्क्कटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>The waved-leaf fig tree: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्जनी|पर्ज्जनी
पर्जनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>पृ to satisfy, aff. क्विप्, जन to produce, aff. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=515" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ज्जन्य|पर्जन्य|पर्जन्यः|पर्ज्जन्यः
पर्ज्जन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A thunder cloud.<BR>3 The muttering of clouds or distant thunder.<BR>4 Any cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, (rain,) Uṇādi aff. अन्य, and ज or य substituted for ष; also पर्य्यन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण<BR>r. 10th cl. (पर्णयति)<BR>To make or be green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ण|पर्णं|पर्णः
पर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 The Pān or betel leaf.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa).<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 An aquatick plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>2 The leaf of the asafœtida (?)<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to please, and Uṇādi aff. न, fem. ff. ङीष्, or पर्ण to be or make green, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णकार|पर्णकारः
पर्णकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A vender of Pān leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णकृच्छ्र|पर्णकृच्छ्रः
पर्णकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>Living upon leaves and water for a limited term, as a religious obligation.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णखण्ड|पर्णखंड|पर्णखण्डः
पर्णखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A tree without apparent blossoms.<BR>2 A tree in general.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णध्वत्
पर्णध्वत्<BR>mfn. (-ध्वत्)<BR>Causing the falling of leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण leaf, ध्वंस to fall, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णनर|पर्णनरः
पर्णनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man of leaves, an effigy stuffed with leaves, made to represent a person deceased, whose body cannot be found, and for whom obsequial rites are performed with this representative.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णभेदिनी
पर्णभेदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A tree, Priyangu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णभोजन|पर्णभोजनः
पर्णभोजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A goat.<BR>2 Any animal eating leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णमाचाल|पर्णमाचालः
पर्णमाचाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Kāmaraṅga, an acid fruit; (Averhoa carambola.)<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, मच to be tall, aff. आलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णमृग|पर्णमृगः
पर्णमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Any wild animal lodging in the boughs of trees, as a monkey, a sloth, a squirrel.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and मृग deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णलता
पर्णलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The betle plant.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णवल्ली
पर्णवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and वल्ली a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णशाला
पर्णशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A hut of leaves and grass, a hermitage.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णसन्तर
पर्णसन्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Sleeping on leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, and सन्तर a bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णसि|पर्णसिः
पर्णसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A summer or water house.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to delight, Uṇādi aff. असि, and नुङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णाल|पर्णालः
पर्णाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A boat.<BR>2 A spade or hoe.<BR>3 Single combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णाशन|पर्णाशनः
पर्णाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Feeding on leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण, a leaf, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णास|पर्णासः
पर्णास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A Tulasi tree with few leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णासि|पर्णासिः
पर्णासि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>A sort of Basil, (Ocymum sanctum), with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, असि to go, (beautiful,) aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णिन्
पर्णिन्<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 The Butea frondosa.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्णोटज|पर्णोटजं
पर्णोटज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A hut of leaves, the residence of holy anchorets, a hermitage.<BR>E.<BR>पर्ण a leaf, and उटज a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द|पर्दः|पर्द्द|पर्द्दः
पर्द<BR>r. 1st cl. (पर्दते)<BR>To fart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्द|पर्द|पर्दः|पर्द्दः
पर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 A quantity of hair.<BR>2 A fart.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to nourish, द Uṇādi aff., or पर्द to fart, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्द्दन|पर्दन|पर्द्दनं
पर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fart, farting.<BR>E.<BR>पर्दृ to fart, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प|पर्पं|पर्पः
पर्प<BR>r. 1st cl. (पर्पति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प|पर्पं|पर्पः
पर्प<BR>n. (-र्पं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 Young grass.<BR>3 A wheel chair, or one on which a cripple can move about.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to be pleased, Uṇādi aff. प, or पर्प to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्पट|पर्पटः
पर्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A medicinal plant with bitter leaves, (apparently the Oldenlandia biflora, though the Hindi name Pāpar is also applied to the Gardenia latifolia, Rox.)<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A thin crisp cake made of any pulse.<BR>2 A red aluminous earth, apparently a sort of Bol, brought from Surāt or Surāṣṭra.<BR>E.<BR>पर्प to go, and अट Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्पटद्रुम|पर्पटद्रुमः
पर्पटद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्परीक|पर्परीकः
पर्परीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to nourish, ईकन् Uṇādi aff., the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्प्पिक|पर्पिक|पर्पिकः
पर्प्पिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A cripple that moves about by the aid of a chair or cradle.<BR>E.<BR>पर्प्प a chair, &c. aff. ष्ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ब|पर्ब्ब
पर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (पर्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यङ्क|पर्यङ्क|पर्यंक|पर्यंकः|पर्यङ्कः|पर्य्यङ्कः
पर्य्यङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A bed.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, अकि to go, aff. अच्; also र being optionally changed to ल, पल्यङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यङ्कबन्धन|पर्यङ्कबन्धन|पर्य्यङ्कबन्धनं
पर्य्यङ्कबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Binding a cloth round the knees, thighs, and back, as seated on the hams.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्यङ्क, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यटन|पर्यटन|पर्यटनं|पर्य्यटनं
पर्य्यटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Wandering about, roaming.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, अटन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यनुयोग|पर्यनुयोग|पर्यनुयोगः|पर्य्यनुयोगः
पर्य्यनुयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Asking, inquiring.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, अनु according to, योग fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्त|पर्यन्त|पर्यंत|पर्यन्तः|पर्य्यन्तः
पर्य्यन्त<BR>m. (-न्तं)<BR>1 Limit, term, boundary, extent.<BR>2 End, termination, close.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Far, (limitative,) as किंपर्य्यन्तं or कियत्पर्य्यन्तं how much, how far.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तभू|पर्यन्तभू|पर्यंतभू
पर्य्यन्तभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>Ground contiguous to the skirts of a river or mountain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, अन्त term, भू earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तस्थ|पर्यन्तस्थ
पर्य्यन्तस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Limitative, boundary, confining.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्यन्त, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तस्थित|पर्यन्तस्थित
पर्य्यन्तस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bounding, confining.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्यन्त, and स्थित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्तिका|पर्यन्तिका|पर्यंतिका
पर्य्यन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Loss of all good qualities, depravity.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, अन्त end, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यन्य|पर्यन्य|पर्य्यन्यः
पर्य्यन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A thunder cloud.<BR>3 The muttering of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, अन्य Uṇādi aff., य substituted for ष; it is also read पर्जन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यय|पर्यय|पर्ययः|पर्य्ययः
पर्य्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Contrariety, opposition.<BR>2 Irregular or inverted order.<BR>3 Neglect of enjoined or customary observances.<BR>E.<BR>परि improperly, अय to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्ययण|पर्ययण|पर्ययणं|पर्य्ययणं
पर्य्ययण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A horse's saddle or housings.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, अयण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवसान|पर्यवसान|पर्यवसानं
पर्य्यवसान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>End, conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अवसान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवसित|पर्यवसित
पर्य्यवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Finished, completed, concluded.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अवसित ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्था|पर्यवस्था
पर्य्यवस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>Opposition, contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>परि opposition, अवस्था staying, station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थातृ|पर्यवस्थातृ
पर्य्यवस्थातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Opposing, obstructing, opposed to or against.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>An antagonist, an opponent, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>परि against, अव before स्था to stand or be, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थान|पर्यवस्थान|पर्यवस्थानं|पर्य्यवस्थानं
पर्य्यवस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Opposition, resistance, contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>परि against, अवस्थान being, standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवस्थित|पर्यवस्थित
पर्य्यवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Opposed to, siding with an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>परि adverse, अवस्थित staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यश्रु|पर्यश्रु
पर्य्यश्रु<BR>mfn. (-श्रुः-श्रुः-श्रु)<BR>Filled or suffused with tears.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अश्रु a tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=516" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवष्टब्ध|पर्यवष्टब्ध
पर्य्यवष्टब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Surrounded, invested.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अवष्टब्ध stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यवष्टम्भन|पर्यवष्टम्भन|पर्यवष्टंभनं
पर्य्यवष्टम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Surrounding, investing.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अवष्टम्भन obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यसन|पर्यसन|पर्यसनं
पर्य्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Casting, sending.<BR>2 Putting off or away.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and अस to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्यत्|पर्यस्यत्
पर्य्यस्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>1 Going forth, issuing.<BR>2 Investing, oversetting.<BR>3 Scattering.<BR>E.<BR>परि before अस to throw, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्त|पर्यस्त|पर्य्यस्तः
पर्य्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Fallen, descended, alighted.<BR>2 Thrown down or off.<BR>3 Overturned, upset.<BR>4 Struck, killed.<BR>5 Dismissed, laid aside.<BR>6 Bound.<BR>E.<BR>परि round, &c. अस्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यस्तिका|पर्यस्तिका
पर्य्यस्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bed.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, अस to be, aff. क्तिन्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याकुल|पर्याकुल
पर्य्याकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Agitated, anxious.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and आकुल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यागलत्|पर्यागलत्
पर्य्यागलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Dropping, falling.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and आङ् before गल to fall, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याचान्त|पर्याचान्त
पर्य्याचान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Sipped, (as water, to rinse the mouth whilst eating.)<BR>E.<BR>परि, and आचान्त sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याण|पर्याण|पर्याणं|पर्य्याणं
पर्य्याण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A saddle, a pack-saddle or cloth serving for one.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, इण् to go, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्त|पर्याप्त|पर्याप्तं|पर्य्याप्तं
पर्य्याप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Obtained, gained.<BR>2 Able, adequate.<BR>3 All, complete, entire, enough, sufficient.<BR>n. adv. (-प्तं)<BR>1 Willing, readily.<BR>2 Ably, powerfully.<BR>3 Satisfactorily.<BR>4 Unwillingly.<BR>E.<BR>परि before आप to acquire, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्तभोग|पर्याप्तभोग
पर्य्याप्तभोग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Possessing or enjoying a sufficiency.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्याप्त, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याप्ति|पर्याप्ति|पर्याप्तिः|पर्य्याप्तिः
पर्य्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Willingness, readiness.<BR>2 Obtaining, acquiring.<BR>3 Satisfaction, repletion, satiety.<BR>4 Entireness, fulness, sufficiency.<BR>5 Adequacy, competency, fitness.<BR>6 Discrimination or distinction of objects according to their natural properties.<BR>7 Preserving, guarding.<BR>8 Warding off a blow.<BR>E.<BR>परि exceeding, आप्ति obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याय|पर्याय|पर्यायः|पर्य्यायः
पर्य्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Order, arrangement, regular and methodical disposal or succession.<BR>2 Manner, kind.<BR>3 Opportunity, occasion.<BR>4 Manufacture, preparation, artificial production.<BR>5 Property of substances, as bitter, cooling, &c.<BR>6 Generic or specific character.<BR>7 Comprehensiveness, aggregation.<BR>8 The text of a vocabulary, or the order of the synonyms for any term.<BR>E.<BR>परि successively, अय to go or proceed, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यायशयन|पर्यायशयन|पर्य्यायशयनं
पर्य्यायशयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Alternate sleeping and watching.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्याय order, शयन sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यायान्न|पर्यायान्न
पर्य्यायान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Food that should have been given to some one else, as that of a Śūdra to a Brahman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्याय, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यालोचन|पर्यालोचन|पर्यालोचनं
पर्य्यालोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Looking round or about.<BR>2 Considering, deliberating.<BR>3 Knowing, recognising.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and आङ् before लोच to see, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्यास|पर्यास|पर्यासः|पर्य्यासः
पर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Inverted order or position.<BR>E.<BR>परि before अस to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्याहार|पर्याहार|पर्याहारः
पर्य्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Conveying, taking.<BR>2 A load.<BR>3 A yoke.<BR>4 Storing hay or grain.<BR>5 An ewer, a pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and आङ् before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युत्सुक|पर्युत्सुक
पर्य्युत्सुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Afflicted, sorrowful, regretting.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and उत्सुक unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदञ्चन|पर्युदञ्चन|पर्युदंचन|पर्युदंचनं|पर्य्युदञ्चनं
पर्य्युदञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Debt.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, उत् over, अञ्च to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदस्त|पर्युदस्त|पर्य्युदस्तः
पर्य्युदस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Prohibited, objected to, (as a ceremony.)<BR>2 Excepted, excluded.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and उद before अस to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युदास|पर्युदास|पर्युदासः|पर्य्युदासः
पर्य्युदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A prohibitive rule or precept.<BR>E.<BR>परि and उद before अस to throw or be, aff. घञ्; also पर्य्युदासन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युपासन|पर्युपासन|पर्युपासनं
पर्य्युपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Joining in or concurrence with any act of reverence.<BR>2 Service, worship.<BR>E.<BR>परि, and उपासना worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युपासीन|पर्युपासीन
पर्य्युपासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Seated or sitting upon.<BR>E.<BR>परि and उप before आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युप्त|पर्युप्त
पर्य्युप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Sown.<BR>2 Set as a gem in a ring.<BR>E.<BR>परि before वप to sow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युषित|पर्युषित|पर्य्युषितं
पर्य्युषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stale, not fresh.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, वस to abide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्युषितभोजिन्|पर्युषितभोजिन्
पर्य्युषितभोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>The eater of stale viands, who will be regenerated as a maggot or worm.<BR>E.<BR>पर्य्युषित stale, भोजिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्य्येषणा|पर्येषणा
पर्य्येषणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Research, investigation of duty by reasoning.<BR>2 Search, inquiry in general.<BR>E.<BR>परि severally, इष to go, with युच्, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व|पर्व्व
पर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (पर्वति)<BR>To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वक|पर्वक|पर्वकं|पर्व्वकं
पर्व्वक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The knee.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व for पर्व्वन् a joint, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वकारिन्|पर्वकारिन्
पर्व्वकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A Brahman who performs ceremonies for hire out of season.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वगामिन्|पर्वगामिन्
पर्व्वगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A man who associates with his wife on festival or holy days.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वणिका|पर्वणिका
पर्व्वणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Specks with pain on the edge of the cornea of the eye.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वन्, and कन् added; also पर्व्वणीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वत|पर्वत|पर्वतः|पर्व्वतः
पर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A mountain, a hill.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 A sort of potherb.<BR>4 A kind of fish, (Silurus pabda, HAM.)<BR>5 One of the divine Ṛṣis, a friend and rival of NĀRADA^1, and mentioned in the Mahābhārata.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व to fill, Uṇādi aff. अतच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260517. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतकाक|पर्वतकाक|पर्वतकाकः|पर्व्वतकाकः
पर्व्वतकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतज|पर्वतज
पर्व्वतज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Mountain, mountain-born.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतवासिन्|पर्वतवासिन्
पर्व्वतवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Living, &c. in the mountains.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 The Gāyatrī.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत, and वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताधारा|पर्वताधारा
पर्व्वताधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and आधार a receptacle or stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतारि|पर्वतारि|पर्वतारिः|पर्व्वतारिः
पर्व्वतारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताशय|पर्वताशय|पर्वताशयः|पर्व्वताशयः
पर्व्वताशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वताश्रय|पर्वताश्रय|पर्वताश्रयः|पर्व्वताश्रयः
पर्व्वताश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Mountaineer, living, &c. in mountains.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A fabulous animal, the Śarabha.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वतीय|पर्वतीय|पर्व्वतीयः
पर्व्वतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Mountainous, mountaineer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वधि|पर्वधि|पर्वधिः|पर्व्वधिः
पर्व्वधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a day of the month, and धि who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=517" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वन्|पर्वन्
पर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>1 A knot, a joint in a cane or body, &c.<BR>2 A name given to certain days in the lunar month, as the full and change of the moon, and the 8th and 14th of each half month.<BR>3 Particular periods of the year, as the equinox, solstice, &c.<BR>4 The moment of the sun's entering a new sign.<BR>5 A festival, a holy day.<BR>6 Opportunity, occasion.<BR>7 A chapter, a book, the division of a work.<BR>8 A moment, an instant.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill or please, Uṇādi aff. वनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वपुष्पी|पर्वपुष्पी
पर्व्वपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, also called Rāmadūtī.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a joint, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वपूर्णता|पर्वपूर्णता
पर्व्वपूर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Preparations for an assembly or festival.<BR>2 Joining, uniting.<BR>3 Completion of a festival.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a festival, and पूर्णता completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वयोनि|पर्वयोनि|पर्वयोनिः|पर्व्वयोनिः
पर्व्वयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A cane or reed, the sugarcane, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a joint, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वरीण|पर्वरीण|पर्व्वरीणं|पर्व्वरीणः
पर्व्वरीण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A festival, &c.: see पर्व्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वरुह्|पर्वरुह्
पर्व्वरुह्<BR>m. (-रुट्)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a joint, and रुह् what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वसन्धि|पर्वसन्धि|पर्वसंधिः|पर्व्वसन्धिः
पर्व्वसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>The full and change of the moon, the junction of the 15th and 1st of a lunar fortnight, or the precise moment of the full and change of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a joining of the month, and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वावधि|पर्वावधि
पर्व्वावधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A peculiar period, the end of a Parva, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व as above, and अवधि limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्व्वित|पर्वित|पर्वितः|पर्व्वितः
पर्व्वित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Silurus pabda, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शु|पर्शुः
पर्शु<BR>m. (-र्शुः)<BR>An axe, a hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>पर an enemy, शु to destroy, Uṇādi aff. कु, deriv. irr.; or स्पृश to touch, changed to पृ, and शुन् Uṇādi aff.; also परशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुका
पर्शुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A rib.<BR>E.<BR>पृ to fill, to complete, शुन् aff. and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुपाणि|पर्शुपाणिः
पर्शुपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>पर्शु an axe, and पाणि the hand, holding an axe in one hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्शुराम|पर्शुरामः
पर्शुराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The first of three RAMAS, being the sixth Avatāra of VIṢṆU, as the son of the Muni JAMADAGNI.<BR>E.<BR>पर्शु an axe, and राम RĀMA; also परशुराम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्श्वध|पर्श्वधः
पर्श्वध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>An axe, a hatchet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्ष|पर्षः
पर्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (पर्षति)<BR>1 To be kind or affectionate to.<BR>2 To be moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्
पर्षद्<BR>f. (-षद् or -षत्)<BR>An assembly, an audience.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to please, Uṇādi aff. अदि; also परिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पर्षद्वल|पर्षद्वलः
पर्षद्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An assistant at an assembly, a spectator, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्षद् as above, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल<BR>r. 1st cl. (पलति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल|पलं|पलः
पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A weight of gold or silver equal to four Karṣas or Suvarṇas; also of four or of eight Tolas, or in common use, of three Tolas, two Māṣas, and eight Rattis.<BR>2 A moment, the sixtieth part of an Indian hour.<BR>3 Flesh.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Straw after threshing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पल to go, to move, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलक्षार|पलक्षारः
पलक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Blood.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, and क्षार what oozes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलगण्ड|पलगंड|पलगण्डः
पलगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh or mortar, compared to it, and गण्ड a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कट|पलंकट|पलङ्कटः
पलङ्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Timid, fearful, frightened.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, कट to go, aff. खच्; whose flesh shrinks with fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कर|पलंकर|पलंकरः|पलङ्करः
पलङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Bile.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलङ्कष|पलंकष|पलंकषः|पलङ्कषः
पलङ्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A Rākṣasa, an imp or goblin.<BR>mf. (-षः-षा)<BR>The Bdellium tree.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A plant, (Ruellia longifolia.)<BR>2 The ichneumon plant: see रास्ना.<BR>3 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>4 Lac, the animal dye.<BR>5 A creeper: see मुण्डीरी.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, and कष what injures, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलभा
पलभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The mid-day shadow of a gnomon, when the sun is in the equinoctial points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलव|पलवः
पलव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A snare or basket of wicker work for catching fish.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, and वा to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलल|पललं|पललः
पलल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Mud, mire, clay.<BR>3 Oil-cake or sesamum seed.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a goblin or imp.<BR>E.<BR>पल to go, Uṇādi aff. कलच्; or पल flesh, and ला to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललज्वर|पललज्वरः
पललज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Bile.<BR>E.<BR>पलल flesh, ज्वर heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललप्रिय|पललप्रियः
पललप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A raven.<BR>E.<BR>पलल, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पललाशय|पललाशयः
पललाशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Swelled neck, bronchocele.<BR>E.<BR>पलल flesh, आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाग्नि|पलाग्निः
पलाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाङ्ग|पलांग|पलाङ्गः
पलाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The Gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, गम to go or get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाण्डु|पलांडु|पलाण्डुः
पलाण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>An onion.<BR>E.<BR>पल to preserve, (from disease,) अण्डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाद|पलादः
पलाद<BR>mf. (-दः-दा)<BR>A Rākṣasa, male or female.<BR>E.<BR>पल flesh, अद who eats; also पलादन mf. (-नः-नी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाप|पलापः
पलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A halter.<BR>2 An elephant's temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलापहा
पलापहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A collyrium: see कुलत्था.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायन|पलायनं
पलायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>परा from, अयन going, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायमान
पलायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Running away.<BR>E.<BR>परा before अच् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायनपरायण
पलायनपरायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Fugitive.<BR>E.<BR>पलायन, and परायण addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलायित|पलायितः
पलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Defeated, flown, run away, retreated.<BR>E.<BR>पलायन flying, इतच् aff., or पल to go, aff. क्त, in the causal form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाल|पलालं|पलालः
पलाल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>Straw.<BR>E.<BR>पल to go, Uṇādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलालदोहद|पलालदोहदः
पलालदोहद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>पलाल straw, दोहद wishing, requiring straw for manure, or from the fruit being sometimes ripened in straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाश|पलाशं|पलाशः
पलाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Green.<BR>2 Unfeeling, unmerciful, cruel.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A leaf.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A tree bearing red blossoms, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>2 A demon, a goblin.<BR>3 A sort of Curcuma, (C. reclinata, Rox.)<BR>4 Ancient Behār or Magadhā.<BR>f. (शी)<BR>1 Lac.<BR>2 A kind of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>पल going, or flesh, अश to spread, to eat, &c. aff. अण् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशक|पलाशकः
पलाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Curcuma reclinata.<BR>2 The Pala's tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशाख्य|पलाशाख्यः
पलाशाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशाम्भा
पलाशाम्भा<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>Ajwaen: see गन्धपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलाशिन्
पलाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 A tree in general.<BR>2 A goblin.<BR>3 A sort of Mimusops, (M. kauki, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पलाश a leaf, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिक्नी
पलिक्नी<BR>f. (-क्नी)<BR>1 An old or greyheaded woman.<BR>2 A cow with calf.<BR>E.<BR>पलित grey hair, aff. ङीप्, and क्न substituted for तः see पलित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=518" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलिघ|पलिघः
पलिघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A glass vessel.<BR>2 A water pot.<BR>3 The gate way of a building.<BR>4 A wall.<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, हन to injure, घ substituted for the radical, and र changed to लः see परिघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पलित|पलितं|पलितः
पलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-क्नी-तं)<BR>Greyhaired, old.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An old man.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An old woman.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Greyness of the hair.<BR>2 Much or ornamented hair.<BR>3 Heat, burning.<BR>4 Mud, mire.<BR>5 Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>पल to go, (towards death,) Uṇādi aff. क्त, or पल flesh, &c. and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यङ्क|पल्यंक|पल्यंकः|पल्यङ्कः
पल्यङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A bedstead.<BR>E.<BR>see पर्य्यङ्क, र being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ययन|पल्ययनं
पल्ययन<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>A saddle, a pack-saddle.<BR>E.<BR>परि before अयन going, र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्युल
पल्युल<BR>r. 10th cl. (पल्युलयति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To purify; also written पल्युल्ल and पल्यूल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्यूल
पल्यूल<BR>r. 10th cl. (पल्यूलयति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To purify; also पल्युल and पल्युल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल|पल्लः
पल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (पल्लति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ल|पल्लः
पल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A large basket, or matted shed used for keeping corn, &c.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 A small village.<BR>2 A city, or rather an affix to words forming the name of a town; it is especially used in the Dekhin, as in Trichinopoly or Trisira-pallī, &c.<BR>3 A small house lizard.<BR>4 A creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>पल्ल to go, aff. अच्; also with इन् aff. पल्लि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लव|पल्लवं|पल्लवः
पल्लव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 A sprout, a shoot, the extremity of a branch bearing new leaves.<BR>2 A branch.<BR>3 Spreading, expansion.<BR>4 A wood.<BR>5 The red dye of lac.<BR>6 Love, the sentiment or passion.<BR>7 A catamite.<BR>8 A bracelet.<BR>9 Unsteadiness, moral or physical.<BR>E.<BR>पद् the foot, लू to cut or break, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवक|पल्लवकः
पल्लवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The paramour of a harlot.<BR>2 A kind of fish, (Cyprinus denticulatus.)<BR>3 A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव love, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवद्रु|पल्लवद्रुः
पल्लवद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The Asoka tree.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवाद|पल्लवादः
पल्लवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव a shoot, अद to eat, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवाधार|पल्लवाधारः
पल्लवाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A branch.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव a sprout, and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवास्त्र|पल्लवास्त्रः
पल्लवास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव a sprout or blossom, and अस्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविक|पल्लविकः
पल्लविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Amorous, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव passion, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवित|पल्लवितं|पल्लवितः
पल्लवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Having new sprouts.<BR>2 Spread, extended.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The red dye of the lac insect.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव a sprout, &c. इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविन्
पल्लविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>पल्लव a sprout, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लि|पल्लिः
पल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>1 A small village.<BR>2 Any village.<BR>3 A house.<BR>4 A number of houses.<BR>5 Any place or station.<BR>6 A house lizard: see पल्ल and पल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिका
पल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lizard.<BR>E.<BR>पल्ली, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वल|पल्वलं
पल्वल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A small pond.<BR>E.<BR>पल to go, Uṇādi aff. वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वलावास|पल्वलावासः
पल्वलावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>पल्वल a pond, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पव|पवं|पवः
पव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Winnowing corn.<BR>2 A marsh.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>4 Purification, purity.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Cow-dung.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवत्
पवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Pure, purifying.<BR>E.<BR>पू to be pure, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवन|पवनं|पवनः
पवन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Pure, clean.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Air, wind, physical or personified, as a deity.<BR>2 Winnowing grain.<BR>3 The domestic fire.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A potter's kiln.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Purifying, purification.<BR>E.<BR>पू to be or make pure, aff. ल्यु or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनव्याधि|पवनव्याधिः
पवनव्याधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 One of KṚṢṆA'S friends and advisers.<BR>2 Wind, as affected morbidly, or rheumatism, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पवन, and व्याधि sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनात्मज|पवनात्मजः
पवनात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Hanumān, the monkey hero.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>पवन wind, (the deity,) and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाल|पवनालः
पवनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Andropogon saccharatus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाश|पवनाशः
पवनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>पवन wind, and अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाशन|पवनाशनः
पवनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>पवन wind, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाशनाश|पवनाशनाशः
पवनाशनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>पवनाशन a snake, and अश who eats; feeding on the serpent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनाहत
पवनाहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken by the wind.<BR>2 Rheumatic.<BR>E.<BR>पवन, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनेष्ट|पवनेष्टः
पवनेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A large kind of Nimb tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवनोम्बुज|पवनोम्बुजं
पवनोम्बुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The Parush tree: see परुष.<BR>E.<BR>पवन air, अम्बु water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमान|पवमानः
पवमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Purifying.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 Household fire.<BR>E.<BR>पूञ् to purify, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमानात्मज|पवमानात्मजः
पवमानात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The householder's perpetual fire.<BR>E.<BR>पवमान, and आत्मज son<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवाका
पवाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A whirlwind.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवि|पविः
पवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित|पवितः
पवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purified, cleansed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवितृ
पवितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-ची-तृ)<BR>Purifying, cleansing.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्र|पवित्रं|पवित्रः
पवित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>1 Pure, clean, purified physically or morally^1.<BR>2 Who or what cleans or purifies, &c.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>2 Copper.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 Rain.<BR>5 Rubbing, cleansing.<BR>6 The vessel in which an Argha or libation or oblation is presented.<BR>7 The Brahminical cord.<BR>8 Ghee.<BR>9 Honey.<BR>10 A couple of Kusa leaves a span long, used at sacrifices to present offerings upon, or to sprinkle Ghee, &c.<BR>11 Kusa grass used to clean or purify Ghee used in a sacrifice.<BR>12 A ring of Kusa grass worn on the fourth finger on some occasions.<BR>13 A text or Mantra of the Vedas.<BR>14 Any divinity, as Agni, &c.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>2 The name of a river, a little to the north-west of Haridvār; the Pabar.<BR>3 The twelfth of the light fortnight of Śrāvaṇa, a festival in honour of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. इत्र.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रक|पवित्रकं|पवित्रकः
पवित्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Packthread, or a rope or net made of it.<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र pure, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रारोपण|पवित्रारोपणं
पवित्रारोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Investiture with the Brahminical cord.<BR>2 Investing the image of KṚṢṆA with it, on the twelfth of the light fortnight of Śrāvaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र, and आरोपण placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रारोहण|पवित्रारोहणं
पवित्रारोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The putting of the Brahminical cord on images of DURGĀ on the eighth of the light half of Srāvaṇa or Āṣārha.<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र, and आरोहण mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रित|पवित्रितः
पवित्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Clean, pure, (literally or metaphorically.)<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र purifying, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=519" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रीकरण
पवित्रीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Purification, cleansing.<BR>2 The instrument or means of purifying.<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र, and करण making, त्रि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रीकृत
पवित्रीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purified, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>पवित्र, and कृत made, त्रि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश
पश<BR>r. 1st cl. (पशति-ते) r. 10th cl. (पाशयति पशयति)<BR>1 To bind, to fetter.<BR>2 To knot or tie.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR>4 To hinder or obstruct.<BR>5 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशव्य|पशव्यं
पशव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Fit or advantageous for cattle, (meadow, pasturage, &c.)<BR>2 Possessed of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशु|पशुः
पशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 An animal in general, a beast.<BR>2 A goat.<BR>3 A subordinate deity, and one of ŚIVA'S followers.<BR>4 Any living being.<BR>5 A sacrifice, an oblation.<BR>6 The divine soul of the universe.<BR>7 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>ind.<BR>See, behold.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, पश substituted, and कु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुका
पशुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Any small animal.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and कन् dimin. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुक्रिया
पशुक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Copulation, coition.<BR>E.<BR>पशु an animal, and क्रिया action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुगायत्री
पशुगायत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A parody of the holy verse of the Vedas, whispered into the ear of an animal about to be sacrificed.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and गायत्री the Gāyatrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुघात|पशुघातः
पशुघात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Slaughter of animals for sacrifice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुता
पशुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The condition or nature of an animal, bestiality, brutality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुत्व
पशुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Sacrifice of an animal.<BR>2 Nature of an animal.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुधर्म्म|पशुधर्म|पशुधर्मः
पशुधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Action or property of animals.<BR>2 Promiscuous cohabitation.<BR>3 The marrying of widows.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and धर्म्म office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपति|पशुपतिः
पशुपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पशु living creature, and पति the master, the creator, or preserver; or पशु ŚIVA'S attendant, and पति master; or according to one legend, पशु an animal, which every deity acknowledged himself to be before his lord and master ŚIVA, when they solicited him to destroy the Asura TRIPURA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपल्वल|पशुपल्वलं
पशुपल्वल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A fragrant, grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपाल|पशुपालः
पशुपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A herdsman.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुपालन
पशुपालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tending or rearing cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and पालन protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुप्रेरण|पशुप्रेरणं
पशुप्रेरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Driving cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु a beast, प्रेरण sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुयाग|पशुयागः
पशुयाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Sacrifice of animals.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and याग sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरक्षण
पशुरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Tending cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरक्षिन्
पशुरक्षिन्<BR>m. (-क्षी)<BR>A herdsman, a shepherd.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and रक्षिन् who guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरज्जु|पशुरज्जुः
पशुरज्जु<BR>m. (-ज्जुः)<BR>A string or tie for fastening cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु an animal, and ज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुराज|पशुराजः
पशुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>पशु a beast, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुरोमन्
पशुरोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The hair of an animal.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and रोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुसम्भव|पशुसंभव
पशुसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced by an animal, (flesh, honey, butter, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and सम्भव product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुहरीतकी
पशुहरीतकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The hog plum.<BR>E.<BR>पशु an animal, हरीतकी myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुहव्य
पशुहव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Sacrifice of animals.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and हव्य oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्
पश्चात्<BR>ind.<BR>After, afterwards, behind, westward.<BR>E.<BR>पश्च considered as a substitute for अपर, and आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्ताप|पश्चात्तापः
पश्चात्ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Repentance.<BR>E.<BR>पश्चात् afterwards, ताप sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चार्द्ध
पश्चार्द्ध<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं)<BR>The remaining half or part of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>पश्व for अपर, and अर्द्ध a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिम|पश्चिमं
पश्चिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 West, western.<BR>2 Behind, after.<BR>mf. (-मः-मा)<BR>The region of VARUṆA, the west.<BR>E.<BR>पश्चात् behind, and डिमच् aff.; Hindus in their prayers, usually facing the east, and consequently having the west behind them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
पश्य<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation of wonder or admiration, (lo, behold, see.)<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, deriv. irr.; also पश्यतु and पशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्य
पश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Who or what sees.<BR>E.<BR>पश्य for दृश to see, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत्
पश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>1 Looking, seeing.<BR>2 Remarking, considering.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A harlot, a courtezan.<BR>E.<BR>दृश to see, शतृ aff. of the present participle, and root irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतस्
पश्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Visibly, in sight.<BR>E.<BR>पश्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतोहर|पश्यतोहरः
पश्यतोहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief, a pilferer, but one who steals in presence of the parties, and proverbially applied to the goldsmith, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पश्यतस् in presence of, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्ववदान
पश्ववदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sacrifice or offering of animals.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and अवदान oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्वाचार|पश्वाचारः
पश्वाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Worship of DEVI.<BR>E.<BR>पशु, and आचार instituted observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष
पष<BR>r. 10th cl. (पाषयति पषयति)<BR>1 To bind, to tie.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To oppose, to hinder.<BR>4 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस
पस<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पसति-ते पासयति पसयति)<BR>1 To bind, to fetter, to tie, to string.<BR>2 To touch.<BR>3 To oppose, to obstruct, to hinder.<BR>4 To go, to move.<BR>5 To injure or kill.<BR>(इ) पसि r. 1st and 10th cls. (पंसति पंसयति)<BR>To annual, to annihilate or destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्त्य|पस्त्यं
पस्त्य<BR>n. (-स्त्यं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>स्त्यै to collect, अप् prefixed, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्नव|पह्नवः
पह्नव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The name of one of the degraded Kṣetrīya races sentenced by SAGARA to wear beards, perhaps a Parthian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लिका
पह्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्त
पांक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Linear, in or by line, or row.<BR>E.<BR>पंक्ति a line, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशव|पांशवः
पांशव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Rock or fossile salt.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशु|पांशुः
पांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 Dust.<BR>2 Manure.<BR>3 Landed property.<BR>E.<BR>पशि to bind, Uṇādi aff. कु; also पांसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुका
पांशुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A menstruous woman.<BR>2 A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकासीस|पांशुकासीसं
पांशुकासीस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Sulphuret of iron.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, and कासीस the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकुली
पांशुकुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A principal road.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, कुल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुकूल|पांशुकूलं
पांशुकूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A blank lease, a title deed, one not made out in any person's name.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु landed property, कूल a mound, (as it were.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुचत्वर|पांशुचत्वरः
पांशुचत्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, चत्वर a level space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुचन्दन|पांशुचंदन|पांशुचन्दनः
पांशुचन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=520" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुचामर|पांशुचामरः
पांशुचामर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tent.<BR>2 A bank overgrown with Dūrbbā grass.<BR>3 Praise.<BR>4 A heap of dust.<BR>5 A small cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, चामर a chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुज|पांशुजं
पांशुज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Salt extracted from soil, rock or fossile salt.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुपत्र|पांशुपत्रं
पांशुपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुमर्द्दन|पांशुमर्दन|पांशुमर्द्दनः
पांशुमर्द्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A channel or basin for water, near or about the root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, and मर्द्दन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुव
पांशुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A cripple: see पीठसर्पिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुर|पांशुरः
पांशुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A gadfly.<BR>2 A cripple carried or moving about in a chair.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, and रा to get, क or ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुल|पांशुलः
पांशुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Dusty, covered or spotted with dust.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of ŚIVA'S weapons; a sort of pole armed at the upper end with transverse pieces, representing the breastbone and ribs adjoining, and surmounted by a skull; also खद्वाङ्ग.<BR>3 A paramour, a gallant.<BR>4 A kind of tree, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 An unchaste woman.<BR>2 A woman during menstruation.<BR>3 The earth.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु dust, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुवर्ष
पांशुवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A shower or fall of dust.<BR>E.<BR>पांशु, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसक
पांसक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Contemptible, vile.<BR>2 Vitiating, spoiling.<BR>E.<BR>पसि to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांसन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Contemptible, wicked, bad, infamous.<BR>2 Vitiating, spoiling, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>पसि to destroy, aff. ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसु|पांसुः
पांसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>1 Dust.<BR>2 Manure.<BR>E.<BR>पसि to bind, &c., aff. कु, also पांशु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा<BR>r. 1st cl. (पिवति)<BR>To drink.<BR>r. 2nd cl. (पाति)<BR>To cherish, to nourish, to protect or preserve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा<BR>mfn. (-पाः-पाः-पं)<BR>1 Who drinks.<BR>2 Who protects or cherishes.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, &c. क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Maturity, natural or artificial, as the state of being cooked or ripened.<BR>2 Cooking, dressing food.<BR>3 A vessel in which any thing is dressed, a saucepan, a boiler, &c.<BR>4 Digestion, assimilation of food.<BR>5 Suppuration, ripeness of a boil.<BR>6 Greyness of the hair.<BR>7 General panick, or the subversion of a country.<BR>8 Fear.<BR>9 An owl.<BR>10 The name of a demon.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>The young of animals.<BR>E.<BR>पच to be or become ripe, aff. घञ्, or पा to nourish, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाककृष्ण|पाककृष्णः
पाककृष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>The Caronda tree, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>पाक ripening, कृष्ण black; bearing a black fruit when ripe; also other similar compounds, as पाककृष्णफल, कृष्णपाक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकज|पाकजं
पाकज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by cooking, maturing, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Black salt.<BR>2 Flatulence.<BR>E.<BR>पाक, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपात्र
पाकपात्र<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A cooking utensil, a boiler, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाक, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकपुटी
पाकपुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A potter's kiln.<BR>E.<BR>पाक backing, पुट to heap, aff. क and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकफल|पाकफलः
पाकफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Caronda.<BR>E.<BR>पाक ripe, फल fruit, (black, understood): see पाककृष्णफल; also पाकफलकृष्ण, फलपाक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकभाण्ड|पाकभाण्डं
पाकभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A culinary utensil.<BR>E.<BR>पाक, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकमत्स्य|पाकमत्स्यः
पाकमत्स्य<BR>m. (-त्स्यः)<BR>Fish sauce.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, मत्स्या fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञ|पाकयज्ञः
पाकयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>An oblation offered on building a house, liberating a bull, &c. or a religious rite of four kinds, oblation to the VIŚVADEVAS, offerings to the spirits, the permanent obsequial rites, and hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>पाक, and यज्ञ sacrifice; the distribution of food being part of each of these ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकयज्ञिक|पाकयज्ञिकः
पाकयज्ञिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The performer of the ceremony called Pākayajña.<BR>E.<BR>पाकयज्ञ, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकरञ्जन|पाकरञ्जनं
पाकरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, रञ्ज to colour, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकल|पाकलं|पाकलः
पाकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Producing maturity.<BR>2 Suppurative, producing suppuration in a boil.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Fever in an elephant.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (C. utilatissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>पाक ripeness, ला to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकलि|पाकलिः
पाकलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of plant, (Bauhinia candida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशाला
पाकशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासन|पाकशासनः
पाकशासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पाक a demon, शासन ruling, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशासनि|पाकशासनिः
पाकशासनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The son of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पाकशासन INDRA, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकशुक्ला
पाकशुक्ला<BR>f. (-क्ला)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, burning, शुक्ल white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकस्थान|पाकस्थानं
पाकस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Cooked, dressed, ripened, naturally or artificially.<BR>E.<BR>पाक cooking, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुक|पाकुकः
पाकुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, Uṇādi aff. णुकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>What may or is to be cooked, matured, &c.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Bitloben, a medicinal salt, impregnated with iron.<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>Nitre, saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, aff. ण्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्ष
पाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>1 Belonging to a half month.<BR>2 Relating to a side or party, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षायण|पाक्षायणः
पाक्षायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Belonging to or occurring in a Pakṣa or fortnight, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष half month, &c. and फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a bird, to a fortnight, to an argument, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A fowler, a bird catcher.<BR>2 An alternative.<BR>E.<BR>पक्ष a fortnight, or पक्षिन् a bird, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाखण्ड|पाखंड|पाखंडः|पाखण्डः
पाखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A heretick, a heterodox Hindu, adopting the exterior marks of the classes, but not respecting the ordinances of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>पा for पाल what nourishes, (mankind, as virtue may be said to do,) and खडि to subvert or destroy, aff. अण्; also पाषण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाङ्क्त्य|पांक्त्य
पाङ्क्त्य<BR>m. (-ङ्क्त्यः)<BR>A Brahman who is or may be worthy to eat in a respectable society at sacrifices, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पंक्ति an assembly, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What produces maturity.<BR>2 What cooks or dresses.<BR>3 Digestive, tonic, what effects digestion.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The bile which assists in digestion.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A cook.<BR>E.<BR>पच to ripen or concoct, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचकस्त्री
पाचकस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A she cook.<BR>E.<BR>पाचक cooking, स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 What cooks or ripens, &c.<BR>2 Digestive.<BR>3 Suppurative.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A medicinal preparation, an infusion, a decoction, &c. of various drugs, chiefly carminatives or gentle stimuli given to bring the vitiated humours in fever, &c. to maturity, a sort of diet drink.<BR>2 Penance, expiation.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Acidity, sourness.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>E.<BR>पच to dress, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=521" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनक|पाचनकः
पाचनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Borax.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of diet drink: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पच to mature, (metals,) in the causal form, ल्युट् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचल|पाचलं|पाचलः
पाचल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cooking, maturing.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Wind.<BR>3 A thing dressed or matured without the aid of fire.<BR>4 Whatever ripens, cooks, causes digestion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पच in the causal form, अलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचा
पाचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>Cooking, maturing.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, causal v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचि|पाचिः
पाचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>Cooking, maturing.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचिका
पाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cooking, maturing.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्
पाजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Strength, power.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish. असुन् Uṇādi aff., and जुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चकपाल|पांचकपाल|पाञ्चकपालः
पाञ्चकपाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Relating to or part of that oblation which is offered in five cups.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चकपाल, q. v., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पांचजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्यः
पाञ्चजन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 KṚṢṆA'S conch.<BR>2 A name of fire.<BR>3 Any shell.<BR>4 A sort of fish, commonly Garae.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चजन a demon, from whose bones the shell was made, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चजन्यधर|पांचजन्यधर|पाञ्चजन्यधरः
पाञ्चजन्यधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चजन्य the conch, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चयाज्ञिक
पाञ्चयाज्ञिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to or included in the five great ceremonies.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Either of the five great sacraments.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चयज्ञ, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चभौतिक|पांचभौतिक
पाञ्चभौतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Consisting or made of the five elements.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चभूत, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चलिका
पाञ्चलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A doll, a puppet: see पाञ्चालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिक|पांचशब्दिकं|पाञ्चशब्दिकं
पाञ्चशब्दिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Musical instruments in general, or of five sorts.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्च, शब्द sound, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चार्थिक|पांचार्थिकः|पाञ्चार्थिकः
पाञ्चार्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A follower or votary of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाल|पांचाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पाञ्चाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Belonging to, dwelling in, ruling over &c. the country of Pañcāla.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sovereign of Pañcāla.<BR>2 The company or association of five trades, the carpenter, weaver, barber, washerman, and shoemaker.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चाल the country so called, and अण् aff. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चालिका|पांचालिका
पाञ्चालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A doll, a puppet: see पाञ्चाली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाञ्चाली|पांचाली
पाञ्चाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>2 A puppet, a doll.<BR>3 Melodious combination of five or six words.<BR>E.<BR>पञ्चाल the country so called, aff. of descent or reference अण्, and fem. aff. ङीप्; coming from that region; also with कन् added, पाञ्चालिका, and by making the second vowel short पाञ्चलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्
पाट्<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, in the causal form, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट|पाटः
पाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Breadth, expanse, extension.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Regular or successive order, series, succession.<BR>E.<BR>पट to spread, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटक|पाटकः
पाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The half of a village.<BR>2 A shore, a bank.<BR>3 Casting dice.<BR>4 A musical instrument.<BR>5 A large span.<BR>5 Expense or loss of capital or stock.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटञ्चर
पाटञ्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>पटच्चर the same, and अण् pleonastick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटन|पाटनं
पाटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cutting.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a pink or pale red colour.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Pale red, rose colour.<BR>2 Rice ripening in the rains.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The Trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 Red Lodh.<BR>3 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>The flower of the Bignonia suave-olens.<BR>E.<BR>पाट extension, and ला to get, aff. ड; also पाटलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलि|पाटलिः
पाटलि<BR>mf. (-लिः)<BR>Trumpet flower.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Rice ripening in the rains.<BR>E.<BR>पाटल pale red, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलित
पाटलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made red, tinted red, reddened.<BR>E.<BR>पाटल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्र
पाटलिपुत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The name of a city, supposed to be the ancient Palibothra, and the modern Patna.<BR>E.<BR>पाटलि the trumpet flower, पू to be pure, त्रन् aff.; also with कन् added, पाटलिपुत्रक; it is also said to be named after its founder and sovereign, पाटलिपुत्र being a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलोपल|पाटलोपलः
पाटलोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>पाटल, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटव|पाटवं
पाटव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Clever, sharp, dexterous.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Cleverness, talent.<BR>2 Health.<BR>3 Eloquence.<BR>E.<BR>पटु clever, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Cunning, crafty, fraudulent.<BR>2 Clever, dexterous.<BR>E.<BR>पटु clever, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटहिका
पाटहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small shrub, (Abrus precatorius): see गुञ्जा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Torn, broken, divided.<BR>E.<BR>पट to divide, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटिन्
पाटिन्<BR>m. (-टी)<BR>A sort of fish described as having many teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीर|पाटीरः
पाटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A field.<BR>2 A pungent root, a sort of radish.<BR>3 The pith or manna of the bambu.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 A sieve, a cribble.<BR>6 Tin.<BR>7 Disease arising from wind.<BR>8 Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>पट to go, &c. in the causal form, ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटूपट
पाटूपट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Going, who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to go, अच् aff. and the root repeated, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ|पाठः
पाठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 Studying the Vedas or scriptures, considered as one of the five great sacraments of the Hindus.<BR>2 Reading, perusal or study in general.<BR>(-ठा)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknidhi.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठक|पाठकः
पाठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A lecturer, a public reader of the Purāṇas or other sacred works, or a Paṇḍita who declares what is the law or custom according to the scriptures.<BR>2 A spiritual preceptor.<BR>3 A reader, a student.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, ण्वुल् aff., or पठ, causal v., वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठन|पाठनं
पाठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Lecturing, teaching.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठभू
पाठभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A place where the Vedas are read or studied.<BR>E.<BR>पाठ reading, (the Vedas,) and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठमञ्जरी
पाठमञ्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A small bird, commonly Sāri, (Gracula religiosa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशाला
पाठशाला<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A college, a school.<BR>E.<BR>पाठ study, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठशालिनी
पाठशालिनी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small bird: see पाठमञ्जरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठान
पाठान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Bdellium.<BR>2 A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Instructed, taught, lectured.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिन्
पाठिन्<BR>m. (-ठी)<BR>1 A plant, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>2 A Brahman, especially one who has finished his sacred studies.<BR>E.<BR>पाठ perusal, and इनि aff; the virtues of the plant are to be read of in medical works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीन|पाठीनः
पाठीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Silurus boalis, HAM.)<BR>2 A public reader or lecturer on the Purāṇas, &c.<BR>3 A tree: see गुग्गुल.<BR>E.<BR>पाठी a Brahman, and ईन् added<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=522" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठ्य|पाठ्यं
पाठ्य<BR>mfn. (-ट्यः-ट्या-ट्यं)<BR>To be read or studied.<BR>E.<BR>पठ to read, ण्यत् aff.; also पठणीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाडिनी
पाडिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण|पाणः
पाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Trade, traffic.<BR>2 Praise.<BR>3 The hand.<BR>E.<BR>पण to be of price, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणि|पाणिः
पाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The hand.<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>A place of sale, a shop, a market.<BR>E.<BR>पण to be of price, &c. Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिका
पाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of spoon or ladle.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिगृहीती
पाणिगृहीती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A bride, one wedded according to the ritual.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and ग्टहीत taken: see the next: when the compound means merely taken by the hand, the form is पाणिग्टहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहण|पाणिग्रहणं
पाणिग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Marriage.<BR>2 Laying hold of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and ग्रहण taking, the junction of the hands of the bride and bridegroom, forming part of this ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्रहणिक
पाणिग्रहणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Matrimonial.<BR>E.<BR>पाणिग्रहण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिग्राह|पाणिग्राहः
पाणिग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Laying hold of the hand.<BR>2 Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and ग्राह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघ|पाणिघः
पाणिघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A drummer, one who plays on a tabor, &c. with his hands.<BR>2 Playing upon a hand instrument.<BR>3 A workman, a handicraftsman.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, हन to strike, ठक् aff. and घ substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिघात|पाणिघातः
पाणिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Striking with the hands, boxing.<BR>2 A boxer, or one who strikes with his hand.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and घात blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिचापल्य
पाणिचापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Fidgeting with the hands, snapping the fingers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिज|पाणिजः
पाणिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, जन to be born, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणितल|पाणितलं
पाणितल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The palm of the hand.<BR>2 A measure of two Tolas.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन|पाणिनः
पाणिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of PĀṆINI: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनि|पाणिनिः
पाणिनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>PĀṆINI, a Muni and inspired grammarian.<BR>E.<BR>पणिन् a proper name, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं|पाणिनीयः
पाणिनीय<BR>m. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Connected with or derived from PĀṆINI, the grammarian, (as a scholar, a rule, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पाणिनि the saint, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन्धम|पाणिंधम|पाणिन्धमः
पाणिन्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Who blows through the hands.<BR>2 Obscure, dark, (as a path, where a noise is made with the hands, to frighten away snakes, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, ध्मा to blow or breathe, aff. खञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिन्धय|पाणिंधय|पाणिन्धयः
पाणिन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Who or what drinks from the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and धे to drink, स्वश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपाद|पाणिपादं
पाणिपाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The hands and feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and पाद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिपीडन|पाणिपीडनं
पाणिपीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, पीडन paining, taking: see पाणिग्रहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिभुज्
पाणिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>The glomerous fig tree, (F. glomerata.)<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and भुज् what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिमत्|पाणिमन्त्
पाणिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Possessed of hands.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिमुक्त|पाणिमुक्तं
पाणिमुक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A missile weapon, one thrown with the hand, as a dart, a spear.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and मुक्त loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिरुह्
पाणिरुह्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A nail.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and रुह to grow, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिवाद|पाणिवादः
पाणिवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A drummer, playing on a drum or tabor with the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, and वाद who sounds; also with कन् added पाणिवादक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिसर्य्या
पाणिसर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A rope, a cord.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि the hand, सृज to go, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिस्थ
पाणिस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Held in the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिहोम
पाणिहोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Offerings made to Brahmans where consecrated fire is not used.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and होम burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणीतल|पाणीतलं
पाणीतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A measure of two Tolas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणौकरण|पाणौकरणं
पाणौकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>पाणौ with the hand, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डर|पांडर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पाण्डर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Pale or yellowish white.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Pale or yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Marüa or Marūvaka.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Many-flowered jasmine.<BR>2 Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>पडि to go, अर Uṇādi aff., and the radical vowel made long; also पाण्डुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डरपुष्पिका
पाण्डरपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Śitala, (perhaps Phrynium dichotomum): see शीतला.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डर pale white, पुष्पी flower, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डव|पांडव|पांडवः|पाण्डवः
पाण्डव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Pāṇḍava or descendant of PĀṆḌU; especially applied to YUDHIṢṬHIRA and his four brothers.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु a proper name, and अण् patronymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवाभील|पांडवाभील|पाण्डवाभीलः
पाण्डवाभील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डव a Pāṇḍava, and अभी courage, (not fear,) ल who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवायन|पांडवायनः|पाण्डवायनः
पाण्डवायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पाडव a Pāṇḍava, and अयन going, accompanying; being the friend and ally of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पांडवेयः|पाण्डवेयः
पाण्डवेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A descendant of Pāṇḍu.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डित्य|पांडित्य|पांडित्यं|पाण्डित्यं
पाण्डित्य<BR>nf. (-त्यं-ती)<BR>Scholarship, learning.<BR>E.<BR>पण्डित a teacher, aff. ष्यञ्, the semivowel rejected before the feminine aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डु|पांडु|पाण्डुः
पाण्डु<BR>mfn. (-ण्डुः-ण्डुः-ण्डु)<BR>Pale or yellowish white.<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>1 Pale or yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>2 The name of a sovereign of ancient Delhi, and nominal father of YUDHIṢṬHIRA and the other four Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>3 The jaundice.<BR>4 A white elephant (?).<BR>f. (-ण्डुः)<BR>A plant, commonly Maṣāni, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>पडि to go, aff. कु, and the penultimate vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुक|पांडुकः|पाण्डुकः
पाण्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The jaundice.<BR>2 A name of Pāṇḍu.<BR>3 A pale or yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बल|पांडुकंबल|पाण्डुकम्बलः
पाण्डुकम्बल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of blanket or warm upper garment.<BR>2 A kind of stone, (Limestone or marble?)<BR>3 The housings of a royal elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, and कम्बल blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुकम्बलिन्
पाण्डुकम्बलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A carriage covered with a sort of blanket.<BR>2 The housings of a royal elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डुकम्बल a blanket, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुनाग|पाण्डुनागः
पाण्डुनाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A plant, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>2 A white elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, नाग a plant or elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपुत्त्र
पाण्डुपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>Either of the Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु and पुत्त्र son; also similar compounds, as पाण्डुनन्दन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुपृष्ठ|पाण्डुपृष्ठः
पाण्डुपृष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Having no distinguishing or auspicious mark on the body, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, &c., and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=523" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुभूम|पाण्डुभूमः
पाण्डुभूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A country with a light-coloured soil.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु, pale, and भूमि earth, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्
पाण्डुमृत्<BR>f. (-मृत्)<BR>1 A country in which the soil is of a whitish colour.<BR>2 Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, and मृत् earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुमृत्तिका|पांडुमृत्तिका
पाण्डुमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The opal.<BR>2 A pale soil.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, and मृत्तिका earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुर|पांडुर
पाण्डुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Of a yellowish white colour.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A pale or yellowish white.<BR>2 The jaundice.<BR>3 A tree: see मरुवक.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The white leprosy, vitiligo.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, and र added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरपृष्ठ|पाण्डुरपृष्ठः
पाण्डुरपृष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Having no distinguishing or auspicious marks on the body, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डुर pale, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुरद्रुम|पाण्डुरद्रुमः
पाण्डुरद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A plant, (Echites antidysenterica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुराग|पांडुराग|पाण्डुरागः
पाण्डुराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Whiteness, pallor.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुलोमा
पाण्डुलोमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A plant, (Glycine debilis)<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु pale, लोमन् hair or fibres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुवर्ण
पाण्डुवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>White.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Whiteness.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुशर्क्करा|पाण्डुशर्करा
पाण्डुशर्क्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Light-coloured gravel, (disease.)<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु, and शर्क्करा sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुशर्म्मिला|पाण्डुशर्मिला|पांडुशर्मिला
पाण्डुशर्म्मिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>E.<BR>पाण्डु a Pāṇḍu prince, शर्म्म fortune, aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्डुसोपाक|पांडुसोपाक|पाण्डुसोपाकः
पाण्डुसोपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The offspring of a Caṇḍāla by a Vaidehī woman, a maker of mats, baskets, &c. a worker with bambus, and reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
पाण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Excellent, praise-worthy.<BR>E.<BR>पण to praise, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्यास्य
पाण्यास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A Brahman who reads the Vedas upon receiving a gift at a Śrāddha.<BR>E.<BR>पाणि, and आस्य face or mouth, having his mouth in his hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात्<BR>m. (-पात्)<BR>1 Falling.<BR>2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, aff. क्विप्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात्<BR>mfn. (पान् पान्ती पात्)<BR>Who or what defends or preserves, a guardian, a protector, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
पात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Preserved, protected.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve, aff. क्त.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Falling, alighting, descending.<BR>2 A name of Rāhu.<BR>3 The node of a planet's orbit.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातक|पातकं|पातकः
पातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Sin, crime.<BR>2 The cause of falling, literally or figuratively.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall or descend, causal form, (from virtue,) aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकयोग
पातकयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Incurring guilt, acting sinfully.<BR>E.<BR>पातक, and योग accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Wicked, sinful, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>पातक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातङ्गि|पातंगि|पातंगिः|पातङ्गिः
पातङ्गि<BR>m. (-ङ्गिः)<BR>Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>पतङ्ग the sun, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातञ्जल|पातंजल|पातञ्जलं
पातञ्जल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The Yoga system of philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>पतञ्जलि the sage by whom it was first taught, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bringing down, causing to fall.<BR>2 Lowering, humbling.<BR>3 Felling, knocking down.<BR>4 Nodding, as in sleep.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall in the causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातव्य
पातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be drunk.<BR>2 To be preserved or protected.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, to preserve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाताल|पातालं|पातालः
पाताल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The regions under the earth, and the abode of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR>2 A hole, a chasm.<BR>3 Submarine fire.<BR>4 The fourth sign from that in which the sun is present.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of apparatus for calcining and subliming metals, formed of two earthen pots, the upper one inverted over the lower, and the two joined together by their necks with cement, and placed in a hole containing fire.<BR>E.<BR>पत to alight, Uṇādi aff. आलञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालनिलय|पातालनिलयः
पातालनिलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A demon, a Daitya.<BR>2 A Naga or infernal serpent.<BR>E.<BR>पाताल hell, and निलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालौकस्
पातालौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>An Asura, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>पाताल hell, ओकस a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाति|पातिः
पाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A master, a lord, a husband.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, Uṇādi aff. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिक|पातिकः
पातिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Gangetick porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>पात trembling, falling, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित
पातित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Felled, struck down.<BR>2 Lowered, depressed, humbled.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिन्
पातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Going, going to, alighting, falling.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिली
पातिली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A trap or snare for catching deer.<BR>2 A small earthen vessel or pot, especially used by religious mendicants.<BR>3 A woman of a particular class.<BR>E.<BR>पात falling, इलच् aff, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Falling frequently or habitually, disposed to fall.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The declivity of a mountain, a precipice.<BR>2 An aquatick animal of a large size; figuratively, the water elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, aff. उकञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातृ
पातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what protects or nourishes.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Ocymum pilosum.)<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
पात्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be fallen, to be alighted.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्त्र
पात्त्र<BR>n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>A preservative from sin, a preserver, a saviour.<BR>E.<BR>पात् and त्र who or what saves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्त्रता
पात्त्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The quality or property of a preservative from sin.<BR>E.<BR>पात्त्र and तल् aff.; also with त्व, पात्त्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रं|पात्रः
पात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>A vessel in general, a plate, a cup, a jar, &c.<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 A sacrificial vase or vessel, comprising various forms of cups, plates, spoons, ladles, &c. so used.<BR>2 The channel of a river, or its course between the near and opposite bank.<BR>3 A king's counsellor or minister.<BR>4 Propriety, fitness.<BR>5 A leaf.<BR>6 The persons of a drama.<BR>7 An order, a command.<BR>8 The body.<BR>9 A fit or competent person.<BR>10 A measure of one Āḍhaka or of eight Sers.<BR>11 A receptacle of any kind, what holds or supports.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A small or portable furnace.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve or retain, aff. त्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रट|पात्रटः
पात्रट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Spare, emaciate, thin.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Ragged garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटीर|पात्रटीरः
पात्रटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An able or competent minister.<BR>2 A vessel of metal, as silver, brass, &c.<BR>3 Rust of iron.<BR>4 Fire.<BR>5 A heron.<BR>6 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र a vessel, &c., and टीर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रता
पात्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Capacity, fitness.<BR>2 Appropriate state or circumstance.<BR>3 The property or capacity of a cup or vessel.<BR>4 Dignity, honor.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र capable, and तल् aff. of the abstract, quality; also with त्व aff., पात्रत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=524" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रपाल|पात्रपालः
पात्रपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large oar used as a rudder.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र a vessel, (a boat,) and पाल what cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रभूत
पात्रभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>The object of a present or of respectful treatment.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र fit, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रभृत्
पात्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र, and भृत् who takes care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसंस्कार|पात्रसंस्कारः
पात्रसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The current of a river.<BR>2 Cleaning a vessel that has been used.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र the channel, and संस्कार completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Measured by a vessel, or the measure Pātra, sown with it, preparing it, &c.<BR>2 Fit, adequate, appropriate.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र, and ष्ठन् aff.; also with घ aff. पात्रिय, and with यत्, पात्र्या, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>1 Having a vessel.<BR>2 Having fit or worthy persons.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीण
पात्रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Measured, sown, cooked, &c. by a Pātra.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीय|पात्रीयं
पात्रीय<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>A sacrificial vessel.<BR>E.<BR>पाच the same, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीर|पात्रीरं|पात्रीरः
पात्रीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An oblation.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र a sacrificial vessel, ईर to go, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेसमित|पात्रेसमितः
पात्रेसमित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A parasite, a person constant at dinners, or feasts, but good for nothing else.<BR>2 A connoisseur in eating.<BR>3 A hypocrite.<BR>E.<BR>पात्रे in a vessel, a plate, &c. and समित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रोपकरण|पात्रोपकरणं
पात्रोपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Decorations of an inferior class, as bells, chowris, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पात्र, and उपकार instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथ|पाथं|पाथः
पाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, and थक् aff.; the more usual form however is पीथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस्<BR>n. (-थः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, and थुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथिस्
पाथिस्<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>1 The sea.<BR>2 The eye.<BR>n. (-थि)<BR>A blotch, a scab.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, Uṇādi aff. इसि, and थुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेय|पाथेयं
पाथेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Provender, or provisions, &c. for a journey.<BR>2 The sign Virgo.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन् road, aff. ढञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोज|पाथोजं
पाथोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>पाथस्, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोद|पाथोदः
पाथोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पाथस् water, दा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधर|पाथोधरः
पाथोधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>पाथस् water, धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोधि|पाथोधिः
पाथोधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पाथस् water, and धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथोनिधि|पाथोनिधिः
पाथोनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पाथस् water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्
पाद्<BR>m. (-पाद् or पात्)<BR>The foot.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, aff. क्विप्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद|पादः
पाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 A quarter.<BR>3 A hill at the foot of a mountain.<BR>4 A ray of light.<BR>5 The root of a tree.<BR>6 The foot or line of a stanza.<BR>7 The line of a hymn or stanza of the Ṛg Veda.<BR>8 The quadrant of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकटक|पादकटकः
पादकटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, and कटक a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादकृच्छ्र|पादकृच्छ्रः
पादकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>A sort of penance, eating once and fasting on alternate nights.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a quarter, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादगण्डिर|पादगण्डिरः
पादगण्डिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Morbid enlargement of the legs and feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, गण्ड a swelling, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादग्रहण|पादग्रहणं
पादग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Respectful obeisance, touching the feet of a Brahman or superior.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचत्वर|पादचत्वरः
पादचत्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A goat.<BR>2 A sand bank.<BR>3 The religious fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>4 Hail.<BR>5 A slanderer, a calumniator.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and चत्वर levelled ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचापल्य
पादचापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Beating or shuffling with the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, &c. चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचार|पादचारः
पादचार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The daily position of the planets.<BR>2 Going on foot.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and चार going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादचारिन्
पादचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A footman, a foot-soldier.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and चर to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादज|पादजः
पादज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Śūdra, or man of the fourth and servile tribe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, (of BRAHMĀ,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतल
पादतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The sole or the lower part of the foot.<BR>adv.<BR>As low as or under the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादतस्
पादतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 At the foot.<BR>2 By or with a quarter.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादत्राण|पादत्राणं
पादत्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A boot, a shoe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाददारी
पाददारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A chap in the feet, a chilblain.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, दृ to rend, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप|पादपः
पादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A foot-stool, a cushion, &c. for the feet.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A shoe, a slipper.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, or root, and पा to drink or preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपरिघदृन
पादपरिघदृन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trampling, treading upon.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and परिघट्टन friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपरुहा
पादपरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A creeping or a parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>पादप a tree, and रुह what mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपाश|पादपाशः
पादपाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A foot-rope for cattle or horses.<BR>2 An anklet of small bells, &c.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A chain for the feet, a fetter.<BR>2 A foot-carpet or mat.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and पाश a fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठ|पादपीठं|पादपीठः
पादपीठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A foot-stool.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and पीठ a stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादपीठिका
पादपीठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Any common or vulgar trade, as that of a barber, &c.<BR>2 A white-stone.<BR>E.<BR>पादपीठ a foot-stool, a work bench, ङीप् depreciative aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रक्षालन|पादप्रक्षालनं
पादप्रक्षालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Washing the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and प्रक्षालन washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रणाम|पादप्रणामः
पादप्रणाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Bowing to the feet, prostration.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and प्रणाम bowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रधारण|पादप्रधारणं
पादप्रधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A shoe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and प्रधारण defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादप्रहार|पादप्रहारः
पादप्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A kick.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and प्रहार striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादबन्धन|पादबंधन|पादबन्धनं
पादबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Stock of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, and बन्धन binding, alluding to the foot-ropes with which cattle are tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादमूल|पादमूलं
पादमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The heel.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरक्षण|पादरक्षणं
पादरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A leather boot or shoe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and रक्षण protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरज्जु|पादरज्जुः
पादरज्जु<BR>f. (-ज्जुः)<BR>An elephant's heel-ropes.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरथ
पादरथ<BR>mf. (-थः-थी)<BR>A shoe, a slipper.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and रथ, a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादरोहण|पादरोहणः
पादरोहण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and रोहण what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवन्दन|पादवंदन
पादवन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Respect, respectful behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and वन्दन saluting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=525" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादवल्मीक|पादवल्मीकः
पादवल्मीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Morbid enlargement of the legs and feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, वल्मीक a hillock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविक|पादविकः
पादविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A traveller, a way-farer.<BR>E.<BR>पदवी a road, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादविरजस्
पादविरजस्<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A shoe, a slipper.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, वि privative, रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशब्द
पादशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>The sound or noise of feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशश्
पादशश्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Verse by verse, stanza by stanza.<BR>2 Foot by foot.<BR>3 By a fourth.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a verse, शशि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशाखा
पादशाखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A toe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशैल|पादशैलः
पादशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A hill near a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and शैल a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादशोथ|पादशोथः
पादशोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Swelling of the feet, gout.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and शोथ a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादसेवन
पादसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Service, duty.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and सेवन waiting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादस्फोट|पादस्फोटः
पादस्फोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Kibe, chilblain, a sore or ulcer on the foot.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, and स्फोट a boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहत
पादहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Trodden on, kicked, touched with the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहर्ष|पादहर्षः
पादहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Tingling of the feet after pressure upon the crural nerves.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादहारक|पादहारकः
पादहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who takes or steals any thing with his feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, हृ to take, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाग्र|पादाग्रं
पादाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The point of the foot.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and अग्र point or tip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गद|पादांगद|पादाङ्गदं
पादाङ्गद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, अङ्ग shape, beauty, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुली
पादाङ्गुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A toe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, अङ्गुली a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्ठ|पादांगुष्ठ|पादाङ्गुष्ठः
पादाङ्गुष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The great toe.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, अङ्गुष्ठ the thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाङ्गुष्ठिका
पादाङ्गुष्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An ornament or ring worn on the great toe.<BR>E.<BR>पादाङ्गुष्ठ the great toe, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात्
पादात्<BR>m. (-दात्)<BR>A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR>E.<BR>पाद foot, अत to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादात|पादातं|पादातः
पादात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Infantry.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and अत to go, aff. अच्, or पदाति a foot-soldier, अण् collective aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाति|पादातिः
पादाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A foot-soldier, a man on foot, or footman.<BR>E.<BR>पाद with अत to go, aff. इन्; also पदाति; also with कन् added, पादातिक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाध्यास
पादाध्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Treading upon, kicking, spurning.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and अध्यास placing upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादानत
पादानत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bowed down to the feet, prostrate.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and आनत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादारक|पादारकः
पादारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The knees or ribs of a boat, supporting the deck on each side, (?).<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, ऋ to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्घ्य
पादार्घ्य<BR>n. (-र्ध्यं)<BR>A donation to Brahmans, or venerable persons.<BR>E.<BR>पाद foot, अर्ध्य a respectful offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादार्द्ध
पादार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>1 An eighth.<BR>2 Half a line of a stanza.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and, अर्द्ध a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादालिन्द|पादालिंदः|पादालिन्दः
पादालिन्द<BR>mf. (-न्दः-न्दा or न्दी)<BR>A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावनेजन
पादावनेजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Washing the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and अवनेजन washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावर्त्त|पादावर्त|पादावर्तः|पादावर्त्तः
पादावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A machine for raising water from a well.<BR>E.<BR>पाद foot, and आवर्त्त revolving, worked by the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादावसेचन
पादावसेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Washing the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and अवसेचन sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाविक|पादाविकः
पादाविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A foot-soldier.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a foot, अब to go, &c. aff. इक or ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादासन
पादासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A foot-stool.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादास्फालन
पादास्फालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trampling, shuffling, or motion of the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and आस्फालन waving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादाहत
पादाहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kicked, trodden, touched by the foot.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिक
पादिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fourth, a fourth.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a quarter, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन्
पादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Footed, having feet.<BR>2 Having a fourth part or share.<BR>3 Having four parts, as a stanza, &c.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A footed aquatic animal, an amphibious animal.<BR>2 The heir of a fourth part of the estate.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादिन|पादिनः
पादिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A fourth part.<BR>E.<BR>पाद a quarter, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुक|पादुकः
पादुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>Who or what goes on foot or with feet.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shoe, a slipper.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and उकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकाकार|पादुकाकारः
पादुकाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A shoemaker.<BR>E.<BR>पादुका a shoe, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादुकाकृत्
पादुकाकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A shoemaker.<BR>E.<BR>पादुका a shoe, and कृत्, who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादू
पादू<BR>f. (-दूः)<BR>A shoe.<BR>E.<BR>पद to go, Uṇādi aff. ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादूकृत्
पादूकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A shoemaker.<BR>E.<BR>पादू a shoe, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादोदक|पादोदकं
पादोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water for the feet, especially that in which the feet of a Brahman have been washed.<BR>E.<BR>पाद, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्य|पाद्यं
पाद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Water, &c. for cleaning the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद the foot, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाद्यपात्र
पाद्यपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A metal vessel for washing the feet.<BR>E.<BR>पाद्य, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान|पानं|पानः
पान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Drinking.<BR>2 A drinking cup or vessel.<BR>3 Preserving, protecting.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Breath, breathing out, expiration.<BR>2 A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, &c. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानगोष्ठिका
पानगोष्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A dram shop, a place where people drink together.<BR>E.<BR>पान drinking, गोष्ठी a station, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानपर
पानपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Drinking, quaffing, who or what drinks assiduously.<BR>2 Looking at amorously.<BR>E.<BR>पान, and पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानपात्र|पानपात्रं
पानपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A glass, a drinking vessel.<BR>E.<BR>पान drinking, पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानबणिज्
पानबणिज्<BR>m. (-णिक्)<BR>A distiller, a vender of spirits.<BR>E.<BR>पान drinking, बणिज् a dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानभाजन|पानभाजनं
पानभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A drinking vessel, a glass, a goblet.<BR>E.<BR>पान, and भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानरत
पानरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drinking, drunken.<BR>E.<BR>पान, and रत engaged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानशौण्ड|पानशौंड|पानशौण्डः
पानशौण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A hard drinker.<BR>E.<BR>पान, and शौण्ड intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानस|पानसं
पानस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>A spirituous liquor prepared from the fruit of the Jack tree.<BR>E.<BR>पनस the Jack, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानात्यय|पानात्ययः
पानात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Morbid state after intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>पान, and अत्यय end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=526" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानिल|पानिलं
पानिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A drinking vessel.<BR>E.<BR>पान drinking, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीय|पानीयं
पानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Drinkable, to be drunk.<BR>2 To be cherished, protected or preserved.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, अनीयर participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयनकुल|पानीयनकुलः
पानीयनकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An otter.<BR>E.<BR>पानीय water, नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयपृष्ठज|पानीयपृष्ठजः
पानीयपृष्ठज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An aquatick plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>पानीय water, पृष्ठ surface, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयमूलक|पानीयमूलकं
पानीयमूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica): see सोमराजी.<BR>E.<BR>पानीय water, मूल root, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयशालिका
पानीयशालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A place where water, &c. is distributed.<BR>E.<BR>पानीय water, शाला a place, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पानीयामलक|पानीयामलकं
पानीयामलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>पानीय water, and आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पान्थ|पांथ|पांथः|पान्थः
पान्थ<BR>mf. (-न्यः-न्या)<BR>A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>पथिन् a road, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप|पापं|पापः
पाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Mischievous, destructive, malignant.<BR>2 Vile, low, abandoned, vicious.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A wicked man, a wretch, a profligate.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Sin, crime, wickedness, vice.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve (from it), and प Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापक|पापकं|पापकः
पापक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर
पापकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wicked, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर्त्तृ|पापकर्तृ
पापकर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्ती-र्त्तृ)<BR>Sinful, wicked, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and कर्त्तृ who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकर्म्मन्|पापकर्मन्
पापकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Wicked, sinful.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापकृत्
पापकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Sinful, wicked, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>पाप sin, कृ to commit, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापगोचर
पापगोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Evidently involved in the consequences of sin.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and गोचर visible object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापग्रह|पापग्रहः
पापग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Any ill omened aspect of the stars, as the conjunction of the sun or Budha with the moon in its last quarter.<BR>2 Rāhu.<BR>3 Saturn.<BR>4 Mars.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and ग्रह asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापघ्न|पापघ्नः
पापघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing sin.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and घ्न destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचक
पापचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what matures or cooks often or much.<BR>E.<BR>पच to cook, &c. frequent. v., ण्वुल् aff.; also पापाचक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचर्य्य|पापचर्य|पापचर्यः
पापचर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A sinner.<BR>2 A fiend, a Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and चर्य्या practice, or चर्य्य to be gone (in or by.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचेतस्
पापचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Wicked, vile.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and चेतस् understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापचेली
पापचेली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknidhi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>पच to ripen, reiterated पापच, (rheumatism,) ईर to dissipate, affs. अच् and ङीप्, and र changed to ल; also with कन् added in the fem. form पापचेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापति
पापति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Who or what alights, goes or falls much or frequently.<BR>E.<BR>पत to alight, &c. frequent. v, किन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापदर्शिन्
पापदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Malevolent, looking at faults.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापदृश्वन्
पापदृश्वन्<BR>mfn. (-श्वा-श्वा-श्व)<BR>Conscious of guilt, knowing an act to be wicked.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and दृश to see, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनापित|पापनापितः
पापनापित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A vile or bad barber.<BR>E.<BR>पाप sinful, नापित a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनाशिन्
पापनाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Purifying, sin-destroying.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and नाशिन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापनिरति
पापनिरति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Wicked, villainous, a wretch.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and निरति attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापपति|पापपतिः
पापपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A paramour, a gallant.<BR>E.<BR>पाप wicked, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापपुरुष|पापपुरुषः
पापपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A personification of all sin, or a male, whose head is Brahmanicide, whose arms are theft, whose heart is wine drinking, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापबुद्धि
पापबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Evil-minded, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and बुद्धि intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापमति
पापमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Of a corrupt mind, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापमुक्त|पापमुक्तः
पापमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Freed from sin, liberated from all crime.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and मुक्त set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापयोनि|पापयोनिः
पापयोनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Birth in some inferior state, as an animal, &c. as the punishment of sin.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and योनि womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापरोग|पापरोगः
पापरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A disease, considered as the punishment of sin in a former life.<BR>2 Small pox.<BR>E.<BR>पाप sin, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापर्द्धि
पापर्द्धि<BR>f. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>Hunting, chase.<BR>E.<BR>पाप sin, and ऋद्वि thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापल|पापलं
पापल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Giving or taking sin.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A measure.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापविनिग्रह|पापविनिग्रहः
पापविनिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Restraining or punishing wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and विनिग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापशमन
पापशमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Palliating or removing crime.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sin-offering.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and शमन appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापसम्मित
पापसम्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Equal in sin, of like guilt.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and सम्मित measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापात्मन्
पापात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A sinner, a reprobate, a wretch.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापानुवसित
पापानुवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Addicted to sin.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and अनुवसित dwelling with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापापनुत्ति|पापापनुत्तिः
पापापनुत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Expiation.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and अपनुत्ति removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापाशय
पापाशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Wicked, sinful.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and आशय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिन्
पापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Wicked, sinful, bad, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापिष्ठ
पापिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very wicked.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पापीयस्
पापीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very wicked.<BR>E.<BR>पाप, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाप्मन्
पाप्मन्<BR>m. (-प्मा)<BR>Sin, wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve (from it), मनिन् Uṇādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामघ्न|पामघ्नः
पामघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>पामन् scab, and अघ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन्
पामन्<BR>nf. (-म-मा)<BR>Cutaneous eruption, herpes, scab.<BR>E.<BR>पै to dry, aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामन|पामनः
पामन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Diseased with herpes.<BR>E.<BR>पामन् herpes, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामर|पामरः
पामर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Wicked, vile, low, base.<BR>2 Stupid, an idiot, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>पाम scab, and रा to get, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामरोद्धारा
पामरोद्धारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant: see गुडुची.<BR>E.<BR>पामर here said to mean bile, उद् before हृ to take away, aff. घञ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पामारि|पामारिः
पामारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>पामा scab, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाम्प
पाम्प<BR>mfn. (-म्पः-म्पी-म्पं)<BR>Belonging to the river, (Pampā.)<BR>E.<BR>पम्पा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय|पायं
पाय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, अच् aff. and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायस|पायसः
पायस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Made of or from milk or water.<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>1 An oblation of milk, rice, and sugar.<BR>2 Turpentine.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Milk.<BR>E.<BR>पयस् milk, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=527" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायसिक
पायसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fond of or relating to a mixture of milk, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पायस, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायिक|पायिकः
पायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A foot-soldier, a footman.<BR>E.<BR>पा to cherish, ण्वुल् aff., and युक् and इट् augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पायु|पायुः
पायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve, Uṇādi aff. उण् and युक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाय्य|पाय्यं
पाय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Low, vile, reprehensible, contemptible.<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>1 Measure.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Drinking.<BR>4 Practice, profession.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार<BR>r. 10th cl. (पारयति)<BR>To accomplish, to finish, to get through or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार|पारं|पारः
पार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The further or opposite bank of a river.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The end, the extremity, the last.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The name of a river, said to flow from the Pāriyātra mountains, or the centrical and western portion of the Vindhya chain.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A quantity of water.<BR>2 A rope for tying an elephant's feet.<BR>3 A small water jar.<BR>4 The pollen of a flower.<BR>5 A drinking vessel, a glass, a cup.<BR>6 A milk pail.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, ईर to go to or towards; or पार to cross over; or पॄ to fill, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक|पारकः
पारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 What purifies, protects, cherishes, pleases, &c.<BR>2 What enables any one to cross, (a river or the world.)<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to please, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारक्य|पारक्यं|पारक्यः
पारक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>1 An enemy, hostile, inimical.<BR>2 Alien, belonging to another.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Pious conduct, doing any thing for the sake of future happiness.<BR>E.<BR>परक or पारक, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग|पारगः
पारग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Crossing, crossing over.<BR>2 Going over or beyond the world.<BR>E.<BR>पार the opposite bank, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारगत|पारगतः
पारगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Crossed.<BR>2 Gone over the world, pure, holy.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina deified teacher.<BR>E.<BR>पार the further bank, (of the world,) and गत attained, gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारग्रामिक
पारग्रामिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Hostile, inimical.<BR>E.<BR>पर an enemy, ग्राम a number, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारज्
पारज्<BR>m. (-रक्)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy, Uṇādi aff. अजि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारजायिक|पारजायिकः
पारजायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An adulterer.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, जाया wife, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारटीट|पारटीटः
पारटीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A stone, a rock.<BR>E.<BR>पार across, and टीट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारण|पारणं|पारणः
पारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>1 Eating or drinking after a fast, breaking a fast.<BR>2 Satisfying, satisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy, aff. ल्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत|पारतः
पारत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>पार fulness, (from पॄ to please,) and तन to spread or diffuse, aff. ड, also पारद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारतन्त्र्य|पारतंत्र्य|पारतंत्र्यं|पारतन्त्र्यं
पारतन्त्र्य<BR>n. (-न्त्र्यं)<BR>Subservience, slavery, dependence.<BR>E.<BR>परतन्त्र dependant, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारत्रिक|पारत्रिकं
पारत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the next world.<BR>E.<BR>परत्र, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारद|पारदः
पारद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>पार as in पारत, and द what gives, from दा with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदण्डक|पारदण्डकः
पारदण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a country, part of Orissa.<BR>E.<BR>पार beyond, दण्डक the Daṇḍaka forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदारिक|पारदारिकः
पारदारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An adulterer.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, दार wife, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदार्य्य|पारदार्य|पारदार्यं
पारदार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Adultery.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, दार a wife, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेशिक|पारदेशिकः
पारदेशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Foreign, abroad.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A traveller.<BR>2 A foreigner.<BR>E.<BR>परदेश, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदेश्य|पारदेश्यः
पारदेश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-शी-श्यं)<BR>Belonging to another country.<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>1 A traveller, one gone to a foreign country.<BR>2 A foreigner.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, देश country, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारदृश्वन्
पारदृश्वन्<BR>mfn. (-श्वा-श्वा-श्व)<BR>Long-sighted, far-seeing, wise.<BR>E.<BR>पार, and दृश to see, क्वनिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारधेनु|पारधेनुः
पारधेनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>A particular and low cast, the Ayogava. Also, पारधेनुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृत|पारभृतं
पारभृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A present, an offering.<BR>E.<BR>पर, भृत prepared, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारभृतीय
पारभृतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a present.<BR>E.<BR>पारभृत, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमार्थिक|पारमार्थिकः
पारमार्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Preferable, best, most desirable.<BR>E.<BR>परमार्थ chief object, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमिक
पारमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Supreme, chief, best.<BR>E.<BR>परम best, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारमित
पारमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Crossed, traversed.<BR>2 Transcendant, (as spiritual knowledge.)<BR>E.<BR>पारस् across, and इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य्य|पारम्पर्य|पारंपर्य|पारंपर्यं|पारम्पर्य्यं
पारम्पर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Traditional instruction, tradition.<BR>2 Continuous order or succession.<BR>E.<BR>परम्पर from one to another, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारम्पर्य्योपदेश|पारम्पर्योपदेश|पारंपर्योपदेश|पारंपर्योपदेशः|पारम्पर्य्योपदेशः
पारम्पर्य्योपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Traditional instruction.<BR>E.<BR>पारम्पर्य्य, and उपदेश instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारय
पारय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Able, adequate, fit for.<BR>2 Satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयत्
पारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Satisfying, filling.<BR>2 Being able or competent to.<BR>3 Being alive, living.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारयिष्णु
पारयिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Gratifying, pleasing, satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to please, causal v., इष्णु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारलौकिक
पारलौकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the next world.<BR>E.<BR>परलोक another world, aff. ठक्, and both vowels changed by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारवत|पारवतः
पारवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A pigeon. See पारावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशव|पारशवः
पारशव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Made or derived from an axe.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The son of a Śūdra woman by a Brahman.<BR>2 A son by another's wife, an adulterine.<BR>3 An iron weapon.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, शत्र to go, अच् aff. and अण् implying descent, added; or पार crossing, शव a corpse, a living corpse; or परशु an axe, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारशीक|पारशीकः
पारशीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Persia.<BR>2 A native of Persia.<BR>3 A Persian horse; also पारसीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वध|पारश्वधः
पारश्वध<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>One armed with an axe, a hatchet-man, a pioneer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>परश्वध an axe, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वधिक|पारश्वधिकः
पारश्वधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A soldier, or any other man armed with an axe.<BR>E.<BR>पारश्वध an axe, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारश्वय
पारश्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिक|पारसिकः
पारसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Persia; also पारसीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसिक|पारसिकः
पारसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The kingdom of Persia.<BR>2 A Persian, an inhabitant of Persia.<BR>3 A Persian horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारस्त्रैणेय|पारस्त्रैणेयः
पारस्त्रैणेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An adulterine, the son of another's wife.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, स्त्री woman, ठक् aff. of descent, and इणञ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापत|पारापतः
पारापत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A pigeon; also पारावत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=528" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारापार|पारापारः
पारापार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The two banks of a river.<BR>E.<BR>पार the further bank, and अपार the near bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायण|पारायणं
पारायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Totality, entireness, completeness.<BR>2 Going over, reading or doing any thing completely.<BR>3 Going across.<BR>4 Reading a Purāṇa, or causing it to be read.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 Action, act.<BR>3 Considering, meditating.<BR>4 Light.<BR>E.<BR>पार the boundary or limit, and अयन going to, extending: when used attributively it remains always neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारायणिक|पारायणिकः
पारायणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A pupil, a scholar.<BR>2 A lecturer, a reader of the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>पारायण reading through, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारारुक|पारारुकः
पारारुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A rock.<BR>E.<BR>पार the further bank, ऋ to go to, aff. उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावत|पारावतः
पारावत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A dove, a pigeon.<BR>2 A monkey.<BR>3 A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>4 A mountain.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The name of a river in the peninsula.<BR>2 The fruit of the Annona reticulata.<BR>3 A form of song, peculiar to the cowherds.<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (life, &c.) अव to go, to preserve, शतृ participial aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावतपदी
पारावतपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>Heart pea: see पारावताङ्घी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छ|पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छः
पारावताङ्घ्रिपिच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावताङ्घ्री
पारावताङ्घ्री<BR>f. (-ङ्घ्री)<BR>Heart pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)<BR>E.<BR>पारावत a pigeon, अङ्घ्रि a foot, the root being compared to a pigeon's foot; also similar compounds, as पारावतपदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावार|पारावारं|पारावारः
पारावार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The near and opposite banks of a stream.<BR>E.<BR>पार the further bank, वृ to surround, with आङ् prefix, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारावारीण|पारावारीणः
पारावारीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 On both sides of a river, &c.<BR>2 One who goes to both sides.<BR>E.<BR>पार the opposite side, अवार this side, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर|पाराशरं|पाराशरः
पाराशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of the poet VYĀSA.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The rules of PARĀŚARA or VYĀSA, for the conduct of the mendicant orders.<BR>E.<BR>पराशर, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरकल्पिक|पाराशरकल्पिकः
पाराशरकल्पिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A follower of PARĀŚARA, the institutor of rules for the mendicant order.<BR>E.<BR>पराशर the sage, कल्प aff., and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरि|पाराशरिः
पाराशरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>पराशर, and इञ् patronymick aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशरिन्
पाराशरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The religious mendicant or Brahman, who having passed through the three stages of student, householder, and ascetick, leads a vagrant life, and subsists upon alms.<BR>E.<BR>पाराशर्य्य VYĀSA, the author of the rules of this order, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाराशर्य्य|पाराशर्य|पाराशर्यः|पाराशर्य्यः
पाराशर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>पराशर the father of the poet, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिकाङ्क्षिन्|पारिकांक्षिन्
पारिकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्क्षी)<BR>1 An ascetick, one who devotes his days to devout contemplation.<BR>2 The religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>परि implying secession, (abandoning worldly wishes,) काङ्क्षि to desire, and णिनि aff.; or पारि derived from पर, supreme felicity, and कांक्षिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजात|पारिजातः
पारिजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A tree of paradise.<BR>2 The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgenis.)<BR>E.<BR>पारि said to mean, above, and जात produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिजातक|पारिजातकः
पारिजातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree of paradise.<BR>2 The coral tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाय्य|पारिणाय्यं
पारिणाय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Belonging to specifically or peculiarly.<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>Property received at the time of marriage by a woman.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, around, णी to get, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिणाह्य|पारिणाह्यं
पारिणाह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>Household furniture and utensils.<BR>E.<BR>परिणाह and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितथ्या
पारितथ्या<BR>f. (-थ्या)<BR>A trinket worn on the forehead, where the hair is parted.<BR>E.<BR>परि every way (splendid), तथा there, यञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारितोषिक|पारितोषिकं
पारितोषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Delighting, making happy.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A reward, a gratuity.<BR>E.<BR>परितोष satisfaction, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिन्द्र|पारिंद्र|पारिंद्रः|पारिन्द्रः
पारिन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A lion: see परिन्द्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपन्थिक|पारिपंथिक|पारिपंथिकः|पारिपन्थिकः
पारिपन्थिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A robber, a thief, a highwayman.<BR>E.<BR>परि around, पथिन the road, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपाट्य|पारिपाट्यं
पारिपाट्य<BR>n. (-ट्यं)<BR>Regularity, methodicalness, successiveness.<BR>E.<BR>परिपाटी orderly course, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्र|पारिपात्रं|पारिपात्रः
पारिपात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The name of a mountain, apparently the centrical or western portion of the Vindhya chain, which skirts the province of Malva.<BR>E.<BR>परि every way, पा to cherish, ष्ट्रन् aff.; or with कन् added, पारिपात्रक; also read पारियात्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपात्रक
पारिपात्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountain so called: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिपार्श्विक|पारिपार्श्विकः
पारिपार्श्विक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An actor, who serves as a sort of chorus to the drama, and is one of the interlocutors in the prologue.<BR>2 An attendant.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, पार्श्व the side, (of the manager, &c.) aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लव|पारिप्लवं|पारिप्लवः
पारिप्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Perturbed, troubled in mind.<BR>2 Trembling, tremulous, unsteady.<BR>E.<BR>परिप्लव, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिप्लाव्य|पारिप्लाव्यः
पारिप्लाव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A goose.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Perplexity, agitation.<BR>2 Tremulousness.<BR>E.<BR>परिप्लव, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभद्र|पारिभद्रः
पारिभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>2 The Nimb tree.<BR>3 A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadāru).<BR>4 The Saral, also a sort of pine, (P. longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>परि completely, भद्र auspicious, aff. अण्; also with कन् added, पारिभद्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिभाव्य|पारिभाव्यं
पारिभाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Surety, security, bail.<BR>2 A drug, a sort of costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>परिभू a surety, or परिभव overcoming (disease), aff. यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमाण्डल्य|पारिमांडल्य|पारिमांडल्यं|पारिमाण्डल्यं
पारिमाण्डल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>An atom, as a measure of space, a mote in a sun beam.<BR>E.<BR>परिमण्डल a ball, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुखिक|पारिमुखिकः
पारिमुखिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Present, before or about the face.<BR>E.<BR>परि about, मुख the face, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिमुख्य|पारिमुख्यं
पारिमुख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Presence, being before the face.<BR>E.<BR>परिमुख, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्र|पारियात्रः
पारियात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The name of a mountain: see पारिपात्र, also with कन् added, पारियात्रक, or with ठक aff. पारियात्रिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियानिक|पारियानिकः
पारियानिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A travelling cart or carriage.<BR>E.<BR>परि every way, यान going, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिरक्षक|पारिरक्षकः
पारिरक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ascetick or religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>पारि said to mean, future happiness, from परि, and रक्षक who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिश|पारिशः
पारिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A tree: see गर्द्धभाण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद|पारिषदः
पारिषद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Belonging or relating to an assembly.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A spectator, a person present at an assembly or congregation.<BR>E.<BR>परिषद् an assembly, aff. अञ्; or with ण्य aff. पारिषद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिषद्य|पारिषद्यः
पारिषद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A spectator: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=529" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहारिक|पारिहारिकः
पारिहारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Taking away, seizing.<BR>2 Surrounding.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A maker of garlands.<BR>E.<BR>परिहार seizure, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारिहार्य्य|पारिहार्य|पारिहार्यः|पारिहार्य्यः
पारिहार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A bracelet.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Taking, seizure.<BR>E.<BR>परिहार, and ष्पञ् aff.; also परिहार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीक्षित|पारीक्षितः
पारीक्षित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The name of a sovereign, to whom the Śrī Bhāgavata, or life of KṚṢṆA, is supposed to have been addressed.<BR>2 The successor of the preceding; also JANAMEJAYA.<BR>E.<BR>परीक्षित्. the king so called, and अण् pleonasm or patronymic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीण|पारीणः
पारीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 On the other or opposite side.<BR>2 Who goes or crosses to the other side.<BR>E.<BR>पार the other side, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारीन्द्र|पारींद्र|पारींद्रः|पारीन्द्रः
पारीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A large snake, (Böa.)<BR>E.<BR>पर another, (animal,) and इन्द्र lord, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारु|पारुः
पारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, Uṇādi aff. रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारुष्य|पारुष्यं|पारुष्यः
पारुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 Abuse, reproach, scurrilous, opprobrious or unfriendly speech.<BR>2 The property of harshness, &c. in speaking.<BR>3 The forest or grove of INDRA.<BR>4 Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>5 Severity, violence, either in word or deed, as वाक्पारुष्यं defamation, abuse, or violence of words, and दण्डपारुष्यं personal injury, assault or violence of blows.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>परुष harsh, contumelious, &c. aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारेरक|पारेरकः
पारेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sword, a scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>पार collectively, foes, from पर an enemy, ईर to penetrate, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्घट|पार्घटं
पार्घट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Ashes.<BR>E.<BR>पार from पर another, घट to endeavour, aff. अच्, and the final vowel of पार rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थ|पार्थः
पार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 A king, a prince.<BR>2 A name of the Pāṇḍu prince ARJUNA.<BR>3 A name of KĀRTAVĪRYA.<BR>4 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>पृथा a proper name, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थक्य|पार्थक्यं
पार्थक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Severalty, individuality, difference.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separate, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थव|पार्थवं
पार्थव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Greatness, immensity.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु great, अण् aff.; also पृथुता, पृथुत्व, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिव|पार्थिवं|पार्थिवः
पार्थिव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा or वी-वं)<BR>1 Earthen, made or derived from earth.<BR>2 Ruling or possessing the earth.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A king, a prince.<BR>2 An earthen vessel.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी the earth, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्पर|पार्परः
पार्पर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्व|पार्व
पार्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>Relating to a Parva, a particular day of the month, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वन् and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वण|पार्वण|पार्व्वणः
पार्व्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A sort of deer.<BR>2 The general funeral ceremony to be offered to all the manes at the Parva, or conjunction of the sun and moon, at which double oblations are offered; three cakes to the father, paternal grandfather, and great grandfather; and three to the maternal grandfather, his father, and grandfather; and the crumbs of each set to the remoter ancestors in each line.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व a knot, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वत|पार्वत|पार्व्वतः
पार्व्वत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Mountain, produced in the mountains.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree called the large Nimb, (Melia sempervirens.)<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ, in her capacity of daughter of HIMĀLA, the sovereign of the snowy mountains.<BR>2 DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>3 A female cowherd or Gopī.<BR>4 The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>5 Another tree, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>6 A red clay, commonly called Saurāṣṭrī, or Surat earth.<BR>7 A name applied to several rivers.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, अण् aff. of descent or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतीनन्दन|पार्वतीनन्दन|पार्वतीनंदन|पार्वतीनन्दनः|पार्व्वतीनन्दनः
पार्व्वतीनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>पार्व्वती the goddess, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतीय|पार्वतीय|पार्वतीयः
पार्व्वतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Mountain, mountaineer.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वतीय, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वतेय|पार्वतेय|पार्व्वतेयं|पार्व्वतेयः
पार्व्वतेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Mountain or mountain-born, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Antimony.<BR>2 A plant bearing a pungent fruit.<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्व्वायनान्तीय|पार्वायनान्तीय
पार्व्वायनान्तीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Occurring at the end of a Parva or a solstice, (a sacrifice, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पर्व्व, and अयन solstice, अन्त end, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शव|पार्शवः
पार्शव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A warrior armed with an axe.<BR>E.<BR>पर्शु an axe, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व<BR>mfn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वा-र्श्वं)<BR>Near, proximate, by the side of.<BR>mn. (-र्श्वः-र्श्वं)<BR>1 A side, the part of the body below the armpit.<BR>2 The curve or circumference of a wheel.<BR>3 Side of any square figure.<BR>n. (-र्श्वं)<BR>1 A multitude of ribs, the thorax.<BR>2 A fraudulent or crooked expedient.<BR>m. (-र्श्वः)<BR>The twenty-third Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश^1 to touch, श्वण Uṇādi aff., and पृ substituted for the root, or पर्शु a rib, aff. अण्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: M also in WIL1819.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वक|पार्श्वकः
पार्श्वक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A pilferer, a swindler, any one who seeks wealth or other objects, by dishonest or indirect means.<BR>2 A rib.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व a dishonest means, a side, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वगत
पार्श्वगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Close to, beside.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतस्
पार्श्वतस्<BR>ind.<BR>By or from the side of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व the side, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतीय|पार्श्वतीयः
पार्श्वतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to the side of.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्वतस्, and छ aff.; the final अस् rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तन|पार्श्वपरिवर्तन|पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तनं
पार्श्वपरिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Turning upon the side.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व, and परिवर्त्तन turning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वभाग|पार्श्वभागः
पार्श्वभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The side, the flank.<BR>E.<BR>पाश्व the side, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशय
पार्श्वशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-र्य)<BR>1 Sleeping on.<BR>2 Sleeping beside the side.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व, and शी to sleep, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वशूल|पार्श्वशूलः
पार्श्वशूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Spasm of the chest, stitch.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व, and शूल sharp pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वस्थ|पार्श्वस्थः
पार्श्वस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Staying near or close to, or at the side.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A sort of chorus to the Indian drama, an actor in the prelude, and interpreter of the plot.<BR>2 An associate, a companion.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व the side, (of the manager, &c.) स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वाचान्त
पार्श्वाचान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Food not to be taken after one of the party has washed his mouth.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व, and आचान्त sipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वास्थि|पार्श्वास्थिः
पार्श्वास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>A rib.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व the side, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं|पार्श्विकः
पार्श्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Lateral, belonging to the side, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A juggler.<BR>2 A partisan, a sidesman, an associate or companion.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व the side, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वोदरप्रिय|पार्श्वोदरप्रियः
पार्श्वोदरप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>पार्श्व the side, उदर the belly. and प्रिप fond of; going sidelong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=530" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षत|पार्षतः
पार्षत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Pāṇḍu prince.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत the name of a king, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद|पार्षदः
पार्षद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A spectator, a person present in a congregation or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>पर्षद an assembly, अण् aff.; also with ण्य aff., पार्षद्य; or derived from परिषद, पारिषद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णि|पार्ष्णिः
पार्ष्णि<BR>mf. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>1 The heel.<BR>2 The rear of an army.<BR>3 The back.<BR>4 Enquiry, asking.<BR>5 A kick.<BR>f. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>1 A violent woman, one intoxicated literally or figuratively, &c.<BR>2 A name of KUNTĪ the mother of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, &c. Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिग्राह|पार्ष्णिग्राहः
पार्ष्णिग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An enemy in the rear.<BR>2 A commander in the rear of his army or reserve.<BR>E.<BR>पार्ष्णि the rear, and ग्राह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णित्र|पार्ष्णित्रं
पार्ष्णित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A reserve, a body of forces in the rear.<BR>E.<BR>पार्ष्णि the rear, and त्रा to preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पालयति)<BR>To guard, to preserve or protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल|पालः
पाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Who or what guards or preserves.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A nourisher, a protector.<BR>2 A spitting pot.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The sharp edge of a sword.<BR>2 A woman with a beard.<BR>3 A louse.<BR>4 A line, a row or range.<BR>5 A pot, a boiler.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, aff. अच्; ङीष् added; also with इ aff. पालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक|पालकः
पालक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what protects, nourishes, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A horse-keeper, a groom.<BR>2 A cherisher, a protector, a guardian.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाप्य|पालकाप्यः
पालकाप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>A name of a Muni or saint, a form of the divine physician DHANVANTARI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालघ्न|पालघ्नः
पालघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A mushroom.<BR>E.<BR>पाल earth, derived from पाल to nourish, and घ्न destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क|पालंकः|पालङ्कः
पालङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>2 A sort of beet root, (Beta bengalensis.)<BR>3 A hawk.<BR>f. (-ङ्की)<BR>Incense, the resin of the olibanum; also पालङ्क्या.<BR>E.<BR>पाल nourishing, अङ्क what goes or gives, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालङ्क्या
पालङ्क्या<BR>f. (-ङ्क्या)<BR>Gum olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>पालङ्क the olibanum tree, यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Preserving, guarding, protecting, cherishing, nourishing.<BR>2 The milk of a cow that has recently calved.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयत्
पालयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Protecting, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to protect, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ<BR>mfn. (ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Protecting, cherishing, a protector, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Of a green colour.<BR>2 Belonging to the Palāśa tree, made of its wood, &c.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Green, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>पलाश a leaf, or the tree, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाशखण्ड|पालाशखंड|पालाशखण्डः
पालाशखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A country in India, the western part of Behar.<BR>E.<BR>पलाश belonging to the Palāśa tree, &c. खण्ड district; abounding in the Butea frondosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालि|पालिः
पालि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 The sharp edge of a sword, or any cutting instrument.<BR>2 The tip of the ear.<BR>3 A line, a row or range.<BR>4 A mark, a spot, a stain.<BR>5 A louse.<BR>6 A woman with a beard.<BR>7 A boundary, a limit.<BR>8 A raised bank, a causeway, a bridge.<BR>9 A circumference.<BR>10 Maintenance of a scholar during the period of his studies, by his teacher.<BR>11 Praise, eulogium.<BR>12 The hip or haunch.<BR>13 A Prastha or measure so called.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, इ aff., and in most cases, ङीष् being optionally added, also पाली: see पाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिका
पालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The sharp edge of a cutting instrument.<BR>2 A sort of ladle or knife for skimming milk, curds, &c.<BR>3 The lobe of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>पाली as above, with कन् added; see also पालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित|पालितः
पालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cherished, nourished.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Śākhoṭa tree.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्
पालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Who or what nourishes or protects.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to protect, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्द|पालिंदः|पालिन्दः
पालिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>Teöri; see the next.<BR>E.<BR>पाल to nourish, (the bee,) aff. किन्दच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिन्धी
पालिन्धी<BR>f. (-न्धी)<BR>A plant, commonly Teöri, (Convolvulus turpethum), the black sort.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, aff. किन्धच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Who or what renders pure, a purifier, purificatory.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Fire, or its deified personification.<BR>2 Social fire, one lighted in common.<BR>3 A fire lighted on taking possession of a house.<BR>4 A saint, a person purified by religious abstraction.<BR>5 A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by attrition, (Premna spinosa).<BR>6 Leadwort, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>7 Marking nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>8 A vermifuge plant: see विडङ्ग.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Wife of AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकारणि|पावकारणिः
पावकारणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by attrition.<BR>E.<BR>पावक fire, अरणि touch-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकि|पावकिः
पावकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>पावक, and इञ् aff. indirectly this deity is the son of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Pure, purified.<BR>2 Purifying, expurgatory, purificatory.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Penance, expiation, purification by acts of austerity and devotion.<BR>3 Cow-dung.<BR>4 The Eleocarpus seed.<BR>5 A kind of grass, (Costus.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The inspired poet VYĀSA.<BR>2 Fire generally, or for various ceremonial purposes.<BR>3 Incense.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>2 A cow.<BR>3 The Ganges, or the goddess GAṄGĀ.<BR>4 Holy basil.<BR>E.<BR>पू to cleanse or purify, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनध्वनि|पावनध्वनिः
पावनध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A conch shell.<BR>E.<BR>पावन, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमान
पावमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Purificatory, purifying.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An expiatory text.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावित
पावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>Purified.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाविन्
पाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Who or what purifies.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाव्य
पाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What is to be or must be purified.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश|पाशः
पाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A fetter, a chain, a tye, the string for fastening tamed animals, or the net or noose for catching birds, deer, &c.<BR>2 A noose as a weapon of combat.<BR>3 In composition with words signifying hair, quantity, as केशपाशः much or flowing hair.<BR>4 In composition with कर्ण, beauty, as कर्णपाशः a handsome ear.<BR>5 In composition with छत्र and other woods, depreciation, as छत्रपाशः an inelegant or shabby umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>पश to bind, aff. घञ्; where it is used in composition, it is in fact but a technical aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशक|पाशकः
पाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dice, particularly the long sort used in playing Chaupai.<BR>E.<BR>पश to bind, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=531" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशपाणि|पाशपाणिः
पाशपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>E.<BR>पाश a sort of noose, and पाणि the hand, VARUṆA being represented as holding a cord in one hand, shaped like a sling or a noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबद्ध
पाशबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Noosed, snared, caught or bound.<BR>E.<BR>पाश, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशबन्ध|पाशबंध|पाशबन्धः
पाशबन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>A noose, a snare, a halter, a net, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पाश, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशभृत्
पाशभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 VARUṆA.<BR>2 A soldier, &c. armed with a noose.<BR>E.<BR>पाश, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A flock, a herd.<BR>E.<BR>पशु an animal, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशवपालन|पाशवपालनं
पाशवपालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pasturage or meadow grass.<BR>E.<BR>पाशव, and पालन supporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशित|पाशितः
पाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tied, fettered, bound.<BR>E.<BR>पाश a fetter, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 One armed with a net or noose.<BR>2 A deer-catcher or fowler, using a net or noose.<BR>3 A name of VARUṆA.<BR>4 A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>पाश a fetter, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशीकृत|पाशीकृतः
पाशीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tied, fettered.<BR>E.<BR>पाश a fetter, कृत made, and ई substituted for the final of the first word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A follower and worshipper of ŚIVA, in one of his forms as the supreme deity of the Hindū triad.<BR>2 A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>पशुपति a name of ŚIVA, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपतास्त्र|पाशुपतास्त्रं
पाशुपतास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>ŚIVA'S trident.<BR>E.<BR>पाशुपत, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्य|पाशुपाल्यं
पाशुपाल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>The business of a grazier, rearing and keeping cattle.<BR>E.<BR>पशु an animal, पाल nourishing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्य|पाश्चात्यः
पाश्चात्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Behind, being behind.<BR>2 Subsequent.<BR>3 Western.<BR>E.<BR>पश्चात्, and जा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>A number of nooses.<BR>E.<BR>पाश, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषक|पाषकः
पाषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ornament for the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्ड|पाषंड|पाषण्डः
पाषण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A heretick, an impostor, one who not conforming to the orthodox tenets of Hindū faith, assumes the external characteristicks of tribe or sect, a Jain, a Bauddha, &c.<BR>2 Any sect not Hindū.<BR>E.<BR>पाप sin, षण to give, ड aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डक|पाषंडक|पाषंडकः|पाषण्डकः
पाषण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A heretick, an impostor.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषण्डिन्|पाषंडिन्
पाषण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>A heretick, &c.: see पाषण्ड.<BR>E.<BR>पाषण्ड, and इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाण|पाषाणः
पाषाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A stone in general.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small stone used as a weight.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to grind, (condiments upon,) घञ् aff. आनच् added, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणदारक|पाषाणदारकः
पाषाणदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of hatchet for cutting stones, a stonecutter's chisel.<BR>E.<BR>पाषाण a stone, and दारक what tears or breaks; also पाषाणदारण, from दारण rending, tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणदारण|पाषाणदारणः
पाषाणदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An instrument for cutting stones; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणभेदिन्
पाषाणभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR>E.<BR>पाषाण a stone, and भेदिन् dividing; growing amongst stones and rocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाहात|पाहातः
पाहात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पि
पि<BR>r. 1st. cl. (पियति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक|पिकः
पिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Indian cuckoo, (Cuculus Indicus.)<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The female.<BR>E.<BR>पि imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकबन्धु|पिकबंधु|पिकबन्धुः
पिकबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>पिक the Kokila, and बन्धु friend; the favourite haunt of that bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकराग|पिकरागः
पिकराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>पिक, and राग fondness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकवल्लभ|पिकवल्लभः
पिकवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>पिक, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकाक्ष|पिकाक्षः
पिकाक्ष<BR>n. (-क्ष)<BR>A vegetable, and perfume, commonly Rocanī.<BR>E.<BR>पिक the Kokila, and अक्ष an eye; having red blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकाङ्ग|पिकाङ्गः
पिकाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A small bird, commonly Cāṭakīya.<BR>E.<BR>पिक the Kokila, and अङ्ग body or form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकानन्द|पिकानंद|पिकानन्दः
पिकानन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The spring season.<BR>E.<BR>पिक the Kokila, and आनन्द delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक्क|पिक्कः
पिक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A young elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पिक् imitative sound, and कै to utter, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्ग|पिंग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Of a tawny colour.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>2 A rat.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A young animal.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 A yellow dye: see गोरोचना.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>3 A tubular vessel of the body, which according to the Yoga system, is the channel of respiration and circulation for one side.<BR>4 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>5 Turmerick.<BR>6 Bambu manna.<BR>(-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of Mimosa, (M. suma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to colour, aff. अच्; or पिङ्ग tawny, aff. टाप्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गकपिशा|पिंगकपिशा
पिङ्गकपिशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग tawny, and कपिश brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गचक्षुस्|पिंगचक्षुस्
पिङ्गचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग tawny, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गजट|पिंगजट|पिङ्गजटः
पिङ्गजट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग tawny, and जटा braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गल|पिंगल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a tawny colour, brown, yellowish.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Tawny, (the colour,) a dull brown, or yellow.<BR>2 An attendant upon the sun.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A fabulous being in the form of a Nāga, or serpent of the lower regions, to whom a treatise on prosody is ascribed; he is hence considered as a Muni, or inspired and divine personage.<BR>5 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>6 One of KUVERA'S divine treasures.<BR>7 A monkey.<BR>8 Fire.<BR>9 An ichneumon.<BR>10 A sort of poison.<BR>11 A small owl.<BR>12 The 51st year of the Hindū cycle.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Brass.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The female elephant of the south quarter.<BR>2 A pious whore, commemorated in the Bhāgavata.<BR>3 A particular vessel of the body, the right of three canals which run from the os-coccygis to the head, and which are the chief passages of breath and air, according to the anatomy of the Yoga school of philosophy.<BR>4 An astrological house or period.<BR>5 The Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>6 Heartpea.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to colour, Uṇādi aff. अलच्; or पिङ्गल of a tawny hue, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गलिका|पिंगलिका
पिङ्गलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of crane: see वलाक.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्गल of a tawny colour, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाक्ष|पिंगाक्ष|पिङ्गाक्षः
पिङ्गाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग reddish brown, and अक्ष an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गाश|पिंगाश|पिंगाशः|पिङ्गाशः
पिङ्गाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A sort of fish, (Pimelodius pangasius, HAM.)<BR>2 The head man or proprietor of a village.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Virgin gold.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग tawny, आश flesh, from अश to eat, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गास्य|पिङ्गास्यः
पिङ्गास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A fish: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिङ्गेक्षण|पिंगेक्षण|पिङ्गेक्षणः
पिङ्गेक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पिङ्ग tawny, and ईक्षण eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=532" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्ड|पिचंड|पिचंडं|पिचंडः|पिचण्डः
पिचण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The belly.<BR>2 The back of an animal.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, चम to eat, aff. ड, initial of the prefix rejected; also पिचिण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्डिल|पिचंडिल|पिचण्डिलः
पिचण्डिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bigbellied, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>पिचण्ड the belly, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचण्डिका
पिचण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The instep; also पिचिण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचव्य|पिचव्यः
पिचव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>The cotton plant.<BR>E.<BR>पिचु cotton, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचिण्ड|पिचिंड|पिचिंडं|पिचिंडः|पिचिण्डः
पिचिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The belly or abdomen.<BR>2 The back of an animal.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, चम to eat, aff. ड, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचिण्डिल|पिचिंडिल|पिचिण्डिलः
पिचिण्डिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bigbellied, corpulent, potbellied.<BR>E.<BR>पिचिण्ड a belly, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचु|पिचुः
पिचु<BR>m. (-चुः)<BR>1 Cotton.<BR>2 The name of an Asura.<BR>3 A Karṣa or weight of two Tolas: see कर्ष.<BR>4 A sort of leprosy.<BR>5 One of the eight faces of BHAIRAVA.<BR>E.<BR>पिच Sautra root, to rub, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुक|पिचुकः
पिचुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुतूल|पिचुतूलं
पिचुतूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cotton.<BR>E.<BR>पिचु and तूल both meaning the same, cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमन्द|पिचुमंद|पिचुमन्दः
पिचुमन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The Nimb tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR>E.<BR>पिचु a sort of leprosy, and मन्द to be slow, in the causal form, to make slow or check, aff. अच्; also पिचुमर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुमर्द्द|पिचुमर्द|पिचुमर्दः|पिचुमर्द्दः
पिचुमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>The Nimb tree: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पिचु as before, मृद to destroy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचुल|पिचुलः
पिचुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Cotton; also पिचु.<BR>2 The tamarisk, (T. Indica.)<BR>3 A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>4 The diver or water-crow.<BR>E.<BR>पिचु cotton, ला to get, &c. aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्च
पिच्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (पिच्चति)<BR>To cut, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्चट|पिच्चटं|पिच्चटः
पिच्चट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Tin.<BR>2 Lead.<BR>3 Inflammation of the eyes, ophthalmia.<BR>E.<BR>पिच्च to divide, aff. अच्, and ढौक for ढौक to go, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (पिच्छति)<BR>1 To pain or torture.<BR>2 To hinder.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पिच्छयति)<BR>To cut, to divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छ|पिच्छं|पिच्छः
पिच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>1 The tail of a peacock.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A tail in general.<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>1 The gum of the silk cotton tree.<BR>2 A line, a row or range.<BR>3 A diseased affection of a horse's feet.<BR>4 The nut of the Areca, betel nut.<BR>5 A plantain.<BR>6 The scum of boiled rice.<BR>7 A sort of body dress, or jacket.<BR>8 The venomous saliva of a snake.<BR>9 The Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>10 A sheath, a coat or cover.<BR>E.<BR>पिच्छ to divide, aff. घञ् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छलदला
पिच्छलदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba.)<BR>E.<BR>पिच्छल for पिच्छिल a tree, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छवत्
पिच्छवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Tailed, having a tail.<BR>E.<BR>पिच्छ, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छवाण
पिच्छवाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छितिका
पिच्छितिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Sisu, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिल|पिच्छिलं|पिच्छिलः
पिच्छिल<BR>mfn. subst. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Sauce mixed with rice gruel.<BR>2 Sauce, gravy, or condiments with water or Ghee.<BR>3 Broth, soup.<BR>4 Moist, and split pulse.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>2 A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR>3 A timber tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>5 An esculent root, (Arum Indicum.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The tamarisk, (Tamarix Indica).<BR>mfn. adj. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having a tail.<BR>E.<BR>पिच्छा rice water, scum, &c. and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिच्छिलत्वच्
पिच्छिलत्वच्<BR>m. (-त्वक्)<BR>1 An orange.<BR>2 Orange peel.<BR>E.<BR>पिच्छिल said to mean an orange, and त्वच् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिज
पिज<BR>(इ) पिजि r. 2nd cl. (पिंक्ते)<BR>1 To tinge, to dye or colour, to impinge.<BR>2 To touch.<BR>3 To tinkle.<BR>4 To adore.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पिञ्जति पिञ्जयति)<BR>1 To kill or injure.<BR>2 To be strong.<BR>3 To give.<BR>4 To dwell.<BR>5 To speak.<BR>6 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्ज|पिंज|पिञ्जं|पिञ्जः
पिञ्ज<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं)<BR>Disturbed in mind, confused, confounded.<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>n. (-ञ्जं)<BR>Strength, power.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>1 Hurting, injuring, injury.<BR>2 Cotton.<BR>3 Turmerick.<BR>4 A sort of palm (?)<BR>5 A switch.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to hurt or kill, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जट|पिंजट|पिंजटः|पिञ्जटः
पिञ्जट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The concrete rheum of the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to give pain, अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जन|पिंजन|पिंजनं|पिञ्जनं
पिञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bow used for cleaning cotton.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to touch, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जर|पिंजर|पिञ्जरं|पिञ्जरः
पिञ्जर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Yellow or tawny, reddish yellow.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of colour, tawny brown, a reddish yellow, or a mixture of red and yellow.<BR>2 A horse, probably a bay or chesnut horse.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>3 A cage.<BR>4 The ribs or the cavity formed by them, the thorax: see पञ्जर.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to dye or tinge, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जल|पिंजल|पिञ्जलं|पिञ्जलः
पिञ्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Confounded, overcome with terror or grief.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An army panick-struck, or in great disorder.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The leaf of the Kuśa grass.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Two blades of Kusa grass, used as a vessel, or to take up articles with, at sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to hurt, &c. aff. अलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जान|पिञ्जानं
पिञ्जान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जिका|पिंजिका
पिञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A roll of cotton, from which the threads are spun.<BR>E.<BR>पिञ्जा cotton, कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूल|पिञ्जूलं
पिञ्जूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The wick of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to hurt, &c. Uṇādi aff. ऊलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जूष|पिंजूष|पिंजूषः|पिञ्जूषः
पिञ्जूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The wax of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to stain, ऊष aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जेट|पिंजेट|पिंजेटः|पिञ्जेटः
पिञ्जेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The excretion, or concrete rheum of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिञ्जोला|पिंजोला
पिञ्जोला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The noise, or rustling of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट<BR>r. 1st cl. (पेटयति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To assemble or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट|पिटं|पिटः
पिट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A basket for holding grain, a sort of cupboard or granary made of bambus or canes.<BR>2 A basket, a box.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A house, a hovel.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटक|पिटकं|पिटकः
पिटक<BR>mfn. subst. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A boil.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A basket, a box.<BR>2 A large basket, or receptacle of basket work, for keeping grain, &c. a granary.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, aff. क्वुन्; also षिट and पेटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्काकी
पिटङ्काकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Colocynth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटङ्काश|पिटङ्काशः
पिटङ्काश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A species of pike, (Esox scolopax.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिटाक|पिटाकः
पिटाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a saint.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, and आक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिट्टक|पिट्टकं
पिट्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The tartar or excretion of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ|पिठः
पिठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (पेठति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To feel pain or affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठ|पिठः
पिठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Pain, distress.<BR>E.<BR>पिठ, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिठर|पिठरं|पिठरः
पिठर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A pot, a pan.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A churning stick.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>3 A sort of building, a hut or watch box made of bambus and mats, or as it is [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">Page534</a>] sometimes explained, a kind of store room or scullery.<BR>E.<BR>पिठ pain, रा to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=533" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिड
पिड<BR>(इ,) पिडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (पिण्डति-ते पिण्डयति)<BR>To accumulate, to assemble, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिडक|पिडकः
पिडक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A small boil, a pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्ड|पिंड|पिण्डं|पिण्डः
पिण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>A lump, a heap, a cluster, a quantity or collection.<BR>mf. (-ण्डः-ण्डी)<BR>An oblation to deceased ancestors, as a ball or lump of meat, or rice, mixed up with milk, curds, flowers, &c. and offered to the manes at the several Śrāddhas, by the nearest surviving relations.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A ball, a globe.<BR>2 A mouthful, or roundish lump of food, considered as equivalent to a mouthful.<BR>3 Presenting water or cake to a deceased relation.<BR>4 The body.<BR>5 The side immediately below the armpit.<BR>6 A part of a house; a sort of portico or shed, in front of the door.<BR>7 Coarse, gross, thick, solid.<BR>8 Strength, power.<BR>9 Myrrh.<BR>10 Frankincense.<BR>11 The China rose.<BR>12 Food.<BR>13 Flesh, meat.<BR>14 The projection of an elephant's frontal sinus.<BR>15 The embryo or fetus in an early stage of gestation.<BR>16 A sum, (in arithmetic^1.)<BR>17 (In astronomy) The twenty-fourth part of the quadrant of a circle, or 3°-45'<BR>n. (-पडं)<BR>1 Livelihood, means of living.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>3 Fresh butter.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A long gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaria.)<BR>2 A sort of palm, (Phœnix dactylifera.)<BR>3 A flowering shrub, (Tabernæmontana coronaria flor. plen.)<BR>4 Performance of certain gesticulations, accompanying the silent repetition of prayers, &c. in meditation on real or divine knowledge.<BR>5 The nave of a wheel.<BR>6 A house.<BR>E.<BR>पिडि to heap, to gather, to collect, &c. aff. अच् or घञ्, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डक|पिंडक|पिंडकं|पिण्डकं|पिंडकः|पिण्डकः
पिण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Incense.<BR>2 A goblin, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डकन्द|पिण्डकन्दः
पिण्डकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>See पिण्डालु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डखर्ज्जूर|पिण्डखर्जूर|पिण्डखर्ज्जूरः
पिण्डखर्ज्जूर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A sort of date tree.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, a cluster, and खर्ज्जूर the date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डगोस|पिंडगोस|पिण्डगोसः
पिण्डगोस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Gum myrrh; also पिण्ड and गोस severally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डतैलक|पिंडतैलक|पिण्डतैलकः
पिण्डतैलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Incense, olibanum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डद|पिंडद|पिण्डदः
पिण्डद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Who or what gives the funeral cake to deceased ancestors.<BR>2 One who supports or feeds another.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The nearest male relation.<BR>2 A patron, a master.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डदान|पिंडदान
पिण्डदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Presentation of the obsequial cake.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डन|पिंडन|पिंडनं|पिण्डनः
पिण्डन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A mound or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डनिर्वपन
पिण्डनिर्वपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Presenting obsequial cakes to the manes.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and निर्वपन offering funeral oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपाद|पिंडपाद|पिण्डपादः
पिण्डपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump of flesh, and पाद a foot: also पिण्डपाद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपुष्प|पिंडपुष्प|पिण्डपुष्पं|पिण्डपुष्पः
पिण्डपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 The flower of the Asoca tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>2 The China rose.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>4 A flower, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a cluster, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डपुष्पक|पिण्डपुष्पकः
पिण्डपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, पुष्प a flower, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डफला
पिण्डफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमात्रोपजीविन्
पिण्डमात्रोपजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living, breathing, having no intellectual existence.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, माच only, उपजीविन् subsisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमुस्ता
पिण्डमुस्ता<BR>f. (-स्वा)<BR>A sort of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, and मुस्ता Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डमूल|पिंडमूल|पिण्डमूलं
पिण्डमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The carrot, (Daucus carota.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड lump of flesh, and मूल a root; also with कन् added पिण्डमूलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डल|पिंडल|पिंडलः|पिण्डलः
पिण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bridge, a causeway, a passage over a stream or ravine, &c. or a mound raised to form a path across inundated fields.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a heap, (of earth, &c.) and ला to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डवीज
पिण्डवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A flowering shrub, (Oleander odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डस|पिंडस|पिंडसः|पिण्डसः
पिण्डस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A beggar, a mendicant living upon alms.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a ball of rice, &c. सद to go or get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डात|पिंडात|पिंडातः|पिण्डातः
पिण्डात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Incense.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड the same, अत to be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डाभ्र|पिंडाभ्र|पिण्डाभ्रं
पिण्डाभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, and अभ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डायस|पिंडायस|पिण्डायसं
पिण्डायस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Steel.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and अयस iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डार|पिंडार|पिण्डारं|पिंडारः|पिण्डारः
पिण्डार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A keeper or attendant on buffaloes.<BR>2 A cowherd.<BR>3 A beggar, a religious mendicant.<BR>4 A tree, (Trewia nudiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a heap, ऋ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डालु|पिण्डालुः
पिण्डालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>An esculent and medical root, described as sweet, cooling, and diuretic^1.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, and आलु an esculent root.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डाश|पिंडाश|पिण्डाशः
पिण्डाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>A beggar.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a piece of meat, आश who eats; also पिण्डाशनः and पिण्डाशिन् (-शी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डि|पिंडि|पिंडिः|पिण्डिः
पिण्डि<BR>f. (-ण्डिः)<BR>The nave of a wheel.<BR>E.<BR>पिडि to collect, (the spokes,) aff. इन्; also पिण्डी and पिण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिका|पिंडिका
पिण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The nave of a wheel.<BR>2 The instep.<BR>3 A stool or seat of various shapes and dimensions.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्डी as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डित|पिंडित|पिण्डितं|पिण्डितः
पिण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Multiplied, added.<BR>2 Counted, numbered.<BR>3 Thick, massy, lumpish.<BR>4 Collected, heaped together.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a lump, a heap, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिन्|पिंडिन्
पिण्डिन्<BR>mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि)<BR>Having a Piṇḍa or ball of food, (a ceremony, an ancestor, &c.)<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A beggar.<BR>2 An offerer of oblations.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डिल|पिंडिल|पिण्डिलः
पिण्डिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A bridge, a mound, a causeway.<BR>2 An astrologer, an arithmetician, a calculator of nativities, &c.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (C. madraspatanus.)<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a heap, &c. इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीकरण
पिण्डीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Heaping, making up into a lump or ball.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीकृत
पिण्डीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made into a lump or ball.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and कृत made, च्वि augm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीतक|पिण्डीतकः
पिण्डीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (Vangueria spinosa, Rox.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Tabernæmontana coronaria.)<BR>3 A plant, commonly Marüa; see मरुवक.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्डी a plant, तन to spread, to resemble, aff. ड and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीतगर|पिण्डीतगरः
पिण्डीतगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, a species of tabernæmontana.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्डी the same, and तगर T. coronaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीभूत
पिण्डीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lumped, heaped, made up in a lump or ball.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and भूत become, च्वि augm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीर|पिंडीर|पिण्डीरः
पिण्डीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Sapless, juiceless, arid, dry.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The pomegranate.<BR>2 Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a ball, &c. ऋ to go, to resemble, aff. अप्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डीशूर|पिंडीशूर|पिण्डीशूरः
पिण्डीशूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cot quean, an effeminate braggart.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्डी a house, and शूर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=534" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोद्धरण|पिंडोद्धरण
पिण्डोद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Participating in obsequial offerings, presenting them to common ancestors.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड, and उद्वरण sharing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्डोलि|पिंडोलि|पिंडोलिः|पिण्डोलिः
पिण्डोलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Orts, leavings of a meal, or fragments dropped from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>पिडि to heap, aff. ओलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्या
पिण्या<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)<BR>E.<BR>पण to praise, ण्यत् aff., and इ substituted for the radical vowel: see पण्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिण्याक|पिण्याकं|पिण्याकः
पिण्याक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The sediments of seeds, &c. ground for oil; oil-cake, or the seeds after expression.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>3 Asafœtida.<BR>4 Incense.<BR>E.<BR>पिषु to pound or bruise, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितामह|पितामहः
पितामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A paternal grandfather.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ, the great father of all.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A paternal grandmother.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, and मह aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृ
पितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father.<BR>dual (-रौ)<BR>Mother and father, parents.<BR>plu. always. (-रः)<BR>1 Paternal ancestors.<BR>2 The manes, or the deceased and deified progenitors of mankind, inhabiting a peculiar region or heaven, or according to some, the orbit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>पा to nourish, Uṇādi aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक|पितृकं
पितृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Paternal, ancestral, parental, obsequial, relating or belonging to parents or progenitors.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a sire, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितॄक्थ
पितॄक्थ<BR>n. (-क्थं)<BR>Paternal property.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and ऋक्थ wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकर्म्मन्|पितृकर्मन्
पितृकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकार्य्य|पितृकार्य
पितृकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and कार्य्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृकानन|पितृकाननं
पितृकानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ an ancestor, and कानन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृक्रिया
पितृक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and क्रिया ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगण|पितृगणः
पितृगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A class of progenitors, the sons of the Ṛṣis or Prajāpatis: the principal classes are the Sonasads descended from VIRĀṬA, the Agniṣvāttas from MARĪCI, Barhiṣads from ATRI, Somapās from BHṚGU, Haviṣmats from AṄGIRAS, Ājyapas from PULASTYA, Sukālins from VASIṢṬHA; there are also the Agnidagdhas and Anagnidagdhas, Kāvyas and Saumyas.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ father (of mankind), गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगामिन्
पितृगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Belonging to, or pertaining to a father.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृगृह|पितृगृहं
पितृगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A burying ground, a cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a deceased ancestor, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृघातक|पितृघातकः
पितृघातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A parricide.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and घातक slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतर्पण|पितृतर्पणं
पितृतर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The part of the hand between the middle finger and thumb, sacred to the manes.<BR>2 Gifts in honour of deceased relations, distributed at the Śrāddhas or funeral ceremonies.<BR>3 The act of throwing water out of the right hand at seasons of ablution, by way of offering to the manes, or deceased ancestors in general.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, a progenitor, and तर्पण satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतस्
पितृतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From or by the father.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतिथि|पितृतिथिः
पितृतिथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>Day of new moon, on which she rises invisible.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and तिथि a lunar day, sacred to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृतीर्थ|पितृतीर्थं
पितृतीर्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>1 Gaya, the city so called, where the performance of funeral sacrifices is peculiarly efficacious and meritorious.<BR>2 The part between the forefinger and thumb, sacred to the manes.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and तीर्थ a place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृत्व
पितृत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Paternity.<BR>2 The state or condition of a Pitṛ, or deified progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to पितृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदान|पितृदानं
पितृदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift in honour of deceased ancestors.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and दान giving or gift; also with कन् added, पितृदानक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृदैवत
पितृदैवत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The tenth lunar asterism or Magha.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and दैवत divinity, presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपति|पितृपतिः
पितृपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a deceased progenitor, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपद
पितृपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The world or state of the manes.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and पद degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपात्र
पितृपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A cup or vessel used at obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and पात्र a cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृपितृ
पितृपितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A paternal grandfather.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, and पितृ the same, a father's father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्रसू
पितृप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 Twilight.<BR>2 A father's mother.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a deceased progenitor, and प्रसू the parent; the first is the time when the manes are abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृप्राप्त
पितृप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Received from a father.<BR>2 Inherited patrimonially.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबन्धु|पितृबंधु|पितृबन्धुः
पितृबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A remote or cognate kinsman by the father's side, as the son of the paternal grandfather's sister, of the paternal grandmother's sister, and of the father's maternal uncle.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and बन्धु a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृबान्धव|पितृबान्धवः
पितृबान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A remote kinsman of the paternal line: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and बान्धव a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभक्ति
पितृभक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Filial duty to a father.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and भक्ति devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभोजन|पितृभोजनः
पितृभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Food offered to the manes.<BR>2 A father's food.<BR>3 A kind of pulse: see Māṣa.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृभ्रातृ
पितृभ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father's brother.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and भ्रातृ a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमन्दिर|पितृमंदिर
पितृमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The paternal mansion.<BR>2 A cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and मन्दिर a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृमेध|पितृमेधः
पितृमेध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and मेध sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयज्ञ|पितृयज्ञः
पितृयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृयान
पितृयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The carriage of the manes, a car to convey holy persons after their decease to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a progenitor, and यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृलोक|पितृलोकः
पितृलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The world or sphere of the manes: it is variously situated, but principally in the Bhuvas region or midheaven.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवत्
पितृवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a father living, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवन|पितृवनं
पितृवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a deceased progenitor, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवनेचर|पितृवनेचरः
पितृवनेचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A goblin.<BR>E.<BR>पितृवन a cemetery, in the seventh case, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवसति|पितृवसतिः
पितृवसति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a deceased progenitor, and वसति an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृवाक्पर
पितृवाक्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Obedient to parents.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, वाच् speech, पर attentive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्य|पितृव्यः
पितृव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A paternal uncle.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, and व्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=535" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृव्रत|पितृव्रतः
पितृव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Who worships the manes.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Worship of ancestors, obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and व्रत obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृश्राद्ध
पितृश्राद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>The obsequial ceremony of a father.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and श्राद्ध the rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृष्वसृ
पितृष्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A father's sister.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, and खसृ a sister, स changed to ष; the compound may also be पितुःष्वसृ, पितुःखसृ, पितुस्खसृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृसन्निभ|पितृसंनिभ|पितृसन्निभः
पितृसन्निभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Fatherly.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and सन्निभ like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृसामान्य
पितृसामान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Ancestors collectively.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and सामान्य universality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृसू
पितृसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 Twilight.<BR>2 A father's mother.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a ghost, and सू producing: see पितृप्रसू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्थान|पितृस्थानः
पितृस्थान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A guardian, a protector.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The abode of the manes.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and स्थान like, or in place of; a place, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्थानीय|पितृस्थानीयः
पितृस्थानीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A guardian.<BR>E.<BR>पितृस्थान, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृस्वस्रीय
पितृस्वस्रीय<BR>mf. (-यः-या)<BR>A maternal aunt's son or daughter.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and स्वस्रीय sister's son, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पितृहन्
पितृहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A parricide.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्त|पित्तं
पित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, दी to destroy, or देङ् to nourish, aff. क्त, deriv. irr., or तप to inflame, aff. क्त, and the radical letters transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तघ्न
पित्तघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Antibilious.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त bile, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तज्वर|पित्तज्वरः
पित्तज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Bilious fever.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त bile, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तद्राविन्
पित्तद्राविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Removing bile, causing it to flow.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त, and द्राविन् what disperses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तरक्त|पित्तरक्तं
पित्तरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Plethora: see रक्तपित्त.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त, and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्तल|पित्तलं
पित्तल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bilious, relating to the bilious humour.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Brass.<BR>2 The Bhojpatra or Birch tree, of which the bark is used for writing upon, &c.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>E.<BR>पित्त bile, ला to get, to resemble, (in colour,) aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्र्य|पित्र्यं|पित्र्यः
पित्र्य<BR>mfn. (-त्र्याः-त्र्या-त्र्यं)<BR>1 Paternal, ancestral.<BR>2 Obsequial, relating to deceased progenitors.<BR>m. (-त्र्यः)<BR>A father's elder brother.<BR>n. (-त्र्यं)<BR>The part of the hand between the forefinger and thumb, sacred to the manes.<BR>f. (-त्र्या)<BR>1 One of the lunar asterisms, also Magha.<BR>2 Day of full moon.<BR>3 Ceremonies performed in honour of the deceased on the day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, and यत् aff., रीङ् substituted for ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सत्|पित्सन्त्
पित्सत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Habitually falling or coming down.<BR>2 Obtained, gained.<BR>m. (-सन्)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall or alight, शतृ aff., and desiderative form; the reduplicate syllable omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पित्सल|पित्सलं|पित्सलः
पित्सल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A road, a path, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत to go, Uṇādi aff. सल, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिदधत्
पिदधत्<BR>mfn. (-धन्-धन्ती-धत्)<BR>Covering, veiling, hiding.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before षा to have, शूतृ aff. and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधान|पिधानं
पिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A covering, a cover or concealment.<BR>2 A lid, a top or cover.<BR>3 A sheath.<BR>4 A wrapper, a cloak, &c.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, धा to have or hold, (from sight,) ल्युट् aff., and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनद्ध|पिनद्धः
पिनद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Clothed, accoutred, dressed.<BR>E.<BR>अपि, and नह to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनस
पिनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Cold, catarrh: see पीनस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनह्य
पिनह्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having put on or dressed.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before, नह to tie, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाक|पिनाकं|पिनाकः
पिनाक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The bow of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A trident or threepronged spear.<BR>3 The trident of ŚIVA.<BR>4 A shower of dust.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A musical instrument, a sort of viol.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve, (the world,) Uṇādi aff. आक, the radical vowel changed to इ, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिनाकिन्
पिनाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पिनाक ŚIVA'S bow or trident, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिन्यास|पिन्यासं|पिन्यासः
पिन्यास<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before न्यस (compounded of नि and अस to throw), to be given or place in condiments, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषत्|पिपतिषन्त्
पिपतिषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Inclined or addicted to falling repeatedly.<BR>m. (-षन्)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to come down, in the desiderative form, and शतृ participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषा
पिपतिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Wish or inclination to come down, to fall, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपतिषु|पिपतिषुः
पिपतिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Disposed to fall or descend.<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>पत to fall, desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपविषु
पिपविषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to purify.<BR>E.<BR>पू to be pure, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासत्|पिपासन्त्
पिपासत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Thirsty, thirsting.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासा
पिपासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Thirst.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink in the desiderative form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासित|पिपासितः
पिपासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thirsty, athirst.<BR>E.<BR>पिपासा thirst, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपासु|पिपासुः
पिपासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Thirsty, athirst.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, desid. form, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीतकी
पिपीतकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The twelfth of the month Vaiśākha, when giving away water is an act of merit.<BR>E.<BR>पिपीतक the name of a Brahman, said to have instituted the rite, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपीलक|पिपीलकः
पिपीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A large black ant.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>The common small red ant.<BR>E.<BR>पील to stop, repeated, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिपृच्छिषु
पिपृच्छिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to ask.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पटा
पिप्पटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पल|पिप्पलं|पिप्पलः
पिप्पल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>2 A bird.<BR>3 The sleeve of a jacket or coat.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Longpepper.<BR>E.<BR>(-पा) to preserve, aff. कलच्, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलक|पिप्पलकं
पिप्पलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A nipple.<BR>2 Sewing thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलि|पिप्पलिः
पिप्पलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Long-pepper: see पिप्पल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पलीमूल|पिप्पलीमूलं
पिप्पलीमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of long-pepper.<BR>E.<BR>पिप्पली, and मल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्पिका
पिप्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The tartar of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>पाय to increase, aff. इक, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिप्लु|पिप्लुः
पिप्लु<BR>m. (-प्लुः)<BR>A freckle, a mark.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, प्लुष to burn or inflame, aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पियाल|पियालः
पियाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, called in Hindi also Chironji, (whence it has been named Chironjia sapida, Rox. in the catalogue it is termed Buchanania latifolia, Rox.); in Bengal, commonly Piya or Piyal.<BR>E.<BR>पीय a Sautra root, to regard, Uṇādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल
पिल<BR>r. 10th cl. (पेलयति)<BR>To throw, to cast or send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=536" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलुक|पिलुकः
पिलुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree: see पीलु.<BR>E.<BR>पिल to send, aff. कु, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिलुनी
पिलुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant: see मूर्व्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्ल|पिल्लः
पिल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ली-ल्लं)<BR>Blear-eyed.<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A bleared eye.<BR>E.<BR>पिल्ल considered as a substitute for क्लिन्न wet, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिल्लका
पिल्लका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पिल्ल blear-eyed, aff. कन्; the elephant's eye being usually moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिव
पिव<BR>(इ,) पिवि r. 1st cl. (पिन्वते)<BR>To sprinkle, to wet or moisten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिव
पिव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Who or what drinks.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिवत्
पिवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Drinking.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिश
पिश<BR>r. 1st cl. (पिशति)<BR>1 To be decomposed, to be reduced to constituent parts.<BR>2 To be organised.<BR>3 To enlighten, to light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्ग|पिशंग|पिशङ्गः
पिशङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Of a tawny or brown colour.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>पिश to be a component part, अङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गता
पिशङ्गता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Tawniness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, पिशङ्गत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशङ्गिन्|पिशंगिन्
पिशङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>Brown, tawny.<BR>E.<BR>पिशङ्ग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाच|पिशाचः
पिशाच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A sprite, a fiend, a malevolent being something between an infernal imp and a ghost, but always described as fierce and malignant.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A female imp, a she demon.<BR>E.<BR>पिश for पिशित flesh, and अश to eat, aff. अण्, deriv. irr.; also with कन् added, पिशाचक, पिशाचिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचकिन्
पिशाचकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>पिशाच a demon, इनि aff., and कुक् augment; the treasures of this deity being guarded by Piśācas, and other malignant beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचद्रु|पिशाचद्रुः
पिशाचद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>पिशाच a goblin, and द्रु a tree; the favourite haunt of these beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचवृक्ष|पिशाचवृक्षः
पिशाचवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Śākhoṭa tree: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पिशाच, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशाचसभ|पिशाचसभं
पिशाचसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 An assemblage of goblins or fiends.<BR>2 The place or hall of their assembly, pandemonium.<BR>E.<BR>पिशाच a goblin, and सभा assembly, but neuter in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशित|पिशितं
पिशित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to be a component part, part. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशन|पिशिताशनः
पिशिताशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Eating meat.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A demon, a fiend, a cannibal.<BR>E.<BR>पिशित, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशिताशिन्
पिशिताशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Eating flesh or meat, carnivorous.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A goblin, a cannibal.<BR>E.<BR>पिशित, and अश to eat, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुन|पिशुनं|पिशुनः
पिशुन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Cruel, wicked.<BR>2 Vile, low, contemptible.<BR>3 Stupid, a fool.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A spy, an informer.<BR>2 A name of NĀRADA.<BR>3 A crow.<BR>4 Cotton.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>पिश to be a part, उनन् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवचन
पिशुनवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Evil speech, abuse, detraction, slander.<BR>E.<BR>पिशुन, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिशुनवाक्य
पिशुनवाक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Evil speech, bad report, detraction, slander.<BR>E.<BR>पिशुन, and वाक्य speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष
पिष<BR>r. 7th cl. (पिषष्टि)<BR>To grind, to pound, to bruise or powder.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पेषयति)<BR>1 To injure.<BR>2 To give.<BR>3 To be strong.<BR>4 To dwell.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पेषति पेषयति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्ट|पिष्टं
पिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Ground, pounded, bruised.<BR>2 Clasped, (as the hands,) squeezed, rubbed together.<BR>3 Kneaded.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Lead.<BR>2 The flour or meal of any thing that is ground.<BR>E.<BR>पिष to pound or bruise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टक|पिष्टकं|पिष्टकः
पिष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cake made of the flour or meal of any grain.<BR>2 A disease of the eyes, opacity of the cornea.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Oilcake.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट what is pounded, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टप|पिष्टपं|पिष्टपः
पिष्टप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A world, a division of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to go, अप् Uṇādi aff., and टन् augment; also पिष्टप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपचन|पिष्टपचनं
पिष्टपचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A boiler, a seether, a sauce-pan.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट meal, &c. and पचन cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपशु|पिष्टपशुः
पिष्टपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A type or effigy of a victim, made with flour.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाकभृत्
पिष्टपाकभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A boiler.<BR>E.<BR>विष्ट meal, पाक cooking, and भृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपाचक
पिष्टपाचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A boiler.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट, and पाचक what cooks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टपूर|पिष्टपूरः
पिष्टपूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Meal, made up into a sort of cake with clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट meal, and पॄ to complete, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टमय
पिष्टमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of meal or flour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट that which is ground, and मयट् transformative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टवर्त्ति|पिष्टवर्ति|पिष्टवर्तिः|पिष्टवर्त्तिः
पिष्टवर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A small cake, made of barley, rice or pulse ground to meal.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट meal, and वृत to be, and इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टसौरभ|पिष्टसौरभं
पिष्टसौरभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट ground, and सौरभ fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टात|पिष्टातः
पिष्टात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Perfumed powder, for scenting rooms, garments, &c. especially the scented dust, which the Hindus sprinkle over each other at the Holī or spring festival.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट pounded, (saffron, &c.) and अत to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिष्टिक|पिष्टिकं
पिष्टिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A cake made of rice flour.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The meal of pulse steeped in water, peeled and ground.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट ground, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिस
पिस<BR>(ऋ) पिसृ r. 1st cl. (पेसति)<BR>To go or move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पेसयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To be strong.<BR>3 To injure or hurt.<BR>4 To give.<BR>5 To dwell.<BR>(इ) पिसि r. 10th cl. (पिंसयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>3 To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
पिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered, hidden, concealed.<BR>2 Filled with.<BR>E.<BR>अपि before षा to have, aff. क्त, and the initial of the prefix rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पी
पी<BR>(ङ,) पीङ् r. 4th cl. (पीयते)<BR>To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीच|पीचं
पीच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>The lower jaw, the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठ|पीठं
पीठ<BR>mfn. (-ठः-ठी-ठं)<BR>1 A stool, a seat, a chair.<BR>2 The seat of the religious student, made properly of Kuśa grass.<BR>3 A place where some limb of PĀRVATĪ is supposed to have fallen, as after Daksha's sacrifice, her dead body was carried about by ŚIVA, and cut in pieces by the discus of VIṢṆU: there are fifty-one such places.<BR>4 Complement of a segment, (in Geometry.)<BR>E.<BR>पिठ to feel pain, to be weary, aff. घञ्; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठकेलि|पीठकेलिः
पीठकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A male confidant, a parasite.<BR>E.<BR>पीठ a seat, and केलि sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठमर्द|पीठमर्दः|पीठमर्द्द|पीठमर्द्दः
पीठमर्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A parasite, a companion.<BR>E.<BR>पीठ a seat, and मृद to rub, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठसर्पिन्
पीठसर्पिन्<BR>m. (-र्पी)<BR>A cripple, who moves about on a wheeled chair, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पीठ a seat, and सर्पिन् who moves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीठस्थान
पीठस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A place where some limb of PĀRVATĪ is supposed to have fallen: see पीठ.<BR>E.<BR>पीठ, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड
पीड<BR>(ऋ) पीडृ r. 10th cl. (पीडयति)<BR>1 To give pain.<BR>2 To oppose or resist.<BR>3 To stir, to agitate.<BR>4 To squeeze or pinch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=537" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडन|पीडनं
पीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Inflicting pain, paining, distressing.<BR>2 Devastation, laying a country waste.<BR>3 Squeezing, pressing, rubbing.<BR>E.<BR>पीड to give pain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडा
पीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 Pain, anguish, suffering.<BR>2 Compassion, charity, pity.<BR>3 Devastation, laying waste.<BR>4 A chaplet, a garland for the head.<BR>5 The Saral tree, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>पीड to pain, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकर
पीडाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Giving pain, afflicting, tormenting.<BR>E.<BR>पीडा, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडाकरण
पीडाकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Torturing, tormenting.<BR>E.<BR>पीडा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीडित|पीडितं
पीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bound, tied.<BR>2 Pained, suffering pain or distress.<BR>3 Laid waste, destroyed, devastated.<BR>4 Rubbed, chafed.<BR>5 Squeezed, pressed.<BR>E.<BR>पीडा pain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीड्यमान
पीड्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being pained or afflicted.<BR>2 Suffering from.<BR>3 Being squeezed or pressed.<BR>E.<BR>पीड to pain, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत|पीतं|पीतः
पीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Of a yellow colour.<BR>2 Drank, quaffed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Yellow, the colour.<BR>2 Safflower.<BR>3 A topaz, a yellow gem.<BR>4 A yellow pigment, prepared from the urine of kine.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Drinking.<BR>2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Turmerick.<BR>2 A medical plant, commonly Atais, (Betula.)<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, aff. क्त; imbibed, literally, or figuratively, by the eye sight, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतक|पीतकं|पीतकः
पीतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>3 Aloe-wood.<BR>4 Brass.<BR>5 Honey.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of gentian, (G. Cherayta.)<BR>2 The Tūn tree.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकदली
पीतकदली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of plantain.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, कदली plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकन्द|पीतकंद|पीतकन्दं
पीतकन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>The carrot.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकावेर|पीतकावेरं
पीतकावेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Saffron.<BR>2 Brass.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, कावेर vile shape or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतकाष्ठ|पीतकाष्ठं
पीतकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Yellow sanders.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, काष्ठ wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतघोषा
पीतघोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A sort of creeper with yellow flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and घोषा the plant; yellow Ghoṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचन्दन|पीतचंदन|पीतचन्दनं
पीतचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A yellow fragrant wood, considered as a yellow species of Sandal wood.<BR>2 Turmerick.<BR>3 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतचम्पक|पीतचंपक|पीतचम्पकः
पीतचम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, चम्पक a flower, and कन् aff. of comparison; like the Campa in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतता
पीतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Yellowness.<BR>E.<BR>पीत्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व पीतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीततुण्ड|पीततुंड|पीततुण्डः
पीततुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The tailor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and तुण्ड a beak; the whole bird is of a light yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीततैला
पीततैला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of creeper, a species of the heart-pea.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदारु
पीतदारु<BR>n. (-रुः)<BR>1 A sort of pine, (P. Devadāru.)<BR>2 Another kind of pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतदुग्धा
पीतदुग्धा<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>1 A cow tied up to be milked.<BR>2 Any milch cow.<BR>E.<BR>पीत drank, दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतद्रु|पीतद्रुः
पीतद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>1 A sort of Curcuma, (C. zanthorrhizon.)<BR>2 A species of pine, (P. longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतन|पीतनं|पीतनः
पीतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>2 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>3 The waved leaf fig tree.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Saffron.<BR>2 A sort of pine: see पीतदारु.<BR>3 Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, णी to go, or be, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपर्णी
पीतपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, commonly Bichati; a name applied to the nettle, or a plant of the same class, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपादा
पीतपादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A small bird, the Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतपुष्प|पीतपुष्पं|पीतपुष्पः
पीतपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A species of Karṇikāra.<BR>2 A sort of Tabernæmontana.<BR>f. (-ष्पा-ष्पी)<BR>Yellow barleria.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and पुष्प a flower; it may be applied to any plant with yellow flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतफल|पीतफलः
पीतफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतबालुका
पीतबालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Turmerick.<BR>2 Yellow sand.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and बालुका sand or dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमणि|पीतमणिः
पीतमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A yellow gem, a topaz.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमस्तक
पीतमस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small bird, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and मस्तक the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमुण्ड
पीतमुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, मुण्ड the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतमुद्ग|पीतमुद्गः
पीतमुद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A sort of bean, a yellow variety of the Phaseo lus Mūṅg.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and मुद्ग Mūṅg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतयूथी
पीतयूथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतरक्त|पीतरक्तं
पीतरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A yellow coloured gem, perhaps the topaz.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and रक्त coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतराग|पीतरागं|पीतरागः
पीतराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The fibres of the lotus.<BR>2 A yellow colour.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतल|पीतलः
पीतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a yellow colour.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Yellow, the colour.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतलक|पीतलकं
पीतलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>पीतल yellow, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतलोह|पीतलोहं
पीतलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Yellow brass, queen's metal, or a mixed metal, resembling gold.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतवासस्
पीतवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Dressed in yellow.<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतशाल|पीतशालः
पीतशाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and शास्त the Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसार|पीतसारं|पीतसारः
पीतसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 A yellow gem, a topaz.<BR>3 A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A yellow sort of Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसारि
पीतसारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Antimony.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, सार essence, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसालक|पीतसालकः
पीतसालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, सार essence, aff. क, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतसोम
पीतसोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Brāhmaṇa, by whom the juice of the acid asclepias is drank at a ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and सोम the juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतस्कन्ध|पीतस्कंध|पीतस्कन्धः
पीतस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>पीत for पीन large, and स्कन्ध a shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतस्फटिक|पीतस्फटिकः
पीतस्फटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A precious gem, the topaz.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, and स्फटिक crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताब्धि|पीताब्धिः
पीताब्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>The Muni AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>पीत drank, (by whom,) and अब्धि the ocean; the saint having on one occasion swallowed up the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताम्बर|पीतांबर|पीताम्बरः
पीताम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dressed in yellow clothes.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU in that form.<BR>2 A dancer or actor. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">Page539</a>]<BR>3 A religious mendicant, wearing yellow garments.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, अम्बर vesture, raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=538" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीताश्मन्
पीताश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>A topaz or any yellow gem.<BR>E.<BR>पीत, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीति|पीतिः
पीति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A horse.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Drinking.<BR>2 A dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतिका
पीतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Turmerick.<BR>2 Yellow jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>पीत yellow, कन् aff., and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतिन्
पीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, क्तिन् aff., इन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीतु|पीतुः
पीतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 The chief elephant of a herd.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, (or dry up water,) and वुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीत्वा
पीत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having drank.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथ|पीथं|पीथः
पीथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 Time.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, Uṇādi aff. थक्, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीथि|पीथिः
पीथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>A horse: see पीति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीन|पीनः
पीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fat, bulky, corpulent, large.<BR>E.<BR>प्यै to grow or enlarge, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनस|पीनसः
पीनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Cough, catarrh.<BR>2 Cold, affecting the nose, inflammation of the schneiderian membrane.<BR>E.<BR>पीन fat, षो to destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनसिन्
पीनसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Having a cold.<BR>E.<BR>पीनस, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीनोध्नी
पीनोध्नी<BR>f. (-ध्नी)<BR>A cow with full or large udders.<BR>E.<BR>पीन large, उधस् an udder, डीष् aff. and अनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयु|पीयुः
पीयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Time.<BR>3 An owl.<BR>4 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>पीय a Sautra root, to regard, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूष|पीयूषं|पीयूषः
पीयूष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The food of the gods, ambrosia, nectar.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>The milk of a cow during the first seven days after calving.<BR>E.<BR>पीय Sautra root, to be kind or love, ऊषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषमहस्
पीयूषमहस्<BR>m. (-हाः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पीयूष nectar, and महस् light; whose rays are filled with nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीयूषरुचि|पीयूषरुचिः
पीयूषरुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>पीयूष nectar; and रुचि light: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पील
पील<BR>r. 1st cl. (पीलति)<BR>1 To stop, to cease to be or do.<BR>2 To become stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलक|पीलकः
पीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The large black ant.<BR>E.<BR>पील to stop, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलु|पीलुः
पीलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>1 The name of a tree, applied in some places to the Careya arborea, and in others to the Salvadora persica; it is very commonly assigned also to all exotic, and unknown trees.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 A flower.<BR>5 The blossom of the Saccharum sara.<BR>6 An atom.<BR>7 An insect.<BR>8 The metacarpus, the central part of the hand.<BR>9 The stem of the palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>पील to stop, aff. कु; also with कन् added पीलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीलुपर्णी
पीलुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A plant: see पीलु.<BR>2 Bryonia grandis.<BR>3 A sort of drug.<BR>E.<BR>पीलु the tree, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीव
पीव<BR>r. 1st cl. (पीवति)<BR>To be fat or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवन्
पीवन्<BR>mfn. (-वा-वा-व)<BR>1 Fat, large.<BR>2 Strong, robust.<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>प्यै to swell or increase, Uṇādi aff. क्वनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवर|पीवरः
पीवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Fat, large.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>(-री)<BR>1 A young woman.<BR>2 A cow.<BR>E.<BR>प्ये to increase, Uṇādi aff. ष्वरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवरस्तनी
पीवरस्तनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A cow with large udders.<BR>2 A woman with large breasts.<BR>E.<BR>पीवर large, and स्तन a breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पीवा
पीवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, वन Uṇādi aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंयोग|पुंयोगः
पुंयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Association or cohabitation with men.<BR>E.<BR>पुम्, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंलिङ्ग|पुंलिङ्गं
पुंलिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The male organ.<BR>2 The masculine gender, (in grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>पुम् male, and लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंवृष|पुंवृषः
पुंवृष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The musk rat.<BR>E.<BR>पुम् male, and वृष a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चली
पुंश्चली<BR>f. (ली)<BR>A harlot, an unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>पुस a man, and चल to go, aff. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंश्चिह्न|पुंश्चिह्नं
पुंश्चिह्न<BR>n. (-ह्नं)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>पुम् male, and चिह्न mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस
पुंस<BR>r. 10th cl. (पुसयति)<BR>To punish, to pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंसवन|पुंसवनं
पुंसवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The first of the essential ceremonies of Hindū initiation; a religious and domestic festival held on the mother's perceiving the first signs of a living conception.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>E.<BR>पुम् a male, षू to bear, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुंस्त्व|पुंस्त्वं
पुंस्त्व<BR>n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 Manhood, virility.<BR>E.<BR>पुम् man, and त्व aff. of the abstract; also with तल् aff., पुंस्ता f. (-स्ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कश|पुक्कशः
पुक्कश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A Caṇḍāla, an outcaste: see पुक्कस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुक्कस|पुक्कसः
पुक्कस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Low, vile.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A Caṇḍāla, or man of an impure and degraded tribe or occupation, born of the Niṣāda by a Śūdra female.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 Indigo.<BR>2 A bud, a blossom.<BR>3 A woman of the Pukkasa tribe.<BR>E.<BR>पु for पुण्य purity, कु bad (understood,) कस to go, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्ख|पुंख|पुंखं|पुंखः|पुङ्खः
पुङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>The feathered part of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>पुम् man, खन to destroy, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्ग|पुंग|पुंगं|पुंगः|पुङ्गः
पुङ्ग<BR>mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं)<BR>A heap, a collection, a quantity.<BR>E.<BR>पुं man, and गम to go, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गल|पुंगल|पुंगलः|पुङ्गलः
पुङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The soul.<BR>E.<BR>पुं man, and गल to pervade, aff. अच्; also read पुद्गल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुङ्गव|पुंगव|पुङ्गवः
पुङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 A drug, commonly Māṣāni.<BR>3 (In composition,) Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>E.<BR>पुं male, and गौ a cow, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छ|पुच्छं|पुच्छः
पुच्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (पुच्छति)<BR>To err, to be careless or inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छ|पुच्छं|पुच्छः
पुच्छ<BR>mn. (-च्छः-च्छं)<BR>1 A tail, the tail, the hinder part.<BR>2 A horse's tail.<BR>3 The tail of the peacock.<BR>4 Any hairy tail.<BR>E.<BR>पुच्छ to be careless, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छटि|पुच्छटिः
पुच्छटि<BR>n. (-टिः)<BR>Snapping or cracking the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुच्छिन्
पुच्छिन्<BR>mfn. (-च्छी-च्छिनी-च्छि)<BR>Having a tail.<BR>m. (-च्छी)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>पुच्छ a tail, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्ज|पुंज|पुंजः|पुञ्जः
पुञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>A heap, a quantity, a collection.<BR>E.<BR>पुं man, जन to be born, aff. ड; also पुङ्ग and पुञ्जि f. (-ञ्जिः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुञ्जिष्ठ|पुञ्जिष्ठः
पुञ्जिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Heaped, accumulated.<BR>E.<BR>पुञ्जि, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट|पुटं|पुटः
पुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (पोटति)<BR>To rub, to press, to grind or pound.<BR>r. 6th cl. (पुटति)<BR>To embrace, to intertwine.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पोटयति)<BR>1 To be or become small, or shallow.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>4 To reduce to powder, to grind.<BR>(पुटयति)<BR>To fasten, to string, to bind together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट|पुटं|पुटः
पुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>1 A cover, a covering.<BR>2 A plate or vessel, made of leaves.<BR>3 A cloth worn to cover the privities.<BR>4 An eyelid.<BR>5 A cup or concavity, made of a leaf folded or doubled.<BR>6 A concavity, a shallow cup or receptacle, as the hollow of the hand.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A horse's hoof.<BR>2 A narrowing or contracting of any thing.<BR>3 A folding or doubling of any thing, so as to form a cup or concavity.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Two vessels [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">Page540</a>] joined together, the upper one inverted for the sublimation or digestion of medicaments.<BR>E.<BR>पुट to rub or bind, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=539" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटक|पुटकं
पुटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A bag or vessel made of a leaf doubled over in a funnel-like shape.<BR>3 Any shallow cup or concavity.<BR>E.<BR>पुट to unite, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटकिनी
पुटकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुटक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटग्रीव|पुटग्रीवः
पुटग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A pot, a jar, a pitcher.<BR>2 A brass jug.<BR>E.<BR>पुट a contracting, from पुट, and ग्रीवा the neck; having a narrow neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटपाक|पुटपाकः
पुटपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Digesting, subliming.<BR>E.<BR>पुट, and पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटभेद|पुटभेदः
पुटभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The bend of a river.<BR>2 A city, a town.<BR>3 A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>पुट a contraction, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटभेदन|पुटभेदनं
पुटभेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटिका
पुटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटित|पुटितं
पुटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sewn, stitched.<BR>2 Rubbed, ground.<BR>3 Contracted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Closing or shutting the hands, to hold any thing, the hollow of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पुट rubbing, &c. and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटोटज
पुटोटज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A white umbrella or parasol.<BR>E.<BR>पुट a covering, and उटज a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुटोरक
पुटोरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>पुट a covering, and उरक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुट्ट
पुट्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (पुट्टयति)<BR>To decrease, to diminish, to be or become small, low or shallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुड
पुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (पुडति)<BR>1 To leave, to quit.<BR>2 To cover.<BR>(इ) पुडि r. 1st cl. (पुण्डति)<BR>To rub, to grind or pound, to reduce to dust or powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण
पुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (पुणति)<BR>To be pure or virtuous, to do a pious or holy act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरिन्
पुण्डरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A drug, commonly Puṇḍarīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीक|पुंडरीक|पुंडरीकं|पुण्डरीकं|पुण्डरीकः
पुण्डरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The elephant of the south-east quarter.<BR>2 A leopard.<BR>3 A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR>4 A fragrant kind of mango.<BR>5 Fever affecting an elephant.<BR>6 A variety of the sugarcane.<BR>7 A silk worm (कोषकार?)<BR>8 A student's waterpot.<BR>9 White, the colour.<BR>10 A sort of leprosy.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A white lotus.<BR>2 A lotus in general.<BR>3 A white umbrella.<BR>4 A kind of drug.<BR>E.<BR>पुडि to rub or grind, or according to some, to adorn, Uṇādi aff. ईक, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीकाक्ष|पुंडरीकाक्ष|पुण्डरीकाक्षं|पुण्डरीकाक्षः
पुण्डरीकाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A drug.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्डरीक a lotus, and अक्षि an eye, aff. षच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डरीयक|पुण्डरीयकं
पुण्डरीयक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>2 A drug, commonly Puṇḍarīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्डर्य्य|पुण्डर्य|पुंडर्यं|पुण्डर्य्यं
पुण्डर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A creeper, a medicinal plant, used as a remedy for diseased eyes.<BR>E.<BR>पुडि to dissipate, (disease,) अर्य्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्र|पुंड्र|पुंड्रः|पुण्ड्रः
पुण्ड्र<BR>n. (-ण्ड्रं)<BR>1 A red variety of the common sugarcane, (Saccharum officinarum.)<BR>2 The name of a Daitya or infernal being, considered as incarnate in ŚIŚUPĀLA.<BR>3 A mark or line made on the forehead with Sandal, &c.<BR>4 A sort of creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>5 A worm.<BR>6 A white lotus.<BR>7 The name of a country, the greater part of Bengal and part of Behar.<BR>m. plu. (-ण्ड्राः)<BR>The inhabitants of that country.<BR>E.<BR>पुडि to rub, aff. रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रक|पुंड्रक|पुंड्रकः|पुण्ड्रकः
पुण्ड्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>2 A sort of sugarcane: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ड्रकेलि|पुंड्रकेलि|पुण्ड्रकेलिः
पुण्ड्रकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्ड्र sugarcane, and केलि pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्य|पुण्यं
पुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>1 Virtuous, pure, righteous.<BR>2 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>3 Fragrant.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Virtue, moral or religious merit.<BR>2 A good action.<BR>3 Purity, purification.<BR>4 A trough for watering cattle.<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>E.<BR>पूञ् to be or make pure, यत् Uṇādi aff., and ण्वुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यक|पुण्यकं|पुण्यकः
पुण्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A meritorious act or obligation of a religious nature, as fasting, praying, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकर्म्मन्|पुण्यकर्मन्
पुण्यकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Pious, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकव्रत|पुण्यकव्रतं
पुण्यकव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The worship of KṚṢṆA for a year, with daily presents, to be performed by a woman desirous of a son.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्यक, and व्रत religious obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यकृत्
पुण्यकृत्<BR>mf. (-कृत्)<BR>Virtuous, pious.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, and कृत् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यगन्ध|पुण्यगंध|पुण्यगन्धः
पुण्यगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The Champak, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य pure, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजन|पुण्यजनः
पुण्यजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A fiend, a goblin, a Rākṣasa.<BR>2 A Yakṣa, a divine being attendant on KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>3 A pious or virtuous man.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtuous, and जन man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यजनेश्वर|पुण्यजनेश्वरः
पुण्यजनेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KUVERA, the Hindu deity of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्यजन a Yakṣa, and ईश्वर master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यतीर्थ
पुण्यतीर्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>A holy shrine or place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and तीर्थ sacred pool, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यतृण|पुण्यतृणं
पुण्यतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>White Kusa grass.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and तृण grass: it is much used in religious ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यदर्शन|पुण्यदर्शनः
पुण्यदर्शन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य lucky, and दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यफल|पुण्यफलः
पुण्यफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A grove, a garden.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The reward or consequence of good actions.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य handsome or virtue, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभाज्
पुण्यभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Virtuous, addicted to virtue.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभू
पुण्यभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>The holy land of the Hindūs; the central part of Asia, bounded on the north by the Himāla, on the south by the Vindhya mountains, and on the east and west by the sea.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, and भू land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यभूमि|पुण्यभूमिः
पुण्यभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 The holy land: see the last.<BR>2 The mother of a male child.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यरात्र|पुण्यरात्रः
पुण्यरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A night on which any religious commemoration or ceremony is held.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and रात्रि night, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यलोक|पुण्यलोकः
पुण्यलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Heaven, paradise.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यवत्|पुण्यवन्त्
पुण्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Fortunate, well-fated.<BR>2 Virtuous, pious, righteous.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, &c. aff. मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यविजित
पुण्यविजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Merited, acquired by merit.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and विजित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यशील
पुण्यशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यश्लोक|पुण्यश्लोकः
पुण्यश्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A name of NALA.<BR>2 The epithet is also applied to YUDHIṢṬHIRA, and to VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A name of DRAUPADĪ.<BR>2 Of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य holy, श्वोक verse: who is celebrated in sacred poems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=540" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्ययोग|पुण्ययोगः
पुण्ययोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The influence or effect of virtuous actions.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यस्थान
पुण्यस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sacred place, holy ground.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य virtue, and स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्यात्मन्
पुण्यात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Holy, pious.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याह|पुण्याहं
पुण्याह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A holy day.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य holy, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्याहवाचन|पुण्याहवाचनं
पुण्याहवाचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Repeating at sacrifices, &c. ‘This is a holy day,’ three times.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्याह, and वाचन saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुण्योदय|पुण्योदयः
पुण्योदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Good fortune, as the result of virtuous acts in a former life.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्य, and उदय rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्
पुत्<BR>n. (पुत्)<BR>A hell to which the childless are condemned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्तिका
पुत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small bee.<BR>E.<BR>पुत to go, तिका Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्र
पुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A child, in the language of the Vedas.<BR>3 The fifth mansion from the point of conjunction of the sun, and a zodiacal sign.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>A daughter.<BR>du. always, (त्त्रौ)<BR>Son and daughter.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्, and त्रा to preserve, the hell, (from,) aff. क; or पूञ् to purify, aff. त्त्र; one त may be rejected in writing this word, and its derivatives, leaving पुत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रक
पुत्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A son, as it were, used as a term of endearment.<BR>3 A fabulous animal: see शरभ.<BR>4 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>5 A particular mountain.<BR>6 A sort of tree.<BR>7 A grasshopper.<BR>f. (-त्रका or त्रिका)<BR>A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्र a son, कन् pleonasm; in the feminine form the substitution of इ for the penultimate vowel is optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रकाम्या
पुत्त्रकाम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>Wish or affection for progeny.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and काम्यच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रजीव
पुत्त्रजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A tree, from the fruit of which necklaces are made of supposed prolific efficacy, (Nagelia putranjiva, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र a child, and जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रञ्जीवक
पुत्त्रञ्जीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र a child, and जीव to live, aff. खश् and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रद
पुत्त्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what confers offspring.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रपौत्रीण
पुत्त्रपौत्रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Descended from son to son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and पौत्र a grandson, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रपौत्रीणता
पुत्त्रपौत्रीणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Perpetual descent from son to son, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रपौत्रीण, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रप्रतिनिधि
पुत्त्रप्रतिनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A substitute for a son, as an adopted-son, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and प्रतिनिधि a substitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रवत्
पुत्त्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a son or offspring.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रवल
पुत्त्रवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having a son or child.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रश्रेणी
पुत्त्रश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रसू
पुत्त्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of a son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र a son, and सू a parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्राचार्य्य
पुत्त्राचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A father instructed in sacred science by his son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and आचार्य्य a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रान्नाद
पुत्त्रान्नाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>One who is maintained by his son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र a son, अन्न food, and आद who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिका
पुत्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>2 A doll, a puppet.<BR>3 The cotton or pappus of the tamarisk.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्री a daughter, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र
पुत्त्रिकापुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 The son of a daughter, appointed to raise issue for her father; one of the twelve heirs acknowledged by the old Hindu law.<BR>2 A grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रिका a daughter, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ
पुत्त्रिकाभर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A daughter's husband.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रिका, and भर्त्तृ husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू
पुत्त्रिकाप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of a daughter.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रिका, and प्रसू a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिकासुत
पुत्त्रिकासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A daughter's son, a grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रिका, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रिन्
पुत्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्त्री)<BR>The father of a son.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The mother of a son, or of children generally.<BR>2 A parasite plant.<BR>3 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र a son or offspring, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीय
पुत्त्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a son, or child.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and छ aff.; also पुत्त्र्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रीयत्
पुत्त्रीयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Wishing for a son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and क्यच् aff. or nominal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेप्सु
पुत्त्रेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desiring a son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and ईप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रेष्टि
पुत्त्रेष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A sacrifice performed for the purpose of obtaining children.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र offspring, and इष्टि sacrifice; also with कन् added in the feminine form, पुत्त्रेष्टिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य
पुत्त्रैश्वर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Resignation of property or power by a father to his son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and ऐश्वर्य्य masterhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुत्त्र्य
पुत्त्र्य<BR>mfn. (-त्त्र्यः-त्त्र्या-त्त्र्यं)<BR>Belonging to a son, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुथ
पुथ<BR>r. 4th cl. (पुथ्यति)<BR>To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पोथयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>(इ) पुथि r. 1st cl. (पुंथति)<BR>1 To hurt.<BR>2 To suffer pain or uneasiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुद्गल|पुद्गलः
पुद्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome, of a handsome form or figure.<BR>2 Having form or property.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 The soul.<BR>E.<BR>पूर what fills, and गल what decays, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपाक
पुनःपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Repeated boiling or cooking.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and पाक dressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुनर्
पुनःपुनर्<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly, again and again.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःपुना
पुनःपुना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The Pumpun river in Behar.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, repeated, irr.; perhaps from the meandering course of the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनःसंस्कार|पुनःसंस्कारः
पुनःसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Repetition of any essential ceremony, as reinvestiture with the sacrificial string of a Brahman, who has forfeited it by unknowingly drinking spirits, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, संस्कार ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्
पुनर्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Again.<BR>2 But, on the contrary.<BR>3 Assuredly, certainly.<BR>4 A particle indicating division or change of subject.<BR>E.<BR>पण to praise, अर् aff., and the radical vowel changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागत
पुनरागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Come back, returned.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरागमन|पुनरागमनं
पुनरागमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Returning, coming back.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and आगमन coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनराधान
पुनराधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Renewing or replacing a consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and आधान placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्त्त|पुनरावर्त|पुनरावर्तः
पुनरावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Return, revolution.<BR>2 Repeated birth.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरावर्त्तिन्|पुनरावर्तिन्
पुनरावर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>1 Returning.<BR>2 Subject to successive births.<BR>E.<BR>पुनरावर्त्त, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=541" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्त|पुनरुक्तं
पुनरुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Repeated, said over again.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Tautology, repetition.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्तजन्मन्
पुनरुक्तजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, उक्त said, and जन्मन् birth; whose investiture is called a second birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनरुक्ति|पुनरुक्तिः
पुनरुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Repetition, tautology.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मन्
पुनर्जन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Re-born, born again.<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Regeneration.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and जन्म birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्जन्मजय
पुनर्जन्मजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Liberation, final emancipation, freedom from transmigration.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्जन्म, and जय victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्नव|पुनर्नवः
पुनर्नव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Hog weed, (Boerhavia diffusa alata.)<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, and नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भव|पुनर्भवः
पुनर्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Re-born, born again.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Regeneration.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भविन्
पुनर्भविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>The sentient soul.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, भव being, and इनि possessive aff.; existing again after the dissolution of one body in another form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्भू
पुनर्भू<BR>mfn. (-र्भूः-र्भूः-र्भू)<BR>Re-born, regenerated.<BR>f. (-र्भूः)<BR>1 A virgin widow re-married.<BR>2 Re-existence.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, (a wife, &c.) भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वचन
पुनर्वचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Repeated text or injunction.<BR>2 Saying any thing again.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, and वचन speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसु|पुनर्वसुः|पुनर्व्वसुः
पुनर्वसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>The seventh of the lunar asterisms, containing according to some authorities two, and to others, four stars; (in this sense it is properly confined to the dual number पुनर्व्वसू, though in the Vedas it is used in the singular.)<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 The name of a saint, and grammarian; also KĀTYĀYANA.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>5 Commencement of wealth.<BR>6 A Loka or division of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, वस to dwell, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुनर्वसू|पुनर्व्वसू
पुनर्वसू<BR>m. du. (-सूः)<BR>An asterism: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नक्षत्र|पुंनक्षत्र
पुन्नक्षत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An asterism under which males are procreated.<BR>E.<BR>पु for पुमस्, and नक्षत्र asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुन्नाग|पुंनाग|पुन्नागः
पुन्नाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A tree, from the flowers of which a yellowish dye is prepared, (Rottleria tinctoria).<BR>2 A white lotus.<BR>3 Nutmeg.<BR>4 A chief, a head or pre-eminent man.<BR>5 A white elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पुं male, नाग an elephant, or aff. of eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुपूषत्
पुपूषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Wishing to cleanse or purify.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुपूषा
पुपूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Wish to cleanse or purify.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, desid. v., affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुल|पुप्फुलः
पुप्फुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Flatulence, wind in the bowels.<BR>E.<BR>फुल to blow, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुप्फुस|पुप्फुसः
पुप्फुस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The lungs.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to swell, deriv. irr. it is also written फुप्फुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुमनुज
पुमनुज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born after, like, or according to a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुं, and अनुज born after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुमस्
पुमस्<BR>m. (पुमान्)<BR>A man or male.<BR>E.<BR>पा to preserve, (his own duties,) Uṇādi aff. डुम and सुम् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुम्वत्
पुम्वत्<BR>ind.<BR>Manlily, like a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुं, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्
पुर्<BR>f. (-पूः)<BR>A city.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to lead, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःसर|पुरःसरः
पुरःसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>One who goes first or before.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A leader, a preceder.<BR>adv. n. (-रं)<BR>By or with, i. e. preceded by, attended with, as कोपपुरःसर with rage.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् before, सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरःस्फुरत्
पुरःस्फुरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Opening or becoming manifest^1; before one.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, and स्फुरत् budding.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (पुरति)<BR>To precede, to lead, to go before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर|पुरं|पुरः
पुर<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>A town, a city: a place containing large buildings surrounded by a ditch, and extending not less than one Kos in length, is called a city, a Pura or Nagara; if it extends not less than half a Kos, it is called a Kheṭa or town; if less than that, a Karvaṭa, or small market town; and any cluster of houses less than that, is a Grāma or village.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 Pātaliputra or Patna.<BR>3 The body.<BR>4 The calyx of a flower, or any receptacle or cup formed of leaves.<BR>5 Skin.<BR>6 An upper story.<BR>7 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of resin, bdellium.<BR>2 Yellow barleria.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The east.<BR>2 A perfume.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to precede, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरज्योतिस्
पुरज्योतिस्<BR>n. (-तिः)<BR>The region or world of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>पुर primary, from पुर to precede, with क aff., and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जन|पुरंजन|पुरंजनः|पुरञ्जनः
पुरञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Life, the living principle.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Understanding.<BR>E.<BR>पुर the body, and जन what produces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जय|पुरंजय|पुरञ्जयः
पुरञ्जय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Victorious, conquering cities.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The proper name of a king, the third of the race of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, जी to conquer, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरञ्जर|पुरंजरः
पुरञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The armpit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरट|पुरटं
पुरट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरण|पुरणः
पुरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill, क्यु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतटी
पुरतटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A market, a village or small fair.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, तट a bank, and ङीप् diminutive or depreciative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरतस्
पुरतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Before, in front.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to precede, aff. अतसुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरदेवता
पुरदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The tutelary deity of a town.<BR>E.<BR>पुर, and देवता deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्वार|पुरद्वारं
पुरद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A city gate.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, and द्वार a gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरद्विष्
पुरद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a name of Tripura, the demon, and द्विष् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्द|पुरंद
पुरन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, दो to destroy, ड aff. with the power of ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्दर|पुरंदर|पुरन्दरं|पुरंदरः|पुरन्दरः
पुरन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A thief, a house-breaker.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of pepper, (Piper chavya.)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A name of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, दॄ to tear or rend, aff. खक्ष्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरन्ध्रि|पुरंध्रि|पुरंध्रिः|पुरन्ध्रिः
पुरन्ध्रि<BR>f. (-न्ध्रिः-न्ध्री)<BR>A woman, whose husband and children are living.<BR>E.<BR>पुर the body, घृ to uphold, aff. खच्, fem. aff. ङीप्, or the final is optionally short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरवासिन्
पुरवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Inhabiting a city or town.<BR>E.<BR>पुद, and वासिन् inhabitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरश्छद|पुरश्छदः
पुरश्छद<BR>(-दः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR>m. du. (-दौ)<BR>The nipples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्
पुरस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Eastward.<BR>2 In front, before.<BR>3 Prior, first.<BR>4 Formerly.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to precede, aff. असुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करण|पुरस्करणं
पुरस्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making perfect, &c.: see पुरस्कार.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस, and करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्करणीय
पुरस्करणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be respected, &c.: see पुरस्कर्त्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कर्त्तव्य|पुरस्कर्तव्य
पुरस्कर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be made complete or perfect.<BR>2 To be prepared, to be fitted out.<BR>3 To be set before.<BR>4 To be treated with deference or respect.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, कृ to make, तव्य aff.; also पुरस्करणीय and पुरस्काय्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=542" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कार|पुरस्कारः
पुरस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Making perfect or complete, finishing, polishing.<BR>2 Preparing, getting ready.<BR>3 Arranging, putting in array.<BR>4 Placing before.<BR>5 Honouring, respecting.<BR>6 Worshipping.<BR>7 Sprinkling with holy water.<BR>8 Promise.<BR>9 Accusation.<BR>10 Attacking, assailing.<BR>11 Anticipating, expecting.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कार्य्य|पुरस्कार्य
पुरस्कार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be prepared, to be fitted out, &c.: see पुरस्कर्त्तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्क्रिया
पुरस्क्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Making perfect, &c.: see पुरस्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्कृत|पुरस्कृतः
पुरस्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made perfect, finished, polished.<BR>2 Prepared.<BR>3 Placed in front.<BR>4 Revered, adored, worshipped.<BR>5 Honoured, respected.<BR>6 Sprinkled with holy water, initiated, anointed.<BR>7 Promised, agreed.<BR>8 Accused, calumniated.<BR>9 Facing, and contending with an enemy.<BR>10 Distrest or harassed by an enemy.<BR>11 Anticipated.<BR>E.<BR>पुर before, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरस्नात्
पुरस्नात्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Eastward.<BR>2 In front, before.<BR>3 Prior, first, preceding.<BR>4 Formerly.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to go before, अस्ताति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरा
पुरा<BR>ind.<BR>1 An ancient story.<BR>2 Old.<BR>3 Past.<BR>4 Long past.<BR>5 Near.<BR>6 Future.<BR>7 Proximate future.<BR>E.<BR>पुर to precede, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराकृत|पुराकृतं
पुराकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Done formerly or of old, done long ago.<BR>2 Done or observed precedingly.<BR>3 Begun, commenced.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराण|पुराणं|पुराणः
पुराण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A Purāṇa or sacred and poetical work, supposed to be compiled or composed by the poet VYĀSA; and comprising the whole body of Hindu theology: each Purāṇa should treat of five topics especially; the creation, the destruction, and renovation of worlds; the genealogy of gods and heroes; the reigns of the Menus, and the transactions of their descendants: but great variety prevails in this respect, and few contain historical or genealogical matter. There are eighteen acknowledged Purāṇas.<BR>1 BRĀHMA.<BR>2 Pādma, or the lotus.<BR>3 Brahmāṇḍa, or the egg of BRAHMA.<BR>4 Āgneya, or Agni fire.<BR>5 VAIṢṆAVA, or of VIṢṆU.<BR>6 Garuḍa.<BR>7 Brahmavaivarta, or transformations of BRAHMA, that is of KṚṢṆA, identified with the Supreme.<BR>8 ŚAIVA, or of ŚIVA.<BR>9 Liṅga.<BR>10 NĀRADĪYA.<BR>11 SKANDA.<BR>12 MĀRKAṆḌEYA, so called from a Muni of that name.<BR>13 Bhaviṣyat, or prophetic.<BR>14 Mātsya, or the fish.<BR>15 Vārāha, or boar.<BR>16 Kaurma, or of the Kūrma or tortoise.<BR>17 Vāmana, or dwarf, and<BR>18 The Bhāgavata, or life of KṚṢṆA, which last is by some considered as a spurious and modern work: the Brahmavaivarta is also of very modern origin. The Purāṇas are reckoned to contain four hundred thousand stanzas: there are also eighteen Upapurāṇas or similar poems of inferior sanctity, and different appellations; the whole constitute the popular or poetical creed of the Hindus, and some of them or particular parts of them, are very generally read, and studied.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A karṣa or measure of silver equal to sixteen Paṇas of Cowries.<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं)<BR>Old, ancient.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा old, and द्यु aff. or पुरा the same, णी to get or be, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणग|पुराणगः
पुराणग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A reader or reciter of the Purāṇas.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पुराण a sacred poem, and ग who goes or pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराणपुरुष|पुराणपुरुषः
पुराणपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पुराण old or primeval, and पुरुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातन|पुरातनः
पुरातन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Old, ancient.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा old, द्यु aff., and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरातल
पुरातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The part below the seven worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराध्यक्ष|पुराध्यक्षः
पुराध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The governor or mayor of a city.<BR>E.<BR>पुर, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरारि|पुरारिः
पुरारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुर the demon Pura, or more properly Tripura, and अरि foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरार्द्धविस्तर|पुरार्द्धविस्तरः
पुरार्द्धविस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Part of a town, a suburb, a ward, a division.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, अर्द्ध part, विस्तर extending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावसु|पुरावसुः
पुरावसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>A name of BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा in former life, वसु a VASU or demigod, so called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुराविद्
पुराविद्<BR>mfn. (-विट्)<BR>Knowing or acquainted with the past.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्त|पुरावृत्तं
पुरावृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>1 History, traditionary or heroic.<BR>2 Any old or legendary event.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा old, (time, or story,) and आवृत्त happened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरावृत्तकथा
पुरावृत्तकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>An old story.<BR>E.<BR>पुरावृत्त, and कथा tale; also पुरावृत्ताख्यान, and similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरासुहृत्
पुरासुहृत्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुर the demon, and असुहृत् a friend, with the negative prefix: see पुरारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरि|पुरिः
पुरि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 A town, a city.<BR>2 A river.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to fill or to cherish, इ Uṇādi aff.: see पुर, and पुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीतत्
पुरीतत्<BR>mn. (-तत्)<BR>An entrail, a gut.<BR>E.<BR>पुरि or पुरि for पुर body, and तन to spread, to stretch, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीमोह|पुरीमोहः
पुरीमोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The thorn apple, (Datura): see घुस्तूर.<BR>E.<BR>पुरी a town, and मोह intoxicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीष|पुरीषं
पुरीष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Fæces, excrement, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to nourish or fill, (the body,) aff. ईषन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषण|पुरीषणः
पुरीषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Fæces: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषम|पुरीषमः
पुरीषम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The black kidney bean, (Phaseolus mas or P. radiatus).<BR>E.<BR>पुरीष fæces, मा to mete or measure, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरीषोत्सर्ग|पुरीषोत्सर्गः
पुरीषोत्सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Voiding excrement.<BR>E.<BR>पुरीष, and उत्सर्ग abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरु|पुरुः
पुरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Much, many, exceeding.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The name of a king, the sixth monarch of the lunar line.<BR>2 Heaven, or the world and residence of immortals.<BR>3 The farina of a flower.<BR>4 The name of a Daityas.<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>The name of a river, said to run a little to the north-west of the Sarsūti.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to cherish or fill, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुद
पुरुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु much, दा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंशक|पुरुदंशकः
पुरुदंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु much, दंशक who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुदंशस्
पुरुदंशस्<BR>m. (-शाः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु much, दशि to destroy, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुरवस्
पुरुरवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>KUVERA: see पुरूरवस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुष|पुरुषः
पुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A man, generally or individually, a male, mankind.<BR>2 The soul.<BR>3 God, the Supreme Being.<BR>4 VIṢṆU.<BR>5 BRAHMĀ.<BR>6 Life, the living principle.<BR>7 An atom.<BR>8 A follower of the Sāṃkhya philosophy.<BR>9 A friend.<BR>10 A tree: see पुन्नाग.<BR>11 A sort of tree, commonly Tila or Tilaka.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The mountain Meru.<BR>E.<BR>पुर the body, षम to abide, aff. क, and the vowel changed; or पुर to precede, Uṇādi aff. कुषन्; also पुरूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=543" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषक|पुरुषकं|पुरुषकः
पुरुषक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rearing as a horse, standing like a man on two feet.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषकार|पुरुषकारः
पुरुषकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Manly act, virility.<BR>2 Effort, exertion.<BR>3 Any act of man, manhood.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and कार a doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषता
पुरुषता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Manhood, manliness.<BR>2 Valour.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पुरुष; also पुरुषत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषत्व|पुरुषत्वं
पुरुषत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Manhood, virility, manly nature or property.<BR>2 Valour, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषत्रा
पुरुषत्रा<BR>ind.<BR>With or amongst men or mankind, worldly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष mankind, and त्रा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषदन्तिका
पुरुषदन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal root; see मेदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषदध्न
पुरुषदध्न<BR>mfn. (-ध्नः-ध्नी-ध्नं)<BR>Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, दध्नच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्धयस
पुरुषद्धयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and द्धयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषद्वेषिन्
पुरुषद्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Manhating, misanthropic.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>An ill tempered, or fractious woman.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and द्वेषिन् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपशु|पुरुषपशुः
पुरुषपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A man, a human animal.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and पशु beast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुङ्गव|पुरुषपुंगव|पुरुषपुङ्गवः
पुरुषपुङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An eminent, or excellent man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and पुङ्गव a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषपुण्डरीक|पुरुषपुंडरीक|पुरुषपुण्डरीकः
पुरुषपुण्डरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An excellent or superior man.<BR>2 The seventh of the nine persons called Vāsudevas or Kṛṣṇas by the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुव mankind, and पुण्डरीक a lotus, or here used to signify pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषमात्र|पुरुषमात्रः
पुरुषमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Of the height, or measure of a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and माचच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषर्षभ|पुरुषर्षभः
पुरुषर्षभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>An excellent man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषवर्जित
पुरुषवर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Desolate, destitute of human beings.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and वर्जित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषव्याघ्र|पुरुषव्याघ्रः
पुरुषव्याघ्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>1 A vulture.<BR>2 An eminent, or distinguished man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and व्याघ्र a tiger; also implying preeminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषशार्द्दूल|पुरुषशार्दूल|पुरुषशार्दूलः
पुरुषशार्द्दूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An eminent man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and शार्द्दूल a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसमवाय|पुरुषसमवायः
पुरुषसमवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A number of men.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and समवाय assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषसिंह|पुरुषसिंहः
पुरुषसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An eminent man.<BR>2 The fifth of the Vāsudevas, according to the Jainas, and the son of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष mankind, and सिंह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाद्य|पुरुषाद्यः
पुरुषाद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>1 A name of the first Jaina pontiff of the present age, ṚṢABHA.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष mankind, and आद्य first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाधम|पुरुषाधमः
पुरुषाधम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A low man, an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and अधम low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाधिकार|पुरुषाधिकारः
पुरुषाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Manly office or duty.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and अधिकार duty<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषार्थ|पुरुषार्थः
पुरुषार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A human object: as the gratification of desire, acquirement of wealth, discharge of duty, and final emancipation.<BR>n. adv. (-र्थ)<BR>For or on account of man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषायुस्
पुरुषायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Life of man, human existence.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषाशिन्
पुरुषाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a cannibal.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषास्थिमालिन्
पुरुषास्थिमालिन्<BR>n. (-ली)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, अस्थि a bone, माला a necklace, and इनि poss. aff.; wearing a necklace of human skulls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोक्ति
पुरुषोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>The name or title of a man.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोक्तिक
पुरुषोक्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Destitute, having no friends.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुषोक्ति, and कन् aff. having only the name of man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुषोत्तम|पुरुषोत्तमः
पुरुषोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An excellent or superior man.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A Jina, one of the generic terms for a deified chief of the Jaina sect.<BR>4 The fourth of the nine Vāsudevas of the Jainas, the son of SOMA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष mankind, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुह|पुरुहं
पुरुह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु many, हन् to destroy or surpass, aff. ड; also पुरुहृ with डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहु
पुरुहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरुहूत|पुरुहूतः
पुरुहूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु much, हूत worshipped or invoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरूरवस्
पुरूरवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>1 The son of BUDDHA, and second king of the lunar dynasty.<BR>2 A demigod, of the class of Viśvadevas.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु much, रु to sound, Uṇādi aff. असि, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोग|पुरोगः
पुरोग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Going before, preceding.<BR>2 Chief, principal, pre-eminent.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् before, and गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगत
पुरोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Preceded, gone before.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगति|पुरोगतिः
पुरोगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Preceding, going before.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Precedence, going before.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् in front, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगम|पुरोगमः
पुरोगम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Going before, preceding.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् before, and गम who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगमन
पुरोगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going before, preceding.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोगामिन्
पुरोगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going in front or before, preceding.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोटि|पुरोटिः
पुरोटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>The current of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश|पुरोडाशः
पुरोडाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Ghee or clarified butter as offered in oblations to fire, with cakes of ground barley meal, that have been well steeped in it.<BR>2 The orts, or leavings of any substance, used in an oblation to fire.<BR>3 A sort of flat ladle or spoon, used for placing the cakes in the sacrificial fire.<BR>4 The juice of the acid asclepias as drank at certain sacrifices.<BR>5 A Mantra, or prayer recited in offering oblations to fire.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् first, दिश to shew, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.; the first ceremony on all sacred occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाशीय
पुरोडाशीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit to be offered in oblations.<BR>E.<BR>पुरोडाश, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोडाश्य|पुरोडाश्यं
पुरोडाश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Fit or proper for offering with Ghee in oblation to fire.<BR>E.<BR>पुरोडाश as above, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोद्भव
पुरोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Of former or prior origin.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A drug; also called Mahāmeda.<BR>E.<BR>पुरम् formerly, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोधस्
पुरोधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>The family or domestic priest.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् before, धा to have, असि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोपनीत
पुरोपनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Formerly had or possessed.<BR>E.<BR>पुरा, and उपनीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=544" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोभागिन्
पुरोभागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Malevolent, censorious.<BR>2 Taking the first share.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् first, भज to serve, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुरोहित|पुरोहितः
पुरोहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Purohita or family priest, conducting all the ceremonials and sacrifices of a house or family.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस्, first, and हित held, revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुर्व|पुर्व्व
पुर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (पुर्वति)<BR>To fill.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पुर्वयति)<BR>1 To dwell or inhabit.<BR>2 To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल<BR>r. 1st cl. (पोलति) 6th cl. (पुलति) and 10th cl. (पोलयति)<BR>To be great or large, to be lofty or high, to be heaped up or piled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल|पुलः
पुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Vast, great, extensive.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Erection of the hairs of the body, considered as a proof of exquisite delight.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 One of the paces of a horse, the canter or gallop.<BR>2 The soft palate or uvula.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be great, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलक|पुलकं|पुलकः
पुलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Erection of the hairs of the body, considered as occasioned by internal pleasure or satisfaction.<BR>2 An insect of any class, affecting animals whether externally or internally.<BR>3 A sort of stone.<BR>4 Flaw or defect in a gem.<BR>5 A ball of bread and sweetmeats with which elephants are fed.<BR>6 Yellow orpiment.<BR>7 A Gandharba or heavenly quirister.<BR>8 A wine goblet or glass.<BR>9 A sort of mustard.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be great, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकाङ्ग|पुलकांग|पुलकाङ्गः
पुलकाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The noose or cord of VARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकालय|पुलकालयः
पुलकालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकित
पुलकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Having the hairs of the body erect.<BR>2 Joyful.<BR>E.<BR>पुलक, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकिन्
पुलकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Having the down of the body erect.<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A sort of Kadamba, (Nauclea k.)<BR>E.<BR>पुलक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलकोद्गम|पुलकोद्गमः
पुलकोद्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Erection of the hairs of the body.<BR>E.<BR>पुलक the same, उद्गम arising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्ति|पुलस्तिः
पुलस्ति<BR>m. (-स्तिः)<BR>The name of one of the seven Ṛṣis, and son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पुल great, अस to throw or cast down, Uṇādi aff. ति; otherwise with स्त्यै to collect, and क aff. पुलस्त्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलस्त्य|पुलस्त्यः
पुलस्त्य<BR>m. (-स्त्यः)<BR>A Ṛṣi so named: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलह|पुलहः
पुलह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>One of the seven divine sages, the sons of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पुल great, हा to abandon, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाक|पुलाकं|पुलाकः
पुलाक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 Shrivelled or blighted grain.<BR>2 Rice water, (according to some medical authorities.)<BR>3 A lump of boiled rice.<BR>4 Brevity, compendium, abbreviation.<BR>5 Smallness, a little.<BR>6 Dispatch, celerity.<BR>E.<BR>पुल greatness, अक to be or go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलाकिन्
पुलाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>पुलाक dry grain, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलायित|पुलायितं
पुलायित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A horse's gallop.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be great, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन|पुलिनं|पुलिनः
पुलिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An island of alluvial formation, or one from which the water has recently withdrawn, or a small island or bank left in the middle of a river, upon the falling of the waters.<BR>2 Any island.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be great, इनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिन्द|पुलिंद|पुलिंदः|पुलिन्दः
पुलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A barbarian, a Mleccha, a savage or mountaineer, one who uses an uncultivated and unintelligible dialect.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be large, Uṇādi aff. किन्दच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलिरिक|पुलिरिकः
पुलिरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमजा
पुलोमजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोमन् a saint so called, and जा born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमजित्
पुलोमजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोमन् as below, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमद्विष्
पुलोमद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोम, and द्विष् hostile; and other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमन्
पुलोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The name of a Ṛṣi or saint, the father-in-law of INDRA, and destroyed by that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमभिद्
पुलोमभिद्<BR>m. (-भित्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोम, and भिद to tear or destroy; the god having destroyed his father-in-law to prevent his curse, for the violation of the daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुलोमारि|पुलोमारिः
पुलोमारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The god INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोम the saint PULOMĀ, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुल्ल
पुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Expanded, full blown or spread.<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>A flower.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be large, aff. क्त, form irr.: see फुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष
पुष<BR>r. 1st cl. (पोषति) 4th cl. (पुष्यति) and 9th cl. (पुष्णाति)<BR>To cherish or nurture, to rear, to bring up.<BR>(इर) पुषिर r. 4th cl. (पुष्यति)<BR>To share or divide.<BR>r. 10th. cl. (पोषयति)<BR>To put on, to wear.<BR>With परि or सम्,<BR>to cherish much, or bring up with care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषा
पुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Cherishing.<BR>2 A plant: see लाङ्गलिकी.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to cherish, aff. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुषित|पुषितं
पुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Nourished, nurtured.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. क्त; also without the augment पुष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कर|पुष्करं|पुष्करः
पुष्कर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum or Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>4 The tip of an elephant's trunk.<BR>5 The head of a drum, or place where any musical instrument is struck.<BR>6 A drug, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>7 The name of a celebrated place of pilgrimage, now called Pokur, in the province of Ajmere, about four miles from the city of Ajmere, consisting of a small town on the bank of a lake, whence its name.<BR>8 The blade of a sword.<BR>9 The sheath of a sword.<BR>10 One of the seven great Dvīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR>11 An arrow.<BR>12 The art or science of dancing.<BR>13 War, battle.<BR>14 Intoxication.<BR>15 A cage.<BR>16 A part.<BR>17 Union.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A pond or lake.<BR>2 A disease.<BR>3 The Indian crane.<BR>4 A sort of snake.<BR>5 The name of a king, the brother of NALA.<BR>6 The son of VARUṆA.<BR>7 The name of a mountain, that in Puṣkara Dvīpa.<BR>8 A drum.<BR>9 One of the principal clouds, that which occasions dearth.<BR>10 An inauspicious astrological combination of a lucky lunation with an unlucky day, and three-fourths of a lunar mansion.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, Uṇādi aff. करन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करमूलक|पुष्करमूलकं
पुष्करमूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The root of the Costus speciosus.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्कर as above, and मूलक root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करशिफा
पुष्करशिफा<BR>f. (-फा)<BR>The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करस्रज्
पुष्करस्रज्<BR>n. du. (-जौ)<BR>The two sons of AŚVINĪ, and physicians of Svarga or paradise.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्कर a lotus, and स्रज् a necklace or chaplet; wearing such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कराह्व|पुष्कराह्वः
पुष्कराह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्कर a lotus, and आह्वा an appellation; whence also any name of the lotus is applicable to the bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्करिन्
पुष्करिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An elephant.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A square or large pond.<BR>2 A piece of water, a lake.<BR>3 A pool, where the lotus does or may grow.<BR>4 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्कर as above, इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=545" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्कल|पुष्कलं|पुष्कलः
पुष्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Excellent, eminent, chief, best.<BR>2 Much, many.<BR>3 Full, filled, complete.<BR>4 Near, approached.<BR>5 Good, salutary.<BR>6 Possessed of all good things.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The mountain Meru.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The holy place Puṣkara.<BR>2 The son of VARUṆA.<BR>3 A measure of eight Kuñcis or sixty-four handfuls; in some places it means four times a double handful.<BR>4 Alms to the extent of four mouthfuls of food.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, and कलन् Uṇādi aff.; otherwise पुष्कर as above, and ल interchanged with र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्ट|पुष्टं|पुष्टः
पुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Nourished, cherished.<BR>2 Burnt.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to cherish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टाङ्ग
पुष्टाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Fat, fattened.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्ट, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टि|पुष्टिः
पुष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Cherishing, nourishing.<BR>2 Increase, advance, thriving, prosperity.<BR>3 One of the Mātṛkās or divine mothers, nourishment personified.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिका
पुष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An oyster.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्ट, and कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिकान्त|पुष्टिकान्तः
पुष्टिकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्टि prosperity, कान्त friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्टिद|पुष्टिदः
पुष्टिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Increase, thriving.<BR>2 A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पुष्टि, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प<BR>r. 4th. cl. (पुष्पति)<BR>To flower, to blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प|पुष्पं
पुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 A flower in general.<BR>2 The menses.<BR>3 Expansion, expanding.<BR>4 The vehicle or car of KUVERA.<BR>5 A disease of the eyes, specks on the eye, albugo.<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>The capital of KARṆA, or Bhāgalpur.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प to flower, &c. अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पक|पुष्पकं
पुष्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Calx of brass.<BR>2 The chariot of KUVERA.<BR>3 A disease of the eyes, albugo, specks on the eye.<BR>4 A bracelet of diamonds or jewels.<BR>5 A cup or vessel of iron.<BR>6 A small earthen fire-place or furnace.<BR>7 A sort of collyrium.<BR>8 Green vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकरण्डक|पुष्पकरण्डकं
पुष्पकरण्डक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Avanti or Oujein, or the grove in its vicinity considered as sacred to MAHĀDEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and करण्डक a basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकरण्डिनी
पुष्पकरण्डिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Oujein: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकासीश
पुष्पकासीश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>The green sulphate of iron.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and कासीश green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकीट|पुष्पकीटः
पुष्पकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 Any insect affecting flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकेतन|पुष्पकेतनः
पुष्पकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Hindu Cupid.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पकेतु|पुष्पकेतुः
पुष्पकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Calx of brass.<BR>2 The god of love.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and केतु mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पगण्डिका
पुष्पगण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Contrary purpose or effort of a man and woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पगिरि
पुष्पगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A fabulous mountain, the favourite resort of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and गिरि a mountain, the hill of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पघातक|पुष्पघातकः
पुष्पघातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and घातक destroyer; the stem decaying after the plant flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचय|पुष्पचयः
पुष्पचय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A quantity of flowers.<BR>2 Gathering flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and चय gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचाप|पुष्पचापः
पुष्पचाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>KĀMADEVA, the Hindu Cupid.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and चाप a bow; who arms his bow with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पचामर|पुष्पचामरः
पुष्पचामर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A plant, (Artemisia.)<BR>2 A fragrant plant, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and चामर a Chowri, having a large bushy flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पद|पुष्पदः
पुष्पद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what gives flowers.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदन्त|पुष्पदंत|पुष्पदन्तः
पुष्पदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The elephant of the north-west quarter.<BR>2 A chief of the Gandharbas or Vidyādharas, attendant upon ŚIVA.<BR>3 One of the Jinas or Jaina teachers.<BR>4 A Nāga or serpent of the infernal regions.<BR>m. dual. (-न्तौ)<BR>The sun and moon.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पदन्तक|पुष्पदन्तकः
पुष्पदन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chief of the Gandharbas.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पद्रव|पुष्पद्रवः
पुष्पद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The exudation or saccharine matter of flowers.<BR>2 An infusion of flowers, as rose water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and द्रव oozing, distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पध|पुष्पधः
पुष्पध<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>The offspring of an outcaste Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पधन्वन्
पुष्पधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and धनु a bow, अनङ् aff. otherwise पुष्पधनुः see पुष्पचाष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिकर
पुष्पनिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Throwing flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and नि before कॄ to throw, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिक्ष|पुष्पनिक्षः
पुष्पनिक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and निक्ष who kisses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पनिर्यास|पुष्पनिर्यासः
पुष्पनिर्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Nectar of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and निर्य्यास extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पन्धय|पुष्पंधय|पुष्पंधयः|पुष्पन्धयः
पुष्पन्धय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, धे to drink, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपथ|पुष्पपथः
पुष्पपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प the menses, and पथिन् a road अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पपुर|पुष्पपुरं
पुष्पपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Pātaliputra or Palibothra.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पप्रचय|पुष्पप्रचयः
पुष्पप्रचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Gathering fruit or flowers, &c. any way except by the hand.<BR>2 Stealing flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and प्र before चि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पप्रचाय|पुष्पप्रचायः
पुष्पप्रचाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gathering flowers with the hand.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and प्र before चि to collect, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पफल|पुष्पफलः
पुष्पफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Elephant or wood apple.<BR>2 A pumpkin gourd.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पभव|पुष्पभवः
पुष्पभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Nectar of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमञ्जरिका|पुष्पमंजरिका
पुष्पमञ्जरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पमास|पुष्पमासः
पुष्पमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Spring.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and मास a month or season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परक्त|पुष्परक्तः
पुष्परक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Dyed red with vegetable colour, as safflower, &c.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A shrub, (Hibiscus phæniceus.)<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प flower, and रक्त coloured, red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परथ|पुष्परथः
पुष्परथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A car or carriage for travelling or pleasure, or any purpose except war.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परस|पुष्परसः
पुष्परस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The nectar or honey of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परसाह्वय|पुष्परसाह्वयं
पुष्परसाह्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Honey, nectar.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्परस, and आह्वय name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पराग|पुष्परागः
पुष्पराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A topaz.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परेणु|पुष्परेणुः
पुष्परेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>The dust or farina of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्परोचन|पुष्परोचनः
पुष्परोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and रोचन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलाव|पुष्पलावः
पुष्पलाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A flower-seller, a garland-maker.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A female flower-gatherer.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and लाव who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलिक्ष|पुष्पलिक्षः
पुष्पलिक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, लिह to lick, स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पलिह्
पुष्पलिह्<BR>m. (-लिट्)<BR>A large black bee.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and लिह to lick, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=546" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवत्|पुष्पवन्त्
पुष्पवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having flowers, flowery.<BR>m. always dual. (-न्तौ)<BR>The sun and moon.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, or expansion as at rising, &c. and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवन्त
पुष्पवन्त<BR>m. dual. (-न्तौ)<BR>The sun and moon.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, अव to prevent, भच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवर्ष|पुष्पवर्षः
पुष्पवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A rain of flowers, flowers cast from heaven upon a hero or demigod, or on any great occasion.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and वर्ष raining; also पुष्पवर्षण, पुष्पवृष्टि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवाटी
पुष्पवाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A flower garden.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and वाटी a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पवृष्टि|पुष्पवृष्टिः
पुष्पवृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>See पुष्पवर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशकटी
पुष्पशकटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Raining flowers, on any great occasion of rejoicing in earth and heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशर|पुष्पशरः
पुष्पशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and शर an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशरासन|पुष्पशरासनः
पुष्पशरासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and शरासन a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशून्य|पुष्पशून्यः
पुष्पशून्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Not bearing flowers, flowerless.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and शून्य void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशालिन्
पुष्पशालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Flowery.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पश्री
पुष्पश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>Abundance, or beauty of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and श्री wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पसमय|पुष्पसमयः
पुष्पसमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Spring.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and समय a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पसार|पुष्पसारः
पुष्पसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पस्वेद|पुष्पस्वेदः
पुष्पस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and स्वेद sweat, or exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पहासा
पुष्पहासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and हास who smiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पहीन
पुष्पहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flowerless, not flowering.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>2 A woman whose menstruation has ceased, a barren woman.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, &c. and हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाजीव|पुष्पाजीवः
पुष्पाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A flowerman, a maker of garlands.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and आजीव livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाजीविन्
पुष्पाजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A flowerman, a maker of garlands.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, आजीव livelihood, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाञ्जन|पुष्पांजन|पुष्पाञ्जनं
पुष्पाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, and अञ्जन collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाञ्जलि|पुष्पांजलि|पुष्पाञ्जलिः
पुष्पाञ्जलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>Presenting a nosegay or flowers, held in both hands opened, and hollowed.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and अञ्जलि the hands joined, and opened; also similar compounds, as कुसुमाञ्जलि, प्रसूनाञ्जलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पावचय|पुष्पावचयः
पुष्पावचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gathering flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and अवचय collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पावचायिन्
पुष्पावचायिन्<BR>mf. (-यी-यिनी)<BR>A flower-gatherer.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and अवचायिन् who collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पासव|पुष्पासवं
पुष्पासव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Honey.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पास्त्र|पुष्पास्त्रः
पुष्पास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>KANDARPA, the Hindu Cupid.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and अस्त्र a weapon; pointing his darts with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाहर
पुष्पाहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what takes flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and आहर who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिका
पुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The tartar of the teeth.<BR>2 The mucus of the glans penis, or urethra.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, कन् aff. of comparison, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पित|पुष्पितः
पुष्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Flowered, in flower.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिताग्रा
पुष्पिताग्रा<BR>f. (-ग्रा)<BR>A form of metre, a mixed kind and a variety of the Aupacchandasika; the line consisting of four or six short syllables, a pyrrhic or a dactyl, two trochees and a spondee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिन्
पुष्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्पी-ष्पिणी-ष्पि)<BR>Flowering, bearing flowers.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पेषु|पुष्पेषुः
पुष्पेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्य|पुष्यः
पुष्य<BR>mf. (-ष्यः-ष्या)<BR>1 The eighth lunar asterism, comprising three stars, of which one is δ Cancer.<BR>2 The month Paus, (Dec.-Jan.)<BR>3 The Kali, or fourth age.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. क्यप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यरथ|पुष्यरथः
पुष्यरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Any sort of car or carriage, except a war chariot.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्य the asterism, and रथ a car; also पुष्परथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यलक|पुष्यलकः
पुष्यलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The musk deer.<BR>2 A pin, a bolt, a stake.<BR>3 A naked mendicant. It is read in some places पुष्पलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (पुस्तयति)<BR>1 To respect.<BR>2 To disregard, to treat with disrespect.<BR>3 To bind.<BR>4 To smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Filled.<BR>2 Covered.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Smearing, anointing, painting, plastering, &c.<BR>2 Any thing made of metal, wood or clay, &c.<BR>nf. (-स्तं-स्ती)<BR>A book, a manuscript.<BR>E.<BR>पुस्त to bind, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तक|पुस्तकं|पुस्तकः
पुस्तक<BR>nf. (-कं-की)<BR>A book, a manuscript.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकर्म्मन्|पुस्तकर्मन्
पुस्तकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Plaistering, painting, &c. see पुस्त.<BR>E.<BR>पुस्त as above, कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्फुस
पुस्फुस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The lungs; also पुप्फुस and फुप्फुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू<BR>(ङ) पूङ् r. 1st cl. (पवते) (ञ्) पूञ् r. 9th cl. (पुनाति पुनीते)<BR>To purify, to cleanse, physically or metaphorically.<BR>r. 4th cl. (पूयते)<BR>To grow or become pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूग|पूगं|पूगः
पूग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The betelnut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>2 A heap, a quantity, a multitude.<BR>3 Disposition, property, nature.<BR>4 The Jack tree.<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The fruit of the faufel, the betelnut.<BR>E.<BR>पू to cleanse, गन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगकृत
पूगकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Assembled, collected.<BR>E.<BR>पूग, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपात्र|पूगपात्रं
पूगपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A betel-box.<BR>E.<BR>पूग, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपीठ|पूगपीठं|पूगपीठः
पूगपीठ<BR>n. (-ठं)<BR>A spitting pot.<BR>E.<BR>पूग betel, and पीठ a stool; chewing the pān producing an increased excretion of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपुष्पिका
पूगपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Flowers and betel presented to the principal guests at a marriage festival.<BR>E.<BR>पूग, and पुष्प a flower, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगफल|पूगफलं
पूगफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The Areca nut.<BR>E.<BR>पूग, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगरोट|पूगरोटः
पूगरोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The marshy date tree, (Phoenix or Elate paludosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पूग Areca, and रुट् to shine, to resemble, aff. घञ्; also with कन् added पूगरोटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज
पूज<BR>r. 10th cl. (पूजयनि)<BR>To adore, to reverence, to worship.<BR>With सम्,<BR>to pay respect to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजक|पूजकः
पूजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Worshipping, a worshipper.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजत्
पूजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>Worshipping, reverencing.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजन|पूजनं
पूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worship, worshipping: see पूजा.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजनीय
पूजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be worshipped or revered.<BR>E.<BR>पूज and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=547" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितव्य
पूजयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितृ
पूजयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Worshipping, a worshipper.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजा
पूजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Worship, culture, respect, homage of superiors or adoration of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, aff. अङ् and टाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजार्ह|पूजार्हः
पूजार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Worshipful, venerable, respectable, sacred.<BR>E.<BR>पूजा worship, अर्ह fit, deserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजित|पूजितः
पूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Worshipped, adored, reverenced.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजिल|पूजिलः
पूजिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Venerable, respectable, worshipful, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A deity.<BR>E.<BR>पूजा, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्य|पूज्यः
पूज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Worshipful, venerable, fit for or deserving adoration, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A father-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्यमान
पूज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being reverenced or respected.<BR>E.<BR>पूज to worship, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूण
पूण<BR>r. 10th cl. (पूणयति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्कारी
पूत्कारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The capital of the Nāgas.<BR>2 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
पूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pure, purified.<BR>2 Threshed, winnowed.<BR>3 Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>4 Speaking the truth, sincere, honest.<BR>5 Foul smelling, stinking.<BR>6 Guarded, defended.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Truth, speaking truth.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A conch shell.<BR>2 Kusa grass.<BR>m. du. (-तौ)<BR>The buttocks.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतायी
पूतक्रतायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पूतक्रतु INDRA, ङीप् aff.; in place of उ, ऐच् is inserted, and then changed before ई to आय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतु|पूतक्रतुः
पूतक्रतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पूत pure, and क्रतु sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतद्रु|पूतद्रुः
पूतद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>पूत, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतधान्य|पूतधान्यं
पूतधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>पूत, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतना
पूतना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>2 The name of a female demon killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 A disease, atrophy and wasting in a child, ascribed to the malignant operations of the female fiend PŪTANĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पूत to be pure, nominal verb, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनारि|पूतनारिः
पूतनारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पूतना a female fiend, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनासूदन|पूतनासूदनः
पूतनासूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पूतना, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनाहन्
पूतनाहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पूतना, and हन् who kills: see the three words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप
पूतपाप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Purified, freed from sin.<BR>E.<BR>पूत, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप्मन्
पूतपाप्मन्<BR>mfn. (-प्मा-प्मा-प्म)<BR>Purified from sin.<BR>E.<BR>पूत, and पाप्मन् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतफल|पूतफलः
पूतफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The jack tree.<BR>E.<BR>पूत fetid, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतात्मन्
पूतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 A saint, an ascetic, a pure or purified person.<BR>2 A man of a cleanly person, or purified by ablution.<BR>E.<BR>पूत purified, आत्मन् spirit or self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
पूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Purity, purification.<BR>2 A stench, a stink.<BR>3 Civet.<BR>E.<BR>पू to be pure, or पूय to stink, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिक|पूतिकं|पूतिकः
पूतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Grey bonduc, (Cæsalpinia bonducella, Rox.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A potherb, (Basella lucida, &c.)<BR>2 A civet or polecat.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Ordure, excrement.<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stink, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकरज|पूतिकरजः
पूतिकरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>E.<BR>पूतिक the same, रञ्ज to colour, aff. अण्; also with the nasal retained पूतिकरञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकर्णक|पूतिकर्णकः
पूतिकर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fetid ulceration of the ear.<BR>E.<BR>पूति, and कर्ण the ear, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकामुख|पूतिकामुखः
पूतिकामुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>पूतिका a potherb, and मुख face, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकाष्ठ|पूतिकाष्ठं
पूतिकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A sort of pine, (P. devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति purity, काष्ठ wood; also with कन् added पूतिकाष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्ध|पूतिगंध|पूतिगन्धं|पूतिगन्धः
पूतिगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Ill-smelling.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stink, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्धि|पूतिगंधि|पूतिगन्धिः
पूतिगन्धि<BR>mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>Ill-smelling.<BR>E.<BR>पूति stinking, गन्ध smell, and इन् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्धिक|पूतिगन्धिकः
पूतिगन्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ill-smelling, fetid.<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stink, गन्ध smell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतितैला
पूतितैला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum halicacabum.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति stink, तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिपुष्पिका
पूतिपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A variety of the common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति stinking, and पुष्प a flower, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिनस्य|पूतिनस्यः
पूतिनस्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Fetid exhalation from the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>पूति, and नस्य nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिफला
पूतिफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Psoralea corilifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति stinking, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिफली
पूतिफली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति stink, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमांस
पूतिमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Dead or decayed flesh.<BR>E.<BR>पूति, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवात|पूतिवातः
पूतिवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>2 Foul air.<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stink, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवृक्ष|पूतिवृक्षः
पूतिवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति a foul smell, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिशारिजा
पूतिशारिजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The pole or civet-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतीक|पूतीकः
पूतीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>2 The polecat or civet-cat.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stink or purity, कन् added, and the penultimate optionally long; also पूतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतीकरज
पूतीकरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.) Also पूतीक, पूतिक, पूतिकरज, पूतीकरञ्ज, or पूतिकरञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्यण्ड|पूत्यंड|पूत्यण्डः
पूत्यण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The musk deer.<BR>2 An insect with a fetid smell, the winged bug.<BR>E.<BR>पूति a stench, and अण्ड the testicle or any egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पून|पूनः
पून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lost, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. क्र, deriv. irr; also पूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूप|पूपः
पूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A cake.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. पक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपला
पूपला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of sweet cake, fried with Ghee or oil.<BR>E.<BR>पूप cake, ला to get or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपशाला
पूपशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A baker's or confectioner's shop.<BR>E.<BR>पूप, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपाली
पूपाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of cake or biscuit, made of meal or barley, half baked or fried.<BR>E.<BR>पूप cake, आङ् before, ला to be or resemble, aff. क, fem. aff. ङीप्; also with कन् added पूपालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=548" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपिका
पूपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of cake, half baked or fried in oil or Ghee.<BR>E.<BR>पूय a cake, कन् aff. of comparison, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय<BR>(ई) पूयी r. 1st cl. (पूयते)<BR>1 To split or cleave.<BR>2 To stink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Pus, matter, discharge from an ulcer or wound.<BR>E.<BR>पूय to stink, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयन|पूयनं
पूयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pus, discharge from a wound or sore.<BR>E.<BR>पूय to stink, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयरक्त|पूयरक्तः
पूयरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 Ichor, sanies.<BR>2 Discharge of sanies from the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>पूय, and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयशोणित
पूयशोणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Ichor, sanies.<BR>E.<BR>पूय, and शोणित blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयारि|पूयारिः
पूयारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The Nimb tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR>E.<BR>पूय pus, and अरि inimical; the leaves being used to produce discussion, or the absorption of matter that has formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयालस|पूयालसः
पूयालस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Suppuration at the joints, white swelling.<BR>2 Matter in the eye.<BR>E.<BR>पूय, and अलस idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर<BR>r. 4th cl. (ई) पूरी (पूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To satisfy.<BR>2 To fill.<BR>3 To be satisfied.<BR>4 To be full.<BR>r. 10th cl. (पूरयति)<BR>To satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर<BR>mfn. subst. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A sort of unleavened cake, fried with Ghee or oil.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A piece of water, a large quantity of water, a lake.<BR>2 The healing or cleansing of ulcers.<BR>adj. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Full, filled.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to fill, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरक|पूरकः
पूरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Filling, completing, or that which fills or completes.<BR>2 Filling up.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) The multiplier.<BR>3 Closing the right nostril, and drawing up air through the left, a religious ceremonial.<BR>4 The funeral cake or cakes that must be given to complete the obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to fill, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरकृत
पूरकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Filled.<BR>E.<BR>पूर, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरण|पूरणं|पूरणः
पूरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं)<BR>Filling, completing.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Act of filling, completing or making up.<BR>2 The final obsequial ball or cake.<BR>3 Multiplication, (in arithmetic.)<BR>4 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>5 Rain, raining.<BR>nf. (-णं-णी)<BR>The cross threads in weaving a piece of cloth.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A bridge, a causeway.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 A medicinal oil or embrocation.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to fill, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयितृ
पूरयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Filling.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to fill, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयित्वा
पूरयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having filled.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to fill, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिका
पूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of unleavened cake, fried with Ghee or oil.<BR>E.<BR>पूरी as above, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरित|पूरितं
पूरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Filled, full, complete.<BR>2 Multiplied.<BR>3 Overspread.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to be full, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरुष|पूरुषः
पूरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Man, male, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to be full, (the world,) aff. कुषन्; it is also written पुरुष, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण<BR>r. 10th cl. (पूर्णयति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Full, filled, complete.<BR>2 All, entire.<BR>3 Strong, powerful, able.<BR>4 Selfish, self-indulgent.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>1 Fifth, tenth, or fifteenth day of the half month.<BR>2 Full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर to be full, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णक|पूर्णकः
पूर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cock.<BR>f. (-र्णिका)<BR>A sort of bird, described as having a double or cleft beak; also नासाच्छिन्नी.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णकाम|पूर्णकामः
पूर्णकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Satisfied, satiated.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण fulfilled, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णकुम्भ|पूर्णकुंभ|पूर्णकुम्भः
पूर्णकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A water vessel, one filled with holy water, used at the consecration of a king.<BR>2 A full cup or jar.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, and कुम्भ a water jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णपाच
पूर्णपाच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 A full cup or vessel.<BR>2 A vessel filled with clothes or ornaments, which are scrambled for by the guests and relations at a festival.<BR>3 A vessel full of rice, presented at a sacrifice to the superintending and officiating priests; the Pūrṇa Pātra is properly a measure of 256 handfuls of rice; it may also be composed of as much as will satisfy one great eater.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, and पाच a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमा
पूर्णमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, मा the moon; also पूर्णिमा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमास|पूर्णमासः
पूर्णमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A monthly sacrifice, performed on the day of full moon; also पार्णमास.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण complete, मास the month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णवीज|पूर्णवीजः
पूर्णवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The citron.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णानक
पूर्णानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A vessel full of clothes, &c. at a feast: see पूर्णपात्र.<BR>2 The sound of a drum.<BR>3 A moon-beam.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, अन to go, or be, aff. वुन्; also read पूर्णालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णालक|पूर्णालकं
पूर्णालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A vessel of clothes or ornaments to be scrambled for.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, अल to ornament, aff. ण्वुल्; also sometimes written पूर्णानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णिमा
पूर्णिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण full, (the moon,) इमक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णेन्दु|पूर्णेंदु|पूर्णेन्दुः
पूर्णेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>The moon, the full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ण, and इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्त|पूर्त|पूर्त्तं|पूर्त्तः
पूर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Filled, full, complete.<BR>2 Covered, concealed.<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>1 An act of pious liberality, as digging a well, planting a grove, building a temple, &c.<BR>2 Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to cherish or fill, aff. क्त, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्ति|पूर्ति|पूर्तिः|पूर्त्तिः
पूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Fulness, completion.<BR>E.<BR>पॄ to satisfy or fill, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्तिन्|पूर्तिन्
पूर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिणी-र्त्ति)<BR>Filling, completing.<BR>2 Effective.<BR>E.<BR>प to satisfy, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्व|पूर्व|पूर्वः|पूर्व्वः
पूर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (पूर्व्वति)<BR>To fill.<BR>10th cl. (पूर्व्वयति)<BR>1 To dwell.<BR>2 To invite: the root is written either पूर्ब्ब or पूर्व्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्व|पूर्व|पूर्वः|पूर्व्वः
पूर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>1 First, former, prior, preceding, initial.<BR>2 East, eastern.<BR>3 All, entire.<BR>4 Before, in front of.<BR>m. plu. (-र्व्वाः)<BR>Ancestors, forefathers.<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>The east.<BR>n. (-र्व्वं)<BR>An ancient tradition.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्ब्ब or पूर्व्व to fill, to dwell, &c. aff. अच्; hence the derivative, and its compounds may be written either with ब or व; the second of the duplicate consonants may also be rejected, making it पूर्ब or पूर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वक|पूर्वक|पूर्वकः
पूर्व्वक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Prior, before, preceding.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकाल|पूर्वकाल|पूर्वकालः
पूर्व्वकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Former time.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकालीन|पूर्वकालीन
पूर्व्वकालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ancient, belonging to former times.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकाष्ठा|पूर्वकाष्ठा
पूर्व्वकाष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>The east, the eastern quarter.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and काष्ठा quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकृत|पूर्वकृत
पूर्व्वकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done formerly, or in a prior existence.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वगङ्गा|पूर्वगङ्गा|पूर्वगंगा
पूर्व्वगङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The Narmadā river.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व formerly, (called) गङ्गा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वचोदित|पूर्वचोदित
पूर्व्वचोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Formerly stated, before-mentioned, aforesaid.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and चोदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=549" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वज|पूर्वज|पूर्वजः|पूर्व्वजः
पूर्व्वज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Born or produced before either in time or place.<BR>2 Eastern, born in the east.<BR>3 Elder.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 An elder brother.<BR>2 The son of the elder wife, even though last born.<BR>m. plu. (-जाः)<BR>1 The deified progenitors of mankind.<BR>2 Ancestors, forefathers in general.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व formerly or first, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वजिन|पूर्वजिन|पूर्व्वजिनः
पूर्व्वजिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Bauddha teacher; also MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR>m. plu. (-नाः)<BR>The twenty-four Jinas or Jaina saints of a former æra.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and जिन a Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वतन|पूर्वतन
पूर्व्वतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Former.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and द्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदिक्पति|पूर्वदिक्पति|पूर्वदिक्पतिः|पूर्व्वदिक्पतिः
पूर्व्वदिक्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व east, दिश् quarter, and पति regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदिश्|पूर्वदिश्
पूर्व्वदिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्)<BR>The eastern region.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and दिश a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदृष्ट|पूर्वदृष्ट
पूर्व्वदृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Formerly seen.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेव|पूर्वदेव|पूर्वदेवः|पूर्व्वदेवः
पूर्व्वदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 An Asura or demon.<BR>2 A Pitṛ, or progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व before, देव a god; the first being the elder offspring of KAŚYAPA, the parent of both gods and demons, and the second being the progenitor of gods and men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेवता|पूर्वदेवता
पूर्व्वदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A primeval deity, a Pitṛ or progenitor of gods as well as men.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेश|पूर्वदेश|पूर्वदेशः|पूर्व्वदेशः
पूर्व्वदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The eastern country, or eastern part of India.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व eastern, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेह|पूर्वदेह
पूर्व्वदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A former body, a prior existence.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपक्ष|पूर्वपक्ष|पूर्वपक्षः|पूर्व्वपक्षः
पूर्व्वपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A proposition, an assertion; the first part of an argument, to which assent or refutation is necessary.<BR>2 The first half of a lunar month.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, पक्ष argument, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपक्षपाद|पूर्वपक्षपाद|पूर्व्वपक्षपादः
पूर्व्वपक्षपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The first division of legal proceeding, the plaint.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वपक्ष, and पाद quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपद|पूर्वपद|पूर्व्वपदं
पूर्व्वपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The first member of a compounded word, of a sentence, a verse, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व preceding, and पद a word, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपदिक|पूर्वपदिक
पूर्व्वपदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Relating to the first member of a compound term.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वपद, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपर्व्वत|पूर्वपर्वत|पूर्वपर्वतः|पूर्व्वपर्व्वतः
पूर्व्वपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व eastern, and पर्व्वत a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वप्रवृत्त|पूर्वप्रवृत्त
पूर्व्वप्रवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Formerly fixed, or done.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and प्रवृत्त undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वफल्गुनी|पूर्वफल्गुनी
पूर्व्वफल्गुनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The eleventh lunar asterism; the first Phalgunī, the twelfth Nakṣatra, being termed Uttara or subsequent; this asterism figured by a couch contains two stars, one of which is δ Leonis.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, and फल्गुनी the name of the two asterisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वफल्गुनीभव|पूर्वफल्गुनीभव|पूर्व्वफल्गुनीभवः
पूर्व्वफल्गुनीभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The planet Jupiter.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वफल्गुनी as above, and भव being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा|पूर्वभाद्रपदा
पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा<BR>f. (दा)<BR>The first of the two lunar asterisms, called Bhādrapadā, and twenty-sixth, of the whole, containing two stars.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, and भाद्रपदा the asterism so named; it is also read पूर्व्वभद्रपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभाषिन्|पूर्वभाषिन्
पूर्व्वभाषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Polite, complaisant, condescending to speak first.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभुक्ति|पूर्वभुक्ति|पूर्वभुक्तिः
पूर्व्वभुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Prior possession.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and भुक्ति enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वमारिन्|पूर्वमारिन्
पूर्व्वमारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Dying first.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, मृ to die, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वयक्ष|पूर्वयक्ष|पूर्व्वयक्षः
पूर्व्वयक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>One of the Jinas or Jaina teachers.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व formerly, यक्ष a demigod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरङ्ग|पूर्वरङ्ग|पूर्वरंग|पूर्वरङ्गः|पूर्व्वरङ्गः
पूर्व्वरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The commencement of a drama, or the prelude to instrumental or vocal performance; a prologue, an overture.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, रङ्ग a stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वराग|पूर्वराग|पूर्वरागः|पूर्व्वरागः
पूर्व्वराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Affection arising from some cause before the parties meet.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरात्र|पूर्वरात्र|पूर्वरात्रः|पूर्व्वरात्रः
पूर्व्वरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The first part of the night.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व preceding, रात्रि night, and the final changed to अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरूप|पूर्वरूप|पूर्व्वरूपं
पूर्व्वरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Indication of some approaching change.<BR>2 Symptom of occurring disease.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व previous, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वलक्षण|पूर्वलक्षण
पूर्व्वलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Indication of something about to occur, as sickness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and लक्षण sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववत्|पूर्ववत्|पूर्ववन्त्
पूर्व्ववत्<BR>ind.<BR>As before, as aforesaid, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववाद|पूर्ववाद|पूर्ववादः|पूर्व्ववादः
पूर्व्ववाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A former plaint or averment.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व former, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववादिन्|पूर्ववादिन्
पूर्व्ववादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>One who has made a former plea or complaint.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्ववाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वशैल|पूर्वशैल|पूर्वशैलः|पूर्व्वशैलः
पूर्व्वशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व eastern, शैल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसर|पूर्वसर|पूर्व्वसरः
पूर्व्वसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Preceding, going before.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, सृ to go, aff. ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसन्ध्या|पूर्वसन्ध्या
पूर्व्वसन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>Dawn, daybreak.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व prior, and सन्ध्या junction, (of the day.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसार|पूर्वसार|पूर्व्वसारः
पूर्व्वसार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Going eastwards.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व east, and सृ to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसाहस|पूर्वसाहस|पूर्वसाहसः
पूर्व्वसाहस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The first or heaviest fine, or punishment.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाचरित|पूर्वाचरित
पूर्व्वाचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done or followed formerly.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and आचरित observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाद्रि|पूर्वाद्रि|पूर्वाद्रिः|पूर्व्वाद्रिः
पूर्व्वाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The eastern mountain.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व eastern, and अद्रि mountain: see पूर्व्वशैल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वापर|पूर्वापर
पूर्व्वापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>First and last, prior and subsequent.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Proof, and thing to be proved.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and अपर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाभ्यास|पूर्वाभ्यास|पूर्वाभ्यासः
पूर्व्वाभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Former practice, or experience.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and अभ्यास practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वार्द्ध|पूर्वार्ध|पूर्वार्धः
पूर्व्वार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धः)<BR>The first or east half of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वावतर
पूर्व्वावतर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>First accession or attack, (of any passion, disease, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and अवतर befalling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वावेदक|पूर्वावेदक|पूर्वावेदकः
पूर्व्वावेदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plaintiff, one who has made a complaint before another.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and आवेदक who represents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाषाढा|पूर्वाषाढा
पूर्व्वाषाढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>The first of two constellations, each called Āṣārhā, and the 20th of the lunar asterisms, containing two stars of which one is δ Sagitarii.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, आषाढा Āṣārhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाह्न|पूर्वाह्न
पूर्व्वाह्न<BR>m. (-ह्नः)<BR>The first part of the day, the forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाह्नेतन
पूर्व्वाह्नेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वाह्र as above, द्यु aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वेण|पूर्वेण
पूर्व्वेण<BR>ind.<BR>In the east, easterly, eastward.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व the east, and the form of the 3rd case used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वेद्युस्|पूर्वेद्युस्
पूर्व्वेद्युस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A former day, yesterday.<BR>2 The morning, dawn, the first part of the day.<BR>3 A day or portion of a day on which [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">Page551</a>] religious ceremonies are to be performed.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व former or first, and एद्युस् aff. for द्यु a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=550" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोक्त|पूर्वोक्त
पूर्व्वोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Said formerly, before-mentioned, aforesaid.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोत्तर|पूर्वोत्तर
पूर्व्वोत्तर<BR>nf. (-रं-रा)<BR>The north-east.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व east, and उत्तर north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोदित|पूर्वोदित
पूर्व्वोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Aforesaid, aforementioned.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल|पूलः
पूल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पूलति पूलयति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect or heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष|पूषः
पूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (पूषति)<BR>1 To increase or grow: see पुष.<BR>2 To nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष|पूषः
पूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The mulberry, (Morus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>पूष to grow, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषन्
पूषन्<BR>m. (-षा)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>पूष to nourish, aff. कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषभासा
पूषभासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The capital of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पूष the sun, भास् light, aff. टाप्, splendid as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषसुहृत्
पूषसुहृत्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>पूष the sun, and सुहृत् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ<BR>r. 3rd cl. (पिपर्त्ति)<BR>1 To protect, to nourish.<BR>2 To fill.<BR>5th cl. (पृणोति)<BR>To satisfy, to please or content.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (परति पारयत्ति)<BR>To fill, as the stomach or a vessel.<BR>r. 6th cl. (but with वि and आङ् prefixed, and ङ aff.) व्यापृङ् (व्याप्रियते)<BR>To be busy or active, to labor, to make exertions: see पॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्का
पृक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, कन् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्त|पृक्तं
पृक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Touched, mixed, in contact or combination with.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Wealth, possessions.<BR>E.<BR>पृच to mix, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ति|पृक्तिः
पृक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Touch, contact.<BR>E.<BR>पृच to touch, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच
पृच<BR>(ई) पृची r. 2nd cl. (पृक्ते) r. 7th cl. (पृणक्ति)<BR>To touch, to be or bring in contact.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (पर्चति पर्चयति)<BR>1 To hinder or restrain.<BR>2 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छक|पृच्छकः
पृच्छक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An inquirer, an investigator, an inquisitive person.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, वुन् aff., र changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छण
पृच्छण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Asking, inquiring.<BR>E.<BR>पृच्छ to ask, ल्युट् aff., र changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छा
पृच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>Asking, questioning, a question or inquiry.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to inquire, aff. अङ् and टाप्, the semivowel changed to the corresponding vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृज
पृज<BR>(ई) पृजी r. 2d cl. (पृक्ते)<BR>To touch, to be in contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृड
पृड<BR>r. 6th cl. (पृडति)<BR>To delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृण
पृण<BR>r. 6th cl. (पृणति)<BR>To please or gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतना
पृतना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 An army.<BR>2 A small army or division consisting of 243 elephants, as many chariots, 729 horse, and 1215 foot.<BR>E.<BR>पृ to fill, तन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनासाह्
पृतनासाह्<BR>m. (-षाट्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पृतना an army, षह to bear or be equal to, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ|पृथः
पृथ<BR>r. 10th cl. (पर्थयति)<BR>To throw or cast, to send or direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्
पृथक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Without, except.<BR>2 Separately, severally.<BR>E.<BR>पृथ to throw or dismiss, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्करण
पृथक्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Separating, distinguishing.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक्, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्कृत
पृथक्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Separated, sundered, made distinct.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्क्षेत्र
पृथक्क्षेत्र<BR>m. plu. (-चाः)<BR>Children of one father by wives of different classes.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separately, and क्षेच a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्त्व|पृथक्त्वं
पृथक्त्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Individuality, separateness, severalty.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to पृथक्; also with तल्, पृथक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्त्वचा
पृथक्त्वचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>A plant, commonly Mūrvā, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separately, त्वच् skin; having a fibrous bark from which bow-strings are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पर्णी
पृथक्पर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separate, पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पिण्ड|पृथक्पिण्डः
पृथक्पिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A relation connected by oblation of water only.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक्, and पिण्ड obsequial cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मता
पृथगात्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Discrimination, judgment.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् severally, आत्मन् real nature, तल् aff.; distinguishing the different nature of different things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मन्
पृथगात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Several, separate, individual.<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>Individualised spirit, or that of an individual, as detached from universal spirit, or the soul of all.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक्, and आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मिका
पृथगात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Individuality, separate or individual state of being.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separately, आत्मन् self, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्गुण
पृथग्गुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Having distinct properties.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक्, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्जन|पृथग्जनः
पृथग्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An ignorant man, a fool.<BR>2 A man of a low cast.<BR>3 A sinner, a wicked or vicious man.<BR>m. plu. (-नाः)<BR>Children of one father by different mothers.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् separate, away from, (virtue, &c.) and जन a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्विध|पृथग्विधः
पृथग्विध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Various, diversified, multiform.<BR>E.<BR>पृथक् several, विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथवी
पृथवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The earth: see पृथिवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथा
पृथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>KUNTĪ, the wife of PĀṆḌU.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, aff. अङ् and टाप्, and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथाज|पृथाजः
पृथाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The son of KUNTĪ, ARJUNA, &c.<BR>2 Name of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>पृथा, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथापति|पृथापतिः
पृथापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>PĀṆḌU, the nominal father of the Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>E.<BR>पृथा KUNTĪ, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिका
पृथिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A centipede.<BR>E.<BR>पृथ to throw, aff. क्वुन् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवि|पृथिविः
पृथिवि<BR>f. (-विः)<BR>The earth: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, Uṇādi aff. षिवन्, fem. aff. ङीप्, and the vowel substituted for the semivowel; also with the antepenultimate^1 vowel changed to अ, पृथवी; or dropped altogether, पृथ्वी; or without the fem. aff. पृथिवि.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीक्षित्
पृथिवीक्षित्<BR>m. (-क्षित्)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी, and क्षित् who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीतल
पृथिवीतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The surface of the ground.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी, and तल surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीपति|पृथिवीपतिः
पृथिवीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A drug, commonly Ṛṣabha.<BR>3 YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी the earth, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीपाल|पृथिवीपालः
पृथिवीपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king, a sovereign, a ruler.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी the earth, and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीशक्र|पृथिवीशक्रः
पृथिवीशक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>पृथिवी the earth, and शक्र INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु<BR>mfn. (-थुः-थु or थ्वी-थुः)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Smart, clever.<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 The fifth monarch of the solar dynasty in the second age.<BR>2 A name of Agni or fire.<BR>f. (-थुः)<BR>1 A pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>2 A medicinal substance, commonly Hiṅgupatrī.<BR>3 Opium.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, aff. कु, and र changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=551" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुक|पृथुकं|पृथुकः
पृथुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>The young of any animal.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Rice or grain flattened.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hingupatri: see पृथु.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, aff. कुकन् or पृथु as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुरोमन्
पृथुरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A fish in general.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large, and रोमन् hair of the human body, to which the scales of the fish may be considered analogous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुल|पृथुलं
पृथुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Great, large.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A medicinal substance, Hiṅgupatrī.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुशेखर|पृथुशेखरः
पृथुशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुस्कन्ध|पृथुस्कंध|पृथुस्कन्धः
पृथुस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A boar.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large; स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथूदर|पृथूदरः
पृथूदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Large-bellied, stout, corpulent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वी
पृथ्वी<BR>f. (-थ्वी)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>3 A medical substance and condiment, perhaps the leaf of the asafœtida plant, Hiṅgupatrī.<BR>4 The mother of the seventh Jina, or Jains deified teacher, SUPĀRŚVA.<BR>5 Cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>the feminine form of पृथु, or पृथु the king so named, and ङीप् aff.; the domain of king PṚTHU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीका
पृथ्वीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Large cardamoms.<BR>2 Small cardamoms.<BR>3 A small pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>पृथ्वी as above, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीभर|पृथ्वीभरः
पृथ्वीभर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A species of the Atyaṣṭi metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृदाकु|पृदाकुः
पृदाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A scorpion.<BR>3 A tiger.<BR>4 A leopard or the small hunting leopard.<BR>5 An elephant.<BR>6 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>पर्द to fart, Uṇādi aff. काकु; the vowel substituted for the semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि<BR>mfn. (-श्निः-श्निः-श्नि)<BR>1 Small, short, thin.<BR>2 Delicate, feeble.<BR>f. (-श्निः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 A queen, the wife of SUTAPĀ, who being regenerated after death, became DEVAKĪ the mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 The earth.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृश to touch, नि Uṇādi aff., and the initial rejected; also पृष्णि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निका
पृश्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निगर्ब्भ
पृश्निगर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पृश्नि the wife of a saint incarnate in DEVAKĪ, and गर्ब्भ the embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निधर|पृश्निधरः
पृश्निधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निपर्णी
पृश्निपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia, according to some of its synonyms, but in ROXBURGH'S Catalogue, Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>पृश्नि small, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निभद्र|पृश्निभद्रः
पृश्निभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>पृश्नि DEVAKĪ, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निशृङ्ग|पृश्निशृंग|पृश्निशृङ्गः
पृश्निशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU, in that incarnation.<BR>2 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>पृश्नि small, and शृङ्ग a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नी
पृश्नी<BR>f. (-श्नी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, नि aff., and डीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष
पृष<BR>(उ) पृषु r. 1st cl. (पर्षति)<BR>1 To sprinkle.<BR>2 To weary.<BR>3 To hurt, to injure.<BR>4 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्|पृषन्त्
पृषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Sprinkling.<BR>n. sing. (-षत्) du. (-षती) plu. (-षन्ति)<BR>A drop of water or any liquid.<BR>mf. (-षन्-षती)<BR>The porcine deer.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. अति, or participial aff. शटृ; also पृषत् and पृषन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत|पृषतः
पृषत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A drop of water.<BR>2 The porcine deer.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. अतच्: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषताम्पति|पृषतांपति|पृषताम्पतिः
पृषताम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Air, wind, or its deified personification.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् a deer, in the second case plural, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषताश्व|पृषताश्वः
पृषताश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् the porcine deer, and अश्व a horse: see पृषदश्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्क|पृषत्कः
पृषत्क<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>पृपत् a deer, and कन् added; swift as a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदश्व|पृषदश्वः
पृषदश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The god of air, or wind divinely personified.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् the porcine deer, or a drop of rain, and अश्व a horse; whose steeds are like deer, or may be considered as the drops of rain, accompanying a gale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदाज्य|पृषदाज्यं
पृषदाज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Ghee mixed with curds, forming an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् sprinkling, and आज्य Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषद्वल|पृषद्वलः
पृषद्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A horse of the wind.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् a deer, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषन्ति|पृषंति|पृषंतिः|पृषन्तिः
पृषन्ति<BR>n. (-न्ति)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, aff. भिच्; according to the best authorities, however, this word is the plural inflection of पृषत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषाकरा
पृषाकरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A small stone used as a weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषातक|पृषातकं
पृषातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An oblation of Ghee and curds.<BR>E.<BR>पृष sprinkling, अत to go or be, अच् and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोदर|पृषोदरः
पृषोदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Having a spot or circle on the belly.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत् a drop of any thing liquid, and उदर the belly, form irregular and special; the word is most commonly in use as a grammatical term, being the leading word of a class in which the formation of each is peculiar to itself, and being thence applied to designate the rule which comprehends the whole of the series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोद्यान|पृषोद्यानं
पृषोद्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A small garden.<BR>E.<BR>पृषत्, and उद्यान a garden, त rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Asked, inquired.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, क्त aff. and the vowel substituted for the semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टि|पृष्टिः
पृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 Touch.<BR>E.<BR>स्पृष to touch, &c. aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट्वा
पृष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having asked.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ|पृष्ठं
पृष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>1 The back.<BR>2 The rear, the last, the back or hinder part of any thing.<BR>3 The surface or superficies.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठग्रन्थि|पृष्ठग्रंथि|पृष्ठग्रन्थिः
पृष्ठग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>A hump on the back.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठचक्षुस्
पृष्ठचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतस्
पृष्ठतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Behind, at the back of.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठदृष्टि|पृष्ठदृष्टिः
पृष्ठदृष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ, and दृष्टि sight, looking behind him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठफल
पृष्ठफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Superficial contents of any figure.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांसाद|पृष्ठमांसादः
पृष्ठमांसाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>A backbiter, a talebearer, a slanderer.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, मांस the flesh, अद to eat, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांसादन|पृष्ठमांसादनं
पृष्ठमांसादन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>A backbiter.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Backbiting, slandering.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठमांस, and अदन eating: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवंश|पृष्ठवंशः
पृष्ठवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The back-bone.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, and वंश a bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवाह्
पृष्ठवाह्<BR>m. (-वाट् or वाड्)<BR>An ox of burthen, or one in training.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ, and वाह who bears; also प्रष्टवाह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवाह्य|पृष्ठवाह्यः
पृष्ठवाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>An ox of burthen, carrying any thing on his back.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, वह to bear, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशय
पृष्ठशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sleeping on the back.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=552" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशृङ्ग|पृष्ठशृंग|पृष्ठशृङ्गः
पृष्ठशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, and शृङ्ग a horn, whose horn bends over towards the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशृङ्गिन्|पृष्ठशृंगिन्
पृष्ठशृङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 An eunuch.<BR>3 A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>4 A ram.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ्य|पृष्ठ्यं|पृष्ठ्यः
पृष्ठ्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठ्यः-ष्ठ्या-ष्ठ्यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the back.<BR>m. (-ष्ठ्यः)<BR>A pack horse.<BR>n. (-ष्ठ्यं)<BR>A multitude of back bones.<BR>E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णि|पृष्णिः
पृष्णि<BR>mfn. (-ष्णिः-ष्णिः-ष्णि)<BR>Small, short or thin: see पृश्नि.<BR>f. (-ष्णिः)<BR>1 The heel: see पार्ष्णि.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>पृष to sprinkle, नि Uṇādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पॄ
पॄ<BR>r. 3rd cl. (पिपर्त्ति) 9th cl. (पृणाति) 10th cl. (पारयति)<BR>1 To nourish, to protect.<BR>2 To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचक|पेचकः
पेचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An owl.<BR>2 The root of an elephant's tail.<BR>3 The tip of it.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 A bed.<BR>6 A louse.<BR>E.<BR>पच to spread, Uṇādi aff. वुन्, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचकिन्
पेचकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पेचक the root of an elephant's tail, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचिल|पेचिलः
पेचिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>पेच for पेचक as above, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचु
पेचु<BR>m. (-चुः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>E.<BR>पिच to hurt, उ aff.; also with उलट् aff. पेचुल, fem. पेचुली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचुली
पेचुली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>An esculent root: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेट|पेटः
पेट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा or टी)<BR>A basket, a large basket.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, घञ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटक|पेटकं|पेटकः
पेटक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A basket for holding clothes, books, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Multitude, quantity.<BR>E.<BR>पिट to collect, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटाक|पेटाकः
पेटाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A basket.<BR>E.<BR>पेटा, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटिका
पेटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A box, a basket.<BR>E.<BR>पेटा, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेडा
पेडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>A basket, a large basket.<BR>E.<BR>पिड to collect, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेण
पेण<BR>(ऋ) पेणृ r. 1st cl. (पेणति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To embrace.<BR>3 To grind: it is more usually read पैणृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेत्व|पेत्वं|पेत्वः
पेत्व<BR>m. (-त्वः)<BR>A small part.<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Nectar.<BR>2 Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, इत्व Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेपीयमान
पेपीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>To be drank repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, reit. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेय|पेयं
पेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Drinkable, drink.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Milk.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Rice gruel.<BR>2 Decoction of any thing after straining.<BR>3 Any drink with a small quantity of boiled rice.<BR>4 Anise, (Pimpinella anisum.)<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूष|पेयूषं|पेयूषः
पेयूष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>1 The milk of a cow, which has calved within seven days.<BR>2 Fresh Ghee.<BR>3 Amṛta or nectar.<BR>E.<BR>पीय Sautra root, for पा to drink, ऊसुन् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel changed; otherwise पीयूष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
पेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 The golden mountain.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>पा to drink, Uṇādi aff. रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरोज|पेरोजं
पेरोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The turquoise: it is the Persian word فيروزه<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल|पेलं|पेलः
पेल<BR>(ऋ) पेणृ r. 1st cl. (पेलति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल|पेलं|पेलः
पेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A small part.<BR>2 Going.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A testicle.<BR>E.<BR>पिल to send, aff. घञ्, or पेल to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलव|पेलवं
पेलव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Delicate, fine.<BR>2 Thin, slim, slender.<BR>3 Soft.<BR>E.<BR>पेल, वा to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलिन्
पेलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>पेल going, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेव
पेव<BR>(ऋ) पेवृ r. 1st cl. (पेवते)<BR>To gratify by service, to serve, to attend on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशल|पेशलः
पेशल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Dexterous, clever.<BR>2 Beautiful, agreeable.<BR>3 Fraudulent, crafty.<BR>4 Soft, smooth.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिश to be a component part, अलच् aff; also पेषल and पेसल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्कृत्
पेशस्कृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A sort of insect, a kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशि|पेशिः
पेशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>f. (-शिः or शी)<BR>1 An egg.<BR>2 Split pease.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to be a part, Uṇādi aff. इन्; also with ङीप् added in the fem. form पेशी, as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 The egg of a bird.<BR>2 A blown bud.<BR>3 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>4 A ball of flesh or meat.<BR>5 A sheath, a scabbard.<BR>6 A muscle.<BR>7 The name of a river.<BR>8 The name of a female imp or demon.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to be a component part, aff. इन् and ङीप् added; also पेशि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेश्वर
पेश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what grinds.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to grind, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष|पेषः
पेष<BR>(ऋ) पेषृ r. 1st cl. (पेषते)<BR>To resolve or endeavour diligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषण|पेषणं
पेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Grinding, reducing to dust or powder.<BR>2 A hand mill, a stone and muller, any apparatus for grinding or pounding.<BR>3 A plant, (a sort of Euphorbia with three lobes, commonly Teṅkāṭasij.)<BR>E.<BR>पिश to grind, aff. ल्युट्; also पेषणि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणि|पेषणिः
पेषणि<BR>f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>A stone slab on which condiments, &c. are ground, with a muller.<BR>E.<BR>पिश to grind, aff. अनि and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषल|पेषलः
पेषल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Dexterous, clever.<BR>2 Beautiful, handsome: see पेशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषाक|पेषाकः
पेषाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small slab for grinding any thing upon.<BR>E.<BR>पिष to grind, Uṇādi aff. आक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस
पेस<BR>(ऋ) पेसृ r. 1st cl. (पेसति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेसल|पेसलः
पेसल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Dexterous.<BR>2 Handsome: see पेशल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्वर
पेस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Destructive.<BR>2 Moving, going.<BR>3 Splendid.<BR>E.<BR>पिस to hurt, &c. वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पै
पै<BR>r. 1st cl. (पायति)<BR>To dry, to wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैञ्जूष|पैंजूष|पैंजूषः|पैञ्जूषः
पैञ्जूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The ear.<BR>E.<BR>पिजि to injure, aff. ऊषन्, and the radical vowel augmented, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठर|पैठरं
पैठर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Boiled in a pot, (flesh, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पिठर a vessel, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठीनसि|पैठीनसिः
पैठीनसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>A Muni, author of a system of laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण
पैण<BR>(ऋ) पैणृ r. 1st cl. (पैणति)<BR>1 To go or approach.<BR>2 To command or direct, (an act.)<BR>3 To touch or embrace.<BR>4 To pound or grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्डिन्य|पैंडिन्य|पैंडिन्यं|पैण्डिन्यं
पैण्डिन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Mendicity, living upon alms.<BR>E.<BR>पिण्ड a ball of meat or rice, इनि poss. aff., यञ् aff. of condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामह|पैतामहं
पैतामह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the grandfather, inherited from him, (property, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>पितामह, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृक|पैतृकं
पैतृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Paternal, ancestral, belonging or relating to the father or to progenitors.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकभूमि|पैतृकभूमिः
पैतृकभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 Father-land, the country of one's ancestors.<BR>2 A paternal estate.<BR>E.<BR>पैतृक, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकष्वसेय
पैतृकष्वसेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A paternal aunt's son.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The daughter of a paternal aunt.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, स्वसृ a sister, aff. ढक्, whence the vowel of स्वसृ is rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृस्वस्रीय
पैतृस्वस्रीय<BR>mf. (-यः-या)<BR>The son or daughter of a father's sister.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a father, स्वसृ a sister, छण् aff. whence the ऋ of स्वसृ is changed to री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्त|पैत्तः
पैत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ती-त्तं)<BR>Biliary, bilious.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिक|पैत्तिकः
पैत्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bilious, biliary.<BR>E.<BR>पित्त, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=553" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Paternal, ancestral, relating or belonging to a parent or progenitor.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The part of the hand between the thumb and forefinger, or according to some the root of the forefinger.<BR>2 A year, month, day, &c. of the Pitṛs.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ a parent, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्राहोरात्र|पैत्राहोरात्रः
पैत्राहोरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A day and night of the Pitṛs, or progenitors, equal to a month of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>पैत्र relating to the manes, अहन् a day, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्रिक
पैत्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Paternal, ancestral.<BR>E.<BR>पितृ, and ठञ् aff. and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैल|पैलः
पैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sage, the promulgator of the Ṛk Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच<BR>mfn. (-चः-ची-चं)<BR>Infernal, demoniacal, relating or belonging to a Piśāca or goblin.<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A mode of marriage, the ravishment of a girl by her lover.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A present to a friend, or to secure friendly regard made at a religious ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>पिशाच an imp, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन|पैशुनं
पैशुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Information, reporting evil of others.<BR>2 Roguery.<BR>E.<BR>पिशुन a spy, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन्य|पैशुन्यं
पैशुन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Information, espionage, &c.<BR>2 Depravity; wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>पिशुन a spy, a rogue, aff. यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं)<BR>Ground or made up into a cake.<BR>f. (-ष्टी)<BR>Spirituous liquor distilled from meal.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट ground, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A quantity of cakes.<BR>2 Spirituous liquor distilled from meal.<BR>E.<BR>पिष्ट, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगण्ड|पोगंड|पोगण्डः
पोगण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Deformed, having a redundant or defective member.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A boy, one from his fifth to his sixteenth year.<BR>E.<BR>अपि certainly, गडि to be a part of the cheek, अच् aff., the अ of the prefix is rejected, and the इ changed to ओ; otherwise, अप depreciative prefix, गम to go, and the deriv. irr.; also अपोगण्ड; in the second sense it also occurs पौगण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट|पोटः
पोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The foundation of a house, &c.<BR>2 Uniting, mixing.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>1 A woman having a beard.<BR>2 A female servant or slave.<BR>(-टी)<BR>A large alligator.<BR>E.<BR>पुट to shine, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटगल|पोटगलः
पोटगल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A reed, (Arundo tibialis, Rox.)<BR>2 A sort of grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>3 A fish.<BR>E.<BR>पोट uniting (with the wind), गल to go, aff. अच्, waving in the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटलिका
पोटलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bundle or packet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटिक|पोटिकः
पोटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट्टली
पोट्टली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A bundle, a parcel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोडु|पोडुः
पोडु<BR>m. (-डुः)<BR>The lower surface of the parietal bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत|पोतः
पोत<BR>mf. (-तः-ती)<BR>The young of any animal.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A young elephant of ten years old.<BR>2 A vessel, a ship, a boat.<BR>3 The site of a house or dwelling.<BR>4 Cloth.<BR>E.<BR>पूञ् to purify, तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतकी
पोतकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A potherb, (Basella lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>पूत nominal verb, from पूत a stench, वुञ् aff., ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतज|पोतजः
पोतज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An animal that produces young at once without the intervention of any medium; elephants and some other animals being supposed in Hindu physiology to carry the young without the aid of an ovarium or uterus.<BR>E.<BR>पोत young, and जन to bear, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतबणिज्
पोतबणिज्<BR>m. (-णिक्)<BR>A voyaging merchant.<BR>E.<BR>पात a boat, and वणिक् a trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतरक्ष|पोतरक्षः
पोतरक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The rudder of a boat, or large oar used as one.<BR>E.<BR>पोत a boat, रक्ष to preserve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतलकप्रिय|पोतलकप्रियः
पोतलकप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>One of the Jinas or Jaina deified teachers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतवाह|पोतवाहः
पोतवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A rower, a boatman, a steersman, a towman, or one of the crew that keeps watch at the mast-head.<BR>E.<BR>पोत a boat, वह to bear, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोताच्छादन|पोताच्छादनं
पोताच्छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>पोत cloth, आच्छादन covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोताधान|पोताधानं
पोताधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Small fry, a shoal of young fish.<BR>E.<BR>पोव, and आधान taking; being caught in bags.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतास|पोतासः
पोतास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A sort of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतिका
पोतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>पूत nominal verb, to stink, aff. वुन्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतृ
पोतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 One of the officiating priests at a sacrifice.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>पू to make pure, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्र|पोत्रं
पोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The snout of a hog.<BR>2 The share of a plough.<BR>2 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पू to make pure, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रायुध|पोत्रायुधः
पोत्रायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>पोक्ष a snout, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिदंष्ट्राज
पोत्रिदंष्ट्राज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A gem, supposed to be found in the tooth of a hog.<BR>E.<BR>पोत्रि a hog, दंष्ट्रा a tooth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिन्
पोत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>पोत्र the snout, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिरथा
पोत्रिरथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>One of the Śaktis or female divinities of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>पोत्रि a hog, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोथकी
पोथकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Red pimples on the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोपुव
पोपुव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Purifying or cleansing much or repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>पू to purify, intens. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोल|पोलः
पोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Magnitude, bulk.<BR>2 A heap, a quantity.<BR>E.<BR>पुल to be great, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिका
पोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Flat cakes made of barley or wheat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिन्द|पोलिंद|पोलिंदः|पोलिन्दः
पोलिन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A part of a boat supporting the deck, (the knees or ribs of a boat?)<BR>E.<BR>पोल magnitude, इदि to be supreme, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष|पोषः
पोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. पोषण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषण|पोषणं
पोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषणीय
पोषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be cherished or protected.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषयित्नु|पोषयित्नुः
पोषयित्नु<BR>mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु)<BR>Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, in the causal form, इत्नुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषितव्य
पोषितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cherished or protected.<BR>E.<BR>पुष, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृ
पोष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what nourishes, cherishes, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1 Grey bonduc.<BR>2 A protector, a cherisher.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृवर|पोष्टृवरः
पोष्टृवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what nourishes best.<BR>E.<BR>पोष्टृ, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्य|पोष्यः
पोष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>To be cherished or taken care of.<BR>E.<BR>पुष to nourish, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यत्व
पोष्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Cherishing dependants.<BR>2 Being taken care of.<BR>E.<BR>पोष्य, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यपुत्त्र
पोष्यपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>An adopted son.<BR>E.<BR>पोष्य, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यवर्ग|पोष्यवर्गः
पोष्यवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A class of persons or objects to be cherished, as parents, children, guests, and the sacred fire.<BR>E.<BR>पोष्य, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=554" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंश्चल्य|पौंश्चल्यं
पौंश्चल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Female incontinency, harlotry.<BR>E.<BR>पुंश्चली a lewd woman, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंसवन|पौंसवनं
पौंसवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>One of the Saṃskāras or essential ceremonies of the Hindu religion; a religious observance, held when signs of a living conception take place.<BR>E.<BR>पुंसवन, q. v., with अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंस्न|पौंस्नं
पौंस्न<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Virile, manly, relating to or good for man.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Manhood.<BR>E.<BR>पुं man, स्नञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डर्य्य|पौण्डर्य|पौंडर्यं|पौण्डर्य्यं
पौण्डर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A drug, commonly Puṇḍarīya.<BR>E.<BR>अण् added to पुण्डर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्र|पौंड्र|पौंड्रः|पौण्ड्रः
पौण्ड्र<BR>m. (-ण्ड्रः)<BR>1 A country, extending from Rangpur across the Ganges to the Jangel Mehals and part of south Behar, including therefore the greater part of Bengal.<BR>2 A sort of sugar-cane of a pale straw colour.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्ड्र the same, aff. अण्; also with कन् added पौण्ड्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रक|पौंड्रक|पौंड्रकः|पौण्ड्रकः
पौण्ड्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The pale straw-coloured species of sugar-cane.<BR>2 A man of a mixed caste, from the Vaiśya and female of the distiller caste, whose business it is to boil sugar.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to पौण्ड्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रवर्द्धन
पौण्ड्रवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A country, one of the divisions of central India, (Behar.)<BR>E.<BR>पौण्ड्र the sugar-cane, and वर्द्धन encreasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रिक|पौंड्रिक|पौंड्रिकः|पौण्ड्रिकः
पौण्ड्रिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pale straw variety of the sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>पुण्ड the same, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतव|पौतवं
पौतव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Measure.<BR>E.<BR>पू to be made pure or correct, तन् aff. and अण् added; also यौतव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिनासिक्य
पौतिनासिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Fœtor of the nostrils.<BR>E.<BR>पूतिनासिका a foul nose, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्तिक|पौत्तिकं
पौत्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Honey of a pale colour.<BR>E.<BR>पूत्तिका a small bee, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्र
पौत्त्र<BR>mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं)<BR>Relating to a son.<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A son's son, a grandson.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>A grand-daughter, either in the male or female line, though more usually implying a son's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र or पुत्त्री a son or daughter, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिक
पौत्त्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a son or a grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्र or पौत्त्र, and ठञ् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिकेय
पौत्त्रिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A daughter's son.<BR>E.<BR>पुत्त्रिका, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिन्
पौत्त्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्त्री-त्त्रिणी-त्त्रि)<BR>Having a grandson.<BR>E.<BR>पोत्त्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुनिक|पौनःपुनिकः
पौनःपुनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Repeated, reiterated, again and again.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्, repeated, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुन्य|पौनःपुन्यं
पौनःपुन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Reiteration, repetition.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर् again, repeated, aff. यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त|पौनरुक्तं
पौनरुक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Tautology.<BR>E.<BR>पुनरुक्त, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भव|पौनर्भवः
पौनर्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Repeated, additional.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>One of the sons or heirs admitted by the old Hindu law; the son of a twice married woman.<BR>E.<BR>पुनर्भव, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>City, citizen, relating to or produced in a town or city.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>पुर a city, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरक|पौरकं|पौरकः
पौरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A garden round a house.<BR>E.<BR>पौर citizen, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजन|पौरजनः
पौरजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A citizen.<BR>E.<BR>पौर, जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरव|पौरवः
पौरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Of the race of Puru, descended from Puru.<BR>E.<BR>पुरु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरसख्य
पौरसख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Connexion or equality by inhabiting the same city for ten years, fellow-citizenship.<BR>E.<BR>पौर relating to a city, सख्य friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्य|पौरस्त्यः
पौरस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>Prior, first, initial.<BR>E.<BR>पुरस् formerly, अण् aff. of relation, पौरस्, and त्यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्री
पौरस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A woman residing in a town or city.<BR>E.<BR>पौरा, and स्त्री a female; also similar compounds, as पौरयोषित, पौराङ्गना, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराण
पौराण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Relating to the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>पुराण, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिक|पौराणिकः
पौराणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or belonging to the Purāṇas, Paurānic.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman, well read in the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>पुराल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष|पौरुषं|पौरुषः
पौरुष<BR>mfn. subst. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>The measure of a man, equal to the height to which he reaches with both arms elevated, and the fingers extended.<BR>adj.<BR>Manly, of or belonging to man.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 The property of manhood, virility, manliness.<BR>2 Action, or action incidental to the state of humanity.<BR>3 Semen virile.<BR>4 Strength, power, vigour.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषता
पौरुषता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Manhood, manly strength or spirit.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to पौरुष; also with त्व, पौरुषत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेय|पौरुषेयः
पौरुषेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made by, derived from, or relating to man, human, manly, virile, &c.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A crowd, or number of men.<BR>2 Manslaughter, murder.<BR>3 Law, as affecting persons.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुष a man, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोगव|पौरोगवः
पौरोगव<BR>mf. (-वः-वी)<BR>Overseer or superintendant of the kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>पुरुस् first, गौ the eye, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाश|पौरोडाशः
पौरोडाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A prayer recited upon making an oblation of clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>पुरोडाश butter offered to fire, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशिक|पौरोडाशिकः
पौरोडाशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A priest who recites the prayer used in offering an oblation of clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>पौरोडाश, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित्य|पौरोहित्यं
पौरोहित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>The character or functions of family priest.<BR>E.<BR>पुरोहित, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास|पौर्णमासः
पौर्णमास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A ceremony performed at the full of the moon, by persons maintaining a perpetual fire.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्णमास a rite, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिम|पौर्णिमः
पौर्णिम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An ascetic.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Day of full moon.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्णिमा, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्त्तिक|पौर्तिक
पौर्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्त्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्व|पौर्व
पौर्व्व<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>Relating, or belonging to the past, to the east, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वपदिक|पौर्वपदिक
पौर्व्वपदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the first member of a compound.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वपद, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वदेहिक|पौर्वदेहिक
पौर्व्वदेहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to a former body or existence.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वदेह, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वार्द्धिक|पौर्वार्धिक
पौर्व्वार्द्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Dwelling or being in the eastern division of a town, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वार्द्ध eastern half or part, and ठञ् aff.; also with घञ्, पौर्व्वार्द्ध; and with यत्, पूर्व्वार्द्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वापर्य्य|पौर्वापर्य|पौर्वापर्यं|पौर्वापर्य्य
पौर्व्वापर्य्य<BR>n. (-य्यं)<BR>Priority and subsequence.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वापर first and last, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वाह्णिक|पौर्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिकः
पौर्व्वाह्णिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to or produced in the forepart of the day.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्वाह्ण forenoon, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=555" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्विक|पौर्विक
पौर्व्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Prior, primary, former.<BR>E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलस्त्य|पौलस्त्यः
पौलस्त्य<BR>m. (-स्त्यः)<BR>1 KUVERA.<BR>2 RĀVAṆA.<BR>3 Either of the brothers of RĀVAṆA, VIBHĪṢAṆA or KUMBHAKARṆA.<BR>f. (-स्ती)<BR>The sister of RĀVAṆA, ŚŪRPANAKHĀ.<BR>E.<BR>पुलस्त्य a saint so named, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलि|पौलिः
पौलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>Grain half dressed, or scorched or fried with Ghee, and made into a sort of cake.<BR>E.<BR>पौल a heap, इञ् aff., and ङीप् added for the fem.; also with कन added पौलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलिका
पौलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of cake: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोमी
पौलोमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>पुलोमन् a saint, the father of the goddess, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष|पौषः
पौष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The month Pauṣa, (December-January.)<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>Day of full moon in the month Pauṣa.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्य the asterism in which the moon is full in this month, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कर|पौष्करं
पौष्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Relating to a pond, to a lotus, to fragrant Costus, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्कर, q. v., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करिणी
पौष्करिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A large pond or reservoir.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्करिणी the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्टिक|पौष्टिकं
पौष्टिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Preservative, protective, nutritive, &c.<BR>2 Nutritious, fattening.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A cloth worn when the ceremony of tonsure is performed.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्टि nourishing, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्ण|पौष्णं
पौष्ण<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>The last of the twenty-eight lunar asterisms; also REVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>पूषन् the sun, in this name regent of the asterism, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्प|पौष्पं
पौष्प<BR>mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पी-ष्पं)<BR>Flowery, floral, relating or belonging to flowers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पक|पौष्पकं
पौष्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The oxid of brass, considered as a collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्पक the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पी
पौष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A name of Palibothra.<BR>E.<BR>पुष्प a flower, अण् aff., and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ना
प्ना<BR>f. (-प्ना)<BR>ŚIVA'S braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याट्
प्याट्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of calling, ho! hola!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याय
प्याय<BR>(ओ) (ई) ओप्यायी r. 1st cl. (प्यायते)<BR>To grow or increase, to enlarge or swell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युष
प्युष<BR>(इर) प्युषिर r. 4th cl. (प्युष्यति)<BR>1 To burn.<BR>2 To share or divide.<BR>r. 10th cl. (प्युषयति)<BR>To relinquish, to part with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युस
प्युस<BR>r. 4th cl. (प्युस्यति)<BR>1 To divide.<BR>2 To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यै
प्यै<BR>(ङ) प्यैङ् r. 1st cl. (प्यायते)<BR>To grow or increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix, implying,<BR>1 Progressive motion, (forth, forward, away, &c.)<BR>2 Excess or excellence, (very, much, exceeding.)<BR>3 Appearance, manifestation.<BR>It corresponds with the Latin particles Pro and Prœ, as in प्रकर्त्तुं To do much or well; प्रक्रमितुं To go forth or over; प्रकर्षितुं To excel; प्रकाशितुं To display; प्रस्थातुं To go forth, set out; प्रकमम् Very willingly; प्रमृगम् When the deer go forth (the time, &c.) See the following compounds.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, &c. aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकट|प्रकटं
प्रकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>Displayed, unfolded, manifest, apparent.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying manifestation, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटित|प्रकटितं
प्रकटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Manifested, displayed.<BR>2 Evident, apparent.<BR>3 Opened, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कट to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटीकरण
प्रकटीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making visible or apparent, displaying, manifesting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकट, and करण making, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटीकृत
प्रकटीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made manifest, open, or visible.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकट, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्प|प्रकंप|प्रकंपः|प्रकम्पः
प्रकम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कपि to tremble, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पन|प्रकंपन|प्रकम्पनः
प्रकम्पन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Trembling violently.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Wind, air.<BR>2 A hell.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Violent or excessive motion, great trembling.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying excess, कम्पन trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पमान
प्रकम्पमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shaking, trembling violently.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कषि to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पयत्
प्रकम्पयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कपि to tremble, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
प्रकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who or what does much or well.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A heap, a quantity.<BR>2 A bundle of flowers, a nosegay.<BR>3 Aid, assistance, friendship.<BR>4 Usage, custom, continuance of a similar practice.<BR>5 Respect.<BR>6 Seduction, abduction.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Aloe wood, (Agallochum.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Theatrical dress or disguise, as wearing a woman's garb, &c.<BR>2 An episodical incident in a drama.<BR>3 An open piece of ground, the meeting of four roads, or the proper site of any magical operations.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृ to make, aff. ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरण|प्रकरणं
प्रकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 An introduction, a prologue or prelude.<BR>2 A poetical fiction or poem, in which the story and principal persons are wholly imaginary; the term is especially applied to a dramatic poem.<BR>3 A chapter, a section, a book, a place of pausing or stopping.<BR>4 Treating with respect.<BR>5 Doing much or well.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A minor drama of the same character as the Prakaraṇa, but of less extent; also प्रकरणिका.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृ to make, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकश
प्रकश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, कश to hurt, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्ष|प्रकर्षः
प्रकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Excellence, eminence, superiority.<BR>2 Specialty, intensity, universality.<BR>3 Absoluteness, definitiveness.<BR>4 (In grammar,) The effect of the prefix प्र upon roots.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृश to attract, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षगमन
प्रकर्षगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going absolutely or finally, departure.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकर्ष, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षण
प्रकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Drawing, attracting.<BR>2 Ploughing, drawing furrows.<BR>3 Excellence, superiority.<BR>4 Realizing by the use of a pledge more than the interest of the loan.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृष to attract, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षित
प्रकर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Drawn, drawn out.<BR>2 Exceeded in profit, (the interest of the loan.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Profit on a pledge beyond the interest of a loan.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृष to make furrows, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पित
प्रकल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done, made.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृप to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्ड|प्रकांड|प्रकांडं|प्रकांडः|प्रकाण्डः
प्रकाण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 The stem of a tree, the part between the root and the branches.<BR>2 A branch, a shoot.<BR>3 Excellence, happiness, (or used as an attributive without admitting variation of gender,) excellent, best, happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying excess or superiority, कम to desire, aff. ड, and the penultimate vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्डर|प्रकांडर|प्रकांडरः|प्रकाण्डरः
प्रकाण्डर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाण्ड a stem, रा to get, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामम्
प्रकामम्<BR>ind.<BR>Voluntarily, willingly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying much, very, काम desire, will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=556" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकार|प्रकारः
प्रकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Difference.<BR>2 Similitude.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Sort, kind, species.<BR>2 Way, mode, manner.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृ to do, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश|प्रकाशं|प्रकाशः
प्रकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>1 Like, resembling.<BR>2 Open, manifest, blown, expanded.<BR>3 Famous, celebrated.<BR>4 Public.<BR>n. adv. (-शं)<BR>1 Openly, publicly.<BR>2 (In dramatic language), Aloud.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Sunshine, lustre, light.<BR>2 Expansion, diffusion, manifestation; the word being equally applicable to physical or moral subjects, as the blowing of a flower, diffusion of celebrity, the publicity of an event, or the manifestation of a truth.<BR>3 A laugh, a smile.<BR>4 Publicity.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>White or bellmetal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying motion or eminence, काश to shine, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशक|प्रकाशकः
प्रकाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What irradiates, what makes open or apparent, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An illuminator, an expounder, an illustrator.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाश to make light or evident, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशकज्ञातृ
प्रकाशकज्ञातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाशक illuminator (the sun), and ज्ञातृ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशता
प्रकाशता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Manifestation, visibility.<BR>2 Luminousness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाश, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, प्रकाशत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशन|प्रकाशनः
प्रकाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Illuminating, giving light.<BR>2 Making clear or manifest.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before, काश to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशमान
प्रकाशमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Splendid, brilliant, radiant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before काश to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशात्मन्
प्रकाशात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाश light, आत्मन् self; light itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशित|प्रकाशितं
प्रकाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Evident, apparent, manifest, visible.<BR>2 Published, promulgated.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकाश manifestation, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्ण|प्रकीर्णं|प्रकीर्णः
प्रकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Spread abroad, published, promulgated.<BR>2 Expanded, opened.<BR>3 Miscellaneous, mixed.<BR>4 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>5 Agitated, excited, wild.<BR>6 Waved, waving.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 A Chowri, a cow-tail used as a fan.<BR>2 A chapter, a section.<BR>3 A collection of miscellaneous rules.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृ to throw or cast, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्णक|प्रकीर्णकं|प्रकीर्णकः
प्रकीर्णक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A Chowri, the tail of the Bos grunniens, used as a whisk or fan.<BR>2 The section or chapter of a book.<BR>3 Extent, length, especially of a stanza or book.<BR>4 (In law,) A case not provided for by the Śāstras, and to be decided by the authority of the judge or king.<BR>5 A miscellany.<BR>6 Any collection of heterogeneous objects not arranged under any distinct classes or heads.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to प्रकीर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्ति|प्रकीर्ति|प्रकीर्तिः
प्रकीर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Fame, celebrity.<BR>2 Declaration.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कॄ to scatter, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्तित|प्रकीर्तित|प्रकीर्त्तितं
प्रकीर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Declared, explained, said, revealed.<BR>2 Celebrated, renowned.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कॄ to scatter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्य्य|प्रकीर्य|प्रकीर्यः|प्रकीर्य्यः
प्रकीर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be spread abroad or about, to be diffused, promulgated, expanded, or extended.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र progressive motion, कॄ to throw or cast, aff. यक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुपित
प्रकुपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Enraged, incensed.<BR>2 Disordered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुप to be angry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्व्वत्|प्रकुर्वत्
प्रकुर्व्वत्<BR>mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वती-र्व्वत्)<BR>1 Behaving respectfully to, waiting upon, serving, honouring.<BR>2 Doing much or well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृ to do, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्व्वाण|प्रकुर्वाण
प्रकुर्व्वाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Attending, or behaving to with respect.<BR>2 Doing much or well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and कृ to make, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुल|प्रकुलं
प्रकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A handsome or excellent body.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellent, कुल the body; also read प्रह्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृत|प्रकृतः
प्रकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made, completed, accomplished.<BR>2 Commenced.<BR>3 Continuing or engaged in what has been begun.<BR>4 Wished, expected.<BR>5 Important, interesting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृति|प्रकृतिः
प्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Nature; in philosophy, the passive or material cause of the world, as opposed to the active or spiritual; and in mythology, a goddess, the personified will of the Supreme in the creation, identified with Māyā or illusion, and in an especial manner the prototype of the female sex; hence it is the same with the Śakti or personified energy or bride of a deity, as LAKṢMĪ, DURGĀ, &c. in some systems Prakṛti is considered the same with the Supreme Being.<BR>2 The natural state or condition of any thing.<BR>3 A radical form or predicament of being, as illusion, intelligence, consciousness, and the five elements, or Ākāśa, fire, air, earth, and water.<BR>4 The five elements collectively.<BR>5 Cause, origin.<BR>6 A woman or womankind.<BR>7 A mother.<BR>8 An animal.<BR>9 The male organ of generation.<BR>10 The female organ of generation.<BR>11 An uninflected word; the radical form of a word, before the affixes forming cases, &c. are subjoined.<BR>12 A requisite of regal administration, of which seven are enumerated; the king, the minister, an ally, treasure, territory, fortresses, and an army: the corporations or companies of citizens are sometimes added, making an eighth class.<BR>13 A form of metre, consisting of a stanza of four lines, each line containing twenty-one syllables.<BR>14 (In arithmetic,) A given coefficient. (In anatomy,) Temperament, the predominance of one of the humours at the time of generation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying priority or precedence, कृ to make, aff. क्तिन् or क्तिच्; being the first step towards creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतितरल
प्रकृतितरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Volatile, fickle.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकृति nature, and तरल changing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिस्थ
प्रकृतिस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Natural, genuine, unmixed.<BR>2 Inherent, innate.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकृति, and स्थ what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृशित
प्रकृशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Thin, emaciate.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृश to be thin, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्ट|प्रकृष्टं
प्रकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Chief, principal, pre-eminent.<BR>2 Remote, far, long (as a road).<BR>E.<BR>प्र eminently, कृश to attract, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्टत्व
प्रकृष्टत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Eminence, superiority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकृष्ट, and त्व aff.; also with तल् aff. प्रकृष्टता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोप|प्रकोपः
प्रकोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Irritation, provocation, enraging.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुप to be angry, causal v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपणीय
प्रकोपणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be incensed or enraged.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुप to be angry, causal v., अनीयर् aff. and the न optionally changed; also प्रकोपनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपन
प्रकोपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Irritating, provoking.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुप to be angry, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपित
प्रकोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Irritated, provoked.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुप to be angry, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठ|प्रकोष्ठः
प्रकोष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 The fore-arm.<BR>2 Part of the frame of a door.<BR>3 A court in a house, or open space surrounded by buildings.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कुष to draw, स्थन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=557" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्खर|प्रक्खरः
प्रक्खर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A horse's armour; also प्रखर and प्रक्षर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रन्तृ|प्रक्रंतृ
प्रक्रन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>1 Who proceeds or goes.<BR>2 Conquering, overpowering, surpassing.<BR>3 Who begins, a beginner.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्रम to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रम|प्रक्रमः
प्रक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Proceeding, going.<BR>2 Leisure, opportunity.<BR>3 Beginning.<BR>4 Surpassing, overcoming.<BR>E.<BR>प्र first or most, क्रम to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमणीय
प्रक्रमणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be gone or proceeded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्रम to go, अनीयर् aff.; also प्रक्रमितव्य and प्रक्रम्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रममाण
प्रक्रममाण<BR>(-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Proceeding.<BR>2 Beginning.<BR>3 Overcoming.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्रम to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रान्त|प्रक्रांत|प्रक्रान्तः
प्रक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Gone, proceeded.<BR>2 Gone beyond, surpassed.<BR>3 Begun.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्रम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रिया
प्रक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Bearing royal insignia.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, क्रिया business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीडित
प्रक्रीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Playing, sporting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before, क्रीड to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्त
प्रकॢप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Made, prepared.<BR>2 Mixed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before कृप to make, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लिन्न|प्रक्लिन्नः
प्रक्लिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Satisfied.<BR>2 Wet, soaked.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excess, क्लिद to wet, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वण|प्रक्वणः
प्रक्वण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sound of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, क्वण to sound, aff. अप्; also प्रक्वाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वाण|प्रक्वाणः
प्रक्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sound of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्वण to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षर|प्रक्षरः
प्रक्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Iron armour for the defence of a horse or elephant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र best, क्षर to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालक
प्रक्षालक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what washes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षल to cleanse, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालन|प्रक्षालनं
प्रक्षालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning, washing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र thoroughly, क्षल r. 10th cl. to clean, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालित|प्रक्षालितः
प्रक्षालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Washed, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षल r. 10th cl. to clean, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्त
प्रक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Thrown, cast, hurled.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षिप to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्तवत्
प्रक्षिप्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Throwing, having thrown.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षिप to throw, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीण
प्रक्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Decayed, wasting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षि to waste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीवित
प्रक्षीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षीव to be drunk, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेप|प्रक्षेपः
प्रक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Throwing, casting.<BR>2 Throwing into or upon.<BR>3 Any thing added, or thrown in to drugs when in course of decoction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षिप to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपण|प्रक्षेपणं
प्रक्षेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Throwing, casting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्षिप to throw, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडन|प्रक्ष्वेडनः
प्रक्ष्वेडन<BR>mf. (-नः-ना)<BR>1 An iron arrow.<BR>2 Clamour, a loud indistinct noise.<BR>E.<BR>प्र especially, क्ष्विद to sound indistinctly, aff. ल्यु, deriv. irr.; otherwise प्रक्ष्वेदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदन|प्रक्ष्वेदनः
प्रक्ष्वेदन<BR>mf. (-नः-ना)<BR>1 An iron arrow.<BR>2 Calling aloud, clamour:<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदित
प्रक्ष्वेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Clamorous, shouting, making a loud indistinct noise.<BR>2 Unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before, क्ष्विद to sound, क्त aff.; also read प्रक्ष्वेडित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदितवत्
प्रक्ष्वेदितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Noisy.<BR>2 Unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before क्ष्विद to make a noise, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखर|प्रखरः
प्रखर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very hot or acrid.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Iron armour, for the defence of a horse or elephant.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>3 A mule.<BR>E.<BR>प्र very much, खन to hurt, aff. रक, deriv. irr.; or प्र before खर an ass, or hot, sharp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्य|प्रख्यः
प्रख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Like, resembling, (in composition.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ख्या to say, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यात|प्रख्यातः
प्रख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Celebrated, famous, notorious.<BR>2 Pleased, happy.<BR>3 Bespoken, forestalled, claimed by right of preemption.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, ख्यात famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यातभाण्ड
प्रख्यातभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A commodity that is to be first offered for sale to some person, (as the Raja, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रख्यात claimed, भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यातवप्तृक|प्रख्यातवप्तृकः
प्रख्यातवप्तृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gentleman, a Hidalgo, the son of some body.<BR>E.<BR>प्रख्यात known, वप्तृ a father, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्याति|प्रख्यातिः
प्रख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Publicity, notoriety.<BR>2 Praise, eulogium.<BR>3 Fame.<BR>E.<BR>प्र pre-eminence, &c. and ख्याति reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यानीय
प्रख्यानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be celebrated or made known.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ख्या to say, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगण्ड|प्रगंड|प्रगंडः|प्रगण्डः
प्रगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The upper arm, from the elbow to the shoulder.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>An outer wall or rampart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, गण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगत
प्रगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Separate, apart.<BR>2 Gone with difficulty.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगतजानु|प्रगतजानुः
प्रगतजानु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart.<BR>E.<BR>प्रगत separated, and जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगतजानुक|प्रगतजानुकः
प्रगतजानुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र away, गत gone, जानु the knee, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगदित
प्रगदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Speaking, beginning to speak.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before गद to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगमन|प्रगमनं
प्रगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Progress, advance.<BR>2 Difficult progress.<BR>3 Going afar or apart.<BR>4 Disputing, words.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and गम to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भ|प्रगल्भः
प्रगल्भ<BR>mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं)<BR>1 Bold, confident.<BR>2 Prompt, ready.<BR>3 Resolute, energetic.<BR>4 Illustrious, eminent.<BR>5 Strong, able.<BR>6 Shameless, impudent, audacious.<BR>m. (-ल्भः)<BR>The fire used for oblations at the birth of a child.<BR>f. (-ल्भा)<BR>A woman who courts her husband's caresses, a bold or confident woman.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, गल्भ to be proud, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भता
प्रगल्भता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Energy, resolution.<BR>2 Confidence, boldness.<BR>3 Audacity, arrogance.<BR>4 Power, eminence, consequence.<BR>5 Perverseness, wilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् aff. of the abstract, added to the last; also with त्व, प्रगल्भत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगाढ|प्रगाढं
प्रगाढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>2 Hard, difficult.<BR>3 Hard, firm.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>Pain, privation, penance.<BR>n. adv. (-ढं)<BR>1 Much, exceedingly.<BR>2 Tightly, firmly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before गाढ much, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगातृ
प्रगातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>A capital singer.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellent, and गातृ who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगीत
प्रगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sung, vocal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण|प्रगुणः
प्रगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Straight.<BR>2 Honest, upright, straight in morals.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellent, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण्य
प्रगुण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>1 More, exceeding.<BR>2 Excellent.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before गुण a quality or quantity, and क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=558" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृहीत
प्रगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Collected, strung together.<BR>2 Accepted, admitted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृह्य|प्रगृह्यं
प्रगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be taken, accepted, admitted, &c.<BR>mn. (-ह्यः-ह्यं)<BR>The class of letters or syllables not subject to the rules of euphony, as the final ई or उ of the dual number, &c. as हरी एतौ, विष्णू इमौ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगे
प्रगे<BR>ind.<BR>Dawn, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगेतन|प्रगेतनः
प्रगेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating, or belonging to the morning.<BR>E.<BR>प्रगे morning, and द्यु aff., तन् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगोपण
प्रगोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Protection, preservation, salvation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र especially, गोपन preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रह|प्रग्रहः
प्रग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>2 Confinement, restriction, restraint, captivity.<BR>3 A prisoner, a captive, either man or beast in confinement.<BR>4 A rein, a rope or halter for horses, and cattle.<BR>5 The string suspending a balance.<BR>6 Favour, kindness.<BR>7 An arm.<BR>8 A ray of light.<BR>9 A sort of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ग्रह to take or seize, aff. अप्; otherwise with घञ्, aff. प्रग्राह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रहण|प्रग्रहणं
प्रग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>2 Assuming.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ग्रह to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्राह|प्रग्राहः
प्रग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Seizing.<BR>2 Taking, taking up, bearing, carrying.<BR>3 The string of a balance.<BR>4 A rein, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ग्रह to take, घञ् aff.; see प्रग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रीव|प्रग्रीवः
प्रग्रीव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>1 A window, a lattice, a balcony.<BR>2 A summer house, a pleasure house.<BR>3 A building on the top of a palace, a painted turret.<BR>4 A wooden balustrade or fence on the edge of a building.<BR>5 A stable.<BR>6 The top of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excessive or excellent, and ग्रीवा a neck; the neck as it were of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्ल
प्रग्ल<BR>mfn. (-ग्लः-ग्ला-ग्लं)<BR>Wearied, fatigued, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ग्लै to be weary, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघटाविद्
प्रघटाविद्<BR>m. (-विद्)<BR>A general reader, but not a profound one.<BR>E.<BR>प्रघटा said to imply novelty, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघण|प्रघणः
प्रघण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A terrace before a house.<BR>2 A copper pot.<BR>3 An iron crow or club.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हन to strike, aff. अप्, and the radical letter changed; also प्रघाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघन|प्रघनः
प्रघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A covered terrace before a house.<BR>2 A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हन to strike or hurt, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघस|प्रघसः
प्रघस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Voracious.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Eating much.<BR>2 A Daitya, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, घस for अद to eat, aff. अप् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघाण|प्रघाणः
प्रघाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A covered terrace or small portico before the door of a house.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हन to strike, (with the feet,) aff. अप्, and the radical vowel changed optionally; also प्रघण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघात|प्रघातः
प्रघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Combat, battle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र violently, घात striking; also प्राघात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघान|प्रघानः
प्रघान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A covered terrace before the door of a house, a porch, a portico: see प्रघन, and प्रघण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघूर्ण|प्रघूर्णः
प्रघूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Turning round or rolling violently.<BR>2 Wandering, roaming.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A guest, a visitor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before घूर्ण to turn round, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघोषक|प्रघोषकः
प्रघोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, घोष sound, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्र|प्रचक्रं
प्रचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>An army in motion, or as sometimes explained, foraging.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चक्र a division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्षस्
प्रचक्षस्<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>The regent of Jupiter, VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चक्ष to speak, Uṇādi aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचण्ड|प्रचंड|प्रचण्डः
प्रचण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Excessively hot or burning.<BR>2 Intolerable, insupportable.<BR>3 Bold, confident, presuming.<BR>4 Wrathful, passionate.<BR>5 Violent, strong.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A sort of Nerium with white flowers.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>One of DURGĀ'S emanations or attendants.<BR>E.<BR>प्र very, चण्ड hot, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचण्डमूर्त्ति|प्रचण्डमूर्ति|प्रचण्डमूर्त्तिः
प्रचण्डमूर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रचण्ड Nerium, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचय|प्रचयः
प्रचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A heap, a quantity, a number.<BR>2 Gathering, (as fruit or flowers, but especially by means of a stick or other implement.)<BR>3 Slight union or aggregation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चि to gather, aff. अच्; also with घञ् aff., प्रचाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचर|प्रचरः
प्रचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A road, a path.<BR>2 Usage, custom, currency.<BR>3 Going well or widely.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चर to go, aff. ट; also with घञ् aff., प्रचार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरण|प्रचरणं
प्रचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 Circulating, being current.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चर to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरत्
प्रचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Going, well, quickly, widely, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरित
प्रचरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, going.<BR>2 Pursued, practised, (as an art or business.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चर to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचल|प्रचलः
प्रचल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 What goes much or widely.<BR>2 Current, circulating, customary.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलत्
प्रचलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Going, proceeding far or much.<BR>2 Prevailing, circulating, being customary or current.<BR>3 Being recognised, (as authority or law, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलन|प्रचलनं
प्रचलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Moving, going much or widely.<BR>2 Circulating, being customary or current.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाक|प्रचलाकः
प्रचलाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A peacock's tail.<BR>2 Archery, shooting with arrows.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, aff. आकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाकिन्
प्रचलाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>प्रचलाक a peacock's tail, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलायित|प्रचलायितं
प्रचलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rolling about, tossing, tumbling, (as in sleep.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलित
प्रचलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone far or wide, wandering, roving.<BR>2 Set in motion, shaken.<BR>3 Current, customary, circulating, prevailing.<BR>4 Recognised, received, (as authority or law, &c.)<BR>5 Rolling (as the eye).<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचाय|प्रचायः
प्रचाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Gathering any thing with the hand.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, चि to collect, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचाल|प्रचालः
प्रचाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The stick or body of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चल to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचार|प्रचारः
प्रचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 Custom, usage.<BR>3 Conduct.<BR>4 Currency.<BR>5 Appearance, manifestation.<BR>6 Pasture ground.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चर to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचित
प्रचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Collected, gathered together.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चि to assemble, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुर|प्रचुरं|प्रचुरः
प्रचुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चुर to steal, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरपुरुष|प्रचुरपुरुषः
प्रचुरपुरुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Abounding with men, populous, numerous.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>प्रचुर, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकरण|प्रचुरीकरणं
प्रचुरीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Adding to, augmenting, increasing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रचुर, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=559" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकृत
प्रचुरीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Augmented, in quantity or number.<BR>E.<BR>प्रचुर, and कृत make, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतस्
प्रचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>1 VARUṆA, the regent of water.<BR>2 The name of a saint and lawgiver.<BR>m. plu. (-सः)<BR>The ten sons of PRĀCĪNAVARHIS by the daughter of VARUṆA, and the progenitors of DAKṢA.<BR>E.<BR>प्र best, first, चेतस् the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतृ
प्रचेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चि to collect, (the reins,) aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेल|प्रचेलं
प्रचेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चेल to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेलक|प्रचेलकः
प्रचेलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>प्र well, fast, चेल to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदन|प्रचोदनं
प्रचोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Saying, enjoining, prescribing.<BR>2 Sending, directing.<BR>3 A rule or law.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चुद to direct, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदित|प्रचोदितः
प्रचोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Prescribed, directed.<BR>2 Sent, directed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र thoroughly, चुद to direct, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदिनी
प्रचोदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before चुद to send, aff. ल्यु and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युत
प्रच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fallen from, deviated from.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before च्यु to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छ
प्रच्छ<BR>(औ) प्रच्छौ r. 6th cl. (पृच्छति)<BR>1 To ask or inquire.<BR>2 To desire, to know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छणा
प्रच्छणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Asking, addressing, inviting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद|प्रच्छदः|प्रछद
प्रच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cover, a wrapper.<BR>E.<BR>प्र completely, छद to cover, aff. अञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदपट|प्रच्छदपटः
प्रच्छदपट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A cover, a wrapper, either of a person or thing, as a cloak, a veil, a sheet, a curtain, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छद a cover, and पट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्न|प्रच्छन्नं
प्रच्छन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Covered, clothed.<BR>2 Unavowed, disguised.<BR>3 Private, concealed, secret.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 A private door within a house.<BR>2 A lattice, a loop hole.<BR>3 Any private door.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before च्छद to hide, aff. क्त, what is concealed or secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दिका|प्रच्छर्द्दिका
प्रच्छर्दिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Vomiting, sickness.<BR>E.<BR>प्र violently, छर्द to vomit, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादन|प्रच्छादनं
प्रच्छादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An upper or outer garment.<BR>2 Covering, concealing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र completely, छद to cover, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादित|प्रच्छादितं
प्रच्छादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Covered, clothed, hidden, concealed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before छद to cover, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज|प्रजः
प्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, ड aff. who is re-born in his children; see प्रजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजन|प्रजनः
प्रजन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 Impregnating, begetting.<BR>2 Impregnation or pregnancy of cattle in general.<BR>3 The season for a cow's taking the bull, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A progenitor, an impregnator.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनन|प्रजननं
प्रजनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The vulva.<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Going well or quickly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनार्थम्
प्रजनार्थम्<BR>adv. ind.<BR>For the sake of procreation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजन, and अर्थ on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिका
प्रजनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिष्णु
प्रजनिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Being born or produced.<BR>2 Producing, generating.<BR>3 Growing or standing, (as corn.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्प|प्रजल्पः
प्रजल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 Prattle, gossip.<BR>2 Talking heedlessly to a lover.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and जल्प talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजव|प्रजवः
प्रजव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Great speed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जव quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Swift, speedy.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A runner, a courier, an express.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जव speed, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजा
प्रजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 Progeny, offspring.<BR>2 People, subjects.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, aff. ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाकाम
प्रजाकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Desirous of offspring.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागर|प्रजागरः
प्रजागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Waking, watching.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जागर wakefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाता
प्रजाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman who has borne a child.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जात born, (from whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाद
प्रजाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Who or what gives offspring.<BR>2 What removes barrenness, (as a medicine, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजादान|प्रजादानं
प्रजादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा people, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाधर्म्म|प्रजाधर्म
प्रजाधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The duty of children or of subjects.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानत्|प्रजानन्त्
प्रजानत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>1 Sensible, intelligent.<BR>2 Knowing, understanding.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A sensible woman.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ज्ञा to know, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाप|प्रजापः
प्रजाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा people, subjects, and प who protects, from पा with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापति|प्रजापतिः
प्रजापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The epithet common to the ten divine personages, who were first created by BRAHMA; they are also termed Brahmādikas, and their names are MARĪCI, ATRI, AṄGIRAS, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, PRACETAS, VASIṢṬHA, BHṚGU, and NĀRADA: some authorities make the Prajāpatis only seven in number, others reduce them to three, or DAKṢA, NĀRADA, and BHṚGU, and others make them twenty-one.<BR>3 A king, a sovereign.<BR>4 A father.<BR>5 A son-in-law, a daughter's husband.<BR>6 The sun.<BR>7 Fire.<BR>8 A name of VIŚVAKARMA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा people or the world, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजायिनी
प्रजायिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A mother, or bearer of children.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जन to be born, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावत्|प्रजावन्त्
प्रजावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having progeny.<BR>2 Having subjects.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A brother's wife.<BR>2 The wife of an elder brother.<BR>3 A mother.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा offspring, and मतुप poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावृद्धि|प्रजावृद्धिः
प्रजावृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Increase of progeny.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाहित|प्रजाहितं
प्रजाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Favourable or good for children or subjects, &c. kind to them, useful to them, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा people, and हित friendly, useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजीन
प्रजीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before जि to surpass or overcome, क्त aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजीवन|प्रजीवनं
प्रजीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजुष्ट
प्रजुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Strongly attached to, devoted to, intent on.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and जुष to serve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजेश्वर|प्रजेश्वरः
प्रजेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजा subject, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञ|प्रज्ञः
प्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Wise, learned; also प्राज्ञ.<BR>2 Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart: see प्रज्ञु.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 A clever or sensible woman.<BR>2 Understanding, wisdom, knowledge.<BR>3 The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">Page561</a>] goddess of arts and eloquence, SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ज्ञा, to know, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=560" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञप्ति|प्रज्ञप्तिः
प्रज्ञप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>An appointment, an agreement, an engagement.<BR>(-प्ती)<BR>One of the Vidyā Devīs of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ज्ञा to know, causal v., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाकाय|प्रज्ञाकायः
प्रज्ञाकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A Bauddha saint; also MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रज्ञा knowledge, कै to sound, अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्
प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A name of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रज्ञा, and चक्षुस् the eye: being physically blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञात
प्रज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Famous, notorious.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञान|प्रज्ञानं
प्रज्ञान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>2 A mark, a sign, a token.<BR>E.<BR>प्र exceeding, ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावत्|प्रज्ञावन्त्
प्रज्ञावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Wise, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रज्ञा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाहीन
प्रज्ञाहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Silly, unwise, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रज्ञा, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिन्
प्रज्ञिन्<BR>m. (-ज्ञी)<BR>A sage, a scholar, a wise or learned man.<BR>E.<BR>प्रज्ञा wisdom, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञु|प्रज्ञुः
प्रज्ञु<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु)<BR>Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र separate, जानु the knee, and ज्ञु substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलित|प्रज्वलितः
प्रज्वलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blazing, radiant.<BR>2 Burnt.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying excess, ज्वलित burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वालित
प्रज्वालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lighted, kindled.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ज्वल to blaze, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रडीन|प्रडीनं
प्रडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Flying rapidly, or flying in every direction.<BR>2 Taking flight, beginning to fly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र intensitive, डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रण|प्रणः
प्रण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Old, ancient.<BR>E.<BR>प्र substituted for पुराण, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणत|प्रणतः
प्रणत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bending, bowed, stooping, inclined.<BR>2 Skilful, clever.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणतवत्
प्रणतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Bowing, bent, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow down, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणतशिरस्
प्रणतशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Inclined, stooping, having the head or top bowed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणत, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणति|प्रणतिः
प्रणति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Salutation, reverence, obeisance, courtesy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदित
प्रणदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, sounding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णद to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणमत्
प्रणमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>Bowing to, saluting with reverence or respect.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणमित
प्रणमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bending, bowing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow, क्त aff. with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणय|प्रणयः
प्रणय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Affection, friendly or fond regard.<BR>2 Acquaintance.<BR>3 Asking, begging.<BR>4 Affectionate solicitation.<BR>5 Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR>6 Trust, confidence.<BR>7 Reverence, obeisance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णी to get, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयत्
प्रणयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Leading, conducting.<BR>2 Dispensing.<BR>3 Decreeing, awarding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and णी to lead, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयन|प्रणयनं
प्रणयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Leading, conducting.<BR>2 Dispensing, distributing.<BR>3 Sentencing, awarding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णी to guide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयमान|प्रणयमानः
प्रणयमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Loverś quarrels.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणय, and मान indignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयवत्|प्रणयवन्त्
प्रणयवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Attached to, loving.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणय, and पतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविहति|प्रणयविहतिः
प्रणयविहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Denial, refusal, non-compliance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणय requiring, विहति rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिन्
प्रणयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>1 Affectionate, kind.<BR>2 Intimate, familiar.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A husband or lover.<BR>f. (-यिणी)<BR>A wife or mistress.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणय affection, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणर्त्तन
प्रणर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dancing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to dance, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणव|प्रणवः
प्रणव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The mystical name of the Deity, or syllable Om.<BR>2 A small kind of drum or tabor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णु to praise, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणवक|प्रणवकः
प्रणवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The mystical name of the Deity.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणव, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणश्यत्
प्रणश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>1 Perishing, falling away.<BR>2 Endeavouring to escape.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before नश to destroy, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणष्ट
प्रणष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Destroyed, lost, annihilated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and नष्ट destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणष्टविनय
प्रणष्टविनय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Uncivil, uncomplaisant, rude.<BR>E.<BR>प्रनष्ट, and विनय decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाद|प्रणादः
प्रणाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A loud noise, especially expressing approbation or delight, a huzza, a shout.<BR>2 A low sound expressive of great pleasure, a murmur or sigh or rapture.<BR>3 A disease of the ear, a noise or buzzing in the ear from thickening of the membranes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाम|प्रणामः
प्रणाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Respectful or reverential salutation, addressed especially to a Brahman or deity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णम to bow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाय्य|प्रणाय्यः
प्रणाय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>1 Devoid of passion or desire.<BR>2 Disobedient, disagreeing.<BR>3 Upright, straight, in rectitude.<BR>4 Beloved.<BR>E.<BR>प्र away, णी to go, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाल|प्रणालः
प्रणाल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>An issue from a pond, a drain, a watercourse.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before नल to bind, aff. घञ्; also with कन् added in the fem. form प्रणालिका (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाश|प्रणाशः
प्रणाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Loss, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णश to be destroyed, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशिन्
प्रणाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णश to be destroyed, causal v., घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिघ्नत्
प्रणिघ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्)<BR>Preparing or threatening to strike.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before हन to strike, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसित
प्रणिंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Kissed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, णिसि to kiss, क्त aff.; also read प्रनिंसित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसितव्य
प्रणिंसितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be kissed, what may or ought to be kissed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णिशि to kiss, तव्य aff.; also read प्रनिंसितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधान|प्रणिधानं
प्रणिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Great effort, stress, energy.<BR>2 Profound religious meditation.<BR>3 Access, entrance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि prefixed to धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधि|प्रणिधिः
प्रणिधि<BR>m. (-घिः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>2 Asking, solicitation or request.<BR>3 Care, attention.<BR>4 A follower.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनदत्
प्रणिनदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Sounding deep or like thunder.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before नद to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनाद|प्रणिनादः
प्रणिनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A deep sound, that of thunder or its like.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before नद to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतन|प्रणिपतनं
प्रणिपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Saluting, bowing or doing homage to.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before पत to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=561" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतित
प्रणिपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bowed down in reverence, saluting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before पत to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपत्य
प्रणिपत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having bowed down or in reverence, having saluted respectfully.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before पत to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपात|प्रणिपातः
प्रणिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Salutation, reverence, obeisance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before पत to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिहित|प्रणिहितं
प्रणिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Delivered, entrusted, consigned.<BR>2 Obtained, received, acquired.<BR>3 Acknowledged, admitted.<BR>4 Placed, fixed, deposited.<BR>5 Prudent, advised, careful, wary.<BR>6 Determined.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before धा to have, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीत|प्रणीतं|प्रणीतः
प्रणीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dressed (as food), cooked, &c.<BR>2 Made, done, constructed.<BR>3 Thrown, cast, sent.<BR>4 Entered, approached.<BR>5 Proper, fit.<BR>6 Said, declared.<BR>7 Delivered, given.<BR>8 Decreed, sentenced, awarded.<BR>9 Composed, written.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Fire, consecrated by prayers or mystical formulæ.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A vessel used at sacrifices, a sort of cup.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णी to get, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत|प्रणुतं
प्रणुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुद्
प्रणुद्<BR>mfn. (-णुत् or णुद्)<BR>Enjoining, directing, who or what commands or enjoins.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णुद् to command, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुन्न
प्रणुन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Shaken, trembling.<BR>2 Sent, dispatched.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णुद to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेय|प्रणेयः
प्रणेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Docile, submissive, agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णी to lead, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोद|प्रणोदः
प्रणोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Directing, ordering.<BR>2 Guiding, driving, (as horses.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णुद to send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदित
प्रणोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Ordered, directed.<BR>2 Driven, guided.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before णुद to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतति|प्रततिः
प्रतति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 A creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तन to spread, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतती
प्रतती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>ङीप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन|प्रतनः
प्रतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Old, ancient.<BR>E.<BR>प्र prior, with द्युल् aff. and तन् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतनु
प्रतनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु)<BR>Thin, delicate, minute.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and तनु thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कण|प्रतर्कणं
प्रतर्कण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Reasoning, discussion, doubt, logic^1.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तर्क to reason, aff. ल्युट्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतल|प्रतलं|प्रतलः
प्रतल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of the seven principal divisions of the lower regions.<BR>E.<BR>प्र exceeding, तल lowness, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतान|प्रतानः
प्रतान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 A low spreading creeper.<BR>3 A disease, fainting, epilepsy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तन to spread, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानिन्
प्रतानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Spreading, extending.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A spreading, creeper.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तन to spread, aff. ल्युट्, and इनि and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रताप|प्रतापः
प्रताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Majesty, dignity, the possession of rank and power.<BR>2 Spirit, energy.<BR>3 Splendour, brilliancy.<BR>4 Heat.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तप to shine, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापन|प्रतापनं|प्रतापनः
प्रतापन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A hell.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Inflicting pain or punishment, burning, consuming.<BR>2 Paining, distressing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तप to heat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापवत्|प्रतापवन्त्
प्रतापवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत)<BR>Majestick, glorious.<BR>E.<BR>प्रताप, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापस|प्रतापसः
प्रतापस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A species of gigantic Asclepias, with white flowers.<BR>E.<BR>प्रताप heat, षो to destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापिन्
प्रतापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>1 Shining, splendid.<BR>2 Dignified, powerful.<BR>3 Burning.<BR>4 Distressing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रताप, and इति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रताम्
प्रताम्<BR>mfn. (-तान्)<BR>1 Desiring.<BR>2 Being afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तम to desire, क्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतार|प्रतारः
प्रतार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Crossing over.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तॄ to cross, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारक|प्रतारकः
प्रतारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cheat.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तॄ to cross, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारण|प्रतारणं
प्रतारण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Fraud, cheating, deceit, overreaching, trick.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तॄ to cross, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारित|प्रतारितः
प्रतारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cheated, deceived, tricked.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तॄ to pass over, (to overreach,) aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix, implying,<BR>1 Substitution, (instead, in lieu); as प्रद्युम्नःकेशवातप्रति.<BR>2 Several order, (severally, each by each); as वृक्षं प्रति षिञ्चति; प्रतिवेदं each Vedā; प्रतिदिनं every day; प्रतिछिद्रं each opening; प्रतिगर्भं every birth; प्रत्येक one by one.<BR>3 Direction, designation, (to, towards, upon); as वृक्षं प्रति विद्योतते विद्युत्.<BR>4 Belonging to, (as a part or portion.)<BR>5 Exchange, return, (again, back again, re) तिलेभ्यः प्रति माषान् यच्छति.<BR>6 A little, &c. as शाकप्रति, सूपप्रति.<BR>7 Opposition in place, as प्रतिसूर्य्यं against the sun, प्रतिवात against the wind.<BR>8 With respect to, अनेकभार्य्यं, प्रत्याह.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, डति aff.; in the following compounds the final इ of प्रति is optionally long, before derivatives formed with घञ्, as प्रतिहार or प्रतीहार, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक|प्रतिकः
प्रतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Worth sixteen Pans of Cowries.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति substituted for कार्षापण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्म्मन्|प्रतिकर्मन्
प्रतिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 Dress, decoration, personal embellishment.<BR>2 Retaliation, requital.<BR>3 Remedy, redress.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति belonging to (the body), and कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकाय|प्रतिकायः
प्रतिकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A butt, a mark; the effigy of a man, for archers to practise at.<BR>2 An effigy, an image, a picture.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, and काय the body; a repetition or reflection of the form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकार|प्रतिकारः
प्रतिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Revenge, retaliation.<BR>2 Remedying, counteracting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, against, and कार making; also प्रतीकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकाश|प्रतिकाशः
प्रतिकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Like, resembling, (used in composition.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति to or again, and काश or कास what shines; also प्रतिकास, प्रतीकास, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकास|प्रतिकासः
प्रतिकास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Like, (in composition): see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकुञ्चित|प्रतिकुंचित
प्रतिकुञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, curved.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and कुचि to be curved, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूप|प्रतिकूपः
प्रतिकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A moat, a ditch.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति implying little, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूल|प्रतिकूलं
प्रतिकूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Contrary, adverse, cross-grained, reverse, inverted.<BR>2 Contradictory, cross, perverse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति for प्रतीप averted, and कूल a bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलता
प्रतिकूलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Opposition, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिकूल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, प्रतिकूलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृत
प्रतिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Requited, returned.<BR>2 Counteracted.<BR>3 Remedred.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृति|प्रतिकृतिः
प्रतिकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 An effigy, a figure, an image, a picture, a reflection, a shadow, a reflected image.<BR>2 Retaliation, return, revenge.<BR>3 A substitute.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, &c. and कृति making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=562" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृष्ट|प्रतिकृष्टं
प्रतिकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Inferior, low, vile.<BR>2 Twice ploughed, or ploughed back again.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, and कृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रिया
प्रतिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Return, requital.<BR>2 Retaliation.<BR>3 Remedying, counteracting.<BR>4 Embellishment, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षण|प्रतिक्षणं
प्रतिक्षण<BR>adv. n. (-णं)<BR>Momentarily, every moment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति several order, and क्षण an instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षय|प्रतिक्षयः
प्रतिक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A guard, an attendant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, क्षय injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षिप्त|प्रतिक्षिप्तः
प्रतिक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं).<BR>1 Dismissed, rejected, turned away.<BR>2 Sent, dispatched.<BR>3 Opposed, repelled, resisted.<BR>4 Abused, reviled.<BR>5 Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, against, and क्षिप्त thrown, sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षुत|प्रतिक्षुतं
प्रतिक्षुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sneezing, wheezing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति repeatedly, क्षुत sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगत|प्रतिगतं
प्रतिगत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Flying backwards and forwards, wheeling in flight.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति repetition, and गत gone; going and coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्जत्|प्रतिगर्ज्जत्
प्रतिगर्जत्<BR>mfn. (-र्ज्जन्-र्ज्जन्ती-र्ज्जत्)<BR>Echoing, reverberating.<BR>2 Murmuring or rebelling.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before गर्ज्ज to growl, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगिरि|प्रतिगिरिः
प्रतिगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Any inferior mountain, or any thing like a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and गिरि a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृहीत
प्रतिगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken, accepted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, ग्रह to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृहीतृ
प्रतिगृहीतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who takes or accepts, an accepter, a receiver.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before गृह to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृह्य
प्रतिगृह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be taken, what may be accepted, &c.<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having taken.<BR>2 Bringing up the rear.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and ग्रह to take, क्यप् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रह|प्रतिग्रहः
प्रतिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Acceptance, assent.<BR>2 Proper donation to Brahmans, whatever is a fit present to a Brahman at suitable periods.<BR>3 The acceptance of such a gift.<BR>4 A spitting pot.<BR>5 The reserve of an army, a detachment posted with the general four hundred yards in the rear of the line.<BR>6 The sun near the moon's node.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, &c. and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहण|प्रतिग्रहणं
प्रतिग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Receiving presents.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहणीय
प्रतिग्रहणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taken or accepted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, ग्रह to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राह|प्रतिग्राहः
प्रतिग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A spitting pot.<BR>2 Accepting gifts.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ग्रह to take, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राह्य
प्रतिग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be accepted or taken.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and ग्रह to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ|प्रतिघः
प्रतिघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Adverse, inimical.<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 Wrath, rage.<BR>2 Mutual beating, combat, fighting.<BR>3 Fainting.<BR>4 An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, severally, and घ striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघात|प्रतिघातः
प्रतिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A return blow, repulse, rebound.<BR>2 Warding off a blow.<BR>3 Preventing, prohibiting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हन to kill, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातन|प्रतिघातनं
प्रतिघातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति mutually, हन to kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातिन्
प्रतिघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Repelling, repulsing.<BR>2 Hostile, opposed to.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिघात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ्न|प्रतिघ्नं
प्रतिघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ्नत्
प्रतिघ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्)<BR>1 Opposing, impeding.<BR>2 Destructive.<BR>3 Hostile.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हन to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिचिन्तन|प्रतिचिंतन|प्रतिचिंतनं
प्रतिचिन्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Thinking repeatedly, considering, meditating upon.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and चिति to think, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छन्द|प्रतिच्छंद|प्रतिच्छंदः|प्रतिच्छन्दः|प्रतिछन्द
प्रतिच्छन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A reflected image, any image, a picture, a statue.<BR>2 A substitute.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, छदि to cover, aff. अच्; also with कन् added प्रतिछन्दक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिछाया|प्रतिच्छाया
प्रतिछाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 An image, a statue, a bas-relief, a picture.<BR>2 A reflected image, a shade or shadow.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, छाया a shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिछेद|प्रतिच्छेद|प्रतिच्छेदः
प्रतिछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Opposition, resistance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजङ्घा|प्रतिजंघा
प्रतिजङ्घा<BR>f. (-ङ्घा)<BR>The fore part of the thigh.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before, and जङ्घा the thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजल्पक|प्रतिजल्पकः
प्रतिजल्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Reply in assent, respectful concurrence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and जल्पक talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजागर|प्रतिजागरः
प्रतिजागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Attention, watchfulness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति towards, and जागर watchful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजिह्वा
प्रतिजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>The uvula, or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, or like, जिह्वा the tongue; also with कन् added in the fem. form, प्रतिजिह्विका (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजीवन|प्रतिजीवनं
प्रतिजीवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Resuscitation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 Promise, agreement, engagement, assent.<BR>2 Admission, acknowledgment.<BR>3 (In logic,) The proposition, the assertion to be proved.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति mutually, ज्ञा to know, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञात|प्रतिज्ञातं
प्रतिज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Promised, agreed.<BR>2 Admitted, acknowledged.<BR>3 Propounded, asserted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति mutually, ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञातव्य
प्रतिज्ञातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be promised.<BR>2 To be assented to.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ज्ञा to know, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञान|प्रतिज्ञानं
प्रतिज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Promise, agreement, assent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञान्तर
प्रतिज्ञान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A subsequent proposition on failure of the first, (in logic.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापचक
प्रतिज्ञापचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bond, a written contract.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा agreement, and पच a leaf, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाय
प्रतिज्ञाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having promised.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before, ज्ञा to know, ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविरोध|प्रतिज्ञाविरोधः
प्रतिज्ञाविरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Denial of a logical proposition.<BR>2 Acting contrary to promise or agreement.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and विरोध opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित
प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Promised in marriage, betrothed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and विवाहित married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञासन्न्यास|प्रतिज्ञासंन्यास|प्रतिज्ञासंन्यासः
प्रतिज्ञासन्न्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A bandonment of the original proposition, (in logic.)<BR>2 Breaking a promise.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and सन्न्यास quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाहानि
प्रतिज्ञाहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Giving up the argument.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and हाति abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञेय|प्रतिज्ञेयः
प्रतिज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be promised or accepted.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The reciter or pronouncer of a panegyric, the proclaimer of rank and titles, a herald, a bard, a panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ज्ञा to know, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितत्त्वसिद्धान्त
प्रतितत्त्वसिद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Conclusion or notion adopted by each disputant severally.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, तत्त्व truth, and सिद्धान्त conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितन्त्र
प्रतितन्त्र<BR>adv. n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 According to each Tantra.<BR>2 According to each opinion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and तन्त्र a doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=563" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिताल|प्रतितालः
प्रतिताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of air or melody.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The key of a door or padlock, or an instrument to open a door.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति relating to, ताल tune, or a lock, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदान|प्रतिदानं
प्रतिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The return or re-delivery of a deposit.<BR>2 Barter, exchange.<BR>3 Giving back or in return for.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, दानं a giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदारण|प्रतिदारणं
प्रतिदारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति reciprocally, and दारण tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिन|प्रतिदिनं
प्रतिदिन<BR>adv. n. (-नं)<BR>Every day, day by day.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिवन्
प्रतिदिवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A day.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, दिव to shine, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्; also with the vowel lengthened, प्रतिदीवन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिशं
प्रतिदिशं<BR>adv. n. (-शं)<BR>Every where, all around.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and दिश a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदेय|प्रतिदेयं
प्रतिदेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be returned, to be given back, or as an equivalent.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A pledge, a pawn.<BR>2 An article purchased and given back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिद्वन्द्व|प्रतिद्वंद्व|प्रतिद्वन्द्वः
प्रतिद्वन्द्व<BR>n. (-न्द्वं)<BR>Opposition, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, द्वन्द्व a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिद्वन्द्विन्|प्रतिद्वंद्विन्
प्रतिद्वन्द्विन्<BR>mfn. (-न्द्वी-न्द्विनी-न्द्वि)<BR>Hostile, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिद्वन्द्व, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वनि|प्रतिध्वनिः
प्रतिध्वनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Echo, an echo.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वान|प्रतिध्वानं|प्रतिध्वानः
प्रतिध्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Echo, reiterated or repeated sound.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, ध्वान sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनप्तृ
प्रतिनप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>A great grandson, a son's grandson.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, repeated, and नप्तृ a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनव|प्रतिनवं
प्रतिनव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>New, young, fresh, recent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति intensitive prefix, and नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाद|प्रतिनादः
प्रतिनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Echo, resonance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादित
प्रतिनादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Echoing, re-sounding.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिनाद, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधि|प्रतिनिधिः
प्रतिनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 A resemblance of a real form, an image, a statue, a picture, &c.<BR>2 A surety.<BR>3 A substitute.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, धा to have, with नि prefix, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिनद|प्रतिनिनदः
प्रतिनिनद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An echo, a reverberation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and निनद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवर्त्तन|प्रतिनिवर्तन|प्रतिनिवर्तनं
प्रतिनिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Turning back or away from.<BR>2 Returning.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and नि before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवृत्त
प्रतिनिवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Turned away from, desisted from, leaving, withdrawn from.<BR>2 Come back, returned.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and नि before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिश
प्रतिनिश<BR>adv. n. (-शं)<BR>By night, every night.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and निशा a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप|प्रतिपः
प्रतिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king of the lunar race, father of ŚANTANU, and grandfather of BHĪṢMA; also प्रतीप.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, and प who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्ष|प्रतिपक्षः
प्रतिपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 A respondent, an opponent.<BR>3 A defendant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, and पक्ष a part, a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्ति|प्रतिपत्तिः
प्रतिपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Fame, reputation.<BR>2 Gaining, getting, obtaining, acquirement.<BR>3 Action, worldly practice or activity, as opposed to religious contemplation.<BR>4 Use, application, profit.<BR>5 Arrogance, audacity, confidence.<BR>6 Knowledge, determination, ascertainment.<BR>7 Elevation, exaltation, promotion, acquirement of rank or dignity.<BR>8 Acknowledgment, assent, admission.<BR>9 Inspiring trust or confidence, satisfying, shewing in proof.<BR>10 Respectful or affectionate behaviour to.<BR>11 Purpose, design.<BR>12 Comprehending, including.<BR>13 Distribution, disposal.<BR>14 Giving, presentation.<BR>15 Blinding, misleading, deceiving.<BR>16 Throwing Ghee on the fire, or images into a sacred stream, or any similar rite from which no advantage is expected.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally or towards, &c. पद to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपटह|प्रतिपत्तिपटहः
प्रतिपत्तिपटह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A large drum; the state drum allowed only to chiefs of a certain rank.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपत्ति celebrity, and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिमत्|प्रतिपत्तिमन्त्
प्रतिपत्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Active, prompt.<BR>2 Celebrated.<BR>3 High in rank.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपत्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख
प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Obstinate, unyielding.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपत्ति, and पराङ्मुख averse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तूर्य्य|प्रतिपत्तूर्य|प्रतिपत्तूर्य्यं
प्रतिपत्तूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपट् rank, and तूर्य्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद्<BR>f. (-पद् or पत्)<BR>1 The first day of a lunar fortnight, the first of the moon's increase or wane.<BR>2 Understanding, intellect.<BR>3 Rank, consequence.<BR>4 A kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, पद to go, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद
प्रतिपद<BR>ind. or n. adv. (-दं)<BR>Step by step, at each step.<BR>2 Continually, every moment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पद step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपन्न|प्रतिपन्नं
प्रतिपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Known, understood, ascertained, determined.<BR>2 Promised, engaged, assented to, accepted.<BR>3 Overcome, conquered, subdued.<BR>4 Obtained, gained.<BR>5 Done, effected, accomplished.<BR>6 Undertaken.<BR>7 Replied.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, and पद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाण|प्रतिपाणः
प्रतिपाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Stake, gage, the thing played for.<BR>2 A counter pledge, the thing staked against another.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पण to have price, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादक|प्रतिपादकः
प्रतिपादक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What produces effects, causes, &c.<BR>2 Explanatory.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पद to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादन|प्रतिपादनं
प्रतिपादन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Ascertaining, determining, rendering clear or intelligible.<BR>3 Action, worldly conduct or interest.<BR>4 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>5 Producing, causing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, and पद to go, causal v., aff, ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादित
प्रतिपादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Delivered, given.<BR>2 Caused.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before पद to go, causal form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादुक
प्रतिपादुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Determining, ascertaining.<BR>2 Making manifest or clear.<BR>3 What causes or effects.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before पद to go, causal v., उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालक|प्रतिपालकः
प्रतिपालक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what protects or defends.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 A protector.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before पाल to protect, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालन|प्रतिपालनं
प्रतिपालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Protecting, defending, cherishing.<BR>2 Following, practising.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पाल to cherish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालनीय
प्रतिपालनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be cherished or protected.<BR>2 To be observed or followed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पाल to cherish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालित
प्रतिपालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cherished, protected.<BR>2 Practised, followed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before पाल to cherish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=564" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाल्य|प्रतिपाल्यं
प्रतिपाल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>To be cherished or protected.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before, पाल to cherish, यत् aff.; also प्रतिपालितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपुरुष|प्रतिपुरुषः
प्रतिपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A deputy, a substitute.<BR>n. adv. (-षं)<BR>Every man, man by man.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजक
प्रतिपूजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A reverer, one who does homage.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पूजक who worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजन|प्रतिपूजनं
प्रतिपूजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Exchange of civilities, mutual obeisance or reverence.<BR>2 Offering homage or respect.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पूजन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजित
प्रतिपूजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Treated with reverence or respect.<BR>2 Exchanged as civilities.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पूजित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूज्य
प्रतिपूज्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having offered homage to.<BR>2 Having exchanged respectful salutations.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and पूज to worship, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रयाण|प्रतिप्रयाणं
प्रतिप्रयाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Return, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and प्रयाण who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसव|प्रतिप्रसवः
प्रतिप्रसव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Precept for an act which under other circumstances is forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and प्रसव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसूत|प्रतिप्रसूतः
प्रतिप्रसूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Re-enjoined, after having been forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and प्रसूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफल|प्रतिफलं|प्रतिफलः
प्रतिफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 An image, a shadow, a reflection.<BR>2 Return, requital, retaliation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलन|प्रतिफलनं
प्रतिफलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A reflected image.<BR>2 Requital, return.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and फल to bear fruit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलित|प्रतिफलितं
प्रतिफलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Represented, reflected, shadowed.<BR>2 Requited, returned.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and फल to bear fruit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफुल्लक|प्रतिफुल्लकः
प्रतिफुल्लक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Flowered, having flowers.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, फुल्ल blown, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबद्ध|प्रतिबद्धः
प्रतिबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Disappointed, thwarted, crossed, vexed.<BR>2 Obstructed, opposed, prevented.<BR>3 Set, inlaid.<BR>4 Bound.<BR>5 Connected with.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबधक
प्रतिबधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An opposer, an injurer.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, बध to kill, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्ध|प्रतिबंध|प्रतिबंधः|प्रतिबन्धः
प्रतिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>2 Disappointment.<BR>2 Connexion.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबंधक|प्रतिबन्धकः
प्रतिबन्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Impeding, obstructing, an obstructor or opposer.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A branch, a shoot.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An impediment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिबन्ध obstacle, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धकारिन्
प्रतिबन्धकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Who or what hinders, obstructs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिबन्ध, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धन|प्रतिबंधन|प्रतिबंधनं
प्रतिबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Obstructing, impeding.<BR>2 Binding, confinement.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and बन्ध to bind, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धि|प्रतिबंधिः|प्रतिबन्धिः
प्रतिबन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>Contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and बन्ध to bind, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबल|प्रतिबलः
प्रतिबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Able, adequate, powerful.<BR>2 Of equal strength.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति intensitive prefix, and बल strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्ध
प्रतिबुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Exalted, rendered prosperous or great.<BR>2 Known, celebrated.<BR>2 Wakened, awake.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and बुध to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोध|प्रतिबोधः
प्रतिबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Waking, awaking.<BR>2 Instructing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before बुध to know, घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट्, प्रतिबोधन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधित
प्रतिबोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Instructed, taught.<BR>2 Awakened.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and बोधित taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभणित
प्रतिभणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Answered, replied.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and भणित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभय|प्रतिभयं
प्रतिभय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Formidable, fearful, frightful.<BR>n. (-य)<BR>Fear.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति completely, and भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Understanding, intellect, especially as opening or expanding.<BR>2 Sharpness, brilliancy of conception.<BR>3 Light, splendor.<BR>4 Reflected light.<BR>5 Audacity, boldness, confidence, consequence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before भा to shine, affs. ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाग|प्रतिभागः
प्रतिभाग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A share of small articles, as fruit, flowers, &c. paid daily to the Raja for household expenditure.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and भाग a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान|प्रतिभानं
प्रतिभान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Boldness, audacity.<BR>2 Brilliancy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before भा to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानवत्|प्रतिभानवन्त्
प्रतिभानवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Bold, prompt, audacious.<BR>2 Bright, brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभान, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान्वित|प्रतिभान्वितः
प्रतिभान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Confident, bold, audacious.<BR>2 Acquiring knowledge or experience.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभा confidence, अन्वित joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभामुख|प्रतिभामुखः
प्रतिभामुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Confident, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभा consequence, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाव|प्रतिभावः
प्रतिभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Corresponding character or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and माव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावत्|प्रतिभावन्त्
प्रतिभावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Confident, bold.<BR>2 Knowing, shrewd.<BR>3 Bright, luminous.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभा light, lustre, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाववत्
प्रतिभाववत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Social.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभाव, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाहानि|प्रतिभाहानिः
प्रतिभाहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Loss or absence of knowledge, want of sense.<BR>2 Dulness, darkness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभा knowledge, and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिन्न
प्रतिभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Separated, divided.<BR>2 Pierced.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before भिद to break, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभू
प्रतिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A surety.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति implying substitution, भू to be, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदन|प्रतिभेदनं
प्रतिभेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Piercing, cutting, penetrating.<BR>2 Separating, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before भिद to break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिम|प्रतिमः
प्रतिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Like, resembling, (in composition.)<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A resemblance, a figure, an image, a picture.<BR>2 An idol.<BR>3 The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, मा to measure, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमता
प्रतिमता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Reflection, image, shadow.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिम, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, प्रतिमत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमान|प्रतिमानं
प्रतिमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Resemblance, an image, a picture.<BR>2 An idol.<BR>3 The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before मा to measure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमानभाग
प्रतिमानभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिमान, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमार्ग्गक|प्रतिमार्गक|प्रतिमार्गकः
प्रतिमार्ग्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति contrary, मार्ग a road, and कन् aff., having come back part of the way to earth, after being raised to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमाला
प्रतिमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An exercise analogous to capping verses, reciting verse for verse, as a trial of memory or skill.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुक्त|प्रतिमुक्तः
प्रतिमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Clothed, armed, accoutred.<BR>2 Thrown mutually or at one another.<BR>3 Loosed or liberated repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, मुच to loosen, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=565" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुख
प्रतिमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>(In dramatic composition), A secondary plot or incident, calculated either to promote or obstruct the catastrophe.<BR>adv. n. (-खं)<BR>In front, before, in presence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुखागत
प्रतिमुखागत<BR>m. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Come before, or in front of.<BR>2 Run against.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिमुख, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमेन्दु
प्रतिमेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>The image, reflection or resemblance of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिमा, and इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमूषिका
प्रतिमूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्न|प्रतियत्नः
प्रतियत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Active, vigorous, diligent, making effort or exertion.<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>1 Desire, wish.<BR>2 Taking prisoner, making captive.<BR>3 Comprehension.<BR>4 Acting well or properly.<BR>5 Acquiring a new virtue or accomplishment.<BR>6 Making complete or perfect.<BR>7 A making or preparing.<BR>8 Retaliating, recrimination, revenge.<BR>9 Opposition, counteraction.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति much or against, and यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातना
प्रतियातना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A resemblance of real forms, a picture, a statue, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, यातना an applying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोग|प्रतियोगः
प्रतियोग<BR>m. (-गं)<BR>1 Opposition, contradiction, controversy.<BR>2 Cooperation, association.<BR>3 Existing, as the counterpart of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, युज् to join, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिता
प्रतियोगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Mutual co-operation.<BR>2 Opposition.<BR>3 Existence as a counterpart.<BR>4 Dependant existence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतियोगिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिन्
प्रतियोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Who or what impedes or opposes.<BR>2 What co-operates with.<BR>m. (गी)<BR>1 An opponent.<BR>2 A partner, an associate.<BR>3 A counterpart.<BR>4 Any thing or object dependant upon another and not existing without it.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतियोग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षण|प्रतिरक्षणं
प्रतिरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Preserving.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and रक्षण keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरम्भ|प्रतिरंभ|प्रतिरंभः|प्रतिरम्भः
प्रतिरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Passion, rage, violent or passionate abuse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before रभि to sound, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिराच
प्रतिराच<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Every night.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति repeatedly, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुद्ध
प्रतिरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Impeded, hindered.<BR>2 Obstructed, opposed.<BR>3 Surrounded, invested, blockaded.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before रुध to oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुरूषु
प्रतिरुरूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to speak or tell.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and रु to cry, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरूप|प्रतिरूपं
प्रतिरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A picture, an image, the counterpart of any real form.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, रूप form; also with कन् added, प्रतिरूपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोद्धृ
प्रतिरोद्धृ<BR>mfn. (-द्धा-द्धी-द्धृ)<BR>Who or what opposes, hinders, prevents, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before रूध to obstruct, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोध|प्रतिरोधः
प्रतिरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Opposition, impediment.<BR>2 An opponent.<BR>3 Concealing, hiding.<BR>4 Siege, blockade.<BR>5 Theft.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before रुध to oppose, and घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट्, प्रतिरोधन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधक|प्रतिरोधकः
प्रतिरोधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A thief, a robber.<BR>2 An obstacle.<BR>3 An opponent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, रुध to obstruct, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधिन्
प्रतिरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Who or what obstructs, opposes, impedes, controverts, &c.<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>1 A thief, a robber.<BR>2 An opponent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, रुध to hinder, aff. धिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलम्भ|प्रतिलंभः|प्रतिलम्भः
प्रतिलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Obtaining, getting.<BR>2 Censure, reviling, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before लभि to sound, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. प्रतिलम्भित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोम|प्रतिलोमः
प्रतिलोम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Left, not right.<BR>2 Reverse, inverted, contrary to the natural course or order, against the hair or grain.<BR>3 Low, vile, base, depraved.<BR>4 In law, contrary to caste.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति reverting, and लोमन् hair of the body, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोमज|प्रतिलोमजः
प्रतिलोमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born in the inverse order of the classes, as of a Kṣatriya father and Brahman mother, of a Vaiśya father and Kṣatriya or Brahman mother, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिलोम, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचन|प्रतिवचनं
प्रतिवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A reply, an answer, a rejoinder.<BR>2 An echo.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, back again, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचस्
प्रतिवचस्<BR>n. (-चः)<BR>1 An answer, a reply.<BR>2 An echo.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, and वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवसथ|प्रतिवसथः
प्रतिवसथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A village.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before वस to abide, अथच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्य|प्रतिवाक्यं
प्रतिवाक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Answerable, admitting or requiring an answer.<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>A reply, an answer.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before वाक्य a speech, or वाक् speech, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाच्
प्रतिवाच्<BR>f. (-वाक्)<BR>An answer, a reply.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाणि|प्रतिवाणिः
प्रतिवाणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 An answer.<BR>2 A rejoinder.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before वाणि speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवात|प्रतिवातः
प्रतिवात<BR>n. adv. (-तं)<BR>To leeward, against the wind.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाप|प्रतिवापः
प्रतिवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Addition of substances to medicines, either during or after decoction.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and वप to sow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादिन्
प्रतिवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A defendant, a respondent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासर|प्रतिवासरः
प्रतिवासर<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Day by day.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, and वासर a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासिन्
प्रतिवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>A neighbour, neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति near, about, and वासिन् who resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधान|प्रतिविधानं
प्रतिविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Arrangement, array.<BR>2 Subsidiary, or substituted ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and विधान precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविम्ब|प्रतिविंब|प्रतिविम्बं|प्रतिविम्बः
प्रतिविम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A resemblance or counterpart of real forms, as a picture, an image, a shadow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति back again, and विम्ब an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविम्बात
प्रतिविम्बात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिविम्ब, अत what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविषा
प्रतिविषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, commonly Ataich or Atis, (Betula.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, and विष venom; an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविष्णु
प्रतिविष्णु<BR>ind. (-ष्णु)<BR>To or in place of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and विष्णु, the deity so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविहित
प्रतिविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Arranged, arrayed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and वि before धा to have, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश|प्रतिवेशः
प्रतिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The residence of a neighbour, a neighbouring house or neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, विश to enter, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशवासिन्
प्रतिवेशवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Neighbouring, a neighbour.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिवेश, and वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशिन्
प्रतिवेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>A neighbour, neighbouring.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिवेश neighbourhood, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशङ्कनीय
प्रतिशङ्कनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be ever held in fear or doubt.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and शङ्कनीय to be apprehended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशङ्का
प्रतिशङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>Constant fear or doubt.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशासन|प्रतिशासनं
प्रतिशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sending a servant on a message, ordering or dispatching an inferior after calling him to attend.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, शासन ruling; also प्रतिशास्ति f. (-स्तिः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=566" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशिष्ट|प्रतिशिष्टं
प्रतिशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Celebrated, famous.<BR>2 Sent, ordered, dispatched.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति intensitive, and शिष्ट celebrated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशीन
प्रतिशीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Melted, fluid, dropping, oozing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्यै to drop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्या
प्रतिश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>Catarrh.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्यै to go, to run, affixes अङ् and टाप्; also प्रतिश्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्याय|प्रतिश्यायः
प्रतिश्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Catarrh.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्यै to go, to drop, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रय|प्रतिश्रयः
प्रतिश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An assembly.<BR>2 A house, a dwelling.<BR>3 An asylum, a place of refuge.<BR>4 A place of sacrifice, the room or building where the sacrifice is performed.<BR>5 A place where food, &c. is given away.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति completely, श्री to serve, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रव|प्रतिश्रवः
प्रतिश्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Promise, assent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्रु to hear, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवण|प्रतिश्रवणं
प्रतिश्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Assenting to, listening to, with attention and obedience.<BR>2 Promising.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, श्रु to hear, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत्
प्रतिश्रुत्<BR>f. (-श्रुत्)<BR>1 Repeated sound, echo.<BR>2 Promise.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्रु to hear, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत|प्रतिश्रुतः
प्रतिश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Promised, assented, agreed, accepted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति mutually, श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्ध|प्रतिषिद्धः
प्रतिषिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Forbidden, prohibited.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against सिद्ध granted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्धसेवन
प्रतिषिद्धसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Doing what is prohibited.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिषिद्ध, and सेवन following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्धसेविन्
प्रतिषिद्धसेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Following or doing what is forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिसिद्ध, and सेविन् who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेद्धृ
प्रतिषेद्धृ<BR>mfn. (-द्धा-द्धी-द्धृ)<BR>A prohibitor or prohibitive, prohibiting or forbidding.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सिद्ध to make complete, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेध|प्रतिषेधः
प्रतिषेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Prohibition, forbidding, exception, contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सिद्व to be perfect, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधक|प्रतिषेधकः
प्रतिषेधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what forbids, preventive, prohibitive.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सिध to complete, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधन|प्रतिषेधनं
प्रतिषेधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Prohibiting, inhibition.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, सिद्भ to complete, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्क|प्रतिष्कः
प्रतिष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>A spy, an emissary.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before कष to strike, aff. ड, and सुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कश|प्रतिष्कशः
प्रतिष्कश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary, a Hurkaru.<BR>2 A companion.<BR>3 A leader, a preceder.<BR>4 A whip, a leather thong.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before कश to hurt or kill, अच् and सुट् augment; if it is used attributively to imply the application of a whip, the augment is not inserted, as प्रतिकशाश्वः a horse that is whipped on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कष|प्रतिष्कषः
प्रतिष्कष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A whip, a leather thong.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before कष to hurt, aff. अच् and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कस|प्रतिष्कसः
प्रतिष्कस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A spy, a messenger, an emissary.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before कस to go, aff. अच् and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टब्ध
प्रतिष्टब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Obstructed, impeded, stopped.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ष्टभि to hinder, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टम्भ|प्रतिष्टंभ|प्रतिष्टंभः|प्रतिष्टम्भः
प्रतिष्टम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Obstacle, impediment, opposition.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ष्टभि to hinder, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठ|प्रतिष्ठः
प्रतिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Famous.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 Fame, celebrity.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 The accomplishment of a religious ceremony or any set of rites, especially those instituted for the attainment of supernatural and magical powers.<BR>4 A form of metre, consisting of a stanza of four lines, of four syllables each: it is also applied to a form of the Gāyatrī, being a triplet of 8, 7, and 6 syllable lines, making altogether 21 syllables.<BR>5 Place, site.<BR>6 Staying, standing, fixation.<BR>7 Limit, boundary.<BR>8 Accomplishment, completion, (in general.)<BR>9 Consecration of a monument erected in honour of a deity, or of the image of a deity.<BR>10 Endowment of a temple, portioning or marrying a daughter, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The father of SUPĀRŚVA, the seventh Jaina pontiff.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before स्था to stay or stand, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठान|प्रतिष्ठानं
प्रतिष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Site, situation.<BR>2 Celebrity.<BR>3 The capital of the early kings of the lunar dynasty, opposite to Allahabad.<BR>4 The capital of SĀLIVĀHANA in the Dekhin.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापन|प्रतिष्ठापनं
प्रतिष्ठापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fixing, placing, locating.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापित
प्रतिष्ठापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set up, located, fixed, erected.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before स्था to stay, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठासु
प्रतिष्ठासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Wishing or intending to stay or remain.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिं before स्था to stay, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठित|प्रतिष्ठितः
प्रतिष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated.<BR>2 Completed, finished.<BR>3 Consecrated.<BR>4 Endowed, portioned.<BR>5 Established in life, married, &c.<BR>6 Placed, situated.<BR>7 Established, fixed.<BR>8 Applicable or applied to.<BR>9 Comprised or included in.<BR>10 Prized, valued.<BR>11 Secured, acquired.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिष्ठा as above, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्णात
प्रतिष्णात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pure, (as a thread.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ष्णा to bathe, क्त aff., in any other sense प्रतिस्नात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहार|प्रतिसंहारः
प्रतिसंहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Compression, diminution.<BR>2 Comprehension.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and सम् before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृत
प्रतिसंहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Comprehended, included.<BR>2 Compressed, reduced in bulk.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and संहृत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसन्धान|प्रतिसंधान|प्रतिसंधानं
प्रतिसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Self-command, suppression of feeling for a time.<BR>3 Praise, panegyrick.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and सम् before धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमाधान|प्रतिसमाधानं
प्रतिसमाधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A remedy, a cure.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, सम and आङ् before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर|प्रतिसरः
प्रतिसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>A servant, servile, dependant.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The rear of an army.<BR>2 A garland, a wreath.<BR>3 A bracelet.<BR>4 Cicatrizing or healing, as a sore.<BR>5 A form of magic or incantation.<BR>6 Daybreak, morning.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 A string worn round the hand at nuptials, &c.<BR>2 Ornament, adorning.<BR>3 The junction of the frontal sinuses of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सृ to go, aff. अप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर्ग|प्रतिसर्गः
प्रतिसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 The portion of a Purāṇa, which treats of the destruction and renovation of the world.<BR>2 Secondary creation, or the creation of the world by the agency of BRAHMĀ, and other divine beings regarded as the agents of one Supreme Being.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, सर्ग going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसव्य|प्रतिसव्यं
प्रतिसव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Inverted, reverse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति intensitive, and सव्य the left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसान्धानिक|प्रतिसांधानिक|प्रतिसांधानिकः|प्रतिसान्धानिकः
प्रतिसान्धानिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bard, a panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिसन्धान praise, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=567" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारण|प्रतिसारणं
प्रतिसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Repelling, repulsion.<BR>2 Applying remedies to a wound.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, सृ to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारित
प्रतिसारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Repelled, repulsed.<BR>2 Dressed, as a wound.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसीरा
प्रतिसीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>An outer tent, a screen or wall of cloth.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before षिञ् to bind, affs. रक् and टाप्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्य्य|प्रतिसूर्य|प्रतिसूर्यः|प्रतिसूर्य्यः
प्रतिसूर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>n. adv. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Opposite to the sun.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सूर्य्य the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्य्यक|प्रतिसूर्यक|प्रतिसूर्यकः|प्रतिसूर्य्यकः
प्रतिसूर्य्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>2 The sun's disk.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before or about, सूर्य्य the sun, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृष्ट|प्रतिसृष्टः
प्रतिसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Sent, dispatched.<BR>2 Celebrated.<BR>3 Given.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before सृज to create, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्कन्ध
प्रतिस्कन्ध<BR>n. adv. (-न्धं)<BR>Upon the shoulders.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नात
प्रतिस्नात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bathed, washed. प्रति before ष्णा to bathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पन्दन|प्रतिस्पंदन|प्रतिस्पंदनं
प्रतिस्पन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Throbbing, vibration.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and स्पन्दन throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्द्धा
प्रतिस्पर्द्धा<BR>f. (-र्द्धा)<BR>Emulation, rivalry, the wish or effort to excel or overcome.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति definitive prefix, and स्पर्द्धा emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्द्धिन्
प्रतिस्पर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>1 Envious, emulous, a rival.<BR>2 Refractory, rebellious.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिस्पर्द्धा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्याय
प्रतिस्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Catarrh.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before श्यै to drop, aff. अच्; see प्रतिश्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्रोतस्
प्रतिस्रोतस्<BR>n. adv.<BR>Against the stream.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and स्रोतस् current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहत|प्रतिहतः
प्रतिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Disappointed.<BR>2 Opposed, obstructed.<BR>3 Fallen, overthrown.<BR>4 Sent, dispatched.<BR>5 Hated, disliked.<BR>6 Tied, bound.<BR>7 Struck, hurt, killed, especially in return or requital.<BR>8 Repulsed, repelled.<BR>9 Reflected.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हत hurt or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतमति
प्रतिहतमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Averse to, hating, disliking.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिहत, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहति|प्रतिहतिः
प्रतिहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Repulse, rebound, beating back or again.<BR>2 Disappointment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and हति striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहनन|प्रतिहननं
प्रतिहनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Striking again, returning a blow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and हनन striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहन्यमान
प्रतिहन्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being foiled or disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिहन to disappoint, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहरण|प्रतिहरणं
प्रतिहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Avoiding, shunning.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहस्त|प्रतिहस्तः
प्रतिहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A deputy, a substitute.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and हस्त the hand; also with कन added प्रतिहस्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहार|प्रतिहारः
प्रतिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A door.<BR>2 A door-keeper.<BR>3 A juggler.<BR>4 Trick, disguise.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारक|प्रतिहारकः
प्रतिहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to प्रतिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारण|प्रतिहारणं
प्रतिहारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Entrance, permission to enter a door.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हृ to take, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहास|प्रतिहासः
प्रतिहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Returning a laugh, laughing with or at.<BR>2 A shrub, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति intensitive, हस to smile, aff. घञ्, whence it is also प्रतीहास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसा
प्रतिहिंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Retaliation, revenge.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and हिंसा injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक|प्रतीकः
प्रतीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Contrary, adverse.<BR>2 Inverted, reversed, against the natural order or state.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A limb, a member.<BR>2 A part, a portion.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ई to go, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकार|प्रतीकारः
प्रतीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Revenge, retaliation.<BR>2 Remedying, obviating, correcting.<BR>3 Remedying, administering medicines.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against (re), and कार making, re-action, the इ is made long in consequence of the aff. being घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकाश|प्रतीकाशः
प्रतीकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Like, resembling, (in composition.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before काश to shine, aff. घञ्, it is also written प्रतीकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षक
प्रतीक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Expecting.<BR>2 Looking at.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षण
प्रतीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Looking to or at, considering, referring to.<BR>2 Respecting.<BR>3 Expecting, waiting for.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षणीय
प्रतीक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be had in view, to be considered or regarded.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षा
प्रतीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Reference, regard to, consideration, looking to or at.<BR>2 Hope, expectation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षित
प्रतीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Contemplated, considered, had regard to.<BR>2 Respected, honoured.<BR>3 Expected, looked for, hoped.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षिन्
प्रतीक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>Expecting, looking or waiting for.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीक्षा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्य|प्रतीक्ष्यः
प्रतीक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 To be considered, to be had regard to.<BR>2 To be expected.<BR>3 Venerable, respectable.<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered, having expected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष to see, aff. ण्यत् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघात|प्रतीघातः
प्रतीघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Warding off or returning as a blow.<BR>2 Preventing, prohibiting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिघात, and the इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीची
प्रतीची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The west quarter: see प्रत्यच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीन|प्रतीचीनं
प्रतीचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>West, western.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीची the west, and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्य|प्रतीच्यः
प्रतीच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Western, west.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीच for प्रत्यच् west, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत|प्रतीतः
प्रतीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated, renowned.<BR>2 Known.<BR>3 Glad, delighted, pleased.<BR>4 Respectful.<BR>5 Past, gone.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before इ to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीति|प्रतीतिः
प्रतीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Knowledge, understanding.<BR>2 Fame, notoriety.<BR>3 Respect.<BR>4 Delight.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before इ to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीप|प्रतीपं|प्रतीपः
प्रतीप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Turned away, having the face averted.<BR>2 Backwards, following an order or course the reverse of natural, against the grain or stream.<BR>3 Retrograde, coming back.<BR>4 Disobedient, refractory, perverse.<BR>5 Cross, contradictory.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The father of ŚANTANU, and grandfather of BHĪṢMA.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Comparing new objects with some established object, as with the moon, &c. inverse comparison.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before अप् water, and the अ changed to इ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपदर्शिनी
प्रतीपदर्शिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीप turning the face away, and दर्शिनी looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपवचन
प्रतीपवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Contradiction.<BR>2 A perverse or evasive answer, a speech to a third person without replying to a previous speaker.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीप, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=568" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीमान
प्रतीमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A measure of capacity.<BR>E.<BR>प्रती, and मा to measure, ल्युट् aff. and the vowel of the prep. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीयमान
प्रतीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being believed or trusted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before इ to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीयिवस्
प्रतीयिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-युसी-वस्)<BR>Coming back, returning.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति back, ईय to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीर|प्रतीरं
प्रतीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A shore or bank.<BR>E.<BR>प्र beyond, तीर shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवाप|प्रतीवापः
प्रतीवाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Calcining or fluxing metals.<BR>2 Throwing one substance into another to alter its form or state.<BR>3 Adding any thing to a medicine during or after decoction.<BR>4 A public danger or calamity, as a plague, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before वप to spread, aff. घञ्, whence the vowel of the prefix is lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेश|प्रतीवेशः
प्रतीवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A neighbouring residence, a neighbourhood: see प्रतिवेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेशिन्
प्रतीवेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिती-शि)<BR>A neighbour, living in the neighbourhood.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिवेश a neighbourhood, and इनि aff.; also प्रतिवेशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहार|प्रतीहारः
प्रतीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A door.<BR>2 A porter, a warder.<BR>3 An agreement for return of assistance, alliance, confederacy.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female door-keeper.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति severally, mutually, हृ to convey, aff. घञ्; also प्रतिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहास|प्रतीहासः
प्रतीहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before हस to smile, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुद|प्रतुदः
प्रतुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A bird of game, a falcon, a hawk, or rather one that kills or strikes with his beak, including also the owl, parrot, crow, raven, peacock, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तुद to torment, (with the beak,) and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टुषु
प्रतुष्टुषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>1 Wishing to praise.<BR>2 Wishing to prepare or make ready.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ष्टु to praise, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूणी
प्रतूणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Pain shooting from the rectum along the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूर्ण
प्रतूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Quick, fleet. प्र before त्वर to make haste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोद|प्रतोदः
प्रतोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A goad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र thoroughly, तुद to torment, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोली
प्रतोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A high street, the principal road through a town or village.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तुल to weigh, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोलीक
प्रतोलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having a high street, (a town.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्त|प्रत्तं
प्रत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Given, presented.<BR>2 Given in marriage, either betrothed or married.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, aff. क्त, form special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्तवत्
प्रत्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Giving, presenting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, क्तथतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्न|प्रत्नः
प्रत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Old, ancient.<BR>E.<BR>प्र for प्रगे here said to mean old, त्न aff., and गे rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्
प्रत्यक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Subsequent, behind, following in time or place.<BR>2 Western: see प्रत्यच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्पर्णी
प्रत्यक्पर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यच् uniform, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्पुष्पी
प्रत्यक्पुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यच् uniform, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्श्रेणी
प्रत्यक्श्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Dantī.<BR>2 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक् western, and श्रेणी line or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Perceptible, perceivable, present, cognizable by any of the organs of sense.<BR>E.<BR>अक्ष an organ of sense, with प्रति indicative prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षतस्
प्रत्यक्षतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Evidently, perceptibly.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and तस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षदर्शन|प्रत्यक्षदर्शनं
प्रत्यक्षदर्शन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A witness, an eye-witness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष what is present, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षप्रमाण
प्रत्यक्षप्रमाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Ocular or visible proof.<BR>2 An organ or faculty of perception.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and प्रमाण proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभूत
प्रत्यक्षभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Manifested, become visible.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभोग|प्रत्यक्षभोगः
प्रत्यक्षभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Enjoyment or use of any thing with the consciousness of the owner.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षवादिन्
प्रत्यक्षवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and वादिन् who declares: admitting of no other evidence than actual presence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षिन्
प्रत्यक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>Seeing, perceiving, conscious of what is perceptible.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष perceptible, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकरण
प्रत्यक्षीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making manifest or apparent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकृत
प्रत्यक्षीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Manifested, displayed, made present or visible.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यगाशापति|प्रत्यगाशापतिः
प्रत्यगाशापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यक् west, आशा a quarter, पति regent or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्र|प्रत्यग्रः
प्रत्यग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 New, fresh, recent.<BR>2 Pure, purified.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before अग्र first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रता
प्रत्यग्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Newness, freshness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to प्रत्यग्र; also with त्व, प्रत्यग्रत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रथ|प्रत्यग्रथः
प्रत्यग्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A country; also अहिच्छत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रवयस्
प्रत्यग्रवयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>Youth.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यग्र, and वयस् age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्ग|प्रत्यंग|प्रत्यङ्गं
प्रत्यङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>An organ of perception.<BR>n. adv.<BR>On the body, or the limbs severally.<BR>n. subst. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A minor member of the body, as the chin, nose, ear, &c.<BR>2 A subdivision of science, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति belonging to, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्गिरा
प्रत्यङ्गिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A form of DURGĀ, one of the goddesses of the Tāntrikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्मुख
प्रत्यङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Facing the west.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यञ्च, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यच्
प्रत्यच् or प्रत्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (प्रत्यङ् प्रतीची प्रत्यक्)<BR>1 Behind or subsequent, following in time or place.<BR>2 West, western.<BR>3 Uniform, unmixed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before अञ्च to go, aff. क्विन्, the neuter form is used as a particle: see प्रत्यक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यदन
प्रत्यदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating, food.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनन्तर|प्रत्यनंतर
प्रत्यनन्तर<BR>n. adv. (-रं)<BR>Next in succession.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and अनन्तर without an interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनीक|प्रत्यनीकः
प्रत्यनीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Injuring one who cannot retaliate.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, अनीक an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यन्त|प्रत्यंत|प्रत्यन्तः
प्रत्यन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Bordering, skirting, contiguous.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The country of the Mlecchas or savages.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति about, अन्त the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वत|प्रत्यन्तपर्वत|प्रत्यंतपर्वत|प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वतः
प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small hill near a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्थन्त skirting, and पर्व्वत a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञात
प्रत्यभिज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Recognised, known.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अभि before ज्ञा to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञान|प्रत्यभिज्ञानं
प्रत्यभिज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Recognition, knowing, recognising.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अभि before ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=569" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवाद|प्रत्यभिवादः
प्रत्यभिवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Returning a salute or obeisance, the benediction of a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति (re), अभिवाद salute; also प्रत्यभिवादनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियोग|प्रत्यभियोगः
प्रत्यभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A counter plaint or charge, an accusation brought against the accuser or plaintiff.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, अभियोग accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यय|प्रत्ययः
प्रत्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Trust, faith, belief, confidence.<BR>2 Oath, ordeal.<BR>3 Cause, motive.<BR>4 Usage, custom, practice.<BR>5 Fame, celebrity.<BR>6 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>7 Knowledge, apprehension.<BR>8 An affix to roots and words forming derivatives and inflections.<BR>9 A dependant, a subject.<BR>10 Instrument, means of agency, a helpmate or associate, applicable either to persons or things.<BR>11 A householder who keeps a sacred fire.<BR>12 Religious contemplation.<BR>13 A hole.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, against, to or towards, इण् to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययकारिणी
प्रत्ययकारिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A seal, a signet.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यय confidence, and कारिणी causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययित|प्रत्ययितः
प्रत्ययित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Trusted, confidential.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यय confidence, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययिन्
प्रत्ययिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Trusting, believing, having faith in.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ
प्रत्यर्थ<BR>n. (-र्थं)<BR>1 A reply, an answer, a counter-representation.<BR>2 Opposition, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति successive order, and अर्थ representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिन्
प्रत्यर्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>1 Hostile, inimical.<BR>2 Opposing, contradicting, rejecting.<BR>m. (-र्थी)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 (In law,) A defendant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, against (re), अर्थ meaning, intention, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पण|प्रत्यर्पणं
प्रत्यर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The returning of a thing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति back, अर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पित|प्रत्यर्पितं
प्रत्यर्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Returned, restored, re-delivered.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, अर्पित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्श|प्रत्यवमर्शः
प्रत्यवमर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Counsel, advice, injunction.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अव before मृश to advise, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसान|प्रत्यवसानं
प्रत्यवसान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अव prefixed to षो to destroy, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसित|प्रत्यवसितं
प्रत्यवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अव before षो to destroy, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कन्द|प्रत्यवस्कंद|प्रत्यवस्कंदः|प्रत्यवस्कन्दः
प्रत्यवस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A special plea at law; admission of a fact, but qualifying or explaining it so as not to allow it to be matter of accusation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति against, अव before स्कदि to go, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. प्रत्यवस्कन्दन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थातृ
प्रत्यवस्थातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अव before स्था to stay, to oppose or encounter, and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थान|प्रत्यवस्थानं
प्रत्यवस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Former state or place, in statu quo.<BR>2 Opposition, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and अवस्थान situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवाय|प्रत्यवायः
प्रत्यवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Disappearance, either of what exists, or non-production of what does not exist.<BR>3 Reverse, contrary course or proceeding.<BR>4 Disappointment.<BR>5 Disarrangement.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and अव before इण to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यश्मन्
प्रत्यश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति like, अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यहम्
प्रत्यहम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 In the morning.<BR>2 Day by day, every day.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, implying succession, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकार|प्रत्याकारः
प्रत्याकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A scabbard, a sheath.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति like, आकार form<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकलित
प्रत्याकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Interposed.<BR>2 Introduced, as a step in legal process.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before कल to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यात|प्रत्याख्यातः
प्रत्याख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Removed, set aside.<BR>2 Informed, apprised.<BR>3 Discouraged, prohibited, forbidden.<BR>4 Denied, refused.<BR>5 Celebrated, notorious.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before आख्यात said, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यान|प्रत्याख्यानं
प्रत्याख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rejection, refutation, disallowance, disregard.<BR>2 Denial, refusal.<BR>3 Reproach.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति reverse, आङ् before ख्या to say, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्येय
प्रत्याख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be declined or refused.<BR>2 To be refuted, denied, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before ख्या to speak, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागत
प्रत्यागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Come back, returned.<BR>2 Arrived at.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागम|प्रत्यागमः
प्रत्यागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Return.<BR>2 Arrival.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and आगम coming; also प्रत्यागमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागार
प्रत्यागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Former place or state.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and आगार mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिष्ट|प्रत्यादिष्टः
प्रत्यादिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Removed, set aside.<BR>2 Informed, apprised.<BR>3 Warned, cautioned.<BR>4 Declared, (as from heaven.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before आदिष्ट shewn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादेश|प्रत्यादेशः
प्रत्यादेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Rejection, disallowance.<BR>2 Information, apprising, informing.<BR>3 Warning, caution.<BR>4 Refusal, denial.<BR>5 Heavenly annunciation or declaration.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before दिश to shew, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानयन|प्रत्यानयनं
प्रत्यानयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bringing back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before णी to lead, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानिनीषु
प्रत्यानिनीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous of bringing back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before णी to bring, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानीत
प्रत्यानीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Brought back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before नी to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यालीढ|प्रत्यालीढं
प्रत्यालीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>n. (-ढं)<BR>An attitude in shooting, the left foot advanced and right retracted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before लिह to lick, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावर्त्तन|प्रत्यावर्तन|प्रत्यावर्तनं
प्रत्यावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Returning, coming back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावृत्त
प्रत्यावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Returned, come back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याशा
प्रत्याशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Hope, expectation, desire.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति specific, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याशिन्
प्रत्याशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Hoping, expecting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्याशा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासङ्कलित|प्रत्यासंकलित
प्रत्यासङ्कलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Added to.<BR>2 Ascertained, determined.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before सङ्कलित added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्न|प्रत्यासन्नः
प्रत्यासन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Near, proximate, contiguous.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before आसन्न near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासर|प्रत्यासरः
प्रत्यासर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The rear of an army.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before सृ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासार|प्रत्यासारः
प्रत्यासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The rear of an army.<BR>2 A form of array.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before सृ to go, aff. घञ्; also प्रत्यासर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहत
प्रत्याहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Repelled, resisted, repulsed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरण|प्रत्याहरणं
प्रत्याहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Restraining the organs of sense.<BR>2 Taking back.<BR>3 Withholding.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=570" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरणीय
प्रत्याहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be restrained or controlled.<BR>2 Resumable, to be taken back.<BR>3 To be withheld, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.; also प्रत्याहर्त्तव्य and प्रत्याहार्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहार|प्रत्याहारः
प्रत्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Abstraction, insensibility, restraining the organs so as to be indifferent to disagreeable or agreeable excitement.<BR>2 Abridgement, compendium.<BR>3 (In grammar,) Combination of two or more letters of the alphabet to form a class of letters.<BR>4 Substitution of one thing for another.<BR>5 Withholding.<BR>6 Taking back.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before हृ to seize or convey, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृत
प्रत्याहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Withheld.<BR>2 Restrained.<BR>3 Resumed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्ति|प्रत्युक्तिः
प्रत्युक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Answer, reply.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, बच to speak, aff. क्तिन्, the semivowel changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत
प्रत्युत<BR>ind.<BR>On the contrary, on the other hand, otherwise.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and उत whether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्त्रम
प्रत्युक्त्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Act or effort tending to a main object.<BR>2 First step or measure in any business.<BR>3 Declaration of war.<BR>4 Setting out to assail an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उत् before क्रम to go, aff. अच्; also प्रत्युक्त्रामण and प्रत्युक्त्रान्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्त्रान्ति
प्रत्युक्त्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Act, tending to a main object, &c., see the last.<BR>E.<BR>as above, see प्रत्युक्त्रम, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्तर|प्रत्युत्तरं
प्रत्युत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A rejoinder, a reply to an answer, an answer.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, उत्तर an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थान|प्रत्युत्थानं
प्रत्युत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rising from a seat, as a mark of respect.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उत् before स्था to stay, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्न|प्रत्युत्पन्नः
प्रत्युत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Reproduced, regenerated.<BR>2 Prompt, ready.<BR>3 (In arithmetic,) Multiplied.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 Multiplication.<BR>2 The product of a sum in multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति again, उत्पन्न produced, or प्रति and उत् before पन्न made, done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नजाति|प्रत्युत्पन्नजातिः
प्रत्युत्पन्नजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>(In arithmetic,) Assimilation of fractional increase.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्युत्पन्न, and जाति reduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नमति|प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः
प्रत्युत्पन्नमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Confident, bold, arrogant.<BR>2 Sharp, subtle, quick.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्युत्पन्न prompt, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गत
प्रत्युद्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Met.<BR>2 Risen as from a seat.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, उद्गत gone up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गम|प्रत्युद्गमः
प्रत्युद्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Rising, as from a seat.<BR>2 Going to meet a guest, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उद् before गम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमनीय|प्रत्युद्गमनीयं
प्रत्युद्गमनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be placed near, upon or before.<BR>2 To be worshipped or reverenced.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A pair of bleached cloths, or the upper and lower garments, as worn at meals and sacrifices, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उत् before गम to go, अनीयर् aff. of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमन|प्रत्युद्गमनं
प्रत्युद्गमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rising from a seat, as a mark of respect, &c.<BR>2 Going forth or out, going to meet any one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उत् before गम to go, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट्, प्रत्युद्गमनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धरण|प्रत्युद्धरणं
प्रत्युद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Recovering, re-obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उट् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धृत
प्रत्युद्धृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Recovered.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति and उट् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकार|प्रत्युपकारः
प्रत्युपकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Requital of aid or assistance, mutual assistance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and उपकार aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकारिन्
प्रत्युपकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Requiting a favour or kindness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्युपकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युप्त
प्रत्युप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Set, inlaid, studded.<BR>2 Sown.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before वप to sow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युष|प्रत्युषः
प्रत्युष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The morning, dawn, daybreak.<BR>E.<BR>see प्रत्यूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषस्
प्रत्युषस्<BR>n. (-षः)<BR>Morning.<BR>E.<BR>see प्रत्यूषस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषं|प्रत्यूषः
प्रत्यूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Morning.<BR>2 One of the demigods called VASUS.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ऊष to be sick, aff. क; also with उष to burn, प्रत्युष; and with असि aff. प्रत्यूषस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषस्
प्रत्यूषस्<BR>n. (-षः)<BR>Morning, dawn.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ऊष to be sick, and अमि aff.; also प्रत्यूष and प्रत्यूषस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूह|प्रत्यूहः
प्रत्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Obstacle, impediment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before ऊह to infer, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्येक|प्रत्येकं
प्रत्येक<BR>n. adv. (-कं)<BR>Singly, one by one, one at a time.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति, and एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्येतृ
प्रत्येतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Believing, trusting, having confidence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before इ to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथ
प्रथ<BR>r. 1st cl. (प्रथते)<BR>To be famous or renowned.<BR>r. 10th cl. (प्राथयति)<BR>1 To throw or cast.<BR>2 To scatter, to spread.<BR>3 To celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथन|प्रथनं
प्रथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Spreading, extension, scattering.<BR>2 Throwing, projecting.<BR>3 Celebrating.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to cast, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 First, prior, initial.<BR>2 Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, अमच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमसाहस|प्रथमसाहसः
प्रथमसाहस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The first or lowest degree of fine or punishment.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथम, and साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथयत्|प्रथयन्त्
प्रथयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Displaying, making manifest, famous, &c.<BR>2 Seeing, beholding.<BR>3 Casting, throwing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथा
प्रथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथित|प्रथितः
प्रथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated.<BR>2 Made known, declared.<BR>3 Spread, scattered.<BR>4 Stretched.<BR>5 Cast, thrown.<BR>6 Intent upon, engaged in, occupied by, devoted to.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथा fame, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिति|प्रथितिः
प्रथिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Celebrity, notoriety.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, ति Uṇādi aff., and इट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमन्
प्रथिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Greatness, magnitude.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large, इमनिच् aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमिन्
प्रथिमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Large, great, having size or magnitude.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथिमा magnitude, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिष्ठ|प्रथिष्ठः
प्रथिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very large.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large, इष्ठन् superl. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथीयस्
प्रथीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very large.<BR>E.<BR>पृथु large, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुक|प्रथुकः
प्रथुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The young of any animal.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथ to be famous, कुकन् aff.: see पृथुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद|प्रदः
प्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>A giver, giving, bountiful.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A gift, a donation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, and श aff. or अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं|प्रदक्षिणः
प्रदक्षिण<BR>mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Reverential salutation, by circumambulating a person or object, keeping the right side towards them.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दक्षिण the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदत्त|प्रदत्तं
प्रदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given, bestowed, conferred.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=571" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर|प्रदरः
प्रदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Splitting, rending, tearing.<BR>2 Fracture, a breaking.<BR>3 A disease of women, (Mænorrhagia.)<BR>4 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>प्र intensitive, दृ to tear, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शक|प्रदर्शकः
प्रदर्शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A teacher, an expounder.<BR>2 A prophet.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दर्शक who shews.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शन|प्रदर्शनं
प्रदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Shewing.<BR>2 Explaining generally, not exclusively.<BR>3 Explaining or specifying.<BR>4 Prophesying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दृश to see, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शित|प्रदर्शितः
प्रदर्शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mentioned, specified.<BR>2 Shewn.<BR>3 Prophesied.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दृश to see, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदल|प्रदलः
प्रदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दल to tear, or the र of प्रदर changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदव|प्रदवः
प्रदव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Who or what annoys, distresses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>दु to annoy, with प्र prefix, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदातृ
प्रदातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>A donor, who or what gives.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदान|प्रदानं
प्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 A goad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, or दो to cut, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिग्ध|प्रदिग्धं
प्रदिग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Smeared, anointed.<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>A kind of sauce or gravy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिग्ध smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्)<BR>Intermediate point of the compass, or half quarter, as north-east, south-west, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying division, and दिश् a point or quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिष्ट
प्रदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Appointed, directed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिश to shew, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप|प्रदीपः
प्रदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दीप to shine, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपन|प्रदीपनः
प्रदीपन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Inflaming, illuminating.<BR>2 Stimulating, exciting, who or what does so.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The act of inflaming, exciting, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of mineral poison, of a red colour, and caustic operation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दीप to inflame, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्त
प्रदीप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Kindled, burning.<BR>2 Excited, stimulated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दीप to inflame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुह्
प्रदुह्<BR>mfn. (-घुक्)<BR>Who or what milks much or well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दुह to milk, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेय|प्रदेयः
प्रदेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A gift.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेश|प्रदेशः
प्रदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A place in general, a country, a district, &c.<BR>2 A foreign country, abroad.<BR>3 A short span, measured from the tip of the thumb to that of the forefinger.<BR>4 A wall.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशन|प्रदेशनं
प्रदेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A gift, a present, a bribe or offering, any thing given to the gods, to superiors, or friends, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिश to show, aff ल्युट्, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशिनी
प्रदेशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The forefinger.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिश to shew, aff. णिनि, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेह|प्रदेहः
प्रदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Unguent, unction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिह to plaster, aff. घज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोष|प्रदोषः
प्रदोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Evening, the first part of the night.<BR>2 Fault, offence, defect, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying commencement, &c. and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्यु
प्रद्यु<BR>n. adv. (-द्यु)<BR>Heavenly, holy, securing heaven.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्यु for द्युस् heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्न|प्रद्युम्नः
प्रद्युम्न<BR>m. (-म्नः)<BR>KĀMA, the Hindū CUPID, reborn as the son of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>प्र pre-eminent, द्यम्न power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युतित
प्रद्युतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Illuminated, irradiated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्यु to shine, क्त aff. and the vowel unchanged; also प्रद्योतित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योत|प्रद्योतः
प्रद्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excess, and द्योत shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतन|प्रद्योतनं|प्रद्योतनः
प्रद्योतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sun.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Blazing, shining, light.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excess, द्युत to shine, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतित
प्रद्योतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Illuminated, lighted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्यु to shine, क्त aff.; also प्रद्युदित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राव|प्रद्रावः
प्रद्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Flight, retreat, running away.<BR>2 Going, going quick or well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्रु to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राविन्
प्रद्राविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Who retreats, flies, goes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्रु to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष्<BR>mfn. (-द्विट्)<BR>Who hates or dislikes, hostile, inimical.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्विष to hate, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विषत्
प्रद्विषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षती-षत्)<BR>Hating, hostile, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and द्विषत् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेष्टृ
प्रद्वेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who hates or dislikes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्विव to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध
प्रध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Who or what has or holds.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षा to have, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधन|प्रधनं
प्रधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Tearing, rending, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धा to have, aff. क्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षित
प्रधर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Haughty, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धृष to be proud, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षितवत्
प्रधर्षितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Proud, arrogant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धृष to be proud, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधान|प्रधानं|प्रधानः
प्रधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Nature, the natural state of any thing, or the cause of the material world.<BR>2 The SUPREME GOD.<BR>3 Intellect, understanding.<BR>4 Chief, principal, (in this sense, it is always neuter and confined to the singular number.)<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 The first companion of a king, his minister, his eunuch or confident, &c. a courtier, a noble.<BR>2 An elephant-driver.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानतस्
प्रधानतस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to eminence or superiority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानता
प्रधानता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Excellence, superiority, supremacy.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to प्रधान; also with त्व, प्रधानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानधातु|प्रधानधातुः
प्रधानधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Semen virile.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान principal, and धातु radical part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानमन्त्रिन्|प्रधानमंत्रिन्
प्रधानमन्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-न्त्री)<BR>Prime minister.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान, and मन्त्रिन् counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानाङ्ग|प्रधानांग
प्रधानाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The chief member of the body, the chief person of a state, branch of a science, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान, and अङ्ग limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानामात्य|प्रधानामात्यः
प्रधानामात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>Prime minister.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान, and अमात्य minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानोत्तम
प्रधानोत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Warlike, braver.<BR>2 Eminent, illustrious.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावन|प्रधावनः
प्रधावन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>प्र violently, घ to shake, aff. ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधि|प्रधिः
प्रधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The periphery of a wheel.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधिमण्डल
प्रधिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The circumference of a wheel.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधि, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूपित
प्रधूपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heated, burnt.<BR>2 Lighted, inflamed.<BR>3 Afflicted.<BR>4 Excited.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman in trouble or affliction. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">Page573</a>]<BR>2 The quarter to which the sun is proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धूप to heat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=572" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्ट
प्रधृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Proud, arrogant.<BR>2 Treated with contumely.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before धृष to be proud, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंस|प्रध्वंसः
प्रध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Destruction, loss.<BR>E.<BR>प्र entirely, ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसिन्
प्रध्वंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Destroying, annihilating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ध्वंस to destroy, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वनयत्
प्रध्वनयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Causing to sound.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ध्वन to sound, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मा
प्रध्मा<BR>mfn. (-ध्माः-ध्माः-ध्म)<BR>Blowing violently.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ध्मा to blow, aff. विच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्रुह्
प्रध्रुह्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>1 Injurious, doing wrong or violence to.<BR>2 Rebellious, refractory.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before द्रुह to seek to hurt, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनर्त्तित|प्रनर्तित
प्रनर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, agitated, set in motion.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before नृत to dance, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनाल|प्रनालः
प्रनाल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>A water-course, a canal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before नल to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिघातन|प्रनिघातनं
प्रनिघातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and नि before हन to kill or hurt, ल्युट् aff., and the radical letters changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्च|प्रपंच|प्रपंचः|प्रपञ्चः
प्रपञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>1 Reverse, opposition, reversion or inversion.<BR>2 Extent, expanse.<BR>3 Heap, abundance, quantity.<BR>4 Delusion, deceit, trick or fraud.<BR>5 Joke, jest.<BR>6 Prolixity, copiousness, in style or composition.<BR>7 Error, illusion.<BR>8 The world.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पचि to spread, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चित|प्रपंचित|प्रपञ्चितं
प्रपञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expanded, diffused.<BR>2 Erring, mistaken.<BR>3 Tricked, deceived, beguiled.<BR>4 Declared fully, explained, treated at length.<BR>E.<BR>प्रपञ्च prolixity, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतन|प्रपतनं
प्रपतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Destruction.<BR>3 Falling.<BR>4 Alighting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पत to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतित
प्रपतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead.<BR>2 Decayed.<BR>3 Fallen.<BR>4 Come down.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पत to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ|प्रपथः
प्रपथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Languid, enervated, relaxed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पथ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपद|प्रपदं
प्रपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The point of the foot, the tip of the toes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र projecting, and पद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदीन
प्रपदीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Relating to the top of the foot, extending to it, fitting it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रपद, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्न|प्रपन्नः
प्रपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Taking refuge with.<BR>2 Reaching, arriving at.<BR>3 Seeking, adhering to.<BR>4 Effecting, producing.<BR>5 Promised, assented to.<BR>6 Attained, obtained, possessed of.<BR>7 Poor.<BR>8 Distressed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपर्ण
प्रपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A fallen leaf.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायन|प्रपलायनं
प्रपलायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flight, running away.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पलायन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायित
प्रपलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Routed, defeated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पलायित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायिन्
प्रपलायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A fugitive, one who deserts his cause.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पलायिन् who flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपवण
प्रपवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Purifying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पू to purify, ल्युट् aff. न optionally changed, whence also प्रपवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपवणीय
प्रपवणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be purified or cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पू to purify, अनीयर् aff.; also प्रपवनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपश्यत्
प्रपश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>Foreseeing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and पश्यत् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपा
प्रपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A place where water is distributed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पा to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणि|प्रपाणिः
प्रपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The palm of the hand.<BR>E.<BR>प्र prostrate, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणीय
प्रपाणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Drinkable.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पा to drink, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपात|प्रपातः
प्रपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A cliff, a precipice.<BR>2 A cascade, or water-fall.<BR>3 A bank, a shore.<BR>4 Facing an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पत to descend, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाथ|प्रपाथः
प्रपाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पथ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादिक|प्रपादिकः
प्रपादिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपायिन्
प्रपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Who or what drinks.<BR>2 Who or what protects.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पा to drink, &c. घिनुण् aff. and आय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपावन|प्रपावनं
प्रपावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A grove, a pleasure garden.<BR>E.<BR>प्रपा a place of refreshment, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामह|प्रपितामहः
प्रपितामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A paternal great grandfather.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A paternal great grandmother.<BR>E.<BR>प्र preceding, पितामह a grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपित्सु
प्रपित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing or intending to descend, alight, fall, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before पत to go, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाड|प्रपुनाडः
प्रपुनाड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A sort of Cassia, (C. tora): see प्रपुन्नाड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नड|प्रपुंनड|प्रपुन्नडः
प्रपुन्नड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>Cassia tora: see प्रपुन्नाड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्ना
प्रपुन्ना<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>A sort of grass, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाड|प्रपुंनाड|प्रपुन्नाडः
प्रपुन्नाड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia tora.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellently, पुपस् manking, and णल to smell, aff. अण्, the स of पुमस् is rejected, and the ल of the radical changed optionally to ड; the antepenultimate is occasionally short, and one of the conjunct न is sometimes rejected; whence the word is variously written, प्रपुन्नाल, or प्रपुन्नड, or प्रपुनाड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाल|प्रपुंनाल|प्रपुन्नालः
प्रपुन्नाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Cassia tora: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरण|प्रपूरणं
प्रपूरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The drawing out of a bow string for the purpose of shooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरिका
प्रपूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A prickly nightshade, (Solanum Jacquini.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौण्डरीक|प्रपौण्डरीकं|प्रपौण्डरीकः
प्रपौण्डरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small herbaceous plant, used in medicine, and as a perfume, commonly Punderya; in medicine it forms the basis of applications to ulcers, and bad eyes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellent, पुण्डरीक the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्र|प्रपौत्रः
प्रपौत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A great grandson.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A great granddaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र preceding, पौच a son's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रप्यान
प्रप्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fat, bulky.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before प्याय to be fat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्ल|प्रफुल्लः
प्रफुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>1 Blown, as a flower.<BR>2 Smilling.<BR>3 Shining.<BR>4 Glad, pleased.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before फुल्ल flowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लनयन
प्रफुल्लनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having full or sparkling eyes.<BR>E.<BR>प्रफुल्ल, and नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लवदन
प्रफुल्लवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having a cheerful or smiling countenance, looking gay or happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रफुल्ल, and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्ध|प्रबंध|प्रबंधः|प्रबन्धः
प्रबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 Continuous application or action, continuance, uninterruptedness.<BR>2 A connected discussion, or narrative.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बधि to bind, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धकल्पना|प्रबंधकल्पना
प्रबन्धकल्पना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A feigned story, a work of imagination, whether founded on fact or not.<BR>E.<BR>प्रबन्ध a connected narrative, and कल्पना a making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=573" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबल|प्रबलः
प्रबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sprout, a shoot.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बल to be strong, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधमान
प्रबाधमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Paining, afflicting, tormenting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बाध to pain, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाल|प्रबालं|प्रबालः
प्रबाल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Coral.<BR>2 A shoot, a sprout, a new leaf.<BR>3 The neck of a lute.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An animal.<BR>2 A pupil.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बल to be strong, and aff. घञ्; also प्रबालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालवत्|प्रबालवन्त्
प्रबालवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having new leaves or shoots.<BR>E.<BR>प्रबाल, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुद्ध|प्रबुद्धः
प्रबुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Wise, learned.<BR>2 Blown, expanded.<BR>3 Wakened, awake, roused.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बुद्ध to be wise, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोध|प्रबोधः
प्रबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Vigilance, wakefulness, active or vigilant state of being.<BR>2 Intellect, understanding.<BR>3 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>4 Sense, consciousness.<BR>5 Awaking either from ignorance or sleep.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बुध to understand, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधन|प्रबोधनं
प्रबोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Awakening, arousing, exciting, reviving.<BR>2 Instructing.<BR>3 Reviving the fragrance of a perfume, which had lost its scent.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The lunation on which VIṢṆU is supposed to wake from his sleep, the eleventh of the light half of Kartik; also प्रबोधिनी.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बुध to know or understand, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधित
प्रबोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Aroused, awakened.<BR>2 Instructed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before बुध to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधिता
प्रबोधिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभङ्ग|प्रभंगः|प्रभङ्गः
प्रभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Breaking down, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भञ्ज to break, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्जन|प्रभंजन|प्रभंजनं|प्रभञ्जनः
प्रभञ्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Breaking, destroying.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भञ्ज to break, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्रभव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Superior, powerful.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Generative cause, the basis or root of being or existence.<BR>2 The operative cause, or immediate origin of being, as the father or mother, &c.<BR>3 The place of receiving existence, or where an object is first perceived, as हिमवान् गङ्गा प्रभवः the Himavān mountain, (is) the place where Gaṅgā is first seen.<BR>4 Birth, production.<BR>5 The basis or origin of water, i. e. light.<BR>6 The name of a Muni.<BR>7 Strength, superiority, power.<BR>E.<BR>प्र superiority or manifestation, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवन|प्रभवनं
प्रभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Being born or produced.<BR>2 Ruling, presiding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भू to be, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्रभविष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Mighty, potent.<BR>2 Born completely or well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भू to be, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णुता
प्रभविष्णुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Consequence, importance, power, authority, supremacy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भू to be, इष्णुच् aff., and तल् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव्य
प्रभव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be born or produced.<BR>2 Fit for rule.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भू to be, aff. क्यप्; also प्रभवनीय and प्रभवितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Light, radiance.<BR>2 The city of KUVERA.<BR>3 One of the wives of the sun.<BR>4 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>प्र exceeding, भा to shine, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकर|प्रभाकरः
प्रभाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभा light, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकीट|प्रभाकीटः
प्रभाकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The firefly.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभा light, कीट insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाज्
प्रभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Who or what shares or divides.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भज to divide, and खि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाञ्जन|प्रभाञ्जनः
प्रभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रभा light, beauty, अञ्ज to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभात|प्रभातं
प्रभात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Morning, dawn, daybreak.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भा to shine, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभान|प्रभानं
प्रभान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Light, radiance, shining.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भा to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभानीय
प्रभानीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be irradiated or lighted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भा to shine, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाव|प्रभावः
प्रभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Majesty, dignity, magnanimity, high spirit.<BR>2 Power, strength.<BR>3 Spirit.<BR>4 Tranquillizing, conciliation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र pre-eminence, भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावज|प्रभावजः
प्रभावज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Proceeding from conscious majesty or power.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभाव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावत्|प्रभावन्त्
प्रभावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Luminous, radiant, splendid.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The mother of MALLI the 19th of the Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>2 The lute of one of the demigods attendant on ŚIVA, or other principal deities.<BR>3 A form of poetical metre.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभा light or splendour, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास|प्रभासः
प्रभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A place of pilgrimage, in the west of India,<BR>2 One of the eight VASUS.<BR>3 One of the Gaṇādhipas of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भास to shine, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्न|प्रभिन्नः
प्रभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Well cut or detached.<BR>2 Severed, separated.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A furious elephant, one in rut or from whose temples the juice is exuding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, भिन्न broken, or seized with fury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु<BR>mfn. (-भु-भ्वी-भु)<BR>1 Strong, able.<BR>2 Always, eternal.<BR>3 A superior, an owner, a proprietor, a master or mistress, &c.<BR>m. (-भुः)<BR>1 A master, a lord.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 Quicksilver.<BR>4 Sound.<BR>E.<BR>प्र pre-eminent, भू to be, aff. क्विप्, and the final vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुता
प्रभुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Greatness, power, supremacy, lordship or sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभु master, aff. तल्; also with त्व aff. प्रमुत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्त|प्रभुभक्तः
प्रभुभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Faithful, devoted.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A good horse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभु a master, and भक्त worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूत|प्रभूतं
प्रभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Much, abundant.<BR>2 Gone up or upwards.<BR>3 Been, become, produced.<BR>4 High, lofty.<BR>5 Governed, presided over.<BR>6 Mature, perfect.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, &c. भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतता
प्रभूतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Abundance, plenty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also प्रभूतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्रभूष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Strong, able.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भू to be, aff. ष्णुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृति|प्रभृतिः
प्रभृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Manner, kind.<BR>2 Etcetera, others, rest, remainder, (in composition); as गर्म्मुत्प्रभृतयःतृणं the grass called Garmut and other sorts; मुनयः सोमश्रवः प्रभृतयः the Munis, Somaśravas, and the rest; ततः प्रभृति thence, after that.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भृ to nourish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेद|प्रभेदः
प्रभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Kind, sort, difference.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भेद kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रश्यमान
प्रभ्रश्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Falling down, being broken off or down.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भ्रंश to break, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्ट
प्रभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Fallen, dropping, fallen off.<BR>2 Broken.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before भ्रंश to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टक|प्रभ्रष्टकं
प्रभ्रष्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A chaplet of flowers suspended from the middle lock of hair.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before म्रंश to fall or depend, aff. क्त and कन added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=574" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्रमग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Immersed, drowned.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and मग्न plunged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गन
प्रमङ्गन<BR>mfn. (-नं)<BR>Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मगि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गित
प्रमङ्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, proceeded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मगि to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमणस्
प्रमणस्<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Joyful, cheerful.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying pleasure, and मनस् the mind; also प्रमनस्, न being optionally changed to ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्रमत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Careless, negligent.<BR>2 Blundering, a blunderer.<BR>3 Intoxicated.<BR>4 Insane.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ|प्रमथः
प्रमथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 An attendant on ŚIVA.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>f. (-था)<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>2 Pain, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excess, मथ to churn, (the enemies of ŚIVA,) aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथन|प्रमथनं
प्रमथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Paining, distressing.<BR>3 Agitating, churning.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मथ to churn, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथालय|प्रमथालयः
प्रमथालय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Hell.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमथ pain, and आलय an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथाधिप|प्रमथाधिपः
प्रमथाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमथ a follower of ŚIVA, and अधिप master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथित|प्रमथितं
प्रमथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well-churned.<BR>2 Pained, distressed.<BR>3 Trampled down.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Butter-milk without water.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मथि to churn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्रमद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Mad, intoxicated, figuratively with passion or literally with liquor.<BR>2 Violent.<BR>3 Careless.<BR>4 Impassioned.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Joy, pleasure, delight, rapture.<BR>2 Datura, (D. metel.)<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A woman, a handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद mad, drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदकानन|प्रमदकाननं
प्रमदकानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A royal garden or pleasure ground.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमद pleasure, and कानन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदवन|प्रमदवनं
प्रमदवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A royal garden or pleasure ground attached to the Haram.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमद pleasure, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदाकानन|प्रमदाकाननं
प्रमदाकानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A royal garden.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमदा a woman, and कानन a wood: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदावन|प्रमदावनं
प्रमदावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A royal garden or pleasure ground attached especially to the private apartments of the palace.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमदा a woman, and वन a grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्रमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying pleasure, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्यु
प्रमन्यु<BR>mfn. (-न्युः-न्युः-न्यु)<BR>Distressed, sorrowful.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and मन्यु grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमय|प्रमयः
प्रमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मी to injure, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 True knowledge, or knowledge exempt from all error.<BR>2 Consciousness, perception.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to mete or measure, aff. अङ् and टाप्; that by which every object is measured or estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाण|प्रमाणं|प्रमाणः
प्रमाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Cause, motive.<BR>2 Limit.<BR>3 Proof, testimony, authority.<BR>4 A scripture, a work of sacred authority.<BR>5 Measure, quantity.<BR>6 A speaker of the truth.<BR>7 Always, eternal.<BR>8 A title of VIṢṆU.<BR>9 Principal, capital.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to measure, aff. ल्युट्; that by which all is measured; this word is generally restricted to the singular number, as वेदाः-प्रमाणं the Vedas are the authority; it is also confined to the neuter gender, as पुत्त्रः प्रमाणं the boy is a witness; some exceptions occur however, as प्रमाणः पुरुषः, प्रमाणा स्त्री the man witness, the woman witness; and in the following rule, प्रत्यक्षानुभानोपमानशब्दाः-प्रमाणानि perception, inference, comparison, and sound, are proofs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणतस्
प्रमाणतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 According to proof or authority.<BR>2 Agreeably to measure, to weight, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपुरुष|प्रमाणपुरुषः
प्रमाणपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An umpire, an arbitrator, a judge.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणयत्
प्रमाणयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Receiving, admitting, or obeying, &c. as authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, nominal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणाभाव|प्रमाणाभावः
प्रमाणाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Want or absence of proof or authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिका
प्रमाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकरण
प्रमाणीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Establishing or admitting as authority or proof.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and करण making, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकृत
प्रमाणीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Admitted or established as proof or authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीभूत
प्रमाणीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Proving, establishing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामह|प्रमातामहः
प्रमातामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A maternal great grandfather.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A maternal great grandmother.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मातामह a grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्रमातृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-बी-तृ)<BR>Proving, evidence, who or what is proof or authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to measure, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथ|प्रमाथः
प्रमाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Killing.<BR>2 Paining, afflicting, torturing.<BR>3 Violence.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मथि to churn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्रमाथिन्<BR>mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>1 Afflicting, inflicting pain or sorrow.<BR>2 Killing, destroying.<BR>3 Breaking, cutting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मथ to churn, to grind, to pain, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद|प्रमादः
प्रमाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Inadvertence, carelessness, error, inaccuracy.<BR>3 Intoxication.<BR>4 Insanity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद to be mad, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादवत्|प्रमादवन्त्
प्रमादवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Heedless, careless, incautious, inconsiderate, unreflecting.<BR>2 Insane.<BR>3 Intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाद carelessness, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An imprudent or careless woman.<BR>2 A deflowered girl.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद to be careless, ण्वुल् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Careless, indifferent.<BR>2 Insane.<BR>3 Intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद to be inebriate, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद्य
प्रमाद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Carelessness.<BR>2 Insanity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद to be mad, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद्यतस्
प्रमाद्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From carelessness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाद्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापण|प्रमापणं
प्रमापण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मीञ् to hurt or kill, पुक augment, from its taking the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.; the न of the affix also being unchanged, the word is written प्रमापन n. (-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापिन्
प्रमापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Killing, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मी to kill, causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
प्रमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood, established, proved.<BR>2 Measured.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to measure, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिताक्षरा
प्रमिताक्षरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिति|प्रमितिः
प्रमिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 True knowledge, or knowledge derived from the senses, inference, analogy or information.<BR>2 Measuring.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to measure, (by which,) क्तिन् aff., and radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=575" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीढ|प्रमीढः
प्रमीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Thick.<BR>2 Passed, passed as urine.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मिह to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीणत्
प्रमीणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>1 Overcoming, subduing.<BR>2 Injuring, killing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मी to hurt or kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीत|प्रमीतः
प्रमीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead, deceased.<BR>2 Immolated, sacrificed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मी to hurt or kill, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्रमीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Lassitude, enervation, exhaustion from indolence or fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मील to twinkle, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुख|प्रमुखं|प्रमुखः
प्रमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 Chief, principal.<BR>2 Best, most excellent.<BR>3 First.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A chief, a sage, any respectable man.<BR>2 A heap, a multitude.<BR>3 A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Time being, the present.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुख the face, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुखत्व
प्रमुखत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Superiority, predominance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमुख, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, प्रमुखता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद्<BR>mfn. (-मुत्)<BR>Pleased, happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुद to be pleased, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदित|प्रमुदितः
प्रमुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, glad, content, happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excess, मुद to be pleased, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढ
प्रमूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 A fool, foolish, stupid.<BR>2 Bewildered, deceived.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and मूढ a fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढसंज्ञ
प्रमूढसंज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Bewildered, infatuated.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमूढ, and सज्ञा sign of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृत
प्रमृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered, concealed, withdrawn or gone out of sight.<BR>2 Dead.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Tillage, cultivation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मृ to die, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृष्ट
प्रमृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Polished, bright, clear.<BR>2 Rubbed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मृज to clean, or मृष to rub, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदित
प्रमेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Greasy, unctuous.<BR>2 Becoming or made unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मिद to be unctuous, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदितवत्
प्रमेदितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Being or made unctuous.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मिद to be unctuous, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेय
प्रमेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Proveable, what may or ought to be proved.<BR>2 Measurable, finite.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The thing to be proved. In logic, the second head, or topic, including twelve objects, as the soul, body, &c. or the form and end of existence.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मा to measure, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेह|प्रमेहः
प्रमेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Urinary affection, as change in the colour, quantity, or consistence of the urine; twenty-one varieties are enumerated, including diabetes, gonorrhœa, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying change, मिह to pass urine, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोचन|प्रमोचनं
प्रमोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Liberating, setting free.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुच to liberate, ल्युट् aff.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of cucumber: see गवाक्षी.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुच to loose, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोद|प्रमोदः
प्रमोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Pleasure, happiness, delight.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुद to be pleased, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदित|प्रमोदितः
प्रमोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Happy, delighted.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमोद happiness, इतच् aff.; or प्र before मुद to be happy, क्त aff., and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदिन्
प्रमोदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Happy, delighted.<BR>2 Delighting, making happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमोद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोह|प्रमोहः
प्रमोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Fascination.<BR>2 Fainting, insensibility.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मुह to be bewildered, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लोचा
प्रम्लोचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>One of the Apsaras, or nymphs of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयच्छन्
प्रयच्छन्<BR>mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छती-च्छत्)<BR>Giving, presenting, bestowing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दा to give, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत|प्रयतः
प्रयत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well-governed, restrained, self-subdued.<BR>2 Careful, prudent.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A holy or pious person, one purified by austerity and mortification.<BR>E.<BR>प्र intensely, यत to endeavour, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतात्मन्
प्रयतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Devout, pious, of a holy spirit.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयत, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्न|प्रयत्नः
प्रयत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>1 Continued or persevering effort, exertion.<BR>2 Act, action.<BR>2 (In logic,) Active effort of three kinds, engaging in any act, prosecuting it, and completing it.<BR>4 Caution, care.<BR>5 Articulation of sounds.<BR>E.<BR>प्र intensitive, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नतस्
प्रयत्नतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Particularly, especially, with especial effort, care or pains.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयत्न, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नवत्|प्रयत्नवन्त्
प्रयत्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Active, zealous, enterprising, assiduous, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयत्न effort, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस्<BR>mfn. (-याः-याः-यः)<BR>Valuable, precious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्त|प्रयस्तं
प्रयस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Seasoned, dressed with sauces and condiments.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यस to take pains, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाग|प्रयागः
प्रयाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 A celebrated place of pilgrimage, the confluence of the Ganges and Jumna, with the supposed subterraneous addition of the Sarasvatī; the modern Allahabad. The term in composition is applied to many places of reputed sanctity, situated at the confluence of two rivers, as Deva-Prayāga, Rudra-Prayāga, Karṇa-Prayāga, and Nanda-Prayāga, in the Himāla mountains, which with Prayoga or Allahabad, constitute the five principal places so termed.<BR>3 A name of INDRA.<BR>4 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, यज to worship, and घञ् aff.; actual worship, or the place where worship is peculiarly efficacious; Allahabad is one of the places where BRAHMĀ is supposed to have consummated ten Aśvamedhas or sacrifices of the horse, in commemoration of his recovery of the four Vedas from ŚAṄKHĀSURA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयागभय|प्रयागभयः
प्रयागभय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयाग sacrifice, especially of the horse or Aśvamedha, and भय fear; INDRA being dethroned by the performance of a hundred such sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाज|प्रयाजः
प्रयाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A principal ceremony or sacrifice.<BR>2 A part of a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यज to sacrifice, aff. घञ्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाण|प्रयाणं
प्रयाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>2 Going forth or to a distance.<BR>3 Departure.<BR>4 Death.<BR>5 March of an assailing force, attack, invasion.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, aff. ल्युट्; also with कन् added, प्रयाणक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणकाल|प्रयाणकालः
प्रयाणकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Time of departure.<BR>2 Death.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयाण, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणार्ह
प्रयाणार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Worthy of death.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयाण, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयात|प्रयातः
प्रयात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Removed, gone away or to a distance.<BR>3 Deceased.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of BHṚGU.<BR>2 A sleepy or lazy fellow.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यत to endeavour, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापण|प्रयापणं
प्रयापण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sending, dispatching.<BR>2 Expelling, driving away.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.; also न being unchanged, यापन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापणीय
प्रयापणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be sent or sent away.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.; also प्रयापनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=576" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापित
प्रयापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Driven or sent away, made to go or pass away.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापिन्
प्रयापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>Causing to go, who or what sends, or sends away, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाप्यमाण
प्रयाप्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being sent or made to go, pass away, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, causal v., pass. v., शानच् aff.; also प्रयाप्यमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाम|प्रयामः
प्रयाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Checking, restraining.<BR>2 Scarcity, dearth.<BR>3 Competition of buyers in consequence of scarcity.<BR>4 Length, either of space or time.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यम to refrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाम्य
प्रयाम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-य्यं)<BR>To be checked, controlled, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यम to check, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयास|प्रयासः
प्रयास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Trouble, labour, fatigue.<BR>2 Desire for or pursuit of any object.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यस to make exertion, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयासभाज्
प्रयासभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Capable of exertion or fatigue, active, energetic.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयास, and भाज् sharing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयास्यत्
प्रयास्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>Going, about to go or depart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before या to go, शतृ aff. to the fut. tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्त|प्रयुक्तं
प्रयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Endowed with, possessing as an attribute, &c.<BR>2 Resulting from, consequential.<BR>3 Appointed, nominated.<BR>4 Associated or connected with.<BR>5 Applied, employed.<BR>6 Compact, closely united.<BR>7 Done, to or for.<BR>8 Abstracted, lost in meditation.<BR>9 Lent, (as money.)<BR>10 Asleep.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Cause.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्ति|प्रयुक्तिः
प्रयुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Occasion, cause, main object or end.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज्<BR>mfn. (-युक्)<BR>Who or what joins or is connected with, literally or figuratively, as a cause, motive, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्य
प्रयुज्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having acted or behaved to or towards.<BR>2 Having connected.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्यमान
प्रयुज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being united or connected with.<BR>2 Being used, employed, applied, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुञ्जान
प्रयुञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Adding, joining.<BR>2 Using, employing.<BR>3 Appointing, deputing.<BR>4 Performing, doing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत|प्रयुतं
प्रयुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Joined, combined, united.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Ten hundred thousand, a million.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before यु to join, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत्सु|प्रयुत्सुः
प्रयुत्सु<BR>m. (-त्सुः)<BR>1 A warrior.<BR>2 A name of INDRA.<BR>3 A name of the wind.<BR>4 A ram.<BR>5 An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युद्ध to contend, in the desiderative form, with उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्ध|प्रयुद्धं
प्रयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युद्ध the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्धार्थ|प्रयुद्धार्थः
प्रयुद्धार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>War, battle, going to war or battle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र initiatory, युद्ध war, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तव्य
प्रयोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Applicable, suitable, to be applied or employed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to unite, aff. तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोग|प्रयोगः
प्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Occasion, cause, motive, object.<BR>2 Consequence, result.<BR>3 Affair, matter.<BR>4 Appointing, appointment.<BR>5 Application, use, employment.<BR>6 Ceremonial form, course of proceeding.<BR>7 Magic, magical rites.<BR>8 Subduing, fascinating.<BR>9 Device, contrivance.<BR>10 Example, comparison.<BR>11 Act, action.<BR>12 Dramatic action or performance^1.<BR>13 Principal, loan bearing interest.<BR>14 Lending money at interest.<BR>15 Profits of usury or trade.<BR>16 A horse.<BR>17 Text, authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगतस्
प्रयोगतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 According to or in consequence of.<BR>2 Actually, in action.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to प्रयोग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगार्थ|प्रयोगार्थः
प्रयोगार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>Act, tending to a main object.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयोग aim or end, and अर्थ purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगिन्
प्रयोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Having some object in view, calculated for some particular purpose.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयोग object, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजक|प्रयोजकः
प्रयोजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Who or what causes or induces any act.<BR>2 Who or what deputes or appoints.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A founder or institutor of any ceremony.<BR>2 A law-giver, a legislator.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजककर्त्तृत्व|प्रयोजककर्तृत्व
प्रयोजककर्त्तृत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Acting as an instigator or promoter.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयोजक, and कर्त्तृत्व agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजन|प्रयोजनं
प्रयोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cause, occasion.<BR>2 Motive, origin.<BR>3 Purpose, object, intention, design.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनवत्|प्रयोजनवन्त्
प्रयोजनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Designing, purposing.<BR>2 Having a cause, caused, produced.<BR>E.<BR>प्रयोजन, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजयत्
प्रयोजयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Behaving to or towards, shewing, displaying.<BR>2 Combining, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्य|प्रयोज्यं|प्रयोज्यः
प्रयोज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>1 To be set to work, to be appointed or directed.<BR>2 To be used, practised, employed, &c.<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Capital, principal.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A servant, a slave.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before युज to join, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुदित
प्ररुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wept, weeping.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before रुद to weep, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढ|प्ररूढः
प्ररूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Rooted, fastened, growing or proceeding from a root.<BR>2 Grown, increased.<BR>3 Born, produced.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>The belly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before रुह to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोचन
प्ररोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Stimulating, exciting.<BR>2 Propitiating.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Praise of the author of a drama, &c. in the prelude, to secure the favour of the spectators.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before रुच to, be light, causal v., युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोह|प्ररोहः
प्ररोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A bud, a shoot.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before रुह to grow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहिन्
प्ररोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Budding, sprouting.<BR>E.<BR>प्ररोह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपत्
प्रलपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>Speaking, talking.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लप to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपित|प्रलपितः
प्रलपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Said, spoken, declared.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लप to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्ब|प्रलंब|प्रलम्बः
प्रलम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>1 Hanging down, depending from, pendulous.<BR>2 Slow, dilatory.<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 Depending, hanging on or from.<BR>2 The new shoot or bud of a creeping plant.<BR>3 A garland of flowers worn round the neck.<BR>4 A branch.<BR>5 The female breast.<BR>6 Tin.<BR>7 The name of a Daitya, killed by BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लवि to oppose, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बघ्न|प्रलंबघ्न|प्रलम्बघ्नः
प्रलम्बघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रलम्ब a demon, killed by BALADEVA, and घ्न who kills; also similar compounds, as प्रलम्बभित्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बभिद्
प्रलम्बभिद्<BR>m. (-भित्)<BR>BALADEVA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रलम्ब, and भित् who destroys: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बाण्ड|प्रलंबांड|प्रलम्बाण्डः
प्रलम्बाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A man having large testicles.<BR>E.<BR>प्रलम्ब pendulous, and अण्ड testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=577" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बित|प्रलंबित|प्रलम्बितः
प्रलम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suspended, pendulous, hanging.<BR>E.<BR>प्रलम्ब hanging, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलब्ध
प्रलब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Over-reached, cheated, deceived.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लभ to gain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्भ|प्रलंभ|प्रलंभः|प्रलम्भः
प्रलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Fraud, cheating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लभि to get, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलय|प्रलयः
प्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The end of a Kalpa, or destruction of the world.<BR>2 Death, dying, loss, destruction, dissolution, annihilation.<BR>3 Fainting, syncope, loss of sense or consciousness.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ली to destroy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलाप|प्रलापः
प्रलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Unmeaning or incoherent speech.<BR>2 Speaking.<BR>3 Discourse, conversation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लप to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिन्
प्रलापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>1 Talking much, or unmeaningly, chattering.<BR>2 Speaking to, conversing with.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लप to speak, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलिप
प्रलिप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Who or what smears, plasters, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लिप to anoint, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीन
प्रलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Destroyed, annihilated.<BR>2 Unconscious, insensible.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ली to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीनता
प्रलीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Destruction, annihilation.<BR>2 The end of the universe.<BR>3 Unconsciousness, loss of sense.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, प्रलीनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपक|प्रलेपकः
प्रलेपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what anoints, smears, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plasterer.<BR>2 A slow fever.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लिप to smear, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठित
प्रलोठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rolling, heaving, tossing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लुठ to roll, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठन|प्रलोठनं
प्रलोठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rolling on the ground, heaving, tossing, (as of the ocean.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लुठ to roll, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभ|प्रलोभः
प्रलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Desire, cupidity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लुभ to covet, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभन|प्रलोभनं
प्रलोभन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Allurement, inducement.<BR>2 Attraction, attracting, seducing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लुभ to desire, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक
प्रवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>प्रु to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तव्य
प्रवक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be expounded or explained.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तृ
प्रवक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>Who speaks or declares.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A teacher, an expounder.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचन|प्रवचनं|प्रवचनः
प्रवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A Veda, scripture.<BR>2 Excellent speech or language, eloquence.<BR>3 Teachinge, expounding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principal, वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनीय|प्रवचनीयः
प्रवचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 A good speaker.<BR>2 To be well or elegantly spoken.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, aff. अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनपटु
प्रवचनपटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु)<BR>Eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवचन, and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवट|प्रवटः
प्रवट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वट to divide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवण|प्रवणः
प्रवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Declivity, declining, steep.<BR>2 Bent, bowed.<BR>3 Attached or adhering to, filled with, possessed of, endowed with.<BR>4 Curved, crooked.<BR>5 Swift.<BR>6 Generous.<BR>7 Humble, modest.<BR>8 Wasted, decayed.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A place where four roads meet.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वन to sound, &c. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवदत्
प्रवदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>1 Speaking to or with, conversing, addressing.<BR>2 Speaking much or well.<BR>3 Arguing, a disputant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वद to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवपण|प्रवपणं
प्रवपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sowing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वप to sow, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयण|प्रवयणं
प्रवयण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A goad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अज to go, वी substituted for the root, and aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयस्
प्रवयस्<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>An old man.<BR>E.<BR>प्र past, and वयस् life or age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर|प्रवरं|प्रवरः
प्रवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Best, most excellent.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Offspring, descendants.<BR>2 Family, race, kindred.<BR>3 A black sort of kidney bean.<BR>4 Covering, screening.<BR>5 A Muni, who contributes to the continuation of, and credit of a particular caste or tribe of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ to chuse, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरललित
प्रवरललित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of the Aṣṭī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग|प्रवर्गः
प्रवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृज to abandon, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग्य|प्रवर्ग्यः
प्रवर्ग्य<BR>m. (-र्ग्यः)<BR>An officiating priest.<BR>n. (-र्ग्यं)<BR>A particular ceremony or sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवर्ग, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्त|प्रवर्त|प्रवर्तः
प्रवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Engaging in, undertaking.<BR>2 Excitement, stimulus.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, घञ् aff.: see प्रवर्त्तन and प्रवृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्त्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Inciting, stimulating, inducing, who or what sets in action.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The original instigator of any act, the author, the principal.<BR>2 An arbiter, a judge.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The entrance of the first person of the drama on the close of the introduction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तन|प्रवर्तन|प्रवर्तनं|प्रवर्त्तनं
प्रवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Action, business, worldly interest or activity as opposed to abstract contemplation.<BR>2 Fixing, establishing.<BR>3 Engaging in, (any work.)<BR>4 Beginning.<BR>5 Inciting, stimulating.<BR>6 Directing, superintending.<BR>7 Informing.<BR>8 Revolving.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Order, permission, the sense of the precative, or qualified imperative tense.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, aff. (-युच्,) fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तमान|प्रवर्तमान
प्रवर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Engaging in, practising, doing.<BR>2 Being used or employed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तित|प्रवर्तित|प्रवर्त्तितः
प्रवर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Informed, apprized.<BR>2 Stimulated, excited, instigated.<BR>3 Revolving, going round.<BR>4 Made, rendered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्द्धन
प्रवर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>What causes to grow or increase.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Increase, augmenting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृध to increase, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ह|प्रवर्हः
प्रवर्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Chief, principal, first.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृह to increase, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवलाकिन्
प्रवलाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 One with a variegated girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसत्
प्रवसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-मत्)<BR>Residing abroad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसन|प्रवसनं
प्रवसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going abroad, sojourning in a foreign country.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह|प्रवहः
प्रवह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Going forth, or from a town.<BR>2 One of the seven Vāyus, or winds.<BR>3 Wind, air.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहण|प्रवहणं
प्रवहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A covered car, a litter or carriage for women.<BR>E.<BR>प्र forth, वह to bear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहत्
प्रवहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>1 Bearing.<BR>2 Receiving, enjoying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लि|प्रवह्लिः
प्रवह्लि<BR>f. (-ह्णिः-ह्णी)<BR>A riddle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वल्ह to speak, aff. इन्, and ङीप् optionally added: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिका
प्रवह्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A riddle, an enigma, a conundrum or charade, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वल्ह to speak or tell, aff. क्वुन्; the conjunct consonants of the root are transposed; also प्रवह्लि and प्रवह्ली, and with कन् added to the latter प्रवह्लीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्
प्रवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Eloquent, oratorical, speaking, a speaker.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=578" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचक|प्रवाचकः
प्रवाचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Speaking well, eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणी
प्रवाणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A weaver's shuttle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वी to go, aff. ल्युट, fem. aff. ङीप्; also प्रवाणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाद|प्रवादः
प्रवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Rumour, report.<BR>2 Discourse, conversation.<BR>3 Mutual defiance, the conversation of antagonists prior to combat.<BR>E.<BR>प्र spreading, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादिन्
प्रवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Who or what speaks, reports, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वद to speak, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवापिन्
प्रवापिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A sower, one who sows seed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वप to sow, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवार|प्रवारः
प्रवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Covering, clothing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ to cover, aff. घञ्; also with अप् aff., and in other senses, प्रवर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारण|प्रवारणं
प्रवारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A desirable gift.<BR>2 Prohibition, objection, opposition.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ to chuse, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवास|प्रवासः
प्रवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A temporary or foreign residence, a habitation away from home.<BR>E.<BR>प्र far or removed, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासत्
प्रवासत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Dwelling or being abroad or absent.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासन|प्रवासनं
प्रवासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Dwelling abroad, sojourning, lodging.<BR>3 Exile.<BR>E.<BR>प्र away, वस to dwell, or divide, causal v., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासित
प्रवासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expelled, expatriated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासिन्
प्रवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>A traveller, a sojourner, one living away from home.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवास a foreign or strange habitation, and इनि aff.; or प्र before वस to dwell, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाह|प्रवाहः
प्रवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Stream, flow, continuous passage.<BR>2 Action, occupation, active life.<BR>3 A pond.<BR>4 A swift horse.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>Sand.<BR>E.<BR>प्र continually, वह to bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहक|प्रवाहकः
प्रवाहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what bears or carries well.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An imp, a goblin.<BR>f. (-हिका)<BR>Diarrhoea.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, aff. ण्वुल्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहकम्
प्रवाहकम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 At the same time.<BR>2 Above, over; also in this sense, प्रवाहिका ind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविकशत्
प्रविकशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Expanding, opening, blossoming.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before कश to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्याति|प्रविख्यातिः
प्रविख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Celebrity, reputation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि prefixed to ख्या to say, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवितत
प्रवितत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread out, expanded.<BR>2 Dishevelled.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before तन to spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारण|प्रविदारणं
प्रविदारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 War, battle, combat.<BR>2 Tearing, rending, breaking.<BR>3 Tumult, crowd, confusion.<BR>4 Bursting, budding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि prefixed to दॄ to tear to pieces, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारित
प्रविदारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Torn, rent, severed.<BR>2 Opened, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before दॄ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभक्त
प्रविभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Partitioned, divided, separated, shared.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and विभक्त divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभाग|प्रविभागः
प्रविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Division, a part.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and विभाग division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविर|प्रविरः
प्रविर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before रा to get or be, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरल
प्रविरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Apart, separate.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and विरल distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलुप्त
प्रविलुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Lost, removed, fallen or rubbed off.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before लुप to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविविक्त
प्रविविक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Separated, detached.<BR>2 Solitary.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and विविक्त detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविव्राजयिषु
प्रविव्राजयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing or intending to banish.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before व्रज to go, causal desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्लेष|प्रविश्लेषः
प्रविश्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Separation, parting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि negative prefix before श्लिष to unite, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषण्ण
प्रविषण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>Sad, dejected, spiritless.<BR>E.<BR>प्र much, घिषण्ण dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषा
प्रविषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant, commonly Atis or Ataich.<BR>E.<BR>प्र against (anti), and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्ट|प्रविष्टः
प्रविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Entered, gone in or into.<BR>2 Entered upon, (as an affair,) engaged in.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीण|प्रवीणः
प्रवीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Skilful, clever, conversant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र implying excellence, and वीणा a lute, or वीण a nominal verb, to play on a lute, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीणता
प्रवीणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Proficiency, skill.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवीण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, प्रवीणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीर|प्रवीरः
प्रवीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Best, most excellent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hero, a warrior.<BR>2 A chief, a person of rank or distinction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र preeminent, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्त|प्रवृत्तः
प्रवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Fixed, settled, determined, done.<BR>2 Engaged in, undertaking, occupied by.<BR>3 Begun, beginning.<BR>4 Doing, acting.<BR>5 Undisputed, (as dominion.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तकर्म्मन्|प्रवृत्तकर्मन्
प्रवृत्तकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Any act the cause of being born again.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवृत्त, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तचक्रता
प्रवृत्तचक्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Absolute dominion.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवृत्त fixed, चक्र rule, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्ति|प्रवृत्तिः
प्रवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Activity, occupation, active life, as opposed to contemplative devotion; or it is defined to consist of the wish to do, knowledge of the means of success, and accomplishing the desired object.<BR>2 Prosecution, perseverance.<BR>3 Addiction to, predilection for.<BR>4 Practice, conduct.<BR>5 Tidings, intelligence.<BR>6 Continuous flow, stream, current.<BR>7 The juice that exudes from the elephant's temples, when in rut.<BR>8 Oujein, or any holy place.<BR>9 (In arithmetic,) The multiplier.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृत to be or abide, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिज्ञ|प्रवृत्तिज्ञः
प्रवृत्तिज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>An emissary, an agent, a spy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवृत्ति news, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्ध|प्रवृद्धः
प्रवृद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Full grown.<BR>2 Expanded, diffused, spread abroad or dispersed.<BR>3 Swoln, (as a river.)<BR>4 Full, deep, (as a sigh.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृद्ध to increase or grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक|प्रवेकः
प्रवेक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Chief, head, principal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विच to distinguish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्षण
प्रवेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Foressing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and अव before ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्षित
प्रवेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Foreseen, anticipated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and अव before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्ष्यत्
प्रवेक्ष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यन्-क्ष्यन्ती-क्ष्यत्)<BR>Foreseeing, anticipating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and अव before ईक्ष to see, शतृ aff. the first syllable made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेट|प्रवेटः
प्रवेट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विट to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणि|प्रवेणिः
प्रवेणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 The hair twisted, and undecorated, as worn by women in the absence of their husbands.<BR>2 An elephant's [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">Page580</a>] housings.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वेणृ to go, aff. इण्; also with डीप् added, प्रवेणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=579" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्रवेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Unornamented hair.<BR>2 An elephant's housings.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपण
प्रवेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Shaking, agitation, tremulous motion.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वेपृ to tremble, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेल|प्रवेलः
प्रवेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The yellow variety of kidney bean.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वेल to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश|प्रवेशः
प्रवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Intentness on an object, engaging closely in a pursuit or purpose.<BR>2 Entrance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशक|प्रवेशकः
प्रवेशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what enters.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An inferior actor who announces the entrance of the principal characters.<BR>3 An entry.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशन|प्रवेशनं
प्रवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The entrance to a house, the principal door or gate.<BR>2 Entering, entrance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशित
प्रवेशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Called or sent in.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sent in, thrown in, or into, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, causal v., ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>To be entered, to be pervaded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, यत् aff.; also प्रवेशनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्ट|प्रवेष्टः
प्रवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 An arm.<BR>2 The forearm, or wrist.<BR>3 An elephant's gums.<BR>4 An elephant's housings.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वेष्ट to encompass, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्टव्य
प्रवेष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be entered, to be penetrated or pervaded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before विश to enter, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्त|प्रव्यक्तं
प्रव्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Evident, apparent, manifest.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and वि before अञ्ज to spread, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यथित
प्रव्यथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distressed, pained.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before व्यथ to pain, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजित|प्रव्रजितः
प्रव्रजित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An ascetic or mendicant.<BR>2 The pupil, or attendant of a Jaina or Bauddha mendicant.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A female devotee or ascetic.<BR>2 Spikenard, (Valeriana Jatamansi).<BR>3 A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī, (Sphoeranthus molis?^1 ?)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before व्रज to go, aff. क्त.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्या
प्रव्रज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 Roaming, travelling, wandering about, as a religious mendicant especially.<BR>2 Abandonment of the world.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before व्रज to go, aff. यम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्यावसित|प्रव्रज्यावसितः
प्रव्रज्यावसित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ascetic, who has broken his observance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रव्रज्या, and अवसित finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजन|प्रव्राजनं
प्रव्राजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Banishment.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before व्रज to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंशन
प्रशंशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Praising, eulogising: see प्रशंसन.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंश to praise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंशा
प्रशंशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंश to praise, अङ् and टाप् affs.: see प्रशंसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसन|प्रशंसनं
प्रशंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Praising, eulogising.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंस to praise, ल्युट् aff.; also प्रशंशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसनीय
प्रशंसनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be praised, praise-worthy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंस to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसा
प्रशंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Praise, applause, flattery, commendation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र especially, शंस to praise, affs. अङ् and टाप्; the root is also read शंश, when this word and the analogous derivatives are read प्रशंशा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसित
प्रशंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, eulogised.<BR>E.<BR>प्रशंसा, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसितव्य
प्रशंसितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be praised, praise-worthy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंस to praise, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्वन्
प्रशत्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शद् to go, and क्वनिप् Uṇādi aff., र inserted before ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Pacifying, tranquillising.<BR>3 Quiescence, reposing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to pacify, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमित
प्रशमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Allayed, appeased, relieved, tranquillised, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be calm, causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमय्य
प्रशमय्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having appeased.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be calm, causal v., ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम्यमान
प्रशम्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Pacified, quieted, appeased, flattered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be at rest, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्त|प्रशस्तं
प्रशस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right.<BR>2 Good, excellent, best.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंस to praise or commend, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्ति|प्रशस्तिः
प्रशस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>1 Excellence, eminence.<BR>2 Eulogy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शंस to praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखिक
प्रशाखिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small branch or twig.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शाखा a branch, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्त|प्रशांत|प्रशान्तः
प्रशान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Calmed, calm, tranquillised.<BR>2 Ceased, discontinued, (as active effort.)<BR>3 Ended.<BR>4 Relieved.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be calm, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तचेष्ट|प्रशांतचेष्ट
प्रशान्तचेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Resting.<BR>E.<BR>प्रशान्त, and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तात्मन्|प्रशांतात्मन्
प्रशान्तात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Peaceful, calm, composed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रशान्त, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तोज
प्रशान्तोज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Weakened, prostrate in strength.<BR>E.<BR>प्रशान्त, and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्ति|प्रशांति|प्रशांतिः|प्रशान्तिः
प्रशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Calm, quiet, tranquillity, moral or physical.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be calm, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाम्
प्रशाम्<BR>mfn. (प्रशान्)<BR>Quiet, tranquil.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be tranquil, क्विप् aff., and the penultimate long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाम|प्रशामः
प्रशाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Tranquility, quiescence.<BR>2 Allaying, pacifying.<BR>3 Laying, suppressing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शम to be at rest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासन|प्रशासनं
प्रशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Governing, ruling.<BR>2 Enacting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शास to rule, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासित
प्रशासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Governed, ruled.<BR>2 Promulgated, enacted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शास to rule, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासितृ
प्रशासितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A ruler or governor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before शास to govern, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्च्योतत्
प्रश्च्योतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>Sprinkling, scattering.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्च्युत to sprinkle, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्न|प्रश्नः
प्रश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>A question, a demand, an inquiry.<BR>f. (-श्नी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, aff. नङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नदूती
प्रश्नदूती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A riddle, an enigma, an intricate or enigmatical question.<BR>E.<BR>प्रश्न a question, and टूती playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रथ|प्रश्रथः
प्रश्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Laxity, relaxation, flaccidity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्रथ to be loose, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रय|प्रश्रयः
प्रश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Affection, affectionate regard or solicitation.<BR>2 Respect.<BR>3 Courtesy, civility.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्री to serve, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=580" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रवण
प्रश्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A fountain, a cascade, a water-fall.<BR>2 Oozing, flowing.<BR>3 A range of mountains in the south, part of the western Ghats.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्रु to ooze or drop, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रित|प्रश्रितः
प्रश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Modest, humble, well-behaved.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्रि to serve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रित|प्रश्रितः
प्रश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Flowing, oozing, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्रि to drop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लथ|प्रश्लथः
प्रश्लथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Languid, flaccid, loose, relaxed, unnerved.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before श्लथ to be loose, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टव्य
प्रष्टव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be asked.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टृ
प्रष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Asking, demanding, an asker or questioner.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठ|प्रष्ठः
प्रष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 A leader, a conductor, one who goes first or before.<BR>2 Prior, preceding.<BR>3 Chief, principal, best.<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>The wife of a leader or chief.<BR>E.<BR>प्र pre-eminent, स्था to stay or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठवाह्
प्रष्ठवाह्<BR>m. (-वाट्-वाड्)<BR>A young bull or steer, training for the plough, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रष्ठ a leader, and वह to bear, aff. ण्डि or विच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठौही
प्रष्ठौही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A cow pregnant with her first calf.<BR>E.<BR>प्रष्ठ here said to be the first birth, and वह to bear, aff. ण्वि or विच, fem. aff. ङीप्, and व is changed to ऊ, which with the preceding vowel becomes औ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस
प्रस<BR>r. 1st cl. (प्रसते)<BR>1 To spread or diffuse.<BR>2 To bring forth young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्त|प्रसक्तं
प्रसक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Eternal, constant, continual.<BR>2 Opened, expanded.<BR>3 Obtained, gained, attained.<BR>4 Attached to, devoted to, (person or thing,) engaged in.<BR>5 United to, connected with, accompanying.<BR>6 Applied to, used, employed.<BR>n. adv. (-क्तं)<BR>Continually, incessantly, eternally.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षञ्ज to unite or embrace, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्ति|प्रसक्तिः
प्रसक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Union, connexion.<BR>2 Adherence or attachment to.<BR>3 Energy, perseverance.<BR>4 Acquiring.<BR>5 Inference, conclusion, deduction.<BR>6 A topic, or subject of conversation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षञ्ज to unite, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्ग|प्रसंग|प्रसंगः|प्रसङ्गः
प्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Introduction, insertion.<BR>2 Association, connexion.<BR>3 Addiction or attachment to.<BR>4 Connected language or style.<BR>5 Connected reasoning or argument.<BR>6 Double or conjoint result, producing two effects, attaining two objects by one act.<BR>7 Revealing a secret.<BR>8 (In dramatic language,) A second or subsidiary incident or plot.<BR>E.<BR>प्र preceding, षञ्ज to join, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसञ्जन|प्रसंजन|प्रसंजनं
प्रसञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bringing into use, employing, applying, bringing to bear.<BR>2 Combining, connecting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षञ्ज to unite, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्ति|प्रसत्तिः
प्रसत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Purity, cleanness, brightness, transparency.<BR>2 Favour, graciousness, complacency.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सद to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्वन्
प्रसत्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>1 Virtue, piety.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Acquisition, accomplishment.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षद to go, क्वरप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्न|प्रसन्नः
प्रसन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Clear, clean, bright, pellucid.<BR>2 Pleased, delighted.<BR>3 Complacent, gracious, favourable.<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>1 Propitiating, pleasing.<BR>2 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र principally, &c. सद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नता
प्रसन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Brightness, pellucidness, clearness, purity.<BR>2 Favour, kindness, being pleased with.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसन्न clear, and तल aff.; also with त्व, प्रसन्नत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नमुख
प्रसन्नमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Agreeable looking, smiling, looking pleased.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसन्न, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नेरा
प्रसन्नेरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसन्न clear, and ईरा wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभ|प्रसभः
प्रसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Violence.<BR>adv.<BR>1 Violently, forcibly.<BR>2 Much, exceedingly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र gone, passed, सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षण|प्रसमीक्षणं
प्रसमीक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Considering, deliberating, discussing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and सम् before ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षा
प्रसमीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Deliberation, judgment.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and सम् before ईक्ष to see, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्ष्य
प्रसमीक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>To be weighed, considered, discussed, &c.<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and सम् before ईक्ष to see, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर|प्रसरः
प्रसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Who or what proceeds, projects, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Spreading, extending.<BR>2 Space, room.<BR>3 Occasion, opportunity.<BR>4 Affectionate solicitation.<BR>5 Speed, velocity.<BR>6 Battle, war.<BR>7 Multitude, assemblage.<BR>8 An iron arrow.<BR>9 A projection, a process.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. अप् or घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरण|प्रसरणं
प्रसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going forth or round.<BR>2 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>3 Spreading over the country to forage.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रसरणी and प्रसरणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणि|प्रसरणिः
प्रसरणि<BR>f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>Surrounding an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. अनि, and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरत्
प्रसरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>1 Expanding, spreading, bursting.<BR>2 Proceeding, projecting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पक
प्रसर्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An uninvited guest, an intruder.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृप to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पण|प्रसर्पणं
प्रसर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Spreading, stretching, expanding.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृप to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पत्
प्रसर्पत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>Advancing, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृप to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव|प्रसवः
प्रसव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Bringing forth, bearing, (as young.)<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Offspring, posterity.<BR>4 Fruit.<BR>5 A blossom, a flower.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सू to bear, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवक|प्रसवकः
प्रसवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, commonly Piyāl, (Buchanania latifolia).<BR>E.<BR>प्रसव a flower, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवत्
प्रसवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Bearing.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A woman in labour.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सू to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवबन्धन|प्रसवबंधन|प्रसवबन्धनं
प्रसवबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The footstalk of a leaf or flower, the petiole or peduncle.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसव a flower, and बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थली
प्रसवस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसव, and श्यल place, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवितृ
प्रसवितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A father.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सू to bear or have offspring, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसविन्
प्रसविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Having or bearing young.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसव, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव्य|प्रसव्यं
प्रसव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Contrary, reverse, inverted, reverted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र inclined towards, सव्य the left or wrong side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह|प्रसहः
प्रसह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A beast or bird of prey.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सह to be able, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहन|प्रसहनः
प्रसहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A beast or bird of prey.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Embracing, an embrace.<BR>2 Defeat.<BR>3 Bearing, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सह to bear, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=581" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्य
प्रसह्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Forcibly, violently.<BR>2 Exceedingly.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excessively, सह to be able, यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्यचौर|प्रसह्यचौरः
प्रसह्यचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A robber, a plunderer.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसह्य violently, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाद|प्रसादः
प्रसाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Clearness, cleanness, brightness.<BR>2 Favour, kindness, propitiousness, approbation.<BR>3 Well being, welfare.<BR>4 Composure, calmness of mind.<BR>5 Poetry written in an elegant but an easy style.<BR>6 Perspicuity.<BR>7 Connexion, association.<BR>8 Food that has been offered to an idol, or of which a spiritual teacher has partaken.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सद to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादन|प्रसादनं|प्रसादनः
प्रसादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Boiled rice.<BR>2 Cleaning, freeing from soil or impurities.<BR>3 Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Worship.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सद to go, aff. ल्युट्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादयत्
प्रसादयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Pleasing, propitiating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सद to go, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादस्थ
प्रसादस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Kind, propitious.<BR>2 Happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसाद, and स्थ who or what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादित
प्रसादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased, propitiated.<BR>2 Worshipped.<BR>3 Purified, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षद to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधक|प्रसाधकः
प्रसाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Who or what accomplishes or perfects.<BR>2 Who or what cleanses or purifies.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Wild rice.<BR>2 A dresser, a female attendant, one who decorates or adorns.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before साध to accomplish, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधन|प्रसाधनं|प्रसाधनः
प्रसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Dress, decoration, embellishment.<BR>2 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A comb.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A drug, commonly Siddhi.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before साध to accomplish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधित|प्रसाधितः
प्रसाधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ornamented, decorated.<BR>2 Accomplished, completed, done.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before साध to finish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाध्य
प्रसाध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Accomplishable, what may be done.<BR>2 To be done for, destroyed, defeated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and साध to accomplish, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसार|प्रसारः
प्रसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Going about, spreading, extending.<BR>2 Going to forage, spreading over the country for grass and fuel.<BR>E.<BR>प्र afar, सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारण|प्रसारणं
प्रसारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going about, spreading.<BR>2 Expanding, extending.<BR>3 Unfolding.<BR>4 Surrounding an enemy.<BR>5 The dispersion of an army by detachments for that purpose, or for collecting forage.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Pœderia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रसरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारित
प्रसारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stretched, expanded, extended.<BR>2 Laid out.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारिन्
प्रसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Going along gently, gliding, flowing, creeping.<BR>2 Spreading, expanding.<BR>3 Spreading around, or about.<BR>4 Expanded, unfolded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसित|प्रसितं
प्रसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Diligent, attentive, adhering to, or engaged in.<BR>2 Ingrossed by, devoted or attached to.<BR>3 Bound, fastened.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pus, matter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षिञ् to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिति|प्रसितिः
प्रसिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Ligament, fetters, binding, tye.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षिञ् to bind, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्ध|प्रसिद्धः
प्रसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated.<BR>2 Adorned, ornamented.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धि|प्रसिद्धिः
प्रसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Fame, celebrity, notoriety.<BR>2 Ornament, decoration.<BR>3 That which is notorious or known.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षिध to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्त
प्रसुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Sleeping, asleep, fast asleep.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and सुप्त slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A mare.<BR>3 A spreading creeper.<BR>4 The plantain.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सू to bear, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूका
प्रसूका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूत|प्रसूतं|प्रसूतः
प्रसूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born, engendered.<BR>2 Bearing, bringing forth, delivered.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A flower.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman who has borne a child, or one who is recently delivered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षू to bear, aff. क्त, fem. aff. टाप्; also प्रसूतिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूति|प्रसूतिः
प्रसूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Bringing forth, (as young.)<BR>2 Birth, production.<BR>3 Offspring, children, a son or daughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षू to bear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman who has had a child, or one who has been recently delivered.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसूता the same, pleonastic aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिज|प्रसूतिजं
प्रसूतिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Pain, affliction, mental or corporeal.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसूति birth, and ज produced; attending man from birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसून|प्रसूनं
प्रसून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Born, produced.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A flower, a bud, a blossom.<BR>2 Fruit.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षू to bear, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनेषु|प्रसूनेषुः
प्रसूनेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसून a flower, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत|प्रसृतं|प्रसृतः
प्रसृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dispersed, extended, spread abroad.<BR>2 Stretched.<BR>3 Long, lengthened.<BR>4 Modest, humble.<BR>5 Swift, quick.<BR>6 Gone.<BR>7 Attached to, engaged in, occupied.<BR>8 Appointed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The palm of the hand, hollowed as if to hold liquids.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The leg.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A measure of two Palas.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृति|प्रसृतिः
प्रसृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The palm of the hand hollowed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सृ to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेक|प्रसेकः
प्रसेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>2 Dropping, oozing.<BR>3 Running or watering of the mouth and nose.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सिच to sprinkle, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिका
प्रसेदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small garden.<BR>E.<BR>प्र excellence, सद to go, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिवस्
प्रसेदिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-टुषी-वस्)<BR>Pleased, propitiated, favourable.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षद to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेव|प्रसेवः
प्रसेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Part of a lute: see the next.<BR>2 A sack.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षिव to tie or sew, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवक|प्रसेवकः
प्रसेवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A part of a lute, a wooden vessel covered with leather, placed under the neck to render the sound deeper.<BR>2 A crooked piece of wood at the end of a lute.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before षेव to serve, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दन|प्रस्कंदन|प्रस्कंदनं|प्रस्कन्दनं|प्रस्कन्दनः
प्रस्कन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Purging, diarrhœa.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्कन्द to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दिका|प्रस्कंदिका
प्रस्कन्दिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Diarrhœa.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before खन्द to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्न|प्रस्कन्नः
प्रस्कन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Fallen, dropped.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A sinner, an outcast, one who has violated the usages of his caste or order.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्कन्द to go, to drop, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तर|प्रस्तरः
प्रस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A stone or rock.<BR>2 A jewel, a precious stone.<BR>3 A couch, made of flowers or grass.<BR>4 Any bed or couch.<BR>5 A tabular form of representing the long and short vowels of poetical metre.<BR>6 Notation of music.<BR>7 A handful or bundle of Kuśa grass used at sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तृ to spread, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=582" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तार|प्रस्तारः
प्रस्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A jungle, a thicket or wood, overgrown with grass.<BR>2 A bed made with blossoms, leaves, &c.<BR>3 Any bed or couch.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तृ to spread, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्ताव|प्रस्तावः
प्रस्ताव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Opportunity, occasion, season.<BR>2 Occasional or introductory eulogium.<BR>3 Subject matter of a composition.<BR>4 A chapter, a section.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तु to praise, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावना
प्रस्तावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Commencement, introduction.<BR>2 A dramatic prelude, an introductory dialogue, usually spoken by the manager and one of the actors.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तु to praise, aff. ल्युट्; the commencement of books, &c. being usually the praise of gods or princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावसदृश
प्रस्तावसदृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Suited to the occasion, appropriate, seasonable.<BR>E.<BR>प्रस्ताव, and सदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तिर|प्रस्तिरः
प्रस्तिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bed or couch made of blossoms, flowers, leaves, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तॄ to spread, aff. अच्, and इर substituted for अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीत|प्रस्तीतः
प्रस्तीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Crowded, clustering.<BR>2 Sounded, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्त्यै to crowd, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीम
प्रस्तीम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Crowded together, swarming, clustering.<BR>2 Sounded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्त्यै to crowd, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुत|प्रस्तुतः
प्रस्तुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said, revealed, propounded, declared.<BR>2 Ready, prepared.<BR>3 Praised, panegyrised.<BR>4 Accomplished, done.<BR>5 Happened, come to pass.<BR>6 Made or consisting of.<BR>7 Approached, proximate.<BR>8 Done with effort or energy.<BR>9 Expected, desired.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तृत|प्रस्तृतः
प्रस्तृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread.<BR>2 Disappeared.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्तृ to spread, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Expanding, spread.<BR>2 What stays well, firm, solid.<BR>3 Who goes on a journey or march, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A measure of quantity, four Kuḍavas, or forty-eight double handfuls.<BR>2 Table land on the top of a mountain.<BR>3 A level expanse.<BR>4 A Prastha of any thing, or any thing measuring a Prastha.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stand, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थपुष्प|प्रस्थपुष्पः
प्रस्थपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A sort of Tulasi, or basil with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>प्रस्थ the top of a mountain, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थान|प्रस्थानं
प्रस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going forth, proceeding, departing.<BR>2 March of an assailant.<BR>3 March.<BR>4 An inferior kind of drama, the personages of which are slaves and outcastes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र away, away from, स्था to stay, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानविघ्न|प्रस्थानविघ्नः
प्रस्थानविघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Non-attendance at a festival, impeding its taking place, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रस्थान proceeding, and विघ्न obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानिक
प्रस्थानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a departure.<BR>E.<BR>प्रस्थान, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापन|प्रस्थापनं
प्रस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sending away.<BR>2 Appointment on an embassy.<BR>3 Harrying, carrying off cattle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापनीय
प्रस्थापनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be sent away.<BR>2 To be carried or driven off.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stay, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापित|प्रस्थापितः
प्रस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, dispatched.<BR>2 Sent away, dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र reverse, स्था to stay, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थायिन्
प्रस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Who or what goes, travels, marches, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stay, इनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थित
प्रस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, departed, set forth, (on a journey, a march, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stay, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थिति|प्रस्थितिः
प्रस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Going forth or away.<BR>2 Journey.<BR>3 March.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुट|प्रस्फुटः
प्रस्फुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Blown, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्फुट to blossom, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुरित
प्रस्फुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Swollen.<BR>2 Budded.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्फुर to expand, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फोटन|प्रस्फोटनं
प्रस्फोटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A winnowing basket.<BR>2 Striking, beating.<BR>3 Expanding, budding, opening, blowing.<BR>4 Winnowing corn.<BR>5 Ripening.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्फट to blossom, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्मृति|प्रस्मृतिः
प्रस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Forgetfulness, forgetting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र privative, स्मृति recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रवण|प्रस्रवणं|प्रस्रवणः
प्रस्रवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A pool of water formed by dripping of springs in the mountains.<BR>2 Dripping or fall of water, cascade, cataract.<BR>3 Washing away of rocks, &c. by the dripping of water.<BR>4 Oozing, leaking, dripping.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Sweat, perspiration.<BR>2 Pissing, urining.<BR>3 A range of mountains in the peninsula; also Malayavān.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्रु to drop, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रश्रबण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्राव|प्रस्रावः
प्रस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Flowing, dropping.<BR>2 Urine.<BR>E.<BR>प्र forth, स्रु to ooze, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रुत
प्रस्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Oozed, issued, dropped.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्रु to drop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वान|प्रस्वानः
प्रस्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A loud noise.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्वन to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्विन्न
प्रस्विन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Perspiring, covered with perspiration.<BR>2 Heated, sweated.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्विद to sweat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेद|प्रस्वेदः
प्रस्वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Great or excessive perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>प्र intensitive, स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदित
प्रस्वेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Perspiring, sweating.<BR>2 Heated, sweated.<BR>3 Hot, causing perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before स्विद to sweat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदितवत्
प्रस्वेदितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Suffering or producing perspiration.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ष्विद to sweat, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणेमि|प्रहणेमिः
प्रहणेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहत|प्रहतं
प्रहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Struck, wounded, killed.<BR>2 Repelled, repulsed, overcome, defeated.<BR>3 Spread, expanded.<BR>4 Contiguous, bounding, limitative.<BR>5 Learned, accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>प्र again, and हत struck, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर|प्रहरः
प्रहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A watch, an 8th part of the day, or a division comprising about three hours.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरण|प्रहरणं
प्रहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>2 A covered car, a litter for women, or any litter, or small covered car for diversion.<BR>3 War, battle.<BR>4 Striking, killing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणकलिका
प्रहरणकलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A species of the Śarkarī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिन्
प्रहरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A watchman, a bellman.<BR>E.<BR>प्रहर a watch, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिष्यत्
प्रहरिष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Taking, intending or wishing to take.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, हृ to take, with a future sense, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्त्तृ|प्रहर्तृ
प्रहर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Striking, a striker, a combatant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्ष|प्रहर्षः
प्रहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Delight, joy, rapture.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृष to rejoice, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षण|प्रहर्षणं|प्रहर्षणः
प्रहर्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Happy, delighted.<BR>2 Delighting.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The planet Mercury, or its ruler.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Turmerick.<BR>2 A form of metre.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृष to rejoice, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षिणी
प्रहर्षिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=583" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षित
प्रहर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Delighted, very happy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृष to rejoice, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसत्|प्रहसन्त्
प्रहसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Laughing, laughing heartily.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हस to smile, aff. शतृ; fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसन|प्रहसनं
प्रहसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Loud, violent or hearty laughter.<BR>2 Mirth, merriment.<BR>3 Sarcasm, satire, as a branch of rhetorical composition.<BR>4 Reproof, ridicule, irony.<BR>5 A farce, a comedy.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हस to laugh, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसित
प्रहसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Laughter, mirth.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and हस to laugh, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्त|प्रहस्तः
प्रहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR>E.<BR>प्र exchanging, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहापण
प्रहापण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Driving away, forced abandonment or departure.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हा to quit, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहार|प्रहारः
प्रहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Striking, wounding, killing.<BR>2 A blow.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारण|प्रहारणं
प्रहारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A desirable gift.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रवारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारार्त्त|प्रहारार्त
प्रहारार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Bruised, wounded, hurt by a blow.<BR>n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>Lasting and acute pain from a wound or maim.<BR>E.<BR>प्रहार striking, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहास|प्रहासः
प्रहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Loud laughter.<BR>2 Blowing, (as a flower.)<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 An actor, a dancer.<BR>5 A place of pilgrimage; also सोमतीर्थ.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हस to laugh, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासिन्
प्रहासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Laughing aloud.<BR>2 Diverting, causing laughter.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A jester, a buffoon, a clown.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हस to laugh, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहि|प्रहिः
प्रहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A well.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृ to take, Uṇādi aff. इन्, and the final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहित|प्रहितं
प्रहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, dispatched.<BR>2 Appointed, commissioned.<BR>3 Stretched out, extended.<BR>4 Placed.<BR>5 Discharged, as an arrow from a bow.<BR>6 Learned.<BR>7 Suitable, appropriate.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sauce, gravy, condiment.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीण|प्रहीणः
प्रहीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Left, abandoned.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Removal, loss, waste, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हा to quit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीणजीवित
प्रहीणजीवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead, slain.<BR>E.<BR>प्रहीण, and जीवित life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुत|प्रहुतं|प्रहुतः
प्रहुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Offering articles of food to spirits or goblins.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हुत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृत
प्रहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seized.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Striking, killing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्ट
प्रहृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Pleased, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृष to be pleased, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टक|प्रहृष्टकः
प्रहृष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हृष्ट pleased, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेणक|प्रहेणकं
प्रहेणक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Victuals or sweetmeats, &c. distributed at festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलक|प्रहेलकं|प्रहेलकः
प्रहेलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sweetmeats, &c. distributed at festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलिका
प्रहेलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An enigma, a riddle, a puzzling or enigmatical question.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हिल to play, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्राद|प्रह्रादः
प्रह्राद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A prince: see प्रह्लाद.<BR>E.<BR>ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लत्ति|प्रह्लत्तिः
प्रह्लत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Pleasure, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्लद to be glad, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्न|प्रह्लन्नः
प्रह्लन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Pleased, happy, glad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्लाद to be happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्नि|प्रह्लन्निः
प्रह्लन्नि<BR>f. (-न्निः)<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्लद to be happy, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लाद|प्रह्लादः
प्रह्लाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Pleasure, joy, happiness.<BR>2 Sound, noise.<BR>3 The name of HIRAṆYĀKṢA'S pious son and regent of one division of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्लाद gladness or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादित
प्रह्लादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rejoiced, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>प्रह्लाद to be happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्व|प्रह्वः
प्रह्व<BR>mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>1 Bowed, bent, stooping.<BR>2 Intent upon, engaged in, engrossed by.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्वेञ् to call, Uṇādi aff. वन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वाञ्जलि|प्रह्वांजलि
प्रह्वाञ्जलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Stooping or bowing with the palm of the hands joined, and put to the forehead in token of respect.<BR>E.<BR>प्रह्व, and अञ्जलि salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वाय|प्रह्वायः
प्रह्वाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Calling, summoning, invocation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ह्वे to call, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वीकृत
प्रह्वीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Conquered, won, subjected.<BR>2 Bent, bowed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रह्व, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रा
प्रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (प्राति)<BR>To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशु|प्रांशुः
प्रांशु<BR>mfn. (-शुः-शुः-शु)<BR>High, tall, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अंशु a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्
प्राक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Before, prior, preceding, in place or time.<BR>2 East, eastern.<BR>3 Past, gone.<BR>4 First.<BR>5 Between, amongst, amidst.<BR>6 At dawn, early in the morning.<BR>E.<BR>see प्राच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकषिक|प्राकषिकः
प्राकषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A catamite.<BR>2 A dancer, but especially one who employs or hires the wives of others, one who gets his livelihood by another man's wife.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् prefixed to कष to go, Uṇādi aff. किकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाम्य|प्राकाम्यं
प्राकाम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Irresistible will or fiat, one of ŚIVA'S eight attributes.<BR>2 Wilfulness, following or obeying one's own will or inclination.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before कम to desire, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकार|प्राकारः
प्राकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An inclosure, a fence, a rampart, particularly a surrounding wall, &c. elevated on a mound of earth.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् implying initial, first, कृ to make, aff. घञ्; otherwise the prefix is considered as प्र only, the vowel being made long by the affix being घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारीय
प्राकारीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Walled, enclosed by a wall.<BR>2 Of, belonging to, or fit for a wall.<BR>E.<BR>प्राकार, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृत|प्राकृतः
प्राकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Low, common, vulgar, thence especially applicable to a provincial and peculiar dialect of the Sanskrit language.<BR>2 Natural.<BR>3 Belonging to or derived from the philosophical Prakṛti, illusory, material, &c.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A low man or one following a degraded profession.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Any dialect not Sanskrit, it is especially spoken by the female characters and the inferior personages of plays.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकति nature, and अण् aff., or प्र pre-eminently, and अकृत not made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतज्वर|प्राकृतज्वरः
प्राकृतज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Common or usual fever, occurring from affections of the wind, bile, and phlegm, severally, in as many seasons, or the rains, autumn, and spring.<BR>E.<BR>प्राकृत, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतप्रलय|प्राकृतप्रलयः
प्राकृतप्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The total dissolution of the world.<BR>E.<BR>प्राकृत material, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमानुष|प्राकृतमानुषः
प्राकृतमानुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A man in general.<BR>E.<BR>प्राकृत, and मानुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमिच
प्राकृतमिच<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A natural friend or ally; as applied to a sovereign, it means one whose states are removed by an intervening [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">Page585</a>] kingdom from those to which it should be friendly, the प्राकृतारि or natural enemy is the chief of the intervening state, and the प्राकृतोदासीनः or natural neutral is the outer one of the four.<BR>E.<BR>प्राकृत natural, and मिच a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=584" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतिक|प्राकृतिकः
प्राकृतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to Prakṛti, nature or matter, material, natural, illusory, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रकृति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्कूल
प्राक्कूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The tip of Kusa grass placed to the east.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्, and कूल point of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्काल|प्राक्कालः
प्राक्काल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Former age or time.<BR>E.<BR>प्राच्, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्कालीन
प्राक्कालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Anterior, ancient, of a former time.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्काल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>2 Prior, anterior, preceding, former.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् formerly, द्युल् aff., and तन् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तनकर्म्मन्|प्राक्तनकर्मन्
प्राक्तनकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Fate, destiny.<BR>2 Any act formerly done.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्तन prior, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फल्गुणी
प्राक्फल्गुणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The eleventh of the lunar asterisms: see पूर्व्वफल्गुण.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् preceding, and फल्गुणी the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फल्गुणीभव
प्राक्फल्गुणीभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्फल्गुणी, and भय born, born when the moon was in that mansion; also similar compounds, as प्राक्फल्गुणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फाल्गुण
प्राक्फाल्गुण<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्फल्गुणी, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्सन्ध्या|प्राक्संध्या
प्राक्सन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>Dawn.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् the first, सन्ध्य junction of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्शिरस
प्राक्शिरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Facing the east.<BR>2 Having the head to the east in burial.<BR>E.<BR>प्राच्, and शिरम the head, मच added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राखर्य्य|प्राखर्य|प्राखर्यं|प्राखर्य्यं
प्राखर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Sharpness.<BR>2 Pungency.<BR>3 Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रखर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागभाव|प्रागभावः
प्रागभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Antecedent privation, the non-existence of any thing which may yet be. In law, the non-possession of property that may be possessed.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् prior, अ negative, and भाव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्य|प्रागल्भ्यं
प्रागल्भ्य<BR>n. (-ल्भ्यं)<BR>1 Confidence, boldness, determination.<BR>2 Arrogance, effrontery.<BR>3 Importance, rank.<BR>E.<BR>प्रगल्भ confident, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागुदीची
प्रागुदीची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The north-east.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् the east, and उदीची the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागुदीची
प्रागुदीची<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going before, a precursor.<BR>E.<BR>प्राच, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्ज्योतिष|प्राग्ज्योतिषः
प्राग्ज्योतिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A country, Kāmarūpa, part of Asam.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् formerly, ज्योतिष light; being the scene of BRAHMĀ'S penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भार|प्राग्भारः
प्राग्भार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The top or peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् first, भार burthen; also read प्राग्भाव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भाव|प्राग्भावः
प्राग्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Prior existence.<BR>2 Superiority, excellence.<BR>3 The top of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक्, and भाव being or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भावतस्
प्राग्भावतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From a prior state of being.<BR>E.<BR>प्राग्भाव, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रहर|प्राग्रहरः
प्राग्रहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and अग्र first, हर who surpasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्राट|प्राग्राटं|प्राग्राटः
प्राग्राट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Thin curds.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अग्र the top, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्र्य|प्राग्र्यं
प्राग्र्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं)<BR>Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>प्र prefixed to अग्र्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्वंश|प्राग्वंशः
प्राग्वंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The room opposite to that which contains the materials for an oblation, and in which the family and friends of the sacrificer assemble.<BR>2 A former dynasty or race.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् before, and वंश a race, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघात|प्राघातः
प्राघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before हन to kill, aff. घञ्, and the vowel of the prefix optionally made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघार|प्राघारः
प्राघार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Dropping, oozing, trickling, aspersion, or pouring out of any oily substance.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before घृ^1 to sprinkle or drop, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुण|प्राघुणः
प्राघुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A guest, a visitor, one demanding hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before घुण to turn round, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघूर्णिक|प्राघूर्णिकः
प्राघूर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A guest.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before घूर्ण going about, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्ग|प्रांग|प्रांगं|प्राङ्गः
प्राङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sort of small tabor or drum.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अञ्ज to go or be, aff. ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्गण|प्रांगण|प्रांगणं|प्राङ्गणं
प्राङ्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A sort of drum.<BR>2 A court, a yard.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अगि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्न्याय|प्राङ्न्यायः
प्राङ्न्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Plea of a former trial, special plea.<BR>E.<BR>प्राक् former, न्याय proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्मुख
प्राङ्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खी-खं)<BR>Facing the east.<BR>E.<BR>प्राञ्च्, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्
प्राच् or प्राञ्च<BR>mfn. (प्राङ् प्राची प्राक्)<BR>1 East, eastern.<BR>2 Before, in front.<BR>3 Former, prior, first.<BR>4 At top, above.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The east.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अञ्ज to go, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार
प्राचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Contrary to rectitude, deviating from the ordinary institutions and observances.<BR>E.<BR>प्र reverse, and आचार ordinance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार्य्य|प्राचार्य|प्राचार्यः
प्राचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A scholar, a pupil.<BR>E.<BR>प्र meaning प्राप्त obtained, and आचार्य्य a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचिका
प्राचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A musquito.<BR>2 The female falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 East, eastern.<BR>2 Former, prior, ancient, old.<BR>3 Placed towards the east.<BR>fn. (-ना-नं)<BR>A bound hedge, a fence, a wall.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>2 The ichneumon plant: see रास्ना.<BR>E.<BR>प्राच् the east, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनतिलक|प्राचीनतिलकः
प्राचीनतिलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीन eastern, and तिलक mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनपनस|प्राचीनपनसः
प्राचीनपनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीन् eastern, and पनस the jack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनवर्हिस्
प्राचीनवर्हिस्<BR>m. (-र्हिः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 A king.<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीन eastern, and वर्हिस् light; presiding over the eastern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनामलक|प्राचीनामलकं
प्राचीनामलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीन eastern, आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनावीत|प्राचीनावीतं
प्राचीनावीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The sacrificial thread, worn over the right arm, and passing under the left, as at Śrāddhas.<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीन east, and आवीत hung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनावीतिन्
प्राचीनावीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A Brahman wearing his cord over his right shoulder, as at Śrāddhas.<BR>E.<BR>प्राचीतावीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीपति|प्राचीपतिः
प्राचीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>प्राची the east, and पति master, regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीर|प्राचीरं
प्राचीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A bound hedge, a fence, a wall, an inclosure, a rampart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ prefixed to चि to collect, aff. क्रन्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतस|प्राचेतसः
प्राचेतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>VĀLMĪKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>m. plu. (-साः)<BR>The ten sons of Prācīnavarhis.<BR>E.<BR>प्रचेतस, the father of the poet, and अण् aff.; it also occurs प्राचेतस् (-ताः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>Eastern, easterly.<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>The eastern country, the country south or east of the SARASVATĪ, which [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">Page586</a>] flows from the north-east to the south-west.<BR>E.<BR>प्राच् the east, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=585" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्छ्|प्राछ्
प्राच्छ्<BR>m. (-प्राट)<BR>An inquirer, a questioner.<BR>E.<BR>प्रच्छ to ask, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजक|प्राजकः
प्राजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A coachman, a driver.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अज to go, causal form, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजन|प्राजनं|प्राजनः
प्राजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A goad.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अज to go, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A form of marriage, the gift of a girl, respectfully by her father to her lover.<BR>2 A name of Allahabad or Prayāga.<BR>3 The first of the persons, called Vāsudevas, by the Jainas.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 A sort of penance, eating once a day for three days in the morning, once in the night for three days, subsisting three days on food given as alms, and fasting three days more.<BR>2 A particular sacrifice performed before appointing a daughter to raise issue in default of male heirs.<BR>3 The asterism Rohiṇī.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Giving away the whole of one's property before entering upon the life of an ascetic or mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रजापति BRAHMĀ, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजितृ
प्राजितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A coachman, a charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अज to go, causal v., तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञ|प्राज्ञः
प्राज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Patient in investigation.<BR>2 Wise, clever, sensible.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a learned or wise man.<BR>2 A skilful or clever man.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>Knowledge, understanding.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा-ज्ञी)<BR>A clever or intelligent woman.<BR>f. (-ज्ञी)<BR>The wife of a Paṇḍita.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ before ज्ञा to know, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञत्व
प्राज्ञत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Learning, wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>प्राज्ञ, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, प्राज्ञता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञमान|प्राज्ञमानः
प्राज्ञमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Respect for learned men.<BR>E.<BR>प्राज्ञ, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञमानिन्
प्राज्ञमानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Respecting men of learning.<BR>E.<BR>प्राज्ञमान, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्य|प्राज्यं
प्राज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अञ्ज to pervade, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जल|प्रांजल|प्राञ्जलः
प्राञ्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Honest, upright, sincere.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अञ्ज to go, aff. अलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलि|प्रांजलि
प्राञ्जलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Putting the hands together to the forehead, a mark of respect.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and अञ्जलि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राड्विवाक|प्राड्विवाकः
प्राड्विवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A judge, a magistrate.<BR>E.<BR>प्राट् who asks, and विवाक् who decides or discriminates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण|प्राणः
प्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Full, replete, filled.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Air inhaled, inspiration, breath.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 Life, vitality.<BR>4 A vital organ or part.<BR>5 Strength, power.<BR>6 Myrrh.<BR>7 Poetical talent or inspiration.<BR>8 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>9 A title of BRAHMĀ, the supreme spirit.<BR>10 An aspiration in the articulation of letters.<BR>m. plu. (-णाः)<BR>The five vital airs or modes of inspiration and expiration collectively.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अन to breathe, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणक|प्राणकः
प्राणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An animal or sentient being.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes.<BR>3 A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणकर्म्मन्|प्राणकर्मन्
प्राणकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Vital action.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणत्|प्राणन्त्
प्राणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>Living, breathing.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण nominal v. to live, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणत्याग|प्राणत्यागः
प्राणत्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Abandoning life, dying, suicide.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and त्याग relinquishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणथ|प्राणथः
प्राणथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A strong or powerful man.<BR>3 A progenitor of mankind.<BR>4 A place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अन to breathe or be strong, Uṇādi aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणद|प्राणदं|प्राणदः
प्राणद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what gives life.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Blood.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणधारण
प्राणधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sustenance, supporting life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and धारण upholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन|प्राणनं|प्राणनः
प्राणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Life, living.<BR>2 The throat.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अन to live or breathe, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणनाथ|प्राणनाथः
प्राणनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन्त|प्राणंत|प्राणंतः|प्राणन्तः
प्राणन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A sort of collyrium: see रसाञ्जन.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 Sneezing.<BR>2 Hickup.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अन to breathe, Uṇādi aff. भच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणपरिग्रह|प्राणपरिग्रहः
प्राणपरिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Life, existence.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and परिग्रह possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणप्रद
प्राणप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Saving life, when in imminent danger.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and प्रद who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणप्रदा
प्राणप्रदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, प्रद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणबाध
प्राणबाध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Extreme peril or distress, fear for life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and बाध obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणभास्वत्|प्राणभास्वन्त्
प्राणभास्वत्<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, भास्वत् the sun, the sun being produced or rising from the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणभृत्
प्राणभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Living, sentient.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमय
प्राणमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Living, breathing, endowed with breath or life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमयकोष|प्राणमयकोषः
प्राणमयकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>One of the cases or investitures of the soul, the vital or organic case.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणमय, and कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयत्
प्राणयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Rescuing, restoring to life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण nom. v. caus. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयात्रा
प्राणयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>Support of life, subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and यात्रा proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणव्यय|प्राणव्ययः
प्राणव्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Death, expenditure of life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and व्यय expence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसंयम|प्राणसंयमः
प्राणसंयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A peculiar religious exercise: see पाणायाम.<BR>2 Suspending the breath.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण breath, सम् before यम to restrain, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसद्मन्
प्राणसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण vital air, and सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसमा
प्राणसमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, समा equal to, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहर
प्राणहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Destructive, taking away life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and हर who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहारक|प्राणहारकं
प्राणहारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Aconite.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and हारक what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहारिन्
प्राणहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Mortal, deadly.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and हारिन् what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाद
प्राणाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Fatal, deadly.<BR>E.<BR>प्राश, and अद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाधिनाथ|प्राणाधिनाथः
प्राणाधिनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, अधि over, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणान्त|प्राणांत|प्राणान्तः
प्राणान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Death.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणान्तिक|प्राणांतिक
प्राणान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Fatal, destructive of life.<BR>2 Capital, (as punishment.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Murder, assassination.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and अन्तिक final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणापहारिन्
प्राणापहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Deadly, fatal.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and अपहारिन् what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=586" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणापान
प्राणापान<BR>m. du. (-नौ)<BR>1 The Aśvinī kumāras.<BR>2 Two of the vital airs.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and अपान the air expelled by the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाबाध|प्राणाबाधः
प्राणाबाध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Any act injurious to life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण, and आङ् before वाध to pain, अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणायाम|प्राणायामः
प्राणायाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Breathing in a peculiar way through the nostrils, during the mental recitation of the names or attributes of some deity; it is differently performed: the Vaidyas or followers of the Veda close the right nostril first with the thumb, and inhale breath through the left, then they close both nostrils, and finally open the right for exhalation: the followers of the Tantras close the left nostril first, and exhale also through it; these operations are severally called पुरक, कुम्भक, and रेचक.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण breath, आ before यम to restrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिणिषु
प्राणिणिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing for life.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण nom. v., desid. form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिद्यूत|प्राणिद्यूतं
प्राणिद्यूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Cock fighting, ram fighting, setting animals to fight for wagers.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणि a living being, and द्यूत gaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिन्
प्राणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Living, breathing.<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>An animal, a sentient or living being.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण vital air, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिपीडा
प्राणिपीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Cruelty to animals.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणिन्, and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिमाता
प्राणिमाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A mother.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणिन्, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिहिंसा
प्राणिहिंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Doing harm to any living creature.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणि, and हिंसा injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिहित
प्राणिहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Favourable or good for living beings.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A shoe, a boot.<BR>E.<BR>प्राणि an animal, (man,) and हित suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणीत्य|प्राणीत्यं
प्राणीत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Debt.<BR>E.<BR>प्रणीत taken, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणेश|प्राणेशः
प्राणेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A husband.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>प्राण life, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्यङ्ग|प्राण्यंग
प्राण्यङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Any animal part or product, (as flesh, bone, milk, Ghee, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्राणिन, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःकृत्य|प्रातःकृत्यं
प्रातःकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Morning duty or ceremonies, worship, ablution, purification, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर, and कृत्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःसन्ध्या|प्रातःसंध्या
प्रातःसन्ध्या<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>1 Dawn.<BR>2 The morning sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर, and सन्ध्या part of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःसमय|प्रातःसमयः
प्रातःसमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Early morning, day break.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर्, and समय season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःस्नान|प्रातःस्नानं
प्रातःस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Morning ablution, bathing at sun-rise.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर्, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्
प्रातर्<BR>ind.<BR>Morning, dawn.<BR>E.<BR>प्र initial, अत to go, अर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातराश|प्रातराशः
प्रातराश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The morning meal, breakfast.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर् morning, अश to eat, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातराशित
प्रातराशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Breakfasted, having had the morning meal.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर, and आशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्गेय|प्रातर्गेयः
प्रातर्गेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be sung or chanted in the morning.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A minstrel, a bard, but one who especially wakes the sovereign or prince by his morning chant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर् in the morning, गेय to be sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्भोक्तृ
प्रातर्भोक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>Who or what eats early.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर् morning, and भोक्तृ who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्भोजन|प्रातर्भोजनं
प्रातर्भोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Breakfast, the morning meal.<BR>E.<BR>प्रातर् morning, and भाजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिका
प्रातिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Decrepitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूलिक
प्रातिकूलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Opposed to, opposing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिकूल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूल्य|प्रातिकूल्यं
प्रातिकूल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Contrariety, contradiction, opposition.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिकूल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिजनीन
प्रातिजनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fit for or suitable to dependants, family, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिजन, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष
प्रातिपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>1 Hostile, belonging to an enemy.<BR>2 Adverse, contrary.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपक्ष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपदिक|प्रातिपदिकः
प्रातिपदिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A crude noun, a noun before any of its inflections are formed with appropriate affixes.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and अति before पद an inflected word, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपथिक|प्रातिपथिकः
प्रातिपथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Hostile, opposing.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिपथ, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभाव्य|प्रातिभाव्यं
प्रातिभाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Security, the act of becoming bail or surety, or being answerable for the appearance of the debtor, for his being trust-worthy, or for the payment of his debt in case of his failing to do it.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिभू, a security, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोम्य|प्रातिलोम्यं
प्रातिलोम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Inverted order.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिलोम, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्य|प्रातिवेश्यः
प्रातिवेश्य<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>A next-door neighbour.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिवेश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिस्विक|प्रातिस्विकं
प्रातिस्विक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Own, peculiar, proper.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति to or towards, स्व own, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहर
प्रातिहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिहार the same, and अण् pleonastic: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारक|प्रातिहारकः
प्रातिहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to प्रातिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारिक|प्रातिहारिकः
प्रातिहारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler, a conjuror.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतिहार disguise, trick, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीप|प्रातीपः
प्रातीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of ŚĀNTANU.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीप the father of this prince, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीपिक
प्रातीपिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Reverse, contrary, retrograde.<BR>E.<BR>प्रतीप, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्ययिक
प्रात्ययिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Trusty, confidential, having faith in.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A surety.<BR>E.<BR>प्रत्यय, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमकल्पिक|प्राथमकल्पिकः
प्राथमकल्पिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A student, one who has just commenced the perusal of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथम first, कल्प beginning, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमिक|प्राथमिकः
प्राथमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>First, of the first, initial, initiative.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथम, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथम्य|प्राथम्यं
प्राथम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Firstness, priority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रथम, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादक्षिण्य|प्रादक्षिण्यं
प्रादक्षिण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Circumambulation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रदक्षिण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भाव|प्रादुर्भावः
प्रादुर्भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Appearance, manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>प्राटुम्, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्कृत
प्रादुष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Manifested, made apparent.<BR>E.<BR>प्राटुस, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुस्
प्रादुस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Evidently, apparently, manifestly.<BR>2 Visible, apparent.<BR>3 Name, appellation.<BR>4 Existence.<BR>5 Co-existence.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अद to go, or eat, Uṇādi aff. उस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेश|प्रादेशः
प्रादेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The span of the thumb and forefinger.<BR>2 Place, country.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before दिश to shew, aff. घञ्; whence the vowel of the prefix is optionally long: see प्रदेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशन|प्रादेशनं
प्रादेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before दिश to give, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोष|प्रादोषः
प्रादोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Belonging, or relating to the evening.<BR>E.<BR>प्रदोष evening, aff. अण्; also with ठञ् aff. प्रादोषिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=587" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्य|प्राधान्यं
प्राधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Supremacy, superiority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान chief, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्यतस्
प्राधान्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Chiefly.<BR>E.<BR>प्रधान्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधीत
प्राधीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Brahman who has finished his studies.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and अधीत read over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्ययन|प्राध्ययनं
प्राध्ययन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reading, study.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अधि to read through, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्व|प्राध्वं|प्राध्वः
प्राध्व<BR>mfn. (-ध्वः-ध्वा-ध्वं)<BR>1 Distant, remote, long, as a road or journey.<BR>2 Bowed, bent.<BR>3 Binding, confining.<BR>m. (-ध्वः)<BR>A car, a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अध्वन् a road, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्वम्
प्राध्वम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 In conformity, conformably.<BR>2 Crooked, crookedly, stooping.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before ध्वन to sound, aff. डम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्त|प्रांत|प्रांतः|प्रान्तः
प्रान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Edge, margin, border, end.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्ततस्|प्रांततस्
प्रान्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>Bordering, marginally, along or upon the extremity.<BR>E.<BR>प्रान्त the edge, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तदुर्ग|प्रांतदुर्ग
प्रान्तदुर्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>A suburb or collection of houses out of the walls of the town, a Petta, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रान्त skirting, टुर्ग the fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तर|प्रांतर|प्रांतरं|प्रान्तरं
प्रान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A long and unshaded road, a lonesome or tiresome path.<BR>2 A forest.<BR>3 The hollow of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>प्र considerable, अन्तर space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तरशून्य|प्रांतरशून्य|प्रान्तरशून्यः
प्रान्तरशून्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>A long and tiresome road.<BR>E.<BR>प्रान्तर spacious, and शून्य empty, void.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप
प्राप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Watery, abounding with water.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापक|प्रापकः
प्रापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Procuring, causing to obtain.<BR>2 Obtaining, who or what obtains.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप to obtain, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापण|प्रापणं
प्रापण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आप to gain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणिक|प्रापणिकः
प्रापणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A trader, a dealer.<BR>2 A retail dealer.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before पण to deal, to transact business, किकन Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापित
प्रापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Brought, placed.<BR>2 Procured.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आप to gain, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्त|प्राप्तः
प्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Obtained, gained, received, procured.<BR>2 Fixed, placed.<BR>3 Proper, right.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आप to gain, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तकाल|प्राप्तकालः
प्राप्तकाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Fated, destined, one whose fated time has come.<BR>2 Opportune, in season.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तपञ्चत्व|प्राप्तपंचत्व|प्राप्तपञ्चत्वं
प्राप्तपञ्चत्व<BR>mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त obtained, पञ्चत्व death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तबुद्धि
प्राप्तबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>1 Enlightened, instructed, intelligent.<BR>2 Recovering, becoming conscious, (after fainting.)<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तभार|प्राप्तभारः
प्राप्तभार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A draft ox or beast of burthen.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and भार load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तभाव|प्राप्तभावः
प्राप्तभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Wise.<BR>2 Handsome.<BR>3 Of a good disposition.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A bullock.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त gained, भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तरूप|प्राप्तरूपः
प्राप्तरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Learned, wise.<BR>2 Handsome, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त gained or proper, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तार्थ|प्राप्तार्थः
प्राप्तार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-थं)<BR>Successful, having gained an object.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तापराध
प्राप्तापराध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Offending, being in fault.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तावसर|प्राप्तावसरः
प्राप्तावसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opportune, seasonable, taking or finding occasion.<BR>E.<BR>प्राप्त, and अवसर opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्ति|प्राप्तिः
प्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Gain, profit.<BR>2 Acquiring, getting, obtaining.<BR>3 Improvement, success.<BR>4 Rise, ascent.<BR>5 Collection, assemblage, quantity.<BR>6 Happy denouement, successful termination of a plot.<BR>7 Guessing, discovering from a hint.<BR>8 One of the eight superhuman faculties, the power of obtaining every thing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आप to get or obtain, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्य|प्राप्यं
प्राप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Attainable, obtainable.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आप to attain, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबल्य|प्राबल्यं
प्राबल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Power, vigour.<BR>2 Predominance.<BR>E.<BR>प्रबल strong, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधिक|प्राबोधिकः
प्राबोधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Dawn, daybreak.<BR>E.<BR>प्रबोध waking, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभव|प्राभवं
प्राभव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Superiority, pre-eminence.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभु a master, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभवत्य|प्राभवत्यं
प्राभवत्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Power, authority.<BR>E.<BR>प्रभवन् being superior, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृत|प्राभृतं
प्राभृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A present, an offering to a deity or sovereign, or a gift to a friend, a bribe, the Nezer of Hindustan.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before भृ to nourish, aff. क्त; also with कन् aff. प्राभृतक, n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाणिक|प्रामाणिकः
प्रामाणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Exercising or proceeding from some evidence or authority, &c.<BR>2 Being of authority.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A president, the chief or head of a trade, &c.<BR>2 A learned man, one who supports his arguments by reference to books, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण testimony, authority, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्य|प्रामाण्यं
प्रामाण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Authority, proof.<BR>E.<BR>प्रमाण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाद्य|प्रामाद्यं|प्रामाद्यः
प्रामाद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A tree, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Madness, frenzy, fury, intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before मद to delight, aff. अच् and ण्यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामीत्य|प्रामीत्यं
प्रामीत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Debt.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before मा to measure, क्यप् aff., and तुक aug.; also read प्राणीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राय|प्रायः
प्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Like, resembling, (used in composition.)<BR>2 Exceeding, much.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Fasting to death, as a religious or penitentiary act, and especially after abandoning all worldly goods, and desires.<BR>2 Quantity, abundance.<BR>3 Death, dying.<BR>4 A state or condition of life, age, youth, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Sin.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इन् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायण|प्रायणं
प्रायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Death, voluntary death.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायशस्
प्रायशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Usually, commonly, for the most part.<BR>E.<BR>प्राय, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायिक|प्रायिकं
प्रायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Common, usual.<BR>E.<BR>प्राय, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्त|प्रायश्चित्तं
प्रायश्चित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Expiation, penance.<BR>E.<BR>प्राय sin, चित्त or चित्ति reflection, and सुट् aug. hence also प्रायश्चित्ति, f. (-त्तिः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तविधि
प्रायश्चित्तविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Rules for penance or expiation.<BR>E.<BR>प्रायश्चित्त, and विधि rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायस्
प्रायस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Frequently, generally, for the most part.<BR>2 Abundantly, largely.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इण् or अय to go, aff. असुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायुधेषिन्
प्रायुधेषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>प्र mostly, आयुध a weapon, इप् to wish, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोपवेशन
प्रायोपवेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fasting to death.<BR>E.<BR>प्राय, and उपवेशन sitting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोपवेशनिका
प्रायोपवेशनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sitting down to die by fasting.<BR>E.<BR>प्राय, उपवेश sitting down, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्ध|प्रारब्धं
प्रारब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Begun, beginning.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before रभ to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्धि|प्रारब्धिः
प्रारब्धि<BR>f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>1 Beginning, commencement.<BR>2 A rope or fastening for an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before रभ to commence, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=588" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारम्भ|प्रारंभ|प्रारंभः|प्रारम्भः
प्रारम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Beginning.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before रभि to begin, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थक|प्रार्थकः
प्रार्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Asking, an asker, a solicitor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to seek, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थन|प्रार्थनं
प्रार्थन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to ask, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थनीय|प्रार्थनीयं
प्रार्थनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be asked or begged.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The third or Dvāpara age of the world.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to ask, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितृ
प्रार्थयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>One who asks or solicits, a beggar, an inquirer, a solicitor.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to seek, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थित|प्रार्थितः
प्रार्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Asked, begged, solicited.<BR>2 Said, spoken.<BR>3 Obstructed or opposed by an enemy.<BR>4 Killed, hurt.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to ask, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थितवत्
प्रार्थितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अर्थ to ask, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्ब|प्रालंब|प्रालम्बं|प्रालम्बः
प्रालम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A garland hanging round the neck, and reaching to the breast.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before लवि to hang or fall, aff. अच्; also with कन् added प्रालम्बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्बिका|प्रालंबिका
प्रालम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A garland, a necklace.<BR>E.<BR>प्रालम्ब a garland, &c. कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
प्रालेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Frost.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before लीच् to unite with, aff. अच्; प्रलय here said to mean a mountain, अण् aff. of derivation, and the penultimate vowel changed to ए.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेयांशु|प्रालेयांशुः
प्रालेयांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>प्रालेय frost or cold, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावट|प्रावटः
प्रावट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before वट to encompass. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर|प्रावरः
प्रावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An inclosure, a fence, a hedge.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before वृ to surround, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरण|प्रावरणं
प्रावरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 An upper or outer garment.<BR>2 Any covering.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before वृ to cover, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावार|प्रावारः
प्रावार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An upper or outer garment, a cloak, a mantle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ with आङ् prefix, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारकीट|प्रावारकीटः
प्रावारकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A body louse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रावार the outward garment, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावीण्य|प्रावीण्यं
प्रावीण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Cleverness, skilfulness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रवीण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावुर्वृषु
प्रावुर्वृषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to wear.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ् before वृ to wear, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत|प्रावृतं|प्रावृतः
प्रावृत<BR>mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A veil, a wrapper, a cloak or mantle.<BR>adj.<BR>Covered, inclosed, encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ with आङ् prefix, to cover, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृति|प्रावृतिः
प्रावृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An inclosure, a fence, a bound hedge.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृ with आङ prefix, to inclose, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्
प्रावृष्<BR>f. (-वृट्)<BR>The rainy season, two months, about July and August.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वृष to sprinkle, aff. क्विप् and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषा
प्रावृषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The season of the rains.<BR>E.<BR>प्रावृष् as above, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषायणी
प्रावृषायणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रावृष् the rains, फक aff.; growing in the rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिक|प्रावृषिकः
प्रावृषिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Produced, &c. in the rainy season.<BR>m. (-कृः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>प्रावृष the rains, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिज|प्रावृषिजः
प्रावृषिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in the rains.<BR>E.<BR>प्रावृष् in the 7th case, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेण्य|प्रावृषेण्यः
प्रावृषेण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्य)<BR>1 Produced in the rains.<BR>2 Much, abundant.<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रावृष the rains, and एण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशन
प्रावेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A manufactory, a workshop.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before आवेशन entering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशन|प्राशनं
प्राशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Feeding, causing to taste or eat.<BR>2 Tasting.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अश to eat, intransitive or causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित|प्राशितं
प्राशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Eaten, devoured.<BR>2 Tasted, taken into the mouth without reaching to the throat.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Oblation to deified progenitors.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित्र|प्राशित्रं
प्राशित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Any edible article.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अश to eat, इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्निक|प्राश्निकः
प्राश्निक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An assistant at a spectacle or assembly.<BR>2 An inquirer, an asker.<BR>E.<BR>प्रश्न a question, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्य
प्राश्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having tasted or sipped.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अश to eat, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास|प्रासः
प्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bearded dart.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अस to throw, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासक|प्रासकः
प्रासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A die, dice.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अस to throw, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग|प्रासंग|प्रासंगः|प्रासङ्गः
प्रासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A yoke for cattle.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and आङ before सञ्ज to join, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्गिक|प्रासंगिक
प्रासङ्गिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Proceeding from or belonging to any connexion or relation.<BR>2 Relevant, belonging to any topic.<BR>3 Inherent, innate.<BR>4 Inseparably connected with.<BR>5 Incidental, episodical.<BR>E.<BR>प्रसङ्ग, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग्य|प्रासंग्य|प्रासंग्यः|प्रासङ्ग्यः
प्रासङ्ग्य<BR>m. (-ड्ग्यः)<BR>A beast of draught, an ox, yoked or in training.<BR>E.<BR>प्रासङ्ग a yoke, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाद|प्रासादः
प्रासाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A temple, a palace, a building consecrated to a deity, or inhabited by a prince.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before सद to go, aff. घञ, and the vowel of the prefix lengthened, or आङ् prefixed to the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादकुक्कुट|प्रासादकुक्कुटः
प्रासादकुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>प्रासाद a palace, and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादपृष्ठ|प्रासादपृष्ठः
प्रासादपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A terrace or balcony on the top of a large house.<BR>E.<BR>प्रासाद, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादशृङ्ग|प्रासादशृंग
प्रासादशृङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A turret, a spire on a palace or temple.<BR>E.<BR>प्रासाद, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीय
प्रासादीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of or belonging to a palace.<BR>E.<BR>प्रासाद्, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spearman, a lancer, a soldier armed with a dart or spear.<BR>E.<BR>प्रास a dart, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्त
प्रास्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Thrown, thrown off or away.<BR>2 Thrown into.<BR>3 Expelled, turned out, banished.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थिक|प्रास्थिकः
प्रास्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bought for a Prastha, containing a Prastha, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रस्थ a certain measure, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह|प्राहः
प्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Instruction in the art of acting or dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्ण|प्राह्णः
प्राह्ण<BR>m. (-ह्णः)<BR>The forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>प्र prior, अह्न the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णे
प्राह्णे<BR>ind.<BR>In the morning, in the forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>the seventh case of the last word, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतन|प्राह्णेतनः
प्राह्णेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging to the forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>प्राह्णे in the morning, aff. द्यु, and तुक aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतमाम्
प्राह्णेतमाम्<BR>ind.<BR>Early in the day, in the forenoon.<BR>E.<BR>प्राह्णे with तमप् aff. and आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Beloved, dear, desired.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A husband, a lover.<BR>2 A sort of drug, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>3 A sort of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">Page590</a>] deer.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A wife or mistress.<BR>3 Small cardamoms.<BR>4 News, information.<BR>5 Arabian jasmine.<BR>6 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>7 A species of the Supratiṣṭhā metre.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, aff. क, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=589" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियक|प्रियकः
प्रियक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>3 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>4 A variegated or spotted deer.<BR>5 A bee.<BR>6 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकार
प्रियकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Kind, favourable, affectionate, doing good to, or treating kindly.<BR>2 Suiting, congenial.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and कृ to do, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकृत्
प्रियकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Kind, friendly, a friend, a benefactor.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्कर|प्रियंकर|प्रियङ्करः
प्रियङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Amiable, exciting or attracting regard.<BR>2 Acting kindly or affectionately to.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय beloved, कृ to make, aff. खच्; also with अण् aff. प्रियकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्करण|प्रियंकरण
प्रियङ्करण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 Acceptable, grateful to.<BR>2 Acting kindly to, who or what does so.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Gratifying, treating kindly, (the act.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्गु|प्रियंगु|प्रियंगुः|प्रियङ्गुः
प्रियङ्गु<BR>(-ङ्गुः)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, and perfume, commonly known by the name Priyangu, and described in some places as a fragrant seed.<BR>2 Panick seed, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>3 Black mustard seed.<BR>4 Long pepper.<BR>5 A peculiar tree: see कटुकी.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय desired, गम to go, aff. डुन् and मुम् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतम|प्रियतमः
प्रियतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-भं)<BR>Dearest, most beloved.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, (Celosia cristata)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय desirable, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतर|प्रियतरः
प्रियतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dearer, more dear.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and तरप् comparative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियता
प्रियता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Love, affection.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय beloved, तस्न् aff.; also with त्व, aff. प्रियत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियदर्शन|प्रियदर्शनः
प्रियदर्शन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Handsome, lovely, good looking.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A parrot.<BR>2 A tree, (Mimusops kauki.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय beloved, and दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियप्राय|प्रियप्रायं
प्रियप्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Eloquent, well spoken, of pleasing speech.<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>Eloquence in language.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय desired, प्राय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियप्रेप्सु|प्रियप्रेप्सुः
प्रियप्रेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Lamenting the loss or absence of any beloved object, wishing or grieving for it.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय beloved, and प्रेप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियभाषण
प्रियभाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Speaking kindly.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and भाष्ण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियमधु|प्रियमधुः
प्रियमधु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>BALARĀMA, the half brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय fond, मधु wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियमाण
प्रियमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Beloved, affectionate.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्बद
प्रियम्बद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Sweet or pleasant speaking.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sort of demigod or Vidyādhara.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय kind, desired, वद to speak, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भविष्णु|प्रियंभविष्णु
प्रियम्भविष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Become dear to, or beloved by.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, भू to be, खिष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भविष्णुता
प्रियम्भविष्णुता<BR>n. (-ता)<BR>Amiability, becoming beloved by.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भावुक|प्रियंभावुक
प्रियम्भावुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Become dear to, or beloved by.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and भू to be, खुकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भावुकता
प्रियम्भावुकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Amiability, becoming beloved, the state or condition.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवर्णी
प्रियवर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय desired, वर्ण class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवादिन्
प्रियवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Sweet or pleasant spoken, flattering, a flatterer.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय kind, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसख|प्रियसखः
प्रियसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A tree, (Khayar, or Mimosa catechu)<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A female friend or companion, a confidante.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय desired, सखि a friend, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसत्य|प्रियसत्यं
प्रियसत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Pleasant, and true.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Eloquent, or pleasing, as well as true, (discourse.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय loved, and सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसन्देश|प्रियसंदेश|प्रियसंदेशः|प्रियसन्देशः
प्रियसन्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A tree bearing a fragrant flower, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय a friend, and सन्देश intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाख्य
प्रियाख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Announcing good tidings.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and आख्य who says.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाल|प्रियालः
प्रियाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, commonly Piyal, (Buchanania latifolia, ROXBURGH'S catalogue, but the name is applied to different trees.)<BR>E.<BR>पृ to satisfy, aff. कालन् and the radical vowel changed to रि; also with कन् added प्रियालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>and with the vowel protracted, प्रियाल.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>also as derived from पीय a Sautra root, पीयाल or पियाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियासु
प्रियासु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Fond of life.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियैषिन्
प्रियैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Friendly, affectionate, wishing to please.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय, and एषिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियोदित|प्रियोदितं
प्रियोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Well or kindly spoken, pleasingly uttered.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Kindly or gentle speech.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय kind, &c. and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री<BR>(ङ्) प्रीङ् r. 4th cl. (प्रीयते) (ञ्) प्रीञ्^1 r. 9th cl. (प्रीणाति प्रीणीते) and 1st and 10th cls. (प्रियति-ते प्राययति-ते or प्रीणयति)<BR>1 To please, to delight, to satisfy.<BR>2 To be pleased or satisfied.<BR>3 To desire or love.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीण|प्रीणः
प्रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>2 Pleased, satisfied.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणन|प्रीणनं
प्रीणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Satisfaction, satisfying, satiety.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणयित्वा
प्रीणयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having pleased or propitiated.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीत|प्रीतः
प्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pleased, happy, glad.<BR>2 Pleased or satisfied with.<BR>3 Gracious, kind, affectionate.<BR>4 Beloved, dear to.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतात्मन्
प्रीतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्मः)<BR>Pleased, satisfied, content.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीति|प्रीतिः
प्रीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Joy, pleasure, happiness.<BR>2 Love, affection, regard.<BR>3 The wife of KĀMA, or Cupid.<BR>4 The second of the twenty-seven astronomical Yogas.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिकर
प्रीतिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Pleasing, agreeable to.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिजुषा
प्रीतिजुषा<BR>f. (-षाः)<BR>The wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति the wife of KĀMA, जुष to serve, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिद|प्रीतिदः
प्रीतिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Affectionate, inspiring love or regard.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A jester, a buffoon.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति affection, pleasure, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=590" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिदान
प्रीतिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A kind or friendly present.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति affection, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिदाय|प्रीतिदायः
प्रीतिदाय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A gift or token of affection.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and दाय a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिपूर्व्वक
प्रीतिपूर्व्वक<BR>n. adv. (-कं)<BR>Through favour or kindness.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and पूर्व्वक an antecedent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमत्|प्रीतिमन्त्
प्रीतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Kind, affectionate.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमनस्
प्रीतिमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>1 Content, happy.<BR>2 Kind.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिवचस्
प्रीतिवचस्<BR>n. (-चः)<BR>Gracious or kindly speech.<BR>E.<BR>प्रीति, and वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतु
प्रीतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीयमाण
प्रीयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being pleased or propitiated.<BR>E.<BR>प्री to please, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रु
प्रु<BR>(ङ्) प्रुङ्^1 r. 1st cl. (प्रवते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष
प्रुष<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) प्रुषु (प्रोषति)<BR>To burn, to consume with fire.<BR>r. 9th cl. (प्रुष्णाति)<BR>To be unctuous or bland.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR>3 To fill.<BR>4 To set free.<BR>5 To be fond of or kind to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्ट|प्रुष्टः
प्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Burnt.<BR>E.<BR>प्रुष to burn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्व|प्रुष्वः
प्रुष्व<BR>m. (-ष्वः)<BR>1 A season of the year, a period of two months.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>f. (-ष्वा)<BR>A drop of water.<BR>E.<BR>प्रुष to burn, Uṇādi aff. क्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षक|प्रेक्षकः
प्रेक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spectator, a beholder, one of an audience.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षण|प्रेक्षणं
प्रेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The eye.<BR>2 Any public show or spectacle, a sight.<BR>3 A place where public exhibitions are held.<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Seeing, viewing, looking at, regarding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणिक
प्रेक्षणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Looking, who looks at.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman fond of seeing shows.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेक्षण seeing, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीय
प्रेक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Visible, apparent.<BR>2 Looking or appearing like.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.; also with कन् added, प्रेक्षणीयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षमाण
प्रेक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Looking at or on, beholding, regarding.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्यमाण
प्रेक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being seen or looked at.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षा
प्रेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Intellect, understanding.<BR>2 Dancing.<BR>3 Seeing, viewing, observing.<BR>4 Seeing a play or entertainment of dancing, &c.<BR>5 The branch of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षित
प्रेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld, looked at.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईक्ष to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खण|प्रेंखण
प्रेङ्खण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Going, wandering.<BR>2 Entering.<BR>3 Twinging.<BR>4 A minor drama in one act.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इखि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खत्
प्रेङ्खत्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्खन्-ङ्खन्ती-ङ्खत्)<BR>1 Touching, being in contact with.<BR>2 Scattering, diffusing.<BR>3 Shaking, moving.<BR>4 Wandering, roving.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इखि to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खा|प्रेंखा
प्रेङ्खा<BR>f. (-ङ्खा)<BR>1 A swing, a sort of hammock or swinging cot, either for travelling or diversion.<BR>2 Wandering, roaming, travelling about.<BR>3 A horse's going or motion.<BR>4 Dancing.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इखि to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खित|प्रेंखित|प्रेङ्खितं
प्रेङ्खित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-नं)<BR>1 Shaken, moving, set in motion, swung, &c. Joined to, being in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इखि to go, aff. क्त or प्रेङ्खा a swing, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलन|प्रेंखोलनं|प्रेङ्खोलनं
प्रेङ्खोलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A swing, a swing cot or hammock.<BR>E.<BR>प्रङ्खोल to swing or shake, nominal verb, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलित|प्रेङ्खोलितं
प्रेङ्खोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Agitated, shaken, swung, set in motion.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेङ्खोल nominal verb, to swing, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A ghost, a goblin a sprite, an evil being, especially animating the carcases of the dead.<BR>2 The spirit before obsequial rites are performed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकर्म्मन्|प्रेतकर्मन्
प्रेतकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Funeral or obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and कम्मन् act; also प्रेतकार्य्य, प्रेतक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकार्य्य|प्रेतकार्य|प्रेतकार्य्यं
प्रेतकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Obsequial ceremonies, any usages observed in honour of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत dead, कार्य्य practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकृत्य
प्रेतकृत्य<BR>nf. (-त्यं-त्या)<BR>Obsequial rites.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and कृत्य a ceremony; also प्रेतकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतगृह|प्रेतगृहं
प्रेतगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A cemetery, a burying ground.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत a sprite, and गृह abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतत्व
प्रेतत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The character or state of a departed spirit.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतधूम|प्रेतधूमः
प्रेतधूम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The smoke of a funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनदी
प्रेतनदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>The river of hell.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत a goblin, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनर|प्रेतनरः
प्रेतनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A ghost, a corpse.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनिर्हारक|प्रेतनिर्हारकः
प्रेतनिर्हारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A man employed to carry forth dead bodies.<BR>2 A kinsman who does so.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, निर् out, हृ to take, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपक्ष|प्रेतपक्षः
प्रेतपक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The dark half of the month.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and पक्ष a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपटह|प्रेतपटहः
प्रेतपटह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A drum played at the death of a person.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत dead, and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपति|प्रेतपतिः
प्रेतपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>YAMA, ruler of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत dead, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपात्र
प्रेतपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel used in obsequial presentations.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतराज|प्रेतराजः
प्रेतराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतलोक|प्रेतलोकः
प्रेतलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The region of disembodied spirits, in which they remain for one year, or until the obsequial rites are completed.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and लोक region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतवन|प्रेतवनं
प्रेतवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A burying ground, a cemetery, a place where bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत a sprite, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतवाहित|प्रेतवाहितः
प्रेतवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Possessed by a devil or fiend.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत a sprite, and वाहित borne, actuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतशुद्धि|प्रेतशुद्धिः
प्रेतशुद्धि<BR>m. (-द्धिः)<BR>Purification after the death of a kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and शुद्धि purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतहार|प्रेतहारः
प्रेतहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One who carries a corpse, a near kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and हार who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतान्न
प्रेतान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Food offered to the manes, or distributed on a person's death.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतोद्देश|प्रेतोद्देशः
प्रेतोद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An offering to the manes.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत, and उद्देश object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्य
प्रेत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 In the next world.<BR>2 Having died.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत dead, and यत् aff,; or प्र before इ to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सु
प्रेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desirous of obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before अप to obtain, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=591" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन्<BR>mn. (-मा-म)<BR>1 Affection, kindness, tender regard.<BR>2 Pleasure, sport, pastime, joy.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Air.<BR>E.<BR>प्र for प्रिय loved, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमपर
प्रेमपर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Affectionate, loving, constant.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेम, and पर attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमपातन|प्रेमपातनं
प्रेमपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rheum, tears.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेम tenderness, पातन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयस्
प्रेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Dearest, most beloved, very dear.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A wife, a mistress.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय dear, and ईयसुम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयोपत्य|प्रेयोपत्यः
प्रेयोपत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेयस् dear, and अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरण|प्रेरणं
प्रेरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sending, directing.<BR>2 Ordering, commanding.<BR>3 Passion, operation of the organs of sense.<BR>4 The sense of the causal verb.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईर to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरित|प्रेरितः
प्रेरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sent, directed, dispatched.<BR>2 Ordered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईर to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्यभाव|प्रेत्यभावः
प्रेत्यभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Being born again after dying.<BR>E.<BR>प्रेत्य, भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेन्वन
प्रेन्वन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pervading, spreading.<BR>2 Satisfying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईर to go, इवि to pervade, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्त्वन्
प्रेर्त्वन्<BR>m. (-र्त्वा)<BR>The ocean.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ईर to go, Uṇādi aff. क्वनिप्, and तुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष|प्रेषः
प्रेष<BR>(ऋ) प्रेषृ r. 1st cl. (प्रेषते)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष|प्रेषः
प्रेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Sending, directing, dispatching.<BR>2 Pain, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go or send, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषण|प्रेषणं
प्रेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sending, dispatching.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषित|प्रेषितं
प्रेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sent, directed.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषितवत्
प्रेषितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान-वती-वत्)<BR>Sent, having sent.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Most or very dear.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>1 A wife.<BR>2 The leg.<BR>E.<BR>प्रिय dear, aff. इष्ठन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्य|प्रेष्यः
प्रेष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A servant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, or प्रेष to send, aff. ण्यत्; also प्रैष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष|प्रैषः
प्रैष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Sorrow, distress, affliction.<BR>2 Pain, suffering.<BR>3 Sending, directing.<BR>4 Phrenzy, intoxication, insanity.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, aff. घञ्; also प्रेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष्य|प्रैष्यः
प्रैष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A servant, a slave.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Service, servitude.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before इष to go, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्त|प्रोक्तं
प्रोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Said, declared.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्तवत्
प्रोक्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having or had said, was saying.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वच to speak, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षण|प्रोक्षणं
प्रोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Killing animals in sacrifice, immolation of victims.<BR>2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>3 Sprinkling with water, &c.<BR>4 A text to be repeated when animals are offered.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उक्ष to sprinkle, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणीपात्र
प्रोक्षणीपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel for sprinkling water, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोक्षण, and पात्र a vessel, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षित|प्रोक्षितं
प्रोक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>2 Killed, slaughtered.<BR>3 Offered in sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उक्ष to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छलत्|प्रोच्छलन्त्
प्रोच्छलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्तो-लत्)<BR>Flowing, issuing, coming out or up.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before शल to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छून
प्रोच्छून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Swelled, swoln.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and उच्छून swelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्जासन|प्रोज्जासनं
प्रोज्जासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before जस to hurt or kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झन|प्रोज्झनं
प्रोज्झन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Leaving, quitting, letting go.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उञ्झ to leave, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झित|प्रोज्झितं
प्रोज्झित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, shunned, avoided.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उज्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोण्ठ|प्रोंठः|प्रोण्ठः
प्रोण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत|प्रोतं
प्रोत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sewn or stitched.<BR>2 Tied, strung.<BR>3 Set, inlaid.<BR>4 Impaled.<BR>5 Joined, connected.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Cloth, clothes.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वे to weave or sew, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोतोत्सादन|प्रोतोत्सादनं
प्रोतोत्सादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A parasol, a Catta, an umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोत cloth, उत् over, सादन a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्फल|प्रोत्फलः
प्रोत्फल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of palm tree.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् above, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सादन
प्रोत्सादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Contriving, device.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before पद to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारण|प्रोत्सारणं
प्रोत्सारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Clearing away, getting rid of, expelling.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before सृ to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारित
प्रोत्सारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Relinquished, left, given up.<BR>2 Got rid of, ejected, expelled.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साह|प्रोत्साहः
प्रोत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Effort, exertion.<BR>2 Stimulus, incitement.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहक|प्रोत्साहकः
प्रोत्साहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The instigator or adviser of any act, or, in law, of any crime.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोत्साह with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहन|प्रोत्साहनं
प्रोत्साहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Instigating, exciting, stimulating.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before सह to bear, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहित
प्रोत्साहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Incited, instigated, stimulated, encouraged.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before सह to bear, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ<BR>(ऋ) प्रोथृ r. 1st cl. (प्रोथति-ते)<BR>1 To be able, adequate or competent.<BR>2 To be complete or ample.<BR>3 To destroy, to subdue or overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Travelling, wayfaring, a traveller.<BR>2 Notorious, famous.<BR>3 Placed, fixed.<BR>mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>The nose of a horse or the tip of it.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The loins or hip.<BR>2 Old clothes.<BR>3 The embryo or fœtus.<BR>E.<BR>प्रु to go, Uṇādi aff. थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घुष्ट
प्रोद्घुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Resonant, sounding well.<BR>2 Making a loud noise.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and उद्वुष्ट sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घोषण|प्रोद्घोषणं
प्रोद्घोषण<BR>n. (णं)<BR>Sounding or crying aloud.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before घुष to cry, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्भिन्न
प्रोद्भिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Breaking forth, (as seeds, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and उद्भिन्न put forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोन्नत
प्रोन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Towering, very lofty.<BR>E.<BR>प्र, and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोम्भन
प्रोम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Filling.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उम्भ to fill, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोम्भित
प्रोम्भित<BR>mfn. (-त-ता-तं)<BR>Filled.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उम्भ to fill, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोर्णुनविषु
प्रोर्णुनविषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to cover.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ऊर्णु to cover, desid. v., उ aff. and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोर्णुनूषु
प्रोर्णुनूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to cover.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ऊर्णु to cover, desid. v., उ aff. the augment इ omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लाघित
प्रोल्लाघित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Recovered from sickness, convalescent.<BR>2 Strong, robust.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before लाघ to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लिखत्
प्रोल्लिखत्<BR>mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्)<BR>Marking, making lines, scratches, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उल्लिख to mark, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=592" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लेखन|प्रोल्लेखनं
प्रोल्लेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Scratching, marking, drawing lines or marks.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and उत् before लिख to write, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष|प्रोषः
प्रोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Burning.<BR>E.<BR>प्रुष to burn, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषित|प्रोषितः
प्रोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abroad, absent, away from home, sojourning in another country.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितभर्तृका|प्रोषितभर्त्तृका
प्रोषितभर्तृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose husband is absent.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोषित abroad, भर्तृ a husband, aff. कन् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितमरण
प्रोषितमरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Dying in a foreign country.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोषित absent, and मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितवत्
प्रोषितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Strange, a stranger, a sojourner.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वस to dwell, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठ|प्रोष्ठः
प्रोष्ठ<BR>mf. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी)<BR>A sort of carp, (Cyprinus Pausius, HAM.)<BR>m. (ष्ठः)<BR>An ox.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before उष to burn, aff. थन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपदा
प्रोष्ठपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>One of the constellations, the twenty-sixth or twenty-seventh, containing stars in the wing of Pegasus: see माद्रपदा.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोष्ठ here said to mean an ox, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपाद|प्रोष्ठपादः
प्रोष्ठपाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Born under the sign Proṣṭha padā.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोष्ठपद, and अण् aff. in this sense; in any other, the form is प्रोष्ठपद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह|प्रोहः
प्रोह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Skilful, clever.<BR>2 Logical, reasoning, a reasoner, a disputant.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An elephant's foot.<BR>2 A joint, a knot.<BR>3 The ancle of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, or ऊह to reason, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोहणीय
प्रोहणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be reasoned or argued.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before ऊह to reason, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढ|प्रौढं
प्रौढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Full-grown.<BR>2 Confident, bold, arrogant.<BR>3 Impudent.<BR>4 Full, (as the moon.)<BR>5 Thick, heavy, (darkness, &c.).<BR>5 Forward, (as the hand to seize any thing.)<BR>7 Raised, lifted up.<BR>8 Controverted.<BR>9 Old.<BR>10 Married.<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>1 A woman from thirty years of age to fifty-five.<BR>2 A description of the Nāyikā or mistress, a woman whose feelings are violent or impetuous, or one who is not in any awe of her lover or husband.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढि|प्रौढिः
प्रौढि<BR>f. (ढिः)<BR>1 Enterprise, zeal, confident or audacious exertion.<BR>2 Investigation, controversy, discussion.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before वह to bear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढपाद|प्रौढपादः
प्रौढपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>One who sits with his feet upon a seat.<BR>E.<BR>प्रौढ raised, and पाद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौण|प्रौणः
प्रौण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Clever, learned, skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौर्णुवितृ
प्रौर्णुवितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Extending over, covering.<BR>E.<BR>प्र and ऊर्णु to cover, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठपद|प्रौष्ठपदः
प्रौष्ठपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The month Bhādra, (August-September.)<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>Full moon in Bhādra.<BR>E.<BR>प्रोष्ठपदा the sign, and अण् aff.; when the moon is near the wing of Pegasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (प्लक्षति-ते)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 Waved leaf fig tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR>2 Another tree, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>3 The holy fig, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>4 One of the seven Dvīpas or continents, into which the world is divided.<BR>5 A private or back door.<BR>E.<BR>प्लुष to burn, Uṇādi aff. स, and अ substituted for the penultimate vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Who or what goes by leaps or jumps, leaping, jumping, a tumbler.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Jumping, leaping, plunging, going by leaps or plunges.<BR>2 Swimming, floating, diving.<BR>3 A raft, a float.<BR>4 A frog.<BR>5 A monkey.<BR>6 A sheep.<BR>7 A diver, or bird so called, (Pelicanus fusicollis.)<BR>8 A sort of duck.<BR>9 A man of a low or degraded tribe.<BR>10 Waved-leaf fig tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR>11 The continuous protracted accent, the lengthened sound of vowels in poetry or the Vedas.<BR>12 Protracting a sentence through several stanzas.<BR>13 A declivity or shelving ground.<BR>14 A piece of water.<BR>15 A sort of basket or snare of basket work for catching fish.<BR>16 An enemy.<BR>17 Sending, directing.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 A sort of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>2 Fragrant grass in general, or another sort.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवक|प्लवकः
प्लवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tumbler, a dancer, a man who walks on the edge of a sword, a rope-dancer, &c.<BR>2 An outcast.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव a tumbler, &c. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवग|प्लवगः
प्लवग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A monkey, an ape.<BR>2 A frog.<BR>3 The charioteer of the sun.<BR>4 A sort of bird, the diver.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव leaping, and ग who goes, from गम with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवगति|प्लवगतिः
प्लवगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 Going by leaps and jumps.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव leaping, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवङ्ग|प्लवंग|प्लवंगः|प्लवङ्गः
प्लवङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A monkey.<BR>2 A deer.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव leaping, गम to go, aff. खच् with the power of ड, whence the nasal is inserted, and final syllable rejected; also प्लव, प्लवग, and प्लवङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवङ्गम|प्लवंगम|प्लवंगमः|प्लवङ्गमः
प्लवङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A monkey, an ape.<BR>2 A frog.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव leaping, गम to go, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवन|प्लवनः
प्लवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Jumping, leaping.<BR>2 A deluge, an inundation.<BR>3 Swimming, plunging into.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवमान
प्लवमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Bounding, springing, leaping.<BR>2 Swimming.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवाका
प्लवाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A boat, a raft.<BR>E.<BR>प्लव tossing, अक what goes, टाप् fem. aff.; also प्लविका, from प्लु with वुन् aff. and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्ष|प्लाक्षं
प्लाक्ष<BR>m. (क्षं)<BR>The fruit of the Hibiscus populneoides.<BR>E.<BR>प्लक्ष, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव|प्लावः
प्लाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Submersion.<BR>2 Filling a vessel till it runs over.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, causal v., घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट, प्लावनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव्य
प्लाव्य<BR>mfn. (व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be jumped, leaped, &c.<BR>2 To be submerged or inundated.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाविन्
प्लाविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिह
प्लिह<BR>r. 1st cl. (प्लेहते)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहन्
प्लिहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>The spleen: see प्लीहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहा
प्लिहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The spleen: see प्लीहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ली
प्ली<BR>r. 9th cl. (प्लीणाति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहघ्न|प्लीहघ्नः
प्लीहघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Andersonia rohitaka, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>प्लीह the spleen, (the disease, &c.) घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहन्
प्लीहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>The spleen; the organ or the disease of it, as in English; in the latter sense, however, it is equally applied to the enlargement of the mesenteric glands, &c.<BR>E.<BR>प्लिह to increase, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, and the vowel made long; otherwise being प्लिहन्; and with क and टाप् affs., and the vowel long or short प्लिहा or प्लीहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहशत्रु|प्लीहशत्रुः
प्लीहशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A medical plant, commonly Rohera or Rohiṇī, (Andersonia rohitaka, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>प्लीह for प्लीहन् the spleen, (the disease,) and शत्रु enemy; also प्लीहाशत्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहारि|प्लीहारिः
प्लीहारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>प्लीहा the spleen, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=593" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लु
प्लु<BR>(ङ) प्लुङ् r. 1st cl. (प्लवते)<BR>1 To go, to approach.<BR>2 To go by leaps, to jump, &c.<BR>With उत् prefixed,<BR>To leap up.<BR>With वि,<BR>To plunge in, to be submerged or inundated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुक्षि|प्लुक्षिः
प्लुक्षि<BR>m. (-क्षिः)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>प्लुष to burn, Uṇādi aff. सि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुत|प्लुतं|प्लुतः
प्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Jumped, leaped, gone by leap or jump, &c.<BR>2 Thrown or tossed up.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Bounding, capering, one of a horse's paces.<BR>3 Leaping, jumping, tumbling.<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>The third sound given to vowels; the protracted or continuous sound, being three times the length of the short vowel, and occupying three moments in its utterance.<BR>E.<BR>प्लु to go by leaps, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष|प्लुषः
प्लुष<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) प्लुषु (प्लोषति) r. 4th cl. (ऌ) प्लुषॢ (प्लुष्यति)<BR>To burn.<BR>r. 9th cl. (प्लुष्णाति)<BR>1 To be unctuous.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR>3 To fill.<BR>4 To set free.<BR>5 To be fond of or kind to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष|प्लुषः
प्लुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Burning, combustion.<BR>E.<BR>प्लुष to burn, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्ट|प्लुष्टः
प्लुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Burnt.<BR>E.<BR>प्लुष to burn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुस
प्लुस<BR>(इर) प्लुसिर r. 4th cl. (प्लुस्यति)<BR>1 To burn.<BR>2 To share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लेव
प्लेव<BR>(ऋ) प्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (प्लेवते)<BR>To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लोष|प्लोषः
प्लोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Burning, combustion.<BR>E.<BR>प्लुष to burn, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (प्साति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा<BR>f. (प्सा)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>प्सा to eat, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सात|प्सातं
प्सात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>प्सा to eat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सान|प्सानं
प्सान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Food.<BR>E.<BR>प्सा to eat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ<BR>The twenty-second consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, the aspirate of the preceding letter, and expressed by Ph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ<BR>m. (फः)<BR>1 Increasing, swelling, enlarging, expanding.<BR>2 Performance of a mystical rite, by which KUVERA'S attendants are propitiated.<BR>3 A high wind, a gale.<BR>4 Wind expelled in yawning.<BR>5 Fruitfulness, fertility.<BR>6 An augmentor or increaser.<BR>nf. (फं फा)<BR>Unprofitable or idle speech.<BR>n. (फं)<BR>1 Angry speech.<BR>2 Bursting with some little noise, as air bubbles, boiling water, &c.; bubbling, boiling.<BR>f. (फा)<BR>Distress, anxiety.<BR>E.<BR>फल to bear fruit, or स्फाय to swell, aff. ड; in the latter case, the initial is rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्क|फक्कः
फक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (फक्कति)<BR>1 To creep, to move slowly or sluggishly.<BR>2 To behave ill, to practise ill or improper conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्किका
फक्किका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A position, an assertion or argument, to be proved or maintained.<BR>2 Logical exposition or elucidation.<BR>3 A sophism.<BR>4 A trick.<BR>5 Illusion.<BR>6 Fraud.<BR>E.<BR>फक्क to move slowly, aff. किकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिका
फञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>2 A species of Hedysarum, (H. alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, (disease,) aff. ण्वुल्, and the radical initial changed to फ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिपुत्रिका
फञ्जिपुत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>फञ्जि as above, and पुत्रिका infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट|फटः
फट<BR>mfn. subst. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>The expanded hood or neck of the Cobra de capello.<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 A cheat.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to burst or expand, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट्
फट्<BR>ind.<BR>Exclamation of no meaning, forming part of a Mantra or incantation.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to burst, aff. क्विप् and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फडिङ्गा|फडिंगा
फडिङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण<BR>r. 1st cl. (फणति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To produce easily or readily.<BR>3 To be unoily.<BR>Causal form, (फाणयति)<BR>1 To dilute.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(फणयति)<BR>To cause to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण<BR>mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>The expanded hood or neck of the Cobra de capello, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फण to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणकर|फणकरः
फणकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake, especially the Cobra de capello, or COLUBER naja.<BR>E.<BR>फण the hood, and कर who makes; also फणाकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणधर|फणधरः
फणधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>फण the hood, and धर who has; also फणाधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणभृत्
फणभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>फण a hood, and भृत् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणमणि|फणमणिः
फणमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A jewel supposed to be in the head of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>फण, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणवत्|फणवन्त्
फणवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>फणा a hood, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाकर|फणाकरः
फणाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake: see फणकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाधर|फणाधरः
फणाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake: see फणधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाभर|फणाभरः
फणाभर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>फण the hood expanded, भृ to possess, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणावत्|फणावन्त्
फणावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A snake: see फणवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिकेशर|फणिकेशरः
फणिकेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>फणिन् a snake, and केशर filaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिखेल|फणिखेलः
फणिखेल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A quail.<BR>E.<BR>फणि a snake, and खेल who plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिज्झक|फणिज्झकः
फणिज्झक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, also Marüa.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Rāmadūtī, apparently a sort of basil with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>फणि for फणी a snake, and उज्झ to abandon, aff. वुन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणित|फणितः
फणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Diluted.<BR>E.<BR>फण to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणितल्पग|फणितल्पगः
फणितल्पग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>फणि a snake, तल्प a bed, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिन्
फणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>फण a hood, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिप्रिय|फणिप्रियः
फणिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>फणि for फणी a snake, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणीश्वर|फणीश्वरः
फणीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The great serpent ANANTA.<BR>E.<BR>फणि a snake, and ईश्वर sovereign; also फणीन्द्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्ड|फंडः|फण्डः
फण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The belly.<BR>E.<BR>फण to go, Uṇādi aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फत्कारिन्
फत्कारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>फत् imitative sound, and कारिन who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर|फरं
फर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A shield.<BR>E.<BR>र substituted for ल; see फल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फरुवक|फरुवकं
फरुवक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A betel box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर्फरीक|फर्फरीकः
फर्फरीक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sweetness.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to expand, Uṇādi aff. ईकन्, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल|फलं|फलः
फल<BR>r. 1st cl. (फलति)<BR>1 To produce or bear fruit.<BR>2 To make fruitful, to fructify.<BR>3 To go.<BR>(ञि, आ); ञिफला r. 1st cl. (फलति)<BR>To divide, to cleave or split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल|फलं|फलः
फल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The fruit of any plant, fruit in general.<BR>2 Fruit (metaphorically), result, produce, consequence.<BR>3 Prosperity, flourishing, thriving.<BR>4 Gain, profit, acquisition.<BR>5 Recompense, reward.<BR>6 A shield.<BR>7 The blade of a sword or knife, the head of an arrow, &c.<BR>8 A sort of fragrant berry and drug, commonly Kakoli.<BR>9 A nutmeg.<BR>10 The three myrobalans collectively.<BR>11 The menstrual discharge.<BR>12 Gift, giving.<BR>13 A ploughshare.<BR>14 The quotient of a sum, (in arithmetic.)<BR>15 The area of a circle, &c.<BR>16 An equation.<BR>17 (In astronomy,) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">Page595</a>] The anomalistic equation of a planet.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Echites antidysenterica, Rox.): see कुटज.<BR>E.<BR>फल to bear or produce fruit, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=594" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलक|फलकं|फलकः
फलक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A shield.<BR>2 A bench.<BR>3 A plank.<BR>4 A layer.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bone, the os frontis, or bone of the forehead.<BR>2 A leaf or page for writing on.<BR>3 A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The buttocks.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, or फल to split or divide, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकपाणि|फलकपाणिः
फलकपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A soldier armed with a shield.<BR>E.<BR>फलक, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकामना
फलकामना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Desire of any consequence.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and कामना desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकिन्
फलकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Having, or being armed with a shield, &c.<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A sort of fish, commonly Phalāi.<BR>E.<BR>फलक as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकेशर|फलकेशरः
फलकेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The cocoanut tree^1.<BR>E.<BR>फल the fruit, and केशर hair, covered with a fibrous coat like hair.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकोषक|फलकोषकः
फलकोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The scrotum or testicles.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, कोष sheath, and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकृष्ण|फलकृष्णः
फलकृष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>A small fruit, (Carissa carandas.)<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and कृष्ण black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलग्रहि|फलग्रहिः
फलग्रहि<BR>mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि)<BR>Fruitful, bearing fruit in due season.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, ग्रह to take, aff. इन्, also फलेग्रहि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलग्राहिन्
फलग्राहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, ग्रह to take, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलखण्डन
फलखण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disappointing.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and खण्डन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलचमस|फलचमसः
फलचमस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The bark of the Indian fig, ground and eaten with curds, by way of penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्
फलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Yielding fruit, profit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल to bear fruit, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्रय|फलत्रयं
फलत्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Three sorts of fruit collectively, as the fruit of the vine, the Parush, and the Gmelina arborea.<BR>2 The three myrobalans.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्रिक|फलत्रिकं
फलत्रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The three myrobalans collectively.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and त्रिक three-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलद|फलदः
फलद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Yielding or bearing fruit, results, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and द what gives; also फलदातृ, फलदायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलन|फलनं
फलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fructifying, bearing fruit, producing consequences.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिवृत्ति|फलनिवृत्तिः
फलनिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Cessation of consequences.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and निवृत्ति stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिर्वृत्ति
फलनिर्वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Final consequence or result.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and निर्वृत्ति completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिष्पत्ति|फलनिष्पत्तिः
फलनिष्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Bearing fruit.<BR>2 Yielding profit or desired results.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and निष्पत्ति putting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपाक|फलपाकः
फलपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ripening of fruit.<BR>2 The fulness of consequences.<BR>3 The Caronda.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and पाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपाकान्ता
फलपाकान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>An annual plant.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, पाक ripening or ripeness, and अन्त end; dying after bearing fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपातन
फलपातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knocking down or gathering fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and पातन felling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपुच्छ|फलपुच्छः
फलपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A sort of esculent root or bulb.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूर|फलपूरः
फलपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and पूर to fill, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूरक|फलपूरकः
फलपूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Common citron.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रद|फलप्रदः
फलप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Yielding fruit, productive, yielding a reward, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and प्रद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रयुक्त
फलप्रयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Connected with or producing consequences, yielding fruit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and प्रयुक्त applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्राप्ति|फलप्राप्तिः
फलप्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Obtaining the desired result or fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and प्राप्ति acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभाज्
फलभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Having or receiving fruit, consequence, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभूमि|फलभूमिः
फलभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Any region not included in the known continent, as heaven, hell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, (of actions,) and भूमि earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभोग|फलभोगः
फलभोग<BR>m. (गः)<BR>1 Receipt or enjoyment of consequences.<BR>2 Possession of rent or profit, usufruct.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभोगिन्
फलभोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Who receives the profits, consequences, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and भोगिन् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलमुद्गरिका
फलमुद्गरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of date.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and मुद्गर a mallet, aff. कन् in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलवत्|फलवन्त्
फलवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Bearing fruit.<BR>2 Yielding results, or consequences.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलशाडव|फलशाडवः
फलशाडव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, शाड to extol, aff. अव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलशालिन्
फलशालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Bearing or yielding fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलश्रेष्ठ|फलश्रेष्ठः
फलश्रेष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The mango.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलस|फलसः
फलस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The jack or bread fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, सह to be able, aff. डः see पनस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसम्पद्|फलसंपद्
फलसम्पद्<BR>f. (-पद् or पत्)<BR>Prosperity, success.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and सम्पत् abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसम्भव
फलसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced in or by fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and सम्भव born; also फलसम्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसाधन
फलसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Means or instrument of success.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and साघन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसिद्धि|फलसिद्धिः
फलसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Realising an object, reaping the fruit of any act.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and सिद्धि perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलहानि|फलहानिः
फलहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Loss of fruit or profit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलानुसरण
फलानुसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rate or aggregate of profits.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and अनुसरण conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाकाङ्क्षा|फलाकांक्षा
फलाकाङ्क्षा<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षा)<BR>Hope or expectation of favourable consequences.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and आकाङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलादन|फलादनः
फलादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाध्यक्ष|फलाध्यक्षं|फलाध्यक्षः
फलाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree, commonly Khirani, (Mimusops Kauki.)<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलान्त|फलान्तः
फलान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit or blossom, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलापेक्षा
फलापेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Regard to or expectation of consequences.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and अपेक्षा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलापेत
फलापेत<BR>mfn. (तः-ता-तं)<BR>Unproductive, unfertile.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and अपेत deprived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलायोषित्
फलायोषित्<BR>f. (-त्)<BR>A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाशन|फलाशनः
फलाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=595" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाशिन्
फलाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Living on fruits.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलासक्त
फलासक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Doing any thing for the sake of reward.<BR>2 Fond of or seeking to pluck fruit.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and आसक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलित|फलितं|फलितः
फलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fruitful, bearing fruit.<BR>2 Successful, yielding a result.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन्
फलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Bearing fruit, fruitful.<BR>2 Productive of consequences.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A sort of fish, commonly Phalāi (Mystus kapirat.)<BR>2 A tree, especially in fruit.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>2 A potherb, (Echites dichotoma.)<BR>3 A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाभोग
फलाभोग<BR>m. (गः)<BR>Non-enjoyment of profits, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and अभोग non-use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलूष|फलूषः
फलूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, and ऊषन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेग्रहि|फलेग्रहिः
फलेग्रहि<BR>mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि)<BR>Bearing fruit in season, fruitful.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, ग्रह to take, aff. इन्; ए substituted irregularly for the final of फल; also फलग्रहि and फलेग्राहिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेग्राहिन्
फलेग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Bearing fruit in due season.<BR>E.<BR>as above, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेरुहा
फलेरुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, in the seventh case, रुह to grow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोच्चय|फलोच्चयः
फलोच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Collecting of fruits.<BR>2 A collection of fruits.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and उच्चय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोत्तमा
फलोत्तमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A small sort of rope.<BR>2 The benefit arising from sacred study.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, उत्तभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोपेत
फलोपेत<BR>mfn. (त-ता-तं)<BR>Having or yielding fruit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and उपेत possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोत्पति
फलोत्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The mango.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, उत् over, पति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोदय|फलोदयः
फलोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Gain, profit.<BR>2 Heaven, paradise.<BR>3 Joy, happiness.<BR>4 Consequence, result.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, gain, &c. उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोद्देश|फलोद्देशः
फलोद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Regard to results.<BR>E.<BR>फल, and उद्देश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोनि
फलोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्क|फल्कः
फल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>An expanded or extended body.<BR>E.<BR>फल to separate, Uṇādi aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गु|फल्गुः
फल्गु<BR>mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)<BR>1 Pithless, sapless.<BR>2 Vain, unprofitable, unmeaning, useless.<BR>3 Weak, feeble.<BR>f. (-ल्गुः)<BR>1 The opposite-leaved fig tree, (F. oppositi-folia, Rox.)<BR>2 The name of a river which is said to run underneath Gaya.<BR>3 Falsehood, false or lying speech.<BR>4 A red powder, usually of the root of wild ginger, coloured with sappan wood, and thrown over one another by the Hindus, at the Holi festival.<BR>5 The spring season.<BR>E.<BR>फल to bear fruit, Uṇādi aff. गुक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुन|फल्गुनः
फल्गुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>2 The month Phālguna.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The constellation Phalgunī.<BR>E.<BR>फल to bear fruit, Uṇādi aff. उनन् and गुक् aug.: see फाल्गुन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुनाल|फल्गुनालः
फल्गुनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The month Phālguna.<BR>E.<BR>फल्गु, and अल equal to, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्य|फल्यं
फल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>A bud, a flower.<BR>E.<BR>फल fruit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्लकिन्
फल्लकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A fish, caught in ponds, commonly Phalāi, (Mystus kapirat.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाट्
फाट्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाणि|फाणिः
फाणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 Unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>2 Flour or meal mixed with curds.<BR>E.<BR>स्फायी to swell, Uṇādi aff. नि, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाणित|फाणितं
फाणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Raw sugar, the inspissated juice of the sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>फण to go, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाण्ट|फांट|फाण्टं|फाण्टः
फाण्ट<BR>mfn. (-ण्टः-ण्टा-ण्टं)<BR>Readily prepared, made by an extemporaneous easy process, (decoction, &c.).<BR>n. (-ण्टं)<BR>1 Diluted decoction, decoction easily prepared.<BR>2 The first particles of butter that are produced by churning.<BR>E.<BR>फण to prepare easily, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल|फालं|फालः
फाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Made of cotton, (vesture.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The share of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>फल to divide, in the causal form, aff. अच्; or फल fruit, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फालकृष्ट|फालकृष्टः
फालकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Furrowed, ploughed.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A ploughed field.<BR>E.<BR>फाल, and कृष्ट furrowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुन|फाल्गुनः
फाल्गुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>2 A sort of tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>3 A month, commonly called by the name Phālguna, (February-March.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Day of full moon on the month Phālguna, on which the Holī or great vernal festival of the Hindus is celebrated.<BR>2 A name common to the eleventh and twelfth lunar asterisms, distinguished by the epithets first and last, or पूर्व्व and उन्तरः see पूर्व्वफाल्गुनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनानुज|फाल्गुनानुजः
फाल्गुनानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Spring.<BR>E.<BR>फाल्गुन the month, अनु according, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनिक|फाल्गुनिकः
फाल्गुनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Phālguna.<BR>E.<BR>फाल्गुनी day of full moon in this month, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फि|फिः
फि<BR>m. (फिः)<BR>Anger, passion.<BR>E.<BR>फल to separate, aff. डि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिङ्गक|फिंगकः|फिङ्गकः
फिङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The fork-tailed shrike.<BR>E.<BR>फिङ्ग imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुक|फुकः
फुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुट|फुटः
फुट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>The hood or expanded neck of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुट to swell, aff. क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्
फुत्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Expression of disregard or contempt, (Phoo, hoot.)<BR>2 Imitative sound, implying the bubbling or boiling of water &c. or of blowing into any liquid.<BR>E.<BR>स्फुर to swell, aff. क्विप्, स rejected, and तुक् added, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कर|फुत्करः
फुत्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>फुत् boiling, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कार|फुत्कारः
फुत्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Arrogant, contemptuous, disdainful.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sound of bubbling, &c.<BR>2 Blowing or breathing into, (as to cool it.)<BR>E.<BR>फुत् expression of contempt, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कृत
फुत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blown up, (as a bubble.)<BR>2 Blown into, cooled by blowing into it.<BR>E.<BR>फुत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुप्फुस|फुप्फुसः
फुप्फुस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The lungs: see पुप्फुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल<BR>r. 1st. cl. (फुल्लति)<BR>To blow or blossom, to bud or flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>1 Blown, opened, expanded as a flower.<BR>2 Opened (as the eyes with pleasure, &c.), smiling, gay.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल to blow, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लदामन्
फुल्लदामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>A species of the Atidhṛti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लनयन|फुल्लनयनः
फुल्लनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Full or large-eyed.<BR>2 Smiling, looking happy.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल, and नयन the eye; also similar compounds, as फुल्लनेत्र, फुल्लदृष्टि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=596" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लफाल|फुल्लफालः
फुल्लफाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Winnowing corn.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल blown, and फाल for स्फाल् spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लरीक|फुल्लरीकः
फुल्लरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ललोचन|फुल्ललोचनः
फुल्ललोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Full-eyed.<BR>2 Looking pleased or happy.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A large full eye.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A species of the antelope.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल full, expanded, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लवत्|फुल्लवन्त्
फुल्लवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Blossoming, blowing.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल to blow, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लवदन
फुल्लवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Looking pleased or happy.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल, and वदन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लि|फुल्लिः
फुल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>Blowing, blossoming.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल to blow, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लिति
फुल्लिति<BR>f. (तिः)<BR>Flowering, blossoming.<BR>E.<BR>फुल्ल to blow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्
फूत्<BR>ind.<BR>Imitative sound of bubbling, sobbing, &c.: see फुत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कार
फूत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Bubbling.<BR>2 Sobbing.<BR>3 Blowing or breathing into any liquid.<BR>E.<BR>फूत्, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कृत
फूत्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bubbled, bubbling, made to sound so.<BR>2 Blown or breathed into, (a liquid.)<BR>3 Sounded as in sobbing.<BR>E.<BR>फूत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेन|फेनः
फेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Froth, foam.<BR>2 Cuttle fish bone, supposed to be the indurated foam of the sea.<BR>3 Vapour.<BR>E.<BR>स्फायी to swell, नक् Uṇādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनक|फेनकः
फेनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Cuttle fish bone.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Rice, ground and boiled with water.<BR>2 The soap berry.<BR>E.<BR>फेन froth, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनता
फेनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Frothiness, vapour.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to फेन; also with त्व, फेनत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनल|फेनलः
फेनल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Frothy, foamy.<BR>E.<BR>फेन froth, अलच् poss. aff.; also with इलच् similar aff. फेनिल, and with the usual possessive मतुप्, फेनवत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनवत्|फेनवन्त्
फेनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Frothy, foaming, bubbling.<BR>E.<BR>फेन froth, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनवाहिन्
फेनवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>फेन foam, वह to bear, aff. णिनि; INDRA having used the foam of the sea for his thunderbolt, to kill the demon VṚTRĀSURA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाग्र|फेनाग्रं
फेनाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>A bubble.<BR>E.<BR>फेन foam, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनायमान|फेनायमानः
फेनायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Foaming, frothing.<BR>E.<BR>फेन nom. verb to foam, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाशनि|फेनाशनिः
फेनाशनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>फेन foam, and अशनि the thunderbolt: see फेनवाहिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिका
फेनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Froth arising from treacle.<BR>E.<BR>फेन foam, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिल|फेनिलं|फेनिलः
फेनिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Frothy, foamy.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The soap plant, (Sapindus detergens, Rox.)<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>2 The fruit of the Vangueria spinosa.<BR>E.<BR>फेन froth or foam, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेर|फेरः
फेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरण्ड|फेरंड|फेरंडः|फेरण्डः
फेरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>फे imitative sound, रम to sport, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरव|फेरवः
फेरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or cheat.<BR>2 Malicious, noxious, injurious.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A jackal or shacal.<BR>2 A demon, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>फे imitative sound, रु to utter, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरु|फेरुः
फेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>फे imitative sound, रु to cry, aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल|फेलं
फेल<BR>(ऋ) फेलृ r. 10th cl. (फेलति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलक|फेलकः
फेलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Orts, leavings of a meal, or droppings from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>फेल to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेला
फेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Orts, leavings.<BR>E.<BR>फेल to go, अच् aff., fem. aff. टाप्; also फेलक and फेलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलि|फेलिः
फेलि<BR>f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>Orts, leavings.<BR>E.<BR>फेल to go, इन् aff., ङीप् optionally added; also with टाप् and कन् added, फेलिका f. (-का)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ्वल
फ्वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (फ्वलति)<BR>To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब<BR>The twenty-third consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, corresponding to the letter B, and often confounded with the analogous semivowel ब or V, with which some grammarians consider it to be at all times optionally interchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 A name of VARUṆA.<BR>2 A water jar.<BR>E.<BR>बण to sound, &c. aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिष्ठ|बंहिष्ठः
बंहिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very much, excessively many.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, इष्ठन् superlative aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहीयस्
बंहीयस्<BR>mfn. (यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very many.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, ईयसुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बठ
बठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (बठति)<BR>To be large, powerful, or able: better also वठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवा
बडवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A mare.<BR>2 A female slave.<BR>3 The nymph AŚVINĪ, or the personified asterism which is designated by a horse's head.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength or force, and वा to go to, affs. क and टाप्, and ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवाग्नि|बडवाग्निः
बडवाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Submarine fire: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>बडवा a mare, and अग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवानल|बडवानलः
बडवानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Submarine fire; in mythology, a being consisting of flame, but with the head of a mare, who sprang from the thighs of ŪRVA, and was received by the ocean.<BR>E.<BR>बडवा a mare, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवाहृत|बडवाहृतः
बडवाहृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The gallant of a female slave, and thence also a slave.<BR>E.<BR>वडवा, and हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवामुख|बडवामुखः
बडवामुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Submarine fire: see बडवानल.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>बडवा a mare, and मुख head, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवासुत
बडवासुत<BR>m. dual. (-तौ)<BR>The two sons of AŚVINĪ, and the physicians of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>बडवा the nymph AŚVINĪ, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण|बणः
बण<BR>r. 1st cl. (बणति)<BR>To sound; better also वण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण|बणः
बण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>बण to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिक्पथ
बणिक्पथ<BR>n. (थं)<BR>Traffick, commerce.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज्, and पथ् for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिक्पुत्त्र
बणिक्पुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>The son of a merchant, or a young merchant or trader.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>A young woman of the same tribe.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज्, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्बन्धु|बणिग्बन्धुः
बणिग्बन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>E.<BR>बणिज् a trader, and बन्धु the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्भाव|बणिग्भावः
बणिग्भाव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Traffick, trade, commerce.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज् a trader, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्वह|बणिग्वहः
बणिग्वह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज् a trader, बह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्
बणिज्<BR>m. (-णिक)<BR>1 A merchant, a trader.<BR>2 The sixth of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas, corresponding to the half of a lunar day.<BR>f. (-णिक्)<BR>Trade, traffick.<BR>E.<BR>पण to transact business, इजि Uṇādi aff., and ब substituted for प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्य|बणिज्यं
बणिज्य<BR>nf. (-ज्यं-ज्या)<BR>Trade, traffick.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज् a trader, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद
बद<BR>r. 1st cl. (बदति)<BR>To be steady or firm.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (बदति-ते बादयति-ते)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To declare or communicate [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">Page598</a>] information: in these two senses, the root is more commonly and correctly written वद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=597" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>1 The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba or scandens.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The seed of the cotton pod.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>Cotton.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>2 A medicinal drug, commonly Varāhakrāntī.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>2 The berry or pod of the cotton.<BR>E.<BR>बद to be firm, Uṇādi aff. अर; or if derived from वद to give information, it is read by some authorities बदर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरामलक|बदरामलकं
बदरामलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>वदर the jujube, and आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरि|बदरिः
बदरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The jujube: see बदर.<BR>E.<BR>बद to be firm, aff. अरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीछदा|बदरीच्छदा
बदरीछदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A kind of perfume, apparently a dried shell fish.<BR>2 A tree, apparently a species of the zizyphus.<BR>E.<BR>बदर, the jujube, छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीपत्रक|बदरीपत्रकं
बदरीपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of perfume, a leaf.<BR>E.<BR>बदरी the jujube, पत्र a leaf, and कन् aff. of comparison added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीफला
बदरीफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, commonly blue Śephālikā or nyctanthes.<BR>E.<BR>बदरी the jujube, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीशैल|बदरीशैलः
बदरीशैल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A part of the Himālaya range, and a celebrated place of pilgrimage; the Bhadrināṭh of modern travellers, or a town and temple on the west bank of the Alakanandā river, in the province of Srinagar.<BR>E.<BR>बदरी the jujube, and शैल mountain; also बदरीवन n. (-नं) The wood of jujubes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>2 Checked, suppressed.<BR>3 Fixed, firm.<BR>4 Withheld.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धकोप
बद्धकोप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>One who governs or suppresses wrath.<BR>E.<BR>वद्ध, and कोप passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धमूल|बद्धमूलं
बद्धमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fast or firmly rooted.<BR>E.<BR>बद्ध, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धशिख|बद्धशिखः
बद्धशिख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Young, a pupil, a child, one whose hair has not been shaven.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A sort of pungent root, called by some a kind of garlic.<BR>E.<BR>बद्ध tied, and शिखा a crest or lock of hair, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धाञ्जलि|बद्धांजलि
बद्धाञ्जलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Saluting respectfully, putting the hands joined to the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>बद्ध attached, अञ्जलि the palms joined and hand touching the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धानुशय
बद्धानुशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Of fixed intent.<BR>2 Taking aim.<BR>E.<BR>वद्ध, and अनुशय purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध<BR>r. 1st cl. (बीभत्सते)<BR>1 To bind or tie.<BR>2 To hate, to despise, to loath.<BR>3 To suffer change or affection of the mind.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (बधति बाधयति)<BR>1 To tie, to bind.<BR>2 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter, slaying, murder.<BR>2 A killer, a slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>बध substituted for हन to kill, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधक
बधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A slaughterer, a killer.<BR>E.<BR>हन changed to बध, and कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधकाङ्क्षिन्
बधकाङ्क्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्क्षि)<BR>Wishing death.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and काङ्क्षिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधकाम्या
बधकाम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>Intent or desire to kill.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and काम्या desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधजीविन्
बधजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A hunter, a fowler, a butcher, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बध killing, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधत्र
बधत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A weapon.<BR>E.<BR>बध to kill, Uṇādi aff. त्रच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधदण्ड
बधदण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Capital punishment.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधस्थली
बधस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A place of slaughter or execution.<BR>E.<BR>बध killing, स्थल ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधस्थान
बधस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Place of slaughter or execution.<BR>E.<BR>बध killing, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधाङ्गक
बधाङ्गक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Poison.<BR>E.<BR>बध killing, अङ्ग the body, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधार्ह
बधार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Deserving death.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Deaf.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, (the hearing,) aff. किरन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधू
बधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, aff. ऊ; it is more usually derived from वह to bear, and is consequently written with the semivowel: see वधू, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोदर्क
बधोदर्क<BR>mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं)<BR>Effecting or causing death.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and उदर्क future result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोद्यत
बधोद्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Murderous, felonious, an assassin, a murderer.<BR>E.<BR>बध killing, and उद्यत endeavouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोपाय
बधोपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Instrument or means of putting to death.<BR>E.<BR>बध, and उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्य
बध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Deserving death.<BR>2 Condemned to death.<BR>E.<BR>बध for हन to kill, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यता
बध्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>2 Fitness to be killed.<BR>E.<BR>बध्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, बध्यत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यभूमि
बध्यभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Place of public execution.<BR>E.<BR>बध्य, and भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यस्थान
बध्यस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Place of execution.<BR>E.<BR>बध्य, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्वा
बध्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having tied or bound.<BR>2 Having killed.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to tie, or बध to kill, and क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्रं|बध्र
बध्रं<BR>n. (-ध्रं)<BR>Lead.<BR>f. (-ध्री)<BR>A thong.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, aff. ष्ट्रन्; see वर्द्ध and वर्द्धी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्र्य
बध्र्य<BR>n. (-ध्र्यं)<BR>A shoe, a slipper.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind or tie, ष्ट्रान् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन
बन<BR>(बनु) r. 8th cl. (बनुते)<BR>To ask or beg, preferably written वन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध|बंध|बंधः|बन्धः
बन्ध<BR>r. 9th cl. (बध्नाति) r. 10th cl. (बन्धयति)<BR>To bind or tie;<BR>with आङ् prefixed,<BR>To loosen, to let loose.<BR>With अनु,<BR>1 To follow.<BR>2 To be affixed or attached to.<BR>With नि,<BR>to disunite.<BR>With सम,<BR>to connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध|बंध|बंधः|बन्धः
बन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>1 A pledge, a deposit.<BR>2 A binding, a tie or fetter, &c.<BR>3 Binding, tying.<BR>4 The body.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to tie, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धक|बंधक|बन्धकं|बंधकः|बन्धकः
बन्धक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Exchanging, barter.<BR>2 A city.<BR>3 A binding.<BR>4 Binding, confinement.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pledge.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 An unchaste woman, a harlot, a wanton.<BR>2 A barren woman.<BR>3 A she elephant.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, ण्वुल् aff. fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धतन्त्र|बंधतंत्र
बन्धतन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A complete army, or one with its four divisions, of chariots, elephants, horse, and foot.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध binding, तन्त्र an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धन|बंधन|बन्धनं
बन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Binding, tying, confining.<BR>2 A rope for tying cattle.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>4 Hurting, injuring.<BR>mfn. subst. (नः-ना or नी-नं)<BR>The implement of binding or tying, a rope, a chain, a bandage, a ligature, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to tie, aff. ल्युट् or बुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनग्रन्थि|बंधनग्रंथि|बन्धनग्रन्थिः
बन्धनग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>1 A rope for tying cattle.<BR>2 The knot of a ligature.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धन tying, and ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनरज्जु
बन्धनरज्जु<BR>f. (-ज्जुः)<BR>1 A rope for tying cattle, &c.<BR>2 Any rope or string used for tying.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धन tying, रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनवेश्मन्|बंधनवेश्मन्
बन्धनवेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>A prison.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धन confinement, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनालय|बंधनालय|बन्धनालयः
बन्धनालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A prison.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धन confinement, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=598" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धस्तम्भ|बंधस्तंभ|बन्धस्तम्भः
बन्धस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध a binding, and लम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धित्र|बन्धित्रं|बंधित्रः|बन्धित्रः
बन्धित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Love, desire.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, इत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धु|बंधु|बंधुः|बन्धुः
बन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>1 A kinsman, a relation, but especially a distant or cognate kinsman, and subsequent in right of inheritance to the gentile or Sagotra; the Bandhu, is of three kinds; the kinsman of the person himself, of his father, or his mother, as his father's brother's son, and his mother's sister's or brother's son; and the same reckoning upwards, as his father's father's sister's son, &c.<BR>2 A friend.<BR>3 A brother.<BR>4 A flower, (Pentapetes phænicea.)<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind or connect, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुक|बंधुक|बंधुकः|बन्धुकः
बन्धुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flower: see बन्धूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजन|बंधुजन|बन्धुजनः
बन्धुजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A relation, a friend.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजीव|बंधुजीव|बन्धुजीवः
बन्धुजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A flower, (Pentapetes Phoenicea.)<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु a friend, जीव to live, aff. अच्; also कन् being added, बन्धुजीबक (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुता|बंधुता
बन्धुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A multitude of relations.<BR>2 Relationship.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु a kinsman, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुत्व|बंधुत्वं
बन्धुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Relationship.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, बन्धुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदत्त|बंधुदत्त
बन्धुदत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Given by a kinsman.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>One kind of female property, that given to a girl at her marriage by her own relations.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुर|बंधुर|बन्धुरं|बन्धुरः
बन्धुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Uneven, undulating, wavy, partially even, and depressed.<BR>2 Bowed, bent.<BR>3 Pleasing, delightful, handsome, beautiful.<BR>4 Deaf.<BR>5 Injurious, mischievous.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A goose.<BR>2 A flower, (Pentapetes Phœnicea.)<BR>3 A drug, commonly Bireng.<BR>4 A bird.<BR>5 A crane.<BR>6 A drug, commonly Ṛṣabha.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A diadem, a crest.<BR>2 The dregs of oil, or oil cake.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A whore, a prostitute.<BR>f. plu. (-राः)<BR>The meal of parched corn.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, उरच् Uṇādi aff.; also with ऊरच्, aff. बन्धूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुहीन|बंधुहीन
बन्धुहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Friendless, relationless.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु, and हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूक|बंधूक|बंधूकः|बन्धूकः
बन्धूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A shrub bearing a red flower, (Pentapetes Phœnicea, but also applied to the Ixora Bandhuca.).<BR>2 A tree, (Pentaptera.)<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, ऊक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूकपुष्प|बन्धूकपुष्पः
बन्धूकपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पं)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>बन्धूक the Pentapetes or Ixora, and पुष्प flower; having a similar flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूर|बंधूर|बन्धूरः
बन्धूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Wavy, undulating, uneven.<BR>2 Bowing, bent.<BR>3 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hole, a chasm.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, Uṇādi aff. ऊरच्; also वन्धुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूलि|बंधूलि|बंधूलिः|बन्धूलिः
बन्धूलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A flower, (Pentapetes, &c.): see बन्धूक.<BR>E.<BR>वन्ध, and ऊलिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्य|बंध्य|बन्ध्यः
बन्ध्य<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं)<BR>1 Barren, unfruitful, not bearing fruit in due season.<BR>2 Detained, confined, under arrest.<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>1 A childless woman.<BR>2 A barren cow.<BR>3 A perfume, commonly Bālā.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभूवस्
बभूवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-भूषी-वः)<BR>Been, become.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्र
बभ्र<BR>r. 1st cl. (बभ्रति)<BR>To go; also वभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रवी
बभ्रवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>बभ्रु ŚIVA, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रि|बभ्रिः
बभ्रि<BR>mfn. (-भ्रिः-भ्रिः-भ्रि)<BR>Who or what has, holds, possesses, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to cherish, किन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रु|बभ्रुः
बभ्रु<BR>mfn. (-भ्रुः-भ्रुः or भ्रूः-भ्रु)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Tawny, &c.<BR>3 Baldheaded through disease.<BR>m. (-भ्रुः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 AGNI or fire.<BR>4 A large ichneumon.<BR>5 The name of a Muni or holy sage.<BR>6 A rat.<BR>n. (-भ्रु)<BR>1 A tawny or brown colour.<BR>2 Any object of that colour.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to fill, aff. कु, and the initial repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भर|बंभर|बंभरः|बम्भरः
बम्भर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>बम्भ imitative sound, रा to make, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भराली|बंभराली
बम्भराली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A fly.<BR>E.<BR>बम्भ imitative sound, रा to make, लच् aff.; also भम्भराली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर
बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Best, excellent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A boon, a blessing, &c.<BR>2 A son-in-law.<BR>3 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>4 A catamite.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>f. (-र)<BR>Asparagus racemosus.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The three myrobalans.<BR>n. or ind. (-रं)<BR>Slightly desired, preferable.<BR>E.<BR>बॄ to select, &c. अप् aff; the root is more usually written वॄ, and the derivative वर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्ब|बर्ब
बर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (बर्ब्बति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बट|बर्बट|बर्बटः|बर्ब्बटः
बर्ब्बट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>बर्ब्ब to go, अट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बणा|बर्बणा
बर्ब्बणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A blue fly.<BR>E.<BR>बर्ब्ब to go, aff. युच् or derived from वर् imitative sound, and बण or वण् to sound, aff. अच्, बर्ब्बण or वर्ब्बण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बर|बर्बर|बर्बरः
बर्ब्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blockhead, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ब्ब to go, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह<BR>r. 1st cl. (बर्हते)<BR>1 To be pre-eminent or excellent; (also वर्ह, but less usually.)<BR>2 To speak or tell.<BR>3 To kill or hurt.<BR>4 To cover.<BR>5 To remember.<BR>6 To spread.<BR>7 To give. (In these senses it is more usually वर्ह.)<BR>r. 10th cl. (बर्हयति)<BR>To hurt or kill; also वर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह<BR>mn. (-र्हः-र्हं)<BR>1 A peacock's tail.<BR>2 A leaf.<BR>3 Dependants, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>बर्ह to spread, &c. aff. अच्; this word and the corresponding forms are more usually derived from वृह to increase, &c. and are written with the semivowel: see वर्ह, वर्हिस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (बलति बलयति)<BR>1 To live.<BR>2 To hoard grain.<BR>3 To prevent or obstruct wealth.<BR>r. 1st cl. (बलते)<BR>1 To kill.<BR>2 To go.<BR>r. 10th cl. (बालयते)<BR>To explain.<BR>(बालयति)<BR>To support, nourish, rear, as a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, stout, robust, powerful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA, and the third of the three incarnations termed RĀMAS.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 A demon, slain by INDRA.<BR>4 The Varuṇa tree.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Strength, power.<BR>2 Bulkiness.<BR>3 Form, figure.<BR>4 An army, forces.<BR>5 Gum myrrh.<BR>6 Semen virile.<BR>7 The body.<BR>8 The leaf of a tree.<BR>9 Blood.<BR>10 Rigour, severity.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>बल to live, aff. अच्; in some of the senses it may be derived from वल to go or surround, and may then be written with the semivowel: see वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्ष|बलक्षः
बलक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>White, (the colour, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and क्षै to waste, aff. क; this word is more properly written वलक्ष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलज|बलजं
बलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by or from strength or power.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A field.<BR>2 A city gate.<BR>3 Fruit.<BR>4 War.<BR>5 Pith, marrow.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A pretty or handsome woman.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद्विष्
बलद्विष्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and द्विष् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेव|बलदेवः
बलदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>बल the same, and देव divine, or बल strength, and देव who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=599" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलनिग्रह
बलनिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Weakening, reducing strength or power.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रसू
बलप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>ROHIṆĪ, the mother of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्र|बलभद्रः
बलभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 BALADEVA, as above.<BR>2 ANANTA, the great serpent, considered as identified with the preceding, BALADEVA being regarded by some authorities as an incarnation of ANANTA.<BR>3 A strong or robust man.<BR>4 A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 A young girl, a maiden.<BR>2 A drug, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and भद्र auspicious, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्रिका
बलभद्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal plant, Trāyamāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>बलभद्रा the same, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभिद्
बलभिद्<BR>mfn. (-भिद्)<BR>Breaking or routing an army.<BR>m. (-भिद्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and भिद् who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलराम|बलरामः
बलराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The demigod named BALARĀMA, half brother to KṚṢṆA, and the third of the RĀMAS; according to some, the eighth Avatāra of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, रम to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलल|बललः
बलल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>BALARĀMA: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, aff. लच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्|बलवन्त्
बलवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Strong, stout, lusty, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्ता
बलवत्ता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Strength, power.<BR>E.<BR>बलवत्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्द्धन
बलवर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Strengthening.<BR>2 Ennobling.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and वर्द्धन augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्द्धिन्
बलवर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>Strengthening.<BR>f. (-र्द्धिनी)<BR>A plant: see जीबक.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and वर्द्धिन् what augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलविन्यास|बलविन्यासः
बलविन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Array of troops.<BR>E.<BR>बल forces, and विन्यास disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवृत्रनिसूदन
बलवृत्रनिसूदन<BR>m. (नः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बल, वृत्र two demons, and निसूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवृत्रहन्
बलवृत्रहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बलवृत्र as before, हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलव्यसन
बलव्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Defeat or rout of an army.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and व्यसन calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलशालिता
बलशालिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pride of, or confidence in strength or prowess.<BR>E.<BR>बलशालि, and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलशालिन्
बलशालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having strength, confident of strength, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसूदन|बलसूदनः
बलसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बल the demons, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलस्थिति|बलस्थितिः
बलस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A royal residence, a royal camp or quarters.<BR>E.<BR>बल forces, स्थिति station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहन्
बलहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and हन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहीन
बलहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Weak, infirm.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहीनता
बलहीनता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Exhaustion, weakness, prostration of strength, infirmity from fatigue or age, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बलहीन, and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाका
बलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of crane.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, अक् to go, aff. अच्; it is preferably written वलाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाञ्चिता|बलांचिता
बलाञ्चिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A sort of Vīṇā or lute, called also RĀMA'S lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाट|बलाटः
बलाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of beam, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and अट what goes or grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्कार|बलात्कारः
बलात्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Violence, oppression, exaction.<BR>2 (In law) The detention of the person of a debtor by his creditor, and the violent measures taken by the latter, (flogging, &c.) to recover his debt.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, अत to go, aff. क्विप्, बलात्, and कार making, doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्मिका
बलात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, आत्मन् self, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाध्यक्ष|बलाध्यक्षः
बलाध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Commander of an army, a general.<BR>E.<BR>वल, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलान्वित
बलान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strong, powerful.<BR>2 Leading an army.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलानुज|बलानुजः
बलानुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>बल BALARĀMA, and अनुज younger born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलापकर्षम्
बलापकर्षम्<BR>ind.<BR>By force.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and अपकर्ष removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाबल
बलाबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong and weak.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and अबल feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलावलेप|बलावलेपः
बलावलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Pride of strength or prowess.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and अबलेप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाय|बलायः
बलाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, अय to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाराति|बलारातिः
बलाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बल a demon, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलालक|बलालकः
बलालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Caronda, (Carissa carandas.)<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, आङ् before ला to get, aff. बुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाश|बलाशः
बलाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The phlegmatic humour.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, अश to eat or destroy, aff. अच्; also with कन् added बलाशक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलास|बलासः
बलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The phlegmatic humour.<BR>E.<BR>बल life or strength, अस to pervade, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासम|बलासमः
बलासम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>One of the Jaina saints.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, असम unequalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाह|बलाहं|बलाहः
बलाह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, आहा to quit, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहक|बलाहकः
बलाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 One of the Nāgas or infernal serpents.<BR>4 The name of a demon.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, अ the negative prefix to हा to abandon, aff.<BR>E.<BR>क्वुन् strength, this word is differently derived also, and preferably written वलाहक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलि|बलिः
बलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 Tax, royal revenue.<BR>2 An oblation, a religious offering in general.<BR>3 The handle of a Chowrie or fly-flapper.<BR>4 Presentation of food to all created beings, one of the five great sacraments of the Hindu religion: it consists in throwing a small parcel of the offering, Ghee or rice, or the like, into the open air at the back of the house.<BR>5 The sacrifice of an animal, or raw flesh offered to the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>6 Fragments of food left at an oblation or a meal.<BR>7 An animal, or one which is fit for an oblation.<BR>8 Three folds of skin at the end of the rectum.<BR>9 A king, and Daitya, also MAHĀBALI, the virtuous sovereign of Mahābali-pura, tricked out of the dominion he had obtained over earth and heaven, by VIṢṆU, in the Vāmana or dwarf Avatāra, and left, in consideration of his merits, the sovereignty of Pātāla, or the infernal regions.<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>1 A wrinkle, skin shrivelled by old age.<BR>2 The fold of skin in stout persons, especially females, upon the upper part of the belly, or between the ensiform cartilage and the navel.<BR>3 The ridge of a thatch.<BR>E.<BR>बल to live, or बध to hurt or kill, ध changed to ल, aff. इन् or इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=600" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिक
बलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The edge of a thatch.<BR>E.<BR>बलि the ridge, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर
बलिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Offering sacrifices.<BR>2 Producing wrinkles.<BR>E.<BR>बलि before कृ to make, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकरम्भ|बलिकरम्भः
बलिकरम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Sacrificial cake.<BR>E.<BR>बलि, and करम्भ a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर्म्मन्|बलिकर्मन्
बलिकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Offering of oblations to all creatures.<BR>E.<BR>बलि, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिदान|बलिदानं
बलिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Offering victims in sacrifice.<BR>2 Giving food to all beings.<BR>E.<BR>बलि, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिध्वंसिन्
बलिध्वंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>बलि the king so named, and ध्वंसिन् injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्
बलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Strong, stout, robust.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A buffalo.<BR>3 A bull.<BR>4 A hog.<BR>5 Phlegm.<BR>6 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>7 A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>8 A sort of jasmine, (J. pubescens.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Sida cordifolia.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन|बलिनः
बलिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shrivelled, wrinkled, flabby, flaccid.<BR>E.<BR>बलि wrinkled skin, aff. न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिनन्दन|बलिनंदन|बलिनन्दनः
बलिनन्दन<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>VĀṆĀSURA, the son of BALI.<BR>E.<BR>बलि, and नन्दन the son; BALI had however four sons, to either of whom the epithet is applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्दम|बलिंदम|बलिंदमः
बलिन्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>बलि, and दम to humble, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिपुष्ट|बलिपुष्टः
बलिपुष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>बलि fragments of food, and पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिप्रिय|बलिप्रियः
बलिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Lodh tree.<BR>E.<BR>बलि sacrifice, and प्रिय fond of; said to grow the quicker for being perfumed and illuminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभ|बलिभः
बलिभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Shrivelled, withered, flaccid, wrinkled.<BR>E.<BR>बलि a wrinkle, भ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभुज्
बलिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 A sparrow.<BR>3 A crane.<BR>E.<BR>बलि the orts of a meal or sacrifice, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमत्|बलिमन्त्
बलिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Wrinkled, shrivelled, flaccid.<BR>E.<BR>बलि a wrinkle, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमन्दिर|बलिमंदिर|बलिमन्दिरं
बलिमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>बलि the Daitya, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमुख|बलिमुखः
बलिमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>बलि a wrinkle, and मुख a face: also बलीमुख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिष्ठ|बलिष्ठः
बलिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very strong, more or most powerful.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and इष्ठन् super. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिष्णु|बलिष्णुः
बलिष्णु<BR>mfn. (ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Arrogant, disrespectful.<BR>E.<BR>बल to be powerful, इष्णु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसङ्ग
बलिसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The lash of a whip.<BR>2 A number of monkeys.<BR>3 The base of an ant hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसद्मन्
बलिसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>The infernal regions.<BR>E.<BR>बलि the Daitya, sovereign of Pātāla, and मद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिहन्
बलिहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>बलि BALI, and हन् to injure, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीन|बलीनः
बलीन<BR>m. (नः)<BR>A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीमुख|बलीमुखः
बलीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>बली a wrinkle, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीयस्
बलीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very strong, exceedingly powerful.<BR>E.<BR>बल strong, ईयसुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीयस्त्व
बलीयस्त्व<BR>n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>Superiority in strength.<BR>E.<BR>बलीयस्, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीवर्द्द|बलीवर्द|बलीवर्दः|बलीवर्द्दः
बलीवर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>A bull or ox.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, and वर्द्ध increasing, ली substituted for ल, and द final for ध; also वरीबर्द्द and वलीवर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपविष्ट
बलोपविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Endowed with or possessed of strength.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and उपविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपेत
बलोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Possessed of strength.<BR>E.<BR>बल, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्य|बल्यं|बल्यः
बल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Strong, vigorous.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Semen virile.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>बल strength, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बष्कयणी
बष्कयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A cow bearing many calves: see बष्कयणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहि|बहिः
बहि<BR>(इ) बहि r. 1st cl. (वंहते)<BR>To grow or increase; also वहि, but upon inferior authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहु
बहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-हुः-ह्वी-हु)<BR>1 Much, many.<BR>2 Large, great.<BR>E.<BR>बहि to increase, Uṇādi aff. कु; it is less correctly derived from वह to obtain, and written वहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुक|बहुकः
बहुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crab.<BR>2 A gallinule.<BR>3 A plant, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>4 The digger of a tank, (जलखातके.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुकण्टक|बहुकण्टकः
बहुकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A prickly plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>2 The marshy date tree.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, कण्ट a thorn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुकर|बहुकरः
बहुकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 A sweeper.<BR>2 Industrious, labouring.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A camel.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A broom.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, कृ to do, अप् or टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुक्षम|बहुक्षमः
बहुक्षम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and क्षम to bear, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगन्ध|बहुगन्धं|बहुगन्धः
बहुगन्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Smelling, strong-scented.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Olibanum.<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine.<BR>2 The bud of the Champac.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, गन्ध odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगर्ह्यवाच्
बहुगर्ह्यवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Talking much, and blameably.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, गर्ह्य reproachable, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगुण
बहुगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Many times.<BR>2 Having many good qualities.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and गुण quality, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुग्रन्थि|बहुग्रन्थिः
बहुग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>Tamarisk, (Tamarix diœca.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and ग्रन्थि a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुग्रह
बहुग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>What takes or holds much.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and ग्रह what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतन्त्रि|बहुतन्त्रिः
बहुतन्त्रि<BR>mfn. (-न्त्रिः-न्त्री-न्त्रि)<BR>Many-fibred, (applicable only to the body.)<BR>E.<BR>वहु many, and तन्त्री a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतन्त्रीक|बहुतंत्रीक|बहुतन्त्रीकः
बहुतन्त्रीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Many-stringed, (a musical instrument, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, तन्त्री a wire, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतर
बहुतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Much, many, most.<BR>E.<BR>तरप् aff. added to बहु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतस्
बहुतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From or by much, or many.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतिथ|बहुतिथः
बहुतिथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-थी-थं)<BR>Manieth, (the ordinary of many.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, much, डट् aff. and तिथुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्र
बहुत्र<BR>ind.<BR>In many ways, or places, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, many, त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्व|बहुत्वं
बहुत्व<BR>n. (त्वं)<BR>Plurality, multitude, muchness, abundance.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्वक्क|बहुत्वक्कः
बहुत्वक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>The Bhoj, or Birch tree.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, त्वच् skin or bark, कन् aff. having several layers of bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्वच्
बहुत्वच्<BR>m. (-त्वक्)<BR>The Bhojpatra, or Birch tree.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and त्वच् bark: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=601" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुद
बहुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Liberal, munificent.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदक्षिण
बहुदक्षिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Accompanied with many presents, (a ceremony.)<BR>2 Liberal, bountiful.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and दक्षिणा a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदण्डिक|बहुदण्डिकः
बहुदण्डिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having many staff-bearers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, दण्डिन् having a staff, कन् aff.; also in the masculine form बहुदण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदुग्ध|बहुदुग्धः
बहुदुग्ध<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>A cow giving much milk.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and टुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदुग्धिका
बहुदुग्धिका<BR>f. (-काः)<BR>A plant, yielding a caustic milky juice, (Euphorbia, of various sorts.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, टुग्ध milk, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदोष
बहुदोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Full of faults or defects, very wicked, very bad.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदृष्ट
बहुदृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Experienced.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधन
बहुधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wealthy, rich.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधा
बहुधा<BR>ind.<BR>In many ways, sorts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधागत
बहुधागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dispersed, scattered.<BR>E.<BR>बहुधा, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधार|बहुधारं
बहुधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुनाद|बहुनादः
बहुनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The conch shell.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपटु|बहुपटुः
बहुपटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-ट्वी-टु)<BR>Very clever.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपत्र|बहुपत्रं|बहुपत्रः
बहुपत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Many-leaved.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>An onion.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Talc.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A drug, (Trigonella foenugræcum.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, पत्र a leaf, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपर्णी
बहुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Trigonella fœnugræcum.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपाद्
बहुपाद्<BR>m. (-पाद्)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, पाद foot; also बहुपाद.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>alluding to the branches, which grow downwards and take root again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपुत्त्र
बहुपुत्त्र<BR>mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं)<BR>Having many children.<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus).<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, पुत्त्र a child or produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रज|बहुप्रजः
बहुप्रज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Having a numerous progeny.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A sort of grass: see मुञ्ज.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, प्रजा offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रतिज्ञ|बहुप्रतिज्ञः
बहुप्रतिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Complicated, containing more than one circumstance.<BR>2 (In law) Comprising many counts, (a plaint, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, प्रतिज्ञा assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रद|बहुप्रदः
बहुप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Munificent, bountiful.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रवाह
बहुप्रवाह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Flowing in many streams.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and प्रवाह course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रसू
बहुप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of many children.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and प्रसू who bears offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुफल|बहुफलः
बहुफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Fertile, fruitful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The opposite leaved fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुभाग्य
बहुभाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and भाग्य fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुभुज्
बहुभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Voracious.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमत
बहुमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thought much of, respected, considered.<BR>2 Having many different opinions.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमति|बहुमतिः
बहुमति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Value, estimation, prizing or preferring.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमल|बहुमलः
बहुमल<BR>m. (-लं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमार्ग|बहुमार्गं|बहुमार्गः
बहुमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A place where four roads meet.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमान|बहुमानः
बहुमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Respect, reverence.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूर्त्ति|बहुमूर्ति|बहुमूर्तिः|बहुमूर्त्तिः
बहुमूर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति)<BR>Multiform.<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, भूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूर्द्धन्
बहुमूर्द्धन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धा-र्द्धा-र्द्ध)<BR>Many-headed.<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, मूर्द्धन् a forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूल|बहुमूलः
बहुमूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Many-rooted, having many roots.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of reed or grass: see इक्कट and इत्कट.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and मूल a root; also with कन् added, बहुमूलक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूल्य|बहुमूल्यं
बहुमूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Costly, precious.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and मूल price, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरूप|बहुरूपः
बहुरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Multiform.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Resin.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>4 Love, CUPID.<BR>5 A chameleon.<BR>6 BRAHMĀ.<BR>7 Hair.<BR>8 One of the Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, रूप shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरेख
बहुरेख^1<BR>m. plu. (-खाः)<BR>Wrinkles, furrows, marks of care or pain.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, रेखा a line.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161210. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 306. note: m. noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरेतस्
बहुरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and रेतम् seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरोमन्
बहुरोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A sheep.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुल|बहुलं|बहुलः
बहुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Much, many.<BR>2 Black.<BR>3 Variously applicable, comprehensive, (a rule, &c.)<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 AGNI or fire.<BR>2 The dark half of a month.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The sky.<BR>f. plu. (-लाः)<BR>The Pleiades.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Indigo.<BR>2 Cardamoms.<BR>3 A cow.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, ला to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलत्व|बहुलत्वं
बहुलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Abundance, muchness.<BR>2 Comprehensiveness, (of a rule.)<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल् बहुलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलीकरण|बहुलीकरणं
बहुलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Multiplying, magnifying, making much.<BR>2 Winnowing.<BR>E.<BR>बहुल, and करण making, with च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलीकृत|बहुलीकृतं
बहुलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Threshed and winnowed.<BR>2 Made manifold or much.<BR>E.<BR>बहुल much, कृत made, and च्चि substituted for the final of the former, by which the ई is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवचन
बहुवचन<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>The plural number, (in grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and वचन saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवार|बहुवारः
बहुवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fruit, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, वॄ to nourish, aff. अण्; also with कन् added, बहुवारक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुविध|बहुविधः
बहुविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Various, multiform, of many sorts or kinds.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुविलीर्ण
बहुविलीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Widely spread or diffused.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A shrub bearing a small red and black berry, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, विलीर्ण spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवीज|बहुवीजं
बहुवीज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Having many or much seed.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The custard apple, (Annona squamosa.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and वीज a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवीर्य्य|बहुवीर्य|बहुवीर्यः|बहुवीर्य्यः
बहुवीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>E.<BR>वहु much, and वीर्य्य seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुव्रीहि|बहुव्रीहिः
बहुव्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>One of the forms of grammatical composition, the compounding two or more words to furnish an epithet or attributive, as बहुमाल or बहुमालक having many necklaces, from वहु, and माला A necklace.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and व्रीहि grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=602" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशत्रु|बहुशत्रुः
बहुशत्रु<BR>mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु)<BR>Having many enemies.<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशस्
बहुशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Abundantly, plentifully.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, many, शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशाख
बहुशाख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Having many branches or ramifications.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुश्रुत
बहुश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Well taught, learned.<BR>2 Acquainted with the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and श्रुत heard, or श्रुति Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुश्रेयस्
बहुश्रेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Having many excellencies.<BR>2 Very excellent.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and श्रेयस् best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुस्पृश्
बहुस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (स्पृक्)<BR>Expanded, spread, diffused.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and स्पृश् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसन्तति|बहुसंतति|बहुसंततिः|बहुसन्ततिः
बहुसन्तति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A species of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa)<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, सन्तति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसुता
बहुसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus.)<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, सुत a birth or shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसू
बहुसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 A sow.<BR>2 The mother of many children.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, and सू bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसूति|बहुसूतिः
बहुसूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A cow bearing many calves.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, सू to bear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुस्वन|बहुस्वनः
बहुस्वन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, स्वन noise or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहूदक|बहूदकः
बहूदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having much water.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्ल
बह्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (बह्लते)<BR>1 To be pre-eminent or excellent, (also वह्ल, but less usually.)<BR>2 To speak or tell.<BR>3 To kill or hurt.<BR>4 To cover, to spread.<BR>5 To give, (also बह्ल in these five senses, and more accurately.)<BR>6 To remember.<BR>r. 10th cl. (बह्लयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वर्थ
बह्वर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Important, having much meaning.<BR>2 Having many objects.<BR>E.<BR>बहु, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वपत्य|बह्वपत्यः
बह्वपत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A cow that has borne many calves.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वाशिन्
बह्वाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Voracious, gluttonous.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वृच्
बह्वृच्<BR>f. (-ह्वृक्)<BR>The Ṛg Veda.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, ऋच् a hymn or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वृची
बह्वृची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The wife of a Brahman conversant with the Ṛg Veda.<BR>E.<BR>बहु many, ऋच् a prayer or incantation, aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बा
बा<BR>ind.<BR>1 As, like.<BR>2 Or, either: see वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाड
बाड<BR>(ऋ) बाडृ r. 1st cl. (-बाडते)<BR>To bathe, to dive and emerge. Vopadeva differs from other authorities in writing this with an initial व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडव|बाडवं|बाडवः
बाडव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Submarine fine.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A stud, a collection of mares.<BR>E.<BR>बाडव a mare, and अण् aff. of derivation: see बडवानल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडवाग्नि|बाडवाग्निः
बाडवाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Hell.<BR>E.<BR>बडवाग्नि submarine fire, and अण् aff. of place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडवेय
बाडवेय<BR>m. du. (-यौ)<BR>The two sons of AŚVINĪ and physicians of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>बडवा a mare, Saṃjñā changed into a mare, and ढक् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडव्य|बाडव्यं
बाडव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A number of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>बाडव a Brahman, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडीर|बाडीरः
बाडीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A servant, a hired labourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाण|बाणः
बाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An arrow, &c.: see वाण.<BR>E.<BR>बण or वण to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणगोचर|बाणगोचरः
बाणगोचर<BR>m. (-रं)<BR>The course of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>बाण, and गोचर object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणि|बाणिः
बाणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 Speech.<BR>2 The goddess of speech, &c.: see वाणि.<BR>E.<BR>बण or वण to speak, in the causal form, aff. इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिज|बाणिजः
बाणिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A merchant, a trader.<BR>2 Submarine fire.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज्, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिजिक|बाणिजिकः
बाणिजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Submarine fire.<BR>2 A trader, a merchant.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज trade, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिज्य|बाणिज्यं
बाणिज्य<BR>mf. (-ज्यं-ज्या)<BR>Trade, traffic, commerce.<BR>E.<BR>बणिज् a trader, with ष्यञ् aff. or बाणिज् the same, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादर|बादरं|बादरः
बादर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Made of cotton.<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>The cotton plant.<BR>E.<BR>बदर cotton, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध<BR>(ऋ) बाधृ r. 1st cl. (बाधते)<BR>1 To resist, to oppose.<BR>2 To annoy or afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Opposing, hindering.<BR>2 Annoyance.<BR>3 Refutation arising from incompatibility or contradiction of assigned cause and effect (in logic).<BR>E.<BR>बाध to oppose, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधक|बाधकः
बाधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What hinders, opposes, pains, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बाध, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधन|बाधनं
बाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Impeding, opposing.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to oppose, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधमान
बाधमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Paining, annoying.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to annoy, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यमान
बाध्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being harassed or tormented.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to annoy, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधित|बाधितः
बाधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Obstructed, impeded.<BR>2 Pained, tormented.<BR>3 Self-refuted (in logic), contradictory, incompatible.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धकिनेय|बांधकिनेय|बांधकिनेयः|बान्धकिनेयः
बान्धकिनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bastard, the son of a disloyal wife.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धकी a wanton, aff. ढक्, and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धव|बांधव|बांधवः|बान्धवः
बान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A relation, a kinsman: see बन्धु.<BR>2 A friend.<BR>E.<BR>बन्धु a kinsman, अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धवाक्रोशिन्
बान्धवाक्रोशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Calling upon or bewailing a kinsman.<BR>E.<BR>बान्धव, and आक्रोशिन् who calls aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाभ्रवी
बाभ्रवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>बभ्रु ŚIVA, with अण् and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्ब्बटीर|बार्बटीर|बार्बटीरः|बार्ब्बटीरः
बार्ब्बटीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Tin.<BR>2 A shoot of the mango.<BR>3 The son of an unchaste woman, a bastard.<BR>E.<BR>बर्ब्बटी a whore, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल|बालं|बालः
बाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Ignorant, unwise, uninstructed.<BR>2 Young, infantine, a child.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>1 An infant, a child; it usually means the young child, under five years old, but is equally applicable till sixteen years of age.<BR>2 A colt.<BR>3 A five year old elephant.<BR>4 An elephant's tail.<BR>5 A horse's tail.<BR>6 Any tail.<BR>7 Hair.<BR>8 A sort of fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A perfume, perhaps a sort of fragrant grass, (Andropogon schænanthus.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Small cardamoms.<BR>2 A woman, a female.<BR>3 Aloes.<BR>4 Another plant, commonly Acnadhi.<BR>5 The cocoa-nut.<BR>6 Turmeric.<BR>7 A sort of jasmine.<BR>8 A flower, (Hibiscus tortuosus, Rox.)<BR>9 Pure, (applied specially to a female animal, as a heifer, &c. fit for an oblation.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of ear-ring.<BR>E.<BR>बल to live, aff. घञ्, it sometimes occurs, but less accurately perhaps, with a palatial initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालक|बालकं|बालकः
बालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A boy, an infant: see the last.<BR>2 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>3 The tail of a horse or elephant.<BR>4 A finger ring. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">Page604</a>]<BR>5 A bracelet.<BR>6 A perfume; also द्रीवेर.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>1 A female infant.<BR>2 Sand.<BR>3 The knot or flower of an ear-ring.<BR>4 The rustling of leaves.<BR>5 Small cardamoms.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of Hibiscus, (H. mutabilis.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=603" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकत्व
बालकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Childhood, childishness.<BR>E.<BR>बालक, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, बालकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकीय
बालकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Childish, infantine.<BR>E.<BR>बालक, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकृमि|बालकृमिः
बालकृमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A louse.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, and कृमि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालखिल्य|बालखिल्यः
बालखिल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A divine personage, of the size of the thumb, sixty thousand of whom were produced from the hair of BRAHMA'S body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालगर्ब्भिणी
बालगर्ब्भिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A cow with calf for the first time.<BR>E.<BR>बाल young, गर्ब्भिणी pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालचर्य्य|बालचर्य|बालचर्यः|बालचर्य्यः
बालचर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>बाल a child, and चर्य्य usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतनय|बालतनयः
बालतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A young son.<BR>2 A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>बाल young or small, and तनय offspring, leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतन्त्र|बालतंत्र|बालतन्त्रं
बालतन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>Midwifery, care of a lying-in woman, and her child.<BR>E.<BR>बाल an infant, and तन्त्र rule, management.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतृण|बालतृणं
बालतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Young grass.<BR>E.<BR>बाल young, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालदलक|बालदलकः
बालदलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>बाल small, दल a leaf, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालधन
बालधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The property of a minor or infant.<BR>E.<BR>बाल, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालधि|बालधिः
बालधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A hairy tail, as a horse's, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, धा to have, कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपत्र|बालपत्रः
बालपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>बाल young or small, and पत्र a leaf; also with कन् added, बालपत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपाश्या
बालपाश्या<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>1 An ornament of gold or silver, &c. worn between the hair divided on the forehead.<BR>2 A string of pearls binding the hair.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, पाश a tie or quantity, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपुष्पी
बालपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A sort of jasmine, (J. auriculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>बाल the hair, and पुष्प flower; worn in the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालभद्रक|बालभद्रकः
बालभद्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of mineral poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालभाव|बालभावः
बालभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Childhood.<BR>E.<BR>बाल, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालमूषिका
बालमूषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small rat or mouse.<BR>E.<BR>बाल small, भूषिका a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालयज्ञोपवीतक|बालयज्ञोपवीतकं
बालयज्ञोपवीतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of substitute for the sacrificial thread, a string or scarf as worn by children, (?)<BR>E.<BR>बाल a child, and यज्ञोपवीत the Brahminical cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालराज|बालराजं
बालराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>बाल young, and राज what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवत्स|बालवत्सः
बालवत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>A pigeon, a dove.<BR>E.<BR>बाल a child, and वत्स dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवासस्
बालवासस्<BR>m. (-साः)<BR>Woollen garments.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, (of cows, goats, &c.) and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवायज|बालवायजं
बालवायज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवाह्य|बालवाह्यः
बालवाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, वह to endeavour, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालव्यजन|बालव्यजनं
बालव्यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A Chowrie, a whisk, a fly-flapper.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, and व्यजन a fan; it being made usually of the tail of the Yak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालव्रत|बालव्रतः
बालव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Bauddha saint; also named MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालसन्ध्याभ|बालसंध्याभ|बालसन्ध्याभः
बालसन्ध्याभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Of a purple colour.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Purple, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>बाल young, and सन्ध्या twilight, आङ् before भा to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालसूर्य्य|बालसूर्य|बालसूर्य्यं
बालसूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>बाल young, सूर्य्य the sun; also with कन् added, बालसूर्य्यक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालहस्त|बालहस्तः
बालहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>The tail of a horse, or any hairy animal.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, and हस्त the hand, to which organ it is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालाक्षी
बालाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A plant, commonly Keśapuṣṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालातप|बालातपः
बालातप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The rays of the rising sun.<BR>E.<BR>बाल, and आतप light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालापत्य
बालापत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Young offspring or progeny.<BR>E.<BR>बाल, and अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालि|बालिः
बालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A monkey, the son of INDRA, killed by RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>बाल hair, and इन् aff.; being born from the hair of his mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिन्
बालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The monkey son of INDRA.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The constellation Aśvinī.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश|बालिशं|बालिशः
बालिश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Young.<BR>2 Ignorant.<BR>3 Careless, heedless.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A pillow.<BR>E.<BR>बाड to emerge, इन् aff., बाडि or बालि, and शो to destroy, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश्य|बालिश्यं
बालिश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>1 Thoughtlessness, heedlessness.<BR>2 Youth.<BR>3 Folly.<BR>E.<BR>बालिश, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिसम्भव
बालिसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Name of a celebrated monkey, the son of BALI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिहन्तृ|बालिहंतृ
बालिहन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>बालि the monkey, and हन्तृ killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालीश|बालीशः
बालीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Pain in making water from gravel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालु|बालुः
बालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A drug, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>E.<BR>बल to live, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुक|बालुकं|बालुकः
बालुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drug and perfume; also Elavāluka.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Sand, gravel.<BR>2 (Also बालुकी) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 A sand bath.<BR>E.<BR>बल to live, (by its means,) उकञ् aff. or बालु as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकागड|बालुकागडः
बालुकागड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Cheilodipterus culius and butis, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>बालुका sand, and गड to scatter, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकात्मिका
बालुकात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sugar.<BR>E.<BR>बालुका sand, आत्मन् identity, कन् aff. in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकाप्रभा
बालुकाप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>One of the seven hells of the Jainas, the hell of sand.<BR>E.<BR>बालुका sand, and प्रभा splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुङ्की|बालुंकी
बालुङ्की<BR>f. (-ङ्की)<BR>A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.) also बालुकी, बालुङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुङ्गी|बालुंगी
बालुङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of cucumber: see the last; also with कन् added बालुङ्गिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालूक|बालूकः
बालूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालेय|बालेयः
बालेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Soft.<BR>2 Fit or proper for a child.<BR>3 Fit or proper for a tax, a sacrifice, &c.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An ass.<BR>2 A demon, a Daitya.<BR>3 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>बलि a tax, a sacrifice, or बाल a child, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालेयशाक|बालेयशाकः
बालेयशाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>बालेय an ass, and शाक a potherb; also बालेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालोपवीत|बालोपवीतं
बालोपवीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The sacrificial thread, or a substitute for it as worn by children.<BR>2 A cloth covering the privities.<BR>E.<BR>बाल a child, उपवीत the thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल्य|बाल्यं
बाल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Childhood.<BR>E.<BR>बाल a child, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाष्प|बाष्पं|बाष्पः
बाष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 Vapour, steam.<BR>2 A tear, tears, rheum.<BR>3 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to oppose, Uṇādi aff. प, and ध changed to ष; according to other etymologies, this word is वाष्प, or बास्प, and वास्प<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=604" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह|बाहः
बाह<BR>(ऋ) बाहृ r. 1st cl. (बाहते)<BR>1 To resolve, to attempt perseveringly or resolutely, to endeavour diligently; also वाहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह|बाहः
बाह<BR>mf. (-हः-हा)<BR>The arm.<BR>E.<BR>बाह to endeavour, aff. अच्; it is sometimes read वाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहु|बाहुः
बाहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>1 The arm.<BR>2 The side of any angular geometrical figure, the leg of a triangle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बाध to oppose, उ Uṇādi aff. and ध changed to ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुक|बाहुकः
बाहुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A servant, servile, dependant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The name of NALA, after his change of form, by the bite of KARKOṬAKA Nāga.<BR>2 A monkey.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु an arm, कन् aff. or कृ to do, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुकुन्थ|बाहुकुंथ|बाहुकुन्थः
बाहुकुन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>A wing.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, कुन्थ what adheres to, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुकुब्ज
बाहुकुब्ज<BR>mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं)<BR>Crooked armed.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु an arm, and कुब्ज bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुज|बाहुजः
बाहुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The Kṣatriya or warrior, born from the arms of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A parrot.<BR>3 Sesamum growing wild, or spontaneously.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुत्राण|बाहुत्राणं
बाहुत्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Armour for the arms.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुदन्तिन्|बाहुदंतिन्
बाहुदन्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु an arm, दन्त a tooth, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुदा
बाहुदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The name of a river, said to rise in the snowy chain of the Himālaya, and probably the modern Behut, the classical Hydaspes.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु an arm, and दा bestower; alluding to a legend of a saint's recovering his lost arms, by bathing in this stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुप्रहरण|बाहुप्रहरणः
बाहुप्रहरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>A striker, a boxer.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Boxing, wrestling.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु, and प्रहरण striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुभूषा
बाहुभूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>An armlet, an ornament worn round the upper arm.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, and भूषा an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुमय
बाहुमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or done with the arms.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुमूल|बाहुमूलं
बाहुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The arm-pit.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुयुद्ध|बाहुयुद्धं
बाहुयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Close fight, personal struggle, boxing, wrestling.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, and युद्ध fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल|बाहुलं|बाहुलः
बाहुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Fire or its deity.<BR>2 The month Kārttika.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Mail worn on the arm.<BR>2 A term in grammar, implying various or irregular formation, or construction, or such as is analogous to this word.<BR>E.<BR>बहुल fire, and अण् aff.; also with कन् added, बाहुलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुलेय|बाहुलेयः
बाहुलेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>बाहुला the Pleiades, considered as nymphs, and nurses of this god; aff. of relation ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल्य|बाहुल्यं
बाहुल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Plenty, abundance, quantity.<BR>E.<BR>बहुल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुवीर्य्य|बाहुवीर्य
बाहुवीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Personal prowess.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु, and वीर्य्य heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुसहस्रभृत्
बाहुसहस्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A king killed by PARAŚURĀMA, also named KĀRTAVĪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>बाहु an arm, सहस्र a thousand, and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहूबाहवि
बाहूबाहवि<BR>ind.<BR>Arm to arm, hand to hand, (fighting, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>बाहु the arm, repeated, इच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिट
बिट<BR>r. 1st cl. (वेटति)<BR>To curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिद
बिद<BR>(इ) बिदि r. 1st cl. (बिन्दति)<BR>To make or constitute a part; the root is obsolete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रक्षु|बिभ्रक्षुः
बिभ्रक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>1 Desirous to destroy or lose.<BR>2 Wishing to scorch, fry, parch.<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to break, to fry, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रज्जिषु|बिभ्रज्जिषुः
बिभ्रज्जिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to fry or scorch.<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल|बिलं|बिलः
बिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (बिलति) r. 10th cl. (बेलयति)<BR>To break, to tear or rend, to divide or detach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिस्
बिस्<BR>(इर) बिसिर् r. 4th cl. (बिस्यति)<BR>To throw or cast, to send or direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
बीभत्स<BR>mfn. subst. (-त्सः-त्सा-त्सं)<BR>1 Disgust, abhorrence.<BR>adj.<BR>Detesting, loathing, changed or averted in mind.<BR>2 Cruel, mischievous.<BR>3 Compassionate.<BR>4 Wicked.<BR>5 Envious.<BR>E.<BR>बध to bind, to hate, &c. aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (बुक्कति बुक्कयति-ते)<BR>1 To bark.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>r. 10th cl.<BR>To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क<BR>subst. mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्की-क्कं)<BR>The heart.<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>बुक्क to bark, &c., aff. अच्; also बुक्कन् mn. (-क्का-क्क) also बुक्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कन|बुक्कनं
बुक्कन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Barking, (as of a dog.)<BR>E.<BR>बुक्क to bark, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्काग्रमांस|बुक्काग्रमांसं
बुक्काग्रमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The heart.<BR>E.<BR>बुक्क the heart, अग्र principal, मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कार|बुक्कारः
बुक्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The roar or barking of a lion.<BR>E.<BR>बुक्क to bark, आर aff.; the lion of Hindustan barks much like a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुड
बुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (बुडति)<BR>1 To leave, to abandon.<BR>2 To cover, to clothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद
बुद<BR>(उ, इर) उबुदिर् r. 1st cl. (बुदति-ते)<BR>To discern, to apprehend, to perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Known, understood.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 A generic name for a deified teacher of the Bauddha sect, amongst whom numerous Buddhas are reckoned; the name is especially applied to the ninth incarnation of VIṢṆU and the apparent founder of the religion of the Buddhas; the term is often confounded, but improperly, with a Jina: see जिन.<BR>2 A sage, a wise or learned man.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, aff. क्तः see बुध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धद्रव्य|बुद्धद्रव्यं
बुद्धद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Avarice, covetous accumulation.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्ध known, द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धि|बुद्धिः
बुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिजीविन्
बुद्धिजीविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Rational, an intellectual being.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि, and जीविन् alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिविनाश
बुद्धिविनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Loss or deficiency of understanding.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि, and विनाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिभृत्
बुद्धिभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Wise, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि, and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिमत्|बुद्धिमन्त्
बुद्धिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Wise, learned.<BR>2 Famed, known.<BR>3 Humble, docile.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि wisdom, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिसहाय|बुद्धिसहायः
बुद्धिसहाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि understanding, and सहाय companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिहीन
बुद्धिहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ignorant, silly, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि, And हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिहीनत्व
बुद्धिहीनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Folly, ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धिहीन, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, बुद्धिहीनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धीन्द्रिय|बुद्धींद्रिय|बुद्धीन्द्रियं
बुद्धीन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An organ of intellect, as the mind, eye, ear, nose, tongue, and skin.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि understanding, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=605" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यवज्ञान
बुद्ध्यवज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disregard of or contempt for one's understanding.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्धि, and अवज्ञान disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्बुद|बुद्बुदः
बुद्बुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A bubble.<BR>E.<BR>बुद imitative sound, बुद to perceive, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध|बुधः
बुध<BR>(औ) औबुध r. 1st cl. (बोधति) r. 4th cl. (बुध्यते-ति) also (उ, इर) उबुधिर् r. 1st cl. (बोधति-ते)<BR>To know, to understand.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>to look for, expect.<BR>With प्रति and वि,<BR>to wake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध|बुधः
बुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 BUDHA, the son of the moon, and regent of the planet MERCURY, with whom he is identified.<BR>2 A wise or learned man, a sage.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Indian spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know or understand, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधजन|बुधजनः
बुधजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A wise man.<BR>E.<BR>बुध, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधतात|बुधतातः
बुधतात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The moon, the father of BUDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधवार|बुधवारः
बुधवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Wednesday.<BR>E.<BR>बुध MERCURY, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधसुत|बुधसुतः
बुधसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>PURŪRAVAS, the first king of the lunar dynasty.<BR>E.<BR>बुध BUDHA or MERCURY, and the son of SOMA, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधान|बुधानः
बुधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A wise man, a sage.<BR>2 A holy teacher.<BR>3 One who speaks kindly.<BR>4 A worshipper or adorer of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, आनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधित|बुधितं
बुधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Known, understood.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधिल|बुधिलः
बुधिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, Uṇādi aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्न|बुध्नः
बुध्न<BR>m. (-ध्नः)<BR>1 The root of a tree.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, Uṇādi aff. नक्; also व्रध्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्द
बुन्द<BR>(उ, इर) उबुन्दिर् r. 1st. cl. (बुन्दति-ते)<BR>To discern, to perceive, literally or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्ध
बुन्ध<BR>(उ, इर्) उबुन्धिर् r. 1st. cl. (बुन्धति-ते)<BR>To discern, to perceive: see बुन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षा
बुभुक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, in the desid. form, aff. अड् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षित|बुभुक्षितः
बुभुक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hungry.<BR>E.<BR>बुभुक्षा hunger, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षु
बुभुक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to eat.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सा
बुभुत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>The wishing to know.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सु
बुभुत्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing to know.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूषा
बुभूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Desire to be or become.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, desid. v. affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूषु
बुभूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to be or become.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूर्षु
बुभूर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>1 Wishing to fill.<BR>2 Desirous to nourish, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुल
बुल<BR>r. 10th cl. (बोलयति)<BR>To sink, to dive, to plunge and again emerge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुलि|बुलिः
बुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>The vulva.<BR>E.<BR>बुल to emerge, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुष|बुषं
बुष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Chaff; also बुस.<BR>2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस|बुसं
बुस<BR>r. 4th cl. (बुस्यति)<BR>To dismiss, to loose, to quit or leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस|बुसं
बुस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Chaff.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 Dry cow-dung.<BR>4 The thick part of sour curds.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A younger sister, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>बुस to abandon, aff. क; also बुष, स being changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त|बुस्तं
बुस्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (बुस्तयति)<BR>1 To regard, to respect.<BR>2 To disregard, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त|बुस्तं
बुस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Force-meat ball.<BR>2 Fried meat.<BR>3 The inner part of the jack fruit.<BR>E.<BR>बुस्त to disrespect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बूक्क|बूक्कं
बूक्क<BR>mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्कं)<BR>The heart: also बुक्क; also with a final न्, बूक्कन्^1<BR>mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्क)<BR>also बृक्क.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृक्क|बृक्कं
बृक्क<BR>mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्कं)<BR>1 The heart.<BR>2 The kidney.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, ऋ substituted for ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बॄ
बॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (बृणाति)<BR>1 To choose or select.<BR>2 To support or nourish; also in the first sense, वॄ more usually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध|बोधः
बोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Wisdom, intellect.<BR>2 Awakening, arousing.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to understand, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधक|बोधकः
बोधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spy, an informer.<BR>2 A teacher.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to understand, causal form, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधकर|बोधकरः
बोधकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Who teaches, informs, awakes, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An awakener, a sort of minstrel who awakens the prince or chief in the morning, by music.<BR>E.<BR>वोध awakening, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधन|बोधनं|बोधनः
बोधन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>2 Teaching, informing.<BR>3 Awaking, arousing.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Burning incense.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनीय|बोधनीयः
बोधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be explained or expounded, to be rendered intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, in the causal form, aff. अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधयत्
बोधयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Informing, apprising.<BR>2 Teaching.<BR>3 Arousing, waking.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोद्धव्य
बोद्धव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be informed, taught, waked, &c.<BR>2 Requiring to be taught or explained.<BR>3 Necessary to be understood.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधि|बोधिः
बोधि<BR>mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 A branch of holy study; keeping the mind awake to the knowledge of the true GOD.<BR>2 Intellect, understanding.<BR>3 The holy fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधितरु|बोधितरुः
बोधितरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The holy fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>बोधि wisdom, and तरु the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिद्रुन
बोधिद्रुन<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>बोधि knowledge, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिसत्त्व|बोधिसत्त्वं|बोधिसत्त्वः
बोधिसत्त्व<BR>m. (-त्त्वः)<BR>A Buddha, or Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>बोधि intellect, सत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध्य
बोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>To be informed, taught, waked, &c.<BR>E.<BR>बुध to know, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्ध|बौद्धं|बौद्धः
बौद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>A Bauddha, or follower of the religion of the Buddhas.<BR>E.<BR>बुद्ध a Buddha, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौध|बौधः
बौध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A name of PURŪRAVAS, the son of BUDHA, and grandson of SOMA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>बुध MERCURY, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्युष
ब्युष<BR>r. 4th cl. (ब्युष्यति)<BR>To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रण
ब्रण<BR>r. 1st cl. (ब्रणति)<BR>To sound; व्रण more properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रतति|ब्रततिः
ब्रतति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 A creeper.<BR>2 Expansion.<BR>E.<BR>प्र before तन् to spread, aff. क्तिच्, and प changed to ब; also ब्रतति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्न|ब्रध्नः
ब्रध्न<BR>m. (-ध्नः)<BR>1 The root of a tree.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 A son.<BR>6 The body.<BR>E.<BR>बन्ध to bind, aff. नक्, and ब्रध substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मकन्यका
ब्रह्मकन्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The goddess SARASVATI.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and कन्या the daughter; being born from the head of that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=606" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मगिरि|ब्रह्मगिरिः
ब्रह्मगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and गिरि a hill; the hill of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघातक|ब्रह्मघातकः
ब्रह्मघातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The slayer of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and घातक who kills; also ब्रह्मघातिन् m. (-ती)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघ्न|ब्रह्मघ्नः
ब्रह्मघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The slayer of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचर्य्य|ब्रह्मचर्य|ब्रह्मचर्यं|ब्रह्मचर्यः|ब्रह्मचर्य्यं
ब्रह्मचर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The Brahmacarya or Brahmacārī, the religious student: see ब्रह्मचारिन्.<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>The order or condition of the religious student.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda, and चर्य्य observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचर्य्यस्खलन|ब्रह्मचर्यस्खलन
ब्रह्मचर्य्यस्खलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Incontinence.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मचर्य्य, and स्खलन deviating from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचारिन्
ब्रह्मचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The Brahmacārī or religious student; the young Brahman, from the time of his investiture with the cord, to the period of his becoming a householder: it is also applied to a person, who continues with his spiritual teacher, through life, studying the Vedas, and observing the duties of the student; it is also given as a title to Paṇḍitas learned in the Vedas; to a class of ascetics; by the Tantras, it is assigned to persons whose chief virtue is the observance of continence; and it is assumed by many religious vagabonds.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>A woman leading a life of continence.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda, and चर to go or follow, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मजन्मन्
ब्रह्मजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Second or spiritual birth, investiture.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Vedas, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मजीविन्
ब्रह्मजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>An impure Brahman, one who converts his religious duties into a trade, and performs sacrifice, teaches the Veda, &c. for hire.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् an officiating priest, and जीविन् who gets a living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मज्ञ|ब्रह्मज्ञः
ब्रह्मज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A sage, one who has spiritual wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मज्ञान|ब्रह्मज्ञानं
ब्रह्मज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spiritual wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्य|ब्रह्मण्यः
ब्रह्मण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Relating to or connected with BRAHMĀ, or a Brahman.<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>1 The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR>2 The planet SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मतत्त्व
ब्रह्मतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The true knowledge of Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मत्व|ब्रह्मत्वं
ब्रह्मत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Identification with BRAHMĀ or GOD.<BR>2 Godhead.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMA, त्व aff. of the abstract; also with तल् aff. ब्रह्मता, or with भूय added ब्रह्मभूय n. (-यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मद|ब्रह्मदः
ब्रह्मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda or holy knowledge, and द who gives; also ब्रह्मदातृ ब्रह्मदायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदण्ड|ब्रह्मदंड|ब्रह्मदण्डः
ब्रह्मदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A plant: see ब्रह्मयष्टि.<BR>2 A curse, an anathema.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदत्त|ब्रह्मदत्तः
ब्रह्मदत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>One of the sovereigns of the race of Ikṣvāku, enumerated by the Jains.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म by or to BRAHMĀ, दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदर्भा
ब्रह्मदर्भा<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and दर्भा sacrificial grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदान
ब्रह्मदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Instruction in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and दान gift; also ब्रह्मदायः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदारु|ब्रह्मदारुः
ब्रह्मदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The mulberry, (Morus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मद्विष्
ब्रह्मद्विष्<BR>mfn. (-द्विट्)<BR>Hostile to Brahmans, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and द्विष् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन्<BR>m. (-ह्या)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ, the first deity of the Hindu triad, and the operative creator of the world.<BR>2 A Brahman.<BR>3 The superintending or presiding priest at a sacrifice.<BR>4 One of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>5 One of the principal servants of the Jinas.<BR>n. (-ह्म)<BR>1 The divine cause, and essence of the world, from which all created things are supposed to emanate, and to which they return; the unknown God.<BR>2 The practice of austere devotion.<BR>3 The Vedas or scripture.<BR>4 Holy knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>वृह to increase, (mankind,) aff. मनिन् and the initial letter changed to ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मनाभ|ब्रह्मनाभः
ब्रह्मनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ, and नाभि the navel; BRAHMĀ having arisen to create the world, in a lotus, which sprang from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाण|ब्रह्मनिर्वाण|ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाणं
ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Absorption into or identification with the Supreme.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and निर्व्वाण final absorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपद
ब्रह्मपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The place or nature of spiritual being.<BR>2 The station or rank of a Brahman or of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपादप|ब्रह्मपादपः
ब्रह्मपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपुत्त्र
ब्रह्मपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A sort of poison.<BR>2 The Brahmaputra or Burampooter river.<BR>3 A place of pilgrimage, probably the source of the stream.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>1 The Sarasvatī river.<BR>2 The goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ, and पुत्त्र offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपुरी
ब्रह्मपुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The capital of BRAHMĀ on the mountain Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन्, and पुरी the city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मबन्धु|ब्रह्मबंधु|ब्रह्मबन्धुः
ब्रह्मबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>1 The epithet or appellative of a Brahman.<BR>2 A term of abuse.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूत
ब्रह्मभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become as or one with the Supreme or with spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूति|ब्रह्मभूतिः
ब्रह्मभूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Twilight.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूय|ब्रह्मभूयं
ब्रह्मभूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Identification with BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and भूय being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममय
ब्रह्ममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Consisting of or identified with spirit.<BR>2 Belonging to or fit for a Brahman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममूर्द्धभृत्
ब्रह्ममूर्द्धभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, मूर्द्धन् the forehead, and भृत् who has: having in a dispute cut off one of BRAHMĀ'S heads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयज्ञ|ब्रह्मयज्ञः
ब्रह्मयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>The study of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Veda or the Supreme Being, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयष्टि|ब्रह्मयष्टिः
ब्रह्मयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and यष्टि a stick; also with कन् added in the fem. form, ब्रह्मंयष्टिका, or with ङीप् added ब्रह्मयष्टी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयोग|ब्रह्मयोगः
ब्रह्मयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Cultivation of spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and योग addition to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयोनि|ब्रह्मयोनिः
ब्रह्मयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A particular mountain.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मराक्षस|ब्रह्मराक्षसः
ब्रह्मराक्षस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A demon or fiend of the Brahminical class.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and राक्षस a goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरात्रि|ब्रह्मरात्रिः
ब्रह्मरात्रि<BR>m. (-त्रिः)<BR>1 A name of YĀJÑAVALKYA, a saint and legislator.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, रा to give, ष्ट्रिन् aff.; conferring the knowledge of BRAHMĀ upon JANAKA in return for his bounty.<BR>2 A night of BRAHMĀ, equal to a thousand divine ages.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=607" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरीति|ब्रह्मरीतिः
ब्रह्मरीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and रीति calx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मर्षि|ब्रह्मर्षिः
ब्रह्मर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A divine saint, a Ṛṣi of a particular class, including VAŚIṢṬHA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and ऋषि a saint; the saints of this class are supposed to be of the Brahminical order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मर्षिदेश|ब्रह्मर्षिदेशः
ब्रह्मर्षिदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A part of India, including the four countries of Kuru-kṣetra, Matsya, Pañcāla, and Śūrasena or Mathurā.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मर्षि a Ṛṣi, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मलोक|ब्रह्मलोकः
ब्रह्मलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A division of the universe, the supposed eternal residence of the spirits of the pious.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवद्य|ब्रह्मवद्यं
ब्रह्मवद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Knowledge or declaration of BRAHMĀ, the knowledge of the universal permeation of one spirit, as taught by the Vedānta system of philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>BRAHMĀ or the spiritual deity, वद to speak or declare, aff. क्यप्; also with the aff. यत्, and the semivowel changed, ब्रह्मोद्य n. (-द्यं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्|ब्रह्मवर्चस्
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्<BR>n. (-र्च्चः)<BR>The power or sanctity of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and वर्च्चस् splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस|ब्रह्मवर्चस|ब्रह्मवर्च्चसं
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Holiness, resulting from the study and observance of the Vedas.<BR>2 The sanctity or superhuman power of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Vedas, and वर्च्चस् splendour, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्विन्|ब्रह्मवर्चस्विन्
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Endowed with sanctity, pure, pious.<BR>2 Having Brahmanical power or virtue.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्त्त|ब्रह्मवर्त|ब्रह्मवर्तः|ब्रह्मवर्त्तः
ब्रह्मवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A district of western India; also ब्रह्मावर्त्त.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and वृत to abide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्द्धन
ब्रह्मवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and वर्द्धन increasing, favouring; being highly proper for utensils of worship, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवाद|ब्रह्मवादः
ब्रह्मवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Citing the Vedas.<BR>2 Declaring or teaching spiritual knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म scripture. and वाद speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवादिन्
ब्रह्मवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A follower of the Vedānta system of philosophy, one who maintains all things are spirit.<BR>2 A defender or expounder of the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda or BRAHMĀ, GOD, and वादिन् who recites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविद्
ब्रह्मविद्<BR>m. (-वित् or विद्)<BR>A sage, one who knows the nature of the Supreme Spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविद्या
ब्रह्मविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Knowledge of spirit.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविन्दु|ब्रह्मविंदु|ब्रह्मविन्दुः
ब्रह्मविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>Saliva sputtered out in reading the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म scripture, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवृन्दा
ब्रह्मवृन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>The capital of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन्, and वृन्द heap, assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेद|ब्रह्मवेदः
ब्रह्मवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Knowledge of BRAHMĀ, monotheism.<BR>2 Knowledge of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and वेद knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवृक्ष|ब्रह्मवृक्षः
ब्रह्मवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>2 The glomerous fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेदि|ब्रह्मवेदिः
ब्रह्मवेदि<BR>f. (-दिः)<BR>A country: see ब्रह्मावर्त्त.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and वेदि a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेदिन्
ब्रह्मवेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Knowing or acquainted with the Vedas, with spiritual knowledge, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मशल्य|ब्रह्मशल्यः
ब्रह्मशल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa Arabica.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and शल्य a stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मशासन|ब्रह्मशासनं
ब्रह्मशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An edict or grant, &c. addressed to Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and शासन governing or an edict, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसत्र
ब्रह्मसत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Study and teaching of the Vedas.<BR>2 The constant study of them.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and सत्र sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसर्प|ब्रह्मसर्पः
ब्रह्मसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A sort of snake.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसम्भव|ब्रह्मसंभव|ब्रह्मसंभवः|ब्रह्मसम्भवः
ब्रह्मसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced from BRAHMĀ.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The second of the persons called Vāsudevas or Kṛṣṇas by the Jains.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and सम्भव offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसायुज्य|ब्रह्मसायुज्यं
ब्रह्मसायुज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Identification with BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and सायुज्य intimate union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसार्ष्टिता
ब्रह्मसार्ष्टिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Equality with BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and सार्ष्टिता sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसुवर्च्चला|ब्रह्मसुवर्चला
ब्रह्मसुवर्च्चला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, an infusion of which is to be drank in expiation of having any thing touched by a dog, cat, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and सुवर्च्चला linseed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसू
ब्रह्मसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>1 ANIRUDDHA, the son of KĀMA.<BR>2 KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and सू the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूत्र|ब्रह्मसूत्रं
ब्रह्मसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The sacrificial or Brahmanical thread.<BR>2 An aphorism of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूनु|ब्रह्मसूनुः
ब्रह्मसूनु<BR>m. (नुः)<BR>A sovereign, according to the Jains, of the race of Ikṣvāku.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and सूनु son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्वरूप
ब्रह्मस्वरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Of the nature of spirit, of the same essence as the Godhead.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and स्वरूप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महत्या
ब्रह्महत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 Brahmanicide, killing a Brahman.<BR>2 Any crime equally heinous.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महन्
ब्रह्महन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>The murderer or slayer of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन्, and हन who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महुत|ब्रह्महुतं
ब्रह्महुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The performance of hospitality, &c., that one of the great sacraments which consists in the veneration of mankind.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, हुत worshipped; being the most worthy of respect, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माक्षर
ब्रह्माक्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sacred and mysterious name of the deity.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म GOD, अक्षर a letter, the Oṃkāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माग्रभू
ब्रह्माग्रभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माञ्जलि|ब्रह्मांजलि|ब्रह्माञ्जलिः
ब्रह्माञ्जलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 Joining both hands together, whilst reading the Vedas, either as an act of humility or to mark the accentuation of the Sāma Veda.<BR>2 Paying obeisance to the spiritual preceptor at the beginning or end of a lecture.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Vedas, and अञ्जलि the hands joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माणी
ब्रह्माणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The female energy of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माण्ड|ब्रह्मांड|ब्रह्माण्डं
ब्रह्माण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The globe, the world.<BR>2 One of the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and अण्ड an egg, to which it is compared; in creation there are said to have been innumerable Brahmāṇḍas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माधिगमन
ब्रह्माधिगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Perusal of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and अधिगमन going through; also ब्रह्मधिगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माधिगामिक
ब्रह्माधिगामिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or contributing to a course of sacred study.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्माधिगम, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माभ्यास|ब्रह्माभ्यासः
ब्रह्माभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Study or repetition of scripture.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्न, and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माम्भस्|ब्रह्मांभस्
ब्रह्माम्भस्<BR>n. (-म्भः)<BR>Cow's urine.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् a Brahman, and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मारण्य|ब्रह्मारण्यं
ब्रह्मारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A place where the Vedas are read and explained.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda, and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=608" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मावर्त्त|ब्रह्मावर्त|ब्रह्मावर्तः|ब्रह्मावर्त्तः
ब्रह्मावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तं)<BR>The country to the north-west of Dehli, lying between the rivers Sarasvatī, and Dṛṣadvatī.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brahman, and आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मासन|ब्रह्मासनं
ब्रह्मासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A posture suited to devout and religious meditation.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मास्व
ब्रह्मास्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>1 The BRAHMĀ weapon, a fabulous weapon originally from BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The imprecation of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and अस्व a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माहुति|ब्रह्माहुतिः
ब्रह्माहुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An oblation of ghee.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda, and आहुति an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मी
ब्रह्मी<BR>f. (-ह्मी)<BR>1 A sort of fish, commonly Pancal, (Macrognathus Pancalus, HAM.)<BR>2 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वृह to grow or increase, affs. मनिन and ङीप्^1; also ब्रह्मी.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोज्झता
ब्रह्मोज्झता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Neglecting or forgetting the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and उज्झता abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोद्य|ब्रह्मोद्यं
ब्रह्मोद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Reciting or explaining the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and वद to speak, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मौदन|ब्रह्मौदनं|ब्रह्मौदनः
ब्रह्मौदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Boiled rice distributed to priests at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् a Brahman, and ओदन boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म<BR>mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मी-ह्मं)<BR>Relating or belonging to BRAHMĀ, the Vedas, &c.<BR>n. (-ह्मं)<BR>1 The part of the hand under the root of the thumb.<BR>2 A mode of marriage, the presentation of the bride elegantly adorned, by the father, to the bridegroom whom he has invited.<BR>m. (-ह्मः)<BR>NĀRADA the sage, and son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-ह्मी)<BR>1 One of the eight divine mothers of created beings, or the personified energies of the gods; the Śakti or energy of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The goddess of speech SARASVATĪ.<BR>3 The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>4 A sort of potherb, (Ruta graveolens.)<BR>5 A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>6 A sort of fish.<BR>7 The asterism Rohiṇī.<BR>8 A she frog.<BR>9 A yellow coloured ant.<BR>10 The wife of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A man of the first Hindu tribe, a Brahman.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 An assemblage of Brahmans, a council, a conclave.<BR>2 A portion of the Vedas, that which comprises the precepts that inculcate religious duties, the maxims which explain those precepts, and the arguments which relate to theology; it is, however, now often blended with other portions.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The wife of a Brahman, or a woman of the Brahmanical tribe.<BR>2 A wasp.<BR>3 A small ant.<BR>4 A potherb, (Ruta graveolens.)<BR>5 A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>6 A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् the Veda, &c. अण् aff., and the final syllable of the original word retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणचाण्डाल|ब्राह्मणचांडाल|ब्राह्मणचाण्डालः
ब्राह्मणचाण्डाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An outcaste Brahman, one who is attended by a wife of another caste, or the son of a Śūdra by a Brahman female.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and चाण्डाल an outcaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजाति|ब्राह्मणजातिः
ब्राह्मणजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The Brahmanical tribe or caste.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and जाति tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजातीय
ब्राह्मणजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to the Brahmanical race.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and जातीय generic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजीविका
ब्राह्मणजीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The occupation or subsistence of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणता
ब्राह्मणता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Brahmanhood.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, ब्राह्मणत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणबध
ब्राह्मणबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Brahmanicide.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणब्रुव|ब्राह्मणब्रुवः
ब्राह्मणब्रुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Brahman by birth but not by attention to his duties; one who subsists by avocations properly limited to the other tribes.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण a Brahman, and ब्रुव who speaks, who calls himself (improperly) a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणयष्टिका
ब्राह्मणयष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण a Brahman, and यष्टि a staff, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणसंस्थ
ब्राह्मणसंस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Belonging to or abiding with a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and संस्थ what stays with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणहित|ब्राह्मणहितः
ब्राह्मणहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suitable to or fit for a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणातिक्रम|ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः
ब्राह्मणातिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Disregarding or disrespecting Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and अतिक्रम going over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणात्मक
ब्राह्मणात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Belonging to, one or with or containing Brahmans, the Brāhmaṇa section of the Vedas, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and आत्मक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणादर्शन
ब्राह्मणादर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Absence of Brahmanical instruction or guidance.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and अदर्शन not showing or teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति|ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तिः
ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>The protection or preservation of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and अभ्युपपत्ति defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणायन|ब्राह्मणायनः
ब्राह्मणायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Brahman, sprung from learned and holy progenitors.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण, and फञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणीगामिन्
ब्राह्मणीगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>The gallant of a woman of the Brahmanical tribe, or the wife of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मणी a female Brahman, and गामिन् who goes to or with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्य|ब्राह्मण्यः
ब्राह्मण्य<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>The planet SATURN.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 An assembly of Brahmans.<BR>2 The state, quality, or business of a Brahman, Brahmanhood.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्मन्, and यञ् aff., or बाह्मण, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मदेया
ब्राह्मदेया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A girl to be wedded by the Brāhma form.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्म, and देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मपिङ्गा
ब्राह्मपिङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>Silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्माहोरात्र|ब्राह्माहोरात्रः
ब्राह्माहोरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A day and night of BRAHMĀ, a period of two thousand ages of the gods or two Kalpas of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मण relating to BRAHMĀ, अहन् a day, and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मिका
ब्राह्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मी, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मीपुत्त्र
ब्राह्मीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>The son of a woman married according to the Brāhma form.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्मी, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्य|ब्राह्म्यं
ब्राह्म्य<BR>n. (-ह्म्यं)<BR>1 The worship or veneration of Brahmans, considered as one of the great sacraments.<BR>2 Astonishment.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रह्म, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्यहुत
ब्राह्म्यहुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Respect shown to guests, especially to Brahmans, hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>ब्राह्म्य, and हुत sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रुवत्
ब्रुवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वती-वत्)<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रू to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रुवाण|ब्रुवाणः
ब्रुवाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Speaking, telling, saying.<BR>E.<BR>ब्रू to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रू
ब्रू<BR>(ञ) ब्रूञ् r. 2nd cl. (ब्रवीति or आह)<BR>To speak or tell: आह is optionally substituted for this root before the first five inflections of the present tense, and वच in several other tenses<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ<BR>The twenty-fourth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, and aspirate of the last letter, or Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=609" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ<BR>n. (भं)<BR>1 A star.<BR>2 An asterism.<BR>3 A planet.<BR>m. (भः)<BR>1 A name of ŚUKRA, regent of the planet VENUS.<BR>2 A bee.<BR>3 Error, delusion.<BR>f. (भा)<BR>1 Light, lustre, splendor.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>f. (भी)<BR>Fear.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, or भी to fear, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्किका
भक्किका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्त|भक्तं|भक्तः
भक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Attached or attentive to, devoted to, engrossed by.<BR>2 Served, worshipped.<BR>3 Dressed, cooked.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 Boiled rice.<BR>2 Food.<BR>3 Any edible grain boiled with water.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A follower, a votary.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकर|भक्तकरः
भक्तकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Factitious incense, incense prepared from various fragrant resins and perfumes.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त dressed, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकार|भक्तकारः
भक्तकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cook.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त boiled rice, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तछन्द|भक्तच्छन्द|भक्तच्छंद
भक्तछन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>Appetite, wish for food.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त, and छन्द will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तजा
भक्तजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तता
भक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Devotedness, implied faith in and attachment to.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, भक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ततूर्य्य|भक्ततूर्य|भक्ततूर्य्यं
भक्ततूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Music played at the hour of eating, amongst princes and great men.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त rice or food, and तूर्य्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तद
भक्तद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A supporter, a maintainer.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त, and द who gives; also भक्तदायक, भक्तदायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदातृ
भक्तदातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A maintainer, a feeder.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त food, and दातृ donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदास|भक्तदासः
भक्तदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A slave, one maintained in consideration of service.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त food, दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ति|भक्तिः
भक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Service, worship.<BR>2 Faith, belief.<BR>3 Devotion or attachment to.<BR>4 Part, portion.<BR>5 Fracture, division.<BR>6 Metonymy.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, or भञ्ज to break, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिमत्|भक्तिमन्त्
भक्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-भान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Faithful, devoted to.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तियोग|भक्तियोगः
भक्तियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Devotion or worship, as shewn by implicit faith in any divinity.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ति, and योग devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिल|भक्तिलः
भक्तिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A good horse.<BR>2 A follower, a votary.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ति service, &c. ला to afford, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष|भक्षः
भक्ष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भक्षति भक्षयति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षक|भक्षकः
भक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Gluttonous, voracious, gourmand.<BR>2 A feeder, an eater, who or what eats.<BR>f. (-क्षिका)<BR>A meal, a feed.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षकार|भक्षकारः
भक्षकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A confectioner, a pastry cook.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष food, and कार who prepares; also भक्षङ्कार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षण|भक्षणं
भक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षणीय|भक्षणीयं
भक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Eatable, to be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष, and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षमाण
भक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षयत्
भक्षयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षित|भक्षितं
भक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षितव्य
भक्षितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be eaten, what may be eaten<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, तव्य aff.; also भक्षयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्य|भक्ष्यं
भक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>Eatable. n (-क्ष्यं) Food.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यकार|भक्ष्यकारः
भक्ष्यकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A baker.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष्य eatable, and कार who makes or prepares; also भक्ष्यंकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यमाण
भक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>To be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>भक्ष to eat, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग|भगं|भगः
भग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>1 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>2 Fortune, prosperity.<BR>3 Beauty, splendor.<BR>4 Excellence, greatness.<BR>5 Desire, wish, love.<BR>6 Strength, vigour.<BR>7 Effort, exertion.<BR>8 Fame, glory.<BR>9 Knowledge..<BR>10 Absence of passion, the tranquillity of the religious man, who has divested himself of worldly excitability.<BR>11 Omnipotence, supreme or divine power.<BR>12 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>13 Final emancipation.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 One of the twelve suns or Ādityas.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 A form of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, &c. ग aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदेवता
भगदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Hymeneal divinity.<BR>E.<BR>भग, and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगन्दर|भगंदर|भगंदरः|भगन्दरः
भगन्दर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fistula in ano.<BR>E.<BR>भग the vulva, दृ to divide, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवत्|भगवन्त्
भगवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Respectable, worshipful, adorable, and hence the common appellative of a prince or deity.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>One of the generic titles of a Jina or Jaina deified sage.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 A name of GAURĪ.<BR>2 Any goddess.<BR>E.<BR>भग fortune, supremacy, &c. and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाङ्कुर|भगांकुर|भगाङ्कुरः
भगाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The clitoris.<BR>E.<BR>भग, and अङ्कुर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाल|भगालं
भगाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The human skull.<BR>E.<BR>भग ŚIVA, अल to adorn, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगालिन्
भगालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भगाल a skull, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनी
भगिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A sister.<BR>2 A woman in general.<BR>E.<BR>भग prosperity, desire, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथ|भगीरथः
भगीरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A king whose austerities brought GAṄGĀ, the river, from heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोस्
भगोस्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle used as a respectful term of address.<BR>E.<BR>भगवत् reverend, and ओस् irregularly substituted for the three final letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्न|भग्नं
भग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Torn, broken.<BR>2 Overcome, defeated.<BR>3 Disregarded, despised.<BR>4 Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नजानु
भग्नजानु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु)<BR>Having a broken leg.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न, and जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपृष्ठ|भग्नपृष्ठः
भग्नपृष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Confronting, encountering, coming before or in front of.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न disregarded, and पृष्ठ the back; heedless of what is behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नप्रक्रम
भग्नप्रक्रम<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Disorder, confusion<BR>2 Want of method or arrangement in composition.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न, and प्रक्रम proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नसन्धिक|भग्नसंधिक|भग्नसन्धिकं
भग्नसन्धिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Butter-milk.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न broken, सन्धि union, and कप् aff., divided by churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नात्मन्
भग्नात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न broken, and आत्मन् the body; having been cut in two by the trident of ŚIVA, as a punishment for having violated the wife of VṚHASPATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नाश|भग्नाशः
भग्नाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न, and आशा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नी
भग्नी<BR>f. (-ग्नी)<BR>A sister.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to share, aff. क्त, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नोद्यम
भग्नोद्यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Labouring in vain.<BR>E.<BR>भग्न, and उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्कारी|भंकारी
भङ्कारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्क्तृ
भङ्क्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्त)<BR>Breaking, a breaker, who or what breaks.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, तृप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=610" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग|भंग|भंगः|भङ्गः
भङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Breaking, splitting.<BR>2 A chasm, a fissure, a division.<BR>3 Defeat, discomfiture.<BR>4 Disappointment.<BR>5 Fear.<BR>6 Dishonesty, fraud, circumvention, cheating.<BR>7 Going, motion.<BR>8 A wave.<BR>9 A water-course, a canal.<BR>10 Disease in general.<BR>11 A disease, (hemiplegia, palsy.)<BR>12 Interruption of the voice.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Teori.<BR>3 A fibrous plant from which a sort of flax is obtained, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गभाज्
भङ्गभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Breaking, being broken.<BR>E.<BR>भङ्ग, and भाज् partaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गवासा|भंगवासा
भङ्गवासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Turmerick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गसार्थ|भंगसार्थ|भङ्गसार्थः
भङ्गसार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Crafty, fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>भङ्ग breaking, fraud, &c. स for सम् with, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गान|भङ्गानः
भङ्गान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Cyprinus Banggana, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>भङ्ग a wave, अन to live, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गारी|भंगारी
भङ्गारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गि|भंगि|भंगिः|भङ्गिः
भङ्गि<BR>f. (-ङ्गिः-ङ्गी)<BR>1 Fracture, division, separation.<BR>2 Fraud, deception, trick, disguise.<BR>3 Irony.<BR>4 Wit, repartee.<BR>5 A wave.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, aff. इन् and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गील|भंगील
भङ्गील<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Defect in the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुर|भंगुर|भङ्गुरः
भङ्गुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Crooked, bent.<BR>2 Fraudulent, crafty, dishonest.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The bend or elbow of a river.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, aff. घुरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग्य|भंग्यं|भङ्ग्यं
भङ्ग्य<BR>n. (-ङ्ग्यं)<BR>A field of hemp.<BR>E.<BR>भङ्गा hemp, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भज
भज<BR>r. 1st cl. (औ) भजौ (भजति)<BR>1 To serve, to worship.<BR>2 To possess, to enjoy, (carnally.)<BR>r. 10th cl. (भजयति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To dress or cook.<BR>3 To separate or divide: see भाज.<BR>(इ) भजि r. 10th. cl. (भंजयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak:<BR>with वि prefixed,<BR>to measure;<BR>with प्र and वि,<BR>to discriminate, to discuss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजत्
भजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>1 Serving, waiting upon.<BR>2 Enjoying carnally.<BR>3 Dividing, sharing.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजन|भजनं
भजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Service, adoration.<BR>2 Possessing or enjoying carnally.<BR>3 Sharing.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sound of the conch.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजमान|भजमानः
भजमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Serving, waiting.<BR>2 Enjoying, possessing, (carnally.)<BR>3 Dividing, sharing.<BR>4 Right, fit, proper.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve, &c., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्ज
भञ्ज<BR>(ओ, औ) ओभञ्जौ r. 7th cl. (भनक्ति)<BR>To break, to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जक|भंजक|भञ्जकः
भञ्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what breaks, severs, divides, destroys, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जत्
भञ्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्)<BR>Breaking, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जन|भंजन|भञ्जनं|भञ्जनः
भञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breaking, destroying.<BR>2 Afflicting.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जनक|भंजनक|भंजनकः|भञ्जनकः
भञ्जनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A disease of the mouth, contortion of the lips, and decay of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्जन, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जरु|भंजरु|भंजरुः|भञ्जरुः
भञ्जरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tree growing near a temple.<BR>E.<BR>भञ्ज to break, अरुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट|भटः
भट<BR>r. 1st cl. (भटति)<BR>1 To hold or cherish.<BR>2 To hire or maintain.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>(इ) भटि r. 10th cl. (भंटयति)<BR>To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट|भटः
भट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A warrior, a soldier, a combatant.<BR>2 A barbarian, or outcast of a particular tribe.<BR>3 A goblin.<BR>E.<BR>भट to maintain, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटित्र|भटित्रं
भटित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Roasted on a spit, (meat, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>भट to nourish, इत्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्ट|भट्टः
भट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 A philosopher, a learned man, especially one conversant with the philosophical systems.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>3 Best, excellent.<BR>4 Authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टार|भट्टारः
भट्टार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Worshipful, reverend, entitled to homage or respect: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारक|भट्टारकः
भट्टारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Venerable, respectable, entitled to reverence or to homage.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sage, a Muni or saint.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>3 (In theatrical language) A king.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>5 A term especially applied to a Bauddha teacher.<BR>E.<BR>भट to nourish, aff. क्विप्, तृ to pass, aff. ण्वुल्, त changed to ट; otherwise with टल to be confused, the same aff., and ल changed to ष; a cherisher and punisher, a distributor of rewards and punishments; again, भट्ट said here to mean, authority, ऋ to go to or obtain, अण् aff., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारकवार|भट्टारकवारः
भट्टारकवार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Sunday.<BR>E.<BR>भट्टारक, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टिनी
भट्टिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A queen, who has been consecrated as well as her husband; (a theatrical term.)<BR>2 The wife of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>भट्ट authority: see etymology of the last word, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भड|भडः
भड<BR>(इ) भडि r. 1st cl. (भण्डते)<BR>1 To rally, to deride or treat with merriment.<BR>2 To jest, to joke.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>4 To upbraid, to reprove.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भण्डति भण्डयति)<BR>To do an auspicious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भडिल|भडिलः
भडिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A servant.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>E.<BR>भड a Sautra root, to be happy, Uṇādi aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण
भण<BR>r. 1st cl. (भणति)<BR>To sound, to utter articulate sound, to speak or say.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>to reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणित|भणितं
भणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, spoken, uttered.<BR>E.<BR>भण to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणिति|भणितिः
भणिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Speech, speaking.<BR>E.<BR>भण to speak, aff. क्तिन्, with the augment इट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्टाकी
भण्टाकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>भट to nourish, aff. आक, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ड|भंड|भंडः|भण्डः
भण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A mime, a jester, a buffoon, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>भडि to deride, &c. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डक|भंडक|भंडकः|भण्डकः
भण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डन|भंडन|भंडनं|भण्डनं
भण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Armour, mail.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 Evil, wickedness, mischief.<BR>E.<BR>भडि to blame, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डहासिनी|भंडहासिनी
भण्डहासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>भण्ड a jester, and हासिनी who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डि|भंडि|भंडिः|भण्डिः
भण्डि<BR>f. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी)<BR>1 A plant, from the wood of which a red dye is prepared; Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith, Rox.)<BR>2 A wave.<BR>E.<BR>भडि to be auspicious, &c. aff. इन्; also with कन् added भण्डिका, also भण्डिरी and भण्डीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिर|भण्डिरः
भण्डिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Madder.<BR>E.<BR>see भण्डिल, भण्डीरी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिल|भंडिल|भण्डिलः
भण्डिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 A messenger, one sent or dispatched.<BR>2 Fortunate, happy, prosperous, auspicious.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa sirisha).<BR>E.<BR>भडि to be happy, &c. Uṇādi aff. इलच्; also र being substituted for ल, भण्डिर, or the short vowel being lengthened, भण्डील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डीरी
भण्डीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The Bengal madder tree: see भण्डि.<BR>E.<BR>भडि to be auspicious, ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=611" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डील|भण्डीलः
भण्डील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Sirisha tree: see भण्डिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डूक|भण्डूकः
भण्डूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>भडि to be auspicious, ऊकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद
भद<BR>(इ) भदि r. 1st and 10th cls. (भन्दति-ते भन्दयति)<BR>1 To do an auspicious act.<BR>2 To be happy, well, prosperous, &c.<BR>3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदन्त|भदंत|भदंतः|भदन्तः
भदन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>1 Reverend, venerable, worshipped or adored.<BR>2 Brilliant, splendid.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A Saugata, a Bauddha, a heterodox or sceptical philosopher.<BR>2 A devotee, an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>भदि to be happy or pleased, to shine, Uṇādi aff. झच्, and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदाक|भदाकः
भदाक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Prosperous, fortunate, auspicious.<BR>E.<BR>भदि to be happy, Uṇādi aff. आकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्र|भद्रं|भद्रः
भद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Happy, prosperous, lucky, propitious.<BR>2 Best, excellent.<BR>3 Pure, pious, virtuous.<BR>n. subst. (-द्रं)<BR>Prosperity, fortune, happiness.<BR>(adv.)<BR>Happy, well, right.<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 Iron or steel.<BR>nf. (-द्रं-द्री)<BR>One of the astrological periods called Karaṇas, the seventh; also called Viṣṭī, regarded as an unlucky period.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A wagtail.<BR>3 A bull.<BR>4 A heap, a multitude.<BR>5 A description of elephant, one of four classes into which they are divided.<BR>6 Mount Meru.<BR>7 One of the nine persons termed Śuklabalas by the Jainas.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>2 The ichneumon plant: see रास्ना.<BR>3 Indigo.<BR>4 Asclepias pseudosarsa.<BR>5 A shrub, (Pœderia foetida.)<BR>6 A medicinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>7 A name of the second, seventh, and twelfth days of the lunar fortnight.<BR>8 A female Śakti or deity of the Jainas.<BR>9 One of the four divisions of the Ganges, according to the Purāṇas, that which flows to the northern Kuru.<BR>10 A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>11 A cow.<BR>12 Turmerick.<BR>E.<BR>भदि to be happy, Uṇādi aff. रन् and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रक|भद्रकं|भद्रकः
भद्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>2 Respectable, worthy, estimable.<BR>3 Lucky, fortunate.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकाली
भद्रकाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 One of the forms of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus pertenuis or rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र ŚIVA, क्ल to approximate, aff. घञ and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकुम्भ|भद्रकुंभ|भद्रकुम्भः
भद्रकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A golden jar filled with water from a holy place, or with the water of the Ganges, and used especially at the consecration of a king.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and कुम्भ a water jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रगन्धिका
भद्रगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A creeping plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa, the narrow-leaved variety.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and गन्ध smell, aff. कन् and टाप्; some copies read भद्रवल्लिका in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रङ्कर|भद्रंकर|भद्रङ्करः
भद्रङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness or prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र happy, and कृ to make, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रचूड|भद्रचूडः
भद्रचूड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A sort of Euphorbia, (E. tirucalli.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र propitious, and चूडा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रदारु
भद्रदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रदार्व्वादिक
भद्रदार्व्वादिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A class of thirty-nine medicinal plants, and substances.<BR>E.<BR>भद्रदारु the pine, आदि etcetera, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रनामन्
भद्रनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The woodpecker.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and नामन a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपदा
भद्रपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A name given to the 26th and 27th lunar asterisms: see भाद्रपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपर्णा
भद्रपर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A shrub, (Pœderia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, पर्ण a leaf, and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपर्णी
भद्रपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र lucky, पर्ण a leaf, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रबलन|भद्रबलनः
भद्रबलन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र conferring happiness, and बल to be strong, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रबला
भद्रबला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A shrub, (Poederia foetida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमल्लिका
भद्रमल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुस्तक|भद्रमुस्तकः
भद्रमुस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र lucky, and मुस्तक Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रयव|भद्रयवः
भद्रयव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The seed of the Echites or Wrightea antidysenterica.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र lucky, and यव seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्ररेणु|भद्ररेणुः
भद्ररेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवती
भद्रवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवर्म्मन्|भद्रवर्मन्
भद्रवर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>Double jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवल्ली
भद्रवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>2 The large Bengal creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र lucky, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्रय|भद्रश्रयं
भद्रश्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, श्रय for आश्रय asylum, place of growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्री
भद्रश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र best, श्री excellence or beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रसोमा
भद्रसोमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A name of GAṄGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र ŚIVA, स with or equal to, उमा the wife of ŚIVA; equally dear with UMĀ to that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राकरण|भद्राकरणं
भद्राकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Shaving.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, with डाच् aff., and कृ to do, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रात्मज|भद्रात्मजः
भद्रात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sword, a scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र iron, and आत्मज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रारक|भद्रारकः
भद्रारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One of the eighteen minor Dvīpas, or divisions of the world.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र prosperity, ऋ to go to, or attain, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रालपत्रिका
भद्रालपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shrub, (Poederia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, अल what is equal to, and पत्र a leaf, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राली
भद्राली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A shrub, (Poederia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>भद्रा the same plant, ला to go or be, aff. ड and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राश्व|भद्राश्वं|भद्राश्वः
भद्राश्व<BR>n. (-श्वं)<BR>One of the four Mahā Dvīpas, into which the known world is divided, according to some systems; or according to another system, one of the nine Khāṇḍas, or smaller divisions of the continent; in either case it is the east division.<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>One of the nine sons of AGNĪDHRA, to whom the division of the earth called Bhadrāśva was assigned, and from whom it was so named.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राश्रय|भद्राश्रयः
भद्राश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, and आश्रय abode, habitat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रासन|भद्रासनं
भद्रासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A throne.<BR>2 A peculiar posture, in which abstract meditation is performed by the devotee; the legs bent, and crossed underneath, and turned so as to bring the ancles in contact with the perineum, whilst the soles of the feet are [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">Page613</a>] held close to the sides.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious or beautiful, and आसन a seat or sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=612" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रोदनी
भद्रोदनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दिल|भंदिल|भंदिलं|भन्दिलं
भन्दिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Good, happiness, welfare, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>भदि to be auspicious, Uṇādi aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भपति|भपतिः
भपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>भ a star, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भ|भंभ|भंभः|भम्भः
भम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Smoke.<BR>2 A fly.<BR>E.<BR>भम् imitative sound, भा to emit sound, to shine, &c., and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भरालिका|भंभरालिका
भम्भरालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A gnat, a musquito.<BR>E.<BR>भम्भराली a fly, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भराली|भंभराली
भम्भराली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A fly, especially of a large sort.<BR>E.<BR>भम् imitative sound, repeated, रा to make, and लच् aff.; making a buzzing noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भासार|भम्भासारः
भम्भासार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sovereign of Magadha; also ŚREṆIKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भय|भयं|भयः
भय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Frightful, fearful, horrible, dreadful.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Fear, alarm, fright, dread.<BR>2 The flower of the Trapa bispinosa.<BR>E.<BR>भी to be afraid, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयकारक
भयकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Terrifying, frightening.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and कारक what causes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयङ्कर|भयंकर|भयङ्करं|भयंकरः
भयङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Fearful, formidable, frightful.<BR>E.<BR>भय fear, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद
भयद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Fearful, terrifying.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयदर्शिन्
भयदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Fearful, frightful.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and दर्शिन् appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयदाय
भयदाय<BR>m. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Terrific.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and दाय what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद्रुत|भयद्रुतः
भयद्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Routed, put to flight.<BR>E.<BR>भय fear, द्रुत flown, fled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रतीकार|भयप्रतीकारः
भयप्रतीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Removal of fear.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and प्रतीकार counteraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रद
भयप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Causing or inspiring fear.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and प्रद who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रस्ताव|भयप्रस्तावः
भयप्रस्ताव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Season or occasion of alarm.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and प्रस्ताव occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयभ्रष्ट|भयभ्रष्टः
भयभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Put to flight.<BR>E.<BR>भय fear, भ्रष्ट fallen, gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविधायिन्
भयविधायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Alarming, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and विधायिन् causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविप्लुत
भयविप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Panick-struck.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and विप्लुत immersed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयसंहृष्टरोमन्
भयसंहृष्टरोमन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Horrified.<BR>E.<BR>भय, संहृष्टरोमन् having the hair erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयस्थान
भयस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Seat or part exposed to peril or hurt.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहेतु|भयहेतुः
भयहेतु<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>Cause of alarm.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयातुर
भयातुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Afraid.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and आतुर affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयार्त्त|भयार्त
भयार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Frightened, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and आर्त्त afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानक|भयानकः
भयानक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Frightful, formidable, terrific.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Terror.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 RĀHU the personified ascending node.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>3 The Rasa or sentiment of terror, as excited by poetical or dramatic composition.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, आनक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयापह|भयापहः
भयापह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भय fear, अप before हा to quit, to oppose or remove from, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयावह|भयावहः
भयावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Formidable, fearful.<BR>E.<BR>भय fear, वह to bear, aff. अच्, and आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयैकप्रवण
भयैकप्रवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Engrossed by fear.<BR>E.<BR>भय, एक alone, प्रवण bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयोत्तर
भयोत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Attended with or succeeded by fear.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and उत्तर subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयोपशम
भयोपशम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Encouraging, allaying fear.<BR>E.<BR>भय, and उपशम tranquillising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर|भरः
भर<BR>adv. m. (-रः)<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>noun.<BR>2 A measure of value, two thousand Palas.<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं)<BR>Who or what cherishes, upholds, supports, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to cherish, अप् aff., or with घञ् aff. भार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरट|भरटः
भरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A potter.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to cherish, Uṇādi aff. अटन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण|भरणं|भरणः
भरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Cherishing, maintaining, nourishing, supporting.<BR>2 Wages, hire.<BR>3 The constellation Bharaṇī.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The name of the second lunar asterism, containing three stars, (Musca,) and figured by the pudendum muliebre.<BR>2 A creeper, commonly Ghosha.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीभू
भरणीभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The personified ascending node or Rāhu.<BR>E.<BR>भरणी the asterism personified as a nymph, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीय|भरणीयः
भरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be cherished or maintained, a dependant.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः|भरण्डः
भरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A master, an owner, a lord, a husband.<BR>2 A sovereign, a king.<BR>3 A king.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. अण्डन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्य|भरण्यं
भरण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>To be cherished or protected.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 Cherishing, maintaining.<BR>3 The asterism Bharaṇī.<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>भरण maintaining, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यभुज्
भरण्यभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>A labourer, a hireling, one who works for hire.<BR>E.<BR>भरण्य wages or hire, भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्याह्वा
भरण्याह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A plant, commonly Rāmadūtī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यु|भरण्युः
भरण्यु<BR>m. (-ण्युः)<BR>1 A master, a protector.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, अन्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत्|भरन्त्
भरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Upholding, supporting, having, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to cherish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत|भरतः
भरत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>2 The son of DUṢYANTA by ŚAKUNTALĀ.<BR>3 The name of a sage or Muni,<BR>4 The name of a celebrated writer on dramatic composition, of which he is also sometimes considered as the inventor; the term is also applied to his work, which appears to have been a body of Sūtras, or rules, relating to every branch of theatrical writing and exhibition; it is said to be lost, but is constantly quoted by the commentators on the Nāṭakas, or Indian dramas.<BR>5 An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR>6 A barbarian, a mountaineer, a savage.<BR>7 A weaver.<BR>8 A descendant of BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, अतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतपुत्त्रक
भरतपुत्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An actor, a mime.<BR>E.<BR>भरत the dramatic author, पुत्त्र a son, and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतप्रसू
भरतप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A name of KAIKEYĪ, wife of DAŚARATHA, and mother of BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>भरत as above, and प्रसू parent; hence equally applicable to ŚAKUNTALĀ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=613" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतवर्ष|भरतवर्षः
भरतवर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>India.<BR>E.<BR>भरत the son of DUṢYANTA, and वर्ष region; he is supposed to have been the first emperor or monarch of all India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरताग्रज|भरताग्रजः
भरताग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भरत, and अग्रज elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरथ|भरथः
भरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A sovereign, a king.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. अथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाज|भरद्वाजः
भरद्वाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A skylark.<BR>2 The name of a Muni.<BR>3 The son of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>भरत् upholding, and वाज a wing; also भारद्वाज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाजक|भरद्वाजकः
भरद्वाजक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A lark.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
भरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or ती-तं)<BR>1 Green, of a green colour.<BR>2 Nourished.<BR>3 Filled.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिमन्
भरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. इमनिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरु|भरुः
भरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>4 A husband, a lord.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुज|भरुजः
भरुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A small sort of Shakal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुटक|भरुटकं
भरुटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग|भर्गः
भर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>4 Cooking, frying.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, aff. घञ्; having scorched KĀMADEVA to ashes, with a look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ज्जन|भर्जन|भर्जनं
भर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Frying.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तव्य|भर्तव्य|भर्त्तव्यं
भर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cherished or maintained.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृ|भर्तृ
भर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>1 A cherisher, a nourisher, a protector.<BR>2 A holder, a supporter.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>1 A husband.<BR>2 A lord, a master.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, &c. aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृघ्नी|भर्तृघ्नी
भर्त्तृघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>The murderess of her husband.<BR>E.<BR>भर्त्तृ a husband, हन to kill, aff. ङीष्, and घ्न substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृता|भर्तृता
भर्त्तृता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Masterhood.<BR>2 Husbandship.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, भर्त्तृत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृताङ्गत|भर्तृताङ्गत
भर्त्तृताङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subject, married.<BR>E.<BR>भर्त्तृता 2nd case, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृदारक|भर्तृदारक|भर्तृदारकः|भर्त्तृदारकः
भर्त्तृदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A young prince, designated as successor, and associated to the empire, (in theatrical language.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>(In theatrical language,) A princess.<BR>E.<BR>भर्त्तृ the master or monarch, and दारक the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृहरि|भर्तृहरि|भर्तृहरिः|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्त्तृहरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The brother of VIKRAMĀDITYA, A prince and poet.<BR>E.<BR>भर्त्तृ a prince, and हरि VIṢṆU, a deity amongst kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्रिम
भर्त्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Maintained, nourished, supported.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, क्ति aff. and मप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स
भर्त्स<BR>r. 10th cl. (भर्त्सयति-ते)<BR>To reprove, to reproach, to abuse or menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सन|भर्त्सनं
भर्त्सन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Threat, menace.<BR>2 Reproach, abuse, cursing, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>भर्त्स to abuse, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्भ
भर्भ<BR>r. 1st cl. (भर्भति)<BR>To injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्म|भर्म|भर्मं|भर्म्मं
भर्म्म<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Hire, wages.<BR>3 The navel.<BR>4 A particular coin.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. मन्, whence it is properly भर्म्भन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्मण्या|भर्मण्या
भर्म्मण्या<BR>f. (-ण्या)<BR>Wages, hire.<BR>E.<BR>भर्म्भन् hire, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्मन्|भर्मन्
भर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 The navel.<BR>4 A coin, a piece of money.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्व|भर्व्व
भर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (भर्वति)<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल
भल<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भलते भलयते)<BR>To describe, to expound, to explain.<BR>r. 1st cl.<BR>1 To hurt, to injure.<BR>2 To give.<BR>r. 10th cl.<BR>To throw up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलता
भलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A shrub, (Poederia foetida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (भल्लते)<BR>1 To tell, to describe.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>3 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A bear.<BR>mn. (-ल्लः-ल्लं)<BR>A kind of arrow.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>1 An arrow, with a crescent-shaped head.<BR>2 The marking nut plant; also भल्लातकी.<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल to hurt or kill, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लक|भल्लकः
भल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लपुच्छी
भल्लपुच्छी<BR>f. (-च्छी)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल a bear, पुच्छ a tail; to which the flower is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लात|भल्लातः
भल्लात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Marking nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातक|भल्लातकः
भल्लातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>The marking nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल an arrow, अत to resemble, aff. घञ् with कन् added; wounding like a weapon; also भल्लात, भल्ली, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लिका
भल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Marking nut.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to भल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लूक|भल्लूकः
भल्लूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल to hurt, aff. उक; also भल्लूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लूक|भल्लूकः
भल्लूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल to injure, Uṇādi aff. ऊक; also भाल्लुक and भल्लुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Being, existing, the self-support of something already produced.<BR>2 Birth.<BR>3 Origin, production.<BR>4 The place or means of being.<BR>5 The state of being.<BR>6 The being or becoming possessed of any thing, as family, cattle, &c.<BR>7 Welfare, prosperity.<BR>8 Obtaining, acquisition.<BR>9 Excellence, superiority.<BR>10 The world.<BR>11 A deity, a god.<BR>12 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A fruit, the fruit of the Dillenia speciosa.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवघस्मर|भवघस्मरः
भवघस्मर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fire in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, घस्मर voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
भवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Thou; but used as a respectful term of address, as Sir or Lord, and governing the verb in the third person.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, डवतुप Uṇādi aff.<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Being, existing.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A poisoned arrow.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to be, participial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Yours, your honour's.<BR>E.<BR>भवत् as above, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवद्भी
भवद्भी<BR>mfn. (-द्भीः-द्भिः-द्भि)<BR>Afraid.<BR>E.<BR>भवत् being, and भी fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन|भवनं|भवनः
भवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 A nature, a quality.<BR>3 The place of abiding or being, site, field, spot, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनाशिनी
भवनाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Seryu or Serju river, which runs from the Himāla chain and falls into the Goggrah, with which it is then confounded.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, and नाशिनी destructress; giving eternal happiness, being a sacred stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनीय|भवनीयं
भवनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be or become, what is or ought to be.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, अनीयर् aff. of the gerund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनोदर
भवनोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The interior apartments.<BR>E.<BR>भवन, and उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्त|भवंत|भवंतः|भवन्तः
भवन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Time in general, or time present.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्ति|भवंति|भवंतिः|भवन्तिः
भवन्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>Time being, the present.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. झिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभाज्
भवभाज्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>Living, sharing the world.<BR>E.<BR>भव, and भाज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=614" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूति|भवभूतिः
भवभूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The author of MĀLATĪMĀDHAVA, and other dramas.<BR>E.<BR>भव the world, भूति increase, in wisdom, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवरुद्
भवरुद्<BR>f. (-रुद् or -रुत्)<BR>A drum played at funerals.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, रुद् to weep or wail, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भववीति|भववीतिः
भववीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Liberation from the world, cessation from worldly acts.<BR>2 End of the world.<BR>E.<BR>भव, and वीति passing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवात्मजा
भवात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The goddess MANASĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृश्
भवादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Like you, your like.<BR>E.<BR>भवत् you, दृश् to shew, aff. क्विप्; also भवादृश, and भवादृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानी
भवानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The goddess PĀRVATĪ or DURGĀ, in her pacific and amiable form.<BR>E.<BR>भव ŚIVA, fem. aff. ङीप्, and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानीगुरु|भवानीगुरुः
भवानीगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The personified Himālaya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>भवानी the goddess, and गुरु here put for father: DURGĀ in this form being the daughter of the mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभाव
भवाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Non-existence of the world.<BR>2 A sage, one unaffected by worldly infirmities.<BR>E.<BR>भव, and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभिभाविन्
भवाभिभाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Superior to or overcoming the world.<BR>E.<BR>भव, and अभिभाविन् disgracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवायना
भवायना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>भव the world, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविक|भविकं
भविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Prosperous, happy, welfaring.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Prosperity, welfare.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, (for well being,) and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवित|भवितः
भवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Been, become.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्य|भवितव्यं
भवितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be or become, what is to be.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, तव्य aff. of the gerund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्यता
भवितव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fate, destiny.<BR>E.<BR>भवितव्य what is to be, तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितृ
भवितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Actually being, or disposed to be.<BR>2 Wellbeing, faring well.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन्
भविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Living, being, having life and sensation.<BR>E.<BR>भव being, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन|भविनः
भविन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A poet, a versifier.<BR>E.<BR>भव the world, इनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविल|भविलः
भविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Being, existing, what is or exists.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्णु|भविष्णुः
भविष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Actually being or disposed to be.<BR>2 Being well, existing happily, virtuously, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, इष्णुच् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्य|भविष्यः
भविष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Future, what will be.<BR>E.<BR>see भविष्यत्, the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यत्|भविष्यन्त्
भविष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>What is to be, what will be, future.<BR>n. (-ष्यत्)<BR>The future.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, शतृ participial aff., स्य augment, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्य|भव्यं|भव्यः
भव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Happy, auspicious, prosperous.<BR>2 Well, proper, fit, right.<BR>3 True.<BR>4 To be or become, what is to be.<BR>5 A being, what is or exists.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>The Kāmaraṅga, a small fruit tree, (Averhoa carambola.)<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>1 A name of UMĀ.<BR>2 A large sort of pepper.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 A bone.<BR>2 Fruit, result.<BR>3 Being, existence.<BR>mn. (-व्यः-व्यं)<BR>One division of the poetical Rasas or sentiments.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भशिरा
भशिरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A sort of beet, (Beta Bengalensis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष|भषः
भष<BR>r. 1st cl. (-भषति)<BR>1 To bark or growl.<BR>2 To reproach, to speak malevolently, to rail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष|भषः
भष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>भष to bark. aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषक|भषकः
भषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>भष to bark, वुन् aff.; it is sometimes written भसक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषण|भषणं|भषणः
भषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Barking.<BR>E.<BR>भष to bark, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषत्
भषत्<BR>m. (-त्)<BR>1 The heart.<BR>2 Wood.<BR>3 The thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस
भस<BR>r. 3d cl. (वभस्ति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To blame or abuse; this root is usually restricted to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद्
भसद्<BR>f. (-सद्)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>3 The mons veneris.<BR>4 Time.<BR>5 A sort of duck.<BR>6 A float, a raft.<BR>E.<BR>भस to shine, अदि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन|भसनः
भसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A large bee.<BR>E.<BR>भस to sound, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन्त|भसंत|भसंतः|भसन्तः
भसन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Time.<BR>E.<BR>भस to shine, aff. झच्^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसित|भसितं
भसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Ashes.<BR>E.<BR>भस to shine, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसूचक|भसूचकः
भसूचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An astronomer or astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>भ a star, सूचक an intelligencer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रका
भस्त्रका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bellows.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to भस्त्रा; also भस्त्रिका, and भस्त्राका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रा
भस्त्रा<BR>f. (-स्त्रा)<BR>A bellows, a large hide with valves, and a clay nozzle, which is used for this purpose.<BR>E.<BR>भस to shine, त्रन Uṇādi aff., fem. aff. टाप्; also with ङीष् aff. भस्त्री, and with कन् in the fem. form added भस्त्रका or भस्त्रिका optionally; and with the feminine termination retained also, भस्त्राका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्राका
भस्त्राका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bellows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रिक
भस्त्रिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A bellows-blower, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An inflated skin on which rafts, &c. are floated.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bellows: see भस्त्र.<BR>E.<BR>भस्त्र a bellows, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्री
भस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A bellows: see भस्त्रा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मक|भस्मकं
भस्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A disease of the eyes, thickening of the membranes, and indistinctness of vision.<BR>2 Morbid appetite, constant craving for food, with general decay.<BR>3 An anthelmintic plant, commonly Bireng.<BR>4 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन् ashes, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मकार|भस्मकारः
भस्मकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>भह्मन् ashes, and कार agent; using the ashes of wood in place of soap or ley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मगन्धिका|भस्मगंधिका
भस्मगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन् ashes, and गन्ध smell, aff. कन्, and टाप्; also भस्मगन्धिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मगर्भा
भस्मगर्भा<BR>f. (-र्भ)<BR>1 The Sisu tree, or a variety of it, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>E.<BR>भस्म ashes, and गर्भ place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मतूल|भस्मतूलं
भस्मतूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A number of villages.<BR>2 A shower of dust.<BR>3 Frost or snow.<BR>E.<BR>भस्म ashes, तूल to weigh, and aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मन्
भस्मन्<BR>n. (-स्म)<BR>Ashes.<BR>E.<BR>भस to shine, Uṇādi aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मवेधक|भस्मवेधकः
भस्मवेधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>भस्म ashes, and वेधक distresser; whiter than ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मसात्
भस्मसात्<BR>ind.<BR>Ashes, to ashes, as स भस्मसाच्चकारारीन् He reduced the enemies to ashes.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन्, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्माह्वय|भस्माह्वयः
भस्माह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन् ashes, आह्वय a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीकरण|भस्मीकरणं
भस्मीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Reducing to ashes.<BR>2 Calcining.<BR>E.<BR>भह्म, and करण doing, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीकृत
भस्मीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reduced to ashes.<BR>2 Calcined, (as a metal.)<BR>E.<BR>भस्म, and कृत made, with च्चि aug.; also भस्मकृत and भस्मसात्कृत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीभूत
भस्मीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reduced to ashes.<BR>2 Being mere ashes, i. e. being wholly worthless.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन्, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=615" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
भा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (-भाति)<BR>1 To shine, to be luminous, splendid or beautiful.<BR>2 To be pleased.<BR>3 To be angry.<BR>4 To blow.<BR>5 To be, to exist.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>to flash.<BR>With प्र or वि,<BR>to shine brightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
भा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>3 The shadow of a gnomon.<BR>m. (भाः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकूट|भाकूटः
भाकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A mountain, apparently the part of the Himālaya, called Bhākūr.<BR>2 A sort of fish.<BR>E.<BR>भा light, कूट peak or quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकोष|भाकोषः
भाकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भा light, कोष receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्त|भाक्तं
भाक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>1 A follower, a dependant, one to whom food is regularly given.<BR>2 Grain, edible grain, as rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त food, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्तिक|भाक्तिकः
भाक्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One who is fed by another, a dependant, a retainer.<BR>E.<BR>भक्त food, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग|भागः
भाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A portion, a share, a part.<BR>2 Fate, fortune, luck.<BR>3 A half rupee.<BR>4 Part of any thing given as interest.<BR>5 A division of time, the thirtieth part of a Rāśi or zodiacal sign.<BR>6 A degree, the 360th part of the circumference of a great circle.<BR>7 A fraction.<BR>E.<BR>भज to share, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागक|भागकः
भागक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what divides.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>(In arithmetic), A divisor.<BR>E.<BR>भज, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागजाति|भागजातिः
भागजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Assimilation of fractions.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागधेय|भागधेयं|भागधेयः
भागधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 An heir, a co-heir.<BR>2 Royal revenue.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Fate, destiny, luck.<BR>E.<BR>भाग a part, and घेय to be taken, or घेय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागन|भागनं
भागन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The period, during which the sun passes through the twelve signs of the zodiac, thence by ellipsis, the zodiac.<BR>2 The circumference of a great circle.<BR>E.<BR>भाग to divide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागशस्
भागशस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to a share or portion, in parts or portions.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागहर|भागहरः
भागहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Taking a part, sharing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A coheir.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Division.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, and हर who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागार्थिन्
भागार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिणी-र्थि)<BR>Desirous of a share.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, and अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागानुबन्धजाति|भागानुबन्धजातिः
भागानुबन्धजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Assimilation of fractional increase.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, अनुवन्ध accession, जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागापवाहजाति|भागापवाहजातिः
भागापवाहजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Assimilation of fractional decrease.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, अपवाह taking away, जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिक|भागिकं
भागिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Bearing interest, subject to a deduction for interest.<BR>2 Having a part.<BR>3 Relating to a part.<BR>4 Fractional.<BR>E.<BR>भाग a part, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिन्
भागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Who or what shares.<BR>2 Having parts, consisting of parts or shares.<BR>mf. (-गी-गिनी)<BR>A co-heir or co-heiress.<BR>E.<BR>भाग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिनेय|भागिनेयः
भागिनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sister's son.<BR>E.<BR>भगिनी a sister, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीरथी
भागीरथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>भगीरथ a pious monarch, at whose intercession the Ganges first descended from heaven, affs. अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागुरि|भागुरिः
भागुरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A celebrated grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्य|भाग्यं
भाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>1 To be portioned or divided.<BR>2 Bearing interest, subject to a deduction of some part on that account.<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Destiny, fortune, good or ill luck.<BR>E.<BR>भज to divide, ण्यत् aff.; or भाग a part, and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गीन|भांगीन|भांगीनं|भाङ्गीनं
भाङ्गीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bearing hemp, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>भङ्ग hemp, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
भाज्<BR>mfn. (भाक्)<BR>Who or what participates or possesses, used chiefly in composition, as धनभाज् rich, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भाज् to divide, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज
भाज<BR>r. 10th cl. (भाजयति)<BR>To divide, to separate; it is usually employed with वि prefixed, especially in a legal sense, as to divide or portion an inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजक्
भाजक्<BR>ind.<BR>Swiftly, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजन|भाजनं
भाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Any vessel, as a pot or cup, a plate, &c.<BR>2 A clever, capable, or fit person.<BR>3 Sharing, dividing.<BR>4 (In arithmetic,) Division.<BR>E.<BR>भज to serve or share, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजित|भाजितं
भाजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Divided, portioned.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A portion, a share.<BR>E.<BR>भाज to divide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्य|भाज्यं
भाज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Divisible, to be portioned or divided.<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>1 A portion, a share, an inheritance.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) The dividend.<BR>E.<BR>भाज to divide, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटक|भाटकं|भाटकः
भाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Price, especially paid for the use of any thing or person; wages, hire.<BR>E.<BR>भट to hire or maintain, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटि|भाटिः
भाटि<BR>f. (-ठिः)<BR>Wages, hire, fee.<BR>E.<BR>भट to hire, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण|भाणः
भाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sort of dramatic entertainment, described as one, in which one only of the interlocutors appears on the scene; or as the narrative of some intrigue, told either by the hero or a third person.<BR>E.<BR>भण to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाणिका
भाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A comic drama in one act.<BR>E.<BR>भाण, and कन् dimin. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्ड|भांड|भांडं|भाण्डं|भाण्डः
भाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 Any vessel, a pot, a cup, a plate, &c.<BR>2 Any musical instrument.<BR>3 Any implement or utensil.<BR>4 Capital, principal.<BR>5 An ornament in general.<BR>6 An ornament round a horse's neck and breast.<BR>7 The bed of a river, the space between its banks.<BR>8 Mimickry, buffoonery, the practice of the Bhaṇḍa or professional jester.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A tree, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>E.<BR>भदि to be auspicious, aff. अच्, or भण to sound, aff. ड, deriv. irr., or भण्ड a jester, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डक|भांडक|भांडकं|भांडकः|भाण्डकः
भाण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cup, a plate, a vessel, or utensil.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Goods, merchandise^1.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड, and कन् added.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुट|भांडपुट|भाण्डपुटः
भाण्डपुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, पुट to rub, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुष्प|भाण्डपुष्पः
भाण्डपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक|भांडप्रतिभांडक
भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Rule of barter, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड, and प्रति for, again, भाण्डक goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक|भांडप्रतिभांडक
भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The contents of any vessel.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड, and भरक what fills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डवादन
भाण्डवादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Playing on musical instruments.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड, and वादन sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डागार|भांडागार|भाण्डागारः
भाण्डागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A store-room, a place where household goods and utensils are kept.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A treasury.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिक|भांडिक|भांडिकः|भाण्डिकः
भाण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A musician, one especially who is to waken the prince or chief in the morning, by vocal, or instrumental music.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, (an instrument,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिन्
भाण्डिन्<BR>mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि)<BR>Having a vessel, utensil, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=616" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिवाह|भांडिवाह|भाण्डिवाहः
भाण्डिवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्डि for भाण्डी having a bason, and वाह who works or labours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिल|भांडिल|भांडिलः|भाण्डिलः
भाण्डिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डीर|भांडीर|भांडीरः|भाण्डीरः
भाण्डीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, ईर to bring, aff. क; referable perhaps to the legend that describes the infant KṚṢṆA, taking his meals under a tree of this kind in the woods of Vṛndāvana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात्
भात्<BR>mfn. (-भान्-भान्ती-भाती-भात्)<BR>Shining, splendid.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात|भातं|भातः
भात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shone, bright, resplendent.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Morning, dawn.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भातु|भातुः
भातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्र|भाद्रः
भाद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The name of a month, (August-September,) when the moon is full near the wing of Pegasus.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र for भद्रपदा, and अण् aff.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रपद|भाद्रपदः
भाद्रपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The month Bhādra.<BR>E.<BR>भद्रपदा the asterism, and अण् aff.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A name common to the twenty-sixth and twenty-seventh lunar asterisms, distinguished by the epithets prior, and subsequent, or पूर्व्व and उत्तरः see पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भद्रा said to mean a cow, and पद foot, अण् added optionally, whence it is often read भद्रपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमातुर|भाद्रमातुरः
भाद्रमातुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The son of a virtuous and loyal wife.<BR>E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, मातृ a mother, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानु|भानुः
भानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Light.<BR>3 A ray of light.<BR>4 A master.<BR>5 A sovereign, a prince.<BR>6 The father of the fifteenth Jaina pontiff.<BR>7 Beauty.<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, Uṇādi aff. नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुफला
भानुफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The plantain, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>भानु the sun, फल the fruit; being offered in the worship of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुमत्|भानुमन्त्
भानुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Luminous, splendid, resplendent.<BR>2 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भानु light, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुवार|भानुवारः
भानुवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sunday.<BR>E.<BR>भानु the sun, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानेमि|भानेमिः
भानेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भा light, नेमि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाभ
भाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Bright, (as a planet.)<BR>E.<BR>भ, and आभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
भाम<BR>r. 1st cl. (भामते) r. 10th cl. (भामयति)<BR>To be angry or wrathful, to be impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
भाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Passion, wrath.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>4 A sister's husband.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A passionate woman.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, and मन् Uṇādi aff.; or भाम to be angry, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामक|भामकः
भामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sister's husband.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
भामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-भिनी-मि)<BR>Angry, passionate.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A passionate woman.<BR>E.<BR>भाम passion, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार|भारः
भार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A weight of gold, equal to two thousand Palas.<BR>2 A yoke for carrying burthens.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A weight, a burthen.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Bhāratavarṣa or India proper, so called from BHARATA, the son of DUṢYANTA, whose patrimony it was. (E. भरत the prince, and अण् aff.)<BR>2 The great sacred epic poem of the Hindus. (E. भार weight, त aff., भारत; having been put by the Ṛṣis in a scale, and weighed against the four Vedas which it was found to outweigh; thence its usual prefix of Mahā or great: a special grammatical rule, however, derives it from भरत the prince so named, because the war narrated in it occurred amongst his descendants.)<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An actor, a mime.<BR>2 A name of fire.<BR>3 A descendant of BHARATA.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The goddess of speech.<BR>2 Speech.<BR>3 A quail.<BR>4 A branch of the dramatic art, dramatic recitation or declamation, the delivery of the dialogue that is composed in elaborate Sanscrit stanzas.<BR>E.<BR>भरत the inventor of the Indian drama, aff. अण्; or the name of a sage, whose devotions brought the goddess SARASVATĪ from heaven; or again, भॄ to nourish, aff. अतच्, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाज|भारद्वाजं|भारद्वाजः
भारद्वाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of DROṆA, the military preceptor of the Kurus, and Pāṇḍus.<BR>2 One of the seven Ṛṣis.<BR>3 A name of the Muni AGASTYA.<BR>4 The son of VṚHASPATI.<BR>5 A skylark.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A bone.<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>भरद्वाज a lark, and अण् pleonastick or derivative aff.; in the latter case it refers to a legend of the Ṛṣi BHARADVĀJA having been nursed by a lark, in consequence of being abandoned at his birth by his natural parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारय|भारयः
भारय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयष्टि|भारयष्टिः
भारयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A pole or yoke for carrying burthens; a stick carried over the shoulder, with strings attached to either end of it, forming at their lower extremity a noose, in which the articles to be conveyed are suspended.<BR>E.<BR>भार a burthen, and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारव|भारवं
भारव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A bow-string.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Holy basil.<BR>E.<BR>भार a weight, वा to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवत्|भारवन्त्
भारवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Loaded, burthened, bearing a burthen.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाह|भारवाहः
भारवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A porter, a bearer of burthens.<BR>E.<BR>भार a burthen, वह to bear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहन|भारवाहनः
भारवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A beast of burthen, (as a camel, &c.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A vehicle for burthens, a waggon.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहिक|भारवाहिकः
भारवाहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Carrying burthens.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A porter.<BR>E.<BR>भारवाह, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहिन्
भारवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A porter.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and वाहिन् who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवि|भारविः
भारवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The name of a poet, the author of the Kirātārjunīya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवृक्ष|भारवृक्षः
भारवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A fragrant substance, commonly Kākṣi, considered variously as a vegetable or mineral product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसह
भारसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Able to carry loads.<BR>2 Fit for the yoke.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and सह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहर|भारहरः
भारहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A porter.<BR>E.<BR>भार a burthen, and हर who takes, from हृ with ट aff.; also with अण् aff. भारहार, and कन् added, भारहारक; or with घिनुण, भारहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहार|भारहारः
भारहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A porter.<BR>2 Carrying a load.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहारिक
भारहारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Bearing a load, relating or referring to it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भारहार, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराक्रान्त|भाराक्रांत
भाराक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Loaded, laden, bearing a burthen.<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A species of the Atyaṣṭi metre.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and आक्रान्त overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारि|भारिः
भारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>भॄ to threaten, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A porter.<BR>E.<BR>भार a burthen, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिन्
भारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A porter.<BR>E.<BR>भार a burthen, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्धरण
भारोद्धरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking up or bearing a burthen.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and उद्धरण taking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=617" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्वहन
भारोद्वहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bearing a load.<BR>E.<BR>भार, and उद्वहन up lifting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गव|भार्गवः
भार्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>2 A name of ŚUKRA regent of VENUS, and preceptor of the Titans or demons.<BR>3 An archer.<BR>4 An elephant.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>3 Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon, the Agrostis linearis of LINNÆUS; according to the Hindus, a black variety.)<BR>E.<BR>भृगु a Muni, the ancestor of PARAŚURĀMA, &c., and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवप्रिय|भार्गवप्रियः
भार्गवप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The diamond.<BR>E.<BR>भार्गव ŚUKRA, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गी
भार्गी<BR>f. (-र्गी)<BR>A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>भर्ग BRAHMĀ, and अण् aff., sacred to that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्द्वाजी
भार्द्वाजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>a various reading of भारद्वाजी as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्या|भार्या
भार्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A wife, espoused according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>भॄ to nourish, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्याट|भार्याट|भार्य्याटः
भार्य्याट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A man who lets out his wife for prostitution.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या wife, अट to go, aff. अच्; who lives by his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्याटिक|भार्याटिक|भार्याटिकः|भार्य्याटिकः
भार्य्याटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A henpecked husband, one overruled by his wife.<BR>2 A kind of deer.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या a wife, अट to go or be with, aff. अच्, भार्य्याट, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यातिक्रम
भार्य्यातिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Adultery.<BR>2 Connubial intercourse.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या, and अतिक्रम approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यात्व|भार्यात्व
भार्य्यात्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The condition or state of a wife.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यापति|भार्यापति
भार्य्यापति<BR>m. dual only. (-ती)<BR>Husband and wife.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या wife, and पति a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यारु|भार्यारु|भार्यारुः|भार्य्यारुः
भार्य्यारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The name of a mountain.<BR>2 A sort of deer.<BR>3 The father of a child by another man's wife.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या a wife, ऋ to go to or with, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्योढ|भार्योढ
भार्य्योढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>Married.<BR>E.<BR>भार्य्या, and ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल|भालं
भाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The forehead.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>भल to explain, and अञ् aff., a man's fortunes being supposed to be legible on his forehead; or भा to shine, aff. लच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शन|भालदर्शनं|भालदर्शनः
भालदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>भाल, and दर्शन appearing; being used to stain the forehead with particular lines, and marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदृश्
भालदृश्<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भाल, and दृश् the eye, having the third eye in his forehead; also similar compounds, as भाललोचन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालाङ्क|भालांक|भालाङ्कः
भालाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A sort of fish, commonly the Rohi, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>2 A saw.<BR>3 A sort of potherb.<BR>4 A man born with lucky lines on his forehead.<BR>5 A tortoise.<BR>6 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भाल the forehead, and अङ्क a spot or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लुक|भाल्लुकः
भाल्लुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>भल्ल to injure, aff. उकञ् or ऊकञ्, whence also भाल्लूक; and with उक aff. भल्लुक, भल्लूक, &c., q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव|भावः
भाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 State or condition of being.<BR>2 Natural state of being, innate property, disposition, nature.<BR>3 Meaning, purpose, intention.<BR>4 Mind, soul.<BR>5 State or affection of mind, emotion, passion, sentiment, especially as an object of amatory and dramatic poetry; two kinds of Bhāvas are usually enumerated, the Sthāyi, and Vyabhicārī; the first of which comprehends eight varieties, and the second thirty-three; the list blends both feelings and effects, and sorrow, and sleep, and passion, and death, &c. are equally classed amongst the Bhāvas; dramatic writers add two other classes, the Vibhāvas or preceding states of mind, leading to a particular condition of mind or body, and Anubhāvas the external signs of any state of mind.<BR>6 Birth.<BR>7 Act, action.<BR>8 Movement, gesture.<BR>9 Wanton sport or pastime.<BR>10 Corporeal expression of amorous sentiments; or love, of which the origin and effects are ascribed to the organs of the body.<BR>11 Thing, substance.<BR>12 A being, a living thing.<BR>13 The place of birth, or pudendum muliebre.<BR>14 Superhuman power.<BR>15 The abstract idea conveyed by any word.<BR>16 The simple idea derived from the root, as expressed in one class of derivatives, as a going, a doing, &c.<BR>17 Advice, instruction.<BR>18 A learned man, a Paṇḍita, (in theatrical language; but especially applied to the manager, or principal performer.)<BR>19 Venerable, respectable.<BR>20 The world, the universe.<BR>21 An organ of sense or passion.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावक|भावकः
भावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The external expression of amatory sentiments.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावज|भावजः
भावज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Love, KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भाव sentiment, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत|भावतः
भावत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Yours, your honour's.<BR>E.<BR>भवत् you, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Yours, (but used respectfully,) your honour's.<BR>E.<BR>भवत् you, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावन|भावनं|भावनः
भावन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Mental perception, recollection, the present consciousness of past ideas or perceptions.<BR>2 Imagination.<BR>3 Religious and abstract meditation.<BR>4 Looking about, (literally or figuratively,) observing, investigating.<BR>5 Causing to be.<BR>6 Decorating any person or object with flowers, perfume, &c., scenting, anointing.<BR>7 Steeping, infusion, especially repeatedly drying the article by day and keeping it moist at night.<BR>8 (In arithmetic,) Composition.<BR>9 (In law,) Ascertainment, proof.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, in the causal form, to bring present or into being, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावबोधक|भावबोधकः
भावबोधक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The sign or indication of any sentiment or passion.<BR>E.<BR>भाव sentiment, and बोधक what indicates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयत्
भावयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Fancying, imagining, calling to mind.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशवलता
भावशवलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Co-existence of various emotions.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and शवलता variety of colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशान्ति
भावशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Allaying, any transitory or incidental emotion.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and शान्ति quieting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसंशुद्धि
भावसंशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Purification of the natural condition or quality.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and संशुद्धि purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसन्धि|भावसंधि|भावसंधिः
भावसन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>Co-existence of two emotions.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसमाहित
भावसमाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Of restrained purpose or thought, abstracted, devout.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and समाहित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाट|भावाटः
भावाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The external expression or indication of amatory feeling.<BR>2 A pious or holy man.<BR>3 An actor.<BR>4 A libidinous man.<BR>5 Dress, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>भाव the sentiment or disposition, अट to go with, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावानुग
भावानुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Natural, simple, not forced or assumed.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and अनुग according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाभास|भावाभासः
भावाभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Simulation of feeling or emotion.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and आभास appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=618" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावार्थ|भावार्थः
भावार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 The simple inherent or abstract meaning of words.<BR>2 The obvious purport of a phrase or sentence.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाव
भावाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Tender, compassionate.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and अव what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविक|भाविकः
भाविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Natural, innate.<BR>2 Sentimental, relating to feeling, &c.<BR>3 Future.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A figure of rhetoric, describing the past or future as present.<BR>E.<BR>भाव, and ठक् aff., or भू to be, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित|भावितः
भावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Occupied with, pervaded by, having as an inherent or pervading property.<BR>2 Animated, inspired.<BR>3 Imagined, conceived.<BR>4 Perfumed, scented.<BR>5 Mixed, (with any thing as an ingredient, as asafoetida or other fragrant substances in curry, &c.)<BR>6 Obtained, got.<BR>7 Promised, agreed, acknowledged.<BR>8 Steeped, infused, digested, &c.<BR>9 (In arithmetic,) Supposed, as the product of unknown quantities.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, passive or causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितवत्
भावितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Imagining, conceiving.<BR>2 Infusing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, causal v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितात्मन्
भावितात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Intent upon, engaged in.<BR>E.<BR>भावित pervaded, आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्र|भावित्रं
भावित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The three worlds: earth, heaven, and hell, collectively.<BR>E.<BR>भू to exist, णित्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Future, what will be or what is about to be, proximately future.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A wanton woman.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावोदय
भावोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Accession or occurrence of emotions.<BR>E.<BR>भवा, उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right.<BR>2 Actually being or disposed to be.<BR>3 (In composition with other nouns,) Becoming what it was not before, as आढ्यंभावुक one who becomes rich.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Happiness, auspiciousness.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sister's husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. उकञ्; used in composition, the aff. is खुकञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 What must, will, or ought to be.<BR>2 To be investigated or determined.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष
भाष<BR>(ऋ) भाषृ r. 1st cl. (भाषते)<BR>To speak: with परि prefixed, to explain, to expound; with सम्, to discourse, to converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषण|भाषणं
भाषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Speaking, speech.<BR>2 Declaration of satisfaction at the end of a drama.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषत्
भाषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>भाष, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषमाण
भाषमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Speech.<BR>2 Common or vernacular speech.<BR>3 SARASVATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>4 One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषापाद|भाषापादः
भाषापाद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The plaint, the charge, the first of the four divisions of a law suit.<BR>E.<BR>भाषा speech, averment, and पाद quarter, division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषासम|भाषासमः
भाषासम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A figure of rhetoric, arrangement of a sentence so that it is both Sanscrit and Prākṛta.<BR>E.<BR>भाषा, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken, uttered, said.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Speech.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्य|भाष्यं
भाष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>To be said or spoken.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 A commentary, but particularly the explanation and application of a technical Sūtra or aphorism; hence applied to many of the annotations on the grammatical aphorisms of PĀṆINI, to comments on the Vedas, &c.<BR>2 A sort of building.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकर|भाष्यकरः
भाष्यकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A commentator or expounder of technical texts or aphorisms; commonly applied as an epithet of PĀTAÑJALI, the author of the Mahābhāṣya or commentary on the annotations of KĀTYĀYANA, on PĀṆINI'S grammatical aphorisms.<BR>E.<BR>भाष्य as above, and कार who makes; also with कृत्, भाष्यकृत्, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यमाण
भाष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being spoken to or addressed.<BR>E.<BR>भाष to speak, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास<BR>(ऋ) भासृ r. 1st cl. (भासते)<BR>To shine.<BR>With प्र and नि prefixed,<BR>To appear to, to seem likely or probable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास्<BR>f. (-भाः)<BR>1 Light.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>3 Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास<BR>mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>Light, lustre, shining.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A vulture.<BR>2 A sort of bird, described as a water-fowl.<BR>3 A cock.<BR>4 A station of cowherds.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्त|भासंत|भासन्तः
भासन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>2 Shining, splendid.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 A kind of waterfowl.<BR>mf. (-न्तः-न्ती)<BR>A star.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, झच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासयत्
भासयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Shining, radiant.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासस्
भासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासु|भासुः
भासु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुर|भासुरं|भासुरः
भासुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Shining, splendid.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A species of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Crystal.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>E.<BR>भास to shine, घुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Resplendent, shining.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 A hero.<BR>4 The name of a celebrated astronomer.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>भा light, and कृ to make, अच् aff., and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करप्रिय|भास्करप्रियः
भास्करप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The ruby.<BR>E.<BR>भास्कर the sun, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वत्|भास्वन्त्
भास्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>Luminous, splendid, shining.<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Light.<BR>3 A hero.<BR>f. (-स्वता)<BR>The city of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>भास् light, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वर|भास्वरं|भास्वरः
भास्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Shining, radiant.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A day.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>भास् to shine, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्मन
भास्मन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Ashy, ashen, made or consisting of ashes.<BR>E.<BR>भस्मन्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष
भिक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (भिक्षते)<BR>1 To beg.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR>3 To fail of obtaining.<BR>4 To solicit any thing through cupidity or covetousness.<BR>5 To be weary or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षण|भिक्षणं
भिक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Begging, asking alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्ष to beg, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षमाण
भिक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्ष to beg, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षा
भिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Hire, wages.<BR>3 Begging, asking.<BR>4 The thing obtained by begging, alms.<BR>5 A mouthful or handful of food, given as alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्ष to beg or obtain by begging, अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=619" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाक|भिक्षाकः
भिक्षाक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A mendicant, a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, and काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचर|भिक्षाचरः
भिक्षाचर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A mendicant, a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, चर to go, aff. ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाटन|भिक्षाटनं|भिक्षाटनः
भिक्षाटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Begging, mendicancy.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, and अटन going about for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षान्न
भिक्षान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Food obtained as alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षापात्र
भिक्षापात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A beggar's bowl, a vessel for collecting alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशित्व|भिक्षाशित्वं
भिक्षाशित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Profligacy, roguery.<BR>2 Mendicancy, subsisting on alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षाशिन् a beggar, त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशिन्
भिक्षाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 A beggar, a mendicant, subsisting on alms.<BR>2 Dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, अश to eat, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षार्ह
भिक्षार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Fit for a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षित
भिक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Begged, sought as alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्ष to beg, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षु|भिक्षुः
भिक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>1 The mendicant; the Hindu who has entered the fourth order, and subsists wholly upon alms.<BR>2 The fourth order of the Hindus.<BR>3 A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्ष to beg, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुक|भिक्षुकः
भिक्षुक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>A beggar.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षु a beggar, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुसंघाटी
भिक्षुसंघाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Old or ragged raiment, the garb of a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षु a beggar, सम् with, घट to endeavour, aff. अण् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षोत्कर
भिक्षोत्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Scattering alms.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, उत् before कॄ to scatter, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त|भित्तं
भित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>A part, a portion, a fragment, a bit.<BR>E.<BR>भिट् to divide, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्ति|भित्तिः
भित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 A wall of earth or masonry.<BR>2 A thing broken or divided.<BR>3 A place, a part.<BR>4 Opportunity, occasion.<BR>5 An asylum.<BR>6 Breaking, tearing, dividing.<BR>7 A flaw, a defect.<BR>8 A rent, a fissure.<BR>9 A fragment, a bit, a broken piece or part.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to divide, to break, to tear, &c. aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिका
भित्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A wall.<BR>2 A small house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिचौर|भित्तिचौरः
भित्तिचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>भित्ति a wall, and चौर a thief; the mud wall of the Hindu cottages being easily and commonly cut through, for burglarious purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद्<BR>(इर) भिदिर् r. 7th cl. (भिनत्ति-भिंत्ते)<BR>To break, to break or tear to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद्<BR>mfn. (-भिद् or भित्)<BR>Who or what breaks, divides, severs, destroys, &c.<BR>f. (-भिट् or भित्)<BR>1 Kind, sort, difference.<BR>2 Breaking, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, and aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदक|भिदकं|भिदकः
भिदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sword.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदा
भिदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Tearing, rending.<BR>2 Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to divide, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदि|भिदिः
भिदि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, Uṇādi aff इ, and the vowel unchanged; also भिट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदिर|भिदिरं
भिदिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break or split, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदु|भिदुः
भिदु<BR>m. (-दुः)<BR>The thunderbolt. of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to split, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुर|भिदुरं|भिदुरः
भिदुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Brittle.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, (the earth, the mountains, &c.) कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदेलिम
भिदेलिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>To be, or what may be broken.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, केलिमर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्य|भिद्यः
भिद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A river, a male river.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, (its banks,) क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्यमान
भिद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being divided, pierced, broken, &c.<BR>2 Being separated or distinguished.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्र|भिद्रं|भिद्रः
भिद्र<BR>mn. (-द्रः-द्रं)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, Uṇādi aff. रक्; also भिदु, भिदुर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दत्
भिन्दत्<BR>mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दती-न्दत्)<BR>Breaking, destroying.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दपाल|भिंदपाल|भिंदपालः|भिन्दपालः
भिन्दपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A short arrow thrown from the hand, or shot through a tube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्न|भिन्नः
भिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Split, broken, torn, rent.<BR>2 Divided, distinguished, other, different.<BR>3 Separated, detached.<BR>4 Blown, budded, opened.<BR>5 Neglected, deviated from.<BR>6 Connected, joined.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A flaw in a jewel.<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 A bit, a portion.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) A fraction.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, to divide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नक|भिन्नकः
भिन्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A heterodox sectary, a Bauddha, a seceder.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न broken, separated, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगात्रिका
भिन्नगात्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.)<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न divided, गात्र the body, aff. of comparison कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगुणन
भिन्नगुणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Multiplication of fractions.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and गुणन multiplying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नघन|भिन्नघनः
भिन्नघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cube of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and घन a cube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदेह
भिन्नदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Wounded.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्ननौक
भिन्ननौक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Wrecked.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and नौका a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभागहर|भिन्नभागहरः
भिन्नभागहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Division of fractions.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and भागहर division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभाण्ड
भिन्नभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A potsherd, a broken plate or vessel.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभिन्नात्मन्
भिन्नभिन्नात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>Chick pea, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमर्म्मन्|भिन्नमर्मन्
भिन्नमर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Pierced in the joints, mortally wounded.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and मर्म्मन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवत्
भिन्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Divided, scattered.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्ग|भिन्नवर्गः
भिन्नवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Square of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and बर्ग a square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवृत्ति
भिन्नवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>1 Neglecting the prescribed observances.<BR>2 Following an occupation not suited to birth or caste.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नव्यवकलित
भिन्नव्यवकलित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Subtraction of fractions.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and व्यवकलित subtraction; also भिन्नव्यवकलनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नसङ्कलित|भिन्नसंकलित
भिन्नसङ्कलित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Addition of fractions.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and सङ्कलित addition; also भिन्नसङ्कलनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नस्वर
भिन्नस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Hesitating (in speech.)<BR>2 Hoarse, discordant.<BR>E.<BR>भिन्न, and स्वर a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिया
भिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Fear.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, टाप् aff., and इयङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल
भिल<BR>r. 10th cl. (भिलयति)<BR>To divide or separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्ल|भिल्लः
भिल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A barbarian of a particular tribe, perhaps the modern Bheel, a savage race dwelling especially along the course of the Narmadā, and subsisting chiefly by plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषग्जित|भिषग्जितं
भिषग्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>भिषज् a physician, and जित subdued, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=620" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्
भिषज्<BR>m. (-षक्)<BR>A Vaidya or physician.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, अजि Uṇādi aff., and षुक् augment; or भिषज् a Kaṇḍvādi root, to overcome, (disease,) aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्सटा
भिस्सटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Scorched rice.<BR>E.<BR>भिस्सा boiled rice, टीक to go or resemble, ड aff.; this word is variously read भिस्सिटा, भिष्मिटा, भिष्मिष्टा, भिष्मिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्सा
भिस्सा<BR>f. (-स्सा)<BR>Boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>भिट् to break, aff. क्विप्, षो to destroy, aff. क, and the द of भिट् changed irr. to स; also read भिष्माः see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
भी<BR>(ञि) ञिभी r. 3rd cl. (बिभेति)<BR>To dread, to fear, to be afraid of: also, r. 1st and 10th cls. (भयति भाययति) but not always admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
भी<BR>f. (भीः)<BR>Fear, dread.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीत|भीतं
भीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Afraid, frightened, fearful, timid.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Fear, alarm, apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतङ्कार|भीतंकार|भीतंकारं
भीतङ्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Fear-inspiring.<BR>E.<BR>भीत, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतभीत
भीतभीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Much frightened.<BR>E.<BR>भीत afraid, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतवत्
भीतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Afraid.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीति|भीतिः
भीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Fear, apprehension.<BR>2 Trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीम|भीमं|भीमः
भीम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Horrible, fearful, terrific.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Horror, terror.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>3 A kind of sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A whip.<BR>3 A sort of perfume: see रोचना.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, Uṇādi aff. मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमकर्म्मन्|भीमकर्मन्
भीमकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Dreadful, destructive.<BR>E.<BR>भीम, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमदर्शन
भीमदर्शन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Frightful, hideous.<BR>E.<BR>भीम, and दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमनाद|भीमनादः
भीमनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A loud or fearful sound.<BR>E.<BR>भीम formidable, नाद voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमर|भीमरं|भीमरः
भीमर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>भीम fear, रा to give or get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमरथी
भीमरथी<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>1 A particular night, supposed to be the ordinary period of human life; the seventh night, in the seventh month, of the seventy-seventh year; a person after this period is exempt from all religious or specific observances.<BR>2 The name of a river in the Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>भीम formidable, रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविक्रम
भीमविक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Tremendous in power or strength.<BR>E.<BR>भीम, and विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविक्रान्त|भीमविक्रांत|भीमविक्रान्तः
भीमविक्रान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>भीम formidable, विक्रान्त power, valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविग्रह
भीमविग्रह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Gigantic, terrific in appearance.<BR>E.<BR>भीम, and विग्रह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमवेग
भीमवेग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Terribly swift or rapid.<BR>E.<BR>भीम, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमशासन|भीमशासनः
भीमशासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>भीम formidable, शासन edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमसेन|भीमसेनः
भीमसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The third of the five Pāṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>भीम formidable, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरु|भीरुः
भीरु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः or -रूः-रु)<BR>Timid, fearful.<BR>f. (-रुः-रूः)<BR>1 A timid woman.<BR>2 A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>3 A sort of prickly night-shade.<BR>4 A shakal.<BR>5 A centipede.<BR>6 A tiger.<BR>7 A goat.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, Uṇādi aff. क्रु; also र being changed to उ, भीलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुक|भीरुकं|भीरुकः
भीरुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Timid, fearful.<BR>2 Formidable.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A wood, a forest.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An owl.<BR>2 A bear.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, Uṇādi aff. क्रुकन्; also ल being substituted for र, भीलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुचेतस्
भीरुचेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>भीरु timid, and चेतस् disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुता
भीरुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fear, timidity, fearfulness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to भीरु; also with त्व, भीरुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुमय
भीरुमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Terrific, frightful.<BR>E.<BR>भीरु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुरन्ध्र|भीरुरंध्र|भीरुरन्ध्रः
भीरुरन्ध्र<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>An oven, a furnace.<BR>E.<BR>भीरु fearful, and रन्ध्र a chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुहृदय|भीरुहृदयः
भीरुहृदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>भीरु timid, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः or लूः-लु)<BR>Timid, fearful: see भीरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलुक|भीलुकः
भीलुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Timid, fearful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bear: see भीरुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषण|भीषणः
भीषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Horrible, terrific, formidable.<BR>2 Hard, harsh.<BR>3 Exciting the sentiment of horror, applied to poetical compositions.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Horror, terror, the property that excites fear.<BR>2 The sentiment of horror as the object of poetical composition.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषयमाण
भीषयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Terrifying, frightening.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, causal v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषा
भीषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Terrifying, frightening, intimidation.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, causal v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्म|भीष्मं|भीष्मः
भीष्म<BR>mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मा-ष्मं)<BR>Horrible, terrific, fearful.<BR>n. (-ष्मं)<BR>Horror, horribleness, the property of exciting fear or terror.<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The grand-uncle of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>3 An imp, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, मक् Uṇādi aff. and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मसू
भीष्मसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>भीष्म the prince so named, and सू mother, being the mother of BHĪṢMA by ŚĀNTANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त|भुक्तं
भुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Eaten, eating, (either that which is eaten, or the person who has eaten.)<BR>2 Possessed, enjoyed.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Food.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तवत्|भुक्तवन्त्
भुक्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having eaten.<BR>2 Having possessed.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तशेष|भुक्तशेषः
भुक्तशेष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Orts, leavings.<BR>E.<BR>भुक्त, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तसमुज्झित|भुक्तसमुज्झितं
भुक्तसमुज्झित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Orts, leavings, either after a meal or what has dropped from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>भुक्त eaten, समुज्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्ति|भुक्तिः
भुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Possession, fruition, usufruct.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त्वा
भुक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having possessed, eaten, enjoyed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुग्न|भुग्नः
भुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Crooked, curved.<BR>2 Bent, bowed, bending, stooping.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to curve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज|भुजः
भुज<BR>r. 7th cl. (भुनक्ति भुंक्ते)<BR>1 To save, to cherish or protect.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>3 To enjoy.<BR>4 To suffer or endure.<BR>(ओ, ञौ) ओभुजौ r. 6th cl. (भुजति)<BR>To bend, to make crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज|भुजः
भुज<BR>mf. (-जः-जा)<BR>1 The arm.<BR>2 The hand.<BR>3 The arm or leg of a geometrical figure, as a square or triangle.<BR>4 A bending, a curve.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to bend, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=621" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजकोटर|भुजकोटरः
भुजकोटर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The armpit.<BR>E.<BR>भुज the arm, and कोटर a hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजग|भुजगः
भुजग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>भुज a curve, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगदारण|भुजगदारणः
भुजगदारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>भुजग a snake, and दारण destroyer; this word, and similar compounds, may be applied equally to any of the natural enemies of the serpent race, as the ardea, the peacock, the ichneumon, &c. ut infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगान्तक|भुजगांतक|भुजगान्तकः
भुजगान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>भुजग a snake, and अन्तक destroyer: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगाभोजिन्
भुजगाभोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>भुजग a snake, and आभोजिन् who eats: see भुजगदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगाशन|भुजगाशनः
भुजगाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>भुजग a snake, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्ग|भुजंग|भुजंगः|भुजङ्गः
भुजङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A catamite, a lecher.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A female snake.<BR>E.<BR>भुज a curve, गम to go, खच् aff.; also भुजङ्गम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गघातिनी|भुजंगघातिनी
भुजङ्गघातिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant considered as an antidote, commonly Kaṅkālika, and said to be a sort of mustard (?).<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, घातिनी destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गप्रयात|भुजंगप्रयात|भुजङ्गप्रयातं
भुजङ्गप्रयात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गभुज्|भुजंगभुज्
भुजङ्गभुज्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>1 The bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गभोजिन्|भुजंगभोजिन्
भुजङ्गभोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>The large Indian serpent, (Böa constrictor.)<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, and भोजिन् who eats; devouring the smaller races.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गम|भुजंगम|भुजंगमः|भुजङ्गमः
भुजङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>भुज bending, गम to go, and खच् aff.; also भुजग, and भुजङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गविजृम्बित
भुजङ्गविजृम्बित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of the Utkṛti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गशिशु|भुजंगशिशु|भुजङ्गशिशुः
भुजङ्गशिशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A species of the Vṛhatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गसंगता
भुजङ्गसंगता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Another species of the Vṛhatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गहन्|भुजंगहन्
भुजङ्गहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, and हन् who kills: see भुजङ्गदारण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गाक्षी|भुजंगाक्षी
भुजङ्गाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A plant, (the ichneumon plant): see रास्ना.<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, अक्ष to pervade, affs. अण् and ङीप्; otherwise भुजङ्ग and अक्ष an eye; the flowers being compared to the eye of the snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गाख्य|भुजंगाख्य|भुजङ्गाख्यः
भुजङ्गाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, and आख्या a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजशिरस्
भुजशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The shoulder, the shoulder blade.<BR>E.<BR>भुज the arm, शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाकण्ट|भुजाकंट|भुजाकण्टः
भुजाकण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>भुजा the hand, and कण्ट a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजादल|भुजादलः
भुजादल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A hand.<BR>E.<BR>भुजा the arm, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजान्तर|भुजांतर|भुजान्तरं
भुजान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The breast, the chest.<BR>E.<BR>भुज the arm, and अन्तर intervening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजापीड|भुजापीडः
भुजापीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>Clasping or enfolding in the arms.<BR>E.<BR>भुज, and आपीड pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजि|भुजिः
भुजि<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, इ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजिष्य|भुजिष्यः
भुजिष्य<BR>mf. (-ष्यः-ष्या)<BR>A servant, a slave.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>1 An independant man.<BR>2 A string worn round the wrist.<BR>(-ष्या)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to be crooked, Uṇādi aff. किष्यन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यमान
भुज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being enjoyed or possessed.<BR>2 Being eaten.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यु|भुज्युः
भुज्यु<BR>m. (-ज्युः)<BR>Eating.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, युक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुञ्जान|भुञ्जानः
भुञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 An enjoyer, a possessor.<BR>2 Eating, feeding.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, aff. शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुड
भुड<BR>(इ) भुडि r. 1st cl. (भुण्डते)<BR>To support, to maintain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरिज्
भुरिज्<BR>f. (-रिक्)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, इजि Uṇādi aff., and उर substituted for the radical vowel; also भूरिज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन|भुवनं
भुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A world.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Heaven.<BR>4 Man, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, क्यु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन्यु|भुवन्युः
भुवन्यु<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 A master or lord.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. कन्युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवनत्रय
भुवनत्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The three worlds: heaven, earth, and hell.<BR>E.<BR>भुवन, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवर्लोक|भुवर्लोकः
भुवर्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One of the divisions of the universe, the space between the earth and the sun, and the haunt of the Siddhas, Munis, and other saintly beings.<BR>E.<BR>भुवस् heaven, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवस्
भुवस्<BR>ind.<BR>Heaven, æther, sky, or atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुविस्
भुविस्<BR>n. (-विः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. इसि, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुशुण्डी|भुशुंडी
भुशुण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A weapon, apparently a kind of fire arms or rocket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू<BR>r. 1st cl. (भवति)<BR>1 To be, to become, to exist.<BR>2 To be born or produced.<BR>r. 10th cl. (भावयति)<BR>1 To mix.<BR>2 To think.<BR>3 To be clear or pure.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भवति-त भावयति-ते)<BR>To obtain. The first form of this root takes most of the prefixes, and then possesses a great variety of applications.<BR>With अधि,<BR>To rule or preside over.<BR>With अनु,<BR>1 To feel, to apprehend or perceive.<BR>2 To do, to make.<BR>3 To enjoy.<BR>4 To investigate.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To overcome.<BR>2 To pain or afflict.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To be born or produced.<BR>With परा,<BR>To be vanquished.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To become manifest, to appear, to come into sight or existence.<BR>2 To be equal to in personal conflict, to be a match for.<BR>3 To rule, to be supreme, to preside over.<BR>4 To be beyond or over.<BR>5 To proceed.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To be substituted for.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To disrespect.<BR>2 To surround.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To see.<BR>2 To uphold.<BR>3 To prove.<BR>4 To have majesty, or power.<BR>With वि and अति,<BR>व्यतिभवते,<BR>To be mutually or reciprocally.<BR>With सं,<BR>1 To be possible.<BR>2 To exist, to be born or produced.<BR>3 To contain.<BR>4 To overcome.<BR>5 To be able or adequate.<BR>6 To associate, to collect, to mix or assemble.<BR>7 To nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू<BR>f. (भूः)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Place, site, the place of being or abiding.<BR>3 Sacrificial fire.<BR>ind. (भू)<BR>The lowest of the seven hells.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूक|भूकं|भूकः
भूक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm.<BR>2 Time.<BR>3 Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, Uṇādi aff. कक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकदम्ब|भूकदंब|भूकदम्बः
भूकदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and कदम्ब nauclea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकम्प|भूकंप|भूकम्पः
भूकम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>An earth-quake.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and कम्प a trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकर्ण|भूकर्णः
भूकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>(In astronomy), The radius of the equator.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and कर्ण a sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकल|भूकलः
भूकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A restiff unmanageable horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=622" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकश्यप|भूकश्यपः
भूकश्यप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of VASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and कश्यप KAŚYAPA; being an incarnation of that personage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकाक|भूकाकः
भूकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small kind of heron.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकेश|भूकेशः
भूकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>2 The Indian fig.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>(-शा)<BR>A Rākṣasī or female goblin.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूक्षित्
भूक्षित्<BR>m. (-क्षित्-क्षिट्)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, क्षि to destroy, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगर्भ|भूगर्भः
भूगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A name of BHAVABHŪTI, the author of the Mālatī Mādhava, and other dramas.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, गर्भ fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगर|भूगरं
भूगर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Poison.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and गर poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगोल|भूगोलः
भूगोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The terrestrial globe, the earth.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and गोल a ball or globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूचक्र
भूचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>(In astronomy,) The equinoctial line.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूच्छाया|भूछाया
भूच्छाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजन्तु|भूजंतु|भूजन्तुः
भूजन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and जन्तु a being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजम्बू|भूजंबू
भूजम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>1 Wheat.<BR>2 The fruit of the Vikaṅkaṭa, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and जम्बू rose apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत|भूतं|भूतः
भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Been, become.<BR>2 Being, existing.<BR>3 Gone, past.<BR>4 (In composition,) Like, resembling.<BR>5 Obtained, got.<BR>6 Proper, right.<BR>7 True.<BR>8 Known.<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 A goblin, a ghost, a malignant spirit, haunting cemeteries, lurking in trees, animating carcases, and deluding or devouring human beings.<BR>2 A living being.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A son, a child.<BR>2 A demigod of a particular class.<BR>3 The fourteenth day of the dark half of the lunar month.<BR>4 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 An element; five Bhūtas are enumerated: earth, fire, water, air, and Ākāśa or æther.<BR>2 (In law,) Fact, matter of fact, the real state of the case, or what has actually been.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. क्त of the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकेश|भूतकेशः
भूतकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Root of sweet flag.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a spirit, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतक्रान्ति|भूतक्रांति|भूतक्रान्तिः
भूतक्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Possession by evil spirits.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, क्रान्ति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगण|भूतगणः
भूतगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A class of sprites or goblins.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगन्धा
भूतगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Murā, a sort of perfume.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and गन्ध a perfume; used perhaps in the ceremonies with which those beings are worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतग्राम|भूतग्रामः
भूतग्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Any aggregate of elementary matter, the body, the world.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and ग्राम a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतघ्न|भूतघ्नः
भूतघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 Garlic.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī<BR>2 Holy basil.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a sprite, and घ्न what destroys or removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतजटा
भूतजटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and जटा clustered locks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतदया
भूतदया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Compassion or tenderness to all creatures.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and दया clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधात्री
भूतधात्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a living being, and धात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाथ|भूतनाथः
भूतनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a spirit or element, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनायिका
भूतनायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a spirit, and नायिका leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाशन|भूतनाशनं|भूतनाशनः
भूतनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>2 Mustard.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The Eleocarpus seed.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and नाशन dispelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपुष्प|भूतपुष्पः
भूतपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>भूत a sprite, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्णिमा
भूतपूर्णिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Day of full moon in Aśvin.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a sprite, and पूर्णिमा full moon: the Bhūtas being worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्व्वम्|भूतपूर्वम्
भूतपूर्व्वम्<BR>ind.<BR>Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतबलि|भूतबलिः
भूतबलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Throwing the remnants of an offering on the ground for animals or outcastes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and बलि an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभर्त्तृ|भूतभर्तृ
भूतभर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Supporting the elements, living beings, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and भर्त्तृ who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभाव
भूतभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Elementary.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभृत्
भूतभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Supporting the elements, living beings, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and भृत् sustaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमात्र
भूतमात्र<BR>nf. (-त्रं-त्रा)<BR>The rudiment of an element.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and मात्र element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतयज्ञ|भूतयज्ञः
भूतयज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 Offering viands, &c. to all created beings.<BR>2 Worshipping evil spirits.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतल
भूतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The earth, the face of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवत्|भूतवन्त्
भूतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Being, been.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवास|भूतवासः
भूतवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविक्रिया
भूतविक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Epilepsy, possession by evil spirits.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and विक्रिया change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवेशी
भूतवेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A species of the Nebāri, (Nyctanthes tristis,) with white flowers.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, विश to pervade, अण् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवृक्ष|भूतवृक्षः
भूतवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>2 A species of Bignonia, (B. Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंसार|भूतसंसारः
भूतसंसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The world of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a sentient being, and संसार world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसर्ग|भूतसर्गः
भूतसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Elementary nature.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and सर्ग nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसञ्चार|भूतसंचार|भूतसंचारः|भूतसञ्चारः
भूतसञ्चार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Possession by evil spirits.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Fire in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, सम् with चर to go, aff. घञ्; also f. (-रिणी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसम्पृक्त
भूतसम्पृक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्त)<BR>Combined with elementary matter.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and सम्पृक्त united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसम्प्लव|भूतसंप्लव|भूतसंप्लवः
भूतसम्प्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A deluge, a drowning of the world.<BR>E.<BR>भूत all beings, and सम्प्लव swimming, floating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतस्थ
भूतस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Residing or existing in the elements.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतात्मन्
भूतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 War, conflict.<BR>5 The elementary or vital principle, or the proximate cause of life and action.<BR>E.<BR>भूत an element, आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतादि|भूतादिः
भूतादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>God, the originator of beings.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and आदि first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतारि|भूतारिः
भूतारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Asafœtida.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्त्त|भूतार्त|भूतार्त्तः
भूतार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Possessed by an evil spirit.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a spirit, आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावास|भूतावासः
भूतावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>भत, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=623" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूताविष्ट|भूताविष्टः
भूताविष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Occupied or possessed by a devil.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a spirit, आविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावेश|भूतावेशः
भूतावेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Possession by a devil or evil spirit.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, and आवेश entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूति|भूतिः
भूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Power, dignity.<BR>2 Superhuman power, as attributable to ŚIVA especially, and attainable by the practice of austere and magical rites.<BR>3 Prosperity, success.<BR>4 Production, birth.<BR>5 Ashes.<BR>6 Fried meat.<BR>7 The rut of elephants.<BR>8 State of being, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिक|भूतिकं|भूतिकः
भूतिक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>1 A sort of gentian, (G. cherayta.)<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthus.)<BR>3 Another kind of grass.<BR>4 A medicinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>5 Ligusticum ajwaen.<BR>E.<BR>भूत being or spirit, &c. aff. ठक्; also भूतीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकाम|भूतिकामः
भूतिकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Desirous of wealth, aggrandisement, &c.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A king's counsellor, a minister of state.<BR>2 VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>भूति, and काम who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकील|भूतिकीलः
भूतिकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A moat, a ditch.<BR>2 A celler, a place under ground for concealing wealth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकृत्य
भूतिकृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Any ceremony of a festive character, as a marriage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूति, and कृत्य rite; also भूतिकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिगर्भ|भूतिगर्भः
भूतिगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>BHAVABHŪTI, the dramatic poet.<BR>E.<BR>भूति superhuman power, and गर्भ embryo, being resuscitate^1d by his contemporary, and rival KĀLIDĀSA, after having lost his life in an intrigue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिनिधान|भूतिनिधानं
भूतिनिधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The twenty-fourth lunar mansion, Dhaniṣṭhā.<BR>E.<BR>भूति prosperity, and निधान receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतीक|भूतीकं
भूतीक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>1 A sort of gentian.<BR>2 A kind of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>4 Another sort of grass.<BR>E.<BR>भूत being, aff. ईकक्, otherwise भूतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेज्य
भूतेज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>A worshipper of spirits.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and इज्या worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेश|भूतेशः
भूतेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भूत an imp, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोपहत
भूतोपहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Possessed by an evil spirit.<BR>E.<BR>भूत, and उपहत affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्तम|भूत्तमं
भूत्तम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, उत्तभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्वा
भूत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having been or become.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूदार|भूदारः
भूदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, दृ to tear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूदेव|भूदेवः
भूदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूधन|भूधनः
भूधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूधर|भूधरः
भूधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A kind of chemical or medicinal apparatus; a sand bath in which a covered crucible is placed, and the fire is lighted above as well as below it.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, धृ to support, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूध्र|भूध्रः
भूध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, धृ to hold, aff. अप्, and the vowel changed to its analogous semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनाग|भूनागः
भूनाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and नाग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनिम्ब|भूनिम्बः
भूनिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A species of gentian, commonly Cherayta, (Gentiana cherayta, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and निम्ब the Nimb tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनेतृ
भूनेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and नेतृ a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूप|भूपः
भूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A sovereign, a prince, a king.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, पा to cherish, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपति|भूपतिः
भूपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपद|भूपदः
भूपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A tree.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac).<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and पद foot, root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपरिधि|भूपरिधिः
भूपरिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The equinoctial line.<BR>2 The circumference of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and परिधि a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपाल|भूपालः
भूपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपुत्त्री
भूपुत्त्री<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and पुत्त्री a daughter; being turned up out of the soil by a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभुज्
भूभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, भुज् to enjoy, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभृत्
भूभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, भृत् sustaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमन्
भूमन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Much, many.<BR>E.<BR>भू for बहु many, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमय
भूमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or consisting of earth.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A name of Chāyā or shadow personified, the wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>भू earth, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमि|भूमिः
भूमि<BR>f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Place, site in general.<BR>3 The base of any figure in geometry.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, and मि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिका
भूमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Theatrical dress, the costume of any character, represented on the stage.<BR>2 Decorating images, temples, gateways, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि place of being, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिचम्पक|भूमिचम्पकः
भूमिचम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Kæmpferia rotunda.)<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, and चम्पक Michelia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिज|भूमिजं|भूमिजः
भूमिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced of or on the earth.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 Hell.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिजम्बु|भूमिजम्बुः
भूमिजम्बु<BR>f. (-म्बुः-म्बू)<BR>A tree, (Premna herbacea.)<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, and जम्बु Eugenia; also with कन् added to either form, भूमिजम्बुका, and भूमिजम्बूका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिजीविन्
भूमिजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>The Vaiśya or Hindu of the third, or agricultural and mercantile tribe.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and जीविन् who gets a livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिदान
भूमिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Donation of landed property.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिदेव|भूमिदेवः
भूमिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिप|भूमिपः
भूमिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A prince, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भमि the earth, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपक्ष|भूमिपक्षः
भूमिपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A horse of a good breed.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and पक्ष part or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपति|भूमिपतिः
भूमिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपतित्व
भूमिपतित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Princedom, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिभृत्
भूमिभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and भृत् who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपिशाच|भूमिपिशाचः
भूमिपिशाच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The palmyra tree, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, पिशाच goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिमण्डा|भूमिमंडा
भूमिमण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, मडि to ornament, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिरक्षक|भूमिरक्षकः
भूमिरक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse of a good breed.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, रक्ष to preserve, aff. वुन्; it is also written भूमिरक्ष, and भूमिपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिलाभ|भूमिलाभः
भूमिलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, लाभ acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=624" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिलेपन|भूमिलेपनं
भूमिलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cow-dung.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, and लेपन plastering; the clay floors of houses, temples, &c. being usually kneaded up with this article.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिवर्द्धन
भूमिवर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Increasing or adding to the earth.<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>A corpse.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिशय|भूमिशयः
भूमिशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sleeping on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and शी to sleep, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिष्ठ
भूमिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Standing or staying on the earth.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसम्भव|भूमिसंभव|भूमिसंभवः
भूमिसम्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced in or of the earth.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and सम्भव born: see भूपुत्त्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्नु|भूमिस्नुः
भूमिस्नु<BR>m. (-स्नुः)<BR>An earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्पृश्
भूमिस्पृश्<BR>m. (-स्पृक्)<BR>1 A man, man, mankind.<BR>2 The Vaiśya or Hindu of the third tribe, the cultivator or trader.<BR>3 A thief, one who creeps along the ground to carry off his plunder.<BR>4 A blind man.<BR>5 A cripple, a lame man.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, the ground, and स्पृश who touches, from स्पृश, with क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीन्द्र|भूमींद्र|भूमीन्द्रः
भूमीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि earth, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्यामलकी
भूम्यामलकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, आमलकी a myrobalan; also भूम्यासनी f. (-नी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूय|भूयं|भूयः
भूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Abstract state, but used in composition, as ब्रह्मभूय the state of BRAHMA, or identification with BRAHMA, becoming of the same nature, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्
भूयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Much, many.<BR>ind.<BR>Frequently, repeatedly, again.<BR>2 Exceeding, over, above.<BR>E.<BR>बहु much, इयसुन् affix of the superlative, भू substituted for बहु, and the ई of the aff. rejected; also with इष्ठन् aff. भूयिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठ|भूयिष्ठं
भूयिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Many, very many, much, most: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरि|भूरिः
भूरि<BR>mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>Much, many.<BR>ind.<BR>Much, exceeding.<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 A day.<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिज्
भूरिज्<BR>f. (-रिक्)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to support, इजि Uṇādi aff., and ऋ changed to ऊर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिधामन्
भूरिधामन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>1 Splendid, bright.<BR>2 Illustrious.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि, and धामन् splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिपुष्पा
भूरिपुष्पा<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>Fennel: see शतपुष्पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिप्रेमन्
भूरिप्रेमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिफेना
भूरिफेना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि much, and फेन cuttle-fish bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिमाय|भूरिमायः
भूरिमाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A shakal.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि much, माय deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिलाभ|भूरिलाभः
भूरिलाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Very profitable or beneficial.<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Great gain.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि, and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिशस्
भूरिशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Manifold, many by many.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि many, शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुण्डी
भूरुण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>A sort of sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, रुह to grow; or रुद्ध to oppose, क aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुह|भूरुहः
भूरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्ज|भूर्ज|भूर्जः
भूर्ज्ज<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>The Bhoj or Bhojpatra, a tree growing in the snowy mountains, a kind of birch; the bark is used for writing on, and very generally for Hooka snakes.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and ऊर्ज्ज to be strong or hardy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्जकण्डक
भूर्ज्जकण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of one of the inferior or mixed classes, sprung from an outcast Brahman by a woman of the same tribe.<BR>E.<BR>भूर्ज्ज the Bhoj, and कण्ठ the throat, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्जपत्र|भूर्जपत्र|भूर्जपत्रः|भूर्ज्जपत्रः
भूर्ज्जपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The Bhojpatra: see भूर्ज्ज.<BR>E.<BR>भूर्ज्ज as above, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्णि|भूर्णिः
भूर्णि<BR>f. (-र्णिः)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A desart, a country ill supplied with water.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, Uṇādi aff. नि, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्लोक|भूर्लोकः
भूर्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The earth, the habitation of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>भूः the earth, and लोक the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलता
भूलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A worm, an earthworm.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशक्र|भूशक्रः
भूशक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and शक्र INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशुद्धि|भूशुद्धिः
भूशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Purifying the ground by sweeping, burning, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and शुद्धि purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूश्रवस्
भूश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>An ant or mole hill.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and श्रु to exude, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष
भूष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भूषति भूषयति)<BR>To decorate, to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषण|भूषणं|भूषणः
भूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ornament, embellishment.<BR>E.<BR>भूष to adorn, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषयितव्य
भूषयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be decorated or ornamented.<BR>E.<BR>भष, and तव्य aff.; also भूषणीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषा
भूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Adorning, decorating with trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भूष to adorn, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषित|भूषितः
भूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Adorned, decorated, dressed.<BR>E.<BR>भूष to adorn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Being, existing.<BR>2 Being well, faring well.<BR>E.<BR>भू to be, स्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुत|भूसुतः
भूसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>SĪTĀ the wife of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and सुत the offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्तृण|भूस्तृणं|भूस्तृणः
भूस्तृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schænanthus.)<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, तृण grass, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्पृश्
भूस्पृश्<BR>m. (-स्पृक)<BR>Man, a man, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>भू the earth, and स्पृश् who touches: see भूमिस्पृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वर्ग|भूस्वर्गः
भूस्वर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The mountain Sumeru.<BR>E.<BR>भू, and स्वर्ग paradise; a heaven on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वामिन्
भूस्वामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A landlord, a landholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ<BR>(ञ्) भृञ् r. 1st cl. (भरति-ते) (डु ञ्) डुभृञ् r. 3rd cl. (विभर्त्ति विभृते)<BR>1 To nourish, to cherish, to foster, to maintain.<BR>2 To fill.<BR>3 To hold or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंस|भृकुंसः
भृकुंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A male actor or dancer in female apparel.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रु an eye-brow, कुसि to speak, aff. अच्, रु changed to ऋ; also with कन् added भृकुंसक, and रु unchanged भ्रकुंस; also from कुशि, भृकुंश, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटि|भृकुटिः
भृकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>A frown, a contraction of the brows.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रु the eye-brow, कुट to be or make crooked, aff. कि, and ङीप् optionally added, भृ substituted for भ्रु; otherwise भ्रुकुटि, भ्रुकुटी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगु|भृगुः
भृगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>1 The name of a celebrated Muni, and one of the ten Brahmādikas or Prajāpatis, the sons of BRAHMĀ, and first created of beings.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>3 ŚUKRA, the regent of VENUS.<BR>4 A precipice.<BR>5 Table land, the level summit of a mountain.<BR>6 The Ṛṣi JAMADAGNI, the father of PARAŚURĀMA and grandson of the Muni BHṚGU.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry (in religious fervour), Uṇādi aff. कु; र is changed to ऋ, the स rejected, and the final ज becomes ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=625" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुपति|भृगुपतिः
भृगुपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The hero, and Avatar PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भृगु implying the race of BHṚGU or JAMADAGNI, and पति master, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुसुत|भृगुसुतः
भृगुसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 ŚUKRA or VENUS, the son of the Muni BHṚGU, and the preceptor of the DAITYAS.<BR>2 The hero PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>भृगु the saint BHṚGU, or his descendant JAMADAGNI, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगूणाम्पति|भृगूणांपति
भृगूणाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The first of the three incarnations of VIṢṆU called RĀMAS; PARAŚURĀMA the son of JAMADAGNI.<BR>E.<BR>भृगु in the sixth case plural, and पति master, chief of the BHṚGUS or race of BHṚGU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्ग|भृंग|भृङ्गं|भृंगः|भृङ्गः
भृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A large black bee, the humble bee.<BR>2 A catamite, a libertine, a lecher.<BR>3 A plant, (Eclipta or Verbesina prostrata.)<BR>4 A wasp, either the common kind, or the Vespa solitaria.<BR>5 A golden vase.<BR>6 The fork-tailed shrike, (Lanius cærulescens.)<BR>7 A bird, apparently a sort of shrike different from the preceding.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Woody cassia.<BR>2 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, गन् Uṇādi aff., and नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गक|भृंगकः|भृङ्गकः
भृङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird, a sort of shrike, (Lanius malabaricus.)<BR>E.<BR>कन्, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गज|भृंगज|भृङ्गजं
भृङ्गज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गपर्णिका|भृंगपर्णिका
भृङ्गपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Small or Guzerati cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरजस्
भृङ्गरजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>Eclipta prostrata: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गराज|भृङ्गराजः
भृङ्गराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A spreading shrub, (Eclipta or Verbesina prostrata, or perhaps more properly, Verbesina scandens.)<BR>2 A sort of bird, apparently the variety of shrike termed Malabar, (Lanius malabaricus).<BR>3 The humble bee.<BR>4 A particular sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग a bee, and राज to shine, aff. अच्; or with रजस dust, भृङ्गरजस्; and with राजन् shining, ruling, भृङ्गराजन् m. (-जा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरिट
भृङ्गरिट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>One of ŚIVA'S door-keepers.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग a bee, रट to speak or make a noise, to buzz, aff. अच्, and the penultimate changed to इ; also with इन् aff., and the penultimate long or short, the word is read भृङ्गरिटि, भृङ्गरीट, and भृङ्गरीटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरोल|भृंगरोल|भृङ्गरोलः
भृङ्गरोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग a bee, रु to cry, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गवल्लभ|भृंगवल्लभ|भृङ्गवल्लभः
भृङ्गवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गसोदर|भृङ्गसोदरः
भृङ्गसोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, apparently a variety of Eclipta or Verbesina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गार|भृंगार|भृंगारं|भृङ्गारं|भृंगारः|भृङ्गारः
भृङ्गार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A golden vase, especially used at royal ceremonials.<BR>2 A shrub, (Eclipta prostrata, &c. see भृङ्गराज.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Cloves.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to contain, (water, &c.) आरन् Uṇādi aff., and गुक् augment; or भृङ्ग a bee, and अरि an enemy; fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गारिका|भृंगारिका
भृङ्गारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग a bee, अरि an enemy, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गावली|भृंगावली
भृङ्गावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A line or flight of bees.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग, and आवली a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गिन्|भृंगिन्
भृङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>One of ŚIVA'S chamberlains.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्ग a bee, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गीफल|भृङ्गीफलः
भृङ्गीफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The hog-plum: see आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गीश|भृङ्गीशः
भृङ्गीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भृङ्गी the attendant of the deity, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज
भृज<BR>(ई) भृजी r. 1st cl. (भर्जते)<BR>To parch, to fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्जन|भृज्जनं|भृज्जनः
भृज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A frying pan.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, Uṇādi aff. क्युन्, and the root changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत|भृतः
भृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hired, paid, maintained.<BR>2 Cherished, supported.<BR>3 Filled.<BR>4 Having, being possessed of, or endowed with.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A servant.<BR>2 A hired labourer.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतक|भृतकः
भृतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hired labourer.<BR>2 A servant.<BR>E.<BR>भृत hired, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापक|भृतकाध्यापकः
भृतकाध्यापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hired teacher, one who gives instructions for pay.<BR>E.<BR>भृतक, and अध्यापक a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापित|भृतकाध्यापितः
भृतकाध्यापित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A student who pays his teacher.<BR>E.<BR>भृतक, and अध्यापित instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतभूति
भृतभूति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Prosperous, powerful, exalted.<BR>2 Smeared with ashes.<BR>E.<BR>भृत possessed, and भूति power, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतरन्ध्र
भृतरन्ध्र<BR>mfn. (-न्ध्रः-न्ध्रा-न्ध्रं)<BR>Filled up, (as a hole or depression.)<BR>E.<BR>भृत, and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृति|भृतिः
भृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 Capital, principal.<BR>3 Nourishment, maintenance.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिभुज्
भृतिभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A hired labourer or servant.<BR>E.<BR>भृति hire, भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be nourished or maintained.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A dependant.<BR>2 A servant, a slave.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Hire, wages.<BR>E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. क्यप्, with तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यत्व|भृत्यत्वं
भृत्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Servitude, service, dependance.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, भृत्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यध्यापन
भृत्यध्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Teaching, (especially the Vedas,) for hire.<BR>E.<BR>भृति, and अध्यापन instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभरण
भृत्यभरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Maintaining or cherishing dependants, servants, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and भरण nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभर्त्तृ|भृत्यभर्तृ
भृत्यभर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A master of a family taking good care of his dependants.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and भर्त्तृ who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवात्सल्य
भृत्यवात्सल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Kindness to dependants or servants.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and वात्सल्य tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यविनिवेश
भृत्यविनिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Fixing or planting firmly.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and विनिवेश placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवृत्ति|भृत्यवृत्तिः
भृत्यवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Maintenance of servants or dependants.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यशालिन्
भृत्यशालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having many servants.<BR>E.<BR>भृत्य, and शालिन् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृमि|भृमिः
भृमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A whirlwind, a hurricane, a high wind.<BR>2 An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, इन् Uṇādi aff., and the semivowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश|भृशं
भृश<BR>(इर्, उ) इर् भृशु r. 4th cl. (भृश्यति)<BR>To fall, to fall down, literally or figuratively, as from a height, from dignity or virtue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश|भृशं
भृश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Much, exceeding.<BR>n. adv. (-शं)<BR>Much, exceedingly.<BR>ind. (भृशम्)<BR>1 Much.<BR>2 Eminently, superiorly, better.<BR>3 Repeatedly.<BR>4 Beautifully.<BR>E.<BR>भृश to fall, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृशस्विद्
भृशस्विद्<BR>mfn. (-स्विद्)<BR>Perspiring violently.<BR>E.<BR>भृश, and स्विद् to sweat, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्ट|भृष्टः
भृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Fried.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, aff. क्त, the vowel substituted for the semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टान्न|भृष्टान्नं
भृष्टान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Rice boiled, and then fried.<BR>E.<BR>भृष्ट fried, अन्न boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=626" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टि|भृष्टिः
भृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Frying.<BR>2 An uninhabited or lonely garden, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, aff. क्तिन्, the semivowel changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भॄ
भॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (भृणाति^1)<BR>1 To blame or censure.<BR>2 To nourish, to maintain, to support.<BR>3 To hold.<BR>4 To fry.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: cf wil1819, mw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेक|भेकः
भेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 The female of the frog, or a small frog.<BR>2 A kind of creeper, (Hydrocotyle Asiatica.)<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकपर्णी
भेकपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A creeper, (Hydrocotyle Asiatica.)<BR>E.<BR>भेक a frog, and पर्ण a leaf; resembling the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकभुज्
भेकभुज्<BR>m. (-क्)<BR>A serpent, a snake.<BR>E.<BR>भेक, and भुज who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेड|भेडः
भेड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A ram, a sheep.<BR>2 A raft, a float.<BR>3 The name of a saint.<BR>f. (-डी)<BR>A ewe.<BR>E.<BR>भिल a Sautra root, to separate, aff. अच्, and ल changed to ड; also with कन् added, भेडक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेतव्य
भेतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be feared or apprehended.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तृ
भेत्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ)<BR>Who or what divides, disunites, &c.<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>1 A divider or separator.<BR>2 A factious or seditious man, a traitor, or one who secretly corresponds with an enemy, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to divide, to sow dissension, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद|भेदः
भेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Dividing, separating.<BR>2 Tearing, rending, breaking, &c.<BR>3 Distinction, kind, sort, species, difference.<BR>4 Disunion, disagreement.<BR>5 Sowing dissension, breaking the unanimity of confederates, one of the means of success against an opponent.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to divide, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदक|भेदकः
भेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A breaker, who or what breaks or divides.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mischief-maker.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदकर
भेदकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Separating, disuniting.<BR>2 Causing dissension.<BR>E.<BR>भेद, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदन|भेदनं|भेदनः
भेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Dividing, separating, literally or figuratively, as tearing, breaking, specifying, discriminating, causing separation or dissension, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदप्रत्यय|भेदप्रत्ययः
भेदप्रत्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Belief in the reality of the multiform appearances of the world, in opposition to the doctrine that every thing is GOD.<BR>E.<BR>भेद difference, प्रत्यय faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदित|भेदितः
भेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Divided, separated, literally or figuratively.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, aff. क्त; also भिन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिन्
भेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Who or what divides, &c.<BR>2 Having a distinction or division.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>The ratan.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to divide, धिनुण् aff. or भेद sort, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिर|भेदिरं
भेदिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदुर|भेदुरं
भेदुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to split, (rocks, &c.) उरच् aff.; also भिदुर, and भेदिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद्य|भेद्यं
भेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 To be broken.<BR>2 To be divided, pierced, cut, &c.<BR>3 To be disconcerted or deterred.<BR>4 To be set at variance or disunited.<BR>E.<BR>भिद to break, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेन|भेनः
भेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>भ a star, a planet, and इन a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरि|भेरिः
भेरि<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A kettle drum.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, to cause fear, Uṇādi aff. कीन्; otherwise, रन् aff., and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्ड|भेरुंड|भेरुण्डं|भेरुण्डः
भेरुण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Formidable, fearful.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>One of the Yakṣiṇīs, or female attendants on DURGĀ.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A particular deity; a form of ŚIVA, according to the Tantras.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Conception, impregnation.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, deriv. irr.; it is sometimes read भेरण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेल|भेलं|भेलः
भेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Ignorant, unwise, foolish.<BR>2 Fearful, timid.<BR>3 Unsteady, figuratively or literally.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A raft, a float.<BR>2 The name of a Muni, the supposed author of some medical works.<BR>E.<BR>भी to fear, Uṇādi aff. रन्, and the final changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेलक|भेलकं|भेलकः
भेलक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेष
भेष<BR>(ऋ) भेषृ r. 1st cl. (भेषति-ते)<BR>1 To fear or dread.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज|भेषजं
भेषज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A remedy, a drug, a medicament.<BR>2 A kind of fennel, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>भेष here interpreted disease, जि to conquer, aff. ड; or भिषज् a root of a particular class, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजाङ्ग|भेषजांग|भेषजाङ्गं
भेषजाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The vehicle or medium in which medicine is administered, as water gruel, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भेषज a drug, and अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष|भैक्षं
भैक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 Alms, what is collected by begging.<BR>2 Begging, mendicancy.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा alms, given and received, aff. अण्; also भैक्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचरण
भैक्षचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Plying for alms, begging.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष, and चरण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचर्य्या|भैक्षचर्या
भैक्षचर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Begging, collecting alms.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष, and चर्य्या practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षजीविका
भैक्षजीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Living upon alms, begging, mendicancy.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष aggregate alms, जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षभुज्
भैक्षभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष alms, and भुज् who subsists; also भैक्षाशिन्, भिक्षाशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाशिन्
भैक्षाशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष, and आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाहार|भैक्षाहारः
भैक्षाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mendicant, one living on charity.<BR>E.<BR>भैक्ष, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष्य|भैक्ष्यं
भैक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>Mendicity, begging.<BR>E.<BR>भिक्षा, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरव|भैरवं|भैरवः
भैरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Formidable, horrible, terrific.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Horror, the property of exciting terror.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA, but more especially an inferior manifestation or form of the deity, eight of which are called by the common name Bhairava, and are severally termed ASITĀṄGA, RURU, CAṆḌA, KRODHA, UNMATTA, KUPATI, BHĪṢAṆA, and SAṂHĀRA, all alluding to terrific properties of mind or body.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>3 A musical mode; that which is calculated to excite emotions of terror.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name or form of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भीरु fearful, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवकारक
भैरवकारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Formidable.<BR>E.<BR>भैरव, and कारक what causes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज|भैषजं|भैषजः
भैषज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sort of quail.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A medicament.<BR>E.<BR>भिषज a medicament, and अण् referential or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज्य|भैषज्यं
भैषज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>भैषज the same, ञय pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भो
भो<BR>ind.<BR>A vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, डो aff., more commonly भोम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तव्य|भोक्तव्यं
भोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be used or enjoyed.<BR>2 To be eaten.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, &c., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृ
भोक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>1 Enjoying, an enjoyer.<BR>2 An eater.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, &c., aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृत्व|भोक्तृत्वं
भोक्तृत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Possession, enjoyment.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=627" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्ष्यमाण
भोक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being about to eat.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, and शानच् aff., here of the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग|भोगः
भोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>4 Eating.<BR>5 A snake's body.<BR>6 A snake's expanded hood.<BR>7 Hire.<BR>8 The hire of dancing girls or courtezans.<BR>9 A snake.<BR>10 An army in column.<BR>11 (In arithmetic,) The numerator of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगुच्छ
भोगगुच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>Price paid to harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगृह|भोगगृहं
भोगगृह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The inner or private apartment, the haram.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपति|भोगपतिः
भोगपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A viceroy, a governor.<BR>2 A person having possession or usufruct.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपाल|भोगपालः
भोगपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A groom.<BR>E.<BR>भोग pleasure, and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपिशाचिका
भोगपिशाचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Hunger.<BR>E.<BR>भोग eating, पिशाचिका an imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभूमि|भोगभूमिः
भोगभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Svarga or paradise.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and भूमि soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभृतक|भोगभृतकः
भोगभृतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A servant or slave, who works for maintenance only.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and भृत्तक a hireling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगलाभ|भोगलाभः
भोगलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Interest or profit made by the use of any thing pledged.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवत्|भोगवन्त्
भोगवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Enjoying, having enjoyment.<BR>2 Delightful, pleasurable, yielding enjoyment.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 Dancing, acting.<BR>3 Singing.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The capital of the Nāgas, or serpents.<BR>2 The Ganges of the lower regions.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, aff. मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगसद्मन्
भोगसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>The inner apartment, the haram.<BR>E.<BR>भोग pleasure, and सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगस्थान
भोगस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The body as the seat, of sensual enjoyment.<BR>2 A haram, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्ह
भोगार्ह<BR>n. (-र्हं)<BR>Wealth, property.<BR>E.<BR>भोग, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावली
भोगावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Praise, eulogium, the panegyric of professional encomiasts or bards.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, आवली a row or range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावास|भोगावासः
भोगावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The haram, the inner or women's apartment.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिक|भोगिकः
भोगिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A horse-keeper, a groom.<BR>E.<BR>भोग pleasure, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिकान्त|भोगिकांत|भोगिकान्तः
भोगिकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>भोगि a snake, and कान्त friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
भोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Enjoying, possessing, an enjoyer, &c.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A king, a prince.<BR>3 A barber.<BR>4 The head man of a village.<BR>5 A person who accumulates money for a particular expenditure.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The capital of the Nāgas.<BR>2 A royal concubine.<BR>E.<BR>भोग enjoyment, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिवल्लभ|भोगिवल्लभं
भोगिवल्लभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>भोगिन् a snake, वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगीन्द्र|भोगींद्र|भोगीन्द्रः
भोगीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The serpent ANANTA.<BR>E.<BR>भोगि a snake, इन्द्र a sovereign; also भोगीश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्य|भोग्यं
भोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>To be enjoyed.<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>1 Wealth.<BR>2 Grain.<BR>f. (-ग्या)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज|भोजः
भोज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A country, Patna and Bhāgalpur.<BR>2 The name of a sovereign of Oujein, who is supposed to have flourished about the end of the tenth century; he was a celebrated patron of learned men, and the nine gems, or poets, and philosophers, are often ascribed to his æra.<BR>3 A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, aff. अच्, and the final consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजकट|भोजकटः
भोजकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The country of Bhoja, the present Bhojpur, or the vicinity of Patna and Bhāgalpur.<BR>E.<BR>भोज the same, and कट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजन|भोजनं|भोजनः
भोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनविशेष|भोजनविशेषः
भोजनविशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Choice food, a delicacy.<BR>E.<BR>भोजन, and विशेष superior sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनव्यग्र
भोजनव्यग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Straitened for food.<BR>E.<BR>भोजन, and व्यग्र anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनाधिकार|भोजनाधिकारः
भोजनाधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Commissariat, stewardship, charge of provender.<BR>E.<BR>भोजन, and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनीय
भोजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be enjoyed.<BR>2 To be eaten.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Food.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to enjoy, aff. अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयित्वा
भोजयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having fed.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजाधिप|भोजाधिपः
भोजाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A name of KARṆA, the half brother of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>भोज Bhāgalpur, and अधिप sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्य|भोज्यं
भोज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>To be eaten, edible.<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Food.<BR>E.<BR>भुज to eat, ण्यत् aff., and the final unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यसम्भव|भोज्यसंभव|भोज्यसंभवः|भोज्यसम्भवः
भोज्यसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Chyle, the primary juice of the body.<BR>E.<BR>भोज्य food, and सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटाङ्ग|भोटांग|भोटाङ्गः
भोटाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A country, probably Butan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोभो
भोभो<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of calling or addressing.<BR>E.<BR>भो as above, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोमीरा
भोमीरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलि|भोलिः
भोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, उलिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोस्
भोस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of calling or addressing.<BR>2 An interrogative particle.<BR>E.<BR>भा to shine, aff. डोस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत|भौतः
भौत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>1 Demoniac, relating to sprites or goblins.<BR>2 Elemental.<BR>3 Relating to existing beings.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An attendant upon idols.<BR>2 A worshipper of sprites and goblins.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a goblin, &c., aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिक|भौतिकं|भौतिकः
भौतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating or appertaining to evil spirits.<BR>2 Elemental.<BR>3 Existent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>भूत a sprite, &c., and टक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Earthly, terrestrial, produced in or relating to the earth.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 Hell.<BR>3 Ambergris.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि the earth, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमरत्न|भौमरत्नं
भौमरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>भौम, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमिक|भौमिकः
भौमिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Earthly, terrestrial.<BR>E.<BR>भूमि, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिक|भौरिकः
भौरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The superintendant of gold, the treasurer.<BR>E.<BR>भूरि gold, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्यस
भ्यस<BR>r. 1st cl. (भ्यसते)<BR>To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश|भ्रंशः
भ्रंश<BR>(उ) भ्रंशु r. 4th cl. (भ्रंश्यति)<BR>To fall down; also भ्रंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश|भ्रंशः
भ्रंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Falling, declining from a height, or from propriety.<BR>2 Falling from or off.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रंश to fall, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंस|भ्रंसः
भ्रंस<BR>(उ) भ्रंसु r. 1st cl. (भ्रंसते)<BR>To fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुंस|भ्रकुंसः
भ्रकुंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An actor wearing female apparel.<BR>E.<BR>भ्र for भ्रू the eye-brow, and कुशि or कुसि to speak, aff. अच्; hence also भ्रकुंश, भ्रूकुंस, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुटि|भ्रकुटिः
भ्रकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>A frown.<BR>E.<BR>भ्र for भ्रू the eye-brow, कुट to curve, aff. इन्; also भ्रुकुटि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रण
भ्रण<BR>r. 1st cl. (भ्रणति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम|भ्रमः
भ्रम<BR>(उ) भ्रमु r. 1st cl. (भ्रमति भ्रम्यति)<BR>1 To turn round, to move circularly.<BR>2 To be unsteady or unfixed.<BR>3 To roam, to wander; it is also figuratively applicable to mental [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">Page629</a>] unsteadiness, as to err, to wander, to be ignorant or mistaken, &c.<BR>With परि,<BR>To wander about.<BR>With वि,<BR>To play, to wanton.<BR>With सम्,<BR>1 To hurry.<BR>2 To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=628" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम|भ्रमः
भ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Whirling, going round.<BR>2 Straying, roaming.<BR>3 Error, ignorance, mistake, misapprehension.<BR>4 A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR>5 A drain, a water-course.<BR>6 A lathe, a potter's wheel, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to go round, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमण|भ्रमणं
भ्रमण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Whirling, going round.<BR>2 Wandering, literally or figuratively.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A leech.<BR>2 A sort of game, performed by women for the amusement of a lover or husband.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to go round, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्
भ्रमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>1 Going round, whirling, revolving.<BR>2 Roving.<BR>3 Erring.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्कुटी
भ्रमत्कुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>An umbrella, a concave mat carried on the head for that purpose, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमत्, and कुटी a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमर|भ्रमरः
भ्रमर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>What whirls or goes round.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A large black bee.<BR>2 A lecher, a lover.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Vertigo, epilepsy.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to go round, aff. करन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरक|भ्रमरकः
भ्रमरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Hair curled upon the forehead.<BR>2 A bee.<BR>3 A ball for playing with.<BR>4 A whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमर a bee, &c., कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकीट|भ्रमरकीटः
भ्रमरकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of wasp, that builds a solitary nest in the angles of walls, doors, &c., (Vespa solitaria.)<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमर a bee, and कीट an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरप्रिय|भ्रमरप्रियः
भ्रमरप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of Kadamba tree.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमर a bee, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरविलसिता
भ्रमरविलसिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A species of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरालक|भ्रमरालकः
भ्रमरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hair curled upon the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमर a bee, and अलक a curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमासक्त|भ्रमासक्तः
भ्रमासक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>An armourer, a sword-cleaner, a knifegrinder.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस a turning instrument, a grindstone, and आसक्त diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमि|भ्रमिः
भ्रमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 Whirling, going round.<BR>2 Error, blunder, mistake.<BR>3 A lathe, a potter's wheel.<BR>4 A whirlpool.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमिन्
भ्रमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>Whirling, going round or about.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to go round, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रश
भ्रश<BR>(उ) भ्रशु r. 4th cl. (भ्रश्यति)<BR>To fall down; also भृश and भ्रंश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट|भ्रष्टं
भ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Fallen, lost.<BR>2 Vicious, depraved, fallen from virtue.<BR>3 Fried, parched.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रंश to fall, or भ्रस्ज to fry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टराज्य
भ्रष्टराज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Deposed, deprived of a kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रष्ट, and राज्य principality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रस्ज
भ्रस्ज<BR>(औ) औभ्रस्ज r. 6th cl. (भ्रज्जति-ते)<BR>To broil or fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज|भ्राजः
भ्राज<BR>(टु, ऋ) टुभ्राजृ r. 1st cl. (भ्राजते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजक|भ्राजकं
भ्राजक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>E.<BR>भ्राज to shine, aff. ण्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथु|भ्राजथुः
भ्राजथु<BR>f. (-थुः)<BR>Brilliance, splendour, beauty.<BR>E.<BR>भ्राज to shine, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथुमत्|भ्राजथुमन्त्
भ्राजथुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Splendid.<BR>2 Beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>भ्राजथु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णु|भ्राजिष्णुः
भ्राजिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Elegant, splendid, radiant in ornament and vesture.<BR>E.<BR>भ्राज to shine, aff. इष्णुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृ
भ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A brother, a uterine brother.<BR>Dual only, (-रौ)<BR>Brother and sister.<BR>E.<BR>भ्राज to shine, Uṇādi aff. तृच्, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृक|भ्रातृकः
भ्रातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Fraternal, brotherly, of or belonging to a brother.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृज|भ्रातृजः
भ्रातृज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A brother's son.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृजाया
भ्रातृजाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A sister-in-law, a brother's wife.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and जाया a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृपत्नी
भ्रातृपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A brother's wife.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ, and पत्नी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृभगिन्यौ
भ्रातृभगिन्यौ<BR>dual only, (-न्यौ)<BR>A brother and sister.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and भगिनी a sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृवल
भ्रातृवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having a brother.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रतृ, and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृव्य|भ्रातृव्यः
भ्रातृव्य<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>1 A brother's son.<BR>2 An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृश्वशुर|भ्रातृश्वशुरः
भ्रातृश्वशुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A husband's elder brother.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and श्वशुर a father-in-law, (as it were.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीय|भ्रात्रीयः
भ्रात्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fraternal, belonging or relating to a brother.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A brother's son.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रातृ a brother, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त|भ्रांत|भ्रान्तः
भ्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Whirled, revolved.<BR>2 Blundering, mistaken.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to revolve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्ति|भ्रांति|भ्रांतिः|भ्रान्तिः
भ्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Error, mistake, ignorance.<BR>2 Going round, whirling, revolving.<BR>3 Unsteadiness, locomotion.<BR>4 Going about, wandering.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to go round, aff. क्तिन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिमत्|भ्रांतिमत्|भ्रान्तिमन्त्
भ्रान्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Erring, mistaking.<BR>2 Wandering.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रान्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिहर|भ्रांतिहर|भ्रान्तिहरः
भ्रान्तिहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रान्ति error, and हर who repels or removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम|भ्रामः
भ्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Wandering, roving.<BR>2 Error.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामक|भ्रामकः
भ्रामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>2 A cheat, a rogue.<BR>3 A sort of loadstone.<BR>4 The sun-flower.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामयत्
भ्रामयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Whirling round.<BR>2 Bewildering.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to wander or whirl, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामर|भ्रामरं|भ्रामरः
भ्रामर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Whirling, going round.<BR>2 A dance performed in a ring, dancing round-about.<BR>3 A village.<BR>4 Epilepsy.<BR>5 Honey.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of loadstone.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of PĀRVATĪ, from her having assumed the form of a bee, in order to contend with MAHĀSURA.<BR>2 A Yoginī, or female attendant on DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रमर a bee, &c. aff., अण् or अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरिन्
भ्रामरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Whirling, revolving.<BR>2 Epileptic, giddy.<BR>3 Made of honey or from a bee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रामर, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम्यत्
भ्राम्यत्<BR>mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-भ्यत्)<BR>1 Wandering about. roving, roaming.<BR>2 Erring, deviating.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to wander, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश
भ्राश<BR>(टु, ऋ) टुभ्राशृ r. 1st cl. (भ्राशते भ्राश्यते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं|भ्राष्ट्रः
भ्राष्ट्र<BR>mfn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Fried in a pan.<BR>mn. (ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्रं)<BR>A frying pan.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रस्ज to fry, Uṇādi aff. ष्ट्रन्; and in the attributive, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्री
भ्री<BR>r. 9th cl. (भ्रीणाति भ्रिणीते)<BR>1 To fear.<BR>2 To hold.<BR>3 To cherish, to maintain or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुंस|भ्रुकुंसः
भ्रुकुंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An actor in female apparel.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रु for भ्रू an eyebrow, कुसि or कुशि to shine or speak, aff. अच्; hence also भ्रुकुंश, भ्रूकुंस, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुटि|भ्रुकुटिः
भ्रुकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>A frown.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रु for भ्र an eye-brow, कुट to make crooked, इन् aff.: see भ्रूकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुड
भ्रुड<BR>r. 1st cl. (भ्रुडति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रू
भ्रू<BR>f. (भ्रूः)<BR>An eye-brow.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रम to turn round, Uṇādi aff. डू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=629" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुंस|भ्रूकुंसः
भ्रूकुंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A male actor in female apparel.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रू the eyebrow, कुसि to speak or shine, aff. अच्; also from कुशि, भ्रूकुंश; this word is variously written भ्रुकुंश or भ्रुकुंस, भृकुंश or भृकुंस, and भ्रकुंश or भ्रकुंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुटि|भ्रूकुटिः
भ्रूकुटि<BR>f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>A frown, a look of displeasure.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रू the brow, कुट to be curved, aff. इन्, and ङीप् optionally added; it is also written variously, like the last, and occurs भ्रुकुटि, भृकुटि, or भ्रकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूक्षेप|भ्रूक्षेपः
भ्रूक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A frown.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रू, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण|भ्रूणः
भ्रूण<BR>r. 10th cl. (भ्रूणयते)<BR>1 To hope, to trust.<BR>2 To confide, to be without doubt.<BR>3 To wish for, to desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण|भ्रूणः
भ्रूण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The embryo or fœtus, a child.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रूण to hope, to fear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणघ्न
भ्रूणघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Producing or causing abortion, who or what does so.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रूण, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहत्या
भ्रूणहत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>1 Murder of the fœtus, procuring or causing abortion.<BR>2 Any sin equally heinous.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रूण, and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहन्
भ्रूणहन्<BR>mf. (-हा-घ्नी)<BR>1 One who occasions or procures abortion.<BR>2 The murderer of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रूण the embryo, (or any thing of which the death is equally heinous,) and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूभङ्ग|भ्रूभंग|भ्रूभङ्गः
भ्रूभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A frown.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रू the brow, भङ्ग a breaking, a bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेज
भ्रेज<BR>(ऋ) भ्रेजृ r. 1st cl. (भ्रेजते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष|भ्रेषः
भ्रेष<BR>(ऋ) भ्रेषृ r. 1st cl. (भ्रेषते)<BR>To go, to move, to fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष|भ्रेषः
भ्रेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Deviation from rectitude, declining or falling from virtue, &c.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 Loss.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रेष to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेषण|भ्रेषणं
भ्रेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>भ्रेष to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लक्ष
भ्लक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (भ्लक्षति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लाश
भ्लाश<BR>(टु ऋ) टु भ्लाशृ r. 1st cl. (भ्लाश्यते भ्लाशते)<BR>To shine; sometimes भ्लास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लेष
भ्लेष<BR>(ऋ) भ्लेषृ r. 1st cl. (भ्लेषति-ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म<BR>The twenty-fifth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, corresponding to the letter M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 VIṢṆU.<BR>4 YAMA.<BR>5 Time, season.<BR>6 Poison, venom.<BR>7 A magical or mystical verse or formula.<BR>8 The moon.<BR>9 The abbreviated name of the fourth note of the gamut.<BR>f. (मा)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A mother.<BR>3 Measure.<BR>4 Light, lustre.<BR>5 Knowledge.<BR>6 Binding, tying.<BR>7 Death.<BR>8 A woman's waist.<BR>n. (मं)<BR>1 Good fortune, auspiciousness.<BR>2 Water.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, or मन to worship, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक
मक<BR>(इ) मकि r. 1st cl. (मङ्कते)<BR>1 To decorate, to grace or adorn.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकर|मकरः
मकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A marine monster, confounded usually with the crocodile and shark, but properly a fabulous animal: as a fish; it might be conjectured to be the horned shark, or the unicorn fish; but it is often drawn, as in the pictured signs of the zodiac, with the head and forelegs of an antelope, and the body and tail of a fish: it is the emblem of the god of love.<BR>2 One of the signs of zodiac, corresponding with CAPRICORN, and like the Greek representation of that sign, being an animal in the foreparts, and ending in the tail of a fish.<BR>3 One of KUVERA'S treasures.<BR>E.<BR>म for मुख the mouth, कृ to scatter, aff. अच्; or माङ् prohibitive aff., कृ to do, अच् aff., form irr.; grammarians however, sometimes consider this word as a primitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरकेतन|मकरकेतनः
मकरकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KĀMA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a marine monster, and केतन emblem; being painted on KĀMA'S banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरकेतु|मकरकेतुः
मकरकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>KĀMA: see the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>मकर, and केतु an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरध्वज|मकरध्वजः
मकरध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KĀMA: see the two last.<BR>E.<BR>मकर the Makara, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्द|मकरंदः|मकरन्दः
मकरन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 The nectar or honey of a flower.<BR>2 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 A bee.<BR>4 A fragrant kind of mango.<BR>5 A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum pubescens.)<BR>6 The filament of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>मकर the emblem of KĀMA, and दो to destroy, i. e. to surpass, as an incentive to love, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्दवती
मकरन्दवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>E.<BR>मकरन्द honey, and मतुप् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराकर|मकराकरः
मकराकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a marine monster, and आकर receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराकार|मकराकारः
मकराकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, said to be a species of Karanja or Cæsalpinia.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a fish, आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराङ्क|मकरांक|मकराङ्कः
मकराङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a marine monster, and अङ्क mark, emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरालय|मकरालयः
मकरालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a sort of fish, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराश्व|मकराश्वः
मकराश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a marine monster, and अश्व a horse; riding on the Makara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरिन्
मकरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मकर a marine monster, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुट|मकुटं
मकुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A crest, a head-dress, a crown, a tiara.<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, aff. उट, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुति|मकुतिः
मकुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>An edict or order of the government, addressed to the Śūdra tribe, or to a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुर|मकुरः
मकुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mirror.<BR>2 The stick of a potter's wheel.<BR>3 An unblown flower.<BR>4 A tree with light yellow, and fragrant flowers, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, उरच् Uṇādi aff., and deriv. irr.; also मुकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुल|मकुलः
मकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An opening bud.<BR>2 A kind of tree, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, उलच् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्टक|मकुष्टकः
मकुष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of kidney-bean, a wild variety perhaps of the Phaseolus mungo.<BR>E.<BR>मकु irr. deriv., from मक to adorn, ष्टक to impede, aff. अच्; also मकुष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठ|मकुष्ठः
मकुष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Going lazily, slowly, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A sort of rice.<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, aff. उ, deriv. irr. मकु, and स्था to stand, aff. क; also मुकुष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठक|मकुष्ठकः
मकुष्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean.<BR>E.<BR>मकु ornament: (see the two last); स्था to stay or be, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकूलक|मकूलकः
मकूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti.<BR>E.<BR>मक to adorn, ऊलच् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्क
मक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (-मक्कते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कल|मक्कलः
मक्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A mineral substance, considered variously to be chalk or benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>मक्क to go, to be, aff. ऊलच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=630" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कोल|मक्कोलः
मक्कोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Chalk: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल to go, ओलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (मक्षति)<BR>1 To fill.<BR>2 To be angry.<BR>3 To mix, to combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Hypocrisy, slyness, concealment of one's own defects.<BR>E.<BR>मक्ष to fill, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षिका
मक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fly.<BR>E.<BR>मक्ष to be angry, Uṇādi aff. सिकन्, or मक्ष the same, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षीका
मक्षीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fly.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, the pen. vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख<BR>r. 1st cl. (मखति) also (इ) मखि (मङ्खति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>E.<BR>मख to go, aff. घञ् or घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखत्रातृ
मखत्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>RĀMA, the son of DAŚARATHA, and second incarnation of VIṢṆU so named.<BR>E.<BR>मख sacrifice, and त्रातृ who preserves; his first exploit being the discomfiture of the Rākṣasas, who disturbed the sacrifices of VIŚVAMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखवह्नि|मखवह्निः
मखवह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>मख sacrifice, and वह्नि fire; also similar compounds, as मखाग्नि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखानल|मखानलः
मखानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>मख, and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखासुहृद्
मखासुहृद्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मख sacrifice, here meaning the sacrifice offered by DAKṢA, and असुहृद् unfriendly; having disturbed the ceremony, and slain the sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग|मगः
मग<BR>(इ) r. 1st cl. (मंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A country, South Behār.<BR>2 An inhabitant of that country.<BR>3 A bard, whose peculiar province is to sing the praises of a chief's ancestry in his presence, a family bard or minstrel.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Long pepper.<BR>E.<BR>मगध a Kaṇḍvādi verb, to ask, aff. अच् or मगध the country, अण् aff., with alteration of the vowel optional; hence also मागध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगधेश्वर|मगधेश्वरः
मगधेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of JARĀSANDHA.<BR>E.<BR>मगध South Behar, and ईश्वर king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्न|मग्नः
मग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Plunged, dived, immersed.<BR>2 Sunk, drowned.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to plunge into water, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ<BR>(इ) मघि r. 1st cl. (मंघते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To begin moving.<BR>3 To begin.<BR>4 To move swiftly.<BR>5 To blame.<BR>6 To game.<BR>7 To cheat, to be addicted to dishonest practices.<BR>(मंघति)<BR>To decorate, to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 One of the Dvīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR>2 A country, that of the modern Mugs, or Arrakan.<BR>3 A drug.<BR>4 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>n. (-घं)<BR>A kind of flower.<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>The tenth lunar asterism, containing five stars figured by a house, apparently α. γ. ζ. η. and ν. Leonis: it is sometimes considered to be confined to the plural number (मघाः).<BR>f. (-घा-घी)<BR>A sort of grain.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. कन्, and ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवत्|मघवन्त्
मघवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मघ happiness, (of paradise or Svarga,) मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवन्
मघवन्<BR>m. (-बा)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 One of the twelve Cakravartīs, or universal monarchs of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>मह to sacrifice, कनिन् Uṇādi aff., and वुक् augment, form irr.; before the vowel affs. of the second case plural, and the last five cases, the व of this word is changed to उ, and thence becomes ओ as usual, as मघोनः, मघोना, मघोने, &c.; also with ङीष् aff. the fem. form is मघोनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभव|मघाभवः
मघाभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The planet VENUS or ŚUKRA.<BR>E.<BR>मघा the asterism, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभू
मघाभू<BR>m. (-भू)<BR>ŚUKRA.<BR>E.<BR>मघा, and भु born: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्किल|मंकिल|मंकिलः|मङ्किलः
मङ्किल<BR>m. (-ल)<BR>A fire in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कुर|मंकुर|मंकुरः|मङ्कुरः
मङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, उरच् aff., and the nasal retained; also मकुर and मुकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तृ
मङ्क्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>1 Bathing or drowning; any thing, or person.<BR>2 Cleaning any thing by immersion.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to bathe, aff. तृच्, and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षण|मंक्षण|मंक्षणं|मङ्क्षणं
मङ्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Cuisses or greaves, armour for the thighs or legs; it is sometimes read मङ्क्षण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षु|मंक्षु
मङ्क्षु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Quickly, swiftly, instantly.<BR>2 Much, exceedingly.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to purify, सु aff., and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षुण|मंक्षुण|मङ्क्षुणं
मङ्क्षुण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Cuisses or greaves, armour for the thighs or legs; in some parts of India a sort of iron chain-work petticoat, coming down to the knees, is still worn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ख|मंख|मंखः|मङ्खः
मङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>A mendicant of a particular order.<BR>E.<BR>मखि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ग|मंग|मंगः|मङ्गः
मङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The head of a boat.<BR>E.<BR>मगि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल|मंगल|मङ्गलं|मङ्गलः
मङ्गल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Lucky, fortunate, prosperous, faring well or happily.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Happiness, good fortune.<BR>2 Preserving property, taking care of what has been gained, prudence, carefulness.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 Burnt offering on various occasions of rejoicing.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A name of UMĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A bent grass, (Panicum dactylon,) with white blossoms.<BR>3 A virtuous and obedient wife.<BR>4 The mother of the fifth Jina or Jaina teacher SUMATI.<BR>5 A species of Cæsalpinia.<BR>E.<BR>मगि to go, अलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलच्छाय|मंगलच्छाय|मङ्गलच्छायः
मङ्गलच्छाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Waved leaf fig tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल prosperous, lucky, and च्छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलपाठक|मंगलपाठक|मङ्गलपाठकः
मङ्गलपाठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bard, an encomiast.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल good fortune, and पाठक who reads or recites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलप्रदा
मङ्गलप्रदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल auspiciousness, and प्रदा bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्य|मंगल्य|मङ्गल्यं|मङ्गल्यः
मङ्गल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness, prosperity, &c.<BR>2 Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>3 Pure, pious.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR>2 The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>3 The Vilva, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>4 A sort of pulse, (Cicer lens.)<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A fragrant sort of Agallochum or aloe wood.<BR>2 A kind of Mimosa, (M. Suma, Rox.)<BR>3 A herb, commonly Gojihva, (Hieracium, or according to Rox.'s Catalogue, a herb of the same class, Elephantopus scaber.)<BR>4 A sort of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>5 A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>6 A sort of perfume, commonly Rochana.<BR>7 A kind of Orris root, (Acorus calamus.)<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Sour curds.<BR>2 Sandal.<BR>3 Red lead.<BR>4 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल prosperous, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्यक|मंगल्यक|मंगल्यकः|मङ्गल्यकः
मङ्गल्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Lentils, (Cicer lens.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्यनामधेया
मङ्गल्यनामधेया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल्य auspicious, नामधेया appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गिनी|मंगिनी
मङ्गिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्ग the head of a boat, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच
मच<BR>also (इ) मचि r. 1st cl. (मचते मञ्चते)<BR>1 To be vain or proud.<BR>2 To be wicked.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>4 To pound or grind.<BR>मचि r. 1st cl. (मञ्चते)<BR>1 To hold or have.<BR>2 To be high or tall.<BR>3 To revere, to adore, to worship.<BR>4 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=631" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचर्च्चिका|मचर्चिका
मचर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Excellence, happiness.<BR>2 (In apposition,) Best, excellent, (the gender is unchanged.)<BR>E.<BR>म ŚIVA, चर्च्च to worship, aff. ण्वुल् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्चित्त
मच्चित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Who or what has the mind fixed on me, (God.)<BR>E.<BR>मत् me, चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्छ|मच्छः
मच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A fish in general.<BR>E.<BR>मद to delight, and श aff., form irr.: see मत्स्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जकृत्
मज्जकृत्<BR>n. (-कृत्)<BR>A bone.<BR>E.<BR>मज्ज marrow, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जत्
मज्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जती-ज्जत्)<BR>Plunging in or into, being immersed, dipping, drowning.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to be immersed, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन्
मज्जन्<BR>m. (-ज्जा)<BR>1 The marrow of the bones and flesh.<BR>2 The pith or sap of trees, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to be immersed, (in the centre of the bones, &c.) and कनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन|मज्जनं|मज्जनः
मज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bathing, ablution.<BR>2 Immersion.<BR>3 Drowning.<BR>4 Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to bathe, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जसमुद्भव|मज्जसमुद्भवं|मज्जसमुद्भवः
मज्जसमुद्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Semen genitale.<BR>E.<BR>मज्ज marrow, समुद्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जा
मज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>Marrow, pith, sap.<BR>E.<BR>मज्जन् marrow, and टाप् aff.: see मज्जन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जारजस्
मज्जारजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 A hell.<BR>2 Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जिका
मज्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The female of the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जूषा
मज्जूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A basket.<BR>E.<BR>see मञ्जूषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च|मंच|मंचः|मञ्चः
मञ्च<BR>(उ) मञ्चु r. 1st cl. (मञ्चति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च|मंच|मंचः|मञ्चः
मञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>1 A bed, a bedstead.<BR>2 A platform, a scaffold.<BR>3 An elevated shed raised on bambus in a cornfield, &c., where a watchman is stationed to protect the corn from cattle, birds, wild beasts, &c.<BR>4 A sort of throne or chair of state, or the platform on which it is raised, the dais.<BR>E.<BR>मचि to be high or tall, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चक|मंचक|मंचकं|मञ्चकः
मञ्चक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bed, a bedstead.<BR>2 A platform, a scaffold.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चकाश्रय|मंचकाश्रय|मञ्चकाश्रयः
मञ्चकाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bug.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्चक a bed, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चमण्डप|मञ्चमण्डपः
मञ्चमण्डप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A sort of temporary open shed, a platform erected for particular ceremonies, as marriages, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्च a scaffold, and मण्डप a temporary hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्ज
मञ्ज<BR>r. 10th cl. (मञ्जयति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To clean, to purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जर|मंजर|मंजरं|मञ्जरं
मञ्जर<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>1 A pearl.<BR>2 A compound pedicle.<BR>3 A sort of plant, commonly Tilaka.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, ऋ to go or be, aff. अप्, deriv. irr: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरि|मंजरि|मंजरिः|मञ्जरिः
मञ्जरि<BR>f. (-रिः-री)<BR>1 A compound pedicle, a fruit or flower stalk.<BR>2 A large pearl.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Tilaka.<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A shoot, a sprout.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, ऋ to go or be, aff. इ, deriv. irr., ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरित|मंजरित
मञ्जरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mounted on a stalk, (a bud, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जा|मंजा
मञ्जा<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>1 A compound pedicle: see the last.<BR>2 A she-goat.<BR>E.<BR>मजि to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जि|मंजि|मंजिः|मञ्जिः
मञ्जि<BR>f. (-ञ्जिः-ञ्जी)<BR>A compound pedicle; also मञ्जरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिका|मंजिका
मञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिफला|मंजिफला
मञ्जिफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The plantain, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जि a foot-stalk, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिमन्|मंजिमन्
मञ्जिमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Beauty, elegance.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु handsome, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठा|मंजिष्ठा
मञ्जिष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>Bengal madder, a plant used in medicine, and in dying, (Rubia manjith, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, स्था to stay or be, क aff., deriv. irr.; or मञ्जि a compound pedicle, and स्थ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठाराग|मंजिष्ठाराग|मञ्जिष्ठारागः
मञ्जिष्ठाराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The dye of madder.<BR>2 Permanent attachment.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा, and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जीर|मंजीर|मंजीरं|मंजीरः|मञ्जीरः
मञ्जीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A post, round which passes the string that works the stick of a churn.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्ज to sound, aff. ईरन्; also with कन् added, मञ्जीरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जील|मंजील|मंजीलः|मञ्जीलः
मञ्जील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A village, inhabited chiefly by washermen.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्ज to sound, ईरन् aff., and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जु|मंजु
मञ्जु<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जुः-ञ्जुः-ञ्जु)<BR>Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>E.<BR>मजि to sound, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुकेशिन्|मंजुकेशिन्
मञ्जुकेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Beautiful-haired.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA, or VIṢṆU in that form.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, केश hair, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुगमना|मंजुगमना
मञ्जुगमना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, elegant, and गमन gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुघोष|मञ्जुघोषः
मञ्जुघोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Having a sweet voice or cry.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>One of the Bauddha teachers.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>One of the Apsaras or courtezans of Svarga.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु agreeable, and घोष sound, voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुनाशी|मंजुनाशी
मञ्जुनाशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 The wife of INDRA.<BR>3 A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, and नाश destruction; putting every other beauty to shame by their superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुप्राण|मंजुप्राण|मञ्जुप्राणः
मञ्जुप्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु pleasing, and प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुभद्र|मञ्जुभद्रः
मञ्जुभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A Bauddha; also called Mañjughoṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुभाषिन्
मञ्जुभाषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Speaking sweetly or pleasantly.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A woman speaking kindly.<BR>2 A species of Atijagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु, and भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुल|मंजुल|मञ्जुलं|मञ्जुलः
मञ्जुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Beautiful, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gallinule<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A natural water-course or channel.<BR>2 An arbor, a bower.<BR>3 An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु handsome, ला to be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुवक्त्र|मंजुवक्त्र
मञ्जुवक्त्र<BR>mfn. (-क्त्रः-क्त्रा-क्त्रं)<BR>Lovely, handsome.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जु beautiful, वक्त्र the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुश्री
मञ्जुश्री<BR>m. (-श्रीः)<BR>A Bauddha saint: see मञ्जुघोष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जूषा|मंजूषा
मञ्जूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A basket, a large basket.<BR>2 A stone.<BR>3 Bengal madder.<BR>4 The case in which the great bow that RĀMA broke, was kept.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to make pure or clean by ablution, Uṇādi aff. ऊषन्, and the nasal augment; also with a short vowel मञ्जुषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटती
मटती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटस्फटि|मटस्फटिः
मटस्फटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>Incipient pride (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मट्टक|मट्टकं
मट्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The ridge of a thatch.<BR>2 A sort of grain, (Eleusine corocana.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ|मठं|मठः
मठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (मठति)<BR>1 To be confused or disturbed in mind.<BR>2 To dwell, to inhabit.<BR>(इ) मठि r. 1st cl. (मंठते)<BR>To bewail, to regret, to remember with sorrow or regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ|मठं|मठः
मठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 A school, a college, the residence of young Brahmans, prosecuting sacred studies.<BR>2 A building inhabited by ascetics of the same order.<BR>3 A temple.<BR>4 A cart, a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>मठ to dwell, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=632" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठर|मठरः
मठर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>E.<BR>मत to respect, Uṇādi aff. अरच्, and ठ substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड
मड<BR>(इ) मडि r. 1st cl. (मण्डते)<BR>1 To divide, to separate.<BR>2 To surround, to encompass.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मण्डति मण्डयति)<BR>To adorn, to grace, to decorate.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मण्डयति)<BR>To gladden, to rejoice, to make happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मडक|मडकः
मडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Eleusine corocana.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्डु|मड्डुः
मड्डु<BR>m. (-ड्डुः)<BR>A sort of drum.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to purify, aff. उ, deriv. irr.; also with कन् added, मड्डुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण
मण<BR>r. 1st cl. (मणति)<BR>To sound, to sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणि|मणिः
मणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णिः or -णी)<BR>1 A gem, a jewel, a precious stone.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>3 Fleshy processes pending from the neck of a goat.<BR>4 A small water pot.<BR>5 The glans penis.<BR>6 The clitoris.<BR>7 The wrist.<BR>8 One of the Nāgas or serpent chiefs of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>मण to sound, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिक|मणिकं|मणिकः
मणिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A small water jar, a pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>मणि the same, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकण्ठ|मणिकण्ठः
मणिकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकर्ण|मणिकर्णः
मणिकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Jewel-eared.<BR>E.<BR>मणि, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकर्णिका
मणिकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A holy pool at Benares, in which pilgrims are directed to bathe, and adjacent ghāt.<BR>E.<BR>मणि, and कर्ण the ear, aff. कन्, fem. form. Devi having dropped one of her earrings at this place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकाच|मणिकाचः
मणिकाच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The feathered part of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकानन|मणिकाननं
मणिकानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The neck or throat.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and कानन a wood; abounding with such ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकार|मणिकारः
मणिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A jeweller, a lapidary or worker in precious stones.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिग्रीव|मणिग्रीवः
मणिग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>One of KUVERA'S sons.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिछिद्रा|मणिच्छिद्रा
मणिछिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 Marrow.<BR>2 A sort of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणित|मणितं
मणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Low murmuring sound.<BR>E.<BR>मण to sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणितारक|मणितारकः
मणितारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, तॄ to pass over, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिद्वीप|मणिद्वीपः
मणिद्वीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The crest or hood of the great serpent ANANTA.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and द्वीप a continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिधनुष्
मणिधनुष्<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The rainbow.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and धनुष् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिपूर|मणिपूरं|मणिपूरः
मणिपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The navel.<BR>2 A sort of bodice worn by women, and often richly ornamented with jewels.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The pit of the stomach, as one of the mystical cakras of the body: see चक्र.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and पूर filling, full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिबन्ध|मणिबंध|मणिबन्धः
मणिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The wrist.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and बन्ध binding; where bracelets of precious stones are bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभद्र|मणिभद्रः
मणिभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 One of the Jinas, or Jaina deified teachers.<BR>2 A name of the king of the Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभित्ति|मणिभित्तिः
मणिभित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>The palace of the great serpent, ŚEṢA Nāga.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and भित्ति a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभूमि|मणिभूमिः
मणिभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>A jewel mine, or a place where gems or precious stones are found.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and भूमि ground; also मणिभू f. (-भूः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमण्डप|मणिमण्डपः
मणिमण्डप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 The capital of Śeṣa.<BR>2 The palace of NAIRṚTA, regent of the S. W. quarter.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, and मण्डप a building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमत्|मणिमन्त्
मणिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Having jewels, possessed of or adorned with them.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>मणि, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमध्य
मणिमध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>A species of the Vṛhatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमन्थ|मणिमन्थं
मणिमन्थ<BR>n. (-न्थं)<BR>1 A mountain or range where salt is found<BR>2 Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and मन्थ what churns; also माणिमन्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमाला
मणिमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A necklace, a zone, a fillet, &c. of precious stones.<BR>2 An impression left by a bite.<BR>3 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>4 Light, lustre.<BR>5 A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and माला a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिरत्न
मणिरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A precious gem.<BR>E.<BR>मणि, and रत्न a jewel, or the best of any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिव|मणिवः
मणिव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>One of the Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and व poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिवीज|मणिवीजः
मणिवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिसर|मणिसरः
मणिसर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A string of gems, a necklace, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मणि, and सर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिसौपान
मणिसौपान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A staff or stick set with jewels.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a jewel, सौपान a ladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीचक|मणीचकं|मणीचकः
मणीचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The moon gem, probably a sort of crystal.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kingfisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीवक|मणीवकं
मणीवक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flower.<BR>E.<BR>मण to sound, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड|मंडं|मण्डं|मंडः|मण्डः
मण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 Scum, skimmings, froth, foam, barm, &c., the upper part of any infusion in a state of boiling or ferment.<BR>2 Pith, essence.<BR>3 The head.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 Ornament, decoration.<BR>2 The castor oil tree, (Palma christi.)<BR>3 A sort of potherb.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, Uṇādi aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डन|मंडन|मण्डनं|मण्डनः
मण्डन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Adorning, dressing, decorating, fond of or putting on ornaments.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Ornament, decoration, jewels, trinkets, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डप|मंडपः|मण्डपः
मण्डप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 A temporary building, an open shed or hall, adorned with flowers and erected on festival occasions, as at marriages, &c.<BR>2 An open temple or building consecrated to a deity.<BR>E.<BR>मण्ड ornament, and पा to preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डयन्त|मंडयंतः|मण्डयन्तः
मण्डयन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An ornament, a decoration of trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A woman, a wife.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, Uṇādi aff. झच्. fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डरी|मंडरी
मण्डरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The mole cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डल|मंडल|मण्डलं|मण्डलः
मण्डल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The sun's disk.<BR>2 An orb, a circumference in general or the circle bounding the view, the sensible horizon.<BR>3 (In astronomy,) A great circle, as नाडीमण्डलं the equator, क्रान्तिमण्डलं the ecliptic.<BR>4 A ball, a globe.<BR>5 A wheel.<BR>6 A province, a region, a district, extending twenty, or according to some authorities, forty Yojanas every way.<BR>7 The country or empire, over which the twelve princes termed Cakravartīs are supposed to have ruled; perhaps the peninsula of India, where the term Maṇḍala or Mandel is of constant occurrence, to signify a province or district, as in Coromandet, &c.<BR>8 Surrounding or contiguous countries.<BR>9 A sort of leprosy with circular spots.<BR>10 A heap, a quantity, a multitude or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">Page634</a>] assemblage.<BR>11 An attitude in shooting, the fifth position, in which both knees are bent.<BR>12 The impression or scratch of a finger nail.<BR>13 A sort of perfume, resembling in appearance a dried shell fish.<BR>14 A sort of mystical diagram.<BR>15 A sweetmeat, a sugar-ball.<BR>16 A form of array, an army drawn up in a circle.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Bent grass.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, aff. कलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=633" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलक|मंडलकं|मण्डलकं|मण्डलकः
मण्डलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 An orb or disk.<BR>2 A sort of leprosy, with large round spots.<BR>3 A mirror.<BR>4 A form of array, an army drawn up in a circle.<BR>5 A circular figure or diagram.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलनृत्य|मण्डलनृत्यं
मण्डलनृत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Dancing in a ring, especially a dance imitative of one, said to have been danced by the Gopīs round KṚṢṆA and his mistress RĀDHĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल a circle, and नृत्य dancing^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलाग्र|मण्डलाग्रः
मण्डलाग्र<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>A sword, a scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल a circle, and अग्र top or point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलायित|मंडलायित|मण्डलायितं
मण्डलायित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A ball, a globe.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल a circle, क्यप् aff., and क्त added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलाधीश|मण्डलाधीशः
मण्डलाधीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An emperor, a king of kings.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल an extensive district or empire, and अधीश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलिन्|मंडलिन्
मण्डलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Being in a circle, made up into a coil or ball.<BR>2 Surrounded by.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A large species of snake.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>3 A polecat.<BR>4 A dog.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>6 The ruler or governor of a Maṇḍala or district.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल a circle, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलीकरण|मंडलीकरणं
मण्डलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rounding, gathering in a ball or a circle, coiling, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलीकृत|मंडलीकृत
मण्डलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rounded, made round or globular, gathered in a ball or circle.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलेश|मण्डलेशः
मण्डलेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An emperor, a supreme monarch.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल an empire, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलेश्वर|मण्डलेश्वरः
मण्डलेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sovereign, a monarch.<BR>E.<BR>मण्डल a district, and ईश्वर a sovereign; the power of this prince is limited by AMARA, and the Maṇḍaleśvara is considered as an emperor or supreme prince, only when in addition to his territorial sway, he has performed the Rājasūya sacrifice, or sacrifice in which he has been attended by all his tributary or subject princes: other authorities confound the sovereign of a Maṇḍala, with the Cakravartī or emperor, and with the Samrāj or lord paramount, and others confine him to the government of a district of twenty or forty Yojanas in each direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डहारक|मण्डहारकः
मण्डहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>मण्ड froth, ferment, and हृ to take, aff. अण्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डित|मंडित|मण्डितः
मण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ornamented, adorned.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>One of the eleven persons called Gaṇādhipas by the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूक|मंडूकः|मण्डूकः
मण्डूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 The name of a Muni.<BR>3 A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>f. (-का-की)<BR>Madder, (Rubia Manjith.)<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A female or small frog.<BR>2 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica, or Hydrocotyle Asiatica.)<BR>3 An unchaste or abandoned woman.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to ornament, Uṇādi aff. ऊकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूकपर्ण|मण्डूकपर्णः
मण्डूकपर्ण<BR>mf. (-र्णः-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 Bengal madder, (Rubia Manjith.)<BR>2 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>3 A sort of creeper, (Hydrocotyle Asiatica.)<BR>E.<BR>मण्डूक a frog, and पर्ण a leaf, compared to the animal in shape or colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूर|मंडूरं|मण्डूरं
मण्डूर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>Rust of iron.<BR>E.<BR>मडि to adorn, ऊरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डोदक|मण्डोदकं
मण्डोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Painting figures or flowers, on the walls or floors of an apartment, &c. on festival occasions, with a white pigment made from ground rice.<BR>2 Variegated colour.<BR>E.<BR>मण्ड scum, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्
मत्<BR>ind.<BR>Mine.<BR>E.<BR>irregular substitute for मम possessive case of अत्मट् I, and used in composition, as मत्पुत्त्र my son, मन्नाथ my lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत|मतं|मतः
मत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Admitted, believed, held or entertained, (as opinion, &c.)<BR>3 Respected, reverenced, minded, regarded.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Purpose, intention, wish, mind, (as to have a mind to any thing.)<BR>2 Knowledge.<BR>3 Doctrine, tenet, belief, opinion.<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्ग|मतंग|मतंगः|मतङ्गः
मतङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The name of a Muni.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to please, to be pleased, अङ्गच् Uṇādi. aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्गज|मतंगज|मतंगजः|मतङ्गजः
मतङ्गज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मतङ्ग the saint MATAṄGA, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतल्लिका
मतल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Excellence, happiness: (also attributively, but unvarying in gender,) excellent, best, happiest; there is no etymon of this word, according to the best authorities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मति|मतिः
मति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Understanding, intellect.<BR>2 Wish, desire, inclination.<BR>3 Memory, recollection.<BR>4 Respect, reverence.<BR>5 A potherb.<BR>E.<BR>मन to respect, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिप्रकर्ष|मतिप्रकर्षः
मतिप्रकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Cleverness, talent.<BR>E.<BR>मति, and प्रकर्ष superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिभ्रम|मतिभ्रमः
मतिभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Error, mistake.<BR>E.<BR>मति understanding, and भ्रम error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिभ्रान्ति|मतिभ्रांति|मतिभ्रान्तिः
मतिभ्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Error, mistake, misapprehension.<BR>E.<BR>मति mind, understanding, and भ्रान्ति error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिमत्|मतिमन्त्
मतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Sensible, clever, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>मति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिविभ्रम|मतिविभ्रमः
मतिविभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Error.<BR>E.<BR>मति, and विभ्रम error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिहीन
मतिहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Stupid, ignorant.<BR>E.<BR>मति, and हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्क|मत्कः
मत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Mine, belonging to me, &c.<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>A bug: (see the next.)<BR>E.<BR>मत् for मम mine, and कन् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुण|मत्कुणः
मत्कुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A bug.<BR>2 A flea.<BR>3 An elephant without tusks.<BR>4 A beardless man.<BR>5 The cocoanut.<BR>6 Armour for the thighs or legs.<BR>7 A buffalo.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The pudendum muliebre, without hair on the pubis.<BR>E.<BR>मट् or मत् pleasure, क्वन to sound, aff. अच्, the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुणारि|मत्कुणारिः
मत्कुणारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>E.<BR>मत्कुण a bug, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्त|मत्तः
मत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>2 Intoxicated, (drunk with liquor.)<BR>3 Intoxicated, (with pride, passion, &c.)<BR>4 Furious, mad, insane.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 A furious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>2 A buffalo.<BR>3 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>4 The thorn apple, (Datura.)<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>1 Vinous liquor.<BR>2 A species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>E.<BR>मद to rejoice, &c. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=634" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकाशिनी
मत्तकाशिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An excellent woman.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त intoxicated, and काश to shine, aff. इनि; also from काष or कास, मत्तकाषिणी, and मत्तकासिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकीश|मत्तकीशः
मत्तकीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मत्तक for मत्त furious, and ईश lord, the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तदन्तिन्|मत्तदंतिन्
मत्तदन्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>A furious elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त, and दन्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तमयूर|मत्तमयूरः
मत्तमयूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A wild peacock.<BR>2 A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त, and मयूर a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तर|मत्तरः
मत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Better or more than mine.<BR>E.<BR>मत् for मम mine, and डतरच् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारण|मत्तवारणं|मत्तवारणः
मत्तवारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A furious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A painted wooden turret or veranda, on the top of a large building or palace.<BR>2 An enclosure of trees, &c. round the walls of a princely residence.<BR>3 Pounded betle nut.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त wild, and वारण्ण an elephant, or fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्ताक्रीड
मत्ताक्रीड<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>A species of the Vikṛti metre.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त, and आक्रीड playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तालम्ब|मत्तालम्बः
मत्तालम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A fence or enclosure round the walls of a palace, either artificial as palisades, or natural as a grove of trees, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त mad, wild, (enemies, &c.) आलम्ब delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तेभगमना
मत्तेभगमना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman with a lounging or rolling walk.<BR>E.<BR>मत्त intoxicated, इभ an elephant, गमना who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्पर
मत्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Devoted to me, (GOD.)<BR>E.<BR>मत्, and पर attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्य|मत्यं
मत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 The iron-bound handle of a sickle.<BR>2 The exercise or application of knowledge.<BR>3 The means of acquiring knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>मति knowledge, &c., aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्र
मत्र<BR>(इ) मत्रि r. 1st and 10th cls. (मन्त्रति मन्त्रयति)<BR>To speak privately, to counsel or advise.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To address or salute.<BR>With नि,<BR>To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स|मत्सः
मत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be pleased, स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सगण्ठ|मत्सगण्ठः
मत्सगण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>Fish sauce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Envious.<BR>2 Niggardly, covetous.<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>1 Envy, impatience of another's success or prosperity.<BR>2 Passion, anger.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A gnat, a musquito.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to rejoice, Uṇādi aff. सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरिन्
मत्सरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Wicked, depraved, bad.<BR>2 Envious.<BR>E.<BR>मत्सर envy, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य<BR>mf. (-त्स्यः-त्स्यी)<BR>A fish in general.<BR>m. (-त्स्यः)<BR>1 A particular fish, probably the Śapharī, or the fish in which VIṢṆU was incarnate in his fish Avatāra.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU, from his incarnation as a fish.<BR>3 A country, enumerated amongst the midland divisions of India, (Dinajpur and Rangpur.)<BR>4 One of the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be pleased, Uṇādi aff. स्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यकरण्डिका|मत्स्यकरंडिका
मत्स्यकरण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fish basket.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and करण्ड a basket, कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यगन्धा|मत्स्यगंधा
मत्स्यगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Lāṅgalīya; (the common name is applied to the Nama zeylanica, and the Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>2 The mother of the sacred poet VYĀSA: see मत्स्योदरी.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यघात|मत्स्यघातः
मत्स्यघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Catching fish.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य, and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यजाल|मत्स्यजालं
मत्स्यजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A fishing net.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य fish, and जाल net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डी|मत्स्यंडी
मत्स्यण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>Coarse or unrefined sugar, the juice of the sugar-cane, either after its first boiling, or after it is partially freed from impurities by straining.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slowly, स्यन्द to trickle or ooze, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्, deriv. irr.; also with कन् added, मत्स्यण्डीका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यधानी
मत्स्यधानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A fish basket, a small basket used by fishermen, to put the fish into when caught; it is also sometimes, but less accurately, applied to a kind of snare of reeds or grass, which is left in the water, and entangles the fish that swim with the current.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, धा to have or hold, aff. ल्युट्; also with आङ् prefixed, मत्स्याधानी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यनाशक|मत्स्यनाशकः
मत्स्यनाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An osprey.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and नाशक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यनाशन|मत्स्यनाशनः
मत्स्यनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An osprey.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and नाशन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यपित्ता
मत्स्यपित्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Katuki.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and पित्त bile; being as bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यबन्धिन्|मत्स्यबंधिन्
मत्स्यबन्धिन्<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A fish basket.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and बन्ध confining, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यरङ्ग|मत्स्यरंग|मत्स्यरङ्गः
मत्स्यरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A king-fisher.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and रङ्ग inclination; also with कन् added, मत्स्यरङ्गक; it is also read मत्स्यरङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यराज|मत्स्यराजः
मत्स्यराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The Rohi, a sort of fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>2 The country called Matsya.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and राज supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यवेधन|मत्स्यवेधनं
मत्स्यवेधन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A fish-hook.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bird, the shag.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, विध to pierce, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यसंघात
मत्स्यसंघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A shoal of young or small fish.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and संघात heap, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यसन्तानिक|मत्स्यसंतानिक|मत्स्यसन्तानिकः
मत्स्यसन्तानिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fish baked in a crust of clay and straw, and eaten with condiments and oil.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य fish, सन्तान product, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याक्षी
मत्स्याक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and अक्ष an eye, aff. ङीष्; to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याङ्गी
मत्स्याङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant, (Hingtsha repens, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, अङ्ग the body or form, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याद
मत्स्याद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what feeds upon fish.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यादनी
मत्स्यादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name applied to several plants, as to Jussieua repens, Hingtsha repens, Nama zeylanica, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, अदन eating, food, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याशन|मत्स्याशनः
मत्स्याशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The king-fisher.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्योदरी
मत्स्योदरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of SATYAVATĪ, the mother of VYĀSA.<BR>2 A place of pilgrimage, a particular pool at Benares held in reverence by pilgrims to that sacred city.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and उदर the belly; the mother of VYĀSA was found in the belly of a fish, and retaining a fishy odour, was thence also called MATSYAGANDHA, till the scent was changed to that of a lotus by her paramour the Muni PARĀŚARA, the father of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ
मथ<BR>(ए) मथे r. 1st cl. (मथति)<BR>1 To churn.<BR>2 To stir or agitate.<BR>(इ,) मथि (मन्थति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To afflict.<BR>3 To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=635" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन|मथनं|मथनः
मथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Churning.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, the wood of which is used to produce fire by attrition, (Premna longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मथ to churn, to stir or rub, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथित|मथितं
मथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stirred, churned.<BR>2 Agitated, mentally, distressed, anxious.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Butter-milk, without any watery admixture.<BR>E.<BR>मथ to churn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिन्
मथिन्<BR>m. (-न्था)<BR>A churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>मथि to stir or agitate, aff. इन्, and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरा
मथुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A town in the province of Agra, celebrated as the birth place, and early residence of KṚṢṆA, and still an object of pilgrimage amongst the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>मथि to stir, Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरेश|मथुरेशः
मथुरेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मथुरा a town, and ईश ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथूरा
मथूरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Mathurā as above.<BR>E.<BR>ऊरच् affixed to मथि, instead of उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद|मदः
मद<BR>r. 1st cl. (मादयते) (इ, इर्) मदि r. 1st cl. (मन्दति), and (ई, इर्) मदी r. 4th cl. (माद्यति)<BR>1 To be glad, to be satisfied or content, to rejoice.<BR>2 To be proud.<BR>(इ) मदि r. 1st cl. (मन्दति)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>2 To sleep, to doze, to be lazy or sluggish.<BR>3 To be stupid, to be an idiot or fool.<BR>4 To be elegant.<BR>5 To go or approach.<BR>मद r. 10th cl. (मादयते)<BR>To cause or justify satisfaction or contentment.<BR>मदी r. 1st cl. causal form (मादयति)<BR>1 To delight, to make glad, to exhilarate.<BR>2 To madden or intoxicate, literally or figuratively.<BR>2 To be poor or distressed.<BR>4 To be proud.<BR>With नि prefixed,<BR>(निमादयति)<BR>To articulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद|मदः
मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Joy, pleasure, delight.<BR>2 The juice that flows from an elephant's temples when in rut.<BR>3 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>4 Inebriety, intoxication.<BR>5 Pride, arrogance.<BR>6 Insanity, madness.<BR>7 Semen virile.<BR>8 Musk.<BR>9 A male river.<BR>10 Passion, desire.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>1 A drinking vessel.<BR>2 An instrument for making furrows.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be pleased, &c., aff. अप् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकल|मदकलः
मदकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Speaking inarticulately or like a drunken person.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An elephant in rut.<BR>E.<BR>मद inebriety, &c., कल to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकोहल|मदकोहलः
मदकोहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A bull that has been liberated at some festival, and is allowed to wander about at will.<BR>E.<BR>मद pleasure, कुह to sound, aff. अलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगन्धा|मदगंधा
मदगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मद intoxication, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगमन|मदगमनः
मदगमन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>मद pleasure, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदघ्नी
मदघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A potherb, (Basella lucida, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मद inebriety, घ्नी what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदन|मदनः
मदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>2 The season of spring.<BR>3 A plant commonly Mayana, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>4 Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>5 A bee.<BR>6 A sort of bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>7 Bee's wax.<BR>8 A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>f. (-ना-नी)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मद to exhilarate or rejoice, aff. ल्युट्, fem. aff. टाप्, or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनकाकुरव|मदनकाकुरवः
मदनकाकुरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A pigeon, a dove.<BR>E.<BR>मदन love, काकु change of voice, and रव who utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनपाठक|मदनपाठकः
मदनपाठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मदन spring, and पाठक reader; announcing the season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनवश
मदनवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Subdued by love, in love.<BR>E.<BR>मदन, and वश subdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनललित
मदनललित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Sign or effect of love.<BR>2 A species of the Aṣṭī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनशलाका
मदनशलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A provocative medicine.<BR>2 The Mayana, or more properly the Śārikā, a small bird.<BR>3 The female of the Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मदन love, &c., and शलाका the bird, or a dart, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनसारिका
मदनसारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Śārikā or Śārika, a small bird, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>मदब love, and सारिका the Śālikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनाङ्कुश|मदनांकुश|मदनाङ्कुशः
मदनाङ्कुश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Membrum virile.<BR>2 A finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>मदन KĀMADEVA, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनायुध|मदनायुधः
मदनायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>मदन, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनालय|मदनालयः
मदनालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A sovereign, a prince.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>3 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>मदन pleasure, आलय receptacle, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनावस्था
मदनावस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>Separation of lovers.<BR>E.<BR>मदन love, अव depreciative prefix, स्था to stay, aff. क, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनीय
मदनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be enamoured.<BR>2 Causing or exciting passion.<BR>E.<BR>मद to delight, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनोत्सव|मदनोत्सवः
मदनोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The vernal festival of the Hindus, the Holī.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A courtezan of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>मदन spring or love, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदप्रयोग|मदप्रयोगः
मदप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The issue of the fluid from the forehead of an elephant in rut.<BR>E.<BR>मद the fluid, and प्रयोग junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदभञ्जिनी
मदभञ्जिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>मद inebriety, भञ्ज breaking, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयन्तिका|मदयंतिका
मदयन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयन्ती|मदयंती
मदयन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>मद to delight, झच् Uṇādi aff., and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयित्नु|मदयित्नुः
मदयित्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>1 Love or CUPID.<BR>2 A distiller.<BR>3 A drunken man, a mad man.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>n. (-त्नु)<BR>Vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मद in the causal form, to intoxicate, &c., Uṇādi aff. इत्नुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदराग|मदरागः
मदराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Love or KĀMA.<BR>2 A cock.<BR>E.<BR>मद passion or desire, and राग propensity, inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदविक्षिप्त|मदविक्षिप्तः
मदविक्षिप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A furious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>E.<BR>मद the juice, and विक्षिप्त tossed, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदवृन्द|मदवृंद|मदवृन्दः
मदवृन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मद the juice, and वृन्द a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदस्थल|मदस्थलं
मदस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A tavern, a dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>मद intoxication, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदस्थान|मदस्थानं
मदस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A place where liquor is sold, a tavern, a dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>मद drunkenness, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाढ्य|मदाढ्यः
मदाढ्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>The palm tree.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>A sort of Barleria, with red flowers.<BR>E.<BR>मद intoxication, आद्य fit or proper for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदातङ्क|मदातंक|मदातङ्कः
मदातङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>Pain and sickness, consequent upon ebriety.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and आतङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदात्यय|मदात्ययः
मदात्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Disorder induced by drunkenness; head-ache, sickness, loss of appetite, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मद drunkenness, and अत्यय consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदान्ध|मदांध
मदान्ध<BR>mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>Blind with pride or passion, arrogant, dissolute, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=636" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्नात|मदाम्नातः
मदाम्नात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A drum carried on an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मद pride, आम्नात minded, respected, from मना with आङ् prefix, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्बर|मदांबर|मदाम्बरः
मदाम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मद the frontal fluid, and अम्बर garment, housing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार|मदारः
मदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A rogue.<BR>3 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>4 An elephant in rut.<BR>5 A hog.<BR>6 The name of a king.<BR>7 A sort of perfume, probably musk.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be intoxicated, &c., Uṇādi aff. आरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार्म्मद|मदार्मद|मदार्मदः|मदार्म्मदः
मदार्म्मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sort of fish: see फलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालस
मदालस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Indolent, slothful, overcome with passion or pride.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and अलस idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालापिन्
मदालापिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>The Koïl; or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मद delight, आङ् before लप to speak, aff. णिनि; the song of this bird is constantly heard in the spring in most parts of Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाह्व|मदाह्वः
मदाह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>मद musk, and आह्व name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिर|मदिरः
मदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A red species of Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Wine, spirits, spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>2 A wagtail.<BR>3 A species of the Ākṛti metre.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be delighted, &c., Uṇādi aff. किरन्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिराक्षी
मदिराक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A woman, a mistress, a wife.<BR>E.<BR>मदिरा wine, अक्षि the eye, षच् and ङीष् affs., whose eyes inebriate like wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरागृह|मदिरागृहं
मदिरागृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A tavern, a dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>मदिरा wine, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरासख|मदिरासखः
मदिरासख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The mango, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>मदिरा wine or spirits, and सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरेक्षणा
मदिरेक्षणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A fascinating woman.<BR>E.<BR>मदिरा, and ईक्षण the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिष्ठा
मदिष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>Vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मद what delights or intoxicates, इष्ठन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदीय|मदीयं
मदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Mine, my own.<BR>E.<BR>मत् for मम mine, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्कट|मदोत्कटः
मदोत्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Arrogant, haughty.<BR>2 Furious, mad.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An elephant in rut.<BR>2 A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and उत्कट who is furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोदग्र
मदोदग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Haughty, arrogant.<BR>f. (-ग्रा)<BR>A woman in general.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and उदग्र elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोद्धत|मदोद्धतः
मदोद्धत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>2 Arrogant, drunk with pride.<BR>E.<BR>मद drunkenness, उद्धत struck, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोन्मत्त
मदोन्मत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Drunk or mad with pride, passion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मद, and उन्मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गु|मद्गुः
मद्गु<BR>m. (-द्गुः)<BR>1 An aquatic bird, the shag.<BR>2 An outcaste, the son of a Brahman by a woman of the bard, or panegyrist class, whose employment is hunting wild beasts.<BR>3 A ship, a galley.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to emerge, to dive, उ aff., deriv. irr., or मद to be delighted, (in the water,) and गुक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गुर|मद्गुरः
मद्गुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fish, (Macropteronatus Magur, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>मद to intoxicate, उरच् Uṇādi aff., and गुक् augment, form irr.; also with कन् added, मद्गुरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गुरसी
मद्गुरसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A sort of fish: see मद्गुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्य|मद्यं
मद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Wine, vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be intoxicated (by it), aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपङ्क|मद्यपङ्कः
मद्यपङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, पङ्क mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपासन
मद्यपासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating a relish, or what excites thirst.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, पस to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपीत
मद्यपीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Drunk, a drunkard.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य, and पीत drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपुष्पी
मद्यपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, the blossoms of which are used in distilling: see मद्यवासिनी, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, पुष्प the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यमण्ड|मद्यमंड|मद्यमण्डः
मद्यमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Yeast, barm, froth.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, मण्ड froth, scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यवासिनी
मद्यवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A shrub, the blossoms of which are used in distilling, (Grislea tomentosa, or Lythrum fruticosum.)<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, वस to dwell, aff. णिनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यवीज
मद्यवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A drug used to produce fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य wine, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यसन्धान|मद्यसंधान|मद्यसन्धानं
मद्यसन्धान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Distillation.<BR>E.<BR>मद्य vinous liquor, and सन्धान distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्र|मद्रः
मद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 Joy, delight.<BR>2 A country enumerated amongst those to the N. W. of Hindustan proper.<BR>3 A sovereign of that country.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be delighted, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रक|मद्रकः
मद्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Produced, &c. in the country of Madra.<BR>E.<BR>मद्र a country so named, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रकार|मद्रकारः
मद्रकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Delighting, giving delight.<BR>E.<BR>मद्र delight, कृ to make, aff. अण्; also with खच् aff., मद्रङ्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रसुता
मद्रसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The wife of Pāṇḍu, mother of the two youngest Paṇḍu princes.<BR>E.<BR>मद्र a proper name, and सुता the daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वन्
मद्वन्<BR>m. (-द्वा)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be intoxicated, वनिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वर्गीण|मद्वर्गीणः
मद्वर्गीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Connected with or related to me.<BR>E.<BR>मत् mine, वर्ग a class or number, ख aff.; also with छ aff., मद्वर्ग्गीय; and with यत्, मद्वर्ग्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधु|मधुः
मधु<BR>mfn. (-धुः-ध्वी-धु)<BR>Sweet, literally or figuratively.<BR>n. (-धु)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor, distilled from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia, or according to some explanations wine, or spirit distilled from grapes.<BR>2 Honey.<BR>3 The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR>4 Water.<BR>5 Milk.<BR>6 Sugar.<BR>7 Sweetness, in flavour, sound, or disposition.<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>1 The month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>2 The season of spring.<BR>3 A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>4 The name of a Daitya or demon, slain by VIṢṆU.<BR>5 The Aśoka tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>6 Liquorice.<BR>7 The name of a RĀKṢASA killed by ŚATRUGHNA.<BR>f. (-धुः)<BR>A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind or respect, Uṇādi aff. उ, and ध substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक|मधुकं|मधुकः
मधुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Sweet, (in taste.)<BR>2 Sweet speaking, or sounding, mellifluous, melodious.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bard, a panegyrist, one who recites the lineage and praises of sovereigns in their presence.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>2 A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Liquorice, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Tin.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>2 The sweet lime.<BR>3 A kind of panic seed.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, कै to sound, aff. ड; or मधु honey, कन् aff. of comparison, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकण्ठ|मधुकंठ|मधुकण्ठः
मधुकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo^1.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, (as sweet,) कण्ठ the throat.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकर|मधुकरः
मधुकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bee.<BR>2 A lover.<BR>3 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>4 A fruit, the round sweet lime.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=637" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकर्क्कटिका|मधुकर्कटिका
मधुकर्क्कटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of citron, the round sweet lime.<BR>2 A kind of date.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and कर्क्कटी or कर्क्कटिका a cucumber; some authorities have मधुकुक्कुटिका in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकारिन्
मधुकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकेशट|मधुकेशटः
मधुकेशट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधुके in honey, and शट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकृत्
मधुकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकोष|मधुकोषः
मधुकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The honeycomb or hive.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, कोष receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक्रम|मधुक्रमः
मधुक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Tippling.<BR>2 The honeycomb.<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine or honey, and क्रम order, arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक्षीर|मधुक्षीरः
मधुक्षीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The date tree.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुगुञ्जन|मधुगुञ्जनः
मधुगुञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुघोष|मधुघोषः
मधुघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, and घोष voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुज|मधुजं
मधुज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुजित्
मधुजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the demon so named, and जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुतृण|मधुतृणं|मधुतृणः
मधुतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुदीप|मधुदीपः
मधुदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>KĀMA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spring, and दीप inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुदूत|मधुदूतः
मधुदूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spring, and दूत messenger; blossoming in spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्र|मधुद्रः
मधुद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, द्रु to take, क aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्रव|मधुद्रवः
मधुद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A red variety of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and द्रव dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्रुम|मधुद्रुमः
मधुद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, from the blossoms of which a spirit is distilled, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुधातु|मधुधातुः
मधुधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A sort of pyrites.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, (as yellow,) and धातु mineral, honey-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुधूलि|मधुधूलिः
मधुधूलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Molasses, sugar before it is quite purified.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनालिकेरक|मधुनालिकेरकः
मधुनालिकेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sweet kind of cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, नालिकेरक cocoanut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनेतृ
मधुनेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, नी to get, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनोलेह
मधुनोलेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधुनः of honey, लेह who licks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप|मधुपः
मधुप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्क|मधुपर्कं|मधुपर्कः
मधुपर्क<BR>n. (-र्कं)<BR>A dish of curds, ghee, and honey, to be offered to a respectable guest on his arrival.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, पृच to sprinkle, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्णिका
मधुपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The indigo plant.<BR>2 A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>3 Moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>4 A creeper of the cryptogamia class, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR>5 A shrub, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, पर्ण a leaf, aff. कन्, fem. form; also मधुपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्णी
मधुपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A sort of creeper, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>2 A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>3 The indigo plant.<BR>4 The sweet lime.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, पर्ण the leaf, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपायिन्
मधुपायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Living on honey.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, पा to drink, णिनि aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपालिका
मधुपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, पाल to nourish, वुन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपुरी
मधुपुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Mathurā, a city so called.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Rākṣasa killed by ŚATRUGHNA, and पुरी city or capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपुष्प|मधुपुष्पः
मधुपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>2 The Mimosa Śirīṣa.<BR>3 The Bakul, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine or honey, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप्रिय|मधुप्रियः
मधुप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A shrub, (Ardisia solanacea.)<BR>2 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine, &c., and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुफल|मधुफलः
मधुफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>2 A sweet kind of cocoanut.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमत्|मधुमन्त्
मधुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Sweet, honied.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A species of the Uṣṇih metre.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुभिद्
मधुभिद्<BR>m. (-भिट् or -भित्)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Daitya, and भिट् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमक्षिका
मधुमक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमथन|मधुमथनः
मधुमथन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Daitya, and मथन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमय
मधुमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sweet, luscious.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमल्ली
मधुमल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Double jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and मल्ली jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमस्तक|मधुमस्तकं
मधुमस्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sweetmeat made of flour, honey, oil, and ghee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and मस्तक a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमाध्वीक|मधुमाध्वीकं
मधुमाध्वीक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A spirit distilled from the flowers of the Bassia latifolia.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spirit, and माध्वीक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमूल|मधुमूलं
मधुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spirit, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुयष्टि|मधुयष्टिः
मधुयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and यष्टि a cane or stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुयष्टिका
मधुयष्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Liquorice, (Glycirrhiza glabra, or rather the Abrus precatorius, of which the root is similarly used.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, यष्टि a stick, and कन् added; or without the aff. मधुयष्टी f. (-ष्टी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुर|मधुरं|मधुरः
मधुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Sweet.<BR>2 Pleasing, agreeable, liked.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sweet taste, sweetness.<BR>2 A drug, commonly Jīvaka.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Poison.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>3 Treacle, syrup.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa or panmorium, Rox.)<BR>2 Anise, (Pimpinella anisum.)<BR>3 A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>4 Liquorice.<BR>5 The sweet lime.<BR>6 Marrow.<BR>7 The city Mathurā.<BR>8 A medicinal plant, commonly Kakkoli.<BR>9 Asparagus racemosus.<BR>10 Bengal beet.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and रा to get or be, aff. क; to have the flavour of honey, to be as sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरक|मधुरकः
मधुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Jīvaka.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरकण्टक|मधुरकंटक|मधुरकण्टकः
मधुरकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, and कण्टक bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरजम्बीर|मधुरजम्बीरः
मधुरजम्बीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sweet lime.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, जम्बीर lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरत्वच|मधुरत्वचः
मधुरत्वच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A shrub, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, त्वच् bark, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरनिस्वना
मधुरनिस्वना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A woman with a sweet voice.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, निस्वन who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरवीजपूर
मधुरवीजपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sweet lime.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, वीजपूर a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस|मधुरसः
मधुरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Sweetness, (in flavour.)<BR>2 Sweetness, (in speech.)<BR>3 The sugar-cane.<BR>4 The palm tree.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 A shrub, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>2 A plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine or honey, and रस juice, flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=638" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराक्षर
मधुराक्षर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Sweet, mellifluous, mellow, melodious.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर, and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराम्लक|मधुराम्लकः
मधुराम्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, अम्ल sour, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरालापा
मधुरालापा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The talking Maina, (Turdus salica.)<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, आलाप talking, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिका
मधुरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>मधुरा the same, कन् aff.; this name is applied also to the Anethum panmorium, Rox. and the Bengali derivative Mahuri is applied to common anise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिपु|मधुरिपुः
मधुरिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the demon, and रिपु foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरोदक|मधुरोदकः
मधुरोदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The sea of fresh or sweet water, surrounding Puṣkara dvīpa, and being the outermost of the seven seas.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुल|मधुलं
मधुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine, ला to be or get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलिह्
मधुलिह्<BR>m. (-लिड्-लिट्)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, लिह् to lick, aff. क्विष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलेह
मधुलेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and लेह what licks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलेहिन्
मधुलेहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, लिह to lick, aff. णिनि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवन|मधुवनं|मधुवनः
मधुवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, and वन who speaks or cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवार|मधुवारः
मधुवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Tippling, drinking frequently and repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine, वार quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवीज|मधुवीजः
मधुवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुव्रत|मधुव्रतः
मधुव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुशाख|मधुशाखः
मधुशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Bassia latifolia.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spirituous liquor, शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुशिग्रु|मधुशिग्रुः
मधुशिग्रु<BR>m. (-ग्रुः)<BR>A red variety of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, and शिग्रु the same tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुश्रेणी
मधुश्रेणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, श्रेणी a line or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुष्ठील|मधुष्ठीलः
मधुष्ठील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु spirit, ष्ठीव to eject, aff. क, and ल substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसख|मधुसखः
मधुसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spring, and सख for सखि friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसहाय|मधुसहायः
मधुसहाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and सहाय friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसात्
मधुसात्<BR>ind.<BR>As honey, sweet.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसाद्भूत
मधुसाद्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become sweet.<BR>E.<BR>मधुसात्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसारथि|मधुसारथिः
मधुसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>KĀMA the Hindu CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the spring personified, and सारथि a charioteer, having Vasanta or spring for his coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसिक्थक|मधुसिक्थकः
मधुसिक्थक<BR>m. (-क)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and सिक्थक wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसुहृद्
मधुसुहृद्<BR>m. (-हृद् or -हृत्)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु spring, सुहृत् the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसूदन|मधुसूदनः
मधुसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Bengal beet.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Daitya or honey, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्रवस्
मधुस्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु spirituous liquor, स्रु to drop or distil, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्रवा
मधुस्रवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>2 Liquorice.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, स्रु to drop, aff. अप् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्वर|मधुस्वरः
मधुस्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet or spring, and स्वर note, song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुहन्
मधुहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Daitya, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूक|मधूकं|मधूकः
मधूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मन to respect, ऊक aff., and ध substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूच्छिष्ट|मधूच्छिष्टं
मधूच्छिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, and उच्छिष्ट left, rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूपघ्न|मधूपघ्नं|मधूपघ्नः
मधूपघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>The city Mathurā.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the demon, उपघ्न destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूल|मधूलः
मधूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of Bassia described as growing in watery or mountainous situations.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Liquorice.<BR>2 The sweet lime.<BR>3 The mango tree.<BR>4 A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey or spirit, ला to be or get, aff. ड, and the उ of मधु irregularly long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलक|मधूलकः
मधूलक<BR>mfn. (-लकः लिका-लकं)<BR>Sweet.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of Bassia, growing in watery or mountainous sites.<BR>2 Sweetness.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्य|मध्यं|मध्यः
मध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Middle, intermediate.<BR>2 Right, proper, reasonable.<BR>3 Low, vile.<BR>4 Amongst, amidst.<BR>5 Mean, (in astronomy,) as मध्यछाया middle or mean shadow.<BR>mn. (-ध्यः-ध्यं)<BR>1 The west.<BR>2 Mean or common time in music.<BR>3 The middle, the centre.<BR>4 The waist.<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>1 A young woman, a girl arrived at puberty.<BR>2 The middle finger.<BR>3 A form of metre, a stanza of four lines containing three syllables in each.<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>Cessation, rest, interval.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>1 A very large number, ten Āntyas.<BR>2 A horse's flank.<BR>E.<BR>मां beauty, धा to have, अण् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग
मध्यग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Who or what goes in the centre or betwixt, amongst, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यगन्ध|मध्यगंध|मध्यगन्धः
मध्यगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यचारिन्
मध्यचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Going amongst or amidst.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतस्
मध्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From or in the middle, centrical, centrically.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य the middle, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदेश|मध्यदेशः
मध्यदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The middle region; part of India, bounded by Kurukṣetra on the north, Allahabad on the south, the Himālaya mountains on the east, and the Vindhya mountains on the west; comprising therefore the modern provinces of Allahabad, Agra, Delhi, Oude, &c.; the northern limit is elsewhere defined to be the disappearance of the Sarasvatī.<BR>E.<BR>भध्य middle, and देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम|मध्यमं|मध्यमः
मध्यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Middle, centrical, intervening, intermediate.<BR>2 Middle born, neither the oldest nor youngest.<BR>3 Mean, (in astronomy,) as मध्यमगति mean motion (of a planet.)<BR>mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>The waist, the middle of the body.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 One of the seven musical notes, the fifth note of the Hindu gamut.<BR>2 The middle country: see मध्यदेश.<BR>3 A sort of deer.<BR>4 One of the Grāmas or musical scales of the Hindus, corresponding apparently with the major mode of European music.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A girl arrived at puberty, or in whom menstruation has commenced.<BR>2 The middle finger.<BR>3 A central blossom.<BR>4 A form of metre, a verse of four lines of three syllables each.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, and म aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=639" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपाण्डव|मध्यमपांडव|मध्यमपाण्डवः
मध्यमपाण्डव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>ARJUNA, the third or middle of the PĀṆḌU princes.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, and पाण्डव Pāṇḍava or descendant of PĀṆḌU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमलोक|मध्यमलोकः
मध्यमलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The earth, the world of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, and लोक world; between heaven and hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमभृतक|मध्यमभृतकः
मध्यमभृतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A husbandman.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, and भृतक a labourer; working partly for his own advantage, and partly for that of the landlord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमवयस्क
मध्यमवयस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Middle, aged.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम, and वयस्क aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसंग्रह
मध्यमसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Intriguing with another man's wife, the act of presenting flowers, perfumes, &c. to her, and conversing with her privately.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, संग्रह connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसाहस|मध्यमसाहसं|मध्यमसाहसः
मध्यमसाहस<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>1 Punishment due to crimes of a middling degree.<BR>2 Injuring buildings, throwing down walls, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमिका
मध्यमिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A girl arrived at puberty, one in whom menstruation has commenced.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यमा the same, कन् added, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमीय|मध्यमीयं
मध्यमीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Central, middle.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम middle, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्ययव|मध्ययवः
मध्ययव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A weight of six white mustard seeds.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, and यव barley-corn, the Yava being sometimes considered equal to eight seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यरात्र|मध्यरात्रः
मध्यरात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, रात्र night, and the masculine form in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलोक|मध्यलोकः
मध्यलोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The earth, the dwelling of mortals.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, and लोक world; placed in the middle between heaven and hell; also with कन् added मध्यलोकक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलोकेश|मध्यलोकेशः
मध्यलोकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यलोक the earth, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवर्त्तिन्|मध्यवर्तिन्
मध्यवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>1 Central, middle.<BR>2 Being amongst or amidst.<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A mediator.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य, and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवृत्त
मध्यवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>The navel.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य the middle, and वृत्त abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थ|मध्यस्थः
मध्यस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Centrical, middle.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A middle man, an umpire, an arbitrator, a mediator.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, and स्थ what or who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थता
मध्यस्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Middle state or character.<BR>2 Indifference.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यस्थ middle, and तल् aff. of the abstract; also with त्व, मध्यस्थत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थल|मध्यस्थलं
मध्यस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The waist.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, स्थल place or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्याह्न|मध्याह्नः
मध्याह्न<BR>m. (-ह्नः)<BR>Midday, noon.<BR>E.<BR>मध्य middle, अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वल|मध्वलः
मध्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Tippling, drinking repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>मधु wine, अल to be equal to, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वापात
मध्वापात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Taste or touch of honey.<BR>E.<BR>मधु, and आपात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वालुक|मध्वालुकं
मध्वालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sweet potatoe.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, आलु an esculent root, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वासव|मध्वासवः
मध्वासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A spirituous liquor, distilled from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia.<BR>E.<BR>मधु the Bassia, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वासवनिक|मध्वासवनिकः
मध्वासवनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>मध्वासव spirit, नी to go, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्विजा
मध्विजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन|मनः
मन<BR>r. 4th cl. (मन्यते) (उ,) मनु r. 8th cl. (मनुते)<BR>1 To know, to understand.<BR>2 To regard, to mind.<BR>3 To think, to conceive.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मानयते)<BR>1 To be dull or insensible.<BR>2 To be proud.<BR>3 To oppose, to stop.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मनति मानयति)<BR>To honour, to respect, to worship.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To assent to, to agree.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To desire.<BR>With अव,<BR>To disrespect.<BR>With सम,<BR>To concur, to agree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन|मनः
मन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Indian spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>मन to respect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनआप|मनआपः
मनआप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Pleasing, agreeable, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, आप to go or attract, aff. अच्; the final consonant of the first word is rejected, and the vowels do not coalesce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःकृत
मनःकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Attended to, applying the mind.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिल|मनःशिलः
मनःशिल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, शिला a stone; a mineral delightful to the mind or heart; also with the dental स, मनःसिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसिल
मनःसिल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>Red arsenic: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनन|मननं
मनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Minding, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, aff, ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्
मनस्<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>1 The mind, or considered as the seat of perception and passion, the heart.<BR>2 The intellect, the understanding.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, to understand, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसा
मनसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The goddess of the serpent race, and the particular protectress against their venom.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, aff. ठाप्; the object of love and devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसाज्ञायिन्
मनसाज्ञायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Knowing by the mind, perceiving intellectually.<BR>E.<BR>मनसा third case of मबस्, and ज्ञायिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसादेवी
मनसादेवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The goddess presiding over snakes: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मनसा the same, and देवी goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिज|मनसिजः
मनसिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Mental, intellectual.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>मनसि in the heart or mind, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिशय|मनसिशयः
मनसिशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>मनसि in the heart or mind, and शय who reposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्क
मनस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Mental.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्कार|मनस्कारः
मनस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The attention of the mind to its own sensations, consciousness of pleasure or pain.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् of the mind, and कार operation; the compound also occurs with the seventh case सनसिकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्ताप|मनस्तापः
मनस्ताप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Mental distress.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and ताप sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्ताल|मनस्तालः
मनस्ताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The lion of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, तल to depress, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विता
मनस्विता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Hope, expectation, dependance.<BR>2 Intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्विन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विन्
मनस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Attentive, fixing the mind upon any thing.<BR>2 Intelligent, intellectual.<BR>f. (-स्विनी)<BR>A virtuous wife.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind or heart, aff. विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्
मनाक्<BR>ind.<BR>1 A little.<BR>2 Tardily, slowly.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, आक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाका
मनाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind or know, Uṇādi aff. आक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्कर|मनाक्करं
मनाक्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Doing little, lazy, sluggish.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A sort of Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>मनाक् a little, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनायी
मनायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>The wife of MANU.<BR>E.<BR>मनु the saint, ङीष् aff., and उ changed to ऐ; otherwise मनवी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=640" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनित|मनितं
मनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Known, understood.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीक|मनीकं
मनीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Collyrium, powdered antimony or other substances, used as an application and ornament to the eye.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, to be agreeable, ईकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषा
मनीषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् mind, ईष to go, aff. क, or ईष aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिन्
मनीषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Intellectual, intelligent.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman, a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>मनीषा understanding, इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनु|मनुः
मनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 MANU, the legislator and saint, the son of BRAHMĀ, or a personification of BRAHMĀ himself, the creator of the world, and progenitor of mankind; the name is however a generic term, and in every Kalpa or interval from creation to creation, there are fourteen successive MANUS presiding over the universe for the period of a Manvantara, respectively: in the present creation there have been the six following MANUS: MANU called also SVAYAMBHUVA, the supposed revealer of the code of law possessed by the Hindus, SVAROCIṢA, UTTAMA, TĀMASA, RAIVATA, and CĀKṢUṢA; the seventh or the present MANU is VAIVASVATA, or RAIVATA the second.<BR>2 A man in general.<BR>3 One of the Jaina saints.<BR>4 A Mantra, a mystical verse or formula.<BR>f. (-नुः-नायी-नावी)<BR>The wife of the legislator MANU.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know or understand, (the Vedas or scripture especially,) and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुज|मनुजः
मनुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A man in general.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>मनु the legislator and progenitor of mankind, and ज born, descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुजेन्द्र
मनुजेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>मनुज, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुभू
मनुभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>Man, a man, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>मनु the saint, and भू born: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुराज्
मनुराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>मनु man, and राज् to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुषी
मनुषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>A woman, the wife or female of the man.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष्य a man, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्य|मनुष्यः
मनुष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>Man, a man, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>मनु the progenitor of mankind, यत् aff. of descent, and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यत्व|मनुष्यत्वं
मनुष्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The state or condition of man, manhood, humanity.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to मनुष्य; also with तल्, मनुष्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यधर्म्मन्|मनुष्यधर्मन्
मनुष्यधर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The duty of man.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष्य man, and धर्म्मन् piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्ययज्ञ|मनुष्ययज्ञः
मनुष्ययज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>Hospitality.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष्य a man, and यज्ञ sacrifice, sacrament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यसभा
मनुष्यसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 A multitude, a crowd, a meeting.<BR>2 A place of meeting or assembly.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष्य a man, mankind, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगत
मनोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seated in the mind.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Thoughts, ideas, notions, feelings.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and गत gone to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगवी
मनोगवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, and गो a cow, &c., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगुप्त
मनोगुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Thought or meditated on secretly.<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, and गुप्त cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज
मनोज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or seated in the mind.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजन्मन्
मनोजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Born or seated in the mind.<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the heart or mind, and जन्मन् birth; also मनोज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजव|मनोजवः
मनोजव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>1 Fatherly, parental.<BR>2 Quick in thought or apprehension.<BR>3 Swift, as thought.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A plant: see अग्निजिह्वा.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Quickness of thought or apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, जु to move, to pervade, aff. अच्, or मनस् compounded with जव speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजवस|मनोजवसः
मनोजवस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Fatherly.<BR>E.<BR>मनोज desire, love, वस to abide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञ|मनोज्ञं|मनोज्ञः
मनोज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Beautiful, handsome, lovely, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>1 Red arsenic.<BR>2 The daughter of a sovereign, a princess.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind or heart, ज्ञा to know, to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदण्ड|मनोदंड|मनोदण्डः
मनोदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Restraint or controul over the mind.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and दण्ड castigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोनीत
मनोनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Chosen, preferred.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and नीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभव|मनोभवः
मनोभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind or heart, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभू
मनोभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the heart, भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयायिन्
मनोयायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Swift, quick, as thought.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and यायिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयोनि|मनोयोनिः
मनोयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The deity KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the heart, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरथ|मनोरथः
मनोरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the heart, and रथ vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरम|मनोरमं
मनोरम<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Beautiful, lovely, pleasing.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A goddess, peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>2 A species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, रम to delight, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोलौल्य
मनोलौल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Fancy, caprice, whim.<BR>E.<BR>मनस्, and लौल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहत|मनोहतः
मनोहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहर|मनोहरं|मनोहरः
मनोहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Beautiful, lovely, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, हृ to take or steal, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहारिन्
मनोहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable, lovely.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, हृ to steal, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोह्वा
मनोह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, and ह्वेञ् to call, to arrest, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तव्य|मंतव्य|मन्तव्यं
मन्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be reflected on, to be ascertained or fixed in the mind, to be discussed either mentally or with proper persons.<BR>2 To be thought, believed, conceived, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, aff. तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तु|मंतु|मंतुः|मन्तुः
मन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 Fault, offence, transgression.<BR>2 A man, mankind.<BR>3 A king.<BR>f. (-न्तुः)<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, Uṇādi aff. तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तृ|मंतृ
मन्तृ<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A sage, one who is possessed of holy knowledge.<BR>2 An adviser, a counsellor.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, Uṇādi aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्र|मंत्र|मंत्रः|मन्त्रः
मन्त्र<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>1 A division of the Vedas; in the first or practical part or Kāṇḍam, it includes prayers and hymns, addressed to particular deities, and used at peculiar sacrifices, &c.; in the Uttara Kāṇḍam, it is applied to addresses to BRAHMĀ or God, and to didactic explanations of his nature and attributes, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">Page642</a>] &c.<BR>2 A mystical verse or incantation, (in the Tantras.)<BR>3 A formula sacred to any individual deity, as, Om Viṣṇave nama, Om Śivāya nama, &c.<BR>4 Secret consultation, private advice.<BR>E.<BR>मत्रि to advise or consult privately, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=641" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत्|मंत्रकृत्
मन्त्रकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र advice, and कृत् who gives or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत
मन्त्रकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Consecrated by the Mantra.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगण्डक|मंत्रगंडक|मन्त्रगण्डकः
मन्त्रगण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Knowledge, science.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र advice, गडि to be a part of, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगुप्ति|मंत्रगुप्ति|मन्त्रगुप्तिः
मन्त्रगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Secret counsel.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and गुप्ति concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगूढ|मंत्रगूढ|मन्त्रगूढः
मन्त्रगूढ<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र advice, information, गूढ secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजिह्व|मंत्रजिह्व|मन्त्रजिह्वः
मन्त्रजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र prayer, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रज्ञ|मंत्रज्ञ|मन्त्रज्ञः
मन्त्रज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>2 A counsellor, an adviser.<BR>3 A priest, a sacred teacher.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र advice, &c. and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रण|मंत्रण|मंत्रणं|मन्त्रणं
मन्त्रण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Advising, counselling in private.<BR>E.<BR>मत्रि to counsel, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतस्
मन्त्रतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 From, with, or by, a Mantra or mystical prayer.<BR>2 Advisedly, deliberately.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and तसि substituted for the termination of the fourth or fifth cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रद|मंत्रद|मन्त्रदः
मन्त्रद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A spiritual guide or teacher.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र initiatory text, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदर्शिन्|मंत्रदर्शिन्
मन्त्रदर्शिन्<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>A Brahman learned in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदीधिति|मंत्रदीधिति|मन्त्रदीधितिः
मन्त्रदीधिति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र holy prayer, and दीधिति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रपूतात्मन्
मन्त्रपूतात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and पूतात्मन् pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रफल
मन्त्रफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The object or effect of counsel.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रभेद|मंत्रभेद|मन्त्रभेदः
मन्त्रभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Divulging or betraying counsel.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयत्
मन्त्रयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Counselling, consulting.<BR>E.<BR>मत्रि to advise, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवत्|मंत्रवत्|मन्त्रवन्त्
मन्त्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Accompanied with holy texts, (a ceremony.)<BR>2 Entitled to use the Vedas.<BR>3 Initiated.<BR>4 Having or hearing counsel.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवित्
मन्त्रवित्<BR>m. (-विट्-वित्)<BR>1 A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>2 A counsellor.<BR>3 A priest.<BR>4 A Brahman learned in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र secret council, &c. and विट् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रस्पृश्
मन्त्रस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Obtaining or effecting any thing by means of mystic formulæ or prayers.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र a prayer of the Vedas, &c., and स्पृश् to touch, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रित|मंत्रित|मन्त्रितः
मन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Advised, counselled, planned.<BR>E.<BR>मत्रि to consult, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रित्व|मंत्रित्वं
मन्त्रित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Property or condition of a counsellor, counsellorship.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्रिन्, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिन्|मंत्रिन्
मन्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-न्त्री)<BR>A counsellor or adviser, a king's counsellor or minister.<BR>E.<BR>मचि to advise, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोपष्टम्भ|मंत्रोपष्टंभ|मन्त्रोपष्टम्भः
मन्त्रोपष्टम्भ<BR>m. (-म्मः)<BR>Advice, direction.<BR>E.<BR>मन्त्र, and उपष्टम्भ stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ|मंथ|मंथः|मन्थः
मन्थ<BR>r. 1st cl. (मन्थति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To afflict.<BR>3 To suffer pain.<BR>1st and 9th cls. (मन्थति मथ्नाति)<BR>To agitate, to stir, to churn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ|मंथ|मंथः|मन्थः
मन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 A churning. stick.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A dish made of barley meal with ghee and water, a sort of gruel or porridge.<BR>4 A disease of the eyes, cataract or opacity.<BR>5 Rheum, excretion of the eyes.<BR>6 Killing, destroying.<BR>7 Agitating, stirring, churning.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to churn, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थज|मंथज|मन्थजं
मन्थज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Butter.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ churning, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थदण्डक|मंथदंडक|मन्थदण्डकः
मन्थदण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A churning-stick.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ churning, and दण्डक a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थन|मंथन|मन्थनं|मंथनः|मन्थनः
मन्थन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Agitating, stirring, churning.<BR>2 Killing, injuring.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A churn.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to agitate, &c. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थनघटी|मंथनघटी
मन्थनघटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A churn, a common earthen pot used for the purpose.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थन churning, and घटी a small jar or pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थर|मंथर|मन्थरं|मन्थरः
मन्थर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Slow, lazy, tardy.<BR>2 Large, bulky.<BR>3 Curved, bowed, crooked.<BR>4 Stupid, dull, a fool.<BR>5 Low, vile, little.<BR>6 Low, hollow, (as sound.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A soldier marching slowly.<BR>2 A spy, an informer.<BR>3 A treasury, a store, a repertory.<BR>4 Fruit.<BR>5 An obstacle, a hindrance.<BR>6 A churning-stick.<BR>7 Fresh butter.<BR>8 The month Vaiśākha.<BR>9 Passion, wrath.<BR>10 A deer.<BR>11 A fort, a strong-hold.<BR>12 The mountain Mandara.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Safflower.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to agitate, &c. aff. अरण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थरु|मंथरु|मंथरुः|मन्थरुः
मन्थरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The wind from a Chowrie or whisk.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to agitate, अरुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थशैल|मंथशैल|मन्थशैलः
मन्थशैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Mandara.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ a churningstick, and शैल a mountain, being so employed in churning the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थान|मंथान|मंथानः|मन्थानः
मन्थान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A churning-stick.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to agitate, आनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थिन्|मंथिन्
मन्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-न्थी-न्थिनी-न्थि)<BR>1 Agitating, churning.<BR>2 Paining, afflicting.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A churn.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ to churn, णीनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थोदधि|मंथोदधि|मन्थोदधिः
मन्थोदधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Sea of milk.<BR>E.<BR>मन्थ churning, and उदघि a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द|मंद|मन्दः
मन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>1 Slow, tardy.<BR>2 Dull, stupid, heavy.<BR>3 Foolish, a fool.<BR>4 Unlucky.<BR>5 Sick, diseased.<BR>6 Little.<BR>7 Idle, lazy.<BR>8 Drunken, addicted to drunkenness.<BR>9 Vile, wicked.<BR>10 Self-willed.<BR>11 Cold, phlegmatic, apathetic.<BR>12 Low, (as a tone.)<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A name of SATURN.<BR>2 A sort of elephant.<BR>3 A name of YAMA.<BR>4 (In astronomy,) Anomaly.<BR>5 A destruction of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be lazy, &c. aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दकान्त
मन्दकान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Dull, not bright.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and कान्त shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगत
मन्दगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Going slowly.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगति
मन्दगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Slow moving.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Going slowly.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगमन
मन्दगमन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Who or what moves slowly.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Moving or going slowly.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगामिन्|मंदगामिन्
मन्दगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going slowly or gently.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A soldier marching slowly.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slow, गम to go, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दजननी|मंदजननी
मन्दजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of SŪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द SATURN, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दट|मंदट|मंदटः|मन्दटः
मन्दट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>E.<BR>मदि to please, aff. अटच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=642" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दन|मंदन|मंदनं|मन्दनं
मन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be pleased, (by) Uṇādi aff. क्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दफल
मन्दफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>(In astronomy), The anomalistic equation of a planet.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and फल product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दबुद्धि|मंदबुद्धि
मन्दबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Stupid, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दभाग्य|मंदभाग्य
मन्दभाग्य.<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Wretched, unhappy, unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and भाग्य fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दमति|मंदमति
मन्दमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Dull, stupid, slow of apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and मति intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दयमान
मन्दयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Slow, tardy.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be slow, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दर|मंदर|मन्दरः
मन्दर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Large, bulky.<BR>2 Slow, sluggish, dull, lazy, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The mountain Mandara, with which the ocean was churned by the Suras and Asuras, after the deluge, for the purpose of recovering the sacred things lost in it during that period.<BR>2 The Mandara tree, one of the trees of paradise.<BR>3 Svarga or the paradise of the Hindus.<BR>4 A string of pearls, &c.<BR>5 A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to please, to be lazy, &c. अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दसान|मंदसानः|मन्दसानः
मन्दसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>2 Life, living.<BR>3 Sleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be slow or sleepy, Uṇādi aff. असानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दस्मित|मंदस्मित
मन्दस्मित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A smile, a gentle laugh.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slowly, gently, स्मित smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दहास्य|मंदहास्य
मन्दहास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>A smile, a gentle laugh.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slowly, gently, and हास्य laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक|मंदाक|मन्दाकं|मंदाकः|मन्दाकः
मन्दाक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>Praising, praise.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द to praise, आकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाकिनी|मंदाकिनी
मन्दाकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>2 A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slowly, अक to go, aff. णिनि, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक्रान्ता
मन्दाक्रान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A species of the Atyaṣṭi metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक्ष|मंदाक्ष|मन्दाक्षं
मन्दाक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>Modesty, shame, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slow, retiring, and अक्ष organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दात्मन्|मंदात्मन्
मन्दात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Slow of apprehension, dull.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दादर|मंदादर
मन्दादर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Disregarding, neglecting, disrespecting.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दानिल|मंदानिल|मन्दानिलः
मन्दानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gentle breeze, zephyr.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दायमान
मन्दायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Delaying, going tardily.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to be lazy, causal v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दार|मंदार|मंदारः|मन्दारः
मन्दार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of the five trees of Svarga.<BR>2 The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>3 Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>E.<BR>मदि to delight, &c. aff. आरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दास्य|मन्दास्यं
मन्दास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Shame, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द retiring, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिकुकुर|मन्दिकुकुरः
मन्दिकुकुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिर|मंदिर|मंदिरं|मन्दिरं|मन्दिरः
मन्दिर<BR>nf. (-रं-रा)<BR>A house.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A town.<BR>2 A temple.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sea.<BR>2 The back of the knee, the ham.<BR>3 One of the Gandharbas.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A stable.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to sleep, &c. Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरपशु|मंदिरपशु|मन्दिरपशुः
मन्दिरपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>मन्दिर a house, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीभव
मन्दीभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Tardiness.<BR>2 Stupidity.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द्, and भू to be, अप् aff., च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीभूत
मन्दीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Being slow, dull, stupid, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and भू to be, aff. क्त, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरज
मन्दुरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born in a stable.<BR>E.<BR>मन्दुरा, and ज born, the final of the first rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरा|मंदुरा
मन्दुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A stable.<BR>2 A bed, a mat used as one.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to please, &c. Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोच्छ
मन्दोच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>The apsis of a planet's orbit.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द, and उच्छ high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरी|मंदोदरी
मन्दोदरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A proper name, the wife of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slow, heavy, उदर the belly, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरीश|मन्दोदरीशः
मन्दोदरीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मन्दोदरी as above, and ईश lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरीसुत|मन्दोदरीसुतः
मन्दोदरीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मन्दोदरी the wife of the demon, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोष्ण|मंदोष्ण|मन्दोष्णं
मन्दोष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Temperate, tepid, moderately warm.<BR>n. (-ष्णं)<BR>Warmth, gentle heat.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slack, and उष्ण hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्र|मंद्र|मन्द्रः
मन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A base or low tone, such as the grumbling of clouds, &c.<BR>2 A sort of drum.<BR>E.<BR>मदि to please, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथ|मन्मथः
मन्मथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A name of KĀMA, the god of love.<BR>2 Love, amorous passion or desire.<BR>3 The elephant or wood-apple.<BR>E.<BR>मत् the heart, मथ to agitate, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मन|मन्मनः
मन्मन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Whispering, murmuring, low reiterated sound, especially murmur libidinosum.<BR>E.<BR>मत् the heart or mind, मन to express, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथिन्
मन्मथिन्<BR>mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>Amorous, impassioned, in love.<BR>E.<BR>मन्मथ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मय
मन्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Full of me, like me, (God.)<BR>E.<BR>मत्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यमान
मन्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Thinking, considering.<BR>2 Respecting, attending to.<BR>3 Praising.<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्या
मन्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>The tendon forming the nape of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind, to admire, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्याका
मन्याका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The tendon of the trapezium muscle forming the nape of the neck.<BR>E.<BR>मन्या the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यु|मन्युः
मन्यु<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>1 Sorrow, grief.<BR>2 Distress, indigence.<BR>3 Anger, wrath.<BR>4 A sacrifice.<BR>5 Pride.<BR>E.<BR>मन to know, Uṇādi aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युमत्|मन्युमन्त्
मन्युमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Sorrowful, distressed.<BR>2 Angry, wrathful.<BR>E.<BR>मन्यु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वन्तर|मन्वंतर|मन्वन्तरं
मन्वन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The reign of a MANU, a period equal to seventy-one ages of the gods, or 306,720,000 years of mortals, or with its Sandhi or interval of universal deluge, 308,448,000 years; fourteen Manvantaras constitute a Kalpa; the grand period of creation and destruction, or 4,320,000,000 years; each Manvantara is governed by its distinct MANU, and is provided with its own INDRA, and minor deities; according to Hindu cosmogony, there have been innumerable Manvantaras since the first creation of the world.<BR>E.<BR>मनु MANU, and अन्तर period or interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वान
मन्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Thinking, conceiving.<BR>2 Minding, regarding.<BR>E.<BR>म्ना to mind, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपष्ट|मपष्टः
मपष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo); also मपष्टक, and मपुष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपुष्टक|मपुष्टकः
मपुष्टक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo); also मपष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मभ्र
मभ्र<BR>r. 1st cl. (मभ्रति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममता
ममता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Pride, arrogance, self-sufficiency.<BR>2 The interest or affection entertained for other objects from considering [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">Page644</a>] them as belonging to or connected with one's self.<BR>3 Individuality.<BR>E.<BR>मम mine, the possessive case of अस्मट् I, and तल् aff. of the abstract; also with त्व aff. ममत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=643" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममतायुक्त|ममतायुक्तः
ममतायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Selfish.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A miser, a niggard.<BR>E.<BR>ममता selfishness, and युक्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममापताल|ममापतालः
ममापताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An object of sense.<BR>E.<BR>मव्य to bind, आल Uṇādi aff., य rejected, and म substituted for ब, and आपतुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय|मयः
मय<BR>r. 1st cl. (मयते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय|मयः
मय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A mule.<BR>3 A demon, and the carpenter or architect of the DAITYAS.<BR>4 Hurting, injuring.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Administering remedies, the practice of physic.<BR>E.<BR>मय to go, or मि to scatter, or मी to hurt, aff. अच् or खल् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयट|मयटः
मयट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A hut of grass or leaves.<BR>E.<BR>मय to go, अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयु|मयुः
मयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A Kinnara or chorister of Svarga.<BR>2 A deer.<BR>E.<BR>मि to scatter, (sweet sounds, &c.,) Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुराज|मयुराजः
मयुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>मयु a Kinnara, and राज chief; having these beings attached especially to his court and capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुष्टक|मयुष्टकः
मयुष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>मय to go, aff. उ, मयु one who goes, ष्टक to impede, aff. ड, मयुष्ट, and with the pleonastic addition, कुन् मयुष्टक; also with अच् aff. after मय to go, मयष्ट, and मयष्टक; and again with प substituted for म, मपष्ट, मपष्टक, मपुष्ट or मपुष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूख|मयूखः
मयूख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 Light, lustre, brightness.<BR>2 A ray of light.<BR>3 Flame.<BR>4 Beauty.<BR>5 The pin or gnomon of a sun-dial.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, (time, &c.,) ऊख Uṇādi aff., and मय substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूर|मयूरः
मयूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 A flower, the coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>3 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A peahen.<BR>2 A potherb, (Basella rubra, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मि to scatter, Uṇādi aff. ऊरन् or मही the earth in the seventh case, मह्यां, रु to cry, ड aff., and the formation irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरक|मयूरकं|मयूरकः
मयूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>2 A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचटक|मयूरचटकः
मयूरचटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A house or dunghill cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचूडा
मयूरचूडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>मयूर a peacock, and चूडा the comb or crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरपदक|मयूरपदकं
मयूरपदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of scratch with a finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>मयूर a peacock, पद a foot, and कन् aff. implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरारि|मयूरारिः
मयूरारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A chameleon, a lizard.<BR>E.<BR>मयूर a peacock, and अरि the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरक|मरकः
मरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Epidemic or pestilential disease.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकत|मरकतं
मरकत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>मरक epidemic disease, तॄ to cross or escape, aff. ड; it is also read मरकतक n. (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरक्त|मरक्तं
मरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>An emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरण|मरणं
मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरत|मरतः
मरत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, अतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्द|मरंद|मरंदः|मरन्दः
मरन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The nectar or honey of a flower.<BR>E.<BR>मकरन्द, q. v. the second syllable being rejected; also with कन् added मरन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्दौकस्|मरंदौकस्
मरन्दौकस्<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A flower.<BR>E.<BR>मरन्द nectar or honey, ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मराकाली
मराकाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, commonly Bichati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरार|मरारः
मरार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A granary, a place where grain, &c. is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मराल|मरालः
मराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Soft, mild, bland.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of goose with red legs and bill, or perhaps the Flamingo.<BR>2 Lampblack, used as a collyrium.<BR>3 A duck.<BR>4 A horse.<BR>5 A cloud.<BR>6 A grove or garden of pomegranate trees.<BR>7 A rogue, a scoundrel.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. आलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिच|मरिचं|मरिचः
मरिच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Pepper.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, (venom,) and इच aff.; considered as an antidote; also मरीच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिमन्
मरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीच|मरीचं|मरीचः
मरीच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Pepper, (Piper nigrum.)<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, ईच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचि|मरीचिः
मरीचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>1 A saint, the son of BRAHMĀ, and one of the Prajāpatis, and Brahmādikas, or first created beings, and sovereigns of the world.<BR>2 A niggard, a miser.<BR>mf. (-चिः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to perish, (darkness,) Uṇādi aff. ईचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिका
मरीचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Mirage; vapor which in hot, and sandy countries especially appears at a distance like a sheet of water.<BR>E.<BR>मरीचि a ray of light, कन् aff., implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिमालिन्
मरीचिमालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Splendid, radiant.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>मरीचि, and मालिन् having a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीमृज
मरीमृज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Who or what cleans or rubs repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to rub, reiter. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरु|मरुः
मरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A region or soil destitute of water, sands, a desert.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 The province Marwar, or, in the plu. (-रुवः) The inhabitants.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, (where,) and Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुज|मरुजः
मरुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR>E.<BR>मरु a desert, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुटा
मरुटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A woman with a high forehead.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to perish, (of love for such a woman,) उटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुण्डा|मरुंडा
मरुण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>A woman with a high forehead.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, उण्डच् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्
मरुत्<BR>m. (-रुत्)<BR>1 Wind, air, or its deified personification.<BR>2 A deity, an immortal.<BR>n. (-रुत्)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>f. (-रुत्)<BR>A kind of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, Uṇādi aff. उति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत|मरुतः
मरुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A deity.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpātali.<BR>E.<BR>अच् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्कर|मरुत्करः
मरुत्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, (eructation,) and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्त|मरुत्तः
मरुत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>1 Wind, a gale.<BR>2 The name of a king.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत्, and तप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पथ|मरुत्पथः
मरुत्पथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The atmosphere, sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, and पथ road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पाल|मरुत्पालः
मरुत्पाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पुत्त्र
मरुत्पुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>BHĪMASENA, the second of the PĀṆḌU princes.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the deity of the wind, and पुत्त्र son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्प्लव|मरुत्प्लवः
मरुत्प्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, and प्लव who leaps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्फल|मरुत्फलं
मरुत्फल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्वत्|मरुत्वन्त्
मरुत्वत्<BR>m. (-त्वान्)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 The monkey Hanumān.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्सख|मरुत्सखः
मरुत्सख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, (the deity,) and सखि friend, aff. टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुदान्दोल|मरुदांदोल|मरुदान्दोलः
मरुदान्दोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of fan made of deer's or buffalo's skin.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, आन्दोल agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=644" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्ध्वज|मरुद्ध्वजं
मरुद्ध्वज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Flocculent seeds wafted by the wind.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, ध्वज standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्बद्ध|मरुद्बद्धः
मरुद्बद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A sort of vessel used in sacrifices.<BR>3 A portion of the Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्रथ|मरुद्रथः
मरुद्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A car in which idols are carried.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्रुम|मरुद्रुमः
मरुद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A fœtid mimosa.<BR>E.<BR>मरु dry, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वर्त्मन्
मरुद्वर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>The atmosphere, heaven, sky.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, and वर्त्मन् road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वाह|मरुद्वाहः
मरुद्वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Smoke.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् wind, and वाह vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्विप|मरुद्विपः
मरुद्विप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>मरु the desert, and द्विप the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वृता
मरुद्वृता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The Kāverī river in the peninsula.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् the wind, and वृत covered, screened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुन्माला
मरुन्माला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>2 Another plant, commonly Belśunṭh.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत् a deity, and माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुप्रिय|मरुप्रियः
मरुप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>मरु a sandy soil, and प्रिय fond of; it also occurs मरुत्प्रिय m. (-यः) from मरुत् wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुभू
मरुभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The province of Marwar, or plu. (-भुवः) The inhabitants of Marwar.<BR>E.<BR>मरु sandy, and भू country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुल|मरुलः
मरुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of duck.<BR>E.<BR>मॄ to die, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुवक|मरुवकः
मरुवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A large thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>2 A species of basil (Ocymum), described as having small leaves and red flowers.<BR>3 A variety of the citron or lime, said to be a thorny plant, and to bear a small fruit.<BR>4 A flower, (Artemisia vulgaris.)<BR>5 A tiger.<BR>6 The ascending node.<BR>7 A crane.<BR>E.<BR>मरु a sandy or dry soil, वा to grow or go, aff. क, and कन् added; it sometimes occurs, मरूवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुस्थल
मरुस्थल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>A desart, a dry and desart tract.<BR>E.<BR>मरु, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरूक|मरूकः
मरूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, ऊकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरूद्भवा
मरूद्भवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 A cucumber.<BR>2 Wild cotton.<BR>3 A small species of the fœtid mimosa.<BR>4 A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>मरु dry soil, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरोलि|मरोलिः
मरोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The Makara, a marine monster, apparently the Monodon or unicorn, and usually confounded with the crocodile or shark.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, (by it,) ओलिच् aff.; also with कन् added मरोलिक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्क|मर्कः
मर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 The air, the wind.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>मर्च to sound, or a Sautra root, to move, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कक|मर्ककः
मर्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>मर्क going, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कट|मर्कटः
मर्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A monkey or ape.<BR>2 A spider.<BR>3 The large crane, called in India the adjutant, (Ardea argala.)<BR>4 A kind of venom.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A variety of grey Bonduc, (Guilandina bonduccella.)<BR>2 Cowatch, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>3 A small or female monkey.<BR>E.<BR>मर्क a Sautra root, to go, Uṇādi aff. अटन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटक|मर्कटकः
मर्कटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 An ape.<BR>3 A fruit.<BR>4 A demon.<BR>5 A fish.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटपिप्पली
मर्कटपिप्पली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>मर्कट an ape, and पिप्पली long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटप्रिय|मर्कटप्रियः
मर्कटप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tree, a kind of Mimosa, (M. kauki.)<BR>E.<BR>मर्कट a monkey, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटवास|मर्कटवासः
मर्कटवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A spider's web, a cobweb.<BR>E.<BR>मर्कट a spider, and वास abode; also with कन् added मर्कटवासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटास्य|मर्कटास्यं
मर्कटास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>मर्कट a monkey, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटेन्दु|मर्कटेंदु|मर्कटेन्दुः
मर्कटेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A sort of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्करा
मर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A cave, a hole, a chasm.<BR>2 A vessel.<BR>3 A barren or childless woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्च|मर्च्च
मर्च<BR>r. 4th and 10th cls. (मर्चति मर्चयति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ज्जू|मर्जू
मर्ज्जू<BR>f. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>Cleaning, cleansing, purification.<BR>m. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>1 A washerman.<BR>2 A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, aff. ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त|मर्त|मर्तः|मर्त्तः
मर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A man, a mortal.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, तन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्तव्य|मर्तव्य
मर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Mortal, what must or should die.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त्य
मर्त्त्य<BR>m. (-र्त्त्यः)<BR>1 A man, a mortal.<BR>2 The earth, the world, the habitation of mortals.<BR>f. (-र्त्त्या)<BR>A woman, a female.<BR>E.<BR>मर्त्त as above, यत् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त्यमुख
मर्त्त्यमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A demigod, attendant on KUVERA, a Kinnara, a Yakṣa.<BR>E.<BR>मर्त्त्य a mortal, and मुख chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दन|मर्दन|मर्द्दनं
मर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing, touching.<BR>2 Rubbing, grinding, pounding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to rub or grind, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दनीय|मर्दनीय
मर्द्दनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be rubbed or touched.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to rub, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दयित्वा|मर्दयित्वा
मर्द्दयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having rubbed or touched.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to rub, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दल|मर्दल|मर्दलः|मर्द्दलः
मर्द्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of drum.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to rub or strike, aff. अच्; मर्द्द striking, and ला to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दित|मर्दित|मर्द्दितं
मर्द्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strung, tied.<BR>2 Rubbed, ground, pounded.<BR>3 Obtained, got.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to rub, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ब|मर्ब्ब
मर्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (मर्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मज्ञ|मर्मज्ञ|मर्मज्ञः|मर्म्मज्ञः
मर्म्मज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A learned and intelligent man or Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म secret meaning (of the Śāstras), and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मन्|मर्मन्
मर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 A joint, an articulation of the body.<BR>2 A vital member or organ.<BR>3 Secret meaning or purpose, a secret, any thing hidden or recondite.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मभेदिन्|मर्मभेदिन्
मर्म्मभेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Fatal.<BR>2 Penetrating, piercing.<BR>3 Painful.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म, and भेदिन् what cuts or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मर|मर्मर|मर्मरः|मर्म्मरः
मर्म्मर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The rustling sound of cloth or dry leaves.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of pine, (P. Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, अरन् aff., and मुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मरीक|मर्मरीक|मर्मरीकः|मर्म्मरीकः
मर्म्मरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pauper, a low or humble man.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, (with distress,) Uṇādi aff. ईकन्, and the root reduplicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मविद्|मर्मविद्
मर्म्मविद्<BR>m. (-विट् or -वित्)<BR>A learned and intelligent man or Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म secret meaning (of the Śāstras), and विट् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मवेदिन्|मर्मवेदिन्
मर्म्मवेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An acute and intelligent man.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म secret, and वेदिन् who knows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मस्पृश्|मर्मस्पृश्
मर्म्मस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Sharp, corrosive, giving pain.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म a joint, and स्पृश् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्माविध्|मर्माविध्
मर्म्माविध्<BR>mfn. (-विद् or -वित्)<BR>Piercing or affecting the joints, (pain, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म a joint, व्यध to pierce or pain, aff. क्विप्; the semivowel and following vowel of the radical changed to इ, and the final vowel of the noun made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मिक|मर्मिक|मर्म्मिकः
मर्म्मिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An intelligent and penetrating man.<BR>E.<BR>मर्म्म a joint, and ठक् aff.: see मर्म्मविट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=645" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्य्या|मर्या
मर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A boundary, a limit.<BR>ind.<BR>Bounding, limitative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्य्यादा|मर्यादा
मर्य्यादा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Continuance in the right way, propriety of conduct, steadiness, rectitude.<BR>2 A boundary, a limit.<BR>3 A bank, a shore.<BR>E.<BR>मर्य्या limitative, आदा to have or take, aff. अङ् and टाप्; or परि about, round, prefixed to आदा, and म substituted for प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्व|मर्व्व
मर्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (मर्वति)<BR>1 To fill.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्श|मर्शः
मर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Counsel, advice.<BR>E.<BR>मृश to counsel, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्शण
मर्शण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Advising, counselling, deliberating.<BR>E.<BR>मृश to counsel, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ष|मर्षः
मर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Patience, endurance.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear with, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षण|मर्षणं
मर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Enduring, bearing, patience, resignation.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear with, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षित|मर्षितः
मर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Borne, endured.<BR>2 Patient, content.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Patience.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear with, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षितवत्
मर्षितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान-वती-वत्)<BR>Patient, enduring.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल|मलः
मल<BR>r. 1st cl. (मलते) 10th cl. (मलयति)<BR>1 To hold.<BR>2 To wear.<BR>3 To stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल|मलः
मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Dirty.<BR>2 Miserly, niggardly.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Excretion of the body, as serum, semen, blood, marrow, urine, fæces, earwax, nails, phlegm, tears, rheum, and sweat.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>3 Dirt, filth.<BR>4 Dreg, sediment.<BR>5 Rust.<BR>6 Camphor.<BR>7 Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta): see झटामला.<BR>E.<BR>मल to hold or contain, (in the body,) अच् aff., or मृज to cleanse, Uṇādi aff. कल, and the penultimate and final radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलज|मलजं
मलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced from dregs or dirt, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Pus, matter.<BR>E.<BR>मल as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलदूषित|मलदूषितं
मलदूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Foul, dirty, filthy.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, दूषित faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलन|मलनं|मलनः
मलन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tent.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rubbing, grinding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मल to hold, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपङ्किन्
मलपङ्किन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्की-ङ्किनी-ङ्कि)<BR>Filthy, covered with mud and dirt.<BR>E.<BR>मल, and पङ्क mud, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपू
मलपू<BR>f. (-पूः)<BR>The opposite-leaved fig tree, (Ficus oppositifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>मल sin, पू to purify, aff. क्विप्; it is also read with a final consonant, derived from पूर to complete or fill, मलपूर् f. (-पूः) Also मलयू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलभुज्
मलभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलय|मलयः
मलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A mountain or mountainous range, from which the best Sandal wood is brought, answering to the western Ghāts in the peninsula of India.<BR>2 The country that lies along the Malaya range, or the west coast of the peninsula, Malayālam or Malabar.<BR>3 A garden.<BR>4 The garden of INDRA.<BR>5 One of the minor Dvīpas or divisions of the world.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, commonly Tëori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>E.<BR>मल to hold or contain (Sandal wood), Uṇādi aff. कयन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयगन्धिनी
मलयगन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>One of DURGĀ'S female attendants.<BR>E.<BR>मलय the mountain, and गन्धिन् fragrant; also मलयवासिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयज|मलयजं|मलयजः
मलयज<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>मलय the mountain Malaya, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयाचल|मलयाचलः
मलयाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mountain Malaya.<BR>E.<BR>मलय Malaya, and अचल a mountain; also similar compounds, as मलयाद्रि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयानिल|मलयानिलः
मलयानिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The southerly wind that prevails in central India during the hot weather.<BR>E.<BR>मलय the Malaya mountain, over which the air is supposed to have blown, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयू
मलयू<BR>f. (-यूः)<BR>The opposite-leaved fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>मल sin, यु to join, aff. क्विप्, and the final made long; also with the final short मलयु, or derived from पूञ्, मलपू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलवाहिन्
मलवाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>What conveys or contains soil or filth.<BR>E.<BR>मल, and वाहिन् bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाकर्षिन्
मलाकर्षिन्<BR>m. (-र्षी)<BR>A sweeper, a cleaner.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, fæces, and कृष to draw, with आङ् prefix, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाका
मलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A female messenger.<BR>2 A lewd woman.<BR>3 A female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलापकर्षण|मलापकर्षणं
मलापकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Purification, cleaning, cleansing.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, excrescence, अपकर्षण removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलावह|मलावहं
मलावह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Soiling, dirtying.<BR>2 Defiling, disgracing.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Acceptance of forbidden gifts.<BR>E.<BR>मल, and आवह what brings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलि|मलिः
मलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Having, possession.<BR>E.<BR>मल to hold, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिन|मलिनं
मलिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Dirty, filthy, foul.<BR>2 Black.<BR>3 Vile, bad.<BR>4 Foul, (figuratively,) soiled with crime or vice, sinful, depraved.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Buttermilk.<BR>2 Fault, defect.<BR>3 Borax.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, इनच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनप्रभ
मलिनप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Obscured, beclouded.<BR>E.<BR>मलिन, and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनमुख|मलिनमुखः
मलिनमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>1 Cruel, fierce, savage.<BR>2 Vile, wicked.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 AGNI or fire.<BR>2 A ghost, a goblin.<BR>3 The black-faced monkey.<BR>E.<BR>मलिन black, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनाम्बु|मलिनांबु
मलिनाम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>Ink.<BR>E.<BR>मलिन dirty, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनास्य|मलिनास्यः
मलिनास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A savage, a cruel or ferocious man.<BR>E.<BR>मलिन black, foul, (with fury,) and आस्य the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनित
मलिनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Soiled, defiled.<BR>2 Corrupted, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>मलिन, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिम्लुच|मलिम्लुचः
मलिम्लुच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 Burning, blazing.<BR>3 Fire, air, wind.<BR>4 The intercalary lunar month, introduced every third year, in order to approximate the lunar, and solar modes of computation.<BR>5 A gnat, a musquito.<BR>6 Frost.<BR>E.<BR>मलि possession, and म्लुच to steal, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिष्ठ
मलिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Very foul or unclean.<BR>2 Very wicked.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>मल unclean, इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलीमस|मलीमसं|मलीमसः
मलीमस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>1 Dirty, foul, unclean.<BR>2 Wicked.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 Green vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, ईमसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलीयस्
मलीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very dirty or impure.<BR>2 Very wicked.<BR>E.<BR>मल, and ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलूक|मलूकः
मलूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of worm.<BR>E.<BR>मल dirt, ऊकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल|मल्लः
मल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (मल्लते)<BR>To hold, to have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल|मल्लः
मल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>1 Strong, stout, athletic, robust.<BR>2 Best, excellent.<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 A wrestler, a boxer, by birth; the offspring of an outcaste Kṣatriya by a Kṣatriya female.<BR>2 A cup or vessel.<BR>3 The cheek and temples, the hemicranium.<BR>4 A kind of fish.<BR>5 The residue of an oblation.<BR>f. (-ल्ला)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 Arabian jasmine.<BR>3 Ornamenting the person with coloured unguents.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल to hold, and aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=646" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लक|मल्लकः
मल्लक<BR>mf. (-ल्लकः-ल्लिका)<BR>An oil vessel, a vessel made of the shell of a cocoanut for holding oil, whether for culinary purposes or for burning as a lamp.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल to hold, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लज|मल्लजं
मल्लज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लतूर्य्य|मल्लतूर्य|मल्लतूर्य्यं
मल्लतूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A musical instrument, a drum or trumpet used at athletic contests.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल a wrestler, and तूर्य्य an instrument of music; it also occurs गन्धतूर्य्यं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लनाग|मल्लनागः
मल्लनाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The elephant of INDRA.<BR>2 A name of the saint VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>2 A letter-carrier.<BR>4 A work on amorous topics by VĀTSYĀYANA Muni.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल strong, and नाग an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लभू
मल्लभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A palæstrum or arena, a place for athletic contests; it is also applied to the site of any conflict, as a field of battle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल a wrestler, and भू earth, place; also मल्लभूमि f. (-मिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लयाचा
मल्लयाचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>A match of wrestling or boxing.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल a wrestler, and याचा a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लयुद्ध|मल्लयुद्धं
मल्लयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Wrestling, boxing.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल a wrestler, and युद्ध contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लारी
मल्लारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or divisions of the musical mode Megha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लि|मल्लिः
मल्लि<BR>m. (-ल्लिः)<BR>1 Having, holding.<BR>2 One of the Jinas or Jaina saints, the 19th of the present era.<BR>f. (-ल्लिः-ल्लि)<BR>Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल to hold, Uṇādi aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिक|मल्लिकः
मल्लिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bird, said to be a sort of goose with brown legs and bill.<BR>2 A shuttle.<BR>3 The month Māgha.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>2 A kind of fish.<BR>3 An earthen vessel for holding oil, &c.<BR>4 A goblet, a cup, a drinking vessel.<BR>6 A river.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to मल्लि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिकाक्ष|मल्लिकाक्षः
मल्लिकाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A horse marked with white about the eyes.<BR>2 A sort of goose with brown legs and bill.<BR>E.<BR>मल्लिका the jasmine, and अक्ष the eye, being of like whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिकापुष्प|मल्लिकापुष्पः
मल्लिकापुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>मल्लिका the same, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिगन्धि|मल्लिगंधि
मल्लिगन्धि<BR>n. (-न्धिः)<BR>Aloe wood.<BR>E.<BR>मल्लि jasmine, and गन्धि smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिपच
मल्लिपच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लु|मल्लुः
मल्लु<BR>m. (-ल्लुः)<BR>A bear.<BR>E.<BR>मल्ल to hold, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मव
मव<BR>r. 1st cl. (-मवति)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मवित|मवितः
मवित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Strung, tied.<BR>E.<BR>मू to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मव्य
मव्य<BR>r. 1st cl. (मव्यति)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मश|मशः
मश<BR>r. 1st cl. (मशति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To be angry or irascible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मश|मशः
मश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Anger.<BR>2 Sounding.<BR>3 A musquito.<BR>E.<BR>मश to sound, &c., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशक|मशकः
मशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A gnat, a musquito.<BR>2 A kind of cutaneous eruption, the formation of small pustules or warts.<BR>3 A leather water bag.<BR>E.<BR>मश to be angry, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशकिन्
मशकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>The glomerous fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>मशक a gnat, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशछद|मशच्छद
मशछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशहरी
मशहरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Musquito curtains, bed curtains of gauze, or of any thin substance, used to keep off musquitoes.<BR>E.<BR>मश a musquito, हृ to take off, ट and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशुन|मशुनः
मशुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मष
मष<BR>r. 1st cl. (मषति)<BR>To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मषि|मषिः
मषि<BR>f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>1 Ink.<BR>2 The stalk of the Nyctanthes tristis.<BR>E.<BR>मष to hurt, इन् aff.; also मशि or मसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस|मसः
मस<BR>(इर, ई) इर् मसी r. 4th cl. (मस्यति)<BR>1 To mete or measure by weight, bulk, length, &c.<BR>2 To change form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस|मसः
मस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Measure.<BR>2 Weight.<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसक|मसकः
मसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gnat.<BR>E.<BR>मष to hurt, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसन|मसनं
मसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Hurting.<BR>2 Measuring.<BR>3 A medicinal fruit, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>मष to hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसार|मसारः
मसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An emerald.<BR>E.<BR>मस weight, ऋ to go or get, aff. अण्; also with कन् added मसारक; in some places it seems to be confounded with another gem of a blue colour, perhaps the sapphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसि|मसिः
मसि<BR>mf. (-सिः-सी)<BR>1 Ink.<BR>2 The stalk of the Nyctanthes tristis.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, Uṇādi aff. इन्; it also occurs, मशि, मशी, मषि, and मषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिक|मसिकः
मसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake's hole.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>2 Ink.<BR>E.<BR>मसि the stalk of the plant, &c., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिकूपी
मसिकूपी<BR>f. (-पी)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, कूपी a little well; also with कन् added मसिकूपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिधान|मसिधानं
मसिधान<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, and घान what holds or contains; also मशिधान, मषिधान, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिन|मसिनं
मसिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Alliance by the right of presenting the funeral meat balls to a deceased common progenitor (?)<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure, (affinity,) Uṇādi aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिपण्य|मसिपण्यः
मसिपण्य<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>A scribe, a clerk, an accountant.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, पण्य hireable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिपथ|मसिपथः
मसिपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>मसि, and पथ path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिप्रसू
मसिप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, प्रसू parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिमणि|मसिमणिः
मसिमणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिवर्द्धन
मसिवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>मसि ink, वृद्ध to increase, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीजल|मसीजलं
मसीजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Writing ink.<BR>E.<BR>मसी ink, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीधानी
मसीधानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मसी ink, धानी what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीना
मसीना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसुर|मसुरः
मसुर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>A sort of lentil or pulse, (Ervum hirsutum, or Cicer lens)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, Uṇādi aff. उरच्; more usually मसूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूर|मसूरः
मसूर<BR>mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>A sort of pulse or lentil, (Ervum hirsutum, and Cicer lens)<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A whore.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Small-pox.<BR>2 A small round pillow.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, Uṇādi aff. ऊरन्, मसूर, the pulse; the other meanings refer to this, implying resemblance to the pea in figure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरक|मसूरकः
मसूरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small round pillow.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरविदला
मसूरविदला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A black variety of the plant, commonly called Tëori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>2 A twining shrub, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>मसूर pulse, विदल division; having a leaf like a split pea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरिका
मसूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bawd, a procuress.<BR>2 Small-pox.<BR>E.<BR>मसूरा a whore, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसृण|मसृणं
मसृण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Smooth, soft, not hard, not rough.<BR>2 Bland, mild, unctuous.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Linseed.<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">Page648</a>] or weigh, aff. ऋण, form irr.; or सम equally, smoothly, ऋण to go or be, aff. क, and the initiatory letters irregularly transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=647" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्क
मस्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (मस्कते)<BR>To go, to move: sometimes read मस्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्कर|मस्करः
मस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>मस्क to go, aff. अर, or मकि to adorn, aff. अर, and the nasal rejected, with सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्करिन्
मस्करिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 The Brahman of the fourth and mendicant order.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>मस्कर a bambu, (staff,) and इनि possess. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्ज
मस्ज<BR>(टु ओ) टुमस्जो r. 6th cl. (मज्जति)<BR>1 To immerse, to sink or plunge in water.<BR>2 To purify by washing or bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्त|मस्तं
मस्त<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>The head: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तक|मस्तकं|मस्तकः
मस्तक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The head, the skull.<BR>2 The head or top of any thing.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकस्नेह|मस्तकस्नेहः
मस्तकस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The brain.<BR>E.<BR>मस्तक the head, and स्नेह marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकाख्य|मस्तकाख्यः
मस्तकाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>मस्तक the head, and आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकमूलक
मस्तकमूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The neck, the upper part of it supporting the head.<BR>E.<BR>मस्तक the head, मूल the root, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्ति|मस्तिः
मस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>Weighing, measuring.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तिस्क
मस्तिस्क<BR>m. (-स्कः)<BR>The brain.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ति, मस्क to go or get, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तु
मस्तु<BR>n. (-स्तुः)<BR>The watery part of curds, the whey.<BR>E.<BR>मस to weigh, Uṇādi aff. तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तुलुङ्ग|मस्तुलुंग|मस्तुलुङ्गः
मस्तुलुङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The brain; it also occurs मस्तुलुङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह|महं|महः
मह<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (महति महयति)<BR>To revere, to worship, to adore.<BR>(इ,) महि r. 1st cl. (मंहते)<BR>To grow or increase.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मंहयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह|महं|महः
मह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A festival.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 A buffalo.<BR>4 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. घञ्: see महस and महि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महक|महकः
महक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An excellent man.<BR>2 A tortoise.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महक्क|महक्कः
महक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>Diffusive fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्|महन्त्
महत्<BR>mfn. (-हान्-हती-हत्)<BR>1 Great, large, bulky.<BR>2 Much, many.<BR>3 Best, excellent, illustrious.<BR>n. (-त्)<BR>1 Kingdom, dominion.<BR>2 The intellectual principle, the second principle in creation.<BR>adv.<BR>Much, very, exceeding.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The Vīṇā or lute of NĀRADA, containing seven or one hundred strings.<BR>2 The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, अति Uṇādi aff. In composition, महा is generally substituted, आ being inserted in place of the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्तर|महत्तरः
महत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Greater, more.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man of the fourth or servile tribe, a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>महत् great, and तरप् aff. of comparison, perhaps in derision, or in comparison with the mixed tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्त्व|महत्त्वं
महत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>Greatness, either in bulk or rank.<BR>E.<BR>महत् great, त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महदाश्वर्य्य
महदाश्वर्य्य<BR>n. adv. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Very surprising.<BR>E.<BR>महत्, and आश्चर्य्य surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महद्विल
महद्विल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Æther, heaven, Ākāśa.<BR>E.<BR>महत् great, and विल a variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महदाश्रय|महदाश्रयः
महदाश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dependant upon or attached to the great.<BR>E.<BR>महत्, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्लोक|महर्लोकः
महर्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A division of the universe; a region said to be one Crore of Yojanas above the polar star, and to be the abode of those saints who survive a destruction of the world.<BR>E.<BR>महस् sacrifice, लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्षि|महर्षिः
महर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi or saint of a particular order, including VYĀSA, and others.<BR>E.<BR>मह for महत् great, and ऋषि a saint: see राजर्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महल्लक|महल्लकः
महल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An eunuch employed in a Hāram.<BR>E.<BR>महल्ल said to mean the inner apartments, probably the Arabic word محل and कन् added; otherwise with ठक् added महल्लिक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस्
महस्<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>1 A festival, a sacred festival.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 Greatness, vigour.<BR>4 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस|महसं
महस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>2 Kind, sort, difference.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकच्छ|महाकच्छः
महाकच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 The deity of the ocean VARUṆA.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कच्छ a shore or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकण्टकिनी
महाकण्टकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The Indian prickly pear, (Cactus Indicus.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, कण्टक a thorn, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकन्द|महाकंद|महाकन्दः
महाकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Garlic.<BR>2 A very large esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR>3 A plant, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकपित्थ|महाकपित्थः
महाकपित्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कपित्थ wood apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर
महाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Large-handed, &c.<BR>2 Having a large revenue.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large hand, rent, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and कर a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाय|महाकायः
महाकाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Large, bulky, stout.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name of NANDI, the door-keeper and attendant of ŚIVA.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाल|महाकालः
महाकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name or rather a form of ŚIVA, in his character of the destroying deity, being then represented of a black colour, and of aspect more or less terrific.<BR>2 A name of NANDI, ŚIVA'S porter and attendant.<BR>3 The mango tree.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The wife of the preceding deity, and a terrific form of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>3 One of the Vidyādevīs of the same sect.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, excessively, काल black, or time; in one capacity that of जगद्भक्षकः the world-eater, ŚIVA or MAHĀKĀLA may be considered as a personification of time that destroys all things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाव्य|महाकाव्यं
महाकाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A regular and classical poem.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and काव्य a poem: the title is applied especially to six works; the Kumāra Sambhava, Raghu Vaṃśa, and Megha Dūta of KĀLIDĀSA; the Kirātārjunīya of BHĀRAVĪ; the Naiṣadhīya of ŚRĪHARṢA, and the Śiśupāla Badha of MĀGHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुल|महाकुलः
महाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Eminent by birth, of good family or extraction.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कुल lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुलीन|महाकुलीनः
महाकुलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of good family.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कुलीन of family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकूप|महाकूपः
महाकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A large or deep well.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकूल|महाकूलः
महाकूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a good family.<BR>E.<BR>see महाकुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाक्षीर|महाक्षीरः
महाक्षीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग
महाग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Great, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=648" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागद|महागदः
महागद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Fever.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and गद sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागन्ध|महागंध|महागन्धं|महागन्धः
महागन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A sort of cane growing near water, (Calamus fasciculatus, Rox.)<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A name or form of DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागिरि|महागिरिः
महागिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 Any large mountain.<BR>2 A sacred personage peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग्रीव|महाग्रीवः
महाग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and ग्रीवा a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग्रीविन्
महाग्रीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, ग्रीवा neck, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघास|महाघासः
महाघास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Abounding with grass or fodder.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and घास grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघूर्णा
महाघूर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, much, घूर्ण to roll, aff. अच्, and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघोर|महाघोरः
महाघोर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very formidable, terrific, horrible.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A division of Tartarus or hell.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, much, and घोर terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघोष|महाघोषं|महाघोषः
महाघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A great noise, a loud sound.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A market, a fair.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A plant, commonly called Karkaṭaśṛṅgī or Crab's horn, described as a climbing and milky plant, and supposed to be the Asclepias geminata.<BR>2 Gum olibanum tree.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, घोष sound, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाङ्ग|महांग|महाङ्गः
महाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Bulky, big, large-bodied.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाचण्ड|महाचण्डः
महाचण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 One of YAMA'S attendants.<BR>2 A very violent or passionate man.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, much, चण्ड hot, passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाज|महाजः
महाज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Illustrious, high-born.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A large goat.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and अज a goat, or ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजन|महाजनः
महाजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A virtuous or illustrious man, a great man.<BR>2 A merchant, a trader.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, जन a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजम्बू
महाजम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>A plant, perhaps a kind of Eugenia.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and जम्बू the rose apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजातीय|महाजातीयः
महाजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of an excellent sort or species.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, जातीय of a species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजाली
महाजाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, a sort of Ghoṣa, with yellow flowers.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाज्वाल|महाज्वालः
महाज्वाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>One of the Vidyādevīs or goddesses peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, ज्वाल flame, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातमप्रभा
महातमप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The lowermost division of Naraka or hell.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, तम darkness, and प्रभा flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातरु|महातरुः
महातरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Euphorbia of various kinds.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातल|महातलं
महातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The fifth in descent of the seven Pātālas or regions under the earth, inhabited by various races of evil beings, as the Nāgas, Asuras, Daityas, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and तल depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातारा
महातारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A goddess of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातिक्त|महातिक्तः
महातिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Very bitter.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>The large Nimb tree, (Melia sempervirens.)<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknadhi.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातीक्ष्ण
महातीक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Very sharp (as flavour), or literally (as a weapon), or figuratively, (as perception, &c.)<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>The marking-nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>महा great or much, तीक्ष्ण sharp, acrid, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातेजस्
महातेजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>1 Very bright.<BR>2 Very energetic or vigorous.<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>1 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 AGNI, the deity of fire.<BR>3 A hero, a demigod.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and तेजस् light or glory, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्मन्
महात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Liberal, lofty-minded, magnanimous.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, आत्मन् self, soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादन्त|महादंत|महादन्तः
महादन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 An elephant with large tusks.<BR>2 An elephant's tusk.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादारु
महादारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A sort of pine, (P. Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादेव|महादेवः
महादेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and देव god; the epithet Mahā compounded with a substantive forms many appellatives of these deities especially; thus, ŚIVA is Mahākāla, Mahārudra, Maheśvara, &c. and DURGĀ is named Mahākāyā, Mahāsmṛti, Mahāmedhā, Mahāmohā, &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादुन्दु
महादुन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>A large military drum.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, दुन्दु a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाद्रुम|महाद्रुमः
महाद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधन|महाधनं
महाधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Rich, opulent.<BR>2 Costly, precious, valuable.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any thing costly or precious.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 Incense.<BR>4 Costly raiment.<BR>5 Agriculture.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, घन wealth or price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधातु|महाधातुः
महाधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, chief, and धातु mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानट|महानटः
महानट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and नट a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन्द|महानंद|महानन्दः
महानन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Eternal emancipation or beatitude.<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Wine.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानरक|महानरकः
महानरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>One of the hells or divisions of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and नरक hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानस|महानसं|महानसः
महानस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>A kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, chief, अनस rice or food, टच् added; to which the food is conveyed to be dressed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानाद|महानादः
महानाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A large black rainy cloud.<BR>2 A loud sound.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 A lion.<BR>5 The ear.<BR>6 A camel.<BR>7 A conch shell.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and नाद noise or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिद्रा
महानिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिम्ब|महानिम्बः
महानिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A large kind of Nimb tree, (Melia sempervirens).<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and निम्ब the Nimb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिशा
महानिशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानीच|महानीचः
महानीच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, much, and नीच vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानील|महानीलः
महानील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The emerald.<BR>2 One of the Nāgas.<BR>3 A plant, (Verbesina scandens, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानुभाव|महानुभावः
महानुभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Magnanimous, liberal.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A gentleman.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, अनुभाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानेमि|महानेमिः
महानेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापक्ष|महापक्षः
महापक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A sort of duck.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and पक्ष a side, a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापच
महापच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A potherb.<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>A kind of Eugenia.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and पच a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापथ|महापथः
महापथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The principal path or entrance to a town or house, &c., a main road, a highway.<BR>2 The end of life, the way of all flesh.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, and पथ road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=649" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापथगम|महापथगमः
महापथगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Dying.<BR>E.<BR>महापथ the great way, (by which all mortals travel,) and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापद्म|महापद्मः
महापद्म<BR>m. (-द्मः)<BR>1 One of the principal Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR>2 One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or treasures.<BR>3 A large number, one hundred thousand millions.<BR>4 A Kinnara or attendant on KUVERA.<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>The large white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापातक|महापातकं
महापातक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A crime of the highest degree, as, killing a Brahman, stealing gold from a priest, drinking spirits, adultery with the wife of a spiritual teacher, and associating with persons who have committed these offences.<BR>2 Great crime in general.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, पातक offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापातकिन्
महापातकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>An offender in the highest degree: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>महापातक great sin, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापाप|महापापं
महापाप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 A sin of the highest kind: see महापातक.<BR>2 Heinous crime, or sin in general.<BR>E.<BR>महा excessive, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापासक|महापासकः
महापासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुरुष|महापुरुषः
महापुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A great man.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुरुषदन्ता
महापुरुषदन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुष्पा
महापुष्पा<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A flower, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रभ|महाप्रभः
महाप्रभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Very bright, splendid.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Lamp light, the light of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, प्रभा shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रभु|महाप्रभुः
महाप्रभु<BR>m. (-भुः)<BR>1 A holy man, a saint.<BR>2 A king.<BR>3 INDRA.<BR>4 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, and प्रभु master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रलय|महाप्रलयः
महाप्रलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A destruction of the world, occurring after every period of 4,320,000,000 years.<BR>2 A total destruction of the universe, happening after a period commensurate with the life of BRAHMĀ, or 100 years, each day of which is equal to the period first stated, and each night of which is of similar duration; at the expiration of this term, the seven Lokas, with the saints, gods, and BRAHMĀ himself, are annihilated.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्राण|महाप्राणः
महाप्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A raven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाफल|महाफलः
महाफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A bitter gourd: see इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाफेणा
महाफेणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and फेण froth, foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबल|महाबलं|महाबलः
महाबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, robust, powerful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Lead.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of Sida with yellow flowers, (S. rhombifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great or much, and बल strong, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबाहु|महाबाहुः
महाबाहु<BR>mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु)<BR>Having long arms.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबोधि|महाबोधिः
महाबोधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A Buddha, a deified teacher of the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and बोधि a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाब्राह्मण|महाब्राह्मणः
महाब्राह्मण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A priest who officiates at funeral ceremonies.<BR>2 An eminent Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and ब्राह्मण a Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभद्रा
महाभद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>The Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and भद्रा propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाग
महाभाग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Virtuous in a high degree, pure, holy.<BR>2 Eminent, exalted.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभागता
महाभागता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Possession of the eight cardinal virtues, clemency, &c.<BR>2 Exalted station or merit.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, महाभागत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीत
महाभीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very timid, pusillanimous, cowardly<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A sort of sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>महा much, भीत frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीम|महाभीमः
महाभीम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of ŚĀNTANU.<BR>2 One of ŚIVA'S chamberlains.<BR>E.<BR>महा great or much, and भीम formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीरु|महाभीरुः
महाभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A sort of beetle, found in cow-dung.<BR>E.<BR>महा, much, भीरु fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीष्म|महाभीष्मः
महाभीष्म<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>A name of ŚĀNTANU, a sovereign, and the father of BHĪṢMA.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and भीष्म formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभूत|महाभूतं|महाभूतः
महाभूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A primary element: as air, fire, water, earth, and Ākāśa or ether.<BR>E.<BR>महा principal, and भूत element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामति|महामतिः
महामति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Magnanimous, high-minded.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामद|महामदः
महामद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 An elephant in rut.<BR>2 Great pride or intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and मद fury, or the fluid that issues from the animal's temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामनस्
महामनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>Magnanimous, high-minded, liberal, munificent.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, मनस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामन्त्रिन्|महामंत्रिन्
महामन्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-न्त्री)<BR>The prime minister.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and मन्त्रिन् a counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामहिमन्
महामहिमन्<BR>mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>Very great, high and mighty.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and महिमन् greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्र|महामात्रः
महामात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A king's minister or associate, any high officer in a kingdom: as a counsellor, a general, &c.<BR>2 An elephant driver, a Mahout.<BR>3 Superintendant of the elephants.<BR>4 A man of wealth and consequence.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>1 The wife of a spiritual preceptor.<BR>2 The wife of an officer of state, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and मात्र wealth or retinue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामानसी
महामानसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाया
महामाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 Worldly illusion or unreality.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and माया illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामारी
महामारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and मारी destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाष|महामाषः
महामाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and माष the Phaseolus radiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामुख|महामुखः
महामुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A crocodile, an alligator.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामुनि|महामुनिः
महामुनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A name of AGASTYA.<BR>2 A name of Buddha, or more properly, of any one of the sacred persons called by that name.<BR>3 The epithet of a warlike saint, celebrated in the Mahābhārata.<BR>4 Time.<BR>5 A name of VYĀSA.<BR>n. (-नि)<BR>Coriander.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and मुनि saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामूल्य|महामूल्यं|महामूल्यः
महामूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Costly, precious.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृग|महामृगः
महामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, मृग an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृत्यु|महामृत्युः
महामृत्यु<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामेद|महामेदः
महामेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The coral tree, (Erythrina Indica.)<BR>2 A drug, classed amongst the principal drugs, and described as a tonic, and stimulant.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and मेद marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामैत्र|महामैत्रः
महामैत्र<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect, or a Buddha or form of him.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, मैच friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्ल|महाम्लं
महाम्ल<BR>mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं)<BR>Very acid.<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Acid seasoning.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, very, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=650" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायक्ष|महायक्षः
महायक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A sort of demigod, supposed to attend the Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and यक्ष a divine being, attending usually on KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायज्ञ|महायज्ञः
महायज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>An essential sacrifice, a sacrament of the Hindu religion; five acts are enumerated of this description, severally considered as due to the Vedas, to the gods, to man, to the manes, and to all created beings; they are respectively, study of scripture, offering of sacrifice to the gods, hospitable treatment of guests, libation of water, &c. to deceased progenitors, and the casting of food on the ground or in water as an offering to the gods, to spirits, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and यज्ञ sacrifice or act of worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायन्त्र
महायन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>Any great mechanical work, as a lock, or dyke, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and यन्त्र mechanical contrivance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्
महायशस्<BR>mfn. (-शाः-शाः-शः)<BR>Illustrious, celebrated.<BR>m. (-शाः)<BR>The fifth Jaina of the past era.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्क|महायशस्कः
महायशस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Illustrious, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, यशस् celebrity, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायुग
महायुग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A great Yuga; the aggregate of the four ages, or a period of four million, three hundred and twenty thousand years.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजत|महारजतं
महारजत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and रजत silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजन|महारजनं
महारजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Safflower.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, रञ्ज to color, aff. क्युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारण्य|महारण्यं
महारण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A large forest.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारथ|महारथः
महारथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 A large car.<BR>3 A warrior fighting in a car, or any leader or warrior of note.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारस|महारसं|महारसः
महारस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The date tree, (Phoenix sylvestris.)<BR>2 A species of club rush, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>2 Gruel made from the fermentation of rice water.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराज|महाराजः
महाराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A sovereign, an emperor.<BR>2 A finger nail.<BR>3 A Jaina deified teacher.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, राजन् a king, aff. टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजक|महाराजकः
महाराजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of demigod: see महाराजिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजचूत|महाराजचूतः
महाराजचूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A kind of mango.<BR>E.<BR>महाराज sovereign, chief, and चूत the mango; bearing a superior sort of fruit; also similar compounds, as महाराजाम्र, महाराजफल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजाधिराज
महाराजाधिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A paramount sovereign, an emperor.<BR>E.<BR>महाराज, and अधिराज chief sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजिक|महाराजिकः
महाराजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of demigod, of which there is a class of 226.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, राजि splendour, aff. कन्; or महाराज the epithet of their chief, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारात्र
महारात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Midnight.<BR>E.<BR>भहा great, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारूप|महारूपः
महारूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Resin.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारूपक|महारूपकं
महारूपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drama, a play or dramatic poem.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, रूपक rhetorical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारौरव|महारौरवः
महारौरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>One of the divisions of Tartarus, a hell.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, रुरु a demon, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घ|महार्घं|महार्घः
महार्घ<BR>mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं)<BR>Costly, precious, of great price or value.<BR>m. (-र्घः)<BR>A sort of quail.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, अर्घ cost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्णव|महार्णवः
महार्णव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, अर्णव the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्थ
महार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Significant, meaning.<BR>2 Great, dignified.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A principal object.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and अर्थ sense or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्द्ध
महार्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A plant, commonly Mahāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्ह|महार्हं
महार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>1 Costly, valuable.<BR>2 Very worthy.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराष्ट्र|महाराष्ट्रः
महाराष्ट्र<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>A country in the west of India, that of the original Mahrattas.<BR>f. (-ष्ट्री)<BR>A dialect, Mahratta.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and राष्ट्र kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालक्ष्मी
महालक्ष्मी<BR>f. (-क्ष्मीः)<BR>SARASVATĪ the wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and लक्ष्मी the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालय|महालयः
महालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 GOD, the Supreme being.<BR>2 A place of pilgrimage.<BR>3 A tree, &c. sacred to a deity.<BR>4 The Loka or world of BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 A place of refuge, a sanctuary, an asylum.<BR>6 A temple.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, आलय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोध
महालोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A tree, the bark of which is used as an astringent, (Symplocos racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, लोध the Lodh tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोल|महालोलः
महालोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and लोल moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोह|महालोहं
महालोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, chief, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावन|महावनं
महावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A large forest.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावप|महावपः
महावप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A plant and drug, commonly Mahāmeda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावरा
महावरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Bent grass: see दूर्ब्बा.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावराह|महावराहः
महावराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>VIṢṆU in the boar incarnation.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and वराह a boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावर्त्तन|महावर्तन
महावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Large pay or allowance.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and वर्त्तन maintaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावल्ली
महावल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A large and handsome creeping plant, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावस|महावसः
महावस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The Gangetic porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and वस who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविल|महाविलं
महाविल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>2 A water jar.<BR>3 The heart, the mind.<BR>4 A cave, a hole.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and विल a chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविशिष्ट
महाविशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Endowed with great, or excellent qualities.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, विशिष्ट endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविष|महाविषः
महाविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A small venomous snake, supposed to be twoheaded.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविषुव|महाविषुवं
महाविषुव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The Saṅkrānti or moment of the sun's entering ARIES; the vernal equinox, but varying several days from the European computation.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and विषुव equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीचि|महावीचिः
महावीचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>One of the divisions of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and वीचि a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीज्य|महावीज्यं
महावीज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>The septum of the scrotum, and part of the perinœum.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, वीज seed, यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर|महावीरः
महावीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 GARUḌA the bird, and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>3 A lion.<BR>4 A white horse.<BR>5 Sacrificial fire.<BR>6 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>7 A bird, a sort of hawk.<BR>8 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>9 The last and most celebrated Jina or Jaina teacher of the present age; supposed to have flourished in the province of Behar, in the sixth century before the Christian era.<BR>10 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>11 VIṢṆU.<BR>12 AGNI or fire.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A sort of drug, commonly Kṣīrakākolī, and conceived to be the dried root of a species of lily.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वीर hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर्य्य|महावीर्य|महावीर्यः|महावीर्य्यः
महावीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>2 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>1 A name of SAṂJÑĀ the wife of the sun.<BR>2 Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वीर्य्य essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=651" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावृक्ष|महावृक्षः
महावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Euphorbia, of several species: see स्नुही.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावृहती
महावृहती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वृहती the egg-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावेग|महावेगः
महावेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्याहृति|महाव्याहृतिः
महाव्याहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The three mystical words, Bhūr, Bhuvaḥ, and Svar, the essential part, with Om and Gāyatrī, of the daily Brahminical prayer.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and व्याहृति a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रतिन्
महाव्रतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A devotee, an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and व्रत religious penance or observance, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रीहि
महाव्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A large kind of rice.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and व्रीहि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशङ्ख|महाशंख|महाशङ्खः
महाशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>1 A human bone.<BR>2 The forehead.<BR>3 A thousand millions.<BR>4 One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or treasures.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, शङ्ख a shell, a number, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशक्ति|महाशक्तिः
महाशक्ति<BR>m. (-क्तिः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA the martial deity of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय|महाशयः
महाशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Magnanimous, liberal, munificent.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A gentleman, sir.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, आशय purpose or an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय्या
महाशय्या<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>A throne, a regal seat.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and शय्या bed or couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशल्क|महाशल्कः
महाशल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>A prawn or shrimp.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and शल्क a scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशाक|महाशाकं
महाशाक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A kind of potherb.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशालि|महाशालिः
महाशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A fragrant sort of rice.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, chief, and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशीता
महाशीता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, much, शीता cooling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ति|महाशुक्तिः
महाशुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>The pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, chief, and शुक्ति oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ला
महाशुक्ला<BR>f. (-क्ला)<BR>The goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, very, and शुक्ल white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुभ्र|महाशुभ्रं
महाशुभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and शुभ्र white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशूद्र|महाशूद्रः
महाशूद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The cowherd.<BR>f. (-द्री)<BR>The milk-woman, either wife of a cowherd or a woman of that caste.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, शूद्र Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्मशान|महाश्मशानं
महाश्मशान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The holy city Benares.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and श्मशान cemetery; people going thither to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्यामा
महाश्यामा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and श्याम black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्रमण|महाश्रमणः
महाश्रमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A Jaina or Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and श्रमण labouring, (in devotion.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्री
महाश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>1 A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>2 An epithet of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and श्री prosperity or the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्वेत
महाश्वेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very white.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 A white variety of the Convolvulus paniculatus.<BR>3 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>4 A sort of Clitoria, (C. ternata, with white flowers.)<BR>E.<BR>महा much, and श्वेत white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासत्व
महासत्व<BR>mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं)<BR>Good, virtuous, just.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and सत्व purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासन्न|महासन्नः
महासन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासर्ज|महासर्जः
महासर्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः)<BR>1 A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>2 The jack tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and सर्ज the Śāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासह|महासहः
महासह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Much-enduring.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>2 A flower, (Gomphræna globosa.)<BR>3 A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, सह to bear, aff. अच् or अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासान्तपन|महासांतपन|महासान्तपनं|महासांतपनः
महासान्तपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sort of penance; subsisting for six successive days, respectively, on cow's urine, cowdung, milk, curds, Ghee, and water in which Kusa grass has been boiled, and fasting on the seventh day: instead of one day some authorities assign a period of three days to each, considering the first as the common Sāntapana penance; others omit the two last periods, making it last fifteen days.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and सान्तपन a penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहस|महासाहसं
महासाहस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Excessive violence, brutal assault.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहसिक|महासाहसिकः
महासाहसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A robber, a plunderer, one who carries off property openly, and by force.<BR>2 An assaulter, a violator.<BR>E.<BR>महासाहस violence, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासि|महासिः
महासि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>A large scymitar or sword.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and असि a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासुख|महासुखं|महासुखः
महासुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and सुख happiness, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासूक्ष्म
महासूक्ष्म<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)<BR>Subtile, fine, minute.<BR>f. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Sand.<BR>E.<BR>महा very, सूक्ष्म thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासूत|महासूतः
महासूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासेन|महासेनः
महासेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 A general, the commander of a large force.<BR>3 The father of the eighth Jina or Jaina saint of the present era.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्कन्ध|महास्कंध|महास्कन्धः
महास्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्थली
महास्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and स्थली heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्नायु|महास्नायुः
महास्नायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Any principal vessel of the body.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and स्नायु a tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्वन|महास्वनः
महास्वन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Loud sounding.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An instrument of martial music, a kind of drum or trumpet.<BR>2 A loud sound.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and स्वन sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहव|महाहवः
महाहव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A great battle or war.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and आहव war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहास|महाहासः
महाहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A horse laugh.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and हाद्य laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाह्रस्वा
महाह्रस्वा<BR>f. (-स्वा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महि|महिः
महि<BR>f. (-हिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. इ, more commonly मही, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिका
महिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Frost.<BR>E.<BR>नह to worship, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form; more commonly मिहिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महित|महितं
महित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Proper, right.<BR>2 Worshipped, reverenced, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The trident of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिन|महिनं
महिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Kingdom, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship or be worshipped, Uṇādi aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिन्धक|महिंधकः
महिन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A rat.<BR>2 An ichneumon.<BR>3 The string of a pole for carrying loads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिमन्
महिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Greatness in general, literal or figurative.<BR>2 Magnitude as one of ŚIVA'S attributes, illimitability.<BR>E.<BR>महत् great,^1 इमनिच् aff. of the abstract property.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=652" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिर|महिरः
महिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>मह to be worshipped, aff. इरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिला
महिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A woman, a female.<BR>2 A woman, literally or figuratively intoxicated.<BR>3 A plant bearing a fragrant seed, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship or be worshipped, Uṇādi aff. इलच्; also महला and महेला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिलाह्वया
महिलाह्वया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>महिला a woman, and आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिष|महिषः
महिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 The emblem of one of the Jaina saints.<BR>3 The emblem and vehicle of YAMA.<BR>4 The name of an Asura or demon slain by DURGĀ.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A female buffalo.<BR>2 The wife of a king, but especially the one who has been consecrated or crowned, a queen.<BR>3 A drug.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship or be worshipped, Uṇādi aff. टिषच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषध्वज|महिषध्वजः
महिषध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>YAMA the sovereign of hell, and judge of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>महिष a buffalo, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषमर्द्दिनी|महिषमर्दिनी
महिषमर्द्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>महिष the Asura so named, and मर्द्दिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषवाहन|महिषवाहनः
महिषवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>YAMA, the PLUTO of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>महिष a buffalo, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषाक्ष|महिषाक्षः
महिषाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A plant, supposed to be the Bdellium tree.<BR>E.<BR>महिष a buffalo, and अक्ष eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मही
मही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A river, the Mahī which rises in the province of Malva, and after pursuing a westerly course of about 280 miles, falls into the upper part of the gulf of Cambay.<BR>3 A cow.<BR>4 A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship or be worshipped, aff. इ, and ङीष् added; also without the addition, महि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीक्षित्
महीक्षित्<BR>m. (-क्षित्)<BR>A king, a sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and क्षि to rule, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीतल
महीतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The surface of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीधर|महीधरः
महीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and घर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीध्र|महीध्रः
महीध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and धृ to uphold, aff. क, and the vowel changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीप|महीपः
महीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीपति|महीपतिः
महीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A sovereign, a king.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीपाल|महीपालः
महीपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीप्राचीर|महीप्राचीरं
महीप्राचीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and प्राचीर a boundary; being supposed to surround the earth completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभर्त्तृ|महीभर्तृ
महीभर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and भर्त्तृ who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभुज्
महीभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>मही, and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीमय|महीमयः
महीमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Earthen, made of earth or clay.<BR>E.<BR>मही earth, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीयस्
महीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Greatest, very great.<BR>E.<BR>महत् great, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीय्यमान
महीय्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>To be worshipped, to be reverenced, to be treated with respect.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, शानच् aff., and यङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीरुह|महीरुहः
महीरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and रुह to grow, aff. क; also with क्विप् aff. महीरुह् m. (-रुट्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीलता
महीलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>An earthworm.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीसुत|महीसुतः
महीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The regent of the planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, and सुत son; said to have sprung from the soil, near Oujein, which was sprinkled with the perspiration from ŚIVA'S body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेछ|महेच्छ|महेच्छः
महेछ<BR>mfn. (-छः-छा-छं)<BR>Liberal, magnanimous, high-minded.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and इच्छा wish or design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्र|महेंद्र|महेन्द्रः
महेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 INDRA, the ruler of Svarga.<BR>2 A range of mountains, one of the seven principal chains in Bhārata Varṣa or India, and apparently the northern part of the Ghāts of the peninsula.<BR>E.<BR>महा chief, great, इन्द्र the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्रनगरी|महेंद्रनगरी
महेन्द्रनगरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Amaravatī the city of the immortals, and capital of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>महेन्द्र INDRA, and नगरी capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्राणी
महेन्द्राणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and इन्द्राणी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेरणा
महेरणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, ईरन diffusion; or मह sacrifice, ईर to go to, to be used in, aff. ल्यु; also महेरुणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेला
महेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>मह a festival, इला the earth or site, or मह to worship, इलच् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel irregularly changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेलिका
महेलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश|महेशः
महेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मह great, ईश lord or God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेशबन्धु|महेशबन्धुः
महेशबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>महेश ŚIVA, and बन्धु friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वर|महेश्वरः
महेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 DURGĀ the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>2 Mixed or bell-metal.<BR>3 A flower, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, ईश्वर God, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वरकरच्युता
महेश्वरकरच्युता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The Karatoya river in the north of Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>महेश्वर ŚIVA, कर the hand, and च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेषु|महेषुः
महेषु<BR>f. (-षुः)<BR>A large arrow.<BR>E.<BR>महा, And इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेष्वास|महेष्वासः
महेष्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A warrior, a champion, an archer.<BR>E.<BR>सहेषु, and आस who shoots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोक्ष|महोक्षः
महोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A large bull or ox.<BR>E.<BR>महा large, उक्षम an ox, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्का
महोत्का<BR>f. (-त्का)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, (frequent,) उत्क opportunity, interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्पल|महोत्पलं|महोत्पलः
महोत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, chief, and उत्पल a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्सव|महोत्सवः
महोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A great festival.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्साह|महोत्साहः
महोत्साह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Persevering, diligent, making strenuous and unremitting exertion.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A king, possessing all the appendages and powers of monarchy.<BR>2 Diligence, effort, exertion.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदधि|महोदधिः
महोदधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and उदधि the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदय|महोदयं|महोदयः
महोदय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Kanoj, the ancient city and district.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Final beatitude, emancipation from vitality and absorption into the divine essence.<BR>2 Prosperity, elevation, eminence.<BR>3 Pride.<BR>4 Abandoning, relinquishment.<BR>5 A master, a lord.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and उदय rising, splendor, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदार
महोदार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Mighty, powerful.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and उदार great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोद्यम|महोद्यमः
महोद्यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Diligent, persevering, making strenuous and unremitting effort.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Great effort, energy exertion.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=653" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्नत|महोन्नतः
महोन्नत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Very high.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The palmyra tree.<BR>E.<BR>महा, and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्मद|महोन्मदः
महोन्मद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Intoxication, either literal or figurative, as with pride, passion, &c.<BR>2 A sort of fish, commonly Phalai.<BR>E.<BR>महा much, उन्मद intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोरग|महोरगं|महोरगः
महोरग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>The root of a plant: see तगर.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A sort of demigod of the serpent genus, and forming one of the classes inhabiting Pātāla, &c.<BR>2 Any large snake.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and उरग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस्
महौजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Very mighty or powerful.<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A hero, a champion.<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Great might or power.<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and ओजस् power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस
महौजस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>टच् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषध|महौषधं
महौषध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>1 Garlic.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Atis, (Betula.)<BR>3 Long pepper.<BR>nf. (-धं-धी)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>महा great, and औषध a drug; this word is of course applicable to a great number of plants and substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषधि|महौषधिः
महौषधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 A sort of grass, commonly Dūb.<BR>2 A kind of sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>महा large, and औषधि a deciduous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा<BR>r. 2d cl. (माति) 3d cl. (मिमीते) 4th cl. (मायते)<BR>To mete, to measure: with अनु prefixed, to infer, to conclude: with उप, to resemble; with परि, to measure; with प्र, to be evidence or authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा<BR>ind.<BR>1 A prohibitive and negative particle.<BR>2 A particle implying doubt.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, aff. क्विप्; this particle is used chiefly prefixed to verbs, in the imperative mood, as माकुरु do not do (any act), &c., it is also read sometimes, माङ् the final being redundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस|मांसं|मांसः
मांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>Flesh.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 Indian spikenard, (Valeriana Jatamansi.)<BR>2 A sort of drug, commonly Kākoli.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A worm.<BR>E.<BR>मन to mind, स Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसकाम|मांसकामः
मांसकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Fond of flesh.<BR>E.<BR>मांस, कम to desire, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसकारि
मांसकारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Blood.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and कारि making, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसज|मांसजं
मांसज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Marrow or serum of the flesh, adeps.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसतेजस्
मांसतेजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>The marrow of the flesh, meaning probably adeps.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and तेजस् lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसदलन|मांसदलनः
मांसदलन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and दलन dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसभक्ष|मांसभक्षः
मांसभक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Eating flesh, carnivorous.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and भक्ष eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसल|मांसलं|मांसलः
मांसल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Strong, stout, lusty.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसविक्रय|मांसविक्रयः
मांसविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Selling flesh or meat.<BR>E.<BR>मांस, and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसविक्रयिन्
मांसविक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A vender of the flesh of beasts or birds.<BR>2 A term of reproach, designating a mean or vile person.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, विक्रयिन् who sells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसशील
मांसशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fleshy.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh or meat, and शील possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांससार|मांससारः
मांससार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Adeps, fat, the serum of the flesh.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसस्नेह|मांसस्नेहः
मांसस्नेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Adeps, the serum or marrow of the flesh.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, and स्नेह unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसहासा
मांसहासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Skin.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, हास a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिक|मांसिकः
मांसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender of flesh or meat, whether of beasts or of birds.<BR>E.<BR>मांस flesh, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्द|माकंद|माकंदः|माकन्दः
माकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The mango.<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>1 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>2 Yellow saunders.<BR>3 The name of a city.<BR>E.<BR>मा beauty, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकलि|माकलिः
माकलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 The charioteer of INDRA.<BR>2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्ष
माक्ष<BR>(इ) माक्षि r. 1st cl. (मांक्षति)<BR>To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिक|माक्षिकं|माक्षिकः
माक्षिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A mineral substance, of which two kinds are described; the स्वर्णमाक्षिक or gold Mākṣika, of a bright yellow colour, apparently the common pyritic iron ore: and the रूप्यमाक्षिक or silver Mākṣika, which answers in appearance to the Hepatic pyrites of iron; other names of these ores occur; as, विट्माक्षिक and कांस्यमाक्षिक, or feculent Mākṣika and mixed metal Mākṣika; they are however, perhaps rather synonyms of the gold and silver ore, respectively, than names of distinct species.<BR>2 Honey.<BR>E.<BR>माक्षिका a bee, अण् aff. of derivation; the name is applied to the ore, from its honey-like colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकज|माक्षिकजं
माक्षिकज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Bee's wax.<BR>E.<BR>माक्षिक honey, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकशर्करा
माक्षिकशर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A kind of sugar, candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकाश्रय|माक्षिकाश्रयं
माक्षिकाश्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Bee's wax.<BR>2 A honey-comb.<BR>E.<BR>माक्षिक honey, आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागध|मागधः
मागध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>Belonging to, or produced in the province of Magadha or south Behar.<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A bard, a minstrel, whose duty it is, to recite the praises of sovereigns, their genealogy, and the deeds of their ancestors, in their presence; and to attend on the march of an army, and animate the soldiers by martial songs: the minstrel forms a particular caste, said to spring from a Vaiśya father, and Kṣatriya mother; in mythology, they are said to have been created at once by the will of ŚIVA: under the name of Bhauts, they are still numerous in the west of India, where they are a privileged tribe.<BR>2 Cumin-seed.<BR>m. plu. (-धाः)<BR>The inhabitants or people of Magadha.<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>1 A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>2 Long-pepper, (Piper longum.)<BR>3 A sort of cardamoms grown in Guzerat.<BR>4 Refined sugar.<BR>5 A dialect of Sanskrit: one of the principal forms of Prākṛta, and nearly the same as that used in the sacred books of the Bauddhas and Jainas: in the drama it is the dialect of the attendants and companions of royal person ages.<BR>E.<BR>मगध a Kaṇḍvādi verb to ask, (reward,) aff. अण्; or मगघ the country, and अण् derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ|माघः
माघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 One of the months of the Hindu year, (January-February.)<BR>2 A poet, the author of the ŚIŚUPĀLA Badha, or as it is named after him the Māgha Kāvya, one of the great profane poems of Hindu literature.<BR>f. (-घी)<BR>A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>E.<BR>मघा the asterism, in which the moon is full this month, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ्य|माघ्यं
माघ्य<BR>n. (-घ्यं)<BR>Many-flowered jasmine, (Jasminum multiflorum or pubescens.)<BR>E.<BR>माध the month Māgha, and ष्यञ् aff. of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=654" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलिक|मांगलिक
माङ्गलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Propitious, tending to good fortune, wishing for it, indicating or portending it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गल्य|मांगल्य|माङ्गल्यं
माङ्गल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Welfare, propitiousness.<BR>E.<BR>मङ्गल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माच|माचः
माच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A road, a way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचल|माचलः
माचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A robber, a bandit.<BR>2 An alligator, a crocodile.<BR>3 Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>मा fortune, wealth, चल to go, (by such means,) and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिका
माचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिर|माचिरं
माचिर<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly, without delay.<BR>E.<BR>मा prohibitive, and चिर long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजल|माजलः
माजल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठ|मांजिष्ठ|माञ्जिष्ठं
माञ्जिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Of a red colour.<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Red, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा madder, used as a red dye, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठ|माठः
माठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठ्य
माठ्य<BR>m. (-ट्यः)<BR>A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठर|माठरः
माठर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 One of the sun's attendants.<BR>2 The poet VYĀSA.<BR>3 Name of a Muni.<BR>4 A distiller.<BR>E.<BR>मन to reverence, अरन् Uṇādi aff., ठच् substituted for the radical final, and the vowel optionally long; also माठर्य्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड|माडः
माड<BR>(ऋ) माडृ r. 1st cl. (माडति-ते)<BR>To measure, to weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड|माडः
माड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>Weight or quantity.<BR>E.<BR>माड to weigh, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माडि|माडिः
माडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>A palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्डुक|माड्डुकः
माड्डुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drummer, a player on the sort of drum called Maḍḍaka or Maḍḍu, q. v.<BR>E.<BR>मड्डुक as above, and अण् aff.; also with ठक् aff. माड्डुकिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माढि|माढिः
माढि<BR>f. (-ढिः)<BR>1 The germ of leaves, the young leaf before it opens.<BR>2 Distress, affliction.<BR>3 Evidence or declaration of distress.<BR>4 A back or double tooth.<BR>5 The hem or border of a garment.<BR>6 Poverty, indigence.<BR>7 Anger, passion.<BR>E.<BR>मह to worship, aff. क्तिन्; the final becomes ढ, and the preceding vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणक|माणकं|माणकः
माणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small shrub, (Arum Indicum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव|माणवः
माणव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A child.<BR>2 A man, (in a contemptuous sense,) a manikin.<BR>3 A necklace of sixteen strings.<BR>E.<BR>मनु a man, and अण् aff.; also मानव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवक|माणवकः
माणवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A child, a boy not exceeding sixteen years of age, a manikin.<BR>2 A pupil, a scholar, a religious student.<BR>3 A man, an ignorant or ridiculous man, a childish man.<BR>4 A necklace of twenty strings.<BR>5 A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवीण
माणवीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Boyish, childish, fit or suitable for a child.<BR>E.<BR>माणव as above, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव्य|माणव्यं
माणव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 A number of boys.<BR>2 Boyhood.<BR>E.<BR>माणव a boy, यत् aff. of property or multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिका
माणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A weight of eight Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिक्य|माणिक्यं
माणिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>A ruby.<BR>f. (-क्या)<BR>A house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>मणि a gem, कै to call, यत् or यञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिबन्ध|माणिबंध|माणिबंधं|माणिबन्धं
माणिबन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>E.<BR>मणिबन्ध a mountain, अण् aff.; found there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिमन्थ|माणिमंथ|माणिमंथं|माणिमन्थं
माणिमन्थ<BR>n. (-न्थं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>E.<BR>मणिमन्थ a mountain, from which the salt is supposed to be produced, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातङ्ग|मातंग|मातंगः|मातङ्गः
मातङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A man of a degraded caste, a Cāṇḍāla, an outcaste.<BR>3 A sort of divine being attendant on a Jina.<BR>4 The sacred fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>5 A mountaineer, a barbarian.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>2 The wife of VAŚIṢṬHA.<BR>E.<BR>मतङ्ग a saint, an elephant, &c., and अण् aff. of descent or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरपितृ
मातरपितृ<BR>m. du. (-तरौ)<BR>Parents, mother and father.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ mother, and पितृ father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिश्वन्
मातरिश्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ space in the seventh case, in the heavens, श्वि to increase, Uṇādi aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलि|मातलिः
मातलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The charioteer of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मातुल the father, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातली
मातली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>One of DURGA'S female companions.<BR>E.<BR>माता from मातृ DURGĀ, and आली a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातापितृ
मातापितृ<BR>m. du. (-तरौ)<BR>Mother and father.<BR>E.<BR>माता from मातृ a mother, and पितृ a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातामह|मातामहः
मातामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A maternal grandfather.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A maternal grandmother.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, डामहच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल|मातुलः
मातुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A maternal uncle.<BR>2 Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>3 A sort of grain.<BR>4 A variegated snake.<BR>f. (-ला-ली or -लानी)<BR>1 The wife of a maternal uncle, &c.<BR>2 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>3 Common Bengal San, a sort of Crotolaria, (C. juncea.)<BR>(-लानी)<BR>Pulse of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother and डुलच् aff., fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष् with आनुक् optionally inserted before the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलपुत्त्रक
मातुलपुत्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The son of a maternal uncle.<BR>2 The fruit of the Datura.<BR>E.<BR>मातुल a maternal uncle, &c., and पुत्त्र son, with कन् pleonasm, or aff. of comparison; also similar compounds, as मातुलात्मज m. (-जः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलाहि|मातुलाहिः
मातुलाहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A variegated serpent.<BR>E.<BR>मातुल the same, and अहि snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलि
मातुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>INDRA'S charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुङ्ग|मातुलुंग|मातुलुंगः|मातुलुङ्गः
मातुलुङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Common citron.<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The sweet lime.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुङ्गक|मातुलुङ्गकः
मातुलुङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>E.<BR>मा prohibitive prefix, तुला a balance, गम to go, खच् aff.; with the power of डित्, and कन् added, not sold by weight; also without the additional prefix, मातुलुङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A divine mother, the personified energy of a deity or his wife; in a figurative sense, a mother to mortals; eight divine Mātṛs are enumerated, BRĀHMĪ, the Mātṛ of BRAHMĀ; MAHEŚVARĪ, the Mātṛ of ŚIVA; VAIṢṆAVĪ, of VIṢṆU; AINDRĪ, of INDRA; VĀRĀHĪ, of VIṢṆU, as the Varāha Avatāra; KAUMĀRĪ, of KĀRTTIKEYA; KĀVERĪ or CĀMUṆḌĀ of KUVERA, and CARCIKĀ of ŚIVA, in one of his minor incarnations; another list calls them MAHEŚVARĪ, BRĀHMĪ, NĀRĀYAṆĪ, AINDRĪ, VĀRĀHĪ, KAUMĀRĪ, NARASIṂHĪ, and APARĀJITĀ, differing from the preceding one in the two last names, the first one of which, is the energy of VIṢṆU in the Narasiṃha Avatāra, and the latter a form of DURGĀ; another enumeration makes the Mātṛs sixteen, and another but seven.<BR>3 A cow.<BR>4 A female of the Brahman tribe, or the wife of a Brahman.<BR>5 The earth.<BR>6 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>7 A name of REVATĪ.<BR>8 Space, ether.<BR>E.<BR>मान to respect, Uṇādi aff. तृच्, and the final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=655" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Maternal, belonging to a mother.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A maternal uncle.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A mother.<BR>2 A nurse.<BR>3 The alphabet.<BR>4 A simple sound, a note, a vowel.<BR>5 A goddess.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृकछिद|मातृकच्छिद|मातृकच्छिदः
मातृकछिद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ A mother, क the head, and छिद to cut, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृकेशट|मातृकेशटः
मातृकेशट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A mother's brother.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, and केशट a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगामिन्
मातृगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>An incestuous son.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ, and गामिन् who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगोच
मातृगोच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Belonging to the mother's family.<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>The mother's family.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ, and गोच race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृघातुक|मातृघातुकः
मातृघातुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 A matricide.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, DITI the mother of the gods, and घातुक destroyer, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृपक्ष|मातृपक्षः
मातृपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Belonging or relating to the maternal line, or mother, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ, and पक्ष side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृबन्धु|मातृबंधु|मातृबन्धुः
मातृबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>The cognate relation by the mother's side, as any of the maternal grandfather's or grandmother's sister's or brother's children.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, and बन्धु a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृभोगीण
मातृभोगीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Fit or proper to be possessed, &c. by the mother.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ, भोग enjoyment, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृमुख|मातृमुखः
मातृमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A blockhead, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, and मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृशासित|मातृशासितः
मातृशासित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A blockhead, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, and शासित governed, mother-led.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसृ
मातृष्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A mother's sister.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ mother, and ष्वसृ a sister: also, मातुःष्वसृ, or मातुःस्वसृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसेय|मातृष्वसेयः
मातृष्वसेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A mother's sister's son.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A mother's sister's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>मातृ a mother, ष्वसृ a sister, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वस्रीय|मातृष्वस्रीयः
मातृष्वस्रीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A mother's sister's son.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A mother's sister's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>मातृष्वसृ a maternal aunt, and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृसिंही
मातृसिंही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, and ganderussa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The whole, the entire thing or class of things.<BR>2 (adv.) Only, solely (exclusive and identical, the very thing.)<BR>3 The primitive subtle or invisible type of visible elementary matter.<BR>4 A pleonastic addition to words.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Requisite, material.<BR>2 Quantity, measure.<BR>3 A little.<BR>4 An ear-ring.<BR>5 Wealth, substance.<BR>6 A short vowel.<BR>7 A moment.<BR>8 Quantity in metre or prosody, a syllabic foot.<BR>9 The upper or horizontal limb of the Nāgarī characters.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, Uṇādi aff. चन्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रक
मात्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Mere, only, solely.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर
मात्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Envious, or impatient of another's prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>मत्सर envy, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर्य्य|मात्सर्य|मात्सर्यं|मात्सर्य्यं
मात्सर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Envy, malice.<BR>E.<BR>मत्सर envious, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यिक|मात्स्यिकः
मात्स्यिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>मत्स्य a fish, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ|माथः
माथ<BR>(इ) माथि r. 1st cl. (मांथति)<BR>To hurt or kill, to afflict, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ|माथः
माथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Churning, stirring.<BR>2 A road.<BR>3 Hurting, injuring, killing.<BR>E.<BR>माथ to hurt, aff. अच् or मथ to agitate, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद|मादः
माद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Intoxication, literal or figurative.<BR>2 Pride.<BR>3 Joy, extasy.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be delighted or inebriated, and aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादक|मादकः
मादक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>मद to delight, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादन|मादनं|मादनः
मादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cloves.<BR>2 Delighting, inebriating.<BR>E.<BR>मद to be pleased, in the causal form, to please, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृश्
मादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Like me, resembling me.<BR>E.<BR>मा for अस्मट् I, दृश् to see, aff. क्विन्; also with कञ् or क्स, aff. मादृश and मादृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्री
माद्री<BR>f. (-द्री)<BR>The wife of PĀṆḌU, and mother of the youngest of the Pāṇḍava princes.<BR>E.<BR>मद्र a king, अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रीपति|माद्रीपतिः
माद्रीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of PĀṆḌU.<BR>E.<BR>माद्री the wife of the sovereign, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रीपृथापति
माद्रीपृथापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of PĀṆḌU.<BR>E.<BR>माद्री, and पृथा his other wife, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Made of honey, &c.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The month Vaiśākha.<BR>3 Spring.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 Sugar, clayed or candied.<BR>2 A large creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>3 Spirituous liquor.<BR>4 A bawd.<BR>5 A sort of dentifrice, commonly Misi.<BR>6 Sacred basil.<BR>7 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Sweetness.<BR>E.<BR>मधु honey, &c., and अण् aff. of derivation or reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवक|माधवकः
माधवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spirituous liquor, made from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia.<BR>f. (-विका)<BR>1 A kind of creeper.<BR>2 A female attendant.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीलता
माधवीलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A large creeper bearing white fragrant flowers, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>माधवी the same, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवेष्टा
माधवेष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>माधव, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकरी
माधुकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The alms obtained from five places by the third class of religious mendicants.<BR>E.<BR>मधुकर a mendicant, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमत
माधुमत<BR>m. plu. (-ताः)<BR>The people of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर|माधुरं
माधुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Arabian jasmine or its flower.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>2 Sweetness of temper, amiableness.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, &c., aff. अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्य्य|माधुर्य|माधुर्यं|माधुर्य्यं
माधुर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Sweetness of flavour or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>मधुर sweet, literally or figuratively, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Sweet-speaking or sounding.<BR>2 Made from the Bassia tree.<BR>E.<BR>मधूक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>Middle, mid (day).<BR>E.<BR>मध्य, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यम|माध्यमं
माध्यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Middle born.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यम the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ|माध्यस्थं
माध्यस्थ<BR>n. (-स्थं)<BR>1 Middle state or condition.<BR>2 Indifference to earthly objects.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यस्थ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्य|माध्यस्थ्यं
माध्यस्थ्य<BR>n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>Mediation, intercession.<BR>E.<BR>मध्यस्थ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वक|माध्वकं
माध्वक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Spirit distilled from the flowers of the Bassia.<BR>E.<BR>मधु Bassia, अण् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वी
माध्वी<BR>f. (-ध्वी)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>2 A sort of fish.<BR>E.<BR>मधु sweet, q. v., अण्, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीक|माध्वीकं
माध्वीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Spirituous liquor, distilled from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia.<BR>2 Wine, spirit distilled from grapes.<BR>E.<BR>माध्वी as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान<BR>r. 1st cl. (मीमांसते)<BR>To investigate, to seek or desire knowledge.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मानति मानयति)<BR>To respect, to revere, to worship.<BR>With अप or अव prefixed,<BR>to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Measure in general, whether of weight, length, or capacity.<BR>2 A measure, the fourth or eighth part of a khāri.<BR>3 The computation of the duration of a year, solar, lunar, sydereal, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Arrogance, haughtiness, pride. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">Page657</a>]<BR>2 Female arrogance or indignation.<BR>3 Taking, seizing.<BR>4 A blockhead.<BR>5 An agent.<BR>6 A barbarian.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, ल्युट् aff., or मन to revere, (one's self,) aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=656" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानक|मानकं
मानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A plant, of which the root is sometimes eaten, (Arum indicum.)<BR>f. (-निका)<BR>The fourth or eighth part of a khāri.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानकलि|मानकलिः
मानकलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Coolness, haughtiness, disdain.<BR>E.<BR>मान pride, and कलि quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानग्रन्थि|मानग्रंथि|मानग्रन्थिः
मानग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>1 Fault, transgression.<BR>2 Pride, self-conceit (?)<BR>E.<BR>मान pride, and ग्रन्थि a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानद|मानदः
मानद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Inspiring pride.<BR>2 Measuring.<BR>E.<BR>मान, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानधानिका
मानधानिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननीय|माननीयं
माननीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be respected or revered.<BR>E.<BR>मान to respect, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानरन्ध्री
मानरन्ध्री<BR>f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>A perforated copper vessel, filled with water, to mark the time, &c.: see ताम्री.<BR>E.<BR>मान a measure, and रन्ध्री a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A man, man.<BR>2 A boy.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>3 A daughter of the first Manu.<BR>E.<BR>मनु the progenitor of mankind, and अण् patronymic aff.: see माणव, माणवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवत्|मानवन्त्
मानवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Proud, haughty, high-spirited.<BR>E.<BR>मान, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवर्ज्जित|मानवर्जित|मानवर्जितः
मानवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Humble, lowly.<BR>E.<BR>मान pride, and वर्ज्जित freed from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्य|मानव्यं
मानव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A multitude of boys.<BR>E.<BR>माणव or मानव a boy, यत् aff. of multitude, more properly माणव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Mental.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 The mind, the seat or faculty of reason, and feeling.<BR>2 The lake Mānas, or Mānasarovara in the Himālaya mountains.<BR>3 (In law,) Tacit or implied consent.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>मनस् the mind, aff. अण्, or मनस् BRAHMĀ, the supreme mind, अण् aff. of derivation, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसत्व
मानसत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Thoughtfulness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसालय|मानसालयः
मानसालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A gander or wild swan.<BR>E.<BR>मानस, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसूत्र|मानसूत्रं
मानसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A chain of gold or silver, worn as an ornament round the loins.<BR>E.<BR>मान pride, सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसौकस्
मानसौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>The wild swan or goose.<BR>E.<BR>मानस् the lake Mānasarovara, and ओकस् dwelling; being supposed to migrate yearly from Hindustan to the banks of the lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिता
मानिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pride, dignity.<BR>E.<BR>मानिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, मानित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>1 Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR>2 (In composition,) Who thinks or fancies.<BR>f. (-निनी)<BR>1 A woman, especially one displeased and indignant towards her lover.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>3 A species of the Atiśarkarī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मान pride, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Human.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A man.<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A branch of medicine, the administering of drugs and herbs.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष a man, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्य|मानुष्यं
मानुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Manhood, manliness, humanity, the state or quality of a man or mortal.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष a man, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यक|मानुष्यकं
मानुष्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of men.<BR>E.<BR>मनुष्य a man, and वुञ् aff. of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोज्ञक|मानोज्ञकं
मानोज्ञक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Beauty, agreeableness, loveliness.<BR>E.<BR>मनोज्ञ agreeable, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्य|मांद्य|मांद्यं|मान्द्यं
मान्द्य<BR>n. (-न्द्यं)<BR>1 Sickness, indisposition.<BR>2 Sluggishness, torpor, apathy, stupidity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मन्द slow, sluggish, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A king fostered by INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मां me, धातृ drinker, from धे to drink; having on one occasion sucked Amṛta from the finger of INDRA, who then used the exclamation which afterwards was the name of the prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Respectable, venerable.<BR>E.<BR>मन to respect, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्य|मापत्यः
मापत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A name of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापन|मापनं|मापनः
मापन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Measure, measuring.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Mine.<BR>2 Selfish.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A miser, a niggard.<BR>2 A mother's brother.<BR>E.<BR>ममक mine, from मम the poss. case of अहम् I, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Mine.<BR>E.<BR>मम mine, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A mime, a juggler.<BR>2 An Asura or evil spirit.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Fraud, trick, deceit, illusion.<BR>2 A female juggler.<BR>3 Understanding, human intellect.<BR>4 Compassion.<BR>5 Wickedness, villainy, villainous deception.<BR>6 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>7 Trick in negotiation, political fraud, diplomacy.<BR>8 Philosophical illusion, idealism, unreality of all worldly existence; personified in mythology as a female, the consort of BRAHMĀ or GOD, and the immediate and active cause of creation.<BR>9 The mother of BUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, Uṇādi aff. य; the medium through which all things are seen, and by which they are estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकार|मायाकारः
मायाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A juggler, a mime, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>माया trick or delusion, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकृत्
मायाकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A juggler.<BR>E.<BR>माया trick, and कृत् who practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाचण
मायाचण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Illusive, deceptive.<BR>E.<BR>माया, and चणष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाजीविन्
मायाजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A conjurer, a juggler.<BR>E.<BR>माया trick, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाद|मायादः
मायाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A crocodile, an alligator.<BR>E.<BR>माया illusion, and द who gives or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायादेवीसुत|मायादेवीसुतः
मायादेवीसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>मायादेवी the goddess MĀYĀ or illusion, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायापटु
मायापटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु)<BR>Delusive, expert in deceiving.<BR>E.<BR>माया, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामय
मायामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Illusive, deceptive.<BR>E.<BR>माया, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावत्|मायावन्त्
मायावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Deceptive, illusory.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A name of KAṂSA.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>The wife of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>माया fraud, illusion, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावसिक|मायावसिकः
मायावसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A deceiver, a cheater, a liar.<BR>E.<BR>माया fraud, वस to abide, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाविन्
मायाविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A juggler, a conjurer.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>E.<BR>माया trick, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायासुत|मायासुतः
मायासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>माया the goddess so named, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Illusory, deceptive.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler, a conjurer.<BR>E.<BR>माया trick, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=657" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Deceptive, illusory.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A conjurer, a juggler.<BR>2 A cheat, a deceiver.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 AGNI.<BR>5 BRAHMĀ.<BR>6 KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>माया fraud, &c., and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>E.<BR>मि to scatter or diffuse, (through the body,) उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुराज|मायुराजः
मायुराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Belonging to a peacock, made of its feathers, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A flock of peacocks.<BR>E.<BR>मयूर a peacock, and अण् aff. of multitude, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरिक|मायूरिकः
मायूरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter or killer of peacocks.<BR>E.<BR>मयूर a peacock, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार|मारः
मार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 Killing, slaying, destroying.<BR>3 Obstruction, opposition, impediment.<BR>4 Thorn-apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>5 A name of KĀMA.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of CAṆḌĪ, a form of DURGĀ.<BR>2 Plague, pestilence, epidemic.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. घञ्, or in the causal form, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Epidemic disease, plague.<BR>2 A falcon, a hawk.<BR>3 A slayer, a destroyer.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, causal form, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Emerald, of the colour of an emerald, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मरकत, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजातक|मारजातकः
मारजातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजित्
मारजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>A BUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>मार love, and जित् who overcomes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारण|मारणं
मारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, causal form, to kill, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारात्मक
मारात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Murderous.<BR>E.<BR>मार, and आत्मक्र disposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारि|मारिः
मारि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 Killing.<BR>2 Ruin.<BR>3 Plague, epidemic.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, causal form, इ aff.: see मार and मारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिचिक|मारिचिकं
मारिचिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Peppered, seasoned with pepper.<BR>E.<BR>मरिच pepper, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Killed, slain.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिव्यसनवारक|मारिव्यसनवारकः
मारिव्यसनवारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a royal saint.<BR>E.<BR>मारि plague, व्यसन calamity, वारक stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिष|मारिषः
मारिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A venerable person, (in dramatic language,) especially the title of the manager, or principal actor.<BR>mf. (-षः-षी)<BR>A potherb, (Amaranthus oleraceus.)<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The mother of the sage DAKṢA.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear patiently, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 The name of a Rākṣasa, the companion of RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 A military or royal elephant.<BR>3 A sort of berry, commonly Kakkoli.<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A goddess, peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>मरीच a saint, &c., aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुण्ड|मारुंड|मारुंडः|मारुण्डः
मारुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A serpent's egg.<BR>2 A road.<BR>3 A place spread with cow-dung; some authorities have मारण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 Vital air, one of the three humours of the body.<BR>3 A wind, a demigod, of whom there is a class consisting of forty-nine.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Burnt-offering on conception.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, (by excess of it,) उति aff., and the vowel made long; the demigods, called Mārutas, are said to be the sons of Diti, formed of the divisions of the foetus in utero, by the Vajra, or thunderbolt of INDRA, and to be named from that deity's addressing the foetus he thus divided by मारोदीः weep not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतव्रत|मारुतव्रतं
मारुतव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the duties of a king, his universal presence by means of his emissaries.<BR>E.<BR>मारुत the wind, and व्रत observance, pervading all things like the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतात्मज|मारुतात्मजः
मारुतात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>HANUMĀN, the monkey god.<BR>E.<BR>मारुत air, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतापह|मारुतापहः
मारुतापह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Removing or opposing wind, windy humour, &c.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>मारुत wind, or a disease of that humour, and अपह removing, obviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुताशन|मारुताशनः
मारुताशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fasting, feeding on air.<BR>E.<BR>मारुत the wind, and अशन who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुति|मारुतिः
मारुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A name of HANUMĀN.<BR>2 The Pāṇḍava prince BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>मरुत wind, the deity, and इञ् patronymic aff.; the son of the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कटपिपीलिका
मार्कटपिपीलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small black ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्ड|मार्कंड|मार्कंडः|मार्कण्डः
मार्कण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A Muni, and narrator of one of the Purāṇas.<BR>E.<BR>मृकण्डु the father of the saint, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कंडेयः|मार्कण्डेयः
मार्कण्डेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>MĀRKAṆḌEYA a holy sage, the supposed author or narrator of one of the Purāṇas, named the Mārkaṇḍeya Purāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>मृकण्डु the father of the sage, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग|मार्गः
मार्ग<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मार्गति मार्गयति)<BR>1 To make or prepare.<BR>2 To go.<BR>3 To prepare the way, to make a road.<BR>4 To feather an arrow.<BR>(मार्गयति-ते)<BR>To seek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग|मार्गः
मार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A road, a path or way.<BR>2 Search, seeking, inquiry.<BR>3 The anus.<BR>4 Musk.<BR>5 The month in which the moon is full in the asterism Mṛgaśīrṣa, (November-December.)<BR>6 The constellation Mṛgaśīrṣa.<BR>7 (In geometry,) A section.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to inquire, aff. घञ्, or मृग a deer, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गक|मार्गकः
मार्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Agrahāyaṇa, (November-December.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गण|मार्गणं|मार्गणः
मार्गण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Mendicant, asking, begging, a beggar.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Asking, soliciting, begging.<BR>2 Research, inquiry.<BR>3 Affection, affectionate solicitation or inquiry.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A suppliant, a solicitor.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to ask, to seek, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गणक|मार्गणकः
मार्गणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A suppliant, a beggar.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गधेनु|मार्गधेनुः
मार्गधेनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>A Yojana, a measure of distance equal to 4,000 fathoms or four Kös, above eight miles.<BR>E.<BR>मार्ग a road, and धेनु a milch cow; also with कन् added, मार्गधेनुक (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गव|मार्गवः
मार्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A man of a low caste, born of a Niṣāda by an Ayogava female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिर|मार्गशिरः
मार्गशिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The month Agrahāyaṇa, (November-December.)<BR>E.<BR>मृगशिरस् the asterism in which the moon is full, and अण् aff.: also from मृगशीर्ष with अण् aff. मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशीर्ष|मार्गशीर्षः
मार्गशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>The month Mārgaśīrṣa: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिक|मार्गिकः
मार्गिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A deer-killer, a hunter.<BR>2 A traveller, a wayfarer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, or मार्ग a road, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गित|मार्गितं
मार्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sought, inquired after, pursued.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to seek for, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्य|मार्ग्यं
मार्ग्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>1 To be cleaned or purified.<BR>2 To be sought.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, aff. ण्यत्, or मार्ग to seek, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज|मार्जः|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्ज<BR>r. 1st cl. (मार्जयति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज|मार्जः|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः).<BR>1 Cleaning the body.<BR>2 A washerman.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=658" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जन|मार्जनः|मार्ज्जन|मार्ज्जनं|मार्ज्जनः
मार्जन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>1 Cleaning, cleansing, wiping.<BR>2 Cleaning the person, by wiping, bathing, or rubbing it with oil or fragrant unguents.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The sound of a drum.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A brush, a broom.<BR>2 One of DURGĀ'S attendants.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to clean, aff. युच् or ल्युट्, or मार्ज to sound, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जनीय|मार्जनीयः
मार्जनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be cleaned, to be cleansed or purified.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जार|मार्जारः|मार्ज्जार
मार्जार<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>1 The common cat.<BR>2 The wild or polecat.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, (its skin and face,) आरन् aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारक|मार्जारक|मार्जारकः
मार्ज्जारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>मार्जार a cat, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारकण्ठ|मार्जारकण्ठ|मार्जारकंठ|मार्जारकण्ठः
मार्ज्जारकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A peacock, perhaps a wrong reading for the last, or vice versa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारकर्णिका|मार्जारकर्णिका
मार्ज्जारकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मार्जार a cat, कर्ण the ear, कन् aff. fem. form; also मार्जारकर्णी having the ears of a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारगन्धिका|मार्जारगन्धिका
मार्ज्जारगन्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>E.<BR>मार्जार a cat, गन्ध smell, कन् aff. of comparison; also मार्जारगन्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जाल|मार्जाल|मार्जालः
मार्ज्जाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>see मार्जार, the final being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जालीय|मार्जालीय|मार्जालीयः
मार्ज्जालीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 A Śūdra.<BR>2 Cleaning the body.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to clean, and आलीयच् Uṇādi aff.; it is also written मार्जारीय, from the र and ल being interchanged, or as derived from मार्जार, with छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जित|मार्जित
मार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cleansed.<BR>2 Adorned.<BR>E.<BR>मार्ज to clean, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जिता|मार्जिता
मार्ज्जिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Curds with honey and spice.<BR>E.<BR>मार्ज to clean, aff. क्त, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तण्ड|मार्तण्ड|मार्तंड|मार्तंडः|मार्तण्डः|मार्त्तण्डः
मार्त्तण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>E.<BR>मृतण्ड the progenitor of the sun, aff. अण्; also sometimes मार्त्ताण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिक|मार्तिक|मार्त्तिकः
मार्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Earthen, made of clay or earth.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The lid of a pot or pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्तिका earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दङ्ग|मार्दङ्ग|मार्दंग|मार्दंगः|मार्दङ्गः|मार्द्दङ्गं
मार्द्दङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A town, a city.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A drummer.<BR>E.<BR>मृदङ्ग a drum, (played in or by,) अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दङ्गिक|मार्दङ्गिक|मार्दंगिक|मार्दंगिकः|मार्दङ्गिकः|मार्द्दङ्गिकः
मार्द्दङ्गिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drummer, a player on the drum.<BR>E.<BR>मृदङ्ग a drum, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दव|मार्दव|मार्दवं|मार्द्दवं|मार्द्दवः
मार्द्दव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Softness.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्धव
मार्द्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A man of low caste and occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्वीक
मार्द्वीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made of or from grapes.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Wine.<BR>E.<BR>मृद्धीका a grape, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष|मार्षः
मार्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 A venerable or respectable man, (in dramatic language.)<BR>2 A potherb.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to suffer, aff. अण्; also मारिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टि|मार्ष्टिः
मार्ष्टि<BR>f. (-र्ष्टिः)<BR>1 Cleaning the person, bathing, wiping, smearing it with unguents or oil.<BR>2 Cleaning, cleansing in general.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल|मालं|मालः
माल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A field.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A man.<BR>2 A mountain, a barbarian, one of a particular tribe.<BR>3 A country, lying west and south-west of Bengal; Ramghur, &c., or according to WILFORD, Mālbhūm in Midnapur.<BR>4 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A line, a row.<BR>2 A garland, a string or wreath of flowers.<BR>3 A chaplet of flowers.<BR>4 A string of beads, a rosary. In rhetorical or poetical description, a series or string of epithets, similes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मा fortune, ला to get or be, aff. अङ् and टाप्; or मा to measure, Uṇādi aff. र, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालक|मालकं|मालकः
मालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Nimb tree, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A garland.<BR>E.<BR>माला a garland, कन् aff., and the final of the fem. rejected; also in the fem. form, मालाका and मालिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालती
मालती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 Great-flowered jasmine, (Jasminum grandiflorum.)<BR>2 A bud, a blossom.<BR>3 A young woman.<BR>4 Moonlight.<BR>5 Night.<BR>6 A river.<BR>7 A flower, (Bignonia suaveolens.)<BR>8 A shrub, (Echites caryophyllata.)<BR>9 A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मा LAKṢMĪ, लत Sautra root, to shake, aff. अच् and ङीप्; or मल to hold, अतच् aff.; or माल VIṢṆU, अत to go, (to be presented to,) aff. अण् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतीतीरज|मालतीतीरजः
मालतीतीरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>मालती the river, तीर the bank, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालय|मालयः
मालय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Sandal, the unguent prepared from it.<BR>E.<BR>मलय the mountain whence the wood is brought, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालव|मालवः
मालव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The province of Malva, or<BR>m. plu. (-वाः)<BR>The people of that province; also with ञ्य pleonasm मालव्य, fem. मालवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालसी
मालसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A plant, commonly Keśapuṣṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाका
मालाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A garland, a wreath.<BR>E.<BR>माला the same, and कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकार|मालाकारः
मालाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A flower-seller, a florist, a gardener.<BR>E.<BR>माला a garland, and कार who makes; also मालाकृत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालातृणक|मालातृणकं
मालातृणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schoenanthus.)<BR>E.<BR>माला a wreath, तृण grass, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालादीपक
मालादीपक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>In rhetoric, affinity of various objects, by a common property.<BR>E.<BR>माला, and दीपक illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाफल
मालाफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The seed of the Eleocarpus, of which common rosaries, are made.<BR>E.<BR>माला a rosary, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिक|मालिकः
मालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a garland, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A florist, a flower-gatherer or seller.<BR>2 A sort of bird.<BR>3 A colorist, a painter.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Double jasmine, (Jasminum zambac, floribus multiplicatis.)<BR>2 A daughter.<BR>3 A necklace, an ornament of the neck.<BR>4 A garland of flowers, a wreath.<BR>5 The name of a river.<BR>6 A spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>7 Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>8 A palace.<BR>E.<BR>माला a garland, ठक् aff., or कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A florist, a gatherer and vender of flowers, a gardener.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>1 A name of UMĀ or DURGĀ.<BR>2 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>3 The city Campā, the modern Bhāgalpur.<BR>4 A poetical stanza, consisting of alternate verses or hemistichs of eight and seven syllables; it is especially used to conclude a section or canto.<BR>5 The wife of a flower-gatherer, or a female vender of garlands, &c.<BR>6 A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>7 A shrub, (Echites caryophyllata.)<BR>E.<BR>माला a garland, इनि aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालु|मालुः
मालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>मल to hold, Uṇādi aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुधान|मालुधानः
मालुधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A variegated snake.<BR>2 One of the Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla (?)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>मालु a creeper, and धान having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=659" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूर|मालूरः
मालूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>मा fortune, लू to cut, and रक् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालेय|मालेयः
मालेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to a garland, &c.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Large cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>माला, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्य|माल्यं
माल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Proper or fit for a garland, &c.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 A flower.<BR>2 A garland, a wreath.<BR>3 A chaplet, a garland for the forehead.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>माला a garland, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यवत्|माल्यवन्त्
माल्यवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A mountainous range, described as one of the smaller mountains of India proper; lying eastward of mount Meru.<BR>f. (-वता)<BR>Name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>माल्य a wreath, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लवी
माल्लवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A wrestling or boxing match.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माशब्दिक|माशब्दिकः
माशब्दिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Prohibitive, prohibiting, a prohibitor, a forbidder.<BR>E.<BR>मा particle of negation or prohibition, शब्द a sound, a word, and ठक् aff., implying the person or thing whence it proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष|माषः
माष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>2 A jeweller's or goldsmith's weight, variously reckoned at five, eight, or ten Rattis, or seeds of the Abrus precatorius; the weight in common use, is about seventeen grains troy.<BR>3 A blockhead, a fool.<BR>4 A cutaneous disease.<BR>E.<BR>मष to hurt, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषक|माषकः
माषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A weight of silver of two Rattis or about 4½ grains.<BR>2 The same in gold.<BR>3 A Māṣa: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषपर्णी
माषपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A kind of leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>माष the kidney bean, and पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीष् resembling it in the leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषवर्द्धक
माषवर्द्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goldsmith, a jeweller.<BR>E.<BR>माष the weight so called, and वृद्ध to increase, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषशस्
माषशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Māṣa by Māṣa, (given away, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>माष a particular weight, and शसि aff. of successive order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीण|माषीणं
माषीण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A field of kidney-beans.<BR>E.<BR>माष as above, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष्य|माष्यं
माष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>A field of kidney-beans.<BR>E.<BR>माष as above, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास्<BR>m. (-माः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A month.<BR>E.<BR>मा splendor, light, अस् to be, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास|मासं|मासः
मास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A month, the twelfth part of the Hindu year; it is usually a lunar one, consisting of thirty Tithis, but it may be a Saura or solar month, being equal to the sun's passage through a sign of the zodiac; there is also a Sāvana month, consisting of thirty risings and settings of the sun; a Nākṣatra month, or month regulated by the lunar asterisms, and a fifth description of month called Vārhaspatya, depending on the motions of the planet JUPITER; the lunar month also, being of two kinds, as reckoned from the new or from the full moon, completes six different modes of monthly computation.<BR>2 A jeweller's weight: see माष.<BR>E.<BR>मास् the moon, aff. अण् or मस to measure, (the year by it,) aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासजात
मासजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>A month old.<BR>E.<BR>मास, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासज्ञ|मासज्ञः
मासज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR>E.<BR>मास a month, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासन|मासनं
मासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A medicinal seed, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासप्रमित|मासप्रमितः
मासप्रमित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>New moon.<BR>E.<BR>मास, and प्रमित measured (by).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासमान|मासमानः
मासमान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>मास a month, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासर|मासरः
मासर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The scum of boiled rice.<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure, aff. अरन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासवर्त्तिका|मासवर्तिका
मासवर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>मास a month, वृत to be, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासान्त|मासांत|मासान्तः
मासान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>मास the month, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिक|मासिकं|मासिकः
मासिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Monthly, relating or belonging to a month.<BR>2 Payable in a month, (a debt, &c.)<BR>3 Hired by the month, (a servant.)<BR>4 Lasting for a month.<BR>5 Happening or occurring at the end of a month, what will occur a month hence, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A particular Śrāddha, or obsequial sacrifice performed every day of new moon.<BR>E.<BR>मास a month, and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासीन
मासीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Of a month, a month old.<BR>E.<BR>मास, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासुरी
मासुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The beard.<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure, aff. उरन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्म
मास्म<BR>ind.<BR>A prohibitive particle.<BR>E.<BR>मा prohibitive, and स्म termination added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्य
मास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Of or lasting a month, a month old.<BR>E.<BR>मास, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माह
माह<BR>(उ, or ऋ) माहु or माहृ r. 1st cl. (माहति-ते)<BR>To mete, to measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहन|माहनः
माहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>मा prohibitive prefix, हन to kill, aff. अच्, radical letters unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहा
माहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>मा prohibitive prefix, and हन् to kill, affs. ड and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुल|माहाकुलः
माहाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Of a respectable family.<BR>E.<BR>महाकुल of respectable lineage, and अञ् aff. of descent; also with खञ् aff., माहाकुलीन, or with ख, महाकुलीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनिक
माहाजनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Fit for or suitable to great persons, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महाजन, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्मिक
माहात्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Glorious, majestic<BR>2 Magnanimous.<BR>3 Of great sanctity or honour.<BR>E.<BR>महात्मन्, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्म्य|माहात्म्यं
माहात्म्य<BR>n. (-त्म्यं)<BR>1 Majesty, greatness, might.<BR>2 The peculiar efficacy or virtue of any divinity or sacred shrine, &c.<BR>3 A work, giving an account of the merits of any holy place or object.<BR>E.<BR>महात्मन् great, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानाम्निक|माहानाम्निकः
माहानाम्निक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman versed in a peculiar portion of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>महानाम्नी a portion of the Vedas so called, and ठञ् aff.; also with the final dropped, माहानामिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराजिक
माहाराजिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Imperial, royal, fit for a king, &c.<BR>E.<BR>महाराज, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिन|माहिनं
माहिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Kingdom, dominion.<BR>E.<BR>महिन the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिर|माहिरः
माहिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष
माहिष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Belonging to or derived from a buffalo, (flesh, milk, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>महिष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्य|माहिष्यः
माहिष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यं)<BR>A man of a mixed class, sprung from a Kṣatriya father and Vaiśya mother.<BR>E.<BR>महिष a buffalo, and यत् aff., with अण् added; attendance on cattle forming with the practice of astronomy and music, the business of the Māhiṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र<BR>mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्री-न्द्रं)<BR>Relating to or belonging to INDRA, fit or proper for, (as an oblation to him, &c.)<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>The [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">Page661</a>] wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>महेन्द्र the deity, and अण् aff.; also with छ, माहेन्द्रीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=660" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेय|माहेयः
माहेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Earthen, made of or from earth.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Coral.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A cow.<BR>E.<BR>मही the earth, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वरी
माहेश्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 One of the divine mothers or energies of the gods, the Śakti of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>महेश्वर ŚIVA, अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि<BR>(डु ञ्) डुमिञ् r. 5th cl. (मिनोति मिनुते)<BR>To cast, to throw, to throw about, to scatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिच्छ
मिच्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (मिच्छति)<BR>1 To pain, to inflict pain or distress.<BR>2 To obstruct, to hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Measured.<BR>2 Moderate, limited, few or little.<BR>3 Known, understood.<BR>4 Scattered, sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>मा to mete, or मि to scatter, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितङ्गम|मितंगम|मितंगमः|मितङ्गमः
मितङ्गम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Going deliberately or slowly.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A she-elephant.<BR>E.<BR>मित measured, गम to go, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितद्रु|मितद्रुः
मितद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मित what is measured, (the earth,) and द्रु to go, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितभुज्
मितभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Moderate, temperate.<BR>E.<BR>मित, and भुज् who eats, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितम्पच|मितंपच|मितम्पचः
मितम्पच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>Miserly, niggardly, a niggard, a miser.<BR>E.<BR>मित measured, (food,) and पच who cooks, from पच with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितवाच्
मितवाच्<BR>mfn. (-क्)<BR>Prudent in speaking, of measured speech.<BR>E.<BR>मित, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितार्थ
मितार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Of certain or restricted meaning.<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>A cautious emissary.<BR>E.<BR>मित, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताशन|मिताशनः
मिताशन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Abstemious, moderate in diet, eating little and sparingly.<BR>E.<BR>मित measured, and अशन who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिति|मितिः
मिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Measuring, measure.<BR>2 Weighing, weight.<BR>3 Value.<BR>4 Knowledge.<BR>5 Proof, evidence.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्र|मित्त्रं|मित्रं|मित्रः
मित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A friend.<BR>2 An ally; in this form it is always neuter; but it is convertible into an attributive, and is then of three genders, (मित्रः मित्रा मित्रं) Friendly, a friend.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, the mother of ŚATRUGHNA.<BR>E.<BR>मिद to be affectionate, aff. क्त्र; hence more properly written मित्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रकार्य्य|मित्रकार्य
मित्रकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A friendly deed, friendship.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and कार्य्यं act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रत्व|मित्रत्वं
मित्रत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Friendship, friendliness.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र with त्व aff.; also with तल्, मित्रता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्रुह
मित्रद्रुह<BR>m. (-द्रुक्)<BR>A false or treacherous friend.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and द्रुह who injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्विष्
मित्रद्विष्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A treacherous friend.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and द्विष् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रभेद|मित्रभेदः
मित्रभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Breach of friendship.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and भेद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयु|मित्रयुः
मित्रयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Attractive, winning or acquiring friends.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A rememberer or retainer of traditions, a person acquainted with popular and unrecorded customs.<BR>2 A friend.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a friend, या to obtain, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयुद्ध|मित्रयुद्धं
मित्रयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>The contest of friends, the conflict of allies.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रलब्धि|मित्रलब्धिः
मित्रलब्धि<BR>f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>Acquirement of friendship.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a friend, and लब्धि acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रलाभ|मित्रलाभः
मित्रलाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Acquirement of a friend or friendship, forming friendship, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a friend, and लाभ gain, acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रवत्सल|मित्रवत्सलः
मित्रवत्सल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Acquiring friendship, winning, captivating, engaging.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a friend, and वत्सल a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रशीस्
मित्रशीस्<BR>m. (-शीः)<BR>A ruler over his friends or allies.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र, and शास to govern, क्विप् aff. and ई substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीयत्
मित्रीयत्<BR>mfn. (-यत्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Becoming or acting as a friend, desiring friendship.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र nominal verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ|मिथः
मिथ<BR>(ऋ) मिथृ r. 1st cl. (मिथति-ते)<BR>1 To understand.<BR>2 To injure, to hurt.<BR>3 To unite, to pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथस्
मिथस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Mutually, reciprocally.<BR>2 Privately.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ to pair, aff. असुन्, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिला
मिथिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A city, giving name also to a kingdom, lying north-east of Bengal, the modern Tirhut.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ to be agitated, (enemies by that kingdom,) and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुन|मिथुनं|मिथुनः
मिथुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A couple, a pair, a brace, male and female.<BR>2 Copulation.<BR>3 Union, junction.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sign of the zodiac Gemini.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ to unite, उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनीभाव|मिथुनीभावः
मिथुनीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Amorous inclination.<BR>E.<BR>मिथुन, and भाव property, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या<BR>ind.<BR>Falsely, untruly.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ to injure, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचरत्
मिथ्याचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Acting or practising falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and आचरत् observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचार|मिथ्याचारः
मिथ्याचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Acting falsely.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यादृष्टि|मिथ्यादृष्टिः
मिथ्यादृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Denial of future existence, atheism, heresy.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsely, and दृष्टि vision, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याध्यवसिति|मिथ्याध्यवसितिः
मिथ्याध्यवसिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A figure of rhetoric, confirmation of one error or impossibility by another.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsehood, अध्यवसिति perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ
मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Treacherous, guilty of a breach of promise.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and प्रतिज्ञा promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रसुप्त
मिथ्याप्रसुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Pretendedly asleep, but not so in reality.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and प्रसुप्त asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभियोग|मिथ्याभियोगः
मिथ्याभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Groundless plaint or demand.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsely, अभियोग plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशंसन|मिथ्याभिशंसनं
मिथ्याभिशंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A false accusation.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsely, अभिशंसन accusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशंसिन्
मिथ्याभिशंसिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A false or unjust accuser.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsely, अभिशंसिन् who accuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यामति|मिथ्यामतिः
मिथ्यामति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Error, ignorance, mistake.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या falsely, and मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावदत्
मिथ्यावदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Speaking falsely.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and वदत् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावादिन्
मिथ्यावादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Lying, a liar.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योत्तर|मिथ्योत्तरं
मिथ्योत्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A false or prevaricating reply.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योपचार|मिथ्योपचारः
मिथ्योपचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Pretended friendly services.<BR>E.<BR>मिथ्या, and उपचार assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद्<BR>r. 1st cl. (मेदति)<BR>1 To be proud.<BR>2 To be humble.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मेदयति) (इ) मिदि r. 1st and 10th cls. (मिन्दति मिन्दयति) also (ञि, आ,) ञिमिदा r. 1st cl. (मेदते) r. 4th cl. (मेद्यति)<BR>1 To be unctuous, to be oily or greasy.<BR>2 To liquefy, to melt.<BR>3 To [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">Page662</a>] anoint.<BR>4 To have affection or regard for.<BR>5 To be soft, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>(ऋ) मिदृ r. 1st cl. (मेदति-ते)<BR>1 To understand.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=661" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्ध|मिद्धं
मिद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>1 Sloth, indolence.<BR>2 Sleepiness, torpor.<BR>3 Dulness, heaviness of spirits or intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षा|मिमंक्षा
मिमङ्क्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Wishing to bathe or plunge into.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to bathe, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षु
मिमङ्क्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to bathe, to plunge into, to be immersed in.<BR>E.<BR>मस्ज to bathe, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषा
मिमन्थिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Desire or purpose to destroy.<BR>E.<BR>मथि to shake, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषु
मिमन्थिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to destroy, shake, overturn, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मथ to injure, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल
मिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (मिलति or मिलति-ते)<BR>To be connected or united with, to mix, to associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलन|मिलनं
मिलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Mixing with, being in contact with, associating with, &c.<BR>2 Encountering, meeting.<BR>E.<BR>मिल to mix, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलित|मिलितः
मिलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Mixed, united, combined or connected with.<BR>2 Found, met with, encountered.<BR>E.<BR>मिल to mix, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिव
मिव<BR>(इ) मिवि r. 1st cl. (मिन्वति)<BR>1 To sprinkle or moisten.<BR>2 (According to some authorities,) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश
मिश<BR>r. 1st cl. (मेशति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशि|मिशिः
मिशि<BR>f. (-शिः-शी)<BR>1 A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium.)<BR>2 Indian spikenard.<BR>3 Common anise.<BR>E.<BR>मिश to sound, कि aff., and ङीष् optionally added; also मिषि, मिसि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (मिश्रयति)<BR>To mix, to join, to blend, to combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Mixed, mingled, blended.<BR>n. (-श्रं)<BR>Mixing, mixture.<BR>m. (-श्रः)<BR>1 An elephant, the fourth of the four classes in which elephants are arranged.<BR>2 A respectable person; in which sense it is a common affix to proper names; or compounded with आर्य्य, as आर्य्यमिश्राः.<BR>E.<BR>मिश्र to mix, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रक|मिश्रकं|मिश्रकः
मिश्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An adulterator of commodities, &c.<BR>2 A mixer, a compounder.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A garden of the gods, a grove of paradise.<BR>2 A description of song or singing.<BR>E.<BR>मिश्र mingled, (flowers, &c.) and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रकावन
मिश्रकावन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The grove of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मिश्रका for मिश्रक a divine garden, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रण|मिश्रणं
मिश्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Mixing, uniting.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Addition.<BR>E.<BR>मिश्र to mix, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रित|मिश्रितं
मिश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Respected, respectable.<BR>2 Mixed, mingled.<BR>3 Added.<BR>E.<BR>मिश्र to mix, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रेया
मिश्रेया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium, Rox.)<BR>2 Another kind, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>3 Common anise, (Pimpinella anisum.)<BR>E.<BR>मिश्र mixture, इड् to go or get, अचू aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष|मिषं|मिषः
मिष<BR>r. 1st cl. (उ) मिषु (मेषति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>r. 6th cl. (मिषति)<BR>To contend with, to emulate, to contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष|मिषं|मिषः
मिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Fraud, trick, deception.<BR>2 Envy.<BR>E.<BR>मिष to vie, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषि|मिषिः
मिषि<BR>f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>1 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>2 A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मस to measure, इन् and ङीष् aff., स changed to ष, and इ substituted for the radical vowel; also मिसि, मिशि, and with कन् added मिषिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्ट|मिष्टं|मिष्टः
मिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Sprinkled, wetted.<BR>2 Sweet, sugary.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A sweetmeat.<BR>E.<BR>मिष to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टकर्त्तृ|मिष्टकर्तृ
मिष्टकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A confectioner, a good cook.<BR>E.<BR>मिष्ट, and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टान्न|मिष्टान्नं
मिष्टान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Sauce, gravy, seasoning, a mixture of sugar and acids, &c. eaten with bread or rice.<BR>E.<BR>मिष्ट sprinkled, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसि|मिसिः
मिसि<BR>f. (-सिः-सी)<BR>1 A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium, Rox.)<BR>2 Another kind, (A. sowa.)<BR>3 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>4 A sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>5 Common anise, (Pimpinella anisum.)<BR>E.<BR>मस to mete, aff. इन्, and optionally ङीष्; the radical vowel changed to इ, deriv. irr.; also मिशि and मिषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्र
मिस्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (मिस्रयति)<BR>To mix, to mingle or join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह
मिह<BR>(औ) मिहौ r. 1st cl. (मेहति)<BR>To sprinkle, to shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिका
मिहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Frost.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to sprinkle, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिर|मिहिरः
मिहिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A sage.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>5 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to sprinkle or scatter, (radiance, &c.) Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिराण|मिहिराणः
मिहिराण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मिहिर the sun, अन to live, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
मी<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मयति माययति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To know.<BR>(टु, ङ्) टु मीङ् r. 4th cl. (मीयते)<BR>To part with life, to die.<BR>(ञ्^1) मीञ् r. 9th cl. (मीनाति मीनीते)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ|मीढं|मीढः
मीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Passed as urine.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढुष्टम|मीढुष्टमः
मीढुष्टम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीन|मीनः
मीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 The sign of the zodiac Pisces.<BR>E.<BR>मी to hurt, Uṇādi aff. नक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनकेतन|मीनकेतनः
मीनकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनगोधिका
मीनगोधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pond, a pool.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and गोधिका a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनरङ्ग|मीनरंग|मीनरङ्गः
मीनरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A kingfisher.<BR>E.<BR>मीन fish, रञ्ज to annoy, aff. अच्; it is also written but perhaps incorrectly मीनरङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनर|मीनरः
मीनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A marine monster, sometimes applied to the shark and alligator: see मकर.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, रा to seize, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाक्षी
मीनाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>The daughter of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and अक्षि the eye, टच् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाघातिन्
मीनाघातिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>1 A crane.<BR>2 A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>मीन fish, and आघातिन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाण्ड|मीनांड
मीनाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Fish-spawn, roe, milt.<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and अण्ड egg, spawn, ङीष् aff., to which the last is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनालय|मीनालयः
मीनालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाम्रीण|मीनाम्रीणः
मीनाम्रीण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A wagtail.<BR>2 A sort of sauce, fish sauce.<BR>E.<BR>मीन fish, आम्र the mango, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीम
मीम<BR>(ऋ) मीमृ r. 1st cl. (मीमति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसक|मीमांसकः
मीमांसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Mīmāṃsaka, a follower of the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>मीमांसा the doctrine so termed, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसा
मीमांसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>One of the philosophical systems of the Hindus, or rather a two-fold system, the two parts of which form two of the six Darśanas or schools of philosophy; the first part, the Pūrva Mīmāṃsā, or Mīmāṃsā simply, originates with [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">Page663</a>] the Muni JAIMINI, and illustrates the Karma kāṇḍa of the Vedas, or the practical part, (the ritual,) of religion and devotion, including also moral and legal obligations. The second part, or Uttara Mīmāṃsā, ascribed to VYĀSA, is the same as the Vedānta, founded on the Jñāna-kāṇḍa or theological portion of the Vedas, and treating of the spiritual worship of the Supreme Being or soul of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>मान to seek knowledge, aff. अङ् and टाप्; the derivative takes the augment of the reduplicate form of the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=662" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीर|मीरः
मीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मी to scatter, रक् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मील|मीलं
मील<BR>r. 1st cl. (मीलति)<BR>To wink or twinkle, to close or contract the eye-lids: with उत् prefixed, to awake, (and figuratively) to expand, to bud, to blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलत्
मीलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Winking, twinkling, closing, (as the eyes.)<BR>E.<BR>मील to wink, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलन|मीलनं
मीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Twinkling, blinking, winking.<BR>E.<BR>मील to twinkle, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलित|मीलितं
मीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Twinkled.<BR>2 Unblown, partly opened, as a young bud, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Indirect allusion or description, (in rhetoric.)<BR>E.<BR>मील to twinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव
मीव<BR>r. 1st cl. (मीवति)<BR>To be large or corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवन्
मीवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>मी to move, वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवर|मीवरः
मीवर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Mischievous, hurting, killing.<BR>E.<BR>मी to hurt or kill, ष्वरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवा
मीवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The worm of the intestines, Ascarides, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मी to hurt, Uṇādi aff. वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मु|मुः
मु<BR>m. (मुः)<BR>1 Binding, confinement.<BR>2 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>3 Eternal beatitude or final emancipation.<BR>4 A funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>मू to bind, aff. क्विप् or मुच to loosen, &c., aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकन्दक|मुकंदक|मुकंदकः|मुकन्दकः
मुकन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The onion; also मुकुन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकु|मुकुः
मुकु<BR>f. (-कुः)<BR>Freedom, liberation.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let loose, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुट|मुकुटं
मुकुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A crest, a diadem, a tiara.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Snapping the fingers.<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, aff. उट, and उ substituted for the radical vowel, form irr.; also मकुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्द|मुकुंद|मुकुंदः|मुकुन्दः
मुकुन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 Gum olibanum.<BR>3 A precious gem.<BR>4 Quicksilver.<BR>5 One of KUVERA'S Nidhis, or divine treasures.<BR>E.<BR>मुकु liberation, (from passion, &c.) in the second case मुकुं, and टा to give, aff. क, or मुच to liberate, or मुकु as before, उन्द to wet, to sprinkle, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दक|मुकुंदकः|मुकुन्दकः
मुकुन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An onion; also मुकन्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दु|मुकुन्दुः
मुकुन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>Gum olibanum; also मुकुन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुर|मुकुरः
मुकुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mirror.<BR>2 The handle of a potter's lathe.<BR>3 A tree, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>4 A bud.<BR>5 Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>मक to adorn, उरच् Uṇādi aff., and उ optionally substituted for the radical vowel, deriv. irr.; also मकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुल|मुकुलं|मुकुलः
मुकुल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 An opening bud.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 The soul or spirit.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let loose, (the flower, &c.) उलच् aff., and च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलित
मुकुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Half-closed, (as a bud.)<BR>2 Half-shut, (as the eye,) blinking, winking.<BR>E.<BR>मुकुल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलीकृत
मुकुलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Closed, shut, (as a bud.)<BR>E.<BR>मुकुल, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्ठक|मुकुष्ठकः
मुकुष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus lobatus.) Also मकुष्ठक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकूलक|मुकूलकः
मुकूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>E.<BR>मकि to adorn, ऊलच् aff. कन् added, उ substituted for the radical vowel, deriv. irr.; also मकूलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त|मुक्तः
मुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Released, liberated, loosed, let go.<BR>2 Liberated from corporal existence, finally happy.<BR>3 Discharged, loosed as a weapon; this may be in two ways, as पाणिमुक्त thrown with the hand, as a dart, &c., and यन्त्रमुक्त thrown from an instrument, as an arrow from a bow, &c.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>The spirit released from mundane existence, and re-integrated with its divine original.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to set free, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तक|मुक्तकं
मुक्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Any missile weapon.<BR>2 A stanza or sentence completing the sense of a passage.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त loosed, let fly, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकञ्चुक|मुक्तकंचुक|मुक्तकञ्चुकः
मुक्तकञ्चुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake that has cast his slough.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त let loose, and कञ्चुक the slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकण्ठम्
मुक्तकण्ठम्<BR>ind.<BR>Aloud, as shouting or crying.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त, and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तचक्षुस्
मुक्तचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तसङ्ग|मुक्तसंग|मुक्तसंगः
मुक्तसङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Disinterested, free from worldly attachment or improper bias.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त, and सङ्ग attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तहस्त
मुक्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Parting with, giving away, liberal.<BR>2 Loosed, let go.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताकलाप|मुक्ताकलापः
मुक्ताकलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A pearl necklace, a string of pearls.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and कलाप a sort of chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तागार|मुक्तागारं|मुक्तागारः
मुक्तागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and आगार abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताप्रलम्ब
मुक्ताप्रलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A pearl necklace.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and प्रलम्ब string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताप्रसू
मुक्ताप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and प्रसू mother, mother of pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताफल|मुक्ताफलं
मुक्ताफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Camphor.<BR>2 A pearl.<BR>3 A sort of fruit, the custard apple.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and फल fruit, comparable to a pearl in whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तामुक्त|मुक्तामुक्तः
मुक्तामुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Loosed, and not loosed; applied especially to weapons which may be wielded or hurled, as a club, a javelin, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्त loosed, अमुक्त not loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तालता
मुक्तालता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A pearl necklace.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तावली
मुक्तावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A pearl necklace.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and आवली a line, a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तास्फोट|मुक्तास्फोटः
मुक्तास्फोट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>A pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, and स्फुट to burst, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ति|मुक्तिः
मुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Final beatitude, the delivery of the soul from the body and exemption from further transmigration; the re-absorption of the emancipated spirit into its great primary source, identification with GOD.<BR>2 Liberation, setting or becoming free or loose.<BR>E.<BR>मुघ to let loose, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त्वा
मुक्त्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having set free, loose, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to free, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख|मुखं|मुखः
मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 First, initial.<BR>2 Chief, pre-eminent, principal.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 The mouth.<BR>2 The face.<BR>3 The entrance to a house.<BR>4 Commencement.<BR>5 A means, an expedient.<BR>6 Sound. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">Page664</a>]<BR>7 The opening division of a drama, the first act, &c.<BR>8 The previous or preparatory incidents of a drama.<BR>9 The Vedas scripture.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The beak of a bird.<BR>E.<BR>खन to dig, Uṇādi aff. अच् with the power of ड, by which the final is rejected, मुट् initial augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=663" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखगन्धक|मुखगंधक|मुखगन्धकः
मुखगन्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An onion.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and गन्धक scenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखघण्टा
मुखघण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>Howling, uttering a particular cry of grief, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुस्व the mouth, and घण्टा a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखचपला
मुखचपला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A species of the Āryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखचीरी
मुखचीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The tongue.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and चीरी the cry or chirp of the cricket, or a cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखज|मुखजः
मुखज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Derived or proceeding from the mouth, born in the mouth, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A Brahman, born from the mouth of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखतस्
मुखतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>मुख, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखतीय|मुखतीयं
मुखतीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating or pertaining to the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>मुलतस् as above, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखदूषण|मुखदूषणः
मुखदूषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The onion.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and टूषण fouling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखधौता
मुखधौता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and धौत cleansed, (by it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखनिवासिनी
मुखनिवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The goddess SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and निवासिनी abiding; as the goddess of speech, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखनिरीक्षक|मुखनिरीक्षकः
मुखनिरीक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An idler, a lazy man.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the face, निरीक्षक contemplating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखपूरण|मुखपूरणं
मुखपूरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A mouthful of water for rinsing the mouth<BR>2 A mouthful.<BR>3 Filling the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and पूरण filling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखभूषण|मुखभूषणं
मुखभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Betel, the leaf of the piper betel eaten with the Areca nut, catechu, caustic lime, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and भूषण an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखम्पच|मुखंपच|मुखंपचः
मुखम्पच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A beggar, a petitioner.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and पच who ripens, (his purpose,) from पच with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखयन्त्रण|मुखयंत्रण|मुखयन्त्रणं
मुखयन्त्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The bit of a bridle.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and यन्त्रण restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखर|मुखरः
मुखर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Foul-mouthed, speaking harshly or scurrilously.<BR>2 Sounding, noisy.<BR>3 Speaking in ridicule of, rallying, mocking, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A leader.<BR>2 A conch shell.<BR>3 Leading, preceding.<BR>4 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and र aff. implying depreciation, or रा to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरित
मुखरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounding, ringing, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>मुखर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरीकरण
मुखरीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rallying, mocking.<BR>E.<BR>मुखर, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखलाङ्गल|मुखलांगल|मुखलाङ्गलः
मुखलाङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and लाङ्गल a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखवाद्य|मुखवाद्यं
मुखवाद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 A musical instrument played with the mouth, a jew's harp(?)<BR>2 Making a noise with the mouth by striking it with the hand, playing on the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth. and वाद्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखवासन|मुखवासनः
मुखवासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A perfume for the mouth, any drug, as camphor or orris-root so used, or a composition usually taken in the form of a pill.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and वासन perfuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखविलुण्ठिका|मुखविलुंठिका
मुखविलुण्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखविष्ठा
मुखविष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and विष्ठा fæces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखव्यादान|मुखव्यादानं
मुखव्यादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Opening the mouth wide.<BR>E.<BR>मुख, with वि and आङ् prefixed to दा to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशफ|मुखशफः
मुखशफ<BR>mfn. (-फः-फा-फं)<BR>Foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशोधन|मुखशोधनं|मुखशोधनः
मुखशोधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Pungency, sharp or pungent flavour<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and शोधन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशोधिन्
मुखशोधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>The lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and शोधिन् what cleanses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखष्ठील|मुखष्ठीलः
मुखष्ठील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखसम्भव|मुखसंभव|मुखसंभवः|मुखसम्भवः
मुखसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, (of BRAHMĀ,) and सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखसुर|मुखसुरं
मुखसुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The moisture of the lips.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and सुरा spirituous liquor, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखस्राव|मुखस्रावः
मुखस्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Spittle, saliva.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, स्रु to drop, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखाग्नि|मुखाग्निः
मुखाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 The conflagration of a forest.<BR>2 A sort of goblin with a face of fire.<BR>3 Fire put into the mouth of the corpse at the time of lighting the funeral pile.<BR>4 A sacrificial or consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>मुच mouth, face, or chief, principal, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखास्त्र|मुखास्त्रः
मुखास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखोल्का
मुखोल्का<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>Fire in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>मुख face or mouth, and उल्का flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्य|मुख्यः
मुख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Chief, primary, principal.<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>1 A principal or essential rite or ordinance.<BR>2 Reading or teaching the Vedas.<BR>3 The month when reckoned from new moon to new moon.<BR>E.<BR>मुख chief, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यता
मुख्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Pre-eminence, being best or chief.<BR>E.<BR>मुख्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, मुख्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यशस्
मुख्यशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Principally, particularly.<BR>E.<BR>मुख्य, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुगूह|मुगूहः
मुगूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्ध|मुग्धः
मुग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Lovely, beautiful.<BR>2 Stupid, ignorant, an idiot, a fool.<BR>3 Simple, silly.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>A young and lovely female.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धता
मुग्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Loveliness.<BR>2 Ignorance, stupidity.<BR>3 Simplicity.<BR>E.<BR>मुग्ध, and तल् added; also मुग्धत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धानन
मुग्धानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Lovely-faced.<BR>E.<BR>मुग्ध, and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच
मुच<BR>(ऌ औ) औ मुचॢ r. 6th cl. (मुञ्चति-ते)<BR>1 To be loose or free.<BR>2 To forsake or abandon.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मोचयति)<BR>1 To let loose, to let go, to discharge as arrows, to part with, as wealth, &c.<BR>2 To gladden, to delight.<BR>(मोचते)<BR>To deceive, to cheat.<BR>(इ) मुचि r. 1st cl. (मुंचते)<BR>1 To be vain or proud.<BR>2 To be wicked.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>4 To grind or pound.<BR>5 To cheat, to deceive.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To give much.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To obtain liberation.<BR>2 To give or bestow.<BR>3 To lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचक|मुचकः
मुचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Lac, the dye.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to loosen, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचिर|मुचिरः
मुचिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Munificent, generous, liberal in giving, a donor, a giver.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let loose, to part with wealth, and किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुकुन्द|मुचुकुंद|मुचुकुंदः|मुचुकुन्दः
मुचुकुन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A tree, (Pterospermum salicifolium.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुटी
मुचुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 Snapping the fingers.<BR>2 The fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=664" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुज
मुज<BR>r. 1st cl. (मोजति मोजयति) also (इ,) मुजि (मुञ्जति मुञ्जयति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्च
मुञ्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (मुञ्चति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चक|मुञ्चकः
मुञ्चक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चत्
मुञ्चत्<BR>mfn. (ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्)<BR>1 Letting go or loose.<BR>2 Shooting, discharging.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज|मुंज|मुंजः|मुञ्जः
मुञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 A sort of grass, from the fibres of which a string is prepared, of which the triple thread worn by the Brahman as a girdle should be formed, (Saccharum munja, Rox.)<BR>2 The Brahmanical girdle, or in common use, the sacred string or cord.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>मुजि to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जकेश|मुंजकेश|मुञ्जकेशः
मुञ्जकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुञ्ज a sort of grass, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जकेशिन्|मुंजकेशिन्
मुञ्जकेशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुञ्ज the plant, केश hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जबन्धन|मुंजबंधन
मुञ्जबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Investiture with the girdle or with the Brahmanical cord.<BR>E.<BR>मुञ्ज, and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जर|मुंजर|मुंजरं|मुञ्जरं
मुञ्जर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The fibrous root of a lotus.<BR>E.<BR>मुञ्ज a sort of grass, रा to go or resemble, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जातक|मुञ्जातकः
मुञ्जातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Munja grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट
मुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (मोटति) 6th cl. (मुटति); and 10th cl. (मोटयति); also (इ) मुटि r. 1st. cl. (मुण्टति^1)<BR>1 To rub, to press, to grind or pound, to reduce to powder.<BR>2 To break down, to trample on.<BR>6th cl. (मुटति)<BR>To reprove, to rebuke, to blame.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुठ
मुठ<BR>(इ) मुठि r. 1st cl. (मुंठति)<BR>1 To guard, to protect, to defend or cherish.<BR>2 To fly, to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुड
मुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (मुडति)<BR>1 To quit, to leave.<BR>2 To clothe or cover.<BR>(इ) मुडि r. 1st cl. (मुण्डते)<BR>1 To be pure or clean.<BR>2 To cleanse.<BR>3 To sink, (as in water.)<BR>4 To sink, (in estimation,) to be despised or disregarded. (मुण्डति)<BR>5 To shave or cut.<BR>6 To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण
मुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (मुणति)<BR>To vow or promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड|मुंड|मुण्डं|मुण्डः
मुण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Shaved, bald, having no hair on the head.<BR>2 Low, mean.<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 The forehead.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A bald pate.<BR>2 A barber.<BR>3 The name of a Daitya or demon.<BR>4 RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>5 The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>मुडि to shave or cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डक|मुंडक|मुण्डकं|मुंडकः|मुण्डकः
मुण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barber.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>मुडि to shave, aff. वुन्, or मुण्ड the head, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डचणक|मुण्डचणकः
मुण्डचणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डन|मुंडन|मुंडनं|मुण्डनं
मुण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaving, shearing, outing^1.<BR>E.<BR>मुडि to shave or cut, aff. ल्युट्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डफल|मुंडफल|मुण्डफलः
मुण्डफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्ड the head, and फल, fruit; the fruit being one step towards a human head, made by VIŚVĀMITRA, when he purposed establishing an opposition creation to that of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डमण्डली
मुण्डमण्डली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A number of shaven heads.<BR>2 A mass of troops of an inferior description.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्ड, and मण्डली a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डशालि|मुंडशालि|मुण्डशालिः
मुण्डशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A kind of grain or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डित|मुंडित|मुण्डितं
मुण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bald, shorn, shaven.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्ड bald, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डितशिरस्
मुण्डितशिरस्<BR>mfn. (-राः-राः-रः)<BR>Bald-pated, shaven-headed.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्डित, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डितिका
मुण्डितिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डिन्|मुंडिन्
मुण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्ड shaving, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरिका
मुण्डीरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरी
मुण्डीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, described as a creeper, bearing a red and yellow flower, and commonly called by the same name, Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुत्य|मुत्यं
मुत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुथ
मुथ<BR>(इ) मुथि r. 1st cl. (मुन्थति)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद
मुद<BR>r. 1st cl. (मोदते)<BR>To rejoice, to be glad.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मोदयति)<BR>To mix, to blend, to unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
मुद्<BR>f. (मुद् मुत्)<BR>1 Pleasure, delight, joy.<BR>2 Intoxication, phrensy.<BR>3 A wife.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to be pleased, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदा
मुदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Happiness, joy.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to be happy, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदान्वित
मुदान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, happy.<BR>E.<BR>मुदा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदित|मुदितः
मुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, delighted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pleasure, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to rejoice, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदिर|मुदिरः
मुदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A lover, a libertine.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to be pleased, Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदी
मुदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to please, affs. क and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>1 A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>2 A cover, as a lid or cloth.<BR>E.<BR>मुदि to please, Uṇādi aff. ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गपर्णी
मुद्गपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>E.<BR>मुद्ग P. mungo, पर्ण a leaf, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गभुज्
मुद्गभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>मुद्ग kidney-bean, and भुज् who eats; also मुद्गभोजिन् m. (-जी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गर|मुद्गरं|मुद्गरः
मुद्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A mallet, a mace, a weapon formed like a carpenter's hammer.<BR>2 A staff, armed with iron, and larger at the lower extremity, used for breaking clods of earth, &c.<BR>3 A carpenter's hammer.<BR>4 A sort of flower, said to be a kind of jasmine, perhaps Jasminum zambac, the wild variety.<BR>E.<BR>मुट् pleasure, गॄ to swallow or destroy, aff. अच्; also with र changed to ल, मुद्गल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गष्ठ
मुद्गष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus lobatus.)<BR>E.<BR>मुद्ग P. mungo, स्था to stay, to resemble, aff. क; also with कन् added, मुद्गष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रा
मुद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 A seal, a signet.<BR>2 A seal ring.<BR>3 The mark of a seal or similar impression, a stamp, a print, &c.<BR>4 A mode of intertwining the fingers during religious worship.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to please, (by it,) Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राङ्कित|मुद्राङ्कितः
मुद्राङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stamped, sealed.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A mint.<BR>E.<BR>मुद्रा a seal, and अङ्कित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रिका
मुद्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sealed or signed paper.<BR>E.<BR>मुद्र a seal, and कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रित|मुद्रितं
मुद्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sealed.<BR>2 Marked, struck, stamped.<BR>3 Contracted, closed, sealed up.<BR>4 Unblown, (as a flower.)<BR>E.<BR>मुद्रा a seal, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुधा
मुधा<BR>ind.<BR>In vain, uselessly, unprofitably, idly.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, aff. का, and ह changed to ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनि|मुनिः
मुनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A holy sage, a pious and learned person, endowed with more or less of a divine nature, or having attained it by rigid abstraction and mortification; the title is applied to the Ṛṣis, the Brahmādikas, and to a great number of persons distinguished for their writings, considered as [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">Page666</a>] inspired, as PĀṆINI, VYĀSA, &c.<BR>2 An ascetic, a devotee.<BR>3 An Arhat or Jaina deified teacher.<BR>4 The saint AGASTYA.<BR>5 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>6 Another tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मन to be revered, Uṇādi aff. इन्, and उ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=665" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिद्रुम|मुनिद्रुमः
मुनिद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>मुनि the saint AGASTYA, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपित्तल|मुनिपित्तलं
मुनिपित्तल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a devotee, and पित्तल brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुङ्गव|मुनिपुंगव|मुनिपुङ्गवः
मुनिपुङ्गव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A pre-eminent sage.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage, and पुङ्गव (in composition) pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुत्त्रक
मुनिपुत्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage, पुत्त्र a child, and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपूग|मुनिपूगः
मुनिपूग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A kind of Areca, (A. triandra, or gracilis, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage, and पूग the Areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिभेषज|मुनिभेषजं
मुनिभेषज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Fasting.<BR>2 The fruit of the yellow myrobalan.<BR>3 The saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage and भेषज a drug or medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिसुव्रत|मुनिसुव्रतः
मुनिसुव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The twentieth Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिस्थान|मुनिस्थानं
मुनिस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A hermitage, the abode or retirement of holy sages.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि an ascetic, and स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनीन्द्र|मुनींद्र|मुनीन्द्रः
मुनीन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A superior Muni or sage.<BR>2 A Buddha, a Bauddha sage or teacher.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुन्यन्न
मुन्यन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Wild grain, roots, fruit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a hermit, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षु|मुमुक्षुः
मुमुक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>1 A sage, abstracted from all human passion and feeling, and preparing himself for eternal emancipation.<BR>2 Any one anxious for liberation, especially from mundane existence.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to liberate, in the desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषु|मुमुषिषुः
मुमुषिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to steal.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषुवत्
मुमुषिषुवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like a thief.<BR>E.<BR>मुमु, and षिषुवति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षा
मुमूर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Wish to die, impatience of life.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षु|मुमूर्षुः
मुमूर्षु<BR>m. (-र्षुः)<BR>A man at the point of death, a dying man.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, desiderative or expectative form, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर|मुरं|मुरः
मुर<BR>r. 6th cl. (मुरति)<BR>To encircle, to entwine, to bind together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्
मुर्<BR>f. (-मूः)<BR>Fainting.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to faint, aff. क्विप्, and the छ rejected after र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर|मुरं|मुरः
मुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The name of a DAITYA killed by VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A vegetable perfume.<BR>(-रं)<BR>Surrounding, encircling.<BR>E.<BR>मुर to encircle, aff. क, or अङ् and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरज|मुरजः
मुरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A small drum, a tabor.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 The wife of KUVERA.<BR>2 A large drum.<BR>E.<BR>मुर encircling, with wood, &c., and ज born, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजफल|मुरजफलः
मुरजफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The jack fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरण्ड|मुरण्डः
मुरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A country on the north-west of Hindustan, called also Lampaka, and now Lamgan.<BR>m. plu. (-ण्डाः)<BR>The inhabitants of Lamgan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरद|मुरदः
मुरद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The conch of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुर a demon, दो to cut, (to alarm,) aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरन्दला|मुरंदला
मुरन्दला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Narmadā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरमण्ड
मुरमण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Pimples on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुररिपु|मुररिपुः
मुररिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुर the demon, and रिपु enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरला
मुरला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Narmadā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरली
मुरली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A flute, a pipe.<BR>E.<BR>मुर surrounding, ला to get or have, aff. क and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलीधर|मुरलीधरः
मुरलीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मुरली a flute, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरहन्
मुरहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुर the demon, and हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरारि|मुरारिः
मुरारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मुर the demon, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्च्छ
मुर्च्छ<BR>(आ) मुर्च्छा r. 1st cl. (मूर्च्छति)<BR>1 To be faint, to lose consciousness or perception.<BR>2 To increase, to grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्भिणी
मुर्भिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A small fire place or fire pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मुर|मुर्मुरः
मुर्मुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>2 A fire of chaff.<BR>3 One of the horses of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्व|मुर्व्व
मुर्व<BR>(ई) मुर्व्वी r. 1st cl. (मुर्वति)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल
मुल<BR>r. 10th cl. (मोलयति)<BR>To plant: more usually मूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशटी
मुशटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A kind of panick seed, (Panicum italicum,) described as a white variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशली
मुशली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A small house lizard: see मुषली; also with कन added, मुशलिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष
मुष<BR>r. 1st cl. (मोषति) r. 9th cl. (मुष्णाति)<BR>To steal, to rob, to plunder.<BR>r. 4th cl. (मुष्यति)<BR>1 To cut, to divide, to break.<BR>2 To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषक|मुषकः
मुषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A rat: see मूषक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल|मुषलः
मुषल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A club, a mace.<BR>2 A pestle for cleaning rice.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A house lizard.<BR>2 A plant, (Curculigo orchioides): see मुशली, मुसल, and मुसली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषलामुषलि
मुषलामुषलि<BR>ind.<BR>Club to club, (fighting, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मुषल repeated, and इच् added; also मुसलामुमली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल्य|मुषल्यः
मुषल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Meriting pounding to death: see मुसल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषा
मुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A crucible.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, aff. अङ् and टाप्, also मूषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषित|मुषितं
मुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stolen, robbed.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, a. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्क|मुष्कः
मुष्क<BR>m. (-ष्कः)<BR>1 The scrotum.<BR>2 The testicle.<BR>3 A heap, a quantity.<BR>4 A thief.<BR>5 A stout man.<BR>6 A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, (semen, &c.) कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कक|मुष्ककः
मुष्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्क a thief, (of disease,) and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कद्वय
मुष्कद्वय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The testicles.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्क, and द्वय pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कर|मुष्करः
मुष्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A man with large testicles.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्क testicle, and रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कशून्य|मुष्कशून्यः
मुष्कशून्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A eunuch, a guard of the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्क testicle, and शून्य wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्ट
मुष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टि|मुष्टिः
मुष्टि<BR>mf. (-ष्टिः-ष्टी)<BR>1 The fist, the closed hand.<BR>2 The hilt or handle of a sword, &c.<BR>3 A handful or Pala, the initiatory measure in the tables of the measures of grain.<BR>4 Filching, stealing.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal or take, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिक|मुष्टिकः
मुष्टिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A goldsmith.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि stealing, and कृ to make, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिकान्तक|मुष्टिकांतक|मुष्टिकान्तकः
मुष्टिकान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of BALADEVA the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिद्यूत|मुष्टिद्यूतं
मुष्टिद्यूत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A kind of game, odd or even.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि the fist, and द्यूत gaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=666" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिन्धम|मुष्टिंधम
मुष्टिन्धम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Who blows in or on his closed fists.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि, and ध्मा to breathe, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिन्धय|मुष्टिंधय|मुष्टिंधयः|मुष्टिन्धयः
मुष्टिन्धय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A child.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि the fist, and धे to drink or suck, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिपात|मुष्टिपातः
मुष्टिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Pummelling, boxing.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिबन्ध|मुष्टिबंध|मुष्टिबन्धः
मुष्टिबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Clenching the fist.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि the fist, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिसंग्राहपीडित
मुष्टिसंग्राहपीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Squeezed, pressed, griped.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि, सङ्ग्राह taking, पीडित squeezed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टीमुष्टि
मुष्टीमुष्टि<BR>ind.<BR>Fist to fist, (fighting,) fisticuffs.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि repeated in this sense, and the first final made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्णत्
मुष्णत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्णन्-ष्णन्ती-ष्णत्)<BR>1 Stealing, robbing.<BR>2 Depriving of.<BR>3 Obscuring, eclipsing.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस
मुस<BR>(इर) मुसिर r. 4th cl. (मुस्यति)<BR>To divide, to cut or break to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल|मुसलं|मुसलः
मुसल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A pestle, a wooden pestle used for cleaning rice.<BR>2 A club.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>2 A house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>मुस to break, aff. कलच्; it is also read with its compounds and derivatives मुषल, मुषली, and sometimes मुशल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलिन्
मुसलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मुसल a pestle, or pestle-like club, used by him as a weapon, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल्य|मुसल्यः
मुसल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Deserving death by pounding with a pestle.<BR>E.<BR>मुसल a pestle, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त|मुस्तं|मुस्तः
मुस्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (मुस्तयति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त|मुस्तं|मुस्तः
मुस्त<BR>mf. (-स्तः-स्ता)<BR>A sort of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>मुस्त to accumulate, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तक|मुस्तकः
मुस्तक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>2 A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>मुस्त to accumulate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्ताद|मुस्तादः
मुस्ताद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>मुस्ता Cyperus, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तु|मुस्तुः
मुस्तु<BR>m. (-स्तुः)<BR>The fist.<BR>E.<BR>मुस to break, तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्र|मुस्रं
मुस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A pestle.<BR>E.<BR>मुस to divide, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह
मुह<BR>r. 4th cl. (ऊ) मुहू (मुह्यति)<BR>To be foolish, to be incapable of discrimination or judgment, to be bereft of sense or wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहिर|मुहिरः
मुहिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Love, desire, KĀMADEVA.<BR>2 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to grow foolish, Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुर्भाषा
मुहुर्भाषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Tautology, repetition.<BR>E.<BR>मुहुस् repeatedly, and भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुस्
मुहुस्<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly, reiteratedly, again and again.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, Uṇādi aff. उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्त्त<BR>mn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्तं)<BR>A division of time, the thirtieth part of a day and night, or an hour of forty-eight minutes.<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>हुर्च्छ to be crooked or fraudulent, क्त aff., form irr., and मुक् initiatory augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहेर|मुहेरः
मुहेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fool, a blockhead, an ignoramus.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, एरक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू<BR>r. 1st cl. (मवते)<BR>To bind, to tie, to make fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू<BR>f. (-मूः)<BR>Binding, tying.<BR>E.<BR>मू to tie, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूक|मूकः
मूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Dumb.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 A demon.<BR>3 A pauper.<BR>E.<BR>मू imitative sound, and कै to utter, aff. क, or मू to bind, कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Foolish, ignorant.<BR>2 Cold, apathetic, stupid.<BR>3 Perplexed, in doubt.<BR>4 Deceived, erring.<BR>m. (-ढः)<BR>1 An idiot, a fool.<BR>2 A sluggard.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढगर्भ|मूढगर्भः
मूढगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 A bad presentation of the child at birth, causing difficult delivery.<BR>2 A dead foetus.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ, and गर्भ the foetus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढग्राह|मूढग्राहः
मूढग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Infatuation.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ, and ग्राह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढचेतस्
मूढचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Insane, bewildered.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढता
मूढता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Folly, silliness, ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ, and तल् aff.; also मूढत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढात्मन्
मूढात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Foolish, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
मूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>E.<BR>मू to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र|मूत्रं
मूत्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (मूत्रयति)<BR>To urine, to make water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र|मूत्रं
मूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Urine, piss.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र to piss, घञ् aff., or मुच to loose, Uṇādi aff. त्रन्, and ऊ substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रकृच्छ्र|मूत्रकृच्छ्रं
मूत्रकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>1 Strangury.<BR>2 Unrinary affection in general, as gravel, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र urine, and कृच्छ्र pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रदोष|मूत्रदोषः
मूत्रदोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Gonorrhoea, considered as an urinary complaint.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र urine, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रपुट|मूत्रपुटं
मूत्रपुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The lower belly.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र urine, and पुट to be shallow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रग्रन्थि|मूत्रग्रन्थिः
मूत्रग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>Obstruction at the neck of the bladder.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and ग्रन्थि knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रमार्ग|मूत्रमार्गः
मूत्रमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The urethra.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and मार्ग passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रल|मूत्रलं
मूत्रल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Diuretic.<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>A cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र urine, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रशुक्र
मूत्रशुक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>Milky urine, depositing a thick white sediment.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and शक्र semen, which is supposed to give the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रसङ्ग|मूत्रसंग|मूत्रसंगः
मूत्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Urinary obstruction.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and सङ्ग being with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्राघात|मूत्राघातः
मूत्राघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Suppression of urine.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and आधात impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रातीत
मूत्रातीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Difficult or slow passage of urine.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्राशय|मूत्राशयः
मूत्राशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The bladder.<BR>2 The lower belly, the pubic region.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र urine, and आशय place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रित|मूत्रितः
मूत्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pissed, voided as urine.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र to urine aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रोत्सङ्ग|मूत्रोत्संग
मूत्रोत्सङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Obstructed or tardy flow of urine, discharge of it mixed with blood, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मूत्र, and उत्सङ्ग adhesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख<BR>mfn. (-र्खः-र्खा-र्खं)<BR>Foolish, ignorant, stupid, idiotic.<BR>m. (-र्खः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>E.<BR>मूर्ख substituted for मुह to be foolish, aff. अच्, or मुर substituted for the root, with ख Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खभ्रातृक|मूर्खभ्रातृकः
मूर्खभ्रातृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The brother of a fool.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्ख a fool, भ्रातृ a brother, and कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छत्
मूर्च्छत्<BR>mfn. (-र्च्छन्-र्च्छन्ती-र्च्छत्)<BR>Fainting, swooning.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to faint, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छन
मूर्च्छन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Fainting, syncope, swooning.<BR>2 Mixing, meeting.<BR>3 A tone or semitone as placed in its scale, the seventh part of a Grāma or scale.<BR>4 Calcining quicksilver with sulphur, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to faint, to become insensible, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छा
मूर्च्छा<BR>f. (-र्च्छा)<BR>Fainting, loss of consciousness or sense.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छा to be faint, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=667" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छाल
मूर्च्छाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Fainted, fainting, insensible.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्च्छा fainting, (the act,) and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छावत्
मूर्च्छावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Faint.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्च्छा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छित
मूर्च्छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fainting, fainted, insensible.<BR>2 Stupid, ignorant.<BR>3 Tall, lofty.<BR>4 Grown, increased, augmented.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to be faint, to grow or increase, &c., aff. क्त, or मूर्च्छा as above, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ण|मूर्णः
मूर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्व्व to bind, aff. क्त; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्त|मूर्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Fainting, fainted, losing sense or consciousness.<BR>2 Solid, material, endowed with form or shape.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to lose consciousness, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्ति|मूर्ति|मूर्तिः|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 Matter, substance, solidity.<BR>2 The body.<BR>3 Figure, form, body in general, or any definite shape or image.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्च्छ to faint, to become insensible, aff. क्तिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्तिमत्|मूर्तिमत्|मूर्तिमन्त्
मूर्त्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Material, substantial, having shape or substance.<BR>2 Incarnate.<BR>n. (-मत्)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्त्ति shape, &c., मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धक
मूर्द्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The man of the second or military class.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध the head, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धकर्प्परी
मूर्द्धकर्प्परी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>An umbrella, or inverted basket carried on the head for the same purpose.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्धं the head, कर्प्पर a sort of pan, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धखोल
मूर्द्धखोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of umbrella: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध the head, खोल or खोलक a helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धज
मूर्द्धज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Hair, the hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध the head, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धन्
मूर्द्धन्<BR>m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, form irr., or मुर्व्व to bind, the same aff., धङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धपुष्प
मूर्द्धपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A tree, commonly Siris, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्धं the head, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धरस
मूर्द्धरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The scum of boiled rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध head, top, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धवेष्टन
मूर्द्धवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A turban, a fillet, a diadem, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध the head, and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धाभिषिक्त
मूर्द्धाभिषिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>1 A man of the second or military class, the Kṣatriya or soldier.<BR>2 A king, a prince.<BR>3 A chief minister, a counsellor of state.<BR>4 The name of a mixed class, sprung from a Brahman, and female of the second or Kṣatriya tribe; the principal of the mixed races, and soldier by profession.<BR>E.<BR>मूर्द्ध the head, and अभिषिक्त sprinkled, anointed; kings being consecrated by having poured on their heads, while seated on a throne prepared for the purpose, water from some sacred stream, mixed with honey, clarified butter, and spirituous liquor, as well as two sorts of grass and the sprouts of corn: the term applies to the Kṣatriya as identified with the king, the duties of royalty, belonging especially, to the military caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्ध्वन्
मूर्द्ध्वन्<BR>m. (-र्द्ध्वा)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 The base, (in geometry.)<BR>E.<BR>मुर्व्व to bind, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, and ध्वङ् substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्व्वा|मूर्वा
मूर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा-र्व्वी)<BR>A sort of creeper, from the fibres of which bowstrings are made, (Sanseviera zeylanica); they should also form the girdle worn by the Kṣatriya class.<BR>E.<BR>मुर्व्व to bind, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल|मूलं|मूलः
मूल<BR>r. 1st cl. (मूलति-ते)<BR>To stand, to be rooted or firm.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मूलयति)<BR>1 To plant or transplant.<BR>2 To grow as a plant, to sprout, to shoot or germinate.<BR>With उद् prefixed,<BR>to root up or out, to eradicate, to exterminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल|मूलं|मूलः
मूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A root, the root of a tree, &c.<BR>2 Origin, commencement.<BR>3 Capital, principal.<BR>4 Near, proximate.<BR>5 Own, peculiar, proper.<BR>6 The root of the Arum campanulatum.<BR>7 The original text of any work, as opposed to the Ṭīkā or comment.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>The nineteenth lunar asterism, containing eleven stars, which appear to be the same as those in the SCORPION'S tail.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A small house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>मूल to stand, to be rooted or firm, aff. क, or मू to bind, Uṇādi aff. क्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलक|मूलकं|मूलकः
मूलक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The radish, (Raphanus sativus.)<BR>2 A large, sort of yam.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकपण|मूलकपणः
मूलकपण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A handful of radishes, &c. for sale.<BR>E.<BR>मूलक, and पण measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकमूला
मूलकमूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, commonly Kṣīrakākolī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकर्म्मन्|मूलकर्मन्
मूलकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Magic.<BR>E.<BR>मूल original or essential, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकारिका
मूलकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fire place.<BR>E.<BR>मूल primary, (work,) and कारिका an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकृच्छ्र|मूलकृच्छ्रः
मूलकृच्छ्र<BR>n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>A sort of penance, subsisting for a given time on the roots of plants only.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलखानक|मूलखानकः
मूलखानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A digger for roots.<BR>E.<BR>मूल, and खानक a digger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलज|मूलजं|मूलजः
मूलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born from a root, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A plant growing from a root, as a lotus, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलदेव|मूलदेवः
मूलदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of KAṂSA, the uncle of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मूल original, and देव a deity; the incarnation of a demi-god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलद्रव्य|मूलद्रव्यं
मूलद्रव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Capital, principal, stock.<BR>E.<BR>मूल capital, and द्रव्य substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलधन|मूलधनं
मूलधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Capital, principal, stock.<BR>E.<BR>मूल capital, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलपर्णी
मूलपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Hydrocotyle asiatica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलभद्र|मूलभद्रः
मूलभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A name of KAṂSA, the uncle of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>मूल origin, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलभृत्य|मूलभृत्यः
मूलभृत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>An old or hereditary servant.<BR>E.<BR>मूल, and भृत्य dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलविभुज|मूलविभुजः
मूलविभुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A car, a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>मूल the root, (the axle,) and विभुज what bends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलशाकट|मूलशाकटः
मूलशाकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>Fit or cultivated for esculent roots, (as the arum, the radish, and others, a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, and शाकट aff.; also with शाकिन aff. मूलशाकिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलस्थान
मूलस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Ether, heaven, space or atmosphere.<BR>2 GOD.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>GAURĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मूल primary origin, &c., and स्थान place, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिक|मूलिकः
मूलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Radical, (literal or figurative,) primary, principal.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A devotee, living on roots.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन्
मूलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Having a root, stock, origin, &c.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=668" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलेर|मूलेरः
मूलेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Indian spikenard.<BR>E.<BR>मूल to be rooted, Uṇādi aff. एरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्य|मूल्यं
मूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 To be eradicated, to be pulled or plucked up by the root.<BR>2 To be bent from the root, &c.<BR>3 To be bought, purchasable.<BR>4 To be bought for a fair or just price.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Price.<BR>2 Wages, hire.<BR>3 An article purchased.<BR>E.<BR>मूल principal, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष|मूषः
मूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (मूषति)<BR>To steal, to rob or plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष|मूषः
मूष<BR>mf. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>1 A rat, a mouse.<BR>2 A crucible.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A sort of grass, (Andropogon serratum.)<BR>E.<BR>मूष to steal, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषक|मूषकः
मूषक<BR>mf. (-कः-का-षिका)<BR>1 A mouse, a rat.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषकाराति|मूषकारातिः
मूषकाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>मूषक a rat, and अराति enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषण|मूषणं
मूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Stealing, pilfering.<BR>E.<BR>मूष to steal, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषत्
मूषत्<BR>mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्)<BR>Stealing, plundering.<BR>E.<BR>मूष, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषाकर्णी
मूषाकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>मूषा a rat, कर्ण the ear; to which the leaf of the plant is compared, fem. aff. ङीष्; also मूषिकपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषातुत्थ|मूषातुत्थं
मूषातुत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>मूषा a crucible, and तुत्थ sulphate of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिक|मूषिकः
मूषिक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A rat, a mouse.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, commonly Siris, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>2 A thief, a plunderer.<BR>3 A country, the part of the Malabar coast between Quilon and Cape Comorin.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>2 A crucible.<BR>E.<BR>मूष to steal, Uṇādi aff. किनन्, and the vowel made long; also मूषिका, and मूषा, मूषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकपर्णी|मूषिकपर्ण्णी
मूषिकपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>An aquatic plant of the cryptogamia class (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>मूषिक a rat, (ears, understood,) and पर्णी a leaf, aff. ङीष्, having a leaf compared to a mouse's ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाङ्क|मूषिकांक|मूषिकाङ्कः
मूषिकाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>मूषिक a rat, and अङ्क a mark or emblem; being usually painted riding on a rat or attended by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाञ्चन|मूषिकांचन|मूषिकाञ्चनः
मूषिकाञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>मूषिक a rat, and अञ्चन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाराति|मूषिकारातिः
मूषिकाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>मूषिक, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाह्वय|मूषिकाह्वयः
मूषिकाह्वय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>मूषिक a rat, and आह्वय appellation; also मूषिकाह्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषित
मूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stolen.<BR>E.<BR>मूष, and क्त, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिपर्णिका
मूषिपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मूषि for मूषी, and कन् added to पर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीक|मूषीकः
मूषीक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A rat, a mouse.<BR>E.<BR>मूष to steal, कीकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्यायण|मूष्यायणः
मूष्यायण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Born of unknown parents, of concealed birth or origin.<BR>E.<BR>अमूष्यायण the son of somebody, and the initiatory vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृ
मृ<BR>(मृ) r. 6th cl. (म्रियते)<BR>To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृकण्डक|मृकण्डकः
मृकण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a saint; also called MĀRKAṆḌEYA.<BR>E.<BR>मृकण्ड the name of his father, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृकण्डु|मृकण्डुः
मृकण्डु<BR>m. (-ण्डुः)<BR>The saint MĀRKAṆḌEYA.<BR>E.<BR>मृकण्डु his father, अण् aff., but the word unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष
मृक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (मृक्षति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect, to fill.<BR>r. 10th cl. (मृक्षयति)<BR>1 To mix, to mingle, to blend or combine.<BR>2 To speak incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग<BR>r. 4th cl. (मृग्यति) r. 10th cl. (मृगयते)<BR>To seek, to pursue, to hunt, to chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A deer, an antelope.<BR>2 An animal in general.<BR>3 Research, inquiry, investigation.<BR>4 Asking, soliciting, begging.<BR>5 A kind of elephant, one with white marks on his forehead.<BR>6 The fifth lunar constellation, more usually Mṛgaśiras: see मृगशिरस्.<BR>7 The month in which the moon is full in the constellation Mṛgaśiras.<BR>8 A particular sacrifice.<BR>9 Musk.<BR>10 Hunting, chase.<BR>11 One of the four classes into which men are divided, in erotic works.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>1 A description of woman, perhaps the same as the one termed त्रित्रिणी, the corresponding female to the male called मृग.<BR>2 A female deer, a doe.<BR>3 A species of the Madhya metre.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to search, to chase, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगक्षीर|मृगक्षीरं
मृगक्षीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Doe's milk.<BR>E.<BR>मृग for मृगी a female deer, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगचैटक
मृगचैटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wild or pole cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजालिका
मृगजालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A net for confining deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and जालिका a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजीवन|मृगजीवनः
मृगजीवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and जीवन living, subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगण
मृगण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Search, inquiry, research.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to search for or after, aff. युच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्
मृगतृष्<BR>f. (-तृट्)<BR>Vapour floating over sands or desarts, and appearing at a distance like water.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, तृष् to thirst, aff. क्विप्; deer being deceived by it; also with अङ्, and टाप् aff. मृगतृषा, and with तृष्णा thirst, मृगतृष्णा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृषा
मृगतृषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Mirage: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्णा
मृगतृष्णा<BR>f. (-ष्णा)<BR>Sultry vapour, mirage: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्णिका
मृगतृष्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sultry vapour.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगदशक्
मृगदशक्<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>मृग deer, and दंशक who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगद्युत्
मृगद्युत्<BR>m. (-द्युत्)<BR>A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>मृग and द्यु to go, क्विप् aff. and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगद्यू
मृगद्यू<BR>m. (-द्यूः)<BR>A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>मृग, and दिब to play, क्विप् aff., and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगधूर्त्तक|मृगधूर्तक|मृगधूर्तकः|मृगधूर्त्तकः
मृगधूर्त्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and धूर्त्तक a cheat; preying upon them only in consequence of his luring them into his reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनाभि|मृगनाभिः
मृगनाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, (the musk deer,) and नाभि the navel; the musk being formed in a bag attached to the belly of the animal about the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनाभिज
मृगनाभिज<BR>nf. (-जं-जा)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, नाभि the navel, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनेत्र
मृगनेत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>Possessing or relating to the constellation Mṛgaśīrṣa.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A woman with beautiful eyes, or eyes like a deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग the asterism, णा to get, तृच् aff., and अप् added, or मृग a deer, and नेत्र the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपति|मृगपतिः
मृगपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>मृग an animal or a deer, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपद
मृगपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A deer's foot.<BR>E.<BR>मृग, and पद for पाद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपालिका
मृगपालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The musk deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, पाल to nourish, वुन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपिप्लु|मृगपिप्लुः
मृगपिप्लु<BR>m. (-प्लुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and पिप्ल a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=669" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगबधाजीव|मृगबधाजीवः
मृगबधाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, बध killing, and आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगबन्धिनी|मृगबंधिनी
मृगबन्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A net for confining deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and बन्धिनी confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगभोजनी
मृगभोजनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Bitter apple or Colocynth.<BR>E.<BR>मृग, and भोजन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमद|मृगमदः
मृगमद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and मद passion, or fluid that distils from the elephant's temples when in rut, and to which this secretion is considered analogous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमातृका
मृगमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female antelope.<BR>E.<BR>मृग, and मातृ mother कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमान
मृगमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Seeking, pursuing, hunting.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to seek, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगया
मृगया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Chase, hunting.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to search or seek, यत् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगयु|मृगयुः
मृगयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A jackal.<BR>3 A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, या to go, कु Uṇādi aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगराज्
मृगराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>मृग an animal, and राज् who rules over; also with a final vowel, मृगराज m. (-जः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगरिपु|मृगरिपुः
मृगरिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>मृग an animal, and रिपु the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगरोमज|मृगरोमजं
मृगरोमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Woollen, (cloth, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मृग an animal, रोम hair, and ज produced, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगलाञ्छन|मृगलांछन|मृगलाञ्छनः
मृगलाञ्छन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, लाच्छन symbol, sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगवाहन|मृगवाहनः
मृगवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगव्य|मृगव्यं
मृगव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 Chase, hunting.<BR>2 The butt or mark in archery.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, व्यथ to destroy, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशिरस्
मृगशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>The fifth lunar mansion, containing three stars, one of which is λ ORIONIS, and figured by an antelope's head, whence its name.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and शिरस् the head; also मृगशिरा f. (-रा) or मृगशिरस् m. (-राः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशीर्ष|मृगशीर्षं|मृगशीर्षः
मृगशीर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>The constellation Mṛgaśiras: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and शीर्ष the head; also f. (-र्षा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाक्षी
मृगाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>1 Bitter apple, (Cucumis coloquintida.)<BR>2 A woman with eyes like a deer's.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाङ्क|मृगांक|मृगाङ्कः
मृगाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and अङ्क a mark, a symbol, or अकि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाजिन
मृगाजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A deer skin.<BR>E.<BR>मृग, and अजिन a skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाजीव|मृगाजीवः
मृगाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A hyena.<BR>2 A hunter.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and आजीव who lives by or preys upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाण्डजा|मृगांडजा
मृगाण्डजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, अण्ड testicle, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाद्
मृगाद्<BR>m. (-ट् or -त्)<BR>A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, अद to eat, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगादन|मृगादनः
मृगादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A hyena.<BR>2 A leopard.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Colocynth, (Cucumis coloquintida.)<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगान्तक|मृगांतक|मृगान्तकः
मृगान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Cīta or hunting leopard.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाराति|मृगारातिः
मृगाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगारि|मृगारिः
मृगारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>3 A dog, a hound.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाविध्
मृगाविध्<BR>m. (-विट्)<BR>A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>E.<BR>मृग a deer, व्यध to destroy, with आङ् prefix, and क्विप् aff., and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगित|मृगितः
मृगित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sought, pursued.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to chase, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्र|मृगेंद्र|मृगेन्द्रः
मृगेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>मृग an animal, and इन्द्र lord, master<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्रचटक|मृगेंद्रचटक|मृगेन्द्रचटकः
मृगेन्द्रचटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hawk, a falcon.<BR>E.<BR>मृगेन्द्र a lion, and चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्रमुख
मृगेन्द्रमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 The lion's mouth.<BR>2 A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>मृगेन्द्र, and मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगैर्व्वारु|मृगैर्वारु
मृगैर्व्वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A white deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्य|मृग्यः
मृग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>To be sought or inquired for.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to search, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्यमान
मृग्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being sought or inquired after.<BR>E.<BR>मृग to search, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज|मृजः
मृज<BR>(ऊ) मृजू r. 2nd cl. (मार्ष्टि) 1st and 10th cls. (मार्जति मार्जयति)<BR>1 To clean, to cleanse.<BR>2 To be clean or pure.<BR>3 To ornament.<BR>4 To sound.<BR>With अप or प्र prefixed,<BR>1 To sweep, to sweep away.<BR>2 To clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज|मृजः
मृज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A musical instrument, probably a sort of tabor or drum.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 Cleaning the body, by washing, anointing, &c.<BR>2 Purification, ablution.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, to sound, aff. क or अङ्, and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजान्वय
मृजान्वय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Clean, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>मृजा, and अन्वय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्य|मृज्यं
मृज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>To be cleaned or purified.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to cleanse, क्यप् aff.; also मार्ग्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड|मृडः
मृड<BR>r. 6th cl. (मृडति) r. 9th cl. (-मृड्णाति)<BR>1 To delight, to make happy.<BR>2 To rejoice, to be happy or delighted.<BR>r. 9th cl. (according to some authorities,)<BR>To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड|मृडः
मृड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The fire that completes an oblation.<BR>f. (-डानी)<BR>DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मृड to be pleased or delighted, aff. क, fem. aff. ङीष्, with आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडङ्कण|मृडङ्कणः
मृडङ्कण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A child, a pupil.<BR>E.<BR>मृड to be pleased, Uṇādi aff. कङ्कण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडीक|मृडीकः
मृडीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>मृड to delight, Uṇādi aff. कीकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण
मृण<BR>r. 6th cl. (मृणाति)<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणाल|मृणालं|मृणालः
मृणाल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>The film or fibres attached to the stalk of a lotus.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A small fibre in the stalk of the waterlily.<BR>E.<BR>मृण to hurt, Uṇādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालिन्
मृणालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A lotus.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>मृणाल a fibre, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्मय
मृण्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of earth or clay, (as porcelain, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>मृत्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत|मृतं
मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dead, expired, extinct, defunct.<BR>2 Calcined, reduced, (metals.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Solicited alms.<BR>2 Death.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतक|मृतकं|मृतकः
मृतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A dead body, a corpse.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतकल्प|मृतकल्पः
मृतकल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Insensible, fainted.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, and कल्प aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतकान्तक|मृतकांतक|मृतकान्तकः
मृतकान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, and कान्तक fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतण्ड|मृतंडः|मृतण्डः
मृतण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतपा
मृतपा<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>A man of the lowest caste, who for a subsistence collects dead men's clothes; conveys dead bodies to the river side to be burnt; executes criminals, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मृत, and पा who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=670" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतमत्त|मृतमत्तः
मृतमत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>मृत a corpse, and मत्त fond of, mad for; also with कन् added मृतमत्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतवत्सा
मृतवत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>A woman or female animal, whose offspring never live long.<BR>E.<BR>मृत, and वत्स young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतशङ्का
मृतशङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>The fear entertained of a person's being dead.<BR>E.<BR>मृत, and शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतसञ्जीवनी|मृतसंजीवनी
मृतसञ्जीवनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A Mantra for reviving the dead.<BR>E.<BR>मृत, सञ्जीवनी reviving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नात|मृतस्नातः
मृतस्नात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bathed after mourning.<BR>2 Dying immediately after ablution.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, and स्नात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नान|मृतस्नानं
मृतस्नान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Funeral ablution, bathing after mourning.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्वमोक्तृ
मृतस्वमोक्तृ<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>The name of a royal saint.<BR>E.<BR>मृत death, स्व his own, and मोक्तृ liberator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृताण्ड|मृतांड|मृताण्डः
मृताण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, and अण्ड egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतामद|मृतामदं|मृतामदः
मृतामद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, मद to please, आङ् prefix, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतालक|मृतालकं
मृतालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant sort of earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृत earth, अल to adorn, causal form, aff. अण्, and कन् added; also मृत्तालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृति|मृतिः
मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतोद्भव|मृतोद्भवः
मृतोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>मृत dead, destroyed, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कर|मृत्करः
मृत्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A potter.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, and कर who works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कांश्य
मृत्कांश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>An earthen vessel, a mug, a pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, and कांश्य a goblet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्किरा
मृत्किरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>An earth worm.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, and किर a hog, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्खलिनी
मृत्खलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्ताल|मृत्तालं
मृत्ताल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of fragrant earth; also called Surat earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, ताल site, place of abiding; also with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्तालक|मृत्तालकं
मृत्तालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>and with a single consonant, मृतालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्तिका
मृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Earth, clay, soil.<BR>2 A fragrant earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, and तिकन् pleonastic addition, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्फली
मृत्फली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of Costus.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, and फल a fruit, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यु|मृत्युः
मृत्यु<BR>mfn. subst. (-त्युः-त्युः-त्यु)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>YAMA the judge of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, Uṇādi aff. त्युक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युञ्जय|मृत्युंजय|मृत्युंजयः|मृत्युञ्जयः
मृत्युञ्जय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and जय conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युनाशक|मृत्युनाशकः
मृत्युनाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and नाशक destroyer, remover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युपुष्प|मृत्युपुष्पः
मृत्युपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>Sugar cane.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and पुष्प flower; dying after flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युफल|मृत्युफलः
मृत्युफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A sort of fruit considered as poisonous.<BR>f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>The plantain.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युभङ्गुरक|मृत्युभङ्गुरकः
मृत्युभङ्गुरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A drum beat on funeral occasions.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, भङ्गुर crooked, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युभृत्य|मृत्युभृत्यः
मृत्युभृत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>Sickness, malady, disease.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, भृत्य servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युवञ्चन|मृत्युवंचन|मृत्युवञ्चनः
मृत्युवञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A raven or a kind of crow, the carrion crow.<BR>3 A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death or decay, and वञ्चन deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युवीज|मृत्युवीजः
मृत्युवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The bambu.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युसूति|मृत्युसूतिः
मृत्युसूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्यु death, and सूति bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्सा
मृत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>1 Good or rich soil.<BR>2 A fragrant earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, स aff. of superior quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्ना
मृत्स्ना<BR>f. (-त्स्ना)<BR>1 Good soil.<BR>2 A fragrant sort of earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृत् earth, स्न aff. of excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्नाभाण्डक|मृत्स्नाभाण्डकः
मृत्स्नाभाण्डक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pitcher, an earthen vessel for carrying water.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्स्ना earth, and भाण्डक vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद
मृद<BR>r. 9th cl. (मृद्नाति)<BR>1 To grind, to powder, to reduce to dust or powder.<BR>2 To trample on, to tread under foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
मृद्<BR>f. (मृद् मृत्)<BR>1 Earth, soil, clay.<BR>2 A fragrant earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to trample on, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्कुर|मृदंकुरः|मृदङ्कुरः
मृदङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The green pigeon, (Columba hariala, BUC.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्ग|मृदंग|मृदंगः|मृदङ्गः
मृदङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A tabour, a small drum.<BR>2 A double drum.<BR>3 A sound, a noise.<BR>4 A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to be trampled on, to be beat, Uṇādi aff. अङ्गच्; also with कन् added मृदङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्गफल|मृदंगफल|मृदङ्गफलः
मृदङ्गफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The jack tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>मृदङ्ग a drum, and फल a fruit; perhaps alluding to its size and shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदर
मृदर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Sportive, sporting.<BR>2 Passing quickly away, transient.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, दर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदा
मृदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Earth, clay, soil.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to trample on, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदाकर|मृदाकरः
मृदाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>मृदा earth, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदित|मृदितः
मृदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed, ground.<BR>2 Trodden or trampled on.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to reduce to powder, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदिनी
मृदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Good soil or earth.<BR>E.<BR>मृद् earth, इनि aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदु|मृदुः
मृदु<BR>mfn. (-दुः-द्वी-दु)<BR>1 Soft.<BR>2 Blunt, not sharp.<BR>3 Gentle, mild.<BR>f. (-द्वी)<BR>The brown grape.<BR>E.<BR>म्रद to rub, aff. कु, and the semivowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुकोष्ठ
मृदुकोष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A man of lax bowels, one easily affected by medicine.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु, and कोष्ठ intestinal canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुगमना
मृदुगमना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A goose, a swan.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुचर्म्मिन्|मृदुचर्मिन्
मृदुचर्म्मिन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मी)<BR>The Bhojpatra tree.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, चर्म्म skin or bark, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुच्छद|मृदुच्छदः
मृदुच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The Bhojpatra or birch tree.<BR>2 A kind of Pīlu, or tree growing in the hills.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and च्छद covering or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुता
मृदुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Softness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to मृदु; also with त्व, मृदुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुत्वच|मृदुत्वचः
मृदुत्वच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch tree, the bark of which peels off, and is used in making Hooka-snakes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and त्वच skin; also with a final consonant मृदुत्वच्, (-त्वक्.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुन्नक|मृदुन्नकं
मृदुन्नक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपर्व्वन्|मृदुपर्वन्
मृदुपर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>A cane or ratan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपाणि
मृदुपाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Having a soft and delicate hand.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु, and पाणि hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपुष्प|मृदुपुष्पः
मृदुपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Sirisha tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुल|मृदुलं
मृदुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Soft.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुरोमवत्|मृदुरोमवन्त्
मृदुरोमवत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, रोमन् hair, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुलोमक|मृदुलोमकः
मृदुलोमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, लोभ hair, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=671" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुवात
मृदुवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A gentle breeze, zephyr.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदूत्पल|मृदूत्पलं
मृदूत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The blue lotus, (Nymphæa cærulea)<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्भाण्ड|मृद्भांड
मृद्भाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>An earthen vessel.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वङ्ग|मृद्वंग|मृद्वङ्गं
मृद्वङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Of soft or tender frame or body.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A delicate woman.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and अङ्ग body, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वीका
मृद्वीका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A grape.<BR>E.<BR>मृद to hurt, कीकन् aff., and उक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध|मृधं
मृध<BR>(उ) मृधु r. 1st cl. (मर्द्धति-ते)<BR>1 To be moist or wet.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध|मृधं
मृध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>मृध to hurt or kill, aff. घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृन्मरु|मृन्मरुः
मृन्मरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A stone, a rock.<BR>E.<BR>मृद् earth, and मरु dry as a desart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृल्लोष्ट|मृल्लोष्टः
मृल्लोष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A clod of earth or clay.<BR>E.<BR>मृत्, and लोष्ट a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश
मृश<BR>(औ) मृशौ r. 6th cl. (मृशति)<BR>1 To touch.<BR>2 To see, to perceive.<BR>3 To consult, to consider, to deliberate.<BR>With परा,<BR>To counsel, to advise.<BR>With वि,<BR>To consider, to discuss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष
मृष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मर्षति-ते मर्षयति-ते) and 4th cl. (मृष्यति-ते)<BR>To bear, to suffer, to endure patiently.<BR>(उ) मृषु r. 1st cl. (मर्षति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To be angry.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be distressed, to bear hardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषा
मृषा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Falsely.<BR>2 Uselessly, in vain.<BR>E.<BR>मृष to bear, with का aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषार्थक|मृषार्थकं
मृषार्थक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An impossibility, an absurdity, (in speech or composition); the sense of which is evidently false, as कूर्म्मलोमतनुत्राणः, शशशृङ्गधनुर्धरः, his armour is of tortoise wool, and his bow the horn of a hare.<BR>E.<BR>मृषा falsely, अर्थ meaning, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषालक|मृषालकः
मृषालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावाद|मृषावादः
मृषावाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Irony, ironical praise.<BR>2 Falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>मृषा falsely, and वाद speech, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावादिन्
मृषावादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Speaking falsely, lying, a liar.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A false accuser, one who brings forward an unjust or unfounded accusation.<BR>E.<BR>मृषा falsely, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषोद्य|मृषोद्यं|मृषोद्यः
मृषोद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Speaking falsely, lying, a liar.<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>मृषा falsely, वद to speak, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
मृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>2 Touched, rubbed.<BR>3 Sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to clean, or मृष to rub, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
मृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Touching, contact.<BR>2 Cleaning.<BR>3 Sprinkling.<BR>4 Preparing the food for a meal.<BR>E.<BR>मृज to clean, or मृष to sprinkle, &c., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टेरुक|मृष्टेरुकः
मृष्टेरुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A liberal man, a donor, a benefactor.<BR>2 A churlish or inhospitable man.<BR>3 An eater of sweetmeats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मॄ
मॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (मृणाति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मे
मे<BR>r. 1st cl. (मयते)<BR>1 To barter or exchange.<BR>2 To return, to restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलकन्यका
मेकलकन्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The Narmadā river.<BR>E.<BR>मेकल or मेखल the name of a Ṛṣi the supposed father, or of a mountain, the source of the stream, and कन्यका daughter; hence also मेखलकन्यका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलाद्रिजा
मेकलाद्रिजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The Narmadā or Nerbadda river.<BR>E.<BR>मेकलाद्रि the Mekala mountain, part of the Vindhya range, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखला
मेखला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>2 A sword knot, a string or chain fastened to the hilt, and in fighting bound round the wrist to secure the weapon.<BR>3 A sword-belt.<BR>4 The edge or swell of a mountain.<BR>5 The Narmadā river.<BR>6 The sacrificial string of a Brahman when made of deer skin.<BR>7 A sort of figure, made on the four sides of the hole in which sacrificial fire is offered.<BR>8 A triple zone or string worn round the loins by the three first classes; the girdle of the Brahman should be of the fibres of the Munja or of Kuśa grass, that of the Kṣatriya of a Mūrvā or bowstring, and that of the Vaiśya of a thread of the Śaṇa, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मि to scatter, खलच् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलापद
मेखलापद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The hip and loins.<BR>E.<BR>मेखला a zone, and पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिन्
मेखलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Wearing a girdle.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A youth of the Brahman tribe, who previous to his marriage wears a girdle suited to his caste.<BR>E.<BR>मेखला, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ|मेघः
मेघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>3 A demon, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to sprinkle, aff. अच्, and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघकफ|मेघकफः
मेघकफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघकाल|मेघकालः
मेघकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The rains, the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघगर्ज्जन|मेघगर्जन
मेघगर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Thunder.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ, and गर्ज्जन noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघङ्कर|मेघंकर
मेघङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cloud-producing, (rainy season.)<BR>E.<BR>मेघ, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघचिन्तक|मेघचिंतक|मेघचिन्तकः
मेघचिन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucus.)<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, चिन्तक who thinks of; being supposed to drink no water but rain, and therefore naturally anxious for cloudy and rainy weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघज|मेघजं|मेघजः
मेघज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Cloud-born, produced in or from the clouds.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A large pearl.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघजाल|मेघजालं
मेघजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Talc.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and जाल a net; some copies read मेघनाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघजीवक|मेघजीवकः
मेघजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Cātaka.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and जीवक living: see मेघचिन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघज्योतिस्
मेघज्योतिस्<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A flash of lightning or the fire of it.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघतिमिर|मेघतिमिरं
मेघतिमिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Cloudiness, cloudy or rainy weather.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and तिमिर darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघदीप|मेघदीपः
मेघदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>मेव a cloud, and दीप inflamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघद्वार
मेघद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Sky, heaven, ether.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and द्वार the gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनाद|मेघनादः
मेघनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 A name of VARUṆA, deity of water.<BR>3 The noise or grumbling of clouds.<BR>4 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>5 A sort of amaranth, (Amaranthus polygamus.)<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and नाद sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनादजित्
मेघनादजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>LAKṢMAṆA, the favourite brother and companion of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>मघनाद the son of RĀVAṆA, and जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=672" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनादानुलासिन्
मेघनादानुलासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>मेघनाद the muttering of clouds, अनुलस to be delighted by, and णिनि aff.; pairing in the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनामन्
मेघनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud; and नामन् appellation, or it may apply to every term for a cloud, being a synonym of the grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनिर्घोष|मेघनिर्घोषः
मेघनिर्घोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The muttering or grumbling of clouds, low or distant thunder.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and निर्घोष sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघपुष्प|मेघपुष्पं|मेघपुष्पः
मेघपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 River water.<BR>3 Hail.<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>One of VIṢṆU'S horses.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघप्रसव|मेघप्रसवः
मेघप्रसव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and प्रसव a parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघभूति|मेघभूतिः
मेघभूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघमाला
मेघमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A gathering or succession of clouds.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and माला a necklace or garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघयोनि|मेघयोनिः
मेघयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and योनि place of birth or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघराग|मेघरागः
मेघराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>One of the six modes of music.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and राग mode; being supposed capable of bringing down rain from heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवर्णा|मेघवर्ण्णा
मेघवर्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवर्त्मन्
मेघवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>Sky, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and वर्त्मन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवह्नि|मेघवह्निः
मेघवह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>The fire of lightning, or electrical coruscations in the clouds.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवाहन|मेघवाहनः
मेघवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of INDRA.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघविस्फुर्ज्जित
मेघविस्फुर्ज्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Thunder.<BR>2 A species of the Atidhṛti metre.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ, and विस्फुर्ज्जित bursting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवेश्मन्
मेघवेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>Sky, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and वेश्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघसुहृद्
मेघसुहृद्<BR>m. (-हृद्)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and सुहृद् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघागम|मेघागमः
मेघागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The rains, the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघानन्दिन्|मेघानंदिन्
मेघानन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and आनन्दिन् delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघास्थि
मेघास्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघास्पद|मेघास्पदं
मेघास्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Heaven, ether, sky, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>मेघ a cloud, and आस्पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघोदर|मेघोदरः
मेघोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The father of the fifth Jina or Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचक|मेचकं|मेचकः
मेचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Black, dark, of a dark or black colour.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Black or dark-blue, (the colour.)<BR>2 The eye of a peacock's tail.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 Smoke.<BR>5 A plant, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sulphuret of antimony.<BR>E.<BR>मच to mix, Uṇādi aff. वुन्, and the vowel changed to ए.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचकापगा
मेचकापगा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>The Yamunā river.<BR>E.<BR>मेचक dark, and अपगा the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेट|मेटः
मेट<BR>(ऋ) मेदृ r. 1st cl. (मेटति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेटुला
मेटुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>मेट to be mad, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेठ|मेठः
मेठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 An elephant-keeper or feeder.<BR>2 A ram; also read मेण्ठ and मेण्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेडृ
मेडृ<BR>(ऋ) मेडृ r. 1st. cl. (मेडति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्र|मेढ्रः
मेढ्र<BR>m. (-ढ्रः)<BR>1 The penis.<BR>2 A ram.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to urine, ष्ट्रन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्रशृङ्गी
मेढ्रशृङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A milky plant, the fruit of which is crooked, and therefore compared to a ram's horn, (Asclepias geminata?)<BR>E.<BR>मेढ्र a ram, शृङ्ग a horn, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ठ|मेंठ|मेंठः|मेण्ठः
मेण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>An elephant-keeper; also read मेठ as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ड|मेंड|मेंडः|मेण्डः
मेण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>An elephant-keeper or feeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ढ|मेंढ|मेंढः|मेण्ढः
मेण्ढ<BR>m. (-ण्ढः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to urine, घञ् aff., नुम् inserted and the final changed; also with कन् added मेण्ढक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथ
मेथ<BR>(ऋ) मेथृ r. 1st cl. (मेथति-ते)<BR>1 To understand, to comprehend.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure.<BR>3 To associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथि|मेथिः
मेथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>The part of a threshing floor, round which the cattle turn to tread out the corn.<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>A sort of grass, (Trigonella foenugræcum.)<BR>E.<BR>मथ to understand, &c. इन् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्; also with कन् added in the fem. form मेथिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद|मेदः
मेद<BR>(ऋ) मेदृ r. 1st cl. (मेदति-ते)<BR>To understand, to kill or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद|मेदः
मेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Adeps, fat, the supposed proper seat of which is the abdomen.<BR>2 One of the outcast tribes.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A drug, described as a sort of root resembling ginger, brought from the Morung district; it is one of the eight principal medicaments, and is said to be of cooling and emollient properties, and of particular use in fever and consumption.<BR>E.<BR>मिद to be greasy or unctuous, aff. घञ्; also मेदस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदक|मेदकः
मेदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR>E.<BR>मिद to be unctuous, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्
मेदस्<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>1 Marrow; applicable not merely to the marrow of the bones, but more properly, to the serous or adipose secretion that spreads amongst the muscular fibres, and which is considered as performing the same functions to the flesh that the marrow of the bones performs to them: in Hindu physiology its proper seat is said to be the abdomen.<BR>2 Morbid or unnatural corpulency.<BR>E.<BR>मिद to be unctuous, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्कृत्
मेदस्कृत्<BR>n. (-स्कृत्)<BR>Flesh.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस् adeps, and कृत् made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्विन्
मेदस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>1 Robust, stout, strong.<BR>2 Fat, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनी
मेदिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस् adeps, इनि and ङीप् affs.; being made, according to the legend, of the adeps of two demons slain by BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनीद्रव|मेदिनीद्रवः
मेदिनीद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Dust.<BR>E.<BR>मेदिनी the earth, and द्रु to get, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुर|मेदुरः
मेदुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Smooth, soft, bland, unctuous, saponaceous, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मिद to be unctuous, घुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोग्रन्थि|मेदोग्रंथि|मेदोग्रन्थिः
मेदोग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>A fatty tumor.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and ग्रन्थि knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोज|मेदोजं
मेदोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A bone.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस् marrow, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोधरा
मेदोधरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A membrane in the abdomen, containing the fat, the omentum.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and धरा what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोर्व्वुद
मेदोऽर्व्वुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Fatty tumors unattended with pain.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and अर्व्वुद a tumor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोवह
मेदोवह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A vessel carrying fat, a lymphatic.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and वह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोवृद्धि|मेदोवृद्धिः
मेदोवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Corpulence.<BR>2 Enlargement of the scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>मेदस्, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध|मेधः
मेध<BR>(ऋ) मेधृ r. 1st cl. (मेधति-ते)<BR>1 To understand, to comprehend.<BR>2 To associate.<BR>3 To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=673" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध|मेधः
मेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Sacrifice, offering, oblation.<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Apprehension, conception, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>मेध to associate, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधाजित्
मेधाजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The name of a saint and grammarian; also KĀTYĀYANA.<BR>E.<BR>मेधा apprehension, and जित् victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधारुद्र|मेधारुद्रः
मेधारुद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The poet KĀLIDĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधाविन्
मेधाविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Intelligent, comprehending, of ready comprehension or conception.<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>1 A parrot.<BR>2 A Paṇḍita, a learned man, a sage, a teacher.<BR>3 The inspired writer Vyāḍi.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मेधा apprehension, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधि|मेधिः
मेधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A post fixed in the centre of a threshing-floor or barn, to which the cattle are attached, as they turn round it to tread out the corn.<BR>E.<BR>मेध to associate or connect, (the oxen, &c.) and इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधिर|मेधिरः
मेधिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Intelligent, possessing a ready and just apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>मेधा apprehension, किरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्य|मेध्यं|मेध्यः
मेध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 Pure, purified.<BR>2 Fit for a sacrifice or oblation.<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>A kind of orris root, described as the red sort.<BR>3 A sort of pigment; see रोचना.<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>1 Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>2 Barley.<BR>3 A goat.<BR>E.<BR>मेध to associate, aff. ण्यत्, or मेध a sacrifice, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनका
मेनका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>One of the courtezans of Svarga, and wife to Himālaya.<BR>E.<BR>मे to me, का any one, न not, (equal or comparable.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनकात्मजा
मेनकात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>DURGĀ or PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मेनका the wife of the personified Himālaya mountain, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनकाप्राणेश|मेनकाप्राणेशः
मेनकाप्राणेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The personified Himālaya mountain.<BR>E.<BR>मेनका the Apsaras so named, and प्राणेश husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेना
मेना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The wife of Himālaya; see मेनका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाजा
मेनाजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मेना for मेनका the mother of the goddess, and जा born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाद|मेनादः
मेनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 A goat.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>मे imitative cry, mew, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाधव|मेनाधवः
मेनाधव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Himālaya, the personified mountain, and father of DURGĀ, as PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मेना the wife of the mountain, and धव husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेन्धी|मेंधी
मेन्धी<BR>f. (-न्धी)<BR>A plant, from the leaves of which a reddish dye is prepared, with which the palms of the hands, tips of the fingers, soles of the feet, and finger nails are stained, (Lawsonia inermis); also मेन्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेप
मेप<BR>(ऋ) मेपृ r. 1st cl. (मेपते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेब
मेब<BR>(ऋ) मेबृ r. 1st cl. (मेबते)<BR>To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेय
मेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Measurable, what is to be measured.<BR>E.<BR>मा to measure, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरक|मेरकः
मेरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An Asura, and foe to VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरु|मेरुः
मेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The sacred mountain Meru, in the centre of the seven continents, compared to the cup or seed-vessel of the lotus, the leaves of which are formed by the different Dvīpas: its height is said by the Hindus to be 84,000 Yojanas, sixteen thousand of which are below the surface of the earth: the shape is variously described, as square, conical, columnar, spherical, or spiral; and the four faces of it are of various colours, or white towards the east, yellow to the south, back to the west, and red towards the north: the river Ganges falls from heaven on its summit, and flows thence to the surrounding worlds in four streams; the southern branch is the Ganges of India, the northern running into Tartary is the Bhadrasomā, the eastern is the Sītā, and the western the Cakṣu or Oxus: on the summit of Meru BRAHMĀ resides, attended and worshipped by the Ṛṣis, Gandharbas, &c.; the regents of the points of the compass occupy the corresponding faces of the mountain, the whole of which consists of gold and gems: considered in any but a fabulous light, mount Meru appears to mean the high land of Tārtary, immediately to the north of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>E.<BR>मि to scatter, (radiance,) Uṇādi aff. रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुक|मेरुकः
मेरुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fragrant resin, incense.<BR>E.<BR>मेरु mount Meru, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुयन्त्र
मेरुयन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>A spindle.<BR>E.<BR>मेरु, and यन्त्र implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेल|मेलः
मेल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>Meeting, union, assemblage; in the modern dialects, applied to a large concourse of people collected at stated periods for religious or commercial purposes, as at Haridvār, &c.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Ink.<BR>2 Antimony or any collyrium.<BR>E.<BR>मिल to mix, to meet, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट्, aff. मेलन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलक|मेलकः
मेलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Meeting, union, assemblage.<BR>E.<BR>मेल the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलन|मेलनं
मेलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Meeting, assembling.<BR>2 Encounter.<BR>3 Associating with.<BR>4 Mixing with.<BR>5 Adding to.<BR>E.<BR>मिल to mix, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलयत्
मेलयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Mixing, adding, or causing to be mixed with, or added to.<BR>E.<BR>मिल to mix, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलानन्द|मेलानंद|मेलानन्दः
मेलानन्द<BR>mf. (-न्दः-न्दा)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मेला ink, आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलान्धु|मेलान्धुः
मेलान्धु<BR>f. (-न्धुः)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मेला ink, अन्धु a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलाम्बु|मेलांबु|मेलाम्बुः
मेलाम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>मेला ink, अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेव
मेव<BR>(ऋ) मेवृ r. 1st cl. (मेवते)<BR>To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेष|मेषः
मेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A ram.<BR>2 The sign Aries.<BR>3 A kind of drug.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A sort of small cardamom, brought from Guzerat. (-षी) An ewe.<BR>E.<BR>मिष to contend with, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषविषाणिका
मेषविषाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see मेढ्रशुङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>मेष a ram, विषाण a horn, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषशृङ्ग|मेषशृङ्गः
मेषशृङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A kind of creeping plant, (Asclepias geminata, &c.); see मेढ्रशृङ्गी.<BR>E.<BR>मेष a ram, and शृङ्ग horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाक्षिकुसुम|मेषाक्षिकुसुमः
मेषाक्षिकुसुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A sort of Cassia, (C. tora.)<BR>E.<BR>मेष a ram, अक्षि the eye, and कुसुम a flower; which is compared to a sheep's eye; also analogous terms, as मेषलोचन, &c.; it is also read मेषाख्य and मेषाह्व, &c. as being named from the Meṣa or ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाण्ड|मेषांड|मेषाण्डः
मेषाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>मेष a ram, and अण्ड the testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषालु|मेषालुः
मेषालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A sort of shrub, commonly Ververa or Berbera, (Ocimum pilosum.)<BR>E.<BR>मेष a ram, and आलु esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषिका
मेषिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An ewe.<BR>E.<BR>मेषी an ewe, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेह|मेहः
मेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Urinary disease, especially inflammatory affection of the urethra, including gonorrhoea, &c.<BR>3 A ram.<BR>4 Urine, piss.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to pass as urine, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहत्
मेहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Urining, passing urine.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to urine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहन|मेहनं|मेहनः
मेहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Membrum virile.<BR>2 Urine, piss.<BR>3 Passing urine, pissing.<BR>E.<BR>मिह to urine, aff. ल्यट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=674" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहिन्
मेहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Urining.<BR>2 Suffering from urinary affections.<BR>E.<BR>मेह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र|मैत्रं|मैत्रः
मैत्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>Of or belonging to a friend, friendly, amicable.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 The anus.<BR>nf. (-त्रं-त्री)<BR>1 Friendship.<BR>2 A name of the seventeenth lunar asterism, (see the next.)<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a friend, or the sun, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रभ|मैत्रभं
मैत्रभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The seventeenth lunar asterism; also ANURĀDHA.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र the deity, presiding over the asterism, अण् aff. of relation, मैत्र belonging to Mitra, and भ an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुण|मैत्रावरुणः
मैत्रावरुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र the sun, and वरुण the deity of water, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुणि|मैत्रावरुणिः
मैत्रावरुणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>मित्रवरुण a sage, the father of this saint, and इञ् aff.; or मित्र the sun, and वरुण VARUṆA, alluding to a legend of the birth of the saint from a contest between these deities, for the possession of URVAŚĪ one of the courtezans of INDRA'S heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रीवल
मैत्रीवल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेय|मैत्रेयः
मैत्रेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Of or relating to a friend.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A man of a mixed caste, the son of a Vaideha by an Ayogava mother: his business is to announce the hours in verse.<BR>2 The seventh Buddha, or one still to come.<BR>3 The name of a saint or Muni, the disciple of PARĀŚARA, to whom the Viṣṇu Purāṇa is narrated.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र a proper name, or मित्र a friend, and ढक् aff. of descent or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयक|मैत्रेयकः
मैत्रेयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crier or chaunter of the hours: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>मैत्रेय, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयिका
मैत्रेयिका<BR>f. (-कां)<BR>The contest of friends or allies.<BR>E.<BR>मैत्रेय relating to friends, वुञ् aff. of animosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र्य|मैत्र्यं
मैत्र्य<BR>nf. (-त्र्यं-त्री)<BR>Friendship.<BR>E.<BR>मित्र friend, ष्यञ् aff. of property, fem. aff. ङीष्, and the semivowel of the aff. rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिल|मैथिलः
मैथिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Belonging to, born in, &c. Mithila.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>मिथिला, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन|मैथुनं
मैथुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Copulation.<BR>2 Union, association.<BR>3 Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>मिथुन a couple, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाक|मैनाकः
मैनाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountain, or rock in the sea between the southern end of the Peninsula and Laṅkā.<BR>E.<BR>मेनका the wife of Himāla, and अण् aff. of descent, being in mythology her son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाकस्वसृ
मैनाकस्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ as PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>मैनाक as above, and स्वसृ sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनिक|मैनिकः
मैनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>मीन a fish, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्द|मैंद|मैंदः|मैन्दः
मैन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The name of a demon killed by VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्दहन्|मैंदहन्
मैन्दहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>मैन्द as above, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरेय|मैरेयं|मैरेयः
मैरेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A sort of spirituous liquor, from the blossoms of the Lythrum fruticosum, with sugar, &c.<BR>E.<BR>मिरा said to be the name of a country or drug, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तव्य
मोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be loosed or let go, to be liberated.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let go, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष|मोक्षः
मोक्ष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (मोक्षति मोक्षयति)<BR>To let go, to release, to discharge, to send, to cast or throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष|मोक्षः
मोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 Final and eternal happiness, the liberation of the soul from the body, and its exemption from further transmigration.<BR>2 Death.<BR>3 Liberation, freedom.<BR>4 A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>5 Acquittance of an obligation, as by a son to his father.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष to let loose or free, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षक|मोक्षकः
मोक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what sets at liberty.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A deliverer, a liberator.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षण|मोक्षणं
मोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Letting go or free, liberating.<BR>2 Squandering.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष to let go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षणीय
मोक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be, or what may be liberated.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष, and अनीयर् aff.; also मोक्ष्य and मोक्षितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षित
मोक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Let go, liberated, at large.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षोपाय|मोक्षोपायः
मोक्षोपाय<BR>mfn. (-यः)<BR>A sage, a saint, a devotee.<BR>E.<BR>मोक्ष emancipation, उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघ|मोघं|मोघः
मोघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>1 Vain, useless, fruitless.<BR>2 Left, abandoned.<BR>f. (-घः)<BR>Trumpet-flower, (Bignonia suave olens.)<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A fence, a hedge.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, aff. अच्, and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघकर्म्मन्|मोघकर्मन्
मोघकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Following vain practices, observing useless-ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>मोघ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघज्ञान
मोघज्ञान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Cultivating vain knowledge or any but religious wisdom.<BR>E.<BR>मोघ, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघाश
मोघाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Indulging vain hopes.<BR>E.<BR>मोघ, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघोली
मोघोली<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A fence, a hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच|मोचं|मोचः
मोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>1 The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>2 The plantain, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>A plantain, (the fruit.)<BR>E.<BR>मुच to let loose, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचक|मोचकः
मोचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>2 The silk cotton tree.<BR>3 The plantain tree.<BR>4 A plant, commonly Ghaṇṭāpārali.<BR>5 A devotee, one who has divested himself of worldly passion and desire.<BR>6 A liberator.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to be let loose, aff. वुन्, or causal form, aff. अच्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचन|मोचनं
मोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Liberating, setting free.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to be free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचनीय
मोचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be liberated or let loose.<BR>2 To be resigned or given up.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to be loose, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचरस|मोचरसः
मोचरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>मोच the Bombax, and रस juice; also similar compounds, as माचनिर्य्यास, मोचसार, मोचस्राव, मोचस्रुत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचाट|मोचाटः
मोचाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A kind of pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>2 Sandal.<BR>3 The heart of the plantain tree.<BR>4 A plantain, (the fruit.)<BR>E.<BR>मोच a plantain, &c., अट to go, (to be used with, to resemble, &c.) aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचिनी
मोचिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A prickly nightshade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच्य
मोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 To be let loose.<BR>2 To be given up.<BR>E.<BR>मुच to be free, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटकी
मोटकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटन|मोटनं|मोटनः
मोटन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rubbing, grinding, pressing.<BR>E.<BR>मुट to rub, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटनक|मोटनकं
मोटनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>2 A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोट्टायित|मोट्टायितं
मोट्टायित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the ten Bhāvas, or properties of women, the silent expression of returned affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोण|मोणः
मोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Dried fruit.<BR>2 A sort of water-fly, (the crocodile fly?)<BR>3 A basket for carrying snakes in.<BR>E.<BR>मुण to vow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोद|मोदः
मोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Joy, delight, happiness.<BR>2 Fragrance.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to rejoice, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=675" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदक|मोदकः
मोदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Delighting, rejoicing, causing happiness or delight.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A sort of sweetmeat.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to be glad, in the causal form, to make glad, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयत्
मोदयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Delighting, pleasing.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine.<BR>2 A wild sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>E.<BR>मुद to be pleased, causal form, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदित|मोदितः
मोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pleased, delighted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>E.<BR>मुद to rejoice, aff. क्त, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरट|मोरटं|मोरटः
मोरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Root of sugar cane.<BR>2 The blossom of the Alangium hexapetalum.<BR>3 Milk of seven days standing, or when it has lost its milky nature.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A sort of creeper, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>मुर to surround, aff. अटन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषक|मोषकः
मोषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषण|मोषणं
मोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Stealing.<BR>E.<BR>मुष, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषयित्नु|मोषयित्नुः
मोषयित्नु<BR>m. (-त्नुः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषा
मोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Stealing, theft.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to steal, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष्टृ
मोष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>मुष to rob, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोह|मोहं|मोहः
मोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Fainting, loss of consciousness or sense.<BR>2 Ignorance, folly, foolishness; it is applied especially to that spiritual ignorance which leads men to believe in the reality of worldly objects, and to addict themselves to mundane or sensual enjoyment.<BR>3 Pain, affliction.<BR>4 Error, mistake.<BR>5 Bewilderment, distraction.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be ignorant or foolish, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहन|मोहनं|मोहनः
मोहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>Fascinating, stupefying, depriving of sense or understanding.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Copulation.<BR>2 One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA.<BR>3 Temptation, seduction, the overpowering of reason and reflection by worldly or sensual allurements.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The thorn-apple, (Datura.)<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>2 A kind of jasmine, commonly the Tripura or Tipperah jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, (causal form,) aff. युच् or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहित
मोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Puzzled, perplexed.<BR>2 Beguiled, deceived.<BR>E.<BR>मुह to be foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिन्
मोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Illusive, fallacious, beguiling.<BR>E.<BR>मोह, and इनि aff.; or मुह to be foolish, causal v., घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिनी
मोहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A kind of jasmine, commonly Tripuramāli.<BR>E.<BR>मोह folly, इनि aff., and ङीष् fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकुलि|मौकुलिः
मौकुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A crow; some books have मौकलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिक|मौक्तिकं
मौक्तिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>मुक्ता a pearl, ठक् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकप्रसवा
मौक्तिकप्रसवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>The pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>मौक्तिक, and प्रसवा a mother; mother of pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकशुक्ति|मौक्तिकशुक्तिः
मौक्तिकशुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>A pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>मौक्तिक a pearl, and शुक्ति an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्य|मौक्यं
मौक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Dumbness.<BR>E.<BR>सूक, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर्य्य|मौखर्य|मौखर्यं|मौखर्य्यं
मौखर्य्य<BR>nf. (-र्य्यं-री)<BR>Scurrility, defamation.<BR>E.<BR>मुखर foul-mouthed, ष्यञ् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख्य|मौख्यं
मौख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Pre-eminence.<BR>E.<BR>मुख chief, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौग्ध
मौग्ध<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>1 Simplicity, silliness.<BR>2 Ignorance.<BR>3 A feminine property: asking a lover to tell what is already known.<BR>E.<BR>मुग्ध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जी|मौंजी
मौञ्जी<BR>f. (-ञ्जी)<BR>The girdle of a Brahman made of three strings of Munja grass.<BR>E.<BR>मुञ्जा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जीबन्धन|मौंजीबंधन
मौञ्जीबन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Investiture with the distinguishing cord.<BR>E.<BR>मौञ्जी the girdle, and बन्धन binding; both being assumed at the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौढ्य|मौढ्यं
मौढ्य<BR>n. (-ढ्यं)<BR>Ignorance, folly, especially spiritual folly: see मोह.<BR>E.<BR>मूढ a fool, ष्यञ् aff. of property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्ड्य|मौंड्यं
मौण्ड्य<BR>n. (-ण्ड्यं)<BR>Baldness, natural or artificial.<BR>E.<BR>मुण्ड, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलि|मौद्गलिः
मौद्गलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गीन|मौद्गीनं
मौद्गीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fit for, or bearing, &c. (kidney-beans.)<BR>E.<BR>मुद्ग kidney-bean, and खञ् aff.; also with अण्, aff. मौद्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौन|मौनं
मौन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Silence, taciturnity.<BR>E.<BR>मुनि a sage, (who practices it,) and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिन्
मौनिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>Silent, taciturn.<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>An ascetic, a hermit, a religious sage, one who has overcome his passions and retired from the world<BR>E.<BR>मीन silence, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरजिक|मौरजिकः
मौरजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A player on a drum.<BR>E.<BR>मुरज a drum, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्ख्य|मौर्ख्यं
मौर्ख्य<BR>n. (-र्ख्यं)<BR>Stupidity, folly, fatuity.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्ख a fool, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व्वी|मौर्वी
मौर्व्वी<BR>f. (-र्व्वी)<BR>A bow-string.<BR>E.<BR>सूर्व्वा the plant, from the fibres of which bow-strings were made, अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल|मौलः
मौल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Radical, proceeding from a root or origin.<BR>2 Of pure blood, descended from a respectable and primitive family without any improper intermixture.<BR>E.<BR>मूल a root, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली or -ली)<BR>1 A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>2 Hair ornamented and braided round the head.<BR>3 A diadem, a Tiara.<BR>4 The head.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>मूल the root or base, aff. इञ् or मूल a name, and इञ् aff. of descent, or मू to bind, लि aff., and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टा
मौष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Boxing, sparring, playing at fistycuffs.<BR>E.<BR>मुष्टि the fist, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्त्त|मौहूर्त|मौहूर्तः|मौहूर्त्तः
मौहूर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>मुहूर्त्त an hour, and अण् aff.; also with ठक् aff. मौहूर्त्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्ना
म्ना<BR>r. 1st cl. (मनति)<BR>To fix in the memory by frequent practice or repetition, to study, to acquire by study, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष|म्रक्षः
म्रक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (म्रक्षति)<BR>1 To accumulate.<BR>2 To smear, to anoint.<BR>10th cl. (म्रक्षयति)<BR>1 To mix.<BR>2 To speak incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष|म्रक्षः
म्रक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Slyness, hypocrisy, concealment of one's vices or defects.<BR>E.<BR>म्रक्ष to anoint, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षण|म्रक्षणं
म्रक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Oil.<BR>2 Smearing the body with fragrant oils or unguents.<BR>E.<BR>म्रक्ष to smear or anoint, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रच
म्रच<BR>r. 1st cl. (म्रचति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद
म्रद<BR>r. 1st cl. (म्रदते)<BR>1 To grind, to pound, to reduce to powder or dust.<BR>2 To tread or trample on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमन्
म्रदिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Softness.<BR>E.<BR>मृद् soft, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमान्वित
म्रदिमान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Soft.<BR>2 Kind.<BR>E.<BR>म्रदिमन्, and अन्वित endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिष्ठ|म्रदिष्ठः
म्रदिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very soft, exceedingly soft, softest.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative, ऋ changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदीयस्
म्रदीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Softer, milder.<BR>E.<BR>मृदु soft, and इयसुन् aff. of the comparative, and the vowel changed to the semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रियमाण
म्रियमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Dying.<BR>E.<BR>मृ to die, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुच
म्रुच<BR>(उ) म्रुचु r. 1st cl. (म्रोचति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुंच
म्रुंच<BR>(उ) म्रुञ्च r. 1st cl. (म्रुञ्चति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=676" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेट
म्रेट<BR>(ऋ) म्रेदृ r. 1st cl. (म्रेटति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेड
म्रेड<BR>(ऋ) मेडृ r. 1st cl. (म्रेडति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष
म्लक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (म्लक्षयति)<BR>1 To mix, to unite.<BR>2 To speak incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लान|म्लानं
म्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Foul, dirty.<BR>2 Languid, weary.<BR>3 Faded, withered.<BR>E.<BR>म्लै to be languid, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानि|म्लानिः
म्लानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Weariness, languor.<BR>2 Foulness, filth.<BR>3 Fading, decay.<BR>E.<BR>म्लै to be languid, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Indistinct, (as speech.)<BR>2 Languid.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Indistinct speech.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ to speak indistinctly, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुक्त
म्लुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Mixed, intermixed, inlaid, set.<BR>E.<BR>म्लुच to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच
म्लुच<BR>(उ) म्लुचु r. 1st cl. (म्लोचति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>With अभि and नि prefixed,<BR>To go down, to set as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च
म्लुञ्च<BR>(उ) म्लुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (म्लुञ्चति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेछ|म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः
म्लेछ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (म्लेछति म्लेछयति)<BR>1 To speak inarticulately or incorrectly, to use a provincial or barbarous dialect.<BR>2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 The generic term for a barbarian or foreigner; that is, for one speaking any language but Sanskrit, and not subject to the usual Hindu institutions.<BR>2 A sinner, a criminal.<BR>3 Indistinct or barbarous speech.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ to speak inarticulately, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छकन्द|म्लेच्छकंद|म्लेच्छकन्दः
म्लेच्छकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Garlic.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छजाति|म्लेच्छजातिः
म्लेच्छजाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A Mleccha or barbarian, or a man of an outcast race. The tribes enumerated under this head by MANU, but who are by him said to be properly, degraded Kṣatriyas, appear to be chiefly the inhabitants of the countries bordering immediately upon India, both to the north and south: as far as modern research and similarity of appellation may be trusted, the tribes of Mlecchas are as follows: the Pauṇḍrakas, (the people of provinces bordering on Bengal and Behar, and to the south of the Ganges,) Oḍras, (Urīyas,) Drāviras, (people of the southern part of the Coromandel coast,) Cāmbojas, (Arachosians,) Yavanas, (Greeks or Bactrians,) Śakas, (the people of the Sacha region or Sakai,) Pāravas, (Paropamisans,) Pahlavas, (the ancient Persians,) Cīnas, (Chinese,) Kirātas, (generally mountaineers, here perhaps especially the inhabitants of the Himāla or Imaus,) Daradas, (Daradoe,) and Khasas, (Scūthi or Chasas.)<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and जाति tribe, class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छदेश|म्लेच्छदेशः
म्लेच्छदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The countries bordering on India, or those inhabited by people of a different faith and language; defined to be any, where the black antelope is not found.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, an outcast, and देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजन|म्लेच्छभोजनं|म्लेच्छभोजनः
म्लेच्छभोजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Half ripe barley.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ an outcaste, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमण्डल|म्लेच्छमंडल|म्लेच्छमण्डलं
म्लेच्छमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The country of the Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ, and मण्डल region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमुख|म्लेच्छमुखं
म्लेच्छमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and मुख countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छवाच्
म्लेच्छवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Speaking a barbarous dialect.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छाश|म्लेच्छाशः
म्लेच्छाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, अश to eat, aff. अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छास्य|म्लेच्छास्यं
म्लेच्छास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and आस्य face, which would seem to allude to the fair complexion of the Greek or Mohammedan invaders of Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छित|म्लेच्छितं
म्लेच्छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken incorrectly or barbarously.<BR>m. (-तं)<BR>1 Foreign or barbarous language.<BR>2 Ungrammatical speech.<BR>E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, इतच् aff., or म्लेच्छ to speak inaccurately, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेट
म्लेट<BR>(ऋ) म्लेदृ r. 1st cl. (म्लेटति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेड
म्लेड<BR>(ऋ) म्लेडृ r. 1st cl. (म्लेडति)<BR>To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेव
म्लेव<BR>(ऋ) म्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (म्लेवते)<BR>To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लै
म्लै<BR>r. 1st cl. (म्लायति म्लपयति)<BR>1 To be faint or languid, to yawn with languor or fatigue.<BR>2 To fade, to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य<BR>The twenty-sixth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, or semivowel Y; in Bengal, it is usually pronounced J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who goes, a goer, a mover.<BR>m. (यः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 Union, joining.<BR>3 Fame, celebrity.<BR>4 Barley.<BR>5 Light, lustre.<BR>6 Abandoning.<BR>7 YAMA.<BR>f. (या)<BR>1 Pudendum muliebre.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 A car, a carriage.<BR>4 Prohibiting, restraining, checking.<BR>5 Religious meditation.<BR>6 Getting, obtaining.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, यम to check, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक|यकः
यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Which, (of many.)<BR>E.<BR>यट् which, and अकच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The liver.<BR>E.<BR>य union, (of the parts of the body,) कृ to make, aff. क्विप् and तुक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदात्मिका
यकृदात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR>E.<BR>यकृत् the liver, and आत्मन self, कन् aff., fem. form; like it in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृद्वैरी
यकृद्वैरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A plant, a sort of tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>E.<BR>यकृत् liver, and वैर inimical to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (यक्षयते)<BR>To worship, to honour or adore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A demigod, attendant especially on KUVERA, and employed in the care of his gardens and treasures.<BR>2 A name of KUVERA.<BR>3 The residence of INDRA.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>The wife of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष to worship, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षकर्द्दम|यक्षकर्दम|यक्षकर्दमः|यक्षकर्द्दमः
यक्षकर्द्दम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Perfumed paste, used especially for anointing the body, and consisting of camphor, agallochum, musk and Kakkola; or the three first, with saffron and Sandal in equal proportions.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष the demigod, and कर्द्दम clay; a perfume of which these beings are supposed to be fond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षधूप|यक्षधूपः
यक्षधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Resin in general.<BR>2 Turpentine, the resinous exudation of the pine.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष the demigod, and धूप perfume or incense, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरस|यक्षरसः
यक्षरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष the demigod, and रस taste, fondness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज्
यक्षराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>KUVERA, the deity of wealth, and lord of the demigods called Yakṣas.<BR>2 A palæstrum, a place prepared for wrestling or boxing.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष a Yakṣa, and राज् who rules or shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज|यक्षराजः
यक्षराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>KUVERA: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष the demigod, so called, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=677" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराट्पुरी
यक्षराट्पुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Alakā the capital of KUVERA, supposed to be seated on mount Kailāsa.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष्राज KUVERA, and पुरी city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरात्रि|यक्षरात्रिः
यक्षरात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः)<BR>The night of the day of full moon in the month Kārttika: see दीपाली.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष the demigod, and रात्रि night; these spirits being supposed to be then abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षामलक|यक्षामलकं
यक्षामलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, described as a sort of date.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष a Yakṣa, and आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षावास|यक्षावासः
यक्षावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष demigod, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिणी
यक्षिणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 The wife of KUVERA.<BR>2 The wife of a Yakṣa.<BR>3 A sort of female fiend, attached to the service of DURGĀ, and frequently maintaining, like a sylph or fairy, an intercourse with mortals.<BR>E.<BR>यक्षिन् a name of KUVERA, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षेन्द्र|यक्षेन्द्रः
यक्षेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A name of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष, and इन्द्र lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षेश
यक्षेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष, and ईश lord; also यक्षेश्वर and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षोडुम्बरक|यक्षोडुम्बरकं
यक्षोडुम्बरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The fruit of the Ficus religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मघ्नी
यक्ष्मघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>The raisin, or dried grape.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष्म consumption, and घ्न destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मन्
यक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Pulmonary consumption.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष to worship, and मनिन् Uṇādi aff.; also with मन् aff. यक्ष्म m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्यमाण
यक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Proposing or wishing to worship.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष to worship, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्न्त
यङ्न्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>(In grammar,) The frequentative deponent verb.<BR>E.<BR>यङ्, and अन्त termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्लुगन्त
यङ्लुगन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The frequentative active verb.<BR>E.<BR>यङ्, लुक् dropped, and अन्त termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज|यजः
यज<BR>r. 1st cl. (यजति)<BR>1 To worship a deity.<BR>2 To associate with.<BR>3 To present or endow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्
यजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>Sacrificing, worshipping.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत|यजतः
यजत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A Brahman who has maintained his consecrated fire.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, अत्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन|यजनं
यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Offering sacrifices, performing worship.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन्त|यजन्तः
यजन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A sacrificer, a worshipper.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, aff. झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमान|यजमानः
यजमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Worshipping.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An employer of priests at a sacrifice, the person who institutes its performance, and pays the expence of it.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, शानच् aff. of the present participle, with मक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजाक|यजाकः
यजाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A donor, a benefactor, a liberal giver of presents, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यज to present, Uṇādi aff. आकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजि|यजिः
यजि<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>A sacrificer, one who institutes or performs a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुर्वेद|यजुर्वेदः|यजुर्व्वेदः
यजुर्वेद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The Yajur Veda: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>ययुस्, and वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस्<BR>n. (-जुः)<BR>The Yajur or Yajuṣ, one of the four Vedas; it is divided into two principal portions, the white and black, or Vājasaneyi and Taittirīya, the former of which is attributed to the saint YĀJÑAVALKYA, to whom it was revealed by the sun, in the form of a horse; and the latter to TITTIRI, to whom it was communicated by YĀSKA, the first pupil of its original author, the sage VAIŚAMPĀYANA: according to the Purāṇas, the Taittirīya portion was named from Tittiri a partridge; the disciples of VAIŚAMPĀYANA being changed into those birds, to pick up the texts of the Veda, as they were disgorged in a tangible shape by YĀJÑAVALKYA, at the command of VAIŚAMPĀYANA: both portions of this Veda are very full on the subject of religious rites, and the prayers peculiar to it, are chiefly in measured and poetical prose.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, Uṇādi aff. उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञ|यज्ञः
यज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A sacrifice, a ceremony in which oblations are presented.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, aff. नङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकर्म्मन्|यज्ञकर्मन्
यज्ञकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Any sacrificial act or ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकृत्
यज्ञकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A sacrificer, a worshipper, or priest conducting a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञद्रुह्
यज्ञद्रुह्<BR>m. (-ध्रुक्)<BR>A Rākṣasa, an imp.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and द्रुह् to wrong, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपशु|यज्ञपशुः
यज्ञपशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 Any animal offered in sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ a sacrifice, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपात्र
यज्ञपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A sacrificial vessel.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपुरुष|यज्ञपुरुषः
यज्ञपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and पुरुष man or male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभाजन|यज्ञभाजनं
यज्ञभाजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sacrificial vessel.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and भाजन vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभूमि|यज्ञभूमिः
यज्ञभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Place prepared for a sacrifice, or where it is offered.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवराह|यज्ञवराहः
यज्ञवराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>VIṢṆU in the boar incarnation.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and वराह the boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवाट|यज्ञवाटः
यज्ञवाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A place prepared and enclosed for a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ a sacrifice, and वाट inclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशिष्ट
यज्ञशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>What is left from a sacrifice or oblation.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and शिष्ट remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशेष|यज्ञशेषः
यज्ञशेष<BR>n. (-षः)<BR>The reliques of a sacrifice or oblation.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसार|यज्ञसारः
यज्ञसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसिद्धि|यज्ञसिद्धिः
यज्ञसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Performance of sacrifice.<BR>2 Obtaining the objects of a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसूत्र|यज्ञसूत्रं
यज्ञसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The characteristic thread, worn by the three principal classes of Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञस्थान|यज्ञस्थानं
यज्ञस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A place of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाङ्ग|यज्ञांग|यज्ञाङ्गः
यज्ञाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The glomerous fig, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>2 A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>3 A part of any sacrificial ceremony.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ a sacrifice, and अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञान्त|यज्ञान्तः
यज्ञान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A supplementary sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ the principal, and अन्त end, finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञारि|यज्ञारिः
यज्ञारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A demon, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ a sacrifice, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिक|यज्ञिकः
यज्ञिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Pālaś tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Proper for or suitable to a sacrifice.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The third Yug or age.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=678" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियदेश|यज्ञियदेशः
यज्ञियदेश<BR>f. (-शः)<BR>The country of the Hindus; those districts in which the ritual and institutes of the Hindu system are enforced; properly the country in which the black deer or antelope is native.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञिय sacrificial, and देश a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियशाला
यज्ञियशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A temple, a shrine, a place of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञिय to be sacrificed, (where,) and शाला hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोडुम्बर|यज्ञोडुम्बरः
यज्ञोडुम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The glomerous fig tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and उडुम्बर the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीत|यज्ञोपवीतं
यज्ञोपवीत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The sacrificial cord, originally worn by the three principal casts of Hindus: at present from the loss of the pure Kṣatriya and Vaiśya casts in Bengal, confined to the Brahmanical order.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and उपवीत thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीतिन्
यज्ञोपवीतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A Brahman, &c. invested with the sacred thread.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञोपवीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्यु|यज्युः
यज्यु<BR>m. (-ज्युः)<BR>A Brahman, Conversant with the Yajur Veda.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, Uṇādi aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वन्
यज्वन्<BR>m. (-ज्वा)<BR>A sacrificer in due form, or agreeably to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वनांपति
यज्वनांपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>यज्वन् a sacrificer in the sixth case plural, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत|यतः
यत<BR>(ई) यती r. 1st cl. (यतते)<BR>1 To resolve or determine in consequence of a wish or desire, to apply or endeavour<BR>2 strenuously, to energize, to persevere.<BR>r. 10th cl. (यातयति)<BR>1 To distress or afflict.<BR>2 To beat.<BR>3 To order.<BR>4 To collect, to assemble.<BR>5 To work, to make or manufacture.<BR>6 To prevent, to remove.<BR>7 To return, to give back, to requite.<BR>8 To barter or exchange.<BR>9 To purify.<BR>With निर् or नि prefixed,<BR>To chastise, to punish, to inflict pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत्<BR>ind.<BR>Because, as, since, wherefore, correlative of तत् thence, therefore, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यम to check, to restrain, क्विप् and तुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत|यतः
यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Governed, controlled.<BR>2 Limited, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>यम to check, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतचित्त
यतचित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Resigned, subdued, one of well-governed thoughts or feelings.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and चित्त the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतचित्तात्मन्
यतचित्तात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Having power over the soul and spirit, of subdued mind.<BR>E.<BR>यतचित्त, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतत्
यतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>Striving, making effort.<BR>E.<BR>यत to make effort, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतन|यतनं
यतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Making effort or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>यत to make effort, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतनीय
यतनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be exerted or persevered, to be made as an effort.<BR>E.<BR>यत to make effort अनीयर्, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतम|यतमः
यतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Which, (of many.)<BR>E.<BR>यद् which, डतमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमान
यतमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Making effort, striving, struggling, persevering.<BR>E.<BR>यत to strive, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमैथुन
यतमैथुन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Disinclined to sexual intercourse, abstaining from it.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and मैथुन coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतर|यतरः
यतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Which, (of two,) whether.<BR>E.<BR>यट् which, डतरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतव्रत
यतव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Firm to an engagement or vow.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतस्
यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Because, as since, whence: see यत्.<BR>E.<BR>यद् which, what, and तसि substituted for the termination of the 5th case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतात्मन्
यतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Of subdued or well-governed spirit.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतात्मवत्|यतात्मवन्त्
यतात्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Self-subdued, having the mind and all its powers in subjection.<BR>E.<BR>यतात्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यताहार
यताहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Temperate, abstemious.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
यति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A sage, whose passions are completely under subjection.<BR>2 A religious mendicant, especially one of the Jaina sect.<BR>3 Stopping, ceasing, rest, term.<BR>4 Restraining, controlling^1, checking.<BR>f. (-तीः)<BR>1 A pause in poetry or metre, a stop, a rest.<BR>2 Union, joining.<BR>3 Passion, sentiment.<BR>4 A widow.<BR>E.<BR>यत to endeavour, &c., aff. इन्, or यम् to restrain, aff. क्तिन्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिन्
यतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A sage with subdued passions.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A widow.<BR>E.<BR>यत restraining, from यम with क्त aff., and इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिपात्र
यतिपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel for collecting alms, made of wood, or a hollow bambu, an earthen bowl, or a gourd.<BR>E.<BR>यति, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिमैथुन|यतिमैथुनं
यतिमैथुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The copulation or cohabitation of holy personages.<BR>E.<BR>यति as above, and मैथुन coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतुका
यतुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, Cakāvat commonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतेन्द्रिय|यतेंद्रिय
यतेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Chaste, pure, of subdued passions.<BR>E.<BR>यत, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्कर
यत्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Doing what.<BR>E.<BR>यत्, and कृ to do, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्त
यत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Striven, resolved, exerted.<BR>E.<BR>यत to resolve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्न|यत्नः
यत्न<BR>m. (-त्नः)<BR>Effort, exertion, perseverance, energy.<BR>E.<BR>यत to endeavour strenuously or continuously, aff. नङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्नतस्
यत्नतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Vigorously, strenuously.<BR>E.<BR>यत्न, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्नवत्|यत्नवन्त्
यत्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Persevering, diligent, making effort or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>यत्न effort, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्य
यत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>To be exerted or made as an effort.<BR>E.<BR>यत to exert, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र
यत्र<BR>ind.<BR>Where, in what place.<BR>E.<BR>यद what, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र
यत्र<BR>(इ) यत्रि r. 1st and 10th cls. (यन्त्रति यन्त्रयति)<BR>To confine, to restrain, to subdue or regulate: the root may also be written यन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथा
यथा<BR>ind.<BR>As, according to; correlative to तथा so: it is also commonly used in composition to form adverbs: यथाकालं seasonably, यथाक्रमं regularly, यथान्यायं fitly, suitably, यथाशास्त्रं according to scripture, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यद् what, थाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथांशतस्
यथांशतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Proportionably, in due proportion.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, according to, अंश part, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकथा
यथाकथा<BR>ind.<BR>As much as, tantum quantum: it is especially used as a term of disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and कथा how.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकथाच
यथाकथाच<BR>ind.<BR>Rarely, unfrequently, seldomer than proper.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as much, and कथा how much, with च the particle, and.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकर्त्तव्य|यथाकर्तव्य
यथाकर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>What is right or proper to be done.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकल्प
यथाकल्प<BR>adv. (-ल्पं)<BR>As designed.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and कल्प making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकाम
यथाकाम<BR>adv. (-मं)<BR>At pleasure, as you please.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=679" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकामिन्
यथाकामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Wilful, independant, uncontrolled, following one's own inclinations.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, according to, काम desire, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाक्रम|यथाक्रमं
यथाक्रम<BR>adv. n. (-मं)<BR>In order, orderly, successively, methodically.<BR>E.<BR>यथा agreeably to, क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथागत
यथागत<BR>adv. n. (-तं)<BR>Applied to a person's being sent away or returning as he came.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाजात|यथाजातः
यथाजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Foolish, stupid, a fool, a natural.<BR>2 Barbarous, outcast.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and जात born, as simple as at birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथातथ|यथातथं
यथातथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Right, true.<BR>ind. or adv. n. (-थं)<BR>Properly, suitably.<BR>noun. (-थं)<BR>Narrative of events, history.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and तथा so, with the termination of the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथातथा
यथातथा<BR>adv.<BR>In any way, any how.<BR>E.<BR>यथा and तथा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथापूर्व्व|यथापूर्व|यथापूर्व्वं
यथापूर्व्व<BR>n. adv. (-र्व्वं)<BR>1 In order or succession.<BR>2 Formerly, precedingly, in prior time or place.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and पूर्व्व formerly, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाभिमतम्
यथाभिमतम्<BR>ind.<BR>According to one's wish or purpose.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and अभिमत purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथामुखीन|यथामुखीनः
यथामुखीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Like, resembling, shewing similarly or reflecting.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, मुख the countenance, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथायथम्
यथायथम्<BR>ind.<BR>As, thereto appertaining.<BR>E.<BR>यथा repeated, with the termination of the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थ|यथार्थं
यथार्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Right, proper.<BR>2 According to the sense.<BR>adv. or ind.n. (-र्थं)<BR>Properly, suitably.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, अर्थ property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थता
यथार्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rectitude, propriety, fitness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, यथार्थत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्ह|यथार्हं
यथार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Proper, suitable, appropriate.<BR>n. adv. or ind. (-र्हं)<BR>Properly, suitably.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, अर्हम् properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हतस्
यथार्हतस्<BR>adv.<BR>Properly, fitly.<BR>E.<BR>यथार्ह, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हवर्ण|यथार्हवर्णः
यथार्हवर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A spy, a secret emissary.<BR>E.<BR>यथार्ह properly, suitably, वर्ण form, colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावकाश
यथावकाश<BR>adv. n. or ind. (-शं)<BR>According to opportunity.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and अवकाश season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावत्
यथावत्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Truly, exactly, as it was, according to law or usage.<BR>2 Accordingly, conformably.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावसर
यथावसर<BR>adv. n. or ind. (-रं)<BR>According to opportunity.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and अवसर opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाविधि
यथाविधि<BR>ind. or n. adv.<BR>According to rule.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and विधि precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावृत्त
यथावृत्त<BR>adv. (-त्तं)<BR>Circumstantially, relating a thing as it happened.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and वृत्त being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशक्ति
यथाशक्ति<BR>adv. n. (-क्ति)<BR>Extent of capability, as much as possible.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as much as, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशास्त्र|यथाशास्त्रं
यथाशास्त्र<BR>adv. n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>According to the Śāstras, agreeably to scripture.<BR>E.<BR>यथा agreeably to, शास्त्र the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथासुख
यथासुख<BR>adv. (-खं)<BR>Happily.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्थित|यथास्थितं
यथास्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Right, proper, fit, true.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Circumstantially, or all that happened or existed.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and स्थित fixed, established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्वम्
यथास्वम्<BR>ind.<BR>As, according, or appertaining to, properly, peculiarly.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, and स्व own, peculiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेप्सित|यथेप्सितं
यथेप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>adv. n. or ind.(-तं)<BR>1 Willingly, voluntarily.<BR>2 Wilfully, independantly.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, इप्सित (participle past, desiderative form of आप to obtain), desired, wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेष्ट|यथेष्टं
यथेष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>adv. n. or ind. (-ष्टं)<BR>According to will or inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेष्टचारिन्
यथेष्टचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, इष्ट wished, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथोचित|यथोचितं
यथोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Right, proper.<BR>adv. n. or ind. (-तं)<BR>Properly, suitably.<BR>E.<BR>यथा, and उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथोदित|यथोदितं
यथोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>As said or explained.<BR>E.<BR>यथा as, उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्
यद्<BR>mfn. relative pronoun (-यः-या-यत्)<BR>Who, which, what.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, Uṇādi aff. अदि, with the power of डित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदा
यदा<BR>ind.<BR>When, at what time.<BR>E.<BR>यट् what, दाच् aff., and the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदि
यदि<BR>ind.<BR>If; particle of suspicion or doubt.<BR>E.<BR>यत to make effort, इञ् aff., and the radical final changed to द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदु|यदुः
यदु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 The name of a king, the ancestor of KṚṢṆA, and the eldest son of YAYĀTI, the fifth monarch of the lunar dynasty.<BR>2 A country on the west of the Jumna river about Mathurā and Vṛndāvana, over which YADU ruled, and named after him: according to some authorities, however, the kingdom of YADU, is the Dekshin or Peninsula of India.<BR>m. plu. (-वाः)<BR>1 The Yādavas, the people of YADU.<BR>2 Descendants of king YADU: more usually however यादवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदुनाथ|यदुनाथः
यदुनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>यटु the son of YAYĀTI, but here put for his race, and नाथ lord, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छा
यदृच्छा<BR>f. (-च्छा)<BR>1 Wilfulness, independence, following one's own fancies.<BR>2 (In grammar,) A noun which is neither a generic nor specific term, nor noun of agency; one either not derived from authority, or not possessing meaning.<BR>E.<BR>यत् what, which, ऋच्छ to go, aff. अ and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छाभिज्ञ|यदृच्छाभिज्ञः
यदृच्छाभिज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A voluntary or self-offered witness.<BR>E.<BR>यदृच्छा, and अभिज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्यपि
यद्यपि<BR>adv.<BR>Although.<BR>E.<BR>यदि, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्वत्
यद्वत्<BR>ind.<BR>As, in what manner, correlative to तद्वत्.<BR>E.<BR>यट्, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तृ|यंतृ
यन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>A check, a restraint, any person or thing that restrains, &c.<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>1 A charioteer.<BR>2 An elephantdriver.<BR>E.<BR>यम to restrain, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (यन्त्रति यन्त्रयति)<BR>To restrain: see यत्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>1 A machine in general, any implement or apparatus.<BR>2 A diagram of a mystical nature, or astrological character.<BR>3 A sort of vessel.<BR>4 Restraining, checking, controlling.<BR>E.<BR>यम to check, Uṇādi aff. त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रक|यंत्रक|यन्त्रकं|यंत्रकः|यन्त्रकः
यन्त्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lathe.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wife's younger sister.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्र a machine or restraining, &c., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रगृह|यंत्रगृह|यन्त्रगृहं
यन्त्रगृह<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>1 An oil mill.<BR>2 A manufactory.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्र any machine, the apparatus used for grinding substances yielding oil, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रगोल|यन्त्रगोलः
यन्त्रगोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Common pea.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्र a machine, and गोल. round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रण|यंत्रण|यंत्रणं|यन्त्रणं
यन्त्रण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Pain, anguish, affliction.<BR>2 Binding, confining.<BR>3 Checking, controlling, especially the passions.<BR>E.<BR>यत्रि to restrain, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=680" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रपेषणी
यन्त्रपेषणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A handmill.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्र a machine, and पेषणी a stone for grinding on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रित|यंत्रित|यन्त्रितः
यन्त्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bound, tied, chained, fettered.<BR>2 Checked, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्र restraining, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रितकथ
यन्त्रितकथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Restrained in speech, constrained to be silent.<BR>E.<BR>यन्त्रित, and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यभ
यभ<BR>(औ) यभौ r. 1st cl. (यभति)<BR>To copulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम<BR>r. 1st cl. (औ उ) औयमु (यच्छति)<BR>To stop, to cease, to refrain.<BR>With नि prefixed,<BR>1 To remove, to dispel.<BR>2 To observe as a vow or religious rite.<BR>3 To regulate, to restrain.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To rise, to mount on.<BR>2 To make effort or exertion.<BR>3 To lift up, to raise.<BR>With वि and आङ्,<BR>To exercise.<BR>With सम् and नि,<BR>To restrain. In some senses it takes the deponent form, as<BR>with आङ्, prefix,<BR>(आयच्छते)<BR>To put forth, to use or employ any part of one's own body, as the hand, &c.<BR>(आयच्छति)<BR>1 To seize.<BR>2 To go to, to proceed to.<BR>With सम्,<BR>(संयच्छते)<BR>To heap together any thing that is one's own.<BR>(संयच्छति)<BR>To associate with.<BR>With उप,<BR>(उपयच्छते)<BR>1 To marry.<BR>2 To agree or accede to.<BR>3 To master by learning.<BR>r. 10th cl. (यमयति यामयति)<BR>1 To feed, to give food to.<BR>2 To restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Twin, fellow, one of a pair or brace.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Restraining, controlling.<BR>2 Forbearance, refraining.<BR>3 Cessation, stop, conclusion, finish.<BR>4 Religious restraint or obligation.<BR>5 Penance, purification, the performance of those acts which remove impurity of any kind.<BR>6 Any of the five acts or virtues, which constitute pure characters, as refraining from violence or injury, patience, sincerity, obedience to a spiritual teacher, and the observance of all purificatory ceremonies.<BR>7 A festival.<BR>8 A crow.<BR>9 A name of the planet SATURN.<BR>10 YAMA, the deity of Naraka or hell, where his capital is placed, in which he sits in judgment on the dead, and distributes rewards and punishments, sending the good to Svarga, and the wicked to the division of Naraka or Tartarus appropriated to their crimes: he corresponds with the Grecian god PLUTO, and the judge of hell MINOS, and in Hindu mythology is often identified with Death and Time: he is the son of SŪRYA or the sun, and brother of the personified YAMUNĀ or Jumna river.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A brace, a couple, a pair.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The Yamunā river.<BR>E.<BR>यम to restrain, &c., aff. अच् or अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमक|यमकं|यमकः
यमक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Twin, fellow, one of a pair or twins.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A religious obligation or observance.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A species of alliteration, the repetition of similar words or syllables either in a similar or a dissimilar sense in various parts of a stanza, beginning, middle, or end of each hemistich, or pervading the whole verse: ten varieties are enumerated.<BR>2 A couple of like articles; (in medicine,) serum and marrow: (in diet,) oil and ghee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकालिन्दी
यमकालिन्दी<BR>f. (-न्दी)<BR>SAṂJÑĀ, the wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and कालिन्दी the Yamunā river; their mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकीट|यमकीटः
यमकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An earthworm.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदग्नि|यमदग्निः
यमदग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>1 The saint JAMADAGNI, the father of the first RĀMA.<BR>2 PARAŚURĀMA, son of the preceding.<BR>E.<BR>see जमदाग्नि, य being substituted for ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदूत|यमदूतः
यमदूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An infernal spirit, the messenger or minister of YAMA, employed to bring the souls of the dead to YAMA'S judgment seat, and thence conduct them to their final destination.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and टूत a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदूतक|यमदूतकः
यमदूतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 A messenger or minister of YAMA.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The tamarisk tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् pleonasm or aff. of comparison, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदेवता
यमदेवता<BR>nf. (-तं-ता)<BR>The lunar asterism Bharaṇī.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, देवता deity, the deity or regent of this constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमन|यमनं|यमनः
यमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Binding, confining.<BR>2 Term, cessation, rest.<BR>3 Controlling, restraining.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>यम to restrain, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमनिका
यमनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wall or screen of cloth surrounding a tent.<BR>E.<BR>यम stop or check, aff. ल्युट्, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमप्रिय|यमप्रियः
यमप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमभगिनी
यमभगिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The YAMUNĀ or Jumnā river.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and भगिनी sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमरथ|यमरथः
यमरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमराज्
यमराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>YAMA, the Indian PLUTO.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and राज् ruler; also with a final vowel यमराज m. (-जः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमल|यमलं|यमलः
यमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pair, a brace, a couple.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of dress, a body and petticoat.<BR>(-ला)<BR>Violent hiccough.<BR>E.<BR>यम to refrain, to cease, aff. कलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमलार्जुनहन्
यमलार्जुनहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>यमलार्जुन a tree so named in the forest of Vṛndāvana, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमवाहन|यमवाहनः
यमवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमव्रत|यमव्रतं
यमव्रत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the duties of royalty, punishing offences without regard to persons, or without partiality or prejudice.<BR>E.<BR>यम the judge of Tartarus, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसभ
यमसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The court or tribunal of Yama.<BR>E.<BR>यम, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसभनीय
यमसभनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to the court of Yama.<BR>E.<BR>यमसभ, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसात्कृत
यमसात्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made over to, devoted to, or sent to YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>यम with साति aff., and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमस्वसृ
यमस्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 The YAMUNĀ or Jumnā river.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and स्वसृ the sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमानी
यमानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, आङ् before नी to obtain, aff. अण् and ङीष्; with ण्वुल् aff. यमानिका; it is more usually read यवानी, and यवानिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमान्तक|यमान्तकः
यमान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमिन्
यमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Who or what restrains, checks, &c.<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A sage, who has subdued his senses.<BR>E.<BR>यम restraint, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुना
यमुना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The YAMUNĀ or Jumnā river, which rises on the south side of the Himāla range, at a short distance to the north-west of the source of the Ganges, and which after a course of about 378 miles falls into that river immediately below Allahabad; in mythology, the personified river is considered as the daughter of SŪRYA, and sister of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>यम to stop, (at the Ganges,) and उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=681" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाजनक|यमुनाजनकः
यमुनाजनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>SŪRYA, or the sun.<BR>E.<BR>यमुना the river, and जनक parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाभिद्
यमुनाभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद् or भित्)<BR>BALADEVA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>यमुना the Yamunā, and भिद् divider; having divided the river into two parts with his ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाभ्रातृ
यमुनाभ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A name of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>यमुना the Yamunā, and भ्रातृ brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमेरुका
यमेरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A Gong, a metal plate, or a large drum used to strike the hours or watches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययाति|ययातिः
ययाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A monarch of India, the fifth of the lunar race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययी
ययी<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, Uṇādi aff. ई, and the root repeated, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययु|ययुः
ययु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 A horse fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>2 Any horse.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, Uṇādi aff. उ, the root reiterated, and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यर्हि
यर्हि<BR>adv.<BR>Wherefore, when.<BR>E.<BR>यट्, and र्हिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Barley, (Hordeum hexastichon.)<BR>2 The measure of a barley corn, considered as equal to six mustard seeds.<BR>3 A natural line across the thumb at the second joint, when it may be compared to a grain of barley, and supposed to indicate good fortune.<BR>4 Speed, velocity.<BR>5 A double convex lens.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join or mix, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक|यवकः
यवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्य|यवक्यं
यवक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Fit for or producing barley, a field, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यवक barley, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षार|यवक्षारः
यवक्षार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Saltpetre, nitre, nitrate of potash.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and क्षार ashes or salt; being prepared, according to some of the commentators, accurately enough, from burnt barley, the potash being thus procured; according to others however it is so termed, from the crystals being supposed to resemble the spike of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षोद|यवक्षोदः
यवक्षोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Barley meal.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and क्षोद meal or powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवगण्ड|यवगण्डः
यवगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of eruption on the face.<BR>E.<BR>यव for युव youth, and गण्ड affecting the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवज|यवजः
यवज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Nitre.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and ज born: see यवक्षार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवन|यवनः
यवन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A country; probably Bactria, or it may be extended from that colony to Ionia, (to which word it bears some resemblance,) or still further to Greece: by late Hindu writers, it is most commonly applied to Arabia.<BR>2 A Yavana, apparently originally a Greek, but since applied to both the Mohammedan and European invaders of India, and often used as a general term for any foreign or barbarous race.<BR>3 Speed, velocity.<BR>4 A swift horse.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of a Yavana.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, aff. युच्, or जु to be swift, and the consonant changed to its analogous semivowel: or योनि the womb, (of the cow of VASIṢṬHA,) and अण् aff.; being born for the purpose of opposing the armies of VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनप्रिय|यवनप्रियं
यवनप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>यवन a Yavana, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनाचार्य्य|यवनाचार्य|यवनाचार्यः|यवनाचार्य्यः
यवनाचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>An astronomical writer, frequently quoted by Varāhamihira, and other ancient Hindu astronomers: perhaps PTOLEMY, or the Greek astronomers collectively.<BR>E.<BR>यवन a Yāvana, and आचार्य्य a holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनारि|यवनारिः
यवनारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>यवन a Yavana, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनाल|यवनालः
यवनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of grass, very generally cultivated, and the grain extensively eaten, (Andropogon or Holcus bicolor.)<BR>2 Barley straw.<BR>E.<BR>यत्र barley, and नाल culm or stalk; also यावनाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनालज|यवनालजः
यवनालज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Nitre.<BR>E.<BR>यवनाल barley straw, and ज produced: see यवक्षार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनिका
यवनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An outer tent, a screen of cloth surrounding a tent or tents.<BR>E.<BR>see जवनिका, ज being changed to य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनेष्ट|यवनेष्टं|यवनेष्टः
यवनेष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Lead.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 Garlick.<BR>2 A sort of onion.<BR>2 The Nimb tree.<BR>E.<BR>यवन a Yavana, a barbarian, and इष्ट wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवप्रख्या
यवप्रख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>A small hard indolent tumor like a barley corn.<BR>E.<BR>यव, and प्रख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवफल|यवफलः
यवफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 Indian spikenard.<BR>3 A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica)<BR>4 An onion.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, &c., and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमध्य|यवमध्यं|यवमध्यः
यवमध्य<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>A form of penance, diminishing the food daily during the dark fortnight, fasting on the new moon, and gradually augmenting the food till the full moon.<BR>f. (-ध्या)<BR>A form of metre, a triplet, the divisions of which are of unequal length, the middle line having one syllable more than the first or last.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, मध्य centrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमय|यवमयः
यवमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of or from barley.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवलास|यवलासः
यवलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Nitre, saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and लस to like, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवशूक|यवशूकः
यवशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Nitre, saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and शूक the beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवस|यवसं
यवस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Meadow or pasture grass.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवसुर|यवसुरं
यवसुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Spirituous or fermented liquor distilled from barley, beer.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, सुरा wine, ष aff., in the neuter gender; also यवसुरा the second member being unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवागू
यवागू<BR>f. (-गूः)<BR>Sour gruel, prepared by the spontaneous fermentation of water in which rice has been boiled.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, आगूच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवाग्रज|यवाग्रजः
यवाग्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>यत्र barley, अग्र the top or ear, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवान|यवानः
यवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Swift, fleet.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>E.<BR>यव speed, नी to possess, prefix आङ्, and aff. ड; also with कन् added, fem. form यवानिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवास|यवासः
यवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A flower, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, Uṇādi aff. आस; also with कन् added, यवासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठ|यविष्ठः
यविष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Youngest, very young.<BR>m. (-ष्ठ)<BR>A younger brother.<BR>E.<BR>युवन् young, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative; also with कन् added, यविष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठवत्|यविष्ठवन्त्
यविष्ठवत्<BR>adv.<BR>Like a youth.<BR>E.<BR>यविष्ठ, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीयस्
यवीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Youngest, very young.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A younger brother.<BR>E.<BR>युवन् young, इयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
यव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Fit for barley, sown with barley, &c.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A month.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःपटह|यशःपटहः
यशःपटह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A drum, a double drum.<BR>E.<BR>यशस् fame, and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=682" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःशेष|यशःशेषः
यशःशेष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>यशस् fame, and शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्
यशस्<BR>n. (-शः)<BR>1 Glory, fame, celebrity, reputation.<BR>2 Splendour, lustre.<BR>3 Praise, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>अश to pervade, to spread abroad, aff. असुन, and युट् augment, substituted for the initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्कर|यशस्करः
यशस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Rendering famous, conferring celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>यशस् fame, कृ to make, aff. टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्काम
यशस्काम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Ambitious, desirous of fame or glory.<BR>E.<BR>यशस्, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्काम्यत्
यशस्काम्यत्<BR>mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-म्यत)<BR>Desiring fame or glory.<BR>E.<BR>यशस्, and काम्यत् desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्वत्|यशस्वन्त्
यशस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>यशस् fame, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्विन्
यशस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Famed, renowned, celebrated.<BR>f. (-स्विनी)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>यशस् fame, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्य
यशस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Conferring fame.<BR>E.<BR>यशस्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशोघ्न
यशोघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Destroying fame, rendering infamous.<BR>E.<BR>यशस्, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि<BR>mf. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टी)<BR>1 A staff, a stick.<BR>2 A staff armed with iron, &c. used as a weapon, a club, a mace.<BR>3 A necklace.<BR>4 Any creeping plant.<BR>5 Liquorice.<BR>6 A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>7 A string, a thread, especially as strung with pearls, &c.<BR>8 A thread in general.<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 A flag-staff.<BR>2 The arm and forearm.<BR>E.<BR>यक्ष to worship, aff. क्तिन्, and the क of the compound final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिक|यष्टिकः
यष्टिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird, the lapwing.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A necklace, especially of but one string.<BR>2 A pond, a pool.<BR>3 Liquorice.<BR>4 A club, a staff, a bludgeon.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिग्रह|यष्टिग्रहः
यष्टिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A club-bearer, one carrying a staff or stick.<BR>E.<BR>यष्टि a stick, and ग्रह to take, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिमधु
यष्टिमधु<BR>n. (-धु)<BR>Liquorice, or the root of the Abrus precatorius, which is used for it.<BR>E.<BR>यष्टि a stick, and मधु honey; also with कन् added, fem. form यष्टिमधुका, and with the final of the first word long. यष्टीमधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टृ
यष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>A sacrificer, one who employs priests for a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, aff. तृच्, and ज changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस
यस<BR>(इर उ) इर् यसु r. 1st and 4th cls. (यसति यस्यति)<BR>To endeavour, to persevere, to make strenuous and persevering exertion.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>To labour.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To exude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्य
यस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 To be done with energy or perseverance.<BR>2 To be killed or put to death.<BR>E.<BR>यस to strive यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्यत्व
यस्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Death, being killed.<BR>2 Effort, energy.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यह्व|यह्वः
यह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A sacrificer, an institutor of sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, वन् Uṇādi aff., and हुक् augment, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
या<BR>r. 2nd cl. (याति)<BR>1 To go, to go to.<BR>2 To obtain, to get.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To follow.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To approach, to reach.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To come, to arrive.<BR>With उप,<BR>To give way, to yield.<BR>With निर्,<BR>1 To go out or forth.<BR>2 To go readily or quickly.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To go to.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To go to or towards.<BR>With प्रति and उत्,<BR>To meet, to advance to.<BR>With सम and अभि,<BR>To approach.<BR>With सम and आङ्,<BR>To arrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याग|यागः
याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A sacrifice, any ceremony in which offerings and oblations are presented.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच
याच<BR>(दु, ऋ) दुयाहृ r. 1st cl. (याचति-ते)<BR>1 To ask or beg, to solicit, to request.<BR>2 To offer, to tender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचक|याचकः
याचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Beggar, mendicant, asking, one who asks or solicits.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनक|याचनकः
याचनक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Beggar, mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>याचन an asker, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचना
याचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचमान|याचमानः
याचमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Asking, soliciting.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनीय
याचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be asked, begged, &c.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचित|याचितं
याचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Asked, begged, solicited.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितक|याचितकं
याचितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A thing borrowed for use.<BR>E.<BR>याचित asked, and कन् added; what is got by solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्य|याच्यं
याच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>To be asked, begged, &c.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्यमान
याच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being asked or solicited.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्ञा
याच्ञा<BR>f. (-च्ञा)<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>E.<BR>याच to ask, नङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज|याजः
याज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Boiled rice, or generally, food.<BR>E.<BR>यज to present, aff. घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजक|याजकः
याजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An officiating priest, a Brahman who conducts any part of a sacrifice.<BR>2 A royal elephant.<BR>3 A furious elephant.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजन|याजनं
याजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Conducting a sacrifice or causing its performance.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजि|याजिः
याजि<BR>m. (-जिः)<BR>A sacrificer, an institutor of sacrificial ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, Uṇādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजिन्
याजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>Sacrificing, one who officiates at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्य|याज्यं|याज्यः
याज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>To be offered or sacrificed.<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>A sacrificer, the person for whom it is performed.<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Property or presents derived from officiating at sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुष|याजुषं|याजुषः
याजुष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>Belonging to or relating to the Yajur Veda.<BR>E.<BR>यजुर or यजुस् the Veda, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञदत्ति
याज्ञदत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञदत्त a proper name, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्क्य|याज्ञवल्क्यः
याज्ञवल्क्य<BR>m. (-ल्क्यः)<BR>A celebrated saint and legislator; the supposed author of a celebrated code of laws, and the first reputed teacher of the white portion of the Yajur Veda revealed to him by the sun.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञवल्क the father of the saint, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञसेनी
याज्ञसेनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञसेन the father of the princess, and अण् patronymic aff., ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक|याज्ञिकः
याज्ञिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sacrificer, an institutor of a sacrifice.<BR>2 An officiating priest at a sacrificial ceremony.<BR>3 Kuśa or sacrificial grass.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक्य|याज्ञिक्यं
याज्ञिक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Sacrifice, sacrificial ceremonies.<BR>E.<BR>याज्ञिक a sacrificer, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिय|याज्ञियः
याज्ञिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Fit for sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>यज्ञिय, and अण added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=683" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात्<BR>ind.<BR>An interjection,<BR>1 of pleasure;<BR>2 alarm;<BR>3 restlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात्<BR>m. (-यान्-यान्ती-यात्)<BR>Going.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात|यातं|यातः
यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, went.<BR>2 Obtained, got.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Driving or guiding an elephant with a goad.<BR>E.<BR>यत to endeavour, or या to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातना
यातना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Pain, agony, sharp or acute pain.<BR>2 Pain or punishment inflicted by YAMA or his ministers, the pains of hell.<BR>E.<BR>यत to inflict pain, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातयाम|यातयामं
यातयाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Old.<BR>2 Used, impaired.<BR>3 Rejected, abandoned.<BR>4 Raw, half ripe or dressed.<BR>E.<BR>यात gone or got, याम forbearance, relinquishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातव्य
यातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be gone.<BR>2 To be gone against, to be attacked or invaded.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
यातु<BR>mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु)<BR>A goer, one who goes or moves.<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A demon, a goblin, an imp or evil spirit.<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 A traveller, a wayfarer.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, तु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातुधान|यातुधानः
यातुधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A goblin, an evil spirit.<BR>E.<BR>यातु the same, धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृ
यातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A charioteer, a driver.<BR>2 A husband's brother's wife.<BR>E.<BR>यत to endeavour assiduously, Uṇādi aff. ऋत्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्य|यात्यं|यात्यः
यात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>An infernal or condemned spirit.<BR>E.<BR>यत to endeavour, causal form, aff. यत्, to be made to toil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रा
यात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Going, moving, proceeding, marching, travelling.<BR>2 Passing away time.<BR>3 Practice, usage, custom.<BR>4 A holy festival, but especially the procession of idols, &c. which usually forms part of the ceremonies on such an occasion.<BR>5 An expedient, a means.<BR>6 The march of an assailing force.<BR>7 Going to pilgrimage.<BR>8 A sort of dramatic entertainment.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, Uṇādi aff. त्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्राकरण
यात्राकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Setting forth on a journey, a march, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यात्रा, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्राप्रसङ्ग|यात्राप्रसंगः
यात्राप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Performing a pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>यात्रा, and प्रसङ्ग engaging in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रिक|यात्रिकः
यात्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to a march, &c.<BR>2 Customary, usual.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A pilgrim.<BR>2 A traveller.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Provision, supplies, conveyance, &c. for a march.<BR>E.<BR>यात्रा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रोत्सव|यात्रोत्सवः
यात्रोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A public festival.<BR>E.<BR>यात्रा procession, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथातथ्य|याथातथ्यं
याथातथ्य<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>Rectitude, truth, propriety.<BR>E.<BR>यथातथा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थिक
याथार्थिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Just, true, right.<BR>E.<BR>यथार्थ, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थ्य|याथार्थ्यं
याथार्थ्य<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>Application, use, accomplishment, attainment of an object.<BR>E.<BR>यथाथ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादईश|यादईशः
यादईश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>यादस् an aquatic animal, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादःपति|यादःपतिः
यादःपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 VARUṆA, regent of water.<BR>E.<BR>यादस् a fish, &c., and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादव|यादवः
यादव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 KṚṢṆA, as descended from the family of Yadu.<BR>2 A Yādava, or descendant of Yadu.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Stock of cattle.<BR>E.<BR>यदु a proper name, and अण् aff. of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादस्
यादस्<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>Any aquatic or amphibious animal.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, (with speed,) असुन् aff., and दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादसांनाथ
यादसांनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>VARUṆA, the deity of water.<BR>E.<BR>यादस् an aquatic animal, in the sixth case plural, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादसाम्पति|यादसांपति|यादसांपतिः
यादसाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>VARUṆA, the ocean.<BR>E.<BR>यादसाम्, and पति lord: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृच्छिक|यादृच्छिकः
यादृच्छिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Independant, following one's own will.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ministering priest who does as he pleases.<BR>E.<BR>यदृच्छा, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृश्
यादृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक)<BR>As like, how like, which like.<BR>E.<BR>यट् what, दृश to see, क्विन् aff., form irr.; also with खञ् aff. यादृश; mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) and with क्स added यादृक्ष (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादोनिवासस्
यादोनिवासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>यादम् an aquatic animal, and निवासस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान|यानं|यानः
यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Any vehicle or form of conveyance, as a carriage, a litter, a horse, an elephant, &c.<BR>2 Going, marching, proceeding.<BR>3 Invading, marching against an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानपात्र|यानपात्रं
यानपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A vessel, a ship, a boat.<BR>E.<BR>यान going, (by water,) and पात्र a cup or vessel; also with कन् added यानपात्रक; n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानमुख|यानमुखं
यानमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>The forepart of a carriage, the pole or part where the yoke is fixed.<BR>E.<BR>यान a vehicle, and मुख face or front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानस्वामिन्
यानस्वामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>The owner of a vehicle.<BR>E.<BR>यान, and स्वामिन master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापन|यापनं
यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Spending or passing away time.<BR>2 Abiding staying, being.<BR>3 Rejection, ejection, expelling, expulsion.<BR>4 Allaying, alleviating, (as pain or sickness.)<BR>E.<BR>या to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापनीय
यापनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be passed or spent as time.<BR>2 To be allayed or relieved though not cured, (disease or a sick person.)<BR>E.<BR>या to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्ता
याप्ता<BR>f. (-प्ता)<BR>Twisted or matted hair.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, in the causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्य|याप्यः
याप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>1 Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>2 To be passed or spent, (as time, &c.)<BR>3 (In medicine,) To be alleviated or relieved though not cured, (disease.)<BR>E.<BR>या to go, causal form, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्ययान|याप्ययानं
याप्ययान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A litter, a palanquin.<BR>E.<BR>याप्य vile, and यान carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम|यामः
याम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Relating to YAMA, done by him, ordered by him, &c.<BR>(-मः)<BR>1 The eighth part of a day, a watch of three hours.<BR>2 Forbearance.<BR>3 Cessation, term.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, (through the day,) मन् Uṇādi aff., or यम to restrain, aff. घञ् or यम, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामघोष|यामघोषः
यामघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A cock.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A clock, a metal plate on which the hours are struck, or a drum used for a similar purpose.<BR>E.<BR>याम a watch, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामनाली
यामनाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A metal plate on which the hours are struck, or a drum used for that purpose.<BR>E.<BR>याम a watch, and नाली the same instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामनेमि|यामनेमिः
यामनेमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामल|यामलं
यामल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR>E.<BR>यमल the same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामवती
यामवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>याम a watch, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=684" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामातृ
यामातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A daughter's husband.<BR>E.<BR>य substituted for ज; see जामातृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामि|यामिः
यामि<BR>f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>1 A sister.<BR>2 A virtuous woman.<BR>3 Night.<BR>4 The south.<BR>5 A daughter, or daughter-in-law, newly married.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, मि aff., or य substituted for ज, see जामि, or यम YAMA, and अण् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिका
यामिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>याम a watch, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनी
यामिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>याम a watch, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनीपति|यामिनीपतिः
यामिनीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>यामिनी night, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामीर|यामीरः
यामीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>यामी night, रा to have or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुन|यामुनं
यामुन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating to the Yamunā river.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Antimony, or rather the sulphuret of antimony, generally used as an application to darken the eyelashes, and strengthen the eyes.<BR>E.<BR>यमुना the Jumna river, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुनेष्ठक
यामुनेष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामेय|यामेयः
यामेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sister's son.<BR>E.<BR>यामि a sister, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्य|याम्यः
याम्य<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 The saint AGASTYA.<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>1 The south.<BR>2 The lunar asterism, Bharaṇī.<BR>3 Night.<BR>E.<BR>यम YAMA, ण्यत् aff.; being sacred to or governed by that deity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्यायन|याम्यायनं
याम्यायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The sun's course, south of the line.<BR>E.<BR>याम्य the south, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायजूक|यायजूकः
यायजूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The performer of frequent sacrifices.<BR>E.<BR>यज to sacrifice, aff. ऊक, the root repeated, and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायावर|यायावरः
यायावर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Going repeatedly.<BR>2 Wandering, vagrant.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A horse fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>2 The saint JARATKĀRU.<BR>3 A Brahman who has preserved his household fire.<BR>4 A vagrant mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, in the reiterative form, and वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायिन्
यायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Going, who or what goes.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, णिनि aff., युक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव|यावः
याव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Relating to barley.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Lac, the red animal dye.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, aff. अण्; the nest yielding a sort of resinous substance used as sealing-wax: or यव barley, to which the grains of the dye are compared, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावक|यावकं|यावकः
यावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Half-ripe barley.<BR>2 Awnless barley.<BR>3 Forced rice.<BR>4 A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus.)<BR>5 A kind of pulse, (Dolichos biflorus.)<BR>6 A kind of pulse said to be peculiar to Kashmir.<BR>7 Lac.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, aff. वुन्, and अण् added, or याव as above, pleonastic aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावच्छक्य
यावच्छक्य<BR>adv. (-क्यं)<BR>To the utmost of one's power.<BR>E.<BR>यावत्, and शक्य able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावज्जीव|यावज्जीवं
यावज्जीव<BR>n. adv. (-वं)<BR>For life, as long as life.<BR>E.<BR>यावत् until, जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावत्|यावन्त्
यावत्<BR>mfn. (-यावान्, यावती यावत्)<BR>As much, how much, such.<BR>ind.<BR>1 As much as.<BR>2 As many as.<BR>3 As long as.<BR>4 As far as, unto, until; the correlative of तावत्.<BR>5 When, (i. e. as much, applied to time.)<BR>E.<BR>यत् what or which, डवतुप् aff., and आ substituted for the pronominal final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावतिथ|यावतिथः
यावतिथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>That which is as far as, or as much as, &c. the ordinal of the particle यावत्.<BR>E.<BR>यावत् as much as, &c., and तिथक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावत्तावत्
यावत्तावत्<BR>ind.<BR>1 As much as, quantum-tantum.<BR>2 (In algebra,) The relation of the unknown number and its co-efficient.<BR>E.<BR>यावत्, and तावत् so much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
यावन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a Yavana, Ionian, Mohammedan, &c.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Incense.<BR>E.<BR>यवन the country of the Yavanas, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावनाल|यावनालः
यावनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus bicolor.)<BR>E.<BR>यवनाल, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावशूक|यावशूकः
यावशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Nitre, saltpetre.<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, शूक the spike, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावस|यावसः
यावस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A quantity or heap of grass.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, Uṇādi aff. असच् with the effect of णित्, which makes the vowel long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव्य|याव्यं
याव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be mixed or joined, miscible.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join or mix, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याशोधरेय|याशोधरेयः
याशोधरेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The son of ŚĀKYAMUNI, the probable founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याष्टीक|याष्टीकः
याष्टीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A warrior armed with a club.<BR>E.<BR>यष्टि a stick, a club, ठक् aff., and both vowels made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास|यासः
यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A sort of bird, the Sārikā.<BR>E.<BR>यस to endeavour, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्यत्
यास्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>Going, who or what will be going.<BR>E.<BR>या to go, शतृ aff., with the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षमान
यियक्षमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Purposing or wishing to worship.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षु
यियक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Desirous of sacrificing.<BR>E.<BR>यज to worship, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषा
यियविषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Wish to mix, blend, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषु
यियविषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to mix or blend.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु<BR>r. 2nd cl. (यौति)<BR>1 To mix, to join, to blend.<BR>2 To separate or not mix.<BR>r. 10th cl. (यावयति)<BR>To censure, to blame, to disrespect, to despise.<BR>(ञ) युञ् r. 9th cl. (युनाति युनीते)<BR>To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्
युक्<BR>ind.<BR>Badly, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्त|युक्तं|युक्तः
युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Joined, combined, united, identified.<BR>2 Right, fit, proper.<BR>3 Proved, concluded by inference or argument.<BR>4 Moderate, limited.<BR>5 Possessing, endowed with, as virtues, qualities, &c.<BR>6 Intent on, attached to, as a study or pursuit.<BR>7 Employed or engaged in business, &c.<BR>8 Occupied in performance of the religious exercise called Yoga.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>The sage who has acquired the command of his feelings and passions, and who performs the customary devotional offices without any regard to their result.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>A measure of four cubits.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A plant, commonly Elāni.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join or mix, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तरसा
युक्तरसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A plant, commonly Elāni, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>युक्त mixed, joined, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तायस्
युक्तायस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>A sort of wooden spade or shovel.<BR>E.<BR>युक्त bound, joined, and अयस् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्ति|युक्तिः
युक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Union, connection, joining.<BR>2 Propriety, fitness.<BR>3 Usage, custom, traditionary and unwritten law.<BR>4 Inference, deduction from circumstance or argument, the reason of a thing or argument.<BR>5 Insertion of circumstanced in written [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">Page686</a>] evidence, specification in writing of place, time, &c. considered as one of the means of verifying such evidence.<BR>6 A figure of rhetoric, emblematic or mystical expression of purpose, so as to conceal it from all but its immediate object.<BR>7 Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>8 Connection of dramatic events, the production of one incident by another.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=685" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग<BR>(इ) युगि r. 1st cl (युंगति)<BR>To except, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>1 A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR>2 An age, as the Kṛta, Tretā, Dvāpara, and Kali.<BR>3 A lustre, or period of five years.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A yoke.<BR>2 A measure of four cubits.<BR>3 A drug, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, aff. अच्, and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगकीलक|युगकीलकः
युगकीलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The pin of a yoke.<BR>E.<BR>युग a yoke, and कील a pin or bolt, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगक्षय|युगक्षयः
युगक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Destruction of the world.<BR>E.<BR>युग, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगन्धर|युगंधर|युगंधरं|युगंधरः|युगन्धरः
युगन्धर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 The pole of a carriage, or wood to which the yoke is fixed.<BR>2 The name of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>युग a yoke, धृ to hold or support, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्
युगपत्<BR>ind.<BR>1 At one time, at once.<BR>2 Together, conjointly.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, गपतक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्र|युगपत्रः
युगपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Mountain ebony: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्रक|युगपत्रकः
युगपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>f. (-त्रिका)<BR>The Sisu tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>E.<BR>युग a pair, and पत्र a leaf, aff. कन्, double-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपार्श्वग|युगपार्श्वगः
युगपार्श्वग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A young ox in training.<BR>E.<BR>युग a yoke, पार्श्व a side, and ग who goes, or with कन् aff. युगपार्श्वंक m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगल|युगलं
युगल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pair, a brace, a couple.<BR>E.<BR>युग a pair, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगांशक|युगांशकः
युगांशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>युग an age, and अंशक a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगान्त|युगांत|युगान्तः
युगान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A destruction of the universe.<BR>2 The end of an age.<BR>E.<BR>युग an age, either generally or individually, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगान्तबन्धु
युगान्तबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>A real friend, a friend in need.<BR>E.<BR>युगान्त, and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म<BR>n. (-ग्मं)<BR>1 A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR>2 Mixing, uniting.<BR>3 A couple of verses.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, Uṇādi aff. मक्, and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मक
युग्मक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A couple.<BR>2 A couple of verses connected by the construction of the sentence, the sense being completed only by the two together.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मपत्र|युग्मपत्रः
युग्मपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Mountain ebony.<BR>E.<BR>युग्म a couple, and पत्र a leaf, double-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मपत्रिका
युग्मपत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A timber tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>E.<BR>युग्म a pair, and पत्र a leaf, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मफलोत्तम
युग्मफलोत्तम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A plant, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR>E.<BR>युग्म double, फल fruit, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Fit or proper to be yoked or harnessed.<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Any vehicle or conveyance.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>An animal yoked.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, aff. यत् or क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युच्छ
युच्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (युच्छति)<BR>To be inattentive or negligent, to err or mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज
युज<BR>(औ) युजौ r. 4th cl. (युज्यते)<BR>To confine the thoughts, to keep the mind fixed in abstract meditation.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (योजति योजयति)<BR>To bind, to tie, to connect.<BR>(योजयत)<BR>To blame. (औ, इर,)<BR>औ युजिर r. 7th cl. (युनक्ति युंक्ते)<BR>To join, to mix, to unite, &c.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>1 To ask, to inquire.<BR>2 To reprove.<BR>With अभि,<BR>1 To utter, to speak.<BR>2 To accuse.<BR>With उत्,<BR>To make effort.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To seize, to take, to lay hold of.<BR>2 To eat.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To order, to appoint.<BR>2 To join.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To be fit or due.<BR>2 To attach or apply to.<BR>3 To lend money.<BR>4 To make effort.<BR>5 To combine or connect.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To separate, to sunder.<BR>2 To send.<BR>With वि and नि,<BR>1 To appoint or employ.<BR>2 To expend.<BR>3 To send.<BR>4 To involve in or force upon.<BR>With वि and प्र,<BR>to separate, to part, to divide.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To unite, to combine.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To think profoundly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज्<BR>n. (-युक्)<BR>A pair, a couple.<BR>m. (-युक् युग्)<BR>A sage, one who devotes his time to abstract contemplation.<BR>ind. (-जौ)<BR>The twin sons of AŚVINĪ, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>m. (-युङ्^1)<BR>A joiner, one who joins or unites.<BR>f. (-युक्)<BR>A measure of three hundred poles.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, to meditate, &c., aff. क्विन्; also युजिर् the same, with the same aff., when न is inserted after the vowel, before the first five affixes in the masc. and fem. genders.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जत्
युञ्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्)<BR>1 Uniting, joining.<BR>2 Uniting spiritually, practising devotion.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, &c., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जान|युंजान|युञ्जानः
युञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Uniting, combining, joining with.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A charioteer.<BR>2 A Brahman engaged in the religious exercise called Yoga.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, &c., aff. शानच्, and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
युत<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) युतृ (योतते)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
युत्<BR>ind.<BR>Badly, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Joined, combined, connected, identified.<BR>2 Attached to, engaged in or by.<BR>3 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A measure of four cubits.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युतक|युतकं
युतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Joined, combined.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>2 A pair, a brace.<BR>3 Nuptial presents.<BR>4 The end of a cloth worn by women.<BR>5 A garment worn by women; it is applied, it is said, both to the petticoat, and the upper wrapper or cloth.<BR>6 The ends of a cloth.<BR>7 The edge of a winnowing basket.<BR>8 Asylum.<BR>9 Forbearance, cessation.<BR>10 Alliance, acquaintance, forming an alliance or friendship.<BR>E.<BR>युत joined, &c., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युति|युतिः
युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Joining, uniting.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Addition.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्ध|युद्धं
युद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>War, battle, contest, conflict.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्घरङ्ग
युद्घरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A name of the deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>युद्ध war, and रङ्ग delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्घसार
युद्घसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>युद्ध war, सृ to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्घोन्मत्त
युद्घोन्मत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Fierce or frantic in battle.<BR>E.<BR>युद्ध, and उन्मत्त frantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध
युध<BR>(औ) r. 4th cl. औयुध (युध्यते)<BR>To fight, to contend in battle, to slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
युध्<BR>f. (-युत् or -युट्)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधान|युधानः
युधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A man of the second or military order, a soldier, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, Uṇādi aff. आनच्, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=686" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिष्ठिर|युधिष्ठिरः
युधिष्ठिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The elder of the five Pāṇḍava princes, and leader in the great war, between them and the Kurus, in the beginning of the fourth age; the nominal son of PĀṆḌU, whom he succeeded in the sovereignty of India, but according to the legend, begotten on Kunti by the deity YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>युधि in war or battle, and ष्ठिर for स्थिर firm; it is also sometimes read युद्घस्थिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्म|युध्मः
युध्म<BR>m. (-ध्मः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 A bow.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 A warrior, a combatant.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, मक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्यमान
युध्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fighting, warring.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युप
युप<BR>r. 4th cl. (ईर्) युपीर (युप्यति)<BR>To confuse, to perplex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयु|युयुः
युयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्खुर|युयुक्खुरः
युयुक्खुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hyena.<BR>E.<BR>युयुक् joined, खुर a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्षमान
युयुक्षमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Wishing to join or unite.<BR>2 Devout, wishing to effect spiritual union with the divine essence.<BR>E.<BR>युज to be devout or to join, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सा
युयुत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Wish or purpose to fight, enmity, pugnacity.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सारहित
युयुत्सारहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Cowardly, having no intention to fight.<BR>E.<BR>युयुत्सा, and रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सु|युयुत्सुः
युयुत्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing or ready to make war or fight, pugnacious, hostile, ambitious.<BR>m. (-त्सुः)<BR>A combatant.<BR>E.<BR>युध to make war, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधान|युयुधानः
युयुधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A proper name, one of the chiefs of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>2 A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, in the reduplicate form, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवखलति
युवखलति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः or -ती-ति)<BR>Bald in youth.<BR>E.<BR>युवन्, and खलति bald; also युवाखलति, and fem. युवतिःखलति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवगण्ड|युवगण्डः
युवगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Eruptions on the face peculiar to youth.<BR>E.<BR>युव a young person, from युवन्, and गण्ड what affects the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवजरत्|युवजरन्त्
युवजरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रती-रत्)<BR>Being old as it were in youth, oldfashioned, or prematurely infirm.<BR>E.<BR>युवन्, and जरत् old; also युवाजरत्, and in the fem. युवतिःजरती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवजानि|युवजानिः
युवजानि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Having a young wife.<BR>E.<BR>युव, and जानि wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्
युवन्<BR>mfn. (-युवा-युवति or -ती or यूनी-युव)<BR>1 Young.<BR>2 Best, excellent.<BR>3 Endowed with native or natural strength.<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>A young man or one of the virile age, or from sixteen to seventy.<BR>f. (-तिः-ती or यूनी)<BR>A young woman, one from sixteen to thirty.<BR>(-तिः)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix or associate, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, the fem. form takes ति, and optionally adds ङीष् in one form, with which affix the semivowel व is changed to its congener उ, and the two short vowels coalesce into one long one, making यूनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवनाश्वज|युवनाश्वजः
युवनाश्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A name of MĀNDHĀTĀ, an early sovereign of the Solar dynasty.<BR>E.<BR>युवनाश्व his father, who appears as the eighth monarch of the Solar line, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवपलित
युवपलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Grey-haired in youth.<BR>E.<BR>युवन्, and पलित gray-haired; also युवापलित, and fem. युवतिःपलिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज|युवराजः
युवराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A young prince, especially the heir apparent, associated to the throne.<BR>2 One of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR>E.<BR>युव young, and राजन् a prince, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज्य
युवराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>The dignity of heir apparent and associate in the throne.<BR>E.<BR>युवराज, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्
युष्मद्<BR>2nd personal pronoun. mf. (-त्वं)<BR>Thou.<BR>E.<BR>युष Sautra root, to serve, to worship, Uṇādi aff. मदिक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्वाच्य
युष्मद्वाच्य<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>(In grammar,) The second person.<BR>E.<BR>युष्मट्, and वाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यू
यू<BR>f. (-यूः)<BR>The water in which pulse, &c. has been boiled, pease-soup, &c.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, aff. क्विप्, and vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूक|यूकः
यूक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A louse.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, (with the hair,) Uṇādi aff. कन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूति|यूतिः
यूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Joining, mixing.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, aff. क्तिच्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथ|यूथं
यूथ<BR>m. (-थं)<BR>A multitude of birds or beasts, a herd, a flock.<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, थक् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथनाथ|यूथनाथः
यूथनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A large elephant, the leader of a wild herd.<BR>E.<BR>यूथ a multitude, (of elephants,) and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथप|यूथपः
यूथप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The leader of a wild herd of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>यूथ a herd, and प who protects: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथभ्रष्ट|यूथभ्रष्टः
यूथभ्रष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>An elephant turned out or driven from a herd.<BR>E.<BR>यूथ the herd, and भ्रष्ट expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथशस्
यूथशस्<BR>adv.<BR>Gregariously, in flocks.<BR>E.<BR>यूथ, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथिका
यूथिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A sort of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>2 Globe amaranth.<BR>E.<BR>यूथी the jasmine, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूनि|यूनिः
यूनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Joining, union, junction.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join or mix, aff. क्तिन्, न substituted for the final, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूप|यूपः
यूप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 A sacrificial post, a pillar usually made of bambus, or the wood of the Khadira, to which the victim at a sacrifice is bound.<BR>2 A trophy, a column erected in honour of a victory.<BR>E.<BR>यु to bind (the victim), प Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपकटक|यूपकटकः
यूपकटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wooden ring on the top of a sacrificial post, or according to some authorities, an iron ring at its base.<BR>E.<BR>यूप the post, and कटक् a ring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपकर्ण|यूपकर्णः
यूपकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A part of a sacrificial post sprinkled with ghee.<BR>E.<BR>यूप the post, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपद्रु|यूपद्रुः
यूपद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>E.<BR>यूप a sacrificial post, and द्रु a tree; the wood of this tree being especially fit for the sacrificial post; also यूपद्रुम m. (-मः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपलक्ष्य|यूपलक्ष्यः
यूपलक्ष्य<BR>m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>यूप a sacrificial post, put for any post, and लक्ष्य an aim; a sort of net being made about a post, on which birds may alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपाग्र|यूपाग्रं
यूपाग्र<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>The top of the sacrificial post.<BR>E.<BR>यूप as above, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपोच्छ्रय
यूपोच्छ्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The ceremony of erecting the sacrificial post.<BR>E.<BR>यूप a sacrificial post, and उच्छ्रय elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष|यूषं|यूषः
यूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (यूषति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष|यूषं|यूषः
यूष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>Pease soup, pease porridge, the water in which pulse of various kinds has been boiled.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica); also पूष.<BR>E.<BR>यूष to hurt, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष
येष<BR>(ऋ) येषृ r. 1st cl. (येषते)<BR>To resolve, to endeavour diligently, to persevere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्तव्य
योक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be joined or united.<BR>2 To be performed, (as devotion.)<BR>3 To be united spiritually.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्र|योक्त्रं
योक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>The tie of the yoke of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, Uṇādi aff. त्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=687" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग|योगः
योग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Junction, joining, union.<BR>2 Combination, association, meeting, conflux.<BR>3 Religious and abstract meditation.<BR>4 Keeping the body in a fixed posture.<BR>5 Devotion, spiritual worship of GOD, or union with the Supreme Being by means of abstract contemplation; this does not necessarily imply an abandonment of the world or relinquishment of the usual observances of religion, but it involves internal indifference to objects of pleasure and pain, and utter disregard of the consequences or fruit of ceremonial rites.<BR>6 The particular practice of the preceding sort of devotion, or the exercise of that abstraction by which union with GOD is supposed to be obtained; in the Gītā it is described as sitting on Kuśa grass, with the body firm, the eyes fixed on the tip of the nose, and the mind intent on the Deity; in the Tantras a fanciful operation is prescribed, by which the vital spirit seated in the lower part of the body, and the etherial spirit placed in the head, are supposed to be brought into combination in the brain, when the devotee becomes united with BRAHMA.<BR>7 The system of philosophy which treats of the union of the soul with BRAHMA or GOD; it is the same as the Pātañjali doctrine, and constitutes one of the six Darśanas or philosophical schools of the Hindus.<BR>8 Magic, or the acquisition of supernatural powers by the mystical and magical worship of ŚIVA and DURGĀ especially.<BR>9 Consequence, result, the main end or object of any thing or act.<BR>10 Connexion of one thing with another, as of cause with effect, predicate with subject, quality with substance, &c.<BR>11 Acquisition of something not possessed before, accession of property or wealth; in grammar this application is assigned to any unusual construction of words or compounds, unauthorised by rule, but sanctioned by the authority that employs them.<BR>12 A rule, an aphorism.<BR>13 Propriety, fitness.<BR>14 Side, part, cause or argument to be maintained or defended.<BR>15 Thing, substance.<BR>16 Wealth.<BR>17 A drug, a medicament, especially^1 a compound of various ingredients.<BR>18 Fraud, trick.<BR>19 A logician.<BR>20 A spy, an informer.<BR>21 A violator of truth or confidence.<BR>22 A conveyance, a carriage, a boat, &c.<BR>23 A means, an expedient.<BR>24 Armour.<BR>25 Putting on armour.<BR>26 Lucky conjuncture.<BR>27 (In arithmetic,) Addition.<BR>28 (In astronomy,) The leading or principal star of a lunar mansion.<BR>29 The twenty-seventh part of 360° of a great circle measured on the plane of the ecliptic, and used in calculating the longitudes of the sun and moon; each Yogas has a distinct name; astrologers also enumerate twenty-eight Yogas differently named from the foregoing, and corresponding with the twenty-eight Nakṣatras, or the divisions of the moon's path, but varying according to the day of the week.<BR>30 A period, or the time during which the sum of the motions of the sun and moon amount to one Nakṣatra, the mean duration of which is 23hs. 47' 44".<BR>E.<BR>युज to join literally or figuratively, as with GOD, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक्षेम|योगक्षेमं|योगक्षेमः
योगक्षेम<BR>n. (-मः)<BR>1 Charge of property, keeping of cattle, &c. for another.<BR>2 Insurance or charge for secure conveyance of goods, and the profit on their sale.<BR>3 Profit, gain, keeping the old and making fresh gains.<BR>4 Such articles as are not divisible amongst coheirs.<BR>5 Welfare, well-being.<BR>6 National prosperity the good government of a state, or the means of maintaining^1 it; as the Raja, minister, priest, &c. forming the administration.<BR>E.<BR>योग profit, and क्षेम safety or preservation; or योग association, and क्षेम patience.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक्षेमकर
योगक्षेमकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A keeper, one who takes charge of property, &c.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगचर|योगचरः
योगचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>योग possession of superhuman powers, and चर going, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगतस्
योगतस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Suitably, properly.<BR>2 Seasonably, in due season.<BR>3 Through devotion, magic, &c.<BR>4 Conjointly.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगदान|योगदानं
योगदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A fraudulent gift.<BR>2 Communicating the Yoga doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगनाविक|योगनाविकः
योगनाविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Silurus ascita.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगनिद्रा
योगनिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>1 The sleep of VIṢṆU during the deluge.<BR>2 A goddess, a form of DURGĀ or VIṢṆU'S sleep personified.<BR>E.<BR>योग mystery, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगपट्ट|योगपट्टं
योगपट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A cloth drawn round the lower extremities of the ascetic as he squats to perform religious abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>योग a religious exercise, and पट्ट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवाहिन्
योगवाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A menstruum or medium for mixing medicines.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and वाहिन् conveyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवाही
योगवाही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>1 Alkali.<BR>2 Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>योग joining of metals, वाह effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगविक्रय|योगविक्रयः
योगविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Fraudulent sale.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगविद्
योगविद्<BR>m. (-वित्)<BR>1 A follower of the Yoga doctrines.<BR>2 A practiser of devotional exercises.<BR>3 A magician.<BR>4 A compounder of medicines.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगसेवा
योगसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Practising religious abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and सेवा observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाधमन|योगाधमनं
योगाधमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fraudulent pledge.<BR>E.<BR>योग fraud, and आधमन a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगारूढ|योगारूढः
योगारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Engaged in devotional exercises.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and आरूढ mounted on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगासन|योगासनं
योगासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A religious posture, the position in which the devotee sits to perform the religious exercise called Yoga.<BR>E.<BR>योग as above, and आसन seat or sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिन्
योगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>1 Who or what joins, or effects junction or connection, &c.<BR>2 Possessed of superhuman powers.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>1 A devotee, an ascetic in general.<BR>2 The religious or devout man, who performs worldly actions and ceremonies without regard to their results, and keeps his mind fixed upon BRAHMA or GOD alone.<BR>3 The performer of the particular act of meditation called Yoga.<BR>4 A magician, a conjuror, one supposed to have obtained supernatural powers.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A female fiend or sprite attendant on, and created by DURGA; in some places eight Yoginīs are enumerated by name.<BR>E.<BR>योग as above, इनि aff., or युज to join, aff. घिणुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिनिद्रा
योगिनिद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>Light sleep, wakefulness.<BR>E.<BR>योगिन् a saint, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेश|योगेशः
योगेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The city of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 The saint and legislator YĀJÑAVALKYA.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 Any principal Muni or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">Page689</a>] Yogi.<BR>E.<BR>यीग a Yogi or religious personage, &c., and ईश lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=688" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेश्वर|योगेश्वरः
योगेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A principal sage or ascetic.<BR>2 A magician, one who has superhuman faculties.<BR>3 A deity, the object of devout contemplation.<BR>E.<BR>योग, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेष्ट|योगेष्टं
योगेष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Lead.<BR>E.<BR>योग affinity, (of metals or amalgamation,) इष्ट desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्य|योग्यं|योग्यः
योग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>1 Clever, skilful.<BR>2 Fit or proper for a Yoga, or for religious meditation.<BR>3 Powerful, able.<BR>4 Fit, proper, suitable.<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>1 A drug, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>2 A cake.<BR>3 A vehicle or conveyance.<BR>4 Sandal.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>A calculator of expedients.<BR>f. (-ग्या)<BR>1 Military exercise.<BR>2 Medical practice.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join or mix, aff. ण्यत्, or योग union, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्यता
योग्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fitness, suitableness, propriety.<BR>E.<BR>योग्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, योग्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
योजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 GOD, the SUPREME BEIṄG, the soul of the world.<BR>2 A measure of distance equal to four Krośas, which at 8000 cubits or 4000 yards to the Krośa or Kos, will be exactly nine miles; other computations make the Yojana but about five miles, or even no more than four miles and a half.<BR>2 Joining, union, junction.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनगन्धा
योजनगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>1 Musk.<BR>2 A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>3 A name of SATYAVATĪ, the mother of the sage and poet VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>योजन a Yojana, and गन्ध smell; whose odour is perceptible miles off; also with कन् added, fem. form, योजनगन्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनपर्णी
योजनपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>Bengal madder.<BR>E.<BR>योजन joining, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनवल्ली
योजनवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>योजन joining, and वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनीय
योजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be joined.<BR>2 To be added.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजयितृ
योजयितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Joining, combining, who or what unites.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजित|योजितं
योजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Mixed, joined.<BR>E.<BR>युज to join, aff. क्त, more usually युक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योतु|योतुः
योतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Measure in general.<BR>2 Cleaning, purifying.<BR>3 A cleanser, a purifier.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, or not to mix, and तुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्र|योत्रं
योत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The tie that fastens the yoke of a plough to the neck of the ox.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्स्यमान
योत्स्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>About to fight, ready to fight.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, desid. v., future tense, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धव्य
योद्धव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be fought, what must or ought to be fought.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धृ
योद्धृ<BR>m. (-द्धा)<BR>A warrior, a combatant.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योध|योधः
योध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A warrior, a soldier, a combatant.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधमुख्य|योधमुख्यः
योधमुख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A leader, a chief warrior.<BR>E.<BR>योध, and मुख्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधयत्
योधयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Fighting, warring.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधवीर
योधवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hero, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>योध, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधसंराव|योधसंरावः
योधसंराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Mutual defiance, challenging or braving each other.<BR>E.<BR>योध a warrior, संराव cry or shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधहर
योधहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Carrying soldiers fit for war, (horses.)<BR>E.<BR>योध, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधिन्
योधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>युध to fight, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधेय|योधेयः
योधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>युद्घ war, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनल|योनलः
योनल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus sorghum.)<BR>E.<BR>यव barley, and नल culm or stalk, the व of the first word changed to उ, and उ with the inherent vowel of य changed to ओ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनि|योनिः
योनि<BR>mf. (-निः-निः or नी)<BR>1 The vulva.<BR>2 A mine.<BR>3 Cause, origin.<BR>4 Water.<BR>5 Place or site of birth or production in general.<BR>E.<BR>यु to join or mix, Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिदेवता
योनिदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The 11th Nakṣatra or lunar asterism; also Pūrvaphalgunī.<BR>E.<BR>योनि the vulva, and दवता presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिनासा
योनिनासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The upper part of the vulva, or the union of the labiæ.<BR>E.<BR>योनि the womb, and नासा the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिरञ्जन|योनिरंजन
योनिरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The menstrual excretion.<BR>E.<BR>योनि pudendum, and रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिलिङ्ग|योनिलिंग
योनिलिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The clitoris.<BR>E.<BR>योनि the pudendum, and लिङ्ग the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिसंवृत्ति|योनिसंवृत्तिः
योनिसंवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Contraction or closure of the vagina.<BR>E.<BR>योनि, and संवृत्ति contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिसङ्कर|योनिसंकर|योनिसंकरः
योनिसङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fault or blemish of birth on the mother's side, as from inferiority of caste, &c.<BR>E.<BR>योनि, and सङ्कर mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योन्यर्शस्
योन्यर्शस्<BR>n. (-र्शः)<BR>An affection of the vulva, Menorrhagia, or prolapsus uteri.<BR>E.<BR>योनि the vulva, and अर्शस् piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषा
योषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>युष to serve, Sautra root, causal form, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्
योषित्<BR>f. (-षित्)<BR>A woman in general.<BR>E.<BR>युष Sautra root, to serve, to worship, to hurt, इति Uṇādi aff.; also with टाप् added योषिता f. (-ता.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्कृत
योषित्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done by a woman, contracted by her, &c.<BR>E.<BR>योषित्, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्तिक|यौक्तिकः
यौक्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Connective, binding.<BR>2 Inferrible, deducible.<BR>3 Customary, usual.<BR>4 Right, proper.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A minister or associate to one's pleasure or amusements.<BR>E.<BR>युक्ति union, association, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगक|यौगकः
यौगक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the religious practice, &c. called Yoga.<BR>E.<BR>योग as above, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगिक|यौगिकः
यौगिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Customary, usual, common.<BR>2 Relating to the Yoga, &c.<BR>3 Proper, regular, (as the sense of words, depending upon their derivation or construction.)<BR>E.<BR>योग, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनशतिक|यौजनशतिकः
यौजनशतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Proceeding or extending a hundred Yojanas.<BR>E.<BR>योजन a measure so named, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनिक|यौजनिकः
यौजनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Extending or proceeding a Yojana.<BR>E.<BR>योजन a Yojana, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौट
यौट<BR>(ऋ) यौटृ r. 1st cl. (यौटति)<BR>To bind, to tie, to join or fasten; also read यौडृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतक|यौतकं
यौतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A nuptial gift, presents made to a bride, at her marriage, by her father or friends; some consider it also implying a gift to the bridegroom.<BR>E.<BR>युतक the same, pleonastic aff. अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=689" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतव|यौतवं
यौतव<BR>n. (-व)<BR>Measure in general.<BR>E.<BR>योतु the same, अण् aff.; some authorities read यौवत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधेय|यौधेयः
यौधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>योधेय the same, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौन|यौनं
यौन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Relating to the womb or place of origin, uterine.<BR>2 Connected by female alliance, marriage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>योनि, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवत|यौवतं
यौवत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Measure in general.<BR>2 An assemblage of young women.<BR>E.<BR>यु to mix, deriv. irr., or युवती a young woman, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवन|यौवनं
यौवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Youth manhood.<BR>2 An assemblage of young women.<BR>E.<BR>युवन young, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनकण्टक|यौवनकण्टकं|यौवनकण्टकः
यौवनकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Pimples on the face, especially in young persons.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन youth, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनदर्प|यौवनदर्पः
यौवनदर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>Pride of youth, rashness, conceit.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन, and दर्प pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनदशा
यौवनदशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>The period of youth.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन, and दशा state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनपिडका
यौवनपिडका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Blotches or pimples on the face in youth.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन, and पिडका a pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनलक्षण|यौवनलक्षणं
यौवनलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The breast, the bosom.<BR>2 Beauty, handsomeness.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन youth, लक्षण mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनवत्|यौवनवन्त्
यौवनवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Youthful.<BR>E.<BR>यौवन, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनाश्व|यौवनाश्वः
यौवनाश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A name of MĀNDHĀTĀ, one of the kings of the solar dynasty.<BR>E.<BR>युवनाश्च a proper name, and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माक|यौष्माकं
यौष्माक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Yours, belonging to you.<BR>E.<BR>युष्माक for युष्मट् you, and aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माकीन|यौष्माकीनं
यौष्माकीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Yours, thine.<BR>E.<BR>युष्माक for युष्मट् thou, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र<BR>The twenty-seventh consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, corresponding to the letter R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र<BR>m. (रः)<BR>1 Fire or Agni.<BR>2 Heat, warmth.<BR>3 Burning, scorching.<BR>4 Love, desire.<BR>5 Speed.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Giving.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>f. (री)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give, रम to play, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहति|रंहतिः
रंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Speed, velocity, in general, or the speed of a chariot.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, क्तिन् aff., हुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहस्
रंहस्<BR>n. (-हः)<BR>Speed, velocity.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, हुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक|रकः
रक<BR>r. 10th cl. (राकयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक|रकः
रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The sun gem.<BR>2 Crystal.<BR>3 A hard shower.<BR>E.<BR>रक to obtain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्त|रक्तं|रक्तः
रक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Dyed, tinged, coloured, stained.<BR>2 Red, of a red colour.<BR>3 Fond of, attached to, affected with love or interest towards any object.<BR>4 Pure, purified.<BR>5 Sporting, engaging in play or pastime.<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>Red, the colour.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>3 Copper.<BR>4 Minium.<BR>5 Vermilion.<BR>6 The fruit of the Flacourtia cataphracta.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>1 The Gunja plant, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>2 Lac.<BR>3 Bengal madder.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour or dye, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तक|रक्तकः
रक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant bearing a red blossom, (Pentapetes phoenicea; it is also applied to the Ixora bandhuca.)<BR>2 Globe amaranth, (Gomphræna globosa, the red variety.)<BR>3 Red garments or cloth.<BR>4 A man affected with passion or fondness.<BR>5 A gamboller, a player, one who plays or sports.<BR>6 Safflower.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्द|रक्तकंद|रक्तकन्दः
रक्तकन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 Coral.<BR>2 A sort of onion.<BR>3 A kind of yam (Dioscorea purpurea?)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्दल|रक्तकंदल|रक्तकन्दलः
रक्तकन्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, कन्द, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकमल|रक्तकमलं
रक्तकमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and कमल the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकाञ्चन|रक्तकाञ्चनः
रक्तकाञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and काञ्चन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकुमुद|रक्तकुमुदं
रक्तकुमुद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and कुमुद the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकैरव|रक्तकैरवं|रक्तकैरवः
रक्तकैरव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and कैरव a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकोकनद|रक्तकोकनदं|रक्तकोकनदः
रक्तकोकनद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and कोकनद a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तगुल्म|रक्तगुल्मः
रक्तगुल्म<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>1 A disease, a hard lump in the abdomen of the female after conception, perhaps scirrhus of the ovarium.<BR>2 A clot of blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and गुल्म cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तघ्न|रक्तघ्नः
रक्तघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A small tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A kind of grass, a variety of the Dūb grass.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, and घ्न removing; anti-plethoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तचन्दन|रक्तचंदन|रक्तचन्दनं
रक्तचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Red wood, either red Sandal or sappan wood.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तचूर्ण|रक्तचूर्णं
रक्तचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 Red lead.<BR>2 Any red powder.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, चूर्ण powder, dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तजन्तुक|रक्तजन्तुकः
रक्तजन्तुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An earthworm.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and जन्तु an insect, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तजिह्व|रक्तजिह्वः
रक्तजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ततुण्ड|रक्ततुंड|रक्ततुण्डः
रक्ततुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and तुण्ड a beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तत्व
रक्तत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Redness.<BR>2 Passion, affection.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to रक्त; also with तल्, रक्तता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तदन्ती
रक्तदन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, दन्त a tooth, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तदृश्
रक्तदृश्<BR>mfn. (-दृक्)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-दृक्)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तधातु|रक्तधातुः
रक्तधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Red chalk or red orpiment.<BR>2 Copper.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तनयन
रक्तनयन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and नयन the eye, red-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तनासिक|रक्तनासिकः
रक्तनासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तप|रक्तपः
रक्तप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Who or what drinks blood.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An imp, a goblin.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 A leech.<BR>2 A female goblin.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, and प what drinks, from पा with क aff. and टाप् for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपक्ष|रक्तपक्षः
रक्तपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पक्ष wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपदी
रक्तपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A plant, variously considered as a sort of sensitive plant or a species of Lycopodium.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, पद foot or root, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपात|रक्तपातः
रक्तपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Spilling of blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त and पात causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपाता
रक्तपाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, and पात nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपाद|रक्तपादः
रक्तपाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Red-footed.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पाद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपायिन्
रक्तपायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A bug.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, and पायिन् what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=690" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपारद|रक्तपारदं|रक्तपारदः
रक्तपारद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Native vermilion, cinnabar.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पारद quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपिण्ड|रक्तपिंड|रक्तपिण्डं
रक्तपिण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The China rose, (Hibiscus rosa sinensis.)<BR>2 A climbing plant, (Ventilago madraspatana.)<BR>3 A spontaneous discharge of blood from the nose and mouth.<BR>4 A red pimple or boil.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पिण्ड lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपित्त|रक्तपित्तं
रक्तपित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>Plethora, spontaneous hæmorrhages from the mouth, nose, rectum and cuticle, accompanied with fever and headache, vomiting, purging, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पित्त bile, the bile being of that colour; or रक्त blood, and पित्त bile, it being supposed to be an affection of both fluids or humors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपित्तहा
रक्तपित्तहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Variety of bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्तपित्त the disease, and हा what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपुष्प|रक्तपुष्पः
रक्तपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 Nerium odorum, the red variety.<BR>2 A small tree, (Andersonia rohitaca, Rox.)<BR>mf. (-ष्पः-ष्पा)<BR>The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>1 The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR>2 Bryony, (Bryonia grandis.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and पुष्प flower, whence it may be applied to any plant bearing red blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपुष्पक|रक्तपुष्पकः
रक्तपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>2 A small tree, (Andersonia rohitaca, Rox.)<BR>3 A red flower, (Ixora bandhuca, or Pentapetes phoenicea.)<BR>4 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>5 The coral tree.<BR>6 A tree from which a red dye is prepared, (Rottleria tinctorea.)<BR>f. (-ष्पिका)<BR>A sort of sensitive plant or species of Lycopodium.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तफल|रक्तफलः
रक्तफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तफेनज|रक्तफेनजः
रक्तफेनज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A part of the body, apparently intending the lungs.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, फेन froth or phlegm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तबालुक
रक्तबालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमञ्जर|रक्तमञ्जरः
रक्तमञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, मञ्जरी a pedicle, aff. टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमण्डल
रक्तमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमय
रक्तमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Bloody, full or consisting of blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमोक्षण|रक्तमोक्षणं
रक्तमोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Bleeding, letting blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and मोक्षण loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तयष्टि|रक्तयष्टिः
रक्तयष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तरेणु|रक्तरेणुः
रक्तरेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 Red lead.<BR>2 The blossom of the Palāśa, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>3 A sort of cloth.<BR>4 An angry man.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and रेणु dust; also with कन् added in the second meaning रक्तरेणुका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तलोचन|रक्तलोचनः
रक्तलोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A pigeon.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवटी
रक्तवटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Small pox.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and वटी a pustule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवरटी
रक्तवरटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>Small pox.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, वरटी a pustule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवर्ण|रक्तवर्णः
रक्तवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Red, of a red colour.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 An earthworm.<BR>2 Red, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवर्द्धन
रक्तवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवसन|रक्तवसनः
रक्तवसन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dressed in red.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The mendicant, or Brahman of the fourth order, especially as occasionally clad in red garments.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and वसन vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवाहिन्
रक्तवाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Conveying blood, (as an artery.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and वाहिन् what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तविद्रधि|रक्तविद्रधिः
रक्तविद्रधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A sore or ulcer from a vitiated state of blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and विद्रधि a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तविन्दु
रक्तविन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A red spot forming a flaw in a gem.<BR>2 A drop of blood.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त fed, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवीज|रक्तवीजः
रक्तवीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The pomegranate.<BR>2 The name of a demon killed by DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and वीज the seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवृन्ता
रक्तवृन्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and वृन्त a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशालि|रक्तशालिः
रक्तशालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A red variety of rice, (Oriza sativa.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशासन|रक्तशासनं
रक्तशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and साशन an edict; from the document perhaps being sealed or signed with a preparation of this substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तश्राव
रक्तश्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Venesection, bleeding.<BR>2 A kind of dock or sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and श्राव causing to flow; also रक्तश्रावणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसंकोच
रक्तसंकोच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Safflower.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, (a dye,) सङ्कोच a contracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसङ्कोचक|रक्तसंकोचक
रक्तसङ्कोचक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसंज्ञ
रक्तसंज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red or blood, and संज्ञा appellation; also similar compounds, as रक्तनामन्, रक्तनामक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसन्ध्याक
रक्तसन्ध्याक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra.).<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, सन्ध्या twilight, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसरोरुह|रक्तसरोरुहं
रक्तसरोरुह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and सरोरुह a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसौगन्धिक|रक्तसौगन्धिकं
रक्तसौगन्धिक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A kind of dock or sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, &c., and सौगन्धिक a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तहंसा
रक्तहंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs or female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तहीन
रक्तहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bloodless, cold-blooded.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताक्त|रक्ताक्तं
रक्ताक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Sprinkled with blood.<BR>2 Dyed red.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Red wood, (Pterocarpus santolinus; applied also to the Cæsalpinia sappan.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and आक्त sprinkled, spread<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताक्ष|रक्ताक्षः
रक्ताक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>2 A pigeon.<BR>3 The Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa.)<BR>4 A tyrant, a savage, a barbarous or cruel man.<BR>5 The Indian crane.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and अक्षि the eye, aff. ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताङ्ग|रक्तांग|रक्ताङ्गं|रक्ताङ्गः
रक्ताङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The planet MARS.<BR>2 A plant, (a species of Crinum.)<BR>3 A bug.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Coral.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तातीसार|रक्तातीसारः
रक्तातीसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Dysentery.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and अतीसार diarrhoea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताधार|रक्ताधारः
रक्ताधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The skin.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त blood, आघार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताधिमन्थ|रक्ताधिमन्थः
रक्ताधिमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>Inflammation of the eyes, ophthalmia with sponginess of the vessels so as to discharge blood on being touched.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and अधिमन्थ ophthalmia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताभिष्यन्द
रक्ताभिष्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Redness of the vessels of the eye with flow of tears.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and अभिष्यन्द flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताम्बर|रक्तांबर|रक्ताम्बरं|रक्ताम्बरः
रक्ताम्बर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Dressed in red.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Any vagrant devotee, wearing red garments.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताम्लान|रक्ताम्लानः
रक्ताम्लान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Globe amaranth, the red variety.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and अम्लान amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तालु|रक्तालुः
रक्तालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A sort of yam, (Dioscorea purpurea.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, and आलु yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=691" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तावसेचन
रक्तावसेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Letting blood, bleeding.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and अवसेचन sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताशय|रक्ताशयः
रक्ताशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Viscus in which the blood is contained or secreted, viz. the heart, the liver, and the spleen.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and आशय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ति|रक्तिः
रक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Affection, attachment.<BR>2 Addiction to.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to be affected, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तिका
रक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Abrus precatorius).<BR>2 The seed of the Abrus precatorius used as a weight, or a fictitious weight, denominated from the seeds originally so used; the seed weighs about 1 and (5/16) troy grain, the artificial ratti or Raktikā should be double that weight, but in common use it averages nearly 2 grains and a quarter.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तेक्षण
रक्तेक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Red-eyed, having the eyes inflamed or blood-shot.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त, and ईक्षण the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोत्पल|रक्तोत्पलं|रक्तोत्पलः
रक्तोत्पल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra.)<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, उत्पल lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोत्पलाभ|रक्तोत्पलाभः
रक्तोत्पलाभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Red.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Redness, red, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>रक्तोत्पल the red lotus, आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोपल|रक्तोपलं
रक्तोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Indurated ochre, or clay iron stone.<BR>E.<BR>रक्त red, उपला a stone, hence applied also to red ochre, red orpiment, red chalk, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष|रक्षः
रक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (रक्षति)<BR>To guard, to protect, to cherish, to preserve.<BR>With परि,<BR>To save from ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष|रक्षः
रक्ष<BR>mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)<BR>1 Preserving, protecting.<BR>2 Lac.<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Ashes.<BR>2 A sort of bracelet, a twist of thread or tinsel, with a small packet containing a few carminative seeds, bound round the wrist at particular periods, especially the day of full moon in Śrāvaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षःसभ|रक्षःसभं
रक्षःसभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A multitude or assemblage of goblins.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षस् a demon, and सभा assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षक|रक्षकः
रक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what protects, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A guardian, a protector.<BR>2 A watch, a guard.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षण|रक्षणं|रक्षणः
रक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Preserving, protecting, defending.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणीय
रक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be guarded, preserved, protected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणीरक|रक्षणीरकः
रक्षणीरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Urinary affection, as gonorrhoea, &c. elsewhere read रक्षणारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षत्
रक्षत्<BR>mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्)<BR>Preserving, guarding, protecting.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्
रक्षस्<BR>n. (-क्षः)<BR>A Rakṣas, an evil spirit, apparently distinguishable into three classes: one sort of Rakṣas is of a demi-celestial nature, and is ranked with the attendants on KUVERA; another corresponds to a goblin, an imp, or ogre, haunting cemeteries, animating dead bodies, disturbing sacrifices, and ensnaring and devouring human beings; the third kind approaches more to the nature of the Titan, or relentless and powerful enemy of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, (KUVERA'S treasures, &c.) असुन् aff.; also राक्षम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्पाश
रक्षस्पाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A contemptible Rakṣas<BR>E.<BR>रक्षस्, and पाश aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षाधिकृत|रक्षाधिकृतः
रक्षाधिकृत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A governor, a magistrate.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षा, and अधिकृत set over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षापेक्षक|रक्षापेक्षकः
रक्षापेक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A door-keeper or porter.<BR>2 A guard of the women's apartments.<BR>3 A catamite.<BR>4 An actor, a mime.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष preserving, अप before ईक्ष to see, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षित|रक्षितं
रक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Preserved, protected, defended.<BR>2 Kept, detained.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितव्य
रक्षितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be guarded, protected, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितृ
रक्षितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what protects, defends, &c., a protector, a guard.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिन्
रक्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>Who or what preserves or protects.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिवर्ग|रक्षिवर्गः
रक्षिवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A guard, a sentinel.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षि from रक्षिन् a preserver, and वर्ग class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोगण
रक्षोगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A class or troop of evil spirits.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षस्, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोघ्न|रक्षोघ्नं|रक्षोघ्नः
रक्षोघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Marking-nut plant.<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>1 Sour gruel made from the fermentation of rice water.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षम् a goblin, and घ्न destroying, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोजननी
रक्षोजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>रक्षम् a sprite, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्ण|रक्ष्णः
रक्ष्ण<BR>m. (-क्ष्णः)<BR>Preserving, guarding, defence, protection.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, aff. नङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्य
रक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>To be guarded, protected, preserved, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्यमाण
रक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Preserved.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रख
रख<BR>r. 1st cl. (रखति) also (इ) रखि r. 1st cl. (रंखति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रग
रग<BR>r. 1st cl. (ए) (रगे) (रगति)<BR>To suspect, to doubt, to fear.<BR>r. 10th cl. (रागयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR>(इ) रगि r. 1st cl. (रंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघ
रघ<BR>(इ) रघि r. 1st cl. (रंघते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (रंघयति)<BR>To shine;<BR>also without the indicatory letter, r. 10th cl. (राघयति)<BR>To taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघु|रघुः
रघु<BR>m. (-घुः)<BR>1 The name of a sovereign of Oude, the great grandfather of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>2 The family or descendants of RAGHU.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to shine, कु Uṇādi aff., ल changed to र, and the nasal augment rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुकार|रघुकारः
रघुकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The poet KĀLIDĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the race of RAGHU, which forms the subject of a poem by this writer, and कार author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनन्दन|रघुनन्दनः
रघुनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>RĀMA, the second incarnation of VIṢṆU, under that appellation.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the king RAGHU, and नन्दन a son or descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनाथ|रघुनाथः
रघुनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the race of RAGHU, and नाथ lord, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवंश|रघुवंशः
रघुवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The race or family of RAGHU; hence also the name of a poem by KĀLIDĀSA, which treats of the ancestors of RĀMA, from DILĪPA to that prince, and his descendants to AGNIVARṆA; nearly one half relates to the history of RAGHU and as much to that of RĀMA, the remainder is occupied with the remaining princes.<BR>E.<BR>रघु as above, and वंश race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवर|रघुवरः
रघुवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the race of RAGHU, and वर eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=692" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघूद्वह|रघूद्वहः
रघूद्वह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the race of RAGHU, and उद्वह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क|रंक|रङ्कः
रङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>1 Niggardly, avaricious, a miser.<BR>2 Slow, dull.<BR>E.<BR>रकि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्कु|रंकु|रंकुः|रङ्कुः
रङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>A sort of deer, (the spotted axis.)<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. कु, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग|रंग|रङ्गं|रंगः|रङ्गः
रङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Paint, colour, tint, dye.<BR>2 Dancing, acting, singing, &c.<BR>3 A field of battle.<BR>4 The place where acting, &c. is exhibited, a stage.<BR>5 A place answering to an amphitheatre.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Tin.<BR>E.<BR>रगि to go, aff. अच्, or रञ्ज to colour, aff. घञ्, the final changed and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गज|रंगज|रङ्गजं
रङ्गज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गजीवक|रंगजीवक|रङ्गजीवकः
रङ्गजीवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग a stage or colour, &c., and जीवक who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गभूति|रंगभूति|रङ्गभूतिः
रङ्गभूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Aśvin, (September-October,) on the night of which LAKṢMĪ descended, promising wealth to all who were awake.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग dancing and singing, and भूति being, the night being spent in playing ancient chess, in Nāces, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गभूमि|रंगभूमि|रङ्गभूमिः
रङ्गभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 A field of battle.<BR>2 A stage, a theatre, a place where dancing is exhibited, or the Indian dramas were represented.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग dancing, &c., and भूमि ground, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमल्ली
रङ्गमल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A lute.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग singing, &c., मल्ल to hold, affs. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृ|रंगमातृ
रङ्गमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A bawd.<BR>2 Lac, the animal dye.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग passion or colour, &c., and मातृ parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृका
रङ्गमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Lac, or the insect which forms the red dye so called.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, and मातृ parent, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गलासिनी
रङ्गलासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, (of the stalk,) लस to shine, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गवीज
रङ्गवीज<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग tin, वीज seed or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गशाला|रंगशाला
रङ्गशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A hall for public exhibitions, as Nāces, plays, &c., a ball-room, a theatre.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग acting, &c., and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गाजीव|रंगाजीव|रङ्गाजीवः
रङ्गाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A painter.<BR>2 An actor, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, &c., and जाजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गावतरण|रंगावतरण
रङ्गावतरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Acting, playing, exhibiting in public.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग, and अवतरण alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गावतारक|रङ्गावतारकः
रङ्गावतारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An actor, a buffoon.<BR>2 A boxer.<BR>3 A bard or panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग acting, dancing, अव depreciative prefix, तॄ to pass, वुन् aff.; also with णिनि aff., रङ्गावतारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गिन्|रंगिन्
रङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Colouring, dying.<BR>2 Impassioned, having propensity or passion.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus).<BR>E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्घस्|रंघस्
रङ्घस्<BR>n. (-ङ्घः)<BR>Speed, velocity: see रंहस; ह being changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रच
रच<BR>r. 10th cl. (रचयति)<BR>1 To make mechanically, to work, to manufacture.<BR>2 To write, to compose, to make as a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचक
रचक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A maker, a composer.<BR>E.<BR>रच to make, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचना
रचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Orderly and becoming arrangement or disposition in general.<BR>2 Decoration or dressing of the hair.<BR>3 Stringing flowers, &c., weaving wreaths, chaplets, or similar decorations.<BR>4 Military array, the arrangement of troops.<BR>5 Literary composition, whether in verse or prose.<BR>6 Suspending garlands, &c. at the doors of a house or building on festival occasions.<BR>7 Making or preparing any thing.<BR>E.<BR>रच to make, to manufacture, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचित|रचितः
रचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made, manufactured.<BR>2 Written, composed.<BR>3 Strung.<BR>E.<BR>रच to make, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज|रजं|रजः
रज<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>1 Dust.<BR>2 The pollen of flowers.<BR>3 The menstrual excretion.<BR>4 The second property of humanity, the quality of passion.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, &c., aff. अच्, and the nasal rejected; this word more commonly occurs रजस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजःशय|रजःशयः
रजःशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रजम् dust, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजःसारथि|रजःसारथिः
रजःसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् dust, and सारथि charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजक|रजकः
रजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A washerman.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A washerman's wife or a washerwoman.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, (clothes,) ष्वुन् or क्वुन् aff.; in the latter case the fem. is रजिका a washerwoman, and रजकी a washerman's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजत|रजतं
रजत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A necklace.<BR>2 Silver.<BR>3 Gold.<BR>4 Elephant's teeth, ivory.<BR>5 The name of a lake.<BR>6 The name of a mountain, perhaps Kailāsa: see रजताद्रि.<BR>7 White, (the colour.)<BR>8 Blood.<BR>9 An asterism, a constellation.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, &c., अतच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजतद्युति|रजतद्युतिः
रजतद्युति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>रजत silver, and द्युति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजतप्रस्थ|रजतप्रस्थः
रजतप्रस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>Mount Kailāsa, the residence of KUVERA and his attendant demigods.<BR>E.<BR>रजत white, (or silver,) and प्रस्थ table land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजताद्रि|रजताद्रिः
रजताद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>Mount Kailāsa: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>रजत silver, and अद्रि mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजन|रजनं|रजनः
रजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Colouring, dyeing, painting.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, Uṇādi aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनि|रजनिः
रजनि<BR>f. (-निः-नी)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The indigo plant.<BR>3 Turmerick.<BR>4 Lac.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, अनि Uṇādi aff., and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिकर|रजनिकरः
रजनिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रजनि, and कर who makes; also रजनीकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिचर|रजनिचरः
रजनिचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A goblin.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>रजनि, and चर who goes; also रजनीचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीकर|रजनीकरः
रजनीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीगन्ध
रजनीगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The tuberose, (Polianthes tuberosa.)<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and गन्ध smell, emitting a powerful smell after sun-set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीचर|रजनीचरः
रजनीचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A Rākṣasa, a fiend, a goblin, a ghost.<BR>2 A watchman.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीजल|रजनीजलं
रजनीजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Frost, hoar frost, dew.<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and जल water, falling at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीमुख|रजनीमुखं
रजनीमुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Evening, beginning of the night.<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and मुख commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीहासा
रजनीहासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes arbor tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>रजनी night, and हास a smile; the flowers blossoming at night, and diffusing a powerful scent after sun-set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्
रजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>1 The second condition of humanity, the quality or property of passion; that which produces sensual desire, worldly coveting, pride, and falsehood, and is the cause of pain.<BR>2 Dust.<BR>3 The dust or pollen of a flower.<BR>4 The menstrual evacuation.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, to be attached to, Uṇādi aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=693" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजसानु|रजसानुः
रजसानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 The heart or mind.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, to feel affection for, and सानु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्वल|रजस्वलः
रजस्वल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् dust, &c., and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजित
रजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Affected, moved, attracted, or excited by.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to affect, causal v., and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोबन्ध|रजोबंध|रजोबन्धः
रजोबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Suppression of menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>रजस्, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोबल|रजोबलं
रजोबल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् dust, बल heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोरस|रजोरसं|रजोरसः
रजोरस<BR>m. (-सं)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् dust, and रस essence, or perhaps this and the preceding should be the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोहर|रजोहरः
रजोहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् dust, dirt, and हर who removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जु|रज्जुः
रज्जु<BR>m. (-ज्जुः)<BR>1 A rope, a cord, a tie, a string.<BR>2 A lock of braided hair.<BR>E.<BR>सृज to create, &c. Uṇādi aff. उ, and the radical स rejected, and the vowel changed to its semivowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जुदालक|रज्जुदालकः
रज्जुदालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Wild fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्ज
रञ्ज<BR>(औ) r. 1st cl. औरञ्ज (रजति-ते) 4th cl. (रज्यति-ते)<BR>To dye, to tinge, to give tint or colour to any thing.<BR>r. 1st cl. (रजति)<BR>To be attached to or intent on, to have one's affections or passions engaged by any object.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>To be fond of or attached to.<BR>With अप and वि,<BR>To be averse, to dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जक|रंजक|रञ्जकं|रञ्जकः
रञ्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 What incites or affects.<BR>2 What colours, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Colouring, dyeing.<BR>2 A colorist, a painter.<BR>3 A dyer.<BR>4 A stimulus, an inciter of affection, &c.<BR>5 Biliary humour on which vision depends.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, वुन aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जन|रंजन|रञ्जनं|रञ्जनः
रञ्जन<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 Colouring, dyeing, painting, &c.<BR>2 Affecting the heart, exciting passion, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Red Sandal or Sappan wood.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>2 Bengal madder.<BR>3 Another plant, commonly Śuṇḍārocanī, (a species of Crinum?)<BR>4 A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जित|रंजित
रञ्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Moved or affected.<BR>2 Coloured, dyed, tinted.<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रट
रट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (रटति रटयति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटत्
रटत्<BR>mfn. (-टन्-टन्ती-टत्)<BR>Speaking.<BR>E.<BR>रट to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन|रटनं
रटन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Speaking.<BR>E.<BR>रट, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन्ती|रटंती
रटन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>The fourteenth of the dark half of Māgha, when bathing is enjoined.<BR>E.<BR>रट to speak, झच्^1. aff., the waters speak.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312. note: There is a जश् affix, but I think झच् is meant here.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटित|रटितं
रटित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken, said.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The roaring of flame.<BR>E.<BR>रट to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रठ
रठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (रठति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण|रणं|रणः
रण<BR>r. 1st cl. (रणति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण|रणं|रणः
रण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>War, battle.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>2 The quill or bow of a lute, &c.<BR>3 Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>रण to sound, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणकामिन्
रणकामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Desirous of war, wishing to fight<BR>E.<BR>रण, and कामिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणत्
रणत्<BR>mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>1 Warring, fighting.<BR>2 Going.<BR>3 Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>रण to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणतूर्य्य|रणतूर्य|रणतूर्य्यं
रणतूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A military drum.<BR>E.<BR>रण war, and तूर्य्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणपण्डित|रणपण्डितः
रणपण्डित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A warrior.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and पण्डित learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणप्रिय|रणप्रियं|रणप्रियः
रणप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Warlike.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>रण, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणमत्त|रणमत्तः
रणमत्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>रण war, and मत्त mad, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरङ्क|रणरंक|रणरङ्कः
रणरङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The part of an elephant's face between his tusks.<BR>E.<BR>रण war, and रङ्क slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरण|रणरणं|रणरणः
रणरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Regret, anxiety, anxious regret, sorrow, of which the object is lost or absent.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A musquito, a gnat.<BR>E.<BR>रण war, and noise, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरणक|रणरणकः
रणरणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Anxiety, regret: see the last.<BR>2 Love, desire.<BR>E.<BR>रण to sound, repeated, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणसङ्कुल|रणसंकुल|रणसङ्कुलं
रणसङ्कुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Mixed or tumultuary combat.<BR>E.<BR>रण war, संकुल a mingling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणस्तम्भ|रणस्तंभ|रणस्तम्भः
रणस्तम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A trophy, a pillar.<BR>2 A country, Chitore.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and स्तम्भ a pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाङ्गण|रणांगण
रणाङ्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A field of battle.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and अङ्गण a court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाजिर
रणाजिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A field of battle.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and अजिर a court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाभियोग|रणाभियोगः
रणाभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Engaging in battle.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and अभियोग encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणित|रणितं
रणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sounded, made as a noise.<BR>2 Warred.<BR>E.<BR>रण to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणोत्साह|रणोत्साहः
रणोत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Prowess.<BR>E.<BR>रण, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डक|रंडकः|रण्डकः
रण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barren tree.<BR>E.<BR>रण्डा a widow, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डा
रण्डा<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>2 A widow.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, ड Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत|रतं
रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Occupied or engaged by, actively intent on.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Coition, copulation.<BR>2 A privity, a private part.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतकील|रतकीलः
रतकील<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and कील a pin, a fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतकूजित|रतकूजितं
रतकूजित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Lascivious murmur.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and कूजित murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतगुरु|रतगुरुः
रतगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and गुरु teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतज्वर|रतज्वरः
रतज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>रत coition, ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रततालिन्
रततालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A libertine, a lecher, a whoremonger.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, तल to complete, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतताली
रतताली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, तल to complete or effect, and अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतनारीच|रतनारीचः
रतनारीच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 KĀMA or love.<BR>3 Sonitus in coitu.<BR>4 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>E.<BR>रत coition, नारी a female, चि to collect, or चर to go, aff. क or ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतनिधि|रतनिधिः
रतनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A wagtail.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतर्द्धिक
रतर्द्धिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A day.<BR>2 Bathing for pleasure.<BR>3 The aggregate of four auspicious objects, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, ऋधि increase, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतव्रण|रतव्रणः
रतव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतशायिन्
रतशायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and शायिन् who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतहिण्डक|रतहिण्डकः
रतहिण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>2 A ravisher, one who carries off and violates a woman.<BR>E.<BR>रत coition, हिडि to go, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतान्दुक|रतान्दुकः
रतान्दुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, and अन्दुक a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतान्ध्री
रतान्ध्री<BR>f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>Fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतामर्द्ध
रतामर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रत coition, आङ् before मृध to rub, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=694" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतायनी
रतायनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, अयन a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतार्थिन्
रतार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Libidinous, lascivious.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A libidinous woman, a wanton harlot.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, अथ seeking, soliciting, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रति|रतिः
रति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Passion, desire.<BR>2 Coition, copulation.<BR>3 A privity, a private part.<BR>4 The wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिकुहर|रतिकुहरं
रतिकुहर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>रति copulation, and कुहर a cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिक्रिया
रतिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>रति the same, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिगृह|रतिगृहं
रतिगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The vagina.<BR>E.<BR>रति, and गृह abode, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिपति|रतिपतिः
रतिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The deity of love, KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>रति the wife of the god, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिप्रिय|रतिप्रियः
रतिप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>रति the wife of the deity, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिमदा
रतिमदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E.<BR>रति copulation, मद to delight, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिमन्दिर|रतिमंदिर|रतिमन्दिरं
रतिमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Pudendum muliebre.<BR>E.<BR>रति copulation, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिरमण|रतिरमणः
रतिरमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR>E.<BR>रति the goddess so named, and रसण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिलक्ष|रतिलक्षं
रतिलक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>Copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिसत्वरा
रतिसत्वरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>रति copulation, सत्वर quick; perhaps considered as an aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतू
रतू<BR>f. (-तूः)<BR>1 The Ganges of heaven.<BR>2 An honest woman, one who speaks the truth.<BR>E.<BR>ऋत a Sautra root, कू Uṇādi aff., and अम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतोद्वह|रतोद्वहः
रतोद्वह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Koil or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>रत copulation, उद्वह exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्न|रत्नं
रत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>1 A jewel, a gem.<BR>2 Any thing the best of its kind, or figuratively, the jewel of the species.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, Uṇādi aff. न, and त substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नकन्दल|रत्नकंदल|रत्नकन्दलः
रत्नकन्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and कन्दल a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नकूट|रत्नकूटः
रत्नकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A mountain in the Dekshin.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नगर्भ|रत्नगर्भः
रत्नगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 The god of wealth, KUVERA.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नप्रभा
रत्नप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The first of the seven hells or purgatories, according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and प्रभा splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नमय
रत्नमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Gemmed, full or made of gems.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नमुख्य|रत्नमुख्यं
रत्नमुख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>The diamond.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and मुख्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवत्|रत्नवन्त्
रत्नवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having gems.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवर्षुक|रत्नवर्षुकं
रत्नवर्षुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The carriage of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and वर्षुक showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवृक्ष
रत्नवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसानु|रत्नसानुः
रत्नसानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The mountain Meru.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and सानु ridge of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसू
रत्नसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and सू a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाकर|रत्नाकरः
रत्नाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A jewel mine.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाङ्क|रत्नाङ्कः
रत्नाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The car of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न a jewel, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नावलि
रत्नावलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A necklace of gems.<BR>E.<BR>रत्न, and आवलि a row; also रत्नावली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नि|रत्निः
रत्नि<BR>mf. (-त्निः-त्नी)<BR>1 A sort of cubit, measured from the elbow to the end of the closed fist; it is also computed at twenty-one breadths of the middle of the thumb.<BR>2 The closed hand, the fist.<BR>E.<BR>ऋ to go, कत्निच् aff., the vowel changed to the semivowel, otherwise अरत्नि, and as derived from सृ to go, सरत्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्यङ्ग|रत्यंग|रत्यङ्गं
रत्यङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The male or female organ.<BR>E.<BR>रति copulation, अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ|रथः
रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A car, a war-chariot.<BR>2 A car, a carriage in general, any vehicle or mode of conveyance.<BR>3 A limb, a member.<BR>4 The body.<BR>5 A foot.<BR>6. A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, Uṇādi aff. क्थन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकट्या
रथकट्या<BR>f. (-ट्या)<BR>A multitude of cars.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and कट्यच् aff. of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकर|रथकरः
रथकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and कर who makes; also रथकार and रथकृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकार|रथकारः
रथकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A carpenter.<BR>2 A man sprung from the male of the Māhiṣya, and woman of the Keren or writer caste; by profession, a maker of cars, a coach-maker.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकुटुम्बिन्|रथकुटुंबिन्
रथकुटुम्बिन्<BR>m. (-म्बी)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and कुटुम्बिन who takes care of as a part of his family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथगर्भक|रथगर्भकः
रथगर्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A car or litter borne on men's shoulders.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, गर्भ an embryo, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथगुप्ति|रथगुप्तिः
रथगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>A piece of wood, or an iron net-work, encompassing a war-chariot, to secure it from being injured by weapons or collision.<BR>E.<BR>रथ car, and गुप्ति screening, preserving; also रथगोपन n. (-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथचरण|रथचरणः
रथचरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and चरण the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथद्रु|रथद्रुः
रथद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>A timber tree, (Dalbergia ougeiniensis.)<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and द्रु the tree, the wood being used for wheels, &c.; also रथद्रुम m. (-मः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथन्तर|रथंतर|रथन्तरः
रथन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The Sāma Veda.<BR>E.<BR>रथ (as by) a car, तॄ to pass (the world), खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथपर्य्याय|रथपर्याय|रथपर्य्यायः
रथपर्य्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of cane, the ratan.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and पर्य्याय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथपाद|रथपादः
रथपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A wheel.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and पाद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथप्सा
रथप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथयात्रा
रथयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A festival at which the chariots of the gods go in procession: in Bengal and Orissa it is applied to the procession of the car of KṚṢṆA, as JAGANNĀTHA, on the second of the light fortnight of Āṣārha.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथवाहक
रथवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A charioteer.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and वाहक what conveys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाङ्ग|रथांग|रथाङ्गं|रथाङ्गः
रथाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A wheel.<BR>2 Any part of a carriage.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The ruddy goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाङ्गपाणि|रथाङ्गपाणिः
रथाङ्गपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>रथाङ्ग a wheel, (the discus with which one of his, hands is armed,) and पाणि the hand; also रथाङ्गिन् and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=695" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाभ्र|रथाभ्रः
रथाभ्र<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>रथ the same, and अभ्र a cloud or water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाभ्रपुष्प|रथाभ्रपुष्पः
रथाभ्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A sort of reed: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>रथाभ्र the same, and पुष्प a flower; also रथ, रथाभ्र, and अभ्रपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारूढ
रथारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Mounted on or riding in a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारोहण
रथारोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Riding in a car.<BR>2 Fighting in a warchariot.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and आरोहण mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारोहिन्
रथारोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Riding in a car.<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A warrior who fights in a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and आरोहिन् who mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथार्भक
रथार्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and अर्भक small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथावरोहण
रथावरोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Alighting from a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and अवरोहण descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथावरोहिन्
रथावरोहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Descending from a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and अवरोहिन् who descends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिक|रथिकः
रथिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The owner of a car, or one who rides in it.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and ष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन्
रथिन्<BR>m. (-थी)<BR>1 A warrior who fights in a car.<BR>2 The owner of or rider in a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन|रथिनः
रथिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The master of a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and इन a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिर|रथिरः
रथिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The owner of or rider in a car.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, and इरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथोपस्थ|रथोपस्थः
रथोपस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>The charioteer's seat for driving.<BR>E.<BR>रथ, उप near, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ्य|रथ्यः
रथ्य<BR>m. (-थ्यः)<BR>A car or carriage horse.<BR>f. (-थ्यं)<BR>1 A multitude of cars.<BR>2 A high street.<BR>3 A main or carriage road.<BR>4 A place where several roads meet.<BR>n. (-थ्यं)<BR>A wheel.<BR>E.<BR>रथ a car, and य or यत् affixes of multitude or fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद|रदः
रद<BR>r. 1st cl. (रदति)<BR>1 To divide, to split, to tear or break.<BR>2 To dig, to delve, to root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद|रदः
रद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A tooth.<BR>2 Splitting, tearing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>रद to divide, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदछद|रदच्छद|रदच्छदः
रदछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>रद a tooth, and छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदन|रदनः
रदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tearing, rending.<BR>E.<BR>रद to divide, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदनछद|रदनच्छद|रदनच्छदः
रदनछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>रदन a tooth, and छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदिन्
रदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>रद a tooth, a tusk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्ध
रद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Hurt, injured.<BR>E.<BR>रध to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्धृ
रद्धृ<BR>mfn. (-द्धा-द्धी-द्धृ)<BR>Injurious, hurtful, who or what hurts.<BR>E.<BR>रध to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रध
रध<BR>(ऌ उ) ऌरधु r. 1st cl. (राध्यति)<BR>1 To finish, to complete, to accomplish.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>3 To be right or correct.<BR>4 To cook or mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधित
रधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hurt, injured.<BR>E.<BR>रध to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधितृ
रधितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Injurious, hurtful.<BR>E.<BR>रध to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ति
रन्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Pleasure, sport.<BR>2 Cessation, stop.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तिदेव|रंतिदेव|रंतिदेवः|रन्तिदेवः
रन्तिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A king of the lunar dynasty; also called ŚAŚIDEVA.<BR>3 A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रम, and देव a deity, or who sports or plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तु|रंतुः|रन्तुः
रन्तु<BR>f. (-न्तुः)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 A river.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, &c., aff. तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धक
रन्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Injurious, hurtful.<BR>E.<BR>रध to hurt, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्र|रंध्र|रंध्रं
रन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>1 A hole, a fissure, a cavity, a chasm.<BR>2 A fault, a defect.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. क्विप्, धृ to have or hold, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्रबभ्रु|रंध्रबभ्रु|रन्ध्रबभ्रुः
रन्ध्रबभ्रु<BR>m. (-भ्रुः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>रन्ध्र a hole, and बभ्रु an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप
रप<BR>r. 1st cl. (रपयति)<BR>To speak, to say or tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रफ
रफ<BR>(इ) रफि r. 1st. cl. (रफति रंफति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब|रबः
रब<BR>(इ) रबि r. 1st cl. (रंबते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्ध
रब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Begun.<BR>E.<BR>रभ to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्धृ
रब्धृ<BR>mfn. (-ब्धा-ब्ध्री-ब्धृ)<BR>Beginning, who or what begins.<BR>E.<BR>रभ to begin, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ
रभ<BR>(औ) औरभ r. 1st cl. (रभते) or more usually (आरभते)<BR>To begin, to make a beginning, to begin willingly, &c.<BR>2 To be pleased with.<BR>(इ) रभि r. 1st cl. (रंभते)<BR>To sound.<BR>With परि prefixed,<BR>To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस|रभसः
रभस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 Joy, delight.<BR>3 Consideration of causes and events, or the past and future.<BR>4 Regret, sorrow for something lost or absent.<BR>E.<BR>रभ to begin, असच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम<BR>(औ, उ) औरमु r. 1st cl. (रमते)<BR>To sport or play;<BR>with some prefixes this root forms an active verb, as with आङ्, उप, and वि;<BR>आरमति<BR>to rest, to repose, &c.;<BR>with उप the form is optional, if the sense is intransitive, as<BR>(उपरमति or -ते)<BR>To stop or cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Dear, beloved.<BR>2 Pleasing, delighting, charming.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A husband, a lover.<BR>2 The deity of love, KĀMA.<BR>3 A sort of tree called a red variety of the Aśoka, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A wife, a mistress.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमक|रमकः
रमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lover, a gallant.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमठ|रमठं
रमठ<BR>n. (-ठं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, अठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमठध्वनि|रमठध्वनिः
रमठध्वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण|रमणं|रमणः
रमण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Causing pleasure, pleasing, charming, delightful.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sporting, playing.<BR>2 Dalliance, amorous sport.<BR>3 Coition, copulation.<BR>4 The mons veneris.<BR>5 A sort of cucumber.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of KĀMA or love.<BR>2 A husband.<BR>3 A lover, a gallant.<BR>4 An ass.<BR>f. (-णा or -णी)<BR>1 A woman, or an agreeable woman, a wife, a mistress, &c.<BR>2 A kind of metre, having eleven syllables in the first and third, and twelve in the second and fourth Pādas of every stanza.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, युच् or ल्युट् aff., fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीय|रमणीयं
रमणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>रम to please, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीयता
रमणीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Agreeableness, pleasantness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, रमणीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण्य|रमण्यं
रमण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Sport, pleasure, wanton sport or dalliance.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, अन्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमत्
रमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>Playing, sporting.<BR>E.<BR>रम to play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमति|रमतिः
रमति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A lover, a gallant.<BR>2 Paradise, heaven.<BR>3 A crow.<BR>4 Time.<BR>5 Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport or stop, &c. Uṇādi aff. उति, but the final of the radical retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रममान
रममान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Sporting, playing.<BR>E.<BR>रम to please, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमापति|रमापतिः
रमापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>रमा LAKṢMĪ, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमाप्रिय|रमाप्रियं|रमाप्रियः
रमाप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रमा LAKṢMĪ, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=696" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ|रंभः|रम्भः
रम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 The name of a monkey.<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>1 A plantain.<BR>2 One of the Apsaras or courtezans of Svarga.<BR>3 A harlot, a whore.<BR>4 A name of GAURĪ.<BR>5 Lowing, as of a cow.<BR>E.<BR>रभि to sound, to begin, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भक
रम्भक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Begining, who or what begins.<BR>2 Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>रभि to sound, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भित
रम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Lowing, (of kine.)<BR>E.<BR>रभि to sound, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्य|रम्यः
रम्य<BR>mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>1 Pleasing, delightful, agreeable, charming.<BR>2 Handsome.<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>The champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 The root of a species of cucumber.<BR>2 Semen virile.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्यक|रम्यकं
रम्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 One of the minor Dvīpas or divisions of the world, lying to the north of Ilāvṛta; also called रमणक, and रमण्यक.<BR>2 The root of the Paṭola, a sort of cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>रम्य agreeable, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्यता
रम्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Agreeableness, pleasantness.<BR>2 Gracefulness, beauty.<BR>E.<BR>रम्य with तल् aff.; also with त्व, रम्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्र|रम्रः
रम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>1 Purple, or the colour of the dawn.<BR>2 Beauty, splendor.<BR>E.<BR>रम to please, aff. रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय|रयः
रय<BR>r. 1st cl. (रयते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय|रयः
रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Speed, velocity.<BR>2 The stream or current of a river.<BR>E.<BR>रय to go, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिष्ठ|रयिष्ठः
रयिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Fleetest, very fleet.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 KUVERA.<BR>2 Fire or AGNI.<BR>3 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>रय speed used attributively, quick, and इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रल्लक|रल्लकः
रल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A blanket.<BR>2 An eye-lash.<BR>3 A sort of deer.<BR>E.<BR>रम to please, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् with the final dropped रत् comfort, pleasure, ला to give, aff. क्विप्-रल्ल, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव|रवः
रव<BR>(इ) रवि r. 1st cl. (रम्बति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव|रवः
रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sound in general, cry, noise, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रु to cry out, to sound, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवण|रवणं|रवणः
रवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Sounding, sonorous.<BR>2 Hot, warm.<BR>3 Unsteady, fickle or shaking.<BR>4 Jesting, a jester.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A camel.<BR>2 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Bell-metal.<BR>2 Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>रु to sound, Uṇādi aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवथ|रवथः
रवथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>रु to cry or sound, Uṇādi aff. अथन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवि|रविः
रवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The right canal for the passage of the vital air.<BR>E.<BR>रु to sound, passive form, to be praised or glorified, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविकान्त|रविकांत|रविकान्तः
रविकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The sun-stone, a sort of crystal.<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and कान्त in this compound, a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविनन्दन|रविनन्दनः
रविनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The monkey chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविनाथ|रविनाथं
रविनाथ<BR>n. (-थः)<BR>A lotus.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A flower, (Pentapetes phoenicea.)<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविन्द
रविन्द<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>Lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and दा to give, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविप्रिय|रविप्रियं|रविप्रियः
रविप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 The red lotus.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमण्डल
रविमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The disk of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>रवि, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमार्ग
रविमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>The sun's path.<BR>E.<BR>रवि, and मार्ग road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमार्गभङ्ग
रविमार्गभङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Very high, stopping the course of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>रविमार्ग, and भङ्ग what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविलोह|रविलोहं
रविलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविवार|रविवारः
रविवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sunday.<BR>E.<BR>रवि, and वार a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविसंज्ञक
रविसंज्ञक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>रवि the sun, and संज्ञक^1 appellation.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशना
रशना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The tongue.<BR>2 A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>E.<BR>see रसन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मि|रश्मिः
रश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 A rein.<BR>3 An eye-lash.<BR>E.<BR>अश to pervade, Uṇādi aff. मि, and रश substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मिजाल
रश्मिजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A blaze or stream of light.<BR>E.<BR>रश्मि, and जाल heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस|रसं|रसः
रस<BR>r. 1st cl. (रसति)<BR>To sound.<BR>r. 10th cl. (रसयति)<BR>1 To taste, to relish.<BR>2 To love, to regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस|रसं|रसः
रस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Flavour, taste, as sweet, salt, pungent, bitter, sour, and astringent.<BR>2 Taste, sentiment, emotion, as an object of poetry or composition; eight sentiments are usually enumerated, Śṛṅgāra or love, Hāsya or mirth, Karuṇā or tenderness, Raudra or anger, Vīra or heroism, Bhayānaka or terror, Bībhatsa or disgust, and Adbhuta or surprise: Śānta, tranquillity or content, or Vātsalya, paternal tenderness, is sometimes considered as the ninth.<BR>3 Affection of the mind, passion.<BR>4 Juice, exudation, a fluid, a liquid, or liquified substance.<BR>5 Poison.<BR>6 Semen virile.<BR>7 Water.<BR>8 The primary or essential juice or fluid of the body, whence blood, serum, sweat, &c. are supposed to be engendered; it corresponds best with chyle, but is probably of a fanciful nature.<BR>9 Gum myrrh.<BR>10 Quicksilver, from its being a semi-fluid metal, and according to certain alchymical notions possessed of supernatural power over the juices of the body, &c.<BR>11 A mineral or a metallic salt, as sulphur, borax, talc, blue or green vitriol, &c.; they are however usually called Upa or inferior Rasas.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 The tongue.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Aknadhi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>4 A sort of grain, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>5 The frankincense tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>6 The grape.<BR>7 A medical drug, commonly Kākoli.<BR>E.<BR>रस to taste, to love, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसक|रसकः
रसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Stewed or boiled meat.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकर्प्पूर|रसकर्पूर|रसकर्पूरं
रसकर्प्पूर<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>A white sublimate or a muriate of mercury, made in close vessels with sulphur, mercury, and common salt; the crystals formed in the first operation are sublimed a second time, which seems to be the only essential difference between this and the preparations called Rasapuṣpa; ut infra.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and कर्प्पूर camphor; from its white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकला
रसकला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A low sweet sound.<BR>2 Singing upon intoxication.<BR>E.<BR>रस taste or vinous juice, and कला a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकेसर
रसकेसर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, and केसर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसगन्ध|रसगन्धं|रसगन्धः
रसगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>रस exudation, गन्ध fragrance; also with कन् added, रसगन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसगर्भ|रसगर्भं
रसगर्भ<BR>n. (-र्भं)<BR>1 A mineral preparation used as a stibium.<BR>2 Vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>रस quicksilver, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज|रसजं|रसजः
रसज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced by or in passion, flavour, fluids, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Blood.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Any insect engendered by [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">Page698</a>] the acetous fermentation of liquids.<BR>2 Molasses, treacle.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, the primary juice or chyle, &c., and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=697" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्ञ|रसज्ञः
रसज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Discriminating or acquainted with tastes, sentiments, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>1 A poet, a writer who understands the different Rasas or sentiments to be described.<BR>2 An alchymist, one who has obtained a command over the magical properties of mercury.<BR>3 A physician, a medical preparer and administerer of mercurial and chemical compounds.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>The tongue.<BR>E.<BR>रस as above, and ज्ञ who or what knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्ञता
रसज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Poetical skill or taste.<BR>2 Knowledge of flavours.<BR>3 Alchymy.<BR>E.<BR>रसज्ञ, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रसज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्येष्ठ|रसज्येष्ठः
रसज्येष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 The sweet flavour or taste, sweetness.<BR>2 The sentiment of love.<BR>E.<BR>रस taste or sentiment, and ज्येष्ठ eldest, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसत्
रसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Speaking, sounding.<BR>2 Tasting, having flavour.<BR>E.<BR>रस to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसतेजस्
रसतेजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>The blood.<BR>E.<BR>रस chyle, and तेजस् light, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसधातु|रसधातुः
रसधातु<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>रस fluid, and धातु metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसन|रसनं|रसनः
रसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tasting, taste.<BR>2 Sound, noise.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The tongue.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Rasan.<BR>3 A woman's girdle, a sort of chain worn round the loins.<BR>4 A plant, (Pæderia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>रस to sound or taste, aff. युच्; or अश to eat, युच् Uṇādi aff., and रश substituted; also रशना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनाथ|रसनाथः
रसनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, fluid, and नाथ chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनायक|रसनायकः
रसनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनालिह्
रसनालिह्<BR>m. (-लिट्)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रसना the tongue, and लिह to lick, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनिवृत्ति|रसनिवृत्तिः
रसनिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Loss of taste, flavour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनेत्रिका
रसनेत्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, नेत्र the eye, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसपुष्प
रसपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A preparation of mercury, a kind of muriate formed by subliming in close vessels, a mixture of sulphur, mercury, and common salt.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसफल|रसफलः
रसफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>रस water or juice, and फल the fruit, the nut containing a saccharine fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभङ्ग|रसभंग|रसभङ्गः
रसभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Interruption or destruction of passion or sentiment, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभव|रसभवं
रसभव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The blood.<BR>E.<BR>रस chyle, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभस्मन्
रसभस्मन्<BR>n. (-स्म)<BR>Calx or oxid of mercury.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and भस्मन ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयित्वा
रसयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having tasted.<BR>E.<BR>रस to taste, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसराज|रसराजः
रसराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>रस a mineral, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्|रसवन्त्
रसवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Including a secondary or subsidiary feeling or passion.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्|रसवन्त्
रसवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Juicy.<BR>2 Well-flavoured.<BR>3 Tasteful, applied to a composition, &c.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A kitchen.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, flavour, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसविक्रय|रसविक्रयः
रसविक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Selling juices or liquors, as the juice of the sugar cane, or wine, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसशोधन|रसशोधनं|रसशोधनः
रसशोधन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>रस a metal, &c., and शोधन purifying; being used as a flux in refining and melting metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्ध
रससिद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>An alchymist, an adept: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्धि|रससिद्धिः
रससिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>The knowledge of alchymy, the possession of peculiar familiarity with mercury, obtained by the performance of chemical operations conjoined with certain mystical and magical rites, and the securing thence to the adept, of happiness, health, and wealth, the power of transmuting metals, and the art of prolonging life.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and सिद्धि accomplishment, especially of some supernatural object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसान्तर
रसान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Change or diversion of passion or sentiment.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and अन्तर different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिन्दूर|रससिन्दूरं
रससिन्दूर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of factitious cinnabar, made with zinc, mercury, blue vitriol, and nitre, fused together; the compound is used as an escharotic.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and सिन्दूर minium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसस्थान|रसस्थानं
रसस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cinnabar or vermilion.<BR>E.<BR>रस mercury, and स्थान abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाखन|रसाखनः
रसाखन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>रसा the earth, and खन who digs or picks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाञ्जन|रसाञ्जनं
रसाञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sort of collyrium, prepared either with the calx of brass, or with the Amomum anthorrhiza.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, &c., अञ्जन collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसातल|रसातलं
रसातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Pātāla; the seven infernal regions under the earth, and the residence of the Nāgas, Asuras, Daityas, and other races of monstrous and demoniacal beings, under the various governments of Śeṣa, Bali, and other chiefs: this is not to be confounded with Naraka or Tartarus, the proper hell or abode of guilty mortals after death.<BR>2 The lowest of the seven divisions of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>रसा the earth, and तल below, underneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसादान|रसादानं
रसादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sucking, suction.<BR>2 Drying, drying up, absorbing.<BR>E.<BR>रसा water or juice, &c., आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाधार|रसाधारः
रसाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>रस water, आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाभास|रसाभासः
रसाभास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Concealment of sentiment, attributing evident emotions to some cause different from the real one.<BR>E.<BR>रस sentiment, and आभास unreal exposition or display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाभिनिवेश|रसाभिनिवेशः
रसाभिनिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Accession of sentiment or passion.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and अभिनिवेश intentness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायक|रसायकः
रसायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायन|रसायनं|रसायनः
रसायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Alchymy, chemistry.<BR>2 The employment of mercury in medicine.<BR>3 A medicine preventing old age, and prolonging life, the Elixir Vitœ of the alchymists.<BR>4 Poison.<BR>5 Butter-milk.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 GARUḌA.<BR>2 An anthelmintic drug commonly Vireng, (Embelia ribes?)<BR>3 An alchymist.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A vessel conveying nutrition, a lacteal, an absorbent.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, quicksilver, &c., and अयन a road, a going, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायनफला
रसायनफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>E.<BR>रसायन juice, abiding, and फला fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाल|रसालं|रसालः
रसाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sugar-cane.<BR>2 The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>3 The jack tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>4 The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>5 Wheat.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Frankincense.<BR>2 Gum myrrh.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The tongue.<BR>2 Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>3 A flower, (Hedysarum gangeticum.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">Page699</a>]<BR>4 A grape.<BR>5 Curds mixed up with sugar and spices.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, आङ् before ला to yield, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=698" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालसा
रसालसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A tubular vessel of the body, a nerve, a tendon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालिहा
रसालिहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसास्वादिन्
रसास्वादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Tasting, relishing.<BR>2 Sensitive, having taste.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>रस flavour, and आस्वादिन् who tastes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाह्व|रसाह्वः
रसाह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वः)<BR>Turpentine, resin.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, and आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>1 Flavoured, having taste or flavour.<BR>2 Tasteful, as a composition, &c.<BR>3 Having a taste for poetry, &c.<BR>4 Sentimental.<BR>5 Impassioned.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 A libertine.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Curds with sugar and spice.<BR>2 Molasses, the juice of the sugar-cane.<BR>3 The tongue.<BR>4 A woman's zone or girdle.<BR>E.<BR>रस flavour, sentiment, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gilded, plated, washed or spread with gold, &c.<BR>2 Sounded.<BR>3 Having taste, or flavour, or sentiment.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The rattling of thunder.<BR>2 Voice, sound in general.<BR>3 Wine, vinous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>रस to sound, aff. क्त, or रस fluid, (metal, &c,) and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितवत्
रसितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Tasting, having tasted, or having a taste for.<BR>2 Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>रस to have flavour, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिताशिन्
रसिताशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>1 Eating or seizing with a noise or roar.<BR>2 Drinking wine.<BR>E.<BR>रसित, and आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितृ
रसितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Sounding, making a noise.<BR>2 Tasting, relishing.<BR>E.<BR>रस to sound, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिन्
रसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Tasting.<BR>2 Impassioned.<BR>3 Humorous.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसुन|रसुनः
रसुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Garlick.<BR>E.<BR>see लसुन, र being changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसेन्द्र|रसेंद्र|रसेन्द्रः
रसेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>2 The philosopher's stone, the touch of which turns iron to gold.<BR>E.<BR>रस a mineral, and इन्द्र best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोत्पत्ति|रसोत्पत्तिः
रसोत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Production of taste or flavour.<BR>2 Development of passion or sentiment.<BR>3 Generation of the vital fluids.<BR>E.<BR>रस, and उत्पत्ति production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोन|रसोनः
रसोन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A kind of garlick, (Allium ascalonicum.)<BR>E.<BR>रस flavour, taste, ऊन to be less or deficient, aff. अच्, being supposed to contain in the leaves, stalk, root, &c., every flavour except sourness; also with कन् added, रसोनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोपल|रसोपलं
रसोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>रस water, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्न|रस्नं
रस्न<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Thing, substance.<BR>E.<BR>रस juice, &c., and नक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Juicy.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Blood.<BR>E.<BR>रस chyle, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह|रहः
रह<BR>r. 1st cl. (रहति) r. 10th. cl. (रहयति)<BR>To quit, to leave, to forego, to lose or abandon.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be separate or away from.<BR>(इ) रहि r. 1st cl. (रंहति)<BR>To go, to move with speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह|रहः
रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Solitariness, privacy.<BR>E.<BR>रह to be private, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहण|रहणं
रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Quitting, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>रह to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहत्
रहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>Leaving, abandoning.<BR>E.<BR>रह to leave, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
रहस्<BR>n. subst. (-हः)<BR>1 Solitariness, privacy.<BR>2 Copulation.<BR>3 A privity.<BR>4 A religious or mystic truth.<BR>ind. or n. adv. (-हः)<BR>Solitary, private, in private, secretly, privily.<BR>E.<BR>रह to abandon, (society, &c.,) and असुन् aff., or रम to sport or play, with the same aff., and अह substituted for the radical finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस
रहस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 Heaven.<BR>E.<BR>रह to leave, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्य|रहस्यं
रहस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Private, secret, either fit to be concealed or occurring in secret.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>A secret, a mystery, any thing hidden, recondite or mysterious.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>The name of a river, perhaps the Sarasvatī, from its being supposed to flow in an unknown channel.<BR>E.<BR>रहस् secret, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहाट|रहाटः
रहाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A counsellor, a minister.<BR>2 A ghost, a spirit.<BR>3 Spring.<BR>E.<BR>रह privately, अट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहित|रहितं
रहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left, quitted, abandoned.<BR>2 Free from, devoid of.<BR>E.<BR>रह to leave, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहीभूत
रहीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Alone, solitary, in private.<BR>E.<BR>रह, and भूत been, with च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (राति)<BR>1 To get, to gain, to receive.<BR>2 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Full moon, or the day of full moon.<BR>2 A girl in whom menstruation has commenced.<BR>3 Scab, itch.<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give, (good fortune,) क Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Infernal, demoniacal.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An evil spirit, a demon, a vampire, a fiend, but who appears to be of various descriptions, and is either a powerful Titan or enemy of the gods in a superhuman or incarnate form, as RĀVAṆA and others; an attendant on KUVERA, and guardian of his treasures; or a mischievous and cruel goblin or ogre, haunting cemeteries, animating dead bodies, and devouring human beings.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 A female fiend; the female of the preceding.<BR>2 A large tooth, a tusk.<BR>3 A sort of perfume, commonly Cor.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 A form of marriage, the violent seizure and rape of a girl after the repulse or destruction of her relatives.<BR>2 Surgery, cure by the knife or cautery.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, to be preserved, (from whom,) aff. असुन्, and अण् pleonasm added; or रक्षस् a demon, and अण् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसेन्द्र|राक्षसेन्द्रः
राक्षसेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 The demon RĀVAṆA.<BR>2 KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>राक्षस a demon, and इन्द्र lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Lac, the red animal dye.<BR>E.<BR>रक्ष to preserve, (colour,) अ aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राख
राख<BR>(ऋ) राखृ r. 1st cl. (रालति)<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>2 To adorn.<BR>3 To suffice, to be able or competent.<BR>4 To impede or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राग|रागः
राग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Colour, hue, tint, dye.<BR>2 Affection, prepossession, love, desire.<BR>3 Mental affection in general, as sorrow, joy, &c.<BR>4 Envy, impatience of another's success.<BR>5 A mode of music; of which six are enumerated, viz. Bhairava, Mālava, Sāraṅga, Hindola, Vasanta, Dīpaka, and Megha; they are personified in poetry and mythology.<BR>6 A king, a sovereign.<BR>7 The Raja Guṇa, the property or quality of passion.<BR>8 Greediness, cupidity.<BR>9 Colouring, painting, dying.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A sort of grain, commonly Raggy, much cultivated in the south of India, (Eleusine corocana, or Cynosurus corocanus.)<BR>E.<BR>रञ्ज to colour, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागचूर्ण|रागचूर्णः
रागचूर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A name of KĀMA.<BR>2 A tree yielding an astringent resin or extract, the wood of which is used in dying, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>3 Red lead.<BR>4 The red powder thrown over one another by the Hindus, at the vernal festival named Holī.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion or colour, and चर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=699" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागछन्न|रागच्छन्न|रागच्छन्नः
रागछन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>राग, and छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागद|रागदः
रागद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Colouring.<BR>2 Inspiring passion.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>राग colour, दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागरज्जु|रागरज्जुः
रागरज्जु<BR>m. (-ज्जुः)<BR>The deity of love, KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion, desire, and रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागलता
रागलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion, desire, and लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवत्|रागवन्त्
रागवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Coloured.<BR>2 Impassioned.<BR>E.<BR>राग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवृन्त|रागवृन्तः
रागवृन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion, and वृन्त the stalk of a flower, the support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागषाढव
रागषाढव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A sweetmeat^1 of unripe mangoes dressed with treacle and oil.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागसूत्र|रागसूत्रं
रागसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The thread or string of a balance.<BR>2 A string or thread of silk.<BR>3 Any coloured thread or string.<BR>E.<BR>राग colour, and सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागान्वित
रागान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Affected by passion.<BR>2 Coloured.<BR>E.<BR>राग, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागार्ह
रागार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>1 One who excites hopes and disappoints them.<BR>2 Who or what is an object of affection.<BR>E.<BR>राग, and अर्ह fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागाशनि|रागाशनिः
रागाशनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion, अश to throw (away), अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन्<BR>m. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>1 Passionate, impassioned.<BR>2 Colouring, painting.<BR>3 Coloured, dyed.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>1 A dyer, a painter.<BR>2 A libertine, a lover.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A shrewd and intriguing woman.<BR>2 A modification of a musical mode, of which five are assigned to each mode; in mythology, personified as a female, and the wife of the Rāga.<BR>E.<BR>राग passion, and इनि aff., or रञ्ज to colour, &c., and धिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ
राघ<BR>(ऋ,) राघृ r. 1st cl. (राघते)<BR>To be able or equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघव|राघवः
राघव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A name of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>2 A sort of fish.<BR>E.<BR>रघु the ancestor of the demigod, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कल|रांकलः|राङ्कलः
राङ्कल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कव|रांकव|राङ्कवं
राङ्कव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Woollen, made of the hair of a sort of deer or any other animal.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A woollen garment.<BR>E.<BR>रङ्कु a kind of deer, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज|राजः
राज<BR>(ऋ,) राजृ r. 1st cl. (राजते or irregularly रेजते)<BR>To shine:<BR>With निर् prefixed,<BR>To overcome, to subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज्<BR>m. (राट्)<BR>A king, a monarch or prince.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजक|राजकं|राजकः
राजक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Ruling, a ruler.<BR>2 Splendid, irradiating, bright in itself, and the cause of brilliancy in others.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An assemblage of princes.<BR>E.<BR>राजन् a prince, and वुञ् aff. of multitude; or राज to shine, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकर|राजकरः
राजकर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Tax or toll imposed by the king.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and कर tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकदम्ब|राजकदम्बः
राजकदम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A sort of Kadamba.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, कदम्ब Nauclea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकशेरु|राजकशेरुः
राजकशेरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, कशेरु scirpus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकार्य्य|राजकार्य
राजकार्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Royal duties, state affairs.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and कार्य्यं act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकीय|राजकीयः
राजकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Royal, kingly.<BR>E.<BR>राजन a king, क substituted for the final, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुल
राजकुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A royal race.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A prince, a king.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and कुल family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुष्माण्ड|राजकुष्माण्डः
राजकुष्माण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and कुष्माण्ड a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकृत्वन्
राजकृत्वन्<BR>m. (-त्वा)<BR>A king-maker, one who raises him to the throne, &c.<BR>E.<BR>राजन्, and कृ to make, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगामिन्
राजगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going to the prince or ruler, devolving or falling to the king, (as property, &c. to which there are no heirs.)<BR>E.<BR>राज the king, and गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगुरु|राजगुरुः
राजगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The king's spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and गुरु preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजग्रीव|राजग्रीवः
राजग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A sort of flat fresh water fish, commonly Phalai.<BR>E.<BR>राज shining, ग्रीव the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजघ|राजघः
राजघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Sharp, hot.<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A king-killer, a slayer of sovereigns, a regicide.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and घ for घ्न, who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजचिह्नक|राजचिह्नकं
राजचिह्न^1क<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The male or female organs of generation.<BR>E.<BR>राज chief, चिह्न^2 mark, and कन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजजक्ष्मन्
राजजक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Pulmonary consumption.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, principal, and जक्ष्मन् for यक्ष्मन् consumption; also राजयक्ष्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजजम्बू
राजजम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>1 A large kind of eugenia or rose apple.<BR>2 A sort of date tree.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and जम्बू Eugenia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत|राजतं
राजत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Silver, made of silver, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रजत silver, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतान्वित
राजतान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Plated, inlaid.<BR>E.<BR>राजत, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजताल|राजतालः
राजताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and ताल palm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतिमिष
राजतिमिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and तिमिष a kind of gourd; it is also read राजतेमिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतेजस्
राजतेजस्<BR>n. (-जः)<BR>Majesty, kingly dignity.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and तेजस् splendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत्व|राजत्वं
राजत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Sovereignty, royalty.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, त्व aff. of the abstract; also with तल्, राजता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदण्ड|राजदण्डः
राजदण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 Punishment ordered by the king.<BR>2 A baton, a sceptre.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and दण्ड a staff, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदन्त|राजदन्तः
राजदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An upper and foretooth, applied to the two middle ones.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदर्शन
राजदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A levee, an audience.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदेशीय|राजदेशीयः
राजदेशीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A petty prince or chief, one something less than a king.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and देशीयर् aff. implying something less or defective, or with देश्य aff. of the same power, राजदेश्य m. (-श्यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्वार
राजद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The gate of the palace.<BR>E.<BR>राज for राजा king, द्वार gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्रोह|राजद्रोहः
राजद्रोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Oppression, tyranny.<BR>2 Rebellion.<BR>E.<BR>राज, द्रोह violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्रोहिन्
राजद्रोहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A rebel, a traitor.<BR>E.<BR>राजद्रोह, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधन
राजधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Royal revenue or right to property.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधर्म्म|राजधर्म|राजधर्मः|राजधर्म्मः
राजधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>1 Royal duty.<BR>2 The duty of the military tribe.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधर्म्मविटु
राजधर्म्मविटु<BR>m. (-वित्)<BR>A statesman, one who knows the duties of royalty.<BR>E.<BR>राजधर्म्म, and विटु who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=700" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधान
राजधान<BR>mf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A royal city, a capital, a metropolis.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, धान holding, containing; also with कन् added in the n. or f. (राजधानकं-राजधानिका.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधान्य|राजधान्यं
राजधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>A sort of grain, (Panicum frumentaceum, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधुरा
राजधुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Royal state or function, government.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and धुरा a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्
राजन्<BR>m. (-जा)<BR>1 A king, a prince, a sovereign.<BR>2 A soldier by birth, a man of the regal and military tribe.<BR>3 A master.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>5 A Yakṣa.<BR>6 INDRA.<BR>7 (In composition,) Royal, denoting eminence or excellence.<BR>f. (-ज्ञी)<BR>1 A queen, a princess, the wife of a king.<BR>2 The wife of the sun.<BR>3 Deepcoloured brass, consisting of three parts of copper to one of zinc or tin.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनय|राजनयः
राजनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Polity.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and नय conduct: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनीति|राजनीतिः
राजनीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Regal polity, civil and military government.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and नीति polity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनील|राजनीलं
राजनील<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The emerald.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्य|राजन्यः
राजन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>1 A Kṣatriya, a man of the military or regal tribe.<BR>2 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>3 A tree, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, अन्य Uṇādi aff., or राजन् a king, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यक|राजन्यकं
राजन्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A number of Kṣatriyas or men of the military tribe.<BR>E.<BR>राजन्य a soldier, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्वत्|राजन्वन्त्
राजन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वान्-न्वती-न्वत्)<BR>Possessing or governed by a just and active monarch, (a country, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>राजन् a king, (or by distinction a good king,) and मतुप् poss. aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपटोल|राजपटोलः
राजपटोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and पटोल the same; also with कन् added, राजपटोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपट्ट|राजपट्टः
राजपट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>1 A gem, said to be an inferior kind of diamond brought from Viraśa Deśa, a country in the north-west of India.<BR>2 A tiara or royal fillet.<BR>E.<BR>र ज a king, and पट्ट a bandage, worn in the tiara or diadem of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपत्नी
राजपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>A queen.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुत्त्र
राजपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 The planet MERCURY.<BR>2 A Kṣatriya or man of the military tribe.<BR>3 A soldier by profession, but one of a mixed birth or fabulous origin.<BR>4 The son of a king, a prince.<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine.<BR>2 A bitter gourd.<BR>3 The musk shrew.<BR>4 A kind of brass or bell-metal.<BR>5 A princess.<BR>6 A woman of the Rajput tribe.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king or the moon, and पुत्त्र a son, a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुत्त्रिका
राजपुत्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kind of bird.<BR>2 A king's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and पुत्त्र a child, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुरुष|राजपुरुषः
राजपुरुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A guard, a watchman, a constable, &c.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुष्प|राजपुष्पः
राजपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजफणिञ्झक
राजफणिञ्झक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The orange tree.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and फणिञ्झक a sort of lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजफल|राजफलं
राजफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A cucumber, (Trichosanthes dioeca.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजबदर|राजबदरं|राजबदरः
राजबदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A plant, (a sort of Justicia.)<BR>2 Salt.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The jujube.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and बदर the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभट्टिका
राजभट्टिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A water-fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभद्रक|राजभद्रकः
राजभद्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and भद्रक auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभाज्
राजभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Belonging to or claimed by the king.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभूय|राजभूयं
राजभूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Royalty, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and भूष condition of being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभृत्य|राजभृत्यः
राजभृत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A courtier, a servant of the king, any public officer.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and भृत्य a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभोग्य|राजभोग्यं
राजभोग्य<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>A tree, (Chironjia sapida, or Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Mace.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and भोग्य enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमण्डूक|राजमण्डूकः
राजमण्डूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A large kind of frog.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and मण्डूक a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमल्ल|राजमल्लः
राजमल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A king's wrestler.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and मल्ल a wrestler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमार्ग|राजमार्गः
राजमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A royal road, one passable for horses and elephants, and forty cubits broad.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमाष|राजमाषः
राजमाष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and माष a sort of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमुद्ग|राजमुद्गः
राजमुद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and मुद्ग P. mungo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयक्ष्मन्
राजयक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>Pulmonary consumption.<BR>E.<BR>राज chief, and यक्ष्मन् phthisis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयुध्वन्
राजयुध्वन्<BR>m. (-ध्वा)<BR>An enemy, a rebel, one making war against a prince.<BR>E.<BR>राज, युध to make war, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयोग्य|राजयोग्यः
राजयोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Proper or suitable for a sovereign, princely, royal.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and योग्य what is fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरङ्ग|राजरंग|राजरङ्गं
राजरङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and रङ्ग tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराज|राजराजः
राजराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A name of KUVERA.<BR>2 An emperor, a universal monarch, or king of kings.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, (of a king or kings,) or a Yakṣa, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजर्षि|राजर्षिः
राजर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A kind of saint; that holy and superhuman personage which a king or man of the military class may become by the practice of religious austerities; seven classes of Ṛṣis are enumerated, the Devarṣi, Brahmarṣi, Maharṣi, Paramarṣi, Rājarṣi, Kāṇḍarṣi, and Śrutarṣi: the order is variously given, but the Rājarṣi is inferior to the four preceding ones, and the two last mean the inspired saints and supposed authors of the Hindu scriptures.<BR>E.<BR>राज king, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्षण
राजलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Royal insignia.<BR>2 Any natural mark indicating royalty.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मन्
राजलक्ष्मन्<BR>m. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, लक्ष्मन् a mark or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलेख|राजलेखः
राजलेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A royal letter or order.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and लेख a writing; also राजलेख्यं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवंश्य|राजवंश्यः
राजवंश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Of royal parentage or descent.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and वंश family, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवत्|राजवन्त्
राजवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Governed by a just and able monarch, (a country, &c.)<BR>2 Royal, kingly.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=701" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवर्त्मन्
राजवर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>A royal or main road.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवला
राजवला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Pæderia foetida.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and वल surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवल्ली
राजवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A small gourd, (Momordica charantia.) राज royal, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवसति|राजवसतिः
राजवसति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A throne.<BR>2 A palace.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and वसति abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह|राजवाहः
राजवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and वाह a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह्य|राजवाह्यः
राजवाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A royal elephant.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and वाह्य a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवि|राजविः
राजवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and वि a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवीजिन्
राजवीजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Springing from a royal race.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, वीज seed, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवृक्ष|राजवृक्षः
राजवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The Piyāl tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>2 A sort of tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>3 Euphorbia of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशन
राजशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A plant, from the fibres of which a coarse cordage and canvas are prepared, (Corchorus capsularis or olitorius.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and शन Crotolaria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशफर|राजशफरः
राजशफर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Iliśa or Hilsa fish, (Clupanodon Ilisha, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>राज king, and शफर another sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशय्या
राजशय्या<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>A royal seat or throne.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and शय्या a bed or couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशासन
राजशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A royal edict.<BR>2 A royal badge.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and शासन an edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशुक|राजशुकः
राजशुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of parrot, (Psittacus Lori.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and शुक a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशृङ्ग|राजशृंग|राजशृङ्गं|राजशृङ्गः
राजशृङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The royal Catta or umbrella.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus batachus.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस|राजसः
राजस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Relating to, or derived, &c. from the quality of passion.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>2 The state of being in this world or the next, in which the Raja Guṇa or quality of passion predominates: it is divided into three classes; the first class comprises the Gandharbas, Yakṣas, Guhyakas, &c.; the second, kings and heroes; and the third, boxers, wrestlers, gamblers, tipplers, actors, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रजस् the quality of passion, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसत्ता
राजसत्ता<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>Majesty, royal dignity.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and सत्ता existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसदन|राजसदनं
राजसदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A palace.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and सदन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्प|राजसर्पः
राजसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A large kind of snake, (Boa.)<BR>E.<BR>राज, and सर्प a snake; the king of snakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसभा
राजसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A royal assembly or court.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्षप|राजसर्षपः
राजसर्षप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma, or S. ramosa, Rox.)<BR>2 A mustard seed, as a measure of weight.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and सर्षप mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसायुज्य|राजसायुज्यं
राजसायुज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Royalty, sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, सायुज्य state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसारस|राजसारसः
राजसारस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and सारम the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसिंह
राजसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A great king.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूय|राजसूयः
राजसूय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A sacrifice performed^1 only by a universal monarch, attended by his tributary princes; as in the case of YUDHIṢṬHIRA, and others.<BR>2 A lotus.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A sort of rice.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, (by him,) and षू to be produced, to be effected, aff. क्यप्; or राज the moon, for the moon plant, of which the acid juice is drank at the ceremony, and सु to bring forth, the same aff., deriv. irr.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूयक
राजसूयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a royal sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूययाजिन्
राजसूययाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A priest officiating at the royal sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>राजसूय, and याजिन् who sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसेवक
राजसेवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A courtier, a royal attendant.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and सेवक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्कन्ध|राजस्कन्धः
राजस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्व|राजस्वं
राजस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>Royal revenue, impost, duty, tax.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहंस|राजहंसः
राजहंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A white goose with red legs and bill, or more properly perhaps the flamingo.<BR>2 A drake.<BR>3 An excellent king.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and हंस a goose, the king goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहर्षण|राजहर्षणं
राजहर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A city, a town.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and हर्षण delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहस्तिन्
राजहस्तिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A royal elephant.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and हस्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहासक|राजहासकः
राजहासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of large fish, (Cyprinus niloticus.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, हासक diverting, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाज्ञा
राजाज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>A royal edict or command.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and आज्ञा order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजातन|राजातनः
राजातन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and आङ् before तन to stretch, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजादन|राजादनं|राजादनः
राजादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>2 Another tree, (Mimusops kauki.)<BR>3 The Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, and अदन eating; also राजातन, and राजादनफल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिराज|राजाधिराजः
राजाधिराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A paramount sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>राजा, and अधिराज superior prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजान्न|राजान्नं
राजान्न<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A sort of rice, of a superior quality, said to grow in the Āndhra country.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्र|राजाम्रः
राजाम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>A superior sort of mango.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, अम्र mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्क|राजार्कः
राजार्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>Gigantic swallow wort. (Asclepias gigantea, with white flowers.)<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and अर्क swallow wort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्ह|राजार्हं
राजार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Royal, noble, fit or proper for a king.<BR>n. (-र्हं)<BR>Aloe wood, (Amyris agallocha, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>राज a sovereign, and अर्ह proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजालुक|राजालुकः
राजालुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, आलु a yam, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावर्त्त|राजावर्त|राजावर्तः|राजावर्त्तः
राजावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A gem, described as an inferior kind of diamond, brought from the country Virāṭa.<BR>E.<BR>राज a king, आवर्त्तं a turning; it is considered as a lucky possession for princes, though not esteemed as an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावलि|राजावलिः
राजावलि<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>A line of kings, a royal dynasty or genealogy.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाहि|राजाहिः
राजाहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>A sort of snake said to be two-headed.<BR>E.<BR>राज royal, and अहि a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजि|राजिः
राजि<BR>f. (-जिः-जी)<BR>1 A row, a line.<BR>2 An unbroken row, a continuous line.<BR>3 A small vessel of the body.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, इज् Uṇādi aff., ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=702" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिका
राजिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Black mustard, (Sinapis racemosa, Rox.)<BR>2 A field.<BR>3 A line, a row, a range.<BR>4 A continuous or unbroken line.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, क्वुन् aff., fem. form, or राजि as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजित
राजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Adorned, embellished.<BR>2 Illuminated, irradiated.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिल|राजिलः
राजिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.)<BR>E.<BR>राजि a line, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीव|राजीवं|राजीवः
राजीव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Attending on or living about a prince.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A large fish, (Cyprinus niloticus, BUC.)<BR>2 A kind of deer.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>E.<BR>राजी a line, a row, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेन्द्र|राजेंद्र|राजेन्द्रः
राजेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>An emperor.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेभ
राजेभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A state elephant.<BR>E.<BR>राज, and इभ an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्य|राज्यं
राज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>1 A government, a country, a principality, a kingdom.<BR>2 Administration or exercise of sovereignty or government.<BR>E.<BR>राज for राजन् a prince, and यत् or यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यच्युत
राज्यच्युत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A prince who has lost his kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and च्युत fallen from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यच्युति
राज्यच्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Deposal, loss of sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and च्युति falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यधुरा
राज्यधुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Administration, government.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and धुरा burthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभङ्ग|राज्यभंग|राज्यभङ्गः
राज्यभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Subversion of a sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभाज्
राज्यभाज्<BR>m. (-भाक्)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and भाज् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभ्रंश|राज्यभ्रंशः
राज्यभ्रंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Deposal or loss of a kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and भ्रंश falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभ्रष्ट
राज्यभ्रष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A deposed sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and म्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यरक्षा
राज्यरक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Protection or defence of a kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and रक्षा preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यलोभ|राज्यलोभः
राज्यलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Ambition.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याङ्ग|राज्यांग|राज्याङ्गं
राज्याङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A requisite of regal administration; variously enumerated, as seven, eight, or nine, viz. first, the monarch; second, the prime minister; third, a friend or ally; fourth, treasure; fifth, territory; sixth, a strong hold; and seventh, an army; the eighth is the population or companies of citizens, and the ninth the Purohita or spiritual adviser.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य royalty, and अङ्ग limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याधिकार|राज्याधिकारः
राज्याधिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Government of a kingdom.<BR>2 Right or title to a sovereignty.<BR>E.<BR>राज्य, and अधिकार superintendence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटि|राटिः
राटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>रट to speak, to sound, aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढा
राढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>1 Beauty, splendour, light, lustre.<BR>2 A country or district, part of Bengal west of the Hugli river.<BR>E.<BR>रह to quit, aff. घञ्, and ह changed to ढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राण|राणं
राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>2 A peacock's tail.<BR>E.<BR>रण to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रक|रात्रकं|रात्रकः
रात्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A period of five nights collectively.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man who takes up his abode in a harlot's house for one year.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रि|रात्रिः
रात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः-त्री)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give, (pleasure or rest,) त्रिप् Uṇādi aff., ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचर|रात्रिचरः
रात्रिचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Going or moving at night.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A goblin, a fiend, a ghost or evil spirit.<BR>2 A thief, a robber.<BR>3 A guard, a patrole.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, (by night,) and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिज
रात्रिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Nocturnal, born or produced at night.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A star, a constellation.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजल|रात्रिजलं
रात्रिजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Dew, mist, fog.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागर|रात्रिजागरः
रात्रिजागर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Keeping watch at night, sitting up at night.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and जागर who wakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागरण
रात्रिजागरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sitting up all night.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि, and जागरण waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागरद|रात्रिजागरदः
रात्रिजागरद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A musquito, a gnat.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रिजागर waking by night, and द who gives or makes, from दा to give, or from दो to cut, who stings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिञ्चर|रात्रिंचर|रात्रिञ्चरः
रात्रिञ्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A ghost, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, चर to go, ट aff., and मुम् augment; also रात्रिचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमट|रात्रिमटः
रात्रिमट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A ghost, a goblin.<BR>2 A theif.<BR>3 A guard.<BR>4 A night-walker.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, अट to go, aff. अच्, and मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमणि|रात्रिमणिः
रात्रिमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिम्मन्य|रात्रिंमन्य
रात्रिम्मन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Thinking it night.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि, and मन्य who believes, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रियोग|रात्रियोगः
रात्रियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Coming on of night.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि, and योग joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवासस्
रात्रिवासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविगम|रात्रिविगमः
रात्रिविगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Dawn, day-light.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, विगम stop, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्
रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, विश्लेष separation, and गामिन् who goes, these birds being supposed to pass the night apart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेद|रात्रिवेदः
रात्रिवेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि the night, and वेद who knows, who knows its measure or duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेदिन्
रात्रिवेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and वेदिन् who knows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहास|रात्रिहासः
रात्रिहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, and हास what smiles, blossoming at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहिण्डक|रात्रिहिण्डकः
रात्रिहिण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A guard of the interior or women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, हिडि to go, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यट|रात्र्यटः
रात्र्यट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An imp, a goblin.<BR>2 A ghost.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>4 A night-walker.<BR>E.<BR>रात्रि night, अट to go, aff. अच्; also with a nasal inserted, रात्रिमट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Cooked, dressed.<BR>2 Perfected, as a religious vow; observed, as a fast, &c.<BR>3 Perfect, in mysterious or magical power, adept, initiated.<BR>4 Perfect in general, accomplished; finished, complete, mature, &c.<BR>E.<BR>राध to accomplish or be accomplished, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धान्त|राद्धांत|राद्धान्तः
राद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>Demonstrated truth, proved and established fact or conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>राद्ध established, अन्त end, result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध<BR>(औ) औराध r. 4th cl. (राध्यति) 5th cl. (राध्नोति)<BR>1 To bring any thing to fulness or completion, to finish, to effect, to accomplish, to complete.<BR>2 To attain completion, to succeed, to be finished or accomplished.<BR>With अप prefixed,<BR>To offend, to be in fault.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To worship, to propitiate by worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The month Vaiśākha, (April-May.)<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 The asterism, in which the moon is full in the month Vaiśākha; the sixteenth of the Nakṣatras, containing four stars in the shape of a festoon; the stars are supposed to be α ν ι Libra, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">Page704</a>] and Scorpionis.<BR>2 A celebrated Gopī, the favourite mistress of KṚṢṆA, during his residence in Vṛndāvana amongst the cow-herds.<BR>3 Lightning.<BR>4 An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR>5 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>6 A flower, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>E.<BR>राध to accomplish, aff. अ, टाप् fem. aff., or राधा the asterism, अण् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=703" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधन|राधनं
राधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Completing, accomplishing, succeeding, effecting.<BR>2 Obtaining, acquisition.<BR>3 Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>4 The means or instrument of accomplishing any thing.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Speech, speaking.<BR>E.<BR>राध to accomplish, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधरङ्क|राधरङ्कः
राधरङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 A plough.<BR>2 Thin rain.<BR>3 Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाकान्त|राधाकान्तः
राधाकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा, and कान्त beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधातनय|राधातनयः
राधातनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>KARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा, and तनय son; see राधासुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधानाथ
राधानाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधापुत्त्र
राधापुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>KARṆA<BR>E.<BR>राधा, and पुत्त्र son: see राधासुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाभेदिन्
राधाभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A name of ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा the mistress of KṚṢṆA, and भेदिन् dividing; having prevailed on KṚṢṆA to abandon her.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधावल्लभ
राधावल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधावेधिन्
राधावेधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा the mistress of KṚṢṆA, and वेधिन् who hurts or wounds: see राधाभेदिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधासुत|राधासुतः
राधासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>KARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा the name of the wife of the charioteer of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA, by whom the prince, after exposure by his own mother KUNTĪ, was found and fostered, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेय|राधेयः
राधेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of KARṆA.<BR>E.<BR>राधा a proper name, and ढक् aff.: see राधासुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राप्य|राप्यः
राप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be said or spoken.<BR>E.<BR>रप to speak, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Black.<BR>2 White.<BR>3 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name common to three incarnations of VIṢṆU, or PARAŚURĀMA, the son of the Muni JAMADAGNI, born at the commencement of the second or Tretā Yug, for the purpose of punishing the tyrannical kings of the Kṣatriya race; RĀMACANDRA, the son of DAŚARATHA, king of Oude, born at the close of the second age, to destroy the demons who infested the earth, and especially RĀVAṆA the Daitya sovereign of Ceylon; and BALARĀMA, the elder and half-brother of KṚṢṆA, the son of ROHIṆĪ, born at the end of the Dvāpara or third age.<BR>2 A name of VARUṆA, regent of the waters.<BR>3 A horse.<BR>4 A sort of deer.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A woman, a female, a pleasing or beautiful female.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>3 A river.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>2 A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकरी
रामकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the Rāgiṇīs, or female personifications of the musical modes.<BR>E.<BR>राम delighting, and करी who makes; also रामकली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकर्पूर
रामकर्पूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fragrant sort of grass.<BR>E.<BR>राम pleasant, and कर्पूर (smelling like) camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकली
रामकली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A Rāgiṇī.<BR>E.<BR>राम pleasant, कला sound or note, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामगिरि|रामगिरिः
रामगिरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The name of a mountain, variously applied, but especially assigned to a mountain called Compteh or Citrakūṭa in Bundelkund, and to another near Nagpore, called now Rāmtek.<BR>E.<BR>राम the hero, and गिरि a mountain, the mountain of RĀMA; being one of his halting places in his progress from Oude to the Peninsula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामचन्द्र|रामचंद्र|रामचन्द्रः
रामचन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The hero RĀMACANDRA, the second incarnation of VIṢṆU under the name of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>राम, and चन्द्र the moon, the moon-like RĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामजननी
रामजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The mother of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>राम, and जननी mother; hence it is equally applicable to REṆUKĀ, the mother of PARAŚURĀMA, and to KAUŚALYĀ, the mother of RĀMACANDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठ|रामठं|रामठः
रामठ<BR>n. (-ठं)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>रम to please, अठ Uṇādi aff., and the radical vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयक|रामणीयकं
रामणीयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>E.<BR>रमणीय the same, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदूत|रामदूतः
रामदूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The monkey HANUMĀN, the friend and messenger of RĀMA.<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>A shrub, apparently a variety of basil with small leaves.<BR>E.<BR>राम RĀMA, and दूत a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामपूग|रामपूगः
रामपूग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A small species of the areca or betel-nut tree, (Areca triandra, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>राम RAMA, and पूग areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्र|रामभद्रः
रामभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The hero RĀMACANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>राम the same, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामवीणा
रामवीणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A sort of Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>राम RAMA, and वीणा a lute; it may be also ironically applicable to the horn blown by BALARĀMA, and called still the Rāmsinh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामशर|रामशरः
रामशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A variety of the Saccharum Sara, a sort of grass.<BR>E.<BR>राम RĀMA, and शर the Sara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसख|रामसखः
रामसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The monkey king SUGRĪVA.<BR>E.<BR>राम RĀMA, and सख friend; RĀMA having restored him to his throne, whence he had been driven by another monkey chief BALI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामायण|रामायणं
रामायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 The first epic poem of the Hindus, recording the adventures of RĀMA the son of DAŚARATHA, sovereign of Oude; written by the poet VĀLMIKI.<BR>2 A name of several poems on the life and adventures of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>राम the prince so named, and अयन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिल|रामिलः
रामिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>2 A lover, a husband.<BR>E.<BR>राम pleasing, agreeable, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः|राम्भः
राम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The bambu, staff of a religious student.<BR>E.<BR>रम्भा a bambu, aff. अञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायण|रायणं
रायण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Sounding, crying, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>रै to sound, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायभाटी
रायभाटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>The current or flow of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारस्यमान
रारस्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Crying aloud and repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>रस to cry, reit. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राल|रालः
राल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Resin, the resinous and fragrant exudation of the Shorea robusta.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give or get, aff. अलच्; also अराल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राव|रावः
राव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>रु to cry or sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The sovereign of Laṅkā or Ceylon, killed by RĀMACANDRA.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Noise, tumult.<BR>E.<BR>रु to cry (in the causal form), aff. ल्युट्, afflicting mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणारि|रावणारिः
रावणारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The hero RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रावण RĀVAṆA, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणि|रावणिः
रावणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The eldest son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>रावण, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश
राश<BR>(ऋ,) राशृ r. 1st and 4th cls. (राशते राश्यते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=704" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशि|राशिः
राशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>1 A heap, a quantity.<BR>2 A sign of the zodiac.<BR>3 Arithmetical or algebraic quantity.<BR>4 A part and its divisor, or numerator and denominator.<BR>5 A congeries of number or quantity.<BR>E.<BR>अश to pervade, इण् Uṇādi aff. and रुट् initial augment; or रश to sound, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिगत
राशिगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heaped, accumulated.<BR>2 Computed, summed either by arithmetic or algebra.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिचक्र|राशिचक्रं
राशिचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>The zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>राशि a sign, and चक्र a wheel or circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभाग|राशिभागः
राशिभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A fraction.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभोग|राशिभोगः
राशिभोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Passage of a planet through a sign of the zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकरण
राशीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Heaping, piling, gathering.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकृत
राशीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heaped, piled, gathered.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीभूत
राशीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Heaped, piled.<BR>E.<BR>राशि, and भूत become, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र<BR>mn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्रं)<BR>1 An inhabited country or realm, a region.<BR>2 Any public calamity, as plague, famine, &c.<BR>E.<BR>राज to shine or govern, aff. ष्ट्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रनिवासिन्
राष्ट्रनिवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>An inhabitant of any civilized country.<BR>E.<BR>राष्ट्र a district, and निवासिन a dweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिक|राष्ट्रिकः
राष्ट्रिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging to or inhabiting a country.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A prickly sort of night-shade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>राष्ट्र a country, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of or belonging to a kingdom, produced or born in it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>राष्ट्र a region, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रीय|राष्ट्रीयः
राष्ट्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a region or realm.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A king's brother-in-law, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>राष्ट्र a region, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास<BR>(ऋ) रासृ r. 1st cl. (रासते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Confused noise, uproar, hubbub.<BR>2 Sound in general.<BR>3 Speech, discourse.<BR>4 A chain.<BR>5 A festival amongst the cowherds, including songs and dances, especially the circular dance as performed by KṚṢṆA and the Gopīs or cowherdesses.<BR>6 A game played by children.<BR>E.<BR>रस to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>An ass.<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>The she ass.<BR>E.<BR>रास to sound, अभच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभधूसर
रासभधूसर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Grey or light-brown, ass-grey.<BR>E.<BR>रासभ and धूसर grey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभवन्दिनी
रासभवन्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>रासभ an ass, वदि to praise, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासयात्रा
रासयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A festival in honour of KṚṢṆA on the full moon of Kārttika.<BR>E.<BR>रास, and यात्रा festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेरस|रासेरसः
रासेरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 An assembly, a company, a party.<BR>2 A game or festival peculiar to the cowherds: see रास.<BR>3 Love, desire, the passion or sentiment.<BR>4 Alchymy: see रससिद्धि.<BR>5 The sixth night after delivery, on which the family and friends sit up all night.<BR>6 Sport, mirth, pastime.<BR>7 Any festival or holiday.<BR>E.<BR>रास noise, &c., and रस flavour, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना<BR>f. (-स्ना)<BR>1 A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>2 Another plant, (the serpent ophioxylon ?)<BR>3 A sort of perfume.<BR>E.<BR>स्स to sound, नक् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहु|राहुः
राहु<BR>m. (-हुः)<BR>The ascending node; in mythology, the son of SIṂHIKĀ, a Daitya, with the tail of a dragon, whose head was severed from his body by VIṢṆU, but being immortal, the head and tail retained their separate existence, and being transferred to the stellar sphere, became the authors of eclipses; the first especially, by endeavouring at various times to swallow the sun and moon.<BR>E.<BR>रह to abandon, (the planets which it has vainly attempted to devour,) aff. उ, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रस्त
राहुग्रस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>Eclipsed, (as the sun or moon.)<BR>E.<BR>राहु, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रास|राहुग्रासः
राहुग्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Immersion of a planet in an eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>राहु, and ग्रास mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्राह|राहुग्राहः
राहुग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the dragon's head, and ग्राह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुभेदिन्
राहुभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the Daitya, भेदिन् the divider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुमूर्द्धभिद्
राहुमूर्द्धभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद्)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the Daitya, मूर्द्ध the head, and भिट् who divides, who decapitates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुलसू
राहुलसू<BR>m. (-सूः)<BR>A name of the legislator Buddha or Śākyasiṃha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुसंस्पर्श|राहुसंस्पर्शः
राहुसंस्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>An eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the dragon's head, and संस्पर्श seizure, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुहन्
राहुहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the Daitya, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूच्छिष्ट|राहूच्छिष्टः
राहूच्छिष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Garlick.<BR>E.<BR>राहु the demon, उच्छिष्ट vomited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूत्सृष्ट|राहूत्सृष्टः
राहूत्सृष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Garlick.<BR>E.<BR>राहू the Daitya, and उत्सृष्ट created.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि<BR>r. 5th cl. (रिणोति)<BR>To hurt or injure.<BR>r. 6th cl. (रियति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि<BR>m. (रिः)<BR>1 The tone of voice by which the note Ṛṣabha is uttered.<BR>2 Dancing, tumbling.<BR>3 Waste, loss.<BR>f. (रिः)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>4 Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give, &c. aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक
रिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The heart, the mind.<BR>2 Law, litigation.<BR>E.<BR>रिच to divide, &c., aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्त|रिक्तं
रिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Empty, void.<BR>2 Poor, indigent.<BR>3 Unloaded, unburthened.<BR>4 Purged.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 A wood, a forest.<BR>2 A vacuity, a vacuum.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>The fourth, ninth, or fourteenth days of the lunar fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>रिच to void by stool, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तक|रिक्तकं
रिक्तक<BR>m. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Void, empty.<BR>2 Unladen, unburthened.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तता
रिक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Vacuity, void, space.<BR>E.<BR>रिक्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रिक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तभाण्ड
रिक्तभाण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>Having no vessels or effects.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>An empty vessel.<BR>E.<BR>रिक्त, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तहस्त
रिक्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Empty-handed.<BR>E.<BR>रिक्त, and हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थ|रिक्थं
रिक्थ<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Substance, property, wealth.<BR>E.<BR>रिच् to separate, Uṇādi aff. थक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थहारिन्
रिक्थहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिनी-रि)<BR>Taking or inheriting property.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 An heir, one who succeeds to the property of the deceased, and gives the funeral cake.<BR>2 A maternal uncle.<BR>3 The seed of the Indian fig.<BR>E.<BR>रिक्थ wealth, and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=705" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थिन्
रिक्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्थी-क्थिनी-क्थि)<BR>Wealthy, possessing property.<BR>m. (-क्थी)<BR>A successor or an heir.<BR>E.<BR>रिक्थ wealth, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्षा
रिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 A nit.<BR>2 A mote in a sun-beam.<BR>E.<BR>see लिक्षा, ल being changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख
रिख<BR>r. 1st cl. (रिखति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख
रिख<BR>(इ) रिखि r. 1st cl. (रिंखति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिग
रिग<BR>(इ) रिगि r. 1st cl. (रिंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्ख|रिङ्खः
रिङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>1 Disappointing, deceiving.<BR>2 A horse's hoof.<BR>3 One of a horse's paces.<BR>4 Dancing.<BR>5 Sliding, slipping.<BR>E.<BR>रिखि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्खण|रिंखण|रिंखणं|रिङ्खणं
रिङ्खण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Slipping, sliding, stumbling, tumbling; or figuratively, deviating from rectitude or virtue.<BR>E.<BR>रिखि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गण|रिंगण|रिंगणं|रिङ्गणं
रिङ्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Creeping, (as a child on all fours.)<BR>2 Tumbling, slipping, sliding.<BR>3 Deviating from rectitude, sliding from virtue.<BR>E.<BR>रिगि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिच
रिच<BR>r. 1st and 10 cls. (रेचति-रेचयति)<BR>To join, to unite.<BR>2 To divide, to scatter or separate.<BR>3 To purge.<BR>(औइर्) औ रिचिर r. 7th cl. (रिणक्ति-रिंक्ते)<BR>To purge, to evacuate fæces frequently.<BR>With अति prefixed,<BR>To exceed, to be more than enough.<BR>With वि,<BR>To purge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिज
रिज<BR>r. 1st cl. (रेजते)<BR>To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिटि|रिटिः
रिटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>1 The crackling or roaring of flame.<BR>2 A musical instrument.<BR>3 Black salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपु|रिपुः
रिपु<BR>m. (-पुः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>रप to speak, to abuse, aff. उ, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुघातिन्
रिपुघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Killing a foe.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>E.<BR>रिपु an enemy, and घातिन् destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुञ्जय|रिपुंजय
रिपुञ्जय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Victorious.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Name of a king.<BR>E.<BR>रिपु, जि to conquer, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुता
रिपुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Hostility, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>रिपु, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रिपुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्र|रिप्रः
रिप्र<BR>mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं)<BR>Vile, bad, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>री to hurt, Uṇādi aff. र, the vowel made short, and पुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफ
रिफ<BR>r. 6th cl. (रिफति)<BR>1 To speak, to say or tell.<BR>2 To fight.<BR>3 To blame, to censure.<BR>4 To hurt or injure.<BR>5 To give.<BR>6 To praise, to flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ|रिंफ
रिम्फ<BR>r. 6th cl. (रिम्फति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ|रिंफ
रिम्फ<BR>n. (-म्फं)<BR>The zodiac.<BR>E.<BR>रिम्फ to hurt, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसा
रिरंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Wish to sport.<BR>E.<BR>रम to play, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसु
रिरंसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Desirous to sport.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, उ aff. desid. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरी
रिरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Pale brass, prince's metal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>री to go, क्रिन् aff., ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिव
रिव<BR>(इ) रिवि r. 1st cl. (रिण्वति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश|रिशः
रिश<BR>r. 6th cl. (रिशति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill or attempt to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्य|रिश्यः
रिश्य<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>रिश to hurt, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष
रिष<BR>r. 1st cl. (रेषति) r. 4th cl. (रिष्यति)<BR>To hurt, to kill, or attempt to kill.<BR>r. 9th cl. (रिष्णाति)<BR>To separate, to depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषि|रिषिः
रिषि<BR>n. (-षिः)<BR>A saint.<BR>E.<BR>रि substituted for ऋ; see ऋषि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्ट|रिष्टं|रिष्टः
रिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Hurt, injured.<BR>2 Unlucky.<BR>3 Lucky.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Happiness, prosperity.<BR>2 Good luck, fortune.<BR>3 Bad luck, ill fortune.<BR>4 Destruction, loss, privation.<BR>5 Sin.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A sword.<BR>2 The soap plant.<BR>3 A demon, destroyed by VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>रिष to hurt or injure, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टक|रिष्टकः
रिष्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus of several species.)<BR>E.<BR>रिष्ट the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टि|रिष्टिः
रिष्टि<BR>m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A sword.<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Prosperity, good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>रिष to hurt, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्य|रिष्यः
रिष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>रिष to hurt, to be hurt, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्व|रिष्वः
रिष्व<BR>mfn. (-ष्वः-ष्वा-ष्वं)<BR>Mischievous, injurious.<BR>E.<BR>रिष to hurt, Uṇādi aff. वन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिह
रिह<BR>r. 1st cl. (रेहति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
री<BR>r. 9th cl. (रीणाति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR>3 To howl, as a wild beast.<BR>(ङ) रीङ् r. 4th cl. (रीयते)<BR>1 To distil, to ooze, to drop.<BR>2 To fall, to alight.<BR>r. 2nd cl. (रेति)<BR>To bear or conceive, (as a child.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीज्या
रीज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 Reproach, censure.<BR>2 Shame, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढक|रीढकः
रीढक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The backbone.<BR>E.<BR>रिह to hurt, aff. क्त, and the vowel made long, रीढ, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढा
रीढा<BR>f. (-ढा)<BR>Disrespect, irreverence, disregard.<BR>E.<BR>रिह to kill, &c., aff. क्त, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीण|रीणं
रीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Oozing, dripping, leaking, distilling.<BR>E.<BR>री to leak, to run out, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीति|रीतिः
रीति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 Usage, custom, practice, local or traditionary observance.<BR>2 Oozing, leaking, distilling.<BR>3 Brass, pale brass, or prince's metal.<BR>4 Rust of iron.<BR>5 Calx of brass.<BR>6 Scoria of any metal, or the oxide formed on the surface of metals by their exposure to heat and air.<BR>7 Boundary, limit.<BR>8 Going, motion.<BR>9 Natural property or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>री to go, to run out, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीतिका
रीतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>रीति brass, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीतिपुष्प|रीतिपुष्पं
रीतिपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>रीति brass, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीव
रीव<BR>r. 1st cl. (रीवते)<BR>1 To take.<BR>2 To screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु<BR>(टु) टुरु r. 2nd cl. (रौति)<BR>To sound, to make a particular sort of sound.<BR>(ड,) रुङ् r. 1st cl. (रवते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>4 To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु<BR>m. (रुः)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Noise, sound.<BR>f. (रुः)<BR>1 Fear, alarm.<BR>2 Cutting, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>रु to sound, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक|रुकः
रुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A liberal man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्प्रतिक्रिया
रुक्प्रतिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The practice of physic, curing, remedying.<BR>E.<BR>रुक् from रुच् disease, प्रतिक्रिया resisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्म|रुक्मं|रुक्मः
रुक्म<BR>n. (-क्मं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, Uṇādi aff. मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मकारक|रुक्मकारकः
रुक्मकारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A gold-smith.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्म gold, and कारक a worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मवत्|रुक्मवन्त्
रुक्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Golden.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>A species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिदर्प|रुक्मिदर्पः
रुक्मिदर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्मिन् a king, and दर्प pride; proud of overcoming him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिदारिन्
रुक्मिदारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्मिन् a prince, and दारिन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिन्
रुक्मिन्<BR>m. (-क्मी)<BR>The name of a prince slain by BALARĀMA.<BR>f. (-क्मिणी)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A princess carried off. and married by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्म gold, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=706" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिभिद्
रुक्मिभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद्)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्मि a prince, the elder brother of RUKMIṆĪ, and भिद् breaker, conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्सद्मन्
रुक्सद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>Excrement, fæces.<BR>E.<BR>रुज् disease, सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष|रुक्षः
रुक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Harsh, unkind.<BR>2 Rough, hard.<BR>3 Rugged, uneven.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. स्; it is more properly written रूक्ष, as derived from रूक्ष to be rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्न|रुग्नः
रुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Bent, crooked, curbed.<BR>2 Broken.<BR>3 Impaired, injured.<BR>4 Diseased, sick, infirm.<BR>E.<BR>रुज to be disordered, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्नता
रुग्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Crookedness.<BR>E.<BR>रुग्न, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रुग्नत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच
रुच<BR>r. 1st cl. (रोचति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To please, to be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
रुच्<BR>f. (रुक्)<BR>1 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>2 Beauty, loveliness.<BR>3 Lightning.<BR>4 Wish, desire.<BR>5 The chattering of the parrot or Maina.<BR>6 The Ṛg Veda.<BR>E.<BR>रुच् to shine, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added रुचा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचक|रुचकं|रुचकः
रुचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Agreeable, pleasing.<BR>2 Sharp, acrid.<BR>3 Tonic, stomachic.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>2 An ornament of the neck or breast.<BR>3 A tooth.<BR>4 A pigeon.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Salt.<BR>2 Natron, alkali.<BR>3 Borax.<BR>4 A garland, a chaplet.<BR>5 A curl on a horse's neck.<BR>6 The woody Cassia.<BR>7 Any auspicious or fortunate object.<BR>8 A perfume, commonly Rocanā.<BR>9 An anthelmintic medicine, commonly Virenga, (Embelia ribes?)<BR>10 A sort of temple.<BR>11 A stomachic.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, &c. in the causal form, क्वुन् aff.; the embellisher, the polisher, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचि|रुचिः
रुचि<BR>f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>1 Light, lustre.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>3 Passion.<BR>4 Wish, desire.<BR>5 A ray of light.<BR>6 Intent application to any object or undertaking.<BR>7 Hunger, appetite.<BR>8 Taste, sentiment.<BR>E.<BR>रुच् to shine, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिकर
रुचिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Beautifying.<BR>2 Sharpening, as the appetite, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रुचि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचित|रुचितं
रुचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sweet.<BR>2 Sharpened, (as the appetite.)<BR>3 Digested.<BR>4 Bright, brightened.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to please, Uṇādi aff. कितच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिर|रुचिरं
रुचिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Beautiful, charming, pleasing.<BR>2 Sweet.<BR>3 Stomachic, restorative.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to please, Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरमुद्
रुचिरमुद्<BR>mfn. (-द्)<BR>Exquisite, affording great pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>रुचिर, and मुद what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरानन
रुचिरानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>रुचिर, and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरापाङ्गी
रुचिरापाङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A beautiful charming woman.<BR>E.<BR>रुचिर, and अपाङ्ग corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिष्य|रुचिष्यं
रुचिष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>1 Sweet.<BR>2 Stomachic.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to be agreeable, Uṇādi aff. किष्यन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्य|रुच्यं|रुच्यः
रुच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>2 Stomachic, tonic.<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>A husband, a lover.<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>A digestive, a tonic.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to please, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज
रुज<BR>(औ ओ) औरुजो r. 6th cl. (रुजति)<BR>1 To afflict, to disorder, to afflict with pain or disease.<BR>2 To bend or break.<BR>r. 10th cl. (रोजयति)<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
रुज्<BR>f. (रुक्)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>रुज् to be or make sick, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added रुजा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजत्
रुजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>1 Breaking.<BR>2 Giving pain, making ill or sick.<BR>2 Being sick.<BR>E.<BR>रुज to afflict. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजा
रुजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 Overthrow, destruction.<BR>3 An ewe.<BR>E.<BR>रुज to be or make sick, aff. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजाकर|रुजाकरं|रुजाकरः
रुजाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Sickening, making sick or ill.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One of the Bhāvas or sentiments, the sickness induced by passion or love.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An acid fruit, (the fruit of the Averrhoa carambola.)<BR>E.<BR>रुजा sickness, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुट
रुट<BR>r. 1st cl. (रोटते)<BR>1 To resist or oppose.<BR>2 To strive again.<BR>3 To tumble or roll for passion.<BR>r. 10th cl. (रोटयति)<BR>1 To be angry.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(इ) रुटि r. 1st cl. (रुण्ठति)<BR>To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुठ
रुठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (रोठति)<BR>To strike, to fell, to knock down, to overturn.<BR>(रोठते)<BR>To resist, to oppose.<BR>(इ) रुठि r. 1st cl. (रुण्ठति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To steal.<BR>3 To be idle.<BR>4 To be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुणस्करा
रुणस्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A cow easily milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड|रुंड|रुण्डः
रुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A headless body, retaining life and mixing in combat.<BR>E.<BR>रुडि for रुटि or रुठि to take or steal, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्डिका|रुंडिका
रुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The threshold of a door.<BR>2 A field of battle.<BR>3 A female messenger or go-between.<BR>4 Superhuman power.<BR>E.<BR>रुण्ड as above, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुत|रुतं
रुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The cry of birds, &c.<BR>2 Any cry or noise.<BR>E.<BR>रु to sound, to make a particular sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतव्याज|रुतव्याजः
रुतव्याज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Mimicry.<BR>2 Simulated cry or sound.<BR>E.<BR>रुत, and व्याज disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतायत
रुतायत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rendered vocal by the cry of birds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रुत cry, used as a verb, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद
रुद<BR>(इर) रुदिर r. 2nd cl. (रोदिति)<BR>1 To weep.<BR>2 To call or address weeping.<BR>With उप and आङ्,<BR>To weep for another, to sympathize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
रुद्<BR>f. (रुत्)<BR>1 Grief.<BR>2 Pain, affliction.<BR>3 Disease.<BR>4 Sound, noise.<BR>5 Cry, wail, lamentation.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदत्
रुदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दती-दत्)<BR>Weeping, wailing.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदथ|रुदथः
रुदथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A dog.<BR>2 A pupil, a scholar.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, अथन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदित|रुदितं
रुदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Crying, weeping, wept, (by whom.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Weeping.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्ध|रुद्धं
रुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Surrounded, begirt, as with a fence or river, &c.<BR>2 Secured, protected from access.<BR>3 Obstructed, stopped, shut up.<BR>4 Opposed, stopped, impeded.<BR>5 Besieged, invested, blockaded.<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>A siege.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to close, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्यमान
रुद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being weeping or wailing.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्र|रुद्रः
रुद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 A name or form of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A demi-god, an inferior manifestation of ŚIVA, or according to one legend, a being born from the forehead of BRAHMĀ: the RUDRAS are eleven in number, and are severally named, AJAIKAPĀDA, AHIVRADHNA, VIRŪPĀKṢA, SUREŚVARA, JAYANTA, BAHURŪPA, TRYAMBAKA, APARĀJITA, SAVITRA, and HARA.<BR>f. (-द्री)<BR>A sort of lute or guitar.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, रक् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel unchanged; the name is given to ŚIVA, because according to his own declaration, he disperses the tears of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">Page708</a>] mortals: to the demi-gods, because they wept at their birth, or because they made the enemies of the gods weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=707" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रज|रुद्रजः
रुद्रज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and ज born, being supposed to be the semen of the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रपत्नी
रुद्रपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>1 Linseed, (Linum.)<BR>2 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रप्रिया
रुद्रप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica)<BR>2 The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, &c., and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रभू
रुद्रभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and भू site or haunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रबलि
रुद्रबलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>Oblations of meat, &c. presented to the RUDRAS.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र a RUDRA, and बलि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रसू
रुद्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of eleven children.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र a RUDRA, of whom there are eleven, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राक्रीड|रुद्राक्रीडः
रुद्राक्रीड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and आक्रीड place of sport; being supposed to dance and sport in such places at evening twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राक्ष|रुद्राक्षं|रुद्राक्षः
रुद्राक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree, (Eleocarpus ganitrus, Rox.)<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The berry of the Eleocarpus, of which rosaries are usually made.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and अक्ष from अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राणी
रुद्राणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ, as the wife of RUDRA or ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रावास|रुद्रावासः
रुद्रावास<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Benares.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रारि|रुद्रारिः
रुद्रारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>KĀMA, the deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध
रुध<BR>r. 4th cl. (with अनु prefixed) (अनुरुध्यते)<BR>1 To desire, to wish for, to love.<BR>2 To be kind to.<BR>3 To consent, to concur.<BR>4 To lament or be sorry for.<BR>(ञि औ इर) ञि औरुधिर् r. 7th cl. (रुणद्धि रुंद्धे)<BR>1 To impede, to oppose, to obstruct, to block or confine.<BR>2 To invest, to blockade, to besiege.<BR>With अभि and सम् prefixed,<BR>To prevent.<BR>With अव,<BR>To guard.<BR>With उप,<BR>To blockade.<BR>With प्रति or वि,<BR>To oppose, to resist.<BR>With सम् and नि,<BR>To shut up, to surround or blockade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिर|रुधिरं|रुधिरः
रुधिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to obstruct, किरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिरपायिन्
रुधिरपायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A Rākṣasa, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>रुधिर, and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्वा
रुध्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having stopped, checked, impeded, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to hinder. क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुन्धत्
रुन्धत्<BR>mfn. (-न्धन्-न्धती-न्धत्)<BR>1 Hindering, opposing, stopping.<BR>2 Resisting, refusing.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to hinder, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुप
रुप<BR>r. 4th cl. (रुप्यति)<BR>To confound, to perplex, to confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुभेटि
रुभेटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>Fog, vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुमा
रुमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 The wife of the monkey SUGRĪVA.<BR>2 The district, or more properly the salt mines of Sambhar, a town in Ajmer, twenty miles west of Jayanagar.<BR>E.<BR>रु to weep, मन् aff., with टाप् fem. aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुम्र|रुम्रः
रुम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>ARUṆA, or the dawn.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, Uṇādi aff. रव्, and रु substituted for the initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरु|रुरुः
रुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A sort of deer.<BR>2 A Daitya flayed by ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>रु to weep, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुत्सु
रुरुत्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु).<BR>1 Wishing to oppose or obstruct.<BR>2 Wishing to bind or tie up, (as the hair.)<BR>E.<BR>रुध to oppose, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुदिषु
रुरुदिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing or purposing to wail or weep, ready to cry.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवत्
रुवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>Crying, calling, howling.<BR>E.<BR>रु to cry, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवथु
रुवथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>2 A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवु|रुवुः
रुवु<BR>m. (-वुः)<BR>The castor-oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>रु to weep, कु aff., and the final vowel changed to उव; also with कन् added रुवुक, and with the first or second vowel made long, रुवुक and रुवूक; also, as differently derived, उरुवूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुश
रुश<BR>r. 6th cl. (रुशति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR>(इ) रुशि r. 10th cl. (रुंशयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशत्|रुशन्त्
रुशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>1 Maledictory, imprecative.<BR>2 Cursing, imprecating.<BR>E.<BR>रुश to seek to injure, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष
रुष<BR>r. 1st cl. (रोषति) 4th cl. (रुष्यति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to kill or attempt to kill.<BR>(इर्) रुषिर r. 4th and 10th cls. (रुष्यति रोषयति)<BR>To be angry, to be passionate or wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
रुष्<BR>f. (रुट्)<BR>Anger, wrath, passion.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added रुषा f. (-षा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषित|रुषितः
रुषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Enraged, angry.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, aff. क्त with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्ट|रुष्टः
रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Angry, enraged.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्टि|रुष्टिः
रुष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Wrath, rage, anger.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह|रुहः
रुह<BR>(ञि औ) ञिऔरुह r. 1st cl. (रोहति)<BR>1 To grow from seed, to grow as a tree, &c.<BR>2 To be produced or become manifest.<BR>3 To be born.<BR>With अधि prefixed,<BR>To go up or over, to ascend.<BR>With अधि and आङ्,<BR>To ascend.<BR>With अव,<BR>To descend.<BR>With आङ्.<BR>1 To mount, to ride on.<BR>2 To rise, to ascend.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To grow, to shoot forth as a branch or shoot taking fresh root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह|रुहः
रुह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>1 Growing, springing up.<BR>2 Mounted, ascended.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहक|रुहकं
रुहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A hole, a vacuity, a cave, a chasm.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to go or mount, (insects, &c.,) and क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहा
रुहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्वन्
रुह्वन्<BR>m. (-ह्वा)<BR>A tree.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. क्वनिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष|रूक्षं|रूक्षः
रूक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (रूक्षयति)<BR>To be harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष|रूक्षं|रूक्षः
रूक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Harsh, rough, not smooth or soft.<BR>2 Rough to the taste, astringent, austere, not bland or sapid.<BR>3 Rugged, uneven.<BR>4 Harsh, unkind, unfriendly.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree in general.<BR>E.<BR>रूक्ष to be harsh or rough, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्षता
रूक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Roughness.<BR>2 Harshness.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्ष, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रूक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढ|रूढं|रूढः
रूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>2 Famous, notorious.<BR>3 Certain, ascertained.<BR>4 Budded, blown.<BR>5 Much, exceeding.<BR>6 Increased, grown.<BR>7 Traditional, conventional, or known, applied especially to words of foreign or unknown origin, but of which the employment and application are familiar.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to be born, &c., and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढि|रूढिः
रूढि<BR>f. (-ढिः)<BR>1 Birth, production.<BR>2 Growing, growth.<BR>3 Fame, notoriety.<BR>4 Traditional or customary meaning of words, as opposed to their etymological signification; it is especially applied to words of foreign or uncertain origin, and incapable of etymological analysis.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=708" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढिशब्द|रूढिशब्दः
रूढिशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>A word used in a peculiar but familiar sense.<BR>E.<BR>रूढि, and शब्द noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप|रूपं
रूप<BR>r. 10th cl. (रूपयति)<BR>To form, to express form, to represent shape either to the eye or the understanding.<BR>With नि prefixed,<BR>1 To discuss, to investigate.<BR>2 To explain, to describe, to declare, to expound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप|रूपं
रूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Like, resembling, (in composition, as पितृरूपः पुत्त्रः a son like his father.)<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Natural property or disposition nature.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>3 Form, figure.<BR>4 Appearance, semblance.<BR>5 Cattle generally, flocks and herds, &c.<BR>6 A verse.<BR>7 Declension, conjugation, the inflection of nouns or verbs.<BR>8 A play, a dramatic poem.<BR>9 Acquiring familiarity with any book or authority by frequent perusal, learning by heart or rote.<BR>10 An image, a figure, a reflection or resemblance of any real object.<BR>11 Colour, form, any object of vision.<BR>12 (In arithmetic,) Discrete or distinct quantity, an entire number.<BR>13 Known quantity, whence the first syllable Rū is used in algebra to express the same.<BR>E.<BR>रूप to express form, aff. क, or रु to sound, Uṇādi aff. प, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपक|रूपकं|रूपकः
रूपक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A drama, a dramatic poem.<BR>2 Shape, form, figure.<BR>3 A figure of rhetoric in general.<BR>4 A particular class of rhetorical or poetical figures, including various modes of poetical description, or the illustration and exhibition of visible things and persons.<BR>5 Identification of the objects of a comparison; their being not only like, but the very same.<BR>6 Symptom of disease.<BR>f. (-पिका)<BR>Swallow wort.<BR>E.<BR>रूप form, figure, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपतत्त्व|रूपतत्त्वं
रूपतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>Natural or inherent disposition or property, nature.<BR>E.<BR>रूप form, and तत्त्व truth, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपधृत्
रूपधृत्<BR>mfn. (-धृत्)<BR>Having the form, resembling, like.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and धृ to have, क्विप् aff., and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपनाशन|रूपनाशनः
रूपनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>रूप form, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपभृत्
रूपभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Having form or beauty.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and भृ to possess, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपयत्
रूपयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Describing, representing.<BR>E.<BR>रूप to form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपलावण्य
रूपलावण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Elegance, loveliness.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and लावण्य beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपवत्|रूपवन्त्
रूपवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Having shape or colour, &c.<BR>2 Well-shaped, beautiful, handsome.<BR>E.<BR>रूप form, &c., and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपसम्पट्
रूपसम्पट्<BR>f. (-त् or -ट्)<BR>Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and सम्पट् fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपाजीवा
रूपाजीवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>रूप beauty, and आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपाधिबोध|रूपाधिबोधः
रूपाधिबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>The perception, evidence, or influence of the senses, i. e. of colour, sound, odour, flavour, and contact.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and अधिबोध perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपास्त्र|रूपास्त्रः
रूपास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>रूप beauty, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिन्
रूपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि)<BR>1 Beautiful, having a handsome form or shape.<BR>2 Having form or shape.<BR>E.<BR>रूप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्य|रूप्यं
रूप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 Wrought silver.<BR>3 Wrought gold.<BR>E.<BR>रूप form, colour, &c., and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्याध्यक्ष|रूप्याध्यक्षः
रूप्याध्यक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The master of the mint, the superintendant of the silver, or silver coinage.<BR>E.<BR>रूप्य silver, and अध्यक्ष superintendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूवुक|रूवुकः
रूवुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The castor oil tree, (Ricinus communis): see रूवु; also रूवूक, and रुवुक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूष
रूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (रूषति)<BR>To decorate, to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषक|रूषकः
रूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>E.<BR>रूष to adorn, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषित|रूषितं
रूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pounded, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>2 Covered, spread over, coated, inlaid.<BR>3 Adorned, decorated.<BR>4 Made rough or rugged.<BR>E.<BR>रूष to adorn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रे
रे<BR>A vocative particle, but expressive of contempt or disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक<BR>(ऋ) रेकृ r. 1st cl. (रेकते)<BR>1 To suspect or think probable.<BR>2 To excite or entertain doubt: in the last case with आङ् usually prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>2 Fear, apprehension.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Looseness, purging.<BR>2 An outcaste, a low man.<BR>3 A frog.<BR>E.<BR>रेक to suspect, to fear, aff. अच्, or रिच to purge, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेकणस्
रेकणस्<BR>n. (-णः)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>रिच to divide, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, नुट् augment, and च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखा
रेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A line, a continuous line.<BR>2 Deceit, fraud.<BR>3 A little.<BR>4 Fulness, satisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>see लेखा, the initial being changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचक|रेचकं|रेचकः
रेचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Purgative, aperient.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cathartic, a purgative.<BR>2 Nitre, saltpetre.<BR>3 The purging-nut plant, (Croton tiglium.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A purge.<BR>E.<BR>रिच् to evacuate by stool, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचन|रेचनं
रेचन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Purging, looseness.<BR>f. (-ना-नी)<BR>A drug, commonly Śuṇḍārocanī.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A plant, Tëori, (Convolvulus turpethum,) the white sort.<BR>2 Another plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>E.<BR>रिच to purge, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचित
रेचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left void or empty, freed from, cleared.<BR>2 Purged.<BR>E.<BR>रिच to purge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज
रेज<BR>(ऋ) रेजृ r. 1st cl. (रेजते)<BR>To shine: this root is not universally admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
रेज्<BR>m. (रेट्)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>रेज् to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेट
रेट<BR>(ऋ) रेदृ r. 1st cl. (रेटति-ते)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणु|रेणुः
रेणु<BR>mf. (-णुः-णु)<BR>Dust.<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Pāpar.<BR>E.<BR>रि to hurt, Uṇādi aff. नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुका
रेणुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of perfume and medicine, of a bitter and slightly pungent taste, and greyish colour; it is procured in grains about the size of those of pepper.<BR>2 The wife of the saint JAMADAGNI and mother of PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>3 A sort of pulse, (Ervum or Cicer lens.)<BR>E.<BR>रेणु sand, dust, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुकासुत|रेणुकासुतः
रेणुकासुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>PARAŚURĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रेणुका the mother of the hero, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुरूषित|रेणुरूषितः
रेणुरूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dusty, covered over with dust.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>रेणु dust, and रूषित made rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुवास|रेणुवासः
रेणुवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bee.<BR>E.<BR>रेणु dust (the pollen of flower), and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुसार|रेणुसारः
रेणुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>रेण dust, and सार essence; also with कन् added रेणुसारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतजा
रेतजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=709" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतन|रेतनं
रेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस्
रेतस्<BR>n. (-तः)<BR>1 The seminal fluid.<BR>2 Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>री to ooze, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्य|रेत्यं
रेत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>री to go, यत् aff., and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्र|रेत्रं
रेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 Quicksilver.<BR>3 Nectar or ambrosia.<BR>4 Perfumed or aromatic powder, pulvilio.<BR>E.<BR>री to flow, ष्ट्रन् aff., and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप<BR>(ऋ) रेपृ r. 1st cl. (रेपति-ते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>1 Low, vile, inferior, contemptible.<BR>2 Cruel, savage.<BR>E.<BR>रि to injure, प aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेपस्
रेपस्<BR>mfn. (-पाः-पाः-पः)<BR>1 Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>2 Cruel, savage.<BR>3 Miserly, niggardly, a miser.<BR>4 Wicked, abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>रप to speak, to revile, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, and ए substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफ|रेफः
रेफ<BR>mfn. (-फः-फा-फं)<BR>1 Low, vile, contemptible, wicked.<BR>2 Defamed, reviled.<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>1 The letter र्.<BR>2 Passion, affection of the mind.<BR>E.<BR>र the letter R with the inherent short vowel, and इफ aff.; or रिफ् to defame, to reproach, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफस्
रेफस्<BR>mfn. (-फाः-फाः-फः)<BR>1 Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>2 Wicked, abandoned.<BR>3 Miserly, a niggard.<BR>4 Cruel, savage.<BR>E.<BR>रिफ् to reproach, aff. असुन्; also रेफ, रेपस्, and रेप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेब
रेब<BR>(ऋ) रेबृ r. 1st cl. (रेबते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभ|रेभः
रेभ<BR>(ऋ) रेभृ r. 1st cl. (रेभते)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभण|रेभणं
रेभण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The lowing of kine.<BR>E.<BR>रेभ to sound, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिहाण|रेरिहाणः
रेरिहाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 An Asura; an evil spirit.<BR>3 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेव
रेव<BR>(ऋ) रेवृ (रेवते)<BR>1 To go by leaps or jumps, to leap, to jump.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR>3 To flow as a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवट|रेवटं|रेवटः
रेवट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A conch shell with sinistral convolutions, or the spiral lines turning from the right to the left.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Oil of the Morunga tree.<BR>2 A plantain, the fruit.<BR>3 A hog.<BR>4 Dust.<BR>5 A whirlwind.<BR>6 A conjuror, a juggler, a snake dancer.<BR>E.<BR>रेव to go, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत|रेवतः
रेवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A prince, the father of the wife of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवति|रेवतिः
रेवति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>The wife of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवती
रेवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The wife of BALARĀMA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 The last of the Nakṣatras or lunar asterisms, containing thirty two stars, figured by a tabor; one of the stars is ζ piscium.<BR>3 One of the Mātṛs or energies of the gods.<BR>4 A cow.<BR>E.<BR>रेवत the name of a king, the father of BALARĀMA'S wife, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीभव|रेवतीभवः
रेवतीभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The planet SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>रेवती the nymph or asterism personified, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीरमण|रेवतीरमणः
रेवतीरमण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रेवती the wife of BALARĀMA, and रमण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीश|रेवतीशः
रेवतीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>रेवत the wife of this demigod, and ईश lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्त|रेवन्तः
रेवन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The fifth MANU of the present Kalpa; also called RAIVATA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्तमनुसू
रेवन्तमनुसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>SAṂJÑĀ, wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>रेवन्त Revanta, मनु the MANU, and सू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवा
रेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 The Nerbadda, or Narmadā river, which rises in the mountain Āmrakūṭa, or Amerkantak, in the province of Gondvāna, and runs nearly due west about 750 miles, when it falls into the sea below Baroach.<BR>2 RATI, the wife of KĀMA.<BR>3 The indigo plant.<BR>E.<BR>रेव to flow, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष
रेष<BR>(ऋ) रेषृ r. 1st cl. (रेषते)<BR>1 To utter an inarticulate sound.<BR>2 To neigh.<BR>3 To howl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
रेष्<BR>mfn. (रेट्)<BR>Who or what neighs, howls, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रेष to neigh, विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषण|रेषणं
रेषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Howling, roaring.<BR>E.<BR>रेष to sound inarticulately, aff. ल्युट्; also with अङ् and टाप्, aff. रेषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषित
रेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, made as a noise.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Neighing, roaring.<BR>E.<BR>रेष to sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्टृ
रेष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>An injurer.<BR>E.<BR>रिष to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै<BR>r. 1st cl. (रायति)<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै<BR>m. (-राः)<BR>1 Wealth, property, substance.<BR>2 Gold.<BR>3 Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>रा to give, Uṇādi aff. डै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैत्य
रैत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्यी-त्यं)<BR>Brazen, made of brass.<BR>E.<BR>रीति, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत|रैवतः
रैवत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A mountain, the eastern part of the Vindhya range, or that part in which the Revā rises.<BR>2 A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 A Daitya or demon.<BR>5 The fifth MANU of the present Kalpa.<BR>E.<BR>रेवा the Revā river, aff. अञ्, and त added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतक|रैवतकं|रैवतकः
रैवतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The mountain Raivata.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding; also with ठक् added to रेवत, रैवतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोक|रोकं|रोकः
रोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>2 A boat.<BR>3 Moving, shaking.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Buying with ready money.<BR>2 Light.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग|रोगः
रोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease in general, or a disease.<BR>2 A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>रुज to be or make sick, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगग्रस्त
रोगग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगघ्न|रोगघ्नं
रोगघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Curative, medical.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगभू
रोगभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and भू the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगराज|रोगराजः
रोगराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Consumption.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and राज principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगलक्षण|रोगलक्षणं
रोगलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The symptoms or sign of a disease, or of its progress.<BR>E.<BR>रोग a disease, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशान्तक|रोगशान्तकः
रोगशान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A physician.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and शान्तक alleviator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशान्ति|रोगशान्तिः
रोगशान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Cure or alleviation of disease.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and शान्ति appeasing; also रोगशमः and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशिल्पिन्
रोगशिल्पिन्<BR>m. (-ल्पी)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and शिल्पिन् an artisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगह|रोगहं
रोगह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, हा to abandon, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहन्
रोगहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A physician.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and हन to destroy, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहर
रोगहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Curative, medicinal.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहारिन्
रोगहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Curative, medicinal.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A physician.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, हृ to remove, to take away, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगान्तक|रोगान्तकः
रोगान्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Curative, medicinal.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A physician.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगान्वित
रोगान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=710" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगार्त्त|रोगार्त
रोगार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Suffering pain or sickness.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिता
रोगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>रोगिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रोगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिन्
रोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Diseased, ill, sick, affected with sickness or disease.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिवल्लभ|रोगिवल्लभं
रोगिवल्लभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A drug, a medicament.<BR>E.<BR>रोगि a sick man, and वल्लभ the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगोपशम|रोगोपशमः
रोगोपशम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Cure or alleviation of disease.<BR>E.<BR>रोग, and उपशम allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग्य|रोग्यं
रोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>1 Counter-indicated, as menstrua or regimen, &c., what is improper to be taken in any disease or with the medicines administered.<BR>2 Related to or connected with disease.<BR>E.<BR>रोग sickness, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचक|रोचकः
रोचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What pleases, brightens, strengthens, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Hunger, appetite.<BR>2 The plantain.<BR>3 A sort of onion.<BR>4 A stomachic, a carminative, any medicine, fruit or fossil, supposed to strengthen the tone of the stomach and restore lost appetite.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, &c., and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचन|रोचनः
रोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>1 Splendid, beautiful.<BR>2 Irradiating, illumining, beautifying.<BR>3 Gratifying, pleasing.<BR>4 Whetting, sharpening, (the appetite.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A species of the silk-cotton tree.<BR>2 The onion.<BR>3 A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaca.)<BR>4 The Cassia fistula.<BR>5 The pomegranate.<BR>6 The citron.<BR>7 A stomachic, a carminative.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A yellow pigment, commonly Gorocanā, and supposed to be the concrete bile of the cow, or according to some authorities, to be found in the head of the animal, used as a medicine, a dye, and perfume.<BR>2 The manna of bambus.<BR>3 A excellent woman.<BR>4 A red lotus.<BR>f. (-ना-नी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Śuṇḍārocanī, a sort of Crinum?<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A variety of Tëori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>2 Red arsenic.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचनिका
रोचनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Śuṇḍārocanī.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to रोचनी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचमान|रोचमानः
रोचमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Splendid, shining.<BR>2 Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tuft or curl of hair round the neck of a horse or on the lower part of it.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, aff. शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिष्णु|रोचिष्णुः
रोचिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Elegantly dressed or ornamented.<BR>2 Splendid, brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिस्
रोचिस्<BR>n. (-चिः)<BR>Light.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, इसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोची
रोची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोच्य|रोच्यं
रोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>To be illuminated or enlightened.<BR>E.<BR>रुच to shine, aff. ण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोड|रोडः
रोड<BR>(ऋ) रोडृ r. 1st cl. (रोडति)<BR>1 To be mad.<BR>2 To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदन|रोदनं
रोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Weeping, crying.<BR>2 A tear, tears.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदस्
रोदस्<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>1 Heaven.<BR>2 Earth.<BR>dual. (-सी)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदसी
रोदसी<BR>f. (-सी).<BR>1 Heaven, paradise.<BR>2 Earth.<BR>f. dual. (-स्यौ)<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>ङीप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
रोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A bank, a shore.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to obstruct, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधन|रोधनः
रोधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Impeding, that which impedes or obstructs, an obstacle, a hinderer or hindrance.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Impeding, obstructing.<BR>2 Besieging, blockading.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to obstruct, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधवक्रा
रोधवक्रा<BR>f. (-क्रा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>रोध a bank, and वक्र the course of a stream, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधस्
रोधस्<BR>n. (-धः)<BR>A bank, a shore.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to obstruct, and असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधोवक्रा
रोधोवक्रा<BR>f. (-क्रा)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>रोधस् a bank, and वक्र winding course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्र|रोध्रं|रोध्रः
रोध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>n. (-घ्रं)<BR>1 Offence, transgression.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>रुध to obstruct, and रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
रोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 Confusing, disturbing, (the ideas.)<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A hole, a vacuity, a chasm.<BR>E.<BR>रुप to disturb, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपक|रोपकः
रोपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what plants, raises, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A weight of metal or a coin, the seventieth part of a Suvarṇa.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to rise, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपण|रोपणं|रोपणः
रोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Placing in or upon.<BR>2 Planting.<BR>3 Raising.<BR>4 A disturbing or bewildering of the mind, a confusing, or confusion of ideas.<BR>4 Cicatrizing, healing.<BR>5 A healing application to sores or wounds.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to ascend, causal v., or रुप to bewilder, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपित
रोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed in or upon.<BR>2 Planted.<BR>3 Raised, elevated. Bewildered, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to rise, causal v., or रुप to bewilder, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
रोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Water.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकर्णक|रोमकर्णकः
रोमकर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair, and कर्ण the ear, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकूप|रोमकूपः
रोमकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A pore of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair, and कूप a well, a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकेशर|रोमकेशरं
रोमकेशर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A Chowri.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair of an animal, (especially of the Yac,) and केशर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमगुच्छ|रोमगुच्छः
रोमगुच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>A Chowri, a sort of whisk.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair, (see the last word,) and गुच्छ a cluster; also with कन् added, रोमगुच्छक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्
रोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>रु to make, Uṇādi aff. मनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थ|रोमंथः|रोमन्थः
रोमन्थ<BR>n. (-न्थं)<BR>Ruminating, chewing the cud, or also eating, without chewing what has been once swallowed and again brought into the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>रोग disease, and मन्थ to destroy or remove, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.; this habit in animals being indispensable^1 to digestion and health.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमबद्ध
रोमबद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Made of or fastened with the hair of animals, (as horse hair, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>रोम, and बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमभूमि|रोमभूमिः
रोमभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>The skin.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair, and भूमि soil, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमलता
रोमलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A line of hair extending to the navel.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमवत्|रोमवन्त्
रोमवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Hairy, woolly.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair of the body, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविकार|रोमविकारः
रोमविकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair of the body, and विकार change of state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविक्रिया
रोमविक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair, and विक्रिया change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविध्वंश
रोमविध्वंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A body louse.<BR>E.<BR>रोम, and विध्वंश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमश|रोमशः
रोमश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Hairy, woolly.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A ram, a sheep.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>E.<BR>रोमन् hair, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्ष|रोमहर्षः
रोमहर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair of the body, and हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=711" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्षण|रोमहर्षणं|रोमहर्षणः
रोमहर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Horripilation, erection or rigidity of the hair of the body, conceived to be occasioned by and to express exquisite delight.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 SŪTA, the pupil of VYĀSA, and supposed narrator of the events recorded in the Purāṇas.<BR>2 Beleric myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair, and हर्ष्ण delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्च|रोमांच|रोमाञ्चः
रोमाञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>Horripilation, rigidity and erection of the hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>रोम the hair, अञ्च to worship, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्चित|रोमांचित|रोमाञ्चितः
रोमाञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having the hair of the body erect, considered as a proof of exquisite pleasure; enraptured, delighted.<BR>E.<BR>रोमाञ्च horripilation, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाली
रोमाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A line of hair, extending across the navel.<BR>E.<BR>रोमन् hair, and आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमावली
रोमावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A line of hair across the middle of the belly or navel.<BR>E.<BR>रोम, and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमोद्गम|रोमोद्गमः
रोमोद्गम<BR>m. (मः)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair, उद्गम rising; also रोमोद्ग m. (-द्गः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमोद्भेद|रोमोद्भेदः
रोमोद्भेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>रोम hair of the body, and उद्भेद breaking forth, protrusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदा
रोरुदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Violent weeping.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, frequent. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदावत्|रोरुदावन्त्
रोरुदावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Weeping or wailing violently.<BR>E.<BR>रोरुदा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुद्यमान
रोरुद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Crying bitterly.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, frequent. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोल|रोलः
रोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>2 Moist ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोलम्ब|रोलंबः|रोलम्बः
रोलम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>Distrustful, unbelieving.<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 A bee.<BR>2 Dry or arid soil.<BR>E.<BR>रोड to be mad, अम्बच् aff., and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोसंसा
रोसंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष|रोषः
रोष<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Anger, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषण|रोषणः
रोषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Angry, passionate.<BR>m. (-णं)<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>2 A touchstone.<BR>3 Arid or desart soil.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषवाहण
रोषवाहण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Angry, feeling and displaying wrath.<BR>E.<BR>रोष, and वह to bear, causal v., युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष्टृ
रोष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Violent, wrathful, angry.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be angry, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोह|रोहः
रोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A bud, a blossom.<BR>2 Mounting, ascending.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहक|रोहकः
रोहक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A rider, riding, mounted, one who rides on any animal or is carried in any vehicle.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sort of goblin.<BR>2 Rising, growing, mounting.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to rise, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहग
रोहग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The name of a mountain, Adam's peak in Ceylon.<BR>E.<BR>रोह rising, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहण|रोहणं|रोहणः
रोहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 Rising in or on, mounting, ascending.<BR>3 Growing as a plant.<BR>4 A mountain; see the last.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहन्त|रोहंतः|रोहन्तः
रोहन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A kind of tree.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. झच्, fem, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहि|रोहिः
रोहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A seed.<BR>3 A pious or religious man, one observing a vow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिण|रोहिणं|रोहिणः
रोहिण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The Indian fig tree.<BR>2 A fragrant grass.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A part of the fore-noon, extending to mid-day, in which Śrāddhas are especially to be observed.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. इनच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणिका
रोहिणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman red with anger, &c. or with red pigments.<BR>E.<BR>रोहिणी fem. form, of रोहित red, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीपति|रोहिणीपतिः
रोहिणीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रोहिणी the nymph, (see रोहिन्,) and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीवल्लभ|रोहिणीवल्लभः
रोहिणीवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रोहिणी the nymph, and वल्लभ the lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीश|रोहिणीशः
रोहिणीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>रोहिणी the nymph, and ईश lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित्
रोहित्<BR>m. (-हित्)<BR>The sun.<BR>f. (-हित्)<BR>1 A deer, a doe.<BR>2 A sort of creeper.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to go or grow, Uṇādi aff. इति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित|रोहितं|रोहितः
रोहित<BR>mfn. (रोहितः रोहिता or रोहिणी रोहितं)<BR>Red, of a red colour.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Red, (the colour.)<BR>2 The Rohi fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>3 A kind of deer.<BR>4 A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka, Rox.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 INDRA'S bow unbent and invisible to mortals.<BR>2 Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>3 Blood.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow or go, Uṇādi aff. इतन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितक|रोहितकः
रोहितक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितश्व
रोहितश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>1 A name of AGNI.<BR>2 The son of HARIŚCANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>रेहित् a deer, or red, and अश्व a horse; also from रोहित sometimes read रोहिताश्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितिका
रोहितिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose face is stained with red pigments, or who is red with rage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>रोहित red, fem. form, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितेय|रोहितेयः
रोहितेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka.)<BR>E.<BR>रोहित the same, ढक् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिन्
रोहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>1 The Indian fig tree.<BR>2 The holy fig tree.<BR>3 The Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR>f. (-हिणिः-हिणी)<BR>1 The fourth lunar asterism, figured by a wheeled carriage, and containing five stars, probably, α β γ δ ε Tauri; in mythology, the asterism is personified as one of the daughters of Dakṣa, and wives of the moon.<BR>2 The mother of BALARĀMA.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 One of the Vidyādevīs of the Jainas.<BR>2 A cow.<BR>3 Inflammatory affection of the throat.<BR>4 Lightning.<BR>5 The name of a medicinal plant.<BR>6 The moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>7 A woman stained with red pigments, or red with passion, &c.<BR>8 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>9 Bengal madder.<BR>10 A girl nine years old.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिष|रोहिषः
रोहिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A sort of grass.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The Rohi, a kind of fish.<BR>2 A deer said to resemble an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्ष्य|रौक्ष्यं
रौक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Roughness, ruggedness.<BR>2 Harshness, unkindness.<BR>E.<BR>रुक्ष hard, व्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौचनिक
रौचनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Died or coloured with Rocana, of a yellowish or orange tint.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The tartar of the teeth.<BR>E.<BR>रोचना a pigment, and ठ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौच्य|रौच्यः
रौच्य<BR>m. (-च्यः)<BR>An ascetic with a staff of Bilva wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौट
रौट<BR>(ऋ) रौटृ r. 1st cl. (रौटति)<BR>To treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौड
रौड<BR>(ऋ) रौडृ r. 1st cl. (रौडति)<BR>To treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्र|रौद्रं|रौद्रः
रौद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>1 Formidable, fearful, terrific.<BR>2 Sharp, acute.<BR>3 Relating or belonging to RUDRA or ŚIVA.<BR>4 Violent, wrathful, irascible.<BR>mn. (-द्रः-द्रं)<BR>Wrath, rage, (the sentiment as an object of poetical description)<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 Heat, warmth.<BR>2 The cold season.<BR>3 YAMA.<BR>f. (-द्री)<BR>GAURI, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, &c., and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=712" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रता
रौद्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Fierceness, formidableness.<BR>E.<BR>रौद्र, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रौद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रदर्शन
रौद्रदर्शन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Formidable, terrific.<BR>E.<BR>रौद्र, and दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्य|रौप्यं
रौप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्यी-प्यं)<BR>Silver, of silver.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>रूप्य the same, अण् pleonasm or aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौम|रौमं
रौम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A sort of salt; see the next.<BR>E.<BR>रुम the place where it is found, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमक|रौमकं
रौमक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A kind of salt, according to some authorities, brought from a mountain in Ajmere, but in fact procured from a salt lake near the town of Sāmbher, about twenty miles west of Jayanagar.<BR>E.<BR>रुम the district of Ruma or Sāmbher, aff. अण्, and कन् added; also रौम, and रौमलवण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमलवण|रौमलवणं
रौमलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sāmbher salt; see the last.<BR>E.<BR>रौम as above, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरव|रौरवः
रौरव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Formidable, horrible, terrific.<BR>2 Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>3 Unsteady, slipping.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 One of the divisions of Naraka or Tartarus.<BR>2 A savage, a monster.<BR>E.<BR>रुद to weep, deriv. irr., or रुरु said to mean a living being, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिण|रौहिणं|रौहिणः
रौहिण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणेय|रौहिणेयं|रौहिणेयः
रौहिणेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>2 The planet MERCURY.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An emerald.<BR>mf. (-यः-यी)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>रोहिणी the nymph, &c., and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिष|रौहिषं|रौहिषः
रौहिष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A sort of deer.<BR>2 The Rohi fish.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A kind of grass.<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, Uṇādi aff. ठिषच्, and the vowel changed to औ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल<BR>The twenty-eighth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, the letter L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल<BR>m. (लः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 Cutting.<BR>f. (ला)<BR>1 Giving.<BR>2 Receiving, taking.<BR>f. (ली)<BR>1 Embracing, adhering or clinging to.<BR>2 Liquifying, melting.<BR>E.<BR>ला to give or take, &c., aff. क or ड, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक|लकः
लक<BR>r. 10th cl. (लाकयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक|लकः
लक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The forehead.<BR>2 The ear or spike of wild rice.<BR>E.<BR>लक to taste, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकच|लकचः
लकच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A tree: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुच|लकुचः
लकुच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A species of the bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus Lacucha, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>लक to taste, उच aff.; also अ substituted for उ, लकच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तक|लक्तकः
लक्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Old and tattered cloth, a rag or rags.<BR>2 Lac, the dye.<BR>E.<BR>लक to obtain, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तकर्मन्|लक्तकर्म्मन्
लक्तकर्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A tree used in dyeing, a red variety of the Lodh tree.<BR>E.<BR>लक्त for रक्त coloured, and कर्म्मन् office, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष|लक्षं
लक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (लक्षयति-ते)<BR>1 To see, to look at, to notice or inspect.<BR>2 To mark, to make any mark on.<BR>3 To define, to discriminate.<BR>With उप prefixed,<BR>To remark.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To know, to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष|लक्षं
लक्ष<BR>nf. (-क्षं-क्षा)<BR>A Lac, one hundred thousand.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 Fraud, disguise.<BR>2 A mark or butt.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark, or see, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण|लक्षणं|लक्षणः
लक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A mark, a spot.<BR>2 A name, an appellation.<BR>3 Sight, seeing.<BR>4 An indication, a predicate, any thing by which an object is designated or distinguished.<BR>5 A symptom or any indication of actual disease.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>2 The Indian crane.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The female of the Indian crane.<BR>2 A goose.<BR>3 An ellipsis, a word, &c. understood, though not inserted.<BR>4 The force or application of a word or phrase.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to see, to mark, aff. ल्युट्, or लक्ष as before, Uṇādi aff. न, and अट् augment; also with मुट् augment, लक्ष्मण, which in the masc. and fem. forms is the more usual reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षित|लक्षितः
लक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen.<BR>2 Marked.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मण|लक्ष्मणं|लक्ष्मणः
लक्ष्मण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Prosperous, fortunate.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The son of DAŚARATHA by SUMITRĀ, the half-brother and faithful companion of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>2 The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A mark, a spot or sign.<BR>2 A name, an appellation.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The female of the Sāras.<BR>2 A kind of drug.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark or see, Uṇādi aff. न, and मुट् augment; also with अट् augment, लक्षण as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मणप्रसू
लक्ष्मणप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>SUMITRĀ, one of DAŚARATHA'S four wives, the mother of LAKṢMAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मण, प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मन्
लक्ष्मन्<BR>n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>1 A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR>2 Chief, principal.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark, &c., मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मी
लक्ष्मी<BR>f. (-क्ष्मीः)<BR>1 LAKṢMĪ, one of the three principal female deities of the Hindus, the wife of VIṢṆU, and goddess of wealth and prosperity.<BR>2 Fortune, success, prosperity.<BR>3 SĪTĀ the wife of RĀMA.<BR>4 Beauty, splendour.<BR>5 The name of a medicinal root, commonly Vṛddhi.<BR>6 Another root, termed Ṛddhi.<BR>7 A plant: see प्रियङ्गु.<BR>8 The wife of a hero.<BR>9 Turmeric.<BR>10 A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to see, &c., Uṇādi aff. ई, and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीगृह|लक्ष्मीगृहं
लक्ष्मीगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess, and गृह abode, appearing at the creation, floating over the water on the expanded petals of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपति|लक्ष्मीपतिः
लक्ष्मीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A king, a sovereign prince.<BR>3 The clove tree.<BR>4 The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel)<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess of prosperity, and पति master, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपल
लक्ष्मीपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुत्त्र
लक्ष्मीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>3 Either of the sons of RĀMA and SĪTĀ.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess, or SĪTĀ, (she being LAKṢMĪ. incarnate,) and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुष्प|लक्ष्मीपुष्पः
लक्ष्मीपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess of fortune, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीमत्
लक्ष्मीमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>The bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी prosperity, मतुप् aff., and the म unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीवत्|लक्ष्मीवन्त्
लक्ष्मीवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Prosperous, fortunate, wealthy, thriving.<BR>2 Beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी prosperity, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीश|लक्ष्मीशः
लक्ष्मीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The mango tree.<BR>3 A prosperous man.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess of fortune, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीसहज|लक्ष्मीसहजः
लक्ष्मीसहज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess, सह with, ज born; rising as well as LAKṢMĪ from the ocean, at the time it was churned by the gods and Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=713" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्य|लक्ष्यं|लक्ष्यः
लक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 To be seen or noted.<BR>2 To be defined or described.<BR>3 To have attributes or predicates attached.<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 A mark, a butt.<BR>2 A mark, a sign.<BR>3 Fraud, disguise.<BR>4 A Lac, a hundred thousand.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to see, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लख
लख<BR>r. 1st cl. (लखति) (इ) लखि (लंखति)<BR>To go, to move, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग
लग<BR>(ए) लगे r. 1st cl. (लगति)<BR>To be with or near, to touch, to be in contact or union with.<BR>(इ) लगि r. 1st cl. (लंगनि)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To go limpingly, to be lame.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लागयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगड|लगडं
लगड<BR>mfn. (-डः-डा-डं)<BR>Beautiful, handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगित|लगितं
लगित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Obtained, gained.<BR>2 Connected with, attached to.<BR>E.<BR>लग to be in contact with, aff. क्त, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुड|लगुडः
लगुड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A staff, a stick.<BR>2 An iron club, or one bound with iron.<BR>E.<BR>लग to go, aff. डुलच्, and ल changed to ड; also लगुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुर|लगुरः
लगुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A club, a stick.<BR>E.<BR>see the last; ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुरहस्त
लगुरहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A man armed with a stick, a mace or staffbearer.<BR>E.<BR>लगुर, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्न|लग्नं|लग्नः
लग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Attached to, intent on.<BR>2 Ashamed.<BR>3 Joined to, connected with.<BR>n. (-ग्नं)<BR>The rising of a sign, its appearance above the horizon; the oblique ascension, or the divisions of the equator, which rise in succession with each sign in an oblique sphere; also defined as the arc of the equator, which passes the meridian in the same time with each sign of the ecliptic; in popular acceptation it is the moment of the sun's entrance into a zodiacal sign.<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>A bard, a panegyrist.<BR>E.<BR>लग to be with or near, or लस्ज to be ashamed, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नक|लग्नकः
लग्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A security, a surety.<BR>E.<BR>लग्न engaged or associated, (in the business,) aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नभुज|लग्नभुजः
लग्नभुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Ascensional difference.<BR>E.<BR>लग्न, and भुज arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्निका
लग्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A girl ten years old, one before menstruation.<BR>E.<BR>लस्ज to be ashamed, aff. कन्, fem. form; also नग्निका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ
लघ<BR>r. 10th cl. (-लाघयति)<BR>1 To taste.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR>(इ) लघि r. 1st cl. (लंघते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To fast, to abstain from food.<BR>(लङ्घति)<BR>1 To dry, to dry up.<BR>2 To diminish, to lessen.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लङ्घयति)<BR>To speak.<BR>With उत् or वि prefixed,<BR>To go beyond or over, to cross, to pass, to leap or spring over; also morally, to exceed, to transgress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघट्
लघट्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to go, अटि Uṇādi aff., and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघटि|लघटिः
लघटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to go, Uṇādi aff. अटिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिमन्
लघिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Lightness, absence of weight.<BR>2 Diminutiveness.<BR>3 Insignificance.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, aff. इमनिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिष्ठ|लघिष्ठः
लघिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Lightest, very light.<BR>2 Very small, least.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघीयस्
लघीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Lightest, most or very light.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, and ईयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघु|लघुः
लघु<BR>mfn. (-घुः-घुः-घ्वी-घु)<BR>1 Light, not heavy.<BR>2 Swift, quick.<BR>3 Sapless, pithless.<BR>4 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>5 Small, little.<BR>6 Light, vain, frivolous.<BR>7 Insignificant, mean, low.<BR>8 Weak, feeble.<BR>9 Clean, pure.<BR>10 Short, (as a vowel.)<BR>n. adv. (-घु)<BR>Quickly, swiftly.<BR>subst. (-घु)<BR>1 A black kind of Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>2 The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>f. (-घुः)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>f. (-घ्वी)<BR>1 A slight or delicate woman.<BR>2 A small light carriage.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to go, Uṇādi aff. कु, and the nasal not inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुकाय|लघुकायः
लघुकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>लघु small, and काय a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुखद्विका
लघुखद्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small bedstead.<BR>E.<BR>लघु small, खद्विका a bedstead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुगर्ग|लघुगर्गः
लघुगर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A kind of fish, probably a variety of the Pimelodus.<BR>E.<BR>लघु small, and गर्ग for गर्गर a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुचेतस्
लघुचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Low-minded, frivolous.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुजङ्गल|लघुजंगल|लघुजङ्गलः
लघुजङ्गल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of quail.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, जङ्गल flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुता
लघुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Lightness.<BR>2 Meanness, insignificance.<BR>E.<BR>तल added to लघु; also with त्व, लघुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुदुन्दुभि|लघुदुन्दुभिः
लघुदुन्दुभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A small kettle-drum.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, small, and दुन्दुभि a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुपत्रक|लघुपत्रकः
लघुपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Śuṇḍārocanī, (Crinum?)<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, small, and पत्रक a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुप्रयत्न
लघुप्रयत्न<BR>mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>Indolent, impotent.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and प्रयत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमांस|लघुमांसः
लघुमांस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, (of digestion,) and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमित्र
लघुमित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A friend or ally of little power or value.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुलय|लघुलयं
लघुलय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum).<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, लय contexture (in Tatties, &c.) or लघु and लय, both meaning the same root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवासस्
लघुवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>1 Thinly or lightly dressed.<BR>2 Wearing clean or pure clothing.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवृत्ति
लघुवृत्ति<BR>mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>1 Low, vile.<BR>2 Ill done, mismanaged.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवृत्तिता
लघुवृत्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Insignificance, meanness.<BR>2 Mismanagement, bad conduct.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमूल
लघुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>In algebra, the least root with reference to the additive quantities.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुहस्त|लघुहस्तः
लघुहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Ready or light-handed.<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A good archer.<BR>E.<BR>लघु quick, and हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघूकरण
लघूकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Reducing in weight or consequence.<BR>2 Thinking little of, contemning.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघूकृत
लघूकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made light, reduced in weight.<BR>2 Reduced in consequence, made insignificant.<BR>3 Thought lightly of.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वाशिन्
लघ्वाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Eating little, moderate.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वाहार
लघ्वाहार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Temperate, abstemious.<BR>E.<BR>लघु, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्का|लंका
लङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>1 The capital of RĀVAṆA in Ceylon; the name is extended also to the island, which according to the notions of the Hindus, is much more considerable in size, and lies further from the continent than in reality; it is described as being equal to 1/12th of the equatorial circumference of the earth, and is one of the places lying under the first meridian, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">Page715</a>] whence the longitude is computed; it is thus placed in the Eastern ocean, South of Ceylon, and according to WILFORD is the peninsula of Malacca: according to some Hindu accounts also, it is distinct from Ceylon, from which island Laṅkā is said to be just visible.<BR>2 A goddess or evil spirit, one of the Śākinīs, perhaps the same as the tutelar deity of the city of Laṅkā.<BR>3 An unchaste woman.<BR>4 A branch.<BR>E.<BR>लक to obtain (happiness, in which), aff. अच्, and नुग irr. augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=714" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कादाहिन्|लंकादाहिन्
लङ्कादाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>The monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>लङ्का the city, and दाहिन् burner; having set fire to the city with his burning tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कापति|लंकापति|लङ्कापतिः
लङ्कापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>RĀVAṆA the Daitya.<BR>E.<BR>लङ्का the city, and पति master, ruler; also लङ्काधिपति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कायिका
लङ्कायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>लक to taste, root of the 10th cl. aff. ण्वुल् fem. form, and नुम् augment; also य being changed to प, लङ्कापिका, and by a different derivation लङ्कोपिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कास्थायिन्
लङ्कास्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Residing or being in Laṅkā.<BR>m.<BR>A plant.<BR>(-नी)<BR>(Euphorbia Tirucalli.)<BR>E.<BR>लङ्का Laṅkā or Ceylon, and स्थायिन् what abides or grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्केश|लंकेश|लङ्केशः
लङ्केश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The Daitya RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>लङ्का the city Laṅkā, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कोपिका
लङ्कोपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>E.<BR>लङ्का Laṅkā or Ceylon, वप to sow or be sown, aff. क्वुन् fem. form, and the semivowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्खनी|लंखनी
लङ्खनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग|लंग|लंगः|लङ्गः
लङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः.)<BR>1 Union, association, proximate connection.<BR>2 A lecher, a catamite.<BR>3 Limping, lameness.<BR>E.<BR>लगि to be near or with, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गूल|लंगूल|लंगूलं|लङ्गूलं
लङ्गूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The tail of an animal.<BR>E.<BR>लगि to go, ऊलच् aff., more commonly लाङ्गूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घन|लंघन|लंघनं|लङ्घनं
लङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Fasting, abstinence.<BR>2 Going, proceeding.<BR>3 Leaping, springing, going by leaps or jumps.<BR>4 Jumping over or beyond.<BR>5 Exceeding, transgressing, disregarding propriety, going beyond proper bounds.<BR>6 Storming a fort, entering by escalade, &c.<BR>7 Capturing a fort in any way.<BR>8 One of a horse's paces, curvetting, bounding.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to go, to fast, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घनीय|लंघनीय
लङ्घनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be passed.<BR>2 Transgressible.<BR>3 To be fasted.<BR>E.<BR>लघि to go, अनीयर् aff.; also लङ्घ्य and लङ्घितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लच्छ|लछ
लच्छ<BR>r. 1st cl. (लच्छति)<BR>To mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज
लज<BR>r. 1st cl. (लजति) also (इ) लजि (लञ्जति)<BR>1 To fry.<BR>2 To affront, to insult.<BR>(ओ ई) ओलजी r. 6th cl. (लजति-ते)<BR>To be ashamed, to be modest or bashful.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लाजयति)<BR>To hide, to cover, to screen or clothe:<BR>also (लजति) or (इ) लजि (लञ्जयति)<BR>1 To be manifest or apparent.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(इ) लजि (लञ्जयति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To dwell.<BR>3 To injure.<BR>4 To be strong.<BR>5 To censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लजकारिका
लजकारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>लज for लज्जा shame, कारिका making, shewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जत्
लज्जत्<BR>mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्)<BR>Being ashamed, blushing, shrinking.<BR>E.<BR>लस्ज to be ashamed, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जमान
लज्जमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>लस्ज to be ashamed, aff. शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जा
लज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>Shame, modesty, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>लस्ज to be modest, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाकर
लज्जाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रा-रं)<BR>Shameful, causing shame.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाकारिन्
लज्जाकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-रि-रिणी-रि)<BR>Causing or occasioning shame.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and कारिन् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जान्वित
लज्जान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ashamed, bashful.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जारहित
लज्जारहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shameless, immodest.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जालु|लज्जालुः
लज्जालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा shame, हालुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जावत्|लज्जावन्त्
लज्जावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Modest, bashful.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाशील|लज्जाशीलः
लज्जाशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bashful, modest.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा modest, शील possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाहीन
लज्जाहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shameless, impudent.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जित|लज्जितः
लज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ashamed, modest.<BR>E.<BR>लज्जा Modesty, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्ज्या
लज्ज्या<BR>f. (-ज्ज्या)<BR>Modesty, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>लस्ज to be ashamed, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज|लंज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लञ्ज<BR>r. 10th cl. (लञ्जयति)<BR>1 To be manifest.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज|लंज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लञ्ज<BR>m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>1 A foot.<BR>2 The end of the lower garment tucked into the waist band.<BR>3 A tail.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>1 An adulteress.<BR>2 Sleep.<BR>3 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>4 A current.<BR>E.<BR>लजि to be strong, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्जिका|लंजिका
लञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>लजि to censure, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट|लटः
लट<BR>r. 1st cl. (लटति)<BR>1 To be a child, to talk or be like one.<BR>2 To speak a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट|लटः
लट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A block head, a fool, one speaking ignorantly or foolishly.<BR>2 Fault, defect.<BR>3 A thief.<BR>E.<BR>लट to be or talk as a child, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटक|लटकः
लटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vile or contemptible man.<BR>E.<BR>लट to talk as a child, and वुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्ट|लट्टः
लट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A vile or bad man, a wretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्व|लट्वः
लट्व<BR>m. (-ट्वः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A division of music.<BR>3 A low and wild tribe, a tribe of mountaineers.<BR>f. (-ट्वा)<BR>1 A bird said, to be a kind of sparrow.<BR>2 A fruit, a variety of the Karanja.<BR>3 A bad or unchaste woman.<BR>4 Curls on the forehead or hanging down on the face.<BR>5 Safflower.<BR>6 A Sweetmeat.<BR>E.<BR>लट to be like a child, Uṇādi aff. क्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड
लड<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (लडति लडयति)<BR>1 To frolic, to sport or dally.<BR>2 To loll (the tongue.)<BR>3 To use the tongue.<BR>4 To stir with the tongue.<BR>5 To stir, to agitate.<BR>6 To pain.<BR>r. 10th cl. (-लाडयति)<BR>1 To nurse, to foster, to attend closely.<BR>2 To shake.<BR>3 To feel desire.<BR>(औ इ) औलडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (लंडति लंडयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To toss or throw up.<BR>3 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लडह|लडहः
लडह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Beautiful, pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्ड|लड्डः
लड्ड<BR>m. (-ड्डः)<BR>A wretch, a villain, a low or bad man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्डुक|लड्डुकः
लड्डुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A class of sweetmeats, or a sweetmeat; a sort of ball made with flour fried with oil or Ghee, and mixed with sugar and spices, and distinguished into different kinds, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">Page716</a>] according to some slight varieties in its less essential ingredients; also read लड्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=715" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लता
लता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A creeper, a creeping or winding plant in general.<BR>2 A branch.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>4 A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>5 Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)<BR>6 The large Bengal creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>7 A sort of grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>8 A vegetable and medicinal substance, commonly Latākastūrī or the musk-creeper, said to grow in the Dekshin.<BR>9 Thread.<BR>E.<BR>लत a Sautra root, to hurt, to enfold, &c., aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताकस्तूरिका
लताकस्तूरिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Latākastūrī.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and कस्तूरिका musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताजिह्व|लताजिह्वः
लताजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and जिह्वा the tongue, which becomes masc. in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतातरु|लतातरुः
लतातरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 The orange tree.<BR>2 The palm tree.<BR>3 The Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and तरु a tree: fit for creepers to cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताद्रुम|लताद्रुमः
लताद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A timber tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतान्त|लतांत
लतान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>A flower.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतापनस|लतापनसः
लतापनस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The water-melon.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and पनस the jack, to the fruit of which the melon may be compared in size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताप्रतानिनी
लताप्रतानिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A spreading creeper.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and प्रतानिनी spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामणि|लतामणिः
लतामणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामरुत्
लतामरुत्<BR>f. (-रुत्)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामाधवी
लतामाधवी<BR>f. (-बी)<BR>The Mādhavī creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper in general, माधबी the particular one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामृग|लतामृगः
लतामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>An ape or monkey.<BR>E.<BR>लता, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतायष्टि|लतायष्टिः
लतायष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and यष्टि stick or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतायावक|लतायावकं
लतायावक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Coral.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, यावक barley, or similar grain; of similar shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतारसन|लतारसनः
लतारसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and रसना the tongue, but made masc. in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतार्क|लतार्कः
लतार्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>A green onion.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and अर्क to heat, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतालक|लतालकः
लतालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and अलक a curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतावेष्टन
लतावेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, and वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतावेष्टितक|लतावेष्टितकं
लतावेष्टितक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>An embrace, embracing.<BR>E.<BR>लता a creeper, (like it,) वेष्टित a surrounding or enfolding, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताशङ्ख|लताशङ्खः
लताशङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.) This word is elsewhere read लताशङ्कु or लतातरु and शङ्कुतरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतिका
लतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A twining plant.<BR>E.<BR>लता the same, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लत्तिका
लत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lizard.<BR>E.<BR>लत a Sautra root, to hurt, तिकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप
लप<BR>(ऋ) लपृ r. 1st cl. (लपति)<BR>To speak, to utter.<BR>With अनु prefixed,<BR>1 To talk like, to mimic.<BR>2 To repeat.<BR>With अप,<BR>To deny.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To address, to speak to.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To talk incoherently^1.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To gain, to get.<BR>With वि,<BR>To lament, to bewail.<BR>With वि and प्र,<BR>To contradict, to dispute.<BR>With सम,<BR>1 To converse, to discourse.<BR>2 To be cunning or crafty.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपन|लपनं
लपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The mouth.<BR>2 Talking.<BR>E.<BR>लप to speak, ल्युट् aff. of the instrument or act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपित|लपितं
लपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken, said.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Voice or speech.<BR>E.<BR>लप to speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब|लबः
लब<BR>(इ) लबि r. 1st cl. (लंबते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To fall or tumble, to be prostrate.<BR>With अव prefixed,<BR>1 To hold, to support.<BR>2 To hang from or on, to depend from.<BR>3 To rest upon.<BR>4 To hang with the head downwards.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To trust in, to depend on.<BR>With वि,<BR>To delay, to detain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध|लब्धः
लब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Gained, acquired, obtained, received, got.<BR>f. (-ब्धा)<BR>A woman whose husband or lover is faithless.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धचेतस्
लब्धचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>Recovered, restored to one's senses, come to a right mind.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and चेतस् intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धजन्मन्
लब्धजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Born.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धधन
लब्धधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धवर्ण|लब्धवर्णः
लब्धवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Sage, learned, a sage, a Paṇḍita.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध got, and वर्ण praise, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धविद्य
लब्धविद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Learned.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धसंज्ञ
लब्धसंज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Revived, recovered from fainting.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and संज्ञा consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धावकाश
लब्धावकाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Having found an opportunity or interval.<BR>E.<BR>लब्ध, and अवकाश opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्रिम
लब्ध्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Obtained.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to gain, क्त्रिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्वा
लब्ध्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having gained or got.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get, क्त्राच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ
लभ<BR>(डु अष) औख्^1 r. 1st cl. (लभते)<BR>To obtain, to get or gain.<BR>(इ) लभि r. 1st cl. (लम्भते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To injure.<BR>3 To revile.<BR>4 To gain.<BR>With उप prefixed.<BR>1 To apprehend, to understand.<BR>2 To delay.<BR>With उप and आङ्,<BR>To revile, to abuse.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभस|लभसः
लभस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Wealth.<BR>2 A solicitor, one who asks or solicits.<BR>3 A horse's foot rope.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get, Uṇādi aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्य|लभ्यं
लभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>1 Attainable, procurable.<BR>2 Fit, right, proper.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लमक|लमकः
लमक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lover, a gallant.<BR>E.<BR>रम to sport, Uṇādi aff. वुन्, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पट|लंपट|लम्पटः
लम्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A lecher, a libertine, a whore-monger, a gallant.<BR>2 The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पटता
लम्पटता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Libertinism, dissoluteness.<BR>E.<BR>लम्पट, and तल् aff.; also लम्पटत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पाक|लंपाक|लम्पाकः
लम्पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A country, the district of Lamghan in Cabul.<BR>2 A libertine, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पापटह|लम्पापटहः
लम्पापटह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A kettle drum, a state drum, the Nakāra of the Muselmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब|लंब|लम्बः
लम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>1 Spacious, capacious.<BR>2 Great, large, broad, long, expanded either in breadth or length, or both.<BR>3 Pendulous, depending.<BR>m. (-म्बं)<BR>1 A bribe, a present.<BR>2 Moving a man at a sort of backgammon or draughts.<BR>3 A perpendicular, (in geometry.)<BR>4 (In astronomy,) The arc between the pole and zenith of any place.<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>1 A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 A name of GAURĪ or DURGĀ.<BR>3 A bitter gourd.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to fall, to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=716" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बक|लंबक|लंबकः|लम्बकः
लम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A section, a chapter.<BR>2 A perpendicular, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लवि to fall, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बकर्ण|लंबकर्ण|लम्बकर्णः
लम्बकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A goat.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 A goblin or Rākṣasa.<BR>4 A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>5 A hare.<BR>6 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>लम्ब large or pendulous, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बज्या
लम्बज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>Sine or cosine of the latitude.<BR>E.<BR>लम्ब, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बन|लंबन|लम्बनं|लंबनः|लम्बनः
लम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Depending, descending, falling.<BR>2 A long necklace, one which depends from the neck to the navel.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to fall, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बमान|लम्बमानं
लम्बमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Depending, descending, hanging or falling, going down.<BR>2 Being large or bulky.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to fall, &c., and शानच् aff., मुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बिका|लंबिका
लम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The uvula or soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to hang down, aff. क्वुन् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बित|लंबित|लम्बितः
लम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suspended, depending, falling or hanging down.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to fall down, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बुषा|लंबुषा
लम्बुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A necklace of seven strings.<BR>E.<BR>लबि to depend, उषच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बोदर|लंबोदर|लम्बोदरः
लम्बोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A glutton.<BR>E.<BR>लम्ब large, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बौष्ठ|लंबौष्ठ|लम्बौष्ठः
लम्बौष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>लम्ब large, and ओष्ठ a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भन|लंभन|लंभनं|लम्भनं
लम्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abuse, reviling.<BR>2 Gaining, getting.<BR>E.<BR>लभि to sound, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भयत्
लम्भयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Causing to get, procuring, producing.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भा
लम्भा<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>A sort of chain enclosure or fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भित|लंभित
लम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Caused to get, given to, procured for.<BR>2 Applied to, employed, adapted.<BR>3 Spoken to, addressed.<BR>4 Heightened, improved, rendered more perfect or intense.<BR>5 Cherished.<BR>6 Gained.<BR>7 Abused.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to gain, causal form, or लभि to revile, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय|लयः
लय<BR>r. 1st cl. (लयते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय|लयः
लय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Equal time in music and dancing.<BR>2 Adhering or clinging to, embracing, uniting.<BR>3 A house, a dwelling.<BR>4 Sport, pastime.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>2 Loss, destruction.<BR>3 Fusion, melting.<BR>E.<BR>ली to adhere to, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयपुत्त्री
लयपुत्त्री<BR>f. (-त्त्री)<BR>An actress, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>लय equal time in music, &c., and पुत्त्री the daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयालम्ब|लयालम्बः
लयालम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR>E.<BR>लय equal time, &c., and आलम्ब who moves to; it also occurs लयारम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लर्व्व|लर्व
लर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (लर्वति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल
लल<BR>r. 1st cl. (ललति)<BR>1 To sport, to dally.<BR>2 To loll, as the tongue, &c.: see लड, of which it is considered as a various reading only.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लालयते)<BR>1 To desire, to wish for, to seek to obtain.<BR>2 To sport, to wanton.<BR>3 To lay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल
लल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Sporting, frolicking.<BR>2 Lolling, wagging.<BR>3 Wishing, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>लड or लल to sport, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललजिह्व
ललजिह्व<BR>mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>Fierce, savage, (as a beast of prey, &c.)<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>E.<BR>लल lapping, licking, and जिह्व the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललत्
ललत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Shaking, tremulous.<BR>2 Licking, lapping, stirring or touching with the tongue, lolling the tongue, &c.<BR>3 Wantoning, dallying.<BR>E.<BR>लड to loll, to frolick, &c. participial aff. शतृ, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललदम्बु|ललदम्बुः
ललदम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>लल trembling, अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन|ललनं|ललनः
ललन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Pleasure, sport, pastime.<BR>2 Lolling the tongue.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Śāl tree.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A woman in general.<BR>2 A wanton woman.<BR>3 The tongue.<BR>E.<BR>लड to frolic, &c., aff. ल्युट्, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन्तिका|ललंतिका
ललन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A necklace hanging as low as the navel.<BR>2 A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>E.<BR>ललत् sporting, lolling, &c. fem. form, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाक|ललाकः
ललाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>लड to frolick, aff. आकन्, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाट|ललाटं
ललाट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>लल wish or dalliance, from लड with अच् aff., and अट् to go or be, aff. अण्; also with कन् added ललाटक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटतट
ललाटतट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट, and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटन्तप|ललाटंतप|ललाटंतपः|ललाटन्तपः
ललाटन्तप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Burning, scorching, (as the sun.)<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट the forehead, तप to scorch or inflame, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटपट्ट|ललाटपट्टः
ललाटपट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>1 A tiara, a fillet.<BR>2 The forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट, and पट्ट a cloth or any flat surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटफलक
ललाटफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The open forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट, and फलक a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटरेखा
ललाटरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A line on the forehead, supposed to indicate long life.<BR>2 A wrinkled or corrugated brow.<BR>3 A coloured sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट the forehead, and रेखा a line; also ललाटलेखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटिका
ललाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An ornament worn on the forehead, a jewel or star suspended there, or a kind of tiara bound over it.<BR>2 A mark made with Sandal on the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट the forehead, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाम|ललामं|ललामः
ललाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Beautiful, agreeable, charming, (in this sense some authorities confine it to the neuter gender, and to its use compounded with another word.)<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A mark or sign.<BR>2 A banner, a flag, a symbol or ensign.<BR>3 A mark on the forehead.<BR>4 A horn.<BR>5 A tail.<BR>6 Majesty, dignity.<BR>7 Chief, principal.<BR>8 A horse.<BR>9 An ornament.<BR>10 A horse's ornament.<BR>11 A coloured mark on the forehead of a horse or bull, &c.<BR>12 A mane.<BR>13 A line, a row.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An ornament worn in the ear.<BR>E.<BR>लल to play, &c., aff. क्विप्, अम to go, to contribute to or occasion, aff. अण्; also with कनिन्, aff. ललामन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामक|ललामकं
ललामक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A chaplet of flowers falling over the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>ललाम a mark on the forehead, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामन्
ललामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>1 A mark or sign, &c.: see ललाम.<BR>2 A species of stanza having ten syllables in the first two Pādas, eleven in the third, and thirteen in the fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललित|ललितं|ललितः
ललित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>2 Beautiful, lovely.<BR>3 Wanton, dallying.<BR>4 Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>5 Graceful.<BR>6 Gay, cheerful, careless.<BR>7 Slow, gentle.<BR>8 Destroyed.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 A branch of feminine action, arising from the passion or sentiment of love, and expressive of satisfaction and triumph; softness and delicacy of gesture or motion, putting on appropriate ornaments, &c.<BR>2 Love of pleasure and gaiety. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">Page718</a>]<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Musk.<BR>2 A woman in general.<BR>3 A wanton.<BR>E.<BR>लड to frolick, &c. or लल to desire, aff. क्त; in the first case, ड changed to ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=717" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव|लवं|लवः
लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Cutting.<BR>2 Loss, destruction.<BR>3 Reaping.<BR>4 Small, little; (according to some authorities, this when used attributively changes its gender, making लवः लवा लवं; according to others it is invariably masc.)<BR>5 Smallness, littleness.<BR>6 A minute division of time, the sixtieth part of the twinkling of an eye.<BR>7 A larger division of time, two Kāṣṭhas or 36 twinklings of the eye, or about 1/2 a second.<BR>8 One of the sons of RĀMACANDRA.<BR>9 A kind of quail.<BR>10 Hair, wool, &c.; that which is cut or shorn from domestic animals.<BR>11 (In arithmetic,) The numerator of a fraction.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 The nutmeg.<BR>2 Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>लु to cut, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवक|लवकः
लवक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what cuts, reaps, cuts off, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवङ्ग|लवंग|लवङ्गं|लवंगः|लवङ्गः
लवङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The clove tree, (Myristica caryophyllata.)<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Cloves, the fruit.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, Uṇādi aff. अङ्गच्; also with कन् added, लवङ्गक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवण|लवणं|लवणः
लवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Salt, saline.<BR>2 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Sea salt.<BR>2 Rock or fossile salt.<BR>3 Factitious salt, or salt obtained by boiling clay found near the sea-shore, or any earth impregnated with saline particles.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The saline or salt taste, saltness.<BR>2 The sea of salt water.<BR>3 The name of a Rākṣasa mentioned in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 Light, lustre, beauty.<BR>2 A small river in Tirhut.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, (rawness, or to assist digestion,) aff. ल्यु, and the final letter made nasal by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणखानि|लवणखानिः
लवणखानि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A salt mine in general, or the district of Sāmbher in Ajmere, celebrated for its fossile salt.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, and खानि a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणसमुद्र|लवणसमुद्रः
लवणसमुद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The sea of salt water.<BR>E.<BR>लवण, and समुद्र ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणाकर|लवणाकरः
लवणाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A salt mine.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, and आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणोत्तम|लवणोत्तमं
लवणोत्तम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Nitre.<BR>2 Rock or river salt.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणोद|लवणोदः
लवणोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The sea of salt water.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Brine.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन|लवनं
लवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Reaping.<BR>2 Cutting.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A coarse kind of custard apple, (Annona reticulata.)<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवली
लवली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A kind of creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवशस्
लवशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Piece meal, in pieces.<BR>E.<BR>लव a bit, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाक|लवाकः
लवाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sickle or reaping-hook.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, Uṇādi aff. आकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाणक|लवाणकः
लवाणक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sickle, a reaping-hook.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, आणक Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवि|लविः
लवि<BR>mfn. (-विः-विः-वि)<BR>Cutting, edged, sharp, (as an instrument, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवित्र|लवित्रं
लवित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A sickle, a small reaping-hook.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. इत्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवेप्सु
लवेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Wishing to cut or reap.<BR>E.<BR>लव, and ईप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव्य
लव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cut.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लश
लश<BR>r. 10th cl. (लाशयति)<BR>To be skilful or clever, to do any thing skilfully and scientifically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुन|लशुनं|लशुनः
लशुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Garlick.<BR>E.<BR>अश to eat, Uṇādi aff. उनन्, and लश substituted for the root; also with the vowel of the aff. long लशून n. (-नं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुनीय
लशुनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Garlicky.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Cat's eye.<BR>E.<BR>लशुन, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष
लष<BR>r. 1st and 4th cls. (लषति-त or -लष्यति-ते)<BR>To desire, to like, to love.<BR>(अभि is usually prefixed.) r. 10th cl. (लाषयति)<BR>To be skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्व|लष्वः
लष्व<BR>m. (-ष्वः)<BR>A dancer, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>लष to be skilled in any art, (as dancing, &c.) and वन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस|लसं
लस<BR>r. 1st cl. (लसति)<BR>1 To embrace.<BR>2 To sport or play.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लासयति)<BR>1 To be skilful, to do any thing skilfully or scientifically.<BR>2 To work.<BR>With उत् prefixed,<BR>1 To shine, to be brilliant or splendid.<BR>2 To be happy or delighted.<BR>With वि,<BR>To gambol, to sport, especially amorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसत्
लसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Sporting, playing.<BR>2 Shining.<BR>3 Glancing, (as rays of light.)<BR>E.<BR>लस to sport, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसा
लसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>लस to sport, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसिका
लसिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Saliva, spittle.<BR>E.<BR>रस to taste, &c., aff. वुन्, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्ज
लस्ज<BR>(ओ ई) ओलस्जी r. 6th cl. (लज्जते)<BR>To be modest or ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्त|लस्तः
लस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Grasped, embraced.<BR>2 Skilled, skilful.<BR>E.<BR>लस to embrace, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तक|लस्तकः
लस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The middle of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>लस्त grasped, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तकिन्
लस्तकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>लस्तक the middle of a bow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहरि|लहरिः
लहरि<BR>f. (-रिः-री)<BR>A large wave or surf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ला
ला<BR>r. 2nd cl. (लाति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To get, to receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षणिक|लाक्षणिकः
लाक्षणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Secondary, inferior, subordinate.<BR>2 Indicatory, characteristic.<BR>3 Technical.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A technical term, a word implying a definition.<BR>E.<BR>लक्षण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षण्य
लाक्षण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Indicative, symptomatic, relating to a mark or sign, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लक्षण, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षा
लाक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Lac, a red dye, or an insect which is analogous to the cochineal insect, and like it forms when dried and prepared, a dye of a red colour; the nest is formed of a resinous substance which is used as sealing wax, and is usually termed Shel lac.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark or stain, aff. अ, and अण् added, the vowel made long: or लक्ष a hundred thousand, and अण् aff.; made by a multitude of the insects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षातरु|लाक्षातरुः
लाक्षातरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>लाक्षा lac, and तरु a tree; the insect being especially found in this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षाप्रसादन|लाक्षाप्रसादनः
लाक्षाप्रसादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The red Lodh, a tree from the bark of which an astringent infusion is prepared, which is used to fix colour in dyeing.<BR>E.<BR>लाक्षा lac, and प्रसादन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षावृक्ष|लाक्षावृक्षः
लाक्षावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Butea frondosa.<BR>E.<BR>लाक्षा the lac, and वृक्ष a tree: see लाक्षातरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षिक
लाक्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Made of lac, &c.<BR>2 Relating to a large number or a lakh.<BR>E.<BR>लाक्षा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाख
लाख<BR>(ऋ) लाखृ r. 1st cl. (लाखति)<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>2 To adorn.<BR>3 To suffice, to be able or competent to.<BR>4 To refuse or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघ
लाघ<BR>(ऋ) लाघृ r. 1st cl. (लाघते)<BR>To be able or competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=718" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघव|लाघवं
लाघव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Health.<BR>2 Lightness, delicacy, minuteness.<BR>3 Meanness, insignificance.<BR>4 Frivolity.<BR>E.<BR>लघु light, &c., and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गल|लांगल|लांगलं|लाङ्गलं|लाङ्गलः
लाङ्गल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A plough.<BR>2 The penis.<BR>3 The palm tree.<BR>4 A sort of flower.<BR>5 The main beam of a house.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 An aquatic shrub, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>2 A creeping shrub, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>3 Another creeper, (Nama repens.)<BR>4 A plant, (Gloriosa superba.)<BR>E.<BR>लगि to go, to limp, &c., Uṇādi aff. कल, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलग्रह|लांगलग्रह|लाङ्गलग्रहः
लाङ्गलग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A ploughman.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गल a plough, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलग्रहण
लाङ्गलग्रहण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Guiding the plough, ploughing.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गल, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलदण्ड|लांगलदंड|लाङ्गलदण्डः
लाङ्गलदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The pole or shaft of a plough.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गल a plough, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलपद्धति|लांगलपद्धति|लाङ्गलपद्धतिः
लाङ्गलपद्धति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A furrow.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गल a plough, and पद्धति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिक|लांगलिक|लाङ्गलिकः
लाङ्गलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a plough.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>One of thirty-four species of the fixed, or mineral and vegetable poisons.<BR>f. (-का-की)<BR>A small creeper, commonly Lāṅgalī, (Gloriosa superba); or, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गली a name of several plants, aff. कन्, fem. form, or लाङ्गल, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिन्|लांगलिन्
लाङ्गलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>2 The cocoanut tree.<BR>3 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गल a plough, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुल|लांगुल|लांगुलं|लाङ्गुलं
लाङ्गुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A horse's tail.<BR>E.<BR>लगि to go, aff. उलच् see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूल|लांगूल|लांगूलं|लाङ्गूलं
लाङ्गूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A hairy tail, (as a horse's, &c.)<BR>2 The penis.<BR>3 A granary, a basket or shed for holding corn or grain.<BR>E.<BR>लगि to go, Uṇādi aff. ऊलच्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूलिन्|लांगूलिन्
लाङ्गूलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Tailed.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>लाङ्गूल a tail, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाच्छ|लाछ
लाच्छ<BR>(इ) लाच्छि r. 1st cl. (लाञ्छति)<BR>To mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज|लाजं|लाजः
लाज<BR>r. 1st cl. (लाजति) (इ) लाजि (लांजति)<BR>1 To blame or censure.<BR>2 To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज|लाजं|लाजः
लाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Grain, wetted or sprinkled.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>f. (-जा) or masc. plu. (-जाः)<BR>Fried grain.<BR>E.<BR>लाज to fry, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छन|लांछन|लांछनं|लाञ्छनं|लाञ्छनः
लाञ्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A name, an appellation.<BR>2 A mark or sign.<BR>E.<BR>लाच्छि to mark, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट|लाटः
लाट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Old or worn, spoiled, shabby, (as clothes, ornaments, &c.)<BR>2 Childish.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Cloth, clothes.<BR>2 Fault, defect.<BR>3 Idle or inebriate language.<BR>4 Repetition of words in the same sense, but a different application.<BR>5 The name of a country, the upper part of the Dekhin, Lār or Larice.<BR>E.<BR>लट to be childish, aff. घञ्, or लाट Kaṇḍvādi root, to live, aff. अच्, or लट childish, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाटानुप्रास|लाटानुप्रासः
लाटानुप्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A figure of rhetoric; repetition of a word in the same sense, but with a different application.<BR>E.<BR>लाट, and अनुप्रास alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप|लापः
लाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Speaking, talking.<BR>E.<BR>लप to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप्य|लाप्यं
लाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be said or spoken.<BR>E.<BR>लप to speak, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ<BR>r. 10th cl. (लाभयति)<BR>To throw, to send or direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Gain, profit.<BR>2 Gain in general, acquirement, acquisition.<BR>E.<BR>लभ to get or gain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभकृत्
लाभकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Gaining, making profit.<BR>E.<BR>लाभ, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभलिप्सु
लाभलिप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Covetous, grasping, desirous of gain or profit.<BR>E.<BR>लाभ, and लिप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभालाभ
लाभालाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Profit and loss.<BR>E.<BR>लाभ, and अलाभ not gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामज्जक|लामज्जकं
लामज्जक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum, a fragrant grass.<BR>E.<BR>ला what takes or removes (heat, &c.), मज्जा the pith, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालन|लालनं|लालनः
लालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Wheedling, coaxing.<BR>E.<BR>लल to sport, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालप्यमान
लालप्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Bewailing or supplicating much.<BR>E.<BR>लप to speak, freq. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालष्यमान
लालष्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wishing to enjoy.<BR>E.<BR>लष to desire, freq. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालसा
लालसा<BR>mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>1 Ardent desire.<BR>2 Regret, sorrow, missing, wishing for any person or object absent.<BR>3 Soliciting, asking.<BR>4 The longing of pregnant women.<BR>5 Wanton sport, dalliance.<BR>E.<BR>लल to desire, to wish for, असण् Uṇādi aff. or लष to wish, or लस् to sport, aff. घञ् and टाप्, and the root reiterated, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालसीक|लालसीकं
लालसीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Sauce, gravy.<BR>E.<BR>लालसा desire, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाला
लाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Saliva, spittle.<BR>E.<BR>लल to wish, अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटिक|लालाटिकः
लालाटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to the forehead, worn on it, belonging to it, &c.<BR>2 Contemplating the forehead, looking at it, &c.<BR>3 Low, vile.<BR>4 Relating to fate or destiny.<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>1 An attentive servant, one who watches a master's countenance, and learns by it what is necessary to be done.<BR>2 An idler, one who is unable to work.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mode of embracing.<BR>E.<BR>ललाट the forehead, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालामेह|लालामेहः
लालामेह<BR>m. हः<BR>Passing mucous urine.<BR>E.<BR>लाला, and मेह urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाविष|लालाविषः
लालाविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An insect, whose spittle is venomous or acrid, as a spider, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लाला saliva, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालास्राव|लालास्रावः
लालास्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>लाला saliva, स्रु to distil, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिक|लालिकः
लालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A jesting or evasive reply, equivoque.<BR>E.<BR>लाला saliva, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित
लालित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Loved, desired.<BR>2 Cherished, treated tenderly.<BR>3 Coaxed, wheedled, seduced.<BR>E.<BR>लल to desire, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित्य|लालित्यं
लालित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Beauty, loveliness.<BR>2 Gaiety.<BR>3 Gracefulness, &c.<BR>E.<BR>ललित, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिन्
लालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Wheedling, coaxing, fondling.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A seducer.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>A wanton.<BR>E.<BR>लल to sport, causal v., घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालुका
लालुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव|लावः
लाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Cutting down.<BR>mf. (-वः-वा)<BR>A sort of quail, (Perdix chinensis.)<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, to eat (corn,) causal form, aff. अच्; also with कन् added, लावक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण|लावणं
लावण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 Salted, dressed or cooked with salt.<BR>2 Salt, belonging or relating to it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावणिक|लावणिकं|लावणिकः
लावणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Salted, cooked or dressed with salt.<BR>2 Relating to salt, &c.<BR>3 Lovely, beautiful.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender of salt, a salt merchant.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A vessel holding salt, a saltcellar.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=719" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्य|लावण्यं
लावण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 Saltness, the taste or property of salt.<BR>2 Beauty, loveliness.<BR>E.<BR>लवण salt, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्यश्री
लावण्यश्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>Great beauty.<BR>E.<BR>लावण्य, and श्री wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्यार्जित|लावण्यार्जितं
लावण्यार्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Property belonging to a woman, consisting of that which has been presented to her at her marriage as a token of respect, as a mark of kindness, or by her father or mother-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>लावण्य loveliness, and अर्जित acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाविक|लाविकः
लाविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>लव cutting, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावु|लावुः
लावु<BR>f. (-वुः-वूः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaria.)<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, to destroy, (disease,) aff. उण्; also with कन् added लावुका, and with अ or आङ् prefixed, अलावु, आलावु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव्य
लाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cut, to be cut off or drown.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास|लासः
लास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Dancing in general.<BR>2 Dancing, as practised by women: see लास्य.<BR>3 Pulse that has been steeped or slightly boiled, pea-water, &c. not thickened to the consistency of Yūṣa or pease soup.<BR>4 Dalliance, wanton sport, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लस to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासक|लासकं|लासकः
लासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A dancer, an actor, a mime.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>3 Embracing, enfolding, surrounding.<BR>4 One who sports or gambols.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A turret, a room on the top of a building.<BR>f. (-लासिका or लासकी)<BR>1 A female dancer, a Nāc girl.<BR>2 A wanton, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>लस to embrace, to be skilful, (in the art of dancing,) and aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्फोटनी
लास्फोटनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A gimlet, an auger.<BR>E.<BR>ललन going, आस्फोटन piercing, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्य|लास्यं|लास्यः
लास्य<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Dancing in general.<BR>2 Symphony, or union of song, dance, and instrumental music.<BR>3 A mode of dancing; the Nāc of India, or dance practised by women chiefly, and confined to attitude and gesticulation, with a shuffling motion of the feet seldom lifted from the ground; this style is said to have been invented by PĀRVATĪ, and communicated by her to the daughter of Vāṇāsura, by whom her female friends and companions were instructed in it; as a species, it is opposed to the Tāṇḍava, the more boisterous dance of ŚIVA, and his followers or men.<BR>4 A part or embellishment of dramatic composition, the occasional introduction of music and singing; also abrupt transition from Prākṛta to Sanscrit and Sanscrit to Prākṛta, &c.<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A dancer.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>A female dancer.<BR>E.<BR>लम to be skilled in the art of dancing, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्यक|लास्यकं
लास्यक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Dancing in general, or a particular style of dancing.<BR>E.<BR>लास्य as above, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्याङ्ग
लास्याङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>A part of a drama, of the Lāsya order: see लास्य.<BR>E.<BR>लास्य, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लि|लिः
लि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 Weariness, fatigue.<BR>2 Loss, destruction.<BR>3 End, term.<BR>4 Equality, sameness.<BR>5 A bracelet.<BR>E.<BR>ला to take, or ली to melt, &c., aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिकुच|लिकुचं|लिकुचः
लिकुच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A sort of bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.)<BR>E.<BR>लकुच q. v. and इ substituted for the first vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षा
लिक्षा<BR>m. (-क्षा)<BR>A nit, a young louse.<BR>E.<BR>a various reading of लिक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षा
लिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 A nit, a young louse, or the egg of a louse.<BR>2 A poppy seed, considered as a measure of weight, or 1/6th of a mustard seed.<BR>E.<BR>लक्ष to mark, aff. घञ्, इ substituted for the radical vowel and the deriv. irr.; also क्क being substituted for the final लिक्का, and with कन् added, fem. form, लिक्षिका again with ई substituted for the radical vowel लीक्षा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख|लिखः
लिख<BR>r. 6th cl. (लिखति)<BR>To write.<BR>r. 1st cl. (लेखति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख|लिखः
लिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 Writing.<BR>2 A writer.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखखत्
लिखखत्<BR>mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खती-खत्)<BR>1 Writing.<BR>2 Painting, delineating.<BR>3 Scratching, making streaks or lines.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखन|लिखनं
लिखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Scripture, writing.<BR>2 A writing, a written document.<BR>3 Scratching.<BR>4 Scarifying.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, aff. क्युच्, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित|लिखितं|लिखितः
लिखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Written.<BR>2 Drawn, delineated, painted: (painting being considered a sort of writing)<BR>3 Drawn as lines, scratched.<BR>4 Scarified.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Scripture, writing.<BR>2 A writing, a manuscript, a written book or paper.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित्वा
लिखित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having written, delineated, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्या
लिख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>A poppy seed, considered as a minute measure of weight, variously estimated at four or eight Trasareṇus or motes, or the sixth part of a mustard seed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिग
लिग<BR>(इ) लिगि r. 1st cl. (लिङ्गति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (लिङ्गति लिङ्गयति)<BR>To paint, to variegate.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिगु|लिगुः
लिगु<BR>n. (-गु)<BR>1 The heart, the mind.<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>1 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>2 A deer.<BR>3 Part of the earth.<BR>E.<BR>लग to be near or with, Uṇādi aff. कु, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग|लिंग|लिंगं|लिङ्गं
लिङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A mark, a spot, a stain, a sign, a token, &c.<BR>2 The penis.<BR>3 The phallus, or ŚIVA under that emblem.<BR>4 Inference, probable conclusion.<BR>5 The premises leading to a conclusion.<BR>6 Nature or Prakṛti, according to the Sāṃkhya philosophy, which considers this as the active power in creation.<BR>7 Gender, (as पुंलिङ्गः the masculine gender, &c.)<BR>8 The order of the religious student.<BR>9 Symptom or mark of disease.<BR>E.<BR>लिगि to go, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गक|लिंगक|लिंगकः|लिङ्गकः
लिङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग the penis, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गन|लिंगन|लिंगनं
लिङ्गन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Licking.<BR>2 Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गनाश|लिंगनाश|लिङ्गनाशः
लिङ्गनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Loss of any characteristic mark, &c.<BR>2 Loss of vision from cataract, &c. considered to be discoloration of the pupil, either red, white, or yellow.<BR>3 Loss of the penis.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग mark (of the eye), नाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवर्द्धन
लिङ्गवर्द्धन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग the penis, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवर्द्धिनी
लिङ्गवर्द्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवृत्ति|लिंगवृत्ति|लिङ्गवृत्तिः
लिङ्गवृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>A religious hypocrite, one who assumes the dress, &c. of an ascetic in order to get a livelihood.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग a mark, external shew or sign, (as the clotted hair, &c.) and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गस्थ|लिङ्गस्थः
लिङ्गस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A religious student.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गालिका
लिङ्गालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small mouse or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गार्च्चन|लिङ्गार्चन|लिंगार्चन
लिङ्गार्च्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Worship of the Liṅga or phallus.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग, and अर्च्चण worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=720" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिन्|लिंगिन्
लिङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Having marks, &c.<BR>2 Indicated, characterized.<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A hypocrite, a pretended devotee.<BR>3 An ascetic.<BR>4 A religious student.<BR>5 A worshipper of ŚIVA in the phallic type.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग a mark, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिवेष|लिङ्गिवेषः
लिङ्गिवेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The dress or the insignia of a religious student, the skin, staff, bowl, &c.<BR>2 The dress or appearance of a follower of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>लिङ्ग, and वेष attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप|लिपः
लिप<BR>(ञि औ) ञि औलिप r. 6th cl. (-लिम्पति-ते)<BR>1 To increase or add to.<BR>2 To anoint, to smear, to plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप|लिपः
लिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Smearing, plastering.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपि|लिपिः
लिपि<BR>f. (-पिः-पी)<BR>1 Writing in general, handwriting.<BR>2 A writing, a written paper or book, &c.<BR>3 Painting, drawing.<BR>4 Smearing, anointing, plastering.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to spread (ink) Uṇādi aff. इन् with ङीप् optionally added, the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिकर|लिपिकरः
लिपिकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि writing, and कर who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिका
लिपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Writing or a writing.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि writing, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिकार|लिपिकारः
लिपिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि writing, and कार who makes, from कृ to make, and अण् aff.; also with ट aff. लिपिकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिज्ञ
लिपिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>One who can write.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिसज्जा
लिपिसज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>Implements or materials for writing.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि, सज्जा preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्त|लिप्तं
लिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Smeared, anointed, plastered, spread.<BR>2 Eaten.<BR>3 Envenomed, spread or touched with any poisonous substance.<BR>4 Embraced, united, connected with, &c.<BR>5 Defiled or contaminated by.<BR>6 Stained, soiled.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, aff. क्त, or in the last sense ली to cling to, Uṇādi aff. त, with पुट् augment, and the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तक|लिप्तकः
लिप्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A poisoned arrow.<BR>E.<BR>लिप्त poisoned, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तवत्
लिप्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Anointed, plastered.<BR>2 Touched.<BR>3 Vitiated, defiled.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तहस्त
लिप्तहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Having the hands stained or smeared.<BR>E.<BR>लिप्त, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सा
लिप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>लिप्स the desiderative form of लभ to get, (to wish to get,) aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सित
लिप्सित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Coveted, desired.<BR>E.<BR>लिप्स to wish to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सु|लिप्सुः
लिप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Desirous, desiring, wishing, cupidinous.<BR>E.<BR>लिप्स desiderative of लभ, (see the last,) and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्प|लिंप|लिंपः|लिम्पः
लिम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Smearing, anointing, plastering.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, (taking in its derivative forms the nasal augment,) and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पट|लिंपट|लिम्पटः
लिम्पट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A lecher, a whore-monger.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि to smear with unguents, अटच् aff.; also लम्पट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पाक|लिंपाक|लिम्पाकं|लिंपाकः|लिम्पाकः
लिम्पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The lime tree, (Citrus acida.)<BR>2 An ass.<BR>E.<BR>लिपि to smear, aff. काकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिवि|लिविः
लिवि<BR>f. (-विः-वी)<BR>Writing, hand-writing, or a writing, a manuscript.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear (with ink), Uṇādi aff. इन्, with the vowel unchanged, and व substituted for प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिविकर|लिविकरः
लिविकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>लिवि writing, and कर who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिविङ्कर|लिविंकर|लिविङ्करः
लिविङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A writer, a scribe.<BR>E.<BR>लिवि writing, कृ to practise, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश
लिश<BR>(औ) लिशौ r. 4th cl. (लिश्यते)<BR>To lessen or become less.<BR>r. 6th cl. (लिशति)<BR>To go, to move, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिष्व|लिष्वः
लिष्व<BR>m. (-ष्वः)<BR>A dancer, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>लष to be skilled (in dancing), Uṇādi aff. क्वन्, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह|लिहः
लिह<BR>r. 2nd cl. (लेढि लीढे)<BR>To taste, to taste with the tongue, to lick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली<BR>r. 4th cl. (लीयते) r. 9th cl. (लिनाति)<BR>1 To join, to adhere or cling to, to be in union or connexion with.<BR>2 To obtain.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लयति लाययति लापयति लालयति or लीनयति)<BR>To melt, to liquefy, to fuse or dissolve.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To waste away.<BR>With प्र and वि,<BR>To acquire or gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली<BR>f. (-लीः)<BR>Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>ली to embrace, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीक्का
लीक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A nit: see लिक्का.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीक्षा
लीक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>A nit: see लिक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढ|लीढः
लीढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>2 Licked.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick or taste, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढमुक्त
लीढमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Rejected after being tasted.<BR>E.<BR>लीढ, and मुक्त let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीन|लीनः
लीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Embraced, clung or adhered to.<BR>2 Melted, dissolved.<BR>3 Dissolved with softness, overcome with passion.<BR>4 Diffused.<BR>5 Effaced, wiped away.<BR>6 Staying, being situated.<BR>7 Left, departed.<BR>E.<BR>ली to be in contact, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीला
लीला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A branch of feminine action, proceeding from love; or the imitation of a lover's manner, speech, gait, &c. by his mistress, to pass the time in his absence.<BR>2 Play, sport, pastime in general.<BR>3 Amorous or wanton sport.<BR>4 A species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>E.<BR>ली embrace, ला to get or give, aff. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाखेल
लीलाखेल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Playful.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A species of the Atiśarkarī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलायित|लीलायितं
लीलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done or written sportively, or in the way of sport or pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>लीला used as a verb, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलावती
लीलावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A wanton or sportful woman.<BR>E.<BR>लीला, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलोद्यान|लीलोद्यानं
लीलोद्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A pleasure ground, a garden.<BR>E.<BR>लीला sport, and उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लु
लु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>Cutting, lopping, shearing, reaping, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच
लुच<BR>(इ) लुचि r. 1st cl. (लुञ्चति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To pare or peel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच्
लुच्<BR>f. (-लुक्)<BR>Cutting off, dropping, rejecting.<BR>E.<BR>लुच to cut, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चित|लुंचित
लुञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cut.<BR>2 Peeled.<BR>E.<BR>लुच to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुज
लुज<BR>(इ) लुजि r. 10th cl. (लुञ्जयति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To injure.<BR>3 To be strong.<BR>4 To dwell.<BR>5 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट
लुट<BR>(ऌ) लुटॢ r. 1st cl. (लोटति-ते) r. 4th cl. (लुट्यति)<BR>1 To stir, to agitate.<BR>2 To be joined or connected with.<BR>3 To roll upon the ground.<BR>r. 1st cl. (लोटति)<BR>1 To resist or oppose.<BR>2 To strike again.<BR>3 To shine.<BR>r. 6th cl. (लुटति)<BR>To embrace.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लोटयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(इ) लुटि r. 1st and 10th [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">Page722</a>] cls. (लुण्टति लुण्टयति)<BR>1 To steal, to rob or plunder.<BR>2 To disregard, to disobey or disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=721" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्यत्
लुट्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ट्यन्-ट्यन्ती-ट्यत्)<BR>Rolling about, (in pain or grief.)<BR>E.<BR>लुट to roll about, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ
लुठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (लोठति)<BR>To knock down.<BR>(लोठते)<BR>To resist or oppose.<BR>r. 6th cl. (लुठति)<BR>To be connected or in contact with, to rest in or on.<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (लोठते लुठति)<BR>1 To roll on the ground.<BR>2 To flow, to trickle.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लोठयति)<BR>To rob.<BR>(इ) लुठि r. 1st cl. (लुण्ठति)<BR>1 To be lazy.<BR>2 To repel, to resist or oppose.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR>4 To steal.<BR>5 To be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठत्
लुठत्<BR>mfn. (-ठन्-ठन्ती-ठत्)<BR>1 Rolling on the ground, falling down.<BR>2 Flowing, trickling.<BR>E.<BR>लुठ to roll, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठन|लुठनं
लुठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>2 Rolling on the ground with sorrow or vexation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लुट or लुठ to cast one's self on the ground, aff. क्युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठित|लुठितः
लुठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rolling on the ground, (as a horse, &c.)<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A horse rolling himself on the ground, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लुठ to roll on the ground, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुड
लुड<BR>r. 1st cl. (लोडति)<BR>To agitate, to stir, to churn.<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (लोडति लुडति)<BR>1 To be in connexion or contact with any thing, to join, to adhere to, to rest in or on, &c.<BR>2 To embrace.<BR>r. 6th cl. (-लुडति)<BR>To cover, to conceal.<BR>(इ) लुडि r. 10th cl. (लुण्ठयति)<BR>1 To be agitated.<BR>2 To plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टक|लुण्टकः
लुण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of potherb, (Chironia centauroides, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>लुटि to be prostrate, &c., aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टा|लुंटा
लुण्टा<BR>f. (-ण्टा)<BR>A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>लुटि or लुठि to roll on the ground, aff. अङ् and टाप्; also लुण्ठा and लुण्ठि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टाक|लुंटाक|लुण्टाकः
लुण्टाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A robber, a thief.<BR>E.<BR>लुटि to rob, काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठत्
लुण्ठत्<BR>mfn. (-ण्ठन्-ण्ठन्ती-ण्ठत्)<BR>Rolling on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>लुठि to roll, &c. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठन|लुंठन|लुंठनं|लुण्ठनं
लुण्ठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Rolling on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>लुठि To roll on the ground, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठा|लुंठा
लुण्ठा<BR>f. (-ण्ठा)<BR>A horse's rolling on the ground: see the last, and लुण्टा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठाक|लुंठाक|लुंठाकः|लुण्ठाकः
लुण्ठाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>लुठि to roll on the ground, काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठी|लुंठी
लुण्ठी<BR>f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>लुठि to roll on the ground, aff. अच् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डी|लुंडी
लुण्डी<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>Observing the rules of princely conduct, acting and judging rightly.<BR>E.<BR>लुडि to be agitated, &c., aff. अच् and ङीप्; also with कन् added, fem. form लुण्डिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुथ
लुथ<BR>(इ) लुथि r. 1st cl. (लुन्थति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>2 To afflict.<BR>3 To suffer pain or affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप
लुप<BR>r. 4th cl. (लुप्यति)<BR>To disturb, to bewilder, to perplex and confound the understanding.<BR>(ऌ औ ऋ) औलुपॢ^1 r. 6th cl. (लुम्पति-ते)<BR>1 To cut, to divide, to cut off or down.<BR>2 To rob.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्त|लुप्तं
लुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Gone, lost, disappeared.<BR>2 (In grammar,) Cut, off, rejected.<BR>n. (-प्तं)<BR>Booty, plunder.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to rob, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तता
लुप्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Disappearance, non-existence.<BR>E.<BR>लुप्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, लुप्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रिय
लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Deprived of funeral rites.<BR>E.<BR>लुप्त, पिण्डोदक cake and water, क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तोपमा
लुप्तोपमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>An imperfect comparison.<BR>E.<BR>लुप्त, and उपमा simile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब
लुब<BR>(इ) लुबि r. 1st and 10th cls. (लुम्बति लुम्बयति)<BR>To hurt, to pain, to afflict or torment.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लुम्बयति)<BR>To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्ध|लुब्धः
लुब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Covetous, greedy, desirous, cupidinous.<BR>m. (-ब्धः)<BR>1 A hunter.<BR>2 A lecher, a libertine.<BR>E.<BR>लुभ to desire, to wish for vehemently, to covet, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धक|लुब्धकः
लुब्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hunter.<BR>2 A libertine, a rake, a whoremonger.<BR>3 A covetous or greedy man.<BR>E.<BR>लुब्ध desirous, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभ
लुभ<BR>r. 4th cl. (लुभ्यति)<BR>To desire, to covet.<BR>r. 6th cl. (लुभति)<BR>To bewilder, to perplex or delude.<BR>With प्र or सं,<BR>To attract or allure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभित|लुभितः
लुभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Perplexed, deluded, fascinated.<BR>E.<BR>लुभ to fascinate, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुल
लुल<BR>r. 1st cl. (लोलति)<BR>1 To stir or agitate, to make tremulous.<BR>2 To be attached to or connected with, to join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलाप|लुलापः
लुलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>लुल to agitate, aff. क, stirring, shaking, (in the mud,) आप् to get or obtain, aff. अच्; it is also read लुलाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलित|लुलितः
लुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, trembling, tremulous, agitated, stirred.<BR>2 Heaving, panting.<BR>3 Agreeable, pleasing, beautiful, elegant.<BR>4 Injured, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>लुल to agitate, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुष|लुषः
लुष<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (लोषति लोषयति)<BR>1 To rob, to steal.<BR>2 To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुषभ|लुषभः
लुषभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>An elephant in rut.<BR>E.<BR>रुष to be enraged, Uṇādi aff. अभच्, with लुष substituted for the root, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लू
लू<BR>(लू) r. 9th cl. (लुनाति लुनीते)<BR>To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूता
लूता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A spider.<BR>2 An ant.<BR>3 Local inflammation produced by the urine of a spider.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, क्तन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूतिका
लूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>लूता a spider, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लून|लूनः
लून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Cut.<BR>2 Wounded.<BR>3 Cut off.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनक|लूनकः
लूनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An animal.<BR>2 Sort, species, difference.<BR>3 A wound, a division, what is cut or broken.<BR>E.<BR>लून cut, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनि|लूनिः
लूनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Cutting, reaping.<BR>E.<BR>लू To cut, aff. क्तिन्, and न substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूम|लूमं
लूम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 A tail.<BR>2 A hairy tail, as a horse's, a monkey's, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूमविष|लूमविषः
लूमविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Any animal that stings with its tail, as a scorpion, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लूम a tail, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष
लूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (लूषति)<BR>To adorn, to decorate.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लोषयति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure.<BR>2 To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लृञ्च
लृञ्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (लृञ्चति)<BR>To put away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A letter, an epistle.<BR>2 A god, a deity.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A line, a mark or row, &c.<BR>2 Writing, hand-writing.<BR>3 Delineation, painting.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, aff. घञ्; it is applied to the second sense, because the figures of the gods are written or delineated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखक|लेखकः
लेखक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A writer, a scribe, a clerk, a copyist, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लिस्व to write, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखन|लेखनं|लेखनः
लेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Writing, scripture.<BR>2 The bark of the Bhoj tree, which is used for writing on in Nepal and Upper Hindustan.<BR>3 Vomiting.<BR>4 The leaf of the palm tree.<BR>5 Scraping or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">Page723</a>] cleaning the tongue.<BR>6 Scarifying, scratching.<BR>7 Reducing corpulency, thinning.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of grass or reed, of which pens are made, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A pen, a style.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, aff. of the act or instrument ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=722" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनवस्ति|लेखनवस्तिः
लेखनवस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>Use of enemas to reduce corpulency.<BR>E.<BR>लेखन, and वस्ति a glyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनिक|लेखनिकः
लेखनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A letter-carrier, an express, a postman.<BR>2 One who signs a paper by proxy, who makes his mark, from inability to write, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लेखन writing, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनीय|लेखनीयः
लेखनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be written.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An accusation or defence in law, which are required to be given in writing.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखर्षभ|लेखर्षभः
लेखर्षभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>लेख a deity, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखहार|लेखहारः
लेखहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A letter-carrier.<BR>E.<BR>लेख a letter, हृ to convey, aff. अण्; also with कन् added, लेखहारक, or with णिनि, लेखहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखित|लेखितं
लेखित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Written.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, क्त aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्य|लेख्यं
लेख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>1 To be written.<BR>2 To be scarified.<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>1 A letter, an epistle.<BR>2 A manuscript.<BR>3 A drawing, a delineation.<BR>4 A written accusation or defence.<BR>E.<BR>लिख to write, ख्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यक
लेख्यक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Written, in writing, epistolary.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यकृत
लेख्यकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done in writing, contracted, executed.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यचूर्णिका
लेख्यचूर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A brush, a pencil.<BR>E.<BR>लख्य a delineation, चूर्ण to pound or grind, aff. वुन् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यपत्र|लेख्यपत्रः
लेख्यपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A leaf or sheet of any thing for writing.<BR>2 A written paper, a writing, a letter.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यपत्रक
लेख्यपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The palm tree.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A leaf of the palm or any other substance used for writing on.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य writing, पत्र a leaf, कन् aff.; books in the south of India, &c. being made of the leaves of the palmyra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यप्रसङ्ग|लेख्यप्रसंगः
लेख्यप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Written contract, record, or document.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य, and प्रसङ्ग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यस्थान|लेख्यस्थानं
लेख्यस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An office, a counting house, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य writing or what is to be written, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यारूढ
लेख्यारूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>Recorded, committed to writing.<BR>E.<BR>लेख्य, and आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप<BR>(ऋ) लेपृ r. 1st cl. (लेपते)<BR>To go, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Plastering, smearing.<BR>2 Food.<BR>3 Mortar, plaster, Chunam.<BR>4 Stain, spot, smearing.<BR>5 The wipings of the hand which has offered funeral oblations to three ancestors, and which are considered as an oblation to ancestors in the 4th, 5th, and 6th degrees.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपक|लेपकः
लेपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, (Chunam). ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपन|लेपनं|लेपनः
लेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Smearing, plastering, anointing.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपभागिन्
लेपभागिन्<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>An ancestor in the 4th, 5th, and 6th degrees.<BR>E.<BR>लेप, and भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपभुज्
लेपभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A paternal ancestor of the 4th, 5th, or 6th degree.<BR>E.<BR>लेप, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपिन्
लेपिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Who or what smears, plasters, anoints, &c.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR>E.<BR>लेप to plaster, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्य|लेप्यं
लेप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be spread, as unguent or plaster, to be anointed or plastered.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>Plastering, spreading or smearing ointment, mortar, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लिप to plaster, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यकृत्
लेप्यकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR>E.<BR>लेप्य plastering, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यमयी
लेप्यमयी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>लेप्य plastering, मयट् aff., made of wood with a coat of plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यस्त्री
लेप्यस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A woman, perfumed with fragrant unguents.<BR>E.<BR>लेप्य plastering, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A worm breeding in the stomach.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick, root red., क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिहान|लेलिहानः
लेलिहान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Who or what licks.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick, aff. शानच्, root reduplicate, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश<BR>adj. masc. only. (-शः)<BR>Small, little.<BR>subst.<BR>1 Smallness, littleness.<BR>2 A little.<BR>E.<BR>लिश to be small, aff. घञ्, some authorities vary the gender of the attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टु|लेष्टुः
लेष्टु<BR>m. (-ष्टुः)<BR>A clod of earth.<BR>E.<BR>लिश to become less or small, तुन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टुघ्न|लेष्टुघ्नः
लेष्टुघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>E.<BR>लेष्टु a clod of earth, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टुभेदन|लेष्टुभेदनः
लेष्टुभेदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>E.<BR>लेष्टु a clod of earth, and भेदन breaking; also लेष्टुभेदिन् and लोष्टभेदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेसिक|लेसिकः
लेसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The rider on an elephant, who sits on the animal's loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह|लेहः
लेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Food.<BR>2 Licking, tasting.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to taste, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहन|लेहनं
लेहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Licking, tasting with the tongue.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to taste, to lick, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन्
लेहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Who or what licks, laps, tastes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन|लेहिनः
लेहिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to lick, aff. इन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह्य|लेह्यं
लेह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be licked.<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 The food or beverage of the gods, nectar, ambrosia.<BR>2 Syrup, electuary.<BR>E.<BR>लिह to taste, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैण
लैण<BR>(ऋ) लैणृ r. 1st cl. (लैनति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To command or direct an act.<BR>3 To touch or embrace.<BR>4 To pound or grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक|लोकः
लोक<BR>(ऋ) लोकृ r. 1st cl. (लोकति)<BR>To see.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लोकयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक|लोकः
लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Man, mankind.<BR>2 A world, a division of the universe; in general three Lokas are enumerated, or heaven, hell, and earth: another classification enumerates seven, exclusive of the infernal regions; or Bhūr-loka the earth, Bhuvar-loka the space between the earth and the sun, the region of the Munis, Siddhis, &c.; Svarloka the heaven of INDRA, between the sun and the polar star; Maharloka the usual abode of BHṚGU, and other saints, who are supposed to be co-existent with BRAHMĀ: during the conflagration of these lower worlds, the saints ascend to the next, or Janaloka, which is described as the abode of BRAHMĀ'S sons, SANAKA, SĀNANDA, SANĀTANA, and SANATKUMĀRA; above this, is the fifth world [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">Page724</a>] or the Tapoloka, where the deities called Vairāgis reside; the seventh world, Satyaloka or Brahmaloka, is the abode of BRAHMĀ, and translation to this world exempts beings from further birth; the three first worlds are destroyed at the end of each Kalpa or day of BRAHMĀ; the three last at the end of his life, or of 100 of his years; the fourth Loka is equally permanent, but is uninhabitable from heat, at the time the three first are burning: another enumeration calls these seven worlds, earth, sky, heaven, middle region, place of births, mansion of the blest, and abode of truth, placing the sons of BRAHMĀ in the sixth division, and stating the fifth or Janaloka to be that, where animals destroyed in the general conflagration are born again.<BR>3 Sight, seeing.<BR>4 An element, a primary or radical part of being.<BR>E.<BR>लोक to see, aff. घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=723" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककृत्
लोककृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The Creator, BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकचक्षुस्
लोकचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, चक्षुच् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकजित्
लोकजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>1 A conqueror of the world.<BR>2 A sage.<BR>3 A Buddha or Bauddha deified teacher.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and जित् who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकत्रय
लोकत्रय<BR>n. (-यं-यी)<BR>The three worlds, heaven, earth, and hell.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनाथ|लोकनाथः
लोकनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A sovereign of the universe.<BR>2 One of the Jaina or Bauddha saints.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनीय
लोकनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Visible, to be seen.<BR>E.<BR>लोक to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपाल|लोकपालः
लोकपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A king, a sovereign.<BR>2 A divinity who protects the regions, or the sun, moon, fire, wind, INDRA, YAMA, VARUṆA, and KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and पाल a cherisher; also लोकपालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रवाद|लोकप्रवादः
लोकप्रवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Common or current report or saying.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and प्रवाद report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रसिद्ध
लोकप्रसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Notorious, well known.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and प्रसिद्ध celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबान्धव|लोकबांधव|लोकबान्धवः
लोकबान्धव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and बान्धव the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमातृ
लोकमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU, and goddess of wealth and fortune.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and मातृ the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकयात्रा
लोकयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 Worldly affairs, civil conduct, usage, practice.<BR>2 Resort of men, traffic, intercourse.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरञ्जन|लोकरंजन
लोकरञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Popularity, gaining public confidence.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and रञ्जन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकलोचन|लोकलोचनं
लोकलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाद|लोकवादः
लोकवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Rumour, report.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाह्य
लोकवाह्य<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>An outcaste, one who observes no sort of institutes, and feeds on the flesh of horses and kine.<BR>E.<BR>लोक mankind, and वाह्य for वहिर् without, excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविक्रुष्ट
लोकविक्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Censured or condemned by the world.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and विक्रुष्ट censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुत
लोकविश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, famous.<BR>2 Current.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and विश्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुति|लोकविश्रुतिः
लोकविश्रुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Unfounded rumour or report.<BR>2 Fame, notoriety.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and विश्रुति rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवृत्त
लोकवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Worldly or idle conversation and intercourse.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकात्मन्
लोकात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>The universal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तर|लोकांतर
लोकान्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Another world.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and अन्तर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरगत
लोकान्तरगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dead.<BR>E.<BR>लोकान्तर, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरप्राप्त
लोकान्तरप्राप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Dead.<BR>E.<BR>लोकान्तर, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायत|लोकायतं|लोकायतः
लोकायत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The system of atheistical philosophy taught by Cārvāka.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, आङ् before यति to strive, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतिक|लोकायतिकः
लोकायतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A follower of the Cārvāka doctrine, an atheist, an unbeliever.<BR>E.<BR>लोकायत as above, and ठक् aff. with the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकालोक|लोकालोकः
लोकालोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountainous belt, surrounding the outermost of the seven seas and bounding the world.<BR>E.<BR>लोक seeing, and अलोक not seeing; causing light and darkness, as interposed between the Dvīpas and the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकित
लोकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>लोक to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश|लोकेशः
लोकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A king, an emperor.<BR>3 A Jaina deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश्वर|लोकेश्वरः
लोकेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A king.<BR>3 A Jaina deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>लोक the world, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश्वरात्मजा
लोकेश्वरात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A female deity peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>लोकेश्वर a Jaina sage, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच|लोचं
लोच<BR>(ऋ) लोचृ r. 1st cl. (लोचते)<BR>To see, to perceive, to view or inspect.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लोचयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचक|लोचकः
लोचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A ball or lump of flesh or meat.<BR>2 The pupil of the eye.<BR>3 Stibium or lamp-black, &c. so used.<BR>4 An ornament, worn by women on the forehead.<BR>5 Blue or black vesture.<BR>6 An ear-ring.<BR>7 The plantain tree.<BR>8 A bow-string.<BR>9 A wrinkled or contracted eye-brow.<BR>10 Folly, stupidity.<BR>11 The rejected slough of the snake.<BR>E.<BR>लोच to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचन|लोचनं
लोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The eye.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A goddess of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>लोच to see, ल्यु or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचनामय|लोचनामयः
लोचनामय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Diseased affection of the eye, Ophthalmia, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लोचन the eye, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचमर्कट|लोचमर्कटः
लोचमर्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचमस्तक|लोचमस्तकः
लोचमस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>लोच sight, seeing, and मस्तक head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट
लोट<BR>(ऋ) लोदृ r. 1st cl. (लोटति)<BR>To be mad or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोटन|लोटनं
लोटन<BR>n. (नं)<BR>Tumbling, rolling.<BR>E.<BR>लुट to roll, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड
लोड<BR>(ऋ) लोडृ r. 1st cl. (लोडति)<BR>To be mad, to be frantic or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत|लोतं|लोतः
लोत<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 Plunder, booty, stolen goods.<BR>2 A tear, tears.<BR>3 A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, Uṇādi aff. तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत्र|लोत्रं
लोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Plunder, booty, stolen goods.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध|लोधः
लोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A sort of tree: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध्र|लोध्रः
लोध्र<BR>m. (-ध्रः)<BR>A tree, the bark of which is used in dyeing, (Symplocos racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>रुध to hinder, aff. रन्, and ल substituted for र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप|लोपः
लोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Rejection, cutting off in general, especially used as a grammatical term for dropping letters, syllables, &c.<BR>2 Disappearance, destruction.<BR>3 Erasure.<BR>4 Annulling, cancelling.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=724" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपा
लोपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The wife of the Muni AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to disturb, aff. अच् and टाष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाक|लोपाकः
लोपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Shakāl.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to cut, आकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपापक|लोपापकः
लोपापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Shakāl.<BR>f. (-पिका)<BR>A fox.<BR>E.<BR>लोप rejection (offal), आप to take, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपामुद्रा
लोपामुद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>लोप losing (reputation), अमुद्रा sad, not happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपामुद्रापति|लोपामुद्रापतिः
लोपामुद्रापति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The Muni AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>लोपामुद्रा as above, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाशक|लोपाशकः
लोपाशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Shakāl.<BR>f. (-शिका)<BR>1 A female Shakāl.<BR>2 A fox.<BR>E.<BR>लोप rejection, अश to eat, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्य
लोप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be rejected, erased, lost, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to cut off, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्त्र|लोप्त्रं
लोप्त्र<BR>nf. (-प्त्रं-प्त्री)<BR>Plunder, booty.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to cut off, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ|लोभः
लोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Covetousness, cupidity, intense or greedy desire.<BR>E.<BR>लुभ to desire or covet, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभमोहित
लोभमोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Beguiled or overcome by cupidity.<BR>E.<BR>लोभ, and मोहित beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभविरह|लोभविरहः
लोभविरह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Free from cupidity.<BR>E.<BR>लोभ, and हिरह separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभाकृष्ट
लोभाकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Tempted or attracted by greediness or desire.<BR>E.<BR>लोभ, and आकृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभिन्
लोभिन्<BR>mfn. (-भी-भिनी-भि)<BR>Desirous, cupidinous, covetous, greedy.<BR>E.<BR>लोभ desire, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ्य|लोभ्यः
लोभ्य<BR>mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>Desirable.<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>E.<BR>लुभ to covet or desire, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोम|लोमं|लोमः
लोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tail, a hairy tail.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकर्ण|लोमकर्णः
लोमकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, कर्ण an ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकूप|लोमकूपः
लोमकूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A pore of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>लोम, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमघ्न|लोमघ्नं
लोमघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Falling of the hair, morbid baldness.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair of the body, applied here to the hair of the head, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमन्
लोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>रू to sound, मनिन् Uṇādi aff., and र changed, or लू to cut, मनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमपाद|लोमपादः
लोमपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The name of a king of Aṅga, the eastern division of Bengal, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमपादपुरी
लोमपादपुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Campā, the capital of Lomapāda, the modern Bhāgalpur, and its vicinity.<BR>E.<BR>लोमपाद a king, and पुरी the city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमविष|लोमविषः
लोमविष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An animal, whose hair is supposed to be poisonous, as a tiger, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमश|लोमशः
लोमश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Hairy, covered with or made of hair.<BR>2 Woollen.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A ram.<BR>2 The name of a Ṛṣi celebrated in the Mahābhārata.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 A fox.<BR>2 A sort of Bonduc.<BR>3 A plant, (Leea hirta.)<BR>4 Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>5 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens)<BR>6 A medicinal plant, commonly Mahāmeda.<BR>7 Sida cordifolia.<BR>8 A female demi-divine being, an attendant on DURGĀ, one of the Śākinīs.<BR>9 Green vitriol.<BR>10 Orris root.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair or down, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमशपर्णिनी
लोमशपर्णिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>E.<BR>लोमश hairy, पर्ण a leaf, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमशमार्जार|लोमशमार्जारः|लोमशमार्ज्जारः
लोमशमार्जार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The pole-cat.<BR>E.<BR>लोमश hairy, and मार्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमसार|लोमसारः
लोमसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The emerald.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, and सार strength, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमहर्षण|लोमहर्षणं|लोमहर्षणः
लोमहर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Horripilation, erection of the hair of the body.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, and हर्षण rejoicing, supposed to be an indication of great pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमहृत्
लोमहृत्<BR>mfn. (-हृत्)<BR>Depilatory.<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाञ्च|लोमांच|लोमाञ्चः
लोमाञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>Horripilation; see रोमाञ्ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमालिका
लोमालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A fox.<BR>E.<BR>लोम hair, आली a line, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल|लोलः
लोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Shaking, tremulous.<BR>2 Rolling, tossing.<BR>3 Agitated, alarmed.<BR>4 Fickle, unsteady.<BR>5 Desiring, wishing, cupidinous.<BR>6 Greedy.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The tongue.<BR>2 The goddess LAKṢMĪ, or the goddess of wealth and fortune.<BR>3 A species of the Śarkarī metre.<BR>E.<BR>लोड to be frantic, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलजिह्व
लोलजिह्व<BR>mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>Greedy, insatiable.<BR>E.<BR>लोल, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलमान
लोलमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Rolling, tossing, rolling on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>लोड to be frantic, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलाक्षि
लोलाक्षि<BR>mfn. (-क्षिः-क्षिः-क्षी-क्षि)<BR>Having a rolling eye.<BR>E.<BR>लोल, and अक्षि the eye; also लोलचक्षुस्, लोलनयन, लोललोचन, लोलनेत्र, and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलिका
लोलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of dock or sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलित|लोलितः
लोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, tremulous, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>लुल to agitate, aff. क्त, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुप|लोलुपः
लोलुप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Very desirous or covetous, wishing, longing for, greedy, insatiable.<BR>E.<BR>लुप to desire, aff. अच्, and the intensitive form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुभ|लोलुभः
लोलुभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Very cupidinous, excessively desirous, very covetous or greedy.<BR>E.<BR>लुभ to desire or covet, aff. अच्, and the intensitive form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुव
लोलुव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Cutting much or often.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, freq. v., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलूया
लोलूया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Determination to cut.<BR>E.<BR>लू to cut, intensitive v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलूयावत्
लोलूयावत्<BR>mfn. (वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Resolved to cut or cut off.<BR>E.<BR>लोलूया, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट|लोष्टं|लोष्टः
लोष्ट<BR>r. 1st cl. (लोष्टते)<BR>To heap, to assemble, to collect or gather into a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट|लोष्टं|लोष्टः
लोष्ट<BR>mn. (-ष्टः-ष्टं)<BR>A clod, a lump of earth.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Rust of iron or iron filings.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट to heap, aff. अच्; or लू to cut, Uṇādi aff. क्त, with change of the radical vowel, and सुट् augment; also with कन् added लोष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टघ्न|लोष्टघ्नः
लोष्टघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट a clod, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टभेदन|लोष्टभेदनः
लोष्टभेदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A harrow.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट a clod, and भेदन what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टमय
लोष्टमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of a clod or of earth.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टमर्द्दिन्|लोष्टमर्दिन्
लोष्टमर्द्दिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दी-र्द्दिणी-र्द्दि)<BR>Who or what breaks clods of earth.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट, and मर्द्दिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टु|लोष्टुः
लोष्टु<BR>m. (-ष्टुः)<BR>A lump of earth.<BR>E.<BR>लोष्ट to heap, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोह|लोहं|लोहः
लोह<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>1 Iron, either crude or wrought.<BR>2 Steel.<BR>3 Any metal.<BR>4 A weapon.<BR>5 Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>6 Blood.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A red-coloured goat.<BR>E.<BR>ल to cut, aff. ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=725" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकण्टक|लोहकण्टकः
लोहकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thorny shrub.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकान्त|लोहकांत|लोहकान्तं|लोहकान्तः
लोहकान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The loadstone.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and कान्त in this compound a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकार|लोहकारः
लोहकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blacksmith, an ironsmith.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and कार who works in; also with कन् added लोहकारक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकिट्ट|लोहकिट्टं
लोहकिट्ट<BR>n. (-ट्टं)<BR>Rust of iron, or iron filings.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and किट्ट soil or sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहचूर्ण|लोहचूर्णं
लोहचूर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Iron filings.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहज|लोहजं
लोहज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Bell-metal.<BR>2 Rust of iron, or iron filings.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहजित्
लोहजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The diamond.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and जित् conquering, (in hardness.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहदारक|लोहदारकः
लोहदारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A hell.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and दारक what tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहद्राविन्
लोहद्राविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>लोह metal, and द्राविन् what fuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहनाल|लोहनालः
लोहनाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An iron arrow.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and नाल a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहपृष्ठ|लोहपृष्ठः
लोहपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A heron.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहप्रतिमा
लोहप्रतिमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 An image of iron.<BR>2 An anvil.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and प्रतिमा an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमय|लोहमयं
लोहमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of iron.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, aff. मयट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमारक|लोहमारकः
लोहमारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes triandra, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and मारक destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहराजक
लोहराजक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>लोह metal, राज shining, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहल|लोहलः
लोहल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Lisping, speaking inarticulately.<BR>2 Iron, irony.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The principal ring of a chain.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, ला to get or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहवर|लोहवरं
लोहवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>लोह a metal, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहवर्म्मन्|लोहवर्मन्
लोहवर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Mail, iron armour.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and वर्म्मन् armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहशङ्कु|लोहशंकु|लोहशङ्कुः
लोहशङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>1 A hell.<BR>2 An iron pike.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and शङ्कु a pike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहश्लेषण|लोहश्लेषणः
लोहश्लेषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Borax.<BR>E.<BR>लोह metal, श्चिष to embrace, to lay hold of, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहाभिसार|लोहाभिसारः
लोहाभिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Lustration of arms, ceremonies performed on the ninth of the light half of the month Aśvin; formerly a celebration observed by princes before opening a campaign, but now usually confined to the domestic decoration and worship of the soldier's weapons.<BR>E.<BR>लोह a weapon, अभि about, सृ to go, aff. घञ्; also लोहाभिहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहाभिहार|लोहाभिहारः
लोहाभिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Lustration of arms.<BR>E.<BR>लोह a weapon, अभि about, हृ to take, aff. घञ्; also लोहाभिसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहामिष|लोहामिषः
लोहामिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The flesh of a goat with red hair.<BR>E.<BR>लोह, and आमिष flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिका
लोहिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of large shallow bowl, sometimes of iron, but usually of wood and bound with iron, for the purpose of washing rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित|लोहितं|लोहितः
लोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or ती-तं)<BR>Red, of a red colour.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Red, the colour.<BR>2 The planet MARS.<BR>3 One of the male rivers.<BR>4 The Rohi, a kind of fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>5 A sort of deer.<BR>6 A snake.<BR>7 A deity, a demi-god.<BR>8 A sort of bean, (Ervum hirsutum.)<BR>9 A form of array.<BR>10 A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 A red kind of Agallochum.<BR>3 Saffron.<BR>4 Red sanders.<BR>5 War, battle.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman red with anger or with colour, &c.<BR>2 A sort of creeper, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>रुह to grow, इतन् Uṇādi aff., and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितक|लोहितकं|लोहितकः
लोहितक<BR>mfn. (-कः-तिका or -णिका-कं)<BR>Red.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A ruby.<BR>2 The planet MARS.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Calx of brass.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितचन्दन|लोहितचंदन|लोहितचन्दनं
लोहितचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितमृत्तिका
लोहितमृत्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and मृत्तिका soil, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताक्ष|लोहिताक्षः
लोहिताक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Red-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताङ्ग|लोहितांग|लोहिताङ्गः
लोहिताङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितानन|लोहिताननः
लोहितानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Red-faced.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An ichneumon.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितायस्
लोहितायस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and अयस् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिनी
लोहिनी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A woman red with anger, or painted red.<BR>E.<BR>see रोहित, the fem. aff. being ङीप्, and the penultimate consonant changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहोत्तम|लोहोत्तमं
लोहोत्तम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>लोह a metal, and उत्तस best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकायतिक|लौकायतिकः
लौकायतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An atheist, a materialist, a Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>लोकायत a particular heterodox doctrine, and ठक् aff.; also लोकायतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिक|लौकिकः
लौकिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mundane, worldly, human, what prevails amongst or is familiar to mankind.<BR>E.<BR>लोक mankind, the world, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिकता
लौकिकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Worldliness.<BR>2 Worldly currency, or custom.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also लौकिकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौक्य
लौक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Mundane, human.<BR>E.<BR>लोक, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौह|लौहः
लौह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Iron, made of iron, &c.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Iron.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>An iron vessel, a pot.<BR>E.<BR>लोह iron, and अण् deriv. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहबन्ध|लौहबंध|लौहबन्धः
लौहबन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>An iron chain or fetters.<BR>E.<BR>लौह, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहभाण्ड|लौहभांड|लौहभाण्डः
लौहभाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A pestle and mortar, usually of metal.<BR>E.<BR>लौह, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहभू
लौहभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>A sort of iron vessel, a boiler, a caldron.<BR>E.<BR>लौह iron, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहात्मन्
लौहात्मन्<BR>f. (-त्मा)<BR>A sort of iron boiler, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लौह made of iron, and आत्मन् substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित|लौहितः
लौहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The trident of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहितीक|लौहितीकः
लौहितीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Reddish, like or resembling red, &c.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित red, and ईकक aff. implying similarity in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित्य|लौहित्यं|लौहित्यः
लौहित्य<BR>nf. (-त्यं-ती)<BR>Redness.<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>1 A male river.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>लोहित as above, ष्यञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्पी
ल्पी<BR>r. 9th cl. (ल्पिनाति)<BR>To unite, to join, to be connected or attached to: it is also read ल्यी-ह्णी-ल्वी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्वी
ल्वी<BR>r. 9th cl. (ल्विनाति)<BR>1 To go, to move or approach.<BR>2 To join or be connected with, to mix with, to unite.<BR>3 To obtain: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व<BR>The twenty-ninth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet, or more properly the semivowel V; it is often confounded. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">Page727</a>] with the labial consonant or ब, with which it is also optionally interchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=726" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 The arm.<BR>3 A name of VARUṆA.<BR>4 Addressing.<BR>5 Auspiciousness.<BR>6 Strong, powerful.<BR>7 A dwelling.<BR>8 The residence of VARUṆA.<BR>9 The ocean.<BR>10 Water.<BR>11 Shaving.<BR>12 Like, as.<BR>f. (वा)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Hurting, injury.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 Weaving.<BR>5 A weaver.<BR>n. (वं)<BR>A sort of incantation or Mantra, of which the object is the deity VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, to injure, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश|वंशः
वंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Race, lineage, family.<BR>2 Assemblage, multitude.<BR>3 A bambu.<BR>4 The back-bone, the spine.<BR>mf. (-शः-शी)<BR>1 A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR>2 Bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>वंश to shine, घ aff., and नुम् augment; or वन् to sound, to serve, aff. श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक|वंशकं|वंशकः
वंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A small fish, (Cynoglossus lingua, HAM.)<BR>2 A large kind of sugar-cane.<BR>nf. (-शकं-शिका)<BR>Aloe wood.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of pipe or flute.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकफ|वंशकफं
वंशकफ<BR>n. (-फं)<BR>Flocks of cotton or cottony pods floating in the air.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकर|वंशकरः
वंशकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Making or perpetuating a family.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकीर्त्ति|वंशकीर्ति
वंशकीर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति)<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक्षय|वंशक्षयः
वंशक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Decay of a family.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and क्षय decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक्षीरी
वंशक्षीरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The manna of the bambu.<BR>E.<BR>वंश the bambu, and क्षीर milk; being of a milky colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशचरित्र
वंशचरित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A genealogical table or list, the history of a race or dynasty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and चरित्र an account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशज|वंशजः
वंशज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>1 Sprung from a good family.<BR>2 Produced by the bambu.<BR>nf. (-जं-जा)<BR>Bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, lineage, &c., and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशधर|वंशधरः
वंशधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Who or what supports a family.<BR>2 Carrying or holding a bambu, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशनालिका
वंशनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pipe, a reed or flute.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, नाल a tube, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपत्रक|वंशपत्रकं|वंशपत्रकः
वंशपत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Cynoglossus lingua, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, and पत्र a leaf, the shape of the fish resembling that of the leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपत्रपतित|वंशपत्रपतितं
वंशपत्रपतित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A species of the Atyaṣṭī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपरम्परा|वंशपरंपरा
वंशपरम्परा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Family, lineage, descent.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and परम्पर successive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशभोज्य
वंशभोज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Hereditary estate.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and भोज्य to be possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशरोचना
वंशरोचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>An earthy concretion of a milk-white colour, formed in the hollow of the bambu, and known by the name of bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>वंश the bambu, रुच to shine, aff. युच्; also र being changed to ल, वंशलोचना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशलोचना
वंशलोचना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The manna of the bambu: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवर्द्धन
वंशवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Increasing or exalting a family.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and वर्द्धन augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवितति|वंशविततिः
वंशवितति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A clump of bambus.<BR>2 Family, descent.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and वितति extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशविशुद्ध
वंशविशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Of a good family.<BR>2 Of a good bambu, (made, constructed.)<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and विशुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवृद्धि
वंशवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Prosperity of a family.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशशलाका
वंशशलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The bambu pipe that forms the body of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>2 Any small bambu pin or stake, as the bar of a cage, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, and शलाका a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशसमाचार
वंशसमाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Family usage.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and समाचार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशस्थविल|वंशस्थविलं
वंशस्थविल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशहीन
वंशहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having no kindred or family.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशाग्र|वंशाग्रं
वंशाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The shoot of a bambu.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशाङ्कुर|वंशांकुर|वंशाङ्कुरः
वंशाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The shoot of a bambu.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and अङ्कुर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशावली
वंशावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A pedigree, a genealogy.<BR>E.<BR>वंश, and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशानुचरित|वंशानुचरितं
वंशानुचरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A pedigree, a genealogical list, or history.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a family, अनु implying succession, and चरित proceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिक|वंशिकं
वंशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a family, a bambu, &c.<BR>nf. (-कं-का)<BR>Aloe wood.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशीधर|वंशीधरः
वंशीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A piper.<BR>2 A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वंशी, and धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश्य|वंश्यः
वंश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>1 Of a good family.<BR>2 Of the same family.<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>1 A son.<BR>2 A pupil, a scholar.<BR>3 A kinsman, from seven generations above and seven below.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a family, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहिष्ठ
वंहिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Most, very much or great.<BR>E.<BR>वंह substituted for वृन्दारक great, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहीयस्
वंहीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very much or very large.<BR>E.<BR>वंह for वृन्दारक, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक
वक<BR>(इ) वकि r. 1st cl. (वंकते)<BR>1 To be crooked, (literally or figuratively); to be curved or bent, to be depraved or wicked.<BR>2 To bend, to make crooked.<BR>3 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक
वक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>2 A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>3 KUVERA.<BR>4 The name of a demon.<BR>5 A small apparatus for calcining or subliming metals or minerals, consisting of two crucibles, one inverted over the other, luted together and placed over a fire.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, or वकि to be crooked, aff. घञ् or अच्; in the latter case the nasal augment is not inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकचिञ्चिका
वकचिञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकजित्
वकजित्<BR>n. (-जित्)<BR>A name of BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>वक a demon, and जित् the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकधूप|वकधूपः
वकधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Compound perfume: see वृकधूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकनिसूदन|वकनिसूदनः
वकनिसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>वक the demon, and निसूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकपुष्प|वकपुष्पः
वकपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>वक curving, from वकि to be crooked, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकवृत्ति|वकवृत्तिः
वकवृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>A false or hypocritical devotee: see वकव्रतिन्.<BR>E.<BR>वक, and वृत्ति livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकवैरिन्
वकवैरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>वक the demon, and वैरिन् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकव्रतिन्
वकव्रतिन्<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A false devotee, a religious hypocrite, or one who assumes the appearance of devotion or meditation, for interested purposes.<BR>E.<BR>वक a crane, व्रत observance, and इनि aff.; compared to the crane, who stands by a pool demure and sly, and apparently absorbed in contemplation, till he sees a fish on which to dart; also with ठक्, aff. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">Page728</a>] वकव्रतिक, and derived from वक, and चर who goes, वकचर or वकव्रतचर m. (-रः) &c.; see वैडालव्रतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=727" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकाची
वकाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकुल|वकुलः
वकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A sort of drug, commonly Kākolī.<BR>E.<BR>वक to be crooked, aff. उलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकेरुका
वकेरुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A small crane.<BR>2 The branch of a tree bent by the wind.<BR>E.<BR>वक a crane, or crooked, ईर to go or be, aff. उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकोट
वकोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A crane.<BR>E.<BR>वक to be crooked. ओटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्क
वक्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (वक्कते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्य|वक्तव्यः
वक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 Fit or proper to be said or spoken, to be spoken or uttered.<BR>2 Vile, bad, reprehensible.<BR>3 Subject, dependant.<BR>4 Low, base.<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>1 A rule, a dictum, a sentence.<BR>2 Speech.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, and तव्य aff., of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्यता
वक्तव्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Blame, reprehension.<BR>2 The nature or property of what is to be said, or the occasion for it.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुकाम
वक्तुकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Desirous of speaking.<BR>E.<BR>वक्तु for वक्तुम् to speak, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तृ
वक्तृ<BR>mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>1 Speaking, a speaker.<BR>2 Loquacious, talkative.<BR>3 Speaking well or sensibly, eloquent.<BR>4 Wise, learned.<BR>5 Speaking truly or truth, honest, sincere.<BR>m. (-क्ता)<BR>1 An expounder, a teacher.<BR>2 An orator, a speaker.<BR>E.<BR>वच् to speak, तृच् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्र|वक्त्रं
वक्त्र<BR>n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>1 The mouth or face.<BR>2 A sort of garment.<BR>3 Metre, verse, especially of the Vedas.<BR>4 A plant: see तगरसूल.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, Uṇādi aff. त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रखुर|वक्त्रखुरः
वक्त्रखुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tooth.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, and खुर a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रज|वक्त्रजः
वक्त्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, (of BRAHMĀ,) ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रताल|वक्त्रतालं
वक्त्रताल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A musical instrument, played on with the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, ताल tune; it may also signify, making a noise with the mouth, by striking it with the hand at the moment of uttering sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रतुण्ड|वक्त्रतुण्डः
वक्त्रतुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र, and तुण्ड beak or nose, having the proboscis of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रपट्ट|वक्त्रपट्टः
वक्त्रपट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A bag containing corn tied round a horse's head.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, and पट्ट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रभेदिन्
वक्त्रभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>Pungency, pungent or acrid flavour.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, and भेदिन् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रशोधिन्
वक्त्रशोधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A lime.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, and शोधिन् what cleanses; also वक्त्रशोधन m. (-नः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रासव|वक्त्रासवः
वक्त्रासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Saliva.<BR>E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, and आसव wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्र|वक्रं|वक्रः
वक्र<BR>mfn. (-क्रः-क्रा-क्रं)<BR>1 Crooked, curved, bowed or bent.<BR>2 Cruel, malignant.<BR>3 Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>4 Indirect, evasive.<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>The winding course of a river or water-fall, the arm or bend of a stream.<BR>2 A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>1 A name of SATURN.<BR>2 The planet MARS.<BR>3 RUDRA or ŚIVA.<BR>4 The demon TRIPURA.<BR>E.<BR>वकि to go crookedly, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रखड्ग|वक्रखड्गः
वक्रखड्ग<BR>m. (-ड्गः)<BR>A sabre or scimitar.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and खड्ग a sword; also वक्रखड्गकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रगामिन्
वक्रगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>1 Who or what goes tortuously.<BR>2 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रग्रीव|वक्रग्रीवः
वक्रग्रीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A camel.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रचञ्चु|वक्रचंचु|वक्रचञ्चुः
वक्रचञ्चु<BR>m. (-ञ्चुः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and चञ्चु the beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रता
वक्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Crookedness.<BR>2 Wickedness.<BR>3 Craft, cunning.<BR>4 Evasive or indirect speech.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र, and तल् added; also with त्व, वक्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रतुण्ड|वक्रतुंड|वक्रतुण्डः
वक्रतुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, तुण्ड a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रदंष्ट्र|वक्रदंष्ट्रः
वक्रदंष्ट्र<BR>m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and दंष्ट्र a tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रनक्र|वक्रनक्रः
वक्रनक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>A low or depraved man.<BR>2 A parrot.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and नक्र the nose, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रनासिक|वक्रनासिकः
वक्रनासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रपुच्छ|वक्रपुच्छः
वक्रपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and पुच्छ a tail; also वक्रपुच्छिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रपुष्प|वक्रपुष्पः
वक्रपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and पुष्प the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रबालधि|वक्रबालधिः
वक्रबालधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, बालधि a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रभणित|वक्रभणितं
वक्रभणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Indirect speech, equivoque, evasion.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and भणित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रम|वक्रमः
वक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>अव reverse, क्रम to go, aff. अच्, and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रवक्त्र|वक्रवक्त्रः
वक्रवक्त्र<BR>m. (-क्त्रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्राग्र|वक्राग्रं
वक्राग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>A plant, commonly Betu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्राङ्ग|वक्रांग|वक्राङ्गः
वक्राङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A goose.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र bending, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रि|वक्रिः
वक्रि<BR>mfn. (-क्रिः-क्रिः-क्रि)<BR>Speaking falsely, uttering untruths, prevaricating, lying.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र to be crooked, (metaph.) क्रिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिन्
वक्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-क्री-क्रिणी-क्रि)<BR>1 Crooked.<BR>2 Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>m. (-क्री)<BR>A Jaina or Bauddha.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, fraudulent, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिम
वक्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Bent, curved.<BR>E.<BR>वकि to go crookedly, क्रिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिमन्
वक्रिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Crookedness, curvature.<BR>2 Craftiness, cunning.<BR>E.<BR>बक्र, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीकरण
वक्रीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Curving, bending, distorting.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीकृत
वक्रीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bent, made crooked.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र, and कृत made, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीभाव|वक्रीभावः
वक्रीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Curvature, curve.<BR>2 Fraudulent or dishonest disposition.<BR>E.<BR>वक्री, and भाव property, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीभूत
वक्रीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bent, crooked.<BR>2 Dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रोक्ति|वक्रोक्तिः
वक्रोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Equivoque, evasion, pun, the covert expression of something else than the words used naturally imply, either from the manner in which they are uttered, or some other sense of which they are susceptible.<BR>2 Hint, insinuation.<BR>3 Sarcasm.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, dishonest, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रोष्ठिका
वक्रोष्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A gentle smile, one in which the teeth are not shewn.<BR>E.<BR>वक्र crooked, ओष्ठ the lip, and कन् aff., fem. form; also वक्रोष्टिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष|वक्षः
वक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (वक्षति)<BR>1 To be angry.<BR>2 To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षःसम्मर्द्धिनी
वक्षःसम्मर्द्धिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Wife of the bosom.<BR>E.<BR>वक्षस्, and सम्मर्द्दिनी who rubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षण|वक्षणं
वक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The breast: see वक्षस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=728" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्
वक्षस्<BR>n. (-क्षः)<BR>The breast, the bosom, the chest.<BR>m. (-क्षाः)<BR>An ox, (confined to the Vedas.)<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, or वक्ष to accumulate, aff. असुन्, in the first case सुट् is inserted; again वह to bear, असुन् aff., सुट् augment, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्स्थल
वक्षस्स्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The breast, the heart.<BR>E.<BR>वक्षस्, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोज|वक्षोजं|वक्षोजः
वक्षोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>वक्षस् the breast or chest, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोरुह|वक्षोरुहः
वक्षोरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The female breast.<BR>E.<BR>वक्षस् the chest, and रुह what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष्यमाण|वक्ष्यमाणः
वक्ष्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being to be said or described.<BR>E.<BR>वच् to say, desid. pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वख
वख<BR>r. 1st cl. (वखति) (इ) वखि (वंखति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग
वग<BR>(इ) वगि r. 1st cl. (वंगति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To go lamely, to limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वगाह|वगाहः
वगाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Bathing, ablution.<BR>E.<BR>अव before गाह to agitate, aff. अच्, and the initial rejected; also अवगाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्नु|वग्नुः
वग्नु<BR>m. (-ग्नुः)<BR>A speaker.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, नु Uṇādi aff., and च changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वघ
वघ<BR>(इ) वघि r. 1st cl. (वंघते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To blame or censure.<BR>3 To begin.<BR>4 To begin moving.<BR>5 To move swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क|वंक|वंकः|वङ्कः
वङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 The bend or elbow of a river, the winding course of a stream.<BR>2 Crookedness.<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>The pummel of a saddle.<BR>E.<BR>वकि to curve or bend, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्किल|वंकिल|वंकिलः|वङ्किलः
वङ्किल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्क crookedness, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्य|वङ्क्यः
वङ्क्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं)<BR>Crooked, curved.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to go, ण्यत् aff., and च changed to क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्रि|वंक्रि|वंक्रिः|वङ्क्रिः
वङ्क्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्क्रिः)<BR>1 A rib.<BR>2 The wood of a thatch.<BR>3 A particular musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>वकि to be crooked, and क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षण|वंक्षणं|वङ्क्षणः
वङ्क्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The groin, the public and iliac regions.<BR>E.<BR>वाञ्छि to desire, ल्युट् aff., and the form irr., or वक्ष to accumulate, ल्युट् aff., and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षु|वंक्षु|वंक्षुः|वङ्क्षुः
वङ्क्षु<BR>f. (-ङ्क्षुः)<BR>A small arm or branch of the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्क्ष to accumulate, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग|वंग|वङ्गं|वङ्गः
वङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Lead.<BR>2 Tin.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Bengal, or the eastern parts of the modern province.<BR>2 Cotton.<BR>3 The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>वगि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गन|वङ्गनः
वङ्गन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The egg-plant.<BR>E.<BR>वगि to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गशुल्वज|वंगशुल्वज|वङ्गशुल्वजं
वङ्गशुल्वज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Brass.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्ग tin, शुल्व copper, and ज produced; an alloy of tin and copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गसेन|वङ्गसेनः
वङ्गसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्ग Bengal, सि to sew, aff. ल्युट्; also with कन् added, वङ्गसेनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गारि|वंगारि|वङ्गारिः
वङ्गारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्ग lead, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गुला
वङ्गुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A mode of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच|वचः
वच<BR>(औ) औवच r. 1st cl. (वचति) 2nd cl. (वक्ति) and 10th cl. (वाचयति)<BR>1 To speak, to tell.<BR>2 To inform.<BR>3 To read, to expound: (the second cl. is the most usual form of the root, in which its inflections however are very irregular.)<BR>With प्र,<BR>To begin to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच|वचः
वच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A parrot.<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>1 Orris root, (Acorus calamus; also Zinziber Zedoaria.)<BR>2 The Sārikā, (Turdus Salica.)<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचक्नु|वचक्नुः
वचक्नु<BR>mfn. (-क्नुः-क्नुः-क्नु)<BR>Talkative, loquacious, eloquent.<BR>m. (-क्नुः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, Uṇādi aff. अक्नुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचन|वचनं
वचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Speech, speaking.<BR>2 A sentence, a text, a dictum, an aphorism, a rule.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनकर|वचनकरः
वचनकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Obedient.<BR>2 Speaking.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The author or enunciator of a precept.<BR>E.<BR>वचन्, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनक्रम|वचनक्रमः
वचनक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Discourse, order of words.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनग्राहिन्
वचनग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Compliant, conformable, submissive, humble.<BR>E.<BR>वचन speech, ग्राहिन् taking, obeying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनविरुद्ध
वचनविरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Contrary to a text or precept.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and विरुद्ध opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनविरोध|वचनविरोधः
वचनविरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Incongruity, contradiction, inconsistency of texts.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and विरोध opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनव्यक्ति|वचनव्यक्तिः
वचनव्यक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Distinctness or perspicuity of a text.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and व्यक्ति plainness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीय|वचनीयः
वचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be spoken or said.<BR>2 Censurable, to be noticed or reproved.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीयता
वचनीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Rumour, report, especially ill report, detraction, scandal.<BR>2 Blame, reprehension.<BR>E.<BR>वचनीव to be censured, तल् aff.; also with त्व aff., वचनीयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनमात्र
वचनमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Mere words, assertion unsupported by facts.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनशत
वचनशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Repeated speech or declaration.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनेस्थित|वचनेस्थितः
वचनेस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Compliant, conformable, obedient.<BR>E.<BR>वचने in the word, and स्थित who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचलु|वचलुः
वचलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>Offence, fault.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, अलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्
वचस्<BR>n. (-चः)<BR>1 Speech, voice.<BR>2 Words, a speech.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्कर|वचस्करः
वचस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Obedient, compliant.<BR>E.<BR>वचस्, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज
वज<BR>r. 1st cl. (बजति)<BR>To go.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वाजयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To prepare, to make.<BR>3 To prepare the way.<BR>4 To trim or feather an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्र|वज्रं|वज्रः
वज्र<BR>mfn. (-ज्रः-ज्रा-ज्रं)<BR>1 Hard, impenetrable, adamantine.<BR>2 Cross, forked.<BR>mn. (-ज्रः-ज्रं)<BR>1 A thunder-bolt in general, or the thunder-bolt of INDRA.<BR>2 The diamond, (the gem being considered analogous^1 in hardness to the thunder-bolt, or in fact to be the same substance.)<BR>3 A diagram, the figure of which is supposed to be that of the thunder-bolt.<BR>4 A child or pupil.<BR>5 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>6 Sour gruel.<BR>7 The blossom of the sesamum.<BR>8 Harsh language.<BR>m. (-ज्रः)<BR>1 One of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>2 Kuśa grass.<BR>f. (-ज्रा-ज्री)<BR>A species of Euphorbia.<BR>f. (-ज्रा)<BR>1 A plant: see गुडुची.<BR>2 A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वज to go, रक् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रक|वज्रकं
वज्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of salt, an impure carbonate of soda.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकङ्कट|वज्रकंकट|वज्रकङ्कटः
वज्रकङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Hanumān, the monkey demigod.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, (as hard,) and कङ्कट armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकण्टक|वज्रकण्टकः
वज्रकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Euphorbia.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र a thunder-bolt, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकपालिन्
वज्रकपालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>One of the Bauddha saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रक्षार|वज्रक्षारं
वज्रक्षार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An alkaline earth, an impure carbonate of soda.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र diamond, and क्षार alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=729" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रजित्
वज्रजित्<BR>m. (जित्)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and जित् who conquers; being invulnerable to repeated shocks of INDRA'S bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रज्वाला
वज्रज्वाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A clap of thunder.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the bolt, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रटीक|वज्रटीकः
वज्रटीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रतुण्ड|वज्रतुंड|वज्रतुण्डः
वज्रतुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The deity GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A vulture.<BR>4 A gnat, a musquito.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and तुण्ड face or beak, as hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रदन्त|वज्रदंत|वज्रदन्तः
वज्रदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र a thunder-bolt, (as hard,) and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रदशन|वज्रदशनः
वज्रदशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र, and दशन a tooth: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रद्रु|वज्रद्रुः
वज्रद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>Euphorbia of various species.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र thunderbolt, (as hard,) and द्रु a tree; also वज्रद्रुम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रद्रुम|वज्रद्रुमः
वज्रद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Euphorbia: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रधर|वज्रधरः
वज्रधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 INDRA, as the JUPITER Tonans of the Hindus.<BR>2 A Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and धर who has or holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रनिर्घोष|वज्रनिर्घोषः
वज्रनिर्घोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A clap of thunder.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the bolt, and निर्घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रनिष्पेष|वज्रनिष्पेषः
वज्रनिष्पेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A clap of thunder.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the bolt, and निष्पेष here meaning the sound produced by friction or concussion, from निर् forth, पिष to grind, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपाणि|वज्रपाणिः
वज्रपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and पाणि the hand: see वज्रधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपात|वज्रपातः
वज्रपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A thunder-bolt, a stroke of lightning.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र, and पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपुष्प|वज्रपुष्पं
वज्रपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>The blossom of the sesamum.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र a diamond, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रबध
वज्रबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Death by lightning.<BR>2 Cross multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र, and बय killing, or multiplying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रमय
वज्रमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Hard, adamantine.<BR>2 Hard-hearted.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्ररद|वज्ररदः
वज्ररद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र a thunder-bolt, (as hard,) and रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रवल्ली
वज्रवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A species of sun-flower, (Heliotropium.)<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रवाराही
वज्रवाराही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A female personification of Māyā or unreality, amongst the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रशृङ्खला
वज्रशृङ्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A female deification peculiar to the Jainas, and one of their sixteen Vidyā-Devīs.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र a diamond^1, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रसूर्य्य|वज्रसूर्य|वज्रसूर्य्यः
वज्रसूर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राङ्ग|वज्रांग|वज्राङ्गः
वज्राङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A snake.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A sort of grain, (Coix barbata.)<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, (as hard,) and अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राघात|वज्राघातः
वज्राघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A thunder-bolt or stroke.<BR>2 A sudden calamity.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र^1, and आघात blow.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राभ|वज्राभः
वज्राभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Precious Opal.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the diamond, (in hardness perhaps,) आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राभ्यास|वज्राभ्यासः
वज्राभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Cross multiplication.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र, and अभ्यास practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राशनि|वज्राशनिः
वज्राशनि<BR>m. (निः)<BR>INDRA'S thunder-bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रिन्
वज्रिन्<BR>m. (-ज्री)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 A Jaina deified saint.<BR>3 A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>वज्र the thunder-bolt, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च
वञ्च<BR>(उ) वञ्च r. 1st cl. (वञ्चति)<BR>To go.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वञ्चते वञ्चयते)<BR>To delude, to cheat, to trick or deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चक|वंचक|वञ्चकः
वञ्चक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Fraudulent, crafty.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A jackal or Shakal.<BR>2 A tame or house ichneumon.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>4 A low or vile man.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चथ|वंचथ|वंचथः|वञ्चथः
वञ्चथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A rogue, a knave, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, Uṇādi aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चन|वंचन|वंचनं|वञ्चनं
वञ्चन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cheating, fraud.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चनीय
वञ्चनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be tricked or cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चयित्वा
वञ्चयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चित|वंचित|वञ्चितः
वञ्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tricked, deceived, cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, aff. क्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चुक|वंचुक|वञ्चुकः
वञ्चुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Crafty, fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to cheat, aff. उकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्य|वञ्च्यं
वञ्च्य<BR>mfn. (-ञ्च्या-ञ्च्या-ञ्च्यं)<BR>1 To be gone.<BR>2 To be cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुल|वंजुल|वञ्जुलः
वञ्जुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A tree, (Dalbergia Ougeinensis.)<BR>2 Another tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>3 Common cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>4 A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>5 A sort of bird.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A cow that yields abundance of milk.<BR>E.<BR>वञ्च to go, aff. उलच्, and च changed to ज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुलप्रिय|वंजुलप्रिय|वञ्जुलप्रियः
वञ्जुलप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The ratan, (Calamus rotang.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट|वटः
वट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वटति वटयति)<BR>1 To surround or encompass.<BR>2 To tie or string, to connect.<BR>3 To partition, to divide.<BR>r. 1st cl. causal form (वटयति)<BR>To speak.<BR>(इ) वटि r. 4th and 10th cls. (वण्ट्यति वण्टयति)<BR>To partition, to separate or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट|वटः
वट<BR>subst. mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>A string, a rope, a tie.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The large Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>2 A round figure, a circle, a cypher, a ball or globe.<BR>3 Pulse ground and fried with oil or butter.<BR>4 A small shell, a cowrie.<BR>5 Equality in shape or dimension.<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, to tie, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटक|वटकः
वटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Pulse ground and fried in oil or butter.<BR>2 A weight of eight Māṣas.<BR>f. (-टिका)<BR>A pill, a bolus.<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटपत्रा
वटपत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A plant, from the fibrous leaves of which bowstrings, &c. are made, (Aletris hyacinthoides: Sanseviera zeylanica, Rox.'s Cata.)<BR>E.<BR>वट a string, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटर|वटरः
वटर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Wicked, villainous.<BR>2 Slippery, unsteady.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A cock.<BR>2 A thief.<BR>3 A cloth worn round the head, a turban.<BR>4 A mat.<BR>5 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>6 A churning stick.<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटवासिन्
वटवासिन्<BR>mf. (-सी-सिनी)<BR>A sort of demigod, male and female; a YAKṢA or YAKṢIṆĪ, KUVERA'S special attendants.<BR>E.<BR>वट the Indian fig in which these spirits are supposed to be fond of abiding, वास abode, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटाकर|वटाकरः
वटाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cord, a rope, a string.<BR>E.<BR>वट surrounding, आकर what makes, from कृ to make, with आङ् prefix, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटावीक|वटावीकः
वटावीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A notorious thief, a dakoit, a robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटि|वटिः
वटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A sort of tick or body louse.<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिन्
वटिन्<BR>mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>1 Stringed, having a string.<BR>2 Circular, globular.<BR>E.<BR>वट, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=730" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटु|वटुः
वटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>1 The Brahmacārī or religious student, after his investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>2 A lad, a youth in general.<BR>3 A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, (with the string, &c.) or to speak, उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटुक|वटुकः
वटुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A lad, a young man in general, or one fit to receive the sacrificial thread.<BR>2 A religious student.<BR>3 A stupid fellow, a blockhead.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटूकरण
वटूकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Investiture with the sacred and characteristic thread.<BR>E.<BR>वटु a lad after investiture, कृ to make, aff. ल्युट्. and the vowel of वटु made long or technically, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठ
वठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (वठति)<BR>To be large, powerful or able;<BR>also वट (इ) वठि (वंठते)<BR>To move alone or unaccompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठर|वठरः
वठर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Vile, wicked, abandoned.<BR>2 Stupid, slow, dull.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A blockhead, a fool.<BR>2 A physician.<BR>3 A waterpot.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, अरच् aff., and च changed to ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड
वड<BR>(इ) वडि r. 1st cl. (वण्डते)<BR>1 To partition, to share or divide.<BR>2 To surround or encompass.<BR>3 To cover: in the first sense it is sometimes read as a root of the 10th cl. (वंडयति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडभि|वडभिः
वडभि<BR>f. (-भिः or भी)<BR>1 The wooden frame of a thatch.<BR>2 A temporary building or awning on the top of a palace, or a room or turret so situated.<BR>E.<BR>वल to cover, अभच् aff., इन् added, and again optionally ङीष्, ल changed to ड; otherwise वलभि and वलभी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडा
वडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Pulse ground and fried with oil or butter.<BR>E.<BR>वल to cover, अच् and टाप् aff., and ल changed to its congener ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडिश
वडिश<BR>nf. (-शं-शा or -शी)<BR>A fish-hook.<BR>E.<BR>वटिन् having a string, a bait, शो to destroy, and ड aff.; the radical ट changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड्र|वड्रं
वड्र<BR>mfn. (-ड्रः-ड्रा-ड्रं)<BR>Large, great.<BR>E.<BR>वल to cover, रक् aff., ल changed to ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण|वणः
वण<BR>(ऋ) वणृ r. 1st cl. (वणति)<BR>To sound; also वन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट|वंट|वण्टः
वण्ट<BR>r. 10th cl. (वण्टयति)<BR>To partition, to separate or divide; also वटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट|वंट|वण्टः
वण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>1 A part, a portion.<BR>2 A man unmarried.<BR>3 The handle of a sickle.<BR>E.<BR>वटि to divide, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टक|वंटक|वंटकः|वण्टकः
वण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A part, a portion, a share.<BR>E.<BR>वटि to divide, घञ् and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टन|वंटन|वंटनं
वण्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Portioning, partitioning, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>वटि to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टनीय
वण्टनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Divisible, to be divided.<BR>E.<BR>वटि to divide, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ|वंठ|वण्ठः
वण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 An unmarried man.<BR>2 A dwarf.<BR>3 A javelin.<BR>E.<BR>वठि to go alone, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठर|वंठर|वंठरः|वण्ठरः
वण्ठर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The new shoot of the Tāla or palm tree.<BR>2 The sheath that envelopes the young bambu.<BR>3 A rope for tying a goat, &c.<BR>4 A breast.<BR>5 A dog's tail.<BR>6 A dog.<BR>7 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वठि to go alone, aff. अरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड|वंड|वण्डः
वण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>1 Maimed, defective, crippled, but especially in the hands.<BR>2 Impotent, emasculated.<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A man who is circumcised or has no prepuce.<BR>2 An ox without his tail.<BR>f. (-ण्डः)<BR>An unchaste woman.<BR>E.<BR>वण to sound, &c., aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डर|वंडर|वंडरः|वण्डरः
वण्डर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A niggard, a miser.<BR>2 A eunuch or attendant on the woman's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डाल|वंडाल|वंडालः|वण्डालः
वण्डाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A description of conflict, the contest of heroes.<BR>2 A boat.<BR>3 A spade, a hoe.<BR>E.<BR>वडि to divide, आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्
वत्<BR>ind.<BR>As, like, similar: this is more generally considered as an affix to words, termed technically वति, as ब्राह्मणवत् like a Brahman, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
वत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Uttered, sounded, spoken.<BR>2 Asked, begged.<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle analogous to ah, oh, &c. expressing sorrow.<BR>2 Compassion.<BR>3 Pleasure.<BR>4 Oh, ho, a vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>वन to ask or beg, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतंस|वतंसः
वतंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 An ear-ring.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>E.<BR>अव before तसि to adorn, and अच् aff., the initial rejected; also अवतंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतण्ड|वतण्डः
वतण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The name of a Muni.<BR>E.<BR>अव before वडि to beat, aff. अच्, and अ rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतोका
वतोका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cow miscarrying from accident.<BR>E.<BR>अव before तोक offspring, and अ rejected; also अवतोका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स<BR>n. (-त्सं)<BR>The breast, the chest.<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>1 A calf.<BR>2 A year.<BR>mf. (-त्सः-त्सा)<BR>A term of endearment, used to children, scholars, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, kindly to, Uṇādi aff. स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सक|वत्सकं|वत्सकः
वत्सक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A calf.<BR>2 A child.<BR>3 A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>E.<BR>वत्स, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सकाम
वत्सकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Fond of or anxious about a child.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A cow anxious after her calf, a mother anxious after her child, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, and काम to desire, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सगुरु
वत्सगुरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A master.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स, and गुरु teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सतर|वत्सतरः
वत्सतर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A steer.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, and तरप् aff. of excess; more than a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सतन्त्री
वत्सतन्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>The rope that ties a calf.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स, and तन्त्री a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सनाभ|वत्सनाभः
वत्सनाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>An active poison; also called Mīthā Zeher, the root of the Aconite ferox brought from Nepal.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, and नभ to injure, अण् aff.; the root is sometimes compared to the nipple of a cow, whence perhaps this etymology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सपत्तन|वत्सपत्तनं
वत्सपत्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The name of a city in the north of India; one place to which it is applied is now a village in the district of Gorakhpur.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, and पत्तन a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सर|वत्सरः
वत्सर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A year.<BR>E.<BR>वद to abide, and सरन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सरान्तक|वत्सरांतक|वत्सरान्तकः
वत्सरान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Name of a month, Phalguna.<BR>E.<BR>वत्सर, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सल|वत्सलः
वत्सल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Affectionate, kind.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Affection, fondness.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A cow anxious for her calf.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a child, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सलता
वत्सलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Tenderness, affection.<BR>E.<BR>वत्सल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, वत्सलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्साक्षी
वत्साक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सादनी
वत्सादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, &c., अदन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सीय|वत्सीयः
वत्सीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Proper or fit for a calf.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A cowherd.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, &c., and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद|वदः
वद<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वदति-ते वदयति-ते)<BR>1 To inform, to speak to or tell, to declare.<BR>2 To speak articulately.<BR>3 To abide.<BR>With अनु,<BR>(अनुवदते)<BR>To speak similarly or subsequent.<BR>With अप prefixed,<BR>(अपवदति-ते)<BR>To reprove, to censure.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To salute respectfully or by name.<BR>With उप,<BR>(उपवदते)<BR>To explain.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To speak out or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">Page732</a>] plainly.<BR>With परि,<BR>(परिवदति)<BR>To speak against.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To rumour, to slander.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>(प्रतिवदति)<BR>To reply to or answer.<BR>With वि,<BR>(विवदते)<BR>To dispute.<BR>With वि and प्र,<BR>(विप्रवदति or -ते)<BR>To wrangle or dispute together.<BR>With वि and सं,<BR>To break a promise.<BR>With सम and प्र,<BR>(सष्प्रवदते)<BR>To speak articulately in concert;<BR>(सष्प्रवदति)<BR>To utter or articulate sounds together.<BR>(इ,) वदि (वंदते)<BR>1 To salute with reverence or respect.<BR>2 To praise, to eulogize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=731" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद|वदः
वद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Speaking, able to speak, speaking well or sensibly.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदत्
वदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन|वदनं
वदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The mouth, the face.<BR>2 The summit or apex of a triangle.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनसरोज
वदनसरोज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The face of a mistress.<BR>E.<BR>वदन, and सरोज a lotus; also similar compounds, as वदनाम्बुरुह, वदनारविन्द, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनासव|वदनासवः
वदनासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Saliva, the moisture of the lips.<BR>E.<BR>वदन the mouth, and आसव spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनेन्दु
वदनेन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>The face.<BR>E.<BR>वदन, and इन्दु the moon; also similar compounds, as वदनत्रन्द्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्ति|वदन्तिः
वदन्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः-न्ती)<BR>Speech, discourse, talk.<BR>E.<BR>वद to say or speak, झिच् Uṇādi aff., ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्य|वदन्यः
वदन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Munificent, bountiful.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, aff. अन्य; also वदान्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदमान
वदमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Saying, calling.<BR>2 Glorifying, boasting.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदरिक
वदरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The jujube: see वदरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदान्य|वदान्यः
वदान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 Liberal, munificent.<BR>2 Speaking kindly or agreeably.<BR>3 Eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, आन्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदाल|वदालः
वदाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sheat-fish, (Silurus Boalis, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, aff. आलच्; also with कन् added, वदालक. m. (-कः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदावद|वदावदः
वदावद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Speaking, a speaker, able to speak, able to speak well, eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, aff. अच्, the root repeated, and आ inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधु|वधुः
वधु<BR>f. (-धुः)<BR>1 A son's wife.<BR>2 A wife in general.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, उ aff., more commonly वधू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुका
वधुका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A wife.<BR>E.<BR>वधु for वधू, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुटी
वधुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A daughter-in-law: see वधूटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधू
वधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>1 Woman in general, a female.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>3 A young wife, one recently married, a bride.<BR>4 A son's wife.<BR>5 A sort of bulbous root, (Curcuma reclinata.)<BR>6 A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata): see पृक्का.<BR>7 A plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, उ aff., and ह changed to ध; also derived from षध to bind, in which case it is written वधू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूजन|वधूजनः
वधूजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>वधू a female, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूटी
वधूटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A son's wife.<BR>2 A young woman living in her father's house, whether married or unmarried.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, कूटट् aff., and ह changed to घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूशयन
वधूशयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A lattice, a loop-hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
वन<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वनति वनयति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To serve, to honour.<BR>3 To help.<BR>4 To be distressed.<BR>(उ) वनु r. 1st and 10th cls. (वनति वनयति)<BR>1 To act, to transact business.<BR>2 To injure;<BR>also r. 8th cl. (वनुते)<BR>To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
वन<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A forest, a wood, a grove.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A residence, a dwelling or abode.<BR>3 A house.<BR>4 A cascade or fountain.<BR>E.<BR>वन to sound, to serve, to seek, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकचु
वनकचु<BR>m. (-चुः)<BR>A species of Arum, (A. colocasia^1.)<BR>E.<BR>वन, and कचु the same.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकरिन्
वनकरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A wild elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and करिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकार्प्पासी|वनकार्पासी
वनकार्प्पासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Wild cotton, or a plant resembling it, (Hibiscus vitifolius.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and कार्प्पासी cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकुक्कुट|वनकुक्कुटः
वनकुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>Wild fowl.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगज
वनगज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A wild elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगहन
वनगहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A thicket.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and गहन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगुप्त|वनगुप्तः
वनगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A spy, an emissary.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगो
वनगो<BR>f. (-गौः)<BR>The Gāyal, (Bos gavæus.)<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, and गो a cow; also वनगव m. (-वः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगोचर|वनगोचरः
वनगोचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Frequenting forests.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hunter, a forester.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A forest.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and गोचर an object, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचन्दन|वनचंदन|वनचन्दनं
वनचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>2 A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचारिन्
वनचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Forest, forester, savage.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनछाग|वनच्छाग|वनच्छागः
वनछाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A wild goat.<BR>2 A hog.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and छाग a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनछिद्|वनच्छिद्
वनछिद्<BR>m. (-ट्)<BR>A wood-cutter.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and छिट् who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनच्छेद
वनच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Cutting timber.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and छेद who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनज|वनजं|वनजः
वनज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Wild, forest, born or produced in a wood.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनजीविन्
वनजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A wood-man, a forester.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and जीविन who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनतिक्त|वनतिक्तः
वनतिक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A sort of myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknadhi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनतिक्तिका
वनतिक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A climbing plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् in the fem. form added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनद|वनदः
वनद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वन water, and द what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनदीप|वनदीपः
वनदीप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Champak, (Michelia Champaca.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and दीप a lamp or illuminator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपल्लव|वनपल्लवः
वनपल्लव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपांशुल|वनपांशुलः
वनपांशुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and पांशुल a low man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपादप
वनपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A forest tree.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रवेश|वनप्रवेशः
वनप्रवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Entering a forest, commencing to live as a hermit.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and प्रवेश entry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रिय|वनप्रियं|वनप्रियः
वनप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Kökila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनभुज्
वनभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Ṛṣabha.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमल्ली
वनमल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>Wild jasmine.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, मल्ली Jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=732" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमाक्षिका
वनमाक्षिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A gad fly.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and माक्षिका fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमाला
वनमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The chaplet or garland worn by KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and माला necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमालिन्
वनमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Dvāraka the capital of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A female energy of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वनमाला as above, इनि and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमुच्
वनमुच्<BR>m. (-मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वन water, and मुच् to let loose, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमुद्ग|वनमुद्गः
वनमुद्ग<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and मुद्ग kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमूत|वनमूतः
वनमूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वन water, and मूत sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनर|वनरः
वनर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, रम to play, aff. ड; also वानर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनराज|वनराजः
वनराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and राजन् a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनराजि|वनराजिः
वनराजि<BR>mfn. (-जिः-जिः-जी-जि)<BR>Embellishing or beautifying a forest.<BR>E.<BR>वन, राजृ to shine, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवर्त्तिन्|वनवर्तिन्
वनवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिणी-र्त्ति)<BR>Residing in the woods.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवह्नि|वनवह्निः
वनवह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>A wood on fire.<BR>E.<BR>वन a forest, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवास|वनवासः
वनवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Living in the woods, as a hermit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासन|वनवासनः
वनवासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A civet or pole cat.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, वस to dwell, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासिन्
वनवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Wild, forest, who or what dwells in woods.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 An anchoret, a hermit.<BR>2 A forester.<BR>E.<BR>वन forest, वास abode, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनविडाल
वनविडाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of wild cat, (Felis caracal.)<BR>E.<BR>वन, and विडाल a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनव्रीहि|वनव्रीहिः
वनव्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>Rice growing wild in pools or swamps, and considered by botanists, as the parent stock of all the varieties cultivated in India.<BR>E.<BR>वन wood or water, and व्रीहि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनशृङ्गाट|वनशृङ्गाटः
वनशृङ्गाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, (Ruellia longifolia): see गोक्षुर.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and शृङ्गाट the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनशोभन|वनशोभनं
वनशोभन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>वन water, and शोभन adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनश्वन्
वनश्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा)<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>3 A civet or pole cat.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and श्वन् a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसङ्कट|वनसंकट|वनसङ्कटः
वनसङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Ervum hirsutum.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and सङ्कट what contracts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसमूह|वनसमूहः
वनसमूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A multitude of groves or forests.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and समूह a collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसरोजिनी
वनसरोजिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>वन wild, and सरोजिनी Hibiscus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थ|वनस्थः
वनस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Wild, savage, forest or grove-abiding, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 A deer.<BR>2 A hermit, an ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>वन (in) a wood, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थायिन्
वनस्थायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Being or abiding in a wood.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A hermit, an anchoret.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and स्थायिन् who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थित
वनस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Situate or being in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and स्थित् what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पति|वनस्पतिः
वनस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A tree that bears fruit but no apparent blossoms, as several species of the fig, the jack, &c.<BR>2 A tree in general.<BR>3 An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>वन forest, and पति lord, सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनहास|वनहासः
वनहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A sort of tall grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, and हास a smile, from हस to laugh, with घञ् aff.; also with कन् added, वनहासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाकम्प
वनाकम्प<BR>m. (-म्पः)<BR>Shaking of the trees of a wood by the wind.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and आकम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाखु|वनाखुः
वनाखु<BR>m. (-खुः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and आखु a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाखुक|वनाखुकः
वनाखुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus Moong.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाज|वनाजः
वनाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and अज a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाटु|वनाटुः
वनाटु<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A blue fly.<BR>E.<BR>वन a thicket, अट to go, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनान्त|वनांत|वनान्तः
वनान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The skirts of a wood.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाभिलाव
वनाभिलाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Wood-destroying.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and अभिलाव destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनामल|वनामलः
वनामल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fruit, (Carissa carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, and आमल for आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायु|वनायुः
वनायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A country distinguished for its breed of horses; also वानायु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायुज|वनायुजः
वनायुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A horse of the Vanāyu breed.<BR>E.<BR>वनायु a country, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनार्च्चक|वनार्चक|वनार्चकः|वनार्च्चकः
वनार्च्चक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flower-gatherer.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, अर्च्च to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनालिका
वनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, अल to adorn, aff. वुन्, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाश्रय|वनाश्रयः
वनाश्रय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Forest, forester, who or what is in a forest.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A raven, or perhaps more properly a sort of crow.<BR>2 Dwelling in a forest.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाश्रित
वनाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Leading the life of a hermit, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and आश्रित repaired to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाहिर|वनाहिरः
वनाहिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनि|वनिः
वनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>वन to worship, Uṇādi aff. इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिका
वनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woody place, a grove.<BR>E.<BR>वनी, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनित|वनितः
वनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Solicited, begged.<BR>2 Served.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman in general.<BR>2 A beloved woman, a wife, a mistress.<BR>E.<BR>वन to ask, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्ठु|वनिष्ठुः
वनिष्ठु<BR>m. (-ष्ठुः)<BR>The entrails of an animal offered in sacrifice.^1<BR>E.<BR>वन to worship, इष्ठुच् Uṇādi aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीक|वनीकः
वनीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A beggar; also वनीयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयक|वनीयकः
वनीयक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A beggar, a mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>वन to ask, इन् aff.; क्यच् and वुन् added; also य being changed to प, वनीपक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेक्षुद्रा
वनेक्षुद्रा<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A tree, commonly Karanja.<BR>E.<BR>वने in a wood, क्षुद्रा small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचर|वनेचरः
वनेचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Who or what inhabits a wood, forest, forester.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A forester, one of a savage tribe inhabiting woods, a sylvan, a satyr.<BR>2 An imp, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>वने in a forest, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचराग्र्य
वनेचराग्र्य<BR>m. (-ग्र्यः)<BR>An ascetic, an anchorite, a sage.<BR>E.<BR>वनेचर, and अग्र्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेशय
वनेशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Living in the woods.<BR>E.<BR>वने, शी to sleep, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनैकदेश
वनैकदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A part of a thicket.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and एकदेश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोत्साह|वनोत्साहः
वनोत्साह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A rhinoceros.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोद्देश
वनोद्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A part of a thicket.<BR>E.<BR>वन, and उद्देश direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोद्भव
वनोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced in a forest.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Wild cotton.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=733" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनौकस्
वनौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>1 A forester.<BR>2 A monkey, an ape.<BR>E.<BR>वन wood, and ओकस् dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दका
वन्दका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दा the same, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दथ|वंदथ|वंदथः|वन्दथः
वन्दथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A panegyrist, a eulogist, a bard.<BR>2 One deserving praise or eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>वन्द to praise, Uṇādi aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दन|वंदन|वंदनं|वन्दनं
वन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The face or mouth.<BR>2 Obeisance to a Brahman or superior by touching the feet, &c.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 Reverence, worship, adoring.<BR>2 Begging, soliciting, asking.<BR>3 The hip (?)<BR>4 A drug for reviving the dead.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Praise, praising, especially the gods or great men.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, aff. ल्युट् or युच्, fem. aff. ङीष् or टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमाला|वंदनमाला
वन्दनमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The ornamented arch of a gate-way.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दन praising, and माला a garland; being hung with flowers on marriages and festival occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमालिका|वंदनमालिका
वन्दनमालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The ornamented arch of a gate-way.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दन praising, माला a garland, कन् aff. in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनीय|वंदनीय|वन्दनीयः
वन्दनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Praise-worthy, to be eulogised or praised.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A yellow substance used as a pigment, said in the Tantras to be procured from the head of a cow: see रोचना.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दा|वंदा
वन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>1 A parasite plant, (Epidendrum tessellatum, &c.)<BR>2 Any parasite plant.<BR>3 A female beggar.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दाका
वन्दाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दा, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दार|वन्दारः
वन्दार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दा the same, ऋ to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारु|वंदारु|वन्दारुः
वन्दारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>1 Civil, complimentary, polite.<BR>2 Praising, celebrating.<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A panegyrist, a bard.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, आरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दि|वन्दिः
वन्दि<BR>f. (-न्दिः-न्दी)<BR>1 A captive, a prisoner, a man or beast confined.<BR>2 A ladder or stairs.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, aff. इन्, and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिग्राह|वन्दिग्राहः
वन्दिग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A house-breaker, especially one who breaks into the place in which the sacred fire is preserved, into an armoury, or a temple.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दि captive, (what is confined or shut up,) and ग्राह who seizes; also वन्दिचौर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिचौर|वन्दिचौरः
वन्दिचौर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief, a house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दि, and चौर thief; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन्<BR>m. (-न्दी)<BR>1 A panegyrist, a bard, a herald, a servant whose duty it is to proclaim the titles of a great man as he passes along, or a poet, who sings the praises of a prince in his presence, or accompanies an army, to chaunt martial songs: considered as one of a distinct tribe, he is the son of a Kṣatriya by a Śūdra female.<BR>2 A praiser, a flatterer.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिपाठ|वन्दिपाठः
वन्दिपाठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A complimentary stanza, a panegyric, a eulogium, often improvisatore, recited by a bard, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वन्दि a bard, and पाठ reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दीकार|वन्दीकारः
वन्दीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thief, a house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्य|वंद्य
वन्द्य<BR>mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्यं)<BR>To be praised, commendable, laudable.<BR>f. (-न्द्या)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, यत् aff., or यक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्र|वंद्र|वन्द्रं|वंद्रः|वन्द्रः
वन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>A worshipper, a votary, a follower.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, aff. रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्य|वन्यं|वन्यः
वन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Forest, savage, wild, produced in a wood, &c.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>1 A multitude of groves.<BR>2 A quantity of water, a flood, a deluge.<BR>3 A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, &c., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्र|वन्रः
वन्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A copartner, a coheir, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वत to ask, and रन Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप|वपः
वप<BR>(डु) डुवप r. 1st cl. (वपति)<BR>1 To sow seed.<BR>2 To procreate.<BR>3 To shave.<BR>4 To weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप|वपः
वप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Shaving.<BR>2 Sowing seed.<BR>3 Weaving.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>1 The mucous or glutinous secretion of the flesh or bones; according to some, also the marrow of the bones.<BR>2 Any hole or cavity.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow seed, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपन|वपनं
वपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sowing seed.<BR>2 Shaving.<BR>3 Semen virile.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A barber's shop.<BR>E.<BR>वप to shave, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपाकृत्
वपाकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>Marrow.<BR>E.<BR>वपा, and कृत what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपिल|वपिलः
वपिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A father.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow seed, (figuratively,) and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुन|वपुनः
वपुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A deity.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, उवन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्टमा
वपुष्टमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्मात्
वपुष्मात्<BR>mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्)<BR>Having a body, corporeal^1, incarnate.<BR>E.<BR>वपुस्, and मतुप् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्
वपुस्<BR>n. (-पुः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 A handsome form or figure.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, Uṇādi aff. उसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तव्य
वप्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be sown.<BR>2 To be given, conferred, implanted, &c.<BR>3 To be immitted seminally, to be impregnated or begotten.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, तव्य aff.; also वपनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तृ
वप्तृ<BR>mfn. (-प्ता-प्ती-प्तृ)<BR>A sower, a planter, &c.<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>1 A father, a progenitor.<BR>2 A poet, a sage.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्र|वप्रं|वप्रः
वप्र<BR>mn. (-प्रः-प्रं)<BR>1 A field.<BR>2 A rampart, a mud wall, earth taken from the ditch of a town and raised as a wall or buttress, or as the foundation of a wall of masonry, &c.<BR>3 The foundation of any building.<BR>4 The gate of a fortified city.<BR>5 A shore or bank.<BR>6 Dust, earth.<BR>7 A mound, a hillock.<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>A father.<BR>n. (-प्रं)<BR>Lead.<BR>f. (-प्री)<BR>A hillock, an ant-hill.<BR>E.<BR>वरु to sow, रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक्रीडा
वप्रक्रीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Butting, as of an elephant or bull, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वप्र a mound, and कीडा sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रानत
वप्रानत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bowed or stooping to butt at a wall or bank.<BR>E.<BR>वप्र, and आनत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रान्तर
वप्रान्तर<BR>ind.<BR>In or between banks, mounds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वप्र, and आन्तर् within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राभिघात|वप्राभिघातः
वप्राभिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Butting at a bank or mound.<BR>E.<BR>वप्र, and अभिघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राम्भस्
वप्राम्भस्<BR>n. (-म्भः)<BR>The water near or along the bank.<BR>E.<BR>वप्र, and अम्भस water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रि|वप्रिः
वप्रि<BR>m. (-प्रिः)<BR>A field.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, Uṇādi aff. क्रिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वभ्र
वभ्र<BR>r. 1st cl. (-वभ्रति)<BR>To go; also वभ्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम<BR>(टु उ) टुवमु r. 1st cl. (वमति)<BR>To vomit, to eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम<BR>mf. (-मः-मी)<BR>Vomiting.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, aff. अच्; also वमन and वमि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथु|वमथुः
वमथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>1 Vomiting, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>2 Water ejected from an elephant's trunk.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, aff. अथुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=734" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमन|वमनं|वमनः
वमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Vomiting, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>2 Causing vomiting, an emetic.<BR>3 Pain.<BR>4 Offering oblations to fire.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमि|वमिः
वमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>1 Vomiting, sickness.<BR>2 An emetic.<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>1 A name of fire.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित|वमितः
वमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sickened, made to vomit.<BR>E.<BR>वम to be sick, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित्वा
वमित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having vomited or been sick.<BR>E.<BR>वम to be sick, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिन्
वमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Vomiting, sick.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्री
वम्री<BR>f. (-म्री)<BR>A small ant burrowing in trees; also वम्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्रीकूट|वम्रीकूटः
वम्रीकूट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>An ant-hill, a hillock.<BR>E.<BR>वम्री a sort of ant, कूट a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय|वयं|वयः
वय<BR>r. 1st cl. (वयते)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थ|वयःस्थः
वयःस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Middle-aged, young, &c.: see वयस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्
वयस्<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 Age, time of life.<BR>3 Youth.<BR>E.<BR>वय to go, असुन् aff., or वी as substituted for अज to go, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्क
वयस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Relating to age, aged.<BR>E.<BR>वयस्, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्थ|वयस्थः
वयस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Young, in the prime of life.<BR>2 Mature, middle-aged, past childhood, or from sixteen to seventy.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A friend, an associate, a cotemporary.<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 The moon plant, (Asclepias acida)<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>3 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>4 Small cardamoms.<BR>5 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>6 A medicinal root, commonly Kākolī.<BR>7 A woman's female friend or companion, a confidante.<BR>8 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>वयस् life, स्था to be or stay, aff. क, fem. aff. टाप्, the final of the former changed to Visarga, and that optionally rejected; hence, also वयःस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्य|वयस्यः
वयस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Aged, relating to age.<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A friend, a cotemporary, an associate or companion.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>A woman's female friend or confidante.<BR>E.<BR>वयस् life, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुन|वयुनं|वयुनः
वयुन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A temple.<BR>E.<BR>वी substituted for अज to go, and उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोगत
वयोगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Aged, very old.<BR>E.<BR>वयस्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधस्
वयोधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>A young or middle-aged man.<BR>E.<BR>वयस् youth or manhood, धा to have, Uṇādi aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधिक
वयोधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Very old.<BR>E.<BR>वयस्, and अधिक exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर<BR>r. 10th cl. (वरयति)<BR>To desire, to obtain, to covet or ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Best, excellent.<BR>2 Eldest.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A boon, a blessing, especially in the gift of a Brahman or deity.<BR>2 Engaging, selecting, appointing.<BR>3 Requesting, soliciting, especially prevailing on a person by intreaty to undertake any business.<BR>4 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>5 A husband, a bridegroom.<BR>6 A son-in-law.<BR>7 A catamite.<BR>8 A drug: see गुग्गुल.<BR>9 Wish, desire.<BR>10 A sparrow.<BR>n. adv. (वरं) or ind. (वरम)<BR>Better, preferable.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The three myrobalans.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇuka.<BR>3 A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Asparagus racemosus.<BR>2 A name of CHĀYĀ, wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to select, to cover, &c., aff. अप् or अच्; it is also derived from वृ, and is then written with an initial consonant: see वर; also वर to desire, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक|वरकं|वरकः
वरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The cover or awning of a boat.<BR>2 A wild kidneybean.<BR>3 A towel, a wiper.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक्रतु|वरक्रतुः
वरक्रतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, क्रतु sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरचन्दन|वरचंदन|वरचन्दनं
वरचन्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A dark sort of Sandal or Agallochum.<BR>2 A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरट|वरटं|वरटः
वरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A gander.<BR>2 A man of a barbarous or foreign race.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>Many-flowered jasmine.<BR>f. (-टः-टी)<BR>1 A goose.<BR>2 A wasp, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, aff. अटन्; fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण|वरणं|वरणः
वरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Appointing, selecting, choosing.<BR>2 Surrounding, inclosing.<BR>3 Screening, covering.<BR>4 Nourishing, supporting.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An outer building, an enclosure, a wall of masonry, &c. raised on a mound of earth.<BR>2 A causeway, a bridge.<BR>3 A camel.<BR>4 A tree, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>5 Any tree.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A rivulet, running past the north of Benares, into the Ganges, now called the Berṇā.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose or appoint, aff. चयु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणसी
वरणसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The city Benares, more usually वाराणसी.<BR>E.<BR>वरणा a rivulet as above, and असि another running on the south of the city, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणीय
वरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be applied to or solicited for a boon, &c.<BR>2 To be selected.<BR>E.<BR>वर to ask as a boon, or वृ to choose, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्ड|वरंड|वरंडः|वरण्डः
वरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A portico.<BR>2 Pimples on the face.<BR>3 A multitude.<BR>4 A heap of grass.<BR>5 The string of a fish-hook.<BR>6 A packet, a package.<BR>n. (-ण्डा)<BR>A small bird, (Turdus.)<BR>E.<BR>वृञ् to cover, &c., Uṇādi aff. अण्डन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डक|वरंडक|वरण्डकः
वरण्डक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Fearful, terrified.<BR>2 Large, great.<BR>3 Miserly, a miser.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A howdah, a chair or canopy on the back of an elephant.<BR>2 A wall.<BR>3 Eruption or pimples on the face.<BR>4 A ball, a globe.<BR>E.<BR>वरण्ड as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डालु|वरंडालुः|वरण्डालुः
वरण्डालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>The castor oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरतनु|वरतनुः
वरतनु<BR>f. (-नुः)<BR>An elegant woman.<BR>E.<BR>वर, and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्करी
वरत्करी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रा
वरत्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>1 An elephant's or horse's leather girth.<BR>2 A thong, a strip of leather.<BR>E.<BR>वृञ् to cover or surround, Uṇādi aff. अत्रन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्वच|वरत्वचः
वरत्वच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>The Nimb tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, and त्वच् skin, the final vowel added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरद|वरदः
वरद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Granting a prayer, conferring a boon.<BR>2 Propitious, favourable.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A benefactor.<BR>2 Fire for burnt-offerings of a propitiatory character.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A girl, a virgin.<BR>E.<BR>वर a blessing, &c., and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदान
वरदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Granting a boon.<BR>2 A place of pilgrimage.<BR>E.<BR>वर a blessing, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरपर्णाख्य|वरपर्णाख्यः
वरपर्णाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रद
वरप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Conferring a boon.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>वर a boon, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रदान
वरप्रदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Conferring a boon.<BR>E.<BR>वर, and प्रदान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरफल|वरफलः
वरफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoa-nut tree.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरमुखी
वरमुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>Reṇukā, a sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्
वरम्<BR>ind.<BR>Better, sooner, rather, preferable: see वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्बरा
वरम्बरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The nux vomica plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=735" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितृ
वरयितृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A husband.<BR>E.<BR>वर to choose, in the causal form, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वररुचि|वररुचिः
वररुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A poet and philosopher, one of the ornaments of the court of Bhoja, or one of the nine gems usually ascribed to VIKRAMĀDITYA'S court.<BR>E.<BR>वर pre-eminent, better, रुचि light or renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरल|वरलः
वरल<BR>mf. (-लः-ला or -ली)<BR>A wasp.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>वर, and ला to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलब्ध|वरलब्धः
वरलब्ध<BR>m. (-ब्धः)<BR>A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवत्सला
वरवत्सला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The wife of a father-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>वर a bridegroom, and वत्सल affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवर्णिनी
वरवर्णिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 An excellent woman.<BR>2 A virtuous woman.<BR>3 A woman in general.<BR>4 Turmeric.<BR>5 Lāc.<BR>6 A brownish yellow pigment; also रोचना and गोरोहना.<BR>7 A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>8 A name of GAURĪ.<BR>9 SARASVATĪ.<BR>10 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, बर्ण class or colour, aff. इनि and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवारण
वरवारण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A fine elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वर, and वारण an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवाह्लीक|वरवाह्लीकं
वरवाह्लीक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>वर, and वाह्लीक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवृद्ध|वरवृद्धः
वरवृद्ध<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वर better, and वृद्ध old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराक|वराकः
वराक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Low, vile, impure.<BR>2 Poor, pitiable.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 War.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, &c., षाकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्ग|वरांग|वराङ्गं|वराङ्गः
वराङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 A privity, a private part, male or female.<BR>3 Cassia bark.<BR>4 An elegant form or body.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, excellent, अङ्ग body or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गक|वराङ्गकं
वराङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Woody Cassia.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गना|वरांगना
वराङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A lovely woman.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गरूपोपेत|वराङ्गरूपोपेतः
वराङ्गरूपोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Handsome and well-shaped.<BR>E.<BR>वराङ्ग excellent body, रूप form, and उपेत invested, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराट|वराटः
वराट<BR>n. (-टः)<BR>1 A cord, a rope.<BR>2 A Cowri: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटक|वराटकः
वराटक<BR>mfn. subst. (-टकः-टिका-टकं)<BR>1 A rope, a cord, a string.<BR>2 The small shell, called a Cowri, and used as a coin.<BR>3 The seed-vessel of the lotus.<BR>m. (-टिका)<BR>The Nagesara plant.<BR>E.<BR>वृञ् to surround, aff. अटच्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटकरजस्
वराटकरजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A plant, commonly Nagesara, (Mesua ferrea).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराण|वराणः
वराण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, and णी to obtain, with आङ् prefix, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराणसी
वराणसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Benares.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अनस् water, ङीप् aff., i. e. the Ganges, on whose bank the city is situated; also वाराणसी and वरणसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरादन|वरादनं
वरादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A sort of Mimusops, (M. Kauki, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराम्र|वराम्रः
वराम्र<BR>m. (-म्रः)<BR>An acid fruit, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अम्र acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारक|वरारकं
वरारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The diamond.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, ऋ to go or be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारोह|वरारोहः
वरारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 An elephant-driver.<BR>2 Mounting, riding.<BR>3 A rider on an elephant or horse.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 A handsome or elegant woman.<BR>2 The hip or flank.<BR>E.<BR>वर excellent, आरोह mounting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालक|वरालकः
वरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Caronda fruit, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अल to be equal to, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालि|वरालिः
वरालि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 A division of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालिका
वरालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, supreme, आलि a female friend, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराशि|वराशिः
वराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>Coarse cloth.<BR>E.<BR>वर covering, अश to pervade, aff. इन्; also वरासि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासन|वरासनं|वरासनः
वरासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A cistern, a reservoir.<BR>2 The China rose.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A whoremonger.<BR>2 A door-keeper.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, &c., आसन seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासि|वरासिः
वरासि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>1 Coarse cloth.<BR>2 A swordsman.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Dirty clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वर covering, अस to be, aff. इन् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराह|वराहः
वराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A hog.<BR>2 A name of VIṢṆU in the third Avatāra or descent, in which he assumed the shape of a boar.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>5 A sort of measure.<BR>6 One of the eighteen smaller Dvīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, हन to injure, with आङ् prefix, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकान्ता
वराहकान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A sort of yam.<BR>E.<BR>वराह a hog, and कान्ता beloved; also वराही.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकालिन्
वराहकालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A flower, (Helianthus annuns.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहक्रान्ता
वराहक्रान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A plant, a sort of sensitive plant according to some authorities, but to others, a kind of moss, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.); it is also considered sometimes, but erroneously, as synonymous with वराही Dioscorea.<BR>E.<BR>वराह a hog, and क्रान्त passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहनामन्
वराहनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>An esculent root: see वाराही.<BR>E.<BR>वराह a hog, and नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवसित|वरिवसितः
वरिवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Served, honoured, adored, as a deity or spiritual teacher.<BR>E.<BR>वरिवस्या service, इतच् aff., and य optionally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्या
वरिवस्या<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Service, honour, especially such devoted obedience as a pupil pays his spiritual preceptor.<BR>E.<BR>वरिवस indeclinable, here said to imply veneration, and क्याच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यित|वरिवस्यितः
वरिवस्यित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Served, adored.<BR>E.<BR>वरिवस्या as above, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिशी
वरिशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A fish-hook.<BR>E.<BR>see वडिशी, ड, and र being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष|वरिषं
वरिष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A year.<BR>m. plu. (-षाः)<BR>The rains or rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. इषन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिषाप्रिय|वरिषाप्रियः
वरिषाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>वरिषा the rainy season, and प्रिय fond of; being supposed to drink rain water only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Largest, greatest, most large.<BR>2 Heaviest, mightiest.<BR>3 Best, dearest, most preferable or beloved.<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 Pepper.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>The Francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>वर् substituted for उरु large, or वरु best, and इष्ठन्. affix of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीयस्
वरीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>1 Very large, largest, most large.<BR>2 Best, most preferable or excellent.<BR>3 Extremely young, tender, infantine.<BR>m. (-यान्)<BR>The eighteenth of the astronomical periods called Yogas.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, or substituted for उरु, and इयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=736" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवर्द्द|वरीवर्द|वरीवर्दः|वरीवर्द्दः
वरीवर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>An ox or bull.<BR>E.<BR>see वलीवर्द्द, ब and ल being changed to व and र; also वलीवर्द्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीषु|वरीषुः
वरीषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, ईषुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण|वरुणः
वरुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 VARUṆA, the deity of the waters and regent of the west.<BR>2 Water or the ocean.<BR>3 A tree, (Tapia cratoeva, or Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>4 A name of the sun, or rather of one of the twelve forms of that luminary, or Ādityas.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to enclose (the earth), or वृ to select or prefer, being chosen by the gods for his office, and उनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणात्मजा
वरुणात्मजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>E.<BR>वरुण VARUṆA or the ocean personified, and आत्मजा daughter; being amongst the precious things produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणानी
वरुणानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The wife of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वरुण, with ङीप् aff. and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्र|वरुत्रं
वरुत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>An upper and outer garment.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, उत्र Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ|वरूथं|वरूथः
वरूथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A sort of wooden fender or ledge round a carriage, as a defence from the effects of collision.<BR>n. (-थं)<BR>1 Armour, mail.<BR>2 Leather, skin.<BR>3 A house or dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to surround, Uṇādi aff. ऊथन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिन्
वरूथिन्<BR>m. (-थी)<BR>1 A guard, a defender.<BR>2 A car.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An army.<BR>E.<BR>वरूथ part of a car, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण
वरेण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>Chief, principal, pre-eminent.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to select, Uṇādi aff. एण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेन्द्र|वरेन्द्रः
वरेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 A chief, a sovereign.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>Ancient Gaur, the capital and district so named.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, इन्द्र chief, and with ङीप् aff.; the favorite country of the deity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेश्वर|वरेश्वरः
वरेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, principal, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोट|वरोटं|वरोटः
वरोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, commonly Marüa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोल|वरोलः
वरोल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, ओलच् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्; the fem. form may also mean, a smaller kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कर|वर्करः
वर्कर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>Any young animal.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A lamb.<BR>2 A goat.<BR>3 Pleasure, pastime, sport, mirth, festivity.<BR>E.<BR>वृक to take, aff. अरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कराट|वर्कराटः
वर्कराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A side glance, a wink, a leer.<BR>2 The rays of the meridian sun.<BR>mn. (-टः-टं)<BR>The marks of a lover's finger nails on the bosom of a woman.<BR>E.<BR>वर्कर a young animal, अट to be or resemble, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कुट|वर्कुटः
वर्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A pin, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग|वर्गः|वर्ग्ग
वर्ग<BR>n. (-र्गः)<BR>A class, a tribe, a multitude of similar things, whether animate or inanimate; as Ka-verga, the class of guttural letters; Tri-verga, a class of three (objects, as love, duty, and wealth); the Śūdra-varga, the Śūdra tribe.<BR>2 A chapter, a book, a section.<BR>3 A square number, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, to except (any thing else), aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गघन|वर्गघनः
वर्गघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The square of a cube.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ग, and घन a cube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गमूल|वर्गमूलं
वर्गमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A square root.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ग, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीय|वर्गीयः
वर्गीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Belonging to a class, a tribe, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ग, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्घ
वर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्घति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्च|वर्च|वर्च्चः
वर्च्च<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्च्चते)<BR>To shine.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्च्चयति)<BR>1 To cut.<BR>2 To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चटी|वर्चटी
वर्च्चटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 A kind of rice.<BR>2 A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्|वर्चस्
वर्च्चस्<BR>n. (-र्च्चः)<BR>1 Form, figure, shape.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 Ordure, fæces.<BR>m. (-र्च्चाः)<BR>The son of CANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वर्च्च to shine, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्क|वर्चस्क|वर्चस्कः|वर्च्चस्कः
वर्च्चस्क<BR>mn. (-स्कः-स्कं)<BR>Fæces, excrement.<BR>E.<BR>वर्च to shine, असुन् aff., and कन् depreciative aff. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्विन्|वर्चस्विन्
वर्च्चस्विन्<BR>mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>Bright, glorious.<BR>E.<BR>वर्च्चस, and विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्ज|वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्जः
वर्ज्ज<BR>mfn. (-र्ज्जः-र्ज्जा-र्ज्जं)<BR>1 Free from, devoid of.<BR>2 Excepted.<BR>m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>1 Leaving, abandoning.<BR>2 Excepting.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to abandon, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जक|वर्जक
वर्ज्जक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what leaves, shuns, excepts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जन|वर्जन|वर्जनं|वर्ज्जनं
वर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Quitting, abandonment, shunning, avoiding.<BR>2 Injury, hurting.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to abandon, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जयित्वा|वर्जयित्वा
वर्ज्जयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having shunned or avoided.<BR>2 Having omitted, excepting, leaving out.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, aff. क्त्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जित|वर्जित|वर्ज्जितः
वर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abandoned, avoided.<BR>2 Given.<BR>3 Excluded, excepted.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जनीय|वर्जनीय|वर्ज्जनीयं
वर्ज्जनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Improper, censurable, wicked, proper to be avoided.<BR>2 Irregular, to be excepted.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, and अनीयर् aff. of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्ज्य
वर्ज्ज्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ज्ज्यः-र्ज्ज्या-र्ज्ज्यं)<BR>1 To be shunned.<BR>2 To be excepted, excluded, left out.<BR>n. (-र्ज्ज्यं)<BR>A point in each lunar mansion during the passage of the moon, in which no business should be begun.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्णः|वर्ण्ण
वर्ण<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्णयति)<BR>1 To colour, to paint, to dye.<BR>2 To send or cast, to direct, to order.<BR>3 To praise, to extol, to proclaim qualities.<BR>4 To describe.<BR>5 To spread or extend.<BR>6 To grind or pound.<BR>7 To make exertions.<BR>8 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्णः|वर्ण्ण
वर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>1 A tribe, a class, a caste, an order.<BR>2 Colour, hue, tint.<BR>3 Coloured cloth thrown over the back of an elephant, an elephant's housings.<BR>4 Quality, property.<BR>5 Fame, celebrity.<BR>6 Praise.<BR>7 Gold.<BR>8 Religious observance.<BR>9 The order or arrangement of a song or poem.<BR>10 A musical mode.<BR>11 Staining the body with coloured unguents.<BR>12 Beauty, lustre.<BR>13 Theatrical dress or embellishment.<BR>mn. (-र्णः-र्णं)<BR>1 Perfume for the person.<BR>2 A letter of the alphabet.<BR>3 Form, figure.<BR>4 Sort, kind.<BR>5 Touch, the purity of gold, as ascertained by its streak on the touch-stone.<BR>6 In arithmetic, a co-efficient.<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>Saffron.<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A leguminous shrub, (Cytisus cajan.)<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to paint, &c., aff. अच् or घञ्, or वृ to cover or screen, Uṇādi aff. नक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक|वर्णकं|वर्णकः|वर्ण्णक
वर्णक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 Perfume for the person, especially pounded or ground.<BR>2 Sandal.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A paint, a pigment, as indigo, orpiment, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A panegyrist, a bard, a poetical encomiast, by tribe and profession.<BR>2 A circle, an orb.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Touch, standard, fineness or purity of gold.<BR>E.<BR>वण to colour, &c., ण्वुल् aff., or वर्ण as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णकवि|वर्णकविः
वर्णकवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>The son of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण praise, and कवि a bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णकूपिका|वर्ण्णकूपिका
वर्णकूपिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An ink-stand.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, and कूप a well, कन् aff. of comparison, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक्रम|वर्णक्रमः
वर्णक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Order of caste or tribe.<BR>2 Alphabetical arrangement, the alphabet.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and क्रम course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=737" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णगत
वर्णगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Coloured.<BR>2 Described.<BR>3 Algebraic.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णचारक|वर्णचारकः|वर्ण्णचारक
वर्णचारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A painter.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, चर to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णज्येष्ठ|वर्णज्येष्ठः|वर्ण्णज्येष्ठ
वर्णज्येष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण caste, ज्येष्ठ elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णतस्
वर्णतस्<BR>ind.<BR>By or with colour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णतूलि|वर्णतूलिः|वर्ण्णतूलि
वर्णतूलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, and तूलि a brush; also with कन् added, वर्णतूलिका f. (-का.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णद|वर्णदं|वर्ण्णद
वर्णद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Dying, colouring.<BR>2 Giving tribe, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदातृ
वर्णदातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and दातृ what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदूत|वर्णदूतः|वर्ण्णदूत
वर्णदूत<BR>m. (-त)<BR>A letter, an epistle.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter of the alphabet, &c., and टूत sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदूषक
वर्णदूषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Disturbing or violating the distinctions of caste.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and टूषक what violates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णधर्म्म|वर्णधर्म|वर्णधर्मः|वर्णधर्म्मः
वर्णधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The particular occupation or duty of each caste or tribe.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a tribe, धर्म्म virtue, moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णन|वर्णनं
वर्णन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Describing, expatiating, explaining, pointing out qualities or excellencies, &c.<BR>2 Colouring, painting, writing.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Praise, panegyric.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to colour, युच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णनीय
वर्णनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be described, delineated, praised, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to colour, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णपत्र
वर्णपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A pallet, a leaf, &c. on which a painter mixes his colours.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a colour, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमातृ
वर्णमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमातृका
वर्णमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>SARASVATĪ, the goddess of speech and eloquence.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, and मातृका divine parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमाला
वर्णमाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The alphabet.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णरेखा
वर्णरेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A white aluminous fossil often confounded with chalk, of which it is considered a species.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णलेखा
वर्णलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णवत्|वर्णवन्त्
वर्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having tribe, colour, &c.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णविलोडक|वर्णविलोडकः
वर्णविलोडक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plagiarist.<BR>2 A house-breaker.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण praise, and वि before लोड to be mad, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णवृत्त
वर्णवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Metre regulated by the number of syllables.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and वृत्त metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णश्रेष्ठ|वर्णश्रेष्ठः
वर्णश्रेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Of a good tribe, caste, kind, &c.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसंहार|वर्णसंहारः
वर्णसंहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An assemblage or mixture of the four tribes.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and संहार assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्कर|वर्णसंकर|वर्णसंकरः|वर्णसङ्करः
वर्णसङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Mixture or confusion of castes.<BR>2 A man or tribe of mixed origin, or from a father and mother of different castes.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and सङ्कर mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्घाट|वर्णसंघाट
वर्णसङ्घाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An alphabet or assemblage of letters.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, हन to kill, with सम् prefixed, and घञ् aff., and घट substituted for the radical letters; also with घत वर्णसङ्घात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्घात|वर्णसंघात|वर्णसंघातः
वर्णसङ्घात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The alphabet: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसि|वर्णसिः
वर्णसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to surround, असि Uṇādi aff., and नुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णहीन
वर्णहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाङ्का|वर्णांका
वर्णाङ्का<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, अकि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाट|वर्णाटः
वर्णाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A singer.<BR>2 A painter.<BR>3 An actor, a mime.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, &c., अट to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णात्मन्
वर्णात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>A word.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, and आत्मन् the soul or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णापसद|वर्णापसदः
वर्णापसद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>An outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and अपसद who is or goes out from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णापेत
वर्णापेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Degraded, outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and अपेत devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाश्रम
वर्णाश्रम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>The class and state of a person.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and आश्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाश्रमधर्म्म|वर्णाश्रमधर्म
वर्णाश्रमधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The duties of tribe and order.<BR>E.<BR>वर्णाश्रम, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णि|वर्णिः
वर्णि<BR>n. (-र्णि)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to colour, &c., Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिक|वर्णिकः
वर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A writer, a scribe, a secretary, &c.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pen.<BR>2 Ink.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णित|वर्णितः
वर्णित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Praised, eulogised, extolled.<BR>2 Described, explained.<BR>3 Painted.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णितवत्
वर्णितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Relating, describing, was relating or related, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण to describe, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिन्
वर्णिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि)<BR>Belonging to a caste or tribe, of that caste, &c.<BR>m. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A painter.<BR>2 A scribe, a writer.<BR>3 A religious student.<BR>4 A man of either of the four regular castes.<BR>f. (-र्णिनी)<BR>1 A woman, a wife.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण colour, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिबध
वर्णिबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Killing or occasioning the death of a man of either of four castes.<BR>E.<BR>वर्णिन्, and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिलिङ्गिन्|वर्णिलिंगिन्
वर्णिलिङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>An ascetic, or one wearing the marks of a religious student.<BR>E.<BR>वर्णिन्, and लिङ्गिन् having a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णु|वर्णुः
वर्णु<BR>m. (-र्णुः)<BR>The name of a river and district.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to surround, Uṇādi aff. णु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णोपेत
वर्णोपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having caste, tribe, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तक|वर्तक|वर्तकः|वर्त्तकं|वर्त्तकः
वर्त्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who is or abides, exists, lives, &c.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>1 A sort of quail, (Perdix olivacea.)<BR>2 A horse's hoof.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of mixed or bell-metal, commonly Vidri.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तजन्मन्|वर्तजन्मन्
वर्त्तजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. घञ्, वर्त्त abiding, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तन|वर्तन|वर्तनः|वर्त्तनं|वर्त्तनः
वर्त्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fixed, stationary, stable.<BR>nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>1 Staying, abiding, being, the property of a fixed presence.<BR>2 A road, a way.<BR>3 A ball at one end of a spindle to assist its rotatory motion.<BR>4 Grinding.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>2 Occupation, profession.<BR>3 Salary, hire, wages.<BR>4 A ball of cotton from which the threads are spun.<BR>5 A ball, a globe.<BR>6 Appointing.<BR>7 Turning.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dwarf.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, to be fixed, &c, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनदान|वर्तनदान
वर्त्तनदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift of a situation, of wages or means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वर्त्तन, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनविनियोग|वर्तनविनियोग|वर्तनविनियोगः
वर्त्तनविनियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Appointment or assignment of salary, wages, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्त्तन, and विनियोग appointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनाभाव|वर्तनाभाव
वर्त्तनाभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Destitution, want of means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वर्त्तन, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनि|वर्तनि|वर्तनिः|वर्त्तनिः
वर्त्तनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The eastern country, or eastern India.<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A road.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, Uṇādi aff. अनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=738" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनीय|वर्तनीय
वर्त्तनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be lived, or dwelt in.<BR>2 What may be.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तमान|वर्तमान|वर्तमानः|वर्त्तमानः
वर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being, existing, living, being present.<BR>2 Dwelling or abiding in.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>(In grammar,) The present tense.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तमानता|वर्तमानता
वर्त्तमानता<BR>f. (ता)<BR>Being, being present, the property of time present.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last: also with त्व aff. वर्त्तमानत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तयत्|वर्तयत्
वर्त्तयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Living, subsisting.<BR>2 Dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तरूक|वर्तरूक|वर्तरूकः|वर्त्तरूकः
वर्त्तरूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A river so named.<BR>2 A puddle, a pool of water.<BR>3 A crow's nest.<BR>4 A door-keeper, a chamberlain; it is also written वर्त्तरूढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्ति|वर्ति|वर्तिः|वर्त्तिः
वर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्ती)<BR>1 Perfume for the person.<BR>2 The wick of a lamp.<BR>3 A lamp.<BR>4 A tent, a bougie.<BR>5 A collyrium prepared from various substances and dried in a lozenge form; it is exhibited ground with water or milk.<BR>6 A line, a ruled line.<BR>7 The ends of a cloth.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, Uṇādi aff. इन्, ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिका|वर्तिका
वर्त्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A quail.<BR>2 The wick of a lamp.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. aff. टाप्; also वर्त्तक and वर्त्तका, or वृत the same, तिकन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तित|वर्तित
वर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Caused or made to be or exist.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तितव्य|वर्तितव्य
वर्त्तितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be lived.<BR>2 To be dwelt, remained, or continued.<BR>3 To be practised in.<BR>4 What may be, possible, probable.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिन्|वर्तिन्
वर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>1 Abiding, fixed, stationary.<BR>2 Being.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिष्णु|वर्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णुः
वर्त्तिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Staying, abiding, being stationary or fixed.<BR>2 Facing (an enemy,) standing firm in battle.<BR>3 A circle.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तुल|वर्तुल|वर्तुलः|वर्त्तुलं|वर्त्तुलः
वर्त्तुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Round, circular, globular, spherical.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A pea.<BR>2 A ball.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A ball of clay at the end of a spindle to assist its rotation.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मन्
वर्त्मन्<BR>n. (-र्त्म)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 An eyelid.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मनि|वर्त्मनिः
वर्त्मनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A road, a way.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, अनि Uṇādi aff., and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मावबन्ध
वर्त्मावबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Rigidity of the eyelids, so that they cannot shut.<BR>E.<BR>वर्त्म, and अवबन्ध contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स्यत्|वर्त्स्यन्त्
वर्त्स्यत्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्स्यन्-र्त्स्यन्ती-र्त्स्यत्)<BR>Purposing to augment.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध to augment, शतृ aff. with the future form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध
वर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Bamanaiṭhi.<BR>2 Increase, augmentation.<BR>3 Cutting.<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>Red lead.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to grow or increase, aff. घञ्, or वर्ध to divide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धक
वर्द्धक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Increasing, causing to grow or increase.<BR>2 Dividing.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bamanaiṭhi.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to grow, or वर्द्ध to divide, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धकि
वर्द्धकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>A carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ध to cut, अच् aff., कष to injure, इ aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धकिन्
वर्द्धकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A carpenter.<BR>E.<BR>वर्धक cutting, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धन
वर्द्धन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Growing, thriving.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Increasing, growing, thriving.<BR>2 Augmenting, causing to increase.<BR>3 Cutting, dividing.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A small water jar.<BR>2 A brush, a broom.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, or वध to cut, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धमान
वर्द्धमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Prosperous, thriving.<BR>2 Increasing, growing.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The castor oil tree.<BR>2 A lid, a cover, especially a shallow earthen platter or saucer, used also as a top to water-jars, &c.<BR>3 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A sort of riddle or charade.<BR>5 The last and most celebrated of the twenty-four Jinas or Jaina teachers of the present æra.<BR>6 A mystical figure or diagram.<BR>7 A district and city, Burdwan.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्रि to increase, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धमानक
वर्द्धमानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lid, a cover.<BR>E.<BR>वर्द्धमान as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धित
वर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Grown, expanded, increased, thriven.<BR>2 Full, filled.<BR>3 Cut, divided.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, or वर्द्ध to cut, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धापन
वर्द्धापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cutting, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>वर्द्ध to cut, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धिन्
वर्द्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>Increasing, thriving.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धिष्णु
वर्द्धिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Increasing, growing, thriving.<BR>2 Enlarging, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, aff. इष्णुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध्र
वर्द्ध्र<BR>nf. (-र्द्ध्र-र्द्ध्री)<BR>A leathern thong or girth for securing^1 a saddle.<BR>n. (-र्द्ध्रं)<BR>Leather.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, Uṇādi aff. रन्; also वर्द्धी.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध|वर्द्धं|वर्द्धः|वर्धः
वर्ध<BR>r. 10 cl. (वर्धयति)<BR>1 To cut or pierce, to divide.<BR>2 To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्पस्
वर्पस्<BR>n. (-र्पः)<BR>Form, figure.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, aff. असुन, and पुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्फ
वर्फ<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्फति)<BR>1 To move, to go.<BR>2 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मकषा|वर्मकषा
वर्म्मकषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A plant; also Carmakaṣā or Carmaghās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मन्|वर्मन्
वर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्महर|वर्महर
वर्म्महर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One who takes arms or who spoils another of them.<BR>E.<BR>वर्म्म, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मित|वर्मित|वर्म्मितः
वर्म्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Armed, accoutred.<BR>E.<BR>वर्म्म mail, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्य्य|वर्य|वर्यः|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Chief, principal.<BR>2 To be applied to for aid or a boon, &c.<BR>3 To be chosen or selected.<BR>4 To be yielded to or indulged.<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>A girl choosing her own husband.<BR>E.<BR>वर to ask as a boon, or वृ to choose, यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वट|वर्वट
वर्व्वट<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वणा|वर्वणा
वर्व्वणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A blue fly.<BR>E.<BR>वर् imitative sound, and वण or वण to utter, aff. अच्; also वर्व्वणा and वर्व्वणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वर|वर्वर|वर्वरः|वर्व्वरं|वर्व्वरः
वर्व्वर<BR>mfn. subst. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>A sort of basil, (Ocymum pilosum, Rox.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A low man, one of a degraded tribe or occupation, an out-caste, a barbarians.<BR>2 A region, a country, the country inhabited by barbarians.<BR>3 Woolly or curly hair, as the hair of an African.<BR>4 A shrub, (Shiponanthus Indica.)<BR>5 A sort of worm.<BR>6 The noise or clash of weapons^1.<BR>7 A mode of dancing.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>1 A sort of potherb.<BR>2 A small bee.<BR>3 The Baya or Indian grosbeak^2, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Vermilion.<BR>2 Gum myrrh.<BR>3 A sort of Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, Uṇādi aff. करक्ष्, or the same root, with अच् aff., in the reiterative form; it is also derived from बर्ब to go, and is variously written बर्ब्बर, वर्शर, वर्व्वर, and वर्व्वर, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वरीक|वर्वरीक|वर्वरीकः|वर्व्वरीकः
वर्व्वरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Curly or woolly hair.<BR>2 A shrub, commonly Bamanaiṭhi.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 A sort of basil.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to select, Uṇādi aff. ईकन्, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वरोत्थ
वर्व्वरोत्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>White Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>वर्व्वर the country of barbarians, and उत्थ what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=739" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वा|वर्वा
वर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A sort of basil, (Ocymum pilosum, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वि|वर्वि|वर्विः|वर्व्विः
वर्व्वि<BR>m. (-र्व्विः)<BR>A glutton.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to chuse, Uṇādi aff. विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (-वर्षति)<BR>To be wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष<BR>mn. (-र्षः-र्षं)<BR>1 Rain, raining.<BR>2 Sprinkling, affusion.<BR>3 A year.<BR>4 A Varṣa, or division of the known continent; nine are reckoned; Kuru, Hiraṇmaya, Romānaka, Ilāvṛta, Hari, Ketumālā, Bhadrāśva, Kinnara, and Bharata.<BR>5 Jambu Dvīpa, or India.<BR>6 A cloud.<BR>m. plu. (-र्षाः)<BR>The rains or rainy season, containing two months, according to the Hindu classification of the seasons, which some systems consider to be Śrāvaṇa and Bhādra, and others, Bhādra and Āśvina; the duration of the monsoon is however longer, being reckoned from Āṣārha to Kārttika, or from the middle of June to the beginning of October.<BR>f. sing. (-र्षा)<BR>A sort of gramineous plant: see पृक्का.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. अच्, or वॄ to screen, &c., Uṇādi aff. स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षकर|वर्षकरः
वर्षकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Making or producing rain.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A cricket.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rain, कृ to make or mark, ट aff.; the cricket chirping-especially in wet weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षकोष|वर्षकोषः
वर्षकोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 An astrologer.<BR>2 A month.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष a year, and कोष a vocabulary, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षज|वर्षजं
वर्षज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced in the rains or rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष the rains, and ज born; also वर्षेज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षण|वर्षणं
वर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Raining, rain.<BR>2 Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षणि|वर्षणिः
वर्षणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 Abiding, staying.<BR>2 Act, action.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, अनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षत्|वर्षन्त्
वर्षत्<BR>mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षन्ती-र्षत्)<BR>Raining, showering, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to rain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षधर|वर्षधरः
वर्षधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An eunuch or attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rain, and घर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षधर्ष
वर्षधर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>An eunuch or attendant on the women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षपर्व्वत|वर्षपर्वत|वर्षपर्वतः|वर्षपर्व्वतः
वर्षपर्व्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A mountainous range, supposed to separate the various Varṣas or divisions of the globe from each other: six ranges are enumerated from south to north; viz. Himavān, Hemakūṭa, Niṣadha, Nīla, Śveta, and Śṛṅgī or Śṛṅgavān; Meru constitutes the seventh; other names occur.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष as above, and पर्व्वत a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षपाकिन्
वर्षपाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rain, and पाकिन् ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षप्रिय|वर्षप्रियः
वर्षप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rain, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षवर|वर्षवरः
वर्षवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A eunuch, a castrated attendant, one employed in the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष seminal sprinkling, वर free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षशत
वर्षशत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A century.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षसहस्र
वर्षसहस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A thousand years.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षांश|वर्षांशः
वर्षांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A month.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष a year, and अंश a part; also with कन् added, वर्षांशक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाकाल|वर्षाकालः
वर्षाकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाकालीन
वर्षाकालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Belonging to or produced in the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षाकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाङ्ग|वर्षांग|वर्षाङ्गः
वर्षाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A month.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष a year, and अङ्ग a limb or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाघोष|वर्षाघोषः
वर्षाघोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>mfn. वर्षा, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाप्रभञ्जन|वर्षाप्रभञ्जनः
वर्षाप्रभञ्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Rain-scattering.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A high wind, a gale.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा, and प्रभञ्जन scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाभू
वर्षाभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A frog.<BR>f. (-भ्वी)<BR>1 Hog-weed.<BR>2 An earth-worm, (Iulus.)<BR>3 A she frog or any small frog.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा the rains, भू to be, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षामद|वर्षामदः
वर्षामद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष the rains, आमद who rejoices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाम्भःपारणाव्रत
वर्षाम्भःपारणाव्रत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Cātaka.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षाम्भस् rain water, पारणा attention, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षायुत
वर्षायुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Ten thousand years.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and अयुत ten thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षारात्र|वर्षारात्रः
वर्षारात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A rainy night.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षार्च्चिस्|वर्षार्चिस्
वर्षार्च्चिस्<BR>m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा the rains, अर्च्चिस् light, visible in the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षालङ्कायिका
वर्षालङ्कायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant: see पृक्का.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and लङ्कायिक synonymous; conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षावसान|वर्षावसानः
वर्षावसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Autumn, the autumnal season.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षा the rains, and अवसान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिक
वर्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Raining, rainy, relating or belonging to the rains.<BR>2 Shedding, showering, pouring down.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Aloe wood or Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिन्
वर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>1 Raining.<BR>2 Sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिष्ठ|वर्षिष्ठः
वर्षिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Oldest, very old.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष substituted for वृद्घ old, and इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षीयस्
वर्षीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very aged, or old.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष substituted for वृद्ध old, and इयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुक|वर्षुकः
वर्षुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Rainy, watery.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुकाब्द|वर्षुकाब्दः
वर्षुकाब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>A rainy cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षुक rainy, and अब्द a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षेज|वर्षेजः
वर्षेज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced in the rains.<BR>E.<BR>वर्षे in the rains, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षैक
वर्षैक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Yearly, annual.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षोपल|वर्षोपलः
वर्षोपल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rain, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्म|वर्ष्मं
वर्ष्म<BR>n. (-र्ष्मं)<BR>The body: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्मन्
वर्ष्मन्<BR>n. (-र्ष्म)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 Measure.<BR>3 Height, elevation.<BR>4 A handsome form.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. मनिन्; also with a final vowel वर्ष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्य
वर्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं)<BR>1 To be rained or showered.<BR>2 To be sprinkled.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह|वर्हं
वर्ह<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्हते) r. 10th cl. (वर्हयति)<BR>1 To speak or tell.<BR>2 To kill or hurt.<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्हते)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To be excellent or pre-eminent: in this sense it is more properly वर्ह.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्हयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह|वर्हं
वर्ह<BR>n. (-र्हं)<BR>1 A peacock's tail.<BR>2 A leaf.<BR>3 A sort of perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>4 Train, retinue.<BR>E.<BR>वृह to increase, aff. अच्; also वर्ह or बर्ह to cover, &c. aff. अच्; in the latter case it is written बर्ह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हण|वर्हणं
वर्हण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A leaf.<BR>E.<BR>वृह to grow, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हभार
वर्हभार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tuft of peacock's feathers at the shaft of a lance or handle of a club.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ह, and भार load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=740" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःपुष्प|वर्हिःपुष्पं
वर्हिःपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Ganṭhiāla, a sort of vegetable perfume.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् Kuśa grass, and पुष्प flower, having a similar blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःशुष्मन्
वर्हिःशुष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>A name of fire or AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिम् Kuśa grass, शुष to dry, aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःष्ठ|वर्हिःष्ठं
वर्हिःष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>A perfume, commonly Bāla.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् Kuśa grass, and स्था to be, aff. क, growing in the same places: the Visarga of वर्हिस् optionally retained; also वर्हिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिकुसुम|वर्हिकुसुमं
वर्हिकुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Ganṭhiāla; also वर्हिःपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिण|वर्हिणः
वर्हिण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ह a peacock's tail, and इनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिणवाहन|वर्हिणवाहनः
वर्हिणवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The deity Kārttikeya.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिण a peacock, and वाहन a vehicle; mounted on that bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिध्वजा
वर्हिध्वजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A name of the goddess CAṆḌĪ.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हि for वर्ही a peacock, and ध्वज an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिन्
वर्हिन्<BR>m. (-र्ही)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ह a peacock's tail, and इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिपुष्प|वर्हिपुष्पं
वर्हिपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पः)<BR>A vegetable perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हि a peacock, and पुष्प flower; also वर्हिःपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिर्ज्योतिस्
वर्हिर्ज्योतिस्<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of fire.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् Kuśa grass, and ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिर्मुख
वर्हिर्मुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A deity, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् fire, and मुख mouth; most offerings passing through fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिश्शुष्मन्
वर्हिश्शुष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् an oblation, शुष्मन् who dries up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिषट्
वर्हिषट्<BR>m. (-षत् or -षट्)<BR>A Pitṛ or progenitor of a particular class.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिष् Kuśa grass, अट् to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्केश|वर्हिष्केशः
वर्हिष्केश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिम् light, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्ठ|वर्हिष्ठं
वर्हिष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>1 A perfume, commonly Bāla, perhaps a species of Andropogon.<BR>2 The resin of the Pinus longifolia.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस् Kuśa grass, and स्था to stay, aff. क, the final of वर्हिस् changed to Visarga, and optionally rejected; see वर्हिःष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्मत्
वर्हिष्मत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्मन्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्)<BR>1 Having Kuśa or sacrificial grass.<BR>2 Having fire or light, blazing, shining.<BR>E.<BR>वर्हिस्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिस्
वर्हिस्<BR>m. (-र्हिः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>mn. (-हिः)<BR>1 Sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>2 Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>2 Ganṭhiāla, a vegetable perfume.<BR>E.<BR>वृह to increase, aff. इसि, or वर्ह to excel, &c., with the same aff.; in the latter case this word and its corresponding ones are written with an initial consonant बर्हिस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल|वलं|वलः
वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (वलते)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To move.<BR>3 To surround or enclose.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वालयति)<BR>To cherish or maintain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल|वलं|वलः
वल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An army, forces.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, aff. अच्; see बल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्ष|वलक्षः
वलक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>White.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>White, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>वल to go, aff. क्विप्; वल् going, अक्ष to pervade, aff. अच्; also बलक्ष, and अवलक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्षगु
वलक्षगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>वलक्ष white, गौ a ray of light, the final vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलग्न|वलग्नं|वलग्नः
वलग्न<BR>mn. (-ग्नः-ग्नं)<BR>The middle; also अवलग्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलभि|वलभिः
वलभि<BR>mf. (-भिः-भी)<BR>1 The wooden frame of a thatch.<BR>2 A turret or temporary building on the roof of a house.<BR>E.<BR>वल to cover, अभस् aff., इन् and ङीष् added; also वडभि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलम्ब|वलंब|वलम्बः
वलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A perpendicular.<BR>E.<BR>अव, and लवि to depend, घञ् aff., the initial rejected; also अवलम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलय|वलयं|वलयः
वलय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>A bracelet, an armlet.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Sore throat, inflammation of the larynx, &c.<BR>2 A boundary, an inclosure.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, कयन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयित|वलयितं
वलयित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>वलय an inclosure, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाका
वलाका<BR>f. (-का-की)<BR>A small kind of crane.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, aff. आकन्; also बलाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलासक|वलासकः
वलासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>2 A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाहक|वलाहकः
वलाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A Daitya, a demon.<BR>4 One of the Nāgas.<BR>5 One of the horses of KṚṢṆA'S car.<BR>E.<BR>वलाका a crane, हा to go, aff. नु, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलि|वलिः
वलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>1 A line or streak made with fragrant unguents on the person.<BR>2 Natural line or folds of skin, a wrinkle.<BR>3 Offerings to the spirits of air.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, aff. इन्; see बलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिक|वलिकं|वलिकः
वलिक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>The edge of a thatch.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, Uṇādi aff. इकक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिक्रिया
वलिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Making lines on the person.<BR>2 Making offerings^1 to all beings.<BR>E.<BR>वलि, and क्रिया act; see बलि, &c.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलित|वलितः
वलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Moved, constrained.<BR>2 Surrounded.<BR>E.<BR>वल to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिश|वलिशं
वलिश<BR>nf. (-शं-शिः or -शी)<BR>A fish-hook.<BR>E.<BR>वटिन् a bait, शो to destroy, aff. ड, ट changed to ड, and ड again interchangeable with ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूक|वलूकं|वलूकः
वलूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of the lotus.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, Uṇādi aff. ऊक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क|वल्कं|वल्कः
वल्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (वल्कयति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क|वल्कं|वल्कः
वल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>1 The bark of a tree.<BR>2 The scales of a fish.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, कक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कल|वल्कलं|वल्कलः
वल्कल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 The bark of a tree.<BR>2 A garment made of bark.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कवत्|वल्कवन्त्
वल्कवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having scales or bark, wearing a dress made of the bark of trees, &c.<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>वल्क a scale, &c., मतुप् possess. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्किल|वल्किलः
वल्किल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>वल्क bark, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कुत|वल्कुतं
वल्कुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Bark, rind.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, कुतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ग
वल्ग<BR>r. 1st cl. (वल्गति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To go by leaps, to jump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गत्
वल्गत्<BR>mfn. (-ल्गन्-ल्गान्ती-ल्गत्)<BR>1 Going.<BR>2 Jumping.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ग to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गा
वल्गा<BR>f. (-ल्गा)<BR>A bridle, a rein.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ग to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गित|वल्गितं
वल्गित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Leaped, jumped, gone by bounds or leaps.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Running.<BR>2 A horse's gallop.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ग to go by jumps, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गु|वल्गुः
वल्गु<BR>mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>m. (-ल्गुः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, Uṇādi aff. उ, and गुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुक|वल्गुकं
वल्गुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 A wood.<BR>3 Price.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुपत्र|वल्गुपत्रः
वल्गुपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A wild sort of pulse; see वनमुद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुल|वल्गुलः
वल्गुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The flying fox.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुलिका
वल्गुलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गूयत्
वल्गूयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Become handsome or beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>वल्गु used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=741" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भ
वल्भ<BR>r. 1st cl. (वल्भते)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भन|वल्भनं
वल्भन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating.<BR>2 Food.<BR>E.<BR>वल्भ to eat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भित
वल्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Eaten.<BR>E.<BR>वल्भ to eat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मिक|वल्मिकः
वल्मिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ant-hill; also वल्भीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मिकि|वल्मिकिः
वल्मिकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>An ant-hill; also वल्भीकि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मीक|वल्मीकं|वल्मीकः
वल्मीक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A hillock, ground thrown up by moles, &c., but especially the large accumulations of soil, sometimes made by the white ant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The poet VĀLMĪKI.<BR>2 Elephantiasis, or swellings of the neck, chest, hands and feet, which break and discharge ichor in many places.<BR>E.<BR>बल to cover, or बल to live, कीकच् Uṇādi aff., and मुम् augment; in the latter case this word and the corresponding ones are written बल्भीक, &c.; also वल्मिक, वल्मीकि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्युल
वल्युल and वल्यूल<BR>r. 10th cl. (वल्यूलयति)<BR>1 To cut<BR>2 To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल|वल्लः
वल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (वल्लते)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल|वल्लः
वल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>1 Winnowing corn.<BR>2 A Māṣa of silver.<BR>3 A weight of three Rattis.<BR>4 Prohibiting, prohibition.<BR>5 Covering.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to move, &c., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लकी
वल्लकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>The Vīṇā, or Indian lute.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभ|वल्लभः
वल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Beloved, desired, dear.<BR>2 Supreme, superintending.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A lover, a husband, a friend.<BR>2 A horse with good marks.<BR>3 A superintendant, an overseer.<BR>4 The chief herdsman.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A mistress, a wife.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, अभच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभपालक|वल्लभपालकः
वल्लभपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A groom, a horse-keeper.<BR>E.<BR>वल्लभ a good horse, and पालक who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरि|वल्लरिः
वल्लरि<BR>f. (-रिः or -री)<BR>1 A compound pedicle.<BR>2 A creeping or twining plant.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लव|वल्लवः
वल्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A cook.<BR>2 A herdsman.<BR>3 A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A cowherdess.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल covering, and व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लि|वल्लिः
वल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः-ल्ली)<BR>1 A creeper, a climbing or creeping plant.<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, इन् aff., and ङीप् occasionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीज|वल्लीजं
वल्लीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Pepper.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ली a creeper, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लुर|वल्लुरं
वल्लुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 An arbour, a bower, a place overgrown with creeping plants.<BR>2 An uncultivated field or place overrun with wild grass.<BR>3 A sand, a desart, a place destitute of water.<BR>4 A field.<BR>5 A compound pedicle.<BR>6 A solitude, a wild.<BR>7 A thicket, a wood.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, उर aff.; also बल्लूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लूर|वल्लूरं|वल्लूरः
वल्लूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं).<BR>1 Dried flesh.<BR>2 Hog's flesh, the flesh of the wild hog.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 An uncultivated field, or one overrun with grass.<BR>2 A thicket.<BR>3 A desart.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, ऊर Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल्या
वल्ल्या<BR>f. (-ल्ल्या)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्वज|वल्वजः
वल्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A sort of coarse grass, (Eleusine Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वल्ल to cover, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ह
वल्ह<BR>r. 1st cl. (वल्हते) r. 10th cl. (वल्हयति)<BR>To speak or tell.<BR>r. 1st cl. (वल्हते)<BR>1 To kill or hurt.<BR>2 To cover.<BR>3 To be preeminent; in which sense it is more properly बल्ह.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वल्हयति)<BR>To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश|वशं|वशः
वश<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वष्टि)<BR>To desire, to will, to wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश|वशं|वशः
वश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Humbled, subdued, tamed, overpowered.<BR>2 Enthralled, subdued by charms and incantations, fascinated, charmed, enchanted.<BR>mn. (-शः-शं)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>1 Authority, supremacy, mastership.<BR>2 Subjection, submission, the state of being completely tamed and over-powered.<BR>3 Birth.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The residence of harlots.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A wife.<BR>3 A daughter.<BR>4 A cow.<BR>5 A barren cow.<BR>6 A female elephant.<BR>7 A husband's sister.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire, aff. अप्, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशका
वशका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An obedient and docile wife.<BR>E.<BR>वश subject, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशक्रिया
वशक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Subduing or overpowering by drugs, gems, charms, or incantations.<BR>2 The drugs, &c. so used.<BR>E.<BR>वश subjection, क्रिया business or agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशग
वशग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Obedient, subject.<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>An obedient wife.<BR>E.<BR>वश subject, and ग who goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशङ्गत|वशंगत
वशङ्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subject, obedient.<BR>E.<BR>वश, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशम्बद
वशम्बद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Submissive, acknowledging obedience or subjection.<BR>E.<BR>वश subjection, वद to speak, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशवर्त्तिन्|वशवर्तिन्
वशवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Obsequious, acting under subjection, or according to the pleasure of another.<BR>E.<BR>वश, and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशाकु
वशाकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशाद्यक
वशाद्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A porpoise, the Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशानुग
वशानुग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Obedient, submissive.<BR>E.<BR>वश, and अनुग who pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशापायिन्
वशापायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वशा subjection, पा to preserve, इनि aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशि|वशिः
वशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>Subjugating, fascinating, bewitching, holding others in magical or mysterious submission to one's will.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire (supremacy), and इन् affix; also with तल् and त्व affs. वशिता and वशित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिक|वशिकः
वशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Void, empty.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Aloe wood.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire, इन् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिता
वशिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Fascinating, bewitching.<BR>2 Subjection, holding in order or subjugation; also वशित्वं.<BR>E.<BR>वशिन्, and तल् or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिन्
वशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Subdued, subjugated, in subjection.<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A sage with subdued passions.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The Śami tree, (Mimosa Sama, Rox.)<BR>2 A parasite plant.<BR>E.<BR>वश, इनि, and ङीप् affixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिर|वशिरं|वशिरः
वशिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>2 A sort of long pepper.<BR>3 Orris root.<BR>E.<BR>वश to desire, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिष्ठ|वशिष्ठः
वशिष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>VAŚIṢṬHA, a Ṛṣi or divine sage of the first order; he is also a Brahmādika, a Prajāpati, and one of the seven stars of Ursa Major.<BR>E.<BR>अव before शास to govern, to instruct, (the other saints,) aff. क्त, the first vowel of the prefix rejected; also written वशिष्ट and वसिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकरण|वशीकरणं
वशीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Subduing or overcoming by drugs, charms, &c., enchanting, charming.<BR>2 Subduing in general.<BR>E.<BR>वश subduing, and करण making, च्चि augment, leaving ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकृत
वशीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bewitched, fascinated, subjected to another's will.<BR>E.<BR>वशी, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीभूत|वशीभूतः
वशीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subjugated, subject to another's will.<BR>E.<BR>वशी, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=742" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीर|वशीरः
वशीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pungent fruit resembling pepper, (Pothos officinalis); also वशिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्य|वश्यं|वश्यः
वश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>Docile, tame, humble, governable.<BR>2 To be tamed or humbled.<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>A dependant, a slave.<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>A docile and obedient wife.<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>वश subjection, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यका
वश्यका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An obedient wife.<BR>E.<BR>वश्या, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यता
वश्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Humility, subjugation, disposition to, or fitness for subjection.<BR>E.<BR>वश्य, and तल् aff.; also वश्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यात्मन्
वश्यात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Of subdued mind.<BR>E.<BR>वशी, and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष
वष<BR>r. 1st cl. (बषति)<BR>To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्
वषट्<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation used on making an oblation to a deity with fire.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear or convey, aff. डषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कर्त्तृ|वषट्कर्तृ
वषट्कर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>The priest who pours the oiled butter into the fire at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>वषट् an exclamation, &c., and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कार|वषट्कारः
वषट्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Burnt-offering, oblation with fire.<BR>E.<BR>वषट् the exclamation used on this occasion, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कृत|वषट्कृतं
वषट्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Offered or sacrificed with fire.<BR>E.<BR>वषट् as above, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्क
वष्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (वष्कते) r. 10th cl. (वष्कयति)<BR>1 To see.<BR>2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कय|वष्कयः
वष्कय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A one year old calf.<BR>E.<BR>वष्क to go, अयन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयणी
वष्कयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A cow bearing many calves.<BR>E.<BR>वष्कय a calf, णी to have, aff. ड and ङीष्; also वष्कय, with इनि and ङीप् aff., वष्कयिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस
वस<BR>(औ) औवस r. 1st and 10th cls. (वसति वसयति)<BR>To dwell or inhabit.<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वस्ते)<BR>To cover with dress, to wear as clothes.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वासयति)<BR>1 To be affectionate, to love.<BR>2 To cut or divide.<BR>3 To kill.<BR>4 To accept.<BR>(इर, उ) इरवसु r. 4th cl. (वस्यति)<BR>To be straight, to be unbending; literally or figuratively.<BR>With अधि prefixed,<BR>To sit upon, to occupy.<BR>With उप,<BR>To fast.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To dwell in or inhabit.<BR>2 To dress.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To dwell abroad.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To cohabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसत्
वसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सती-सत्)<BR>1 Dwelling, inhabiting.<BR>2 Wearing, as clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसति|वसतिः
वसति<BR>f. (-तिः or -ती)<BR>1 A house, a dwelling.<BR>2 Abiding, abode, residence.<BR>3 Night.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, अति Uṇādi aff., ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन|वसनं
वसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cloth or clothes.<BR>2 Covering, clothing.<BR>3 A dwelling, a house.<BR>4 An ornament worn by women round the loins.<BR>E.<BR>वस to be clothed, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसनसद्मन्
वसनसद्मन्<BR>n. (-द्म)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>वसन, and सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्त|वसंत|वसंतः|वसन्तः
वसन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Vasanta, the season of spring, or its deified personification.<BR>2 Dysentery, diarrhoea.<BR>3 Small-pox.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, Uṇādi aff. झच्, as applied to the season, when love is especially present on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकुसुम|वसन्तकुसुमः
वसन्तकुसुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A tree, (Cordia myxa and latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and कुसुम a flower; blossoming in the spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तघोषिन्|वसंतघोषिन्
वसन्तघोषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>The Indian cuckoo or Koïl.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and घोषिन who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तज
वसन्तज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in the spring.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>A festival in honour of KĀMADEVA, held in the month Chaitra.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तदूत|वसंतदूत|वसन्तदूतः
वसन्तदूत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>2 The month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>3 The fifth Rāga or musical mode, called also Hindola.<BR>4 The mango tree.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>1 The trumpet flower.<BR>2 A large and beautiful creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and दूत the messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तद्रु|वसंतद्रु|वसन्तद्रुः
वसन्तद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and द्रु a tree, or वसन्तद्रुम; the mango blossoms in March or April, and is then an object of great beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तसख|वसंतसख|वसन्तसखः
वसन्तसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>KĀMADEVA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तोत्सव|वसंतोत्सव|वसन्तोत्सवः
वसन्तोत्सव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The celebration of the return of spring, formerly held on the full moon of Chaitra, but now on the full moon of Phālguna, being identified with the Dola yātra or Holi.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसा
वसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 The serum or marrow of the flesh, considered by some authorities as distinct from the marrow of the bones, though regarded by others as the same substance.<BR>2 Adeps, fat, suet.<BR>E.<BR>वस to divide (in the body), अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाद्य
वसाद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>The Gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus Gangeticus); also वसाद्यक and वशाद्यक, the last perhaps incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसान
वसान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Wearing, putting on, (as clothes.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to clothe, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसापायिन्
वसापायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वसा, and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसार
वसार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Wish, purpose, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसि|वसिः
वसि<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>1 Dwelling, abode.<BR>2 A dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, Uṇādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित
वसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stored, (as grain.)<BR>2 Dwelling, inhabiting.<BR>3 Put on, worn.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Abiding, residence.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The power of subduing all things: see वशिता.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, &c., aff. क्त, or वशिता as above, and श changed to स.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसितृ
वसितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what wears.<BR>E.<BR>वस to put on, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित्वा
वसित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having put on (as clothes), wearing.<BR>E.<BR>वस to wear, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिर|वसिरं
वसिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Sea salt.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pungent fruit, considered as a sort of pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide (in the sea), इरन् aff.; also, as derived from वश to desire, वशिर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठ|वसिष्ठः
वसिष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A celebrated Muni.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide (in the practice of religious austerities), aff. णिनि, वसिन् superlative aff., इष्टन् added, pre-eminent amongst the ascetics; also वशिष्ठ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>1 Sweet, sweet-flavoured.<BR>2 Dry, dried.<BR>n. (-सु)<BR>1 Wealth, thing, substance.<BR>2 A gem, a jewel.<BR>3 A medicinal root, commonly Vṛddhi.<BR>4 Water.<BR>5 Gold.<BR>6 A yellow kind of kidney-bean.<BR>7 A sort of salt.<BR>8 The number eight, i. e. the eight Vasus.<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>1 A kind of demigod, of whom eight are enumerated, viz. DHAVA, DHRUVA, SOMA or the moon, VIṢṆU, ANILA or wind, ANALA or fire, PRABHŪṢA and PRABHĀVA.<BR>2 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>3 A ray of light.<BR>4 The tie of a yoke.<BR>5 A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>6 The name of a king.<BR>7 A name of KUVERA.<BR>8 A tree in general.<BR>9 A lake, a pool.<BR>10 A rein, a halter.<BR>11 A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>12 ŚIVA.<BR>13 The sun.<BR>14 A kind of fish.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide or dwell, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=743" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुक|वसुकं|वसुकः
वसुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fossil salt, brought from a district in Ajmere, Sāmbher salt.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A shrub, (Gigantic Asclepias.)<BR>2 A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding, or वसु wealth, कै to sound, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुकीट|वसुकीटः
वसुकीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A supplicant, a beggar, a petitioner.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदा
वसुदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, and दा who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेव|वसुदेवः
वसुदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>VASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वसु a Vasu, a deity, the incarnation of one of the Vasus; or वसु wealth दिव to shine, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवता
वसुदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The constellation Dhaniṣṭha.<BR>E.<BR>वसु the Vasus, and देवता divinity; presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवभू
वसुदेवभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वसुदेव, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेव्या
वसुदेव्या<BR>f. (-व्या)<BR>1 The asterism Dhaniṣṭha.<BR>2 The ninth day of the fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधर्म्मिका|वसुधर्मिका
वसुधर्म्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधा
वसुधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, धा to have or contain, aff. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधाधर
वसुधाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>वसुधा, and घर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधाधिप
वसुधाधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>वसुधा, and अधिप sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधानगर
वसुधानगर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The capital of VARUṆA in the western ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधारा
वसुधारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A female Śakti peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>2 The capital of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, धृ to have, aff. घञ् and टाप्; some authorities read वसुभारा for KUVERA'S capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुन्धरा|वसुंधरा
वसुन्धरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, धृ to have, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुप्राण|वसुप्राणः
वसुप्राण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Fire or its deity, AGNI.<BR>E.<BR>वसु a Vasu, and प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुमत्|वसुमन्त्
वसुमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Wealthy, rich.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुरोचिस्
वसुरोचिस्<BR>n. (-चिः)<BR>A religious ceremony in which the demigods called Vasus especially are worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>वसु as above, रुच to shine, इसि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुल|वसुलः
वसुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A deity, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, ला to have, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुषेण|वसुषेणः
वसुषेण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of KARṆA, the illegitimate brother of the PĀṆḌU princes.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, and सेना an army; surrounded by hosts of beggars for his wealth, of which he was liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुस्थली
वसुस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The city of KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>वसु wealth, स्थल place or site, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुहट्ट|वसुहट्टः
वसुहट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>The Vakapushpa, (Sesbana grandiflora); also वसुहट्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूक|वसूकं|वसूकः
वसूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Sāmbher salt.<BR>2 The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>E.<BR>see वसुक; the उ of वसुक optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूरा
वसूरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A whore, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क|वस्कः
वस्क<BR>r. 1st cl. (वस्कते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क|वस्कः
वस्क<BR>m. (-स्कः)<BR>1 Application, perseverance.<BR>2 Going, motion.<BR>E.<BR>वस्क to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कय|वस्कयः
वस्कय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A calf of one year, a yearling.<BR>E.<BR>वस्क to go, अयन् aff.; also वष्कय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कयणी
वस्कयणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A cow bearing many calves.<BR>E.<BR>वस्कय a calf, णी to have, aff. ड and ङीप्; also वष्कयणी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कराटिका
वस्कराटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त|वस्तं|वस्तः
वस्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (वस्तयते)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To go or move.<BR>3 To ask, to beg, to solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त|वस्तं|वस्तः
वस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A goat.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त to kill, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तमोदा
वस्तमोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen): see अजमोदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तव्य
वस्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be dwelt in, or inhabited, resided, remained at, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तान्त्री
वस्तान्त्री<BR>f. (-न्त्री)<BR>1 Benzoin or storax.<BR>2 A plant, commonly Ajaśṛṅgī.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त a goat, and अन्त्र entrail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्ति|वस्तिः
वस्ति<BR>mf. (-स्तिः)<BR>1 The lower belly, hypogastric or pubic region.<BR>2 The bladder.<BR>3 A glyster, syringe, or bag made of bladder or gut, with a wooden or metallic nozzle.<BR>4 Abiding, dwelling, staying. plur. only (-स्तयः) The ends of a cloth.<BR>E.<BR>वस to wear as clothes, Uṇādi aff. ति, or वस to abide, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिकर्म्माद्य
वस्तिकर्म्माद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>The soap-berry, (Sapindus detergens.)<BR>E.<BR>वस्ति the ends of cloth, कर्म्म business, and आद्य principal; used in washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिमल|वस्तिमलं
वस्तिमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Urine, piss.<BR>E.<BR>वस्ति the belly, and मल excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिशिरस्
वस्तिशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 The neck of the bladder.<BR>2 The pipe of the glyster bag.<BR>E.<BR>वस्ति, and शिरस् head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिशोधन
वस्तिशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A diuretic.<BR>E.<BR>वस्ति, and शोधन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तु
वस्तु<BR>n. (-स्तु)<BR>1 Thing, matter, substance.<BR>2 Natural disposition, essential property, nature, essence.<BR>3 The pith or substance of any thing.<BR>4 The main plot or subject of a poem or play.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, Uṇādi aff. तुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुक|वस्तुकं
वस्तुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide (in the ground), उकञ् aff., and तुट् augment; also वास्तुक, वास्तूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुतस्
वस्तुतस्<BR>ind.<BR>In fine, in fact, essentially, substantially.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुमात्र
वस्तुमात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Outline of any subject, skeleton of a discourse.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुहानि
वस्तुहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Loss of substance or property.<BR>E.<BR>बस्तु, and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तूत्थापन
वस्तूत्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Producing any change or incident in a play by magic.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and उत्थापन raising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्वन्तर
वस्त्वन्तर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Another thing or subject.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and अन्तर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्वभाव|वस्त्वभावः
वस्त्वभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Insubstantial existence.<BR>2 Loss or destruction of property.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and अभाव non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्य|वस्त्यं
वस्त्य<BR>n. (-स्त्यं)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, ति aff., and यत् added; this word has many etymologies; it is also read पस्त्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्र|वस्त्रं
वस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 Cloth, clothes, raiment.<BR>2 Covering, a cover.<BR>E.<BR>वस to wear as clothes, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रकुट्टिम|वस्त्रकुट्टिमं
वस्त्रकुट्टिम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>An umbrella.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, and कुद्दिभ a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रगृह|वस्त्रगृहं
वस्त्रगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रग्रन्थि|वस्त्रग्रंथि|वस्त्रग्रन्थिः
वस्त्रग्रन्थि<BR>m. (-न्थिः)<BR>The string or twist by which the lower garments are fastened above the hips.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, and ग्रन्थि knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रनिर्णेजक|वस्त्रनिर्णेजकः
वस्त्रनिर्णेजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र, and निर्णेजक who washes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रपुत्त्रिका
वस्त्रपुत्त्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, पुत्त्री infant (as it were), कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रभेदक|वस्त्रभेदकः
वस्त्रभेदक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, clothes, भेदक who pierces or cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रभेदिन्
वस्त्रभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A tailor.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, and भेदिन् who pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयुग्म
वस्त्रयुग्म<BR>n. (-ग्मं)<BR>A pair of cloths.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र, and युग्म a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=744" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयोनि|वस्त्रयोनिः
वस्त्रयोनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>The basis or material of cloth, as cotton, silk, wool, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्राञ्चल|वस्त्रांचल|वस्त्राञ्चलः
वस्त्राञ्चल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The end or hem of a garment.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र, and अञ्चल the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रापहारक
वस्त्रापहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stealer of clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र, and अपहारक who carries off; also वस्त्रापहारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्न|वस्नं|वस्नः
वस्न<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Price.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes.<BR>3 Wealth.<BR>4 Death.<BR>5 Abiding, dwelling.<BR>6 Thing, substance.<BR>7 Skin.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, Uṇādi aff. न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्नन|वस्ननं
वस्नन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An ornament for a woman's loins, a zone, a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्नसा
वस्नसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A tendon, a nerve, a fibre, described as a hollow tube resembling a string, attached to the bones, and supposed to be for the passage of the vital air.<BR>E.<BR>वस्न skin, षो to destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्निक
वस्निक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Hireling, mercenary.<BR>2 Purchasable.<BR>3 Relating to hire, wages, price, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त hire, &c., and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्वौकसारा
वस्वौकसारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 The capital of INDRA.<BR>2 Alakā, the residence of KUVERA.<BR>3 A lake attached to Alakā or Amaravati, and belonging to either deity.<BR>E.<BR>वसु the Vasus, ओकस् a residence, रा to contain, with आङ् prefixed, and क and टाप् affs., the favorite haunts of these demigods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह|वहः
वह<BR>r. 1st cl. (वहति)<BR>To bear, to carry, to convey or transport.<BR>(वहते)<BR>To flow as a stream.<BR>(इ) वहि r. 10th cl. (वंहयति)<BR>To shine.<BR>r. 1st cl. (वंहते)<BR>To grow or increase; this last root is more properly बहि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह|वहः
वह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Bearing, conveying.<BR>2 Any vehicle or means of conveyance, as a horse, a car, &c.<BR>3 The shoulder of an ox.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>5 A road, a way.<BR>6 Any male river.<BR>7 A measure of four Droṇas.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहंलिह
वहंलिह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>An ox.<BR>E.<BR>वह the shoulder, लिह to lick, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत्
वहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>1 Bearing, conveying.<BR>2 Assuming, taking.<BR>3 Wearing.<BR>4 Having, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत|वहतः
वहत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 An ox.<BR>2 A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, Uṇādi aff. अत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहति|वहतिः
वहति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 An ox.<BR>2 A friend, a counsellor.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, अति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहतु|वहतुः
वहतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 An ox.<BR>2 A traveller.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, Uṇādi aff. अतु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन|वहनं
वहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Bearing, conveying.<BR>2 Flowing, as a stream.<BR>3 Any vehicle.<BR>4 A raft, a float, a boat.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहनीय
वहनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be carried or borne.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन्त|वहंत|वहंतः|वहन्तः
वहन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 An infant.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, Uṇādi aff. झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहमान
वहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Bearing, conveying.<BR>2 Having, possessing.<BR>3 Flowing.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहल|वहलः
वहल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Hard, firm, compact.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. कलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहलचक्षुस्
वहलचक्षुस्<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A climbing and milky plant, (Asclepias geminata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिःकुटीचर|वहिःकुटीचरः
वहिःकुटीचर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस् externally, कुटी crookedly, चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिःस्थ
वहिःस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>External, outer.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्, and स्था to stay, ड aff.; also वहिःस्थित, वहिःस्थायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित|वहितः
वहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, celebrated.<BR>2 Borne, conveyed.<BR>3 Obtained.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित्र|वहित्रं
वहित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A raft, a float, a boat, a vessel.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, Uṇādi aff. इत्र; also with कन् added, वहित्रक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिन्
वहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Bearing, conveying.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A boat, a vessel.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिरङ्ग
वहिरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 An outer or external part, limb, member, property, &c.<BR>2 A stranger, an indifferent person.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस्, and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिरिन्द्रिय
वहिरिन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>An organ of sense or perception, an organ of action, as the eye, hand, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्, and इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्गत
वहिर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone out or forth.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्गमन
वहिर्गमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्देश|वहिर्द्देश
वहिर्देश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A foreign country.<BR>2 A place without a town or village.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्, and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्द्वार|वहिर्द्वारं
वहिर्द्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>An outer gate.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर् for वहिस् outer, and द्वार door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठक|वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठकः
वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A portico, a covered terrace before the door of a house.<BR>E.<BR>वहिर्द्वार an outer door, प्रकोष्ठ an elbow, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्भव
वहिर्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced externally.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस् outwardly, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्भूत|वहिर्भूतः
वहिर्भूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Being out or without, expelled, excluded.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस्, and भूत being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्म्मुख|वहिर्मुख|वहिर्मुखः
वहिर्म्मुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्लम्ब
वहिर्लम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>Obtuse-angular.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस्, and लम्ब a perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिश्चर|वहिश्चरः
वहिश्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A crab.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस् externally, and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्करण
वहिष्करण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Expelling, excluding, excepting.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस् out, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्कृत
वहिष्कृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expelled, excluded, excepted.<BR>E.<BR>वहिस्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिस्
वहिस्<BR>ind.<BR>Out, outwards, external.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. इस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहीरु
वहीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A tendon, a nerve, a muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्नि|वह्निः
वह्नि<BR>m. (-ह्निः)<BR>1 Fire, or its deity AGNI.<BR>2 Lead wort, (Plumbago zeylanica.)<BR>3 Marking-nut plant.<BR>4 Appetite, digestion, the metaphorical fire of the stomach.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, (the oblations presented to the gods,) and नि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निकर
वह्निकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>1 Making fire, lighting.<BR>2 Stomachic, giving appetite.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, (appetite,) कृ to make, aff. अच् or ट, and टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निगन्ध|वह्निगंध|वह्निगन्धः
वह्निगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Incense or resin.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निगर्भ|वह्निगर्भः
वह्निगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>A bambu.<BR>f. (-र्भा)<BR>A sort of Mimosa, (M. Suma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and गर्भ embryo; taking or producing fire by friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निदीपक|वह्निदीपकः
वह्निदीपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Safflower.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and दीपक what shines like or resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=745" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निनामन्
वह्निनामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>1 Marking-nut plant.<BR>2 Lead wort.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and नामन् appellation; the synonyms of fire being equally applicable to those plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निभोग्य|वह्निभोग्यं
वह्निभोग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, भोग्य to be consumed or enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमन्थ|वह्निमन्थः
वह्निमन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by attrition, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and मन्थ churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमारक|वह्निमारकं
वह्निमारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and मारक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमित्र|वह्निमित्रः
वह्निमित्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and मित्र the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निरेतस्
वह्निरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and रेतस् semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निलोह
वह्निलोह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवधू
वह्निवधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>The wife of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि, and वधू the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवर्ण|वह्निवर्णं
वह्निवर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>The red water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवल्लभ|वह्निवल्लभः
वह्निवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Resin.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and वल्लभ friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवीज
वह्निवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A particle, to be repeated as the peculiar prayer of fire in the Tantra system: the syllable Ran रं.<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निशिख|वह्निशिखं
वह्निशिख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>1 Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A potherb, (Echites dichotoma.)<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and शिखा crest; also अग्निशिस्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निशिखर|वह्निशिखरः
वह्निशिखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A flower, coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>वह्नि fire, and शिखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्य|वह्यं
वह्य<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>1 A vehicle, a conveyance of any sort.<BR>2 A cart.<BR>f. (-ह्या)<BR>The wife of a Muni or saint.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वाति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To blow as the wind.<BR>With निर् prefixed,<BR>To blow out, to extinguish.<BR>3 To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of,<BR>1 Comparison, (as, like, so);<BR>2 Alternative or option, (or, either, else, sometimes);<BR>3 Doubt and consideration, (or, whether);<BR>4 Exception, (only, no other);<BR>5 Asseveration or confirmation, (indeed, even, very);<BR>6 A conjunction, (and.)<BR>7 An expletive.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, aff. क्विप्, the व is sometimes changed to ब, and the word is read बा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांश|वांशः
वांश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Bambu, of or belonging to, made from a bambu, &c.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The manna of the bambu.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a bambu, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशिक|वांशिकः
वांशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A flute-player, a piper, a fifer.<BR>2 A bambu-cutter, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वंश a pipe, aff. ठक् or ठन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःकिटि|वाःकिटिः
वाःकिटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>A porpoise.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, and किटि a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःपुष्प
वाःपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःसदन|वाःसदनं
वाःसदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A large water-jar.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, सदन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक|वाकं|वाकः
वाक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a crane.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A flight of cranes.<BR>E.<BR>वक, and अण् or अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुची
वाकुची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>वा wind, and कुच् to contract, क aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कलह|वाक्कलहः
वाक्कलह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>Quarrel, dispute.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and कलह disturbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कीर|वाक्कीरः
वाक्कीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A wife's brother.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् a speech, a phrase, and कीर parrot: having giving rise to a proverb; as a cock parrot is, so is the hen; i. e. of the same breed and disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चपल
वाक्चपल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Frivolous, inconsistent, (in speech.)<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and चपल changeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चापल्य
वाक्चापल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Gossipping, chattering, idle or improper talk.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छल|वाक्छलं
वाक्छल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Prevarication, equivocation.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, छल disguise, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छलान्वित
वाक्छलान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Equivocating, evasive.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्छल, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पटु
वाक्पटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु)<BR>Eloquent, able in speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पटुता
वाक्पटुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Eloquence.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, वाकपटुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पति|वाक्पतिः
वाक्पति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Eloquent.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पथ|वाक्पथः
वाक्पथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Suitable or seasonable for discourse.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and पथ path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पारुष्य|वाक्पारुष्यं
वाक्पारुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Abuse, scurrility, defamation, wordy violence or assault.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, पारुष्य violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्य|वाक्यं
वाक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>1 A sentence.<BR>2 A rule or aphorism.<BR>3 Speech.<BR>4 (In astronomy,) The solar process for all astronomical computations.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यखण्डन|वाक्यखंडन
वाक्यखण्डन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Refuting or criticising an assertion.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्य, and खण्डन breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यप्रयोग|वाक्यप्रयोगः
वाक्यप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Employment or application of speech or language.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्य, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविन्यास|वाक्यविन्यासः
वाक्यविन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Syntax, order, or arrangement of a sentence.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्य, and विन्यास disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविशारद
वाक्यविशारद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Eloquent.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्य, and विशारद skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यस्थ
वाक्यस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Contained in a sentence.<BR>2 Obedient, attentive.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्य, and स्थ what stays; also वाक्यस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्ष
वाक्ष<BR>(इ) वाक्षि r. 10th cl. (वाङ्क्षति)<BR>To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागपहारक|वागपहारकः
वागपहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A stealer of books.<BR>2 A reader of prohibited works or passages.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, अपहारक seizer, stealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागर|वागरः
वागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sage, a holy man, one desirous of final emancipation.<BR>2 A scholar, a Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman.<BR>3 A hero, a brave man, one who is intrepid or fearless.<BR>4 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>5 A whetstone.<BR>6 An obstacle, an impediment, or cause of obstruction.<BR>7 Submarine fire.<BR>8 A wolf.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, ऋ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागसि|वागसिः
वागसि<BR>f. (-सिः)<BR>Sharp or searching speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and असि a sword, piercing men's thoughts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागा
वागा<BR>f. (-गा)<BR>A bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागारु|वागारुः
वागारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Breaking promise or faith, disappointing, a disappointer or deceiver.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, ऋ to go, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश|वागीशः
वागीश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Eloquent, well spoken.<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 An author, an orator, a poet, &c.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश्वर|वागीश्वरः
वागीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An orator, a learned man.<BR>2 A Bauddha deified sage; also MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुजी
वागुजी<BR>f. (-जी)<BR>A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, गुज to sound inarticulately, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=746" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुण|वागुणः
वागुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An acid fruit, (Averrhoa carambola.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरा
वागुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A net, a snare, a noose.<BR>E.<BR>वा to hurt, उर Uṇādi aff., and गन् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरावृत्ति|वागुरावृत्तिः
वागुरावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Catching wild animals.<BR>E.<BR>वागुरा a snare, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरिक|वागुरिकः
वागुरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter, a deer-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>वागुरा a net, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागृषभ|वागृषभः
वागृषभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A learned or eloquent man.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागृषभत्व
वागृषभत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Eloquence, learning, erudition.<BR>E.<BR>वागृषभ, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुद|वाग्गुदः
वाग्गुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, गुद to sport, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलि|वाग्गुलिः
वाग्गुलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The betel-bearer, an officer or servant whose business it is to have the box of Pān ready for his prince or master.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, (command,) गुर to obey, कि aff., and र changed to ल, or गृ to swallow, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलिक|वाग्गुलिकः
वाग्गुलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A betel-bearer.<BR>E.<BR>ठक् pleonasm, added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्डम्बर|वाग्डंबर|वाग्डम्बरः
वाग्डम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Graceful or eloquent language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दण्ड|वाग्दंड|वाग्दण्डः
वाग्दण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 Reproof, reprimand.<BR>2 Restraint or controul of speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दत्त
वाग्दत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Promised.<BR>f. (-त्ता)<BR>A virgin betrothed.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दरिद्र|वाग्दरिद्रः
वाग्दरिद्र<BR>mf. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>Of few words, speaking little and humbly or guardedly.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, दरिद्र poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दल|वाग्दलं
वाग्दल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A lip.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दुष्ट|वाग्दुष्टः
वाग्दुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Abusive, ill-spoken, speaking ill, either morally or grammatically.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A Brahman who has past the proper time of life, without receiving the initiatory Mantra, the investiture of the thread, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, दुष्ट bad, faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवता
वाग्देवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 VṚHASPATI.<BR>2 An eloquent man or writer.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवी
वाग्देवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, and देवी goddess, the goddess of eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दोष|वाग्दोषः
वाग्दोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Speaking ill, defamation, abuse.<BR>2 Ungrammatical speech.<BR>3 Uttering a disagreeable sound.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्बन्धन|वाग्बंधन
वाग्बन्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Silencing, stopping any one's speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and वन्धन obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मिन्
वाग्मिन्<BR>mfn. (-ग्मी-ग्मिनी-ग्मि)<BR>1 Loquacious, talkative, speaking much.<BR>2 Speaking well, eloquent.<BR>m. (-ग्मी)<BR>A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, ग्मिनि aff.; hence also वागिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मूल
वाग्मूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Having root or origin in speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मात्र
वाग्मात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Mere speech, words alone.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्य|वाग्यः
वाग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>1 Speaking little, and cautiously or humbly.<BR>2 Speaking truly.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>1 Humility, self-disparagement.<BR>2 Doubt, alternative (?)<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यत|वाग्यतः
वाग्यत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reserved in speech, taciturn, silent.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and यत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यतस्
वाग्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Silently.<BR>E.<BR>वाग्य speaking little, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्याम|वाग्यामः
वाग्याम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A dumb man, one silent from necessity.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, यम to restrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विनिःसृत
वाग्विनिःसृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Emitted or put forth by speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्, and विनिःसृत issued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विलास|वाग्विलासः
वाग्विलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Graceful or elegant speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and विलास sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्यापार|वाग्व्यापारः
वाग्व्यापार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Manner, style or habit of speaking.<BR>2 Customary phraseology.<BR>E.<BR>वाक्, and व्यापार usual practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क|वांक|वांकः|वाङ्कः
वाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The ocean, the sea.<BR>E.<BR>वङ्क a bend or creek, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मय|वाङ्मयं
वाङ्मय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Eloquent, rhetorical.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 Eloquence.<BR>2 Rhetorical composition, rhetoric, belles lettres.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>वाक् speech, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मुख|वाङ्मुखं
वाङ्मुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The opening of a speech, an exordium.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, मुख principal or beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्
वाच्<BR>f. (-वाक्,)<BR>1 Speech.<BR>2 Speaking.<BR>3 SARASVATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>4 A phrase, a proverb or adage.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच|वाचं|वाचः
वाच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A plant: see मदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचंयम|वाचंयमः
वाचंयम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A holy sage, practising rigid taciturnity, devoid of passions, and unmoved by pain or pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, यम to restrain, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक|वाचकः
वाचक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Declaratory, explaining, speaking.<BR>2 Verbal, expressed by words.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A word, a significant sound.<BR>2 A speaker.<BR>3 A messenger.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकता
वाचकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Expressiveness, significance.<BR>E.<BR>वाचक, and तल् aff.; also वाचकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकपद
वाचकपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A clear and explicit term.<BR>E.<BR>वाचक, and पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनिक
वाचनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Verbal.<BR>2 Textual.<BR>E.<BR>वचन, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचसाम्पति|वाचसांपति|वाचसाम्पतिः
वाचसाम्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, regent of the planet JUPITER, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, in the second case pural, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पति|वाचस्पतिः
वाचस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>VṚHASPATI: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, in the sixth case, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचा
वाचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>Speech.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् as above, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाट|वाचाटः
वाचाट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Talkative, talking much and idly or blamably.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, आटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाल|वाचालः
वाचाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Talkative, chattering, gabbling, talking much and idly or blamably.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, and आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिक|वाचिकं|वाचिकः
वाचिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Verbal.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>News, tidings, intelligence.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकपत्र|वाचिकपत्रं
वाचिकपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 A letter, a despatch.<BR>2 A newspaper, a gazette.<BR>E.<BR>वाचिक news, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकहारक|वाचिकहारकः
वाचिकहारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A letter, an epistle.<BR>2 A messenger, a courier.<BR>E.<BR>वाचिक news, हृ to convey, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्ति|वाचोयुक्तिः
वाचोयुक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति)<BR>Speaking much or well.<BR>E.<BR>वाच् speech in the sixth case, and युक्ति joining, fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्तिपटु|वाचोयुक्तिपटुः
वाचोयुक्तिपटु<BR>m. (-टुः-टुः or -ट्वी-टु)<BR>Eloquent, speaking much or well.<BR>E.<BR>वाचोयुक्ति as above, and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्छ|वाछ
वाच्छ<BR>(इ) वाच्छि r. 1st cl. (वाच्छति)<BR>To wish or desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्य|वाच्यं
वाच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 Vile, bad.<BR>2 Vile, contemptible, low, outcast.<BR>3 Fit or proper to be spoken or said.<BR>4 Attributive, adjective, to be predicated of any thing.<BR>5 Declinable as an [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">Page748</a>] adjective, taking the three genders.<BR>n. (-च्यं)<BR>1 Blame, reviling.<BR>2 A predicate, that which may be said of any thing.<BR>3 (In grammar,) The voice or mode of a verb: कर्त्तृवाच्यं the active voice, कर्म्मणिवाच्यं the passive voice.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=747" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यता
वाच्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Infamy, ill repute.<BR>2 Blame, reproach.<BR>3 The quality of that which may be said of any thing.<BR>4 Conjugation.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, वाच्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाज|वाजं|वाजः
वाज<BR>mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>A wing.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 The feather of an arrow.<BR>2 Speed.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>4 A Muni.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A Mantra or prayer which concludes a sacrifice.<BR>4 Rice offered at a Śrāddha or obsequial ceremony.<BR>5 Rice in general.<BR>5 The acidulous mixture of ground meal and water left to ferment.<BR>E.<BR>वज to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजपेय|वाजपेयं|वाजपेयः
वाजपेय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>A particular sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>वाज the acetous fermentation of meal and water, and पेय to be drank, (by the gods.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजभोजिन्
वाजभोजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A particular sacrifice: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>वाज sour gruel, भुज to eat, aff. णिनि, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिगन्ध|वाजिगन्धः
वाजिगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The name of a plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वाजिन् a horse, and गन्ध smell; also वाजिगन्धक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिता
वाजिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The condition of having wings.<BR>2 The nature of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>वाजिन् a horse, &c., तल् aff.; also with त्व, वाजित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिदन्त|वाजिदन्तः
वाजिदन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>E.<BR>वाजि a horse, and दन्त a tooth, to which the flower is compared; also with कन् added, वाजिदन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन्
वाजिन्<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A bird.<BR>4 A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>f. (-जिनी)<BR>A mare.<BR>E.<BR>वाज speed or a feather, &c., and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन|वाजिनं
वाजिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Curd of two milk whey, or the whey from which the curds have been separated.<BR>E.<BR>वज to prepare, aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिपृष्ठ|वाजिपृष्ठः
वाजिपृष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>Globe amaranth.<BR>E.<BR>वाजि a horse, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभूमि|वाजिभूमिः
वाजिभूमि<BR>f. (-मिः)<BR>Place where horses are bred.<BR>E.<BR>वाजिन्, and भूमि place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिशाला
वाजिशाला<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A stable.<BR>E.<BR>वाजि a horse, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकर
वाजीकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Aphrodisiac.<BR>E.<BR>वाजिन् a horse, कर what makes, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकरण|वाजीकरणं
वाजीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Stimulus or excitement of amorous desires by aphrodisiacs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वाजि a horse, करण making, and च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छत्
वाञ्छत्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्छन्-ञ्छन्ती-ञ्छत्)<BR>Wishing, desiring.<BR>E.<BR>वाछि to wish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छन|वांछन|वांछनं
वाञ्छन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Desiring, wishing.<BR>E.<BR>वाछि to desire, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छनीय
वाञ्छनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Desirable, to be wished for.<BR>E.<BR>वाछि to wish, and अनीयर् aff.; also वाञ्छितव्य and वाच्छ्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छा|वांछा
वाञ्छा<BR>f. (-ञ्छा)<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्छि to wish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छित|वांछित|वाञ्छितं
वाञ्छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>वाच्छि to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिन्|वांछिन्
वाञ्छिन्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्छी-ञ्छिनी-ञ्छि)<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR>f. (-ञ्छिनी)<BR>A libidinous woman, a wanton.<BR>E.<BR>वाञ्छा desire, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्
वाट्<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation on making an offering of boiled butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट|वाटं|वाटः
वाट<BR>mfn. adj. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>Made of the Indian fig tree, of its wood, &c.<BR>subst. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>1 An enclosure, a piece of enclosed ground, whether a simple enclosure, as a courtyard, or one for trees and plants, as an orchard, a garden, a plantation, &c.<BR>2 A road.<BR>3 A mud wall, a bound hedge or any enclosure of a town or village, &c.<BR>4 A sort of grain, (Panicum spicatum.)<BR>5 The groin.<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>1 The site of a house or building.<BR>2 A house, a dwelling.<BR>3 A plant: see वाट्यालक.<BR>E.<BR>वट to surround, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटधान|वाटधानः
वाटधान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The descendant of an outcast Brahman by a Brahman female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटशृङ्खला
वाटशृङ्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of chain enclosure or fence (?).<BR>E.<BR>वाट an enclosure, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिका
वाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The site of a house.<BR>2 A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>3 A garden, an orchard.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to वाटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिदीर्घ
वाटिदीर्घ<BR>m. (-र्घः)<BR>A sort of grass, commonly Icadā.<BR>E.<BR>वाटी an enclosure, दीर्घ long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्टक|वाट्टकं
वाट्टक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fried barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्य|वाट्यः
वाट्य<BR>mfn. (-ट्यः-ट्या-ट्यं)<BR>Belonging to a house or garden, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वाटी, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यपुष्प
वाट्यपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Sandal.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>वाट्य belonging to a house or garden, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्या
वाट्या<BR>f. (-ट्या)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>वाटी a garden, यत् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्याल|वाट्यालः
वाट्याल<BR>mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>A herbaceous shrub, (Sida cordifolia): see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यालक|वाट्यालकः
वाट्यालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bariyāla, (Sida cordifolia).<BR>E.<BR>वाटी a garden, in the sixth case, अल to adorn, with अण् aff., and कन् added, the ornament of a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाड|वाडः
वाड<BR>(ऋ) वाडृ r. 1st cl. (वाडते)<BR>To bathe, to dive and emerge: the best authorities read this बाडृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवेय|वाडवेयः
वाडवेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढ
वाढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Much, abundant, exceeding.<BR>2 Hard, firm.<BR>adv. n. or ind. (-ढं)<BR>1 Much, excessive, excessively.<BR>2 Very well, well, (assent, promise.)<BR>3 A particle signifying conclusion, deduction.<BR>E.<BR>वह to take, to bear, aff. क्त, and the form. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढविक्रम
वाढविक्रम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Powerful, very strong, mighty.<BR>E.<BR>वाढ, and विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाण|वाणः
वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A name of fire.<BR>3 The name of a sovereign considered also as an Asura or infernal being, the son of BĀLĪ, and destroyed by VIṢṆU.<BR>4 The udder of a cow.<BR>5 Alone, solitary.<BR>6 A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>1 Blue Barleria.<BR>2 The root or feathered part of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>वण or बण to sound or go, aff. घञ्; whence this word and other derivatives are sometimes also written with an initial ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणदण्ड|वाणदण्डः
वाणदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A weaver's loom.<BR>E.<BR>वाण an arrow, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणनिकृत
वाणनिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pierced, wounded by an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>वाण, and निकृत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणपाणि
वाणपाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>Armed with arrows.<BR>E.<BR>वाण, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=748" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणपुर|वाणपुरं
वाणपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The capital of VĀṆA Rāja.<BR>E.<BR>वाण, and पुर city; also with the final consonant वाणपुर्. f. (-पूः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणमोक्षण
वाणमोक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Shooting an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>वाण, and मोक्षण letting fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणवार|वाणवारः
वाणवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Armour.<BR>2 A breastplate, a cuirass.<BR>E.<BR>वाण an arrow, वृ to cover or screen, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणसुता
वाणसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>UṢĀ, the daughter of VĀṆA, and wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>वाण, and सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणहन्
वाणहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वाण VĀṆA Rāja, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणारि|वाणारिः
वाणारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वाण the demon, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणाश्रय|वाणाश्रयः
वाणाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>वाण an arrow, and आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणासन|वाणासनं
वाणासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>वाण an arrow, असन throwing, or आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणि|वाणिः
वाणि<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>1 Weaving.<BR>2 A species of the Aṣṭī metre.<BR>E.<BR>वण to sound, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज्य|वाणिज्यं
वाणिज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>Traffic, trade: see वाणिज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिन्
वाणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>1 Having an arrow.<BR>2 Speaking.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A sharp or clever woman, an intriguing woman.<BR>2 An actress, a dancer, a Nāc girl.<BR>3 A furious woman, one literally or figuratively intoxicated.<BR>E.<BR>वाण an arrow, or वाणि speech, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणी
वाणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 SARASVATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>2 Speech, sound.<BR>E.<BR>वण to sound, aff. इञ्, and ङीप् or ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात<BR>r. 1st cl. (वातयति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To serve.<BR>3 To be happy.<BR>4 To give pleasure in travelling.<BR>5 To blow gently, to fan or ventilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
वात्<BR>mfn. (वान् वाती वान्ती वात्)<BR>Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 Rheumatism, gout, inflammation of the joints.<BR>2 Air, wind, as one of the humours of the body.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, Uṇādi aff. तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातक|वातकः
वातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, कृ to make, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकिन्
वातकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Rheumatic, gouty.<BR>E.<BR>वात inflammation of the joints, and इनि aff., कूक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुण्डलिका|वातकुंडलिका
वातकुण्डलिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Scanty and painful flow of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुम्भ|वातकुंभ|वातकुम्भः
वातकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The part of an elephant's forehead below the frontal sinuses.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and कुम्भ a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेतु|वातकेतुः
वातकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Dust.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and केतु a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेलि|वातकेलिः
वातकेलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>1 Speaking in murmurs, especially amorous converse.<BR>2 The marks of finger nails on the lover's person.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, केलि playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगामिन्
वातगामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगुल्म|वातगुल्मः
वातगुल्म<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>1 A gale, a high wind.<BR>2 Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, गुल्म a cluster, a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातग्रस्त
वातग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Epileptic.<BR>2 Rheumatic.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातघ्न
वातघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing disorders from wind.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and घ्न who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातज
वातज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced by or arising from wind.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातज्वर|वातज्वरः
वातज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Fever arising from vitiated wind.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाततूल|वाततूलं
वाततूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cottony flocks or seeds floating in the air.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, तूल cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातथुडा
वातथुडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>1 A gale, a high wind.<BR>2 Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR>3 A handsome woman.<BR>4 A disease, a sort of small pox.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, हुड to reap, aff. क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातध्वज|वातध्वजः
वातध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and ध्वज banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपित्त
वातपित्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Rheumatism attended with fever.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and पित्त bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपुत्त्र
वातपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪMA.<BR>2 The monkey HANUMĀN.<BR>3 A cheat, a swindler.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपोथ|वातपोथः
वातपोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वात rheumatism, पुथ to hurt, aff. अण्; also वातपोथक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातप्रमी
वातप्रमी<BR>m. (-मीः)<BR>A swift antelope.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, प्र before मा to measure, to surpass or outgo, Uṇādi aff. ईप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातफुल्ल
वातफुल्ल<BR>mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>Inflated, puffed up with wind.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and फुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातफुल्लान्त्र|वातफुल्लान्त्रं
वातफुल्लान्त्र<BR>n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>Cholic, flatulence, borborygmi.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, फुल्ल swoln, अन्त्र the intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमज|वातमजः
वातमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Going in or against the wind.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An antelope.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, अज to go, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमण्डली|वातमंडली
वातमण्डली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A whirlwind.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, मण्डल a region, aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमृग|वातमृगः
वातमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A swift antelope.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरंहस्
वातरंहस्<BR>mfn. (-हाः-हाः-हः)<BR>Swift, (as the wind.)<BR>E.<BR>वात, and रंहस् speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर
वातर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Windy, stormy.<BR>2 Swift, (as the wind.)<BR>E.<BR>वात, रा to get, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्त|वातरक्तं
वातरक्त<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and रक्त blood; ascribed to a vitiated state of the blood and the aerial humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्तघ्न|वातरक्तघ्नः
वातरक्तघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>A plant, commonly Kukurmurā.<BR>E.<BR>वातरक्त gout, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्तारि|वातरक्तारिः
वातरक्तारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>वातरक्त acute gout, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरथ|वातरथः
वातरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरायण|वातरायणः
वातरायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 An arrow's flight, the discharge of an arrow, a bow shot.<BR>3 A saw.<BR>4 The peak of a mountain.<BR>5 A mad man, one wild or intoxicated, either literally or figuratively.<BR>6 An idler, one who lives to no purpose.<BR>7 The Saral, a sort of pine tree.<BR>E.<BR>वातर, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरूष|वातरूषः
वातरूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A gale, a breeze.<BR>2 The rainbow.<BR>3 A bribe.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, रूष to rage, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरोग|वातरोगः
वातरोग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Rheumatism, gout.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरोगिन्
वातरोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Rheumatic, afflicted with gout or rheumatism, especially of the acute kind.<BR>E.<BR>वातरोग acute rheumatism, &c., aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर्द्धि
वातर्द्धि<BR>m. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>1 A sort of cup or vessel made of wood, with an iron foot or stand.<BR>2 A mace, a club or stick bound with iron.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, ऋद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातल|वातलः
वातल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Windy, stormy.<BR>2 Flatulent.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of pulse, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>2 Wind.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A morbid state of the uterus.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, ला to get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातलमण्डली
वातलमण्डली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A whirlwind.<BR>E.<BR>वातल windy, मण्डल a region, aff. ङीप्; also वातमण्डली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=749" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवत्|वातवन्त्
वातवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Windy, gusty.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवलासक
वातवलासक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Nervous or low fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवस्ति|वातवस्तिः
वातवस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>Suppression of urine.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and वस्ति the bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवृद्धि|वातवृद्धिः
वातवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Swelled testicle.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातव्याधि|वातव्याधिः
वातव्याधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Any morbid affection attributed to disorder of the wind.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and व्याधि disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवैरिन्
वातवैरिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>The castor oil tree, &c.; see वातारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशीर्ष|वातशीर्षं
वातशीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The lower belly.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, शीर्ष the head or source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशूल
वातशूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cholic with flatulence.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and शूल cholic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशोणित|वातशोणितं
वातशोणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, शोणित blood; ascribed to a vitiated state of these two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातसह|वातसहः
वातसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Gouty, rheumatic.<BR>E.<BR>वात the disease, and सह bearing, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातसारथि|वातसारथिः
वातसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, and सारथि charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातस्कन्ध|वातस्कन्धः
वातस्कन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>The portion of the atmosphere where the wind blows.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, स्कन्ध part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताट|वाताटः
वाताट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A horse of the sun.<BR>2 An antelope.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातानुलोमन
वातानुलोमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Forcing the wind downwards, as in inflating the lungs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातापि|वातापिः
वातापि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>The name of an Asura devoured by AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, पा to drink, aff. कि, and आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातापिद्विष्
वातापिद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>The Muni AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>वातापि, and द्विष who hates; also similar names, as वातापिसूदन, बातापिहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातामोदा
वातामोदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Musk.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, आमोदा a diffusive fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताय
वाताय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A leaf.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, अय to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायन|वातायनं|वातायनः
वातायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A window, an eyelet or loop-hole.<BR>2 A porch, a portico, a covered shed, a pavilion.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायु|वातायुः
वातायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>An antelope, a deer.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, (like,) अय to go, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातारि|वातारिः
वातारि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 The castor oil tree.<BR>2 A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>वात rheumatism, अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताली
वाताली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A whirlwind, a gale.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताश्व|वाताश्वः
वाताश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A swift horse, or one of a good breed.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातासह|वातासहः
वातासह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Rheumatic, gouty.<BR>E.<BR>बात rheumatism, and आसह who bears or suffers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहत
वाताहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stirred or shaken by the wind.<BR>2 Affected by rheumatism.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहति|वाताहतिः
वाताहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 The action of the wind.<BR>2 The occurrence of arthritic pains.<BR>E.<BR>वात, and आहति striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाति|वातिः
वाति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, Uṇādi aff. अति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिक|वातिकः
वातिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Windy, stormy.<BR>2 Rheumatic.<BR>3 Produced by or proceeding from wind, (disease, &c.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Fever or inflammation ascribed to a vitiated state of the aerial humour.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, &c., ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिग|वातिगः
वातिग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Acquainted with or working in minerals or fossils, &c.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>वाति wind, and ग who counts, from गण with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिङ्गण|वातिंगण|वातिङ्गणः
वातिङ्गण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The egg-plant.<BR>E.<BR>वाति wind, गण to count, aff. खच्, curing rheumatism, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातीय|वातीयं
वातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Windy, relating or belonging to wind, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Sour rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>वात the wind, छ aff.; acidulated by air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुल|वातुलः
वातुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Gouty, rheumatic.<BR>2 Mad, crazy.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A whirlwind, a gale.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, &c., and उलच् aff.; more commonly वातूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुलि|वातुलिः
वातुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>A large bat, commonly the flying-fox.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, उलि aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातूल|वातूलः
वातूल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Gouty, rheumatic.<BR>2 Mad, insane, inebriate.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A whirlwind, a gale, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, ऊलच् aff.; also वातुल; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातृ
वातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्या
वात्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>Strong wind, a gale, a whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>वात wind, यत् implying quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सक|वात्सकं
वात्सक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A herd of calves.<BR>E.<BR>वत्स a calf, वुञ् aff. of number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सल्य|वात्सल्यं|वात्सल्यः
वात्सल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Tenderness, affection, fondness.<BR>E.<BR>वत्सल affectionate, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सीपुत्त्र
वात्सीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>वात्सी a girl born of a Śūdra woman by a Brahman, and पुत्त्र son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्यायन|वात्स्यायनः
वात्स्यायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The name of a Muni.<BR>E.<BR>वात्स्य the father of the sage, and फक् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद|वादः
वाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Demonstrated conclusion, reply, result.<BR>2 Discourse, discussion, defined as the speech of one desirous to know the truth.<BR>3 A plaint, an accusation.<BR>4 Sound, sounding.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादकर
वादकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Causing or making a dispute.<BR>E.<BR>वाद, and कर what makes; also वादकृत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादन|वादनं|वादनः
वादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sound, sounding, (as musical instruments.)<BR>E.<BR>वद to sound, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादयत्
वादयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Sounding, playing, (as on a musical instrument.)<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादयुद्ध
वादयुद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Controversy, dispute.<BR>E.<BR>वाद, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरङ्ग|वादरंग|वादरंगः|वादरङ्गः
वादरङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The religious fig tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरत
वादरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Adhering to or following a doctrine.<BR>2 Addicted to controversy, disputatious.<BR>E.<BR>वाद, and रत fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरायण|वादरायणः
वादरायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A name of VYĀSA, the compiler of the Vedas, and reputed author of the Purāṇas, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वादर a place of pilgrimage, अयन going, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादल|वादलं|वादलः
वादल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Liquorice, or the root of the Abrus precatorius, which is used for it.<BR>E.<BR>वा for वात wind, दल to disperse, aff. अच्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादवादिन्
वादवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A Jaina.<BR>E.<BR>वाद result, truth, and वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादसाधन
वादसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Argument, maintaining a controversy.<BR>E.<BR>वाद, and साधन instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादानुवाद
वादानुवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Attack and rejoinder, plaint and reply.<BR>E.<BR>वाद, and अनुवाद subsequent dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादान्य|वादान्यः
वादान्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Munificent, liberal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वदान्य, and अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादाल|वादालः
वादाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sheat fish.<BR>E.<BR>वदाल the same, अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=750" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादि|वादिः
वादि<BR>mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि)<BR>Wise, learned, skilful, sage.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, (wisely, &c.,) इञ् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित्र|वादित्रं
वादित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>वद to sound, Uṇādi aff. णित्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिन्
वादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Speaking, discoursing.<BR>2 Asserting, declaring.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A sage, an expounder of the law and the Śāstras.<BR>2 A plaintiff, an accuser.<BR>3 Leading or key note, (in music.)<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिराज्
वादिराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>A Bauddha sage; also MAÑJUGHOṢA.<BR>E.<BR>वादि a sage, and राज् chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिश|वादिशः
वादिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A learned and virtuous man, a sage, a seer.<BR>E.<BR>वादि truth or true conclusion, and इशच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्य|वाद्यं|वाद्यः
वाद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>Any musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>वद to sound, aff. ण्यत्; to be sounded or played.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यनिर्घोष
वाद्यनिर्घोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>The sound of musical instruments.<BR>E.<BR>वाद्य a musical instrument, and निर्घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यभाण्ड|वाद्यभांड|वाद्यभाण्डं
वाद्यभाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>1 A multitude of musical instruments, a band.<BR>2 Any musical instrument.<BR>E.<BR>वाद्य a musical instrument, and भाण्ड assemblage or vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध|वाधः
वाध<BR>(ऋ) ऐवाधृ r. 1st cl. (वाधते)<BR>To distress, to give pain: more correctly बाध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधुक्य|वाधुक्यं
वाधुक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>वधुका a wife, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधू
वाधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>A vessel, a boat, a raft.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. ऊण्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान<BR>mfn. subst. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Dry fruit.<BR>adj.<BR>Dry, dried.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Living.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>3 A mat of straw.<BR>4 A heavy sea, the rolling of water from wind, &c.; hence the high tide in the Indian rivers, commonly called the Bore.<BR>5 A hole in the wall of a house.<BR>6 A perfume, a fragrance.<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating to a wood, a house, &c.: see वन.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A number or multitude of woods.<BR>E.<BR>वै to dry or wither, aff. क्त; form irr.: in other of its applications वन to sound, aff. घञ्; or वन a wood, water, a house, &c., and अण् referential aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानप्रस्थ|वानप्रस्थः
वानप्रस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>1 The Brahman of the third order, who has passed through the conditions of student and householder, and has left his house and family for lonely meditation in woods and wilds; the hermit, the anchoret.<BR>2 A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>3 The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, अण् aff., वान a solitude in the woods, &c., प्रस्थ who goes forth to, from स्था to stay, with प्र prefix, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानर|वानरः
वानर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>An ape, a monkey.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>वात what relates to a wood, रा to get, aff. क, a Sylvan; or वा implying resemblance, and नर a man, or वन a wood, रत to play, aff. ड, वनर, and अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानरप्रिय|वानरप्रियः
वानरप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A tree, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वानर a monkey, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानराघात|वानराघातः
वानराघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree, commonly Lodh, (Symplocos racemosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वीनर a monkey, आघात struck, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानरेन्द्र|वानरेंद्र|वानरेन्द्रः
वानरेन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>1 The monkey chief, SUGRĪVA.<BR>2 HANUMĀN.<BR>E.<BR>वानर, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानल|वानलः
वानल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A kind of holy basil, distinguished as the black species of Tulasī, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानस्पत्य|वानस्पत्यः
वानस्पत्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A tree bearing fruits from blossoms, as the mango, eugenia, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वनस्पति a tree bearing fruits without blossoms, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायु|वानायुः
वानायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A country to the north-west of India; also वनायु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायुज|वानायुजः
वानायुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A Vānāyu horse, considered as one of a particularly good breed.<BR>E.<BR>वनायु, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीर|वानीरः
वानीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of cane or ratan, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>वन water, ईर aff., and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेय|वानेयं
वानेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to water, &c.<BR>m. (यः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>वन water, ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त|वांत|वान्तः
वान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Vomited, ejected from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>वन to vomit, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ताद|वांताद|वान्तादः
वान्ताद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वान्त what is ejected from the mouth, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ति|वांति|वान्तिः
वान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Vomiting, ejecting from the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>वम to vomit, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिकृत्
वान्तिकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Emetic.<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A thorny plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वान्ति vomiting, and कृत् what makes; an emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिद
वान्तिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Emetic.<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Katiuki, (Wrightea antidysenterica; and Colotropis gigantea, BROWN.)<BR>E.<BR>वान्ति vomiting, and द what produces; an emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>A multitude of groves or thickets.<BR>E.<BR>वन a wood, यञ् aff. of multitude; also with यत् aff. वन्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप|वापः
वाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Shaving.<BR>2 Sowing seed.<BR>3 Weaving.<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow seed, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापदण्ड|वापदंड|वापदण्डः
वापदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A weaver's loom.<BR>E.<BR>वाप weaving, दण्ड a stick; also वायदण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापि|वापिः
वापि<BR>f. (-पिः or -पी)<BR>A large oblong pond, a pool, a lake.<BR>E.<BR>वप, to sow seed, (of the lotus, &c.) Uṇādi aff. इञ्, and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापित|वापितं
वापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sown as seed.<BR>2 Shaven.<BR>E.<BR>वाप shaving, &c., इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापीह|वापीहः
वापीह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Cātaka, a bird, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>वापी a pool, हां to abandon, aff. क; drinking rain water only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप्य|वाप्यं
वाप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be sown, what may or ought to be sown.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>वप to sow, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Left, not right.<BR>2 Reverse, contrary, inverted.<BR>3 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>4 Vile, base, wicked.<BR>5 Short.<BR>6 Crooked.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>3 An udder, a breast.<BR>4 A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>5 An animal, a sentient being.<BR>6 A snake.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Wealth, possessions.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 GAURĪ.<BR>3 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>4 SARASVATĪ.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 A mare.<BR>2 A she-ass.<BR>3 A young female elephant.<BR>4 The female of the jackal.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, Uṇādi aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामता
वामता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Perverseness, contrariety.<BR>2 Craftiness, wickedness.<BR>3 Loveliness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to वाम; also with त्व, वामत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामदेव|वामदेवः
वामदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वाम contrary, (to human institutions,) देव who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Short, dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>2 Depressed, pressed flat or down.<BR>3 Low, vile, base.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU in his character of the dwarf, in which he appeared on his fifth [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">Page752</a>] descent from heaven, to prevent BALI from obtaining dominion of the three worlds.<BR>2 The elephant that supports the south quarter.<BR>3 A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>f. (नी)<BR>1 A female dwarf.<BR>2 A sort of woman; also वामनिका.<BR>3 A disease of the vagina.<BR>E.<BR>वम to eject from the mouth, and ल्यु or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=751" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनीकृत
वामनीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shortened, flattened.<BR>E.<BR>वामन, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूर|वामलूरः
वामलूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ant or mole hill, especially the hillocks of ground thrown up by the white ant.<BR>E.<BR>वाम inverted, reversed, लू to cut, aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलोचन
वामलोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fine-eyed.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>वाम beautiful, and लोचन eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाक्षी
वामाक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>वाम beautiful, and अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाचार|वामाचारः
वामाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The doctrine of the Tantras according to one system.<BR>E.<BR>वाम left, and आचार institute; the left hand ritual, the use of flesh, spirits, &c. forming part of the Vāmācāra ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाचारिन्
वामाचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A follower of the left hand portion of the Tantras.<BR>E.<BR>वामाचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामापीडन|वामापीडनः
वामापीडन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Salvadora Persica, &c.): see पीलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामावर्त्त|वामावर्त|वामावर्तः
वामावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A conch shell with the spiral turn running from right to left.<BR>E.<BR>वाम, and आवर्त्त a turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिल|वामिलः
वामिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Proud, haughty, intolerant.<BR>2 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>E.<BR>वम to eject from the mouth, (the faults of others,) aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय|वायः
वाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Weaving.<BR>E.<BR>वे to weave, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायक|वायकः
वायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A number, a multitude, a heap.<BR>E.<BR>बय to go ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायदण्ड|वायदंड|वायदण्डः
वायदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A weaver's loom.<BR>E.<BR>वाय weaving, दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायन|वायनं
वायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sweetmeats or cakes, forming a light refreshment, which is not supposed to be any breach of a religious fast.<BR>2 Sweetmeats or cakes, part of an offering to a deity, or prepared on particular occasions, as marriages, &c. and sent as presents to friends and acquaintances.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, ल्युट् aff.; also with कन् added, वायनक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Windy, relating or belonging to wind.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The quarter or region of the wind; the northwest<BR>E.<BR>वायु air, wind, and अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव्य|वायव्यं
वायव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>Relating to the wind, sacred to the deity of the wind, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायस|वायसः
वायस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A crow.<BR>2 Agallochum, (Amyris Agallocha.)<BR>3 Turpentine.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>1 A species of fig, (Ficus oppositifolia, Rox.)<BR>4 A vegetable, (Solanum Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>वय to go, Uṇādi aff. असच्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसाराति|वायसारातिः
वायसाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An owl.<BR>E.<BR>वायस a crow, and अराति an enemy; also similar compounds, as वायसारि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसेक्षु|वायसेक्षुः
वायसेक्षु<BR>m. (-क्षुः)<BR>A sort of long grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR>E.<BR>वायस a crow, and इक्षु the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसोली
वायसोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>E.<BR>वायस a crow, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायु|वायुः
वायु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>1 Air, wind, or its personified deification.<BR>2 The air of the body.<BR>3 Morbid affection of the windy humour.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, उण् Uṇādi aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुकेतु|वायुकेतुः
वायुकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Dust.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and केतु a symbol, a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुकोण|वायुकोणः
वायुकोण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The north-west.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and कोण corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगण्ड|वायुगंड|वायुगण्डः
वायुगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>Flatulence, indigestion.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, गडि to be a part of, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगति
वायुगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Quick, swift, as the wind.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगुल्म|वायुगुल्मः
वायुगुल्म<BR>m. (-ल्मः)<BR>1 A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR>2 A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and गुल्म a cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुग्रस्त
वायुग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Affected by wind, flatulent, epileptic.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुघ्न
वायुघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Destroying or curing windy disorders.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुजात|वायुजातः
वायुजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>HANUMAN.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुदारु|वायुदारुः
वायुदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, दृ to scatter, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुनिवृत्ति|वायुनिवृत्तिः
वायुनिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Calm, lull.<BR>2 Cure of windy disorders.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and निवृत्ति stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुपुत्त्र
वायुपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A name of BHĪMA.<BR>2 A name of HANUMAN.<BR>E.<BR>वायु the god of wind, and पुत्त्र a son; also similar compounds, as वायुतनय, वायुनन्दन, वायुसुत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुफल|वायुफलं
वायुफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The rainbow.<BR>2 Hail.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्ष|वायुभक्षः
वायुभक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Eating air, fasting.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 An ascetic.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्षण|वायुभक्षणः
वायुभक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Fasting, living on air.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभूत
वायुभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Becoming as the wind, going every where at will.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुरोषा
वायुरोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, रुष् to rage, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवर्त्मन्
वायुवर्त्मन्<BR>m. (-र्त्मा)<BR>The atmosphere, sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and वर्त्मन् path or road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवाह|वायुवाहः
वायुवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Smoke, vapour.<BR>E.<BR>वायु the wind, and वाह vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवाहिनी
वायुवाहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A vessel of the body, supposed, as the arteries were once imagined, to convey the aerial humour.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, वाहिनी bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवेगसम
वायुवेगसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Swift as the wind.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, वेग speed, सम equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसख|वायुसखः
वायुसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, and सखि friend, aff. टच्; also without the aff. वायुसखि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसम्भव
वायुसम्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>HANUMAN.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसम
वायुसम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Like wind, unsubstantial.<BR>2 Swift.<BR>E.<BR>वायु, and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय्वास्पद|वाय्वास्पदं
वाय्वास्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Ether, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>वायु wind, आस्पद place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्
वार्<BR>n. (-वाः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to surround, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार|वारं|वारः
वार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A multitude, a quantity, a flock or herd, a heap.<BR>2 Occasion, opportunity.<BR>3 A day of the week.<BR>4 A moment.<BR>5 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>6 A door-way, a gate.<BR>7 Achyranthes aspera.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A vessel for holding spirituous liquor.<BR>adv.<BR>A time, as वारं वारं many a time, repeatedly, often: see वारम्बारं.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, to choose, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारक|वारकं|वारकः
वारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Opposing, obstructing, an obstacle or agent of resistance.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A horse's paces.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The seat of pain.<BR>2 A sort of fragrant grass: see वाल.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, &c., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=752" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकिन्
वारकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>2 A horse with good marks.<BR>3 An enemy.<BR>4 An ascetic, one living upon leaves, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वारक an obstacle, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकीर|वारकीरः
वारकीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A wife's brother.<BR>2 Marine fire.<BR>3 A louse.<BR>4 A small comb.<BR>5 A horse of high spirit, a war horse, a charger.<BR>6 A bearer of burthens, a porter.<BR>E.<BR>वार् an obstacle, कॄ to scatter, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्क|वारंक|वारंकः|वारङ्कः
वारङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>वार water, अकि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्ग|वारंग|वारंगः|वारङ्गः
वारङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The handle of a sword or knife, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to select, aff. अङ्गच्, and the radical vowel changed to the Vṛddhi form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारट|वारटं
वारट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>1 A field.<BR>2 A number of fields.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A goose; also वरटा.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, अट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारण|वारणं|वारणः
वारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Resistance, opposition, prohibition, obstacle or impediment.<BR>2 Defence, protecting, guarding.<BR>3 Warding off a blow, guarding, warding.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Armour, a cuirass, or mail for the body.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वॄ to cover or screen, to defend, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणबुषा
वारणबुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The plantain or banana, (Musa sapientum.)<BR>E.<BR>वारण an elephant, बुष or बुस to cast off, aff. क; hence it is written also वारणबुसा; also वारवुषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणवल्लभा
वारणवल्लभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The plantain tree.<BR>E.<BR>वारण an elephant, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारत्र|वारत्रं
वारत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Leather fit for or made into thongs.<BR>E.<BR>वारत्रा a thong, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारनारी
वारनारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A harlot.<BR>E.<BR>वार, and नारी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारबुषा
वारबुषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A Banana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारमुख्या
वारमुख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>The head of a set of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वार a troop, and मुख्या a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारम्वारम्
वारम्वारम्<BR>ind.<BR>Repeatedly, again and again.<BR>E.<BR>वार a day, a time, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A wasp.<BR>2 A goose.<BR>E.<BR>वार a flock, a flight, ला to get, and क and टाप् aff.; also वरला, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवधू
वारवधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>The chief of a set of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वार a number, and वधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवाण|वारवाणः
वारवाण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>Armour for the body or breast, an iron cuirass, or a thick quilted jacket worn for the same purpose.<BR>E.<BR>वार opposing, वाण an arrow; also वाणवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवाणि|वारवाणिः
वारवाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 A player on the flute.<BR>2 A singer, a musician.<BR>3 A judge.<BR>4 A year.<BR>f. (-णिः or -णी)<BR>1 The chief of a set of harlots.<BR>2 A whore.<BR>E.<BR>वार a multitude, वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारविलासिनी
वारविलासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A harlot, a whore.<BR>E.<BR>वार a multitude, and विलासिनी a wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवेला
वारवेला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A portion of the day in which any act religious or secular is suspended.<BR>E.<BR>वार, and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारसुन्दरी|वारसुंदरी
वारसुन्दरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A whore, a prostitute.<BR>E.<BR>वार the multitude, सुन्दरी a beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारसेवा
वारसेवा<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A set of courtezans.<BR>2 Prostitution, harlotry.<BR>E.<BR>वार the multitude, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारस्त्री
वारस्त्री<BR>f. (-स्त्री)<BR>A whore.<BR>E.<BR>वार the many, and स्त्री a woman; a common woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारांनिधि
वारांनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वारां of water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराङ्गना|वारांगना
वाराङ्गना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A harlot.<BR>E.<BR>वार, and अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसी
वाराणसी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>The holy city Benares.<BR>E.<BR>वर best, अनस् water, affs. अण् and ङीष्, i. e. the Ganges on which it stands; also वराणसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसेय|वाराणसेयः
वाराणसेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Produced at or born in Benares, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वाराणसी the city, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारासन|वारासनं
वारासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A large water jar, a cistern, a reservoir.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, आसन place of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह|वाराहः
वाराह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Relating to a boar, belonging to, derived from, &c.<BR>f. ही<BR>1 An esculent root, a Yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR>2 One of the divine mothers.<BR>3 A measure.<BR>4 The earth.<BR>5 A sow.<BR>E.<BR>वराह a hog or VIṢṆU, &c., अण् aff., and ङीप् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारि|वारिः
वारि<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A vegetable perfume, commonly Bāla.<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>1 A name of SARASVATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>2 The place where an elephant is tied or fastened.<BR>3 A captive, a prisoner.<BR>f. (-रिः or -री)<BR>1 A water-pot, whether large or small, a pitcher, a jar.<BR>2 The rope that fastens an elephant.<BR>3 A hole or trap for catching elephants.<BR>E.<BR>वृञ् to surround, Uṇādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकण्टक|वारिकण्टकः
वारिकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>2 Another plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and कण्डक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकर्णिका
वारिकर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Pistia stratiotes)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and कर्णिका here meaning leaf or leaflet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकर्पूर|वारिकर्पूरः
वारिकर्पूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Ilīśa fish, (Cluponodon Ilisha, HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and कर्पूर camphor, to which it is compared in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकुब्ज|वारिकुब्जः
वारिकुब्ज<BR>m. (-ब्जः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, कुब्ज Achyranthes; also with कन् added, वारिकुब्जक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिक्रिमि|वारिक्रिमिः
वारिक्रिमि<BR>m. (-मिः)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and क्रिमि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचत्वर|वारिचत्वरः
वारिचत्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>2 A piece of water.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, चत्वर expanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचर|वारिचरः
वारिचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Aquatic, living or moving in water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचामर|वारिचामरं
वारिचामर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of weed, (Vallisneria.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and चामर Chowri or brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिज|वारिजं|वारिजः
वारिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Aquatic, born or produced in or by water.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A conch shell.<BR>2 Any bivalve shell.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 Salt.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित
वारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hindered, prevented, impeded.<BR>E.<BR>वॄ to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारितस्कर|वारितस्करः
वारितस्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, तस्कर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित्रा
वारित्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A sort of umbrella, or portable shed of leaves carried on the head as one.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, त्रा to preserve, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिद|वारिदं|वारिदः
वारिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>What yields water.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A sort of vegetable perfume; see वाल.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and द what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिद्र|वारिद्रः
वारिद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The Cātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, दृ to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिधि|वारिधिः
वारिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The sea.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, धा to contain, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिनाथ|वारिनाथः
वारिनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 The deity VARUṆA.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 A cloud.<BR>4 The habitation of the Nāgas, or serpent race.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=753" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिनिधि|वारिनिधिः
वारिनिधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>The sea, the ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and निधि a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिपथिक|वारिपथिकः
वारिपथिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Proceeding or conveyed by water.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, पथिन् a road, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिपर्णी
वारिपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिप्रवाह|वारिप्रवाहः
वारिप्रवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A cascade, a water-fall.<BR>2 A current or flow of water.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and प्रवाह a fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिप्रश्नी
वारिप्रश्नी<BR>f. (-श्नी)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, प्रश्नि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिबदरा
वारिबदरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, वदर jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिबालक|वारिबालकं
वारिबालक<BR>m. (-कं)<BR>A perfume: see वाल.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, वाल a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमसि|वारिमसिः
वारिमसि<BR>n. (-सिः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, मसि ink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमुच्
वारिमुच्<BR>m. (-मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and मुच् what emits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमूली
वारिमूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिर
वारिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Giving or shedding water.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि, and रा to give, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरथ|वारिरथः
वारिरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A raft, a float.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and रथ a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरारव
वारिरारव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Sounding like clouds or thunder.<BR>E.<BR>वारिर, and आरव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिराशि|वारिराशिः
वारिराशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिलोमन्
वारिलोमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>A name of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवदन|वारिवदनं
वारिवदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and वदन countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवास|वारिवासः
वारिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A distiller or dealer in spirituous liquors.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवाह|वारिवाहः
वारिवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and वाह what bears; also वारिवाहन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवाहन|वारिवाहनः
वारिवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिश|वारिशः
वारिश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, शीङ्^1 to sleep, aff. ड.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: cf root SI in WIL.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीट|वारीटः
वारीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वारि the trap for an elephant, अट to go, aff. अच्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीश|वारीशः
वारीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वार water, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारु|वारुः
वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A war elephant carrying a standard.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, aff. उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुठ|वारुठः
वारुठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>A bier, the bed on which the corpse is carried.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to cover, aff. उठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणि|वारुणिः
वारुणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>वरुण VARUṆA, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणी
वारुणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Any spirituous liquor, or more properly, a particular kind prepared from hogweed, ground with the juice of the date or palm, and then distilled.<BR>2 The west, the region of VARUṆA.<BR>3 The 25th lunar asterism, of which VARUṆA is the ruling deity.<BR>4 A species of Dūrbbā grass.<BR>E.<BR>वरुण the deity VARUṆA, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणीवल्लभ|वारुणीवल्लभः
वारुणीवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वारुणी the asterism, and वल्लभ loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण्ड|वारुंड|वारुंडः|वारुण्डः
वारुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The chief of the serpent race (?).<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्ड)<BR>1 The rheum of the eyes.<BR>2 The wax of the ear.<BR>3 A vessel for baling water out of a boat.<BR>E.<BR>वॄ to screen, aff. उण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेण
वारेण<BR>ind.<BR>Frequently, repeatedly.<BR>E.<BR>वार a time in the third case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेन्द्री|वारेंद्री
वारेन्द्री<BR>f. (-न्द्री)<BR>Part of Bengal and Behar, or a tract of inundation north of the Ganges, and part of the present Zila of Rājṣāhi.<BR>E.<BR>वरेन्द्र a king, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष
वार्क्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्क्षः-र्क्षी-र्क्षं)<BR>Made of or derived from a tree.<BR>n. (-र्क्षं)<BR>A forest.<BR>f. (-र्क्षी)<BR>The name of a female mentioned in the Mahābhārata, a sort of Dryad.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष्य|वार्क्ष्यं
वार्क्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-र्क्ष्यः-र्क्ष्यी-र्क्ष्यं)<BR>Made of or with trees.<BR>n. (-क्ष्य)<BR>A stockade.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्णिक|वार्णिकः
वार्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ण a letter, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त|वार्त|वार्त्तं|वार्त्तः
वार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>1 Well, healthy.<BR>2 Following any business or profession.<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Health.<BR>2 Chaff.<BR>f. (-र्त्ता)<BR>1 Tidings, news, intelligence.<BR>2 Rumour, report.<BR>3 Livelihood, business, profession.<BR>4 Agriculture or trade, the proper occupation of the Vaiśya.<BR>5 Abiding, staying, being.<BR>6 The egg-plant.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति being, &c., aff. अण् or ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताक|वार्ताक|वार्ताकः|वार्त्ताकः
वार्त्ताक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The egg-plant: see वार्त्ताकु, उ being changed to अ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकर्म्मन्|वार्ताकर्मन्
वार्त्ताकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The peculiar occupation of the third or Vaiśya class, agriculture, trade, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वार्त्ता, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकि|वार्ताकि|वार्ताकिः
वार्त्ताकि<BR>f. (-किः or -की)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, काकिन् aff.; ङीप् or इन् fem. aff., form irr.; also वार्त्ताकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकिन्|वार्ताकिन्
वार्त्ताकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>The egg-plant; also वार्त्ताकि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकु|वार्ताकु|वार्ताकुः|वार्त्ताकुः
वार्त्ताकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, काकु Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तायन|वार्तायन|वार्त्तायनः
वार्त्तायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A spy, an emissary, an agent, an embassador, an intelligencer, a newsmonger.<BR>E.<BR>वार्त्ता news, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तावह|वार्तावह|वार्त्तावहः
वार्त्तावह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A chandler.<BR>2 A messenger.<BR>E.<BR>वार्त्ता news, वह to bear, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तावृत्ति
वार्त्तावृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>A householder.<BR>E.<BR>वार्त्ता news, and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तिक|वार्तिक|वार्त्तिकं|वार्त्तिकः
वार्त्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to news, bringing or conveying intelligence, &c.<BR>2 Commentatory, explanatory, belonging to a comment or gloss, (as a rule, &c.)<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An intelligencer, an informer, an agent or envoy.<BR>2 A man of the third or mercantile tribe.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A gloss, a commentary, especially a supplementary explanation added to a grammatical or philosophical aphorism, and its immediate elucidation, supplying or illustrating both text and comment; it is defined to be, the exposition of the meaning, of that which is said, of that which is left unsaid, and of that which is ill or imperfectly said.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A quail.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति news, &c., or a comment, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त्रघ्न
वार्त्त्रघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The prince ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्रघ्न INDRA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्दर|वार्दर|वार्द्दरं
वार्द्दर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Silk.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 The seed of the Abrus precatorius.<BR>4 A conch shell.<BR>5 A sort of curl on the right side of a horse's neck, considered as an auspicious mark.<BR>6 Speech.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, दृ to divide, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=754" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्दल|वार्दल|वार्दलः|वार्द्दलं|वार्द्दलः
वार्द्दल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A rainy day, bad weather, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An inkstand.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, and द what gives, वार्द a cloud, ला to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक
वार्द्धक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A number of old men.<BR>2 Old age.<BR>3 The infirmity, &c. of old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्य
वार्द्धक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धि
वार्द्धि<BR>m. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषि
वार्द्धुषि<BR>m. (-षिः)<BR>A usurer.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि interest or increase, वृधुषि substituted, aff. ठक्, and the क rejected; also वार्द्धुषिक, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिक
वार्द्धुषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A usurer: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिन्
वार्द्धुषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A usurer.<BR>E.<BR>वृधुषि substituted for वृद्धि, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुष्य
वार्द्धुष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>Usurious loan, usury, interest.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि increase, aff. ष्यञ्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध
वार्द्ध<BR>nf. (-र्द्धं-र्द्धी)<BR>A thong.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध to increase, to lengthen, aff. ष्ट्र, and अञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धीणस
वार्द्धीणस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>An old white goat with long ears.<BR>E.<BR>वार्द्धी a leather thong, and नस for नासिका a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्भट|वार्भटः
वार्भट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An alligator.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, भट to maintain, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मण|वार्मण|वार्मणं|वार्म्मणं
वार्म्मण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A number of coats of mail.<BR>E.<BR>वर्म्मण् armour, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मिण|वार्मिण|वार्म्मिणं
वार्म्मिण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A number of men in armour.<BR>E.<BR>वर्म्मिन् a man in armour, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मुच्|वार्मुच्
वार्म्मुच्<BR>m. (-र्म्मुक्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, भुच् to let loose, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्य|वार्य|वार्यं|वार्यः|वार्य्यं
वार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be selected or appointed.<BR>2 To be impeded, checked, stopped, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृङ् to choose, aff. ण्यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्यमाण|वार्यमाण
वार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being prevented, impeded, prohibited, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to select, passive v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्युद्भव|वार्युद्भव|वार्य्युद्भवं
वार्य्युद्भव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>वारि water, उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्योक|वार्योक|वार्योकः
वार्य्योक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>वारि, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्राशि
वार्राशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वार्, and राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्व्वट|वार्वट|वार्वटः|वार्व्वटः
वार्व्वट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A boat, a vessel.<BR>E.<BR>वार् water, वट to surround, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष
वार्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-ष)<BR>Belonging to a year, to the rains, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिक|वार्षिकं|वार्षिकः
वार्षिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Yearly, annual, or belonging to a year.<BR>2 Growing, &c. in the rainy season, or fit for or suited to it, &c.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A drug, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR>E.<BR>वर्ष rains, or a year, and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिला
वार्षिला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>वार्ष belonging to rain, from वर्ष, with अण् aff., इलच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षुक|वार्षुकः
वार्षुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sprinkling, wetting, that which sprinkles, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हत|वार्हतं
वार्हत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The fruit of the Solanum jacquini.<BR>E.<BR>वृहति the plant, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हद्रथ|वार्हद्रथः
वार्हद्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of JARĀSAṂDHA.<BR>E.<BR>वृहद्रथ the father of this prince, and अण् patronymic; also with इञ् aff. वार्हद्रथि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत
वार्हस्पत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Sacred to VṚHASPATI.<BR>E.<BR>वृहस्पति, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत्य
वार्हस्पत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Ethics, morality.<BR>E.<BR>वृहस्पति the supposed original author of this science, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालक|वालकः
वालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bracelet.<BR>2 A finger-ring.<BR>E.<BR>वल to surround, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्क|वाल्कं
वाल्क<BR>mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्की-ल्कं)<BR>Made of the bark of trees.<BR>E.<BR>वल्क bark, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्कल|वाल्कलं
वाल्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Made of bark.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A dress made of the bark of trees worn by ascetics.<BR>E.<BR>वल्कल bark, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मिकि|वाल्मिकिः
वाल्मिकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>The author of the Rāmāyaṇa; also वाल्मीकि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीक|वाल्मीकः
वाल्मीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>VĀLMĪKA or VĀLMĪKI, the author of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>वल्मीक an ant-hill, aff. अण्, or with इञ् aff. वाल्मीकि; so immersed in abstraction as to be overrun with ant's nests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूक|वावदूकः
वावदूक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Talking much, gabbling, prattling.<BR>E.<BR>वद to speak, Uṇādi aff. ऊक, the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूकता
वावदूकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Garrulity, loquaciousness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, वावटूकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावय|वावयः
वावय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of Basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावहि
वावहि<BR>mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि)<BR>Who or what bears or carries much.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत
वावृत<BR>(उ) r. 4th cl. वावृतु (वावृत्यते)<BR>1 To choose or select.<BR>2 To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्त|वावृत्तः
वावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Chosen, appointed.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. क्त, and the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्यमान
वावृत्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Choosing, preferring.<BR>E.<BR>वावृत to choose, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश
वाश<BR>(ऋ) वाशृ r. 4th cl. (वाश्यते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To cry as a bird.<BR>3 To call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशत्
वाशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Crying or singing like a bird.<BR>E.<BR>वाश to cry, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशन|वाशनं
वाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The cry or song of birds, bees, and the like.<BR>E.<BR>वाश to sound as a bird, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशा
वाशा<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A plant, (Justicia ganderussa): see वास, and वासक; also with कन् added वाशिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशि|वाशिः
वाशि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>वाश to sound, Uṇādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशित|वाशितं|वाशितः
वाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Perfumed, scented.<BR>2 Sung, called, cried.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The cry of birds or animals.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वाष to call, or वास to perfume, aff. क्त, and स changed to श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशिष्ठ|वाशिष्ठः
वाशिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Relating to the sage VASIṢṬHA.<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>The Goomti river, which rising in the Kemaün hills, pursues a winding and south-easterly course, and passing Lucknow and Jonpur falls into the Ganges, below Benares.<BR>E.<BR>वशिष्ठ the saint, अण् aff., derived from him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशुरा
वाशुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>वाश to sound, Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्र|वाश्रं|वाश्रः
वाश्र<BR>m. (-श्रः)<BR>A day.<BR>n. (-श्रं)<BR>1 An edifice, a dwelling, a building.<BR>2 A place where four roads meet.<BR>E.<BR>वाश to sound, Uṇādi aff. रक्; also read वास्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्कल|वाष्कलः
वाष्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Large, great.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्प|वाष्पं|वाष्पः
वाष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 Vapour, hot mist, steam, &c.<BR>2 A tear.<BR>3 Iron.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A drug.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, or वै to dry, aff. प, form irr.; also बाष्प derived from वाध to oppose, and ध changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पका
वाष्पका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to वाष्प vapour; also वाष्पिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाकल
वाष्पाकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Uttered or articulated with tears.<BR>E.<BR>वाष्प, and आकल what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=755" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाकुल
वाष्पाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Interrupted by tears.<BR>E.<BR>वाष्प, and आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पिका
वाष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR>E.<BR>वाष्प a tear, कन् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पोद्भव
वाष्पोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Starting of tears.<BR>E.<BR>वाष्प, and उद्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास<BR>r. 10th cl. (वासयति)<BR>To introduce another quality, but especially fragrant odors, to perfume, to incense, to fumigate, &c.<BR>(ऋ) वासृ r. 4th cl. (वास्यते)<BR>To sound, especially as a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A house, a habitation.<BR>2 Site, situation, abode, or place of staying or abiding.<BR>3 Cloth, clothes.<BR>4 Perfuming.<BR>mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, aff. घञ्, or वास to fumigate, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासःकुटी
वासःकुटी<BR>f. (-टी)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>वासस् cloth, and कुटी a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासक|वासकः
वासक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A shrub, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>E.<BR>वास to perfume, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासकसज्जा
वासकसज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>A woman dressed with all her ornaments, and having her apartments, &c. decorated to receive her lover.<BR>E.<BR>वास clothes, कन् pleonasm, and सज्जा accoutrements; also with कन् added, वासकसज्जिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासकर्णी
वासकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A hall, where public exhibitions, as Nāces, &c. are held.<BR>E.<BR>वास a house, कर्ण the ear, aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासगृह|वासगृहं
वासगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The inner part of a house, an inner or sleeping room, a bed-chamber.<BR>E.<BR>वास abiding, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासत|वासतः
वासत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासतेय
वासतेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Habitable, fit or proper to be dwelt in.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>वसति abode, or night, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
वासन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fit for clothes, or a dwelling, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Perfuming, fumigating or perfuming with fragrant vapour, or with incense, &c.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes.<BR>3 Abiding, abode.<BR>4 A particular posture in which abstract meditation is performed; it is also a posture conceived to be peculiarly proper in princes and chiefs, and is then described as sitting with the knees bent and the feet turned backwards.<BR>5 Knowledge.<BR>6 A water-jar.<BR>7 A box, a basket, a vessel, &c.<BR>8 An envelope.<BR>9 Any receptacle.<BR>10 Steeping, infusing.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 The knowledge of any thing derived from memory, the present consciousness of past perceptions.<BR>2 Fancy, imagination.<BR>3 Trust, confidence.<BR>4 Ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, &c., aff. युच्; or वसन clothes, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासनस्थ
वासनस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Packed, folded, enveloped.<BR>E.<BR>वासन a box, &c., and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्त|वासंत|वासन्तः
वासन्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>1 Placed, situated.<BR>2 Vernal, relating to the season of spring, suitable to it, produced in it, &c.<BR>3 Young, in the spring of life.<BR>4 Diligent in the performance of religious ceremonies.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A camel.<BR>2 The Indian cuckoo.<BR>3 Any young animal, or a young elephant.<BR>4 A catamite.<BR>5 The southern wind, zephyr.<BR>6 A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>7 The black kind of Moong or bean.<BR>8 A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>9 The Koïl or Indian cuckoo.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A large creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>2 A species of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>3 Long pepper.<BR>4 Trumpet flower.<BR>5 A festival in honour of KĀMADEVA, held in the month Chaitra.<BR>6 A species of the Śarkarī metre.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, aff. झच्, and the vowel made long; or वसन्त spring, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तक|वासन्तकं
वासन्तक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Sown or growing in spring.<BR>2 Suitable to the spring season.<BR>3 Relating or belonging to it, vernal.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तिक|वासंतिक|वासन्तिकः
वासन्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An actor, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>वसन्त spring, aff. ठक्; the spring being the festival season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासयोग|वासयोगः
वासयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Fragrant powder sprinkled on the clothes, especially the red powder scattered about at the Holi festival.<BR>E.<BR>वास perfume, and योग joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासर|वासरं|वासरः
वासर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>A day.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>One of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, in the causal form, Uṇādi aff. अर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासरसङ्ग|वासरसंग|वासरसङ्गः
वासरसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Morning.<BR>E.<BR>वासर, and सङ्ग connexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासव|वासवः
वासव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>वसु a Vasu, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासस्
वासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Cloth, clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वस to cover or clothe, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाससज्जा
वाससज्जा<BR>f. (-ज्जा)<BR>A woman drest in all her ornaments to receive her lover.<BR>E.<BR>वास clothes, सज्ज armed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासागार|वासागारं|वासागारः
वासागार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The inner or sleeping apartment.<BR>E.<BR>वास abiding, and आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासि|वासिः
वासि<BR>mf. (-सिः-सी)<BR>A small hatchet or chopper, an adze.<BR>m. (-सिः)<BR>Abiding, dwelling.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, Uṇādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिका
वासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant. (Justicia): see वासक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
वासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Perfumed, scented.<BR>2 Clothed, dressed.<BR>3 Famous, celebrated.<BR>4 Steeped, infused.<BR>5 Spiced, seasoned, (sauces, &c.)<BR>6 Peopled, populous, flourishing, (a country.)<BR>7 Having, possessing.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 The cry of birds.<BR>2 Knowledge in general, but especially that derived from memory.<BR>3 Sound.<BR>4 Rendering a country populous and flourishing, causing it to be inhabited.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, or clothe, causal form, or वास to call, (as a bird,) aff. क्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
वासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Abiding, staying.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A white sort of Jhiṇṭi, (Barleria.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ट|वासिष्टं
वासिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ठ|वासिष्ठं|वासिष्ठः
वासिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Explained or composed by the sage VASIṢṬHA, a part of the Vedas or a particular prayer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वसिष्ठ, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासु|वासुः
वासु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The soul, or the SUPREME BEIṄG considered as the soul of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide (eternally,) उण् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकि|वासुकिः
वासुकि<BR>m. (-किः)<BR>The serpent VĀSUKI, sovereign of the snakes.<BR>E.<BR>वसु a jewel, क the head, वसुक here said to be a name of KAŚYAPA, aff. of descent इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकेय|वासुकेयः
वासुकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The serpent VĀSUKI.<BR>E.<BR>see the last, aff. ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकेयस्वसृ
वासुकेयस्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>A name of MANASĀ, the wife of JARATKĀRU, and goddess presiding over snakes.<BR>E.<BR>वासुकेय the serpent VĀSUKI, and स्वसृ a sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुदेव|वासुदेवः
वासुदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A descendant of VASUDEVA, the general appellation of a class of persons peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>वसुदेव the father of the deity, and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुपूज्य|वासुपूज्यः
वासुपूज्य<BR>m. (-ज्यः)<BR>The twelfth Jina or Jaina teacher of the present era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=756" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुभद्र|वासुभद्रः
वासुभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वासु the soul, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुरा
वासुरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 The earth.<BR>3 A woman.<BR>4 A female elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वास to perfume, or वस to abide, in the causal form, aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासू
वासू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>A young girl, (in theatrical language.)<BR>E.<BR>वस to abide, in the causal form, (to take to dwell with one,) aff. ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासोद
वासोद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Who or what gives clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वासस्, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासोयुग
वासोयुग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>A suit of clothes.<BR>E.<BR>वासस्, and युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासौकस्
वासौकस्<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>The inner or private apartments.<BR>E.<BR>वास dwelling, and ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त
वास्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ती-स्तं)<BR>Made or derived from a goat.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव|वास्तवं
वास्तव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Determined, demonstrated, fixed, substantiated.<BR>2 Real, substantial.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>An appointment.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु thing, substance, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तविक|वास्तविकं|वास्तविकः
वास्तविक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Real, material, substantial, genuine.<BR>2 Determinate.<BR>E.<BR>वस्तु, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तवोषा
वास्तवोषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>वास्तव an appointment, and ऊषा a libidinous woman: the season in which she makes an assignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव्य|वास्तव्यः
वास्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be abided or dwelt in, to be fixed as a habitation.<BR>2 To be taken care of, (as a dependant.)<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>A kinsman, a dependant.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, causal form, aff. of the future participle तव्यर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तु
वास्तु<BR>mn. (-स्तुः-स्तु)<BR>1 The site of a habitation.<BR>2 A house, a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>वस to dwell, Uṇādi aff. तुन्, and the radical vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुक|वास्तुकं
वास्तुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A potherb: see वास्तूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुसंशमन
वास्तुसंशमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A ceremony or sacrifice performed on entering a new habitation.<BR>E.<BR>वास्तु, and संशमन consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुसंशमनीय
वास्तुसंशमनीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A ceremony performed on entering a new mansion.<BR>E.<BR>छ added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तूक|वास्तूकं
वास्तूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album, and other edible species.)<BR>E.<BR>वास्तु the site of a house, ठक् aff., and form irr. (growing there); also with the vowel unaltered कास्तुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तेय|वास्तेयं
वास्तेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Abdominal, relating or belonging to the belly.<BR>E.<BR>वस्ति, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तोस्पति
वास्तोस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वास्तु the site of a dwelling, in the sixth case, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त्र|वास्त्रः
वास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः-स्त्री-स्त्रं)<BR>Cloth, made of or covered with cloth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वस्त्र cloth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्प|वास्पः
वास्प<BR>m. (-स्पः)<BR>1 Vapor.<BR>2 Tears; more correctly वाष्प, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्पविक्लव
वास्पविक्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Weeping, bursting into tears.<BR>E.<BR>वास्प, and विक्लव distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्पाविलेक्षण
वास्पाविलेक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Suffused with tears, weeping.<BR>E.<BR>वास्प, आविल turbid, ईक्षण the sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह|वाहः
वाह<BR>(ऋ) वाहृ r. 1st cl. (वाहते)<BR>To endeavour: the root is preferably read वाहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह|वाहः
वाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A measure of capacity containing ten Kumbhas, or nearly equal to the weight of an English wey or a ton in freight.<BR>3 A bull.<BR>4 Air, wind.<BR>5 The arm.<BR>6 A buffalo.<BR>7 A vehicle, a carriage or conveyance of any kind.<BR>8 A bearer, a porter, a carrier of burthens, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहक|वाहकः
वाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A horseman.<BR>2 A porter, a carrier.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहद्विषत्|वाहद्विषन्त्
वाहद्विषत्<BR>m. (-षन्)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>वाह a horse, and द्विषत् inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहन|वाहनं
वाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A vehicle, a conveyance of any kind, as a horse, an elephant, a carriage.<BR>2 Carrying, conveying, &c.<BR>3 Marking effort or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, in the causal form, or वाह to endeavour, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहभ्रंश्
वाहभ्रंश्<BR>mfn. (-भ्रट्)<BR>Falling from a vehicle, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वाह, भ्रंश to fall, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहयत्
वाहयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Employing, making use of.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहस|वाहसः
वाहस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>2 A watercourse.<BR>3 A potherb, (Marsilia dentata.)<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, in the causal form, aff. असच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिक|वाहिकः
वाहिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A large drum.<BR>2 A car, &c. drawn by oxen.<BR>E.<BR>वाह bearing, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित|वाहितं
वाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Exerted, endeavoured.<BR>E.<BR>वाह to endeavour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित्थ|वाहित्थं
वाहित्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>The part of an elephant's forehead below the frontal globes.<BR>E.<BR>वाहिन्, स्था to stay, aff. क, and स changed to त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिन्
वाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>Bearing, carrying.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनी
वाहिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 An army.<BR>2 A body of forces consisting of 81 elephants, 81 cars, 243 horse, 405 foot, a cohort, a battalion.<BR>3 A river.<BR>E.<BR>वाह a vehicle, &c., aff. इनि; fem. aff. ङीप्, comprising the conveyances of cars, horse, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनीनिवेश|वाहिनीनिवेशः
वाहिनीनिवेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A camp.<BR>E.<BR>वाहिनी, and निवेश encampment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनीपति|वाहिनीपतिः
वाहिनीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A general, a commanding officer.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वाहिनी an army or river, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहीक|वाहीकः
वाहीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Of burthen, bearing burthens.<BR>2 Outer, external.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of a country, part of the Punjab.<BR>E.<BR>वाह bearing, or वाहिर् external, aff. ईकक् or ईकञ्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्य|वाह्यं|वाह्यः
वाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>1 To be carried or borne.<BR>2 Outer, external.<BR>n. (-ह्यं)<BR>A carriage, a vehicle.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A beast of burthen, an ox, a horse, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. ण्यत्, or वहिर् external, यञ् aff.: see वाह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यतस्
वाह्यतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Externally, solitarily.<BR>E.<BR>तसि added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यमान
वाह्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being carried or conveyed.<BR>2 Being induced, urged, incited, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लि|वाह्लिः
वाह्लि<BR>f. (-ह्लिः)<BR>A country: see वाह्लीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लिक|वाह्लिकं|वाह्लिकः
वाह्लिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Balkh: see वाह्लीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लिज|वाह्लिजः
वाह्लिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born in Vahli or Vāhlika country.<BR>m. यः<BR>A Turki horse.<BR>E.<BR>वाह्लि, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लीक|वाह्लीकं|वाह्लीकः
वाह्लीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A country lying north-west of Afghanistan, Balkh.<BR>2 A horse from Balkh, considered as one of a good breed.<BR>3 One of the principal Gandharbas or choristers of heaven.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Saffron.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>वल्ह to be preeminent, इकन् or ईकन् aff., वह्लिक or वह्लीक; again, अण्. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">Page758</a>] pleonastic or derivative added, वाह्लिक; or वाह्लीक, the conjunct letters of the root being transposed; saffron, &c. are supplied still to India, especially from Kashmir, Khorasan, and the countries in that direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=757" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वि|विः
वि<BR>mf. (-विः-वी)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 The eye.<BR>3 Heaven.<BR>4 The region of the wind.<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix, implying:<BR>1 Certainty, ascertainment, as विवेक्तुं to determine, to judge.<BR>2 Separation, disjunction, as वियोक्तु to disjoin.<BR>3 Aversion, repugnance, as विरोद्धु to oppose.<BR>4 Impatience, intolerance, as विनृष्टं to be impatient.<BR>5 Variety, difference, विशेष्टु to distinguish.<BR>6 Cause, motive, विघातुं to prescribe or order.<BR>7 Motion, progress, विचरितुं to go.<BR>8 Privation, विणीतुं to take away. It generally corresponds to the English adjuncts, a, ex, de, dis, in, un, &c. and is frequently an expletive.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, Uṇādi aff. इन् with the effect of डित् or ड, which ejects the final syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंश|विंशः
विंश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Twentieth.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति twenty, and डट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशक|विंशकः
विंशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Twenty, collectively, or an aggregate of twenty.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति, and ड्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशति|विंशतिः
विंशति<BR>always f. sing. (-तिः)<BR>Twenty, a score.<BR>du. (-ती)<BR>Two twenties.<BR>plu. (-तयः)<BR>Many twenties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतिक|विंशतिकः
विंशतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Worth twenty, produced from or bought with twenty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति twenty, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतितम|विंशतितमः
विंशतितम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Twentieth.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति, and तमट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतीश|विंशतीशः
विंशतीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A governor of twenty villages.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति, and ईश sovereign; also विंशतीशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशिन्
विंशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>Twenty, (collectively,) a score.<BR>E.<BR>विंशति, and डिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक|विकं
विक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The milk of a prolific cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कट|विकंकट|विकंकटः|विकङ्कटः
विकङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A plant, (Ruellia longifolia, &c.): see गोक्षुर.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, ककि to go, aff. अटन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कत|विकंकत|विकंकतः|विकङ्कतः
विकङ्कत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small tree.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, separate, ककि to go or grow, अतच् aff., or वि a bird, ककि, &c. as before; on which the birds roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकच|विकचः
विकच<BR>mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>1 Blown, opened, expanded, spread, (as a flower, &c.)<BR>2 Bald, having little or no hair on the head.<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>1 A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>2 The planet KETU, or the personified descending node.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, separate, कच to go, aff. अच्, or वि privative, and कच hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकट|विकटः
विकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Formidable, frightful, hideous, horrible.<BR>3 Large-toothed.<BR>4 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>5 Changed in form or appearance.<BR>6 Obscure, obsolete.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A bile, a tumour.<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A female divinity peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying separation or expansion, कट to go or be, aff. अच्, or with कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकण्टक|विकण्टकः
विकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A herbaceous plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>E.<BR>वि expanding, कण्ट a thorn, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थन|विकत्थनं
विकत्थन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Speaking idly.<BR>2 Praising ironically.<BR>3 Vaunting, boastful.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Irony, ironical or unmerited praise.<BR>2 Praise in general.<BR>3 Assigning any thing to an unreal origin.<BR>4 Boasting.<BR>5 Repeating, proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying difference or extension, and कत्थन praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थनीय
विकत्थनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be praised, commendable.<BR>2 Ridiculous, to be praised ironically.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कत्थ to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्था
विकत्था<BR>f. (-त्था)<BR>1 Praise.<BR>2 Irony, ironical praise.<BR>3 Boasting.<BR>4 Repeating, proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>वि, कत्थ to praise, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थिन्
विकत्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्थी-त्थिनी-त्थि)<BR>Who or what boasts, praises, proclaims, &c.: see विकथन.<BR>E.<BR>वि, कत्य to boast, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्प|विकंप
विकम्प<BR>mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>1 Trembling.<BR>2 Heaving.<BR>3 Unsteady, not firm or continued..<BR>4 Shrinking form.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and कम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्पित|विकंपित|विकम्पितः
विकम्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Trembling, tremulous, agitated.<BR>2 Palpitating, heaving.<BR>3 Broken, interrupted, unsteady.<BR>4 Shrinking from.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कपि to tremble, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर|विकरः
विकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying difference, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकराल|विकरालः
विकराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Formidable, frightful.<BR>E.<BR>वि intensitive, and कराल frightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ण|विकर्णः
विकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Ear-less.<BR>m. (-र्णं)<BR>One of the KURU princes.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and कर्ण an ear, or a proper name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्णिक|विकर्णिकः
विकर्णिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sārasvata, a district in the north-west of Hindustan, generally considered as part of the Punjab, though sometimes confounded with Kashmir.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and कर्ण KARṆA; aff. ठक्; the region from which KARṆA was proscribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्त्तन|विकर्तन|विकर्तनः|विकर्त्तनः
विकर्त्तन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A son who has usurped his father's kingdom.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृत to cut, aff. ल्युट्; having been shorn of some of his beams, by VIŚVAKARMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मकृत्|विकर्मकृत्
विकर्म्मकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>1 Acting illegally, one who does forbidden acts.<BR>2 Busy in various ways.<BR>E.<BR>विकर्म्म, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मक्रिया|विकर्मक्रिया
विकर्म्मक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Illegal or immoral act.<BR>E.<BR>विकर्म्म, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मन्|विकर्मन्
विकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Various business or duty.<BR>2 Prohibited or unlawful act.<BR>3 Fraud.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मस्थ|विकर्मस्थ|विकर्म्मस्थः
विकर्म्मस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Doing what is illegal or immoral, engaged in prohibited acts.<BR>2 Engaged in various business.<BR>E.<BR>विकर्म्म, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मिक|विकर्मिक|विकर्मिकः
विकर्म्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Doing forbidden acts.<BR>2 Transacting various affairs.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Clerk or superintendant of markets or fairs.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, कर्म्म business, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ष|विकर्षः
विकर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Pulling, pulling apart or out.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>वि separate, कृष to attract, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षण|विकर्षणं|विकर्षणः
विकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Pulling, drawing, dragging.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृष to attract, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल|विकलः
विकल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Confused, confounded, agitated.<BR>2 Defective, imperfect.<BR>3 Decayed, impaired, withered, waned.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>A woman in whom menstruation has ceased.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The 1/60th of a Kalā, the second of a degree.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and कला a digit of the moon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलपाणिक|विकलपाणिकः
विकलपाणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cripple with a crooked or withered arm.<BR>E.<BR>विकल defective, पाणि the hand, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलाङ्ग|विकलांग|विकलाङ्गः
विकलाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Deformed, crippled, maimed.<BR>E.<BR>विकल defective, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीकरण|विकलीकरणं
विकलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Spoiling, breaking, maiming.<BR>2 Confusing, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>विकल, and करण making, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीकृत
विकलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Broken, injured, impaired.<BR>2 Sick, lame, maimed.<BR>3 Confused, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>विकल, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=758" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीभूत
विकलीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Agitated, distressed.<BR>2 Maimed, defective.<BR>E.<BR>विकल, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलेन्द्रिय|विकलेंद्रिय
विकलेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Having any of the organs of sense impaired or defective.<BR>E.<BR>विकल, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्प|विकल्पः
विकल्प<BR>m. (-ल्पः)<BR>1 Error, ignorance, mistake.<BR>2 Alternative, option.<BR>3 Doubt, indecision.<BR>4 (In rhetoric,) Antithesis of opposites.<BR>5 (In grammar, &c.,) Admission of more than one form or rule.<BR>E.<BR>वि distinction, and कल्प making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पयत्
विकल्पयत्<BR>mfn. (यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Doubting, deliberating, weighing alternatives.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृप to be able, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पित
विकल्पित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made or acknowledged as optional.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृप to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकश्वर|विकश्वरः
विकश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opening, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>वि separately, कश to go, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकषा
विकषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before कष to injure, अच् aff.; also विकसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकष्वर
विकष्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opening, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कष to go, aff. वरच्; also विकस्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस|विकसः
विकस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The moon.<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Bengal madder.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कस to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसत्
विकसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Opening, expanding.<BR>2 Budding, blowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कस to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसित|विकसितं
विकसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blown, as a flower, budded, opened, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, कस to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्वर|विकस्वरः
विकस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opening, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, कस to go, aff. वरच्; also derived from कश or कष, विकश्यर, and विकष्वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार|विकारः
विकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Change of form or nature, alteration or deviation from the natural state.<BR>2 Sickness, disease change from the state of health.<BR>3 Passion, feeling, emotion, transition from the natural or quiescent condition of the soul.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying alteration, कृ to make, aff. अण्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
विकारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Changed, converted, made to undergo a changing.<BR>2 Rendered unfavourable or unfriendly.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृ to make, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
विकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Producing a change.<BR>2 Undergoing a change.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृ to make, णिनि aff., or विकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाल|विकालः
विकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Twilight.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying prohibition, (of peculiar ceremonies,) and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकालक|विकालकः
विकालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Evening, twilight.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>A perforated copper vessel, which is placed in a pan of water, and being filled at the expiration of a certain period, defines that period: a sort of Clepsydra, or water clock.<BR>E.<BR>वि before काल time, and कन् added, or वि before कल to go, aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
विकाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Solitude, loneliness, privacy.<BR>2 Display, manifestation, open or splendid appearance.<BR>3 Opening, expanding.<BR>4 Budding, blowing, (as a flower.)<BR>5 Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>6 Ether, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>वि before काश to shine, aff. घञ्; the vowel of the prefix is more usually made long: see विकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशता
विकाशता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Appearance, display.<BR>2 Loneliness.<BR>3 Expansion.<BR>E.<BR>विकाश shining, aff. तल्; also with त्व, विकाशत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशन|विकाशनं
विकाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Expansion, extent.<BR>2 Manifestation.<BR>3 Blowing, (of a flower.)<BR>E.<BR>विकाश, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशभृत्
विकाशभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>1 Expanding, being full.<BR>2 Blown, budded.<BR>E.<BR>विकाश, and भृत् who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशिन्
विकाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Expanding, spreading.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कश to go, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाषिन्
विकाषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Expanding, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कष to go, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासिन्
विकासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Expanding, opening, budding, blowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कस to go, aff. घिनुण्; also with कश or कष the same, विकाशिन्, and विकाषिन् as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिर|विकिरः
विकिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 A well.<BR>3 A fallen fragment, a scattered portion.<BR>4 Scattering.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, &c., कॄ to scatter, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरत्
विकिरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Throwing, scattering, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कॄ to scatter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरण|विकिरणं|विकिरणः
विकिरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Scattering, spreading about or abroad.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Gigantic swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before कॄ to scatter, aff. यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्ण|विकीर्णः
विकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Scattered, spread about, extended, diffused.<BR>2 Celebrated, famous.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying extension, कॄ to scatter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्य्य|विकीर्य
विकीर्य्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having or being scattered.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and कॄ to scatter, aff. ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्य्यमाण|विकीर्यमाण
विकीर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being tossed, agitated, scattered, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कॄ to scatter, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुर्व्वाण|विकुर्वाण|विकुर्व्वाणः
विकुर्व्वाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Joyful, cheerful, happy.<BR>2 Undergoing or making a change of form, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृ to make or do, चानश or शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुस्र|विकुस्रः
विकुस्र<BR>m. (-स्रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कस to shine, रक् Uṇādi aff., and उ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणन|विकूणनं
विकूणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A side glance, a leer, a wink.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कूण to contract or close, (the eyes,) aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणिका
विकूणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The nose.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कूण to sound, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत|विकृतं
विकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Entertaining the feeling of disgust, averse, estranged.<BR>2 Sick, diseased.<BR>3 Altered, changed, either in form or feeling.<BR>4 Imperfect, unfinished, incomplete.<BR>5 Overcome by feeling or passion.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Disgust, aversion.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतवदन
विकृतवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having the face distorted.<BR>E.<BR>विकृत, and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृताकार
विकृताकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Changed in aspect, form, or appearance.<BR>E.<BR>विकृत, and आकार form; also विकृताकृति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृताङ्ग
विकृताङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Distorted, deformed.<BR>E.<BR>विकृत, and अङ्ग the limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृति|विकृतिः
विकृति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 Change of any kind, as of purpose, mind. form, nature, &c. either permanent or temporary.<BR>2 Sickness, disease, change from the natural or healthy state.<BR>3 Fear, apprehension.<BR>4 Spirituous liquor.<BR>5 A species of metre: the stanza consists of four lines of two syllables each, variously arranged.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying alteration or reverse, कृ to make, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्ट|विकृष्टः
विकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Pulled, drawn, (as a bow-string.)<BR>2 Attracted.<BR>3 Dragged, drawn, in general.<BR>4 Sounded, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कृष to draw, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=759" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेश
विकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Bald.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>1 A small braid or tress of hair, first tied up severally, and then collected into the Veṇī or larger braid.<BR>2 A woman without hair.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally or privative, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेशिका
विकेशिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pledget, a piece of rag smeared with ghee or other substances and applied as a dressing to a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोष|विकोषः
विकोष<BR>m. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Uncovered, denuded, unsheathed.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and कोष a sheath, a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकौतुक
विकौतुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Incurious, indifferent.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and कौतुक curious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्क|विक्कः
विक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A young elephant.<BR>E.<BR>विक imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रम|विक्रमः
विक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Heroism, prowess, heroic valour.<BR>2 Great power or strength.<BR>3 Walking, going, proceeding.<BR>4 Overpowering, overcoming.<BR>5 Strength in general.<BR>6 The name of a sovereign of Ougein: see विक्रमादित्य.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, to move, to walk, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रममाण
विक्रममाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>2 Overpowering.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमादित्य|विक्रमादित्यः
विक्रमादित्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>The name of a celebrated prince, the sovereign of Ougein, and reputed founder of an æra still in use amongst the Hindus, commencing 56 years before the Christian æra; there are however many princes of this name, and it has been applied to Rāja BHOJA, to ŚĀLIVĀHANA, and PṚTHVĪ Rāja, as well as to five or six others; the name also occurs variously written, as VIKRAMA, ĀDITYA, VIKRAMASENA, VIKRAMASIṂHA, VIKRAMĀRKA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रम power, and आदित्य the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमार्क|विक्रमार्कः
विक्रमार्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>A name of the sovereign VIKRAMĀDITYA: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रम heroism, and अर्क the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमार्ज्जित|विक्रमार्जित
विक्रमार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conquered, acquired by valour.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रम, and अर्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमिन्
विक्रमिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रम strength, valour, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रय|विक्रयं|विक्रयः
विक्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sale, selling, vending.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयानुशय|विक्रयानुशयः
विक्रयानुशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Rescission of sale.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रय, and अनुशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयण|विक्रयणं
विक्रयण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Selling, vending.<BR>E.<BR>वि reverse, क्री to buy, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिक|विक्रयिकः
विक्रयिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender, a dealer, a salesman.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रय sale, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिन्
विक्रयिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A seller, a vender.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रय sale, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्त|विक्रांत|विक्रान्तं|विक्रान्तः
विक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Valiant, mighty.<BR>2 Overcoming, victorious.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A hero, a warrior.<BR>2 A lion.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Valour.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, aff. क्त, in an active sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्ति|विक्रांति|विक्रांतिः|विक्रान्तिः
विक्रान्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 A horse's canter or gallop.<BR>2 Prowess, heroic strength and valour.<BR>3 Great power or strength.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तृ|विक्रांतृ
विक्रान्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>1 Valiant.<BR>2 Victorious.<BR>m. (-न्ता)<BR>A hero, a victor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रम to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रायक|विक्रायकः
विक्रायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender, a seller.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, खुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रिया
विक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Change of mind, form, purpose, condition, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, and क्रिया action; see विकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीत|विक्रीतः
विक्रीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sold.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीय
विक्रीय<BR>ind.<BR>Having sold.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुष्ट|विक्रुष्टं
विक्रुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Harsh, rugged, or unkind, (as speech.)<BR>2 Called out, exclaimed.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 A cry of alarm or for help.<BR>2 Abuse.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रुश to call, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेतृ
विक्रेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A vender, a seller.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेय|विक्रेयं
विक्रेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Vendible, saleable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्री to buy, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोशन|विक्रोशनं
विक्रोशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Abusing, reviling.<BR>2 Calling out.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रश to curse, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोष्टृ
विक्रोष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>1 Who reviles, abuses, speaks harshly, &c.<BR>2 Who calls or cries out.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्रुश to cry, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लव|विक्लवः
विक्लव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Overcome with fear or agitation, confused, confounded, lost, bewildered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्लु to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लवता
विक्लवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Timidity, fear.<BR>E.<BR>विक्लव, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विक्लवत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिन्न|विक्लिन्नः
विक्लिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Old.<BR>2 Withered, shrivelled, decayed.<BR>3 Wet, moist.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्लिद to moisten, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षण
विक्षण<BR>adv. n. (-णं)<BR>Momentarily, for a moment.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and क्षण a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षत|विक्षतः
विक्षत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck, hurt, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षत broken, torn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षाव|विक्षावः
विक्षाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Cough.<BR>2 Sound.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षु to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिपत्
विक्षिपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>1 Throwing, tossing.<BR>2 Agitating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षिप to throw, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्त|विक्षिप्तः
विक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>2 Thrown, cast.<BR>3 Agitated, bewildered, perplexed.<BR>4 Sent, dispatched.<BR>5 Refuted, falsified.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, and क्षिप्त thrown or sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीण
विक्षीण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Wasted, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षै to decay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीणक|विक्षीणकः
विक्षीणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The chief of a class of demigods, enumerated amongst those attached to ŚIVA, and the ministers of destruction amongst men by plague, pestilence, &c.<BR>2 A meeting or assembly of the gods.<BR>3 A place prohibited to eaters of meat.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षीण wasted, (by whom,) and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेप|विक्षेपः
विक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Casting, throwing, or throwing away.<BR>2 Sending, dispatching.<BR>3 Confusion, perplexity, fear proceeding from ignorance or error.<BR>4 Looking about vaguely or wildly, as of a woman for her absent lover.<BR>5 Refuting an argument, establishing its falsehood.<BR>6 Celestial latitude.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षिप to throw, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपण|विक्षेपणं
विक्षेपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Scattering, dispersing.<BR>2 Sending, dispatching.<BR>3 Throwing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षिप् to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपध्रुव|विक्षेपध्रुवः
विक्षेपध्रुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>(In astronomy), The greatest inclination of a planet's orbit.<BR>E.<BR>विक्षेप, and ध्रुव are.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षोभ|विक्षोभः
विक्षोभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 Agitating, shaking.<BR>2 Conflict, struggle.<BR>3 Fearing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before क्षभ to stir, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख|विखः
विख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Noseless; also विखु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखण्डित|विखंडित
विखण्डित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Broken, divided.<BR>2 Refuted.<BR>E.<BR>वि before खण्डित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=760" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखासा
विखासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखु|विखुः
विखु<BR>mfn. (-खुः-खुः-खु)<BR>Noseless; also विखु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखुर|विखुरः
विखुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A goblin, a demon, a Rākṣasa.<BR>E.<BR>वि before खुर to cut, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्य|विख्यः
विख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative prefix, and ख्य substituted for नस or नासिका; also other as arbitrary terms, or विख, विग्र, विग्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यात|विख्यातः
विख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, notorious, famous.<BR>2 Avowed, confessed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ख्या to say or tell, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्याति|विख्यातिः
विख्याति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fame, celebrity, notoriety.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ख्या to say or tell, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यापन|विख्यापनं
विख्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Confessing, acknowledging, avowing, declaring.<BR>2 Explaining, expounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ख्या to say, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्र|विख्रः
विख्र<BR>mfn. (-ख्रः-ख्रा-ख्रं)<BR>Noseless; also विख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्रु|विख्रुः
विख्रु<BR>mfn. (-ख्रुः-ख्रुः-ख्रु)<BR>Noseless; also विख and विखु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणन|विगणनं
विगणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Reckoning, computing.<BR>2 Considering, deliberating.<BR>3 Discharge of a debt.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गणन counting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणय्य
विगणय्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having deliberated or weighed.<BR>2 Having reckoned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गण to number, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणित
विगणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reckoned, calculated.<BR>2 Weighed, considered.<BR>3 Discharged, (as a debt.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before गण to count, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगत|विगतः
विगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, departed, disappeared.<BR>2 Separated, severed, parted.<BR>3 Freed or exempt from.<BR>4 Lost.<BR>5 Gloomy, dark, obscured.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying disunion, (of light, &c.,) गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतकल्मष
विगतकल्मष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>1 Pure, righteous.<BR>2 Unsoiled.<BR>E.<BR>विगत, and कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतज्वर
विगतज्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Exempted from decay.<BR>2 Cured of fever.<BR>E.<BR>विगत, and ज्वरा decay, or ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतराग
विगतराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Devoid of passion or affection.<BR>E.<BR>विगत, and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतश्रीक|विगतश्रीकः
विगतश्रीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unfortunate, unprosperous.<BR>E.<BR>विगत gone, श्री prosperity, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्पृह
विगतस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Indifferent, devoid of wish or desire.<BR>E.<BR>विगत, and स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतार्त्तवा|विगतार्तवा
विगतार्त्तवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A woman past child-bearing.<BR>E.<BR>विगत gone, आर्त्तव the menstrual excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम|विगमः
विगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Separation, parting.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर|विगरः
विगर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An abstemious man, one who feeds on wind.<BR>2 A naked man.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हण|विगर्हणं
विगर्हण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Abuse, abusing, censure, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गर्ह to abuse, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणीय
विगर्हणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Bad, wicked, reprehensible.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गर्ह to abuse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हित|विगर्हितः
विगर्हित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abused, reviled.<BR>2 Low, vile.<BR>3 Bad, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गर्ह to abuse, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्य
विगर्ह्य<BR>mfn. (-र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं)<BR>Blamable, reprehensible.<BR>ind.<BR>Having blamed or reviled.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गर्ह to abuse, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्यकथा
विगर्ह्यकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Scandal, abuse.<BR>E.<BR>विगर्ह्य, and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलत्
विगलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>1 Oozing, dropping, flowing.<BR>2 Fading, dispersing, weakening, (as emotion, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before गल to ooze, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलित|विगलितः
विगलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Fallen, dropped, oozed, flowing.<BR>2 Removed, gone.<BR>3 Dissipated, dispersed.<BR>4 Decayed, impaired.<BR>5 Slackened, untied, (as a knot.)<BR>6 Loose, disordered, (as dress.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before गल to ooze, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलितकेश
विगलितकेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>Having the hair dishevelled.<BR>E.<BR>विगलित, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाढ|विगाढः
विगाढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Immersed, plunged, bathed, bathing.<BR>2 Much, exceeding.<BR>3 Flowing copiously.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गाह to bathe, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगान|विगानं
विगान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Ill report, detraction, scandal.<BR>2 Censure, reproach.<BR>E.<BR>वि depreciative prefix, गै to sing or sound, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह|विगाहः
विगाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Bathing.<BR>2 Plunging into, literally or figuratively, (as water, a crowd, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before गाह to bathe, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाहमान|विगाहमानः
विगाहमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Beholding, perceiving.<BR>2 Knowing.<BR>3 Bathing.<BR>4 Going, proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गाह to agitate, aff. शानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह्य
विगाह्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having bathed or plunged in.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गाह to agitate, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीत
विगीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Contradicted, contradictory, inconsistent.<BR>2 Abused, reproached.<BR>3 Sung or said in various ways.<BR>4 Sung ill.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीति|विगीतिः
विगीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Reproach, abuse.<BR>2 Contradiction.<BR>3 Singing in various styles.<BR>4 Singing ill.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and गीति singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगुण|विगुणः
विगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Void of all qualities.<BR>2 Bad, worthless, having no merit.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगूढ|विगूढः
विगूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Concealed, hidden.<BR>2 Blamed, reproached, censured.<BR>E.<BR>वि before गुह to conceal, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृहीत
विगृहीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opposed, obstructed, prevented.<BR>2 Encountered, as in fight.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to seize, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृह्य
विगृह्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having warred or contended with.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृह्यमाण
विगृह्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being warred upon or contended with.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to take, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्र|विग्रः
विग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative prefix, and ग्र substituted for नासिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रह|विग्रहः
विग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 Extension, diffusion.<BR>3 A portion, a part.<BR>4 Shape, form, figure.<BR>5 (A grammatical term,) the proper application or sense of a compound word.<BR>mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>1 War, battle.<BR>2 Opposition, encounter.<BR>E.<BR>वि various, (happiness, &c.) ग्रह to take, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहावर|विग्रहावरं
विग्रहावर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The back.<BR>E.<BR>विग्रह the body, and अवर the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्राह्य
विग्राह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be warred or contended with.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटिका
विघटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sixtieth part of a Gharī, equal to 24 seconds.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and घटिका a Gharī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघन|विघनः
विघन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A mallet, a hammer, an implement for striking.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to strike, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टन|विघट्टनं
विघट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>2 Striking.<BR>3 Opening, undoing, untying.<BR>4 Offending.<BR>E.<BR>वि, घटृ to rub, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टित|विघट्टितं
विघट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed, touched.<BR>2 Offended.<BR>3 Struck.<BR>4 Untied, undone.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घट्ट or rub, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=761" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघस|विघसं|विघसः
विघस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The residue of food offered to the gods, to the manes, to a venerable guest, or a spiritual preceptor.<BR>2 Food in general.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अद to eat, aff. अप्, and घस substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसाश|विघसाशः
विघसाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>One who eats the remains of an offering.<BR>E.<BR>विघस, and आश eating; also विघसाशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघात|विघातः
विघात<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 Impediment, obstacle.<BR>2 Prohibition or prevention.<BR>3 Opposition.<BR>4 Destruction.<BR>5 A blow.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to kill or hurt, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातसिद्धि|विघातसिद्धिः
विघातसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Removing obstacles or impediments.<BR>E.<BR>विघात, and सिद्धि attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातिन्
विघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Opposing, impeding, preventing.<BR>2 Removing, destroying.<BR>3 Wounding, killing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to hurt or strike, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघुष्ट
विघुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Cried, proclaimed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घुष्ट cried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघुष्य
विघुष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having proclaimed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घुष to cry, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघोषण
विघोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Proclamation, crying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घुष to cry aloud, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्न|विघ्नः
विघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>2 The Caronda, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to be injured (by it), and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकर
विघ्नकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Opposing, impeding, obstructing.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकारिन्
विघ्नकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Impeding, obstructing.<BR>2 Fearful, formidable, terrible.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and कारिन् causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्ननाशक|विघ्ननाशकः
विघ्ननाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what removes difficulties, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न, and नाशक who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्ननाशन|विघ्ननाशनः
विघ्ननाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Removing obstacles.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and नाशन removing; the deity being supposed capable of either causing or removing difficulties and impediments, and being therefore especially worshipped at the commencement of any undertaking: also other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नराज|विघ्नराजः
विघ्नराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an impediment, and राज ruler: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नलेश
विघ्नलेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Slight obstacle or impediment.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नविनायक|विघ्नविनायकः
विघ्नविनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and विनायक remover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नसिद्धि|विघ्नसिद्धिः
विघ्नसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Removal of obstacles.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नहारिन्
विघ्नहारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, हारिन् who removes see विघ्ननाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नित|विघ्नितः
विघ्नित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stopped, prevented, obstructed, impeded.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नेश|विघ्नेशः
विघ्नेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and ईश lord: see विघ्ननाशन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विङ्ख|विंख|विंखः|विङ्खः
विङ्ख<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>A horse's hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच
विच<BR>(औइर्) औ विचिर् r. 7th cl. (विनक्ति विंक्ते)<BR>1 To differ, to be separate or distinct. To divide, to separate, especially in judgment, to discriminate, to judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचकिल|विचकिलः
विचकिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of jasmine.<BR>2 A flower, commonly Dona, (Artemisia.)<BR>3 A shrub, (Vangueria spinosa)<BR>E.<BR>वि before चक to be satisfied, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षण|विचक्षणः
विचक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Clever, able, wise, sensible.<BR>2 Proficient, skilful.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A learned Brahman or Paṇḍita, a holy teacher.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चक्ष to speak, (sensibly,) and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षुस्
विचक्षुस्<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>1 Blind.<BR>2 Sad, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचय|विचयः
विचय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Search, research.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचयन|विचयनं
विचयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Search, research, seeking.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचरत्|विचरन्त्
विचरत्<BR>mfn. (-रत्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Wandering, roaming, going about.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, चर to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्च्चिका|विचर्चिका
विचर्च्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Herpes, scab.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर्च्च to speak or tell, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचल|विचलः
विचल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Unsteady, unfixed, moving, going.<BR>2 Conceited.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चल the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलत्
विचलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>Moving, going, shaking, waving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चल to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलन|विचलनं
विचलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Fickleness, unsteadiness.<BR>2 Self-praise, conceit.<BR>3 Deviating from.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चल to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलित|विचलितः
विचलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, departed.<BR>2 Deviated from.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चल to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार|विचारः
विचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The exercise of judgment or reason on a present object, investigation, consideration, deliberation.<BR>2 Dispute, discussion.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारक|विचारकः
विचारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An investigator, a judge.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारकता
विचारकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Investigation, discussion.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also त्व, विचारकत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारकर्त्तृ|विचारकर्तृ
विचारकर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A judge, an investigator.<BR>E.<BR>विचार, and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारण|विचारणं
विचारण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Deliberation, investigation, the exercise of judgment, or decision after due examination or discussion.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The Mīmāṃsā system of philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, causal form, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारणीय|विचारणीयं
विचारणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be discussed or investigated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारभू
विचारभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>1 The judgment seat of YAMA, the judge of the dead.<BR>2 Any meeting for literary or judicial investigation.<BR>E.<BR>विचार discussion or judgment, and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारस्थल
विचारस्थल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A logical disputation.<BR>E.<BR>विचार, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारित|विचारितः
विचारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Judged, discussed, determined, decided.<BR>E.<BR>विचार discussion, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारिन्
विचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Judging, discussing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार्य्य|विचार्य|विचार्य्यं
विचार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be discussed, weighed, deliberated. &c.<BR>ind.<BR>Having deliberated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, causal v., ण्यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार्य्यमाण|विचार्यमाण
विचार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being investigated or discussed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चर to go, passive v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचाल|विचालं|विचालः
विचाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Intervening, intermediate.<BR>E.<BR>वि disjunctive prefix, चल to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचि|विचिः
विचि<BR>f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>A wave.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, क्विप् aff., also वीची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=762" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिकित्सा
विचिकित्सा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>2 Error, mistake.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कित to doubt, in the reduplicate form, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्र|विचित्रं|विचित्रः
विचित्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>1 Variegated, spotted.<BR>2 Painted, coloured.<BR>3 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>4 Wonderful, surprising.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Variegated, (the colour.)<BR>2 Surprise.<BR>3 Speech implying apparently the reverse of the object intended.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चित्र variegated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रक|विचित्रकः
विचित्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Wonderful, surprising.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Astonishment, wonder.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रचीनांशुक
विचित्रचीनांशुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Shot or watered China silk.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र, and चीनांशुक China cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रता
विचित्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Wonder, wonderfulness.<BR>2 Being variegated, variety of colour or tint, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विचित्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रदेह|विचित्रदेहः
विचित्रदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>1 Having the body painted, &c.<BR>2 Elegant.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र spotted, variegated, (with different tints,) and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रवीर्य्य|विचित्रवीर्य|विचित्रवीर्यः|विचित्रवीर्य्यः
विचित्रवीर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>A sovereign, the 22nd monarch of the lunar dynasty in the third age, the son of ŚĀNTANU and husband of PĀṆḌU'S mother.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र wonderful, वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रवीर्य्यसू|विचित्रवीर्यसू
विचित्रवीर्य्यसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of VICITRAVĪRYA by ŚĀNTANU; also of VYĀSA by PARĀŚARA.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्रवीर्य्य as above, and सू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्राङ्ग|विचित्रांग|विचित्राङ्गः
विचित्राङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Elegant, well-formed, handsome.<BR>2 Having the body of various colours.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 A tiger.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र variegated or beautiful, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रित|विचित्रितः
विचित्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wonderful.<BR>2 Painted, variegated.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्त्य
विचिन्त्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having reflected.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चित to think, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्त्यमान
विचिन्त्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being to be thought of or considered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चिति to think, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वत्
विचिन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्)<BR>Thinking, considering.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वत्क|विचिन्वत्कः
विचिन्वत्क<BR>m. (-त्कः)<BR>1 A hero.<BR>2 Discrimination, judging.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वान
विचिन्वान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Thinking, considering, deliberating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचीर्ण
विचीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Entered.<BR>2 Occupied or inhabited by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतन
विचेतन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unconscious, senseless, lifeless.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv. चेतना sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतस्
विचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>1 Sad, perplexed, unhappy.<BR>2 Ignorant, stupid.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying privation, चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेष्टित|विचेष्टितः
विचेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Investigated, ascertained, inquired into or looked after.<BR>2 Inconsiderate, ill-judged.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Evil or malicious act.<BR>2 Exertion, effort.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चेष्टित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युत|विच्युतः
विच्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thrown or slipped off.<BR>2 Fallen or deviated from, neglecting, (as a duty.)<BR>3 Sloughed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छ
विच्छ<BR>r. 6th cl. (विच्छायति)<BR>To go or approach, (the form is irr.)<BR>r. 10th cl. (विच्छयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछन्द|विच्छन्द|विच्छंद|विच्छंदः|विच्छन्दः
विछन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A building of several stories, and surrounded by a portico, or having a portico to the east and west only; a palace, a temple.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छन्द wish, will; also with कन् added, विछन्दक, and derived from छृदि to be splendid, with वुन् aff. विछर्द्दक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछर्द्दक|विच्छर्दक|विच्छर्दकः|विच्छर्द्दक|विच्छर्द्दकः
विछर्द्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A large and handsome building, the temple of a god, or the palace of a prince: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछर्द्दन|विच्छर्दन|विच्छर्दनं|विच्छर्द्दन
विछर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Disregarding.<BR>2 Wasting.<BR>3 Being sick.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छृदि to vomit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछर्द्दित|विच्छर्दित|विच्छर्द्दित
विछर्द्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Disregarded, neglected.<BR>2 Diminished, impaired.<BR>3 Vomited.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छृद to vomit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विछाय|विच्छाय|विच्छायं|विच्छायः
विछाय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The shadow of a flock of birds.<BR>E.<BR>वि a bird, छाय a shadow, which in this sort of compound becomes neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छित्ति|विच्छित्तिः
विच्छित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Cutting, cutting off, excision.<BR>2 Dividing, fracture.<BR>3 Separation or absence.<BR>4 Loss, disappearance, destruction.<BR>5 Cæsura, pause, in a verse.<BR>6 The boundary or limits of a house, &c.<BR>7 A property of the Nāyikā or mistress, carelessness or irregularity in dress and decoration through flurry and agitation.<BR>7 Colouring the body with coloured unguents.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छिद to cut, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्न|विच्छिन्नः
विच्छिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्नी-न्नं)<BR>1 Cut, separated, severed.<BR>2 Absent or separated from.<BR>2 Divided, parted, portioned.<BR>4 Shared, divided equally.<BR>5 Crooked, curved.<BR>6 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>7 Hidden or cut off from view, intercepted.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, छिद to cut, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेद|विच्छेदः
विच्छेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Separation, disjunction, removal.<BR>2 Prohibition, prevention.<BR>3 Dividing, cutting.<BR>4 The division of a book, a section, a chapter.<BR>5 Space, interval.<BR>6 Dissension, difference.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छिद to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदक
विच्छेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>What separates, divides, cuts, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sector, a cutter.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छिद to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदन|विच्छेदनं
विच्छेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Separating, severing, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छिद to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदनीय
विच्छेदनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Divisible, to be divided or separated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before छिद to cut, aff. अनीयर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज
विज<BR>(औ इर) औ विजिर r. 3rd cl. (विवेक्ति)<BR>1 To be distinct or separate, to differ.<BR>2 To separate or divide, especially by reason; to judge, to distinguish, to discriminate.<BR>(ओ, ई,) ओविजी r. 6th cl. (विजते, or usually with उद् prefixed उद्विजते) also r. 7th cl. (विनक्ति)<BR>1 To fear, to be afraid.<BR>2 To tremble with fear.<BR>3 To shake or tremble.<BR>4 To be agitated or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
विजन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Private, lonely, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and जन man, people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनन|विजननं
विजनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Birth, bearing, delivery.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जन to be born, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनित
विजनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Born, begotten.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जन to be born, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
विजन्मन्<BR>n. (-न्म)<BR>Birth, separate or several birth.<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A man born from a degraded Vaiśya.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजपिल|विजपिलं
विजपिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजय|विजयः
विजय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Victory, triumph, conquest.<BR>2 A name of ARJUNA.<BR>3 A divine car or chariot of the gods.<BR>4 The father of the twenty-first Jina.<BR>5 One of the persons named ŚUKLA BĀLAS by the Jainas.<BR>6 The god of Hades, YAMA.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>2 One of the female friends or attendants of [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">Page764</a>] DURGĀ.<BR>3 One of the wives of YAMA.<BR>4 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa,) or the tops of the plant used as a narcotic.<BR>5 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>6 Orris root.<BR>7 A peculiar lunar day; the third, eighth, or thirteenth of a fortnight; it is also applied to the tenth of the light half of the month Āśvina (Sept-Oct.), on which the image of DURGĀ, set up during the great festival in honour of her, is cast into the water.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=763" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयकुञ्जर|विजयकुंजर|विजयकुञ्जरः
विजयकुञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A royal or war elephant.<BR>E.<BR>विजय victory, and कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयछन्द|विजयच्छन्द|विजयच्छन्दः
विजयछन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A kind of necklace, one of 504 rows or strings.<BR>E.<BR>विजय triumph, &c., and छन्द covering, from छदि, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयनन्दन|विजयनन्दनः
विजयनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sovereign of the race of IKṢVĀKU.<BR>E.<BR>विजय victory or a proper name, and नन्दन the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमर्द्दल|विजयमर्दल|विजयमर्दलः|विजयमर्द्दलः
विजयमर्द्दल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large military drum.<BR>E.<BR>विजय victory, and मर्द्दल a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमान
विजयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Victorious, triumphant.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयसिद्धि|विजयसिद्धिः
विजयसिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Success, victory.<BR>E.<BR>विजय, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयासप्तमी
विजयासप्तमी<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>The seventh day of the light half of a month falling on a Sunday.<BR>E.<BR>विजया victory, सप्तमी the seventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन्
विजयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Victorious, triumphant, conquering, a conqueror.<BR>E.<BR>विजय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन|विजयिनं
विजयिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sauce mixed with the water of boiled rice; also विजिन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर|विजरः
विजर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल|विजलं
विजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sauce, &c. mixed with rice water or gruel.<BR>E.<BR>विज to shake, aff. कलच्; also विजिल, विज्जन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
विजात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Born severally.<BR>2 Base born, of mixed origin.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The mother of children, a matron.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, जात born, (from whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजाति|विजातिः
विजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A different species or tribe.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
विजातीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Of a different caste.<BR>2 Of mixed origin.<BR>3 Dissimilar, of a different sort or nature.<BR>E.<BR>वि, जाती caste, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
विजानत्<BR>mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>1 Possessing various or extended knowledge.<BR>2 Knowing, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and ज्ञा to know, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीष|विजिगीषः
विजिगीष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Desirous of victory, emulative, anxious to overcome or conquer, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, in the desiderative form, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषा
विजिगीषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Competition, emulation, wish to surpass, overcome, or subdue.<BR>E.<BR>जि to conquer, with वि prefixed, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषु|विजिगीषुः
विजिगीषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous to conquer or overcome.<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>1 A warrior.<BR>2 An invader, an antagonist.<BR>3 A disputant.<BR>4 An opponent in general, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिग्राहयिषु
विजिग्राहयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to excite to war.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to take, desid. of the causal v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिघृक्षु
विजिघृक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Determined or wishing to encounter, oppose, fight with, overcome, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ग्रह to take, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित|विजितः
विजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conquered, defeated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितवत्|विजितवन्त्
विजितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Victorious, conquering.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितव्य
विजितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be apprehended or feared.<BR>E.<BR>विज to fear, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितात्मन्
विजितात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Self-subdued.<BR>E.<BR>विजित, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितृ
विजितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what separates, divides, &c.<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A judge, a discriminator, a distinguisher.<BR>2 A partner or co-heir.<BR>E.<BR>विज to separate, &c., aff. तृच्, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितेन्द्रिय|विजितेंद्रिय
विजितेन्द्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Of subdued organs or passions.<BR>E.<BR>विजित, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित्य
विजित्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having conquered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिन|विजिनं|विजिनः
विजिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Mixed with rice gruel, &c. (sauce or condiments.)<BR>E.<BR>विज to shake, aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिविल|विजिविलं
विजिविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Mixed with rice water, or gruel, (sauce or condiments, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>विज to shake, aff. इलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिविल|विजिविलं
विजिविल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Mixed with rice water, (sauces, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षा
विजिहीर्षा<BR>f. (-र्षा)<BR>Wish or intention to take pleasure or sport.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षु
विजिहीर्षु<BR>mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>Wishing, or seeking for sport or amusement.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
विजिह्म<BR>mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं)<BR>1 Curved, bent.<BR>2 Crooked in mind or purpose, dishonest, depraved.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and जिह्म straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्मता
विजिह्मता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Crookedness.<BR>2 Craftiness.<BR>E.<BR>विजिह्म, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भण|विजृंभण|विजृंभणं|विजृम्भणं
विजृम्भण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Pastime, sport, especially amorous.<BR>2 Budding, blossoming, expanding.<BR>3 Yawning.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जृभि to yawn, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भित|विजृंभित|विजृम्भितं|विजृम्भितः
विजृम्भित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Blossomed, expanded, opened, unfolded.<BR>2 Yawning, gaping.<BR>3 Sported, wantoned.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 Pastime, sport.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जृभि to yawn or open, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजेतृ
विजेतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Victorious, a victor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जन|विज्जनं
विज्जन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Mixed with rice-water or gruel, (sauce, gravy, &c.): see विजिल; it also occurs विज्जिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जल|विज्जलं
विज्जल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Mixed with rice-water, &c.: see विजिल.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
विज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Skilful, able, clever, conversant.<BR>2 Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying separation, discrimination, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञता
विज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wisdom, learning.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, विज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्त
विज्ञप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Stated, reported, represented.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=764" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्ति|विज्ञप्तिः
विज्ञप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Information, representation, respectful communication of information, or opinion on any subject.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal form, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञबुद्धि|विज्ञबुद्धिः
विज्ञबुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Indian spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञात|विज्ञातः
विज्ञात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Celebrated, famous, known, notorious.<BR>2 Known, understood.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञान|विज्ञानं
विज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Knowledge, science, learning, worldly knowledge or wisdom, that which comprehends any subject, except an understanding of the true nature of GOD or BRAHMA, acquirable by abstract meditation, and the study of the Vedas; it also is described as conversancy with the arts of painting, &c., and with books, as the Smṛti Śāstras, or works on law, and other branches of science or literature.<BR>2 Business, employment.<BR>3 Music.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानपाद|विज्ञानपादः
विज्ञानपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानमातृक|विज्ञानमातृकः
विज्ञानमातृक<BR>n. (-कः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha religion.<BR>E.<BR>विज्ञान knowledge, and मातृक parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानिक|विज्ञानिकः
विज्ञानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Clever, skilful, conversant; also वैज्ञानिक.<BR>E.<BR>विज्ञान, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापक|विज्ञापकः
विज्ञापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what makes known.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An informant.<BR>2 An instructor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापन|विज्ञापनं
विज्ञापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Teaching, instruction, communication of knowledge not religious, &c.<BR>2 Representing, informing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापनीय
विज्ञापनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be made known, represented, taught, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापित
विज्ञापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Apprised, informed.<BR>2 Instructed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ज्ञा to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञेय|विज्ञेयं
विज्ञेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Cognizable, comprehensible, what is to be or may be known or understood.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying discrimination, ज्ञा to know, यत् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्वर
विज्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Exempt from decay.<BR>2 Free from fever.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and ज्वरा decay, or ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विझर्झर
विझर्झर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Harsh, disagreeable, (as sound.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before झर्झर clanging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जमर
विञ्जमर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The white of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जोली|विंजोली
विञ्जोली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A line, a row, a range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट|विटः
विट<BR>r. 1st cl. (वेटति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>2 To curse.<BR>(इ) विटि r. 10th cl. (विण्टयति)<BR>To decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट|विटः
विट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A catamite, a pathic.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 An attendant on a dissolute character or courtezan.<BR>4 A paramour, a gallant.<BR>5 A mountain.<BR>6 The Khayar tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>7 A medicinal salt: see विडल्वण.<BR>8 A rat.<BR>9 The orange tree.<BR>10 A branch and its shoot.<BR>E.<BR>विट to sound, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्क|विटंक|विटंकः|विटङ्कः
विटङ्क<BR>mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>A dove-cot, an aviary.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, टकि to bind, aff. घञ्; also with कन् added विटङ्कक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटप|विटपः
विटप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>1 The branch of a tree with its new sprout or shoot.<BR>2 A new shoot.<BR>3 A branch.<BR>4 Expansion, spreading.<BR>5 A clump, a cluster.<BR>6 The perinæum or septum of the scrotum.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The keeper of pathics.<BR>E.<BR>विट a branch, &c., and पा to cherish, aff. क, or विट to sound, Uṇādi aff. अप, with the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिन्
विटपिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 The large Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>विटप a branch or shoot, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटमाक्षिक|विटमाक्षिकः
विटमाक्षिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mineral: see माक्षिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटलवण|विटलवणं
विटलवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A medicinal salt: see विट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटि|विटिः
विटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>Yellow saunders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्कारिका
विट्कारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of bird, (probably a variety of the Turdus Salica of Buchannan.)<BR>E.<BR>विट् from विष् fæces, and कारिका working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्खदिर|विट्खदिरः
विट्खदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fetid Mimosa.<BR>E.<BR>विट् fæces, and खदिर Mimosa catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्चर|विट्चरः
विट्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The tame or village hog.<BR>E.<BR>विट् filth, ordure, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पण्य
विट्पण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Goods, merchandise.<BR>E.<BR>विट् a Vaiśya, and पण्य wares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पति|विट्पतिः
विट्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 A son-in-law, a daughter's husband.<BR>2 A head merchant.<BR>E.<BR>विश् a Vaiśya, &c., and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्लवण
विट्लवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A fetid salt: see विड.<BR>E.<BR>विट् ordure, लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्सङ्ग|विट्संग|विट्संगः
विट्सङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Constipation.<BR>E.<BR>विट्, and सङ्ग aggregate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्सारिका
विट्सारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A bird, a sort of thrush; a variety of the bird, usually though inaccurately called Maina in Bengal.<BR>E.<BR>विट् fæces, and सारिका the same bird, or another species of the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठङ्क|विठंक
विठङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड|विडं|विडः
विड<BR>r. 6th cl. (वेडति)<BR>1 To divide, to break.<BR>2 To curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड्<BR>f. (विड्)<BR>A bit, a fragment.<BR>E.<BR>विड to break, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड|विडं|विडः
विड<BR>n. (-डं)<BR>1 Factitious salt, or salt procured by boiling soil found near the sea shore, or any earth impregnated with saline particles.<BR>2 A particular fetid kind of salt, used as a tonic aperient, commonly called black salt or Vitlavan, or Bitnoben, prepared by fusing fossile salt with a small portion of Emblic myrobalans; the produce is muriate of soda with small quantities of muriate of lime, sulphur, and oxid of iron.<BR>3 A part, a fracture, a bit.<BR>E.<BR>विड to divide, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडगन्ध
विडगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>The medicinal salt called Vitlavan: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>विड salt, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Clever, able, skilful, conversant.<BR>mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं)<BR>A vegetable and medicinal substance, considered of great efficacy as a vermifuge.<BR>E.<BR>विड to break, to curse, Uṇādi aff. अङ्गच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बन|विडंबन|विडंबनं|विडम्बनं
विडम्बन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Afflicting, distressing.<BR>2 Vexation, mortification.<BR>3 Frustrating, rendering vain.<BR>4 Imitation, copying, especially assuming a similar appearance or dress, disguise, masquerade.<BR>5 The supernatural assumption of a borrowed form, transformation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before डवि to heap, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बनीय
विडम्बनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be distressed or annoyed.<BR>2 To be assumed as a disguise.<BR>E.<BR>वि before डवि to heap, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बयत्
विडम्बयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Assuming, putting on, (as a borrowed dress or appearance.)<BR>2 Imitating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before डवि to heap, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बित|विडंबित|विडम्बितः
विडम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Low, poor, abject, distressed.<BR>2 Vexed, mortified.<BR>3 Assumed, put on, (as a borrowed form, &c.,) simulated, transformed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before डवि to heap, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=765" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडारक|विडारकः
विडारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>see the next, the ल being changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाल|विडालः
विडाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A cat.<BR>2 The eye-ball.<BR>E.<BR>विड to divide, to tear, (rats,) Uṇādi aff. कालक; also with कन् added, विडालक, and ल being changed to र, विडारक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालक|विडालकं|विडालकः
विडालक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Application of ointment to the external part of the eye, especially to the eye-lids, of which the lashes have fallen off or been ulcerated.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालपद|विडालपदः
विडालपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A measure of weight, the same as the Karṣa or weight of sixteen Māṣas.<BR>E.<BR>विडाल a cat, पद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीन|विडीनं
विडीन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>One of the different modes of flight attributed to birds, imitative flight.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, and डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडुल|विडुलः
विडुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडूरज|विडूरजं
विडूरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडोजस्
विडोजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>A name of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>विड् a fragment; (splitting mountains, &c. with his thunderbolt,) or विट् from विश् a Vaiśya, (here meaning a subject or man in general,) and ओजस् strength, splendour; also विडौजस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्ग्रह|विड्ग्रहः
विड्ग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Constipation.<BR>E.<BR>विट्, and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्ज|विड्जः
विड्ज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced from ordure.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A fungus.<BR>E.<BR>विट्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्भव
विड्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced from ordure.<BR>E.<BR>विट्, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्भुज्
विड्भुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Feeding on ordure.<BR>E.<BR>विष्, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्लवण|विड्लवणं
विड्लवण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A medicinal salt, commonly black salt, Vitlavan or Bitnoben: see विड.<BR>E.<BR>विड to divide, aff. क्विप्, and लवण salt; also विट्लवण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्वराह|विड्वराहः
विड्वराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A village or tame hog.<BR>E.<BR>विट् fæces, ordure, and वराह a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंस|वितंसः
वितंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A cage, a net, a chain or any apparatus for confining beasts or birds.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तसि to adorn, aff. घञ्; also वीतंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्ड|वितंडः|वितण्डः
वितण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A sort of lock or bolt with three divisions or wards.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 Controversy, argument, the subversion of another's opinion or interpretation, and establishment of one's own.<BR>2 Criticism.<BR>3 An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>4 Benzoin or styrax (?)<BR>5 The Oleander plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>6 A ladle, a spoon.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तडि to beat, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वितत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stretched, spread, expanded.<BR>2 Pervaded, diffused.<BR>3 Lengthened.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Any stringed instrument.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तत stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितति|विततिः
वितति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 Quantity, collection.<BR>3 A clump, a cluster, (of trees, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before तन to stretch, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततीकरण
विततीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Spreading, stretching.<BR>E.<BR>वितत, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततीकृत
विततीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stretched, spread, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वितत the same, कृत made, and च्चि augment, leaving ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत्य
वितत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having spread.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तन to spread, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ|वितथं
वितथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>False, untrue.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, तथ्य true, अच् aff., and the semivowel rejected; or वि before तम to desire, क्थन् aff., and म rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितद्रु|वितद्रुः
वितद्रु<BR>f. (-द्रुः)<BR>The name of a river, said to be situated in the Punjab.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तम to desire, aff. रु, and दङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनु|वितनुः
वितनु<BR>mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु)<BR>Thin, graceful, delicate.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and तनु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्तु|वितंतुः|वितन्तुः
वितन्तु<BR>m. (-न्तुः)<BR>A good horse.<BR>f. (-न्तुः)<BR>A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्वत्
वितन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वती-न्वत्)<BR>Spreading, stretching, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तन to stretch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरण|वितरणं
वितरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>2 Passing, crossing.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying privation, &c., and तॄ to cross, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्
वितमस्<BR>mfn. (-माः-माः-मः)<BR>1 Light, free from darkness.<BR>2 Exempt from the quality of ignorance.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv. तमस् darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क|वितर्कः
वितर्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>1 Reasoning, discussion.<BR>2 Doubt, deliberation.<BR>3 A teacher, an instructor in divine knowledge.<BR>4 Consideration of probabilities, mental anticipation of alternatives, conjecture.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying discrimination, &c., तर्क to reason or doubt, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कण|वितर्कणं
वितर्कण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Reasoning, discussion, whether mental or controversial, argument, reflection.<BR>2 Apprehension, doubt.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तर्क to reason, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्य
वितर्क्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having deliberated, considered, &c.<BR>mfn. (-र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं)<BR>Doubtful, questionable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तर्क to reason, ल्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धि
वितर्द्धि<BR>f. (-र्द्धिः-र्द्धी)<BR>1 A quadrangular building, or sort of covered terrace of wood in the centre of the court-yard of a temple or palace.<BR>2 A quadrangular resting place made of wood, a seat, a bench.<BR>3 A place in a court-yard for sitting in or standing under.<BR>4 A floor on four posts in the midst of a quadrangular house.<BR>5 A temporary stage or shed in the middle of a court-yard, for performing sacrifices, representing plays, &c.<BR>6 A terrace furnished with pillars, a verandah, a balcony.<BR>7 A covered temporary terrace on which idols are sometimes placed and worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, तर्द to injure, aff. इन्; also ङीष् optionally added, and with कन् added in the fem. form वितर्द्धिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितल|वितलं
वितल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>One of the seven divisions of Pātāla, the second in descent below the earth.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तल to be low or deep, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ति|वितस्तिः
वितस्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>A long span measured by the extended thumb and little finger, considered equal to twelve fingers.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, तस to throw, Uṇādi aff. ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Empty, pithless, sapless.<BR>2 Empty, vacant.<BR>3 Dull, stupid.<BR>4 Wicked, abandoned.<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 An awning, a canopy.<BR>3 Sacrifice, offering, oblation.<BR>4 The sacrificial hearth or hole in which the sacred fires are kept.<BR>5 A heap, a quantity.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A form of the metre Anuṣṭubh, or verse of four lines of eight syllables each; each line of the stanza named Vitāna consists of two Iambics, one Trochee, and one Spondee.<BR>2 Leisure, rest, interval of occupation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तन to spread, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानक|वितानकं|वितानकः
वितानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 An awning, a canopy, especially a cloth spread over a large open hall or court, or any open space in which dancing, singing, &c. are exhibited, at solemn or [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">Page767</a>] religious festivals.<BR>2 A heap, a quantity.<BR>3 An expanse.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=766" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकरण
वितानीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Covering, overspreading, (as a canopy.)<BR>E.<BR>वितान, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकृत
वितानीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spread or extended over, (as a canopy.)<BR>E.<BR>वितान, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितायमान
वितायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being overspread, covered, shaded, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तन to stretch, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितिष्ठमान
वितिष्ठमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Staying, being.<BR>2 Fixed, stationary.<BR>3 Permanent.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्था to stay, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वितीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Crossed, overpassed.<BR>2 Subdued, overcome.<BR>3 Effaced, rubbed out.<BR>4 Conferred, bestowed.<BR>5 Afforded, yielded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तॄ to cross, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्न|वितुन्नं
वितुन्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>1 A potherb, (Marsilia quadrifolia.)<BR>2 An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, तुन्न pained, tortured; allaying pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नक|वितुन्नकं|वितुन्नकः
वितुन्नक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Coriander seed.<BR>2 Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुष्ट
वितुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Displeased, dissatisfied.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्ण
वितृष्ण<BR>mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं)<BR>Content, satisfied, free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., तृष्णा thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्णता
वितृष्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>2 Content.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., तृष्णता cupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (वित्तयति)<BR>To quit, to abandon, especially by giving away, to give alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Judged, investigated, examined, discussed.<BR>2 Known, notorious, famous.<BR>3 Gained, acquired.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Wealth, property, thing, substance.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, to discuss, to acquire, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तद|वित्तदः
वित्तद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A benefactor, one who gives away property.<BR>E.<BR>वित्त wealth, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तवत्|वित्तवन्त्
वित्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Rich, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>वित्त, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तहीन
वित्तहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Poor, indigent.<BR>E.<BR>वित्त, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्ति|वित्तिः
वित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Discussion, discrimination, judgment, investigation.<BR>2 Knowledge.<BR>3 Gain, acquisition.<BR>4 Probability, likelihood.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, &c., aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तेहा
वित्तेहा<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>Cupidity, avarice.<BR>E.<BR>वित्त, and ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्त|वित्रस्तः
वित्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ती-स्तं)<BR>Frightened, alarmed, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>वि before त्रस to fear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रास|वित्रासः
वित्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Fear, alarm.<BR>E.<BR>वि before त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्सन|वित्सनः
वित्सन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ
विथ<BR>(ऋ) विथृ r. 1st cl. (वेथते)<BR>To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुर|विथुरः
विथुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A thief.<BR>2 An imp, a demon.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to fear, Uṇādi aff. उरन्, the semivowel changed to इ, and that unaltered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्या
विथ्या<BR>f. (-थ्या)<BR>A plant, commonly Gojihwa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद|विदः
विद<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वेत्ति वेदि)<BR>To know.<BR>With नि prefixed,<BR>To be sad or depressed.<BR>With सम्,<BR>(संवित्ते)<BR>To meditate, to know, to gain holy knowledge by abstract meditation.<BR>r. 4th cl. (विद्यते)<BR>To be, to exist, to be present, to exist actually.<BR>r. 7th cl. (विन्ते)<BR>To consider, to reason.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेदयते)<BR>1 To be sensible.<BR>2 To know.<BR>3 To declare, to describe or explain; (in this sense नि is usually prefixed.)<BR>4 To dwell, to inhabit.<BR>5 To be fixed or steady.<BR>6 To suffer pain.<BR>With नि, or वि and नि prefixed,<BR>To deliver, to impart or communicate.<BR>With प्रति,<BR>To deliver, to give.<BR>(औ ऌ) औ विटॢ r. 6th cl. (विन्दति-ते)<BR>To gain, to get, to acquire or possess.<BR>With परि,<BR>To marry first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद्<BR>mfn. (वित्)<BR>Who or what knows.<BR>E.<BR>विद् to know, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
विदग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>1 Clever, shrewd, knowing.<BR>2 Sharp, witty.<BR>3 Intriguing.<BR>4 Undigested.<BR>5 Burnt.<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>1 A libertine, a lecher, an intriguer.<BR>2 A learned or clever man, a scholar, a Paṇḍita.<BR>f. (-ग्धा)<BR>A sharp knowing woman.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दह to burn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धता
विदग्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Sharpness, shrewdness, cleverness, wit.<BR>E.<BR>तल् aff. of the abstract, added to the last; also with त्व aff. विदग्धत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदत्
विदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्)<BR>Wise, intelligent, learned, knowing.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथ|विदथः
विदथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A wise or learned man, a sage, a scholar.<BR>2 A saint, a devotee.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, Uṇādi aff. अथ, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदधत्
विदधत्<BR>mfn. (-धन्-धती-धत्)<BR>Having, wearing, assuming.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर|विदरं|विदरः
विदर<BR>m. (-रं)<BR>Tearing, rending.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The Indian prickly pear, (Cactus Indicus.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भ|विदर्भः
विदर्भ<BR>mf. (-र्भः-र्भा)<BR>A district and city to the south-west of Bengal, the modern Bara-Nagpur or Berar proper.<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>Any dry or desart soil.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and दर्भ the sacred grass; not growing in that country in consequence of the curse of a saint, whose son had died of a wound from a blade of the grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भजा
विदर्भजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>2 DAMAYANTĪ the wife of NALA, and heroine of the Naiṣadha or poem so called.<BR>3 RUKMIṆĪ the wife of KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>विदर्भ the country, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
विदल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Opened, expanded, blown, (as a flower, &c.)<BR>2 Rent, split.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A shallow basket made of split bambus, a vessel of wicker work.<BR>2 Split peas.<BR>3 Pomegranate bark.<BR>4 The cuttings or chips of any substance, that which has been pared or split.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Dividing, separating.<BR>2 A cake.<BR>3 Mountain ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before दल tearing, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलित
विदलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Rent, torn, split.<BR>2 Blown, expanded, (as a flower.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before दल to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलीकरण
विदलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Rending, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>विदल, and करण making, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलीकृत
विदलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Divided, separated.<BR>2 Cut, split, torn, broken.<BR>E.<BR>विदल dividing, कृत made, and च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदश्यमान
विदश्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being bitten.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दशि to bite, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदा
विदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>2 Intellect, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदार|विदारः
विदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Tearing, rending.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>3 An inundation, an overflow, the rising of a river or pond above its banks.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>2 A climbing plant, (Ipomoea paniculata.)<BR>3 Bubo, swelling in the groin, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, to divide, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=767" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारक|विदारकं|विदारकः
विदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A divider, a render or tearer.<BR>2 A tree or rock in the middle of a stream, dividing its course.<BR>3 A hole or pit for water sunk in the bed of a dry river, &c.<BR>f. (-रिका)<BR>1 A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>2 A bubo.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to divide, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारण|विदारणं|विदारणः
विदारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Tearing, breaking, splitting, severing, dividing.<BR>2 Paining, afflicting.<BR>3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>War, battle.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A tree, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारयत्
विदारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Tearing, rending, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारित
विदारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Torn, rent, split, broken.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दॄ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारीगन्धा
विदारीगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>विदारी a plant, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारु|विदारुः
विदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A lizard.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदार्य्य|विदार्य
विदार्य्य<BR>ind. (-र्य्यः)<BR>Having torn or rent.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and दॄ to tear, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाह|विदाहः
विदाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Heat, burning.<BR>2 Pungency.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दह to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहिन्
विदाहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>1 Burning, hot.<BR>2 Pungent, acrid.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दह to burn, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिक्चङ्ग|विदिक्चङ्गः
विदिक्चङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>विदिश् a point of the compass, and चङ्ग handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित|विदितं|विदितः
विदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Known, understood.<BR>2 Promised, agreed, assented.<BR>3 Represented, submitted, solicited.<BR>4 Apprised, informed, who or what knows.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A sage, a learned man.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Information, representation.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित्वा
विदित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having known.<BR>2 Having promised.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, क्ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिश्
विदिश्<BR>f. (-दिक्)<BR>An intermediate point of the compass.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying separation, and दिश् a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्ण|विदीर्णः
विदीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Torn, split, burst or broken.<BR>2 Expanded, opened.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दृ to tear, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्य्यमाण|विदीर्यमाण
विदीर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being torn, split, broken, cut, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दॄ to rend, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदु|विदुः
विदु<BR>m. (-दुः)<BR>1 The hollow between the frontal globes of an elephant.<BR>2 The hippopotamus.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, (the goad,) aff. कु; also with कू aff. विदू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुर|विदुरः
विदुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Wise, knowing, intelligent.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A libertine, an intriguer.<BR>2 A learned or clever man.<BR>3 The younger brother and counsellor of DHṚTARĀṢṬRA.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुल|विदुलः
विदुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of reed, (Calamus rotang); also the same growing in water, (C. fasciculatus.)<BR>2 Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, &c., Uṇādi aff. उलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदून
विदून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Agitated, distressed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and दु to distress, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूर|विदूरः
विदूर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very far or remote.<BR>E.<BR>वि intervening, and दूर distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरग|विदूरगः
विदूरग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Spreading, going far or wide.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दूर far, remote, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरज|विदूरजं
विदूरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूराद्रि|विदूराद्रिः
विदूराद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The name of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>विदूर remote, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषक|विदूषकः
विदूषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-षिका-कं)<BR>1 Facetious, witty, a wag, a jester.<BR>2 Censorious, detracting, a detractor or abuser of other people.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An actor, especially an interlocutor with the audience between the acts or scenes, a jester, a buffoon.<BR>2 (In dramatic language,) The humble and jocose companion of the principal character.<BR>3 A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दूष to be or make bad, aff. क्कुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषण|विदूषणं
विदूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Censuring, reviling, abuse, satire.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दूष to make bad or faulty, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेश|विदेशः
विदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A foreign country, abroad.<BR>2 Any place away from home.<BR>E.<BR>वि variety, देश place or country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशगत
विदेशगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone abroad.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशगमन
विदेशगमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Travelling, going abroad.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशज
विदेशज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Foreign, exotic.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशस्थ
विदेशस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Who or what remains abroad.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशिन्
विदेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Foreign, foreigner, exotic.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेह|विदेहः
विदेह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Incorporeal, without body.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A sovereign of the family of JANAKA, king of Mithilā.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A district in the province of Behar, the same as the ancient Mithilā, or the modern Tirhut.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्ध|विद्धः
विद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pierced, perforated.<BR>2 Thrown, cast, directed, sent.<BR>3 Like, resembling.<BR>4 Opposed, impeded.<BR>5 Beaten, whipped.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>विध to pierce, or व्यध to beat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्धकर्ण|विद्धकर्णः
विद्धकर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>Having the ears pierced or slit.<BR>mf. (-र्णः-र्णा or -र्णी)<BR>A plant, commonly Aknadhi, (Cissampelos hexandra, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>विद्ध pierced, and कर्ण the ear; also in the latter sense, with कन् added विद्धकर्णिका; also अविद्धकर्ण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमान|विद्यमानः
विद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being, being present or in existence.<BR>2 Actual, real, in possession, (as property.)<BR>E.<BR>विद to be, 4th cl. and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्या
विद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Knowledge, learning, science, whether sacred or profane, though more especially the former: it is sometimes classed into fourteen divisions; or the four Vedas; the six Aṅgas, or grammar, astronomy, &c.; the Purāṇas as the eleventh class; and the Mīmāṃsā or theology, Nyāya or logic, and Dharma or law, as the remaining three.<BR>2 The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>3 A tree, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>4 A magical pill or bolus, by putting which into the mouth a person has the power of ascending to heaven.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, and aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याकर|विद्याकरः
विद्याकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Giving wisdom or science.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A learned man.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and कर what makes, or आकर a mine: see विद्याघर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यागम|विद्यागमः
विद्यागम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Acquirement of knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याचण|विद्याचणः
विद्याचण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Famous for learning or knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या knowledge, and चणप् aff. in this particular meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=768" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याचुञ्चु|विद्याचुञ्चुः
विद्याचुञ्चु<BR>mfn. (-ञ्चुः-ञ्चुः-ञ्चु)<BR>Famous for knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या knowledge, and चुञ्चुप् aff. implying celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादल|विद्यादलः
विद्यादल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Bhojpatra tree.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and दल a leaf: being used for writing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादान|विद्यादानं
विद्यादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving knowledge or science.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादेवी
विद्यादेवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A female divinity, one of a class of sixteen, peculiar apparently to the mythological system of the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या science, and देवी a goddess; a goddess of learning or science, a muse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याधन|विद्याधनं
विद्याधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Property acquired by science, as by instruction, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या knowledge, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याधर|विद्याधरः
विद्याधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A demigod of a particular order or class, a spirit of the air.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या a magical pill, as above, and धर who has or holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुपालन
विद्यानुपालन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Patronising learning.<BR>2 Studying, acquiring learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अनुपालन encouraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुपालिन्
विद्यानुपालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Studied, acquiring or having acquired learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अनुपालिन् who prosecutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुसेवन
विद्यानुसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cultivating science or learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अनुसेवन pursuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुसेविन्
विद्यानुसेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Cultivating learning, engaged in study.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अनुसेविन् addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याप्राप्ति|विद्याप्राप्तिः
विद्याप्राप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Acquirement of knowledge.<BR>2 Acquisition made by or through learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and प्राप्ति gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याभ्यास|विद्याभ्यासः
विद्याभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Study, diligent application.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्ज्जन|विद्यार्जन
विद्यार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Acquiring knowledge.<BR>2 Acquiring any thing by knowledge, as by teaching, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अर्ज्जन gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्ज्जित|विद्यार्जित
विद्यार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gained by or through knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अर्ज्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्थ|विद्यार्थः
विद्यार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>Seeking for knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्थिन्
विद्यार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Seeking for knowledge.<BR>m. (-र्थी)<BR>A pupil, a student.<BR>E.<BR>विद्यार्थ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालब्ध
विद्यालब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>Gained by or through learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालय|विद्यालयः
विद्यालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A school, a college.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and आलय a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालाभ|विद्यालाभः
विद्यालाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 Acquisition of learning.<BR>2 Acquirement by or through learning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यावत्|विद्यावन्त्
विद्यावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Learned, possessed of learning or science.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या learning, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याविशिष्ट
विद्याविशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Possessed of learning or science.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and विशिष्ट endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याविहीन
विद्याविहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ignorant, uninstructed.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and विहीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याव्रतस्नातक|विद्याव्रतस्नातकः
विद्याव्रतस्नातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Brahman who has finished his studies and period of studentship.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and व्रत a religious obligation, स्नातक a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यास्नातक|विद्यास्नातकः
विद्यास्नातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The student who has finished his religious studies.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and स्नातक a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याहीन
विद्याहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Ignorant, uninstructed.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
विद्युत्<BR>f. (-द्युत्)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>वि intensitive or privative, and द्युत light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्वत्|विद्युत्वन्त्
विद्युत्वत्<BR>mfn. (-त्वान्-त्वती-त्वत्)<BR>Having or containing lightning, electrical, (a cloud, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>विद्युत् lightning, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्प्रिय|विद्युत्प्रियं
विद्युत्प्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Bell-metal.<BR>E.<BR>विद्युत् lightning, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युल्लता
विद्युल्लता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Zigzag lightning.<BR>E.<BR>विद्युत्, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योतमान
विद्योतमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Shining, blazing, flashing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्युत to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योपार्ज्जन|विद्योपार्जन
विद्योपार्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Acquisition of knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and उपार्ज्जन collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योपार्ज्जित|विद्योपार्जित
विद्योपार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Acquired by or through learning, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विद्या, and उपार्ज्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्र|विद्रं|विद्रः
विद्र<BR>n. (-द्रं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm.<BR>2 Piercing, perforating.<BR>E.<BR>विघ to pierce, aff. रक्, form irr., or वि before द्रा to sleep, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधि|विद्रधिः
विद्रधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Phlegmonoid inflammation; especially deep seated, or internal abscess.<BR>E.<BR>विद्र piercing, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधिनाशन|विद्रधिनाशनः
विद्रधिनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera Morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>विद्रधि a bile or abscess, नाशन destroying, discussing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रव|विद्रवः
विद्रव<BR>m. (-बः)<BR>1 Flight, escape, retreat.<BR>2 Fear, agitation, panic.<BR>3 Intellect, understanding.<BR>4 Censure, abuse, reproach.<BR>5 Liquefaction.<BR>6 Flowing out, oozing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to fly, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राव|विद्रावः
विद्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Flight, retreat, running away.<BR>2 Liquefaction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to go, causal v., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावक
विद्रावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Liquefying, causing to flow or melt.<BR>2 Driving away.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to flow, &c., causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावण|विद्रावणं
विद्रावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Causing to flow or melt, fusing, liquefying.<BR>2 Driving away, chasing, defeating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to run, &c. causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावित|विद्रावितं
विद्रावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Liquefied, fused.<BR>2 Driven away, put to flight.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to flow, &c., causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुत|विद्रुतः
विद्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Liquid, liquefied, fluid, as an oily or metallic substance upon being heated.<BR>2 Flown, fled.<BR>3 Running, going fast.<BR>4 Agitated, alarmed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्रु to ooze, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुम|विद्रुमः
विद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Coral.<BR>2 A tree bearing precious gems.<BR>3 A young sprout or shoot.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying species, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुमलता
विद्रुमलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A sort of vegetable perfume.<BR>E.<BR>विद्रुम coral, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वत्कल्प|विद्वत्कल्पः
विद्वत्कल्प<BR>mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>Less learned, a little learned.<BR>E.<BR>विद्वत् learned, and कल्प aff. of diminution or inferiority; also with the similar affs. देशीयर् and देश्य, विद्वद्देशीय and विद्वद्देश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वस्
विद्वस्<BR>mfn. (-द्वान्-दुषी-द्वत्)<BR>1 Intelligent, wise.<BR>2 Learned.<BR>m. (-द्वान्)<BR>A sage, a seer, one who knows the true nature of the soul and of GOD.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, वसु aff. in lieu of शतृ, the usual affix of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्
विद्विष्<BR>mfn. (-द्विट्)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्विष to hate, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष|विद्विषः
विद्विष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Hating, adverse, inimical.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्विष to hate, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्ट
विद्विष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Hated, disliked.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्विष to hate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=769" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष|विद्वेषः
विद्वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Enmity, hatred.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्विष to hate, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषिन्
विद्वेषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Inimical, hostile, hating.<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>विद्वेष enmity, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष्टृ
विद्वेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>Who or what hates, adverse, inimical.<BR>E.<BR>वि before द्विष to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध|विधः
विध<BR>r. 6th cl. (विधते)<BR>1 To administer, to govern, to rule or command.<BR>2 To pierce, to perforate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध|विधः
विध<BR>mf. (-धः-धा)<BR>1 Form, formula, rule.<BR>2 Manner, kind, sort.<BR>3 Fodder, the food of horses, elephants, &c.<BR>4 Prosperity, thriving.<BR>5 Hire, wages.<BR>6 Act, action.<BR>7 Piercing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, aff. क, or अङ्, and fem. aff. टाप्; or विध to rule, &c., aff. क; the masculine form, though it does occur, is not common, except in composition, when the word is used attributively, as द्विविध of two sorts. mfn. (-धः-धा-धं), &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवन|विधवनं
विधवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to shake, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवा
विधवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A widow.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, धव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवागामिन्
विधवागामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>One who has intercourse with a widow.<BR>E.<BR>विधवा, and गामिन् who approaches, (carnally.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवावेदन
विधवावेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marrying a widow.<BR>E.<BR>विधवा, and आवेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधव्य|विधव्यं
विधव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Trembling, tremor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to shake, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधस्
विधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally or every kind, धा to have, Uṇādi aff. असुन्, and the radical vowel dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातव्य
विधातव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be done or performed.<BR>2 To be done according to rule, to be observed as a rite or ceremony.<BR>3 To be ruled or regulated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
विधातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Love or KĀMA.<BR>3 Fate.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, धा to have or contain, (all things,) aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृभू
विधातृभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>NĀRADA, the Muni and son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>विधातृ BRAHMĀ, and भू offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्रायुस्
विधात्रायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>The sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्री
विधात्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>Long-pepper.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, तृच् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधान|विधानं
विधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Act, action, general or particular, though more especially the performance of such acts or rites as are prescribed in the sacred books of the Hindus.<BR>2 Rule, precept, ordinance, injunction.<BR>3 An elephant's fodder.<BR>4 Form, mode, manner.<BR>5 Sending, ordering.<BR>6 Means, expedient.<BR>7 Wealth.<BR>8 Worship.<BR>9 Active enmity or act of hostility.<BR>10 Gaining, getting, taking.<BR>11 Conflict or contrast of opposite feelings.<BR>12 (In grammar,) Affixing, prefixing, taking as an affix, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधान|विधानं
विधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Having, possessing, assuming, wearing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानक|विधानकं
विधानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Pain.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, ल्युट् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानग|विधानगः
विधानग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a wise or learned man or teacher.<BR>E.<BR>विधान action, the performance of those acts prescribed by the Śāstras, and ग who goes or performs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानज्ञ|विधानज्ञः
विधानज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A Paṇḍita, &c.: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>विधान, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाय
विधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken, assumed, put on, placed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायक|विधायकः
विधायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Consigning, delivering, one who entrusts or deposits any thing, or causes it to be fixed or secure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, (causal form,) aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायकत्व
विधायकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Consignment or delivery of any thing, making any thing firm or secure.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, विधायकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायिन्
विधायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Causing, occasioning, making.<BR>2 Placing, fixing, securing.<BR>3 Delivering, entrusting.<BR>4 Establishing as a rule or law.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have or hold, causal form, aff. धिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाव्य|विधाव्यं
विधाव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Shaking, agitation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घू to shake, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधास्यत्
विधास्यत्<BR>mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यती-स्यत्)<BR>1 Purposing or willing to do, make, cause, &c.<BR>2 Intending to direct, enjoin, prescribe, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, शतृ aff. in the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधि|विधिः
विधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 A sacred precept, an act or rite prescribed by the Vedas for effecting certain consequences.<BR>2 Rule, form, formula.<BR>3 Fate, luck, destiny.<BR>4 BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 Time.<BR>6 Order, injunction, command.<BR>7 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>8 Act, action, general or particular.<BR>9 A text, a sentence in some authority of law or religion, prescribing any particular act or observance.<BR>10 Kind, sort, manner.<BR>11 Fodder, food for elephants or horses.<BR>12 A sacred work, a Śāstra, scripture, the law, (by metonymy.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, or विध to rule, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिघ्न
विधिघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Who or what deviates from, disregards, or disturbs rules or modes of proceeding.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिज्ञ|विधिज्ञः
विधिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Who or what knows the prescribed mode, form, &c.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A Brahman who knows the ritual.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधितस्
विधितस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to rule.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
विधित्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>Wish to do or make, design, purpose, desire.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सु
विधित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing to make, produce, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदर्शिन्
विधिदर्शिन्<BR>m. (-र्शी)<BR>A priest whose business at a sacrifice is to see that every thing is done according to the prescribed rules, and to correct any deviation from them.<BR>E.<BR>विधि a sacred precept, and दर्शिन् who sees; also विधिदर्शक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदेशक|विधिदेशकः
विधिदेशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A priest who corrects errors at a sacrifice: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>विधि the proper form, and देशक who shews.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिपूर्व्वक
विधिपूर्व्वक<BR>n. adv. (-कं)<BR>After or according to rule.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and पर्व्वक prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रयोग|विधिप्रयोगः
विधिप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Acting upon or in conformity to a rule, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रसङ्ग
विधिप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Application of or acting upon a rule.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and प्रसङ्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियज्ञ|विधियज्ञः
विधियज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A ceremonial act of worship.<BR>E.<BR>विधि precept, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियोग|विधियोगः
विधियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 The occurrence of predoomed events.<BR>2 Combination for any act or rite.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and योग union, accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=770" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवत्
विधिवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Agreeable to rule, conformably to established ordinances.<BR>E.<BR>विधि a precept, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिहीन
विधिहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Unauthorised, irregular.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधीयमान
विधीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being defined, enjoined, directed, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधु|विधुः
विधु<BR>m. (-धुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 Camphor.<BR>4 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>5 A Rākṣasa, a fiend, a goblin.<BR>6 An expiatory oblation.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pain or hurt, Uṇādi aff. कु, and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुक्षय|विधुक्षयः
विधुक्षय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The wane of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>विधु, and क्षय decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुत|विधुतः
विधुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left, abandoned, relinquished.<BR>2 Shaken, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धु to tremble, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुति|विधुतिः
विधुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to agitate, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुनन|विधुननं
विधुनन<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>Tremour, trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू in the 10th cl. to shake, aff. ल्युट्, and the vowel short; also विधूनन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्तुद|विधुंतुद|विधुंतुदः|विधुन्तुदः
विधुन्तुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>विध the moon, तुद to torment, aff. खश् or क, and the nasal inserted, the cause of the moon's eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्वत्
विधुन्वत्<BR>mfn. (-न्वत्-न्वती-न्वत्)<BR>Shaking, tossing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घु to agitate, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुपञ्जर|विधुपञ्जरः
विधुपञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A scimitar, a sabre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुप्रिया
विधुप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A lunar mansion; in mythology, personified as a nymph, the daughter of DAKṢA, and wife of CANDRA or the moon.<BR>E.<BR>बिधु the moon, and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Agitated, distressed, overcome with anxiety, distress, &c.<BR>2 Bewildered, confused, (with fear, liquor, &c.)<BR>3 Separate, absent from a mistress or lover.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Separation.<BR>2 Agitation of mind from terror or distress, &c.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Curds mixed up with sugar and spices.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धुर् a load, a burthen, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवन|विधुवनं
विधुवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trembling, tremor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to agitate, ल्युट् aff., and उवङ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूत|विधूतं
विधूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken.<BR>2 Trembling, tremulous.<BR>3 Unsteady.<BR>4 Abandoned.<BR>5 Tossed, waving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to agitate, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूति|विधूतिः
विधूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Shaking, agitation, tremor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घू to shake, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनन|विधूननं
विधूनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, trembling, tremor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before घू to agitate, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनित|विधूनितं
विधूनित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, (literally or figuratively,) agitated, alarmed.<BR>2 Harassed, annoyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to shake, 10th cl. aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूय
विधूय<BR>ind.<BR>Having shaken, shaking, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to shake, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूयमान
विधूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being shaken, shaking, waving, agitated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धू to shake, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृत|विधृतं
विधृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seized, held.<BR>2 Withheld, restrained.<BR>3 Having, possessing, assumed, taken.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Disregard of an injunction or desire.<BR>2 Dissatisfaction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेय|विधेयः
विधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 Compliant, tractable, governable.<BR>2 To be done, what is or ought to be practised.<BR>3 Proper to be enjoined as a rule or law.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयता
विधेयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Necessary or proper act or conduct.<BR>2 Docility, submission.<BR>3 Fitness for enactment as a rule or law.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also विधेयत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयमार्ग
विधेयमार्ग<BR>n. (-र्गं)<BR>Attempting or seeking to do any necessary act.<BR>E.<BR>विधेय, and मार्ग seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयपद
विधेयपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>An affair to be done, an object to be accomplished.<BR>E.<BR>विधेय, and पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यत्|विध्यन्त्
विध्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्)<BR>Piercing, striking, killing.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यमान
विध्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being pierced, struck, wounded, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस|विध्वंसः
विध्वंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Aversion, disrespect, enmity, dislike.<BR>2 Offence, insult.<BR>3 Destruction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ध्वंस to fall, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
विध्वंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Hostile, adverse.<BR>2 Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ध्वंस to fall, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनत|विनतः
विनत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bent, bowed, stooping.<BR>2 Crooked, curved.<BR>3 Humble, modest.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The wife of KAŚYAPA, and mother of ARUṆA and GARUḌA.<BR>2 A sort of basket.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नम to bow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतासूनु|विनतासूनुः
विनतासूनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR>2 GARUḌA, the younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>विनता the mother of these two, and सूनु the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनति|विनतिः
विनति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Bowing, bending.<BR>2 Humility, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नम to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद|विनदः
विनद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>2 A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>वि, नद to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्य
विनद्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sounded, sounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नद to sound, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमन|विनमनं
विनमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bending, bowing, bending down.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नम to bend, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमित
विनमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bowed down, declined.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नमित bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
विनम्र<BR>mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>1 Bent, bowed.<BR>2 Humble, modest.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नम्र bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Modesty, affability, humility, mildness.<BR>2 Reverence, obeisance.<BR>3 Decorum, decency, propriety, of conduct or behaviour.<BR>4 Training, discipline.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A plant, (Sida cordifolia, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to obtain or guide, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयग्राहिन्
विनयग्राहिन्<BR>mfn. (-हि-हिणी-हि)<BR>Compliant, tractable, humble, governable.<BR>E.<BR>विनय humility, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयप्रमाथिन्
विनयप्रमाथिन्<BR>mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>Behaving ill or improperly.<BR>E.<BR>विनय, and प्रमाथिन् vexing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयभाज्
विनयभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भा)<BR>Modest, well-behaved.<BR>E.<BR>विनय, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयवाच्
विनयवाच्<BR>mfn. (-वाक्)<BR>Speaking humbly or modestly.<BR>f. (-वाक्)<BR>Modest speech.<BR>E.<BR>विनय, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयस्थ|विनयस्थः
विनयस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Compliant, tractable, governable.<BR>E.<BR>विनय humility, and स्थ who stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्द्दत्|विनर्दत्
विनर्द्दत्<BR>mfn. (-र्द्दन्-र्द्दन्ती-र्द्दत्)<BR>Sounding, making a noise.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नर्द्द to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=771" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशन|विनशनं|विनशनः
विनशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Destroying, destruction.<BR>2 A country, northwest of Delhi, Kurukṣetra, the vicinity of the modern Paniput.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to destroy, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्यत्
विनश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यती-श्यत्)<BR>Perishing, decaying, perishable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्वर
विनश्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Perishable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, क्वरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्ट|विनष्टः
विनष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Lost, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नष्ट the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्टि|विनष्टिः
विनष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Disappearance, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to finish, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनस|विनसः
विनस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सी-सं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and नस for नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना<BR>ind.<BR>Without, except.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, ना aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाकृत|विनाकृतं
विनाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Abandoned, left, relinquished.<BR>E.<BR>विना except, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिका
विनाडिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The 60th part of an Indian hour.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नाडिका a Nārī, or hour of twenty-four minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाथ
विनाथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Deserted, unprotected, unowned.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., नाथ a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायक|विनायकः
विनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A Buddha, a Bauddha deified teacher.<BR>2 GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 A Guru, or spiritual preceptor.<BR>5 An obstacle, an impediment or difficulty.<BR>f. (-यिका)<BR>The wife of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to conduct, to obtain, aff. खुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाश|विनाशः
विनाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Disappearance, destruction, loss, annihilation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशक|विनाशकः
विनाशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Destroying, a destroyer.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, causal form, aff. वुञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशयत्
विनाशयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशित
विनाशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशिन्
विनाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिणी-शि)<BR>1 Destroyer, destructive.<BR>2 Perishing, being destroyed.<BR>3 Undergoing change or transformation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नश to perish, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशोन्मुख|विनाशोन्मुखं
विनाशोन्मुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Ripe, mature.<BR>E.<BR>विनाश perishing, उन्मुख in the presence of; verging to rottenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासक|विनासकः
विनासक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Noseless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, नासिका the nose, or नासा with कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाह|विनाहः
विनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The top or cover of a well.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नह to bind or tie, aff. घञ्; also वीनाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसरण
विनिःसरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Going forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before सू to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसृत
विनिःसृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before सृत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्त|विनिक्षिप्तः
विनिक्षिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Tossed, thrown, sent.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before क्षिप्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षेप|विनिक्षेपः
विनिक्षेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Tossing, throwing, sending.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before क्षिप to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिघ्नत्
विनिघ्नत्<BR>mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्)<BR>Killing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्र|विनिद्रः
विनिद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Blown, budded.<BR>2 Awake, awakened, sleepless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्रत्व|विनिद्रत्वं
विनिद्रत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Vigilance, wakefulness, waking.<BR>E.<BR>विनिद्र sleepless, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, विनिद्रता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिधाय
विनिधाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken or placed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नि before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपात|विनिपातः
विनिपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Falling, falling down, (literally or figuratively, as from a height, or from dignity, virtue, &c.)<BR>2 Calamity, unavoidable evil, the infliction of the gods or of fate.<BR>3 Disrespect.<BR>4 Pain, distress.<BR>5 Death, destruction.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, prefixed to पत to fall, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातशंसिन्
विनिपातशंसिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Portentous, announcing misfortune or destruction.<BR>E.<BR>बिनिपात, and शंसिन् what proclaims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातित
विनिपातित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Killed, destroyed.<BR>2 Thrown down.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नि before पत to fall, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपात्य
विनिपात्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having killed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before पत to fall, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमय|विनिमयः
विनिमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Barter, exchange.<BR>2 A pledge, a deposite or security.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, prefixed to मी to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियत
विनियत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Regulated, restrained.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before यम to restrain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम|विनियमः
विनियम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Restraint, government.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before यम to restrain, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम्य
विनियम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having restrained, checked, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before यम to restrain, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुक्त
विनियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Separated, sundered or detached from, absent, parted.<BR>2 Appointed, attached to.<BR>3 Parted with for a specific purpose.<BR>4 Applied to, employed in.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before युज to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोक्तव्य
विनियोक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be employed in, applied to, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before युज to join, तव्यर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोग|विनियोगः
विनियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Giving or parting with any thing for a consideration, or in expectation of some advantage.<BR>2 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>3 Separation or detachment from.<BR>4 Impediment.<BR>5 Appointment to any office, &c.<BR>6 Application to or employment in.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before युज to join, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोजित|विनियोजितः
विनियोजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Appointed, appropriated, applied, (as to any particular duty or purpose, &c.)<BR>2 Attached or joined to.<BR>3 Deputed, appointed.<BR>4 Employed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि, before युज to join, aff. क्त, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गत
विनिर्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone out or from.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before गम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गम|विनिर्गमः
विनिर्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Going forth or out.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before गम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जय|विनिर्जयः
विनिर्जय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Victory, conquest.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before जि to conquer, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्ज्जित|विनिर्जित
विनिर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conquered, overcome.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before जि to conquer, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णय|विनिर्णयः
विनिर्णय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and निर्णय the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णीत
विनिर्णीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Certain, determined, ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>वि before निर्णीत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्द्धूत
विनिर्द्धूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Scattered, dissipated, dispersed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and निर्द्धूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्धूय
विनिर्धूय<BR>ind.<BR>Having dispersed, scattered, thrown off, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर्, before धू to agitate, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=772" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुक्त
विनिर्मुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Liberated, let loose or free.<BR>2 Exempt, free from.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर् before मुच to loose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्य्यत्|विनिर्यत्
विनिर्य्यत्<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यन्-र्य्यन्ती-र्य्यत्)<BR>Going out or forth, issuing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर् before या to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्वृत्त|विनिर्वृत्तः
विनिर्वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Excited, occasioned, produced, occurring.<BR>2 Completed, finished.<BR>E.<BR>वि and निर् privative or intensitive prefixes, वृत to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवारित
विनिवारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Kept off, resisted, prevented.<BR>2 Screened, covered, kept out of view.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि before वॄ to chuse, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्त|विनिवृत्तः
विनिवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Stopped, ceased, ended, refrained, resting or desisting, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि privatives, वृत to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्ति|विनिवृत्तिः
विनिवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Stop, term, cessation.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि before वृत to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चय|विनिश्चयः
विनिश्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and निश्चय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चल
विनिश्चल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Firm, steady, immovable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before निश्चल steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चित
विनिश्चित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Certain, determined, ascertained.<BR>E.<BR>वि before निश्चित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वसत्
विनिश्वसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>1 Sighing.<BR>2 Breathing hard.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि before श्वस to breathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वास|विनिश्वासः
विनिश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Strong expiration, sighing, breathing hard.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नि before श्वस to breathe, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत|विनिहतः
विनिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Struck, wounded.<BR>2 Overcome.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A portent, a comet, a meteor.<BR>2 A great or unavoidable calamity; the infliction of fate or heaven.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि intensitive prefixes, हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिह्नुत
विनिह्नुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Hidden, concealed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and निह्वुत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीत|विनीतः
विनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Modest, humble, unassuming, unpretending.<BR>2 Compliant, governable, tractable.<BR>3 Placid, meek, virtuous, gentle, having the passions restrained, and the senses under subjection.<BR>4 Well-behaved, decent, decorous.<BR>5 Taken.<BR>6 Trained, (as a horse or ox, &c.)<BR>7 Thrown, sent, dismissed.<BR>8 Lovely, handsome.<BR>9 Led, conveyed.<BR>10 Chastised, punished.<BR>11 Plain, neat, (in dress, &c.)<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A horse trained for the manege.<BR>2 A merchant, a trader.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to guide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतक|विनीतकं
विनीतक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A mediate conveyance, as a bearer carrying a litter, or a horse dragging a carriage.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying sort or kind, and णी to take, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतात्मन्
विनीतात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>1 Well-behaved.<BR>2 Humble, lowly.<BR>E.<BR>विनीत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीय|विनीयः
विनीय<BR>ind.<BR>Having taken.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Sediment, dregs.<BR>2 Sin.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to take, aff. क्यप् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्यमान
विनुद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being sent, ordered, dispatched, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नुद to send, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
विनेतृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>1 A guide, an instructor, a teacher.<BR>2 A king, a ruler.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to conduct, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेय|विनेयः
विनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be taken, to be taken away or separated, &c.<BR>2 To be governed or directed, docile, governable.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to take or obtain, &c., aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेश्यत्
विनेश्यत्<BR>mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>Wishing or intending to take or take away, to deprive of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to take, शतृ aff. with a future sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोक्ति|विनोक्तिः
विनोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>The rhetorical use of the word, ‘without;’ as, का निशाशशि ना विना What is the night without the moon.<BR>E.<BR>विना, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोद|विनोदः
विनोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>2 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>3 Dismissing, abandoning.<BR>4 Interest, interesting pursuit or occupation.<BR>5 Pleasure, gratification.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नुद to order, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदित
विनोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dismissed, dissipated, sent or driven away.<BR>2 Allayed, soothed.<BR>3 Delighted, made happy.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नुद to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द|विन्दः
विन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>Who or what finds, gets, gains, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विद to gain, श aff., नुन् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दु|विंदु|विन्दुः
विन्दु<BR>mfn. (-न्दुः-न्दुः-न्दु)<BR>1 Intelligent, knowing.<BR>2 Liberal, munificent.<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 A drop of water or any liquid.<BR>2 A spot, a dot, a mark.<BR>3 The bite or mark of a tooth.<BR>4 The part of the forehead between the eye-brows.<BR>5 A mark or spot of coloured paint on an elephant's face or trunk.<BR>6 The dot over a letter representing the nasal termination.<BR>7 A secondary but connecting incident in a drama.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, to be, to be a part of, Uṇādi aff. उ, and the nasal augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुचित्रक|विन्दुचित्रकः
विन्दुचित्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The spotted deer.<BR>E.<BR>विन्दु a spot, and चित्रक variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुजाल|विन्दुजालं
विन्दुजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Coloured marks or spots on an elephant's face and trunk, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विन्दु a spot, and जाल multitude; also with कन् added, विन्दुजालक n. (-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुतन्त्र|विन्दुतन्त्रः
विन्दुतन्त्र<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>A die, a dice.<BR>E.<BR>विन्दु a dot, and तन्त्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुरेखक|विन्दुरेखकः
विन्दुरेखक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>विन्दु a spot, and रेखा a line, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्धपत्र
विन्धपत्र<BR>f. (-त्रः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bel Saṇṭh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्य|विंध्यः|विन्ध्यः
विन्ध्य<BR>m. (-न्ध्यः)<BR>1 The Vindhya or Bindh mountain, or the mountainous range which runs across India from the province of Behar, nearly to Guzerat, and properly divides Hindustan from the Dekhin.<BR>2 A hunter.<BR>f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>1 A fruit, (Annona reticulata.).<BR>2 Small cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying opposition, ध्यै to think, and क aff., form irr.; the mountain is supposed to obstruct the course of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यकूट|विन्ध्यकूटः
विन्ध्यकूट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The saint AGASTYA.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्य the mountain, and कूट to give pain, aff. क, or with युच् aff. विन्ध्यकूटन; Vindhya the personified mountain, having once prostrated himself before AGASTYA his spiritual guide, was ordered by the saint to remain in that posture, as a punishment for the presumption, which had induced him to attempt rivalling the heighth of Meru and Himālaya. The legend appears to originate in the little elevation of the Vindhya chain compared with its extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यवासिन्
विन्ध्यवासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>The saint and grammarian VYĀḌI.<BR>f. (-सिनी)<BR>1 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2 A village and temple sacred to DURGĀ under the forms of Yoga Māyā, and Bhoga Māyā, and a place of great resort amongst the Hindus, situated about three miles from Mirzāpur on the Ganges.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्य the mountain, and वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=773" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यस्थ|विन्ध्यस्थः
विन्ध्यस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>The name of a Muni; also VYĀḌI, a saint, and inspired grammarian.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्य the mountain, and स्थ abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याचल
विन्ध्याचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The Vindhya range of mountains.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्य, and अचल a mountain; also विन्ध्यपर्ब्बत, विन्ध्यशैल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याटवी
विन्ध्याटवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>The great Vindhya forest, which appears to have spread at one time from near Mathura to the Narmadā.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्य, and अटवी a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याबलीपुत्त्र
विन्ध्याबलीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A name of the demon BĀṆA or VĀṆA.<BR>E.<BR>विन्ध्यावली the mother of the demon, and पुत्त्र son; also विन्ध्यावलीसुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Judged, discussed.<BR>2 Gained, obtained.<BR>3 Fixed, placed.<BR>4 Known.<BR>5 Married, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, and aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्त|विन्यस्तः
विन्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Placed, deposited, fixed.<BR>2 Delivered.<BR>3 Offered, presented.<BR>E.<BR>वि and नि before अस to be or throw, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्याक|विन्याकः
विन्याक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यास|विन्यासः
विन्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Assemblage, collecting, collecting or depositing any thing.<BR>2 Site, place, receptacle, that in or on which any thing is placed or deposited.<BR>3 Orderly arrangement or disposition.<BR>4 Entrusting, depositing.<BR>5 A deposit.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and नि prefixed to अस to take, to throw or place, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप
विप<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेपयति)<BR>To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
विपक्त्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Matured, ripened.<BR>2 Fulfilled, come to pass, as the consequence of former actions.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and पच to cook, क्त्रि aff., and मप् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
विपक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Opposed or adverse to, contrary, inimical.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 An enemy, an adversary.<BR>2 A disputant, an opponent.<BR>3 Exception, (in grammar, &c.)<BR>4 (In logic,) An argument or syllogism in which the proposition to be maintained is wanting.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying opposite, contrary, and पक्ष part or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षतस्
विपक्षतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Hostilely, inimically.<BR>E.<BR>विपक्ष, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षता
विपक्षता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Hostility, enmity, opposition.<BR>2 Controversy, contradiction in argument.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to विपक्ष; also with त्व विपक्षत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षपात
विपक्षपात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Indifferent, impartial.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., पक्षपात an adherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्चिका|विपंचिका
विपञ्चिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lute.<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form, added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्ची|विपंची
विपञ्ची<BR>f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>1 A lute.<BR>2 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पचि to extend, (causal form,) to diffuse sounds, aff. अच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण|विपणः
विपण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Sale, contract of sale.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पण to be of price, aff. घञ् or घ; also with ल्युट्, विपणन n. (-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणि|विपणिः
विपणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 A place where things are sold, a shop, a stall.<BR>2 A fair, a market, a market place.<BR>3 The street of a market.<BR>4 An article or commodity for sale.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पण to transact business, aff. इक्, and fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणिन्
विपणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>A dealer, a trafficker, a shop-keeper or merchant.<BR>E.<BR>विपण sale, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्काल|विपत्कालः
विपत्काल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Time of calamity or misfortune, adversity.<BR>E.<BR>विपट्, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्ति|विपत्तिः
विपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Adversity, calamity, misfortune.<BR>2 Pain, agony.<BR>3 Death, dying.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, पत् to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तियुक्त
विपत्तियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>विपत्ति, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिरहित
विपत्तिरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Properous, happy.<BR>E.<BR>विपत्ति, and रहित free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्सागर|विपत्सागरः
विपत्सागर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Heavy calamity.<BR>E.<BR>विपत्, and सागर ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथ|विपथः
विपथ<BR>mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>A bad road.<BR>E.<BR>वि depreciative prefix, and पथ for पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद्<BR>f. (-पत् or पद्)<BR>Calamity, adversity, misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पद to go, क्विप् aff.; also with टाप् added, विपदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदा
विपदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>Adversity.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदुद्धार|विपदुद्धारः
विपदुद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Extrication from misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>विपत्, and उद्धार lifting up; also विपटुद्धरणं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्ग्रस्त
विपद्ग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Overtaken by or involved in calamity.<BR>E.<BR>विपट्, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्युक्त
विपद्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Unhappy, unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>विपट्, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्रहित
विपद्रहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>विपट्, and रहित left by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्न|विपन्नः
विपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Unfortunate, declined, fallen into adversity or misfortune.<BR>2 Lost, destroyed, annihilated.<BR>3 Dead, defunct.<BR>m. (-न्नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, and पद to go, aff. क्त; also with कन् added विपन्नक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणाम|विपरिणामः
विपरिणाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Change of state or form.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि before णम to bow, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामिन्
विपरिणामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Undergoing or producing change of state or form.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि before णम to bow, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्त्तन|विपरिवर्तन|विपरिवर्तनं
विपरिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Turning back or away from.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and परिवर्त्तन turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्त्तित|विपरिवर्तित
विपरिवर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Turned back or away from, reverted, averted.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि before वृत to turn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीत|विपरीतः
विपरीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reverse, inverse, opposite, contrary.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A lewd woman, a dishonest wife.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि implying contrariety or reverse, before इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकारिन्
विपरीतकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Perverse, contradictory, acting contrary to another's wishes.<BR>E.<BR>विपरीत, and कारिन् who does; also विपरीतकर, विपरीतकर्त्तृ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतगति
विपरीतगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Going backwards or reversely.<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Inverse or reverse motion.<BR>E.<BR>विपरीत, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतता
विपरीतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Contrariety, reverse or opposite state or condition.<BR>E.<BR>विपरीत, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विपरीतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्णक|विपर्णकः
विपर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Palāśa tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वि separate, पर्ण a leaf, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यय|विपर्यय|विपर्ययः|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्य्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Contrariety, opposition.<BR>2 Reverse in general, and thence applied to that of which reverse is predicated, as misery, calamity, (the reverse of fortune); error, misapprehension, (the reverse of reason or truth); inverted order or succession, (the reverse of that which is usual or prescribed,) &c.<BR>3 Destruction, annihilation.<BR>4 Perverseness of disposition.<BR>5 Change of purpose or conduct.<BR>6 Enmity, hostility.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि implying reverse, and इ to go, aff. अच्; also with घञ् aff. विपर्य्याय m. (-यः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=774" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यस्त|विपर्यस्त
विपर्य्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Opposite, contrary, reverse.<BR>2 Conceived to be real (what is not so).<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि before अस to be, or to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्याय|विपर्याय|विपर्यायः|विपर्य्यायः
विपर्य्याय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Contrariety, &c.; see विपर्य्यय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यास|विपर्यास|विपर्यासः|विपर्य्यासः
विपर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Contrariety, opposition.<BR>2 Reverse.<BR>3 Investing imaginary things with real attributes, imagining what is unreal or false to be real or true.<BR>E.<BR>वि and परि before अस to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपल|विपलं
विपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A moment, an instant, either a Pala or second, or (1/6)th of it; a simple breathing or (1/16)th of the latter.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and पल a second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायन|विपलायनं
विपलायन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Flying, running away.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and पलायन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायित
विपलायित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Put to flight, run away.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पलायित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपव्य|विपव्यं
विपव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be cleansed or purified.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पूञ् to purify, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित्<BR>m. (-श्चित्)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman, a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, affs. क्विप् and तुक्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्य
विपश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>Knowledge.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, पश्य seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्यिन्
विपश्यिन्<BR>m. (-श्यी)<BR>A Bauddha saint, the first of the seven principal Buddhas.<BR>E.<BR>विपश्य, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाक|विपाकः
विपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Cooking, dressing.<BR>2 Ripening, maturing.<BR>3 Flavour, taste..<BR>4 Unexpected or improbable result.<BR>5 Poverty, distress.<BR>6 Change of form or state.<BR>7 The consequences of actions, either in this or in a former birth; the operation of time in maturing their results.<BR>8 Assimilation of food, its conversion into a state differing from its original one, digestion.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पच to ripen, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठ|विपाठः
विपाठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डुर
विपाण्डुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Pale, pallid, white.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and पाण्डुर pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादन|विपादनं
विपादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Destroying, killing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पद to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादनीय
विपादनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be killed, fit or proper to be destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पद to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.; also विपाद्य and विपादयितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A kibe, a sore or blister on the foot.<BR>2 A riddle, an enigma.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पद to go, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादित
विपादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Killed, destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पद to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाल
विपाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unattended, unguarded.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., पाल a keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश्<BR>f. (-पाट्)<BR>The Vipāś or Vipāśā river.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश
विपाश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Unnoosed, unfettered, freed from a noose or tie.<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>1 The Vipāśā or the Beyāh river in the Pañjāb.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and पाश् or पाशा a noose, from पश to bind, causal form, with अच् and टाप् or क्विप् aff.; hence also विपाश्; the name applies to the river as having destroyed the cord which the Muni VAŚIṢṬHA had tied round his neck, when about to hang himself through grief for the death of his sons slain by VIŚVĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिन|विपिनं
विपिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A wood, a forest.<BR>E.<BR>वेप to shake, Uṇādi aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Broad.<BR>3 Deep, profound.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The mountain Meru, or rather the western branch of it.<BR>2 The Himālaya mountain.<BR>3 A respectable man.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 A form of the Āryā metre in which the line is irregularly divided by the Cœsura or pause: three species of this form are reckoned; the Ādivipulā with the pause in the first line, Antyavipulā in the second, and Ubhayavipulā in both lines.<BR>E.<BR>वि before पुल to be large or lofty, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलक
विपुलक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Free from horripilation.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and पुलक erection of the hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलता
विपुलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Magnitude, extent.<BR>E.<BR>विपुल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व विपुलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलरस|विपुलरसः
विपुलरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>विपुल much, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलेक्षण
विपुलेक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Large-eyed.<BR>E.<BR>विपुल, and ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूय|विपूयः
विपूय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Munja grass, (Saccharum Munja.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before पुञ् to cleanse, aff. क्यप्; that which is to be cleaned before making into ropes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्र|विप्रः
विप्र<BR>m. (-प्रः)<BR>1 A Brahman.<BR>2 (In prosody,) A foot of four short syllables.<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्रा Sautra root, to fill or complete, (the essential observances,) and क aff.; or वप to shave, Uṇādi aff. रन्, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकार|विप्रकारः
विप्रकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Injury, contumely, abuse.<BR>2 Wickedness.<BR>3 Opposition, counteraction.<BR>4 Retaliation.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र depreciative prefixes, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारिन्
विप्रकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Opposed to, treating with contempt.<BR>2 Retaliating.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before कृ to do, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत|विप्रकृतः
विप्रकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Reviled, abused, treated with contempt or contumely.<BR>2 Opposed, counteracted.<BR>3 Injured, offended.<BR>4 Retaliated, requited.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before कृत made; made little or nothing of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृति|विप्रकृतिः
विप्रकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Abuse, injury, contumely.<BR>2 Retaliation, retort.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र implying depreciation or mutuality, and कृति action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्ट|विप्रकृष्टः
विप्रकृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Remote, distant.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before कृष to attract, aff. क्त; also with कन् added, विप्रकृष्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकार|विप्रतिकारः
विप्रतिकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Contradiction, counteraction, opposition.<BR>2 Reverse.<BR>3 Retaliation.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्रति before कृ to do, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकृत
विप्रतिकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opposed, counteracted.<BR>2 Requited.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्रति before कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्ति|विप्रतिपत्तिः
विप्रतिपत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Perplexity, confusion.<BR>2 Various acquirement.<BR>3 Mutual connexion with or relation to.<BR>4 Conversancy.<BR>5 Contradiction, difference, discrepancy.<BR>6 Contest, dispute.<BR>7 Opposition of interests.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, or implying variety, and प्रतिपत्ति knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्य
विप्रतिपद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 To be opposed, contradicted, contested.<BR>2 To be acquired.<BR>E.<BR>प्रति before पद to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्यमान
विप्रतिपद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being disputed or contested.<BR>2 Being in course of acquirement.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्रति before पद to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्न
विप्रतिपन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Bewildered, perplexed, confused, uncertain.<BR>2 Conversant or acquainted with in various ways, severally or mutually.<BR>3 Connected with.<BR>4 Contested, disputed.<BR>5 Contradicted.<BR>6 Opposed, (as interests.)<BR>E.<BR>वि, and प्रतिपन्न ascertained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=775" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसार|विप्रतिसारः
विप्रतिसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Repentance: see विप्रतीसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसिद्ध
विप्रतिसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Contradicted, opposed.<BR>2 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and प्रति implying opposition, and सिद्ध proved, perfected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसार|विप्रतीसारः
विप्रतीसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Repentance.<BR>2 Evil, wickedness, evil action.<BR>3 Hate, enmity.<BR>4 Rage, wrath.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, प्रति to or towards, सार going, conduct; the इ of प्रति optionally long; otherwise विप्रतिसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदह|विप्रदहः
विप्रदह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Dried fruit or roots, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्ट
विप्रदुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Spoiled, vitiated, defiled.<BR>2 Bad, corrupt.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before टुष्ट the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्टभाव
विप्रदुष्टभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Bad, vicious, sensual, corrupt.<BR>E.<BR>विप्रटुष्ट, and भाव disposition or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमोच्य
विप्रमोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>To be liberated or freed from.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before मुच् to loose, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयाण|विप्रयाणं
विप्रयाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before या to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुक्त|विप्रयुक्तः
विप्रयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Separated, disjoined, sundered, away or absent from.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying separation, प्रयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोग|विप्रयोगः
विप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Separation, absence, especially the separation of lovers.<BR>2 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>3 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>4 Deserving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्रयोग union, contiguity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्ध|विप्रलब्धः
विप्रलब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Tricked, cheated, deceived.<BR>2 Disappointed.<BR>f. (-ब्धी)<BR>A mistress whose lover is not true to his appointment.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलंभः|विप्रलम्भः
विप्रलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Tricking, deceiving, disappointing, deceiving by a false affirmation or by not keeping a promise.<BR>2 Separation, especially of lovers.<BR>3 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>4 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र implying reverse, लभि to get or gain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलाप|विप्रलापः
विप्रलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Quarrel, wrangling, mutual contradiction.<BR>2 Idle or unmeaning discourse, nonsense.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र implying contradiction or reciprocity, and लाप talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुम्पक
विप्रलुम्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Rapacious, exacting, avaricious.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before लुपि to cut off, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवास|विप्रवासः
विप्रवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Residence in a foreign country.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र implying separation, वस to abide, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासन|विप्रवासनं
विप्रवासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Residence abroad.<BR>2 Banishment.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before वस to dwell, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A female fortune-teller.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, पृच्छ to ask, aff. इञ्, with नङ् augment, and ठन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रसात्
विप्रसात्<BR>ind.<BR>As, like as, one with, a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>विप्र, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रस्व
विप्रस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>The property of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>विप्र, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रापवाद
विप्रापवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Abuse of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>विप्र, and अपवाद reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
विप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Disliked, unbeloved, disagreeable.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Offence, transgression.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष्<BR>f. (-प्रुट)<BR>1 A drop of water, &c.<BR>2 A spot, a mark, a dot.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, प्रुष to burn, aff. क्विप्; also विप्लुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
विप्रोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Absent, away from.<BR>2 Banished.<BR>E.<BR>वि and प्र before वस to dwell, aff. क्त, the semivowel changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषितभर्त्तृका|विप्रोषितभर्तृका
विप्रोषितभर्त्तृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A woman whose husband or lover is absent.<BR>E.<BR>विप्रोषित absent, भर्त्तृ a husband, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोष्य
विप्रोष्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having been absent, returning, coming home.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and प्र before वस to dwell, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लव|विप्लवः
विप्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Tumult, confusion, trouble.<BR>2 Evil, calamity.<BR>3 Rapine, extortion.<BR>4 Sin, wickedness.<BR>5 Predatory or irregular warfare.<BR>6 Affray, scuffle.<BR>7 Terrifying an enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>8 Confusion, perplexity, (of thought or speech.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्लु to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव|विप्लावः
विप्लाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Deluging, inundating.<BR>2 Devastating.<BR>3 Causing tumult or public disturbance.<BR>4 A horse's canter or gallop.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and प्लु to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव्य
विप्लाव्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having cast away, defiled, contaminated.<BR>2 Having taught at improper seasons.<BR>3 Having caused to be deluged, devastated, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्लु to go, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुत|विप्लुतः
विप्लुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Depraved, wicked, addicted to evil practices, as gaming, whoring, &c.<BR>2 Committing any crime.<BR>3 Contrary, adverse, averse.<BR>4 Inundated, immersed.<BR>5 Devastated, ravaged.<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्लु to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुष्
विप्लुष्<BR>f. (-प्लुट)<BR>1 A drop of any fluid.<BR>2 A spot, a dot.<BR>E.<BR>वि before प्लुष to burn, aff. क्विप्; also विप्लुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्सा
विप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Repetition, succession: see वीप्सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
विफल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Vain, idle, unmeaning, fruitless, useless.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलता
विफलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unprofitableness, fruitlessness.<BR>E.<BR>विफल, and तल् added; also विफलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकरण
विफलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Frustrating, foiling, defeating.<BR>2 Doing any thing in vain.<BR>E.<BR>विफल, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकृत
विफलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rendered vain, frustrated.<BR>2 Done in vain.<BR>E.<BR>विफल, and कृत done, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभविष्णु
विफलीभविष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>Become unprofitable.<BR>E.<BR>विफल, and भविष्णु become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभविष्णुता
विफलीभविष्णुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unprofitableness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also, विफलीभविष्णुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभूत
विफलीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Become useless.<BR>E.<BR>विफल, and भत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्ध|विबंध|विबंधः|विबन्धः
विबन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>Ischury or constipation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before बन्ध to bind, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाधा
विबाधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>Pain, agony, anguish.<BR>E.<BR>वि various, बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
विबुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Awake, aroused.<BR>2 Unconscious.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and बुद्ध wakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध|विबुधः
विबुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A god, an immortal.<BR>2 A Paṇḍita, a learned man, a teacher.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, बुध to know, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोध|विबोधः
विबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Inattention, absence.<BR>2 Intelligence.<BR>3 Awaking.<BR>4 Discovering any circumstance.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative or intensitive, and बोध understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधित
विबोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Awakened.<BR>2 Instructed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before बुध to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्त|विभक्तः
विभक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Divided, portioned, partitioned.<BR>2 Separated, parted.<BR>3 Dividing, sharing, a partner.<BR>4 Distinct.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, भज to divide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=776" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तज|विभक्तजः
विभक्तज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A son born after partition of the family property between his parents and brethren.<BR>E.<BR>विभक्त divided, (being or having been,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्ति|विभक्तिः
विभक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Part, portion, inheritance or share of inheritance, &c.<BR>2 A division, a partition.<BR>3 Inflexion of nouns, declension.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भज to divide, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभंगः|विभङ्गः
विभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Breaking, fracture.<BR>2 Division.<BR>3 Bending, contracting, (especially of the eye-brows.)<BR>4 Expression or play of features.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and भजि to break, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभजनीय|विभजनीयं
विभजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be portioned or partitioned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भज to divide, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्य
विभज्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having divided, portioned, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भज to divide, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्यमान
विभज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Divisible, portionable, to be or being divided or parted.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भज to divide, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभव|विभवः
विभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Substance, thing, property, wealth.<BR>2 Emancipation from existence.<BR>3 Supreme or superhuman power.<BR>4 Magnanimity, lofty-mindedness.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, privation, &c., and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>2 Light, lustre.<BR>3 Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, भा to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाकर|विभाकरः
विभाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>विभा light, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाग|विभागः
विभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Part, portion, share.<BR>2 The share or portion of an inheritance.<BR>3 Partition of inheritance.<BR>4 (In arithmetic,) The numerator of a fraction.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variously, and भाग a portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागकल्पना
विभागकल्पना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Apportioning or allotment of shares or portions.<BR>E.<BR>विभाग a division, and कल्पना a making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागतस्
विभागतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Proportionately, according to a part or share.<BR>E.<BR>विभाग, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागभाज्
विभागभाज्<BR>m. (-भाक्)<BR>One who shares in a portion, of property already distributed, applied especially to a son by a father and mother of the same tribe, born subsequent to a distribution of property amongst his parents and brethren, in which case he inherits the portion allotted or reserved to the parents.<BR>E.<BR>विभाग a portion, and भाक् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागशस्
विभागशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Proportionately, according to a part or share.<BR>E.<BR>विभाग, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्य|विभाज्यं
विभाज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>Divisible, portionable, what may be divided or apportioned.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, भज to divide, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात्
विभात्<BR>mfn. (-भान्-भान्ती-भाती-भात्)<BR>Shining, splendid.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भा to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात|विभातं
विभात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Dawn, day-break.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भा to shine, aff. क्त; also विभातक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव|विभावः
विभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A friend or acquaintance.<BR>2 One of the Bhāvas or classes of properties into which the objects of poetical composition are divided; the causative or exciting property, as dress, perfumes, &c. of amorous desire; extravagant gesture of mirth; distress or pain of tenderness; arms and tumult of wrath or heroism, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि various, and भाव property, disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
विभावक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Discussing, shewing, illustrating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भू to think, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन|विभावनं
विभावन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Discussion, examination, discrimination.<BR>2 Perceiving, seeing, distinguishing.<BR>3 Conceiving, imagination.<BR>4 Ascertaining or judging of facts.<BR>5 Describing effects not arising from the usual causes (in rhetoric.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before भू in the 10th cl. to think, &c., aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावनीय
विभावनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Distinguishable, ascertainable, to be judged or determined.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and भू to think, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावरी
विभावरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 Turmeric.<BR>3 A bawd.<BR>4 A harlot.<BR>5 The shreds of a garment torn in a scuffle (?).<BR>E.<BR>वि before भा to shine, (with stars,) क्वनिप् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्, and रच् substituted for the final; also विभाव amorous excitement, रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावस्
विभावस्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>विभा, and क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावसु|विभावसुः
विभावसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>4 A sort of necklace or garland.<BR>E.<BR>विभा light, वसु being, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावित|विभावितः
विभावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, perceived, marked.<BR>2 Judged, discriminated.<BR>3 Conceived, imagined.<BR>4 Known, understood.<BR>5 Proved, established.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भू 10th cl. to know or perceive, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावितत्व
विभावितत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The state of being perceived or judged.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव्य
विभाव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be seen or observed, remarkable, distinguishable.<BR>2 To be conceived or imagined.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भू to be, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
विभाषा<BR>f. or ind. (-षा)<BR>Alternative, either of two ways.<BR>E.<BR>वि alternative, and भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासा
विभासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Light, shining.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भास to be luminous, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासित
विभासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Lighted, shining.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भास to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभित्सु
बिभित्सु<BR>mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>Wishing or purposing to hit or pierce.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भिद to break, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्यमान
विभिद्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Being wounded; pierced, broken.<BR>2 Being divided or scattered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भिद to break, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्न|विभिन्नः
विभिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Pierced, wounded.<BR>2 Broken.<BR>3 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>4 Mixed, intermixed, mingling.<BR>5 Various, different.<BR>6 Disappointed.<BR>7 Bewildered, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भिद to break, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्नता
विभिन्नता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The state of being broken, scattered, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विभिन्नत्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीत|विभीतं|विभीतः
विभीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., भीत afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतक|विभीतकं|विभीतकः
विभीतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>E.<BR>विभीत fearless, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषण|विभीषणः
विभीषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Fearful, formidable, terrific, horrible.<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>The property of exciting fear.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The brother of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भी to fear, युच् aff., and षुक augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
विभु<BR>mfn. (-भुः-भुः or भ्वी-भु)<BR>1 Omnipresent, all-pervading.<BR>2 Always, eternal.<BR>3 Firm, solid, hard.<BR>m. (-भुः)<BR>1 A master, an owner.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 BRAHMĀ.<BR>4 VIṢṆU.<BR>5 A servant.<BR>6 Ether.<BR>7 Space.<BR>8 Time.<BR>9 The soul.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भू to be, aff. डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=777" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुग्न
विभुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Bent, bowed, crooked.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भुज to bend, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुता
विभुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Power, supremacy.<BR>E.<BR>विभु, and तल् aff.; also विभुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूति|विभूतिः
विभूति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 Superhuman power, consisting of eight faculties, especially attributed to ŚIVA, and supposed to be attainable by human beings, through a course of austere worship, attended with magical rites, in honor of that deity and his spouse DURGĀ: the eight properties thus supposed to be assumable at will are, अणिमा extreme minuteness or invisibility; लघिमा extreme lightness or incorporeality; प्राप्ति attaining or reaching any thing, as illustrated by the power of touching the moon with the tip of the finger; प्राकाम्यं the fulfilment of every wish; महिमा illimitable bulk; ईशिता supreme dominion over animate or inanimate nature; वशिता the power of enchanting or changing the course of nature, and कामावशायिता the accomplishment of every promise or engagement.<BR>2 Power, dignity, dominion.<BR>3 Ashes of cow-dung, &c. with which ŚIVA is said to have smeared his body, and thence used in imitation of him by devotees.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying change of form, &c., भू to be, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूतिमत्|विभूतिमन्त्
विभूतिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Superhuman.<BR>2 Smeared with ashes.<BR>E.<BR>विभूति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषण|विभूषणं
विभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Ornament, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, and भूषण adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
विभूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Lustre, splendour, beauty.<BR>2 Ornament, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भूष to adorn, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषित|विभूषितः
विभूषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Adorned, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, भूष to adorn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत|विभृतः
विभृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Held, retained.<BR>2 Upheld, supported.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भृत supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेद|विभेदः
विभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Dividing, breaking.<BR>2 Wounding, piercing.<BR>3 Variety, distinction.<BR>4 Bewildering, perplexing.<BR>5 A division or separation.<BR>6 Enmity, opposition.<BR>7 Contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भिद to break, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेदन
विभेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breaking, dividing.<BR>2 Separating, literally or figuratively, as setting at variance.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भिद to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रत्|बिभ्रन्त्
बिभ्रत्<BR>mfn. (-भ्रन्-भ्रती-भ्रत्)<BR>Having, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भृ to support, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम|विभ्रमः
विभ्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 One of the classes of feminine actions proceeding from the passion of love, flurry, confusion.<BR>2 Error, mistake, blunder.<BR>3 Hurry, flurry.<BR>4 Doubt, apprehension.<BR>5 Beauty.<BR>6 Whirling, going round.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>Old age.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भ्रम to err, &c., aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रष्ट
विभ्रष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Lost, gone.<BR>2 Broken off or from, fallen, separated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भ्रस्ज to be broken, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज्<BR>mfn. (-भ्राड् or -भ्राट्)<BR>1 Elegant, richly dressed or decorated.<BR>2 Splendid, luminous, shining.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भ्राज to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राजमान
विभ्राजमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Resplendent, glittering.<BR>E.<BR>वि, भ्राज to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राण
विभ्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भृ to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्त|विभ्रांत|विभ्रान्तः
विभ्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Hurried, flurried, erring, &c. through precipitation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भ्रम to err, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तशील|विभ्रांतशील|विभ्रान्तशीलः
विभ्रान्तशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Mad, drunk, intoxicated, or insane.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A monkey.<BR>2 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>E.<BR>विभ्रान्त wandering, and शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रांतिः|विभ्रान्तिः
विभ्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Error, confusion.<BR>2 Hurry, flurry, precipitation.<BR>3 Whirling, going round.<BR>E.<BR>वि before भ्रम to err, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
विमत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Disliking, averse or hostile to.<BR>2 Disagreeing, of a different opinion.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>वि adverse, and मत disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
विमति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Dislike, aversion.<BR>2 Difference of opinion, dissent.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्सर
विमत्सर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unenvious, unambitious.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., मत्सर envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
विमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>1 Sad, perplexed, disordered, heartbroken.<BR>2 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR>3 Averse, disliking, displeased.<BR>4 Absent, thinking of something else.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and मनस् the mind; having no mind or heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
विमनस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Sad, bewildered, heart-broken, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीकृत
विमनीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Altered in mind or feeling.<BR>2 Sad, sorrowful.<BR>3 Displeased, offended.<BR>E.<BR>विमनस्, and कृत made with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीभूत
विमनीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Changed in mind or feeling, &c.: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>विमनस्, and भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमय|विमयः
विमय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मि to scatter, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्द|विमर्द|विमर्दः|विमर्द्दः
विमर्द्द<BR>m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>2 The trituration of perfumes.<BR>3 Touch, contact.<BR>4 Destroying, killing.<BR>5 A plant, (Cassia esculenta.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before मृद to grind, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दन|विमर्दन|विमर्दनं|विमर्द्दनं
विमर्द्दन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing, pounding, grinding.<BR>2 Killing, destroying.<BR>3 The trituration of perfumes.<BR>4 Conjunction of the sun and moon, or eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मृद to rub, &c., aff. ल्युट्; also विमर्द्दक m. (-कः) and विमर्द्दना f. (-ना.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दार्द्ध|विमर्दार्ध
विमर्द्दार्द्ध<BR>n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>(In astronomy,) The time from the apparent conjunction to the end of an eclipse.<BR>E.<BR>विमर्द्द, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दोत्थ|विमर्दोत्थ|विमर्द्दोत्थः
विमर्द्दोत्थ<BR>m. (-त्थः)<BR>A pleasing scent.<BR>E.<BR>विमर्द्द rubbing, and उत्थ what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्श|विमर्शः
विमर्श<BR>n. (-र्शः)<BR>Discussion, investigation, reasoning, examination by reason.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying discrimination, मृश to perceive, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शन|विमर्शनं
विमर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Investigating, discussing.<BR>E.<BR>वि, मृश to judge, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शिन्
विमर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Thinking, deliberating.<BR>E.<BR>विमश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्ष|विमर्षः
विमर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Irritation, impatience.<BR>2 Displeasure, dissatisfaction.<BR>3 Interruption of the prosperous course of a dramatic story, reverse.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मृष to endure, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षिन्
विमर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>1 Impatient, intolerant.<BR>2 Averse, disliking.<BR>E.<BR>विमर्ष, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
विमल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Clean, pure, (either literally, as clothes, &c., or figuratively, as the heart or mind.)<BR>2 Beautiful.<BR>3 White. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">Page779</a>]<BR>4 Transparent.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Carmaghās.<BR>2 A sort of soil.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An Arhat or Jaina deified sage.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Silver gilt.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=778" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलमणि|विमलमणिः
विमलमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>विमल clean, clear, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलात्मक|विमलात्मकः
विमलात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Clean, pure.<BR>E.<BR>विमल clean, and आत्मन् nature, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलात्मन्
विमलात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Pure, undefiled.<BR>E.<BR>विमल, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलाद्रि|विमलाद्रिः
विमलाद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>A particular mountain.<BR>E.<BR>विमल clean, or crystal, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलार्थक|विमलार्थकः
विमलार्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Clear, clean, pure.<BR>E.<BR>विमल clean, अर्थ purpose, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमस्तकित
विमस्तकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Beheaded, decapitated.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., मस्त the head, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांस|विमांसं|विमांसः
विमांस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>Unclean meat, as the flesh of dogs, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि depreciative prefix, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
विमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A step-mother, a father's wife.<BR>E.<BR>वि different, मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृज|विमातृजः
विमातृज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A step-mother's son.<BR>E.<BR>विमातृ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
विमान<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 A car or chariot of the gods, sometimes serving as a seat or throne, and at others carrying them through the skies self-directed and self-moving.<BR>2 Any car or vehicle.<BR>3 A horse.<BR>4 A palace, the palace of an emperor or supreme monarch.<BR>5 Disrespect, dishonour.<BR>6 Measure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मन to understand, with घञ् aff., or मा to measure, aff. ल्युट्, or वि priv., मान honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानित
विमानित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dishonoured.<BR>E.<BR>विमान, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्ग|विमार्गः
विमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A broom, a brush.<BR>2 A bad road.<BR>3 A wrong road, literally or figuratively, evil conduct.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मृज to clean, aff. घञ्, or वि privative, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गण|विमार्गणं
विमार्गण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Searching, seeking.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मृग to search, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
विमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Loosed, liberated.<BR>2 Hurled, thrown.<BR>3 Quitted, abandoned.<BR>4 Issued or let loose from, given vent to.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुक्त the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्ति|विमुक्तिः
विमुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Liberation, especially final emancipation from future existence.<BR>2 Separation, parting.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुक्ति the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुख|विमुखः
विमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>1 Averted, having the face cast down or turned away.<BR>2 Opposed.<BR>E.<BR>वि reverse, and मुख the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखता
विमुखता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Disappearance, departure.<BR>2 Turning away.<BR>3 Opposition.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also विमुखत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखिता
विमुखिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Turning away from, enmity.<BR>2 Departure.<BR>3 Opposition.<BR>E.<BR>विमुखिन्, and तल् aff.; also विमुखित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखिन्
विमुखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खि-खिनी-खि)<BR>1 Averted, turned away.<BR>2 Hostile, averse to or from.<BR>E.<BR>विमुख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखीकरण
विमुखीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Turning away from, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>विमुख, and करण doing, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखीकृत
विमुखीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Turned away from, averted, departed.<BR>E.<BR>विमुख, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
विमुग्ध<BR>mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>Bewildered, absorbed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुह to be bewildered, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्यमान
विमुच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being let loose or liberated, in the act of spreading abroad.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुच to be loosed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
विमुद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>1 Blown, budded, opened as a bud or flower.<BR>2 Unsealed, unclosed.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
विमूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Bewildered, discomposed.<BR>2 Foolish.<BR>3 Beguiled, led astray, seduced, tempted.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and मुह to be foolish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढसंज्ञ
विमूढसंज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Senseless, unconscious.<BR>E.<BR>विमूढ, and सज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढात्मन्
विमूढात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Beguiled, foolish.<BR>E.<BR>विमूढ, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृदित
विमृदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed.<BR>2 Ground, pounded.<BR>E.<BR>वि, मृद to rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्य
विमृश्य<BR>mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>To be discussed or reflected upon.<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered.<BR>E.<BR>वि, मृश to reflect, युच् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्यकारिन्
विमृश्यकारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Acting after due deliberation.<BR>E.<BR>विमृश्य, and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्ष|विमोक्षः
विमोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>Liberation, freedom, being or letting loose.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मोक्ष the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षण|विमोक्षणं
विमोक्षण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Quitting, abandoning, resigning.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मोक्षण the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचन|विमोचनं
विमोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Liberating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुच to set free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचित
विमोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Liberated, set free.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुच to liberate, causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
विमोहन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>Fascinating, seducing, bewitching, tempting, (the instrument or agent.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Seducing, tempting, confounding the mind and exciting the passions, (the act.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुह to be foolish, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहित|विमोहितः
विमोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fascinated, beguiled.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मुह to be foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विंबः|विम्बः
विम्ब<BR>mn. (-म्बः-म्बं)<BR>1 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>2 An image, a picture, a shadow, a reflected or represented form.<BR>3 The gourd of the Momordica monadelpha.<BR>nf. (-म्बं-म्बा or -म्बी)<BR>A cucurbitaceous plant with red fruit, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>E.<BR>वि to go, to shine, वन Uṇādi aff., and मुस् augment, with the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बक|विंबक|विम्बकं
विम्बक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>2 The gourd of the Momordica monadelpha or the plant itself.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बजा
विम्बजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>The Momordica monadelpha or the gourd.<BR>E.<BR>विम्ब the plant, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बट|विंबट|विंबटः|विम्बटः
विम्बट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>The mustard plant, (Sinapis dichotoma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>विम्ब as above, अट to go or grow (like), aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बागत
विम्बागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Reflected.<BR>E.<BR>विम्ब, and आगत arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बिका|विंबिका
विम्बिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A cucurbitaceous plant bearing a bright red gourd, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>2 The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>E.<BR>कन् in the fem. form, added to विम्ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बित|विंबित
विम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pictured, imaged, reflected.<BR>E.<BR>विम्ब, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बु|विंबु|विंबुः|विम्बुः
विम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बोष्ठ|विम्बोष्ठः
विम्बोष्ठ^1<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं)<BR>Red-lipped, having lips like the Vimba fruit.<BR>E.<BR>विम्ब as above, and ओष्ठ the lip; also विम्बौष्ठ^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: cf wil1819.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Dhaval Patel on 20160113. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/189. note: eH  vimbeHzWa not grammatically possible. Author mentions vimbOzWa as alternate. SKD has vimbOzWaH..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=779" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लान
विम्लान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Fresh, pure, free from soil or decay.<BR>2 Refreshed.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., म्लान decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापन|विम्लापनं
विम्लापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cleaning, wiping.<BR>2 Refreshing, reviving.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., म्लै to decay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियच्चारिन्
वियच्चारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A kite.<BR>E.<BR>वियत् the sky, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत्<BR>n. (-यत्)<BR>Sky, heaven, ether, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, यम to refrain or cease, aff. क्विप, and तुक् final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियति|वियतिः
वियति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>वि before यत to endeavour, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्गङ्गा|वियद्गंगा
वियद्गङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>The Ganges or river of heaven.<BR>E.<BR>वियत् heaven, गङ्गा the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्गति
वियद्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Moving in the air.<BR>E.<BR>वियत्, and गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्भूति|वियद्भूतिः
वियद्भूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Darkness.<BR>E.<BR>वियत् the sky, and भूति superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियन्मणि|वियन्मणिः
वियन्मणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>वियत् the sky, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम|वियमः
वियम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Forbearance, restraint.<BR>2 Rest, cessation, stop.<BR>3 Pain or distress of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>वि before यम to check or restrain, aff. अप्; also वियाम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियात|वियातः
वियात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shameless, impudent, ill-behaved.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying prevention, and यात wished; wishing for what is prohibited or improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियाम|वियामः
वियाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Forbearance, restraint.<BR>2 Rest, stop, cessation.<BR>3 Pain or distress of various kinds.<BR>E.<BR>वि before यम to restrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुक्त|वियुक्तः
वियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Separated, sundered.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and युक्त jointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोग|वियोगः
वियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Absence, separation, especially of lovers.<BR>2 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगभाज्
वियोगभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Suffering separation.<BR>E.<BR>वियोग separation, भज् to serve, to be subject to, causal form, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Separated, absent, remote, apart.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR>E.<BR>वियोग separation, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजित|वियोजितः
वियोजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Separated, disjoined, disunited.<BR>2 Parted from, deprived of.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, योजित joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Averse, indifferent, free from inclination or affection.<BR>2 Stoical, void of attachment to worldly objects.<BR>3 Empassioned, interested, feeling passion or regard for any person or any thing.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative or pleonastic, before रञ्ज to feel passion, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तभाव
विरक्तभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Disinclined to, disliking.<BR>E.<BR>विरक्त, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ति|विरक्तिः
विरक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Aversion, disinclination.<BR>2 Absence of affection.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रञ्ज to affect, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचत्
विरचत्<BR>mfn. (-चन्-चन्ती-चत्)<BR>Making, composing, fabricating, embellishing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रच to make, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचन|विरचनं
विरचन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Making.<BR>2 Composing.<BR>3 Embellishing.<BR>4 Embellishment, any artificial and ornamental fabric or contrivance.<BR>E.<BR>वि before र to make, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचित|विरचितः
विरचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made, prepared, effected.<BR>2 Written, composed.<BR>3 Trimmed, ornamented.<BR>4 Contrived, constructed, arranged.<BR>E.<BR>वि pleonasm, and रच made, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरच्य
विरच्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having made.<BR>E.<BR>वि, रच to make, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
विरजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>Free from dust.<BR>f. (-जाः)<BR>A woman who has ceased to menstruate.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, रजस् the menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्तमस्
विरजस्तमस्<BR>m. (-माः)<BR>A virtuous man, one free form the two properties of ignorance and passion.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, रजस the quality of passion, and तमस् that of ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजा
विरजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A plant, commonly कवित्थानी.<BR>2 A sort of grass, commonly Dūb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीकृत
विरजीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Exempt or freed from passion.<BR>2 Clean, freed from dust, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., रजस् passion, &c., कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीभूत
विरजीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Free from passion, pure, holy.<BR>2 Clean, clear.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., रजस् passion, भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्च|विरंच|विरंचः|विरञ्चः
विरञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रच to create, aff. अच्, and नुम् augment, more properly विरिञ्च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरट|विरटः
विरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 The name of a king.<BR>2 The shoulder.<BR>3 A black kind of Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरण|विरणं
विरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthum.)<BR>E.<BR>see वीरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
विरत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stopped, ceased, rested.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रम to stop or rest, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरति|विरतिः
विरति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Stop, cessation, term, rest.<BR>2 End, term.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रम to play, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमत्
विरमत्<BR>mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>1 Resting, stopping.<BR>2 Sporting.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रम to sport, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Fine, delicate, thin, (but with interstices.)<BR>2 Loose, relaxed.<BR>4 Apart, wide, separated by an interval.<BR>4 Remote, rare, occurring at distant or repeated intervals of time.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Sour curds.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, रा to go or be, aff. कलन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलजानुक
विरलजानुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man with bandy legs.<BR>E.<BR>विरल wide, and जानु the knee, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलद्रवा
विरलद्रवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Gruel made of rice or other grain, with the addition, of Ghee, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विरल apart, द्रु to ooze, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Insipid.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरह|विरहः
विरह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Separation, parting, absence, especially the separation of lovers.<BR>2 Forbearance, cessation, relinquishment.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रह to abandon, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहय्य
विरहय्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रह to quit, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहार्त्त|विरहार्त
विरहार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Pained by the absence of a lover.<BR>E.<BR>विरह, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
विरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Left, abandoned, deserted, relinquished.<BR>2 Void of exempt, or free from.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रह to abandon, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Separate, sundered, absent or apart from.<BR>f. (-हिणी)<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>2 A woman absent from her husband or lover.<BR>E.<BR>विरह absence, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्कण्ठिता|विरहोत्कंठिता
विरहोत्कण्ठिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A woman whose lover or husband is absent.<BR>E.<BR>विरह separation, उत्कण्ठित afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराग|विरागः
विराग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The absence of desire or passion, indifference, philosophy, the disregard of all sensual enjoyment either in [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">Page781</a>] this world or the next.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and राग passion, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=780" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागार्ह|विरागार्हः
विरागार्ह<BR>mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>Void of passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>विराग the absence of desire, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागिन्
विरागिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>Void of passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>विराग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज्<BR>m. (-राट्)<BR>1 A man of the regal or military class.<BR>2 Splendour, beauty.<BR>3 The first progeny of BRAHMĀ, who having divided himself into male and female, produced from the female, VIRĀJ; VIRĀJ then by himself produced the first Menu or SVAYAMBHUVA, who was the progenitor of the Prajāpatis, and the secondary framer of the visible world: in other places VIRĀJ is the same as BRAHMĀ, and assumer of the androgynous form in his own person.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally or separately, &c., राज to shine, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजत्
विराजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>Shining, splendid, handsome.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and राज to shine, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजमान|विराजमानः
विराजमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Splendid, brilliant, handsome.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राज to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजित|विराजितः
विराजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Illuminated, irradiated, splendid.<BR>2 Manifested, made visible.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राज to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराट|विराटः
विराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A country, one of the midland divisions of India, probably Berar.<BR>2 A sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रट to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटज|विराटजः
विराटज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>An inferior sort of diamond, said to be found in the country Virāṭa.<BR>E.<BR>विराट the country, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराणिन्
विराणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रण battle, aff. अण्, and इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्ध
विराद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Treated with disrespect, reviled, abused.<BR>2 Opposed.<BR>3 Offended.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राध to accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्धृ
विराद्धृ<BR>mfn. (-द्धा-द्धी-द्धृ)<BR>1 Thwarting, opposing.<BR>2 Offending, injuring.<BR>3 Abusive, calumnious.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राध to accomplish, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध|विराधः
विराध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Opposition, prevention.<BR>2 Vexation, annoyance.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राध to accomplish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधान|विराधानं
विराधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pain, agony, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्यत्
विराध्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्)<BR>1 Opposing, thwarting.<BR>2 Offending, annoying, injuring.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राध to accomplish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराम|विरामः
विराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 End, conclusion, cessation, term.<BR>2 Rest, cessation from labour.<BR>3 Stop, pause.<BR>4 Interval between words or sentences.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रम to stop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराल|विरालः
विराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>विडाल as above, and ड changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराव|विरावः
विराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रु to make a noise, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
विराविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि)<BR>Shouting, roaring, crying, &c.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A broom.<BR>2 The name of a river.<BR>3 Weeping, crying.<BR>E.<BR>विराव noise, इनि and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिक्त|विरिक्तः
विरिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Purged.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रिच to void by stool, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्च|विरिंच|विरिंचः|विरिञ्चः
विरिञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>BRAHMĀ: see विरिञ्चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चन|विरिंचन|विरिंचनः|विरिञ्चनः
विरिञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BRAHMĀ: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चि|विरिंचि|विरिंचिः|विरिञ्चिः
विरिञ्चि<BR>m. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying various kinds, (of beings,) रच to make or create, इन् aff., the radical vowel changed to इ, and नुम् augment; also withअच् aff. विरिञ्च, and with युच्, विरिञ्चन; some authorities omit the change of the radical vowel, and write विरञ्च and विरञ्चि, but these seem to be less accurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्ध|विरिब्धः
विरिब्ध<BR>m. (-ब्धः)<BR>A note, a tone.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रेभ to sound, क्त aff., इट् augment, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुग्न
विरुग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>1 Broken, bent.<BR>2 Blunted.<BR>3 Destroyed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुज to be sick, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद|विरुदं|विरुदः
विरुद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Crying.<BR>2 Proclaiming.<BR>E.<BR>वि, रुद to cry, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
विरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Opposed, hindered.<BR>2 Reverse, contrary, opposite.<BR>3 Inconsistent, (in argument,) incongruous, a nonsequitur.<BR>4 Opposed in quality, as sweet with sour, &c.<BR>5 Disagreeing with each other, (as articles of medicine or food.)<BR>6 Hostile, adverse.<BR>7 Excluded, disqualified.<BR>8 Surrounded, blockaded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुध to stop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धता
विरुद्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Opposition, contraiety.<BR>2 Incongruity.<BR>3 Enmity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to विरुद्ध; also with त्व, विरुद्धत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धभुज्
विरुद्धभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Eating incompatible things.<BR>E.<BR>विरुद्ध, and भुज who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धभोजन
विरुद्धभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Incompatible food.<BR>E.<BR>विरुद्ध, and भोजन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धान्न
विरुद्धान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Incompatible food.<BR>E.<BR>विरुद्ध, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूक्षण|विरूक्षणं
विरूक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Astringent, drying.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Censure, blame, reviling, abuse.<BR>2 Oath, imprecation.<BR>3 Contracting, roughening, acting as an astringent.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रूक्ष to be rough, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढ|विरूढः
विरूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Budded, blossomed.<BR>2 Born.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुह to grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
विरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा or -पी-पं)<BR>1 Deformed, monstrous.<BR>2 Unusual in form or nature, unnatural.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Irregular or monstrous shape.<BR>2 Difference of nature or character.<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>The wife of YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
विरूपक<BR>mfn. (-कः-पिका-कं)<BR>1 Frightful, hideous.<BR>2 Deformed, mis-shapen.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपकरण
विरूपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Disfiguring.<BR>E.<BR>विरूप, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपाक्ष|विरूपाक्षः
विरूपाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of the Rudras.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, रूप form, and अक्ष the eye; having three eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेक|विरेकः
विरेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Purging, evacuation by stool.<BR>2 A purgative.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रिच to purge, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचन|विरेचनं|विरेचनः
विरेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Purging, evacuation by stool.<BR>2 A purgative.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रिच to purge, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचित
विरेचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purged, evacuated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रिच to purge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेच्य
विरेच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>To be purged.<BR>E.<BR>वि, रिच to purge, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेफ|विरेफः
विरेफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>1 A river in general.<BR>2 The absence of the letter र.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, रेफ the letter र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेभित|विरेभितः
विरेभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sounded, uttered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रेभे to sound, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोक|विरोकं|विरोकः
विरोक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A hole, a chasm.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुच to shine, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचन|विरोचनः
विरोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 The son of the sovereign PRAHLĀDA.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुच to shine, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=781" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनसुत|विरोचनसुतः
विरोचनसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>BALI, the sovereign of Mahābalipura.<BR>E.<BR>विरोचन the son of PRAHLĀDA, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचिष्णु
विरोचिष्णु<BR>mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>1 Shining.<BR>2 Illuminating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुच to be light, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध|विरोधः
विरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Enmity, animosity.<BR>2 Restraint, check, controul, confinement.<BR>3 Opposition, contradiction.<BR>4 Preventing, hindrance.<BR>5 War.<BR>6 Calamity, misfortune.<BR>7 Surrounding, investing, siege, blockade.<BR>8 Impediment to a successful progress of the story (in a play).<BR>9 Antithesis, contrast.<BR>10 Opposition of qualities (in articles of food or medicine, &c.)<BR>11 Inconsistency, (in argument.)<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>Fixed rule, ordinance, institute.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुध to stop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधन|विरोधनं
विरोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Opposition, resistance, contradiction.<BR>2 Hindering, obstructing, preventing.<BR>3 Incongruity, inconsistency.<BR>4 Taunting, provoking.<BR>5 Encountering or defying peril.<BR>6 Investing, blockading.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुध to stop, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिकृत्
विरोधिकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The forty-fifth year of the Indian cycle.<BR>E.<BR>विरोधि opposition, कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
विरोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>1 Inimical, adverse, hostile.<BR>2 Opposing, preventing.<BR>3 Obstructive.<BR>4 Exclusive, disqualifying.<BR>5 Contradictory, inconsistent.<BR>6 Quarrelsome, contentious.<BR>7 Of opposite and incompatible quality, (food, medicine, &c.)<BR>8 Besieging, blockading.<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>1 An enemy, an opponent.<BR>2 The twenty-fourth year of the cycle.<BR>E.<BR>विरोध enmity, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधोक्ति|विरोधोक्तिः
विरोधोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Quarrel, dispute, mutual contradiction.<BR>E.<BR>विरोध contradiction, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहित
विरोहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Left, destitute, forsaken.<BR>E.<BR>वि, रुह to ascend, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल|विलं|विलः
विल<BR>r. 6th cl. (विलति)<BR>1 To wear, to put on, to clothe or cover.<BR>2 To break or divide.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेलयति)<BR>To throw, to cast, to direct or send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल|विलं|विलः
विल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>2 A cave, a cavern.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 One of INDRA'S horses.<BR>2 A sort of reed or cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>विल to divide, &c., aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
विलक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>1 Astonished, surprised.<BR>2 Abashed, ashamed.<BR>3 Markless, having no mark or aim.<BR>4 Contra-indicated, having a character or mark contrary to what is usual or natural.<BR>5 Having no characteristic mark or property.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लक्ष to see, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
विलक्षण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Other, different.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 State or condition for which no cause can be assigned, vain and causeless state.<BR>2 Seeing, observing.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative or negative, and लक्षण a mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षत्व
विलक्षत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Shame.<BR>2 Surprise.<BR>3 Absence of mark or aim.<BR>4 Absence of distinguishing property.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to विलक्ष; also with तल् aff. विलक्षता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
विलक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Seen, observed.<BR>2 Affected without a cause.<BR>3 Undiscriminated, unmarked.<BR>E.<BR>वि inten. or priv., and लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्न|विलग्नं
विलग्न<BR>mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>Joined or attached to, fixed on or connected with.<BR>n. (-ग्नं)<BR>The waist, the middle.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लग to be connected with, क्त aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घन|विलंघन|विलंघनं
विलङ्घन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Overstepping, transgressing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लघि to leap over, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घनीय
विलङ्घनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be transgressed or overstepped.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लघि to leap over, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घित|विलंघित
विलङ्घित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Transgressed, overstepped.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लघि to leap over, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज|विलज्जः
विलज्ज<BR>mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>Shameless, impudent, unabashed.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, लज्जा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्जमान
विलज्जमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Modest.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लस्ज to be modest, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपत्
विलपत्<BR>mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>1 Speaking, talking.<BR>2 Prating, talking idly or wildly.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लप to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपन|विलपनं
विलपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The dirt or sediment of any oily substance, as of clarified butter, &c.<BR>2 Talking, chattering, talking idly or wildly.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लप to speak, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपित|विलपितं
विलपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Said.<BR>2 Chattered.<BR>3 Lamented, spoken in grief, spoken idly.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लप to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब|विलंब|विलंबः|विलम्बः
विलम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 Falling or hanging down, pendulousness.<BR>2 Slowness, tardiness, delay.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लबि to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बन|विलंबन|विलंबनं|विलम्बनं
विलम्बन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Delaying, retarding.<BR>2 Hanging on or from, depending.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लबि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बमान
विलम्बमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Suspended on, hanging on or from.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लबि to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बित|विलंबित|विलम्बितं
विलम्बित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Falling, pendulous, hanging or fallen down.<BR>2 Slow, tardy, retarded.<BR>3 Slow, (as time in music,) adagio.<BR>E.<BR>विलम्ब delay, &c., इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिन्|विलंबिन्
विलम्बिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>1 Delaying, retarding.<BR>2 Pendulous, depending, hanging on or from.<BR>m. (-म्बी)<BR>The thirty-second year of the Indian cycle.<BR>E.<BR>विलम्ब slowness, delay, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलंभः|विलम्भः
विलम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Gift, donation, giving.<BR>E.<BR>वि reverse, लभि to get or gain, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलय|विलयः
विलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Destruction of the world.<BR>2 Destruction in general.<BR>3 Liquefaction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ली to liquefy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयन|विलयनं
विलयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Destroying.<BR>2 Corroding, eating away.<BR>3 Liquefying.<BR>4 Removing, taking away.<BR>5 Attenuating, (as the fluids of the body.)<BR>6 An attenuant.<BR>7 An escharotic.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ली to melt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलला
विलला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of Sida, (S. cordifolia, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before लल to shake, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलवासिन्
विलवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Living in a hole, burrowing.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विल a hole, and वासिन् who inhabits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलशय|विलशयः
विलशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Living or burrowing in holes.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विल a hole, शी to sleep, aff. श.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसत्|विलसन्त्
विलसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>1 Shining, beautiful, splendid.<BR>2 Sportive, wanton.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लस to shine, &c., aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसन|विलसनं
विलसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sporting, dallying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लस to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसित
विलसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sportive, wanton.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Wanton pastime or gestures.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लस to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाप|विलापः
विलाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Lamentation, the language of grief and distress.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लप to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाल|विलालः
विलाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 An instrument, a machine.<BR>2 A cat.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लल to desire, &c., aff. घञ्, or विडाल as above, and ड changed to its congener ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=782" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलास|विलासः
विलास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 One kind of feminine action, considered as proceeding from and indicative of amorous sentiments; change of place, posture, gait or look, on the approach of the lover, as hiding at his approach, assuming a look of displeasure, &c.<BR>2 Sport, pastime, play, especially amorous pastime, dalliance, wantonness.<BR>3 Grace, elegance.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लस to desire, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासकानन
विलासकानन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A pleasure ground.<BR>E.<BR>विलास sport, and कानन a wood, a grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासमन्दिर|विलासमन्दिरं
विलासमन्दिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A pleasure house, a summer house, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विलास sport, and मन्दिर a building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासवत्|विलासवन्त्
विलासवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sportive, dallying, wanton.<BR>E.<BR>विलास, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासविभवानस|विलासविभवानसः
विलासविभवानस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Greedy, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिका
विलासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A drama in one act on any light subject or adventure.<BR>E.<BR>वि, लस to shine, ण्वुल् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
विलासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Wanton, sportive, dallying.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 A sensualist, an enjoyer.<BR>5 A snake.<BR>6 ŚIVA.<BR>7 KṚṢṆA.<BR>8 KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>f. (-सिनी)<BR>1 A woman.<BR>2 A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>विलास pastime, &c., aff. इनि or वि, लस to shine, घिनुण् aff.; also read विलाषिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्त
विलिप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Anointed, plastered, smeared.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लिप to smear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीन|विलीनः
विलीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Liquid, liquified, semifluid, as melted oil or butter, &c.<BR>2 Disappeared, perished, removed from sight, either temporarily or permanently.<BR>3 Imagined, formed or infused, as in the mind.<BR>4 Contiguous to, in contact with, united or blended with.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ली to melt, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्त
विलुप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Seized, taken.<BR>2 Cut off.<BR>3 Lost.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुप to cut off, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभित
विलुभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bewildered, disturbed, agitated.<BR>2 Shaken, (by the wind.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to beguile, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुलित
विलुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Tremulous, shaking, waving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुल to agitate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखन|विलेखनं
विलेखन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Digging, delving, rooting up.<BR>2 Dividing, splitting.<BR>3 Making marks or furrows.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लिख to write, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप|विलेपः
विलेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Ointment, unguent, especially fragrant unguent of Sandal, Agallochum, &c..<BR>2 Mortar, plaster.<BR>3 Anointing, plastering.<BR>(-पी)<BR>Rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लिप to anoint or smear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपन|विलेपनं
विलेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Perfume for the person, unguent or oil of Sandal, saffron, camphor, bdellium, &c.<BR>2 Smearing the body with fragrant oils, &c.<BR>2 Plastering.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A woman adorned with perfumes, &c.<BR>2 Rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लिप to smear, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप्य|विलेप्यः
विलेप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>To be spread or plastered.<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>Ricegruel.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लिप to smear, aff. ण्यत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेवासिन्
विलेवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Living or burrowing in holes.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विल 7th case, वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेशय|विलेशयः
विलेशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>3 A hare.<BR>4 Any animal living or burrowing in holes.<BR>E.<BR>विल a hole, in the seventh case, and शय who sleeps or dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक|विलोकः
विलोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Solitary, lonely.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., लोक a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकन|विलोकनं
विलोकन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>Sight, seeing, looking.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोकृ to see, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनीय
विलोकनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Agreeable, beautiful, fit to be seen or looked at.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोक to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनीयता
विलोकनीयता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Loveliness, beauty.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकयत्|विलोकयन्त्
विलोकयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Seeing, looking at.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोक to see, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकित|विलोकितं
विलोकित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोकृ to see, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचन|विलोचनं
विलोचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The eye.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोच to see, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनपात|विलोचनपातः
विलोचनपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A glance, a look.<BR>E.<BR>विलोचन, and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनाम्बु|विलोचनांबु
विलोचनाम्बु<BR>n. (-म्बु)<BR>Tears.<BR>E.<BR>विलोचन, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोटक|विलोटकः
विलोटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Clupea cultrata.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुट to roll on the ground, aff. खुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडन|विलोडनं
विलोडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Agitating, shaking, churning.<BR>2 Rolling or tossing.<BR>E.<BR>वि, लुड to agitate, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडित|विलोडितं
विलोडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Agitated, churned, shaken.<BR>2 Rolling or tumbling on the ground.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लोड to be tremulous, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपन|विलोपनं
विलोपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>2 Deluding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुप to cut, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ|विलोभः
विलोभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Attraction, delusion, seduction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to delude, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभन|विलोभनं
विलोभन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Allurement, attraction, temptation, seduction.<BR>2 Beguiling, perplexing.<BR>3 Praise, commendation, especially by contrast with inferiority.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to delude, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभित
विलोभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Allured, beguiled.<BR>2 Deceived.<BR>3 Praised.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to delude, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्य
विलोभ्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having beguiled, fascinated, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to delude, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्यमान
विलोभ्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being fascinated, overcome, beguiled, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुभ to beguile, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोम|विलोमं|विलोमः
विलोम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Reverse, opposite, contrary, backward, against the hair or grain.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Reverse, opposite course or order, &c.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>3 VARUṆA, regent of the waters.<BR>4 A dog.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>A water-wheel or machine for raising water.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying difference, &c., and लोम the hair of the body; also with कन् added विलोमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमक्रिया
विलोमक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Doing any thing backwards or in reverse order.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Rule of Inversion.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमज
विलोमज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born of a father of an inferior caste and mother of a superior.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम inverse order, and ज born; also विलोमजात, विलोमोत्पन्न, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमजिह्व|विलोमजिह्वः
विलोमजिह्व<BR>m. (-ह्वः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम reversed, जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमत्रैराशिक
विलोमत्रैराशिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Rule of Three inverse.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम, and त्रैराशिक rule of Three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमवर्ण|विलोमवर्णः
विलोमवर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A man of mixed or inferior birth.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम contrary to the proper order, (of marriage, &c.) and वर्ण a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=783" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमविधि|विलोमविधिः
विलोमविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>1 Inverted or reversed ceremony.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Rule of Inversion.<BR>E.<BR>विलोम, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Shaking, trembling, tremulous.<BR>2 Fickle, unsteady.<BR>3 Rolling, (as the eyes.)<BR>4 Tossing, waving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुल to agitate, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलता
विलोलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Tremulousness.<BR>2 Unsteadiness.<BR>3 Rolling, (of the eyes.)<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विलोलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलन|विलोलनं
विलोलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Shaking, stirring, agitating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुल to agitate, causal v., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलित
विलोलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, agitated, tossed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before लुल to agitate, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलौकस्
विलौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>Any animal living in holes, a reptile.<BR>E.<BR>विल, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्ल|विल्लं
विल्ल<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>1 A pit, a hole.<BR>2 Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>विल a hole, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्लमूला
विल्लमूला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of yam: see वाराही.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A fruit tree, commonly named Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>n. (-ल्वं)<BR>1 The fruit of the Bel.<BR>2 A measure, the same as the Pala.<BR>E.<BR>विल to divide, Uṇādi aff. वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>2 The wish to speak.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, in the desiderative form, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षित|विवक्षितः
विवक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>2 Purposed, intended.<BR>3 Literal, not figurative, (a word or phrase.)<BR>4 Intended to be spoken or said.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>An object desired.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Purpose, wish, what one wishes to declare or speak.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षु
विवक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing to speak.<BR>E.<BR>वच to speak, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवञ्चिषु|विवंचिषु
विवञ्चिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Crafty, deceitful.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वञ्च to trick, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवत्सा
विवत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>A cow whose calf is dead.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., वत्स a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदत्
विवदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>1 Disputing, contending.<BR>2 Litigating.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, वद to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदमान|विवदमानः
विवदमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Disagreeing, contending, maintaining different arguments.<BR>2 Litigating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वद to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवध|विवधः
विवध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A road, a highway.<BR>2 A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>3 A load.<BR>4 Storing grain or hay, &c.<BR>5 An ewer, a pitcher.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वध to strike, aff. घञ्; also वीवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिक|विवधिकः
विवधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chandler.<BR>E.<BR>विवध storing grain, ठन् aff., and the vowel unchanged; also वैवधिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवन्दिषु
विवन्दिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Desirous or wishing to praise.<BR>E.<BR>वदि to praise, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर|विवरं|विवरः
विवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>2 Fault, defect.<BR>3 Separation, disjunction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृञ् to choose, to cover, &c., and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरण|विवरणं
विवरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Explanation, exposition, gloss, comment.<BR>2 Interpretation, translation.<BR>3 Uncovering, exposing, laying bare or open.<BR>4 Detailing, describing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृ to select (the meaning), aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरनालिका
विवरनालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR>E.<BR>विवर a hole, a perforation, नाल a pipe, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरिषु
विवरिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing to make manifest or declare.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृ to choose, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जन|विवर्जन|विवर्जनं
विवर्ज्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Abandoning, leaving, shunning.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृज to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जनीय|विवर्जनीय
विवर्ज्जनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be avoided, shunned, quitted, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृज to abandon, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जयत्|विवर्जयत्
विवर्ज्जयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Avoiding, leaving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृज to quit, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जित|विवर्जित
विवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Left, abandoned, avoided, shunned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृज to leave, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
विवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Low, vile.<BR>2 Bad coloured.<BR>3 Wanting colour.<BR>4 Changing colour.<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A man of a low caste, one of degrading occupation, an outcaste.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्णवदन
विवर्णवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Pale-faced.<BR>E.<BR>विवर्ण colourless, वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्त|विवर्त|विवर्तः|विवर्त्तः
विवर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Assemblage, collection, heap or multitude.<BR>2 Dancing.<BR>3 Going or turning round, revolving, returning.<BR>4 Human error, worldly ignorance, the confounding of truth and falsehood, or the mistaking of unreal objects and conceiving them to be what they are not, as mirage for water, a rope for a snake, &c.<BR>5 Modification, various or altered state or condition.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तन|विवर्तन|विवर्तनं|विवर्त्तनं
विवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Going round, circumambulating an altar, &c.<BR>2 Revolving, turning round.<BR>3 Whirling, causing to go round.<BR>4 Returning.<BR>5 Passing through in succession, as various lives, various hells, &c.<BR>5 Being, abiding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तमान|विवर्तमान
विवर्त्तमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Turning back or round, recoiling, revolving, returning, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तित|विवर्तित
विवर्त्तित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Revolved, returned.<BR>2 Whirled round.<BR>3 Turned back or away.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्द्धन
विवर्द्धन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Increase.<BR>2 Cutting, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृध to increase, to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्द्धित
विवर्द्धित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Increased, enlarged.<BR>2 Cut, divided.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृध to increase, to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
विवश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>1 Subject, subjected.<BR>2 Independant.<BR>3 Apprehensive of death, unwilling though about to die.<BR>4 Desirous of death, sedate at that period, or having the soul free from worldly cares and fears.<BR>5 Uncontrouled, unrestrained, unsubdued.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वश to wish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्त्र
विवस्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Unclothed, naked.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., and वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वत्|विवस्वन्त्
विवस्वत्<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>1 A god.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR>4 The seventh or present MANU; also VAIVASVATA.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The city of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying variety, वस to cover or hide, affix क्विप्, विवस् here said therefore to imply various covering, as a garment of light, i. e. the rays of the sun, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवात्
विवात्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वान्ती-वाती-वात्)<BR>Blowing, blowing gently.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वा to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाद|विवादः
विवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Contest, contention.<BR>2 Contest at law, a legal dispute, litigation, a law suit.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वद to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादानुगत|विवादानुगतः
विवादानुगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Disputed, litigated.<BR>E.<BR>विवाद a law suit, अनु according to, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=784" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादार्थिन्
विवादार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Seeking for a dispute or quarrel.<BR>m. (-र्थी)<BR>A litigant, a prosecutor, a plaintiff.<BR>E.<BR>विवाद, and अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादास्पदीभूत
विवादास्पदीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Litigated, contested at law.<BR>E.<BR>विवाद, and आस्पद place, भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Disputing, contending, a litigant.<BR>E.<BR>विवाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवार|विवारः
विवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Dilatation, expansion.<BR>2 Open or expanded state of the organs of speech for the articulation of vowels and sibilants.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृ to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास|विवासः
विवास<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Without clothes, naked^1.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Banishment.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., and वास vesture or abode.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासकरण
विवासकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Banishing, transporting.<BR>E.<BR>विवास, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासन|विवासनं
विवासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Exile, banishment.<BR>E.<BR>वि away, वासन abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासित
विवासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Banished, expelled.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and वस to dwell, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास्य
विवास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>To be expelled or transported.<BR>E.<BR>वि away, वस to dwell, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह|विवाहः
विवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Marriage.<BR>E.<BR>वि mutually, वह to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहित|विवाहितः
विवाहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Married.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वह to bear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह्य|विवाह्यः
विवाह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>Marriageable, to be married.<BR>m. (-ह्यः)<BR>A son-in-law, a bridegroom.<BR>E.<BR>विवाह marriage, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्त|विविक्तं
विविक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Lonely, solitary, desart.<BR>2 Pure, faultless.<BR>3 Separated, distinguished, disjoined, detached.<BR>4 Discriminative, judicious, a judge.<BR>5 Discriminated, judged.<BR>6 Profound, (as judgment or thought.)<BR>7 Intent on.<BR>E.<BR>वि before विच to be or make separate, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तभाव
विविक्तभाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Intent upon any object.<BR>E.<BR>विविक्त, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तसेविन्
विविक्तसेविन्<BR>mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>Solitary, retired, recluse, seeking or affecting solitude.<BR>E.<BR>विविक्त, and सेविन् who serves or pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षत्
विविक्षत्<BR>mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षती-क्षत्)<BR>Wishing or purposing to enter.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, desid. v., शतृ Aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षा
विविक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Wish or purpose to enter.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षु
विविक्षु<BR>mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>Wishing or intending to enter.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्य
विविच्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having considered, discussed, judged.<BR>E.<BR>विच to judge, with वि prefixed, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविदिवस्
विविदिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-द्युषी-वस्)<BR>Obtaining, getting.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, वसु aff., with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविद्वस्
विविद्वस्<BR>mfn. (-द्वान्-दुषी-द्वस)<BR>Knowing, wise.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविध|विविधं
विविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Various, multiform, of many sorts.<BR>E.<BR>वि before विधि sort, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविशिवस्
विविशिवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-श्युषी-वस्)<BR>Entering.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, root rep., वसु aff., इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविश्वस्
विविश्वस्<BR>mfn. (-श्वान्-शुषी-श्वस्)<BR>Entering, who or what enters.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, वसु aff., root rep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीत|विवीतः
विवीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An inclosed spot of ground, abounding in grass, wood, &c., a preserved pasture, a paddock, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and वीत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीतभर्त्तृ|विवीतभर्तृ
विवीतभर्त्तृ<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>The superintendant or owner of a preserved pasture.<BR>E.<BR>विवीत a paddock, &c., and भर्त्तृ a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्त
विवृक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Abandoned, left.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A woman disliked or deserted by her husband.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृच to abandon, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत|विवृतं
विवृत<BR>m. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expanded, extended, extensive, large.<BR>2 Evident, displayed, made manifest.<BR>3 Exposed, discovered.<BR>4 Opened.<BR>5 Explained, interpreted, expounded.<BR>6 Open (as the organs of speech for the articulation of vowels and sibilants.)<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A disease, an ulcer attended with much pain and heat.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृ to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृताक्ष|विवृताक्षः
विवृताक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Large-eyed.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A cock.<BR>E.<BR>विवृत large, अक्षि the eye, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृति|विवृतिः
विवृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Explanation, exposition, gloss, comment, interpretation.<BR>2 Making clear or manifest.<BR>3 Discovery, exposure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृ to prefer or choose, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्त|विवृत्तं
विवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Turned or twisted round, whirling, revolving, rolling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सत्
विवृत्सत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>Wishing to be.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सितृ
विवृत्सितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Who or what wishes to be.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, desid. v., तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्ति|विवृत्तिः
विवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Turning round, rolling, whirling, tumbling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृत to be, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्ध
विवृद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Augmented, increased.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and वृद्ध the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धि|विवृद्धिः
विवृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Growth, increase, augmentation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वृद्धि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक|विवेकः
विवेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Discrimination, judgment, the faculty of distinguishing things by their properties, and classing them according to their real not apparent nature; in the Vedānta system, it is applied to the power of separating Brahma or invisible spirit, from the ostensible world, truth from untruth, or reality from illusion.<BR>2 Discussion, investigation.<BR>3 A reservoir, a bath.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, विच to judge, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकता
विवेकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Judgment, discrimination, the faculty or property of judgment.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विवेकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकदृश्वत्व
विवेकदृश्वत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Discrimination, discernment.<BR>E.<BR>विवेकदृश्वन्, and त्व aff.; or with तल्, विवेकदृश्वता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकदृश्वन्
विवेकदृश्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा)<BR>A wise or discerning man.<BR>E.<BR>विवेक, and दृश्वन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिता
विवेकिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Discussion, discrimination, discriminativeness.<BR>E.<BR>विवेकी discriminative, and तल् aff.; also विवेकित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Judicious, discriminative.<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A sage, a philosopher, a judge.<BR>E.<BR>वि before विच to judge, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तव्य
विवेक्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be discussed or judged.<BR>E.<BR>वि before विच to judge, तव्य aff.; also विवेच्य and विवेचनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचन|विवेचनं
विवेचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Discrimination, judgment, distinguishing truth from falsehood.<BR>E.<BR>वि before विच to judge, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=785" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचनीय|विवेचनीयः
विवेचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be judged or discussed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, विच् to judge, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ<BR>m. (-ढा)<BR>A husband, a bridegroom, a lover.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वह to obtain, aff. तृन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्रुवत्
विव्रुवत्<BR>mfn. (-वन्-वती-वत्)<BR>Silent, refraining from or refusing to speak.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative वुवत् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Affectation of indifference, one of the branches of amorous dalliance, or feminine actions, tending to excite love or desire.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वा to go, aff. कु, विवु said here to mean a particular gait, and ओक house, place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश|विशं
विश<BR>r. 6th cl. (विशति)<BR>1 To enter, to pervade.<BR>With आङ् or प्र prefixed,<BR>1 To go in, to enter.<BR>2 To occupy or engross.<BR>With उप,<BR>1 To sit, to sit down.<BR>2 To approach.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To dwell, to abide.<BR>2 To place or station.<BR>With नि or अभि and नि,<BR>1 To rest, to halt, to sit down, especially before or in presence of.<BR>2 To conceal.<BR>With निर्,<BR>To go out or forth.<BR>With परि,<BR>To place before, to present.<BR>With सम,<BR>To lie down, to repose.<BR>With सम् and नि,<BR>To be near, to be close to or in the neighbourhood.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To introduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश|विशं
विश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>The film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश्<BR>m. (विट्)<BR>1 A man of the mercantile tribe.<BR>2 A man in general.<BR>f. (विट्)<BR>1 Entrance.<BR>2 A daughter.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क|विशंक|विशङ्कः
विशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कट|विशंकट|विशङ्कटः
विशङ्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा or -टी-टं)<BR>Great, large.<BR>E.<BR>वि the particle, and शङ्कटच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कमान
विशङ्कमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-न)<BR>Fearing, apprehending.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शकि to doubt, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशत्
विशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Entering.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
विशद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Of a white colour.<BR>2 Clear, pure, pellucid.<BR>3 Evident, apparent, manifest.<BR>4 Beautiful.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>White, the colour.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शद to wither or perish, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशय|विशयः
विशय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>2 Refuge, asylum.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयिन्
विशयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Dubious, uncertain.<BR>2 Doubting.<BR>E.<BR>विशय doubt, इनि aff., or वि before शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशर|विशरः
विशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शृ to injure or kill, aff. अप्; also with ल्युट्, aff. विशरण n. (-णं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
विशल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Free from thorns or spikes.<BR>2 Free from care or pain.<BR>f. (-ल्या)<BR>1 A twining shrub, (Menispermum cordifolium.)<BR>2 A sort of potherb, the kind not ascertained.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>4 Another, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>5 A sort of fruit, Langaliya.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and शल्य a stalk or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्यकृत्
विशल्यकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>A plant, (Echites dichotoma, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसन|विशसनं|विशसनः
विशसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>2 Dissecting, cutting.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sabre, a crooked sword.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शस to hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसित|विशसितः
विशसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hurt, killed.<BR>2 Cut, dissected.<BR>3 Wellmannered.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शस to injure, aff. क्त, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसितृ
विशसितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>1 Killing.<BR>2 Dissecting.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शस to kill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
विशस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Praised, celebrated.<BR>2 Arrogant, ill-mannered, rude.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शस to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
विशस्त्र<BR>mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं)<BR>Disarmed, unarmed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाकार
विशाकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Euphorbia of various kinds.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाख|विशाखः
विशाख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Branchless.<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR>3 A solicitor, a petitioner, a beggar.<BR>4 A spindle.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The sixteenth lunar asterism, figured by a festoon, and containing four, or according to some, two stars, one of which is α or κ Libra.<BR>2 A cucurbitaceous plant, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>E.<BR>वि without, शाख a branch, or विशाखा the asterism, (by which personified the god was cherished,) अण् aff., and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखज|विशाखजः
विशाखज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The orange, (Citrus aurantium.)<BR>E.<BR>विशाख the asterism, and जन् to be born; aff. ड; coming into season, when the sun is in this asterism, or about the end of October.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखल|विशाखलं
विशाखल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An attitude in shooting.<BR>E.<BR>विशाखा the same, and लच् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाय|विशायः
विशाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Sleeping, and watching alternately.<BR>E.<BR>वि intervening, शी to sleep, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारण|विशारणं
विशारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शॄ to injure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Learned, wise.<BR>2 Confident, bold, presuming.<BR>3 Famous, celebrated.<BR>E.<BR>विशाल great, extensive, (fame, &c.) and दा to give, aff. क, the ल changed to र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Great, large.<BR>2 Broad.<BR>3 Great, eminent, illustrious.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sort of deer.<BR>2 A sort of bird.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 The city Ougein.<BR>2 Bitter apple, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR>E.<BR>वि particle, and शालच् aff., or विश to enter, Uṇādi aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालकुल
विशालकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Well born.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An illustrious family.<BR>E.<BR>विशाल, and कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालता
विशालता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Width, breadth.<BR>2 Magnitude, bulk.<BR>2 Eminence, distinction.<BR>E.<BR>विशाल large, तल् aff. of the abstract; also विशालत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालत्वच्
विशालत्वच्<BR>m. (-त्वक्)<BR>A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>विशाल large, and त्वच् skin or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालाक्ष|विशालाक्षः
विशालाक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Having large or beautiful eyes.<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 GARUḌA.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>विशाल large, and अक्षि the eye, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 An iron crow.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A spade, a hoe.<BR>2 A highway, a broad or carriage road.<BR>3 A very minute arrow, a sort of needle or spindle.<BR>4 A barber's wife.<BR>5 A sick room, or the dwelling of the sick.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying possessed of, &c., and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिञ्जान
विशिञ्जान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिजि to sound, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशित
विशित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sharpened.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शि to sharpen, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=786" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिप|विशिपं
विशिप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>A palace, a temple.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, अप Uṇādi aff., and इ substituted for the pen. vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्ट|विशिष्टः
विशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Endowed with, possessed of, having, inherent or attached to.<BR>2 Excellent, superior, distinguished.<BR>3 Especial, peculiar.<BR>4 Having distinctive and exclusive properties.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिष to tell qualities, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टता
विशिष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Excellence, distinction.<BR>2 Individuality, having distinguishing or characteristic qualities.<BR>3 Peculiarity, as of duty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also विशिष्टत्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्ण|विशीर्णः
विशीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Dry, dried up, withered, decayed.<BR>2 Wasted, impaired.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शॄ to injure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्य्य|विशीर्य
विशीर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To crumble or fall to ruin, likely or fit to.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शॄ to injure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्य्यमाण|विशीर्यमाण
विशीर्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being wasted or destroyed, decaying, perishing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शॄ to injure, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
विशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Ill-behaved, indecorous, immoral.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., शील behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्ध|विशुद्धं
विशुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pure, purified, clean, cleansed, free from vice or fault.<BR>2 Pious, virtuous.<BR>3 Humble, modest, compliant.<BR>4 Corrected.<BR>E.<BR>वि intensitive prefix, and शुद्ध pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धि|विशुद्धिः
विशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Purity, purification.<BR>2 Equality, similarity.<BR>3 Removal of doubt.<BR>4 Correctness.<BR>5 In Algebra, a subtractive quantity.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धिभाज्
विशुद्धिभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Pure, free from soil or vice.<BR>E.<BR>विशुद्धि, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशृङ्खल|विशृंखल|विशृङ्खलः
विशृङ्खल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Unchecked, unrestrained, unfettered, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
विशेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Sort, kind, manner.<BR>2 Difference, individual or specific identity and consequent distinction from every other individual or species.<BR>3 (In logic,) The peculiar attribute, (predicabile proprium,) the cause of perception of exclusion.<BR>4 Excellence, superiority.<BR>5 A limb, a member.<BR>6 A mark on the forehead with Sandal.<BR>7 A figure of rhetoric, distinguished as of three kinds, all implying variety of means or effect.<BR>E.<BR>वि discriminative prefix, शिष to attribute or distinguish by attributes, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
विशेषक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Discriminative, distinguishing, attributive, characteristic.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 A mark on the forehead made with Sandal, &c., and worn either as an ornament or sectarial distinction.<BR>2 An attribute, a predicate.<BR>3 An arrangement of poetical composition.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिष to attribute, or distinguish, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकाम
विशेषकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Amorous, desirous.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and काम who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषगुण|विशेषगुणः
विशेषगुण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>An object of a single and distinct kind, as the soul, mind, time, place, and the atoms of earth, water, light, and air.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषज्ञ
विशेषज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Wise, intelligent.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
विशेषण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Discriminative, attributive.<BR>2 Distinctive, (as a property, &c.)<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Distinguishing, discriminating.<BR>2 An epithet, an attribute, an adjective.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिष to distinguish by attributes, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणीय
विशेषणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be discriminated or distinguished, what may or ought to be marked as distinct.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिष to distinguish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषतस्
विशेषतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Especially, particularly, specifically.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषधर्म्म|विशेषधर्म|विशेषधर्मः
विशेषधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Peculiar or different duty.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and घर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषभावना
विशेषभावना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 Reflecting on or perceiving differences.<BR>2 (In algebra,) Composition by the difference of the products.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and भावना considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषलक्षण
विशेषलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Specific or characteristic mark or sign.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषवचन
विशेषवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Special or different text.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and वचन a text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविद्वस्
विशेषविद्वस्<BR>m. (-द्वान्)<BR>A sage, a philosopher.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष excellence, and विद्वान् learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविधि|विशेषविधिः
विशेषविधि<BR>f. (-घिः)<BR>Special rule or observance.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषित|विशेषितं
विशेषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Divided, distinguished, separated.<BR>2 Predicated, attributed, having as an attribute or being distinguished by it.<BR>3 Excellent, superior.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष sort, kind, &c., इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषोक्ति|विशेषोक्तिः
विशेषोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 A figure of rhetoric, coupling cause with effect, so as to explain any peculiar manner or condition.<BR>2 Panegyric, recapitulation of merits.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष sort, kind, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्य|विशेष्यः
विशेष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>To be distinguished or discriminated.<BR>2 Distinguishing, to be discriminated by.<BR>3 Principal, primary, chief.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A name, a substantive.<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>The object of a predicate.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शिष to distinguish by its attributes, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोक|विशोकः
विशोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Without grief, happy.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधन|विशोधनं
विशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning, purifying, freeing from soil, defect, or sin.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A plant, commonly Nāgadanti.<BR>2 The capital of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुघ to be pure, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनीय
विशोधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be cleaned or purified, to be freed from soil, fault, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुध to be pure, causal v., अनीयर् aff.; also विशोधितव्य and विशोध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित
विशोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purified, cleansed, freed from soil, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुघ to be pure, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित्व
विशोधित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Cleaning, purifying.<BR>2 Clearing, freeing from obstructions.<BR>E.<BR>विशोघिन्, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, विशोधिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधिन्
विशोधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>1 Cleaning, purifying.<BR>2 Clearing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुध to be pure, causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषण|विशोषणं
विशोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Drying, desiccating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुष to be dry, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषित
विशोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dried, dried up.<BR>E.<BR>वि before शुष to be dry, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्न|विश्नः
विश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>Lustre, shining.<BR>E.<BR>विच्छ to shine, नङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रणन|विश्रणनं
विश्रणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Gift, giving, donation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रण to give, ल्युट् aff.; also विश्राणन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्ध|विश्रब्धः
विश्रब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Trusted, confided in, confided to.<BR>2 Patient, tranquil.<BR>3 Lowly-minded, not lofty, not magnanimous. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">Page788</a>]<BR>4 Excessive, exceeding, much.<BR>5 Firm, steady.<BR>6 Rested, reposed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रम to be weary or स्रम्भ to trust, &c. aff. क्तः see विस्रब्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=787" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धता
विश्रब्धता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Trust-worthiness.<BR>E.<BR>विश्रब्ध, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम|विश्रमः
विश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Rest, repose, cessation from fatigue or work.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, श्रम to be weary, aff. अच्; also विश्राम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रमित
विश्रमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Wearied, exhausted.<BR>E.<BR>विश्रम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भ|विश्रंभ|विश्रंभः|विश्रम्भः
विश्रम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Trust, confidence.<BR>2 Affection, affectionate inquiry.<BR>3 Festive or sportive noise or tumult.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रम्भ to trust, aff. घञ्, and the initial optionally changed; also विस्रम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्य
विश्रम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having rested.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रम to be weary, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रय|विश्रयः
विश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Abode, asylum.<BR>2 Dependance upon.<BR>E.<BR>वि, श्री to serve, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रयिन्
विश्रयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>1 Living or dwelling in.<BR>2 Serving, depending on.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्री to serve, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणन|विश्राणनं
विश्राणन<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Gift, giving, donation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रण to give, r. 10th cl. aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणित
विश्राणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bestowed, given.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रण to give, r. 10th cl. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्त|विश्रांत|विश्रान्तः
विश्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Rested, reposed.<BR>2 Ceasing, desisting from.<BR>3 Calm, composed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रान्त the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्ति|विश्रांति|विश्रांतिः|विश्रान्तिः
विश्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Rest, repose, cessation from toil or occupation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रम to be weary, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राम|विश्रामः
विश्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Rest, repose.<BR>2 Pause, stop, cessation.<BR>3 Tranquillity, composure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रम to be weary, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राव|विश्रावः
विश्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Fame, celebrity.<BR>2 Flowing, dropping.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रु to hear or to drop, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रावण
विश्रावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Causing to flow or drop.<BR>2 Bleeding.<BR>3 Apprising, causing to hear.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रु to ooze, &c., causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुत|विश्रुतः
विश्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famous, celebrated, notorious.<BR>2 Known.<BR>3 Pleased, delighted, happy.<BR>4 Dropped, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुति|विश्रुतिः
विश्रुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Celebrity, fame, notoriety.<BR>2 Oozing, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्रु to hear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
विश्लथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Languid, relaxed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्लथ loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथाङ्ग
विश्लथाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Weak, relaxed, nerveless.<BR>E.<BR>विश्लथ, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्ट
विश्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Separated, disunited.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्लिष to unite, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेष|विश्लेषः
विश्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Separation, distance, especially of lovers, or husband and wife.<BR>2 Disunion, disjunction, separation in general.<BR>3 (In arithmetic,) The converse of addition.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्लिष to unite, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषजाति|विश्लेषजातिः
विश्लेषजाति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>(In arithmetic,) The assimilation of difference, the reduction of fractional difference.<BR>E.<BR>विश्लेष, and जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व<BR>mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं)<BR>All, entire, whole, universal.<BR>n. (-श्वं)<BR>The world, the universe.<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>A deity of a particular class in which ten are enumerated; their names are VASU, SATYA, KRATU, DAKṢA, KĀLA, KĀMA, DHṚTI, KURU, PURURĀVAN, and MADRAVA: They are worshipped particularly at the funeral obsequies in honor of deceased progenitors in general, and receive an oblation of clarified butter at the daily and domestic Śrāddha.<BR>nf. (-श्वं-श्वा)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>f. (-श्वा)<BR>A tree, the bark of which is said to be used in dying red, commonly Atis, (Betula.)<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, to pervade, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकद्रु|विश्वकद्रुः
विश्वकद्रु<BR>mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>Wicked, vile.<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>1 A dog trained for the chase.<BR>2 Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, कन् pleonasm, द्रु to run, to pursue, aff. डु, or विश्व with कदि to cry or call, aff. डु, and र augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकर्म्मन्|विश्वकर्मन्
विश्वकर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The son of BRAHMĀ, and artist of the gods.<BR>3 A saint.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व universal, कर्म्म work, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकर्म्मसुता|विश्वकर्मसुता
विश्वकर्म्मसुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>SAṂJÑĀ, one of the wives of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वकर्म्म the artist of the gods, and सुता the daughter; also विश्वकर्म्मजा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वका
विश्वका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of gull, (Larus ridibundus.)<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, कै to cry, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकृत्
विश्वकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Who or what makes all.<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>1 The creator, the maker of all things.<BR>2 The carpenter or architect, and artist of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकेतु|विश्वकेतुः
विश्वकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>ANIRUDDHA, an incarnation of KĀMA, as the son of PRADYUMNA.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व universe, केतु a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वक्सेन
विश्वक्सेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A particular form of that deity, to whom the fragments of a sacrifice to VIṢṆU are offered.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वक every way. and सेना an army, more properly विष्वक्सेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगन्धा|विश्वगंधा
विश्वगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगायत्
विश्वगायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Spreading or going in every direction.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वक् and आयत् going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगोप्तृ
विश्वगोप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and गोप्तृ preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वङ्कर|विश्वंकर|विश्वंकरः|विश्वङ्करः
विश्वङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>All-creating, making all.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The eye.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजन
विश्वजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>All men, mankind.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजनीन
विश्वजनीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Good for or suitable to all men.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वजन, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजनीय
विश्वजनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Suitable or relating to all men.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, जन mankind, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजन्य
विश्वजन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Fit or good for all men.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वजन, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजित्
विश्वजित्<BR>mfn. (-तित्)<BR>All-subduing.<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>1 A particular ceremony or sacrifice.<BR>2 The cord or noose of VARUṆA.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and जित् what subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वञ्च्
विश्वञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-श्वङ्-शुची-श्वक्)<BR>Going every where.<BR>ind. or adv. n. (-श्वक्)<BR>Every where, universally.<BR>E.<BR>विञ्च all, अञ्च to go, aff. क्विप्; it is more usually written both in simple and compound forms विष्वञ्च, from a different etymology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतस्
विश्वतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Every where, all around, universally.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वदेव|विश्वदेवः
विश्वदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A Viśvadeva, a deity of a particular class: see विश्व.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, दिव to sport, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वद्र्यञ्च्
विश्वद्र्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्)<BR>Moving every where or universally.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वक every where, अद्रि substituted for the final, अञ्च to go, aff. क्विप्; also विष्वद्र्यञ्च्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=788" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वधारिन्
विश्वधारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>All-sustaining.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A deity.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and धारिन् upholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वनाथ|विश्वनाथः
विश्वनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA, especially as the object of peculiar adoration at Benares.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व the universe, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वपा
विश्वपा<BR>m. (-पाः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and पा who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वप्सन्
विश्वप्सन्<BR>m. (-प्सा)<BR>1 Fire, or the deity of fire, AGNI.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, प्सा to eat, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वबोध|विश्वबोधः
विश्वबोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and बोध who explains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभुज्
विश्वभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>1 Enjoying or possessing all things.<BR>2 Eating all things.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभू
विश्वभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>The third of the seven Buddhas, according to some systems.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभेषज|विश्वभेषजं|विश्वभेषजः
विश्वभेषज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all (diseases), भेषज a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभोजन
विश्वभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating all sorts of food.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभोजस्
विश्वभोजस्<BR>m. (-जाः)<BR>One who enjoys all things.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, भुज to enjoy, Uṇādi aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वमदा
विश्वमदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, मद to intoxicate, aff. लङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वम्भर|विश्वंभर|विश्वंभरः|विश्वम्भरः
विश्वम्भर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>All-sustaining.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all (things), भृ to support or nourish, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वम्भराधिप
विश्वम्भराधिप<BR>m. (पः)<BR>A king.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वम्भरा the earth, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वयु|विश्वयुः
विश्वयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, यु to join, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वराज्
विश्वराज्<BR>m. (-राट् or -राड्)<BR>A universal sovereign.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and राज who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरूप|विश्वरूपः
विश्वरूप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Taking all forms, existing in all forms, universal, omnipresent.<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरेतस्
विश्वरेतस्<BR>m. (-ताः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and रेतम् seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरोचन|विश्वरोचनः
विश्वरोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, रोचन digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वविधायिन्
विश्वविधायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A deity, a creator.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and विघायिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्ववेदस्
विश्ववेदस्<BR>m. (-दाः)<BR>A sage, a saint, one who knows all things.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, विदि to know, aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्यापक
विश्वव्यापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>All-pervading, every where diffused.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and व्यापक what pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्यापिन्
विश्वव्यापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>All-diffused or pervading.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and व्यापिन् what spreads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्याप्ति
विश्वव्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Universal diffusion or permeation.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and व्याप्ति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसन
विश्वसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Trusting, confiding in.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्वस to breathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसह
विश्वसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>All-enduring.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>1 The earth.<BR>2 One of the tongues of fire.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, सह to bear, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसारक|विश्वसारकं
विश्वसारक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The prickly pear, (Cactus Indicus, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, सार essence, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसित|विश्वसितः
विश्वसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Trusted, believed or confided in.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्वस to breathe, aff. क्त, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसृज्
विश्वसृज्<BR>m. (-सृक् or -सृग् or -सृट् or -सृड्)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all (the universe), सृज to create, aff. क्विन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्त|विश्वस्तः
विश्वस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Trusted, confided in, faithful.<BR>f. (-स्ता)<BR>A widow.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying kind or sort, or in the fem. form, privation, and श्वस to live or breathe, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्रष्टृ
विश्वस्रष्टृ<BR>m. (-ष्टा)<BR>The creator of all, GOD.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व, and स्रष्ट्ट creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाची
विश्वाची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>One of the Apsaras or courtezans of Svarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वात्मन्
विश्वात्मन्<BR>m. (-त्मा)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>n. (-त्म)<BR>The soul of the world, the universal spirit, GOD.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाधायस्
विश्वाधायस्<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>A deity, a god.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, आङ् before धा to hold or support, असि aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामिच
विश्वामिच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A Muni, the son of GĀDHI, originally of the military order, but who became by long and painful austerities a Brahmarṣi, in which character he appears in the Rāmāyaṇa, as the early preceptor and counsellor of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, मिच the friend, and the vowel of the prefix made long in this sense; if attributively used, the compound is विश्वमिच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामिचप्रिय
विश्वामिचप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The cocoanut tree.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वामिच the saint VIŚVĀMITRA, and प्रिय beloved, having been created by the saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वावसु|विश्वावसुः
विश्वावसु<BR>m. (-सुः)<BR>One of the Gandharbas or celestial singers.<BR>f. (-सुः)<BR>A particular night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास|विश्वासः
विश्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Trust, faith, confidence.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्वस to breathe or live, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासकारण
विश्वासकारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Cause or motive of trust.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and करण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासकृत्
विश्वासकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Inspiring confidence or faith.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and कृत् who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासघात|विश्वासघातः
विश्वासघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Violation of trust, treachery.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and घात destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासघातक|विश्वासघातकः
विश्वासघातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A traitor, one who betrays confidence.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and घातक who destroys; also विश्वासघातिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासपात्र
विश्वासपात्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A confidential agent, one worthy to be trusted.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and पात्र vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासप्रद
विश्वासप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Inspiring confidence.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासप्रतिपन्न
विश्वासप्रतिपन्न<BR>m. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Confiding, trusting.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and प्रतिपन्न possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासभङ्ग|विश्वासभङ्गः
विश्वासभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Breach of faith, violation of confidence.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासभूमि|विश्वासभूमिः
विश्वासभूमि<BR>f. (मिः)<BR>An object of trust, a person worthy of confidence.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and भूमि soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासस्थान
विश्वासस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An object or person of trust or confidence.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासित
विश्वासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Inspired with confidence.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्वस to breathe, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासिन्
विश्वासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>1 Trusting, confiding in.<BR>2 Honest, trusty.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्य
विश्वास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 To be trusted or depended on, to be believed.<BR>2 To be encouraged or inspired with confidence.<BR>ind.<BR>Having encouraged or inspired with confidence.<BR>E.<BR>वि before श्वस to breathe, ण्यत् aff. or causal v., and यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=789" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्यता
विश्वास्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Trust-worthiness.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वास्य, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेदेवृ
विश्वेदेवृ<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>The clitoris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेश|विश्वेशः
विश्वेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व all, and ईश lord: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेश्वर|विश्वेश्वरः
विश्वेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA, under a form or appellation in which especially he is worshipped at Benares, where a celebrated temple is appropriated to him in the character of lord or god of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व the universe, and ईश्वर god; also similar compounds, as विश्वेश, विश्वनाथ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष|विषं|विषः
विष<BR>r. 6th cl. (विषति)<BR>To pervade.<BR>(औ) औविष r. 9th cl. (विष्णाति)<BR>To have no occasion or use for, to separate or withdraw from.<BR>(उ) विषु r. 1st cl. (वेषति)<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>(औ इर ऌ) औ इर विषॢ r. 3rd cl. (विवेष्टि विविष्टे)<BR>To pervade, to spread or extend through nature, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष्<BR>f. (-विट्)<BR>1 Fæces, ordure, excrement.<BR>2 Diffusion, spreading.<BR>E.<BR>विष to pervade, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष|विषं|विषः
विष<BR>mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>Poison, venom.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 The fibres attached to the stalk of the lotus.<BR>3 Gum myrrh.<BR>4 A vegetable poison, (Aconitum ferox.)<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>A tree, the bark of which is used in dyeing of a red colour.<BR>E.<BR>विष to pervade, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषक्त
विषक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Clinging or adhering to closely.<BR>2 In contact with.<BR>E.<BR>वि before षञ्ज to embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघा
विषघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>A twining shrub, (Menispermum cordifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, हन् to destroy, aff. ड, and घ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघातिन्
विषघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>A tree, (Mimosa sirisa.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and घातिन् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघ्न|विषघ्नः
विषघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>1 A tree, (Mimosa sirisa.)<BR>2 A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>3 Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>2 A plant, commonly Bichati.<BR>3 Turmeric.<BR>4 Bitter apple or colocynth.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषजुष्ट
विषजुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Poisoned, suffering from poison.<BR>2 Poisonous.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and जुष्ट united with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषणि
विषणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ड|विषंड|विषंडं|विषण्डं
विषण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>The fibres of the stalk of the water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ण|विषण्णः
विषण्ण<BR>mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>Dejected, desponding, spiritless, disinclined to exertion.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्णता
विषण्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dejection, lassitude, want of energy or spirit, especially as one of the effects of unsuccessful love.<BR>E.<BR>विषण्ण relaxed, तल् aff. of the abstract; also with त्व, विषण्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्णवदन
विषण्णवदन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Looking sad or dejected.<BR>E.<BR>विषण्ण, and वदन face: also विषण्णमुख, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषतुल्य
विषतुल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>Fatal, deadly.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and तुल्य equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषत्वर
विषत्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषद|विषदं|विषदः
विषद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Yielding or giving poison.<BR>2 Shedding water.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Green vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison or water, and दा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदंष्ट्रा
विषदंष्ट्रा<BR>f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>A medicinal plant and antidote, commonly Sarpa or Sāmpkaṅkāli, or snake skin.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदन्तक|विषदंतक|विषदन्तकः
विषदन्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, दन्त tooth, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदर्शनमृत्युक|विषदर्शनमृत्युकः
विषदर्शनमृत्युक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of pheasant.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, (perhaps put for the snake,) दर्शन seeing, मृत्युक who dies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधर|विषधरः
विषधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Venomous, poisonous.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, घर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधर्म्मा|विषधर्मा
विषधर्म्मा<BR>f. (-र्म्मा)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधात्री
विषधात्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>The wife of Jaratkāru, and goddess presiding over snakes.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, घात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनाशन|विषनाशनः
विषनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A tree, (Mimosa sirisa.)<BR>2 An antidote.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Removing or curing poison.<BR>E.<BR>षिव poison, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनाशिन्
विषनाशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>Antidote.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A plant: see विषदंष्ट्रा.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, नाशिन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनुद्
विषनुद्<BR>m. (-नुत्)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, नुद् to eject, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषपुष्प|विषपुष्पं|विषपुष्पः
विषपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>The blue lotus.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषपुष्पक|विषपुष्पकः
विषपुष्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sickness or disease induced by eating poisonous flowers.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, पुष्प a flower, or विषपुष्प the Vangueria, &c., कन् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषप्रयोग|विषप्रयोगः
विषप्रयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Employing or administering poison.<BR>E.<BR>विण, and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभक्षण
विषभक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking poison.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and भक्षण feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभिषज्
विषभिषज्<BR>m. (-षक्)<BR>A dealer in antidotes, a snake-catcher, or one who pretends to cure the bite of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and भिषज् a doctor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभुजङ्ग|विषभुजंग|विषभुजङ्गः
विषभुजङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A poisonous snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and भुजङ्ग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभृत्
विषभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Venomous, poisonous.<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and भृत् who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषम|विषमं|विषमः
विषम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Difficult, (of access,) rough, uneven.<BR>2 Difficult, &c. (of comprehending,) as a book.<BR>3 Painful, difficult, troublesome, (in general.)<BR>4 Odd, (in numbers.)<BR>5 Unparalleled, unequalled.<BR>6 Wicked, dishonest.<BR>7 Fearful, frightful, awful.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Difficulty, pain.<BR>2 Unevenness, inequality.<BR>3 Oddness, (in numeration.)<BR>4 An inaccessible place, a thicket, a precipice.<BR>5 (In rhetoric,) Description of unusual or incompatible cause and effect.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative or contra-indicative, before सम even, smooth, equal, &c., and स after the इ of the prefix, changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमकर्ण|विषमकर्णः
विषमकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>The hypothenuse of a right angled triangle, formed between the gnomon and the two sides of the shadow.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and कर्ण hypothenuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमकर्म्मन्|विषमकर्मन्
विषमकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मा)<BR>1 An odd or unparalleled act.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) The finding of quantities from their difference or that of their squares.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमखात
विषमखात<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>An irregular excavation or one with unequal sides.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and खात excavation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमचतुरस्र|विषमचतुरस्रः
विषमचतुरस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>An unequal four-sided figure, a trapezium.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and चतुरस्र four-angled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमछद|विषमच्छद|विषमच्छदः
विषमछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd, and छद a leaf; having seven leaves on a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमछाया|विषमच्छाया
विषमछाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The shadow of the gnomon at noon when the sun is in the equinoxes.<BR>E.<BR>विषम oblique, and छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=790" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमज्वर|विषमज्वरः
विषमज्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A violent fever.<BR>2 Irregularly remittent fever.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and ज्वर a fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमत्रिभुज|विषमत्रिभुजः
विषमत्रिभुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A scalene triangle.<BR>E.<BR>विषम unequal, त्रिभुज triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमनयन|विषमनयनः
विषमनयन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd, नयन an eye; having a third eye in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमन्त्र|विषमंत्र|विषमन्त्रः
विषमन्त्र<BR>m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>A snake-catcher, one who by pretended charms, &c. attracts snakes and cures the bite.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>A charm for curing snake bites.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, मन्त्र a charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषममय|विषममयं
विषममय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Resulting from or produced by inequality.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमरूप्य|विषमरूप्यं
विषमरूप्य<BR>mfn. (प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>Resulting from or produced by unequal quantities or qualities.<BR>E.<BR>विषम uneven, and रूप्य aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमविभाग|विषमविभागः
विषमविभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Unequal division of property amongst coheirs.<BR>E.<BR>विषम uneven, विभाग portion of inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशायिन्
विषमशायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी यिनी-यि)<BR>Sleeping irregularly.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and शायिन् who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशिष्ट|विषमशिष्टः
विषमशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Unjust, unfair, (division.)<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशील
विषमशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Uneven.<BR>2 Uneasy, difficult.<BR>E.<BR>विषभ, and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमसाहस
विषमसाहस<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Temerity, daring.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and माहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमस्थ|विषमस्थः
विषमस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Standing unevenly.<BR>2 Inaccessible, safely posted.<BR>3 Being in difficulty or misfortune.<BR>E.<BR>विषम uneven, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाशन
विषमाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Eating irregularly, either as to quantity or time.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाक्ष|विषमाक्षः
विषमाक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd, अक्षि the eye, aff. टच्; having a third eye, or one in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमायुध|विषमायुधः
विषमायुध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd, आयुध a weapon, armed with five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाशय
विषमाशय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Crafty, dishonest.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made or become uneven, irregular, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विषम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीय|विषमीयं
विषमीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Produced or resulting from inequalities.<BR>E.<BR>विषम uneven, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमुष्टि|विषमुष्टिः
विषमुष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A kind of shrub of medicinal properties, commonly termed Biṣdori or Karsinh.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, मुष्टि a handful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमृत्यु|विषमृत्युः
विषमृत्यु<BR>m. (-त्युः)<BR>A sort of bird, a kind of pheasant.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमेक्षण|विषमेक्षणः
विषमेक्षण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd (three), ईक्षण eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमेषु|विषमेषुः
विषमेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd (five), इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषय|विषयः
विषय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Any object of sense, any thing perceivable by the senses, as colour, form, flavour, odour, and sound.<BR>2 An object in general, as of affection or desire, &c.<BR>3 Worldly object or pursuit, affair, business, transaction, &c.<BR>4 A country, whether inhabited or uninhabited.<BR>5 Refuge, asylum.<BR>6 Department, sphere, element, home, province, that which is peculiarly known or frequented, as a particular study by its professors, a particular town by its townsfolk, water by fish, air by birds, &c.<BR>7 A collection of villages.<BR>8 Any thing indigenous or peculiar to a province, &c.<BR>9 A religious obligation or observance.<BR>10 Semen virile.<BR>11 A lover, a hus band.<BR>E.<BR>वि before षि to bind, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयक
विषयक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Relating to, concerning, (any object.)<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकत्व
विषयकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>State of an affair, circumstance or thing.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकर्म्मन्|विषयकर्मन्
विषयकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Worldly concern or act.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकाम
विषयकाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Desire of worldly goods or pleasures.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयात्मक
विषयात्मक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Identical with or affecting sensual or worldly objects.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and आत्मक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयवासिन्
विषयवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>Engaged in the affairs of life.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and वासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 An organ of sense.<BR>3 KĀMADEVA.<BR>4 An epicurean, a sensualist, one heedful of objects of sense or attentive to worldly objects.<BR>5 A materialist, one who disbelieves the existence of that which is not cognizable by the senses.<BR>E.<BR>विषय an object of sense, अय to go, to follow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयासक्त
विषयासक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Attached to objects of sense, devoted to the world.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and आसक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Attached to objects of sense, carnal, sensual.<BR>2 Conversant with or interested in worldly occupations or enjoyments.<BR>n. (-यि)<BR>An organ of sense.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 The deity KĀMA.<BR>3 A sensualist.<BR>4 A materialist, one who denies the existence of any thing which is not an object of sense.<BR>5 A man of business or of the world.<BR>E.<BR>विषय an organ of sense, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयोपसेवा
विषयोपसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Sensuality.<BR>E.<BR>विषय, and उपसेय addiction to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषल|विषलं|विषलः
विषल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Poison, venom.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषविद्या
विषविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>The administration of antidotes, the cure of poisons by drugs or charms.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषविधान
विषविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Administering poison judicially, or by way of ordeal.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and विधान rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवेग|विषवेगः
विषवेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Absorption of venom, as shewn by some bodily effects or changes.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and वेग natural excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवैद्य|विषवैद्यः
विषवैद्य<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>A dealer in antidotes, one professing by charms, &c. to cure the bite of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and वैद्य a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषशूक|विषशूकः
विषशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, and शूक a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषशृङ्गिन्|विषशृंगिन्
विषशृङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसूचक|विषसूचकः
विषसूचक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and सूचक informer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसृक्कन्
विषसृक्कन्<BR>m. (-क्का)<BR>A wasp.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and सृक्कन् the corner of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषहर|विषहरः
विषहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>An antidote, removing venom.<BR>f. (-रा or -री)<BR>The goddess of the serpent race, the sister of VĀSUKI, and wife of JARATKĀRU.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, हृ to take, aff. अप् or टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषहृदय
विषहृदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Malicious, malignant, cherishing hatred or hostility.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
विषह्य<BR>mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>To be borne or endured.<BR>ind.<BR>Having borne.<BR>E.<BR>वि before षह to bear, aff. यत् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=791" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा<BR>ind. Aptote noun.<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>षो to destroy (ignorance), with वि prefixed, and ओ Uṇādi aff.; see विष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाङ्कुर|विषांकुर|विषाङ्कुरः
विषाङ्कुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A spear, a dart.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, अङ्कर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाण|विषाणं|विषाणः
विषाण<BR>subst. mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 The horn of an animal.<BR>2 The tusks of an elephant.<BR>3 The tusk or fang of the boar.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 A plant, the fruit of which is compared to the horn of a ram, &c. commonly Meṣa Śṛṅgī.<BR>2 A medicinal root: see क्षीरकाकोली.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A sort of Costus (C. speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before अस to be, चानश् aff.; the initial of the radical rejected, and स changed to ष; otherwise, वि before षण to serve, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिका
विषाणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of plant, commonly Meṣa Śṛṅgī.<BR>E.<BR>विषाणी as above, and कन् pleonasm, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन्<BR>m. (-णी)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>3 Any animal with horns.<BR>E.<BR>विषाण a horn or tusk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाद|विषादः
विषाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Lassitude, dejection, lowness of spirits, want of energy, especially as the result of unrequited love.<BR>2 Distress, affliction.<BR>3 Disappointment.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सद to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादिन्
विषादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Dejected, disconsolate, sorrowful.<BR>E.<BR>विषाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषानन|विषाननः
विषानन<BR>n. (-नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषान्तक|विषांतक|विषान्तकः
विषान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and अन्तक destroyer; having swallowed the poison that was produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषापह|विषापहः
विषापह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A kind of birth wort, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and अपह removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषायुध|विषायुधः
विषायुध<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषार|विषारः
विषार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, ऋ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषालु
विषालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Venomous, poisonous.<BR>E.<BR>विष, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषास्य|विषास्यः
विषास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A snake.<BR>f. (-स्या)<BR>Marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>विष poison, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषीदत्
विषीदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Sorrowing, despairing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before षद to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषु
विषु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Many, various.<BR>2 Equally, same, like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुण|विषुणः
विषुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Having or possessing various or uniform motion or extension.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वञ्च going every where, न poss. aff., and the final consonant of the primitive rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुप|विषुपं
विषुप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>The equinox: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुव|विषुवं
विषुव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The equinox.<BR>E.<BR>विषु equally, (the night and day,) and व or प aff.; also विषुप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवछाया|विषुवच्छाया
विषुवछाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The shadow of the gnomon at noon when the sun is in the equinoctial points.<BR>E.<BR>विषुव, and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवत्|विषुवन्त्
विषुवत्<BR>n. (-वत्)<BR>The equinox.<BR>E.<BR>विषु equally, (long, the day and night,) and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवदिन
विषुवदिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The day of the equinox.<BR>E.<BR>विषुव, and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवसङ्क्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रांति|विषुवसंक्रान्तिः
विषुवसङ्क्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>The passage of the sun to the next sign at the equinoxes.<BR>E.<BR>विषुव, and सङ्क्रान्ति sun's entrance into a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्क|विष्कः
विष्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (विष्कयति)<BR>To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्तृ
विष्कन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्त्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Going, going in various directions, dispersing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्कदि to go, तृन् aff.; also विस्कन्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्द|विष्कंद|विष्कंदः|विष्कन्दः
विष्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Going, dispersing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्कदि to go, अच् aff.; also विस्कन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्न
विष्कन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Gone.<BR>2 Gone in various directions, dispersed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्कन्द to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ|विष्कंभ|विष्कंभः|विष्कम्भः
विष्कम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 The first of the twenty-seven astronomical periods, called Yogas, or Yoga star of the first lunar mansion.<BR>2 Obstacle, hindrance, impediment, resistance.<BR>3 Spreading, extension.<BR>4 Act, doing any thing.<BR>5 A posture of the devotees called Yogits.<BR>6 One of the performers at a dramatic entertainment, either an actor who in the intervals of the scenes explains to the audience the progress of the story, or one or two of the personages of the drama, who do the same in a soliloquy or dialogue.<BR>7 A tree.<BR>8 The bolt or bar of a door.<BR>9 A post, the roof-tree of a house.<BR>10 The diameter of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ष्कभि to stop or hinder, aff. घञ्; also with कन् added विस्कम्भक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भक|विष्कंभक
विष्कम्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Yoga, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भिन्|विष्कंभिन्
विष्कम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>Obstructive, impeding.<BR>m. (-म्भी)<BR>The bolt or bar of a door.<BR>E.<BR>विष्कम्भ obstruction, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्किर|विष्किरः
विष्किर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 Pulling or tearing to pieces.<BR>E.<BR>वि before कॄ to scatter, and क aff., with सुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट|विष्टः
विष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Entered, penetrated, pervaded.<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Fæces.<BR>E.<BR>विष to pervade, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप|विष्टपं|विष्टपः
विष्टप<BR>mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>A world.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, (into which,) प aff, deriv. irr.; also विष्टभृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टभ
विष्टभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>A world.<BR>E.<BR>विश to pervade, अभच् aff., and the vowel unchanged; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टब्ध
विष्टब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Hindered, obstructed.<BR>2 Stayed, fixed firm, well-supported.<BR>3 Placed in or upon.<BR>4 Paralysed, made stiff or motionless.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तभि to stop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ|विष्टंभ|विष्टंभः|विष्टम्भः
विष्टम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Impediment, hindrance, obstacle.<BR>2 Stopping, staying.<BR>3 Placing in or upon.<BR>4 A disease, obstruction of urine or fæces, ischury, constipation.<BR>5 Paralysis, loss of motion.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तभि to stop or hinder, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भिन्|विष्टंभिन्
विष्टम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>1 Stopping, impeding, what hinders or obstructs.<BR>2 Checking (as perspiration), chilling.<BR>3 Making motionless.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तभि to stop, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टर|विष्टरः
विष्टर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A handful of Kuśa or sacred grass.<BR>3 A seat, a stool, a chair, a couch, &c.<BR>4 The seat of the Brahman, either real or in effigy, as presiding at a sacrifice.<BR>5 A bed.<BR>6 A seat made of twenty-five straws of Kuśa grass tied up in a sheaf.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. अप, and स changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरश्रवस्
विष्टरश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>विष्टर a tree, श्रु to hear, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरस्थ
विष्टरस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Sitting on a seat, or reclining on a bed of leaves.<BR>E.<BR>विष्टर, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टार|विष्टारः
विष्टार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A form of metre, a species of the order termed Paṅkti, consisting of a verse of four lines, the first and last of which consist of eight syllables each, and the second and third of twelve each.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. घञ्, and स changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
विष्टि<BR>mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि)<BR>Working, labouring, a workman.<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Unpaid labour, working without wages.<BR>2 Occupation, act, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">Page793</a>] action.<BR>3 Hire, wages.<BR>4 The seventh of the variable Karaṇas, or astrological periods so termed, each answering to half a lunar day.<BR>5 Sending, dispatching.<BR>6 Consigning to torture, casting into hell, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, (into pain by it,) and क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=792" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठल|विष्ठलं
विष्ठल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A place situated remote or apart.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying apart, स्थल a place, and स changed to ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>Fæces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्था to stay, (in the intestines,) aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णु|विष्णुः
विष्णु<BR>m. (-ष्णुः)<BR>VIṢṆU, one of the three principal Hindu deities, and the preserver of the world: during the periods of temporary annihilation, he is supposed to sleep on the waters floating on the serpent Śeṣa: BRAHMĀ is fabled to have sprung from a lotus, which originally grew from the navel of VIṢṆU, and the holy river Ganges is said to spring from his foot: the different Avatāras are considered as emanations of this deity, and in KṚṢṆA, he is supposed to have been really and wholly incarnate: LAKṢMĪ his wife, and he is usually represented as a mild and benevolent deity.<BR>2 AGNI or fire.<BR>3 One of the demigods called Vasus.<BR>4 A pure or pious man.<BR>5 The name of an ancient law-giver.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter or pervade (the universe), नु Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुक्रान्ता
विष्णुक्रान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A flower, (Clitorea ternatea.)<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, and क्रान्त overcome; prized by or sacred to that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुगुप्त|विष्णुगुप्तः
विष्णुगुप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>The saint KAUṆḌILYA.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु, and गुप्त hidden, having been concealed by VIṢṆU when pursued by ŚIVA, whom he had incensed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुगृह|विष्णुगृहं
विष्णुगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>The name of a city or country; also Stambapur.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, and गृह residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुदैवत्या
विष्णुदैवत्या<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>The twelfth lunar day of each fortnight.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, and दैवत्य divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुपद|विष्णुपदं
विष्णुपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 The sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>2 The sea of milk.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 One of the twelve Saṅkrāntis or periods, at which the sun enters a sign of the zodiac, especially the first sign after the equinox.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु, and पद् abode, or foot; where VIṢṆU resides or rests, or proceeding from his foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुरथ|विष्णुरथः
विष्णुरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु, and रथ car or conveyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुलिङ्गी
विष्णुलिङ्गी<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A quail.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, and लिङ्ग a mark, ङीप् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुवल्लभ
विष्णुवल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Beloved by VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 A plant, (Echites caryophyallata.)<BR>2 A small fragrant shrub, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>3 LAKṢMI.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, and वल्लभ the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुवाहन|विष्णुवाहनं|विष्णुवाहनः
विष्णुवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पन्द|विष्पंद|विष्पंदः|विष्पन्दः
विष्पन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Throbbing, beating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्यन्दि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फार|विष्फारः
विष्फार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The twang of a bow.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फर or स्फुर to expand, aff. घञ्; in the latter आ is substituted for the vowel, and स is changed to ष, also विस्फार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्य|विष्यः
विष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>Deserving death by poison.<BR>E.<BR>विष venom, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्द|विष्यंदः|विष्यन्दः
विष्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Flowing, issuing, trickling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ष्यदि to go, अच् aff.; also read विस्यन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्दमान
विष्यन्दमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Flowing-trickling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ष्यदि to go, शानच् aff.; also read विस्यन्दमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्व|विष्वः
विष्व<BR>mfn. (-ष्वः-ष्वा-ष्वं)<BR>Injurious, mischievous.<BR>E.<BR>विष to pervade, Uṇādi aff. व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्
विष्वक्<BR>ind.<BR>Every way, all around: see विष्वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्सेन|विष्वक्सेनः
विष्वक्सेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वक् every where, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्सेनप्रिया
विष्वक्सेनप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 A sort of yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR>2 LAKṢMĪ.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वक्सेन VIṢṆU, and प्रिया beloved by, sacred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वग्गत
विष्वग्गत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone all about, spread, extended.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वक्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वग्गति
विष्वग्गति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Going all about.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वक्, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वच्
विष्वच् or विष्वञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-ष्वङ्-षूची-ष्वक्)<BR>Going every where, allpervading.<BR>n. (-ष्वक्)<BR>The equinox.<BR>E.<BR>विषु variously (in various directions), or equally, अञ्च् to go, क्विन् aff.; it is also written, but less accurately विश्वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वणन|विष्वणनं
विष्वणन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Food, eating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्वन to sound, (with the lips, to smack the lips,) and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वद्र्यच्
विष्वद्र्यच् or -द्र्यञ्च्<BR>mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्)<BR>Going every where.<BR>E.<BR>विष्वच् every where, with अद्री augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वाण|विष्वाणः
विष्वाण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>Eating, food.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्वन to sound, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयुक्त
विसंयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Separate, detached.<BR>2 Omitting.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., संयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयोग|विसंयोगः
विसंयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Separation.<BR>2 Omission.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस|विसं
विस<BR>r. 4th cl. (विस्यति)<BR>1 To throw, to send.<BR>2 To put forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस|विसं
विस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily.<BR>E.<BR>विस to send, to put forth, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसकण्ठिका
विसकण्ठिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small crane.<BR>E.<BR>विस the fibres of the lotus stalk, aff. अंच्, कण्ठ the throat, and कन् aff. fem. form, implying comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसङ्कट|विसंकट|विसंकटः|विसङ्कटः
विसङ्कट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>वि and सम before कट to encompass, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसछेद|विसच्छेद
विसछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A part of the fibres of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>विस, and छेद a section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसज|विसजं
विसज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>विस the fibres of the stalk, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसज्ञ
विसज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Lifeless, bereft of sense.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., सज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसनाभि|विसनाभिः
विसनाभि<BR>m. (-भिः)<BR>A quantity of lotuses.<BR>E.<BR>विस the fibres of the stalk, and नाभि navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसनासिका
विसनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of crane.<BR>E.<BR>विस the film of the lotus stalk, and नासिका the nose or beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसपुष्प
विसपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>E.<BR>विस the stalk, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसप्रसून|विसप्रसूनं
विसप्रसून<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR>E.<BR>विस the fibres of the stalk, and प्रसून a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसम्बाद
विसम्बाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Disappointing, deceiving, falsifying one's word, deceiving by a false affirmation or not keeping a promise.<BR>2 Contradiction, disagreeing.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reverse, सम्बाद agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसम्बादिन्
विसम्बादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>1 Cunning, crafty, fraudulent.<BR>2 Disputing, contesting.<BR>E.<BR>विसम्बाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=793" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर|विसरः
विसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A multitude, an assemblage, a flock, a herd, a crowd.<BR>2 Spreading, extending, going forth or abroad.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ग|विसर्गः
विसर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 Abandoning, relinquishment, getting rid of or free from any thing.<BR>2 Departure, going away.<BR>3 Separation.<BR>4 Gift, donation.<BR>5 Final emancipation or beatitude, exemption from worldly existence.<BR>6 Evacuation of excrement, voiding by stool, &c.<BR>7 The soft aspirate or Visarga, marked by two perpendicular dots (:), and as the substitute of the letters स or र, the termination of various inflections both of nouns and verbs.<BR>8 A division of the sun's course, the southern course.<BR>9 Light, splendour.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जन|विसर्जनं|विसर्ज्जनं
विसर्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Gift, donation.<BR>2 Quitting, relinquishing.<BR>3 Sending, dispatching.<BR>4 Dismissing, sending away.<BR>5 Throwing the image, &c. into holy water, as the concluding rite of the festival of a deity.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ज्जनीय|विसर्जनीय|विसर्जनीयः
विसर्ज्जनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be left, abandoned, given away, &c. (proper or fit to.)<BR>E.<BR>वि, सृज to leave, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जित|विसर्ज्जित
विसर्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Abandoned, left.<BR>2 Given, given away.<BR>2 Dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्प|विसर्पः
विसर्प<BR>m. (-र्पः)<BR>1 Spreading.<BR>2 Going.<BR>3 Going variously.<BR>4 Flying, gliding.<BR>5 Unwished consequence of any act.<BR>6 Erysipelatous inflammation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृप to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पघ्न
विसर्पघ्न<BR>n. (-घ्नं)<BR>Bees wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पण|विसर्पणं
विसर्पण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Spreading, extending.<BR>2 Going gently.<BR>3 Flying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृप to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पत्
विसर्पत्<BR>mfn. (-र्पन्-र्पन्ती-र्पत्)<BR>1 Going, going along.<BR>2 Flying gently.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृप to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पिन्
विसर्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि)<BR>Spreading over or along, gliding, going gently.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृप to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसल|विसलं
विसल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A shoot, a sprout.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, सल to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसार|विसारः
विसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A fish.<BR>2 Going smoothly, creeping, gliding.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Wood, timber.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The region of the winds.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, and घञ् aff., or वि priv., and सार pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारित|विसारितः
विसारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Effected, performed.<BR>2 Set on foot, occasioned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारिन्
विसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Flowing, gliding, creeping.<BR>2 Spreading, diffusing.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>विसार going smoothly, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसिनी
विसिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>विस the fibres of the lotus, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूचिका
विसूचिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Spasmodic cholera.<BR>2 Symptom of a disease.<BR>E.<BR>वि, सूच to apprise, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरण|विसूरणं
विसूरण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Sorrow, distress.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and सूर to hurt, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरित|विसूरितं
विसूरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Repentance.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A fever.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सूर to hurt, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृजत्
विसृजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>1 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>2 Giving, giving away.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृज्य
विसृज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>To be left or abandoned.<BR>ind.<BR>Having dismissed, left, got rid of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत|विसृतं
विसृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spread, extended, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत्वर|विसृत्वरः
विसृत्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Going smoothly, gliding, creeping, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, क्वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृमर|विसृमरः
विसृमर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Creeping, flowing, gliding.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, क्मरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्ट|विसृष्टः
विसृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Expelled, cast off or out.<BR>2 Abandoned, relinquished, got rid of.<BR>3 Given away.<BR>4 Dismissed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृज to let go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्टि|विसृष्टिः
विसृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Leaving, quitting.<BR>2 Giving.<BR>3 Dismissing.<BR>E.<BR>वि away, सृज to leave, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्तृ
विस्कन्तृ<BR>mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>Going, going away, dispersing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ष्कदि to go, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्द
विस्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Going, dispersing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्कदि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्त|विस्तः
विस्त<BR>mn. (-स्तः-स्तं)<BR>A weight of gold, a Karṣa of sixteen Māṣas, about half an ounce troy.<BR>E.<BR>विस to convey, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तर|विस्तरः
विस्तर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 Prolixity, detail.<BR>3 Affection or affectionate solicitation.<BR>4 Number, assemblage.<BR>5 Abundance, quantity.<BR>6 A seat, a stool.<BR>7 A bed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to spread over or cover, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरशस्
विस्तरशस्<BR>ind.<BR>Fully, at length.<BR>E.<BR>विस्तर, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तार|विस्तारः
विस्तार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Spreading, extension, diffusion.<BR>2 Vastness, expanse.<BR>3 Breadth, amplitude.<BR>4 Amplification.<BR>5 Diameter of a circle.<BR>6 The branch of a tree with its new shoots.<BR>7 A shrub.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to cover, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्ण|विस्तीर्णः
विस्तीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Large, great.<BR>2 Spread, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to cover or spread, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्णता
विस्तीर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Diffusion, extension.<BR>2 Vastness.<BR>E.<BR>विस्तीर्ण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विस्तीर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्णपर्ण|विस्तीर्णपर्णं
विस्तीर्णपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>A sort of esculent root, (Arum Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>विस्तीर्ण large, and पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृत|विस्तृतः
विस्तृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spread, diffused, extended.<BR>2 Broad, expanded.<BR>3 Ample.<BR>4 Diffuse.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृति|विस्तृतिः
विस्तृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Spreading, expansion.<BR>2 The diameter of a circle.<BR>3 Breadth.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्द्धमान
विस्पर्द्धमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Emulating, envying.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्पर्द्धं to envy, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पष्ट|विस्पष्टः
विस्पष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Apparent, manifest, open.<BR>2 Plain, intelligible.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्पष्ट apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार|विस्फारः
विस्फार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The twang of a bow string.<BR>2 Trembling, agitation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फर to shake, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फारित|विस्फारितः
विस्फारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>2 Evident, apparent.<BR>3 Twanged or drawn as a bow-string.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फर to tremble, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार्य्यमाण|विस्फार्यमाण
विस्फार्य्यमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Being made open or manifest.<BR>2 Being drawn or twanged as a bow-string.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फर to tremble, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरत्
विस्फुरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Swelling, enlarging.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फुर to swell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरित|विस्फुरितः
विस्फुरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, tremulous.<BR>2 Swollen, enlarged.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फुर to tremble, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलत्
विस्फुलत्<BR>mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती लत्)<BR>1 Going briskly or merrily.<BR>2 Shaking, trembling.<BR>3 Appearing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फुल to shake, &c., and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=794" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलिङ्ग|विस्फुलिंग|विस्फुलिंगः|विस्फुलिङ्गः
विस्फुलिङ्ग^1<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A sort of poison.<BR>2 A spark of fire.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फु imitative sound, लिंग to go, aff. अच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Dhaval Patel on 20151215. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/171. note: Convention error. WIL has 'liNga' as headword and not 'liMga'..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फूर्जथु|विस्फूर्जथुः
विस्फूर्जथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Thunder.<BR>E.<BR>वि, स्फूर्ज्ज to thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फोट|विस्फोटः
विस्फोट<BR>mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>1 Boil, pustule.<BR>2 Small-pox.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्फुट to hurt or break, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मय|विस्मयः
विस्मय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Wonder, surprise, astonishment.<BR>2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>3 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मि to smile, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयाकुल
विस्मयाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bewildered, astounded.<BR>E.<BR>विस्मय, and आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयान्वित|विस्मयान्वितः
विस्मयान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>विस्मय surprise, अन्वित affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयिन्
विस्मयिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>विस्मय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरण|विस्मरणं
विस्मरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Forgetting.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मृ to remember, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरणीय
विस्मरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be forgotten.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., स्मृ to remember, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मर्य्य|विस्मर्य
विस्मर्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>To be forgotten.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मृ to remember, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मापन|विस्मापनः
विस्मापन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Deceit, illusion.<BR>2 A magical or enchanted city, one that appears and disappears unexpectedly, or in unexpected situations, a city of the Gandharbas.<BR>3 KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>4 Astonishing, surprising, causing wonder or surprise.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मि to smile, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मित|विस्मितः
विस्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मि to smile, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृत|विस्मृतः
विस्मृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Forgotten.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and स्मृत remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृति|विस्मृतिः
विस्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Forgetting, forgetfulness.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., and स्मृति recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मेर
विस्मेर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्मि to smile, र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्यन्द
विस्यन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>Flowing, trickling.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ष्यदि to flow, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्र|विस्रं
विस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A smell like that of raw meat.<BR>E.<BR>विस to send, aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंस|विस्रंसः
विस्रंस<BR>mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>1 Relaxation, laxness.<BR>2 Debility, decay.<BR>E.<BR>वि, स्रंस to fall, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंसन
विस्रंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Loosening, unfastening, untying^1.<BR>2 Falling.<BR>3 Flowing, dropping.<BR>4 A laxative, an aperient.<BR>E.<BR>वि separate, स्रंस to fall, ल्युट् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रगन्धि|विस्रगंधि|विस्रगन्धिः
विस्रगन्धि<BR>m. (-न्धिः)<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>E.<BR>विस्र the smell of raw meat, and गन्धि smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रता
विस्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rawness of smell.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to विस्र as above; also with त्व, विस्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रब्ध|विस्रब्धः
विस्रब्ध<BR>mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>1 Trusted, confided in.<BR>2 Placid, tamed, humble.<BR>3 Steady, diligent.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रंभ to trust, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भ|विस्रंभ|विस्रम्भः
विस्रम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 Trust, confidence.<BR>2 Affection, regard, affectionate solicitation.<BR>3 Acquaintance.<BR>4 Killing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रम्भ^1 to trust, aff. घञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भिन्
विस्रम्भिन्<BR>mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>Trusting, confiding in.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रम्भ to trust, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रसा
विस्रसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Decrepitude, the infirmity of old age.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रंस to fall, aff. अङ् and टाप्, and the radical nasal dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रस्त
विस्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Loosened, detached, fallen.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रंस to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावण|विस्रावणं
विस्रावण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Causing to flow.<BR>2 Bleeding.<BR>3 Distilling.<BR>4 A spirit distilled from molasses.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्रु to drop, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावित
विस्रावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Bled.<BR>2 Caused to flow.<BR>E.<BR>वि, स्रु to flow, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्राव्य
विस्राव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be bled, requiring bleeding.<BR>2 To be made to flow.<BR>E.<BR>वि, स्रु to ooze, causal v., यत aff.; also पिस्रावितव्य and विस्रावणीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रुत|विस्रुतः
विस्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spread, stretched.<BR>2 Dropped, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, स्रु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वर|विस्वरः
विस्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Discordant, unharmonious.<BR>E.<BR>वि deprec., स्वर sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वाद
विस्वाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Insipid, flavourless.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., स्वाद flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहग|विहगः
विहग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>5 The moon.<BR>6 A planet.<BR>E.<BR>विह for विहायस् in the sky, and ग who goes; also विहङ्गम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्ग|विहंग|विहंगः|विहङ्गः
विहङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं)<BR>Going swiftly, flying.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>5 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>विह for विहायस् in the air, and ग who goes: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गम|विहंगम|विहंगमः|विहङ्गमः
विहङ्गम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A bird.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A pole or yoke for carrying burthens.<BR>E.<BR>विह for विहायम् in the air, गम to go, aff. खच्, whence the nasal is inserted; also with the final rejected, विहङ्ग, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गराज|विहंगराज|विहंगराजः|विहङ्गराजः
विहङ्गराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>विहङ्ग a bird, and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गिका|विहंगिका
विहङ्गिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of pole or yoke for carrying burthens.<BR>E.<BR>विहङ्ग a bird, and कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत|विहतः
विहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Opposed, impeded, resisted.<BR>2 Hurt, killed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A Bauddha or Jaina temple.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to hurt or kill, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहति|विहतिः
विहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Striking, killing.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A friend or companion.<BR>E.<BR>वि, हन to strike, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहनन|विहननं
विहनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Opposition, obstruction, impediment.<BR>2 Injury, hurting.<BR>3 Killing.<BR>4 A bow for cleaning cotton.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन to kill or hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर|विहरः
विहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Separation, disunion, absence.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to convey, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरण|विहरणं
विहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Taking, taking off or away.<BR>2 Going about for pleasure or exercise.<BR>E.<BR>वि, हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरणीय
विहरणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taken away.<BR>2 To be rambled or sported.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसन|विहसनं
विहसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Laughing gently, smiling.<BR>E.<BR>वि, हस to laugh, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसित|विहसितं
विहसित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A gentle laugh, a smile.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हस to laugh, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्त|विहस्तः
विहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Confounded, perplexed, bewildered.<BR>2 Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>वि without, हस्त a hand, helpless, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा<BR>ind. Aptote noun.<BR>Heaven, paradise.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हा to abandon, Uṇādi aff. आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहापित|विहापितं
विहापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Given.<BR>2 Extorted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हा to abandon, causal form, aff. क्त. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">Page796</a>] giving being considered as the abandonment of the thing given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=795" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहाय|विहायः
विहाय<BR>ind.<BR>Having left or abandoned.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हा to quit, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायत
विहायत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस्
विहायस्<BR>mn. (-याः-यः)<BR>The sky or atmosphere.<BR>m. (-याः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हय to go, causal form, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस|विहायसं|विहायसः
विहायस<BR>mn. (-सः-सं)<BR>Heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A bird.<BR>E.<BR>अच् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायसा
विहायसा<BR>ind.<BR>Heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR>E.<BR>the third case of विहायस् used as an aptote noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहार|विहारः
विहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Walking for pleasure or amusement.<BR>2 Wandering, roaming, going about.<BR>3 A Bauddha or Jaina convent.<BR>4 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>5 The shoulder.<BR>6 A sort of bird.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, aff. घञ्; also वीहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिन्
विहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Taking pleasure or relaxation.<BR>E.<BR>विहार sport, &c., and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहास|विहासः
विहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A gentle laugh or smile.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and हास laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
विहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Placed, deposited.<BR>2 Improper, unsuitable, unfit.<BR>3 Done, acted, made.<BR>4 Appointed, fixed.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, aff. क्त, or वि priv., and हित applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितवत्
विहितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Doing, performing, making.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितागस्
विहितागस्<BR>mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः)<BR>Faulty, offending, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>विहित done, अगस् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिताञ्जलि
विहिताञ्जलि<BR>mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि)<BR>Making a respectful obeisance.<BR>E.<BR>विहित, and अञ्जलि salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित्रिम
विहित्रिम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Done according to rule.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, क्त्रि aff., and मप् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीन|विहीनः
विहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Abandoned, left, deserted, deprived of.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हा to abandon, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत|विहृतं
विहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sported, played.<BR>2 Expanded.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the feminine acts or properties indicating love, hesitation, reluctance (in a female) to avow her feelings to her lover.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृति|विहृतिः
विहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Opening, expansion.<BR>2 Sport, pastime.<BR>E.<BR>वि apart, हृ to convey, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत्य
विहृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having sported.<BR>2 Having or being spread.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to take, ल्यप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठ|विहेठः
विहेठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>Hurting, injury.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हेठ to annoy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठक|विहेठकः
विहेठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An injurer, a reviler, one who inflicts pain or injury on another.<BR>E.<BR>वि, हेठ to annoy, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठन|विहेठनं
विहेठन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Injury, hurting, wounding, killing.<BR>2 Rubbing, grinding.<BR>3 Afflicting, distressing.<BR>4 Pain, sorrow, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हेठ to annoy or hurt, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल|विह्वलः
विह्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Agitated, alarmed, overcome with fear or agitation, beside one's self, unable to restrain one's self.<BR>2 Distressed, afflicted.<BR>3 Fused, liquid.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ह्वल to shake, aff. अच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलता
विह्वलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Agitation, anxiety.<BR>E.<BR>विह्वल, and तल् aff. also with त्व, विह्वलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वेति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To pervade.<BR>3 To conceive, to be impregnated.<BR>4 To desire.<BR>5 To throw or send.<BR>6 To eat.<BR>With सम् prefixed,<BR>To invest, to inclose, to cover or wrap round or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी<BR>m. (-वीः)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 Covering.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक|वीकः
वीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, वि substituted for the root, कन् Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीकाश|वीकाशः
वीकाश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Solitude, privacy.<BR>2 Display, manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before काश to shine, aff. अच्, and the vowel of the prefix long, by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष|वीक्षं|वीक्षः
वीक्ष<BR>mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 Surprise, astonishment.<BR>2 A visible object.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ईक्ष to see, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षण|वीक्षणं
वीक्षण<BR>nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>Sight, seeing.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ईक्ष to see, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणीय
वीक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Visible, perceptible.<BR>E.<BR>वीक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षमाण
वीक्षमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Seeing, looking at.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ईक्ष to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षापन्न|वीक्षापन्नः
वीक्षापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Astonished, surprised.<BR>E.<BR>वीक्ष sight, आपन्न disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षित|वीक्षितं|वीक्षितः
वीक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Seen, beheld.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A look, a glance.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ईक्ष to see, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं|वीक्ष्यः
वीक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Visible, perceptible.<BR>2 Astonishing, wonderful.<BR>ind.<BR>Having seen.<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Wonder, surprise.<BR>2 A visible object.<BR>m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>1 A dancer, an actor.<BR>2 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ईक्ष to see, aff. यत् or ल्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्खा|वींखा
वीङ्खा<BR>f. (-ङ्खा)<BR>1 Going, moving, locomotion, progress, proceeding.<BR>2 Dancing.<BR>3 A particular mode of moving.<BR>4 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>5 One of a horse's paces.<BR>E.<BR>वि before इखि to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचयन
वीचयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Research, enquiry.<BR>E.<BR>वि before चि to collect, ल्युट् aff., and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचि|वीचिः
वीचि<BR>mf. (-चिः-चिः or -ची)<BR>1 A wave.<BR>2 A small or rippling wave.<BR>3 Pleasure, delight, happiness.<BR>4 Leisure, interval, rest.<BR>5 A ray of light.<BR>6 Small, little.<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to weave, Uṇādi aff. ईचि, and the radical vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिमालिन्
वीचिमालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>वीचि a wave, and माला a necklace, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेजयति)<BR>To fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Seed, (of plants, &c.)<BR>2 Cause, origin in general.<BR>3 Semen virile.<BR>4 Receptacle, place of deposit or preparation.<BR>5 Truth, divine truth, as the seed or cause of being.<BR>6 Marrow.<BR>7 Algebra, analysis.<BR>8 The mystical letter or syllable which forms the essential part of the Mantra of any deity.<BR>9 The origin of the business of a drama.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, जन to be born or produced, (from it,) aff. ड, and the vowel made long; or व्येञ् to cover, aff. क्विप्, वी covering, जन to be born, aff. ड; or वि implying possession, ई LAKṢMĪ, or prosperity, जन to be produced (by it), with the same affix: there are other derivations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजक|वीजकः
वीजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजकोश|वीजकोशः
वीजकोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 The seed vessel of the lotus.<BR>2 Any seed vessel.<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A pod, a legume.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and कोश or कोष receptacle; whence also वीजकोष m. (-षः) वीजकोषी f. (-षी) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजगणित
वीजगणित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Algebra.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and गणित calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=796" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजगुप्ति|वीजगुप्तिः
वीजगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>A legume, a pod.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, गुप्ति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजतस्
वीजतस्<BR>ind.<BR>From or according to the seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजन|वीजनं|वीजनः
वीजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A fan.<BR>2 Thing, substance.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A sort of pheasant.<BR>2 The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपुष्प|वीजपुष्पं
वीजपुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Common citron.<BR>2 A thorny plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वीज a seed, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपुष्पिका
वीजपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus sorghum.)<BR>E.<BR>वीज a seed, पुष्प a flower, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपूर|वीजपूरः
वीजपूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Common citron or a variety, (Citrus medica.)<BR>E.<BR>वीज a seed, and पूर what is full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपूर्ण|वीजपूर्णः
वीजपूर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>Common citron, or according to some authorities, a large kind of lime.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and पूर्ण filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजप्रद
वीजप्रद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Sowing seed, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Generating, or a generator.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and पद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजप्ररोह
वीजप्ररोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Growing from seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and प्ररोह growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजमातृका
वीजमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The pericarp or seed-vessel of the lotus.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and मातृका parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजरुह|वीजरुहः
वीजरुह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Growing from seed.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Grain, corn.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवत्|वीजवन्त्
वीजवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Who or what has seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवर
वीजवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and वर what screens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजसू
वीजसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, and सू parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजा
वीजा<BR>ind.<BR>By or with seed, sowing with seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and डाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजाकृत|वीजाकृतं
वीजाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ploughed or harrowed after sowing, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वीज a seed, and कृत made, with डाच् added to the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजित
वीजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sown with, having for seed.<BR>2 Fanned.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and इतच् aff. or वीज to fan, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिन्
वीजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Having seed, origin, &c.<BR>m. (-जी)<BR>A father, a progenitor.<BR>E.<BR>वीज semen, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजोत्कृष्ट
वीजोत्कृष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Good seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज, and उत्कृष्ट excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजोदक|वीजोदकं
वीजोदक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>वीज origin or original, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्य|वीज्यः
वीज्य<BR>mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>1 Sprung from some family.<BR>2 Sprung from seed.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed or origin, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्यमान
वीज्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Fanned.<BR>E.<BR>वीज to fan, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटिका
वीटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The betel plant, (Piper betel.)<BR>2 The preparation of the Areca nut with spices and chunam, and enveloped in the leaf of the Piper betel, Betel, Paun.<BR>3 A tye, a fastening.<BR>E.<BR>वि before इट् to go, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form; also वीटि or वीटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणा
वीणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The Vīṇā, or Indian lute, a fretted instrument of the guitar kind, usually having seven wires or strings, and a large gourd at each end of the finger board; the extent of the instrument is two octaves: it is supposed to be the invention of NĀRADA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and has many varieties, enumerated according to the number of strings, &c.<BR>2 Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, &c., Uṇādi aff. न, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणादण्ड|वीणादंड|वीणादण्डः
वीणादण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The neck of a Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>वीणा a lute, and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणानुवन्ध
वीणानुवन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>The tie of a lute or lower part of the tail piece, where the wires are fixed.<BR>E.<BR>वीणा the lute, and अनुवन्ध appendage, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणावाद|वीणावादः
वीणावाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A player on the Vīṇā, a lutanist.<BR>E.<BR>वीणा a lute, and वाद who causes to speak or sound; also with कन added, वीणावादक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणास्य|वीणास्यः
वीणास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>NĀRADA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and inventor of the Vīṇā or lute.<BR>E.<BR>वीणा, and आस्य the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतंस|वीतंसः
वीतंस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A cage, a chain or net, &c. for confining birds or beasts.<BR>2 An enclosure for tranquillising or taming them, an aviary, a menagerie.<BR>3 A place for keeping game, a preserve.<BR>E.<BR>वि before तसि to adorn, aff. घञ्, and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
वीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, departed.<BR>2 Exempt or freed from.<BR>3 Loosed, let go, unbound.<BR>4 Tranquil, quiet, tame.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A horse or elephant, untrained to or unfit for war.<BR>2 Goading an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतकल्मष
वीतकल्मष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Free from sin or soil.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतकाम
वीतकाम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतदम्भ|वीतदम्भः
वीतदम्भ<BR>mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं)<BR>Humble, lowly, not proud.<BR>E.<BR>वीत gone, दम्भ pride, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतन|वीतनः
वीतन<BR>mfn. (-नौ)<BR>The sides or cartilages of the larynx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतभय|वीतभयः
वीतभय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fearless, undaunted.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and भष fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतराग|वीतरागः
वीतराग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Exempt from passions or affections.<BR>2 Bleached, colourless.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Any sage with subdued passions.<BR>2 A Bauddha deified sage.<BR>E.<BR>वीत gone, and राग passion, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतविरुद्धबुद्धि
वीतविरुद्धबुद्धि<BR>mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>Peaceable, without hostile intentions.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, विरुद्ध opposed, and वुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशङ्क
वीतशङ्क<BR>mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>Fearless.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and शङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशोक|वीतशोकः
वीतशोक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Free from care or sorrow.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Aśoka tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>E.<BR>वीत gone, and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतस्पृह
वीतस्पृह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Free from desire.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीति|वीतिः
वीति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Going, moving, motion.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>3 Engendering, producing.<BR>4 Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>5 Light, lustre.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिहोत्र|वीतिहोत्रः
वीतिहोत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 AGNI or fire.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>वीति a horse. होत्र clarified butter, the usual offering or oblation with fire; also वीतिहोत्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतोत्तर
वीतोत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Unable or disinclined to reply, having no answer.<BR>E.<BR>वीत, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथि|वीथिः
वीथि<BR>f. (-थिः or -थी)<BR>1 A road.<BR>2 A row, a line.<BR>3 A terrace in front of a house.<BR>4 A stall, a shop.<BR>5 A sort of drama, in one act, and by one or by two performers, the dramatic narration of an amatory story or intrigue.<BR>E.<BR>विथ to ask or beg, aff. इन्, and the vowel made long; also ङीष् optionally added, and with कन् aff., fem. form, वीथिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=797" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथ्यङ्ग|वीथ्यङ्गः
वीथ्यङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Dialogue, &c. suited to, and constituting the dramatic entertainment called Vīthi, though employed in other kinds, as quibble, equivoque, jest, abuse, and the like.<BR>E.<BR>वीथि, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्र|वीध्रं|वीध्रः
वीध्र<BR>mfn. (-ध्रः-ध्रा-ध्रं)<BR>Clean, clear, pure.<BR>E.<BR>वि before इन्ध to shine, Uṇādi aff. रक, and the first consonant rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाह|वीनाहः
वीनाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The top or cover of a well.<BR>E.<BR>वि before नह to bind, aff. घञ्; also विनाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीपा
वीपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीप्सा
वीप्सा<BR>f. (-प्सा)<BR>Several or successive order, the arrangement of things or properties each by each, or in succession, as वृक्षं वृक्षं सिञ्चति he waters tree after tree.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अप to go, or get, desiderative form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीबुकोश|वीबुकोशः
वीबुकोश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A Cowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीभ
वीभ<BR>(ऋ) वीभृ r. 1st cl. (वीभते)<BR>To praise; also read चीभृ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर<BR>r. 10th cl. (वीरयति)<BR>To be powerful or valiant, to make heroic or irresistible effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Excellent, eminent, (used chiefly in composition.)<BR>2 Heroic.<BR>3 Powerful, mighty.<BR>4 Strong, robust.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hero, a warrior, a champion.<BR>2 Heroism, the heroic Rasa or feeling, as an object of poetical description especially.<BR>3 The last Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present æra.<BR>4 An actor, a mime.<BR>5 A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>6 Fire.<BR>7 Sacrificial fire.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A matron, a wife and mother.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly Murā.<BR>3 A medicinal root, commonly Kṣīrakākolī.<BR>4 A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>5 A drug, (Elavāluka.)<BR>6 Plaintain tree.<BR>7 A sort of Asclepias, (A. rosea.)<BR>8 Opposite-leaved fig tree.<BR>9 A sort of Convolvulus, (C. paniculatus, the white and dark kinds.)<BR>10 A small tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>11 Spirituous liquor or a particular kind of it.<BR>12 The aloe.<BR>13 A plant, commonly Atis.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A reed, (Arundo tibialis.)<BR>2 The root of the ginger plant. (?)<BR>3 Pepper.<BR>4 Rice-gruel.<BR>5 The root of the Costus speciosus.<BR>6 The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>अज to go, and वी substituted for the root, रक् Uṇādi aff., or वीर to be powerful, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरजयन्तिका|वीरजयंतिका
वीरजयन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A war-dance, a dance performed by soldiers after a victory or on going to battle.<BR>2 War, battle.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, जि to conquer, झच् aff., fem. form, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरण|वीरणं
वीरण<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A side glance, a leer.<BR>3 A deep place.<BR>E.<BR>वि a bird, ईर to go, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतर|वीरतरं|वीरतरः
वीरतर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A distinguished hero.<BR>3 A corpse. (?)<BR>E.<BR>वीर powerful, तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतरु|वीरतरुः
वीरतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 A large tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna, Rox.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Barleria longifolia, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and तरु the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरता
वीरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Heroism.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to वीर; also with त्व aff. वीरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरधन्वन्
वीरधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरन्धर|वीरंधर|वीरंधरः
वीरन्धर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 Fighting with wild beasts.<BR>3 A leather cuirass or jacket.<BR>4 The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, धृ to hold, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपत्नी
वीरपत्नी<BR>f. (-त्नी)<BR>The wife of a hero.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and पत्नी the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपाण
वीरपाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The drink of warriors, taken during the battle for refreshment, or before it, to elevate courage.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and पान drink; the न is optionally changed, whence it also occurs वीरपान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभद्र|वीरभद्रः
वीरभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>1 A horse fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>2 A distinguished hero.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, &c. वीरण.<BR>4 One of ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR>5 One of the Rudras.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभद्रक|वीरभद्रकं
वीरभद्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभार्य्या|वीरभार्या
वीरभार्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>The wife of a hero.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and भार्य्या a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमातृ
वीरमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The mother of a hero.<BR>E.<BR>वीर, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमुद्रिका
वीरमुद्रिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>An ornament or ring worn on the middle toe.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, मुद्रा a seal, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीररेणु|वीररेणुः
वीररेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>E.<BR>त्रीर a hero, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवत्|वीरवन्त्
वीरवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having a champion or hero.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A woman whose husband is living.<BR>E.<BR>वीर, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवत्सा
वीरवत्सा<BR>f. (-त्सा)<BR>The mother of a hero.<BR>E.<BR>वीर, and वत्स the child, (of whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरविप्लावक|वीरविप्लावकः
वीरविप्लावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman, who performs his oblations with money, procured from the lower or Śūdra tribe.<BR>E.<BR>वीर sacrificial fire, वि before प्लु to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवृक्ष|वीरवृक्षः
वीरवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>1 The marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>2 A large tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>3 A sort of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus sorghum.)<BR>E.<BR>वीर strong or a hero, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसू
वीरसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>1 The mother of a hero.<BR>2 The mother of a male child.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेन|वीरसेनं|वीरसेनः
वीरसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The father of NALA Rāja.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and सेना a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेनज|वीरसेनजः
वीरसेनज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>NALA, a prince and hero of several celebrated poems, as the Naiṣadha, Nalodaya, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वीरसेन the father of the prince, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसैन्य
वीरसैन्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरस्कन्ध|वीरस्कंध|वीरस्कन्धः
वीरस्कन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A buffalo.<BR>E.<BR>वीर powerful, स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहन्
वीरहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>A Brahman, who has suffered the sacred domestic fire to become extinct, either from carelessness, impiety, or absence.<BR>E.<BR>वीर sacrificial fire, and हन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराशंसन|वीराशंसनं
वीराशंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 The post of danger, the place in battle which is most perilous and exposed.<BR>2 Keeping watch.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, आङ् before शसि to wish, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरासन|वीरासनं
वीरासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sleeping out in the open air, a bivouac.<BR>2 A field of battle.<BR>3 A kneeling posture.<BR>E.<BR>वीर, and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुध्
वीरुध्<BR>f. (-रुट् or -रुत्)<BR>1 A creeper or spreading creeper.<BR>2 A branch and shoot.<BR>E.<BR>वि before रुध to impede, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix made long; also टाप् being added, वीरुधा f. (-धा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरेश्वर|वीरेश्वरः
वीरेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 VĪRABHADRA, one of ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR>2 A great hero.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and ईश्वर lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=798" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोञ्झ
वीरोञ्झ<BR>m. (-ञ्झः)<BR>A Brahman, who omits offering burnt offerings or neglects his sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>वीर fire, उञ्झ to abandon, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोपजीविक|वीरोपजीविकः
वीरोपजीविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman, who claims alms or presents, on the merit of having preserved his sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>वीर sacrificial fire, and उपजीविक living by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्य|वीर्य|वीर्यं|वीर्य्यं
वीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Strength, vigour, power.<BR>2 Dignity, consequence.<BR>3 Fortitude, firmness.<BR>4 Semen virile.<BR>5 Splendour, lustre.<BR>6 Heroism, valour.<BR>7 Seed, (of plants, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वीर a hero, and यत् aff., or वीर to be strong, and अच् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यवत्|वीर्यवत्|वीर्यवन्त्
वीर्य्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Strong, stout, robust.<BR>2 Overcoming, victorious.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य strength, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यविरहित|वीर्यविरहित
वीर्य्यविरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Devoid of prowess or vigour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and विरहित deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यविशिष्ट|वीर्यविशिष्ट
वीर्य्यविशिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Possessed of courage, vigour, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and विशिष्ट endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यहानि|वीर्यहानि
वीर्य्यहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>1 Loss of vigour or courage.<BR>2 Impotence.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and हानि loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यहीन|वीर्यहीन
वीर्य्यहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Seedless.<BR>2 Cowardly.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यावदान|वीर्यावदान
वीर्य्यावदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Effecting any thing by prowess.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and अवदान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यावधूत|वीर्यावधूत
वीर्य्यावधूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Overcome or surpassed in prowess.<BR>E.<BR>वीर्य्य, and अवधूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवध|वीवधः
वीवध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A yoke for carrying burthens.<BR>2 A burthen.<BR>2 Storing or heaping corn.<BR>4 A road: see विवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवधिक|वीवधिकः
वीवधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की)<BR>1 A chandler.<BR>2 A man or woman carrying a load by means of a yoke.<BR>E.<BR>वीवध as above, ठन् aff., and the first vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीहार|वीहारः
वीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A holy place, a temple, a sanctuary, but especially a Jaina or Bauddha convent.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हृ to convey, aff. घञ्; also विहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुग
वुग<BR>(इ) वुगि r. 1st cl. (वुंगति)<BR>To except, to leave, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुट
वुट<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वोटयति)<BR>To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुध
वुध<BR>(इ) बुधि r. 10th cl. (वुन्धयति)<BR>To injure, to hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुस
वुस<BR>r. 4th cl. (वुस्यति)<BR>To throw or cast off; also बुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूष
वूष<BR>r. 10th cl. (वूषयति)<BR>To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ<BR>(ड,) वृङ् r. 9th cl. (वृणीते)<BR>To serve, to do homage or worship, to conciliate by service or adoration.<BR>(ञ) वृञ् r. 1st cl. (वरति-ते) r. 5th cl. (वृणोति वृणुते) r. 10th cl. (वारयति-ते)<BR>1 To choose, to select, to prepare.<BR>2 To appoint, to invite.<BR>3 To screen, to invest, to cover.<BR>With अप prefixed,<BR>To cover, to screen, to shield or defend.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>To inclose, to cover, to surround.<BR>With नि or निर्,<BR>To cease, to refrain from, to finish or end.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To surround.<BR>2 To depend upon.<BR>With वि,<BR>To become evident or apparent, to open or appear.<BR>With सम्,<BR>To conceal.<BR>With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To wrap up, to involve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहण|वृंहणः
वृंहण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा or -णी-णं)<BR>Nourishing, fattening, nutritious.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of sweetmeat made of sugar, milk, spices, &c. fried in Ghee, and powdered with coarse sugar or treacle.<BR>E.<BR>वृहि to increase, and ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहणीय
वृंहणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be nourished, what ought to or may be.<BR>E.<BR>वृहि to grow, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहित|वृंहितं
वृंहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Grown, increased.<BR>2 Cherished, nourished.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The roar of elephants.<BR>E.<BR>वृहि to grow or increase, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक|वृकः
वृक<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्कते)<BR>To take or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक|वृकः
वृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wolf.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>3 The Vakapushpa tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>4 A Shakal.<BR>5 Turpentine.<BR>6 Compounded perfume.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>वृक to take, aff. क, or वृ to hide or screen, Uṇādi aff. कक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकदंश|वृकदंशः
वृकदंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वृक a wolf, and दंश who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकधूप|वृकधूपः
वृकधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Compounded perfume.<BR>2 Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>वृक the same meanings, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकाराति|वृकारातिः
वृकाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वृक a wolf, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकारि|वृकारिः
वृकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>वृक a wolf, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकोदर|वृकोदरः
वृकोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 Name of BHĪMA.<BR>E.<BR>वृक a wolf, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ण|वृक्णं
वृक्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्णः-क्णा-क्णं)<BR>Cut, divided, broken.<BR>E.<BR>व्रश्च to cut, aff. क्त, form irr.; also read वृक्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्णवत्
वृक्णवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Cutting, severing.<BR>E.<BR>व्रश्च to cut, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष|वृक्षः
वृक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (वृक्षते)<BR>1 To appoint.<BR>2 To cover.<BR>3 To take or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष|वृक्षः
वृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A tree in general.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष to cover, (to shade,) aff. घञ् or व्रश्च to cut, and स Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षक|वृक्षकः
वृक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A small tree, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>2 Any tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षकुक्कुट|वृक्षकुक्कुटः
वृक्षकुक्कुट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A wild cock.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षखण्ड|वृक्षखंड
वृक्षखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A grove.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षचर|वृक्षचरः
वृक्षचर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Going or living in trees.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A monkey.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, or any other synonym, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षछाया|वृक्षच्छाया
वृक्षछाया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The shade of a single tree.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The shade of many trees, or a grove.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and छाया shade; in the second sense, it takes the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षतल
वृक्षतल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The foot of a tree or ground about it.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षधूप|वृक्षधूपः
वृक्षधूप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनाथ|वृक्षनाथः
वृक्षनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनिर्य्यास|वृक्षनिर्यास|वृक्षनिर्यासः
वृक्षनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Gum, resin.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनिवास
वृक्षनिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Dwelling or living in a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षपाक|वृक्षपाकः
वृक्षपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and पाक what ripens or perfects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभवन|वृक्षभवनं
वृक्षभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A hollow in a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and भवन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभिद्
वृक्षभिद्<BR>f. (-भिद् or -भित्)<BR>An axe.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and भिद् breaking, cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभेदिन्
वृक्षभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A carpenter's chisel.<BR>2 A hatchet.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and भेदिन् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमय
वृक्षमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Abounding with trees.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमर्कटिका
वृक्षमर्कटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A squirrel.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, मर्कट a monkey, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमृद्भू
वृक्षमृद्भू<BR>m. (-द्भूः)<BR>A sort of cane or reed, (Calamus fascicularis.)<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, मृद् earth, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=799" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षरुह
वृक्षरुह<BR>mf. (-हः-हा)<BR>A parasite plant, (Cymbidum tessalloides, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and रुह growing, having its roots attached to the trunk or branches of another plant or tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षरोपण
वृक्षरोपण<BR>n. (-ण)<BR>Planting trees.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and रोपण planting; also वृक्षारोपण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षवाटिका
वृक्षवाटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A garden, a grove, one belonging to the residence of a minister of state, a courtezan, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and वाटिका or वाटी an enclosure; hence also वृक्षवाटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षश|वृक्षशः
वृक्षश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and शी to sleep, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षशायिका
वृक्षशायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A squirrel.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, शी to sleep, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षस्थ
वृक्षस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>What is or stays in or on a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and स्थ who or what stays, also वृक्षस्थायिन्, वृक्षस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाग्र
वृक्षाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाङ्घ्रि|वृक्षाङ्घ्रिः
वृक्षाङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>The root of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and अङ्घ्रि foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षादन|वृक्षादनः
वृक्षादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A carpenter's chisel or adze.<BR>2 A hatchet, a chopper.<BR>3 The Indian fig tree.<BR>4 The Piyāl tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A parasite plant, (Epidendron.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, अदन eating or food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षादिरुहक|वृक्षादिरुहकं
वृक्षादिरुहक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Embracing.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्षादि trees, &c., रुह ascended, and कन् aff. of comparison; entwining as a creeper round a tree, &c.; also derived from रुह with क्त aff. वृक्षादिरूढ n. (-ढं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाम्ल|वृक्षाम्लं|वृक्षाम्लः
वृक्षाम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>n. (-म्लं)<BR>Acid seasoning, or the fruit of the tamarind so used.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षारोपक|वृक्षारोपकः
वृक्षारोपक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A planter of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and आरोपक who plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षारोपण
वृक्षारोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Planting trees.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and आरोपण planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षालय|वृक्षालयः
वृक्षालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bird in general.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षावास|वृक्षावासः
वृक्षावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 An ascetic, one who lives in the hollows of trees.<BR>2 A bird.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षोत्थ
वृक्षोत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>Growing on or borne by a tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष, and उत्थ what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षोत्पल|वृक्षोत्पलः
वृक्षोत्पल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large handsome tree, commonly Kaniyar or Karṇikāra, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree, and उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृच
वृच<BR>(ई) वृची r. 7th cl. (वृणक्ति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To quit, to abandon, to shun or avoid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृज
वृज<BR>(ई) वृजी r. 1st cl. (वर्जति) 2nd cl. (वृक्ते) 7th cl. (वृणक्ति) 10th cl. (वर्ज्जयति)<BR>1 To quit, to shun, to avoid, to except, to abandon.<BR>2 (In the 7th cl.) To cover.<BR>With अप,<BR>To relinquish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजन|वृजनं|वृजनः
वृजन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Crooked.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sin.<BR>2 Sky, atmosphere.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Hair.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, &c., Uṇādi aff. क्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजि|वृजिः
वृजि<BR>f. (-जिः)<BR>A country, probably that to the west of Dehli and Agra, or the modern Bruj.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to quit, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिक
वृजिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of the district of Vrij or Bruj, (as a dialect, a native, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वृजि as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिन|वृजिनं|वृजिनः
वृजिन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Crooked, bent, curved.<BR>2 Wicked.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sin, vice, wickedness.<BR>2 Red leather.<BR>3 Distress, affliction.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Hair.<BR>E.<BR>वृज to cover, Uṇādi aff. इनच्. and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण
वृण<BR>r. 6th cl. (वृणति)<BR>To please, to gratify.<BR>(उ) (वृणु) r. 8th cl. (वृणोति)<BR>To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वत्
वृण्वत्<BR>mfn. (-ण्वन्-ण्वती-ण्वत्)<BR>Choosing, electing, preferring, (especially as a husband or wife.)<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वाण
वृण्वाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Choosing.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, शानच् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत|वृतः
वृत<BR>(उ) वृतु r. 1st cl. (वर्त्तते)<BR>To be, to exist, to stay, to stand, to be fixed or stable.<BR>r. 4th cl. (वृत्यते)<BR>1 To choose, to select or appoint.<BR>2 To serve.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्त्तयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>With अति prefixed,<BR>1 To surpass or overcome.<BR>2 To pass over or beyond.<BR>3 To transgress.<BR>With अनु,<BR>1 To follow, to imitate.<BR>2 To proceed.<BR>With अप,<BR>To turn back or round.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>1 To turn round, to revolve.<BR>2 To do repeatedly.<BR>With नि,<BR>To make artificially.<BR>With नि or निर्,<BR>To stop, to cease, to complete or terminate.<BR>With परि,<BR>1 To surround.<BR>2 To exchange.<BR>3 To excel, to be pre-eminent.<BR>4 To advance.<BR>5 To retreat or return.<BR>6 To turn round.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To engage in any active pursuit.<BR>With प्रति and नि,<BR>To go away, to depart.<BR>With वि,<BR>1 To roll, to whirl, to turn round.<BR>2 To revolve.<BR>With वि and नि,<BR>To return.<BR>With वि and परि,<BR>To revolve, (in the mind.)<BR>With सम and अभि,<BR>To leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत|वृतः
वृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Chosen, selected, preferred.<BR>2 Agreed or assented to.<BR>3 Served.<BR>4 Covered, screened, defended.<BR>5 Affected by.<BR>6 Vitiated, spoiled.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to prefer, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृति|वृतिः
वृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Selecting, choosing, preferring, appointing.<BR>2 Soliciting, asking, requesting.<BR>3 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>4 An enclosure, a place enclosed for particular cultivation, and especially that of the Piper betel, which in many parts of India is surrounded and screened by mats.<BR>5 Hiding, secreting.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिङ्कर|वृतिंकर|वृतिंकरः|वृतिङ्करः
वृतिङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वृति surrounding, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त|वृत्तं|वृत्तः
वृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Chosen, selected, appointed.<BR>2 Done, performed, engaged in or undertaken.<BR>3 Past, gone, been.<BR>4 Over, finished.<BR>5 Dead, deceased.<BR>6 Read, studied, read through.<BR>7 Covered.<BR>8 Round.<BR>9 Firm, hard.<BR>10 Unobstructed, unimpaired.<BR>11 Famous, celebrated.<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>1 Verse, metre.<BR>2 Conduct, observance of enjoined practice in private or social life.<BR>3 Practice, profession, means of gaining a subsistence.<BR>4 Procedure, event, occurrence.<BR>5 A circle.<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A tortoise.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तखण्ड|वृत्तखण्डः
वृत्तखण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Sector or segment of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and खण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तज्ञ
वृत्तज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Who or what knows men's actions.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ततस्
वृत्ततस्<BR>ind.<BR>In or relating to observance or duty, by caste or duty, not implying agency; as वृत्ततः पापं "by or according to caste, a sin".<BR>E.<BR>तसि substituted for the termination of the third case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तपुष्प|वृत्तपुष्पः
वृत्तपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त round, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तफल|वृत्तफलं|वृत्तफलः
वृत्तफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त round, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=800" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तवत्|वृत्तवन्त्
वृत्तवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Discharging the duties of caste or calling, correct, well-conducted.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तसम्पन्न|वृत्तसंपन्न
वृत्तसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Well-behaved or conducted, behaving with propriety.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त duty, and सम्पन्न perfect in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तसादिन्
वृत्तसादिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Worthless, mean, vile.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and षद to go (from), घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तस्थ|वृत्तस्थः
वृत्तस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Discharging the duties of caste or calling.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त established practice, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ताध्ययनर्द्धि
वृत्ताध्ययनर्द्धि<BR>f. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>Holiness, sanctity, resulting from observance of the rules of life and study of scripture.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त conduct, अध्ययन study, and ऋद्धि^1 prosperity, increase.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161130. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 301. note: The 'r' is print error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुवर्त्तिन्|वृत्तानुवर्तिन्
वृत्तानुवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>Obedient, conforming to rule.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, अनु according to, वर्त्तिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुसार|वृत्तानुसारः
वृत्तानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Conforming to prescribed practice.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुसारिन्
वृत्तानुसारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Conforming to established rule or practice, doing what is enjoined or proper.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्तानुसार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तान्त|वृत्तांत|वृत्तान्तः
वृत्तान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 Tidings, rumor, intelligence.<BR>2 Sort, kind, difference.<BR>3 Mode, manner.<BR>4 Whole.<BR>5 Interval, rest, leisure, opportunity.<BR>6 Topic, subject.<BR>7 A tale, a story.<BR>8 Property, nature.<BR>9 Alone, solitary.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त observance, &c., and अन्त, end, term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ति|वृत्तिः
वृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Livelihood, profession, means of acquiring subsistence.<BR>2 Style or character of dramatic representation, or composition, considered to be of four sorts, or Kauśikī, which exhibits love or passion; Bhāratī, which appears to implies declamation especially; Sātvatī, of which the subject is virtue and heroism; and Ārabhaṭī, which treats of magic, delusion, wrath, and battle.<BR>3 Style in general.<BR>4 Gloss, comment, explanation, exposition.<BR>5 Being, abiding, staying.<BR>6 Seizing, stopping, withholding, restraining.<BR>7 Circumference of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिकर्षित
वृत्तिकर्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Attracted by or impelled to for the sake of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and कर्षित attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिता
वृत्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 State of existence.<BR>2 Profession, subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, वृत्तित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिदान
वृत्तिदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving maintenance, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिमत्|वृत्तिमन्त्
वृत्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Abiding, stationary.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिहेतु|वृत्तिहेतुः
वृत्तिहेतु<BR>f. (-तुः)<BR>Cause or means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तौजस्
वृत्तौजस्<BR>mfn. (-जाः-जा-जः)<BR>Mighty, irresistible.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्त, and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्य
वृत्त्य<BR>mfn. (-त्त्यः-त्त्या-त्त्यं)<BR>1 To be chosen, preferable, eligible.<BR>2 Excellent, eminent.<BR>3 To be abided or stayed.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to select, aff. क्यप् or वृञ् with the same aff., and तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्यर्थम्
वृत्त्यर्थम्<BR>ind.<BR>For the sake of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and अर्थम् for the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्यनुप्रास|वृत्त्यनुप्रासः
वृत्त्यनुप्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Alliteration suited to any style or expression.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and अनुप्रास alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्युपाय|वृत्त्युपायः
वृत्त्युपाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Means of subsistence.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्ति, and उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्र|वृत्रः
वृत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 Darkness.<BR>3 A demon slain by INDRA.<BR>4 A cloud.<BR>5 A name of INDRA.<BR>6 The name of a mountain.<BR>7 Sound, noise.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to be or abide, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रद्विष्
वृत्रद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्र the demon, and द्विष् the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रभोजन|वृत्रभोजनः
वृत्रभोजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A kind of potherb, described by some as a sort of cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>वृच INDRA, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रहन्
वृत्रहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्र a demon, and हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रारि|वृत्रारिः
वृत्रारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृत्र a demon, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथा
वृथा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Useless, fruitless.<BR>2 Wrong, incorrect.<BR>3 In vain.<BR>4 Compounded with articles of food, it implies they are hot.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, &c., aff. थाक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाकथा
वृथाकथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>Idle talk.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाघात
वृथाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Striking or killing any being unnecessarily.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाट्या
वृथाट्या<BR>f. (-त्टा)<BR>Going about or travelling for pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and अट्या roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथादान|वृथादानं
वृथादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Unprofitable donation, gift to encomiasts, harlots, wrestlers, money lost at play, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा vain, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथापशुघ्न
वृथापशुघ्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The slayer of an animal except for sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and पशु an animal, घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथालम्भ|वृथालम्भः
वृथालम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>Cutting or plucking unnecessarily.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and लभि to get, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथोत्पन्न
वृथोत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Born or produced in vain.<BR>E.<BR>वृथा, and उत्यन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध|वृद्धं|वृद्धः
वृद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Old, aged, ancient.<BR>2 Full grown, large, expanded to the proper size.<BR>3 Wise, learned.<BR>4 Heaped, accumulated.<BR>5 Increased, augmented.<BR>m. (-द्धः)<BR>1 An old man, or one past seventy.<BR>2 A sage, a saint.<BR>f. (-द्धा)<BR>An old woman, either one past child-bearing, or one with grey hair.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>Benzoin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase or grow, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धकाक|वृद्धकाकः
वृद्धकाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of crow or raven.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old or large, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धत्व|वृद्धत्वं
वृद्धत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, and त्व aff. of the abstract; also वृद्धता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धदारक|वृद्धदारकः
वृद्धदारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A climbing plant (Lettsomia neryosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, and दारक tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धनाभि|वृद्धनाभिः
वृद्धनाभि<BR>mfn. (-भिः-भिः-भी-भि)<BR>Pot-bellied, corpulent.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध large, and नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रपितामह|वृद्धप्रपितामहः
वृद्धप्रपितामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A paternal great greatgrandfather.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A paternal great greatgrandmother.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, प्रपितामह great grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रमातामह|वृद्धप्रमातामहः
वृद्धप्रमातामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A maternal great greatgrandfather.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A maternal great greatgrandmother.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध, and प्रमातामह maternal greatgrandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धभाव|वृद्धभावः
वृद्धभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धराज|वृद्धराजः
वृद्धराज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of dock or sorrel: see अम्लबेतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धवाहन|वृद्धवाहनः
वृद्धवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध large, and वाहन vehicle or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धविभीतक|वृद्धविभीतकः
वृद्धविभीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old or large, विभीतक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धश्रवस्
वृद्धश्रवस्<BR>m. (-वाः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध aged, and श्रवस् hearing; who listens to the old or wise; or वृद्ध large, and श्रवस् the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=801" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसंघ
वृद्धसंघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>An assembly of old men, a council or meeting of elders.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध an elder, and संघ assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसूत्रक|वृद्धसूत्रकं
वृद्धसूत्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Flocculent seeds flying in the air.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, and सूत्र thread, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसेवा
वृद्धसेवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Reverence for old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाङ्गुलि|वृद्धांगुलि|वृद्धाङ्गुलिः
वृद्धाङ्गुलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>The thumb.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध large, and अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धारण्य
वृद्धारण्य<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>A place where the Purāṇas, or other sacred works are read and expounded.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध a Paṇḍita, a scholar, and अरण्य a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धावस्था
वृद्धावस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>The condition or period of old age.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध, and अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाश्रम
वृद्धाश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Roaming, travelling, wandering about.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध, and आश्रम order or state of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धि|वृद्धिः
वृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Increase, augmentation in general, as in bulk, consequence, wealth, &c.<BR>2 The third of the three conditions or objects of regal power, extension of power or revenue, or any indication of progression.<BR>3 Rise, ascending, mounting.<BR>4 Prosperity, success.<BR>5 One of the eight principal drugs or medical roots, described as mild and cooling, sweet and bitter, &c., as a remedy for phlegm, leprosy and worms.<BR>6 The eleventh of the astronomical Yogas, or Yoga star of the 11th lunar mansion.<BR>7 A particular period or division of time.<BR>8 The increase of the digits of the sun or moon.<BR>9 Enlargement of the scrotum, either from swelled testicle or hydrocele or other morbid affections.<BR>10 Interest, usury, especially returning the principal, (as in the case of seed corn lent,) with a proportionate increment.<BR>11 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>12 A heap, a quantity, assemblage, multitude.<BR>13 Wealth, property.<BR>14 Cutting off, abscission.<BR>15 (In law,) Forfeiture, deduction.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, aff. कि, or in the two last senses वर्द्ध to cut, aff. कि, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिकर
वृद्धिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Yielding or causing increase, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिका
वृद्धिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of drug: see वृद्धि.<BR>E.<BR>कब् added to वृद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिजीविका
वृद्धिजीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The profession of usury.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि usury, and जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिपत्र
वृद्धिपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A kind of razor or lancet.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि, and पत्र blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिमत्|वृद्धिमन्त्
वृद्धिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Augmented, increased.<BR>2 Rich.<BR>3 Prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिश्राद्ध|वृद्धिश्राद्धं
वृद्धिश्राद्ध<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>A Śrāddha or sacrifice to progenitors on any prosperous occasion, as the birth of a son, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि, and श्राद्ध ceremony so termed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धोक्ष|वृद्धोक्षः
वृद्धोक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An old bull.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्ध old, and उक्ष a bull or ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध्याजीव|वृद्ध्याजीवः
वृद्ध्याजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A usurer.<BR>E.<BR>वृद्धि usury, and आजीव who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध
वृध<BR>(उ,) वृधु r. 1st cl. (वर्द्धते)<BR>To increase or grow.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्द्धयति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसान|वृधसानः
वृधसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A man.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to grow or increase, aff. असानच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसानु|वृधसानुः
वृधसानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>1 A man.<BR>2 A leaf.<BR>3 Act, action.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to increase, असानु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्न
वृध्न<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>Bubo in the groin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्य|वृध्यं
वृध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>To be increased or augmented.<BR>E.<BR>वृध to grow, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्त|वृंत|वृंतं|वृन्तं
वृन्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>1 The footstalk of a leaf or fruit.<BR>2 The nipple.<BR>3 The stand of a water jar.<BR>E.<BR>वृञ् to choose, क्त aff., and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्ताक|वृंताक|वृंताकः|वृन्ताकः
वृन्ताक<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>वृन्त footstalk, and अक to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्तिता
वृन्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>E.<BR>वृन्त a stalk, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्द|वृंद|वृन्दं|वृन्दः
वृन्द<BR>mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>All, many.<BR>n. (-न्दं)<BR>A heap, a multitude, a quantity, an aggregation.<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum).<BR>E.<BR>वृण to please, aff. दन, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दार|वृंदार|वृन्दारः
वृन्दार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome, pleasing.<BR>2 Eminent, reputable.<BR>E.<BR>वृन्द a quantity, and आरक aff. implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दारक|वृंदारक|वृन्दारकः
वृन्दारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Handsome, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>2 Best, excellent, chief.<BR>3 Much, great.<BR>4 Reputable, respectable, eminent.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A deity, an immortal.<BR>2 A chief, the head or leader of a crowd or herd, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वृन्द a heap, and आरकन् aff., implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिष्ठ|वृंदिष्ठ|वृन्दिष्ठः
वृन्दिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Very beautiful or charming, very excellent or elevated, very reputable or venerable.<BR>E.<BR>वृन्दारक chief, excellent, वृन्द substituted, and इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. super.; also with ईयसुन् the same, वृन्दीयस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दीयस्|वृंदीयस्
वृन्दीयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Very eminent or excellent.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश|वृशः
वृश<BR>r. 4th cl. (वृश्यति)<BR>To choose, to prefer or select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश|वृशः
वृश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A rat.<BR>2 A flower, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>f. (-शा)<BR>A drug.<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, शक् Uṇādi aff.; also वृष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिक|वृश्चिकः
वृश्चिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>2 The sign Scorpio.<BR>3 A hairy caterpillar.<BR>4 A crab.<BR>5 A sort of beetle found in cow-dung.<BR>6 A centipede.<BR>7 A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>8 The month when the sun is in Scorpio.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A potherb, (Basella.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रश्च to cut, Uṇādi aff. किकन्, and the semivowel changed to the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिकप्रिया
वृश्चिकप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR>E.<BR>वृश्चिक a scorpion, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिकाली
वृश्चिकाली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A line of scorpions.<BR>2 A shrub, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR>E.<BR>वृश्चिक a scorpion, and आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष|वृषं|वृषः
वृष<BR>(उ) वृषु r. 1st cl. (वर्षति)<BR>1 To sprinkle.<BR>2 To hurt or kill.<BR>3 To weary.<BR>4 To give.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्षयति-ते)<BR>1 To conceive, to be impregnated.<BR>2 To possess supreme or supernatural power.<BR>3 To be powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष|वृषं|वृषः
वृष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 The sign of the zodiac Taurus.<BR>3 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>4 Virtue personified, as a bull or the bull of ŚIVA.<BR>5 A man of a lecherous disposition, one of the four descriptions into which men are divided in erotic works.<BR>6 A rat.<BR>7 A drug, commonly Ṛṣabha.<BR>8 A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>9 (In composition,) Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>10 A name of KARṆA.<BR>11 VIṢṆU.<BR>12 An enemy, an adversary.<BR>13 Particular ground, judged proper for the foundation of a house.<BR>14 Love or KĀMA.<BR>15 A strong or athletic man.<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>A peacock's plumage or tail.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">Page803</a>]<BR>2 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The seat of the religious student or one used by ascetics, formed of Kusa grass.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=802" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषकर्णी
वृषकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण|वृषणः
वृषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The testicles or scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, (seminal fluid,) aff. क्यु or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषणकच्छू
वृषणकच्छू<BR>f. (-च्छूः)<BR>Ulceration of the scrotum.<BR>E.<BR>वृषण, and कच्छू a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषणश्व|वृषणश्वः
वृषणश्व<BR>m. (-श्वः)<BR>The horse of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृषन् INDRA, and अश्व the horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण्वसु
वृषण्वसु<BR>n. (-सुः)<BR>The treasure of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>वृषन् INDRA, and वसु wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषदंशक|वृषदंशकः
वृषदंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a rat, and दंशक devourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषध्वज|वृषध्वजः
वृषध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 A virtuous man.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, a rat, or virtue, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषन्
वृषन्<BR>m. (-षा)<BR>1 INDRA, as god of the firmament.<BR>2 KARṆA, the hero.<BR>3 Pain, sorrow.<BR>4 Insensibility from extreme pain.<BR>5 A bull.<BR>6 A horse.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषनाशन|वृषनाशनः
वृषनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Vireng, (Embelia ribes).<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपति|वृषपतिः
वृषपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A bull set at liberty.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपर्णी
वृषपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>E.<BR>वृष a rat, and पर्ण a leaf; fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपर्व्वन्|वृषपर्वन्
वृषपर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A demon.<BR>3 A wasp.<BR>4 A sort of grass, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, &c., पर्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभ|वृषभः
वृषभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A bull.<BR>2 (In composition,) Pre-eminent, excellent.<BR>3 The orifice of the ear.<BR>4 An elephant's ear.<BR>5 A drug; also Ṛṣabha, described as a root resembling the horn of a bull, brought from the Himālaya mountains, of cooling and tonic properties, and serviceable in catarrh and consumption.<BR>6 The first of the Jaina pontiffs of the present era.<BR>f. (-भी)<BR>1 A widow.<BR>2 Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. अभच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभगति|वृषभगतिः
वृषभगति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वृषभ a bull, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभध्वज|वृषभध्वजः
वृषभध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वृषभ a bull, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभासा
वृषभासा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>The capital of INDRA, and the immortals.<BR>E.<BR>वृष the bull of ŚIVA, भास् splendour, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषय|वृषयः
वृषय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An asylum, a place of refuge or shelter.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to screen, Uṇādi aff. कयन्, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषल|वृषलः
वृषल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 A Śūdra, or man of the servile tribe.<BR>3 The sovereign CANDRAGUPTA.<BR>4 Garlick.<BR>5 A sinner, a reprobate, a wicked or unrighteous man.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A girl twelve years old, in whom menstruation has commenced, and who is unmarried.<BR>2 A barren woman.<BR>3 A woman during menstruation.<BR>4 The mother of a still-born child.<BR>5 A woman of a low caste.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, or virtue, &c., and ल to take, aff. क, or वृष to sprinkle, कल Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलत्व
वृषलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The condition or state of a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to वृषल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलात्मज|वृषलात्मजः
वृषलात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The son of a reprobate.<BR>E.<BR>वृषल a wicked man, and आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीसेवन
वृषलीसेवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Intercourse with a Śūdra female.<BR>E.<BR>वृषली, and सेवन frequenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलोचन|वृषलोचनः
वृषलोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A rat.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषवाहन|वृषवाहनः
वृषवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषशचु
वृषशचु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वृष KARṆA, and शत्रु the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषसृक्की
वृषसृक्की<BR>f. (-क्की)<BR>A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्यन्ती|वृषस्यंती
वृषस्यन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A lascivious woman.<BR>2 A cow in heat.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a man of a particular class, or a bull, forming with the increments सुक्, and क्यच a nominal verb, implying desire of such a man, &c. participial aff. of the present tense शतृ, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपायी
वृषाकपायी<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>1 The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>2 GAURĪ.<BR>3 SVĀHĀ, the wife of AGNI.<BR>4 ŚACI, the wife of INDRA.<BR>5 A shrub, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>6 A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>वृषाकपि VIṢṆU, &c., ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपि|वृषाकपिः
वृषाकपि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>1 KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 AGNI, or fire.<BR>E.<BR>वृष virtue, अ not, कपि to shake or agitate, इ aff., and the radical augment rejected; or वृषा INDRA, अकपि untrembling, as before; or वृष virtue, or वृषा INDRA, and कपि an ape, being the ape as it were of the greater gods: other etymologies occur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाङ्क|वृषांक|वृषाङ्कः
वृषाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A pious man.<BR>3 Marking-nut plant.<BR>4 An eunuch, one employed in the Zenana.<BR>E.<BR>वृष the bull of the deity, or virtue, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाङ्कज|वृषांकज|वृषाङ्कजः
वृषाङ्कज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A very small drum, held in one hand, and played by means of a string attached to it.<BR>E.<BR>वृषाङ्क ŚIVA, and ज born, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाञ्चन|वृषांचन|वृषाञ्चनः
वृषाञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, and अञ्चन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाणक|वृषाणकः
वृषाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A form of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a bull, अन to be, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषान्तक|वृषान्तकः
वृषान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वृष virtue, अन्त end, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायण|वृषायणः
वृषायण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाहार|वृषाहारः
वृषाहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>वृष a rat, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषिन्
वृषिन्<BR>m. (-षी)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>वृष his plumage, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषी
वृषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>The seat or cushion of an ascetic; also वृसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषोत्सर्ग|वृषोत्सर्गः
वृषोत्सर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>Setting a bull at liberty on occasion of a sacrifice or obsequial oblation.<BR>E.<BR>वृष, and उत्सर्ग letting loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टि|वृष्टिः
वृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Rain.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिकर
वृष्टिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Raining, sprinkling.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिकाल|वृष्टिकालः
वृष्टिकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिघ्नी
वृष्टिघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Guzeratty cardamoms.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि rain, and घ्न destructive, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिजीवन|वृष्टिजीवनः
वृष्टिजीवन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Nourished or watered by rain.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि rain, जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिभू
वृष्टिभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि rain, and भू being, or being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिमत्|वृष्टिमन्त्
वृष्टिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मात्-मती-मत्)<BR>Rainy, full of rain.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>वृष्टि, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णि|वृष्णिः
वृष्णि<BR>mfn. (-ष्णिः-ष्णिः-ष्णि)<BR>1 Heretical, heterodox.<BR>2 Angry, passionate.<BR>m. (-ष्णिः)<BR>1 A ram.<BR>2 One of the descendants of YADU.<BR>3 VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>4 A heretic, a sectary.<BR>5 A ray of light.<BR>6 INDRA.<BR>7 AGNI.<BR>8 Air or wind.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, Uṇādi aff. नि, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्य|वृष्यं|वृष्यः
वृष्य<BR>mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>1 Errhine, aphrodisiac, provocative, (food or medicine.)<BR>2 To be sprinkled or aspersed.<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>Kidneybean, (Phaseolus radiatus).<BR>f. (-ष्या)<BR>A drug, commonly Ridādhi.<BR>E.<BR>वृष to sprinkle, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=803" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्यगन्धा
वृष्यगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह
वृह<BR>r. 1st cl. (वर्हति) also (इ) वृहि (वृंहति)<BR>1 To grow or increase.<BR>2 (In the second form only,) To roar, as a wild beast.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (वृहति वृहयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To shine.<BR>(ऊ) वृहू r. 6th cl. (वृहति)<BR>To make any effort or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्चित्त|वृहच्चित्तः
वृहच्चित्त<BR>m. (-त्तः)<BR>A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्छरीर
वृहच्छरीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Large bodied, gigantic.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्छल्क|वृहच्छल्कः
वृहच्छल्क<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>A prawn.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् great, and शल्क scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहज्जन
वृहज्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A great or illustrious man.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहढक्का
वृहढक्का<BR>f. (-क्का)<BR>A large drum.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, ढक्का a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्|वृहन्त्
वृहत्<BR>mfn. (-हन्-हती-हत)<BR>1 Great, large.<BR>2 Great, much.<BR>f. (-हती)<BR>1 A small kind of egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>2 A kind of prickly nightshade, (Solanum hirsutum.)<BR>3 A large lute.<BR>4 A form of metre, the stanza of which consists of thirtysix syllables.<BR>5 A mantle, a wrapper.<BR>6 A reservoir, a place containing water.<BR>7 Speech.<BR>E.<BR>वृह to grow or increase, Uṇādi aff. अति, with the effect of the participial aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतिका
वृहतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 An upper garment, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR>2 A small sort of egg-plant.<BR>E.<BR>वृहती as above, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतिपति
वृहतिपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>वृहति speech, eloquence, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्क|वृहत्कः
वृहत्क<BR>mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं)<BR>Large, great.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कन्द|वृहत्कन्दः
वृहत्कन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>A bulbous root, considered in some places as a large kind of onion, in others as a sort of garlick.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, large, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्काय
वृहत्काय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Large bodied, bulky, gigantic.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कालशाक|वृहत्कालशाकः
वृहत्कालशाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shrub, (Cassia purpurea, or a large variety of it.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and कालशाक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्काश|वृहत्काशः
वृहत्काश<BR>n. (-शं)<BR>A large kind of the grass Kāś, (Saccharum spontaneum).<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, काश the same grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कुक्षि|वृहत्कुक्षिः
वृहत्कुक्षि<BR>mfn. (-क्षिः-क्षिः or क्षी-क्षि)<BR>Corpulent, large or pot-bellied.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, कुक्षि the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्तृण|वृहत्तृणः
वृहत्तृण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>The bambu.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्त्वच्
वृहत्त्वच्<BR>m. (-त्त्वक्)<BR>A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and त्वच् skin or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पाटलि|वृहत्पाटलिः
वृहत्पाटलि<BR>f. (-लिः)<BR>Thorn-apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, पाटलि the Bignonia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पाद|वृहत्पादः
वृहत्पाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Large footed.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and पाद foot or root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पुष्प
वृहत्पुष्प<BR>mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पा-ष्पं)<BR>Having large flowers.<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>Crotolaria of various species.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदङ्ग|वृहदङ्गः
वृहदङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Large bodied, bulky.<BR>2 Large limbed.<BR>3 Having many parts.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A large elephant, such a one as is usually the leader of a wild herd.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदम्ल|वृहदम्लः
वृहदम्ल<BR>m. (-म्लः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Averrhoa carambola.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large or much, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदसृङ्मति
वृहदसृङ्मति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An evil spirit, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, असृक् blood, and मति inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्गृह|वृहद्गृहः
वृहद्गृह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A country, described as lying behind the Vindhya mountains, near the province of Malva, and perhaps comprising Bundelkhand, or the adjoining district.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and गृह a house; also read वृहद्गुह from गुह a cave, the country being mountainous, and the people probably having been Troglodytes or dwellers in caves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्गोल|वृहद्गोलं
वृहद्गोल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A water-melon.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and गोल round, or a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्द्युति
वृहद्द्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Radiance, splendor, a great light.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, and द्युति light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्धल|वृहद्धलं
वृहद्धल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The furrow made by a plough.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, हल a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्भद्दारिका
वृहद्भद्दारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A name of UMĀ or DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् great, and भद्दारिका princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्भानु|वृहद्भानुः
वृहद्भानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, many, and भानु a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्रथ|वृहद्रथः
वृहद्रथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 INDRA.<BR>2 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>3 A particular Mantra.<BR>4 A division of the Sāma Veda.<BR>f. (-थी)<BR>The name of a river.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्रावी
वृहद्रावी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>A small owl.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् great, much, राव cry, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्वात|वृहद्वातः
वृहद्वात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A grain, generally eaten by the natives of India, (Andropogon sorghum.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् much, and वात wind, supposed to generate this humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्वीज|वृहद्वीजः
वृहद्वीज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Having much or large seed.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहन्नल|वृहन्नलः
वृहन्नल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A large sort of reed, (Arundo gigantea.)<BR>2 ARJUNA.<BR>3 The arm.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् large, and नल a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहन्निवेश
वृहन्निवेश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Large, bulky, protuberant.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत्, and निषेश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पति|वृहस्पतिः
वृहस्पति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The regent of the planet JUPITER, identified astronomically with the planet; in Mythology, he is the son of AṄGIRAS, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>2 The name of a saint and law-giver.<BR>E.<BR>वृहत् great, illustrious, (as the deities,) and पति master or Guru, सुट् augment, and the final of the first member rejected; it also occasionally occurs वृहतांपति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पतिचक्र|वृहस्पतिचक्रं
वृहस्पतिचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>The cycle of 60 years.<BR>E.<BR>वृहस्पति, and चक्र a cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वॄ
वॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (वृणाति)<BR>1 To choose.<BR>2 To support or nourish, (in this sense it is more usually written with the labial initial.)<BR>(ञ) वृञ r. 9th cl. (वृणाति वृणीते)<BR>1 To choose, to elect or select.<BR>2 To cover, to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वे
वे<BR>r. 1st cl. (वयति वयते)<BR>To weave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेकट|वेकटः
वेकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A youth, an adolescent.<BR>2 A sort of fish, (perhaps the common Bekti.)<BR>3 A jeweller.<BR>4 An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेग|वेगः
वेग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 Speed, dispatch, velocity.<BR>2 Impetus, momentum.<BR>3 Stream, current.<BR>4 Sudden impulse, transition of mind. as from passion to apathy, &c.<BR>5 Determination, promptitude, energy, that effect of mind which is considered as the source of action.<BR>6 Pleasure, delight.<BR>7 Love, the sentiment or passion.<BR>8 External indication of any internal effect, proceeding from passion, medicine, poison, &c., as convulsion, horripilation, sweat, &c.<BR>9 Expulsion or evacuation of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">Page805</a>] natural excretions.<BR>10 Semen virile.<BR>11 The flight of an arrow.<BR>12 The fruit of a kind of mango.<BR>E.<BR>वीज to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=804" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगतस्
वेगतस्<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly, speedily.<BR>E.<BR>वेग, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगनाशन|वेगनाशनः
वेगनाशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Phlegm, the phlegmatic humor.<BR>E.<BR>वेग activity or speed, and नाशन injuring, inducing corpulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगरोध|वेगरोधः
वेगरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Check, remora.<BR>2 Obstruction of the natural excretions.<BR>E.<BR>वेग, and रोध hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्|वेगवन्त्
वेगवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Quick, expeditious.<BR>2 Agitated.<BR>E.<BR>वेग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्तर
वेगवत्तर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Very quick.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A species of metre, having nine syllables for the first and third pādas, and eleven for the second and fourth.<BR>E.<BR>वेगवत्, and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्तम
वेगवत्तम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Very quick or swift.<BR>E.<BR>वेगवत्, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगविधारण
वेगविधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Stopping, retarding.<BR>2 Constipation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वेग, and विघारण withholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगसर|वेगसरः
वेगसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mule.<BR>E.<BR>वेग speed, सर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगाघात|वेगाघातः
वेगाघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Stop, check.<BR>2 Obstruction of the natural excretions.<BR>E.<BR>वेग, and आघात resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगित|वेगितः
वेगित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Quickened, expedited.<BR>E.<BR>वीज to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिता
वेगिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Speed, quickness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the next; also वगित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिन्
वेगिन्<BR>mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>Swift, fleet, rapid.<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>1 A courier, an express.<BR>2 A hawk.<BR>E.<BR>वेग speed, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेचा
वेचा<BR>f. (-चा)<BR>Hire, wages.<BR>E.<BR>विच to distinguish, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजानी
वेजानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेटा
वेटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>The abode of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेडा
वेडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>A boat.<BR>E.<BR>विड to curse, aff. अच्, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण|वेणः
वेण<BR>(ऋ) वेणृ r. 1st cl. (वेणति-ते)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To know.<BR>3 To reflect or remember.<BR>4 To discern.<BR>5 To hold or take a musical instrument.<BR>6 To play on an instrument.<BR>7 To take. The root is also read वेनृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण|वेणः
वेण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A musician, one by birth, the son of a woman of the Ambaṣṭha, and man of the Vaideha caste.<BR>E.<BR>वेण to play on a musical instrument, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणि|वेणिः
वेणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>Unornamented and braided hair; the hair as worn especially by widows and women whose husbands are absent, when it is simply collected from the forehead and temples as well as the back of the head, and twisted together into a single braid, which is then suffered to fall like a tail down the back, no sort of ornament being worn on the head; the term is also applied generally to any braid of hair, or to a braid of the long hair, of which many are made, and the whole are then twisted together, and worn as a sort of rose or flower at the back of the head.<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>1 Assemblage of water, as the conflux of rivers, &c. in that case it rather implies their parallel course, ending in a common point of union; as at Allahabad, where the GAṄGĀ, YAMUNĀ, and as is supposed, the SARASVATI, all coming from the north, unite; this and other similar places, thence receive the name of Triveṇi.<BR>2 Weaving.<BR>(-णी)<BR>1 Stream, current.<BR>2 A ewe.<BR>3 A sort of grass, (Andropogon serratum.)<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, Uṇādi aff. नि, and in some cases ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिका
वेणिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Braided hair.<BR>E.<BR>वेणी as above, कन् fem. form, added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिवेधनी
वेणिवेधनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणीर|वेणीरः
वेणीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The soap-berry, (Sapindus detergens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणु|वेणुः
वेणु<BR>m. (-णुः)<BR>1 A bambu.<BR>2 A flute, a pipe.<BR>3 A king so named.<BR>E.<BR>वी substituted for अज to go, aff. नु, or वन to sound, कु aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुक|वेणुकं|वेणुकः
वेणुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A pike used for driving an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and कन् aff.; having a bambu shaft or handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुकर्क्कर|वेणुकर्कर|वेणुकर्करः
वेणुकर्क्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A thorny plant, commonly Karir or Karil.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and कर्क्कर hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुध्म|वेणुध्मः
वेणुध्म<BR>m. (-ध्मः)<BR>A player on a fife or flute.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, ध्मा to blow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुनिस्रुति|वेणुनिस्रुतिः
वेणुनिस्रुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The sugar-cane.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and निस्रुति oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुपत्री
वेणुपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A plant, one synonym of which, Hingupatri, appears to relate to the Asafœtida or some similar plant, whilst the corresponding compound Banspatra both in Hindi and Bengali, is applied to a species of Amaranthus, (A. lanceifolius, Rox., or A. atro-purpureus, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and पत्र a leaf, fem. aff. ङीष्, having long slender leaves, like those of the bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुवाद|वेणुवादः
वेणुवाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A player on a flute.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a flute or pipe, वाद who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतन|वेतनं
वेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Hire, wages.<BR>2 Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>3 Silver.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, तनन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनदान
वेतनदान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Hiring, paying wages.<BR>E.<BR>वेतन, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनादान
वेतनादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Non-payment of wages.<BR>E.<BR>वेतन, and अदान not giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस|वेतसः
वेतस<BR>mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>The ratan, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to sew or weave, Uṇādi aff. असच्, and तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतसपत्र
वेतसपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The leaf of the ratan.<BR>2 A lancet.<BR>E.<BR>वेतस, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस्वत्|वेतस्वन्त्
वेतस्वत्<BR>mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>Reedy, abounding in reeds or canes, (a place or soil, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वेतस् a cane, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेताल|वेतालः
वेताल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A sprite, a goblin, especially one haunting cemeteries and animating dead bodies.<BR>2 A door-keeper.<BR>E.<BR>व in the seventh case वे in air, and ताल habitation, fixation, from तल् to fix, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्तृ
वेत्तृ<BR>mfn. (-त्ता-त्री-त्तृ)<BR>1 Knowing, understanding, acquainted with.<BR>2 Who obtains or acquires.<BR>m. (-त्ता)<BR>1 A sage, one who knows the nature of the soul and GOD.<BR>2 A husband, an espouser.<BR>E.<BR>विद् to know, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्र|वेत्रः
वेत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A reed, a cane, the Ratan.<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A stick, a staff.<BR>E.<BR>वि to go, Uṇādi aff. त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रकीय|वेत्रकीयः
वेत्रकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>A bounding with reeds or canes.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a cane, छ aff., and कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रधर|वेत्रधरः
वेत्रधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A door-keeper, a warder.<BR>2 A staff-bearer, a mace-bearer.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a staff, and धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रधारक|वेत्रधारकः
वेत्रधारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A door-keeper, a warder, a porter.<BR>2 A macebearer.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a stick, and धारक having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=805" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रवती
वेत्रवती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The Betwa river, which rises in the province of Malva, and following a north-easterly direction for about 340 miles, falls into the Jumna below Calpi.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a ratan, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रासन|वेत्रासनं
वेत्रासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A small cot or oblong low couch of basket work; when furnished with bambu sticks and a pole, it forms the common Duli or litter.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a cane, and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रिन्
वेत्रिन्<BR>m. (-त्री)<BR>A porter, a door-keeper.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a strick, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेथ
वेथ<BR>(ऋ) वेथृ r. 1st cl. (वेथते)<BR>To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद|वेदः
वेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A Veda, the generic term for the sacred writings or scripture of the Hindus; supposed to have been revealed by BRAHMĀ, and after being preserved by tradition for a considerable period, to have been arranged in the present form by VYĀSA; the principal Vedas are three in number, the Ṛc, Yajus, and Sāma, to which a fourth, the Atharva, is usually added, and the Itihāsa and Purāṇas, or ancient history and mythology, are sometimes considered as a fifth.<BR>2 Metre.<BR>3 Gloss, comment, explanation.<BR>4 Knowledge.<BR>5 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know (duty and religion from it). aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदकौलेयक|वेदकौलेयकः
वेदकौलेयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, कुल race, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदगर्भ|वेदगर्भः
वेदगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 A Brahman, a man of the sacerdotal tribe.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and गर्भ embryo or womb, figuratively for origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदगुप्ति|वेदगुप्तिः
वेदगुप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>The preservation of the Vedas by the Brahmanical tribe.<BR>E.<BR>वेद a Veda, and गुप्ति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदज्ञ|वेदज्ञः
वेदज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A Brahman skilled in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदण्ड|वेदंड|वेदंडः|वेदण्डः
वेदण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदतत्त्व
वेदतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The true doctrine or substance of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदत्रय
वेदत्रय<BR>nf. (-यं-यी)<BR>The three first Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदन|वेदनं
वेदन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Sensation, perception, knowledge conveyed by the senses.<BR>2 Pain, smart, agony.<BR>3 Knowledge.<BR>4 The ceremony of holding the ends of a mantle, to be observed by a Śūdra female, on her marriage with a man of either of the first three classes.<BR>5 Presenting, delivering.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The true skin or cutis.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, &c., युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनाद
वेदनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sound of chaunting or repeating the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दक|वेदनिंदक|वेदनिन्दकः
वेदनिन्दक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An atheist, a disbeliever.<BR>2 A Jaina or Bauddha, or any seceder from the belief of the divine origin and character of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद scripture, and निन्दक defaming, disrespecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दा|वेदनिंदा
वेदनिन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Reviling the Vedas, heresy, disbelief.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and निन्दा blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनीय
वेदनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be known or perceived.<BR>2 To be, or to be made known.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपारग|वेदपारगः
वेदपारग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Brahman skilled in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Veda, and पारग who crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपुण्य
वेदपुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>The sanctity of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and पुण्य holiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमातृ
वेदमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The mystical prayer or Gāyatrī, personified as the mother or source of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमुख्या
वेदमुख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>A sort of insect, the winged bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदय
वेदय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Who or what knows or obtains.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदरक्षण
वेदरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The conservation of the Vedas, as a duty of the Brahmanical order.<BR>E.<BR>वेद a Veda, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवचन
वेदवचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A text of the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and वचन dictum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवाक्य
वेदवाक्य<BR>n. (-क्यं)<BR>Text of the Veda.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and वाक्य sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवास|वेदवासः
वेदवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वेद a Veda, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्
वेदविद्<BR>m. (-विद् or वित्)<BR>A Brahman versed in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and विद to know, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्वस्
वेदविद्वस्<BR>m. (-द्वान्)<BR>A Brahman learned in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and विद्वस् a learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविहित
वेदविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taught or declared in the Vedas, scriptural.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and विहित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवृत्त
वेदवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>The doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and वृत्त done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदव्यास|वेदव्यासः
वेदव्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The Muni VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, वि and आङ् severally, before अस to throw or place, aff. घञ्, the compiler and arranger of the Vedas; he having first collected and arranged the Hindu scriptures into the four parts, in which they at present exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदशब्द
वेदशब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>A word or term in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and शब्द a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदशास्त्र
वेदशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>The Vedas or any part of them.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and शास्त्र an inspired writing, a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसंहिता
वेदसंहिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A collection of the formulæ of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and संहिता a compendium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस्
वेदस्<BR>m. (-दाः)<BR>The Vedas collectively.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसन्न्यास|वेदसंन्यास|वेदसंन्यासः
वेदसन्न्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Discontinuing the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and सन्न्यास relinquishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसन्न्यासिक|वेदसंन्यासिक
वेदसन्न्यासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The religious ascetic or member of the fourth order, who discontinues the ritual of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, सन्न्यास, and ठक् aff.; also with इनि, वेदसन्न्यासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसम्मत|वेदसंमत
वेदसम्मत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Conformable to the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and सम्मत concurrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाङ्ग|वेदांग|वेदाङ्गं
वेदाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A sacred science, considered as subordinate to, and in some sense, a part of the Vedas: six sciences come under this denomination; Śīkṣā, or the science of pronunciation and articulation; Kalpa the detail of religious ceremonies; Vyākaraṇa, or grammar; Candas, prosody; Jyotiṣ, or astronomy; and Nirukti, or the explanation of the difficult or obscure words and phrases that occur in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदादिवर्ण
वेदादिवर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>The mystical name of GOD.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, आदि first, and वर्ण letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाधिगम|वेदाधिगमः
वेदाधिगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Perusal or study of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and अधिगम going over or through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्ययन
वेदाध्ययन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Study of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and अध्ययन reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्ययिन्
वेदाध्ययिन्<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>A student of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and अध्ययिन् who reads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्यापक|वेदाध्यापकः
वेदाध्यापक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A teacher of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and अध्यापक teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्यापन
वेदाध्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Teaching the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and अध्यापन teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=806" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्त|वेदांत|वेदान्तः
वेदान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>The theological part of the Vedas; considered collectively it is contained in the many numerous passages or chapters of the Vedas termed Upaniṣads, which inculcate an abstract and speculative monotheistical worship, and these have been further explained and illustrated by later writers: the founder of the school is VYĀSA, and subsequently ŚAṂKARĀCĀRYA is its most eminent teacher.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and अन्त end, sum, scope or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तग|वेदांतग
वेदान्तग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Vedāntī.<BR>E.<BR>वेदान्त, and ग who goes over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तज्ञ|वेदांतज्ञ
वेदान्तज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A Vedāntī.<BR>E.<BR>वेदान्त, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तिन्|वेदांतिन्
वेदान्तिन्<BR>m. (-न्ती)<BR>A Vedāntī, a follower of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>E.<BR>वेदान्त the theism of the Vedas, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तोपगत
वेदान्तोपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Derived from or produced by the Vedānta.<BR>E.<BR>वेदान्त, and उपगत derived from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाभ्यास|वेदाभ्यासः
वेदाभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 The repetition of the mystical syllable Om.<BR>2 Study of scripture.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदार|वेदारः
वेदार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A chameleon, a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदि|वेदिः
वेदि<BR>f. (-दिः-दी)<BR>1 Ground for placing the vessels used at an oblation, or for binding the victim, or lighting the sacrificial fire; it is more or less raised and of various shapes; an altar, &c.<BR>2 A quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or palace, usually furnished with a raised floor or seat, and covered with a roof supported by pillars: see वितर्दि.<BR>3 A seal ring.<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a teacher.<BR>f. (-दिः)<BR>A name of SARASVATĪ, the wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, &c. Uṇādi aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिका
वेदिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A quadrangular open shed in the middle of a court yard, erected for various purposes: see वितर्द्दि.<BR>2 Ground prepared for sacrificial ceremonies, a rude kind of altar.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिजा
वेदिजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>DRAUPADĪ, the sister and wife of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>वेदि an altar, and ज born; born from sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित|वेदितः
वेदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Set forth, represented, made known.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितव्य|वेदितव्यं
वेदितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be known or ascertained.<BR>2 To be made known, to be explained or expounded.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, causal form, aff. तव्यर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितृ
वेदितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Wise, learned.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, तृच् aff., with the augment इट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित्व
वेदित्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Knowledge, experience.<BR>E.<BR>वेदिन् who knows, त्व aff.; also with तल्, वेदिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिन्
वेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Who or what knows.<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A Paṇḍita, a learned Brahman, a teacher.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>n. (-दि)<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदीश|वेदीशः
वेदीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वेदी SARASVATĪ, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोक्त|वेदोक्तः
वेदोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Scriptural, taught or declared in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदय|वेदोदयः
वेदोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>SŪRYA, or the sun.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Veda, (the Sāma Veda,) and उदय rise, origin; being said to have proceeded from the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदित|वेदोदितः
वेदोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taught in the Vedas, scriptural.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the Vedas, and उदित spoken, from वद to speak, with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोपकरण
वेदोपकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A subordinate branch of the study of the Vedas: see वेदाङ्ग.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and उपकरण implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्य|वेद्यं
वेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>1 To be known or ascertained.<BR>2 To be explained or taught.<BR>E.<BR>विद to know, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध|वेधः
वेध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Perforation, piercing.<BR>2 Depth, (in measurement.)<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधक|वेधकं|वेधकः
वेधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Sharp, piercing, a piercer or perforator.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Grain, rice in the ear.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधन|वेधनं
वेधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Piercing, perforation.<BR>2 Depth, (in measurement.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 An instrument for piercing an elephant's ear.<BR>2 A small gimblet or perforating instrument used to pierce gems, shells, &c.<BR>3 An augre, a gimblet, &c. or any similar instrument.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनिका
वेधनिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small-pointed perforating instrument, used especially to make holes in jewels, pearls, shells, &c., an augre, an awl, a gimblet, &c.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to वेधन as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधमुख्यक|वेधमुख्यकः
वेधमुख्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>E.<BR>वेध piercing, (figuratively for pervading as by its odour,) मुख्य principal, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्
वेधस्<BR>m. (-धाः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A wise or learned man.<BR>4 The sun.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धा to have, Uṇādi aff. असि, and वेध substituted for the root and prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस|वेधसं
वेधस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The root of the thumb, considered as sacred to BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वेधस् BRAHMĀ, and अण् added, the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधित|वेधितः
वेधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pierced, perforated.<BR>E.<BR>व्यघ to pierce, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिन्
वेधिन्<BR>mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>Piercing, perforating.<BR>f. (-धिनी)<BR>A leech.<BR>E.<BR>व्यघ piercing, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध्य|वेध्यं
वेध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>To be pierced or perforated.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>A mark, a butt.<BR>E.<BR>व्यघ to pierce, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन<BR>r. 1st cl. (वेनति)<BR>To go, &c.: see वेण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>वी substituted for अज to go, Uṇādi aff. न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्ना
वेन्ना<BR>f. (-न्ना)<BR>A river.<BR>E.<BR>वन to sound, Uṇādi aff. न, and इ with the usual change, substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेप|वेपः
वेप<BR>(टु ऋ) टुवेपृ r. 1st cl. (वेपते)<BR>To shake or tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथु|वेपथुः
वेपथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Trembling, tremor.<BR>E.<BR>वेप to tremble, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपन|वेपनं
वेपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Tremor, trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वेप to tremble, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपमान
वेपमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Trembling, shaking.<BR>E.<BR>वेप to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपस्
वेपस्<BR>n. (-पः)<BR>Trembling.<BR>E.<BR>वेप to tremble, aff. असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेम|वेमः
वेम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A loom.<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to weave, aff. मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेमन्
वेमन्<BR>mn. (-मा-म)<BR>A loom.<BR>E.<BR>वेञ् to weave, मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेर|वेरं|वेरः
वेर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 The body.<BR>2 The egg-plant.<BR>3 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>वी to go, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरक|वेरकं|वेरकः
वेरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरट|वेरटः
वेरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A low man, one of mixed or inferior caste.<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The fruit of the Jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल|वेलं|वेलः
वेल<BR>(ऋ) वेऌ r. 1st cl. (वेलति)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>2 To shake, to tremble.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेलयति)<BR>To count or declare the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल|वेलं|वेलः
वेल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A garden.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Time.<BR>2 Tide, flow, current.<BR>3 Boundary, limit.<BR>4 Sea-shore.<BR>5 Easy or sudden death. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">Page808</a>]<BR>6 Sickness, disease.<BR>7 The food of ŚIVA.<BR>8 Speech.<BR>9 Leisure, interval, opportunity.<BR>10 The wife of Budha.<BR>11 The gums.<BR>E.<BR>वेल to go, aff. अच् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=807" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलाकुल
वेलाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Agitated by the tide.<BR>E.<BR>वेला, and आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलाकूल|वेलाकूलं
वेलाकूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Tamlūck, the district or kingdom as it formerly existed, the southern part of the present Hūgli district, forming the west bank of the Hūgli river, at its union with the sea: a village called Beercool, derived from this word probably, is still found in the maps, near the sea shore immediately south of the boundary of the Hūgli district.<BR>E.<BR>वेला tide, and कूल bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलामूल
वेलामूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The sea shore.<BR>E.<BR>वेला, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलायाम्
वेलायाम्<BR>ind.<BR>1 On the sea shore, coast wise, &c.<BR>2 Seasonably, opportunely.<BR>E.<BR>वेला a shore, &c. in the seventh case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल|वेल्लं|वेल्लः
वेल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (-वेल्लति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To tremble or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल|वेल्लं|वेल्लः
वेल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>Going, moving, shaking.<BR>mn. (-ल्लः-ल्लं)<BR>A plant, the seed of which is used as a vermifuge.<BR>E.<BR>वेल्ल to shake, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लज|वेल्लजं
वेल्लज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Black pepper, (Piper nigrum.)<BR>E.<BR>वेल्ल shaking, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लन|वेल्लनं
वेल्लन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rolling on the ground, (as a horse.)<BR>2 A sort of rolling pin with which cakes, &c. are prepared.<BR>3 Shaking.<BR>4 Going.<BR>E.<BR>वेल्ल to shake, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लहल|वेल्लहलः
वेल्लहल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A libertine, a debauchee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लि|वेल्लिः
वेल्लि<BR>f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>A creeping plant.<BR>E.<BR>वेल्ल to shake, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लिका
वेल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, commonly Bel Sunṭh.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लित|वेल्लितं|वेल्लितः
वेल्लित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>2 Crooked.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>2 Shaking.<BR>E.<BR>वेल्ल to shake, to move, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेवी
वेवी<BR>r. 2nd cl. (वेवीते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To pervade.<BR>3 To conceive or become pregnant.<BR>4 To desire.<BR>5 To throw or send.<BR>6 To eat; also वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Dress, decoration.<BR>2 Disguise, masquerade.<BR>3 The abode of harlots.<BR>4 A house in general.<BR>4 Entrance, ingress.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, (literally or figuratively, as to enter or occupy the mind,) aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशक|वेशकः
वेशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what enters.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A house.<BR>f. (-शिका)<BR>Entrance, ingress.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशदान|वेशदानः
वेशदान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The sun-flower.<BR>E.<BR>वेश ornament, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशधारिन्
वेशधारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A hypocrite, a false devotee.<BR>E.<BR>वेश disguise, and घारिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशभृत्
वेशभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>1 Dressed, adorned.<BR>2 Disguised.<BR>E.<BR>वेश, and भृत who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन|वेशनं
वेशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 Entering.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन्त|वेशंत|वेशंतः|वेशन्तः
वेशन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A basin, a small pond.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, झच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशर|वेशरः
वेशर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mule; also वेसर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशवार|वेशवारः
वेशवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A condiment, as pepper, cloves, mace, &c.: see वेसवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशिन्
वेशिन्<BR>mfn. (-शि-शिनी-शि)<BR>Assuming a particular dress or form.<BR>E.<BR>वेश, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मन्
वेश्मन्<BR>n. (-श्म)<BR>A house.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मनकुल|वेश्मनकुलः
वेश्मनकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The musk shrew or rat.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्म a house, and नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मभू
वेश्मभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>The site of a habitation.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्म a house, and भ ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मस्थूणा
वेश्मस्थूणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>The main post of a house.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्म् a dwelling, and स्थूणा a pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्य|वेश्यं
वेश्य<BR>n. (-श्यं)<BR>The habitation of harlots.<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>1 A harlot, a prostitute, a whore.<BR>2 A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, ण्यत् aff. or वेश ornament, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्यागण|वेश्यागणः
वेश्यागण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A company of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या, and गण a number, a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याचार्य्य|वेश्याचार्य|वेश्याचार्यः|वेश्याचार्य्यः
वेश्याचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A catamite.<BR>2 The master or keeper of dancing girls, prostitutes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या a whore, and आचार्य्य spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याजनसमाश्रय|वेश्याजनसमाश्रयः
वेश्याजनसमाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The habitation of harlots, a brothel.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या a whore, जन people, सम् collective particle, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्यावार
वेश्यावार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A number or company of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या, and वार assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याश्रय|वेश्याश्रयः
वेश्याश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A brothel, the habitation of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या a whore, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष|वेषः
वेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>Ornament, dress, decoration.<BR>E.<BR>विष to invest, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषण|वेषणं|वेषणः
वेषण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A shrub, (Cassia sophora.)<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Entrance, ingress, possession, occupation.<BR>E.<BR>विष to enter, &c., aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषवार|वेषवारः
वेषवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A condiment; also वेसवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट<BR>r. 1st cl. (वेष्टते)<BR>To surround, to inclose, to encompass or circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A fence, an enclosure.<BR>2 Surrounding, enclosing.<BR>3 A turban.<BR>4 Exudation, gum, resin in general.<BR>5 Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट to surround, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टक|वेष्टकं|वेष्टकः
वेष्टक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Surrounding, a surrounder, that which encompasses or encloses.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A turban.<BR>2 Exudation, resin, gum^1, &c.<BR>3 Turpentine.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A wall, a fence.<BR>2 A pumpkin gourd.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट as above, with कन् added, or वेष्ट to surround, aff. वुन्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टन|वेष्टनं
वेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>2 A wall, an enclosure, a fence.<BR>3 A turban.<BR>4 A diadem, a tiara.<BR>5 The outer ear, or the meatus auditorius and the concha.<BR>9 An attitude in dancing, a particular disposition of the hands; also a crossing of the feet.<BR>7 Bdellium.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट to surround aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टनीय
वेष्टनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be surrounded or encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट to surround, अनीयर् aff.; also वेष्टितव्य and वेष्ट्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टयित्वा
वेष्टयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having bound round or encompassed.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट to surround, causal v., क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टवंश|वेष्टवंशः
वेष्टवंश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A sort of bambu, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट surrounding, and वंश a bambu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टित|वेष्टितं|वेष्टितः
वेष्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Surrounded, encompassed, enclosed.<BR>2 Stopped, secured from access.<BR>3 Bound, round, enveloped, wrapped up.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Encompassing, encircling.<BR>2 One of the gestures or attitudes of dancing, particular motion of the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">Page809</a>] fingers or a crossing of the feet.<BR>E.<BR>वेष्ट surrounding, इतच् aff. or वेष्ट the verb, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=808" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्य|वेष्यः
वेष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>विष to pervade, Uṇādi aff. प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेस
वेस<BR>(ऋ) वेसृ r. 1st cl. (वेसति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसर|वेसरः
वेसर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A mule; also वेशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसवार|वेसवारः
वेसवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A condiment, as ground coriander, mustard, pepper, spice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विस to send, aff. घञ्, वेस despatching, वॄ to choose, aff. अण्; also वेशवार and वेषवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह
वेह<BR>(ऋ) वेहृ r. 1st cl. (वेहते)<BR>To resolve or endeavour diligently; also sometimes read वेहृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहत्
वेहत्<BR>f. (-हत्)<BR>A cow miscarrying from taking the bull unseasonably.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हन् to kill (the embryo), Uṇādi aff. अति; the radical final rejected, and vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्ल
वेह्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (वेह्लति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To tremble; also वेल and वेल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै<BR>(ॐ) ओवै r. 1st cl. (वायति)<BR>To dry, to become dried or withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै<BR>ind.<BR>1 A particle of affirmation, (so, indeed.)<BR>2 An expletive. A vocative particle.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, aff. डै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैंशतिक|वैंशतिकः
वैंशतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Purchased with twenty.<BR>E.<BR>विंशतिक relating to twenty, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्ष|वैकक्षं
वैकक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>1 A garland worn over one shoulder and under the other, like the sacrificial thread.<BR>2 An upper garment, a wrapper, a mantle.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying possessed of or belong to, कक्ष the flank, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्षक|वैकक्षकं
वैकक्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A garland or string of flowers worn as a scarf or like the sacrificial cord, over the left shoulder and under the right arm, hanging down below the hip.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last; also as derived from वि, and कक्ष with ठक् aff. वैकक्षिक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकङ्कत|वैकङ्कतः
वैकङ्कत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A plant, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonasm, added to विकङ्कत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकटिक|वैकटिकः
वैकटिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A jeweller.<BR>E.<BR>विकट difficult (occupation), and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्पिक|वैकल्पिकः
वैकल्पिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Doubtful, indeterminate.<BR>2 Alternative.<BR>E.<BR>विकल्प, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्य|वैकल्यं
वैकल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Lameness, mutilation.<BR>2 Deficiency, defect.<BR>3 Non-existence.<BR>4 Incompetency, insufficiency.<BR>5 Agitation, flurry.<BR>E.<BR>विकल defective, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकाल|वैकालः
वैकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Evening, afternoon.<BR>E.<BR>वि gone, काल time, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकालिक
वैकालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Occurring in or belonging to the afternoon.<BR>E.<BR>विकाल, and ठक् aff.; also with खञ्, वैकालीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकुण्ठ|वैकुंठ|वैकुंठः|वैकुण्ठः
वैकुण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>n. (-ण्ठं)<BR>1 The paradise or world of Vaikuṇṭha or VIṢṆU; its site is variously described, either as in the northern ocean, or on the eastern peak of mount Meru.<BR>2 Talc.<BR>E.<BR>विकुण्ठा the wife of ŚUBHRA, and mother of VIṢṆU, in one form, अण् patronymic aff.: other etymologies occur, as वि privative, &c. and कुण्ठ said to mean destruction, he who is indestructible; or वि before the same, explained knowledge or abode, being omniscient or omnipresent, &c.; again वि various, and कुण्ठ illusion, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत|वैकृतं|वैकृतः
वैकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Changed, in mind or form.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Aversion, disgust.<BR>2 Change in mind or form.<BR>E.<BR>विकृत the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृतापह
वैकृतापह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Removing or preventing change<BR>E.<BR>वैकृत, and अपह what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत्य|वैकृत्यं
वैकृत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Changed, in form or mind.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Aversion, disgust.<BR>2 Change, alteration.<BR>E.<BR>विकृत the same, ष्यञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्रान्त|वैक्रांत|वैक्रांतं|वैक्रान्तं
वैक्रान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>A kind of gem, said to resemble a diamond, and to be of similar properties; it is also considered to be a burnt diamond, and to be the common load-stone or magnet.<BR>E.<BR>विक्रान्त a warrior, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्लव्य|वैक्लव्यं
वैक्लव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Confusion, bewilderment, commotion.<BR>E.<BR>विक्लव confused, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखानस|वैखानसः
वैखानस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A man of the third religious order, a hermit, an anchoret.<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>A vessel used for frying meal to be offered in sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>वि before खन to dig, deriv. irr.; subsisting on roots, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैगुण्य|वैगुण्यं
वैगुण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं).<BR>1 Absence of attributes or qualities.<BR>2 Contrariety of properties or qualities.<BR>3 Inferiority, badness, vileness.<BR>4 Fault, defect.<BR>E.<BR>विगुण void of properties or merit, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचक्षण्य|वैचक्षण्यं
वैचक्षण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Skill, cleverness, proficiency.<BR>E.<BR>विचक्षण clever, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्य
वैचित्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Confusion of ideas, distraction, grief.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्ति wandering, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्र्य|वैचित्र्यं
वैचित्र्य<BR>n. (-त्र्यं)<BR>1 Variety.<BR>2 Surprisingness.<BR>E.<BR>विचित्र astonishing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजनन|वैजननं|वैजननः
वैजनन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The last month of uterine gestation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जन to be born, aff. ल्युट्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्त|वैजयंत|वैजयंतः|वैजयन्तः
वैजयन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 The palace of INDRA.<BR>2 The banner or emblem of INDRA.<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 A flag, a banner, an ensign.<BR>2 A small tree, (Sesbana Ægyptiaca.)<BR>3 Another tree, (Premna spinosa, &c.)<BR>4 A kind of garland.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, भृञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्तिक|वैजयंतिक|वैजयंतिकः|वैजयन्तिकः
वैजयन्तिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A flag-bearer.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A plant, (Sesbana Ægyptiaca.)<BR>2 A flag, a banner.<BR>E.<BR>वैजयन्ती a flag, with ठक् aff., or कन् pleonasm, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयि|वैजयिः
वैजयि<BR>m. (-यिः)<BR>The third Cakravartī or emperor according to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>विजया a proper name, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजात्य|वैजात्यं
वैजात्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>1 Difference or deviation from ordinary character or conduct.<BR>2 Exclusion from caste.<BR>3 Difference of caste or species.<BR>4 Looseness, wantonness.<BR>E.<BR>वि before जाति species, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजिक|वैजिकं|वैजिकः
वैजिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Seminal, relating to seed or origin.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Cause, origin, motive.<BR>2 Oil prepared from the Śigru or Morunga.<BR>3 The spiritual cause of existence, soul, spirit.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A young shoot or sprout.<BR>E.<BR>वीज seed, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैज्ञानिक|वैज्ञानिकः
वैज्ञानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Skilful, clever, dexterous, proficient.<BR>E.<BR>विज्ञान knowledge, science, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैडालव्रतिक|वैडालव्रतिकः
वैडालव्रतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hypocrite, a religious impostor, one who under the appearance of piety and virtue is covetous, malicious, and cruel.<BR>E.<BR>विडाल a cat, व्रत observance, and ठक् aff.; acting like a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण|वैणः
वैण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A cutter of bambus, a worker in bambu work.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, अण् aff., and the primitive final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=809" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणव|वैणवं|वैणवः
वैणव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Produced by or made of a bambu.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A bambu staff in general.<BR>2 A worker in bambu or wickerwork.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणविक|वैणविकः
वैणविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A player on a flute.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a pipe, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणिक|वैणिकः
वैणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A lutist, a player on the Vīṇā or Indian lute.<BR>E.<BR>वीणा the Vīṇā, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुक|वैणुकं|वैणुकः
वैणुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A goad or bambu pike headed with iron, used to drive an elephant.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A player on a pipe or flute.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a flute, कञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुकेय
वैणुकेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a bambu, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वेणु a bambu, and छण् aff., with कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण्य|वैण्यः
वैण्य<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>A name of PṚTHU, the fifth sovereign of the solar race.<BR>E.<BR>वेण the father of this monarch, and यञ् aff.; also read वैन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतंसिक|वैतंसिकः
वैतंसिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vender of the flesh or meat, either of beasts or birds.<BR>E.<BR>वीतंस a snare or net, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतनिक|वैतनिकः
वैतनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A hireling, a labourer.<BR>2 A stipendiary.<BR>E.<BR>वेतन wages, hire, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतरणि|वैतरणिः
वैतरणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 The river of hell.<BR>2 The mother of the Rākṣasas.<BR>E.<BR>वि various, तरण crossing, aff. इञ् or अण्, and ङीष् aff., or वि prohibitive, तरणी crossing; or वितरण giving, (liberality in life securing a passage); or again, वि priv. तरणी a boat, passed without a boat; the affix is the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतस|वैतसः
वैतस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A sort of cane, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>वेतस the Ratan, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतान
वैतान<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Sacrificial, sacred, (as fire.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Oblation with fire.<BR>E.<BR>वितान the hole in the hearth in which sacred fire is kept, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानिक|वैतानिकः
वैतानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Sacrificial, sacred, (as fire.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Burnt-offering, especially of clarified butter, as presented daily by the Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>वितान the hearth, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानोपासना
वैतानोपासना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>The regular presentation of burnt-offering morning and evening.<BR>E.<BR>वैतान sacrificial, (fire,) and उपासना service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालिक|वैतालिकः
वैतालिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A bard whose duty it is to awaken a chief or prince at dawn with music and song.<BR>2 A singer out of tune (?)<BR>3 One who has a demon for a familiar, the servant of a Vetāla.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, &c. ताल tune, अण् aff., and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालीय
वैतालीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A kind of metre, or tetrastich, the first and third lines of which contain the time of fourteen short syllables, and the second and fourth of sixteen; it admits of some varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रक|वैत्रकः
वैत्रक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Cany, reedy, relating to a cane, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a cane, छण aff., with कुक augment, and the final of the aff. rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रकीय|वैत्रकीयः
वैत्रकीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Relating to a stick or cane.<BR>E.<BR>वेत्र a stick, and छण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद|वैदः
वैद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Relating to or connected with a wise man, learned, knowing.<BR>E.<BR>विट् who knows, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध|वैदग्धं
वैदग्ध<BR>n. (-ग्धं)<BR>1 Cleverness, skill, dexterity.<BR>2 Acuteness, sharpness.<BR>3 Craft, cunning.<BR>E.<BR>विदग्ध clever, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध्य|वैदग्ध्यं
वैदग्ध्य<BR>n. (-ग्ध्यं-ग्धी)<BR>1 Cunning, craft.<BR>2 Cleverness, dexterity, skill.<BR>3 Knowingness, sharpness, wit.<BR>E.<BR>विदग्घ clever, sharp, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदर्भ|वैदर्भं|वैदर्भः
वैदर्भ<BR>n. (-र्भं)<BR>Crafty or indirect speech.<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 The sovereign of VIDARBHĀ, the father of DAMAYANTĪ, &c.<BR>2 Gum boil.<BR>f. (-र्भी)<BR>1 The law of VIDARBHĀ, as one by which cousins german were allowed to intermarry in that country, &c.<BR>2 The wife of AGASTYA.<BR>3 DAMAYANTĪ, the wife of NALA.<BR>4 RUKMIṆĪ, one of KṚṢṆA'S wives.<BR>E.<BR>विदर्भा the country so named, and अण् aff. of derivation or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदल|वैदलं|वैदलः
वैदल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Wicker, of cane, wicker or basket work.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 A shallow cup or saucer made of clay usually, though sometimes of metal, and sometimes of wood or wicker.<BR>2 Any seat or vessel of basket or wicker work.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A flat unleavened cake, made of flower, &c. with cumin or coriander seeds, and fried in Ghee.<BR>2 Any leguminous vegetable or grain, as peas, beans, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before दल to divide, aff. अच्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिक|वैदिकः
वैदिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की or का-कं)<BR>Scriptural, derived from or conformable to the Vedas.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Brahman well versed in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>वेद, and ठञ् or ङीप्^1 aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161212. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batches 309-312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिकत्व
वैदिकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Scriptural character or origin.<BR>E.<BR>वैदिक relating to the Vedas, and त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुष्य|वैदुष्यं
वैदुष्य<BR>nf. (-ष्यं-षी)<BR>Learning, sapience.<BR>E.<BR>विदूस् a learned man, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदूर्य्य|वैदूर्य|वैदूर्य्यं
वैदूर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>A gem of a dark colour, the lapis lazuli.<BR>E.<BR>विदूर said to be the name of a mountain where the stone is found, or a city where it is polished, and ञ्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेशिक|वैदेशिकः
वैदेशिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Foreign, stranger.<BR>E.<BR>विदेश, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेह|वैदेहः
वैदेह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A trader by caste, or profession.<BR>2 An attendant on the women's apartments: see the next.<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>1 SĪTĀ, the daughter of JANAKA.<BR>2 Long-pepper.<BR>3 The wife of a trader or woman of the Vaideha caste.<BR>4 A sort of pigment, commonly Rocanā.<BR>E.<BR>विदेह the country, अण् aff. of origin or production, &c.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेहक|वैदेहकः
वैदेहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A trader by profession.<BR>2 A man of a mixed caste, the offspring of a Vaiśya father and Brahman mother, whose business is attendance in the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>विदेह the country, वुञ् aff., or वि various, दिह to collect, (goods, &c.), aff. ण्वुल् and अण् added; or विदेह a king, the supposed author of rules for merchants, वुञ्^1 aff. or with अण् aff. and ठक् added वैदहिक.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्य|वैद्यः
वैद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-दी-द्यं)<BR>1 Medical, practising or relating to medicine.<BR>2 Relating or conformable to the Vedas.<BR>m. (-द्यः)<BR>1 A physician.<BR>2 A tree, (Justicia ganderussa, &c.)<BR>3 A learned man.<BR>4 A follower of the Vedas, or one well read in them.<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>A drug, commonly Kākoli.<BR>E.<BR>वेद the medical or Āyur Vedas, or the Vedas in general, and यञ् or ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यनाथ|वैद्यनाथः
वैद्यनाथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A name of DHANVANTARI.<BR>E.<BR>वैद्य a physician, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यबन्धु|वैद्यबन्धुः
वैद्यबन्धु<BR>m. (-न्धुः)<BR>Cassia fistula.<BR>E.<BR>वैद्य a physician, बन्धु the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यमातृ
वैद्यमातृ<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>E.<BR>वैद्य a physician, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यसिंही
वैद्यसिंही<BR>f. (-ही)<BR>A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>E.<BR>वैद्य medical, and सिंह pre-eminent, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=810" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध|वैधः
वैध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धी-धं)<BR>According to rule, preceptive, ritual.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधव्य|वैधव्यं
वैधव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>Widowhood.<BR>E.<BR>विधवा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधर्म्म्य
वैधर्म्म्य<BR>n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>1 Irreligion, injustice, impropriety.<BR>2 Difference of duty or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>वि before धर्म्म virtue, &c., ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधात्र|वैधात्रः
वैधात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>SANATKUMĀRA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and eldest of the progenitors of mankind.<BR>E.<BR>विधातृ BRAHMĀ, and अण् aff. of descent; it is applicable also to the other three sons of the same deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधिक
वैधिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Ritual, preceptive, according to rule, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विधि, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधेय|वैधेयः
वैधेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Foolish, ignorant, an idiot, a fool.<BR>E.<BR>विधेय performance of religious ceremonials, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध्यत|वैध्यतः
वैध्यत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>YAMA'S porter or chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतक|वैनतकं
वैनतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A vessel for holding or pouring ghee, used at sacrifices with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतेय|वैनतेयः
वैनतेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>विनता the mother of this being, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनयिक|वैनयिकः
वैनयिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Relating to morals or behaviour.<BR>2 Enforcing proper conduct.<BR>3 Magisterial.<BR>E.<BR>विनय, and ठक् aff.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chariot used formerly in battle, a war carriage.<BR>E.<BR>वि before णी to get, अण् aff., and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनायिक|वैनायिकः
वैनायिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Bauddha, a follower of Buddha.<BR>E.<BR>विनायक a Buddha or teacher of this sect, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनाशिक|वैनाशिकं|वैनाशिकः
वैनाशिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A dependant, a subject, a slave.<BR>2 A spider.<BR>3 An astrologer.<BR>E.<BR>विनाश loss, destruction, aff. ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनीतक|वैनीतकः
वैनीतक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A mediate conveyance, as a porter carrying a letter, a horse dragging a chariot, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, णी to take, aff. क्त, with कन् and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपरीत्य|वैपरीत्यं
वैपरीत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR>E.<BR>विपरीत contrary, aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैबोधिक|वैबोधिकः
वैबोधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A watchman, a bell man, one who announces the hours.<BR>E.<BR>विबोध awakening, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभव|वैभवं
वैभव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Grandeur, wealth.<BR>E.<BR>विभव, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभाजित्र|वैभाजित्रं
वैभाजित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Apportioning, dividing.<BR>E.<BR>विभाजयितृ one who makes a division or causes it to be made, अञ् aff., and the semivowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्र|वैभ्रं
वैभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>The heaven of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, भ्राज् to shine, ड aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्राज|वैभ्राजं
वैभ्राज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A garden of the gods, a celestial grove or garden.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, भ्राज to shine, aff. अच्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्र|वैमात्रः
वैमात्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A step-mother's son.<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A step-mother's daughter.<BR>E.<BR>वि different, मातृ a mother, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्रेय|वैमात्रेयः
वैमात्रेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A step-mother's son.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A half sister, or one by a different mother.<BR>E.<BR>विमातृ a step-mother, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमानिक|वैमानिकः
वैमानिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a heavenly car, borne in one, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विमान, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुक्त|वैमुक्तं|वैमुक्तः
वैमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Liberated, emancipated, being at liberty or loose.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>Liberation.<BR>E.<BR>विमुक्त free, loose, and अण् aff. implying property or possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुख्य|वैमुख्यं
वैमुख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>1 Turning away the face.<BR>2 Flight, retreat.<BR>E.<BR>विमुख, and ख्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमेय|वैमेयः
वैमेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR>E.<BR>वि before मेङ् to barter, यत् aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयर्थ्य|वैयर्थ्यं
वैयर्थ्य<BR>n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR>E.<BR>व्यर्थ useless, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाकरण|वैयाकरणः
वैयाकरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Grammatical, relating to grammar.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A grammarian.<BR>E.<BR>व्याकरण grammar, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र|वैयाघ्रः
वैयाघ्र<BR>mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्री-घ्रं)<BR>Covered with a tiger-skin, (a car, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयात्य|वैयात्यं
वैयात्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Immodesty, boldness.<BR>E.<BR>वियात, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयुष्ट|वैयुष्टः
वैयुष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं)<BR>Early, betimes, occurring or performed in the morning.<BR>E.<BR>व्युष्ट morning, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैर|वैरं
वैर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Enmity, hostility.<BR>2 Heroism, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>वीर a warrior, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरकर|वैरकरः
वैरकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Causing or occasioning enmity, mischief-making.<BR>E.<BR>वैर, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरकार|वैरकारः
वैरकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>E.<BR>वैर, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरक्त्य|वैरक्त्यं
वैरक्त्य<BR>n. (-क्त्य)<BR>Aversion, displeasure, dislike.<BR>E.<BR>विरक्त, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरङ्गिक|वैरंगिकः|वैरङ्गिकः
वैरङ्गिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ascetic, a devotee, one who has subdued passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, रङ्ग passion, aff. ठक् or ठञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरनिर्य्यातन|वैरनिर्यातन|वैरनिर्यातनं
वैरनिर्य्यातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Revenge, retaliation, requital of an injury.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity, निर्य्यातन donation, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरप्रतिक्रिया
वैरप्रतिक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Revenge.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity, प्रतिक्रिया return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरशुद्धि|वैरशुद्धिः
वैरशुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Revenge, retaliation.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity, शुद्धि purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग|वैरागं
वैराग<BR>n. (-गं)<BR>Absence of worldly passion or desire.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, राग passion, अण् aff. or with ष्यञ् aff. वैराग्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिक|वैरागिकः
वैरागिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>An ascetic, one with subdued passions.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, राग passion, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिन्
वैरागिन्<BR>m. (-गी)<BR>An ascetic, a devotee, one who has subdued his worldly desires: at present the term in common use is applied to a particular class of religious mendicants.<BR>E.<BR>वैराग absence of passion, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्य|वैराग्यं
वैराग्य<BR>n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Subjection of the appetite and passions, absence of worldly desires.<BR>E.<BR>विराग, and ष्यञ् aff.: see वैराग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट|वैराटः
वैराट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>An earth worm.<BR>E.<BR>वि before राज् to shine, aff. क्विप्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट्या
वैराट्या<BR>f. (-ट्या)<BR>One of the sixteen goddesses of the Bauddhas, termed Vidyādevīs or goddesses of learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरानुवन्धिन्
वैरानुवन्धिन्<BR>m. (-न्धी)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The solar ray which is charged with heat.<BR>E.<BR>वैर heroism or strength, अनुवन्धिन् connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरायमाण
वैरायमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Hostile, inimical, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity used as a verb, with क्यङ् and शानच् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरारोह
वैरारोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Desperate or arduous combat.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity or heroism, आरोह ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिता
वैरिता<BR>(-ता)<BR>1 Enmity.<BR>2 Heroism.<BR>E.<BR>वैरिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, वैरित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Hostile, inimical.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 A hero.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्य|वैरूप्यं
वैरूप्य<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>1 Deformity.<BR>2 Difference of form, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विरुप, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचन|वैरोचनः
वैरोचन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The third of the Buddhas, called Dhyāni Buddhas.<BR>2 BALI, the sovereign so named.<BR>3 The son of AGNI.<BR>4 The son of SŪRYA, or the sun.<BR>5 A Siddha, a sort of demi-god [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">Page812</a>] or deified mortal.<BR>E.<BR>विरोचन the sun, &c., and aff. of descent अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=811" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचननिकेतन|वैरोचननिकेतनं
वैरोचननिकेतन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Pātāla the intermediate region between the earth and Tartarus or Naraka, over part of which BALI presides.<BR>E.<BR>वैरोचन the prince BALI, and निकेतन abode; the sovereign of this name being an incarnate Daitya or hereditary foe of the gods, and being invested with a sovereignty in the lower regions after his humiliation by VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनि|वैरोचनिः
वैरोचनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A BUDDHA.<BR>2 BALI.<BR>3 The son of SŪRYA.<BR>E.<BR>विरीचन the sun, &c., and इञ aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचि|वैरोचिः
वैरोचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>The demon or Daitya VĀṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोद्धार|वैरोद्धारः
वैरोद्धार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Revenge, retaliation.<BR>E.<BR>वैर enmity, and उद्धार a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्ष्य|वैलक्ष्यं
वैलक्ष्य<BR>n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 Contrariety, reverse, inversion.<BR>2 Contrary course or conduct to that which is usual or natural.<BR>3 Absence of any characteristic.<BR>E.<BR>विलक्ष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्षण्य|वैलक्षण्यं
वैलक्षण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>Difference, contrariety.<BR>E.<BR>विलक्षण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्व|वैल्वं
वैल्व<BR>mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वी-ल्वं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the Vilva tree.<BR>n. (-ल्वं)<BR>The fruit of the Vilva, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>विल्व the plant, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्वमय
वैल्वमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of the Vilva, of the wood, &c. of that plant.<BR>E.<BR>वैल्व relating to the Bel, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवधिक|वैवधिकः
वैवधिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A chandler, a vender of grain, oil, ghee, fruit, sweetmeats, &c.<BR>E.<BR>विवध storing grain, &c., aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्य|वैवर्ण्यं
वैवर्ण्य<BR>n. (-र्ण्यं)<BR>1 Change of colour or complexion.<BR>2 Change of colour in general.<BR>3 Deviation or secession from tribe or caste, &c.<BR>4 Heterogeneousness, difference.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative or contra-indicative, and वर्ण colour, tribe, &c., aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वत|वैवस्वतः
वैवस्वत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 YAMA.<BR>2 One of the RUDRAS.<BR>3 The seventh MANU, or the MANU of the present period.<BR>4 The planet Saturn.<BR>E.<BR>विवस्वत् the sun, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Nuptial, matrimonial, relating to marriage.<BR>E.<BR>विवाह marriage, ठक् aff. of reference or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशद्य|वैशद्यं
वैशद्य<BR>n. (-द्यं)<BR>1 Whiteness.<BR>2 Cleanness, purity.<BR>E.<BR>विशद white, &c., and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशंपायनः|वैशम्पायनः
वैशम्पायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sage, the original teacher of the Yajur Veda, and narrator of the Mahābhārata to JANAMEJAYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस|वैशसं
वैशस<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Hindrance, impediment.<BR>2 Slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्र|वैशस्त्रं
वैशस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 Government. sway, rule.<BR>2 The state of being disarmed or defenceless.<BR>E.<BR>विशस्तृ ruling, अञ् aff., and the pen. vowel changed, or वि privative, शस्र a weapon, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाख|वैशाखं|वैशाखः
वैशाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 The month in which the moon is full near the southern scale, (April-May,) the first month in the Hindu calendar.<BR>2 A churning stick.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>The day of full moon in the month Vaiśākha.<BR>E.<BR>विशाखा the constellation in which the moon is full this month, अण् aff. or विशाखा said to mean here, pervading, revolving, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Harlotry, allurement of harlots.<BR>E.<BR>वेश्या, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The Vaiśeṣika doctrine, or branch of the Nyāya or logical school of philosophy, instituted by KAṆĀDA.<BR>E.<BR>विशष difference, (from the original Nyāya of GAUTAMA,) ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्टा
वैशिष्टा<BR>n. (-ष्ट्यं)<BR>1 Endowment with, possession of.<BR>2 Distinction.<BR>E.<BR>विशिष्ट, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्य|वैशेष्यं
वैशेष्य<BR>n. (-ष्यं)<BR>1 Specific or generic distinction.<BR>2 Superiority, pre-eminence.<BR>E.<BR>विशेष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्य|वैश्यः
वैश्य<BR>m. (-श्यः)<BR>The Vaiśya, or man of the third or agricultural and mercantile tribe.<BR>f. (-श्या)<BR>A woman of the Vaiśya caste.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, (fields, &c.) क्विप् aff., and यञ pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यक्रिया
वैश्यक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>1 Trade, agriculture.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्य, and क्रिया act, business; also वैश्यकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यवृत्ति
वैश्यवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Agriculture or trade.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्य, and वृत्ति subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवण|वैश्रवणः
वैश्रवण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>विश्रवस् the father of the deity, aff. अण्, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणालय|वैश्रवणालयः
वैश्रवणालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्रवण KUVERA, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणावास|वैश्रवणावासः
वैश्रवणावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्रवण KUVERA, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणोदय|वैश्रवणोदयः
वैश्रवणोदय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्रवण KUVERA, and उदय prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Sacred or dedicated to the Viśvadevas, offered to them, relating to them, &c.<BR>2 Relating to all divinities.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Offering to all the divinities.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Species of the Paṅkti metre.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वदेव, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवकर्म्मन्|वैश्वदेवकर्मन्
वैश्वदेवकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्मा)<BR>Oblation or offering to the deities collectively.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्वदेव, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवहोम
वैश्वदेवहोम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Oblation to the Viśvadevas.<BR>E.<BR>वैश्वदेव, and होम burnt-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानर|वैश्वानरः
वैश्वानर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Relating to, fit for, &c. all men.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>AGNI or fire.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A particular sacrifice to be performed at the beginning of every year.<BR>E.<BR>विश्वानर a Muni, or विश्व all, नर mankind, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वी
वैश्वी<BR>f. (-श्वी)<BR>The second of the constellations called Āṣārhā, and twenty-first of the whole.<BR>E.<BR>विश्व a Viśvadeva, अण् and ङीष् aff.; those deities presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषम्य|वैषम्यं
वैषम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>1 Inequality, unevenness.<BR>2 Solitariness, singleness.<BR>3 Difficult.<BR>E.<BR>विषम odd, uneven, &c., aff. ष्यञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषयिक|वैषयिकः
वैषयिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sensualist, one addicted to the pleasures of sense.<BR>3 One occupied with worldly objects or interests.<BR>E.<BR>विषय an object of sense, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्टुत|वैष्टुतं
वैष्टुत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR>E.<BR>वि before स्तु to praise, aff. क्त, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्ट्र|वैष्ट्रं|वैष्ट्रः
वैष्ट्र<BR>n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>A world.<BR>E.<BR>विश to enter, ष्ट्रन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णव|वैष्णवं|वैष्णवः
वैष्णव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Relating or belonging to VIṢṆU.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A follower of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>1 One of the Mātṛs, the personified energy or Śakti of VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>3 A flower, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>4 Sacred basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>E.<BR>विष्णु VIṢṆU, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसारिन
वैसारिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, णिनि aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसूचन|वैसूचनं
वैसूचन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A man's assuming female attire, (in the drama.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before सूच to make known, क्युच् aff., and अण added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=812" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहासिक|वैहासिकः
वैहासिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A comic^1 actor, a buffoon, an actor.<BR>E.<BR>वि before हास laughter, mirth, aff. ठञ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोटा
वोटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>A female servant or slave.<BR>E.<BR>पुट to contract, aff. अच्, and व being substituted for प, perhaps more correctly वोटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्र|वोड्रः
वोड्र<BR>m. (-ड्रः)<BR>1 A large snake, (Bor or Boa Constrictor.)<BR>2 A sort of fish.<BR>f. (-ड्री)<BR>The fourth part of a Paṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढव्य|वोढव्यः
वोढव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be borne or carried.<BR>2 Able to bear or carry.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, तव्यर् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढु|वोढुः
वोढु<BR>m. (-ढुः)<BR>The son of a woman living in her father's house, and whose husband is absent.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, उ aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढृ
वोढृ<BR>m. (-ढा)<BR>1 A bridegroom.<BR>2 A porter, a bearer.<BR>3 A charioteer.<BR>4 A bull.<BR>5 A guide, a leader.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, aff. तृच्, ह changed to ढ, and ओ substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोण्ट|वोंट|वोंटः|वोण्टः
वोण्ट<BR>m. (-ण्टः)<BR>A stalk, a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोद|वोदः
वोद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Wet, moist, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोदाल|वोदालः
वोदाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sheat fish, (Silurus Boalis, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोर
वोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR>E.<BR>Apparently not a Sanscrit word, though occurring in regular compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरक|वोरकः
वोरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A scribe, a writer.<BR>E.<BR>see वोलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरट|वोरटः
वोरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A sort of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरपट्टी
वोरपट्टी<BR>f. (-ट्टी)<BR>A sort of mat or mattress^1 for sleeping on.<BR>E.<BR>वोर Dolichos catjang, and पट्टी coarse cloth; perhaps made of the straw.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरव|वोरवः
वोरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A kind of rice, perhaps that called Boro, which is cut in March or April.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरुखान|वोरुखानः
वोरुखान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A horse, described as of a white and red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल|वोलं|वोलः
वोल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, to smell, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोलक|वोलकः
वोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A scribe.<BR>f. (-लिका)<BR>A sort of cake or pudding made with flower and sugar.<BR>E.<BR>वा to go, and उलच् aff., and कन् added; also ल being changed to र, वोरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लह
वोल्लह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A horse, with light mane and tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोहित्थ|वोहित्थं|वोहित्थः
वोहित्थ<BR>n. (-त्थं)<BR>A vessel, a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौषट्
वौषट्<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation used on offering an oblation to the gods or manes.<BR>E.<BR>वह to bear, (what is borne by this,) and डौषट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशक|व्यंशकः
व्यंशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>E.<BR>वि various, अंश part, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशुक|व्यंशुकः
व्यंशुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Undressed, naked.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., and अंशुक a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसक|व्यंसकः
व्यंसक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cheat, a rogue, a juggler.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अंस to divide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसन|व्यंसनं
व्यंसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cheating, tricking, deceiving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अंस to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसनीय
व्यंसनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be deceived or cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अंस to divide, अनीयर् aff.; also व्यंसितव्य and व्यंस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसित|व्यंसितः
व्यंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Deceived, tricked, cheated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अंस to divide, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्त|व्यक्तः
व्यक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Wise, learned.<BR>2 Evident, manifest, apparent, absolutely and specifically known or understood.<BR>3 Individual, specific.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्ज to make clear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तत्व
व्यक्तत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Distinctness, manifestation.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also व्यक्तता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तदृष्टार्थ|व्यक्तदृष्टार्थः
व्यक्तदृष्टार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>Perceiving, understanding, present.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्त evident, दृष्ट seen, अर्थ meaning or object, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तराशि|व्यक्तराशिः
व्यक्तराशि<BR>f. (-शिः)<BR>Known or absolute quantity, (in arithmetic^1)<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्त, and राशि quantity.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तलक्ष्मन्
व्यक्तलक्ष्मन्<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मा-क्ष्म)<BR>Evident by certain signs or marks, manifested, characterised.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्त, and लक्ष्मन् a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ति|व्यक्तिः
व्यक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Individuality, specific appearance or being.<BR>2 Appearance, manifestation.<BR>3 Case, inflexion, or the proper form of any inflected word.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अघ to make clear, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तिता
व्यक्तिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Individuality.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to व्यक्ति; also with त्व, व्यक्तित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीकरण
व्यक्तीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Making distinct or manifest.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्ति, and करण making, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीकृत
व्यक्तीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made clear or manifest.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्ति, and कृत made, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीभूत
व्यक्तीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distinct, clear.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्त, and भूत become, च्चि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तोदित
व्यक्तोदित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Manifested, displayed.<BR>2 Spoken plainly.<BR>E.<BR>व्यक्त, and उदित risen or said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्र|व्यग्रः
व्यग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>1 Bewildered, perplexed, distracted.<BR>2 Alarmed, agitated, frightened.<BR>3 Engaged in, zealous, eager.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अग्र chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्रता
व्यग्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Perplexity, anxiety.<BR>2 Zeal.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, व्यग्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग|व्यंग|व्यङ्गः
व्यङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>1 Deformed, lame.<BR>2 Bodiless.<BR>3 Ill-arranged.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A frog.<BR>2 A cripple.<BR>3 Discoloration of the face, dark spots on the cheek.<BR>E.<BR>वि depreciative, &c., अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गार
व्यङ्गार<BR>mfn. (-र;-रा-रं)<BR>Having no fire alight.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., अङ्गार hot coals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गुल|व्यंगुल|व्यंगुलं
व्यङ्गुल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The 60th part of a digit or Aṅgula.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अङ्गुल a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग्य|व्यंग्य|व्यङ्ग्यः
व्यङ्ग्य<BR>m. (-ङ्ग्यः)<BR>1 Figurative or poetical speech, elliptical language or that which conveys something more than the simple meaning of the words.<BR>2 Sarcasm, the covert but intelligible expression of suspicion or contempt.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्च to make clear or manifest, घञ् aff., and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच
व्यच<BR>r. 6th cl. (व्यचति)<BR>To cheat, to trick, to defraud or deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यज|व्यजः
व्यज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A fan.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अज to go, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजन|व्यजनं
व्यजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A fan.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अज to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जक|व्यंजक|व्यञ्जकः
व्यञ्जक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 External indication of passion or feeling.<BR>2 A sign, a mark, a symbol.<BR>3 Figurative or elliptical expression.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्ज to manifest, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जकत्व
व्यञ्जकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>The nature or existence of figurative or poetical expression.<BR>E.<BR>व्यञ्जक, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जन|व्यंजन|व्यंजनं|व्यञ्जनं
व्यञ्जन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A mark, a spot, a sign, a token.<BR>2 Paraphernalia, insignia.<BR>3 The beard.<BR>4 A privy part, either male or female.<BR>5 Sauce, condiment.<BR>6 A consonant.<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Figurative expression.<BR>2 Irony, sarcasm.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्ज to make clear or evident, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जनावृत्ति|व्यञ्जनावृत्तिः
व्यञ्जनावृत्ति,<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>Rhetorical or elliptical style.<BR>E.<BR>व्यञ्जना, and वृत्ति style.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जयत्
व्यञ्जयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Making visible or manifest.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अञ्ज to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=813" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जित|व्यंजित
व्यञ्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Distinguished, characterised.<BR>2 Manifested, visible.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्ज to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जिजिषु
व्यञ्जिजिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Wishing or trying to expose, detect. make manifest, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अञ्ज to go, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यडम्बक|व्यडंबक|व्यडंबकः|व्यडम्बकः
व्यडम्बक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The castor oil plant, (Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before अड to strive, aff. अच्, व्यड here said to mean excretion, अवि to go, to cause, ण्वुल् aff.; form irr.; also with युच् aff. व्यडम्बन m. (-नः) and by another reading, व्यडम्बर; other etymologies are given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
व्यतिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Reciprocal, acting on or with one another.<BR>2 Pervading, who or what spreads through or over.<BR>3 Contiguous to, in contact with.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>2 Reciprocity, reciprocal action or relation.<BR>3 Reverse.<BR>4 Contact, contiguity.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before कृ to make, to do, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम|व्यतिक्रमः
व्यतिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Inverted or retrograde order, inversion, reverse.<BR>2 Contrariety, opposition in general; as the contrary of what is right or wrong, crime, vice; the contrary of prosperity, adversity, misfortune, &c.<BR>3 Retraction, non-performance, (as of contracts.)<BR>4 Passing over or beyond.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before क्रम to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रान्त|व्यतिक्रांत
व्यतिक्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>Reversed, inverted.<BR>2 Retracted.<BR>3 Passed over.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before क्रम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिक्त|व्यतिरिक्तः
व्यतिरिक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Different, distinct.<BR>2 Excepted.<BR>3 Withdrawn, withheld.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before रिच to unite, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक|व्यतिरेकः
व्यतिरेक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Difference, separateness.<BR>2 A figure in rhetoric, the dissimilitude of things compared in some respects to each other.<BR>3 Exception, exclusion.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before रिच to unite, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति
व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>Comprehensive argument derived from negatives or non-existence.<BR>E.<BR>व्यतिरेक, and व्याप्ति pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकिन्
व्यतिरेकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किणी-कि)<BR>1 Different, reverse.<BR>2 Excepting. distinguishing.<BR>E.<BR>व्यतिरेक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक्युदाहरण
व्यतिरेक्युदाहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Illustration by contrast or negatives.<BR>E.<BR>व्यतिरेकिन्, and उदाहरण example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषक्त
व्यतिषक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Mutually connected, joined, related, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before षञ्ज to embrace, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्ग|व्यतिषंग|व्यतिषंगः|व्यतिषङ्गः
व्यतिषङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Mutual or reciprocal junction or relation.<BR>2 Fastening, tying together.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before षञ्ज to embrace, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्गवत्
व्यतिषङ्गवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Connected, united, mixed.<BR>E.<BR>व्यतिषङ्ग, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहार|व्यतिहारः
व्यतिहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Barter, exchange.<BR>2 Exchange of blows or abuse.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before हृ to take, aff. घञ्; also व्यतीहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीत|व्यतीतः
व्यतीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Past, gone.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अतीत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीपात|व्यतीपातः
व्यतीपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Great and portentous calamity, or a portent, indicating or occasioning it and therefore identified with it, as a comet, an earthquake, &c.<BR>2 Disrespect, contempt.<BR>3 The seventeenth of the astrological Yogas.<BR>4 Day of new moon when it falls on a Sunday, and the moon is in certain mansions, Śravaṇā, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अति before पत to fall, &c., aff. घञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहार|व्यतीहारः
व्यतीहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Barter, exchange.<BR>2 Exchange of blows or abuse.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अति implying reciprocity, हृ to take, aff. घञ्, and इ optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यय|व्यत्ययः
व्यत्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR>2 Inverted or retrograde order.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अति before इ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्त
व्यत्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Reversed, inverted, contrary, opposite.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अति before अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यास|व्यत्यासः
व्यत्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR>2 Inverted or retrograde order.<BR>3 Reversed position.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अति before अस to throw or send, aff. ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ
व्यथ<BR>r. 1st cl. (व्यथते)<BR>1 To fear.<BR>2 To be disquieted or unhappy.<BR>3 To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथक|व्यथकः
व्यथक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Inflicting pain, torturing, painful.<BR>2 Distressing, afflicting.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to give pain, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथन|व्यथनं
व्यथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Giving pain, paining.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथनीय
व्यथनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be put to pain, what may be or ought to be pained.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ, and अनीयर् aff.; also व्यथ्य and व्यथितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथयत्
व्यथयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Paining, distressing.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to pain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथा
व्यथा<BR>f. (-था)<BR>1 Pain.<BR>2 Distress.<BR>3 Alarm, fear.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to fear, to suffer pain, &c., aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथाकर
व्यथाकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Painful, excruciating.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथा, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथारहित
व्यथारहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Free from pain.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथा, and रहित quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथित|व्यथितः
व्यथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pained, tortured.<BR>2 Distressed, afflicted.<BR>3 Disturbed, troubled.<BR>4 Alarmed, frightened.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथा pain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्यमान
व्यथ्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Being agitated, distressed, pained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्यथ to suffer pain, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध|व्यधः
व्यध<BR>r. 4th cl. (औ) औव्यध (विध्यति)<BR>To beat, to strike, to pierce, to tear, to hurt or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यघ
व्यघ<BR>m. (-घः)<BR>1 Perforating, piercing.<BR>2 Striking, smiting.<BR>E.<BR>व्यघ to strike, to hurt, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यघन
व्यघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Piercing, perforating.<BR>E.<BR>व्यघ to pierce, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यघित
व्यघित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made, done, caused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्य|व्यध्यः
व्यध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>To be pierced or wounded.<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>A butt, a mark to shoot at.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्व|व्यध्वः
व्यध्व<BR>m. (-ध्वः)<BR>A bad road.<BR>E.<BR>वि depreciative, अध्वन् a road, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनाद|व्यनुनादः
व्यनुनाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Reverberation, loud and extending sound or noise.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अनु before नद to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनादयत्
व्यनुनादयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Causing to reverberate, filling with sound or noise.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अनु before नद to sound, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यप
व्यप<BR>r. 10th cl. (व्यापयति)<BR>To diminish, to lessen, to decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगत
व्यपगत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, gone away.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अप before गम to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगम|व्यपगमः
व्यपगम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Going away, departure.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अप before गम to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रपमाण
व्यपत्रपमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Ashamed.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अपत्रप to be shameless, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=814" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिष्ट
व्यपदिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Named.<BR>2 Informed.<BR>3 Tricked.<BR>4 Pleaded in excuse.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before दिश to show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेश|व्यपदेशः
व्यपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 Dishonesty, fraud, craft.<BR>2 Stratagem, device.<BR>3 Name, appellation.<BR>4 Information, notice, apprising.<BR>5 Hint.<BR>6 Excuse, pretext.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before दिश to show, aff. धञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेष्टृ
व्यपदेष्टृ<BR>mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्ट)<BR>1 Deceiving, a cheat.<BR>2 One who shows, names, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before दिश to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनीत
व्यपनीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taken away, removed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before नीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपण|व्यपरोपणं
व्यपरोपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Extirpating, expelling.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before रुह to grow, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपित
व्यपरोपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Extirpated, eradicated, expelled.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before रुह to grow, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृति|व्यपाकृतिः
व्यपाकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Repelling, denial.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अप implying opposition, and आङ् before कृ to make, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रय|व्यपाश्रयः
व्यपाश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Taking refuge with, relying upon, trusting to.<BR>2 Expectation.<BR>E.<BR>वि, अप and आङ् before श्री to serve, aff. अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित
व्यपाश्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having taken refuge with, relying upon, trusting to, who or what does so.<BR>E.<BR>वि, अप and आङ् before श्री to serve, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित्य
व्यपाश्रित्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having sought or taken refuge with.<BR>E.<BR>वि, अप, and आङ् before श्री to serve, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष
व्यपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Expectant, waiting, attentive.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before ईक्ष to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षण|व्यपेक्षणं
व्यपेक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Expecting, looking for.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before ईक्ष to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षणीय
व्यपेक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be expected or looked for.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before ईक्ष to see, अनीयर् aff.; also व्यपेक्ष्य and व्यपक्षितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षा
व्यपेक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 Expectation, especially if reciprocal.<BR>2 Mutual connexion or relation.<BR>3 Application, use.<BR>4 (In grammar,) the mutual application of two rules.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, अपेक्षा looking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षित
व्यपेक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Looked to reciprocally.<BR>2 Mutually related.<BR>3 Employed, applied.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अपेक्षित expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेत
व्यपेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Gone, passed away, got rid of.<BR>2 Opposed, contrary.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before इ to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोढ
व्यपोढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Opposite, contrary, reverse.<BR>2 Driven off or away.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अप before वह to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्य
व्यपोह्य<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having driven away, got rid of.<BR>2 Having passed through a place.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अप before वह to convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचार|व्यभिचारः
व्यभिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Following improper courses, doing what is prohibited or wicked.<BR>2 Erring, straying, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>3 Wandering from an argument.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अभि before चर to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिन्
व्यभिचारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Following or doing what is improper.<BR>2 Going astray, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>A property, or class of properties into which feelings and emotions, as objects of poetical description, are classed: the Bhāvas called Vyabhicāris are thirty-two in number, to which two others are sometimes added, making thirty-four, viz.<BR>1 Nirveda, humility, self-abasement;<BR>2 Glāni, weakness, exhaustion;<BR>3 Śaṅkā, apprehension;<BR>4 Asūyā, calumny;<BR>5 Mada, inebriety;<BR>6 Śrama, fatigue;<BR>7 Ālasya, indolence;<BR>8 Dainya, indigence, distress;<BR>9 Cintā, secret desire, contemplation of the object beloved;<BR>10 Moha, loss of sense or presence of mind from fear, anxiety, &c.;<BR>11 Smṛti, recollection, but especially the recollection of an absent or faithless lover excited by present objects;<BR>12 Dhṛti, the enjoyment or consciousness of amatory woe, resignation or abandonment to despair, &c.;<BR>13 Vrīḍā, shame;<BR>14 Capalatā, fickleness, unsteadiness, want of firmness and steadiness;<BR>15 Harṣa, delight;<BR>16 Avega, hurry, flurried haste;<BR>17 Jaraṭha, ignorance, imbecility;<BR>18 Garva, pride, arrogance;<BR>19 Viṣāda, want of energy or spirits, depression of mind;<BR>20 Autsukya, regret, painful remembrance of some object lost or absent;<BR>21 Nidrā, sluggishness, sleepiness;<BR>22 Apasmāra, epilepsy;<BR>23 Supta, sleep;<BR>24 Vibodha, waking;<BR>25 Amarṣa, wrathful impatience;<BR>26 Avahittha, dissimulation;<BR>27 Ugratā, passion, rage;<BR>28 Mati, intelligence, knowledge;<BR>29 Upālambha, reviling, railing;<BR>20 Vyādhi, sickness, disease;<BR>21 Unmada, madness, delirium;<BR>22 Maraṇa, death; the other two are,<BR>23 Trāsa, fear;<BR>24 Vitarka, doubt, deliberation.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>A wanton woman, an unchaste wife.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अभि before चर to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभ्र
व्यभ्र<BR>mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं)<BR>Unclouded.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., अभ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय<BR>r. 1st cl. (व्ययति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR>r. 10th cl. (व्यययति)<BR>1 To lessen, to diminish.<BR>2 To send.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्ययते व्यययति)<BR>To expend, to disburse, to abandon wealth, to give away money, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Expenditure, spending.<BR>2 Destruction, disappearance.<BR>3 Misfortune, downfall^1, decline.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय to expend, &c., aff. अच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययन|व्ययनं
व्ययन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Spending.<BR>2 Destroying.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययमान
व्ययमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Spending, expending.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय to spend, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययित|व्ययितः
व्ययित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expended, spent.<BR>2 Gone, dissipated, dispersed.<BR>3 Declined, fallen into decay.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय to expend, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययिन्
व्ययिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Spending.<BR>2 Declining, falling into calamity.<BR>3 Wasting, decaying.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीकरण
व्ययीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Expending, wasting.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय, and करण making, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीकृत
व्ययीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Expended, spent, wasted.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीभूत
व्ययीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spent, wasted.<BR>E.<BR>व्यय, and भत been, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्ण|व्यर्ण्ण
व्यर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Asked.<BR>2 Gone.<BR>E.<BR>अर्द्द to ask, with वि prefix, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थ|व्यर्थं
व्यर्थ<BR>mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>1 Useless, vain, unprofitable.<BR>2 Unmeaning.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and अर्थ meaning, object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थक
व्यर्थक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Vain, useless.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थकता
व्यर्थकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR>E.<BR>व्यर्थक, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थता
व्यर्थता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR>2 Absence of meaning, nonsense.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to अर्थ; also with त्व, व्यर्थत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=815" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीक|व्यलीकं|व्यलीकः
व्यलीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Disagreeable, displeasing, offensive.<BR>2 Improper, unfit to be done.<BR>3 Painful.<BR>4 Strange.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Pain, torture.<BR>2 Fault, transgression.<BR>3 Any thing displeasing.<BR>4 Any improper act.<BR>5 Reverse.<BR>6 Cheating, tricking.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A catamite.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अल to be able or to adorn, aff. ईकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीकता
व्यलीकता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Impropriety.<BR>2 Disagreeableness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also व्यलीकत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलन|व्यवकलनं
व्यवकलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Subtraction.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अव before कल to reckon, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलित|व्यवकलितः
व्यवकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subtracted, deducted.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Subtraction.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before कल to count, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवक्रोशन|व्यवक्रोशनं
व्यवक्रोशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Wrangling, altercation, mutual abuse.<BR>2 Abuse, reviling.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before क्रुश to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवछिन्न|व्यवच्छिन्न|व्यवच्छिन्नं
व्यवछिन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Different, separate, divided.<BR>2 Distinguished, discriminated.<BR>3 Cut in pieces.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before छिद to cut, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवछेद|व्यवच्छेद|व्यवच्छेदः
व्यवछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Dividing, separating.<BR>2 A division.<BR>3 Discrimination.<BR>4 Contrast, distinction.<BR>5 Letting fly an arrow, shooting, darting.<BR>6 Cutting in pieces.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before छिद to cut, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवतिष्ठमान
व्यवतिष्ठमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Arranged, placed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्थ to stay, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>1 A covering, a screen, any thing which holds or conceals from sight.<BR>2 The state of being covered, concealment, disappearance.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before धा to have, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधान|व्यवधानं
व्यवधान<BR>m. (-नं)<BR>1 Covering, disappearance, either the thing which conceals, or the state of being concealed from sight.<BR>2 Intervening, intervention, space.<BR>3 The intervention of a letter, (in grammar.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before धा to have, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधायक|व्यवधायकः
व्यवधायक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Concealing, screening, hiding.<BR>2 Intervening, intermediate, separating.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before धा to have, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधि|व्यवधिः
व्यवधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Covering, or a covering: see व्यवघान.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before धा to have, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसाय|व्यवसायः
व्यवसाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Effort, exertion, persevering or industrious effort, perseverance, industry.<BR>2 Following any business or profession.<BR>3 Plan, device, trick.<BR>4 Resolve, determination.<BR>5 Boasting.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before षो to destroy, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायात्मिक
व्यवसायात्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Laborious, relating to exertion.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवसाय, and आत्मन् self, with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायिन्
व्यवसायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Active, energetic, persevering, resolute.<BR>2 Engaged in business.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवसाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसित|व्यवसितः
व्यवसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Tricked, cheated.<BR>2 Energetic, taking pains, making effort or exertion.<BR>3 Resolved, determined.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before षो to destroy, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>1 Separating, placing remote or apart.<BR>2 Placing or staying in or on.<BR>3 A decree, a written declaration of the law; applied in practice to the written extracts from the codes of law, stated as the opinions of the Hindu law officers attached to the courts of justice.<BR>4 An engagement, an agreement, a contract.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्था to stay or be, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिक्रम|व्यवस्थातिक्रमः
व्यवस्थातिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Breaking an agreement or contract.<BR>2 Disregarding the law.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवस्था, and अतिक्रम transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तन|व्यवस्थातिवर्तन
व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Breaking an agreement or contract.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवस्था, and अतिवर्त्तन transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तिन्|व्यवस्थातिवर्तिन्
व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तिन्<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>One who does not keep an engagement, perform a contract, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवस्था, and अतिवर्त्तिन् going from or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापन|व्यवस्थापनं
व्यवस्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Declaring, deciding, laying down as law.<BR>2 Fixing, determining.<BR>3 Appointing.<BR>4 Placing apart.<BR>5 Placing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापित
व्यवस्थापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Declared, determined.<BR>2 Caused to be placed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्था to stay, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थित|व्यवस्थितः
व्यवस्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Separated, distant.<BR>2 Excerpted, extracted.<BR>3 Invariable, constant.<BR>4 Appointed.<BR>5 Declared, decreed.<BR>6 Staying, or fixed in or on.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्था to be, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थिति|व्यवस्थितिः
व्यवस्थिति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Constancy, perseverance.<BR>2 Determining, appointing.<BR>3 Extracting.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्त्तव्य|व्यवहर्तव्य
व्यवहर्त्तव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be litigated or decided judicially.<BR>2 To be done or transacted.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before हृ to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्त्तृ|व्यवहर्तृ
व्यवहर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तृ-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Transacting business, engaged in affairs.<BR>2 Observing or following established usages.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>1 A judge, an umpire, one conducting a judicial procedure.<BR>2 A litigant, a plaintiff, one instituting a dispute at law.<BR>3 Partaker, associate.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before हृ to take, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार|व्यवहारः
व्यवहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The practice of the courts, or civil and criminal law, judicial procedure, administrative justice, as the examination of evidence, &c.<BR>2 Title of jurisprudence, any act cognizable in courts of justice.<BR>3 Contest at law, law suit, litigation.<BR>4 Usage, custom.<BR>5 Profession, business.<BR>6 Steadiness, propriety, adherence to law and custom.<BR>7 A contract.<BR>8 A sort of tree.<BR>9 Mathematical or arithmetical determination or ascertainment.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and अव implying dissension, and हृ to take, aff. घञ्, the term being explained to mean especially, a dispute between two parties, or the counter-statements of plaintiff and defendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारज्ञ|व्यवहारज्ञः
व्यवहारज्ञ<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>A person who has passed his minority, a young man of age, or one who has passed his sixteenth year, at which period he can assert his own rights in a court of law.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार a law suit, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारदर्शन|व्यवहारदर्शनं
व्यवहारदर्शन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Judicial investigation, trial.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार legal proceeding, and दर्शन seeing, inspecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपद|व्यवहारपदं
व्यवहारपद<BR>n. (-दः)<BR>A title of jurisprudence, any act cognizable in a court of law: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and पद object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपाद|व्यवहारपादः
व्यवहारपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A division of legal proceedings, one of the four parts which are necessary to conduct a regular suit, or the plaint, the defence, the proof, and the decision.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार a law suit, and पाद a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=816" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारप्राप्त
व्यवहारप्राप्त<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A youth who has come of age.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारमातृका
व्यवहारमातृका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Legal procedure or process in general, simple judicature, law as in all ordinary cases administered.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार legal contest, and मातृका parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारमार्ग|व्यवहारमार्गः
व्यवहारमार्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>A title of jurisprudence: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and मार्ग road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविधि|व्यवहारविधिः
व्यवहारविधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Law, the law, the precepts or code by which judicature is to be regulated and decisions to be made.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार legal process, and विधि a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविषय|व्यवहारविषयः
व्यवहारविषय<BR>mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>A title of jurisprudence, an act which may become the object of dispute amongst men, and should therefore be regulated by law; according to MANU, there are eighteen heads, but these are the principal only, and many things not comprised under them may still be actionable; the eighteen are:<BR>1 ऋणादानं debt;<BR>2 निक्षेपः deposit;<BR>3 अस्वामिविक्रयः sale without ownership;<BR>4 सम्भूयसमुत्थानं concerns amongst partners;<BR>5 दत्तस्यानपकर्म्म subtraction of what has been given;<BR>6 वेतनादानं non-payment of wages;<BR>7 सम्विद्व्यतिक्रमः non-performance of agreement;<BR>8 क्रयविक्रयानुशयः rescission of sale and purchase;<BR>9 स्वामिपालयोर्विवादः disputes between master and servant;<BR>10 सीमाविवादः disputes about boundaries;<BR>11 वाक्पारुष्यं defamation, abuse;<BR>12 दण्डपारुष्यं assault;<BR>13 स्तेयं theft, larceny;<BR>14 साहसं robbery, and other violence;<BR>15 स्त्रीसंग्रहणं adultery;<BR>16 स्त्रीपुंधर्म्मः duties of man and wife;<BR>17 विभागः portioning of property, inheritance;<BR>18 द्यूतं gambling of any kind, as fighting animals, laying wagers, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार legal process, and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारस्थान|व्यवहारस्थानं
व्यवहारस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A title of jurisprudence: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार legal procedure, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहाराभिशस्त
व्यवहाराभिशस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Prosecuted, accused, proceeded against legally.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and अभिशस्त accused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारायोग्य|व्यवहारायोग्यः
व्यवहारायोग्य<BR>mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>Unfitted or unsuited to legal proceedings.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>1 A minor.<BR>2 One incompetent to conduct business.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and अयोग्य unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Customary, usual.<BR>2 Engaged in customary duty or avocation.<BR>3 Connected with or relating to legal process.<BR>4 Litigant, being party to a suit.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिका
व्यवहारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Usage, custom.<BR>2 A brush, a broom.<BR>3 A plant, commonly Ingua.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to व्यवहार, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिन्
व्यवहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Litigant, litigating, engaged in a law suit.<BR>2 Relating to legal process.<BR>3 Customary, usual.<BR>4 Following one's ordinary affairs or avocation.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार्य्य|व्यवहार्य|व्यवहार्य्यः
व्यवहार्य्य<BR>mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>1 To be observed or practised, as a duty or avocation, customary, usual.<BR>2 Actionable, subject to legal process.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before हृ to take or convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहास
व्यवहास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Mutual laughter.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before हस to laugh, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्यवहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Placed or situated contiguously to, attached or adhering to, &c.<BR>2 Intervening, separating.<BR>3 Covered, concealed.<BR>4 Excelled, surpassed, put to shame.<BR>5 Done, acted, performed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before धा to have or hold, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवाय|व्यवायं|व्यवायः
व्यवाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 Copulation.<BR>2 Covering, disappearance.<BR>3 Purity.<BR>4 Interval, space.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Light, lustre.<BR>E.<BR>वि and अव before इण to go, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायिन्
व्यवायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>1 Lecherous.<BR>2 Pervading, diffusive.<BR>m. (-यी)<BR>1 A lecher, a libertine.<BR>2 A drug, an aphrodisiac.<BR>2 Any article that produces general excitement, as wine, poison, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवाय copulation, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्नुवान
व्यश्नुवान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Occupying, pervading.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अश to pervade, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसन|व्यसनं
व्यसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Calamity, misfortune.<BR>2 Fate.<BR>3 Fault, vice, crime, frailty, arising from desire, or from anger; ten vices or faults are enumerated under the first head, or hunting, gambling, sleeping in the day, calumny, whoring, dancing, singing, playing, idle roaming, and drinking: the second comprehends eight, depravity, violence, injury, envy, malice, fraud, abuse, and assault.<BR>4 Sin.<BR>5 Fated consequence.<BR>6 Evil destiny, ill luck.<BR>7 Fruitless effort.<BR>8 Incompetence, inability.<BR>9 Intent, application or attachment to an object.<BR>10 Falling.<BR>11 Air, wind.<BR>12 Individuality.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अस to throw, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनप्रहारिन्
व्यसनप्रहारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Troublesome, giving trouble or pain.<BR>E.<BR>व्यसन, and प्रहारिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनार्त्तं|व्यसनार्त|व्यसनार्त्त|व्यसनार्त्तः
व्यसनार्त्तं<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Afflicted, suffering pain or calamity.<BR>E.<BR>व्यसन misfortune, and आर्त्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिता
व्यसनिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Wickedness.<BR>2 Calamity.<BR>E.<BR>व्यसनिन्, and तल् aff.; also त्व, व्यसनित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिन्
व्यसनिन्<BR>mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>1 Addicted to evil practices, as to gaming, drinking, wenching, &c.<BR>2 Calamitous, unfortunate.<BR>E.<BR>व्यसन vice, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनीय
व्यसनीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A profligate, a debauchee.<BR>E.<BR>व्यसन, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसु
व्यसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>Inanimate, lifeless.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्त|व्यस्तः
व्यस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Confounded, confused, bewildered.<BR>2 Pervaded, penetrated, spread.<BR>3 Present and essential, or inherent in all the parts of any thing, in opposition to the Samasta, or that which pervades the whole together.<BR>4 Reverse, inverse.<BR>5 Opposite.<BR>6 Opposed to, set or struck against.<BR>7 Tossed, thrown up, or about.<BR>8 Reversed, inverted.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, &c., अस to be or pervade, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तता
व्यस्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Agitation, bewilderment.<BR>2 Severalty, individuality.<BR>3 Inherence.<BR>E.<BR>व्यस्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, व्यस्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तपद|व्यस्तपदं
व्यस्तपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 Perplexed and indistinct statement, want of precision in an accusation or defence, (in law.)<BR>2 (In grammar,) A simple or uncompounded word.<BR>E.<BR>व्यस्त perplexed, पद a sentence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तविधि|व्यस्तविधिः
व्यस्तविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>Inversion, rule for inversion.<BR>E.<BR>व्यस्त, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तार|व्यस्तारं|व्यस्तारः
व्यस्तार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The issue of the fluid from the temples of the elephant.<BR>E.<BR>व्यस्त pervaded, ऋ to go, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यह्न
व्यह्न<BR>mfn. (-ह्नः-ह्ना-ह्नं)<BR>Done or produced, &c. in two days.<BR>E.<BR>वि severally, and अह्नं for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरण|व्याकरणं
व्याकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Grammar.<BR>2 Explaining, expounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कृ to make or do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=817" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकार|व्याकारः
व्याकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Change of form.<BR>2 Deformity.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकीर्ण
व्याकीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>Scattered, tossed, or thrown about or away.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कॄ to scatter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुल|व्याकुलः
व्याकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Confounded, bewildered, perplexed, overcome with fear, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि before आकुल the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलता
व्याकुलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Perplexity, agitation, alarm.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, व्याकुलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलमनस्
व्याकुलमनस्<BR>mfn. (-नाः-ना-नः)<BR>Agitated, flurried, bewildered.<BR>E.<BR>व्याकुल, and मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलित
व्याकुलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Agitated, flurried, perplexed.<BR>E.<BR>व्याकुल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकूति|व्याकूतिः
व्याकूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Fraud, deception, disguise.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कू to sound, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृत
व्याकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Expounded, explained, made clear.<BR>2 Transformed, changed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कृ to make, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृति|व्याकृतिः
व्याकृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Explaining, making clear.<BR>2 Grammar.<BR>3 Change of form.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कृ to make, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोश|व्याकोशः
व्याकोश<BR>mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>Budded, blown.<BR>E.<BR>वि, and आङ् implying separation, कोश or कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोष|व्याकोषः
व्याकोष<BR>mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>Budded, blown, (as a flower.)<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या<BR>f. (-ख्या)<BR>Exposition, explanation, gloss, comment.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before ख्या to relate, aff. अङ् and टाप्; also with ल्युट् aff. व्याख्यान n. (-नं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यागम्य|व्याख्यागम्यं
व्याख्यागम्य<BR>n. (-म्यं)<BR>Indistinct averment, proceeding from grammatical inaccuracy or faulty construction.<BR>E.<BR>व्याख्या an explanation, and आगम्य to be attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यात|व्याख्यातः
व्याख्यात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Spoken, said.<BR>2 Conquered, overcome.<BR>3 Explained, expounded.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before ख्या to say, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यान|व्याख्यानं
व्याख्यान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Explaining, expounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before ख्या to say, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्येय
व्याख्येय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be explained or described.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before ख्या to say, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टन|व्याघट्टनं
व्याघट्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>2 Churning.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घट्ट to use effort, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टित
व्याघट्टित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Rubbed, rubbed together.<BR>2 Stirred, churned.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घट्ट to use effort, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघात|व्याघातः
व्याघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 Obstacle, impediment.<BR>2 Striking, beating.<BR>3 Destroying, destruction.<BR>4 The thirteenth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>5 A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>6 A rhetorical figure, the production of two different effects from a similar cause or by similar agency.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हन to strike, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातक
व्याघातक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what opposes, resists, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हन् to strike, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातिन्
व्याघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Who or what opposes, resists, beats, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हन to strike, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघारित
व्याघारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sprinkled, lubricated, (as with oil or ghee.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घृ^1 to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्र|व्याघ्रः
व्याघ्र<BR>m. (-घ्रः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 (In composition,) Best, pre-eminent.<BR>3 A variety of the castor oil plant.<BR>4 A tree, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>f. (-घ्री)<BR>A prickly sort of nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घ्रा to smell, Uṇādi aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रचर्म्मन्|व्याघ्रचर्मन्
व्याघ्रचर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>A tiger's skin.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र, and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रदल|व्याघ्रदलः
व्याघ्रदल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A red variety of the castor oil tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनख|व्याघ्रनखं|व्याघ्रनखः
व्याघ्रनख<BR>nf. (-खं-खी)<BR>1 A tiger's claw.<BR>2 A sort of perfume.<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>1 A kind of root.<BR>2 A scratch or impression of the finger nails.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र tiger, and नख a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनखक|व्याघ्रनखकं
व्याघ्रनखक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A scratch, the impression of a finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and नख a nail, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनायक|व्याघ्रनायकः
व्याघ्रनायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रपाद|व्याघ्रपादः
व्याघ्रपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A plant, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>2 A saint and lawgiver, so named from having feet like those of a tiger.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and पाद the foot or paw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रपुच्छ|व्याघ्रपुच्छः
व्याघ्रपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>The castor oil tree, (Palma Christi, or Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्राट|व्याघ्राटः
व्याघ्राट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A skylark.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रास्य|व्याघ्रास्यः
व्याघ्रास्य<BR>m. (-स्यः)<BR>A cat.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and आस्य the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याज|व्याजः
व्याज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Deceit, fraud, craft, cunning.<BR>2 Disguise, either of purpose or person.<BR>3 Wickedness.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अज to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजनिन्दा
व्याजनिन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Apparent censure, but covert praise, a figure of rhetoric.<BR>E.<BR>व्याज disguise, and निन्दा censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजस्तुति|व्याजस्तुतिः
व्याजस्तुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Praise or censure, conveyed in language that expresses the contrary, affected reproach or ironical commendation.<BR>E.<BR>व्याज disguise, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजोक्ति|व्याजोक्तिः
व्याजोक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Covert expression of any thing so as to mislead others from its real cause.<BR>E.<BR>व्याज craft or disguise, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याड|व्याडः
व्याड<BR>m. (-डः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A carnivorous animal or beast of prey.<BR>3 INDRA.<BR>4 A villain, a rogue.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अड to make effort, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडि|व्याडिः
व्याडि<BR>m. (-डिः)<BR>The name of a celebrated grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्त|व्यात्तं
व्यात्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Vast, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before अत to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्युक्षी
व्यात्युक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>Bathing for amusement, sporting in water.<BR>E.<BR>वि, आङ् and अति before उक्ष to sprinkle, aff. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादान|व्यादानं
व्यादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Opening, setting open or ajar.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before दा to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध|व्याधं|व्याधः
व्याध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 A hunter, one who lives by killing deer, &c.<BR>2 A low or wicked man.<BR>E.<BR>व्यध to pierce, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधभीत|व्याधभीतः
व्याधभीत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A deer.<BR>E.<BR>व्याध a hunter, and भीत afraid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाम|व्याधामः
व्याधाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before धा to have, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाव|व्याधावः
व्याधाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घू to tremble, causal form, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधि|व्याधिः
व्याधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease in general.<BR>2 Leprosy.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिकर
व्याधिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Causing sickness.<BR>E.<BR>व्याधि, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिघात|व्याधिघातः
व्याधिघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>E.<BR>व्याघि disease, हन to destroy, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिघ्न|व्याधिघ्नः
व्याधिघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Causing or removing disease.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघि, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=818" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधित|व्याधितः
व्याधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sick, ill, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>व्याधि sickness, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधियुक्त
व्याधियुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Sick, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघि, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिरहित
व्याधिरहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Free from disease, convalescent.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघि, and रहित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधुत|व्याधुतः
व्याधुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Shaken, shaking, trembling, tremulous.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before घु to shake, aff. क्त; also from घू with क्त, व्याधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध्युपशम
व्याध्युपशम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Allaying or curing disease.<BR>E.<BR>व्याघि, and उपशम allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यान|व्यानः
व्यान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>One of the five vital airs, that which is diffused throughout the body.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अन to breathe, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापक|व्यापकः
व्यापक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Diffusive, comprehensive, spreading or extending widely.<BR>2 (In law,) Comprehending all the points of an argument, pervading the whole plea.<BR>3 (In logic,) Embracing the whole of an argument or objection.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Essential and inherent property.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अप to pervade, ण्वुल् aff. implying the agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापकत्व
व्यापकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Diffusion, pervadence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last; also with तल्, व्यापकता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद्<BR>f. (-पद्)<BR>1 Death, decease.<BR>2 Calamity.<BR>3 Derangement.<BR>4 Disease.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन|व्यापनं
व्यापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Spreading through or throughout, pervading, penetrating.<BR>E.<BR>वि before आप to obtain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन्न|व्यापन्नः
व्यापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Dead, deceased, expired.<BR>2 Hurt, injured, killed.<BR>3 Deranged, disordered.<BR>4 Vitiated, diseased.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापाद|व्यापादः
व्यापाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Evil design, malice prepense, the wish or project to injure another person.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, causal form, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादन|व्यापादनं
व्यापादन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaying.<BR>2 Wishing or seeking to injure any one, ill-will, malice.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादयितव्य
व्यापादयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be killed, what may or ought to be put to death.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, causal v., तव्य aff.; also व्यापादनीय and व्यापाद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादित|व्यापादितः
व्यापादित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Hurt, injured.<BR>2 Slain, killed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पद to go, causal form, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादितवत्
व्यापादितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having killed, killing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ before पद to go, causal v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापिन्
व्यापिन्<BR>mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>Diffusive, comprehensive.<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>The pervading property or power, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आप to pervade, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापार|व्यापारः
व्यापार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Occupation, business, trade, profession.<BR>2 Exercise, practice.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारयत्
व्यापारयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Setting to work, employing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारिन्
व्यापारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Motor, motive, the cause or agent of motion or occupation.<BR>2 Busy, occupied.<BR>3 Exercising, practising.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, causal form, aff. णिनि or व्यापार business, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृत|व्यापृतः
व्यापृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Engaged, occupied, busy.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A minister, a member of royal government.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्त|व्याप्तं
व्याप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Pervaded, occupied (or penetrated by) thoroughly and essentially, (as the universe by spirit, &c.)<BR>2 Celebrated, famous.<BR>3 Filled, full.<BR>4 Placed, fixed.<BR>5 Obtained.<BR>6 Encircled, encompassed, surrounded.<BR>7 Open, apart, outspread, expanded.<BR>E.<BR>वि before आप to pervade, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्ति|व्याप्तिः
व्याप्ति<BR>f. (-प्तिः)<BR>1 Pervading, inherence, the inherent and essential presence of any one thing or property in another, as of oil in the sesamum seed, heat in fire, or the Deity in the universe, &c.<BR>2 Getting, obtaining, gain.<BR>3 Universal permeation, omnipresence, as one of ŚIVA'S superhuman properties.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आप to pervade, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिज्ञान
व्याप्तिज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge of the existence of a substance from observation of the presence of its inherent properties.<BR>E.<BR>व्याप्ति, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिमत्|व्याप्तिमन्त्
व्याप्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Diffusive, pervading.<BR>E.<BR>व्याप्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिलक्षण
व्याप्तिलक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Sign or proof of the existence or non-existence of an inherent property or attribute.<BR>E.<BR>व्याप्ति, and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्य|व्याप्यं|व्याप्यः
व्याप्य<BR>mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>1 Permeable, penetrable.<BR>2 Capable of containing any inherent property.<BR>n. (-प्यं)<BR>1 An instrument or agent.<BR>2 The thing or substance which may be the site or subject of attributes or inherent properties.<BR>3 The subject of an inference, as fire inferred from the presence of smoke, &c.<BR>4 A drug, (Costus speciosus.)<BR>E.<BR>वि before आप to pervade, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्व|व्याप्यत्वं
व्याप्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Capacity of being penetrated or essentially affected by.<BR>E.<BR>व्याप्य, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, व्याप्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्वासिद्धि|व्याप्यत्वासिद्धिः
व्याप्यत्वासिद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>(In logic,) Imperfect conclusion, one not comprehending all the points of the argument.<BR>E.<BR>व्याप्यत्व, and असिद्धि nonconclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभ्युक्षी
व्याभ्युक्षी<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>Gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure.<BR>E.<BR>वि, आङ् and अभि before उक्ष to sprinkle, aff. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याम|व्यामः
व्याम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A fathom, or the space between the tips of the fingers of either hand when the arms are extended.<BR>2 Disregard, disrespect (?)<BR>3 Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अम to go, with आङ् pref. and aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामन|व्यामनं
व्यामन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Disregard, disrespect.<BR>E.<BR>वि before अम to go, with आङ् prefixed, and ल्युट् aff. or वि privative, म्ना to mind, आङ् pref. and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्ष|व्यामर्षः
व्यामर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>1 Rubbing out, erasure.<BR>2 Impatience.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before मृष to rub, &c., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिल्य
व्यामिल्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having closed^1 and opened, having twinkled, &c.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before मिल to twinkle, ल्यप् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिश्र|व्यामिश्रं
व्यामिश्र<BR>mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं)<BR>Mixed, blended, mingled.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामृष्ट
व्यामृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Rubbed, rubbed out, effaced.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before मृष to rub, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायछमान|व्यायच्छमान
व्यायछमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Quarrelling.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before इण् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायत|व्यायतं
व्यायत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Busy, occupied.<BR>2 Long.<BR>3 Hard, firm.<BR>4 Much, excessive.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before यम to stop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम|व्यायामः
व्यायाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Fatigue, labour.<BR>2 A fathom, measured by the distance to which both arms extended reach.<BR>3 Gymnastics, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">Page820</a>] athletic exercise, as playing with heavy clubs, wielding a bow with a chain in place of a string, alternate rising and falling at full length on the ground, &c.<BR>4 Manhood, manliness.<BR>5 A difficulty.<BR>6 A difficult or impassable defile, &c.<BR>7 Business, occupation.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before यम to refrain, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=819" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामशील
व्यायामशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Active, robust, athletic, taking exercise.<BR>E.<BR>व्यायाम, and शील practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिन्
व्यायामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Taking exercise, undergoing fatigue, active, athletic.<BR>E.<BR>व्यायाम, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम्य
व्यायाम्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having exercised, practised as gymnastics, &c. disciplined as troops.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before यम to restrain, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायोग|व्यायोगः
व्यायोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A kind of dramatic exhibition or composition in one act, the subject of which is some contest or war of a heroic kind, and of which woman is not the cause.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before युज to unite, aff. घञ्; in which the valiant are associated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याल|व्यालः
व्याल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Wicked, villainous, bad.<BR>2 Cruel, fierce.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A beast of prey.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>4 A vicious elephant.<BR>5 A king.<BR>6 A species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before अल to adorn, or अड to make effort, aff. अच्; also व्याड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालक|व्यालकः
व्यालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A vicious elephant.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालग्राह|व्यालग्राहः
व्यालग्राह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A snake-catcher.<BR>E.<BR>व्याल a snake, and ग्रह to seize, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालग्राहिन्
व्यालग्राहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A snake-catcher, one who lives by catching and exhibiting snakes.<BR>E.<BR>व्याल a snake, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालतम
व्यालतम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Very injurious, cruel or fierce.<BR>E.<BR>व्याल and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालमृग|व्यालमृगः
व्यालमृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A fierce or wild stag.<BR>E.<BR>व्याल, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालायुध|व्यालायुधं|व्यालायुधः
व्यालायुध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>A sort of perfume; see नखी.<BR>E.<BR>व्याल a beast of prey (a tiger), and आयुध a weapon; compared to the claw of the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालिखत्
व्यालिखत्<BR>mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्)<BR>1 Drawing lines, delineating, scratching, piercing.<BR>2 Extending to, in contact with.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before लिख to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालीन
व्यालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Thick, clustering.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before ली to waste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोल
व्यालोल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Tremulous, shaking, waving.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before लोल to shake, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलन|व्यावकलनं
व्यावकलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Subtraction, (in arithmetic.)<BR>E.<BR>वि with आङ् and अव before कल to count, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलित
व्यावकलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Subtracted.<BR>E.<BR>वि with आङ् and अव before कल to count, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावक्रोशी
व्यावक्रोशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>Mutual imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>वि with आङ् and अव before क्रुश to cry out, aff. णच् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावभाषी
व्यावभाषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>Mutual abuse or imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>वि implying reciprocity, and अव depreciation, भाष to speak, affs. णच् and ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त|व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त्तः
व्यावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>1 Going round, revolving.<BR>2 Encompassing.<BR>3 Choosing, appointing.<BR>4 Ruptured navel, (umbilical hernia.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृत to be, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्तन|व्यावर्तन|व्यावर्तनं
व्यावर्त्तन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Rolling round, revolving.<BR>2 A volute, a fold, a band.<BR>3 Encompassing, surrounding.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृत to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारिक|व्यावहारिकः
व्यावहारिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Usual, customary.<BR>2 Juridical, judicial, legal, relative or referring to judicial procedure.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>व्यवहार litigation, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहासी
व्यावहासी<BR>f. (-सी)<BR>Mutual or reciprocal laughter.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हस to laugh, णच् and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याविध
व्याविध<BR>mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>Of various kinds or sorts.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before विघ sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत
व्यावृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Covered, screened.<BR>2 Removed, excepted.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृति|व्यावृतिः
व्यावृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Exception, exclusion.<BR>2 Covering, screening^1.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्तिन् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्त|व्यावृत्तः
व्यावृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>1 Chosen, appointed.<BR>2 Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>3 Fenced, screened.<BR>4 Removed, uncovered.<BR>5 Excepted, excluded.<BR>6 Praised, hymned.<BR>7 Rolled backwards.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृत to be, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्ति|व्यावृत्तिः
व्यावृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>2 Rejection, exception, exclusion.<BR>3 Choice, selection.<BR>4 Screening, surrounding.<BR>5 Rolling back.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृत to be, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यास|व्यासः
व्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A celebrated saint and author, the supposed original compiler of the Vedas and Purāṇas; also the founder of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>2 Diffusion, extension.<BR>3 Detail, distinction, severalty.<BR>4 A measure.<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>The diameter of a circle.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before अस to pervade, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासक्त|व्यासक्तः
व्यासक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Bewildered, confused.<BR>2 Connected with, attached or devoted to.<BR>3 Detached, separated.<BR>E.<BR>वि before आसक्त attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासङ्ग|व्यासंग|व्यासंगः|व्यासङ्गः
व्यासङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 Confusion, perplexity.<BR>2 Separation, detachment.<BR>3 Attachment, addition.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before षञ्ज to embrace, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासिद्ध|व्यासिद्धः
व्यासिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>2 Contraband, not allowed to be sold but to particular persons or in certain places.<BR>E.<BR>वि privative, and आसिद्ध perfected, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहत|व्याहतः
व्याहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Confused, alarmed.<BR>2 Repelled, repulsed.<BR>3 Driven out, expelled.<BR>4 Disappointed.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हन to strike, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहार|व्याहारः
व्याहार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Voice, speech.<BR>2 A word, an articulate sound.<BR>3 Jest, joke, humorous speech.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरण|व्याहरणं
व्याहरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Uttering, pronouncing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरत्
व्याहरत्<BR>mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>Speaking, uttering, pronouncing.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत
व्याहृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Uttered, pronounced, said.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृति|व्याहृतिः
व्याहृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Voice, speech.<BR>2 A word, an articulate sound.<BR>3 A mystical word or sound, as Om, Svar, Bhūr, Bhuvas, &c., which are the Mahā Vyāhṛtis, and commence the daily prayers of the Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=820" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत्य
व्याहृत्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having said or uttered.<BR>E.<BR>वि and आङ् before हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत|व्युतः
व्युत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sewn, woven.<BR>E.<BR>वि before उत woven; also व्यूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युति|व्युतिः
व्युति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Sewing, weaving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ऊय to weave, aff. क्तिन्, form irr.; also व्यूति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम|व्युत्क्रमं|व्युत्क्रमः
व्युत्क्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Inverted order, irregular arrangement.<BR>E.<BR>वि and उत् before क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थान|व्युत्थानं
व्युत्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Independence, following one's own inclination.<BR>2 Opposition, contradiction, doing that which is prohibited.<BR>3 Obstruction, prohibition, hindering or opposing any one.<BR>4 Completion of religious contemplation, the end. of a period of abstraction.<BR>E.<BR>वि and उत् before स्था to stay or be, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पत्ति|व्युत्पत्तिः
व्युत्पत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Science, learning, conversancy with or proficience in literature or science.<BR>2 Formation of words, derivation, etymology.<BR>E.<BR>वि and उत् before पद to go, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पन्न|व्युत्पन्नः
व्युत्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>1 Learned, studied, conversant or proficient in literature.<BR>2 Completed, finished.<BR>3 Derived, formed as a derivative word.<BR>4 Generated, begotten.<BR>E.<BR>वि and उत् before पद to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्त
व्युदस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Put off, thrown aside, (especially as feeling or affection.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and उट् before अस to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्य
व्युदस्य<BR>ind.<BR>Having thrown off or put away, (as desire, feeling, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>वि and उद before अस to throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदास|व्युदासः
व्युदास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Indifference to, disregard for.<BR>2 Making ill or unprofitable use of any thing, throwing away.<BR>E.<BR>वि and उद before अस to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपदेश|व्युपदेशः
व्युपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Pretext, deception, plausible but false council.<BR>E.<BR>वि priv., उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष
व्युष<BR>r. 10th cl. (व्युषयति)<BR>To abandon, to reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
व्युष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Burned.<BR>2 Dawned, become daylight or dawn.<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1 Dawn, break of day.<BR>2 Day.<BR>3 Fruit, consequence.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वस to abide, aff. क्त, and व changed to उ, or व्युष to burn, when it is more properly read व्युष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्टि|व्युष्टिः
व्युष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 Fruit, consequence.<BR>2 Increase, prosperity.<BR>3 Praise.<BR>E.<BR>वि and वस to abide, aff. क्तिन्, and व changed to उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युस
व्युस<BR>(इर) व्युसिर r. 4th cl. (व्युस्यति)<BR>To leave, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
व्यूढ<BR>mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>1 Arranged, arrayed, placed in order or array.<BR>2 Compact, firm, well-knit.<BR>3 Large, great.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वह to bear, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढकङ्कट|व्यूढकंकट|व्यूढकङ्कटः
व्यूढकङ्कट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Armed, mailed.<BR>E.<BR>व्यूढ arranged, and कङ्कट mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढोरस्क
व्यूढोरस्क<BR>mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं)<BR>Broad-chested.<BR>E.<BR>व्यूढ, उरस् the breast, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढि|व्यूढिः
व्यूढि<BR>f. (-ढिः)<BR>Array, orderly arrangement or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वह to bear, or ऊह to reason, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्यूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Woven.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ऊत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूति|व्यूतिः
व्यूति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 Weaving.<BR>E.<BR>वि before वेञ् to weave, aff. क्तिन् and व changed to ऊ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह|व्यूहः
व्यूह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 Military array, the arrangement of troops in various positions; as दण्डव्यूहः the array in line, भोगव्यूहः in column, मण्डलव्यूहः in circle, असंहतव्यूहः in mixed order; also various fanciful forms, as the शकटः or car-shape, मकरः or marine monster-like, पताका flag-shape, &c.<BR>2 A flock, a multitude.<BR>3 Logic, reasoning.<BR>4 Making, manufacture.<BR>5 The body.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ऊह to reason, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहन|व्यूहनं
व्यूहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Arraying, array, arrangement.<BR>2 Structure of the body, disposition of the members.<BR>E.<BR>वि before ऊह to reason, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहपार्ष्णि|व्यूहपार्ष्णिः
व्यूहपार्ष्णि<BR>m. (-र्ष्णिः)<BR>The rear of an army.<BR>E.<BR>व्यूह array, and पार्ष्णि the heel or back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहभङ्ग|व्यूहभङ्गः
व्यूहभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Throwing into disorder, breaking an array.<BR>E.<BR>व्यूह, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहभेद|व्यूहभेदः
व्यूहभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Piercing or breaking an array.<BR>E.<BR>व्यूह, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ये
व्ये<BR>(ञ) व्येञ् (व्ययति)<BR>To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योकार|व्योकारः
व्योकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A blacksmith.<BR>E.<BR>व्यो an imitative sound, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमकेश|व्योमकेशः
व्योमकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>वोम heaven, and केश hair; also with इनि poss. aff. added व्योमकेशिन् (-शी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमचारिन्
व्योमचारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A god.<BR>2 A bird. A saint.<BR>3 A Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम heaven, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमचारिपुर|व्योमचारिपुरं
व्योमचारिपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA, suspended midway between heaven and earth.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम heaven, चारि going, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमधूम|व्योमधूमः
व्योमधूम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम heaven, and घूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमन्
व्योमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>1 Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A temple, sacred to the sun, or place where he is especially worshipped.<BR>E.<BR>व्येञ् to cover, Uṇādi aff. मनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमनासिका
व्योमनासिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A sort of quail.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम heaven, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममञ्जर|व्योममंजर|व्योममञ्जरं
व्योममञ्जर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A flag, a banner.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम the sky, and मञ्जर a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममण्डल|व्योममंडल|व्योममण्डलं
व्योममण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A flag, a banner.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम sky, and मण्डल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममुद्गर|व्योममुद्गरः
व्योममुद्गर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A gust of wind.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम the sky, and मुद्गर a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममाय
व्योममाय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Measuring the sky, high as the heavens.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम, and माय what measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमयान|व्योमयानं
व्योमयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A carriage of the gods.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम the sky, and यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमविस्तृत
व्योमविस्तृत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The expanse or firmament.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम, and विल्तृत spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमसद्
व्योमसद्<BR>m. (-सद्)<BR>A spirit of heaven, a divinity.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम, and सद् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमस्थली
व्योमस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम the sky, and स्थली base or site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमस्पृश्
व्योमस्पृश्<BR>mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>Sky-touching, lofty.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम, and स्पृश् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमाभ|व्योमाभः
व्योमाभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>व्योम sky, and आभ shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योष|व्योषं
व्योष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>The aggregate of three spices, or black-pepper, longpepper, and dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>वि variously, उष to burn, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रजति व्राजयति)<BR>To go, to travel.<BR>With परि prefixed,<BR>To wander about, as a mendicant.<BR>r. 10th cl.<BR>To prepare, to perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A cow-pen, a station of cowherds.<BR>2 A road.<BR>3 A flock, a herd, a multitude.<BR>4 The district about Agra and [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">Page822</a>] Mathurā, the scene of KṚṢṆA'S juvenile adventures.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Wandering, roaming.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, aff. घ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=821" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजत्
व्रजत्<BR>mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>Going, roaming.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजन|व्रजनं
व्रजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Going, roaming.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजभू
व्रजभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>A tree, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रज a cow-pen, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजाजिर
व्रजाजिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A cow-yard, a cattle fold or pen.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज, and अजिर a yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजित
व्रजित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Gone, going.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Roaming.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या<BR>f. (-ज्या)<BR>1 Wandering about, either as an act of religious austerity or in quest of alms.<BR>2 March of an assailant, attack, invasion.<BR>3 March in general.<BR>4 A class, a flock, a tribe.<BR>5 A theatre.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्यावत्|व्रज्यावन्त्
व्रज्यावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Wandering, roaming.<BR>2 Going gracefully.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज्या, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण|व्रणं|व्रणः
व्रण<BR>r. 1st cl. (व्रणति)<BR>To sound.<BR>r. 10th cl. (व्रणयति)<BR>To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण|व्रणं|व्रणः
व्रण<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>A tumor, a boil; an ulcer, a wound.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण to wound, an abscess, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणकृत्
व्रणकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Making a sore, wounding, ulcerating, corroding, &c.<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>Marking-nut plant, (Semecarpus anacardium.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रण a sore, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणद्विष्
व्रणद्विष्<BR>m. (-द्विट्)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>वृण a sore, and द्विष् hostile to, healing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणधूपन
व्रणधूपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Fumigating a sore.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण, and धूपन burning incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणवस्तु
व्रणवस्तु<BR>n. (-स्तुः)<BR>Part liable to ulcerate, as skin, flesh, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण, and वस्तु substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणवेदना
व्रणवेदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>Pain of a wound or sore.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण, and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणशोधन
व्रणशोधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cleaning or cicatrising a sore.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण, and शोधन cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणह|व्रणहः
व्रणह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The castor oil tree.<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>A sort of creeper, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रण a sore, and हन to destroy, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणिन्
व्रणिन्<BR>mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>Having a boil, a sore or wound.<BR>E.<BR>व्रण, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रत|व्रतं|व्रतः
व्रत<BR>mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>1 Any meritorious act of devotion, the voluntary or vowed observance, or imposition of any penance, austerity, or privation, as fasting, continence, exposure to heat and cold, &c.<BR>2 Eating.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, aff. अतच्, र substituted for the vowel, or व्रज to go, (to heaven by it,) घ aff. and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतति|व्रततिः
व्रतति<BR>f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>1 Expansion, spreading.<BR>2 A creeper.<BR>E.<BR>वृत to abide, अति aff., the vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतभिक्षा
व्रतभिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>Soliciting alms, as one of the ceremonies accompanying investiture.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत the observance of investiture, and भिक्षा begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतलोपन
व्रतलोपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Violating a religious vow or obligation.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत, and लोपन cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतसंग्रह
व्रतसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Engaging in any act of devotion, taking on one's self some voluntary religious obligation.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत a vow, and संग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्नातक|व्रतस्नातकः
व्रतस्नातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The Brahman who has completed his term of studentship.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत, and स्नातक a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रताचरण
व्रताचरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Observing a religious obligation, especially continence, as the duty of the student.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत, and आचरण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतादेश|व्रतादेशः
व्रतादेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Investiture of a youth of either of the first three classes with the characteristic cord.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत the observance, and आदेश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>Engaged in or observing a religious vow or obligation.<BR>m. (-ती)<BR>1 An employer of priests.<BR>2 An ascetic, a devotee, one engaged in the observance of a vow or penance.<BR>3 The religious student.<BR>E.<BR>व्रत a vow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतोपवास|व्रतोपवासः
व्रतोपवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Fasting, a fast, (as a religious penance or obligation.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रत, and उपवास fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रध्न
व्रध्न<BR>m. (-ध्नः)<BR>The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च
व्रश्च<BR>(ओ उ) ओव्रश्चु r. 6th cl. (वृश्चति)<BR>To cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं|व्रश्चनः
व्रश्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A small saw or chisel.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Cutting.<BR>E.<BR>व्रश्च to cut, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजि|व्राजिः
व्राजि<BR>f. (-जिः)<BR>A gale of wind.<BR>E.<BR>व्रज to go, इञ् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात|व्रातः
व्रात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A multitude, an assemblage.<BR>2 The descendant of an outcaste Brahman, &c.<BR>3 The company and attendants at a marriage feast.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Manual or bodily labour.<BR>2 Day labour, employment of a precarious kind.<BR>E.<BR>वृ to choose, aff. अतच्, and the vowel made long; or व्रत a religious observance, or व्रात्य an outcaste, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A cooly, a hired porter or labourer.<BR>2 One who has no fixed or stated employment.<BR>E.<BR>व्रात bodily labour, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्य|व्रात्यः
व्रात्य<BR>m. (-त्यः)<BR>A Brahman, or man of the three first classes, in whose youth the customary observances have been omitted, and who has not received his investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>f. (-त्या)<BR>A female of a fallen Brahman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्रात, and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यता
व्रात्यता<BR>f. (ता)<BR>The condition of one who has lost caste by neglect of the initiatory observances.<BR>E.<BR>व्रात्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, व्रात्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोम|व्रात्यस्तोमः
व्रात्यस्तोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>A particular sacrifice performed to recover the rights forfeited by an improper delay of the ceremony of investiture.<BR>E.<BR>व्रात्य one not invested, &c., and स्तोम a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री<BR>r. 4th cl. (व्रीयते) r. 9th cl. (व्रीणाति or व्रीणीते)<BR>1 To choose or elect.<BR>2 To cover or screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड<BR>r. 4th cl. (व्रीडयति)<BR>1 To be modest, to be bashful or ashamed.<BR>2 To throw, to direct or send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड<BR>mf. (-डः-डा)<BR>Shame, bashfulness.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीड to be ashamed, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडन|व्रीडनं
व्रीडन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Bashfulness, modesty.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीड to be ashamed, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडानत
व्रीडानत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ashamed, hanging down the head with shame.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीडा, and आनत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडान्वित
व्रीडान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Modest.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीडा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Ashamed, modest.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीड to be ashamed, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस
व्रीस<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रीसति व्रीसयति)<BR>To hurt or injure, to kill or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=822" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि<BR>m. (-हिः)<BR>1 Rice of various kinds: eight principal sorts are enumerated by native authorities, but the varieties are more numerous.<BR>2 Rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR>E.<BR>व्री to choose. हि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिक|व्रीहिकः
व्रीहिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Having rice, bearing rice, &c.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिकाञ्चन|व्रीहिकाञ्चनः
व्रीहिकाञ्चन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sort of pulse, (Ervum lens or hirsutum, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिन्
व्रीहिन्<BR>mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि)<BR>Having rice, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिभेद|व्रीहिभेदः
व्रीहिभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A sort of grain, (Panicum miliaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, and भेद sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिमय|व्रीहिमयः
व्रीहिमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made or consisting of rice.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A rice cake offered with ghee as an oblation.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिराजिक
व्रीहिराजिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Panic seed, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>2 Another species, (Panicum miliaceum.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, राजिक shining, excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीह्यगार|व्रीह्यगारं
व्रीह्यगार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A granary, a shed where rice or other grain is stored.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, अगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड
व्रुड<BR>r. 6th cl. (व्रुडति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>2 To heap.<BR>3 To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस
व्रूस<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रूसति व्रूसयति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैह|व्रैहः
व्रैह<BR>mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>Made of or with rice.<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Fit for or sown with rice, (a field, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>व्रीहि rice, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली<BR>r. 9th cl. (व्लीणाति or व्लीणीते)<BR>1 To choose or select.<BR>2 To cover, to screen.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष
व्लेक्ष<BR>r. 10th cl. (व्लेक्षयति)<BR>To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श<BR>The thirtieth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet and first of the three sibilants; it is termed the palatal sibilant, and corresponds to Sh pronounced softly, as in Shun; in the Roman character it is distinguished by an accent, as S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 A weapon.<BR>n. adv. (शं) or ind. (शं or शम्)<BR>Happy, happily, auspiciously.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep or शो to pare, &c. aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Happy, prosperous, fortunate.<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A sort of snake.<BR>E.<BR>शम् happily, and युस aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंय्य
शंय्य<BR>mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>Happy, fortunate.<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>Knowledge, understanding.<BR>E.<BR>शम् happily, यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>2 The iron head of a pestle.<BR>E.<BR>शं good fortune, and व poss. aff.; also as differently derived, read शम्ब and सम्ब, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>शं happily, वृ to choose or cover, aff. अरप्, more usually read शम्बर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस|शंसः
शंस<BR>(उ,) शंसु r. 1st cl. (शंसति)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>2 To hurt.<BR>3 To wish.<BR>4 To calumniate.<BR>With अभि prefixed,<BR>To accuse wrongfully.<BR>With आङ्<BR>1 To hope.<BR>2 To speak.<BR>With प्र,<BR>To praise, to flatter; this root and its derivatives are sometimes read with the palatal sibilant final or शंश, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>1 Speech.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 Praise, flattery, eulogium.<BR>E.<BR>शंस to praise, &c. aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Certain, ascertained.<BR>2 Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR>3 Said, declared.<BR>4 Praised, celebrated.<BR>5 Wished, desired.<BR>E.<BR>शंस to wish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ<BR>m. (-स्ता)<BR>An encomiast, a panegyrist, a flatterer.<BR>E.<BR>शंस to praise, तृन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्थ|शंस्थः
शंस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Happy, prosperous, well-faring.<BR>E.<BR>शं happily, स्था to stay or be^1, aff. क.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्था
शंस्था<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>Happy, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>शम् happily, ष्ठा to stay or be, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्य|शंस्यः
शंस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 Desirable, to be wished.<BR>2 Meritorious, to be praised.<BR>E.<BR>शंस to praise, &c. aff. क्यप्; also शस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक<BR>r. 4th cl. (शक्यति-ते) r. 5th cl. (इर ऌ) इरशक्तृ (शक्नोति)<BR>1 To bear patiently, to endure, to be patient.<BR>2 To be able to effect, to be competent or powerful.<BR>(इ) शकि r. 1st cl. (शङ्कते)<BR>1 To think probable, to suspect.<BR>2 To fear, to apprehend.<BR>With आङ्,<BR>to dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A sovereign, any prince who gives his name to an era, especially applied to Śālivāhana.<BR>2 A particular caste, the followers or descendants of ŚAKA, or Sālivāhana.<BR>3 A country, or<BR>m. plu. (-काः)<BR>The inhabitants, the Sacœ, the Scythians.<BR>4 An era: see शाक.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट<BR>mfn. subst. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>A cart.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A Daitya slain by KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A cart load.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, अटन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटविल|शकटविलः
शकटविल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटहन्
शकटहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शकट the demon so named, and हन destroyer; also similar compounds, as शकटारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाल
शकटाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The minister of NANDA: also read ŚAKATĀRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाह्वा
शकटाह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>The fourth lunar asterism, Rohiṇī, the stars of which are represented as a cart.<BR>E.<BR>शकट a cart, आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A small cart, a toy-cart.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to शकटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>A part, a portion, a piece.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Skin.<BR>2 Bark.<BR>3 A kind of (black) pigment or die.<BR>4 The scales of a fish.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, कलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>शकल skin or scales, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकरण
शकलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Parting, dividing, cutting or breaking in pieces.<BR>E.<BR>शकल, and करण making, with च्चि. augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकृत
शकलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Parted, cut in pieces, wounded.<BR>E.<BR>शकल, कृत made, augment च्चि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकव
शकव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकशकायत्
शकशकायत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>Rustling, making a noise (as the leaves of a tree in the wind.)<BR>E.<BR>शकत् imitative sound, nominal verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकान्तक|शकांतक|शकान्तकः
शकान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The prince, VIKRAMĀDITYA.<BR>2 The name of SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>E.<BR>शक an era or a Scythian, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाब्द|शकाब्दः
शकाब्द<BR>n. (-ब्दं)<BR>1 A year of the Śaka era, or era of SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>E.<BR>शक, and अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A silly brother in law of a Raja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकारि|शकारिः
शकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>VIKRAMĀDITYA, the celebrated sovereign of Oujein.<BR>E.<BR>शक a Saca or Scythian, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=823" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 A kind of bird, either the Indian vulture or the common kite, (Falco cheela); it is also applied to the Pondicherry eagle, (Falco ponticeriana.)<BR>3 A sort of hymn or song, sung at festivals to solicit or secure lucky events.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any lucky or auspicious object or omen.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, उन Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञा
शकुनज्ञा<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>A small house lizard.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन a bird, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
शकुनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 The maternal uncle of the Kaurava princes, and counsellor of DURYODHANA.<BR>3 One of the astronomical periods called Karaṇas.<BR>4 The Indian kite or eagle, (Falco cheela.)<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A hen sparrow.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, उनि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिप्रपा
शकुनिप्रपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A trough or little well for watering birds.<BR>E.<BR>शकुनि a bird, प्र before पा to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनीश्वर|शकुनीश्वरः
शकुनीश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A name of GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>शकुनि a bird, and ईश्वर chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः|शकुन्तः
शकुन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A bird.<BR>2 A kind of bird, the Indian vulture.<BR>3 Another sort of bird, described as of aquatic habits, perhaps a kind of maritime or fishing falcon.<BR>4 A sort of insect.<BR>5 The blue jay.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, उन्त Uṇādi aff.; also शकुन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The daughter of MENAKĀ, the courtezan of Svarga, by the sage VIŚVĀMITRA, brought up by KAṆVA the hermit, and afterwards married to DUṢYANTA, by whom she became the mother of BHARATA, the sovereign of all India.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन्त a bird, ला to get, aff. क, and टाप्, being born in a solitary forest, and protected by the birds till found by KAṆVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तलात्मज|शकुन्तलात्मजः
शकुन्तलात्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>BHARATA, the sovereign of India.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन्तला as above, and आत्मज the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः|शकुन्तिः
शकुन्ति<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 A kind of bird: see शकुन्त, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, Uṇādi aff. उन्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तिका|शकुंतिका
शकुन्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A locust, a cricket.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन्त a bird, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुल|शकुलः
शकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, aff. उलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलगण्ड|शकुलगण्डः
शकुलगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A kind of fish, the gilt-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलाक्षक|शकुलाक्षकः
शकुलाक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon), with white blossoms.<BR>E.<BR>शकुल a fish, अक्षि the eye, अच् substituted for the final vowel; the blossoms being compared to the eye of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलादनी
शकुलादनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A medicinal plant, commonly Kaṭuki, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>2 A creeping plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>3 A drug, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>4 An earth worm.<BR>E.<BR>शकुल a fish, अद to eat, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलार्भक|शकुलार्भकः
शकुलार्भक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of gilt-head, (Sparus emarginatus.)<BR>E.<BR>शकुल a fish, and अर्भक a young one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्
शकृत्<BR>n. (-कृत्)<BR>Fæces, excrement.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, (to expel,) Uṇādi aff. ऋतन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्करि|शकृत्करिः
शकृत्करि<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A calf.<BR>E.<BR>शकृत् ordure, कृ to make, इन् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्कार|शकृत्कारः
शकृत्कार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Making ordure or fæces.<BR>E.<BR>शकृत् ordure, and कार who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृद्वार
शकृद्वार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>शकृत् fæces, and द्वार passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्कर|शक्करः
शक्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 A zone, a girdle.<BR>3 A form of metre, a stanza of four lines of fourteen syllables each.<BR>4 A woman of an impure caste; it is also read शक्वर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करि|शक्करिः
शक्करि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A bull; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त|शक्तः
शक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Able, capable, strong, powerful.<BR>2 Speaking civilly, able to please by the manner of speaking.<BR>3 Diligent, attentive, intent.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तता
शक्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Ability, power.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शक्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 Power, regal power as resulting from majesty, perseverance, and counsel.<BR>2 Power, strength, prowess.<BR>3 An iron spear or dart.<BR>4 The energy or active power of a deity, personified as his wife, as GAURI of ŚIVA, LAKṢMĪ of VIṢṆU, &c.<BR>5 The female organ as the counterpart of the phallic personification of ŚIVA, and worshipped either literally or figuratively by a sect of Hindus, thence termed Śāktas.<BR>6 Allaying or appeasing opposition.<BR>7 Force or signification of words.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिग्रह|शक्तिग्रहः
शक्तिग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>2 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>3 A spearman, a lancer.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, and ग्रह who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तितस्
शक्तितस्<BR>ind.<BR>According to power or ability.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तित्रय
शक्तित्रय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The three ingredients of regal power; or king, minister, and vigour.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and चय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिधर|शक्तिधरः
शक्तिधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 A spearman, a lancer.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, and धर the holder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिपर्ण|शक्तिपर्णः
शक्तिपर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति strength, (giving it,) and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिपाणि|शक्तिपाणिः
शक्तिपाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA, the Hindu MARS.<BR>2 A spearman.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिभृत्
शक्तिभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA, see the last.<BR>2 A soldier armed with a spear.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, and भृत् who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिमत्|शक्तिमन्त्
शक्तिमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>Powerful, mighty.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिवैकल्य
शक्तिवैकल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Inability, deficiency of power or strength.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and वैकल्य imperfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिहीन
शक्तिहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Powerless, impotent.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिहेतिक|शक्तिहेतिकः
शक्तिहेतिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spearman, a lancer, a soldier armed with an iron lance.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, हेति a weapon, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तु|शक्तुः
शक्तु<BR>mn. (-क्तुः-क्तु) according to some authorities only m. plu. (शक्तवः)<BR>The powder or flour of barley and other grain, first fried and then ground.<BR>E.<BR>शच to go, &c. तुन् aff.; also read सक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तुफला
शक्तुफला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्त farina, and फल fruit; also शक्तुफली, and सक्तुफला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त्यपेक्ष
शक्त्यपेक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>Being according to, or having reference to, ability, power, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति, and अपेक्षा regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्न|शक्नः
शक्न<BR>mfn. (-क्नः-क्ना-क्नं)<BR>Speaking civilly or pleasingly: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नु|शक्नुः
शक्नु<BR>mfn. (-क्नुः-क्नुः-क्नु)<BR>Speaking civilly or kindly.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, (to please by speaking,) aff. क्नु; also with the vowel rejected शक्न, and with क्ल aff. शक्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्मन्
शक्मन्<BR>m. (-क्मा)<BR>Power, strength.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्य|शक्यः
शक्य<BR>mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>Possible, practicable, to be effected or done.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=824" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्यता
शक्यता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Possibility.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शक्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्यप्रतीकार
शक्यप्रतीकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A possible remedy or counteragent.<BR>E.<BR>शक्य, and प्रतीकार remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्र|शक्रः
शक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>INDRA, the chief of the inferior gods, and ruler of Svarga or paradise.<BR>2 A plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>3 A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>शक to possess power, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रक्रीडाचल|शक्रक्रीडाचलः
शक्रक्रीडाचल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Mount Meru.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, क्रीडा sport, pleasure, and अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रगोप|शक्रगोपः
शक्रगोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>An insect of a red colour, (Coccinella or ladybird of various species.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, गो light, &c. and पा to preserve, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रज|शक्रजः
शक्रज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रजात|शक्रजातः
शक्रजात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A crow.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रजित्
शक्रजित्<BR>m. (-जित्)<BR>The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and जित् victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रधनुस्
शक्रधनुस्<BR>n. (-नुः)<BR>The bow of INDRA, the rain-bow.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and धनुस् the bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रध्वज|शक्रध्वजः
शक्रध्वज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A pole or flag set up in honour of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र, and ध्वज a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रनन्दन|शक्रनंदन|शक्रनन्दनः
शक्रनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and नन्दन son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रपादप|शक्रपादपः
शक्रपादप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A sort of pine, (P. devadaru, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रपुष्पी
शक्रपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A sort of potherb; also Viśalyā.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र the Pentaptera arjuna, and पुष्प a flower; having similar flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभवन|शक्रभवनं
शक्रभवन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sky, heaven.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and भवन abode; being the god of the firmament: it also occurs शक्रभुवन, from भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभिद्
शक्रभिद्<BR>m. (-भिद्)<BR>The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and भिद् defeater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभूभवा
शक्रभूभवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>Colocynth, (Cucumis coloquintida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रमूर्द्ध्वन्
शक्रमूर्द्ध्वन्<BR>m. (-र्द्ध्वा)<BR>An ant hill, a hillock.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, मूर्द्ध्वन् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रवाहन|शक्रवाहनः
शक्रवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cloud.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशरासन|शक्रशरासनं
शक्रशरासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The rain-bow.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, शरासन a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशाला
शक्रशाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A place prepared for sacrifices to be offered in.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशिरस्
शक्रशिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>An ant hill<BR>E.<BR>शक्र. INDRA, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसारथि|शक्रसारथिः
शक्रसारथि<BR>m. (-थिः)<BR>The charioteer of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र, and सारथि a coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसुत|शक्रसुतः
शक्रसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 The monkey king BALI.<BR>2 ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसुधा
शक्रसुधा<BR>f. (-धा)<BR>The resin of the Boswellia thurifera, or gum olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and सुधा ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसृष्टा
शक्रसृष्टा<BR>f. (-ष्टा)<BR>Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, सृष्ट created; springing originally, it is said, from the ground on which INDRA spilt a drop of nectar as he was drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राख्य|शक्राख्यः
शक्राख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राणी
शक्राणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>SACĪ, the wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, ङीष् aff. and आनुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राशन|शक्राशनं|शक्राशनः
शक्राशन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, अशन food: created by him; springing from the drops of Amṛta, which fell on the ground from the bodies of the monkies slain in the war with RĀVAṆA, and who were restored to life by INDRA by a shower of Amṛta, or the liquor of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रोत्सव|शक्रोत्सवः
शक्रोत्सव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A festival in honour of INDRA on the twelfth of the month Bhādra.<BR>E.<BR>शक्र INDRA, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ल|शक्लः
शक्ल<BR>mfn. (-क्लः-क्ला-क्लं)<BR>Speaking civilly or kindly.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, (to delight simply by speaking,) and क्ल Uṇādi affix; also शक्न and शक्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन्<BR>m. (-क्वा)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be powerful, and वनिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वर|शक्वरः
शक्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull, an ox.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A finger.<BR>2 A river.<BR>3 A zone, a girdle.<BR>4 A form of metre, a stanza of four lines of fourteen syllables each, and comprising many varieties according to the different feet of which the lines are composed.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able or strong, क्वरप् aff., or वनिप् aff. with र augment, and the final rejected: the feminine form is also derived from शक्वन् with ङीप् affix, and र augment, and the word is also read शक्कर and शक्करी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क|शंक|शंकः|शङ्कः
शङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>A draft ox.<BR>f. (-ङ्का)<BR>1 Fear, terror, apprehension.<BR>2 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>3 A species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR>E.<BR>शकि to fear, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कनीय|शंकनीय
शङ्कनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Doubtful, questionable, to be doubted or apprehended.<BR>E.<BR>शकि to fear or doubt, अनीयर् aff.; also शङ्कितव्य and शङ्क्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कर|शंकर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness or good fortune.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 The name of a celebrated teacher of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Bengal madder.<BR>E.<BR>शं good fortune, कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्करप्रिय|शंकरप्रिय|शंकरप्रियः|शङ्करप्रियः
शङ्करप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The francoline partridge.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कर ŚIVA, and प्रिय dear, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कान्वित
शङ्कान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Apprehensive, doubtful, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का, अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्काभियोग|शङ्काभियोगः
शङ्काभियोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Accusation or charge on suspicion.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का, and अभियोग charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कामय
शङ्कामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Fearful, afraid.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कास्पद
शङ्कास्पद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Cause or matter of doubt or apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का, and आस्पद site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्काहीन
शङ्काहीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Free from doubt or apprehension.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का, and हीन free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कित|शंकित|शङ्कितः
शङ्कित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Alarmed, frightened.<BR>2 Weak, unsteady.<BR>3 Doubtful, uncertain.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्का fear, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कितवर्णक|शङ्कितवर्णकः
शङ्कितवर्णक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A thief.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कित frightened, वर्ण a caste, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कु|शंकु|शंकुः|शङ्कुः
शङ्कु<BR>m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>1 The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>2 A javelin.<BR>3 A pin, a stake, a pale.<BR>4 The gnomon of a dial, usually twelve fingers long.<BR>5 A long thin column in front of a pagoda.<BR>6 The penis.<BR>7 A number.<BR>8 The small fibres of a leaf.<BR>9 The scate fish, (Raia Sankur, HAM.)<BR>10 A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR>11 A goose.<BR>12 An ant hill.<BR>13 A goblin, a demon.<BR>14 A Gandharba attached to ŚIVA.<BR>15 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>16 KĀMA.<BR>17 Sin.<BR>18 Fear, terror.<BR>E.<BR>शकि to doubt or apprehend, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=825" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुकर्ण|शंकुकर्ण|शङ्कुकर्णः
शङ्कुकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कु a javelin, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुचि|शंकुचिः|शङ्कुचिः
शङ्कुचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>A scate fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुतरु|शंकुतरु|शङ्कुतरुः
शङ्कुतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कु a stake, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुवृक्ष|शंकुवृक्ष|शङ्कुवृक्षः
शङ्कुवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Śāl tree.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कु a pin or stake, and वृक्ष tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुर|शंकुर|शङ्कुरः
शङ्कुर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Formidable, fearful, frightful.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कु fear, रा to give or cause, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुला|शंकुला
शङ्कुला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A pair of nippers, used to cut the betel nut into small pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कोच|शंकोचः|शङ्कोचः
शङ्कोच<BR>m. (-चः)<BR>A scate fish; also शङ्कु, शङ्कुचि, and शङ्कोचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क्य
शङ्क्य<BR>mfn. (-ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं)<BR>To be feared or doubted.<BR>E.<BR>शकि to fear. यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्ख|शंख|शंखं|शंखः|शङ्खः
शङ्ख<BR>mn. (-ङ्खः-ङ्खं)<BR>The conch shell used by the Hindus, in two ways especially; offering libations with it, or when perforated at one end blowing it as a horn at sacrifices: used in this manner also, frequent, mention of it occurs in the battle pieces of the poets, each hero being provided with a Conch as his horn.<BR>m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>1 One of KUVERA'S treasures.<BR>2 The temple or temporal bone, sometimes comprising however the frontal bone also.<BR>3 A perfume, commonly Nakhi, apparently a dried shell fish.<BR>4 A military drum.<BR>5 One of the eight chiefs of the Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla, described as of a yellow colour.<BR>6 An elephant's cheek.<BR>7 A large number, ten or a hundred billions.<BR>8 The name of a saint and legislator.<BR>9 A poet, one of the nine gems, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शम to pacify, &c. Uṇādi aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खक|शंखक|शंखकं|शङ्खकं|शंखकः|शङ्खकः
शङ्खक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A bracelet, (often made of the conch shell.)<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The conch shell.<BR>2 Pain, and heat with a puffiness in the temples and forehead.<BR>3 The temples.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खकार|शंखकार|शङ्खकारः
शङ्खकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A worker in shells.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, and कार maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खचरी|शंखचरी
शङ्खचरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Sandal marks on the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख the forehead, and चर to go, aff. टच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खचर्च्ची|शङ्खचर्ची
शङ्खचर्च्ची<BR>f. (-र्च्ची)<BR>Sandal marks made across the forehead.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख the forehead, चर्च to anoint, affs. अच् and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खज|शङ्खजः
शङ्खज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A large pearl, of the shape of a pigeon's egg.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a shell, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खध्म|शंखध्म|शङ्खध्मः
शङ्खध्म<BR>m. (-ध्मः)<BR>A shell blower.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, and घ्म who blows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खनख|शंखनख|शंखनखः|शङ्खनखः
शङ्खनख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A small shell.<BR>2 A perfume, commonly नखी.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, and नख the nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खपाल|शंखपाल|शङ्खपालः
शङ्खपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 A Nāga or serpent of Pātāla.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, &c., and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खपुष्पी
शङ्खपुष्पी<BR>f. (-ष्पी)<BR>A sort of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, पुष्प a flower, ङीप् aff. implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खप्रस्थ|शङ्खप्रस्थः
शङ्खप्रस्थ<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>Spots in the moon.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a shell, and प्रस्थ pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खभृत्|शंखभृत्
शङ्खभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>Having a conch or shell.<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, and भृत् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खमुख|शंखमुख|शङ्खमुखः
शङ्खमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>An alligator.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a conch, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिका
शङ्खिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>E.<BR>शंख a shell, कन् implying resemblance, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिन्|शंखिन्
शङ्खिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्खी-ङ्खिनी-ङ्खि)<BR>Possessing or having a conch or shell, &c.<BR>m. (-ङ्खी)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 The ocean.<BR>3 A shell blower.<BR>4 A worker in shells.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A sort of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>2 A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>3 A description of woman, one of the four classes into which females are divided in erotic writings: the Śaṅkhinī is described as tall, with long hair, neither stout nor thin, of irascible disposition and strong passions.<BR>4 A goddess or Śakti worshipped by the Bauddhas.<BR>5 A female spirit or goblin.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख a shell, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिनीवास|शङ्खिनीवासः
शङ्खिनीवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच
शच<BR>r. 1st cl. (शचते)<BR>To speak articulately, to say or tell.<BR>(इ,) शचि r. 1st cl. (शंचते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचि|शचिः
शचि<BR>f. (-चिः or ची)<BR>1 The wife of INDRA.<BR>2 A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>3 The astronomical Karaṇa or period named Viṣṭi.<BR>E.<BR>शच to speak articulately, aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added; also सचि, and सची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचीपति|शचीपतिः
शचीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शची the wife of the deity, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट|शटः
शट<BR>r. 1st cl. (शटति)<BR>1 To be diseased or sick.<BR>2 To divide, to pierce or separate.<BR>3 To go.<BR>4 To be low spirited, to be weary or dejected.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शाटयति)<BR>To flatter, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट|शटः
शट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>Sour, astringent, acid.<BR>E.<BR>शट to pain, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटा
शटा<BR>f. (-टा)<BR>An ascetic's clotted hair: see सटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटी
शटी<BR>f. (-टिः or -टी)<BR>Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet,) otherwise considered as a synonym of the Ambahaldi, or Curcuma Amhaldi, the mango-smelling ginger, so termed because the fresh root possesses the smell of a green mango.<BR>E.<BR>शट to divide (remove disease), aff. इन, and ङीष optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ<BR>r. 1st cl. (शठति)<BR>1 To cheat, to defraud or deceive.<BR>2 To kill or hurt.<BR>3 To suffer pain.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शाठयति)<BR>1 To finish.<BR>2 To leave unfinished.<BR>3 To go or move.<BR>(शठयति)<BR>1 To speak ill.<BR>2 To speak well.<BR>3 To abstain from speaking.<BR>(शाठयते)<BR>To flatter, to coax, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ<BR>mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं)<BR>Wicked, depraved, perverse, dishonest.<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 An umpire, a mediator, an arbitrator.<BR>2 A rogue, a knave.<BR>3 A blockhead, a fool.<BR>4 An idler.<BR>5 A false husband or lover, one who pretends affection to one female whilst his heart is fixed on another.<BR>6 Thorn apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>n. (-ठं)<BR>1 A sort of root, commonly Tagara.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>3 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>शठ to be wicked, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठता
शठता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Wickedness, depravity.<BR>E.<BR>शट wicked, तल् aff.; also शठत्व n. (-त्वं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शड
शड<BR>(इ) शडि r. 1st cl. (शंडते)<BR>1 To disease or disorder.<BR>2 To hurt or wound.<BR>3 To collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
शण<BR>r. 1st cl. (शणति)<BR>1 To give.<BR>2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
शण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>2 Bengal Saṇ, a plant from which a kind of hemp is prepared, (Crotolaria juncea and other kinds.)<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शण to give, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणतन्तु
शणतन्तु<BR>f. (-न्तुः)<BR>The thread or string made of the flax of the Crotolaria juncea.<BR>E.<BR>शण, and तन्तु string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणतान्तव
शणतान्तव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Made of Saṇ string.<BR>E.<BR>शणतन्तु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=826" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणपर्णी
शणपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>E.<BR>शण Saṇ, and पर्ण a leaf, having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणपुष्पिका
शणपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Crotolaria of several species.<BR>E.<BR>शण the Saṇ, पुष्प a flower, aff. ङीष्, and कन् added, fem. form, implying resemblance; also शणपुष्पी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणसूत्र|शणसूत्रं
शणसूत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 The fibre or flax of the Saṇ plant, or string made from it.<BR>2 A net made of hemp or of Saṇ, or the thread of the Crotolaria juncea.<BR>3 Cordage, twine.<BR>E.<BR>शण hemp, &c. सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणालु
शणालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणीर|शणीरं
शणीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A rock or small island in the midst of the river Śoṇa.<BR>2 An insular spot inclosed by the branches of the Serjū, where it falls into the Ganges above Cūprah, at Bhṛgurāśrama or Bageressan; called also, the bank of the Dardarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड|शंड|शण्डं|शंडः|शण्डः
शण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A bull at liberty.<BR>2 A eunuch.<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>A multitude of lotus flowers.<BR>E.<BR>शण or षण to give, aff. ड, hence also षण्ड, and differently derived, शण्ठ or षण्ट the more usual form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डता
शण्डता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The state of a bull let loose or at liberty.<BR>2 Emasculation.<BR>E.<BR>शण्ड a bull at liberty, &c. तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डिल|शण्डिलः
शण्डिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The name of a Muni, and ancestor of a particular family of Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>शण्ड a eunuch, and इलच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ढ|शंढ|शंढः|शण्ढः
शण्ढ<BR>m. (-ण्ढः)<BR>1 A eunuch.<BR>2 A eunuch or emasculated attendant, as employed in a Haram or seraglio.<BR>3 An impotent man.<BR>4 A bull at liberty.<BR>5 A mad man or a drunken man.<BR>E.<BR>शम to bear or endure, Uṇādi aff. ढ; also षण्ढ and शण्ड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत|शतं
शत<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक|शतकः
शतक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A hundred.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A century, a cento, a collection of one hundred stanzas, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकीर्त्ति|शतकीर्ति|शतकीर्त्तिः
शतकीर्त्ति<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>A Jina or Jaina pontiff of the last age.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकुम्भ|शतकुंभ|शतकुम्भः
शतकुम्भ<BR>n. (-म्भं)<BR>Gold.<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>The name of a mountain.<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>A plant, (Phyalis flexuosa.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and कुम्भ a water jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकोटि|शतकोटिः
शतकोटि<BR>m. (-टिः)<BR>INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and कोटि edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक्रतु|शतक्रतुः
शतक्रतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, क्रतु sacrifice; a hundred Aśvamedhas or sacrifices of an unbroken horse, elevating the sacrificer to the place and title of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतखाण्ड
शतखाण्ड<BR>n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतगु
शतगु<BR>mfn. (-गुः-गुः-गु)<BR>Possessed of a hundred cows, with as many, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शत and गु for गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतगुण
शतगुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>A hundred times, a hundred fold.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and गुण a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतघ्नी
शतघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>1 A weapon; it is generally supposed to be a sort of fire arms, or the ancient Indian rocket, but it is also described as a stone set round with iron spikes.<BR>2 A female scorpion.<BR>3 A plant, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>4 A disease of the throat, apparently enlargement of the tonsils.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, हन to kill, aff. अण् and ङीष्, and the radical letters changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतच्छद|शतच्छदः
शतच्छद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The wood-pecker.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, च्छद a feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततम|शततमः
शततम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>Hundredth.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, तमट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततारा
शततारा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The constellation Śatabhiṣā, q. v.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred or many, and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतद्रु|शतद्रुः
शतद्रु<BR>f. (-द्रुः)<BR>The Setlej river, which rises in the Himālaya mountains, in the vicinity it is supposed of the Rāvanhrad or lake, and running to the S. W.unites in the Pañjāb with the Beyah or Vipāśā, when it forms the Hyphasis of the Greeks, and falls into the Indus below Multan.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred (fold, or in a hundred branches), द्रु to flow, Uṇādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतद्वार
शतद्वार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hundred-gated, having a hundred or a number of doors or outlets.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधा
शतधा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>ind.<BR>In a hundred ways, a hundredfold.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred (blossoms), धा to have, क and टाप् affs. or शत the same, and घाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधामन्
शतधामन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, (i. e. many,) घामन् body; being multiplied in as many shapes as the creation exhibits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधार|शतधारं
शतधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Flowing in many streams.<BR>2 Having many edges, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, घारा an edge, टच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधृति|शतधृतिः
शतधृति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and धृति sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपत्र|शतपत्रं|शतपत्रः
शतपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A lotus in general, (Nelumbium speciosum or Nymphæa nelumbo).<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>3 A wood-pecker.<BR>4 A parrot, the king parrot or Loory.<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>A woman.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, पत्र a leaf or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपत्रक|शतपत्रकः
शतपत्रक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The wood-pecker.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपथिक|शतपथिकः
शतपथिक<BR>mf. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Following a variety of paths or doctrines.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, पथिन् a road and figuratively a doctrine, aff. षिकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपदी
शतपदी<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A centipede, jaulus.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and पद a foot, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपद्म|शतपद्मं
शतपद्म<BR>n. (-द्मं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred (leaves), and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वन्|शतपर्वन्
शतपर्व्वन्<BR>m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>A bambu.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred or many, पर्व्वन् a joint or knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वा|शतपर्वा
शतपर्व्वा<BR>f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>1 Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>2 Orris root.<BR>3 The wife of ŚUKRA.<BR>4 Day of full moon in the month Āśvina.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, पर्व्वन् a joint or period, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्विका|शतपर्विका
शतपर्व्विका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 Bent grass or Dūb.<BR>2 Orris root.<BR>3 Barley.<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वेश|शतपर्वेश|शतपर्व्वेशः
शतपर्व्वेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The planet VENUS or its regent.<BR>E.<BR>शतपर्व्वा the wife of ŚUKRA, and ईश lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपाद्
शतपाद्<BR>f. (-पाद् or -पात्)<BR>A centipede.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and पाद् a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपादिका
शतपादिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>2 A centipede.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, पाद a foot or root, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपुष्प|शतपुष्पः
शतपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The poet BHĀRAVI, the author of the Kirātārjunīya.<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>A sort of dill or fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=827" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपुष्पिका
शतपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Anethum, (sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् fem. form, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोन|शतपोनः
शतपोन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोनक|शतपोनकः
शतपोनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Fistula in ano with many external openings.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोरक
शतपोरक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतप्रास|शतप्रासः
शतप्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and प्रास a dart, to which the leaves are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभिषज्
शतभिषज्<BR>f. (-षक्)<BR>One of the lunar asterisms, see the next.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, भिषज् a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभिषा
शतभिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>The twenty-fifth of the Nakṣatras or lunar mansions, containing 100 stars, one of which is λ Aquarii.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, भिषज् to cure, aff. ड; requiring many physicians; as the Hindus say DHANVANTARI himself cannot cure any person affected with disease, whilst the moon is in this asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभीरु|शतभीरुः
शतभीरु<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>Arabian jasmine, (J. zambac.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred (dangers), भीरु timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमख|शतमखः
शतमख<BR>m. (-स्वः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and मख a sacrifice: the performance of a hundred Aśvamedhas obtaining this situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमन्यु|शतमन्युः
शतमन्यु<BR>m. (-न्युः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and मन्यु a sacrifice; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमान|शतमानः
शतमान<BR>mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>1 A Pala of silver.<BR>2 An Āḍhaka or measure so termed.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमारिन्
शतमारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A man who has killed a hundred others.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and मारिन् a killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमार्ज|शतमार्जः
शतमार्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः)<BR>An armourer, a cutler.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, (many, weapons,) and मार्ज who cleans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमुख
शतमुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>1 Having a hundred mouths.<BR>2 Having a hundred openings or outlets.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and मुस्व mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमूली
शतमूली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred or many, मूल a root, fem. aff. ङीष्; also with कन् added शतमूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतयष्टिक|शतयष्टिकः
शतयष्टिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A necklace of 100 strings.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, यष्टि a string, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतलक्ष
शतलक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A hundred Lakhs, ten millions.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and लक्ष a hundred thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतलुम्पक|शतलुम्पकः
शतलुम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A name of the poet BHĀRAVI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवर्ष
शतवर्ष<BR>mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं)<BR>Of a hundred years, a century old.<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>A century.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and वर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवीर्य्या|शतवीर्या
शतवीर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>White Dūb grass, (Panicum dactylon with white blossoms.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, वीय्य seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवेधिन्
शतवेधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>A sort of dock or sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha or Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, व्यध to pierce, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशस्
शतशस्<BR>ind.<BR>By hundreds, a hundred fold.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशाख
शतशाख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>1 Having many branches.<BR>2 Multiform, various.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्र|शतसहस्रं
शतसहस्र<BR>n. (-स्रं)<BR>A hundred thousand.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्रशस्
शतसहस्रशस्<BR>ind.<BR>By myriads.<BR>E.<BR>शस् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसाहस्र
शतसाहस्र<BR>mfn. (-स्रः-स्री-स्रं)<BR>Having a hundred thousand, bought with, consisting of, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शतसहस्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतह्रदा
शतह्रदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>2 The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, ह्रद a ray of light, or ह्राद sound, and the vowel made short; read also, शतह्रादा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताक्ष
शताक्ष<BR>mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>Hundred eyed.<BR>f. (-क्षी)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa).<BR>3 The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताङ्ग|शतांग|शताङ्गः
शताङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A car, a chariot.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानक|शतानकं
शतानक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A place where dead bodies are burnt or buried, a burial ground, a cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, आनक a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानन्द|शतानंद|शतानन्दः
शतानन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>1 BRAHMĀ.<BR>2 VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>3 The car of VIṢṆU.<BR>4 The Muni GAUTAMA, the founder of the logical school of philosophy.<BR>5 The eldest son of GAUTAMA, (according to the Rāmāyaṇa,) and Purohita or religious adviser of JANAKA of Mithila.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred or many, and आनन्द who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानीक|शतानीकः
शतानीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An old man.<BR>2 The name of a sovereign, the son and successor of JANAMEJAYA.<BR>3 The name of a saint, the pupil of VYĀSA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, आङ् before नी to obtain, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतायुस्
शतायुस्<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A man a hundred years old, an old man.<BR>E.<BR>शत, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतार|शतारं
शतार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The thunderbolt.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, ऋ to go, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतारुस्
शतारुस्<BR>nf. (-रुः-रुषी)<BR>A leprous disease of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>शत hundred or many, and अरुस् a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतार्णा
शतार्णा<BR>f. (-र्णा)<BR>A plant, (Anethum sowa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावर|शतावरः
शतावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A fine of a hundred (Paṇas, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>शत, and अवर inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावरी
शतावरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A shrub, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>2 The wife of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred (roots), आङ् before वृ to choose, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावर्त्त|शतावर्त|शतावर्तः|शतावर्त्तः
शतावर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावर्त्तिन्|शतावर्तिन्
शतावर्त्तिन्<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, आवर्त्त revolving, (appearances, or in the mind of his worshippers), इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताह्वा
शताह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा-ह्वी)<BR>A sort of dill or fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and आह्ना name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिक|शतिकः
शतिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Indicative of a hundred, (as a sign or omen.)<BR>2 Doing or effecting any thing with a hundred.<BR>3 Bearing tax or interest per hundred.<BR>4 Bought with a hundred.<BR>5 Changed with or for a hundred, &c.<BR>6 Relating or belonging to a hundred.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, and ठक or ठञ् or ठन् aff.; also with यत् aff. शत्य in the same acceptations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेर|शतेरः
शतेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>2 Injury, detriment, hurt.<BR>E.<BR>शद to decay, to go, Uṇādi aff. एरक, and द changed to त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेश|शतेशः
शतेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The ruler or head man of a hundred (villages).<BR>E.<BR>शत, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्त्रि
शत्त्रि<BR>m. (-त्त्रिः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, त्त्रिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्य|शत्यः
शत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>Bought with a hundred, &c. see शतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रु|शत्रुः
शत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>1 An enemy, a foe, an adversary.<BR>2 A political enemy, a neighbouring prince as being one with whom disputes are likely to occur.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, Uṇādi aff. त्रुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=828" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुंसह
शत्रुंसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Bearing or patient with an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, सह to bear, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघात
शत्रुघात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Who beats or kills an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, and घात who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघ्न|शत्रुघ्नः
शत्रुघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Killing a foe.<BR>m. (-घ्नः)<BR>The second brother of RĀMACANDRA, the son of SUMITRĀ, and uterine brother of LAKṢMAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु an enemy, and घ्न destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघ्नजननी
शत्रुघ्नजननी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>SUMITRĀ, the mother of LAKṢMAṆA, and ŚATRUGHNA.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रुघ्न ŚATRUGHNA, and जननी the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुञ्जय|शत्रुंजय|शत्रुंजयः|शत्रुञ्जयः
शत्रुञ्जय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Subduing an enemy.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The mountain Vimala, or Girnār, or a mountainous range in Guzerat.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु a foe, जि to conquer, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुता
शत्रुता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Hostility, enmity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to शत्रु; also शत्रुत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुनिकाय
शत्रुनिकाय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A number or host of enemies.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, and निकाय a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुनिलय
शत्रुनिलय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The dwelling of a foe.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, and निलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुन्तप|शत्रुंतप|शत्रुन्तपः
शत्रुन्तप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Humbling or subduing enemies.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, तप to harass, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुपक्ष|शत्रुपक्षः
शत्रुपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>An antagonist, an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु, and पक्ष side or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुमर्द्दन|शत्रुमर्दन|शत्रुमर्दनः|शत्रुमर्द्दनः
शत्रुमर्द्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>ŚATRUGHNA, the brother of RĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु a foe, मर्द्दन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्वरी
शत्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, क्वरप् aff.; fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद|शदः
शद<BR>(औ ऌ) औ शदॢ r. 1st and 6th cls. (शीयते)<BR>1 To perish gradually, to wither or decay.<BR>2 To fall.<BR>3 To throw down.<BR>4 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद|शदः
शद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A vegetable, any edible vegetable product, as fruits, roots, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शद to wither, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रि|शद्रिः
शद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>3 ARJUNA.<BR>f. (-द्रिः)<BR>Lightning.<BR>4 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रु|शद्रुः
शद्रु<BR>mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>1 Wasting, decaying.<BR>2 Going, moving.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकावली
शनकावली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A shrub, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनपर्णी
शनपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनि|शनिः
शनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The planet SATURN or its regent.<BR>E.<BR>शो to destroy, or शण to give, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिज
शनिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Black pepper.<BR>E.<BR>शनि SATURN, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रसू
शनिप्रसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>CHĀYA, the wife of the sun.<BR>E.<BR>शनि SATURN, and प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रिय|शनिप्रियं
शनिप्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The emerald or sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>शनि SATURN, and प्रिय dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिवार|शनिवारः
शनिवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Saturday.<BR>E.<BR>शनि the planet, and वार in this and similar compounds, a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैश्चर|शनैश्चरः
शनैश्चर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The planet SATURN or its mythological personification.<BR>E.<BR>शनैस् slowly, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 Slowly, tardily.<BR>2 Independantly, at will.<BR>E.<BR>शण to give, (to produce,) aff. ऐम्, and the consonant changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix of assent or acceptance, as शप्करोति he accepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप|शपः
शप<BR>r. 1st cl. (शपति-ते) r. 4th cl. (शप्यति-ते)<BR>1 To revile, to wish evil or imprecations on, to curse, to swear.<BR>2 To take an oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप|शपः
शप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 An oath.<BR>2 An imprecation, a curse, cursing.<BR>3 A corpse; also शव.<BR>E.<BR>शप to curse, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथ|शपथः
शपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 An oath, asseveration by oath or ordeal.<BR>2 An imprecation, a curse.<BR>3 Cursing, wishing ill to.<BR>E.<BR>शप to swear, Uṇādi aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपन|शपनं
शपन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An oath, confirmation of the truth by oath or ordeal.<BR>2 Abuse, imprecation, cursing, malediction.<BR>E.<BR>शप to curse, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपमान
शपमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Revilling, imprecating.<BR>2 Swearing.<BR>E.<BR>शप to curse, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त|शप्तः
शप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>1 Cursed, anathematised.<BR>2 Sworn, taken as an oath.<BR>m. (-प्तः)<BR>A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum).<BR>E.<BR>शप to curse, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफ|शफं|शफः
शफ<BR>mn. (-फः-फं)<BR>1 A hoof in general.<BR>2 The root of a tree.<BR>3 The hoof of a horse.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be tranquil, aff. अच्, and the final changed to फ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफर|शफरः
शफर<BR>mf. (-रः-री)<BR>A small fish, (Cyprinus Sophore HAM.)<BR>E.<BR>शफ a hoof, रा to give, (to resemble,) aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफराधिप|शफराधिपः
शफराधिप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The Ilisha or Hilsa fish, (Ilisha clupanodon.)<BR>E.<BR>शफर a carp, and अधिप chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द<BR>r. 10th cl. (शब्दयति)<BR>To sound, to make or utter sound;<BR>with the prefixes प्र, प्रति, or वि, as well as uncompounded, this root means also:<BR>1 To promise.<BR>2 To make clear or manifest, to explain.<BR>3 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द<BR>m. (-ब्दः)<BR>1 Sound in general.<BR>2 A sound, a word.<BR>4 (In grammar,) A declinable word, as noun, pronoun, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दकार|शब्दकारः
शब्दकार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Making sound, sounding, sonorous.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, &c. कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दग्रह|शब्दग्रहः
शब्दग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 Receiving or catching sound.<BR>3 A fabulous arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, ग्रह what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचोर|शब्दचोरः
शब्दचोर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A plagiary.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and चोर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sounding, sonorous.<BR>(-नं)<BR>Sounding, uttering sounds.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द to sound, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दब्रह्मन्
शब्दब्रह्मन्<BR>n. (-ह्म)<BR>Inspired writ, the Vedas as uncreated and identifiable with the supreme spirit.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and ब्रह्मन् the supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दभेदिन्
शब्दभेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A name of ARUṆA.<BR>2 The anus.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, noise, and भेदिन् breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दयोनि|शब्दयोनिः
शब्दयोनि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>A root, a radical word.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and योनि place of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवेधिन्
शब्दवेधिन्<BR>m. (-धी)<BR>ARJUNA.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, and वेधिन् piercing; terrifying his enemies by his shouts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशक्ति|शब्दशक्तिः
शब्दशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Force or signification of words.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशासन
शब्दशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The rules of grammar.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and शासन regulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशास्त्र
शब्दशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Philology, grammar, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and शास्त्र a science, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसंग्रह
शब्दसंग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A vocabulary, a lexicon.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and संग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दादि
शब्दादि<BR>m. (-दिः)<BR>The objects of sense, as sound, form, scent, juice, contact; or what affords matter for the exercise of hearing, seeing, smelling, tasting and touching.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and आदि other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाधिष्ठान|शब्दाधिष्ठानं
शब्दाधिष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The ear.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, अधिष्ठान receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=829" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुरूप
शब्दानुरूप<BR>n. (-पं)<BR>1 Conformity or proportion to the sound.<BR>2 Imitation of sound.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and अनुरूप conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुशासन
शब्दानुशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The acceptation or sense of words.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and अनुशासन government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दायमान
शब्दायमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sounding.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound, nominal verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दार्थ|शब्दार्थः
शब्दार्थ<BR>m. (-र्थः)<BR>1 The sense or meaning of words.<BR>2 Words and sense.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and अर्थं sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दालङ्कार|शब्दालंकार|शब्दालंकारः
शब्दालङ्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Rhetorical use of words; verbal figure, as alliteration, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द, and अलङ्कार ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दित
शब्दित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sounded.<BR>2 Uttered, articulated.<BR>3 Explained, made public or manifest.<BR>4 Converted into a noun, &c. शब्द to sound, क्त aff.; or शब्द, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम|शमः
शम<BR>r. 4th cl. (इर् उ) इरशमु (शाम्यति)<BR>1 To be pacified, to be calmed or appeased.<BR>2 To pacify, to calm.<BR>3 To be tranquil, to have the passions tamed and quiescent.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शमयते)<BR>To look, to look at or inspect.<BR>(शमयति)<BR>To allay, to appease.<BR>(शामयति)<BR>To display.<BR>With उप prefixed,<BR>To tranquillize, to allay, to tame.<BR>With नि,<BR>1 To hear.<BR>2 To restrain or prevent.<BR>With प्र,<BR>1 To destroy.<BR>2 To be very tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम|शमः
शम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Quiet of mind, stoicism, indifference, the absence of passion, as one of the qualities of the Vedāntī or follower of the Vedānta doctrine; it is defined to be the exclusion of every idea not derived from the precepts of that philosophy, and is so far synonymous^1 with abstract meditation on BRAHMĀ, or GOD.<BR>2 Quiet, tranquillity, rest, calm, (in general.)<BR>3 Final happiness, emancipation from human existence.<BR>4 Cure, convalescence, alleviation of pain or disease.<BR>5 Abuse, imprecation, malediction.<BR>6 The hand.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be pacified or calm, aff. घञ्, and the vowel not made long.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमक|शमकः
शमक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Pacifier, pacificator, tranquillizing.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be tranquil, ण्वुल् aff., of attributive agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथ|शमथः
शमथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Quiet, tranquillity, (see the last.)<BR>2 A counsellor, a minister.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be calm, Uṇādi aff. अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing animals for sacrifice, immolation.<BR>2 Mental tranquillity, calmness, indifference.<BR>3 Abuse, malediction.<BR>4 Hurt, injury.<BR>5 Chewing.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 YAMA, the ruler of Tartarus.<BR>2 An antelope.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be tranquil, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनस्वसृ
शमनस्वसृ<BR>f. (-सा)<BR>Yamunā or Jumna the personified river.<BR>E.<BR>शमन YAMA, and स्वसृ the sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीषद|शमनीषदः
शमनीषद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A Rākṣasa, an evil spirit, a goblin.<BR>E.<BR>शमन night, षद who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमयत्
शमयत्<BR>mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>1 Appeasing. allaying.<BR>2 Terminating, stopping.<BR>E.<BR>शम to pacify, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमल|शमलं
शमल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Fœces, ordure.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be quiet, Uṇādi aff. कल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमान्तक|शमांतक|शमान्तकः
शमान्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The deity KĀMA or love.<BR>E.<BR>शम mental or devotional tranquillity, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमि|शमिः
शमि<BR>f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>A legume or pod.<BR>f. (-मी)<BR>1 The Śami tree, (Acacia suma, Rox.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>E.<BR>शम to pacify (sickness,) aff. इन्, ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित|शमितः
शमित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Pacified, appeased.<BR>2 Quiet, tranquil, sedate, calm.<BR>3 Alleviated, relieved.<BR>4 Tempered, moderated.<BR>5 Relaxed, intermitted.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be pacified or calm, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Tranquil, pacific, tranquillized.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be tranquil, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिर|शमिरः
शमिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A variety of the Śami tree.<BR>E.<BR>शमी the Śami tree, रा to get, (to resemble,) aff. क, and the vowel made short; also शमीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिरोह|शमिरोहः
शमिरोह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शमि for शमी the Śami tree, and रोह who ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीगर्भ|शमीगर्भः
शमीगर्भ<BR>m. (-र्भः)<BR>1 A man of the sacerdotal class, a Brahman.<BR>2 A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>शमी the mimosa, (the wood of which is essential for certain sacrifices, &c.) and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीधान्य|शमीधान्यं
शमीधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Pulse, grain which grows in legumes or pods.<BR>E.<BR>शमी a legume, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीपत्री
शमीपत्री<BR>f. (-त्री)<BR>A sort of Sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR>E.<BR>शमी Acacia Suma, and पत्र the leaf; having a similar leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीर|शमीरः
शमीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A small variety of the Mimosa Suma.<BR>E.<BR>शमी the Śami tree, and र aff. of diminution; also sometimes read शमिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पा|शंपा
शम्पा<BR>f. (-म्पा)<BR>Lightning.<BR>E.<BR>शम् happiness, पा to drink, क, and टाप् aff.; destroying pleasure by its awful appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पाक|शंपाक|शम्पाकः
शम्पाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A kind of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>2 Bringing to maturity or ripeness, cooking, maturing.<BR>3 The lac pigment.<BR>E.<BR>शम् pleasure, and पाक what matures; also सम्पाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब|शंब|शम्बः
शम्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (शम्बति)<BR>To go.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शम्बयति)<BR>To accumulate, to collect or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब|शंब|शम्बः
शम्ब<BR>mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>Happy, fortunate.<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>1 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>2 The iron head of a pestle.<BR>3 An iron chain worn round the loins.<BR>4 The second ploughing of a field.<BR>E.<BR>शम् happiness, and ब possessive aff., or शम्ब to accumulate, aff. अच्: it is also read संव, शंव, and सम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शम्बर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A religious observance.<BR>3 Wealth.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A Daitya.<BR>2 A sort of deer.<BR>3 A mountain.<BR>4 A fish in general.<BR>5 War.<BR>6 Best, excellent.<BR>7 A Bauddha.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A drug or medicinal plant, (Anthericum tuberosum.)<BR>2 A female juggler.<BR>E.<BR>शम्ब to accumulate, अरन् aff., or शं happiness, वृ to choose, aff. अप्; also read शंवर, and सम्बर or संवर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरसूदन|शंबरसूदन|शम्बरसूदनः
शम्बरसूदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A name of KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>शम्बर the Daitya, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरारि|शंबरारि|शम्बरारिः
शम्बरारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>KĀMA, the Hindu deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>शम्बर the Daitya, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलं|शंबलः|शम्बलः
शम्बल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Provender for a journey, stock for travelling expences.<BR>2 A bank, a shore.<BR>3 Envy, impatience or dislike of another's success.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A procuress, a bawd.<BR>E.<BR>शम्ब to go, to collect, अलच् aff.; also शंवल, and सम्बल or संवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बाकृत|शम्बाकृतं
शम्बाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Twice ploughed, (a field.)<BR>E.<BR>शम्ब a second ploughing, कृत made, and डाच् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बु|शंबु|शंबुः|शम्बुः
शम्बु<BR>m. (-म्बुः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>see शम्बूक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक|शंबुक|शंबुकः|शम्बुकः
शम्बुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bivalve shell: see शम्बूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक्क|शंबुक्क|शंबुक्कः|शम्बुक्कः
शम्बुक्क<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>A bivalve shell: see the next, शम्बूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बूक|शंबूक|शंबूकः|शम्बूकः
शम्बूक<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A conch shell.<BR>2 A snail.<BR>3 A Śūdra, who had become a devotee in the time of RĀMACANDRA, and was slain by him.<BR>4 The edge of the frontal protuberance of the elephant.<BR>5 The name of a [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">Page831</a>] Daitya.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be tranquil, ऊकन् aff., and वुक् augment; also with the vowel short, शम्बुक, and the final consonant then rejected, शम्बु; it is also read, शम्बुक्क, and with the first vowel long, शाम्बूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=830" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भ|शंभ|शंभः|शम्भः
शम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>1 INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>2 The iron bound head of a club or pestle.<BR>3 A happy man.<BR>E.<BR>शम् particle of auspiciousness, भा to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भली|शंभली
शम्भली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A bawd, a procuress.<BR>E.<BR>शम् pleasure, भल to describe, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भु|शंभु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शम्भु<BR>m. (-म्भुः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 A Jina or Jaina sanctified teacher.<BR>4 A Siddha, a demi-divine being.<BR>5 A sage, a venerable man.<BR>9 A kind of Asclepias.<BR>E.<BR>शम् auspicious particle, भू to be, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुतनय|शंभुतनय|शंभुतनयः|शम्भुतनयः
शम्भुतनय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 GAṆEŚA.<BR>E.<BR>शम्भु ŚIVA, and तनय son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुनन्दन|शंभुनंदन|शंभुनन्दन|शंभुनन्दनः|शम्भुनन्दनः
शम्भुनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>2 A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शम्भु ŚIVA, and नन्दन son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुप्रिया|शंभुप्रिया
शम्भुप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Emblic myrobalan.<BR>2 An epithet of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शम्भु ŚIVA, and प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्या
शम्या<BR>f. (-म्या)<BR>1 The pin of a yoke.<BR>2 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>3 A stick, a staff.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be kept quiet, य aff., fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्यापात|शम्यापातः
शम्यापात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The cast of a stick.<BR>E.<BR>शम्या, and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय|शयः
शय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यी-यं)<BR>Asleep, sleeping.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A hand.<BR>2 A snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>3 Sleep, sleeping.<BR>4 A bed, a couch.<BR>5 Abuse, imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, aff. घ, or टच् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयण्ड|शयंड|शयण्डः
शयण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>Asleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, अण्डच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयथ|शयथः
शयथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>Asleep, sleeping.<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>2 A sort of snake, the Boa.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, अथच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयन|शयनं
शयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Sleep.<BR>2 A bed, a couch.<BR>3 Copulation.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनगृह
शयनगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A bed chamber.<BR>E.<BR>शयन, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनागार|शयनागारः
शयनागार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bed chamber.<BR>E.<BR>शयन, and आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीय|शयनीयं
शयनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Fit for or suitable to sleep, to be slept on, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A bed, a couch.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, अनीयर् aff. of the future participle; also with कन् added शयनीयक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनैकादशी
शयनैकादशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The eleventh day of the light half of Āṣārha, on which VIṢṆU'S sleep commences.<BR>E.<BR>शयन, and एकादशी eleventh lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयान|शयानः
शयान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sleeping, asleep.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयानक|शयानकः
शयानक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A snake.<BR>2 A chamæleon, a lizard.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, आनक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयालु|शयालुः
शयालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Sleepy, slothful, sluggish.<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>1 A snake, the Boa.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>3 A Shakāl.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, आलुच् aff.; implying disposition or habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित|शयितः
शयित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Asleep.<BR>m. (-तं)<BR>A plant, (Cordia myxa).<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Sleep, sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयितवत्
शयितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sleeping, asleep.<BR>E.<BR>शीङ् to sleep, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित्वा
शयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having slept.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयु|शयुः
शयु<BR>m. (-युः)<BR>A large snake, (Boa.)<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, and उ Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुन|शयुनः
शयुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A large kind of snake, (Boa.)<BR>E.<BR>शीङ् to sleep, Uṇādi aff. उनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्या
शय्या<BR>f. (-य्या)<BR>1 A bed, a couch, a sofa.<BR>2 Tying in knots, stringing.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, क्यप् aff., and अयङ् substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर|शरं|शरः
शर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A sort of reed or grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 The upper part or cream of slightly curdled milk.<BR>4 Mischief, injury, hurt.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 Versed sine of an arc.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, aff. अप्, also सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरकाण्ड|शरकांड|शरकाण्डः
शरकाण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The stem of the Saccharum.<BR>2 The shaft of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and काण्ड stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरच्चन्द्र|शरच्चंद्र|शरच्चन्द्रः
शरच्चन्द्र<BR>m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>The autumnal moon.<BR>E.<BR>शरट्, and चन्द्र moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरज|शरजं|शरजः
शरज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Butter made from new milk or milk one day old.<BR>E.<BR>शर cream, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरजन्मन्
शरजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A name of KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शर a sort of grass, and जन्मन् birth: having been brought up in thickets of that grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरट|शरटः
शरट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>2 Safflower, the plant.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, अटन् aff.; also सरट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण|शरणं
शरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 A preserver, a protector, what or who protects or preserves.<BR>3 Preservation, protection, defence.<BR>4 Killing, slaying.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E.<BR>श to injure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणागत|शरणागतः
शरणागत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Refugee, appellant, one who comes for protection or refuge.<BR>E.<BR>शरण protection, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणापन्न
शरणापन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Taken refuge.<BR>E.<BR>शरण, and आपन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणार्थिन्
शरणार्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Unfortunate, wretched, involved in calamity or ruin, and dependant on others for protection or aid.<BR>E.<BR>शरण protection, and अर्थिन् soliciting, requiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणार्पक|शरणार्पकः
शरणार्पक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Unfortunate, calamitous, distressed, ruined, (see the last.)<BR>E.<BR>शरण protection, aid, and अर्पक who causes to be afforded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणि|शरणिः
शरणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>A road, a path, a way.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, अनि aff., more usually सरणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणैषिन्
शरणैषिन्<BR>mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि)<BR>Seeking for an asylum or protection.<BR>E.<BR>शरण, and एषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्ड|शरंड|शरंडः|शरण्डः
शरण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 A bird in general.<BR>2 A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>3 A kind of ornament.<BR>4 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>5 A libertine, a lecher.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, (fruit, &c.) अण्डन् Uṇādi aff.; also सरण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
शरण्य<BR>mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>To be protected or aided, poor, miserable, helpless.<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>1 A protection, a protector, that which or who affords refuge and defence.<BR>2 A house.<BR>3 Protection, defence.<BR>4 Injury, hurt.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, Uṇādi अन्य; or शरण protection, and यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्यु|शरण्युः
शरण्यु<BR>m. (-ण्युः)<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>2 Wind, air.<BR>3 A protector, a defender.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, अन्यु aff.; also सरण्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्कामिन्
शरत्कामिन्<BR>m. (-मी)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>शरट् autumn, and कामिन् desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्काल|शरत्कालः
शरत्काल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The autumnal season.<BR>E.<BR>शरत्, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्कालीन
शरत्कालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Autumnal.<BR>E.<BR>शरत्काल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्पर्व्वन्|शरत्पर्वन्
शरत्पर्व्वन्<BR>n. (-र्व्व)<BR>A festival, on the full moon of Āśvina, (September-October): see कोजागर.<BR>E.<BR>शरट् autumn, and पर्व्वन् a holiday^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्
शरद्<BR>f. (-रत् or रट्)<BR>1 The season of autumn or the sultry season; the two months succeeding the rains; according to the Vaidikas, comprising the months Bhādra and Āśvina, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">Page832</a>] and according to the Paurāṇikas, Āśvina and Kārttika, fluctuating thus from August to November.<BR>2 A year.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, अदि Uṇādi aff.; also with टाप् added शरदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=831" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदा
शरदा<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A year.<BR>2 The sultry season.<BR>E.<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदिज|शरदिजं
शरदिज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Autumnal, produced in Śarat or the season of autumn.<BR>E.<BR>शरट् as above in the 7th case, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरधि|शरधिः
शरधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A quiver.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, धा to have or contain, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरन्मुख
शरन्मुख<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>Commencement of the spring season.<BR>E.<BR>शरट्, and मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपात|शरपातः
शरपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>An arrow's fall or flight.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपातस्थान
शरपातस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A bowshot, an arrow's flight.<BR>E.<BR>शरपात, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपुङ्खा|शरपुंखा
शरपुङ्खा<BR>f. (-ङ्खा)<BR>The feathers of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, and पुङ्ख the feathered part of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरफल
शरफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The blade or barb of an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and फल blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभ|शरभः
शरभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A fabulous animal, supposed to have eight legs, and to inhabit particularly the snowy mountains.<BR>2 A young elephant.<BR>3 A monkey in RAMA'S army.<BR>4 A camel.<BR>5 A grasshopper.<BR>6 A locust.<BR>E.<BR>श to injure, Uṇādi aff. अभच् or शर an arrow, भा to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभू
शरभू<BR>m. (-भूः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शर the grass, and भू born; being reared in this grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरमय|शरमयं
शरमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of or consisting of Śara grass, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शर the grass, and मयट् aff. implying in this and other compounds change of form for any purpose except food or clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरमल्ल|शरमल्लः
शरमल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A small bird, considered a sa variety of the SArika or Maina, (Turdus gosalica, BUC. Mss.)<BR>E.<BR>शर the Śara grass, and मल्ल to hold or occupy, aff. अङ्; some authorities have शरमन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयु|शरयुः
शरयु<BR>f. (-युः-यू)<BR>The Seryu or Serjū river; it is preferably, and more usually written सरयु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरल|शरलः
शरल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Upright, honest.<BR>2 Crooked, fraudulent.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, a sort of pine.<BR>E.<BR>सृ to go, कलच् aff.; and स changed to श; whence the word is preferably read सरल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलक|शरलकं
शरलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलता
शरलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Uprightness, sincerity.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to शरल; also with त्व, शरलत्व; also सरलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव
शरव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A lid, a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवणोद्भव|शरवणोद्भवः
शरवणोद्भव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शर saccharum, वन a thicket or jungle, and उद्भव born: see शरजन्मन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवर्ष|शरवर्षः
शरवर्ष<BR>m. (-र्षः)<BR>A flight or shower of arrows.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवर्षिन्
शरवर्षिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>Raining or shooting arrows.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and वर्षिन् showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवाणि|शरवाणिः
शरवाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>1 The head of an arrow.<BR>2 A foot soldier, an archer.<BR>3 A maker of arrows.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, वण to sound, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवृष्टि|शरवृष्टिः
शरवृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>A heavy fall or shower of arrows.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्य|शरव्यं
शरव्य<BR>n. (-व्यं)<BR>A mark, a butt.<BR>E.<BR>शरु a weapon, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराघात|शराघातः
शराघात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Shooting, (with a bow.)<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, and आघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराटि|शराटिः
शराटि<BR>f. (-टि)<BR>A sort of bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR>E.<BR>शर water or mischief, अट to go, aff. इन्; or from अत to go, शराति; and otherwise derived also शराडि and शरालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराडि|शराडिः
शराडि<BR>f. (-डिः)<BR>A bird: see शरालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराति|शरातिः
शराति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A bird: see शराटि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराभ्यास|शराभ्यासः
शराभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Archery, practice with the bow and arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारि|शरारिः
शरारि<BR>f. (-रिः)<BR>A sort of bird, commonly the Āli or Śarāli, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR>E.<BR>शर water or mischief, ऋ to go, aff. इ; also ल being substituted, शरालि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारीमुखी
शरारीमुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>Scissars.<BR>E.<BR>शरारी, मुख mouth or beak, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु<BR>mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>Mischievous, noxious, hurtful.<BR>E.<BR>शृ to hurt, आरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारोप|शरारोपः
शरारोप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>A bow.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, आरोप a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरालि|शरालिः
शरालि<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>Śarāli A kind of bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, अल to be equal to, (in speed,) aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added; also शरारि, शराडि, शराटि, &c., and with कन् added, fem. form शरालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराव|शरावं|शरावः
शराव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A lid, a cover.<BR>2 A shallow cup or dish.<BR>3 A platter.<BR>4 A measure equal to two Kuḍavas.<BR>E.<BR>शर mischief, (from it,) अव to preserve, aff. अण् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावती
शरावती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>A river so named.<BR>E.<BR>शर a sort of grass, मतुप् aff. fem. form, and the final of the first word made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराश्रय|शराश्रयः
शराश्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A quiver.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, and आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरासन|शरासनं
शरासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A bow.<BR>2 Shooting arrows.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, अस to throw, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराहत
शराहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck by an arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शर, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरिमन्
शरिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Bearing, bringing forth.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, इमनिच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीर|शरीरं
शरीर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The body.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, to be injured, Uṇādi aff. ईरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरक|शरीरकं|शरीरकः
शरीरक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A small or delicate body.<BR>2 The body.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and कन् diminutive, or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरकर्षण
शरीरकर्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Emaciating or afflicting the body.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and कर्षण attracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरज|शरीरजः
शरीरज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Born or produced by the body, &c.<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Sickness, disease.<BR>2 The deity KĀMA or love.<BR>3 A son.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर the body, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरजन्मन्
शरीरजन्मन्<BR>mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म)<BR>Born or produced of or from the body.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरपाक|शरीरपाकः
शरीरपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Decay, emaciation.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and पाक a ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरबन्धक|शरीरबंधक|शरीरबन्धकः
शरीरबन्धक<BR>m. (-क)<BR>A hostage.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and बन्धक a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरभाज्
शरीरभाज्<BR>mfn. (-भाक्)<BR>Embodied, corporeal, having body.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरयात्रा
शरीरयात्रा<BR>f. (-त्रा)<BR>Subsistence, support.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरयोग
शरीरयोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Bodily union.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरशुश्रूषा
शरीरशुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Personal attendance.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=832" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरशोषण
शरीरशोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Drying up, withering.<BR>2 Emaciating the body.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरसंस्कार|शरीरसंस्कारः
शरीरसंस्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Purification of the body by various ceremonies at conception, birth, initiation, death, &c.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Decoration or adorning the person.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and संस्कार making perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरावरण|शरीरावरणं
शरीरावरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The skin.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर the body, and आवरण enclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरिन्
शरीरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Embodied, corporeal, having body.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>An animal or sentient being.<BR>n. (-रि)<BR>Life or soul connected with the body, or incorporate.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर body, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरु|शरुः
शरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>1 Passion, anger.<BR>2 The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 Any weapon.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरेष्ट|शरेष्टः
शरेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>शर an arrow, and इष्ट desired; the blossoms of the mango being amongst those which tip the darts of CUPID.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करा
शर्करा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A potsherd, the fragment of a broken pot.<BR>2 A stony nodule, or gravel.<BR>3 A soil or spot abounding in stony or gritty fragments.<BR>4 Clayed or candid sugar.<BR>5 A part, a piece.<BR>6 Gravel, (the disease.)<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. करन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्कराप्रभा
शर्कराप्रभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The hell of gravel according to the Jainas, the second division of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>शर्करा gravel, and प्रभा illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करावत्|शर्करावन्त्
शर्करावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Gritty, gravelly, full of stony particles.<BR>E.<BR>शर्करा gravel, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिक|शर्करिकः
शर्करिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Stony, gravelly.<BR>E.<BR>शर्क्करा gravel, &c., and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिल|शर्करिलः
शर्करिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Abounding in stony or gravelly particles, (a spot, a place.)<BR>E.<BR>शर्करा gravel, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्घ
शर्घ<BR>r. 1st cl. (शर्घति)<BR>To wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्द्ध
शर्द्ध<BR>m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>Farting, a fart.<BR>E.<BR>शृध to fart, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्द्धञ्जह
शर्द्धञ्जह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Causing flatulence.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Any leguminous grain or pulse, as beans, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शर्द्ध farting, and हा to let go or loose, aff. खश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ब्ब|शर्ब
शर्ब्ब<BR>r. 1st cl. (शर्ब्बति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मद|शर्मद|शर्मदः
शर्म्मद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Conferring prosperity, making happy, propitious.<BR>E.<BR>शर्म्मन्, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मन्|शर्मन्
शर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Happy, glad.<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Happiness, pleasure.<BR>m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>A name or appellation common to and proper for Brahmans.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure or destroy, (ill fortune,) मनिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मवत्|शर्मवत्|शर्मवन्त्
शर्म्मवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Lucky, auspicious.<BR>E.<BR>शर्म्मन्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मर|शर्मर|शर्मरः|शर्म्मरः
शर्म्मर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A sort of garment or cloth.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A species of Curcuma, (C. zanthorhizon.)<BR>E.<BR>शर्म्म pleasure, रा to give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्य्या|शर्या
शर्य्या<BR>f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्व|शर्व|शर्वः|शर्व्वः
शर्व्व<BR>r. 1st cl. (शर्व्वति)<BR>To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्व|शर्व|शर्वः|शर्व्वः
शर्व्व<BR>m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. व; also सर्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वरी|शर्वरी
शर्व्वरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Night.<BR>2 A woman.<BR>3 Turmeric.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, अरच् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वला|शर्वला
शर्व्वला<BR>f. (-ला or ली)<BR>An iron crow.<BR>E.<BR>शर्व to go, कलच् aff.; also सर्व्वला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वाणी|शर्वाणी
शर्व्वाणी<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शर्व्व ŚIVA, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment; the wife of SARVA; also सर्वाणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वरीक|शर्वरीक
शर्व्वरीक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A low or vile man, a rogue, a wretch.<BR>2 A cruel or mischievous man.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, ईकन् Uṇādi aff., रक् augment, and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल|शलं|शलः
शल<BR>r. 1st cl. (शलते)<BR>1 To move, to shake, to tremble or stir.<BR>2 To cover.<BR>(-शलति)<BR>To go, to move to or towards.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शालयति)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल|शलं|शलः
शल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>The quill of a porcupine.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A name of BHṚṄGI, ŚIVA'S attendant.<BR>2 BRAHMĀ.<BR>3 A kind of field.<BR>4 A dart, a spear.<BR>5 A stake.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलक|शलकः
शलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spider.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलङ्ग|शलंग|शलंगः|शलङ्गः
शलङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A king.<BR>2 A sort of salt.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, Uṇādi aff. अङ्गच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलभ|शलभः
शलभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A grasshopper.<BR>2 A locust.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, अभच् Uṇādi aff.: see शरभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलल|शललं
शलल<BR>nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>The quill of a porcupine.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, to project, aff. कलच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाका
शलाका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A javelin, a dart.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A porcupine.<BR>4 The rib of an umbrella, the bar of a cage, &c. or any such small stake, rod, peg, or pin: it is applied also in common use, to a thin slip of bambu, serving when tipped with sulphur for a match; to a round pointed piece of wood or bambu serving as a toothpick, to a similar piece employed as a tent or probe, or to a larger one used as a ruler, &c.<BR>5 A bone.<BR>6 An oblong quadrangular piece of ivory or bone used in playing a particular game, a domino.<BR>7 A fibrous stick used as a brush or pencil.<BR>8 A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>9 The Sārika, (Turdus Gosalica, BUC.)<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, Uṇādi aff. आकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाकापरि
शलाकापरि<BR>ind.<BR>Beat at a game played with pieces of stick.<BR>E.<BR>शलाका a match, &c., and परि implying in this and similar compounds, reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाकापुरुष
शलाकापुरुष<BR>m. plu. (-षाः)<BR>Sixty-three persons considered by the Jainas as sacred and divine, viz. the 24 Jinas, 12 Cakravartīs, 9 Vāsudevas, 9 Baladevas, and 9 Prativāsudevas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाट|शलाटः
शलाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A cart load, considered as twenty times one hundred Palas.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, aff. आटन्, and the र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाटु|शलाटुः
शलाटु<BR>mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु)<BR>Unripe, moist, (as fruit.)<BR>m. (-टुः)<BR>A kind of root.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, आटु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाभोलि|शलाभोलिः
शलाभोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालु|शलालुः
शलालु<BR>n. (-लु)<BR>A sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालुक|शलालुकः
शलालुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Purchased with or procured for the substance termed Śalālu.<BR>E.<BR>शलालु as above, and ष्टन् aff.; also with ठक् aff. शालालुक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्क|शल्कं
शल्क<BR>n. (-ल्कं)<BR>1 A part, a portion.<BR>2 Bark, rind.<BR>3 The scale of a fish.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, Uṇādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कल|शल्कलं
शल्कल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The scale of a fish.<BR>2 Bark, rind.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कलिन्
शल्कलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>शल्कल a scale, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्किन्
शल्किन्<BR>m. (-ल्की)<BR>A fish.<BR>E.<BR>शल्क a scale, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्भ
शल्भ<BR>r. 1st cl. (शल्भते)<BR>1 To praise, to flatter or coax.<BR>2 To talk, to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=833" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मलि|शल्मलिः
शल्मलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>The silk-cotton tree: see शाल्मलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्य|शल्यं|शल्यः
शल्य<BR>mn. (-ल्यः-ल्यं)<BR>A dart, a javelin.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 A bambu rod or stake.<BR>2 Any stake or thorn.<BR>3 An arrow.<BR>4 An iron crow.<BR>5 Sin, crime.<BR>6 Difficulty, embarrassment, distress.<BR>7 An arrow, a thorn, or other extraneous substance which has lodged in the body.<BR>8 Abuse, defamation.<BR>9 Poison.<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>1 A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>2 A porcupine.<BR>3 A hedgehog.<BR>4 A peg, a pin, &c.<BR>5 A boundary.<BR>6 A king, the maternal uncle of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, aff. यत् or य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक|शल्यकः
शल्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A stake, a thorn.<BR>2 A dart, a pike.<BR>3 A porcupine.<BR>4 A hedgehog.<BR>5 A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>शल्य as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यकण्ठ|शल्यकंठ|शल्यकण्ठः
शल्यकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>A porcupine.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य a stake, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक्रिया
शल्यक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The extraction of extraneous substances lodged in the body.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यवत्|शल्यवन्त्
शल्यवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Shooting arrows.<BR>2 Set with stakes.<BR>3 Harassed with difficulties, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यवारङ्ग
शल्यवारङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The part by which an arrow or the like lodged in the body is to be laid hold of for its extraction.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य, and वारङ्ग the place of seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यशास्त्र
शल्यशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>That part of Surgery which treats of the extraction of extraneous substances lodged in the body.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य, and शास्त्र science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यारि|शल्यारिः
शल्यारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य the prince, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्योद्धार|शल्योद्धारः
शल्योद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Extraction of foreign substances from the body.<BR>2 Cleansing or purifying a new house.<BR>E.<BR>शल्य, and उद्घार taking out or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल|शल्लं|शल्लः
शल्ल<BR>m. (-ल्लः)<BR>A frog.<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>Bark, rind.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लक|शल्लकं|शल्लकः
शल्लक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Bark, rind.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A porcupine.<BR>2 The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, aff. क्वुन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लकीद्रव|शल्लकीद्रवः
शल्लकीद्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Incense, Olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>शल्लकी the Boswellia thurifera, and द्रव exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्व|शल्वः
शल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>A country so named in the north of India.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, क्वन् aff., more usually शाल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव|शवं|शवः
शव<BR>r. 1st cl. (शवति)<BR>1 To go or approach.<BR>2 To alter, to change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव|शवं|शवः
शव<BR>mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>A dead body, a corpse.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>शव to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवकाम्य|शवकाम्यः
शवकाम्य<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>शव a corpse, and काम्य desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवदाह|शवदाहः
शवदाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Burning a corpse.<BR>E.<BR>शव, and दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवदाहिन्
शवदाहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A person who burns a corpse.<BR>E.<BR>शव, and दाहिन् who burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवयान|शवयानं
शवयान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>The litter or bed on which a dead body is carried to be burnt.<BR>E.<BR>शव a corpse, and यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवर|शवरः
शवर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A barbarian, one inhabiting the mountainous districts of India, and wearing the feathers of the peacock, &c. as decorations.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 A name of ŚIVA.<BR>4 The hand.<BR>5 A Śāstra, a sacred treatise.<BR>E.<BR>शव a corpse, रा to take, aff. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवराल
शवराल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A sort of Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरालय|शवरालयः
शवरालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>The abode of an outcaste or low tribe.<BR>E.<BR>शवर a barbarian, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरावास|शवरावासः
शवरावास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The abode of an outcaste or barbarous tribe.<BR>E.<BR>शवर a barbarian, and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शवल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Variegated, of a variegated colour.<BR>2 Imitative.<BR>3 Articulate.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A variegated colour.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>1 A brindled cow.<BR>2 The cow of plenty, KĀMADHENU.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Water.<BR>2 A religious observance peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>E.<BR>शव to curse, कल aff., and प changed to व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवलता
शवलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Variegation, variety of colour.<BR>E.<BR>शवल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शवलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवलीकृत
शवलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Variegated.<BR>E.<BR>शवल, and कृत made, with च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसाधन
शवसाधन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A mystical and magical ceremony performed with a dead body.<BR>E.<BR>शव, and साधन implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसान|शवसानः
शवसान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A traveller, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A cemetery.<BR>E.<BR>शव to go, with असानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश|शशः
शश<BR>r. 1st cl. (शशति)<BR>To jump, to leap, to move by springing or leaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश|शशः
शश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 A hare or rabbit.<BR>2 The Lodh tree, (Symplocos racemosa.)<BR>3 Gum myrrh.<BR>4 A man of mild and virtuous character, but uxorious^1 and woman-led, one of the four characters in which men are classed by erotic writers.<BR>5 The spots on the moon, supposed to resemble the figure of a hare.<BR>E.<BR>शश to go by leaps or jumps, aff. अच.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशक|शशकः
शशक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशत्
शशत्<BR>mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>Leaping, jumping.<BR>E.<BR>शश to leap, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशधर|शशधरः
शशधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, and धर having; either as an emblem on his banners, or fancifully, as the spots on the moon's face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशप्लुतक|शशप्लुतकं
शशप्लुतक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mark or scratch of the finger nail.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, प्लुतक jumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशबिन्दु|शशबिंदु|शशबिन्दुः
शशबिन्दु<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU, or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 A sovereign.<BR>3 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शश a bare, and बिन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशभृत्
शशभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, and भृत् who cherishes: see शशधर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशमात्र
शशमात्र<BR>mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>As large as or of the size of a hare.<BR>E.<BR>शश, and मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलाञ्छन|शशलांछन|शशलाञ्छनः
शशलाञ्छन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शश, and लाञ्छन mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलोमन्
शशलोमन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>The skin of the hare or rabbit.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare or rabbit, and लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशविषाण
शशविषाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>The horn of a hare; any thing improbable or extraordinary.<BR>E.<BR>शश, and विषाण a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशस्थली
शशस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>The Doab, the country between the Ganges and Yamunā rivers.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, स्थल place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्क|शशांक|शशाङ्कः
शशाङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, and अङ्क a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्कलेखा|शशांकलेखा
शशाङ्कलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>A digit of the moon.<BR>E.<BR>शशाङ्क, and लेखा a streak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशादन|शशादनः
शशादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A hawk or falcon.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare or rabbit, and अदन what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिदेव|शशिदेवः
शशिदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A sovereign, named also रन्तिदेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिन्
शशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 The emblem of one of the Jinas.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिपाद
शशिपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A moon-beam.<BR>E.<BR>शशि, and पाद a ray; also similar compounds, as शशिकर, शशिकिरण, शशिमयूख, शशिरश्मि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=834" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिप्रभ|शशिप्रभं
शशिप्रभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The white esculent water-lily.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>शशि the moon, and प्रभ shining, (blossoming,) or प्रभा lustre, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिलेखा
शशिलेखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A digit of the moon.<BR>2 A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>3 A metre, a variety of the line of the Atijagatī stanza of thirteen syllables, or of the Atisaceari of fifteen syllables.<BR>E.<BR>शशि the moon, and लेखा a line or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिवदना
शशिवदना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A woman with a face like the moon.<BR>2 A species of the Gāyatrī metre.<BR>E.<BR>शशि, and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिशेखर|शशिशेखरः
शशिशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 One of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR>E.<BR>शशि the moon, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशीश|शशीशः
शशीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शशि, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशोर्ण|शशोर्णं|शशोर्ण्ण
शशोर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>The hair of the hare or rabbit.<BR>E.<BR>शश a hare, &c., and ऊर्णा wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वत्|शश्वन्त्
शश्वत्<BR>ind.<BR>Again and again, frequently, repeatedly, perpetually.<BR>E.<BR>शश to go by jumps, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष
शष<BR>r. 1st cl. (-शषति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुल|शष्कुलः
शष्कुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Galedupa arborea, Rox.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The outer ear or opening of the external auditory passage.<BR>2 Rice or barley water, &c.<BR>3 A sort of pie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्प|शष्पं|शष्पः
शष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>1 Young grass.<BR>2 Loss of intellect or confidence.<BR>E.<BR>शस to hurt, Uṇādi aff. प, and स changed to ष; also शस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस
शस<BR>(इ) and the preposition आङ् always prefixed आशसि r. 1st cl. (आशंसते)<BR>1 To bless, to wish good to, to confer a benediction.<BR>2 To wish, to desire.<BR>3 To speak.<BR>(उ) शसु r. 1st cl. (शसति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>With अभि,<BR>To intreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसन|शसनं
शसन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Immolation, offering an animal in sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>शस to hurt, aff. ल्युट्; also शमन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त<BR>(इ) शस्ति r. 2nd cl. (शंस्ति)<BR>To sleep, (peculiar to the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right.<BR>2 Praised, eulogised.<BR>3 Best, excellent.<BR>n. (-स्तं)<BR>1 Happiness, excellence.<BR>2 The body.<BR>E.<BR>शस to bless, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तक|शस्तकं
शस्तक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A defence for the finger of an archer.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तकेशक|शस्तकेशकः
शस्तकेशक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having much or beautiful hair.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त excellent, केश hair, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्र|शस्त्रं|शस्त्रः
शस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 A weapon in general.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>3 Steel.<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A sword, a scymitar.<BR>f. (-स्री)<BR>A knife.<BR>E.<BR>शस to hurt, aff. ष्ट्रन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रक|शस्त्रकं
शस्त्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Iron.<BR>2 Steel.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र a weapon, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकार|शस्त्रकारः
शस्त्रकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An armourer.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्रह|शस्त्रग्रहः
शस्त्रग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>Taking arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्राहिन्
शस्त्रग्राहिन्<BR>m. (-ही)<BR>A man armed.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and ग्राहिन् who takes<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रघुष्टकर
शस्त्रघुष्टकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Clanging.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and धुष्ट sounded, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रजाल
शस्त्रजाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A quantity of weapons.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and जाल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रजीविन्
शस्त्रजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A soldier by profession.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र a weapon, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रत्याग
शस्त्रत्याग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Throwing away a weapon.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and त्याग abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रधर|शस्त्रधरः
शस्त्रधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An armed man or soldier.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपाणि|शस्त्रपाणिः
शस्त्रपाणि<BR>mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि)<BR>A warrior armed, having weapons in the hand.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपात
शस्त्रपात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The stroke of a weapon.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपूत
शस्त्रपूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Purified by arms, absolved from guilt by dying in the field of battle.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and पूत purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रप्रहरण
शस्त्रप्रहरण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Taking arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and प्रहरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रभृत्
शस्त्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>An armed man, a soldier.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र a weapon, and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रमार्ज|शस्त्रमार्जः|शस्त्रमार्ज्ज
शस्त्रमार्ज<BR>m. (-र्जः)<BR>An armourer.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र a weapon, and भाज cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रवृत्ति|शस्त्रवृत्तिः
शस्त्रवृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>A soldier, a man at arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसंहति|शस्त्रसंहतिः
शस्त्रसंहति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 A quantity or number of weapons.<BR>2 An arsenal, an armoury.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसमूह
शस्त्रसमूह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>1 A quantity or number of weapons.<BR>2 An arsenal, an armoury.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and ममूह a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहत|शस्त्रहतः
शस्त्रहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Struck or killed by a weapon.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र, and हत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहस्त|शस्त्रहस्तः
शस्त्रहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>A man carrying arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्र a weapon, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राजीव|शस्त्राजीवः
शस्त्राजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A soldier.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र a weapon, and आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राभ्यास|शस्त्राभ्यासः
शस्त्राभ्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Military exercise or practice.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र a weapon, and अभ्यास practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्र
शस्त्रास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>Use of weapons.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and अस्त्र a weapon, or means of offence or defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्
शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>A soldier, a warrior.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्रास्त्र, and भृत who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व
शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The military profession, the use of arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-स्त्री-स्त्रिणी-स्त्रि)<BR>Armed, having weapons.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोत्थापन
शस्त्रोत्थापन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Raising a weapon, (as to strike.)<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and उत्थापन taking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोद्यम|शस्त्रोद्यमः
शस्त्रोद्यम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Lifting up a weapon, (as to strike.)<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and उद्यम lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोपजीविन्
शस्त्रोपजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>A soldier, a man at arms.<BR>E.<BR>शस्त्र, and उपजीविन् living by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्प|शस्पं|शस्पः
शस्प<BR>n. (-स्पं)<BR>1 Young grass.<BR>2 Loss of confidence or understanding.<BR>E.<BR>शस to injure, प aff., and the sibilant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 Excellent, best.<BR>2 To be hurt or injured.<BR>3 Desirable, to be wished.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>1 Fruit.<BR>2 Corn, grain in general.<BR>3 Good quality, merit.<BR>E.<BR>शस to hurt, aff. यत्; or शसि to wish, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यक्षेत्र
शस्यक्षेत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A corn field.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य, and क्षेत्र a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यध्वंशिन्
शस्यध्वंशिन्<BR>m. (-शी)<BR>A timber tree, commonly Toon, (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>E.<BR>शस्य fruit, and ध्वंसिन् injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यभक्षक
शस्यभक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Graminivorous.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य, and भक्षक what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यभक्षण
शस्यभक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Feeding upon grain.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य, and भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यमञ्जरी|शस्यमंजरी
शस्यमञ्जरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 The ear or spike of corn.<BR>2 The fruit stalk.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य, and मञ्जरी pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यरक्षक
शस्यरक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A watchman over a field of corn.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य, and रक्षक who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यशूक|शस्यशूकं
शस्यशूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The beard of corn.<BR>E.<BR>शस्य corn, and शूक beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसम्बर|शस्यसंबर|शस्यसम्बरः
शस्यसम्बर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>शस्य fruit, and सम्बर surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=835" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यारु|शस्यारुः
शस्यारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A small variety of the Mimosa suma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशप|शांशपः
शांशप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पी-पं)<BR>Made of Śiśu wood, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिंशपा the Śiśu, अण् aff., and आङ् substituted for the first vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक|शाकं|शाकः
शाक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A potherb in general, any leaf, flower, fruit, stalk, root, &c. used as a vegetable.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 One of the seven Dvīpas or divisions of the world; the sixth, surrounded by the sea of milk or white sea.<BR>2 Power, strength.<BR>3 The Sirisha tree, (Acacia sirisa.)<BR>4 The Teak tree, (Tectona grandis.)<BR>5 An era, a period usually commencing with some celebrated prince, as YUDHIṢṬHIRA, VIKRAMĀDITYA, ŚĀLIVĀHANA, &c. thence denominated ŚĀKEŚVARAS, &c.; the term in ordinary use is applied especially to the era of ŚĀLIVĀHANA, commencing 76 or 78 years after the Christian era.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकट|शाकटं|शाकटः
शाकट<BR>mfn. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>Relating to a cart, (a cart-load, a carthorse, &c.)<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A draught ox.<BR>E.<BR>शकट a cart, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिक|शाकटिकः
शाकटिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Going in or on a cart.<BR>E.<BR>शकट a cart, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटीन|शाकटीनः
शाकटीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Belonging or relating to a cart.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A cart-load as a measure of weight or value.<BR>E.<BR>शकट a cart, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकतरु|शाकतरुः
शाकतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपण|शाकपणः
शाकपण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A handful or similar quantity, as a measure of potherbs.<BR>E.<BR>शाक, and पण price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकरी
शाकरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>One of the dialects of dramatic Prākṛta, that spoken by the Sakāra.<BR>E.<BR>शकार, अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवालेय|शाकवालेयः
शाकवालेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bamanaiṭhi; also वालेयशाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकम्भरी|शाकंभरी
शाकम्भरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 DURGĀ.<BR>2 A city, supposed to be the modern Sāmbher.<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, भृ to nourish, aff. खश्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकम्भरीय|शाकंभरीय|शाकम्भरीयं
शाकम्भरीय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A fossile salt brought from a lake in the vicinity of Sāmbher, a town in Ajmere.<BR>E.<BR>शाकम्भरी the city, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलिक|शाकलिकः
शाकलिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Having a piece or part.<BR>E.<BR>शकल a part, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकविल्व|शाकविल्वः
शाकविल्व<BR>m. (-ल्वः)<BR>The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, विल्व the Bel fruit; also with कन् added शाकविल्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवीर|शाकवीरः
शाकवीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, and वीर eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवृक्ष|शाकवृक्षः
शाकवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The Teak tree.<BR>E.<BR>शाक the same, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकट|शाकशाकटं
शाकशाकट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A field of vegetables, a kitchen garden.<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, and शाकट aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकिन|शाकशाकिनं
शाकशाकिन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A field cultivated for esculent plants, a field of vegetables, a kitchen garden.<BR>E.<BR>शाक a vegetable, and शाकिन aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकश्रेष्ठ|शाकश्रेष्ठः
शाकश्रेष्ठ<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाख्य|शाकाख्यं|शाकाख्यः
शाकाख्य<BR>m. (-ख्यः)<BR>The Teak tree.<BR>E.<BR>शाक the same, and आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाङ्ग|शाकांग|शाकाङ्गं
शाकाङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Pepper.<BR>E.<BR>शाक a potherb, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिनी
शाकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A female divinity of an inferior character, attendant especially on ŚIVA and DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुण|शाकुणः
शाकुण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Repentant, regretting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन|शाकुनः
शाकुन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>1 Of or relating to birds.<BR>2 Ominous, portentous.<BR>E.<BR>शाकुन, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिक|शाकुनिकः
शाकुनिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or relating to birds, omens, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Interpretation of omens, dreams, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन a bird, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलेय|शाकुंतलेयः|शाकुन्तलेयः
शाकुन्तलेय<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>BHARATA, the sovereign of India.<BR>E.<BR>शकुन्तला the nymph, and ढक् aff.; being the son of ŚAKUNTALĀ and DUṢYANTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुलिक|शाकुलिकः
शाकुलिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>शकुल a fish, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्कर|शाक्करः
शाक्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An ox.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A form of metre.<BR>E.<BR>शक्कर, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त|शाक्तः
शाक्त<BR>m. (-क्तः)<BR>A worshipper of the female principle.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति the divine energy in its feminine personification, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तीक|शाक्तीकः
शाक्तीक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Speared, spearing, relating to or done with a spear.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A spearman, a lancer.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति a spear, aff. ईकक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त्य|शाक्त्यः
शाक्त्य<BR>m. (-क्त्यः)<BR>A worshipper of the female principle or Śakti.<BR>E.<BR>शक्ति the personified energy of a divinity, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्य|शाक्यः
शाक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>1 BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha religion.<BR>2 The name of a tribe.<BR>E.<BR>शक to be able, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यमुनि|शाक्यमुनिः
शाक्यमुनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA, the real or supposed founder of the Bauddha religion.<BR>E.<BR>शाक्य said to be the name of a family or tribe, originating with one of the race of Ikṣvāku, condemned to take up his abode in a forest of Sāka trees, and मुनि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यसिंह|शाक्यसिंहः
शाक्यसिंह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A name of BUDDHA.<BR>E.<BR>शाक्य the name of his tribe, and सिंह chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख|शाखः
शाख<BR>(ऋ) शाखृ r. 1st cl. (शाखते)<BR>To pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख|शाखः
शाख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>A plant, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 A branch, the branch of a tree.<BR>2 A branch or subdivision of the Vedas, consisting of the several Saṃhitās or collections of prayers in each Veda, as received in different schools, modified more or less either in the arrangement of the whole text, or in particular portions of it.<BR>3 An arm.<BR>4 A sect, a faction, a party.<BR>5 Any subdivision.<BR>6 Any part of an animal not endowed with sensibility, as a horn, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शाख to pervade, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखानगर|शाखानगरं
शाखानगर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A suburb.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch or subdivision, and नगर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापुर|शाखापुरं
शाखापुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A suburb.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch, and पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाभेद|शाखाभेदः
शाखाभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Difference of school or doctrine.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा, and भेद difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखामृग|शाखामृगः
शाखामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>1 A monkey, an ape.<BR>2 A squirrel.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा the branch of a tree, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखारण्ड|शाखारंड|शाखारण्डः
शाखारण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A Brahman who has changed his Śākhā or peculiar school of the Vedas for another.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch of the Vedas, रम to sport, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाशिफा
शाखाशिफा<BR>f. (-फा)<BR>A root proceeding from a branch, as in the Indian fig, the branches of which shoot downwards to the ground and take fresh root there.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch, and शिफा a fibrous root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखिन्
शाखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>Branched, branching, having branches, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>m. (-खी)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 A Veda.<BR>3 An inhabitant of the northern districts bordering on India, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">Page837</a>] a Turk or Tartar.<BR>4 The name of a king.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=836" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखोट|शाखोटः
शाखोट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A small tree, (Trophis aspera); also with कन् added शाखोटकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्य|शाख्यः
शाख्य<BR>mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>Branching, ramifying.<BR>E.<BR>शाखा a branch, (literally or figuratively,) and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कर|शांकर|शाङ्करं|शांकरः|शाङ्करः
शाङ्कर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A bull.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A form of metre.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कर ŚIVA, and अण् aff.; also read शाक्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्करि|शांकरि|शांकरिः|शाङ्करिः
शाङ्करि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>2 GAṆEŚA.<BR>3 Fire.<BR>4 A Muni.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्कर ŚIVA, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कुची
शाङ्कुची<BR>f. (-ची)<BR>The scate fish; also शंकुची, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्ख|शांखं|शाङ्खः
शाङ्ख<BR>n. (-ङ्खं)<BR>The sound of the conch shell.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख the shell, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खिक|शांखिक|शांखिकः|शाङ्खिकः
शाङ्खिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Made from, relating to, &c. the Śaṅkha or conch.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A shell cutter, a worker in shells.<BR>2 A player on the Śaṅkha, a shell blower.<BR>E.<BR>शङ्ख the conch shell, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्गुष्ठा
शाङ्गुष्ठा<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटक|शाटकं|शाटकः
शाटक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>A petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>शट to go, (round the limbs,) ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटी
शाटी<BR>mf. (-टः-टी)<BR>A petticoat.<BR>E.<BR>शट to praise or flatter, to go, &c. aff. ण, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्य
शाट्य<BR>n. (-ट्यं)<BR>Wickedness, villainy.<BR>E.<BR>शठ wicked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड
शाड<BR>(ऋ) शाडृ r. 1st cl. (शाडते)<BR>1 To flatter, to praise, to coax.<BR>2 To boast.<BR>3 To float or swim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्वल|शाड्वलः
शाड्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Abounding in fresh grass, green, verdant.<BR>E.<BR>शाद young grass, ड्वलच् aff., and the final changed, also शाड्वल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>Made of or from Bengal flax or Śaṇa.<BR>mf. (-णः-णी)<BR>1 A touchstone.<BR>2 A whet or grindstone.<BR>3 A weight of four Māṣas.<BR>4 A saw.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Coarse cloth, sack cloth, canvas.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>1 Ragged or torn raiment.<BR>2 A new unseamed and single breadth of cloth, given to the religious student at his investiture for his upper garment.<BR>3 A ragged garment given to the Jaina ascetic at his initiation.<BR>4 A small tent or screen, used especially as a retiring room for actors, and tumblers, &c.<BR>5 Gesture, gesticulation, making signs with the hands or eyes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शण to give, aff. घञ्; or शो to sharpen, and ण aff.; or शण Saṇ, and अण् aff. of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणाजीव|शाणाजीवः
शाणाजीव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An armourer.<BR>E.<BR>शाण a whetstone, आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणि|शाणिः
शाणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>A plant from the fibres of which a coarse cloth is prepared, (Corchorus olitorius.)<BR>E.<BR>शण Bengal Śaṇ, and ईञ् aff. implying descent or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शांडिल्यः|शाण्डिल्यः
शाण्डिल्य<BR>m. (-ल्यः)<BR>1 A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>2 A Muni from whom one of the three principal families of the Kanouj or Kanyākubja Brahmans is said to be descended.<BR>3 A form of AGNI or fire.<BR>E.<BR>शण्डिल a saint, यञ् aff. of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Happy, well, prosperous.<BR>2 Feeble, thin.<BR>3 Sharpened, whetted, sharp.<BR>4 Handsome, bright.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Joy, pleasure, happiness.<BR>E.<BR>शो to reduce or diminish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भ|शातकुंभ|शातकुंभं|शातकुम्भं|शातकुम्भः
शातकुम्भ<BR>n. (-म्भं)<BR>Gold.<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E.<BR>शतकुम्भ said to be the name of a mountain, and अण् aff. implying production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकौम्भ|शातकौंभ|शातकौंभं|शातकौम्भं
शातकौम्भ<BR>n. (-म्भं)<BR>Gold.<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonasm, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
शातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Withering, decaying, becoming thin or small.<BR>E.<BR>शो to wither, aff. ल्युट्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकी
शातपत्रकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>Moonlight.<BR>E.<BR>शतपत्र a lotus, कन् added, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमन्यव
शातमन्यव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Relating to INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>शतमन्यु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमान|शातमानं
शातमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Bought with the measure of one hundred.<BR>E.<BR>शत a hundred, मान measure, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातशिख
शातशिख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>Sharp pointed, (as the nails, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>शात, and शिखा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातोदरी
शातोदरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A woman with a small belly or waist.<BR>E.<BR>शात, and उदर the belly, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>An enemy.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Enmity, hostility.<BR>2 A multitude of enemies.<BR>E.<BR>शत्रु an enemy, and अण् pleonasm, or aff. of quality or number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवीय
शात्रवीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Hostile, inimical, belonging or relating to an enemy.<BR>E.<BR>शात्रव, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद|शादः
शाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 Mud.<BR>2 Young grass.<BR>E.<BR>शो to wither, द Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादहरित|शादहरितः
शादहरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Green or fresh with young grass.<BR>E.<BR>शाद young grass, and हरित green<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Abounding in fresh or green grass.<BR>E.<BR>शाद young grass, द्वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान|शानः
शान<BR>r. 1st cl. intensitive form (शिशांसति-ते)<BR>To whet, to sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान|शानः
शान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A touchstone.<BR>2 A grindstone.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A sort of cucumber.<BR>E.<BR>शो to make small or sharpen, aff. ल्युट्. also शाण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त|शांत|शान्तं|शान्तः
शान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Calm, tranquil, pacified.<BR>2 Allayed, alleviated.<BR>3 Meek, humble.<BR>4 Purified, cleansed, freed from, (as soil.)<BR>5 Stilled, hushed, (as wind, &c.)<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 An ascetic, one whose passions are subdued and who is engrossed by meditating on the deity.<BR>2 One of the Rasas or conditions of feeling, delineated in poetry or the drama, tranquillity or tranquil devotion, quietism, the assiduous exercise of meditation, &c. and indifference to all objects of pleasure or pain.<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>Appeasing, pacifying.<BR>ind. (शान्तम)<BR>A prohibitive particle or interjection, implying negation, aversion, disgust, (fie! for shame! Heaven forbid!)<BR>E.<BR>शम to be appeased, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तचेतस्|शांतचेतस्
शान्तचेतस्<BR>mfn. (-ताः-ता-तः)<BR>Composed, calm, unanxious.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तता
शान्तता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Quietness, calmness, meekness.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शान्तत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनव|शांतनव|शांतनवः|शान्तनवः
शान्तनव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>BHĪṢMA, the reputed great uncle of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>E.<BR>शान्तनु a prince, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनु|शांतनु|शान्तनुः
शान्तनु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The 21st sovereign of the lunar dynasty in the third age, the father of BHĪṢMA by Gaṅgā, or the Ganges personified.<BR>E.<BR>शं good fortune, (personified,) तनु the body, and the first vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तमल
शान्तमल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Exempt from soil, literally or figuratively.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त cleansed, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरय
शान्तरय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Slackened in speed.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and रय rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=837" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तविवाद
शान्तविवाद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Reconciled, appeased.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तात्मन्
शान्तात्मन्<BR>mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>Calm, composed, of resigned or composed spirit.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तार्च्चिस्|शान्तार्चिस्
शान्तार्च्चिस्<BR>mfn. (-र्च्चिः-र्च्चिः-र्च्चि)<BR>Extinguished, put or gone out.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त, and अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ति|शांति|शांतिः|शान्तिः
शान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 Quiet, tranquillity, stoicism, the absence of passion, and indifference to objects of pleasure or pain; it is especially applied to the tranquillity of devotion, or quietism, by which the mind is wholly fixed on the subject of its meditation or worship, and is utterly disregardless of external impressions.<BR>2 Good fortune, auspiciousness, felicity.<BR>3 Rest, repose.<BR>4 Expiatory or propitiatory rites to avert any evil.<BR>5 Preliminary ceremonies to avert inauspicious accidents at any religious celebration.<BR>6 Remission, alleviation.<BR>m. (-न्तिः)<BR>1 The sixteenth Jina or Jaina deified sage of the present era.<BR>2 One of the Jaina emperors of the universe.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be appeased, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिक|शांतिक
शान्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Propitiatory, expiatory.<BR>2 Producing ease or quiet, &c.<BR>3 Relating to quiet, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर
शान्तिकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Tranquillising, calming, appeasing, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर्त्तृ|शान्तिकर्तृ
शान्तिकर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Conferring tranquillity, calming, appeasing.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>Any divinity who averts evil.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति, and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकाम|शान्तिकामः
शान्तिकाम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Desire of tranquillity and exemption from calamity.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति peace, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिगृह|शांतिगृह|शान्तिगृहं
शान्तिगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A private apartment near the place of sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति devotion, गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिद
शान्तिद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Tranquillising, calming, allaying.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिहोम|शांतिहोम|शान्तिहोमः
शान्तिहोम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Burnt offerings, to prevent or avert threatening or possible evils.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति, and होम burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युद|शांत्युद
शान्त्युद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Water offered at sacrifices for propitiation.<BR>E.<BR>शान्ति, and उद water; also शान्त्युदकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युदकुम्भ
शान्त्युदकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A vessel holding lustral water.<BR>E.<BR>शान्त्युद, and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व<BR>r. 10th cl. (शान्त्वयति)<BR>To console, to comfort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व<BR>n. (-न्त्वं)<BR>1 Conciliation.<BR>2 Comforting, consoling.<BR>E.<BR>शम to appease or allay (opposition), deriv. irr.; or शान्त्व to console, aff. अच्; also सान्त्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वति|शान्त्वतिः
शान्त्वति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A plant, (Siphonanthus indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाप|शापः
शाप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>1 Oath, affirmation by oath or ordeal.<BR>2 Curse, imprecation.<BR>3 Abuse.<BR>E.<BR>शप to swear, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापग्रस्त
शापग्रस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Having incurred or suffering under a curse.<BR>E.<BR>शाप, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापज
शापज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Arising from a curse, being the effect of one.<BR>E.<BR>शाप, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापठिक|शापठिकः
शापठिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापमुक्त
शापमुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Freed from a curse.<BR>E.<BR>शाप, and मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापान्त|शापांत|शापान्तः
शापान्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>The end of a curse or period of an imprecation.<BR>E.<BR>शाप, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापास्त्र|शापास्त्रः
शापास्त्र<BR>m. (-स्त्रः)<BR>A Muni, a saint.<BR>E.<BR>शाप a curse, and अस्त्र a weapon; a curse denounced by such a personage, being formidable even to the deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापित
शापित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sworn, made to take an oath.<BR>E.<BR>शप to swear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापोद्धार|शापोद्धारः
शापोद्धार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Deliverance from a curse or its effects.<BR>E.<BR>शाप, and उद्धार extricating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफरिक|शाफरिकः
शाफरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A fisherman.<BR>E.<BR>शफर a kind of fish, put for any, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द<BR>mfn. (-ब्दः-ब्दी-ब्दं)<BR>1 Sonorous, sounding.<BR>2 Nominal, (as inflection.)<BR>f. (-ब्दी)<BR>SARASVATĪ, goddess of speech and eloquence.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द sound or a word, and अण् attributive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to sounds or words.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A proficient in the senses and forms of nouns or words.<BR>E.<BR>शब्द a sound, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन्<BR>n. (-म)<BR>Conciliation, appeasing, reconciling.<BR>E.<BR>शम to appease, aff. मनिन्, and the vowel made long; also शामन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन|शामनं|शामनः
शामन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>2 Tranquillity, peace.<BR>E.<BR>शम to be pacified, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्र|शामित्रं
शामित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Sacrificing.<BR>2 Tying cattle.<BR>3 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>E.<BR>शम to appease, इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरी|शांबरी
शाम्बरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A female juggler.<BR>E.<BR>शम्बर a demon, अण् added, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बविक|शांबविक|शांबविकः|शाम्बविकः
शाम्बविक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A worker in shells.<BR>E.<BR>शम्बु, a shell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बुक|शांबुक|शांबुकः|शाम्बुकः
शाम्बुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A bivalve shell.<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonasm added to शम्बु; also read शाम्बूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शाम्भव<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>1 A sort of poison.<BR>2 A worshipper of ŚIVA. The son of ŚAMBHU or ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शम्भु a name of ŚIVA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
शायक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>2 A sword.<BR>E.<BR>शो to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.; also सायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिका
शायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Sleeping.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन्<BR>mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>Lying down.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार<BR>r. 10th cl. (शारयति)<BR>1 To be weak.<BR>2 To weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Variegated, (in colour,)<BR>2 Yellow.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A piece or man at chess, backgammon, &c.<BR>3 Hurting, injuring.<BR>4 A mixture of blue and yellow, a green.<BR>5 Spotting, variegating.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Kuśa grass.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारंगः|शारङ्गः
शारङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Of a variegated colour.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The Cātaka (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>2 A deer.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 A bee.<BR>5 A peacock.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A musical instrument, a stringed instrument played with a bow, a sort of fiddle.<BR>E.<BR>शार injuring or variegated, गम to go, or get, aff. खच्; more usually, सारङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारता
शारता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Variegation of colour.<BR>2 Yellowness.<BR>E.<BR>तल added to शार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>1 Modest, diffident.<BR>2 New.<BR>3 Produced in the sultry season.<BR>4 Autumnal.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A year.<BR>2 Grain or rice ripening in the sultry season.<BR>3 A sort of kidney bean, yellow Mūṅg.<BR>4 Autumnal sickness.<BR>5 Sunshine, (in autumn.)<BR>f. (-दा)<BR>1 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 A title of DURGĀ.<BR>3 A musical instrument, a sort of lute or guitar.<BR>f. (-दी)<BR>A plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>2 A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>3 Day of full [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">Page839</a>] moon in the month Kārttika (October-November.)<BR>E.<BR>शरट् the autumn, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=838" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिक|शारदिकं|शारदिकः
शारदिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A particular obsequial ceremony, an annual or autumnal Śrāddha.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Autumnal sickness.<BR>2 Heat or sunshine in autumn.<BR>E.<BR>शारद autumn, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिन्
शारदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Autumnal.<BR>E.<BR>शारद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदीय
शारदीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Autumnal.<BR>E.<BR>शारद, and छ added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारि|शारिः
शारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A piece or man at chess, draughts, Chauper, &c.<BR>2 An elephant's housings or armour.<BR>3 Fraud, trick.<BR>mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>A bird: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A bird, the proper or hill Maina, (Gracula religiosa); it is also applied to the small bird usually called Maina in Bengal, (Turdus salica, BUC.) of which several varieties are distinguished by the Hindus.<BR>2 A bow or stick that may be used for playing the Vīṇā or any stringed instrument.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारित
शारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Variegated, coloured.<BR>E.<BR>शार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिफल|शारिफलं
शारिफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A chequered cloth or table for playing draughts, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शारि a piece, फल fruit; also with कन् added शारिफलक mn. (-कः-कं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिवा
शारिवा<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>A plant: as synonymous with Śyāma, (Echites frutescens), but more usually considered synonymous with Anantamūla, (Asclepias pseudosarsa,) the broad leaved variety, the root of which has been used as a substitute for Sarsaparilla^1, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शारि injuring, from शॄ with इञ् aff., and वन added.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिशृङ्खला
शारिशृङ्खला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A sort of die or dice, used for playing with.<BR>E.<BR>शारि a man or piece, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Corporeal, bodily, belonging to or produced from the body.<BR>2 Spiritual in connexion with the body, incorporate.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The soul or spirit whilst incorporate.<BR>2 A drug (?)<BR>3 Excrement, excretion.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Personal chastisement, corporeal punishment.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर the body, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>1 Corporeal, relating to what is corporeal.<BR>2 Incorporate.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरिक|शारीरिकः
शारीरिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to the body, corporeal.<BR>2 Contained in the body, incorporate.<BR>E.<BR>शरीर, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
शारुक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Mischievous, noxious, injurious.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, उकण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्क|शार्कः
शार्क<BR>m. (-र्कः)<BR>Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कक|शार्ककः
शार्कक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The froth of milk, syllabub, cream.<BR>2 A lump or ball of meat, &c.<BR>3 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कर|शार्करः
शार्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Stony, gravelly.<BR>2 Sugary.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The froth or skim of milk.<BR>E.<BR>शर्करा sugar, gravel, &c. aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करक|शार्करकः
शार्करक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Gravelly, stony, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शार्कर the same, and कक् added; also from शर्कर with ठक् aff. शार्करिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करीय|शार्करीयः
शार्करीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Stony, gravelly, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शर्करा gravel, &c., and छ attributive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्ग|शार्ंग|शार्ङ्गं|शार्ङ्गः
शार्ङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-र्ङ्गः-र्ङ्गी-र्ङ्गं)<BR>Horny, made of horn, &c.<BR>n. (-र्ङ्गं)<BR>1 A bow in general.<BR>2 The bow of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गिन्|शार्ंगिन्
शार्ङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-र्ङ्गी)<BR>1 A bowyer, an archer.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शाङ्ग a bow, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूल|शार्दूलः|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>2 Another animal.<BR>3 A Rākṣasa.<BR>4 A sort of bird.<BR>5 (In composition,) Pre-eminent, excellent.<BR>6 A form of metre, a variety of the class Dhṛti, or stanza of four lines of 18 syllables each; also of the class Atidhṛti, in which there are 19 syllables in the line.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, टूलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलललित|शार्द्दूलललितं
शार्दूलललित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A species of the Dhṛti metre, of 4 lines of 18 syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलवाहन|शार्द्दूलवाहनः
शार्दूलवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Jaina teacher.<BR>E.<BR>शार्दूल a tiger, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलविक्रीडित|शार्द्दूलविक्रीडितं
शार्दूलविक्रीडित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A form of metre, a variety of the class Atidhṛti or stanza, of 4 lines of 19 syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वर|शार्व्वरं
शार्वर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Murderous, mischievous.<BR>2 Nocturnal.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Darkness, gloom.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>Night.<BR>E.<BR>शर्वरी night, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल|शालः
शाल<BR>(ऋ) शालृ r. 1st cl. (शालते)<BR>1 To flatter, to praise.<BR>2 To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल|शालः
शाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A kind of fish, (Ophiocephalus wrahl, HAM.)<BR>2 The celebrated sovereign SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>3 The name of a river.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A house.<BR>2 A hall.<BR>3 A large branch of a tree.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, घञ् aff. or शाल to praise, aff. अच्; in several of the meanings it is also written, साल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायन|शालङ्कायनः
शालङ्कायन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The name of a saint.<BR>2 ŚIVA'S attendant NANDI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायनजीवसू
शालङ्कायनजीवसू<BR>f. (-सूः)<BR>The mother of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालज|शालजः
शालज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of fish, the Śāl or Sol, (Ophicephalus wrahl, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालनिर्य्यास|शालनिर्यास|शालनिर्यासः
शालनिर्य्यास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Resin, the resinous exudation of the Śāl or Shorea robusta.<BR>E.<BR>शाल the Śāl tree, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालपर्णी
शालपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>शाल the Śāl, and पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीष्, having similar leaves; also सालपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालभञ्जिका|शालभंजिका
शालभञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A doll, a puppet.<BR>2 A whore, a harlot.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालभञ्जी|शालभंजी
शालभञ्जी<BR>f. (-ञ्जी)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>शाल Śāl wood, भञ्ज to rub, (to plane, &c., in order to make dolls,) affs. अच्, and ङीष्; also with कन् added शालभञ्जिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालवेष्ट|शालवेष्टः
शालवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Resin, the resin of the Śāl tree, used as incense, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शाल the Śāl tree, and वेष्ट exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालसार|शालसारः
शालसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A tree.<BR>2 Asafætida; also सालसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकिन्
शालाकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>1 A surgeon.<BR>2 A barber.<BR>3 A spearman, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शलाका a probe, a dart, &c. अण् aff. of reference, and इनि poss. aff. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाङ्की
शालाङ्की<BR>f. (-ङ्की)<BR>A doll, a puppet.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a hall, अकि to go, affs. अच्, and ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाजिर|शालाजिरः
शालाजिर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>A hollow earthen cup or saucer.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, जॄ to become old, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाञ्चि|शालाञ्चिः
शालाञ्चि<BR>f. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>A creeping plant, the leaves of which are used as a vegetable, (Achyranthes triandra.)<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, अञ्च to go, aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालानी
शालानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>शाल the Śāl tree, आङ् before नी to get, (to resemble in the leaf,) aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालामृग|शालामृगः
शालामृग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>A Shakal.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=839" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालार|शालारं
शालार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A ladder, a flight of stairs or steps.<BR>2 A birdcage.<BR>3 The claw of an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, ऋ to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालावृक|शालावृकः
शालावृक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A monkey.<BR>2 A dog.<BR>3 A Shakal.<BR>4 A deer.<BR>5 A cat.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, वृक a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालि|शालिः
शालि<BR>n. (-लि)<BR>1 Rice in general, but especially in two classes; one like white rice growing in deep water, and the other a red sort, requiring only a moist soil: there are a great many varieties of this grain.<BR>2 The civet or pole cat.<BR>E.<BR>शाड to float or swim, aff. इन, and ड changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिक|शालिकः
शालिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating or belonging to a hall, the Śāl tree, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>2 A village of artificers.<BR>3 A toll, a tax.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>E.<BR>शाल the Śāl tree, कन् fem. form, aff. of comparison; or शाला a hall, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिञ्च|शालिञ्चः
शालिञ्च<BR>m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>A creeper, the leaf of which is used as a vegetable, (Achyranthes triandra, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिता
शालिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Possessing, having.<BR>2 Confidence in, relying upon.<BR>E.<BR>शालिन्, and तल् aff. or with त्व, शालित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>1 Belonging to a house, domestic, &c.<BR>2 Possessing, having.<BR>3 Shining or resplendent with.<BR>E.<BR>शाल a house, and इनि aff.; in the second form it is the same as शील; the इ being changed to आ when used in composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिनीकरण|शालिनीकरणं
शालिनीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिपिष्ट|शालिपिष्टं
शालिपिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>शालि rice, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिवाहन|शालिवाहनः
शालिवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A sovereign of India, whose capital was Pratiṣṭhāna in the Dekhin, and institutor of the era now called Śakā, beginning 76 or 78 years after CRIST.<BR>E.<BR>शालि from शाल the Śāl tree, or a proper name, that of a Yakṣa transformed to a lion, on which the prince rode when an infant, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्र|शालिहोत्रः
शालिहोत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>शालि rice, corn, and होत्र an oblation; also with इनि added शालिहोत्रिन् m. (-त्री)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Ashamed, bashful.<BR>2 Like, resembling.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>An opulent householder, one who devotes his attention to worldly affairs.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, ख aff. (fit or worthy to enter it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्व|शालीनत्वं
शालीनत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Modesty.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last, also with तल्, शालीनता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्वविवर्ज्जित
शालीनत्वविवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Immodest.<BR>E.<BR>शालीनत्व, and विवर्ज्जित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालु|शालुः
शालु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>1 An astringent substance.<BR>2 A sort of perfume, commonly called Cor.<BR>3 A frog.<BR>n. (-लु)<BR>The root of the water lily.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, उ aff., and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुक|शालुकं|शालुकः
शालुक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of a lotus: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूक|शालूकं|शालूकः
शालूक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The esculent root of the different kinds of Nymphæa or water lily.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, to shake, Uṇādi aff. ऊकन्; also with a short vowel शालुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूर|शालूरः
शालूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A frog.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, ऊलच् aff. and the radical vowel made long; also शालुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेय|शालेयं|शालेयः
शालेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Fit for rice, (a field, &c.)<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>शालि rice, and ढंक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालोत्तरीय|शालोत्तरीयः
शालोत्तरीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A name of PĀṆINI, the inspired grammarian.<BR>E.<BR>शाला a house, the house of his preceptor, उत्तरीय latter, last; having been expelled it for stupidity, and acquiring his subsequent science by his worship of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मल|शाल्मलः
शाल्मल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 The silk cotton tree.<BR>2 One of the Dvīpas to divisions of the continent.<BR>3 The gum of the silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलि|शाल्मलिः
शाल्मलि<BR>mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>1 The silk cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>2 One of the seven Dvīpas, islands or great divisions of the known continent; denominated from the tree first mentioned, said to grow there: it is surrounded by the sea of Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E.<BR>शल to go, causal form, क्विप् aff. शाल् exuding, emitting, मल to hold, aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added; also with अच् aff. शाल्मल, and with the first vowel short, शल्मलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिन्
शाल्मलिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>The silk cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलीवेष्ट|शाल्मलीवेष्टः
शाल्मलीवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>The gum of the silk cotton tree.<BR>E.<BR>शाल्मलि the tree, and वेष्ट exudation; also with कन् added शाल्मलीवेष्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्व|शाल्वः
शाल्व<BR>m. plu. (-ल्वाः)<BR>The inhabitants of one of the central divisions of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>1 Tawny, (of that colour.)<BR>2 Relating to the purification of defilement from the contact or consanguinity of a corpse, &c.<BR>3 Relating to a dead body.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>2 The young of any animal, see the next.<BR>E.<BR>शष a dead body, and अण् aff.; or शव to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावक|शावकः
शावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The young of any animal.<BR>E.<BR>शाव, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>Low, vile.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Fault, offence.<BR>2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>3 The Lodh tree, (Symplocos racemosus.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>2 A sort of Prākṛta, that spoken by barbarians.<BR>E.<BR>शवर a man of low or degraded caste, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावरभेदाख्य
शावरभेदाख्य<BR>n. (-ख्यं)<BR>Copper.<BR>E.<BR>शावर relating to a low race, भेद class, and आख्य appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावाशौच
शावाशौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>Impurity from the demise of a relation.<BR>E.<BR>शाव, and अशौच impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Eternal, perpetual.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 A name of VYĀSA.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 The sun.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Heaven, ether.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>The earth.<BR>E.<BR>शश्वत् perpetually, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Eating flesh or fish.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्कुली flesh, अण् aff. form irr.: see शौष्कुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिक|शाष्कुलिकं
शाष्कुलिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A multitude of pies.<BR>E.<BR>शष्कुली a sort of pie, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास|शासः
शास<BR>(उ,) शासु r. 2nd cl. (शास्ति)<BR>1 To instruct, to inform.<BR>2 To order, to direct, to enact.<BR>3 To rule, to govern.<BR>(शास्ते)<BR>1 To wish or desire:<BR>with आङ् prefixed,<BR>r. 1st cl. (आशासते) r. 2nd cl. (आशास्ते)<BR>To wish well to, to bless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 An order, an edict, a command.<BR>2 A royal grant of land or of privileges, a charter, &c. usually inscribed on stone or copper.<BR>3 A writing, a deed, a written contract or agreement.<BR>4 A Śāstra or scripture.<BR>5 Devotion, or devotional tranquillity, the government of the passions.<BR>6 Governing, ruling, government.<BR>E.<BR>शास to order or direct, aff. ल्युट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपत्र
शासनपत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>A plate of copper, a stone or sheet of paper, &c. on which an edict or grant is inscribed.<BR>E.<BR>शासन, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=840" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहर|शासनहरः
शासनहर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A royal messenger, one bearing an edict or grant.<BR>E.<BR>शासन an edict, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be governed or directed.<BR>E.<BR>शास to rule, अनीयर् aff.; also शासितव्य and शास्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Governed, ruled.<BR>E.<BR>शास to rule, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Ordering, commanding, a governor or commander.<BR>E.<BR>शास to order, तृच् aff. with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्ति|शास्तिः
शास्ति<BR>f. (-स्तिः)<BR>1 A command, an order.<BR>2 Governing, ruling, ordering.<BR>3 A sceptre.<BR>4 Correction, punishment.<BR>E.<BR>शास to govern, aff. क्तिन् or ति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ<BR>mfn. (-स्ता-स्ती-स्तृ)<BR>1 A ruler, one who rules or governs.<BR>2 A teacher, teaching, instructing.<BR>m. (-स्ता)<BR>A Buddha or Jina, or the deified teacher of one or both those sects.<BR>E.<BR>शास to govern, &c. aff. तृच्, and the augment omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 An order or command.<BR>2 Scripture, science, institutes of religion, law or letters, especially considered as of divine origin or authority: used singly, it implies works of literature or science in general, and it is therefore customarily connected with some other word to limit its application, as the Vedānta Śāstras, or treatises of philosophical theology; the Dharma Śāstras, books of law, &c.: it is also applied to less important branches of knowledge, as the Kāvya Śāstras, or poetical works; Śilpi Śāstras, works on the mechanical arts; and Kāma Śāstras, or erotic^1 compositions; in the singular number it is also used comprehensively to signify the body of all that has been written on the subject, as Dharma Śāstra, the institutes or code of law; Kāvya Śāstra, poetry; Alaṅkāra Śāstra, rhetoric, &c.<BR>3 A book in general.<BR>E.<BR>शास to govern or teach, aff. ष्ट्रन्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्रकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>1 A Ṛṣi, a holy personage of divine character.<BR>2 An author in general.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a Śāstra or scripture, &c., and कृत् the author; the principal compositions in Hindu religion, law, and literature, being attributed to sanctified and superhuman personages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रगण्ड|शास्त्रगंड|शास्त्रगण्डः
शास्त्रगण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>A general and superficial scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचक्षुस्
शास्त्रचक्षुस्<BR>n. (-क्षुः)<BR>Grammar.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र science, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञ|शास्त्रज्ञः
शास्त्रज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Acquainted with the Śāstras, skilled in the knowledge of law and religion especially.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a sacred work, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञता
शास्त्रज्ञता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Knowledge of the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्रज्ञ, and तल् aff.; also शास्त्रज्ञत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञान
शास्त्रज्ञान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Knowledge derived from the study of sacred works.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्व
शास्त्रतत्त्व<BR>n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>The truth or true knowledge taught in sacred works.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञ|शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञः
शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Understanding the works of sacred science.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>An astrologer, an astronomer.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र sacred or astronomical science, तत्त्व the truth, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतस्
शास्त्रतस्<BR>ind.<BR>After or according to the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदर्शिन्
शास्त्रदर्शिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>Skilled in sacred science.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र Śāstra, and दर्शिन् who inspects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रनिन्दा
शास्त्रनिन्दा<BR>f. (-न्दा)<BR>Revilling or denying the authority of sacred works.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and निन्दा reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रप्रसङ्ग|शास्त्रप्रसंगः
शास्त्रप्रसङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The subject of the Śāstras.<BR>2 Discussing works of sacred literature.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and प्रसङ्ग attaching to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवत्|शास्त्रवन्त्
शास्त्रवत्<BR>ind.<BR>Conformably or according to written authority.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवत्|शास्त्रवन्त्
शास्त्रवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Having or following sacred institutes, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविट्
शास्त्रविट्<BR>mfn. (-विट्)<BR>Understanding or conversant with the scriptures, skilled in sacred science.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a Śāstra, and विट् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविधान
शास्त्रविधान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sacred ritual, ceremonial precept.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and विधान direction; also शास्त्रविधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्ध|शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्धः
शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Contrary to law or religion, illegal, forbidden.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a Śāstra, and विप्रतिषिद्ध prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध|शास्त्रविप्रतिषेधः
शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Any act contrary to the legal and religious institutes of the Hindus.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र an institute, and वि and प्रति contra-indicative prefixes before षिद्ध to accomplish, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरुद्ध
शास्त्रविरुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Contrary to law or religion.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and विरुद्ध opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरोध|शास्त्रविरोधः
शास्त्रविरोध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>1 Opposition or deviation from sacred authority.<BR>2 Contradiction or incompatibility of different systems.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and विरोध contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रशिल्पिन
शास्त्रशिल्पिन<BR>plu. m. (-नः)<BR>The people of Kashmir.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a treatise, and शिल्पिन an artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रसिद्ध
शास्त्रसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Established or proved by sacred institutes or divine works.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and सिद्ध established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राचरण|शास्त्राचरणः
शास्त्राचरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Versed in the scriptures, well read in the works of sacred science, a Paṇḍita.<BR>2 A follower of the Vedas, one whose conduct is regulated by their precepts.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र a sacred treatise, and आचरण who goes through or studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रातिक्रम|शास्त्रातिक्रमः
शास्त्रातिक्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>Behaving ill or immorally, transgressing, acting contrary to the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अतिक्रम surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठान
शास्त्रानुष्ठान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Following the Śāstras, conforming to the law or ritual, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अनुष्ठान conforming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठित
शास्त्रानुष्ठित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Who or what obeys or follows sacred institutes, &c.<BR>2 Established or authorised by the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अनुष्ठित following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुसार|शास्त्रानुसारः
शास्त्रानुसार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Conformity to sacred ordinances.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राभिज्ञ
शास्त्राभिज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>Learned, versed in the Śāstras.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अभिज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन्<BR>m. (-स्त्री)<BR>A Paṇḍita, a teacher of holy science, or one skilled in it.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Scriptural, authorised by or conformable to sacred institutes.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रोक्त
शास्त्रोक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Said or declared in a work of sacred authority.<BR>E.<BR>शास्त्र, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>1 To be regulated or ordained, to be enforced, to be provided for by any act of government or judicature.<BR>2 Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR>E.<BR>शास to govern, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=841" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि<BR>(ञ,) शिञ् r. 5th cl. (शिनोति शिनुते)<BR>1 To make thin or small.<BR>2 To whet, to sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि<BR>m. (-शिः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 Auspiciousness, good fortune.<BR>3 Peace, composure, calm.<BR>E.<BR>शि to whet, or शो to destroy, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा<BR>f. (-पा)<BR>A tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>2 The Asoka tree.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quick, or शीर्ष the head or top; पा to cherish, or पत to fall, &c, aff. क or ड, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु<BR>mfn. (-क्कुः-क्कुः-क्कु)<BR>Idle, lazy, following no business or profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थ|शिक्थं
शिक्थ<BR>n. (-क्थं)<BR>Bee's wax; also शिक्थकं and सिक्थकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्य|शिक्यं
शिक्य<BR>nf. (-क्यं-क्या)<BR>1 The string or loop suspended from either end of a pole or yoke to receive the burthen.<BR>2 The burthen so carried.<BR>3 The strings of a balance.<BR>E.<BR>श्रंस to fall, Uṇādi aff. यत्; शि substituted for the root, and कुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्याधार
शिक्याधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The hook or eye at each end of a pole or beam, to which the strings of a yoke or balance are fastened.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्या as above, and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यित|शिक्यितं
शिक्यित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Suspended or carried in a sort of loop.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्य a loop, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष
शिक्ष<BR>r. 1st cl. (शिक्षते)<BR>To learn, to acquire science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षक|शिक्षकः
शिक्षक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>A learner, a teacher.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्ष to learn, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणीय
शिक्षणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be taught or learnt.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्ष to learn, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा<BR>f. (-क्षा)<BR>1 One of the six Vedāṅgas or sciences attached to the Vedas: the proper pronunciation of the vocal sounds which occur in them, as explained by PĀṆINI.<BR>2 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>3 Learning, study, the acquisition of knowledge.<BR>4 Modesty, humility.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्ष to learn, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाकर|शिक्षाकरः
शिक्षाकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 VYĀSA.<BR>2 An instructor.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्षा the science of pronunciation, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाशक्ति|शिक्षाशक्तिः
शिक्षाशक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>Dexterity, skill.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्षा discipline, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Skilful, clever, conversant.<BR>2 Modest, diffident.<BR>3 Disciplined, exercised.<BR>4 Tame, trained, (as an animal.)<BR>5 Docile.<BR>6 Studied, learned.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्षा studying, इतच् aff. or शिक्ष to study, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितव्य
शिक्षितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be taught or learnt.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्ष to learn, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिताक्षर|शिक्षिताक्षरः
शिक्षिताक्षर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A pupil, a scholar.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्षित studied, (by whom,) and अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्य
शिक्ष्य<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>1 To be taught, teachable.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्ष to learn, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिख
शिख<BR>(इ) r. 1st cl. (शिङ्खति)<BR>To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखंडः|शिखण्डः
शिखण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1 The tail of a peacock.<BR>2 Locks left on the crown or the sides of the head, at the period of tonsure in children: see the next.<BR>E.<BR>शिखिन् a peacock or any crested object, अम to be or belong to, ड aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखंडकः|शिखण्डकः
शिखण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Locks of hair left at the time of tonsure; three or five locks left in children in general, or especially those of the military class, in which latter case, the hair is left in a semicircular patch on each side of the head, covering rather more than the temporal bones, and following much the same outline: see काकपक्ष.<BR>2 The crest or lock of hair left on the crown of the head.<BR>3 A peacock's tail.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, अण्ड an egg, and कन् pleonasm, or aff. of comparison; also शिखाण्डक and शिखण्ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखंडिकः|शिखण्डिकः
शिखण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A cock.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिखण्ड a crest, &c. aff. ठक् or कन् in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिन्|शिखंडिन्
शिखण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 A peacock's tail.<BR>3 A cock.<BR>4 An arrow.<BR>5 A Ṛṣi, either of the seven represented by the stars of the greater bear: see चित्रशिखण्डिन्.<BR>6 The son of DRUPADA, by metamorphosis: see below.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A kind of jasmine, (J. auriculatum.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>3 The daughter of DRUPADA, afterwards changed to a male.<BR>E.<BR>शिखण्ड a crest, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखर|शिखरं|शिखरः
शिखर<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>1 The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>2 The top of a tree.<BR>3 Point, end, top in general.<BR>4 Horripilation.<BR>5 The armpit.<BR>6 A piece of a ruby or a gem, described as of the colour of the ripe pomegranate seed or a bright red.<BR>7 The edge or point of a sword.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A plant, from the fibres of which bow-strings were made, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and रच् poss. aff., and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरवासिनी
शिखरवासिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शिस्वर the peak, (of the Himālaya.) and वासिनी abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>Crested, peaked, pointed.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A tree.<BR>3 A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>4 A strong-hold, a hill-fort.<BR>5 The lapwing.<BR>f. (-रिणी)<BR>1 A form of metre, a species of the class Atyaṣṭi or verse of four lines of 17 syllables each.<BR>2 A dish of curds and sugar with spices.<BR>3 An excellent woman.<BR>4 Arabian jasmine.<BR>5 A line of hair extending across the navel.<BR>E.<BR>शिस्वर a point or peak, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखलोहित|शिखलोहितः
शिखलोहित<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A plant, commonly Kukurmurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 Point, top in general.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>3 A peacock's crest.<BR>4 A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>5 Flame.<BR>6 A radicating branch.<BR>7 Any branch.<BR>8 A plant, commonly Lāṅgalīya.<BR>9 Chief, principal.<BR>10 Fever, proceeding from libidinous excitement or love.<BR>11 A ray of light.<BR>E.<BR>शीङ् to sleep, Uṇādi aff. ख, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाण्डक|शिखाण्डकः
शिखाण्डक<BR>(-कः)<BR>Hair left on each side of the head: see शिखण्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखातरु|शिखातरुः
शिखातरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A candlestick or lampstand.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा flame, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाधर|शिखाधरः
शिखाधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Crested, pointed.<BR>2 Having a top knot.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाधार|शिखाधारः
शिखाधार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and धार who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखामूल|शिखामूलं
शिखामूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A carrot, a turnip, or any root with a tuft of leaves growing from it.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावत्|शिखावन्त्
शिखावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>2 The personified descending node.<BR>3 A lamp.<BR>f. (-वती)<BR>A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावर|शिखावरः
शिखावर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The jack fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावल|शिखावलः
शिखावल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Crested, pointed.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=842" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावृक्ष|शिखावृक्षः
शिखावृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The stand of lamp.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा flame, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावृद्धि|शिखावृद्धिः
शिखावृद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Usurious interest payable daily. शिक्षा a tuft of hair, and वृद्धि interest; growing constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिग्रीव|शिखिग्रीवं
शिखिग्रीव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>E.<BR>शिखि for शिखिन् a peacock, ग्रीवा the neck, अच् added, being of the same colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिध्वज|शिखिध्वजः
शिखिध्वज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 Smoke.<BR>2 The deity KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शिखि a peacock, or fire, and ध्वज an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिन्
शिखिन्<BR>mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>1 Crested.<BR>2 Having a lock of hair on the top of the head.<BR>m. (-खी)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A peacock.<BR>3 A bull.<BR>4 An arrow.<BR>5 A tree.<BR>6 A cock.<BR>7 KETU, the personified descending node.<BR>8 A horse.<BR>9 A mountain.<BR>10 A Brahman.<BR>11 A lamp.<BR>12 A religious mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>शिखा a crest, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिपुच्छ|शिखिपुच्छं
शिखिपुच्छ<BR>n. (-च्छं)<BR>A peacock's tail.<BR>E.<BR>शिखि a peacock, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिमण्डल|शिखिमण्डलः
शिखिमण्डल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>E.<BR>शिखि a peacock, and मण्डल district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिवर्द्धक
शिखिवर्द्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A pumpkin gourd.<BR>E.<BR>शिखि a peacock, and वर्द्धक increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिवाहन|शिखिवाहनः
शिखिवाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>E.<BR>शिखि a peacock, and वाहन a vehicle, the deity being mounted on this bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिशिखा
शिखिशिखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>1 Flame.<BR>2 A peacock's crest.<BR>E.<BR>शिखिन्, and शिखा a crest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिशेखर
शिखिशेखर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A peacock's crest.<BR>E.<BR>शिखिन्, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रु|शिग्रुः
शिग्रु<BR>m. (-ग्रुः)<BR>1 A tree, (Morunga guilandina and hyperanthera.)<BR>2 A potherb in general.<BR>E.<BR>शि to sharpen, रुक् aff., and ग augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुज|शिग्रुजं
शिग्रुज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The seed of the Morunga.<BR>E.<BR>शिग्रु, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुमूल
शिग्रुमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The pungent root of the Morunga.<BR>E.<BR>शिग्रु, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुवीज
शिग्रुवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>The seed of the Morunga.<BR>E.<BR>शिग्रु, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिघ
शिघ<BR>(इ) शिघि r. 1st cl. (शिंघति)<BR>To smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाण|शिंघाण|शिङ्घाणं|शिंघाणः|शिङ्घाणः
शिङ्घाण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Any glass vessel.<BR>2 The mucus of the nose.<BR>3 Rust of iron.<BR>E.<BR>शिघि to smell, आणक Uṇādi affix, and the final optionally rejected; also शिंघाणक and शिंहाणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकं|शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणकः
शिङ्घाणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Phlegm.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>The mucus of the nose.<BR>E.<BR>शिघि to smell, aff. आणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घित|शिंघित|शिङ्घितं
शिङ्घित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smelled.<BR>E.<BR>शिघि to smell, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिच्
शिच्<BR>f. (शिक्)<BR>The string of a pole for carrying burdens.<BR>E.<BR>श्रंस to fall, deriv. irr.: see शिक्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिज
शिज<BR>(इ) शिजि r. 2nd cl. (शिंक्ते)<BR>1 To make an inarticulate sound.<BR>2 To tinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज|शिंज|शिंजः|शिञ्जः
शिञ्ज<BR>mf. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा)<BR>The tinkling sound of silver and other metallic ornaments worn round the waist, arm, or ancles, &c.<BR>f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>A bow string.<BR>E.<BR>शिजि to make an inarticulate sound, aff. अङ् and टाप्: also शिञ्जिनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जञ्जिका|शिंजंजिका
शिञ्जञ्जिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A chain worn round a man's loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जित|शिंजित|शिञ्जितं
शिञ्जित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>The tinkling of metallic ornaments worn as rings, chains, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिञ्जा inarticulate sound, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जिन्
शिञ्जिन्<BR>mfn. (-ञ्जी-ञ्जिनी-ञ्जि)<BR>Tinkling, making a tinkling sound.<BR>f. (-ञ्जिनी)<BR>1 A bow-string.<BR>2 Metallic rings worn round the toes, an ornament of the feet.<BR>E.<BR>शिञ्जा a tinkling, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिट
शिट<BR>r. 1st cl. (शेटति)<BR>To disregard, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Thin, emaciated, wasted, declined.<BR>2 Weak, feeble.<BR>3 Sharpened, whetted.<BR>E.<BR>शि to sharpen, or शो to pare or whet, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितता
शितता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Sharpness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शितत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितद्रु|शितद्रुः
शितद्रु<BR>f. (-द्रुः)<BR>The Śatadru or Setlej river.<BR>E.<BR>शित weakened, द्रु to flow, aff. कुः see शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितधार
शितधार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Sharp-edged.<BR>E.<BR>शित, and धारा an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितशूक|शितशूकः
शितशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Barley.<BR>2 Wheat.<BR>E.<BR>शित sharpened, शूक the beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिताग्र|शिताग्रः
शिताग्र<BR>mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>Sharp-pointed.<BR>m. (-ग्रः)<BR>A thorn.<BR>E.<BR>शित, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितास्त्रभृत्
शितास्त्रभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>Armed with sharp weapons.<BR>E.<BR>शित, अस्त्र a weapon, भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-ती-ति)<BR>1 Black.<BR>2 White.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch.<BR>E.<BR>शि to sharpen, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.; or शत to go, Uṇādi aff. इन्, and इ substituted for the radical vowel; also सिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिकण्ठ|शितिकंठ|शितिकण्ठः
शितिकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A gallinule.<BR>3 A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शिति black, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिचार|शितिचारः
शितिचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A potherb, (apparently Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिछद|शितिच्छद|शितिच्छदः
शितिछद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>शिति white, छद a feather; also सितछद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिपक्ष|शितिपक्षः
शितिपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>शिति white, पक्ष a wing; also सितपक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिरत्न
शितिरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A sapphire.<BR>E.<BR>शिति, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिसारक|शितिसारकः
शितिसारक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>शिति black, and सार essence, resin, कन् added; yielding a strong black resin that is used for caulking boats, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितेषु
शितेषु<BR>m. (-षुः)<BR>A sharp arrow.<BR>E.<BR>शित, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Loose, lax, flaccid, flabby.<BR>2 Languid, inert, feeble.<BR>3 Ineffective, unenergetic.<BR>4 Relaxed, slackened.<BR>5 Not rigidly observed.<BR>6 Loosely retained or possessed.<BR>7 Abandoned, got rid of, shaken off.<BR>E.<BR>श्रथ to be lax or loose, Uṇādi aff. किरच्, the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलता
शिथिलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Relaxation, looseness, being unfastened, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शिथिलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलित
शिथिलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Let go, loosed, released.<BR>2 Relaxed, loosened.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलबल
शिथिलबल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Weakened, relaxed.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलवसु
शिथिलवसु<BR>mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>1 Reduced in wealth.<BR>2 Shining with diminished rays.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and वसु wealth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलशक्ति
शिथिलशक्ति<BR>mfn. (-क्तिः-शिः-क्ति)<BR>Impaired in strength or power.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलीकरण
शिथिलीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Loosening, unfastening.<BR>2 Impairing, weakening, reducing.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and करण doing, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलीकृत
शिथिलीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Unbound, unfastened. slackened.<BR>2 Reduced, impaired, weakened.<BR>3 Let loose.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and कृत made, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनि|शिनिः
शिनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A proper name, a chief of the Kṣatriya tribe.<BR>E.<BR>शि to make thin or small, Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनेर्नप्तृ
शिनेर्नप्तृ<BR>m. (-प्ता)<BR>A name of SĀTYAKI, one of the chiefs of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>E.<BR>शिनि a proper name, and नप्तृ grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=843" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपविष्ट|शिपविष्टः
शिपविष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Bald, &c.: see शिपिविष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपि|शिपिः
शिपि<BR>m. (-पिः)<BR>A ray of light.<BR>f. (-पिः)<BR>Skin, leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिविष्ट|शिपिविष्टः
शिपिविष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A bald man.<BR>2 A man naturally void of prepuce.<BR>3 ŚIVA.<BR>4 VIṢṆU.<BR>5 A leper.<BR>E.<BR>शिपि a ray of light, and विष्ट entered; also शिपविष्ट and शिविपिष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफा
शिफा<BR>f. (-फा)<BR>1 A fibrous root.<BR>2 Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>3 A river.<BR>4 A mother.<BR>5 Turmerick.<BR>6 The root of a water lily.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, फक् aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकन्द|शिफाकन्दः
शिफाकन्द<BR>mn. (-न्दः-न्दं)<BR>The root of a water lily.<BR>E.<BR>शिफा a fibrous root, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाधर|शिफाधरः
शिफाधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A branch.<BR>E.<BR>शिफा a fibrous root, and धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफारुह|शिफारुहः
शिफारुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>शिफा a fibrous root, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्ब|शिंबः|शिम्बः
शिम्ब<BR>m. (-म्बः)<BR>A sort of large shrub, (Cassia alata.)<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>A legume, a pod; also सिम्बा.<BR>E.<BR>शि to make small, deriv. irr.; also शिम्बि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बि|शिम्बिः
शिम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बिः-म्बी)<BR>A legume, a pod.<BR>E.<BR>शि to make small or sharpen, deriv. irr.; also शिम्बा, and सिम्बा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिक|शिम्बिकः
शिम्बिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus max.)<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A legume, a pod.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last; also शिम्बा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिपर्णी
शिम्बिपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>E.<BR>शिम्बि a pod, and पर्ण leaf, aff. ङीष्; also with कन् added fem. form शिम्बिपर्णिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर|शिरं|शिरः
शिर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 The root of the pepper plant.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>Any vessel of the body, really, or supposed to be, of a tubular form, as a nerve, a tendon, a gut, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, क aff.: see शिरस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःकपालिन्
शिरःकपालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>A devotee carrying a human scull as his emblem.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, कपाल the scull, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःपीडा
शिरःपीडा<BR>f. (-डा)<BR>Pain of the head, head-ache.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस्, and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःफल|शिरःफलः
शिरःफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The cocoa-nut tree.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःस्नात
शिरःस्नात<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Having the head bathed.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् and स्नात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरज|शिरजः
शिरज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिर the head, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस्<BR>n. (-रः)<BR>1 The head.<BR>2 The top of a tree.<BR>3 The van of an army.<BR>4 Chief, principal, head.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to honour, in the passive form, to be honoured, (by the other members,) असुन् Uṇādi aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिज|शिरसिजः
शिरसिज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरसि seventh case, in the head, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिरुह्
शिरसिरुह्<BR>m. (-रुट्)<BR>The hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरसि on the head, रुह् what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्क|शिरस्कं
शिरस्क<BR>n. (-स्कं)<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>2 A turban, a hat or cap.<BR>f. (-स्का)<BR>A litter, a palanquin.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्तापिन्
शिरस्तापिन्<BR>m. (-पी)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, तप to inflame, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्त्र|शिरस्त्रं
शिरस्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>2 A cap, a turban, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and त्रै to protect, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्त्राण|शिरस्त्राणं
शिरस्त्राण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>2 A cap, a turban, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, त्राण the instrument of defence^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्य|शिरस्यः
शिरस्य<BR>mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>Of or on the head.<BR>n. (-स्यं)<BR>Clean unentangled hair.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्स्थ
शिरस्स्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्स्थः-स्स्था-स्स्थं)<BR>At or on the head, at the top, &c.<BR>m. (-स्थः)<BR>A chief, a leader.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् head, chief, and स्था to stay or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरापत्र|शिरापत्रः
शिरापत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The elephant or wood apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E.<BR>शिरा a vein, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिराल|शिरालं
शिराल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Veiny, tendinous, skinny, showing the tendons or veins.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An acid fruit, (Averrhoa carambola.)<BR>E.<BR>शिरा a vein, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरालक|शिरालकः
शिरालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Cissus quadrangularis.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरावृत्त|शिरावृत्तं
शिरावृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरि|शिरिः
शिरि<BR>m. (-रिः).<BR>1 A sword.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A murderer, a killer.<BR>4 A locust.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure or kill, Uṇādi aff. इ, and the radical vowel changed to इर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरीष|शिरीषः
शिरीष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>A kind of tree, (Atracia sirisa.)<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. ईषन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोगृह|शिरोगृहं
शिरोगृह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>A room on the top of the house, a turret.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् top, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोग्रीव|शिरोग्रीवं
शिरोग्रीव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>The head and neck.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, ग्रीव the neck, the compound neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधरा
शिरोधरा<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>The neck.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and धर what upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधि|शिरोधिः
शिरोधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>The neck.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, धा to hold, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमणि|शिरोमणिः
शिरोमणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>A gem worn in a crest, or on the top of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमर्म्मन्|शिरोमर्मन्
शिरोमर्म्मन्<BR>m. (-र्म्म)<BR>A hog.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and मर्म्मन् vitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरत्न|शिरोरत्नं
शिरोरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A gem worn in the crest.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and रत्न a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुजा
शिरोरुजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>1 A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>2 Pain or diseased affection of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and रुजा sickness; a remedy being prepared from the leaves of the plant for head-ache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुह्
शिरोरुह्<BR>m. (-रुट्)<BR>Hair.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, रुह to grow, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुह|शिरोरुहः
शिरोरुह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The hair of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, रुह to grow, क aff.; also शिरोरुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरोग|शिरोरोगः
शिरोरोग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>Disease of the head.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस्, and रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोर्त्ति|शिरोर्ति|शिरोर्त्तिः
शिरोर्त्ति<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>Pain of the head, head-ache, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and आर्त्ति pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवर्त्तिन्|शिरोवर्तिन्
शिरोवर्त्तिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>At the head or top, &c.<BR>m. (-र्त्ती)<BR>A chief; one at the head of affairs or of an army.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस्, and वर्त्तिन् staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवल्ली
शिरोवल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The crest or comb of the peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and वल्ली a creeper; it is also read शिरोत्रन्दि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवृत्त|शिरोवृत्तं
शिरोवृत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>Pepper.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head or top, and वृत्त surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवेष्ट|शिरोवेष्टः
शिरोवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A turban.<BR>2 A cap.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and वेष्ट what surrounds; also शिरोवेष्टन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवेष्टन|शिरोवेष्टनं
शिरोवेष्टन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A turban.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and वेष्टन enfolding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोस्थि
शिरोस्थि<BR>n. (-स्थि)<BR>A scull.<BR>E.<BR>शिरस् the head, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल|शिलं|शिलः
शिल<BR>r. 6th cl. (शिलति)<BR>To glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=844" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल|शिलं|शिलः
शिल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Gleaning ears of corn.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A stone, a rock.<BR>2 Arsenic.<BR>3 A flat stone on which condiments, &c. are ground with a muller.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>1 The timber of a door frame.<BR>2 A transverse beam, or a beam or stone placed across the top of a post or pillar.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 A small earth worm.<BR>2 A dart, a spike.<BR>E.<BR>शिल to glean, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकर्णी
शिलाकर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकुट्टक|शिलाकुट्टकः
शिलाकुट्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A stone cutter's chisel.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, कुट्ट to cut, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकुसुम
शिलाकुसुम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Storax: see शिलाज.<BR>E.<BR>शिला and कुसुम flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाघन
शिलाघन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Firm or hard as a stone or rock.<BR>E.<BR>शिला, and घन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाज|शिलाजं
शिलाज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in a mountain or rock, fossile, mineral.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 Storax or Benzoin, the resins of the Styrax benzoinum or S. officinale, which are usually confounded by the Hindus.<BR>2 Iron.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, and ज born; the balsams being supposed to be fossile productions, and to exude from the soil of mountainous places; being confounded with bitumen or petroleum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाजतु
शिलाजतु<BR>n. (-तु)<BR>1 Bitumen.<BR>2 Red chalk.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and जतु lac; it is supposed to ooze from the stones of mountains in the hot weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाजित्
शिलाजित्<BR>f. (-जित्)<BR>Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and जित् what conquers or excels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाटक|शिलाटकः
शिलाटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A room on the top of a house.<BR>2 A hole.<BR>3 A fence, an enclosure.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, अट to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलातल
शिलातल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The surface of a rock or stone.<BR>E.<BR>शिला, and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलात्मज|शिलात्मजं
शिलात्मज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, आत्मन् self, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलात्मिका
शिलात्मिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A crucible.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, आत्मन् substance, कन् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलादद्रु|शिलादद्रुः
शिलादद्रु<BR>m. (-द्रुः)<BR>Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and दद्रु herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाधातु|शिलाधातुः
शिलाधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>1 Chalk.<BR>2 Red chalk.<BR>3 A white fossile substance; an aluminous earth of a white colour, and thence considered to be a sort of chalk.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone or rock, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापट्ट|शिलापट्टः
शिलापट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A flat stone for grinding condiments, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and पट्ट a flat surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापुत्त्र
शिलापुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>A mullar or roller for grinding condiments, &c. on a flat stone.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a flat stone, and पुत्त्र child; also शिलापुत्त्रक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापुष्प|शिलापुष्पं
शिलापुष्प<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>Storax or Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाफलक
शिलाफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A layer or table of rock or stone.<BR>E.<BR>शिला, फलक a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाभव|शिलाभवं
शिलाभव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Storax or Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाभेद|शिलाभेदः
शिलाभेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>1 A plant, (Plectranthus scutellaroides.)<BR>2 A stone cutter's chisel.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and भेद what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलामय
शिलामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Made of stone.<BR>E.<BR>शिला, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलारस|शिलारसः
शिलारस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Incense, Benjaminor Olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलावल्का
शिलावल्का<BR>f. (-ल्का)<BR>A medicinal substance said to be of cooling and lithonthriptic properties, commonly termed Silābāk; a sort of lichen or moss.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone or rock, and वल्क bark; also termed शिलावल्कल, शिलात्वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलावृष्टि|शिलावृष्टिः
शिलावृष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Hail.<BR>E.<BR>शिला, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाव्याधि|शिलाव्याधिः
शिलाव्याधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock or stone, and व्याधि sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलासन|शिलासनं
शिलासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Benzoin or Storax.<BR>2 A stone bench or seat.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone or rock, and असन abiding or आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलासार|शिलासारं
शिलासार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Iron.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलि|शिलिः
शिलि<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>The lower timber of a door.<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>The Bhojpatra or birch tree.<BR>E.<BR>शिल to glean, इन् aff.: see शिल and शिला, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्र|शिलींध्र|शिलीन्ध्रं|शिलींध्रः|शिलीन्ध्रः
शिलीन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>1 The flower of the plaintain tree.<BR>2 Hail.<BR>3 A mushroom.<BR>m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>1 A sort of tree.<BR>2 A kind of fish; also चित्रफलक.<BR>f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>1 Earth, clay.<BR>2 A small earth worm.<BR>3 A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्रक|शिलींध्रक|शिलीन्ध्रकं
शिलीन्ध्रक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A mushroom, one growing out of cowdung, a fungus.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीपद|शिलीपदः
शिलीपद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Enlarged or Tropical leg; also श्लीपद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीमुख|शिलीमुखः
शिलीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 A bee.<BR>2 An arrow.<BR>3 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>4 War.<BR>E.<BR>शिली a dart, (a sting,) and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलेय|शिलेयं
शिलेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Like a stone or rock, as hard, &c.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>Storax.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, ढक् aff. and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोच्चय|शिलोच्चयः
शिलोच्चय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>2 A high mountain.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone or rock, उत् up, चि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोञ्छ|शिलोञ्छः
शिलोञ्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>1 Following more than one occupation.<BR>2 Gleaning.<BR>E.<BR>शिला gleaning, उच्छ to gather or glean, aff. अच्; gleaning a subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोञ्छवृत्ति
शिलोञ्छवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>1 Livelihood gained by gleaning.<BR>2 Extraordinary occupation.<BR>E.<BR>शिलोञ्छ, and वृति subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोत्थ|शिलोत्थं
शिलोत्थ<BR>mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>Growing from or upon rock or stone.<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Benzoin or Storax.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, and उत्थ what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोद्भव|शिलोद्भवं
शिलोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Produced from stone or rock.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 A superior sort of Sandal wood, either the white or brass coloured sort.<BR>2 Storax or Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone or rock, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलौकस्
शिलौकस्<BR>m. (-काः)<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्प|शिल्पं
शिल्प<BR>n. (-ल्पं)<BR>1 An art, any manual or mechanical art.<BR>2 A sort of spoon or ladle, used at sacrifices to throw the Ghee or butter into the fire.<BR>E.<BR>शिल to be clever or skilled, प Uṇādi aff., and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पक|शिल्पकं
शिल्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of drama: one exhibiting magical and mystical rites.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प manual art, and कन् aff.; also read शिल्पिकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पकर्म्मन्|शिल्पकर्मन्
शिल्पकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>Manual labour, handicraft.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प, and कर्म्मन् act; also शिल्पक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पकार|शिल्पकारः
शिल्पकार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>An artisan, a mechanic.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प a handicraft, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पविद्या
शिल्पविद्या<BR>f. (-द्या)<BR>Art, mechanical or manual skill.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प, and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पशाल
शिल्पशाल<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A work-shop, a manufactory.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प art. and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=845" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिक
शिल्पिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Manual, mechanic.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 Handicraft.<BR>2 A sort of drama; see शिल्पक.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिन्
शिल्पिन्<BR>mfn. (-ल्पी-ल्पिनी-ल्पि)<BR>1 An artist, an artificer or artisan.<BR>2 Belonging or relating to a mechanical profession or art.<BR>f. (-ल्पिनी)<BR>A drug or herb, a kind of grass said to be known by the name of Lahānasipi, and described as sweet and cooling, and bearing seeds of tonic and restorative properties; also शिल्पिका, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्प art, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिशाल
शिल्पिशाल<BR>nf. (-लं-ला)<BR>A work-shop, a manufactory.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्पि an artisan, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिशास्त्र
शिल्पिशास्त्र<BR>n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>A treatise or set of treatises on works of art.<BR>E.<BR>शिल्पि an artist, and शास्त्र book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिव|शिवं|शिवः
शिव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Prosperous, happy.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The deity ŚIVA, the most formidable of the Hindu triad, the destroyer of creation: the adoration of which he is the object, is of a more gloomy nature in general than that of the rest, and he is the particular god of the Tāntrikas or followers of the books called Tantras.<BR>2 Final emancipation from existence, eternal happiness.<BR>3 A pillar or post to which cattle are tied.<BR>4 An auspicious planetary conjunction.<BR>5 Scripture, the Vedas.<BR>6 A drug, commonly Elavāluka.<BR>7 A perfume, Puṇḍarīya.<BR>8 Bdellium.<BR>9 One of the astronomical periods termed Yogas.<BR>10 Quicksilver.<BR>11 The penis.<BR>12 The phallic emblem of ŚIVA.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>2 Auspiciousness, well being.<BR>3 Water.<BR>4 Sea or fossile salt.<BR>5 Borax.<BR>f. (-वा)<BR>1 The goddess DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>2 The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR>3 Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>4 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>5 A shakal.<BR>6 The mother of the twenty-second Jina.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, Uṇādi aff. वन्, on or in whom or which, the universe reposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवक|शिवकः
शिवक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A post to which cows or calves are tied.<BR>E.<BR>शिव the same, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवकर|शिवकरः
शिवकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious, making happy.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A Jina of the last age.<BR>E.<BR>शिव good fortune, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवकीर्त्तन|शिवकीर्तन|शिवकीर्तनः|शिवकीर्त्तनः
शिवकीर्त्तन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 An attendant on ŚIVA.<BR>2 KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Praising or hymning ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवगति|शिवगतिः
शिवगति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Happy, prosperous.<BR>2 Worshipping ŚIVA.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>One of the Jinas of the past age.<BR>E.<BR>शिव auspiciousness, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवघर्म्मज|शिवघर्मज|शिवघर्मजः|शिवघर्म्मजः
शिवघर्म्मज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The planet MARS.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, घर्म्म perspiration, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवङ्कर|शिवंकर|शिवङ्करः
शिवङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious, conferring happiness or good fortune.<BR>E.<BR>शिव good fortune, कृ to make, aff. खच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवचतुर्दशी
शिवचतुर्दशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>A festival in honour of ŚIVA, on the fourteenth of the dark half of Māgha.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and चतुर्दशी fourteenth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवज्ञ
शिवज्ञ<BR>mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>1 Knowing what is good or propitious.<BR>2 Worshipping ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>A female devotee of the Śaiva sect.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and ज्ञा to know, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवताति|शिवतातिः
शिवताति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>Propitious, conferring happiness or fortune.<BR>E.<BR>शिव happiness, तातिल् aff.; also शिवतातिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदत्त|शिवदत्तं
शिवदत्त<BR>n. (-त्तं)<BR>The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदारु
शिवदारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Devadaru tree, (Pinus Deodar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदूतिका
शिवदूतिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>One of the Mātṛs or divine mothers.<BR>E.<BR>शिवटूती DURGĀ, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदूती
शिवदूती<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and टूती, from टूत a messenger, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवधातु|शिवधातुः
शिवधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>The milk stone, opal or chalcedony.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवपुरी
शिवपुरी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>The holy city Benares.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and पुरी the city; being sacred to ŚIVA especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवप्रिय|शिवप्रियं|शिवप्रियः
शिवप्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Dear to or esteemed by ŚIVA.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>3 Crystal.<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The seeds of the Eleocarpus.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवमल्ली
शिवमल्ली<BR>f. (-ल्ली)<BR>The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and मल्ली jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवरस|शिवरसः
शिवरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>The water of boiled rice or pulse three days old, and undergoing spontaneous fermentation.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ease, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवरात्रि|शिवरात्रिः
शिवरात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः)<BR>A celebrated festival in honour of ŚIVA on the fourteenth of the moon's wane or dark fortnight in Māgha.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववल्लभ|शिववल्लभः
शिववल्लभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Loved or esteemed by ŚIVA.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>2 Gigantic swallow wort.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववाहन|शिववाहनः
शिववाहन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A bull.<BR>E.<BR>शिव the deity, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववीज|शिववीजं
शिववीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and वीज semen, its supposed origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवशेखर|शिवशेखरः
शिवशेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाक्ष|शिवाक्षं
शिवाक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>The seed of the Eleocarpus.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and अक्ष from अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवानी
शिवानी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 A flower, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>2 A name of DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शिव the deity, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाप्रिय|शिवाप्रियः
शिवाप्रिय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A goat.<BR>E.<BR>शिवा DURGA, and प्रिय beloved by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाराति|शिवारातिः
शिवाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>शिवा a shakal, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवालय|शिवालयं|शिवालयः
शिवालय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Red Tulasī or basil.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A cemetery or place where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>2 Any temple dedicated to ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवास्मृति|शिवास्मृतिः
शिवास्मृति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवि|शिविः
शिवि<BR>m. (-विः)<BR>1 A beast of prey.<BR>2 The Bhojpatra or birch tree.<BR>3 A king so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A palanquin, a litter.<BR>E.<BR>शिव nominal verb, to give pleasure or ease, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविपिष्ट|शिविपिष्टः
शिविपिष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>A name of ŚIVA: see शिपिविष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविर|शिविरं
शिविर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A camp.<BR>2 A royal camp or residence.<BR>3 A guard or defence for the soldiers.<BR>4 A sort of grain.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep or rest, किरच् Uṇādi aff. and वुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवीरथ|शिवीरथः
शिवीरथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A palanquin, a litter.<BR>E.<BR>शिवी for शिविका the same, and रथ a conveyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषा
शिशयिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Drowsiness, sleepiness, wish to sleep.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=846" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषु
शिशयिषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Sleepy, drowsy.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिर|शिशिरः
शिशिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Cold, frigid, chilly, freezing.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Frost.<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>The cold season, comprising two months from about the middle of January to that of March.<BR>E.<BR>शश to go, (the sun, north of the equator,) किरच् Uṇādi aff. and the radical vowel changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिरकाल|शिशिरकालः
शिशिरकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The dewy season; see the last.<BR>E.<BR>शिशिर, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशु|शिशुः
शिशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 The young of man or any animal, a child, a calf, a pup, &c.<BR>2 A pupil, a scholar.<BR>3 A boy under eight years of age.<BR>4 A lad, or boy not more than sixteen.<BR>E.<BR>शो to destroy, Uṇādi aff. उ, and the root repeated, with इ substituted for the semivowel to which the radical vowel is changed in its inflections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक|शिशुकः
शिशुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A porpoise.<BR>2 Another fish, resembling a porpoise.<BR>3 A child, a young animal.<BR>4 A tree.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक्रन्द|शिशुक्रंद|शिशुक्रन्दः
शिशुक्रन्द<BR>m. (-न्दः)<BR>The weeping of an infant or child.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, and क्रन्द weeping; also शिशुक्रन्दन n. (-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक्रन्दीय|शिशुक्रन्दीयः
शिशुक्रन्दीय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A book or work treating of infantine or juvenile grievances.<BR>E.<BR>शिशुक्रन्द as above, and छ aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुगन्धा|शिशुगंधा
शिशुगन्धा<BR>f. (-न्धा)<BR>Double jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुत्व|शिशुत्वं
शिशुत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Boyhood, pupilage, the period before sixteen.<BR>2 Childhood, the period up to eight years of age.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, त्व abstract aff.; also with तल् aff. शिशुता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपाल|शिशुपालः
शिशुपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The sovereign of a country in the central part of India or Cedi, opposed to KṚṢṆA and slain by him: his death forms the subject of one of the Hindu epic poems, thence named Śiśupāla Badha, by MĀGHA.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपालक|शिशुपालकः
शिशुपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A king: see the last.<BR>2 A plant, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, पाल who or what pleases or cherishes, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपालहन्
शिशुपालहन्<BR>m. (-हा)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शिशुपाल the king so named, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुमार|शिशुमारः
शिशुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 The gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus gangeticus.)<BR>2 The heavenly porpoise, or collection of the stars and planets.<BR>3 A name or form of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, and मार what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुवाहक|शिशुवाहकः
शिशुवाहक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, वह to bear, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुवाह्यक|शिशुवाह्यकः
शिशुवाह्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wild goat.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, वह to bear, ण्यत् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्न|शिश्नं|शिश्नः
शिश्न<BR>m. (-श्नः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>शश to move, aff. नक्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्विदान|शिश्विदानः
शिश्विदान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Innocent, virtuous.<BR>2 Guilty, sinful, wicked.<BR>E.<BR>श्वित to be white, (pure or virtuous,) आनच् Uṇādi aff., त changed to द, and the reduplicate form of the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष
शिष<BR>r. 1st cl. (शेषति)<BR>To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (शेषति शेषयति)<BR>1 To leave a residue, not to use the whole.<BR>2 (usually with षि prefixed,) To excel.<BR>(ऌ and with षि prefixed) विशिष्टृ r. 7th cl. (विषिनष्टि)<BR>To assign attributes or qualities to, to distinguish, to individualize, to specify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
शिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Obedient, docile.<BR>2 Ordered, commanded, disciplined, trained.<BR>3 Chief, principal, eminent, select.<BR>4 Left, remaining.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>1 A courtier, a counsellor.<BR>2 A chief.<BR>E.<BR>शास to order, aff. क्त, form irr., or शिष to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टता
शिष्टता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Good behaviour, urbanity, civility.<BR>2 Docility.<BR>3 The property of being left or remaining.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्टि, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शिष्टित्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टसभा
शिष्टसभा<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>A council of state, an assembly of chief officers.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्ट, and सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टसभाचार
शिष्टसभाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>History or tradition of eminent persons.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्ट, and सभाचार account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टाचार|शिष्टाचारः
शिष्टाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Well-behaved.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Good manners, proper behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्ट, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टि|शिष्टिः
शिष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>1 An order or command.<BR>2 Ruling, commanding.<BR>3 Correcting, keeping in order.<BR>4 Personal correction or chastisement.<BR>E.<BR>शास to order, aff. क्तिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट्वा
शिष्ट्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having confessed publicly, or proclaimed.<BR>2 Having governed, regulated, trained, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शास to rule or शिष to hurt, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्य|शिष्यः
शिष्य<BR>(-ष्यः)<BR>1 A pupil, a scholar.<BR>2 Passion, anger.<BR>3 Violence.<BR>E.<BR>शास to order, aff. क्यप्, and the vowel changed to इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्यशिष्टि|शिष्यशिष्टिः
शिष्यशिष्टि<BR>f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>Chastisement or correction of a pupil.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्य, and शिष्टि correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्ल|शिह्लः
शिह्ल<BR>m. (-ह्लः)<BR>Incense, benjamin or olibanum.<BR>E.<BR>ष्णिह to melt, लक् aff.; deriv. irr.; more usually सिह्ल, also with कन् added, शिह्लक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी<BR>(ङ) शीङ् r. 2nd cl. (शेते)<BR>To sleep: with अति prefixed, to be profuse or copious, to be much or more, to exceed: with अधि to abide, to be; with सम् to doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी<BR>f. (शीः)<BR>1 Sleep, repose.<BR>2 Devotion, tranquillity, indifference to every thing but the object of worship.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक
शीक<BR>r. 1st cl. (ऋ) शीकृ (शेकते)<BR>To wet or moisten, to sprinkle.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शेकयति)<BR>1 To endure patiently, to be patient.<BR>2 To touch.<BR>3 To wet, to moisten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकर|शीकरं|शीकरः
शीकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Thin rain, or rain driven by wind.<BR>2 A drop of water.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>A sort of pine or its resin.<BR>E.<BR>शीक to sprinkle, aff. अरन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकरौघ
शीकरौघ<BR>mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>Abounding with mist, spray or thin rain.<BR>E.<BR>शीकर, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र|शीघ्रं
शीघ्र<BR>mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्रा-घ्रं)<BR>Quick, speedy.<BR>m. (-घ्रः)<BR>(In astronomy,) Parallax.<BR>n. adv. (-घ्रं)<BR>Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E.<BR>शिघ to smell, रक् aff. deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रग|शीघ्रगः
शीघ्रग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>Going quick.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रगामिन्
शीघ्रगामिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>Going quick or expeditiously.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quickly, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रचेतन|शीघ्रचेतनः
शीघ्रचेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quickly, चेतन thinking, knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रजन्मन्
शीघ्रजन्मन्<BR>m. (-न्मा)<BR>A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonduccella.)<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quick, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रता
शीघ्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Quickness, speed.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीघ्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=847" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रवेधिन्
शीघ्रवेधिन्<BR>m. (-घी)<BR>A good archer, a good shot.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quick, and वेधिन् who pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रायमाण
शीघ्रायमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Becoming quick or expeditious.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र nominal verb to be quick, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिय|शीघ्रियः
शीघ्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Quick, fleet.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 The fighting of cats.<BR>E.<BR>शीघ्र quick, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cold, chilly, frigid.<BR>2 Idle, lazy.<BR>3 Cold, dull, apathetic, stupid.<BR>4 Decocted, boiled.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Cold, coldness.<BR>2 Water.<BR>3 Cold weather or the six months of the rainy, dewy and cold seasons.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>2 A kind of ratan, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>3 A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>4 The Nīmb tree.<BR>5 Camphor.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 The wife of RĀMA.<BR>2 A furrow.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, aff. क्त, the fem. form more usually occurs सीता, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक|शीतकः
शीतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Cold weather or the cold season, winter.<BR>2 A lazy man, one who is dilatory or dull.<BR>3 One devoid of care or anxiety, a happy man.<BR>4 A plant, (Marsilea dentata.)<BR>5 A scorpion.<BR>E.<BR>क added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकाल|शीतकालः
शीतकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Cold weather, winter.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकालीन
शीतकालीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Produced in winter.<BR>E.<BR>शीतकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकृच्छ्र|शीतकृच्छ्रः
शीतकृच्छ्र<BR>m. (-च्छ्रः)<BR>A religious penance, drinking cold water three days, cold milk three days, cold Ghee three days, and fasting three.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकुम्भ|शीतकुम्भः
शीतकुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>f. (-म्भा)<BR>An aquatic plant.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, कुम्भ a water-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक्षार|शीतक्षारं|शीतक्षारः
शीतक्षार<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Refined Borax.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and क्षार nitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतगन्ध|शीतगंध|शीतगन्धं|शीतगन्धः
शीतगन्ध<BR>n. (-न्धं)<BR>White Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतगु|शीतगुः
शीतगु<BR>m. (-गुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and गु neut. form of गो a ray of light, here forming a masc. compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतचम्पक|शीतचंपक|शीतचम्पकः
शीतचम्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A lamp.<BR>2 Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>3 A mirror.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, cool, and चम्पक a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतता
शीतता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Cold, coldness.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीतत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपर्णी
शीतपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A plant, (Cleome pentaphylla.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपल्लव
शीतपल्लव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A plant, (Ardisea solanacea.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपाकिनी
शीतपाकिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>E.<BR>शीत the cold (in a cold climate), पाक ripening, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपाकी
शीतपाकी<BR>f. (-की)<BR>1 A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>2 A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, (in cold weather, &c.) पाक a ripening, ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपुष्प|शीतपुष्पः
शीतपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>The Sirisha tree.<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, (in the cold weather, &c.) and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपुष्पक|शीतपुष्पकं|शीतपुष्पकः
शीतपुष्पक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Storax or Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold (in the snowy mountains), पुष्प a flower, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतप्रभ|शीतप्रभः
शीतप्रभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and प्रभ shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभानु|शीतभानुः
शीतभानु<BR>m. (-नुः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and भानु the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभीरु|शीतभीरुः
शीतभीरु<BR>f. (-रुः)<BR>Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत the cold, and भीरु afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभोजिन्
शीतभोजिन्<BR>mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि)<BR>Eating cold viands.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, भुज to eat, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमयूख|शीतमयूखः
शीतमयूख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, मयूख a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमरीचि|शीतमरीचिः
शीतमरीचि<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, मरीचि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमूलक|शीतमूलकं
शीतमूलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and मूलक a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरम्य|शीतरम्यः
शीतरम्य<BR>m. (-म्यः)<BR>A lamp.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and रम्य agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरुच्
शीतरुच्<BR>m. (-रुक्)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and रुच् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतल|शीतलं|शीतलः
शीतल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Cold, chilly, frigid.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Green vitriol.<BR>2 Storax.<BR>3 Sandal.<BR>4 White Sandal.<BR>5 A lotus.<BR>6 A pearl.<BR>7 Cold, coldness.<BR>8 The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>2 A Jina or Jaina teacher, the 10th of the twenty-four Tīrthakaras.<BR>3 A religious ceremony observed upon the sun's entering Aries.<BR>4 The moon.<BR>5 A small tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>6 The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>7 A sort of camphor.<BR>8 Turpentine.<BR>f. (-ला-ली)<BR>1 A plant, perhaps intending the Phrynium dichotymum, from the split stems of which a smooth, cool mat is made, thence termed Sitalpāti.<BR>2 Small-pox.<BR>3 The goddess presiding over or inflicting small-pox.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, लच् poss. aff., or ला to give or get, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलता
शीतलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Coldness, coolness.<BR>E.<BR>शीतल, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीतलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलप्रद|शीतलप्रदः
शीतलप्रद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Sandal.<BR>E.<BR>शीतल cold, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलवात|शीतलवातः
शीतलवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A cool wind.<BR>E.<BR>शीतल, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलवातक|शीतलवातकः
शीतलवातक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>शीतल cool, वात wind, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलषष्ठी
शीतलषष्ठी<BR>f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>The sixth of the light half of Māgha, when only cold food is eaten.<BR>E.<BR>शीतल, and षष्ठी sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतशिव|शीतशिवं|शीतशिवः
शीतशिव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>1 A sort of resin, (Storax benzoin.)<BR>2 Rock salt.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>2 The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR>E.<BR>शीत cool, and शिव auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतशूक|शीतशूकः
शीतशूक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Barley.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and शूक an awn or beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतसह|शीतसहः
शीतसह<BR>mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>Bearing or enduring cold.<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A Pīlu, or tree so named, growing in the Himāla mountains.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and सह enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतहर
शीतहर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Removing cold.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतांशु|शीतांशुः
शीतांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 Camphor.<BR>2 The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताकुल
शीताकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Benumbed, frozen.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताद|शीतादः
शीताद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Scorbutic affection of the gums.<BR>E.<BR>शीत, and अद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताद्रि|शीताद्रिः
शीताद्रि<BR>m. (-द्रिः)<BR>The snowy mountains.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतार्त्त|शीतार्त|शीतार्त्तः
शीतार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Cold, chilled, shivering, suffering or shrinking from cold.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतालु|शीतालुः
शीतालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>Cold, shivering, shrinking from cold.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, आलुच् aff., here implying aversion or impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताश्मन्
शीताश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>The moon gem, crystal.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतीभाव|शीतीभावः
शीतीभाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 Final emancipation.<BR>2 Coolness, composure.<BR>3 Cold, coldness.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, भाव nature, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=848" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतोत्तम|शीतोत्तमं
शीतोत्तम<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>Water.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्य|शीत्यं
शीत्य<BR>mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>1 Ploughed, tilled: more usually सीत्य.<BR>2 To be cooled or chilled.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, or शीता a furrow, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्कार|शीत्कारः
शीत्कार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Uttering a sound expressive of pleasurable sensations.<BR>E.<BR>शीत् imitative sound, and कार making; also with कृत made, uttered, शीत्कृत n. (-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु<BR>mn. (-धुः-घु)<BR>Rum, distilled from molasses.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, or rest, Uṇādi aff. धक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुगन्ध|शीधुगंध|शीधुगन्धः
शीधुगन्ध<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>E.<BR>शीधु rum, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुप|शीधुपः
शीधुप<BR>mf. (-पः-पी)<BR>A drinker of spirits, a dram-drinker.<BR>E.<BR>शीधु spirits, and पा to drink, aff. टक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Thick, congealed, (as oil or butter.)<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>2 A large snake.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीफालिका
शीफालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis): see शेफालिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ
शीभ<BR>(ऋ) शीभृ r. 10th cl. (शीभते)<BR>1 To praise, to flatter.<BR>2 To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभव|शीभवः
शीभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Thin rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्य|शीभ्यः
शीभ्य<BR>m. (-भ्यः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A bull.<BR>E.<BR>शीभ to praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीयमान
शीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Going away, dissipating, dispersing, departing.<BR>E.<BR>शद to go, शानच् aff., शीय substituted for the radical letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर|शीरः
शीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, रक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं.)<BR>1 Thin, small, slender.<BR>2 Wasted, withered, decayed.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णता
शीर्णता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Emaciation, withering.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णनाला
शीर्णनाला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण shrivelled or slender, नाल stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपत्र|शीर्णपत्रः
शीर्णपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>A tree, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण withered, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपाद|शीर्णपादः
शीर्णपाद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>YAMA, the deity of Tartarus.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण shrivelled, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपुष्पिका
शीर्णपुष्पिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण shrunk, पुष्प a flower, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णवृन्त|शीर्णवृंत|शीर्णवृन्तं|शीर्णवृन्तः
शीर्णवृन्त<BR>n. (-न्तं)<BR>A water-melon.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण slender, and वृन्त footstalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णाङ्घ्रि|शीर्णांघ्रि|शीर्णाङ्घ्रिः
शीर्णाङ्घ्रि<BR>m. (-ङ्घ्रिः)<BR>YAMA, judge of the dead.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ण shrivelled, and अङ्घ्रि a foot: being shrunk up in consequence of a curse of his mother's.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्व्वि|शीर्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्व्वि<BR>mfn. (-र्व्विः-र्व्विः-र्व्वि)<BR>Mischievous, malignant, hurtful, savage.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, क्विन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ष|शीर्षं
शीर्ष<BR>n. (-र्षं)<BR>The head.<BR>E.<BR>see शिरस्, for which it is substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षक|शीर्षकं|शीर्षकः
शीर्षक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>2 The skull.<BR>3 Judgment, award, sentence, the fruit or result of judicial investigation.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Rāhu, the personified ascending node.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षकस्थ
शीर्षकस्थ<BR>mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>1 Staying in or on the head.<BR>2 Abiding by an award, agreeing to submit to the penalty imposed by it.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्षक, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षघातिन्
शीर्षघातिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Beheading, decapitating.<BR>2 Striking or injuring the head.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष the head, हन to strike, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षछेद|शीर्षच्छेद|शीर्षच्छेदः
शीर्षछेद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>Decapitating.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष, and छेद cutting; also शीर्षछेदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षछेदक|शीर्षच्छेदक
शीर्षछेदक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Meriting decapitation.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष the head, and छेद cutting, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षछेदिन्|शीर्षच्छेदिन्
शीर्षछेदिन्<BR>mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>Who or what decapitates.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष, and छेदिन् who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षछेद्य|शीर्षच्छेद्य|शीर्षच्छेद्यः
शीर्षछेद्य<BR>mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>Meriting death by decapitation.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष the head, छेद्य to be cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्य|शीर्षण्यः
शीर्षण्य<BR>n. (-ण्यं)<BR>A helmet.<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>Clean and unentangled hair.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्षन् substituted for शिरस्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षरक्ष|शीर्षरक्षं
शीर्षरक्ष<BR>n. (-क्षं)<BR>A helmet.<BR>E.<BR>शीर्ष the head, and रक्ष preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील<BR>r. 1st cl. (शीलति)<BR>1 To meditate, to consider, to reflect profoundly and abstractedly.<BR>2 To worship, to adore.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (शीलति शीलयति)<BR>To practise, to exercise, (as the memory, &c.) to repeat.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शीलयति)<BR>1 To wear.<BR>2 To have or be endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Possessed of, endowed with, practising, versed in, &c.<BR>2 Behaving, conducted.<BR>3 Well-behaved, well-disposed.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Nature, quality.<BR>2 Disposition, inclination.<BR>3 Good conduct or disposition, steady and uniform observance of law and morals.<BR>4 Beauty.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A large snake.<BR>E.<BR>शील to meditate, to learn, &c., aff. घञ्; or शी to sleep, and लक् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलत्व
शीलत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Disposition, quality.<BR>2 Conversancy.<BR>E.<BR>शील, and त्व added; also with तल्, शीलता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलन|शीलनं
शीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Careful study of the Śāstras or sacred writings.<BR>E.<BR>शील to meditate, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवत्|शीलवन्त्
शीलवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Of a good or amiable disposition.<BR>E.<BR>शील good conduct, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्त
शीलवृत्त<BR>mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>Moral, steady, and uniform in good behaviour.<BR>E.<BR>शील, and वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलसम्पन्न
शीलसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Well-conducted, of proper conduct or disposition.<BR>E.<BR>शील, and सम्पन्न abounding with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलित|शीलितं
शीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Skilled, learned, conversant, exercised.<BR>2 Having, endowed with.<BR>3 Made or consisting of.<BR>E.<BR>शील to learn, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन्<BR>m. (-वा)<BR>A large snake, the Boa.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, क्वनिप् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवल|शीवलं
शीवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>2 Benzoin or Storax.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, (on the water,) वलच् aff., and the vowel unchanged; also शैवाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंशुमार|शुंशुमारः
शुंशुमार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A porpoise; more usually शिशुमार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु<BR>ind.<BR>1 Handsomely, brilliantly, elegantly.<BR>2 Well, right.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to be splendid, aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक|शुकं|शुकः
शुक<BR>r. 1st cl. (शोकति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>2 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक|शुकं|शुकः
शुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A parrot.<BR>2 The son of VYĀSA, the author or narrator of the Bhāgavata.<BR>3 The minister of RĀVAṆA.<BR>4 The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>5 A plant, commonly Seyālkānta.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A drug and perfume, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>2 Cloth, clothes.<BR>3 The ends or hem of a cloth.<BR>4 A turban, a helmet.<BR>5 A plant, [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">Page850</a>] (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, कक् Uṇādi aff., and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=849" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकछद|शुकच्छद|शुकच्छदं
शुकछद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>A fragrant root, of which various kinds are said to be known.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and च्छद a cover or wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकजिह्वा
शुकजिह्वा<BR>f. (-ह्वा)<BR>A plant, commonly Sūya Tonta or parrot's beak.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकतरु|शुकतरुः
शुकतरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>The Śirīṣa, (Acacia Sirisha.)<BR>E.<BR>शुक the same, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकदेव|शुकदेवः
शुकदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The son of VYĀSA; see शुक.<BR>E.<BR>शुक, and देव divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकद्रुम|शुकद्रुमः
शुकद्रुम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The Śirīṣa tree: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनामा
शुकनामा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>A plant; see शुकजिह्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनास|शुकनासः
शुकनास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 A tree, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>2 Another tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>E.<BR>शुक, and नास the nose, the flowers being compared to a parrot's beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपितामह
शुकपितामह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>The sage PARĀŚARA, father of VYĀSA, and grandfather of ŚUKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुच्छ|शुकपुच्छः
शुकपुच्छ<BR>m. (-च्छः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, पुच्छ the tail; of similar colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुच्छक|शुकपुच्छकं
शुकपुच्छक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A perfume and medicinal root, commonly Ganṭhiāla.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, पुच्छ the tail, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकप्रिया
शुकप्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>The rose-apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकम्
शुकम्<BR>ind.<BR>Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवर्ह|शुकवर्हं
शुकवर्ह<BR>n. (-ह)<BR>Ganṭhiāla, a perfume.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and वर्ह a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवल्लभ|शुकवल्लभः
शुकवल्लभ<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवाह|शुकवाहः
शुकवाह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and वाह who is borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकादन|शुकादनः
शुकादन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The pomegranate.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकानना
शुकानना<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A plant, commonly Sūya Tonta.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, and आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Sour, acid.<BR>2 Pure, clean.<BR>3 Harsh, hard.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>1 Flesh.<BR>2 Sour-gruel.<BR>3 Vinegar, acid, or an acid preparation made from roots or fruits, by steeping them in oil and salt, drying them, and then leaving them in water, where they undergo the acetous fermentation: the fluid produce is used as vinegar.<BR>4 Crabbed or harsh speech.<BR>5 A hymn of the Vedas.<BR>f. (-क्ता)<BR>A sort of sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to be pure, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ति|शुक्तिः
शुक्ति<BR>f. (-क्तिः)<BR>1 A pearl oyster.<BR>2 A conch.<BR>3 A small shell.<BR>4 A cockle.<BR>5 A sort of perfume, in appearance a dried shell fish.<BR>6 A portion of the skull used as a cup, &c.<BR>7 A curl or feather on a horse's neck or breast.<BR>8 A weight of two Karṣas or half a Pala. A disease of the cornea, formation of specks on it.<BR>E.<BR>शुच् to sorrow, &c., aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिका
शुक्तिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 A pearl oyster.<BR>2 A sort of dock or sorrel.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति as above, or शुक्त sour, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिज|शुक्तिजं
शुक्तिज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति the oyster, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपुट
शुक्तिपुट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>The pearl oyster shell.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति, and पुट a bag or sheathe<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपेशी
शुक्तिपेशी<BR>f. (-शी)<BR>The envelope of the pearl or pearl oyster shell.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति, and पेशी a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिबधू
शुक्तिबधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>Mother of pearl or the pearl oyster.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति, and बधू wife or female; in which the pearl, it is supposed, is bred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिमत्|शुक्तिमन्त्
शुक्तिमत्<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>One of the seven principal mountains or mountainous ranges of India.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति a pearl oyster, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिवीज
शुक्तिवीज<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति the oyster, and वीज a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिस्पर्श|शुक्तिस्पर्शः
शुक्तिस्पर्श<BR>m. (-र्शः)<BR>Dusky spots on a pearl, causing it to be of little value.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति a pearl, and स्पर्श contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्र|शुक्रं|शुक्रः
शुक्र<BR>m. (-क्रः)<BR>1 The planet VENUS or its regent, the son of BHṚGU, and preceptor of the Daityas or Titans.<BR>2 A name of fire.<BR>3 The month Jyeṣṭha, (April-May.)<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 Semen virile.<BR>2 A morbid affection of the iris, change of colour, ulceration, &c. accompanied by imperfect vision.<BR>E.<BR>शुच् to grieve, &c., Uṇādi aff. रन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रकर|शुक्रकरः
शुक्रकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Producing semen, spermatic.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The marrow of the bones.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र seed, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रभुज्
शुक्रभुज्<BR>m. (-भुक्)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र semen, भुज to eat, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रभू
शुक्रभू<BR>f. (-भूः)<BR>The marrow of the bones.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र semen, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रल
शुक्रल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Spermatic, augmenting the seminal secretion.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A fragrant grass, considered by some as a sort of Cyperus, and by others, Zedoary.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र semen, and लच् aff., or ला to get or give, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रवार|शुक्रवारः
शुक्रवार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>Friday.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र ŚUKRA, the regent of VENUS, or the planet, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रिय|शुक्रियः
शुक्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Sacred to ŚUKRA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र as above, and घन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रशिष्य|शुक्रशिष्यः
शुक्रशिष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A demon, a Titan, a powerful being opposed to the gods.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र the teacher of this race, and शिष्य a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्राचार्य्य|शुक्राचार्य
शुक्राचार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The regent of VENUS.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्र, and आचार्य्य teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ल|शुक्लं|शुक्लः
शुक्ल<BR>mfn. (-क्लः-क्ला-क्लं)<BR>White, of a white colour.<BR>m. (-क्लः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 One of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>n. (-क्लं)<BR>1 Silver.<BR>2 Fresh butter.<BR>3 A disease of the cornea, opacity, albugo.<BR>m. (-क्लः)<BR>One half of a month: see शुक्लपक्ष.<BR>f. (-क्ला)<BR>1 A name of SARASVATĪ.<BR>2 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to be pure, &c., Uṇādi aff. रन्, and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लकण्ठक|शुक्लकंठक|शुक्लकण्ठकः
शुक्लकण्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of gallinule or water-hen.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, कण्ठ the throat, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लकर्म्मन्|शुक्लकर्मन्
शुक्लकर्म्मन्<BR>mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>Innocent, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, pure, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लत्व|शुक्लत्वं
शुक्लत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Whiteness.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and त्व aff.; also with तल् aff. शुक्लता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लदुग्ध|शुक्लदुग्धः
शुक्लदुग्ध<BR>m. (-ग्धः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लधातु|शुक्लधातुः
शुक्लधातु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>Chalk.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपक्ष|शुक्लपक्षः
शुक्लपक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The light half of a month, the fifteen days of the moon's increase, or from new to full moon.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and पक्ष part or fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपुष्प|शुक्लपुष्पः
शुक्लपुष्प<BR>m. (-ष्पः)<BR>1 The white variety of Amaranth, (Gomphrœna globosa.)<BR>2 A species of jasmine, (Jasminum pubescens.) [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">Page851</a>]<BR>f. (-ष्पा)<BR>1 A shrub, (Phrynium dichotomum.)<BR>2 A sort of sun-flower.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=850" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपृष्ठक|शुक्लपृष्ठकः
शुक्लपृष्ठक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A small tree, (Vitex nigundo.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लबल|शुक्लबलः
शुक्लबल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A name, common to nine persons peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and बल a BALADEVA, there being nine white BALADEVAS, corresponding to the nine KṚṢṆAS, or black VĀSUDEVAS, according to the notions of this sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लमण्डल|शुक्लमण्डलं
शुक्लमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The white of the eye, the cornea.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लवर्ग|शुक्लवर्गः
शुक्लवर्ग<BR>m. (-र्गः)<BR>1 A class of white objects, or the conch, pearloyster, and cowrie, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लवायस|शुक्लवायसः
शुक्लवायस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>A crane.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and वायस a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लाङ्ग|शुक्लांग|शुक्लाङ्गः
शुक्लाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Having a white body or limbs.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लापाङ्ग|शुक्लापांग|शुक्लापाङ्गः
शुक्लापाङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>A peacock.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and अपाङ्ग the corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लिमन्
शुक्लिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Whiteness.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लीकरण
शुक्लीकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Whitening, making white.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल, and करण making, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लीकृत
शुक्लीकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Made white, whitened.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल, and कृत made, च्चि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लोपला
शुक्लोपला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>2 Any white stone.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्षि|शुक्षिः
शुक्षि<BR>m. (-क्षिः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry up, Uṇādi aff. क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्ग|शुंग|शुंगः|शुङ्गः
शुङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 The Indian fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>2 The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1 The sheath or calyx of a young bud.<BR>2 The waved leaf fig.<BR>3 The awn of barley, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शम to rest or pacify, aff. गच्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्गिन्|शुंगिन्
शुङ्गिन्<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>शुङ्ग the calyx of the bud, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच
शुच<BR>r. 1st cl. (शोचति)<BR>To regret, to grieve for.<BR>r. 4th cl. (ई इर) ईशुचिर (शुच्यति)<BR>1 To be wet.<BR>2 To be clean or pure.<BR>3 To stink, to be fetid.<BR>4 To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच्<BR>f. (शुक्)<BR>1 Sorrow, grief, distress, regret.<BR>2 Calamity, affliction.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to regret, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added, शुचा f. (-चा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि<BR>mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Clean, cleansed, purified.<BR>3 Pure, pious, exempt from passion or vice.<BR>4 Correct, free from fault or error.<BR>m. (-चिः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 Purification by ablution, &c.<BR>3 Judicial acquittal.<BR>4 Mental purity, virtue, goodness.<BR>5 Accuracy, correctness.<BR>6 The condition of the religious student.<BR>7 A faithful and tried minister or friend.<BR>8 The month Āṣārha, (June-July.)<BR>9 The month Jyeṣṭha, (May-June.)<BR>10 The hot season.<BR>11 The passion or sentiment of love.<BR>12 ŚIVA.<BR>13 The sun.<BR>14 The moon.<BR>15 The planet VENUS, or its ruler.<BR>16 A name of fire.<BR>17 A Brahman.<BR>18 Oblation to fire at the first feeding of an infant.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to purify, Uṇādi aff. इन्, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित
शुचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Sad, lamenting.<BR>2 Pure, clean, cleansed.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to grieve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिता
शुचिता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Purity, cleanness.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शुचित्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिप्रणी
शुचिप्रणी<BR>f. (-णीः)<BR>Sipping water, rinsing the mouth, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि purification, and प्रणी effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमणि|शुचिमणिः
शुचिमणि<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि white, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिरोचिस्
शुचिरोचिस्<BR>m. (-चीः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि white, and रोचिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिव्रत
शुचिव्रत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Pious, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि, and व्रत obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्मित
शुचिस्मित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Smiled, smiling sweetly, accompanied with a sweet smile.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि white, (from the teeth being shewn,) and स्मित smiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य
शुच्य<BR>(ई) शुच्यी r. 1st cl. (शुच्यति)<BR>1 To bathe.<BR>2 To distil.<BR>3 To express or squeeze out.<BR>4 To churn.<BR>5 To pain or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर्य्य|शुटीर्य|शुटीर्यं|शुटीर्य्यं
शुटीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Heroism, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>शौटीर a hero, यत् aff.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीरता
शुटीरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Valour, heroism.<BR>E.<BR>शौटीर a hero, तल् aff., and the diphthong changed to the short vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ
शुठ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (शोठति शोठयति) also (इ) शुठि (शुण्ठतिशुण्ठयति)<BR>1 To be prevented or obstructed.<BR>2 To have any impediment to motion, to be lame, &c.<BR>2 To be lazy, to be dull or slow.<BR>4 To be or become dry or desiccated.<BR>5 To dry, to desiccate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण
शुण<BR>r. 6th cl. (शुणति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुंठिः|शुण्ठिः
शुण्ठि<BR>f. (-ण्ठिः-ण्ठी)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>शुठि to be stopped, (by it, phlegm,) aff. अच्, and fem. aff. ङीप्, or in one case इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्य|शुंठ्य
शुण्ठ्य<BR>n. (-ण्ठ्यं)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>शुठि to be stopped, (disease by it,) and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड|शुंड|शुंडः|शुण्डः
शुण्ड<BR>m. (-ण्डः)<BR>The exudation from an elephant's temples.<BR>f. (-ण्डा)<BR>1 A tavern.<BR>2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>3 An animal called the waterelephant, the hippopotamus perhaps.<BR>4 An elephant's proboscis or trunk.<BR>5 The stalk of the lotus.<BR>6 A whore.<BR>7 A bawd.<BR>E.<BR>शुण to go, aff. ड, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुंडकः|शुण्डकः
शुण्डक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A distiller.<BR>2 A military flute or fife (?)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डापान|शुंडापान|शुण्डापानं
शुण्डापान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A place where spirits are sold, a tavern, a dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा spirits, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुंडारः|शुण्डारः
शुण्डार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A distiller, a vintner.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा spirits, र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डाल|शुंडाल|शुंडालः|शुण्डालः
शुण्डाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा his trunk, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिका|शुंडिका
शुण्डिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>The soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा an elephant's proboscis, कन् fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिन्|शुंडिन्
शुण्डिन्<BR>m. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 A distiller, a preparer and vender of spirituous liquor.<BR>2 An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा spirits, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रि|शुतुद्रिः
शुतुद्रि<BR>f. (-द्रिः)<BR>The Śatadru river or Setlej; see शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रु|शुतुद्रुः
शुतुद्रु<BR>f. (-द्रुः-द्रूः)<BR>The Śatadru river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध|शुद्धं|शुद्धः
शुद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>1 Pure, purified, clean, cleansed.<BR>2 Faultless, correct.<BR>3 Alone, only, mere, simple.<BR>4 White.<BR>5 Whetted, sharp, (as an arrow.)<BR>6 Authorised, admitted.<BR>7 Innocent.<BR>8 Acquitted.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>1 Pure spirit.<BR>2 Rock salt.<BR>E.<BR>शुध to be or make pure, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धकोटि|शुद्धकोटिः
शुद्धकोटि<BR>f. (-टिः)<BR>One of the sides of a right-angled triangle.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and कोटि flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धजङ्घ|शुद्धजंघ|शुद्धजङ्घः
शुद्धजङ्घ<BR>m. (-ङ्घः)<BR>An ass.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध clean, pure, and जङ्घा the thigh or leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धत्व
शुद्धत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Purity, cleanness, freedom from soil or defect.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to शुद्ध; also with तल्, शुद्धता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धदत्|शुद्धदन्त्
शुद्धदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>White-toothed, having handsome teeth.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=851" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धधी
शुद्धधी<BR>mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि)<BR>Of pure understanding.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धबध
शुद्धबध<BR>m. (-धः)<BR>Simple putting to death, i. e. in any ordinary way.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and बध putting to death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धमति|शुद्धमतिः
शुद्धमति<BR>mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>1 Of pure or sincere purposes, honest, free from guile.<BR>2 Intelligent.<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>One of the Jaina pontiffs of the last age.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध pure, मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवर्ण
शुद्धवर्ण<BR>mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>1 Of a good colour, caste, &c.<BR>2 Welllettered.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and वर्ण colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवल्लिका
शुद्धवल्लिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध pure, वल्ली pedicle, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवासस्
शुद्धवासस्<BR>mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>Clean, having clean vesture.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and वासस् clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धानुमान
शुद्धानुमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A figure of rhetoric.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध correct, and अनुमान inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्त|शुद्धांत|शुद्धान्तः
शुद्धान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>1 A seraglio, a Haram.<BR>2 The private or women's apartments in the palace of a prince.<BR>3 The king's wife or concubine.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध pure, and अन्त end, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्तपालक|शुद्धांतपालक|शुद्धान्तपालकः
शुद्धान्तपालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A eunuch or an attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्धान्त the Haram, and पालक a guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्तयुज्
शुद्धान्तयुज्<BR>f. (-युक्)<BR>Change of mode or key in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धापह्नुति|शुद्धापह्नुतिः
शुद्धापह्नुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>A figure of rhetoric.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध correct, अपह्नुति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धि|शुद्धिः
शुद्धि<BR>f. (-द्धिः)<BR>1 Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>2 Purity, purification.<BR>3 Correction, correctness.<BR>4 Innocence established by ordeal or trial, acquittal.<BR>E.<BR>शुध to be or make pure, &c., aff. क्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धिभृत्
शुद्धिभृत्<BR>mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>1 Clean, clear, free from soil.<BR>2 Pure, virtuous.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्धि, and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धोदन
शुद्धोदन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>King of KAPILA and father of ŚĀKYA.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्ध, and ओदन rice, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धोदनसुत|शुद्धोदनसुतः
शुद्धोदनसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>ŚĀKYA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्धोदन the father of this personage, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध
शुध<BR>(ओ ऌ) औशुधॢ r. 4th cl. (शुध्यति)<BR>To be or become pure or purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन|शुनः
शुन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dog.<BR>E.<BR>शुण to go, अच् aff.: see शुनि, श्वन्, &c.; also with कन् added शुनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनाशीर|शुनाशीरः
शुनाशीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>सु good, venerable, नासीर van of his army, the स in each case changed; also शुनासीर, and more correctly, सुनासीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनि|शुनिः
शुनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>शुण to go, इक् aff. or श्वन् with ङीष् aff., and the semivowel changed<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनिन्धय|शुनिंधय
शुनिन्धय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Suckled by a bitch.<BR>E.<BR>शुनी, and धे to suck, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनीर|शुनीरः
शुनीर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A number of dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध
शुन्ध<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (शुन्धति-ते शुन्धयति-ते)<BR>1 To be or become pure.<BR>2 To cleanse, to purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्यु|शुंध्युः|शुन्ध्युः
शुन्ध्यु<BR>m. (-न्ध्युः)<BR>Fire.<BR>E.<BR>शुधि to purify, चुश् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
शुन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Empty, void.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 A number of dogs.<BR>2 A cypher.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, and यत् aff., the vowel substituted for the semivowel, more commonly शून्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ<BR>r. 1st cl. (शोभति-ते) r. 6th cl. (शुभति)<BR>1 To be splendid, to shine.<BR>2 To be beautiful or handsome.<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (शोभति शुभति)<BR>To hurt or injure, to kill.<BR>r. 1st cl. (शोभति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right, fortunate, auspicious.<BR>2 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>3 Splendid, shining.<BR>4 Eminent, distinguished.<BR>5 Learned, versed in the Vedas, &c.<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>1 Good, good fortune, auspiciousness, happiness.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>One of the astrological Yogas.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 An assemblage of the gods.<BR>2 A female friend and companion of the goddess UMĀ.<BR>3 Bambu manna.<BR>4 Bent grass.<BR>5 The Śami tree.<BR>6 A yellow pigment: see गोरोचना.<BR>7 Light, lustre.<BR>8 Beauty.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु<BR>mfn. (-युः-युः-यु)<BR>Happy, fortunate, prosperous.<BR>E.<BR>शुभं happy, युस् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर
शुभकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Propitious, producing good, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and कर what makes: also शुभङ्कर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर्म्मन्|शुभकर्मन्
शुभकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>1 Pious or virtuous act.<BR>2 Reputable occupation or employment.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभग
शुभग<BR>mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>1 Elegant, graceful.<BR>2 Fortunate, propitious.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and गम to go or obtain, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभङ्कर|शुभंकर|शुभङ्करः
शुभङ्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious, conferring happiness or fortune.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ happiness, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभद|शुभदः
शुभद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Propitious, auspicious.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदन्ती|शुभदंती
शुभदन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>1 The female elephant of the N. W. quarter.<BR>2 A woman with good teeth.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ handsome, दन्त tooth, ङीप् aff.; elsewhere read शुभ्रदन्ती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभफल
शुभफल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Happy result or consequence.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभलग्न|शुभलग्नः
शुभलग्न<BR>m. (-ग्नः)<BR>An auspicious moment.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and लग्न rise of a planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभवासन|शुभवासनः
शुभवासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>Perfume for the mouth.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ auspicious, वासन perfuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभशील
शुभशील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a good disposition.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभस्थली
शुभस्थली<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A room or hall in which sacrifices are offered.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ auspicious, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाङ्ग
शुभाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Handsome, elegant.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 The wife of KĀMA.<BR>2 The wife of KUVERA.<BR>3 A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ handsome, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाचार
शुभाचार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Virtuous.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>A female attendant on UMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाञ्जन|शुभाञ्जनः
शुभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga): see शोभाञ्जन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभानन
शुभानन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Handsome, good-looking.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>A handsome woman.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभान्वित|शुभान्वितः
शुभान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Happy, prosperous, fortunate.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ good fortune, and अन्वित endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभापाङ्गा|शुभापांगा
शुभापाङ्गा<BR>f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>A beautiful woman.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and अपाङ्ग the corner of the eye, for the eye or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाशुभ
शुभाशुभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>Prosperous and unfortunate, good and evil.<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>Good and ill fortune.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and अशुभ unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभेतर
शुभेतर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>2 Evil, bad.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ, and इतर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र<BR>mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं)<BR>1 White.<BR>2 Shining.<BR>m. (-भ्रः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 Sandal.<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>1 Talc.<BR>2 Silver.<BR>3 Green vitriol.<BR>f. (-भ्रा)<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>2 Crystal.<BR>3 Bambu manna.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=852" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रकृत्
शुभ्रकृत्<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>The thirty-sixth year of the Indian cycle.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ्र white, and कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रदन्ती
शुभ्रदन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>The female elephant of the north-west quarter.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ्र white, दन्त a tusk, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्ररश्मि|शुभ्ररश्मिः
शुभ्ररश्मि<BR>m. (-श्मिः)<BR>The sun.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ्र white, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रांशु|शुभ्रांशुः
शुभ्रांशु<BR>m. (-शुः)<BR>1 The moon.<BR>2 Camphor.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ्र white, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रि|शुभ्रिः
शुभ्रि<BR>m. (-भ्रिः)<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to be propitious, क्रिन् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुंभः|शुम्भः
शुम्भ<BR>r. 1st and 6th cls. (शुम्भति)<BR>1 To shine, to be splendid or beautiful.<BR>2 To be handsome.<BR>3 To hurt or injure.<BR>4 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुंभः|शुम्भः
शुम्भ<BR>m. (-म्भः)<BR>An Asura or demon slain by DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भघातिनी|शुंभघातिनी
शुम्भघातिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शुम्भ the Asura, and घातिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भपुर|शुम्भपुरं
शुम्भपुर<BR>nf. (-रं-री)<BR>A city and district, perhaps the modern Sambhalpur, in the district of Gondvāna.<BR>E.<BR>शुम्भ the Asura, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भमर्द्दिनी|शुम्भमर्दिनी|शुंभमर्दिनी
शुम्भमर्द्दिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शुम्भ the Asura, and मर्द्दिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर
शुर<BR>(ई) शुरी r. 4th cl. (शूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To hurt, to kill.<BR>2 To be stupid or insensible; also शूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर
शुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A lion.<BR>E.<BR>शुर to injure, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क|शुल्कं|शुल्कः
शुल्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (शुल्कयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>2 To gain or acquire.<BR>3 To create.<BR>4 To abandon, to leave or forsake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क|शुल्कं|शुल्कः
शुल्क<BR>mn. (-ल्कः-ल्कं)<BR>1 Toll, duty, customs or taxes.<BR>2 A present made by the bridegroom to the bride, at the time of bringing her home to his family; a marriage settlement or dower.<BR>3 Money given to the parents of the bride.<BR>4 Money given at the purchase of any thing to ratify the bargain.<BR>5 The profits of household labour, employment of domestic utensils, care of milch cattle, preservation of ornaments, superintendence of servants, &c. when considered as the perquisite of the wife and her own legal property.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्क to quit, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कस्थान
शुल्कस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Any object of taxation or duty.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्क, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कहानि
शुल्कहानि<BR>f. (-निः)<BR>Loss or forfeiture of wages, dower, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्क, and हानि privation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्ल|शुल्लं
शुल्ल<BR>n. (-ल्लं)<BR>A cord, a rope or string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व|शुल्वं
शुल्व<BR>r. 10th cl. (शुल्वयति)<BR>1 To measure.<BR>2 To create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व|शुल्वं
शुल्व<BR>subst. mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वा-ल्वी-ल्वं)<BR>1 A rope, a cord, a string.<BR>n. (-ल्वं)<BR>1 Copper.<BR>2 A sacrificial observance.<BR>3 Institute, law.<BR>4 A quantity of water.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्व to measure, aff. अच्; or शुघ to be pure, &c., Uṇādi aff. वन्, and ध changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्वारि|शुल्वारिः
शुल्वारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>Sulphur.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्व copper, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुमा
शुशुमा<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>The wife of ŚUKRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रुवस्
शुश्रुवस्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वुषी^1-वत्^2)<BR>Heard, having heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, aff. क्वसु.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: f.  SuSruvuzI per Kale 124. (thanks to SergeA).<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161216. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/323, batch 315-320. note: n. Also per Kale..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषक|शुश्रूषकः
शुश्रूषक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A servant, comprehending five descriptions of persons, a pupil, a religious pupil or the member of a religious community under a common head, a hired servant, an officer or deputy, and a slave.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, desid. v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषण|शुश्रूषणं
शुश्रूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Service, serving.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, desiderative form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषा
शुश्रूषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>1 Service, serving of five kinds: see शुश्रूषक.<BR>2 Saying, speaking, telling.<BR>2 Wishing to hear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, desiderative form, अच् aff., fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषापर
शुश्रूषापर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Diligent or attentive in service.<BR>E.<BR>शुश्रूषा, and पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषु
शुश्रूषु<BR>mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>Obedient, serving, attending.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष|शुषः
शुष<BR>(औ, ऌ) औशुषॢ r. 4th cl. (शुष्यति^1)<BR>To dry.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20161123. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष|शुषः
शुष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Drying.<BR>2 A hole in the ground.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषि|शुषिः
शुषि<BR>f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>1 A hole, a chasm.<BR>2 Drying.<BR>3 The hollow or groove in the fang of a snake.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, aff. कि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिर|शुषिरं|शुषिरः
शुषिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Perforated, bored, pierced, full of holes or spaces.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 A hole, a vacuity, a chasm.<BR>2 A wind-instrument.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>2 A rat.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>1 A sort of perfume, commonly Nalī.<BR>2 A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, Uṇādi aff. किरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिल|शुषिलः
शुषिल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, किरच् aff., semivowel changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्क|शुष्कः
शुष्क<BR>mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>1 Dry, dried.<BR>2 Groundless, causeless.<BR>3 Unproductive, unprofitable.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, aff. क, or Uṇādi aff. कक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कता
शुष्कता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Dryness.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शुष्कत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कमांस|शुष्कमांसं
शुष्कमांस<BR>n. (-सं)<BR>1 Dry flesh.<BR>2 Dried meat.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क dry, मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कल|शुष्कलं|शुष्कलः
शुष्कल<BR>mfn. subst. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>Dry flesh.<BR>adj.<BR>Eating fish and flesh.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, कलच् Uṇādi aff. or शुष्क, and ला to take, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कवैर
शुष्कवैर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Groundless enmity.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क, and वैर enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कव्रण|शुष्कव्रणः
शुष्कव्रण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A scar, a cicatrised sore.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क dry, and व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्काङ्ग|शुष्काङ्गः
शुष्काङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Emaciate, withered.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क dry, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कान्न
शुष्कान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Rice in the husk.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क, and अन्न rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कार्द्र|शुष्कार्द्रं
शुष्कार्द्र<BR>n. (-र्द्रं)<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्क dry, and आर्द्र ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्ण|शुष्णः
शुष्ण<BR>m. (-ष्णः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, न Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्म|शुष्मं|शुष्मः
शुष्म<BR>m. (-ष्मः)<BR>1 The sun.<BR>2 Fire.<BR>3 Air, wind.<BR>n. (-ष्मं)<BR>1 Light, lustre.<BR>2 Strength, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मन्
शुष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>Fire.<BR>n. (-ष्म)<BR>1 Light, lustre.<BR>2 Strength, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्यत्
शुष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Drying.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक|शूकं|शूकः
शूक<BR>mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1 The awn of barley, &c.<BR>2 A bristle, a spicula.<BR>3 Compassion, clemency, tenderness.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>शो to make sharp or thin, ऊक aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकक|शूककः
शूकक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 Barley, or a bearded kind of wheat resembling it.<BR>2 The sentiment of compassion or tenderness.<BR>E.<BR>कन added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूककीट|शूककीटः
शूककीट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>A caterpillar.<BR>E.<BR>शूक a bristle, (the hairs on the insect,) and कीट a worm; also with कन् added शूककीटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकतृण|शूकतृणं
शूकतृण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>A kind of grass.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकधान्य|शूकधान्यं
शूकधान्य<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>Awned or bearded grain, as barley, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकपिण्डि|शूकपिंडि|शूकपिण्डिः
शूकपिण्डि<BR>f. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, and पिण्डि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=853" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकर|शूकरः
शूकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A hog.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>1 A kind of moss, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>2 A sow.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, (a bristle,) र aff., or शू imitative sound, कृ to make, with अच् and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकराक्रान्ता
शूकराक्रान्ता<BR>f. (-न्ता)<BR>A kind of moss, &c.: see the last; also वराहक्रान्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकल|शूकलः
शूकल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकवत्|शूकवन्त्
शूकवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Awned, bearded.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकशिम्बा|शूकशिंबा
शूकशिम्बा<BR>f. (-म्बा)<BR>Cowach.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, and शिम्बा a pod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकशिम्बि|शूकशिम्बिः
शूकशिम्बि<BR>f. (-म्बिः-म्बी)<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, and शिम्बि a pod; also with कन् added शूकशिम्बिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकापुट्ट
शूकापुट्ट<BR>m. (-ट्टः)<BR>A gem, perhaps amber.<BR>E.<BR>शूक an awn, आङ् before पुट्ट to become small, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकिन्
शूकिन्<BR>mfn. (-की-किनी-कि)<BR>Awned, bearded, (as grain.)<BR>E.<BR>शूक, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकुल
शूकुल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A fish in general.<BR>2 A kind of fish.<BR>3 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक्ष्म|शूक्ष्मं|शूक्ष्मः
शूक्ष्म<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)<BR>Minute, small, fine, subtile.<BR>m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR>1 Fraud, dishonesty.<BR>2 Universal spirit.<BR>E.<BR>स substituted for श in the more correct form सूक्ष्म, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्र|शूद्रः
शूद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A man of the fourth or servile tribe, said to have sprung from the feet of BRAHMĀ.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>A woman of the Śūdra tribe.<BR>f. (-द्री or -द्राणी)<BR>The wife of a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to purify or cleanse, Uṇādi aff. रक्, the vowel made long, and च changed to द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रता
शूद्रता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>The nature or condition of a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शूद्रत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रधर्म्म|शूद्रधर्म|शूद्रधर्म्मः
शूद्रधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>The duty of the Śūdra tribe, the service of the other three.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र a Śūdra, and धर्म्म moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रप्रेष्य|शूद्रप्रेष्यः
शूद्रप्रेष्य<BR>m. (-ष्यः)<BR>A man of the three first classes, who has become a servant to one of the fourth.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र a Śūdra, and प्रेष्य a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रभिक्षित
शूद्रभिक्षित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Alms begged or received from a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and भिक्षित begged as alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रभूयिष्ठ
शूद्रभूयिष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Abounding with Śūdras.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and भूयिष्ठ many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रयाजक|शूद्रयाजकः
शूद्रयाजक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A priest who conducts sacrifices for Śūdras.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and याजक sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रराज्य
शूद्रराज्य<BR>n. (-ज्यं)<BR>A country of which a Śūdra is king.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and राज्य kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रवृत्ति|शूद्रवृत्तिः
शूद्रवृत्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>The duty or occupation of a Śūdra.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र, and वृत्ति employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रशासन|शूद्रशासनं
शूद्रशासन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An edict or grant, &c. addressed to persons of the servile caste.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र a Śūdra, and शासन edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रापरिणयन
शूद्रापरिणयन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marrying a Śūdra female.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्रा, and परिणयन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रापुत्त्र
शूद्रापुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>The son of any man by a Śūdra woman.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्रा, and पुत्त्र son; also शूद्रासुतः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रार्त्ता|शूद्रार्ता
शूद्रार्त्ता<BR>f. (-र्त्ता)<BR>A plant, Priyangu commonly.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र a Śūdra, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रावेदन
शूद्रावेदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Marrying a woman of the fourth class.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्रा, and आवेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रावेदिन्
शूद्रावेदिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>A man of the three first classes, who has a Śūdra wife.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्रा, and आवेदिन् who marries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्राभार्य्य|शूद्राभार्य|शूद्राभार्यः|शूद्राभार्य्यः
शूद्राभार्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>The husband of a Śūdra woman.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्रा Śūdra woman, and भार्य्या a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Swelled, increased, grown.<BR>2 Morbidly swollen.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>1 A shambles, a slaughter-house.<BR>2 The soft palate.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to increase, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूनावत्
शूनावत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A butcher, one who keeps a place where animals are killed for sale.<BR>E.<BR>शूना a shambles, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्य|शून्यं|शून्यः
शून्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>1 Empty, void.<BR>2 Lonely, desart.<BR>n. (-न्यं)<BR>1 Heaven, sky, æther.<BR>2 A dot, a spot.<BR>3 A cypher.<BR>4 A vacuum.<BR>f. (-न्या)<BR>1 A hollow reed.<BR>2 The prickly pear.<BR>E.<BR>शुन a dog, यत् aff. of fitness, and the vowel substituted for the semivowel, and made optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यगेह
शून्यगेह<BR>n. (-हं)<BR>An empty or deserted house.<BR>E.<BR>शून्य, and गेह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यत्व
शून्यत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>1 Vacuity, emptiness.<BR>2 Unreality, the false or illusory nature of all existence.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to शून्य; also with तल्, शून्यता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यमध्य|शून्यमध्यः
शून्यमध्य<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>A hollow reed.<BR>E.<BR>शून्य empty, and मध्य the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यवादिन्
शून्यवादिन्<BR>m. (-दी)<BR>1 A Bauddha.<BR>2 An atheist.<BR>E.<BR>शून्य vacuum, and वादिन् declaring; denying the existence of any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यस्थान
शून्यस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>An empty place.<BR>E.<BR>शून्य, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यहस्त
शून्यहस्त<BR>mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>Empty-handed.<BR>E.<BR>शून्य, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूयमान
शूयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Swelling, enlarging, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to swell, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर<BR>r. 10th cl. (शूरयते)<BR>1 To be valiant or powerful.<BR>2 To make great effort or exertion.<BR>(ई) शूरी r. 4th cl. (शूर्य्यते)<BR>1 To hurt or kill.<BR>2 To be stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hero.<BR>2 The sun.<BR>3 A lion.<BR>4 A boar.<BR>5 The grandfather of KṚṢṆA.<BR>6 The Śāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>E.<BR>शु to bear, Sautra root, Uṇādi aff. क्रन्, and the vowel made long, or शूर to be brave, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरण|शूरणः
शूरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum, Rox.)<BR>2 A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>शूरी to hurt, (some diseases,) aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरणोद्भुज|शूरणोद्भुजः
शूरणोद्भुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>शूरण the Arum, and उद् before भुज to eat, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरता
शूरता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Heroism, prowess.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to शूर; also with त्व, शूरत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरदेव|शूरदेवः
शूरदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The second Jina of the future era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमान
शूरमान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Vaunting, pride of prowess.<BR>E.<BR>शूर, and मान pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमानिन्
शूरमानिन्<BR>m. (-नी)<BR>A boaster, one who thinks himself a hero.<BR>E.<BR>शूर, and मन to think, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरम्मन्य|शूरंमन्य
शूरम्मन्य<BR>m. (-न्यः)<BR>A boaster, one who thinks himself a hero<BR>E.<BR>शूर, and मन to think, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरसेन|शूरसेनः
शूरसेन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The country about Mathura.<BR>2 The name of a prince.<BR>E.<BR>शूर a hero, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्पः|शूर्प्प
शूर्प<BR>r. 10th cl. (शूर्पयति)<BR>To mete or measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्प|शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्पः
शूर्प्प<BR>mn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पं)<BR>1 A winnowing basket.<BR>2 A measure of two Droṇas.<BR>f. (-र्प्पी)<BR>A small kind of winnowing basket, a toy for children.<BR>2 The sister of RĀVAṆA: see शूर्प्पनखा.<BR>E.<BR>शृ to injure, Uṇādi aff. प, and ऊ substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=854" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पक|शूर्पक|शूर्पकः
शूर्प्पक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A demon, the enemy of KĀMADEVA.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प to measure, aff. ण्वुल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पकर्ण|शूर्पकर्ण|शूर्पकर्णः
शूर्प्पकर्ण<BR>m. (-र्णः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प a winnowing basket, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पकाराति|शूर्पकाराति|शूर्पकारातिः
शूर्प्पकाराति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्पक a demon, and अराति an enemy; also शूर्प्पकारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पनखा|शूर्पनखा
शूर्प्पनखा<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>The sister of the Daitya RĀVAṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प a winnowing basket, and नख a finger nail, (having them as large,) fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्, whence also शूर्प्पनस्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पनिष्पाव|शूर्पनिष्पाव
शूर्प्पनिष्पाव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A measure (a basket) of winnowed corn.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प, and निष्पाव winnowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पपर्णी|शूर्पपर्णी
शूर्प्पपर्णी<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पवात|शूर्पवात|शूर्पवातः
शूर्प्पवात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>The air as agitated by the shaking of the winnowing basket.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प a basket, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पश्रुति|शूर्पश्रुति|शूर्पश्रुतिः
शूर्प्पश्रुति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>An elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प a winnowing basket, and श्रुति an ear; as large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्म्म|शूर्म|शूर्मः|शूर्म्मः
शूर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>An iron image, &c.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्म्मि|शूर्मि|शूर्मिः|शूर्म्मिः
शूर्म्मि<BR>mf. (-र्म्मिः-र्म्मी)<BR>1 An iron image.<BR>2 An anvil.<BR>E.<BR>शु for शोभा beauty, and उर्म्मि a wave or line, ङीष् optionally added; deriv. irr.: also with इ rejected, and कन् added, fem. form शूर्म्मिका; again, as differently read, सूर्म्मि, स्युर्म्मि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल|शूलं|शूलः
शूल<BR>r. 1st cl. (शूलति)<BR>1 To disorder, to distemper or disease.<BR>2 To make a loud noise.<BR>3 To impale, to transfix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल|शूलं|शूलः
शूल<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>1 Sharp pain in general, or especially in the belly, as cholic, &c. or in the joints, from rheumatism^1 or gout.<BR>2 A weapon, a pike, a dart.<BR>3 An iron pin or spit.<BR>4 A banner, an ensign.<BR>5 An astrological Yoga, that of the 9th lunar mansion.<BR>6 Death, dying.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>1 A whore.<BR>2 An instrument used for putting criminals to death, a stake for impaling them.<BR>E.<BR>शूल to disease, &c., aff. अच्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलक|शूलकः
शूलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A restive horse.<BR>E.<BR>शूल to distress, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलघातन|शूलघातनं
शूलघातन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Iron rust or filings.<BR>E.<BR>शूल pain, and घातन what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलघ्न|शूलघ्नः
शूलघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing or allaying sharp pain, sedative, anodyne.<BR>E.<BR>शूल, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधन्वन्
शूलधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a pike or the three-pronged one, the trident of this deity, धन्वन् a bow, put for a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधर|शूलधरः
शूलधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>f. (-रा)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a pike or trident, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधृक्
शूलधृक्<BR>f. (-धृक्)<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a trident, and धृष to be bold, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलनाशन|शूलनाशनं
शूलनाशन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>White Sochal salt.<BR>E.<BR>शूल cholic, and नाशन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलशत्रु|शूलशत्रुः
शूलशत्रु<BR>m. (-त्रुः)<BR>The castor oil plant, (Ricinus communis.)<BR>E.<BR>शूल cholic, and शत्रु hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलहस्त|शूलहस्तः
शूलहस्त<BR>m. (-स्तः)<BR>One armed with a lance or pike.<BR>E.<BR>शूल, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलहृत्
शूलहृत्<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>Asafoetida.<BR>E.<BR>शूल cholic, and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलाकृत|शूलाकृतं
शूलाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Roasted on a spit, (meat.)<BR>E.<BR>शूल a spit, and कृत made, with डाच् augment, spitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलाग्र
शूलाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The point of a pike, stake, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शूल, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिक|शूलिकं|शूलिकः
शूलिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Roat meat.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hare.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a spit, and ठ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन्
शूलिन्<BR>mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>Suffering sharp pain, having the cholic, &c.<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>1 MAHĀDEVA.<BR>2 A spearman.<BR>3 A stakebearer.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a trident, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन|शूलिनः
शूलिन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Indian fig tree.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a stake, इनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलोत्खा
शूलोत्खा<BR>f. (-त्खा)<BR>A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्य|शूल्यं
शूल्य<BR>mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>1 Roasted, (on a spit.)<BR>2 Deserving impalement.<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>Roasted meat.<BR>E.<BR>शूल a spit, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष|शूषः
शूष<BR>r. 1st cl. (शूषति)<BR>To bring forth, to propagate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृकाल|शृकालः
शृकाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A jackal: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगाल|शृगालः
शृगाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 A shakal or jackal.<BR>2 A coward, a poltroon.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>4 An ill-natured or harsh-speaking man.<BR>5 A demon so named.<BR>6 KṚṢṆA.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 Flight, retreat.<BR>2 A fox.<BR>3 A she jackal.<BR>E.<BR>शृज to create or abandon, (deceit, &c.) कालन् aff., or शृंग a horn, अ negative prefix, ला to possess, aff. क, deriv. irr.; also सृगाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालकण्टक|शृगालकण्टकः
शृगालकण्टक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, commonly Seyālkānta or jackal's thorn, (Zizyphus scandens.)<BR>E.<BR>शृगाल, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालकोलि|शृगालकोलिः
शृगालकोलि<BR>m. (-लिः)<BR>A sort of jujube.<BR>E.<BR>शृगाल a jackal, and कोलि the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालजम्बू|शृगालजंबू
शृगालजम्बू<BR>f. (-म्बूः)<BR>1 A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>2 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>E.<BR>शृगाल a jackal, and जम्बू roseapple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालिका
शृगालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>1 The female jackal.<BR>2 A fox.<BR>3 Running away, flight, retreat.<BR>4 A plant, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR>E.<BR>शृगाली as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलं|शृंखलः|शृङ्खलः
शृङ्खल<BR>subst. mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>A belt or chain worn round a man's body.<BR>2 A chain for confining an elephant.<BR>3 A chain, a fetter in general.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, here said to mean a link, and खल to collect, aff. अच्; or शिञ्जा the tinkling of a chain, and स्खल to go, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलक|शृंखलक|शृंखलकः|शृङ्खलकः
शृङ्खलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A young camel with wooden rings or clogs on his feet.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्खल a chain, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलता
शृङ्खलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 Connexion, concatenation.<BR>2 Restraint.<BR>E.<BR>तल् added to शृङ्खल; also with त्व, शृङ्खलत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलित|शृंखलित|शृङ्खलितः
शृङ्खलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Bound, chained, fettered, captive.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्खला a chain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्ग|शृंग|शृंगं|शृङ्गं|शृङ्गः
शृङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>1 A horn.<BR>2 A mark, a sign.<BR>3 The top of a mountain.<BR>4 Sovereignty, mastership.<BR>6 Dignity, elevation.<BR>6 A fountain, an artificial one or jet d'eau.<BR>7 A lotus.<BR>8 Very sharp.<BR>9 Minutely fine.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>1 A medicinal root, commonly Jīvaka.<BR>2 A Muni so named.<BR>f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 Gold.<BR>2 A fish, (Silurus Singio, HAM.)<BR>3 A plant, (Betula.)<BR>4 Ṛṣabha, a medicinal root, shaped like a bull's horn.<BR>5 Another plant, a kind of Rhus, with an excrescence or gall in the bark, compared to a crab's horn.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. गन्, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गक|शृंगक|शृंगकं|शृंगकः|शृङ्गकः
शृङ्गक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A medicinal root, commonly Jivaka.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गला
शृङ्गला<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A plant, a kind of Rhus, having an excrescence in the bark formed by an insect, which is compared in shape to the horn of a goat or a crab.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गवेर|शृंगवेर
शृङ्गवेर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>Ginger.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, and वेर body or shape; also with कन् added, शृङ्गवेरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=855" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाट|शृंगाट|शृङ्गाटं|शृंगाटः|शृङ्गाटः
शृङ्गाट<BR>n. (-टं)<BR>A place where four roads meet.<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Ruellia or Barleria longifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, अट to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाटक|शृंगाटक|शृङ्गाटकं|शृंगाटकः|शृङ्गाटकः
शृङ्गाटक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A place where four roads meet.<BR>2 An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>2 A door.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A collection or mountain of three peaks.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृंगारः|शृङ्गारः
शृङ्गार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 Love, the passion or sentiment as an object of poetical description or dramatic representation.<BR>2 Copulation, coition.<BR>3 Marks made with red-lead on an elephant's head and trunk by way of ornament.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>1 Cloves.<BR>2 Redlead.<BR>3 Fragrant powder for the dress or person.<BR>4 Ginger.<BR>5 Agallochum.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग eminence, dignity, ऋ to go to or obtain, and अण् aff.; being the chief of the poetical Rasas; or शॄ to hurt, आरन् Uṇādi aff. with नुम्, and गुक् augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृंगारकः|शृङ्गारकः
शृङ्गारक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Horned, having a horn or crest.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग, and आरकन् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारभूषण|शृंगारभूषण|शृङ्गारभूषणं
शृङ्गारभूषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Red-lead.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्गार love, and भूषण adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारयोनि|शृंगारयोनि|शृङ्गारयोनिः
शृङ्गारयोनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>The deity of love or KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्गार the passion, and योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारित|शृंगारित
शृङ्गारित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Stained with red-lead, reddened.<BR>2 Affected with passion.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्गार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारिन्|शृंगारिन्
शृङ्गारिन्<BR>mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>1 Feeling, or relating to the passion of love.<BR>2 Stained with red lead.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>1 An empassioned lover.<BR>2 Dress, decoration.<BR>3 An elephant.<BR>4 The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्गार love, इनि aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गि|शृंगि|शृंगिः|शृङ्गिः
शृङ्गि<BR>f. (-ङ्गिः)<BR>A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus Singio, HAM.)<BR>mn. (-ङ्गिः-ङ्गि)<BR>Gold for ornaments: see शृङ्ग and शृङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिक|शृंगिक|शृंगिकं|शृङ्गिकं
शृङ्गिक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A plant, (Betula.)<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a fish, &c., कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिकनक
शृङ्गिकनक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Gold for ornaments.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्गि the same, and कनक gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृंगिणः|शृङ्गिणः
शृङ्गिण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Horned.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A ram.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, इनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिन्|शृंगिन्
शृङ्गिन्<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>1 Horned.<BR>2 Crested, peaked.<BR>m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>2 A mountain.<BR>3 A tree.<BR>f. (-ङ्गिणी)<BR>1 A cow.<BR>2 Arabian jasmine.<BR>3 Heart pea.<BR>4 Katuki, a medicinal plant.<BR>E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, &c., इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणि|शृणिः
शृणि<BR>f. (-णिः)<BR>The hook for goading an elephant.<BR>E.<BR>शॄ to injure, नि aff., and the radical vowel made short; also सृनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृण्वत्
शृण्वत्<BR>mfn. (-ण्वन्-ण्वन्ती-ण्वत्)<BR>Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Boiled, (water, milk or Ghee.)<BR>E.<BR>श्रा to boil, aff. क्त, form. irr.; as applied to any other substances, the form is श्राण or श्रपित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध
शृध<BR>(उ) शृधु r. 1st cl. (शर्द्धति)<BR>To fart.<BR>(शर्द्धति-ते)<BR>To be moist or wet.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (शर्द्धति शर्द्धयति)<BR>To insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधू
शृधू<BR>f. (-धूः)<BR>The anus.<BR>E.<BR>शृध to fart, &c., Uṇādi aff. कू; also read शृधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (शृणाति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>With वि prefixed, pass. v.<BR>(विशीर्य्यते)<BR>To be injured or impaired, to waste or decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखर|शेखरं|शेखरः
शेखर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A garland of flowers worn on the crown of the head.<BR>2 A crest.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The root of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR>E.<BR>शिथि to go, अरन् aff., and the nasal omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरित
शेखरित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Crested, tufted, topped, peaked.<BR>E.<BR>शेखर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेणवी
शेणवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेणा
शेणा<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Understanding, mind, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेप|शेपः
शेप<BR>m. (-पः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, प aff.; also शेफस्, also read शेपस् n. (-पः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपाल|शेपालः
शेपाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>Vallisneria: see शैवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफ|शेफः
शेफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, फ aff.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफस्
शेफस्<BR>n. (-फः)<BR>The penis.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, (semine effuso,) असुन् aff., and फुट् augment; also with पुट augment, शेपस्, and with a final vowel, शेप or शेफ; again, व being substituted for प, शेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालि|शेफालिः
शेफालि<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>A plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिका
शेफालिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A flower, (Nyctanthes arbor-tristis.)<BR>E.<BR>शेफा sleeping, from शी with फ aff., अलि a bee, fem. aff. ङीष्, and कन् added; also शेफालि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेमुषी
शेमुषी<BR>f. (-षी)<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>E.<BR>शे derived from शीङ् to sleep, with the aff. विच्; implying, ignorance or delusion; मुष to steal, to take away, affs. क and ङीष्; or शम to pacify, (the senses,) क्वसु participial aff., fem. form, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेल
शेल<BR>(ऋ) शेऌ r. 1st cl. (शेलति)<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>2 To shake, to tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलु|शेलुः
शेलु<BR>m. (-लुः)<BR>A small tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>E.<BR>शिल to glean, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव|शेवः
शेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The penis.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>3 Heighth, elevation.<BR>4 Happiness.<BR>ind. (-वम्)<BR>Hail, homage, a term of exclamation or salutation addressed to the deities.<BR>E.<BR>शीङ् to sleep, Uṇādi aff. वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवधि|शेवधिः
शेवधि<BR>m. (-धिः)<BR>A treasure as belonging to KUVERA, a Nidhi or substance of extraordinary rarity and value, possessed only by the god of wealth.<BR>E.<BR>शेव happiness, धा to have, कि aff.; or शे in future, अवधि boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवल|शेवलं
शेवल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra): see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाल|शेवालं
शेवाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, (on the water,) वालन् Uṇādi aff.; also व being changed to प, शेपाल, and the pen. vowel shortened, शेवल; also शैवल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्यित
शेश्यित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Fast asleep, sleeping much.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, intens. v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्यितवत्
शेश्यितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Sleeping much or soundly.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, intens. v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्वीयमान
शेश्वीयमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Enlarging, expanding.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to increase, intens. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष|शेषं|शेषः
शेष<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>Remainder, leavings, rest, balance; what is left, omitted or rejected.<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 The king of the serpent race, as a large thousand-headed snake, at once the couch and canopy of VIṢṆU, and the upholder of the world, which rests on one of his heads.<BR>2 A name of BALADEVA.<BR>3 Killing, destroying, finishing.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Flowers and other things that have been offered to an idol, and are then distributed amongst the worshippers and attendants.<BR>E.<BR>शिष to specify, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषकाल|शेषकालः
शेषकाल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The last term, the time of death.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=856" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभाग|शेषभागः
शेषभाग<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>The last or remaining part.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभुज्
शेषभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Who eats the leavings of others.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभोजन
शेषभोजन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Eating the rest of the food after feeding the family, guests, &c.<BR>2 Eating the leavings of a meal.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरक्षण
शेषरक्षण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Taking care that an undertaking is brought to a conclusion.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरात्रि|शेषरात्रिः
शेषरात्रि<BR>f. (-त्रिः)<BR>The last watch of the night.<BR>E.<BR>शेष the remainder, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषान्न
शेषान्न<BR>n. (-न्नं)<BR>Leavings of a meal, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषावस्था
शेषावस्था<BR>f. (-स्था)<BR>The last state or condition of life.<BR>E.<BR>शेष, and अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शै
शै<BR>r. 1st cl. (शायस्रे)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष|शैक्षः
शैक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>A young Brahman in his noviciate, one who has begun to read the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>शिक्षा the pronunciation of the language of the Vedas, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख|शैखः
शैख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The offspring of an outcaste Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरिक|शैखरिकः
शैखरिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>E.<BR>शेखर a crest or top, ठक् aff.; also with ढक् aff. शैखरेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्य|शैत्यं
शैत्य<BR>n. (-त्यं)<BR>Cold, coldness.<BR>E.<BR>शीत cold, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिल्य|शैथिल्यं
शैथिल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>1 Looseness, laxity.<BR>2 Flaccidity.<BR>3 Slackness, remission.<BR>4 Relaxation of rule or connexion.<BR>E.<BR>शिथिल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैनेय|शैनेयः
शैनेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>SĀTYAKI, the charioteer of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरीयक|शैरीयकः
शैरीयक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A shrub, (Barleria cristata); also शैरेयक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल|शैलं|शैलः
शैल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>1 Mountainous, mountaineer, &c.<BR>2 Stony, rocky.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A mountain.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 Bitumen.<BR>2 Storax.<BR>3 A sort of collyrium: see रसाञ्जन.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A concise interpretation of a grammatical aphorism.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a rock, a stone, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलक|शैलकं
शैलक<BR>n. (कं)<BR>Storax or Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलकटक|शैलकटकः
शैलकटक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The brow or slope of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and कटक flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलज|शैलजं
शैलज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced in or on mountains, rocks, &c.<BR>n. (-जं)<BR>1 A fragrant resinous substance, (Storax or Benzoin.)<BR>2 Bitumen.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलजन|शैलजनः
शैलजन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A mountaineer.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलधन्वन्
शैलधन्वन्<BR>m. (-न्वा)<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलधर|शैलधरः
शैलधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, and धर who upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलनिर्य्यास|शैलनिर्यास|शैलनिर्यासः|शैलनिर्य्यासं
शैलनिर्य्यास<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Storax, Benzoin.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a rock, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलपति|शैलपतिः
शैलपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>The Himālaya.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलभित्ति|शैलभित्तिः
शैलभित्ति<BR>f. (-त्तिः)<BR>A stone-cutter's chisel or axe, an instrument for dividing or cutting stones.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, भिद to divide, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलमय
शैलमय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Rocky.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलरन्ध्र|शैलरंध्र
शैलरन्ध्र<BR>n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>A cavern, a cave.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशिखर
शैलशिखर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The crest or peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and शिखर a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशिविर|शैलशिविरं
शैलशिविर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The ocean.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a rock, and शिविर a camp or palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशृङ्ग
शैलशृङ्ग<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>The peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलसार
शैलसार<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Hard, firm, as a rock.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाग्र|शैलाग्रं
शैलाग्र<BR>n. (-ग्रं)<BR>The peak of a mountain.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाट|शैलाटः
शैलाट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>2 A mountaineer, a savage, a barbarian.<BR>3 An attendant on an idol.<BR>4 Crystal.<BR>E.<BR>शैल a mountain, and अट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालिन्
शैलालिन्<BR>m. (-ली)<BR>An actor, a dancer.<BR>E.<BR>शिलालिन् a Muni, said to have been the author of the principles of acting, &c., अण् aff., शैलाल his institutes, and इनि aff. of profession or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलिक्य|शैलिक्यः
शैलिक्य<BR>m. (-क्यः)<BR>An impostor, a pretended devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूष|शैलूषः
शैलूष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>An actor, a dancer, a tumbler, &c.<BR>2 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>3 The master of the band, or one who beats time.<BR>4 The Bel tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E.<BR>शिलूष one of the early teachers of the arts of acting, &c., अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेय|शैलेयं|शैलेयः
शैलेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Produced in the mountains, &c., mountainous, mountaineer^1.<BR>2 Mountain-like.<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>1 A fragrant resin, (Storax or Benzoin.)<BR>2 A vegetable perfume, commonly Murā.<BR>3 Rock salt.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A bee.<BR>f. (-यी)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a mountain, ढक् aff.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलोपशल्य
शैलोपशल्य<BR>n. (-ल्यं)<BR>The skirts of a mountain or low land at its base.<BR>E.<BR>शैल, and उपशल्य neighbouring space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल्य|शैल्यं
शैल्य<BR>nf. (-ल्यं-ली)<BR>Hardness, stoniness.<BR>E.<BR>शिला a stone, a rock, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव|शैवं|शैवः
शैव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>Relating or appertaining to the god ŚIVA.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>A worshipper of ŚIVA.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra).<BR>E.<BR>शिव the deity, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवल|शैवलं|शैवलः
शैवल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An aquatic plant.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A drug, commonly termed Padamkāṭh.<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, (on the water,) वलञ् aff.; also शैवाल, शेवाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवलिनी
शैवलिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A river in general.<BR>E.<BR>शैवल Vallisneria, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवाल|शैवालं
शैवाल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>E.<BR>शी to sleep, (on the water,) वालन् aff., शेवाल, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव्य|शैव्यः
शैव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-वी-व्यं)<BR>Relating to ŚIVA, &c.<BR>m. (-व्यः)<BR>1 One of the horses of KṚṢṆA car.<BR>2 A king and champion in the Pāṇḍava army.<BR>E.<BR>शिव, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशव|शैशवं
शैशव<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>Childhood, pupilage, the period under sixteen.<BR>E.<BR>शिशु a child, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैष्योपाध्यायिका
शैष्योपाध्यायिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Instruction of youth, tuition.<BR>E.<BR>शिष्य a pupil, उपाध्याय a preceptor, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शो
शो<BR>r. 4th cl. (श्यति)<BR>1 To reduce or make small, to pare.<BR>2 To whet or sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोक|शोकः
शोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Sorrow, grief.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to regret, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकचर्चा|शोकचर्च्चा
शोकचर्चा<BR>f. (-र्चा)<BR>Indulgence in sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and चर्चा search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकछिद्|शोकच्छिद्
शोकछिद्<BR>mfn. (-छिद्)<BR>Consoling, allaying, removing sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and छिद what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकनिहत
शोकनिहत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Afflicted, overcome with grief.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and निहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकभङ्ग
शोकभङ्ग<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>Dissipating or removing sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शाक, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=857" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकमूर्च्छित
शोकमूर्च्छित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Involved in distress, swooning with grief.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and मूर्च्छित fainted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकस्थान
शोकस्थान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Site, circumstance, or occasion of sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाकुल
शोकाकुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Overcome with sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and आकुल bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाग्नि|शोकाग्निः
शोकाग्नि<BR>m. (-ग्निः)<BR>Deep distress, violent grief.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and अग्नि fire; also similar compounds, as शोकानल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाग्निसन्तप्त|शोकाग्निसंतप्त
शोकाग्निसन्तप्त<BR>mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>Distressed.<BR>E.<BR>शोकाग्नि, and सन्तप्त inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापनुद
शोकापनुद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>1 Alleviating, consoling.<BR>2 Being consoled.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and अपनुद what drives away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापनोद|शोकापनोदः
शोकापनोद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A teacher of holy wisdom, a philosopher.<BR>E.<BR>शोक worldly care, अप away, नुद to send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापहर्त्तृ|शोकापहर्तृ
शोकापहर्त्तृ<BR>mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>Allaying or dissipating grief.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and अपहर्त्तृ what drives away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकारि|शोकारिः
शोकारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR>E.<BR>शोक sorrow, अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकार्त्त|शोकार्त
शोकार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Pained, afflicted by sorrow.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकोद्भव
शोकोद्भव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Born or produced from or caused by grief.<BR>E.<BR>शोक, and उद्भब produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचन|शोचनं
शोचन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sorrowing, sorrowful.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sorrow, grief, grieving.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to grieve, aff. युच् or ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचनीय
शोचनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be grieved or lamented, what may or ought to be.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to be sad, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित
शोचित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sorrowful, afflicted.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि to grieve, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचितव्य
शोचितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be grieved for, lamentable.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to grieve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित्वा
शोचित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Grieving or having grieved for.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि to lament, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिष्केश|शोचिष्केशः
शोचिष्केश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Fire or its deity.<BR>E.<BR>शोचिस् light, and केश hair, having locks of flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिस्
शोचिस्<BR>n. (-चिः)<BR>Light, lustre, radiance, flame.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to be or make pure, Uṇādi aff. इसि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्य
शोच्य<BR>mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>1 To be lamented or bewailed.<BR>2 To be cleansed or purified.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to grieve, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्यक
शोच्यक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A low man.<BR>E.<BR>शोच्य to be purified (from), कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ<BR>m. (-ठः)<BR>1 A fool, a blockhead.<BR>2 A sluggard, an idler.<BR>3 A rogue, a cheat.<BR>4 A low man, one of a degraded tribe or business.<BR>5 A villain, a criminal, a sinner.<BR>E.<BR>शुठ to be prevented or stopped, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण<BR>(ऋ) शोणृ r. 1st cl. (शोणति)<BR>1 To be red.<BR>2 To move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं)<BR>1 Crimson, of a crimson colour.<BR>2 Red in the face, from passion, &c.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 Crimson, the colour of the red lotus.<BR>2 A horse of a reddish or bright chesnut colour.<BR>3 The Śoṇa river, which rises in the table land of Amarakaṇṭaka, and running first northerly and then easterly for 500 miles, falls into the Ganges above Patna.<BR>4 A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>5 Fire or its deity.<BR>6 An ocean.<BR>7 A red sort of sugar-cane.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Red-lead.<BR>2 Blood.<BR>E.<BR>शोण to be red, aff. अच्, fem. aff. ठाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणक|शोणकः
शोणक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणरत्न|शोणरत्नं
शोणरत्न<BR>n. (-त्नं)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>शोण deep red, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणाक|शोणाकः
शोणाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>शोण red, अक to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणित|शोणितं
शोणित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Red, crimson, purple.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Blood.<BR>2 Saffron.<BR>E.<BR>शोण redness, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितप
शोणितप<BR>mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>Who or what drinks blood.<BR>E.<BR>शोणित, and पा to drink, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितपुर|शोणितपुरं
शोणितपुर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The city of Bānāsur.<BR>E.<BR>शोणित red, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितोक्षित
शोणितोक्षित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Stained or sprinkled with blood.<BR>E.<BR>शोणित, and उक्षित moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितोपल|शोणितोपलः
शोणितोपल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>A ruby.<BR>E.<BR>शोणित red, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिमन्
शोणिमन्<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>Redness.<BR>E.<BR>शोण, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथ|शोथः
शोथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>Swelling, intumescence.<BR>E.<BR>शु to go, (to grow,) Uṇādi aff. थन्; also with कन् added शोथक m. (-कः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथघ्न|शोथघ्नः
शोथघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Discutient, removing swellings.<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Hogweed, (Boerhavia diffusa.)<BR>E.<BR>शोथ swelling, घ्न removing, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथजित्
शोथजित्<BR>mfn. (-जित्)<BR>Discutient.<BR>f. (जित्)<BR>Hogweed: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>शोथ swelling, and जित् overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथहृत्
शोथहृत्<BR>mfn. (-हृत्)<BR>Discutient, removing swellings.<BR>m. (-हृत्)<BR>Marking-nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>शोथ swelling, and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधक|शोधकः
शोधक<BR>mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>Who or what cleans, purifies, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A refiner.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) The subtrahend.<BR>E.<BR>शुध to be pure, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधन|शोधनं|शोधनः
शोधन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Cleaning, purifying, &c., that which cleanses, refines, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Cleaning, cleansing, purifying.<BR>2 Correcting, freeing from faults or errors.<BR>3 Correcting, as a writing.<BR>4 Subtraction, (in arithmetic.)<BR>5 The refining of metals.<BR>6 A sort of refining, practised for chemical or medical purposes; exposing the metals to heat, and then sprinkling them with the urine of cows, &c.<BR>7 Payment, acquittance.<BR>8 Fæces, ordure.<BR>9 Green vitriol.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The lime.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A broom.<BR>E.<BR>शुघ to be or make pure, aff. ल्युट् or युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनीय|शोधनीयः
शोधनीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>1 To be corrected.<BR>2 To be cleansed or purified.<BR>3 To be refined.<BR>4 To be subtracted.<BR>5 To be liquidated (as a debt), due.<BR>E.<BR>शुघ to purify, aff. अनीयर्; also शोध्य and शोधितव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधयित्वा
शोधयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>1 Having paid or discharged.<BR>2 Having cleared, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुघ to be pure, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधित|शोधितं
शोधित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>2 Strained.<BR>3 Corrected.<BR>4 Refined.<BR>5 Purified.<BR>6 Discharged, liquidated, (as a debt.)<BR>E.<BR>शुध to clean, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध्य|शोध्यः
शोध्य<BR>mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>1 To be purified, cleaned, refined, &c.<BR>2 Payable, due.<BR>3 To be subtracted.<BR>m. (-ध्यः)<BR>An accused person, one to be justified or tried.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>A constant number to be subtracted in some astronomical computations.<BR>E.<BR>शुध to be pure, यत aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोफ|शोफः
शोफ<BR>m. (-फः)<BR>Intumescense.<BR>E.<BR>शु to go, aff. फ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभ
शोभ<BR>mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>1 Handsome.<BR>2 Bright.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>1 Light, lustre, radiance, splendour.<BR>2 Beauty.<BR>3 Distinguished merit.<BR>4 A species of the Kṛti metre.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, aff. अच, fem. aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=858" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभकृत्
शोभकृत्<BR>mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>Beautifying.<BR>m. (-कृत्)<BR>1 The thirty-sixth year of the Hindu cycle.<BR>2 Marking-nut plant.<BR>E.<BR>शोभ handsome, and कृन् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभन|शोभनं|शोभनः
शोभन<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>2 Shining, splendid.<BR>3 Richly dressed or ornamented.<BR>4 Propitious, auspicious.<BR>5 Virtuous, moral, decorous, good.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 The fifth Yoga.<BR>2 A planet.<BR>3 Burnt-offering for auspicious results.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 Shining, being splendid or handsome.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनक|शोभनकः
शोभनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनाचरित
शोभनाचरित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Virtuous practice.<BR>E.<BR>शोभन, and आचरित done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभमाण
शोभमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Fair, splendid, shining.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, &c., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभाञ्जन|शोभांजन|शोभाञ्जनः
शोभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A tree, commonly Sajinā or Sahajnā, (Hyperanthera morunga); the legumes, blossoms, and leaves are esculent, and the root of the young tree is used as a substitute for horse-radish: in medicine the root is used as a rubefacient externally, as a stimulant internally, and the expressed oil of the seeds is employed to relieve arthritic pains, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शोभा beauty, अञ्ज to pervade or anoint, and ल्युट् or युच् aff; also शौभाञ्जन and सोभाञ्जन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभित
शोभित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Beautified, decorated.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुच्यमान
शोशुच्यमान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Sorrowing or grieving deeply.<BR>E.<BR>शुच to be sorrowful, intens. v., शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोष|शोषः
शोष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Pulmonary consumption.<BR>2 Drying.<BR>3 Intumescence, swelling.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषण|शोषणं|शोषणः
शोषण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Suction, sucking.<BR>2 Drying up.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA, or CUPID.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषयित्वा
शोषयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having dried up.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषित|शोषितः
शोषित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Dried, dried up, desiccated.<BR>E.<BR>शुष to dry, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोस्
शोस्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle of reproach or contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक|शौकं
शौक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 A flock of parrots.<BR>2 Sorrowfulness.<BR>E.<BR>शुक a parrot, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्त|शौक्तं
शौक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ती-क्तं)<BR>Acid, acetic.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्त vinegar, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिक
शौक्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 Acid, acetic.<BR>2 Relating to a pearl, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्त or शुक्ति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तेय|शौक्तेयं
शौक्तेय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>A pearl.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ति a pearl-oyster, ढक् aff.; also from शुक्तिका with the same, शौक्तिकेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्लिकेय|शौक्लिकेयः
शौक्लिकेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A sort of poison.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्लिक a country, ढक् aff.: according to some it is the venom of a snake of the Amphisbœna kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्ल्य|शौक्ल्यं
शौक्ल्य<BR>n. (-क्ल्यं)<BR>Whiteness.<BR>E.<BR>शुक्ल white, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौच|शौचं
शौच<BR>n. (-चं)<BR>1 Purification by ablution, &c. from personal defilement.<BR>2 Purification at given periods from defilement caused by the death of a relation, &c.<BR>3 The state or property of freedom from defilement, purity, cleanness.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि purity, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचविधि
शौचविधि<BR>f. (-धिः)<BR>The rules of purification after defilement by the death of a relation, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शौच, and बिधि precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचाचार|शौचाचारः
शौचाचार<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A rule of purification, the mode in which the person is to be cleansed by ablution, &c. after voiding any excrement or contracting any impurity.<BR>E.<BR>शौच purification, and आचार rule, rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेय|शौचेयः
शौचेय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>A washerman.<BR>E.<BR>शुचि cleaning, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेप्सु
शौचेप्सु<BR>mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु)<BR>Wishing or intending to be purified.<BR>E.<BR>शौच, and इप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौट
शौट<BR>(ऋ) शौटृ r. 1st cl. (शौटति)<BR>To be proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर|शौटीरः
शौटीर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>Proud, haughty.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A hero.<BR>2 An ascetic, one who abandons the world.<BR>3 A proud or haughty man, but of low tribe or occupation, an upstart.<BR>E.<BR>शौट to be proud, and ईरन् Uṇādi aff.; also as derived from शौड the same, शौडीर; also the short vowel being substituted for the diphthong, शुटीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर्य्य|शौटीर्य|शौटीर्यं|शौटीर्य्यं
शौटीर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Heroism, prowess.<BR>2 Pride, arrogance.<BR>E.<BR>शौटीर a hero, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड
शौड<BR>(ऋ) शौडृ r. 1st cl. (शौडति)<BR>To be proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्ड|शौंड|शौण्डः
शौण्ड<BR>mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>1 Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>2 Fond of, addicted to, (as liquor.)<BR>f. (-ण्डी)<BR>1 Long-pepper.<BR>2 Another sort, (Piper chavya.)<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा spirituous liquor, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डर्य्य|शौण्डर्य|शौंडर्य
शौण्डर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिक|शौंडिक|शौंडिकः|शौण्डिकः
शौण्डिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A distiller and vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>f. (-की)<BR>A female keeper of a tavern or dram shop.<BR>E.<BR>शुण्डा spirits, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिर
शौण्डिर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>2 Elevated, looking upwards; more properly, शौडीर, and शौटीर as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्र|शौद्रः
शौद्र<BR>mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं)<BR>Śaudra, servile, relating or belonging to the last class.<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>The son of a man of either of the first three classes by a Śūdra woman, the last of the twelve sons acknowledged in the ancient Hindu law.<BR>E.<BR>शूद्र a Śūdra, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्धोदनि|शौद्धोदनिः
शौद्धोदनि<BR>m. (-निः)<BR>BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR>E.<BR>शुद्धोदन a prince of the family of IKṢVĀKU, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौधिका
शौधिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A white variety of panic seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनक|शौनकः
शौनक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of an inspired legislator older than MANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनिक|शौनिकः
शौनिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A butcher, a poulterer, a vender of the flesh of beasts or birds.<BR>2 Chase, hunting.<BR>E.<BR>शूना a slaughterhouse, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभ|शौभं|शौभः
शौभ<BR>n. (-भं)<BR>The city of HARIŚCANDRA, suspended in the air.<BR>m. (-भः)<BR>1 A god, a divinity.<BR>2 The betel-nut.<BR>E.<BR>शुभ auspicious, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभनेय|शौभनेयः
शौभनेय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>1 Sprung from a handsome mother.<BR>2 Relating to any thing handsome or brilliant.<BR>E.<BR>शोभना a handsome woman, aff. ढक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभाञ्जन|शौभांजन|शौभांजनः|शौभाञ्जनः
शौभाञ्जन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The Sajina tree.<BR>E.<BR>अण् pleonasm, added to शोभाञ्जन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभिक|शौभिकः
शौभिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A juggler, a conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरि|शौरिः
शौरि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>1 A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2 The planet SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>शूर a proper name or a hero, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्प्प|शौर्प|शौर्पः
शौर्प्प<BR>mfn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पी-र्प्पं)<BR>Measured by a winnowing basket, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शूर्प्प a basket, अण् aff.; also with ठक् aff. शौर्प्पिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य्य|शौर्य|शौर्यं|शौर्य्यं
शौर्य्य<BR>n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>1 Valour, heroism, prowess.<BR>2 The heroic drama, or that which treats of war, magic, &c.<BR>E.<BR>शूर a hero, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=859" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य्योपार्ज्जित|शौर्योपार्जित
शौर्य्योपार्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Acquired by valour.<BR>E.<BR>शौर्य्य, and उपार्ज्जित acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्क|शौल्कं|शौल्कः
शौल्क<BR>mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्की-ल्कं)<BR>Relating to customs or duties, levied as a tax, &c.<BR>m. (-ल्कः)<BR>A superintendant of tolls or customs, a custom-house officer.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्क a toll or tax, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किक|शौल्किकः
शौल्किक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to a tax, a toll, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Superintendant of tolls or customs.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्क a toll, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्विक|शौल्विकः
शौल्विक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A coppersmith.<BR>E.<BR>शुल्व copper, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिक|शौवस्तिकं
शौवस्तिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Of or belonging to to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस्तन् of to-morrow, ठक् added, with तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिकत्व
शौवस्तिकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Ephemeralness, duration for a day.<BR>E.<BR>शौवस्तिक, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवापद|शौवापदं
शौवापद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Relating to a beast of prey, savage, wild, ferocious, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्वापद a beast of prey, अण् aff., and औ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौष्कल|शौष्कलः
शौष्कल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>Eating fish and flesh.<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The price of dried meat.<BR>E.<BR>शुष्कली dried flesh, aff. अण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत
श्चुत<BR>(इर) श्चुतिर r. 1st cl. (श्चोतति)<BR>1 To ooze, to drop or distil.<BR>2 To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोत|श्चोतः
श्चोत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR>E.<BR>श्चुत to sprinkle, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युत
श्च्युत<BR>(इर) श्च्युतिर् r. 1st cl. (श्च्योतति)<BR>1 To sprinkle.<BR>2 To ooze, to drop or distil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युतित
श्च्युतित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Dropping, flowing.<BR>2 Shed, sprinkled, issued, oozed.<BR>E.<BR>श्च्युत to sprinkle, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योत|श्च्योतः
श्च्योत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>Sprinkling, pouring forth, aspersion.<BR>E.<BR>श्च्युत to sprinkle, aff. घञ्; also श्चोत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योतत्
श्च्योतत्<BR>mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>1 Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>2 Shedding.<BR>E.<BR>श्च्युत to ooze, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मन्
श्मन्<BR>Aptote noun.<BR>The face, the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशान|श्मशानं
श्मशान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>E.<BR>श्म substituted for शव a corpse, and शान for शयन place of repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवासिन्
श्मशानवासिन्<BR>mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>A ghost, a gole, a sprite, male or female, abiding in cemeteries, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्मशान a cemetery, and वासिन् who abides; also श्मशाननिवासिन्, श्मशानवर्त्तिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवेश्मन्
श्मशानवेश्मन्<BR>m. (-श्मा)<BR>1 MAHĀDEVA.<BR>2 A ghost.<BR>E.<BR>श्मशान a cemetery, and वेश्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रु
श्मश्रु<BR>n. (-श्रु)<BR>The beard.<BR>E.<BR>श्मन् for मुख the face, श्रि to serve, Uṇādi aff. डुन्, form irr.; also श्मश्रुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुमुखी
श्मश्रुमुखी<BR>f. (-खी)<BR>A woman with a beard.<BR>E.<BR>श्मश्रु a beard, and मुख the face, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुल
श्मश्रुल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Bearded, having a beard.<BR>E.<BR>श्मश्रु, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुवर्द्धक
श्मश्रुवर्द्धक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A barber.<BR>E.<BR>श्मश्रु, and वर्द्धक who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रूयमाण
श्मश्रूयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Being as if bearded, having something like a beard.<BR>E.<BR>श्मश्रु used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मील
श्मील<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्मीलति)<BR>1 To wink, to contract the eyelids.<BR>2 To twinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलन|श्मीलनं
श्मीलन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Winking, twinkling.<BR>E.<BR>श्मील, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलित|श्मीलितं
श्मीलित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Winked, blinked.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>A wink, winking.<BR>E.<BR>श्मील to wink, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>Viscous, thick, adhesive, as clarified butter, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Smoke.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याम|श्यामः
श्याम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>1 Black or dark-blue.<BR>2 Green.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A sacred fig tree at Prayāga or Allahabad.<BR>2 A cloud.<BR>3 The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>4 A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>5 Black, (the colour.)<BR>6 Green, (the colour.)<BR>7 Thorn-apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>mf. (-मः-मा)<BR>A sort of grain, (Panicum frumentaceum).<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>1 Pepper.<BR>2 Sea salt.<BR>f. (-मा)<BR>1 A woman, described as one who has not borne children; also described as a female of slender make; or one from eight to sixteen; or one who resembles in darkness of complexion, the blossom of the Priyangu, or its stalk, in shape.<BR>2 Night.<BR>3 Shade, shadow.<BR>4 The Jumnā river.<BR>5 A form of DURGĀ.<BR>6 A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>7 A sort of Convolvulus, (C. turpethum,) with black flowers.<BR>8 A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>9 Indigo.<BR>10 A twining shrub, (Ichnocarpus frutescens.)<BR>11 Turmeric.<BR>12 Holy basil.<BR>12 A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>14 A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>15 A small singing bird with black plumage, commonly Shāma, (Turdus macrourus.)<BR>16 A cow.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, Uṇādi aff. मक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामक|श्यामकं|श्यामकः
श्यामक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of grain, (Panicum frumentaceum, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>श्यामा the same, कन् added, m. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामकण्ठ|श्यामकंठ|श्यामकण्ठः
श्यामकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>2 ŚIVA.<BR>3 A small kind of bird.<BR>E.<BR>श्याम black or blue, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामत्व
श्यामत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Blackness.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to श्याम; also with तल्, श्यामता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामपत्र|श्यामपत्रः
श्यामपत्र<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>The Tamāla tree, (Xanthocymus pictorius.)<BR>E.<BR>श्याम black, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामभास्
श्यामभास्<BR>mfn. (-भाः-भाः-भः)<BR>Black as jet, of a glossy black hue.<BR>E.<BR>श्याम, and भास् shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामल|श्यामलः
श्यामल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Of a black or dark-blue colour.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>1 Black, (the colour.)<BR>2 Black-pepper.<BR>3 The religious fig tree.<BR>4 A large bee.<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>श्याम black, ला to have, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामलता
श्यामलता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A climbing plant, (Ichnocarpus frutescens.)<BR>E.<BR>श्याम, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाक|श्यामाकः
श्यामाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A kind of grain generally eaten by the Hindus, (Panicum frumentaceum; also P. colonum.)<BR>E.<BR>श्यामा the same, कन् added, and the final retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाङ्ग|श्यामांग|श्यामाङ्गः
श्यामाङ्ग<BR>mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>Black-bodied, black.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>The planet MERCURY or its ruler.<BR>E.<BR>श्याम black, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामापूजा
श्यामापूजा<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>Worship of ŚYĀMĀ or DURGĀ, on the new moon of Kārttika.<BR>E.<BR>श्यामा, and पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामित
श्यामित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Blackened, turned or become black.<BR>E.<BR>श्याम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याल|श्यालः
श्याल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A wife's brother.<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>A wife's sister.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, aff. कालन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालक|श्यालकः
श्यालक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A wife's brother.<BR>f. (-लिका-लकी)<BR>A wife's sister.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव<BR>mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>Of a brown colour.<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Brown, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, व aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यावतैल|श्यावतैलः
श्यावतैल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>श्याव brown, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यावदत्|श्यावदन्त्
श्यावदत्<BR>mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>Dark or black toothed, (naturally so.)<BR>E.<BR>श्याव dark or brown, दतृ for दन्त a tooth; also श्यावदन्त and श्यावदन्तक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=860" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता or -नी-तं)<BR>White, of a white colour.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>White, (the colour.)<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, Uṇādi aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येतकोलक|श्येतकोलकः
श्येतकोलक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A sort of fish, (Cyprinus sophore, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येन|श्येनः
श्येन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 A hawk, a falcon.<BR>2 White, (the colour.)<BR>3 Whiteness, paleness.<BR>4 Violence, desperation.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>1 The female hawk.<BR>2 A species of the Triṣṭubh metre.<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, इञ् Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनकरण
श्येनकरण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Acting rashly or desperately.<BR>2 Burning on a separate funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>श्येन, and करण acting; also श्येनकरणिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनचित्
श्येनचित्<BR>m. (-चित्)<BR>1 A hawk feeder or keeper.<BR>2 A receptacle shaped like a hawk for a sacrificial fire.<BR>E.<BR>श्येन a hawk, and चित् what collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनजीविन्
श्येनजीविन्<BR>m. (-वी)<BR>One who sells hawks or lives by training them.<BR>E.<BR>श्येन, and जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनोपदेश
श्येनोपदेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>Recommendation or injunction to women, to burn on a separate funeral pile.<BR>E.<BR>श्येन violence, and उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्यायते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनम्पाता|श्यैनंपाता
श्यैनम्पाता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Hawking, hunting.<BR>E.<BR>श्येन a hawk, पात falling, ञ aff., with नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योणाक|श्योणाकः
श्योणाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>E.<BR>श्यै to go, डुणाक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रक
श्रक<BR>(इ) श्रकि r. 1st cl. (श्रंकते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रग
श्रग<BR>(इ) श्रगि r. 1st cl. (श्रंगति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण
श्रण<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रणति, श्राणयति) usually with वि prefixed, (विश्राणयति)<BR>To give, to present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत्<BR>ind.<BR>A particle and prefix implying belief or reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ
श्रथ<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रथति, श्रथयति)<BR>1 To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>2 To let loose or discharge, to set free, to liberate.<BR>3 To bind or tie.<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्राथयति)<BR>1 To apply diligently, to endeavour sedulously.<BR>2 To delight frequently.<BR>3 To march.<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्रथयति)<BR>To be weak or infirm.<BR>(इ) श्रथि r. 1st cl. (श्रंथते)<BR>1 To be loose or lax, to be slack or flaccid.<BR>2 To let loose, to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथन|श्रथनं
श्रथन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Tying, stringing.<BR>2 Loosening, untying.<BR>E.<BR>श्रथ to tie, &c., aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधत्
श्रद्दधत्<BR>mfn. (-धन्-धती-धत्)<BR>Believing, having faith.<BR>E.<BR>श्रत्, and दधत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधान|श्रद्दधानः
श्रद्दधान<BR>mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>1 Trusting, believing.<BR>2 Venerating, respecting.<BR>E.<BR>श्रत् particle of faith or respect, धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध<BR>nf. (-द्धं-द्धा)<BR>1 Respect, reverence.<BR>2 Wish, desire.<BR>3 Faith, belief.<BR>4 Purity.<BR>E.<BR>श्रत् a particle implying belief, &c., धा to hold or have, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धाकृत
श्रद्धाकृत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Done with faith.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धान्वित
श्रद्धान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Believing, faithful.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and अन्वित endowed with; also श्रद्धासमन्वित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धामय
श्रद्धामय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Believing, full of faith.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धायुक्त
श्रद्धायुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Having faith, believing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धारहित
श्रद्धारहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Distrusting, unbelieving.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and रहित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु<BR>mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>1 Faithful, believing.<BR>2 Wishing, desirous.<BR>f. (-लुः)<BR>A pregnant woman longing for any thing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा faith, आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धावत्|श्रद्धावन्त्
श्रद्धावत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Believing, trusting, having faith.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः|श्रन्थः
श्रन्थ<BR>r. 9th cl. (श्रथ्नाति)<BR>1 To set free, to let loose, to liberate.<BR>2 To gladden, to delight frequently.<BR>3 To string, to tie together.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रन्थति श्रन्थयति)<BR>To arrange, to place in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः|श्रन्थः
श्रन्थ<BR>m. (-न्थः)<BR>1 Loosening, liberating.<BR>2 Looesness, flaccidity.<BR>3 Tying, binding, stringing.<BR>4 A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्रन्थ to tie, &c., aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थन|श्रंथन|श्रंथनं|श्रन्थनं
श्रन्थन<BR>nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>1 Stringing flowers, &c.<BR>2 Killing, destroying.<BR>3 Tying, binding.<BR>4 Loosening, untying.<BR>E.<BR>श्रन्थ to tie or unite, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थित|श्रंथित|श्रन्थितः
श्रन्थित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Strung, connected, bound together.<BR>2 Overcome, surpassed, overpowered.<BR>3 Hurt, injured.<BR>4 Loosed, let loose.<BR>E.<BR>श्रन्थ to tie, or श्रथि to hurt, &c., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपण|श्रपणं|श्रपणः
श्रपण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Boiling in a pot.<BR>E.<BR>श्रै to boil, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपयित्वा
श्रपयित्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having boiled or dressed.<BR>E.<BR>श्रै to cook, causal v., क्त्रा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपित|श्रपितं
श्रपित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Boiled, (any thing except water, milk or Ghee.)<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>श्रै to cook or boil, causal v., aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम<BR>(ञि इर, उ) श्रमु r. 4th cl. (श्राम्यति)<BR>1 To perform acts of austere devotion, to undergo mortification or penance.<BR>2 To be wearied or fatigued.<BR>3 To be distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 Military exercise.<BR>2 Weariness, fatigue.<BR>3 Labour, exertion, toil.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be wearied, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमजल
श्रमजल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>Perspiration from exertion or fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Following a low or degraded business or profession.<BR>2 Base, vile, bad.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 A religious character, an ascetic, a Yati, one devoted to meditation for the purpose of obtaining final emancipation from existence, probably the Sarmanes of the Greek writers.<BR>2 A beggar, the religious mendicant.<BR>f. (-णा or णी)<BR>1 Indian spikenard, (Valeriana Jatamansi.)<BR>2 Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>3 A handsome woman.<BR>4 A woman of low caste or business.<BR>5 A female mendicant.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be wearied, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमसिद्ध
श्रमसिद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Accomplished by labour or exertion.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम, and सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमार्त्त|श्रमार्त
श्रमार्त्त<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>Exhausted, overcome with fatigue.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन्<BR>mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>1 Wearying, tiring, undergoing or incurring weariness or fatigue.<BR>2 Laborious, diligent.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be weary, aff. घिनुण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्भ
श्रम्भ<BR>(उ) श्रम्भु r. 1st cl. (श्रम्भते)<BR>To be careless or inattentive, to err, to neglect, to mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रय|श्रयः
श्रय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Asylum, refuge, protection.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयण|श्रयणं
श्रयण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Asylum, refuge, shelter, protection.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयणीय
श्रयणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be defended or sheltered.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
श्रव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 Oozing, dripping.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, &c., aff. अप्; also श्रवण, स्रव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=861" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवण|श्रवणं|श्रवणः
श्रवण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Produced in or under the sign ŚRAVAṆĀ.<BR>mn. (-णः-णं)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 Hearing.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>1 Service.<BR>2 Dripping, oozing.<BR>mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>The twenty-third of the lunar asterisms, represented by three footsteps, and containing three stars or α, β and γ Aquilæ.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, &c., aff. ल्युट् or युच्; or श्रवणा the asterism, अण् aff. of derivation, and the effect rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणपथ|श्रवणपथः
श्रवणपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>The ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवण, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणाधिकारिन्
श्रवणाधिकारिन्<BR>m. (-री)<BR>A speaker, an addresser.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवण, and अघिकारिन् connected with or acting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणेन्द्रिय|श्रवणेंद्रिय
श्रवणेन्द्रिय<BR>n. (-यं)<BR>The organ of hearing, the ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवण, and इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणोदर
श्रवणोदर<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The hollow of the outer ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवण, and उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस्<BR>n. (-वः)<BR>The ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, aff. असुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाप्य|श्रवाप्यः
श्रवाप्य<BR>m. (-प्यः)<BR>An animal fit or proper for sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to drip, (Ghee,) आप्य Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठ
श्रविष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>Produced in or under the sign ŚRAVIṢṬHĀ.<BR>f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>The twenty-fourth lunar asterism, also called DHANIṢṬHĀ, corresponding to the DOLPHIN.<BR>E.<BR>श्रव an ear, मतुप् poss. aff., इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative, and the possessive rejected; the attributive is formed by the aff. अण, and that again or its effect optionally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठाज|श्रविष्ठाजः
श्रविष्ठाज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The planet MERCURY.<BR>E.<BR>श्रविष्ठा the asterism, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रा
श्रा<BR>r. 2nd cl. (श्राति)<BR>1 To boil, to cook, to mature, to ripen, &c.<BR>2 To sweat.<BR>Causal form (श्रपयति)<BR>To render mature or ripe by cooking, &c.<BR>(श्रापयति)<BR>To heat, to cause to sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राण|श्राणं
श्राण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>1 Boiled, dressed, (any thing except butter, milk, or water.)<BR>2 Moist, wet.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>Rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>श्रै to cook, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्ध|श्राद्धं
श्राद्ध<BR>mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>Faithful, believing.<BR>n. (-द्धं)<BR>A funeral ceremony observed^1 at various fixed periods and for different purposes, consisting of offerings with water and fire to the gods and manes, and gifts and food to the relations present and assisting Brahmans; it is especially performed for a parent recently deceased, or for three paternal ancestors, or for all ancestors collectively, and is supposed necessary to secure the ascent and residence of the souls of the deceased in a world appropriated to the manes. The following distributions of this ceremony are specified; the पार्व्वणं in honor of three ancestors, एकोद्दिष्टं of one, नित्यं regular, नैमित्तिकं occasionally, काम्यं for the attainment of some particular object, आह्निकं daily, वृद्धिः for the obtaining of increase of prosperity, and सपिण्डनं in which the balls of meat offered to the deceased individually and collectively are blended together. There are many other kinds: those for a person recently deceased are one on the day after mourning expires, and twelve others in twelve successive months; one at the end of the third fortnight, one in the sixth month, and one in the twelfth, concluding with a Sapiṇḍana, on the anniversary of the person's death; in general they are all performed in the course of the two or three first days, and the Śrāddha for the deceased is only annually repeated. There is also a sort of Śrāddha performed daily during the days of mourning, usually ten, on which a funeral cake is presented, increasing one or more each day till ten cakes are offered.<BR>E.<BR>श्रद्धा faith, अण् or ण aff. of possession or relation, as the abandonment or presentation of meat, &c. through faith of its efficacy, in behalf of the souls of the deceased.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकर
श्राद्धकर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The offerer of an obsequial oblation.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकर्म्मन्|श्राद्धकर्मन्
श्राद्धकर्म्मन्<BR>n. (-र्म्म)<BR>The rite or ceremony of funeral oblation.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and कर्म्मन् act; also श्राद्धक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकृत्
श्राद्धकृत्<BR>m. (कृत्)<BR>The celebrator of an obsequial rite.<BR>E.<BR>श्चाद्ध, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धद|श्राद्धदः
श्राद्धद<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>The offerer of an obsequial rite.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेव|श्राद्धदेवः
श्राद्धदेव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध the funeral ceremony called Śrāddha, and देव deity; as judge and monarch of the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेवता
श्राद्धदेवता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>A divinity presiding over obsequial rites, a Pitṛ or progenitor, or YAMA.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धभुज्
श्राद्धभुज्<BR>mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>Eating or partaking of the food prepared at a Śrāddha or obsequial rite.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धशिष्ट
श्राद्धशिष्ट<BR>n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Food that has been presented to the manes.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध, and शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>1 The object, receiver, or enjoyer of an obsequial oblation.<BR>2 Anything relating to a Śrāddha.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध as above, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिन्
श्राद्धिन्<BR>mfn. (-द्धी-द्धिनी-द्धि)<BR>The object or receiver of a funeral oblation.<BR>E.<BR>श्राद्ध as above, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्त|श्रांत|श्रान्तः
श्रान्त<BR>mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>1 Wearied, fatigued.<BR>2 Calmed, tranquil.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>An ascetic, one with subdued passions.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be weary, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्तसंवाहन|श्रान्तसंवाहनं
श्रान्तसंवाहन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Affording rest or relief to the weary, giving them seats, beds, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रान्त wearied, संवाहन relieving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रांतिः|श्रान्तिः
श्रान्ति<BR>f. (-न्तिः)<BR>Weariness, exhaustion.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्रामयति)<BR>1 To call, to summon, to invite.<BR>2 To counsel, to advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>1 A month.<BR>2 A temporary shed, or platform and canopy.<BR>3 Time.<BR>E.<BR>श्रम to be weary, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रामणेर|श्रामणेरः
श्रामणेर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A follower or disciple and servant of the principal Jainas or Jinas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राय|श्रायः
श्राय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>Sacred or belonging to the goddess ŚRĪ.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>Refuge, reliance, shelter or protection.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, aff. अण्, or in the attributive form श्री the goddess, घञ् aff., and इ substituted for the primitive vowel changed to अय, and अ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायस|श्रायसः
श्रायस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सी-सं)<BR>Produced in or on the best, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेयम् the best, अण् aff., and the form changed by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव|श्रावः
श्राव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Oozing, dropping, flowing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to ooze, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावक|श्रावकः
श्रावक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 The lay votary of a Buddha or Jina.<BR>2 A crow.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>1 Produced in or under the asterism Śravaṇā.<BR>2 Relating to the ear or hearing.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>1 The month Śrāvaṇa or Śravaṇā, (July-August.)<BR>2 A heretic, an impostor. [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">Page863</a>]<BR>n. (णं)<BR>Causing to be heard.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, commonly Katuki.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>Day of full moon in the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवणा the asterism, &c., aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=862" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Relating to or produced in the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>E.<BR>श्रवणा the asterism in which the moon is full this month, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणीय
श्रावणीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>To be declared or pronounced, to be made to be heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावन्ती
श्रावन्ती<BR>f. (-न्ती)<BR>A city, also Dharmapattan.<BR>E.<BR>श्र to ooze, causal form, भच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावयितव्य
श्रावयितव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be declared, to be made to be heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावष्ठीय
श्रावष्ठीय<BR>mfn. (-यः-यं)<BR>Produced in or under the asterism ŚRAVIṢṬHĀ, relating to it, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रविष्ठा, and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावित
श्रावित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Spoken or read, caused to be heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव्य
श्राव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>1 To be heard.<BR>2 To be read or related, to be caused to be heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, ण्यत् aff., or causal v., and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि<BR>(श्रि) r. 1st cl. (श्रयति-ते)<BR>To serve.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>1 To seek asylum, to depend upon, to have recourse to.<BR>2 To be near to.<BR>3 To use, to employ.<BR>With अप and आङ्,<BR>To quit, to forsake.<BR>With उत् or सम and उत्,<BR>To be high or elevated.<BR>With वि, अप, and आङ्,<BR>1 To fall, to prostrate, to worship.<BR>2 To expect, to rely upon, to trust to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
श्रित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Cherished, protected, refuged.<BR>2 Served, honored, worshipped.<BR>3 Joined with, contiguous to, connected with.<BR>4 Covered, overspread.<BR>5 Having, possessing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितवत्
श्रितवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>1 Served, honored.<BR>2 Taking refuge with.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिमन्य
श्रिमन्य<BR>mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>Haughty, confident in wealth, beauty, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्री, and मन्य who thinks, the vowel of the first made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष
श्रिष<BR>(उ) श्रिषु r. 10th cl. (श्रेषति)<BR>To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री<BR>r. 9th cl. (श्रीणाति श्रीणीते)<BR>To cook, to dress.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रयति-ते श्रायति-ते)<BR>To satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री<BR>f. (-श्रीः)<BR>1 Fortune, prosperity, success, thriving.<BR>2 Wealth.<BR>3 Beauty, splendour, lustre.<BR>4 Light.<BR>5 The three objects of life collectively, or love, duty, and wealth.<BR>6 Dress, decoration.<BR>7 State, paraphernalia.<BR>8 Superhuman power.<BR>9 Intellect, understanding.<BR>10 Elevation, consequence.<BR>11 Fame, glory.<BR>12 The goddess LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU, and deity of plenty and prosperity.<BR>13 A name of SARASVATI.<BR>14 The mother of KUNTHU, the seventeenth Jina of the present age.<BR>15 The Saral tree, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>16 Cloves.<BR>17 A prefix to the names of deities, forming a kind of invocation at the beginning of a letter, &c. and often used repeatedly, as Śrī Śrī DURGĀ; also a prefix of respect to proper names of persons, as Śri JAYADEVA; also of works, as Śrī Bhāgavata: this use of it is elliptical; the possessive aff. मतुप् or adj. युक्त joined, &c. being understood, and the sense will then be, the splendid, the illustrious, the famous, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, (i. e. whom the world worships,) क्विप् aff. and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठ|श्रीकंठ|श्रीकण्ठः
श्रीकण्ठ<BR>m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>1 ŚIVA.<BR>2 A country N. W. of Dehli, or about Tahnesar.<BR>3 BHAVABHŪTI, the author of the Mālati Mādhava, a celebrated drama.<BR>E.<BR>श्री prosperity or eloquence, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छन|श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छनः
श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>BHAVABHŪTI, the poet.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीकण्ठ, and पद the name or title, लाञ्छन a mark; he who is known by the title of Śrīkaṇṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठसख|श्रीकंठसख|श्रीकण्ठसखः
श्रीकण्ठसख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीकण्ठ ŚIVA, and सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकर|श्रीकरं|श्रीकरः
श्रीकर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>Giving fortune or prosperity.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>The red lotus.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, and कर who makes or confers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकरण|श्रीकरणं
श्रीकरण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A pen.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the word Śrī, and करण implement of making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकान्त|श्रीकांत|श्रीकान्तः
श्रीकान्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, and कान्त husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकारी
श्रीकारी<BR>f. (-री)<BR>An antelope.<BR>E.<BR>श्री increasing, (nourishment,) कर maker, aff. ङीष्, the flesh being considered as highly digestible and nutritive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीखण्ड|श्रीखंड|श्रीखण्डः
श्रीखण्ड<BR>mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>Sandal wood.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, and खण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीगदित
श्रीगदित<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>One of the minor dramatic compositions, a piece in one act, dedicated chiefly to the goddess of prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>श्री, and गदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीगर्ब्भ
श्रीगर्ब्भ<BR>m. (-र्ब्भः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, and गर्ब्भ womb or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीग्रह|श्रीग्रहः
श्रीग्रह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A place for watering birds.<BR>E.<BR>श्री wealth, and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीघन|श्रीघनं|श्रीघनः
श्रीघन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Sour curds.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR>E.<BR>श्री prosperity, and घन a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीचक्र|श्रीचक्रं
श्रीचक्र<BR>n. (-क्रं)<BR>1 A magical diagram.<BR>2 An astrological division of the body, the uterine or pubic region.<BR>3 A wheel of INDRA'S car.<BR>4 The circle of the globe or earth.<BR>E.<BR>श्री prosperity, &c., and चक्र a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीज|श्रीजः
श्रीज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The deity of love.<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीद|श्रीदः
श्रीद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>Conferring wealth, prosperity, &c.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>KUVERA, the god of riches.<BR>E.<BR>श्री wealth, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीधर|श्रीधरः
श्रीधर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A Jina of the past period.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, or good fortune, and घर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनन्दन|श्रीनंदन|श्रीनन्दनः
श्रीनन्दन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>The deity of love, KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and नन्दन the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनिकेतन|श्रीनिकेतनः
श्रीनिकेतन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, and निकेतन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनिवास|श्रीनिवासः
श्रीनिवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, and निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपति|श्रीपतिः
श्रीपति<BR>m. (-तिः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A king, a prince.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess of fortune or rank, and पति husband or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपथ|श्रीपथः
श्रीपथ<BR>m. (-थः)<BR>A highway, a royal road.<BR>E.<BR>श्री royal paraphernalia, and पथ for पयिन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपर्ण|श्रीपर्णं
श्रीपर्ण<BR>n. (-र्णं)<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>2 A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by attrition, (Premna spinosa).<BR>f. (-र्णी)<BR>1 A shrub, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>2 A medicinal plant, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>3 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>4 An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes).<BR>E.<BR>श्री beauty or the goddess, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपर्णिका
श्रीपर्णिका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A medicinal shrub, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपिष्ट|श्रीपिष्टः
श्रीपिष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the Śarala or pine, and पिष्ट pounded, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=863" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपुत्त्र
श्रीपुत्त्र<BR>m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>1 A horse.<BR>2 KĀMA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, or the goddess, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीफल|श्रीफलः
श्रीफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>f. (-ली)<BR>1 The indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>2 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>श्री beauty or the goddess, (to whom it may be offered,) and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीभद्र
श्रीभद्र<BR>m. (-द्रः)<BR>A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीभ्रातृ
श्रीभ्रातृ<BR>m. (-ता)<BR>A horse.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, भ्रातृ brother; being recovered as well as LAKṢMĪ, at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमत्|श्रीमन्त्
श्रीमत्<BR>mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>1 Wealthy, opulent.<BR>2 Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>3 Prosperous, fortunate, thriving.<BR>4 Famous, illustrious.<BR>m. (-मान्)<BR>1 A tree, commonly Tila or Tilaka.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>4 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री beauty, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमस्तक|श्रीमस्तकः
श्रीमस्तक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Garlick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमुख|श्रीमुखः
श्रीमुख<BR>m. (-खः)<BR>The seventh year of the Indian cycle.<BR>E.<BR>श्री prosperity, and मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुक्त|श्रीयुक्तः
श्रीयुक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>1 Famous, illustrious.<BR>2 Fortunate, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>श्री prosperity, and युक्त joined with, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुत|श्रीयुतः
श्रीयुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Famous, illustrious.<BR>2 Fortunate, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, and युत joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीरस|श्रीरसः
श्रीरस<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the Śarala tree or pine, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीराग|श्रीरागः
श्रीराग<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The third of the Rāgas or personified musical modes.<BR>E.<BR>श्री illustrious, राग the mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीराम|श्रीरामः
श्रीराम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>RĀMACANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री celebrated, and राम the name of the prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>1 Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>2 Rich, wealthy.<BR>E.<BR>श्री fortune, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्स|श्रीवत्सः
श्रीवत्स<BR>m. (-त्सः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 A particular mark, usually said to be a curl of hair, on the breast of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA, and represented in delineations of him by .<BR>3 A hole in a wall made for felonious purposes.<BR>4 The emblem of the tenth Jina, or the mark above ascribed to VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and वत्स dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सकिन्
श्रीवत्सकिन्<BR>m. (-की)<BR>A horse having a curl of hair on his breast.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीवत्स the mark of VIṢṆU, कन् aff. of comparison, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सभृत्
श्रीवत्सभृत्<BR>m. (-भृत्)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीवत्स the mark so termed, and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सलाञ्छन|श्रीवत्सलांछन|श्रीवत्सलाञ्छनः
श्रीवत्सलाञ्छन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीवत्स the figure so named, and लाञ्छन sign, mark, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्साङ्क|श्रीवत्साङ्कः
श्रीवत्साङ्क<BR>m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>VIṢṆU: see the last.<BR>E.<BR>श्रीवत्स, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवराह|श्रीवराहः
श्रीवराह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>E.<BR>श्री illustrious, वराह the boar Avatāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवास|श्रीवासः
श्रीवास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Turpentine.<BR>2 VIṢṆU.<BR>3 A lotus.<BR>4 ŚIVA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the Śarala or pine, or LAKṢMĪ, &c., and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवासस्
श्रीवासस्<BR>n. (-सः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवृक्ष|श्रीवृक्षः
श्रीवृक्ष<BR>m. (-क्षः)<BR>The holy fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>E.<BR>श्री auspicious, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवृक्षक|श्रीवृक्षकः
श्रीवृक्षक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A curl or lock of hair on the chest of a horse: a various reading perhaps for श्रीवत्सक; see श्रीवत्सकिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवेष्ट|श्रीवेष्टः
श्रीवेष्ट<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>Turpentine.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the Śarala or pine tree, and वेष्ट extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीश|श्रीशः
श्रीश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>1 VIṢṆU.<BR>2 RĀMACANDRA.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess LAKṢMĪ, also incarnate in SĪTĀ, and ईश husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसज्ञ
श्रीसज्ञ<BR>n. (-ज्ञं)<BR>Cloves.<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and सज्ञा appellation, the names of the goddess being all applied to the spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसहोदर|श्रीसहोदरः
श्रीसहोदर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>The moon.<BR>E.<BR>श्री the goddess, and सहोदर uterine brother; being reproduced with her and other objects, at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीहस्तिनी
श्रीहस्तिनी<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>The sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, हस्त the hand, इनि and ङीष् aff.; held in the hand of the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु<BR>r. 1st cl. form irr. (शृणोति)<BR>To hear:<BR>form reg. (श्रवति)<BR>To go, to move, especially as a fluid, to drop, to ooze, to flow.<BR>With प्रति or सम् prefixed,<BR>To promise, to assent or agree to.<BR>With वि,<BR>To be famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुग्वारु|श्रुग्वारुः
श्रुग्वारु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुघ्निका
श्रुघ्निका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत|श्रुतं|श्रुतः
श्रुत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Heard.<BR>2 Understood.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Sacred science, holy writ, &c.<BR>2 The object of hearing, that which is heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतकीर्त्ति|श्रुतकीर्ति|श्रुतकीर्त्तिः
श्रुतकीर्त्ति<BR>mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति)<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR>m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 A divine sage.<BR>2 A generous man, a benefactor, a donor.<BR>f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>1 A river.<BR>2 The wife of BHARATA.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत heard, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतदेवी
श्रुतदेवी<BR>f. (-वी)<BR>SARASVATĪ.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत that which is heard, (science, &c.) and देवी presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतधर|श्रुतधरः
श्रुतधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Recollecting, remembering what has been heard.<BR>2 Having or observing the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत, and घर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्षि|श्रुतर्षिः
श्रुतर्षि<BR>m. (-र्षिः)<BR>A Ṛṣi of a particular order; one by whom holy writ has been heard, not taught; as the author of the Suśruta, a medical work, the son of VIŚVĀMITRA, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत heard, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतवत्|श्रुतवन्त्
श्रुतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Hearing, having heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतश्रवोनुज|श्रुतश्रवोनुजः
श्रुतश्रवोनुज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>The planet ŚANI or SATURN.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुतश्रवस् one of the other sons of SŪRYA, and अनुज younger born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतादान|श्रुतादानं
श्रुतादान<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Citing the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत holy writ, and आदान referring to, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्न|श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्नः
श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्न<BR>mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>Well read in sacred science, conversant with the Vedas, and the branches of knowledge or philosophy, dependant on them.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत heard, (knowledge of grammar, &c. that has been taught viva voce,) अध्ययन perusal, (of the Vedas,) सस्पन्न accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतान्वित|श्रुतान्वितः
श्रुतान्वित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Acquainted with or conforming to the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुति|श्रुतिः
श्रुति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>1 The Vedas, severally or collectively, scripture, holy writ.<BR>2 An ear.<BR>3 Hearing.<BR>4 Intelligence, news, rumour, report.<BR>5 (In music,) A division of the octave, a quarter tone or interval, of which twenty-two are enumerated; four constituting a major tone, three a minor, and two a semitone: the Śrutis are personified as nymphs.<BR>6 The constellation Śravaṇā.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=864" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकट|श्रुतिकटः
श्रुतिकट<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>1 Penance, expiation.<BR>2 A snake.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति the Vedas, or an ear, &c., and कट to go, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकथित|श्रुतिकथितः
श्रुतिकथित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Taught or prescribed by the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति as above, and कथित said, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिचोदन|श्रुतिचोदनः
श्रुतिचोदन<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>Holy precept or injunction, the doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and चोदन saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिजीविका
श्रुतिजीविका<BR>f. (-का)<BR>Law, the code of laws.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति the Vedas, and जीविका living; existing according to scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतितत्पर|श्रुतितत्परः
श्रुतितत्पर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Hearing, having ears.<BR>2 Studying the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति hearing, or the Vedas, and तत्पर attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिद्वैध
श्रुतिद्वैध<BR>n. (-धं)<BR>Disagreement or contradiction of any two passages in the Vedas, or of two Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and द्वैध difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिधर|श्रुतिधरः
श्रुतिधर<BR>mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>1 Having, being versed in, or observing the Vedas.<BR>2 Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and घर who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिन्
श्रुतिन्<BR>mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>1 Hearing.<BR>2 Observing, obeying.<BR>3 Having or following the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमूल
श्रुतिमूल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>1 The root of the ear.<BR>2 The text of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमण्डल
श्रुतिमण्डल<BR>n. (-लं)<BR>The outer ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवर्ज्जित|श्रुतिवर्जित|श्रुतिवर्ज्जितः
श्रुतिवर्ज्जित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Deaf.<BR>2 Ignorant or unread in the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति hearing, or the Vedas, and वर्ज्जित abandoned, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविषय|श्रुतिविषयः
श्रुतिविषय<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>An object or doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति. and विषय an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिस्मृतिविहित
श्रुतिस्मृतिविहित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Scriptural, declared by the Vedas and the law.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and स्मृति and विहित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्यनुप्रास|श्रुत्यनुप्रासः
श्रुत्यनुप्रास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>Alliteration.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति hearing, and अनुप्रास similarity of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्युक्त
श्रुत्युक्त<BR>mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>Said or enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति, and उक्त said; also श्रुत्युदित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्वा
श्रुत्वा<BR>ind.<BR>Having heard.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुव|श्रुवः
श्रुव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>n. (-वं)<BR>A sort of ladle used for pouring Ghee or oiled butter at a sacrifice.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to ooze or leak, aff. क, more usually श्रुव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुश्रुतवत्
श्रुश्रुतवत्<BR>mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>Hearing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, reiterated, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रूयमाण
श्रूयमाण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Hearing, being hearing.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणि|श्रेणिः
श्रेणि<BR>mf. (-णिः-णिः or-णी)<BR>1 A line, a row, a range.<BR>2 A company of artisans following the same business.<BR>3 A corporation, a company of traders or those dealing in the same articles.<BR>4 A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR>E.<BR>श्रि to serve, नि Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिक|श्रेणिकः
श्रेणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>The name of one of the kings of Magadhā, contemporary with and patron of ŚĀKYASIṂHA.<BR>f. (-का)<BR>A tent.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेणि a line, &c., कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणीभूत
श्रेणीभूत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>1 Made or become a heap.<BR>2 Arranged, set in rows.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेणि a range, भूत become, च्चि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेधी
श्रेधी<BR>f. (-धी)<BR>1 A set or succession of substances.<BR>2 (In arithmetic,) Progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्
श्रेयस्<BR>mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>Best, excellent, most excellent.<BR>ind.<BR>Well, most excellent.<BR>n. (-यः)<BR>1 Virtue, moral merit.<BR>2 Final happiness.<BR>3 Good fortune, auspiciousness, prosperity.<BR>m. (-प्रान्)<BR>The 11th Jina or Jaina pontiff.<BR>f. (-यसी)<BR>1 A plant resembling pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>2 A shrub, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>3 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>E.<BR>श्र substituted for प्रशस्त good, and ईयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्कर
श्रेयस्कर<BR>mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>1 Conferring, or the means of, future felicity.<BR>2 Propitious.<BR>3 Making better or superior.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेयस्, and कर who or what does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्काम
श्रेयस्काम<BR>mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>Desiring final felicity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेयस्, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्त्व
श्रेयस्त्व<BR>n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>1 Superiority, betterness.<BR>2 Final felicity, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेयस्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयांश
श्रेयांश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>The eleventh Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present era; also श्रेयांस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयोर्थिन्
श्रेयोर्थिन्<BR>mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>Desirous of good, ambitious.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेयस्, and अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठ|श्रेष्ठं|श्रेष्ठः
श्रेष्ठ<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>1 Best, excellent, most excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>2 Oldest, senior.<BR>m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>1 KUVERA.<BR>2 A king.<BR>3 A Brahman.<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>Cow's milk.<BR>E.<BR>श्र for प्रशस्त best, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठकाष्ठ|श्रेष्ठकाष्ठः
श्रेष्ठकाष्ठ<BR>n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>The main pillar of a house.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेष्ठ best, and काष्ठ timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठता
श्रेष्ठता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Superiority, betterness, excellence.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेष्ठ, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, श्रेष्ठत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठाश्रम|श्रेष्ठाश्रमः
श्रेष्ठाश्रम<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>The householder.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेष्ठ best, आश्रम order or state; the householder being considered the best of the four orders, as he supports the other three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठिन्
श्रेष्ठिन्<BR>mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि)<BR>Best, chief.<BR>m. (-ष्ठी)<BR>1 An artist eminent by birth.<BR>2 The head or chief of a body of persons following the same trade or occupation, a president, a foreman.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेष्ठ excellence, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रै
श्रै<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्रायति)<BR>1 To boil, to cook.<BR>2 To melt, to liquefy.<BR>3 To sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रैष्ठ्य|श्रैष्ठ्यं
श्रैष्ठ्य<BR>n. (-ष्ठ्यं)<BR>Superiority, betterness, preference.<BR>E.<BR>श्रेष्ठ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण<BR>(ऋ) श्रोणृ r. 1st cl. (श्रोणति)<BR>To accumulate, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Dressed, cooked, matured.<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A cripple.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>1 The constellation Śravaṇā.<BR>2 Rice-gruel.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोण to heap together, aff. अच्; or शॄ to injure, Uṇādi aff. न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणि|श्रोणिः
श्रोणि<BR>f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>1 The hip and loins.<BR>2 A road, a way.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोण to heap, aff. इन्; or श्रु to hear, Uṇādi aff. नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिफलक|श्रोणिफलकं
श्रोणिफलक<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>1 The hip and loins, or the hip only.<BR>2 The hip-bone, the os ilium.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोणि the same, and फल fruit, कन् aff. of comparison, or फलक a plank; also श्रोणिफल n. (-लं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिविम्ब
श्रोणिविम्ब<BR>n. (-म्बं)<BR>A string worn round the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
श्रोतस्<BR>n. (-तः)<BR>1 The ear.<BR>2 The current of a stream.<BR>3 An organ of sense.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear or to leak, aff. असुन्, and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतव्य|श्रोतव्यं
श्रोतव्य<BR>mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>To be heard or listened to.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, तव्य aff. of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ<BR>mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>Hearing, a hearer, who hears.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्र|श्रोत्रं
श्रोत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>The ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, Uṇādi aff. त्रन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रसुख
श्रोत्रसुख<BR>mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>Melodious, musical, sounding agreeably.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्र, and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रादि
श्रोत्रादि<BR>ind.<BR>The five senses.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्र, and आदि etcetera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय<BR>mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>Modest, docile, well-behaved.<BR>m. (-यः)<BR>1 A Brahman versed in the study of the Vedas.<BR>2 A Brahman following [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">Page866</a>] a particular branch or school of the Vedas.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्र considered as substituted for छन्दस् the metre of the Vedas, and खन् aff.; or श्रोत्र the ear, said also to mean the Vedas, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=865" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियता
श्रोत्रियता<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>Conversancy with the Vedas, the duty of a Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्रिय a priest acquainted with the Vedas, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियस्व
श्रोत्रियस्व<BR>n. (-स्वं)<BR>The property of a learned Brahman.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्रिय, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत|श्रौतं|श्रौतः
श्रौत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>Relating or belonging to the Vedas, to the ear, hearing, &c.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Preservation of the sacred fire.<BR>2 Any observance ordained by the Vedas.<BR>f. (-ती)<BR>Comparison expressed by a particle, so, as, like, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्रुति the Vedas, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतस्मार्त्तक्रिया|श्रौतस्मार्तक्रिया
श्रौतस्मार्त्तक्रिया<BR>f. (-या)<BR>Acts conformable to law and religion.<BR>E.<BR>श्रौत and स्मार्त्त, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतस्मार्त्तधर्म्म|श्रौतस्मार्तधर्म
श्रौतस्मार्त्तधर्म्म<BR>m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>Duty enjoined by the Vedas and laws.<BR>E.<BR>श्रौत and स्मार्त्त, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत्र|श्रौत्रं
श्रौत्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>1 Conversancy with the Vedas.<BR>2 The ear.<BR>E.<BR>श्रोत्र the ear, or श्रोत्रिय a Brahman studied in scripture, अण् aff.; in the second case the last syllable rejected as well as the pen. vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट्<BR>ind.<BR>An exclamation used in making an offering with fire to the gods or manes.<BR>E.<BR>श्रु to hear, (the prayer being heard in consequence,) and डौषट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्र्याह्व|श्र्याह्वं
श्र्याह्व<BR>n. (-ह्वं)<BR>The lotus.<BR>E.<BR>श्री LAKṢMĪ, and आह्वा appellation, the goddess appearing in the first instance from within the flower, and thence deriving many of her names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक
श्लक<BR>(इ) श्लकि r. 1st cl. (श्लंकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण<BR>mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>1 Small, fine, minute.<BR>2 Gentle, mild, amiable.<BR>3 Honest, sincere.<BR>4 Plain, even, smooth.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, क्स्न aff., the short vowel substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लग
श्लग<BR>(इ) श्लगि r. 1st cl. (श्लंङ्गति)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्लथयमि)<BR>To be weak, to be relaxed, loose, flaccid.<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्लथयति)<BR>To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ<BR>mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>1 Loose, flaccid, relaxed.<BR>2 Dishevelled (hair).<BR>3 Untied, unfastened.<BR>E.<BR>श्लथ to be relaxed, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख
श्लाख<BR>(ऋ) श्लाखृ r. 1st cl. (श्लाखति)<BR>To pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ
श्लाघ<BR>(ऋ) श्लाघृ r. 1st cl. (श्लाघते)<BR>1 To praise, to eulogise.<BR>2 To flatter, to coax, to wheedle.<BR>3 To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा<BR>f. (-घा)<BR>1 Praise, panegyric, flattery, eulogium.<BR>2 Service, obedience.<BR>3 Wish, desire.<BR>E.<BR>श्लाघ to praise, aff. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित
श्लाघित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Praised, commended.<BR>E.<BR>श्लाघ to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्य|श्लाघ्यः
श्लाघ्य<BR>mfn. (-घ्यः-घ्या-घ्यं)<BR>Venerable, respectable, praise-worthy, entitled to praise or veneration.<BR>E.<BR>श्लाघा praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकु|श्लिकुः
श्लिकु<BR>m. (-कुः)<BR>1 A servant, a slave.<BR>2 A blackguard.<BR>3 A lecher, a libertine or debauchee.<BR>n. (-कु)<BR>Astronomy. astrology.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, Uṇādi aff. कु, and क substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष
श्लिष<BR>r. 4th cl. (ञि ओऌ) श्लिषॢ (श्लिष्यति) r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्लेषति श्लेषयति)<BR>1 To embrace.<BR>2 To adhere or cling to.<BR>3 To unite, to join or connect.<BR>(उ) श्लिषु r. 1st cl. (श्लिपति)<BR>To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिषा
श्लिषा<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>Embracing, an embrace.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट|श्लिष्टः
श्लिष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>1 Embraced.<BR>2 Touched by, clung or adhered to.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्यत्
श्लिष्यत्<BR>mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्)<BR>Embracing, clinging, adhering to, being in close contact with.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, शवृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपद|श्लीपदं
श्लीपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>Morbid enlargement of the legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदप्रभव|श्लीपदप्रभवः
श्लीपदप्रभव<BR>m. (-वः)<BR>The mango tree.<BR>E.<BR>श्लीपद swelled^1 leg, and प्रभव production.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदापह|श्लीपदापहः
श्लीपदापह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A plant, (Nageia putranjiva.)<BR>E.<BR>श्लीपद, and अपह removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Prosperous, fortunate, affluent, happy.<BR>E.<BR>श्री good fortune, लच् poss. aff., and र changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष|श्लेषः
श्लेष<BR>m. (-षः)<BR>1 Union, junction, the proximity of contact.<BR>2 Association, society, presence.<BR>3 Embracing, an embrace.<BR>4 Adhering or clinging to, &c.<BR>5 A figure of rhetoric, choice or connexion of words so as to admit of a double interpretation, a species of paronomasia or pun.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मक|श्लेष्मकः
श्लेष्मक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>Phlegm, the watery or phlegmatic humor.<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्मन् the same, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मघ्न
श्लेष्मघ्न<BR>mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं)<BR>Removing phlegm.<BR>f. (-घ्ना)<BR>1 Arabian jasmine.<BR>2 A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>Hogweed.<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्म phlegm, and घ्न removing, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मज
श्लेष्मज<BR>mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>Produced or proceeding from phlegm.<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्मन्, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण<BR>mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>Phlegmatic.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्मन् the humor, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन्<BR>m. (-ष्मा)<BR>The phlegmatic humor, one of the three principal humors or fluids of the body.<BR>E.<BR>श्लिष to embrace or adhere to, (the body,) aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मल|श्लेष्मलः
श्लेष्मल<BR>mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>Phlegmatic, abounding or affected with phlegm, &c.<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Cordia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्म phlegm, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मह|श्लेष्महः
श्लेष्मह<BR>m. (-हः)<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्म phlegm, and ह destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मात|श्लेष्मातः
श्लेष्मात<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A small tree, (Cordia latifolia.)<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्मन् phlegm, अत to go, (to remove,) aff. अच्; also with कन् added श्लेष्मातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लैष्मिक
श्लैष्मिक<BR>mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>Allaying or exciting phlegm, phlegmatic.<BR>E.<BR>श्लेष्मन् phlegm, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक|श्लोकः
श्लोक<BR>(ऋ) श्लोकृ r. 1st cl. (श्लोकते)<BR>1 To put together, to compose, as verses.<BR>2 To be put together or composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक|श्लोकः
श्लोक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>1 A verse, a stanza.<BR>2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>E.<BR>श्लोक to compose, (as verses,) aff. अच्; according to the Rāmāyaṇa, irr. derived from शोक sorrow: the first verse ever composed, having been the involuntary expression of VĀLMĪKI'S grief at beholding a bird killed by a fowler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकत्व
श्लोकत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं)<BR>Versification.<BR>E.<BR>त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण|श्लोणः
श्लोण<BR>(ऋ) श्लोणृ r. 1st cl. (श्लोणति)<BR>To heap together, to collect or assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वःश्रेयस|श्वःश्रेयसं
श्वःश्रेयस<BR>mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>Happy, prosperous.<BR>n. adv. (-सं)<BR>1 Happy, well, right.<BR>subst.<BR>2 BRAHMA, the Supreme Being.<BR>3 Happiness, prosperity.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस् particle, implying happiness, श्रेयस् [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">Page867</a>] best, excellent, and a final अच् or vowel added to the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=866" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक|श्वकः
श्वक<BR>(इ) श्वकि r. 1st cl. (श्वंकते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक्रीडिन्
श्वक्रीडिन्<BR>m. (-डी)<BR>A dog-feeder or trainer.<BR>E.<BR>श्व, and क्रीडिन् who plays with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वग
श्वग<BR>(इ) श्वगि r. 1st cl. (श्वंगति)<BR>To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वगण|श्वगणः
श्वगण<BR>m. (-णः)<BR>A pack or number of dogs.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वगणिक|श्वगणिकः
श्वगणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter.<BR>mf. (-कः-का)<BR>1 A dog feeder.<BR>2 One carried by dogs.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, गण a number, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच
श्वच<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्वचते) (इ) श्वचि (श्वंचते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज
श्वज<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्वजते) also (इ) श्वजि (श्वंजते)<BR>To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ
श्वठ<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्वाठयति) (इ) श्वठि (श्वण्ठयति)<BR>1 To finish.<BR>2 To leave defective or unfinished.<BR>3 To go, to move.<BR>(श्वठयति)<BR>1 To speak amiss.<BR>2 To speak well.<BR>3 To abstain from speaking: see शठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वदंष्ट्रा
श्वदंष्ट्रा<BR>f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>1 A dog's tooth.<BR>2 A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>E.<BR>श्व for श्वन् a dog, दंष्ट्रा a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वधूर्त्त|श्वधूर्त|श्वधूर्तः|श्वधूर्त्तः
श्वधूर्त्त<BR>m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, and धूर्त्त a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन्<BR>m. (-श्वा श्वानौ श्वानः) accu. plu. (शुनः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (शुनी)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to increase, Uṇādi aff. कनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वनिश|श्वनिशं
श्वनिश<BR>nf. (-शं-शा)<BR>A night on which dogs bark and howl.<BR>E.<BR>श्व for श्वन् a dog, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपच|श्वपचः
श्वपच<BR>mf. (-चः-चा)<BR>1 A man or woman of a low and degraded caste.<BR>2 A dog-feeder or keeper.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, पच to cook (for his food), or to cherish as his property, and अच् aff.; also with क्विप् aff. श्वपच् m. (-पक्) and with अण् aff. श्वपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपद
श्वपद<BR>n. (-दं)<BR>1 A dog's foot^1.<BR>2 A mark like one, to be branded on the forehead of a thief.<BR>E.<BR>श्व, and पद a foot.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210731. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपाक|श्वपाकः
श्वपाक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A man of a degraded and outcast tribe, the son of an Ugrā woman by a Kṣatrī male, and classed with the Caṇḍāla, with whom he is ordered to live out of the town, to feed from broken vessels, and wear the clothes of the dead; to possess no other property than asses and dogs, and to be excluded from all intercourse with other tribes; he can only be employed as public executioner, or to carry out the bodies of those who die without kindred.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, पच to cook, (to feed on or to cherish,) aff. अण्: see श्वपच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वफल|श्वफलः
श्वफल<BR>m. (-लः)<BR>The lime or citron.<BR>E.<BR>श्व for श्वन् a dog, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभीरु|श्वभीरुः
श्वभीरु<BR>m. (-रुः)<BR>A jackal.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, and भीरु afraid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र|श्वभ्रं
श्वभ्र<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्वभ्रयति)<BR>1 To live in misery or distress.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR>3 To make a hole, to pierce or perforate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र|श्वभ्रं
श्वभ्र<BR>n. (-भ्रं)<BR>A hole, a gap, a chasm.<BR>E.<BR>श्वभ्र to pierce, aff. अच्, or श्व a dog, भृ to cherish, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथु|श्वयथुः
श्वयथु<BR>m. (-थुः)<BR>Swelling, intumescence.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to swell, aff. अथुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयीचि|श्वयीचिः
श्वयीचि<BR>f. (-चिः)<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>E.<BR>श्वि to increase, Uṇādi aff. ईचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वर्त्त|श्वर्त
श्वर्त्त<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्वर्त्तयति)<BR>1 To live in misery or distress.<BR>2 To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल
श्वल<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्वलति)<BR>To run, to go quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्क
श्वल्क<BR>r. 10th cl. (श्वल्कयति)<BR>To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्ल
श्वल्ल<BR>r. 1st cl. (श्वल्लति)<BR>To run, to go fast or quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववत्|श्ववन्त्
श्ववत्<BR>ind.<BR>Like a dog, cur-like.<BR>E.<BR>श्व, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववत्|श्ववन्त्
श्ववत्<BR>m. (-वान्)<BR>A dog-feeder or trainer.<BR>E.<BR>श्व, and मतुप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववृत्ति|श्ववृत्तिः
श्ववृत्ति<BR>m. (-त्तिः)<BR>Service, servitude.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वव्याघ्र|श्वव्याघ्रः
श्वव्याघ्र<BR>m. (-घ्रः)<BR>The hunting leopard or Ciṭa.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, and व्याघ्र a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर|श्वशुरः
श्वशुर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>1 A father-in-law, a wife's or husband's father.<BR>2 A venerable man, one to be treated as a father-in-law.<BR>m. du. (-रौ)<BR>A father and mother-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>शु a particle, implying respect, अश to pervade, Uṇādi aff. उरच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर्य्य|श्वशुर्य|श्वशुर्यः|श्वशुर्य्यः
श्वशुर्य्य<BR>m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>1 A brother-in-law, a wife's or husband's brother.<BR>2 A husband's younger brother.<BR>E.<BR>श्वशुर a father-in-law, and यत् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रू
श्वश्रू<BR>f. (-श्रूः)<BR>A mother-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>श्वशुर a father-in-law, the उ and अ rejected, र conjoined with श, and ऊङ् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रूश्वशुर
श्वश्रूश्वशुर<BR>m. du. (-रौ)<BR>Mother and father-in-law.<BR>E.<BR>श्वश्रू, and श्वशुर conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस
श्वस<BR>r. 2nd cl. (श्वसिति)<BR>1 To breathe.<BR>2 To live.<BR>With आङ् prefixed,<BR>To recover or revive, to console.<BR>With उत्,<BR>1 To open, to expand.<BR>2 To console.<BR>With निर्,<BR>1 To breathe out, to expire.<BR>2 To sigh.<BR>With वि,<BR>To have trust or faith in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस्<BR>ind.<BR>1 To-morrow.<BR>2 A particle, implying auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसत्
श्वसत्<BR>mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सती-सत्)<BR>Breathing, sighing.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस to breathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसन|श्वसनं|श्वसनः
श्वसन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>2 A thorny plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>1 Breathing, breath.<BR>2 Sighing.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस to breathe, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनासन
श्वसनासन<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>श्वसन breathing, असन food; eating air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनेश्वर|श्वसनेश्वरः
श्वसनेश्वर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>E.<BR>श्वसन breath, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनोत्सुक|श्वसनोत्सुकः
श्वसनोत्सुक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A snake.<BR>E.<BR>श्वसन breathing, and उत्सुक delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसित|श्वसितं
श्वसित<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>Sighed, breathed, sighing, breathing.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>1 Breathing, breath.<BR>2 Sighing, a sigh.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसुत
श्वसुत<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>A plant, (Conyza lacera, &c.)<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्तन|श्वस्तनं
श्वस्तन<BR>mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Future, what will be to-morrow, &c.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस् to-morrow, ट्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्त्य|श्वस्त्यं
श्वस्त्य<BR>mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>To-morrow's, what will be to-morrow.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस् to-morrow, and त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्पृष्ट
श्वस्पृष्ट<BR>mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>Touched by a dog, defiled.<BR>E.<BR>श्व, and स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वागणिक|श्वागणिकः
श्वागणिक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A hunter.<BR>mf. (-कः-की)<BR>1 A dog-keeper, one who lives by feeding or keeping dogs.<BR>2 One who rides or is drawn by dogs.<BR>E.<BR>श्वगण a number of dogs, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वादन्त|श्वादंत|श्वादंतः|श्वादन्तः
श्वादन्त<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>A dog's tooth.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन a dog, दन्त a tooth, and the vowel termination of the first word made long in this and similar compounds, as श्वाकर्ण, श्वापुच्छ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान|श्वानः
श्वान<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>A dog.<BR>f. (-नी)<BR>A bitch.<BR>E.<BR>a various reading of श्वन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वापद|श्वापदः
श्वापद<BR>mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>Ferocious, savage, relating or belonging to a beast of prey.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>A beast of prey in general.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, आपद to resemble, aff. अच्; or श्वपद with अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=867" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाविध्
श्वाविध्<BR>m. (-विद् or वित्)<BR>A porcupine.<BR>E.<BR>श्वन् a dog, आङ् before व्यध to pierce, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाश्व|श्वाश्वः
श्वाश्व<BR>n. (-श्वः)<BR>BHAIRAVA, or ŚIVA, in a terrific form.<BR>E.<BR>श्व a dog, and अश्व a horse, being usually represented mounted on a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वास|श्वासः
श्वास<BR>m. (-सः)<BR>1 Breath, breathing.<BR>2 Air, wind.<BR>3 Sighing, a sigh.<BR>E.<BR>श्वस to breathe, aff. ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासप्रश्वासधारण|श्वासप्रश्वासधारणं
श्वासप्रश्वासधारण<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>Breathing through the nostrils for a few seconds as a religious exercise: see प्राणायाम.<BR>E.<BR>श्वास inspiration, प्रश्वास expiration, and धारण holding or checking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासहेति|श्वासहेतिः
श्वासहेति<BR>f. (-तिः)<BR>Sleep, sleepiness.<BR>E.<BR>श्वास breathing or sighing, and हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासारि|श्वासारिः
श्वासारि<BR>m. (-रिः)<BR>A plant, commonly Bamanaiṭhi.<BR>E.<BR>श्वास breath, and अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासिन्
श्वासिन्<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>Air, wind.<BR>E.<BR>श्वास breath, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वि
श्वि<BR>(इर टु and ओ) टुओश्वि r. 1st cl. (श्वयति)<BR>1 To move, to go, or go to.<BR>2 To grow, to increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित
श्वित<BR>(आ) श्विता r. 1st cl. (श्वेतते)<BR>To be white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्र|श्वित्रं
श्वित्र<BR>n. (-त्रं)<BR>Whiteness of the skin, vitiligo.<BR>E.<BR>श्वित to be white, Uṇādi aff. रक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रघ्नी
श्वित्रघ्नी<BR>f. (-घ्नी)<BR>A plant, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR>E.<BR>श्वित्र vitiligo, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रिन्
श्वित्रिन्<BR>mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि)<BR>Affected with vitiligo or whiteness of the skin.<BR>E.<BR>श्वित्र, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विद
श्विद<BR>(इ) श्विदि r. 1st cl. (श्विंदते)<BR>To be white, to become or continue so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वॄ
श्वॄ<BR>r. 9th cl. (श्वृणाति)<BR>To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत|श्वेतं|श्वेतः
श्वेत<BR>mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>White.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>1 White, (the colour.)<BR>2 The planet VENUS, or its regent ŚUKRA.<BR>3 The sixth range of mountains, dividing the known continent, the white mountains separating the Varṣas of Hiraṇmaya and Romanaka.<BR>4 One of the minor Dvīpas or divisions of the world; in fable the White Island, identified geographically by WILFORD, with Britain.<BR>5 A white cloud.<BR>6 Cumminseed.<BR>7 A conch.<BR>mf. (-तः-ता)<BR>A small white shell used as a coin, a Cowri.<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>Silver.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>1 A grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>2 A plant, Kāṣṭha Pātāla (?)<BR>3 A flower, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>4 Hogweed.<BR>5 Bent grass with white blossoms.<BR>6 Bambu manna.<BR>7 Crystal.<BR>8 Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>E.<BR>श्वित to be white, aff. अच् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतक|श्वेतकं|श्वेतकः
श्वेतक<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>A Cowri.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>Silver.<BR>E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकुञ्जर|श्वेतकुंजर|श्वेतकुञ्जरः
श्वेतकुञ्जर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>INDRA'S elephant.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकेतु|श्वेतकेतुः
श्वेतकेतु<BR>m. (-तुः)<BR>A Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and केतु a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकेश|श्वेतकेशः
श्वेतकेश<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>A variety of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and केश a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकोल|श्वेतकोलः
श्वेतकोल<BR>n. (-लः)<BR>The Saphara fish, (Cyprinus Sophore, HAM.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतखदिर|श्वेतखदिरः
श्वेतखदिर<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>A white variety of the Mimosa catechu.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत, and खदिर the Khayar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतगज|श्वेतगजः
श्वेतगज<BR>m. (-जः)<BR>1 A white elephant.<BR>2 The elephant of INDRA.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतगरुत्
श्वेतगरुत्<BR>m. (-रुत्)<BR>A goose.<BR>E.<BR>श्वेत white, and गरुत् a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=WIL&page=868" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=wil" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतछद|श्वेतच्छद|श्वेतच्छदः
